__d(function(e,a,h,t,o,n,s){o.exports={book:"Gen",name:"Genesis",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the beginning, God created the heavens and the earth."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The earth was formless and empty. Darkness was on the surface of the deep and God\u2019s Spirit was hovering over the surface of the waters."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet there be light,\u201d and there was light."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"God saw the light, and saw that it was good. God divided the light from the darkness."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"God called the light \u201cday\u201d, and the darkness he called \u201cnight\u201d. There was evening and there was morning, the first day."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet there be an expanse in the middle of the waters, and let it divide the waters from the waters.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"God made the expanse, and divided the waters which were under the expanse from the waters which were above the expanse; and it was so."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"God called the expanse \u201csky\u201d. There was evening and there was morning, a second day."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet the waters under the sky be gathered together to one place, and let the dry land appear;\u201d and it was so."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"God called the dry land \u201cearth\u201d, and the gathering together of the waters he called \u201cseas\u201d. God saw that it was good."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet the earth yield grass, herbs yielding seeds, and fruit trees bearing fruit after their kind, with their seeds in it, on the earth;\u201d and it was so."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The earth yielded grass, herbs yielding seed after their kind, and trees bearing fruit, with their seeds in it, after their kind; and God saw that it was good."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"There was evening and there was morning, a third day."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet there be lights in the expanse of the sky to divide the day from the night; and let them be for signs to mark seasons, days, and years;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and let them be for lights in the expanse of the sky to give light on the earth;\u201d and it was so."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"God made the two great lights: the greater light to rule the day, and the lesser light to rule the night. He also made the stars."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"God set them in the expanse of the sky to give light to the earth,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and to rule over the day and over the night, and to divide the light from the darkness. God saw that it was good."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There was evening and there was morning, a fourth day."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet the waters abound with living creatures, and let birds fly above the earth in the open expanse of the sky.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"God created the large sea creatures and every living creature that moves, with which the waters swarmed, after their kind, and every winged bird after its kind. God saw that it was good."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"God blessed them, saying, \u201cBe fruitful, and multiply, and fill the waters in the seas, and let birds multiply on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"There was evening and there was morning, a fifth day."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet the earth produce living creatures after their kind, livestock, creeping things, and animals of the earth after their kind;\u201d and it was so."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"God made the animals of the earth after their kind, and the livestock after their kind, and everything that creeps on the ground after its kind. God saw that it was good."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cLet\u2019s make man in our image, after our likeness. Let them have dominion over the fish of the sea, and over the birds of the sky, and over the livestock, and over all the earth, and over every creeping thing that creeps on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"God created man in his own image. In God\u2019s image he created him; male and female he created them."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"God blessed them. God said to them, \u201cBe fruitful, multiply, fill the earth, and subdue it. Have dominion over the fish of the sea, over the birds of the sky, and over every living thing that moves on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cBehold, I have given you every herb yielding seed, which is on the surface of all the earth, and every tree, which bears fruit yielding seed. It will be your food."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"To every animal of the earth, and to every bird of the sky, and to everything that creeps on the earth, in which there is life, I have given every green herb for food;\u201d and it was so."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"God saw everything that he had made, and, behold, it was very good. There was evening and there was morning, a sixth day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The heavens, the earth, and all their vast array were finished."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"On the seventh day God finished his work which he had done; and he rested on the seventh day from all his work which he had done."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"God blessed the seventh day, and made it holy, because he rested in it from all his work of creation which he had done."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the history of the generations of the heavens and of the earth when they were created, in the day that the LORD God made the earth and the heavens."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"No plant of the field was yet on the earth, and no herb of the field had yet sprung up; for the LORD God had not caused it to rain on the earth. There was not a man to till the ground,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but a mist went up from the earth, and watered the whole surface of the ground."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD God formed man from the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD God planted a garden eastward, in Eden, and there he put the man whom he had formed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Out of the ground the LORD God made every tree to grow that is pleasant to the sight, and good for food, including the tree of life in the middle of the garden and the tree of the knowledge of good and evil."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"A river went out of Eden to water the garden; and from there it was parted, and became the source of four rivers."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The name of the first is Pishon: it flows through the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and the gold of that land is good. Bdellium and onyx stone are also there."]],f:["or, aromatic resin"]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The name of the second river is Gihon. It is the same river that flows through the whole land of Cush."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The name of the third river is Hiddekel. This is the one which flows in front of Assyria. The fourth river is the Euphrates."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The LORD God took the man, and put him into the garden of Eden to cultivate and keep it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The LORD God commanded the man, saying, \u201cYou may freely eat of every tree of the garden;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"but you shall not eat of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil; for in the day that you eat of it, you will surely die.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD God said, \u201cIt is not good for the man to be alone. I will make him a helper comparable to him.\u201d"]],f:["or, suitable for, or appropriate for."]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Out of the ground the LORD God formed every animal of the field, and every bird of the sky, and brought them to the man to see what he would call them. Whatever the man called every living creature became its name."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The man gave names to all livestock, and to the birds of the sky, and to every animal of the field; but for man there was not found a helper comparable to him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD God caused the man to fall into a deep sleep. As the man slept, he took one of his ribs, and closed up the flesh in its place."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The LORD God made a woman from the rib which he had taken from the man, and brought her to the man."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The man said, \u201cThis is now bone of my bones, and flesh of my flesh. She will be called \u2018woman,\u2019 because she was taken out of Man.\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Therefore a man will leave his father and his mother, and will join with his wife, and they will be one flesh."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The man and his wife were both naked, and they were not ashamed."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the serpent was more subtle than any animal of the field which the LORD God had made. He said to the woman, \u201cHas God really said, \u2018You shall not eat of any tree of the garden\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said to the serpent, \u201cWe may eat fruit from the trees of the garden,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"but not the fruit of the tree which is in the middle of the garden. God has said, \u2018You shall not eat of it. You shall not touch it, lest you die.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The serpent said to the woman, \u201cYou won\u2019t really die,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"for God knows that in the day you eat it, your eyes will be opened, and you will be like God, knowing good and evil.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was a delight to the eyes, and that the tree was to be desired to make one wise, she took some of its fruit, and ate. Then she gave some to her husband with her, and he ate it, too."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Their eyes were opened, and they both knew that they were naked. They sewed fig leaves together, and made coverings for themselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They heard the LORD God\u2019s voice walking in the garden in the cool of the day, and the man and his wife hid themselves from the presence of the LORD God among the trees of the garden."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD God called to the man, and said to him, \u201cWhere are you?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The man said, \u201cI heard your voice in the garden, and I was afraid, because I was naked; so I hid myself.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cWho told you that you were naked? Have you eaten from the tree that I commanded you not to eat from?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The man said, \u201cThe woman whom you gave to be with me, she gave me fruit from the tree, and I ate it.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD God said to the woman, \u201cWhat have you done?\u201d"],[0,"The woman said, \u201cThe serpent deceived me, and I ate.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD God said to the serpent,"],[1,"\u201cBecause you have done this,"],[2,"you are cursed above all livestock,"],[2,"and above every animal of the field."],[1,"You shall go on your belly"],[2,"and you shall eat dust all the days of your life."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will put hostility between you and the woman,"],[2,"and between your offspring and her offspring."],[1,"He will bruise your head,"],[2,"and you will bruise his heel.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"To the woman he said,"],[1,"\u201cI will greatly multiply your pain in childbirth."],[2,"You will bear children in pain."],[1,"Your desire will be for your husband,"],[2,"and he will rule over you.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"To Adam he said,"],[1,"\u201cBecause you have listened to your wife\u2019s voice,"],[2,"and have eaten from the tree,"],[2,"about which I commanded you, saying, \u2018You shall not eat of it,\u2019"],[2,"the ground is cursed for your sake."],[1,"You will eat from it with much labor all the days of your life."]]},{v:18,l:[[2,"It will yield thorns and thistles to you;"],[2,"and you will eat the herb of the field."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"You will eat bread by the sweat of your face until you return to the ground,"],[2,"for you were taken out of it."],[1,"For you are dust,"],[2,"and you shall return to dust.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The man called his wife Eve because she would be the mother of all the living."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD God made garments of animal skins for Adam and for his wife, and clothed them."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD God said, \u201cBehold, the man has become like one of us, knowing good and evil. Now, lest he reach out his hand, and also take of the tree of life, and eat, and live forever\u2014\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD God sent him out from the garden of Eden, to till the ground from which he was taken."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"So he drove out the man; and he placed cherubim at the east of the garden of Eden, and a flaming sword which turned every way, to guard the way to the tree of life."]],f:["cherubim are powerful angelic creatures, messengers of God with wings. See Ezekiel 10."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The man knew Eve his wife. She conceived, and gave birth to Cain, and said, \u201cI have gotten a man with the LORD\u2019s help.\u201d"]],f:["or, lay with, or, had relations with","or, became pregnant"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Again she gave birth, to Cain\u2019s brother Abel. Abel was a keeper of sheep, but Cain was a tiller of the ground."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"As time passed, Cain brought an offering to the LORD from the fruit of the ground."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Abel also brought some of the firstborn of his flock and of its fat. The LORD respected Abel and his offering,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"but he didn\u2019t respect Cain and his offering. Cain was very angry, and the expression on his face fell."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Cain, \u201cWhy are you angry? Why has the expression of your face fallen?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If you do well, won\u2019t it be lifted up? If you don\u2019t do well, sin crouches at the door. Its desire is for you, but you are to rule over it.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Cain said to Abel, his brother, \u201cLet\u2019s go into the field.\u201d While they were in the field, Cain rose up against Abel, his brother, and killed him."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Cain, \u201cWhere is Abel, your brother?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI don\u2019t know. Am I my brother\u2019s keeper?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cWhat have you done? The voice of your brother\u2019s blood cries to me from the ground."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now you are cursed because of the ground, which has opened its mouth to receive your brother\u2019s blood from your hand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"From now on, when you till the ground, it won\u2019t yield its strength to you. You will be a fugitive and a wanderer on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Cain said to the LORD, \u201cMy punishment is greater than I can bear."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Behold, you have driven me out today from the surface of the ground. I will be hidden from your face, and I will be a fugitive and a wanderer on the earth. Whoever finds me will kill me.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cTherefore whoever slays Cain, vengeance will be taken on him sevenfold.\u201d The LORD appointed a sign for Cain, so that anyone finding him would not strike him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Cain left the LORD\u2019s presence, and lived in the land of Nod, east of Eden."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Cain knew his wife. She conceived, and gave birth to Enoch. He built a city, and named the city after the name of his son, Enoch."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Irad was born to Enoch. Irad became the father of Mehujael. Mehujael became the father of Methushael. Methushael became the father of Lamech."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Lamech took two wives: the name of the first one was Adah, and the name of the second one was Zillah."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Adah gave birth to Jabal, who was the father of those who dwell in tents and have livestock."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"His brother\u2019s name was Jubal, who was the father of all who handle the harp and pipe."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Zillah also gave birth to Tubal Cain, the forger of every cutting instrument of bronze and iron. Tubal Cain\u2019s sister was Naamah."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Lamech said to his wives,"],[1,"\u201cAdah and Zillah, hear my voice."],[2,"You wives of Lamech, listen to my speech,"],[1,"for I have slain a man for wounding me,"],[2,"a young man for bruising me."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"If Cain will be avenged seven times,"],[2,"truly Lamech seventy-seven times.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Adam knew his wife again. She gave birth to a son, and named him Seth, saying, \u201cfor God has given me another child instead of Abel, for Cain killed him.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"A son was also born to Seth, and he named him Enosh. At that time men began to call on the LORD\u2019s name."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the book of the generations of Adam. In the day that God created man, he made him in God\u2019s likeness."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He created them male and female, and blessed them. On the day they were created, he named them Adam."]],f:["\u201cAdam\u201d and \u201cMan\u201d are spelled with the exact same consonants in Hebrew, so this can be correctly translated either way."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Adam lived one hundred thirty years, and became the father of a son in his own likeness, after his image, and named him Seth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The days of Adam after he became the father of Seth were eight hundred years, and he became the father of other sons and daughters."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All the days that Adam lived were nine hundred thirty years, then he died."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Seth lived one hundred five years, then became the father of Enosh."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Seth lived after he became the father of Enosh eight hundred seven years, and became the father of other sons and daughters."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All of the days of Seth were nine hundred twelve years, then he died."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Enosh lived ninety years, and became the father of Kenan."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Enosh lived after he became the father of Kenan eight hundred fifteen years, and became the father of other sons and daughters."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"All of the days of Enosh were nine hundred five years, then he died."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Kenan lived seventy years, then became the father of Mahalalel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Kenan lived after he became the father of Mahalalel eight hundred forty years, and became the father of other sons and daughters"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and all of the days of Kenan were nine hundred ten years, then he died."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Mahalalel lived sixty-five years, then became the father of Jared."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Mahalalel lived after he became the father of Jared eight hundred thirty years, and became the father of other sons and daughters."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All of the days of Mahalalel were eight hundred ninety-five years, then he died."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Jared lived one hundred sixty-two years, then became the father of Enoch."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Jared lived after he became the father of Enoch eight hundred years, and became the father of other sons and daughters."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"All of the days of Jared were nine hundred sixty-two years, then he died."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Enoch lived sixty-five years, then became the father of Methuselah."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"After Methuselah\u2019s birth, Enoch walked with God for three hundred years, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"All the days of Enoch were three hundred sixty-five years."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Enoch walked with God, and he was not found, for God took him."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Methuselah lived one hundred eighty-seven years, then became the father of Lamech."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Methuselah lived after he became the father of Lamech seven hundred eighty-two years, and became the father of other sons and daughters."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"All the days of Methuselah were nine hundred sixty-nine years, then he died."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Lamech lived one hundred eighty-two years, then became the father of a son."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He named him Noah, saying, \u201cThis one will comfort us in our work and in the toil of our hands, caused by the ground which the LORD has cursed.\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Lamech lived after he became the father of Noah five hundred ninety-five years, and became the father of other sons and daughters."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"All the days of Lamech were seven hundred seventy-seven years, then he died."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Noah was five hundred years old, then Noah became the father of Shem, Ham, and Japheth."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When men began to multiply on the surface of the ground, and daughters were born to them,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"God\u2019s sons saw that men\u2019s daughters were beautiful, and they took any that they wanted for themselves as wives."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cMy Spirit will not strive with man forever, because he also is flesh; so his days will be one hundred twenty years.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The Nephilim were on the earth in those days, and also after that, when God\u2019s sons came in to men\u2019s daughters and had children with them. Those were the mighty men who were of old, men of renown."]],f:["or, giants"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD saw that the wickedness of man was great on the earth, and that every imagination of the thoughts of man\u2019s heart was continually only evil."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD was sorry that he had made man on the earth, and it grieved him in his heart."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cI will destroy man whom I have created from the surface of the ground\u2014man, along with animals, creeping things, and birds of the sky\u2014for I am sorry that I have made them.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But Noah found favor in the LORD\u2019s eyes."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the history of the generations of Noah: Noah was a righteous man, blameless among the people of his time. Noah walked with God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Noah became the father of three sons: Shem, Ham, and Japheth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The earth was corrupt before God, and the earth was filled with violence."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"God saw the earth, and saw that it was corrupt, for all flesh had corrupted their way on the earth."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Noah, \u201cI will bring an end to all flesh, for the earth is filled with violence through them. Behold, I will destroy them and the earth."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Make a ship of gopher wood. You shall make rooms in the ship, and shall seal it inside and outside with pitch."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"This is how you shall make it. The length of the ship shall be three hundred cubits, its width fifty cubits, and its height thirty cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall make a roof in the ship, and you shall finish it to a cubit upward. You shall set the door of the ship in its side. You shall make it with lower, second, and third levels."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I, even I, will bring the flood of waters on this earth, to destroy all flesh having the breath of life from under the sky. Everything that is on the earth will die."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But I will establish my covenant with you. You shall come into the ship, you, your sons, your wife, and your sons\u2019 wives with you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Of every living thing of all flesh, you shall bring two of every sort into the ship, to keep them alive with you. They shall be male and female."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Of the birds after their kind, of the livestock after their kind, of every creeping thing of the ground after its kind, two of every sort will come to you, to keep them alive."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Take with you some of all food that is eaten, and gather it to yourself; and it will be for food for you, and for them.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Thus Noah did. He did all that God commanded him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Noah, \u201cCome with all of your household into the ship, for I have seen your righteousness before me in this generation."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall take seven pairs of every clean animal with you, the male and his female. Of the animals that are not clean, take two, the male and his female."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Also of the birds of the sky, seven and seven, male and female, to keep seed alive on the surface of all the earth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"In seven days, I will cause it to rain on the earth for forty days and forty nights. I will destroy every living thing that I have made from the surface of the ground.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Noah did everything that the LORD commanded him."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Noah was six hundred years old when the flood of waters came on the earth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Noah went into the ship with his sons, his wife, and his sons\u2019 wives, because of the floodwaters."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Clean animals, unclean animals, birds, and everything that creeps on the ground"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"went by pairs to Noah into the ship, male and female, as God commanded Noah."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"After the seven days, the floodwaters came on the earth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In the six hundredth year of Noah\u2019s life, in the second month, on the seventeenth day of the month, on that day all the fountains of the great deep burst open, and the sky\u2019s windows opened."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It rained on the earth forty days and forty nights."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"In the same day Noah, and Shem, Ham, and Japheth\u2014the sons of Noah\u2014and Noah\u2019s wife and the three wives of his sons with them, entered into the ship\u2014"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"they, and every animal after its kind, all the livestock after their kind, every creeping thing that creeps on the earth after its kind, and every bird after its kind, every bird of every sort."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Pairs from all flesh with the breath of life in them went into the ship to Noah."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Those who went in, went in male and female of all flesh, as God commanded him; then the LORD shut him in."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The flood was forty days on the earth. The waters increased, and lifted up the ship, and it was lifted up above the earth."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The waters rose, and increased greatly on the earth; and the ship floated on the surface of the waters."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The waters rose very high on the earth. All the high mountains that were under the whole sky were covered."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The waters rose fifteen cubits higher, and the mountains were covered."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"All flesh died that moved on the earth, including birds, livestock, animals, every creeping thing that creeps on the earth, and every man."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"All on the dry land, in whose nostrils was the breath of the spirit of life, died."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Every living thing was destroyed that was on the surface of the ground, including man, livestock, creeping things, and birds of the sky. They were destroyed from the earth. Only Noah was left, and those who were with him in the ship."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The waters flooded the earth one hundred fifty days."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"God remembered Noah, all the animals, and all the livestock that were with him in the ship; and God made a wind to pass over the earth. The waters subsided."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The deep\u2019s fountains and the sky\u2019s windows were also stopped, and the rain from the sky was restrained."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The waters continually receded from the earth. After the end of one hundred fifty days the waters receded."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The ship rested in the seventh month, on the seventeenth day of the month, on Ararat\u2019s mountains."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The waters receded continually until the tenth month. In the tenth month, on the first day of the month, the tops of the mountains were visible."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of forty days, Noah opened the window of the ship which he had made,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and he sent out a raven. It went back and forth, until the waters were dried up from the earth."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He himself sent out a dove to see if the waters were abated from the surface of the ground,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but the dove found no place to rest her foot, and she returned into the ship to him, for the waters were on the surface of the whole earth. He put out his hand, and took her, and brought her to him into the ship."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He waited yet another seven days; and again he sent the dove out of the ship."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The dove came back to him at evening and, behold, in her mouth was a freshly plucked olive leaf. So Noah knew that the waters were abated from the earth."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He waited yet another seven days, and sent out the dove; and she didn\u2019t return to him any more."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"In the six hundred first year, in the first month, the first day of the month, the waters were dried up from the earth. Noah removed the covering of the ship, and looked. He saw that the surface of the ground was dry."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"In the second month, on the twenty-seventh day of the month, the earth was dry."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"God spoke to Noah, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cGo out of the ship, you, your wife, your sons, and your sons\u2019 wives with you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Bring out with you every living thing that is with you of all flesh, including birds, livestock, and every creeping thing that creeps on the earth, that they may breed abundantly on the earth, and be fruitful, and multiply on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Noah went out, with his sons, his wife, and his sons\u2019 wives with him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Every animal, every creeping thing, and every bird, whatever moves on the earth, after their families, went out of the ship."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Noah built an altar to the LORD, and took of every clean animal, and of every clean bird, and offered burnt offerings on the altar."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD smelled the pleasant aroma. The LORD said in his heart, \u201cI will not again curse the ground any more for man\u2019s sake because the imagination of man\u2019s heart is evil from his youth. I will never again strike every living thing, as I have done."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"While the earth remains, seed time and harvest, and cold and heat, and summer and winter, and day and night will not cease.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"God blessed Noah and his sons, and said to them, \u201cBe fruitful, multiply, and replenish the earth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The fear of you and the dread of you will be on every animal of the earth, and on every bird of the sky. Everything that moves along the ground, and all the fish of the sea, are delivered into your hand."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Every moving thing that lives will be food for you. As I gave you the green herb, I have given everything to you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But flesh with its life, that is, its blood, you shall not eat."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I will surely require accounting for your life\u2019s blood. At the hand of every animal I will require it. At the hand of man, even at the hand of every man\u2019s brother, I will require the life of man."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Whoever sheds man\u2019s blood, his blood will be shed by man, for God made man in his own image."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Be fruitful and multiply. Increase abundantly on the earth, and multiply in it.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"God spoke to Noah and to his sons with him, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for me, behold, I establish my covenant with you, and with your offspring after you,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and with every living creature that is with you: the birds, the livestock, and every animal of the earth with you, of all that go out of the ship, even every animal of the earth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I will establish my covenant with you: All flesh will not be cut off any more by the waters of the flood. There will never again be a flood to destroy the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cThis is the token of the covenant which I make between me and you and every living creature that is with you, for perpetual generations:"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I set my rainbow in the cloud, and it will be a sign of a covenant between me and the earth."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When I bring a cloud over the earth, that the rainbow will be seen in the cloud,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I will remember my covenant, which is between me and you and every living creature of all flesh, and the waters will no more become a flood to destroy all flesh."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The rainbow will be in the cloud. I will look at it, that I may remember the everlasting covenant between God and every living creature of all flesh that is on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"God said to Noah, \u201cThis is the token of the covenant which I have established between me and all flesh that is on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Noah who went out from the ship were Shem, Ham, and Japheth. Ham is the father of Canaan."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"These three were the sons of Noah, and from these the whole earth was populated."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Noah began to be a farmer, and planted a vineyard."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He drank of the wine and got drunk. He was uncovered within his tent."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Ham, the father of Canaan, saw the nakedness of his father, and told his two brothers outside."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Shem and Japheth took a garment, and laid it on both their shoulders, went in backwards, and covered the nakedness of their father. Their faces were backwards, and they didn\u2019t see their father\u2019s nakedness."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Noah awoke from his wine, and knew what his youngest son had done to him."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He said,"],[1,"\u201cCanaan is cursed."],[2,"He will be a servant of servants to his brothers.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"He said,"],[1,"\u201cBlessed be the LORD, the God of Shem."],[2,"Let Canaan be his servant."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"May God enlarge Japheth."],[2,"Let him dwell in the tents of Shem."],[2,"Let Canaan be his servant.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Noah lived three hundred fifty years after the flood."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"All the days of Noah were nine hundred fifty years, and then he died."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this is the history of the generations of the sons of Noah and of Shem, Ham, and Japheth. Sons were born to them after the flood."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Japheth were: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The sons of Gomer were: Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The sons of Javan were: Elishah, Tarshish, Kittim, and Dodanim."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Of these were the islands of the nations divided in their lands, everyone after his language, after their families, in their nations."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Ham were: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The sons of Cush were: Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. The sons of Raamah were: Sheba and Dedan."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Cush became the father of Nimrod. He began to be a mighty one on the earth."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He was a mighty hunter before the LORD. Therefore it is said, \u201clike Nimrod, a mighty hunter before the LORD\u201d."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The beginning of his kingdom was Babel, Erech, Accad, and Calneh, in the land of Shinar."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Out of that land he went into Assyria, and built Nineveh, Rehoboth Ir, Calah,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and Resen between Nineveh and the great city Calah."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Mizraim became the father of Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Pathrusim, Casluhim (which the Philistines descended from), and Caphtorim."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Canaan became the father of Sidon (his firstborn), Heth,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the Jebusites, the Amorites, the Girgashites,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the Hivites, the Arkites, the Sinites,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"the Arvadites, the Zemarites, and the Hamathites. Afterward the families of the Canaanites were spread abroad."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The border of the Canaanites was from Sidon\u2014as you go toward Gerar\u2014to Gaza\u2014as you go toward Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboiim\u2014to Lasha."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Ham, after their families, according to their languages, in their lands and their nations."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Children were also born to Shem (the elder brother of Japheth), the father of all the children of Eber."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The sons of Shem were: Elam, Asshur, Arpachshad, Lud, and Aram."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The sons of Aram were: Uz, Hul, Gether, and Mash."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Arpachshad became the father of Shelah. Shelah became the father of Eber."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"To Eber were born two sons. The name of the one was Peleg, for in his days the earth was divided. His brother\u2019s name was Joktan."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Joktan became the father of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Obal, Abimael, Sheba,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab. All these were the sons of Joktan."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Their dwelling extended from Mesha, as you go toward Sephar, the mountain of the east."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Shem, by their families, according to their languages, lands, and nations."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the families of the sons of Noah, by their generations, according to their nations. The nations divided from these on the earth after the flood."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The whole earth was of one language and of one speech."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"As they traveled east, they found a plain in the land of Shinar, and they lived there."]],f:["LXX reads \u201cfrom the east\u201d."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They said to one another, \u201cCome, let\u2019s make bricks, and burn them thoroughly.\u201d They had brick for stone, and they used tar for mortar."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cCome, let\u2019s build ourselves a city, and a tower whose top reaches to the sky, and let\u2019s make a name for ourselves, lest we be scattered abroad on the surface of the whole earth.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD came down to see the city and the tower, which the children of men built."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cBehold, they are one people, and they all have one language, and this is what they begin to do. Now nothing will be withheld from them, which they intend to do."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Come, let\u2019s go down, and there confuse their language, that they may not understand one another\u2019s speech.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So the LORD scattered them abroad from there on the surface of all the earth. They stopped building the city."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore its name was called Babel, because there the LORD confused the language of all the earth. From there, the LORD scattered them abroad on the surface of all the earth."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the history of the generations of Shem: Shem was one hundred years old when he became the father of Arpachshad two years after the flood."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Shem lived five hundred years after he became the father of Arpachshad, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Arpachshad lived thirty-five years and became the father of Shelah."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Arpachshad lived four hundred three years after he became the father of Shelah, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Shelah lived thirty years, and became the father of Eber."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Shelah lived four hundred three years after he became the father of Eber, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Eber lived thirty-four years, and became the father of Peleg."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Eber lived four hundred thirty years after he became the father of Peleg, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Peleg lived thirty years, and became the father of Reu."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Peleg lived two hundred nine years after he became the father of Reu, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Reu lived thirty-two years, and became the father of Serug."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Reu lived two hundred seven years after he became the father of Serug, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Serug lived thirty years, and became the father of Nahor."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Serug lived two hundred years after he became the father of Nahor, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Nahor lived twenty-nine years, and became the father of Terah."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Nahor lived one hundred nineteen years after he became the father of Terah, and became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Terah lived seventy years, and became the father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this is the history of the generations of Terah. Terah became the father of Abram, Nahor, and Haran. Haran became the father of Lot."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Haran died in the land of his birth, in Ur of the Chaldees, while his father Terah was still alive."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Abram and Nahor married wives. The name of Abram\u2019s wife was Sarai, and the name of Nahor\u2019s wife was Milcah, the daughter of Haran, who was also the father of Iscah."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Sarai was barren. She had no child."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Terah took Abram his son, Lot the son of Haran, his son\u2019s son, and Sarai his daughter-in-law, his son Abram\u2019s wife. They went from Ur of the Chaldees, to go into the land of Canaan. They came to Haran and lived there."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The days of Terah were two hundred five years. Terah died in Haran."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the LORD said to Abram, \u201cLeave your country, and your relatives, and your father\u2019s house, and go to the land that I will show you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will make of you a great nation. I will bless you and make your name great. You will be a blessing."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will bless those who bless you, and I will curse him who treats you with contempt. All the families of the earth will be blessed through you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"So Abram went, as the LORD had told him. Lot went with him. Abram was seventy-five years old when he departed from Haran."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Abram took Sarai his wife, Lot his brother\u2019s son, all their possessions that they had gathered, and the people whom they had acquired in Haran, and they went to go into the land of Canaan. They entered into the land of Canaan."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Abram passed through the land to the place of Shechem, to the oak of Moreh. At that time, Canaanites were in the land."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared to Abram and said, \u201cI will give this land to your offspring.\u201d"],[0,"He built an altar there to the LORD, who had appeared to him."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He left from there to go to the mountain on the east of Bethel and pitched his tent, having Bethel on the west, and Ai on the east. There he built an altar to the LORD and called on the LORD\u2019s name."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Abram traveled, still going on toward the South."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a famine in the land. Abram went down into Egypt to live as a foreigner there, for the famine was severe in the land."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When he had come near to enter Egypt, he said to Sarai his wife, \u201cSee now, I know that you are a beautiful woman to look at."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It will happen that when the Egyptians see you, they will say, \u2018This is his wife.\u2019 They will kill me, but they will save you alive."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Please say that you are my sister, that it may be well with me for your sake, and that my soul may live because of you.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When Abram had come into Egypt, some Egyptians saw that the woman was very beautiful."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The princes of Pharaoh saw her, and praised her to Pharaoh; and the woman was taken into Pharaoh\u2019s house."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He dealt well with Abram for her sake. He had sheep, cattle, male donkeys, male servants, female servants, female donkeys, and camels."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The LORD afflicted Pharaoh and his house with great plagues because of Sarai, Abram\u2019s wife."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Pharaoh called Abram and said, \u201cWhat is this that you have done to me? Why didn\u2019t you tell me that she was your wife?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Why did you say, \u2018She is my sister,\u2019 so that I took her to be my wife? Now therefore, see your wife, take her, and go your way.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh commanded men concerning him, and they escorted him away with his wife and all that he had."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Abram went up out of Egypt\u2014he, his wife, all that he had, and Lot with him\u2014into the South."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Abram was very rich in livestock, in silver, and in gold."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He went on his journeys from the South as far as Bethel, to the place where his tent had been at the beginning, between Bethel and Ai,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"to the place of the altar, which he had made there at the first. There Abram called on the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Lot also, who went with Abram, had flocks, herds, and tents."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The land was not able to bear them, that they might live together; for their possessions were so great that they couldn\u2019t live together."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"There was strife between the herdsmen of Abram\u2019s livestock and the herdsmen of Lot\u2019s livestock. The Canaanites and the Perizzites lived in the land at that time."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Abram said to Lot, \u201cPlease, let there be no strife between you and me, and between your herdsmen and my herdsmen; for we are relatives."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t the whole land before you? Please separate yourself from me. If you go to the left hand, then I will go to the right. Or if you go to the right hand, then I will go to the left.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Lot lifted up his eyes, and saw all the plain of the Jordan, that it was well-watered everywhere, before the LORD destroyed Sodom and Gomorrah, like the garden of the LORD, like the land of Egypt, as you go to Zoar."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"So Lot chose the Plain of the Jordan for himself. Lot traveled east, and they separated themselves from one another."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Abram lived in the land of Canaan, and Lot lived in the cities of the plain, and moved his tent as far as Sodom."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now the men of Sodom were exceedingly wicked and sinners against the LORD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Abram, after Lot was separated from him, \u201cNow, lift up your eyes, and look from the place where you are, northward and southward and eastward and westward,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"for I will give all the land which you see to you and to your offspring forever."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I will make your offspring as the dust of the earth, so that if a man can count the dust of the earth, then your offspring may also be counted."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Arise, walk through the land in its length and in its width; for I will give it to you.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Abram moved his tent, and came and lived by the oaks of Mamre, which are in Hebron, and built an altar there to the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the days of Amraphel, king of Shinar; Arioch, king of Ellasar; Chedorlaomer, king of Elam; and Tidal, king of Goiim,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"they made war with Bera, king of Sodom; Birsha, king of Gomorrah; Shinab, king of Admah; Shemeber, king of Zeboiim; and the king of Bela (also called Zoar)."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All these joined together in the valley of Siddim (also called the Salt Sea)."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They served Chedorlaomer for twelve years, and in the thirteenth year they rebelled."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"In the fourteenth year Chedorlaomer and the kings who were with him came and struck the Rephaim in Ashteroth Karnaim, the Zuzim in Ham, the Emim in Shaveh Kiriathaim,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and the Horites in their Mount Seir, to El Paran, which is by the wilderness."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They returned, and came to En Mishpat (also called Kadesh), and struck all the country of the Amalekites, and also the Amorites, that lived in Hazazon Tamar."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The king of Sodom, and the king of Gomorrah, the king of Admah, the king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (also called Zoar) went out; and they set the battle in array against them in the valley of Siddim"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"against Chedorlaomer king of Elam, Tidal king of Goiim, Amraphel king of Shinar, and Arioch king of Ellasar; four kings against the five."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now the valley of Siddim was full of tar pits; and the kings of Sodom and Gomorrah fled, and some fell there. Those who remained fled to the hills."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They took all the goods of Sodom and Gomorrah, and all their food, and went their way."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They took Lot, Abram\u2019s brother\u2019s son, who lived in Sodom, and his goods, and departed."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"One who had escaped came and told Abram, the Hebrew. At that time, he lived by the oaks of Mamre, the Amorite, brother of Eshcol and brother of Aner. They were allies of Abram."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When Abram heard that his relative was taken captive, he led out his three hundred eighteen trained men, born in his house, and pursued as far as Dan."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He divided himself against them by night, he and his servants, and struck them, and pursued them to Hobah, which is on the left hand of Damascus."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He brought back all the goods, and also brought back his relative Lot and his goods, and the women also, and the other people."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Sodom went out to meet him after his return from the slaughter of Chedorlaomer and the kings who were with him, at the valley of Shaveh (that is, the King\u2019s Valley)."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Melchizedek king of Salem brought out bread and wine. He was priest of God Most High."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He blessed him, and said, \u201cBlessed be Abram of God Most High, possessor of heaven and earth."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Blessed be God Most High, who has delivered your enemies into your hand.\u201d"],[0,"Abram gave him a tenth of all."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Sodom said to Abram, \u201cGive me the people, and take the goods for yourself.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Abram said to the king of Sodom, \u201cI have lifted up my hand to the LORD, God Most High, possessor of heaven and earth,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"that I will not take a thread nor a sandal strap nor anything that is yours, lest you should say, \u2018I have made Abram rich.\u2019"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I will accept nothing from you except that which the young men have eaten, and the portion of the men who went with me: Aner, Eshcol, and Mamre. Let them take their portion.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things the LORD\u2019s word came to Abram in a vision, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, Abram. I am your shield, your exceedingly great reward.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Abram said, \u201cLord GOD, what will you give me, since I go childless, and he who will inherit my estate is Eliezer of Damascus?\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai\u201d."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Abram said, \u201cBehold, you have given no children to me: and, behold, one born in my house is my heir.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the LORD\u2019s word came to him, saying, \u201cThis man will not be your heir, but he who will come out of your own body will be your heir.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD brought him outside, and said, \u201cLook now toward the sky, and count the stars, if you are able to count them.\u201d He said to Abram, \u201cSo your offspring will be.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He believed in the LORD, who credited it to him for righteousness."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He said to Abram, \u201cI am the LORD who brought you out of Ur of the Chaldees, to give you this land to inherit it.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cLord GOD, how will I know that I will inherit it?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cBring me a heifer three years old, a female goat three years old, a ram three years old, a turtledove, and a young pigeon.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He brought him all these, and divided them in the middle, and laid each half opposite the other; but he didn\u2019t divide the birds."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The birds of prey came down on the carcasses, and Abram drove them away."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When the sun was going down, a deep sleep fell on Abram. Now terror and great darkness fell on him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He said to Abram, \u201cKnow for sure that your offspring will live as foreigners in a land that is not theirs, and will serve them. They will afflict them four hundred years."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will also judge that nation, whom they will serve. Afterward they will come out with great wealth;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but you will go to your fathers in peace. You will be buried at a good old age."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"In the fourth generation they will come here again, for the iniquity of the Amorite is not yet full.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It came to pass that, when the sun went down, and it was dark, behold, a smoking furnace and a flaming torch passed between these pieces."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In that day the LORD made a covenant with Abram, saying, \u201cI have given this land to your offspring, from the river of Egypt to the great river, the river Euphrates:"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the land of the Kenites, the Kenizzites, the Kadmonites,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Rephaim,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"the Amorites, the Canaanites, the Girgashites, and the Jebusites.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Sarai, Abram\u2019s wife, bore him no children. She had a servant, an Egyptian, whose name was Hagar."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Sarai said to Abram, \u201cSee now, the LORD has restrained me from bearing. Please go in to my servant. It may be that I will obtain children by her.\u201d Abram listened to the voice of Sarai."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Sarai, Abram\u2019s wife, took Hagar the Egyptian, her servant, after Abram had lived ten years in the land of Canaan, and gave her to Abram her husband to be his wife."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He went in to Hagar, and she conceived. When she saw that she had conceived, her mistress was despised in her eyes."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Sarai said to Abram, \u201cThis wrong is your fault. I gave my servant into your bosom, and when she saw that she had conceived, she despised me. May the LORD judge between me and you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But Abram said to Sarai, \u201cBehold, your maid is in your hand. Do to her whatever is good in your eyes.\u201d Sarai dealt harshly with her, and she fled from her face."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel found her by a fountain of water in the wilderness, by the fountain on the way to Shur."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cHagar, Sarai\u2019s servant, where did you come from? Where are you going?\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cI am fleeing from the face of my mistress Sarai.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to her, \u201cReturn to your mistress, and submit yourself under her hands.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to her, \u201cI will greatly multiply your offspring, that they will not be counted for multitude.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to her, \u201cBehold, you are with child, and will bear a son. You shall call his name Ishmael, because the LORD has heard your affliction."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He will be like a wild donkey among men. His hand will be against every man, and every man\u2019s hand against him. He will live opposed to all of his brothers.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"She called the name of the LORD who spoke to her, \u201cYou are a God who sees,\u201d for she said, \u201cHave I even stayed alive after seeing him?\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore the well was called Beer Lahai Roi. Behold, it is between Kadesh and Bered."]],f:["Beer Lahai Roi means \u201cwell of the one who lives and sees me\u201d."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Hagar bore a son for Abram. Abram called the name of his son, whom Hagar bore, Ishmael."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Abram was eighty-six years old when Hagar bore Ishmael to Abram."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Abram was ninety-nine years old, the LORD appeared to Abram and said to him, \u201cI am God Almighty. Walk before me and be blameless."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will make my covenant between me and you, and will multiply you exceedingly.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Abram fell on his face. God talked with him, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for me, behold, my covenant is with you. You will be the father of a multitude of nations."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Your name will no more be called Abram, but your name will be Abraham; for I have made you the father of a multitude of nations."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I will make you exceedingly fruitful, and I will make nations of you. Kings will come out of you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I will establish my covenant between me and you and your offspring after you throughout their generations for an everlasting covenant, to be a God to you and to your offspring after you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will give to you, and to your offspring after you, the land where you are traveling, all the land of Canaan, for an everlasting possession. I will be their God.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Abraham, \u201cAs for you, you shall keep my covenant, you and your offspring after you throughout their generations."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"This is my covenant, which you shall keep, between me and you and your offspring after you. Every male among you shall be circumcised."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall be circumcised in the flesh of your foreskin. It will be a token of the covenant between me and you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He who is eight days old shall be circumcised among you, every male throughout your generations, he who is born in the house, or bought with money from any foreigner who is not of your offspring."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He who is born in your house, and he who is bought with your money, must be circumcised. My covenant shall be in your flesh for an everlasting covenant."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The uncircumcised male who is not circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin, that soul shall be cut off from his people. He has broken my covenant.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Abraham, \u201cAs for Sarai your wife, you shall not call her name Sarai, but her name shall be Sarah."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I will bless her, and moreover I will give you a son by her. Yes, I will bless her, and she will be a mother of nations. Kings of peoples will come from her.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Abraham fell on his face, and laughed, and said in his heart, \u201cWill a child be born to him who is one hundred years old? Will Sarah, who is ninety years old, give birth?\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Abraham said to God, \u201cOh that Ishmael might live before you!\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"God said, \u201cNo, but Sarah, your wife, will bear you a son. You shall call his name Isaac. I will establish my covenant with him for an everlasting covenant for his offspring after him."]],f:["Isaac means \u201che laughs\u201d."]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As for Ishmael, I have heard you. Behold, I have blessed him, and will make him fruitful, and will multiply him exceedingly. He will become the father of twelve princes, and I will make him a great nation."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But I will establish my covenant with Isaac, whom Sarah will bear to you at this set time next year.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"When he finished talking with him, God went up from Abraham."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Abraham took Ishmael his son, all who were born in his house, and all who were bought with his money: every male among the men of Abraham\u2019s house, and circumcised the flesh of their foreskin in the same day, as God had said to him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Abraham was ninety-nine years old when he was circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Ishmael, his son, was thirteen years old when he was circumcised in the flesh of his foreskin."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"In the same day both Abraham and Ishmael, his son, were circumcised."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"All the men of his house, those born in the house, and those bought with money from a foreigner, were circumcised with him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared to him by the oaks of Mamre, as he sat in the tent door in the heat of the day."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He lifted up his eyes and looked, and saw that three men stood near him. When he saw them, he ran to meet them from the tent door, and bowed himself to the earth,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cMy lord, if now I have found favor in your sight, please don\u2019t go away from your servant."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now let a little water be fetched, wash your feet, and rest yourselves under the tree."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I will get a piece of bread so you can refresh your heart. After that you may go your way, now that you have come to your servant.\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cVery well, do as you have said.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham hurried into the tent to Sarah, and said, \u201cQuickly prepare three seahs of fine meal, knead it, and make cakes.\u201d"]],f:["1 seah is about 7 liters or 1.9 gallons or 0.8 pecks"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Abraham ran to the herd, and fetched a tender and good calf, and gave it to the servant. He hurried to dress it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He took butter, milk, and the calf which he had dressed, and set it before them. He stood by them under the tree, and they ate."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cWhere is Sarah, your wife?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cThere, in the tent.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI will certainly return to you at about this time next year; and behold, Sarah your wife will have a son.\u201d"],[0,"Sarah heard in the tent door, which was behind him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now Abraham and Sarah were old, well advanced in age. Sarah had passed the age of childbearing."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Sarah laughed within herself, saying, \u201cAfter I have grown old will I have pleasure, my lord being old also?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Abraham, \u201cWhy did Sarah laugh, saying, \u2018Will I really bear a child when I am old?\u2019"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Is anything too hard for the LORD? At the set time I will return to you, when the season comes around, and Sarah will have a son.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Sarah denied it, saying, \u201cI didn\u2019t laugh,\u201d for she was afraid."],[0,"He said, \u201cNo, but you did laugh.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The men rose up from there, and looked toward Sodom. Abraham went with them to see them on their way."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cWill I hide from Abraham what I do,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"since Abraham will surely become a great and mighty nation, and all the nations of the earth will be blessed in him?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For I have known him, to the end that he may command his children and his household after him, that they may keep the way of the LORD, to do righteousness and justice; to the end that the LORD may bring on Abraham that which he has spoken of him.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cBecause the cry of Sodom and Gomorrah is great, and because their sin is very grievous,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I will go down now, and see whether their deeds are as bad as the reports which have come to me. If not, I will know.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The men turned from there, and went toward Sodom, but Abraham stood yet before the LORD."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Abraham came near, and said, \u201cWill you consume the righteous with the wicked?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"What if there are fifty righteous within the city? Will you consume and not spare the place for the fifty righteous who are in it?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"May it be far from you to do things like that, to kill the righteous with the wicked, so that the righteous should be like the wicked. May that be far from you. Shouldn\u2019t the Judge of all the earth do right?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cIf I find in Sodom fifty righteous within the city, then I will spare the whole place for their sake.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Abraham answered, \u201cSee now, I have taken it on myself to speak to the Lord, although I am dust and ashes."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"What if there will lack five of the fifty righteous? Will you destroy all the city for lack of five?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will not destroy it if I find forty-five there.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He spoke to him yet again, and said, \u201cWhat if there are forty found there?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will not do it for the forty\u2019s sake.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cOh don\u2019t let the Lord be angry, and I will speak. What if there are thirty found there?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will not do it if I find thirty there.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cSee now, I have taken it on myself to speak to the Lord. What if there are twenty found there?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will not destroy it for the twenty\u2019s sake.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cOh don\u2019t let the Lord be angry, and I will speak just once more. What if ten are found there?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will not destroy it for the ten\u2019s sake.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD went his way as soon as he had finished communing with Abraham, and Abraham returned to his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The two angels came to Sodom at evening. Lot sat in the gate of Sodom. Lot saw them, and rose up to meet them. He bowed himself with his face to the earth,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and he said, \u201cSee now, my lords, please come into your servant\u2019s house, stay all night, wash your feet, and you can rise up early, and go on your way.\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cNo, but we will stay in the street all night.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He urged them greatly, and they came in with him, and entered into his house. He made them a feast, and baked unleavened bread, and they ate."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But before they lay down, the men of the city, the men of Sodom, surrounded the house, both young and old, all the people from every quarter."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They called to Lot, and said to him, \u201cWhere are the men who came in to you this night? Bring them out to us, that we may have sex with them.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Lot went out to them through the door, and shut the door after himself."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cPlease, my brothers, don\u2019t act so wickedly."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"See now, I have two virgin daughters. Please let me bring them out to you, and you may do to them what seems good to you. Only don\u2019t do anything to these men, because they have come under the shadow of my roof.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cStand back!\u201d Then they said, \u201cThis one fellow came in to live as a foreigner, and he appoints himself a judge. Now we will deal worse with you than with them!\u201d They pressed hard on the man Lot, and came near to break the door."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But the men reached out their hand, and brought Lot into the house to them, and shut the door."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They struck the men who were at the door of the house with blindness, both small and great, so that they wearied themselves to find the door."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The men said to Lot, \u201cDo you have anybody else here? Sons-in-law, your sons, your daughters, and whomever you have in the city, bring them out of the place:"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"for we will destroy this place, because the outcry against them has grown so great before the LORD that the LORD has sent us to destroy it.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Lot went out, and spoke to his sons-in-law, who were pledged to marry his daughters, and said, \u201cGet up! Get out of this place, for the LORD will destroy the city!\u201d"],[0,"But he seemed to his sons-in-law to be joking."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When the morning came, then the angels hurried Lot, saying, \u201cGet up! Take your wife and your two daughters who are here, lest you be consumed in the iniquity of the city.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But he lingered; and the men grabbed his hand, his wife\u2019s hand, and his two daughters\u2019 hands, the LORD being merciful to him; and they took him out, and set him outside of the city."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It came to pass, when they had taken them out, that he said, \u201cEscape for your life! Don\u2019t look behind you, and don\u2019t stay anywhere in the plain. Escape to the mountains, lest you be consumed!\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Lot said to them, \u201cOh, not so, my lord."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"See now, your servant has found favor in your sight, and you have magnified your loving kindness, which you have shown to me in saving my life. I can\u2019t escape to the mountain, lest evil overtake me, and I die."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"See now, this city is near to flee to, and it is a little one. Oh let me escape there (isn\u2019t it a little one?), and my soul will live.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cBehold, I have granted your request concerning this thing also, that I will not overthrow the city of which you have spoken."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Hurry, escape there, for I can\u2019t do anything until you get there.\u201d Therefore the name of the city was called Zoar."]],f:["Zoar means \u201clittle\u201d."]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The sun had risen on the earth when Lot came to Zoar."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then the LORD rained on Sodom and on Gomorrah sulfur and fire from the LORD out of the sky."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He overthrew those cities, all the plain, all the inhabitants of the cities, and that which grew on the ground."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But Lot\u2019s wife looked back from behind him, and she became a pillar of salt."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham went up early in the morning to the place where he had stood before the LORD."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He looked toward Sodom and Gomorrah, and toward all the land of the plain, and saw that the smoke of the land went up as the smoke of a furnace."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When God destroyed the cities of the plain, God remembered Abraham, and sent Lot out of the middle of the overthrow, when he overthrew the cities in which Lot lived."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Lot went up out of Zoar, and lived in the mountain, and his two daughters with him; for he was afraid to live in Zoar. He lived in a cave with his two daughters."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The firstborn said to the younger, \u201cOur father is old, and there is not a man on the earth to come in to us in the way of all the earth."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Come, let\u2019s make our father drink wine, and we will lie with him, that we may preserve our father\u2019s family line.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They made their father drink wine that night: and the firstborn went in, and lay with her father. He didn\u2019t know when she lay down, nor when she arose."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"It came to pass on the next day, that the firstborn said to the younger, \u201cBehold, I lay last night with my father. Let\u2019s make him drink wine again tonight. You go in, and lie with him, that we may preserve our father\u2019s family line.\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"They made their father drink wine that night also. The younger went and lay with him. He didn\u2019t know when she lay down, nor when she got up."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Thus both of Lot\u2019s daughters were with child by their father."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The firstborn bore a son, and named him Moab. He is the father of the Moabites to this day."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The younger also bore a son, and called his name Ben Ammi. He is the father of the children of Ammon to this day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham traveled from there toward the land of the South, and lived between Kadesh and Shur. He lived as a foreigner in Gerar."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Abraham said about Sarah his wife, \u201cShe is my sister.\u201d Abimelech king of Gerar sent, and took Sarah."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But God came to Abimelech in a dream of the night, and said to him, \u201cBehold, you are a dead man, because of the woman whom you have taken; for she is a man\u2019s wife.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Abimelech had not come near her. He said, \u201cLord, will you kill even a righteous nation?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t he tell me, \u2018She is my sister\u2019? She, even she herself, said, \u2018He is my brother.\u2019 I have done this in the integrity of my heart and the innocence of my hands.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to him in the dream, \u201cYes, I know that in the integrity of your heart you have done this, and I also withheld you from sinning against me. Therefore I didn\u2019t allow you to touch her."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now therefore, restore the man\u2019s wife. For he is a prophet, and he will pray for you, and you will live. If you don\u2019t restore her, know for sure that you will die, you, and all who are yours.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Abimelech rose early in the morning, and called all his servants, and told all these things in their ear. The men were very scared."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Abimelech called Abraham, and said to him, \u201cWhat have you done to us? How have I sinned against you, that you have brought on me and on my kingdom a great sin? You have done deeds to me that ought not to be done!\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Abimelech said to Abraham, \u201cWhat did you see, that you have done this thing?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham said, \u201cBecause I thought, \u2018Surely the fear of God is not in this place. They will kill me for my wife\u2019s sake.\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Besides, she is indeed my sister, the daughter of my father, but not the daughter of my mother; and she became my wife."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When God caused me to wander from my father\u2019s house, I said to her, \u2018This is your kindness which you shall show to me. Everywhere that we go, say of me, \u201cHe is my brother.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Abimelech took sheep and cattle, male servants and female servants, and gave them to Abraham, and restored Sarah, his wife, to him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Abimelech said, \u201cBehold, my land is before you. Dwell where it pleases you.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"To Sarah he said, \u201cBehold, I have given your brother a thousand pieces of silver. Behold, it is for you a covering of the eyes to all that are with you. In front of all you are vindicated.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham prayed to God. So God healed Abimelech, his wife, and his female servants, and they bore children."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For the LORD had closed up tight all the wombs of the house of Abimelech, because of Sarah, Abraham\u2019s wife."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD visited Sarah as he had said, and the LORD did to Sarah as he had spoken."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Sarah conceived, and bore Abraham a son in his old age, at the set time of which God had spoken to him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Abraham called his son who was born to him, whom Sarah bore to him, Isaac."]],f:["Isaac means \u201cHe laughs\u201d."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Abraham circumcised his son, Isaac, when he was eight days old, as God had commanded him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Abraham was one hundred years old when his son, Isaac, was born to him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Sarah said, \u201cGod has made me laugh. Everyone who hears will laugh with me.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cWho would have said to Abraham that Sarah would nurse children? For I have borne him a son in his old age.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The child grew and was weaned. Abraham made a great feast on the day that Isaac was weaned."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Sarah saw the son of Hagar the Egyptian, whom she had borne to Abraham, mocking."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore she said to Abraham, \u201cCast out this servant and her son! For the son of this servant will not be heir with my son, Isaac.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The thing was very grievous in Abraham\u2019s sight on account of his son."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"God said to Abraham, \u201cDon\u2019t let it be grievous in your sight because of the boy, and because of your servant. In all that Sarah says to you, listen to her voice. For your offspring will be named through Isaac."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will also make a nation of the son of the servant, because he is your child.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Abraham rose up early in the morning, and took bread and a container of water, and gave it to Hagar, putting it on her shoulder; and gave her the child, and sent her away. She departed, and wandered in the wilderness of Beersheba."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The water in the container was spent, and she put the child under one of the shrubs."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"She went and sat down opposite him, a good way off, about a bow shot away. For she said, \u201cDon\u2019t let me see the death of the child.\u201d She sat opposite him, and lifted up her voice, and wept."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"God heard the voice of the boy."],[0,"The angel of God called to Hagar out of the sky, and said to her, \u201cWhat troubles you, Hagar? Don\u2019t be afraid. For God has heard the voice of the boy where he is."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Get up, lift up the boy, and hold him with your hand. For I will make him a great nation.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"God opened her eyes, and she saw a well of water. She went, filled the container with water, and gave the boy a drink."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"God was with the boy, and he grew. He lived in the wilderness, and as he grew up, he became an archer."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He lived in the wilderness of Paran. His mother got a wife for him out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time, Abimelech and Phicol the captain of his army spoke to Abraham, saying, \u201cGod is with you in all that you do."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now, therefore, swear to me here by God that you will not deal falsely with me, nor with my son, nor with my son\u2019s son. But according to the kindness that I have done to you, you shall do to me, and to the land in which you have lived as a foreigner.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham said, \u201cI will swear.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Abraham complained to Abimelech because of a water well, which Abimelech\u2019s servants had violently taken away."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Abimelech said, \u201cI don\u2019t know who has done this thing. You didn\u2019t tell me, and I didn\u2019t hear of it until today.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham took sheep and cattle, and gave them to Abimelech. Those two made a covenant."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Abraham set seven ewe lambs of the flock by themselves."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Abimelech said to Abraham, \u201cWhat do these seven ewe lambs, which you have set by themselves, mean?\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou shall take these seven ewe lambs from my hand, that it may be a witness to me, that I have dug this well.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Therefore he called that place Beersheba, because they both swore an oath there."]],f:["Beersheba can mean \u201cwell of the oath\u201d or \u201cwell of seven\u201d."]},{v:32,l:[[0,"So they made a covenant at Beersheba. Abimelech rose up with Phicol, the captain of his army, and they returned into the land of the Philistines."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Abraham planted a tamarisk tree in Beersheba, and there he called on the name of the LORD, the Everlasting God."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Abraham lived as a foreigner in the land of the Philistines many days."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, God tested Abraham, and said to him, \u201cAbraham!\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cNow take your son, your only son, Isaac, whom you love, and go into the land of Moriah. Offer him there as a burnt offering on one of the mountains which I will tell you of.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham rose early in the morning, and saddled his donkey; and took two of his young men with him, and Isaac his son. He split the wood for the burnt offering, and rose up, and went to the place of which God had told him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"On the third day Abraham lifted up his eyes, and saw the place far off."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Abraham said to his young men, \u201cStay here with the donkey. The boy and I will go over there. We will worship, and come back to you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Abraham took the wood of the burnt offering and laid it on Isaac his son. He took in his hand the fire and the knife. They both went together."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Isaac spoke to Abraham his father, and said, \u201cMy father?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere I am, my son.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere is the fire and the wood, but where is the lamb for a burnt offering?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham said, \u201cGod will provide himself the lamb for a burnt offering, my son.\u201d So they both went together."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They came to the place which God had told him of. Abraham built the altar there, and laid the wood in order, bound Isaac his son, and laid him on the altar, on the wood."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Abraham stretched out his hand, and took the knife to kill his son."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel called to him out of the sky, and said, \u201cAbraham, Abraham!\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cDon\u2019t lay your hand on the boy or do anything to him. For now I know that you fear God, since you have not withheld your son, your only son, from me.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham lifted up his eyes, and looked, and saw that behind him was a ram caught in the thicket by his horns. Abraham went and took the ram, and offered him up for a burnt offering instead of his son."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Abraham called the name of that place \u201cThe LORD Will Provide\u201d. As it is said to this day, \u201cOn the LORD\u2019s mountain, it will be provided.\u201d"]],f:["or, the LORD Jireh, or, the LORD Seeing"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel called to Abraham a second time out of the sky,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and said, \u201c\u2018I have sworn by myself,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018because you have done this thing, and have not withheld your son, your only son,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"that I will bless you greatly, and I will multiply your offspring greatly like the stars of the heavens, and like the sand which is on the seashore. Your offspring will possess the gate of his enemies."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All the nations of the earth will be blessed by your offspring, because you have obeyed my voice.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So Abraham returned to his young men, and they rose up and went together to Beersheba. Abraham lived at Beersheba."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Abraham was told, \u201cBehold, Milcah, she also has borne children to your brother Nahor:"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Uz his firstborn, Buz his brother, Kemuel the father of Aram,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Chesed, Hazo, Pildash, Jidlaph, and Bethuel.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Bethuel became the father of Rebekah. These eight Milcah bore to Nahor, Abraham\u2019s brother."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"His concubine, whose name was Reumah, also bore Tebah, Gaham, Tahash, and Maacah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Sarah lived one hundred twenty-seven years. This was the length of Sarah\u2019s life."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Sarah died in Kiriath Arba (also called Hebron), in the land of Canaan. Abraham came to mourn for Sarah, and to weep for her."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Abraham rose up from before his dead and spoke to the children of Heth, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cI am a stranger and a foreigner living with you. Give me a possession of a burying-place with you, that I may bury my dead out of my sight.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Heth answered Abraham, saying to him,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cHear us, my lord. You are a prince of God among us. Bury your dead in the best of our tombs. None of us will withhold from you his tomb. Bury your dead.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham rose up, and bowed himself to the people of the land, to the children of Heth."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He talked with them, saying, \u201cIf you agree that I should bury my dead out of my sight, hear me, and entreat for me to Ephron the son of Zohar,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"that he may sell me the cave of Machpelah, which he has, which is in the end of his field. For the full price let him sell it to me among you as a possession for a burial place.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Ephron was sitting in the middle of the children of Heth. Ephron the Hittite answered Abraham in the hearing of the children of Heth, even of all who went in at the gate of his city, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cNo, my lord, hear me. I give you the field, and I give you the cave that is in it. In the presence of the children of my people I give it to you. Bury your dead.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham bowed himself down before the people of the land."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He spoke to Ephron in the audience of the people of the land, saying, \u201cBut if you will, please hear me. I will give the price of the field. Take it from me, and I will bury my dead there.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Ephron answered Abraham, saying to him,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cMy lord, listen to me. What is a piece of land worth four hundred shekels of silver between me and you? Therefore bury your dead.\u201d"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams, so 400 shekels would be about 4 kg. or 8.8 pounds."]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham listened to Ephron. Abraham weighed to Ephron the silver which he had named in the hearing of the children of Heth, four hundred shekels of silver, according to the current merchants\u2019 standard."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So the field of Ephron, which was in Machpelah, which was before Mamre, the field, the cave which was in it, and all the trees that were in the field, that were in all of its borders, were deeded"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"to Abraham for a possession in the presence of the children of Heth, before all who went in at the gate of his city."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"After this, Abraham buried Sarah his wife in the cave of the field of Machpelah before Mamre (that is, Hebron), in the land of Canaan."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The field, and the cave that is in it, were deeded to Abraham by the children of Heth as a possession for a burial place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham was old, and well advanced in age. The LORD had blessed Abraham in all things."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Abraham said to his servant, the elder of his house, who ruled over all that he had, \u201cPlease put your hand under my thigh."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will make you swear by the LORD, the God of heaven and the God of the earth, that you shall not take a wife for my son of the daughters of the Canaanites, among whom I live."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But you shall go to my country, and to my relatives, and take a wife for my son Isaac.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The servant said to him, \u201cWhat if the woman isn\u2019t willing to follow me to this land? Must I bring your son again to the land you came from?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham said to him, \u201cBeware that you don\u2019t bring my son there again."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD, the God of heaven\u2014who took me from my father\u2019s house, and from the land of my birth, who spoke to me, and who swore to me, saying, \u2018I will give this land to your offspring\u2014he will send his angel before you, and you shall take a wife for my son from there."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If the woman isn\u2019t willing to follow you, then you shall be clear from this oath to me. Only you shall not bring my son there again.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The servant put his hand under the thigh of Abraham his master, and swore to him concerning this matter."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The servant took ten of his master\u2019s camels, and departed, having a variety of good things of his master\u2019s with him. He arose, and went to Mesopotamia, to the city of Nahor."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He made the camels kneel down outside the city by the well of water at the time of evening, the time that women go out to draw water."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cLORD, the God of my master Abraham, please give me success today, and show kindness to my master Abraham."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Behold, I am standing by the spring of water. The daughters of the men of the city are coming out to draw water."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Let it happen, that the young lady to whom I will say, \u2018Please let down your pitcher, that I may drink,\u2019 then she says, \u2018Drink, and I will also give your camels a drink,\u2019\u2014let her be the one you have appointed for your servant Isaac. By this I will know that you have shown kindness to my master.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Before he had finished speaking, behold, Rebekah came out, who was born to Bethuel the son of Milcah, the wife of Nahor, Abraham\u2019s brother, with her pitcher on her shoulder."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The young lady was very beautiful to look at, a virgin. No man had known her. She went down to the spring, filled her pitcher, and came up."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The servant ran to meet her, and said, \u201cPlease give me a drink, a little water from your pitcher.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cDrink, my lord.\u201d She hurried, and let down her pitcher on her hand, and gave him a drink."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When she had finished giving him a drink, she said, \u201cI will also draw for your camels, until they have finished drinking.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"She hurried, and emptied her pitcher into the trough, and ran again to the well to draw, and drew for all his camels."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The man looked steadfastly at her, remaining silent, to know whether the LORD had made his journey prosperous or not."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"As the camels had finished drinking, the man took a golden ring of half a shekel weight, and two bracelets for her hands of ten shekels weight of gold,"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cWhose daughter are you? Please tell me. Is there room in your father\u2019s house for us to stay?\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to him, \u201cI am the daughter of Bethuel the son of Milcah, whom she bore to Nahor.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"She said moreover to him, \u201cWe have both straw and feed enough, and room to lodge in.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The man bowed his head, and worshiped the LORD."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBlessed be the LORD, the God of my master Abraham, who has not forsaken his loving kindness and his truth toward my master. As for me, the LORD has led me on the way to the house of my master\u2019s relatives.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The young lady ran, and told her mother\u2019s house about these words."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Rebekah had a brother, and his name was Laban. Laban ran out to the man, to the spring."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When he saw the ring, and the bracelets on his sister\u2019s hands, and when he heard the words of Rebekah his sister, saying, \u201cThis is what the man said to me,\u201d he came to the man. Behold, he was standing by the camels at the spring."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cCome in, you blessed of the LORD. Why do you stand outside? For I have prepared the house, and room for the camels.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The man came into the house, and he unloaded the camels. He gave straw and feed for the camels, and water to wash his feet and the feet of the men who were with him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Food was set before him to eat, but he said, \u201cI will not eat until I have told my message.\u201d"],[0,"Laban said, \u201cSpeak on.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI am Abraham\u2019s servant."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The LORD has blessed my master greatly. He has become great. The LORD has given him flocks and herds, silver and gold, male servants and female servants, and camels and donkeys."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Sarah, my master\u2019s wife, bore a son to my master when she was old. He has given all that he has to him."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"My master made me swear, saying, \u2018You shall not take a wife for my son from the daughters of the Canaanites, in whose land I live,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"but you shall go to my father\u2019s house, and to my relatives, and take a wife for my son.\u2019"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"I asked my master, \u2018What if the woman will not follow me?\u2019"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u2018The LORD, before whom I walk, will send his angel with you, and prosper your way. You shall take a wife for my son from my relatives, and of my father\u2019s house."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Then you will be clear from my oath, when you come to my relatives. If they don\u2019t give her to you, you shall be clear from my oath.\u2019"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"I came today to the spring, and said, \u2018The LORD, the God of my master Abraham, if now you do prosper my way which I go\u2014"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"behold, I am standing by this spring of water. Let it happen, that the maiden who comes out to draw, to whom I will say, \u201cPlease give me a little water from your pitcher to drink,\u201d"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"then she tells me, \u201cDrink, and I will also draw for your camels,\u201d\u2014let her be the woman whom the LORD has appointed for my master\u2019s son.\u2019"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Before I had finished speaking in my heart, behold, Rebekah came out with her pitcher on her shoulder. She went down to the spring, and drew. I said to her, \u2018Please let me drink.\u2019"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"She hurried and let down her pitcher from her shoulder, and said, \u2018Drink, and I will also give your camels a drink.\u2019 So I drank, and she also gave the camels a drink."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"I asked her, and said, \u2018Whose daughter are you?\u2019 She said, \u2018The daughter of Bethuel, Nahor\u2019s son, whom Milcah bore to him.\u2019 I put the ring on her nose, and the bracelets on her hands."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"I bowed my head, and worshiped the LORD, and blessed the LORD, the God of my master Abraham, who had led me in the right way to take my master\u2019s brother\u2019s daughter for his son."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Now if you will deal kindly and truly with my master, tell me. If not, tell me, that I may turn to the right hand, or to the left.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Laban and Bethuel answered, \u201cThe thing proceeds from the LORD. We can\u2019t speak to you bad or good."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Behold, Rebekah is before you. Take her, and go, and let her be your master\u2019s son\u2019s wife, as the LORD has spoken.\u201d"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"When Abraham\u2019s servant heard their words, he bowed himself down to the earth to the LORD."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"The servant brought out jewels of silver, and jewels of gold, and clothing, and gave them to Rebekah. He also gave precious things to her brother and her mother."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"They ate and drank, he and the men who were with him, and stayed all night. They rose up in the morning, and he said, \u201cSend me away to my master.\u201d"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"Her brother and her mother said, \u201cLet the young lady stay with us a few days, at least ten. After that she will go.\u201d"]]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t hinder me, since the LORD has prospered my way. Send me away that I may go to my master.\u201d"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cWe will call the young lady, and ask her.\u201d"]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"They called Rebekah, and said to her, \u201cWill you go with this man?\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cI will go.\u201d"]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"They sent away Rebekah, their sister, with her nurse, Abraham\u2019s servant, and his men."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"They blessed Rebekah, and said to her, \u201cOur sister, may you be the mother of thousands of ten thousands, and let your offspring possess the gate of those who hate them.\u201d"]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"Rebekah arose with her ladies. They rode on the camels, and followed the man. The servant took Rebekah, and went his way."]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"Isaac came from the way of Beer Lahai Roi, for he lived in the land of the South."]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"Isaac went out to meditate in the field at the evening. He lifted up his eyes and looked. Behold, there were camels coming."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"Rebekah lifted up her eyes, and when she saw Isaac, she got off the camel."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"She said to the servant, \u201cWho is the man who is walking in the field to meet us?\u201d"],[0,"The servant said, \u201cIt is my master.\u201d"],[0,"She took her veil, and covered herself."]]},{v:66,l:[[0,"The servant told Isaac all the things that he had done."]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"Isaac brought her into his mother Sarah\u2019s tent, and took Rebekah, and she became his wife. He loved her. So Isaac was comforted after his mother\u2019s death."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham took another wife, and her name was Keturah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"She bore him Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jokshan became the father of Sheba, and Dedan. The sons of Dedan were Asshurim, Letushim, and Leummim."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The sons of Midian were Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abida, and Eldaah. All these were the children of Keturah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Abraham gave all that he had to Isaac,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but Abraham gave gifts to the sons of Abraham\u2019s concubines. While he still lived, he sent them away from Isaac his son, eastward, to the east country."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"These are the days of the years of Abraham\u2019s life which he lived: one hundred seventy-five years."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Abraham gave up his spirit, and died at a good old age, an old man, and full of years, and was gathered to his people."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Isaac and Ishmael, his sons, buried him in the cave of Machpelah, in the field of Ephron, the son of Zohar the Hittite, which is near Mamre,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"the field which Abraham purchased from the children of Heth. Abraham was buried there with Sarah, his wife."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"After the death of Abraham, God blessed Isaac, his son. Isaac lived by Beer Lahai Roi."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this is the history of the generations of Ishmael, Abraham\u2019s son, whom Hagar the Egyptian, Sarah\u2019s servant, bore to Abraham."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"These are the names of the sons of Ishmael, by their names, according to the order of their birth: the firstborn of Ishmael, Nebaioth, then Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Mishma, Dumah, Massa,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Hadad, Tema, Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Ishmael, and these are their names, by their villages, and by their encampments: twelve princes, according to their nations."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"These are the years of the life of Ishmael: one hundred thirty-seven years. He gave up his spirit and died, and was gathered to his people."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They lived from Havilah to Shur that is before Egypt, as you go toward Assyria. He lived opposite all his relatives."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the history of the generations of Isaac, Abraham\u2019s son. Abraham became the father of Isaac."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Isaac was forty years old when he took Rebekah, the daughter of Bethuel the Syrian of Paddan Aram, the sister of Laban the Syrian, to be his wife."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Isaac entreated the LORD for his wife, because she was barren. The LORD was entreated by him, and Rebekah his wife conceived."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The children struggled together within her. She said, \u201cIf it is like this, why do I live?\u201d She went to inquire of the LORD."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The LORD said to her,"],[1,"\u201cTwo nations are in your womb."],[1,"Two peoples will be separated from your body."],[1,"The one people will be stronger than the other people."],[1,"The elder will serve the younger.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When her days to be delivered were fulfilled, behold, there were twins in her womb."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The first came out red all over, like a hairy garment. They named him Esau."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"After that, his brother came out, and his hand had hold on Esau\u2019s heel. He was named Jacob. Isaac was sixty years old when she bore them."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"The boys grew. Esau was a skillful hunter, a man of the field. Jacob was a quiet man, living in tents."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Now Isaac loved Esau, because he ate his venison. Rebekah loved Jacob."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Jacob boiled stew. Esau came in from the field, and he was famished."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Esau said to Jacob, \u201cPlease feed me with some of that red stew, for I am famished.\u201d Therefore his name was called Edom."]],f:["\u201cEdom\u201d means \u201cred\u201d."]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said, \u201cFirst, sell me your birthright.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau said, \u201cBehold, I am about to die. What good is the birthright to me?\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said, \u201cSwear to me first.\u201d"],[0,"He swore to him. He sold his birthright to Jacob."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Jacob gave Esau bread and lentil stew. He ate and drank, rose up, and went his way. So Esau despised his birthright."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a famine in the land, in addition to the first famine that was in the days of Abraham. Isaac went to Abimelech king of the Philistines, to Gerar."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared to him, and said, \u201cDon\u2019t go down into Egypt. Live in the land I will tell you about."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Live in this land, and I will be with you, and will bless you. For I will give to you, and to your offspring, all these lands, and I will establish the oath which I swore to Abraham your father."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will multiply your offspring as the stars of the sky, and will give all these lands to your offspring. In your offspring all the nations of the earth will be blessed,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"because Abraham obeyed my voice, and kept my requirements, my commandments, my statutes, and my laws.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac lived in Gerar."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The men of the place asked him about his wife. He said, \u201cShe is my sister,\u201d for he was afraid to say, \u201cMy wife\u201d, lest, he thought, \u201cthe men of the place might kill me for Rebekah, because she is beautiful to look at.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When he had been there a long time, Abimelech king of the Philistines looked out at a window, and saw, and, behold, Isaac was caressing Rebekah, his wife."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Abimelech called Isaac, and said, \u201cBehold, surely she is your wife. Why did you say, \u2018She is my sister\u2019?\u201d"],[0,"Isaac said to him, \u201cBecause I said, \u2018Lest I die because of her.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Abimelech said, \u201cWhat is this you have done to us? One of the people might easily have lain with your wife, and you would have brought guilt on us!\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Abimelech commanded all the people, saying, \u201cHe who touches this man or his wife will surely be put to death.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac sowed in that land, and reaped in the same year one hundred times what he planted. The LORD blessed him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The man grew great, and grew more and more until he became very great."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He had possessions of flocks, possessions of herds, and a great household. The Philistines envied him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now all the wells which his father\u2019s servants had dug in the days of Abraham his father, the Philistines had stopped, and filled with earth."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Abimelech said to Isaac, \u201cGo away from us, for you are much mightier than we.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac departed from there, encamped in the valley of Gerar, and lived there."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac dug again the wells of water, which they had dug in the days of Abraham his father, for the Philistines had stopped them after the death of Abraham. He called their names after the names by which his father had called them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Isaac\u2019s servants dug in the valley, and found there a well of flowing water."]],f:["Or, living. Or, fresh."]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The herdsmen of Gerar argued with Isaac\u2019s herdsmen, saying, \u201cThe water is ours.\u201d So he called the name of the well Esek, because they contended with him."]],f:["\u201cEsek\u201d means \u201ccontention\u201d."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They dug another well, and they argued over that, also. So he called its name Sitnah."]],f:["\u201cSitnah\u201d means \u201chostility\u201d."]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He left that place, and dug another well. They didn\u2019t argue over that one. So he called it Rehoboth. He said, \u201cFor now the LORD has made room for us, and we will be fruitful in the land.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cRehoboth\u201d means \u201cbroad places\u201d."]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He went up from there to Beersheba."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared to him the same night, and said, \u201cI am the God of Abraham your father. Don\u2019t be afraid, for I am with you, and will bless you, and multiply your offspring for my servant Abraham\u2019s sake.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He built an altar there, and called on the LORD\u2019s name, and pitched his tent there. There Isaac\u2019s servants dug a well."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Abimelech went to him from Gerar with Ahuzzath his friend, and Phicol the captain of his army."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Isaac said to them, \u201cWhy have you come to me, since you hate me, and have sent me away from you?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cWe saw plainly that the LORD was with you. We said, \u2018Let there now be an oath between us, even between us and you, and let\u2019s make a covenant with you,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"that you will do us no harm, as we have not touched you, and as we have done to you nothing but good, and have sent you away in peace.\u2019 You are now the blessed of the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"He made them a feast, and they ate and drank."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They rose up some time in the morning, and swore an oath to one another. Isaac sent them away, and they departed from him in peace."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The same day, Isaac\u2019s servants came, and told him concerning the well which they had dug, and said to him, \u201cWe have found water.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He called it \u201cShibah\u201d. Therefore the name of the city is \u201cBeersheba\u201d to this day."]],f:["Shibah means \u201coath\u201d or \u201cseven\u201d.","Beersheba means \u201cwell of the oath\u201d or \u201cwell of the seven\u201d"]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"When Esau was forty years old, he took as wife Judith, the daughter of Beeri the Hittite, and Basemath, the daughter of Elon the Hittite."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"They grieved Isaac\u2019s and Rebekah\u2019s spirits."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Isaac was old, and his eyes were dim, so that he could not see, he called Esau his elder son, and said to him, \u201cMy son?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cSee now, I am old. I don\u2019t know the day of my death."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please take your weapons, your quiver and your bow, and go out to the field, and get me venison."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Make me savory food, such as I love, and bring it to me, that I may eat, and that my soul may bless you before I die.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Rebekah heard when Isaac spoke to Esau his son. Esau went to the field to hunt for venison, and to bring it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Rebekah spoke to Jacob her son, saying, \u201cBehold, I heard your father speak to Esau your brother, saying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u2018Bring me venison, and make me savory food, that I may eat, and bless you before the LORD before my death.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now therefore, my son, obey my voice according to that which I command you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Go now to the flock and get me two good young goats from there. I will make them savory food for your father, such as he loves."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall bring it to your father, that he may eat, so that he may bless you before his death.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said to Rebekah his mother, \u201cBehold, Esau my brother is a hairy man, and I am a smooth man."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"What if my father touches me? I will seem to him as a deceiver, and I would bring a curse on myself, and not a blessing.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"His mother said to him, \u201cLet your curse be on me, my son. Only obey my voice, and go get them for me.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He went, and got them, and brought them to his mother. His mother made savory food, such as his father loved."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Rebekah took the good clothes of Esau, her elder son, which were with her in the house, and put them on Jacob, her younger son."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"She put the skins of the young goats on his hands, and on the smooth of his neck."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"She gave the savory food and the bread, which she had prepared, into the hand of her son Jacob."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He came to his father, and said, \u201cMy father?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere I am. Who are you, my son?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said to his father, \u201cI am Esau your firstborn. I have done what you asked me to do. Please arise, sit and eat of my venison, that your soul may bless me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac said to his son, \u201cHow is it that you have found it so quickly, my son?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cBecause the LORD your God gave me success.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac said to Jacob, \u201cPlease come near, that I may feel you, my son, whether you are really my son Esau or not.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob went near to Isaac his father. He felt him, and said, \u201cThe voice is Jacob\u2019s voice, but the hands are the hands of Esau.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He didn\u2019t recognize him, because his hands were hairy, like his brother Esau\u2019s hands. So he blessed him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cAre you really my son Esau?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBring it near to me, and I will eat of my son\u2019s venison, that my soul may bless you.\u201d"],[0,"He brought it near to him, and he ate. He brought him wine, and he drank."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"His father Isaac said to him, \u201cCome near now, and kiss me, my son.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He came near, and kissed him. He smelled the smell of his clothing, and blessed him, and said,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, the smell of my son"],[2,"is as the smell of a field which the LORD has blessed."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"God give you of the dew of the sky,"],[2,"of the fatness of the earth,"],[2,"and plenty of grain and new wine."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Let peoples serve you,"],[2,"and nations bow down to you."],[1,"Be lord over your brothers."],[2,"Let your mother\u2019s sons bow down to you."],[1,"Cursed be everyone who curses you."],[2,"Blessed be everyone who blesses you.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"As soon as Isaac had finished blessing Jacob, and Jacob had just gone out from the presence of Isaac his father, Esau his brother came in from his hunting."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He also made savory food, and brought it to his father. He said to his father, \u201cLet my father arise, and eat of his son\u2019s venison, that your soul may bless me.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac his father said to him, \u201cWho are you?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am your son, your firstborn, Esau.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac trembled violently, and said, \u201cWho, then, is he who has taken venison, and brought it to me, and I have eaten of all before you came, and have blessed him? Yes, he will be blessed.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"When Esau heard the words of his father, he cried with an exceedingly great and bitter cry, and said to his father, \u201cBless me, even me also, my father.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYour brother came with deceit, and has taken away your blessing.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIsn\u2019t he rightly named Jacob? For he has supplanted me these two times. He took away my birthright. See, now he has taken away my blessing.\u201d He said, \u201cHaven\u2019t you reserved a blessing for me?\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac answered Esau, \u201cBehold, I have made him your lord, and all his brothers I have given to him for servants. I have sustained him with grain and new wine. What then will I do for you, my son?\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau said to his father, \u201cDo you have just one blessing, my father? Bless me, even me also, my father.\u201d Esau lifted up his voice, and wept."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac his father answered him,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, your dwelling will be of the fatness of the earth,"],[1,"and of the dew of the sky from above."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"You will live by your sword, and you will serve your brother."],[1,"It will happen, when you will break loose,"],[1,"that you will shake his yoke from off your neck.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau hated Jacob because of the blessing with which his father blessed him. Esau said in his heart, \u201cThe days of mourning for my father are at hand. Then I will kill my brother Jacob.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"The words of Esau, her elder son, were told to Rebekah. She sent and called Jacob, her younger son, and said to him, \u201cBehold, your brother Esau comforts himself about you by planning to kill you."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Now therefore, my son, obey my voice. Arise, flee to Laban, my brother, in Haran."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Stay with him a few days, until your brother\u2019s fury turns away\u2014"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"until your brother\u2019s anger turns away from you, and he forgets what you have done to him. Then I will send, and get you from there. Why should I be bereaved of you both in one day?\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"Rebekah said to Isaac, \u201cI am weary of my life because of the daughters of Heth. If Jacob takes a wife of the daughters of Heth, such as these, of the daughters of the land, what good will my life do me?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac called Jacob, blessed him, and commanded him, \u201cYou shall not take a wife of the daughters of Canaan."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Arise, go to Paddan Aram, to the house of Bethuel your mother\u2019s father. Take a wife from there from the daughters of Laban, your mother\u2019s brother."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"May God Almighty bless you, and make you fruitful, and multiply you, that you may be a company of peoples,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and give you the blessing of Abraham, to you and to your offspring with you, that you may inherit the land where you travel, which God gave to Abraham.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaac sent Jacob away. He went to Paddan Aram to Laban, son of Bethuel the Syrian, the brother of Rebekah, Jacob\u2019s and Esau\u2019s mother."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Esau saw that Isaac had blessed Jacob and sent him away to Paddan Aram, to take him a wife from there, and that as he blessed him he gave him a command, saying, \u201cYou shall not take a wife of the daughters of Canaan;\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and that Jacob obeyed his father and his mother, and was gone to Paddan Aram."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Esau saw that the daughters of Canaan didn\u2019t please Isaac, his father."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So Esau went to Ishmael, and took, in addition to the wives that he had, Mahalath the daughter of Ishmael, Abraham\u2019s son, the sister of Nebaioth, to be his wife."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob went out from Beersheba, and went toward Haran."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He came to a certain place, and stayed there all night, because the sun had set. He took one of the stones of the place, and put it under his head, and lay down in that place to sleep."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He dreamed and saw a stairway set upon the earth, and its top reached to heaven. Behold, the angels of God were ascending and descending on it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Behold, the LORD stood above it, and said, \u201cI am the LORD, the God of Abraham your father, and the God of Isaac. I will give the land you lie on to you and to your offspring."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Your offspring will be as the dust of the earth, and you will spread abroad to the west, and to the east, and to the north, and to the south. In you and in your offspring, all the families of the earth will be blessed."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Behold, I am with you, and will keep you, wherever you go, and will bring you again into this land. For I will not leave you until I have done that which I have spoken of to you.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob awakened out of his sleep, and he said, \u201cSurely the LORD is in this place, and I didn\u2019t know it.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He was afraid, and said, \u201cHow awesome this place is! This is none other than God\u2019s house, and this is the gate of heaven.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob rose up early in the morning, and took the stone that he had put under his head, and set it up for a pillar, and poured oil on its top."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He called the name of that place Bethel, but the name of the city was Luz at the first."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Jacob vowed a vow, saying, \u201cIf God will be with me, and will keep me in this way that I go, and will give me bread to eat, and clothing to put on,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"so that I come again to my father\u2019s house in peace, and the LORD will be my God,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"then this stone, which I have set up for a pillar, will be God\u2019s house. Of all that you will give me I will surely give a tenth to you.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jacob went on his journey, and came to the land of the children of the east."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He looked, and saw a well in the field, and saw three flocks of sheep lying there by it. For out of that well they watered the flocks. The stone on the well\u2019s mouth was large."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"There all the flocks were gathered. They rolled the stone from the well\u2019s mouth, and watered the sheep, and put the stone back on the well\u2019s mouth in its place."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Jacob said to them, \u201cMy relatives, where are you from?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cWe are from Haran.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDo you know Laban, the son of Nahor?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cWe know him.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cIs it well with him?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cIt is well. See, Rachel, his daughter, is coming with the sheep.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBehold, it is still the middle of the day, not time to gather the livestock together. Water the sheep, and go and feed them.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cWe can\u2019t, until all the flocks are gathered together, and they roll the stone from the well\u2019s mouth. Then we will water the sheep.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was yet speaking with them, Rachel came with her father\u2019s sheep, for she kept them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When Jacob saw Rachel the daughter of Laban, his mother\u2019s brother, and the sheep of Laban, his mother\u2019s brother, Jacob went near, and rolled the stone from the well\u2019s mouth, and watered the flock of Laban his mother\u2019s brother."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Jacob kissed Rachel, and lifted up his voice, and wept."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Jacob told Rachel that he was her father\u2019s relative, and that he was Rebekah\u2019s son. She ran and told her father."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When Laban heard the news of Jacob, his sister\u2019s son, he ran to meet Jacob, and embraced him, and kissed him, and brought him to his house. Jacob told Laban all these things."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Laban said to him, \u201cSurely you are my bone and my flesh.\u201d Jacob stayed with him for a month."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Laban said to Jacob, \u201cBecause you are my relative, should you therefore serve me for nothing? Tell me, what will your wages be?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban had two daughters. The name of the elder was Leah, and the name of the younger was Rachel."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Leah\u2019s eyes were weak, but Rachel was beautiful in form and attractive."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jacob loved Rachel. He said, \u201cI will serve you seven years for Rachel, your younger daughter.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban said, \u201cIt is better that I give her to you, than that I should give her to another man. Stay with me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob served seven years for Rachel. They seemed to him but a few days, for the love he had for her."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said to Laban, \u201cGive me my wife, for my days are fulfilled, that I may go in to her.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban gathered together all the men of the place, and made a feast."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"In the evening, he took Leah his daughter, and brought her to Jacob. He went in to her."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Laban gave Zilpah his servant to his daughter Leah for a servant."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In the morning, behold, it was Leah! He said to Laban, \u201cWhat is this you have done to me? Didn\u2019t I serve with you for Rachel? Why then have you deceived me?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban said, \u201cIt is not done so in our place, to give the younger before the firstborn."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Fulfill the week of this one, and we will give you the other also for the service which you will serve with me for seven more years.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob did so, and fulfilled her week. He gave him Rachel his daughter as wife."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Laban gave Bilhah, his servant, to his daughter Rachel to be her servant."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He went in also to Rachel, and he loved also Rachel more than Leah, and served with him seven more years."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD saw that Leah was hated, and he opened her womb, but Rachel was barren."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Leah conceived, and bore a son, and she named him Reuben. For she said, \u201cBecause the LORD has looked at my affliction; for now my husband will love me.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"She conceived again, and bore a son, and said, \u201cBecause the LORD has heard that I am hated, he has therefore given me this son also.\u201d She named him Simeon."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"She conceived again, and bore a son. She said, \u201cNow this time my husband will be joined to me, because I have borne him three sons.\u201d Therefore his name was called Levi."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"She conceived again, and bore a son. She said, \u201cThis time I will praise the LORD.\u201d Therefore she named him Judah. Then she stopped bearing."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Rachel saw that she bore Jacob no children, Rachel envied her sister. She said to Jacob, \u201cGive me children, or else I will die.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob\u2019s anger burned against Rachel, and he said, \u201cAm I in God\u2019s place, who has withheld from you the fruit of the womb?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cBehold, my maid Bilhah. Go in to her, that she may bear on my knees, and I also may obtain children by her.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"She gave him Bilhah her servant as wife, and Jacob went in to her."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Bilhah conceived, and bore Jacob a son."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Rachel said, \u201cGod has judged me, and has also heard my voice, and has given me a son.\u201d Therefore she called his name Dan."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Bilhah, Rachel\u2019s servant, conceived again, and bore Jacob a second son."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Rachel said, \u201cI have wrestled with my sister with mighty wrestlings, and have prevailed.\u201d She named him Naphtali."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When Leah saw that she had finished bearing, she took Zilpah, her servant, and gave her to Jacob as a wife."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Zilpah, Leah\u2019s servant, bore Jacob a son."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Leah said, \u201cHow fortunate!\u201d She named him Gad."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Zilpah, Leah\u2019s servant, bore Jacob a second son."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Leah said, \u201cHappy am I, for the daughters will call me happy.\u201d She named him Asher."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Reuben went in the days of wheat harvest, and found mandrakes in the field, and brought them to his mother, Leah. Then Rachel said to Leah, \u201cPlease give me some of your son\u2019s mandrakes.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Leah said to her, \u201cIs it a small matter that you have taken away my husband? Would you take away my son\u2019s mandrakes, also?\u201d"],[0,"Rachel said, \u201cTherefore he will lie with you tonight for your son\u2019s mandrakes.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob came from the field in the evening, and Leah went out to meet him, and said, \u201cYou must come in to me; for I have surely hired you with my son\u2019s mandrakes.\u201d"],[0,"He lay with her that night."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"God listened to Leah, and she conceived, and bore Jacob a fifth son."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Leah said, \u201cGod has given me my hire, because I gave my servant to my husband.\u201d She named him Issachar."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Leah conceived again, and bore a sixth son to Jacob."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Leah said, \u201cGod has endowed me with a good dowry. Now my husband will live with me, because I have borne him six sons.\u201d She named him Zebulun."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Afterwards, she bore a daughter, and named her Dinah."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"God remembered Rachel, and God listened to her, and opened her womb."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"She conceived, bore a son, and said, \u201cGod has taken away my reproach.\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"She named him Joseph, saying, \u201cMay the LORD add another son to me.\u201d"]],f:["Joseph means \u201cmay he add\u201d."]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"When Rachel had borne Joseph, Jacob said to Laban, \u201cSend me away, that I may go to my own place, and to my country."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Give me my wives and my children for whom I have served you, and let me go; for you know my service with which I have served you.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban said to him, \u201cIf now I have found favor in your eyes, stay here, for I have divined that the LORD has blessed me for your sake.\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cAppoint me your wages, and I will give it.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said to him, \u201cYou know how I have served you, and how your livestock have fared with me."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For it was little which you had before I came, and it has increased to a multitude. The LORD has blessed you wherever I turned. Now when will I provide for my own house also?\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban said, \u201cWhat shall I give you?\u201d"],[0,"Jacob said, \u201cYou shall not give me anything. If you will do this thing for me, I will again feed your flock and keep it."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"I will pass through all your flock today, removing from there every speckled and spotted one, and every black one among the sheep, and the spotted and speckled among the goats. This will be my hire."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"So my righteousness will answer for me hereafter, when you come concerning my hire that is before you. Every one that is not speckled and spotted among the goats, and black among the sheep, that might be with me, will be considered stolen.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban said, \u201cBehold, let it be according to your word.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"That day, he removed the male goats that were streaked and spotted, and all the female goats that were speckled and spotted, every one that had white in it, and all the black ones among the sheep, and gave them into the hand of his sons."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He set three days\u2019 journey between himself and Jacob, and Jacob fed the rest of Laban\u2019s flocks."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob took to himself rods of fresh poplar, almond, and plane tree, peeled white streaks in them, and made the white appear which was in the rods."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He set the rods which he had peeled opposite the flocks in the watering troughs where the flocks came to drink. They conceived when they came to drink."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The flocks conceived before the rods, and the flocks produced streaked, speckled, and spotted."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Jacob separated the lambs, and set the faces of the flocks toward the streaked and all the black in Laban\u2019s flock. He put his own droves apart, and didn\u2019t put them into Laban\u2019s flock."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Whenever the stronger of the flock conceived, Jacob laid the rods in front of the eyes of the flock in the watering troughs, that they might conceive among the rods;"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"but when the flock were feeble, he didn\u2019t put them in. So the feebler were Laban\u2019s, and the stronger Jacob\u2019s."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"The man increased exceedingly, and had large flocks, female servants and male servants, and camels and donkeys."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob heard Laban\u2019s sons\u2019 words, saying, \u201cJacob has taken away all that was our father\u2019s. He has obtained all this wealth from that which was our father\u2019s.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jacob saw the expression on Laban\u2019s face, and, behold, it was not toward him as before."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Jacob, \u201cReturn to the land of your fathers, and to your relatives, and I will be with you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob sent and called Rachel and Leah to the field to his flock,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cI see the expression on your father\u2019s face, that it is not toward me as before; but the God of my father has been with me."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You know that I have served your father with all of my strength."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Your father has deceived me, and changed my wages ten times, but God didn\u2019t allow him to hurt me."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If he said, \u2018The speckled will be your wages,\u2019 then all the flock bore speckled. If he said, \u2018The streaked will be your wages,\u2019 then all the flock bore streaked."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Thus God has taken away your father\u2019s livestock, and given them to me."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"During mating season, I lifted up my eyes, and saw in a dream, and behold, the male goats which leaped on the flock were streaked, speckled, and grizzled."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The angel of God said to me in the dream, \u2018Jacob,\u2019 and I said, \u2018Here I am.\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He said, \u2018Now lift up your eyes, and behold, all the male goats which leap on the flock are streaked, speckled, and grizzled, for I have seen all that Laban does to you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I am the God of Bethel, where you anointed a pillar, where you vowed a vow to me. Now arise, get out from this land, and return to the land of your birth.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Rachel and Leah answered him, \u201cIs there yet any portion or inheritance for us in our father\u2019s house?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t we considered as foreigners by him? For he has sold us, and has also used up our money."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For all the riches which God has taken away from our father are ours and our children\u2019s. Now then, whatever God has said to you, do.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jacob rose up, and set his sons and his wives on the camels,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and he took away all his livestock, and all his possessions which he had gathered, including the livestock which he had gained in Paddan Aram, to go to Isaac his father, to the land of Canaan."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now Laban had gone to shear his sheep; and Rachel stole the teraphim that were her father\u2019s."]],f:["teraphim were household idols that may have been associated with inheritance rights to the household property."]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob deceived Laban the Syrian, in that he didn\u2019t tell him that he was running away."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So he fled with all that he had. He rose up, passed over the River, and set his face toward the mountain of Gilead."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban was told on the third day that Jacob had fled."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He took his relatives with him, and pursued him seven days\u2019 journey. He overtook him in the mountain of Gilead."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"God came to Laban the Syrian in a dream of the night, and said to him, \u201cBe careful that you don\u2019t speak to Jacob either good or bad.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban caught up with Jacob. Now Jacob had pitched his tent in the mountain, and Laban with his relatives encamped in the mountain of Gilead."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Laban said to Jacob, \u201cWhat have you done, that you have deceived me, and carried away my daughters like captives of the sword?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Why did you flee secretly, and deceive me, and didn\u2019t tell me, that I might have sent you away with mirth and with songs, with tambourine and with harp;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and didn\u2019t allow me to kiss my sons and my daughters? Now you have done foolishly."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"It is in the power of my hand to hurt you, but the God of your father spoke to me last night, saying, \u2018Be careful that you don\u2019t speak to Jacob either good or bad.\u2019"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Now, you want to be gone, because you greatly longed for your father\u2019s house, but why have you stolen my gods?\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob answered Laban, \u201cBecause I was afraid, for I said, \u2018Lest you should take your daughters from me by force.\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Anyone you find your gods with shall not live. Before our relatives, discern what is yours with me, and take it.\u201d For Jacob didn\u2019t know that Rachel had stolen them."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban went into Jacob\u2019s tent, into Leah\u2019s tent, and into the tent of the two female servants; but he didn\u2019t find them. He went out of Leah\u2019s tent, and entered into Rachel\u2019s tent."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Now Rachel had taken the teraphim, put them in the camel\u2019s saddle, and sat on them. Laban felt around all the tent, but didn\u2019t find them."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"She said to her father, \u201cDon\u2019t let my lord be angry that I can\u2019t rise up before you; for I\u2019m having my period.\u201d He searched, but didn\u2019t find the teraphim."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob was angry, and argued with Laban. Jacob answered Laban, \u201cWhat is my trespass? What is my sin, that you have hotly pursued me?"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Now that you have felt around in all my stuff, what have you found of all your household stuff? Set it here before my relatives and your relatives, that they may judge between us two."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThese twenty years I have been with you. Your ewes and your female goats have not cast their young, and I haven\u2019t eaten the rams of your flocks."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"That which was torn of animals, I didn\u2019t bring to you. I bore its loss. Of my hand you required it, whether stolen by day or stolen by night."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"This was my situation: in the day the drought consumed me, and the frost by night; and my sleep fled from my eyes."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"These twenty years I have been in your house. I served you fourteen years for your two daughters, and six years for your flock, and you have changed my wages ten times."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Unless the God of my father, the God of Abraham, and the fear of Isaac, had been with me, surely now you would have sent me away empty. God has seen my affliction and the labor of my hands, and rebuked you last night.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Laban answered Jacob, \u201cThe daughters are my daughters, the children are my children, the flocks are my flocks, and all that you see is mine! What can I do today to these my daughters, or to their children whom they have borne?"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Now come, let\u2019s make a covenant, you and I. Let it be for a witness between me and you.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob took a stone, and set it up for a pillar."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Jacob said to his relatives, \u201cGather stones.\u201d They took stones, and made a heap. They ate there by the heap."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Laban called it Jegar Sahadutha, but Jacob called it Galeed."]],f:["\u201cJegar Sahadutha\u201d means \u201cWitness Heap\u201d in Aramaic.","\u201cGaleed\u201d means \u201cWitness Heap\u201d in Hebrew."]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Laban said, \u201cThis heap is witness between me and you today.\u201d Therefore it was named Galeed"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"and Mizpah, for he said, \u201cThe LORD watch between me and you, when we are absent one from another."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"If you afflict my daughters, or if you take wives in addition to my daughters, no man is with us; behold, God is witness between me and you.\u201d"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Laban said to Jacob, \u201cSee this heap, and see the pillar, which I have set between me and you."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"May this heap be a witness, and the pillar be a witness, that I will not pass over this heap to you, and that you will not pass over this heap and this pillar to me, for harm."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"The God of Abraham, and the God of Nahor, the God of their father, judge between us.\u201d Then Jacob swore by the fear of his father, Isaac."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"Jacob offered a sacrifice in the mountain, and called his relatives to eat bread. They ate bread, and stayed all night in the mountain."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"Early in the morning, Laban rose up, and kissed his sons and his daughters, and blessed them. Laban departed and returned to his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob went on his way, and the angels of God met him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When he saw them, Jacob said, \u201cThis is God\u2019s army.\u201d He called the name of that place Mahanaim."]],f:["\u201cMahanaim\u201d means \u201ctwo camps\u201d."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob sent messengers in front of him to Esau, his brother, to the land of Seir, the field of Edom."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He commanded them, saying, \u201cThis is what you shall tell my lord, Esau: \u2018This is what your servant, Jacob, says. I have lived as a foreigner with Laban, and stayed until now."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I have cattle, donkeys, flocks, male servants, and female servants. I have sent to tell my lord, that I may find favor in your sight.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The messengers returned to Jacob, saying, \u201cWe came to your brother Esau. He is coming to meet you, and four hundred men are with him.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then Jacob was greatly afraid and was distressed. He divided the people who were with him, along with the flocks, the herds, and the camels, into two companies."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIf Esau comes to the one company, and strikes it, then the company which is left will escape.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Jacob said, \u201cGod of my father Abraham, and God of my father Isaac, the LORD, who said to me, \u2018Return to your country, and to your relatives, and I will do you good,\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I am not worthy of the least of all the loving kindnesses, and of all the truth, which you have shown to your servant; for with just my staff I crossed over this Jordan; and now I have become two companies."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Please deliver me from the hand of my brother, from the hand of Esau; for I fear him, lest he come and strike me and the mothers with the children."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You said, \u2018I will surely do you good, and make your offspring as the sand of the sea, which can\u2019t be counted because there are so many.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He stayed there that night, and took from that which he had with him a present for Esau, his brother:"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"two hundred female goats and twenty male goats, two hundred ewes and twenty rams,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"thirty milk camels and their colts, forty cows, ten bulls, twenty female donkeys and ten foals."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He delivered them into the hands of his servants, every herd by itself, and said to his servants, \u201cPass over before me, and put a space between herd and herd.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He commanded the foremost, saying, \u201cWhen Esau, my brother, meets you, and asks you, saying, \u2018Whose are you? Where are you going? Whose are these before you?\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then you shall say, \u2018They are your servant, Jacob\u2019s. It is a present sent to my lord, Esau. Behold, he also is behind us.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He commanded also the second, and the third, and all that followed the herds, saying, \u201cThis is how you shall speak to Esau, when you find him."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall say, \u2018Not only that, but behold, your servant, Jacob, is behind us.\u2019\u201d For, he said, \u201cI will appease him with the present that goes before me, and afterward I will see his face. Perhaps he will accept me.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"So the present passed over before him, and he himself stayed that night in the camp."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He rose up that night, and took his two wives, and his two servants, and his eleven sons, and crossed over the ford of the Jabbok."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He took them, and sent them over the stream, and sent over that which he had."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Jacob was left alone, and wrestled with a man there until the breaking of the day."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When he saw that he didn\u2019t prevail against him, the man touched the hollow of his thigh, and the hollow of Jacob\u2019s thigh was strained as he wrestled."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The man said, \u201cLet me go, for the day breaks.\u201d"],[0,"Jacob said, \u201cI won\u2019t let you go unless you bless me.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cWhat is your name?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cJacob\u201d."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYour name will no longer be called Jacob, but Israel; for you have fought with God and with men, and have prevailed.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob asked him, \u201cPlease tell me your name.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cWhy is it that you ask what my name is?\u201d So he blessed him there."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob called the name of the place Peniel; for he said, \u201cI have seen God face to face, and my life is preserved.\u201d"]],f:["Peniel means \u201cface of God\u201d."]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The sun rose on him as he passed over Peniel, and he limped because of his thigh."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Therefore the children of Israel don\u2019t eat the sinew of the hip, which is on the hollow of the thigh, to this day, because he touched the hollow of Jacob\u2019s thigh in the sinew of the hip."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob lifted up his eyes, and looked, and, behold, Esau was coming, and with him four hundred men. He divided the children between Leah, Rachel, and the two servants."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He put the servants and their children in front, Leah and her children after, and Rachel and Joseph at the rear."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He himself passed over in front of them, and bowed himself to the ground seven times, until he came near to his brother."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau ran to meet him, embraced him, fell on his neck, kissed him, and they wept."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He lifted up his eyes, and saw the women and the children; and said, \u201cWho are these with you?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cThe children whom God has graciously given your servant.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then the servants came near with their children, and they bowed themselves."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Leah also and her children came near, and bowed themselves. After them, Joseph came near with Rachel, and they bowed themselves."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau said, \u201cWhat do you mean by all this company which I met?\u201d"],[0,"Jacob said, \u201cTo find favor in the sight of my lord.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau said, \u201cI have enough, my brother; let that which you have be yours.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said, \u201cPlease, no, if I have now found favor in your sight, then receive my present at my hand, because I have seen your face, as one sees the face of God, and you were pleased with me."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Please take the gift that I brought to you, because God has dealt graciously with me, and because I have enough.\u201d He urged him, and he took it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau said, \u201cLet\u2019s take our journey, and let\u2019s go, and I will go before you.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said to him, \u201cMy lord knows that the children are tender, and that the flocks and herds with me have their young, and if they overdrive them one day, all the flocks will die."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Please let my lord pass over before his servant, and I will lead on gently, according to the pace of the livestock that are before me and according to the pace of the children, until I come to my lord to Seir.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Esau said, \u201cLet me now leave with you some of the people who are with me.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cWhy? Let me find favor in the sight of my lord.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So Esau returned that day on his way to Seir."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Jacob traveled to Succoth, built himself a house, and made shelters for his livestock. Therefore the name of the place is called Succoth."]],f:["succoth means shelters or booths."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob came in peace to the city of Shechem, which is in the land of Canaan, when he came from Paddan Aram; and encamped before the city."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He bought the parcel of ground where he had spread his tent, at the hand of the children of Hamor, Shechem\u2019s father, for one hundred pieces of money."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He erected an altar there, and called it El Elohe Israel."]],f:["El Elohe Israel means \u201cGod, the God of Israel\u201d or \u201cThe God of Israel is mighty\u201d."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Dinah, the daughter of Leah, whom she bore to Jacob, went out to see the daughters of the land."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Shechem the son of Hamor the Hivite, the prince of the land, saw her. He took her, lay with her, and humbled her."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His soul joined to Dinah, the daughter of Jacob, and he loved the young lady, and spoke kindly to the young lady."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Shechem spoke to his father, Hamor, saying, \u201cGet me this young lady as a wife.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jacob heard that he had defiled Dinah, his daughter; and his sons were with his livestock in the field. Jacob held his peace until they came."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Hamor the father of Shechem went out to Jacob to talk with him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The sons of Jacob came in from the field when they heard it. The men were grieved, and they were very angry, because he had done folly in Israel in lying with Jacob\u2019s daughter, a thing that ought not to be done."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Hamor talked with them, saying, \u201cThe soul of my son, Shechem, longs for your daughter. Please give her to him as a wife."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Make marriages with us. Give your daughters to us, and take our daughters for yourselves."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall dwell with us, and the land will be before you. Live and trade in it, and get possessions in it.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Shechem said to her father and to her brothers, \u201cLet me find favor in your eyes, and whatever you will tell me I will give."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Ask me a great amount for a dowry, and I will give whatever you ask of me, but give me the young lady as a wife.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Jacob answered Shechem and Hamor his father with deceit when they spoke, because he had defiled Dinah their sister,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cWe can\u2019t do this thing, to give our sister to one who is uncircumcised; for that is a reproach to us."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Only on this condition will we consent to you. If you will be as we are, that every male of you be circumcised,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"then will we give our daughters to you; and we will take your daughters to us, and we will dwell with you, and we will become one people."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But if you will not listen to us and be circumcised, then we will take our sister, and we will be gone.\u201d"]],f:["Hebrew has, literally, \u201cdaughter\u201d"]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Their words pleased Hamor and Shechem, Hamor\u2019s son."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The young man didn\u2019t wait to do this thing, because he had delight in Jacob\u2019s daughter, and he was honored above all the house of his father."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Hamor and Shechem, his son, came to the gate of their city, and talked with the men of their city, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cThese men are peaceful with us. Therefore let them live in the land and trade in it. For behold, the land is large enough for them. Let\u2019s take their daughters to us for wives, and let\u2019s give them our daughters."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Only on this condition will the men consent to us to live with us, to become one people, if every male among us is circumcised, as they are circumcised."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Won\u2019t their livestock and their possessions and all their animals be ours? Only let\u2019s give our consent to them, and they will dwell with us.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"All who went out of the gate of his city listened to Hamor, and to Shechem his son; and every male was circumcised, all who went out of the gate of his city."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"On the third day, when they were sore, two of Jacob\u2019s sons, Simeon and Levi, Dinah\u2019s brothers, each took his sword, came upon the unsuspecting city, and killed all the males."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They killed Hamor and Shechem, his son, with the edge of the sword, and took Dinah out of Shechem\u2019s house, and went away."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Jacob\u2019s sons came on the dead, and plundered the city, because they had defiled their sister."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They took their flocks, their herds, their donkeys, that which was in the city, that which was in the field,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"and all their wealth. They took captive all their little ones and their wives, and took as plunder everything that was in the house."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Jacob said to Simeon and Levi, \u201cYou have troubled me, to make me odious to the inhabitants of the land, among the Canaanites and the Perizzites. I am few in number. They will gather themselves together against me and strike me, and I will be destroyed, I and my house.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cShould he deal with our sister as with a prostitute?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Jacob, \u201cArise, go up to Bethel, and live there. Make there an altar to God, who appeared to you when you fled from the face of Esau your brother.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jacob said to his household, and to all who were with him, \u201cPut away the foreign gods that are among you, purify yourselves, and change your garments."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s arise, and go up to Bethel. I will make there an altar to God, who answered me in the day of my distress, and was with me on the way which I went.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"They gave to Jacob all the foreign gods which were in their hands, and the rings which were in their ears; and Jacob hid them under the oak which was by Shechem."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They traveled, and a terror of God was on the cities that were around them, and they didn\u2019t pursue the sons of Jacob."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Jacob came to Luz (that is, Bethel), which is in the land of Canaan, he and all the people who were with him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He built an altar there, and called the place El Beth El; because there God was revealed to him, when he fled from the face of his brother."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Deborah, Rebekah\u2019s nurse, died, and she was buried below Bethel under the oak; and its name was called Allon Bacuth."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"God appeared to Jacob again, when he came from Paddan Aram, and blessed him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"God said to him, \u201cYour name is Jacob. Your name shall not be Jacob any more, but your name will be Israel.\u201d He named him Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"God said to him, \u201cI am God Almighty. Be fruitful and multiply. A nation and a company of nations will be from you, and kings will come out of your body."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The land which I gave to Abraham and Isaac, I will give it to you, and to your offspring after you I will give the land.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"God went up from him in the place where he spoke with him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Jacob set up a pillar in the place where he spoke with him, a pillar of stone. He poured out a drink offering on it, and poured oil on it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Jacob called the name of the place where God spoke with him \u201cBethel\u201d."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"They traveled from Bethel. There was still some distance to come to Ephrath, and Rachel travailed. She had hard labor."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When she was in hard labor, the midwife said to her, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for now you will have another son.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"As her soul was departing (for she died), she named him Benoni, but his father named him Benjamin."]],f:["\u201cBenoni\u201d means \u201cson of my trouble\u201d.","\u201cBenjamin\u201d means \u201cson of my right hand\u201d."]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Rachel died, and was buried on the way to Ephrath (also called Bethlehem)."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Jacob set up a pillar on her grave. The same is the Pillar of Rachel\u2019s grave to this day."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Israel traveled, and spread his tent beyond the tower of Eder."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"While Israel lived in that land, Reuben went and lay with Bilhah, his father\u2019s concubine, and Israel heard of it."],[0,"Now the sons of Jacob were twelve."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The sons of Leah: Reuben (Jacob\u2019s firstborn), Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, and Zebulun."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The sons of Rachel: Joseph and Benjamin."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The sons of Bilhah (Rachel\u2019s servant): Dan and Naphtali."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The sons of Zilpah (Leah\u2019s servant): Gad and Asher. These are the sons of Jacob, who were born to him in Paddan Aram."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Jacob came to Isaac his father, to Mamre, to Kiriath Arba (which is Hebron), where Abraham and Isaac lived as foreigners."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The days of Isaac were one hundred eighty years."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Isaac gave up the spirit and died, and was gathered to his people, old and full of days. Esau and Jacob, his sons, buried him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this is the history of the generations of Esau (that is, Edom)."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Esau took his wives from the daughters of Canaan: Adah the daughter of Elon, the Hittite; and Oholibamah the daughter of Anah, the daughter of Zibeon, the Hivite;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and Basemath, Ishmael\u2019s daughter, sister of Nebaioth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Adah bore to Esau Eliphaz. Basemath bore Reuel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Oholibamah bore Jeush, Jalam, and Korah. These are the sons of Esau, who were born to him in the land of Canaan."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Esau took his wives, his sons, his daughters, and all the members of his household, with his livestock, all his animals, and all his possessions, which he had gathered in the land of Canaan, and went into a land away from his brother Jacob."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For their substance was too great for them to dwell together, and the land of their travels couldn\u2019t bear them because of their livestock."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Esau lived in the hill country of Seir. Esau is Edom."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the history of the generations of Esau the father of the Edomites in the hill country of Seir:"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"these are the names of Esau\u2019s sons: Eliphaz, the son of Adah, the wife of Esau; and Reuel, the son of Basemath, the wife of Esau."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The sons of Eliphaz were Teman, Omar, Zepho, and Gatam, and Kenaz."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Timna was concubine to Eliphaz, Esau\u2019s son; and she bore to Eliphaz Amalek. These are the descendants of Adah, Esau\u2019s wife."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Reuel: Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Mizzah. These were the descendants of Basemath, Esau\u2019s wife."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"These were the sons of Oholibamah, the daughter of Anah, the daughter of Zibeon, Esau\u2019s wife: she bore to Esau Jeush, Jalam, and Korah."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the chiefs of the sons of Esau: the sons of Eliphaz the firstborn of Esau: chief Teman, chief Omar, chief Zepho, chief Kenaz,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"chief Korah, chief Gatam, chief Amalek. These are the chiefs who came of Eliphaz in the land of Edom. These are the sons of Adah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Reuel, Esau\u2019s son: chief Nahath, chief Zerah, chief Shammah, chief Mizzah. These are the chiefs who came of Reuel in the land of Edom. These are the sons of Basemath, Esau\u2019s wife."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Oholibamah, Esau\u2019s wife: chief Jeush, chief Jalam, chief Korah. These are the chiefs who came of Oholibamah the daughter of Anah, Esau\u2019s wife."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Esau (that is, Edom), and these are their chiefs."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Seir the Horite, the inhabitants of the land: Lotan, Shobal, Zibeon, Anah,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Dishon, Ezer, and Dishan. These are the chiefs who came of the Horites, the children of Seir in the land of Edom."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The children of Lotan were Hori and Heman. Lotan\u2019s sister was Timna."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"These are the children of Shobal: Alvan, Manahath, Ebal, Shepho, and Onam."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"These are the children of Zibeon: Aiah and Anah. This is Anah who found the hot springs in the wilderness, as he fed the donkeys of Zibeon his father."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"These are the children of Anah: Dishon and Oholibamah, the daughter of Anah."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"These are the children of Dishon: Hemdan, Eshban, Ithran, and Cheran."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"These are the children of Ezer: Bilhan, Zaavan, and Akan."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"These are the children of Dishan: Uz and Aran."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"These are the chiefs who came of the Horites: chief Lotan, chief Shobal, chief Zibeon, chief Anah,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"chief Dishon, chief Ezer, and chief Dishan. These are the chiefs who came of the Horites, according to their chiefs in the land of Seir."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the kings who reigned in the land of Edom, before any king reigned over the children of Israel."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Bela, the son of Beor, reigned in Edom. The name of his city was Dinhabah."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Bela died, and Jobab, the son of Zerah of Bozrah, reigned in his place."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Jobab died, and Husham of the land of the Temanites reigned in his place."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Husham died, and Hadad, the son of Bedad, who struck Midian in the field of Moab, reigned in his place. The name of his city was Avith."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Hadad died, and Samlah of Masrekah reigned in his place."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Samlah died, and Shaul of Rehoboth by the river, reigned in his place."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Shaul died, and Baal Hanan the son of Achbor reigned in his place."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Baal Hanan the son of Achbor died, and Hadar reigned in his place. The name of his city was Pau. His wife\u2019s name was Mehetabel, the daughter of Matred, the daughter of Mezahab."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the names of the chiefs who came from Esau, according to their families, after their places, and by their names: chief Timna, chief Alvah, chief Jetheth,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"chief Oholibamah, chief Elah, chief Pinon,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"chief Kenaz, chief Teman, chief Mibzar,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"chief Magdiel, and chief Iram. These are the chiefs of Edom, according to their habitations in the land of their possession. This is Esau, the father of the Edomites."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob lived in the land of his father\u2019s travels, in the land of Canaan."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"This is the history of the generations of Jacob. Joseph, being seventeen years old, was feeding the flock with his brothers. He was a boy with the sons of Bilhah and Zilpah, his father\u2019s wives. Joseph brought an evil report of them to their father."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now Israel loved Joseph more than all his children, because he was the son of his old age, and he made him a tunic of many colors."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"His brothers saw that their father loved him more than all his brothers, and they hated him, and couldn\u2019t speak peaceably to him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph dreamed a dream, and he told it to his brothers, and they hated him all the more."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cPlease hear this dream which I have dreamed:"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"for behold, we were binding sheaves in the field, and behold, my sheaf arose and also stood upright; and behold, your sheaves came around, and bowed down to my sheaf.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"His brothers asked him, \u201cWill you indeed reign over us? Will you indeed have dominion over us?\u201d They hated him all the more for his dreams and for his words."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He dreamed yet another dream, and told it to his brothers, and said, \u201cBehold, I have dreamed yet another dream: and behold, the sun and the moon and eleven stars bowed down to me.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He told it to his father and to his brothers. His father rebuked him, and said to him, \u201cWhat is this dream that you have dreamed? Will I and your mother and your brothers indeed come to bow ourselves down to the earth before you?\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"His brothers envied him, but his father kept this saying in mind."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"His brothers went to feed their father\u2019s flock in Shechem."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Israel said to Joseph, \u201cAren\u2019t your brothers feeding the flock in Shechem? Come, and I will send you to them.\u201d He said to him, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cGo now, see whether it is well with your brothers, and well with the flock; and bring me word again.\u201d So he sent him out of the valley of Hebron, and he came to Shechem."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"A certain man found him, and behold, he was wandering in the field. The man asked him, \u201cWhat are you looking for?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI am looking for my brothers. Tell me, please, where they are feeding the flock.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The man said, \u201cThey have left here, for I heard them say, \u2018Let\u2019s go to Dothan.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"Joseph went after his brothers, and found them in Dothan."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They saw him afar off, and before he came near to them, they conspired against him to kill him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They said to one another, \u201cBehold, this dreamer comes."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Come now therefore, and let\u2019s kill him, and cast him into one of the pits, and we will say, \u2018An evil animal has devoured him.\u2019 We will see what will become of his dreams.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Reuben heard it, and delivered him out of their hand, and said, \u201cLet\u2019s not take his life.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Reuben said to them, \u201cShed no blood. Throw him into this pit that is in the wilderness, but lay no hand on him\u201d\u2014that he might deliver him out of their hand, to restore him to his father."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When Joseph came to his brothers, they stripped Joseph of his tunic, the tunic of many colors that was on him;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and they took him, and threw him into the pit. The pit was empty. There was no water in it."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"They sat down to eat bread, and they lifted up their eyes and looked, and saw a caravan of Ishmaelites coming from Gilead, with their camels bearing spices and balm and myrrh, going to carry it down to Egypt."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Judah said to his brothers, \u201cWhat profit is it if we kill our brother and conceal his blood?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Come, and let\u2019s sell him to the Ishmaelites, and not let our hand be on him; for he is our brother, our flesh.\u201d His brothers listened to him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Midianites who were merchants passed by, and they drew and lifted up Joseph out of the pit, and sold Joseph to the Ishmaelites for twenty pieces of silver. The merchants brought Joseph into Egypt."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Reuben returned to the pit, and saw that Joseph wasn\u2019t in the pit; and he tore his clothes."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He returned to his brothers, and said, \u201cThe child is no more; and I, where will I go?\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They took Joseph\u2019s tunic, and killed a male goat, and dipped the tunic in the blood."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They took the tunic of many colors, and they brought it to their father, and said, \u201cWe have found this. Examine it, now, and see if it is your son\u2019s tunic or not.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"He recognized it, and said, \u201cIt is my son\u2019s tunic. An evil animal has devoured him. Joseph is without doubt torn in pieces.\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Jacob tore his clothes, and put sackcloth on his waist, and mourned for his son many days."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"All his sons and all his daughters rose up to comfort him, but he refused to be comforted. He said, \u201cFor I will go down to Sheol to my son, mourning.\u201d His father wept for him."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The Midianites sold him into Egypt to Potiphar, an officer of Pharaoh\u2019s, the captain of the guard."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time, Judah went down from his brothers, and visited a certain Adullamite, whose name was Hirah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"There, Judah saw the daughter of a certain Canaanite man named Shua. He took her, and went in to her."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"She conceived, and bore a son; and he named him Er."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"She conceived again, and bore a son; and she named him Onan."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"She yet again bore a son, and named him Shelah. He was at Chezib when she bore him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Judah took a wife for Er, his firstborn, and her name was Tamar."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Er, Judah\u2019s firstborn, was wicked in the LORD\u2019s sight. So the LORD killed him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Judah said to Onan, \u201cGo in to your brother\u2019s wife, and perform the duty of a husband\u2019s brother to her, and raise up offspring for your brother.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Onan knew that the offspring wouldn\u2019t be his; and when he went in to his brother\u2019s wife, he spilled his semen on the ground, lest he should give offspring to his brother."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The thing which he did was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and he killed him also."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then Judah said to Tamar, his daughter-in-law, \u201cRemain a widow in your father\u2019s house, until Shelah, my son, is grown up;\u201d for he said, \u201cLest he also die, like his brothers.\u201d Tamar went and lived in her father\u2019s house."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"After many days, Shua\u2019s daughter, the wife of Judah, died. Judah was comforted, and went up to his sheep shearers to Timnah, he and his friend Hirah, the Adullamite."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Tamar was told, \u201cBehold, your father-in-law is going up to Timnah to shear his sheep.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"She took off the garments of her widowhood, and covered herself with her veil, and wrapped herself, and sat in the gate of Enaim, which is on the way to Timnah; for she saw that Shelah was grown up, and she wasn\u2019t given to him as a wife."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When Judah saw her, he thought that she was a prostitute, for she had covered her face."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He turned to her by the way, and said, \u201cPlease come, let me come in to you,\u201d for he didn\u2019t know that she was his daughter-in-law."],[0,"She said, \u201cWhat will you give me, that you may come in to me?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI will send you a young goat from the flock.\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cWill you give me a pledge, until you send it?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhat pledge will I give you?\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cYour signet and your cord, and your staff that is in your hand.\u201d"],[0,"He gave them to her, and came in to her, and she conceived by him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"She arose, and went away, and put off her veil from her, and put on the garments of her widowhood."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Judah sent the young goat by the hand of his friend, the Adullamite, to receive the pledge from the woman\u2019s hand, but he didn\u2019t find her."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then he asked the men of her place, saying, \u201cWhere is the prostitute, that was at Enaim by the road?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cThere has been no prostitute here.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He returned to Judah, and said, \u201cI haven\u2019t found her; and also the men of the place said, \u2018There has been no prostitute here.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Judah said, \u201cLet her keep it, lest we be shamed. Behold, I sent this young goat, and you haven\u2019t found her.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"About three months later, Judah was told, \u201cTamar, your daughter-in-law, has played the prostitute. Moreover, behold, she is with child by prostitution.\u201d"],[0,"Judah said, \u201cBring her out, and let her be burned.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When she was brought out, she sent to her father-in-law, saying, \u201cI am with child by the man who owns these.\u201d She also said, \u201cPlease discern whose these are\u2014the signet, and the cords, and the staff.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah acknowledged them, and said, \u201cShe is more righteous than I, because I didn\u2019t give her to Shelah, my son.\u201d"],[0,"He knew her again no more."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"In the time of her travail, behold, twins were in her womb."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"When she travailed, one put out a hand, and the midwife took and tied a scarlet thread on his hand, saying, \u201cThis came out first.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"As he drew back his hand, behold, his brother came out, and she said, \u201cWhy have you made a breach for yourself?\u201d Therefore his name was called Perez."]],f:["Perez means \u201cbreaking out\u201d."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Afterward his brother came out, who had the scarlet thread on his hand, and his name was called Zerah."]],f:["Zerah means \u201cscarlet\u201d or \u201cbrightness\u201d."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph was brought down to Egypt. Potiphar, an officer of Pharaoh\u2019s, the captain of the guard, an Egyptian, bought him from the hand of the Ishmaelites that had brought him down there."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD was with Joseph, and he was a prosperous man. He was in the house of his master the Egyptian."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His master saw that the LORD was with him, and that the LORD made all that he did prosper in his hand."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Joseph found favor in his sight. He ministered to him, and Potiphar made him overseer over his house, and all that he had he put into his hand."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"From the time that he made him overseer in his house, and over all that he had, the LORD blessed the Egyptian\u2019s house for Joseph\u2019s sake. The LORD\u2019s blessing was on all that he had, in the house and in the field."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He left all that he had in Joseph\u2019s hand. He didn\u2019t concern himself with anything, except for the food which he ate."],[0,"Joseph was well-built and handsome."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"After these things, his master\u2019s wife set her eyes on Joseph; and she said, \u201cLie with me.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"But he refused, and said to his master\u2019s wife, \u201cBehold, my master doesn\u2019t know what is with me in the house, and he has put all that he has into my hand."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"No one is greater in this house than I am, and he has not kept back anything from me but you, because you are his wife. How then can I do this great wickedness, and sin against God?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"As she spoke to Joseph day by day, he didn\u2019t listen to her, to lie by her, or to be with her."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"About this time, he went into the house to do his work, and there were none of the men of the house inside."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"She caught him by his garment, saying, \u201cLie with me!\u201d"],[0,"He left his garment in her hand, and ran outside."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When she saw that he had left his garment in her hand, and had run outside,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"she called to the men of her house, and spoke to them, saying, \u201cBehold, he has brought a Hebrew in to us to mock us. He came in to me to lie with me, and I cried with a loud voice."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When he heard that I lifted up my voice and cried, he left his garment by me, and ran outside.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"She laid up his garment by her, until his master came home."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"She spoke to him according to these words, saying, \u201cThe Hebrew servant, whom you have brought to us, came in to me to mock me,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and as I lifted up my voice and cried, he left his garment by me, and ran outside.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"When his master heard the words of his wife, which she spoke to him, saying, \u201cThis is what your servant did to me,\u201d his wrath was kindled."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Joseph\u2019s master took him, and put him into the prison, the place where the king\u2019s prisoners were bound, and he was there in custody."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But the LORD was with Joseph, and showed kindness to him, and gave him favor in the sight of the keeper of the prison."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The keeper of the prison committed to Joseph\u2019s hand all the prisoners who were in the prison. Whatever they did there, he was responsible for it."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The keeper of the prison didn\u2019t look after anything that was under his hand, because the LORD was with him; and that which he did, the LORD made it prosper."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, the butler of the king of Egypt and his baker offended their lord, the king of Egypt."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Pharaoh was angry with his two officers, the chief cup bearer and the chief baker."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He put them in custody in the house of the captain of the guard, into the prison, the place where Joseph was bound."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The captain of the guard assigned them to Joseph, and he took care of them. They stayed in prison many days."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They both dreamed a dream, each man his dream, in one night, each man according to the interpretation of his dream, the cup bearer and the baker of the king of Egypt, who were bound in the prison."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Joseph came in to them in the morning, and saw them, and saw that they were sad."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He asked Pharaoh\u2019s officers who were with him in custody in his master\u2019s house, saying, \u201cWhy do you look so sad today?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cWe have dreamed a dream, and there is no one who can interpret it.\u201d"],[0,"Joseph said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t interpretations belong to God? Please tell it to me.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The chief cup bearer told his dream to Joseph, and said to him, \u201cIn my dream, behold, a vine was in front of me,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and in the vine were three branches. It was as though it budded, it blossomed, and its clusters produced ripe grapes."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Pharaoh\u2019s cup was in my hand; and I took the grapes, and pressed them into Pharaoh\u2019s cup, and I gave the cup into Pharaoh\u2019s hand.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph said to him, \u201cThis is its interpretation: the three branches are three days."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Within three more days, Pharaoh will lift up your head, and restore you to your office. You will give Pharaoh\u2019s cup into his hand, the way you did when you were his cup bearer."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But remember me when it is well with you. Please show kindness to me, and make mention of me to Pharaoh, and bring me out of this house."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For indeed, I was stolen away out of the land of the Hebrews, and here also I have done nothing that they should put me into the dungeon.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When the chief baker saw that the interpretation was good, he said to Joseph, \u201cI also was in my dream, and behold, three baskets of white bread were on my head."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"In the uppermost basket there were all kinds of baked food for Pharaoh, and the birds ate them out of the basket on my head.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph answered, \u201cThis is its interpretation. The three baskets are three days."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Within three more days, Pharaoh will lift up your head from off you, and will hang you on a tree; and the birds will eat your flesh from off you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"On the third day, which was Pharaoh\u2019s birthday, he made a feast for all his servants, and he lifted up the head of the chief cup bearer and the head of the chief baker among his servants."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He restored the chief cup bearer to his position again, and he gave the cup into Pharaoh\u2019s hand;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"but he hanged the chief baker, as Joseph had interpreted to them."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Yet the chief cup bearer didn\u2019t remember Joseph, but forgot him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of two full years, Pharaoh dreamed, and behold, he stood by the river."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, seven cattle came up out of the river. They were sleek and fat, and they fed in the marsh grass."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Behold, seven other cattle came up after them out of the river, ugly and thin, and stood by the other cattle on the brink of the river."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The ugly and thin cattle ate up the seven sleek and fat cattle. So Pharaoh awoke."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He slept and dreamed a second time; and behold, seven heads of grain came up on one stalk, healthy and good."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Behold, seven heads of grain, thin and blasted with the east wind, sprung up after them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The thin heads of grain swallowed up the seven healthy and full ears. Pharaoh awoke, and behold, it was a dream."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"In the morning, his spirit was troubled, and he sent and called for all of Egypt\u2019s magicians and wise men. Pharaoh told them his dreams, but there was no one who could interpret them to Pharaoh."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the chief cup bearer spoke to Pharaoh, saying, \u201cI remember my faults today."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Pharaoh was angry with his servants, and put me in custody in the house of the captain of the guard, with the chief baker."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"We dreamed a dream in one night, he and I. Each man dreamed according to the interpretation of his dream."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"There was with us there a young man, a Hebrew, servant to the captain of the guard, and we told him, and he interpreted to us our dreams. He interpreted to each man according to his dream."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"As he interpreted to us, so it was. He restored me to my office, and he hanged him.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Pharaoh sent and called Joseph, and they brought him hastily out of the dungeon. He shaved himself, changed his clothing, and came in to Pharaoh."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to Joseph, \u201cI have dreamed a dream, and there is no one who can interpret it. I have heard it said of you, that when you hear a dream you can interpret it.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph answered Pharaoh, saying, \u201cIt isn\u2019t in me. God will give Pharaoh an answer of peace.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh spoke to Joseph, \u201cIn my dream, behold, I stood on the brink of the river;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and behold, seven fat and sleek cattle came up out of the river. They fed in the marsh grass;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and behold, seven other cattle came up after them, poor and very ugly and thin, such as I never saw in all the land of Egypt for ugliness."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The thin and ugly cattle ate up the first seven fat cattle;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and when they had eaten them up, it couldn\u2019t be known that they had eaten them, but they were still ugly, as at the beginning. So I awoke."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I saw in my dream, and behold, seven heads of grain came up on one stalk, full and good;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and behold, seven heads of grain, withered, thin, and blasted with the east wind, sprung up after them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The thin heads of grain swallowed up the seven good heads of grain. I told it to the magicians, but there was no one who could explain it to me.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph said to Pharaoh, \u201cThe dream of Pharaoh is one. What God is about to do he has declared to Pharaoh."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The seven good cattle are seven years; and the seven good heads of grain are seven years. The dream is one."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The seven thin and ugly cattle that came up after them are seven years, and also the seven empty heads of grain blasted with the east wind; they will be seven years of famine."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"That is the thing which I have spoken to Pharaoh. God has shown Pharaoh what he is about to do."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Behold, seven years of great plenty throughout all the land of Egypt are coming."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Seven years of famine will arise after them, and all the plenty will be forgotten in the land of Egypt. The famine will consume the land,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and the plenty will not be known in the land by reason of that famine which follows; for it will be very grievous."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The dream was doubled to Pharaoh, because the thing is established by God, and God will shortly bring it to pass."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore let Pharaoh look for a discreet and wise man, and set him over the land of Egypt."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Let Pharaoh do this, and let him appoint overseers over the land, and take up the fifth part of the land of Egypt\u2019s produce in the seven plenteous years."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Let them gather all the food of these good years that come, and store grain under the hand of Pharaoh for food in the cities, and let them keep it."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The food will be to supply the land against the seven years of famine, which will be in the land of Egypt; so that the land will not perish through the famine.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"The thing was good in the eyes of Pharaoh, and in the eyes of all his servants."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to his servants, \u201cCan we find such a one as this, a man in whom is the Spirit of God?\u201d"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to Joseph, \u201cBecause God has shown you all of this, there is no one so discreet and wise as you."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"You shall be over my house. All my people will be ruled according to your word. Only in the throne I will be greater than you.\u201d"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to Joseph, \u201cBehold, I have set you over all the land of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Pharaoh took off his signet ring from his hand, and put it on Joseph\u2019s hand, and arrayed him in robes of fine linen, and put a gold chain about his neck."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He made him ride in the second chariot which he had. They cried before him, \u201cBow the knee!\u201d He set him over all the land of Egypt."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to Joseph, \u201cI am Pharaoh. Without you, no man shall lift up his hand or his foot in all the land of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Pharaoh called Joseph\u2019s name Zaphenath-Paneah. He gave him Asenath, the daughter of Potiphera priest of On as a wife. Joseph went out over the land of Egypt."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph was thirty years old when he stood before Pharaoh king of Egypt. Joseph went out from the presence of Pharaoh, and went throughout all the land of Egypt."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"In the seven plenteous years the earth produced abundantly."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He gathered up all the food of the seven years which were in the land of Egypt, and laid up the food in the cities. He stored food in each city from the fields around that city."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Joseph laid up grain as the sand of the sea, very much, until he stopped counting, for it was without number."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"To Joseph were born two sons before the year of famine came, whom Asenath, the daughter of Potiphera priest of On, bore to him."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Joseph called the name of the firstborn Manasseh, \u201cFor\u201d, he said, \u201cGod has made me forget all my toil, and all my father\u2019s house.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cManasseh\u201d sounds like the Hebrew for \u201cforget\u201d."]},{v:52,l:[[0,"The name of the second, he called Ephraim: \u201cFor God has made me fruitful in the land of my affliction.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cEphraim\u201d sounds like the Hebrew for \u201ctwice fruitful\u201d."]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"The seven years of plenty, that were in the land of Egypt, came to an end."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"The seven years of famine began to come, just as Joseph had said. There was famine in all lands, but in all the land of Egypt there was bread."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"When all the land of Egypt was famished, the people cried to Pharaoh for bread, and Pharaoh said to all the Egyptians, \u201cGo to Joseph. What he says to you, do.\u201d"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"The famine was over all the surface of the earth. Joseph opened all the store houses, and sold to the Egyptians. The famine was severe in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"All countries came into Egypt, to Joseph, to buy grain, because the famine was severe in all the earth."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jacob saw that there was grain in Egypt, and Jacob said to his sons, \u201cWhy do you look at one another?\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBehold, I have heard that there is grain in Egypt. Go down there, and buy for us from there, so that we may live, and not die.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Joseph\u2019s ten brothers went down to buy grain from Egypt."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But Jacob didn\u2019t send Benjamin, Joseph\u2019s brother, with his brothers; for he said, \u201cLest perhaps harm happen to him.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The sons of Israel came to buy among those who came, for the famine was in the land of Canaan."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Joseph was the governor over the land. It was he who sold to all the people of the land. Joseph\u2019s brothers came, and bowed themselves down to him with their faces to the earth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Joseph saw his brothers, and he recognized them, but acted like a stranger to them, and spoke roughly with them. He said to them, \u201cWhere did you come from?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cFrom the land of Canaan, to buy food.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph recognized his brothers, but they didn\u2019t recognize him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Joseph remembered the dreams which he dreamed about them, and said to them, \u201cYou are spies! You have come to see the nakedness of the land.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cNo, my lord, but your servants have come to buy food."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"We are all one man\u2019s sons; we are honest men. Your servants are not spies.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cNo, but you have come to see the nakedness of the land!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cWe, your servants, are twelve brothers, the sons of one man in the land of Canaan; and behold, the youngest is today with our father, and one is no more.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph said to them, \u201cIt is like I told you, saying, \u2018You are spies!\u2019"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"By this you shall be tested. By the life of Pharaoh, you shall not go out from here, unless your youngest brother comes here."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Send one of you, and let him get your brother, and you shall be bound, that your words may be tested, whether there is truth in you, or else by the life of Pharaoh surely you are spies.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He put them all together into custody for three days."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph said to them the third day, \u201cDo this, and live, for I fear God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"If you are honest men, then let one of your brothers be bound in your prison; but you go, carry grain for the famine of your houses."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Bring your youngest brother to me; so will your words be verified, and you won\u2019t die.\u201d"],[0,"They did so."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They said to one another, \u201cWe are certainly guilty concerning our brother, in that we saw the distress of his soul, when he begged us, and we wouldn\u2019t listen. Therefore this distress has come upon us.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Reuben answered them, saying, \u201cDidn\u2019t I tell you, saying, \u2018Don\u2019t sin against the child,\u2019 and you wouldn\u2019t listen? Therefore also, behold, his blood is required.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t know that Joseph understood them; for there was an interpreter between them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He turned himself away from them, and wept. Then he returned to them, and spoke to them, and took Simeon from among them, and bound him before their eyes."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Then Joseph gave a command to fill their bags with grain, and to restore each man\u2019s money into his sack, and to give them food for the way. So it was done to them."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"They loaded their donkeys with their grain, and departed from there."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"As one of them opened his sack to give his donkey food in the lodging place, he saw his money. Behold, it was in the mouth of his sack."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He said to his brothers, \u201cMy money is restored! Behold, it is in my sack!\u201d Their hearts failed them, and they turned trembling to one another, saying, \u201cWhat is this that God has done to us?\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They came to Jacob their father, to the land of Canaan, and told him all that had happened to them, saying,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"\u201cThe man, the lord of the land, spoke roughly with us, and took us for spies of the country."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"We said to him, \u2018We are honest men. We are no spies."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"We are twelve brothers, sons of our father; one is no more, and the youngest is today with our father in the land of Canaan.\u2019"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The man, the lord of the land, said to us, \u2018By this I will know that you are honest men: leave one of your brothers with me, and take grain for the famine of your houses, and go your way."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Bring your youngest brother to me. Then I will know that you are not spies, but that you are honest men. So I will deliver your brother to you, and you shall trade in the land.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"As they emptied their sacks, behold, each man\u2019s bundle of money was in his sack. When they and their father saw their bundles of money, they were afraid."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Jacob, their father, said to them, \u201cYou have bereaved me of my children! Joseph is no more, Simeon is no more, and you want to take Benjamin away. All these things are against me.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Reuben spoke to his father, saying, \u201cKill my two sons, if I don\u2019t bring him to you. Entrust him to my care, and I will bring him to you again.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cMy son shall not go down with you; for his brother is dead, and he only is left. If harm happens to him along the way in which you go, then you will bring down my gray hairs with sorrow to Sheol.\u201d"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The famine was severe in the land."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When they had eaten up the grain which they had brought out of Egypt, their father said to them, \u201cGo again, buy us a little more food.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah spoke to him, saying, \u201cThe man solemnly warned us, saying, \u2018You shall not see my face, unless your brother is with you.\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If you\u2019ll send our brother with us, we\u2019ll go down and buy you food;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"but if you don\u2019t send him, we won\u2019t go down, for the man said to us, \u2018You shall not see my face, unless your brother is with you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel said, \u201cWhy did you treat me so badly, telling the man that you had another brother?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThe man asked directly concerning ourselves, and concerning our relatives, saying, \u2018Is your father still alive? Have you another brother?\u2019 We just answered his questions. Is there any way we could know that he would say, \u2018Bring your brother down\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah said to Israel, his father, \u201cSend the boy with me, and we\u2019ll get up and go, so that we may live, and not die, both we, and you, and also our little ones."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I\u2019ll be collateral for him. From my hand will you require him. If I don\u2019t bring him to you, and set him before you, then let me bear the blame forever;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for if we hadn\u2019t delayed, surely we would have returned a second time by now.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Their father, Israel, said to them, \u201cIf it must be so, then do this: Take from the choice fruits of the land in your bags, and carry down a present for the man, a little balm, a little honey, spices and myrrh, nuts, and almonds;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and take double money in your hand, and take back the money that was returned in the mouth of your sacks. Perhaps it was an oversight."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Take your brother also, get up, and return to the man."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"May God Almighty give you mercy before the man, that he may release to you your other brother and Benjamin. If I am bereaved of my children, I am bereaved.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The men took that present, and they took double money in their hand, and Benjamin; and got up, went down to Egypt, and stood before Joseph."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When Joseph saw Benjamin with them, he said to the steward of his house, \u201cBring the men into the house, and butcher an animal, and prepare; for the men will dine with me at noon.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The man did as Joseph commanded, and the man brought the men to Joseph\u2019s house."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The men were afraid, because they were brought to Joseph\u2019s house; and they said, \u201cBecause of the money that was returned in our sacks the first time, we\u2019re brought in; that he may seek occasion against us, attack us, and seize us as slaves, along with our donkeys.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They came near to the steward of Joseph\u2019s house, and they spoke to him at the door of the house,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cOh, my lord, we indeed came down the first time to buy food."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When we came to the lodging place, we opened our sacks, and behold, each man\u2019s money was in the mouth of his sack, our money in full weight. We have brought it back in our hand."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"We have brought down other money in our hand to buy food. We don\u2019t know who put our money in our sacks.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cPeace be to you. Don\u2019t be afraid. Your God, and the God of your father, has given you treasure in your sacks. I received your money.\u201d He brought Simeon out to them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The man brought the men into Joseph\u2019s house, and gave them water, and they washed their feet. He gave their donkeys fodder."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They prepared the present for Joseph\u2019s coming at noon, for they heard that they should eat bread there."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joseph came home, they brought him the present which was in their hand into the house, and bowed themselves down to the earth before him."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He asked them of their welfare, and said, \u201cIs your father well, the old man of whom you spoke? Is he yet alive?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cYour servant, our father, is well. He is still alive.\u201d They bowed down humbly."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He lifted up his eyes, and saw Benjamin, his brother, his mother\u2019s son, and said, \u201cIs this your youngest brother, of whom you spoke to me?\u201d He said, \u201cGod be gracious to you, my son.\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Joseph hurried, for his heart yearned over his brother; and he sought a place to weep. He entered into his room, and wept there."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He washed his face, and came out. He controlled himself, and said, \u201cServe the meal.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"They served him by himself, and them by themselves, and the Egyptians who ate with him by themselves, because the Egyptians don\u2019t eat with the Hebrews, for that is an abomination to the Egyptians."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They sat before him, the firstborn according to his birthright, and the youngest according to his youth, and the men marveled with one another."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He sent portions to them from before him, but Benjamin\u2019s portion was five times as much as any of theirs. They drank, and were merry with him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He commanded the steward of his house, saying, \u201cFill the men\u2019s sacks with food, as much as they can carry, and put each man\u2019s money in his sack\u2019s mouth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Put my cup, the silver cup, in the sack\u2019s mouth of the youngest, with his grain money.\u201d He did according to the word that Joseph had spoken."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"As soon as the morning was light, the men were sent away, they and their donkeys."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When they had gone out of the city, and were not yet far off, Joseph said to his steward, \u201cUp, follow after the men. When you overtake them, ask them, \u2018Why have you rewarded evil for good?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t this that from which my lord drinks, and by which he indeed divines? You have done evil in so doing.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He overtook them, and he spoke these words to them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cWhy does my lord speak such words as these? Far be it from your servants that they should do such a thing!"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, the money, which we found in our sacks\u2019 mouths, we brought again to you out of the land of Canaan. How then should we steal silver or gold out of your lord\u2019s house?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"With whomever of your servants it is found, let him die, and we also will be my lord\u2019s slaves.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cNow also let it be according to your words. He with whom it is found will be my slave; and you will be blameless.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they hurried, and each man took his sack down to the ground, and each man opened his sack."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He searched, beginning with the oldest, and ending at the youngest. The cup was found in Benjamin\u2019s sack."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then they tore their clothes, and each man loaded his donkey, and returned to the city."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah and his brothers came to Joseph\u2019s house, and he was still there. They fell on the ground before him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Joseph said to them, \u201cWhat deed is this that you have done? Don\u2019t you know that such a man as I can indeed do divination?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah said, \u201cWhat will we tell my lord? What will we speak? How will we clear ourselves? God has found out the iniquity of your servants. Behold, we are my lord\u2019s slaves, both we and he also in whose hand the cup is found.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cFar be it from me that I should do so. The man in whose hand the cup is found, he will be my slave; but as for you, go up in peace to your father.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Judah came near to him, and said, \u201cOh, my lord, please let your servant speak a word in my lord\u2019s ears, and don\u2019t let your anger burn against your servant; for you are even as Pharaoh."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"My lord asked his servants, saying, \u2018Have you a father, or a brother?\u2019"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"We said to my lord, \u2018We have a father, an old man, and a child of his old age, a little one; and his brother is dead, and he alone is left of his mother; and his father loves him.\u2019"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You said to your servants, \u2018Bring him down to me, that I may set my eyes on him.\u2019"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"We said to my lord, \u2018The boy can\u2019t leave his father, for if he should leave his father, his father would die.\u2019"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You said to your servants, \u2018Unless your youngest brother comes down with you, you will see my face no more.\u2019"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When we came up to your servant my father, we told him the words of my lord."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Our father said, \u2018Go again and buy us a little food.\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"We said, \u2018We can\u2019t go down. If our youngest brother is with us, then we will go down: for we may not see the man\u2019s face, unless our youngest brother is with us.\u2019"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Your servant, my father, said to us, \u2018You know that my wife bore me two sons."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"One went out from me, and I said, \u201cSurely he is torn in pieces;\u201d and I haven\u2019t seen him since."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"If you take this one also from me, and harm happens to him, you will bring down my gray hairs with sorrow to Sheol.\u2019"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Now therefore when I come to your servant my father, and the boy is not with us; since his life is bound up in the boy\u2019s life;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"it will happen, when he sees that the boy is no more, that he will die. Your servants will bring down the gray hairs of your servant, our father, with sorrow to Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For your servant became collateral for the boy to my father, saying, \u2018If I don\u2019t bring him to you, then I will bear the blame to my father forever.\u2019"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please let your servant stay instead of the boy, my lord\u2019s slave; and let the boy go up with his brothers."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For how will I go up to my father, if the boy isn\u2019t with me?\u2014lest I see the evil that will come on my father.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joseph couldn\u2019t control himself before all those who stood before him, and he called out, \u201cCause everyone to go out from me!\u201d No one else stood with him, while Joseph made himself known to his brothers."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He wept aloud. The Egyptians heard, and the house of Pharaoh heard."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Joseph said to his brothers, \u201cI am Joseph! Does my father still live?\u201d"],[0,"His brothers couldn\u2019t answer him; for they were terrified at his presence."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Joseph said to his brothers, \u201cCome near to me, please.\u201d"],[0,"They came near. He said, \u201cI am Joseph, your brother, whom you sold into Egypt."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now don\u2019t be grieved, nor angry with yourselves, that you sold me here, for God sent me before you to preserve life."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For these two years the famine has been in the land, and there are yet five years, in which there will be no plowing and no harvest."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"God sent me before you to preserve for you a remnant on the earth, and to save you alive by a great deliverance."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So now it wasn\u2019t you who sent me here, but God, and he has made me a father to Pharaoh, lord of all his house, and ruler over all the land of Egypt."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Hurry, and go up to my father, and tell him, \u2018This is what your son Joseph says, \u201cGod has made me lord of all Egypt. Come down to me. Don\u2019t wait."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall dwell in the land of Goshen, and you will be near to me, you, your children, your children\u2019s children, your flocks, your herds, and all that you have."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"There I will provide for you; for there are yet five years of famine; lest you come to poverty, you, and your household, and all that you have.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Behold, your eyes see, and the eyes of my brother Benjamin, that it is my mouth that speaks to you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall tell my father of all my glory in Egypt, and of all that you have seen. You shall hurry and bring my father down here.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He fell on his brother Benjamin\u2019s neck and wept, and Benjamin wept on his neck."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He kissed all his brothers, and wept on them. After that his brothers talked with him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The report of it was heard in Pharaoh\u2019s house, saying, \u201cJoseph\u2019s brothers have come.\u201d It pleased Pharaoh well, and his servants."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to Joseph, \u201cTell your brothers, \u2018Do this: Load your animals, and go, travel to the land of Canaan."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Take your father and your households, and come to me, and I will give you the good of the land of Egypt, and you will eat the fat of the land.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now you are commanded to do this: Take wagons out of the land of Egypt for your little ones, and for your wives, and bring your father, and come."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Also, don\u2019t concern yourselves about your belongings, for the good of all the land of Egypt is yours.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Israel did so. Joseph gave them wagons, according to the commandment of Pharaoh, and gave them provision for the way."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He gave each one of them changes of clothing, but to Benjamin he gave three hundred pieces of silver and five changes of clothing."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He sent the following to his father: ten donkeys loaded with the good things of Egypt, and ten female donkeys loaded with grain and bread and provision for his father by the way."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"So he sent his brothers away, and they departed. He said to them, \u201cSee that you don\u2019t quarrel on the way.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"They went up out of Egypt, and came into the land of Canaan, to Jacob their father."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They told him, saying, \u201cJoseph is still alive, and he is ruler over all the land of Egypt.\u201d His heart fainted, for he didn\u2019t believe them."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They told him all the words of Joseph, which he had said to them. When he saw the wagons which Joseph had sent to carry him, the spirit of Jacob, their father, revived."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Israel said, \u201cIt is enough. Joseph my son is still alive. I will go and see him before I die.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel traveled with all that he had, and came to Beersheba, and offered sacrifices to the God of his father, Isaac."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"God spoke to Israel in the visions of the night, and said, \u201cJacob, Jacob!\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI am God, the God of your father. Don\u2019t be afraid to go down into Egypt, for there I will make of you a great nation."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will go down with you into Egypt. I will also surely bring you up again. Joseph\u2019s hand will close your eyes.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob rose up from Beersheba, and the sons of Israel carried Jacob, their father, their little ones, and their wives, in the wagons which Pharaoh had sent to carry him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They took their livestock, and their goods, which they had gotten in the land of Canaan, and came into Egypt\u2014Jacob, and all his offspring with him,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"his sons, and his sons\u2019 sons with him, his daughters, and his sons\u2019 daughters, and he brought all his offspring with him into Egypt."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the names of the children of Israel, who came into Egypt, Jacob and his sons: Reuben, Jacob\u2019s firstborn."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The sons of Reuben: Hanoch, Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The sons of Simeon: Jemuel, Jamin, Ohad, Jachin, Zohar, and Shaul the son of a Canaanite woman."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The sons of Judah: Er, Onan, Shelah, Perez, and Zerah; but Er and Onan died in the land of Canaan. The sons of Perez were Hezron and Hamul."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The sons of Issachar: Tola, Puvah, Iob, and Shimron."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The sons of Zebulun: Sered, Elon, and Jahleel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Leah, whom she bore to Jacob in Paddan Aram, with his daughter Dinah. All the souls of his sons and his daughters were thirty-three."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The sons of Gad: Ziphion, Haggi, Shuni, Ezbon, Eri, Arodi, and Areli."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The sons of Asher: Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi, Beriah, and Serah their sister. The sons of Beriah: Heber and Malchiel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Zilpah, whom Laban gave to Leah, his daughter, and these she bore to Jacob, even sixteen souls."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of Rachel, Jacob\u2019s wife: Joseph and Benjamin."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"To Joseph in the land of Egypt were born Manasseh and Ephraim, whom Asenath, the daughter of Potiphera, priest of On, bore to him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The sons of Benjamin: Bela, Becher, Ashbel, Gera, Naaman, Ehi, Rosh, Muppim, Huppim, and Ard."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Rachel, who were born to Jacob: all the souls were fourteen."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The son of Dan: Hushim."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The sons of Naphtali: Jahzeel, Guni, Jezer, and Shillem."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Bilhah, whom Laban gave to Rachel, his daughter, and these she bore to Jacob: all the souls were seven."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"All the souls who came with Jacob into Egypt, who were his direct offspring, in addition to Jacob\u2019s sons\u2019 wives, all the souls were sixty-six."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The sons of Joseph, who were born to him in Egypt, were two souls. All the souls of the house of Jacob, who came into Egypt, were seventy."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob sent Judah before him to Joseph, to show the way before him to Goshen, and they came into the land of Goshen."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Joseph prepared his chariot, and went up to meet Israel, his father, in Goshen. He presented himself to him, and fell on his neck, and wept on his neck a good while."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Israel said to Joseph, \u201cNow let me die, since I have seen your face, that you are still alive.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph said to his brothers, and to his father\u2019s house, \u201cI will go up, and speak with Pharaoh, and will tell him, \u2018My brothers, and my father\u2019s house, who were in the land of Canaan, have come to me."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"These men are shepherds, for they have been keepers of livestock, and they have brought their flocks, and their herds, and all that they have.\u2019"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"It will happen, when Pharaoh summons you, and will say, \u2018What is your occupation?\u2019"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"that you shall say, \u2018Your servants have been keepers of livestock from our youth even until now, both we, and our fathers:\u2019 that you may dwell in the land of Goshen; for every shepherd is an abomination to the Egyptians.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joseph went in and told Pharaoh, and said, \u201cMy father and my brothers, with their flocks, their herds, and all that they own, have come out of the land of Canaan; and behold, they are in the land of Goshen.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"From among his brothers he took five men, and presented them to Pharaoh."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to his brothers, \u201cWhat is your occupation?\u201d"],[0,"They said to Pharaoh, \u201cYour servants are shepherds, both we, and our fathers.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They also said to Pharaoh, \u201cWe have come to live as foreigners in the land, for there is no pasture for your servants\u2019 flocks. For the famine is severe in the land of Canaan. Now therefore, please let your servants dwell in the land of Goshen.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh spoke to Joseph, saying, \u201cYour father and your brothers have come to you."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The land of Egypt is before you. Make your father and your brothers dwell in the best of the land. Let them dwell in the land of Goshen. If you know any able men among them, then put them in charge of my livestock.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph brought in Jacob, his father, and set him before Pharaoh; and Jacob blessed Pharaoh."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to Jacob, \u201cHow old are you?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob said to Pharaoh, \u201cThe years of my pilgrimage are one hundred thirty years. The days of the years of my life have been few and evil. They have not attained to the days of the years of the life of my fathers in the days of their pilgrimage.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Jacob blessed Pharaoh, and went out from the presence of Pharaoh."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph placed his father and his brothers, and gave them a possession in the land of Egypt, in the best of the land, in the land of Rameses, as Pharaoh had commanded."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Joseph provided his father, his brothers, and all of his father\u2019s household with bread, according to the sizes of their families."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"There was no bread in all the land; for the famine was very severe, so that the land of Egypt and the land of Canaan fainted by reason of the famine."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Joseph gathered up all the money that was found in the land of Egypt, and in the land of Canaan, for the grain which they bought: and Joseph brought the money into Pharaoh\u2019s house."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When the money was all spent in the land of Egypt, and in the land of Canaan, all the Egyptians came to Joseph, and said, \u201cGive us bread, for why should we die in your presence? For our money fails.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph said, \u201cGive me your livestock; and I will give you food for your livestock, if your money is gone.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"They brought their livestock to Joseph, and Joseph gave them bread in exchange for the horses, and for the flocks, and for the herds, and for the donkeys: and he fed them with bread in exchange for all their livestock for that year."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When that year was ended, they came to him the second year, and said to him, \u201cWe will not hide from my lord how our money is all spent, and the herds of livestock are my lord\u2019s. There is nothing left in the sight of my lord, but our bodies, and our lands."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Why should we die before your eyes, both we and our land? Buy us and our land for bread, and we and our land will be servants to Pharaoh. Give us seed, that we may live, and not die, and that the land won\u2019t be desolate.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joseph bought all the land of Egypt for Pharaoh, for every man of the Egyptians sold his field, because the famine was severe on them, and the land became Pharaoh\u2019s."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"As for the people, he moved them to the cities from one end of the border of Egypt even to the other end of it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Only he didn\u2019t buy the land of the priests, for the priests had a portion from Pharaoh, and ate their portion which Pharaoh gave them. That is why they didn\u2019t sell their land."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then Joseph said to the people, \u201cBehold, I have bought you and your land today for Pharaoh. Behold, here is seed for you, and you shall sow the land."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"It will happen at the harvests, that you shall give a fifth to Pharaoh, and four parts will be your own, for seed of the field, for your food, for them of your households, and for food for your little ones.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cYou have saved our lives! Let us find favor in the sight of my lord, and we will be Pharaoh\u2019s servants.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph made it a statute concerning the land of Egypt to this day, that Pharaoh should have the fifth. Only the land of the priests alone didn\u2019t become Pharaoh\u2019s."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel lived in the land of Egypt, in the land of Goshen; and they got themselves possessions therein, and were fruitful, and multiplied exceedingly."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Jacob lived in the land of Egypt seventeen years. So the days of Jacob, the years of his life, were one hundred forty-seven years."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The time came near that Israel must die, and he called his son Joseph, and said to him, \u201cIf now I have found favor in your sight, please put your hand under my thigh, and deal kindly and truly with me. Please don\u2019t bury me in Egypt,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"but when I sleep with my fathers, you shall carry me out of Egypt, and bury me in their burying place.\u201d"],[0,"Joseph said, \u201cI will do as you have said.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel said, \u201cSwear to me,\u201d and he swore to him. Then Israel bowed himself on the bed\u2019s head."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, someone said to Joseph, \u201cBehold, your father is sick.\u201d He took with him his two sons, Manasseh and Ephraim."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Someone told Jacob, and said, \u201cBehold, your son Joseph comes to you,\u201d and Israel strengthened himself, and sat on the bed."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jacob said to Joseph, \u201cGod Almighty appeared to me at Luz in the land of Canaan, and blessed me,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and said to me, \u2018Behold, I will make you fruitful, and multiply you, and I will make of you a company of peoples, and will give this land to your offspring after you for an everlasting possession.\u2019"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now your two sons, who were born to you in the land of Egypt before I came to you into Egypt, are mine; Ephraim and Manasseh, even as Reuben and Simeon, will be mine."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Your offspring, whom you become the father of after them, will be yours. They will be called after the name of their brothers in their inheritance."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"As for me, when I came from Paddan, Rachel died beside me in the land of Canaan on the way, when there was still some distance to come to Ephrath, and I buried her there on the way to Ephrath (also called Bethlehem).\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel saw Joseph\u2019s sons, and said, \u201cWho are these?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph said to his father, \u201cThey are my sons, whom God has given me here.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cPlease bring them to me, and I will bless them.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now the eyes of Israel were dim for age, so that he couldn\u2019t see well. Joseph brought them near to him; and he kissed them, and embraced them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Israel said to Joseph, \u201cI didn\u2019t think I would see your face, and behold, God has let me see your offspring also.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Joseph brought them out from between his knees, and he bowed himself with his face to the earth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Joseph took them both, Ephraim in his right hand toward Israel\u2019s left hand, and Manasseh in his left hand toward Israel\u2019s right hand, and brought them near to him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Israel stretched out his right hand, and laid it on Ephraim\u2019s head, who was the younger, and his left hand on Manasseh\u2019s head, guiding his hands knowingly, for Manasseh was the firstborn."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He blessed Joseph, and said,"],[1,"\u201cThe God before whom my fathers Abraham and Isaac walked,"],[1,"the God who has fed me all my life long to this day,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"the angel who has redeemed me from all evil, bless the lads,"],[1,"and let my name be named on them,"],[1,"and the name of my fathers Abraham and Isaac."],[1,"Let them grow into a multitude upon the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joseph saw that his father laid his right hand on the head of Ephraim, it displeased him. He held up his father\u2019s hand, to remove it from Ephraim\u2019s head to Manasseh\u2019s head."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Joseph said to his father, \u201cNot so, my father, for this is the firstborn. Put your right hand on his head.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"His father refused, and said, \u201cI know, my son, I know. He also will become a people, and he also will be great. However, his younger brother will be greater than he, and his offspring will become a multitude of nations.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He blessed them that day, saying, \u201cIsrael will bless in your name, saying, \u2018God make you as Ephraim and as Manasseh\u2019\u201d He set Ephraim before Manasseh."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Israel said to Joseph, \u201cBehold, I am dying, but God will be with you, and bring you again to the land of your fathers."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Moreover I have given to you one portion above your brothers, which I took out of the hand of the Amorite with my sword and with my bow.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jacob called to his sons, and said: \u201cGather yourselves together, that I may tell you that which will happen to you in the days to come."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Assemble yourselves, and hear, you sons of Jacob."],[2,"Listen to Israel, your father."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cReuben, you are my firstborn, my might, and the beginning of my strength,"],[2,"excelling in dignity, and excelling in power."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Boiling over like water, you shall not excel,"],[2,"because you went up to your father\u2019s bed,"],[2,"then defiled it. He went up to my couch."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSimeon and Levi are brothers."],[2,"Their swords are weapons of violence."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul, don\u2019t come into their council."],[2,"My glory, don\u2019t be united to their assembly;"],[1,"for in their anger they killed men."],[2,"In their self-will they hamstrung cattle."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce;"],[2,"and their wrath, for it was cruel."],[1,"I will divide them in Jacob,"],[2,"and scatter them in Israel."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cJudah, your brothers will praise you."],[2,"Your hand will be on the neck of your enemies."],[2,"Your father\u2019s sons will bow down before you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Judah is a lion\u2019s cub."],[2,"From the prey, my son, you have gone up."],[1,"He stooped down, he crouched as a lion,"],[2,"as a lioness."],[2,"Who will rouse him up?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The scepter will not depart from Judah,"],[2,"nor the ruler\u2019s staff from between his feet,"],[1,"until he comes to whom it belongs."],[2,"The obedience of the peoples will be to him."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Binding his foal to the vine,"],[2,"his donkey\u2019s colt to the choice vine,"],[1,"he has washed his garments in wine,"],[2,"his robes in the blood of grapes."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"His eyes will be red with wine,"],[2,"his teeth white with milk."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cZebulun will dwell at the haven of the sea."],[2,"He will be for a haven of ships."],[2,"His border will be on Sidon."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIssachar is a strong donkey,"],[2,"lying down between the saddlebags."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He saw a resting place, that it was good,"],[2,"the land, that it was pleasant."],[1,"He bows his shoulder to the burden,"],[2,"and becomes a servant doing forced labor."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDan will judge his people,"],[2,"as one of the tribes of Israel."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Dan will be a serpent on the trail,"],[2,"an adder in the path,"],[1,"that bites the horse\u2019s heels,"],[2,"so that his rider falls backward."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I have waited for your salvation, LORD."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cA troop will press on Gad,"],[2,"but he will press on their heel."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAsher\u2019s food will be rich."],[2,"He will produce royal dainties."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNaphtali is a doe set free,"],[2,"who bears beautiful fawns."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cJoseph is a fruitful vine,"],[2,"a fruitful vine by a spring."],[2,"His branches run over the wall."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The archers have severely grieved him,"],[2,"shot at him, and persecuted him:"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"But his bow remained strong."],[2,"The arms of his hands were made strong,"],[2,"by the hands of the Mighty One of Jacob,"],[2,"(from there is the shepherd, the stone of Israel),"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"even by the God of your father, who will help you,"],[2,"by the Almighty, who will bless you,"],[1,"with blessings of heaven above,"],[2,"blessings of the deep that lies below,"],[2,"blessings of the breasts, and of the womb."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The blessings of your father have prevailed above the blessings of my ancestors,"],[2,"above the boundaries of the ancient hills."],[1,"They will be on the head of Joseph,"],[2,"on the crown of the head of him who is separated from his brothers."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBenjamin is a ravenous wolf."],[2,"In the morning he will devour the prey."],[2,"At evening he will divide the plunder.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"All these are the twelve tribes of Israel, and this is what their father spoke to them, and blessed them. He blessed everyone according to his own blessing."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He instructed them, and said to them, \u201cI am to be gathered to my people. Bury me with my fathers in the cave that is in the field of Ephron the Hittite,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"in the cave that is in the field of Machpelah, which is before Mamre, in the land of Canaan, which Abraham bought with the field from Ephron the Hittite as a burial place."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"There they buried Abraham and Sarah, his wife. There they buried Isaac and Rebekah, his wife, and there I buried Leah:"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"the field and the cave that is therein, which was purchased from the children of Heth.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"When Jacob finished charging his sons, he gathered up his feet into the bed, breathed his last breath, and was gathered to his people."]]}],[{v:1,l:[[0,"Joseph fell on his father\u2019s face, wept on him, and kissed him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Joseph commanded his servants, the physicians, to embalm his father; and the physicians embalmed Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Forty days were used for him, for that is how many days it takes to embalm. The Egyptians wept for Israel for seventy days."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When the days of weeping for him were past, Joseph spoke to Pharaoh\u2019s staff, saying, \u201cIf now I have found favor in your eyes, please speak in the ears of Pharaoh, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u2018My father made me swear, saying, \u201cBehold, I am dying. Bury me in my grave which I have dug for myself in the land of Canaan.\u201d Now therefore, please let me go up and bury my father, and I will come again.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said, \u201cGo up, and bury your father, just like he made you swear.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph went up to bury his father; and with him went up all the servants of Pharaoh, the elders of his house, all the elders of the land of Egypt,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"all the house of Joseph, his brothers, and his father\u2019s house. Only their little ones, their flocks, and their herds, they left in the land of Goshen."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Both chariots and horsemen went up with him. It was a very great company."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They came to the threshing floor of Atad, which is beyond the Jordan, and there they lamented with a very great and severe lamentation. He mourned for his father seven days."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, saw the mourning in the floor of Atad, they said, \u201cThis is a grievous mourning by the Egyptians.\u201d Therefore its name was called Abel Mizraim, which is beyond the Jordan."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"His sons did to him just as he commanded them,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"for his sons carried him into the land of Canaan, and buried him in the cave of the field of Machpelah, which Abraham bought with the field, as a possession for a burial site, from Ephron the Hittite, near Mamre."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Joseph returned into Egypt\u2014he, and his brothers, and all that went up with him to bury his father, after he had buried his father."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joseph\u2019s brothers saw that their father was dead, they said, \u201cIt may be that Joseph will hate us, and will fully pay us back for all the evil which we did to him.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They sent a message to Joseph, saying, \u201cYour father commanded before he died, saying,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u2018You shall tell Joseph, \u201cNow please forgive the disobedience of your brothers, and their sin, because they did evil to you.\u201d\u2019 Now, please forgive the disobedience of the servants of the God of your father.\u201d Joseph wept when they spoke to him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"His brothers also went and fell down before his face; and they said, \u201cBehold, we are your servants.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Joseph said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for am I in the place of God?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As for you, you meant evil against me, but God meant it for good, to save many people alive, as is happening today."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Now therefore don\u2019t be afraid. I will provide for you and your little ones.\u201d He comforted them, and spoke kindly to them."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph lived in Egypt, he, and his father\u2019s house. Joseph lived one hundred ten years."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Joseph saw Ephraim\u2019s children to the third generation. The children also of Machir, the son of Manasseh, were born on Joseph\u2019s knees."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Joseph said to his brothers, \u201cI am dying, but God will surely visit you, and bring you up out of this land to the land which he swore to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Joseph took an oath from the children of Israel, saying, \u201cGod will surely visit you, and you shall carry up my bones from here.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"So Joseph died, being one hundred ten years old, and they embalmed him, and he was put in a coffin in Egypt."]]}]]}},1272,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,s){h.exports={book:"Exod",name:"Exodus",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the names of the sons of Israel, who came into Egypt (every man and his household came with Jacob):"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Reuben, Simeon, Levi, and Judah,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Issachar, Zebulun, and Benjamin,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Dan and Naphtali, Gad and Asher."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All the souls who came out of Jacob\u2019s body were seventy souls, and Joseph was in Egypt already."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Joseph died, as did all his brothers, and all that generation."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The children of Israel were fruitful, and increased abundantly, and multiplied, and grew exceedingly mighty; and the land was filled with them."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there arose a new king over Egypt, who didn\u2019t know Joseph."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said to his people, \u201cBehold, the people of the children of Israel are more and mightier than we."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Come, let\u2019s deal wisely with them, lest they multiply, and it happen that when any war breaks out, they also join themselves to our enemies and fight against us, and escape out of the land.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore they set taskmasters over them to afflict them with their burdens. They built storage cities for Pharaoh: Pithom and Raamses."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But the more they afflicted them, the more they multiplied and the more they spread out. They started to dread the children of Israel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The Egyptians ruthlessly made the children of Israel serve,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and they made their lives bitter with hard service in mortar and in brick, and in all kinds of service in the field, all their service, in which they ruthlessly made them serve."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Egypt spoke to the Hebrew midwives, of whom the name of the one was Shiphrah, and the name of the other Puah,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and he said, \u201cWhen you perform the duty of a midwife to the Hebrew women, and see them on the birth stool, if it is a son, then you shall kill him; but if it is a daughter, then she shall live.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But the midwives feared God, and didn\u2019t do what the king of Egypt commanded them, but saved the baby boys alive."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The king of Egypt called for the midwives, and said to them, \u201cWhy have you done this thing and saved the boys alive?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The midwives said to Pharaoh, \u201cBecause the Hebrew women aren\u2019t like the Egyptian women; for they are vigorous and give birth before the midwife comes to them.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"God dealt well with the midwives, and the people multiplied, and grew very mighty."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Because the midwives feared God, he gave them families."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Pharaoh commanded all his people, saying, \u201cYou shall cast every son who is born into the river, and every daughter you shall save alive.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A man of the house of Levi went and took a daughter of Levi as his wife."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The woman conceived and bore a son. When she saw that he was a fine child, she hid him three months."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When she could no longer hide him, she took a papyrus basket for him, and coated it with tar and with pitch. She put the child in it, and laid it in the reeds by the river\u2019s bank."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"His sister stood far off, to see what would be done to him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Pharaoh\u2019s daughter came down to bathe at the river. Her maidens walked along by the riverside. She saw the basket among the reeds, and sent her servant to get it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"She opened it, and saw the child, and behold, the baby cried. She had compassion on him, and said, \u201cThis is one of the Hebrews\u2019 children.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then his sister said to Pharaoh\u2019s daughter, \u201cShould I go and call a nurse for you from the Hebrew women, that she may nurse the child for you?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh\u2019s daughter said to her, \u201cGo.\u201d"],[0,"The young woman went and called the child\u2019s mother."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Pharaoh\u2019s daughter said to her, \u201cTake this child away, and nurse him for me, and I will give you your wages.\u201d"],[0,"The woman took the child, and nursed him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The child grew, and she brought him to Pharaoh\u2019s daughter, and he became her son. She named him Moses, and said, \u201cBecause I drew him out of the water.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cMoses\u201d sounds like the Hebrew for \u201cdraw out\u201d."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days, when Moses had grown up, he went out to his brothers and saw their burdens. He saw an Egyptian striking a Hebrew, one of his brothers."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He looked this way and that way, and when he saw that there was no one, he killed the Egyptian, and hid him in the sand."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He went out the second day, and behold, two men of the Hebrews were fighting with each other. He said to him who did the wrong, \u201cWhy do you strike your fellow?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWho made you a prince and a judge over us? Do you plan to kill me, as you killed the Egyptian?\u201d"],[0,"Moses was afraid, and said, \u201cSurely this thing is known.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now when Pharaoh heard this thing, he sought to kill Moses. But Moses fled from the face of Pharaoh, and lived in the land of Midian, and he sat down by a well."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the priest of Midian had seven daughters. They came and drew water, and filled the troughs to water their father\u2019s flock."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The shepherds came and drove them away; but Moses stood up and helped them, and watered their flock."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When they came to Reuel, their father, he said, \u201cHow is it that you have returned so early today?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cAn Egyptian delivered us out of the hand of the shepherds, and moreover he drew water for us, and watered the flock.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to his daughters, \u201cWhere is he? Why is it that you have left the man? Call him, that he may eat bread.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses was content to dwell with the man. He gave Moses Zipporah, his daughter."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"She bore a son, and he named him Gershom, for he said, \u201cI have lived as a foreigner in a foreign land.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cGershom\u201d sounds like the Hebrew for \u201can alien there\u201d."]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"In the course of those many days, the king of Egypt died, and the children of Israel sighed because of the bondage, and they cried, and their cry came up to God because of the bondage."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"God heard their groaning, and God remembered his covenant with Abraham, with Isaac, and with Jacob."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"God saw the children of Israel, and God understood."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Moses was keeping the flock of Jethro, his father-in-law, the priest of Midian, and he led the flock to the back of the wilderness, and came to God\u2019s mountain, to Horeb."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel appeared to him in a flame of fire out of the middle of a bush. He looked, and behold, the bush burned with fire, and the bush was not consumed."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cI will go now, and see this great sight, why the bush is not burned.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD saw that he came over to see, God called to him out of the middle of the bush, and said, \u201cMoses! Moses!\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cDon\u2019t come close. Take off your sandals, for the place you are standing on is holy ground.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Moreover he said, \u201cI am the God of your father, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.\u201d"],[0,"Moses hid his face because he was afraid to look at God."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cI have surely seen the affliction of my people who are in Egypt, and have heard their cry because of their taskmasters, for I know their sorrows."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I have come down to deliver them out of the hand of the Egyptians, and to bring them up out of that land to a good and large land, to a land flowing with milk and honey; to the place of the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Amorite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now, behold, the cry of the children of Israel has come to me. Moreover I have seen the oppression with which the Egyptians oppress them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Come now therefore, and I will send you to Pharaoh, that you may bring my people, the children of Israel, out of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to God, \u201cWho am I, that I should go to Pharaoh, and that I should bring the children of Israel out of Egypt?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cCertainly I will be with you. This will be the token to you, that I have sent you: when you have brought the people out of Egypt, you shall serve God on this mountain.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to God, \u201cBehold, when I come to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018The God of your fathers has sent me to you,\u2019 and they ask me, \u2018What is his name?\u2019 what should I tell them?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Moses, \u201cI AM WHO I AM,\u201d and he said, \u201cYou shall tell the children of Israel this: \u2018I AM has sent me to you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"God said moreover to Moses, \u201cYou shall tell the children of Israel this, \u2018The LORD, the God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob, has sent me to you.\u2019 This is my name forever, and this is my memorial to all generations."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Go and gather the elders of Israel together, and tell them, \u2018The LORD, the God of your fathers, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Jacob, has appeared to me, saying, \u201cI have surely visited you, and seen that which is done to you in Egypt."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I have said, I will bring you up out of the affliction of Egypt to the land of the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Amorite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite, to a land flowing with milk and honey.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They will listen to your voice. You shall come, you and the elders of Israel, to the king of Egypt, and you shall tell him, \u2018The LORD, the God of the Hebrews, has met with us. Now please let us go three days\u2019 journey into the wilderness, that we may sacrifice to the LORD, our God.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I know that the king of Egypt won\u2019t give you permission to go, no, not by a mighty hand."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"I will reach out my hand and strike Egypt with all my wonders which I will do among them, and after that he will let you go."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I will give this people favor in the sight of the Egyptians, and it will happen that when you go, you shall not go empty-handed."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But every woman shall ask of her neighbor, and of her who visits her house, jewels of silver, jewels of gold, and clothing. You shall put them on your sons, and on your daughters. You shall plunder the Egyptians.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses answered, \u201cBut, behold, they will not believe me, nor listen to my voice; for they will say, \u2018The LORD has not appeared to you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cWhat is that in your hand?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cA rod.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThrow it on the ground.\u201d"],[0,"He threw it on the ground, and it became a snake; and Moses ran away from it."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cStretch out your hand, and take it by the tail.\u201d"],[0,"He stretched out his hand, and took hold of it, and it became a rod in his hand."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is so that they may believe that the LORD, the God of their fathers, the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob, has appeared to you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD said furthermore to him, \u201cNow put your hand inside your cloak.\u201d"],[0,"He put his hand inside his cloak, and when he took it out, behold, his hand was leprous, as white as snow."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cPut your hand inside your cloak again.\u201d"],[0,"He put his hand inside his cloak again, and when he took it out of his cloak, behold, it had turned again as his other flesh."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt will happen, if they will not believe you or listen to the voice of the first sign, that they will believe the voice of the latter sign."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It will happen, if they will not believe even these two signs or listen to your voice, that you shall take of the water of the river, and pour it on the dry land. The water which you take out of the river will become blood on the dry land.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the LORD, \u201cO Lord, I am not eloquent, neither before now, nor since you have spoken to your servant; for I am slow of speech, and of a slow tongue.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai\u201d."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cWho made man\u2019s mouth? Or who makes one mute, or deaf, or seeing, or blind? Isn\u2019t it I, the LORD?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now therefore go, and I will be with your mouth, and teach you what you shall speak.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cOh, Lord, please send someone else.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Moses, and he said, \u201cWhat about Aaron, your brother, the Levite? I know that he can speak well. Also, behold, he is coming out to meet you. When he sees you, he will be glad in his heart."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall speak to him, and put the words in his mouth. I will be with your mouth, and with his mouth, and will teach you what you shall do."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He will be your spokesman to the people. It will happen that he will be to you a mouth, and you will be to him as God."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall take this rod in your hand, with which you shall do the signs.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went and returned to Jethro his father-in-law, and said to him, \u201cPlease let me go and return to my brothers who are in Egypt, and see whether they are still alive.\u201d"],[0,"Jethro said to Moses, \u201cGo in peace.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses in Midian, \u201cGo, return into Egypt; for all the men who sought your life are dead.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses took his wife and his sons, and set them on a donkey, and he returned to the land of Egypt. Moses took God\u2019s rod in his hand."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cWhen you go back into Egypt, see that you do before Pharaoh all the wonders which I have put in your hand, but I will harden his heart and he will not let the people go."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall tell Pharaoh, \u2018The LORD says, Israel is my son, my firstborn,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and I have said to you, \u201cLet my son go, that he may serve me;\u201d and you have refused to let him go. Behold, I will kill your firstborn son.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"On the way at a lodging place, the LORD met Moses and wanted to kill him."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Then Zipporah took a flint, and cut off the foreskin of her son, and cast it at his feet; and she said, \u201cSurely you are a bridegroom of blood to me.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"So he let him alone. Then she said, \u201cYou are a bridegroom of blood,\u201d because of the circumcision."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Aaron, \u201cGo into the wilderness to meet Moses.\u201d"],[0,"He went, and met him on God\u2019s mountain, and kissed him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Moses told Aaron all the LORD\u2019s words with which he had sent him, and all the signs with which he had instructed him."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron went and gathered together all the elders of the children of Israel."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Aaron spoke all the words which the LORD had spoken to Moses, and did the signs in the sight of the people."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The people believed, and when they heard that the LORD had visited the children of Israel, and that he had seen their affliction, then they bowed their heads and worshiped."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Afterward Moses and Aaron came, and said to Pharaoh, \u201cThis is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018Let my people go, that they may hold a feast to me in the wilderness.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said, \u201cWho is the LORD, that I should listen to his voice to let Israel go? I don\u2019t know the LORD, and moreover I will not let Israel go.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThe God of the Hebrews has met with us. Please let us go three days\u2019 journey into the wilderness, and sacrifice to the LORD, our God, lest he fall on us with pestilence, or with the sword.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Egypt said to them, \u201cWhy do you, Moses and Aaron, take the people from their work? Get back to your burdens!\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said, \u201cBehold, the people of the land are now many, and you make them rest from their burdens.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The same day Pharaoh commanded the taskmasters of the people and their officers, saying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall no longer give the people straw to make brick, as before. Let them go and gather straw for themselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall require from them the number of the bricks which they made before. You shall not diminish anything of it, for they are idle. Therefore they cry, saying, \u2018Let\u2019s go and sacrifice to our God.\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Let heavier work be laid on the men, that they may labor in it. Don\u2019t let them pay any attention to lying words.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The taskmasters of the people went out with their officers, and they spoke to the people, saying, \u201cThis is what Pharaoh says: \u2018I will not give you straw."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Go yourselves, get straw where you can find it, for nothing of your work shall be diminished.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So the people were scattered abroad throughout all the land of Egypt to gather stubble for straw."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The taskmasters were urgent saying, \u201cFulfill your work quota daily, as when there was straw!\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The officers of the children of Israel, whom Pharaoh\u2019s taskmasters had set over them, were beaten, and were asked, \u201cWhy haven\u2019t you fulfilled your quota both yesterday and today, in making brick as before?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the officers of the children of Israel came and cried to Pharaoh, saying, \u201cWhy do you deal this way with your servants?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"No straw is given to your servants, and they tell us, \u2018Make brick!\u2019 and behold, your servants are beaten; but the fault is in your own people.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But Pharaoh said, \u201cYou are idle! You are idle! Therefore you say, \u2018Let\u2019s go and sacrifice to the LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Go therefore now, and work; for no straw shall be given to you; yet you shall deliver the same number of bricks!\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The officers of the children of Israel saw that they were in trouble when it was said, \u201cYou shall not diminish anything from your daily quota of bricks!\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"They met Moses and Aaron, who stood along the way, as they came out from Pharaoh."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They said to them, \u201cMay the LORD look at you and judge, because you have made us a stench to be abhorred in the eyes of Pharaoh, and in the eyes of his servants, to put a sword in their hand to kill us!\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses returned to the LORD, and said, \u201cLord, why have you brought trouble on this people? Why is it that you have sent me?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For since I came to Pharaoh to speak in your name, he has brought trouble on this people. You have not rescued your people at all!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cNow you shall see what I will do to Pharaoh, for by a strong hand he shall let them go, and by a strong hand he shall drive them out of his land.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"God spoke to Moses, and said to him, \u201cI am the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I appeared to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, as God Almighty; but by my name the LORD I was not known to them."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I have also established my covenant with them, to give them the land of Canaan, the land of their travels, in which they lived as aliens."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Moreover I have heard the groaning of the children of Israel, whom the Egyptians keep in bondage, and I have remembered my covenant."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore tell the children of Israel, \u2018I am the LORD, and I will bring you out from under the burdens of the Egyptians, and I will rid you out of their bondage, and I will redeem you with an outstretched arm, and with great judgments."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I will take you to myself for a people. I will be your God; and you shall know that I am the LORD your God, who brings you out from under the burdens of the Egyptians."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will bring you into the land which I swore to give to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob; and I will give it to you for a heritage: I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke so to the children of Israel, but they didn\u2019t listen to Moses for anguish of spirit, and for cruel bondage."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cGo in, speak to Pharaoh king of Egypt, that he let the children of Israel go out of his land.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke before the LORD, saying, \u201cBehold, the children of Israel haven\u2019t listened to me. How then shall Pharaoh listen to me, when I have uncircumcised lips?\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, and gave them a command to the children of Israel, and to Pharaoh king of Egypt, to bring the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the heads of their fathers\u2019 houses. The sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel: Hanoch, and Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi; these are the families of Reuben."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The sons of Simeon: Jemuel, and Jamin, and Ohad, and Jachin, and Zohar, and Shaul the son of a Canaanite woman; these are the families of Simeon."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"These are the names of the sons of Levi according to their generations: Gershon, and Kohath, and Merari; and the years of the life of Levi were one hundred thirty-seven years."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The sons of Gershon: Libni and Shimei, according to their families."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The sons of Kohath: Amram, and Izhar, and Hebron, and Uzziel; and the years of the life of Kohath were one hundred thirty-three years."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. These are the families of the Levites according to their generations."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Amram took Jochebed his father\u2019s sister to himself as wife; and she bore him Aaron and Moses. The years of the life of Amram were one hundred thirty-seven years."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The sons of Izhar: Korah, and Nepheg, and Zichri."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The sons of Uzziel: Mishael, Elzaphan, and Sithri."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Aaron took Elisheba, the daughter of Amminadab, the sister of Nahshon, as his wife; and she bore him Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The sons of Korah: Assir, Elkanah, and Abiasaph; these are the families of the Korahites."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Eleazar Aaron\u2019s son took one of the daughters of Putiel as his wife; and she bore him Phinehas. These are the heads of the fathers\u2019 houses of the Levites according to their families."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"These are that Aaron and Moses to whom the LORD said, \u201cBring out the children of Israel from the land of Egypt according to their armies.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"These are those who spoke to Pharaoh king of Egypt, to bring out the children of Israel from Egypt. These are that Moses and Aaron."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"On the day when the LORD spoke to Moses in the land of Egypt,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cI am the LORD. Tell Pharaoh king of Egypt all that I tell you.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said before the LORD, \u201cBehold, I am of uncircumcised lips, and how shall Pharaoh listen to me?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cBehold, I have made you as God to Pharaoh; and Aaron your brother shall be your prophet."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall speak all that I command you; and Aaron your brother shall speak to Pharaoh, that he let the children of Israel go out of his land."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will harden Pharaoh\u2019s heart, and multiply my signs and my wonders in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But Pharaoh will not listen to you, so I will lay my hand on Egypt, and bring out my armies, my people the children of Israel, out of the land of Egypt by great judgments."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The Egyptians shall know that I am the LORD when I stretch out my hand on Egypt, and bring the children of Israel out from among them.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron did so. As the LORD commanded them, so they did."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Moses was eighty years old, and Aaron eighty-three years old, when they spoke to Pharaoh."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen Pharaoh speaks to you, saying, \u2018Perform a miracle!\u2019 then you shall tell Aaron, \u2018Take your rod, and cast it down before Pharaoh, and it will become a serpent.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron went in to Pharaoh, and they did so, as the LORD had commanded. Aaron cast down his rod before Pharaoh and before his servants, and it became a serpent."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then Pharaoh also called for the wise men and the sorcerers. They also, the magicians of Egypt, did the same thing with their enchantments."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For they each cast down their rods, and they became serpents; but Aaron\u2019s rod swallowed up their rods."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Pharaoh\u2019s heart was hardened, and he didn\u2019t listen to them, as the LORD had spoken."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cPharaoh\u2019s heart is stubborn. He refuses to let the people go."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Go to Pharaoh in the morning. Behold, he is going out to the water. You shall stand by the river\u2019s bank to meet him. You shall take the rod which was turned to a serpent in your hand."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall tell him, \u2018The LORD, the God of the Hebrews, has sent me to you, saying, \u201cLet my people go, that they may serve me in the wilderness. Behold, until now you haven\u2019t listened.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u201cIn this you shall know that I am the LORD. Behold: I will strike with the rod that is in my hand on the waters which are in the river, and they shall be turned to blood."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The fish that are in the river will die and the river will become foul. The Egyptians will loathe to drink water from the river.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cTell Aaron, \u2018Take your rod, and stretch out your hand over the waters of Egypt, over their rivers, over their streams, and over their pools, and over all their ponds of water, that they may become blood. There will be blood throughout all the land of Egypt, both in vessels of wood and in vessels of stone.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron did so, as the LORD commanded; and he lifted up the rod, and struck the waters that were in the river, in the sight of Pharaoh, and in the sight of his servants; and all the waters that were in the river were turned to blood."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The fish that were in the river died. The river became foul. The Egyptians couldn\u2019t drink water from the river. The blood was throughout all the land of Egypt."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The magicians of Egypt did the same thing with their enchantments. So Pharaoh\u2019s heart was hardened, and he didn\u2019t listen to them, as the LORD had spoken."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Pharaoh turned and went into his house, and he didn\u2019t even take this to heart."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"All the Egyptians dug around the river for water to drink; for they couldn\u2019t drink the river water."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Seven days were fulfilled, after the LORD had struck the river."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, \u201cGo in to Pharaoh, and tell him, \u2018This is what the LORD says, \u201cLet my people go, that they may serve me."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"If you refuse to let them go, behold, I will plague all your borders with frogs."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The river will swarm with frogs, which will go up and come into your house, and into your bedroom, and on your bed, and into the house of your servants, and on your people, and into your ovens, and into your kneading troughs."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The frogs shall come up both on you, and on your people, and on all your servants.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cTell Aaron, \u2018Stretch out your hand with your rod over the rivers, over the streams, and over the pools, and cause frogs to come up on the land of Egypt.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Aaron stretched out his hand over the waters of Egypt; and the frogs came up, and covered the land of Egypt."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The magicians did the same thing with their enchantments, and brought up frogs on the land of Egypt."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Pharaoh called for Moses and Aaron, and said, \u201cEntreat the LORD, that he take away the frogs from me and from my people; and I will let the people go, that they may sacrifice to the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Pharaoh, \u201cI give you the honor of setting the time that I should pray for you, and for your servants, and for your people, that the frogs be destroyed from you and your houses, and remain in the river only.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said, \u201cTomorrow.\u201d"],[0,"Moses said, \u201cLet it be according to your word, that you may know that there is no one like the LORD our God."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The frogs shall depart from you, and from your houses, and from your servants, and from your people. They shall remain in the river only.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron went out from Pharaoh, and Moses cried to the LORD concerning the frogs which he had brought on Pharaoh."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD did according to the word of Moses, and the frogs died out of the houses, out of the courts, and out of the fields."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They gathered them together in heaps, and the land stank."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But when Pharaoh saw that there was a respite, he hardened his heart, and didn\u2019t listen to them, as the LORD had spoken."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cTell Aaron, \u2018Stretch out your rod, and strike the dust of the earth, that it may become lice throughout all the land of Egypt.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They did so; and Aaron stretched out his hand with his rod, and struck the dust of the earth, and there were lice on man, and on animal; all the dust of the earth became lice throughout all the land of Egypt."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The magicians tried with their enchantments to produce lice, but they couldn\u2019t. There were lice on man, and on animal."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Then the magicians said to Pharaoh, \u201cThis is God\u2019s finger;\u201d but Pharaoh\u2019s heart was hardened, and he didn\u2019t listen to them, as the LORD had spoken."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cRise up early in the morning, and stand before Pharaoh; behold, he comes out to the water; and tell him, \u2018This is what the LORD says, \u201cLet my people go, that they may serve me."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Else, if you will not let my people go, behold, I will send swarms of flies on you, and on your servants, and on your people, and into your houses. The houses of the Egyptians shall be full of swarms of flies, and also the ground they are on."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will set apart in that day the land of Goshen, in which my people dwell, that no swarms of flies shall be there, to the end you may know that I am the LORD on the earth."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will put a division between my people and your people. This sign shall happen by tomorrow.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The LORD did so; and there came grievous swarms of flies into the house of Pharaoh, and into his servants\u2019 houses. In all the land of Egypt the land was corrupted by reason of the swarms of flies."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh called for Moses and for Aaron, and said, \u201cGo, sacrifice to your God in the land!\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cIt isn\u2019t appropriate to do so; for we shall sacrifice the abomination of the Egyptians to the LORD our God. Behold, if we sacrifice the abomination of the Egyptians before their eyes, won\u2019t they stone us?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"We will go three days\u2019 journey into the wilderness, and sacrifice to the LORD our God, as he shall command us.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said, \u201cI will let you go, that you may sacrifice to the LORD your God in the wilderness, only you shall not go very far away. Pray for me.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cBehold, I am going out from you. I will pray to the LORD that the swarms of flies may depart from Pharaoh, from his servants, and from his people, tomorrow; only don\u2019t let Pharaoh deal deceitfully any more in not letting the people go to sacrifice to the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Moses went out from Pharaoh, and prayed to the LORD."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The LORD did according to the word of Moses, and he removed the swarms of flies from Pharaoh, from his servants, and from his people. There remained not one."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Pharaoh hardened his heart this time also, and he didn\u2019t let the people go."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to Moses, \u201cGo in to Pharaoh, and tell him, \u2018This is what the LORD, the God of the Hebrews, says: \u201cLet my people go, that they may serve me."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For if you refuse to let them go, and hold them still,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"behold, the LORD\u2019s hand is on your livestock which are in the field, on the horses, on the donkeys, on the camels, on the herds, and on the flocks with a very grievous pestilence."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD will make a distinction between the livestock of Israel and the livestock of Egypt; and nothing shall die of all that belongs to the children of Israel.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD appointed a set time, saying, \u201cTomorrow the LORD shall do this thing in the land.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD did that thing on the next day; and all the livestock of Egypt died, but of the livestock of the children of Israel, not one died."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Pharaoh sent, and, behold, there was not so much as one of the livestock of the Israelites dead. But the heart of Pharaoh was stubborn, and he didn\u2019t let the people go."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses and to Aaron, \u201cTake handfuls of ashes of the furnace, and let Moses sprinkle it toward the sky in the sight of Pharaoh."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It shall become small dust over all the land of Egypt, and shall be boils and blisters breaking out on man and on animal, throughout all the land of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"They took ashes of the furnace, and stood before Pharaoh; and Moses sprinkled it up toward the sky; and it became boils and blisters breaking out on man and on animal."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The magicians couldn\u2019t stand before Moses because of the boils; for the boils were on the magicians and on all the Egyptians."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD hardened the heart of Pharaoh, and he didn\u2019t listen to them, as the LORD had spoken to Moses."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cRise up early in the morning, and stand before Pharaoh, and tell him, \u2018This is what the LORD, the God of the Hebrews, says: \u201cLet my people go, that they may serve me."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For this time I will send all my plagues against your heart, against your officials, and against your people; that you may know that there is no one like me in all the earth."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For now I would have stretched out my hand, and struck you and your people with pestilence, and you would have been cut off from the earth;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"but indeed for this cause I have made you stand: to show you my power, and that my name may be declared throughout all the earth,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"because you still exalt yourself against my people, that you won\u2019t let them go."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Behold, tomorrow about this time I will cause it to rain a very grievous hail, such as has not been in Egypt since the day it was founded even until now."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now therefore command that all of your livestock and all that you have in the field be brought into shelter. The hail will come down on every man and animal that is found in the field, and isn\u2019t brought home, and they will die.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who feared the LORD\u2019s word among the servants of Pharaoh made their servants and their livestock flee into the houses."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Whoever didn\u2019t respect the LORD\u2019s word left his servants and his livestock in the field."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cStretch out your hand toward the sky, that there may be hail in all the land of Egypt, on man, and on animal, and on every herb of the field, throughout the land of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses stretched out his rod toward the heavens, and the LORD sent thunder and hail; and lightning flashed down to the earth. The LORD rained hail on the land of Egypt."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"So there was very severe hail, and lightning mixed with the hail, such as had not been in all the land of Egypt since it became a nation."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The hail struck throughout all the land of Egypt all that was in the field, both man and animal; and the hail struck every herb of the field, and broke every tree of the field."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Only in the land of Goshen, where the children of Israel were, there was no hail."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh sent and called for Moses and Aaron, and said to them, \u201cI have sinned this time. The LORD is righteous, and I and my people are wicked."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Pray to the LORD; for there has been enough of mighty thunderings and hail. I will let you go, and you shall stay no longer.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to him, \u201cAs soon as I have gone out of the city, I will spread out my hands to the LORD. The thunders shall cease, and there will not be any more hail; that you may know that the earth is the LORD\u2019s."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But as for you and your servants, I know that you don\u2019t yet fear the LORD God.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"The flax and the barley were struck, for the barley had ripened and the flax was blooming."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"But the wheat and the spelt were not struck, for they had not grown up."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Moses went out of the city from Pharaoh, and spread out his hands to the LORD; and the thunders and hail ceased, and the rain was not poured on the earth."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"When Pharaoh saw that the rain and the hail and the thunders had ceased, he sinned yet more, and hardened his heart, he and his servants."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The heart of Pharaoh was hardened, and he didn\u2019t let the children of Israel go, just as the LORD had spoken through Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cGo in to Pharaoh, for I have hardened his heart and the heart of his servants, that I may show these my signs among them;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and that you may tell in the hearing of your son, and of your son\u2019s son, what things I have done to Egypt, and my signs which I have done among them; that you may know that I am the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron went in to Pharaoh, and said to him, \u201cThis is what the LORD, the God of the Hebrews, says: \u2018How long will you refuse to humble yourself before me? Let my people go, that they may serve me."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Or else, if you refuse to let my people go, behold, tomorrow I will bring locusts into your country,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and they shall cover the surface of the earth, so that one won\u2019t be able to see the earth. They shall eat the residue of that which has escaped, which remains to you from the hail, and shall eat every tree which grows for you out of the field."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Your houses shall be filled, and the houses of all your servants, and the houses of all the Egyptians, as neither your fathers nor your fathers\u2019 fathers have seen, since the day that they were on the earth to this day.\u2019\u201d He turned, and went out from Pharaoh."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh\u2019s servants said to him, \u201cHow long will this man be a snare to us? Let the men go, that they may serve the LORD, their God. Don\u2019t you yet know that Egypt is destroyed?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron were brought again to Pharaoh, and he said to them, \u201cGo, serve the LORD your God; but who are those who will go?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cWe will go with our young and with our old. We will go with our sons and with our daughters, with our flocks and with our herds; for we must hold a feast to the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThe LORD be with you if I let you go with your little ones! See, evil is clearly before your faces."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Not so! Go now you who are men, and serve the LORD; for that is what you desire!\u201d Then they were driven out from Pharaoh\u2019s presence."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cStretch out your hand over the land of Egypt for the locusts, that they may come up on the land of Egypt, and eat every herb of the land, even all that the hail has left.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Moses stretched out his rod over the land of Egypt, and the LORD brought an east wind on the land all that day, and all night; and when it was morning, the east wind brought the locusts."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The locusts went up over all the land of Egypt, and rested in all the borders of Egypt. They were very grievous. Before them there were no such locusts as they, nor will there ever be again."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For they covered the surface of the whole earth, so that the land was darkened, and they ate every herb of the land, and all the fruit of the trees which the hail had left. There remained nothing green, either tree or herb of the field, through all the land of Egypt."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then Pharaoh called for Moses and Aaron in haste, and he said, \u201cI have sinned against the LORD your God, and against you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now therefore please forgive my sin again, and pray to the LORD your God, that he may also take away from me this death.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went out from Pharaoh, and prayed to the LORD."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The LORD sent an exceedingly strong west wind, which took up the locusts, and drove them into the Red Sea. There remained not one locust in all the borders of Egypt."]],f:["\u201cRed Sea\u201d is the translation for the Hebrew \u201cYam Suf\u201d, which could be more literally translated \u201cSea of Reeds\u201d or \u201cSea of Cattails\u201d. It refers to the body of water currently known as the Red Sea, or possibly to one of the bodies of water connected to it or near it."]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But the LORD hardened Pharaoh\u2019s heart, and he didn\u2019t let the children of Israel go."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cStretch out your hand toward the sky, that there may be darkness over the land of Egypt, even darkness which may be felt.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Moses stretched out his hand toward the sky, and there was a thick darkness in all the land of Egypt for three days."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t see one another, and nobody rose from his place for three days; but all the children of Israel had light in their dwellings."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharaoh called to Moses, and said, \u201cGo, serve the LORD. Only let your flocks and your herds stay behind. Let your little ones also go with you.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cYou must also give into our hand sacrifices and burnt offerings, that we may sacrifice to the LORD our God."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Our livestock also shall go with us. Not a hoof shall be left behind, for of it we must take to serve the LORD our God; and we don\u2019t know with what we must serve the LORD, until we come there.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But the LORD hardened Pharaoh\u2019s heart, and he wouldn\u2019t let them go."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Pharaoh said to him, \u201cGet away from me! Be careful to see my face no more; for in the day you see my face you shall die!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cYou have spoken well. I will see your face again no more.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cI will bring yet one more plague on Pharaoh, and on Egypt; afterwards he will let you go. When he lets you go, he will surely thrust you out altogether."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Speak now in the ears of the people, and let every man ask of his neighbor, and every woman of her neighbor, jewels of silver, and jewels of gold.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD gave the people favor in the sight of the Egyptians. Moreover, the man Moses was very great in the land of Egypt, in the sight of Pharaoh\u2019s servants, and in the sight of the people."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cThis is what the LORD says: \u2018About midnight I will go out into the middle of Egypt,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and all the firstborn in the land of Egypt shall die, from the firstborn of Pharaoh who sits on his throne, even to the firstborn of the female servant who is behind the mill, and all the firstborn of livestock."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"There will be a great cry throughout all the land of Egypt, such as there has not been, nor will be any more."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But against any of the children of Israel a dog won\u2019t even bark or move its tongue, against man or animal, that you may know that the LORD makes a distinction between the Egyptians and Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All these servants of yours will come down to me, and bow down themselves to me, saying, \u201cGet out, with all the people who follow you;\u201d and after that I will go out.\u2019\u201d He went out from Pharaoh in hot anger."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cPharaoh won\u2019t listen to you, that my wonders may be multiplied in the land of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron did all these wonders before Pharaoh, but the LORD hardened Pharaoh\u2019s heart, and he didn\u2019t let the children of Israel go out of his land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron in the land of Egypt, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThis month shall be to you the beginning of months. It shall be the first month of the year to you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Speak to all the congregation of Israel, saying, \u2018On the tenth day of this month, they shall take to them every man a lamb, according to their fathers\u2019 houses, a lamb for a household;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and if the household is too little for a lamb, then he and his neighbor next to his house shall take one according to the number of the souls. You shall make your count for the lamb according to what everyone can eat."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Your lamb shall be without defect, a male a year old. You shall take it from the sheep or from the goats."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall keep it until the fourteenth day of the same month; and the whole assembly of the congregation of Israel shall kill it at evening."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They shall take some of the blood, and put it on the two door posts and on the lintel, on the houses in which they shall eat it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They shall eat the meat in that night, roasted with fire, with unleavened bread. They shall eat it with bitter herbs."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t eat it raw, nor boiled at all with water, but roasted with fire; with its head, its legs and its inner parts."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall let nothing of it remain until the morning; but that which remains of it until the morning you shall burn with fire."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"This is how you shall eat it: with your belt on your waist, your sandals on your feet, and your staff in your hand; and you shall eat it in haste: it is the LORD\u2019s Passover."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For I will go through the land of Egypt in that night, and will strike all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, both man and animal. I will execute judgments against all the gods of Egypt. I am the LORD."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The blood shall be to you for a token on the houses where you are. When I see the blood, I will pass over you, and no plague will be on you to destroy you when I strike the land of Egypt."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"This day shall be a memorial for you. You shall keep it as a feast to the LORD. You shall keep it as a feast throughout your generations by an ordinance forever."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread; even the first day you shall put away yeast out of your houses, for whoever eats leavened bread from the first day until the seventh day, that soul shall be cut off from Israel."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"In the first day there shall be to you a holy convocation, and in the seventh day a holy convocation; no kind of work shall be done in them, except that which every man must eat, only that may be done by you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall observe the feast of unleavened bread; for in this same day I have brought your armies out of the land of Egypt. Therefore you shall observe this day throughout your generations by an ordinance forever."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month at evening, you shall eat unleavened bread, until the twenty first day of the month at evening."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There shall be no yeast found in your houses for seven days, for whoever eats that which is leavened, that soul shall be cut off from the congregation of Israel, whether he is a foreigner, or one who is born in the land."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall eat nothing leavened. In all your habitations you shall eat unleavened bread.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Moses called for all the elders of Israel, and said to them, \u201cDraw out, and take lambs according to your families, and kill the Passover."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall take a bunch of hyssop, and dip it in the blood that is in the basin, and strike the lintel and the two door posts with the blood that is in the basin. None of you shall go out of the door of his house until the morning."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For the LORD will pass through to strike the Egyptians; and when he sees the blood on the lintel, and on the two door posts, the LORD will pass over the door, and will not allow the destroyer to come in to your houses to strike you."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall observe this thing for an ordinance to you and to your sons forever."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"It shall happen when you have come to the land which the LORD will give you, as he has promised, that you shall keep this service."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"It will happen, when your children ask you, \u2018What do you mean by this service?\u2019"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"that you shall say, \u2018It is the sacrifice of the LORD\u2019s Passover, who passed over the houses of the children of Israel in Egypt, when he struck the Egyptians, and spared our houses.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"The people bowed their heads and worshiped."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The children of Israel went and did so; as the LORD had commanded Moses and Aaron, so they did."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"At midnight, the LORD struck all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, from the firstborn of Pharaoh who sat on his throne to the firstborn of the captive who was in the dungeon, and all the firstborn of livestock."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Pharaoh rose up in the night, he, and all his servants, and all the Egyptians; and there was a great cry in Egypt, for there was not a house where there was not one dead."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He called for Moses and Aaron by night, and said, \u201cRise up, get out from among my people, both you and the children of Israel; and go, serve the LORD, as you have said!"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Take both your flocks and your herds, as you have said, and be gone; and bless me also!\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The Egyptians were urgent with the people, to send them out of the land in haste, for they said, \u201cWe are all dead men.\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The people took their dough before it was leavened, their kneading troughs being bound up in their clothes on their shoulders."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did according to the word of Moses; and they asked of the Egyptians jewels of silver, and jewels of gold, and clothing."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The LORD gave the people favor in the sight of the Egyptians, so that they let them have what they asked. They plundered the Egyptians."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel traveled from Rameses to Succoth, about six hundred thousand on foot who were men, in addition to children."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"A mixed multitude went up also with them, with flocks, herds, and even very much livestock."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"They baked unleavened cakes of the dough which they brought out of Egypt; for it wasn\u2019t leavened, because they were thrust out of Egypt, and couldn\u2019t wait, and they had not prepared any food for themselves."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Now the time that the children of Israel lived in Egypt was four hundred thirty years."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"At the end of four hundred thirty years, to the day, all of the LORD\u2019s armies went out from the land of Egypt."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"It is a night to be much observed to the LORD for bringing them out from the land of Egypt. This is that night of the LORD, to be much observed by all the children of Israel throughout their generations."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses and Aaron, \u201cThis is the ordinance of the Passover. No foreigner shall eat of it,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"but every man\u2019s servant who is bought for money, when you have circumcised him, then shall he eat of it."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"A foreigner and a hired servant shall not eat of it."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"It must be eaten in one house. You shall not carry any of the meat outside of the house. Do not break any of its bones."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"All the congregation of Israel shall keep it."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"When a stranger lives as a foreigner with you, and would like to keep the Passover to the LORD, let all his males be circumcised, and then let him come near and keep it. He shall be as one who is born in the land; but no uncircumcised person shall eat of it."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"One law shall be to him who is born at home, and to the stranger who lives as a foreigner among you.\u201d"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"All the children of Israel did so. As the LORD commanded Moses and Aaron, so they did."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"That same day, the LORD brought the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt by their armies."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSanctify to me all the firstborn, whatever opens the womb among the children of Israel, both of man and of animal. It is mine.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the people, \u201cRemember this day, in which you came out of Egypt, out of the house of bondage; for by strength of hand the LORD brought you out from this place. No leavened bread shall be eaten."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Today you go out in the month Abib."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It shall be, when the LORD brings you into the land of the Canaanite, and the Hittite, and the Amorite, and the Hivite, and the Jebusite, which he swore to your fathers to give you, a land flowing with milk and honey, that you shall keep this service in this month."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread, and in the seventh day shall be a feast to the LORD."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Unleavened bread shall be eaten throughout the seven days; and no leavened bread shall be seen with you. No yeast shall be seen with you, within all your borders."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall tell your son in that day, saying, \u2018It is because of that which the LORD did for me when I came out of Egypt.\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It shall be for a sign to you on your hand, and for a memorial between your eyes, that the LORD\u2019s law may be in your mouth; for with a strong hand the LORD has brought you out of Egypt."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall therefore keep this ordinance in its season from year to year."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt shall be, when the LORD brings you into the land of the Canaanite, as he swore to you and to your fathers, and will give it to you,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that you shall set apart to the LORD all that opens the womb, and every firstborn that comes from an animal which you have. The males shall be the LORD\u2019s."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Every firstborn of a donkey you shall redeem with a lamb; and if you will not redeem it, then you shall break its neck; and you shall redeem all the firstborn of man among your sons."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"It shall be, when your son asks you in time to come, saying, \u2018What is this?\u2019 that you shall tell him, \u2018By strength of hand the LORD brought us out from Egypt, from the house of bondage."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When Pharaoh stubbornly refused to let us go, the LORD killed all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, both the firstborn of man, and the firstborn of livestock. Therefore I sacrifice to the LORD all that opens the womb, being males; but all the firstborn of my sons I redeem.\u2019"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"It shall be for a sign on your hand, and for symbols between your eyes; for by strength of hand the LORD brought us out of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When Pharaoh had let the people go, God didn\u2019t lead them by the way of the land of the Philistines, although that was near; for God said, \u201cLest perhaps the people change their minds when they see war, and they return to Egypt\u201d;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"but God led the people around by the way of the wilderness by the Red Sea; and the children of Israel went up armed out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Moses took the bones of Joseph with him, for he had made the children of Israel swear, saying, \u201cGod will surely visit you, and you shall carry up my bones away from here with you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They took their journey from Succoth, and encamped in Etham, in the edge of the wilderness."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD went before them by day in a pillar of cloud, to lead them on their way, and by night in a pillar of fire, to give them light, that they might go by day and by night:"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"the pillar of cloud by day, and the pillar of fire by night, didn\u2019t depart from before the people."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, that they turn back and encamp before Pihahiroth, between Migdol and the sea, before Baal Zephon. You shall encamp opposite it by the sea."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Pharaoh will say of the children of Israel, \u2018They are entangled in the land. The wilderness has shut them in.\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will harden Pharaoh\u2019s heart, and he will follow after them; and I will get honor over Pharaoh, and over all his armies; and the Egyptians shall know that I am the LORD.\u201d They did so."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Egypt was told that the people had fled; and the heart of Pharaoh and of his servants was changed toward the people, and they said, \u201cWhat is this we have done, that we have let Israel go from serving us?\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He prepared his chariot, and took his army with him;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and he took six hundred chosen chariots, and all the chariots of Egypt, with captains over all of them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD hardened the heart of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and he pursued the children of Israel; for the children of Israel went out with a high hand."]],f:["or, defiantly."]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The Egyptians pursued them. All the horses and chariots of Pharaoh, his horsemen, and his army overtook them encamping by the sea, beside Pihahiroth, before Baal Zephon."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When Pharaoh came near, the children of Israel lifted up their eyes, and behold, the Egyptians were marching after them; and they were very afraid. The children of Israel cried out to the LORD."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They said to Moses, \u201cBecause there were no graves in Egypt, have you taken us away to die in the wilderness? Why have you treated us this way, to bring us out of Egypt?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t this the word that we spoke to you in Egypt, saying, \u2018Leave us alone, that we may serve the Egyptians\u2019? For it would have been better for us to serve the Egyptians than to die in the wilderness.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the people, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid. Stand still, and see the salvation of the LORD, which he will work for you today; for you will never again see the Egyptians whom you have seen today."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The LORD will fight for you, and you shall be still.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cWhy do you cry to me? Speak to the children of Israel, that they go forward."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Lift up your rod, and stretch out your hand over the sea and divide it. Then the children of Israel shall go into the middle of the sea on dry ground."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Behold, I myself will harden the hearts of the Egyptians, and they will go in after them. I will get myself honor over Pharaoh, and over all his armies, over his chariots, and over his horsemen."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The Egyptians shall know that I am the LORD when I have gotten myself honor over Pharaoh, over his chariots, and over his horsemen.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The angel of God, who went before the camp of Israel, moved and went behind them; and the pillar of cloud moved from before them, and stood behind them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"It came between the camp of Egypt and the camp of Israel. There was the cloud and the darkness, yet it gave light by night. One didn\u2019t come near the other all night."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses stretched out his hand over the sea, and the LORD caused the sea to go back by a strong east wind all night, and made the sea dry land, and the waters were divided."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The children of Israel went into the middle of the sea on the dry ground; and the waters were a wall to them on their right hand and on their left."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The Egyptians pursued, and went in after them into the middle of the sea: all of Pharaoh\u2019s horses, his chariots, and his horsemen."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"In the morning watch, the LORD looked out on the Egyptian army through the pillar of fire and of cloud, and confused the Egyptian army."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He took off their chariot wheels, and they drove them heavily; so that the Egyptians said, \u201cLet\u2019s flee from the face of Israel, for the LORD fights for them against the Egyptians!\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cStretch out your hand over the sea, that the waters may come again on the Egyptians, on their chariots, and on their horsemen.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Moses stretched out his hand over the sea, and the sea returned to its strength when the morning appeared; and the Egyptians fled against it. The LORD overthrew the Egyptians in the middle of the sea."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The waters returned, and covered the chariots and the horsemen, even all Pharaoh\u2019s army that went in after them into the sea. There remained not so much as one of them."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But the children of Israel walked on dry land in the middle of the sea, and the waters were a wall to them on their right hand and on their left."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Thus the LORD saved Israel that day out of the hand of the Egyptians; and Israel saw the Egyptians dead on the seashore."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Israel saw the great work which the LORD did to the Egyptians, and the people feared the LORD; and they believed in the LORD and in his servant Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Moses and the children of Israel sang this song to the LORD, and said,"],[1,"\u201cI will sing to the LORD, for he has triumphed gloriously."],[2,"He has thrown the horse and his rider into the sea."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is my strength and song."],[2,"He has become my salvation."],[1,"This is my God, and I will praise him;"],[2,"my father\u2019s God, and I will exalt him."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is a man of war."],[2,"The LORD is his name."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He has cast Pharaoh\u2019s chariots and his army into the sea."],[2,"His chosen captains are sunk in the Red Sea."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The deeps cover them."],[2,"They went down into the depths like a stone."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Your right hand, LORD, is glorious in power."],[2,"Your right hand, LORD, dashes the enemy in pieces."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"In the greatness of your excellency, you overthrow those who rise up against you."],[2,"You send out your wrath. It consumes them as stubble."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"With the blast of your nostrils, the waters were piled up."],[2,"The floods stood upright as a heap."],[2,"The deeps were congealed in the heart of the sea."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The enemy said, \u2018I will pursue. I will overtake. I will divide the plunder."],[2,"My desire will be satisfied on them."],[2,"I will draw my sword. My hand will destroy them.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You blew with your wind."],[2,"The sea covered them."],[2,"They sank like lead in the mighty waters."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is like you, LORD, among the gods?"],[2,"Who is like you, glorious in holiness,"],[2,"fearful in praises, doing wonders?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You stretched out your right hand."],[2,"The earth swallowed them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou, in your loving kindness, have led the people that you have redeemed."],[2,"You have guided them in your strength to your holy habitation."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The peoples have heard."],[2,"They tremble."],[2,"Pangs have taken hold of the inhabitants of Philistia."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the chiefs of Edom were dismayed."],[2,"Trembling takes hold of the mighty men of Moab."],[2,"All the inhabitants of Canaan have melted away."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Terror and dread falls on them."],[2,"By the greatness of your arm they are as still as a stone,"],[2,"until your people pass over, LORD,"],[2,"until the people you have purchased pass over."]]},{v:17,l:[[2,"You will bring them in, and plant them in the mountain of your inheritance,"],[2,"the place, LORD, which you have made for yourself to dwell in:"],[2,"the sanctuary, Lord, which your hands have established."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will reign forever and ever.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"For the horses of Pharaoh went in with his chariots and with his horsemen into the sea, and the LORD brought back the waters of the sea on them; but the children of Israel walked on dry land in the middle of the sea."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Miriam the prophetess, the sister of Aaron, took a tambourine in her hand; and all the women went out after her with tambourines and with dances."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Miriam answered them,"],[1,"\u201cSing to the LORD, for he has triumphed gloriously."],[1,"He has thrown the horse and his rider into the sea.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses led Israel onward from the Red Sea, and they went out into the wilderness of Shur; and they went three days in the wilderness, and found no water."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When they came to Marah, they couldn\u2019t drink from the waters of Marah, for they were bitter. Therefore its name was called Marah."]],f:["Marah means bitter."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The people murmured against Moses, saying, \u201cWhat shall we drink?\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Then he cried to the LORD. The LORD showed him a tree, and he threw it into the waters, and the waters were made sweet. There he made a statute and an ordinance for them, and there he tested them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIf you will diligently listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice, and will do that which is right in his eyes, and will pay attention to his commandments, and keep all his statutes, I will put none of the diseases on you which I have put on the Egyptians; for I am the LORD who heals you.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"They came to Elim, where there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees. They encamped there by the waters."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"They took their journey from Elim, and all the congregation of the children of Israel came to the wilderness of Sin, which is between Elim and Sinai, on the fifteenth day of the second month after their departing out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The whole congregation of the children of Israel murmured against Moses and against Aaron in the wilderness;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and the children of Israel said to them, \u201cWe wish that we had died by the LORD\u2019s hand in the land of Egypt, when we sat by the meat pots, when we ate our fill of bread, for you have brought us out into this wilderness to kill this whole assembly with hunger.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to Moses, \u201cBehold, I will rain bread from the sky for you, and the people shall go out and gather a day\u2019s portion every day, that I may test them, whether they will walk in my law or not."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It shall come to pass on the sixth day, that they shall prepare that which they bring in, and it shall be twice as much as they gather daily.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron said to all the children of Israel, \u201cAt evening, you shall know that the LORD has brought you out from the land of Egypt."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In the morning, you shall see the LORD\u2019s glory; because he hears your murmurings against the LORD. Who are we, that you murmur against us?\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cNow the LORD will give you meat to eat in the evening, and in the morning bread to satisfy you, because the LORD hears your murmurings which you murmur against him. And who are we? Your murmurings are not against us, but against the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moses said to Aaron, \u201cTell all the congregation of the children of Israel, \u2018Come close to the LORD, for he has heard your murmurings.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As Aaron spoke to the whole congregation of the children of Israel, they looked toward the wilderness, and behold, the LORD\u2019s glory appeared in the cloud."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cI have heard the murmurings of the children of Israel. Speak to them, saying, \u2018At evening you shall eat meat, and in the morning you shall be filled with bread. Then you will know that I am the LORD your God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"In the evening, quail came up and covered the camp; and in the morning the dew lay around the camp."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When the dew that lay had gone, behold, on the surface of the wilderness was a small round thing, small as the frost on the ground."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When the children of Israel saw it, they said to one another, \u201cWhat is it?\u201d For they didn\u2019t know what it was. Moses said to them, \u201cIt is the bread which the LORD has given you to eat."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"This is the thing which the LORD has commanded: \u2018Gather of it everyone according to his eating; an omer a head, according to the number of your persons, you shall take it, every man for those who are in his tent.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["An omer is about 2.2 liters or about 2.3 quarts"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did so, and some gathered more, some less."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When they measured it with an omer, he who gathered much had nothing over, and he who gathered little had no lack. They each gathered according to his eating."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Moses said to them, \u201cLet no one leave of it until the morning.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Notwithstanding they didn\u2019t listen to Moses, but some of them left of it until the morning, so it bred worms and became foul; and Moses was angry with them."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They gathered it morning by morning, everyone according to his eating. When the sun grew hot, it melted."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"On the sixth day, they gathered twice as much bread, two omers for each one; and all the rulers of the congregation came and told Moses."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThis is that which the LORD has spoken, \u2018Tomorrow is a solemn rest, a holy Sabbath to the LORD. Bake that which you want to bake, and boil that which you want to boil; and all that remains over lay up for yourselves to be kept until the morning.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They laid it up until the morning, as Moses ordered, and it didn\u2019t become foul, and there were no worms in it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cEat that today, for today is a Sabbath to the LORD. Today you shall not find it in the field."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Six days you shall gather it, but on the seventh day is the Sabbath. In it there shall be none.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"On the seventh day, some of the people went out to gather, and they found none."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cHow long do you refuse to keep my commandments and my laws?"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Behold, because the LORD has given you the Sabbath, therefore he gives you on the sixth day the bread of two days. Everyone stay in his place. Let no one go out of his place on the seventh day.\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"So the people rested on the seventh day."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"The house of Israel called its name \u201cManna\u201d, and it was like coriander seed, white; and its taste was like wafers with honey."]],f:["\u201cManna\u201d means \u201cWhat is it?\u201d"]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cThis is the thing which the LORD has commanded, \u2018Let an omer-full of it be kept throughout your generations, that they may see the bread with which I fed you in the wilderness, when I brought you out of the land of Egypt.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Moses said to Aaron, \u201cTake a pot, and put an omer-full of manna in it, and lay it up before the LORD, to be kept throughout your generations.\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"As the LORD commanded Moses, so Aaron laid it up before the Testimony, to be kept."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The children of Israel ate the manna forty years, until they came to an inhabited land. They ate the manna until they came to the borders of the land of Canaan."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Now an omer is one tenth of an ephah."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"All the congregation of the children of Israel traveled from the wilderness of Sin, starting according to the LORD\u2019s commandment, and encamped in Rephidim; but there was no water for the people to drink."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore the people quarreled with Moses, and said, \u201cGive us water to drink.\u201d"],[0,"Moses said to them, \u201cWhy do you quarrel with me? Why do you test the LORD?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The people were thirsty for water there; so the people murmured against Moses, and said, \u201cWhy have you brought us up out of Egypt, to kill us, our children, and our livestock with thirst?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses cried to the LORD, saying, \u201cWhat shall I do with these people? They are almost ready to stone me.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cWalk on before the people, and take the elders of Israel with you, and take the rod in your hand with which you struck the Nile, and go."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Behold, I will stand before you there on the rock in Horeb. You shall strike the rock, and water will come out of it, that the people may drink.\u201d Moses did so in the sight of the elders of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He called the name of the place Massah, and Meribah, because the children of Israel quarreled, and because they tested the LORD, saying, \u201cIs the LORD among us, or not?\u201d"]],f:["Massah means testing.","Meribah means quarreling."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Amalek came and fought with Israel in Rephidim."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moses said to Joshua, \u201cChoose men for us, and go out to fight with Amalek. Tomorrow I will stand on the top of the hill with God\u2019s rod in my hand.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So Joshua did as Moses had told him, and fought with Amalek; and Moses, Aaron, and Hur went up to the top of the hill."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When Moses held up his hand, Israel prevailed. When he let down his hand, Amalek prevailed."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But Moses\u2019 hands were heavy; so they took a stone, and put it under him, and he sat on it. Aaron and Hur held up his hands, the one on the one side, and the other on the other side. His hands were steady until sunset."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Joshua defeated Amalek and his people with the edge of the sword."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cWrite this for a memorial in a book, and rehearse it in the ears of Joshua: that I will utterly blot out the memory of Amalek from under the sky.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Moses built an altar, and called its name \u201cThe LORD our Banner\u201d."]],f:["Or, The LORD Nissi. LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThe LORD has sworn: \u2018The LORD will have war with Amalek from generation to generation.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jethro, the priest of Midian, Moses\u2019 father-in-law, heard of all that God had done for Moses and for Israel his people, how the LORD had brought Israel out of Egypt."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jethro, Moses\u2019 father-in-law, received Zipporah, Moses\u2019 wife, after he had sent her away,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and her two sons. The name of one son was Gershom, for Moses said, \u201cI have lived as a foreigner in a foreign land\u201d."]],f:["\u201cGershom\u201d sounds like the Hebrew for \u201can alien there\u201d."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The name of the other was Eliezer, for he said, \u201cMy father\u2019s God was my help and delivered me from Pharaoh\u2019s sword.\u201d"]],f:["Eliezer means \u201cGod is my helper\u201d."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jethro, Moses\u2019 father-in-law, came with Moses\u2019 sons and his wife to Moses into the wilderness where he was encamped, at the Mountain of God."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said to Moses, \u201cI, your father-in-law Jethro, have come to you with your wife, and her two sons with her.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went out to meet his father-in-law, and bowed and kissed him. They asked each other of their welfare, and they came into the tent."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Moses told his father-in-law all that the LORD had done to Pharaoh and to the Egyptians for Israel\u2019s sake, all the hardships that had come on them on the way, and how the LORD delivered them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Jethro rejoiced for all the goodness which the LORD had done to Israel, in that he had delivered them out of the hand of the Egyptians."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Jethro said, \u201cBlessed be the LORD, who has delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians, and out of the hand of Pharaoh; who has delivered the people from under the hand of the Egyptians."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now I know that the LORD is greater than all gods because of the way that they treated people arrogantly.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Jethro, Moses\u2019 father-in-law, took a burnt offering and sacrifices for God. Aaron came with all the elders of Israel, to eat bread with Moses\u2019 father-in-law before God."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, Moses sat to judge the people, and the people stood around Moses from the morning to the evening."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When Moses\u2019 father-in-law saw all that he did to the people, he said, \u201cWhat is this thing that you do for the people? Why do you sit alone, and all the people stand around you from morning to evening?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to his father-in-law, \u201cBecause the people come to me to inquire of God."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When they have a matter, they come to me, and I judge between a man and his neighbor, and I make them know the statutes of God, and his laws.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Moses\u2019 father-in-law said to him, \u201cThe thing that you do is not good."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You will surely wear away, both you, and this people that is with you; for the thing is too heavy for you. You are not able to perform it yourself alone."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Listen now to my voice. I will give you counsel, and God be with you. You represent the people before God, and bring the causes to God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall teach them the statutes and the laws, and shall show them the way in which they must walk, and the work that they must do."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Moreover you shall provide out of all the people able men which fear God: men of truth, hating unjust gain; and place such over them, to be rulers of thousands, rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Let them judge the people at all times. It shall be that every great matter they shall bring to you, but every small matter they shall judge themselves. So shall it be easier for you, and they shall share the load with you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If you will do this thing, and God commands you so, then you will be able to endure, and all these people also will go to their place in peace.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"So Moses listened to the voice of his father-in-law, and did all that he had said."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Moses chose able men out of all Israel, and made them heads over the people, rulers of thousands, rulers of hundreds, rulers of fifties, and rulers of tens."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They judged the people at all times. They brought the hard cases to Moses, but every small matter they judged themselves."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Moses let his father-in-law depart, and he went his way into his own land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the third month after the children of Israel had gone out of the land of Egypt, on that same day they came into the wilderness of Sinai."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When they had departed from Rephidim, and had come to the wilderness of Sinai, they encamped in the wilderness; and there Israel encamped before the mountain."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Moses went up to God, and the LORD called to him out of the mountain, saying, \u201cThis is what you shall tell the house of Jacob, and tell the children of Israel:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u2018You have seen what I did to the Egyptians, and how I bore you on eagles\u2019 wings, and brought you to myself."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now therefore, if you will indeed obey my voice and keep my covenant, then you shall be my own possession from among all peoples; for all the earth is mine;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and you shall be to me a kingdom of priests and a holy nation.\u2019 These are the words which you shall speak to the children of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses came and called for the elders of the people, and set before them all these words which the LORD commanded him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All the people answered together, and said, \u201cAll that the LORD has spoken we will do.\u201d"],[0,"Moses reported the words of the people to the LORD."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cBehold, I come to you in a thick cloud, that the people may hear when I speak with you, and may also believe you forever.\u201d Moses told the words of the people to the LORD."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cGo to the people, and sanctify them today and tomorrow, and let them wash their garments,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and be ready for the third day; for on the third day the LORD will come down in the sight of all the people on Mount Sinai."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall set bounds to the people all around, saying, \u2018Be careful that you don\u2019t go up onto the mountain, or touch its border. Whoever touches the mountain shall be surely put to death."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"No hand shall touch him, but he shall surely be stoned or shot through; whether it is animal or man, he shall not live.\u2019 When the trumpet sounds long, they shall come up to the mountain.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went down from the mountain to the people, and sanctified the people; and they washed their clothes."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said to the people, \u201cBe ready by the third day. Don\u2019t have sexual relations with a woman.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"On the third day, when it was morning, there were thunders and lightnings, and a thick cloud on the mountain, and the sound of an exceedingly loud trumpet; and all the people who were in the camp trembled."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Moses led the people out of the camp to meet God; and they stood at the lower part of the mountain."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All of Mount Sinai smoked, because the LORD descended on it in fire; and its smoke ascended like the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mountain quaked greatly."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When the sound of the trumpet grew louder and louder, Moses spoke, and God answered him by a voice."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD came down on Mount Sinai, to the top of the mountain. The LORD called Moses to the top of the mountain, and Moses went up."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cGo down, warn the people, lest they break through to the LORD to gaze, and many of them perish."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Let the priests also, who come near to the LORD, sanctify themselves, lest the LORD break out on them.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the LORD, \u201cThe people can\u2019t come up to Mount Sinai, for you warned us, saying, \u2018Set bounds around the mountain, and sanctify it.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cGo down! You shall bring Aaron up with you, but don\u2019t let the priests and the people break through to come up to the LORD, lest he break out against them.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"So Moses went down to the people, and told them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"God spoke all these words, saying,"]],f:["After \u201cGod\u201d, the Hebrew has the two letters \u201cAleph Tav\u201d (the first and last letters of the Hebrew alphabet), not as a word, but as a grammatical marker."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cI am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall have no other gods before me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not make for yourselves an idol, nor any image of anything that is in the heavens above, or that is on the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"you shall not bow yourself down to them, nor serve them, for I, the LORD your God, am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers on the children, on the third and on the fourth generation of those who hate me,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and showing loving kindness to thousands of those who love me and keep my commandments."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not misuse the name of the LORD your God, for the LORD will not hold him guiltless who misuses his name."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah.","or, You shall not take the name of the LORD your God in vain"]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cRemember the Sabbath day, to keep it holy."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall labor six days, and do all your work,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but the seventh day is a Sabbath to the LORD your God. You shall not do any work in it, you, nor your son, nor your daughter, your male servant, nor your female servant, nor your livestock, nor your stranger who is within your gates;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"for in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, the sea, and all that is in them, and rested the seventh day; therefore the LORD blessed the Sabbath day, and made it holy."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHonor your father and your mother, that your days may be long in the land which the LORD your God gives you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not murder."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not commit adultery."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not steal."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not give false testimony against your neighbor."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not covet your neighbor\u2019s house. You shall not covet your neighbor\u2019s wife, nor his male servant, nor his female servant, nor his ox, nor his donkey, nor anything that is your neighbor\u2019s.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people perceived the thunderings, the lightnings, the sound of the trumpet, and the mountain smoking. When the people saw it, they trembled, and stayed at a distance."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They said to Moses, \u201cSpeak with us yourself, and we will listen; but don\u2019t let God speak with us, lest we die.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the people, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for God has come to test you, and that his fear may be before you, that you won\u2019t sin.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The people stayed at a distance, and Moses came near to the thick darkness where God was."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cThis is what you shall tell the children of Israel: \u2018You yourselves have seen that I have talked with you from heaven."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You shall most certainly not make gods of silver or gods of gold for yourselves to be alongside me."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall make an altar of earth for me, and shall sacrifice on it your burnt offerings and your peace offerings, your sheep and your cattle. In every place where I record my name I will come to you and I will bless you."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"If you make me an altar of stone, you shall not build it of cut stones; for if you lift up your tool on it, you have polluted it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall not go up by steps to my altar, that your nakedness may not be exposed to it.\u2019"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow these are the ordinances which you shall set before them:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf you buy a Hebrew servant, he shall serve six years, and in the seventh he shall go out free without paying anything."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If he comes in by himself, he shall go out by himself. If he is married, then his wife shall go out with him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If his master gives him a wife and she bears him sons or daughters, the wife and her children shall be her master\u2019s, and he shall go out by himself."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But if the servant shall plainly say, \u2018I love my master, my wife, and my children. I will not go out free;\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"then his master shall bring him to God, and shall bring him to the door or to the doorpost, and his master shall bore his ear through with an awl, and he shall serve him forever."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man sells his daughter to be a female servant, she shall not go out as the male servants do."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If she doesn\u2019t please her master, who has married her to himself, then he shall let her be redeemed. He shall have no right to sell her to a foreign people, since he has dealt deceitfully with her."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If he marries her to his son, he shall deal with her as a daughter."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If he takes another wife to himself, he shall not diminish her food, her clothing, and her marital rights."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If he doesn\u2019t do these three things for her, she may go free without paying any money."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOne who strikes a man so that he dies shall surely be put to death,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but not if it is unintentional, but God allows it to happen; then I will appoint you a place where he shall flee."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If a man schemes and comes presumptuously on his neighbor to kill him, you shall take him from my altar, that he may die."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAnyone who attacks his father or his mother shall be surely put to death."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAnyone who kidnaps someone and sells him, or if he is found in his hand, he shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAnyone who curses his father or his mother shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf men quarrel and one strikes the other with a stone, or with his fist, and he doesn\u2019t die, but is confined to bed;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"if he rises again and walks around with his staff, then he who struck him shall be cleared; only he shall pay for the loss of his time, and shall provide for his healing until he is thoroughly healed."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man strikes his servant or his maid with a rod, and he dies under his hand, the man shall surely be punished."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Notwithstanding, if his servant gets up after a day or two, he shall not be punished, for the servant is his property."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf men fight and hurt a pregnant woman so that she gives birth prematurely, and yet no harm follows, he shall be surely fined as much as the woman\u2019s husband demands and the judges allow."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But if any harm follows, then you must take life for life,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand, foot for foot,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"burning for burning, wound for wound, and bruise for bruise."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man strikes his servant\u2019s eye, or his maid\u2019s eye, and destroys it, he shall let him go free for his eye\u2019s sake."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"If he strikes out his male servant\u2019s tooth, or his female servant\u2019s tooth, he shall let the servant go free for his tooth\u2019s sake."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a bull gores a man or a woman to death, the bull shall surely be stoned, and its meat shall not be eaten; but the owner of the bull shall not be held responsible."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But if the bull had a habit of goring in the past, and this has been testified to its owner, and he has not kept it in, but it has killed a man or a woman, the bull shall be stoned, and its owner shall also be put to death."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"If a ransom is imposed on him, then he shall give for the redemption of his life whatever is imposed."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Whether it has gored a son or has gored a daughter, according to this judgment it shall be done to him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"If the bull gores a male servant or a female servant, thirty shekels of silver shall be given to their master, and the ox shall be stoned."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 30 shekels is about 300 grams or about 10.6 ounces."]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man opens a pit, or if a man digs a pit and doesn\u2019t cover it, and a bull or a donkey falls into it,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"the owner of the pit shall make it good. He shall give money to its owner, and the dead animal shall be his."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf one man\u2019s bull injures another\u2019s, so that it dies, then they shall sell the live bull, and divide its price; and they shall also divide the dead animal."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Or if it is known that the bull was in the habit of goring in the past, and its owner has not kept it in, he shall surely pay bull for bull, and the dead animal shall be his own."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man steals an ox or a sheep, and kills it or sells it, he shall pay five oxen for an ox, and four sheep for a sheep."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"If the thief is found breaking in, and is struck so that he dies, there shall be no guilt of bloodshed for him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If the sun has risen on him, he is guilty of bloodshed. He shall make restitution. If he has nothing, then he shall be sold for his theft."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If the stolen property is found in his hand alive, whether it is ox, donkey, or sheep, he shall pay double."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man causes a field or vineyard to be eaten by letting his animal loose, and it grazes in another man\u2019s field, he shall make restitution from the best of his own field, and from the best of his own vineyard."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf fire breaks out, and catches in thorns so that the shocks of grain, or the standing grain, or the field are consumed; he who kindled the fire shall surely make restitution."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man delivers to his neighbor money or stuff to keep, and it is stolen out of the man\u2019s house, if the thief is found, he shall pay double."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If the thief isn\u2019t found, then the master of the house shall come near to God, to find out whether or not he has put his hand on his neighbor\u2019s goods."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For every matter of trespass, whether it is for ox, for donkey, for sheep, for clothing, or for any kind of lost thing, about which one says, \u2018This is mine,\u2019 the cause of both parties shall come before God. He whom God condemns shall pay double to his neighbor."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man delivers to his neighbor a donkey, an ox, a sheep, or any animal to keep, and it dies or is injured, or driven away, no man seeing it;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"the oath of the LORD shall be between them both, he has not put his hand on his neighbor\u2019s goods; and its owner shall accept it, and he shall not make restitution."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But if it is stolen from him, the one who stole shall make restitution to its owner."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"If it is torn in pieces, let him bring it for evidence. He shall not make good that which was torn."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man borrows anything of his neighbor\u2019s, and it is injured, or dies, its owner not being with it, he shall surely make restitution."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If its owner is with it, he shall not make it good. If it is a leased thing, it came for its lease."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man entices a virgin who isn\u2019t pledged to be married, and lies with her, he shall surely pay a dowry for her to be his wife."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If her father utterly refuses to give her to him, he shall pay money according to the dowry of virgins."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not allow a sorceress to live."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhoever has sex with an animal shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who sacrifices to any god, except to the LORD only, shall be utterly destroyed."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not wrong an alien or oppress him, for you were aliens in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not take advantage of any widow or fatherless child."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If you take advantage of them at all, and they cry at all to me, I will surely hear their cry;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and my wrath will grow hot, and I will kill you with the sword; and your wives shall be widows, and your children fatherless."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf you lend money to any of my people with you who is poor, you shall not be to him as a creditor. You shall not charge him interest."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"If you take your neighbor\u2019s garment as collateral, you shall restore it to him before the sun goes down,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"for that is his only covering, it is his garment for his skin. What would he sleep in? It will happen, when he cries to me, that I will hear, for I am gracious."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not blaspheme God, nor curse a ruler of your people."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not delay to offer from your harvest and from the outflow of your presses."],[0,"\u201cYou shall give the firstborn of your sons to me."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You shall do likewise with your cattle and with your sheep. It shall be with its mother seven days, then on the eighth day you shall give it to me."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall be holy men to me, therefore you shall not eat any meat that is torn by animals in the field. You shall cast it to the dogs."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not spread a false report. Don\u2019t join your hand with the wicked to be a malicious witness."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not follow a crowd to do evil. You shall not testify in court to side with a multitude to pervert justice."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall not favor a poor man in his cause."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf you meet your enemy\u2019s ox or his donkey going astray, you shall surely bring it back to him again."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"If you see the donkey of him who hates you fallen down under his burden, don\u2019t leave him. You shall surely help him with it."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not deny justice to your poor people in their lawsuits."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cKeep far from a false charge, and don\u2019t kill the innocent and righteous; for I will not justify the wicked."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall take no bribe, for a bribe blinds those who have sight and perverts the words of the righteous."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not oppress an alien, for you know the heart of an alien, since you were aliens in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor six years you shall sow your land, and shall gather in its increase,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"but the seventh year you shall let it rest and lie fallow, that the poor of your people may eat; and what they leave the animal of the field shall eat. In the same way, you shall deal with your vineyard and with your olive grove."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSix days you shall do your work, and on the seventh day you shall rest, that your ox and your donkey may have rest, and the son of your servant, and the alien may be refreshed."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBe careful to do all things that I have said to you; and don\u2019t invoke the name of other gods or even let them be heard out of your mouth."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall observe a feast to me three times a year."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall observe the feast of unleavened bread. Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread, as I commanded you, at the time appointed in the month Abib (for in it you came out of Egypt), and no one shall appear before me empty."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"And the feast of harvest, the first fruits of your labors, which you sow in the field; and the feast of ingathering, at the end of the year, when you gather in your labors out of the field."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Three times in the year all your males shall appear before the Lord GOD."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leavened bread. The fat of my feast shall not remain all night until the morning."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall bring the first of the first fruits of your ground into the house of the LORD your God."],[0,"\u201cYou shall not boil a young goat in its mother\u2019s milk."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I send an angel before you, to keep you by the way, and to bring you into the place which I have prepared."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Pay attention to him, and listen to his voice. Don\u2019t provoke him, for he will not pardon your disobedience, for my name is in him."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But if you indeed listen to his voice, and do all that I speak, then I will be an enemy to your enemies, and an adversary to your adversaries."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For my angel shall go before you, and bring you in to the Amorite, the Hittite, the Perizzite, the Canaanite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite; and I will cut them off."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall not bow down to their gods, nor serve them, nor follow their practices, but you shall utterly overthrow them and demolish their pillars."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You shall serve the LORD your God, and he will bless your bread and your water, and I will take sickness away from among you."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"No one will miscarry or be barren in your land. I will fulfill the number of your days."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"I will send my terror before you, and will confuse all the people to whom you come, and I will make all your enemies turn their backs to you."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"I will send the hornet before you, which will drive out the Hivite, the Canaanite, and the Hittite, from before you."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I will not drive them out from before you in one year, lest the land become desolate, and the animals of the field multiply against you."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Little by little I will drive them out from before you, until you have increased and inherit the land."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"I will set your border from the Red Sea even to the sea of the Philistines, and from the wilderness to the River; for I will deliver the inhabitants of the land into your hand, and you shall drive them out before you."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"You shall make no covenant with them, nor with their gods."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They shall not dwell in your land, lest they make you sin against me, for if you serve their gods, it will surely be a snare to you.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to Moses, \u201cCome up to the LORD, you, and Aaron, Nadab, and Abihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel; and worship from a distance."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Moses alone shall come near to the LORD, but they shall not come near. The people shall not go up with him.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses came and told the people all the LORD\u2019s words, and all the ordinances; and all the people answered with one voice, and said, \u201cAll the words which the LORD has spoken we will do.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses wrote all the LORD\u2019s words, then rose up early in the morning and built an altar at the base of the mountain, with twelve pillars for the twelve tribes of Israel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He sent young men of the children of Israel, who offered burnt offerings and sacrificed peace offerings of cattle to the LORD."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Moses took half of the blood and put it in basins, and half of the blood he sprinkled on the altar."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He took the book of the covenant and read it in the hearing of the people, and they said, \u201cWe will do all that the LORD has said, and be obedient.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses took the blood, and sprinkled it on the people, and said, \u201cLook, this is the blood of the covenant, which the LORD has made with you concerning all these words.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Moses, Aaron, Nadab, Abihu, and seventy of the elders of Israel went up."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They saw the God of Israel. Under his feet was like a paved work of sapphire stone, like the skies for clearness."]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He didn\u2019t lay his hand on the nobles of the children of Israel. They saw God, and ate and drank."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cCome up to me on the mountain, and stay here, and I will give you the stone tablets with the law and the commands that I have written, that you may teach them.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses rose up with Joshua, his servant, and Moses went up onto God\u2019s Mountain."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He said to the elders, \u201cWait here for us, until we come again to you. Behold, Aaron and Hur are with you. Whoever is involved in a dispute can go to them.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went up on the mountain, and the cloud covered the mountain."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s glory settled on Mount Sinai, and the cloud covered it six days. The seventh day he called to Moses out of the middle of the cloud."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The appearance of the LORD\u2019s glory was like devouring fire on the top of the mountain in the eyes of the children of Israel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Moses entered into the middle of the cloud, and went up on the mountain; and Moses was on the mountain forty days and forty nights."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, that they take an offering for me. From everyone whose heart makes him willing you shall take my offering."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This is the offering which you shall take from them: gold, silver, bronze,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"blue, purple, scarlet, fine linen, goats\u2019 hair,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"rams\u2019 skins dyed red, sea cow hides, acacia wood,"]],f:["or, fine leather"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"oil for the light, spices for the anointing oil and for the sweet incense,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"onyx stones, and stones to be set for the ephod and for the breastplate."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Let them make me a sanctuary, that I may dwell among them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"According to all that I show you, the pattern of the tabernacle, and the pattern of all of its furniture, even so you shall make it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey shall make an ark of acacia wood. Its length shall be two and a half cubits, its width a cubit and a half, and a cubit and a half its height."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall overlay it with pure gold. You shall overlay it inside and outside, and you shall make a gold molding around it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall cast four rings of gold for it, and put them in its four feet. Two rings shall be on the one side of it, and two rings on the other side of it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall make poles of acacia wood, and overlay them with gold."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall put the poles into the rings on the sides of the ark to carry the ark."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The poles shall be in the rings of the ark. They shall not be taken from it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall put the covenant which I shall give you into the ark."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall make a mercy seat of pure gold. Two and a half cubits shall be its length, and a cubit and a half its width."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall make two cherubim of hammered gold. You shall make them at the two ends of the mercy seat."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Make one cherub at the one end, and one cherub at the other end. You shall make the cherubim on its two ends of one piece with the mercy seat."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The cherubim shall spread out their wings upward, covering the mercy seat with their wings, with their faces toward one another. The faces of the cherubim shall be toward the mercy seat."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You shall put the mercy seat on top of the ark, and in the ark you shall put the covenant that I will give you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"There I will meet with you, and I will tell you from above the mercy seat, from between the two cherubim which are on the ark of the covenant, all that I command you for the children of Israel."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make a table of acacia wood. Its length shall be two cubits, and its width a cubit, and its height one and a half cubits."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall overlay it with pure gold, and make a gold molding around it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You shall make a rim of a hand width around it. You shall make a golden molding on its rim around it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall make four rings of gold for it, and put the rings in the four corners that are on its four feet."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The rings shall be close to the rim, for places for the poles to carry the table."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You shall make the poles of acacia wood, and overlay them with gold, that the table may be carried with them."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You shall make its dishes, its spoons, its ladles, and its bowls with which to pour out offerings. You shall make them of pure gold."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You shall set bread of the presence on the table before me always."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make a lamp stand of pure gold. The lamp stand shall be made of hammered work. Its base, its shaft, its cups, its buds, and its flowers shall be of one piece with it."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"There shall be six branches going out of its sides: three branches of the lamp stand out of its one side, and three branches of the lamp stand out of its other side;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"three cups made like almond blossoms in one branch, a bud and a flower; and three cups made like almond blossoms in the other branch, a bud and a flower, so for the six branches going out of the lamp stand;"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"and in the lamp stand four cups made like almond blossoms, its buds and its flowers;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"and a bud under two branches of one piece with it, and a bud under two branches of one piece with it, and a bud under two branches of one piece with it, for the six branches going out of the lamp stand."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Their buds and their branches shall be of one piece with it, all of it one beaten work of pure gold."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You shall make its lamps seven, and they shall light its lamps to give light to the space in front of it."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Its snuffers and its snuff dishes shall be of pure gold."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"It shall be made of a talent of pure gold, with all these accessories."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:40,l:[[0,"See that you make them after their pattern, which has been shown to you on the mountain."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover you shall make the tabernacle with ten curtains of fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet, with cherubim. You shall make them with the work of a skillful workman."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The length of each curtain shall be twenty-eight cubits, and the width of each curtain four cubits: all the curtains shall have one measure."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Five curtains shall be coupled together to one another, and the other five curtains shall be coupled to one another."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall make loops of blue on the edge of the one curtain from the edge in the coupling, and you shall do likewise on the edge of the curtain that is outermost in the second coupling."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall make fifty loops in the one curtain, and you shall make fifty loops in the edge of the curtain that is in the second coupling. The loops shall be opposite one another."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall make fifty clasps of gold, and couple the curtains to one another with the clasps. The tabernacle shall be a unit."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make curtains of goats\u2019 hair for a covering over the tabernacle. You shall make eleven curtains."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The length of each curtain shall be thirty cubits, and the width of each curtain four cubits: the eleven curtains shall have one measure."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall couple five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves, and shall double over the sixth curtain in the forefront of the tent."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall make fifty loops on the edge of the one curtain that is outermost in the coupling, and fifty loops on the edge of the curtain which is outermost in the second coupling."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall make fifty clasps of bronze, and put the clasps into the loops, and couple the tent together, that it may be one."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The overhanging part that remains of the curtains of the tent\u2014the half curtain that remains\u2014shall hang over the back of the tabernacle."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The cubit on the one side and the cubit on the other side, of that which remains in the length of the curtains of the tent, shall hang over the sides of the tabernacle on this side and on that side, to cover it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall make a covering for the tent of rams\u2019 skins dyed red, and a covering of sea cow hides above."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make the boards for the tabernacle of acacia wood, standing upright."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Ten cubits shall be the length of a board, and one and a half cubits the width of each board."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"There shall be two tenons in each board, joined to one another: thus you shall make for all the boards of the tabernacle."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall make twenty boards for the tabernacle, for the south side southward."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall make forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for its two tenons, and two sockets under another board for its two tenons."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For the second side of the tabernacle, on the north side, twenty boards,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and their forty sockets of silver; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For the far side of the tabernacle westward you shall make six boards."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You shall make two boards for the corners of the tabernacle in the far side."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They shall be double beneath, and in the same way they shall be whole to its top to one ring: thus shall it be for them both; they shall be for the two corners."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There shall be eight boards, and their sockets of silver, sixteen sockets; two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make bars of acacia wood: five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the side of the tabernacle, for the far side westward."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The middle bar in the middle of the boards shall pass through from end to end."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You shall overlay the boards with gold, and make their rings of gold for places for the bars. You shall overlay the bars with gold."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You shall set up the tabernacle according to the way that it was shown to you on the mountain."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make a veil of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, with cherubim. It shall be the work of a skillful workman."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"You shall hang it on four pillars of acacia overlaid with gold; their hooks shall be of gold, on four sockets of silver."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"You shall hang up the veil under the clasps, and shall bring the ark of the covenant in there within the veil. The veil shall separate the holy place from the most holy for you."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"You shall put the mercy seat on the ark of the covenant in the most holy place."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"You shall set the table outside the veil, and the lamp stand opposite the table on the side of the tabernacle toward the south. You shall put the table on the north side."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make a screen for the door of the Tent, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of the embroiderer."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You shall make for the screen five pillars of acacia, and overlay them with gold. Their hooks shall be of gold. You shall cast five sockets of bronze for them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make the altar of acacia wood, five cubits long, and five cubits wide. The altar shall be square. Its height shall be three cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters.","The altar was to be about 2.3\xd72.3\xd71.4 meters or about 7\xbd\xd77\xbd\xd74\xbd feet."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall make its horns on its four corners. Its horns shall be of one piece with it. You shall overlay it with bronze."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall make its pots to take away its ashes; and its shovels, its basins, its meat hooks, and its fire pans. You shall make all its vessels of bronze."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall make a grating for it of network of bronze. On the net you shall make four bronze rings in its four corners."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall put it under the ledge around the altar beneath, that the net may reach halfway up the altar."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall make poles for the altar, poles of acacia wood, and overlay them with bronze."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Its poles shall be put into the rings, and the poles shall be on the two sides of the altar when carrying it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall make it hollow with planks. They shall make it as it has been shown you on the mountain."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make the court of the tabernacle: for the south side southward there shall be hangings for the court of fine twined linen one hundred cubits long for one side."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Its pillars shall be twenty, and their sockets twenty, of bronze. The hooks of the pillars and their fillets shall be of silver."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Likewise for the length of the north side, there shall be hangings one hundred cubits long, and its pillars twenty, and their sockets twenty, of bronze; the hooks of the pillars, and their fillets, of silver."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For the width of the court on the west side shall be hangings of fifty cubits; their pillars ten, and their sockets ten."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The width of the court on the east side eastward shall be fifty cubits."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The hangings for the one side of the gate shall be fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For the other side shall be hangings of fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For the gate of the court shall be a screen of twenty cubits, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of the embroiderer; their pillars four, and their sockets four."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All the pillars of the court around shall be filleted with silver; their hooks of silver, and their sockets of bronze."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The length of the court shall be one hundred cubits, and the width fifty throughout, and the height five cubits, of fine twined linen, and their sockets of bronze."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"All the instruments of the tabernacle in all its service, and all its pins, and all the pins of the court, shall be of bronze."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall command the children of Israel, that they bring to you pure olive oil beaten for the light, to cause a lamp to burn continually."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"In the Tent of Meeting, outside the veil which is before the covenant, Aaron and his sons shall keep it in order from evening to morning before the LORD: it shall be a statute forever throughout their generations on the behalf of the children of Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBring Aaron your brother, and his sons with him, near to you from among the children of Israel, that he may minister to me in the priest\u2019s office: Aaron, with Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar, Aaron\u2019s sons."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall make holy garments for Aaron your brother, for glory and for beauty."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall speak to all who are wise-hearted, whom I have filled with the spirit of wisdom, that they make Aaron\u2019s garments to sanctify him, that he may minister to me in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"These are the garments which they shall make: a breastplate, an ephod, a robe, a fitted tunic, a turban, and a sash. They shall make holy garments for Aaron your brother and his sons, that he may minister to me in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They shall use the gold, and the blue, and the purple, and the scarlet, and the fine linen."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey shall make the ephod of gold, blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of the skillful workman."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It shall have two shoulder straps joined to the two ends of it, that it may be joined together."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The skillfully woven band, which is on it, shall be like its work and of the same piece; of gold, blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall take two onyx stones, and engrave on them the names of the children of Israel."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Six of their names on the one stone, and the names of the six that remain on the other stone, in the order of their birth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"With the work of an engraver in stone, like the engravings of a signet, you shall engrave the two stones, according to the names of the children of Israel. You shall make them to be enclosed in settings of gold."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall put the two stones on the shoulder straps of the ephod, to be stones of memorial for the children of Israel. Aaron shall bear their names before the LORD on his two shoulders for a memorial."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall make settings of gold,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and two chains of pure gold; you shall make them like cords of braided work. You shall put the braided chains on the settings."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make a breastplate of judgment, the work of the skillful workman; like the work of the ephod you shall make it; of gold, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, you shall make it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"It shall be square and folded double; a span shall be its length, and a span its width."]],f:["A span is the length from the tip of a man\u2019s thumb to the tip of his little finger when his hand is stretched out (about half a cubit, or 9 inches, or 22.8 cm.)"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall set in it settings of stones, four rows of stones: a row of ruby, topaz, and beryl shall be the first row;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and the second row a turquoise, a sapphire, and an emerald;"]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and the third row a jacinth, an agate, and an amethyst;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and the fourth row a chrysolite, an onyx, and a jasper. They shall be enclosed in gold in their settings."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The stones shall be according to the names of the children of Israel, twelve, according to their names; like the engravings of a signet, everyone according to his name, they shall be for the twelve tribes."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall make on the breastplate chains like cords, of braided work of pure gold."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You shall make on the breastplate two rings of gold, and shall put the two rings on the two ends of the breastplate."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall put the two braided chains of gold in the two rings at the ends of the breastplate."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The other two ends of the two braided chains you shall put on the two settings, and put them on the shoulder straps of the ephod in its forepart."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall make two rings of gold, and you shall put them on the two ends of the breastplate, on its edge, which is toward the side of the ephod inward."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"You shall make two rings of gold, and shall put them on the two shoulder straps of the ephod underneath, in its forepart, close by its coupling, above the skillfully woven band of the ephod."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They shall bind the breastplate by its rings to the rings of the ephod with a lace of blue, that it may be on the skillfully woven band of the ephod, and that the breastplate may not swing out from the ephod."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Aaron shall bear the names of the children of Israel in the breastplate of judgment on his heart, when he goes in to the holy place, for a memorial before the LORD continually."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You shall put in the breastplate of judgment the Urim and the Thummim; and they shall be on Aaron\u2019s heart, when he goes in before the LORD. Aaron shall bear the judgment of the children of Israel on his heart before the LORD continually."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make the robe of the ephod all of blue."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"It shall have a hole for the head in the middle of it. It shall have a binding of woven work around its hole, as it were the hole of a coat of mail, that it not be torn."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"On its hem you shall make pomegranates of blue, and of purple, and of scarlet, all around its hem; with bells of gold between and around them:"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"a golden bell and a pomegranate, a golden bell and a pomegranate, around the hem of the robe."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"It shall be on Aaron to minister: and its sound shall be heard when he goes in to the holy place before the LORD, and when he comes out, that he not die."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make a plate of pure gold, and engrave on it, like the engravings of a signet, \u2018HOLY TO THE LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You shall put it on a lace of blue, and it shall be on the sash. It shall be on the front of the sash."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"It shall be on Aaron\u2019s forehead, and Aaron shall bear the iniquity of the holy things, which the children of Israel shall make holy in all their holy gifts; and it shall be always on his forehead, that they may be accepted before the LORD."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"You shall weave the tunic with fine linen. You shall make a turban of fine linen. You shall make a sash, the work of the embroiderer."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make tunics for Aaron\u2019s sons. You shall make sashes for them. You shall make headbands for them, for glory and for beauty."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"You shall put them on Aaron your brother, and on his sons with him, and shall anoint them, and consecrate them, and sanctify them, that they may minister to me in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"You shall make them linen pants to cover their naked flesh. They shall reach from the waist even to the thighs."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"They shall be on Aaron and on his sons, when they go in to the Tent of Meeting, or when they come near to the altar to minister in the holy place, that they don\u2019t bear iniquity, and die. This shall be a statute forever to him and to his offspring after him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the thing that you shall do to them to make them holy, to minister to me in the priest\u2019s office: take one young bull and two rams without defect,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"unleavened bread, unleavened cakes mixed with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil. You shall make them of fine wheat flour."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall put them into one basket, and bring them in the basket, with the bull and the two rams."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall bring Aaron and his sons to the door of the Tent of Meeting, and shall wash them with water."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall take the garments, and put on Aaron the tunic, the robe of the ephod, the ephod, and the breastplate, and clothe him with the skillfully woven band of the ephod."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall set the turban on his head, and put the holy crown on the turban."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then you shall take the anointing oil, and pour it on his head, and anoint him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall bring his sons, and put tunics on them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall clothe them with belts, Aaron and his sons, and bind headbands on them. They shall have the priesthood by a perpetual statute. You shall consecrate Aaron and his sons."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall bring the bull before the Tent of Meeting; and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands on the head of the bull."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall kill the bull before the LORD at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall take of the blood of the bull, and put it on the horns of the altar with your finger; and you shall pour out all the blood at the base of the altar."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall take all the fat that covers the innards, the cover of the liver, the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, and burn them on the altar."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But the meat of the bull, and its skin, and its dung, you shall burn with fire outside of the camp. It is a sin offering."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall also take the one ram, and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands on the head of the ram."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall kill the ram, and you shall take its blood, and sprinkle it around on the altar."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall cut the ram into its pieces, and wash its innards, and its legs, and put them with its pieces, and with its head."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall burn the whole ram on the altar: it is a burnt offering to the LORD; it is a pleasant aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall take the other ram, and Aaron and his sons shall lay their hands on the head of the ram."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Then you shall kill the ram, and take some of its blood, and put it on the tip of the right ear of Aaron, and on the tip of the right ear of his sons, and on the thumb of their right hand, and on the big toe of their right foot; and sprinkle the blood around on the altar."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You shall take of the blood that is on the altar, and of the anointing oil, and sprinkle it on Aaron, and on his garments, and on his sons, and on the garments of his sons with him: and he shall be made holy, and his garments, and his sons, and his sons\u2019 garments with him."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Also you shall take some of the ram\u2019s fat, the fat tail, the fat that covers the innards, the cover of the liver, the two kidneys, the fat that is on them, and the right thigh (for it is a ram of consecration),"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and one loaf of bread, one cake of oiled bread, and one wafer out of the basket of unleavened bread that is before the LORD."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall put all of this in Aaron\u2019s hands, and in his sons\u2019 hands, and shall wave them for a wave offering before the LORD."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You shall take them from their hands, and burn them on the altar on the burnt offering, for a pleasant aroma before the LORD: it is an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall take the breast of Aaron\u2019s ram of consecration, and wave it for a wave offering before the LORD. It shall be your portion."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"You shall sanctify the breast of the wave offering and the thigh of the wave offering, which is waved, and which is raised up, of the ram of consecration, even of that which is for Aaron, and of that which is for his sons."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"It shall be for Aaron and his sons as their portion forever from the children of Israel; for it is a wave offering. It shall be a wave offering from the children of Israel of the sacrifices of their peace offerings, even their wave offering to the LORD."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe holy garments of Aaron shall be for his sons after him, to be anointed in them, and to be consecrated in them."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Seven days shall the son who is priest in his place put them on, when he comes into the Tent of Meeting to minister in the holy place."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall take the ram of consecration and boil its meat in a holy place."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Aaron and his sons shall eat the meat of the ram, and the bread that is in the basket, at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They shall eat those things with which atonement was made, to consecrate and sanctify them; but a stranger shall not eat of it, because they are holy."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"If anything of the meat of the consecration, or of the bread, remains to the morning, then you shall burn the remainder with fire. It shall not be eaten, because it is holy."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall do so to Aaron and to his sons, according to all that I have commanded you. You shall consecrate them seven days."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Every day you shall offer the bull of sin offering for atonement. You shall cleanse the altar when you make atonement for it. You shall anoint it, to sanctify it."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Seven days you shall make atonement for the altar, and sanctify it; and the altar shall be most holy. Whatever touches the altar shall be holy."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow this is that which you shall offer on the altar: two lambs a year old day by day continually."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The one lamb you shall offer in the morning; and the other lamb you shall offer at evening;"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"and with the one lamb a tenth part of an ephah of fine flour mixed with the fourth part of a hin of beaten oil, and the fourth part of a hin of wine for a drink offering."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons, so a fourth of a hin is about 1.6 liters."]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The other lamb you shall offer at evening, and shall do to it according to the meal offering of the morning and according to its drink offering, for a pleasant aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"It shall be a continual burnt offering throughout your generations at the door of the Tent of Meeting before the LORD, where I will meet with you, to speak there to you."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"There I will meet with the children of Israel; and the place shall be sanctified by my glory."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"I will sanctify the Tent of Meeting and the altar. I will also sanctify Aaron and his sons to minister to me in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will be their God."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"They shall know that I am the LORD their God, who brought them out of the land of Egypt, that I might dwell among them: I am the LORD their God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make an altar to burn incense on. You shall make it of acacia wood."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Its length shall be a cubit, and its width a cubit. It shall be square, and its height shall be two cubits. Its horns shall be of one piece with it."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall overlay it with pure gold, its top, its sides around it, and its horns; and you shall make a gold molding around it."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall make two golden rings for it under its molding; on its two ribs, on its two sides you shall make them; and they shall be for places for poles with which to bear it."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall make the poles of acacia wood, and overlay them with gold."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall put it before the veil that is by the ark of the covenant, before the mercy seat that is over the covenant, where I will meet with you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Aaron shall burn incense of sweet spices on it every morning. When he tends the lamps, he shall burn it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When Aaron lights the lamps at evening, he shall burn it, a perpetual incense before the LORD throughout your generations."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall offer no strange incense on it, nor burnt offering, nor meal offering; and you shall pour no drink offering on it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Aaron shall make atonement on its horns once in the year; with the blood of the sin offering of atonement once in the year he shall make atonement for it throughout your generations. It is most holy to the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen you take a census of the children of Israel, according to those who are counted among them, then each man shall give a ransom for his soul to the LORD when you count them, that there be no plague among them when you count them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They shall give this, everyone who passes over to those who are counted, half a shekel according to the shekel of the sanctuary (the shekel is twenty gerahs); half a shekel for an offering to the LORD."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces.","a gerah is about 0.5 grams or about 7.7 grains"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Everyone who passes over to those who are counted, from twenty years old and upward, shall give the offering to the LORD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The rich shall not give more, and the poor shall not give less, than the half shekel, when they give the offering of the LORD, to make atonement for your souls."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall take the atonement money from the children of Israel, and shall appoint it for the service of the Tent of Meeting; that it may be a memorial for the children of Israel before the LORD, to make atonement for your souls.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall also make a basin of bronze, and its base of bronze, in which to wash. You shall put it between the Tent of Meeting and the altar, and you shall put water in it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Aaron and his sons shall wash their hands and their feet in it."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When they go into the Tent of Meeting, they shall wash with water, that they don\u2019t die; or when they come near to the altar to minister, to burn an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So they shall wash their hands and their feet, that they not die. This shall be a statute forever to them, even to him and to his descendants throughout their generations.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"\u201cAlso take fine spices: of liquid myrrh, five hundred shekels; and of fragrant cinnamon half as much, even two hundred and fifty; and of fragrant cane, two hundred and fifty;"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 500 shekels is about 5 kilograms or about 11 pounds."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and of cassia five hundred, according to the shekel of the sanctuary; and a hin of olive oil."]],f:["A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You shall make it into a holy anointing oil, a perfume compounded after the art of the perfumer: it shall be a holy anointing oil."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall use it to anoint the Tent of Meeting, the ark of the covenant,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"the table and all its articles, the lamp stand and its accessories, the altar of incense,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"the altar of burnt offering with all its utensils, and the basin with its base."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You shall sanctify them, that they may be most holy. Whatever touches them shall be holy."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You shall anoint Aaron and his sons, and sanctify them, that they may minister to me in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"You shall speak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018This shall be a holy anointing oil to me throughout your generations."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"It shall not be poured on man\u2019s flesh, and do not make any like it, according to its composition. It is holy. It shall be holy to you."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Whoever compounds any like it, or whoever puts any of it on a stranger, he shall be cut off from his people.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cTake to yourself sweet spices, gum resin, onycha, and galbanum: sweet spices with pure frankincense. There shall be an equal weight of each."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"You shall make incense of it, a perfume after the art of the perfumer, seasoned with salt, pure and holy."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"You shall beat some of it very small, and put some of it before the covenant in the Tent of Meeting, where I will meet with you. It shall be to you most holy."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You shall not make this incense, according to its composition, for yourselves: it shall be to you holy for the LORD."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Whoever shall make any like that, to smell of it, he shall be cut off from his people.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I have called by name Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I have filled him with the Spirit of God, in wisdom, and in understanding, and in knowledge, and in all kinds of workmanship,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"to devise skillful works, to work in gold, and in silver, and in bronze,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and in cutting of stones for setting, and in carving of wood, to work in all kinds of workmanship."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Behold, I myself have appointed with him Oholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan; and in the heart of all who are wise-hearted I have put wisdom, that they may make all that I have commanded you:"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"the Tent of Meeting, the ark of the covenant, the mercy seat that is on it, all the furniture of the Tent,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"the table and its vessels, the pure lamp stand with all its vessels, the altar of incense,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"the altar of burnt offering with all its vessels, the basin and its base,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"the finely worked garments\u2014the holy garments for Aaron the priest, the garments of his sons to minister in the priest\u2019s office\u2014"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"the anointing oil, and the incense of sweet spices for the holy place: according to all that I have commanded you they shall do.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak also to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018Most certainly you shall keep my Sabbaths; for it is a sign between me and you throughout your generations, that you may know that I am the LORD who sanctifies you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall keep the Sabbath therefore, for it is holy to you. Everyone who profanes it shall surely be put to death; for whoever does any work therein, that soul shall be cut off from among his people."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Six days shall work be done, but on the seventh day is a Sabbath of solemn rest, holy to the LORD. Whoever does any work on the Sabbath day shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Therefore the children of Israel shall keep the Sabbath, to observe the Sabbath throughout their generations, for a perpetual covenant."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It is a sign between me and the children of Israel forever; for in six days the LORD made heaven and earth, and on the seventh day he rested, and was refreshed.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"When he finished speaking with him on Mount Sinai, he gave Moses the two tablets of the covenant, stone tablets, written with God\u2019s finger."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the people saw that Moses delayed coming down from the mountain, the people gathered themselves together to Aaron, and said to him, \u201cCome, make us gods, which shall go before us; for as for this Moses, the man who brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we don\u2019t know what has become of him.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Aaron said to them, \u201cTake off the golden rings, which are in the ears of your wives, of your sons, and of your daughters, and bring them to me.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people took off the golden rings which were in their ears, and brought them to Aaron."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He received what they handed him, fashioned it with an engraving tool, and made it a molded calf. Then they said, \u201cThese are your gods, Israel, which brought you up out of the land of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When Aaron saw this, he built an altar before it; and Aaron made a proclamation, and said, \u201cTomorrow shall be a feast to the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"They rose up early on the next day, and offered burnt offerings, and brought peace offerings; and the people sat down to eat and to drink, and rose up to play."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, \u201cGo, get down; for your people, whom you brought up out of the land of Egypt, have corrupted themselves!"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They have turned away quickly out of the way which I commanded them. They have made themselves a molded calf, and have worshiped it, and have sacrificed to it, and said, \u2018These are your gods, Israel, which brought you up out of the land of Egypt.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cI have seen these people, and behold, they are a stiff-necked people."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now therefore leave me alone, that my wrath may burn hot against them, and that I may consume them; and I will make of you a great nation.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses begged the LORD his God, and said, \u201cLORD, why does your wrath burn hot against your people, that you have brought out of the land of Egypt with great power and with a mighty hand?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Why should the Egyptians talk, saying, \u2018He brought them out for evil, to kill them in the mountains, and to consume them from the surface of the earth\u2019? Turn from your fierce wrath, and turn away from this evil against your people."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Remember Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, your servants, to whom you swore by your own self, and said to them, \u2018I will multiply your offspring as the stars of the sky, and all this land that I have spoken of I will give to your offspring, and they shall inherit it forever.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So the LORD turned away from the evil which he said he would do to his people."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses turned, and went down from the mountain, with the two tablets of the covenant in his hand; tablets that were written on both their sides. They were written on one side and on the other."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The tablets were the work of God, and the writing was the writing of God, engraved on the tablets."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joshua heard the noise of the people as they shouted, he said to Moses, \u201cThere is the noise of war in the camp.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIt isn\u2019t the voice of those who shout for victory. It is not the voice of those who cry for being overcome; but the noise of those who sing that I hear.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"As soon as he came near to the camp, he saw the calf and the dancing. Then Moses\u2019 anger grew hot, and he threw the tablets out of his hands, and broke them beneath the mountain."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He took the calf which they had made, and burned it with fire, ground it to powder, and scattered it on the water, and made the children of Israel drink it."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Aaron, \u201cWhat did these people do to you, that you have brought a great sin on them?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Aaron said, \u201cDon\u2019t let the anger of my lord grow hot. You know the people, that they are set on evil."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For they said to me, \u2018Make us gods, which shall go before us. As for this Moses, the man who brought us up out of the land of Egypt, we don\u2019t know what has become of him.\u2019"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I said to them, \u2018Whoever has any gold, let them take it off.\u2019 So they gave it to me; and I threw it into the fire, and out came this calf.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"When Moses saw that the people were out of control, (for Aaron had let them lose control, causing derision among their enemies),"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"then Moses stood in the gate of the camp, and said, \u201cWhoever is on the LORD\u2019s side, come to me!\u201d"],[0,"All the sons of Levi gathered themselves together to him."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018Every man put his sword on his thigh, and go back and forth from gate to gate throughout the camp, and every man kill his brother, and every man his companion, and every man his neighbor.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The sons of Levi did according to the word of Moses. About three thousand men fell of the people that day."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cConsecrate yourselves today to the LORD, for every man was against his son and against his brother, that he may give you a blessing today.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, Moses said to the people, \u201cYou have sinned a great sin. Now I will go up to the LORD. Perhaps I shall make atonement for your sin.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses returned to the LORD, and said, \u201cOh, this people have sinned a great sin, and have made themselves gods of gold."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Yet now, if you will, forgive their sin\u2014and if not, please blot me out of your book which you have written.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cWhoever has sinned against me, I will blot him out of my book."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Now go, lead the people to the place of which I have spoken to you. Behold, my angel shall go before you. Nevertheless, in the day when I punish, I will punish them for their sin.\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The LORD struck the people, because of what they did with the calf, which Aaron made."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, \u201cDepart, go up from here, you and the people that you have brought up out of the land of Egypt, to the land of which I swore to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, saying, \u2018I will give it to your offspring.\u2019"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will send an angel before you; and I will drive out the Canaanite, the Amorite, and the Hittite, and the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Go to a land flowing with milk and honey; but I will not go up among you, for you are a stiff-necked people, lest I consume you on the way.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When the people heard this evil news, they mourned; and no one put on his jewelry."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD had said to Moses, \u201cTell the children of Israel, \u2018You are a stiff-necked people. If I were to go up among you for one moment, I would consume you. Therefore now take off your jewelry from you, that I may know what to do to you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel stripped themselves of their jewelry from Mount Horeb onward."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Moses used to take the tent and pitch it outside the camp, far away from the camp, and he called it \u201cThe Tent of Meeting.\u201d Everyone who sought the LORD went out to the Tent of Meeting, which was outside the camp."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When Moses went out to the Tent, all the people rose up, and stood, everyone at their tent door, and watched Moses, until he had gone into the Tent."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When Moses entered into the Tent, the pillar of cloud descended, stood at the door of the Tent, and the LORD spoke with Moses."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All the people saw the pillar of cloud stand at the door of the Tent, and all the people rose up and worshiped, everyone at their tent door."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses face to face, as a man speaks to his friend. He turned again into the camp, but his servant Joshua, the son of Nun, a young man, didn\u2019t depart from the Tent."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the LORD, \u201cBehold, you tell me, \u2018Bring up this people;\u2019 and you haven\u2019t let me know whom you will send with me. Yet you have said, \u2018I know you by name, and you have also found favor in my sight.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now therefore, if I have found favor in your sight, please show me your way, now, that I may know you, so that I may find favor in your sight; and consider that this nation is your people.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cMy presence will go with you, and I will give you rest.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to him, \u201cIf your presence doesn\u2019t go with me, don\u2019t carry us up from here."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For how would people know that I have found favor in your sight, I and your people? Isn\u2019t it that you go with us, so that we are separated, I and your people, from all the people who are on the surface of the earth?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cI will do this thing also that you have spoken; for you have found favor in my sight, and I know you by name.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cPlease show me your glory.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI will make all my goodness pass before you, and will proclaim the LORD\u2019s name before you. I will be gracious to whom I will be gracious, and will show mercy on whom I will show mercy.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou cannot see my face, for man may not see me and live.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD also said, \u201cBehold, there is a place by me, and you shall stand on the rock."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"It will happen, while my glory passes by, that I will put you in a cleft of the rock, and will cover you with my hand until I have passed by;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"then I will take away my hand, and you will see my back; but my face shall not be seen.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cChisel two stone tablets like the first. I will write on the tablets the words that were on the first tablets, which you broke."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Be ready by the morning, and come up in the morning to Mount Sinai, and present yourself there to me on the top of the mountain."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"No one shall come up with you or be seen anywhere on the mountain. Do not let the flocks or herds graze in front of that mountain.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"He chiseled two tablets of stone like the first; then Moses rose up early in the morning, and went up to Mount Sinai, as the LORD had commanded him, and took in his hand two stone tablets."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD descended in the cloud, and stood with him there, and proclaimed the LORD\u2019s name."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD passed by before him, and proclaimed, \u201cThe LORD! The LORD, a merciful and gracious God, slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness and truth,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"keeping loving kindness for thousands, forgiving iniquity and disobedience and sin; and who will by no means clear the guilty, visiting the iniquity of the fathers on the children, and on the children\u2019s children, on the third and on the fourth generation.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses hurried and bowed his head toward the earth, and worshiped."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIf now I have found favor in your sight, Lord, please let the Lord go among us, even though this is a stiff-necked people; pardon our iniquity and our sin, and take us for your inheritance.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBehold, I make a covenant: before all your people I will do marvels, such as have not been worked in all the earth, nor in any nation; and all the people among whom you are shall see the work of the LORD; for it is an awesome thing that I do with you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Observe that which I command you today. Behold, I will drive out before you the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Be careful, lest you make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land where you are going, lest it be for a snare among you;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but you shall break down their altars, and dash in pieces their pillars, and you shall cut down their Asherah poles;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"for you shall worship no other god; for the LORD, whose name is Jealous, is a jealous God."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t make a covenant with the inhabitants of the land, lest they play the prostitute after their gods, and sacrifice to their gods, and one call you and you eat of his sacrifice;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and you take of their daughters to your sons, and their daughters play the prostitute after their gods, and make your sons play the prostitute after their gods."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall make no cast idols for yourselves."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall keep the feast of unleavened bread. Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread, as I commanded you, at the time appointed in the month Abib; for in the month Abib you came out of Egypt."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll that opens the womb is mine; and all your livestock that is male, the firstborn of cow and sheep."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall redeem the firstborn of a donkey with a lamb. If you will not redeem it, then you shall break its neck. You shall redeem all the firstborn of your sons. No one shall appear before me empty."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSix days you shall work, but on the seventh day you shall rest: in plowing time and in harvest you shall rest."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall observe the feast of weeks with the first fruits of wheat harvest, and the feast of harvest at the year\u2019s end."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Three times in the year all your males shall appear before the Lord GOD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For I will drive out nations before you and enlarge your borders; neither shall any man desire your land when you go up to appear before the LORD, your God, three times in the year."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not offer the blood of my sacrifice with leavened bread. The sacrifice of the feast of the Passover shall not be left to the morning."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall bring the first of the first fruits of your ground to the house of the LORD your God."],[0,"\u201cYou shall not boil a young goat in its mother\u2019s milk.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cWrite these words; for in accordance with these words I have made a covenant with you and with Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He was there with the LORD forty days and forty nights; he neither ate bread, nor drank water. He wrote on the tablets the words of the covenant, the ten commandments."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When Moses came down from Mount Sinai with the two tablets of the covenant in Moses\u2019 hand, when he came down from the mountain, Moses didn\u2019t know that the skin of his face shone by reason of his speaking with him."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When Aaron and all the children of Israel saw Moses, behold, the skin of his face shone; and they were afraid to come near him."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Moses called to them, and Aaron and all the rulers of the congregation returned to him; and Moses spoke to them."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Afterward all the children of Israel came near, and he gave them all the commandments that the LORD had spoken with him on Mount Sinai."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"When Moses was done speaking with them, he put a veil on his face."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But when Moses went in before the LORD to speak with him, he took the veil off, until he came out; and he came out, and spoke to the children of Israel that which he was commanded."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The children of Israel saw Moses\u2019 face, that the skin of Moses\u2019 face shone; so Moses put the veil on his face again, until he went in to speak with him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses assembled all the congregation of the children of Israel, and said to them, \u201cThese are the words which the LORD has commanded, that you should do them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u2018Six days shall work be done, but on the seventh day there shall be a holy day for you, a Sabbath of solemn rest to the LORD: whoever does any work in it shall be put to death."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall kindle no fire throughout your habitations on the Sabbath day.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke to all the congregation of the children of Israel, saying, \u201cThis is the thing which the LORD commanded, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u2018Take from among you an offering to the LORD. Whoever is of a willing heart, let him bring it as the LORD\u2019s offering: gold, silver, bronze,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"blue, purple, scarlet, fine linen, goats\u2019 hair,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"rams\u2019 skins dyed red, sea cow hides, acacia wood,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"oil for the light, spices for the anointing oil and for the sweet incense,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"onyx stones, and stones to be set for the ephod and for the breastplate."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Let every wise-hearted man among you come, and make all that the LORD has commanded:"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"the tabernacle, its outer covering, its roof, its clasps, its boards, its bars, its pillars, and its sockets;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"the ark, and its poles, the mercy seat, the veil of the screen;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"the table with its poles and all its vessels, and the show bread;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the lamp stand also for the light, with its vessels, its lamps, and the oil for the light;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and the altar of incense with its poles, the anointing oil, the sweet incense, the screen for the door, at the door of the tabernacle;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the altar of burnt offering, with its grating of bronze, its poles, and all its vessels, the basin and its base;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the hangings of the court, its pillars, their sockets, and the screen for the gate of the court;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"the pins of the tabernacle, the pins of the court, and their cords;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the finely worked garments for ministering in the holy place\u2014the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons\u2014to minister in the priest\u2019s office.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"All the congregation of the children of Israel departed from the presence of Moses."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They came, everyone whose heart stirred him up, and everyone whom his spirit made willing, and brought the LORD\u2019s offering for the work of the Tent of Meeting, and for all of its service, and for the holy garments."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They came, both men and women, as many as were willing-hearted, and brought brooches, earrings, signet rings, and armlets, all jewels of gold; even every man who offered an offering of gold to the LORD."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Everyone with whom was found blue, purple, scarlet, fine linen, goats\u2019 hair, rams\u2019 skins dyed red, and sea cow hides, brought them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Everyone who offered an offering of silver and bronze brought the LORD\u2019s offering; and everyone with whom was found acacia wood for any work of the service, brought it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"All the women who were wise-hearted spun with their hands, and brought that which they had spun: the blue, the purple, the scarlet, and the fine linen."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"All the women whose heart stirred them up in wisdom spun the goats\u2019 hair."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The rulers brought the onyx stones and the stones to be set for the ephod and for the breastplate;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"with the spice and the oil for the light, for the anointing oil, and for the sweet incense."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The children of Israel brought a free will offering to the LORD; every man and woman whose heart made them willing to bring for all the work, which the LORD had commanded to be made by Moses."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the children of Israel, \u201cBehold, the LORD has called by name Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He has filled him with the Spirit of God, in wisdom, in understanding, in knowledge, and in all kinds of workmanship;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and to make skillful works, to work in gold, in silver, in bronze,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"in cutting of stones for setting, and in carving of wood, to work in all kinds of skillful workmanship."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He has put in his heart that he may teach, both he and Oholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"He has filled them with wisdom of heart to work all kinds of workmanship, of the engraver, of the skillful workman, and of the embroiderer, in blue, in purple, in scarlet, and in fine linen, and of the weaver, even of those who do any workmanship, and of those who make skillful works."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBezalel and Oholiab shall work with every wise-hearted man, in whom the LORD has put wisdom and understanding to know how to do all the work for the service of the sanctuary, according to all that the LORD has commanded.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses called Bezalel and Oholiab, and every wise-hearted man, in whose heart the LORD had put wisdom, even everyone whose heart stirred him up to come to the work to do it."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They received from Moses all the offering which the children of Israel had brought for the work of the service of the sanctuary, with which to make it. They kept bringing free will offerings to him every morning."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"All the wise men, who performed all the work of the sanctuary, each came from his work which he did."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They spoke to Moses, saying, \u201cThe people have brought much more than enough for the service of the work which the LORD commanded to make.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses gave a commandment, and they caused it to be proclaimed throughout the camp, saying, \u201cLet neither man nor woman make anything else for the offering for the sanctuary.\u201d So the people were restrained from bringing."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the stuff they had was sufficient to do all the work, and too much."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"All the wise-hearted men among those who did the work made the tabernacle with ten curtains of fine twined linen, blue, purple, and scarlet. They made them with cherubim, the work of a skillful workman."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The length of each curtain was twenty-eight cubits, and the width of each curtain four cubits. All the curtains had one measure."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He coupled five curtains to one another, and the other five curtains he coupled to one another."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He made loops of blue on the edge of the one curtain from the edge in the coupling. Likewise he made in the edge of the curtain that was outermost in the second coupling."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He made fifty loops in the one curtain, and he made fifty loops in the edge of the curtain that was in the second coupling. The loops were opposite to one another."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He made fifty clasps of gold, and coupled the curtains to one another with the clasps: so the tabernacle was a unit."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He made curtains of goats\u2019 hair for a covering over the tabernacle. He made them eleven curtains."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The length of each curtain was thirty cubits, and four cubits the width of each curtain. The eleven curtains had one measure."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He coupled five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He made fifty loops on the edge of the curtain that was outermost in the coupling, and he made fifty loops on the edge of the curtain which was outermost in the second coupling."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He made fifty clasps of bronze to couple the tent together, that it might be a unit."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He made a covering for the tent of rams\u2019 skins dyed red, and a covering of sea cow hides above."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the boards for the tabernacle of acacia wood, standing up."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Ten cubits was the length of a board, and a cubit and a half the width of each board."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Each board had two tenons, joined to one another. He made all the boards of the tabernacle this way."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He made the boards for the tabernacle, twenty boards for the south side southward."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He made forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards: two sockets under one board for its two tenons, and two sockets under another board for its two tenons."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For the second side of the tabernacle, on the north side, he made twenty boards"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and their forty sockets of silver: two sockets under one board, and two sockets under another board."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For the far part of the tabernacle westward he made six boards."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He made two boards for the corners of the tabernacle in the far part."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They were double beneath, and in the same way they were all the way to its top to one ring. He did this to both of them in the two corners."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"There were eight boards and their sockets of silver, sixteen sockets\u2014under every board two sockets."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"He made bars of acacia wood: five for the boards of the one side of the tabernacle,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and five bars for the boards of the other side of the tabernacle, and five bars for the boards of the tabernacle for the hinder part westward."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He made the middle bar to pass through in the middle of the boards from the one end to the other."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He overlaid the boards with gold, and made their rings of gold as places for the bars, and overlaid the bars with gold."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the veil of blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen, with cherubim. He made it the work of a skillful workman."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He made four pillars of acacia for it, and overlaid them with gold. Their hooks were of gold. He cast four sockets of silver for them."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He made a screen for the door of the tent, of blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen, the work of an embroiderer;"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"and the five pillars of it with their hooks. He overlaid their capitals and their fillets with gold, and their five sockets were of bronze."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Bezalel made the ark of acacia wood. Its length was two and a half cubits, and its width a cubit and a half, and a cubit and a half its height."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He overlaid it with pure gold inside and outside, and made a molding of gold for it around it."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He cast four rings of gold for it in its four feet\u2014two rings on its one side, and two rings on its other side."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He made poles of acacia wood and overlaid them with gold."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He put the poles into the rings on the sides of the ark, to bear the ark."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He made a mercy seat of pure gold. Its length was two and a half cubits, and a cubit and a half its width."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He made two cherubim of gold. He made them of beaten work, at the two ends of the mercy seat:"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"one cherub at the one end, and one cherub at the other end. He made the cherubim of one piece with the mercy seat at its two ends."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The cherubim spread out their wings above, covering the mercy seat with their wings, with their faces toward one another. The faces of the cherubim were toward the mercy seat."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the table of acacia wood. Its length was two cubits, and its width was a cubit, and its height was a cubit and a half."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He overlaid it with pure gold, and made a gold molding around it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He made a border of a hand\u2019s width around it, and made a golden molding on its border around it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He cast four rings of gold for it, and put the rings in the four corners that were on its four feet."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The rings were close by the border, the places for the poles to carry the table."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He made the poles of acacia wood, and overlaid them with gold, to carry the table."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He made the vessels which were on the table, its dishes, its spoons, its bowls, and its pitchers with which to pour out, of pure gold."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the lamp stand of pure gold. He made the lamp stand of beaten work. Its base, its shaft, its cups, its buds, and its flowers were of one piece with it."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"There were six branches going out of its sides: three branches of the lamp stand out of its one side, and three branches of the lamp stand out of its other side:"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"three cups made like almond blossoms in one branch, a bud and a flower, and three cups made like almond blossoms in the other branch, a bud and a flower; so for the six branches going out of the lamp stand."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"In the lamp stand were four cups made like almond blossoms, its buds and its flowers;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and a bud under two branches of one piece with it, and a bud under two branches of one piece with it, and a bud under two branches of one piece with it, for the six branches going out of it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Their buds and their branches were of one piece with it. The whole thing was one beaten work of pure gold."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He made its seven lamps, and its snuffers, and its snuff dishes, of pure gold."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He made it of a talent of pure gold, with all its vessels."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the altar of incense of acacia wood. It was square: its length was a cubit, and its width a cubit. Its height was two cubits. Its horns were of one piece with it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He overlaid it with pure gold: its top, its sides around it, and its horns. He made a gold molding around it."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He made two golden rings for it under its molding crown, on its two ribs, on its two sides, for places for poles with which to carry it."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He made the poles of acacia wood, and overlaid them with gold."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He made the holy anointing oil and the pure incense of sweet spices, after the art of the perfumer."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the altar of burnt offering of acacia wood. It was square. Its length was five cubits, its width was five cubits, and its height was three cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He made its horns on its four corners. Its horns were of one piece with it, and he overlaid it with bronze."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He made all the vessels of the altar: the pots, the shovels, the basins, the forks, and the fire pans. He made all its vessels of bronze."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He made for the altar a grating of a network of bronze, under the ledge around it beneath, reaching halfway up."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He cast four rings for the four corners of bronze grating, to be places for the poles."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He made the poles of acacia wood, and overlaid them with bronze."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He put the poles into the rings on the sides of the altar, with which to carry it. He made it hollow with planks."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the basin of bronze, and its base of bronze, out of the mirrors of the ministering women who ministered at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the court: for the south side southward the hangings of the court were of fine twined linen, one hundred cubits;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"their pillars were twenty, and their sockets twenty, of bronze; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets were of silver."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the north side one hundred cubits, their pillars twenty, and their sockets twenty, of bronze; the hooks of the pillars, and their fillets, of silver."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For the west side were hangings of fifty cubits, their pillars ten, and their sockets ten; the hooks of the pillars, and their fillets, of silver."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For the east side eastward fifty cubits,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the hangings for the one side were fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and so for the other side: on this hand and that hand by the gate of the court were hangings of fifteen cubits; their pillars three, and their sockets three."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"All the hangings around the court were of fine twined linen."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The sockets for the pillars were of bronze. The hooks of the pillars and their fillets were of silver. Their capitals were overlaid with silver. All the pillars of the court had silver bands."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The screen for the gate of the court was the work of the embroiderer, of blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen. Twenty cubits was the length, and the height along the width was five cubits, like the hangings of the court."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Their pillars were four, and their sockets four, of bronze; their hooks of silver, and the overlaying of their capitals, and their fillets, of silver."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"All the pins of the tabernacle, and around the court, were of bronze."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the amounts of materials used for the tabernacle, even the Tabernacle of the Testimony, as they were counted, according to the commandment of Moses, for the service of the Levites, by the hand of Ithamar, the son of Aaron the priest."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, of the tribe of Judah, made all that the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"With him was Oholiab, the son of Ahisamach, of the tribe of Dan, an engraver, and a skillful workman, and an embroiderer in blue, in purple, in scarlet, and in fine linen."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"All the gold that was used for the work in all the work of the sanctuary, even the gold of the offering, was twenty-nine talents and seven hundred thirty shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces.","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.32 Troy ounces."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The silver of those who were counted of the congregation was one hundred talents and one thousand seven hundred seventy-five shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary:"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"a beka a head, that is, half a shekel, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, for everyone who passed over to those who were counted, from twenty years old and upward, for six hundred three thousand five hundred fifty men."]],f:["a beka is about 5 grams or about 0.175 ounces","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The one hundred talents of silver were for casting the sockets of the sanctuary and the sockets of the veil: one hundred sockets for the one hundred talents, one talent per socket."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds."]},{v:28,l:[[0,"From the one thousand seven hundred seventy-five shekels he made hooks for the pillars, overlaid their capitals, and made fillets for them."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 1775 shekels is about 17.75 kilograms or about 39 pounds."]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The bronze of the offering was seventy talents and two thousand four hundred shekels."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds","70 talents + 2400 shekels is about 2124 kilograms, or 2.124 metric tons."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"With this he made the sockets to the door of the Tent of Meeting, the bronze altar, the bronze grating for it, all the vessels of the altar,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"the sockets around the court, the sockets of the gate of the court, all the pins of the tabernacle, and all the pins around the court."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the blue, purple, and scarlet, they made finely worked garments for ministering in the holy place, and made the holy garments for Aaron, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the ephod of gold, blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They beat the gold into thin plates, and cut it into wires, to work it in with the blue, the purple, the scarlet, and the fine linen, the work of the skillful workman."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They made shoulder straps for it, joined together. It was joined together at the two ends."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The skillfully woven band that was on it, with which to fasten it on, was of the same piece, like its work: of gold, of blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"They worked the onyx stones, enclosed in settings of gold, engraved with the engravings of a signet, according to the names of the children of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He put them on the shoulder straps of the ephod, to be stones of memorial for the children of Israel, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the breastplate, the work of a skillful workman, like the work of the ephod: of gold, of blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It was square. They made the breastplate double. Its length was a span, and its width a span, being double."]],f:["A span is the length from the tip of a man\u2019s thumb to the tip of his little finger when his hand is stretched out (about half a cubit, or 9 inches, or 22.8 cm.)"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They set in it four rows of stones. A row of ruby, topaz, and beryl was the first row;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and the second row, a turquoise, a sapphire, and an emerald;"]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and the third row, a jacinth, an agate, and an amethyst;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and the fourth row, a chrysolite, an onyx, and a jasper. They were enclosed in gold settings."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The stones were according to the names of the children of Israel, twelve, according to their names; like the engravings of a signet, everyone according to his name, for the twelve tribes."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They made on the breastplate chains like cords, of braided work of pure gold."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They made two settings of gold, and two gold rings, and put the two rings on the two ends of the breastplate."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They put the two braided chains of gold in the two rings at the ends of the breastplate."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The other two ends of the two braided chains they put on the two settings, and put them on the shoulder straps of the ephod, in its front."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They made two rings of gold, and put them on the two ends of the breastplate, on its edge, which was toward the side of the ephod inward."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They made two more rings of gold, and put them on the two shoulder straps of the ephod underneath, in its front, close by its coupling, above the skillfully woven band of the ephod."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They bound the breastplate by its rings to the rings of the ephod with a lace of blue, that it might be on the skillfully woven band of the ephod, and that the breastplate might not come loose from the ephod, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the robe of the ephod of woven work, all of blue."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The opening of the robe in the middle of it was like the opening of a coat of mail, with a binding around its opening, that it should not be torn."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They made on the skirts of the robe pomegranates of blue, purple, scarlet, and twined linen."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They made bells of pure gold, and put the bells between the pomegranates around the skirts of the robe, between the pomegranates;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"a bell and a pomegranate, a bell and a pomegranate, around the skirts of the robe, to minister in, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"They made the tunics of fine linen of woven work for Aaron and for his sons,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"the turban of fine linen, the linen headbands of fine linen, the linen trousers of fine twined linen,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"the sash of fine twined linen, blue, purple, and scarlet, the work of the embroiderer, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"They made the plate of the holy crown of pure gold, and wrote on it an inscription, like the engravings of a signet: \u201cHOLY TO THE LORD\u201d."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They tied to it a lace of blue, to fasten it on the turban above, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus all the work of the tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting was finished. The children of Israel did according to all that the LORD commanded Moses; so they did."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They brought the tabernacle to Moses: the tent, with all its furniture, its clasps, its boards, its bars, its pillars, its sockets,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"the covering of rams\u2019 skins dyed red, the covering of sea cow hides, the veil of the screen,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"the ark of the covenant with its poles, the mercy seat,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"the table, all its vessels, the show bread,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"the pure lamp stand, its lamps, even the lamps to be set in order, all its vessels, the oil for the light,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"the golden altar, the anointing oil, the sweet incense, the screen for the door of the Tent,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"the bronze altar, its grating of bronze, its poles, all of its vessels, the basin and its base,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"the hangings of the court, its pillars, its sockets, the screen for the gate of the court, its cords, its pins, and all the instruments of the service of the tabernacle, for the Tent of Meeting,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"the finely worked garments for ministering in the holy place, the holy garments for Aaron the priest, and the garments of his sons, to minister in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"According to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so the children of Israel did all the work."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Moses saw all the work, and behold, they had done it as the LORD had commanded. They had done so; and Moses blessed them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the first day of the first month you shall raise up the tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall put the ark of the covenant in it, and you shall screen the ark with the veil."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall bring in the table, and set in order the things that are on it. You shall bring in the lamp stand, and light its lamps."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall set the golden altar for incense before the ark of the covenant, and put the screen of the door to the tabernacle."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall set the altar of burnt offering before the door of the tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall set the basin between the Tent of Meeting and the altar, and shall put water therein."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall set up the court around it, and hang up the screen of the gate of the court."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall take the anointing oil, and anoint the tabernacle and all that is in it, and shall make it holy, and all its furniture, and it will be holy."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall anoint the altar of burnt offering, with all its vessels, and sanctify the altar, and the altar will be most holy."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall anoint the basin and its base, and sanctify it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall bring Aaron and his sons to the door of the Tent of Meeting, and shall wash them with water."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall put on Aaron the holy garments; and you shall anoint him, and sanctify him, that he may minister to me in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall bring his sons, and put tunics on them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall anoint them, as you anointed their father, that they may minister to me in the priest\u2019s office. Their anointing shall be to them for an everlasting priesthood throughout their generations.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Moses did so. According to all that the LORD commanded him, so he did."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"In the first month in the second year, on the first day of the month, the tabernacle was raised up."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Moses raised up the tabernacle, and laid its sockets, and set up its boards, and put in its bars, and raised up its pillars."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He spread the covering over the tent, and put the roof of the tabernacle above on it, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He took and put the covenant into the ark, and set the poles on the ark, and put the mercy seat above on the ark."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He brought the ark into the tabernacle, and set up the veil of the screen, and screened the ark of the covenant, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He put the table in the Tent of Meeting, on the north side of the tabernacle, outside of the veil."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He set the bread in order on it before the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He put the lamp stand in the Tent of Meeting, opposite the table, on the south side of the tabernacle."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He lit the lamps before the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He put the golden altar in the Tent of Meeting before the veil;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and he burned incense of sweet spices on it, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He put up the screen of the door to the tabernacle."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He set the altar of burnt offering at the door of the tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting, and offered on it the burnt offering and the meal offering, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He set the basin between the Tent of Meeting and the altar, and put water therein, with which to wash."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Moses, Aaron, and his sons washed their hands and their feet there."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"When they went into the Tent of Meeting, and when they came near to the altar, they washed, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He raised up the court around the tabernacle and the altar, and set up the screen of the gate of the court. So Moses finished the work."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the cloud covered the Tent of Meeting, and the LORD\u2019s glory filled the tabernacle."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Moses wasn\u2019t able to enter into the Tent of Meeting, because the cloud stayed on it, and the LORD\u2019s glory filled the tabernacle."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"When the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle, the children of Israel went onward, throughout all their journeys;"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"but if the cloud wasn\u2019t taken up, then they didn\u2019t travel until the day that it was taken up."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"For the cloud of the LORD was on the tabernacle by day, and there was fire in the cloud by night, in the sight of all the house of Israel, throughout all their journeys."]]}]]}},1273,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,s){h.exports={book:"Lev",name:"Leviticus",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD called to Moses, and spoke to him from the Tent of Meeting, saying,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When anyone of you offers an offering to the LORD, you shall offer your offering of the livestock, from the herd and from the flock."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If his offering is a burnt offering from the herd, he shall offer a male without defect. He shall offer it at the door of the Tent of Meeting, that he may be accepted before the LORD."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He shall lay his hand on the head of the burnt offering, and it shall be accepted for him to make atonement for him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He shall kill the bull before the LORD. Aaron\u2019s sons, the priests, shall present the blood and sprinkle the blood around on the altar that is at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He shall skin the burnt offering and cut it into pieces."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The sons of Aaron the priest shall put fire on the altar, and lay wood in order on the fire;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and Aaron\u2019s sons, the priests, shall lay the pieces, the head, and the fat in order on the wood that is on the fire which is on the altar;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but he shall wash its innards and its legs with water. The priest shall burn all of it on the altar, for a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If his offering is from the flock, from the sheep or from the goats, for a burnt offering, he shall offer a male without defect."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He shall kill it on the north side of the altar before the LORD. Aaron\u2019s sons, the priests, shall sprinkle its blood around on the altar."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He shall cut it into its pieces, with its head and its fat. The priest shall lay them in order on the wood that is on the fire which is on the altar,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but the innards and the legs he shall wash with water. The priest shall offer the whole, and burn it on the altar. It is a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If his offering to the LORD is a burnt offering of birds, then he shall offer his offering from turtledoves or of young pigeons."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The priest shall bring it to the altar, and wring off its head, and burn it on the altar; and its blood shall be drained out on the side of the altar;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and he shall take away its crop and its feathers, and cast it beside the altar on the east part, in the place of the ashes."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He shall tear it by its wings, but shall not divide it apart. The priest shall burn it on the altar, on the wood that is on the fire. It is a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When anyone offers an offering of a meal offering to the LORD, his offering shall be of fine flour. He shall pour oil on it, and put frankincense on it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He shall bring it to Aaron\u2019s sons, the priests. He shall take his handful of its fine flour, and of its oil, with all its frankincense, and the priest shall burn its memorial on the altar, an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"That which is left of the meal offering shall be Aaron\u2019s and his sons\u2019. It is a most holy part of the offerings of the LORD made by fire."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When you offer an offering of a meal offering baked in the oven, it shall be unleavened cakes of fine flour mixed with oil, or unleavened wafers anointed with oil."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"If your offering is a meal offering made on a griddle, it shall be of unleavened fine flour, mixed with oil."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall cut it in pieces, and pour oil on it. It is a meal offering."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If your offering is a meal offering of the pan, it shall be made of fine flour with oil."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall bring the meal offering that is made of these things to the LORD. It shall be presented to the priest, and he shall bring it to the altar."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The priest shall take from the meal offering its memorial, and shall burn it on the altar, an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"That which is left of the meal offering shall be Aaron\u2019s and his sons\u2019. It is a most holy part of the offerings of the LORD made by fire."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018No meal offering which you shall offer to the LORD shall be made with yeast; for you shall burn no yeast, nor any honey, as an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"As an offering of first fruits you shall offer them to the LORD, but they shall not rise up as a pleasant aroma on the altar."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Every offering of your meal offering you shall season with salt. You shall not allow the salt of the covenant of your God to be lacking from your meal offering. With all your offerings you shall offer salt."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If you offer a meal offering of first fruits to the LORD, you shall offer for the meal offering of your first fruits fresh heads of grain parched with fire and crushed."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall put oil on it and lay frankincense on it. It is a meal offering."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The priest shall burn as its memorial part of its crushed grain and part of its oil, along with all its frankincense. It is an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If his offering is a sacrifice of peace offerings, if he offers it from the herd, whether male or female, he shall offer it without defect before the LORD."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He shall lay his hand on the head of his offering, and kill it at the door of the Tent of Meeting. Aaron\u2019s sons, the priests, shall sprinkle the blood around on the altar."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He shall offer of the sacrifice of peace offerings an offering made by fire to the LORD. The fat that covers the innards, and all the fat that is on the innards,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the loins, and the cover on the liver, with the kidneys, he shall take away."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Aaron\u2019s sons shall burn it on the altar on the burnt offering, which is on the wood that is on the fire: it is an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If his offering for a sacrifice of peace offerings to the LORD is from the flock, either male or female, he shall offer it without defect."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If he offers a lamb for his offering, then he shall offer it before the LORD;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and he shall lay his hand on the head of his offering, and kill it before the Tent of Meeting. Aaron\u2019s sons shall sprinkle its blood around on the altar."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He shall offer from the sacrifice of peace offerings an offering made by fire to the LORD; its fat, the entire tail fat, he shall take away close to the backbone; and the fat that covers the entrails, and all the fat that is on the entrails,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the loins, and the cover on the liver, with the kidneys, he shall take away."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The priest shall burn it on the altar: it is the food of the offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If his offering is a goat, then he shall offer it before the LORD."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He shall lay his hand on its head, and kill it before the Tent of Meeting; and the sons of Aaron shall sprinkle its blood around on the altar."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He shall offer from it as his offering, an offering made by fire to the LORD; the fat that covers the innards, and all the fat that is on the innards,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the loins, and the cover on the liver, with the kidneys, he shall take away."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The priest shall burn them on the altar: it is the food of the offering made by fire, for a pleasant aroma; all the fat is the LORD\u2019s."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018It shall be a perpetual statute throughout your generations in all your dwellings, that you shall eat neither fat nor blood.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018If anyone sins unintentionally, in any of the things which the LORD has commanded not to be done, and does any one of them,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"if the anointed priest sins so as to bring guilt on the people, then let him offer for his sin which he has sinned a young bull without defect to the LORD for a sin offering."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He shall bring the bull to the door of the Tent of Meeting before the LORD; and he shall lay his hand on the head of the bull, and kill the bull before the LORD."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The anointed priest shall take some of the blood of the bull, and bring it to the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The priest shall dip his finger in the blood, and sprinkle some of the blood seven times before the LORD, before the veil of the sanctuary."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The priest shall put some of the blood on the horns of the altar of sweet incense before the LORD, which is in the Tent of Meeting; and he shall pour out the rest of the blood of the bull at the base of the altar of burnt offering, which is at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He shall take all the fat of the bull of the sin offering from it: the fat that covers the innards, and all the fat that is on the innards,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the loins, and the cover on the liver, with the kidneys, he shall remove,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"as it is removed from the bull of the sacrifice of peace offerings. The priest shall burn them on the altar of burnt offering."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He shall carry the bull\u2019s skin, all its meat, with its head, and with its legs, its innards, and its dung"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u2014all the rest of the bull\u2014outside of the camp to a clean place where the ashes are poured out, and burn it on wood with fire. It shall be burned where the ashes are poured out."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If the whole congregation of Israel sins, and the thing is hidden from the eyes of the assembly, and they have done any of the things which the LORD has commanded not to be done, and are guilty;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"when the sin in which they have sinned is known, then the assembly shall offer a young bull for a sin offering, and bring it before the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The elders of the congregation shall lay their hands on the head of the bull before the LORD; and the bull shall be killed before the LORD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The anointed priest shall bring some of the blood of the bull to the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The priest shall dip his finger in the blood and sprinkle it seven times before the LORD, before the veil."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He shall put some of the blood on the horns of the altar which is before the LORD, that is in the Tent of Meeting; and the rest of the blood he shall pour out at the base of the altar of burnt offering, which is at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"All its fat he shall take from it, and burn it on the altar."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He shall do this with the bull; as he did with the bull of the sin offering, so he shall do with this; and the priest shall make atonement for them, and they shall be forgiven."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He shall carry the bull outside the camp, and burn it as he burned the first bull. It is the sin offering for the assembly."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When a ruler sins, and unwittingly does any one of all the things which the LORD his God has commanded not to be done, and is guilty,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"if his sin in which he has sinned is made known to him, he shall bring as his offering a goat, a male without defect."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He shall lay his hand on the head of the goat, and kill it in the place where they kill the burnt offering before the LORD. It is a sin offering."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The priest shall take some of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put it on the horns of the altar of burnt offering. He shall pour out the rest of its blood at the base of the altar of burnt offering."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"All its fat he shall burn on the altar, like the fat of the sacrifice of peace offerings; and the priest shall make atonement for him concerning his sin, and he will be forgiven."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If anyone of the common people sins unwittingly, in doing any of the things which the LORD has commanded not to be done, and is guilty,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"if his sin which he has sinned is made known to him, then he shall bring for his offering a goat, a female without defect, for his sin which he has sinned."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He shall lay his hand on the head of the sin offering, and kill the sin offering in the place of burnt offering."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The priest shall take some of its blood with his finger, and put it on the horns of the altar of burnt offering; and the rest of its blood he shall pour out at the base of the altar."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"All its fat he shall take away, like the fat is taken away from the sacrifice of peace offerings; and the priest shall burn it on the altar for a pleasant aroma to the LORD; and the priest shall make atonement for him, and he will be forgiven."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If he brings a lamb as his offering for a sin offering, he shall bring a female without defect."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He shall lay his hand on the head of the sin offering, and kill it for a sin offering in the place where they kill the burnt offering."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The priest shall take some of the blood of the sin offering with his finger, and put it on the horns of the altar of burnt offering; and all the rest of its blood he shall pour out at the base of the altar."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"He shall remove all its fat, like the fat of the lamb is removed from the sacrifice of peace offerings. The priest shall burn them on the altar, on the offerings of the LORD made by fire. The priest shall make atonement for him concerning his sin that he has sinned, and he will be forgiven."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If anyone sins, in that he hears a public adjuration to testify, he being a witness, whether he has seen or known, if he doesn\u2019t report it, then he shall bear his iniquity."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Or if anyone touches any unclean thing, whether it is the carcass of an unclean animal, or the carcass of unclean livestock, or the carcass of unclean creeping things, and it is hidden from him, and he is unclean, then he shall be guilty."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Or if he touches the uncleanness of man, whatever his uncleanness is with which he is unclean, and it is hidden from him; when he knows of it, then he shall be guilty."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Or if anyone swears rashly with his lips to do evil or to do good\u2014whatever it is that a man might utter rashly with an oath, and it is hidden from him\u2014when he knows of it, then he will be guilty of one of these."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It shall be, when he is guilty of one of these, he shall confess that in which he has sinned;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and he shall bring his trespass offering to the LORD for his sin which he has sinned: a female from the flock, a lamb or a goat, for a sin offering; and the priest shall make atonement for him concerning his sin."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If he can\u2019t afford a lamb, then he shall bring his trespass offering for that in which he has sinned, two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, to the LORD; one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He shall bring them to the priest, who shall first offer the one which is for the sin offering. He shall wring off its head from its neck, but shall not sever it completely."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He shall sprinkle some of the blood of the sin offering on the side of the altar; and the rest of the blood shall be drained out at the base of the altar. It is a sin offering."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He shall offer the second for a burnt offering, according to the ordinance; and the priest shall make atonement for him concerning his sin which he has sinned, and he shall be forgiven."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if he can\u2019t afford two turtledoves or two young pigeons, then he shall bring as his offering for that in which he has sinned, one tenth of an ephah of fine flour for a sin offering. He shall put no oil on it, and he shall not put any frankincense on it, for it is a sin offering."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He shall bring it to the priest, and the priest shall take his handful of it as the memorial portion, and burn it on the altar, on the offerings of the LORD made by fire. It is a sin offering."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The priest shall make atonement for him concerning his sin that he has sinned in any of these things, and he will be forgiven; and the rest shall be the priest\u2019s, as the meal offering.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cIf anyone commits a trespass, and sins unwittingly regarding the LORD\u2019s holy things, then he shall bring his trespass offering to the LORD: a ram without defect from the flock, according to your estimation in silver by shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, for a trespass offering."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He shall make restitution for that which he has done wrong regarding the holy thing, and shall add a fifth part to it, and give it to the priest; and the priest shall make atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering, and he will be forgiven."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf anyone sins, doing any of the things which the LORD has commanded not to be done, though he didn\u2019t know it, he is still guilty, and shall bear his iniquity."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He shall bring a ram without defect from of the flock, according to your estimation, for a trespass offering, to the priest; and the priest shall make atonement for him concerning the thing in which he sinned and didn\u2019t know it, and he will be forgiven."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"It is a trespass offering. He is certainly guilty before the LORD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cIf anyone sins, and commits a trespass against the LORD, and deals falsely with his neighbor in a matter of deposit, or of bargain, or of robbery, or has oppressed his neighbor,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"or has found that which was lost, and lied about it, and swearing to a lie\u2014in any of these things that a man sins in his actions\u2014"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"then it shall be, if he has sinned, and is guilty, he shall restore that which he took by robbery, or the thing which he has gotten by oppression, or the deposit which was committed to him, or the lost thing which he found,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"or any thing about which he has sworn falsely: he shall restore it in full, and shall add a fifth part more to it. He shall return it to him to whom it belongs in the day of his being found guilty."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He shall bring his trespass offering to the LORD: a ram without defect from the flock, according to your estimation, for a trespass offering, to the priest."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The priest shall make atonement for him before the LORD, and he will be forgiven concerning whatever he does to become guilty.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cCommand Aaron and his sons, saying, \u2018This is the law of the burnt offering: the burnt offering shall be on the hearth on the altar all night until the morning; and the fire of the altar shall be kept burning on it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The priest shall put on his linen garment, and he shall put on his linen trousers upon his body; and he shall remove the ashes from where the fire has consumed the burnt offering on the altar, and he shall put them beside the altar."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He shall take off his garments, and put on other garments, and carry the ashes outside the camp to a clean place."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The fire on the altar shall be kept burning on it, it shall not go out; and the priest shall burn wood on it every morning. He shall lay the burnt offering in order upon it, and shall burn on it the fat of the peace offerings."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Fire shall be kept burning on the altar continually; it shall not go out."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law of the meal offering: the sons of Aaron shall offer it before the LORD, before the altar."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He shall take from there his handful of the fine flour of the meal offering, and of its oil, and all the frankincense which is on the meal offering, and shall burn it on the altar for a pleasant aroma, as its memorial portion, to the LORD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"That which is left of it Aaron and his sons shall eat. It shall be eaten without yeast in a holy place. They shall eat it in the court of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It shall not be baked with yeast. I have given it as their portion of my offerings made by fire. It is most holy, as are the sin offering and the trespass offering."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Every male among the children of Aaron shall eat of it, as their portion forever throughout your generations, from the offerings of the LORD made by fire. Whoever touches them shall be holy.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the offering of Aaron and of his sons, which they shall offer to the LORD in the day when he is anointed: one tenth of an ephah of fine flour for a meal offering perpetually, half of it in the morning, and half of it in the evening."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"It shall be made with oil in a griddle. When it is soaked, you shall bring it in. You shall offer the meal offering in baked pieces for a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The anointed priest that will be in his place from among his sons shall offer it. By a statute forever, it shall be wholly burned to the LORD."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Every meal offering of a priest shall be wholly burned. It shall not be eaten.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Aaron and to his sons, saying, \u2018This is the law of the sin offering: in the place where the burnt offering is killed, the sin offering shall be killed before the LORD. It is most holy."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The priest who offers it for sin shall eat it. It shall be eaten in a holy place, in the court of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Whatever shall touch its flesh shall be holy. When there is any of its blood sprinkled on a garment, you shall wash that on which it was sprinkled in a holy place."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But the earthen vessel in which it is boiled shall be broken; and if it is boiled in a bronze vessel, it shall be scoured, and rinsed in water."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Every male among the priests shall eat of it. It is most holy."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"No sin offering, of which any of the blood is brought into the Tent of Meeting to make atonement in the Holy Place, shall be eaten. It shall be burned with fire."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law of the trespass offering: It is most holy."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In the place where they kill the burnt offering, he shall kill the trespass offering; and its blood he shall sprinkle around on the altar."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He shall offer all of its fat: the fat tail, and the fat that covers the innards,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and he shall take away the two kidneys, and the fat that is on them, which is by the loins, and the cover on the liver, with the kidneys;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and the priest shall burn them on the altar for an offering made by fire to the LORD: it is a trespass offering."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Every male among the priests may eat of it. It shall be eaten in a holy place. It is most holy."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018As is the sin offering, so is the trespass offering; there is one law for them. The priest who makes atonement with them shall have it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The priest who offers any man\u2019s burnt offering shall have for himself the skin of the burnt offering which he has offered."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Every meal offering that is baked in the oven, and all that is prepared in the pan and on the griddle, shall be the priest\u2019s who offers it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Every meal offering, mixed with oil or dry, belongs to all the sons of Aaron, one as well as another."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law of the sacrifice of peace offerings, which one shall offer to the LORD:"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If he offers it for a thanksgiving, then he shall offer with the sacrifice of thanksgiving unleavened cakes mixed with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil, and cakes mixed with oil."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He shall offer his offering with the sacrifice of his peace offerings for thanksgiving with cakes of leavened bread."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Of it he shall offer one out of each offering for a heave offering to the LORD. It shall be the priest\u2019s who sprinkles the blood of the peace offerings."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The flesh of the sacrifice of his peace offerings for thanksgiving shall be eaten on the day of his offering. He shall not leave any of it until the morning."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if the sacrifice of his offering is a vow, or a free will offering, it shall be eaten on the day that he offers his sacrifice. On the next day what remains of it shall be eaten,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"but what remains of the meat of the sacrifice on the third day shall be burned with fire."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"If any of the meat of the sacrifice of his peace offerings is eaten on the third day, it will not be accepted, and it shall not be credited to him who offers it. It will be an abomination, and the soul who eats any of it will bear his iniquity."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The meat that touches any unclean thing shall not be eaten. It shall be burned with fire. As for the meat, everyone who is clean may eat it;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but the soul who eats of the meat of the sacrifice of peace offerings that belongs to the LORD, having his uncleanness on him, that soul shall be cut off from his people."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When anyone touches any unclean thing, the uncleanness of man, or an unclean animal, or any unclean abomination, and eats some of the meat of the sacrifice of peace offerings which belong to the LORD, that soul shall be cut off from his people.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018You shall eat no fat, of bull, or sheep, or goat."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The fat of that which dies of itself, and the fat of that which is torn of animals, may be used for any other service, but you shall in no way eat of it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For whoever eats the fat of the animal which men offer as an offering made by fire to the LORD, even the soul who eats it shall be cut off from his people."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall not eat any blood, whether it is of bird or of animal, in any of your dwellings."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Whoever it is who eats any blood, that soul shall be cut off from his people.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018He who offers the sacrifice of his peace offerings to the LORD shall bring his offering to the LORD out of the sacrifice of his peace offerings."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"With his own hands he shall bring the offerings of the LORD made by fire. He shall bring the fat with the breast, that the breast may be waved for a wave offering before the LORD."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The priest shall burn the fat on the altar, but the breast shall be Aaron\u2019s and his sons\u2019."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The right thigh you shall give to the priest for a heave offering out of the sacrifices of your peace offerings."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He among the sons of Aaron who offers the blood of the peace offerings, and the fat, shall have the right thigh for a portion."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For the waved breast and the heaved thigh I have taken from the children of Israel out of the sacrifices of their peace offerings, and have given them to Aaron the priest and to his sons as their portion forever from the children of Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the consecrated portion of Aaron, and the consecrated portion of his sons, out of the offerings of the LORD made by fire, in the day when he presented them to minister to the LORD in the priest\u2019s office;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"which the LORD commanded to be given them of the children of Israel, in the day that he anointed them. It is their portion forever throughout their generations."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"This is the law of the burnt offering, the meal offering, the sin offering, the trespass offering, the consecration, and the sacrifice of peace offerings"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"which the LORD commanded Moses in Mount Sinai in the day that he commanded the children of Israel to offer their offerings to the LORD, in the wilderness of Sinai."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cTake Aaron and his sons with him, and the garments, and the anointing oil, and the bull of the sin offering, and the two rams, and the basket of unleavened bread;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and assemble all the congregation at the door of the Tent of Meeting.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses did as the LORD commanded him; and the congregation was assembled at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Moses said to the congregation, \u201cThis is the thing which the LORD has commanded to be done.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Moses brought Aaron and his sons, and washed them with water."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He put the tunic on him, tied the sash on him, clothed him with the robe, put the ephod on him, and he tied the skillfully woven band of the ephod on him and fastened it to him with it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He placed the breastplate on him. He put the Urim and Thummim in the breastplate."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He set the turban on his head. He set the golden plate, the holy crown, on the front of the turban, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Moses took the anointing oil, and anointed the tabernacle and all that was in it, and sanctified them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He sprinkled it on the altar seven times, and anointed the altar and all its vessels, and the basin and its base, to sanctify them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He poured some of the anointing oil on Aaron\u2019s head, and anointed him, to sanctify him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Moses brought Aaron\u2019s sons, and clothed them with tunics, and tied sashes on them, and put headbands on them, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He brought the bull of the sin offering, and Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the bull of the sin offering."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He killed it; and Moses took the blood, and put it around on the horns of the altar with his finger, and purified the altar, and poured out the blood at the base of the altar, and sanctified it, to make atonement for it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He took all the fat that was on the innards, and the cover of the liver, and the two kidneys, and their fat; and Moses burned it on the altar."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But the bull, and its skin, and its meat, and its dung, he burned with fire outside the camp, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He presented the ram of the burnt offering. Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the ram."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He killed it; and Moses sprinkled the blood around on the altar."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He cut the ram into its pieces; and Moses burned the head, and the pieces, and the fat."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He washed the innards and the legs with water; and Moses burned the whole ram on the altar. It was a burnt offering for a pleasant aroma. It was an offering made by fire to the LORD, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He presented the other ram, the ram of consecration. Aaron and his sons laid their hands on the head of the ram."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He killed it; and Moses took some of its blood, and put it on the tip of Aaron\u2019s right ear, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the great toe of his right foot."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He brought Aaron\u2019s sons; and Moses put some of the blood on the tip of their right ear, and on the thumb of their right hand, and on the great toe of their right foot; and Moses sprinkled the blood around on the altar."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He took the fat, the fat tail, all the fat that was on the innards, the cover of the liver, the two kidneys and their fat, and the right thigh;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and out of the basket of unleavened bread that was before the LORD, he took one unleavened cake, one cake of oiled bread, and one wafer, and placed them on the fat and on the right thigh."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He put all these in Aaron\u2019s hands and in his sons\u2019 hands, and waved them for a wave offering before the LORD."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Moses took them from their hands, and burned them on the altar on the burnt offering. They were a consecration offering for a pleasant aroma. It was an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Moses took the breast, and waved it for a wave offering before the LORD. It was Moses\u2019 portion of the ram of consecration, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Moses took some of the anointing oil, and some of the blood which was on the altar, and sprinkled it on Aaron, on his garments, and on his sons, and on his sons\u2019 garments with him, and sanctified Aaron, his garments, and his sons, and his sons\u2019 garments with him."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Aaron and to his sons, \u201cBoil the meat at the door of the Tent of Meeting, and there eat it and the bread that is in the basket of consecration, as I commanded, saying, \u2018Aaron and his sons shall eat it.\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"What remains of the meat and of the bread you shall burn with fire."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"You shall not go out from the door of the Tent of Meeting for seven days, until the days of your consecration are fulfilled: for he shall consecrate you seven days."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"What has been done today, so the LORD has commanded to do, to make atonement for you."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"You shall stay at the door of the Tent of Meeting day and night seven days, and keep the LORD\u2019s command, that you don\u2019t die: for so I am commanded.\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Aaron and his sons did all the things which the LORD commanded by Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"On the eighth day, Moses called Aaron and his sons, and the elders of Israel;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and he said to Aaron, \u201cTake a calf from the herd for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering, without defect, and offer them before the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall speak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018Take a male goat for a sin offering; and a calf and a lamb, both a year old, without defect, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and a bull and a ram for peace offerings, to sacrifice before the LORD; and a meal offering mixed with oil: for today the LORD appears to you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"They brought what Moses commanded before the Tent of Meeting. All the congregation came near and stood before the LORD."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cThis is the thing which the LORD commanded that you should do; and the LORD\u2019s glory shall appear to you.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Moses said to Aaron, \u201cDraw near to the altar, and offer your sin offering, and your burnt offering, and make atonement for yourself, and for the people; and offer the offering of the people, and make atonement for them, as the LORD commanded.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So Aaron came near to the altar, and killed the calf of the sin offering, which was for himself."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The sons of Aaron presented the blood to him; and he dipped his finger in the blood, and put it on the horns of the altar, and poured out the blood at the base of the altar;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but the fat, and the kidneys, and the cover from the liver of the sin offering, he burned upon the altar, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The meat and the skin he burned with fire outside the camp."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He killed the burnt offering; and Aaron\u2019s sons delivered the blood to him, and he sprinkled it around on the altar."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They delivered the burnt offering to him, piece by piece, and the head. He burned them upon the altar."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He washed the innards and the legs, and burned them on the burnt offering on the altar."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He presented the people\u2019s offering, and took the goat of the sin offering which was for the people, and killed it, and offered it for sin, like the first."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He presented the burnt offering, and offered it according to the ordinance."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He presented the meal offering, and filled his hand from there, and burned it upon the altar, in addition to the burnt offering of the morning."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He also killed the bull and the ram, the sacrifice of peace offerings, which was for the people. Aaron\u2019s sons delivered to him the blood, which he sprinkled around on the altar;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and the fat of the bull and of the ram, the fat tail, and that which covers the innards, and the kidneys, and the cover of the liver;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and they put the fat upon the breasts, and he burned the fat on the altar."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Aaron waved the breasts and the right thigh for a wave offering before the LORD, as Moses commanded."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Aaron lifted up his hands toward the people, and blessed them; and he came down from offering the sin offering, and the burnt offering, and the peace offerings."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron went into the Tent of Meeting, and came out, and blessed the people; and the LORD\u2019s glory appeared to all the people."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Fire came out from before the LORD, and consumed the burnt offering and the fat upon the altar. When all the people saw it, they shouted, and fell on their faces."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Nadab and Abihu, the sons of Aaron, each took his censer, and put fire in it, and laid incense on it, and offered strange fire before the LORD, which he had not commanded them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Fire came out from before the LORD, and devoured them, and they died before the LORD."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Moses said to Aaron, \u201cThis is what the LORD spoke of, saying,"],[1,"\u2018I will show myself holy to those who come near me,"],[2,"and before all the people I will be glorified.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"Aaron held his peace."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Moses called Mishael and Elzaphan, the sons of Uzziel the uncle of Aaron, and said to them, \u201cDraw near, carry your brothers from before the sanctuary out of the camp.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So they came near, and carried them in their tunics out of the camp, as Moses had said."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Aaron, and to Eleazar and to Ithamar, his sons, \u201cDon\u2019t let the hair of your heads go loose, and don\u2019t tear your clothes, so that you don\u2019t die, and so that he will not be angry with all the congregation; but let your brothers, the whole house of Israel, bewail the burning which the LORD has kindled."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall not go out from the door of the Tent of Meeting, lest you die; for the anointing oil of the LORD is on you.\u201d They did according to the word of Moses."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to Aaron,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cYou and your sons are not to drink wine or strong drink whenever you go into the Tent of Meeting, or you will die. This shall be a statute forever throughout your generations."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You are to make a distinction between the holy and the common, and between the unclean and the clean."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You are to teach the children of Israel all the statutes which the LORD has spoken to them by Moses.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke to Aaron, and to Eleazar and to Ithamar, his sons who were left, \u201cTake the meal offering that remains of the offerings of the LORD made by fire, and eat it without yeast beside the altar; for it is most holy;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and you shall eat it in a holy place, because it is your portion, and your sons\u2019 portion, of the offerings of the LORD made by fire; for so I am commanded."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The waved breast and the heaved thigh you shall eat in a clean place, you, and your sons, and your daughters with you: for they are given as your portion, and your sons\u2019 portion, out of the sacrifices of the peace offerings of the children of Israel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They shall bring the heaved thigh and the waved breast with the offerings made by fire of the fat, to wave it for a wave offering before the LORD. It shall be yours, and your sons\u2019 with you, as a portion forever, as the LORD has commanded.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses diligently inquired about the goat of the sin offering, and, behold, it was burned. He was angry with Eleazar and with Ithamar, the sons of Aaron who were left, saying,"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u201cWhy haven\u2019t you eaten the sin offering in the place of the sanctuary, since it is most holy, and he has given it to you to bear the iniquity of the congregation, to make atonement for them before the LORD?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Behold, its blood was not brought into the inner part of the sanctuary. You certainly should have eaten it in the sanctuary, as I commanded.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Aaron spoke to Moses, \u201cBehold, today they have offered their sin offering and their burnt offering before the LORD; and such things as these have happened to me. If I had eaten the sin offering today, would it have been pleasing in the LORD\u2019s sight?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When Moses heard that, it was pleasing in his sight."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying to them,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018These are the living things which you may eat among all the animals that are on the earth."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Whatever parts the hoof, and is cloven-footed, and chews the cud among the animals, that you may eat."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Nevertheless these you shall not eat of those that chew the cud, or of those who part the hoof: the camel, because it chews the cud but doesn\u2019t have a parted hoof, is unclean to you."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The hyrax, because it chews the cud but doesn\u2019t have a parted hoof, is unclean to you."]],f:["or rock badger, or cony"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The hare, because it chews the cud but doesn\u2019t have a parted hoof, is unclean to you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The pig, because it has a split hoof, and is cloven-footed, but doesn\u2019t chew the cud, is unclean to you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall not eat their meat. You shall not touch their carcasses. They are unclean to you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You may eat of all these that are in the waters: whatever has fins and scales in the waters, in the seas, and in the rivers, that you may eat."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All that don\u2019t have fins and scales in the seas and rivers, all that move in the waters, and all the living creatures that are in the waters, they are an abomination to you,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and you shall detest them. You shall not eat of their meat, and you shall detest their carcasses."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Whatever has no fins nor scales in the waters is an abomination to you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall detest these among the birds; they shall not be eaten because they are an abomination: the eagle, the vulture, the black vulture,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the red kite, any kind of black kite,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"any kind of raven,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the horned owl, the screech owl, the gull, any kind of hawk,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the little owl, the cormorant, the great owl,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"the white owl, the desert owl, the osprey,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the stork, any kind of heron, the hoopoe, and the bat."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018All flying insects that walk on all fours are an abomination to you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Yet you may eat these: of all winged creeping things that go on all fours, which have long, jointed legs for hopping on the earth."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Even of these you may eat: any kind of locust, any kind of katydid, any kind of cricket, and any kind of grasshopper."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But all winged creeping things which have four feet are an abomination to you."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018By these you will become unclean: whoever touches their carcass shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Whoever carries any part of their carcass shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Every animal which has a split hoof that isn\u2019t completely divided, or doesn\u2019t chew the cud, is unclean to you. Everyone who touches them shall be unclean."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Whatever goes on its paws, among all animals that go on all fours, they are unclean to you. Whoever touches their carcass shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He who carries their carcass shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the evening. They are unclean to you."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018These are they which are unclean to you among the creeping things that creep on the earth: the weasel, the rat, any kind of great lizard,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"the gecko, and the monitor lizard, the wall lizard, the skink, and the chameleon."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"These are they which are unclean to you among all that creep. Whoever touches them when they are dead shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Anything they fall on when they are dead shall be unclean; whether it is any vessel of wood, or clothing, or skin, or sack, whatever vessel it is, with which any work is done, it must be put into water, and it shall be unclean until the evening. Then it will be clean."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Every earthen vessel into which any of them falls and all that is in it shall be unclean. You shall break it."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"All food which may be eaten which is soaked in water shall be unclean. All drink that may be drunk in every such vessel shall be unclean."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Everything whereupon part of their carcass falls shall be unclean; whether oven, or range for pots, it shall be broken in pieces. They are unclean, and shall be unclean to you."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Nevertheless a spring or a cistern in which water is gathered shall be clean, but that which touches their carcass shall be unclean."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"If part of their carcass falls on any sowing seed which is to be sown, it is clean."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But if water is put on the seed, and part of their carcass falls on it, it is unclean to you."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If any animal of which you may eat dies, he who touches its carcass shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"He who eats of its carcass shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the evening. He also who carries its carcass shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Every creeping thing that creeps on the earth is an abomination. It shall not be eaten."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Whatever goes on its belly, and whatever goes on all fours, or whatever has many feet, even all creeping things that creep on the earth, them you shall not eat; for they are an abomination."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"You shall not make yourselves abominable with any creeping thing that creeps. You shall not make yourselves unclean with them, that you should be defiled by them."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"For I am the LORD your God. Sanctify yourselves therefore, and be holy; for I am holy. You shall not defile yourselves with any kind of creeping thing that moves on the earth."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"For I am the LORD who brought you up out of the land of Egypt, to be your God. You shall therefore be holy, for I am holy."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law of the animal, and of the bird, and of every living creature that moves in the waters, and of every creature that creeps on the earth,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"to make a distinction between the unclean and the clean, and between the living thing that may be eaten and the living thing that may not be eaten.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018If a woman conceives, and bears a male child, then she shall be unclean seven days; as in the days of her monthly period she shall be unclean."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In the eighth day the flesh of his foreskin shall be circumcised."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"She shall continue in the blood of purification thirty-three days. She shall not touch any holy thing, nor come into the sanctuary, until the days of her purifying are completed."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But if she bears a female child, then she shall be unclean two weeks, as in her period; and she shall continue in the blood of purification sixty-six days."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When the days of her purification are completed for a son or for a daughter, she shall bring to the priest at the door of the Tent of Meeting, a year old lamb for a burnt offering, and a young pigeon or a turtledove, for a sin offering."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He shall offer it before the LORD, and make atonement for her; then she shall be cleansed from the fountain of her blood."],[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law for her who bears, whether a male or a female."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If she cannot afford a lamb, then she shall take two turtledoves or two young pigeons: the one for a burnt offering, and the other for a sin offering. The priest shall make atonement for her, and she shall be clean.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen a man shall have a swelling in his body\u2019s skin, or a scab, or a bright spot, and it becomes in the skin of his body the plague of leprosy, then he shall be brought to Aaron the priest or to one of his sons, the priests."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine the plague in the skin of the body. If the hair in the plague has turned white, and the appearance of the plague is deeper than the body\u2019s skin, it is the plague of leprosy; so the priest shall examine him and pronounce him unclean."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If the bright spot is white in the skin of his body, and its appearance isn\u2019t deeper than the skin, and its hair hasn\u2019t turned white, then the priest shall isolate the infected person for seven days."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine him on the seventh day. Behold, if in his eyes the plague is arrested and the plague hasn\u2019t spread in the skin, then the priest shall isolate him for seven more days."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine him again on the seventh day. Behold, if the plague has faded and the plague hasn\u2019t spread in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him clean. It is a scab. He shall wash his clothes, and be clean."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But if the scab spreads on the skin after he has shown himself to the priest for his cleansing, he shall show himself to the priest again."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine him; and behold, if the scab has spread on the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean. It is leprosy."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the plague of leprosy is in a man, then he shall be brought to the priest;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and the priest shall examine him. Behold, if there is a white swelling in the skin, and it has turned the hair white, and there is raw flesh in the swelling,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"it is a chronic leprosy in the skin of his body, and the priest shall pronounce him unclean. He shall not isolate him, for he is already unclean."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf the leprosy breaks out all over the skin, and the leprosy covers all the skin of the infected person from his head even to his feet, as far as it appears to the priest,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"then the priest shall examine him. Behold, if the leprosy has covered all his flesh, he shall pronounce him clean of the plague. It has all turned white: he is clean."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But whenever raw flesh appears in him, he shall be unclean."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine the raw flesh, and pronounce him unclean: the raw flesh is unclean. It is leprosy."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Or if the raw flesh turns again, and is changed to white, then he shall come to the priest."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine him. Behold, if the plague has turned white, then the priest shall pronounce him clean of the plague. He is clean."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the body has a boil on its skin, and it has healed,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and in the place of the boil there is a white swelling, or a bright spot, reddish-white, then it shall be shown to the priest."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine it. Behold, if its appearance is deeper than the skin, and its hair has turned white, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean. It is the plague of leprosy. It has broken out in the boil."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But if the priest examines it, and behold, there are no white hairs in it, and it isn\u2019t deeper than the skin, but is dim, then the priest shall isolate him seven days."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"If it spreads in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean. It is a plague."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But if the bright spot stays in its place, and hasn\u2019t spread, it is the scar from the boil; and the priest shall pronounce him clean."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOr when the body has a burn from fire on its skin, and the raw flesh of the burn becomes a bright spot, reddish-white, or white,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"then the priest shall examine it; and behold, if the hair in the bright spot has turned white, and its appearance is deeper than the skin, it is leprosy. It has broken out in the burning, and the priest shall pronounce him unclean. It is the plague of leprosy."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But if the priest examines it, and behold, there is no white hair in the bright spot, and it isn\u2019t deeper than the skin, but has faded, then the priest shall isolate him seven days."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine him on the seventh day. If it has spread in the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean. It is the plague of leprosy."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"If the bright spot stays in its place, and hasn\u2019t spread in the skin, but is faded, it is the swelling from the burn, and the priest shall pronounce him clean, for it is the scar from the burn."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen a man or woman has a plague on the head or on the beard,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"then the priest shall examine the plague; and behold, if its appearance is deeper than the skin, and the hair in it is yellow and thin, then the priest shall pronounce him unclean. It is an itch. It is leprosy of the head or of the beard."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"If the priest examines the plague of itching, and behold, its appearance isn\u2019t deeper than the skin, and there is no black hair in it, then the priest shall isolate the person infected with itching seven days."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"On the seventh day the priest shall examine the plague; and behold, if the itch hasn\u2019t spread, and there is no yellow hair in it, and the appearance of the itch isn\u2019t deeper than the skin,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"then he shall be shaved, but he shall not shave the itch. Then the priest shall isolate the one who has the itch seven more days."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"On the seventh day, the priest shall examine the itch; and behold, if the itch hasn\u2019t spread in the skin, and its appearance isn\u2019t deeper than the skin, then the priest shall pronounce him clean. He shall wash his clothes and be clean."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"But if the itch spreads in the skin after his cleansing,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"then the priest shall examine him; and behold, if the itch has spread in the skin, the priest shall not look for the yellow hair; he is unclean."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"But if in his eyes the itch is arrested and black hair has grown in it, then the itch is healed. He is clean. The priest shall pronounce him clean."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen a man or a woman has bright spots in the skin of the body, even white bright spots,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"then the priest shall examine them. Behold, if the bright spots on the skin of their body are a dull white, it is a harmless rash. It has broken out in the skin. He is clean."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man\u2019s hair has fallen from his head, he is bald. He is clean."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"If his hair has fallen off from the front part of his head, his forehead is bald. He is clean."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"But if a reddish-white plague is in the bald head or the bald forehead, it is leprosy breaking out in his bald head or his bald forehead."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Then the priest shall examine him. Behold, if the swelling of the plague is reddish-white in his bald head, or in his bald forehead, like the appearance of leprosy in the skin of the body,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"he is a leprous man. He is unclean. The priest shall surely pronounce him unclean. His plague is on his head."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe leper in whom the plague is shall wear torn clothes, and the hair of his head shall hang loose. He shall cover his upper lip, and shall cry, \u2018Unclean! Unclean!\u2019"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"All the days in which the plague is in him he shall be unclean. He is unclean. He shall dwell alone. His dwelling shall be outside of the camp."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe garment also that the plague of leprosy is in, whether it is a woolen garment, or a linen garment;"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"whether it is in warp or woof; of linen or of wool; whether in leather, or in anything made of leather;"]],f:["warp and woof are the vertical and horizontal threads in woven cloth"]},{v:49,l:[[0,"if the plague is greenish or reddish in the garment, or in the leather, or in the warp, or in the woof, or in anything made of leather; it is the plague of leprosy, and shall be shown to the priest."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"The priest shall examine the plague, and isolate the plague seven days."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"He shall examine the plague on the seventh day. If the plague has spread in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in the skin, whatever use the skin is used for, the plague is a destructive mildew. It is unclean."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"He shall burn the garment, whether the warp or the woof, in wool or in linen, or anything of leather, in which the plague is, for it is a destructive mildew. It shall be burned in the fire."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf the priest examines it, and behold, the plague hasn\u2019t spread in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in anything of skin;"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"then the priest shall command that they wash the thing that the plague is in, and he shall isolate it seven more days."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"Then the priest shall examine it, after the plague is washed; and behold, if the plague hasn\u2019t changed its color, and the plague hasn\u2019t spread, it is unclean; you shall burn it in the fire. It is a mildewed spot, whether the bareness is inside or outside."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"If the priest looks, and behold, the plague has faded after it is washed, then he shall tear it out of the garment, or out of the skin, or out of the warp, or out of the woof;"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"and if it appears again in the garment, either in the warp, or in the woof, or in anything of skin, it is spreading. You shall burn what the plague is in with fire."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"The garment, either the warp, or the woof, or whatever thing of skin it is, which you shall wash, if the plague has departed from them, then it shall be washed the second time, and it will be clean.\u201d"]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the law of the plague of mildew in a garment of wool or linen, either in the warp, or the woof, or in anything of skin, to pronounce it clean, or to pronounce it unclean."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis shall be the law of the leper in the day of his cleansing: He shall be brought to the priest,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and the priest shall go out of the camp. The priest shall examine him. Behold, if the plague of leprosy is healed in the leper,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"then the priest shall command them to take for him who is to be cleansed two living clean birds, cedar wood, scarlet, and hyssop."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The priest shall command them to kill one of the birds in an earthen vessel over running water."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"As for the living bird, he shall take it, the cedar wood, the scarlet, and the hyssop, and shall dip them and the living bird in the blood of the bird that was killed over the running water."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He shall sprinkle on him who is to be cleansed from the leprosy seven times, and shall pronounce him clean, and shall let the living bird go into the open field."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who is to be cleansed shall wash his clothes, and shave off all his hair, and bathe himself in water; and he shall be clean. After that he shall come into the camp, but shall dwell outside his tent seven days."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It shall be on the seventh day, that he shall shave all his hair off his head and his beard and his eyebrows. He shall shave off all his hair. He shall wash his clothes, and he shall bathe his body in water. Then he shall be clean."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the eighth day he shall take two male lambs without defect, one ewe lamb a year old without defect, three tenths of an ephah of fine flour for a meal offering, mixed with oil, and one log of oil."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","a log is a liquid measure of about 300 ml or 10 ounces"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The priest who cleanses him shall set the man who is to be cleansed, and those things, before the LORD, at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe priest shall take one of the male lambs, and offer him for a trespass offering, with the log of oil, and wave them for a wave offering before the LORD."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He shall kill the male lamb in the place where they kill the sin offering and the burnt offering, in the place of the sanctuary; for as the sin offering is the priest\u2019s, so is the trespass offering. It is most holy."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The priest shall take some of the blood of the trespass offering, and the priest shall put it on the tip of the right ear of him who is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the big toe of his right foot."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The priest shall take some of the log of oil, and pour it into the palm of his own left hand."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The priest shall dip his right finger in the oil that is in his left hand, and shall sprinkle some of the oil with his finger seven times before the LORD."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The priest shall put some of the rest of the oil that is in his hand on the tip of the right ear of him who is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the big toe of his right foot, upon the blood of the trespass offering."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The rest of the oil that is in the priest\u2019s hand he shall put on the head of him who is to be cleansed, and the priest shall make atonement for him before the LORD."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe priest shall offer the sin offering, and make atonement for him who is to be cleansed because of his uncleanness. Afterward he shall kill the burnt offering;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"then the priest shall offer the burnt offering and the meal offering on the altar. The priest shall make atonement for him, and he shall be clean."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf he is poor, and can\u2019t afford so much, then he shall take one male lamb for a trespass offering to be waved, to make atonement for him, and one tenth of an ephah of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering, and a log of oil;"]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","a log is a liquid measure of about 300 ml or 10 ounces"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, such as he is able to afford; and the one shall be a sin offering, and the other a burnt offering."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the eighth day he shall bring them for his cleansing to the priest, to the door of the Tent of Meeting, before the LORD."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The priest shall take the lamb of the trespass offering, and the log of oil, and the priest shall wave them for a wave offering before the LORD."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He shall kill the lamb of the trespass offering. The priest shall take some of the blood of the trespass offering and put it on the tip of the right ear of him who is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the big toe of his right foot."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The priest shall pour some of the oil into the palm of his own left hand;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and the priest shall sprinkle with his right finger some of the oil that is in his left hand seven times before the LORD."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Then the priest shall put some of the oil that is in his hand on the tip of the right ear of him who is to be cleansed, and on the thumb of his right hand, and on the big toe of his right foot, on the place of the blood of the trespass offering."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The rest of the oil that is in the priest\u2019s hand he shall put on the head of him who is to be cleansed, to make atonement for him before the LORD."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He shall offer one of the turtledoves, or of the young pigeons, which ever he is able to afford,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"of the kind he is able to afford, the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, with the meal offering. The priest shall make atonement for him who is to be cleansed before the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the law for him in whom is the plague of leprosy, who is not able to afford the sacrifice for his cleansing."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen you have come into the land of Canaan, which I give to you for a possession, and I put a spreading mildew in a house in the land of your possession,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"then he who owns the house shall come and tell the priest, saying, \u2018There seems to me to be some sort of plague in the house.\u2019"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The priest shall command that they empty the house, before the priest goes in to examine the plague, that all that is in the house not be made unclean. Afterward the priest shall go in to inspect the house."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He shall examine the plague; and behold, if the plague is in the walls of the house with hollow streaks, greenish or reddish, and it appears to be deeper than the wall,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"then the priest shall go out of the house to the door of the house, and shut up the house seven days."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The priest shall come again on the seventh day, and look. If the plague has spread in the walls of the house,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"then the priest shall command that they take out the stones in which is the plague, and cast them into an unclean place outside of the city."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He shall cause the inside of the house to be scraped all over. They shall pour out the mortar that they scraped off outside of the city into an unclean place."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"They shall take other stones, and put them in the place of those stones; and he shall take other mortar, and shall plaster the house."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf the plague comes again, and breaks out in the house after he has taken out the stones, and after he has scraped the house, and after it was plastered,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"then the priest shall come in and look; and behold, if the plague has spread in the house, it is a destructive mildew in the house. It is unclean."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"He shall break down the house, its stones, and its timber, and all the house\u2019s mortar. He shall carry them out of the city into an unclean place."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover he who goes into the house while it is shut up shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"He who lies down in the house shall wash his clothes; and he who eats in the house shall wash his clothes."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf the priest shall come in, and examine it, and behold, the plague hasn\u2019t spread in the house, after the house was plastered, then the priest shall pronounce the house clean, because the plague is healed."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"To cleanse the house he shall take two birds, cedar wood, scarlet, and hyssop."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"He shall kill one of the birds in an earthen vessel over running water."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"He shall take the cedar wood, the hyssop, the scarlet, and the living bird, and dip them in the blood of the slain bird, and in the running water, and sprinkle the house seven times."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"He shall cleanse the house with the blood of the bird, and with the running water, with the living bird, with the cedar wood, with the hyssop, and with the scarlet;"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"but he shall let the living bird go out of the city into the open field. So shall he make atonement for the house; and it shall be clean.\u201d"]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the law for any plague of leprosy, and for an itch,"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"and for the destructive mildew of a garment, and for a house,"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"and for a swelling, and for a scab, and for a bright spot;"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"to teach when it is unclean, and when it is clean."],[0,"This is the law of leprosy."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When any man has a discharge from his body, because of his discharge he is unclean."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This shall be his uncleanness in his discharge: whether his body runs with his discharge, or his body has stopped from his discharge, it is his uncleanness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Every bed on which he who has the discharge lies shall be unclean; and everything he sits on shall be unclean."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Whoever touches his bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He who sits on anything on which the man who has the discharge sat shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018He who touches the body of him who has the discharge shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If he who has the discharge spits on him who is clean, then he shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Whatever saddle he who has the discharge rides on shall be unclean."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Whoever touches anything that was under him shall be unclean until the evening. He who carries those things shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Whomever he who has the discharge touches, without having rinsed his hands in water, he shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The earthen vessel, which he who has the discharge touches, shall be broken; and every vessel of wood shall be rinsed in water."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When he who has a discharge is cleansed of his discharge, then he shall count to himself seven days for his cleansing, and wash his clothes; and he shall bathe his flesh in running water, and shall be clean."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the eighth day he shall take two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, and come before the LORD to the door of the Tent of Meeting, and give them to the priest."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The priest shall offer them, the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering. The priest shall make atonement for him before the LORD for his discharge."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If any man has an emission of semen, then he shall bathe all his flesh in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Every garment and every skin which the semen is on shall be washed with water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"If a man lies with a woman and there is an emission of semen, they shall both bathe themselves in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a woman has a discharge, and her discharge in her flesh is blood, she shall be in her impurity seven days. Whoever touches her shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Everything that she lies on in her impurity shall be unclean. Everything also that she sits on shall be unclean."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Whoever touches her bed shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Whoever touches anything that she sits on shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If it is on the bed, or on anything she sits on, when he touches it, he shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If any man lies with her, and her monthly flow is on him, he shall be unclean seven days; and every bed he lies on shall be unclean."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a woman has a discharge of her blood many days not in the time of her period, or if she has a discharge beyond the time of her period, all the days of the discharge of her uncleanness shall be as in the days of her period. She is unclean."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Every bed she lies on all the days of her discharge shall be to her as the bed of her period. Everything she sits on shall be unclean, as the uncleanness of her period."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Whoever touches these things shall be unclean, and shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if she is cleansed of her discharge, then she shall count to herself seven days, and after that she shall be clean."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"On the eighth day she shall take two turtledoves, or two young pigeons, and bring them to the priest, to the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The priest shall offer the one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering; and the priest shall make atonement for her before the LORD for the uncleanness of her discharge."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Thus you shall separate the children of Israel from their uncleanness, so they will not die in their uncleanness when they defile my tabernacle that is among them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the law of him who has a discharge, and of him who has an emission of semen, so that he is unclean by it;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"and of her who has her period, and of a man or woman who has a discharge, and of him who lies with her who is unclean."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses after the death of the two sons of Aaron, when they came near before the LORD, and died;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and the LORD said to Moses, \u201cTell Aaron your brother not to come at just any time into the Most Holy Place within the veil, before the mercy seat which is on the ark; lest he die; for I will appear in the cloud on the mercy seat."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAaron shall come into the sanctuary with a young bull for a sin offering, and a ram for a burnt offering."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He shall put on the holy linen tunic. He shall have the linen trousers on his body, and shall put on the linen sash, and he shall be clothed with the linen turban. They are the holy garments. He shall bathe his body in water, and put them on."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He shall take from the congregation of the children of Israel two male goats for a sin offering, and one ram for a burnt offering."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAaron shall offer the bull of the sin offering, which is for himself, and make atonement for himself and for his house."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He shall take the two goats, and set them before the LORD at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Aaron shall cast lots for the two goats: one lot for the LORD, and the other lot for the scapegoat."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Aaron shall present the goat on which the lot fell for the LORD, and offer him for a sin offering."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But the goat on which the lot fell for the scapegoat shall be presented alive before the LORD, to make atonement for him, to send him away as the scapegoat into the wilderness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAaron shall present the bull of the sin offering, which is for himself, and shall make atonement for himself and for his house, and shall kill the bull of the sin offering which is for himself."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He shall take a censer full of coals of fire from off the altar before the LORD, and two handfuls of sweet incense beaten small, and bring it within the veil."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He shall put the incense on the fire before the LORD, that the cloud of the incense may cover the mercy seat that is on the covenant, so that he will not die."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He shall take some of the blood of the bull, and sprinkle it with his finger on the mercy seat on the east; and before the mercy seat he shall sprinkle some of the blood with his finger seven times."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen he shall kill the goat of the sin offering that is for the people, and bring his blood within the veil, and do with his blood as he did with the blood of the bull, and sprinkle it on the mercy seat and before the mercy seat."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He shall make atonement for the Holy Place, because of the uncleanness of the children of Israel, and because of their transgressions, even all their sins; and so he shall do for the Tent of Meeting that dwells with them in the middle of their uncleanness."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"No one shall be in the Tent of Meeting when he enters to make atonement in the Holy Place, until he comes out, and has made atonement for himself and for his household, and for all the assembly of Israel."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe shall go out to the altar that is before the LORD and make atonement for it, and shall take some of the bull\u2019s blood, and some of the goat\u2019s blood, and put it around on the horns of the altar."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He shall sprinkle some of the blood on it with his finger seven times, and cleanse it, and make it holy from the uncleanness of the children of Israel."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen he has finished atoning for the Holy Place, the Tent of Meeting, and the altar, he shall present the live goat."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Aaron shall lay both his hands on the head of the live goat, and confess over him all the iniquities of the children of Israel, and all their transgressions, even all their sins; and he shall put them on the head of the goat, and shall send him away into the wilderness by the hand of a man who is ready."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The goat shall carry all their iniquities on himself to a solitary land, and he shall release the goat in the wilderness."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAaron shall come into the Tent of Meeting, and shall take off the linen garments which he put on when he went into the Holy Place, and shall leave them there."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then he shall bathe himself in water in a holy place, put on his garments, and come out and offer his burnt offering and the burnt offering of the people, and make atonement for himself and for the people."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The fat of the sin offering he shall burn on the altar."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who lets the goat go as the scapegoat shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The bull for the sin offering, and the goat for the sin offering, whose blood was brought in to make atonement in the Holy Place, shall be carried outside the camp; and they shall burn their skins, their flesh, and their dung with fire."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He who burns them shall wash his clothes, and bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt shall be a statute to you forever: in the seventh month, on the tenth day of the month, you shall afflict your souls, and shall do no kind of work, whether native-born or a stranger who lives as a foreigner among you;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"for on this day shall atonement be made for you, to cleanse you. You shall be clean from all your sins before the LORD."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"It is a Sabbath of solemn rest to you, and you shall afflict your souls. It is a statute forever."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The priest, who is anointed and who is consecrated to be priest in his father\u2019s place, shall make the atonement, and shall put on the linen garments, even the holy garments."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Then he shall make atonement for the Holy Sanctuary; and he shall make atonement for the Tent of Meeting and for the altar; and he shall make atonement for the priests and for all the people of the assembly."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis shall be an everlasting statute for you, to make atonement for the children of Israel once in the year because of all their sins.\u201d"],[0,"It was done as the LORD commanded Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Aaron, and to his sons, and to all the children of Israel, and say to them, \u2018This is the thing which the LORD has commanded:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Whatever man there is of the house of Israel who kills a bull, or lamb, or goat in the camp, or who kills it outside the camp,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and hasn\u2019t brought it to the door of the Tent of Meeting to offer it as an offering to the LORD before the LORD\u2019s tabernacle: blood shall be imputed to that man. He has shed blood. That man shall be cut off from among his people."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"This is to the end that the children of Israel may bring their sacrifices, which they sacrifice in the open field, that they may bring them to the LORD, to the door of the Tent of Meeting, to the priest, and sacrifice them for sacrifices of peace offerings to the LORD."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The priest shall sprinkle the blood on the LORD\u2019s altar at the door of the Tent of Meeting, and burn the fat for a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They shall no more sacrifice their sacrifices to the goat idols, after which they play the prostitute. This shall be a statute forever to them throughout their generations.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall say to them, \u2018Any man there is of the house of Israel, or of the strangers who live as foreigners among them, who offers a burnt offering or sacrifice,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and doesn\u2019t bring it to the door of the Tent of Meeting to sacrifice it to the LORD, that man shall be cut off from his people."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Any man of the house of Israel, or of the strangers who live as foreigners among them, who eats any kind of blood, I will set my face against that soul who eats blood, and will cut him off from among his people."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the life of the flesh is in the blood. I have given it to you on the altar to make atonement for your souls; for it is the blood that makes atonement by reason of the life."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore I have said to the children of Israel, \u201cNo person among you may eat blood, nor may any stranger who lives as a foreigner among you eat blood.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Whatever man there is of the children of Israel, or of the strangers who live as foreigners among them, who takes in hunting any animal or bird that may be eaten, he shall pour out its blood, and cover it with dust."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For as to the life of all flesh, its blood is with its life. Therefore I said to the children of Israel, \u201cYou shall not eat the blood of any kind of flesh; for the life of all flesh is its blood. Whoever eats it shall be cut off.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Every person that eats what dies of itself, or that which is torn by animals, whether he is native-born or a foreigner, shall wash his clothes, and bathe himself in water, and be unclean until the evening. Then he shall be clean."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But if he doesn\u2019t wash them, or bathe his flesh, then he shall bear his iniquity.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and say to them, \u2018I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall not do as they do in the land of Egypt, where you lived. You shall not do as they do in the land of Canaan, where I am bringing you. You shall not follow their statutes."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall do my ordinances. You shall keep my statutes and walk in them. I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall therefore keep my statutes and my ordinances, which if a man does, he shall live in them. I am the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018None of you shall approach any close relatives, to uncover their nakedness: I am the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your father, nor the nakedness of your mother: she is your mother. You shall not uncover her nakedness."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your father\u2019s wife. It is your father\u2019s nakedness."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your sister, the daughter of your father, or the daughter of your mother, whether born at home or born abroad."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your son\u2019s daughter, or of your daughter\u2019s daughter, even their nakedness; for theirs is your own nakedness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your father\u2019s wife\u2019s daughter, conceived by your father, since she is your sister."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your father\u2019s sister. She is your father\u2019s near kinswoman."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your mother\u2019s sister, for she is your mother\u2019s near kinswoman."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your father\u2019s brother. You shall not approach his wife. She is your aunt."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your daughter-in-law. She is your son\u2019s wife. You shall not uncover her nakedness."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your brother\u2019s wife. It is your brother\u2019s nakedness."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of a woman and her daughter. You shall not take her son\u2019s daughter, or her daughter\u2019s daughter, to uncover her nakedness. They are near kinswomen. It is wickedness."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not take a wife in addition to her sister, to be a rival, to uncover her nakedness, while her sister is still alive."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not approach a woman to uncover her nakedness, as long as she is impure by her uncleanness."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not lie carnally with your neighbor\u2019s wife, and defile yourself with her."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not give any of your children as a sacrifice to Molech. You shall not profane the name of your God. I am the LORD."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not lie with a man as with a woman. That is detestable."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not lie with any animal to defile yourself with it. No woman may give herself to an animal, to lie down with it: it is a perversion."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Don\u2019t defile yourselves in any of these things; for in all these the nations which I am casting out before you were defiled."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The land was defiled. Therefore I punished its iniquity, and the land vomited out her inhabitants."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You therefore shall keep my statutes and my ordinances, and shall not do any of these abominations; neither the native-born, nor the stranger who lives as a foreigner among you"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"(for the men of the land that were before you had done all these abominations, and the land became defiled),"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"that the land not vomit you out also, when you defile it, as it vomited out the nation that was before you."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018For whoever shall do any of these abominations, even the souls that do them shall be cut off from among their people."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall keep my requirements, that you do not practice any of these abominable customs which were practiced before you, and that you do not defile yourselves with them. I am the LORD your God.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to all the congregation of the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018You shall be holy; for I, the LORD your God, am holy."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Each one of you shall respect his mother and his father. You shall keep my Sabbaths. I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Don\u2019t turn to idols, nor make molten gods for yourselves. I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When you offer a sacrifice of peace offerings to the LORD, you shall offer it so that you may be accepted."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"It shall be eaten the same day you offer it, and on the next day. If anything remains until the third day, it shall be burned with fire."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If it is eaten at all on the third day, it is an abomination. It will not be accepted;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but everyone who eats it shall bear his iniquity, because he has profaned the holy thing of the LORD, and that soul shall be cut off from his people."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When you reap the harvest of your land, you shall not wholly reap the corners of your field, neither shall you gather the gleanings of your harvest."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall not glean your vineyard, neither shall you gather the fallen grapes of your vineyard. You shall leave them for the poor and for the foreigner. I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not steal."],[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not lie."],[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not deceive one another."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not swear by my name falsely, and profane the name of your God. I am the LORD."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not oppress your neighbor, nor rob him."],[0,"\u201c\u2018The wages of a hired servant shall not remain with you all night until the morning."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not curse the deaf, nor put a stumbling block before the blind; but you shall fear your God. I am the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall do no injustice in judgment. You shall not be partial to the poor, nor show favoritism to the great; but you shall judge your neighbor in righteousness."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not go around as a slanderer among your people."],[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not endanger the life of your neighbor. I am the LORD."]],f:["literally, \u201cblood\u201d"]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not hate your brother in your heart. You shall surely rebuke your neighbor, and not bear sin because of him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not take vengeance, nor bear any grudge against the children of your people; but you shall love your neighbor as yourself. I am the LORD."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall keep my statutes."],[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not cross-breed different kinds of animals."],[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not sow your field with two kinds of seed;"],[0,"\u201c\u2018Don\u2019t wear a garment made of two kinds of material."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man lies carnally with a woman who is a slave girl, pledged to be married to another man, and not ransomed or given her freedom; they shall be punished. They shall not be put to death, because she was not free."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He shall bring his trespass offering to the LORD, to the door of the Tent of Meeting, even a ram for a trespass offering."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The priest shall make atonement for him with the ram of the trespass offering before the LORD for his sin which he has committed; and the sin which he has committed shall be forgiven him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When you come into the land, and have planted all kinds of trees for food, then you shall count their fruit as forbidden. For three years it shall be forbidden to you. It shall not be eaten."]],f:["literally, \u201cuncircumcised\u201d"]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But in the fourth year all its fruit shall be holy, for giving praise to the LORD."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In the fifth year you shall eat its fruit, that it may yield its increase to you. I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not eat any meat with the blood still in it. You shall not use enchantments, nor practice sorcery."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not cut the hair on the sides of your head or clip off the edge of your beard."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not make any cuttings in your flesh for the dead, nor tattoo any marks on you. I am the LORD."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Don\u2019t profane your daughter, to make her a prostitute; lest the land fall to prostitution, and the land become full of wickedness."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall keep my Sabbaths, and reverence my sanctuary; I am the LORD."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Don\u2019t turn to those who are mediums, nor to the wizards. Don\u2019t seek them out, to be defiled by them. I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall rise up before the gray head and honor the face of the elderly; and you shall fear your God. I am the LORD."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a stranger lives as a foreigner with you in your land, you shall not do him wrong."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The stranger who lives as a foreigner with you shall be to you as the native-born among you, and you shall love him as yourself; for you lived as foreigners in the land of Egypt. I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall do no unrighteousness in judgment, in measures of length, of weight, or of quantity."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"You shall have just balances, just weights, a just ephah, and a just hin. I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons."]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall observe all my statutes and all my ordinances, and do them. I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover, you shall tell the children of Israel, \u2018Anyone of the children of Israel, or of the strangers who live as foreigners in Israel, who gives any of his offspring to Molech shall surely be put to death. The people of the land shall stone that person with stones."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I also will set my face against that person, and will cut him off from among his people, because he has given of his offspring to Molech, to defile my sanctuary, and to profane my holy name."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If the people of the land all hide their eyes from that person when he gives of his offspring to Molech, and don\u2019t put him to death,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"then I will set my face against that man and against his family, and will cut him off, and all who play the prostitute after him to play the prostitute with Molech, from among their people."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The person that turns to those who are mediums and wizards, to play the prostitute after them, I will even set my face against that person, and will cut him off from among his people."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Sanctify yourselves therefore, and be holy; for I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall keep my statutes, and do them. I am the LORD who sanctifies you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018For everyone who curses his father or his mother shall surely be put to death. He has cursed his father or his mother. His blood shall be upon himself."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The man who commits adultery with another man\u2019s wife, even he who commits adultery with his neighbor\u2019s wife, the adulterer and the adulteress shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The man who lies with his father\u2019s wife has uncovered his father\u2019s nakedness. Both of them shall surely be put to death. Their blood shall be upon themselves."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man lies with his daughter-in-law, both of them shall surely be put to death. They have committed a perversion. Their blood shall be upon themselves."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man lies with a male, as with a woman, both of them have committed an abomination. They shall surely be put to death. Their blood shall be upon themselves."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man takes a wife and her mother, it is wickedness. They shall be burned with fire, both he and they, that there may be no wickedness among you."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man lies with an animal, he shall surely be put to death; and you shall kill the animal."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a woman approaches any animal and lies with it, you shall kill the woman and the animal. They shall surely be put to death. Their blood shall be upon them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man takes his sister\u2014his father\u2019s daughter, or his mother\u2019s daughter\u2014and sees her nakedness, and she sees his nakedness, it is a shameful thing. They shall be cut off in the sight of the children of their people. He has uncovered his sister\u2019s nakedness. He shall bear his iniquity."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man lies with a woman having her monthly period, and uncovers her nakedness, he has made her fountain naked, and she has uncovered the fountain of her blood. Both of them shall be cut off from among their people."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall not uncover the nakedness of your mother\u2019s sister, nor of your father\u2019s sister, for he has made his close relative naked. They shall bear their iniquity."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"If a man lies with his uncle\u2019s wife, he has uncovered his uncle\u2019s nakedness. They shall bear their sin. They shall die childless."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man takes his brother\u2019s wife, it is an impurity. He has uncovered his brother\u2019s nakedness. They shall be childless."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall therefore keep all my statutes and all my ordinances, and do them, that the land where I am bringing you to dwell may not vomit you out."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You shall not walk in the customs of the nation which I am casting out before you; for they did all these things, and therefore I abhorred them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But I have said to you, \u201cYou shall inherit their land, and I will give it to you to possess it, a land flowing with milk and honey.\u201d I am the LORD your God, who has separated you from the peoples."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall therefore make a distinction between the clean animal and the unclean, and between the unclean fowl and the clean. You shall not make yourselves abominable by animal, or by bird, or by anything with which the ground teems, which I have separated from you as unclean for you."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall be holy to me, for I, the LORD, am holy, and have set you apart from the peoples, that you should be mine."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018A man or a woman that is a medium or is a wizard shall surely be put to death. They shall be stoned with stones. Their blood shall be upon themselves.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cSpeak to the priests, the sons of Aaron, and say to them, \u2018A priest shall not defile himself for the dead among his people,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"except for his relatives that are near to him: for his mother, for his father, for his son, for his daughter, for his brother,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and for his virgin sister who is near to him, who has had no husband; for her he may defile himself."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He shall not defile himself, being a chief man among his people, to profane himself."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018They shall not shave their heads or shave off the corners of their beards or make any cuttings in their flesh."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They shall be holy to their God, and not profane the name of their God, for they offer the offerings of the LORD made by fire, the bread of their God. Therefore they shall be holy."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018They shall not marry a woman who is a prostitute, or profane. A priest shall not marry a woman divorced from her husband; for he is holy to his God."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall sanctify him, for he offers the bread of your God. He shall be holy to you, for I the LORD, who sanctify you, am holy."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The daughter of any priest, if she profanes herself by playing the prostitute, she profanes her father. She shall be burned with fire."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018He who is the high priest among his brothers, upon whose head the anointing oil is poured, and who is consecrated to put on the garments, shall not let the hair of his head hang loose, or tear his clothes."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He must not go in to any dead body, or defile himself for his father or for his mother."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He shall not go out of the sanctuary, nor profane the sanctuary of his God; for the crown of the anointing oil of his God is upon him. I am the LORD."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018He shall take a wife in her virginity."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He shall not marry a widow, or one divorced, or a woman who has been defiled, or a prostitute. He shall take a virgin of his own people as a wife."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He shall not profane his offspring among his people, for I am the LORD who sanctifies him.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u201cSay to Aaron, \u2018None of your offspring throughout their generations who has a defect may approach to offer the bread of his God."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For whatever man he is that has a defect, he shall not draw near: a blind man, or a lame, or he who has a flat nose, or any deformity,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"or a man who has an injured foot, or an injured hand,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"or hunchbacked, or a dwarf, or one who has a defect in his eye, or an itching disease, or scabs, or who has damaged testicles."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"No man of the offspring of Aaron the priest who has a defect shall come near to offer the offerings of the LORD made by fire. Since he has a defect, he shall not come near to offer the bread of his God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He shall eat the bread of his God, both of the most holy, and of the holy."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He shall not come near to the veil, nor come near to the altar, because he has a defect; that he may not profane my sanctuaries, for I am the LORD who sanctifies them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"So Moses spoke to Aaron, and to his sons, and to all the children of Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cTell Aaron and his sons to separate themselves from the holy things of the children of Israel, which they make holy to me, and that they not profane my holy name. I am the LORD."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTell them, \u2018If anyone of all your offspring throughout your generations approaches the holy things which the children of Israel make holy to the LORD, having his uncleanness on him, that soul shall be cut off from before me. I am the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Whoever of the offspring of Aaron is a leper or has a discharge shall not eat of the holy things until he is clean. Whoever touches anything that is unclean by the dead, or a man who has a seminal emission,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"or whoever touches any creeping thing by which he may be made unclean, or a man from whom he may become unclean, whatever uncleanness he has\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"the person that touches any such shall be unclean until the evening, and shall not eat of the holy things unless he bathes his body in water."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When the sun is down, he shall be clean; and afterward he shall eat of the holy things, because it is his bread."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He shall not eat that which dies of itself or is torn by animals, defiling himself by it. I am the LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018They shall therefore follow my commandment, lest they bear sin for it and die in it, if they profane it. I am the LORD who sanctifies them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018No stranger shall eat of the holy thing: a foreigner living with the priests, or a hired servant, shall not eat of the holy thing."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But if a priest buys a slave, purchased by his money, he shall eat of it; and those who are born in his house shall eat of his bread."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If a priest\u2019s daughter is married to an outsider, she shall not eat of the heave offering of the holy things."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But if a priest\u2019s daughter is a widow, or divorced, and has no child, and has returned to her father\u2019s house as in her youth, she may eat of her father\u2019s bread; but no stranger shall eat any of it."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man eats something holy unwittingly, then he shall add the fifth part of its value to it, and shall give the holy thing to the priest."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The priests shall not profane the holy things of the children of Israel, which they offer to the LORD,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and so cause them to bear the iniquity that brings guilt when they eat their holy things; for I am the LORD who sanctifies them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Aaron, and to his sons, and to all the children of Israel, and say to them, \u2018Whoever is of the house of Israel, or of the foreigners in Israel, who offers his offering, whether it is any of their vows or any of their free will offerings, which they offer to the LORD for a burnt offering:"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"that you may be accepted, you shall offer a male without defect, of the bulls, of the sheep, or of the goats."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But you shall not offer whatever has a defect, for it shall not be acceptable for you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Whoever offers a sacrifice of peace offerings to the LORD to accomplish a vow, or for a free will offering of the herd or of the flock, it shall be perfect to be accepted. It shall have no defect."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall not offer what is blind, is injured, is maimed, has a wart, is festering, or has a running sore to the LORD, nor make an offering by fire of them on the altar to the LORD."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Either a bull or a lamb that has any deformity or lacking in his parts, that you may offer for a free will offering; but for a vow it shall not be accepted."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You must not offer to the LORD that which has its testicles bruised, crushed, broken, or cut. You must not do this in your land."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You must not offer any of these as the bread of your God from the hand of a foreigner, because their corruption is in them. There is a defect in them. They shall not be accepted for you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen a bull, a sheep, or a goat is born, it shall remain seven days with its mother. From the eighth day on it shall be accepted for the offering of an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Whether it is a cow or ewe, you shall not kill it and its young both in one day."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen you sacrifice a sacrifice of thanksgiving to the LORD, you shall sacrifice it so that you may be accepted."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"It shall be eaten on the same day; you shall leave none of it until the morning. I am the LORD."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore you shall keep my commandments, and do them. I am the LORD."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"You shall not profane my holy name, but I will be made holy among the children of Israel. I am the LORD who makes you holy,"]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:33,l:[[0,"who brought you out of the land of Egypt, to be your God. I am the LORD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018The set feasts of the LORD, which you shall proclaim to be holy convocations, even these are my set feasts."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Six days shall work be done, but on the seventh day is a Sabbath of solemn rest, a holy convocation; you shall do no kind of work. It is a Sabbath to the LORD in all your dwellings."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018These are the set feasts of the LORD, even holy convocations, which you shall proclaim in their appointed season."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"In the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month in the evening, is the LORD\u2019s Passover."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"On the fifteenth day of the same month is the feast of unleavened bread to the LORD. Seven days you shall eat unleavened bread."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In the first day you shall have a holy convocation. You shall do no regular work."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But you shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD seven days. In the seventh day is a holy convocation. You shall do no regular work.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When you have come into the land which I give to you, and shall reap its harvest, then you shall bring the sheaf of the first fruits of your harvest to the priest."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He shall wave the sheaf before the LORD, to be accepted for you. On the next day after the Sabbath the priest shall wave it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"On the day when you wave the sheaf, you shall offer a male lamb without defect a year old for a burnt offering to the LORD."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The meal offering with it shall be two tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with oil, an offering made by fire to the LORD for a pleasant aroma; and the drink offering with it shall be of wine, the fourth part of a hin."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You must not eat bread, or roasted grain, or fresh grain, until this same day, until you have brought the offering of your God. This is a statute forever throughout your generations in all your dwellings."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall count from the next day after the Sabbath, from the day that you brought the sheaf of the wave offering: seven Sabbaths shall be completed."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The next day after the seventh Sabbath you shall count fifty days; and you shall offer a new meal offering to the LORD."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall bring out of your habitations two loaves of bread for a wave offering made of two tenths of an ephah of fine flour. They shall be baked with yeast, for first fruits to the LORD."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall present with the bread seven lambs without defect a year old, one young bull, and two rams. They shall be a burnt offering to the LORD, with their meal offering and their drink offerings, even an offering made by fire, of a sweet aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall offer one male goat for a sin offering, and two male lambs a year old for a sacrifice of peace offerings."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The priest shall wave them with the bread of the first fruits for a wave offering before the LORD, with the two lambs. They shall be holy to the LORD for the priest."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You shall make proclamation on the same day that there shall be a holy convocation to you. You shall do no regular work. This is a statute forever in all your dwellings throughout your generations."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When you reap the harvest of your land, you must not wholly reap into the corners of your field. You must not gather the gleanings of your harvest. You must leave them for the poor and for the foreigner. I am the LORD your God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018In the seventh month, on the first day of the month, there shall be a solemn rest for you, a memorial of blowing of trumpets, a holy convocation."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You shall do no regular work. You shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"\u201cHowever on the tenth day of this seventh month is the day of atonement. It shall be a holy convocation to you. You shall afflict yourselves and you shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You shall do no kind of work in that same day, for it is a day of atonement, to make atonement for you before the LORD your God."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For whoever it is who shall not deny himself in that same day shall be cut off from his people."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Whoever does any kind of work in that same day, I will destroy that person from among his people."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"You shall do no kind of work: it is a statute forever throughout your generations in all your dwellings."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"It shall be a Sabbath of solemn rest for you, and you shall deny yourselves. In the ninth day of the month at evening, from evening to evening, you shall keep your Sabbath.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and say, \u2018On the fifteenth day of this seventh month is the feast of booths for seven days to the LORD."]],f:["or, feast of tents, or Succoth"]},{v:35,l:[[0,"On the first day shall be a holy convocation. You shall do no regular work."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Seven days you shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD. On the eighth day shall be a holy convocation to you. You shall offer an offering made by fire to the LORD. It is a solemn assembly; you shall do no regular work."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018These are the appointed feasts of the LORD which you shall proclaim to be holy convocations, to offer an offering made by fire to the LORD, a burnt offering, a meal offering, a sacrifice, and drink offerings, each on its own day\u2014"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"in addition to the Sabbaths of the LORD, and in addition to your gifts, and in addition to all your vows, and in addition to all your free will offerings, which you give to the LORD."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018So on the fifteenth day of the seventh month, when you have gathered in the fruits of the land, you shall keep the feast of the LORD seven days. On the first day shall be a solemn rest, and on the eighth day shall be a solemn rest."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"You shall take on the first day the fruit of majestic trees, branches of palm trees, and boughs of thick trees, and willows of the brook; and you shall rejoice before the LORD your God seven days."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"You shall keep it as a feast to the LORD seven days in the year. It is a statute forever throughout your generations. You shall keep it in the seventh month."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"You shall dwell in temporary shelters for seven days. All who are native-born in Israel shall dwell in temporary shelters,"]],f:["or, booths","or, booths"]},{v:43,l:[[0,"that your generations may know that I made the children of Israel to dwell in temporary shelters when I brought them out of the land of Egypt. I am the LORD your God.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["or, booths"]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"So Moses declared to the children of Israel the appointed feasts of the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cCommand the children of Israel, that they bring to you pure olive oil beaten for the light, to cause a lamp to burn continually."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Outside of the veil of the Testimony, in the Tent of Meeting, Aaron shall keep it in order from evening to morning before the LORD continually. It shall be a statute forever throughout your generations."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He shall keep in order the lamps on the pure gold lamp stand before the LORD continually."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall take fine flour, and bake twelve cakes of it: two tenths of an ephah shall be in one cake."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall set them in two rows, six on a row, on the pure gold table before the LORD."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall put pure frankincense on each row, that it may be to the bread for a memorial, even an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Every Sabbath day he shall set it in order before the LORD continually. It is an everlasting covenant on the behalf of the children of Israel."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It shall be for Aaron and his sons. They shall eat it in a holy place; for it is most holy to him of the offerings of the LORD made by fire by a perpetual statute.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The son of an Israelite woman, whose father was an Egyptian, went out among the children of Israel; and the son of the Israelite woman and a man of Israel strove together in the camp."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The son of the Israelite woman blasphemed the Name, and cursed; and they brought him to Moses. His mother\u2019s name was Shelomith, the daughter of Dibri, of the tribe of Dan."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They put him in custody until the LORD\u2019s will should be declared to them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"\u201cBring him who cursed out of the camp; and let all who heard him lay their hands on his head, and let all the congregation stone him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall speak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018Whoever curses his God shall bear his sin."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He who blasphemes the LORD\u2019s name, he shall surely be put to death. All the congregation shall certainly stone him. The foreigner as well as the native-born shall be put to death when he blasphemes the Name."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018He who strikes any man mortally shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He who strikes an animal mortally shall make it good, life for life."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"If anyone injures his neighbor, it shall be done to him as he has done:"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"fracture for fracture, eye for eye, tooth for tooth. It shall be done to him as he has injured someone."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He who kills an animal shall make it good; and he who kills a man shall be put to death."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall have one kind of law for the foreigner as well as the native-born; for I am the LORD your God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke to the children of Israel; and they brought him who had cursed out of the camp, and stoned him with stones. The children of Israel did as the LORD commanded Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses on Mount Sinai,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When you come into the land which I give you, then the land shall keep a Sabbath to the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall sow your field six years, and you shall prune your vineyard six years, and gather in its fruits;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"but in the seventh year there shall be a Sabbath of solemn rest for the land, a Sabbath to the LORD. You shall not sow your field or prune your vineyard."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"What grows of itself in your harvest you shall not reap, and you shall not gather the grapes of your undressed vine. It shall be a year of solemn rest for the land."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The Sabbath of the land shall be for food for you; for yourself, for your servant, for your maid, for your hired servant, and for your stranger, who lives as a foreigner with you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For your livestock also, and for the animals that are in your land, shall all its increase be for food."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall count off seven Sabbaths of years, seven times seven years; and there shall be to you the days of seven Sabbaths of years, even forty-nine years."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then you shall sound the loud trumpet on the tenth day of the seventh month. On the Day of Atonement you shall sound the trumpet throughout all your land."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall make the fiftieth year holy, and proclaim liberty throughout the land to all its inhabitants. It shall be a jubilee to you; and each of you shall return to his own property, and each of you shall return to his family."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"That fiftieth year shall be a jubilee to you. In it you shall not sow, neither reap that which grows of itself, nor gather from the undressed vines."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For it is a jubilee; it shall be holy to you. You shall eat of its increase out of the field."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018In this Year of Jubilee each of you shall return to his property."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If you sell anything to your neighbor, or buy from your neighbor, you shall not wrong one another."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"According to the number of years after the Jubilee you shall buy from your neighbor. According to the number of years of the crops he shall sell to you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"According to the length of the years you shall increase its price, and according to the shortness of the years you shall diminish its price; for he is selling the number of the crops to you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall not wrong one another, but you shall fear your God; for I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore you shall do my statutes, and keep my ordinances and do them; and you shall dwell in the land in safety."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The land shall yield its fruit, and you shall eat your fill, and dwell therein in safety."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"If you said, \u201cWhat shall we eat the seventh year? Behold, we shall not sow, nor gather in our increase;\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"then I will command my blessing on you in the sixth year, and it shall bear fruit for the three years."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall sow the eighth year, and eat of the fruits from the old store until the ninth year. Until its fruits come in, you shall eat the old store."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The land shall not be sold in perpetuity, for the land is mine; for you are strangers and live as foreigners with me."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"In all the land of your possession you shall grant a redemption for the land."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If your brother becomes poor, and sells some of his possessions, then his kinsman who is next to him shall come, and redeem that which his brother has sold."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"If a man has no one to redeem it, and he becomes prosperous and finds sufficient means to redeem it,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"then let him reckon the years since its sale, and restore the surplus to the man to whom he sold it; and he shall return to his property."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But if he isn\u2019t able to get it back for himself, then what he has sold shall remain in the hand of him who has bought it until the Year of Jubilee. In the Jubilee it shall be released, and he shall return to his property."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man sells a dwelling house in a walled city, then he may redeem it within a whole year after it has been sold. For a full year he shall have the right of redemption."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"If it isn\u2019t redeemed within the space of a full year, then the house that is in the walled city shall be made sure in perpetuity to him who bought it, throughout his generations. It shall not be released in the Jubilee."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But the houses of the villages which have no wall around them shall be accounted for with the fields of the country: they may be redeemed, and they shall be released in the Jubilee."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Nevertheless, in the cities of the Levites, the Levites may redeem the houses in the cities of their possession at any time."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The Levites may redeem the house that was sold, and the city of his possession, and it shall be released in the Jubilee; for the houses of the cities of the Levites are their possession among the children of Israel."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But the field of the pasture lands of their cities may not be sold, for it is their perpetual possession."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If your brother has become poor, and his hand can\u2019t support himself among you, then you shall uphold him. He shall live with you like an alien and a temporary resident."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Take no interest from him or profit; but fear your God, that your brother may live among you."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You shall not lend him your money at interest, nor give him your food for profit."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, to give you the land of Canaan, and to be your God."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If your brother has grown poor among you, and sells himself to you, you shall not make him to serve as a slave."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"As a hired servant, and as a temporary resident, he shall be with you; he shall serve with you until the Year of Jubilee."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Then he shall go out from you, he and his children with him, and shall return to his own family, and to the possession of his fathers."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"For they are my servants, whom I brought out of the land of Egypt. They shall not be sold as slaves."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"You shall not rule over him with harshness, but shall fear your God."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018As for your male and your female slaves, whom you may have from the nations that are around you, from them you may buy male and female slaves."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Moreover, of the children of the aliens who live among you, of them you may buy, and of their families who are with you, which they have conceived in your land; and they will be your property."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"You may make them an inheritance for your children after you, to hold for a possession. Of them you may take your slaves forever, but over your brothers the children of Israel you shall not rule, one over another, with harshness."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If an alien or temporary resident with you becomes rich, and your brother beside him has grown poor, and sells himself to the stranger or foreigner living among you, or to a member of the stranger\u2019s family,"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"after he is sold he may be redeemed. One of his brothers may redeem him;"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"or his uncle, or his uncle\u2019s son, may redeem him, or any who is a close relative to him of his family may redeem him; or if he has grown rich, he may redeem himself."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"He shall reckon with him who bought him from the year that he sold himself to him to the Year of Jubilee. The price of his sale shall be according to the number of years; he shall be with him according to the time of a hired servant."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"If there are yet many years, according to them he shall give back the price of his redemption out of the money that he was bought for."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"If there remain but a few years to the year of jubilee, then he shall reckon with him; according to his years of service he shall give back the price of his redemption."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"As a servant hired year by year shall he be with him. He shall not rule with harshness over him in your sight."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"If he isn\u2019t redeemed by these means, then he shall be released in the Year of Jubilee: he and his children with him."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"For to me the children of Israel are servants; they are my servants whom I brought out of the land of Egypt. I am the LORD your God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall make for yourselves no idols, and you shall not raise up a carved image or a pillar, and you shall not place any figured stone in your land, to bow down to it; for I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall keep my Sabbaths, and have reverence for my sanctuary. I am the LORD."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If you walk in my statutes and keep my commandments, and do them,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"then I will give you your rains in their season, and the land shall yield its increase, and the trees of the field shall yield their fruit."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Your threshing shall continue until the vintage, and the vintage shall continue until the sowing time. You shall eat your bread to the full, and dwell in your land safely."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018I will give peace in the land, and you shall lie down, and no one will make you afraid. I will remove evil animals out of the land, neither shall the sword go through your land."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall chase your enemies, and they shall fall before you by the sword."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Five of you shall chase a hundred, and a hundred of you shall chase ten thousand; and your enemies shall fall before you by the sword."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018I will have respect for you, make you fruitful, multiply you, and will establish my covenant with you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall eat old supplies long kept, and you shall move out the old because of the new."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I will set my tent among you, and my soul won\u2019t abhor you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I will walk among you, and will be your God, and you will be my people."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, that you should not be their slaves. I have broken the bars of your yoke, and made you walk upright."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if you will not listen to me, and will not do all these commandments,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and if you shall reject my statutes, and if your soul abhors my ordinances, so that you will not do all my commandments, but break my covenant,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I also will do this to you: I will appoint terror over you, even consumption and fever, that shall consume the eyes, and make the soul to pine away. You will sow your seed in vain, for your enemies will eat it."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I will set my face against you, and you will be struck before your enemies. Those who hate you will rule over you; and you will flee when no one pursues you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If you in spite of these things will not listen to me, then I will chastise you seven times more for your sins."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I will break the pride of your power, and I will make your sky like iron, and your soil like bronze."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Your strength will be spent in vain; for your land won\u2019t yield its increase, neither will the trees of the land yield their fruit."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If you walk contrary to me, and won\u2019t listen to me, then I will bring seven times more plagues on you according to your sins."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will send the wild animals among you, which will rob you of your children, destroy your livestock, and make you few in number. Your roads will become desolate."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If by these things you won\u2019t be turned back to me, but will walk contrary to me,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"then I will also walk contrary to you; and I will strike you, even I, seven times for your sins."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I will bring a sword upon you that will execute the vengeance of the covenant. You will be gathered together within your cities, and I will send the pestilence among you. You will be delivered into the hand of the enemy."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When I break your staff of bread, ten women shall bake your bread in one oven, and they shall deliver your bread again by weight. You shall eat, and not be satisfied."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If you in spite of this won\u2019t listen to me, but walk contrary to me,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"then I will walk contrary to you in wrath. I will also chastise you seven times for your sins."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You will eat the flesh of your sons, and you will eat the flesh of your daughters."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"I will destroy your high places, and cut down your incense altars, and cast your dead bodies upon the bodies of your idols; and my soul will abhor you."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"I will lay your cities waste, and will bring your sanctuaries to desolation. I will not take delight in the sweet fragrance of your offerings."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"I will bring the land into desolation, and your enemies who dwell in it will be astonished at it."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"I will scatter you among the nations, and I will draw out the sword after you. Your land will be a desolation, and your cities shall be a waste."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Then the land will enjoy its Sabbaths as long as it lies desolate and you are in your enemies\u2019 land. Even then the land will rest and enjoy its Sabbaths."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"As long as it lies desolate it shall have rest, even the rest which it didn\u2019t have in your Sabbaths when you lived on it."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018As for those of you who are left, I will send a faintness into their hearts in the lands of their enemies. The sound of a driven leaf will put them to flight; and they shall flee, as one flees from the sword. They will fall when no one pursues."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They will stumble over one another, as it were before the sword, when no one pursues. You will have no power to stand before your enemies."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"You will perish among the nations. The land of your enemies will eat you up."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Those of you who are left will pine away in their iniquity in your enemies\u2019 lands; and also in the iniquities of their fathers they shall pine away with them."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If they confess their iniquity and the iniquity of their fathers, in their trespass which they trespassed against me; and also that because they walked contrary to me,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"I also walked contrary to them, and brought them into the land of their enemies; if then their uncircumcised heart is humbled, and they then accept the punishment of their iniquity,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"then I will remember my covenant with Jacob, my covenant with Isaac, and also my covenant with Abraham; and I will remember the land."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"The land also will be left by them, and will enjoy its Sabbaths while it lies desolate without them; and they will accept the punishment of their iniquity because they rejected my ordinances, and their soul abhorred my statutes."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Yet for all that, when they are in the land of their enemies, I will not reject them, neither will I abhor them, to destroy them utterly and to break my covenant with them; for I am the LORD their God."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"But I will for their sake remember the covenant of their ancestors, whom I brought out of the land of Egypt in the sight of the nations, that I might be their God. I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the statutes, ordinances, and laws, which the LORD made between him and the children of Israel in Mount Sinai by Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and say to them, \u2018When a man consecrates a person to the LORD in a vow, according to your valuation,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"your valuation of a male from twenty years old to sixty years old shall be fifty shekels of silver, according to the shekel of the sanctuary."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If she is a female, then your valuation shall be thirty shekels."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"If the person is from five years old to twenty years old, then your valuation shall be for a male twenty shekels, and for a female ten shekels."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"If the person is from a month old to five years old, then your valuation shall be for a male five shekels of silver, and for a female your valuation shall be three shekels of silver."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If the person is from sixty years old and upward; if he is a male, then your valuation shall be fifteen shekels, and for a female ten shekels."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But if he is poorer than your valuation, then he shall be set before the priest, and the priest shall assign a value to him. The priest shall assign a value according to his ability to pay."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If it is an animal of which men offer an offering to the LORD, all that any man gives of such to the LORD becomes holy."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He shall not alter it, nor exchange it, a good for a bad, or a bad for a good. If he shall at all exchange animal for animal, then both it and that for which it is exchanged shall be holy."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If it is any unclean animal, of which they do not offer as an offering to the LORD, then he shall set the animal before the priest;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and the priest shall evaluate it, whether it is good or bad. As the priest evaluates it, so it shall be."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But if he will indeed redeem it, then he shall add the fifth part of it to its valuation."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When a man dedicates his house to be holy to the LORD, then the priest shall evaluate it, whether it is good or bad. As the priest evaluates it, so it shall stand."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If he who dedicates it will redeem his house, then he shall add the fifth part of the money of your valuation to it, and it shall be his."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a man dedicates to the LORD part of the field of his possession, then your valuation shall be according to the seed for it. The sowing of a homer of barley shall be valued at fifty shekels of silver."]],f:["1 homer is about 220 liters or 6 bushels","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If he dedicates his field from the Year of Jubilee, according to your valuation it shall stand."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But if he dedicates his field after the Jubilee, then the priest shall reckon to him the money according to the years that remain to the Year of Jubilee; and an abatement shall be made from your valuation."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"If he who dedicated the field will indeed redeem it, then he shall add the fifth part of the money of your valuation to it, and it shall remain his."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"If he will not redeem the field, or if he has sold the field to another man, it shall not be redeemed any more;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"but the field, when it goes out in the Jubilee, shall be holy to the LORD, as a devoted field. It shall be owned by the priests."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If he dedicates a field to the LORD which he has bought, which is not of the field of his possession,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"then the priest shall reckon to him the worth of your valuation up to the Year of Jubilee; and he shall give your valuation on that day, as a holy thing to the LORD."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"In the Year of Jubilee the field shall return to him from whom it was bought, even to him to whom the possession of the land belongs."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"All your valuations shall be according to the shekel of the sanctuary: twenty gerahs to the shekel."]],f:["A gerah is about 0.5 grams or about 7.7 grains.","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018However the firstborn among animals, which belongs to the LORD as a firstborn, no man may dedicate, whether an ox or a sheep. It is the LORD\u2019s."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"If it is an unclean animal, then he shall buy it back according to your valuation, and shall add to it the fifth part of it; or if it isn\u2019t redeemed, then it shall be sold according to your valuation."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Notwithstanding, no devoted thing that a man devotes to the LORD of all that he has, whether of man or animal, or of the field of his possession, shall be sold or redeemed. Everything that is permanently devoted is most holy to the LORD."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018No one devoted to destruction, who shall be devoted from among men, shall be ransomed. He shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018All the tithe of the land, whether of the seed of the land or of the fruit of the trees, is the LORD\u2019s. It is holy to the LORD."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"If a man redeems anything of his tithe, he shall add a fifth part to it."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"All the tithe of the herds or the flocks, whatever passes under the rod, the tenth shall be holy to the LORD."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He shall not examine whether it is good or bad, neither shall he exchange it. If he exchanges it at all, then both it and that for which it is exchanged shall be holy. It shall not be redeemed.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the commandments which the LORD commanded Moses for the children of Israel on Mount Sinai."]]}]]}},1274,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,s){h.exports={book:"Num",name:"Numbers",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the Tent of Meeting, on the first day of the second month, in the second year after they had come out of the land of Egypt, saying,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cTake a census of all the congregation of the children of Israel, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, every male, one by one,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"from twenty years old and upward, all who are able to go out to war in Israel. You and Aaron shall count them by their divisions."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"With you there shall be a man of every tribe, each one head of his fathers\u2019 house."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"These are the names of the men who shall stand with you:"],[0,"Of Reuben: Elizur the son of Shedeur."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Simeon: Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Judah: Nahshon the son of Amminadab."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Issachar: Nethanel the son of Zuar."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Zebulun: Eliab the son of Helon."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Joseph: of Ephraim: Elishama the son of Ammihud; of Manasseh: Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Benjamin: Abidan the son of Gideoni."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Dan: Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Asher: Pagiel the son of Ochran."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Gad: Eliasaph the son of Deuel."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Naphtali: Ahira the son of Enan.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"These are those who were called of the congregation, the princes of the tribes of their fathers; they were the heads of the thousands of Israel."]],f:["or, chiefs, or, leaders"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron took these men who are mentioned by name."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They assembled all the congregation together on the first day of the second month; and they declared their ancestry by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, one by one."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"As the LORD commanded Moses, so he counted them in the wilderness of Sinai."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Reuben, Israel\u2019s firstborn, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, one by one, every male from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Reuben, were forty-six thousand five hundred."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Simeon, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, those who were counted of it, according to the number of the names, one by one, every male from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Simeon, were fifty-nine thousand three hundred."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Gad, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Gad, were forty-five thousand six hundred fifty."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Judah, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Judah, were seventy-four thousand six hundred."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Issachar, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Issachar, were fifty-four thousand four hundred."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Zebulun, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Zebulun, were fifty-seven thousand four hundred."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Joseph: of the children of Ephraim, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Ephraim, were forty thousand five hundred."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Manasseh, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Manasseh, were thirty-two thousand two hundred."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Benjamin, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Benjamin, were thirty-five thousand four hundred."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Dan, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Dan, were sixty-two thousand seven hundred."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Asher, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Asher, were forty-one thousand five hundred."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Naphtali, their generations, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Naphtali, were fifty-three thousand four hundred."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted, whom Moses and Aaron counted, and the twelve men who were princes of Israel, each one for his fathers\u2019 house."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"So all those who were counted of the children of Israel by their fathers\u2019 houses, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war in Israel\u2014"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"all those who were counted were six hundred three thousand five hundred fifty."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"But the Levites after the tribe of their fathers were not counted among them."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"For the LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"\u201cOnly the tribe of Levi you shall not count, neither shall you take a census of them among the children of Israel;"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"but appoint the Levites over the Tabernacle of the Testimony, and over all its furnishings, and over all that belongs to it. They shall carry the tabernacle and all its furnishings; and they shall take care of it, and shall encamp around it."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"When the tabernacle is to move, the Levites shall take it down; and when the tabernacle is to be set up, the Levites shall set it up. The stranger who comes near shall be put to death."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"The children of Israel shall pitch their tents, every man by his own camp, and every man by his own standard, according to their divisions."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"But the Levites shall encamp around the Tabernacle of the Testimony, that there may be no wrath on the congregation of the children of Israel. The Levites shall be responsible for the Tabernacle of the Testimony.\u201d"]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus the children of Israel did. According to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so they did."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe children of Israel shall encamp every man by his own standard, with the banners of their fathers\u2019 houses. They shall encamp around the Tent of Meeting at a distance from it."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThose who encamp on the east side toward the sunrise shall be of the standard of the camp of Judah, according to their divisions. The prince of the children of Judah shall be Nahshon the son of Amminadab."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were seventy-four thousand six hundred."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThose who encamp next to him shall be the tribe of Issachar. The prince of the children of Issachar shall be Nethanel the son of Zuar."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of it, were fifty-four thousand four hundred."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe tribe of Zebulun: the prince of the children of Zebulun shall be Eliab the son of Helon."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of it, were fifty-seven thousand four hundred."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll who were counted of the camp of Judah were one hundred eighty-six thousand four hundred, according to their divisions. They shall set out first."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the south side shall be the standard of the camp of Reuben according to their divisions. The prince of the children of Reuben shall be Elizur the son of Shedeur."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of it, were forty-six thousand five hundred."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThose who encamp next to him shall be the tribe of Simeon. The prince of the children of Simeon shall be Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were fifty-nine thousand three hundred."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe tribe of Gad: the prince of the children of Gad shall be Eliasaph the son of Reuel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were forty-five thousand six hundred fifty."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll who were counted of the camp of Reuben were one hundred fifty-one thousand four hundred fifty, according to their armies. They shall set out second."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen the Tent of Meeting shall set out, with the camp of the Levites in the middle of the camps. As they encamp, so shall they set out, every man in his place, by their standards."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the west side shall be the standard of the camp of Ephraim according to their divisions. The prince of the children of Ephraim shall be Elishama the son of Ammihud."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were forty thousand five hundred."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNext to him shall be the tribe of Manasseh. The prince of the children of Manasseh shall be Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were thirty-two thousand two hundred."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe tribe of Benjamin: the prince of the children of Benjamin shall be Abidan the son of Gideoni."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"His army, and those who were counted of them, were thirty-five thousand four hundred."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll who were counted of the camp of Ephraim were one hundred eight thousand one hundred, according to their divisions. They shall set out third."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the north side shall be the standard of the camp of Dan according to their divisions. The prince of the children of Dan shall be Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were sixty-two thousand seven hundred."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThose who encamp next to him shall be the tribe of Asher. The prince of the children of Asher shall be Pagiel the son of Ochran."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were forty-one thousand five hundred."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe tribe of Naphtali: the prince of the children of Naphtali shall be Ahira the son of Enan."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"His division, and those who were counted of them, were fifty-three thousand four hundred."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll who were counted of the camp of Dan were one hundred fifty-seven thousand six hundred. They shall set out last by their standards.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted of the children of Israel by their fathers\u2019 houses. All who were counted of the camps according to their armies were six hundred three thousand five hundred fifty."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But the Levites were not counted among the children of Israel, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus the children of Israel did. According to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so they encamped by their standards, and so they set out, everyone by their families, according to their fathers\u2019 houses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this is the history of the generations of Aaron and Moses in the day that the LORD spoke with Moses in Mount Sinai."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"These are the names of the sons of Aaron: Nadab the firstborn, and Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the names of the sons of Aaron, the priests who were anointed, whom he consecrated to minister in the priest\u2019s office."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Nadab and Abihu died before the LORD when they offered strange fire before the LORD in the wilderness of Sinai, and they had no children. Eleazar and Ithamar ministered in the priest\u2019s office in the presence of Aaron their father."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cBring the tribe of Levi near, and set them before Aaron the priest, that they may minister to him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They shall keep his requirements, and the requirements of the whole congregation before the Tent of Meeting, to do the service of the tabernacle."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They shall keep all the furnishings of the Tent of Meeting, and the obligations of the children of Israel, to do the service of the tabernacle."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall give the Levites to Aaron and to his sons. They are wholly given to him on the behalf of the children of Israel."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall appoint Aaron and his sons, and they shall keep their priesthood, but the stranger who comes near shall be put to death.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I have taken the Levites from among the children of Israel instead of all the firstborn who open the womb among the children of Israel; and the Levites shall be mine,"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:13,l:[[0,"for all the firstborn are mine. On the day that I struck down all the firstborn in the land of Egypt I made holy to me all the firstborn in Israel, both man and animal. They shall be mine. I am the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, saying,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cCount the children of Levi by their fathers\u2019 houses, by their families. You shall count every male from a month old and upward.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses counted them according to the LORD\u2019s word, as he was commanded."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"These were the sons of Levi by their names: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the names of the sons of Gershon by their families: Libni and Shimei."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Kohath by their families: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Merari by their families: Mahli and Mushi."],[0,"These are the families of the Levites according to their fathers\u2019 houses."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Gershon was the family of the Libnites, and the family of the Shimeites. These are the families of the Gershonites."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who were counted of them, according to the number of all the males from a month old and upward, even those who were counted of them were seven thousand five hundred."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The families of the Gershonites shall encamp behind the tabernacle westward."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Eliasaph the son of Lael shall be the prince of the fathers\u2019 house of the Gershonites."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The duty of the sons of Gershon in the Tent of Meeting shall be the tabernacle, the tent, its covering, the screen for the door of the Tent of Meeting,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"the hangings of the court, the screen for the door of the court which is by the tabernacle and around the altar, and its cords for all of its service."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Kohath was the family of the Amramites, the family of the Izharites, the family of the Hebronites, and the family of the Uzzielites. These are the families of the Kohathites."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"According to the number of all the males from a month old and upward, there were eight thousand six hundred keeping the requirements of the sanctuary."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The families of the sons of Kohath shall encamp on the south side of the tabernacle."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The prince of the fathers\u2019 house of the families of the Kohathites shall be Elizaphan the son of Uzziel."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Their duty shall be the ark, the table, the lamp stand, the altars, the vessels of the sanctuary with which they minister, the screen, and all its service."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest shall be prince of the princes of the Levites, with the oversight of those who keep the requirements of the sanctuary."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Merari was the family of the Mahlites and the family of the Mushites. These are the families of Merari."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Those who were counted of them, according to the number of all the males from a month old and upward, were six thousand two hundred."]],f:["+ 22,000 is the sum rounded to 2 significant digits. The sum of the Gershonites, Kohathites, and Merarites given above is 22,300, but the traditional Hebrew text has the number rounded to 2 significant digits, not 3 significant digits."]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"The prince of the fathers\u2019 house of the families of Merari was Zuriel the son of Abihail. They shall encamp on the north side of the tabernacle."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The appointed duty of the sons of Merari shall be the tabernacle\u2019s boards, its bars, its pillars, its sockets, all its instruments, all its service,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"the pillars of the court around it, their sockets, their pins, and their cords."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who encamp before the tabernacle eastward, in front of the Tent of Meeting toward the sunrise, shall be Moses, with Aaron and his sons, keeping the requirements of the sanctuary for the duty of the children of Israel. The outsider who comes near shall be put to death."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"All who were counted of the Levites, whom Moses and Aaron counted at the commandment of the LORD, by their families, all the males from a month old and upward, were twenty-two thousand."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cCount all the firstborn males of the children of Israel from a month old and upward, and take the number of their names."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"You shall take the Levites for me\u2014I am the LORD\u2014instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel; and the livestock of the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the livestock of the children of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses counted, as the LORD commanded him, all the firstborn among the children of Israel."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"All the firstborn males according to the number of names from a month old and upward, of those who were counted of them, were twenty-two thousand two hundred seventy-three."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"\u201cTake the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel, and the livestock of the Levites instead of their livestock; and the Levites shall be mine. I am the LORD."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"For the redemption of the two hundred seventy-three of the firstborn of the children of Israel who exceed the number of the Levites,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"you shall take five shekels apiece for each one; according to the shekel of the sanctuary you shall take them (the shekel is twenty gerahs);"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces.","A gerah is about 0.5 grams or about 7.7 grains."]},{v:48,l:[[0,"and you shall give the money, with which their remainder is redeemed, to Aaron and to his sons.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses took the redemption money from those who exceeded the number of those who were redeemed by the Levites;"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"from the firstborn of the children of Israel he took the money, one thousand three hundred sixty-five shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary;"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 1365 shekels is about 13.65 kilograms or about 30 pounds."]},{v:51,l:[[0,"and Moses gave the redemption money to Aaron and to his sons, according to the LORD\u2019s word, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cTake a census of the sons of Kohath from among the sons of Levi, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"from thirty years old and upward even until fifty years old, all who enter into the service to do the work in the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the service of the sons of Kohath in the Tent of Meeting, regarding the most holy things."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When the camp moves forward, Aaron shall go in with his sons; and they shall take down the veil of the screen, cover the ark of the Testimony with it,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"put a covering of sealskin on it, spread a blue cloth over it, and put in its poles."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the table of show bread they shall spread a blue cloth, and put on it the dishes, the spoons, the bowls, and the cups with which to pour out; and the continual bread shall be on it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They shall spread on them a scarlet cloth, and cover it with a covering of sealskin, and shall put in its poles."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey shall take a blue cloth and cover the lamp stand of the light, its lamps, its snuffers, its snuff dishes, and all its oil vessels, with which they minister to it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They shall put it and all its vessels within a covering of sealskin, and shall put it on the frame."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the golden altar they shall spread a blue cloth, and cover it with a covering of sealskin, and shall put in its poles."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey shall take all the vessels of ministry with which they minister in the sanctuary, and put them in a blue cloth, cover them with a covering of sealskin, and shall put them on the frame."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey shall take away the ashes from the altar, and spread a purple cloth on it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They shall put on it all its vessels with which they minister about it, the fire pans, the meat hooks, the shovels, and the basins\u2014all the vessels of the altar; and they shall spread on it a covering of sealskin, and put in its poles."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen Aaron and his sons have finished covering the sanctuary and all the furniture of the sanctuary, as the camp moves forward; after that, the sons of Kohath shall come to carry it; but they shall not touch the sanctuary, lest they die. The sons of Kohath shall carry these things belonging to the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe duty of Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest shall be the oil for the light, the sweet incense, the continual meal offering, and the anointing oil, the requirements of all the tabernacle, and of all that is in it, the sanctuary, and its furnishings.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t cut off the tribe of the families of the Kohathites from among the Levites;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"but do this to them, that they may live, and not die, when they approach the most holy things: Aaron and his sons shall go in and appoint everyone to his service and to his burden;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but they shall not go in to see the sanctuary even for a moment, lest they die.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"\u201cTake a census of the sons of Gershon also, by their fathers\u2019 houses, by their families;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"you shall count them from thirty years old and upward until fifty years old: all who enter in to wait on the service, to do the work in the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the service of the families of the Gershonites, in serving and in bearing burdens:"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"they shall carry the curtains of the tabernacle and the Tent of Meeting, its covering, the covering of sealskin that is on it, the screen for the door of the Tent of Meeting,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"the hangings of the court, the screen for the door of the gate of the court which is by the tabernacle and around the altar, their cords, and all the instruments of their service, and whatever shall be done with them. They shall serve in there."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"At the commandment of Aaron and his sons shall be all the service of the sons of the Gershonites, in all their burden and in all their service; and you shall appoint their duty to them in all their responsibilities."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"This is the service of the families of the sons of the Gershonites in the Tent of Meeting. Their duty shall be under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for the sons of Merari, you shall count them by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"you shall count them from thirty years old and upward even to fifty years old\u2014everyone who enters on the service, to do the work of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"This is the duty of their burden, according to all their service in the Tent of Meeting: the tabernacle\u2019s boards, its bars, its pillars, its sockets,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"the pillars of the court around it, their sockets, their pins, their cords, with all their instruments, and with all their service. You shall appoint the instruments of the duty of their burden to them by name."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"This is the service of the families of the sons of Merari, according to all their service in the Tent of Meeting, under the hand of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron and the princes of the congregation counted the sons of the Kohathites by their families, and by their fathers\u2019 houses,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"from thirty years old and upward even to fifty years old, everyone who entered into the service for work in the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Those who were counted of them by their families were two thousand seven hundred fifty."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted of the families of the Kohathites, all who served in the Tent of Meeting, whom Moses and Aaron counted according to the commandment of the LORD by Moses."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who were counted of the sons of Gershon, by their families, and by their fathers\u2019 houses,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"from thirty years old and upward even to fifty years old\u2014everyone who entered into the service for work in the Tent of Meeting,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"even those who were counted of them, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses, were two thousand six hundred thirty."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted of the families of the sons of Gershon, all who served in the Tent of Meeting, whom Moses and Aaron counted according to the commandment of the LORD."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who were counted of the families of the sons of Merari, by their families, by their fathers\u2019 houses,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"from thirty years old and upward even to fifty years old\u2014everyone who entered into the service for work in the Tent of Meeting,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"even those who were counted of them by their families, were three thousand two hundred."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted of the families of the sons of Merari, whom Moses and Aaron counted according to the commandment of the LORD by Moses."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"All those who were counted of the Levites whom Moses and Aaron and the princes of Israel counted, by their families and by their fathers\u2019 houses,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"from thirty years old and upward even to fifty years old, everyone who entered in to do the work of service and the work of bearing burdens in the Tent of Meeting,"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"even those who were counted of them, were eight thousand five hundred eighty."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"According to the commandment of the LORD they were counted by Moses, everyone according to his service and according to his burden. Thus they were counted by him, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cCommand the children of Israel that they put out of the camp every leper, everyone who has a discharge, and whoever is unclean by a corpse."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall put both male and female outside of the camp so that they don\u2019t defile their camp, in the midst of which I dwell.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did so, and put them outside of the camp; as the LORD spoke to Moses, so the children of Israel did."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel: \u2018When a man or woman commits any sin that men commit, so as to trespass against the LORD, and that soul is guilty,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"then he shall confess his sin which he has done; and he shall make restitution for his guilt in full, add to it the fifth part of it, and give it to him in respect of whom he has been guilty."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But if the man has no kinsman to whom restitution may be made for the guilt, the restitution for guilt which is made to the LORD shall be the priest\u2019s, in addition to the ram of the atonement, by which atonement shall be made for him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Every heave offering of all the holy things of the children of Israel, which they present to the priest, shall be his."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Every man\u2019s holy things shall be his; whatever any man gives the priest, it shall be his.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them: \u2018If any man\u2019s wife goes astray and is unfaithful to him,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and a man lies with her carnally, and it is hidden from the eyes of her husband and this is kept concealed, and she is defiled, there is no witness against her, and she isn\u2019t taken in the act;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and the spirit of jealousy comes on him, and he is jealous of his wife and she is defiled; or if the spirit of jealousy comes on him, and he is jealous of his wife and she isn\u2019t defiled;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"then the man shall bring his wife to the priest, and shall bring her offering for her: one tenth of an ephah of barley meal. He shall pour no oil on it, nor put frankincense on it, for it is a meal offering of jealousy, a meal offering of memorial, bringing iniquity to memory."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The priest shall bring her near, and set her before the LORD."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The priest shall take holy water in an earthen vessel; and the priest shall take some of the dust that is on the floor of the tabernacle and put it into the water."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The priest shall set the woman before the LORD, and let the hair of the woman\u2019s head go loose, and put the meal offering of memorial in her hands, which is the meal offering of jealousy. The priest shall have in his hand the water of bitterness that brings a curse."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The priest shall cause her to take an oath and shall tell the woman, \u201cIf no man has lain with you, and if you haven\u2019t gone aside to uncleanness, being under your husband\u2019s authority, be free from this water of bitterness that brings a curse."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But if you have gone astray, being under your husband\u2019s authority, and if you are defiled, and some man has lain with you besides your husband\u2014\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"then the priest shall cause the woman to swear with the oath of cursing, and the priest shall tell the woman, \u201cMay the LORD make you a curse and an oath among your people, when the LORD allows your thigh to fall away, and your body to swell;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and this water that brings a curse will go into your bowels, and make your body swell, and your thigh fall away.\u201d The woman shall say, \u201cAmen, Amen.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The priest shall write these curses in a book, and he shall wipe them into the water of bitterness."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He shall make the woman drink the water of bitterness that causes the curse; and the water that causes the curse shall enter into her and become bitter."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The priest shall take the meal offering of jealousy out of the woman\u2019s hand, and shall wave the meal offering before the LORD, and bring it to the altar."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The priest shall take a handful of the meal offering, as its memorial portion, and burn it on the altar, and afterward shall make the woman drink the water."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When he has made her drink the water, then it shall happen, if she is defiled and has committed a trespass against her husband, that the water that causes the curse will enter into her and become bitter, and her body will swell, and her thigh will fall away; and the woman will be a curse among her people."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"If the woman isn\u2019t defiled, but is clean; then she shall be free, and shall conceive offspring."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law of jealousy, when a wife, being under her husband, goes astray, and is defiled,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"or when the spirit of jealousy comes on a man, and he is jealous of his wife; then he shall set the woman before the LORD, and the priest shall execute on her all this law."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The man shall be free from iniquity, and that woman shall bear her iniquity.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them: \u2018When either man or woman shall make a special vow, the vow of a Nazirite, to separate himself to the LORD,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"he shall separate himself from wine and strong drink. He shall drink no vinegar of wine, or vinegar of fermented drink, neither shall he drink any juice of grapes, nor eat fresh grapes or dried."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"All the days of his separation he shall eat nothing that is made of the grapevine, from the seeds even to the skins."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018All the days of his vow of separation no razor shall come on his head, until the days are fulfilled in which he separates himself to the LORD. He shall be holy. He shall let the locks of the hair of his head grow long."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018All the days that he separates himself to the LORD he shall not go near a dead body."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He shall not make himself unclean for his father, or for his mother, for his brother, or for his sister, when they die, because his separation to God is on his head."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All the days of his separation he is holy to the LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If any man dies very suddenly beside him, and he defiles the head of his separation, then he shall shave his head in the day of his cleansing. On the seventh day he shall shave it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"On the eighth day he shall bring two turtledoves or two young pigeons to the priest, to the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The priest shall offer one for a sin offering, and the other for a burnt offering, and make atonement for him, because he sinned by reason of the dead, and shall make his head holy that same day."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He shall separate to the LORD the days of his separation, and shall bring a male lamb a year old for a trespass offering; but the former days shall be void, because his separation was defiled."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law of the Nazirite: when the days of his separation are fulfilled, he shall be brought to the door of the Tent of Meeting,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and he shall offer his offering to the LORD: one male lamb a year old without defect for a burnt offering, one ewe lamb a year old without defect for a sin offering, one ram without defect for peace offerings,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"a basket of unleavened bread, cakes of fine flour mixed with oil, and unleavened wafers anointed with oil with their meal offering and their drink offerings."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The priest shall present them before the LORD, and shall offer his sin offering and his burnt offering."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He shall offer the ram for a sacrifice of peace offerings to the LORD, with the basket of unleavened bread. The priest shall offer also its meal offering and its drink offering."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The Nazirite shall shave the head of his separation at the door of the Tent of Meeting, take the hair of the head of his separation, and put it on the fire which is under the sacrifice of peace offerings."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The priest shall take the boiled shoulder of the ram, one unleavened cake out of the basket, and one unleavened wafer, and shall put them on the hands of the Nazirite after he has shaved the head of his separation;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and the priest shall wave them for a wave offering before the LORD. They are holy for the priest, together with the breast that is waved and the thigh that is offered. After that the Nazirite may drink wine."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This is the law of the Nazirite who vows and of his offering to the LORD for his separation, in addition to that which he is able to afford. According to his vow which he vows, so he must do after the law of his separation.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Aaron and to his sons, saying, \u2018This is how you shall bless the children of Israel.\u2019 You shall tell them,"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018The LORD bless you, and keep you."]]},{v:25,l:[[2,"The LORD make his face to shine on you,"],[2,"and be gracious to you."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD lift up his face toward you,"],[2,"and give you peace.\u2019"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo they shall put my name on the children of Israel; and I will bless them.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"On the day that Moses had finished setting up the tabernacle, and had anointed it and sanctified it with all its furniture, and the altar with all its vessels, and had anointed and sanctified them;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"the princes of Israel, the heads of their fathers\u2019 houses, gave offerings. These were the princes of the tribes. These are they who were over those who were counted;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and they brought their offering before the LORD, six covered wagons and twelve oxen; a wagon for every two of the princes, and for each one an ox. They presented them before the tabernacle."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cAccept these from them, that they may be used in doing the service of the Tent of Meeting; and you shall give them to the Levites, to every man according to his service.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses took the wagons and the oxen, and gave them to the Levites."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He gave two wagons and four oxen to the sons of Gershon, according to their service."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He gave four wagons and eight oxen to the sons of Merari, according to their service, under the direction of Ithamar the son of Aaron the priest."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But to the sons of Kohath he gave none, because the service of the sanctuary belonged to them; they carried it on their shoulders."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The princes gave offerings for the dedication of the altar in the day that it was anointed. The princes gave their offerings before the altar."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cThey shall offer their offering, each prince on his day, for the dedication of the altar.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He who offered his offering the first day was Nahshon the son of Amminadab, of the tribe of Judah,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and his offering was:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Nahshon the son of Amminadab."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"On the second day Nethanel the son of Zuar, prince of Issachar, gave his offering."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He offered for his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Nethanel the son of Zuar."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"On the third day Eliab the son of Helon, prince of the children of Zebulun,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was a hundred and thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Eliab the son of Helon."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"On the fourth day Elizur the son of Shedeur, prince of the children of Reuben,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Elizur the son of Shedeur."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"On the fifth day Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai, prince of the children of Simeon,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old: this was the offering of Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"On the sixth day, Eliasaph the son of Deuel, prince of the children of Gad,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Eliasaph the son of Deuel."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"On the seventh day Elishama the son of Ammihud, prince of the children of Ephraim,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Elishama the son of Ammihud."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"On the eighth day Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur, prince of the children of Manasseh,"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur."]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[0,"On the ninth day Abidan the son of Gideoni, prince of the children of Benjamin,"]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:64,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:65,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Abidan the son of Gideoni."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[0,"On the tenth day Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai, prince of the children of Dan,"]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:68,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:69,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:71,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai."]]},{v:72,p:1,l:[[0,"On the eleventh day Pagiel the son of Ochran, prince of the children of Asher,"]]},{v:73,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:74,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:75,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:76,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:77,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Pagiel the son of Ochran."]]},{v:78,p:1,l:[[0,"On the twelfth day Ahira the son of Enan, prince of the children of Naphtali,"]]},{v:79,l:[[0,"gave his offering:"],[0,"one silver platter, the weight of which was one hundred thirty shekels,"],[0,"one silver bowl of seventy shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, both of them full of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering;"]]},{v:80,p:1,l:[[0,"one golden ladle of ten shekels, full of incense;"]]},{v:81,p:1,l:[[0,"one young bull,"],[0,"one ram,"],[0,"one male lamb a year old, for a burnt offering;"]]},{v:82,p:1,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering;"]]},{v:83,p:1,l:[[0,"and for the sacrifice of peace offerings, two head of cattle, five rams, five male goats, and five male lambs a year old. This was the offering of Ahira the son of Enan."]]},{v:84,p:1,l:[[0,"This was the dedication offering of the altar, on the day when it was anointed, by the princes of Israel: twelve silver platters, twelve silver bowls, twelve golden ladles;"]]},{v:85,l:[[0,"each silver platter weighing one hundred thirty shekels, and each bowl seventy; all the silver of the vessels two thousand four hundred shekels, according to the shekel of the sanctuary;"]]},{v:86,l:[[0,"the twelve golden ladles, full of incense, weighing ten shekels apiece, according to the shekel of the sanctuary; all the gold of the ladles weighed one hundred twenty shekels;"]]},{v:87,l:[[0,"all the cattle for the burnt offering twelve bulls, the rams twelve, the male lambs a year old twelve, and their meal offering; and twelve male goats for a sin offering;"]]},{v:88,l:[[0,"and all the cattle for the sacrifice of peace offerings: twenty-four bulls, sixty rams, sixty male goats, and sixty male lambs a year old. This was the dedication offering of the altar, after it was anointed."]]},{v:89,p:1,l:[[0,"When Moses went into the Tent of Meeting to speak with the LORD, he heard his voice speaking to him from above the mercy seat that was on the ark of the Testimony, from between the two cherubim; and he spoke to him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Aaron, and tell him, \u2018When you light the lamps, the seven lamps shall give light in front of the lamp stand.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Aaron did so. He lit its lamps to light the area in front of the lamp stand, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"This was the workmanship of the lamp stand, beaten work of gold. From its base to its flowers, it was beaten work. He made the lamp stand according to the pattern which the LORD had shown Moses."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cTake the Levites from among the children of Israel, and cleanse them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall do this to them to cleanse them: sprinkle the water of cleansing on them, let them shave their whole bodies with a razor, let them wash their clothes, and cleanse themselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then let them take a young bull and its meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil; and another young bull you shall take for a sin offering."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall present the Levites before the Tent of Meeting. You shall assemble the whole congregation of the children of Israel."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall present the Levites before the LORD. The children of Israel shall lay their hands on the Levites,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and Aaron shall offer the Levites before the LORD for a wave offering on the behalf of the children of Israel, that it may be theirs to do the service of the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Levites shall lay their hands on the heads of the bulls, and you shall offer the one for a sin offering and the other for a burnt offering to the LORD, to make atonement for the Levites."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall set the Levites before Aaron and before his sons, and offer them as a wave offering to the LORD."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Thus you shall separate the Levites from among the children of Israel, and the Levites shall be mine."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAfter that, the Levites shall go in to do the service of the Tent of Meeting. You shall cleanse them, and offer them as a wave offering."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For they are wholly given to me from among the children of Israel; instead of all who open the womb, even the firstborn of all the children of Israel, I have taken them to me."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For all the firstborn among the children of Israel are mine, both man and animal. On the day that I struck all the firstborn in the land of Egypt, I sanctified them for myself."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I have taken the Levites instead of all the firstborn among the children of Israel."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I have given the Levites as a gift to Aaron and to his sons from among the children of Israel, to do the service of the children of Israel in the Tent of Meeting, and to make atonement for the children of Israel, so that there will be no plague among the children of Israel when the children of Israel come near to the sanctuary.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses, and Aaron, and all the congregation of the children of Israel did so to the Levites. According to all that the LORD commanded Moses concerning the Levites, so the children of Israel did to them."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The Levites purified themselves from sin, and they washed their clothes; and Aaron offered them for a wave offering before the LORD and Aaron made atonement for them to cleanse them."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"After that, the Levites went in to do their service in the Tent of Meeting before Aaron and before his sons: as the LORD had commanded Moses concerning the Levites, so they did to them."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is what is assigned to the Levites: from twenty-five years old and upward they shall go in to wait on the service in the work of the Tent of Meeting;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and from the age of fifty years they shall retire from doing the work, and shall serve no more,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"but shall assist their brothers in the Tent of Meeting, to perform the duty, and shall perform no service. This is how you shall have the Levites do their duties.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai, in the first month of the second year after they had come out of the land of Egypt, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cLet the children of Israel keep the Passover in its appointed season."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"On the fourteenth day of this month, at evening, you shall keep it in its appointed season. You shall keep it according to all its statutes and according to all its ordinances.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses told the children of Israel that they should keep the Passover."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They kept the Passover in the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month at evening, in the wilderness of Sinai. According to all that the LORD commanded Moses, so the children of Israel did."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"There were certain men who were unclean because of the dead body of a man, so that they could not keep the Passover on that day, and they came before Moses and Aaron on that day."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Those men said to him, \u201cWe are unclean because of the dead body of a man. Why are we kept back, that we may not offer the offering of the LORD in its appointed season among the children of Israel?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses answered them, \u201cWait, that I may hear what the LORD will command concerning you.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cSay to the children of Israel, \u2018If any man of you or of your generations is unclean by reason of a dead body, or is on a journey far away, he shall still keep the Passover to the LORD."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In the second month, on the fourteenth day at evening they shall keep it; they shall eat it with unleavened bread and bitter herbs."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They shall leave none of it until the morning, nor break a bone of it. According to all the statute of the Passover they shall keep it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But the man who is clean, and is not on a journey, and fails to keep the Passover, that soul shall be cut off from his people. Because he didn\u2019t offer the offering of the LORD in its appointed season, that man shall bear his sin."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a foreigner lives among you and desires to keep the Passover to the LORD, then he shall do so according to the statute of the Passover, and according to its ordinance. You shall have one statute, both for the foreigner and for him who is born in the land.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"On the day that the tabernacle was raised up, the cloud covered the tabernacle, even the Tent of the Testimony. At evening it was over the tabernacle, as it were the appearance of fire, until morning."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So it was continually. The cloud covered it, and the appearance of fire by night."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Whenever the cloud was taken up from over the Tent, then after that the children of Israel traveled; and in the place where the cloud remained, there the children of Israel encamped."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"At the commandment of the LORD, the children of Israel traveled, and at the commandment of the LORD they encamped. As long as the cloud remained on the tabernacle they remained encamped."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When the cloud stayed on the tabernacle many days, then the children of Israel kept the LORD\u2019s command, and didn\u2019t travel."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Sometimes the cloud was a few days on the tabernacle; then according to the commandment of the LORD they remained encamped, and according to the commandment of the LORD they traveled."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Sometimes the cloud was from evening until morning; and when the cloud was taken up in the morning, they traveled; or by day and by night, when the cloud was taken up, they traveled."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Whether it was two days, or a month, or a year that the cloud stayed on the tabernacle, remaining on it, the children of Israel remained encamped, and didn\u2019t travel; but when it was taken up, they traveled."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"At the commandment of the LORD they encamped, and at the commandment of the LORD they traveled. They kept the LORD\u2019s command, at the commandment of the LORD by Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cMake two trumpets of silver. You shall make them of beaten work. You shall use them for the calling of the congregation and for the journeying of the camps."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When they blow them, all the congregation shall gather themselves to you at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If they blow just one, then the princes, the heads of the thousands of Israel, shall gather themselves to you."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When you blow an alarm, the camps that lie on the east side shall go forward."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When you blow an alarm the second time, the camps that lie on the south side shall go forward. They shall blow an alarm for their journeys."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But when the assembly is to be gathered together, you shall blow, but you shall not sound an alarm."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe sons of Aaron, the priests, shall blow the trumpets. This shall be to you for a statute forever throughout your generations."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When you go to war in your land against the adversary who oppresses you, then you shall sound an alarm with the trumpets. Then you will be remembered before the LORD your God, and you will be saved from your enemies."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAlso in the day of your gladness, and in your set feasts, and in the beginnings of your months, you shall blow the trumpets over your burnt offerings, and over the sacrifices of your peace offerings; and they shall be to you for a memorial before your God. I am the LORD your God.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"In the second year, in the second month, on the twentieth day of the month, the cloud was taken up from over the tabernacle of the covenant."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The children of Israel went forward on their journeys out of the wilderness of Sinai; and the cloud stayed in the wilderness of Paran."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They first went forward according to the commandment of the LORD by Moses."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"First, the standard of the camp of the children of Judah went forward according to their armies. Nahshon the son of Amminadab was over his army."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Nethanel the son of Zuar was over the army of the tribe of the children of Issachar."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Eliab the son of Helon was over the army of the tribe of the children of Zebulun."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The tabernacle was taken down; and the sons of Gershon and the sons of Merari, who bore the tabernacle, went forward."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The standard of the camp of Reuben went forward according to their armies. Elizur the son of Shedeur was over his army."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Shelumiel the son of Zurishaddai was over the army of the tribe of the children of Simeon."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Eliasaph the son of Deuel was over the army of the tribe of the children of Gad."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The Kohathites set forward, bearing the sanctuary. The others set up the tabernacle before they arrived."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The standard of the camp of the children of Ephraim set forward according to their armies. Elishama the son of Ammihud was over his army."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur was over the army of the tribe of the children of Manasseh."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Abidan the son of Gideoni was over the army of the tribe of the children of Benjamin."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The standard of the camp of the children of Dan, which was the rear guard of all the camps, set forward according to their armies. Ahiezer the son of Ammishaddai was over his army."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Pagiel the son of Ochran was over the army of the tribe of the children of Asher."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Ahira the son of Enan was over the army of the tribe of the children of Naphtali."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Thus were the travels of the children of Israel according to their armies; and they went forward."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Hobab, the son of Reuel the Midianite, Moses\u2019 father-in-law, \u201cWe are journeying to the place of which the LORD said, \u2018I will give it to you.\u2019 Come with us, and we will treat you well; for the LORD has spoken good concerning Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cI will not go; but I will depart to my own land, and to my relatives.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cDon\u2019t leave us, please; because you know how we are to encamp in the wilderness, and you can be our eyes."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"It shall be, if you go with us\u2014yes, it shall be\u2014that whatever good the LORD does to us, we will do the same to you.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"They set forward from the Mount of the LORD three days\u2019 journey. The ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant went before them three days\u2019 journey, to seek out a resting place for them."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The cloud of the LORD was over them by day, when they set forward from the camp."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"When the ark went forward, Moses said, \u201cRise up, LORD, and let your enemies be scattered! Let those who hate you flee before you!\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"When it rested, he said, \u201cReturn, LORD, to the ten thousands of the thousands of Israel.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The people were complaining in the ears of the LORD. When the LORD heard it, his anger burned; and the LORD\u2019s fire burned among them, and consumed some of the outskirts of the camp."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The people cried to Moses; and Moses prayed to the LORD, and the fire abated."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The name of that place was called Taberah, because the LORD\u2019s fire burned among them."]],f:["Taberah means \u201cburning\u201d"]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The mixed multitude that was among them lusted exceedingly; and the children of Israel also wept again, and said, \u201cWho will give us meat to eat?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"We remember the fish, which we ate in Egypt for nothing; the cucumbers, and the melons, and the leeks, and the onions, and the garlic;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but now we have lost our appetite. There is nothing at all except this manna to look at.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The manna was like coriander seed, and it looked like bdellium."]],f:["Bdellium is a resin extracted from certain African trees."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The people went around, gathered it, and ground it in mills, or beat it in mortars, and boiled it in pots, and made cakes of it. Its taste was like the taste of fresh oil."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When the dew fell on the camp in the night, the manna fell on it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses heard the people weeping throughout their families, every man at the door of his tent; and the LORD\u2019s anger burned greatly; and Moses was displeased."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Moses said to the LORD, \u201cWhy have you treated your servant so badly? Why haven\u2019t I found favor in your sight, that you lay the burden of all this people on me?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Have I conceived all this people? Have I brought them out, that you should tell me, \u2018Carry them in your bosom, as a nurse carries a nursing infant, to the land which you swore to their fathers\u2019?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Where could I get meat to give all these people? For they weep before me, saying, \u2018Give us meat, that we may eat.\u2019"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I am not able to bear all this people alone, because it is too heavy for me."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If you treat me this way, please kill me right now, if I have found favor in your sight; and don\u2019t let me see my wretchedness.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cGather to me seventy men of the elders of Israel, whom you know to be the elders of the people and officers over them; and bring them to the Tent of Meeting, that they may stand there with you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I will come down and talk with you there. I will take of the Spirit which is on you, and will put it on them; and they shall bear the burden of the people with you, that you don\u2019t bear it yourself alone."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSay to the people, \u2018Sanctify yourselves in preparation for tomorrow, and you will eat meat; for you have wept in the ears of the LORD, saying, \u201cWho will give us meat to eat? For it was well with us in Egypt.\u201d Therefore the LORD will give you meat, and you will eat."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You will not eat just one day, or two days, or five days, or ten days, or twenty days,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but a whole month, until it comes out at your nostrils, and it is loathsome to you; because you have rejected the LORD who is among you, and have wept before him, saying, \u201cWhy did we come out of Egypt?\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cThe people, among whom I am, are six hundred thousand men on foot; and you have said, \u2018I will give them meat, that they may eat a whole month.\u2019"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Shall flocks and herds be slaughtered for them, to be sufficient for them? Shall all the fish of the sea be gathered together for them, to be sufficient for them?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cHas the LORD\u2019s hand grown short? Now you will see whether my word will happen to you or not.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went out, and told the people the LORD\u2019s words; and he gathered seventy men of the elders of the people, and set them around the Tent."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The LORD came down in the cloud, and spoke to him, and took of the Spirit that was on him, and put it on the seventy elders. When the Spirit rested on them, they prophesied, but they did so no more."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But two men remained in the camp. The name of one was Eldad, and the name of the other Medad; and the Spirit rested on them. They were of those who were written, but had not gone out to the Tent; and they prophesied in the camp."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"A young man ran, and told Moses, and said, \u201cEldad and Medad are prophesying in the camp!\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua the son of Nun, the servant of Moses, one of his chosen men, answered, \u201cMy lord Moses, forbid them!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to him, \u201cAre you jealous for my sake? I wish that all the LORD\u2019s people were prophets, that the LORD would put his Spirit on them!\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went into the camp, he and the elders of Israel."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"A wind from the LORD went out and brought quails from the sea, and let them fall by the camp, about a day\u2019s journey on this side, and a day\u2019s journey on the other side, around the camp, and about two cubits above the surface of the earth."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The people rose up all that day, and all of that night, and all the next day, and gathered the quails. He who gathered least gathered ten homers; and they spread them all out for themselves around the camp."]],f:["1 homer is about 220 liters or 6 bushels"]},{v:33,l:[[0,"While the meat was still between their teeth, before it was chewed, the LORD\u2019s anger burned against the people, and the LORD struck the people with a very great plague."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The name of that place was called Kibroth Hattaavah, because there they buried the people who lusted."]],f:["Kibroth Hattaavah means \u201cgraves of lust\u201d"]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"From Kibroth Hattaavah the people traveled to Hazeroth; and they stayed at Hazeroth."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Miriam and Aaron spoke against Moses because of the Cushite woman whom he had married; for he had married a Cushite woman."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cHas the LORD indeed spoken only with Moses? Hasn\u2019t he spoken also with us?\u201d And the LORD heard it."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the man Moses was very humble, more than all the men who were on the surface of the earth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke suddenly to Moses, to Aaron, and to Miriam, \u201cYou three come out to the Tent of Meeting!\u201d"],[0,"The three of them came out."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD came down in a pillar of cloud, and stood at the door of the Tent, and called Aaron and Miriam; and they both came forward."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cNow hear my words. If there is a prophet among you, I, the LORD, will make myself known to him in a vision. I will speak with him in a dream."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"My servant Moses is not so. He is faithful in all my house."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"With him, I will speak mouth to mouth, even plainly, and not in riddles; and he shall see the LORD\u2019s form. Why then were you not afraid to speak against my servant, against Moses?\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against them; and he departed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The cloud departed from over the Tent; and behold, Miriam was leprous, as white as snow. Aaron looked at Miriam, and behold, she was leprous."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Aaron said to Moses, \u201cOh, my lord, please don\u2019t count this sin against us, in which we have done foolishly, and in which we have sinned."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Let her not, I pray, be as one dead, of whom the flesh is half consumed when he comes out of his mother\u2019s womb.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses cried to the LORD, saying, \u201cHeal her, God, I beg you!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cIf her father had but spit in her face, shouldn\u2019t she be ashamed seven days? Let her be shut up outside of the camp seven days, and after that she shall be brought in again.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Miriam was shut up outside of the camp seven days, and the people didn\u2019t travel until Miriam was brought in again."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Afterward the people traveled from Hazeroth, and encamped in the wilderness of Paran."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSend men, that they may spy out the land of Canaan, which I give to the children of Israel. Of every tribe of their fathers, you shall send a man, every one a prince among them.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses sent them from the wilderness of Paran according to the commandment of the LORD. All of them were men who were heads of the children of Israel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"These were their names:"],[0,"Of the tribe of Reuben, Shammua the son of Zaccur."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Simeon, Shaphat the son of Hori."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Judah, Caleb the son of Jephunneh."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Issachar, Igal the son of Joseph."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Ephraim, Hoshea the son of Nun."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Benjamin, Palti the son of Raphu."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Zebulun, Gaddiel the son of Sodi."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Joseph, of the tribe of Manasseh, Gaddi the son of Susi."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Dan, Ammiel the son of Gemalli."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Asher, Sethur the son of Michael."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Naphtali, Nahbi the son of Vophsi."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Gad, Geuel the son of Machi."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the names of the men who Moses sent to spy out the land. Moses called Hoshea the son of Nun Joshua."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Moses sent them to spy out the land of Canaan, and said to them, \u201cGo up this way by the South, and go up into the hill country."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"See the land, what it is; and the people who dwell therein, whether they are strong or weak, whether they are few or many;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and what the land is that they dwell in, whether it is good or bad; and what cities they are that they dwell in, whether in camps, or in strongholds;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and what the land is, whether it is fertile or poor, whether there is wood therein, or not. Be courageous, and bring some of the fruit of the land.\u201d Now the time was the time of the first-ripe grapes."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"So they went up, and spied out the land from the wilderness of Zin to Rehob, to the entrance of Hamath."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They went up by the South, and came to Hebron; and Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai, the children of Anak, were there. (Now Hebron was built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.)"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They came to the valley of Eshcol, and cut down from there a branch with one cluster of grapes, and they bore it on a staff between two. They also brought some of the pomegranates and figs."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"That place was called the valley of Eshcol, because of the cluster which the children of Israel cut down from there."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They returned from spying out the land at the end of forty days."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They went and came to Moses, to Aaron, and to all the congregation of the children of Israel, to the wilderness of Paran, to Kadesh; and brought back word to them and to all the congregation. They showed them the fruit of the land."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They told him, and said, \u201cWe came to the land where you sent us. Surely it flows with milk and honey, and this is its fruit."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"However, the people who dwell in the land are strong, and the cities are fortified and very large. Moreover, we saw the children of Anak there."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Amalek dwells in the land of the South. The Hittite, the Jebusite, and the Amorite dwell in the hill country. The Canaanite dwells by the sea, and along the side of the Jordan.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Caleb stilled the people before Moses, and said, \u201cLet\u2019s go up at once, and possess it; for we are well able to overcome it!\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"But the men who went up with him said, \u201cWe aren\u2019t able to go up against the people; for they are stronger than we.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They brought up an evil report of the land which they had spied out to the children of Israel, saying, \u201cThe land, through which we have gone to spy it out, is a land that eats up its inhabitants; and all the people who we saw in it are men of great stature."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"There we saw the Nephilim, the sons of Anak, who come from the Nephilim. We were in our own sight as grasshoppers, and so we were in their sight.\u201d"]],f:["or, giants","or, giants"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"All the congregation lifted up their voice, and cried; and the people wept that night."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"All the children of Israel murmured against Moses and against Aaron. The whole congregation said to them, \u201cWe wish that we had died in the land of Egypt, or that we had died in this wilderness!"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Why does the LORD bring us to this land, to fall by the sword? Our wives and our little ones will be captured or killed! Wouldn\u2019t it be better for us to return into Egypt?\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They said to one another, \u201cLet\u2019s choose a leader, and let\u2019s return into Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Moses and Aaron fell on their faces before all the assembly of the congregation of the children of Israel."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua the son of Nun and Caleb the son of Jephunneh, who were of those who spied out the land, tore their clothes."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They spoke to all the congregation of the children of Israel, saying, \u201cThe land, which we passed through to spy it out, is an exceedingly good land."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If the LORD delights in us, then he will bring us into this land, and give it to us: a land which flows with milk and honey."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Only don\u2019t rebel against the LORD, neither fear the people of the land; for they are bread for us. Their defense is removed from over them, and the LORD is with us. Don\u2019t fear them.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But all the congregation threatened to stone them with stones."],[0,"The LORD\u2019s glory appeared in the Tent of Meeting to all the children of Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cHow long will this people despise me? How long will they not believe in me, for all the signs which I have worked among them?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I will strike them with the pestilence, and disinherit them, and will make of you a nation greater and mightier than they.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the LORD, \u201cThen the Egyptians will hear it; for you brought up this people in your might from among them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They will tell it to the inhabitants of this land. They have heard that you LORD are among this people; for you LORD are seen face to face, and your cloud stands over them, and you go before them, in a pillar of cloud by day, and in a pillar of fire by night."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now if you killed this people as one man, then the nations which have heard the fame of you will speak, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u2018Because the LORD was not able to bring this people into the land which he swore to them, therefore he has slain them in the wilderness.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now please let the power of the Lord be great, according as you have spoken, saying,"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u2018The LORD is slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness, forgiving iniquity and disobedience; and he will by no means clear the guilty, visiting the iniquity of the fathers on the children, on the third and on the fourth generation.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Please pardon the iniquity of this people according to the greatness of your loving kindness, and just as you have forgiven this people, from Egypt even until now.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cI have pardoned according to your word;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"but in very deed\u2014as I live, and as all the earth shall be filled with the LORD\u2019s glory\u2014"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"because all those men who have seen my glory and my signs, which I worked in Egypt and in the wilderness, yet have tempted me these ten times, and have not listened to my voice;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"surely they shall not see the land which I swore to their fathers, neither shall any of those who despised me see it."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But my servant Caleb, because he had another spirit with him, and has followed me fully, him I will bring into the land into which he went. His offspring shall possess it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Since the Amalekite and the Canaanite dwell in the valley, tomorrow turn and go into the wilderness by the way to the Red Sea.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"\u201cHow long shall I bear with this evil congregation that complain against me? I have heard the complaints of the children of Israel, which they complain against me."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Tell them, \u2018As I live, says the LORD, surely as you have spoken in my ears, so I will do to you."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Your dead bodies shall fall in this wilderness; and all who were counted of you, according to your whole number, from twenty years old and upward, who have complained against me,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"surely you shall not come into the land concerning which I swore that I would make you dwell therein, except Caleb the son of Jephunneh, and Joshua the son of Nun."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But I will bring in your little ones that you said should be captured or killed, and they shall know the land which you have rejected."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"But as for you, your dead bodies shall fall in this wilderness."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Your children shall be wanderers in the wilderness forty years, and shall bear your prostitution, until your dead bodies are consumed in the wilderness."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"After the number of the days in which you spied out the land, even forty days, for every day a year, you will bear your iniquities, even forty years, and you will know my alienation.\u2019"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"I, the LORD, have spoken. I will surely do this to all this evil congregation who are gathered together against me. In this wilderness they shall be consumed, and there they shall die.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The men whom Moses sent to spy out the land, who returned and made all the congregation to murmur against him by bringing up an evil report against the land,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"even those men who brought up an evil report of the land, died by the plague before the LORD."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But Joshua the son of Nun and Caleb the son of Jephunneh remained alive of those men who went to spy out the land."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses told these words to all the children of Israel, and the people mourned greatly."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"They rose up early in the morning and went up to the top of the mountain, saying, \u201cBehold, we are here, and will go up to the place which the LORD has promised; for we have sinned.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cWhy now do you disobey the commandment of the LORD, since it shall not prosper?"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t go up, for the LORD isn\u2019t among you; that way you won\u2019t be struck down before your enemies."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"For there the Amalekite and the Canaanite are before you, and you will fall by the sword because you turned back from following the LORD; therefore the LORD will not be with you.\u201d"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"But they presumed to go up to the top of the mountain. Nevertheless, the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant and Moses didn\u2019t depart out of the camp."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Then the Amalekites came down, and the Canaanites who lived in that mountain, and struck them and beat them down even to Hormah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When you have come into the land of your habitations, which I give to you,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and will make an offering by fire to the LORD\u2014a burnt offering, or a sacrifice, to accomplish a vow, or as a free will offering, or in your set feasts, to make a pleasant aroma to the LORD, of the herd, or of the flock\u2014"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"then he who offers his offering shall offer to the LORD a meal offering of one tenth of an ephah of fine flour mixed with one fourth of a hin of oil."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall prepare wine for the drink offering, one fourth of a hin, with the burnt offering or for the sacrifice, for each lamb."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018For a ram, you shall prepare for a meal offering two tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with the third part of a hin of oil;"]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and for the drink offering you shall offer the third part of a hin of wine, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When you prepare a bull for a burnt offering or for a sacrifice, to accomplish a vow, or for peace offerings to the LORD,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"then he shall offer with the bull a meal offering of three tenths of an ephah of fine flour mixed with half a hin of oil;"]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and you shall offer for the drink offering half a hin of wine, for an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Thus it shall be done for each bull, for each ram, for each of the male lambs, or of the young goats."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"According to the number that you shall prepare, so you shall do to everyone according to their number."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018All who are native-born shall do these things in this way, in offering an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If a stranger lives as a foreigner with you, or whoever may be among you throughout your generations, and will offer an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD, as you do, so he shall do."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For the assembly, there shall be one statute for you and for the stranger who lives as a foreigner, a statute forever throughout your generations. As you are, so the foreigner shall be before the LORD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"One law and one ordinance shall be for you and for the stranger who lives as a foreigner with you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When you come into the land where I bring you,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"then it shall be that when you eat of the bread of the land, you shall offer up a wave offering to the LORD."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Of the first of your dough you shall offer up a cake for a wave offering. As the wave offering of the threshing floor, so you shall heave it."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Of the first of your dough, you shall give to the LORD a wave offering throughout your generations."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018When you err, and don\u2019t observe all these commandments which the LORD has spoken to Moses\u2014"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"even all that the LORD has commanded you by Moses, from the day that the LORD gave commandment and onward throughout your generations\u2014"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"then it shall be, if it was done unwittingly, without the knowledge of the congregation, that all the congregation shall offer one young bull for a burnt offering, for a pleasant aroma to the LORD, with its meal offering and its drink offering, according to the ordinance, and one male goat for a sin offering."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The priest shall make atonement for all the congregation of the children of Israel, and they shall be forgiven; for it was an error, and they have brought their offering, an offering made by fire to the LORD, and their sin offering before the LORD, for their error."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"All the congregation of the children of Israel shall be forgiven, as well as the stranger who lives as a foreigner among them; for with regard to all the people, it was done unwittingly."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018If a person sins unwittingly, then he shall offer a female goat a year old for a sin offering."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The priest shall make atonement for the soul who errs when he sins unwittingly before the LORD. He shall make atonement for him; and he shall be forgiven."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You shall have one law for him who does anything unwittingly, for him who is native-born among the children of Israel, and for the stranger who lives as a foreigner among them."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But the soul who does anything with a high hand, whether he is native-born or a foreigner, blasphemes the LORD. That soul shall be cut off from among his people."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Because he has despised the LORD\u2019s word, and has broken his commandment, that soul shall be utterly cut off. His iniquity shall be on him.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"While the children of Israel were in the wilderness, they found a man gathering sticks on the Sabbath day."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Those who found him gathering sticks brought him to Moses and Aaron, and to all the congregation."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"They put him in custody, because it had not been declared what should be done to him."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cThe man shall surely be put to death. All the congregation shall stone him with stones outside of the camp.\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"All the congregation brought him outside of the camp, and stoned him to death with stones, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them that they should make themselves fringes on the borders of their garments throughout their generations, and that they put on the fringe of each border a cord of blue."]],f:["or, tassels (Hebrew \u05e6\u05b4\u05d9\u05e6\u05b4\u059b\u05ea)","or, tassel"]},{v:39,l:[[0,"It shall be to you for a fringe, that you may see it, and remember all the LORD\u2019s commandments, and do them; and that you don\u2019t follow your own heart and your own eyes, after which you used to play the prostitute;"]],f:["or, tassel"]},{v:40,l:[[0,"so that you may remember and do all my commandments, and be holy to your God."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"I am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, to be your God: I am the LORD your God.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Korah, the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, with Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, and On, the son of Peleth, sons of Reuben, took some men."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They rose up before Moses, with some of the children of Israel, two hundred fifty princes of the congregation, called to the assembly, men of renown."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They assembled themselves together against Moses and against Aaron, and said to them, \u201cYou take too much on yourself, since all the congregation are holy, everyone of them, and the LORD is among them! Why do you lift yourselves up above the LORD\u2019s assembly?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When Moses heard it, he fell on his face."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He said to Korah and to all his company, \u201cIn the morning, the LORD will show who are his, and who is holy, and will cause him to come near to him. Even him whom he shall choose, he will cause to come near to him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Do this: have Korah and all his company take censers,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"put fire in them, and put incense on them before the LORD tomorrow. It shall be that the man whom the LORD chooses, he shall be holy. You have gone too far, you sons of Levi!\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Korah, \u201cHear now, you sons of Levi!"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Is it a small thing to you that the God of Israel has separated you from the congregation of Israel, to bring you near to himself, to do the service of the LORD\u2019s tabernacle, and to stand before the congregation to minister to them;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and that he has brought you near, and all your brothers the sons of Levi with you? Do you seek the priesthood also?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore you and all your company have gathered together against the LORD! What is Aaron that you complain against him?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses sent to call Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab; and they said, \u201cWe won\u2019t come up!"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Is it a small thing that you have brought us up out of a land flowing with milk and honey, to kill us in the wilderness, but you must also make yourself a prince over us?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Moreover you haven\u2019t brought us into a land flowing with milk and honey, nor given us inheritance of fields and vineyards. Will you put out the eyes of these men? We won\u2019t come up.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses was very angry, and said to the LORD, \u201cDon\u2019t respect their offering. I have not taken one donkey from them, neither have I hurt one of them.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Korah, \u201cYou and all your company go before the LORD, you, and they, and Aaron, tomorrow."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Each man take his censer and put incense on it, and each man bring before the LORD his censer, two hundred fifty censers; you also, and Aaron, each with his censer.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"They each took his censer, and put fire in it, and laid incense on it, and stood at the door of the Tent of Meeting with Moses and Aaron."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Korah assembled all the congregation opposite them to the door of the Tent of Meeting."],[0,"The LORD\u2019s glory appeared to all the congregation."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cSeparate yourselves from among this congregation, that I may consume them in a moment!\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"They fell on their faces, and said, \u201cGod, the God of the spirits of all flesh, shall one man sin, and will you be angry with all the congregation?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the congregation, saying, \u2018Get away from around the tent of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses rose up and went to Dathan and Abiram; and the elders of Israel followed him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He spoke to the congregation, saying, \u201cDepart, please, from the tents of these wicked men, and touch nothing of theirs, lest you be consumed in all their sins!\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"So they went away from the tent of Korah, Dathan, and Abiram, on every side. Dathan and Abiram came out, and stood at the door of their tents with their wives, their sons, and their little ones."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said, \u201cHereby you shall know that the LORD has sent me to do all these works; for they are not from my own mind."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"If these men die the common death of all men, or if they experience what all men experience, then the LORD hasn\u2019t sent me."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But if the LORD makes a new thing, and the ground opens its mouth, and swallows them up with all that belong to them, and they go down alive into Sheol, then you shall understand that these men have despised the LORD.\u201d"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"As he finished speaking all these words, the ground that was under them split apart."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The earth opened its mouth and swallowed them up with their households, all of Korah\u2019s men, and all their goods."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"So they, and all that belonged to them went down alive into Sheol. The earth closed on them, and they perished from among the assembly."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:34,l:[[0,"All Israel that were around them fled at their cry; for they said, \u201cLest the earth swallow us up!\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Fire came out from the LORD, and devoured the two hundred fifty men who offered the incense."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, that he take up the censers out of the burning, and scatter the fire away from the camp; for they are holy,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"even the censers of those who sinned against their own lives. Let them be beaten into plates for a covering of the altar, for they offered them before the LORD. Therefore they are holy. They shall be a sign to the children of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Eleazar the priest took the bronze censers which those who were burned had offered; and they beat them out for a covering of the altar,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"to be a memorial to the children of Israel, to the end that no stranger who isn\u2019t of the offspring of Aaron, would come near to burn incense before the LORD, that he not be as Korah and as his company; as the LORD spoke to him by Moses."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"But on the next day all the congregation of the children of Israel complained against Moses and against Aaron, saying, \u201cYou have killed the LORD\u2019s people!\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"When the congregation was assembled against Moses and against Aaron, they looked toward the Tent of Meeting. Behold, the cloud covered it, and the LORD\u2019s glory appeared."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron came to the front of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"\u201cGet away from among this congregation, that I may consume them in a moment!\u201d They fell on their faces."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to Aaron, \u201cTake your censer, put fire from the altar in it, lay incense on it, carry it quickly to the congregation, and make atonement for them; for wrath has gone out from the LORD! The plague has begun.\u201d"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"Aaron did as Moses said, and ran into the middle of the assembly. The plague had already begun among the people. He put on the incense, and made atonement for the people."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He stood between the dead and the living; and the plague was stayed."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Now those who died by the plague were fourteen thousand seven hundred, in addition to those who died about the matter of Korah."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Aaron returned to Moses to the door of the Tent of Meeting, and the plague was stopped."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and take rods from them, one for each fathers\u2019 house, of all their princes according to their fathers\u2019 houses, twelve rods. Write each man\u2019s name on his rod."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall write Aaron\u2019s name on Levi\u2019s rod. There shall be one rod for each head of their fathers\u2019 houses."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall lay them up in the Tent of Meeting before the covenant, where I meet with you."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It shall happen that the rod of the man whom I shall choose shall bud. I will make the murmurings of the children of Israel, which they murmur against you, cease from me.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke to the children of Israel; and all their princes gave him rods, for each prince one, according to their fathers\u2019 houses, a total of twelve rods. Aaron\u2019s rod was among their rods."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Moses laid up the rods before the LORD in the Tent of the Testimony."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, Moses went into the Tent of the Testimony; and behold, Aaron\u2019s rod for the house of Levi had sprouted, budded, produced blossoms, and bore ripe almonds."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moses brought out all the rods from before the LORD to all the children of Israel. They looked, and each man took his rod."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cPut back the rod of Aaron before the covenant, to be kept for a token against the children of rebellion; that you may make an end of their complaining against me, that they not die.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Moses did so. As the LORD commanded him, so he did."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel spoke to Moses, saying, \u201cBehold, we perish! We are undone! We are all undone!"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Everyone who keeps approaching the LORD\u2019s tabernacle, dies! Will we all perish?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Aaron, \u201cYou and your sons and your fathers\u2019 house with you shall bear the iniquity of the sanctuary; and you and your sons with you shall bear the iniquity of your priesthood."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Bring your brothers also, the tribe of Levi, the tribe of your father, near with you, that they may be joined to you, and minister to you; but you and your sons with you shall be before the Tent of the Testimony."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They shall keep your commands and the duty of the whole Tent; only they shall not come near to the vessels of the sanctuary and to the altar, that they not die, neither they nor you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They shall be joined to you and keep the responsibility of the Tent of Meeting, for all the service of the Tent. A stranger shall not come near to you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall perform the duty of the sanctuary and the duty of the altar, that there be no more wrath on the children of Israel."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Behold, I myself have taken your brothers the Levites from among the children of Israel. They are a gift to you, dedicated to the LORD, to do the service of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You and your sons with you shall keep your priesthood for everything of the altar, and for that within the veil. You shall serve. I give you the service of the priesthood as a gift. The stranger who comes near shall be put to death.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Aaron, \u201cBehold, I myself have given you the command of my wave offerings, even all the holy things of the children of Israel. I have given them to you by reason of the anointing, and to your sons, as a portion forever."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"This shall be yours of the most holy things from the fire: every offering of theirs, even every meal offering of theirs, and every sin offering of theirs, and every trespass offering of theirs, which they shall give to me, shall be most holy for you and for your sons."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall eat of it like the most holy things. Every male shall eat of it. It shall be holy to you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is yours, too: the wave offering of their gift, even all the wave offerings of the children of Israel. I have given them to you, and to your sons and to your daughters with you, as a portion forever. Everyone who is clean in your house shall eat of it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI have given to you all the best of the oil, all the best of the vintage, and of the grain, the first fruits of them which they give to the LORD."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The first-ripe fruits of all that is in their land, which they bring to the LORD, shall be yours. Everyone who is clean in your house shall eat of it."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cEverything devoted in Israel shall be yours."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Everything that opens the womb, of all flesh which they offer to the LORD, both of man and animal, shall be yours. Nevertheless, you shall surely redeem the firstborn of man, and you shall redeem the firstborn of unclean animals."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall redeem those who are to be redeemed of them from a month old, according to your estimation, for five shekels of money, according to the shekel of the sanctuary, which weighs twenty gerahs."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces.","A gerah is about 0.5 grams or about 7.7 grains."]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut you shall not redeem the firstborn of a cow, or the firstborn of a sheep, or the firstborn of a goat. They are holy. You shall sprinkle their blood on the altar, and shall burn their fat for an offering made by fire, for a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Their meat shall be yours, as the wave offering breast and as the right thigh, it shall be yours."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"All the wave offerings of the holy things which the children of Israel offer to the LORD, I have given you and your sons and your daughters with you, as a portion forever. It is a covenant of salt forever before the LORD to you and to your offspring with you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Aaron, \u201cYou shall have no inheritance in their land, neither shall you have any portion among them. I am your portion and your inheritance among the children of Israel."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo the children of Levi, behold, I have given all the tithe in Israel for an inheritance, in return for their service which they serve, even the service of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Henceforth the children of Israel shall not come near the Tent of Meeting, lest they bear sin, and die."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But the Levites shall do the service of the Tent of Meeting, and they shall bear their iniquity. It shall be a statute forever throughout your generations. Among the children of Israel, they shall have no inheritance."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For the tithe of the children of Israel, which they offer as a wave offering to the LORD, I have given to the Levites for an inheritance. Therefore I have said to them, \u2018Among the children of Israel they shall have no inheritance.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover you shall speak to the Levites, and tell them, \u2018When you take of the children of Israel the tithe which I have given you from them for your inheritance, then you shall offer up a wave offering of it for the LORD, a tithe of the tithe."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Your wave offering shall be credited to you, as though it were the grain of the threshing floor, and as the fullness of the wine press."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Thus you also shall offer a wave offering to the LORD of all your tithes, which you receive of the children of Israel; and of it you shall give the LORD\u2019s wave offering to Aaron the priest."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Out of all your gifts, you shall offer every wave offering to the LORD, of all its best parts, even the holy part of it.\u2019"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore you shall tell them, \u2018When you heave its best from it, then it shall be credited to the Levites as the increase of the threshing floor, and as the increase of the wine press."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"You may eat it anywhere, you and your households, for it is your reward in return for your service in the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"You shall bear no sin by reason of it, when you have heaved from it its best. You shall not profane the holy things of the children of Israel, that you not die.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and to Aaron, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the statute of the law which the LORD has commanded. Tell the children of Israel to bring you a red heifer without spot, in which is no defect, and which was never yoked."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall give her to Eleazar the priest, and he shall bring her outside of the camp, and one shall kill her before his face."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Eleazar the priest shall take some of her blood with his finger, and sprinkle her blood toward the front of the Tent of Meeting seven times."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"One shall burn the heifer in his sight; her skin, and her meat, and her blood, with her dung, shall he burn."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The priest shall take cedar wood, hyssop, and scarlet, and cast it into the middle of the burning of the heifer."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then the priest shall wash his clothes, and he shall bathe his flesh in water, and afterward he shall come into the camp, and the priest shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He who burns her shall wash his clothes in water, and bathe his flesh in water, and shall be unclean until the evening."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cA man who is clean shall gather up the ashes of the heifer, and lay them up outside of the camp in a clean place; and it shall be kept for the congregation of the children of Israel for use in water for cleansing impurity. It is a sin offering."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He who gathers the ashes of the heifer shall wash his clothes, and be unclean until the evening. It shall be to the children of Israel, and to the stranger who lives as a foreigner among them, for a statute forever."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who touches the dead body of any man shall be unclean seven days."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He shall purify himself with water on the third day, and on the seventh day he shall be clean; but if he doesn\u2019t purify himself the third day, then the seventh day he shall not be clean."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Whoever touches a dead person, the body of a man who has died, and doesn\u2019t purify himself, defiles the LORD\u2019s tabernacle; and that soul shall be cut off from Israel; because the water for impurity was not sprinkled on him, he shall be unclean. His uncleanness is yet on him."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the law when a man dies in a tent: everyone who comes into the tent, and everyone who is in the tent, shall be unclean seven days."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Every open vessel, which has no covering bound on it, is unclean."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhoever in the open field touches one who is slain with a sword, or a dead body, or a bone of a man, or a grave, shall be unclean seven days."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the unclean, they shall take of the ashes of the burning of the sin offering; and running water shall be poured on them in a vessel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"A clean person shall take hyssop, dip it in the water, and sprinkle it on the tent, on all the vessels, on the persons who were there, and on him who touched the bone, or the slain, or the dead, or the grave."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The clean person shall sprinkle on the unclean on the third day, and on the seventh day. On the seventh day, he shall purify him. He shall wash his clothes and bathe himself in water, and shall be clean at evening."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But the man who shall be unclean, and shall not purify himself, that soul shall be cut off from among the assembly, because he has defiled the sanctuary of the LORD. The water for impurity has not been sprinkled on him. He is unclean."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"It shall be a perpetual statute to them. He who sprinkles the water for impurity shall wash his clothes, and he who touches the water for impurity shall be unclean until evening."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhatever the unclean person touches shall be unclean; and the soul that touches it shall be unclean until evening.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel, even the whole congregation, came into the wilderness of Zin in the first month. The people stayed in Kadesh. Miriam died there, and was buried there."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"There was no water for the congregation; and they assembled themselves together against Moses and against Aaron."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The people quarreled with Moses, and spoke, saying, \u201cWe wish that we had died when our brothers died before the LORD!"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Why have you brought the LORD\u2019s assembly into this wilderness, that we should die there, we and our animals?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Why have you made us to come up out of Egypt, to bring us in to this evil place? It is no place of seed, or of figs, or of vines, or of pomegranates; neither is there any water to drink.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron went from the presence of the assembly to the door of the Tent of Meeting, and fell on their faces. The LORD\u2019s glory appeared to them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"\u201cTake the rod, and assemble the congregation, you, and Aaron your brother, and speak to the rock before their eyes, that it pour out its water. You shall bring water to them out of the rock; so you shall give the congregation and their livestock drink.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses took the rod from before the LORD, as he commanded him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Moses and Aaron gathered the assembly together before the rock, and he said to them, \u201cHear now, you rebels! Shall we bring water out of this rock for you?\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Moses lifted up his hand, and struck the rock with his rod twice, and water came out abundantly. The congregation and their livestock drank."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses and Aaron, \u201cBecause you didn\u2019t believe in me, to sanctify me in the eyes of the children of Israel, therefore you shall not bring this assembly into the land which I have given them.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the waters of Meribah; because the children of Israel strove with the LORD, and he was sanctified in them."]],f:["\u201cMeribah\u201d means \u201cquarreling\u201d."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses sent messengers from Kadesh to the king of Edom, saying:"],[0,"\u201cYour brother Israel says: You know all the travail that has happened to us;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"how our fathers went down into Egypt, and we lived in Egypt a long time. The Egyptians mistreated us and our fathers."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When we cried to the LORD, he heard our voice, sent an angel, and brought us out of Egypt. Behold, we are in Kadesh, a city in the edge of your border."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cPlease let us pass through your land. We will not pass through field or through vineyard, neither will we drink from the water of the wells. We will go along the king\u2019s highway. We will not turn away to the right hand nor to the left, until we have passed your border.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Edom said to him, \u201cYou shall not pass through me, lest I come out with the sword against you.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel said to him, \u201cWe will go up by the highway; and if we drink your water, I and my livestock, then I will give its price. Only let me, without doing anything else, pass through on my feet.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou shall not pass through.\u201d Edom came out against him with many people, and with a strong hand."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Thus Edom refused to give Israel passage through his border, so Israel turned away from him."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"They traveled from Kadesh, and the children of Israel, even the whole congregation, came to Mount Hor."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses and Aaron in Mount Hor, by the border of the land of Edom, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cAaron shall be gathered to his people; for he shall not enter into the land which I have given to the children of Israel, because you rebelled against my word at the waters of Meribah."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Take Aaron and Eleazar his son, and bring them up to Mount Hor;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and strip Aaron of his garments, and put them on Eleazar his son. Aaron shall be gathered, and shall die there.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses did as the LORD commanded. They went up onto Mount Hor in the sight of all the congregation."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Moses stripped Aaron of his garments, and put them on Eleazar his son. Aaron died there on the top of the mountain, and Moses and Eleazar came down from the mountain."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"When all the congregation saw that Aaron was dead, they wept for Aaron thirty days, even all the house of Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The Canaanite, the king of Arad, who lived in the South, heard that Israel came by the way of Atharim. He fought against Israel, and took some of them captive."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Israel vowed a vow to the LORD, and said, \u201cIf you will indeed deliver this people into my hand, then I will utterly destroy their cities.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD listened to the voice of Israel, and delivered up the Canaanites; and they utterly destroyed them and their cities. The name of the place was called Hormah."]],f:["\u201cHormah\u201d means \u201cdestruction\u201d."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"They traveled from Mount Hor by the way to the Red Sea, to go around the land of Edom. The soul of the people was very discouraged because of the journey."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The people spoke against God and against Moses: \u201cWhy have you brought us up out of Egypt to die in the wilderness? For there is no bread, there is no water, and our soul loathes this disgusting food!\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD sent venomous snakes among the people, and they bit the people. Many people of Israel died."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The people came to Moses, and said, \u201cWe have sinned, because we have spoken against the LORD and against you. Pray to the LORD, that he take away the serpents from us.\u201d Moses prayed for the people."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cMake a venomous snake, and set it on a pole. It shall happen that everyone who is bitten, when he sees it, shall live.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moses made a serpent of bronze, and set it on the pole. If a serpent had bitten any man, when he looked at the serpent of bronze, he lived."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel traveled, and encamped in Oboth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They traveled from Oboth, and encamped at Iyeabarim, in the wilderness which is before Moab, toward the sunrise."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"From there they traveled, and encamped in the valley of Zered."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"From there they traveled, and encamped on the other side of the Arnon, which is in the wilderness that comes out of the border of the Amorites; for the Arnon is the border of Moab, between Moab and the Amorites."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore it is said in The Book of the Wars of the LORD, \u201cVaheb in Suphah, the valleys of the Arnon,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"the slope of the valleys that incline toward the dwelling of Ar, leans on the border of Moab.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"From there they traveled to Beer; that is the well of which the LORD said to Moses, \u201cGather the people together, and I will give them water.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Israel sang this song:"],[1,"\u201cSpring up, well! Sing to it,"]]},{v:18,l:[[2,"the well, which the princes dug,"],[2,"which the nobles of the people dug,"],[2,"with the scepter, and with their poles.\u201d"],[0,"From the wilderness they traveled to Mattanah;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and from Mattanah to Nahaliel; and from Nahaliel to Bamoth;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and from Bamoth to the valley that is in the field of Moab, to the top of Pisgah, which looks down on the desert."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Israel sent messengers to Sihon king of the Amorites, saying,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"\u201cLet me pass through your land. We will not turn away into field or vineyard. We will not drink of the water of the wells. We will go by the king\u2019s highway, until we have passed your border.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Sihon would not allow Israel to pass through his border, but Sihon gathered all his people together, and went out against Israel into the wilderness, and came to Jahaz. He fought against Israel."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Israel struck him with the edge of the sword, and possessed his land from the Arnon to the Jabbok, even to the children of Ammon; for the border of the children of Ammon was fortified."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Israel took all these cities. Israel lived in all the cities of the Amorites, in Heshbon, and in all its villages."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For Heshbon was the city of Sihon the king of the Amorites, who had fought against the former king of Moab, and taken all his land out of his hand, even to the Arnon."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Therefore those who speak in proverbs say,"],[1,"\u201cCome to Heshbon."],[2,"Let the city of Sihon be built and established;"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"for a fire has gone out of Heshbon,"],[2,"a flame from the city of Sihon."],[1,"It has devoured Ar of Moab,"],[2,"The lords of the high places of the Arnon."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to you, Moab!"],[2,"You are undone, people of Chemosh!"],[1,"He has given his sons as fugitives,"],[2,"and his daughters into captivity,"],[2,"to Sihon king of the Amorites."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"We have shot at them."],[2,"Heshbon has perished even to Dibon."],[1,"We have laid waste even to Nophah,"],[2,"Which reaches to Medeba.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus Israel lived in the land of the Amorites."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Moses sent to spy out Jazer. They took its villages, and drove out the Amorites who were there."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They turned and went up by the way of Bashan. Og the king of Bashan went out against them, he and all his people, to battle at Edrei."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cDon\u2019t fear him, for I have delivered him into your hand, with all his people, and his land. You shall do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived at Heshbon.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"So they struck him, with his sons and all his people, until there were no survivors; and they possessed his land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel traveled, and encamped in the plains of Moab beyond the Jordan at Jericho."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Balak the son of Zippor saw all that Israel had done to the Amorites."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Moab was very afraid of the people, because they were many. Moab was distressed because of the children of Israel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Moab said to the elders of Midian, \u201cNow this multitude will lick up all that is around us, as the ox licks up the grass of the field.\u201d"],[0,"Balak the son of Zippor was king of Moab at that time."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He sent messengers to Balaam the son of Beor, to Pethor, which is by the River, to the land of the children of his people, to call him, saying, \u201cBehold, there is a people who came out of Egypt. Behold, they cover the surface of the earth, and they are staying opposite me."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Please come now therefore, and curse this people for me; for they are too mighty for me. Perhaps I shall prevail, that we may strike them, and that I may drive them out of the land; for I know that he whom you bless is blessed, and he whom you curse is cursed.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The elders of Moab and the elders of Midian departed with the rewards of divination in their hand. They came to Balaam, and spoke to him the words of Balak."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cLodge here this night, and I will bring you word again, as the LORD shall speak to me.\u201d The princes of Moab stayed with Balaam."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"God came to Balaam, and said, \u201cWho are these men with you?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam said to God, \u201cBalak the son of Zippor, king of Moab, has said to me,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u2018Behold, the people that has come out of Egypt covers the surface of the earth. Now, come curse them for me. Perhaps I shall be able to fight against them, and shall drive them out.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Balaam, \u201cYou shall not go with them. You shall not curse the people, for they are blessed.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam rose up in the morning, and said to the princes of Balak, \u201cGo to your land; for the LORD refuses to permit me to go with you.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The princes of Moab rose up, and they went to Balak, and said, \u201cBalaam refuses to come with us.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak again sent princes, more, and more honorable than they."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They came to Balaam, and said to him, \u201cBalak the son of Zippor says, \u2018Please let nothing hinder you from coming to me,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"for I will promote you to very great honor, and whatever you say to me I will do. Please come therefore, and curse this people for me.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam answered the servants of Balak, \u201cIf Balak would give me his house full of silver and gold, I can\u2019t go beyond the word of the LORD my God, to do less or more."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now therefore please stay here tonight as well, that I may know what else the LORD will speak to me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"God came to Balaam at night, and said to him, \u201cIf the men have come to call you, rise up, go with them; but only the word which I speak to you, that you shall do.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam rose up in the morning, and saddled his donkey, and went with the princes of Moab."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"God\u2019s anger burned because he went; and the LORD\u2019s angel placed himself in the way as an adversary against him. Now he was riding on his donkey, and his two servants were with him."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The donkey saw the LORD\u2019s angel standing in the way, with his sword drawn in his hand; and the donkey turned out of the path, and went into the field. Balaam struck the donkey, to turn her into the path."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s angel stood in a narrow path between the vineyards, a wall being on this side, and a wall on that side."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The donkey saw the LORD\u2019s angel, and she thrust herself to the wall, and crushed Balaam\u2019s foot against the wall. He struck her again."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel went further, and stood in a narrow place, where there was no way to turn either to the right hand or to the left."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The donkey saw the LORD\u2019s angel, and she lay down under Balaam. Balaam\u2019s anger burned, and he struck the donkey with his staff."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD opened the mouth of the donkey, and she said to Balaam, \u201cWhat have I done to you, that you have struck me these three times?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam said to the donkey, \u201cBecause you have mocked me, I wish there were a sword in my hand, for now I would have killed you.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"The donkey said to Balaam, \u201cAm I not your donkey, on which you have ridden all your life long until today? Was I ever in the habit of doing so to you?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cNo.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD opened the eyes of Balaam, and he saw the LORD\u2019s angel standing in the way, with his sword drawn in his hand; and he bowed his head, and fell on his face."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to him, \u201cWhy have you struck your donkey these three times? Behold, I have come out as an adversary, because your way is perverse before me."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The donkey saw me, and turned away before me these three times. Unless she had turned away from me, surely now I would have killed you, and saved her alive.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam said to the LORD\u2019s angel, \u201cI have sinned; for I didn\u2019t know that you stood in the way against me. Now therefore, if it displeases you, I will go back again.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to Balaam, \u201cGo with the men; but you shall only speak the word that I shall speak to you.\u201d"],[0,"So Balaam went with the princes of Balak."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"When Balak heard that Balaam had come, he went out to meet him to the City of Moab, which is on the border of the Arnon, which is in the utmost part of the border."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Balak said to Balaam, \u201cDidn\u2019t I earnestly send for you to summon you? Why didn\u2019t you come to me? Am I not able indeed to promote you to honor?\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam said to Balak, \u201cBehold, I have come to you. Have I now any power at all to speak anything? I will speak the word that God puts in my mouth.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam went with Balak, and they came to Kiriath Huzoth."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Balak sacrificed cattle and sheep, and sent to Balaam, and to the princes who were with him."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"In the morning, Balak took Balaam, and brought him up into the high places of Baal; and he saw from there part of the people."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam said to Balak, \u201cBuild here seven altars for me, and prepare here seven bulls and seven rams for me.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak did as Balaam had spoken; and Balak and Balaam offered on every altar a bull and a ram."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Balaam said to Balak, \u201cStand by your burnt offering, and I will go. Perhaps the LORD will come to meet me. Whatever he shows me I will tell you.\u201d"],[0,"He went to a bare height."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"God met Balaam, and he said to him, \u201cI have prepared the seven altars, and I have offered up a bull and a ram on every altar.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD put a word in Balaam\u2019s mouth, and said, \u201cReturn to Balak, and thus you shall speak.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He returned to him, and behold, he was standing by his burnt offering, he, and all the princes of Moab."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He took up his parable, and said,"],[1,"\u201cFrom Aram has Balak brought me,"],[2,"the king of Moab from the mountains of the East."],[1,"Come, curse Jacob for me."],[2,"Come, defy Israel."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"How shall I curse whom God has not cursed?"],[2,"How shall I defy whom the LORD has not defied?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For from the top of the rocks I see him."],[2,"From the hills I see him."],[1,"Behold, it is a people that dwells alone,"],[2,"and shall not be listed among the nations."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can count the dust of Jacob,"],[2,"or count the fourth part of Israel?"],[1,"Let me die the death of the righteous!"],[2,"Let my last end be like his!\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak said to Balaam, \u201cWhat have you done to me? I took you to curse my enemies, and behold, you have blessed them altogether.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered and said, \u201cMust I not take heed to speak that which the LORD puts in my mouth?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak said to him, \u201cPlease come with me to another place, where you may see them. You shall see just part of them, and shall not see them all. Curse them from there for me.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He took him into the field of Zophim, to the top of Pisgah, and built seven altars, and offered up a bull and a ram on every altar."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said to Balak, \u201cStand here by your burnt offering, while I meet God over there.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD met Balaam, and put a word in his mouth, and said, \u201cReturn to Balak, and say this.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He came to him, and behold, he was standing by his burnt offering, and the princes of Moab with him. Balak said to him, \u201cWhat has the LORD spoken?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He took up his parable, and said,"],[1,"\u201cRise up, Balak, and hear!"],[2,"Listen to me, you son of Zippor."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"God is not a man, that he should lie,"],[2,"nor a son of man, that he should repent."],[1,"Has he said, and he won\u2019t do it?"],[2,"Or has he spoken, and he won\u2019t make it good?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I have received a command to bless."],[2,"He has blessed, and I can\u2019t reverse it."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He has not seen iniquity in Jacob."],[2,"Neither has he seen perverseness in Israel."],[1,"The LORD his God is with him."],[2,"The shout of a king is among them."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"God brings them out of Egypt."],[2,"He has as it were the strength of the wild ox."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely there is no enchantment with Jacob;"],[2,"neither is there any divination with Israel."],[1,"Now it shall be said of Jacob and of Israel,"],[2,"\u2018What has God done!\u2019"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, a people rises up as a lioness."],[2,"As a lion he lifts himself up."],[1,"He shall not lie down until he eats of the prey,"],[2,"and drinks the blood of the slain.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak said to Balaam, \u201cNeither curse them at all, nor bless them at all.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"But Balaam answered Balak, \u201cDidn\u2019t I tell you, saying, \u2018All that the LORD speaks, that I must do\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak said to Balaam, \u201cCome now, I will take you to another place; perhaps it will please God that you may curse them for me from there.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak took Balaam to the top of Peor, that looks down on the desert."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Balaam said to Balak, \u201cBuild seven altars for me here, and prepare seven bulls and seven rams for me here.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak did as Balaam had said, and offered up a bull and a ram on every altar."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Balaam saw that it pleased the LORD to bless Israel, he didn\u2019t go, as at the other times, to use divination, but he set his face toward the wilderness."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Balaam lifted up his eyes, and he saw Israel dwelling according to their tribes; and the Spirit of God came on him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He took up his parable, and said,"],[1,"\u201cBalaam the son of Beor says,"],[2,"the man whose eyes are open says;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"he says, who hears the words of God,"],[2,"who sees the vision of the Almighty,"],[2,"falling down, and having his eyes open:"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"How goodly are your tents, Jacob,"],[2,"and your dwellings, Israel!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"As valleys they are spread out,"],[2,"as gardens by the riverside,"],[2,"as aloes which the LORD has planted,"],[2,"as cedar trees beside the waters."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Water shall flow from his buckets."],[2,"His seed shall be in many waters."],[1,"His king shall be higher than Agag."],[2,"His kingdom shall be exalted."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"God brings him out of Egypt."],[2,"He has as it were the strength of the wild ox."],[1,"He shall consume the nations his adversaries,"],[2,"shall break their bones in pieces,"],[2,"and pierce them with his arrows."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He couched, he lay down as a lion,"],[2,"as a lioness;"],[2,"who shall rouse him up?"],[1,"Everyone who blesses you is blessed."],[2,"Everyone who curses you is cursed.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Balak\u2019s anger burned against Balaam, and he struck his hands together. Balak said to Balaam, \u201cI called you to curse my enemies, and, behold, you have altogether blessed them these three times."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore, flee to your place, now! I thought to promote you to great honor; but, behold, the LORD has kept you back from honor.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam said to Balak, \u201cDidn\u2019t I also tell your messengers whom you sent to me, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u2018If Balak would give me his house full of silver and gold, I can\u2019t go beyond the LORD\u2019s word, to do either good or bad from my own mind. I will say what the LORD says\u2019?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now, behold, I go to my people. Come, I will inform you what this people shall do to your people in the latter days.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He took up his parable, and said,"],[1,"\u201cBalaam the son of Beor says,"],[2,"the man whose eyes are open says;"]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"he says, who hears the words of God,"],[2,"knows the knowledge of the Most High,"],[2,"and who sees the vision of the Almighty,"],[2,"falling down, and having his eyes open:"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I see him, but not now."],[2,"I see him, but not near."],[1,"A star will come out of Jacob."],[2,"A scepter will rise out of Israel,"],[1,"and shall strike through the corners of Moab,"],[2,"and crush all the sons of Sheth."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Edom shall be a possession."],[2,"Seir, his enemy, also shall be a possession,"],[2,"while Israel does valiantly."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Out of Jacob shall one have dominion,"],[2,"and shall destroy the remnant from the city.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He looked at Amalek, and took up his parable, and said,"],[1,"\u201cAmalek was the first of the nations,"],[2,"but his latter end shall come to destruction.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He looked at the Kenite, and took up his parable, and said,"],[1,"\u201cYour dwelling place is strong."],[2,"Your nest is set in the rock."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Nevertheless Kain shall be wasted,"],[2,"until Asshur carries you away captive.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He took up his parable, and said,"],[1,"\u201cAlas, who shall live when God does this?"]]},{v:24,l:[[2,"But ships shall come from the coast of Kittim."],[1,"They shall afflict Asshur, and shall afflict Eber."],[2,"He also shall come to destruction.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Balaam rose up, and went and returned to his place; and Balak also went his way."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel stayed in Shittim; and the people began to play the prostitute with the daughters of Moab;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"for they called the people to the sacrifices of their gods. The people ate and bowed down to their gods."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Israel joined himself to Baal Peor, and the LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cTake all the chiefs of the people, and hang them up to the LORD before the sun, that the fierce anger of the LORD may turn away from Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the judges of Israel, \u201cEveryone kill his men who have joined themselves to Baal Peor.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, one of the children of Israel came and brought to his brothers a Midianite woman in the sight of Moses, and in the sight of all the congregation of the children of Israel, while they were weeping at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, saw it, he rose up from the middle of the congregation, and took a spear in his hand."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He went after the man of Israel into the pavilion, and thrust both of them through, the man of Israel, and the woman through her body. So the plague was stopped among the children of Israel."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Those who died by the plague were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cPhinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the priest, has turned my wrath away from the children of Israel, in that he was jealous with my jealousy among them, so that I didn\u2019t consume the children of Israel in my jealousy."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore say, \u2018Behold, I give to him my covenant of peace."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It shall be to him, and to his offspring after him, the covenant of an everlasting priesthood, because he was jealous for his God, and made atonement for the children of Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the name of the man of Israel that was slain, who was slain with the Midianite woman, was Zimri, the son of Salu, a prince of a fathers\u2019 house among the Simeonites."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The name of the Midianite woman who was slain was Cozbi, the daughter of Zur. He was head of the people of a fathers\u2019 house in Midian."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u201cHarass the Midianites, and strike them;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"for they harassed you with their wiles, wherein they have deceived you in the matter of Peor, and in the incident regarding Cozbi, the daughter of the prince of Midian, their sister, who was slain on the day of the plague in the matter of Peor.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After the plague, the LORD spoke to Moses and to Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cTake a census of all the congregation of the children of Israel, from twenty years old and upward, by their fathers\u2019 houses, all who are able to go out to war in Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Moses and Eleazar the priest spoke with them in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cTake a census, from twenty years old and upward, as the LORD commanded Moses and the children of Israel.\u201d"],[0,"These are those who came out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Reuben, the firstborn of Israel; the sons of Reuben: of Hanoch, the family of the Hanochites; of Pallu, the family of the Palluites;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"of Hezron, the family of the Hezronites; of Carmi, the family of the Carmites."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"These are the families of the Reubenites; and those who were counted of them were forty-three thousand seven hundred thirty."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The son of Pallu: Eliab."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The sons of Eliab: Nemuel, Dathan, and Abiram. These are that Dathan and Abiram who were called by the congregation, who rebelled against Moses and against Aaron in the company of Korah when they rebelled against the LORD;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and the earth opened its mouth, and swallowed them up together with Korah when that company died; at the time the fire devoured two hundred fifty men, and they became a sign."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Notwithstanding, the sons of Korah didn\u2019t die."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The sons of Simeon after their families: of Nemuel, the family of the Nemuelites; of Jamin, the family of the Jaminites; of Jachin, the family of the Jachinites;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"of Zerah, the family of the Zerahites; of Shaul, the family of the Shaulites."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"These are the families of the Simeonites, twenty-two thousand two hundred."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The sons of Gad after their families: of Zephon, the family of the Zephonites; of Haggi, the family of the Haggites; of Shuni, the family of the Shunites;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"of Ozni, the family of the Oznites; of Eri, the family of the Erites;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"of Arod, the family of the Arodites; of Areli, the family of the Arelites."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"These are the families of the sons of Gad according to those who were counted of them, forty thousand and five hundred."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of Judah: Er and Onan. Er and Onan died in the land of Canaan."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The sons of Judah after their families were: of Shelah, the family of the Shelanites; of Perez, the family of the Perezites; of Zerah, the family of the Zerahites."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The sons of Perez were: of Hezron, the family of the Hezronites; of Hamul, the family of the Hamulites."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"These are the families of Judah according to those who were counted of them, seventy-six thousand five hundred."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The sons of Issachar after their families: of Tola, the family of the Tolaites; of Puvah, the family of the Punites;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"of Jashub, the family of the Jashubites; of Shimron, the family of the Shimronites."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"These are the families of Issachar according to those who were counted of them, sixty-four thousand three hundred."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The sons of Zebulun after their families: of Sered, the family of the Seredites; of Elon, the family of the Elonites; of Jahleel, the family of the Jahleelites."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"These are the families of the Zebulunites according to those who were counted of them, sixty thousand five hundred."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The sons of Joseph after their families: Manasseh and Ephraim."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The sons of Manasseh: of Machir, the family of the Machirites; and Machir became the father of Gilead; of Gilead, the family of the Gileadites."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Gilead: of Iezer, the family of the Iezerites; of Helek, the family of the Helekites;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and Asriel, the family of the Asrielites; and Shechem, the family of the Shechemites;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and Shemida, the family of the Shemidaites; and Hepher, the family of the Hepherites."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Zelophehad the son of Hepher had no sons, but daughters: and the names of the daughters of Zelophehad were Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"These are the families of Manasseh. Those who were counted of them were fifty-two thousand seven hundred."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Ephraim after their families: of Shuthelah, the family of the Shuthelahites; of Becher, the family of the Becherites; of Tahan, the family of the Tahanites."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Shuthelah: of Eran, the family of the Eranites."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"These are the families of the sons of Ephraim according to those who were counted of them, thirty-two thousand five hundred. These are the sons of Joseph after their families."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The sons of Benjamin after their families: of Bela, the family of the Belaites; of Ashbel, the family of the Ashbelites; of Ahiram, the family of the Ahiramites;"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"of Shephupham, the family of the Shuphamites; of Hupham, the family of the Huphamites."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The sons of Bela were Ard and Naaman: the family of the Ardites; and of Naaman, the family of the Naamites."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Benjamin after their families; and those who were counted of them were forty-five thousand six hundred."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Dan after their families: of Shuham, the family of the Shuhamites. These are the families of Dan after their families."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"All the families of the Shuhamites, according to those who were counted of them, were sixty-four thousand four hundred."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The sons of Asher after their families: of Imnah, the family of the Imnites; of Ishvi, the family of the Ishvites; of Beriah, the family of the Berites."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Of the sons of Beriah: of Heber, the family of the Heberites; of Malchiel, the family of the Malchielites."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"The name of the daughter of Asher was Serah."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"These are the families of the sons of Asher according to those who were counted of them, fifty-three thousand four hundred."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"The sons of Naphtali after their families: of Jahzeel, the family of the Jahzeelites; of Guni, the family of the Gunites;"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"of Jezer, the family of the Jezerites; of Shillem, the family of the Shillemites."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"These are the families of Naphtali according to their families; and those who were counted of them were forty-five thousand four hundred."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted of the children of Israel, six hundred one thousand seven hundred thirty."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"\u201cTo these the land shall be divided for an inheritance according to the number of names."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"To the more you shall give the more inheritance, and to the fewer you shall give the less inheritance. To everyone according to those who were counted of him shall his inheritance be given."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"Notwithstanding, the land shall be divided by lot. According to the names of the tribes of their fathers they shall inherit."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"According to the lot shall their inheritance be divided between the more and the fewer.\u201d"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted of the Levites after their families: of Gershon, the family of the Gershonites; of Kohath, the family of the Kohathites; of Merari, the family of the Merarites."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"These are the families of Levi: the family of the Libnites, the family of the Hebronites, the family of the Mahlites, the family of the Mushites, and the family of the Korahites. Kohath became the father of Amram."]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"The name of Amram\u2019s wife was Jochebed, the daughter of Levi, who was born to Levi in Egypt. She bore to Amram Aaron and Moses, and Miriam their sister."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"To Aaron were born Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar."]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"Nadab and Abihu died when they offered strange fire before the LORD."]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"Those who were counted of them were twenty-three thousand, every male from a month old and upward; for they were not counted among the children of Israel, because there was no inheritance given them among the children of Israel."]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"These are those who were counted by Moses and Eleazar the priest, who counted the children of Israel in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"But among these there was not a man of them who were counted by Moses and Aaron the priest, who counted the children of Israel in the wilderness of Sinai."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"For the LORD had said of them, \u201cThey shall surely die in the wilderness.\u201d There was not a man left of them, except Caleb the son of Jephunneh, and Joshua the son of Nun."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the daughters of Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, of the families of Manasseh the son of Joseph came near. These are the names of his daughters: Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They stood before Moses, before Eleazar the priest, and before the princes and all the congregation, at the door of the Tent of Meeting, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cOur father died in the wilderness. He was not among the company of those who gathered themselves together against the LORD in the company of Korah, but he died in his own sin. He had no sons."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Why should the name of our father be taken away from among his family, because he had no son? Give to us a possession among the brothers of our father.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses brought their cause before the LORD."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u201cThe daughters of Zelophehad speak right. You shall surely give them a possession of an inheritance among their father\u2019s brothers. You shall cause the inheritance of their father to pass to them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall speak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018If a man dies, and has no son, then you shall cause his inheritance to pass to his daughter."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If he has no daughter, then you shall give his inheritance to his brothers."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If he has no brothers, then you shall give his inheritance to his father\u2019s brothers."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If his father has no brothers, then you shall give his inheritance to his kinsman who is next to him of his family, and he shall possess it. This shall be a statute and ordinance for the children of Israel, as the LORD commanded Moses.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cGo up into this mountain of Abarim, and see the land which I have given to the children of Israel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When you have seen it, you also shall be gathered to your people, as Aaron your brother was gathered;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"because in the strife of the congregation, you rebelled against my word in the wilderness of Zin, to honor me as holy at the waters before their eyes.\u201d (These are the waters of Meribah of Kadesh in the wilderness of Zin.)"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke to the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cLet the LORD, the God of the spirits of all flesh, appoint a man over the congregation,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"who may go out before them, and who may come in before them, and who may lead them out, and who may bring them in, that the congregation of the LORD may not be as sheep which have no shepherd.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cTake Joshua the son of Nun, a man in whom is the Spirit, and lay your hand on him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Set him before Eleazar the priest, and before all the congregation; and commission him in their sight."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall give authority to him, that all the congregation of the children of Israel may obey."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He shall stand before Eleazar the priest, who shall inquire for him by the judgment of the Urim before the LORD. At his word they shall go out, and at his word they shall come in, both he and all the children of Israel with him, even all the congregation.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses did as the LORD commanded him. He took Joshua, and set him before Eleazar the priest and before all the congregation."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He laid his hands on him and commissioned him, as the LORD spoke by Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cCommand the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018See that you present my offering, my food for my offerings made by fire, as a pleasant aroma to me, in their due season.\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall tell them, \u2018This is the offering made by fire which you shall offer to the LORD: male lambs a year old without defect, two day by day, for a continual burnt offering."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall offer the one lamb in the morning, and you shall offer the other lamb at evening,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"with one tenth of an ephah of fine flour for a meal offering, mixed with the fourth part of a hin of beaten oil."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"It is a continual burnt offering which was ordained in Mount Sinai for a pleasant aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Its drink offering shall be the fourth part of a hin for each lamb. You shall pour out a drink offering of strong drink to the LORD in the holy place."]],f:["One hin is about 6.5 liters, so 1/4 hin is about 1.6 liters or 1.7 quarts."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The other lamb you shall offer at evening. As the meal offering of the morning, and as its drink offering, you shall offer it, an offering made by fire, for a pleasant aroma to the LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the Sabbath day, you shall offer two male lambs a year old without defect, and two tenths of an ephah of fine flour for a meal offering mixed with oil, and its drink offering:"]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"this is the burnt offering of every Sabbath, in addition to the continual burnt offering and its drink offering."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018In the beginnings of your months, you shall offer a burnt offering to the LORD: two young bulls, one ram, seven male lambs a year old without defect,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and three tenths of an ephah of fine flour for a meal offering mixed with oil, for each bull; and two tenth parts of fine flour for a meal offering mixed with oil, for the one ram;"]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and one tenth part of fine flour mixed with oil for a meal offering to every lamb, as a burnt offering of a pleasant aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Their drink offerings shall be half a hin of wine for a bull, the third part of a hin for the ram, and the fourth part of a hin for a lamb. This is the burnt offering of every month throughout the months of the year."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Also, one male goat for a sin offering to the LORD shall be offered in addition to the continual burnt offering and its drink offering."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018In the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month, is the LORD\u2019s Passover."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"On the fifteenth day of this month shall be a feast. Unleavened bread shall be eaten for seven days."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In the first day shall be a holy convocation. You shall do no regular work,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"but you shall offer an offering made by fire, a burnt offering to the LORD: two young bulls, one ram, and seven male lambs a year old. They shall be without defect,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"with their meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil. You shall offer three tenths for a bull, and two tenths for the ram."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You shall offer one tenth for every lamb of the seven lambs;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering, to make atonement for you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You shall offer these in addition to the burnt offering of the morning, which is for a continual burnt offering."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"In this way you shall offer daily, for seven days, the food of the offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD. It shall be offered in addition to the continual burnt offering and its drink offering."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"On the seventh day you shall have a holy convocation. You shall do no regular work."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Also in the day of the first fruits, when you offer a new meal offering to the LORD in your feast of weeks, you shall have a holy convocation. You shall do no regular work;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"but you shall offer a burnt offering for a pleasant aroma to the LORD: two young bulls, one ram, seven male lambs a year old;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and their meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil, three tenths for each bull, two tenths for the one ram,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"one tenth for every lamb of the seven lambs;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and one male goat, to make atonement for you."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Besides the continual burnt offering and its meal offering, you shall offer them and their drink offerings. See that they are without defect."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018In the seventh month, on the first day of the month, you shall have a holy convocation; you shall do no regular work. It is a day of blowing of trumpets to you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall offer a burnt offering for a pleasant aroma to the LORD: one young bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and their meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil: three tenths for the bull, two tenths for the ram,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and one tenth for every lamb of the seven lambs;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering, to make atonement for you;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"in addition to the burnt offering of the new moon with its meal offering, and the continual burnt offering with its meal offering, and their drink offerings, according to their ordinance, for a pleasant aroma, an offering made by fire to the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the tenth day of this seventh month you shall have a holy convocation. You shall afflict your souls. You shall do no kind of work;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but you shall offer a burnt offering to the LORD for a pleasant aroma: one young bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old, all without defect;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and their meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil: three tenths for the bull, two tenths for the one ram,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"one tenth for every lamb of the seven lambs;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the sin offering of atonement, and the continual burnt offering, and its meal offering, and their drink offerings."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the fifteenth day of the seventh month you shall have a holy convocation. You shall do no regular work. You shall keep a feast to the LORD seven days."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall offer a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, of a pleasant aroma to the LORD: thirteen young bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old, all without defect;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and their meal offering, fine flour mixed with oil: three tenths for every bull of the thirteen bulls, two tenths for each ram of the two rams,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and one tenth for every lamb of the fourteen lambs;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the continual burnt offering, its meal offering, and its drink offering."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the second day you shall offer twelve young bulls, two rams, and fourteen male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the continual burnt offering, with its meal offering and their drink offerings."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the third day: eleven bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the continual burnt offering, and its meal offering, and its drink offering."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the fourth day ten bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering; in addition to the continual burnt offering, its meal offering, and its drink offering."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the fifth day: nine bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the continual burnt offering, and its meal offering, and its drink offering."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the sixth day: eight bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering; in addition to the continual burnt offering, its meal offering, and the drink offerings of it."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the seventh day: seven bulls, two rams, fourteen male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"and their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bulls, for the rams, and for the lambs, according to their number, after the ordinance,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering; in addition to the continual burnt offering, its meal offering, and its drink offering."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018On the eighth day you shall have a solemn assembly. You shall do no regular work;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"but you shall offer a burnt offering, an offering made by fire, a pleasant aroma to the LORD: one bull, one ram, seven male lambs a year old without defect;"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"their meal offering and their drink offerings for the bull, for the ram, and for the lambs, shall be according to their number, after the ordinance,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"and one male goat for a sin offering, in addition to the continual burnt offering, with its meal offering, and its drink offering."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall offer these to the LORD in your set feasts\u2014in addition to your vows and your free will offerings\u2014for your burnt offerings, your meal offerings, your drink offerings, and your peace offerings.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses told the children of Israel according to all that the LORD commanded Moses."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke to the heads of the tribes of the children of Israel, saying, \u201cThis is the thing which the LORD has commanded."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When a man vows a vow to the LORD, or swears an oath to bind his soul with a bond, he shall not break his word. He shall do according to all that proceeds out of his mouth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAlso, when a woman vows a vow to the LORD and binds herself by a pledge, being in her father\u2019s house, in her youth,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and her father hears her vow and her pledge with which she has bound her soul, and her father says nothing to her, then all her vows shall stand, and every pledge with which she has bound her soul shall stand."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But if her father forbids her in the day that he hears, none of her vows or of her pledges with which she has bound her soul, shall stand. The LORD will forgive her, because her father has forbidden her."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf she has a husband, while her vows are on her, or the rash utterance of her lips with which she has bound her soul,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and her husband hears it, and says nothing to her in the day that he hears it; then her vows shall stand, and her pledges with which she has bound her soul shall stand."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But if her husband forbids her in the day that he hears it, then he makes void her vow which is on her and the rash utterance of her lips, with which she has bound her soul. The LORD will forgive her."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut the vow of a widow, or of her who is divorced, everything with which she has bound her soul shall stand against her."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf she vowed in her husband\u2019s house or bound her soul by a bond with an oath,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and her husband heard it, and held his peace at her and didn\u2019t disallow her, then all her vows shall stand, and every pledge with which she bound her soul shall stand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But if her husband made them null and void in the day that he heard them, then whatever proceeded out of her lips concerning her vows, or concerning the bond of her soul, shall not stand. Her husband has made them void. The LORD will forgive her."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Every vow, and every binding oath to afflict the soul, her husband may establish it, or her husband may make it void."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But if her husband says nothing to her from day to day, then he establishes all her vows or all her pledges which are on her. He has established them, because he said nothing to her in the day that he heard them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But if he makes them null and void after he has heard them, then he shall bear her iniquity.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the statutes which the LORD commanded Moses, between a man and his wife, between a father and his daughter, being in her youth, in her father\u2019s house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cAvenge the children of Israel on the Midianites. Afterward you shall be gathered to your people.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke to the people, saying, \u201cArm men from among you for war, that they may go against Midian, to execute the LORD\u2019s vengeance on Midian."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall send one thousand out of every tribe, throughout all the tribes of Israel, to the war.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So there were delivered, out of the thousands of Israel, a thousand from every tribe, twelve thousand armed for war."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Moses sent them, one thousand of every tribe, to the war with Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest, to the war, with the vessels of the sanctuary and the trumpets for the alarm in his hand."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They fought against Midian, as the LORD commanded Moses. They killed every male."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They killed the kings of Midian with the rest of their slain: Evi, Rekem, Zur, Hur, and Reba, the five kings of Midian. They also killed Balaam the son of Beor with the sword."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The children of Israel took the women of Midian captive with their little ones; and all their livestock, all their flocks, and all their goods, they took as plunder."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All their cities in the places in which they lived, and all their encampments, they burned with fire."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They took all the captives, and all the plunder, both of man and of animal."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They brought the captives with the prey and the plunder, to Moses, and to Eleazar the priest, and to the congregation of the children of Israel, to the camp at the plains of Moab, which are by the Jordan at Jericho."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Moses and Eleazar the priest, with all the princes of the congregation, went out to meet them outside of the camp."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Moses was angry with the officers of the army, the captains of thousands and the captains of hundreds, who came from the service of the war."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Moses said to them, \u201cHave you saved all the women alive?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Behold, these caused the children of Israel, through the counsel of Balaam, to commit trespass against the LORD in the matter of Peor, and so the plague was among the congregation of the LORD."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now therefore kill every male among the little ones, and kill every woman who has known man by lying with him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But all the girls, who have not known man by lying with him, keep alive for yourselves."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cEncamp outside of the camp for seven days. Whoever has killed any person, and whoever has touched any slain, purify yourselves on the third day and on the seventh day, you and your captives."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall purify every garment, and all that is made of skin, and all work of goats\u2019 hair, and all things made of wood.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Eleazar the priest said to the men of war who went to the battle, \u201cThis is the statute of the law which the LORD has commanded Moses."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"However the gold, and the silver, the bronze, the iron, the tin, and the lead,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"everything that may withstand the fire, you shall make to go through the fire, and it shall be clean; nevertheless it shall be purified with the water for impurity. All that doesn\u2019t withstand the fire you shall make to go through the water."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall wash your clothes on the seventh day, and you shall be clean. Afterward you shall come into the camp.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u201cCount the plunder that was taken, both of man and of animal, you, and Eleazar the priest, and the heads of the fathers\u2019 households of the congregation;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and divide the plunder into two parts: between the men skilled in war, who went out to battle, and all the congregation."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Levy a tribute to the LORD of the men of war who went out to battle: one soul of five hundred; of the persons, of the cattle, of the donkeys, and of the flocks."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Take it from their half, and give it to Eleazar the priest, for the LORD\u2019s wave offering."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Of the children of Israel\u2019s half, you shall take one drawn out of every fifty, of the persons, of the cattle, of the donkeys, and of the flocks, of all the livestock, and give them to the Levites, who perform the duty of the LORD\u2019s tabernacle.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Eleazar the priest did as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the plunder, over and above the booty which the men of war took, was six hundred seventy-five thousand sheep,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"seventy-two thousand head of cattle,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"sixty-one thousand donkeys,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"and thirty-two thousand persons in all, of the women who had not known man by lying with him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The half, which was the portion of those who went out to war, was in number three hundred thirty-seven thousand five hundred sheep;"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"and the LORD\u2019s tribute of the sheep was six hundred seventy-five."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The cattle were thirty-six thousand, of which the LORD\u2019s tribute was seventy-two."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The donkeys were thirty thousand five hundred, of which the LORD\u2019s tribute was sixty-one."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The persons were sixteen thousand, of whom the LORD\u2019s tribute was thirty-two persons."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Moses gave the tribute, which was the LORD\u2019s wave offering, to Eleazar the priest, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Of the children of Israel\u2019s half, which Moses divided off from the men who fought"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"(now the congregation\u2019s half was three hundred thirty-seven thousand five hundred sheep,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"thirty-six thousand head of cattle,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"thirty thousand five hundred donkeys,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"and sixteen thousand persons),"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"even of the children of Israel\u2019s half, Moses took one drawn out of every fifty, both of man and of animal, and gave them to the Levites, who performed the duty of the LORD\u2019s tabernacle, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"The officers who were over the thousands of the army, the captains of thousands, and the captains of hundreds, came near to Moses."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"They said to Moses, \u201cYour servants have taken the sum of the men of war who are under our command, and there lacks not one man of us."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"We have brought the LORD\u2019s offering, what every man found: gold ornaments, armlets, bracelets, signet rings, earrings, and necklaces, to make atonement for our souls before the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and Eleazar the priest took their gold, even all worked jewels."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"All the gold of the wave offering that they offered up to the LORD, of the captains of thousands, and of the captains of hundreds, was sixteen thousand seven hundred fifty shekels."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 16,750 shekels is about 167.5 kilograms or about 368.5 pounds."]},{v:53,l:[[0,"The men of war had taken booty, every man for himself."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"Moses and Eleazar the priest took the gold of the captains of thousands and of hundreds, and brought it into the Tent of Meeting for a memorial for the children of Israel before the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the children of Reuben and the children of Gad had a very great multitude of livestock. They saw the land of Jazer, and the land of Gilead. Behold, the place was a place for livestock."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then the children of Gad and the children of Reuben came and spoke to Moses, and to Eleazar the priest, and to the princes of the congregation, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cAtaroth, Dibon, Jazer, Nimrah, Heshbon, Elealeh, Sebam, Nebo, and Beon,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"the land which the LORD struck before the congregation of Israel, is a land for livestock; and your servants have livestock.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cIf we have found favor in your sight, let this land be given to your servants for a possession. Don\u2019t bring us over the Jordan.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to the children of Gad, and to the children of Reuben, \u201cShall your brothers go to war while you sit here?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Why do you discourage the heart of the children of Israel from going over into the land which the LORD has given them?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Your fathers did so when I sent them from Kadesh Barnea to see the land."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For when they went up to the valley of Eshcol, and saw the land, they discouraged the heart of the children of Israel, that they should not go into the land which the LORD had given them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned in that day, and he swore, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u2018Surely none of the men who came up out of Egypt, from twenty years old and upward, shall see the land which I swore to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob; because they have not wholly followed me,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"except Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite, and Joshua the son of Nun, because they have followed the LORD completely.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel, and he made them wander back and forth in the wilderness forty years, until all the generation who had done evil in the LORD\u2019s sight was consumed."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, you have risen up in your fathers\u2019 place, an increase of sinful men, to increase the fierce anger of the LORD toward Israel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For if you turn away from after him, he will yet again leave them in the wilderness; and you will destroy all these people.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"They came near to him, and said, \u201cWe will build sheepfolds here for our livestock, and cities for our little ones;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"but we ourselves will be ready armed to go before the children of Israel, until we have brought them to their place. Our little ones shall dwell in the fortified cities because of the inhabitants of the land."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"We will not return to our houses until the children of Israel have all received their inheritance."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For we will not inherit with them on the other side of the Jordan and beyond, because our inheritance has come to us on this side of the Jordan eastward.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses said to them: \u201cIf you will do this thing, if you will arm yourselves to go before the LORD to the war,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and every one of your armed men will pass over the Jordan before the LORD until he has driven out his enemies from before him,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and the land is subdued before the LORD; then afterward you shall return, and be clear of obligation to the LORD and to Israel. Then this land shall be your possession before the LORD."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut if you will not do so, behold, you have sinned against the LORD; and be sure your sin will find you out."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Build cities for your little ones, and folds for your sheep; and do that which has proceeded out of your mouth.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Gad and the children of Reuben spoke to Moses, saying, \u201cYour servants will do as my lord commands."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Our little ones, our wives, our flocks, and all our livestock shall be there in the cities of Gilead;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"but your servants will pass over, every man who is armed for war, before the LORD to battle, as my lord says.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"So Moses commanded concerning them to Eleazar the priest, and to Joshua the son of Nun, and to the heads of the fathers\u2019 households of the tribes of the children of Israel."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Moses said to them, \u201cIf the children of Gad and the children of Reuben will pass with you over the Jordan, every man who is armed to battle before the LORD, and the land is subdued before you, then you shall give them the land of Gilead for a possession;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"but if they will not pass over with you armed, they shall have possessions among you in the land of Canaan.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Gad and the children of Reuben answered, saying, \u201cAs the LORD has said to your servants, so will we do."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"We will pass over armed before the LORD into the land of Canaan, and the possession of our inheritance shall remain with us beyond the Jordan.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses gave to them, even to the children of Gad, and to the children of Reuben, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh the son of Joseph, the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorites, and the kingdom of Og king of Bashan; the land, according to its cities and borders, even the cities of the surrounding land."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The children of Gad built Dibon, Ataroth, Aroer,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Atroth-shophan, Jazer, Jogbehah,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Beth Nimrah, and Beth Haran: fortified cities and folds for sheep."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The children of Reuben built Heshbon, Elealeh, Kiriathaim,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Nebo, and Baal Meon, (their names being changed), and Sibmah. They gave other names to the cities which they built."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The children of Machir the son of Manasseh went to Gilead, took it, and dispossessed the Amorites who were therein."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Moses gave Gilead to Machir the son of Manasseh; and he lived therein."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Jair the son of Manasseh went and took its villages, and called them Havvoth Jair."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Nobah went and took Kenath and its villages, and called it Nobah, after his own name."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the journeys of the children of Israel, when they went out of the land of Egypt by their armies under the hand of Moses and Aaron."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Moses wrote the starting points of their journeys by the commandment of the LORD. These are their journeys according to their starting points."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They traveled from Rameses in the first month, on the fifteenth day of the first month; on the next day after the Passover, the children of Israel went out with a high hand in the sight of all the Egyptians,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"while the Egyptians were burying all their firstborn, whom the LORD had struck among them. The LORD also executed judgments on their gods."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The children of Israel traveled from Rameses, and encamped in Succoth."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They traveled from Succoth, and encamped in Etham, which is in the edge of the wilderness."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They traveled from Etham, and turned back to Pihahiroth, which is before Baal Zephon, and they encamped before Migdol."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They traveled from before Hahiroth, and crossed through the middle of the sea into the wilderness. They went three days\u2019 journey in the wilderness of Etham, and encamped in Marah."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They traveled from Marah, and came to Elim. In Elim, there were twelve springs of water and seventy palm trees, and they encamped there."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They traveled from Elim, and encamped by the Red Sea."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They traveled from the Red Sea, and encamped in the wilderness of Sin."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They traveled from the wilderness of Sin, and encamped in Dophkah."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They traveled from Dophkah, and encamped in Alush."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They traveled from Alush, and encamped in Rephidim, where there was no water for the people to drink."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They traveled from Rephidim, and encamped in the wilderness of Sinai."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They traveled from the wilderness of Sinai, and encamped in Kibroth Hattaavah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They traveled from Kibroth Hattaavah, and encamped in Hazeroth."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They traveled from Hazeroth, and encamped in Rithmah."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They traveled from Rithmah, and encamped in Rimmon Perez."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They traveled from Rimmon Perez, and encamped in Libnah."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They traveled from Libnah, and encamped in Rissah."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They traveled from Rissah, and encamped in Kehelathah."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They traveled from Kehelathah, and encamped in Mount Shepher."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They traveled from Mount Shepher, and encamped in Haradah."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They traveled from Haradah, and encamped in Makheloth."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They traveled from Makheloth, and encamped in Tahath."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They traveled from Tahath, and encamped in Terah."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They traveled from Terah, and encamped in Mithkah."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They traveled from Mithkah, and encamped in Hashmonah."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"They traveled from Hashmonah, and encamped in Moseroth."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They traveled from Moseroth, and encamped in Bene Jaakan."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They traveled from Bene Jaakan, and encamped in Hor Haggidgad."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They traveled from Hor Haggidgad, and encamped in Jotbathah."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"They traveled from Jotbathah, and encamped in Abronah."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"They traveled from Abronah, and encamped in Ezion Geber."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"They traveled from Ezion Geber, and encamped at Kadesh in the wilderness of Zin."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They traveled from Kadesh, and encamped in Mount Hor, in the edge of the land of Edom."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Aaron the priest went up into Mount Hor at the commandment of the LORD and died there, in the fortieth year after the children of Israel had come out of the land of Egypt, in the fifth month, on the first day of the month."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Aaron was one hundred twenty-three years old when he died in Mount Hor."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The Canaanite king of Arad, who lived in the South in the land of Canaan, heard of the coming of the children of Israel."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"They traveled from Mount Hor, and encamped in Zalmonah."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"They traveled from Zalmonah, and encamped in Punon."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"They traveled from Punon, and encamped in Oboth."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"They traveled from Oboth, and encamped in Iye Abarim, in the border of Moab."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"They traveled from Iyim, and encamped in Dibon Gad."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"They traveled from Dibon Gad, and encamped in Almon Diblathaim."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"They traveled from Almon Diblathaim, and encamped in the mountains of Abarim, before Nebo."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"They traveled from the mountains of Abarim, and encamped in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"They encamped by the Jordan, from Beth Jeshimoth even to Abel Shittim in the plains of Moab."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho, saying,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Speak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u201cWhen you pass over the Jordan into the land of Canaan,"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"then you shall drive out all the inhabitants of the land from before you, destroy all their stone idols, destroy all their molten images, and demolish all their high places."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"You shall take possession of the land, and dwell therein; for I have given the land to you to possess it."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"You shall inherit the land by lot according to your families; to the larger groups you shall give a larger inheritance, and to the smaller you shall give a smaller inheritance. Wherever the lot falls to any man, that shall be his. You shall inherit according to the tribes of your fathers."]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut if you do not drive out the inhabitants of the land from before you, then those you let remain of them will be like pricks in your eyes and thorns in your sides. They will harass you in the land in which you dwell."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"It shall happen that as I thought to do to them, so I will do to you.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cCommand the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When you come into the land of Canaan (this is the land that shall fall to you for an inheritance, even the land of Canaan according to its borders),"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"then your south quarter shall be from the wilderness of Zin along by the side of Edom, and your south border shall be from the end of the Salt Sea eastward."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Your border shall turn about southward of the ascent of Akrabbim, and pass along to Zin; and it shall pass southward of Kadesh Barnea; and it shall go from there to Hazar Addar, and pass along to Azmon."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The border shall turn about from Azmon to the brook of Egypt, and it shall end at the sea."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018For the western border, you shall have the great sea and its border. This shall be your west border."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This shall be your north border: from the great sea you shall mark out for yourselves Mount Hor."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"From Mount Hor you shall mark out to the entrance of Hamath; and the border shall pass by Zedad."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then the border shall go to Ziphron, and it shall end at Hazar Enan. This shall be your north border."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall mark out your east border from Hazar Enan to Shepham."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The border shall go down from Shepham to Riblah, on the east side of Ain. The border shall go down, and shall reach to the side of the sea of Chinnereth eastward."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The border shall go down to the Jordan, and end at the Salt Sea. This shall be your land according to its borders around it.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses commanded the children of Israel, saying, \u201cThis is the land which you shall inherit by lot, which the LORD has commanded to give to the nine tribes, and to the half-tribe;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"for the tribe of the children of Reuben according to their fathers\u2019 houses, the tribe of the children of Gad according to their fathers\u2019 houses, and the half-tribe of Manasseh have received their inheritance."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The two tribes and the half-tribe have received their inheritance beyond the Jordan at Jericho eastward, toward the sunrise.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u201cThese are the names of the men who shall divide the land to you for inheritance: Eleazar the priest, and Joshua the son of Nun."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall take one prince of every tribe, to divide the land for inheritance."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"These are the names of the men: Of the tribe of Judah, Caleb the son of Jephunneh."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of the children of Simeon, Shemuel the son of Ammihud."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of Benjamin, Elidad the son of Chislon."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of the children of Dan a prince, Bukki the son of Jogli."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Of the children of Joseph: of the tribe of the children of Manasseh a prince, Hanniel the son of Ephod."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of the children of Ephraim a prince, Kemuel the son of Shiphtan."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of the children of Zebulun a prince, Elizaphan the son of Parnach."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of the children of Issachar a prince, Paltiel the son of Azzan."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of the children of Asher a prince, Ahihud the son of Shelomi."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Of the tribe of the children of Naphtali a prince, Pedahel the son of Ammihud.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"These are they whom the LORD commanded to divide the inheritance to the children of Israel in the land of Canaan."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cCommand the children of Israel to give to the Levites cities to dwell in out of their inheritance. You shall give pasture lands for the cities around them to the Levites."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They shall have the cities to dwell in. Their pasture lands shall be for their livestock, and for their possessions, and for all their animals."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe pasture lands of the cities, which you shall give to the Levites, shall be from the wall of the city and outward one thousand cubits around it."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall measure outside of the city for the east side two thousand cubits, and for the south side two thousand cubits, and for the west side two thousand cubits, and for the north side two thousand cubits, the city being in the middle. This shall be the pasture lands of their cities."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe cities which you shall give to the Levites, they shall be the six cities of refuge, which you shall give for the man slayer to flee to. Besides them you shall give forty-two cities."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"All the cities which you shall give to the Levites shall be forty-eight cities together with their pasture lands."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Concerning the cities which you shall give of the possession of the children of Israel, from the many you shall take many, and from the few you shall take few. Everyone according to his inheritance which he inherits shall give some of his cities to the Levites.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, and tell them, \u2018When you pass over the Jordan into the land of Canaan,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"then you shall appoint for yourselves cities to be cities of refuge for you, that the man slayer who kills any person unwittingly may flee there."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The cities shall be for your refuge from the avenger, that the man slayer not die until he stands before the congregation for judgment."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The cities which you shall give shall be for you six cities of refuge."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall give three cities beyond the Jordan, and you shall give three cities in the land of Canaan. They shall be cities of refuge."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"These six cities shall be refuge for the children of Israel, for the stranger, and for the foreigner living among them, that everyone who kills any person unwittingly may flee there."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if he struck him with an instrument of iron, so that he died, he is a murderer. The murderer shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If he struck him with a stone in the hand, by which a man may die, and he died, he is a murderer. The murderer shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Or if he struck him with a weapon of wood in the hand, by which a man may die, and he died, he is a murderer. The murderer shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The avenger of blood shall himself put the murderer to death. When he meets him, he shall put him to death."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"If he shoved him out of hatred, or hurled something at him while lying in wait, so that he died,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"or in hostility struck him with his hand, so that he died, he who struck him shall surely be put to death. He is a murderer. The avenger of blood shall put the murderer to death when he meets him."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if he shoved him suddenly without hostility, or hurled on him anything without lying in wait,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"or with any stone, by which a man may die, not seeing him, and cast it on him so that he died, and he was not his enemy and not seeking his harm,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"then the congregation shall judge between the striker and the avenger of blood according to these ordinances."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The congregation shall deliver the man slayer out of the hand of the avenger of blood, and the congregation shall restore him to his city of refuge, where he had fled. He shall dwell therein until the death of the high priest, who was anointed with the holy oil."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if the man slayer shall at any time go beyond the border of his city of refuge where he flees,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and the avenger of blood finds him outside of the border of his city of refuge, and the avenger of blood kills the man slayer, he shall not be guilty of blood,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"because he should have remained in his city of refuge until the death of the high priest. But after the death of the high priest, the man slayer shall return into the land of his possession."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018These things shall be for a statute and ordinance to you throughout your generations in all your dwellings."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Whoever kills any person, the murderer shall be slain based on the testimony of witnesses; but one witness shall not testify alone against any person so that he dies."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Moreover you shall take no ransom for the life of a murderer who is guilty of death. He shall surely be put to death."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You shall take no ransom for him who has fled to his city of refuge, that he may come again to dwell in the land before the death of the priest."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018So you shall not pollute the land where you live; for blood pollutes the land. No atonement can be made for the land for the blood that is shed in it, but by the blood of him who shed it."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"You shall not defile the land which you inhabit, where I dwell; for I, the LORD, dwell among the children of Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The heads of the fathers\u2019 households of the family of the children of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, of the families of the sons of Joseph, came near and spoke before Moses and before the princes, the heads of the fathers\u2019 households of the children of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThe LORD commanded my lord to give the land for inheritance by lot to the children of Israel. My lord was commanded by the LORD to give the inheritance of Zelophehad our brother to his daughters."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If they are married to any of the sons of the other tribes of the children of Israel, then their inheritance will be taken away from the inheritance of our fathers, and will be added to the inheritance of the tribe to which they shall belong. So it will be taken away from the lot of our inheritance."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When the jubilee of the children of Israel comes, then their inheritance will be added to the inheritance of the tribe to which they shall belong. So their inheritance will be taken away from the inheritance of the tribe of our fathers.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses commanded the children of Israel according to the LORD\u2019s word, saying, \u201cThe tribe of the sons of Joseph speak what is right."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"This is the thing which the LORD commands concerning the daughters of Zelophehad, saying, \u2018Let them be married to whom they think best, only they shall marry into the family of the tribe of their father."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So shall no inheritance of the children of Israel move from tribe to tribe; for the children of Israel shall all keep the inheritance of the tribe of his fathers."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Every daughter who possesses an inheritance in any tribe of the children of Israel shall be wife to one of the family of the tribe of her father, that the children of Israel may each possess the inheritance of his fathers."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So shall no inheritance move from one tribe to another tribe; for the tribes of the children of Israel shall each keep his own inheritance.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The daughters of Zelophehad did as the LORD commanded Moses:"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"for Mahlah, Tirzah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Noah, the daughters of Zelophehad, were married to their father\u2019s brothers\u2019 sons."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They were married into the families of the sons of Manasseh the son of Joseph. Their inheritance remained in the tribe of the family of their father."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the commandments and the ordinances which the LORD commanded by Moses to the children of Israel in the plains of Moab by the Jordan at Jericho."]]}]]}},1275,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,h,a,s,n){a.exports={book:"Deut",name:"Deuteronomy",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the words which Moses spoke to all Israel beyond the Jordan in the wilderness, in the Arabah opposite Suf, between Paran, Tophel, Laban, Hazeroth, and Dizahab."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It is eleven days\u2019 journey from Horeb by the way of Mount Seir to Kadesh Barnea."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In the fortieth year, in the eleventh month, on the first day of the month, Moses spoke to the children of Israel according to all that the LORD had given him in commandment to them,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"after he had struck Sihon the king of the Amorites who lived in Heshbon, and Og the king of Bashan who lived in Ashtaroth, at Edrei."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Beyond the Jordan, in the land of Moab, Moses began to declare this law, saying,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD our God spoke to us in Horeb, saying, \u2018You have lived long enough at this mountain."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Turn, and take your journey, and go to the hill country of the Amorites and to all the places near there: in the Arabah, in the hill country, in the lowland, in the South, by the seashore, in the land of the Canaanites, and in Lebanon as far as the great river, the river Euphrates."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, I have set the land before you. Go in and possess the land which the LORD swore to your fathers\u2014to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob\u2014to give to them and to their offspring after them.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection.","or, seed"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"I spoke to you at that time, saying, \u201cI am not able to bear you myself alone."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD your God has multiplied you, and behold, you are today as the stars of the sky for multitude."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"May the LORD, the God of your fathers, make you a thousand times as many as you are and bless you, as he has promised you!"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"How can I myself alone bear your problems, your burdens, and your strife?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Take wise men of understanding who are respected among your tribes, and I will make them heads over you.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"You answered me, and said, \u201cThe thing which you have spoken is good to do.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So I took the heads of your tribes, wise and respected men, and made them heads over you, captains of thousands, captains of hundreds, captains of fifties, captains of tens, and officers, according to your tribes."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I commanded your judges at that time, saying, \u201cHear cases between your brothers and judge righteously between a man and his brother, and the foreigner who is living with him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall not show partiality in judgment; you shall hear the small and the great alike. You shall not be afraid of the face of man, for the judgment is God\u2019s. The case that is too hard for you, you shall bring to me, and I will hear it.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I commanded you at that time all the things which you should do."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"We traveled from Horeb and went through all that great and terrible wilderness which you saw, by the way to the hill country of the Amorites, as the LORD our God commanded us; and we came to Kadesh Barnea."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"I said to you, \u201cYou have come to the hill country of the Amorites, which the LORD our God gives to us."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Behold, the LORD your God has set the land before you. Go up, take possession, as the LORD the God of your fathers has spoken to you. Don\u2019t be afraid, neither be dismayed.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"You came near to me, everyone of you, and said, \u201cLet\u2019s send men before us, that they may search the land for us, and bring back to us word of the way by which we must go up, and the cities to which we shall come.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The thing pleased me well. I took twelve of your men, one man for every tribe."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They turned and went up into the hill country, and came to the valley of Eshcol, and spied it out."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They took some of the fruit of the land in their hands and brought it down to us, and brought us word again, and said, \u201cIt is a good land which the LORD our God gives to us.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Yet you wouldn\u2019t go up, but rebelled against the commandment of the LORD your God."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"You murmured in your tents, and said, \u201cBecause the LORD hated us, he has brought us out of the land of Egypt, to deliver us into the hand of the Amorites to destroy us."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Where are we going up? Our brothers have made our heart melt, saying, \u2018The people are greater and taller than we. The cities are great and fortified up to the sky. Moreover we have seen the sons of the Anakim there!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said to you, \u201cDon\u2019t be terrified. Don\u2019t be afraid of them."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The LORD your God, who goes before you, he will fight for you, according to all that he did for you in Egypt before your eyes,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and in the wilderness where you have seen how that the LORD your God carried you, as a man carries his son, in all the way that you went, until you came to this place.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Yet in this thing you didn\u2019t believe the LORD your God,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"who went before you on the way, to seek out a place for you to pitch your tents in: in fire by night, to show you by what way you should go, and in the cloud by day."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The LORD heard the voice of your words and was angry, and swore, saying,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"\u201cSurely not one of these men of this evil generation shall see the good land which I swore to give to your fathers,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"except Caleb the son of Jephunneh. He shall see it. I will give the land that he has trodden on to him and to his children, because he has wholly followed the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Also the LORD was angry with me for your sakes, saying, \u201cYou also shall not go in there."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Joshua the son of Nun, who stands before you, shall go in there. Encourage him, for he shall cause Israel to inherit it."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Moreover your little ones, whom you said would be captured or killed, your children, who today have no knowledge of good or evil, shall go in there. I will give it to them, and they shall possess it."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"But as for you, turn, and take your journey into the wilderness by the way to the Red Sea.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Then you answered and said to me, \u201cWe have sinned against the LORD. We will go up and fight, according to all that the LORD our God commanded us.\u201d Every man of you put on his weapons of war, and presumed to go up into the hill country."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cTell them, \u2018Don\u2019t go up and don\u2019t fight; for I am not among you, lest you be struck before your enemies.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"So I spoke to you, and you didn\u2019t listen; but you rebelled against the commandment of the LORD, and were presumptuous, and went up into the hill country."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The Amorites, who lived in that hill country, came out against you and chased you as bees do, and beat you down in Seir, even to Hormah."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"You returned and wept before the LORD, but the LORD didn\u2019t listen to your voice, nor turn his ear to you."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"So you stayed in Kadesh many days, according to the days that you remained."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then we turned, and took our journey into the wilderness by the way to the Red Sea, as the LORD spoke to me; and we encircled Mount Seir many days."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to me, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cYou have encircled this mountain long enough. Turn northward."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Command the people, saying, \u2018You are to pass through the border of your brothers, the children of Esau, who dwell in Seir; and they will be afraid of you. Therefore be careful."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t contend with them; for I will not give you any of their land, no, not so much as for the sole of the foot to tread on, because I have given Mount Seir to Esau for a possession."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall purchase food from them for money, that you may eat. You shall also buy water from them for money, that you may drink.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God has blessed you in all the work of your hands. He has known your walking through this great wilderness. These forty years, the LORD your God has been with you. You have lacked nothing."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So we passed by from our brothers, the children of Esau, who dwell in Seir, from the way of the Arabah from Elath and from Ezion Geber. We turned and passed by the way of the wilderness of Moab."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cDon\u2019t bother Moab, neither contend with them in battle; for I will not give you any of his land for a possession, because I have given Ar to the children of Lot for a possession.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"(The Emim lived there before, a great and numerous people, and tall as the Anakim."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"These also are considered to be Rephaim, as the Anakim; but the Moabites call them Emim."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The Horites also lived in Seir in the past, but the children of Esau succeeded them. They destroyed them from before them, and lived in their place, as Israel did to the land of his possession, which the LORD gave to them.)"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow rise up and cross over the brook Zered.\u201d We went over the brook Zered."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The days in which we came from Kadesh Barnea until we had come over the brook Zered were thirty-eight years, until all the generation of the men of war were consumed from the middle of the camp, as the LORD swore to them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s hand was against them, to destroy them from the middle of the camp, until they were consumed."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So, when all the men of war were consumed and dead from among the people,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the LORD spoke to me, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cYou are to pass over Ar, the border of Moab, today."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When you come near the border of the children of Ammon, don\u2019t bother them, nor contend with them; for I will not give you any of the land of the children of Ammon for a possession, because I have given it to the children of Lot for a possession.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"(That also is considered a land of Rephaim. Rephaim lived there in the past, but the Ammonites call them Zamzummim,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"a great people, many, and tall, as the Anakim; but the LORD destroyed them from before Israel, and they succeeded them, and lived in their place,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"as he did for the children of Esau who dwell in Seir, when he destroyed the Horites from before them; and they succeeded them, and lived in their place even to this day."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then the Avvim, who lived in villages as far as Gaza: the Caphtorim, who came out of Caphtor, destroyed them and lived in their place.)"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cRise up, take your journey, and pass over the valley of the Arnon. Behold, I have given into your hand Sihon the Amorite, king of Heshbon, and his land; begin to possess it, and contend with him in battle."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Today I will begin to put the dread of you and the fear of you on the peoples who are under the whole sky, who shall hear the report of you, and shall tremble and be in anguish because of you.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"I sent messengers out of the wilderness of Kedemoth to Sihon king of Heshbon with words of peace, saying,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"\u201cLet me pass through your land. I will go along by the highway. I will turn neither to the right hand nor to the left."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You shall sell me food for money, that I may eat; and give me water for money, that I may drink. Just let me pass through on my feet,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"as the children of Esau who dwell in Seir, and the Moabites who dwell in Ar, did to me, until I pass over the Jordan into the land which the LORD our God gives us.\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But Sihon king of Heshbon would not let us pass by him, for the LORD your God hardened his spirit and made his heart obstinate, that he might deliver him into your hand, as it is today."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cBehold, I have begun to deliver up Sihon and his land before you. Begin to possess, that you may inherit his land.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Then Sihon came out against us, he and all his people, to battle at Jahaz."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The LORD our God delivered him up before us; and we struck him, his sons, and all his people."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"We took all his cities at that time, and utterly destroyed every inhabited city, with the women and the little ones. We left no one remaining."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Only the livestock we took for plunder for ourselves, with the plunder of the cities which we had taken."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"From Aroer, which is on the edge of the valley of the Arnon, and the city that is in the valley, even to Gilead, there was not a city too high for us. The LORD our God delivered up all before us."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Only to the land of the children of Ammon you didn\u2019t come near: all the banks of the river Jabbok, and the cities of the hill country, and wherever the LORD our God forbade us."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then we turned, and went up the way to Bashan. Og the king of Bashan came out against us, he and all his people, to battle at Edrei."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cDon\u2019t fear him; for I have delivered him, with all his people and his land, into your hand. You shall do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived at Heshbon.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"So the LORD our God also delivered into our hand Og, the king of Bashan, and all his people. We struck him until no one was left to him remaining."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"We took all his cities at that time. There was not a city which we didn\u2019t take from them: sixty cities, all the region of Argob, the kingdom of Og in Bashan."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All these were cities fortified with high walls, gates, and bars, in addition to a great many villages without walls."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"We utterly destroyed them, as we did to Sihon king of Heshbon, utterly destroying every inhabited city, with the women and the little ones."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But all the livestock, and the plunder of the cities, we took for plunder for ourselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"We took the land at that time out of the hand of the two kings of the Amorites who were beyond the Jordan, from the valley of the Arnon to Mount Hermon."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"(The Sidonians call Hermon Sirion, and the Amorites call it Senir.)"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"We took all the cities of the plain, and all Gilead, and all Bashan, to Salecah and Edrei, cities of the kingdom of Og in Bashan."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"(For only Og king of Bashan remained of the remnant of the Rephaim. Behold, his bedstead was a bedstead of iron. Isn\u2019t it in Rabbah of the children of Ammon? Nine cubits was its length, and four cubits its width, after the cubit of a man.)"]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:12,l:[[0,"This land we took in possession at that time: from Aroer, which is by the valley of the Arnon, and half the hill country of Gilead with its cities, I gave to the Reubenites and to the Gadites;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and the rest of Gilead, and all Bashan, the kingdom of Og, I gave to the half-tribe of Manasseh\u2014all the region of Argob, even all Bashan. (The same is called the land of Rephaim."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Jair the son of Manasseh took all the region of Argob, to the border of the Geshurites and the Maacathites, and called them, even Bashan, after his own name, Havvoth Jair, to this day.)"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I gave Gilead to Machir."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"To the Reubenites and to the Gadites I gave from Gilead even to the valley of the Arnon, the middle of the valley, and its border, even to the river Jabbok, which is the border of the children of Ammon;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the Arabah also, and the Jordan and its border, from Chinnereth even to the sea of the Arabah, the Salt Sea, under the slopes of Pisgah eastward."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"I commanded you at that time, saying, \u201cThe LORD your God has given you this land to possess it. All of you men of valor shall pass over armed before your brothers, the children of Israel."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But your wives, and your little ones, and your livestock, (I know that you have much livestock), shall live in your cities which I have given you,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"until the LORD gives rest to your brothers, as to you, and they also possess the land which the LORD your God gives them beyond the Jordan. Then you shall each return to his own possession, which I have given you.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"I commanded Joshua at that time, saying, \u201cYour eyes have seen all that the LORD your God has done to these two kings. So shall the LORD do to all the kingdoms where you go over."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall not fear them; for the LORD your God himself fights for you.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"I begged GOD at that time, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cLord GOD, you have begun to show your servant your greatness, and your strong hand. For what god is there in heaven or in earth that can do works like yours, and mighty acts like yours?"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Please let me go over and see the good land that is beyond the Jordan, that fine mountain, and Lebanon.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"But the LORD was angry with me because of you, and didn\u2019t listen to me. The LORD said to me, \u201cThat is enough! Speak no more to me of this matter."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Go up to the top of Pisgah, and lift up your eyes westward, and northward, and southward, and eastward, and see with your eyes; for you shall not go over this Jordan."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But commission Joshua, and encourage him, and strengthen him; for he shall go over before this people, and he shall cause them to inherit the land which you shall see.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"So we stayed in the valley near Beth Peor."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now, Israel, listen to the statutes and to the ordinances which I teach you, to do them, that you may live and go in and possess the land which the LORD, the God of your fathers, gives you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall not add to the word which I command you, neither shall you take away from it, that you may keep the commandments of the LORD your God which I command you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Your eyes have seen what the LORD did because of Baal Peor; for the LORD your God has destroyed all the men who followed Baal Peor from among you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But you who were faithful to the LORD your God are all alive today."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Behold, I have taught you statutes and ordinances, even as the LORD my God commanded me, that you should do so in the middle of the land where you go in to possess it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Keep therefore and do them; for this is your wisdom and your understanding in the sight of the peoples who shall hear all these statutes and say, \u201cSurely this great nation is a wise and understanding people.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For what great nation is there that has a god so near to them as the LORD our God is whenever we call on him?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"What great nation is there that has statutes and ordinances so righteous as all this law which I set before you today?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Only be careful, and keep your soul diligently, lest you forget the things which your eyes saw, and lest they depart from your heart all the days of your life; but make them known to your children and your children\u2019s children\u2014"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"the day that you stood before the LORD your God in Horeb, when the LORD said to me, \u201cAssemble the people to me, and I will make them hear my words, that they may learn to fear me all the days that they live on the earth, and that they may teach their children.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You came near and stood under the mountain. The mountain burned with fire to the heart of the sky, with darkness, cloud, and thick darkness."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to you out of the middle of the fire: you heard the voice of words, but you saw no form; you only heard a voice."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He declared to you his covenant, which he commanded you to perform, even the ten commandments. He wrote them on two stone tablets."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The LORD commanded me at that time to teach you statutes and ordinances, that you might do them in the land where you go over to possess it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Be very careful, for you saw no kind of form on the day that the LORD spoke to you in Horeb out of the middle of the fire,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"lest you corrupt yourselves, and make yourself a carved image in the form of any figure, the likeness of male or female,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the likeness of any animal that is on the earth, the likeness of any winged bird that flies in the sky,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"the likeness of anything that creeps on the ground, the likeness of any fish that is in the water under the earth;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and lest you lift up your eyes to the sky, and when you see the sun and the moon and the stars, even all the army of the sky, you are drawn away and worship them, and serve them, which the LORD your God has allotted to all the peoples under the whole sky."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But the LORD has taken you, and brought you out of the iron furnace, out of Egypt, to be to him a people of inheritance, as it is today."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Furthermore the LORD was angry with me for your sakes, and swore that I should not go over the Jordan, and that I should not go in to that good land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"but I must die in this land. I must not go over the Jordan, but you shall go over and possess that good land."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Be careful, lest you forget the covenant of the LORD your God, which he made with you, and make yourselves a carved image in the form of anything which the LORD your God has forbidden you."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God is a devouring fire, a jealous God."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When you father children and children\u2019s children, and you have been long in the land, and then corrupt yourselves, and make a carved image in the form of anything, and do that which is evil in the LORD your God\u2019s sight to provoke him to anger,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I call heaven and earth to witness against you today, that you will soon utterly perish from off the land which you go over the Jordan to possess it. You will not prolong your days on it, but will utterly be destroyed."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The LORD will scatter you among the peoples, and you will be left few in number among the nations where the LORD will lead you away."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"There you will serve gods, the work of men\u2019s hands, wood and stone, which neither see, nor hear, nor eat, nor smell."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But from there you shall seek the LORD your God, and you will find him when you search after him with all your heart and with all your soul."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When you are in oppression, and all these things have come on you, in the latter days you shall return to the LORD your God and listen to his voice."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God is a merciful God. He will not fail you nor destroy you, nor forget the covenant of your fathers which he swore to them."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For ask now of the days that are past, which were before you, since the day that God created man on the earth, and from the one end of the sky to the other, whether there has been anything as great as this thing is, or has been heard like it?"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Did a people ever hear the voice of God speaking out of the middle of the fire, as you have heard, and live?"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Or has God tried to go and take a nation for himself from among another nation, by trials, by signs, by wonders, by war, by a mighty hand, by an outstretched arm, and by great terrors, according to all that the LORD your God did for you in Egypt before your eyes?"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"It was shown to you so that you might know that the LORD is God. There is no one else besides him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Out of heaven he made you to hear his voice, that he might instruct you. On earth he made you to see his great fire; and you heard his words out of the middle of the fire."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Because he loved your fathers, therefore he chose their offspring after them, and brought you out with his presence, with his great power, out of Egypt;"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"to drive out nations from before you greater and mightier than you, to bring you in, to give you their land for an inheritance, as it is today."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Know therefore today, and take it to heart, that the LORD himself is God in heaven above and on the earth beneath. There is no one else."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"You shall keep his statutes and his commandments which I command you today, that it may go well with you and with your children after you, and that you may prolong your days in the land which the LORD your God gives you for all time."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Moses set apart three cities beyond the Jordan toward the sunrise,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"that the man slayer might flee there, who kills his neighbor unintentionally and didn\u2019t hate him in time past, and that fleeing to one of these cities he might live:"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Bezer in the wilderness, in the plain country, for the Reubenites; and Ramoth in Gilead for the Gadites; and Golan in Bashan for the Manassites."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the law which Moses set before the children of Israel."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"These are the testimonies, and the statutes, and the ordinances which Moses spoke to the children of Israel when they came out of Egypt,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"beyond the Jordan, in the valley opposite Beth Peor, in the land of Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived at Heshbon, whom Moses and the children of Israel struck when they came out of Egypt."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"They took possession of his land and the land of Og king of Bashan, the two kings of the Amorites, who were beyond the Jordan toward the sunrise;"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"from Aroer, which is on the edge of the valley of the Arnon, even to Mount Siyon (also called Hermon),"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"and all the Arabah beyond the Jordan eastward, even to the sea of the Arabah, under the slopes of Pisgah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses called to all Israel, and said to them, \u201cHear, Israel, the statutes and the ordinances which I speak in your ears today, that you may learn them, and observe to do them.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD our God made a covenant with us in Horeb."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD didn\u2019t make this covenant with our fathers, but with us, even us, who are all of us here alive today."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke with you face to face on the mountain out of the middle of the fire,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"(I stood between the LORD and you at that time, to show you the LORD\u2019s word; for you were afraid because of the fire, and didn\u2019t go up onto the mountain) saying,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI am the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall have no other gods before me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not make a carved image for yourself\u2014any likeness of what is in heaven above, or what is on the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall not bow yourself down to them, nor serve them, for I, the LORD your God, am a jealous God, visiting the iniquity of the fathers on the children and on the third and on the fourth generation of those who hate me"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and showing loving kindness to thousands of those who love me and keep my commandments."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not misuse the name of the LORD your God; for the LORD will not hold him guiltless who misuses his name."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah.","or, You shall not take the name of the LORD your God in vain;"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cObserve the Sabbath day, to keep it holy, as the LORD your God commanded you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall labor six days, and do all your work;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but the seventh day is a Sabbath to the LORD your God, in which you shall not do any work\u2014neither you, nor your son, nor your daughter, nor your male servant, nor your female servant, nor your ox, nor your donkey, nor any of your livestock, nor your stranger who is within your gates; that your male servant and your female servant may rest as well as you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall remember that you were a servant in the land of Egypt, and the LORD your God brought you out of there by a mighty hand and by an outstretched arm. Therefore the LORD your God commanded you to keep the Sabbath day."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHonor your father and your mother, as the LORD your God commanded you, that your days may be long and that it may go well with you in the land which the LORD your God gives you."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not murder."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not commit adultery."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not steal."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not give false testimony against your neighbor."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not covet your neighbor\u2019s wife. Neither shall you desire your neighbor\u2019s house, his field, or his male servant, or his female servant, his ox, or his donkey, or anything that is your neighbor\u2019s.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke these words to all your assembly on the mountain out of the middle of the fire, of the cloud, and of the thick darkness, with a great voice. He added no more. He wrote them on two stone tablets, and gave them to me."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When you heard the voice out of the middle of the darkness, while the mountain was burning with fire, you came near to me, even all the heads of your tribes, and your elders;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and you said, \u201cBehold, the LORD our God has shown us his glory and his greatness, and we have heard his voice out of the middle of the fire. We have seen today that God does speak with man, and he lives."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now therefore, why should we die? For this great fire will consume us. If we hear the LORD our God\u2019s voice any more, then we shall die."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For who is there of all flesh who has heard the voice of the living God speaking out of the middle of the fire, as we have, and lived?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Go near, and hear all that the LORD our God shall say, and tell us all that the LORD our God tells you; and we will hear it, and do it.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD heard the voice of your words when you spoke to me; and the LORD said to me, \u201cI have heard the voice of the words of this people which they have spoken to you. They have well said all that they have spoken."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Oh that there were such a heart in them that they would fear me and keep all my commandments always, that it might be well with them and with their children forever!"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cGo tell them, \u2018Return to your tents.\u2019"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But as for you, stand here by me, and I will tell you all the commandments, and the statutes, and the ordinances, which you shall teach them, that they may do them in the land which I give them to possess.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall observe to do therefore as the LORD your God has commanded you. You shall not turn away to the right hand or to the left."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"You shall walk in all the way which the LORD your God has commanded you, that you may live and that it may be well with you, and that you may prolong your days in the land which you shall possess."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the commandments, the statutes, and the ordinances, which the LORD your God commanded to teach you, that you might do them in the land that you go over to possess;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that you might fear the LORD your God, to keep all his statutes and his commandments, which I command you\u2014you, your son, and your son\u2019s son, all the days of your life; and that your days may be prolonged."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Hear therefore, Israel, and observe to do it, that it may be well with you, and that you may increase mightily, as the LORD, the God of your fathers, has promised to you, in a land flowing with milk and honey."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Hear, Israel: The LORD is our God. The LORD is one."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall love the LORD your God with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all your might."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"These words, which I command you today, shall be on your heart;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and you shall teach them diligently to your children, and shall talk of them when you sit in your house, and when you walk by the way, and when you lie down, and when you rise up."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall bind them for a sign on your hand, and they shall be for frontlets between your eyes."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall write them on the door posts of your house and on your gates."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall be, when the LORD your God brings you into the land which he swore to your fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, to give you\u2013a land with great and good cities which you didn\u2019t build,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and houses full of all good things which you didn\u2019t fill, and cisterns dug out which you didn\u2019t dig, vineyards and olive trees which you didn\u2019t plant, and you shall eat and be full;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"then beware lest you forget the LORD, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall fear the LORD your God; and you shall serve him, and shall swear by his name."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall not go after other gods, of the gods of the peoples who are around you,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"for the LORD your God among you is a jealous God, lest the anger of the LORD your God be kindled against you, and he destroy you from off the face of the earth."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall not tempt the LORD your God, as you tempted him in Massah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You shall diligently keep the commandments of the LORD your God, and his testimonies, and his statutes, which he has commanded you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall do that which is right and good in the LORD\u2019s sight, that it may be well with you and that you may go in and possess the good land which the LORD swore to your fathers,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"to thrust out all your enemies from before you, as the LORD has spoken."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When your son asks you in time to come, saying, \u201cWhat do the testimonies, the statutes, and the ordinances, which the LORD our God has commanded you mean?\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"then you shall tell your son, \u201cWe were Pharaoh\u2019s slaves in Egypt. The LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and the LORD showed great and awesome signs and wonders on Egypt, on Pharaoh, and on all his house, before our eyes;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and he brought us out from there, that he might bring us in, to give us the land which he swore to our fathers."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The LORD commanded us to do all these statutes, to fear the LORD our God, for our good always, that he might preserve us alive, as we are today."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"It shall be righteousness to us, if we observe to do all these commandments before the LORD our God, as he has commanded us.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD your God brings you into the land where you go to possess it, and casts out many nations before you\u2014the Hittite, the Girgashite, the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite\u2014seven nations greater and mightier than you;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and when the LORD your God delivers them up before you, and you strike them, then you shall utterly destroy them. You shall make no covenant with them, nor show mercy to them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall not make marriages with them. You shall not give your daughter to his son, nor shall you take his daughter for your son."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For that would turn away your sons from following me, that they may serve other gods. So the LORD\u2019s anger would be kindled against you, and he would destroy you quickly."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But you shall deal with them like this: you shall break down their altars, dash their pillars in pieces, cut down their Asherah poles, and burn their engraved images with fire."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For you are a holy people to the LORD your God. The LORD your God has chosen you to be a people for his own possession, above all peoples who are on the face of the earth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD didn\u2019t set his love on you nor choose you, because you were more in number than any people; for you were the fewest of all peoples;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but because the LORD loves you, and because he desires to keep the oath which he swore to your fathers, the LORD has brought you out with a mighty hand and redeemed you out of the house of bondage, from the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Know therefore that the LORD your God himself is God, the faithful God, who keeps covenant and loving kindness to a thousand generations with those who love him and keep his commandments,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and repays those who hate him to their face, to destroy them. He will not be slack to him who hates him. He will repay him to his face."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall therefore keep the commandments, the statutes, and the ordinances which I command you today, to do them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It shall happen, because you listen to these ordinances and keep and do them, that the LORD your God will keep with you the covenant and the loving kindness which he swore to your fathers."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He will love you, bless you, and multiply you. He will also bless the fruit of your body and the fruit of your ground, your grain and your new wine and your oil, the increase of your livestock and the young of your flock, in the land which he swore to your fathers to give you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You will be blessed above all peoples. There won\u2019t be male or female barren among you, or among your livestock."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The LORD will take away from you all sickness; and he will put none of the evil diseases of Egypt, which you know, on you, but will lay them on all those who hate you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall consume all the peoples whom the LORD your God shall deliver to you. Your eye shall not pity them. You shall not serve their gods; for that would be a snare to you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If you shall say in your heart, \u201cThese nations are more than I; how can I dispossess them?\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"you shall not be afraid of them. You shall remember well what the LORD your God did to Pharaoh and to all Egypt:"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the great trials which your eyes saw, the signs, the wonders, the mighty hand, and the outstretched arm, by which the LORD your God brought you out. So shall the LORD your God do to all the peoples of whom you are afraid."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD your God will send the hornet among them, until those who are left, and hide themselves, perish from before you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You shall not be scared of them; for the LORD your God is among you, a great and awesome God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The LORD your God will cast out those nations before you little by little. You may not consume them at once, lest the animals of the field increase on you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But the LORD your God will deliver them up before you, and will confuse them with a great confusion, until they are destroyed."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He will deliver their kings into your hand, and you shall make their name perish from under the sky. No one will be able to stand before you until you have destroyed them."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You shall burn the engraved images of their gods with fire. You shall not covet the silver or the gold that is on them, nor take it for yourself, lest you be snared in it; for it is an abomination to the LORD your God."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall not bring an abomination into your house and become a devoted thing like it. You shall utterly detest it. You shall utterly abhor it; for it is a devoted thing."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall observe to do all the commandments which I command you today, that you may live, and multiply, and go in and possess the land which the LORD swore to your fathers."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall remember all the way which the LORD your God has led you these forty years in the wilderness, that he might humble you, to test you, to know what was in your heart, whether you would keep his commandments or not."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He humbled you, allowed you to be hungry, and fed you with manna, which you didn\u2019t know, neither did your fathers know, that he might teach you that man does not live by bread only, but man lives by every word that proceeds out of the LORD\u2019s mouth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Your clothing didn\u2019t grow old on you, neither did your foot swell, these forty years."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall consider in your heart that as a man disciplines his son, so the LORD your God disciplines you."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall keep the commandments of the LORD your God, to walk in his ways, and to fear him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God brings you into a good land, a land of brooks of water, of springs, and underground water flowing into valleys and hills;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"a land of wheat, barley, vines, fig trees, and pomegranates; a land of olive trees and honey;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"a land in which you shall eat bread without scarcity, you shall not lack anything in it; a land whose stones are iron, and out of whose hills you may dig copper."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall eat and be full, and you shall bless the LORD your God for the good land which he has given you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Beware lest you forget the LORD your God, in not keeping his commandments, his ordinances, and his statutes, which I command you today;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"lest, when you have eaten and are full, and have built fine houses and lived in them;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and when your herds and your flocks multiply, and your silver and your gold is multiplied, and all that you have is multiplied;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"then your heart might be lifted up, and you forget the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"who led you through the great and terrible wilderness, with venomous snakes and scorpions, and thirsty ground where there was no water; who poured water for you out of the rock of flint;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"who fed you in the wilderness with manna, which your fathers didn\u2019t know, that he might humble you, and that he might prove you, to do you good at your latter end;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and lest you say in your heart, \u201cMy power and the might of my hand has gotten me this wealth.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But you shall remember the LORD your God, for it is he who gives you power to get wealth, that he may establish his covenant which he swore to your fathers, as it is today."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall be, if you shall forget the LORD your God, and walk after other gods, and serve them and worship them, I testify against you today that you shall surely perish."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As the nations that the LORD makes to perish before you, so you shall perish, because you wouldn\u2019t listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hear, Israel! You are to pass over the Jordan today, to go in to dispossess nations greater and mightier than yourself, cities great and fortified up to the sky,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"a people great and tall, the sons of the Anakim, whom you know, and of whom you have heard say, \u201cWho can stand before the sons of Anak?\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Know therefore today that the LORD your God is he who goes over before you as a devouring fire. He will destroy them and he will bring them down before you. So you shall drive them out and make them perish quickly, as the LORD has spoken to you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t say in your heart, after the LORD your God has thrust them out from before you, \u201cFor my righteousness the LORD has brought me in to possess this land;\u201d because the LORD drives them out before you because of the wickedness of these nations."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Not for your righteousness or for the uprightness of your heart do you go in to possess their land; but for the wickedness of these nations the LORD your God does drive them out from before you, and that he may establish the word which the LORD swore to your fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Know therefore that the LORD your God doesn\u2019t give you this good land to possess for your righteousness, for you are a stiff-necked people."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Remember, and don\u2019t forget, how you provoked the LORD your God to wrath in the wilderness. From the day that you left the land of Egypt until you came to this place, you have been rebellious against the LORD."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Also in Horeb you provoked the LORD to wrath, and the LORD was angry with you to destroy you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When I had gone up onto the mountain to receive the stone tablets, even the tablets of the covenant which the LORD made with you, then I stayed on the mountain forty days and forty nights. I neither ate bread nor drank water."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD delivered to me the two stone tablets written with God\u2019s finger. On them were all the words which the LORD spoke with you on the mountain out of the middle of the fire in the day of the assembly."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass at the end of forty days and forty nights that the LORD gave me the two stone tablets, even the tablets of the covenant."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cArise, get down quickly from here; for your people whom you have brought out of Egypt have corrupted themselves. They have quickly turned away from the way which I commanded them. They have made a molten image for themselves!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Furthermore the LORD spoke to me, saying, \u201cI have seen these people, and behold, they are a stiff-necked people."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Leave me alone, that I may destroy them, and blot out their name from under the sky; and I will make of you a nation mightier and greater than they.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"So I turned and came down from the mountain, and the mountain was burning with fire. The two tablets of the covenant were in my two hands."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I looked, and behold, you had sinned against the LORD your God. You had made yourselves a molded calf. You had quickly turned away from the way which the LORD had commanded you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I took hold of the two tablets, and threw them out of my two hands, and broke them before your eyes."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I fell down before the LORD, as at the first, forty days and forty nights. I neither ate bread nor drank water, because of all your sin which you sinned, in doing that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, to provoke him to anger."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For I was afraid of the anger and hot displeasure with which the LORD was angry against you to destroy you. But the LORD listened to me that time also."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD was angry enough with Aaron to destroy him. I prayed for Aaron also at the same time."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I took your sin, the calf which you had made, and burned it with fire, and crushed it, grinding it very small, until it was as fine as dust. I threw its dust into the brook that descended out of the mountain."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"At Taberah, at Massah, and at Kibroth Hattaavah you provoked the LORD to wrath."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When the LORD sent you from Kadesh Barnea, saying, \u201cGo up and possess the land which I have given you,\u201d you rebelled against the commandment of the LORD your God, and you didn\u2019t believe him or listen to his voice."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You have been rebellious against the LORD from the day that I knew you."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"So I fell down before the LORD the forty days and forty nights that I fell down, because the LORD had said he would destroy you."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I prayed to the LORD, and said, \u201cLord GOD, don\u2019t destroy your people and your inheritance that you have redeemed through your greatness, that you have brought out of Egypt with a mighty hand."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Remember your servants, Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob. Don\u2019t look at the stubbornness of this people, nor at their wickedness, nor at their sin,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"lest the land you brought us out from say, \u2018Because the LORD was not able to bring them into the land which he promised to them, and because he hated them, he has brought them out to kill them in the wilderness.\u2019"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Yet they are your people and your inheritance, which you brought out by your great power and by your outstretched arm.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time the LORD said to me, \u201cCut two stone tablets like the first, and come up to me onto the mountain, and make an ark of wood."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will write on the tablets the words that were on the first tablets which you broke, and you shall put them in the ark.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So I made an ark of acacia wood, and cut two stone tablets like the first, and went up onto the mountain, having the two tablets in my hand."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He wrote on the tablets, according to the first writing, the ten commandments, which the LORD spoke to you on the mountain out of the middle of the fire in the day of the assembly; and the LORD gave them to me."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I turned and came down from the mountain, and put the tablets in the ark which I had made; and there they are as the LORD commanded me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"(The children of Israel traveled from Beeroth Bene Jaakan to Moserah. There Aaron died, and there he was buried; and Eleazar his son ministered in the priest\u2019s office in his place."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"From there they traveled to Gudgodah; and from Gudgodah to Jotbathah, a land of brooks of water."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"At that time the LORD set apart the tribe of Levi to bear the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, to stand before the LORD to minister to him, and to bless in his name, to this day."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore Levi has no portion nor inheritance with his brothers; the LORD is his inheritance, according as the LORD your God spoke to him.)"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"I stayed on the mountain, as at the first time, forty days and forty nights; and the LORD listened to me that time also. The LORD would not destroy you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cArise, take your journey before the people; and they shall go in and possess the land which I swore to their fathers to give to them.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now, Israel, what does the LORD your God require of you, but to fear the LORD your God, to walk in all his ways, to love him, and to serve the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"to keep the LORD\u2019s commandments and statutes, which I command you today for your good?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Behold, to the LORD your God belongs heaven, the heaven of heavens, and the earth, with all that is therein."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Only the LORD had a delight in your fathers to love them, and he chose their offspring after them, even you above all peoples, as it is today."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Circumcise therefore the foreskin of your heart, and be no more stiff-necked."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God, he is God of gods and Lord of lords, the great God, the mighty, and the awesome, who doesn\u2019t respect persons or take bribes."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He executes justice for the fatherless and widow and loves the foreigner in giving him food and clothing."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore love the foreigner, for you were foreigners in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall fear the LORD your God. You shall serve him. You shall cling to him, and you shall swear by his name."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He is your praise, and he is your God, who has done for you these great and awesome things which your eyes have seen."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Your fathers went down into Egypt with seventy persons; and now the LORD your God has made you as the stars of the sky for multitude."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall love the LORD your God, and keep his instructions, his statutes, his ordinances, and his commandments, always."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Know this day\u2014for I don\u2019t speak with your children who have not known, and who have not seen the chastisement of the LORD your God, his greatness, his mighty hand, his outstretched arm,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"his signs, and his works, which he did in the middle of Egypt to Pharaoh the king of Egypt, and to all his land;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and what he did to the army of Egypt, to their horses, and to their chariots; how he made the water of the Red Sea to overflow them as they pursued you, and how the LORD has destroyed them to this day;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and what he did to you in the wilderness until you came to this place;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and what he did to Dathan and Abiram, the sons of Eliab, the son of Reuben\u2014how the earth opened its mouth and swallowed them up, with their households, their tents, and every living thing that followed them, in the middle of all Israel;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"but your eyes have seen all of the LORD\u2019s great work which he did."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall keep the entire commandment which I command you today, that you may be strong, and go in and possess the land that you go over to possess;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and that you may prolong your days in the land which the LORD swore to your fathers to give to them and to their offspring, a land flowing with milk and honey."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the land, where you go in to possess isn\u2019t like the land of Egypt that you came out of, where you sowed your seed and watered it with your foot, as a garden of herbs;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"but the land that you go over to possess is a land of hills and valleys which drinks water from the rain of the sky,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"a land which the LORD your God cares for. The LORD your God\u2019s eyes are always on it, from the beginning of the year even to the end of the year."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It shall happen, if you shall listen diligently to my commandments which I command you today, to love the LORD your God, and to serve him with all your heart and with all your soul,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"that I will give the rain for your land in its season, the early rain and the latter rain, that you may gather in your grain, your new wine, and your oil."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I will give grass in your fields for your livestock, and you shall eat and be full."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Be careful, lest your heart be deceived, and you turn away to serve other gods and worship them;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and the LORD\u2019s anger be kindled against you, and he shut up the sky so that there is no rain, and the land doesn\u2019t yield its fruit; and you perish quickly from off the good land which the LORD gives you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall lay up these words of mine in your heart and in your soul. You shall bind them for a sign on your hand, and they shall be for frontlets between your eyes."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall teach them to your children, talking of them when you sit in your house, when you walk by the way, when you lie down, and when you rise up."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall write them on the door posts of your house and on your gates;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"that your days and your children\u2019s days may be multiplied in the land which the LORD swore to your fathers to give them, as the days of the heavens above the earth."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For if you shall diligently keep all these commandments which I command you\u2014to do them, to love the LORD your God, to walk in all his ways, and to cling to him\u2014"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"then the LORD will drive out all these nations from before you, and you shall dispossess nations greater and mightier than yourselves."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Every place on which the sole of your foot treads shall be yours: from the wilderness and Lebanon, from the river, the river Euphrates, even to the western sea shall be your border."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"No man will be able to stand before you. The LORD your God will lay the fear of you and the dread of you on all the land that you tread on, as he has spoken to you."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Behold, I set before you today a blessing and a curse:"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"the blessing, if you listen to the commandments of the LORD your God, which I command you today;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and the curse, if you do not listen to the commandments of the LORD your God, but turn away out of the way which I command you today, to go after other gods which you have not known."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"It shall happen, when the LORD your God brings you into the land that you go to possess, that you shall set the blessing on Mount Gerizim, and the curse on Mount Ebal."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t they beyond the Jordan, behind the way of the going down of the sun, in the land of the Canaanites who dwell in the Arabah near Gilgal, beside the oaks of Moreh?"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For you are to pass over the Jordan to go in to possess the land which the LORD your God gives you, and you shall possess it and dwell in it."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"You shall observe to do all the statutes and the ordinances which I set before you today."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the statutes and the ordinances which you shall observe to do in the land which the LORD, the God of your fathers, has given you to possess all the days that you live on the earth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall surely destroy all the places in which the nations that you shall dispossess served their gods: on the high mountains, and on the hills, and under every green tree."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall break down their altars, dash their pillars in pieces, and burn their Asherah poles with fire. You shall cut down the engraved images of their gods. You shall destroy their name out of that place."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall not do so to the LORD your God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But to the place which the LORD your God shall choose out of all your tribes, to put his name there, you shall seek his habitation, and you shall come there."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall bring your burnt offerings, your sacrifices, your tithes, the wave offering of your hand, your vows, your free will offerings, and the firstborn of your herd and of your flock there."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"There you shall eat before the LORD your God, and you shall rejoice in all that you put your hand to, you and your households, in which the LORD your God has blessed you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall not do all the things that we do here today, every man whatever is right in his own eyes;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"for you haven\u2019t yet come to the rest and to the inheritance which the LORD your God gives you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But when you go over the Jordan and dwell in the land which the LORD your God causes you to inherit, and he gives you rest from all your enemies around you, so that you dwell in safety,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"then it shall happen that to the place which the LORD your God shall choose, to cause his name to dwell there, there you shall bring all that I command you: your burnt offerings, your sacrifices, your tithes, the wave offering of your hand, and all your choice vows which you vow to the LORD."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall rejoice before the LORD your God\u2014you, and your sons, your daughters, your male servants, your female servants, and the Levite who is within your gates, because he has no portion nor inheritance with you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Be careful that you don\u2019t offer your burnt offerings in every place that you see;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but in the place which the LORD chooses in one of your tribes, there you shall offer your burnt offerings, and there you shall do all that I command you."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Yet you may kill and eat meat within all your gates, after all the desire of your soul, according to the LORD your God\u2019s blessing which he has given you. The unclean and the clean may eat of it, as of the gazelle and the deer."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Only you shall not eat the blood. You shall pour it out on the earth like water."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You may not eat within your gates the tithe of your grain, or of your new wine, or of your oil, or the firstborn of your herd or of your flock, nor any of your vows which you vow, nor your free will offerings, nor the wave offering of your hand;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"but you shall eat them before the LORD your God in the place which the LORD your God shall choose: you, your son, your daughter, your male servant, your female servant, and the Levite who is within your gates. You shall rejoice before the LORD your God in all that you put your hand to."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Be careful that you don\u2019t forsake the Levite as long as you live in your land."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD your God enlarges your border, as he has promised you, and you say, \u201cI want to eat meat,\u201d because your soul desires to eat meat, you may eat meat, after all the desire of your soul."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"If the place which the LORD your God shall choose to put his name is too far from you, then you shall kill of your herd and of your flock, which the LORD has given you, as I have commanded you; and you may eat within your gates, after all the desire of your soul."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Even as the gazelle and as the deer is eaten, so you shall eat of it. The unclean and the clean may eat of it alike."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Only be sure that you don\u2019t eat the blood; for the blood is the life. You shall not eat the life with the meat."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall not eat it. You shall pour it out on the earth like water."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You shall not eat it, that it may go well with you and with your children after you, when you do that which is right in the LORD\u2019s eyes."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Only your holy things which you have, and your vows, you shall take and go to the place which the LORD shall choose."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"You shall offer your burnt offerings, the meat and the blood, on the LORD your God\u2019s altar. The blood of your sacrifices shall be poured out on the LORD your God\u2019s altar, and you shall eat the meat."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Observe and hear all these words which I command you, that it may go well with you and with your children after you forever, when you do that which is good and right in the LORD your God\u2019s eyes."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD your God cuts off the nations from before you where you go in to dispossess them, and you dispossess them and dwell in their land,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"be careful that you are not ensnared to follow them after they are destroyed from before you, and that you not inquire after their gods, saying, \u201cHow do these nations serve their gods? I will do likewise.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"You shall not do so to the LORD your God; for every abomination to the LORD, which he hates, they have done to their gods; for they even burn their sons and their daughters in the fire to their gods."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Whatever thing I command you, that you shall observe to do. You shall not add to it, nor take away from it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"If a prophet or a dreamer of dreams arises among you, and he gives you a sign or a wonder,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and the sign or the wonder comes to pass, of which he spoke to you, saying, \u201cLet\u2019s go after other gods\u201d (which you have not known) \u201cand let\u2019s serve them,\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"you shall not listen to the words of that prophet, or to that dreamer of dreams; for the LORD your God is testing you, to know whether you love the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall walk after the LORD your God, fear him, keep his commandments, and obey his voice. You shall serve him, and cling to him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"That prophet, or that dreamer of dreams, shall be put to death, because he has spoken rebellion against the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt and redeemed you out of the house of bondage, to draw you aside out of the way which the LORD your God commanded you to walk in. So you shall remove the evil from among you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"If your brother, the son of your mother, or your son, or your daughter, or the wife of your bosom, or your friend who is as your own soul, entices you secretly, saying, \u201cLet\u2019s go and serve other gods\u201d\u2014which you have not known, you, nor your fathers;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"of the gods of the peoples who are around you, near to you, or far off from you, from the one end of the earth even to the other end of the earth\u2014"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"you shall not consent to him nor listen to him; neither shall your eye pity him, neither shall you spare, neither shall you conceal him;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but you shall surely kill him. Your hand shall be first on him to put him to death, and afterwards the hands of all the people."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall stone him to death with stones, because he has sought to draw you away from the LORD your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"All Israel shall hear, and fear, and shall not do any more wickedness like this among you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"If you hear about one of your cities, which the LORD your God gives you to dwell there, that"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"certain wicked fellows have gone out from among you and have drawn away the inhabitants of their city, saying, \u201cLet\u2019s go and serve other gods,\u201d which you have not known,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"then you shall inquire, investigate, and ask diligently. Behold, if it is true, and the thing certain, that such abomination was done among you,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"you shall surely strike the inhabitants of that city with the edge of the sword, destroying it utterly, with all that is therein and its livestock, with the edge of the sword."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You shall gather all its plunder into the middle of its street, and shall burn with fire the city, with all of its plunder, to the LORD your God. It shall be a heap forever. It shall not be built again."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Nothing of the devoted thing shall cling to your hand, that the LORD may turn from the fierceness of his anger and show you mercy, and have compassion on you and multiply you, as he has sworn to your fathers,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"when you listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice, to keep all his commandments which I command you today, to do that which is right in the LORD your God\u2019s eyes."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"You are the children of the LORD your God. You shall not cut yourselves, nor make any baldness between your eyes for the dead."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For you are a holy people to the LORD your God, and the LORD has chosen you to be a people for his own possession, above all peoples who are on the face of the earth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not eat any abominable thing."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"These are the animals which you may eat: the ox, the sheep, the goat,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"the deer, the gazelle, the roebuck, the wild goat, the ibex, the antelope, and the chamois."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Every animal that parts the hoof, and has the hoof split in two and chews the cud, among the animals, you may eat."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Nevertheless these you shall not eat of them that chew the cud, or of those who have the hoof split: the camel, the hare, and the rabbit. Because they chew the cud but don\u2019t part the hoof, they are unclean to you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The pig, because it has a split hoof but doesn\u2019t chew the cud, is unclean to you. You shall not eat their meat. You shall not touch their carcasses."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"These you may eat of all that are in the waters: you may eat whatever has fins and scales."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall not eat whatever doesn\u2019t have fins and scales. It is unclean to you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Of all clean birds you may eat."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But these are they of which you shall not eat: the eagle, the vulture, the osprey,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"the red kite, the falcon, the kite of any kind,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"every raven of any kind,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"the ostrich, the owl, the seagull, the hawk of any kind,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the little owl, the great owl, the horned owl,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the pelican, the vulture, the cormorant,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"the stork, the heron after its kind, the hoopoe, and the bat."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"All winged creeping things are unclean to you. They shall not be eaten."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Of all clean birds you may eat."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not eat of anything that dies of itself. You may give it to the foreigner living among you who is within your gates, that he may eat it; or you may sell it to a foreigner; for you are a holy people to the LORD your God."],[0,"You shall not boil a young goat in its mother\u2019s milk."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall surely tithe all the increase of your seed, that which comes out of the field year by year."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You shall eat before the LORD your God, in the place which he chooses to cause his name to dwell, the tithe of your grain, of your new wine, and of your oil, and the firstborn of your herd and of your flock; that you may learn to fear the LORD your God always."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"If the way is too long for you, so that you are not able to carry it because the place which the LORD your God shall choose to set his name there is too far from you, when the LORD your God blesses you,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"then you shall turn it into money, bind up the money in your hand, and shall go to the place which the LORD your God shall choose."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You shall trade the money for whatever your soul desires: for cattle, or for sheep, or for wine, or for strong drink, or for whatever your soul asks of you. You shall eat there before the LORD your God, and you shall rejoice, you and your household."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"You shall not forsake the Levite who is within your gates, for he has no portion nor inheritance with you."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"At the end of every three years you shall bring all the tithe of your increase in the same year, and shall store it within your gates."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The Levite, because he has no portion nor inheritance with you, as well as the foreigner living among you, the fatherless, and the widow who are within your gates shall come, and shall eat and be satisfied; that the LORD your God may bless you in all the work of your hand which you do."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of every seven years, you shall cancel debts."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"This is the way it shall be done: every creditor shall release that which he has lent to his neighbor. He shall not require payment from his neighbor and his brother, because the LORD\u2019s release has been proclaimed."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Of a foreigner you may require it; but whatever of yours is with your brother, your hand shall release."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"However there will be no poor with you (for the LORD will surely bless you in the land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance to possess)"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"if only you diligently listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice, to observe to do all this commandment which I command you today."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God will bless you, as he promised you. You will lend to many nations, but you will not borrow. You will rule over many nations, but they will not rule over you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If a poor man, one of your brothers, is with you within any of your gates in your land which the LORD your God gives you, you shall not harden your heart, nor shut your hand from your poor brother;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but you shall surely open your hand to him, and shall surely lend him sufficient for his need, which he lacks."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Beware that there not be a wicked thought in your heart, saying, \u201cThe seventh year, the year of release, is at hand,\u201d and your eye be evil against your poor brother and you give him nothing; and he cry to the LORD against you, and it be sin to you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall surely give, and your heart shall not be grieved when you give to him, because it is for this thing the LORD your God will bless you in all your work and in all that you put your hand to."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the poor will never cease out of the land. Therefore I command you to surely open your hand to your brother, to your needy, and to your poor, in your land."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If your brother, a Hebrew man, or a Hebrew woman, is sold to you and serves you six years, then in the seventh year you shall let him go free from you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When you let him go free from you, you shall not let him go empty."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall furnish him liberally out of your flock, out of your threshing floor, and out of your wine press. As the LORD your God has blessed you, you shall give to him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall remember that you were a slave in the land of Egypt, and the LORD your God redeemed you. Therefore I command you this thing today."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"It shall be, if he tells you, \u201cI will not go out from you,\u201d because he loves you and your house, because he is well with you,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"then you shall take an awl, and thrust it through his ear to the door, and he shall be your servant forever. Also to your female servant you shall do likewise."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"It shall not seem hard to you when you let him go free from you, for he has been double the value of a hired hand as he served you six years. The LORD your God will bless you in all that you do."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall dedicate all the firstborn males that are born of your herd and of your flock to the LORD your God. You shall do no work with the firstborn of your herd, nor shear the firstborn of your flock."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall eat it before the LORD your God year by year in the place which the LORD shall choose, you and your household."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"If it has any defect\u2014is lame or blind, or has any defect whatever, you shall not sacrifice it to the LORD your God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall eat it within your gates. The unclean and the clean shall eat it alike, as the gazelle and as the deer."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Only you shall not eat its blood. You shall pour it out on the ground like water."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Observe the month of Abib, and keep the Passover to the LORD your God; for in the month of Abib the LORD your God brought you out of Egypt by night."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall sacrifice the Passover to the LORD your God, of the flock and the herd, in the place which the LORD shall choose to cause his name to dwell there."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall eat no leavened bread with it. You shall eat unleavened bread with it seven days, even the bread of affliction (for you came out of the land of Egypt in haste) that you may remember the day when you came out of the land of Egypt all the days of your life."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"No yeast shall be seen with you in all your borders seven days; neither shall any of the meat, which you sacrifice the first day at evening, remain all night until the morning."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You may not sacrifice the Passover within any of your gates which the LORD your God gives you;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but at the place which the LORD your God shall choose to cause his name to dwell in, there you shall sacrifice the Passover at evening, at the going down of the sun, at the season that you came out of Egypt."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall roast and eat it in the place which the LORD your God chooses. In the morning you shall return to your tents."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Six days you shall eat unleavened bread. On the seventh day shall be a solemn assembly to the LORD your God. You shall do no work."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall count for yourselves seven weeks. From the time you begin to put the sickle to the standing grain you shall begin to count seven weeks."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall keep the feast of weeks to the LORD your God with a tribute of a free will offering of your hand, which you shall give according to how the LORD your God blesses you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall rejoice before the LORD your God: you, your son, your daughter, your male servant, your female servant, the Levite who is within your gates, the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow who are among you, in the place which the LORD your God shall choose to cause his name to dwell there."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall remember that you were a slave in Egypt. You shall observe and do these statutes."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall keep the feast of booths seven days, after you have gathered in from your threshing floor and from your wine press."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall rejoice in your feast, you, your son, your daughter, your male servant, your female servant, the Levite, the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow who are within your gates."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall keep a feast to the LORD your God seven days in the place which the LORD chooses, because the LORD your God will bless you in all your increase and in all the work of your hands, and you shall be altogether joyful."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Three times in a year all of your males shall appear before the LORD your God in the place which he chooses: in the feast of unleavened bread, in the feast of weeks, and in the feast of booths. They shall not appear before the LORD empty."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Every man shall give as he is able, according to the LORD your God\u2019s blessing which he has given you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall make judges and officers in all your gates, which the LORD your God gives you, according to your tribes; and they shall judge the people with righteous judgment."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall not pervert justice. You shall not show partiality. You shall not take a bribe, for a bribe blinds the eyes of the wise and perverts the words of the righteous."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall follow that which is altogether just, that you may live and inherit the land which the LORD your God gives you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You shall not plant for yourselves an Asherah of any kind of tree beside the LORD your God\u2019s altar, which you shall make for yourselves."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Neither shall you set yourself up a sacred stone which the LORD your God hates."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not sacrifice to the LORD your God an ox or a sheep in which is a defect or anything evil; for that is an abomination to the LORD your God."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"If there is found among you, within any of your gates which the LORD your God gives you, a man or woman who does that which is evil in the LORD your God\u2019s sight in transgressing his covenant,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and has gone and served other gods and worshiped them, or the sun, or the moon, or any of the stars of the sky, which I have not commanded,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and you are told, and you have heard of it, then you shall inquire diligently. Behold, if it is true, and the thing certain, that such abomination is done in Israel,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"then you shall bring out that man or that woman who has done this evil thing to your gates, even that same man or woman; and you shall stone them to death with stones."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"At the mouth of two witnesses, or three witnesses, he who is to die shall be put to death. At the mouth of one witness he shall not be put to death."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The hands of the witnesses shall be first on him to put him to death, and afterward the hands of all the people. So you shall remove the evil from among you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"If there arises a matter too hard for you in judgment, between blood and blood, between plea and plea, and between stroke and stroke, being matters of controversy within your gates, then you shall arise, and go up to the place which the LORD your God chooses."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You shall come to the priests who are Levites and to the judge who shall be in those days. You shall inquire, and they shall give you the verdict."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall do according to the decisions of the verdict which they shall give you from that place which the LORD chooses. You shall observe to do according to all that they shall teach you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"According to the decisions of the law which they shall teach you, and according to the judgment which they shall tell you, you shall do. You shall not turn away from the sentence which they announce to you, to the right hand, nor to the left."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The man who does presumptuously in not listening to the priest who stands to minister there before the LORD your God, or to the judge, even that man shall die. You shall put away the evil from Israel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"All the people shall hear and fear, and do no more presumptuously."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When you have come to the land which the LORD your God gives you, and possess it and dwell in it, and say, \u201cI will set a king over me, like all the nations that are around me,\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"you shall surely set him whom the LORD your God chooses as king over yourselves. You shall set as king over you one from among your brothers. You may not put a foreigner over you, who is not your brother."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Only he shall not multiply horses to himself, nor cause the people to return to Egypt, to the end that he may multiply horses; because the LORD has said to you, \u201cYou shall not go back that way again.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He shall not multiply wives to himself, that his heart not turn away. He shall not greatly multiply to himself silver and gold."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall be, when he sits on the throne of his kingdom, that he shall write himself a copy of this law in a book, out of that which is before the Levitical priests."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"It shall be with him, and he shall read from it all the days of his life, that he may learn to fear the LORD his God, to keep all the words of this law and these statutes, to do them;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"that his heart not be lifted up above his brothers, and that he not turn away from the commandment to the right hand, or to the left, to the end that he may prolong his days in his kingdom, he and his children, in the middle of Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The priests and the Levites\u2014all the tribe of Levi\u2014shall have no portion nor inheritance with Israel. They shall eat the offerings of the LORD made by fire and his portion."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They shall have no inheritance among their brothers. The LORD is their inheritance, as he has spoken to them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This shall be the priests\u2019 due from the people, from those who offer a sacrifice, whether it be ox or sheep, that they shall give to the priest: the shoulder, the two cheeks, and the inner parts."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall give him the first fruits of your grain, of your new wine, and of your oil, and the first of the fleece of your sheep."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God has chosen him out of all your tribes to stand to minister in the LORD\u2019s name, him and his sons forever."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"If a Levite comes from any of your gates out of all Israel where he lives, and comes with all the desire of his soul to the place which the LORD shall choose,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"then he shall minister in the name of the LORD his God, as all his brothers the Levites do, who stand there before the LORD."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They shall have like portions to eat, in addition to that which comes from the sale of his family possessions."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When you have come into the land which the LORD your God gives you, you shall not learn to imitate the abominations of those nations."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"There shall not be found with you anyone who makes his son or his daughter to pass through the fire, one who uses divination, one who tells fortunes, or an enchanter, or a sorcerer,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"or a charmer, or someone who consults with a familiar spirit, or a wizard, or a necromancer."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For whoever does these things is an abomination to the LORD. Because of these abominations, the LORD your God drives them out from before you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall be blameless with the LORD your God."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For these nations that you shall dispossess listen to those who practice sorcery and to diviners; but as for you, the LORD your God has not allowed you so to do."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The LORD your God will raise up to you a prophet from among you, of your brothers, like me. You shall listen to him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"This is according to all that you desired of the LORD your God in Horeb in the day of the assembly, saying, \u201cLet me not hear again the LORD my God\u2019s voice, neither let me see this great fire any more, that I not die.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cThey have well said that which they have spoken."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I will raise them up a prophet from among their brothers, like you. I will put my words in his mouth, and he shall speak to them all that I shall command him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"It shall happen, that whoever will not listen to my words which he shall speak in my name, I will require it of him."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But the prophet who speaks a word presumptuously in my name, which I have not commanded him to speak, or who speaks in the name of other gods, that same prophet shall die.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"You may say in your heart, \u201cHow shall we know the word which the LORD has not spoken?\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When a prophet speaks in the LORD\u2019s name, if the thing doesn\u2019t follow, nor happen, that is the thing which the LORD has not spoken. The prophet has spoken it presumptuously. You shall not be afraid of him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD your God cuts off the nations whose land the LORD your God gives you, and you succeed them and dwell in their cities and in their houses,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"you shall set apart three cities for yourselves in the middle of your land, which the LORD your God gives you to possess."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall prepare the way, and divide the borders of your land which the LORD your God causes you to inherit into three parts, that every man slayer may flee there."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"This is the case of the man slayer who shall flee there and live: Whoever kills his neighbor unintentionally, and didn\u2019t hate him in time past\u2014"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"as when a man goes into the forest with his neighbor to chop wood and his hand swings the ax to cut down the tree, and the head slips from the handle and hits his neighbor so that he dies\u2014he shall flee to one of these cities and live."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Otherwise, the avenger of blood might pursue the man slayer while hot anger is in his heart and overtake him, because the way is long, and strike him mortally, even though he was not worthy of death, because he didn\u2019t hate him in time past."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore I command you to set apart three cities for yourselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If the LORD your God enlarges your border, as he has sworn to your fathers, and gives you all the land which he promised to give to your fathers;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and if you keep all this commandment to do it, which I command you today, to love the LORD your God, and to walk ever in his ways, then you shall add three cities more for yourselves, in addition to these three."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"This is so that innocent blood will not be shed in the middle of your land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance, leaving blood guilt on you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But if any man hates his neighbor, lies in wait for him, rises up against him, strikes him mortally so that he dies, and he flees into one of these cities;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"then the elders of his city shall send and bring him there, and deliver him into the hand of the avenger of blood, that he may die."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Your eye shall not pity him, but you shall purge the innocent blood from Israel that it may go well with you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not remove your neighbor\u2019s landmark, which they of old time have set, in your inheritance which you shall inherit, in the land that the LORD your God gives you to possess."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"One witness shall not rise up against a man for any iniquity, or for any sin that he sins. At the mouth of two witnesses, or at the mouth of three witnesses, shall a matter be established."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"If an unrighteous witness rises up against any man to testify against him of wrongdoing,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"then both the men, between whom the controversy is, shall stand before the LORD, before the priests and the judges who shall be in those days;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and the judges shall make diligent inquisition; and behold, if the witness is a false witness, and has testified falsely against his brother,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"then you shall do to him as he had thought to do to his brother. So you shall remove the evil from among you."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Those who remain shall hear, and fear, and will never again commit any such evil among you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Your eyes shall not pity: life for life, eye for eye, tooth for tooth, hand for hand, foot for foot."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When you go out to battle against your enemies, and see horses, chariots, and a people more numerous than you, you shall not be afraid of them; for the LORD your God, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt, is with you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It shall be, when you draw near to the battle, that the priest shall approach and speak to the people,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and shall tell them, \u201cHear, Israel, you draw near today to battle against your enemies. Don\u2019t let your heart faint! Don\u2019t be afraid, nor tremble, neither be scared of them;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for the LORD your God is he who goes with you, to fight for you against your enemies, to save you.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The officers shall speak to the people, saying, \u201cWhat man is there who has built a new house, and has not dedicated it? Let him go and return to his house, lest he die in the battle, and another man dedicate it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"What man is there who has planted a vineyard, and has not used its fruit? Let him go and return to his house, lest he die in the battle, and another man use its fruit."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"What man is there who has pledged to be married to a wife, and has not taken her? Let him go and return to his house, lest he die in the battle, and another man take her.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The officers shall speak further to the people, and they shall say, \u201cWhat man is there who is fearful and faint-hearted? Let him go and return to his house, lest his brother\u2019s heart melt as his heart.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It shall be, when the officers have finished speaking to the people, that they shall appoint captains of armies at the head of the people."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When you draw near to a city to fight against it, then proclaim peace to it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"It shall be, if it gives you answer of peace and opens to you, then it shall be that all the people who are found therein shall become forced laborers to you, and shall serve you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If it will make no peace with you, but will make war against you, then you shall besiege it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When the LORD your God delivers it into your hand, you shall strike every male of it with the edge of the sword;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but the women, the little ones, the livestock, and all that is in the city, even all its plunder, you shall take for plunder for yourself. You may use the plunder of your enemies, which the LORD your God has given you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Thus you shall do to all the cities which are very far off from you, which are not of the cities of these nations."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But of the cities of these peoples that the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance, you shall save alive nothing that breathes;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"but you shall utterly destroy them: the Hittite, the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite, as the LORD your God has commanded you;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"that they not teach you to follow all their abominations, which they have done for their gods; so would you sin against the LORD your God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When you shall besiege a city a long time, in making war against it to take it, you shall not destroy its trees by wielding an ax against them; for you may eat of them. You shall not cut them down, for is the tree of the field man, that it should be besieged by you?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Only the trees that you know are not trees for food, you shall destroy and cut them down. You shall build bulwarks against the city that makes war with you, until it falls."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"If someone is found slain in the land which the LORD your God gives you to possess, lying in the field, and it isn\u2019t known who has struck him,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"then your elders and your judges shall come out, and they shall measure to the cities which are around him who is slain."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It shall be that the elders of the city which is nearest to the slain man shall take a heifer of the herd, which hasn\u2019t been worked with and which has not drawn in the yoke."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The elders of that city shall bring the heifer down to a valley with running water, which is neither plowed nor sown, and shall break the heifer\u2019s neck there in the valley."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The priests the sons of Levi shall come near, for them the LORD your God has chosen to minister to him, and to bless in the LORD\u2019s name; and according to their word shall every controversy and every assault be decided."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"All the elders of that city which is nearest to the slain man shall wash their hands over the heifer whose neck was broken in the valley."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They shall answer and say, \u201cOur hands have not shed this blood, neither have our eyes seen it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Forgive, LORD, your people Israel, whom you have redeemed, and don\u2019t allow innocent blood among your people Israel.\u201d The blood shall be forgiven them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So you shall put away the innocent blood from among you, when you shall do that which is right in the LORD\u2019s eyes."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When you go out to battle against your enemies, and the LORD your God delivers them into your hands and you carry them away captive,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and see among the captives a beautiful woman, and you are attracted to her, and desire to take her as your wife,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"then you shall bring her home to your house. She shall shave her head and trim her nails."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"She shall take off the clothing of her captivity, and shall remain in your house, and bewail her father and her mother a full month. After that you shall go in to her and be her husband, and she shall be your wife."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"It shall be, if you have no delight in her, then you shall let her go where she desires; but you shall not sell her at all for money. You shall not deal with her as a slave, because you have humbled her."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"If a man has two wives, the one beloved and the other hated, and they have borne him children, both the beloved and the hated, and if the firstborn son is hers who was hated,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"then it shall be, in the day that he causes his sons to inherit that which he has, that he may not give the son of the beloved the rights of the firstborn before the son of the hated, who is the firstborn;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"but he shall acknowledge the firstborn, the son of the hated, by giving him a double portion of all that he has; for he is the beginning of his strength. The right of the firstborn is his."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"If a man has a stubborn and rebellious son who will not obey the voice of his father or the voice of his mother, and though they chasten him, will not listen to them,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"then his father and his mother shall take hold of him and bring him out to the elders of his city and to the gate of his place."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They shall tell the elders of his city, \u201cThis our son is stubborn and rebellious. He will not obey our voice. He is a glutton and a drunkard.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"All the men of his city shall stone him to death with stones. So you shall remove the evil from among you. All Israel shall hear, and fear."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"If a man has committed a sin worthy of death, and he is put to death, and you hang him on a tree,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"his body shall not remain all night on the tree, but you shall surely bury him the same day; for he who is hanged is accursed of God. Don\u2019t defile your land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not see your brother\u2019s ox or his sheep go astray and hide yourself from them. You shall surely bring them again to your brother."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"If your brother isn\u2019t near to you, or if you don\u2019t know him, then you shall bring it home to your house, and it shall be with you until your brother comes looking for it, and you shall restore it to him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So you shall do with his donkey. So you shall do with his garment. So you shall do with every lost thing of your brother\u2019s, which he has lost and you have found. You may not hide yourself."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall not see your brother\u2019s donkey or his ox fallen down by the way, and hide yourself from them. You shall surely help him to lift them up again."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"A woman shall not wear men\u2019s clothing, neither shall a man put on women\u2019s clothing; for whoever does these things is an abomination to the LORD your God."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"If you come across a bird\u2019s nest on the way, in any tree or on the ground, with young ones or eggs, and the hen sitting on the young, or on the eggs, you shall not take the hen with the young."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall surely let the hen go, but the young you may take for yourself, that it may be well with you, and that you may prolong your days."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"When you build a new house, then you shall make a railing around your roof, so that you don\u2019t bring blood on your house if anyone falls from there."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not sow your vineyard with two kinds of seed, lest all the fruit be defiled, the seed which you have sown, and the increase of the vineyard."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall not plow with an ox and a donkey together."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall not wear clothes of wool and linen woven together."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall make yourselves fringes on the four corners of your cloak with which you cover yourself."]],f:["or, tassels"]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"If any man takes a wife, and goes in to her, hates her,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"accuses her of shameful things, gives her a bad name, and says, \u201cI took this woman, and when I came near to her, I didn\u2019t find in her the tokens of virginity;\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"then the young lady\u2019s father and mother shall take and bring the tokens of the young lady\u2019s virginity to the elders of the city in the gate."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The young lady\u2019s father shall tell the elders, \u201cI gave my daughter to this man as his wife, and he hates her."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Behold, he has accused her of shameful things, saying, \u2018I didn\u2019t find in your daughter the tokens of virginity;\u2019 and yet these are the tokens of my daughter\u2019s virginity.\u201d They shall spread the cloth before the elders of the city."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The elders of that city shall take the man and chastise him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They shall fine him one hundred shekels of silver, and give them to the father of the young lady, because he has given a bad name to a virgin of Israel. She shall be his wife. He may not put her away all his days."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 100 shekels is about a kilogram or 2.2 pounds."]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"But if this thing is true, that the tokens of virginity were not found in the young lady,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"then they shall bring out the young lady to the door of her father\u2019s house, and the men of her city shall stone her to death with stones, because she has done folly in Israel, to play the prostitute in her father\u2019s house. So you shall remove the evil from among you."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"If a man is found lying with a woman married to a husband, then they shall both die, the man who lay with the woman and the woman. So you shall remove the evil from Israel."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If there is a young lady who is a virgin pledged to be married to a husband, and a man finds her in the city, and lies with her,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"then you shall bring them both out to the gate of that city, and you shall stone them to death with stones; the lady, because she didn\u2019t cry, being in the city; and the man, because he has humbled his neighbor\u2019s wife. So you shall remove the evil from among you."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But if the man finds the lady who is pledged to be married in the field, and the man forces her and lies with her, then only the man who lay with her shall die;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"but to the lady you shall do nothing. There is in the lady no sin worthy of death; for as when a man rises against his neighbor and kills him, even so is this matter;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"for he found her in the field, the pledged to be married lady cried, and there was no one to save her."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"If a man finds a lady who is a virgin, who is not pledged to be married, grabs her and lies with her, and they are found,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"then the man who lay with her shall give to the lady\u2019s father fifty shekels of silver. She shall be his wife, because he has humbled her. He may not put her away all his days."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"A man shall not take his father\u2019s wife, and shall not uncover his father\u2019s skirt."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He who is emasculated by crushing or cutting shall not enter into the LORD\u2019s assembly."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"A person born of a forbidden union shall not enter into the LORD\u2019s assembly; even to the tenth generation shall no one of his enter into the LORD\u2019s assembly."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"An Ammonite or a Moabite shall not enter into the LORD\u2019s assembly; even to the tenth generation shall no one belonging to them enter into the LORD\u2019s assembly forever,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"because they didn\u2019t meet you with bread and with water on the way when you came out of Egypt, and because they hired against you Balaam the son of Beor from Pethor of Mesopotamia, to curse you."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Nevertheless the LORD your God wouldn\u2019t listen to Balaam, but the LORD your God turned the curse into a blessing to you, because the LORD your God loved you."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall not seek their peace nor their prosperity all your days forever."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall not abhor an Edomite, for he is your brother. You shall not abhor an Egyptian, because you lived as a foreigner in his land."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of the third generation who are born to them may enter into the LORD\u2019s assembly."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When you go out and camp against your enemies, then you shall keep yourselves from every evil thing."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If there is among you any man who is not clean by reason of that which happens to him by night, then shall he go outside of the camp. He shall not come within the camp;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"but it shall be, when evening comes, he shall bathe himself in water. When the sun is down, he shall come within the camp."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall have a place also outside of the camp where you go relieve yourself."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall have a trowel among your weapons. It shall be, when you relieve yourself, you shall dig with it, and shall turn back and cover your excrement;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"for the LORD your God walks in the middle of your camp, to deliver you, and to give up your enemies before you. Therefore your camp shall be holy, that he may not see an unclean thing in you, and turn away from you."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not deliver to his master a servant who has escaped from his master to you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He shall dwell with you, among you, in the place which he shall choose within one of your gates, where it pleases him best. You shall not oppress him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"There shall be no prostitute of the daughters of Israel, neither shall there be a sodomite of the sons of Israel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall not bring the hire of a prostitute, or the wages of a male prostitute, into the house of the LORD your God for any vow; for both of these are an abomination to the LORD your God."]],f:["literally, dog"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not lend on interest to your brother: interest of money, interest of food, interest of anything that is lent on interest."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You may charge a foreigner interest; but you shall not charge your brother interest, that the LORD your God may bless you in all that you put your hand to, in the land where you go in to possess it."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When you vow a vow to the LORD your God, you shall not be slack to pay it, for the LORD your God will surely require it of you; and it would be sin in you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But if you refrain from making a vow, it shall be no sin in you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You shall observe and do that which has gone out of your lips. Whatever you have vowed to the LORD your God as a free will offering, which you have promised with your mouth, you must do."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When you come into your neighbor\u2019s vineyard, then you may eat your fill of grapes at your own pleasure; but you shall not put any in your container."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When you come into your neighbor\u2019s standing grain, then you may pluck the ears with your hand; but you shall not use a sickle on your neighbor\u2019s standing grain."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When a man takes a wife and marries her, then it shall be, if she finds no favor in his eyes because he has found some unseemly thing in her, that he shall write her a certificate of divorce, put it in her hand, and send her out of his house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When she has departed out of his house, she may go and be another man\u2019s wife."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If the latter husband hates her, and writes her a certificate of divorce, puts it in her hand, and sends her out of his house; or if the latter husband dies, who took her to be his wife;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"her former husband, who sent her away, may not take her again to be his wife after she is defiled; for that would be an abomination to the LORD. You shall not cause the land to sin, which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When a man takes a new wife, he shall not go out in the army, neither shall he be assigned any business. He shall be free at home one year, and shall cheer his wife whom he has taken."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"No man shall take the mill or the upper millstone as a pledge, for he takes a life in pledge."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"If a man is found stealing any of his brothers of the children of Israel, and he deals with him as a slave, or sells him, then that thief shall die. So you shall remove the evil from among you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Be careful in the plague of leprosy, that you observe diligently and do according to all that the Levitical priests teach you. As I commanded them, so you shall observe to do."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Remember what the LORD your God did to Miriam, by the way as you came out of Egypt."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When you lend your neighbor any kind of loan, you shall not go into his house to get his pledge."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall stand outside, and the man to whom you lend shall bring the pledge outside to you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If he is a poor man, you shall not sleep with his pledge."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall surely restore to him the pledge when the sun goes down, that he may sleep in his garment and bless you. It shall be righteousness to you before the LORD your God."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not oppress a hired servant who is poor and needy, whether he is one of your brothers or one of the foreigners who are in your land within your gates."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"In his day you shall give him his wages, neither shall the sun go down on it, for he is poor and sets his heart on it, lest he cry against you to the LORD, and it be sin to you."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, neither shall the children be put to death for the fathers. Every man shall be put to death for his own sin."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not deprive the foreigner or the fatherless of justice, nor take a widow\u2019s clothing in pledge;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"but you shall remember that you were a slave in Egypt, and the LORD your God redeemed you there. Therefore I command you to do this thing."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"When you reap your harvest in your field, and have forgotten a sheaf in the field, you shall not go again to get it. It shall be for the foreigner, for the fatherless, and for the widow, that the LORD your God may bless you in all the work of your hands."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When you beat your olive tree, you shall not go over the boughs again. It shall be for the foreigner, for the fatherless, and for the widow."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When you harvest your vineyard, you shall not glean it after yourselves. It shall be for the foreigner, for the fatherless, and for the widow."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall remember that you were a slave in the land of Egypt. Therefore I command you to do this thing."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"If there is a controversy between men, and they come to judgment and the judges judge them, then they shall justify the righteous and condemn the wicked."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It shall be, if the wicked man is worthy to be beaten, that the judge shall cause him to lie down and to be beaten before his face, according to his wickedness, by number."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He may sentence him to no more than forty stripes. He shall not give more, lest if he should give more and beat him more than that many stripes, then your brother will be degraded in your sight."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not muzzle the ox when he treads out the grain."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"If brothers dwell together, and one of them dies and has no son, the wife of the dead shall not be married outside to a stranger. Her husband\u2019s brother shall go in to her, and take her as his wife, and perform the duty of a husband\u2019s brother to her."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"It shall be that the firstborn whom she bears shall succeed in the name of his brother who is dead, that his name not be blotted out of Israel."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"If the man doesn\u2019t want to take his brother\u2019s wife, then his brother\u2019s wife shall go up to the gate to the elders, and say, \u201cMy husband\u2019s brother refuses to raise up to his brother a name in Israel. He will not perform the duty of a husband\u2019s brother to me.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then the elders of his city shall call him, and speak to him. If he stands and says, \u201cI don\u2019t want to take her,\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"then his brother\u2019s wife shall come to him in the presence of the elders, and loose his sandal from off his foot, and spit in his face. She shall answer and say, \u201cSo shall it be done to the man who does not build up his brother\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"His name shall be called in Israel, \u201cThe house of him who had his sandal removed.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When men strive against each other, and the wife of one draws near to deliver her husband out of the hand of him who strikes him, and puts out her hand, and grabs him by his private parts,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"then you shall cut off her hand. Your eye shall have no pity."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"You shall not have in your bag diverse weights, one heavy and one light."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall not have in your house diverse measures, one large and one small."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You shall have a perfect and just weight. You shall have a perfect and just measure, that your days may be long in the land which the LORD your God gives you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For all who do such things, all who do unrighteously, are an abomination to the LORD your God."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Remember what Amalek did to you by the way as you came out of Egypt,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"how he met you by the way, and struck the rearmost of you, all who were feeble behind you, when you were faint and weary; and he didn\u2019t fear God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore it shall be, when the LORD your God has given you rest from all your enemies all around, in the land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance to possess it, that you shall blot out the memory of Amalek from under the sky. You shall not forget."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall be, when you have come in to the land which the LORD your God gives you for an inheritance, possess it, and dwell in it,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that you shall take some of the first of all the fruit of the ground, which you shall bring in from your land that the LORD your God gives you. You shall put it in a basket, and shall go to the place which the LORD your God shall choose to cause his name to dwell there."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall come to the priest who shall be in those days, and tell him, \u201cI profess today to the LORD your God, that I have come to the land which the LORD swore to our fathers to give us.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The priest shall take the basket out of your hand, and set it down before the LORD your God\u2019s altar."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall answer and say before the LORD your God, \u201cMy father was a Syrian ready to perish. He went down into Egypt, and lived there, few in number. There he became a great, mighty, and populous nation."]],f:["or, forefather"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The Egyptians mistreated us, afflicted us, and imposed hard labor on us."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then we cried to the LORD, the God of our fathers. The LORD heard our voice, and saw our affliction, our toil, and our oppression."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD brought us out of Egypt with a mighty hand, with an outstretched arm, with great terror, with signs, and with wonders;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and he has brought us into this place, and has given us this land, a land flowing with milk and honey."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now, behold, I have brought the first of the fruit of the ground, which you, the LORD, have given me.\u201d You shall set it down before the LORD your God, and worship before the LORD your God."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall rejoice in all the good which the LORD your God has given to you, and to your house, you, and the Levite, and the foreigner who is among you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When you have finished tithing all the tithe of your increase in the third year, which is the year of tithing, then you shall give it to the Levite, to the foreigner, to the fatherless, and to the widow, that they may eat within your gates and be filled."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You shall say before the LORD your God, \u201cI have put away the holy things out of my house, and also have given them to the Levite, to the foreigner, to the fatherless, and to the widow, according to all your commandment which you have commanded me. I have not transgressed any of your commandments, neither have I forgotten them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I have not eaten of it in my mourning, neither have I removed any of it while I was unclean, nor given of it for the dead. I have listened to the LORD my God\u2019s voice. I have done according to all that you have commanded me."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Look down from your holy habitation, from heaven, and bless your people Israel, and the ground which you have given us, as you swore to our fathers, a land flowing with milk and honey.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Today the LORD your God commands you to do these statutes and ordinances. You shall therefore keep and do them with all your heart and with all your soul."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You have declared today that the LORD is your God, and that you would walk in his ways, keep his statutes, his commandments, and his ordinances, and listen to his voice."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The LORD has declared today that you are a people for his own possession, as he has promised you, and that you should keep all his commandments."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He will make you high above all nations that he has made, in praise, in name, and in honor, and that you may be a holy people to the LORD your God, as he has spoken."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and the elders of Israel commanded the people, saying, \u201cKeep all the commandment which I command you today."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It shall be on the day when you shall pass over the Jordan to the land which the LORD your God gives you, that you shall set yourself up great stones, and coat them with plaster."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall write on them all the words of this law, when you have passed over, that you may go in to the land which the LORD your God gives you, a land flowing with milk and honey, as the LORD, the God of your fathers, has promised you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"It shall be, when you have crossed over the Jordan, that you shall set up these stones, which I command you today, on Mount Ebal, and you shall coat them with plaster."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"There you shall build an altar to the LORD your God, an altar of stones. You shall not use any iron tool on them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall build the LORD your God\u2019s altar of uncut stones. You shall offer burnt offerings on it to the LORD your God."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall sacrifice peace offerings, and shall eat there. You shall rejoice before the LORD your God."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall write on the stones all the words of this law very plainly.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses and the Levitical priests spoke to all Israel, saying, \u201cBe silent and listen, Israel! Today you have become the people of the LORD your God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You shall therefore obey the LORD your God\u2019s voice, and do his commandments and his statutes, which I command you today.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses commanded the people the same day, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cThese shall stand on Mount Gerizim to bless the people, when you have crossed over the Jordan: Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Joseph, and Benjamin."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"These shall stand on Mount Ebal for the curse: Reuben, Gad, Asher, Zebulun, Dan, and Naphtali."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"With a loud voice, the Levites shall say to all the men of Israel,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is the man who makes an engraved or molten image, an abomination to the LORD, the work of the hands of the craftsman, and sets it up in secret.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall answer and say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who dishonors his father or his mother.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who removes his neighbor\u2019s landmark.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who leads the blind astray on the road.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who withholds justice from the foreigner, fatherless, and widow.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who lies with his father\u2019s wife, because he dishonors his father\u2019s bed.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]],f:["i.e., has sexual relations with"]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who lies with any kind of animal.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who lies with his sister, his father\u2019s daughter or his mother\u2019s daughter.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who lies with his mother-in-law.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who secretly kills his neighbor.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who takes a bribe to kill an innocent person.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u2018Cursed is he who doesn\u2019t uphold the words of this law by doing them.\u2019"],[0,"All the people shall say, \u2018Amen.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall happen, if you shall listen diligently to the LORD your God\u2019s voice, to observe to do all his commandments which I command you today, that the LORD your God will set you high above all the nations of the earth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"All these blessings will come upon you, and overtake you, if you listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall be blessed in the city, and you shall be blessed in the field."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall be blessed in the fruit of your body, the fruit of your ground, the fruit of your animals, the increase of your livestock, and the young of your flock."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Your basket and your kneading trough shall be blessed."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall be blessed when you come in, and you shall be blessed when you go out."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD will cause your enemies who rise up against you to be struck before you. They will come out against you one way, and will flee before you seven ways."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD will command the blessing on you in your barns, and in all that you put your hand to. He will bless you in the land which the LORD your God gives you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The LORD will establish you for a holy people to himself, as he has sworn to you, if you shall keep the commandments of the LORD your God, and walk in his ways."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All the peoples of the earth shall see that you are called by the LORD\u2019s name, and they will be afraid of you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD will grant you abundant prosperity in the fruit of your body, in the fruit of your livestock, and in the fruit of your ground, in the land which the LORD swore to your fathers to give you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD will open to you his good treasure in the sky, to give the rain of your land in its season, and to bless all the work of your hand. You will lend to many nations, and you will not borrow."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD will make you the head, and not the tail. You will be above only, and you will not be beneath, if you listen to the commandments of the LORD your God which I command you today, to observe and to do,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and shall not turn away from any of the words which I command you today, to the right hand or to the left, to go after other gods to serve them."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"But it shall come to pass, if you will not listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice, to observe to do all his commandments and his statutes which I command you today, that all these curses will come on you and overtake you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You will be cursed in the city, and you will be cursed in the field."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Your basket and your kneading trough will be cursed."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The fruit of your body, the fruit of your ground, the increase of your livestock, and the young of your flock will be cursed."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You will be cursed when you come in, and you will be cursed when you go out."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD will send on you cursing, confusion, and rebuke in all that you put your hand to do, until you are destroyed and until you perish quickly, because of the evil of your doings, by which you have forsaken me."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD will make the pestilence cling to you, until he has consumed you from off the land where you go in to possess it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The LORD will strike you with consumption, with fever, with inflammation, with fiery heat, with the sword, with blight, and with mildew. They will pursue you until you perish."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Your sky that is over your head will be bronze, and the earth that is under you will be iron."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The LORD will make the rain of your land powder and dust. It will come down on you from the sky, until you are destroyed."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The LORD will cause you to be struck before your enemies. You will go out one way against them, and will flee seven ways before them. You will be tossed back and forth among all the kingdoms of the earth."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Your dead bodies will be food to all birds of the sky, and to the animals of the earth; and there will be no one to frighten them away."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The LORD will strike you with the boils of Egypt, with the tumors, with the scurvy, and with the itch, of which you can not be healed."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The LORD will strike you with madness, with blindness, and with astonishment of heart."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You will grope at noonday, as a blind person gropes in darkness, and you will not prosper in your ways. You will only be oppressed and robbed always, and there will be no one to save you."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You will betroth a wife, and another man shall lie with her. You will build a house, and you won\u2019t dwell in it. You will plant a vineyard, and not use its fruit."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Your ox will be slain before your eyes, and you will not eat any of it. Your donkey will be violently taken away from before your face, and will not be restored to you. Your sheep will be given to your enemies, and you will have no one to save you."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Your sons and your daughters will be given to another people. Your eyes will look and fail with longing for them all day long. There will be no power in your hand."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"A nation which you don\u2019t know will eat the fruit of your ground and all of your work. You will only be oppressed and crushed always,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"so that the sights that you see with your eyes will drive you mad."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The LORD will strike you in the knees and in the legs with a sore boil, of which you cannot be healed, from the sole of your foot to the crown of your head."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The LORD will bring you, and your king whom you will set over yourselves, to a nation that you have not known, you nor your fathers. There you will serve other gods of wood and stone."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You will become an astonishment, a proverb, and a byword among all the peoples where the LORD will lead you away."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"You will carry much seed out into the field, and will gather little in, for the locust will consume it."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"You will plant vineyards and dress them, but you will neither drink of the wine, nor harvest, because worms will eat them."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"You will have olive trees throughout all your borders, but you won\u2019t anoint yourself with the oil, for your olives will drop off."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"You will father sons and daughters, but they will not be yours, for they will go into captivity."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Locusts will consume all of your trees and the fruit of your ground."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"The foreigner who is among you will mount up above you higher and higher, and you will come down lower and lower."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"He will lend to you, and you won\u2019t lend to him. He will be the head, and you will be the tail."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"All these curses will come on you, and will pursue you and overtake you, until you are destroyed, because you didn\u2019t listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice, to keep his commandments and his statutes which he commanded you."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"They will be for a sign and for a wonder to you and to your offspring forever."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Because you didn\u2019t serve the LORD your God with joyfulness and with gladness of heart, by reason of the abundance of all things;"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"therefore you will serve your enemies whom the LORD sends against you, in hunger, in thirst, in nakedness, and in lack of all things. He will put an iron yoke on your neck until he has destroyed you."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"The LORD will bring a nation against you from far away, from the end of the earth, as the eagle flies: a nation whose language you will not understand,"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"a nation of fierce facial expressions, that doesn\u2019t respect the elderly, nor show favor to the young."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"They will eat the fruit of your livestock and the fruit of your ground, until you are destroyed. They also won\u2019t leave you grain, new wine, oil, the increase of your livestock, or the young of your flock, until they have caused you to perish."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"They will besiege you in all your gates until your high and fortified walls in which you trusted come down throughout all your land. They will besiege you in all your gates throughout all your land which the LORD your God has given you."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"You will eat the fruit of your own body, the flesh of your sons and of your daughters, whom the LORD your God has given you, in the siege and in the distress with which your enemies will distress you."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"The man who is tender among you, and very delicate, his eye will be evil toward his brother, toward the wife whom he loves, and toward the remnant of his children whom he has remaining,"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"so that he will not give to any of them of the flesh of his children whom he will eat, because he has nothing left to him, in the siege and in the distress with which your enemy will distress you in all your gates."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"The tender and delicate woman among you, who would not venture to set the sole of her foot on the ground for delicateness and tenderness, her eye will be evil toward the husband that she loves, toward her son, toward her daughter,"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"toward her young one who comes out from between her feet, and toward her children whom she bears; for she will eat them secretly for lack of all things in the siege and in the distress with which your enemy will distress you in your gates."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"If you will not observe to do all the words of this law that are written in this book, that you may fear this glorious and fearful name, THE LORD your God,"]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:59,l:[[0,"then the LORD will make your plagues and the plagues of your offspring fearful, even great plagues, and of long duration, and severe sicknesses, and of long duration."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"He will bring on you again all the diseases of Egypt, which you were afraid of; and they will cling to you."]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"Also every sickness and every plague which is not written in the book of this law, the LORD will bring them on you until you are destroyed."]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"You will be left few in number, even though you were as the stars of the sky for multitude, because you didn\u2019t listen to the LORD your God\u2019s voice."]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"It will happen that as the LORD rejoiced over you to do you good, and to multiply you, so the LORD will rejoice over you to cause you to perish and to destroy you. You will be plucked from the land that you are going in to possess."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"The LORD will scatter you among all peoples, from one end of the earth to the other end of the earth. There you will serve other gods which you have not known, you nor your fathers, even wood and stone."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"Among these nations you will find no ease, and there will be no rest for the sole of your foot; but the LORD will give you there a trembling heart, failing of eyes, and pining of soul."]]},{v:66,l:[[0,"Your life will hang in doubt before you. You will be afraid night and day, and will have no assurance of your life."]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"In the morning you will say, \u201cI wish it were evening!\u201d and at evening you will say, \u201cI wish it were morning!\u201d for the fear of your heart which you will fear, and for the sights which your eyes will see."]]},{v:68,l:[[0,"The LORD will bring you into Egypt again with ships, by the way of which I told you that you would never see it again. There you will offer yourselves to your enemies for male and female slaves, and nobody will buy you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the words of the covenant which the LORD commanded Moses to make with the children of Israel in the land of Moab, in addition to the covenant which he made with them in Horeb."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Moses called to all Israel, and said to them:"],[0,"Your eyes have seen all that the LORD did in the land of Egypt to Pharaoh, and to all his servants, and to all his land;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"the great trials which your eyes saw, the signs, and those great wonders."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But the LORD has not given you a heart to know, eyes to see, and ears to hear, to this day."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I have led you forty years in the wilderness. Your clothes have not grown old on you, and your sandals have not grown old on your feet."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You have not eaten bread, neither have you drunk wine or strong drink, that you may know that I am the LORD your God."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When you came to this place, Sihon the king of Heshbon and Og the king of Bashan came out against us to battle, and we struck them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"We took their land, and gave it for an inheritance to the Reubenites, and to the Gadites, and to the half-tribe of the Manassites."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore keep the words of this covenant and do them, that you may prosper in all that you do."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All of you stand today in the presence of the LORD your God: your heads, your tribes, your elders, and your officers, even all the men of Israel,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"your little ones, your wives, and the foreigners who are in the middle of your camps, from the one who cuts your wood to the one who draws your water,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that you may enter into the covenant of the LORD your God, and into his oath, which the LORD your God makes with you today,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"that he may establish you today as his people, and that he may be your God, as he spoke to you and as he swore to your fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Neither do I make this covenant and this oath with you only,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but with those who stand here with us today before the LORD our God, and also with those who are not here with us today"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"(for you know how we lived in the land of Egypt, and how we came through the middle of the nations through which you passed;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and you have seen their abominations and their idols of wood, stone, silver, and gold, which were among them);"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"lest there should be among you man, woman, family, or tribe whose heart turns away today from the LORD our God, to go to serve the gods of those nations; lest there should be among you a root that produces bitter poison;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and it happen, when he hears the words of this curse, that he bless himself in his heart, saying, \u201cI shall have peace, though I walk in the stubbornness of my heart,\u201d to destroy the moist with the dry."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD will not pardon him, but then the LORD\u2019s anger and his jealousy will smoke against that man, and all the curse that is written in this book will fall on him, and the LORD will blot out his name from under the sky."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD will set him apart for evil out of all the tribes of Israel, according to all the curses of the covenant written in this book of the law."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The generation to come\u2014your children who will rise up after you, and the foreigner who will come from a far land\u2014will say, when they see the plagues of that land, and the sicknesses with which the LORD has made it sick,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"that all of its land is sulfur, salt, and burning, that it is not sown, doesn\u2019t produce, nor does any grass grow in it, like the overthrow of Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboiim, which the LORD overthrew in his anger, and in his wrath."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Even all the nations will say, \u201cWhy has the LORD done this to this land? What does the heat of this great anger mean?\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then men will say, \u201cBecause they abandoned the covenant of the LORD, the God of their fathers, which he made with them when he brought them out of the land of Egypt,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and went and served other gods and worshiped them, gods that they didn\u2019t know and that he had not given to them."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD\u2019s anger burned against this land, to bring on it all the curses that are written in this book."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The LORD rooted them out of their land in anger, in wrath, and in great indignation, and thrust them into another land, as it is today.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The secret things belong to the LORD our God; but the things that are revealed belong to us and to our children forever, that we may do all the words of this law."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall happen, when all these things have come on you, the blessing and the curse, which I have set before you, and you shall call them to mind among all the nations where the LORD your God has driven you,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and return to the LORD your God and obey his voice according to all that I command you today, you and your children, with all your heart and with all your soul,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"that then the LORD your God will release you from captivity, have compassion on you, and will return and gather you from all the peoples where the LORD your God has scattered you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If your outcasts are in the uttermost parts of the heavens, from there the LORD your God will gather you, and from there he will bring you back."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD your God will bring you into the land which your fathers possessed, and you will possess it. He will do you good, and increase your numbers more than your fathers."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD your God will circumcise your heart, and the heart of your offspring, to love the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul, that you may live."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD your God will put all these curses on your enemies and on those who hate you, who persecuted you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall return and obey the LORD\u2019s voice, and do all his commandments which I command you today."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The LORD your God will make you prosperous in all the work of your hand, in the fruit of your body, in the fruit of your livestock, and in the fruit of your ground, for good; for the LORD will again rejoice over you for good, as he rejoiced over your fathers,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"if you will obey the LORD your God\u2019s voice, to keep his commandments and his statutes which are written in this book of the law, if you turn to the LORD your God with all your heart and with all your soul."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"For this commandment which I command you today is not too hard for you or too distant."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It is not in heaven, that you should say, \u201cWho will go up for us to heaven, bring it to us, and proclaim it to us, that we may do it?\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Neither is it beyond the sea, that you should say, \u201cWho will go over the sea for us, bring it to us, and proclaim it to us, that we may do it?\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But the word is very near to you, in your mouth and in your heart, that you may do it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Behold, I have set before you today life and prosperity, and death and evil."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For I command you today to love the LORD your God, to walk in his ways and to keep his commandments, his statutes, and his ordinances, that you may live and multiply, and that the LORD your God may bless you in the land where you go in to possess it."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But if your heart turns away, and you will not hear, but are drawn away and worship other gods, and serve them,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I declare to you today that you will surely perish. You will not prolong your days in the land where you pass over the Jordan to go in to possess it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I call heaven and earth to witness against you today that I have set before you life and death, the blessing and the curse. Therefore choose life, that you may live, you and your descendants,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"to love the LORD your God, to obey his voice, and to cling to him; for he is your life, and the length of your days, that you may dwell in the land which the LORD swore to your fathers, to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, to give them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went and spoke these words to all Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cI am one hundred twenty years old today. I can no more go out and come in. The LORD has said to me, \u2018You shall not go over this Jordan.\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD your God himself will go over before you. He will destroy these nations from before you, and you shall dispossess them. Joshua will go over before you, as the LORD has spoken."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD will do to them as he did to Sihon and to Og, the kings of the Amorites, and to their land, when he destroyed them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD will deliver them up before you, and you shall do to them according to all the commandment which I have commanded you."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Be strong and courageous. Don\u2019t be afraid or scared of them, for the LORD your God himself is who goes with you. He will not fail you nor forsake you.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses called to Joshua, and said to him in the sight of all Israel, \u201cBe strong and courageous, for you shall go with this people into the land which the LORD has sworn to their fathers to give them; and you shall cause them to inherit it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD himself is who goes before you. He will be with you. He will not fail you nor forsake you. Don\u2019t be afraid. Don\u2019t be discouraged.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses wrote this law and delivered it to the priests the sons of Levi, who bore the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, and to all the elders of Israel."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Moses commanded them, saying, \u201cAt the end of every seven years, in the set time of the year of release, in the feast of booths,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"when all Israel has come to appear before the LORD your God in the place which he will choose, you shall read this law before all Israel in their hearing."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Assemble the people, the men and the women and the little ones, and the foreigners who are within your gates, that they may hear, learn, fear the LORD your God, and observe to do all the words of this law,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and that their children, who have not known, may hear and learn to fear the LORD your God, as long as you live in the land where you go over the Jordan to possess it.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cBehold, your days approach that you must die. Call Joshua, and present yourselves in the Tent of Meeting, that I may commission him.\u201d"],[0,"Moses and Joshua went, and presented themselves in the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared in the Tent in a pillar of cloud, and the pillar of cloud stood over the Tent\u2019s door."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Moses, \u201cBehold, you shall sleep with your fathers. This people will rise up and play the prostitute after the strange gods of the land where they go to be among them, and will forsake me and break my covenant which I have made with them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then my anger shall be kindled against them in that day, and I will forsake them, and I will hide my face from them, and they shall be devoured, and many evils and troubles shall come on them; so that they will say in that day, \u2018Haven\u2019t these evils come on us because our God is not among us?\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I will surely hide my face in that day for all the evil which they have done, in that they have turned to other gods."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore write this song for yourselves, and teach it to the children of Israel. Put it in their mouths, that this song may be a witness for me against the children of Israel."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For when I have brought them into the land which I swore to their fathers, flowing with milk and honey, and they have eaten and filled themselves, and grown fat, then they will turn to other gods, and serve them, and despise me, and break my covenant."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"It will happen, when many evils and troubles have come on them, that this song will testify before them as a witness; for it will not be forgotten out of the mouths of their descendants; for I know their ways and what they are doing today, before I have brought them into the land which I promised them.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"So Moses wrote this song the same day, and taught it to the children of Israel."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He commissioned Joshua the son of Nun, and said, \u201cBe strong and courageous; for you shall bring the children of Israel into the land which I swore to them. I will be with you.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When Moses had finished writing the words of this law in a book, until they were finished,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Moses commanded the Levites, who bore the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, saying,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u201cTake this book of the law, and put it by the side of the ark of the LORD your God\u2019s covenant, that it may be there for a witness against you."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For I know your rebellion and your stiff neck. Behold, while I am yet alive with you today, you have been rebellious against the LORD. How much more after my death?"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Assemble to me all the elders of your tribes and your officers, that I may speak these words in their ears, and call heaven and earth to witness against them."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For I know that after my death you will utterly corrupt yourselves, and turn away from the way which I have commanded you; and evil will happen to you in the latter days, because you will do that which is evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, to provoke him to anger through the work of your hands.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses spoke in the ears of all the assembly of Israel the words of this song, until they were finished."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Give ear, you heavens, and I will speak."],[2,"Let the earth hear the words of my mouth."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My doctrine will drop as the rain."],[2,"My speech will condense as the dew,"],[2,"as the misty rain on the tender grass,"],[2,"as the showers on the herb."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will proclaim the LORD\u2019s name."],[2,"Ascribe greatness to our God!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The Rock: his work is perfect,"],[2,"for all his ways are just."],[2,"A God of faithfulness who does no wrong,"],[2,"just and right is he."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They have dealt corruptly with him."],[2,"They are not his children, because of their defect."],[2,"They are a perverse and crooked generation."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Is this the way you repay the LORD,"],[2,"foolish and unwise people?"],[1,"Isn\u2019t he your father who has bought you?"],[2,"He has made you and established you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember the days of old."],[2,"Consider the years of many generations."],[1,"Ask your father, and he will show you;"],[2,"your elders, and they will tell you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"When the Most High gave to the nations their inheritance,"],[2,"when he separated the children of men,"],[1,"he set the bounds of the peoples"],[2,"according to the number of the children of Israel."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD\u2019s portion is his people."],[2,"Jacob is the lot of his inheritance."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He found him in a desert land,"],[2,"in the waste howling wilderness."],[1,"He surrounded him."],[2,"He cared for him."],[2,"He kept him as the apple of his eye."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"As an eagle that stirs up her nest,"],[2,"that flutters over her young,"],[1,"he spread abroad his wings,"],[2,"he took them,"],[2,"he bore them on his feathers."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD alone led him."],[2,"There was no foreign god with him."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He made him ride on the high places of the earth."],[2,"He ate the increase of the field."],[1,"He caused him to suck honey out of the rock,"],[2,"oil out of the flinty rock;"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"butter from the herd, and milk from the flock,"],[2,"with fat of lambs,"],[2,"rams of the breed of Bashan, and goats,"],[2,"with the finest of the wheat."],[2,"From the blood of the grape, you drank wine."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"But Jeshurun grew fat, and kicked."],[2,"You have grown fat."],[2,"You have grown thick."],[2,"You have become sleek."],[1,"Then he abandoned God who made him,"],[2,"and rejected the Rock of his salvation."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"They moved him to jealousy with strange gods."],[2,"They provoked him to anger with abominations."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"They sacrificed to demons, not God,"],[2,"to gods that they didn\u2019t know,"],[2,"to new gods that came up recently,"],[2,"which your fathers didn\u2019t dread."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the Rock who became your father, you are unmindful,"],[2,"and have forgotten God who gave you birth."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD saw and abhorred,"],[2,"because of the provocation of his sons and his daughters."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He said, \u201cI will hide my face from them."],[2,"I will see what their end will be;"],[1,"for they are a very perverse generation,"],[2,"children in whom is no faithfulness."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"They have moved me to jealousy with that which is not God."],[2,"They have provoked me to anger with their vanities."],[1,"I will move them to jealousy with those who are not a people."],[2,"I will provoke them to anger with a foolish nation."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For a fire is kindled in my anger,"],[2,"that burns to the lowest Sheol,"],[2,"devours the earth with its increase,"],[2,"and sets the foundations of the mountains on fire."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will heap evils on them."],[2,"I will spend my arrows on them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall be wasted with hunger,"],[2,"and devoured with burning heat"],[2,"and bitter destruction."],[1,"I will send the teeth of animals on them,"],[2,"with the venom of vipers that glide in the dust."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Outside the sword will bereave,"],[2,"and in the rooms,"],[2,"terror on both young man and virgin,"],[2,"the nursing infant with the gray-haired man."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"I said that I would scatter them afar."],[2,"I would make their memory to cease from among men;"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"were it not that I feared the provocation of the enemy,"],[2,"lest their adversaries should judge wrongly,"],[2,"lest they should say, \u2018Our hand is exalted;"],[2,"the LORD has not done all this.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"For they are a nation void of counsel."],[2,"There is no understanding in them."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that they were wise, that they understood this,"],[2,"that they would consider their latter end!"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"How could one chase a thousand,"],[2,"and two put ten thousand to flight,"],[1,"unless their Rock had sold them,"],[2,"and the LORD had delivered them up?"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"For their rock is not as our Rock,"],[2,"even our enemies themselves concede."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"For their vine is of the vine of Sodom,"],[2,"of the fields of Gomorrah."],[1,"Their grapes are poison grapes."],[2,"Their clusters are bitter."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Their wine is the poison of serpents,"],[2,"the cruel venom of asps."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIsn\u2019t this laid up in store with me,"],[2,"sealed up among my treasures?"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"Vengeance is mine, and recompense,"],[2,"at the time when their foot slides,"],[1,"for the day of their calamity is at hand."],[2,"Their doom rushes at them.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD will judge his people,"],[2,"and have compassion on his servants,"],[1,"when he sees that their power is gone,"],[2,"that there is no one remaining, shut up or left at large."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"He will say, \u201cWhere are their gods,"],[2,"the rock in which they took refuge,"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"which ate the fat of their sacrifices,"],[2,"and drank the wine of their drink offering?"],[1,"Let them rise up and help you!"],[2,"Let them be your protection."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSee now that I myself am he."],[2,"There is no god with me."],[1,"I kill and I make alive."],[2,"I wound and I heal."],[2,"There is no one who can deliver out of my hand."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"For I lift up my hand to heaven and declare,"],[2,"as I live forever,"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"if I sharpen my glittering sword,"],[2,"my hand grasps it in judgment;"],[1,"I will take vengeance on my adversaries,"],[2,"and will repay those who hate me."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make my arrows drunk with blood."],[2,"My sword shall devour flesh with the blood of the slain and the captives,"],[2,"from the head of the leaders of the enemy.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Rejoice, you nations, with his people,"],[2,"for he will avenge the blood of his servants."],[2,"He will take vengeance on his adversaries,"],[2,"and will make atonement for his land and for his people."]],f:["For this verse, LXX reads: Rejoice, you heavens, with him, and let all the angels of God worship him; rejoice you Gentiles, with his people, and let all the sons of God strengthen themselves in him; for he will avenge the blood of his sons, and he will give vengeance, and recompense justice to his enemies, and will reward them that hate him; and the Lord shall purge the land of his people."]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses came and spoke all the words of this song in the ears of the people, he and Joshua the son of Nun."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Moses finished reciting all these words to all Israel."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cSet your heart to all the words which I testify to you today, which you shall command your children to observe to do, all the words of this law."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"For it is no vain thing for you, because it is your life, and through this thing you shall prolong your days in the land, where you go over the Jordan to possess it.\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Moses that same day, saying,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"\u201cGo up into this mountain of Abarim, to Mount Nebo, which is in the land of Moab, that is across from Jericho; and see the land of Canaan, which I give to the children of Israel for a possession."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Die on the mountain where you go up, and be gathered to your people, as Aaron your brother died on Mount Hor, and was gathered to his people;"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"because you trespassed against me among the children of Israel at the waters of Meribah of Kadesh, in the wilderness of Zin; because you didn\u2019t uphold my holiness among the children of Israel."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"For you shall see the land from a distance; but you shall not go there into the land which I give the children of Israel.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the blessing with which Moses the man of God blessed the children of Israel before his death."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said,"],[1,"\u201cThe LORD came from Sinai,"],[2,"and rose from Seir to them."],[1,"He shone from Mount Paran."],[2,"He came from the ten thousands of holy ones."],[2,"At his right hand was a fiery law for them."]],f:["another manuscript reads \u201cHe came with myriads of holy ones from the south, from his mountain slopes.\u201d"]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, he loves the people."],[2,"All his saints are in your hand."],[2,"They sat down at your feet."],[2,"Each receives your words."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Moses commanded us a law,"],[2,"an inheritance for the assembly of Jacob."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He was king in Jeshurun,"],[2,"when the heads of the people were gathered,"],[2,"all the tribes of Israel together."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLet Reuben live, and not die;"],[2,"Nor let his men be few.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"This is for Judah. He said,"],[1,"\u201cHear, LORD, the voice of Judah."],[2,"Bring him in to his people."],[1,"With his hands he contended for himself."],[2,"You shall be a help against his adversaries.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"About Levi he said,"],[1,"\u201cYour Thummim and your Urim are with your godly one,"],[2,"whom you proved at Massah,"],[2,"with whom you contended at the waters of Meribah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He said of his father, and of his mother, \u2018I have not seen him.\u2019"],[2,"He didn\u2019t acknowledge his brothers,"],[2,"nor did he know his own children;"],[1,"for they have observed your word,"],[2,"and keep your covenant."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall teach Jacob your ordinances,"],[2,"and Israel your law."],[1,"They shall put incense before you,"],[2,"and whole burnt offering on your altar."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, bless his skills."],[2,"Accept the work of his hands."],[1,"Strike through the hips of those who rise up against him,"],[2,"of those who hate him, that they not rise again.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"About Benjamin he said,"],[1,"\u201cThe beloved of the LORD will dwell in safety by him."],[2,"He covers him all day long."],[2,"He dwells between his shoulders.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"About Joseph he said,"],[1,"\u201cHis land is blessed by the LORD,"],[2,"for the precious things of the heavens, for the dew,"],[2,"for the deep that couches beneath,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"for the precious things of the fruits of the sun,"],[2,"for the precious things that the moon can yield,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"for the best things of the ancient mountains,"],[2,"for the precious things of the everlasting hills,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"for the precious things of the earth and its fullness,"],[2,"the good will of him who lived in the bush."],[1,"Let this come on the head of Joseph,"],[2,"on the crown of the head of him who was separated from his brothers."]],f:["i.e., the burning bush of Exodus 3:3-4."]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Majesty belongs to the firstborn of his herd."],[2,"His horns are the horns of the wild ox."],[2,"With them he will push all the peoples to the ends of the earth."],[1,"They are the ten thousands of Ephraim."],[2,"They are the thousands of Manasseh.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"About Zebulun he said,"],[1,"\u201cRejoice, Zebulun, in your going out;"],[2,"and Issachar, in your tents."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"They will call the peoples to the mountain."],[2,"There they will offer sacrifices of righteousness,"],[1,"for they will draw out the abundance of the seas,"],[2,"the hidden treasures of the sand.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"About Gad he said,"],[1,"\u201cHe who enlarges Gad is blessed."],[2,"He dwells as a lioness,"],[2,"and tears the arm and the crown of the head."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He provided the first part for himself,"],[2,"for the lawgiver\u2019s portion was reserved for him."],[1,"He came with the heads of the people."],[2,"He executed the righteousness of the LORD,"],[2,"His ordinances with Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"About Dan he said,"],[1,"\u201cDan is a lion\u2019s cub"],[2,"that leaps out of Bashan.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"About Naphtali he said,"],[1,"\u201cNaphtali, satisfied with favor,"],[2,"full of the LORD\u2019s blessing,"],[2,"Possess the west and the south.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"About Asher he said,"],[1,"\u201cAsher is blessed with children."],[2,"Let him be acceptable to his brothers."],[2,"Let him dip his foot in oil."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Your bars will be iron and bronze."],[2,"As your days, so your strength will be."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThere is no one like God, Jeshurun,"],[2,"who rides on the heavens for your help,"],[2,"in his excellency on the skies."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The eternal God is your dwelling place."],[2,"Underneath are the everlasting arms."],[1,"He thrust out the enemy from before you,"],[2,"and said, \u2018Destroy!\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel dwells in safety,"],[2,"the fountain of Jacob alone,"],[1,"In a land of grain and new wine."],[2,"Yes, his heavens drop down dew."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"You are happy, Israel!"],[2,"Who is like you, a people saved by the LORD,"],[2,"the shield of your help,"],[2,"the sword of your excellency?"],[1,"Your enemies will submit themselves to you."],[2,"You will tread on their high places.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses went up from the plains of Moab to Mount Nebo, to the top of Pisgah, that is opposite Jericho. The LORD showed him all the land of Gilead to Dan,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and all Naphtali, and the land of Ephraim and Manasseh, and all the land of Judah, to the Western Sea,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and the south, and the Plain of the valley of Jericho the city of palm trees, to Zoar."]],f:["or, Negev"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cThis is the land which I swore to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, saying, \u2018I will give it to your offspring.\u2019 I have caused you to see it with your eyes, but you shall not go over there.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"So Moses the servant of the LORD died there in the land of Moab, according to the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He buried him in the valley in the land of Moab opposite Beth Peor, but no man knows where his tomb is to this day."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Moses was one hundred twenty years old when he died. His eye was not dim, nor his strength gone."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of Israel wept for Moses in the plains of Moab thirty days, until the days of weeping in the mourning for Moses were ended."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Joshua the son of Nun was full of the spirit of wisdom, for Moses had laid his hands on him. The children of Israel listened to him, and did as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Since then, there has not arisen a prophet in Israel like Moses, whom the LORD knew face to face,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"in all the signs and the wonders which the LORD sent him to do in the land of Egypt, to Pharaoh, and to all his servants, and to all his land,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and in all the mighty hand, and in all the awesome deeds, which Moses did in the sight of all Israel."]]}]]}},1276,[]);
__d(function(e,t,h,o,a,n,i){a.exports={book:"Josh",name:"Joshua",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after the death of Moses the servant of the LORD, the LORD spoke to Joshua the son of Nun, Moses\u2019 servant, saying,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cMoses my servant is dead. Now therefore arise, go across this Jordan, you and all these people, to the land which I am giving to them, even to the children of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I have given you every place that the sole of your foot will tread on, as I told Moses."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"From the wilderness and this Lebanon even to the great river, the river Euphrates, all the land of the Hittites, and to the great sea toward the going down of the sun, shall be your border."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"No man will be able to stand before you all the days of your life. As I was with Moses, so I will be with you. I will not fail you nor forsake you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBe strong and courageous; for you shall cause this people to inherit the land which I swore to their fathers to give them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Only be strong and very courageous. Be careful to observe to do according to all the law which Moses my servant commanded you. Don\u2019t turn from it to the right hand or to the left, that you may have good success wherever you go."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"This book of the law shall not depart from your mouth, but you shall meditate on it day and night, that you may observe to do according to all that is written in it; for then you shall make your way prosperous, and then you shall have good success."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Haven\u2019t I commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Don\u2019t be afraid. Don\u2019t be dismayed, for the LORD your God is with you wherever you go.\u201d"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joshua commanded the officers of the people, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cPass through the middle of the camp, and command the people, saying, \u2018Prepare food; for within three days you are to pass over this Jordan, to go in to possess the land which the LORD your God gives you to possess.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua spoke to the Reubenites, and to the Gadites, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cRemember the word which Moses the servant of the LORD commanded you, saying, \u2018The LORD your God gives you rest, and will give you this land."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Your wives, your little ones, and your livestock shall live in the land which Moses gave you beyond the Jordan; but you shall pass over before your brothers armed, all the mighty men of valor, and shall help them"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"until the LORD has given your brothers rest, as he has given you, and they have also possessed the land which the LORD your God gives them. Then you shall return to the land of your possession and possess it, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave you beyond the Jordan toward the sunrise.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered Joshua, saying, \u201cAll that you have commanded us we will do, and wherever you send us we will go."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Just as we listened to Moses in all things, so will we listen to you. Only may the LORD your God be with you, as he was with Moses."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Whoever rebels against your commandment, and doesn\u2019t listen to your words in all that you command him shall himself be put to death. Only be strong and courageous.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua the son of Nun secretly sent two men out of Shittim as spies, saying, \u201cGo, view the land, including Jericho.\u201d They went and came into the house of a prostitute whose name was Rahab, and slept there."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Jericho was told, \u201cBehold, men of the children of Israel came in here tonight to spy out the land.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Jericho\u2019s king sent to Rahab, saying, \u201cBring out the men who have come to you, who have entered into your house; for they have come to spy out all the land.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman took the two men and hid them. Then she said, \u201cYes, the men came to me, but I didn\u2019t know where they came from."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"About the time of the shutting of the gate, when it was dark, the men went out. Where the men went, I don\u2019t know. Pursue them quickly. You may catch up with them.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But she had brought them up to the roof, and hidden them under the stalks of flax which she had laid in order on the roof."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The men pursued them along the way to the fords of the Jordan River. As soon as those who pursued them had gone out, they shut the gate."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Before they had lain down, she came up to them on the roof."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"She said to the men, \u201cI know that the LORD has given you the land, and that the fear of you has fallen upon us, and that all the inhabitants of the land melt away before you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For we have heard how the LORD dried up the water of the Red Sea before you, when you came out of Egypt; and what you did to the two kings of the Amorites, who were beyond the Jordan, to Sihon and to Og, whom you utterly destroyed."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"As soon as we had heard it, our hearts melted, and there wasn\u2019t any more spirit in any man, because of you: for the LORD your God, he is God in heaven above, and on earth beneath."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please swear to me by the LORD, since I have dealt kindly with you, that you also will deal kindly with my father\u2019s house, and give me a true sign;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and that you will save alive my father, my mother, my brothers, and my sisters, and all that they have, and will deliver our lives from death.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The men said to her, \u201cOur life for yours, if you don\u2019t talk about this business of ours; and it shall be, when the LORD gives us the land, that we will deal kindly and truly with you.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she let them down by a cord through the window; for her house was on the side of the wall, and she lived on the wall."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"She said to them, \u201cGo to the mountain, lest the pursuers find you. Hide yourselves there three days, until the pursuers have returned. Afterward, you may go your way.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The men said to her, \u201cWe will be guiltless of this your oath which you\u2019ve made us to swear."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Behold, when we come into the land, tie this line of scarlet thread in the window which you used to let us down. Gather to yourself into the house your father, your mother, your brothers, and all your father\u2019s household."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"It shall be that whoever goes out of the doors of your house into the street, his blood will be on his head, and we will be guiltless. Whoever is with you in the house, his blood shall be on our head, if any hand is on him."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But if you talk about this business of ours, then we shall be guiltless of your oath which you\u2019ve made us to swear.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cLet it be as you have said.\u201d She sent them away, and they departed. Then she tied the scarlet line in the window."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"They went and came to the mountain, and stayed there three days, until the pursuers had returned. The pursuers sought them all along the way, but didn\u2019t find them."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then the two men returned, descended from the mountain, crossed the river, and came to Joshua the son of Nun. They told him all that had happened to them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They said to Joshua, \u201cTruly the LORD has delivered all the land into our hands. Moreover, all the inhabitants of the land melt away before us.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua got up early in the morning; and they moved from Shittim and came to the Jordan, he and all the children of Israel. They camped there before they crossed over."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"After three days, the officers went through the middle of the camp;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and they commanded the people, saying, \u201cWhen you see the ark of the LORD your God\u2019s covenant, and the Levitical priests bearing it, then leave your place and follow it."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Yet there shall be a space between you and it of about two thousand cubits by measure\u2014don\u2019t come closer to it\u2014that you may know the way by which you must go; for you have not passed this way before.\u201d"]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters, so 2,000 cubits is about 920 meters."]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua said to the people, \u201cSanctify yourselves; for tomorrow the LORD will do wonders among you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua spoke to the priests, saying, \u201cTake up the ark of the covenant, and cross over before the people.\u201d They took up the ark of the covenant, and went before the people."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cToday I will begin to magnify you in the sight of all Israel, that they may know that as I was with Moses, so I will be with you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall command the priests who bear the ark of the covenant, saying, \u2018When you come to the brink of the waters of the Jordan, you shall stand still in the Jordan.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua said to the children of Israel, \u201cCome here, and hear the words of the LORD your God.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Joshua said, \u201cBy this you shall know that the living God is among you, and that he will without fail drive the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Hivite, the Perizzite, the Girgashite, the Amorite, and the Jebusite out from before you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Behold, the ark of the covenant of the Lord of all the earth passes over before you into the Jordan."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now therefore take twelve men out of the tribes of Israel, for every tribe a man."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It shall be that when the soles of the feet of the priests who bear the ark of GOD, the Lord of all the earth, rest in the waters of the Jordan, that the waters of the Jordan will be cut off. The waters that come down from above shall stand in one heap.\u201d"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When the people moved from their tents to pass over the Jordan, the priests who bore the ark of the covenant being before the people,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and when those who bore the ark had come to the Jordan, and the feet of the priests who bore the ark had dipped in the edge of the water (for the Jordan overflows all its banks all the time of harvest),"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the waters which came down from above stood, and rose up in one heap a great way off, at Adam, the city that is beside Zarethan; and those that went down toward the sea of the Arabah, even the Salt Sea, were wholly cut off. Then the people passed over near Jericho."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The priests who bore the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant stood firm on dry ground in the middle of the Jordan; and all Israel crossed over on dry ground, until all the nation had passed completely over the Jordan."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When all the nation had completely crossed over the Jordan, the LORD spoke to Joshua, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cTake twelve men out of the people, a man out of every tribe,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and command them, saying, \u2018Take from out of the middle of the Jordan, out of the place where the priests\u2019 feet stood firm, twelve stones, carry them over with you, and lay them down in the place where you\u2019ll camp tonight.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joshua called the twelve men whom he had prepared of the children of Israel, a man out of every tribe."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Joshua said to them, \u201cCross before the ark of the LORD your God into the middle of the Jordan, and each of you pick up a stone and put it on your shoulder, according to the number of the tribes of the children of Israel;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"that this may be a sign among you, that when your children ask in the future, saying, \u2018What do you mean by these stones?\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"then you shall tell them, \u2018Because the waters of the Jordan were cut off before the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant. When it crossed over the Jordan, the waters of the Jordan were cut off. These stones shall be for a memorial to the children of Israel forever.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did as Joshua commanded, and took up twelve stones out of the middle of the Jordan, as the LORD spoke to Joshua, according to the number of the tribes of the children of Israel. They carried them over with them to the place where they camped, and laid them down there."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Joshua set up twelve stones in the middle of the Jordan, in the place where the feet of the priests who bore the ark of the covenant stood; and they are there to this day."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the priests who bore the ark stood in the middle of the Jordan until everything was finished that the LORD commanded Joshua to speak to the people, according to all that Moses commanded Joshua; and the people hurried and passed over."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When all the people had completely crossed over, the LORD\u2019s ark crossed over with the priests in the presence of the people."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Reuben, and the children of Gad, and the half-tribe of Manasseh crossed over armed before the children of Israel, as Moses spoke to them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"About forty thousand men, ready and armed for war, passed over before the LORD to battle, to the plains of Jericho."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"On that day, the LORD magnified Joshua in the sight of all Israel; and they feared him, as they feared Moses, all the days of his life."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Joshua, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cCommand the priests who bear the ark of the covenant, that they come up out of the Jordan.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua therefore commanded the priests, saying, \u201cCome up out of the Jordan!\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When the priests who bore the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant had come up out of the middle of the Jordan, and the soles of the priests\u2019 feet had been lifted up to the dry ground, the waters of the Jordan returned to their place, and went over all its banks, as before."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The people came up out of the Jordan on the tenth day of the first month, and encamped in Gilgal, on the east border of Jericho."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua set up those twelve stones, which they took out of the Jordan, in Gilgal."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He spoke to the children of Israel, saying, \u201cWhen your children ask their fathers in time to come, saying, \u2018What do these stones mean?\u2019"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Then you shall let your children know, saying, \u2018Israel came over this Jordan on dry land."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For the LORD your God dried up the waters of the Jordan from before you until you had crossed over, as the LORD your God did to the Red Sea, which he dried up from before us, until we had crossed over,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"that all the peoples of the earth may know that the LORD\u2019s hand is mighty, and that you may fear the LORD your God forever.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When all the kings of the Amorites, who were beyond the Jordan westward, and all the kings of the Canaanites, who were by the sea, heard how the LORD had dried up the waters of the Jordan from before the children of Israel until we had crossed over, their heart melted, and there was no more spirit in them, because of the children of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"At that time, the LORD said to Joshua, \u201cMake flint knives, and circumcise again the sons of Israel the second time.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Joshua made himself flint knives, and circumcised the sons of Israel at the hill of the foreskins."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"This is the reason Joshua circumcised them: all the people who came out of Egypt, who were males, even all the men of war, died in the wilderness along the way, after they came out of Egypt."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For all the people who came out were circumcised; but all the people who were born in the wilderness along the way as they came out of Egypt had not been circumcised."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the children of Israel walked forty years in the wilderness until all the nation, even the men of war who came out of Egypt, were consumed, because they didn\u2019t listen to the LORD\u2019s voice. The LORD swore to them that he wouldn\u2019t let them see the land which the LORD swore to their fathers that he would give us, a land flowing with milk and honey."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Their children, whom he raised up in their place, were circumcised by Joshua, for they were uncircumcised, because they had not circumcised them on the way."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When they were done circumcising the whole nation, they stayed in their places in the camp until they were healed."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cToday I have rolled away the reproach of Egypt from you.\u201d Therefore the name of that place was called Gilgal to this day."]],f:["\u201cGilgal\u201d sounds like the Hebrew for \u201croll.\u201d"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The children of Israel encamped in Gilgal. They kept the Passover on the fourteenth day of the month at evening in the plains of Jericho."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They ate unleavened cakes and parched grain of the produce of the land on the next day after the Passover, in the same day."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The manna ceased on the next day, after they had eaten of the produce of the land. The children of Israel didn\u2019t have manna any more, but they ate of the fruit of the land of Canaan that year."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joshua was by Jericho, he lifted up his eyes and looked, and behold, a man stood in front of him with his sword drawn in his hand. Joshua went to him and said to him, \u201cAre you for us, or for our enemies?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cNo; but I have come now as commander of the LORD\u2019s army.\u201d"],[0,"Joshua fell on his face to the earth, and worshiped, and asked him, \u201cWhat does my lord say to his servant?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The prince of the LORD\u2019s army said to Joshua, \u201cTake off your sandals, for the place on which you stand is holy.\u201d Joshua did so."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jericho was tightly shut up because of the children of Israel. No one went out, and no one came in."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cBehold, I have given Jericho into your hand, with its king and the mighty men of valor."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All of your men of war shall march around the city, going around the city once. You shall do this six days."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Seven priests shall bear seven trumpets of rams\u2019 horns before the ark. On the seventh day, you shall march around the city seven times, and the priests shall blow the trumpets."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It shall be that when they make a long blast with the ram\u2019s horn, and when you hear the sound of the trumpet, all the people shall shout with a great shout; then the city wall will fall down flat, and the people shall go up, every man straight in front of him.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua the son of Nun called the priests, and said to them, \u201cTake up the ark of the covenant, and let seven priests bear seven trumpets of rams\u2019 horns before the LORD\u2019s ark.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to the people, \u201cAdvance! March around the city, and let the armed men pass on before the LORD\u2019s ark.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"It was so, that when Joshua had spoken to the people, the seven priests bearing the seven trumpets of rams\u2019 horns before the LORD advanced and blew the trumpets, and the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant followed them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The armed men went before the priests who blew the trumpets, and the ark went after them. The trumpets sounded as they went."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua commanded the people, saying, \u201cYou shall not shout nor let your voice be heard, neither shall any word proceed out of your mouth until the day I tell you to shout. Then you shall shout.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"So he caused the LORD\u2019s ark to go around the city, circling it once. Then they came into the camp, and stayed in the camp."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Joshua rose early in the morning, and the priests took up the LORD\u2019s ark."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The seven priests bearing the seven trumpets of rams\u2019 horns in front of the LORD\u2019s ark went on continually, and blew the trumpets. The armed men went in front of them. The rear guard came after the LORD\u2019s ark. The trumpets sounded as they went."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The second day they marched around the city once, and returned into the camp. They did this six days."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"On the seventh day, they rose early at the dawning of the day, and marched around the city in the same way seven times. On this day only they marched around the city seven times."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"At the seventh time, when the priests blew the trumpets, Joshua said to the people, \u201cShout, for the LORD has given you the city!"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The city shall be devoted, even it and all that is in it, to the LORD. Only Rahab the prostitute shall live, she and all who are with her in the house, because she hid the messengers that we sent."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But as for you, only keep yourselves from what is devoted to destruction, lest when you have devoted it, you take of the devoted thing; so you would make the camp of Israel accursed and trouble it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But all the silver, gold, and vessels of bronze and iron are holy to the LORD. They shall come into the LORD\u2019s treasury.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"So the people shouted and the priests blew the trumpets. When the people heard the sound of the trumpet, the people shouted with a great shout, and the wall fell down flat, so that the people went up into the city, every man straight in front of him, and they took the city."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They utterly destroyed all that was in the city, both man and woman, both young and old, and ox, sheep, and donkey, with the edge of the sword."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Joshua said to the two men who had spied out the land, \u201cGo into the prostitute\u2019s house, and bring the woman and all that she has out from there, as you swore to her.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The young men who were spies went in, and brought out Rahab with her father, her mother, her brothers, and all that she had. They also brought out all of her relatives, and they set them outside of the camp of Israel."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They burned the city with fire, and all that was in it. Only they put the silver, the gold, and the vessels of bronze and of iron into the treasury of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But Rahab the prostitute, her father\u2019s household, and all that she had, Joshua saved alive. She lives in the middle of Israel to this day, because she hid the messengers whom Joshua sent to spy out Jericho."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua commanded them with an oath at that time, saying, \u201cCursed is the man before the LORD who rises up and builds this city Jericho. With the loss of his firstborn he will lay its foundation, and with the loss of his youngest son he will set up its gates.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"So the LORD was with Joshua; and his fame was in all the land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But the children of Israel committed a trespass in the devoted things; for Achan, the son of Carmi, the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the tribe of Judah, took some of the devoted things. Therefore the LORD\u2019s anger burned against the children of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Joshua sent men from Jericho to Ai, which is beside Beth Aven, on the east side of Bethel, and spoke to them, saying, \u201cGo up and spy out the land.\u201d"],[0,"The men went up and spied out Ai."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They returned to Joshua, and said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t let all the people go up, but let about two or three thousand men go up and strike Ai. Don\u2019t make all the people to toil there, for there are only a few of them.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"So about three thousand men of the people went up there, and they fled before the men of Ai."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The men of Ai struck about thirty-six men of them. They chased them from before the gate even to Shebarim, and struck them at the descent. The hearts of the people melted, and became like water."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Joshua tore his clothes, and fell to the earth on his face before the LORD\u2019s ark until the evening, he and the elders of Israel; and they put dust on their heads."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Joshua said, \u201cAlas, Lord GOD, why have you brought this people over the Jordan at all, to deliver us into the hand of the Amorites, to cause us to perish? I wish that we had been content and lived beyond the Jordan!"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Oh, Lord, what shall I say, after Israel has turned their backs before their enemies?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For the Canaanites and all the inhabitants of the land will hear of it, and will surround us, and cut off our name from the earth. What will you do for your great name?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cGet up! Why have you fallen on your face like that?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Israel has sinned. Yes, they have even transgressed my covenant which I commanded them. Yes, they have even taken some of the devoted things, and have also stolen, and also deceived. They have even put it among their own stuff."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore the children of Israel can\u2019t stand before their enemies. They turn their backs before their enemies, because they have become devoted for destruction. I will not be with you any more, unless you destroy the devoted things from among you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Get up! Sanctify the people, and say, \u2018Sanctify yourselves for tomorrow, for the LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u201cThere is a devoted thing among you, Israel. You cannot stand before your enemies until you take away the devoted thing from among you.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"In the morning therefore you shall be brought near by your tribes. It shall be that the tribe which the LORD selects shall come near by families. The family which the LORD selects shall come near by households. The household which the LORD selects shall come near man by man."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"It shall be, that he who is taken with the devoted thing shall be burned with fire, he and all that he has, because he has transgressed the LORD\u2019s covenant, and because he has done a disgraceful thing in Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joshua rose up early in the morning and brought Israel near by their tribes. The tribe of Judah was selected."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He brought near the family of Judah, and he selected the family of the Zerahites. He brought near the family of the Zerahites man by man, and Zabdi was selected."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He brought near his household man by man, and Achan, the son of Carmi, the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the tribe of Judah, was selected."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Joshua said to Achan, \u201cMy son, please give glory to the LORD, the God of Israel, and make confession to him. Tell me now what you have done! Don\u2019t hide it from me!\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Achan answered Joshua, and said, \u201cI have truly sinned against the LORD, the God of Israel, and this is what I have done."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When I saw among the plunder a beautiful Babylonian robe, two hundred shekels of silver, and a wedge of gold weighing fifty shekels, then I coveted them and took them. Behold, they are hidden in the ground in the middle of my tent, with the silver under it.\u201d"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joshua sent messengers, and they ran to the tent. Behold, it was hidden in his tent, with the silver under it."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They took them from the middle of the tent, and brought them to Joshua and to all the children of Israel. They laid them down before the LORD."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Joshua, and all Israel with him, took Achan the son of Zerah, the silver, the robe, the wedge of gold, his sons, his daughters, his cattle, his donkeys, his sheep, his tent, and all that he had; and they brought them up to the valley of Achor."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Joshua said, \u201cWhy have you troubled us? The LORD will trouble you today.\u201d All Israel stoned him with stones, and they burned them with fire and stoned them with stones."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They raised over him a great heap of stones that remains to this day. The LORD turned from the fierceness of his anger. Therefore the name of that place was called \u201cThe valley of Achor\u201d to this day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, and don\u2019t be dismayed. Take all the warriors with you, and arise, go up to Ai. Behold, I have given into your hand the king of Ai, with his people, his city, and his land."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall do to Ai and her king as you did to Jericho and her king, except you shall take its goods and its livestock for yourselves. Set an ambush for the city behind it.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joshua arose, with all the warriors, to go up to Ai. Joshua chose thirty thousand men, the mighty men of valor, and sent them out by night."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He commanded them, saying, \u201cBehold, you shall lie in ambush against the city, behind the city. Don\u2019t go very far from the city, but all of you be ready."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I and all the people who are with me will approach the city. It shall happen, when they come out against us, as at the first, that we will flee before them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They will come out after us until we have drawn them away from the city; for they will say, \u2018They flee before us, like the first time.\u2019 So we will flee before them,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and you shall rise up from the ambush, and take possession of the city; for the LORD your God will deliver it into your hand."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"It shall be, when you have seized the city, that you shall set the city on fire. You shall do this according to the LORD\u2019s word. Behold, I have commanded you.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua sent them out; and they went to set up the ambush, and stayed between Bethel and Ai on the west side of Ai; but Joshua stayed among the people that night."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Joshua rose up early in the morning, mustered the people, and went up, he and the elders of Israel, before the people to Ai."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"All the people, even the men of war who were with him, went up and came near, and came before the city and encamped on the north side of Ai. Now there was a valley between him and Ai."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He took about five thousand men, and set them in ambush between Bethel and Ai, on the west side of the city."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So they set the people, even all the army who was on the north of the city, and their ambush on the west of the city; and Joshua went that night into the middle of the valley."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When the king of Ai saw it, they hurried and rose up early, and the men of the city went out against Israel to battle, he and all his people, at the time appointed, before the Arabah; but he didn\u2019t know that there was an ambush against him behind the city."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Joshua and all Israel made as if they were beaten before them, and fled by the way of the wilderness."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"All the people who were in the city were called together to pursue after them. They pursued Joshua, and were drawn away from the city."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"There was not a man left in Ai or Bethel who didn\u2019t go out after Israel. They left the city open, and pursued Israel."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cStretch out the javelin that is in your hand toward Ai, for I will give it into your hand.\u201d"],[0,"Joshua stretched out the javelin that was in his hand toward the city."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The ambush arose quickly out of their place, and they ran as soon as he had stretched out his hand and entered into the city and took it. They hurried and set the city on fire."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When the men of Ai looked behind them, they saw, and behold, the smoke of the city ascended up to heaven, and they had no power to flee this way or that way. The people who fled to the wilderness turned back on the pursuers."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When Joshua and all Israel saw that the ambush had taken the city, and that the smoke of the city ascended, then they turned back and killed the men of Ai."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The others came out of the city against them, so they were in the middle of Israel, some on this side, and some on that side. They struck them, so that they let none of them remain or escape."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They captured the king of Ai alive, and brought him to Joshua."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When Israel had finished killing all the inhabitants of Ai in the field, in the wilderness in which they pursued them, and they had all fallen by the edge of the sword until they were consumed, all Israel returned to Ai and struck it with the edge of the sword."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"All that fell that day, both of men and women, were twelve thousand, even all the people of Ai."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For Joshua didn\u2019t draw back his hand, with which he stretched out the javelin, until he had utterly destroyed all the inhabitants of Ai."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Israel took for themselves only the livestock and the goods of that city, according to the LORD\u2019s word which he commanded Joshua."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So Joshua burned Ai and made it a heap forever, even a desolation, to this day."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He hanged the king of Ai on a tree until the evening. At sundown, Joshua commanded, and they took his body down from the tree and threw it at the entrance of the gate of the city, and raised a great heap of stones on it that remains to this day."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joshua built an altar to the LORD, the God of Israel, on Mount Ebal,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"as Moses the servant of the LORD commanded the children of Israel, as it is written in the book of the law of Moses: an altar of uncut stones, on which no one had lifted up any iron. They offered burnt offerings on it to the LORD and sacrificed peace offerings."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He wrote there on the stones a copy of Moses\u2019 law, which he wrote in the presence of the children of Israel."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"All Israel, with their elders, officers, and judges, stood on both sides of the ark before the Levitical priests, who carried the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, the foreigner as well as the native; half of them in front of Mount Gerizim, and half of them in front of Mount Ebal, as Moses the servant of the LORD had commanded at the first, that they should bless the people of Israel."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Afterward he read all the words of the law, the blessing and the curse, according to all that is written in the book of the law."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"There was not a word of all that Moses commanded which Joshua didn\u2019t read before all the assembly of Israel, with the women, the little ones, and the foreigners who were among them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When all the kings who were beyond the Jordan, in the hill country, and in the lowland, and on all the shore of the great sea in front of Lebanon, the Hittite, the Amorite, the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite, heard of it"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"they gathered themselves together to fight with Joshua and with Israel, with one accord."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But when the inhabitants of Gibeon heard what Joshua had done to Jericho and to Ai,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"they also resorted to a ruse, and went and made as if they had been ambassadors, and took old sacks on their donkeys, and old, torn-up and bound up wineskins,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and old and patched sandals on their feet, and wore old garments. All the bread of their food supply was dry and moldy."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They went to Joshua at the camp at Gilgal, and said to him and to the men of Israel, \u201cWe have come from a far country. Now therefore make a covenant with us.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of Israel said to the Hivites, \u201cWhat if you live among us? How could we make a covenant with you?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to Joshua, \u201cWe are your servants.\u201d"],[0,"Joshua said to them, \u201cWho are you? Where do you come from?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cYour servants have come from a very far country because of the name of the LORD your God; for we have heard of his fame, all that he did in Egypt,"]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and all that he did to the two kings of the Amorites who were beyond the Jordan, to Sihon king of Heshbon and to Og king of Bashan, who was at Ashtaroth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Our elders and all the inhabitants of our country spoke to us, saying, \u2018Take supplies in your hand for the journey, and go to meet them. Tell them, \u201cWe are your servants. Now make a covenant with us.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"This our bread we took hot for our supplies out of our houses on the day we went out to go to you; but now, behold, it is dry, and has become moldy."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"These wineskins, which we filled, were new; and behold, they are torn. These our garments and our sandals have become old because of the very long journey.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The men sampled their provisions, and didn\u2019t ask counsel from the LORD\u2019s mouth."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Joshua made peace with them, and made a covenant with them, to let them live. The princes of the congregation swore to them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"At the end of three days after they had made a covenant with them, they heard that they were their neighbors, and that they lived among them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The children of Israel traveled and came to their cities on the third day. Now their cities were Gibeon, Chephirah, Beeroth, and Kiriath Jearim."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The children of Israel didn\u2019t strike them, because the princes of the congregation had sworn to them by the LORD, the God of Israel. All the congregation murmured against the princes."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But all the princes said to all the congregation, \u201cWe have sworn to them by the LORD, the God of Israel. Now therefore we may not touch them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"We will do this to them, and let them live; lest wrath be on us, because of the oath which we swore to them.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The princes said to them, \u201cLet them live.\u201d So they became wood cutters and drawers of water for all the congregation, as the princes had spoken to them."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua called for them, and he spoke to them, saying, \u201cWhy have you deceived us, saying, \u2018We are very far from you,\u2019 when you live among us?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now therefore you are cursed, and some of you will never fail to be slaves, both wood cutters and drawers of water for the house of my God.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered Joshua, and said, \u201cBecause your servants were certainly told how the LORD your God commanded his servant Moses to give you all the land, and to destroy all the inhabitants of the land from before you. Therefore we were very afraid for our lives because of you, and have done this thing."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now, behold, we are in your hand. Do to us as it seems good and right to you to do.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"He did so to them, and delivered them out of the hand of the children of Israel, so that they didn\u2019t kill them."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"That day Joshua made them wood cutters and drawers of water for the congregation and for the LORD\u2019s altar to this day, in the place which he should choose."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Adoni-Zedek king of Jerusalem heard how Joshua had taken Ai, and had utterly destroyed it; as he had done to Jericho and her king, so he had done to Ai and her king; and how the inhabitants of Gibeon had made peace with Israel, and were among them,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"they were very afraid, because Gibeon was a great city, as one of the royal cities, and because it was greater than Ai, and all its men were mighty."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore Adoni-Zedek king of Jerusalem sent to Hoham king of Hebron, Piram king of Jarmuth, Japhia king of Lachish, and Debir king of Eglon, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cCome up to me and help me. Let\u2019s strike Gibeon; for they have made peace with Joshua and with the children of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Therefore the five kings of the Amorites, the king of Jerusalem, the king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth, the king of Lachish, and the king of Eglon, gathered themselves together and went up, they and all their armies, and encamped against Gibeon, and made war against it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The men of Gibeon sent to Joshua at the camp at Gilgal, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t abandon your servants! Come up to us quickly and save us! Help us; for all the kings of the Amorites that dwell in the hill country have gathered together against us.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joshua went up from Gilgal, he and the whole army with him, including all the mighty men of valor."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cDon\u2019t fear them, for I have delivered them into your hands. Not a man of them will stand before you.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua therefore came to them suddenly. He marched from Gilgal all night."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD confused them before Israel. He killed them with a great slaughter at Gibeon, and chased them by the way of the ascent of Beth Horon, and struck them to Azekah and to Makkedah."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"As they fled from before Israel, while they were at the descent of Beth Horon, the LORD hurled down great stones from the sky on them to Azekah, and they died. There were more who died from the hailstones than those whom the children of Israel killed with the sword."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joshua spoke to the LORD in the day when the LORD delivered up the Amorites before the children of Israel. He said in the sight of Israel, \u201cSun, stand still on Gibeon! You, moon, stop in the valley of Aijalon!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The sun stood still, and the moon stayed, until the nation had avenged themselves of their enemies. Isn\u2019t this written in the book of Jashar? The sun stayed in the middle of the sky, and didn\u2019t hurry to go down about a whole day."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"There was no day like that before it or after it, that the LORD listened to the voice of a man; for the LORD fought for Israel."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, to the camp to Gilgal."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"These five kings fled, and hid themselves in the cave at Makkedah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Joshua was told, saying, \u201cThe five kings have been found, hidden in the cave at Makkedah.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua said, \u201cRoll large stones to cover the cave\u2019s entrance, and set men by it to guard them;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"but don\u2019t stay there. Pursue your enemies, and attack them from the rear. Don\u2019t allow them to enter into their cities; for the LORD your God has delivered them into your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joshua and the children of Israel had finished killing them with a very great slaughter until they were consumed, and the remnant which remained of them had entered into the fortified cities,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"all the people returned to the camp to Joshua at Makkedah in peace. None moved his tongue against any of the children of Israel."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Then Joshua said, \u201cOpen the cave entrance, and bring those five kings out of the cave to me.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"They did so, and brought those five kings out of the cave to him: the king of Jerusalem, the king of Hebron, the king of Jarmuth, the king of Lachish, and the king of Eglon."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When they brought those kings out to Joshua, Joshua called for all the men of Israel, and said to the chiefs of the men of war who went with him, \u201cCome near. Put your feet on the necks of these kings.\u201d"],[0,"They came near, and put their feet on their necks."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, nor be dismayed. Be strong and courageous, for the LORD will do this to all your enemies against whom you fight.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Afterward Joshua struck them, put them to death, and hanged them on five trees. They were hanging on the trees until the evening."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"At the time of the going down of the sun, Joshua commanded, and they took them down off the trees, and threw them into the cave in which they had hidden themselves, and laid great stones on the mouth of the cave, which remain to this very day."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua took Makkedah on that day, and struck it with the edge of the sword, with its king. He utterly destroyed it and all the souls who were in it. He left no one remaining. He did to the king of Makkedah as he had done to the king of Jericho."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua passed from Makkedah, and all Israel with him, to Libnah, and fought against Libnah."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The LORD delivered it also, with its king, into the hand of Israel. He struck it with the edge of the sword, and all the souls who were in it. He left no one remaining in it. He did to its king as he had done to the king of Jericho."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua passed from Libnah, and all Israel with him, to Lachish, and encamped against it, and fought against it."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The LORD delivered Lachish into the hand of Israel. He took it on the second day, and struck it with the edge of the sword, with all the souls who were in it, according to all that he had done to Libnah."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Then Horam king of Gezer came up to help Lachish; and Joshua struck him and his people, until he had left him no one remaining."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua passed from Lachish, and all Israel with him, to Eglon; and they encamped against it and fought against it."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"They took it on that day, and struck it with the edge of the sword. He utterly destroyed all the souls who were in it that day, according to all that he had done to Lachish."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua went up from Eglon, and all Israel with him, to Hebron; and they fought against it."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They took it, and struck it with the edge of the sword, with its king and all its cities, and all the souls who were in it. He left no one remaining, according to all that he had done to Eglon; but he utterly destroyed it, and all the souls who were in it."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, to Debir, and fought against it."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"He took it, with its king and all its cities. They struck them with the edge of the sword, and utterly destroyed all the souls who were in it. He left no one remaining. As he had done to Hebron, so he did to Debir, and to its king; as he had done also to Libnah, and to its king."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"So Joshua struck all the land, the hill country, the South, the lowland, the slopes, and all their kings. He left no one remaining, but he utterly destroyed all that breathed, as the LORD, the God of Israel, commanded."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Joshua struck them from Kadesh Barnea even to Gaza, and all the country of Goshen, even to Gibeon."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Joshua took all these kings and their land at one time because the LORD, the God of Israel, fought for Israel."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Joshua returned, and all Israel with him, to the camp to Gilgal."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jabin king of Hazor heard of it, he sent to Jobab king of Madon, to the king of Shimron, to the king of Achshaph,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and to the kings who were on the north, in the hill country, in the Arabah south of Chinneroth, in the lowland, and in the heights of Dor on the west,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"to the Canaanite on the east and on the west, the Amorite, the Hittite, the Perizzite, the Jebusite in the hill country, and the Hivite under Hermon in the land of Mizpah."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They went out, they and all their armies with them, many people, even as the sand that is on the seashore in multitude, with very many horses and chariots."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All these kings met together; and they came and encamped together at the waters of Merom, to fight with Israel."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Joshua, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid because of them; for tomorrow at this time, I will deliver them up all slain before Israel. You shall hamstring their horses and burn their chariots with fire.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joshua came suddenly, with all the warriors, against them by the waters of Merom, and attacked them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD delivered them into the hand of Israel, and they struck them, and chased them to great Sidon, and to Misrephoth Maim, and to the valley of Mizpah eastward. They struck them until they left them no one remaining."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Joshua did to them as the LORD told him. He hamstrung their horses and burned their chariots with fire."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Joshua turned back at that time, and took Hazor, and struck its king with the sword; for Hazor used to be the head of all those kingdoms."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They struck all the souls who were in it with the edge of the sword, utterly destroying them. There was no one left who breathed. He burned Hazor with fire."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Joshua captured all the cities of those kings, with their kings, and he struck them with the edge of the sword, and utterly destroyed them, as Moses the servant of the LORD commanded."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But as for the cities that stood on their mounds, Israel burned none of them, except Hazor only. Joshua burned that."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The children of Israel took all the plunder of these cities, with the livestock, as plunder for themselves; but every man they struck with the edge of the sword, until they had destroyed them. They didn\u2019t leave any who breathed."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"As the LORD commanded Moses his servant, so Moses commanded Joshua. Joshua did so. He left nothing undone of all that the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So Joshua captured all that land, the hill country, all the South, all the land of Goshen, the lowland, the Arabah, the hill country of Israel, and the lowland of the same,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"from Mount Halak, that goes up to Seir, even to Baal Gad in the valley of Lebanon under Mount Hermon. He took all their kings, struck them, and put them to death."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Joshua made war a long time with all those kings."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There was not a city that made peace with the children of Israel, except the Hivites, the inhabitants of Gibeon. They took all in battle."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For it was of the LORD to harden their hearts, to come against Israel in battle, that he might utterly destroy them, that they might have no favor, but that he might destroy them, as the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Joshua came at that time, and cut off the Anakim from the hill country, from Hebron, from Debir, from Anab, and from all the hill country of Judah, and from all the hill country of Israel. Joshua utterly destroyed them with their cities."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"There were none of the Anakim left in the land of the children of Israel. Only in Gaza, in Gath, and in Ashdod, did some remain."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So Joshua took the whole land, according to all that the LORD spoke to Moses; and Joshua gave it for an inheritance to Israel according to their divisions by their tribes. Then the land had rest from war."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the kings of the land, whom the children of Israel struck, and possessed their land beyond the Jordan toward the sunrise, from the valley of the Arnon to Mount Hermon, and all the Arabah eastward:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon, and ruled from Aroer, which is on the edge of the valley of the Arnon, and the middle of the valley, and half Gilead, even to the river Jabbok, the border of the children of Ammon;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and the Arabah to the sea of Chinneroth, eastward, and to the sea of the Arabah, even the Salt Sea, eastward, the way to Beth Jeshimoth; and on the south, under the slopes of Pisgah:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and the border of Og king of Bashan, of the remnant of the Rephaim, who lived at Ashtaroth and at Edrei,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and ruled in Mount Hermon, and in Salecah, and in all Bashan, to the border of the Geshurites and the Maacathites, and half Gilead, the border of Sihon king of Heshbon."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Moses the servant of the LORD and the children of Israel struck them. Moses the servant of the LORD gave it for a possession to the Reubenites, and the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the kings of the land whom Joshua and the children of Israel struck beyond the Jordan westward, from Baal Gad in the valley of Lebanon even to Mount Halak, that goes up to Seir. Joshua gave it to the tribes of Israel for a possession according to their divisions;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"in the hill country, and in the lowland, and in the Arabah, and in the slopes, and in the wilderness, and in the South; the Hittite, the Amorite, and the Canaanite, the Perizzite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite:"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Jericho, one;"],[0,"the king of Ai, which is beside Bethel, one;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Jerusalem, one;"],[0,"the king of Hebron, one;"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Jarmuth, one;"],[0,"the king of Lachish, one;"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Eglon, one;"],[0,"the king of Gezer, one;"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Debir, one;"],[0,"the king of Geder, one;"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Hormah, one;"],[0,"the king of Arad, one;"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Libnah, one;"],[0,"the king of Adullam, one;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Makkedah, one;"],[0,"the king of Bethel, one;"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Tappuah, one;"],[0,"the king of Hepher, one;"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Aphek, one;"],[0,"the king of Lassharon, one;"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Madon, one;"],[0,"the king of Hazor, one;"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Shimron Meron, one;"],[0,"the king of Achshaph, one;"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Taanach, one;"],[0,"the king of Megiddo, one;"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Kedesh, one;"],[0,"the king of Jokneam in Carmel, one;"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Dor in the height of Dor, one;"],[0,"the king of Goiim in Gilgal, one;"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"the king of Tirzah, one:"],[0,"all the kings thirty-one."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Joshua was old and well advanced in years. The LORD said to him, \u201cYou are old and advanced in years, and there remains yet very much land to be possessed."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the land that still remains: all the regions of the Philistines, and all the Geshurites;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"from the Shihor, which is before Egypt, even to the border of Ekron northward, which is counted as Canaanite; the five lords of the Philistines; the Gazites, and the Ashdodites, the Ashkelonites, the Gittites, and the Ekronites; also the Avvim,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"on the south; all the land of the Canaanites, and Mearah that belongs to the Sidonians, to Aphek, to the border of the Amorites;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and the land of the Gebalites, and all Lebanon, toward the sunrise, from Baal Gad under Mount Hermon to the entrance of Hamath;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"all the inhabitants of the hill country from Lebanon to Misrephoth Maim, even all the Sidonians. I will drive them out from before the children of Israel. Just allocate it to Israel for an inheritance, as I have commanded you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now therefore divide this land for an inheritance to the nine tribes and the half-tribe of Manasseh.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"With him the Reubenites and the Gadites received their inheritance, which Moses gave them, beyond the Jordan eastward, even as Moses the servant of the LORD gave them:"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"from Aroer, that is on the edge of the valley of the Arnon, and the city that is in the middle of the valley, and all the plain of Medeba to Dibon;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and all the cities of Sihon king of the Amorites, who reigned in Heshbon, to the border of the children of Ammon;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and Gilead, and the border of the Geshurites and Maacathites, and all Mount Hermon, and all Bashan to Salecah;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"all the kingdom of Og in Bashan, who reigned in Ashtaroth and in Edrei (who was left of the remnant of the Rephaim); for Moses attacked these, and drove them out."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Nevertheless the children of Israel didn\u2019t drive out the Geshurites, nor the Maacathites: but Geshur and Maacath live within Israel to this day."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Only he gave no inheritance to the tribe of Levi. The offerings of the LORD, the God of Israel, made by fire are his inheritance, as he spoke to him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Moses gave to the tribe of the children of Reuben according to their families."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Their border was from Aroer, that is on the edge of the valley of the Arnon, and the city that is in the middle of the valley, and all the plain by Medeba;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Heshbon, and all its cities that are in the plain; Dibon, Bamoth Baal, Beth Baal Meon,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jahaz, Kedemoth, Mephaath,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Kiriathaim, Sibmah, Zereth Shahar in the mount of the valley,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Beth Peor, the slopes of Pisgah, Beth Jeshimoth,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"all the cities of the plain, and all the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorites, who reigned in Heshbon, whom Moses struck with the chiefs of Midian, Evi, Rekem, Zur, Hur, and Reba, the princes of Sihon, who lived in the land."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The children of Israel also killed Balaam the son of Beor, the soothsayer, with the sword, among the rest of their slain."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The border of the children of Reuben was the bank of the Jordan. This was the inheritance of the children of Reuben according to their families, the cities and its villages."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses gave to the tribe of Gad, to the children of Gad, according to their families."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Their border was Jazer, and all the cities of Gilead, and half the land of the children of Ammon, to Aroer that is near Rabbah;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and from Heshbon to Ramath Mizpeh, and Betonim; and from Mahanaim to the border of Debir;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and in the valley, Beth Haram, Beth Nimrah, Succoth, and Zaphon, the rest of the kingdom of Sihon king of Heshbon, the Jordan\u2019s bank, to the uttermost part of the sea of Chinnereth beyond the Jordan eastward."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"This is the inheritance of the children of Gad according to their families, the cities and its villages."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Moses gave an inheritance to the half-tribe of Manasseh. It was for the half-tribe of the children of Manasseh according to their families."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Their border was from Mahanaim, all Bashan, all the kingdom of Og king of Bashan, and all the villages of Jair, which are in Bashan, sixty cities."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Half Gilead, Ashtaroth, and Edrei, the cities of the kingdom of Og in Bashan, were for the children of Machir the son of Manasseh, even for the half of the children of Machir according to their families."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the inheritances which Moses distributed in the plains of Moab, beyond the Jordan at Jericho, eastward."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But Moses gave no inheritance to the tribe of Levi. The LORD, the God of Israel, is their inheritance, as he spoke to them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the inheritances which the children of Israel took in the land of Canaan, which Eleazar the priest, Joshua the son of Nun, and the heads of the fathers\u2019 houses of the tribes of the children of Israel, distributed to them,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"by the lot of their inheritance, as the LORD commanded by Moses, for the nine tribes, and for the half-tribe."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For Moses had given the inheritance of the two tribes and the half-tribe beyond the Jordan; but to the Levites he gave no inheritance among them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For the children of Joseph were two tribes, Manasseh and Ephraim. They gave no portion to the Levites in the land, except cities to dwell in, with their pasture lands for their livestock and for their property."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did as the LORD commanded Moses, and they divided the land."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the children of Judah came near to Joshua in Gilgal. Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite said to him, \u201cYou know the thing that the LORD spoke to Moses the man of God concerning me and concerning you in Kadesh Barnea."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I was forty years old when Moses the servant of the LORD sent me from Kadesh Barnea to spy out the land. I brought him word again as it was in my heart."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, my brothers who went up with me made the heart of the people melt; but I wholly followed the LORD my God."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moses swore on that day, saying, \u2018Surely the land where you walked shall be an inheritance to you and to your children forever, because you have wholly followed the LORD my God.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, behold, the LORD has kept me alive, as he spoke, these forty-five years, from the time that the LORD spoke this word to Moses, while Israel walked in the wilderness. Now, behold, I am eighty-five years old, today."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"As yet I am as strong today as I was in the day that Moses sent me. As my strength was then, even so is my strength now for war, to go out and to come in."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now therefore give me this hill country, of which the LORD spoke in that day; for you heard in that day how the Anakim were there, and great and fortified cities. It may be that the LORD will be with me, and I shall drive them out, as the LORD said.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua blessed him; and he gave Hebron to Caleb the son of Jephunneh for an inheritance."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore Hebron became the inheritance of Caleb the son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite to this day, because he followed the LORD, the God of Israel wholeheartedly."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now the name of Hebron before was Kiriath Arba, after the greatest man among the Anakim. Then the land had rest from war."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The lot for the tribe of the children of Judah according to their families was to the border of Edom, even to the wilderness of Zin southward, at the uttermost part of the south."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Their south border was from the uttermost part of the Salt Sea, from the bay that looks southward;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and it went out southward of the ascent of Akrabbim, and passed along to Zin, and went up by the south of Kadesh Barnea, and passed along by Hezron, went up to Addar, and turned toward Karka;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and it passed along to Azmon, went out at the brook of Egypt; and the border ended at the sea. This shall be your south border."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The east border was the Salt Sea, even to the end of the Jordan. The border of the north quarter was from the bay of the sea at the end of the Jordan."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The border went up to Beth Hoglah, and passed along by the north of Beth Arabah; and the border went up to the stone of Bohan the son of Reuben."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The border went up to Debir from the valley of Achor, and so northward, looking toward Gilgal, that faces the ascent of Adummim, which is on the south side of the river. The border passed along to the waters of En Shemesh, and ended at En Rogel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The border went up by the valley of the son of Hinnom to the side of the Jebusite (also called Jerusalem) southward; and the border went up to the top of the mountain that lies before the valley of Hinnom westward, which is at the farthest part of the valley of Rephaim northward."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The border extended from the top of the mountain to the spring of the waters of Nephtoah, and went out to the cities of Mount Ephron; and the border extended to Baalah (also called Kiriath Jearim);"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and the border turned about from Baalah westward to Mount Seir, and passed along to the side of Mount Jearim (also called Chesalon) on the north, and went down to Beth Shemesh, and passed along by Timnah;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and the border went out to the side of Ekron northward; and the border extended to Shikkeron, and passed along to Mount Baalah, and went out at Jabneel; and the goings out of the border were at the sea."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The west border was to the shore of the great sea. This is the border of the children of Judah according to their families."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He gave to Caleb the son of Jephunneh a portion among the children of Judah, according to the commandment of the LORD to Joshua, even Kiriath Arba, named after the father of Anak (also called Hebron)."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Caleb drove out the three sons of Anak: Sheshai, and Ahiman, and Talmai, the children of Anak."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He went up against the inhabitants of Debir: now the name of Debir before was Kiriath Sepher."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Caleb said, \u201cHe who strikes Kiriath Sepher, and takes it, to him I will give Achsah my daughter as wife.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Othniel the son of Kenaz, the brother of Caleb, took it: and he gave him Achsah his daughter as wife."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When she came, she had him ask her father for a field. She got off her donkey, and Caleb said, \u201cWhat do you want?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cGive me a blessing. Because you have set me in the land of the South, give me also springs of water.\u201d"],[0,"So he gave her the upper springs and the lower springs."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Judah according to their families."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The farthest cities of the tribe of the children of Judah toward the border of Edom in the South were Kabzeel, Eder, Jagur,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Kinah, Dimonah, Adadah,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Kedesh, Hazor, Ithnan,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Ziph, Telem, Bealoth,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Hazor Hadattah, Kerioth Hezron (also called Hazor),"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Amam, Shema, Moladah,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Hazar Gaddah, Heshmon, Beth Pelet,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Hazar Shual, Beersheba, Biziothiah,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Baalah, Iim, Ezem,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Eltolad, Chesil, Hormah,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Ziklag, Madmannah, Sansannah,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Lebaoth, Shilhim, Ain, and Rimmon. All the cities are twenty-nine, with their villages."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"In the lowland, Eshtaol, Zorah, Ashnah,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Zanoah, En Gannim, Tappuah, Enam,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Jarmuth, Adullam, Socoh, Azekah,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Shaaraim, Adithaim and Gederah (or Gederothaim); fourteen cities with their villages."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Zenan, Hadashah, Migdal Gad,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Dilean, Mizpah, Joktheel,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Lachish, Bozkath, Eglon,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Cabbon, Lahmam, Chitlish,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Gederoth, Beth Dagon, Naamah, and Makkedah; sixteen cities with their villages."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Libnah, Ether, Ashan,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Iphtah, Ashnah, Nezib,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Keilah, Achzib, and Mareshah; nine cities with their villages."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Ekron, with its towns and its villages;"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"from Ekron even to the sea, all that were by the side of Ashdod, with their villages."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Ashdod, its towns and its villages; Gaza, its towns and its villages; to the brook of Egypt, and the great sea with its coastline."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"In the hill country, Shamir, Jattir, Socoh,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Dannah, Kiriath Sannah (which is Debir),"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Anab, Eshtemoh, Anim,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Goshen, Holon, and Giloh; eleven cities with their villages."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"Arab, Dumah, Eshan,"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"Janim, Beth Tappuah, Aphekah,"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"Humtah, Kiriath Arba (also called Hebron), and Zior; nine cities with their villages."]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"Maon, Carmel, Ziph, Jutah,"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Jezreel, Jokdeam, Zanoah,"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"Kain, Gibeah, and Timnah; ten cities with their villages."]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[0,"Halhul, Beth Zur, Gedor,"]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"Maarath, Beth Anoth, and Eltekon; six cities with their villages."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"Kiriath Baal (also called Kiriath Jearim), and Rabbah; two cities with their villages."]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"In the wilderness, Beth Arabah, Middin, Secacah,"]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"Nibshan, the City of Salt, and En Gedi; six cities with their villages."]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[0,"As for the Jebusites, the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the children of Judah couldn\u2019t drive them out; but the Jebusites live with the children of Judah at Jerusalem to this day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The lot came out for the children of Joseph from the Jordan at Jericho, at the waters of Jericho on the east, even the wilderness, going up from Jericho through the hill country to Bethel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It went out from Bethel to Luz, and passed along to the border of the Archites to Ataroth;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and it went down westward to the border of the Japhletites, to the border of Beth Horon the lower, and on to Gezer; and ended at the sea."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Joseph, Manasseh and Ephraim, took their inheritance."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"This was the border of the children of Ephraim according to their families. The border of their inheritance eastward was Ataroth Addar, to Beth Horon the upper."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The border went out westward at Michmethath on the north. The border turned about eastward to Taanath Shiloh, and passed along it on the east of Janoah."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It went down from Janoah to Ataroth, to Naarah, reached to Jericho, and went out at the Jordan."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"From Tappuah the border went along westward to the brook of Kanah; and ended at the sea. This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Ephraim according to their families;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"together with the cities which were set apart for the children of Ephraim in the middle of the inheritance of the children of Manasseh, all the cities with their villages."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t drive out the Canaanites who lived in Gezer; but the Canaanites dwell in the territory of Ephraim to this day, and have become servants to do forced labor."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This was the lot for the tribe of Manasseh, for he was the firstborn of Joseph. As for Machir the firstborn of Manasseh, the father of Gilead, because he was a man of war, therefore he had Gilead and Bashan."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"So this was for the rest of the children of Manasseh according to their families: for the children of Abiezer, for the children of Helek, for the children of Asriel, for the children of Shechem, for the children of Hepher, and for the children of Shemida. These were the male children of Manasseh the son of Joseph according to their families."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, had no sons, but daughters. These are the names of his daughters: Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They came to Eleazar the priest, and to Joshua the son of Nun, and to the princes, saying, \u201cThe LORD commanded Moses to give us an inheritance among our brothers.\u201d Therefore according to the commandment of the LORD he gave them an inheritance among the brothers of their father."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ten parts fell to Manasseh, in addition to the land of Gilead and Bashan, which is beyond the Jordan;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"because the daughters of Manasseh had an inheritance among his sons. The land of Gilead belonged to the rest of the sons of Manasseh."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The border of Manasseh was from Asher to Michmethath, which is before Shechem. The border went along to the right hand, to the inhabitants of En Tappuah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The land of Tappuah belonged to Manasseh; but Tappuah on the border of Manasseh belonged to the children of Ephraim."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The border went down to the brook of Kanah, southward of the brook. These cities belonged to Ephraim among the cities of Manasseh. The border of Manasseh was on the north side of the brook, and ended at the sea."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Southward it was Ephraim\u2019s, and northward it was Manasseh\u2019s, and the sea was his border. They reached to Asher on the north, and to Issachar on the east."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Manasseh had three heights in Issachar, in Asher Beth Shean and its towns, and Ibleam and its towns, and the inhabitants of Dor and its towns, and the inhabitants of Endor and its towns, and the inhabitants of Taanach and its towns, and the inhabitants of Megiddo and its towns."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Yet the children of Manasseh couldn\u2019t drive out the inhabitants of those cities; but the Canaanites would dwell in that land."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When the children of Israel had grown strong, they put the Canaanites to forced labor, and didn\u2019t utterly drive them out."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The children of Joseph spoke to Joshua, saying, \u201cWhy have you given me just one lot and one part for an inheritance, since we are a numerous people, because the LORD has blessed us so far?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua said to them, \u201cIf you are a numerous people, go up to the forest, and clear land for yourself there in the land of the Perizzites and of the Rephaim, since the hill country of Ephraim is too narrow for you.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Joseph said, \u201cThe hill country is not enough for us. All the Canaanites who dwell in the land of the valley have chariots of iron, both those who are in Beth Shean and its towns, and those who are in the valley of Jezreel.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua spoke to the house of Joseph, that is, to Ephraim and to Manasseh, saying, \u201cYou are a numerous people, and have great power. You shall not have one lot only;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"but the hill country shall be yours. Although it is a forest, you shall cut it down, and it\u2019s farthest extent shall be yours; for you shall drive out the Canaanites, though they have chariots of iron, and though they are strong.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The whole congregation of the children of Israel assembled themselves together at Shiloh, and set up the Tent of Meeting there. The land was subdued before them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Seven tribes remained among the children of Israel, which had not yet divided their inheritance."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Joshua said to the children of Israel, \u201cHow long will you neglect to go in to possess the land, which the LORD, the God of your fathers, has given you?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Appoint for yourselves three men from each tribe. I will send them, and they shall arise, walk through the land, and describe it according to their inheritance; then they shall come to me."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They shall divide it into seven portions. Judah shall live in his borders on the south, and the house of Joseph shall live in their borders on the north."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall survey the land into seven parts, and bring the description here to me; and I will cast lots for you here before the LORD our God."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"However, the Levites have no portion among you; for the priesthood of the LORD is their inheritance. Gad, Reuben, and the half-tribe of Manasseh have received their inheritance east of the Jordan, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave them.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The men arose and went. Joshua commanded those who went to survey the land, saying, \u201cGo walk through the land, survey it, and come again to me. I will cast lots for you here before the LORD in Shiloh.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The men went and passed through the land, and surveyed it by cities into seven portions in a book. They came to Joshua to the camp at Shiloh."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Joshua cast lots for them in Shiloh before the LORD. There Joshua divided the land to the children of Israel according to their divisions."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The lot of the tribe of the children of Benjamin came up according to their families. The border of their lot went out between the children of Judah and the children of Joseph."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Their border on the north quarter was from the Jordan. The border went up to the side of Jericho on the north, and went up through the hill country westward. It ended at the wilderness of Beth Aven."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The border passed along from there to Luz, to the side of Luz (also called Bethel), southward. The border went down to Ataroth Addar, by the mountain that lies on the south of Beth Horon the lower."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The border extended, and turned around on the west quarter southward, from the mountain that lies before Beth Horon southward; and ended at Kiriath Baal (also called Kiriath Jearim), a city of the children of Judah. This was the west quarter."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The south quarter was from the farthest part of Kiriath Jearim. The border went out westward, and went out to the spring of the waters of Nephtoah."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The border went down to the farthest part of the mountain that lies before the valley of the son of Hinnom, which is in the valley of Rephaim northward. It went down to the valley of Hinnom, to the side of the Jebusite southward, and went down to En Rogel."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It extended northward, went out at En Shemesh, and went out to Geliloth, which is opposite the ascent of Adummim. It went down to the stone of Bohan the son of Reuben."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"It passed along to the side opposite the Arabah northward, and went down to the Arabah."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The border passed along to the side of Beth Hoglah northward; and the border ended at the north bay of the Salt Sea, at the south end of the Jordan. This was the south border."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The Jordan was its border on the east quarter. This was the inheritance of the children of Benjamin, by the borders around it, according to their families."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Now the cities of the tribe of the children of Benjamin according to their families were Jericho, Beth Hoglah, Emek Keziz,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Beth Arabah, Zemaraim, Bethel,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Avvim, Parah, Ophrah,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Chephar Ammoni, Ophni, and Geba; twelve cities with their villages."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Gibeon, Ramah, Beeroth,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Mizpeh, Chephirah, Mozah,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Rekem, Irpeel, Taralah,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Zelah, Eleph, the Jebusite (also called Jerusalem), Gibeath, and Kiriath; fourteen cities with their villages. This is the inheritance of the children of Benjamin according to their families."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The second lot came out for Simeon, even for the tribe of the children of Simeon according to their families. Their inheritance was in the middle of the inheritance of the children of Judah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They had for their inheritance Beersheba (or Sheba), Moladah,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Hazar Shual, Balah, Ezem,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Eltolad, Bethul, Hormah,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ziklag, Beth Marcaboth, Hazar Susah,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Beth Lebaoth, and Sharuhen; thirteen cities with their villages;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Ain, Rimmon, Ether, and Ashan; four cities with their villages;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and all the villages that were around these cities to Baalath Beer, Ramah of the South. This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Simeon according to their families."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Out of the part of the children of Judah was the inheritance of the children of Simeon; for the portion of the children of Judah was too much for them. Therefore the children of Simeon had inheritance in the middle of their inheritance."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The third lot came up for the children of Zebulun according to their families. The border of their inheritance was to Sarid."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Their border went up westward, even to Maralah, and reached to Dabbesheth. It reached to the brook that is before Jokneam."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It turned from Sarid eastward toward the sunrise to the border of Chisloth Tabor. It went out to Daberath, and went up to Japhia."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"From there it passed along eastward to Gath Hepher, to Ethkazin; and it went out at Rimmon which stretches to Neah."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The border turned around it on the north to Hannathon; and it ended at the valley of Iphtah El;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Kattath, Nahalal, Shimron, Idalah, and Bethlehem: twelve cities with their villages."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"This is the inheritance of the children of Zebulun according to their families, these cities with their villages."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The fourth lot came out for Issachar, even for the children of Issachar according to their families."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Their border was to Jezreel, Chesulloth, Shunem,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Hapharaim, Shion, Anaharath,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Rabbith, Kishion, Ebez,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Remeth, Engannim, En Haddah, and Beth Pazzez."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The border reached to Tabor, Shahazumah, and Beth Shemesh. Their border ended at the Jordan: sixteen cities with their villages."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Issachar according to their families, the cities with their villages."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The fifth lot came out for the tribe of the children of Asher according to their families."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Their border was Helkath, Hali, Beten, Achshaph,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Allammelech, Amad, Mishal. It reached to Carmel westward, and to Shihorlibnath."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"It turned toward the sunrise to Beth Dagon, and reached to Zebulun, and to the valley of Iphtah El northward to Beth Emek and Neiel. It went out to Cabul on the left hand,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and Ebron, Rehob, Hammon, and Kanah, even to great Sidon."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The border turned to Ramah, to the fortified city of Tyre; and the border turned to Hosah. It ended at the sea by the region of Achzib;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Ummah also, and Aphek, and Rehob: twenty-two cities with their villages."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Asher according to their families, these cities with their villages."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The sixth lot came out for the children of Naphtali, even for the children of Naphtali according to their families."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Their border was from Heleph, from the oak in Zaanannim, Adami-nekeb, and Jabneel, to Lakkum. It ended at the Jordan."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The border turned westward to Aznoth Tabor, and went out from there to Hukkok. It reached to Zebulun on the south, and reached to Asher on the west, and to Judah at the Jordan toward the sunrise."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The fortified cities were Ziddim, Zer, Hammath, Rakkath, Chinnereth,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Adamah, Ramah, Hazor,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Kedesh, Edrei, En Hazor,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Iron, Migdal El, Horem, Beth Anath, and Beth Shemesh; nineteen cities with their villages."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Naphtali according to their families, the cities with their villages."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"The seventh lot came out for the tribe of the children of Dan according to their families."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The border of their inheritance was Zorah, Eshtaol, Irshemesh,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Shaalabbin, Aijalon, Ithlah,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Elon, Timnah, Ekron,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Eltekeh, Gibbethon, Baalath,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Jehud, Bene Berak, Gath Rimmon,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Me Jarkon, and Rakkon, with the border opposite Joppa."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"The border of the children of Dan went out beyond them; for the children of Dan went up and fought against Leshem, and took it, and struck it with the edge of the sword, and possessed it, and lived therein, and called Leshem, Dan, after the name of Dan their forefather."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"This is the inheritance of the tribe of the children of Dan according to their families, these cities with their villages."]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"So they finished distributing the land for inheritance by its borders. The children of Israel gave an inheritance to Joshua the son of Nun among them."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"According to the LORD\u2019s commandment, they gave him the city which he asked, even Timnathserah in the hill country of Ephraim; and he built the city, and lived there."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"These are the inheritances, which Eleazar the priest, Joshua the son of Nun, and the heads of the fathers\u2019 houses of the tribes of the children of Israel, distributed for inheritance by lot in Shiloh before the LORD, at the door of the Tent of Meeting. So they finished dividing the land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Joshua, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to the children of Israel, saying, \u2018Assign the cities of refuge, of which I spoke to you by Moses,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"that the man slayer who kills any person accidentally or unintentionally may flee there. They shall be to you for a refuge from the avenger of blood."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He shall flee to one of those cities, and shall stand at the entrance of the gate of the city, and declare his case in the ears of the elders of that city. They shall take him into the city with them, and give him a place, that he may live among them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"If the avenger of blood pursues him, then they shall not deliver up the man slayer into his hand; because he struck his neighbor unintentionally, and didn\u2019t hate him before."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He shall dwell in that city until he stands before the congregation for judgment, until the death of the high priest that shall be in those days. Then the man slayer shall return, and come to his own city, and to his own house, to the city he fled from.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They set apart Kedesh in Galilee in the hill country of Naphtali, Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim, and Kiriath Arba (also called Hebron) in the hill country of Judah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Beyond the Jordan at Jericho eastward, they assigned Bezer in the wilderness in the plain out of the tribe of Reuben, Ramoth in Gilead out of the tribe of Gad, and Golan in Bashan out of the tribe of Manasseh."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"These were the appointed cities for all the children of Israel, and for the alien who lives among them, that whoever kills any person unintentionally might flee there, and not die by the hand of the avenger of blood, until he stands trial before the congregation."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the heads of fathers\u2019 houses of the Levites came near to Eleazar the priest, and to Joshua the son of Nun, and to the heads of fathers\u2019 houses of the tribes of the children of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They spoke to them at Shiloh in the land of Canaan, saying, \u201cThe LORD commanded through Moses to give us cities to dwell in, with their pasture lands for our livestock.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel gave to the Levites out of their inheritance, according to the commandment of the LORD, these cities with their pasture lands."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The lot came out for the families of the Kohathites. The children of Aaron the priest, who were of the Levites, had thirteen cities by lot out of the tribe of Judah, out of the tribe of the Simeonites, and out of the tribe of Benjamin."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The rest of the children of Kohath had ten cities by lot out of the families of the tribe of Ephraim, out of the tribe of Dan, and out of the half-tribe of Manasseh."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The children of Gershon had thirteen cities by lot out of the families of the tribe of Issachar, out of the tribe of Asher, out of the tribe of Naphtali, and out of the half-tribe of Manasseh in Bashan."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The children of Merari according to their families had twelve cities out of the tribe of Reuben, out of the tribe of Gad, and out of the tribe of Zebulun."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of Israel gave these cities with their pasture lands by lot to the Levites, as the LORD commanded by Moses."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They gave out of the tribe of the children of Judah, and out of the tribe of the children of Simeon, these cities which are mentioned by name:"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and they were for the children of Aaron, of the families of the Kohathites, who were of the children of Levi; for theirs was the first lot."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They gave them Kiriath Arba, named after the father of Anak (also called Hebron), in the hill country of Judah, with its pasture lands around it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But they gave the fields of the city and its villages to Caleb the son of Jephunneh for his possession."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"To the children of Aaron the priest they gave Hebron with its pasture lands, the city of refuge for the man slayer, Libnah with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Jattir with its pasture lands, Eshtemoa with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Holon with its pasture lands, Debir with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Ain with its pasture lands, Juttah with its pasture lands, and Beth Shemesh with its pasture lands: nine cities out of those two tribes."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Out of the tribe of Benjamin, Gibeon with its pasture lands, Geba with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Anathoth with its pasture lands, and Almon with its pasture lands: four cities."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"All the cities of the children of Aaron, the priests, were thirteen cities with their pasture lands."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The families of the children of Kohath, the Levites, even the rest of the children of Kohath, had the cities of their lot out of the tribe of Ephraim."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They gave them Shechem with its pasture lands in the hill country of Ephraim, the city of refuge for the man slayer, and Gezer with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Kibzaim with its pasture lands, and Beth Horon with its pasture lands: four cities."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Out of the tribe of Dan, Elteke with its pasture lands, Gibbethon with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Aijalon with its pasture lands, Gath Rimmon with its pasture lands: four cities."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Out of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Taanach with its pasture lands, and Gath Rimmon with its pasture lands: two cities."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"All the cities of the families of the rest of the children of Kohath were ten with their pasture lands."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"They gave to the children of Gershon, of the families of the Levites, out of the half-tribe of Manasseh Golan in Bashan with its pasture lands, the city of refuge for the man slayer, and Be Eshterah with its pasture lands: two cities."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Out of the tribe of Issachar, Kishion with its pasture lands, Daberath with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Jarmuth with its pasture lands, En Gannim with its pasture lands: four cities."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Out of the tribe of Asher, Mishal with its pasture lands, Abdon with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Helkath with its pasture lands, and Rehob with its pasture lands: four cities."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Out of the tribe of Naphtali, Kedesh in Galilee with its pasture lands, the city of refuge for the man slayer, Hammothdor with its pasture lands, and Kartan with its pasture lands: three cities."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"All the cities of the Gershonites according to their families were thirteen cities with their pasture lands."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"To the families of the children of Merari, the rest of the Levites, out of the tribe of Zebulun, Jokneam with its pasture lands, Kartah with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Dimnah with its pasture lands, and Nahalal with its pasture lands: four cities."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Out of the tribe of Reuben, Bezer with its pasture lands, Jahaz with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Kedemoth with its pasture lands, and Mephaath with its pasture lands: four cities."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Out of the tribe of Gad, Ramoth in Gilead with its pasture lands, the city of refuge for the man slayer, and Mahanaim with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Heshbon with its pasture lands, Jazer with its pasture lands: four cities in all."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"All these were the cities of the children of Merari according to their families, even the rest of the families of the Levites. Their lot was twelve cities."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"All the cities of the Levites among the possessions of the children of Israel were forty-eight cities with their pasture lands."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Each of these cities included their pasture lands around them. It was this way with all these cities."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"So the LORD gave to Israel all the land which he swore to give to their fathers. They possessed it, and lived in it."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The LORD gave them rest all around, according to all that he swore to their fathers. Not a man of all their enemies stood before them. The LORD delivered all their enemies into their hand."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Nothing failed of any good thing which the LORD had spoken to the house of Israel. All came to pass."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joshua called the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cYou have kept all that Moses the servant of the LORD commanded you, and have listened to my voice in all that I commanded you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You have not left your brothers these many days to this day, but have performed the duty of the commandment of the LORD your God."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now the LORD your God has given rest to your brothers, as he spoke to them. Therefore now return and go to your tents, to the land of your possession, which Moses the servant of the LORD gave you beyond the Jordan."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Only take diligent heed to do the commandment and the law which Moses the servant of the LORD commanded you, to love the LORD your God, to walk in all his ways, to keep his commandments, to hold fast to him, and to serve him with all your heart and with all your soul.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joshua blessed them, and sent them away; and they went to their tents."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now to the one half-tribe of Manasseh Moses had given inheritance in Bashan; but Joshua gave to the other half among their brothers beyond the Jordan westward. Moreover when Joshua sent them away to their tents, he blessed them,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and spoke to them, saying, \u201cReturn with much wealth to your tents, with very much livestock, with silver, with gold, with bronze, with iron, and with very much clothing. Divide the plunder of your enemies with your brothers.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh returned, and departed from the children of Israel out of Shiloh, which is in the land of Canaan, to go to the land of Gilead, to the land of their possession, which they owned, according to the commandment of the LORD by Moses."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When they came to the region near the Jordan, that is in the land of Canaan, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh built an altar there by the Jordan, a great altar to look at."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The children of Israel heard this, \u201cBehold, the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh have built an altar along the border of the land of Canaan, in the region around the Jordan, on the side that belongs to the children of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When the children of Israel heard of it, the whole congregation of the children of Israel gathered themselves together at Shiloh, to go up against them to war."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The children of Israel sent to the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh, into the land of Gilead, Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"With him were ten princes, one prince of a fathers\u2019 house for each of the tribes of Israel; and they were each head of their fathers\u2019 houses among the thousands of Israel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They came to the children of Reuben, and to the children of Gad, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh, to the land of Gilead, and they spoke with them, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cThe whole congregation of the LORD says, \u2018What trespass is this that you have committed against the God of Israel, to turn away today from following the LORD, in that you have built yourselves an altar, to rebel today against the LORD?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Is the iniquity of Peor too little for us, from which we have not cleansed ourselves to this day, although there came a plague on the congregation of the LORD,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"that you must turn away today from following the LORD? It will be, since you rebel today against the LORD, that tomorrow he will be angry with the whole congregation of Israel."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"However, if the land of your possession is unclean, then pass over to the land of the possession of the LORD, in which the LORD\u2019s tabernacle dwells, and take possession among us; but don\u2019t rebel against the LORD, nor rebel against us, in building an altar other than the LORD our God\u2019s altar."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t Achan the son of Zerah commit a trespass in the devoted thing, and wrath fell on all the congregation of Israel? That man didn\u2019t perish alone in his iniquity.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the half-tribe of Manasseh answered, and spoke to the heads of the thousands of Israel,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Mighty One, God, the LORD, the Mighty One, God, the LORD, he knows; and Israel shall know: if it was in rebellion, or if in trespass against the LORD (don\u2019t save us today),"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"that we have built us an altar to turn away from following the LORD; or if to offer burnt offering or meal offering, or if to offer sacrifices of peace offerings, let the LORD himself require it."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf we have not out of concern done this, and for a reason, saying, \u2018In time to come your children might speak to our children, saying, \u201cWhat have you to do with the LORD, the God of Israel?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For the LORD has made the Jordan a border between us and you, you children of Reuben and children of Gad. You have no portion in the LORD.\u201d\u2019 So your children might make our children cease from fearing the LORD."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore we said, \u2018Let\u2019s now prepare to build ourselves an altar, not for burnt offering, nor for sacrifice;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"but it will be a witness between us and you, and between our generations after us, that we may perform the service of the LORD before him with our burnt offerings, with our sacrifices, and with our peace offerings;\u2019 that your children may not tell our children in time to come, \u2018You have no portion in the LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore we said, \u2018It shall be, when they tell us or our generations this in time to come, that we shall say, \u201cBehold the pattern of the LORD\u2019s altar, which our fathers made, not for burnt offering, nor for sacrifice; but it is a witness between us and you.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFar be it from us that we should rebel against the LORD, and turn away today from following the LORD, to build an altar for burnt offering, for meal offering, or for sacrifice, besides the LORD our God\u2019s altar that is before his tabernacle!\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"When Phinehas the priest, and the princes of the congregation, even the heads of the thousands of Israel that were with him, heard the words that the children of Reuben and the children of Gad and the children of Manasseh spoke, it pleased them well."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest said to the children of Reuben, to the children of Gad, and to the children of Manasseh, \u201cToday we know that the LORD is among us, because you have not committed this trespass against the LORD. Now you have delivered the children of Israel out of the LORD\u2019s hand.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Phinehas the son of Eleazar the priest, and the princes, returned from the children of Reuben, and from the children of Gad, out of the land of Gilead, to the land of Canaan, to the children of Israel, and brought them word again."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The thing pleased the children of Israel; and the children of Israel blessed God, and spoke no more of going up against them to war, to destroy the land in which the children of Reuben and the children of Gad lived."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The children of Reuben and the children of Gad named the altar \u201cA Witness Between Us that the LORD is God.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After many days, when the LORD had given rest to Israel from their enemies all around, and Joshua was old and well advanced in years,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Joshua called for all Israel, for their elders and for their heads, and for their judges and for their officers, and said to them, \u201cI am old and well advanced in years."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You have seen all that the LORD your God has done to all these nations because of you; for it is the LORD your God who has fought for you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, I have allotted to you these nations that remain, to be an inheritance for your tribes, from the Jordan, with all the nations that I have cut off, even to the great sea toward the going down of the sun."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD your God will thrust them out from before you, and drive them from out of your sight. You shall possess their land, as the LORD your God spoke to you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore be very courageous to keep and to do all that is written in the book of the law of Moses, that you not turn away from it to the right hand or to the left;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"that you not come among these nations, these that remain among you; neither make mention of the name of their gods, nor cause to swear by them, neither serve them, nor bow down yourselves to them;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but hold fast to the LORD your God, as you have done to this day."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the LORD has driven great and strong nations out from before you. But as for you, no man has stood before you to this day."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"One man of you shall chase a thousand; for it is the LORD your God who fights for you, as he spoke to you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Take good heed therefore to yourselves, that you love the LORD your God."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut if you do at all go back, and hold fast to the remnant of these nations, even these who remain among you, and make marriages with them, and go in to them, and they to you;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"know for a certainty that the LORD your God will no longer drive these nations from out of your sight; but they shall be a snare and a trap to you, a scourge in your sides, and thorns in your eyes, until you perish from off this good land which the LORD your God has given you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, today I am going the way of all the earth. You know in all your hearts and in all your souls that not one thing has failed of all the good things which the LORD your God spoke concerning you. All have happened to you. Not one thing has failed of it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"It shall happen that as all the good things have come on you of which the LORD your God spoke to you, so the LORD will bring on you all the evil things, until he has destroyed you from off this good land which the LORD your God has given you,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"when you disobey the covenant of the LORD your God, which he commanded you, and go and serve other gods, and bow down yourselves to them. Then the LORD\u2019s anger will be kindled against you, and you will perish quickly from off the good land which he has given to you.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua gathered all the tribes of Israel to Shechem, and called for the elders of Israel, for their heads, for their judges, and for their officers; and they presented themselves before God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Joshua said to all the people, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018Your fathers lived of old time beyond the River, even Terah, the father of Abraham, and the father of Nahor. They served other gods."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I took your father Abraham from beyond the River, and led him throughout all the land of Canaan, and multiplied his offspring, and gave him Isaac."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I gave to Isaac Jacob and Esau: and I gave to Esau Mount Seir, to possess it. Jacob and his children went down into Egypt."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018I sent Moses and Aaron, and I plagued Egypt, according to that which I did among them: and afterward I brought you out."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I brought your fathers out of Egypt: and you came to the sea. The Egyptians pursued your fathers with chariots and with horsemen to the Red Sea."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When they cried out to the LORD, he put darkness between you and the Egyptians, and brought the sea on them, and covered them; and your eyes saw what I did in Egypt. You lived in the wilderness many days."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018I brought you into the land of the Amorites, that lived beyond the Jordan. They fought with you, and I gave them into your hand. You possessed their land, and I destroyed them from before you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab, arose and fought against Israel. He sent and called Balaam the son of Beor to curse you,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but I would not listen to Balaam; therefore he blessed you still. So I delivered you out of his hand."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You went over the Jordan, and came to Jericho. The men of Jericho fought against you, the Amorite, the Perizzite, the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Girgashite, the Hivite, and the Jebusite; and I delivered them into your hand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I sent the hornet before you, which drove them out from before you, even the two kings of the Amorites; not with your sword, nor with your bow."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I gave you a land on which you had not labored, and cities which you didn\u2019t build, and you live in them. You eat of vineyards and olive groves which you didn\u2019t plant.\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore fear the LORD, and serve him in sincerity and in truth. Put away the gods which your fathers served beyond the River, in Egypt; and serve the LORD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If it seems evil to you to serve the LORD, choose today whom you will serve; whether the gods which your fathers served that were beyond the River, or the gods of the Amorites, in whose land you dwell; but as for me and my house, we will serve the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The people answered, \u201cFar be it from us that we should forsake the LORD, to serve other gods;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"for it is the LORD our God who brought us and our fathers up out of the land of Egypt, from the house of bondage, and who did those great signs in our sight, and preserved us in all the way in which we went, and among all the peoples through the middle of whom we passed."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The LORD drove out from before us all the peoples, even the Amorites who lived in the land. Therefore we also will serve the LORD; for he is our God.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Joshua said to the people, \u201cYou can\u2019t serve the LORD, for he is a holy God. He is a jealous God. He will not forgive your disobedience nor your sins."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"If you forsake the LORD, and serve foreign gods, then he will turn and do you evil, and consume you, after he has done you good.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The people said to Joshua, \u201cNo, but we will serve the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Joshua said to the people, \u201cYou are witnesses against yourselves that you have chosen the LORD yourselves, to serve him.\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cWe are witnesses.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore put away the foreign gods which are among you, and incline your heart to the LORD, the God of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The people said to Joshua, \u201cWe will serve the LORD our God, and we will listen to his voice.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joshua made a covenant with the people that day, and made for them a statute and an ordinance in Shechem."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Joshua wrote these words in the book of the law of God; and he took a great stone, and set it up there under the oak that was by the sanctuary of the LORD."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Joshua said to all the people, \u201cBehold, this stone shall be a witness against us, for it has heard all the LORD\u2019s words which he spoke to us. It shall be therefore a witness against you, lest you deny your God.\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So Joshua sent the people away, each to his own inheritance."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Joshua the son of Nun, the servant of the LORD, died, being one hundred ten years old."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"They buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnathserah, which is in the hill country of Ephraim, on the north of the mountain of Gaash."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Israel served the LORD all the days of Joshua, and all the days of the elders who outlived Joshua, and had known all the work of the LORD, that he had worked for Israel."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They buried the bones of Joseph, which the children of Israel brought up out of Egypt, in Shechem, in the parcel of ground which Jacob bought from the sons of Hamor the father of Shechem for a hundred pieces of silver. They became the inheritance of the children of Joseph."]],f:["Hebrew: kesitahs. A kesitah was a kind of silver coin."]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Eleazar the son of Aaron died. They buried him in the hill of Phinehas his son, which was given him in the hill country of Ephraim."]]}]]}},1277,[]);
__d(function(e,t,h,a,o,n,i){o.exports={book:"Judg",name:"Judges",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After the death of Joshua, the children of Israel asked of the LORD, saying, \u201cWho should go up for us first against the Canaanites, to fight against them?\u201d"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cJudah shall go up. Behold, I have delivered the land into his hand.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah said to Simeon his brother, \u201cCome up with me into my lot, that we may fight against the Canaanites; and I likewise will go with you into your lot.\u201d So Simeon went with him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Judah went up, and the LORD delivered the Canaanites and the Perizzites into their hand. They struck ten thousand men in Bezek."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They found Adoni-Bezek in Bezek, and they fought against him. They struck the Canaanites and the Perizzites."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But Adoni-Bezek fled. They pursued him, caught him, and cut off his thumbs and his big toes."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Adoni-Bezek said, \u201cSeventy kings, having their thumbs and their big toes cut off, scavenged under my table. As I have done, so God has done to me.\u201d They brought him to Jerusalem, and he died there."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of Judah fought against Jerusalem, took it, struck it with the edge of the sword, and set the city on fire."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"After that, the children of Judah went down to fight against the Canaanites who lived in the hill country, and in the South, and in the lowland."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Judah went against the Canaanites who lived in Hebron. (The name of Hebron before that was Kiriath Arba.) They struck Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"From there he went against the inhabitants of Debir. (The name of Debir before that was Kiriath Sepher.)"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Caleb said, \u201cI will give Achsah my daughter as wife to the man who strikes Kiriath Sepher, and takes it.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb\u2019s younger brother, took it, so he gave him Achsah his daughter as his wife."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When she came, she got him to ask her father for a field. She got off her donkey; and Caleb said to her, \u201cWhat would you like?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to him, \u201cGive me a blessing; because you have set me in the land of the South, give me also springs of water.\u201d Then Caleb gave her the upper springs and the lower springs."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The children of the Kenite, Moses\u2019 brother-in-law, went up out of the city of palm trees with the children of Judah into the wilderness of Judah, which is in the south of Arad; and they went and lived with the people."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Judah went with Simeon his brother, and they struck the Canaanites who inhabited Zephath, and utterly destroyed it. The name of the city was called Hormah."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Also Judah took Gaza with its border, and Ashkelon with its border, and Ekron with its border."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The LORD was with Judah, and drove out the inhabitants of the hill country; for he could not drive out the inhabitants of the valley, because they had chariots of iron."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They gave Hebron to Caleb, as Moses had said, and he drove the three sons of Anak out of there."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin didn\u2019t drive out the Jebusites who inhabited Jerusalem, but the Jebusites dwell with the children of Benjamin in Jerusalem to this day."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The house of Joseph also went up against Bethel, and the LORD was with them."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The house of Joseph sent to spy out Bethel. (The name of the city before that was Luz.)"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The watchers saw a man come out of the city, and they said to him, \u201cPlease show us the entrance into the city, and we will deal kindly with you.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He showed them the entrance into the city, and they struck the city with the edge of the sword; but they let the man and all his family go."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The man went into the land of the Hittites, built a city, and called its name Luz, which is its name to this day."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Manasseh didn\u2019t drive out the inhabitants of Beth Shean and its towns, nor Taanach and its towns, nor the inhabitants of Dor and its towns, nor the inhabitants of Ibleam and its towns, nor the inhabitants of Megiddo and its towns; but the Canaanites would dwell in that land."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"When Israel had grown strong, they put the Canaanites to forced labor, and didn\u2019t utterly drive them out."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Ephraim didn\u2019t drive out the Canaanites who lived in Gezer, but the Canaanites lived in Gezer among them."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Zebulun didn\u2019t drive out the inhabitants of Kitron, nor the inhabitants of Nahalol; but the Canaanites lived among them, and became subject to forced labor."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Asher didn\u2019t drive out the inhabitants of Acco, nor the inhabitants of Sidon, nor of Ahlab, nor of Achzib, nor of Helbah, nor of Aphik, nor of Rehob;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"but the Asherites lived among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land, for they didn\u2019t drive them out."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Naphtali didn\u2019t drive out the inhabitants of Beth Shemesh, nor the inhabitants of Beth Anath; but he lived among the Canaanites, the inhabitants of the land. Nevertheless the inhabitants of Beth Shemesh and of Beth Anath became subject to forced labor."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The Amorites forced the children of Dan into the hill country, for they would not allow them to come down to the valley;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"but the Amorites would dwell in Mount Heres, in Aijalon, and in Shaalbim. Yet the hand of the house of Joseph prevailed, so that they became subject to forced labor."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The border of the Amorites was from the ascent of Akrabbim, from the rock, and upward."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel came up from Gilgal to Bochim. He said, \u201cI brought you out of Egypt, and have brought you to the land which I swore to give your fathers. I said, \u2018I will never break my covenant with you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You shall make no covenant with the inhabitants of this land. You shall break down their altars.\u2019 But you have not listened to my voice. Why have you done this?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore I also said, \u2018I will not drive them out from before you; but they shall be in your sides, and their gods will be a snare to you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD\u2019s angel spoke these words to all the children of Israel, the people lifted up their voice and wept."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They called the name of that place Bochim, and they sacrificed there to the LORD."]],f:["\u201cBochim\u201d means \u201cweepers\u201d."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now when Joshua had sent the people away, the children of Israel each went to his inheritance to possess the land."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The people served the LORD all the days of Joshua, and all the days of the elders who outlived Joshua, who had seen all the great work of the LORD that he had worked for Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Joshua the son of Nun, the servant of the LORD, died, being one hundred ten years old."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They buried him in the border of his inheritance in Timnath Heres, in the hill country of Ephraim, on the north of the mountain of Gaash."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"After all that generation were gathered to their fathers, another generation arose after them who didn\u2019t know the LORD, nor the work which he had done for Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and served the Baals."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They abandoned the LORD, the God of their fathers, who brought them out of the land of Egypt, and followed other gods, of the gods of the peoples who were around them, and bowed themselves down to them; and they provoked the LORD to anger."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They abandoned the LORD, and served Baal and the Ashtaroth."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel, and he delivered them into the hands of raiders who plundered them. He sold them into the hands of their enemies all around, so that they could no longer stand before their enemies."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Wherever they went out, the LORD\u2019s hand was against them for evil, as the LORD had spoken, and as the LORD had sworn to them; and they were very distressed."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The LORD raised up judges, who saved them out of the hand of those who plundered them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Yet they didn\u2019t listen to their judges; for they prostituted themselves to other gods, and bowed themselves down to them. They quickly turned away from the way in which their fathers walked, obeying the LORD\u2019s commandments. They didn\u2019t do so."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When the LORD raised up judges for them, then the LORD was with the judge, and saved them out of the hand of their enemies all the days of the judge; for it grieved the LORD because of their groaning by reason of those who oppressed them and troubled them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But when the judge was dead, they turned back, and dealt more corruptly than their fathers in following other gods to serve them and to bow down to them. They didn\u2019t cease what they were doing, or give up their stubborn ways."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel; and he said, \u201cBecause this nation transgressed my covenant which I commanded their fathers, and has not listened to my voice,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I also will no longer drive out any of the nations that Joshua left when he died from before them;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"that by them I may test Israel, to see if they will keep the LORD\u2019s way to walk therein, as their fathers kept it, or not.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So the LORD left those nations, without driving them out hastily. He didn\u2019t deliver them into Joshua\u2019s hand."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the nations which the LORD left, to test Israel by them, even as many as had not known all the wars of Canaan;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"only that the generations of the children of Israel might know, to teach them war, at least those who knew nothing of it before:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"the five lords of the Philistines, all the Canaanites, the Sidonians, and the Hivites who lived on Mount Lebanon, from Mount Baal Hermon to the entrance of Hamath."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They were left to test Israel by them, to know whether they would listen to the LORD\u2019s commandments, which he commanded their fathers by Moses."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The children of Israel lived among the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They took their daughters to be their wives, and gave their own daughters to their sons and served their gods."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and forgot the LORD their God, and served the Baals and the Asheroth."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel, and he sold them into the hand of Cushan Rishathaim king of Mesopotamia; and the children of Israel served Cushan Rishathaim eight years."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When the children of Israel cried to the LORD, the LORD raised up a savior to the children of Israel, who saved them, even Othniel the son of Kenaz, Caleb\u2019s younger brother."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s Spirit came on him, and he judged Israel; and he went out to war, and the LORD delivered Cushan Rishathaim king of Mesopotamia into his hand. His hand prevailed against Cushan Rishathaim."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The land had rest forty years, then Othniel the son of Kenaz died."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel again did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and the LORD strengthened Eglon the king of Moab against Israel, because they had done that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He gathered the children of Ammon and Amalek to himself; and he went and struck Israel, and they possessed the city of palm trees."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The children of Israel served Eglon the king of Moab eighteen years."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But when the children of Israel cried to the LORD, the LORD raised up a savior for them: Ehud the son of Gera, the Benjamite, a left-handed man. The children of Israel sent tribute by him to Eglon the king of Moab."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Ehud made himself a sword which had two edges, a cubit in length; and he wore it under his clothing on his right thigh."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He offered the tribute to Eglon king of Moab. Now Eglon was a very fat man."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When Ehud had finished offering the tribute, he sent away the people who carried the tribute."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But he himself turned back from the stone idols that were by Gilgal, and said, \u201cI have a secret message for you, O king.\u201d"],[0,"The king said, \u201cKeep silence!\u201d All who stood by him left him."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Ehud came to him; and he was sitting by himself alone in the cool upper room. Ehud said, \u201cI have a message from God to you.\u201d He arose out of his seat."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Ehud put out his left hand, and took the sword from his right thigh, and thrust it into his body."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The handle also went in after the blade; and the fat closed on the blade, for he didn\u2019t draw the sword out of his body; and it came out behind."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then Ehud went out onto the porch, and shut the doors of the upper room on him, and locked them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"After he had gone, his servants came and saw that the doors of the upper room were locked. They said, \u201cSurely he is covering his feet in the upper room.\u201d"]],f:["or, \u201crelieving himself\u201d."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They waited until they were ashamed; and behold, he didn\u2019t open the doors of the upper room. Therefore they took the key and opened them, and behold, their lord had fallen down dead on the floor."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Ehud escaped while they waited, passed beyond the stone idols, and escaped to Seirah."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When he had come, he blew a trumpet in the hill country of Ephraim; and the children of Israel went down with him from the hill country, and he led them."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cFollow me; for the LORD has delivered your enemies the Moabites into your hand.\u201d They followed him, and took the fords of the Jordan against the Moabites, and didn\u2019t allow any man to pass over."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They struck at that time about ten thousand men of Moab, every strong man and every man of valor. No man escaped."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"So Moab was subdued that day under the hand of Israel. Then the land had rest eighty years."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"After him was Shamgar the son of Anath, who struck six hundred men of the Philistines with an ox goad. He also saved Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel again did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, when Ehud was dead."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD sold them into the hand of Jabin king of Canaan, who reigned in Hazor; the captain of whose army was Sisera, who lived in Harosheth of the Gentiles."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The children of Israel cried to the LORD, for he had nine hundred chariots of iron; and he mightily oppressed the children of Israel for twenty years."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now Deborah, a prophetess, the wife of Lappidoth, judged Israel at that time."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"She lived under Deborah\u2019s palm tree between Ramah and Bethel in the hill country of Ephraim; and the children of Israel came up to her for judgment."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"She sent and called Barak the son of Abinoam out of Kedesh Naphtali, and said to him, \u201cHasn\u2019t the LORD, the God of Israel, commanded, \u2018Go and lead the way to Mount Tabor, and take with you ten thousand men of the children of Naphtali and of the children of Zebulun?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I will draw to you, to the river Kishon, Sisera, the captain of Jabin\u2019s army, with his chariots and his multitude; and I will deliver him into your hand.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Barak said to her, \u201cIf you will go with me, then I will go; but if you will not go with me, I will not go.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cI will surely go with you. Nevertheless, the journey that you take won\u2019t be for your honor; for the LORD will sell Sisera into a woman\u2019s hand.\u201d Deborah arose, and went with Barak to Kedesh."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Barak called Zebulun and Naphtali together to Kedesh. Ten thousand men followed him; and Deborah went up with him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now Heber the Kenite had separated himself from the Kenites, even from the children of Hobab, Moses\u2019 brother-in-law, and had pitched his tent as far as the oak in Zaanannim, which is by Kedesh."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They told Sisera that Barak the son of Abinoam had gone up to Mount Tabor."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Sisera gathered together all his chariots, even nine hundred chariots of iron, and all the people who were with him, from Harosheth of the Gentiles, to the river Kishon."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Deborah said to Barak, \u201cGo; for this is the day in which the LORD has delivered Sisera into your hand. Hasn\u2019t the LORD gone out before you?\u201d So Barak went down from Mount Tabor, and ten thousand men after him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The LORD confused Sisera, all his chariots, and all his army, with the edge of the sword before Barak. Sisera abandoned his chariot and fled away on his feet."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But Barak pursued the chariots and the army to Harosheth of the Gentiles; and all the army of Sisera fell by the edge of the sword. There was not a man left."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"However Sisera fled away on his feet to the tent of Jael the wife of Heber the Kenite; for there was peace between Jabin the king of Hazor and the house of Heber the Kenite."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jael went out to meet Sisera, and said to him, \u201cTurn in, my lord, turn in to me; don\u2019t be afraid.\u201d He came in to her into the tent, and she covered him with a rug."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cPlease give me a little water to drink; for I am thirsty.\u201d"],[0,"She opened a container of milk, and gave him a drink, and covered him."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cStand in the door of the tent, and if any man comes and inquires of you, and says, \u2018Is there any man here?\u2019 you shall say, \u2018No.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jael, Heber\u2019s wife, took a tent peg, and took a hammer in her hand, and went softly to him, and struck the pin into his temples, and it pierced through into the ground, for he was in a deep sleep; so he fainted and died."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Behold, as Barak pursued Sisera, Jael came out to meet him, and said to him, \u201cCome, and I will show you the man whom you seek.\u201d He came to her; and behold, Sisera lay dead, and the tent peg was in his temples."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So God subdued Jabin the king of Canaan before the children of Israel on that day."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The hand of the children of Israel prevailed more and more against Jabin the king of Canaan, until they had destroyed Jabin king of Canaan."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Deborah and Barak the son of Abinoam sang on that day, saying,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBecause the leaders took the lead in Israel,"],[2,"because the people offered themselves willingly,"],[1,"be blessed, LORD!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear, you kings!"],[2,"Give ear, you princes!"],[1,"I, even I, will sing to the LORD."],[2,"I will sing praise to the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLORD, when you went out of Seir,"],[2,"when you marched out of the field of Edom,"],[1,"the earth trembled, the sky also dropped."],[2,"Yes, the clouds dropped water."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains quaked at the LORD\u2019s presence,"],[2,"even Sinai at the presence of the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIn the days of Shamgar the son of Anath,"],[2,"in the days of Jael, the highways were unoccupied."],[2,"The travelers walked through byways."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The rulers ceased in Israel."],[2,"They ceased until I, Deborah, arose;"],[2,"Until I arose a mother in Israel."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They chose new gods."],[2,"Then war was in the gates."],[2,"Was there a shield or spear seen among forty thousand in Israel?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"My heart is toward the governors of Israel,"],[2,"who offered themselves willingly among the people."],[2,"Bless the LORD!"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSpeak, you who ride on white donkeys,"],[2,"you who sit on rich carpets,"],[2,"and you who walk by the way."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Far from the noise of archers, in the places of drawing water,"],[2,"there they will rehearse the LORD\u2019s righteous acts,"],[2,"the righteous acts of his rule in Israel."],[1,"\u201cThen the LORD\u2019s people went down to the gates."]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"\u2018Awake, awake, Deborah!"],[2,"Awake, awake, utter a song!"],[2,"Arise, Barak, and lead away your captives, you son of Abinoam.\u2019"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThen a remnant of the nobles and the people came down."],[2,"The LORD came down for me against the mighty."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Those whose root is in Amalek came out of Ephraim,"],[2,"after you, Benjamin, among your peoples."],[1,"Governors come down out of Machir."],[2,"Those who handle the marshal\u2019s staff came out of Zebulun."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The princes of Issachar were with Deborah."],[2,"As was Issachar, so was Barak."],[2,"They rushed into the valley at his feet."],[1,"By the watercourses of Reuben,"],[2,"there were great resolves of heart."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Why did you sit among the sheepfolds?"],[2,"To hear the whistling for the flocks?"],[1,"At the watercourses of Reuben,"],[2,"there were great searchings of heart."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Gilead lived beyond the Jordan."],[2,"Why did Dan remain in ships?"],[2,"Asher sat still at the haven of the sea,"],[2,"and lived by his creeks."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Zebulun was a people that jeopardized their lives to the death;"],[2,"Naphtali also, on the high places of the field."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe kings came and fought,"],[2,"then the kings of Canaan fought at Taanach by the waters of Megiddo."],[2,"They took no plunder of silver."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"From the sky the stars fought."],[2,"From their courses, they fought against Sisera."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The river Kishon swept them away,"],[2,"that ancient river, the river Kishon."],[2,"My soul, march on with strength."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the horse hoofs stamped because of the prancing,"],[2,"the prancing of their strong ones."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018Curse Meroz,\u2019 said the LORD\u2019s angel."],[2,"\u2018Curse bitterly its inhabitants,"],[2,"because they didn\u2019t come to help the LORD,"],[2,"to help the LORD against the mighty.\u2019"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cJael shall be blessed above women,"],[2,"the wife of Heber the Kenite;"],[2,"blessed shall she be above women in the tent."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"He asked for water."],[2,"She gave him milk."],[2,"She brought him butter in a lordly dish."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"She put her hand to the tent peg,"],[2,"and her right hand to the workmen\u2019s hammer."],[1,"With the hammer she struck Sisera."],[2,"She struck through his head."],[2,"Yes, she pierced and struck through his temples."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"At her feet he bowed, he fell, he lay."],[2,"At her feet he bowed, he fell."],[2,"Where he bowed, there he fell down dead."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThrough the window she looked out, and cried:"],[2,"Sisera\u2019s mother looked through the lattice."],[1,"\u2018Why is his chariot so long in coming?"],[2,"Why do the wheels of his chariots wait?\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Her wise ladies answered her,"],[2,"Yes, she returned answer to herself,"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018Have they not found, have they not divided the plunder?"],[2,"A lady, two ladies to every man;"],[1,"to Sisera a plunder of dyed garments,"],[2,"a plunder of dyed garments embroidered,"],[2,"of dyed garments embroidered on both sides, on the necks of the plunder?\u2019"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSo let all your enemies perish, LORD,"],[2,"but let those who love him be as the sun when it rises in its strength.\u201d"],[0,"Then the land had rest forty years."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, so the LORD delivered them into the hand of Midian seven years."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The hand of Midian prevailed against Israel; and because of Midian the children of Israel made themselves the dens which are in the mountains, the caves, and the strongholds."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So it was, when Israel had sown, that the Midianites, the Amalekites, and the children of the east came up against them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They encamped against them, and destroyed the increase of the earth, until you come to Gaza. They left no sustenance in Israel, and no sheep, ox, or donkey."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For they came up with their livestock and their tents. They came in as locusts for multitude. Both they and their camels were without number; and they came into the land to destroy it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Israel was brought very low because of Midian; and the children of Israel cried to the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When the children of Israel cried to the LORD because of Midian,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD sent a prophet to the children of Israel; and he said to them, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018I brought you up from Egypt, and brought you out of the house of bondage."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians and out of the hand of all who oppressed you, and drove them out from before you, and gave you their land."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I said to you, \u201cI am the LORD your God. You shall not fear the gods of the Amorites, in whose land you dwell.\u201d But you have not listened to my voice.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel came and sat under the oak which was in Ophrah, that belonged to Joash the Abiezrite. His son Gideon was beating out wheat in the wine press, to hide it from the Midianites."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel appeared to him, and said to him, \u201cThe LORD is with you, you mighty man of valor!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon said to him, \u201cOh, my lord, if the LORD is with us, why then has all this happened to us? Where are all his wondrous works which our fathers told us of, saying, \u2018Didn\u2019t the LORD bring us up from Egypt?\u2019 But now the LORD has cast us off, and delivered us into the hand of Midian.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD looked at him, and said, \u201cGo in this your might, and save Israel from the hand of Midian. Haven\u2019t I sent you?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cO Lord, how shall I save Israel? Behold, my family is the poorest in Manasseh, and I am the least in my father\u2019s house.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cSurely I will be with you, and you shall strike the Midianites as one man.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cIf now I have found favor in your sight, then show me a sign that it is you who talk with me."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Please don\u2019t go away until I come to you, and bring out my present, and lay it before you.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will wait until you come back.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon went in and prepared a young goat and unleavened cakes of an ephah of meal. He put the meat in a basket and he put the broth in a pot, and brought it out to him under the oak, and presented it."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The angel of God said to him, \u201cTake the meat and the unleavened cakes, and lay them on this rock, and pour out the broth.\u201d"],[0,"He did so."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s angel stretched out the end of the staff that was in his hand, and touched the meat and the unleavened cakes; and fire went up out of the rock and consumed the meat and the unleavened cakes. Then the LORD\u2019s angel departed out of his sight."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon saw that he was the LORD\u2019s angel; and Gideon said, \u201cAlas, Lord GOD! Because I have seen the LORD\u2019s angel face to face!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cPeace be to you! Don\u2019t be afraid. You shall not die.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Gideon built an altar there to the LORD, and called it \u201cThe LORD is Peace.\u201d To this day it is still in Ophrah of the Abiezrites."]],f:["or, Shalom"]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"That same night, the LORD said to him, \u201cTake your father\u2019s bull, even the second bull seven years old, and throw down the altar of Baal that your father has, and cut down the Asherah that is by it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Then build an altar to the LORD your God on the top of this stronghold, in an orderly way, and take the second bull, and offer a burnt offering with the wood of the Asherah which you shall cut down.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Gideon took ten men of his servants, and did as the LORD had spoken to him. Because he feared his father\u2019s household and the men of the city, he could not do it by day, but he did it by night."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"When the men of the city arose early in the morning, behold, the altar of Baal was broken down, and the Asherah was cut down that was by it, and the second bull was offered on the altar that was built."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They said to one another, \u201cWho has done this thing?\u201d"],[0,"When they inquired and asked, they said, \u201cGideon the son of Joash has done this thing.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the men of the city said to Joash, \u201cBring out your son, that he may die, because he has broken down the altar of Baal, and because he has cut down the Asherah that was by it.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Joash said to all who stood against him, \u201cWill you contend for Baal? Or will you save him? He who will contend for him, let him be put to death by morning! If he is a god, let him contend for himself, because someone has broken down his altar!\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Therefore on that day he named him Jerub-Baal, saying, \u201cLet Baal contend against him, because he has broken down his altar.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cJerub-Baal\u201d means \u201cLet Baal contend\u201d."]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the Midianites and the Amalekites and the children of the east assembled themselves together; and they passed over, and encamped in the valley of Jezreel."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But the LORD\u2019s Spirit came on Gideon, and he blew a trumpet; and Abiezer was gathered together to follow him."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"He sent messengers throughout all Manasseh, and they also were gathered together to follow him. He sent messengers to Asher, to Zebulun, and to Naphtali; and they came up to meet them."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon said to God, \u201cIf you will save Israel by my hand, as you have spoken,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"behold, I will put a fleece of wool on the threshing floor. If there is dew on the fleece only, and it is dry on all the ground, then I\u2019ll know that you will save Israel by my hand, as you have spoken.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"It was so; for he rose up early on the next day, and pressed the fleece together, and wrung the dew out of the fleece, a bowl full of water."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon said to God, \u201cDon\u2019t let your anger be kindled against me, and I will speak but this once. Please let me make a trial just this once with the fleece. Let it now be dry only on the fleece, and on all the ground let there be dew.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"God did so that night; for it was dry on the fleece only, and there was dew on all the ground."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jerubbaal, who is Gideon, and all the people who were with him, rose up early and encamped beside the spring of Harod. Midian\u2019s camp was on the north side of them, by the hill of Moreh, in the valley."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Gideon, \u201cThe people who are with you are too many for me to give the Midianites into their hand, lest Israel brag against me, saying, \u2018My own hand has saved me.\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now therefore proclaim in the ears of the people, saying, \u2018Whoever is fearful and trembling, let him return and depart from Mount Gilead.\u2019\u201d So twenty-two thousand of the people returned, and ten thousand remained."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Gideon, \u201cThere are still too many people. Bring them down to the water, and I will test them for you there. It shall be, that those whom I tell you, \u2018This shall go with you,\u2019 shall go with you; and whoever I tell you, \u2018This shall not go with you,\u2019 shall not go.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So he brought down the people to the water; and the LORD said to Gideon, \u201cEveryone who laps of the water with his tongue, like a dog laps, you shall set him by himself; likewise everyone who bows down on his knees to drink.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The number of those who lapped, putting their hand to their mouth, was three hundred men; but all the rest of the people bowed down on their knees to drink water."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Gideon, \u201cI will save you by the three hundred men who lapped, and deliver the Midianites into your hand. Let all the other people go, each to his own place.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So the people took food in their hand, and their trumpets; and he sent all the rest of the men of Israel to their own tents, but retained the three hundred men; and the camp of Midian was beneath him in the valley."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"That same night, the LORD said to him, \u201cArise, go down into the camp, for I have delivered it into your hand."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But if you are afraid to go down, go with Purah your servant down to the camp."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You will hear what they say; and afterward your hands will be strengthened to go down into the camp.\u201d Then he went down with Purah his servant to the outermost part of the armed men who were in the camp."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The Midianites and the Amalekites and all the children of the east lay along in the valley like locusts for multitude; and their camels were without number, as the sand which is on the seashore for multitude."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When Gideon had come, behold, there was a man telling a dream to his fellow. He said, \u201cBehold, I dreamed a dream; and behold, a cake of barley bread tumbled into the camp of Midian, came to the tent, and struck it so that it fell, and turned it upside down, so that the tent lay flat.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"His fellow answered, \u201cThis is nothing other than the sword of Gideon the son of Joash, a man of Israel. God has delivered Midian into his hand, with all the army.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"It was so, when Gideon heard the telling of the dream and its interpretation, that he worshiped. Then he returned into the camp of Israel and said, \u201cArise, for the LORD has delivered the army of Midian into your hand!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He divided the three hundred men into three companies, and he put into the hands of all of them trumpets and empty pitchers, with torches within the pitchers."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWatch me, and do likewise. Behold, when I come to the outermost part of the camp, it shall be that, as I do, so you shall do."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When I blow the trumpet, I and all who are with me, then blow the trumpets also on every side of all the camp, and shout, \u2018For the LORD and for Gideon!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So Gideon and the hundred men who were with him came to the outermost part of the camp in the beginning of the middle watch, when they had but newly set the watch. Then they blew the trumpets and broke in pieces the pitchers that were in their hands."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The three companies blew the trumpets, broke the pitchers, and held the torches in their left hands and the trumpets in their right hands with which to blow; and they shouted, \u201cThe sword of the LORD and of Gideon!\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They each stood in his place around the camp, and all the army ran; and they shouted, and put them to flight."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They blew the three hundred trumpets, and the LORD set every man\u2019s sword against his fellow and against all the army; and the army fled as far as Beth Shittah toward Zererah, as far as the border of Abel Meholah, by Tabbath."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The men of Israel were gathered together out of Naphtali, out of Asher, and out of all Manasseh, and pursued Midian."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Gideon sent messengers throughout all the hill country of Ephraim, saying, \u201cCome down against Midian and take the waters before them as far as Beth Barah, even the Jordan!\u201d So all the men of Ephraim were gathered together and took the waters as far as Beth Barah, even the Jordan."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They took the two princes of Midian, Oreb and Zeeb. They killed Oreb at Oreb\u2019s rock, and Zeeb they killed at Zeeb\u2019s wine press, as they pursued Midian. Then they brought the heads of Oreb and Zeeb to Gideon beyond the Jordan."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of Ephraim said to him, \u201cWhy have you treated us this way, that you didn\u2019t call us when you went to fight with Midian?\u201d They rebuked him sharply."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat have I now done in comparison with you? Isn\u2019t the gleaning of the grapes of Ephraim better than the vintage of Abiezer?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"God has delivered into your hand the princes of Midian, Oreb and Zeeb! What was I able to do in comparison with you?\u201d Then their anger was abated toward him when he had said that."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon came to the Jordan and passed over, he and the three hundred men who were with him, faint, yet pursuing."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He said to the men of Succoth, \u201cPlease give loaves of bread to the people who follow me; for they are faint, and I am pursuing after Zebah and Zalmunna, the kings of Midian.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The princes of Succoth said, \u201cAre the hands of Zebah and Zalmunna now in your hand, that we should give bread to your army?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon said, \u201cTherefore when the LORD has delivered Zebah and Zalmunna into my hand, then I will tear your flesh with the thorns of the wilderness and with briers.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He went up there to Penuel, and spoke to them in the same way; and the men of Penuel answered him as the men of Succoth had answered."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He spoke also to the men of Penuel, saying, \u201cWhen I come again in peace, I will break down this tower.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Zebah and Zalmunna were in Karkor, and their armies with them, about fifteen thousand men, all who were left of all the army of the children of the east; for there fell one hundred twenty thousand men who drew sword."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Gideon went up by the way of those who lived in tents on the east of Nobah and Jogbehah, and struck the army; for the army felt secure."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Zebah and Zalmunna fled and he pursued them. He took the two kings of Midian, Zebah and Zalmunna, and confused all the army."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Gideon the son of Joash returned from the battle from the ascent of Heres."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He caught a young man of the men of Succoth, and inquired of him; and he described for him the princes of Succoth, and its elders, seventy-seven men."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He came to the men of Succoth, and said, \u201cSee Zebah and Zalmunna, concerning whom you taunted me, saying, \u2018Are the hands of Zebah and Zalmunna now in your hand, that we should give bread to your men who are weary?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He took the elders of the city, and thorns of the wilderness and briers, and with them he taught the men of Succoth."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He broke down the tower of Penuel, and killed the men of the city."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to Zebah and Zalmunna, \u201cWhat kind of men were they whom you killed at Tabor?\u201d"],[0,"They answered, \u201cThey were like you. They all resembled the children of a king.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThey were my brothers, the sons of my mother. As the LORD lives, if you had saved them alive, I would not kill you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to Jether his firstborn, \u201cGet up and kill them!\u201d But the youth didn\u2019t draw his sword; for he was afraid, because he was yet a youth."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zebah and Zalmunna said, \u201cYou rise and fall on us; for as the man is, so is his strength.\u201d Gideon arose, and killed Zebah and Zalmunna, and took the crescents that were on their camels\u2019 necks."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the men of Israel said to Gideon, \u201cRule over us, both you, your son, and your son\u2019s son also; for you have saved us out of the hand of Midian.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Gideon said to them, \u201cI will not rule over you, neither shall my son rule over you. The LORD shall rule over you.\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Gideon said to them, \u201cI do have a request: that you would each give me the earrings of his plunder.\u201d (For they had golden earrings, because they were Ishmaelites.)"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered, \u201cWe will willingly give them.\u201d They spread a garment, and every man threw the earrings of his plunder into it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The weight of the golden earrings that he requested was one thousand and seven hundred shekels of gold, in addition to the crescents, and the pendants, and the purple clothing that was on the kings of Midian, and in addition to the chains that were about their camels\u2019 necks."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.32 Troy ounces, so 1700 shekels is about 17 kilograms or 37.4 pounds."]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Gideon made an ephod out of it, and put it in Ophrah, his city. Then all Israel played the prostitute with it there; and it became a snare to Gideon and to his house."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So Midian was subdued before the children of Israel, and they lifted up their heads no more. The land had rest forty years in the days of Gideon."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jerubbaal the son of Joash went and lived in his own house."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Gideon had seventy sons conceived from his body, for he had many wives."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"His concubine who was in Shechem also bore him a son, and he named him Abimelech."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Gideon the son of Joash died in a good old age, and was buried in the tomb of Joash his father, in Ophrah of the Abiezrites."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"As soon as Gideon was dead, the children of Israel turned again and played the prostitute following the Baals, and made Baal Berith their god."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The children of Israel didn\u2019t remember the LORD their God, who had delivered them out of the hand of all their enemies on every side;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"neither did they show kindness to the house of Jerubbaal, that is, Gideon, according to all the goodness which he had shown to Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Abimelech the son of Jerubbaal went to Shechem to his mother\u2019s brothers, and spoke with them and with all the family of the house of his mother\u2019s father, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cPlease speak in the ears of all the men of Shechem, \u2018Is it better for you that all the sons of Jerubbaal, who are seventy persons, rule over you, or that one rule over you?\u2019 Remember also that I am your bone and your flesh.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"His mother\u2019s brothers spoke of him in the ears of all the men of Shechem all these words. Their hearts inclined to follow Abimelech; for they said, \u201cHe is our brother.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They gave him seventy pieces of silver out of the house of Baal Berith, with which Abimelech hired vain and reckless fellows who followed him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He went to his father\u2019s house at Ophrah, and killed his brothers the sons of Jerubbaal, being seventy persons, on one stone; but Jotham the youngest son of Jerubbaal was left, for he hid himself."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"All the men of Shechem assembled themselves together with all the house of Millo, and went and made Abimelech king by the oak of the pillar that was in Shechem."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When they told it to Jotham, he went and stood on the top of Mount Gerizim and lifted up his voice, cried out, and said to them, \u201cListen to me, you men of Shechem, that God may listen to you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The trees set out to anoint a king over themselves. They said to the olive tree, \u2018Reign over us.\u2019"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut the olive tree said to them, \u2018Should I stop producing my oil, with which they honor God and man by me, and go to wave back and forth over the trees?\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe trees said to the fig tree, \u2018Come and reign over us.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut the fig tree said to them, \u2018Should I leave my sweetness, and my good fruit, and go to wave back and forth over the trees?\u2019"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe trees said to the vine, \u2018Come and reign over us.\u2019"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe vine said to them, \u2018Should I leave my new wine, which cheers God and man, and go to wave back and forth over the trees?\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen all the trees said to the bramble, \u2018Come and reign over us.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe bramble said to the trees, \u2018If in truth you anoint me king over you, then come and take refuge in my shade; and if not, let fire come out of the bramble, and devour the cedars of Lebanon.\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore, if you have dealt truly and righteously, in that you have made Abimelech king, and if you have dealt well with Jerubbaal and his house, and have done to him according to the deserving of his hands"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"(for my father fought for you, risked his life, and delivered you out of the hand of Midian;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and you have risen up against my father\u2019s house today and have slain his sons, seventy persons, on one stone, and have made Abimelech, the son of his female servant, king over the men of Shechem, because he is your brother);"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"if you then have dealt truly and righteously with Jerubbaal and with his house today, then rejoice in Abimelech, and let him also rejoice in you;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but if not, let fire come out from Abimelech and devour the men of Shechem and the house of Millo; and let fire come out from the men of Shechem and from the house of Millo and devour Abimelech.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jotham ran away and fled, and went to Beer and lived there, for fear of Abimelech his brother."]],f:["\u201cBeer\u201d is Hebrew for \u201cwell\u201d, i.e., a village named for its well."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Abimelech was prince over Israel three years."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then God sent an evil spirit between Abimelech and the men of Shechem; and the men of Shechem dealt treacherously with Abimelech,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"that the violence done to the seventy sons of Jerubbaal might come, and that their blood might be laid on Abimelech their brother who killed them, and on the men of Shechem who strengthened his hands to kill his brothers."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The men of Shechem set an ambush for him on the tops of the mountains, and they robbed all who came along that way by them; and Abimelech was told about it."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Gaal the son of Ebed came with his brothers and went over to Shechem; and the men of Shechem put their trust in him."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They went out into the field, harvested their vineyards, trod the grapes, celebrated, and went into the house of their god and ate and drank, and cursed Abimelech."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Gaal the son of Ebed said, \u201cWho is Abimelech, and who is Shechem, that we should serve him? Isn\u2019t he the son of Jerubbaal? Isn\u2019t Zebul his officer? Serve the men of Hamor the father of Shechem, but why should we serve him?"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I wish that this people were under my hand! Then I would remove Abimelech.\u201d He said to Abimelech, \u201cIncrease your army and come out!\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"When Zebul the ruler of the city heard the words of Gaal the son of Ebed, his anger burned."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He sent messengers to Abimelech craftily, saying, \u201cBehold, Gaal the son of Ebed and his brothers have come to Shechem; and behold, they incite the city against you."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Now therefore, go up by night, you and the people who are with you, and lie in wait in the field."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"It shall be that in the morning, as soon as the sun is up, you shall rise early and rush on the city. Behold, when he and the people who are with him come out against you, then may you do to them as you shall find occasion.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Abimelech rose up, and all the people who were with him, by night, and they laid wait against Shechem in four companies."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Gaal the son of Ebed went out, and stood in the entrance of the gate of the city. Abimelech rose up, and the people who were with him, from the ambush."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"When Gaal saw the people, he said to Zebul, \u201cBehold, people are coming down from the tops of the mountains.\u201d"],[0,"Zebul said to him, \u201cYou see the shadows of the mountains as if they were men.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Gaal spoke again and said, \u201cBehold, people are coming down by the middle of the land, and one company comes by the way of the oak of Meonenim.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zebul said to him, \u201cNow where is your mouth, that you said, \u2018Who is Abimelech, that we should serve him?\u2019 Isn\u2019t this the people that you have despised? Please go out now and fight with them.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Gaal went out before the men of Shechem, and fought with Abimelech."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Abimelech chased him, and he fled before him, and many fell wounded, even to the entrance of the gate."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Abimelech lived at Arumah; and Zebul drove out Gaal and his brothers, that they should not dwell in Shechem."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"On the next day, the people went out into the field; and they told Abimelech."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He took the people and divided them into three companies, and laid wait in the field; and he looked, and behold, the people came out of the city. So, he rose up against them and struck them."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Abimelech and the companies that were with him rushed forward and stood in the entrance of the gate of the city; and the two companies rushed on all who were in the field and struck them."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Abimelech fought against the city all that day; and he took the city and killed the people in it. He beat down the city and sowed it with salt."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"When all the men of the tower of Shechem heard of it, they entered into the stronghold of the house of Elberith."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Abimelech was told that all the men of the tower of Shechem were gathered together."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Abimelech went up to Mount Zalmon, he and all the people who were with him; and Abimelech took an ax in his hand, and cut down a bough from the trees, and took it up, and laid it on his shoulder. Then he said to the people who were with him, \u201cWhat you have seen me do, make haste, and do as I have done!\u201d"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"All the people likewise each cut down his bough, followed Abimelech, and put them at the base of the stronghold, and set the stronghold on fire over them, so that all the people of the tower of Shechem died also, about a thousand men and women."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Then Abimelech went to Thebez and encamped against Thebez, and took it."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"But there was a strong tower within the city, and all the men and women of the city fled there, and shut themselves in, and went up to the roof of the tower."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"Abimelech came to the tower and fought against it, and came near to the door of the tower to burn it with fire."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"A certain woman cast an upper millstone on Abimelech\u2019s head, and broke his skull."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he called hastily to the young man, his armor bearer, and said to him, \u201cDraw your sword and kill me, that men not say of me, \u2018A woman killed him.\u2019 His young man thrust him through, and he died.\u201d"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"When the men of Israel saw that Abimelech was dead, they each departed to his place."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Thus God repaid the wickedness of Abimelech, which he did to his father in killing his seventy brothers;"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"and God repaid all the wickedness of the men of Shechem on their heads; and the curse of Jotham the son of Jerubbaal came on them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After Abimelech, Tola the son of Puah, the son of Dodo, a man of Issachar, arose to save Israel. He lived in Shamir in the hill country of Ephraim."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He judged Israel twenty-three years, and died, and was buried in Shamir."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"After him Jair, the Gileadite, arose. He judged Israel twenty-two years."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He had thirty sons who rode on thirty donkey colts. They had thirty cities, which are called Havvoth Jair to this day, which are in the land of Gilead."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jair died, and was buried in Kamon."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel again did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and served the Baals, the Ashtaroth, the gods of Syria, the gods of Sidon, the gods of Moab, the gods of the children of Ammon, and the gods of the Philistines. They abandoned the LORD, and didn\u2019t serve him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel, and he sold them into the hand of the Philistines and into the hand of the children of Ammon."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They troubled and oppressed the children of Israel that year. For eighteen years they oppressed all the children of Israel that were beyond the Jordan in the land of the Amorites, which is in Gilead."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The children of Ammon passed over the Jordan to fight also against Judah, and against Benjamin, and against the house of Ephraim, so that Israel was very distressed."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The children of Israel cried to the LORD, saying, \u201cWe have sinned against you, even because we have forsaken our God, and have served the Baals.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to the children of Israel, \u201cDidn\u2019t I save you from the Egyptians, and from the Amorites, from the children of Ammon, and from the Philistines?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The Sidonians also, and the Amalekites, and the Maonites, oppressed you; and you cried to me, and I saved you out of their hand."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Yet you have forsaken me and served other gods. Therefore I will save you no more."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Go and cry to the gods which you have chosen. Let them save you in the time of your distress!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel said to the LORD, \u201cWe have sinned! Do to us whatever seems good to you; only deliver us, please, today.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They put away the foreign gods from among them and served the LORD; and his soul was grieved for the misery of Israel."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the children of Ammon were gathered together and encamped in Gilead. The children of Israel assembled themselves together and encamped in Mizpah."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The people, the princes of Gilead, said to one another, \u201cWho is the man who will begin to fight against the children of Ammon? He shall be head over all the inhabitants of Gilead.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jephthah the Gileadite was a mighty man of valor. He was the son of a prostitute. Gilead became the father of Jephthah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Gilead\u2019s wife bore him sons. When his wife\u2019s sons grew up, they drove Jephthah out and said to him, \u201cYou will not inherit in our father\u2019s house, for you are the son of another woman.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then Jephthah fled from his brothers and lived in the land of Tob. Outlaws joined up with Jephthah, and they went out with him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"After a while, the children of Ammon made war against Israel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When the children of Ammon made war against Israel, the elders of Gilead went to get Jephthah out of the land of Tob."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They said to Jephthah, \u201cCome and be our chief, that we may fight with the children of Ammon.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, \u201cDidn\u2019t you hate me, and drive me out of my father\u2019s house? Why have you come to me now when you are in distress?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The elders of Gilead said to Jephthah, \u201cTherefore we have turned again to you now, that you may go with us and fight with the children of Ammon. You will be our head over all the inhabitants of Gilead.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah said to the elders of Gilead, \u201cIf you bring me home again to fight with the children of Ammon, and the LORD delivers them before me, will I be your head?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The elders of Gilead said to Jephthah, \u201cThe LORD will be witness between us. Surely we will do what you say.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jephthah went with the elders of Gilead, and the people made him head and chief over them. Jephthah spoke all his words before the LORD in Mizpah."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah sent messengers to the king of the children of Ammon, saying, \u201cWhat do you have to do with me, that you have come to me to fight against my land?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of the children of Ammon answered the messengers of Jephthah, \u201cBecause Israel took away my land when he came up out of Egypt, from the Arnon even to the Jabbok, and to the Jordan. Now therefore restore that territory again peaceably.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah sent messengers again to the king of the children of Ammon;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and he said to him, \u201cJephthah says: Israel didn\u2019t take away the land of Moab, nor the land of the children of Ammon;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"but when they came up from Egypt, and Israel went through the wilderness to the Red Sea, and came to Kadesh,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"then Israel sent messengers to the king of Edom, saying, \u2018Please let me pass through your land;\u2019 but the king of Edom didn\u2019t listen. In the same way, he sent to the king of Moab, but he refused; so Israel stayed in Kadesh."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then they went through the wilderness, and went around the land of Edom, and the land of Moab, and came by the east side of the land of Moab, and they encamped on the other side of the Arnon; but they didn\u2019t come within the border of Moab, for the Arnon was the border of Moab."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Israel sent messengers to Sihon king of the Amorites, the king of Heshbon; and Israel said to him, \u2018Please let us pass through your land to my place.\u2019"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But Sihon didn\u2019t trust Israel to pass through his border; but Sihon gathered all his people together, and encamped in Jahaz, and fought against Israel."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD, the God of Israel, delivered Sihon and all his people into the hand of Israel, and they struck them. So Israel possessed all the land of the Amorites, the inhabitants of that country."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They possessed all the border of the Amorites, from the Arnon even to the Jabbok, and from the wilderness even to the Jordan."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So now the LORD, the God of Israel, has dispossessed the Amorites from before his people Israel, and should you possess them?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Won\u2019t you possess that which Chemosh your god gives you to possess? So whoever the LORD our God has dispossessed from before us, them will we possess."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now are you anything better than Balak the son of Zippor, king of Moab? Did he ever strive against Israel, or did he ever fight against them?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Israel lived in Heshbon and its towns, and in Aroer and its towns, and in all the cities that are along the side of the Arnon for three hundred years! Why didn\u2019t you recover them within that time?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Therefore I have not sinned against you, but you do me wrong to war against me. May the LORD the Judge be judge today between the children of Israel and the children of Ammon.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"However, the king of the children of Ammon didn\u2019t listen to the words of Jephthah which he sent him."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s Spirit came on Jephthah, and he passed over Gilead and Manasseh, and passed over Mizpah of Gilead, and from Mizpah of Gilead he passed over to the children of Ammon."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah vowed a vow to the LORD, and said, \u201cIf you will indeed deliver the children of Ammon into my hand,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"then it shall be, that whatever comes out of the doors of my house to meet me when I return in peace from the children of Ammon, it shall be the LORD\u2019s, and I will offer it up for a burnt offering.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jephthah passed over to the children of Ammon to fight against them; and the LORD delivered them into his hand."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He struck them from Aroer until you come to Minnith, even twenty cities, and to Abelcheramim, with a very great slaughter. So the children of Ammon were subdued before the children of Israel."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah came to Mizpah to his house; and behold, his daughter came out to meet him with tambourines and with dances. She was his only child. Besides her he had neither son nor daughter."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"When he saw her, he tore his clothes, and said, \u201cAlas, my daughter! You have brought me very low, and you are one of those who trouble me; for I have opened my mouth to the LORD, and I can\u2019t go back.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to him, \u201cMy father, you have opened your mouth to the LORD; do to me according to that which has proceeded out of your mouth, because the LORD has taken vengeance for you on your enemies, even on the children of Ammon.\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Then she said to her father, \u201cLet this thing be done for me. Leave me alone two months, that I may depart and go down on the mountains, and bewail my virginity, I and my companions.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGo.\u201d He sent her away for two months; and she departed, she and her companions, and mourned her virginity on the mountains."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"At the end of two months, she returned to her father, who did with her according to his vow which he had vowed. She was a virgin. It became a custom in Israel"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"that the daughters of Israel went yearly to celebrate the daughter of Jephthah the Gileadite four days in a year."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of Ephraim were gathered together, and passed northward; and they said to Jephthah, \u201cWhy did you pass over to fight against the children of Ammon, and didn\u2019t call us to go with you? We will burn your house around you with fire!\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah said to them, \u201cI and my people were at great strife with the children of Ammon; and when I called you, you didn\u2019t save me out of their hand."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When I saw that you didn\u2019t save me, I put my life in my hand, and passed over against the children of Ammon, and the LORD delivered them into my hand. Why then have you come up to me today, to fight against me?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jephthah gathered together all the men of Gilead, and fought with Ephraim. The men of Gilead struck Ephraim, because they said, \u201cYou are fugitives of Ephraim, you Gileadites, in the middle of Ephraim, and in the middle of Manasseh.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The Gileadites took the fords of the Jordan against the Ephraimites. Whenever a fugitive of Ephraim said, \u201cLet me go over,\u201d the men of Gilead said to him, \u201cAre you an Ephraimite?\u201d If he said, \u201cNo;\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"then they said to him, \u201cNow say \u2018Shibboleth;\u2019\u201d and he said \u201cSibboleth\u201d; for he couldn\u2019t manage to pronounce it correctly, then they seized him and killed him at the fords of the Jordan. At that time, forty-two thousand of Ephraim fell."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jephthah judged Israel six years. Then Jephthah the Gileadite died, and was buried in the cities of Gilead."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"After him Ibzan of Bethlehem judged Israel."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He had thirty sons. He sent his thirty daughters outside his clan, and he brought in thirty daughters from outside his clan for his sons. He judged Israel seven years."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Ibzan died, and was buried at Bethlehem."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"After him, Elon the Zebulunite judged Israel; and he judged Israel ten years."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Elon the Zebulunite died, and was buried in Aijalon in the land of Zebulun."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"After him, Abdon the son of Hillel the Pirathonite judged Israel."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He had forty sons and thirty sons\u2019 sons who rode on seventy donkey colts. He judged Israel eight years."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Abdon the son of Hillel the Pirathonite died, and was buried in Pirathon in the land of Ephraim, in the hill country of the Amalekites."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel again did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight; and the LORD delivered them into the hand of the Philistines forty years."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a certain man of Zorah, of the family of the Danites, whose name was Manoah; and his wife was barren, and childless."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel appeared to the woman, and said to her, \u201cSee now, you are barren and childless; but you shall conceive and bear a son."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now therefore please beware and drink no wine nor strong drink, and don\u2019t eat any unclean thing;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"for, behold, you shall conceive and give birth to a son. No razor shall come on his head, for the child shall be a Nazirite to God from the womb. He shall begin to save Israel out of the hand of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the woman came and told her husband, saying, \u201cA man of God came to me, and his face was like the face of the angel of God, very awesome. I didn\u2019t ask him where he was from, neither did he tell me his name;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"but he said to me, \u2018Behold, you shall conceive and bear a son; and now drink no wine nor strong drink. Don\u2019t eat any unclean thing, for the child shall be a Nazirite to God from the womb to the day of his death.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Manoah entreated the LORD, and said, \u201cOh, Lord, please let the man of God whom you sent come again to us, and teach us what we should do to the child who shall be born.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"God listened to the voice of Manoah, and the angel of God came again to the woman as she sat in the field; but Manoah, her husband, wasn\u2019t with her."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The woman hurried and ran, and told her husband, saying to him, \u201cBehold, the man who came to me that day has appeared to me.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Manoah arose and followed his wife, and came to the man, and said to him, \u201cAre you the man who spoke to my wife?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Manoah said, \u201cNow let your words happen. What shall the child\u2019s way of life and mission be?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to Manoah, \u201cOf all that I said to the woman let her beware."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"She may not eat of anything that comes of the vine, neither let her drink wine or strong drink, nor eat any unclean thing. Let her observe all that I commanded her.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Manoah said to the LORD\u2019s angel, \u201cPlease stay with us, that we may make a young goat ready for you.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to Manoah, \u201cThough you detain me, I won\u2019t eat your bread. If you will prepare a burnt offering, you must offer it to the LORD.\u201d For Manoah didn\u2019t know that he was the LORD\u2019s angel."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Manoah said to the LORD\u2019s angel, \u201cWhat is your name, that when your words happen, we may honor you?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to him, \u201cWhy do you ask about my name, since it is incomprehensible?\u201d"]],f:["or, wonderful"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So Manoah took the young goat with the meal offering, and offered it on the rock to the LORD. Then the angel did an amazing thing as Manoah and his wife watched."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For when the flame went up toward the sky from off the altar, the LORD\u2019s angel ascended in the flame of the altar. Manoah and his wife watched; and they fell on their faces to the ground."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But the LORD\u2019s angel didn\u2019t appear to Manoah or to his wife any more. Then Manoah knew that he was the LORD\u2019s angel."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Manoah said to his wife, \u201cWe shall surely die, because we have seen God.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But his wife said to him, \u201cIf the LORD were pleased to kill us, he wouldn\u2019t have received a burnt offering and a meal offering at our hand, and he wouldn\u2019t have shown us all these things, nor would he have told us such things as these at this time.\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The woman bore a son and named him Samson. The child grew, and the LORD blessed him."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s Spirit began to move him in Mahaneh Dan, between Zorah and Eshtaol."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Samson went down to Timnah, and saw a woman in Timnah of the daughters of the Philistines."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He came up, and told his father and his mother, saying, \u201cI have seen a woman in Timnah of the daughters of the Philistines. Now therefore get her for me as my wife.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then his father and his mother said to him, \u201cIsn\u2019t there a woman among your brothers\u2019 daughters, or among all my people, that you go to take a wife of the uncircumcised Philistines?\u201d"],[0,"Samson said to his father, \u201cGet her for me, for she pleases me well.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But his father and his mother didn\u2019t know that it was of the LORD; for he sought an occasion against the Philistines. Now at that time the Philistines ruled over Israel."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samson went down to Timnah with his father and his mother, and came to the vineyards of Timnah; and behold, a young lion roared at him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s Spirit came mightily on him, and he tore him as he would have torn a young goat with his bare hands, but he didn\u2019t tell his father or his mother what he had done."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He went down and talked with the woman, and she pleased Samson well."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"After a while he returned to take her, and he went over to see the carcass of the lion; and behold, there was a swarm of bees in the body of the lion, and honey."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He took it into his hands, and went on, eating as he went. He came to his father and mother and gave to them, and they ate, but he didn\u2019t tell them that he had taken the honey out of the lion\u2019s body."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"His father went down to the woman; and Samson made a feast there, for the young men used to do so."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When they saw him, they brought thirty companions to be with him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Samson said to them, \u201cLet me tell you a riddle now. If you can tell me the answer within the seven days of the feast, and find it out, then I will give you thirty linen garments and thirty changes of clothing;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but if you can\u2019t tell me the answer, then you shall give me thirty linen garments and thirty changes of clothing.\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cTell us your riddle, that we may hear it.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them,"],[1,"\u201cOut of the eater came out food."],[2,"Out of the strong came out sweetness.\u201d"],[0,"They couldn\u2019t in three days declare the riddle."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"On the seventh day, they said to Samson\u2019s wife, \u201cEntice your husband, that he may declare to us the riddle, lest we burn you and your father\u2019s house with fire. Have you called us to impoverish us? Isn\u2019t that so?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Samson\u2019s wife wept before him, and said, \u201cYou just hate me, and don\u2019t love me. You\u2019ve told a riddle to the children of my people, and haven\u2019t told it to me.\u201d"],[0,"He said to her, \u201cBehold, I haven\u2019t told my father or my mother, so why should I tell you?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"She wept before him the seven days, while their feast lasted; and on the seventh day, he told her, because she pressed him severely; and she told the riddle to the children of her people."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The men of the city said to him on the seventh day before the sun went down, \u201cWhat is sweeter than honey? What is stronger than a lion?\u201d"],[0,"He said to them,"],[1,"\u201cIf you hadn\u2019t plowed with my heifer,"],[2,"you wouldn\u2019t have found out my riddle.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s Spirit came mightily on him, and he went down to Ashkelon and struck thirty men of them. He took their plunder, then gave the changes of clothing to those who declared the riddle. His anger burned, and he went up to his father\u2019s house."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But Samson\u2019s wife was given to his companion, who had been his friend."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But after a while, in the time of wheat harvest, Samson visited his wife with a young goat. He said, \u201cI will go in to my wife\u2019s room.\u201d"],[0,"But her father wouldn\u2019t allow him to go in."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Her father said, \u201cI most certainly thought that you utterly hated her; therefore I gave her to your companion. Isn\u2019t her younger sister more beautiful than she? Please, take her instead.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Samson said to them, \u201cThis time I will be blameless in the case of the Philistines when I harm them.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Samson went and caught three hundred foxes, and took torches, and turned tail to tail, and put a torch in the middle between every two tails."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When he had set the torches on fire, he let them go into the standing grain of the Philistines, and burned up both the shocks and the standing grain, and also the olive groves."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Philistines said, \u201cWho has done this?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cSamson, the son-in-law of the Timnite, because he has taken his wife and given her to his companion.\u201d The Philistines came up, and burned her and her father with fire."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Samson said to them, \u201cIf you behave like this, surely I will take revenge on you, and after that I will cease.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He struck them hip and thigh with a great slaughter; and he went down and lived in the cave in Etam\u2019s rock."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then the Philistines went up, encamped in Judah, and spread themselves in Lehi."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of Judah said, \u201cWhy have you come up against us?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cWe have come up to bind Samson, to do to him as he has done to us.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then three thousand men of Judah went down to the cave in Etam\u2019s rock, and said to Samson, \u201cDon\u2019t you know that the Philistines are rulers over us? What then is this that you have done to us?\u201d"],[0,"He said to them, \u201cAs they did to me, so I have done to them.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cWe have come down to bind you, that we may deliver you into the hand of the Philistines.\u201d"],[0,"Samson said to them, \u201cSwear to me that you will not attack me yourselves.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"They spoke to him, saying, \u201cNo, but we will bind you securely and deliver you into their hands; but surely we will not kill you.\u201d They bound him with two new ropes, and brought him up from the rock."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came to Lehi, the Philistines shouted as they met him. Then the LORD\u2019s Spirit came mightily on him, and the ropes that were on his arms became as flax that was burned with fire; and his bands dropped from off his hands."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He found a fresh jawbone of a donkey, put out his hand, took it, and struck a thousand men with it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Samson said, \u201cWith the jawbone of a donkey, heaps on heaps; with the jawbone of a donkey I have struck a thousand men.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When he had finished speaking, he threw the jawbone out of his hand; and that place was called Ramath Lehi."]],f:["\u201cRamath\u201d means \u201chill\u201d and \u201cLehi\u201d means \u201cjawbone\u201d."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He was very thirsty, and called on the LORD and said, \u201cYou have given this great deliverance by the hand of your servant; and now shall I die of thirst, and fall into the hands of the uncircumcised?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But God split the hollow place that is in Lehi, and water came out of it. When he had drunk, his spirit came again, and he revived. Therefore its name was called En Hakkore, which is in Lehi, to this day."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He judged Israel twenty years in the days of the Philistines."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Samson went to Gaza, and saw there a prostitute, and went in to her."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Gazites were told, \u201cSamson is here!\u201d They surrounded him and laid wait for him all night in the gate of the city, and were quiet all the night, saying, \u201cWait until morning light; then we will kill him.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Samson lay until midnight, then arose at midnight and took hold of the doors of the gate of the city, with the two posts, and plucked them up, bar and all, and put them on his shoulders and carried them up to the top of the mountain that is before Hebron."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass afterward that he loved a woman in the valley of Sorek, whose name was Delilah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The lords of the Philistines came up to her and said to her, \u201cEntice him, and see in which his great strength lies, and by what means we may prevail against him, that we may bind him to afflict him; and we will each give you eleven hundred pieces of silver.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Delilah said to Samson, \u201cPlease tell me where your great strength lies, and what you might be bound to afflict you.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Samson said to her, \u201cIf they bind me with seven green cords that were never dried, then shall I become weak, and be as another man.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the lords of the Philistines brought up to her seven green cords which had not been dried, and she bound him with them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now she had an ambush waiting in the inner room. She said to him, \u201cThe Philistines are on you, Samson!\u201d He broke the cords as a flax thread is broken when it touches the fire. So his strength was not known."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Delilah said to Samson, \u201cBehold, you have mocked me, and told me lies. Now please tell me how you might be bound.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cIf they only bind me with new ropes with which no work has been done, then I will become weak, and be as another man.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So Delilah took new ropes and bound him with them, then said to him, \u201cThe Philistines are on you, Samson!\u201d The ambush was waiting in the inner room. He broke them off his arms like a thread."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Delilah said to Samson, \u201cUntil now, you have mocked me and told me lies. Tell me with what you might be bound.\u201d"],[0,"He said to her, \u201cIf you weave the seven locks of my head with the fabric on the loom.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"She fastened it with the pin, and said to him, \u201cThe Philistines are on you, Samson!\u201d He awakened out of his sleep, and plucked away the pin of the beam and the fabric."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to him, \u201cHow can you say, \u2018I love you,\u2019 when your heart is not with me? You have mocked me these three times, and have not told me where your great strength lies.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When she pressed him daily with her words and urged him, his soul was troubled to death."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He told her all his heart and said to her, \u201cNo razor has ever come on my head; for I have been a Nazirite to God from my mother\u2019s womb. If I am shaved, then my strength will go from me and I will become weak, and be like any other man.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"When Delilah saw that he had told her all his heart, she sent and called for the lords of the Philistines, saying, \u201cCome up this once, for he has told me all his heart.\u201d Then the lords of the Philistines came up to her and brought the money in their hand."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"She made him sleep on her knees; and she called for a man and shaved off the seven locks of his head; and she began to afflict him, and his strength went from him."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cThe Philistines are upon you, Samson!\u201d"],[0,"He awoke out of his sleep, and said, \u201cI will go out as at other times, and shake myself free.\u201d But he didn\u2019t know that the LORD had departed from him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The Philistines laid hold on him and put out his eyes; and they brought him down to Gaza and bound him with fetters of bronze; and he ground at the mill in the prison."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"However, the hair of his head began to grow again after he was shaved."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The lords of the Philistines gathered together to offer a great sacrifice to Dagon their god, and to rejoice; for they said, \u201cOur god has delivered Samson our enemy into our hand.\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When the people saw him, they praised their god; for they said, \u201cOur god has delivered our enemy and the destroyer of our country, who has slain many of us, into our hand.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"When their hearts were merry, they said, \u201cCall for Samson, that he may entertain us.\u201d They called for Samson out of the prison; and he performed before them. They set him between the pillars;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and Samson said to the boy who held him by the hand, \u201cAllow me to feel the pillars on which the house rests, that I may lean on them.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Now the house was full of men and women; and all the lords of the Philistines were there; and there were on the roof about three thousand men and women, who saw while Samson performed."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Samson called to the LORD, and said, \u201cLord GOD, remember me, please, and strengthen me, please, only this once, God, that I may be at once avenged of the Philistines for my two eyes.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Samson took hold of the two middle pillars on which the house rested and leaned on them, the one with his right hand and the other with his left."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Samson said, \u201cLet me die with the Philistines!\u201d He bowed himself with all his might; and the house fell on the lords, and on all the people who were in it. So the dead that he killed at his death were more than those who he killed in his life."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then his brothers and all the house of his father came down and took him, and brought him up and buried him between Zorah and Eshtaol in the burial site of Manoah his father. He judged Israel twenty years."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a man of the hill country of Ephraim, whose name was Micah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said to his mother, \u201cThe eleven hundred pieces of silver that were taken from you, about which you uttered a curse, and also spoke it in my ears\u2014behold, the silver is with me. I took it.\u201d"],[0,"His mother said, \u201cMay the LORD bless my son!\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He restored the eleven hundred pieces of silver to his mother, then his mother said, \u201cI most certainly dedicate the silver to the LORD from my hand for my son, to make a carved image and a molten image. Now therefore I will restore it to you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When he restored the money to his mother, his mother took two hundred pieces of silver, and gave them to a silversmith, who made a carved image and a molten image out of it. It was in the house of Micah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The man Micah had a house of gods, and he made an ephod, and teraphim, and consecrated one of his sons, who became his priest."]],f:["teraphim were household idols that may have been associated with inheritance rights to the household property."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In those days there was no king in Israel. Everyone did that which was right in his own eyes."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"There was a young man out of Bethlehem Judah, of the family of Judah, who was a Levite; and he lived there."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The man departed out of the city, out of Bethlehem Judah, to live where he could find a place, and he came to the hill country of Ephraim, to the house of Micah, as he traveled."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Micah said to him, \u201cWhere did you come from?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cI am a Levite of Bethlehem Judah, and I am looking for a place to live.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Micah said to him, \u201cDwell with me, and be to me a father and a priest, and I will give you ten pieces of silver per year, a suit of clothing, and your food.\u201d So the Levite went in."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The Levite was content to dwell with the man; and the young man was to him as one of his sons."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Micah consecrated the Levite, and the young man became his priest, and was in the house of Micah."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then Micah said, \u201cNow I know that the LORD will do good to me, since I have a Levite as my priest.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days there was no king in Israel. In those days the tribe of the Danites sought an inheritance to dwell in; for to that day, their inheritance had not fallen to them among the tribes of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The children of Dan sent five men of their family from their whole number, men of valor, from Zorah and from Eshtaol, to spy out the land and to search it. They said to them, \u201cGo, explore the land!\u201d"],[0,"They came to the hill country of Ephraim, to the house of Micah, and lodged there."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When they were by the house of Micah, they knew the voice of the young man the Levite; so they went over there and said to him, \u201cWho brought you here? What do you do in this place? What do you have here?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThus and thus has Micah dealt with me, and he has hired me, and I have become his priest.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cPlease ask counsel of God, that we may know whether our way which we go shall be prosperous.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The priest said to them, \u201cGo in peace. Your way in which you go is before the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the five men departed and came to Laish and saw the people who were there, how they lived in safety, in the way of the Sidonians, quiet and secure; for there was no one in the land possessing authority, that might put them to shame in anything, and they were far from the Sidonians, and had no dealings with anyone else."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They came to their brothers at Zorah and Eshtaol; and their brothers asked them, \u201cWhat do you say?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cArise, and let\u2019s go up against them; for we have seen the land, and behold, it is very good. Do you stand still? Don\u2019t be slothful to go and to enter in to possess the land."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When you go, you will come to an unsuspecting people, and the land is large; for God has given it into your hand, a place where there is no lack of anything that is on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The family of the Danites set out from Zorah and Eshtaol with six hundred men armed with weapons of war."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They went up and encamped in Kiriath Jearim in Judah. Therefore they call that place Mahaneh Dan to this day. Behold, it is behind Kiriath Jearim."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They passed from there to the hill country of Ephraim, and came to the house of Micah."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the five men who went to spy out the country of Laish answered and said to their brothers, \u201cDo you know that there is in these houses an ephod, and teraphim, and a carved image, and a molten image? Now therefore consider what you have to do.\u201d"]],f:["teraphim were household idols that may have been associated with inheritance rights to the household property."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They went over there and came to the house of the young Levite man, even to the house of Micah, and asked him how he was doing."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The six hundred men armed with their weapons of war, who were of the children of Dan, stood by the entrance of the gate."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The five men who went to spy out the land went up, and came in there, and took the engraved image, the ephod, the teraphim, and the molten image; and the priest stood by the entrance of the gate with the six hundred men armed with weapons of war."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"When these went into Micah\u2019s house, and took the engraved image, the ephod, the teraphim, and the molten image, the priest said to them, \u201cWhat are you doing?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cHold your peace, put your hand on your mouth, and go with us. Be a father and a priest to us. Is it better for you to be priest to the house of one man, or to be priest to a tribe and a family in Israel?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The priest\u2019s heart was glad, and he took the ephod, the teraphim, and the engraved image, and went with the people."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So they turned and departed, and put the little ones, the livestock, and the goods before them."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When they were a good way from the house of Micah, the men who were in the houses near Micah\u2019s house gathered together and overtook the children of Dan."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"As they called to the children of Dan, they turned their faces, and said to Micah, \u201cWhat ails you, that you come with such a company?\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou have taken away my gods which I made, and the priest, and have gone away! What more do I have? How can you ask me, \u2018What ails you?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Dan said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t let your voice be heard among us, lest angry fellows fall on you, and you lose your life, with the lives of your household.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Dan went their way; and when Micah saw that they were too strong for him, he turned and went back to his house."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They took that which Micah had made, and the priest whom he had, and came to Laish, to a people quiet and unsuspecting, and struck them with the edge of the sword; then they burned the city with fire."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"There was no deliverer, because it was far from Sidon, and they had no dealings with anyone else; and it was in the valley that lies by Beth Rehob. They built the city and lived in it."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They called the name of the city Dan, after the name of Dan their father, who was born to Israel; however the name of the city used to be Laish."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The children of Dan set up for themselves the engraved image; and Jonathan, the son of Gershom, the son of Moses, and his sons were priests to the tribe of the Danites until the day of the captivity of the land."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"So they set up for themselves Micah\u2019s engraved image which he made, and it remained all the time that God\u2019s house was in Shiloh."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days, when there was no king in Israel, there was a certain Levite living on the farther side of the hill country of Ephraim, who took for himself a concubine out of Bethlehem Judah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"His concubine played the prostitute against him, and went away from him to her father\u2019s house to Bethlehem Judah, and was there for four months."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Her husband arose and went after her to speak kindly to her, to bring her again, having his servant with him and a couple of donkeys. She brought him into her father\u2019s house; and when the father of the young lady saw him, he rejoiced to meet him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"His father-in-law, the young lady\u2019s father, kept him there; and he stayed with him three days. So they ate and drank, and stayed there."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"On the fourth day, they got up early in the morning, and he rose up to depart. The young lady\u2019s father said to his son-in-law, \u201cStrengthen your heart with a morsel of bread, and afterward you shall go your way.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So they sat down, ate, and drank, both of them together. Then the young lady\u2019s father said to the man, \u201cPlease be pleased to stay all night, and let your heart be merry.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The man rose up to depart; but his father-in-law urged him, and he stayed there again."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He arose early in the morning on the fifth day to depart; and the young lady\u2019s father said, \u201cPlease strengthen your heart and stay until the day declines;\u201d and they both ate."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When the man rose up to depart, he, and his concubine, and his servant, his father-in-law, the young lady\u2019s father, said to him, \u201cBehold, now the day draws toward evening, please stay all night. Behold, the day is ending. Stay here, that your heart may be merry; and tomorrow go on your way early, that you may go home.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But the man wouldn\u2019t stay that night, but he rose up and went near Jebus (also called Jerusalem). With him were a couple of saddled donkeys. His concubine also was with him."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When they were by Jebus, the day was far spent; and the servant said to his master, \u201cPlease come and let\u2019s enter into this city of the Jebusites, and stay in it.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"His master said to him, \u201cWe won\u2019t enter into the city of a foreigner that is not of the children of Israel; but we will pass over to Gibeah.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He said to his servant, \u201cCome and let\u2019s draw near to one of these places; and we will lodge in Gibeah, or in Ramah.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So they passed on and went their way; and the sun went down on them near Gibeah, which belongs to Benjamin."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They went over there, to go in to stay in Gibeah. He went in, and sat down in the street of the city; for there was no one who took them into his house to stay."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, an old man came from his work out of the field at evening. Now the man was from the hill country of Ephraim, and he lived in Gibeah; but the men of the place were Benjamites."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He lifted up his eyes, and saw the wayfaring man in the street of the city; and the old man said, \u201cWhere are you going? Where did you come from?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cWe are passing from Bethlehem Judah to the farther side of the hill country of Ephraim. I am from there, and I went to Bethlehem Judah. I am going to the LORD\u2019s house; and there is no one who has taken me into his house."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Yet there is both straw and feed for our donkeys; and there is bread and wine also for me, and for your servant, and for the young man who is with your servants. There is no lack of anything.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The old man said, \u201cPeace be to you! Just let me supply all your needs, but don\u2019t sleep in the street.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So he brought him into his house, and gave the donkeys fodder. Then they washed their feet, and ate and drank."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"As they were making their hearts merry, behold, the men of the city, certain wicked fellows, surrounded the house, beating at the door; and they spoke to the master of the house, the old man, saying, \u201cBring out the man who came into your house, that we can have sex with him!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The man, the master of the house, went out to them, and said to them, \u201cNo, my brothers, please don\u2019t act so wickedly; since this man has come into my house, don\u2019t do this folly."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Behold, here is my virgin daughter and his concubine. I will bring them out now. Humble them, and do with them what seems good to you; but to this man don\u2019t do any such folly.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But the men wouldn\u2019t listen to him; so the man grabbed his concubine, and brought her out to them; and they had sex with her, and abused her all night until the morning. When the day began to dawn, they let her go."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Then the woman came in the dawning of the day, and fell down at the door of the man\u2019s house where her lord was, until it was light."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Her lord rose up in the morning and opened the doors of the house, and went out to go his way; and behold, the woman his concubine had fallen down at the door of the house, with her hands on the threshold."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cGet up, and let\u2019s get going!\u201d but no one answered. Then he took her up on the donkey; and the man rose up, and went to his place."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had come into his house, he took a knife and cut up his concubine, and divided her, limb by limb, into twelve pieces, and sent her throughout all the borders of Israel."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"It was so, that all who saw it said, \u201cSuch a deed has not been done or seen from the day that the children of Israel came up out of the land of Egypt to this day! Consider it, take counsel, and speak.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the children of Israel went out, and the congregation was assembled as one man, from Dan even to Beersheba, with the land of Gilead, to the LORD at Mizpah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The chiefs of all the people, even of all the tribes of Israel, presented themselves in the assembly of the people of God, four hundred thousand footmen who drew sword."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"(Now the children of Benjamin heard that the children of Israel had gone up to Mizpah.) The children of Israel said, \u201cTell us, how did this wickedness happen?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The Levite, the husband of the woman who was murdered, answered, \u201cI came into Gibeah that belongs to Benjamin, I and my concubine, to spend the night."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The men of Gibeah rose against me, and surrounded the house by night. They intended to kill me and they raped my concubine, and she is dead."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I took my concubine and cut her in pieces, and sent her throughout all the country of the inheritance of Israel; for they have committed lewdness and folly in Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Behold, you children of Israel, all of you, give here your advice and counsel.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people arose as one man, saying, \u201cNone of us will go to his tent, neither will any of us turn to his house."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But now this is the thing which we will do to Gibeah: we will go up against it by lot;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and we will take ten men of one hundred throughout all the tribes of Israel, and one hundred of one thousand, and a thousand out of ten thousand to get food for the people, that they may do, when they come to Gibeah of Benjamin, according to all the folly that the men of Gibeah have done in Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"So all the men of Israel were gathered against the city, knit together as one man."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The tribes of Israel sent men through all the tribe of Benjamin, saying, \u201cWhat wickedness is this that has happened among you?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now therefore deliver up the men, the wicked fellows who are in Gibeah, that we may put them to death and put away evil from Israel.\u201d"],[0,"But Benjamin would not listen to the voice of their brothers, the children of Israel."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin gathered themselves together out of the cities to Gibeah, to go out to battle against the children of Israel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin were counted on that day out of the cities twenty-six thousand men who drew the sword, in addition to the inhabitants of Gibeah, who were counted seven hundred chosen men."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Among all these soldiers there were seven hundred chosen men who were left-handed. Every one of them could sling a stone at a hair and not miss."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The men of Israel, besides Benjamin, were counted four hundred thousand men who drew sword. All these were men of war."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel arose, went up to Bethel, and asked counsel of God. They asked, \u201cWho shall go up for us first to battle against the children of Benjamin?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said, \u201cJudah first.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel rose up in the morning and encamped against Gibeah."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The men of Israel went out to battle against Benjamin; and the men of Israel set the battle in array against them at Gibeah."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin came out of Gibeah, and on that day destroyed twenty-two thousand of the Israelite men down to the ground."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The people, the men of Israel, encouraged themselves, and set the battle again in array in the place where they set themselves in array the first day."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The children of Israel went up and wept before the LORD until evening; and they asked of the LORD, saying, \u201cShall I again draw near to battle against the children of Benjamin my brother?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said, \u201cGo up against him.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel came near against the children of Benjamin the second day."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Benjamin went out against them out of Gibeah the second day, and destroyed down to the ground of the children of Israel again eighteen thousand men. All these drew the sword."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the children of Israel and all the people went up, and came to Bethel, and wept, and sat there before the LORD, and fasted that day until evening; then they offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The children of Israel asked the LORD (for the ark of the covenant of God was there in those days,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron, stood before it in those days), saying, \u201cShall I yet again go out to battle against the children of Benjamin my brother, or shall I cease?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said, \u201cGo up; for tomorrow I will deliver him into your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel set ambushes all around Gibeah."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The children of Israel went up against the children of Benjamin on the third day, and set themselves in array against Gibeah, as at other times."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin went out against the people, and were drawn away from the city; and they began to strike and kill of the people as at other times, in the highways, of which one goes up to Bethel and the other to Gibeah, in the field, about thirty men of Israel."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin said, \u201cThey are struck down before us, as at the first.\u201d But the children of Israel said, \u201cLet\u2019s flee, and draw them away from the city to the highways.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"All the men of Israel rose up out of their place and set themselves in array at Baal Tamar. Then the ambushers of Israel broke out of their place, even out of Maareh Geba."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Ten thousand chosen men out of all Israel came over against Gibeah, and the battle was severe; but they didn\u2019t know that disaster was close to them."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The LORD struck Benjamin before Israel; and the children of Israel destroyed of Benjamin that day twenty-five thousand one hundred men. All these drew the sword."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"So the children of Benjamin saw that they were struck, for the men of Israel yielded to Benjamin because they trusted the ambushers whom they had set against Gibeah."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The ambushers hurried, and rushed on Gibeah; then the ambushers spread out, and struck all the city with the edge of the sword."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Now the appointed sign between the men of Israel and the ambushers was that they should make a great cloud of smoke rise up out of the city."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The men of Israel turned in the battle, and Benjamin began to strike and kill of the men of Israel about thirty persons; for they said, \u201cSurely they are struck down before us, as in the first battle.\u201d"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"But when the cloud began to arise up out of the city in a pillar of smoke, the Benjamites looked behind them; and behold, the whole city went up in smoke to the sky."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The men of Israel turned, and the men of Benjamin were dismayed; for they saw that disaster had come on them."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Therefore they turned their backs before the men of Israel to the way of the wilderness, but the battle followed hard after them; and those who came out of the cities destroyed them in the middle of it."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"They surrounded the Benjamites, chased them, and trod them down at their resting place, as far as near Gibeah toward the sunrise."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Eighteen thousand men of Benjamin fell; all these were men of valor."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"They turned and fled toward the wilderness to the rock of Rimmon. They gleaned five thousand men of them in the highways, and followed hard after them to Gidom, and struck two thousand men of them."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"So that all who fell that day of Benjamin were twenty-five thousand men who drew the sword. All these were men of valor."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"But six hundred men turned and fled toward the wilderness to the rock of Rimmon, and stayed in the rock of Rimmon four months."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"The men of Israel turned again on the children of Benjamin, and struck them with the edge of the sword\u2014including the entire city, the livestock, and all that they found. Moreover they set all the cities which they found on fire."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the men of Israel had sworn in Mizpah, saying, \u201cNone of us will give his daughter to Benjamin as a wife.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The people came to Bethel and sat there until evening before God, and lifted up their voices, and wept severely."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, why has this happened in Israel, that there should be one tribe lacking in Israel today?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, the people rose early and built an altar there, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The children of Israel said, \u201cWho is there among all the tribes of Israel who didn\u2019t come up in the assembly to the LORD?\u201d For they had made a great oath concerning him who didn\u2019t come up to the LORD to Mizpah, saying, \u201cHe shall surely be put to death.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The children of Israel grieved for Benjamin their brother, and said, \u201cThere is one tribe cut off from Israel today."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"How shall we provide wives for those who remain, since we have sworn by the LORD that we will not give them of our daughters to wives?\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cWhat one is there of the tribes of Israel who didn\u2019t come up to the LORD to Mizpah?\u201d Behold, no one came from Jabesh Gilead to the camp to the assembly."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For when the people were counted, behold, there were none of the inhabitants of Jabesh Gilead there."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The congregation sent twelve thousand of the most valiant men there, and commanded them, saying, \u201cGo and strike the inhabitants of Jabesh Gilead with the edge of the sword, with the women and the little ones."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"This is the thing that you shall do: you shall utterly destroy every male, and every woman who has lain with a man.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They found among the inhabitants of Jabesh Gilead four hundred young virgins who had not known man by lying with him; and they brought them to the camp to Shiloh, which is in the land of Canaan."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The whole congregation sent and spoke to the children of Benjamin who were in the rock of Rimmon, and proclaimed peace to them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Benjamin returned at that time; and they gave them the women whom they had saved alive of the women of Jabesh Gilead. There still weren\u2019t enough for them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The people grieved for Benjamin, because the LORD had made a breach in the tribes of Israel."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then the elders of the congregation said, \u201cHow shall we provide wives for those who remain, since the women are destroyed out of Benjamin?\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThere must be an inheritance for those who are escaped of Benjamin, that a tribe not be blotted out from Israel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"However, we may not give them wives of our daughters, for the children of Israel had sworn, saying, \u2018Cursed is he who gives a wife to Benjamin.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cBehold, there is a feast of the LORD from year to year in Shiloh, which is on the north of Bethel, on the east side of the highway that goes up from Bethel to Shechem, and on the south of Lebonah.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They commanded the children of Benjamin, saying, \u201cGo and lie in wait in the vineyards,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and see, and behold, if the daughters of Shiloh come out to dance in the dances, then come out of the vineyards, and each man catch his wife of the daughters of Shiloh, and go to the land of Benjamin."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"It shall be, when their fathers or their brothers come to complain to us, that we will say to them, \u2018Grant them graciously to us, because we didn\u2019t take for each man his wife in battle, neither did you give them to them; otherwise you would now be guilty.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin did so, and took wives for themselves according to their number, of those who danced, whom they carried off. They went and returned to their inheritance, built the cities, and lived in them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The children of Israel departed from there at that time, every man to his tribe and to his family, and they each went out from there to his own inheritance."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In those days there was no king in Israel. Everyone did that which was right in his own eyes."]]}]]}},1278,[]);
__d(function(e,o,a,t,h,n,i){h.exports={book:"Ruth",name:"Ruth",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the days when the judges judged, there was a famine in the land. A certain man of Bethlehem Judah went to live in the country of Moab with his wife and his two sons."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The name of the man was Elimelech, and the name of his wife Naomi. The names of his two sons were Mahlon and Chilion, Ephrathites of Bethlehem Judah. They came into the country of Moab and lived there."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Elimelech, Naomi\u2019s husband, died; and she was left with her two sons."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They took for themselves wives of the women of Moab. The name of the one was Orpah, and the name of the other was Ruth. They lived there about ten years."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Mahlon and Chilion both died, and the woman was bereaved of her two children and of her husband."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then she arose with her daughters-in-law, that she might return from the country of Moab; for she had heard in the country of Moab how the LORD had visited his people in giving them bread."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"She went out of the place where she was, and her two daughters-in-law with her. They went on the way to return to the land of Judah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Naomi said to her two daughters-in-law, \u201cGo, return each of you to her mother\u2019s house. May the LORD deal kindly with you, as you have dealt with the dead and with me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"May the LORD grant you that you may find rest, each of you in the house of her husband.\u201d"],[0,"Then she kissed them, and they lifted up their voices, and wept."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They said to her, \u201cNo, but we will return with you to your people.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Naomi said, \u201cGo back, my daughters. Why do you want to go with me? Do I still have sons in my womb, that they may be your husbands?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Go back, my daughters, go your way; for I am too old to have a husband. If I should say, \u2018I have hope,\u2019 if I should even have a husband tonight, and should also bear sons,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"would you then wait until they were grown? Would you then refrain from having husbands? No, my daughters, for it grieves me seriously for your sakes, for the LORD\u2019s hand has gone out against me.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"They lifted up their voices and wept again; then Orpah kissed her mother-in-law, but Ruth stayed with her."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cBehold, your sister-in-law has gone back to her people and to her god. Follow your sister-in-law.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Ruth said, \u201cDon\u2019t urge me to leave you, and to return from following you, for where you go, I will go; and where you stay, I will stay. Your people will be my people, and your God my God."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Where you die, I will die, and there I will be buried. May the LORD do so to me, and more also, if anything but death parts you and me.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"When Naomi saw that she was determined to go with her, she stopped urging her."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So they both went until they came to Bethlehem. When they had come to Bethlehem, all the city was excited about them, and they asked, \u201cIs this Naomi?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t call me Naomi. Call me Mara, for the Almighty has dealt very bitterly with me."]],f:["\u201cNaomi\u201d means \u201cpleasant\u201d.","\u201cMara\u201d means \u201cbitter\u201d."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I went out full, and the LORD has brought me home again empty. Why do you call me Naomi, since the LORD has testified against me, and the Almighty has afflicted me?\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"So Naomi returned, and Ruth the Moabitess, her daughter-in-law, with her, who returned out of the country of Moab. They came to Bethlehem in the beginning of barley harvest."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Naomi had a relative of her husband\u2019s, a mighty man of wealth, of the family of Elimelech, and his name was Boaz."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Ruth the Moabitess said to Naomi, \u201cLet me now go to the field, and glean among the ears of grain after him in whose sight I find favor.\u201d"],[0,"She said to her, \u201cGo, my daughter.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"She went, and came and gleaned in the field after the reapers; and she happened to come to the portion of the field belonging to Boaz, who was of the family of Elimelech."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, Boaz came from Bethlehem, and said to the reapers, \u201cMay the LORD be with you.\u201d"],[0,"They answered him, \u201cMay the LORD bless you.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Boaz said to his servant who was set over the reapers, \u201cWhose young lady is this?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The servant who was set over the reapers answered, \u201cIt is the Moabite lady who came back with Naomi out of the country of Moab."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"She said, \u2018Please let me glean and gather after the reapers among the sheaves.\u2019 So she came, and has continued even from the morning until now, except that she rested a little in the house.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Boaz said to Ruth, \u201cListen, my daughter. Don\u2019t go to glean in another field, and don\u2019t go from here, but stay here close to my maidens."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Let your eyes be on the field that they reap, and go after them. Haven\u2019t I commanded the young men not to touch you? When you are thirsty, go to the vessels, and drink from that which the young men have drawn.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she fell on her face and bowed herself to the ground, and said to him, \u201cWhy have I found favor in your sight, that you should take knowledge of me, since I am a foreigner?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Boaz answered her, \u201cI have been told all about what you have done for your mother-in-law since the death of your husband, and how you have left your father, your mother, and the land of your birth, and have come to a people that you didn\u2019t know before."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"May the LORD repay your work, and a full reward be given to you from the LORD, the God of Israel, under whose wings you have come to take refuge.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she said, \u201cLet me find favor in your sight, my lord, because you have comforted me, and because you have spoken kindly to your servant, though I am not as one of your servants.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"At meal time Boaz said to her, \u201cCome here, and eat some bread, and dip your morsel in the vinegar.\u201d"],[0,"She sat beside the reapers, and they passed her parched grain. She ate, was satisfied, and left some of it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When she had risen up to glean, Boaz commanded his young men, saying, \u201cLet her glean even among the sheaves, and don\u2019t reproach her."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Also pull out some for her from the bundles, and leave it. Let her glean, and don\u2019t rebuke her.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So she gleaned in the field until evening; and she beat out that which she had gleaned, and it was about an ephah of barley."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"She took it up, and went into the city. Then her mother-in-law saw what she had gleaned; and she brought out and gave to her that which she had left after she had enough."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Her mother-in-law said to her, \u201cWhere have you gleaned today? Where have you worked? Blessed be he who noticed you.\u201d"],[0,"She told her mother-in-law with whom she had worked, \u201cThe man\u2019s name with whom I worked today is Boaz.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Naomi said to her daughter-in-law, \u201cMay he be blessed by the LORD, who has not abandoned his kindness to the living and to the dead.\u201d Naomi said to her, \u201cThe man is a close relative to us, one of our near kinsmen.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Ruth the Moabitess said, \u201cYes, he said to me, \u2018You shall stay close to my young men until they have finished all my harvest.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Naomi said to Ruth her daughter-in-law, \u201cIt is good, my daughter, that you go out with his maidens, and that they not harm you in any other field.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So she stayed close to the maidens of Boaz, to glean to the end of barley harvest and of wheat harvest; and she lived with her mother-in-law."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Naomi her mother-in-law said to her, \u201cMy daughter, shall I not seek rest for you, that it may be well with you?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now isn\u2019t Boaz our kinsman, with whose maidens you were? Behold, he will be winnowing barley tonight on the threshing floor."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore wash yourself, anoint yourself, get dressed, and go down to the threshing floor; but don\u2019t make yourself known to the man until he has finished eating and drinking."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"It shall be, when he lies down, that you shall note the place where he is lying. Then you shall go in, uncover his feet, and lie down. Then he will tell you what to do.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to her, \u201cAll that you say, I will do.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"She went down to the threshing floor, and did everything that her mother-in-law told her."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When Boaz had eaten and drunk, and his heart was merry, he went to lie down at the end of the heap of grain. She came softly, uncovered his feet, and lay down."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"At midnight, the man was startled and turned himself; and behold, a woman lay at his feet."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWho are you?\u201d"],[0,"She answered, \u201cI am Ruth your servant. Therefore spread the corner of your garment over your servant; for you are a near kinsman.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou are blessed by the LORD, my daughter. You have shown more kindness in the latter end than at the beginning, because you didn\u2019t follow young men, whether poor or rich."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now, my daughter, don\u2019t be afraid. I will do to you all that you say; for all the city of my people knows that you are a worthy woman."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now it is true that I am a near kinsman. However, there is a kinsman nearer than I."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Stay this night, and in the morning, if he will perform for you the part of a kinsman, good. Let him do the kinsman\u2019s duty. But if he will not do the duty of a kinsman for you, then I will do the duty of a kinsman for you, as the LORD lives. Lie down until the morning.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"She lay at his feet until the morning, then she rose up before one could discern another. For he said, \u201cLet it not be known that the woman came to the threshing floor.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBring the mantle that is on you, and hold it.\u201d She held it; and he measured six measures of barley, and laid it on her; then he went into the city."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When she came to her mother-in-law, she said, \u201cHow did it go, my daughter?\u201d"],[0,"She told her all that the man had done for her."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cHe gave me these six measures of barley; for he said, \u2018Don\u2019t go empty to your mother-in-law.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she said, \u201cWait, my daughter, until you know what will happen; for the man will not rest until he has settled this today.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Boaz went up to the gate and sat down there. Behold, the near kinsman of whom Boaz spoke came by. Boaz said to him, \u201cCome over here, friend, and sit down!\u201d He came over, and sat down."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Boaz took ten men of the elders of the city, and said, \u201cSit down here,\u201d and they sat down."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He said to the near kinsman, \u201cNaomi, who has come back out of the country of Moab, is selling the parcel of land, which was our brother Elimelech\u2019s."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I thought I should tell you, saying, \u2018Buy it before those who sit here, and before the elders of my people.\u2019 If you will redeem it, redeem it; but if you will not redeem it, then tell me, that I may know. For there is no one to redeem it besides you; and I am after you.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will redeem it.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Boaz said, \u201cOn the day you buy the field from the hand of Naomi, you must buy it also from Ruth the Moabitess, the wife of the dead, to raise up the name of the dead on his inheritance.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The near kinsman said, \u201cI can\u2019t redeem it for myself, lest I endanger my own inheritance. Take my right of redemption for yourself; for I can\u2019t redeem it.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this was the custom in former time in Israel concerning redeeming and concerning exchanging, to confirm all things: a man took off his sandal, and gave it to his neighbor; and this was the way of formalizing transactions in Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So the near kinsman said to Boaz, \u201cBuy it for yourself,\u201d then he took off his sandal."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Boaz said to the elders and to all the people, \u201cYou are witnesses today, that I have bought all that was Elimelech\u2019s, and all that was Chilion\u2019s and Mahlon\u2019s, from the hand of Naomi."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Moreover, Ruth the Moabitess, the wife of Mahlon, I have purchased to be my wife, to raise up the name of the dead on his inheritance, that the name of the dead may not be cut off from among his brothers and from the gate of his place. You are witnesses today.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people who were in the gate, and the elders, said, \u201cWe are witnesses. May the LORD make the woman who has come into your house like Rachel and like Leah, which both built the house of Israel; and treat you worthily in Ephrathah, and be famous in Bethlehem."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Let your house be like the house of Perez, whom Tamar bore to Judah, of the offspring which the LORD will give you by this young woman.\u201d"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"So Boaz took Ruth and she became his wife; and he went in to her, and the LORD enabled her to conceive, and she bore a son."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The women said to Naomi, \u201cBlessed be the LORD, who has not left you today without a near kinsman. Let his name be famous in Israel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He shall be to you a restorer of life and sustain you in your old age; for your daughter-in-law, who loves you, who is better to you than seven sons, has given birth to him.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Naomi took the child, laid him in her bosom, and became nurse to him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The women, her neighbors, gave him a name, saying, \u201cA son is born to Naomi\u201d. They named him Obed. He is the father of Jesse, the father of David."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this is the history of the generations of Perez: Perez became the father of Hezron,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and Hezron became the father of Ram, and Ram became the father of Amminadab,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and Amminadab became the father of Nahshon, and Nahshon became the father of Salmon,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and Salmon became the father of Boaz, and Boaz became the father of Obed,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and Obed became the father of Jesse, and Jesse became the father of David."]]}]]}},1279,[]);
__d(function(e,a,t,h,o,n,i){o.exports={book:"1Sam",name:"1 Samuel",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was a certain man of Ramathaim Zophim, of the hill country of Ephraim, and his name was Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Elihu, the son of Tohu, the son of Zuph, an Ephraimite."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He had two wives. The name of one was Hannah, and the name of the other Peninnah. Peninnah had children, but Hannah had no children."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This man went up out of his city from year to year to worship and to sacrifice to the LORD of Armies in Shiloh. The two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, priests to the LORD, were there."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When the day came that Elkanah sacrificed, he gave portions to Peninnah his wife and to all her sons and her daughters;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"but he gave a double portion to Hannah, for he loved Hannah, but the LORD had shut up her womb."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Her rival provoked her severely, to irritate her, because the LORD had shut up her womb."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So year by year, when she went up to the LORD\u2019s house, her rival provoked her. Therefore she wept, and didn\u2019t eat."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Elkanah her husband said to her, \u201cHannah, why do you weep? Why don\u2019t you eat? Why is your heart grieved? Am I not better to you than ten sons?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hannah rose up after they had finished eating and drinking in Shiloh. Now Eli the priest was sitting on his seat by the doorpost of the LORD\u2019s temple."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"She was in bitterness of soul, and prayed to the LORD, weeping bitterly."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"She vowed a vow, and said, \u201cLORD of Armies, if you will indeed look at the affliction of your servant and remember me, and not forget your servant, but will give to your servant a boy, then I will give him to the LORD all the days of his life, and no razor shall come on his head.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"As she continued praying before the LORD, Eli saw her mouth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now Hannah spoke in her heart. Only her lips moved, but her voice was not heard. Therefore Eli thought she was drunk."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Eli said to her, \u201cHow long will you be drunk? Get rid of your wine!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Hannah answered, \u201cNo, my lord, I am a woman of a sorrowful spirit. I have not been drinking wine or strong drink, but I poured out my soul before the LORD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t consider your servant a wicked woman; for I have been speaking out of the abundance of my complaint and my provocation.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eli answered, \u201cGo in peace; and may the God of Israel grant your petition that you have asked of him.\u201d"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cLet your servant find favor in your sight.\u201d So the woman went her way and ate; and her facial expression wasn\u2019t sad any more."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They rose up in the morning early and worshiped the LORD, then returned and came to their house to Ramah. Then Elkanah knew Hannah his wife; and the LORD remembered her."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When the time had come, Hannah conceived, and bore a son; and she named him Samuel, saying, \u201cBecause I have asked him of the LORD.\u201d"]],f:["Samuel sounds like the Hebrew for \u201cheard by God.\u201d"]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The man Elkanah, and all his house, went up to offer to the LORD the yearly sacrifice and his vow."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But Hannah didn\u2019t go up, for she said to her husband, \u201cNot until the child is weaned; then I will bring him, that he may appear before the LORD, and stay there forever.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Elkanah her husband said to her, \u201cDo what seems good to you. Wait until you have weaned him; only may the LORD establish his word.\u201d"],[0,"So the woman waited and nursed her son until she weaned him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When she had weaned him, she took him up with her, with three bulls, and one ephah of meal, and a container of wine, and brought him to the LORD\u2019s house in Shiloh. The child was young."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They killed the bull, and brought the child to Eli."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cOh, my lord, as your soul lives, my lord, I am the woman who stood by you here, praying to the LORD."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"I prayed for this child, and the LORD has given me my petition which I asked of him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Therefore I have also given him to the LORD. As long as he lives he is given to the LORD.\u201d He worshiped the LORD there."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hannah prayed, and said,"],[1,"\u201cMy heart exults in the LORD!"],[2,"My horn is exalted in the LORD."],[1,"My mouth is enlarged over my enemies,"],[2,"because I rejoice in your salvation."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no one as holy as the LORD,"],[2,"for there is no one besides you,"],[2,"nor is there any rock like our God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t keep talking so exceedingly proudly."],[2,"Don\u2019t let arrogance come out of your mouth,"],[2,"for the LORD is a God of knowledge."],[2,"By him actions are weighed."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe bows of the mighty men are broken."],[2,"Those who stumbled are armed with strength."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who were full have hired themselves out for bread."],[2,"Those who were hungry are satisfied."],[1,"Yes, the barren has borne seven."],[2,"She who has many children languishes."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe LORD kills and makes alive."],[2,"He brings down to Sheol and brings up."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD makes poor and makes rich."],[2,"He brings low, he also lifts up."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He raises up the poor out of the dust."],[2,"He lifts up the needy from the dunghill"],[2,"to make them sit with princes"],[2,"and inherit the throne of glory."],[1,"For the pillars of the earth are the LORD\u2019s."],[2,"He has set the world on them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He will keep the feet of his holy ones,"],[2,"but the wicked will be put to silence in darkness;"],[2,"for no man will prevail by strength."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who strive with the LORD shall be broken to pieces."],[2,"He will thunder against them in the sky."],[1,"\u201cThe LORD will judge the ends of the earth."],[2,"He will give strength to his king,"],[2,"and exalt the horn of his anointed.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Elkanah went to Ramah to his house. The child served the LORD before Eli the priest."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the sons of Eli were wicked men. They didn\u2019t know the LORD."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The custom of the priests with the people was that when anyone offered a sacrifice, the priest\u2019s servant came while the meat was boiling, with a fork of three teeth in his hand;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and he stabbed it into the pan, or kettle, or cauldron, or pot. The priest took all that the fork brought up for himself. They did this to all the Israelites who came there to Shiloh."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Yes, before they burned the fat, the priest\u2019s servant came, and said to the man who sacrificed, \u201cGive meat to roast for the priest; for he will not accept boiled meat from you, but raw.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"If the man said to him, \u201cLet the fat be burned first, and then take as much as your soul desires;\u201d then he would say, \u201cNo, but you shall give it to me now; and if not, I will take it by force.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The sin of the young men was very great before the LORD; for the men despised the LORD\u2019s offering."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But Samuel ministered before the LORD, being a child, clothed with a linen ephod."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Moreover his mother made him a little robe, and brought it to him from year to year when she came up with her husband to offer the yearly sacrifice."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Eli blessed Elkanah and his wife, and said, \u201cMay the LORD give you offspring from this woman for the petition which was asked of the LORD.\u201d Then they went to their own home."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD visited Hannah, and she conceived and bore three sons and two daughters. The child Samuel grew before the LORD."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Eli was very old; and he heard all that his sons did to all Israel, and how that they slept with the women who served at the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhy do you do such things? For I hear of your evil dealings from all these people."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"No, my sons; for it is not a good report that I hear! You make the LORD\u2019s people disobey."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"If one man sins against another, God will judge him; but if a man sins against the LORD, who will intercede for him?\u201d Notwithstanding, they didn\u2019t listen to the voice of their father, because the LORD intended to kill them."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The child Samuel grew on, and increased in favor both with the LORD and also with men."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"A man of God came to Eli and said to him, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Did I reveal myself to the house of your father when they were in Egypt in bondage to Pharaoh\u2019s house?"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t I choose him out of all the tribes of Israel to be my priest, to go up to my altar, to burn incense, to wear an ephod before me? Didn\u2019t I give to the house of your father all the offerings of the children of Israel made by fire?"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Why do you kick at my sacrifice and at my offering, which I have commanded in my habitation, and honor your sons above me, to make yourselves fat with the best of all the offerings of Israel my people?\u2019"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018I said indeed that your house and the house of your father should walk before me forever.\u2019 But now the LORD says, \u2018Far be it from me; for those who honor me I will honor, and those who despise me will be cursed."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Behold, the days come that I will cut off your arm and the arm of your father\u2019s house, that there will not be an old man in your house."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:32,l:[[0,"You will see the affliction of my habitation, in all the wealth which I will give Israel. There shall not be an old man in your house forever."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The man of yours whom I don\u2019t cut off from my altar will consume your eyes and grieve your heart. All the increase of your house will die in the flower of their age."]],f:["or, blind your eyes with tears"]},{v:34,l:[[0,"This will be the sign to you that will come on your two sons, on Hophni and Phinehas: in one day they will both die."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"I will raise up a faithful priest for myself who will do according to that which is in my heart and in my mind. I will build him a sure house. He will walk before my anointed forever."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"It will happen that everyone who is left in your house will come and bow down to him for a piece of silver and a loaf of bread, and will say, \u201cPlease put me into one of the priests\u2019 offices, that I may eat a morsel of bread.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The child Samuel ministered to the LORD before Eli. The LORD\u2019s word was rare in those days. There were not many visions, then."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"At that time, when Eli was laid down in his place (now his eyes had begun to grow dim, so that he could not see),"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and God\u2019s lamp hadn\u2019t yet gone out, and Samuel had laid down in the LORD\u2019s temple where God\u2019s ark was,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD called Samuel. He said, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He ran to Eli and said, \u201cHere I am; for you called me.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI didn\u2019t call. Lie down again.\u201d"],[0,"He went and lay down."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD called yet again, \u201cSamuel!\u201d"],[0,"Samuel arose and went to Eli and said, \u201cHere I am; for you called me.\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cI didn\u2019t call, my son. Lie down again.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now Samuel didn\u2019t yet know the LORD, neither was the LORD\u2019s word yet revealed to him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD called Samuel again the third time. He arose and went to Eli and said, \u201cHere I am; for you called me.\u201d"],[0,"Eli perceived that the LORD had called the child."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore Eli said to Samuel, \u201cGo, lie down. It shall be, if he calls you, that you shall say, \u2018Speak, LORD; for your servant hears.\u2019\u201d So Samuel went and lay down in his place."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD came, and stood, and called as at other times, \u201cSamuel! Samuel!\u201d"],[0,"Then Samuel said, \u201cSpeak; for your servant hears.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Samuel, \u201cBehold, I will do a thing in Israel at which both the ears of everyone who hears it will tingle."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"In that day I will perform against Eli all that I have spoken concerning his house, from the beginning even to the end."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For I have told him that I will judge his house forever for the iniquity which he knew, because his sons brought a curse on themselves, and he didn\u2019t restrain them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore I have sworn to the house of Eli that the iniquity of Eli\u2019s house shall not be removed with sacrifice or offering forever.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel lay until the morning, and opened the doors of the LORD\u2019s house. Samuel was afraid to show Eli the vision."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then Eli called Samuel and said, \u201cSamuel, my son!\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHere I am.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhat is the thing that he has spoken to you? Please don\u2019t hide it from me. God do so to you, and more also, if you hide anything from me of all the things that he spoke to you.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel told him every bit, and hid nothing from him."],[0,"He said, \u201cIt is the LORD. Let him do what seems good to him.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel grew, and the LORD was with him and let none of his words fall to the ground."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"All Israel from Dan even to Beersheba knew that Samuel was established to be a prophet of the LORD."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared again in Shiloh; for the LORD revealed himself to Samuel in Shiloh by the LORD\u2019s word."]]}],[{v:1,l:[[0,"The word of Samuel came to all Israel."],[0,"Now Israel went out against the Philistines to battle, and encamped beside Ebenezer; and the Philistines encamped in Aphek."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Philistines put themselves in array against Israel. When they joined battle, Israel was defeated by the Philistines, who killed about four thousand men of the army in the field."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When the people had come into the camp, the elders of Israel said, \u201cWhy has the LORD defeated us today before the Philistines? Let\u2019s get the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant out of Shiloh and bring it to us, that it may come among us and save us out of the hand of our enemies.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"So the people sent to Shiloh, and they brought from there the ark of the covenant of the LORD of Armies, who sits above the cherubim; and the two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, were there with the ark of the covenant of God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant came into the camp, all Israel shouted with a great shout, so that the earth resounded."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When the Philistines heard the noise of the shout, they said, \u201cWhat does the noise of this great shout in the camp of the Hebrews mean?\u201d They understood that the LORD\u2019s ark had come into the camp."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The Philistines were afraid, for they said, \u201cGod has come into the camp.\u201d They said, \u201cWoe to us! For there has not been such a thing before."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Woe to us! Who shall deliver us out of the hand of these mighty gods? These are the gods that struck the Egyptians with all kinds of plagues in the wilderness."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Be strong and behave like men, O you Philistines, that you not be servants to the Hebrews, as they have been to you. Strengthen yourselves like men, and fight!\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The Philistines fought, and Israel was defeated, and each man fled to his tent. There was a very great slaughter; for thirty thousand footmen of Israel fell."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"God\u2019s ark was taken; and the two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, were slain."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"A man of Benjamin ran out of the army and came to Shiloh the same day, with his clothes torn and with dirt on his head."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When he came, behold, Eli was sitting on his seat by the road watching, for his heart trembled for God\u2019s ark. When the man came into the city and told about it, all the city cried out."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When Eli heard the noise of the crying, he said, \u201cWhat does the noise of this tumult mean?\u201d"],[0,"The man hurried, and came and told Eli."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now Eli was ninety-eight years old. His eyes were set, so that he could not see."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The man said to Eli, \u201cI am he who came out of the army, and I fled today out of the army.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHow did the matter go, my son?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He who brought the news answered, \u201cIsrael has fled before the Philistines, and there has been also a great slaughter among the people. Your two sons also, Hophni and Phinehas, are dead, and God\u2019s ark has been captured.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"When he made mention of God\u2019s ark, Eli fell from off his seat backward by the side of the gate; and his neck broke, and he died, for he was an old man and heavy. He had judged Israel forty years."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"His daughter-in-law, Phinehas\u2019 wife, was with child, near to giving birth. When she heard the news that God\u2019s ark was taken and that her father-in-law and her husband were dead, she bowed herself and gave birth; for her pains came on her."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"About the time of her death the women who stood by her said to her, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for you have given birth to a son.\u201d But she didn\u2019t answer, neither did she regard it."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"She named the child Ichabod, saying, \u201cThe glory has departed from Israel!\u201d because God\u2019s ark was taken, and because of her father-in-law and her husband."]],f:["\u201cIchabod\u201d means \u201cno glory\u201d."]},{v:22,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cThe glory has departed from Israel; for God\u2019s ark has been taken.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the Philistines had taken God\u2019s ark, and they brought it from Ebenezer to Ashdod."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Philistines took God\u2019s ark, and brought it into the house of Dagon and set it by Dagon."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When the people of Ashdod arose early on the next day, behold, Dagon had fallen on his face to the ground before the LORD\u2019s ark. They took Dagon and set him in his place again."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When they arose early on the following morning, behold, Dagon had fallen on his face to the ground before the LORD\u2019s ark; and the head of Dagon and both the palms of his hands were cut off on the threshold. Only Dagon\u2019s torso was intact."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Therefore neither the priests of Dagon nor any who come into Dagon\u2019s house step on the threshold of Dagon in Ashdod to this day."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But the LORD\u2019s hand was heavy on the people of Ashdod, and he destroyed them and struck them with tumors, even Ashdod and its borders."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When the men of Ashdod saw that it was so, they said, \u201cThe ark of the God of Israel shall not stay with us, for his hand is severe on us and on Dagon our god.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They sent therefore and gathered together all the lords of the Philistines, and said, \u201cWhat shall we do with the ark of the God of Israel?\u201d"],[0,"They answered, \u201cLet the ark of the God of Israel be carried over to Gath.\u201d They carried the ark of the God of Israel there."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It was so, that after they had carried it there, the LORD\u2019s hand was against the city with a very great confusion; and he struck the men of the city, both small and great, so that tumors broke out on them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So they sent God\u2019s ark to Ekron."],[0,"As God\u2019s ark came to Ekron, the Ekronites cried out, saying, \u201cThey have brought the ark of the God of Israel here to us, to kill us and our people.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They sent therefore and gathered together all the lords of the Philistines, and they said, \u201cSend the ark of the God of Israel away, and let it go again to its own place, that it not kill us and our people.\u201d For there was a deadly panic throughout all the city. The hand of God was very heavy there."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The men who didn\u2019t die were struck with the tumors; and the cry of the city went up to heaven."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s ark was in the country of the Philistines seven months."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Philistines called for the priests and the diviners, saying, \u201cWhat shall we do with the LORD\u2019s ark? Show us how we should send it to its place.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cIf you send away the ark of the God of Israel, don\u2019t send it empty; but by all means return a trespass offering to him. Then you will be healed, and it will be known to you why his hand is not removed from you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they said, \u201cWhat should the trespass offering be which we shall return to him?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cFive golden tumors and five golden mice, for the number of the lords of the Philistines; for one plague was on you all, and on your lords."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall make images of your tumors and images of your mice that mar the land; and you shall give glory to the God of Israel. Perhaps he will release his hand from you, from your gods, and from your land."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Why then do you harden your hearts as the Egyptians and Pharaoh hardened their hearts? When he had worked wonderfully among them, didn\u2019t they let the people go, and they departed?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore take and prepare yourselves a new cart and two milk cows on which there has come no yoke; and tie the cows to the cart, and bring their calves home from them;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and take the LORD\u2019s ark and lay it on the cart. Put the jewels of gold, which you return him for a trespass offering, in a box by its side; and send it away, that it may go."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Behold, if it goes up by the way of its own border to Beth Shemesh, then he has done us this great evil; but if not, then we shall know that it is not his hand that struck us. It was a chance that happened to us.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The men did so, and took two milk cows and tied them to the cart, and shut up their calves at home."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They put the LORD\u2019s ark on the cart, and the box with the golden mice and the images of their tumors."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The cows took the straight way by the way to Beth Shemesh. They went along the highway, lowing as they went, and didn\u2019t turn away to the right hand or to the left; and the lords of the Philistines went after them to the border of Beth Shemesh."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The people of Beth Shemesh were reaping their wheat harvest in the valley; and they lifted up their eyes and saw the ark, and rejoiced to see it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The cart came into the field of Joshua of Beth Shemesh, and stood there, where there was a great stone. Then they split the wood of the cart and offered up the cows for a burnt offering to the LORD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The Levites took down the LORD\u2019s ark and the box that was with it, in which the jewels of gold were, and put them on the great stone; and the men of Beth Shemesh offered burnt offerings and sacrificed sacrifices the same day to the LORD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When the five lords of the Philistines had seen it, they returned to Ekron the same day."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"These are the golden tumors which the Philistines returned for a trespass offering to the LORD: for Ashdod one, for Gaza one, for Ashkelon one, for Gath one, for Ekron one;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and the golden mice, according to the number of all the cities of the Philistines belonging to the five lords, both of fortified cities and of country villages, even to the great stone on which they set down the LORD\u2019s ark. That stone remains to this day in the field of Joshua of Beth Shemesh."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He struck of the men of Beth Shemesh, because they had looked into the LORD\u2019s ark, he struck fifty thousand seventy of the men. Then the people mourned, because the LORD had struck the people with a great slaughter."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The men of Beth Shemesh said, \u201cWho is able to stand before the LORD, this holy God? To whom shall he go up from us?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"They sent messengers to the inhabitants of Kiriath Jearim, saying, \u201cThe Philistines have brought back the LORD\u2019s ark. Come down and bring it up to yourselves.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of Kiriath Jearim came and took the LORD\u2019s ark, and brought it into Abinadab\u2019s house on the hill, and consecrated Eleazar his son to keep the LORD\u2019s ark."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"From the day that the ark stayed in Kiriath Jearim, the time was long\u2014for it was twenty years; and all the house of Israel lamented after the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Samuel spoke to all the house of Israel, saying, \u201cIf you are returning to the LORD with all your heart, then put away the foreign gods and the Ashtaroth from among you, and direct your hearts to the LORD, and serve him only; and he will deliver you out of the hand of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then the children of Israel removed the Baals and the Ashtaroth, and served the LORD only."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cGather all Israel to Mizpah, and I will pray to the LORD for you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They gathered together to Mizpah, and drew water, and poured it out before the LORD, and fasted on that day, and said there, \u201cWe have sinned against the LORD.\u201d Samuel judged the children of Israel in Mizpah."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Philistines heard that the children of Israel were gathered together at Mizpah, the lords of the Philistines went up against Israel. When the children of Israel heard it, they were afraid of the Philistines."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of Israel said to Samuel, \u201cDon\u2019t stop crying to the LORD our God for us, that he will save us out of the hand of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Samuel took a suckling lamb, and offered it for a whole burnt offering to the LORD. Samuel cried to the LORD for Israel, and the LORD answered him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As Samuel was offering up the burnt offering, the Philistines came near to battle against Israel; but the LORD thundered with a great thunder on that day on the Philistines and confused them; and they were struck down before Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The men of Israel went out of Mizpah and pursued the Philistines, and struck them until they came under Beth Kar."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samuel took a stone and set it between Mizpah and Shen, and called its name Ebenezer, saying, \u201cThe LORD helped us until now.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cEbenezer\u201d means \u201cstone of help\u201d."]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So the Philistines were subdued, and they stopped coming within the border of Israel. The LORD\u2019s hand was against the Philistines all the days of Samuel."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The cities which the Philistines had taken from Israel were restored to Israel, from Ekron even to Gath; and Israel recovered its border out of the hand of the Philistines. There was peace between Israel and the Amorites."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel judged Israel all the days of his life."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He went from year to year in a circuit to Bethel, Gilgal, and Mizpah; and he judged Israel in all those places."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"His return was to Ramah, for his house was there, and he judged Israel there; and he built an altar to the LORD there."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Samuel was old, he made his sons judges over Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now the name of his firstborn was Joel, and the name of his second, Abijah. They were judges in Beersheba."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His sons didn\u2019t walk in his ways, but turned away after dishonest gain, took bribes, and perverted justice."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the elders of Israel gathered themselves together and came to Samuel to Ramah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cBehold, you are old, and your sons don\u2019t walk in your ways. Now make us a king to judge us like all the nations.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But the thing displeased Samuel when they said, \u201cGive us a king to judge us.\u201d"],[0,"Samuel prayed to the LORD."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Samuel, \u201cListen to the voice of the people in all that they tell you; for they have not rejected you, but they have rejected me as the king over them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"According to all the works which they have done since the day that I brought them up out of Egypt even to this day, in that they have forsaken me and served other gods, so they also do to you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now therefore, listen to their voice. However, you shall protest solemnly to them, and shall show them the way of the king who will reign over them.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel told all the LORD\u2019s words to the people who asked him for a king."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThis will be the way of the king who shall reign over you: he will take your sons and appoint them as his servants, for his chariots and to be his horsemen; and they will run before his chariots."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He will appoint them to him for captains of thousands and captains of fifties; and he will assign some to plow his ground and to reap his harvest; and to make his instruments of war and the instruments of his chariots."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He will take your daughters to be perfumers, to be cooks, and to be bakers."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He will take your fields, your vineyards, and your olive groves, even your best, and give them to his servants."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He will take one tenth of your seed and of your vineyards, and give it to his officers and to his servants."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He will take your male servants, your female servants, your best young men, and your donkeys, and assign them to his own work."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He will take one tenth of your flocks; and you will be his servants."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You will cry out in that day because of your king whom you will have chosen for yourselves; and the LORD will not answer you in that day.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But the people refused to listen to the voice of Samuel; and they said, \u201cNo, but we will have a king over us,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"that we also may be like all the nations; and that our king may judge us, and go out before us, and fight our battles.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel heard all the words of the people, and he rehearsed them in the ears of the LORD."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Samuel, \u201cListen to their voice, and make them a king.\u201d"],[0,"Samuel said to the men of Israel, \u201cEveryone go to your own city.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was a man of Benjamin, whose name was Kish the son of Abiel, the son of Zeror, the son of Becorath, the son of Aphiah, the son of a Benjamite, a mighty man of valor."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He had a son whose name was Saul, an impressive young man; and there was not among the children of Israel a more handsome person than he. From his shoulders and upward he was taller than any of the people."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The donkeys of Kish, Saul\u2019s father, were lost. Kish said to Saul his son, \u201cNow take one of the servants with you, and arise, go look for the donkeys.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He passed through the hill country of Ephraim, and passed through the land of Shalishah, but they didn\u2019t find them. Then they passed through the land of Shaalim, and they weren\u2019t there. Then he passed through the land of the Benjamites, but they didn\u2019t find them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had come to the land of Zuph, Saul said to his servant who was with him, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s return, lest my father stop caring about the donkeys and be anxious for us.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The servant said to him, \u201cBehold now, there is a man of God in this city, and he is a man who is held in honor. All that he says surely happens. Now let\u2019s go there. Perhaps he can tell us which way to go.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to his servant, \u201cBut behold, if we go, what should we bring the man? For the bread is spent in our sacks, and there is not a present to bring to the man of God. What do we have?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The servant answered Saul again and said, \u201cBehold, I have in my hand the fourth part of a shekel of silver. I will give that to the man of God, to tell us our way.\u201d"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 1/4 shekel would be a small coin of about 2.5 grams."]},{v:9,l:[[0,"(In earlier times in Israel, when a man went to inquire of God, he said, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s go to the seer;\u201d for he who is now called a prophet was before called a seer.)"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to his servant, \u201cWell said. Come! Let\u2019s go.\u201d So they went to the city where the man of God was."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"As they went up the ascent to the city, they found young maidens going out to draw water, and said to them, \u201cIs the seer here?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered them and said, \u201cHe is. Behold, he is before you. Hurry now, for he has come today into the city; for the people have a sacrifice today in the high place."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"As soon as you have come into the city, you will immediately find him before he goes up to the high place to eat; for the people will not eat until he comes, because he blesses the sacrifice. Afterwards those who are invited eat. Now therefore go up; for at this time you will find him.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"They went up to the city. As they came within the city, behold, Samuel came out toward them to go up to the high place."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the LORD had revealed to Samuel a day before Saul came, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cTomorrow about this time I will send you a man out of the land of Benjamin, and you shall anoint him to be prince over my people Israel. He will save my people out of the hand of the Philistines; for I have looked upon my people, because their cry has come to me.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When Samuel saw Saul, the LORD said to him, \u201cBehold, the man of whom I spoke to you! He will have authority over my people.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul approached Samuel in the gateway, and said, \u201cPlease tell me where the seer\u2019s house is.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel answered Saul and said, \u201cI am the seer. Go up before me to the high place, for you are to eat with me today. In the morning I will let you go and will tell you all that is in your heart."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As for your donkeys who were lost three days ago, don\u2019t set your mind on them, for they have been found. For whom does all Israel desire? Is it not you and all your father\u2019s house?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul answered, \u201cAm I not a Benjamite, of the smallest of the tribes of Israel? And my family the least of all the families of the tribe of Benjamin? Why then do you speak to me like this?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel took Saul and his servant and brought them into the guest room, and made them sit in the best place among those who were invited, who were about thirty persons."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Samuel said to the cook, \u201cBring the portion which I gave you, of which I said to you, \u2018Set it aside.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The cook took up the thigh, and that which was on it, and set it before Saul. Samuel said, \u201cBehold, that which has been reserved! Set it before yourself and eat; because it has been kept for you for the appointed time, for I said, \u2018I have invited the people.\u2019\u201d So Saul ate with Samuel that day."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had come down from the high place into the city, he talked with Saul on the housetop."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They arose early; and about daybreak, Samuel called to Saul on the housetop, saying, \u201cGet up, that I may send you away.\u201d Saul arose, and they both went outside, he and Samuel, together."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"As they were going down at the end of the city, Samuel said to Saul, \u201cTell the servant to go on ahead of us.\u201d He went ahead, then Samuel said, \u201cBut stand still first, that I may cause you to hear God\u2019s message.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samuel took the vial of oil and poured it on his head, then kissed him and said, \u201cHasn\u2019t the LORD anointed you to be prince over his inheritance?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When you have departed from me today, then you will find two men by Rachel\u2019s tomb, on the border of Benjamin at Zelzah. They will tell you, \u2018The donkeys which you went to look for have been found; and behold, your father has stopped caring about the donkeys and is anxious for you, saying, \u201cWhat shall I do for my son?\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen you will go on forward from there, and you will come to the oak of Tabor. Three men will meet you there going up to God to Bethel: one carrying three young goats, and another carrying three loaves of bread, and another carrying a container of wine."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They will greet you and give you two loaves of bread, which you shall receive from their hand."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAfter that you will come to the hill of God, where the garrison of the Philistines is; and it will happen, when you have come there to the city, that you will meet a band of prophets coming down from the high place with a lute, a tambourine, a pipe, and a harp before them; and they will be prophesying."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s Spirit will come mightily on you, then you will prophesy with them and will be turned into another man."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Let it be, when these signs have come to you, that you do what is appropriate for the occasion; for God is with you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cGo down ahead of me to Gilgal; and behold, I will come down to you to offer burnt offerings and to sacrifice sacrifices of peace offerings. Wait seven days, until I come to you and show you what you are to do.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It was so, that when he had turned his back to go from Samuel, God gave him another heart; and all those signs happened that day."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When they came there to the hill, behold, a band of prophets met him; and the Spirit of God came mightily on him, and he prophesied among them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When all who knew him before saw that, behold, he prophesied with the prophets, then the people said to one another, \u201cWhat is this that has come to the son of Kish? Is Saul also among the prophets?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"One from the same place answered, \u201cWho is their father?\u201d Therefore it became a proverb, \u201cIs Saul also among the prophets?\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When he had finished prophesying, he came to the high place."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul\u2019s uncle said to him and to his servant, \u201cWhere did you go?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cTo seek the donkeys. When we saw that they were not found, we came to Samuel.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul\u2019s uncle said, \u201cPlease tell me what Samuel said to you.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to his uncle, \u201cHe told us plainly that the donkeys were found.\u201d But concerning the matter of the kingdom, of which Samuel spoke, he didn\u2019t tell him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel called the people together to the LORD to Mizpah;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and he said to the children of Israel, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says \u2018I brought Israel up out of Egypt and I delivered you out of the hand of the Egyptians, and out of the hand of all the kingdoms that oppressed you.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But you have today rejected your God, who himself saves you out of all your calamities and your distresses; and you have said to him, \u2018No! Set a king over us!\u2019 Now therefore present yourselves before the LORD by your tribes and by your thousands.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"So Samuel brought all the tribes of Israel near, and the tribe of Benjamin was chosen."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He brought the tribe of Benjamin near by their families and the family of the Matrites was chosen. Then Saul the son of Kish was chosen; but when they looked for him, he could not be found."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Therefore they asked of the LORD further, \u201cIs there yet a man to come here?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD answered, \u201cBehold, he has hidden himself among the baggage.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"They ran and got him there. When he stood among the people, he was higher than any of the people from his shoulders and upward."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Samuel said to all the people, \u201cDo you see him whom the LORD has chosen, that there is no one like him among all the people?\u201d"],[0,"All the people shouted and said, \u201cLong live the king!\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samuel told the people the regulations of the kingdom, and wrote it in a book and laid it up before the LORD. Samuel sent all the people away, every man to his house."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Saul also went to his house in Gibeah; and the army went with him, whose hearts God had touched."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But certain worthless fellows said, \u201cHow could this man save us?\u201d They despised him, and brought him no tribute. But he held his peace."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Nahash the Ammonite came up and encamped against Jabesh Gilead; and all the men of Jabesh said to Nahash, \u201cMake a covenant with us, and we will serve you.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Nahash the Ammonite said to them, \u201cOn this condition I will make it with you, that all your right eyes be gouged out. I will make this dishonor all Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The elders of Jabesh said to him, \u201cGive us seven days, that we may send messengers to all the borders of Israel; and then, if there is no one to save us, we will come out to you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then the messengers came to Gibeah of Saul, and spoke these words in the ears of the people, then all the people lifted up their voice and wept."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, Saul came following the oxen out of the field; and Saul said, \u201cWhat ails the people that they weep?\u201d They told him the words of the men of Jabesh."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"God\u2019s Spirit came mightily on Saul when he heard those words, and his anger burned hot."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He took a yoke of oxen and cut them in pieces, then sent them throughout all the borders of Israel by the hand of messengers, saying, \u201cWhoever doesn\u2019t come out after Saul and after Samuel, so shall it be done to his oxen.\u201d The dread of the LORD fell on the people, and they came out as one man."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He counted them in Bezek; and the children of Israel were three hundred thousand, and the men of Judah thirty thousand."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They said to the messengers who came, \u201cTell the men of Jabesh Gilead, \u2018Tomorrow, by the time the sun is hot, you will be rescued.\u2019\u201d The messengers came and told the men of Jabesh; and they were glad."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore the men of Jabesh said, \u201cTomorrow we will come out to you, and you shall do with us all that seems good to you.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"On the next day, Saul put the people in three companies; and they came into the middle of the camp in the morning watch, and struck the Ammonites until the heat of the day. Those who remained were scattered, so that no two of them were left together."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The people said to Samuel, \u201cWho is he who said, \u2018Shall Saul reign over us?\u2019 Bring those men, that we may put them to death!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cNo man shall be put to death today; for today the LORD has rescued Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samuel said to the people, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s go to Gilgal, and renew the kingdom there.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"All the people went to Gilgal; and there they made Saul king before the LORD in Gilgal. There they offered sacrifices of peace offerings before the LORD; and there Saul and all the men of Israel rejoiced greatly."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said to all Israel, \u201cBehold, I have listened to your voice in all that you said to me, and have made a king over you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now, behold, the king walks before you. I am old and gray-headed. Behold, my sons are with you. I have walked before you from my youth to this day."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Here I am. Witness against me before the LORD and before his anointed. Whose ox have I taken? Whose donkey have I taken? Whom have I defrauded? Whom have I oppressed? Of whose hand have I taken a bribe to make me blind my eyes? I will restore it to you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cYou have not defrauded us, nor oppressed us, neither have you taken anything from anyone\u2019s hand.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThe LORD is witness against you, and his anointed is witness today, that you have not found anything in my hand.\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cHe is witness.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Samuel said to the people, \u201cIt is the LORD who appointed Moses and Aaron, and that brought your fathers up out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now therefore stand still, that I may plead with you before the LORD concerning all the righteous acts of the LORD, which he did to you and to your fathers."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen Jacob had come into Egypt, and your fathers cried to the LORD, then the LORD sent Moses and Aaron, who brought your fathers out of Egypt, and made them to dwell in this place."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But they forgot the LORD their God; and he sold them into the hand of Sisera, captain of the army of Hazor, and into the hand of the Philistines, and into the hand of the king of Moab; and they fought against them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They cried to the LORD, and said, \u2018We have sinned, because we have forsaken the LORD and have served the Baals and the Ashtaroth; but now deliver us out of the hand of our enemies, and we will serve you.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD sent Jerubbaal, Bedan, Jephthah, and Samuel, and delivered you out of the hand of your enemies on every side; and you lived in safety."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen you saw that Nahash the king of the children of Ammon came against you, you said to me, \u2018No, but a king shall reign over us,\u2019 when the LORD your God was your king."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now therefore see the king whom you have chosen and whom you have asked for. Behold, the LORD has set a king over you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If you will fear the LORD, and serve him, and listen to his voice, and not rebel against the commandment of the LORD, then both you and also the king who reigns over you are followers of the LORD your God."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But if you will not listen to the LORD\u2019s voice, but rebel against the commandment of the LORD, then the LORD\u2019s hand will be against you, as it was against your fathers."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore stand still and see this great thing, which the LORD will do before your eyes."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t it wheat harvest today? I will call to the LORD, that he may send thunder and rain; and you will know and see that your wickedness is great, which you have done in the LORD\u2019s sight, in asking for a king.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"So Samuel called to the LORD, and the LORD sent thunder and rain that day. Then all the people greatly feared the LORD and Samuel."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people said to Samuel, \u201cPray for your servants to the LORD your God, that we not die; for we have added to all our sins this evil, to ask for a king.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said to the people, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid. You have indeed done all this evil; yet don\u2019t turn away from following the LORD, but serve the LORD with all your heart."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t turn away to go after vain things which can\u2019t profit or deliver, for they are vain."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For the LORD will not forsake his people for his great name\u2019s sake, because it has pleased the LORD to make you a people for himself."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Moreover, as for me, far be it from me that I should sin against the LORD in ceasing to pray for you; but I will instruct you in the good and the right way."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Only fear the LORD, and serve him in truth with all your heart; for consider what great things he has done for you."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But if you keep doing evil, you will be consumed, both you and your king.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul was thirty years old when he became king, and he reigned over Israel forty-two years."]],f:["The traditional Hebrew text omits \u201cthirty\u201d and \u201cforty-\u201d. The blanks are filled in here from a few manuscripts of the Septuagint."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul chose for himself three thousand men of Israel, of which two thousand were with Saul in Michmash and in the Mount of Bethel, and one thousand were with Jonathan in Gibeah of Benjamin. He sent the rest of the people to their own tents."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jonathan struck the garrison of the Philistines that was in Geba, and the Philistines heard of it. Saul blew the trumpet throughout all the land, saying, \u201cLet the Hebrews hear!\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"All Israel heard that Saul had struck the garrison of the Philistines, and also that Israel was considered an abomination to the Philistines. The people were gathered together after Saul to Gilgal."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The Philistines assembled themselves together to fight with Israel: thirty thousand chariots, six thousand horsemen, and people as the sand which is on the seashore in multitude. They came up and encamped in Michmash, eastward of Beth Aven."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When the men of Israel saw that they were in trouble (for the people were distressed), then the people hid themselves in caves, in thickets, in rocks, in tombs, and in pits."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now some of the Hebrews had gone over the Jordan to the land of Gad and Gilead; but as for Saul, he was yet in Gilgal, and all the people followed him trembling."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He stayed seven days, according to the time set by Samuel; but Samuel didn\u2019t come to Gilgal, and the people were scattering from him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cBring the burnt offering to me here, and the peace offerings.\u201d He offered the burnt offering."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass that as soon as he had finished offering the burnt offering, behold, Samuel came; and Saul went out to meet him, that he might greet him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cWhat have you done?\u201d"],[0,"Saul said, \u201cBecause I saw that the people were scattered from me, and that you didn\u2019t come within the days appointed, and that the Philistines assembled themselves together at Michmash,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"therefore I said, \u2018Now the Philistines will come down on me to Gilgal, and I haven\u2019t entreated the favor of the LORD.\u2019 I forced myself therefore, and offered the burnt offering.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said to Saul, \u201cYou have done foolishly. You have not kept the commandment of the LORD your God, which he commanded you; for now the LORD would have established your kingdom on Israel forever."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But now your kingdom will not continue. The LORD has sought for himself a man after his own heart, and the LORD has appointed him to be prince over his people, because you have not kept that which the LORD commanded you.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel arose, and went from Gilgal to Gibeah of Benjamin. Saul counted the people who were present with him, about six hundred men."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Saul, and Jonathan his son, and the people who were present with them, stayed in Geba of Benjamin; but the Philistines encamped in Michmash."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The raiders came out of the camp of the Philistines in three companies: one company turned to the way that leads to Ophrah, to the land of Shual;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"another company turned the way to Beth Horon; and another company turned the way of the border that looks down on the valley of Zeboim toward the wilderness."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now there was no blacksmith found throughout all the land of Israel, for the Philistines said, \u201cLest the Hebrews make themselves swords or spears\u201d;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but all the Israelites went down to the Philistines, each man to sharpen his own plowshare, mattock, ax, and sickle."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The price was one payim each to sharpen mattocks, plowshares, pitchforks, axes, and goads."]],f:["A payim (or pim) was 2/3 shekel of silver, or 0.26 ounces, or 7.6 grams"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"So it came to pass in the day of battle that neither sword nor spear was found in the hand of any of the people who were with Saul and Jonathan; but Saul and Jonathan his son had them."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The garrison of the Philistines went out to the pass of Michmash."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now it happened on a day that Jonathan the son of Saul said to the young man who bore his armor, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s go over to the Philistines\u2019 garrison that is on the other side.\u201d But he didn\u2019t tell his father."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Saul stayed in the uttermost part of Gibeah under the pomegranate tree which is in Migron; and the people who were with him were about six hundred men,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"including Ahijah the son of Ahitub, Ichabod\u2019s brother, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eli the priest of the LORD in Shiloh, wearing an ephod. The people didn\u2019t know that Jonathan was gone."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Between the passes, by which Jonathan sought to go over to the Philistines\u2019 garrison, there was a rocky crag on the one side and a rocky crag on the other side; and the name of the one was Bozez, and the name of the other Seneh."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The one crag rose up on the north in front of Michmash, and the other on the south in front of Geba."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Jonathan said to the young man who bore his armor, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s go over to the garrison of these uncircumcised. It may be that the LORD will work for us, for there is no restraint on the LORD to save by many or by few.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"His armor bearer said to him, \u201cDo all that is in your heart. Go, and behold, I am with you according to your heart.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jonathan said, \u201cBehold, we will pass over to the men, and we will reveal ourselves to them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If they say this to us, \u2018Wait until we come to you!\u2019 then we will stand still in our place and will not go up to them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But if they say this, \u2018Come up to us!\u2019 then we will go up, for the LORD has delivered them into our hand. This shall be the sign to us.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Both of them revealed themselves to the garrison of the Philistines; and the Philistines said, \u201cBehold, the Hebrews are coming out of the holes where they had hidden themselves!\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The men of the garrison answered Jonathan and his armor bearer, and said, \u201cCome up to us, and we will show you something!\u201d"],[0,"Jonathan said to his armor bearer, \u201cCome up after me, for the LORD has delivered them into the hand of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Jonathan climbed up on his hands and on his feet, and his armor bearer after him, and they fell before Jonathan; and his armor bearer killed them after him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"That first slaughter, which Jonathan and his armor bearer made, was about twenty men, within as it were half a furrow\u2019s length in an acre of land."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a trembling in the camp, in the field, and among all the people; the garrison and the raiders also trembled; and the earth quaked, so there was an exceedingly great trembling."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The watchmen of Saul in Gibeah of Benjamin looked; and behold, the multitude melted away and scattered."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to the people who were with him, \u201cCount now, and see who is missing from us.\u201d When they had counted, behold, Jonathan and his armor bearer were not there."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to Ahijah, \u201cBring God\u2019s ark here.\u201d For God\u2019s ark was with the children of Israel at that time."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"While Saul talked to the priest, the tumult that was in the camp of the Philistines went on and increased; and Saul said to the priest, \u201cWithdraw your hand!\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul and all the people who were with him were gathered together, and came to the battle; and behold, they were all striking each other with their swords in very great confusion."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Now the Hebrews who were with the Philistines before and who went up with them into the camp from all around, even they also turned to be with the Israelites who were with Saul and Jonathan."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Likewise all the men of Israel who had hidden themselves in the hill country of Ephraim, when they heard that the Philistines fled, even they also followed hard after them in the battle."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So the LORD saved Israel that day; and the battle passed over by Beth Aven."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of Israel were distressed that day; for Saul had adjured the people, saying, \u201cCursed is the man who eats any food until it is evening, and I am avenged of my enemies.\u201d So none of the people tasted food."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people came into the forest; and there was honey on the ground."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When the people had come to the forest, behold, honey was dripping, but no one put his hand to his mouth, for the people feared the oath."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But Jonathan didn\u2019t hear when his father commanded the people with the oath. Therefore he put out the end of the rod that was in his hand and dipped it in the honeycomb, and put his hand to his mouth; and his eyes brightened."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Then one of the people answered, and said, \u201cYour father directly commanded the people with an oath, saying, \u2018Cursed is the man who eats food today.\u2019\u201d So the people were faint."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jonathan said, \u201cMy father has troubled the land. Please look how my eyes have brightened because I tasted a little of this honey."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"How much more, if perhaps the people had eaten freely today of the plunder of their enemies which they found? For now there has been no great slaughter among the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They struck the Philistines that day from Michmash to Aijalon. The people were very faint;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and the people pounced on the plunder, and took sheep, cattle, and calves, and killed them on the ground; and the people ate them with the blood."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Then they told Saul, saying, \u201cBehold, the people are sinning against the LORD, in that they eat meat with the blood.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cYou have dealt treacherously. Roll a large stone to me today!\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cDisperse yourselves among the people, and tell them, \u2018Every man bring me here his ox, and every man his sheep, and kill them here, and eat; and don\u2019t sin against the LORD in eating meat with the blood.\u2019\u201d All the people brought every man his ox with him that night, and killed them there."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul built an altar to the LORD. This was the first altar that he built to the LORD."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cLet\u2019s go down after the Philistines by night, and take plunder among them until the morning light. Let\u2019s not leave a man of them.\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cDo whatever seems good to you.\u201d"],[0,"Then the priest said, \u201cLet\u2019s draw near here to God.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul asked counsel of God: \u201cShall I go down after the Philistines? Will you deliver them into the hand of Israel?\u201d But he didn\u2019t answer him that day."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cDraw near here, all you chiefs of the people, and know and see in whom this sin has been today."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"For as the LORD lives, who saves Israel, though it is in Jonathan my son, he shall surely die.\u201d But there was not a man among all the people who answered him."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Then he said to all Israel, \u201cYou be on one side, and I and Jonathan my son will be on the other side.\u201d"],[0,"The people said to Saul, \u201cDo what seems good to you.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Saul said to the LORD, the God of Israel, \u201cShow the right.\u201d"],[0,"Jonathan and Saul were chosen, but the people escaped."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cCast lots between me and Jonathan my son.\u201d"],[0,"Jonathan was selected."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to Jonathan, \u201cTell me what you have done!\u201d"],[0,"Jonathan told him, and said, \u201cI certainly did taste a little honey with the end of the rod that was in my hand; and behold, I must die.\u201d"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cGod do so and more also; for you shall surely die, Jonathan.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"The people said to Saul, \u201cShall Jonathan die, who has worked this great salvation in Israel? Far from it! As the LORD lives, there shall not one hair of his head fall to the ground, for he has worked with God today!\u201d So the people rescued Jonathan, so he didn\u2019t die."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Then Saul went up from following the Philistines; and the Philistines went to their own place."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Saul had taken the kingdom over Israel, he fought against all his enemies on every side: against Moab, and against the children of Ammon, and against Edom, and against the kings of Zobah, and against the Philistines. Wherever he turned himself, he defeated them."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He did valiantly and struck the Amalekites, and delivered Israel out of the hands of those who plundered them."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Now the sons of Saul were Jonathan, Ishvi, and Malchishua; and the names of his two daughters were these: the name of the firstborn Merab, and the name of the younger Michal."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"The name of Saul\u2019s wife was Ahinoam the daughter of Ahimaaz. The name of the captain of his army was Abner the son of Ner, Saul\u2019s uncle."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Kish was the father of Saul, and Ner the father of Abner was the son of Abiel."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"There was severe war against the Philistines all the days of Saul; and when Saul saw any mighty man or any valiant man, he took him into his service."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said to Saul, \u201cThe LORD sent me to anoint you to be king over his people, over Israel. Now therefore listen to the voice of the LORD\u2019s words."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says, \u2018I remember what Amalek did to Israel, how he set himself against him on the way when he came up out of Egypt."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now go and strike Amalek, and utterly destroy all that they have, and don\u2019t spare them; but kill both man and woman, infant and nursing baby, ox and sheep, camel and donkey.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul summoned the people, and counted them in Telaim, two hundred thousand footmen and ten thousand men of Judah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Saul came to the city of Amalek, and set an ambush in the valley."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Saul said to the Kenites, \u201cGo, depart, go down from among the Amalekites, lest I destroy you with them; for you showed kindness to all the children of Israel when they came up out of Egypt.\u201d So the Kenites departed from among the Amalekites."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul struck the Amalekites, from Havilah as you go to Shur, which is before Egypt."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He took Agag the king of the Amalekites alive, and utterly destroyed all the people with the edge of the sword."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But Saul and the people spared Agag and the best of the sheep, of the cattle, of the fat calves, of the lambs, and all that was good, and were not willing to utterly destroy them; but everything that was vile and refuse, that they destroyed utterly."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Samuel, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cIt grieves me that I have set up Saul to be king, for he has turned back from following me, and has not performed my commandments.\u201d Samuel was angry; and he cried to the LORD all night."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel rose early to meet Saul in the morning; and Samuel was told, saying, \u201cSaul came to Carmel, and behold, he set up a monument for himself, turned, passed on, and went down to Gilgal.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel came to Saul; and Saul said to him, \u201cYou are blessed by the LORD! I have performed the commandment of the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cThen what does this bleating of the sheep in my ears and the lowing of the cattle which I hear mean?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cThey have brought them from the Amalekites; for the people spared the best of the sheep and of the cattle, to sacrifice to the LORD your God. We have utterly destroyed the rest.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samuel said to Saul, \u201cStay, and I will tell you what the LORD said to me last night.\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cSay on.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cThough you were little in your own sight, weren\u2019t you made the head of the tribes of Israel? The LORD anointed you king over Israel;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and the LORD sent you on a journey, and said, \u2018Go, and utterly destroy the sinners the Amalekites, and fight against them until they are consumed.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Why then didn\u2019t you obey the LORD\u2019s voice, but took the plunder, and did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to Samuel, \u201cBut I have obeyed the LORD\u2019s voice, and have gone the way which the LORD sent me, and have brought Agag the king of Amalek, and have utterly destroyed the Amalekites."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But the people took of the plunder, sheep and cattle, the best of the devoted things, to sacrifice to the LORD your God in Gilgal.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cHas the LORD as great delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices, as in obeying the LORD\u2019s voice? Behold, to obey is better than sacrifice, and to listen than the fat of rams."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For rebellion is as the sin of witchcraft, and stubbornness is as idolatry and teraphim. Because you have rejected the LORD\u2019s word, he has also rejected you from being king.\u201d"]],f:["teraphim were household idols that may have been associated with inheritance rights to the household property."]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to Samuel, \u201cI have sinned; for I have transgressed the commandment of the LORD and your words, because I feared the people and obeyed their voice."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please pardon my sin, and turn again with me, that I may worship the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said to Saul, \u201cI will not return with you; for you have rejected the LORD\u2019s word, and the LORD has rejected you from being king over Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"As Samuel turned around to go away, Saul grabbed the skirt of his robe, and it tore."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Samuel said to him, \u201cThe LORD has torn the kingdom of Israel from you today, and has given it to a neighbor of yours who is better than you."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Also the Strength of Israel will not lie nor repent; for he is not a man, that he should repent.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cI have sinned; yet please honor me now before the elders of my people and before Israel, and come back with me, that I may worship the LORD your God.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"So Samuel went back with Saul; and Saul worshiped the LORD."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Then Samuel said, \u201cBring Agag the king of the Amalekites here to me!\u201d"],[0,"Agag came to him cheerfully. Agag said, \u201cSurely the bitterness of death is past.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cAs your sword has made women childless, so your mother will be childless among women!\u201d Then Samuel cut Agag in pieces before the LORD in Gilgal."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samuel went to Ramah; and Saul went up to his house to Gibeah of Saul."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Samuel came no more to see Saul until the day of his death, but Samuel mourned for Saul. The LORD grieved that he had made Saul king over Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Samuel, \u201cHow long will you mourn for Saul, since I have rejected him from being king over Israel? Fill your horn with oil, and go. I will send you to Jesse the Bethlehemite, for I have provided a king for myself among his sons.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cHow can I go? If Saul hears it, he will kill me.\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said, \u201cTake a heifer with you, and say, \u2018I have come to sacrifice to the LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Call Jesse to the sacrifice, and I will show you what you shall do. You shall anoint to me him whom I name to you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel did that which the LORD spoke, and came to Bethlehem. The elders of the city came to meet him trembling, and said, \u201cDo you come peaceably?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cPeaceably; I have come to sacrifice to the LORD. Sanctify yourselves, and come with me to the sacrifice.\u201d He sanctified Jesse and his sons, and called them to the sacrifice."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When they had come, he looked at Eliab, and said, \u201cSurely the LORD\u2019s anointed is before him.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But the LORD said to Samuel, \u201cDon\u2019t look on his face, or on the height of his stature, because I have rejected him; for I don\u2019t see as man sees. For man looks at the outward appearance, but the LORD looks at the heart.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesse called Abinadab, and made him pass before Samuel. He said, \u201cThe LORD has not chosen this one, either.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Jesse made Shammah to pass by. He said, \u201cThe LORD has not chosen this one, either.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Jesse made seven of his sons to pass before Samuel. Samuel said to Jesse, \u201cThe LORD has not chosen these.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Samuel said to Jesse, \u201cAre all your children here?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cThere remains yet the youngest. Behold, he is keeping the sheep.\u201d"],[0,"Samuel said to Jesse, \u201cSend and get him, for we will not sit down until he comes here.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He sent, and brought him in. Now he was ruddy, with a handsome face and good appearance. The LORD said, \u201cArise! Anoint him, for this is he.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Samuel took the horn of oil and anointed him in the middle of his brothers. Then the LORD\u2019s Spirit came mightily on David from that day forward. So Samuel rose up and went to Ramah."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now the LORD\u2019s Spirit departed from Saul, and an evil spirit from the LORD troubled him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Saul\u2019s servants said to him, \u201cSee now, an evil spirit from God troubles you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Let our lord now command your servants who are in front of you to seek out a man who is a skillful player on the harp. Then when the evil spirit from God is on you, he will play with his hand, and you will be well.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to his servants, \u201cProvide me now a man who can play well, and bring him to me.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then one of the young men answered and said, \u201cBehold, I have seen a son of Jesse the Bethlehemite who is skillful in playing, a mighty man of valor, a man of war, prudent in speech, and a handsome person; and the LORD is with him.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Saul sent messengers to Jesse, and said, \u201cSend me David your son, who is with the sheep.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesse took a donkey loaded with bread, a container of wine, and a young goat, and sent them by David his son to Saul."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"David came to Saul and stood before him. He loved him greatly; and he became his armor bearer."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Saul sent to Jesse, saying, \u201cPlease let David stand before me, for he has found favor in my sight.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When the spirit from God was on Saul, David took the harp and played with his hand; so Saul was refreshed and was well, and the evil spirit departed from him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the Philistines gathered together their armies to battle; and they were gathered together at Socoh, which belongs to Judah, and encamped between Socoh and Azekah in Ephesdammim."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Saul and the men of Israel were gathered together, and encamped in the valley of Elah, and set the battle in array against the Philistines."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The Philistines stood on the mountain on the one side, and Israel stood on the mountain on the other side: and there was a valley between them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"A champion out of the camp of the Philistines named Goliath of Gath, whose height was six cubits and a span went out."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters. A span is the length from the tip of a man\u2019s thumb to the tip of his little finger when his hand is stretched out (about half a cubit, or 9 inches, or 22.8 cm.) Therefore, Goliath was about 9 feet and 9 inches or 2.97 meters tall."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He had a helmet of bronze on his head, and he wore a coat of mail; and the weight of the coat was five thousand shekels of bronze."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 5000 shekels is about 50 kilograms or 110 pounds."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He had bronze shin armor on his legs and a bronze javelin between his shoulders."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The staff of his spear was like a weaver\u2019s beam; and his spear\u2019s head weighed six hundred shekels of iron. His shield bearer went before him."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 600 shekels is about 6 kilograms or about 13 pounds."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He stood and cried to the armies of Israel, and said to them, \u201cWhy have you come out to set your battle in array? Am I not a Philistine, and you servants to Saul? Choose a man for yourselves, and let him come down to me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If he is able to fight with me and kill me, then will we be your servants; but if I prevail against him and kill him, then you will be our servants and serve us.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The Philistine said, \u201cI defy the armies of Israel today! Give me a man, that we may fight together!\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When Saul and all Israel heard those words of the Philistine, they were dismayed and greatly afraid."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now David was the son of that Ephrathite of Bethlehem Judah, whose name was Jesse; and he had eight sons. The man was an elderly old man in the days of Saul."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The three oldest sons of Jesse had gone after Saul to the battle; and the names of his three sons who went to the battle were Eliab the firstborn, and next to him Abinadab, and the third Shammah."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"David was the youngest; and the three oldest followed Saul."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now David went back and forth from Saul to feed his father\u2019s sheep at Bethlehem."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The Philistine came near morning and evening, and presented himself forty days."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesse said to David his son, \u201cNow take for your brothers an ephah of this parched grain and these ten loaves, and carry them quickly to the camp to your brothers;"]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and bring these ten cheeses to the captain of their thousand; and see how your brothers are doing, and bring back news.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now Saul, and they, and all the men of Israel were in the valley of Elah, fighting with the Philistines."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"David rose up early in the morning and left the sheep with a keeper, and took the provisions and went, as Jesse had commanded him. He came to the place of the wagons as the army which was going out to the fight shouted for the battle."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Israel and the Philistines put the battle in array, army against army."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"David left his baggage in the hand of the keeper of the baggage and ran to the army, and came and greeted his brothers."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"As he talked with them, behold, the champion, the Philistine of Gath, Goliath by name, came up out of the ranks of the Philistines, and said the same words; and David heard them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"All the men of Israel, when they saw the man, fled from him and were terrified."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The men of Israel said, \u201cHave you seen this man who has come up? He has surely come up to defy Israel. The king will give great riches to the man who kills him, and will give him his daughter, and will make his father\u2019s house tax-free in Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"David spoke to the men who stood by him, saying, \u201cWhat shall be done to the man who kills this Philistine and takes away the reproach from Israel? For who is this uncircumcised Philistine, that he should defy the armies of the living God?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"The people answered him in this way, saying, \u201cSo shall it be done to the man who kills him.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Eliab his oldest brother heard when he spoke to the men; and Eliab\u2019s anger burned against David, and he said, \u201cWhy have you come down? With whom have you left those few sheep in the wilderness? I know your pride and the evil of your heart; for you have come down that you might see the battle.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cWhat have I now done? Is there not a cause?\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He turned away from him toward another, and spoke like that again; and the people answered him again the same way."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"When the words were heard which David spoke, they rehearsed them before Saul; and he sent for him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"David said to Saul, \u201cLet no man\u2019s heart fail because of him. Your servant will go and fight with this Philistine.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to David, \u201cYou are not able to go against this Philistine to fight with him; for you are but a youth, and he a man of war from his youth.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Saul, \u201cYour servant was keeping his father\u2019s sheep; and when a lion or a bear came and took a lamb out of the flock,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"I went out after him, struck him, and rescued it out of his mouth. When he arose against me, I caught him by his beard, struck him, and killed him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Your servant struck both the lion and the bear. This uncircumcised Philistine shall be as one of them, since he has defied the armies of the living God.\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cThe LORD, who delivered me out of the paw of the lion and out of the paw of the bear, will deliver me out of the hand of this Philistine.\u201d"],[0,"Saul said to David, \u201cGo! The LORD will be with you.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul dressed David with his clothing. He put a helmet of bronze on his head, and he clad him with a coat of mail."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"David strapped his sword on his clothing and he tried to move, for he had not tested it. David said to Saul, \u201cI can\u2019t go with these, for I have not tested them.\u201d Then David took them off."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"He took his staff in his hand, and chose for himself five smooth stones out of the brook, and put them in the pouch of his shepherd\u2019s bag which he had. His sling was in his hand; and he came near to the Philistine."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The Philistine walked and came near to David; and the man who bore the shield went before him."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"When the Philistine looked around and saw David, he disdained him; for he was but a youth, and ruddy, and had a good looking face."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"The Philistine said to David, \u201cAm I a dog, that you come to me with sticks?\u201d The Philistine cursed David by his gods."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The Philistine said to David, \u201cCome to me, and I will give your flesh to the birds of the sky and to the animals of the field.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said to the Philistine, \u201cYou come to me with a sword, with a spear, and with a javelin; but I come to you in the name of the LORD of Armies, the God of the armies of Israel, whom you have defied."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Today, the LORD will deliver you into my hand. I will strike you and take your head from off you. I will give the dead bodies of the army of the Philistines today to the birds of the sky and to the wild animals of the earth, that all the earth may know that there is a God in Israel,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"and that all this assembly may know that the LORD doesn\u2019t save with sword and spear; for the battle is the LORD\u2019s, and he will give you into our hand.\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Philistine arose, and walked and came near to meet David, David hurried and ran toward the army to meet the Philistine."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"David put his hand in his bag, took a stone and slung it, and struck the Philistine in his forehead. The stone sank into his forehead, and he fell on his face to the earth."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"So David prevailed over the Philistine with a sling and with a stone, and struck the Philistine and killed him; but there was no sword in David\u2019s hand."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Then David ran, stood over the Philistine, took his sword, drew it out of its sheath, killed him, and cut off his head with it."],[0,"When the Philistines saw that their champion was dead, they fled."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"The men of Israel and of Judah arose and shouted, and pursued the Philistines as far as Gai and to the gates of Ekron. The wounded of the Philistines fell down by the way to Shaaraim, even to Gath and to Ekron."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"The children of Israel returned from chasing after the Philistines, and they plundered their camp."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"David took the head of the Philistine and brought it to Jerusalem, but he put his armor in his tent."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"When Saul saw David go out against the Philistine, he said to Abner, the captain of the army, \u201cAbner, whose son is this youth?\u201d"],[0,"Abner said, \u201cAs your soul lives, O king, I can\u2019t tell.\u201d"]]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cInquire whose son the young man is!\u201d"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"As David returned from the slaughter of the Philistine, Abner took him and brought him before Saul with the head of the Philistine in his hand."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"Saul said to him, \u201cWhose son are you, you young man?\u201d"],[0,"David answered, \u201cI am the son of your servant Jesse the Bethlehemite.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had finished speaking to Saul, the soul of Jonathan was knit with the soul of David, and Jonathan loved him as his own soul."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Saul took him that day, and wouldn\u2019t let him go home to his father\u2019s house any more."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then Jonathan and David made a covenant, because he loved him as his own soul."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Jonathan stripped himself of the robe that was on him and gave it to David with his clothing, even including his sword, his bow, and his sash."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"David went out wherever Saul sent him, and behaved himself wisely; and Saul set him over the men of war. It was good in the sight of all the people, and also in the sight of Saul\u2019s servants."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"As they came, when David returned from the slaughter of the Philistine, the women came out of all the cities of Israel, singing and dancing, to meet King Saul with tambourines, with joy, and with instruments of music."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The women sang to one another as they played, and said,"],[1,"\u201cSaul has slain his thousands,"],[2,"and David his ten thousands.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul was very angry, and this saying displeased him. He said, \u201cThey have credited David with ten thousands, and they have only credited me with thousands. What can he have more but the kingdom?\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Saul watched David from that day and forward."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"On the next day, an evil spirit from God came mightily on Saul, and he prophesied in the middle of the house. David played with his hand, as he did day by day. Saul had his spear in his hand;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and Saul threw the spear, for he said, \u201cI will pin David to the wall!\u201d David escaped from his presence twice."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Saul was afraid of David, because the LORD was with him, and had departed from Saul."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore Saul removed him from his presence, and made him his captain over a thousand; and he went out and came in before the people."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"David behaved himself wisely in all his ways; and the LORD was with him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When Saul saw that he behaved himself very wisely, he stood in awe of him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But all Israel and Judah loved David; for he went out and came in before them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Saul said to David, \u201cBehold, my elder daughter Merab. I will give her to you as wife. Only be valiant for me, and fight the LORD\u2019s battles.\u201d For Saul said, \u201cDon\u2019t let my hand be on him, but let the hand of the Philistines be on him.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Saul, \u201cWho am I, and what is my life, or my father\u2019s family in Israel, that I should be son-in-law to the king?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But at the time when Merab, Saul\u2019s daughter, should have been given to David, she was given to Adriel the Meholathite as wife."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Michal, Saul\u2019s daughter, loved David; and they told Saul, and the thing pleased him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Saul said, I will give her to him, that she may be a snare to him and that the hand of the Philistines may be against him. Therefore Saul said to David a second time, \u201cYou shall today be my son-in-law.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul commanded his servants, \u201cTalk with David secretly, and say, \u2018Behold, the king has delight in you, and all his servants love you. Now therefore be the king\u2019s son-in-law.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul\u2019s servants spoke those words in the ears of David. David said, \u201cDoes it seem to you a light thing to be the king\u2019s son-in-law, since I am a poor man and little known?\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The servants of Saul told him, saying, \u201cDavid spoke like this.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cTell David, \u2018The king desires no dowry except one hundred foreskins of the Philistines, to be avenged of the king\u2019s enemies.\u2019\u201d Now Saul thought he would make David fall by the hand of the Philistines."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When his servants told David these words, it pleased David well to be the king\u2019s son-in-law. Before the deadline,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"David arose and went, he and his men, and killed two hundred men of the Philistines. Then David brought their foreskins, and they gave them in full number to the king, that he might be the king\u2019s son-in-law. Then Saul gave him Michal his daughter as wife."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Saul saw and knew that the LORD was with David; and Michal, Saul\u2019s daughter, loved him."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Saul was even more afraid of David; and Saul was David\u2019s enemy continually."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the princes of the Philistines went out; and as often as they went out, David behaved himself more wisely than all the servants of Saul, so that his name was highly esteemed."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul spoke to Jonathan his son and to all his servants, that they should kill David. But Jonathan, Saul\u2019s son, greatly delighted in David."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jonathan told David, saying, \u201cSaul my father seeks to kill you. Now therefore, please take care of yourself in the morning, live in a secret place, and hide yourself."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will go out and stand beside my father in the field where you are, and I will talk with my father about you; and if I see anything, I will tell you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan spoke good of David to Saul his father, and said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t let the king sin against his servant, against David; because he has not sinned against you, and because his works have been very good toward you;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"for he put his life in his hand and struck the Philistine, and the LORD worked a great victory for all Israel. You saw it and rejoiced. Why then will you sin against innocent blood, to kill David without a cause?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul listened to the voice of Jonathan; and Saul swore, \u201cAs the LORD lives, he shall not be put to death.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan called David, and Jonathan showed him all those things. Then Jonathan brought David to Saul, and he was in his presence as before."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"There was war again. David went out and fought with the Philistines, and killed them with a great slaughter; and they fled before him."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"An evil spirit from the LORD was on Saul as he sat in his house with his spear in his hand; and David was playing music with his hand."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Saul sought to pin David to the wall with the spear, but he slipped away out of Saul\u2019s presence; and he stuck the spear into the wall. David fled and escaped that night."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Saul sent messengers to David\u2019s house to watch him and to kill him in the morning. Michal, David\u2019s wife, told him, saying, \u201cIf you don\u2019t save your life tonight, tomorrow you will be killed.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So Michal let David down through the window. He went away, fled, and escaped."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Michal took the teraphim and laid it in the bed, and put a pillow of goats\u2019 hair at its head and covered it with clothes."]],f:["teraphim were household idols that may have been associated with inheritance rights to the household property."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When Saul sent messengers to take David, she said, \u201cHe is sick.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul sent the messengers to see David, saying, \u201cBring him up to me in the bed, that I may kill him.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When the messengers came in, behold, the teraphim was in the bed, with the pillow of goats\u2019 hair at its head."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to Michal, \u201cWhy have you deceived me like this and let my enemy go, so that he has escaped?\u201d"],[0,"Michal answered Saul, \u201cHe said to me, \u2018Let me go! Why should I kill you?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now David fled and escaped, and came to Samuel at Ramah, and told him all that Saul had done to him. He and Samuel went and lived in Naioth."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Saul was told, saying, \u201cBehold, David is at Naioth in Ramah.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul sent messengers to seize David; and when they saw the company of the prophets prophesying, and Samuel standing as head over them, God\u2019s Spirit came on Saul\u2019s messengers, and they also prophesied."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When Saul was told, he sent other messengers, and they also prophesied. Saul sent messengers again the third time, and they also prophesied."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Then he also went to Ramah, and came to the great well that is in Secu: and he asked, \u201cWhere are Samuel and David?\u201d"],[0,"One said, \u201cBehold, they are at Naioth in Ramah.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He went there to Naioth in Ramah. Then God\u2019s Spirit came on him also, and he went on, and prophesied, until he came to Naioth in Ramah."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He also stripped off his clothes. He also prophesied before Samuel and lay down naked all that day and all that night. Therefore they say, \u201cIs Saul also among the prophets?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David fled from Naioth in Ramah, and came and said to Jonathan, \u201cWhat have I done? What is my iniquity? What is my sin before your father, that he seeks my life?\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cFar from it; you will not die. Behold, my father does nothing either great or small, but that he discloses it to me. Why would my father hide this thing from me? It is not so.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David swore moreover, and said, \u201cYour father knows well that I have found favor in your eyes; and he says, \u2018Don\u2019t let Jonathan know this, lest he be grieved;\u2019 but truly as the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, there is but a step between me and death.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jonathan said to David, \u201cWhatever your soul desires, I will even do it for you.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Jonathan, \u201cBehold, tomorrow is the new moon, and I should not fail to dine with the king; but let me go, that I may hide myself in the field to the third day at evening."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"If your father misses me at all, then say, \u2018David earnestly asked leave of me that he might run to Bethlehem, his city; for it is the yearly sacrifice there for all the family.\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If he says, \u2018It is well,\u2019 your servant shall have peace; but if he is angry, then know that evil is determined by him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore deal kindly with your servant, for you have brought your servant into a covenant of the LORD with you; but if there is iniquity in me, kill me yourself, for why should you bring me to your father?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan said, \u201cFar be it from you; for if I should at all know that evil were determined by my father to come on you, then wouldn\u2019t I tell you that?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said to Jonathan, \u201cWho will tell me if your father answers you roughly?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan said to David, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s go out into the field.\u201d They both went out into the field."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Jonathan said to David, \u201cBy the LORD, the God of Israel, when I have sounded out my father about this time tomorrow, or the third day, behold, if there is good toward David, won\u2019t I then send to you and disclose it to you?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD do so to Jonathan and more also, should it please my father to do you evil, if I don\u2019t disclose it to you and send you away, that you may go in peace. May the LORD be with you as he has been with my father."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall not only show me the loving kindness of the LORD while I still live, that I not die;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but you shall also not cut off your kindness from my house forever, no, not when the LORD has cut off every one of the enemies of David from the surface of the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So Jonathan made a covenant with David\u2019s house, saying, \u201cThe LORD will require it at the hand of David\u2019s enemies.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan caused David to swear again, for the love that he had for him; for he loved him as he loved his own soul."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then Jonathan said to him, \u201cTomorrow is the new moon, and you will be missed, because your seat will be empty."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When you have stayed three days, go down quickly and come to the place where you hid yourself when this started, and remain by the stone Ezel."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"I will shoot three arrows on its side, as though I shot at a mark."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Behold, I will send the boy, saying, \u2018Go, find the arrows!\u2019 If I tell the boy, \u2018Behold, the arrows are on this side of you. Take them;\u2019 then come, for there is peace to you and no danger, as the LORD lives."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But if I say this to the boy, \u2018Behold, the arrows are beyond you,\u2019 then go your way, for the LORD has sent you away."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Concerning the matter which you and I have spoken of, behold, the LORD is between you and me forever.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"So David hid himself in the field. When the new moon had come, the king sat himself down to eat food."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The king sat on his seat, as at other times, even on the seat by the wall; and Jonathan stood up, and Abner sat by Saul\u2019s side, but David\u2019s place was empty."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Nevertheless Saul didn\u2019t say anything that day, for he thought, \u201cSomething has happened to him. He is not clean. Surely he is not clean.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day after the new moon, the second day, David\u2019s place was empty. Saul said to Jonathan his son, \u201cWhy didn\u2019t the son of Jesse come to eat, either yesterday, or today?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan answered Saul, \u201cDavid earnestly asked permission of me to go to Bethlehem."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He said, \u2018Please let me go, for our family has a sacrifice in the city. My brother has commanded me to be there. Now, if I have found favor in your eyes, please let me go away and see my brothers.\u2019 Therefore he has not come to the king\u2019s table.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul\u2019s anger burned against Jonathan, and he said to him, \u201cYou son of a perverse rebellious woman, don\u2019t I know that you have chosen the son of Jesse to your own shame, and to the shame of your mother\u2019s nakedness?"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For as long as the son of Jesse lives on the earth, you will not be established, nor will your kingdom. Therefore now send and bring him to me, for he shall surely die!\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan answered Saul his father, and said to him, \u201cWhy should he be put to death? What has he done?\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul cast his spear at him to strike him. By this Jonathan knew that his father was determined to put David to death."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"So Jonathan arose from the table in fierce anger, and ate no food the second day of the month; for he was grieved for David, because his father had treated him shamefully."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"In the morning, Jonathan went out into the field at the time appointed with David, and a little boy with him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He said to his boy, \u201cRun, find now the arrows which I shoot.\u201d As the boy ran, he shot an arrow beyond him."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"When the boy had come to the place of the arrow which Jonathan had shot, Jonathan cried after the boy, and said, \u201cIsn\u2019t the arrow beyond you?\u201d"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Jonathan cried after the boy, \u201cGo fast! Hurry! Don\u2019t delay!\u201d Jonathan\u2019s boy gathered up the arrows, and came to his master."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But the boy didn\u2019t know anything. Only Jonathan and David knew the matter."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Jonathan gave his weapons to his boy, and said to him, \u201cGo, carry them to the city.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"As soon as the boy was gone, David arose out of the south, and fell on his face to the ground, and bowed himself three times. They kissed one another and wept with one another, and David wept the most."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Jonathan said to David, \u201cGo in peace, because we have both sworn in the LORD\u2019s name, saying, \u2018The LORD is between me and you, and between my offspring and your offspring, forever.\u2019\u201d He arose and departed; and Jonathan went into the city."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David came to Nob to Ahimelech the priest. Ahimelech came to meet David trembling, and said to him, \u201cWhy are you alone, and no man with you?\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David said to Ahimelech the priest, \u201cThe king has commanded me to do something, and has said to me, \u2018Let no one know anything about the business about which I send you, and what I have commanded you. I have sent the young men to a certain place.\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now therefore what is under your hand? Please give me five loaves of bread in my hand, or whatever is available.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The priest answered David, and said, \u201cI have no common bread, but there is holy bread; if only the young men have kept themselves from women.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"David answered the priest, and said to him, \u201cTruly, women have been kept from us as usual these three days. When I came out, the vessels of the young men were holy, though it was only a common journey. How much more then today shall their vessels be holy?\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So the priest gave him holy bread; for there was no bread there but the show bread that was taken from before the LORD, to be replaced with hot bread in the day when it was taken away."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now a certain man of the servants of Saul was there that day, detained before the LORD; and his name was Doeg the Edomite, the best of the herdsmen who belonged to Saul."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Ahimelech, \u201cIsn\u2019t there here under your hand spear or sword? For I haven\u2019t brought my sword or my weapons with me, because the king\u2019s business required haste.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The priest said, \u201cBehold, the sword of Goliath the Philistine, whom you killed in the valley of Elah, is here wrapped in a cloth behind the ephod. If you would like to take that, take it, for there is no other except that here.\u201d"],[0,"David said, \u201cThere is none like that. Give it to me.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"David arose and fled that day for fear of Saul, and went to Achish the king of Gath."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The servants of Achish said to him, \u201cIsn\u2019t this David the king of the land? Didn\u2019t they sing to one another about him in dances, saying,"],[1,"\u2018Saul has slain his thousands,"],[2,"and David his ten thousands\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"David laid up these words in his heart, and was very afraid of Achish the king of Gath."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He changed his behavior before them and pretended to be insane in their hands, and scribbled on the doors of the gate, and let his spittle fall down on his beard."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Then Achish said to his servants, \u201cLook, you see the man is insane. Why then have you brought him to me?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Do I lack madmen, that you have brought this fellow to play the madman in my presence? Should this fellow come into my house?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David therefore departed from there and escaped to Adullam\u2019s cave. When his brothers and all his father\u2019s house heard it, they went down there to him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Everyone who was in distress, everyone who was in debt, and everyone who was discontented gathered themselves to him; and he became captain over them. There were with him about four hundred men."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"David went from there to Mizpeh of Moab; and he said to the king of Moab, \u201cPlease let my father and my mother come out to you, until I know what God will do for me.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He brought them before the king of Moab; and they lived with him all the time that David was in the stronghold."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The prophet Gad said to David, \u201cDon\u2019t stay in the stronghold. Depart, and go into the land of Judah.\u201d"],[0,"Then David departed, and came into the forest of Hereth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul heard that David was discovered, with the men who were with him. Now Saul was sitting in Gibeah, under the tamarisk tree in Ramah, with his spear in his hand, and all his servants were standing around him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Saul said to his servants who stood around him, \u201cHear now, you Benjamites! Will the son of Jesse give everyone of you fields and vineyards? Will he make you all captains of thousands and captains of hundreds?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Is that why all of you have conspired against me, and there is no one who discloses to me when my son makes a treaty with the son of Jesse, and there is none of you who is sorry for me, or discloses to me that my son has stirred up my servant against me, to lie in wait, as it is today?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Doeg the Edomite, who stood by the servants of Saul, answered and said, \u201cI saw the son of Jesse coming to Nob, to Ahimelech the son of Ahitub."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He inquired of the LORD for him, gave him food, and gave him the sword of Goliath the Philistine.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king sent to call Ahimelech the priest, the son of Ahitub, and all his father\u2019s house, the priests who were in Nob; and they all came to the king."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cHear now, you son of Ahitub.\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cHere I am, my lord.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said to him, \u201cWhy have you conspired against me, you and the son of Jesse, in that you have given him bread, and a sword, and have inquired of God for him, that he should rise against me, to lie in wait, as it is today?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Ahimelech answered the king, and said, \u201cWho among all your servants is so faithful as David, who is the king\u2019s son-in-law, captain of your body guard, and honored in your house?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Have I today begun to inquire of God for him? Be it far from me! Don\u2019t let the king impute anything to his servant, nor to all the house of my father; for your servant knew nothing of all this, less or more.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cYou shall surely die, Ahimelech, you and all your father\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The king said to the guard who stood about him, \u201cTurn and kill the priests of the LORD, because their hand also is with David, and because they knew that he fled and didn\u2019t disclose it to me.\u201d But the servants of the king wouldn\u2019t put out their hand to fall on the priests of the LORD."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to Doeg, \u201cTurn and attack the priests!\u201d"],[0,"Doeg the Edomite turned, and he attacked the priests, and he killed on that day eighty-five people who wore a linen ephod."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He struck Nob, the city of the priests, with the edge of the sword\u2014both men and women, children and nursing babies, and cattle, donkeys, and sheep, with the edge of the sword."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"One of the sons of Ahimelech the son of Ahitub, named Abiathar, escaped and fled after David."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Abiathar told David that Saul had slain the LORD\u2019s priests."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Abiathar, \u201cI knew on that day, when Doeg the Edomite was there, that he would surely tell Saul. I am responsible for the death of all the persons of your father\u2019s house."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Stay with me. Don\u2019t be afraid, for he who seeks my life seeks your life. You will be safe with me.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David was told, \u201cBehold, the Philistines are fighting against Keilah, and are robbing the threshing floors.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore David inquired of the LORD, saying, \u201cShall I go and strike these Philistines?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said to David, \u201cGo strike the Philistines, and save Keilah.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David\u2019s men said to him, \u201cBehold, we are afraid here in Judah. How much more then if we go to Keilah against the armies of the Philistines?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David inquired of the LORD yet again. The LORD answered him, and said, \u201cArise, go down to Keilah; for I will deliver the Philistines into your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"David and his men went to Keilah and fought with the Philistines, and brought away their livestock, and killed them with a great slaughter. So David saved the inhabitants of Keilah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When Abiathar the son of Ahimelech fled to David to Keilah, he came down with an ephod in his hand."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul was told that David had come to Keilah. Saul said, \u201cGod has delivered him into my hand, for he is shut in by entering into a town that has gates and bars.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Saul summoned all the people to war, to go down to Keilah to besiege David and his men."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"David knew that Saul was devising mischief against him. He said to Abiathar the priest, \u201cBring the ephod here.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Then David said, \u201cO LORD, the God of Israel, your servant has surely heard that Saul seeks to come to Keilah to destroy the city for my sake."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Will the men of Keilah deliver me up into his hand? Will Saul come down, as your servant has heard? LORD, the God of Israel, I beg you, tell your servant.\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said, \u201cHe will come down.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said, \u201cWill the men of Keilah deliver me and my men into the hand of Saul?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said, \u201cThey will deliver you up.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David and his men, who were about six hundred, arose and departed out of Keilah and went wherever they could go. Saul was told that David had escaped from Keilah; and he gave up going there."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"David stayed in the wilderness in the strongholds, and remained in the hill country in the wilderness of Ziph. Saul sought him every day, but God didn\u2019t deliver him into his hand."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"David saw that Saul had come out to seek his life. David was in the wilderness of Ziph in the woods."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan, Saul\u2019s son, arose and went to David into the woods, and strengthened his hand in God."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for the hand of Saul my father won\u2019t find you; and you will be king over Israel, and I will be next to you; and Saul my father knows that also.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They both made a covenant before the LORD. Then David stayed in the woods and Jonathan went to his house."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Ziphites came up to Saul to Gibeah, saying, \u201cDoesn\u2019t David hide himself with us in the strongholds in the woods, in the hill of Hachilah, which is on the south of the desert?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now therefore, O king, come down. According to all the desire of your soul to come down; and our part will be to deliver him up into the king\u2019s hand.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul said, \u201cYou are blessed by the LORD, for you have had compassion on me."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Please go make yet more sure, and know and see his place where his haunt is, and who has seen him there; for I have been told that he is very cunning."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"See therefore, and take knowledge of all the lurking places where he hides himself; and come again to me with certainty, and I will go with you. It shall happen, if he is in the land, that I will search him out among all the thousands of Judah.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"They arose, and went to Ziph before Saul; but David and his men were in the wilderness of Maon, in the Arabah on the south of the desert."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Saul and his men went to seek him. When David was told, he went down to the rock, and stayed in the wilderness of Maon. When Saul heard that, he pursued David in the wilderness of Maon."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Saul went on this side of the mountain, and David and his men on that side of the mountain; and David hurried to get away for fear of Saul, for Saul and his men surrounded David and his men to take them."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But a messenger came to Saul, saying, \u201cHurry and come, for the Philistines have made a raid on the land!\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So Saul returned from pursuing David, and went against the Philistines. Therefore they called that place Sela Hammahlekoth."]],f:["\u201cSela Hammahlekoth\u201d means \u201crock of parting\u201d."]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"David went up from there and lived in the strongholds of En Gedi."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Saul had returned from following the Philistines, he was told, \u201cBehold, David is in the wilderness of En Gedi.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Saul took three thousand chosen men out of all Israel, and went to seek David and his men on the rocks of the wild goats."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He came to the sheep pens by the way, where there was a cave; and Saul went in to relieve himself. Now David and his men were staying in the innermost parts of the cave."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"David\u2019s men said to him, \u201cBehold, the day of which the LORD said to you, \u2018Behold, I will deliver your enemy into your hand, and you shall do to him as it shall seem good to you.\u2019\u201d Then David arose and cut off the skirt of Saul\u2019s robe secretly."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Afterward, David\u2019s heart struck him because he had cut off Saul\u2019s skirt."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said to his men, \u201cThe LORD forbid that I should do this thing to my lord, the LORD\u2019s anointed, to stretch out my hand against him, since he is the LORD\u2019s anointed.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So David checked his men with these words, and didn\u2019t allow them to rise against Saul. Saul rose up out of the cave, and went on his way."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"David also arose afterward, and went out of the cave and cried after Saul, saying, \u201cMy lord the king!\u201d"],[0,"When Saul looked behind him, David bowed with his face to the earth, and showed respect."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"David said to Saul, \u201cWhy do you listen to men\u2019s words, saying, \u2018Behold, David seeks to harm you\u2019?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Behold, today your eyes have seen how the LORD had delivered you today into my hand in the cave. Some urged me to kill you, but I spared you. I said, \u2018I will not stretch out my hand against my lord, for he is the LORD\u2019s anointed.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Moreover, my father, behold, yes, see the skirt of your robe in my hand; for in that I cut off the skirt of your robe and didn\u2019t kill you, know and see that there is neither evil nor disobedience in my hand. I have not sinned against you, though you hunt for my life to take it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"May the LORD judge between me and you, and may the LORD avenge me of you; but my hand will not be on you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"As the proverb of the ancients says, \u2018Out of the wicked comes wickedness;\u2019 but my hand will not be on you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Against whom has the king of Israel come out? Whom do you pursue? A dead dog? A flea?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"May the LORD therefore be judge, and give sentence between me and you, and see, and plead my cause, and deliver me out of your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass, when David had finished speaking these words to Saul, that Saul said, \u201cIs that your voice, my son David?\u201d Saul lifted up his voice and wept."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He said to David, \u201cYou are more righteous than I; for you have done good to me, whereas I have done evil to you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You have declared today how you have dealt well with me, because when the LORD had delivered me up into your hand, you didn\u2019t kill me."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For if a man finds his enemy, will he let him go away unharmed? Therefore may the LORD reward you good for that which you have done to me today."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now, behold, I know that you will surely be king, and that the kingdom of Israel will be established in your hand."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Swear now therefore to me by the LORD that you will not cut off my offspring after me, and that you will not destroy my name out of my father\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"David swore to Saul. Saul went home, but David and his men went up to the stronghold."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel died; and all Israel gathered themselves together and mourned for him, and buried him at his house at Ramah."],[0,"Then David arose and went down to the wilderness of Paran."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"There was a man in Maon whose possessions were in Carmel; and the man was very great. He had three thousand sheep and a thousand goats; and he was shearing his sheep in Carmel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now the name of the man was Nabal; and the name of his wife Abigail. This woman was intelligent and had a beautiful face; but the man was surly and evil in his doings. He was of the house of Caleb."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"David heard in the wilderness that Nabal was shearing his sheep."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"David sent ten young men; and David said to the young men, \u201cGo up to Carmel, and go to Nabal, and greet him in my name."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Tell him, \u2018Long life to you! Peace be to you! Peace be to your house! Peace be to all that you have!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now I have heard that you have shearers. Your shepherds have now been with us, and we didn\u2019t harm them. Nothing was missing from them all the time they were in Carmel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Ask your young men, and they will tell you. Therefore let the young men find favor in your eyes, for we come on a good day. Please give whatever comes to your hand to your servants and to your son David.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When David\u2019s young men came, they spoke to Nabal all those words in the name of David, and waited."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Nabal answered David\u2019s servants and said, \u201cWho is David? Who is the son of Jesse? There are many servants who break away from their masters these days."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Shall I then take my bread, my water, and my meat that I have killed for my shearers, and give it to men who I don\u2019t know where they come from?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So David\u2019s young men turned on their way and went back, and came and told him all these words."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to his men, \u201cEvery man put on his sword!\u201d"],[0,"Every man put on his sword. David also put on his sword. About four hundred men followed David, and two hundred stayed by the baggage."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"But one of the young men told Abigail, Nabal\u2019s wife, saying, \u201cBehold, David sent messengers out of the wilderness to greet our master; and he insulted them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But the men were very good to us, and we were not harmed, and we didn\u2019t miss anything as long as we went with them, when we were in the fields."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They were a wall to us both by night and by day, all the while we were with them keeping the sheep."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now therefore know and consider what you will do; for evil is determined against our master and against all his house, for he is such a worthless fellow that one can\u2019t speak to him.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Abigail hurried and took two hundred loaves of bread, two containers of wine, five sheep ready dressed, five seahs of parched grain, one hundred clusters of raisins, and two hundred cakes of figs, and laid them on donkeys."]],f:["1 seah is about 7 liters or 1.9 gallons or 0.8 pecks"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"She said to her young men, \u201cGo on before me. Behold, I am coming after you.\u201d But she didn\u2019t tell her husband, Nabal."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As she rode on her donkey, and came down hidden by the mountain, behold, David and his men came down toward her, and she met them."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Now David had said, \u201cSurely in vain I have kept all that this fellow has in the wilderness, so that nothing was missed of all that pertained to him. He has returned me evil for good."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"God do so to the enemies of David, and more also, if I leave of all that belongs to him by the morning light so much as one who urinates on a wall.\u201d"]],f:["or, male."]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"When Abigail saw David, she hurried and got off her donkey, and fell before David on her face and bowed herself to the ground."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"She fell at his feet and said, \u201cOn me, my lord, on me be the blame! Please let your servant speak in your ears. Hear the words of your servant."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Please don\u2019t let my lord pay attention to this worthless fellow, Nabal, for as his name is, so is he. Nabal is his name, and folly is with him; but I, your servant, didn\u2019t see my lord\u2019s young men whom you sent."]],f:["\u201cNabal\u201d means \u201cfoolish\u201d."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Now therefore, my lord, as the LORD lives and as your soul lives, since the LORD has withheld you from blood guiltiness and from avenging yourself with your own hand, now therefore let your enemies and those who seek evil to my lord be as Nabal."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Now this present which your servant has brought to my lord, let it be given to the young men who follow my lord."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Please forgive the trespass of your servant. For the LORD will certainly make my lord a sure house, because my lord fights the LORD\u2019s battles. Evil will not be found in you all your days."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Though men may rise up to pursue you and to seek your soul, yet the soul of my lord will be bound in the bundle of life with the LORD your God. He will sling out the souls of your enemies as from a sling\u2019s pocket."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"It will come to pass, when the LORD has done to my lord according to all the good that he has spoken concerning you, and has appointed you prince over Israel,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"that this shall be no grief to you, nor offense of heart to my lord, either that you have shed blood without cause, or that my lord has avenged himself. When the LORD has dealt well with my lord, then remember your servant.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Abigail, \u201cBlessed is the LORD, the God of Israel, who sent you today to meet me!"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Blessed is your discretion, and blessed are you, who have kept me today from blood guiltiness, and from avenging myself with my own hand."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For indeed, as the LORD the God of Israel lives, who has withheld me from harming you, unless you had hurried and come to meet me, surely there wouldn\u2019t have been left to Nabal by the morning light so much as one who urinates on a wall.\u201d"]],f:["or, one male."]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"So David received from her hand that which she had brought him. Then he said to her, \u201cGo up in peace to your house. Behold, I have listened to your voice and have granted your request.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Abigail came to Nabal; and behold, he held a feast in his house like the feast of a king. Nabal\u2019s heart was merry within him, for he was very drunk. Therefore she told him nothing until the morning light."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"In the morning, when the wine had gone out of Nabal, his wife told him these things; and his heart died within him, and he became as a stone."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"About ten days later, the LORD struck Nabal, so that he died."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"When David heard that Nabal was dead, he said, \u201cBlessed is the LORD, who has pleaded the cause of my reproach from the hand of Nabal, and has kept back his servant from evil. The LORD has returned the evildoing of Nabal on his own head.\u201d"],[0,"David sent and spoke concerning Abigail, to take her to himself as wife."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"When David\u2019s servants had come to Abigail to Carmel, they spoke to her, saying, \u201cDavid has sent us to you, to take you to him as wife.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"She arose and bowed herself with her face to the earth, and said, \u201cBehold, your servant is a servant to wash the feet of the servants of my lord.\u201d"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Abigail hurriedly arose and rode on a donkey with her five maids who followed her; and she went after the messengers of David, and became his wife."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"David also took Ahinoam of Jezreel; and they both became his wives."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Saul had given Michal his daughter, David\u2019s wife, to Palti the son of Laish, who was of Gallim."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The Ziphites came to Saul to Gibeah, saying, \u201cDoesn\u2019t David hide himself in the hill of Hachilah, which is before the desert?\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Saul arose and went down to the wilderness of Ziph, having three thousand chosen men of Israel with him, to seek David in the wilderness of Ziph."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Saul encamped in the hill of Hachilah, which is before the desert, by the way. But David stayed in the wilderness, and he saw that Saul came after him into the wilderness."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"David therefore sent out spies, and understood that Saul had certainly come."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then David arose and came to the place where Saul had encamped; and David saw the place where Saul lay, with Abner the son of Ner, the captain of his army. Saul lay within the place of the wagons, and the people were encamped around him."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David answered and said to Ahimelech the Hittite, and to Abishai the son of Zeruiah, brother of Joab, saying, \u201cWho will go down with me to Saul to the camp?\u201d"],[0,"Abishai said, \u201cI will go down with you.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So David and Abishai came to the people by night; and, behold, Saul lay sleeping within the place of the wagons, with his spear stuck in the ground at his head; and Abner and the people lay around him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then Abishai said to David, \u201cGod has delivered up your enemy into your hand today. Now therefore please let me strike him with the spear to the earth at one stroke, and I will not strike him the second time.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Abishai, \u201cDon\u2019t destroy him, for who can stretch out his hand against the LORD\u2019s anointed, and be guiltless?\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, the LORD will strike him; or his day shall come to die, or he shall go down into battle and perish."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD forbid that I should stretch out my hand against the LORD\u2019s anointed; but now please take the spear that is at his head and the jar of water, and let\u2019s go.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So David took the spear and the jar of water from Saul\u2019s head, and they went away. No man saw it, or knew it, nor did any awake; for they were all asleep, because a deep sleep from the LORD had fallen on them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then David went over to the other side, and stood on the top of the mountain far away, a great space being between them;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and David cried to the people, and to Abner the son of Ner, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t you answer, Abner?\u201d"],[0,"Then Abner answered, \u201cWho are you who calls to the king?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Abner, \u201cAren\u2019t you a man? Who is like you in Israel? Why then have you not kept watch over your lord the king? For one of the people came in to destroy your lord the king."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"This thing isn\u2019t good that you have done. As the LORD lives, you are worthy to die, because you have not kept watch over your lord, the LORD\u2019s anointed. Now see where the king\u2019s spear is, and the jar of water that was at his head.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul recognized David\u2019s voice, and said, \u201cIs this your voice, my son David?\u201d"],[0,"David said, \u201cIt is my voice, my lord, O king.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhy does my lord pursue his servant? For what have I done? What evil is in my hand?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please let my lord the king hear the words of his servant. If it is so that the LORD has stirred you up against me, let him accept an offering. But if it is the children of men, they are cursed before the LORD; for they have driven me out today that I shouldn\u2019t cling to the LORD\u2019s inheritance, saying, \u2018Go, serve other gods!\u2019"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now therefore, don\u2019t let my blood fall to the earth away from the presence of the LORD; for the king of Israel has come out to seek a flea, as when one hunts a partridge in the mountains.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul said, \u201cI have sinned. Return, my son David; for I will no more do you harm, because my life was precious in your eyes today. Behold, I have played the fool, and have erred exceedingly.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"David answered, \u201cBehold the spear, O king! Let one of the young men come over and get it."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The LORD will give to every man his righteousness and his faithfulness; because the LORD delivered you into my hand today, and I wouldn\u2019t stretch out my hand against the LORD\u2019s anointed."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Behold, as your life was respected today in my eyes, so let my life be respected in the LORD\u2019s eyes, and let him deliver me out of all oppression.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to David, \u201cYou are blessed, my son David. You will both do mightily, and will surely prevail.\u201d"],[0,"So David went his way, and Saul returned to his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David said in his heart, \u201cI will now perish one day by the hand of Saul. There is nothing better for me than that I should escape into the land of the Philistines; and Saul will despair of me, to seek me any more in all the borders of Israel. So I will escape out of his hand.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David arose and passed over, he and the six hundred men who were with him, to Achish the son of Maoch, king of Gath."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"David lived with Achish at Gath, he and his men, every man with his household, even David with his two wives, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess and Abigail the Carmelitess, Nabal\u2019s wife."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Saul was told that David had fled to Gath, so he stopped looking for him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Achish, \u201cIf now I have found favor in your eyes, let them give me a place in one of the cities in the country, that I may dwell there. For why should your servant dwell in the royal city with you?\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then Achish gave him Ziklag that day: therefore Ziklag belongs to the kings of Judah to this day."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The number of the days that David lived in the country of the Philistines was a full year and four months."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"David and his men went up and raided the Geshurites, the Girzites, and the Amalekites; for those were the inhabitants of the land who were of old, on the way to Shur, even to the land of Egypt."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"David struck the land, and saved no man or woman alive, and took away the sheep, the cattle, the donkeys, the camels, and the clothing. Then he returned, and came to Achish."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Achish said, \u201cAgainst whom have you made a raid today?\u201d"],[0,"David said, \u201cAgainst the South of Judah, against the South of the Jerahmeelites, and against the South of the Kenites.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"David saved neither man nor woman alive to bring them to Gath, saying, \u201cLest they should tell about us, saying, \u2018David did this, and this has been his way all the time he has lived in the country of the Philistines.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Achish believed David, saying, \u201cHe has made his people Israel utterly to abhor him. Therefore he will be my servant forever.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days, the Philistines gathered their armies together for warfare, to fight with Israel. Achish said to David, \u201cKnow assuredly that you will go out with me in the army, you and your men.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Achish, \u201cTherefore you will know what your servant can do.\u201d"],[0,"Achish said to David, \u201cTherefore I will make you my bodyguard forever.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Samuel was dead, and all Israel had mourned for him and buried him in Ramah, even in his own city. Saul had sent away those who had familiar spirits and the wizards out of the land."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The Philistines gathered themselves together, and came and encamped in Shunem; and Saul gathered all Israel together, and they encamped in Gilboa."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When Saul saw the army of the Philistines, he was afraid, and his heart trembled greatly."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When Saul inquired of the LORD, the LORD didn\u2019t answer him by dreams, by Urim, or by prophets."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to his servants, \u201cSeek for me a woman who has a familiar spirit, that I may go to her and inquire of her.\u201d"],[0,"His servants said to him, \u201cBehold, there is a woman who has a familiar spirit at Endor.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul disguised himself and put on other clothing, and went, he and two men with him, and they came to the woman by night. Then he said, \u201cPlease consult for me by the familiar spirit, and bring me up whomever I shall name to you.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said to him, \u201cBehold, you know what Saul has done, how he has cut off those who have familiar spirits and the wizards out of the land. Why then do you lay a snare for my life, to cause me to die?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul swore to her by the LORD, saying, \u201cAs the LORD lives, no punishment will happen to you for this thing.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the woman said, \u201cWhom shall I bring up to you?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cBring Samuel up for me.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When the woman saw Samuel, she cried with a loud voice; and the woman spoke to Saul, saying, \u201cWhy have you deceived me? For you are Saul!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to her, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid! What do you see?\u201d"],[0,"The woman said to Saul, \u201cI see a god coming up out of the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cWhat does he look like?\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cAn old man comes up. He is covered with a robe.\u201d Saul perceived that it was Samuel, and he bowed with his face to the ground, and showed respect."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said to Saul, \u201cWhy have you disturbed me, to bring me up?\u201d"],[0,"Saul answered, \u201cI am very distressed; for the Philistines make war against me, and God has departed from me, and answers me no more, by prophets, or by dreams. Therefore I have called you, that you may make known to me what I shall do.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Samuel said, \u201cWhy then do you ask me, since the LORD has departed from you and has become your adversary?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The LORD has done to you as he spoke by me. The LORD has torn the kingdom out of your hand and given it to your neighbor, even to David."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Because you didn\u2019t obey the LORD\u2019s voice, and didn\u2019t execute his fierce wrath on Amalek, therefore the LORD has done this thing to you today."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD will deliver Israel also with you into the hand of the Philistines; and tomorrow you and your sons will be with me. The LORD will deliver the army of Israel also into the hand of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Saul fell immediately his full length on the earth, and was terrified, because of Samuel\u2019s words. There was no strength in him, for he had eaten no bread all day long or all night long."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman came to Saul and saw that he was very troubled, and said to him, \u201cBehold, your servant has listened to your voice, and I have put my life in my hand, and have listened to your words which you spoke to me."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please listen also to the voice of your servant, and let me set a morsel of bread before you. Eat, that you may have strength when you go on your way.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But he refused, and said, \u201cI will not eat.\u201d But his servants, together with the woman, constrained him; and he listened to their voice. So he arose from the earth and sat on the bed."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The woman had a fattened calf in the house. She hurried and killed it; and she took flour and kneaded it, and baked unleavened bread of it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"She brought it before Saul and before his servants, and they ate. Then they rose up and went away that night."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the Philistines gathered together all their armies to Aphek; and the Israelites encamped by the spring which is in Jezreel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The lords of the Philistines passed on by hundreds and by thousands; and David and his men passed on in the rear with Achish."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the princes of the Philistines said, \u201cWhat about these Hebrews?\u201d"],[0,"Achish said to the princes of the Philistines, \u201cIsn\u2019t this David, the servant of Saul the king of Israel, who has been with me these days, or rather these years? I have found no fault in him since he fell away until today.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But the princes of the Philistines were angry with him; and the princes of the Philistines said to him, \u201cMake the man return, that he may go back to his place where you have appointed him, and let him not go down with us to battle, lest in the battle he become an adversary to us. For with what should this fellow reconcile himself to his lord? Should it not be with the heads of these men?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t this David, of whom people sang to one another in dances, saying,"],[1,"\u2018Saul has slain his thousands,"],[2,"and David his ten thousands\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Achish called David and said to him, \u201cAs the LORD lives, you have been upright, and your going out and your coming in with me in the army is good in my sight; for I have not found evil in you since the day of your coming to me to this day. Nevertheless, the lords don\u2019t favor you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore now return, and go in peace, that you not displease the lords of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Achish, \u201cBut what have I done? What have you found in your servant so long as I have been before you to this day, that I may not go and fight against the enemies of my lord the king?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Achish answered David, \u201cI know that you are good in my sight, as an angel of God. Notwithstanding, the princes of the Philistines have said, \u2018He shall not go up with us to the battle.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore now rise up early in the morning with the servants of your lord who have come with you; and as soon as you are up early in the morning and have light, depart.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"So David rose up early, he and his men, to depart in the morning, to return into the land of the Philistines; and the Philistines went up to Jezreel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When David and his men had come to Ziklag on the third day, the Amalekites had made a raid on the South and on Ziklag, and had struck Ziklag and burned it with fire,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and had taken captive the women and all who were in it, both small and great. They didn\u2019t kill any, but carried them off and went their way."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When David and his men came to the city, behold, it was burned with fire; and their wives, their sons, and their daughters were taken captive."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then David and the people who were with him lifted up their voice and wept until they had no more power to weep."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"David\u2019s two wives were taken captive, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"David was greatly distressed, for the people spoke of stoning him, because the souls of all the people were grieved, every man for his sons and for his daughters; but David strengthened himself in the LORD his God."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"David said to Abiathar the priest, the son of Ahimelech, \u201cPlease bring the ephod here to me.\u201d"],[0,"Abiathar brought the ephod to David."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"David inquired of the LORD, saying, \u201cIf I pursue after this troop, will I overtake them?\u201d"],[0,"He answered him, \u201cPursue, for you will surely overtake them, and will without fail recover all.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"So David went, he and the six hundred men who were with him, and came to the brook Besor, where those who were left behind stayed."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But David pursued, he and four hundred men; for two hundred stayed behind, who were so faint that they couldn\u2019t go over the brook Besor."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They found an Egyptian in the field, and brought him to David, and gave him bread, and he ate; and they gave him water to drink."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They gave him a piece of a cake of figs and two clusters of raisins. When he had eaten, his spirit came again to him; for he had eaten no bread, and drank no water for three days and three nights."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"David asked him, \u201cTo whom do you belong? Where are you from?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am a young man of Egypt, servant to an Amalekite; and my master left me, because three days ago I got sick."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"We made a raid on the South of the Cherethites, and on that which belongs to Judah, and on the South of Caleb; and we burned Ziklag with fire.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to him, \u201cWill you bring me down to this troop?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cSwear to me by God that you will not kill me and not deliver me up into the hands of my master, and I will bring you down to this troop.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had brought him down, behold, they were spread around over all the ground, eating, drinking, and dancing, because of all the great plunder that they had taken out of the land of the Philistines, and out of the land of Judah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"David struck them from the twilight even to the evening of the next day. Not a man of them escaped from there, except four hundred young men who rode on camels and fled."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"David recovered all that the Amalekites had taken, and David rescued his two wives."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There was nothing lacking to them, neither small nor great, neither sons nor daughters, neither plunder, nor anything that they had taken. David brought them all back."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"David took all the flocks and the herds, which they drove before those other livestock, and said, \u201cThis is David\u2019s plunder.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"David came to the two hundred men, who were so faint that they could not follow David, whom also they had made to stay at the brook Besor; and they went out to meet David, and to meet the people who were with him. When David came near to the people, he greeted them."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Then all the wicked men and worthless fellows of those who went with David answered and said, \u201cBecause they didn\u2019t go with us, we will not give them anything of the plunder that we have recovered, except to every man his wife and his children, that he may lead them away and depart.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said, \u201cDo not do so, my brothers, with that which the LORD has given to us, who has preserved us, and delivered the troop that came against us into our hand."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Who will listen to you in this matter? For as his share is who goes down to the battle, so shall his share be who stays with the baggage. They shall share alike.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"It was so from that day forward that he made it a statute and an ordinance for Israel to this day."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"When David came to Ziklag, he sent some of the plunder to the elders of Judah, even to his friends, saying, \u201cBehold, a present for you from the plunder of the LORD\u2019s enemies.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He sent it to those who were in Bethel, to those who were in Ramoth of the South, to those who were in Jattir,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"to those who were in Aroer, to those who were in Siphmoth, to those who were in Eshtemoa,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"to those who were in Racal, to those who were in the cities of the Jerahmeelites, to those who were in the cities of the Kenites,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"to those who were in Hormah, to those who were in Borashan, to those who were in Athach,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"to those who were in Hebron, and to all the places where David himself and his men used to stay."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the Philistines fought against Israel; and the men of Israel fled from before the Philistines, and fell down slain on Mount Gilboa."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Philistines overtook Saul and his sons; and the Philistines killed Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchishua, the sons of Saul."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The battle went hard against Saul, and the archers overtook him; and he was greatly distressed by reason of the archers."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to his armor bearer, \u201cDraw your sword, and thrust me through with it, lest these uncircumcised come and thrust me through and abuse me!\u201d But his armor bearer would not, for he was terrified. Therefore Saul took his sword and fell on it."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When his armor bearer saw that Saul was dead, he likewise fell on his sword, and died with him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Saul died with his three sons, his armor bearer, and all his men that same day together."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When the men of Israel who were on the other side of the valley, and those who were beyond the Jordan, saw that the men of Israel fled and that Saul and his sons were dead, they abandoned the cities and fled; and the Philistines came and lived in them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"On the next day, when the Philistines came to strip the slain, they found Saul and his three sons fallen on Mount Gilboa."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They cut off his head, stripped off his armor, and sent into the land of the Philistines all around, to carry the news to the house of their idols and to the people."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They put his armor in the house of the Ashtaroth, and they fastened his body to the wall of Beth Shan."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When the inhabitants of Jabesh Gilead heard what the Philistines had done to Saul,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"all the valiant men arose, went all night, and took the body of Saul and the bodies of his sons from the wall of Beth Shan; and they came to Jabesh and burned them there."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They took their bones and buried them under the tamarisk tree in Jabesh, and fasted seven days."]],f:["or, salt cedar"]}]]}},1280,[]);
__d(function(e,a,t,o,h,n,i){h.exports={book:"2Sam",name:"2 Samuel",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After the death of Saul, when David had returned from the slaughter of the Amalekites, and David had stayed two days in Ziklag,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"on the third day, behold, a man came out of the camp from Saul, with his clothes torn and earth on his head. When he came to David, he fell to the earth and showed respect."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to him, \u201cWhere do you come from?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cI have escaped out of the camp of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to him, \u201cHow did it go? Please tell me.\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cThe people have fled from the battle, and many of the people also have fallen and are dead. Saul and Jonathan his son are dead also.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to the young man who told him, \u201cHow do you know that Saul and Jonathan his son are dead?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The young man who told him said, \u201cAs I happened by chance on Mount Gilboa, behold, Saul was leaning on his spear; and behold, the chariots and the horsemen followed close behind him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When he looked behind him, he saw me and called to me. I answered, \u2018Here I am.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u2018Who are you?\u2019 I answered him, \u2018I am an Amalekite.\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u2018Please stand beside me, and kill me, for anguish has taken hold of me because my life lingers in me.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So I stood beside him and killed him, because I was sure that he could not live after he had fallen. I took the crown that was on his head and the bracelet that was on his arm, and have brought them here to my lord.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David took hold of his clothes and tore them; and all the men who were with him did likewise."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They mourned, wept, and fasted until evening for Saul and for Jonathan his son, and for the people of the LORD, and for the house of Israel, because they had fallen by the sword."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to the young man who told him, \u201cWhere are you from?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cI am the son of a foreigner, an Amalekite.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to him, \u201cWhy were you not afraid to stretch out your hand to destroy the LORD\u2019s anointed?\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"David called one of the young men and said, \u201cGo near, and cut him down!\u201d He struck him so that he died."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"David said to him, \u201cYour blood be on your head, for your mouth has testified against you, saying, \u2018I have slain the LORD\u2019s anointed.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"David lamented with this lamentation over Saul and over Jonathan his son"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"(and he commanded them to teach the children of Judah the song of the bow; behold, it is written in the book of Jashar):"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYour glory, Israel, was slain on your high places!"],[2,"How the mighty have fallen!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t tell it in Gath."],[2,"Don\u2019t publish it in the streets of Ashkelon,"],[1,"lest the daughters of the Philistines rejoice,"],[2,"lest the daughters of the uncircumcised triumph."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"You mountains of Gilboa,"],[2,"let there be no dew or rain on you, and no fields of offerings;"],[2,"for there the shield of the mighty was defiled and cast away,"],[2,"the shield of Saul was not anointed with oil."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"From the blood of the slain,"],[2,"from the fat of the mighty,"],[2,"Jonathan\u2019s bow didn\u2019t turn back."],[2,"Saul\u2019s sword didn\u2019t return empty."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Saul and Jonathan were lovely and pleasant in their lives."],[2,"In their death, they were not divided."],[1,"They were swifter than eagles."],[2,"They were stronger than lions."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"You daughters of Israel, weep over Saul,"],[2,"who clothed you delicately in scarlet,"],[2,"who put ornaments of gold on your clothing."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"How the mighty have fallen in the middle of the battle!"],[2,"Jonathan was slain on your high places."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"I am distressed for you, my brother Jonathan."],[2,"You have been very pleasant to me."],[2,"Your love to me was wonderful,"],[2,"surpassing the love of women."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"How the mighty have fallen,"],[2,"and the weapons of war have perished!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, David inquired of the LORD, saying, \u201cShall I go up into any of the cities of Judah?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cGo up.\u201d"],[0,"David said, \u201cWhere shall I go up?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cTo Hebron.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"So David went up there with his two wives, Ahinoam the Jezreelitess, and Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"David brought up his men who were with him, every man with his household. They lived in the cities of Hebron."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The men of Judah came, and there they anointed David king over the house of Judah. They told David, \u201cThe men of Jabesh Gilead were those who buried Saul.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"David sent messengers to the men of Jabesh Gilead, and said to them, \u201cBlessed are you by the LORD, that you have shown this kindness to your lord, even to Saul, and have buried him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now may the LORD show loving kindness and truth to you. I also will reward you for this kindness, because you have done this thing."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now therefore let your hands be strong, and be valiant; for Saul your lord is dead, and also the house of Judah have anointed me king over them.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Abner the son of Ner, captain of Saul\u2019s army, had taken Ishbosheth the son of Saul and brought him over to Mahanaim."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He made him king over Gilead, over the Ashurites, over Jezreel, over Ephraim, over Benjamin, and over all Israel."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Ishbosheth, Saul\u2019s son, was forty years old when he began to reign over Israel, and he reigned two years. But the house of Judah followed David."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The time that David was king in Hebron over the house of Judah was seven years and six months."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Abner the son of Ner, and the servants of Ishbosheth the son of Saul, went out from Mahanaim to Gibeon."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Joab the son of Zeruiah and David\u2019s servants went out, and met them by the pool of Gibeon; and they sat down, the one on the one side of the pool and the other on the other side of the pool."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Abner said to Joab, \u201cPlease let the young men arise and compete before us!\u201d"],[0,"Joab said, \u201cLet them arise!\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then they arose and went over by number: twelve for Benjamin and for Ishbosheth the son of Saul, and twelve of David\u2019s servants."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They each caught his opponent by the head and thrust his sword in his fellow\u2019s side; so they fell down together. Therefore that place in Gibeon was called Helkath Hazzurim."]],f:["\u201cHelkath Hazzurim\u201d means \u201cfield of daggers\u201d."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The battle was very severe that day; and Abner was beaten, and the men of Israel, before David\u2019s servants."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The three sons of Zeruiah were there: Joab, Abishai, and Asahel. Asahel was as light of foot as a wild gazelle."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Asahel pursued Abner. He didn\u2019t turn to the right hand or to the left from following Abner."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Abner looked behind him and said, \u201cIs that you, Asahel?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cIt is.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Abner said to him, \u201cTurn away to your right hand or to your left, and grab one of the young men, and take his armor.\u201d But Asahel would not turn away from following him."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Abner said again to Asahel, \u201cTurn away from following me. Why should I strike you to the ground? How then could I look Joab your brother in the face?\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"However, he refused to turn away. Therefore Abner with the back end of the spear struck him in the body, so that the spear came out behind him; and he fell down there and died in the same place. As many as came to the place where Asahel fell down and died stood still."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"But Joab and Abishai pursued Abner. The sun went down when they had come to the hill of Ammah, that lies before Giah by the way of the wilderness of Gibeon."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin gathered themselves together after Abner and became one band, and stood on the top of a hill."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Then Abner called to Joab, and said, \u201cShall the sword devour forever? Don\u2019t you know that it will be bitterness in the latter end? How long will it be then, before you ask the people to return from following their brothers?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab said, \u201cAs God lives, if you had not spoken, surely then in the morning the people would have gone away, and not each followed his brother.\u201d"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So Joab blew the trumpet; and all the people stood still and pursued Israel no more, and they fought no more."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Abner and his men went all that night through the Arabah; and they passed over the Jordan, and went through all Bithron, and came to Mahanaim."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab returned from following Abner; and when he had gathered all the people together, nineteen men of David\u2019s and Asahel were missing."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But David\u2019s servants had struck Benjamin and Abner\u2019s men so that three hundred sixty men died."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They took up Asahel and buried him in the tomb of his father, which was in Bethlehem. Joab and his men went all night, and the day broke on them at Hebron."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was a long war between Saul\u2019s house and David\u2019s house. David grew stronger and stronger, but Saul\u2019s house grew weaker and weaker."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Sons were born to David in Hebron. His firstborn was Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and his second, Chileab, of Abigail the wife of Nabal the Carmelite; and the third, Absalom the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith; and the fifth, Shephatiah the son of Abital;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and the sixth, Ithream, of Eglah, David\u2019s wife. These were born to David in Hebron."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"While there was war between Saul\u2019s house and David\u2019s house, Abner made himself strong in Saul\u2019s house."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now Saul had a concubine, whose name was Rizpah, the daughter of Aiah; and Ishbosheth said to Abner, \u201cWhy have you gone in to my father\u2019s concubine?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Abner was very angry about Ishbosheth\u2019s words, and said, \u201cAm I a dog\u2019s head that belongs to Judah? Today I show kindness to your father Saul\u2019s house, to his brothers, and to his friends, and have not delivered you into the hand of David; and yet you charge me today with a fault concerning this woman!"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"God do so to Abner, and more also, if, as the LORD has sworn to David, I don\u2019t do even so to him:"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"to transfer the kingdom from Saul\u2019s house, and to set up David\u2019s throne over Israel and over Judah, from Dan even to Beersheba.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He could not answer Abner another word, because he was afraid of him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Abner sent messengers to David on his behalf, saying, \u201cWhose is the land?\u201d and saying, \u201cMake your alliance with me, and behold, my hand will be with you to bring all Israel around to you.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cGood. I will make a treaty with you, but one thing I require of you. That is, you will not see my face unless you first bring Michal, Saul\u2019s daughter, when you come to see my face.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"David sent messengers to Ishbosheth, Saul\u2019s son, saying, \u201cDeliver me my wife Michal, whom I was given to marry for one hundred foreskins of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Ishbosheth sent and took her from her husband, Paltiel the son of Laish."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Her husband went with her, weeping as he went, and followed her to Bahurim. Then Abner said to him, \u201cGo! Return!\u201d and he returned."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Abner had communication with the elders of Israel, saying, \u201cIn times past, you sought for David to be king over you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now then do it! For the LORD has spoken of David, saying, \u2018By the hand of my servant David, I will save my people Israel out of the hand of the Philistines, and out of the hand of all their enemies.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Abner also spoke in the ears of Benjamin; and Abner went also to speak in the ears of David in Hebron all that seemed good to Israel and to the whole house of Benjamin."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"So Abner came to David to Hebron, and twenty men with him. David made Abner and the men who were with him a feast."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Abner said to David, \u201cI will arise and go, and will gather all Israel to my lord the king, that they may make a covenant with you, and that you may reign over all that your soul desires.\u201d David sent Abner away; and he went in peace."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, David\u2019s servants and Joab came from a raid and brought in a great plunder with them; but Abner was not with David in Hebron, for he had sent him away, and he had gone in peace."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When Joab and all the army who was with him had come, they told Joab, \u201cAbner the son of Ner came to the king, and he has sent him away, and he has gone in peace.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joab came to the king and said, \u201cWhat have you done? Behold, Abner came to you. Why is it that you have sent him away, and he is already gone?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You know Abner the son of Ner. He came to deceive you, and to know your going out and your coming in, and to know all that you do.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joab had come out from David, he sent messengers after Abner, and they brought him back from the well of Sirah; but David didn\u2019t know it."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When Abner had returned to Hebron, Joab took him aside into the middle of the gate to speak with him quietly, and struck him there in the body, so that he died for the blood of Asahel his brother."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Afterward, when David heard it, he said, \u201cI and my kingdom are guiltless before the LORD forever of the blood of Abner the son of Ner."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Let it fall on the head of Joab and on all his father\u2019s house. Let there not fail from the house of Joab one who has a discharge, or who is a leper, or who leans on a staff, or who falls by the sword, or who lacks bread.\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"So Joab and Abishai his brother killed Abner, because he had killed their brother Asahel at Gibeon in the battle."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Joab and to all the people who were with him, \u201cTear your clothes, and clothe yourselves with sackcloth, and mourn in front of Abner.\u201d King David followed the bier."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They buried Abner in Hebron; and the king lifted up his voice and wept at Abner\u2019s grave; and all the people wept."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The king lamented for Abner, and said, \u201cShould Abner die as a fool dies?"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Your hands weren\u2019t bound, and your feet weren\u2019t put into fetters. As a man falls before the children of iniquity, so you fell.\u201d"],[0,"All the people wept again over him."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"All the people came to urge David to eat bread while it was yet day; but David swore, saying, \u201cGod do so to me, and more also, if I taste bread or anything else, until the sun goes down.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people took notice of it, and it pleased them, as whatever the king did pleased all the people."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"So all the people and all Israel understood that day that it was not of the king to kill Abner the son of Ner."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The king said to his servants, \u201cDon\u2019t you know that a prince and a great man has fallen today in Israel?"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"I am weak today, though anointed king. These men, the sons of Zeruiah are too hard for me. May the LORD reward the evildoer according to his wickedness.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Saul\u2019s son heard that Abner was dead in Hebron, his hands became feeble, and all the Israelites were troubled."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Saul\u2019s son had two men who were captains of raiding bands. The name of one was Baanah and the name of the other Rechab, the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, of the children of Benjamin (for Beeroth also is considered a part of Benjamin;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and the Beerothites fled to Gittaim, and have lived as foreigners there until today)."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jonathan, Saul\u2019s son, had a son who was lame in his feet. He was five years old when the news came about Saul and Jonathan out of Jezreel; and his nurse picked him up and fled. As she hurried to flee, he fell and became lame. His name was Mephibosheth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, Rechab and Baanah, went out and came at about the heat of the day to the house of Ishbosheth as he took his rest at noon."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They came there into the middle of the house as though they would have fetched wheat, and they struck him in the body; and Rechab and Baanah his brother escaped."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now when they came into the house as he lay on his bed in his bedroom, they struck him, killed him, beheaded him, and took his head, and went by the way of the Arabah all night."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They brought the head of Ishbosheth to David to Hebron, and said to the king, \u201cBehold, the head of Ishbosheth, the son of Saul, your enemy, who sought your life! The LORD has avenged my lord the king today of Saul and of his offspring.\u201d"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"David answered Rechab and Baanah his brother, the sons of Rimmon the Beerothite, and said to them, \u201cAs the LORD lives, who has redeemed my soul out of all adversity,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"when someone told me, \u2018Behold, Saul is dead,\u2019 thinking that he brought good news, I seized him and killed him in Ziklag, which was the reward I gave him for his news."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"How much more, when wicked men have slain a righteous person in his own house on his bed, should I not now require his blood from your hand, and rid the earth of you?\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"David commanded his young men, and they killed them, cut off their hands and their feet, and hanged them up beside the pool in Hebron. But they took the head of Ishbosheth and buried it in Abner\u2019s grave in Hebron."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the tribes of Israel came to David at Hebron and spoke, saying, \u201cBehold, we are your bone and your flesh."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In times past, when Saul was king over us, it was you who led Israel out and in. The LORD said to you, \u2018You will be shepherd of my people Israel, and you will be prince over Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So all the elders of Israel came to the king to Hebron, and King David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the LORD; and they anointed David king over Israel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"David was thirty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"In Hebron he reigned over Judah seven years and six months, and in Jerusalem he reigned thirty-three years over all Israel and Judah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The king and his men went to Jerusalem against the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the land, who spoke to David, saying, \u201cThe blind and the lame will keep you out of here,\u201d thinking, \u201cDavid can\u2019t come in here.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Nevertheless David took the stronghold of Zion. This is David\u2019s city."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"David said on that day, \u201cWhoever strikes the Jebusites, let him go up to the watercourse and strike those lame and blind, who are hated by David\u2019s soul.\u201d Therefore they say, \u201cThe blind and the lame can\u2019t come into the house.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"David lived in the stronghold, and called it David\u2019s city. David built around from Millo and inward."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"David grew greater and greater, for the LORD, the God of Armies, was with him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, with cedar trees, carpenters, and masons; and they built David a house."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"David perceived that the LORD had established him king over Israel, and that he had exalted his kingdom for his people Israel\u2019s sake."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"David took more concubines and wives for himself out of Jerusalem, after he had come from Hebron; and more sons and daughters were born to David."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"These are the names of those who were born to him in Jerusalem: Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Ibhar, Elishua, Nepheg, Japhia,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Elishama, Eliada, and Eliphelet."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Philistines heard that they had anointed David king over Israel, all the Philistines went up to seek David, but David heard about it and went down to the stronghold."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now the Philistines had come and spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"David inquired of the LORD, saying, \u201cShall I go up against the Philistines? Will you deliver them into my hand?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said to David, \u201cGo up; for I will certainly deliver the Philistines into your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"David came to Baal Perazim, and David struck them there. Then he said, \u201cThe LORD has broken my enemies before me, like the breach of waters.\u201d Therefore he called the name of that place Baal Perazim."]],f:["\u201cBaal Perazim\u201d means \u201cLord who breaks out\u201d."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They left their images there, and David and his men took them away."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The Philistines came up yet again and spread themselves in the valley of Rephaim."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When David inquired of the LORD, he said, \u201cYou shall not go up. Circle around behind them, and attack them in front of the mulberry trees."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When you hear the sound of marching in the tops of the mulberry trees, then stir yourself up; for then the LORD has gone out before you to strike the army of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"David did so, as the LORD commanded him, and struck the Philistines all the way from Geba to Gezer."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David again gathered together all the chosen men of Israel, thirty thousand."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David arose and went with all the people who were with him from Baale Judah, to bring up from there God\u2019s ark, which is called by the Name, even the name of the LORD of Armies who sits above the cherubim."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They set God\u2019s ark on a new cart, and brought it out of Abinadab\u2019s house that was on the hill; and Uzzah and Ahio, the sons of Abinadab, drove the new cart."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They brought it out of Abinadab\u2019s house which was in the hill, with God\u2019s ark; and Ahio went before the ark."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"David and all the house of Israel played before the LORD with all kinds of instruments made of cypress wood, with harps, with stringed instruments, with tambourines, with castanets, and with cymbals."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When they came to the threshing floor of Nacon, Uzzah reached for God\u2019s ark and took hold of it, for the cattle stumbled."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Uzzah, and God struck him there for his error; and he died there by God\u2019s ark."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"David was displeased because the LORD had broken out against Uzzah; and he called that place Perez Uzzah to this day."]],f:["\u201cPerez Uzzah\u201d means \u201coutbreak against Uzzah\u201d."]},{v:9,l:[[0,"David was afraid of the LORD that day; and he said, \u201cHow could the LORD\u2019s ark come to me?\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So David would not move the LORD\u2019s ark to be with him in David\u2019s city; but David carried it aside into Obed-Edom the Gittite\u2019s house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s ark remained in Obed-Edom the Gittite\u2019s house three months; and the LORD blessed Obed-Edom and all his house."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"King David was told, \u201cThe LORD has blessed the house of Obed-Edom, and all that belongs to him, because of God\u2019s ark.\u201d"],[0,"So David went and brought up God\u2019s ark from the house of Obed-Edom into David\u2019s city with joy."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When those who bore the LORD\u2019s ark had gone six paces, he sacrificed an ox and a fattened calf."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"David danced before the LORD with all his might; and David was clothed in a linen ephod."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So David and all the house of Israel brought up the LORD\u2019s ark with shouting and with the sound of the trumpet."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"As the LORD\u2019s ark came into David\u2019s city, Michal the daughter of Saul looked out through the window and saw King David leaping and dancing before the LORD; and she despised him in her heart."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They brought in the LORD\u2019s ark, and set it in its place in the middle of the tent that David had pitched for it; and David offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before the LORD."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When David had finished offering the burnt offering and the peace offerings, he blessed the people in the name of the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He gave to all the people, even among the whole multitude of Israel, both to men and women, to everyone a portion of bread, dates, and raisins. So all the people departed, each to his own house."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David returned to bless his household. Michal the daughter of Saul came out to meet David, and said, \u201cHow glorious the king of Israel was today, who uncovered himself today in the eyes of his servants\u2019 maids, as one of the vain fellows shamelessly uncovers himself!\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Michal, \u201cIt was before the LORD, who chose me above your father, and above all his house, to appoint me prince over the people of the LORD, over Israel. Therefore I will celebrate before the LORD."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will be yet more undignified than this, and will be worthless in my own sight. But the maids of whom you have spoken will honor me.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Michal the daughter of Saul had no child to the day of her death."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the king lived in his house, and the LORD had given him rest from all his enemies all around,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"the king said to Nathan the prophet, \u201cSee now, I dwell in a house of cedar, but God\u2019s ark dwells within curtains.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Nathan said to the king, \u201cGo, do all that is in your heart, for the LORD is with you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"That same night, the LORD\u2019s word came to Nathan, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cGo and tell my servant David, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cShould you build me a house for me to dwell in?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For I have not lived in a house since the day that I brought the children of Israel up out of Egypt, even to this day, but have moved around in a tent and in a tabernacle."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In all places in which I have walked with all the children of Israel, did I say a word to anyone from the tribes of Israel whom I commanded to be shepherd of my people Israel, saying, \u2018Why have you not built me a house of cedar?\u2019\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now therefore tell my servant David this: \u2018The LORD of Armies says, \u201cI took you from the sheep pen, from following the sheep, to be prince over my people, over Israel."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I have been with you wherever you went, and have cut off all your enemies from before you. I will make you a great name, like the name of the great ones who are on the earth."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I will appoint a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, that they may dwell in their own place and be moved no more. The children of wickedness will not afflict them any more, as at the first,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and as from the day that I commanded judges to be over my people Israel. I will cause you to rest from all your enemies. Moreover the LORD tells you that the LORD will make you a house."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When your days are fulfilled and you sleep with your fathers, I will set up your offspring after you, who will proceed out of your body, and I will establish his kingdom."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He will build a house for my name, and I will establish the throne of his kingdom forever."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will be his father, and he will be my son. If he commits iniquity, I will chasten him with the rod of men and with the stripes of the children of men;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but my loving kindness will not depart from him, as I took it from Saul, whom I put away before you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Your house and your kingdom will be made sure forever before you. Your throne will be established forever.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Nathan spoke to David all these words, and according to all this vision."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David the king went in and sat before the LORD; and he said, \u201cWho am I, Lord GOD, and what is my house, that you have brought me this far?"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"This was yet a small thing in your eyes, Lord GOD, but you have spoken also of your servant\u2019s house for a great while to come; and this among men, Lord GOD!"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"What more can David say to you? For you know your servant, Lord GOD."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For your word\u2019s sake, and according to your own heart, you have worked all this greatness, to make your servant know it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Therefore you are great, LORD God. For there is no one like you, neither is there any God besides you, according to all that we have heard with our ears."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"What one nation on the earth is like your people, even like Israel, whom God went to redeem to himself for a people, and to make himself a name, and to do great things for you, and awesome things for your land, before your people, whom you redeemed to yourself out of Egypt, from the nations and their gods?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You established for yourself your people Israel to be your people forever; and you, LORD, became their God."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, LORD God, the word that you have spoken concerning your servant, and concerning his house, confirm it forever, and do as you have spoken."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Let your name be magnified forever, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies is God over Israel; and the house of your servant David will be established before you.\u2019"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For you, LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, have revealed to your servant, saying, \u2018I will build you a house.\u2019 Therefore your servant has found in his heart to pray this prayer to you."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, O Lord GOD, you are God, and your words are truth, and you have promised this good thing to your servant."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Now therefore, let it please you to bless the house of your servant, that it may continue forever before you; for you, Lord GOD, have spoken it. Let the house of your servant be blessed forever with your blessing.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, David struck the Philistines and subdued them; and David took the bridle of the mother city out of the hand of the Philistines."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He defeated Moab, and measured them with the line, making them to lie down on the ground; and he measured two lines to put to death, and one full line to keep alive. The Moabites became servants to David, and brought tribute."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David also struck Hadadezer the son of Rehob, king of Zobah, as he went to recover his dominion at the River."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"David took from him one thousand seven hundred horsemen and twenty thousand footmen. David hamstrung the chariot horses, but reserved enough of them for one hundred chariots."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadadezer king of Zobah, David struck twenty two thousand men of the Syrians."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then David put garrisons in Syria of Damascus; and the Syrians became servants to David, and brought tribute. The LORD gave victory to David wherever he went."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"From Betah and from Berothai, cities of Hadadezer, King David took a great quantity of bronze."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When Toi king of Hamath heard that David had struck all the army of Hadadezer,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"then Toi sent Joram his son to King David to greet him and to bless him, because he had fought against Hadadezer and struck him; for Hadadezer had wars with Toi. Joram brought with him vessels of silver, vessels of gold, and vessels of bronze."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"King David also dedicated these to the LORD, with the silver and gold that he dedicated of all the nations which he subdued\u2014"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"of Syria, of Moab, of the children of Ammon, of the Philistines, of Amalek, and of the plunder of Hadadezer, son of Rehob, king of Zobah."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"David earned a reputation when he returned from striking down eighteen thousand men of the Syrians in the Valley of Salt."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He put garrisons in Edom. Throughout all Edom, he put garrisons, and all the Edomites became servants to David. The LORD gave victory to David wherever he went."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"David reigned over all Israel; and David executed justice and righteousness for all his people."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Joab the son of Zeruiah was over the army, Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud was recorder,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Zadok the son of Ahitub and Ahimelech the son of Abiathar were priests, Seraiah was scribe,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and David\u2019s sons were chief ministers."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cIs there yet any who is left of Saul\u2019s house, that I may show him kindness for Jonathan\u2019s sake?\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"There was of Saul\u2019s house a servant whose name was Ziba, and they called him to David; and the king said to him, \u201cAre you Ziba?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am your servant.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cIs there not yet any of Saul\u2019s house, that I may show the kindness of God to him?\u201d"],[0,"Ziba said to the king, \u201cJonathan still has a son, who is lame in his feet.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to him, \u201cWhere is he?\u201d"],[0,"Ziba said to the king, \u201cBehold, he is in the house of Machir the son of Ammiel, in Lo Debar.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then King David sent and brought him out of the house of Machir the son of Ammiel, from Lo Debar."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Mephibosheth, the son of Jonathan, the son of Saul, came to David, fell on his face, and showed respect. David said, \u201cMephibosheth?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cBehold, your servant!\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for I will surely show you kindness for Jonathan your father\u2019s sake, and will restore to you all the land of Saul your father. You will eat bread at my table continually.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He bowed down, and said, \u201cWhat is your servant, that you should look at such a dead dog as I am?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king called to Ziba, Saul\u2019s servant, and said to him, \u201cAll that belonged to Saul and to all his house I have given to your master\u2019s son."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Till the land for him\u2014you, your sons, and your servants. Bring in the harvest, that your master\u2019s son may have bread to eat; but Mephibosheth your master\u2019s son will always eat bread at my table.\u201d"],[0,"Now Ziba had fifteen sons and twenty servants."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then Ziba said to the king, \u201cAccording to all that my lord the king commands his servant, so your servant will do.\u201d So Mephibosheth ate at the king\u2019s table like one of the king\u2019s sons."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Mephibosheth had a young son, whose name was Mica. All who lived in Ziba\u2019s house were servants to Mephibosheth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So Mephibosheth lived in Jerusalem, for he ate continually at the king\u2019s table. He was lame in both his feet."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, the king of the children of Ammon died, and Hanun his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cI will show kindness to Hanun the son of Nahash, as his father showed kindness to me.\u201d So David sent by his servants to comfort him concerning his father. David\u2019s servants came into the land of the children of Ammon."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"But the princes of the children of Ammon said to Hanun their lord, \u201cDo you think that David honors your father, in that he has sent comforters to you? Hasn\u2019t David sent his servants to you to search the city, to spy it out, and to overthrow it?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hanun took David\u2019s servants, shaved off one half of their beards, and cut off their garments in the middle, even to their buttocks, and sent them away."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When they told David this, he sent to meet them, for the men were greatly ashamed. The king said, \u201cWait at Jericho until your beards have grown, and then return.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When the children of Ammon saw that they had become odious to David, the children of Ammon sent and hired the Syrians of Beth Rehob and the Syrians of Zobah, twenty thousand footmen, and the king of Maacah with one thousand men, and the men of Tob twelve thousand men."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When David heard of it, he sent Joab and all the army of the mighty men."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of Ammon came out, and put the battle in array at the entrance of the gate. The Syrians of Zobah and of Rehob and the men of Tob and Maacah were by themselves in the field."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now when Joab saw that the battle was set against him before and behind, he chose of all the choice men of Israel and put them in array against the Syrians."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The rest of the people he committed into the hand of Abishai his brother; and he put them in array against the children of Ammon."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIf the Syrians are too strong for me, then you shall help me; but if the children of Ammon are too strong for you, then I will come and help you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Be courageous, and let\u2019s be strong for our people and for the cities of our God; and may the LORD do what seems good to him.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So Joab and the people who were with him came near to the battle against the Syrians, and they fled before him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When the children of Ammon saw that the Syrians had fled, they likewise fled before Abishai, and entered into the city. Then Joab returned from the children of Ammon and came to Jerusalem."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Syrians saw that they were defeated by Israel, they gathered themselves together."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Hadadezer sent and brought out the Syrians who were beyond the River; and they came to Helam, with Shobach the captain of the army of Hadadezer at their head."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"David was told that; and he gathered all Israel together, passed over the Jordan, and came to Helam. The Syrians set themselves in array against David and fought with him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The Syrians fled before Israel; and David killed seven hundred charioteers of the Syrians and forty thousand horsemen, and struck Shobach the captain of their army, so that he died there."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When all the kings who were servants to Hadadezer saw that they were defeated before Israel, they made peace with Israel and served them. So the Syrians were afraid to help the children of Ammon any more."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At the return of the year, at the time when kings go out, David sent Joab and his servants with him, and all Israel; and they destroyed the children of Ammon and besieged Rabbah. But David stayed at Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"At evening, David arose from his bed and walked on the roof of the king\u2019s house. From the roof, he saw a woman bathing, and the woman was very beautiful to look at."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"David sent and inquired after the woman. One said, \u201cIsn\u2019t this Bathsheba, the daughter of Eliam, Uriah the Hittite\u2019s wife?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"David sent messengers, and took her; and she came in to him, and he lay with her (for she was purified from her uncleanness); and she returned to her house."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The woman conceived; and she sent and told David, and said, \u201cI am with child.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"David sent to Joab, \u201cSend me Uriah the Hittite.\u201d Joab sent Uriah to David."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When Uriah had come to him, David asked him how Joab did, and how the people fared, and how the war prospered."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"David said to Uriah, \u201cGo down to your house and wash your feet.\u201d Uriah departed out of the king\u2019s house, and a gift from the king was sent after him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But Uriah slept at the door of the king\u2019s house with all the servants of his lord, and didn\u2019t go down to his house."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When they had told David, saying, \u201cUriah didn\u2019t go down to his house,\u201d David said to Uriah, \u201cHaven\u2019t you come from a journey? Why didn\u2019t you go down to your house?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Uriah said to David, \u201cThe ark, Israel, and Judah, are staying in tents; and my lord Joab and the servants of my lord are encamped in the open field. Shall I then go into my house to eat and to drink, and to lie with my wife? As you live, and as your soul lives, I will not do this thing!\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Uriah, \u201cStay here today also, and tomorrow I will let you depart.\u201d So Uriah stayed in Jerusalem that day and the next day."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When David had called him, he ate and drank before him; and he made him drunk. At evening, he went out to lie on his bed with the servants of his lord, but didn\u2019t go down to his house."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"In the morning, David wrote a letter to Joab and sent it by the hand of Uriah."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He wrote in the letter, saying, \u201cSend Uriah to the forefront of the hottest battle, and retreat from him, that he may be struck and die.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When Joab kept watch on the city, he assigned Uriah to the place where he knew that valiant men were."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The men of the city went out and fought with Joab. Some of the people fell, even of David\u2019s servants; and Uriah the Hittite died also."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then Joab sent and told David all the things concerning the war;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and he commanded the messenger, saying, \u201cWhen you have finished telling all the things concerning the war to the king,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"it shall be that, if the king\u2019s wrath arise, and he asks you, \u2018Why did you go so near to the city to fight? Didn\u2019t you know that they would shoot from the wall?"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Who struck Abimelech the son of Jerubbesheth? Didn\u2019t a woman cast an upper millstone on him from the wall, so that he died at Thebez? Why did you go so near the wall?\u2019 then you shall say, \u2018Your servant Uriah the Hittite is also dead.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"So the messenger went, and came and showed David all that Joab had sent him for."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The messenger said to David, \u201cThe men prevailed against us, and came out to us into the field; and we were on them even to the entrance of the gate."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The shooters shot at your servants from off the wall; and some of the king\u2019s servants are dead, and your servant Uriah the Hittite is also dead.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said to the messenger, \u201cTell Joab, \u2018Don\u2019t let this thing displease you, for the sword devours one as well as another. Make your battle stronger against the city, and overthrow it.\u2019 Encourage him.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"When Uriah\u2019s wife heard that Uriah her husband was dead, she mourned for her husband."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When the mourning was past, David sent and took her home to his house, and she became his wife and bore him a son. But the thing that David had done displeased the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD sent Nathan to David. He came to him, and said to him, \u201cThere were two men in one city: the one rich, and the other poor."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The rich man had very many flocks and herds,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"but the poor man had nothing, except one little ewe lamb, which he had bought and raised. It grew up together with him and with his children. It ate of his own food, drank of his own cup, and lay in his bosom, and was like a daughter to him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"A traveler came to the rich man, and he didn\u2019t want to take of his own flock and of his own herd to prepare for the wayfaring man who had come to him, but took the poor man\u2019s lamb and prepared it for the man who had come to him.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"David\u2019s anger burned hot against the man, and he said to Nathan, \u201cAs the LORD lives, the man who has done this deserves to die!"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He must restore the lamb fourfold, because he did this thing and because he had no pity!\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Nathan said to David, \u201cYou are the man! This is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: \u2018I anointed you king over Israel, and I delivered you out of the hand of Saul."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I gave you your master\u2019s house and your master\u2019s wives into your bosom, and gave you the house of Israel and of Judah; and if that would have been too little, I would have added to you many more such things."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Why have you despised the LORD\u2019s word, to do that which is evil in his sight? You have struck Uriah the Hittite with the sword, have taken his wife to be your wife, and have slain him with the sword of the children of Ammon."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now therefore the sword will never depart from your house, because you have despised me and have taken Uriah the Hittite\u2019s wife to be your wife.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is what the LORD says: \u2018Behold, I will raise up evil against you out of your own house; and I will take your wives before your eyes and give them to your neighbor, and he will lie with your wives in the sight of this sun."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For you did this secretly, but I will do this thing before all Israel, and before the sun.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Nathan, \u201cI have sinned against the LORD.\u201d"],[0,"Nathan said to David, \u201cThe LORD also has put away your sin. You will not die."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"However, because by this deed you have given great occasion to the LORD\u2019s enemies to blaspheme, the child also who is born to you will surely die.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then Nathan departed to his house."],[0,"The LORD struck the child that Uriah\u2019s wife bore to David, and he was very sick."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"David therefore begged God for the child; and David fasted, and went in and lay all night on the ground."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The elders of his house arose beside him, to raise him up from the earth; but he would not, and he didn\u2019t eat bread with them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"On the seventh day, the child died. David\u2019s servants were afraid to tell him that the child was dead, for they said, \u201cBehold, while the child was yet alive, we spoke to him and he didn\u2019t listen to our voice. How will he then harm himself if we tell him that the child is dead?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But when David saw that his servants were whispering together, David perceived that the child was dead; and David said to his servants, \u201cIs the child dead?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cHe is dead.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David arose from the earth, and washed and anointed himself, and changed his clothing; and he came into the LORD\u2019s house, and worshiped. Then he came to his own house; and when he requested, they set bread before him and he ate."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then his servants said to him, \u201cWhat is this that you have done? You fasted and wept for the child while he was alive, but when the child was dead, you rose up and ate bread.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhile the child was yet alive, I fasted and wept; for I said, \u2018Who knows whether the LORD will not be gracious to me, that the child may live?\u2019"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But now he is dead. Why should I fast? Can I bring him back again? I will go to him, but he will not return to me.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"David comforted Bathsheba his wife, and went in to her, and lay with her. She bore a son, and he called his name Solomon. The LORD loved him;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and he sent by the hand of Nathan the prophet, and he named him Jedidiah, for the LORD\u2019s sake."]],f:["\u201cJedidiah\u201d means \u201cloved by the LORD\u201d."]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Joab fought against Rabbah of the children of Ammon, and took the royal city."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Joab sent messengers to David, and said, \u201cI have fought against Rabbah. Yes, I have taken the city of waters."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Now therefore gather the rest of the people together, and encamp against the city and take it; lest I take the city, and it be called by my name.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"David gathered all the people together and went to Rabbah, and fought against it and took it."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He took the crown of their king from off his head; and its weight was a talent of gold, and in it were precious stones; and it was set on David\u2019s head. He brought a great quantity of plunder out of the city."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He brought out the people who were in it, and put them to work under saws, under iron picks, under axes of iron, and made them go to the brick kiln; and he did so to all the cities of the children of Ammon. Then David and all the people returned to Jerusalem."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Absalom the son of David had a beautiful sister, whose name was Tamar; and Amnon the son of David loved her."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Amnon was so troubled that he became sick because of his sister Tamar, for she was a virgin, and it seemed hard to Amnon to do anything to her."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But Amnon had a friend whose name was Jonadab the son of Shimeah, David\u2019s brother; and Jonadab was a very subtle man."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cWhy, son of the king, are you so sad from day to day? Won\u2019t you tell me?\u201d"],[0,"Amnon said to him, \u201cI love Tamar, my brother Absalom\u2019s sister.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonadab said to him, \u201cLay down on your bed and pretend to be sick. When your father comes to see you, tell him, \u2018Please let my sister Tamar come and give me bread to eat, and prepare the food in my sight, that I may see it and eat it from her hand.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"So Amnon lay down and faked being sick. When the king came to see him, Amnon said to the king, \u201cPlease let my sister Tamar come and make me a couple of cakes in my sight, that I may eat from her hand.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David sent home to Tamar, saying, \u201cGo now to your brother Amnon\u2019s house, and prepare food for him.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So Tamar went to her brother Amnon\u2019s house; and he was lying down. She took dough, kneaded it, made cakes in his sight, and baked the cakes."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"She took the pan and poured them out before him, but he refused to eat. Amnon said, \u201cHave all men leave me.\u201d Then every man went out from him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Amnon said to Tamar, \u201cBring the food into the room, that I may eat from your hand.\u201d Tamar took the cakes which she had made, and brought them into the room to Amnon her brother."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When she had brought them near to him to eat, he took hold of her and said to her, \u201cCome, lie with me, my sister!\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"She answered him, \u201cNo, my brother, do not force me! For no such thing ought to be done in Israel. Don\u2019t you do this folly!"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"As for me, where would I carry my shame? And as for you, you will be as one of the fools in Israel. Now therefore, please speak to the king; for he will not withhold me from you.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"However, he would not listen to her voice; but being stronger than she, he forced her and lay with her."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then Amnon hated her with exceedingly great hatred; for the hatred with which he hated her was greater than the love with which he had loved her. Amnon said to her, \u201cArise, be gone!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to him, \u201cNot so, because this great wrong in sending me away is worse than the other that you did to me!\u201d"],[0,"But he would not listen to her."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then he called his servant who ministered to him, and said, \u201cNow put this woman out from me, and bolt the door after her.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"She had a garment of various colors on her, for the king\u2019s daughters who were virgins dressed in such robes. Then his servant brought her out and bolted the door after her."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Tamar put ashes on her head, and tore her garment of various colors that was on her; and she laid her hand on her head and went her way, crying aloud as she went."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Absalom her brother said to her, \u201cHas Amnon your brother been with you? But now hold your peace, my sister. He is your brother. Don\u2019t take this thing to heart.\u201d"],[0,"So Tamar remained desolate in her brother Absalom\u2019s house."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But when King David heard of all these things, he was very angry."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Absalom spoke to Amnon neither good nor bad; for Absalom hated Amnon, because he had forced his sister Tamar."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"After two full years, Absalom had sheep shearers in Baal Hazor, which is beside Ephraim; and Absalom invited all the king\u2019s sons."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Absalom came to the king and said, \u201cSee now, your servant has sheep shearers. Please let the king and his servants go with your servant.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to Absalom, \u201cNo, my son, let\u2019s not all go, lest we be burdensome to you.\u201d He pressed him; however he would not go, but blessed him."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Absalom said, \u201cIf not, please let my brother Amnon go with us.\u201d"],[0,"The king said to him, \u201cWhy should he go with you?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But Absalom pressed him, and he let Amnon and all the king\u2019s sons go with him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Absalom commanded his servants, saying, \u201cMark now, when Amnon\u2019s heart is merry with wine; and when I tell you, \u2018Strike Amnon,\u2019 then kill him. Don\u2019t be afraid. Haven\u2019t I commanded you? Be courageous, and be valiant!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The servants of Absalom did to Amnon as Absalom had commanded. Then all the king\u2019s sons arose, and every man got up on his mule and fled."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"While they were on the way, the news came to David, saying, \u201cAbsalom has slain all the king\u2019s sons, and there is not one of them left!\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king arose, and tore his garments, and lay on the earth; and all his servants stood by with their clothes torn."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Jonadab the son of Shimeah, David\u2019s brother, answered, \u201cDon\u2019t let my lord suppose that they have killed all the young men, the king\u2019s sons, for Amnon only is dead; for by the appointment of Absalom this has been determined from the day that he forced his sister Tamar."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Now therefore don\u2019t let my lord the king take the thing to his heart, to think that all the king\u2019s sons are dead; for only Amnon is dead.\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But Absalom fled. The young man who kept the watch lifted up his eyes and looked, and behold, many people were coming by way of the hillside behind him."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Jonadab said to the king, \u201cBehold, the king\u2019s sons are coming! It is as your servant said.\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"As soon as he had finished speaking, behold, the king\u2019s sons came, and lifted up their voices and wept. The king also and all his servants wept bitterly."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"But Absalom fled and went to Talmai the son of Ammihur, king of Geshur. David mourned for his son every day."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"So Absalom fled and went to Geshur, and was there three years."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"King David longed to go out to Absalom, for he was comforted concerning Amnon, since he was dead."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Joab the son of Zeruiah perceived that the king\u2019s heart was toward Absalom."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Joab sent to Tekoa and brought a wise woman from there, and said to her, \u201cPlease act like a mourner, and put on mourning clothing, please, and don\u2019t anoint yourself with oil; but be as a woman who has mourned a long time for the dead."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Go in to the king and speak like this to him.\u201d So Joab put the words in her mouth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When the woman of Tekoa spoke to the king, she fell on her face to the ground, showed respect, and said, \u201cHelp, O king!\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to her, \u201cWhat ails you?\u201d"],[0,"She answered, \u201cTruly I am a widow, and my husband is dead."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Your servant had two sons; and they both fought together in the field, and there was no one to part them, but the one struck the other and killed him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Behold, the whole family has risen against your servant, and they say, \u2018Deliver him who struck his brother, that we may kill him for the life of his brother whom he killed, and so destroy the heir also.\u2019 Thus they would quench my coal which is left, and would leave to my husband neither name nor remainder on the surface of the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to the woman, \u201cGo to your house, and I will give a command concerning you.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman of Tekoa said to the king, \u201cMy lord, O king, may the iniquity be on me, and on my father\u2019s house; and may the king and his throne be guiltless.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cWhoever says anything to you, bring him to me, and he will not bother you any more.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she said, \u201cPlease let the king remember the LORD your God, that the avenger of blood destroy not any more, lest they destroy my son.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, not one hair of your son shall fall to the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the woman said, \u201cPlease let your servant speak a word to my lord the king.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cSay on.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said, \u201cWhy then have you devised such a thing against the people of God? For in speaking this word the king is as one who is guilty, in that the king does not bring home again his banished one."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For we must die, and are like water spilled on the ground, which can\u2019t be gathered up again; neither does God take away life, but devises means, that he who is banished not be an outcast from him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now therefore, seeing that I have come to speak this word to my lord the king, it is because the people have made me afraid. Your servant said, \u2018I will now speak to the king; it may be that the king will perform the request of his servant.\u2019"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For the king will hear, to deliver his servant out of the hand of the man who would destroy me and my son together out of the inheritance of God."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then your servant said, \u2018Please let the word of my lord the king bring rest; for as an angel of God, so is my lord the king to discern good and bad. May the LORD, your God, be with you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king answered the woman, \u201cPlease don\u2019t hide anything from me that I ask you.\u201d"],[0,"The woman said, \u201cLet my lord the king now speak.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cIs the hand of Joab with you in all this?\u201d"],[0,"The woman answered, \u201cAs your soul lives, my lord the king, no one can turn to the right hand or to the left from anything that my lord the king has spoken; for your servant Joab urged me, and he put all these words in the mouth of your servant."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Your servant Joab has done this thing to change the face of the matter. My lord is wise, according to the wisdom of an angel of God, to know all things that are on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to Joab, \u201cBehold now, I have granted this thing. Go therefore, and bring the young man Absalom back.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab fell to the ground on his face, showed respect, and blessed the king. Joab said, \u201cToday your servant knows that I have found favor in your sight, my lord, O king, in that the king has performed the request of his servant.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joab arose and went to Geshur, and brought Absalom to Jerusalem."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cLet him return to his own house, but let him not see my face.\u201d So Absalom returned to his own house, and didn\u2019t see the king\u2019s face."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now in all Israel there was no one to be so much praised as Absalom for his beauty. From the sole of his foot even to the crown of his head there was no defect in him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When he cut the hair of his head (now it was at every year\u2019s end that he cut it; because it was heavy on him, therefore he cut it), he weighed the hair of his head at two hundred shekels, after the king\u2019s weight."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 200 shekels is about 2 kilograms or about 4.4 pounds."]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Three sons were born to Absalom, and one daughter, whose name was Tamar. She was a woman with a beautiful face."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Absalom lived two full years in Jerusalem, and he didn\u2019t see the king\u2019s face."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Then Absalom sent for Joab, to send him to the king, but he would not come to him. Then he sent again a second time, but he would not come."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Therefore he said to his servants, \u201cBehold, Joab\u2019s field is near mine, and he has barley there. Go and set it on fire.\u201d So Absalom\u2019s servants set the field on fire."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joab arose and came to Absalom to his house, and said to him, \u201cWhy have your servants set my field on fire?\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Absalom answered Joab, \u201cBehold, I sent to you, saying, \u2018Come here, that I may send you to the king, to say, \u201cWhy have I come from Geshur? It would be better for me to be there still. Now therefore, let me see the king\u2019s face; and if there is iniquity in me, let him kill me.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joab came to the king and told him; and when he had called for Absalom, he came to the king and bowed himself on his face to the ground before the king; and the king kissed Absalom."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Absalom prepared a chariot and horses for himself, and fifty men to run before him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Absalom rose up early, and stood beside the way of the gate. When any man had a suit which should come to the king for judgment, then Absalom called to him, and said, \u201cWhat city are you from?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cYour servant is of one of the tribes of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Absalom said to him, \u201cBehold, your matters are good and right; but there is no man deputized by the king to hear you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Absalom said moreover, \u201cOh that I were made judge in the land, that every man who has any suit or cause might come to me, and I would do him justice!\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It was so, that when any man came near to bow down to him, he stretched out his hand, took hold of him, and kissed him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Absalom did this sort of thing to all Israel who came to the king for judgment. So Absalom stole the hearts of the men of Israel."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of forty years, Absalom said to the king, \u201cPlease let me go and pay my vow, which I have vowed to the LORD, in Hebron."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For your servant vowed a vow while I stayed at Geshur in Syria, saying, \u2018If the LORD shall indeed bring me again to Jerusalem, then I will serve the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to him, \u201cGo in peace.\u201d"],[0,"So he arose and went to Hebron."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But Absalom sent spies throughout all the tribes of Israel, saying, \u201cAs soon as you hear the sound of the trumpet, then you shall say, \u2018Absalom is king in Hebron!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Two hundred men went with Absalom out of Jerusalem, who were invited, and went in their simplicity; and they didn\u2019t know anything."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Absalom sent for Ahithophel the Gilonite, David\u2019s counselor, from his city, even from Giloh, while he was offering the sacrifices. The conspiracy was strong, for the people increased continually with Absalom."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"A messenger came to David, saying, \u201cThe hearts of the men of Israel are after Absalom.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to all his servants who were with him at Jerusalem, \u201cArise! Let\u2019s flee, or else none of us will escape from Absalom. Hurry to depart, lest he overtake us quickly and bring down evil on us, and strike the city with the edge of the sword.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The king\u2019s servants said to the king, \u201cBehold, your servants are ready to do whatever my lord the king chooses.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The king went out, and all his household after him. The king left ten women, who were concubines, to keep the house."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The king went out, and all the people after him; and they stayed in Beth Merhak."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All his servants passed on beside him; and all the Cherethites, and all the Pelethites, and all the Gittites, six hundred men who came after him from Gath, passed on before the king."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said to Ittai the Gittite, \u201cWhy do you also go with us? Return, and stay with the king; for you are a foreigner and also an exile. Return to your own place."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Whereas you came but yesterday, should I today make you go up and down with us, since I go where I may? Return, and take back your brothers. Mercy and truth be with you.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Ittai answered the king and said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, and as my lord the king lives, surely in what place my lord the king is, whether for death or for life, your servant will be there also.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Ittai, \u201cGo and pass over.\u201d Ittai the Gittite passed over, and all his men, and all the little ones who were with him."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"All the country wept with a loud voice, and all the people passed over. The king also himself passed over the brook Kidron, and all the people passed over toward the way of the wilderness."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Behold, Zadok also came, and all the Levites with him, bearing the ark of the covenant of God; and they set down God\u2019s ark; and Abiathar went up until all the people finished passing out of the city."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The king said to Zadok, \u201cCarry God\u2019s ark back into the city. If I find favor in the LORD\u2019s eyes, he will bring me again, and show me both it and his habitation;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"but if he says, \u2018I have no delight in you,\u2019 behold, here I am. Let him do to me as seems good to him.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The king said also to Zadok the priest, \u201cAren\u2019t you a seer? Return into the city in peace, and your two sons with you, Ahimaaz your son and Jonathan the son of Abiathar."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Behold, I will stay at the fords of the wilderness until word comes from you to inform me.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Zadok therefore and Abiathar carried God\u2019s ark to Jerusalem again; and they stayed there."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"David went up by the ascent of the Mount of Olives, and wept as he went up; and he had his head covered and went barefoot. All the people who were with him each covered his head, and they went up, weeping as they went up."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Someone told David, saying, \u201cAhithophel is among the conspirators with Absalom.\u201d"],[0,"David said, \u201cLORD, please turn the counsel of Ahithophel into foolishness.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"When David had come to the top, where God was worshiped, behold, Hushai the Archite came to meet him with his tunic torn and earth on his head."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"David said to him, \u201cIf you pass on with me, then you will be a burden to me;"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"but if you return to the city, and tell Absalom, \u2018I will be your servant, O king. As I have been your father\u2019s servant in time past, so I will now be your servant; then you will defeat for me the counsel of Ahithophel.\u2019"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you have Zadok and Abiathar the priests there with you? Therefore whatever you hear out of the king\u2019s house, tell it to Zadok and Abiathar the priests."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Behold, they have there with them their two sons, Ahimaaz, Zadok\u2019s son, and Jonathan, Abiathar\u2019s son. Send to me everything that you shall hear by them.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hushai, David\u2019s friend, came into the city; and Absalom came into Jerusalem."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When David was a little past the top, behold, Ziba the servant of Mephibosheth met him with a couple of donkeys saddled, and on them two hundred loaves of bread, and one hundred clusters of raisins, and one hundred summer fruits, and a container of wine."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The king said to Ziba, \u201cWhat do you mean by these?\u201d"],[0,"Ziba said, \u201cThe donkeys are for the king\u2019s household to ride on; and the bread and summer fruit for the young men to eat; and the wine, that those who are faint in the wilderness may drink.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cWhere is your master\u2019s son?\u201d"],[0,"Ziba said to the king, \u201cBehold, he is staying in Jerusalem; for he said, \u2018Today the house of Israel will restore me the kingdom of my father.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said to Ziba, \u201cBehold, all that belongs to Mephibosheth is yours.\u201d"],[0,"Ziba said, \u201cI bow down. Let me find favor in your sight, my lord, O king.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When King David came to Bahurim, behold, a man of the family of Saul\u2019s house came out, whose name was Shimei, the son of Gera. He came out and cursed as he came."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He cast stones at David and at all the servants of King David, and all the people and all the mighty men were on his right hand and on his left."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Shimei said when he cursed, \u201cBe gone, be gone, you man of blood, and wicked fellow!"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD has returned on you all the blood of Saul\u2019s house, in whose place you have reigned! The LORD has delivered the kingdom into the hand of Absalom your son! Behold, you are caught by your own mischief, because you are a man of blood!\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Abishai the son of Zeruiah said to the king, \u201cWhy should this dead dog curse my lord the king? Please let me go over and take off his head.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cWhat have I to do with you, you sons of Zeruiah? Because he curses, and because the LORD has said to him, \u2018Curse David,\u2019 who then shall say, \u2018Why have you done so?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Abishai and to all his servants, \u201cBehold, my son, who came out of my bowels, seeks my life. How much more this Benjamite, now? Leave him alone, and let him curse; for the LORD has invited him."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It may be that the LORD will look on the wrong done to me, and that the LORD will repay me good for the cursing of me today.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So David and his men went by the way; and Shimei went along on the hillside opposite him and cursed as he went, threw stones at him, and threw dust."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The king and all the people who were with him arrived weary; and he refreshed himself there."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Absalom and all the people, the men of Israel, came to Jerusalem, and Ahithophel with him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When Hushai the Archite, David\u2019s friend, had come to Absalom, Hushai said to Absalom, \u201cLong live the king! Long live the king!\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Absalom said to Hushai, \u201cIs this your kindness to your friend? Why didn\u2019t you go with your friend?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Hushai said to Absalom, \u201cNo; but whomever the LORD and this people and all the men of Israel have chosen, I will be his, and I will stay with him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Again, whom should I serve? Shouldn\u2019t I serve in the presence of his son? As I have served in your father\u2019s presence, so I will be in your presence.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Absalom said to Ahithophel, \u201cGive your counsel what we shall do.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahithophel said to Absalom, \u201cGo in to your father\u2019s concubines that he has left to keep the house. Then all Israel will hear that you are abhorred by your father. Then the hands of all who are with you will be strong.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"So they spread a tent for Absalom on the top of the house, and Absalom went in to his father\u2019s concubines in the sight of all Israel."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The counsel of Ahithophel, which he gave in those days, was as if a man inquired at the inner sanctuary of God. All the counsel of Ahithophel was like this both with David and with Absalom."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Ahithophel said to Absalom, \u201cLet me now choose twelve thousand men, and I will arise and pursue after David tonight."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will come on him while he is weary and exhausted, and will make him afraid. All the people who are with him will flee. I will strike the king only,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and I will bring back all the people to you. The man whom you seek is as if all returned. All the people shall be in peace.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The saying pleased Absalom well, and all the elders of Israel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then Absalom said, \u201cNow call Hushai the Archite also, and let\u2019s hear likewise what he says.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When Hushai had come to Absalom, Absalom spoke to him, saying, \u201cAhithophel has spoken like this. Shall we do what he says? If not, speak up.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Hushai said to Absalom, \u201cThe counsel that Ahithophel has given this time is not good.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Hushai said moreover, \u201cYou know your father and his men, that they are mighty men, and they are fierce in their minds, like a bear robbed of her cubs in the field. Your father is a man of war, and will not lodge with the people."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Behold, he is now hidden in some pit, or in some other place. It will happen, when some of them have fallen at the first, that whoever hears it will say, \u2018There is a slaughter among the people who follow Absalom!\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Even he who is valiant, whose heart is as the heart of a lion, will utterly melt; for all Israel knows that your father is a mighty man, and those who are with him are valiant men."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But I counsel that all Israel be gathered together to you, from Dan even to Beersheba, as the sand that is by the sea for multitude; and that you go to battle in your own person."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So we will come on him in some place where he will be found, and we will light on him as the dew falls on the ground, then we will not leave so much as one of him and of all the men who are with him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Moreover, if he has gone into a city, then all Israel will bring ropes to that city, and we will draw it into the river, until there isn\u2019t one small stone found there.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Absalom and all the men of Israel said, \u201cThe counsel of Hushai the Archite is better than the counsel of Ahithophel.\u201d For the LORD had ordained to defeat the good counsel of Ahithophel, to the intent that the LORD might bring evil on Absalom."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hushai said to Zadok and to Abiathar the priests, \u201cAhithophel counseled Absalom and the elders of Israel that way; and I have counseled this way."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Now therefore send quickly, and tell David, saying, \u2018Don\u2019t lodge tonight at the fords of the wilderness, but by all means pass over, lest the king be swallowed up, and all the people who are with him.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jonathan and Ahimaaz were staying by En Rogel; and a female servant used to go and report to them, and they went and told King David; for they couldn\u2019t risk being seen coming into the city."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But a boy saw them, and told Absalom. Then they both went away quickly and came to the house of a man in Bahurim, who had a well in his court; and they went down there."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The woman took and spread the covering over the well\u2019s mouth, and spread out crushed grain on it; and nothing was known."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Absalom\u2019s servants came to the woman to the house; and they said, \u201cWhere are Ahimaaz and Jonathan?\u201d"],[0,"The woman said to them, \u201cThey have gone over the brook of water.\u201d"],[0,"When they had sought and could not find them, they returned to Jerusalem."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"After they had departed, they came up out of the well and went and told King David; and they said to David, \u201cArise and pass quickly over the water; for thus has Ahithophel counseled against you.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David arose, and all the people who were with him, and they passed over the Jordan. By the morning light there lacked not one of them who had not gone over the Jordan."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"When Ahithophel saw that his counsel was not followed, he saddled his donkey, arose, and went home to his city, set his house in order, and hanged himself; and he died, and was buried in the tomb of his father."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David came to Mahanaim. Absalom passed over the Jordan, he and all the men of Israel with him."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Absalom set Amasa over the army instead of Joab. Now Amasa was the son of a man whose name was Ithra the Israelite, who went in to Abigail the daughter of Nahash, sister to Zeruiah, Joab\u2019s mother."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Israel and Absalom encamped in the land of Gilead."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"When David had come to Mahanaim, Shobi the son of Nahash of Rabbah of the children of Ammon, and Machir the son of Ammiel of Lodebar, and Barzillai the Gileadite of Rogelim,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"brought beds, basins, earthen vessels, wheat, barley, meal, parched grain, beans, lentils, roasted grain,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"honey, butter, sheep, and cheese of the herd, for David and for the people who were with him to eat; for they said, \u201cThe people are hungry, weary, and thirsty in the wilderness.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David counted the people who were with him, and set captains of thousands and captains of hundreds over them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David sent the people out, a third part under the hand of Joab, and a third part under the hand of Abishai the son of Zeruiah, Joab\u2019s brother, and a third part under the hand of Ittai the Gittite. The king said to the people, \u201cI will also surely go out with you myself.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"But the people said, \u201cYou shall not go out, for if we flee away, they will not care for us, neither if half of us die, will they care for us. But you are worth ten thousand of us. Therefore now it is better that you are ready to help us out of the city.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to them, \u201cI will do what seems best to you.\u201d"],[0,"The king stood beside the gate, and all the people went out by hundreds and by thousands."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The king commanded Joab and Abishai and Ittai, saying, \u201cDeal gently for my sake with the young man Absalom.\u201d All the people heard when the king commanded all the captains concerning Absalom."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"So the people went out into the field against Israel; and the battle was in the forest of Ephraim."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The people of Israel were struck there before David\u2019s servants, and there was a great slaughter there that day of twenty thousand men."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the battle was there spread over the surface of all the country, and the forest devoured more people that day than the sword devoured."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Absalom happened to meet David\u2019s servants. Absalom was riding on his mule, and the mule went under the thick boughs of a great oak; and his head caught hold of the oak, and he was hanging between the sky and earth; and the mule that was under him went on."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"A certain man saw it, and told Joab, and said, \u201cBehold, I saw Absalom hanging in an oak.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab said to the man who told him, \u201cBehold, you saw it, and why didn\u2019t you strike him there to the ground? I would have given you ten pieces of silver and a sash.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The man said to Joab, \u201cThough I should receive a thousand pieces of silver in my hand, I still wouldn\u2019t stretch out my hand against the king\u2019s son; for in our hearing the king commanded you and Abishai and Ittai, saying, \u2018Beware that no one touch the young man Absalom.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Otherwise, if I had dealt falsely against his life (and there is no matter hidden from the king), then you yourself would have set yourself against me.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joab said, \u201cI\u2019m not going to wait like this with you.\u201d He took three darts in his hand and thrust them through Absalom\u2019s heart while he was still alive in the middle of the oak."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Ten young men who bore Joab\u2019s armor surrounded and struck Absalom, and killed him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Joab blew the trumpet, and the people returned from pursuing after Israel; for Joab held the people back."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They took Absalom and cast him into a great pit in the forest, and raised over him a very great heap of stones. Then all Israel fled, each to his own tent."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Absalom in his lifetime had taken and reared up for himself the pillar which is in the king\u2019s valley, for he said, \u201cI have no son to keep my name in memory.\u201d He called the pillar after his own name. It is called Absalom\u2019s monument, to this day."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Ahimaaz the son of Zadok said, \u201cLet me now run and carry the king news, how the LORD has avenged him of his enemies.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab said to him, \u201cYou must not be the bearer of news today, but you must carry news another day. But today you must carry no news, because the king\u2019s son is dead.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Joab said to the Cushite, \u201cGo, tell the king what you have seen!\u201d The Cushite bowed himself to Joab, and ran."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Ahimaaz the son of Zadok said yet again to Joab, \u201cBut come what may, please let me also run after the Cushite.\u201d"],[0,"Joab said, \u201cWhy do you want to run, my son, since you will have no reward for the news?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut come what may,\u201d he said, \u201cI will run.\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cRun!\u201d Then Ahimaaz ran by the way of the Plain, and outran the Cushite."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Now David was sitting between the two gates; and the watchman went up to the roof of the gate to the wall, and lifted up his eyes and looked, and, behold, a man running alone."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The watchman shouted and told the king. The king said, \u201cIf he is alone, there is news in his mouth.\u201d He came closer and closer."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The watchman saw another man running; and the watchman called to the gatekeeper and said, \u201cBehold, a man running alone!\u201d"],[0,"The king said, \u201cHe also brings news.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"The watchman said, \u201cI think the running of the first one is like the running of Ahimaaz the son of Zadok.\u201d"],[0,"The king said, \u201cHe is a good man, and comes with good news.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahimaaz called, and said to the king, \u201cAll is well.\u201d He bowed himself before the king with his face to the earth, and said, \u201cBlessed is the LORD your God, who has delivered up the men who lifted up their hand against my lord the king!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cIs it well with the young man Absalom?\u201d"],[0,"Ahimaaz answered, \u201cWhen Joab sent the king\u2019s servant, even me your servant, I saw a great tumult, but I don\u2019t know what it was.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cCome and stand here.\u201d He came and stood still."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the Cushite came. The Cushite said, \u201cGood news for my lord the king, for the LORD has avenged you today of all those who rose up against you.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to the Cushite, \u201cIs it well with the young man Absalom?\u201d"],[0,"The Cushite answered, \u201cMay the enemies of my lord the king, and all who rise up against you to do you harm, be as that young man is.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The king was much moved, and went up to the room over the gate and wept. As he went, he said, \u201cMy son Absalom! My son, my son Absalom! I wish I had died instead of you, Absalom, my son, my son!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab was told, \u201cBehold, the king weeps and mourns for Absalom.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The victory that day was turned into mourning among all the people, for the people heard it said that day, \u201cThe king grieves for his son.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The people sneaked into the city that day, as people who are ashamed steal away when they flee in battle."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The king covered his face, and the king cried with a loud voice, \u201cMy son Absalom, Absalom, my son, my son!\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab came into the house to the king, and said, \u201cToday you have shamed the faces of all your servants who today have saved your life, and the lives of your sons and of your daughters, and the lives of your wives, and the lives of your concubines;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"in that you love those who hate you and hate those who love you. For you have declared today that princes and servants are nothing to you. For today I perceive that if Absalom had lived and we had all died today, then it would have pleased you well."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now therefore arise, go out and speak to comfort your servants; for I swear by the LORD, if you don\u2019t go out, not a man will stay with you this night. That would be worse to you than all the evil that has happened to you from your youth until now.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king arose and sat in the gate. The people were all told, \u201cBehold, the king is sitting in the gate.\u201d All the people came before the king. Now Israel had fled every man to his tent."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"All the people were at strife throughout all the tribes of Israel, saying, \u201cThe king delivered us out of the hand of our enemies, and he saved us out of the hand of the Philistines; and now he has fled out of the land from Absalom."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Absalom, whom we anointed over us, is dead in battle. Now therefore why don\u2019t you speak a word of bringing the king back?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"King David sent to Zadok and to Abiathar the priests, saying, \u201cSpeak to the elders of Judah, saying, \u2018Why are you the last to bring the king back to his house, since the speech of all Israel has come to the king, to return him to his house?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You are my brothers. You are my bone and my flesh. Why then are you the last to bring back the king?\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Say to Amasa, \u2018Aren\u2019t you my bone and my flesh? God do so to me, and more also, if you aren\u2019t captain of the army before me continually instead of Joab.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He bowed the heart of all the men of Judah, even as one man, so that they sent to the king, saying, \u201cReturn, you and all your servants.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king returned, and came to the Jordan. Judah came to Gilgal, to go to meet the king, to bring the king over the Jordan."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Shimei the son of Gera, the Benjamite, who was of Bahurim, hurried and came down with the men of Judah to meet King David."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"There were a thousand men of Benjamin with him, and Ziba the servant of Saul\u2019s house, and his fifteen sons and his twenty servants with him; and they went through the Jordan in the presence of the king."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"A ferry boat went to bring over the king\u2019s household, and to do what he thought good."],[0,"Shimei the son of Gera fell down before the king when he had come over the Jordan."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He said to the king, \u201cDon\u2019t let my lord impute iniquity to me, or remember that which your servant did perversely the day that my lord the king went out of Jerusalem, that the king should take it to his heart."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For your servant knows that I have sinned. Therefore behold, I have come today as the first of all the house of Joseph to go down to meet my lord the king.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"But Abishai the son of Zeruiah answered, \u201cShouldn\u2019t Shimei be put to death for this, because he cursed the LORD\u2019s anointed?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cWhat have I to do with you, you sons of Zeruiah, that you should be adversaries to me today? Shall any man be put to death today in Israel? For don\u2019t I know that I am king over Israel today?\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The king said to Shimei, \u201cYou will not die.\u201d The king swore to him."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Mephibosheth the son of Saul came down to meet the king; and he had neither groomed his feet, nor trimmed his beard, nor washed his clothes, from the day the king departed until the day he came home in peace."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When he had come to Jerusalem to meet the king, the king said to him, \u201cWhy didn\u2019t you go with me, Mephibosheth?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cMy lord, O king, my servant deceived me. For your servant said, \u2018I will saddle a donkey for myself, that I may ride on it and go with the king,\u2019 because your servant is lame."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He has slandered your servant to my lord the king, but my lord the king is as an angel of God. Therefore do what is good in your eyes."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For all my father\u2019s house were but dead men before my lord the king; yet you set your servant among those who ate at your own table. What right therefore have I yet that I should appeal any more to the king?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to him, \u201cWhy do you speak any more of your matters? I say, you and Ziba divide the land.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Mephibosheth said to the king, \u201cYes, let him take all, because my lord the king has come in peace to his own house.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Barzillai the Gileadite came down from Rogelim; and he went over the Jordan with the king to conduct him over the Jordan."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Now Barzillai was a very aged man, even eighty years old. He had provided the king with sustenance while he stayed at Mahanaim, for he was a very great man."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The king said to Barzillai, \u201cCome over with me, and I will sustain you with me in Jerusalem.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Barzillai said to the king, \u201cHow many are the days of the years of my life, that I should go up with the king to Jerusalem?"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"I am eighty years old, today. Can I discern between good and bad? Can your servant taste what I eat or what I drink? Can I hear the voice of singing men and singing women any more? Why then should your servant be a burden to my lord the king?"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Your servant will just go over the Jordan with the king. Why should the king repay me with such a reward?"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Please let your servant turn back again, that I may die in my own city, by the grave of my father and my mother. But behold, your servant Chimham; let him go over with my lord the king; and do to him what shall seem good to you.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"The king answered, \u201cChimham shall go over with me, and I will do to him that which shall seem good to you. Whatever you request of me, that I will do for you.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people went over the Jordan, and the king went over. Then the king kissed Barzillai and blessed him; and he returned to his own place."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"So the king went over to Gilgal, and Chimham went over with him. All the people of Judah brought the king over, and also half the people of Israel."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Behold, all the men of Israel came to the king, and said to the king, \u201cWhy have our brothers the men of Judah stolen you away, and brought the king and his household, over the Jordan, and all David\u2019s men with him?\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"All the men of Judah answered the men of Israel, \u201cBecause the king is a close relative to us. Why then are you angry about this matter? Have we eaten at all at the king\u2019s cost? Or has he given us any gift?\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of Israel answered the men of Judah, and said, \u201cWe have ten parts in the king, and we have also more claim to David than you. Why then did you despise us, that our advice should not be first had in bringing back our king?\u201d The words of the men of Judah were fiercer than the words of the men of Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"There happened to be there a wicked fellow, whose name was Sheba the son of Bichri, a Benjamite; and he blew the trumpet, and said, \u201cWe have no portion in David, neither have we inheritance in the son of Jesse. Every man to his tents, Israel!\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"So all the men of Israel went up from following David, and followed Sheba the son of Bichri; but the men of Judah joined with their king, from the Jordan even to Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David came to his house at Jerusalem; and the king took the ten women his concubines, whom he had left to keep the house, and put them in custody and provided them with sustenance, but didn\u2019t go in to them. So they were shut up to the day of their death, living in widowhood."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said to Amasa, \u201cCall me the men of Judah together within three days, and be here present.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"So Amasa went to call the men of Judah together, but he stayed longer than the set time which had been appointed to him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"David said to Abishai, \u201cNow Sheba the son of Bichri will do us more harm than Absalom did. Take your lord\u2019s servants and pursue after him, lest he get himself fortified cities, and escape out of our sight.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab\u2019s men went out after him with the Cherethites, the Pelethites, and all the mighty men; and they went out of Jerusalem to pursue Sheba the son of Bichri."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When they were at the great stone which is in Gibeon, Amasa came to meet them. Joab was clothed in his apparel of war that he had put on, and on it was a sash with a sword fastened on his waist in its sheath; and as he went along it fell out."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Joab said to Amasa, \u201cIs it well with you, my brother?\u201d Joab took Amasa by the beard with his right hand to kiss him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But Amasa took no heed to the sword that was in Joab\u2019s hand. So he struck him with it in the body and shed out his bowels to the ground, and didn\u2019t strike him again; and he died. Joab and Abishai his brother pursued Sheba the son of Bichri."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"One of Joab\u2019s young men stood by him, and said, \u201cHe who favors Joab, and he who is for David, let him follow Joab!\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Amasa lay wallowing in his blood in the middle of the highway. When the man saw that all the people stood still, he carried Amasa out of the highway into the field, and cast a garment over him when he saw that everyone who came by him stood still."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When he was removed out of the highway, all the people went on after Joab to pursue Sheba the son of Bichri."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He went through all the tribes of Israel to Abel, to Beth Maacah, and all the Berites. They were gathered together, and went also after him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They came and besieged him in Abel of Beth Maacah, and they cast up a mound against the city, and it stood against the rampart; and all the people who were with Joab battered the wall to throw it down."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then a wise woman cried out of the city, \u201cHear, hear! Please say to Joab, \u2018Come near here, that I may speak with you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He came near to her; and the woman said, \u201cAre you Joab?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cI am.\u201d"],[0,"Then she said to him, \u201cHear the words of your servant.\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cI\u2019m listening.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she spoke, saying, \u201cThey used to say in old times, \u2018They shall surely ask counsel at Abel,\u2019 and so they settled a matter."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I am among those who are peaceable and faithful in Israel. You seek to destroy a city and a mother in Israel. Why will you swallow up the LORD\u2019s inheritance?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab answered, \u201cFar be it, far be it from me, that I should swallow up or destroy."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The matter is not so. But a man of the hill country of Ephraim, Sheba the son of Bichri by name, has lifted up his hand against the king, even against David. Just deliver him, and I will depart from the city.\u201d"],[0,"The woman said to Joab, \u201cBehold, his head will be thrown to you over the wall.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the woman went to all the people in her wisdom. They cut off the head of Sheba the son of Bichri, and threw it out to Joab. He blew the trumpet, and they were dispersed from the city, every man to his tent. Then Joab returned to Jerusalem to the king."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Joab was over all the army of Israel, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and over the Pelethites,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Adoram was over the men subject to forced labor, Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud was the recorder,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Sheva was scribe, Zadok and Abiathar were priests,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and Ira the Jairite was chief minister to David."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a famine in the days of David for three years, year after year; and David sought the face of the LORD. The LORD said, \u201cIt is for Saul, and for his bloody house, because he put the Gibeonites to death.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The king called the Gibeonites and said to them (now the Gibeonites were not of the children of Israel, but of the remnant of the Amorites, and the children of Israel had sworn to them; and Saul sought to kill them in his zeal for the children of Israel and Judah);"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and David said to the Gibeonites, \u201cWhat should I do for you? And with what should I make atonement, that you may bless the LORD\u2019s inheritance?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The Gibeonites said to him, \u201cIt is no matter of silver or gold between us and Saul or his house; neither is it for us to put any man to death in Israel.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will do for you whatever you say.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to the king, \u201cThe man who consumed us and who plotted against us, that we should be destroyed from remaining in any of the borders of Israel,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"let seven men of his sons be delivered to us, and we will hang them up to the LORD in Gibeah of Saul, the chosen of the LORD.\u201d"],[0,"The king said, \u201cI will give them.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But the king spared Mephibosheth the son of Jonathan the son of Saul, because of the LORD\u2019s oath that was between them, between David and Jonathan the son of Saul."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But the king took the two sons of Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, whom she bore to Saul, Armoni and Mephibosheth; and the five sons of Merab the daughter of Saul, whom she bore to Adriel the son of Barzillai the Meholathite."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He delivered them into the hands of the Gibeonites; and they hanged them on the mountain before the LORD, and all seven of them fell together. They were put to death in the days of harvest, in the first days, at the beginning of barley harvest."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Rizpah the daughter of Aiah took sackcloth and spread it for herself on the rock, from the beginning of harvest until water poured on them from the sky. She allowed neither the birds of the sky to rest on them by day, nor the animals of the field by night."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"David was told what Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, the concubine of Saul, had done."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So David went and took the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son from the men of Jabesh Gilead, who had stolen them from the street of Beth Shan, where the Philistines had hanged them in the day that the Philistines killed Saul in Gilboa;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and he brought up from there the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son. They also gathered the bones of those who were hanged."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They buried the bones of Saul and Jonathan his son in the country of Benjamin in Zela, in the tomb of Kish his father; and they performed all that the king commanded. After that, God answered prayer for the land."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The Philistines had war again with Israel; and David went down, and his servants with him, and fought against the Philistines. David grew faint;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and Ishbibenob, who was of the sons of the giant, the weight of whose spear was three hundred shekels of bronze in weight, he being armed with a new sword, thought he would kill David."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But Abishai the son of Zeruiah helped him, and struck the Philistine and killed him. Then the men of David swore to him, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t go out with us to battle any more, so that you don\u2019t quench the lamp of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, there was again war with the Philistines at Gob. Then Sibbecai the Hushathite killed Saph, who was of the sons of the giant."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There was again war with the Philistines at Gob, and Elhanan the son of Jaare-Oregim the Bethlehemite killed Goliath the Gittite\u2019s brother, the staff of whose spear was like a weaver\u2019s beam."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"There was again war at Gath, where there was a man of great stature, who had six fingers on every hand and six toes on every foot, twenty-four in number, and he also was born to the giant."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When he defied Israel, Jonathan the son of Shimei, David\u2019s brother, killed him."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"These four were born to the giant in Gath; and they fell by the hand of David and by the hand of his servants."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David spoke to the LORD the words of this song in the day that the LORD delivered him out of the hand of all his enemies, and out of the hand of Saul,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and he said:"],[1,"\u201cThe LORD is my rock,"],[2,"my fortress,"],[2,"and my deliverer, even mine;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"God is my rock in whom I take refuge;"],[2,"my shield, and the horn of my salvation,"],[2,"my high tower, and my refuge."],[2,"My savior, you save me from violence."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I call on the LORD, who is worthy to be praised;"],[2,"So shall I be saved from my enemies."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For the waves of death surrounded me."],[2,"The floods of ungodliness made me afraid."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The cords of Sheol were around me."],[2,"The snares of death caught me."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"In my distress, I called on the LORD."],[2,"Yes, I called to my God."],[1,"He heard my voice out of his temple."],[2,"My cry came into his ears."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the earth shook and trembled."],[2,"The foundations of heaven quaked and were shaken,"],[2,"because he was angry."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Smoke went up out of his nostrils."],[2,"Consuming fire came out of his mouth."],[2,"Coals were kindled by it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He bowed the heavens also, and came down."],[2,"Thick darkness was under his feet."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He rode on a cherub, and flew."],[2,"Yes, he was seen on the wings of the wind."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"He made darkness a shelter around himself,"],[2,"gathering of waters, and thick clouds of the skies."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"At the brightness before him,"],[2,"coals of fire were kindled."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD thundered from heaven."],[2,"The Most High uttered his voice."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent out arrows and scattered them,"],[2,"lightning and confused them."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the channels of the sea appeared."],[2,"The foundations of the world were laid bare by the LORD\u2019s rebuke,"],[2,"at the blast of the breath of his nostrils."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent from on high and he took me."],[2,"He drew me out of many waters."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He delivered me from my strong enemy,"],[2,"from those who hated me, for they were too mighty for me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"They came on me in the day of my calamity,"],[2,"but the LORD was my support."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He also brought me out into a large place."],[2,"He delivered me, because he delighted in me."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD rewarded me according to my righteousness."],[2,"He rewarded me according to the cleanness of my hands."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For I have kept the LORD\u2019s ways,"],[2,"and have not wickedly departed from my God."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"For all his ordinances were before me."],[2,"As for his statutes, I didn\u2019t depart from them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"I was also perfect toward him."],[2,"I kept myself from my iniquity."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness,"],[2,"According to my cleanness in his eyesight."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"With the merciful you will show yourself merciful."],[2,"With the perfect man you will show yourself perfect."]]},{v:27,l:[[2,"With the pure you will show yourself pure."],[2,"With the crooked you will show yourself shrewd."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"You will save the afflicted people,"],[2,"but your eyes are on the arrogant, that you may bring them down."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are my lamp, LORD."],[2,"The LORD will light up my darkness."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"For by you, I run against a troop."],[2,"By my God, I leap over a wall."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"As for God, his way is perfect."],[2,"The LORD\u2019s word is tested."],[2,"He is a shield to all those who take refuge in him."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"For who is God, besides the LORD?"],[2,"Who is a rock, besides our God?"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"God is my strong fortress."],[2,"He makes my way perfect."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes his feet like hinds\u2019 feet,"],[2,"and sets me on my high places."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"He teaches my hands to war,"],[2,"so that my arms bend a bow of bronze."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"You have also given me the shield of your salvation."],[2,"Your gentleness has made me great."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"You have enlarged my steps under me."],[2,"My feet have not slipped."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"I have pursued my enemies and destroyed them."],[2,"I didn\u2019t turn again until they were consumed."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"I have consumed them,"],[2,"and struck them through,"],[2,"so that they can\u2019t arise."],[2,"Yes, they have fallen under my feet."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have armed me with strength for the battle."],[2,"You have subdued under me those who rose up against me."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"You have also made my enemies turn their backs to me,"],[2,"that I might cut off those who hate me."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"They looked, but there was no one to save;"],[2,"even to the LORD, but he didn\u2019t answer them."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I beat them as small as the dust of the earth."],[2,"I crushed them as the mire of the streets, and spread them abroad."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"You also have delivered me from the strivings of my people."],[2,"You have kept me to be the head of the nations."],[2,"A people whom I have not known will serve me."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"The foreigners will submit themselves to me."],[2,"As soon as they hear of me, they will obey me."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"The foreigners will fade away,"],[2,"and will come trembling out of their close places."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD lives!"],[2,"Blessed be my rock!"],[1,"Exalted be God, the rock of my salvation,"]]},{v:48,l:[[2,"even the God who executes vengeance for me,"],[2,"who brings down peoples under me,"]]},{v:49,l:[[2,"who brings me away from my enemies."],[1,"Yes, you lift me up above those who rise up against me."],[2,"You deliver me from the violent man."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will give thanks to you, LORD, among the nations,"],[2,"and will sing praises to your name."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[1,"He gives great deliverance to his king,"],[2,"and shows loving kindness to his anointed,"],[2,"to David and to his offspring, forever more.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the last words of David."],[1,"David the son of Jesse says,"],[2,"the man who was raised on high says,"],[2,"the anointed of the God of Jacob,"],[2,"the sweet psalmist of Israel:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe LORD\u2019s Spirit spoke by me."],[2,"His word was on my tongue."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The God of Israel said,"],[2,"the Rock of Israel spoke to me,"],[2,"\u2018One who rules over men righteously,"],[2,"who rules in the fear of God,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"shall be as the light of the morning when the sun rises,"],[2,"a morning without clouds,"],[2,"when the tender grass springs out of the earth,"],[2,"through clear shining after rain.\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t my house so with God?"],[2,"Yet he has made with me an everlasting covenant,"],[2,"ordered in all things, and sure,"],[2,"for it is all my salvation and all my desire."],[2,"Won\u2019t he make it grow?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"But all the ungodly will be as thorns to be thrust away,"],[2,"because they can\u2019t be taken with the hand."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The man who touches them must be armed with iron and the staff of a spear."],[1,"They will be utterly burned with fire in their place.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the names of the mighty men whom David had: Josheb Basshebeth, a Tahchemonite, chief of the captains; he was called Adino the Eznite, who killed eight hundred at one time."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"After him was Eleazar the son of Dodai the son of an Ahohite, one of the three mighty men with David when they defied the Philistines who were there gathered together to battle, and the men of Israel had gone away."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He arose and struck the Philistines until his hand was weary, and his hand froze to the sword; and the LORD worked a great victory that day; and the people returned after him only to take plunder."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"After him was Shammah the son of Agee, a Hararite. The Philistines had gathered together into a troop where there was a plot of ground full of lentils; and the people fled from the Philistines."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But he stood in the middle of the plot and defended it, and killed the Philistines; and the LORD worked a great victory."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Three of the thirty chief men went down, and came to David in the harvest time to the cave of Adullam; and the troop of the Philistines was encamped in the valley of Rephaim."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"David was then in the stronghold; and the garrison of the Philistines was then in Bethlehem."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"David said longingly, \u201cOh that someone would give me water to drink from the well of Bethlehem, which is by the gate!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The three mighty men broke through the army of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem that was by the gate and took it and brought it to David; but he would not drink of it, but poured it out to the LORD."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBe it far from me, LORD, that I should do this! Isn\u2019t this the blood of the men who risked their lives to go?\u201d Therefore he would not drink it. The three mighty men did these things."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Abishai, the brother of Joab, the son of Zeruiah, was chief of the three. He lifted up his spear against three hundred and killed them, and had a name among the three."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Wasn\u2019t he most honorable of the three? Therefore he was made their captain. However he wasn\u2019t included as one of the three."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had done mighty deeds, killed the two sons of Ariel of Moab. He also went down and killed a lion in the middle of a pit in a time of snow."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He killed a huge Egyptian, and the Egyptian had a spear in his hand; but he went down to him with a staff and plucked the spear out of the Egyptian\u2019s hand, and killed him with his own spear."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada did these things, and had a name among the three mighty men."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He was more honorable than the thirty, but he didn\u2019t attain to the three. David set him over his guard."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Asahel the brother of Joab was one of the thirty: Elhanan the son of Dodo of Bethlehem,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Shammah the Harodite, Elika the Harodite,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Helez the Paltite, Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Abiezer the Anathothite, Mebunnai the Hushathite,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Zalmon the Ahohite, Maharai the Netophathite,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Heleb the son of Baanah the Netophathite, Ittai the son of Ribai of Gibeah of the children of Benjamin,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Benaiah a Pirathonite, Hiddai of the brooks of Gaash."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Abialbon the Arbathite, Azmaveth the Barhumite,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Eliahba the Shaalbonite, the sons of Jashen, Jonathan,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Shammah the Hararite, Ahiam the son of Sharar the Ararite,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Eliphelet the son of Ahasbai, the son of the Maacathite, Eliam the son of Ahithophel the Gilonite,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Hezro the Carmelite, Paarai the Arbite,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Igal the son of Nathan of Zobah, Bani the Gadite,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Zelek the Ammonite, Naharai the Beerothite, armor bearers to Joab the son of Zeruiah,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and Uriah the Hittite: thirty-seven in all."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Again the LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel, and he moved David against them, saying, \u201cGo, count Israel and Judah.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The king said to Joab the captain of the army, who was with him, \u201cNow go back and forth through all the tribes of Israel, from Dan even to Beersheba, and count the people, that I may know the sum of the people.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab said to the king, \u201cNow may the LORD your God add to the people, however many they may be, one hundred times; and may the eyes of my lord the king see it. But why does my lord the king delight in this thing?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Notwithstanding, the king\u2019s word prevailed against Joab and against the captains of the army. Joab and the captains of the army went out from the presence of the king to count the people of Israel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They passed over the Jordan and encamped in Aroer, on the right side of the city that is in the middle of the valley of Gad, and to Jazer;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"then they came to Gilead and to the land of Tahtim Hodshi; and they came to Dan Jaan and around to Sidon,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and came to the stronghold of Tyre, and to all the cities of the Hivites and of the Canaanites; and they went out to the south of Judah, at Beersheba."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So when they had gone back and forth through all the land, they came to Jerusalem at the end of nine months and twenty days."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Joab gave up the sum of the counting of the people to the king; and there were in Israel eight hundred thousand valiant men who drew the sword, and the men of Judah were five hundred thousand men."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"David\u2019s heart struck him after he had counted the people. David said to the LORD, \u201cI have sinned greatly in that which I have done. But now, the LORD, put away, I beg you, the iniquity of your servant; for I have done very foolishly.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When David rose up in the morning, the LORD\u2019s word came to the prophet Gad, David\u2019s seer, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cGo and speak to David, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cI offer you three things. Choose one of them, that I may do it to you.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"So Gad came to David, and told him, saying, \u201cShall seven years of famine come to you in your land? Or will you flee three months before your foes while they pursue you? Or shall there be three days\u2019 pestilence in your land? Now answer, and consider what answer I shall return to him who sent me.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Gad, \u201cI am in distress. Let us fall now into the LORD\u2019s hand, for his mercies are great. Let me not fall into man\u2019s hand.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"So the LORD sent a pestilence on Israel from the morning even to the appointed time; and seventy thousand men died of the people from Dan even to Beersheba."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When the angel stretched out his hand toward Jerusalem to destroy it, the LORD relented of the disaster, and said to the angel who destroyed the people, \u201cIt is enough. Now withdraw your hand.\u201d The LORD\u2019s angel was by the threshing floor of Araunah the Jebusite."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"David spoke to the LORD when he saw the angel who struck the people, and said, \u201cBehold, I have sinned, and I have done perversely; but these sheep, what have they done? Please let your hand be against me, and against my father\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Gad came that day to David and said to him, \u201cGo up, build an altar to the LORD on the threshing floor of Araunah the Jebusite.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"David went up according to the saying of Gad, as the LORD commanded."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Araunah looked out, and saw the king and his servants coming on toward him. Then Araunah went out and bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Araunah said, \u201cWhy has my lord the king come to his servant?\u201d"],[0,"David said, \u201cTo buy your threshing floor, to build an altar to the LORD, that the plague may be stopped from afflicting the people.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Araunah said to David, \u201cLet my lord the king take and offer up what seems good to him. Behold, the cattle for the burnt offering, and the threshing sledges and the yokes of the oxen for the wood."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"All this, O king, does Araunah give to the king.\u201d Araunah said to the king, \u201cMay the LORD your God accept you.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to Araunah, \u201cNo, but I will most certainly buy it from you for a price. I will not offer burnt offerings to the LORD my God which cost me nothing.\u201d So David bought the threshing floor and the oxen for fifty shekels of silver."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 50 shekels is about 0.5 kilograms or 1.1 pounds."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"David built an altar to the LORD there, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings. So the LORD was entreated for the land, and the plague was removed from Israel."]]}]]}},1281,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,h,n,i){h.exports={book:"1Kgs",name:"1 Kings",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now King David was old and advanced in years; and they covered him with clothes, but he couldn\u2019t keep warm."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore his servants said to him, \u201cLet a young virgin be sought for my lord the king. Let her stand before the king, and cherish him; and let her lie in your bosom, that my lord the king may keep warm.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So they sought for a beautiful young lady throughout all the borders of Israel, and found Abishag the Shunammite, and brought her to the king."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The young lady was very beautiful; and she cherished the king, and served him; but the king didn\u2019t know her intimately."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Adonijah the son of Haggith exalted himself, saying, \u201cI will be king.\u201d Then he prepared him chariots and horsemen, and fifty men to run before him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"His father had not displeased him at any time in saying, \u201cWhy have you done so?\u201d and he was also a very handsome man; and he was born after Absalom."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He conferred with Joab the son of Zeruiah and with Abiathar the priest; and they followed Adonijah and helped him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But Zadok the priest, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, Nathan the prophet, Shimei, Rei, and the mighty men who belonged to David, were not with Adonijah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Adonijah killed sheep, cattle, and fatlings by the stone of Zoheleth, which is beside En Rogel; and he called all his brothers, the king\u2019s sons, and all the men of Judah, the king\u2019s servants;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but he didn\u2019t call Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah, and the mighty men, and Solomon his brother."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Nathan spoke to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon, saying, \u201cHaven\u2019t you heard that Adonijah the son of Haggith reigns, and David our lord doesn\u2019t know it?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now therefore come, please let me give you counsel, that you may save your own life and your son Solomon\u2019s life."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Go in to King David, and tell him, \u2018Didn\u2019t you, my lord the king, swear to your servant, saying, \u201cAssuredly Solomon your son shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne\u201d? Why then does Adonijah reign?\u2019"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Behold, while you are still talking there with the king, I will also come in after you and confirm your words.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Bathsheba went in to the king in his room. The king was very old; and Abishag the Shunammite was serving the king."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Bathsheba bowed and showed respect to the king. The king said, \u201cWhat would you like?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to him, \u201cMy lord, you swore by the LORD your God to your servant, \u2018Assuredly Solomon your son shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne.\u2019"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh).","The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now, behold, Adonijah reigns; and you, my lord the king, don\u2019t know it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He has slain cattle and fatlings and sheep in abundance, and has called all the sons of the king, Abiathar the priest, and Joab the captain of the army; but he hasn\u2019t called Solomon your servant."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You, my lord the king, the eyes of all Israel are on you, that you should tell them who will sit on the throne of my lord the king after him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Otherwise it will happen, when my lord the king sleeps with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon will be considered criminals.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, while she was still talking with the king, Nathan the prophet came in."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They told the king, saying, \u201cBehold, Nathan the prophet!\u201d"],[0,"When he had come in before the king, he bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Nathan said, \u201cMy lord, King, have you said, \u2018Adonijah shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne\u2019?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For he has gone down today, and has slain cattle, fatlings, and sheep in abundance, and has called all the king\u2019s sons, the captains of the army, and Abiathar the priest. Behold, they are eating and drinking before him, and saying, \u2018Long live King Adonijah!\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But he hasn\u2019t called me, even me your servant, Zadok the priest, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and your servant Solomon."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Was this thing done by my lord the king, and you haven\u2019t shown to your servants who should sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Then King David answered, \u201cCall Bathsheba in to me.\u201d She came into the king\u2019s presence and stood before the king."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The king vowed and said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, who has redeemed my soul out of all adversity,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"most certainly as I swore to you by the LORD, the God of Israel, saying, \u2018Assuredly Solomon your son shall reign after me, and he shall sit on my throne in my place;\u2019 I will most certainly do this today.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Bathsheba bowed with her face to the earth and showed respect to the king, and said, \u201cLet my lord King David live forever!\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"King David said, \u201cCall to me Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada.\u201d They came before the king."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The king said to them, \u201cTake with you the servants of your lord, and cause Solomon my son to ride on my own mule, and bring him down to Gihon."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel. Blow the trumpet, and say, \u2018Long live King Solomon!\u2019"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Then come up after him, and he shall come and sit on my throne; for he shall be king in my place. I have appointed him to be prince over Israel and over Judah.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada answered the king, and said, \u201cAmen. May the LORD, the God of my lord the king, say so."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"As the LORD has been with my lord the king, even so may he be with Solomon, and make his throne greater than the throne of my lord King David.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"So Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites and the Pelethites went down and had Solomon ride on King David\u2019s mule, and brought him to Gihon."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Zadok the priest took the horn of oil from the Tent, and anointed Solomon. They blew the trumpet; and all the people said, \u201cLong live King Solomon!\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people came up after him, and the people piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth shook with their sound."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Adonijah and all the guests who were with him heard it as they had finished eating. When Joab heard the sound of the trumpet, he said, \u201cWhy is this noise of the city being in an uproar?\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"While he yet spoke, behold, Jonathan the son of Abiathar the priest came; and Adonijah said, \u201cCome in; for you are a worthy man, and bring good news.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Jonathan answered Adonijah, \u201cMost certainly our lord King David has made Solomon king."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The king has sent with him Zadok the priest, Nathan the prophet, Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and they have caused him to ride on the king\u2019s mule."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet have anointed him king in Gihon. They have come up from there rejoicing, so that the city rang again. This is the noise that you have heard."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Also, Solomon sits on the throne of the kingdom."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Moreover the king\u2019s servants came to bless our lord King David, saying, \u2018May your God make the name of Solomon better than your name, and make his throne greater than your throne;\u2019 and the king bowed himself on the bed."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Also thus said the king, \u2018Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who has given one to sit on my throne today, my eyes even seeing it.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"All the guests of Adonijah were afraid, and rose up, and each man went his way."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Adonijah was afraid because of Solomon; and he arose, and went, and hung onto the horns of the altar."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Solomon was told, \u201cBehold, Adonijah fears King Solomon; for, behold, he is hanging onto the horns of the altar, saying, \u2018Let King Solomon swear to me first that he will not kill his servant with the sword.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon said, \u201cIf he shows himself a worthy man, not a hair of his shall fall to the earth; but if wickedness is found in him, he shall die.\u201d"]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"So King Solomon sent, and they brought him down from the altar. He came and bowed down to King Solomon; and Solomon said to him, \u201cGo to your house.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the days of David came near that he should die; and he commanded Solomon his son, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cI am going the way of all the earth. You be strong therefore, and show yourself a man;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and keep the instruction of the LORD your God, to walk in his ways, to keep his statutes, his commandments, his ordinances, and his testimonies, according to that which is written in the law of Moses, that you may prosper in all that you do and wherever you turn yourself."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then the LORD may establish his word which he spoke concerning me, saying, \u2018If your children are careful of their way, to walk before me in truth with all their heart and with all their soul, there shall not fail you,\u2019 he said, \u2018a man on the throne of Israel.\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover you know also what Joab the son of Zeruiah did to me, even what he did to the two captains of the armies of Israel, to Abner the son of Ner and to Amasa the son of Jether, whom he killed, and shed the blood of war in peace, and put the blood of war on his sash that was around his waist and in his sandals that were on his feet."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Do therefore according to your wisdom, and don\u2019t let his gray head go down to Sheol in peace."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But show kindness to the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, and let them be among those who eat at your table; for so they came to me when I fled from Absalom your brother."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, there is with you Shimei the son of Gera, the Benjamite of Bahurim, who cursed me with a grievous curse in the day when I went to Mahanaim; but he came down to meet me at the Jordan, and I swore to him by the LORD, saying, \u2018I will not put you to death with the sword.\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now therefore don\u2019t hold him guiltless, for you are a wise man; and you will know what you ought to do to him, and you shall bring his gray head down to Sheol with blood.\u201d"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"David slept with his fathers, and was buried in David\u2019s city."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The days that David reigned over Israel were forty years; he reigned seven years in Hebron, and he reigned thirty-three years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Solomon sat on David his father\u2019s throne; and his kingdom was firmly established."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Adonijah the son of Haggith came to Bathsheba the mother of Solomon. She said, \u201cDo you come peaceably?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cPeaceably."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He said moreover, I have something to tell you.\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cSay on.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou know that the kingdom was mine, and that all Israel set their faces on me, that I should reign. However, the kingdom is turned around, and has become my brother\u2019s; for it was his from the LORD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Now I ask one petition of you. Don\u2019t deny me.\u201d"],[0,"She said to him, \u201cSay on.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cPlease speak to Solomon the king (for he will not tell you \u2018no\u2019), that he give me Abishag the Shunammite as wife.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Bathsheba said, \u201cAll right. I will speak for you to the king.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Bathsheba therefore went to King Solomon, to speak to him for Adonijah. The king rose up to meet her and bowed himself to her, and sat down on his throne and caused a throne to be set for the king\u2019s mother; and she sat on his right hand."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Then she said, \u201cI ask one small petition of you; don\u2019t deny me.\u201d"],[0,"The king said to her, \u201cAsk on, my mother, for I will not deny you.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cLet Abishag the Shunammite be given to Adonijah your brother as wife.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"King Solomon answered his mother, \u201cWhy do you ask Abishag the Shunammite for Adonijah? Ask for him the kingdom also, for he is my elder brother; even for him, and for Abiathar the priest, and for Joab the son of Zeruiah.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then King Solomon swore by the LORD, saying, \u201cGod do so to me, and more also, if Adonijah has not spoken this word against his own life."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Now therefore as the LORD lives, who has established me and set me on my father David\u2019s throne, and who has made me a house as he promised, surely Adonijah shall be put to death today.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"King Solomon sent Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; and he fell on him, so that he died."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"To Abiathar the priest the king said, \u201cGo to Anathoth, to your own fields, for you are worthy of death. But I will not at this time put you to death, because you bore the Lord GOD\u2019s ark before David my father, and because you were afflicted in all in which my father was afflicted.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:27,l:[[0,"So Solomon thrust Abiathar out from being priest to the LORD, that he might fulfill the LORD\u2019s word which he spoke concerning the house of Eli in Shiloh."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"This news came to Joab; for Joab had followed Adonijah, although he didn\u2019t follow Absalom. Joab fled to the LORD\u2019s Tent, and held onto the horns of the altar."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"King Solomon was told, \u201cJoab has fled to the LORD\u2019s Tent; and behold, he is by the altar.\u201d Then Solomon sent Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, saying, \u201cGo, fall on him.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Benaiah came to the LORD\u2019s Tent, and said to him, \u201cThe king says, \u2018Come out!\u2019\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cNo; but I will die here.\u201d"],[0,"Benaiah brought the king word again, saying, \u201cThis is what Joab said, and this is how he answered me.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to him, \u201cDo as he has said, and fall on him, and bury him, that you may take away the blood, which Joab shed without cause, from me and from my father\u2019s house."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The LORD will return his blood on his own head, because he fell on two men more righteous and better than he, and killed them with the sword, and my father David didn\u2019t know it: Abner the son of Ner, captain of the army of Israel, and Amasa the son of Jether, captain of the army of Judah."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"So their blood will return on the head of Joab and on the head of his offspring forever. But for David, for his offspring, for his house, and for his throne, there will be peace forever from the LORD.\u201d"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Benaiah the son of Jehoiada went up and fell on him, and killed him; and he was buried in his own house in the wilderness."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The king put Benaiah the son of Jehoiada in his place over the army; and the king put Zadok the priest in the place of Abiathar."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The king sent and called for Shimei, and said to him, \u201cBuild yourself a house in Jerusalem, and live there, and don\u2019t go anywhere else."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For on the day you go out and pass over the brook Kidron, know for certain that you will surely die. Your blood will be on your own head.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Shimei said to the king, \u201cWhat you say is good. As my lord the king has said, so will your servant do.\u201d Shimei lived in Jerusalem many days."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of three years, two of Shimei\u2019s slaves ran away to Achish, son of Maacah, king of Gath. They told Shimei, saying, \u201cBehold, your slaves are in Gath.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Shimei arose, saddled his donkey, and went to Gath to Achish to seek his slaves; and Shimei went and brought his slaves from Gath."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Solomon was told that Shimei had gone from Jerusalem to Gath, and had come again."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"The king sent and called for Shimei, and said to him, \u201cDidn\u2019t I adjure you by the LORD and warn you, saying, \u2018Know for certain that on the day you go out and walk anywhere else, you shall surely die\u2019? You said to me, \u2018The saying that I have heard is good.\u2019"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Why then have you not kept the oath of the LORD and the commandment that I have instructed you with?\u201d"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The king said moreover to Shimei, \u201cYou know in your heart all the wickedness that you did to David my father. Therefore the LORD will return your wickedness on your own head."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"But King Solomon will be blessed, and David\u2019s throne will be established before the LORD forever.\u201d"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"So the king commanded Benaiah the son of Jehoiada; and he went out, and fell on him, so that he died. The kingdom was established in the hand of Solomon."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon made a marriage alliance with Pharaoh king of Egypt. He took Pharaoh\u2019s daughter and brought her into David\u2019s city until he had finished building his own house, the LORD\u2019s house, and the wall around Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"However, the people sacrificed in the high places, because there was not yet a house built for the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Solomon loved the LORD, walking in the statutes of David his father, except that he sacrificed and burned incense in the high places."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The king went to Gibeon to sacrifice there, for that was the great high place. Solomon offered a thousand burnt offerings on that altar."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"In Gibeon, the LORD appeared to Solomon in a dream by night; and God said, \u201cAsk for what I should give you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon said, \u201cYou have shown to your servant David my father great loving kindness, because he walked before you in truth, in righteousness, and in uprightness of heart with you. You have kept for him this great loving kindness, that you have given him a son to sit on his throne, as it is today."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now, LORD my God, you have made your servant king instead of David my father. I am just a little child. I don\u2019t know how to go out or come in."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Your servant is among your people which you have chosen, a great people, that can\u2019t be numbered or counted for multitude."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Give your servant therefore an understanding heart to judge your people, that I may discern between good and evil; for who is able to judge this great people of yours?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"This request pleased the Lord, that Solomon had asked this thing."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"God said to him, \u201cBecause you have asked this thing, and have not asked for yourself long life, nor have you asked for riches for yourself, nor have you asked for the life of your enemies, but have asked for yourself understanding to discern justice,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"behold, I have done according to your word. Behold, I have given you a wise and understanding heart, so that there has been no one like you before you, and after you none will arise like you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I have also given you that which you have not asked, both riches and honor, so that there will not be any among the kings like you for all your days."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If you will walk in my ways, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as your father David walked, then I will lengthen your days.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon awoke; and behold, it was a dream. Then he came to Jerusalem and stood before the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, and offered up burnt offerings, offered peace offerings, and made a feast for all his servants."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then two women who were prostitutes came to the king, and stood before him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The one woman said, \u201cOh, my lord, I and this woman dwell in one house. I delivered a child with her in the house."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The third day after I delivered, this woman delivered also. We were together. There was no stranger with us in the house, just us two in the house."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"This woman\u2019s child died in the night, because she lay on it."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"She arose at midnight, and took my son from beside me while your servant slept, and laid it in her bosom, and laid her dead child in my bosom."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When I rose in the morning to nurse my child, behold, he was dead; but when I had looked at him in the morning, behold, it was not my son whom I bore.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The other woman said, \u201cNo! But the living one is my son, and the dead one is your son.\u201d"],[0,"The first one said, \u201cNo! But the dead one is your son, and the living one is my son.\u201d They argued like this before the king."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said, \u201cOne says, \u2018This is my son who lives, and your son is the dead one;\u2019 and the other says, \u2018No! But your son is the dead one, and my son is the living one.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cGet me a sword.\u201d So they brought a sword before the king."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cDivide the living child in two, and give half to the one, and half to the other.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the woman whose the living child was spoke to the king, for her heart yearned over her son, and she said, \u201cOh, my lord, give her the living child, and in no way kill him!\u201d"],[0,"But the other said, \u201cHe shall be neither mine nor yours. Divide him.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king answered, \u201cGive the first woman the living child, and definitely do not kill him. She is his mother.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"All Israel heard of the judgment which the king had judged; and they feared the king, for they saw that the wisdom of God was in him to do justice."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"King Solomon was king over all Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"These were the princes whom he had: Azariah the son of Zadok, the priest;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Elihoreph and Ahijah, the sons of Shisha, scribes; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud, the recorder;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the army; Zadok and Abiathar were priests;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Azariah the son of Nathan was over the officers; Zabud the son of Nathan was chief minister, the king\u2019s friend;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Ahishar was over the household; and Adoniram the son of Abda was over the men subject to forced labor."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon had twelve officers over all Israel, who provided food for the king and his household. Each man had to make provision for a month in the year."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"These are their names: Ben Hur, in the hill country of Ephraim;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Ben Deker, in Makaz, in Shaalbim, Beth Shemesh, and Elon Beth Hanan;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Ben Hesed, in Arubboth (Socoh and all the land of Hepher belonged to him);"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Ben Abinadab, in all the height of Dor (he had Taphath, Solomon\u2019s daughter, as wife);"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Baana the son of Ahilud, in Taanach and Megiddo, and all Beth Shean which is beside Zarethan, beneath Jezreel, from Beth Shean to Abel Meholah, as far as beyond Jokmeam;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Ben Geber, in Ramoth Gilead (the towns of Jair the son of Manasseh, which are in Gilead, belonged to him; and the region of Argob, which is in Bashan, sixty great cities with walls and bronze bars, belonged to him);"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Ahinadab the son of Iddo, in Mahanaim;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Ahimaaz, in Naphtali (he also took Basemath the daughter of Solomon as wife);"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Baana the son of Hushai, in Asher and Bealoth;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat the son of Paruah, in Issachar;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Shimei the son of Ela, in Benjamin;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Geber the son of Uri, in the land of Gilead, the country of Sihon king of the Amorites and of Og king of Bashan; and he was the only officer who was in the land."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah and Israel were numerous as the sand which is by the sea in multitude, eating and drinking and making merry."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Solomon ruled over all the kingdoms from the River to the land of the Philistines, and to the border of Egypt. They brought tribute and served Solomon all the days of his life."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Solomon\u2019s provision for one day was thirty cors of fine flour, sixty measures of meal,"]],f:["1 cor is the same as a homer, or about 55.9 U. S. gallons (liquid) or 211 liters or 6 bushels"]},{v:23,l:[[0,"ten head of fat cattle, twenty head of cattle out of the pastures, and one hundred sheep, in addition to deer, gazelles, roebucks, and fattened fowl."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For he had dominion over all on this side of the River, from Tiphsah even to Gaza, over all the kings on this side of the River; and he had peace on all sides around him."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Judah and Israel lived safely, every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan even to Beersheba, all the days of Solomon."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Solomon had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Those officers provided food for King Solomon, and for all who came to King Solomon\u2019s table, every man in his month. They let nothing be lacking."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They also brought barley and straw for the horses and swift steeds to the place where the officers were, each man according to his duty."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"God gave Solomon abundant wisdom, understanding, and breadth of mind like the sand that is on the seashore."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Solomon\u2019s wisdom excelled the wisdom of all the children of the east and all the wisdom of Egypt."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For he was wiser than all men\u2014wiser than Ethan the Ezrahite, Heman, Calcol, and Darda, the sons of Mahol; and his fame was in all the nations all around."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He spoke three thousand proverbs, and his songs numbered one thousand five."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He spoke of trees, from the cedar that is in Lebanon even to the hyssop that grows out of the wall; he also spoke of animals, of birds, of creeping things, and of fish."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"People of all nations came to hear the wisdom of Solomon, sent by all kings of the earth who had heard of his wisdom."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hiram king of Tyre sent his servants to Solomon, for he had heard that they had anointed him king in the place of his father, and Hiram had always loved David."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Solomon sent to Hiram, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cYou know that David my father could not build a house for the name of the LORD his God because of the wars which were around him on every side, until the LORD put his enemies under the soles of his feet."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But now the LORD my God has given me rest on every side. There is no enemy and no evil occurrence."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Behold, I intend to build a house for the name of the LORD my God, as the LORD spoke to David my father, saying, \u2018Your son, whom I will set on your throne in your place shall build the house for my name.\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now therefore command that cedar trees be cut for me out of Lebanon. My servants will be with your servants; and I will give you wages for your servants according to all that you say. For you know that there is nobody among us who knows how to cut timber like the Sidonians.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When Hiram heard the words of Solomon, he rejoiced greatly, and said, \u201cBlessed is the LORD today, who has given to David a wise son to rule over this great people.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Hiram sent to Solomon, saying, \u201cI have heard the message which you have sent to me. I will do all your desire concerning timber of cedar, and concerning cypress timber."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"My servants will bring them down from Lebanon to the sea. I will make them into rafts to go by sea to the place that you specify to me, and will cause them to be broken up there, and you will receive them. You will accomplish my desire, in giving food for my household.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hiram gave Solomon cedar timber and cypress timber according to all his desire."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Solomon gave Hiram twenty thousand cors of wheat for food to his household, and twenty cors of pure oil. Solomon gave this to Hiram year by year."]],f:["20,000 cors would be about 120,000 bushels or about 4.2 megaliters of wheat, which would weigh about 3,270 metric tons.","20 cors is about 1,100 gallons or about 4220 liters."]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD gave Solomon wisdom, as he promised him. There was peace between Hiram and Solomon, and the two of them made a treaty together."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"King Solomon raised a levy out of all Israel; and the levy was thirty thousand men."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He sent them to Lebanon, ten thousand a month by courses: for a month they were in Lebanon, and two months at home; and Adoniram was over the men subject to forced labor."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Solomon had seventy thousand who bore burdens, and eighty thousand who were stone cutters in the mountains,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"besides Solomon\u2019s chief officers who were over the work: three thousand three hundred who ruled over the people who labored in the work."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The king commanded, and they cut out large stones, costly stones, to lay the foundation of the house with worked stone."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Solomon\u2019s builders and Hiram\u2019s builders and the Gebalites cut them, and prepared the timber and the stones to build the house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the four hundred and eightieth year after the children of Israel had come out of the land of Egypt, in the fourth year of Solomon\u2019s reign over Israel, in the month Ziv, which is the second month, he began to build the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The house which King Solomon built for the LORD had a length of sixty cubits, and its width twenty, and its height thirty cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The porch in front of the temple of the house had a length of twenty cubits, which was along the width of the house. Ten cubits was its width in front of the house."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He made windows of fixed lattice work for the house."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Against the wall of the house, he built floors all around, against the walls of the house all around, both of the temple and of the inner sanctuary; and he made side rooms all around."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The lowest floor was five cubits wide, and the middle was six cubits wide, and the third was seven cubits wide; for on the outside he made offsets in the wall of the house all around, that the beams should not be inserted into the walls of the house."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The house, when it was under construction, was built of stone prepared at the quarry; and no hammer or ax or any tool of iron was heard in the house while it was under construction."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The door for the middle side rooms was in the right side of the house. They went up by winding stairs into the middle floor, and out of the middle into the third."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So he built the house and finished it; and he covered the house with beams and planks of cedar."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He built the floors all along the house, each five cubits high; and they rested on the house with timbers of cedar."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Solomon, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cConcerning this house which you are building, if you will walk in my statutes, and execute my ordinances, and keep all my commandments to walk in them, then I will establish my word with you, which I spoke to David your father."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will not forsake my people Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So Solomon built the house and finished it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He built the walls of the house within with boards of cedar; from the floor of the house to the walls of the ceiling, he covered them on the inside with wood. He covered the floor of the house with cypress boards."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He built twenty cubits of the back part of the house with boards of cedar from the floor to the ceiling. He built this within, for an inner sanctuary, even for the most holy place."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"In front of the temple sanctuary was forty cubits long."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"There was cedar on the house within, carved with buds and open flowers. All was cedar. No stone was visible."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He prepared an inner sanctuary in the middle of the house within, to set the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant there."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Within the inner sanctuary was twenty cubits in length, and twenty cubits in width, and twenty cubits in its height. He overlaid it with pure gold. He covered the altar with cedar."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So Solomon overlaid the house within with pure gold. He drew chains of gold across before the inner sanctuary, and he overlaid it with gold."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He overlaid the whole house with gold, until all the house was finished. He also overlaid the whole altar that belonged to the inner sanctuary with gold."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"In the inner sanctuary he made two cherubim of olive wood, each ten cubits high."]],f:["\u201cCherubim\u201d is plural of \u201ccherub\u201d, an angelic being."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Five cubits was the length of one wing of the cherub, and five cubits was the length of the other wing of the cherub. From the tip of one wing to the tip of the other was ten cubits."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The other cherub was ten cubits. Both the cherubim were of one measure and one form."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"One cherub was ten cubits high, and so was the other cherub."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He set the cherubim within the inner house. The wings of the cherubim were stretched out, so that the wing of the one touched the one wall and the wing of the other cherub touched the other wall; and their wings touched one another in the middle of the house."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He overlaid the cherubim with gold."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He carved all the walls of the house around with carved figures of cherubim, palm trees, and open flowers, inside and outside."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He overlaid the floor of the house with gold, inside and outside."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For the entrance of the inner sanctuary, he made doors of olive wood. The lintel and door posts were a fifth part of the wall."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"So he made two doors of olive wood; and he carved on them carvings of cherubim, palm trees, and open flowers, and overlaid them with gold. He spread the gold on the cherubim and on the palm trees."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He also made the entrance of the temple door posts of olive wood, out of a fourth part of the wall,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"and two doors of cypress wood. The two leaves of the one door were folding, and the two leaves of the other door were folding."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"He carved cherubim, palm trees, and open flowers; and he overlaid them with gold fitted on the engraved work."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He built the inner court with three courses of cut stone and a course of cedar beams."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"The foundation of the LORD\u2019s house was laid in the fourth year, in the month Ziv."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"In the eleventh year, in the month Bul, which is the eighth month, the house was finished throughout all its parts and according to all its specifications. So he spent seven years building it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon was building his own house thirteen years, and he finished all his house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For he built the House of the Forest of Lebanon. Its length was one hundred cubits, its width fifty cubits, and its height thirty cubits, on four rows of cedar pillars, with cedar beams on the pillars."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It was covered with cedar above over the forty-five beams that were on the pillars, fifteen in a row."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"There were beams in three rows, and window was facing window in three ranks."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All the doors and posts were made square with beams; and window was facing window in three ranks."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He made the hall of pillars. Its length was fifty cubits and its width thirty cubits, with a porch before them, and pillars and a threshold before them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He made the porch of the throne where he was to judge, even the porch of judgment; and it was covered with cedar from floor to floor."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"His house where he was to dwell, the other court within the porch, was of the same construction. He made also a house for Pharaoh\u2019s daughter (whom Solomon had taken as wife), like this porch."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"All these were of costly stones, even of stone cut according to measure, sawed with saws, inside and outside, even from the foundation to the coping, and so on the outside to the great court."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The foundation was of costly stones, even great stones, stones of ten cubits and stones of eight cubits."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Above were costly stones, even cut stone, according to measure, and cedar wood."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The great court around had three courses of cut stone with a course of cedar beams, like the inner court of the LORD\u2019s house and the porch of the house."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"King Solomon sent and brought Hiram out of Tyre."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He was the son of a widow of the tribe of Naphtali, and his father was a man of Tyre, a worker in bronze; and he was filled with wisdom and understanding and skill to work all works in bronze. He came to King Solomon and performed all his work."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For he fashioned the two pillars of bronze, eighteen cubits high apiece; and a line of twelve cubits encircled either of them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He made two capitals of molten bronze to set on the tops of the pillars. The height of the one capital was five cubits, and the height of the other capital was five cubits."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"There were nets of checker work and wreaths of chain work for the capitals which were on the top of the pillars: seven for the one capital, and seven for the other capital."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"So he made the pillars; and there were two rows of pomegranates around the one network, to cover the capitals that were on the top of the pillars; and he did so for the other capital."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The capitals that were on the top of the pillars in the porch were of lily work, four cubits."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"There were capitals above also on the two pillars, close by the belly which was beside the network. There were two hundred pomegranates in rows around the other capital."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He set up the pillars at the porch of the temple. He set up the right pillar and called its name Jachin; and he set up the left pillar and called its name Boaz."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"On the tops of the pillars was lily work. So the work of the pillars was finished."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the molten sea ten cubits from brim to brim, round in shape. Its height was five cubits; and a line of thirty cubits encircled it."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Under its brim around there were buds which encircled it for ten cubits, encircling the sea. The buds were in two rows, cast when it was cast."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"It stood on twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east; and the sea was set on them above, and all their hindquarters were inward."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"It was a hand width thick. Its brim was worked like the brim of a cup, like the flower of a lily. It held two thousand baths."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the ten bases of bronze. The length of one base was four cubits, four cubits its width, and three cubits its height."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The work of the bases was like this: they had panels; and there were panels between the ledges;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"and on the panels that were between the ledges were lions, oxen, and cherubim; and on the ledges there was a pedestal above; and beneath the lions and oxen were wreaths of hanging work."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Every base had four bronze wheels and axles of bronze; and its four feet had supports. The supports were cast beneath the basin, with wreaths at the side of each."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Its opening within the capital and above was a cubit. Its opening was round like the work of a pedestal, a cubit and a half; and also on its opening were engravings, and their panels were square, not round."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The four wheels were underneath the panels; and the axles of the wheels were in the base. The height of a wheel was a cubit and half a cubit."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The work of the wheels was like the work of a chariot wheel. Their axles, their rims, their spokes, and their hubs were all of cast metal."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"There were four supports at the four corners of each base. Its supports were of the base itself."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"In the top of the base there was a round band half a cubit high; and on the top of the base its supports and its panels were the same."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"On the plates of its supports and on its panels, he engraved cherubim, lions, and palm trees, each in its space, with wreaths all around."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He made the ten bases in this way: all of them had one casting, one measure, and one form."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He made ten basins of bronze. One basin contained forty baths. Every basin measured four cubits. One basin was on every one of the ten bases."]],f:["1 bath is one tenth of a cor, or about 5.6 U. S. gallons or 21 liters, so 40 baths was about 224 gallons or 840 liters."]},{v:39,l:[[0,"He set the bases, five on the right side of the house and five on the left side of the house. He set the sea on the right side of the house eastward and toward the south."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Hiram made the pots, the shovels, and the basins. So Hiram finished doing all the work that he worked for King Solomon in the LORD\u2019s house:"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"the two pillars; the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars; the two networks to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars;"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"the four hundred pomegranates for the two networks; two rows of pomegranates for each network, to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the pillars;"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"the ten bases; the ten basins on the bases;"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"the one sea; the twelve oxen under the sea;"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"the pots; the shovels; and the basins. All of these vessels, which Hiram made for King Solomon for the LORD\u2019s house, were of burnished bronze."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"The king cast them in the plain of the Jordan, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zarethan."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Solomon left all the vessels unweighed, because there were so many of them. The weight of the bronze could not be determined."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon made all the vessels that were in the LORD\u2019s house: the golden altar and the table that the show bread was on, of gold;"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"and the lamp stands, five on the right side and five on the left, in front of the inner sanctuary, of pure gold; and the flowers, the lamps, and the tongs, of gold;"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"the cups, the snuffers, the basins, the spoons, and the fire pans, of pure gold; and the hinges, both for the doors of the inner house, the most holy place, and for the doors of the house, of the temple, of gold."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus all the work that King Solomon did in the LORD\u2019s house was finished. Solomon brought in the things which David his father had dedicated\u2014the silver, the gold, and the vessels\u2014and put them in the treasuries of the LORD\u2019s house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel with all the heads of the tribes, the princes of the fathers\u2019 households of the children of Israel, to King Solomon in Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant out of David\u2019s city, which is Zion."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"All the men of Israel assembled themselves to King Solomon at the feast in the month Ethanim, which is the seventh month."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All the elders of Israel came, and the priests picked up the ark."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They brought up the LORD\u2019s ark, the Tent of Meeting, and all the holy vessels that were in the Tent. The priests and the Levites brought these up."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"King Solomon and all the congregation of Israel, who were assembled to him, were with him before the ark, sacrificing sheep and cattle that could not be counted or numbered for multitude."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The priests brought in the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant to its place, into the inner sanctuary of the house, to the most holy place, even under the cherubim\u2019s wings."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the cherubim spread their wings out over the place of the ark, and the cherubim covered the ark and its poles above."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The poles were so long that the ends of the poles were seen from the holy place before the inner sanctuary, but they were not seen outside. They are there to this day."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"There was nothing in the ark except the two stone tablets which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"It came to pass, when the priests had come out of the holy place, that the cloud filled the LORD\u2019s house,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"so that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud; for the LORD\u2019s glory filled the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon said, \u201cThe LORD has said that he would dwell in the thick darkness."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I have surely built you a house of habitation, a place for you to dwell in forever.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The king turned his face around and blessed all the assembly of Israel; and all the assembly of Israel stood."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBlessed is the LORD, the God of Israel, who spoke with his mouth to David your father, and has with his hand fulfilled it, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u2018Since the day that I brought my people Israel out of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel to build a house, that my name might be there; but I chose David to be over my people Israel.\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow it was in the heart of David my father to build a house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But the LORD said to David my father, \u2018Whereas it was in your heart to build a house for my name, you did well that it was in your heart."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, you shall not build the house; but your son who shall come out of your body, he shall build the house for my name.\u2019"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD has established his word that he spoke; for I have risen up in the place of David my father, and I sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised, and have built the house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"There I have set a place for the ark, in which is the LORD\u2019s covenant, which he made with our fathers when he brought them out of the land of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon stood before the LORD\u2019s altar in the presence of all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands toward heaven;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and he said, \u201cLORD, the God of Israel, there is no God like you, in heaven above, or on earth beneath; who keeps covenant and loving kindness with your servants who walk before you with all their heart;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"who has kept with your servant David my father that which you promised him. Yes, you spoke with your mouth, and have fulfilled it with your hand, as it is today."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now therefore, may LORD, the God of Israel, keep with your servant David my father that which you have promised him, saying, \u2018There shall not fail from you a man in my sight to sit on the throne of Israel, if only your children take heed to their way, to walk before me as you have walked before me.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore, God of Israel, please let your word be verified, which you spoke to your servant David my father."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But will God in very deed dwell on the earth? Behold, heaven and the heaven of heavens can\u2019t contain you; how much less this house that I have built!"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Yet have respect for the prayer of your servant and for his supplication, LORD my God, to listen to the cry and to the prayer which your servant prays before you today;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"that your eyes may be open toward this house night and day, even toward the place of which you have said, \u2018My name shall be there;\u2019 to listen to the prayer which your servant prays toward this place."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Listen to the supplication of your servant, and of your people Israel, when they pray toward this place. Yes, hear in heaven, your dwelling place; and when you hear, forgive."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man sins against his neighbor, and an oath is laid on him to cause him to swear, and he comes and swears before your altar in this house,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"then hear in heaven, and act, and judge your servants, condemning the wicked, to bring his way on his own head, and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen your people Israel are struck down before the enemy because they have sinned against you, if they turn again to you and confess your name, and pray and make supplication to you in this house,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"then hear in heaven, and forgive the sin of your people Israel, and bring them again to the land which you gave to their fathers."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the sky is shut up and there is no rain because they have sinned against you, if they pray toward this place and confess your name, and turn from their sin when you afflict them,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"then hear in heaven, and forgive the sin of your servants, and of your people Israel, when you teach them the good way in which they should walk; and send rain on your land which you have given to your people for an inheritance."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf there is famine in the land, if there is pestilence, if there is blight, mildew, locust or caterpillar; if their enemy besieges them in the land of their cities, whatever plague, whatever sickness there is,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"whatever prayer and supplication is made by any man, or by all your people Israel, who shall each know the plague of his own heart, and spread out his hands toward this house,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"then hear in heaven, your dwelling place, and forgive, and act, and give to every man according to all his ways, whose heart you know (for you, even you only, know the hearts of all the children of men);"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"that they may fear you all the days that they live in the land which you gave to our fathers."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover, concerning the foreigner, who is not of your people Israel, when he comes out of a far country for your name\u2019s sake"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"(for they shall hear of your great name and of your mighty hand and of your outstretched arm), when he comes and prays toward this house,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"hear in heaven, your dwelling place, and do according to all that the foreigner calls to you for; that all the peoples of the earth may know your name, to fear you, as do your people Israel, and that they may know that this house which I have built is called by your name."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf your people go out to battle against their enemy, by whatever way you shall send them, and they pray to the LORD toward the city which you have chosen, and toward the house which I have built for your name,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"then hear in heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"If they sin against you (for there is no man who doesn\u2019t sin), and you are angry with them and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captive to the land of the enemy, far off or near;"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"yet if they repent in the land where they are carried captive, and turn again, and make supplication to you in the land of those who carried them captive, saying, \u2018We have sinned and have done perversely; we have dealt wickedly,\u2019"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"if they return to you with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their enemies who carried them captive, and pray to you toward their land which you gave to their fathers, the city which you have chosen and the house which I have built for your name,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"then hear their prayer and their supplication in heaven, your dwelling place, and maintain their cause;"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"and forgive your people who have sinned against you, and all their transgressions in which they have transgressed against you; and give them compassion before those who carried them captive, that they may have compassion on them"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"(for they are your people and your inheritance, which you brought out of Egypt, from the middle of the iron furnace);"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"that your eyes may be open to the supplication of your servant and to the supplication of your people Israel, to listen to them whenever they cry to you."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"For you separated them from among all the peoples of the earth to be your inheritance, as you spoke by Moses your servant, when you brought our fathers out of Egypt, Lord GOD.\u201d"]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"It was so, that when Solomon had finished praying all this prayer and supplication to the LORD, he arose from before the LORD\u2019s altar, from kneeling on his knees with his hands spread out toward heaven."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"He stood and blessed all the assembly of Israel with a loud voice, saying,"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"\u201cBlessed be the LORD, who has given rest to his people Israel, according to all that he promised. There has not failed one word of all his good promise, which he promised by Moses his servant."]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"May the LORD our God be with us as he was with our fathers. Let him not leave us or forsake us,"]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"that he may incline our hearts to him, to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, his statutes, and his ordinances, which he commanded our fathers."]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"Let these my words, with which I have made supplication before the LORD, be near to the LORD our God day and night, that he may maintain the cause of his servant and the cause of his people Israel, as every day requires;"]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"that all the peoples of the earth may know that the LORD himself is God. There is no one else."]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cLet your heart therefore be perfect with the LORD our God, to walk in his statutes, and to keep his commandments, as it is today.\u201d"]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[0,"The king, and all Israel with him, offered sacrifice before the LORD."]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"Solomon offered for the sacrifice of peace offerings, which he offered to the LORD, twenty two thousand head of cattle and one hundred twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the children of Israel dedicated the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"The same day the king made the middle of the court holy that was before the LORD\u2019s house; for there he offered the burnt offering, the meal offering, and the fat of the peace offerings, because the bronze altar that was before the LORD was too little to receive the burnt offering, the meal offering, and the fat of the peace offerings."]]},{v:65,p:1,l:[[0,"So Solomon held the feast at that time, and all Israel with him, a great assembly, from the entrance of Hamath to the brook of Egypt, before the LORD our God, seven days and seven more days, even fourteen days."]]},{v:66,l:[[0,"On the eighth day he sent the people away; and they blessed the king, and went to their tents joyful and glad in their hearts for all the goodness that the LORD had shown to David his servant, and to Israel his people."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Solomon had finished the building of the LORD\u2019s house, the king\u2019s house, and all Solomon\u2019s desire which he was pleased to do,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared to Solomon the second time, as he had appeared to him at Gibeon."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cI have heard your prayer and your supplication that you have made before me. I have made this house holy, which you have built, to put my name there forever; and my eyes and my heart shall be there perpetually."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"As for you, if you will walk before me as David your father walked, in integrity of heart and in uprightness, to do according to all that I have commanded you, and will keep my statutes and my ordinances,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"then I will establish the throne of your kingdom over Israel forever, as I promised to David your father, saying, \u2018There shall not fail from you a man on the throne of Israel.\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But if you turn away from following me, you or your children, and not keep my commandments and my statutes which I have set before you, but go and serve other gods and worship them,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"then I will cut off Israel out of the land which I have given them; and I will cast this house, which I have made holy for my name, out of my sight; and Israel will be a proverb and a byword among all peoples."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Though this house is so high, yet everyone who passes by it will be astonished and hiss; and they will say, \u2018Why has the LORD done this to this land and to this house?\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and they will answer, \u2018Because they abandoned the LORD their God, who brought their fathers out of the land of Egypt, and embraced other gods, and worshiped them, and served them. Therefore the LORD has brought all this evil on them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of twenty years, in which Solomon had built the two houses, the LORD\u2019s house and the king\u2019s house"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"(now Hiram the king of Tyre had furnished Solomon with cedar trees and cypress trees, and with gold, according to all his desire), King Solomon gave Hiram twenty cities in the land of Galilee."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Hiram came out of Tyre to see the cities which Solomon had given him; and they didn\u2019t please him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhat cities are these which you have given me, my brother?\u201d He called them the land of Cabul to this day."]],f:["\u201cCabul\u201d sounds like Hebrew for \u201cgood-for-nothing\u201d."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Hiram sent to the king one hundred twenty talents of gold."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 120 talents is about 3.6 metric tons"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the reason of the forced labor which King Solomon conscripted: to build the LORD\u2019s house, his own house, Millo, Jerusalem\u2019s wall, Hazor, Megiddo, and Gezer."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Pharaoh king of Egypt had gone up, taken Gezer, burned it with fire, killed the Canaanites who lived in the city, and given it for a wedding gift to his daughter, Solomon\u2019s wife."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Solomon built in the land Gezer, Beth Horon the lower,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Baalath, Tamar in the wilderness,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"all the storage cities that Solomon had, the cities for his chariots, the cities for his horsemen, and that which Solomon desired to build for his pleasure in Jerusalem, and in Lebanon, and in all the land of his dominion."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As for all the people who were left of the Amorites, the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites, who were not of the children of Israel\u2014"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"their children who were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel were not able utterly to destroy\u2014of them Solomon raised a levy of bondservants to this day."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But of the children of Israel Solomon made no bondservants; but they were the men of war, his servants, his princes, his captains, and rulers of his chariots and of his horsemen."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"These were the five hundred fifty chief officers who were over Solomon\u2019s work, who ruled over the people who labored in the work."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"But Pharaoh\u2019s daughter came up out of David\u2019s city to her house which Solomon had built for her. Then he built Millo."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon offered burnt offerings and peace offerings on the altar which he built to the LORD three times per year, burning incense with them on the altar that was before the LORD. So he finished the house."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"King Solomon made a fleet of ships in Ezion Geber, which is beside Eloth, on the shore of the Red Sea, in the land of Edom."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Hiram sent in the fleet his servants, sailors who had knowledge of the sea, with the servants of Solomon."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They came to Ophir, and fetched from there gold, four hundred and twenty talents, and brought it to King Solomon."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 420 talents is about 12.6 metric tons"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon concerning the LORD\u2019s name, she came to test him with hard questions."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"She came to Jerusalem with a very great caravan, with camels that bore spices, very much gold, and precious stones; and when she had come to Solomon, she talked with him about all that was in her heart."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Solomon answered all her questions. There wasn\u2019t anything hidden from the king which he didn\u2019t tell her."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When the queen of Sheba had seen all the wisdom of Solomon, the house that he had built,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"the food of his table, the sitting of his servants, the attendance of his officials, their clothing, his cup bearers, and his ascent by which he went up to the LORD\u2019s house, there was no more spirit in her."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"She said to the king, \u201cIt was a true report that I heard in my own land of your acts and of your wisdom."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"However, I didn\u2019t believe the words until I came and my eyes had seen it. Behold, not even half was told me! Your wisdom and prosperity exceed the fame which I heard."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Happy are your men, happy are these your servants who stand continually before you, who hear your wisdom."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Blessed is the LORD your God, who delighted in you, to set you on the throne of Israel. Because the LORD loved Israel forever, therefore he made you king, to do justice and righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"She gave the king one hundred twenty talents of gold, and a very great quantity of spices, and precious stones. Never again was there such an abundance of spices as these which the queen of Sheba gave to King Solomon."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The fleet of Hiram that brought gold from Ophir also brought in from Ophir great quantities of almug trees and precious stones."]],f:["possibly an Indian sandalwood, with nice grain and a pleasant scent, and good for woodworking"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The king made of the almug trees pillars for the LORD\u2019s house and for the king\u2019s house, harps also and stringed instruments for the singers; no such almug trees came or were seen to this day."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"King Solomon gave to the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatever she asked, in addition to that which Solomon gave her of his royal bounty. So she turned and went to her own land, she and her servants."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred sixty-six talents of gold,"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 666 talents is about 20 metric tons"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"in addition to that which the traders brought, and the traffic of the merchants, and of all the kings of the mixed people, and of the governors of the country."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"King Solomon made two hundred bucklers of beaten gold; six hundred shekels of gold went to one buckler."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.32 Troy ounces, so 600 shekels is about 6 kilograms or 13.2 pounds or 192 Troy ounces."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He made three hundred shields of beaten gold; three minas of gold went to one shield; and the king put them in the House of the Forest of Lebanon."]],f:["A mina is about 600 grams or 1.3 U. S. pounds."]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with the finest gold."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There were six steps to the throne, and the top of the throne was round behind; and there were armrests on either side by the place of the seat, and two lions standing beside the armrests."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other on the six steps. Nothing like it was made in any kingdom."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"All King Solomon\u2019s drinking vessels were of gold, and all the vessels of the House of the Forest of Lebanon were of pure gold. None were of silver, because it was considered of little value in the days of Solomon."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For the king had a fleet of ships of Tarshish at sea with Hiram\u2019s fleet. Once every three years the fleet of Tarshish came bringing gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"So King Solomon exceeded all the kings of the earth in riches and in wisdom."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"All the earth sought the presence of Solomon to hear his wisdom which God had put in his heart."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Year after year, every man brought his tribute, vessels of silver, vessels of gold, clothing, armor, spices, horses, and mules."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon gathered together chariots and horsemen. He had one thousand four hundred chariots and twelve thousand horsemen. He kept them in the chariot cities and with the king at Jerusalem."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The king made silver as common as stones in Jerusalem, and cedars as common as the sycamore trees that are in the lowland."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The horses which Solomon had were brought out of Egypt. The king\u2019s merchants received them in droves, each drove at a price."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"A chariot was imported from Egypt for six hundred shekels of silver, and a horse for one hundred fifty shekels; and so they exported them to all the kings of the Hittites and to the kings of Syria."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now King Solomon loved many foreign women, together with the daughter of Pharaoh: women of the Moabites, Ammonites, Edomites, Sidonians, and Hittites,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"of the nations concerning which the LORD said to the children of Israel, \u201cYou shall not go among them, neither shall they come among you, for surely they will turn away your heart after their gods.\u201d Solomon joined to these in love."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He had seven hundred wives, princesses, and three hundred concubines. His wives turned his heart away."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When Solomon was old, his wives turned away his heart after other gods; and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as the heart of David his father was."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For Solomon went after Ashtoreth the goddess of the Sidonians, and after Milcom the abomination of the Ammonites."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Solomon did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and didn\u2019t go fully after the LORD, as David his father did."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then Solomon built a high place for Chemosh the abomination of Moab, on the mountain that is before Jerusalem, and for Molech the abomination of the children of Ammon."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So he did for all his foreign wives, who burned incense and sacrificed to their gods."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The LORD was angry with Solomon, because his heart was turned away from the LORD, the God of Israel, who had appeared to him twice,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and had commanded him concerning this thing, that he should not go after other gods; but he didn\u2019t keep that which the LORD commanded."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD said to Solomon, \u201cBecause this is done by you, and you have not kept my covenant and my statutes, which I have commanded you, I will surely tear the kingdom from you, and will give it to your servant."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, I will not do it in your days, for David your father\u2019s sake; but I will tear it out of your son\u2019s hand."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"However, I will not tear away all the kingdom; but I will give one tribe to your son, for David my servant\u2019s sake, and for Jerusalem\u2019s sake which I have chosen.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD raised up an adversary to Solomon: Hadad the Edomite. He was one of the king\u2019s offspring in Edom."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For when David was in Edom, and Joab the captain of the army had gone up to bury the slain, and had struck every male in Edom"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"(for Joab and all Israel remained there six months, until he had cut off every male in Edom),"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Hadad fled, he and certain Edomites of his father\u2019s servants with him, to go into Egypt, when Hadad was still a little child."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They arose out of Midian and came to Paran; and they took men with them out of Paran, and they came to Egypt, to Pharaoh king of Egypt, who gave him a house, and appointed him food, and gave him land."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Hadad found great favor in the sight of Pharaoh, so that he gave him as wife the sister of his own wife, the sister of Tahpenes the queen."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The sister of Tahpenes bore him Genubath his son, whom Tahpenes weaned in Pharaoh\u2019s house; and Genubath was in Pharaoh\u2019s house among the sons of Pharaoh."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When Hadad heard in Egypt that David slept with his fathers, and that Joab the captain of the army was dead, Hadad said to Pharaoh, \u201cLet me depart, that I may go to my own country.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Pharaoh said to him, \u201cBut what have you lacked with me, that behold, you seek to go to your own country?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cNothing, however only let me depart.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"God raised up an adversary to him, Rezon the son of Eliada, who had fled from his lord, Hadadezer king of Zobah."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He gathered men to himself, and became captain over a troop, when David killed them of Zobah. They went to Damascus and lived there, and reigned in Damascus."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He was an adversary to Israel all the days of Solomon, in addition to the mischief of Hadad. He abhorred Israel, and reigned over Syria."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Jeroboam the son of Nebat, an Ephraimite of Zeredah, a servant of Solomon, whose mother\u2019s name was Zeruah, a widow, also lifted up his hand against the king."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"This was the reason why he lifted up his hand against the king: Solomon built Millo, and repaired the breach of his father David\u2019s city."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The man Jeroboam was a mighty man of valor; and Solomon saw that the young man was industrious, and he put him in charge of all the labor of the house of Joseph."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"At that time, when Jeroboam went out of Jerusalem, the prophet Ahijah the Shilonite found him on the way. Now Ahijah had clad himself with a new garment; and the two of them were alone in the field."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Ahijah took the new garment that was on him, and tore it in twelve pieces."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He said to Jeroboam, \u201cTake ten pieces; for the LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018Behold, I will tear the kingdom out of the hand of Solomon and will give ten tribes to you"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"(but he shall have one tribe, for my servant David\u2019s sake and for Jerusalem\u2019s sake, the city which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel),"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"because they have forsaken me, and have worshiped Ashtoreth the goddess of the Sidonians, Chemosh the god of Moab, and Milcom the god of the children of Ammon. They have not walked in my ways, to do that which is right in my eyes, and to keep my statutes and my ordinances, as David his father did."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018However, I will not take the whole kingdom out of his hand, but I will make him prince all the days of his life for David my servant\u2019s sake whom I chose, who kept my commandments and my statutes,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"but I will take the kingdom out of his son\u2019s hand and will give it to you, even ten tribes."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"I will give one tribe to his son, that David my servant may have a lamp always before me in Jerusalem, the city which I have chosen for myself to put my name there."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"I will take you, and you shall reign according to all that your soul desires, and shall be king over Israel."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"It shall be, if you will listen to all that I command you, and will walk in my ways, and do that which is right in my eyes, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as David my servant did, that I will be with you, and will build you a sure house, as I built for David, and will give Israel to you."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"I will afflict the offspring of David for this, but not forever.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Solomon sought to kill Jeroboam, but Jeroboam arose and fled into Egypt, to Shishak king of Egypt, and was in Egypt until the death of Solomon."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Solomon, and all that he did, and his wisdom, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the acts of Solomon?"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"The time that Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel was forty years."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Solomon slept with his fathers, and was buried in his father David\u2019s city; and Rehoboam his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Rehoboam went to Shechem, for all Israel had come to Shechem to make him king."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When Jeroboam the son of Nebat heard of it (for he was yet in Egypt, where he had fled from the presence of King Solomon, and Jeroboam lived in Egypt;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and they sent and called him), Jeroboam and all the assembly of Israel came, and spoke to Rehoboam, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cYour father made our yoke difficult. Now therefore make the hard service of your father, and his heavy yoke which he put on us, lighter, and we will serve you.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDepart for three days, then come back to me.\u201d"],[0,"So the people departed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"King Rehoboam took counsel with the old men who had stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, saying, \u201cWhat counsel do you give me to answer these people?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They replied, \u201cIf you will be a servant to this people today, and will serve them, and answer them with good words, then they will be your servants forever.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"But he abandoned the counsel of the old men which they had given him, and took counsel with the young men who had grown up with him, who stood before him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat counsel do you give, that we may answer these people who have spoken to me, saying, \u2018Make the yoke that your father put on us lighter\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The young men who had grown up with him said to him, \u201cTell these people who spoke to you, saying, \u2018Your father made our yoke heavy, but make it lighter to us\u2019\u2014tell them, \u2018My little finger is thicker than my father\u2019s waist."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now my father burdened you with a heavy yoke, but I will add to your yoke. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jeroboam and all the people came to Rehoboam the third day, as the king asked, saying, \u201cCome to me again the third day.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The king answered the people roughly, and abandoned the counsel of the old men which they had given him,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and spoke to them according to the counsel of the young men, saying, \u201cMy father made your yoke heavy, but I will add to your yoke. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king didn\u2019t listen to the people; for it was a thing brought about from the LORD, that he might establish his word, which the LORD spoke by Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam the son of Nebat."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When all Israel saw that the king didn\u2019t listen to them, the people answered the king, saying, \u201cWhat portion have we in David? We don\u2019t have an inheritance in the son of Jesse. To your tents, Israel! Now see to your own house, David.\u201d So Israel departed to their tents."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But as for the children of Israel who lived in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then King Rehoboam sent Adoram, who was over the men subject to forced labor; and all Israel stoned him to death with stones. King Rehoboam hurried to get himself up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"So Israel rebelled against David\u2019s house to this day."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When all Israel heard that Jeroboam had returned, they sent and called him to the congregation, and made him king over all Israel. There was no one who followed David\u2019s house, except for the tribe of Judah only."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When Rehoboam had come to Jerusalem, he assembled all the house of Judah and the tribe of Benjamin, a hundred and eighty thousand chosen men who were warriors, to fight against the house of Israel, to bring the kingdom again to Rehoboam the son of Solomon."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But the word of God came to Shemaiah the man of God, saying,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Rehoboam the son of Solomon, king of Judah, and to all the house of Judah and Benjamin, and to the rest of the people, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u2018The LORD says, \u201cYou shall not go up or fight against your brothers, the children of Israel. Everyone return to his house; for this thing is from me.\u201d\u2019\u201d So they listened to the LORD\u2019s word, and returned and went their way, according to the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeroboam built Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim, and lived in it; and he went out from there and built Penuel."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Jeroboam said in his heart, \u201cNow the kingdom will return to David\u2019s house."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"If this people goes up to offer sacrifices in the LORD\u2019s house at Jerusalem, then the heart of this people will turn again to their lord, even to Rehoboam king of Judah; and they will kill me, and return to Rehoboam king of Judah.\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So the king took counsel, and made two calves of gold; and he said to them, \u201cIt is too much for you to go up to Jerusalem. Look and behold your gods, Israel, which brought you up out of the land of Egypt!\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He set the one in Bethel, and the other he put in Dan."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"This thing became a sin, for the people went even as far as Dan to worship before the one there."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He made houses of high places, and made priests from among all the people, who were not of the sons of Levi."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Jeroboam ordained a feast in the eighth month, on the fifteenth day of the month, like the feast that is in Judah, and he went up to the altar. He did so in Bethel, sacrificing to the calves that he had made, and he placed in Bethel the priests of the high places that he had made."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He went up to the altar which he had made in Bethel on the fifteenth day in the eighth month, even in the month which he had devised of his own heart; and he ordained a feast for the children of Israel, and went up to the altar to burn incense."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, a man of God came out of Judah by the LORD\u2019s word to Bethel; and Jeroboam was standing by the altar to burn incense."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He cried against the altar by the LORD\u2019s word, and said, \u201cAltar! Altar! The LORD says: \u2018Behold, a son will be born to David\u2019s house, Josiah by name. On you he will sacrifice the priests of the high places who burn incense on you, and they will burn men\u2019s bones on you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He gave a sign the same day, saying, \u201cThis is the sign which the LORD has spoken: Behold, the altar will be split apart, and the ashes that are on it will be poured out.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When the king heard the saying of the man of God, which he cried against the altar in Bethel, Jeroboam put out his hand from the altar, saying, \u201cSeize him!\u201d His hand, which he put out against him, dried up, so that he could not draw it back again to himself."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The altar was also split apart, and the ashes poured out from the altar, according to the sign which the man of God had given by the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The king answered the man of God, \u201cNow intercede for the favor of the LORD your God, and pray for me, that my hand may be restored to me.\u201d"],[0,"The man of God interceded with the LORD, and the king\u2019s hand was restored to him, and became as it was before."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to the man of God, \u201cCome home with me and refresh yourself, and I will give you a reward.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The man of God said to the king, \u201cEven if you gave me half of your house, I would not go in with you, neither would I eat bread nor drink water in this place;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"for so was it commanded me by the LORD\u2019s word, saying, \u2018You shall eat no bread, drink no water, and don\u2019t return by the way that you came.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So he went another way, and didn\u2019t return by the way that he came to Bethel."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now an old prophet lived in Bethel, and one of his sons came and told him all the works that the man of God had done that day in Bethel. They also told their father the words which he had spoken to the king."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Their father said to them, \u201cWhich way did he go?\u201d Now his sons had seen which way the man of God went, who came from Judah."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He said to his sons, \u201cSaddle the donkey for me.\u201d So they saddled the donkey for him; and he rode on it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He went after the man of God, and found him sitting under an oak. He said to him, \u201cAre you the man of God who came from Judah?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to him, \u201cCome home with me and eat bread.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI may not return with you, nor go in with you. I will not eat bread or drink water with you in this place."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For it was said to me by the LORD\u2019s word, \u2018You shall eat no bread or drink water there, and don\u2019t turn again to go by the way that you came.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cI also am a prophet as you are; and an angel spoke to me by the LORD\u2019s word, saying, \u2018Bring him back with you into your house, that he may eat bread and drink water.\u2019\u201d He lied to him."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So he went back with him, ate bread in his house, and drank water."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As they sat at the table, the LORD\u2019s word came to the prophet who brought him back;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and he cried out to the man of God who came from Judah, saying, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Because you have been disobedient to the LORD\u2019s word, and have not kept the commandment which the LORD your God commanded you,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"but came back, and have eaten bread and drank water in the place of which he said to you, \u201cEat no bread, and drink no water,\u201d your body will not come to the tomb of your fathers.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"After he had eaten bread and after he drank, he saddled the donkey for the prophet whom he had brought back."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When he had gone, a lion met him by the way and killed him. His body was thrown on the path, and the donkey stood by it. The lion also stood by the body."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Behold, men passed by and saw the body thrown on the path, and the lion standing by the body; and they came and told it in the city where the old prophet lived."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When the prophet who brought him back from the way heard of it, he said, \u201cIt is the man of God who was disobedient to the LORD\u2019s word. Therefore the LORD has delivered him to the lion, which has mauled him and slain him, according to the LORD\u2019s word which he spoke to him.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He said to his sons, saying, \u201cSaddle the donkey for me,\u201d and they saddled it."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He went and found his body thrown on the path, and the donkey and the lion standing by the body. The lion had not eaten the body nor mauled the donkey."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The prophet took up the body of the man of God, and laid it on the donkey, and brought it back. He came to the city of the old prophet to mourn, and to bury him."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He laid his body in his own grave; and they mourned over him, saying, \u201cAlas, my brother!\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"After he had buried him, he spoke to his sons, saying, \u201cWhen I am dead, bury me in the tomb in which the man of God is buried. Lay my bones beside his bones."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For the saying which he cried by the LORD\u2019s word against the altar in Bethel, and against all the houses of the high places which are in the cities of Samaria, will surely happen.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"After this thing, Jeroboam didn\u2019t turn from his evil way, but again made priests of the high places from among all the people. Whoever wanted to, he consecrated him, that there might be priests of the high places."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"This thing became sin to the house of Jeroboam, even to cut it off and to destroy it from off the surface of the earth."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time Abijah the son of Jeroboam became sick."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jeroboam said to his wife, \u201cPlease get up and disguise yourself, so that you won\u2019t be recognized as Jeroboam\u2019s wife. Go to Shiloh. Behold, Ahijah the prophet is there, who said that I would be king over this people."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Take with you ten loaves of bread, some cakes, and a jar of honey, and go to him. He will tell you what will become of the child.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jeroboam\u2019s wife did so, and arose and went to Shiloh, and came to Ahijah\u2019s house. Now Ahijah could not see, for his eyes were set by reason of his age."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Ahijah, \u201cBehold, Jeroboam\u2019s wife is coming to inquire of you concerning her son, for he is sick. Tell her such and such; for it will be, when she comes in, that she will pretend to be another woman.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"So when Ahijah heard the sound of her feet as she came in at the door, he said, \u201cCome in, Jeroboam\u2019s wife! Why do you pretend to be another? For I am sent to you with heavy news."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Go, tell Jeroboam, \u2018The LORD, the God of Israel, says: \u201cBecause I exalted you from among the people, and made you prince over my people Israel,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and tore the kingdom away from David\u2019s house, and gave it to you; and yet you have not been as my servant David, who kept my commandments, and who followed me with all his heart, to do that only which was right in my eyes,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but have done evil above all who were before you, and have gone and made for yourself other gods, molten images, to provoke me to anger, and have cast me behind your back,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"therefore, behold, I will bring evil on the house of Jeroboam, and will cut off from Jeroboam everyone who urinates on a wall, he who is shut up and he who is left at large in Israel, and will utterly sweep away the house of Jeroboam, as a man sweeps away dung until it is all gone."]],f:["or, male"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The dogs will eat whoever belongs to Jeroboam who dies in the city; and the birds of the sky will eat whoever dies in the field, for the LORD has spoken it.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Arise therefore, and go to your house. When your feet enter into the city, the child will die."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"All Israel will mourn for him and bury him; for he only of Jeroboam will come to the grave, because in him there is found some good thing toward the LORD, the God of Israel, in the house of Jeroboam."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD will raise up a king for himself over Israel who will cut off the house of Jeroboam. This is the day! What? Even now."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For the LORD will strike Israel, as a reed is shaken in the water; and he will root up Israel out of this good land which he gave to their fathers, and will scatter them beyond the River, because they have made their Asherah poles, provoking the LORD to anger."]],f:["That is, the Euphrates."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He will give Israel up because of the sins of Jeroboam, which he has sinned, and with which he has made Israel to sin.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jeroboam\u2019s wife arose and departed, and came to Tirzah. As she came to the threshold of the house, the child died."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All Israel buried him and mourned for him, according to the LORD\u2019s word, which he spoke by his servant Ahijah the prophet."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The rest of the acts of Jeroboam, how he fought and how he reigned, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The days which Jeroboam reigned were twenty two years; then he slept with his fathers, and Nadab his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Rehoboam the son of Solomon reigned in Judah. Rehoboam was forty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city which the LORD had chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, to put his name there. His mother\u2019s name was Naamah the Ammonitess."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Judah did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and they provoked him to jealousy with their sins which they committed, above all that their fathers had done."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For they also built for themselves high places, sacred pillars, and Asherah poles on every high hill and under every green tree."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"There were also sodomites in the land. They did according to all the abominations of the nations which the LORD drove out before the children of Israel."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fifth year of King Rehoboam, Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and he took away the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house and the treasures of the king\u2019s house. He even took away all of it, including all the gold shields which Solomon had made."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"King Rehoboam made shields of bronze in their place, and committed them to the hands of the captains of the guard, who guarded the door of the king\u2019s house."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"It was so, that as often as the king went into the LORD\u2019s house, the guard bore them, and brought them back into the guard room."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Rehoboam, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"There was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam continually."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Rehoboam slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David\u2019s city. His mother\u2019s name was Naamah the Ammonitess. Abijam his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the eighteenth year of King Jeroboam the son of Nebat, Abijam began to reign over Judah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He reigned three years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Maacah the daughter of Abishalom."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He walked in all the sins of his father, which he had done before him; and his heart was not perfect with the LORD his God, as the heart of David his father."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Nevertheless for David\u2019s sake, the LORD his God gave him a lamp in Jerusalem, to set up his son after him and to establish Jerusalem;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"because David did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, and didn\u2019t turn away from anything that he commanded him all the days of his life, except only in the matter of Uriah the Hittite."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now there was war between Rehoboam and Jeroboam all the days of his life."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The rest of the acts of Abijam, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah? There was war between Abijam and Jeroboam."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Abijam slept with his fathers, and they buried him in David\u2019s city; and Asa his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twentieth year of Jeroboam king of Israel, Asa began to reign over Judah."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He reigned forty-one years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Maacah the daughter of Abishalom."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Asa did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, as David his father did."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He put away the sodomites out of the land, and removed all the idols that his fathers had made."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He also removed Maacah his mother from being queen, because she had made an abominable image for an Asherah. Asa cut down her image and burned it at the brook Kidron."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But the high places were not taken away. Nevertheless the heart of Asa was perfect with the LORD all his days."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He brought into the LORD\u2019s house the things that his father had dedicated, and the things that he himself had dedicated: silver, gold, and utensils."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"There was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel all their days."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah, and built Ramah, that he might not allow anyone to go out or come in to Asa king of Judah."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then Asa took all the silver and the gold that was left in the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house, and the treasures of the king\u2019s house, and delivered it into the hand of his servants. Then King Asa sent them to Ben Hadad, the son of Tabrimmon, the son of Hezion, king of Syria, who lived at Damascus, saying,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"\u201cLet there be a treaty between me and you, like that between my father and your father. Behold, I have sent to you a present of silver and gold. Go, break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Ben Hadad listened to King Asa, and sent the captains of his armies against the cities of Israel, and struck Ijon, and Dan, and Abel Beth Maacah, and all Chinneroth, with all the land of Naphtali."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When Baasha heard of it, he stopped building Ramah, and lived in Tirzah."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Then King Asa made a proclamation to all Judah. No one was exempted. They carried away the stones of Ramah, and its timber, with which Baasha had built; and King Asa used it to build Geba of Benjamin, and Mizpah."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now the rest of all the acts of Asa, and all his might, and all that he did, and the cities which he built, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah? But in the time of his old age he was diseased in his feet."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Asa slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David\u2019s city; and Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Nadab the son of Jeroboam began to reign over Israel in the second year of Asa king of Judah; and he reigned over Israel two years."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and walked in the way of his father, and in his sin with which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Baasha the son of Ahijah, of the house of Issachar, conspired against him; and Baasha struck him at Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines; for Nadab and all Israel were besieging Gibbethon."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Even in the third year of Asa king of Judah, Baasha killed him and reigned in his place."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"As soon as he was king, he struck all the house of Jeroboam. He didn\u2019t leave to Jeroboam any who breathed, until he had destroyed him, according to the saying of the LORD, which he spoke by his servant Ahijah the Shilonite;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"for the sins of Jeroboam which he sinned, and with which he made Israel to sin, because of his provocation with which he provoked the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Nadab, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"There was war between Asa and Baasha king of Israel all their days."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"In the third year of Asa king of Judah, Baasha the son of Ahijah began to reign over all Israel in Tirzah for twenty-four years."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and walked in the way of Jeroboam, and in his sin with which he made Israel to sin."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Jehu the son of Hanani against Baasha, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cBecause I exalted you out of the dust and made you prince over my people Israel, and you have walked in the way of Jeroboam and have made my people Israel to sin, to provoke me to anger with their sins,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"behold, I will utterly sweep away Baasha and his house; and I will make your house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The dogs will eat Baasha\u2019s descendants who die in the city; and he who dies of his in the field, the birds of the sky will eat.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Baasha, and what he did, and his might, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Baasha slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirzah; and Elah his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came by the prophet Jehu the son of Hanani against Baasha and against his house, both because of all the evil that he did in the LORD\u2019s sight, to provoke him to anger with the work of his hands, in being like the house of Jeroboam, and because he struck him."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twenty-sixth year of Asa king of Judah, Elah the son of Baasha began to reign over Israel in Tirzah for two years."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"His servant Zimri, captain of half his chariots, conspired against him. Now he was in Tirzah, drinking himself drunk in the house of Arza, who was over the household in Tirzah;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and Zimri went in and struck him and killed him in the twenty-seventh year of Asa king of Judah, and reigned in his place."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When he began to reign, as soon as he sat on his throne, he attacked all the house of Baasha. He didn\u2019t leave him a single one who urinates on a wall among his relatives or his friends."]],f:["or, male"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Thus Zimri destroyed all the house of Baasha, according to the LORD\u2019s word which he spoke against Baasha by Jehu the prophet,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"for all the sins of Baasha, and the sins of Elah his son, which they sinned and with which they made Israel to sin, to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger with their vanities."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Elah, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twenty-seventh year of Asa king of Judah, Zimri reigned seven days in Tirzah. Now the people were encamped against Gibbethon, which belonged to the Philistines."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The people who were encamped heard that Zimri had conspired, and had also killed the king. Therefore all Israel made Omri, the captain of the army, king over Israel that day in the camp."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Omri went up from Gibbethon, and all Israel with him, and they besieged Tirzah."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When Zimri saw that the city was taken, he went into the fortified part of the king\u2019s house and burned the king\u2019s house over him with fire, and died,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"for his sins which he sinned in doing that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, in walking in the way of Jeroboam, and in his sin which he did to make Israel to sin."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Zimri, and his treason that he committed, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the people of Israel were divided into two parts: half of the people followed Tibni the son of Ginath, to make him king, and half followed Omri."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But the people who followed Omri prevailed against the people who followed Tibni the son of Ginath; so Tibni died, and Omri reigned."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"In the thirty-first year of Asa king of Judah, Omri began to reign over Israel for twelve years. He reigned six years in Tirzah."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He bought the hill Samaria of Shemer for two talents of silver; and he built on the hill, and called the name of the city which he built, Samaria, after the name of Shemer, the owner of the hill."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Omri did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and dealt wickedly above all who were before him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For he walked in all the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and in his sins with which he made Israel to sin, to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger with their vanities."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Omri which he did, and his might that he showed, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So Omri slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria; and Ahab his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"In the thirty-eighth year of Asa king of Judah, Ahab the son of Omri began to reign over Israel. Ahab the son of Omri reigned over Israel in Samaria twenty-two years."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Ahab the son of Omri did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight above all that were before him."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"As if it had been a light thing for him to walk in the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, he took as wife Jezebel the daughter of Ethbaal king of the Sidonians, and went and served Baal and worshiped him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He raised up an altar for Baal in the house of Baal, which he had built in Samaria."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Ahab made the Asherah; and Ahab did more yet to provoke the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger than all the kings of Israel who were before him."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"In his days Hiel the Bethelite built Jericho. He laid its foundation with the loss of Abiram his firstborn, and set up its gates with the loss of his youngest son Segub, according to the LORD\u2019s word, which he spoke by Joshua the son of Nun."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah the Tishbite, who was one of the settlers of Gilead, said to Ahab, \u201cAs the LORD, the God of Israel, lives, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to him, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cGo away from here, turn eastward, and hide yourself by the brook Cherith, that is before the Jordan."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall drink from the brook. I have commanded the ravens to feed you there.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So he went and did according to the LORD\u2019s word, for he went and lived by the brook Cherith that is before the Jordan."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The ravens brought him bread and meat in the morning, and bread and meat in the evening; and he drank from the brook."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"After a while, the brook dried up, because there was no rain in the land."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to him, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cArise, go to Zarephath, which belongs to Sidon, and stay there. Behold, I have commanded a widow there to sustain you.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So he arose and went to Zarephath; and when he came to the gate of the city, behold, a widow was there gathering sticks. He called to her and said, \u201cPlease get me a little water in a jar, that I may drink.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"As she was going to get it, he called to her and said, \u201cPlease bring me a morsel of bread in your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cAs the LORD your God lives, I don\u2019t have anything baked, but only a handful of meal in a jar and a little oil in a jar. Behold, I am gathering two sticks, that I may go in and bake it for me and my son, that we may eat it, and die.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said to her, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid. Go and do as you have said; but make me a little cake from it first, and bring it out to me, and afterward make some for you and for your son."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For the LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018The jar of meal will not run out, and the jar of oil will not fail, until the day that the LORD sends rain on the earth.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"She went and did according to the saying of Elijah; and she, he, and her household ate many days."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The jar of meal didn\u2019t run out and the jar of oil didn\u2019t fail, according to the LORD\u2019s word, which he spoke by Elijah."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, the son of the woman, the mistress of the house, became sick; and his sickness was so severe that there was no breath left in him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"She said to Elijah, \u201cWhat have I to do with you, you man of God? You have come to me to bring my sin to memory, and to kill my son!\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cGive me your son.\u201d He took him out of her bosom, and carried him up into the room where he stayed, and laid him on his own bed."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He cried to the LORD and said, \u201cLORD my God, have you also brought evil on the widow with whom I am staying, by killing her son?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He stretched himself on the child three times, and cried to the LORD and said, \u201cLORD my God, please let this child\u2019s soul come into him again.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD listened to the voice of Elijah; and the soul of the child came into him again, and he revived."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Elijah took the child and brought him down out of the room into the house, and delivered him to his mother; and Elijah said, \u201cBehold, your son lives.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said to Elijah, \u201cNow I know that you are a man of God, and that the LORD\u2019s word in your mouth is truth.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After many days, the LORD\u2019s word came to Elijah, in the third year, saying, \u201cGo, show yourself to Ahab; and I will send rain on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah went to show himself to Ahab. The famine was severe in Samaria."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Ahab called Obadiah, who was over the household. (Now Obadiah feared the LORD greatly;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for when Jezebel cut off the LORD\u2019s prophets, Obadiah took one hundred prophets, and hid them fifty to a cave, and fed them with bread and water.)"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ahab said to Obadiah, \u201cGo through the land, to all the springs of water, and to all the brooks. Perhaps we may find grass and save the horses and mules alive, that we not lose all the animals.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"So they divided the land between them to pass throughout it. Ahab went one way by himself, and Obadiah went another way by himself."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"As Obadiah was on the way, behold, Elijah met him. He recognized him, and fell on his face, and said, \u201cIs it you, my lord Elijah?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered him, \u201cIt is I. Go, tell your lord, \u2018Behold, Elijah is here!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cHow have I sinned, that you would deliver your servant into the hand of Ahab, to kill me?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As the LORD your God lives, there is no nation or kingdom where my lord has not sent to seek you. When they said, \u2018He is not here,\u2019 he took an oath of the kingdom and nation that they didn\u2019t find you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now you say, \u2018Go, tell your lord, \u201cBehold, Elijah is here.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It will happen, as soon as I leave you, that the LORD\u2019s Spirit will carry you I don\u2019t know where; and so when I come and tell Ahab, and he can\u2019t find you, he will kill me. But I, your servant, have feared the LORD from my youth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Wasn\u2019t it told my lord what I did when Jezebel killed the LORD\u2019s prophets, how I hid one hundred men of the LORD\u2019s prophets with fifty to a cave, and fed them with bread and water?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now you say, \u2018Go, tell your lord, \u201cBehold, Elijah is here\u201d.\u2019 He will kill me.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said, \u201cAs the LORD of Armies lives, before whom I stand, I will surely show myself to him today.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So Obadiah went to meet Ahab, and told him; and Ahab went to meet Elijah."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When Ahab saw Elijah, Ahab said to him, \u201cIs that you, you troubler of Israel?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cI have not troubled Israel, but you and your father\u2019s house, in that you have forsaken the LORD\u2019s commandments and you have followed the Baals."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now therefore send, and gather to me all Israel to Mount Carmel, and four hundred fifty of the prophets of Baal, and four hundred of the prophets of the Asherah, who eat at Jezebel\u2019s table.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"So Ahab sent to all the children of Israel, and gathered the prophets together to Mount Carmel."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Elijah came near to all the people, and said, \u201cHow long will you waver between the two sides? If the LORD is God, follow him; but if Baal, then follow him.\u201d"],[0,"The people didn\u2019t say a word."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Elijah said to the people, \u201cI, even I only, am left as a prophet of the LORD; but Baal\u2019s prophets are four hundred fifty men."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Let them therefore give us two bulls; and let them choose one bull for themselves, and cut it in pieces, and lay it on the wood, and put no fire under; and I will dress the other bull, and lay it on the wood, and put no fire under it."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You call on the name of your god, and I will call on the LORD\u2019s name. The God who answers by fire, let him be God.\u201d"],[0,"All the people answered, \u201cWhat you say is good.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said to the prophets of Baal, \u201cChoose one bull for yourselves, and dress it first, for you are many; and call on the name of your god, but put no fire under it.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"They took the bull which was given them, and they dressed it, and called on the name of Baal from morning even until noon, saying, \u201cBaal, hear us!\u201d But there was no voice, and nobody answered. They leaped about the altar which was made."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"At noon, Elijah mocked them, and said, \u201cCry aloud, for he is a god. Either he is deep in thought, or he has gone somewhere, or he is on a journey, or perhaps he sleeps and must be awakened.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They cried aloud, and cut themselves in their way with knives and lances until the blood gushed out on them."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"When midday was past, they prophesied until the time of the evening offering; but there was no voice, no answer, and nobody paid attention."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said to all the people, \u201cCome near to me!\u201d; and all the people came near to him. He repaired the LORD\u2019s altar that had been thrown down."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Elijah took twelve stones, according to the number of the tribes of the sons of Jacob, to whom the LORD\u2019s word came, saying, \u201cIsrael shall be your name.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"With the stones he built an altar in the LORD\u2019s name. He made a trench around the altar large enough to contain two seahs of seed."]],f:["1 seah is about 7 liters or 1.9 gallons or 0.8 pecks"]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He put the wood in order, and cut the bull in pieces and laid it on the wood. He said, \u201cFill four jars with water, and pour it on the burnt offering and on the wood.\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cDo it a second time;\u201d and they did it the second time. He said, \u201cDo it a third time;\u201d and they did it the third time."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The water ran around the altar; and he also filled the trench with water."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"At the time of the evening offering, Elijah the prophet came near and said, \u201cLORD, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Israel, let it be known today that you are God in Israel and that I am your servant, and that I have done all these things at your word."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Hear me, LORD, hear me, that this people may know that you, LORD, are God, and that you have turned their heart back again.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s fire fell and consumed the burnt offering, the wood, the stones, and the dust; and it licked up the water that was in the trench."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"When all the people saw it, they fell on their faces. They said, \u201cThe LORD, he is God! The LORD, he is God!\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said to them, \u201cSeize the prophets of Baal! Don\u2019t let one of them escape!\u201d"],[0,"They seized them; and Elijah brought them down to the brook Kishon, and killed them there."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said to Ahab, \u201cGet up, eat and drink; for there is the sound of abundance of rain.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"So Ahab went up to eat and to drink. Elijah went up to the top of Carmel; and he bowed himself down on the earth, and put his face between his knees."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He said to his servant, \u201cGo up now and look toward the sea.\u201d"],[0,"He went up and looked, then said, \u201cThere is nothing.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cGo again\u201d seven times."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"On the seventh time, he said, \u201cBehold, a small cloud, like a man\u2019s hand, is rising out of the sea.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cGo up, tell Ahab, \u2018Get ready and go down, so that the rain doesn\u2019t stop you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"In a little while, the sky grew black with clouds and wind, and there was a great rain. Ahab rode, and went to Jezreel."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s hand was on Elijah; and he tucked his cloak into his belt and ran before Ahab to the entrance of Jezreel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahab told Jezebel all that Elijah had done, and how he had killed all the prophets with the sword."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Jezebel sent a messenger to Elijah, saying, \u201cSo let the gods do to me, and more also, if I don\u2019t make your life as the life of one of them by tomorrow about this time!\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"When he saw that, he arose and ran for his life, and came to Beersheba, which belongs to Judah, and left his servant there."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But he himself went a day\u2019s journey into the wilderness, and came and sat down under a juniper tree. Then he requested for himself that he might die, and said, \u201cIt is enough. Now, O LORD, take away my life; for I am not better than my fathers.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He lay down and slept under a juniper tree; and behold, an angel touched him, and said to him, \u201cArise and eat!\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He looked, and behold, there was at his head a cake baked on the coals, and a jar of water. He ate and drank, and lay down again."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel came again the second time, and touched him, and said, \u201cArise and eat, because the journey is too great for you.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose, and ate and drank, and went in the strength of that food forty days and forty nights to Horeb, God\u2019s Mountain."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He came to a cave there, and camped there; and behold, the LORD\u2019s word came to him, and he said to him, \u201cWhat are you doing here, Elijah?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI have been very jealous for the LORD, the God of Armies; for the children of Israel have forsaken your covenant, thrown down your altars, and killed your prophets with the sword. I, even I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGo out and stand on the mountain before the LORD.\u201d"],[0,"Behold, the LORD passed by, and a great and strong wind tore the mountains and broke in pieces the rocks before the LORD; but the LORD was not in the wind. After the wind there was an earthquake; but the LORD was not in the earthquake."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"After the earthquake a fire passed; but the LORD was not in the fire. After the fire, there was a still small voice."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When Elijah heard it, he wrapped his face in his mantle, went out, and stood in the entrance of the cave. Behold, a voice came to him, and said, \u201cWhat are you doing here, Elijah?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI have been very jealous for the LORD, the God of Armies; for the children of Israel have forsaken your covenant, thrown down your altars, and killed your prophets with the sword. I, even I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cGo, return on your way to the wilderness of Damascus. When you arrive, anoint Hazael to be king over Syria."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Anoint Jehu the son of Nimshi to be king over Israel; and anoint Elisha the son of Shaphat of Abel Meholah to be prophet in your place."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He who escapes from the sword of Hazael, Jehu will kill; and he who escapes from the sword of Jehu, Elisha will kill."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Yet I reserved seven thousand in Israel, all the knees of which have not bowed to Baal, and every mouth that has not kissed him.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So he departed from there and found Elisha the son of Shaphat, who was plowing with twelve yoke of oxen before him, and he with the twelfth. Elijah went over to him and put his mantle on him."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Elisha left the oxen and ran after Elijah, and said, \u201cLet me please kiss my father and my mother, and then I will follow you.\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cGo back again; for what have I done to you?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He returned from following him, and took the yoke of oxen, killed them, and boiled their meat with the oxen\u2019s equipment, and gave to the people; and they ate. Then he arose, and went after Elijah, and served him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Ben Hadad the king of Syria gathered all his army together; and there were thirty-two kings with him, with horses and chariots. He went up and besieged Samaria, and fought against it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He sent messengers into the city to Ahab king of Israel and said to him, \u201cBen Hadad says,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u2018Your silver and your gold are mine. Your wives also and your children, even the best, are mine.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel answered, \u201cIt is according to your saying, my lord, O king. I am yours, and all that I have.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The messengers came again and said, \u201cBen Hadad says, \u2018I sent indeed to you, saying, \u201cYou shall deliver me your silver, your gold, your wives, and your children;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but I will send my servants to you tomorrow about this time, and they will search your house and the houses of your servants. Whatever is pleasant in your eyes, they will put it in their hand, and take it away.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king of Israel called all the elders of the land, and said, \u201cPlease notice how this man seeks mischief; for he sent to me for my wives, and for my children, and for my silver, and for my gold; and I didn\u2019t deny him.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"All the elders and all the people said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t listen, and don\u2019t consent.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore he said to the messengers of Ben Hadad, \u201cTell my lord the king, \u2018All that you sent for to your servant at the first I will do, but this thing I cannot do.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"The messengers departed and brought him back the message."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Ben Hadad sent to him, and said, \u201cThe gods do so to me, and more also, if the dust of Samaria will be enough for handfuls for all the people who follow me.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel answered, \u201cTell him, \u2018Don\u2019t let him who puts on his armor brag like he who takes it off.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When Ben Hadad heard this message as he was drinking, he and the kings in the pavilions, he said to his servants, \u201cPrepare to attack!\u201d So they prepared to attack the city."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, a prophet came near to Ahab king of Israel, and said, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Have you seen all this great multitude? Behold, I will deliver it into your hand today. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahab said, \u201cBy whom?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018By the young men of the princes of the provinces.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"Then he said, \u201cWho shall begin the battle?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cYou.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he mustered the young men of the princes of the provinces, and they were two hundred and thirty-two. After them, he mustered all the people, even all the children of Israel, being seven thousand."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They went out at noon. But Ben Hadad was drinking himself drunk in the pavilions, he and the kings, the thirty-two kings who helped him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The young men of the princes of the provinces went out first; and Ben Hadad sent out, and they told him, saying, \u201cMen are coming out from Samaria.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIf they have come out for peace, take them alive; or if they have come out for war, take them alive.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So these went out of the city, the young men of the princes of the provinces, and the army which followed them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They each killed his man. The Syrians fled, and Israel pursued them. Ben Hadad the king of Syria escaped on a horse with horsemen."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The king of Israel went out and struck the horses and chariots, and killed the Syrians with a great slaughter."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The prophet came near to the king of Israel and said to him, \u201cGo, strengthen yourself, and plan what you must do, for at the return of the year, the king of Syria will come up against you.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The servants of the king of Syria said to him, \u201cTheir god is a god of the hills; therefore they were stronger than we. But let\u2019s fight against them in the plain, and surely we will be stronger than they."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Do this thing: take the kings away, every man out of his place, and put captains in their place."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Muster an army like the army that you have lost, horse for horse and chariot for chariot. We will fight against them in the plain, and surely we will be stronger than they are.\u201d"],[0,"He listened to their voice and did so."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"At the return of the year, Ben Hadad mustered the Syrians and went up to Aphek to fight against Israel."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The children of Israel were mustered and given provisions, and went against them. The children of Israel encamped before them like two little flocks of young goats, but the Syrians filled the country."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"A man of God came near and spoke to the king of Israel, and said, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Because the Syrians have said, \u201cThe LORD is a god of the hills, but he is not a god of the valleys,\u201d therefore I will deliver all this great multitude into your hand, and you shall know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"They encamped opposite each other for seven days. Then on the seventh day the battle was joined; and the children of Israel killed one hundred thousand footmen of the Syrians in one day."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But the rest fled to Aphek, into the city; and the wall fell on twenty-seven thousand men who were left. Ben Hadad fled and came into the city, into an inner room."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"His servants said to him, \u201cSee now, we have heard that the kings of the house of Israel are merciful kings. Please let us put sackcloth on our bodies and ropes on our heads, and go out to the king of Israel. Maybe he will save your life.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"So they put sackcloth on their bodies and ropes on their heads, and came to the king of Israel, and said, \u201cYour servant Ben Hadad says, \u2018Please let me live.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cIs he still alive? He is my brother.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the men observed diligently and hurried to take this phrase; and they said, \u201cYour brother Ben Hadad.\u201d"],[0,"Then he said, \u201cGo, bring him.\u201d"],[0,"Then Ben Hadad came out to him; and he caused him to come up into the chariot."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Ben Hadad said to him, \u201cThe cities which my father took from your father I will restore. You shall make streets for yourself in Damascus, as my father made in Samaria.\u201d"],[0,"\u201cI\u201d, said Ahab, \u201cwill let you go with this covenant.\u201d So he made a covenant with him and let him go."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"A certain man of the sons of the prophets said to his fellow by the LORD\u2019s word, \u201cPlease strike me!\u201d"],[0,"The man refused to strike him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Then he said to him, \u201cBecause you have not obeyed the LORD\u2019s voice, behold, as soon as you have departed from me, a lion will kill you.\u201d As soon as he had departed from him, a lion found him and killed him."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he found another man, and said, \u201cPlease strike me.\u201d"],[0,"The man struck him and wounded him."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"So the prophet departed and waited for the king by the way, and disguised himself with his headband over his eyes."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"As the king passed by, he cried to the king, and he said, \u201cYour servant went out into the middle of the battle; and behold, a man came over and brought a man to me, and said, \u2018Guard this man! If by any means he is missing, then your life shall be for his life, or else you shall pay a talent of silver.\u2019"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds"]},{v:40,l:[[0,"As your servant was busy here and there, he was gone.\u201d"],[0,"The king of Israel said to him, \u201cSo shall your judgment be. You yourself have decided it.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"He hurried, and took the headband away from his eyes; and the king of Israel recognized that he was one of the prophets."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Because you have let go out of your hand the man whom I had devoted to destruction, therefore your life will take the place of his life, and your people take the place of his people.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel went to his house sullen and angry, and came to Samaria."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Naboth the Jezreelite had a vineyard which was in Jezreel, next to the palace of Ahab king of Samaria."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Ahab spoke to Naboth, saying, \u201cGive me your vineyard, that I may have it for a garden of herbs, because it is near my house; and I will give you for it a better vineyard than it. Or, if it seems good to you, I will give you its worth in money.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Naboth said to Ahab, \u201cMay the LORD forbid me, that I should give the inheritance of my fathers to you!\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahab came into his house sullen and angry because of the word which Naboth the Jezreelite had spoken to him, for he had said, \u201cI will not give you the inheritance of my fathers.\u201d He laid himself down on his bed, and turned away his face, and would eat no bread."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But Jezebel his wife came to him, and said to him, \u201cWhy is your spirit so sad that you eat no bread?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cBecause I spoke to Naboth the Jezreelite, and said to him, \u2018Give me your vineyard for money; or else, if it pleases you, I will give you another vineyard for it.\u2019 He answered, \u2018I will not give you my vineyard.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jezebel his wife said to him, \u201cDo you now govern the kingdom of Israel? Arise, and eat bread, and let your heart be merry. I will give you the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So she wrote letters in Ahab\u2019s name and sealed them with his seal, and sent the letters to the elders and to the nobles who were in his city, who lived with Naboth."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"She wrote in the letters, saying, \u201cProclaim a fast, and set Naboth on high among the people."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Set two men, wicked fellows, before him, and let them testify against him, saying, \u2018You cursed God and the king!\u2019 Then carry him out, and stone him to death.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of his city, even the elders and the nobles who lived in his city, did as Jezebel had instructed them in the letters which she had written and sent to them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They proclaimed a fast, and set Naboth on high among the people."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The two men, the wicked fellows, came in and sat before him. The wicked fellows testified against him, even against Naboth, in the presence of the people, saying, \u201cNaboth cursed God and the king!\u201d Then they carried him out of the city and stoned him to death with stones."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Then they sent to Jezebel, saying, \u201cNaboth has been stoned and is dead.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jezebel heard that Naboth had been stoned and was dead, Jezebel said to Ahab, \u201cArise, take possession of the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, which he refused to give you for money; for Naboth is not alive, but dead.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When Ahab heard that Naboth was dead, Ahab rose up to go down to the vineyard of Naboth the Jezreelite, to take possession of it."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cArise, go down to meet Ahab king of Israel, who dwells in Samaria. Behold, he is in the vineyard of Naboth, where he has gone down to take possession of it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall speak to him, saying, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cHave you killed and also taken possession?\u201d\u2019 You shall speak to him, saying, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cIn the place where dogs licked the blood of Naboth, dogs will lick your blood, even yours.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahab said to Elijah, \u201cHave you found me, my enemy?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cI have found you, because you have sold yourself to do that which is evil in the LORD\u2019s sight."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Behold, I will bring evil on you, and will utterly sweep you away and will cut off from Ahab everyone who urinates against a wall, and him who is shut up and him who is left at large in Israel."]],f:["or, male"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will make your house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah, for the provocation with which you have provoked me to anger, and have made Israel to sin.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The LORD also spoke of Jezebel, saying, \u201cThe dogs will eat Jezebel by the rampart of Jezreel."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The dogs will eat whoever dies of Ahab in the city; and the birds of the sky will eat whoever dies in the field.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But there was no one like Ahab, who sold himself to do that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, whom Jezebel his wife stirred up."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He did very abominably in following idols, according to all that the Amorites did, whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"When Ahab heard those words, he tore his clothes, put sackcloth on his body, fasted, lay in sackcloth, and went about despondently."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Elijah the Tishbite, saying,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"\u201cSee how Ahab humbles himself before me? Because he humbles himself before me, I will not bring the evil in his days; but I will bring the evil on his house in his son\u2019s day.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"They continued three years without war between Syria and Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In the third year, Jehoshaphat the king of Judah came down to the king of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to his servants, \u201cYou know that Ramoth Gilead is ours, and we do nothing, and don\u2019t take it out of the hand of the king of Syria?\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cWill you go with me to battle to Ramoth Gilead?\u201d"],[0,"Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, \u201cI am as you are, my people as your people, my horses as your horses.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, \u201cPlease inquire first for the LORD\u2019s word.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king of Israel gathered the prophets together, about four hundred men, and said to them, \u201cShould I go against Ramoth Gilead to battle, or should I refrain?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cGo up; for the Lord will deliver it into the hand of the king.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jehoshaphat said, \u201cIsn\u2019t there here a prophet of the LORD, that we may inquire of him?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cThere is yet one man by whom we may inquire of the LORD, Micaiah the son of Imlah; but I hate him, for he does not prophesy good concerning me, but evil.\u201d"],[0,"Jehoshaphat said, \u201cDon\u2019t let the king say so.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king of Israel called an officer, and said, \u201cQuickly get Micaiah the son of Imlah.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah were sitting each on his throne, arrayed in their robes, in an open place at the entrance of the gate of Samaria; and all the prophets were prophesying before them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah made himself horns of iron, and said, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018With these you will push the Syrians, until they are consumed.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"All the prophets prophesied so, saying, \u201cGo up to Ramoth Gilead and prosper; for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The messenger who went to call Micaiah spoke to him, saying, \u201cSee now, the prophets declare good to the king with one mouth. Please let your word be like the word of one of them, and speak good.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, what the LORD says to me, that I will speak.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had come to the king, the king said to him, \u201cMicaiah, shall we go to Ramoth Gilead to battle, or shall we forbear?\u201d"],[0,"He answered him, \u201cGo up and prosper; and the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to him, \u201cHow many times do I have to adjure you that you speak to me nothing but the truth in the LORD\u2019s name?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI saw all Israel scattered on the mountains, as sheep that have no shepherd. The LORD said, \u2018These have no master. Let them each return to his house in peace.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cDidn\u2019t I tell you that he would not prophesy good concerning me, but evil?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cTherefore hear the LORD\u2019s word. I saw the LORD sitting on his throne, and all the army of heaven standing by him on his right hand and on his left."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u2018Who will entice Ahab, that he may go up and fall at Ramoth Gilead?\u2019 One said one thing, and another said another."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"A spirit came out and stood before the LORD, and said, \u2018I will entice him.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u2018How?\u2019"],[0,"He said, \u2018I will go out and will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets.\u2019"],[0,"He said, \u2018You will entice him, and will also prevail. Go out and do so.\u2019"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now therefore, behold, the LORD has put a lying spirit in the mouth of all these your prophets; and the LORD has spoken evil concerning you.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah came near and struck Micaiah on the cheek, and said, \u201cWhich way did the LORD\u2019s Spirit go from me to speak to you?\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cBehold, you will see on that day when you go into an inner room to hide yourself.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said, \u201cTake Micaiah, and carry him back to Amon the governor of the city and to Joash the king\u2019s son."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Say, \u2018The king says, \u201cPut this fellow in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I come in peace.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cIf you return at all in peace, the LORD has not spoken by me.\u201d He said, \u201cListen, all you people!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went up to Ramoth Gilead."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cI will disguise myself and go into the battle, but you put on your robes.\u201d The king of Israel disguised himself and went into the battle."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the king of Syria had commanded the thirty-two captains of his chariots, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t fight with small nor great, except only with the king of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"When the captains of the chariots saw Jehoshaphat, they said, \u201cSurely that is the king of Israel!\u201d and they came over to fight against him. Jehoshaphat cried out."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"When the captains of the chariots saw that it was not the king of Israel, they turned back from pursuing him."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"A certain man drew his bow at random, and struck the king of Israel between the joints of the armor. Therefore he said to the driver of his chariot, \u201cTurn around, and carry me out of the battle, for I am severely wounded.\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The battle increased that day. The king was propped up in his chariot facing the Syrians, and died at evening. The blood ran out of the wound into the bottom of the chariot."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"A cry went throughout the army about the going down of the sun, saying, \u201cEvery man to his city, and every man to his country!\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king died, and was brought to Samaria; and they buried the king in Samaria."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"They washed the chariot by the pool of Samaria; and the dogs licked up his blood where the prostitutes washed themselves, according to the LORD\u2019s word which he spoke."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Ahab, and all that he did, and the ivory house which he built, and all the cities that he built, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"So Ahab slept with his fathers; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat the son of Asa began to reign over Judah in the fourth year of Ahab king of Israel."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat was thirty-five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty-five years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Azubah the daughter of Shilhi."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He walked in all the way of Asa his father. He didn\u2019t turn away from it, doing that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes. However, the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense on the high places."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat made peace with the king of Israel."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, and his might that he showed, and how he fought, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"The remnant of the sodomites, that remained in the days of his father Asa, he put away out of the land."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"There was no king in Edom. A deputy ruled."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat made ships of Tarshish to go to Ophir for gold, but they didn\u2019t go, for the ships wrecked at Ezion Geber."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Then Ahaziah the son of Ahab said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cLet my servants go with your servants in the ships.\u201d But Jehoshaphat would not."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David\u2019s city. Jehoram his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahaziah the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria in the seventeenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and he reigned two years over Israel."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and walked in the way of his father, and in the way of his mother, and in the way of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, in which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"He served Baal and worshiped him, and provoked the LORD, the God of Israel, to anger in all the ways that his father had done so."]]}]]}},1282,[]);
__d(function(e,h,t,a,o,n,i){o.exports={book:"2Kgs",name:"2 Kings",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moab rebelled against Israel after the death of Ahab."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahaziah fell down through the lattice in his upper room that was in Samaria, and was sick. So he sent messengers, and said to them, \u201cGo, inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron, whether I will recover from this sickness.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"But the LORD\u2019s angel said to Elijah the Tishbite, \u201cArise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and tell them, \u2018Is it because there is no God in Israel that you go to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron?"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh).","The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now therefore the LORD says, \u201cYou will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.\u201d\u2019\u201d Then Elijah departed."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The messengers returned to him, and he said to them, \u201cWhy is it that you have returned?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cA man came up to meet us, and said to us, \u2018Go, return to the king who sent you, and tell him, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Is it because there is no God in Israel that you send to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron? Therefore you will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.\u2019\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat kind of man was he who came up to meet you and told you these words?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered him, \u201cHe was a hairy man, and wearing a leather belt around his waist.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cIt\u2019s Elijah the Tishbite.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king sent a captain of fifty with his fifty to him. He went up to him; and behold, he was sitting on the top of the hill. He said to him, \u201cMan of God, the king has said, \u2018Come down!\u2019\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah answered to the captain of fifty, \u201cIf I am a man of God, then let fire come down from the sky and consume you and your fifty!\u201d Then fire came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he sent to him another captain of fifty with his fifty. He answered him, \u201cMan of God, the king has said, \u2018Come down quickly!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah answered them, \u201cIf I am a man of God, then let fire come down from the sky and consume you and your fifty!\u201d Then God\u2019s fire came down from the sky, and consumed him and his fifty."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he sent the captain of a third fifty with his fifty. The third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Elijah, and begged him, and said to him, \u201cMan of God, please let my life and the life of these fifty of your servants be precious in your sight."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Behold, fire came down from the sky and consumed the last two captains of fifty with their fifties. But now let my life be precious in your sight.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel said to Elijah, \u201cGo down with him. Don\u2019t be afraid of him.\u201d"],[0,"Then he arose and went down with him to the king."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Because you have sent messengers to inquire of Baal Zebub, the god of Ekron, is it because there is no God in Israel to inquire of his word? Therefore you will not come down from the bed where you have gone up, but you will surely die.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So he died according to the LORD\u2019s word which Elijah had spoken. Jehoram began to reign in his place in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, because he had no son."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Ahaziah which he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD was about to take Elijah up by a whirlwind into heaven, Elijah went with Elisha from Gilgal."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Elijah said to Elisha, \u201cPlease wait here, for the LORD has sent me as far as Bethel.\u201d"],[0,"Elisha said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\u201d So they went down to Bethel."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of the prophets who were at Bethel came out to Elisha, and said to him, \u201cDo you know that the LORD will take away your master from over you today?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cYes, I know it. Hold your peace.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said to him, \u201cElisha, please wait here, for the LORD has sent me to Jericho.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\u201d So they came to Jericho."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of the prophets who were at Jericho came near to Elisha, and said to him, \u201cDo you know that the LORD will take away your master from over you today?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cYes, I know it. Hold your peace.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Elijah said to him, \u201cPlease wait here, for the LORD has sent me to the Jordan.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\u201d Then they both went on."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Fifty men of the sons of the prophets went and stood opposite them at a distance; and they both stood by the Jordan."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Elijah took his mantle, and rolled it up, and struck the waters; and they were divided here and there, so that they both went over on dry ground."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When they had gone over, Elijah said to Elisha, \u201cAsk what I shall do for you, before I am taken from you.\u201d"],[0,"Elisha said, \u201cPlease let a double portion of your spirit be on me.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou have asked a hard thing. If you see me when I am taken from you, it will be so for you; but if not, it will not be so.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"As they continued on and talked, behold, a chariot of fire and horses of fire separated them; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Elisha saw it, and he cried, \u201cMy father, my father, the chariots of Israel and its horsemen!\u201d"],[0,"He saw him no more. Then he took hold of his own clothes and tore them in two pieces."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He also took up Elijah\u2019s mantle that fell from him, and went back and stood by the bank of the Jordan."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He took Elijah\u2019s mantle that fell from him, and struck the waters, and said, \u201cWhere is the LORD, the God of Elijah?\u201d When he also had struck the waters, they were divided apart, and Elisha went over."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When the sons of the prophets who were at Jericho facing him saw him, they said, \u201cThe spirit of Elijah rests on Elisha.\u201d They came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cSee now, there are with your servants fifty strong men. Please let them go and seek your master. Perhaps the LORD\u2019s Spirit has taken him up, and put him on some mountain or into some valley.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cDon\u2019t send them.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When they urged him until he was ashamed, he said, \u201cSend them.\u201d"],[0,"Therefore they sent fifty men; and they searched for three days, but didn\u2019t find him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They came back to him while he stayed at Jericho; and he said to them, \u201cDidn\u2019t I tell you, \u2018Don\u2019t go\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The men of the city said to Elisha, \u201cBehold, please, the situation of this city is pleasant, as my lord sees; but the water is bad, and the land is barren.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBring me a new jar, and put salt in it.\u201d Then they brought it to him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He went out to the spring of the waters, and threw salt into it, and said, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018I have healed these waters. There shall not be from there any more death or barren wasteland.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"So the waters were healed to this day, according to Elisha\u2019s word which he spoke."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He went up from there to Bethel. As he was going up by the way, some youths came out of the city and mocked him, and said to him, \u201cGo up, you baldy! Go up, you baldy!\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He looked behind him and saw them, and cursed them in the LORD\u2019s name. Then two female bears came out of the woods and mauled forty-two of those youths."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He went from there to Mount Carmel, and from there he returned to Samaria."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jehoram the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria in the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned twelve years."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, but not like his father and like his mother, for he put away the pillar of Baal that his father had made."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Nevertheless he held to the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin. He didn\u2019t depart from them."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Mesha king of Moab was a sheep breeder; and he supplied the king of Israel with one hundred thousand lambs and the wool of one hundred thousand rams."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But when Ahab was dead, the king of Moab rebelled against the king of Israel."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"King Jehoram went out of Samaria at that time, and mustered all Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He went and sent to Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, saying, \u201cThe king of Moab has rebelled against me. Will you go with me against Moab to battle?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI will go up. I am as you are, my people as your people, my horses as your horses.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cWhich way shall we go up?\u201d"],[0,"Jehoram answered, \u201cThe way of the wilderness of Edom.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king of Israel went with the king of Judah and the king of Edom, and they marched for seven days along a circuitous route. There was no water for the army or for the animals that followed them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said, \u201cAlas! For the LORD has called these three kings together to deliver them into the hand of Moab.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jehoshaphat said, \u201cIsn\u2019t there a prophet of the LORD here, that we may inquire of the LORD by him?\u201d"],[0,"One of the king of Israel\u2019s servants answered, \u201cElisha the son of Shaphat, who poured water on the hands of Elijah, is here.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat said, \u201cThe LORD\u2019s word is with him.\u201d So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat and the king of Edom went down to him."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha said to the king of Israel, \u201cWhat have I to do with you? Go to the prophets of your father, and to the prophets of your mother.\u201d"],[0,"The king of Israel said to him, \u201cNo, for the LORD has called these three kings together to deliver them into the hand of Moab.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha said, \u201cAs the LORD of Armies lives, before whom I stand, surely, were it not that I respect the presence of Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, I would not look toward you, nor see you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But now bring me a musician.\u201d When the musician played, the LORD\u2019s hand came on him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Make this valley full of trenches.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For the LORD says, \u2018You will not see wind, neither will you see rain, yet that valley will be filled with water, and you will drink, both you and your livestock and your other animals."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"This is an easy thing in the LORD\u2019s sight. He will also deliver the Moabites into your hand."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall strike every fortified city and every choice city, and shall fell every good tree, and stop all springs of water, and mar every good piece of land with stones.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"In the morning, about the time of offering the sacrifice, behold, water came by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when all the Moabites heard that the kings had come up to fight against them, they gathered themselves together, all who were able to put on armor, young and old, and stood on the border."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone on the water, and the Moabites saw the water opposite them as red as blood."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThis is blood. The kings are surely destroyed, and they have struck each other. Now therefore, Moab, to the plunder!\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When they came to the camp of Israel, the Israelites rose up and struck the Moabites, so that they fled before them; and they went forward into the land attacking the Moabites."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They beat down the cities; and on every good piece of land each man cast his stone, and filled it. They also stopped all the springs of water and cut down all the good trees, until in Kir Hareseth all they left was its stones; however the men armed with slings went around it and attacked it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When the king of Moab saw that the battle was too severe for him, he took with him seven hundred men who drew a sword, to break through to the king of Edom; but they could not."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Then he took his oldest son who would have reigned in his place, and offered him for a burnt offering on the wall. There was great wrath against Israel; and they departed from him, and returned to their own land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets cried out to Elisha, saying, \u201cYour servant my husband is dead. You know that your servant feared the LORD. Now the creditor has come to take for himself my two children to be slaves.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha said to her, \u201cWhat should I do for you? Tell me, what do you have in the house?\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cYour servant has nothing in the house, except a pot of oil.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cGo, borrow empty containers from all your neighbors. Don\u2019t borrow just a few containers."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Go in and shut the door on you and on your sons, and pour oil into all those containers; and set aside those which are full.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"So she went from him, and shut the door on herself and on her sons. They brought the containers to her, and she poured oil."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When the containers were full, she said to her son, \u201cBring me another container.\u201d"],[0,"He said to her, \u201cThere isn\u2019t another container.\u201d Then the oil stopped flowing."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she came and told the man of God. He said, \u201cGo, sell the oil, and pay your debt; and you and your sons live on the rest.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"One day Elisha went to Shunem, where there was a prominent woman; and she persuaded him to eat bread. So it was, that as often as he passed by, he turned in there to eat bread."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"She said to her husband, \u201cSee now, I perceive that this is a holy man of God who passes by us continually."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Please, let\u2019s make a little room on the roof. Let\u2019s set a bed, a table, a chair, and a lamp stand for him there. When he comes to us, he can stay there.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"One day he came there, and he went to the room and lay there."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He said to Gehazi his servant, \u201cCall this Shunammite.\u201d When he had called her, she stood before him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cSay now to her, \u2018Behold, you have cared for us with all this care. What is to be done for you? Would you like to be spoken for to the king, or to the captain of the army?\u2019\u201d"],[0,"She answered, \u201cI dwell among my own people.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhat then is to be done for her?\u201d"],[0,"Gehazi answered, \u201cMost certainly she has no son, and her husband is old.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cCall her.\u201d When he had called her, she stood in the door."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cAt this season next year, you will embrace a son.\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cNo, my lord, you man of God, do not lie to your servant.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman conceived, and bore a son at that season when the time came around, as Elisha had said to her."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When the child was grown, one day he went out to his father to the reapers."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He said to his father, \u201cMy head! My head!\u201d"],[0,"He said to his servant, \u201cCarry him to his mother.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had taken him and brought him to his mother, he sat on her knees until noon, and then died."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"She went up and laid him on the man of God\u2019s bed, and shut the door on him, and went out."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"She called to her husband and said, \u201cPlease send me one of the servants, and one of the donkeys, that I may run to the man of God and come again.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhy would you want to go to him today? It is not a new moon or a Sabbath.\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cIt\u2019s all right.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she saddled a donkey, and said to her servant, \u201cDrive, and go forward! Don\u2019t slow down for me, unless I ask you to.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"So she went, and came to the man of God to Mount Carmel. When the man of God saw her afar off, he said to Gehazi his servant, \u201cBehold, there is the Shunammite."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Please run now to meet her, and ask her, \u2018Is it well with you? Is it well with your husband? Is it well with your child?\u2019\u201d"],[0,"She answered, \u201cIt is well.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"When she came to the man of God to the hill, she caught hold of his feet. Gehazi came near to thrust her away; but the man of God said, \u201cLeave her alone, for her soul is troubled within her; and the LORD has hidden it from me, and has not told me.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she said, \u201cDid I ask you for a son, my lord? Didn\u2019t I say, \u2018Do not deceive me\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to Gehazi, \u201cTuck your cloak into your belt, take my staff in your hand, and go your way. If you meet any man, don\u2019t greet him; and if anyone greets you, don\u2019t answer him again. Then lay my staff on the child\u2019s face.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"The child\u2019s mother said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, and as your soul lives, I will not leave you.\u201d"],[0,"So he arose, and followed her."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Gehazi went ahead of them, and laid the staff on the child\u2019s face; but there was no voice and no hearing. Therefore he returned to meet him, and told him, \u201cThe child has not awakened.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"When Elisha had come into the house, behold, the child was dead, and lying on his bed."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He went in therefore, and shut the door on them both, and prayed to the LORD."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He went up and lay on the child, and put his mouth on his mouth, and his eyes on his eyes, and his hands on his hands. He stretched himself on him; and the child\u2019s flesh grew warm."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Then he returned, and walked in the house once back and forth, then went up and stretched himself out on him. Then the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He called Gehazi, and said, \u201cCall this Shunammite!\u201d So he called her."],[0,"When she had come in to him, he said, \u201cTake up your son.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Then she went in, fell at his feet, and bowed herself to the ground; then she picked up her son, and went out."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha came again to Gilgal. There was a famine in the land; and the sons of the prophets were sitting before him; and he said to his servant, \u201cGet the large pot, and boil stew for the sons of the prophets.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"One went out into the field to gather herbs, and found a wild vine, and gathered a lap full of wild gourds from it, and came and cut them up into the pot of stew; for they didn\u2019t recognize them."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"So they poured out for the men to eat. As they were eating some of the stew, they cried out and said, \u201cMan of God, there is death in the pot!\u201d And they could not eat it."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said, \u201cThen bring meal.\u201d He threw it into the pot; and he said, \u201cServe it to the people, that they may eat.\u201d And there was nothing harmful in the pot."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"A man from Baal Shalishah came, and brought the man of God some bread of the first fruits: twenty loaves of barley and fresh ears of grain in his sack. Elisha said, \u201cGive to the people, that they may eat.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"His servant said, \u201cWhat, should I set this before a hundred men?\u201d"],[0,"But he said, \u201cGive it to the people, that they may eat; for the LORD says, \u2018They will eat, and will have some left over.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"So he set it before them and they ate and had some left over, according to the LORD\u2019s word."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Naaman, captain of the army of the king of Syria, was a great man with his master, and honorable, because by him the LORD had given victory to Syria; he was also a mighty man of valor, but he was a leper."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Syrians had gone out in bands, and had brought away captive out of the land of Israel a little girl, and she waited on Naaman\u2019s wife."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"She said to her mistress, \u201cI wish that my lord were with the prophet who is in Samaria! Then he would heal him of his leprosy.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Someone went in and told his lord, saying, \u201cThe girl who is from the land of Israel said this.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Syria said, \u201cGo now, and I will send a letter to the king of Israel.\u201d"],[0,"He departed, and took with him ten talents of silver, six thousand pieces of gold, and ten changes of clothing."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He brought the letter to the king of Israel, saying, \u201cNow when this letter has come to you, behold, I have sent Naaman my servant to you, that you may heal him of his leprosy.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When the king of Israel had read the letter, he tore his clothes and said, \u201cAm I God, to kill and to make alive, that this man sends to me to heal a man of his leprosy? But please consider and see how he seeks a quarrel against me.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"It was so, when Elisha the man of God heard that the king of Israel had torn his clothes, that he sent to the king, saying, \u201cWhy have you torn your clothes? Let him come now to me, and he shall know that there is a prophet in Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"So Naaman came with his horses and with his chariots, and stood at the door of the house of Elisha."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Elisha sent a messenger to him, saying, \u201cGo and wash in the Jordan seven times, and your flesh shall come again to you, and you shall be clean.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But Naaman was angry, and went away and said, \u201cBehold, I thought, \u2018He will surely come out to me, and stand, and call on the name of the LORD his God, and wave his hand over the place, and heal the leper.\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t Abanah and Pharpar, the rivers of Damascus, better than all the waters of Israel? Couldn\u2019t I wash in them and be clean?\u201d So he turned and went away in a rage."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"His servants came near and spoke to him, and said, \u201cMy father, if the prophet had asked you do some great thing, wouldn\u2019t you have done it? How much rather then, when he says to you, \u2018Wash, and be clean\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he went down and dipped himself seven times in the Jordan, according to the saying of the man of God; and his flesh was restored like the flesh of a little child, and he was clean."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He returned to the man of God, he and all his company, and came, and stood before him; and he said, \u201cSee now, I know that there is no God in all the earth, but in Israel. Now therefore, please take a gift from your servant.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, before whom I stand, I will receive none.\u201d"],[0,"He urged him to take it; but he refused."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Naaman said, \u201cIf not, then, please let two mules\u2019 load of earth be given to your servant; for your servant will from now on offer neither burnt offering nor sacrifice to other gods, but to the LORD."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In this thing may the LORD pardon your servant: when my master goes into the house of Rimmon to worship there, and he leans on my hand, and I bow myself in the house of Rimmon. When I bow myself in the house of Rimmon, may the LORD pardon your servant in this thing.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cGo in peace.\u201d"],[0,"So he departed from him a little way."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But Gehazi the servant of Elisha the man of God, said, \u201cBehold, my master has spared this Naaman the Syrian, in not receiving at his hands that which he brought. As the LORD lives, I will run after him, and take something from him.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"So Gehazi followed after Naaman. When Naaman saw one running after him, he came down from the chariot to meet him, and said, \u201cIs all well?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cAll is well. My master has sent me, saying, \u2018Behold, even now two young men of the sons of the prophets have come to me from the hill country of Ephraim. Please give them a talent of silver and two changes of clothing.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds"]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Naaman said, \u201cBe pleased to take two talents.\u201d He urged him, and bound two talents of silver in two bags, with two changes of clothing, and laid them on two of his servants; and they carried them before him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When he came to the hill, he took them from their hand, and stored them in the house. Then he let the men go, and they departed."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But he went in, and stood before his master. Elisha said to him, \u201cWhere did you come from, Gehazi?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cYour servant went nowhere.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cDidn\u2019t my heart go with you when the man turned from his chariot to meet you? Is it a time to receive money, and to receive garments, and olive groves and vineyards, and sheep and cattle, and male servants and female servants?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Therefore the leprosy of Naaman will cling to you and to your offspring forever.\u201d"],[0,"He went out from his presence a leper, as white as snow."]],f:["or, seed"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of the prophets said to Elisha, \u201cSee now, the place where we live and meet with you is too small for us."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Please let us go to the Jordan, and each man take a beam from there, and let\u2019s make us a place there, where we may live.\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cGo!\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"One said, \u201cPlease be pleased to go with your servants.\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cI will go.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"So he went with them. When they came to the Jordan, they cut down wood."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But as one was cutting down a tree, the ax head fell into the water. Then he cried out and said, \u201cAlas, my master! For it was borrowed.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The man of God asked, \u201cWhere did it fall?\u201d He showed him the place. He cut down a stick, threw it in there, and made the iron float."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cTake it.\u201d So he put out his hand and took it."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the king of Syria was at war against Israel; and he took counsel with his servants, saying, \u201cMy camp will be in such and such a place.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The man of God sent to the king of Israel, saying, \u201cBeware that you not pass this place, for the Syrians are coming down there.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The king of Israel sent to the place which the man of God told him and warned him of; and he saved himself there, not once or twice."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The king of Syria\u2019s heart was very troubled about this. He called his servants, and said to them, \u201cWon\u2019t you show me which of us is for the king of Israel?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"One of his servants said, \u201cNo, my lord, O king; but Elisha, the prophet who is in Israel, tells the king of Israel the words that you speak in your bedroom.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGo and see where he is, that I may send and get him.\u201d"],[0,"He was told, \u201cBehold, he is in Dothan.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore he sent horses, chariots, and a great army there. They came by night and surrounded the city."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When the servant of the man of God had risen early and gone out, behold, an army with horses and chariots was around the city. His servant said to him, \u201cAlas, my master! What shall we do?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for those who are with us are more than those who are with them.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Elisha prayed, and said, \u201cLORD, please open his eyes, that he may see.\u201d the LORD opened the young man\u2019s eyes, and he saw; and behold, the mountain was full of horses and chariots of fire around Elisha."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When they came down to him, Elisha prayed to the LORD, and said, \u201cPlease strike this people with blindness.\u201d"],[0,"He struck them with blindness according to Elisha\u2019s word."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha said to them, \u201cThis is not the way, neither is this the city. Follow me, and I will bring you to the man whom you seek.\u201d He led them to Samaria."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When they had come into Samaria, Elisha said, \u201cLORD, open these men\u2019s eyes, that they may see.\u201d"],[0,"The LORD opened their eyes, and they saw; and behold, they were in the middle of Samaria."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to Elisha, when he saw them, \u201cMy father, shall I strike them? Shall I strike them?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cYou shall not strike them. Would you strike those whom you have taken captive with your sword and with your bow? Set bread and water before them, that they may eat and drink, then go to their master.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He prepared a great feast for them. After they ate and drank, he sent them away and they went to their master. So the bands of Syria stopped raiding the land of Israel."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Benhadad king of Syria gathered all his army, and went up and besieged Samaria."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There was a great famine in Samaria. Behold, they besieged it until a donkey\u2019s head was sold for eighty pieces of silver, and the fourth part of a kab of dove\u2019s dung for five pieces of silver."]],f:["A kab was about 2 liters, so a fourth of a kab would be about 500 milliliters or about a pint"]},{v:26,l:[[0,"As the king of Israel was passing by on the wall, a woman cried to him, saying, \u201cHelp, my lord, O king!\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIf the LORD doesn\u2019t help you, where could I get help for you? From the threshing floor, or from the wine press?\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Then the king asked her, \u201cWhat is your problem?\u201d"],[0,"She answered, \u201cThis woman said to me, \u2018Give your son, that we may eat him today, and we will eat my son tomorrow.\u2019"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"So we boiled my son and ate him; and I said to her on the next day, \u2018Give up your son, that we may eat him;\u2019 and she has hidden her son.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"When the king heard the words of the woman, he tore his clothes. Now he was passing by on the wall, and the people looked, and behold, he had sackcloth underneath on his body."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cGod do so to me, and more also, if the head of Elisha the son of Shaphat stays on him today.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"But Elisha was sitting in his house, and the elders were sitting with him. Then the king sent a man from before him; but before the messenger came to him, he said to the elders, \u201cDo you see how this son of a murderer has sent to take away my head? Behold, when the messenger comes, shut the door, and hold the door shut against him. Isn\u2019t the sound of his master\u2019s feet behind him?\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still talking with them, behold, the messenger came down to him. Then he said, \u201cBehold, this evil is from the LORD. Why should I wait for the LORD any longer?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha said, \u201cHear the LORD\u2019s word. The LORD says, \u2018Tomorrow about this time a seah of fine flour will be sold for a shekel, and two seahs of barley for a shekel, in the gate of Samaria.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["1 seah is about 7 liters or 1.9 gallons or 0.8 pecks","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces. In this context, it was probably a silver coin weighing that much."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the captain on whose hand the king leaned answered the man of God, and said, \u201cBehold, if the LORD made windows in heaven, could this thing be?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cBehold, you will see it with your eyes, but will not eat of it.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there were four leprous men at the entrance of the gate. They said to one another, \u201cWhy do we sit here until we die?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If we say, \u2018We will enter into the city,\u2019 then the famine is in the city, and we will die there. If we sit still here, we also die. Now therefore come, and let\u2019s surrender to the army of the Syrians. If they save us alive, we will live; and if they kill us, we will only die.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"They rose up in the twilight to go to the camp of the Syrians. When they had come to the outermost part of the camp of the Syrians, behold, no man was there."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the Lord had made the army of the Syrians to hear the sound of chariots and the sound of horses, even the noise of a great army; and they said to one another, \u201cBehold, the king of Israel has hired against us the kings of the Hittites and the kings of the Egyptians to attack us.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore they arose and fled in the twilight, and left their tents, their horses, and their donkeys, even the camp as it was, and fled for their life."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When these lepers came to the outermost part of the camp, they went into one tent, and ate and drank, then carried away silver, gold, and clothing and went and hid it. Then they came back, and entered into another tent and carried things from there also, and went and hid them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then they said to one another, \u201cWe aren\u2019t doing right. Today is a day of good news, and we keep silent. If we wait until the morning light, punishment will overtake us. Now therefore come, let\u2019s go and tell the king\u2019s household.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So they came and called to the city gatekeepers; and they told them, \u201cWe came to the camp of the Syrians, and, behold, there was no man there, not even a man\u2019s voice, but the horses tied, and the donkeys tied, and the tents as they were.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the gatekeepers called out and told it to the king\u2019s household within."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The king arose in the night, and said to his servants, \u201cI will now show you what the Syrians have done to us. They know that we are hungry. Therefore they have gone out of the camp to hide themselves in the field, saying, \u2018When they come out of the city, we shall take them alive, and get into the city.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"One of his servants answered, \u201cPlease let some people take five of the horses that remain, which are left in the city. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are left in it. Behold, they are like all the multitude of Israel who are consumed. Let\u2019s send and see.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore they took two chariots with horses; and the king sent them out to the Syrian army, saying, \u201cGo and see.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"They went after them to the Jordan; and behold, all the path was full of garments and equipment which the Syrians had cast away in their haste. The messengers returned and told the king."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The people went out and plundered the camp of the Syrians. So a seah of fine flour was sold for a shekel, and two measures of barley for a shekel, according to the LORD\u2019s word."]],f:["1 seah is about 7 liters or 1.9 gallons or 0.8 pecks","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces. In this context, it was probably a silver coin weighing that much."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The king had appointed the captain on whose hand he leaned to be in charge of the gate; and the people trampled over him in the gate, and he died as the man of God had said, who spoke when the king came down to him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"It happened as the man of God had spoken to the king, saying, \u201cTwo seahs of barley for a shekel, and a seah of fine flour for a shekel, shall be tomorrow about this time in the gate of Samaria;\u201d"]],f:["1 seah is about 7 liters or 1.9 gallons or 0.8 pecks","A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces. In this context, it was probably a silver coin weighing that much."]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and that captain answered the man of God, and said, \u201cNow, behold, if the LORD made windows in heaven, might such a thing be?\u201d and he said, \u201cBehold, you will see it with your eyes, but will not eat of it.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"It happened like that to him, for the people trampled over him in the gate, and he died."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Elisha had spoken to the woman whose son he had restored to life, saying, \u201cArise, and go, you and your household, and stay for a while wherever you can; for the LORD has called for a famine. It will also come on the land for seven years.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman arose, and did according to the man of God\u2019s word. She went with her household, and lived in the land of the Philistines for seven years."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"At the end of seven years, the woman returned from the land of the Philistines. Then she went out to beg the king for her house and for her land."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now the king was talking with Gehazi the servant of the man of God, saying, \u201cPlease tell me all the great things that Elisha has done.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"As he was telling the king how he had restored to life him who was dead, behold, the woman whose son he had restored to life begged the king for her house and for her land. Gehazi said, \u201cMy lord, O king, this is the woman, and this is her son, whom Elisha restored to life.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When the king asked the woman, she told him. So the king appointed to her a certain officer, saying, \u201cRestore all that was hers, and all the fruits of the field since the day that she left the land, even until now.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha came to Damascus; and Benhadad the king of Syria was sick. He was told, \u201cThe man of God has come here.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to Hazael, \u201cTake a present in your hand, and go meet the man of God, and inquire of the LORD by him, saying, \u2018Will I recover from this sickness?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hazael went to meet him and took a present with him, even of every good thing of Damascus, forty camels\u2019 burden, and came and stood before him and said, \u201cYour son Benhadad king of Syria has sent me to you, saying, \u2018Will I recover from this sickness?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha said to him, \u201cGo, tell him, \u2018You will surely recover;\u2019 however the LORD has shown me that he will surely die.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He settled his gaze steadfastly on him, until he was ashamed. Then the man of God wept."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Hazael said, \u201cWhy do you weep, my lord?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cBecause I know the evil that you will do to the children of Israel. You will set their strongholds on fire, and you will kill their young men with the sword, and will dash their little ones in pieces, and rip up their pregnant women.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Hazael said, \u201cBut what is your servant, who is but a dog, that he could do this great thing?\u201d"],[0,"Elisha answered, \u201cThe LORD has shown me that you will be king over Syria.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he departed from Elisha, and came to his master, who said to him, \u201cWhat did Elisha say to you?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cHe told me that you would surely recover.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, he took a thick cloth, dipped it in water, and spread it on the king\u2019s face, so that he died. Then Hazael reigned in his place."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fifth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel, Jehoshaphat being king of Judah then, Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah began to reign."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He was thirty-two years old when he began to reign. He reigned eight years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did Ahab\u2019s house, for he married Ahab\u2019s daughter. He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"However, the LORD would not destroy Judah, for David his servant\u2019s sake, as he promised him to give to him a lamp for his children always."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"In his days Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah, and made a king over themselves."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then Joram crossed over to Zair, and all his chariots with him; and he rose up by night and struck the Edomites who surrounded him with the captains of the chariots; and the people fled to their tents."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"So Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah to this day. Then Libnah revolted at the same time."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The rest of the acts of Joram, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Joram slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David\u2019s city; and Ahaziah his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twelfth year of Joram the son of Ahab king of Israel, Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah began to reign."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Ahaziah was twenty-two years old when he began to reign; and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Athaliah the daughter of Omri king of Israel."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He walked in the way of Ahab\u2019s house and did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, as did Ahab\u2019s house, for he was the son-in-law of Ahab\u2019s house."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He went with Joram the son of Ahab to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth Gilead, and the Syrians wounded Joram."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"King Joram returned to be healed in Jezreel from the wounds which the Syrians had given him at Ramah, when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. Ahaziah the son of Jehoram, king of Judah, went down to see Joram the son of Ahab in Jezreel, because he was sick."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha the prophet called one of the sons of the prophets, and said to him, \u201cPut your belt on your waist, take this vial of oil in your hand, and go to Ramoth Gilead."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When you come there, find Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi, and go in and make him rise up from among his brothers, and take him to an inner room."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then take the vial of oil, and pour it on his head, and say, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cI have anointed you king over Israel.\u201d\u2019 Then open the door, flee, and don\u2019t wait.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"So the young man, the young prophet, went to Ramoth Gilead."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When he came, behold, the captains of the army were sitting. Then he said, \u201cI have a message for you, captain.\u201d"],[0,"Jehu said, \u201cTo which one of us?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cTo you, O captain.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He arose, and went into the house. Then he poured the oil on his head, and said to him, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018I have anointed you king over the people of the LORD, even over Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You must strike your master Ahab\u2019s house, that I may avenge the blood of my servants the prophets, and the blood of all the servants of the LORD, at the hand of Jezebel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the whole house of Ahab will perish. I will cut off from Ahab everyone who urinates against a wall, both him who is shut up and him who is left at large in Israel."]],f:["or, male"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I will make Ahab\u2019s house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, and like the house of Baasha the son of Ahijah."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The dogs will eat Jezebel on the plot of ground of Jezreel, and there shall be no one to bury her.\u2019\u201d Then he opened the door and fled."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jehu came out to the servants of his lord and one said to him, \u201cIs all well? Why did this madman come to you?\u201d"],[0,"He said to them, \u201cYou know the man and how he talks.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThat is a lie. Tell us now.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHe said to me, \u2018The LORD says, I have anointed you king over Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they hurried, and each man took his cloak, and put it under him on the top of the stairs, and blew the trumpet, saying, \u201cJehu is king.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jehu the son of Jehoshaphat the son of Nimshi conspired against Joram. (Now Joram was defending Ramoth Gilead, he and all Israel, because of Hazael king of Syria;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but King Joram had returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which the Syrians had given him when he fought with Hazael king of Syria.) Jehu said, \u201cIf this is your thinking, then let no one escape and go out of the city to go to tell it in Jezreel.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So Jehu rode in a chariot and went to Jezreel, for Joram lay there. Ahaziah king of Judah had come down to see Joram."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now the watchman was standing on the tower in Jezreel, and he spied the company of Jehu as he came, and said, \u201cI see a company.\u201d"],[0,"Joram said, \u201cTake a horseman, and send to meet them, and let him say, \u2018Is it peace?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"So one went on horseback to meet him, and said, \u201cthe king says, \u2018Is it peace?\u2019\u201d"],[0,"Jehu said, \u201cWhat do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!\u201d"],[0,"The watchman said, \u201cThe messenger came to them, but he isn\u2019t coming back.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he sent out a second on horseback, who came to them and said, \u201cThe king says, \u2018Is it peace?\u2019\u201d"],[0,"Jehu answered, \u201cWhat do you have to do with peace? Fall in behind me!\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The watchman said, \u201cHe came to them, and isn\u2019t coming back. The driving is like the driving of Jehu the son of Nimshi, for he drives furiously.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Joram said, \u201cGet ready!\u201d"],[0,"They got his chariot ready. Then Joram king of Israel and Ahaziah king of Judah went out, each in his chariot; and they went out to meet Jehu, and found him on Naboth the Jezreelite\u2019s land."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When Joram saw Jehu, he said, \u201cIs it peace, Jehu?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cWhat peace, so long as the prostitution of your mother Jezebel and her witchcraft abound?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Joram turned his hands and fled, and said to Ahaziah, \u201cThis is treason, Ahaziah!\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehu drew his bow with his full strength, and struck Joram between his arms; and the arrow went out at his heart, and he sunk down in his chariot."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Then Jehu said to Bidkar his captain, \u201cPick him up, and throw him in the plot of the field of Naboth the Jezreelite; for remember how, when you and I rode together after Ahab his father, the LORD laid this burden on him:"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u2018Surely I have seen yesterday the blood of Naboth, and the blood of his sons,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018and I will repay you in this plot of ground,\u2019 says the LORD. Now therefore take and cast him onto the plot of ground, according to the LORD\u2019s word.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Ahaziah the king of Judah saw this, he fled by the way of the garden house. Jehu followed after him, and said, \u201cStrike him also in the chariot!\u201d They struck him at the ascent of Gur, which is by Ibleam. He fled to Megiddo, and died there."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"His servants carried him in a chariot to Jerusalem, and buried him in his tomb with his fathers in David\u2019s city."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"In the eleventh year of Joram the son of Ahab, Ahaziah began to reign over Judah."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jehu had come to Jezreel, Jezebel heard of it; and she painted her eyes, and adorned her head, and looked out at the window."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"As Jehu entered in at the gate, she said, \u201cDo you come in peace, Zimri, you murderer of your master?\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"He lifted up his face to the window, and said, \u201cWho is on my side? Who?\u201d"],[0,"Two or three eunuchs looked out at him."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThrow her down!\u201d"],[0,"So they threw her down; and some of her blood was sprinkled on the wall, and on the horses. Then he trampled her under foot."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"When he had come in, he ate and drank. Then he said, \u201cSee now to this cursed woman, and bury her; for she is a king\u2019s daughter.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"They went to bury her, but they found no more of her than the skull, the feet, and the palms of her hands."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Therefore they came back, and told him."],[0,"He said, \u201cThis is the LORD\u2019s word, which he spoke by his servant Elijah the Tishbite, saying, \u2018The dogs will eat the flesh of Jezebel on the plot of Jezreel,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"and the body of Jezebel will be as dung on the surface of the field on Jezreel\u2019s land, so that they won\u2019t say, \u201cThis is Jezebel.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Ahab had seventy sons in Samaria. Jehu wrote letters and sent them to Samaria, to the rulers of Jezreel, even the elders, and to those who brought up Ahab\u2019s sons, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cNow as soon as this letter comes to you, since your master\u2019s sons are with you, and you have chariots and horses, a fortified city also, and armor,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"select the best and fittest of your master\u2019s sons, set him on his father\u2019s throne, and fight for your master\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But they were exceedingly afraid, and said, \u201cBehold, the two kings didn\u2019t stand before him! How then shall we stand?\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He who was over the household, and he who was over the city, the elders also, and those who raised the children, sent to Jehu, saying, \u201cWe are your servants, and will do all that you ask us. We will not make any man king. You do that which is good in your eyes.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he wrote a letter the second time to them, saying, \u201cIf you are on my side, and if you will listen to my voice, take the heads of the men who are your master\u2019s sons, and come to me to Jezreel by tomorrow this time.\u201d"],[0,"Now the king\u2019s sons, being seventy persons, were with the great men of the city, who brought them up."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When the letter came to them, they took the king\u2019s sons and killed them, even seventy people, and put their heads in baskets, and sent them to him to Jezreel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"A messenger came and told him, \u201cThey have brought the heads of the king\u2019s sons.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cLay them in two heaps at the entrance of the gate until the morning.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"In the morning, he went out and stood, and said to all the people, \u201cYou are righteous. Behold, I conspired against my master and killed him, but who killed all these?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Know now that nothing will fall to the earth of the LORD\u2019s word, which the LORD spoke concerning Ahab\u2019s house. For the LORD has done that which he spoke by his servant Elijah.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jehu struck all that remained of Ahab\u2019s house in Jezreel, with all his great men, his familiar friends, and his priests, until he left him no one remaining."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose and departed, and went to Samaria. As he was at the shearing house of the shepherds on the way,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Jehu met with the brothers of Ahaziah king of Judah, and said, \u201cWho are you?\u201d"],[0,"They answered, \u201cWe are the brothers of Ahaziah. We are going down to greet the children of the king and the children of the queen.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cTake them alive!\u201d"],[0,"They took them alive, and killed them at the pit of the shearing house, even forty-two men. He didn\u2019t leave any of them."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had departed from there, he met Jehonadab the son of Rechab coming to meet him. He greeted him, and said to him, \u201cIs your heart right, as my heart is with your heart?\u201d"],[0,"Jehonadab answered, \u201cIt is.\u201d"],[0,"\u201cIf it is, give me your hand.\u201d He gave him his hand; and he took him up to him into the chariot."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cCome with me, and see my zeal for the LORD.\u201d So they made him ride in his chariot."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When he came to Samaria, he struck all who remained to Ahab in Samaria, until he had destroyed them, according to the LORD\u2019s word which he spoke to Elijah."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehu gathered all the people together, and said to them, \u201cAhab served Baal a little, but Jehu will serve him much."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now therefore call to me all the prophets of Baal, all of his worshipers, and all of his priests. Let no one be absent, for I have a great sacrifice to Baal. Whoever is absent, he shall not live.\u201d But Jehu did deceptively, intending to destroy the worshipers of Baal."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehu said, \u201cSanctify a solemn assembly for Baal!\u201d"],[0,"So they proclaimed it."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Jehu sent through all Israel; and all the worshipers of Baal came, so that there was not a man left that didn\u2019t come. They came into the house of Baal; and the house of Baal was filled from one end to another."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He said to him who kept the wardrobe, \u201cBring out robes for all the worshipers of Baal!\u201d"],[0,"So he brought robes out to them."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Jehu went with Jehonadab the son of Rechab into the house of Baal. Then he said to the worshipers of Baal, \u201cSearch, and see that none of the servants of the LORD are here with you, but only the worshipers of Baal.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"So they went in to offer sacrifices and burnt offerings. Now Jehu had appointed for himself eighty men outside, and said, \u201cIf any of the men whom I bring into your hands escape, he who lets him go, his life shall be for the life of him.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"As soon as he had finished offering the burnt offering, Jehu said to the guard and to the captains, \u201cGo in and kill them! Let no one escape.\u201d So they struck them with the edge of the sword. The guard and the captains threw the bodies out, and went to the inner shrine of the house of Baal."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They brought out the pillars that were in the house of Baal and burned them."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They broke down the pillar of Baal, and broke down the house of Baal, and made it a latrine, to this day."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Thus Jehu destroyed Baal out of Israel."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"However, Jehu didn\u2019t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin\u2014the golden calves that were in Bethel and that were in Dan."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Jehu, \u201cBecause you have done well in executing that which is right in my eyes, and have done to Ahab\u2019s house according to all that was in my heart, your descendants shall sit on the throne of Israel to the fourth generation.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jehu took no heed to walk in the law of the LORD, the God of Israel, with all his heart. He didn\u2019t depart from the sins of Jeroboam, with which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days the LORD began to cut away parts of Israel; and Hazael struck them in all the borders of Israel"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"from the Jordan eastward, all the land of Gilead, the Gadites, and the Reubenites, and the Manassites, from Aroer, which is by the valley of the Arnon, even Gilead and Bashan."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jehu, and all that he did, and all his might, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Jehu slept with his fathers; and they buried him in Samaria. Jehoahaz his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The time that Jehu reigned over Israel in Samaria was twenty-eight years."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the royal offspring."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But Jehosheba, the daughter of King Joram, sister of Ahaziah, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stole him away from among the king\u2019s sons who were slain, even him and his nurse, and put them in the bedroom; and they hid him from Athaliah, so that he was not slain."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He was with her hidden in the LORD\u2019s house six years while Athaliah reigned over the land."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"In the seventh year Jehoiada sent and fetched the captains over hundreds of the Carites and of the guard, and brought them to him into the LORD\u2019s house; and he made a covenant with them, and made a covenant with them in the LORD\u2019s house, and showed them the king\u2019s son."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He commanded them, saying, \u201cThis is what you must do: a third of you, who come in on the Sabbath, shall be keepers of the watch of the king\u2019s house;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"a third of you shall be at the gate Sur; and a third of you at the gate behind the guard. So you shall keep the watch of the house, and be a barrier."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The two companies of you, even all who go out on the Sabbath, shall keep the watch of the LORD\u2019s house around the king."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You shall surround the king, every man with his weapons in his hand; and he who comes within the ranks, let him be slain. Be with the king when he goes out, and when he comes in.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The captains over hundreds did according to all that Jehoiada the priest commanded; and they each took his men, those who were to come in on the Sabbath with those who were to go out on the Sabbath, and came to Jehoiada the priest."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The priest delivered to the captains over hundreds the spears and shields that had been King David\u2019s, which were in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The guard stood, every man with his weapons in his hand, from the right side of the house to the left side of the house, along by the altar and the house, around the king."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Then he brought out the king\u2019s son, and put the crown on him, and gave him the covenant; and they made him king and anointed him; and they clapped their hands, and said, \u201cLong live the king!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When Athaliah heard the noise of the guard and of the people, she came to the people into the LORD\u2019s house;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and she looked, and behold, the king stood by the pillar, as the tradition was, with the captains and the trumpets by the king; and all the people of the land rejoiced, and blew trumpets. Then Athaliah tore her clothes and cried, \u201cTreason! Treason!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoiada the priest commanded the captains of hundreds who were set over the army, and said to them, \u201cBring her out between the ranks. Kill anyone who follows her with the sword.\u201d For the priest said, \u201cDon\u2019t let her be slain in the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So they seized her; and she went by the way of the horses\u2019 entry to the king\u2019s house, and she was slain there."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoiada made a covenant between the LORD and the king and the people, that they should be the LORD\u2019s people; also between the king and the people."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All the people of the land went to the house of Baal, and broke it down. They broke his altars and his images in pieces thoroughly, and killed Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars. The priest appointed officers over the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He took the captains over hundreds, and the Carites, and the guard, and all the people of the land; and they brought down the king from the LORD\u2019s house, and came by the way of the gate of the guard to the king\u2019s house. He sat on the throne of the kings."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"So all the people of the land rejoiced, and the city was quiet. They had slain Athaliah with the sword at the king\u2019s house."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoash was seven years old when he began to reign."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoash began to reign in the seventh year of Jehu, and he reigned forty years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Zibiah of Beersheba."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jehoash did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes all his days in which Jehoiada the priest instructed him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"However, the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoash said to the priests, \u201cAll the money of the holy things that is brought into the LORD\u2019s house, in current money, the money of the people for whom each man is evaluated, and all the money that it comes into any man\u2019s heart to bring into the LORD\u2019s house,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"let the priests take it to them, each man from his donor; and they shall repair the damage to the house, wherever any damage is found.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But it was so, that in the twenty-third year of King Jehoash the priests had not repaired the damage to the house."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then King Jehoash called for Jehoiada the priest, and for the other priests, and said to them, \u201cWhy aren\u2019t you repairing the damage to the house? Now therefore take no more money from your treasurers, but deliver it for repair of the damage to the house.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The priests consented that they should take no more money from the people, and not repair the damage to the house."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But Jehoiada the priest took a chest and bored a hole in its lid, and set it beside the altar, on the right side as one comes into the LORD\u2019s house; and the priests who kept the threshold put all the money that was brought into the LORD\u2019s house into it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When they saw that there was much money in the chest, the king\u2019s scribe and the high priest came up, and they put it in bags and counted the money that was found in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They gave the money that was weighed out into the hands of those who did the work, who had the oversight of the LORD\u2019s house; and they paid it out to the carpenters and the builders who worked on the LORD\u2019s house,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and to the masons and the stone cutters, and for buying timber and cut stone to repair the damage to the LORD\u2019s house, and for all that was laid out for the house to repair it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But there were not made for the LORD\u2019s house cups of silver, snuffers, basins, trumpets, any vessels of gold or vessels of silver, of the money that was brought into the LORD\u2019s house;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"for they gave that to those who did the work, and repaired the LORD\u2019s house with it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Moreover they didn\u2019t demand an accounting from the men into whose hand they delivered the money to give to those who did the work; for they dealt faithfully."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The money for the trespass offerings and the money for the sin offerings was not brought into the LORD\u2019s house. It was the priests\u2019."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hazael king of Syria went up and fought against Gath, and took it; and Hazael set his face to go up to Jerusalem."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jehoash king of Judah took all the holy things that Jehoshaphat and Jehoram and Ahaziah, his fathers, kings of Judah, had dedicated, and his own holy things, and all the gold that was found in the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house, and of the king\u2019s house, and sent it to Hazael king of Syria; and he went away from Jerusalem."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Joash, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"His servants arose and made a conspiracy, and struck Joash at the house of Millo, on the way that goes down to Silla."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For Jozacar the son of Shimeath, and Jehozabad the son of Shomer, his servants, struck him, and he died; and they buried him with his fathers in David\u2019s city; and Amaziah his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twenty-third year of Joash the son of Ahaziah, king of Judah, Jehoahaz the son of Jehu began to reign over Israel in Samaria for seventeen years."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, and followed the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin. He didn\u2019t depart from it."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Israel, and he delivered them into the hand of Hazael king of Syria, and into the hand of Benhadad the son of Hazael, continually."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Jehoahaz begged the LORD, and the LORD listened to him; for he saw the oppression of Israel, how the king of Syria oppressed them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"(The LORD gave Israel a savior, so that they went out from under the hand of the Syrians; and the children of Israel lived in their tents as before."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Nevertheless they didn\u2019t depart from the sins of the house of Jeroboam, with which he made Israel to sin, but walked in them; and the Asherah also remained in Samaria.)"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For he didn\u2019t leave to Jehoahaz of the people any more than fifty horsemen, and ten chariots, and ten thousand footmen; for the king of Syria destroyed them and made them like the dust in threshing."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jehoahaz, and all that he did, and his might, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Jehoahaz slept with his fathers; and they buried him in Samaria; and Joash his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"In the thirty-seventh year of Joash king of Judah, Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz began to reign over Israel in Samaria for sixteen years."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight. He didn\u2019t depart from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin; but he walked in them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Joash, and all that he did, and his might with which he fought against Amaziah king of Judah, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Joash slept with his fathers; and Jeroboam sat on his throne. Joash was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Elisha became sick with the illness of which he died; and Joash the king of Israel came down to him, and wept over him, and said, \u201cMy father, my father, the chariots of Israel and its horsemen!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha said to him, \u201cTake bow and arrows;\u201d and he took bow and arrows for himself."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He said to the king of Israel, \u201cPut your hand on the bow;\u201d and he put his hand on it. Elisha laid his hands on the king\u2019s hands."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cOpen the window eastward;\u201d and he opened it. Then Elisha said, \u201cShoot!\u201d and he shot. He said, \u201cThe LORD\u2019s arrow of victory, even the arrow of victory over Syria; for you will strike the Syrians in Aphek until you have consumed them.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cTake the arrows;\u201d and he took them. He said to the king of Israel, \u201cStrike the ground;\u201d and he struck three times, and stopped."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The man of God was angry with him, and said, \u201cYou should have struck five or six times. Then you would have struck Syria until you had consumed it, but now you will strike Syria just three times.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Elisha died, and they buried him."],[0,"Now the bands of the Moabites invaded the land at the coming in of the year."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"As they were burying a man, behold, they saw a band of raiders; and they threw the man into Elisha\u2019s tomb. As soon as the man touched Elisha\u2019s bones, he revived, and stood up on his feet."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Hazael king of Syria oppressed Israel all the days of Jehoahaz."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But the LORD was gracious to them, and had compassion on them, and favored them because of his covenant with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and would not destroy them and he didn\u2019t cast them from his presence as yet."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Hazael king of Syria died; and Benhadad his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Jehoash the son of Jehoahaz took again out of the hand of Benhadad the son of Hazael the cities which he had taken out of the hand of Jehoahaz his father by war. Joash struck him three times, and recovered the cities of Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the second year of Joash, son of Joahaz, king of Israel, Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah began to reign."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Jehoaddin of Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, yet not like David his father. He did according to all that Joash his father had done."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"However the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"As soon as the kingdom was established in his hand, he killed his servants who had slain the king his father,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but the children of the murderers he didn\u2019t put to death, according to that which is written in the book of the law of Moses, as the LORD commanded, saying, \u201cThe fathers shall not be put to death for the children, nor the children be put to death for the fathers; but every man shall die for his own sin.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He killed ten thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt, and took Sela by war, and called its name Joktheel, to this day."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then Amaziah sent messengers to Jehoash, the son of Jehoahaz son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, \u201cCome, let\u2019s look one another in the face.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoash the king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, \u201cThe thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, \u2018Give your daughter to my son as wife.\u2019 Then a wild animal that was in Lebanon passed by, and trampled down the thistle."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You have indeed struck Edom, and your heart has lifted you up. Enjoy the glory of it, and stay at home; for why should you meddle to your harm, that you fall, even you, and Judah with you?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But Amaziah would not listen. So Jehoash king of Israel went up; and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Beth Shemesh, which belongs to Judah."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Judah was defeated by Israel; and each man fled to his tent."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Jehoash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Jehoash the son of Ahaziah, at Beth Shemesh and came to Jerusalem, then broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate, four hundred cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He took all the gold and silver and all the vessels that were found in the LORD\u2019s house and in the treasures of the king\u2019s house, the hostages also, and returned to Samaria."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jehoash which he did, and his might, and how he fought with Amaziah king of Judah, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Jehoash slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria with the kings of Israel; and Jeroboam his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah lived after the death of Jehoash son of Jehoahaz, king of Israel, fifteen years."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Amaziah, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem, and he fled to Lachish; but they sent after him to Lachish and killed him there."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They brought him on horses, and he was buried at Jerusalem with his fathers in David\u2019s city."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people of Judah took Azariah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in the place of his father Amaziah."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He built Elath and restored it to Judah. After that the king slept with his fathers."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fifteenth year of Amaziah the son of Joash king of Judah, Jeroboam the son of Joash king of Israel began to reign in Samaria for forty-one years."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight. He didn\u2019t depart from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He restored the border of Israel from the entrance of Hamath to the sea of the Arabah, according to the LORD, the God of Israel\u2019s word, which he spoke by his servant Jonah the son of Amittai, the prophet, who was from Gath Hepher."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For the LORD saw the affliction of Israel, that it was very bitter for all, slave and free; and there was no helper for Israel."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The LORD didn\u2019t say that he would blot out the name of Israel from under the sky; but he saved them by the hand of Jeroboam the son of Joash."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, and all that he did, and his might, how he fought, and how he recovered Damascus, and Hamath, which had belonged to Judah, for Israel, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Jeroboam slept with his fathers, even with the kings of Israel; and Zechariah his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twenty-seventh year of Jeroboam king of Israel, Azariah son of Amaziah king of Judah began to reign."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He was sixteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-two years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Jecoliah of Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, according to all that his father Amaziah had done."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"However, the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD struck the king, so that he was a leper to the day of his death, and lived in a separate house. Jotham, the king\u2019s son, was over the household, judging the people of the land."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Azariah, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Azariah slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in David\u2019s city; and Jotham his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"In the thirty-eighth year of Azariah king of Judah, Zechariah the son of Jeroboam reigned over Israel in Samaria six months."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, as his fathers had done. He didn\u2019t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Shallum the son of Jabesh conspired against him, and struck him before the people and killed him, and reigned in his place."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Zechariah, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"This was the LORD\u2019s word which he spoke to Jehu, saying, \u201cYour sons to the fourth generation shall sit on the throne of Israel.\u201d So it came to pass."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Shallum the son of Jabesh began to reign in the thirty-ninth year of Uzziah king of Judah, and he reigned for a month in Samaria."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Menahem the son of Gadi went up from Tirzah, came to Samaria, struck Shallum the son of Jabesh in Samaria, killed him, and reigned in his place."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Shallum, and his conspiracy which he made, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Menahem attacked Tiphsah and all who were in it and its border areas, from Tirzah. He attacked it because they didn\u2019t open their gates to him, and he ripped up all their women who were with child."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"In the thirty ninth year of Azariah king of Judah, Menahem the son of Gadi began to reign over Israel for ten years in Samaria."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight. He didn\u2019t depart all his days from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Pul the king of Assyria came against the land, and Menahem gave Pul one thousand talents of silver, that his hand might be with him to confirm the kingdom in his hand."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds, so 1000 talents is about 30 metric tons"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Menahem exacted the money from Israel, even from all the mighty men of wealth, from each man fifty shekels of silver, to give to the king of Assyria. So the king of Assyria turned back, and didn\u2019t stay there in the land."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 50 shekels was about 0.5 kilograms or 1.1 pounds."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Menahem, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Menahem slept with his fathers, and Pekahiah his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fiftieth year of Azariah king of Judah, Pekahiah the son of Menahem began to reign over Israel in Samaria for two years."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight. He didn\u2019t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Pekah the son of Remaliah, his captain, conspired against him and attacked him in Samaria, in the fortress of the king\u2019s house, with Argob and Arieh; and with him were fifty men of the Gileadites. He killed him, and reigned in his place."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Pekahiah, and all that he did, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fifty-second year of Azariah king of Judah, Pekah the son of Remaliah began to reign over Israel in Samaria for twenty years."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight. He didn\u2019t depart from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, with which he made Israel to sin."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"In the days of Pekah king of Israel, Tiglath Pileser king of Assyria came and took Ijon, Abel Beth Maacah, Janoah, Kedesh, Hazor, Gilead, and Galilee, all the land of Naphtali; and he carried them captive to Assyria."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Hoshea the son of Elah made a conspiracy against Pekah the son of Remaliah, attacked him, killed him, and reigned in his place, in the twentieth year of Jotham the son of Uzziah."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Pekah, and all that he did, behold, they are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"In the second year of Pekah the son of Remaliah king of Israel, Jotham the son of Uzziah king of Judah began to reign."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Jerusha the daughter of Zadok."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes. He did according to all that his father Uzziah had done."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"However the high places were not taken away. The people still sacrificed and burned incense in the high places. He built the upper gate of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jotham, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"In those days, the LORD began to send Rezin the king of Syria and Pekah the son of Remaliah against Judah."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Jotham slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in his father David\u2019s city; and Ahaz his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the seventeenth year of Pekah the son of Remaliah, Ahaz the son of Jotham king of Judah began to reign."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Ahaz was twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. He didn\u2019t do that which was right in the LORD his God\u2019s eyes, like David his father."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But he walked in the way of the kings of Israel, and even made his son to pass through the fire, according to the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He sacrificed and burned incense in the high places, on the hills, and under every green tree."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Rezin king of Syria and Pekah son of Remaliah king of Israel came up to Jerusalem to wage war. They besieged Ahaz, but could not overcome him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"At that time Rezin king of Syria recovered Elath to Syria, and drove the Jews from Elath; and the Syrians came to Elath, and live there to this day."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So Ahaz sent messengers to Tiglath Pileser king of Assyria, saying, \u201cI am your servant and your son. Come up and save me out of the hand of the king of Syria and out of the hand of the king of Israel, who rise up against me.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Ahaz took the silver and gold that was found in the LORD\u2019s house, and in the treasures of the king\u2019s house, and sent it for a present to the king of Assyria."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The king of Assyria listened to him; and the king of Assyria went up against Damascus and took it, and carried its people captive to Kir, and killed Rezin."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"King Ahaz went to Damascus to meet Tiglath Pileser king of Assyria, and saw the altar that was at Damascus; and King Ahaz sent to Urijah the priest a drawing of the altar and plans to build it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Urijah the priest built an altar. According to all that King Ahaz had sent from Damascus, so Urijah the priest made it for the coming of King Ahaz from Damascus."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When the king had come from Damascus, the king saw the altar; and the king came near to the altar, and offered on it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He burned his burnt offering and his meal offering, poured his drink offering, and sprinkled the blood of his peace offerings on the altar."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The bronze altar, which was before the LORD, he brought from the front of the house, from between his altar and the LORD\u2019s house, and put it on the north side of his altar."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"King Ahaz commanded Urijah the priest, saying, \u201cOn the great altar burn the morning burnt offering, the evening meal offering, the king\u2019s burnt offering and his meal offering, with the burnt offering of all the people of the land, their meal offering, and their drink offerings; and sprinkle on it all the blood of the burnt offering, and all the blood of the sacrifice; but the bronze altar will be for me to inquire by.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Urijah the priest did so, according to all that King Ahaz commanded."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"King Ahaz cut off the panels of the bases, and removed the basin from off them, and took down the sea from off the bronze oxen that were under it, and put it on a pavement of stone."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He removed the covered way for the Sabbath that they had built in the house, and the king\u2019s outer entrance to the LORD\u2019s house, because of the king of Assyria."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Ahaz which he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Ahaz slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David\u2019s city; and Hezekiah his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twelfth year of Ahaz king of Judah, Hoshea the son of Elah began to reign in Samaria over Israel for nine years."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, yet not as the kings of Israel who were before him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Shalmaneser king of Assyria came up against him; and Hoshea became his servant, and brought him tribute."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The king of Assyria discovered a conspiracy in Hoshea; for he had sent messengers to So king of Egypt, and offered no tribute to the king of Assyria, as he had done year by year. Therefore the king of Assyria seized him, and bound him in prison."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then the king of Assyria came up throughout all the land, went up to Samaria, and besieged it three years."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In the ninth year of Hoshea the king of Assyria took Samaria and carried Israel away to Assyria, and placed them in Halah, and on the Habor, the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"It was so because the children of Israel had sinned against the LORD their God, who brought them up out of the land of Egypt from under the hand of Pharaoh king of Egypt, and had feared other gods,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and walked in the statutes of the nations whom the LORD cast out from before the children of Israel, and of the kings of Israel, which they made."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The children of Israel secretly did things that were not right against the LORD their God; and they built high places for themselves in all their cities, from the tower of the watchmen to the fortified city;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and they set up for themselves pillars and Asherah poles on every high hill and under every green tree;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and there they burned incense in all the high places, as the nations whom the LORD carried away before them did; and they did wicked things to provoke the LORD to anger;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and they served idols, of which the LORD had said to them, \u201cYou shall not do this thing.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Yet the LORD testified to Israel and to Judah, by every prophet and every seer, saying, \u201cTurn from your evil ways, and keep my commandments and my statutes, according to all the law which I commanded your fathers, and which I sent to you by my servants the prophets.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Notwithstanding, they would not listen, but hardened their neck like the neck of their fathers who didn\u2019t believe in the LORD their God."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They rejected his statutes and his covenant that he made with their fathers, and his testimonies which he testified to them; and they followed vanity, and became vain, and followed the nations that were around them, concerning whom the LORD had commanded them that they should not do like them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They abandoned all the commandments of the LORD their God, and made molten images for themselves, even two calves, and made an Asherah, and worshiped all the army of the sky, and served Baal."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They caused their sons and their daughters to pass through the fire, used divination and enchantments, and sold themselves to do that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, to provoke him to anger."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD was very angry with Israel, and removed them out of his sight. There was none left but the tribe of Judah only."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Also Judah didn\u2019t keep the commandments of the LORD their God, but walked in the statutes of Israel which they made."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The LORD rejected all the offspring of Israel, afflicted them, and delivered them into the hands of raiders, until he had cast them out of his sight."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For he tore Israel from David\u2019s house; and they made Jeroboam the son of Nebat king; and Jeroboam drove Israel from following the LORD, and made them sin a great sin."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The children of Israel walked in all the sins of Jeroboam which he did; they didn\u2019t depart from them"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"until the LORD removed Israel out of his sight, as he said by all his servants the prophets. So Israel was carried away out of their own land to Assyria to this day."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Assyria brought people from Babylon, from Cuthah, from Avva, and from Hamath and Sepharvaim, and placed them in the cities of Samaria instead of the children of Israel; and they possessed Samaria and lived in its cities."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"So it was, at the beginning of their dwelling there, that they didn\u2019t fear the LORD. Therefore the LORD sent lions among them, which killed some of them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Therefore they spoke to the king of Assyria, saying, \u201cThe nations which you have carried away and placed in the cities of Samaria don\u2019t know the law of the god of the land. Therefore he has sent lions among them; and behold, they kill them, because they don\u2019t know the law of the god of the land.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king of Assyria commanded, saying, \u201cCarry there one of the priests whom you brought from there; and let him go and dwell there, and let him teach them the law of the god of the land.\u201d"]],f:["Hebrew: them"]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"So one of the priests whom they had carried away from Samaria came and lived in Bethel, and taught them how they should fear the LORD."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"However every nation made gods of their own, and put them in the houses of the high places which the Samaritans had made, every nation in their cities in which they lived."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The men of Babylon made Succoth Benoth, and the men of Cuth made Nergal, and the men of Hamath made Ashima,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and the Avvites made Nibhaz and Tartak; and the Sepharvites burned their children in the fire to Adrammelech and Anammelech, the gods of Sepharvaim."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"So they feared the LORD, and also made from among themselves priests of the high places for themselves, who sacrificed for them in the houses of the high places."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They feared the LORD, and also served their own gods, after the ways of the nations from among whom they had been carried away."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"To this day they do what they did before. They don\u2019t fear the LORD, and they do not follow the statutes, or the ordinances, or the law, or the commandment which the LORD commanded the children of Jacob, whom he named Israel;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"with whom the LORD had made a covenant and commanded them, saying, \u201cYou shall not fear other gods, nor bow yourselves to them, nor serve them, nor sacrifice to them;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"but you shall fear the LORD, who brought you up out of the land of Egypt with great power and with an outstretched arm, and you shall bow yourselves to him, and you shall sacrifice to him."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The statutes and the ordinances, and the law and the commandment which he wrote for you, you shall observe to do forever more. You shall not fear other gods."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"You shall not forget the covenant that I have made with you. You shall not fear other gods."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But you shall fear the LORD your God, and he will deliver you out of the hand of all your enemies.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"However they didn\u2019t listen, but they did what they did before."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"So these nations feared the LORD, and also served their engraved images. Their children did likewise, and so did their children\u2019s children. They do as their fathers did to this day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the third year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, Hezekiah the son of Ahaz king of Judah began to reign."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Abi the daughter of Zechariah."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, according to all that David his father had done."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He removed the high places, broke the pillars, and cut down the Asherah. He also broke in pieces the bronze serpent that Moses had made, because in those days the children of Israel burned incense to it; and he called it Nehushtan."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He trusted in the LORD, the God of Israel, so that after him was no one like him among all the kings of Judah, nor among them that were before him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For he joined with the LORD. He didn\u2019t depart from following him, but kept his commandments, which the LORD commanded Moses."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD was with him. Wherever he went, he prospered. He rebelled against the king of Assyria, and didn\u2019t serve him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He struck the Philistines to Gaza and its borders, from the tower of the watchmen to the fortified city."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fourth year of King Hezekiah, which was the seventh year of Hoshea son of Elah king of Israel, Shalmaneser king of Assyria came up against Samaria and besieged it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"At the end of three years they took it. In the sixth year of Hezekiah, which was the ninth year of Hoshea king of Israel, Samaria was taken."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The king of Assyria carried Israel away to Assyria, and put them in Halah, and on the Habor, the river of Gozan, and in the cities of the Medes,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"because they didn\u2019t obey the LORD their God\u2019s voice, but transgressed his covenant, even all that Moses the servant of the LORD commanded, and would not hear it or do it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the fourteenth year of King Hezekiah, Sennacherib king of Assyria came up against all the fortified cities of Judah and took them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Hezekiah king of Judah sent to the king of Assyria at Lachish, saying, \u201cI have offended you. Withdraw from me. That which you put on me, I will bear.\u201d The king of Assyria appointed to Hezekiah king of Judah three hundred talents of silver and thirty talents of gold."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Hezekiah gave him all the silver that was found in the LORD\u2019s house and in the treasures of the king\u2019s house."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"At that time, Hezekiah cut off the gold from the doors of the LORD\u2019s temple, and from the pillars which Hezekiah king of Judah had overlaid, and gave it to the king of Assyria."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Assyria sent Tartan, Rabsaris, and Rabshakeh from Lachish to King Hezekiah with a great army to Jerusalem. They went up and came to Jerusalem. When they had come up, they came and stood by the conduit of the upper pool, which is in the highway of the fuller\u2019s field."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When they had called to the king, Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, and Shebnah the scribe, and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder came out to them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Rabshakeh said to them, \u201cSay now to Hezekiah, \u2018The great king, the king of Assyria, says, \u201cWhat confidence is this in which you trust?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You say (but they are but vain words), \u2018There is counsel and strength for war.\u2019 Now on whom do you trust, that you have rebelled against me?"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Now, behold, you trust in the staff of this bruised reed, even in Egypt. If a man leans on it, it will go into his hand and pierce it. So is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all who trust on him."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But if you tell me, \u2018We trust in the LORD our God,\u2019 isn\u2019t that he whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah has taken away, and has said to Judah and to Jerusalem, \u2018You shall worship before this altar in Jerusalem\u2019?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please give pledges to my master the king of Assyria, and I will give you two thousand horses if you are able on your part to set riders on them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"How then can you turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master\u2019s servants, and put your trust on Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Have I now come up without the LORD against this place to destroy it? The LORD said to me, \u2018Go up against this land, and destroy it.\u2019\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, Shebnah, and Joah, said to Rabshakeh, \u201cPlease speak to your servants in the Syrian language, for we understand it. Don\u2019t speak with us in the Jews\u2019 language, in the hearing of the people who are on the wall.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But Rabshakeh said to them, \u201cHas my master sent me to your master and to you, to speak these words? Hasn\u2019t he sent me to the men who sit on the wall, to eat their own dung, and to drink their own urine with you?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Rabshakeh stood and cried with a loud voice in the Jews\u2019 language, and spoke, saying, \u201cHear the word of the great king, the king of Assyria."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The king says, \u2018Don\u2019t let Hezekiah deceive you, for he will not be able to deliver you out of his hand."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, \u201cThe LORD will surely deliver us, and this city shall not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t listen to Hezekiah.\u2019 For the king of Assyria says, \u2018Make your peace with me, and come out to me; and everyone of you eat from his own vine, and everyone from his own fig tree, and everyone drink water from his own cistern;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of grain and new wine, a land of bread and vineyards, a land of olive trees and of honey, that you may live and not die. Don\u2019t listen to Hezekiah when he persuades you, saying, \u201cThe LORD will deliver us.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Has any of the gods of the nations ever delivered his land out of the hand of the king of Assyria?"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Where are the gods of Hamath and of Arpad? Where are the gods of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivvah? Have they delivered Samaria out of my hand?"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Who are they among all the gods of the countries, that have delivered their country out of my hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of my hand?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"But the people stayed quiet, and answered him not a word; for the king\u2019s commandment was, \u201cDon\u2019t answer him.\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, came with Shebna the scribe and Joah the son of Asaph the recorder to Hezekiah with their clothes torn, and told him Rabshakeh\u2019s words."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When King Hezekiah heard it, he tore his clothes, covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He sent Eliakim, who was over the household, Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cHezekiah says, \u2018Today is a day of trouble, of rebuke, and of rejection; for the children have come to the point of birth, and there is no strength to deliver them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"It may be the LORD your God will hear all the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master has sent to defy the living God, and will rebuke the words which the LORD your God has heard. Therefore lift up your prayer for the remnant that is left.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"So the servants of King Hezekiah came to Isaiah."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Isaiah said to them, \u201cTell your master this: \u2018The LORD says, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid of the words that you have heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Behold, I will put a spirit in him, and he will hear news, and will return to his own land. I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So Rabshakeh returned and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah; for he had heard that he had departed from Lachish."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When he heard it said of Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, \u201cBehold, he has come out to fight against you,\u201d he sent messengers again to Hezekiah, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cTell Hezekiah king of Judah this: \u2018Don\u2019t let your God in whom you trust deceive you, saying, Jerusalem will not be given into the hand of the king of Assyria."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Behold, you have heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands, by destroying them utterly. Will you be delivered?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Have the gods of the nations delivered them, which my fathers have destroyed\u2014Gozan, Haran, Rezeph, and the children of Eden who were in Telassar?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Where is the king of Hamath, the king of Arpad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivvah?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah received the letter from the hand of the messengers and read it. Then Hezekiah went up to the LORD\u2019s house, and spread it before the LORD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Hezekiah prayed before the LORD, and said, \u201cLORD, the God of Israel, enthroned above the cherubim, you are the God, even you alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth. You have made heaven and earth."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Incline your ear, LORD, and hear. Open your eyes, LORD, and see. Hear the words of Sennacherib, which he has sent to defy the living God."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Truly, LORD, the kings of Assyria have laid waste the nations and their lands,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and have cast their gods into the fire; for they were no gods, but the work of men\u2019s hands, wood and stone. Therefore they have destroyed them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now therefore, LORD our God, save us, I beg you, out of his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that you, LORD, are God alone.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to Hezekiah, saying, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says \u2018You have prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria, and I have heard you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"This is the word that the LORD has spoken concerning him: \u2018The virgin daughter of Zion has despised you and ridiculed you. The daughter of Jerusalem has shaken her head at you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Whom have you defied and blasphemed? Against whom have you exalted your voice and lifted up your eyes on high? Against the Holy One of Israel!"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"By your messengers, you have defied the Lord, and have said, \u201cWith the multitude of my chariots, I have come up to the height of the mountains, to the innermost parts of Lebanon, and I will cut down its tall cedars and its choice cypress trees; and I will enter into his farthest lodging place, the forest of his fruitful field."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I have dug and drunk strange waters, and I will dry up all the rivers of Egypt with the sole of my feet.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Haven\u2019t you heard how I have done it long ago, and formed it of ancient times? Now I have brought it to pass, that it should be yours to lay waste fortified cities into ruinous heaps."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Therefore their inhabitants had little power. They were dismayed and confounded. They were like the grass of the field and like the green herb, like the grass on the housetops and like grain blasted before it has grown up."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But I know your sitting down, your going out, your coming in, and your raging against me."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Because of your raging against me, and because your arrogance has come up into my ears, therefore I will put my hook in your nose, and my bridle in your lips, and I will turn you back by the way by which you came.\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis will be the sign to you: This year, you will eat that which grows of itself, and in the second year that which springs from that; and in the third year sow and reap, and plant vineyards and eat their fruit."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The remnant that has escaped of the house of Judah will again take root downward, and bear fruit upward."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For out of Jerusalem a remnant will go out, and out of Mount Zion those who shall escape. The LORD\u2019s zeal will perform this."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the LORD says concerning the king of Assyria, \u2018He will not come to this city, nor shoot an arrow there. He will not come before it with shield, nor cast up a mound against it."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He will return the same way that he came, and he will not come to this city,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"\u2018For I will defend this city to save it, for my own sake and for my servant David\u2019s sake.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"That night, the LORD\u2019s angel went out and struck one hundred eighty-five thousand in the camp of the Assyrians. When men arose early in the morning, behold, these were all dead bodies."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, went home, and lived at Nineveh."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"As he was worshiping in the house of Nisroch his god, Adrammelech and Sharezer struck him with the sword; and they escaped into the land of Ararat. Esar Haddon his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days Hezekiah was sick and dying. Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz came to him, and said to him, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Set your house in order; for you will die, and not live.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he turned his face to the wall, and prayed to the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cRemember now, LORD, I beg you, how I have walked before you in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in your sight.\u201d And Hezekiah wept bitterly."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Before Isaiah had gone out into the middle part of the city, the LORD\u2019s word came to him, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cTurn back, and tell Hezekiah the prince of my people, \u2018The LORD, the God of David your father, says, \u201cI have heard your prayer. I have seen your tears. Behold, I will heal you. On the third day, you will go up to the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I will add to your days fifteen years. I will deliver you and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria. I will defend this city for my own sake, and for my servant David\u2019s sake.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah said, \u201cTake a cake of figs.\u201d"],[0,"They took and laid it on the boil, and he recovered."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah said to Isaiah, \u201cWhat will be the sign that the LORD will heal me, and that I will go up to the LORD\u2019s house the third day?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah said, \u201cThis will be the sign to you from the LORD, that the LORD will do the thing that he has spoken: should the shadow go forward ten steps, or go back ten steps?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah answered, \u201cIt is a light thing for the shadow to go forward ten steps. No, but let the shadow return backward ten steps.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah the prophet cried to the LORD; and he brought the shadow ten steps backward, by which it had gone down on the sundial of Ahaz."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time Berodach Baladan the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah, for he had heard that Hezekiah had been sick."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Hezekiah listened to them, and showed them all the storehouse of his precious things\u2014the silver, the gold, the spices, and the precious oil, and the house of his armor, and all that was found in his treasures. There was nothing in his house, or in all his dominion, that Hezekiah didn\u2019t show them."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Isaiah the prophet came to King Hezekiah, and said to him, \u201cWhat did these men say? From where did they come to you?\u201d"],[0,"Hezekiah said, \u201cThey have come from a far country, even from Babylon.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhat have they seen in your house?\u201d"],[0,"Hezekiah answered, \u201cThey have seen all that is in my house. There is nothing among my treasures that I have not shown them.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah said to Hezekiah, \u201cHear the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u2018Behold, the days come that all that is in your house, and that which your fathers have laid up in store to this day, will be carried to Babylon. Nothing will be left,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u2018They will take away some of your sons who will issue from you, whom you will father; and they will be eunuchs in the palace of the king of Babylon.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hezekiah said to Isaiah, \u201cThe LORD\u2019s word which you have spoken is good.\u201d He said moreover, \u201cIsn\u2019t it so, if peace and truth will be in my days?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Hezekiah, and all his might, and how he made the pool, and the conduit, and brought water into the city, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Hezekiah slept with his fathers, and Manasseh his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-five years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Hephzibah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, after the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For he built again the high places which Hezekiah his father had destroyed; and he raised up altars for Baal, and made an Asherah, as Ahab king of Israel did, and worshiped all the army of the sky, and served them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He built altars in the LORD\u2019s house, of which the LORD said, \u201cI will put my name in Jerusalem.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He built altars for all the army of the sky in the two courts of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He made his son to pass through the fire, practiced sorcery, used enchantments, and dealt with those who had familiar spirits and with wizards. He did much evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, to provoke him to anger."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He set the engraved image of Asherah that he had made in the house of which the LORD said to David and to Solomon his son, \u201cIn this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will put my name forever;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will not cause the feet of Israel to wander any more out of the land which I gave their fathers, if only they will observe to do according to all that I have commanded them, and according to all the law that my servant Moses commanded them.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But they didn\u2019t listen, and Manasseh seduced them to do that which is evil more than the nations did whom the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke by his servants the prophets, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cBecause Manasseh king of Judah has done these abominations, and has done wickedly above all that the Amorites did, who were before him, and has also made Judah to sin with his idols;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"therefore the LORD the God of Israel says, \u2018Behold, I will bring such evil on Jerusalem and Judah that whoever hears of it, both his ears will tingle."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will stretch over Jerusalem the line of Samaria, and the plumb line of Ahab\u2019s house; and I will wipe Jerusalem as a man wipes a dish, wiping it and turning it upside down."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will cast off the remnant of my inheritance and deliver them into the hands of their enemies. They will become a prey and a plunder to all their enemies,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"because they have done that which is evil in my sight, and have provoked me to anger since the day their fathers came out of Egypt, even to this day.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Manasseh shed innocent blood very much, until he had filled Jerusalem from one end to another; in addition to his sin with which he made Judah to sin, in doing that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and all that he did, and his sin that he sinned, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Manasseh slept with his fathers, and was buried in the garden of his own house, in the garden of Uzza; and Amon his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Amon was twenty-two years old when he began to reign; and he reigned two years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Meshullemeth the daughter of Haruz of Jotbah."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, as Manasseh his father did."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He walked in all the ways that his father walked in, and served the idols that his father served, and worshiped them;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and he abandoned the LORD, the God of his fathers, and didn\u2019t walk in the way of the LORD."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The servants of Amon conspired against him, and put the king to death in his own house."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But the people of the land killed all those who had conspired against King Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his place."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Amon which he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He was buried in his tomb in the garden of Uzza, and Josiah his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty-one years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Jedidah the daughter of Adaiah of Bozkath."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, and walked in all the ways of David his father, and didn\u2019t turn away to the right hand or to the left."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"In the eighteenth year of King Josiah, the king sent Shaphan, the son of Azaliah the son of Meshullam, the scribe, to the LORD\u2019s house, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cGo up to Hilkiah the high priest, that he may count the money which is brought into the LORD\u2019s house, which the keepers of the threshold have gathered of the people."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Let them deliver it into the hand of the workers who have the oversight of the LORD\u2019s house; and let them give it to the workers who are in the LORD\u2019s house, to repair the damage to the house,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"to the carpenters, and to the builders, and to the masons, and for buying timber and cut stone to repair the house."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"However, no accounting shall be asked of them for the money delivered into their hand, for they deal faithfully.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Hilkiah the high priest said to Shaphan the scribe, \u201cI have found the book of the law in the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d Hilkiah delivered the book to Shaphan, and he read it."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Shaphan the scribe came to the king, and brought the king word again, and said, \u201cYour servants have emptied out the money that was found in the house, and have delivered it into the hands of the workmen who have the oversight of the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Shaphan the scribe told the king, saying, \u201cHilkiah the priest has delivered a book to me.\u201d Then Shaphan read it before the king."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When the king had heard the words of the book of the law, he tore his clothes."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The king commanded Hilkiah the priest, Ahikam the son of Shaphan, Achbor the son of Micaiah, Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah the king\u2019s servant, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cGo inquire of the LORD for me, and for the people, and for all Judah, concerning the words of this book that is found; for great is the LORD\u2019s wrath that is kindled against us, because our fathers have not listened to the words of this book, to do according to all that which is written concerning us.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hilkiah the priest, Ahikam, Achbor, Shaphan, and Asaiah went to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tikvah, the son of Harhas, keeper of the wardrobe (now she lived in Jerusalem in the second quarter); and they talked with her."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"She said to them, \u201cThe LORD the God of Israel says, \u2018Tell the man who sent you to me,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Behold, I will bring evil on this place and on its inhabitants, even all the words of the book which the king of Judah has read."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Because they have forsaken me and have burned incense to other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the work of their hands, therefore my wrath shall be kindled against this place, and it will not be quenched.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But to the king of Judah, who sent you to inquire of the LORD, tell him, \u201cThe LORD the God of Israel says, \u2018Concerning the words which you have heard,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"because your heart was tender, and you humbled yourself before the LORD when you heard what I spoke against this place and against its inhabitants, that they should become a desolation and a curse, and have torn your clothes and wept before me, I also have heard you,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"\u2018Therefore behold, I will gather you to your fathers, and you will be gathered to your grave in peace. Your eyes will not see all the evil which I will bring on this place.\u2019\u201d\u2019\u201d So they brought this message back to the king."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The king sent, and they gathered to him all the elders of Judah and of Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The king went up to the LORD\u2019s house, and all the men of Judah and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem with him\u2014with the priests, the prophets, and all the people, both small and great; and he read in their hearing all the words of the book of the covenant which was found in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The king stood by the pillar and made a covenant before the LORD to walk after the LORD and to keep his commandments, his testimonies, and his statutes with all his heart and all his soul, to confirm the words of this covenant that were written in this book; and all the people agreed to the covenant."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The king commanded Hilkiah the high priest, and the priests of the second order, and the keepers of the threshold, to bring out of the LORD\u2019s temple all the vessels that were made for Baal, for the Asherah, and for all the army of the sky; and he burned them outside of Jerusalem in the fields of the Kidron, and carried their ashes to Bethel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He got rid of the idolatrous priests whom the kings of Judah had ordained to burn incense in the high places in the cities of Judah and in the places around Jerusalem; those also who burned incense to Baal, to the sun, to the moon, to the planets, and to all the army of the sky."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He brought out the Asherah from the LORD\u2019s house, outside of Jerusalem, to the brook Kidron, and burned it at the brook Kidron, and beat it to dust, and cast its dust on the graves of the common people."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He broke down the houses of the male shrine prostitutes that were in the LORD\u2019s house, where the women wove hangings for the Asherah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He brought all the priests out of the cities of Judah, and defiled the high places where the priests had burned incense, from Geba to Beersheba; and he broke down the high places of the gates that were at the entrance of the gate of Joshua the governor of the city, which were on a man\u2019s left hand at the gate of the city."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Nevertheless the priests of the high places didn\u2019t come up to the LORD\u2019s altar in Jerusalem, but they ate unleavened bread among their brothers."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He defiled Topheth, which is in the valley of the children of Hinnom, that no man might make his son or his daughter to pass through the fire to Molech."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He took away the horses that the kings of Judah had dedicated to the sun, at the entrance of the LORD\u2019s house, by the room of Nathan Melech the officer who was in the court; and he burned the chariots of the sun with fire."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The king broke down the altars that were on the roof of the upper room of Ahaz, which the kings of Judah had made, and the altars which Manasseh had made in the two courts of the LORD\u2019s house, and beat them down from there, and cast their dust into the brook Kidron."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The king defiled the high places that were before Jerusalem, which were on the right hand of the mountain of corruption, which Solomon the king of Israel had built for Ashtoreth the abomination of the Sidonians, and for Chemosh the abomination of Moab, and for Milcom the abomination of the children of Ammon."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He broke in pieces the pillars, cut down the Asherah poles, and filled their places with men\u2019s bones."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the altar that was at Bethel and the high place which Jeroboam the son of Nebat, who made Israel to sin, had made, even that altar and the high place he broke down; and he burned the high place and beat it to dust, and burned the Asherah."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"As Josiah turned himself, he spied the tombs that were there in the mountain; and he sent, and took the bones out of the tombs, and burned them on the altar, and defiled it, according to the LORD\u2019s word which the man of God proclaimed, who proclaimed these things."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cWhat monument is that which I see?\u201d"],[0,"The men of the city told him, \u201cIt is the tomb of the man of God who came from Judah and proclaimed these things that you have done against the altar of Bethel.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cLet him be! Let no one move his bones.\u201d So they let his bones alone, with the bones of the prophet who came out of Samaria."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"All the houses also of the high places that were in the cities of Samaria, which the kings of Israel had made to provoke the LORD to anger, Josiah took away, and did to them according to all the acts that he had done in Bethel."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He killed all the priests of the high places that were there, on the altars, and burned men\u2019s bones on them; and he returned to Jerusalem."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The king commanded all the people, saying, \u201cKeep the Passover to the LORD your God, as it is written in this book of the covenant.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Surely there was not kept such a Passover from the days of the judges who judged Israel, nor in all the days of the kings of Israel, nor of the kings of Judah;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"but in the eighteenth year of King Josiah, this Passover was kept to the LORD in Jerusalem."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover, Josiah removed those who had familiar spirits, the wizards, and the teraphim, and the idols, and all the abominations that were seen in the land of Judah and in Jerusalem, that he might confirm the words of the law which were written in the book that Hilkiah the priest found in the LORD\u2019s house."]],f:["teraphim were household idols."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There was no king like him before him, who turned to the LORD with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with all his might, according to all the law of Moses; and there was none like him who arose after him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Notwithstanding, the LORD didn\u2019t turn from the fierceness of his great wrath, with which his anger burned against Judah, because of all the provocation with which Manasseh had provoked him."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cI will also remove Judah out of my sight, as I have removed Israel; and I will cast off this city which I have chosen, even Jerusalem, and the house of which I said, \u2018My name shall be there.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Josiah, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"In his days Pharaoh Necoh king of Egypt went up against the king of Assyria to the river Euphrates; and King Josiah went against him, but Pharaoh Necoh killed him at Megiddo when he saw him."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"His servants carried him dead in a chariot from Megiddo, brought him to Jerusalem, and buried him in his own tomb. The people of the land took Jehoahaz the son of Josiah, and anointed him, and made him king in his father\u2019s place."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoahaz was twenty-three years old when he began to reign; and he reigned three months in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Hamutal the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, according to all that his fathers had done."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Pharaoh Necoh put him in bonds at Riblah in the land of Hamath, that he might not reign in Jerusalem; and put the land to a tribute of one hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Pharaoh Necoh made Eliakim the son of Josiah king in the place of Josiah his father, and changed his name to Jehoiakim; but he took Jehoahaz away, and he came to Egypt and died there."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Jehoiakim gave the silver and the gold to Pharaoh; but he taxed the land to give the money according to the commandment of Pharaoh. He exacted the silver and the gold of the people of the land, from everyone according to his assessment, to give it to Pharaoh Necoh."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Zebidah the daughter of Pedaiah of Rumah."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, according to all that his fathers had done."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In his days Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up, and Jehoiakim became his servant for three years. Then he turned and rebelled against him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD sent against him bands of the Chaldeans, bands of the Syrians, bands of the Moabites, and bands of the children of Ammon, and sent them against Judah to destroy it, according to the LORD\u2019s word which he spoke by his servants the prophets."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Surely at the commandment of the LORD this came on Judah, to remove them out of his sight for the sins of Manasseh, according to all that he did,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and also for the innocent blood that he shed; for he filled Jerusalem with innocent blood, and the LORD would not pardon."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, and all that he did, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Judah?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Jehoiakim slept with his fathers, and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Egypt didn\u2019t come out of his land any more; for the king of Babylon had taken, from the brook of Egypt to the river Euphrates, all that belonged to the king of Egypt."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months. His mother\u2019s name was Nehushta the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, according to all that his father had done."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"At that time the servants of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up to Jerusalem, and the city was besieged."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to the city while his servants were besieging it,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and Jehoiachin the king of Judah went out to the king of Babylon\u2014he, his mother, his servants, his princes, and his officers; and the king of Babylon captured him in the eighth year of his reign."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He carried out from there all the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house and the treasures of the king\u2019s house, and cut in pieces all the vessels of gold which Solomon king of Israel had made in the LORD\u2019s temple, as the LORD had said."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He carried away all Jerusalem, and all the princes, and all the mighty men of valor, even ten thousand captives, and all the craftsmen and the smiths. No one remained except the poorest people of the land."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He carried away Jehoiachin to Babylon, with the king\u2019s mother, the king\u2019s wives, his officers, and the chief men of the land. He carried them into captivity from Jerusalem to Babylon."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"All the men of might, even seven thousand, and the craftsmen and the smiths one thousand, all of them strong and fit for war, even them the king of Babylon brought captive to Babylon."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The king of Babylon made Mattaniah, Jehoiachin\u2019s father\u2019s brother, king in his place, and changed his name to Zedekiah."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Hamutal the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, according to all that Jehoiakim had done."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For through the anger of the LORD, this happened in Jerusalem and Judah, until he had cast them out from his presence."],[0,"Then Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came, he and all his army, against Jerusalem, and encamped against it; and they built forts against it around it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"So the city was besieged until the eleventh year of King Zedekiah."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"On the ninth day of the fourth month, the famine was severe in the city, so that there was no bread for the people of the land."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then a breach was made in the city, and all the men of war fled by night by the way of the gate between the two walls, which was by the king\u2019s garden (now the Chaldeans were against the city around it); and the king went by the way of the Arabah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But the Chaldean army pursued the king, and overtook him in the plains of Jericho; and all his army was scattered from him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then they captured the king and carried him up to the king of Babylon to Riblah; and they passed judgment on him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They killed Zedekiah\u2019s sons before his eyes, then put out Zedekiah\u2019s eyes, bound him in fetters, and carried him to Babylon."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the fifth month, on the seventh day of the month, which was the nineteenth year of King Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard, a servant of the king of Babylon, came to Jerusalem."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He burned the LORD\u2019s house, the king\u2019s house, and all the houses of Jerusalem. He burned every great house with fire."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All the army of the Chaldeans, who were with the captain of the guard, broke down the walls around Jerusalem."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive the rest of the people who were left in the city and those who had deserted to the king of Babylon\u2014all the rest of the multitude."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But the captain of the guard left some of the poorest of the land to work the vineyards and fields."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The Chaldeans broke up the pillars of bronze that were in the LORD\u2019s house and the bases and the bronze sea that were in the LORD\u2019s house, and carried the bronze pieces to Babylon."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They took away the pots, the shovels, the snuffers, the spoons, and all the vessels of bronze with which they ministered."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The captain of the guard took away the fire pans, the basins, that which was of gold, for gold, and that which was of silver, for silver."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The two pillars, the one sea, and the bases, which Solomon had made for the LORD\u2019s house, the bronze of all these vessels was not weighed."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The height of the one pillar was eighteen cubits, and a capital of bronze was on it. The height of the capital was three cubits, with network and pomegranates on the capital around it, all of bronze; and the second pillar with its network was like these."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the threshold;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and out of the city he took an officer who was set over the men of war; and five men of those who saw the king\u2019s face, who were found in the city; and the scribe, the captain of the army, who mustered the people of the land, and sixty men of the people of the land who were found in the city."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard took them, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The king of Babylon attacked them and put them to death at Riblah in the land of Hamath. So Judah was carried away captive out of his land."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"As for the people who were left in the land of Judah whom Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had left, even over them he made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, governor."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now when all the captains of the forces, they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah governor, they came to Gedaliah to Mizpah, even Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, Johanan the son of Kareah, Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth the Netophathite, and Jaazaniah the son of the Maacathite, they and their men."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Gedaliah swore to them and to their men, and said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid because of the servants of the Chaldeans. Dwell in the land and serve the king of Babylon, and it will be well with you.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But in the seventh month, Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, of the royal offspring came, and ten men with him, and struck Gedaliah so that he died, with the Jews and the Chaldeans that were with him at Mizpah."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"All the people, both small and great, and the captains of the forces arose and came to Egypt; for they were afraid of the Chaldeans."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"In the thirty-seventh year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, on the twenty-seventh day of the month, Evilmerodach king of Babylon, in the year that he began to reign, released Jehoiachin king of Judah out of prison,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and he spoke kindly to him and set his throne above the throne of the kings who were with him in Babylon,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"and changed his prison garments. Jehoiachin ate bread before him continually all the days of his life;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and for his allowance, there was a continual allowance given him from the king, every day a portion, all the days of his life."]]}]]}},1283,[]);
__d(function(e,h,a,t,o,s,n){o.exports={book:"1Chr",name:"1 Chronicles",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Adam, Seth, Enosh,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Kenan, Mahalalel, Jared,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Enoch, Methuselah, Lamech,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Noah, Shem, Ham, and Japheth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Diphath, and Togarmah."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, Kittim, and Rodanim."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Ham: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabta, Raama, Sabteca. The sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Cush became the father of Nimrod. He began to be a mighty one on the earth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Mizraim became the father of Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Pathrusim, Casluhim (where the Philistines came from), and Caphtorim."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Canaan became the father of Sidon his firstborn, Heth,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the Jebusite, the Amorite, the Girgashite,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"the Hivite, the Arkite, the Sinite,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the Arvadite, the Zemarite, and the Hamathite."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Shem: Elam, Asshur, Arpachshad, Lud, Aram, Uz, Hul, Gether, and Meshech."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Arpachshad became the father of Shelah, and Shelah became the father of Eber."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"To Eber were born two sons: the name of the one was Peleg, for in his days the earth was divided; and his brother\u2019s name was Joktan."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Joktan became the father of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Ebal, Abimael, Sheba,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Ophir, Havilah, and Jobab. All these were the sons of Joktan."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Shem, Arpachshad, Shelah,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Eber, Peleg, Reu,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Serug, Nahor, Terah,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Abram (also called Abraham)."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Abraham: Isaac and Ishmael."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"These are their generations: the firstborn of Ishmael, Nebaioth; then Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. These are the sons of Ishmael."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Keturah, Abraham\u2019s concubine: she bore Zimran, Jokshan, Medan, Midian, Ishbak, and Shuah. The sons of Jokshan: Sheba and Dedan."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The sons of Midian: Ephah, Epher, Hanoch, Abida, and Eldaah. All these were the sons of Keturah."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham became the father of Isaac. The sons of Isaac: Esau and Israel."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The sons of Esau: Eliphaz, Reuel, Jeush, Jalam, and Korah."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The sons of Eliphaz: Teman, Omar, Zephi, Gatam, Kenaz, Timna, and Amalek."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The sons of Reuel: Nahath, Zerah, Shammah, and Mizzah."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Seir: Lotan, Shobal, Zibeon, Anah, Dishon, Ezer, and Dishan."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The sons of Lotan: Hori and Homam; and Timna was Lotan\u2019s sister."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The sons of Shobal: Alian, Manahath, Ebal, Shephi, and Onam. The sons of Zibeon: Aiah and Anah."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The son of Anah: Dishon. The sons of Dishon: Hamran, Eshban, Ithran, and Cheran."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"The sons of Ezer: Bilhan, Zaavan, and Jaakan. The sons of Dishan: Uz and Aran."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the kings who reigned in the land of Edom, before any king reigned over the children of Israel: Bela the son of Beor; and the name of his city was Dinhabah."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Bela died, and Jobab the son of Zerah of Bozrah reigned in his place."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Jobab died, and Husham of the land of the Temanites reigned in his place."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Husham died, and Hadad the son of Bedad, who struck Midian in the field of Moab, reigned in his place; and the name of his city was Avith."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Hadad died, and Samlah of Masrekah reigned in his place."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Samlah died, and Shaul of Rehoboth by the River reigned in his place."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Shaul died, and Baal Hanan the son of Achbor reigned in his place."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Baal Hanan died, and Hadad reigned in his place; and the name of his city was Pai. His wife\u2019s name was Mehetabel, the daughter of Matred, the daughter of Mezahab."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Then Hadad died. The chiefs of Edom were: chief Timna, chief Aliah, chief Jetheth,"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"chief Oholibamah, chief Elah, chief Pinon,"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"chief Kenaz, chief Teman, chief Mibzar,"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"chief Magdiel, and chief Iram. These are the chiefs of Edom."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Israel: Reuben, Simeon, Levi, Judah, Issachar, Zebulun,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Dan, Joseph, Benjamin, Naphtali, Gad, and Asher."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Judah: Er, Onan, and Shelah, which three were born to him of Shua\u2019s daughter the Canaanitess. Er, Judah\u2019s firstborn, was wicked in the LORD\u2019s sight; and he killed him."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Tamar his daughter-in-law bore him Perez and Zerah. All the sons of Judah were five."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Perez: Hezron and Hamul."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The sons of Zerah: Zimri, Ethan, Heman, Calcol, and Dara\u2014five of them in all."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The son of Carmi: Achar, the troubler of Israel, who committed a trespass in the devoted thing."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The son of Ethan: Azariah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons also of Hezron, who were born to him: Jerahmeel, Ram, and Chelubai."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Ram became the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab became the father of Nahshon, prince of the children of Judah;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and Nahshon became the father of Salma, and Salma became the father of Boaz,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and Boaz became the father of Obed, and Obed became the father of Jesse;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and Jesse became the father of his firstborn Eliab, Abinadab the second, Shimea the third,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Nethanel the fourth, Raddai the fifth,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Ozem the sixth, and David the seventh;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and their sisters were Zeruiah and Abigail. The sons of Zeruiah: Abishai, Joab, and Asahel, three."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Abigail bore Amasa; and the father of Amasa was Jether the Ishmaelite."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Caleb the son of Hezron became the father of children by Azubah his wife, and by Jerioth; and these were her sons: Jesher, Shobab, and Ardon."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Azubah died, and Caleb married Ephrath, who bore him Hur."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Hur became the father of Uri, and Uri became the father of Bezalel."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Afterward Hezron went in to the daughter of Machir the father of Gilead, whom he took as wife when he was sixty years old; and she bore him Segub."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Segub became the father of Jair, who had twenty-three cities in the land of Gilead."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Geshur and Aram took the towns of Jair from them, with Kenath, and its villages, even sixty cities. All these were the sons of Machir the father of Gilead."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"After Hezron died in Caleb Ephrathah, Abijah, Hezron\u2019s wife, bore him Ashhur the father of Tekoa."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Jerahmeel the firstborn of Hezron were Ram the firstborn, Bunah, Oren, Ozem, and Ahijah."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Jerahmeel had another wife, whose name was Atarah. She was the mother of Onam."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The sons of Ram the firstborn of Jerahmeel were Maaz, Jamin, and Eker."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The sons of Onam were Shammai and Jada. The sons of Shammai: Nadab and Abishur."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The name of the wife of Abishur was Abihail; and she bore him Ahban and Molid."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The sons of Nadab: Seled and Appaim; but Seled died without children."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The son of Appaim: Ishi. The son of Ishi: Sheshan. The son of Sheshan: Ahlai."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The sons of Jada the brother of Shammai: Jether and Jonathan; and Jether died without children."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The sons of Jonathan: Peleth and Zaza. These were the sons of Jerahmeel."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Now Sheshan had no sons, but only daughters. Sheshan had a servant, an Egyptian, whose name was Jarha."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Sheshan gave his daughter to Jarha his servant as wife; and she bore him Attai."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Attai became the father of Nathan, and Nathan became the father of Zabad,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"and Zabad became the father of Ephlal, and Ephlal became the father of Obed,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"and Obed became the father of Jehu, and Jehu became the father of Azariah,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and Azariah became the father of Helez, and Helez became the father of Eleasah,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"and Eleasah became the father of Sismai, and Sismai became the father of Shallum,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"and Shallum became the father of Jekamiah, and Jekamiah became the father of Elishama."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Caleb the brother of Jerahmeel were Mesha his firstborn, who was the father of Ziph, and the sons of Mareshah the father of Hebron."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"The sons of Hebron: Korah, Tappuah, Rekem, and Shema."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Shema became the father of Raham, the father of Jorkeam; and Rekem became the father of Shammai."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"The son of Shammai was Maon; and Maon was the father of Beth Zur."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Ephah, Caleb\u2019s concubine, bore Haran, Moza, and Gazez; and Haran became the father of Gazez."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"The sons of Jahdai: Regem, Jothan, Geshan, Pelet, Ephah, and Shaaph."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Maacah, Caleb\u2019s concubine, bore Sheber and Tirhanah."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"She bore also Shaaph the father of Madmannah, Sheva the father of Machbena and the father of Gibea; and the daughter of Caleb was Achsah."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"These were the sons of Caleb, the son of Hur, the firstborn of Ephrathah: Shobal the father of Kiriath Jearim,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Salma the father of Bethlehem, and Hareph the father of Beth Gader."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"Shobal the father of Kiriath Jearim had sons: Haroeh, half of the Menuhoth."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"The families of Kiriath Jearim: the Ithrites, the Puthites, the Shumathites, and the Mishraites; from them came the Zorathites and the Eshtaolites."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"The sons of Salma: Bethlehem, the Netophathites, Atroth Beth Joab, and half of the Manahathites, the Zorites."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"The families of scribes who lived at Jabez: the Tirathites, the Shimeathites, and the Sucathites. These are the Kenites who came from Hammath, the father of the house of Rechab."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these were the sons of David, who were born to him in Hebron: the firstborn, Amnon, of Ahinoam the Jezreelitess; the second, Daniel, of Abigail the Carmelitess;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"the third, Absalom the son of Maacah the daughter of Talmai king of Geshur; the fourth, Adonijah the son of Haggith;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"the fifth, Shephatiah of Abital; the sixth, Ithream by Eglah his wife:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"six were born to him in Hebron; and he reigned there seven years and six months. He reigned thirty-three years in Jerusalem;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and these were born to him in Jerusalem: Shimea, Shobab, Nathan, and Solomon, four, by Bathshua the daughter of Ammiel;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and Ibhar, Elishama, Eliphelet,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Elishama, Eliada, and Eliphelet, nine."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"All these were the sons of David, in addition to the sons of the concubines; and Tamar was their sister."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon\u2019s son was Rehoboam, Abijah his son, Asa his son, Jehoshaphat his son,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Joram his son, Ahaziah his son, Joash his son,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Amaziah his son, Azariah his son, Jotham his son,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Ahaz his son, Hezekiah his son, Manasseh his son,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Amon his son, and Josiah his son."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The sons of Josiah: the firstborn Johanan, the second Jehoiakim, the third Zedekiah, and the fourth Shallum."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The sons of Jehoiakim: Jeconiah his son, and Zedekiah his son."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The sons of Jeconiah, the captive: Shealtiel his son,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Malchiram, Pedaiah, Shenazzar, Jekamiah, Hoshama, and Nedabiah."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of Pedaiah: Zerubbabel and Shimei. The sons of Zerubbabel: Meshullam and Hananiah; and Shelomith was their sister;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and Hashubah, Ohel, Berechiah, Hasadiah, and Jushab Hesed, five."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The sons of Hananiah: Pelatiah and Jeshaiah; the sons of Rephaiah, the sons of Arnan, the sons of Obadiah, the sons of Shecaniah."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The son of Shecaniah: Shemaiah. The sons of Shemaiah: Hattush, Igal, Bariah, Neariah, and Shaphat, six."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The sons of Neariah: Elioenai, Hizkiah, and Azrikam, three."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The sons of Elioenai: Hodaviah, Eliashib, Pelaiah, Akkub, Johanan, Delaiah, and Anani, seven."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Judah: Perez, Hezron, Carmi, Hur, and Shobal."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Reaiah the son of Shobal became the father of Jahath; and Jahath became the father of Ahumai and Lahad. These are the families of the Zorathites."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"These were the sons of the father of Etam: Jezreel, Ishma, and Idbash. The name of their sister was Hazzelelponi."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Penuel was the father of Gedor and Ezer the father of Hushah. These are the sons of Hur, the firstborn of Ephrathah, the father of Bethlehem."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ashhur the father of Tekoa had two wives, Helah and Naarah."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Naarah bore him Ahuzzam, Hepher, Temeni, and Haahashtari. These were the sons of Naarah."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The sons of Helah were Zereth, Izhar, and Ethnan."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Hakkoz became the father of Anub, Zobebah, and the families of Aharhel the son of Harum."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jabez was more honorable than his brothers. His mother named him Jabez, saying, \u201cBecause I bore him with sorrow.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cJabez\u201d sounds similar to the Hebrew word for \u201cpain\u201d."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Jabez called on the God of Israel, saying, \u201cOh that you would bless me indeed, and enlarge my border! May your hand be with me, and may you keep me from evil, that I may not cause pain!\u201d"],[0,"God granted him that which he requested."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Chelub the brother of Shuhah became the father of Mehir, who was the father of Eshton."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Eshton became the father of Beth Rapha, Paseah, and Tehinnah the father of Ir Nahash. These are the men of Recah."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The sons of Kenaz: Othniel and Seraiah. The sons of Othniel: Hathath."]],f:["Greek and Vulgate add \u201cand Meonothai\u201d"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Meonothai became the father of Ophrah: and Seraiah became the father of Joab the father of Ge Harashim, for they were craftsmen."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The sons of Caleb the son of Jephunneh: Iru, Elah, and Naam. The son of Elah: Kenaz."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The sons of Jehallelel: Ziph, Ziphah, Tiria, and Asarel."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The sons of Ezrah: Jether, Mered, Epher, and Jalon; and Mered\u2019s wife bore Miriam, Shammai, and Ishbah the father of Eshtemoa."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"His wife the Jewess bore Jered the father of Gedor, Heber the father of Soco, and Jekuthiel the father of Zanoah. These are the sons of Bithiah the daughter of Pharaoh, whom Mered took."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of the wife of Hodiah, the sister of Naham, were the fathers of Keilah the Garmite and Eshtemoa the Maacathite."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The sons of Shimon: Amnon, Rinnah, Ben Hanan, and Tilon. The sons of Ishi: Zoheth, and Ben Zoheth."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The sons of Shelah the son of Judah: Er the father of Lecah, Laadah the father of Mareshah, and the families of the house of those who worked fine linen, of the house of Ashbea;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and Jokim, and the men of Cozeba, and Joash, and Saraph, who had dominion in Moab, and Jashubilehem. These records are ancient."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"These were the potters, and the inhabitants of Netaim and Gederah; they lived there with the king for his work."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Simeon: Nemuel, Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, Shaul;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Shallum his son, Mibsam his son, and Mishma his son."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The sons of Mishma: Hammuel his son, Zaccur his son, Shimei his son."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters; but his brothers didn\u2019t have many children, and all their family didn\u2019t multiply like the children of Judah."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They lived at Beersheba, Moladah, Hazarshual,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"at Bilhah, at Ezem, at Tolad,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"at Bethuel, at Hormah, at Ziklag,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"at Beth Marcaboth, Hazar Susim, at Beth Biri, and at Shaaraim. These were their cities until David\u2019s reign."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Their villages were Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Tochen, and Ashan, five cities;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"and all their villages that were around the same cities, as far as Baal. These were their settlements, and they kept their genealogy."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Meshobab, Jamlech, Joshah the son of Amaziah,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Joel, Jehu the son of Joshibiah, the son of Seraiah, the son of Asiel,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Elioenai, Jaakobah, Jeshohaiah, Asaiah, Adiel, Jesimiel, Benaiah,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"and Ziza the son of Shiphi, the son of Allon, the son of Jedaiah, the son of Shimri, the son of Shemaiah\u2014"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"these mentioned by name were princes in their families. Their fathers\u2019 houses increased greatly."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"They went to the entrance of Gedor, even to the east side of the valley, to seek pasture for their flocks."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"They found rich, good pasture, and the land was wide, and quiet, and peaceful, for those who lived there before were descended from Ham."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"These written by name came in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah, and struck their tents and the Meunim who were found there; and they destroyed them utterly to this day, and lived in their place, because there was pasture there for their flocks."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Some of them, even of the sons of Simeon, five hundred men, went to Mount Seir, having for their captains Pelatiah, Neariah, Rephaiah, and Uzziel, the sons of Ishi."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"They struck the remnant of the Amalekites who escaped, and have lived there to this day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel (for he was the firstborn, but because he defiled his father\u2019s couch, his birthright was given to the sons of Joseph the son of Israel; and the genealogy is not to be listed according to the birthright."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For Judah prevailed above his brothers, and from him came the prince; but the birthright was Joseph\u2019s)\u2014"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"the sons of Reuben the firstborn of Israel: Hanoch, Pallu, Hezron, and Carmi."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The sons of Joel: Shemaiah his son, Gog his son, Shimei his son,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Micah his son, Reaiah his son, Baal his son,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and Beerah his son, whom Tilgath Pilneser king of Assyria carried away captive. He was prince of the Reubenites."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"His brothers by their families, when the genealogy of their generations was listed: the chief, Jeiel, and Zechariah,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and Bela the son of Azaz, the son of Shema, the son of Joel, who lived in Aroer, even to Nebo and Baal Meon;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and he lived eastward even to the entrance of the wilderness from the river Euphrates, because their livestock were multiplied in the land of Gilead."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"In the days of Saul, they made war with the Hagrites, who fell by their hand; and they lived in their tents throughout all the land east of Gilead."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Gad lived beside them in the land of Bashan to Salecah:"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Joel the chief, Shapham the second, Janai, and Shaphat in Bashan."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Their brothers of their fathers\u2019 houses: Michael, Meshullam, Sheba, Jorai, Jacan, Zia, and Eber, seven."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"These were the sons of Abihail, the son of Huri, the son of Jaroah, the son of Gilead, the son of Michael, the son of Jeshishai, the son of Jahdo, the son of Buz;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Ahi the son of Abdiel, the son of Guni, chief of their fathers\u2019 houses."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They lived in Gilead in Bashan and in its towns, and in all the pasture lands of Sharon as far as their borders."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All these were listed by genealogies in the days of Jotham king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam king of Israel."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Reuben, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh, of valiant men, men able to bear buckler and sword, able to shoot with bow, and skillful in war, were forty-four thousand seven hundred sixty that were able to go out to war."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They made war with the Hagrites, with Jetur, and Naphish, and Nodab."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They were helped against them, and the Hagrites were delivered into their hand, and all who were with them; for they cried to God in the battle, and he answered them because they put their trust in him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They took away their livestock: of their camels fifty thousand, and of sheep two hundred fifty thousand, and of donkeys two thousand, and of men one hundred thousand."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For many fell slain, because the war was of God. They lived in their place until the captivity."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of the half-tribe of Manasseh lived in the land. They increased from Bashan to Baal Hermon, Senir, and Mount Hermon."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"These were the heads of their fathers\u2019 houses: Epher, Ishi, Eliel, Azriel, Jeremiah, Hodaviah, and Jahdiel\u2014mighty men of valor, famous men, heads of their fathers\u2019 houses."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They trespassed against the God of their fathers, and played the prostitute after the gods of the peoples of the land whom God destroyed before them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"So the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Pul king of Assyria, and the spirit of Tilgath Pilneser king of Assyria, and he carried away the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of Manasseh, and brought them to Halah, Habor, Hara, and to the river of Gozan, to this day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The children of Amram: Aaron, Moses, and Miriam. The sons of Aaron: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Eleazar became the father of Phinehas, Phinehas became the father of Abishua,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Abishua became the father of Bukki. Bukki became the father of Uzzi."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Uzzi became the father of Zerahiah. Zerahiah became the father of Meraioth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Meraioth became the father of Amariah. Amariah became the father of Ahitub."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Ahitub became the father of Zadok. Zadok became the father of Ahimaaz."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Ahimaaz became the father of Azariah. Azariah became the father of Johanan."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Johanan became the father of Azariah, who executed the priest\u2019s office in the house that Solomon built in Jerusalem."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Azariah became the father of Amariah. Amariah became the father of Ahitub."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Ahitub became the father of Zadok. Zadok became the father of Shallum."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Shallum became the father of Hilkiah. Hilkiah became the father of Azariah."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Azariah became the father of Seraiah. Seraiah became the father of Jehozadak."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Jehozadak went into captivity when the LORD carried Judah and Jerusalem away by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Levi: Gershom, Kohath, and Merari."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"These are the names of the sons of Gershom: Libni and Shimei."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The sons of Kohath were Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. These are the families of the Levites according to their fathers\u2019 households."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Of Gershom: Libni his son, Jahath his son, Zimmah his son,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Joah his son, Iddo his son, Zerah his son, and Jeatherai his son."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The sons of Kohath: Amminadab his son, Korah his son, Assir his son,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Elkanah his son, Ebiasaph his son, Assir his son,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Tahath his son, Uriel his son, Uzziah his son, and Shaul his son."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The sons of Elkanah: Amasai and Ahimoth."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"As for Elkanah, the sons of Elkanah: Zophai his son, Nahath his son,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Eliab his son, Jeroham his son, and Elkanah his son."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The sons of Samuel: the firstborn, Joel, and the second, Abijah."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The sons of Merari: Mahli, Libni his son, Shimei his son, Uzzah his son,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Shimea his son, Haggiah his son, Asaiah his son."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"These are they whom David set over the service of song in the LORD\u2019s house after the ark came to rest there."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They ministered with song before the tabernacle of the Tent of Meeting until Solomon had built the LORD\u2019s house in Jerusalem. They performed the duties of their office according to their order."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"These are those who served, and their sons. Of the sons of the Kohathites: Heman the singer, the son of Joel, the son of Samuel,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"the son of Elkanah, the son of Jeroham, the son of Eliel, the son of Toah,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"the son of Zuph, the son of Elkanah, the son of Mahath, the son of Amasai,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"the son of Elkanah, the son of Joel, the son of Azariah, the son of Zephaniah,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"the son of Tahath, the son of Assir, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"the son of Izhar, the son of Kohath, the son of Levi, the son of Israel."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"His brother Asaph, who stood on his right hand, even Asaph the son of Berechiah, the son of Shimea,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"the son of Michael, the son of Baaseiah, the son of Malchijah,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"the son of Ethni, the son of Zerah, the son of Adaiah,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"the son of Ethan, the son of Zimmah, the son of Shimei,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"the son of Jahath, the son of Gershom, the son of Levi."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"On the left hand their brothers the sons of Merari: Ethan the son of Kishi, the son of Abdi, the son of Malluch,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"the son of Hashabiah, the son of Amaziah, the son of Hilkiah,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"the son of Amzi, the son of Bani, the son of Shemer,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"the son of Mahli, the son of Mushi, the son of Merari, the son of Levi."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Their brothers the Levites were appointed for all the service of the tabernacle of God\u2019s house."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"But Aaron and his sons offered on the altar of burnt offering, and on the altar of incense, for all the work of the most holy place, and to make atonement for Israel, according to all that Moses the servant of God had commanded."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Aaron: Eleazar his son, Phinehas his son, Abishua his son,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Bukki his son, Uzzi his son, Zerahiah his son,"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"Meraioth his son, Amariah his son, Ahitub his son,"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"Zadok his son, and Ahimaaz his son."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"Now these are their dwelling places according to their encampments in their borders: to the sons of Aaron, of the families of the Kohathites (for theirs was the first lot),"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"to them they gave Hebron in the land of Judah, and its pasture lands around it;"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"but the fields of the city and its villages, they gave to Caleb the son of Jephunneh."]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"To the sons of Aaron they gave the cities of refuge, Hebron, Libnah also with its pasture lands, Jattir, Eshtemoa with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"Hilen with its pasture lands, Debir with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"Ashan with its pasture lands, and Beth Shemesh with its pasture lands;"]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"and out of the tribe of Benjamin, Geba with its pasture lands, Allemeth with its pasture lands, and Anathoth with its pasture lands. All their cities throughout their families were thirteen cities."]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"To the rest of the sons of Kohath were given by lot, out of the family of the tribe, out of the half-tribe, the half of Manasseh, ten cities."]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"To the sons of Gershom, according to their families, out of the tribe of Issachar, and out of the tribe of Asher, and out of the tribe of Naphtali, and out of the tribe of Manasseh in Bashan, thirteen cities."]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"To the sons of Merari were given by lot, according to their families, out of the tribe of Reuben, and out of the tribe of Gad, and out of the tribe of Zebulun, twelve cities."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"The children of Israel gave to the Levites the cities with their pasture lands."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"They gave by lot out of the tribe of the children of Judah, and out of the tribe of the children of Simeon, and out of the tribe of the children of Benjamin, these cities which are mentioned by name."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of the families of the sons of Kohath had cities of their borders out of the tribe of Ephraim."]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"They gave to them the cities of refuge, Shechem in the hill country of Ephraim with its pasture lands and Gezer with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:68,l:[[0,"Jokmeam with its pasture lands, Beth Horon with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:69,l:[[0,"Aijalon with its pasture lands, Gath Rimmon with its pasture lands;"]]},{v:70,l:[[0,"and out of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Aner with its pasture lands, and Bileam with its pasture lands, for the rest of the family of the sons of Kohath."]]},{v:71,p:1,l:[[0,"To the sons of Gershom were given, out of the family of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Golan in Bashan with its pasture lands, and Ashtaroth with its pasture lands;"]]},{v:72,l:[[0,"and out of the tribe of Issachar, Kedesh with its pasture lands, Daberath with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:73,l:[[0,"Ramoth with its pasture lands, and Anem with its pasture lands;"]]},{v:74,l:[[0,"and out of the tribe of Asher, Mashal with its pasture lands, Abdon with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:75,l:[[0,"Hukok with its pasture lands, and Rehob with its pasture lands;"]]},{v:76,l:[[0,"and out of the tribe of Naphtali, Kedesh in Galilee with its pasture lands, Hammon with its pasture lands, and Kiriathaim with its pasture lands."]]},{v:77,p:1,l:[[0,"To the rest of the Levites, the sons of Merari, were given, out of the tribe of Zebulun, Rimmono with its pasture lands, and Tabor with its pasture lands;"]]},{v:78,l:[[0,"and beyond the Jordan at Jericho, on the east side of the Jordan, were given them out of the tribe of Reuben: Bezer in the wilderness with its pasture lands, Jahzah with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:79,l:[[0,"Kedemoth with its pasture lands, and Mephaath with its pasture lands;"]]},{v:80,l:[[0,"and out of the tribe of Gad, Ramoth in Gilead with its pasture lands, Mahanaim with its pasture lands,"]]},{v:81,l:[[0,"Heshbon with its pasture lands, and Jazer with its pasture lands."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the sons of Issachar: Tola, Puah, Jashub, and Shimron, four."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The sons of Tola: Uzzi, Rephaiah, Jeriel, Jahmai, Ibsam, and Shemuel, heads of their fathers\u2019 houses, of Tola; mighty men of valor in their generations. Their number in the days of David was twenty-two thousand six hundred."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The son of Uzzi: Izrahiah. The sons of Izrahiah: Michael, Obadiah, Joel, and Isshiah, five; all of them chief men."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"With them, by their generations, after their fathers\u2019 houses, were bands of the army for war, thirty-six thousand; for they had many wives and sons."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Their brothers among all the families of Issachar, mighty men of valor, listed in all by genealogy, were eighty-seven thousand."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Benjamin: Bela, Becher, and Jediael, three."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The sons of Bela: Ezbon, Uzzi, Uzziel, Jerimoth, and Iri, five; heads of fathers\u2019 houses, mighty men of valor; and they were listed by genealogy twenty-two thousand thirty-four."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The sons of Becher: Zemirah, Joash, Eliezer, Elioenai, Omri, Jeremoth, Abijah, Anathoth, and Alemeth. All these were the sons of Becher."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They were listed by genealogy, after their generations, heads of their fathers\u2019 houses, mighty men of valor, twenty thousand two hundred."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The son of Jediael: Bilhan. The sons of Bilhan: Jeush, Benjamin, Ehud, Chenaanah, Zethan, Tarshish, and Ahishahar."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"All these were sons of Jediael, according to the heads of their fathers\u2019 households, mighty men of valor, seventeen thousand two hundred, who were able to go out in the army for war."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So were Shuppim, Huppim, the sons of Ir, Hushim, and the sons of Aher."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Naphtali: Jahziel, Guni, Jezer, Shallum, and the sons of Bilhah."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Manasseh: Asriel, whom his concubine the Aramitess bore. She bore Machir the father of Gilead."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Machir took a wife of Huppim and Shuppim, whose sister\u2019s name was Maacah. The name of the second was Zelophehad; and Zelophehad had daughters."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Maacah the wife of Machir bore a son, and she named him Peresh. The name of his brother was Sheresh; and his sons were Ulam and Rakem."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The sons of Ulam: Bedan. These were the sons of Gilead the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"His sister Hammolecheth bore Ishhod, Abiezer, and Mahlah."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of Shemida were Ahian, Shechem, Likhi, and Aniam."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Ephraim: Shuthelah, Bered his son, Tahath his son, Eleadah his son, Tahath his son,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Zabad his son, Shuthelah his son, Ezer, and Elead, whom the men of Gath who were born in the land killed, because they came down to take away their livestock."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Ephraim their father mourned many days, and his brothers came to comfort him."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He went in to his wife, and she conceived and bore a son, and he named him Beriah, because there was trouble with his house."]],f:["\u201cBeriah\u201d is similar to the Hebrew word for \u201cmisfortune\u201d."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"His daughter was Sheerah, who built Beth Horon the lower and the upper, and Uzzen Sheerah."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Rephah was his son, Resheph his son, Telah his son, Tahan his son,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Ladan his son, Ammihud his son, Elishama his son,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Nun his son, and Joshua his son."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Their possessions and settlements were Bethel and its towns, and eastward Naaran, and westward Gezer with its towns; Shechem also and its towns, to Azzah and its towns;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"and by the borders of the children of Manasseh, Beth Shean and its towns, Taanach and its towns, Megiddo and its towns, and Dor and its towns. The children of Joseph the son of Israel lived in these."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Asher: Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi, and Beriah. Serah was their sister."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The sons of Beriah: Heber and Malchiel, who was the father of Birzaith."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Heber became the father of Japhlet, Shomer, Hotham, and Shua their sister."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The sons of Japhlet: Pasach, Bimhal, and Ashvath. These are the children of Japhlet."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The sons of Shemer: Ahi, Rohgah, Jehubbah, and Aram."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The sons of Helem his brother: Zophah, Imna, Shelesh, and Amal."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The sons of Zophah: Suah, Harnepher, Shual, Beri, Imrah,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Bezer, Hod, Shamma, Shilshah, Ithran, and Beera."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The sons of Jether: Jephunneh, Pispa, and Ara."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The sons of Ulla: Arah, Hanniel, and Rizia."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"All these were the children of Asher, heads of the fathers\u2019 houses, choice and mighty men of valor, chief of the princes. The number of them listed by genealogy for service in war was twenty-six thousand men."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Benjamin became the father of Bela his firstborn, Ashbel the second, Aharah the third,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Nohah the fourth, and Rapha the fifth."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Bela had sons: Addar, Gera, Abihud,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Abishua, Naaman, Ahoah,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Gera, Shephuphan, and Huram."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Ehud. These are the heads of fathers\u2019 households of the inhabitants of Geba, who were carried captive to Manahath:"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Naaman, Ahijah, and Gera, who carried them captive; and he became the father of Uzza and Ahihud."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Shaharaim became the father of children in the field of Moab, after he had sent them away. Hushim and Baara were his wives."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"By Hodesh his wife, he became the father of Jobab, Zibia, Mesha, Malcam,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Jeuz, Shachia, and Mirmah. These were his sons, heads of fathers\u2019 households."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"By Hushim, he became the father of Abitub and Elpaal."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The sons of Elpaal: Eber, Misham, and Shemed, who built Ono and Lod, with its towns;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and Beriah and Shema, who were heads of fathers\u2019 households of the inhabitants of Aijalon, who put to flight the inhabitants of Gath;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and Ahio, Shashak, Jeremoth,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Zebadiah, Arad, Eder,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Michael, Ishpah, Joha, the sons of Beriah,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Zebadiah, Meshullam, Hizki, Heber,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Ishmerai, Izliah, Jobab, the sons of Elpaal,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Jakim, Zichri, Zabdi,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Adaiah, Beraiah, Shimrath, the sons of Shimei,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Ishpan, Eber, Eliel,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Abdon, Zichri, Hanan,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Hananiah, Elam, Anthothijah,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Iphdeiah, Penuel, the sons of Shashak,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Shamsherai, Shehariah, Athaliah,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Jaareshiah, Elijah, Zichri, and the sons of Jeroham."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"These were heads of fathers\u2019 households throughout their generations, chief men. These lived in Jerusalem."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The father of Gibeon, whose wife\u2019s name was Maacah, lived in Gibeon"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"with his firstborn son Abdon, Zur, Kish, Baal, Nadab,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Gedor, Ahio, Zecher,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and Mikloth, who became the father of Shimeah. They also lived with their families in Jerusalem, near their relatives."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Ner became the father of Kish. Kish became the father of Saul. Saul became the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Eshbaal."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The son of Jonathan was Merib-baal. Merib-baal became the father of Micah."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tarea, and Ahaz."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Ahaz became the father of Jehoaddah. Jehoaddah became the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri. Zimri became the father of Moza."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Moza became the father of Binea. Raphah was his son, Eleasah his son, and Azel his son."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Azel had six sons, whose names are these: Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. All these were the sons of Azel."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The sons of Eshek his brother: Ulam his firstborn, Jeush the second, and Eliphelet the third."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The sons of Ulam were mighty men of valor, archers, and had many sons, and grandsons, one hundred fifty. All these were of the sons of Benjamin."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"So all Israel were listed by genealogies; and behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel. Judah was carried away captive to Babylon for their disobedience."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now the first inhabitants who lived in their possessions in their cities were Israel, the priests, the Levites, and the temple servants."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In Jerusalem, there lived of the children of Judah, of the children of Benjamin, and of the children of Ephraim and Manasseh:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Uthai the son of Ammihud, the son of Omri, the son of Imri, the son of Bani, of the children of Perez the son of Judah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Of the Shilonites: Asaiah the firstborn and his sons."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Of the sons of Zerah: Jeuel and their brothers, six hundred ninety."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Of the sons of Benjamin: Sallu the son of Meshullam, the son of Hodaviah, the son of Hassenuah;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and Ibneiah the son of Jeroham, and Elah the son of Uzzi, the son of Michri; and Meshullam the son of Shephatiah, the son of Reuel, the son of Ibnijah;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and their brothers, according to their generations, nine hundred fifty-six. All these men were heads of fathers\u2019 households by their fathers\u2019 houses."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the priests: Jedaiah, Jehoiarib, Jachin,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and Azariah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the ruler of God\u2019s house;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah; and Maasai the son of Adiel, the son of Jahzerah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Meshillemith, the son of Immer;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and their brothers, heads of their fathers\u2019 houses, one thousand seven hundred sixty; they were very able men for the work of the service of God\u2019s house."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the Levites: Shemaiah the son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, of the sons of Merari;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and Bakbakkar, Heresh, Galal, and Mattaniah the son of Mica, the son of Zichri, the son of Asaph,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and Obadiah the son of Shemaiah, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun; and Berechiah the son of Asa, the son of Elkanah, who lived in the villages of the Netophathites."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The gatekeepers: Shallum, Akkub, Talmon, Ahiman, and their brothers (Shallum was the chief),"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"who previously served in the king\u2019s gate eastward. They were the gatekeepers for the camp of the children of Levi."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Shallum was the son of Kore, the son of Ebiasaph, the son of Korah, and his brothers, of his father\u2019s house, the Korahites, were over the work of the service, keepers of the thresholds of the tent. Their fathers had been over the LORD\u2019s camp, keepers of the entry."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Phinehas the son of Eleazar was ruler over them in time past, and the LORD was with him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Zechariah the son of Meshelemiah was gatekeeper of the door of the Tent of Meeting."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"All these who were chosen to be gatekeepers in the thresholds were two hundred twelve. These were listed by genealogy in their villages, whom David and Samuel the seer ordained in their office of trust."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So they and their children had the oversight of the gates of the LORD\u2019s house, even the house of the tent, as guards."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"On the four sides were the gatekeepers, toward the east, west, north, and south."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Their brothers, in their villages, were to come in every seven days from time to time to be with them,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"for the four chief gatekeepers, who were Levites, were in an office of trust, and were over the rooms and over the treasuries in God\u2019s house."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They stayed around God\u2019s house, because that was their duty; and it was their duty to open it morning by morning."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Certain of them were in charge of the vessels of service, for these were brought in by count, and these were taken out by count."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Some of them also were appointed over the furniture, and over all the vessels of the sanctuary, over the fine flour, the wine, the oil, the frankincense, and the spices."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of the sons of the priests prepared the mixing of the spices."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Mattithiah, one of the Levites, who was the firstborn of Shallum the Korahite, had the office of trust over the things that were baked in pans."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Some of their brothers, of the sons of the Kohathites, were over the show bread, to prepare it every Sabbath."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the singers, heads of fathers\u2019 households of the Levites, who lived in the rooms and were free from other service, for they were employed in their work day and night."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"These were heads of fathers\u2019 households of the Levites, throughout their generations, chief men. They lived at Jerusalem."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Jeiel the father of Gibeon, whose wife\u2019s name was Maacah, lived in Gibeon."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"His firstborn son was Abdon, then Zur, Kish, Baal, Ner, Nadab,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Gedor, Ahio, Zechariah, and Mikloth."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Mikloth became the father of Shimeam. They also lived with their relatives in Jerusalem, near their relatives."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Ner became the father of Kish. Kish became the father of Saul. Saul became the father of Jonathan, Malchishua, Abinadab, and Eshbaal."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The son of Jonathan was Merib-baal. Merib-baal became the father of Micah."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The sons of Micah: Pithon, Melech, Tahrea, and Ahaz."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Ahaz became the father of Jarah. Jarah became the father of Alemeth, Azmaveth, and Zimri. Zimri became the father of Moza."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Moza became the father of Binea, Rephaiah his son, Eleasah his son, and Azel his son."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Azel had six sons, whose names are Azrikam, Bocheru, Ishmael, Sheariah, Obadiah, and Hanan. These were the sons of Azel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the Philistines fought against Israel; and the men of Israel fled from before the Philistines, and fell down slain on Mount Gilboa."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Philistines followed hard after Saul and after his sons; and the Philistines killed Jonathan, Abinadab, and Malchishua, the sons of Saul."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The battle went hard against Saul, and the archers overtook him; and he was distressed by reason of the archers."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then Saul said to his armor bearer, \u201cDraw your sword, and thrust me through with it, lest these uncircumcised come and abuse me.\u201d"],[0,"But his armor bearer would not, for he was terrified. Therefore Saul took his sword and fell on it."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When his armor bearer saw that Saul was dead, he likewise fell on his sword and died."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Saul died with his three sons; and all his house died together."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When all the men of Israel who were in the valley saw that they fled, and that Saul and his sons were dead, they abandoned their cities, and fled; and the Philistines came and lived in them."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, when the Philistines came to strip the slain, they found Saul and his sons fallen on Mount Gilboa."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They stripped him and took his head and his armor, then sent into the land of the Philistines all around to carry the news to their idols and to the people."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They put his armor in the house of their gods, and fastened his head in the house of Dagon."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When all Jabesh Gilead heard all that the Philistines had done to Saul,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"all the valiant men arose and took away the body of Saul and the bodies of his sons, and brought them to Jabesh, and buried their bones under the oak in Jabesh, and fasted seven days."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"So Saul died for his trespass which he committed against the LORD, because of the LORD\u2019s word, which he didn\u2019t keep, and also because he asked counsel of one who had a familiar spirit, to inquire,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and didn\u2019t inquire of the LORD. Therefore he killed him, and turned the kingdom over to David the son of Jesse."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all Israel gathered themselves to David to Hebron, saying, \u201cBehold, we are your bone and your flesh."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In times past, even when Saul was king, it was you who led out and brought in Israel. The LORD your God said to you, \u2018You shall be shepherd of my people Israel, and you shall be prince over my people Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"So all the elders of Israel came to the king to Hebron; and David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the LORD. They anointed David king over Israel, according to the LORD\u2019s word by Samuel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"David and all Israel went to Jerusalem (also called Jebus); and the Jebusites, the inhabitants of the land, were there."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The inhabitants of Jebus said to David, \u201cYou will not come in here!\u201d Nevertheless David took the stronghold of Zion. The same is David\u2019s city."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"David had said, \u201cWhoever strikes the Jebusites first shall be chief and captain.\u201d Joab the son of Zeruiah went up first, and was made chief."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"David lived in the stronghold; therefore they called it David\u2019s city."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He built the city all around, from Millo even around; and Joab repaired the rest of the city."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"David grew greater and greater, for the LORD of Armies was with him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the chief of the mighty men whom David had, who showed themselves strong with him in his kingdom, together with all Israel, to make him king, according to the LORD\u2019s word concerning Israel."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the number of the mighty men whom David had: Jashobeam, the son of a Hachmonite, the chief of the thirty; he lifted up his spear against three hundred and killed them at one time."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"After him was Eleazar the son of Dodo, the Ahohite, who was one of the three mighty men."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He was with David at Pasdammim, and there the Philistines were gathered together to battle, where there was a plot of ground full of barley; and the people fled from before the Philistines."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They stood in the middle of the plot, defended it, and killed the Philistines; and the LORD saved them by a great victory."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Three of the thirty chief men went down to the rock to David, into the cave of Adullam; and the army of the Philistines were encamped in the valley of Rephaim."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"David was then in the stronghold, and the garrison of the Philistines was in Bethlehem at that time."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"David longed, and said, \u201cOh, that someone would give me water to drink from the well of Bethlehem, which is by the gate!\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The three broke through the army of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Bethlehem that was by the gate, took it, and brought it to David; but David would not drink any of it, but poured it out to the LORD,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cMy God forbid me, that I should do this! Shall I drink the blood of these men who have put their lives in jeopardy?\u201d For they risked their lives to bring it. Therefore he would not drink it. The three mighty men did these things."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Abishai, the brother of Joab, was chief of the three; for he lifted up his spear against three hundred and killed them, and had a name among the three."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Of the three, he was more honorable than the two, and was made their captain; however he wasn\u2019t included in the three."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had done mighty deeds, killed the two sons of Ariel of Moab. He also went down and killed a lion in the middle of a pit on a snowy day."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He killed an Egyptian, a man of great stature, five cubits high. In the Egyptian\u2019s hand was a spear like a weaver\u2019s beam; and he went down to him with a staff, plucked the spear out of the Egyptian\u2019s hand, and killed him with his own spear."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters. Therefore this Egyptian was about 7 feet and 6 inches or 2.28 meters tall."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Benaiah the son of Jehoiada did these things and had a name among the three mighty men."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Behold, he was more honorable than the thirty, but he didn\u2019t attain to the three; and David set him over his guard."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The mighty men of the armies also include Asahel the brother of Joab, Elhanan the son of Dodo of Bethlehem,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Shammoth the Harorite, Helez the Pelonite,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite, Abiezer the Anathothite,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Sibbecai the Hushathite, Ilai the Ahohite,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Maharai the Netophathite, Heled the son of Baanah the Netophathite,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Ithai the son of Ribai of Gibeah of the children of Benjamin, Benaiah the Pirathonite,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Hurai of the brooks of Gaash, Abiel the Arbathite,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Azmaveth the Baharumite, Eliahba the Shaalbonite,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"the sons of Hashem the Gizonite, Jonathan the son of Shagee the Hararite,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Ahiam the son of Sacar the Hararite, Eliphal the son of Ur,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Hepher the Mecherathite, Ahijah the Pelonite,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Hezro the Carmelite, Naarai the son of Ezbai,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Joel the brother of Nathan, Mibhar the son of Hagri,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Zelek the Ammonite, Naharai the Berothite (the armor bearer of Joab the son of Zeruiah),"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Ira the Ithrite, Gareb the Ithrite,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Uriah the Hittite, Zabad the son of Ahlai,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Adina the son of Shiza the Reubenite (a chief of the Reubenites), and thirty with him,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Hanan the son of Maacah, Joshaphat the Mithnite,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Uzzia the Ashterathite, Shama and Jeiel the sons of Hotham the Aroerite,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Jediael the son of Shimri, and Joha his brother, the Tizite,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Eliel the Mahavite, and Jeribai, and Joshaviah, the sons of Elnaam, and Ithmah the Moabite,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Eliel, Obed, and Jaasiel the Mezobaite."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are those who came to David to Ziklag while he was a fugitive from Saul the son of Kish. They were among the mighty men, his helpers in war."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They were armed with bows, and could use both the right hand and the left in slinging stones and in shooting arrows from the bow. They were of Saul\u2019s relatives of the tribe of Benjamin."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The chief was Ahiezer, then Joash, the sons of Shemaah the Gibeathite; Jeziel and Pelet, the sons of Azmaveth; Beracah; Jehu the Anathothite;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Ishmaiah the Gibeonite, a mighty man among the thirty and a leader of the thirty; Jeremiah; Jahaziel; Johanan; Jozabad the Gederathite;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Eluzai; Jerimoth; Bealiah; Shemariah; Shephatiah the Haruphite;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Elkanah, Isshiah, Azarel, Joezer, and Jashobeam, the Korahites;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and Joelah and Zebadiah, the sons of Jeroham of Gedor."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Some Gadites joined David in the stronghold in the wilderness, mighty men of valor, men trained for war, who could handle shield and spear; whose faces were like the faces of lions, and they were as swift as the gazelles on the mountains:"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Ezer the chief, Obadiah the second, Eliab the third,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Mishmannah the fourth, Jeremiah the fifth,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Attai the sixth, Eliel the seventh,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Johanan the eighth, Elzabad the ninth,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Jeremiah the tenth, and Machbannai the eleventh."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"These of the sons of Gad were captains of the army. He who was least was equal to one hundred, and the greatest to one thousand."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"These are those who went over the Jordan in the first month, when it had overflowed all its banks; and they put to flight all who lived in the valleys, both toward the east and toward the west."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of the children of Benjamin and Judah came to the stronghold to David."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"David went out to meet them, and answered them, \u201cIf you have come peaceably to me to help me, my heart will be united with you; but if you have come to betray me to my adversaries, since there is no wrong in my hands, may the God of our fathers see this and rebuke it.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then the Spirit came on Amasai, who was chief of the thirty, and he said, \u201cWe are yours, David, and on your side, you son of Jesse. Peace, peace be to you, and peace be to your helpers; for your God helps you.\u201d Then David received them and made them captains of the band."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of Manasseh also joined David when he came with the Philistines against Saul to battle, but they didn\u2019t help them, for the lords of the Philistines sent him away after consultation, saying, \u201cHe will desert to his master Saul to the jeopardy of our heads.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"As he went to Ziklag, some from Manasseh joined him: Adnah, Jozabad, Jediael, Michael, Jozabad, Elihu, and Zillethai, captains of thousands who were of Manasseh."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They helped David against the band of raiders, for they were all mighty men of valor and were captains in the army."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For from day to day men came to David to help him, until there was a great army, like God\u2019s army."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the numbers of the heads of those who were armed for war, who came to David to Hebron to turn the kingdom of Saul to him, according to the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The children of Judah who bore shield and spear were six thousand eight hundred, armed for war."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Of the children of Simeon, mighty men of valor for the war: seven thousand one hundred."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Of the children of Levi: four thousand six hundred."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Jehoiada was the leader of the household of Aaron; and with him were three thousand seven hundred,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and Zadok, a young man mighty of valor, and of his father\u2019s house twenty-two captains."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Of the children of Benjamin, Saul\u2019s relatives: three thousand, for until then, the greatest part of them had kept their allegiance to Saul\u2019s house."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Of the children of Ephraim: twenty thousand eight hundred, mighty men of valor, famous men in their fathers\u2019 houses."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Of the half-tribe of Manasseh: eighteen thousand, who were mentioned by name, to come and make David king."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Of the children of Issachar, men who had understanding of the times, to know what Israel ought to do, their heads were two hundred; and all their brothers were at their command."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Of Zebulun, such as were able to go out in the army, who could set the battle in array with all kinds of instruments of war: fifty thousand who could command and were not of double heart."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Of Naphtali: one thousand captains, and with them with shield and spear thirty-seven thousand."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Of the Danites who could set the battle in array: twenty-eight thousand six hundred."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Of Asher, such as were able to go out in the army, who could set the battle in array: forty thousand."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"On the other side of the Jordan, of the Reubenites, the Gadites, and of the half-tribe of Manasseh, with all kinds of instruments of war for the battle: one hundred twenty thousand."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"All these were men of war who could order the battle array, and came with a perfect heart to Hebron to make David king over all Israel; and all the rest also of Israel were of one heart to make David king."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"They were there with David three days, eating and drinking; for their brothers had supplied provisions for them."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Moreover those who were near to them, as far as Issachar, Zebulun, and Naphtali, brought bread on donkeys, on camels, on mules, and on oxen: supplies of flour, cakes of figs, clusters of raisins, wine, oil, cattle, and sheep in abundance; for there was joy in Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David consulted with the captains of thousands and of hundreds, even with every leader."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David said to all the assembly of Israel, \u201cIf it seems good to you, and if it is of the LORD our God, let\u2019s send word everywhere to our brothers who are left in all the land of Israel, with whom the priests and Levites are in their cities that have pasture lands, that they may gather themselves to us."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Also, let\u2019s bring the ark of our God back to us again, for we didn\u2019t seek it in the days of Saul.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"All the assembly said that they would do so, for the thing was right in the eyes of all the people."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So David assembled all Israel together, from the Shihor River of Egypt even to the entrance of Hamath, to bring God\u2019s ark from Kiriath Jearim."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"David went up with all Israel to Baalah, that is, to Kiriath Jearim, which belonged to Judah, to bring up from there God the LORD\u2019s ark that sits above the cherubim, that is called by the Name."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They carried God\u2019s ark on a new cart, and brought it out of Abinadab\u2019s house; and Uzza and Ahio drove the cart."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"David and all Israel played before God with all their might, even with songs, with harps, with stringed instruments, with tambourines, with cymbals, and with trumpets."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When they came to Chidon\u2019s threshing floor, Uzza put out his hand to hold the ark, for the oxen stumbled."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s anger burned against Uzza, and he struck him because he put his hand on the ark; and he died there before God."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"David was displeased, because the LORD had broken out against Uzza. He called that place Perez Uzza, to this day."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"David was afraid of God that day, saying, \u201cHow can I bring God\u2019s ark home to me?\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So David didn\u2019t move the ark with him into David\u2019s city, but carried it aside into Obed-Edom the Gittite\u2019s house."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"God\u2019s ark remained with the family of Obed-Edom in his house three months; and the LORD blessed Obed-Edom\u2019s house and all that he had."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David with cedar trees, masons, and carpenters, to build him a house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David perceived that the LORD had established him king over Israel, for his kingdom was highly exalted, for his people Israel\u2019s sake."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David took more wives in Jerusalem, and David became the father of more sons and daughters."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"These are the names of the children whom he had in Jerusalem: Shammua, Shobab, Nathan, Solomon,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ibhar, Elishua, Elpelet,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Nogah, Nepheg, Japhia,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Elishama, Beeliada, and Eliphelet."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Philistines heard that David was anointed king over all Israel, all the Philistines went up to seek David; and David heard of it, and went out against them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now the Philistines had come and made a raid in the valley of Rephaim."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"David inquired of God, saying, \u201cShall I go up against the Philistines? Will you deliver them into my hand?\u201d"],[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cGo up; for I will deliver them into your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"So they came up to Baal Perazim, and David defeated them there. David said, God has broken my enemies by my hand, like waters breaking out. Therefore they called the name of that place Baal Perazim."]],f:["\u201cBaal Perazim\u201d means \u201cThe Lord who breaks out\u201d."]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They left their gods there; and David gave a command, and they were burned with fire."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The Philistines made another raid in the valley."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"David inquired again of God; and God said to him, \u201cYou shall not go up after them. Turn away from them, and come on them opposite the mulberry trees."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When you hear the sound of marching in the tops of the mulberry trees, then go out to battle; for God has gone out before you to strike the army of the Philistines.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"David did as God commanded him; and they attacked the army of the Philistines from Gibeon even to Gezer."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The fame of David went out into all lands; and the LORD brought the fear of him on all nations."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David made himself houses in David\u2019s city; and he prepared a place for God\u2019s ark, and pitched a tent for it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then David said, \u201cNo one ought to carry God\u2019s ark but the Levites. For the LORD has chosen them to carry God\u2019s ark, and to minister to him forever.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David assembled all Israel at Jerusalem, to bring up the LORD\u2019s ark to its place, which he had prepared for it."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"David gathered together the sons of Aaron and the Levites:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"of the sons of Kohath, Uriel the chief, and his brothers one hundred twenty;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"of the sons of Merari, Asaiah the chief, and his brothers two hundred twenty;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"of the sons of Gershom, Joel the chief, and his brothers one hundred thirty;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"of the sons of Elizaphan, Shemaiah the chief, and his brothers two hundred;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"of the sons of Hebron, Eliel the chief, and his brothers eighty;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"of the sons of Uzziel, Amminadab the chief, and his brothers one hundred twelve."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"David called for Zadok and Abiathar the priests, and for the Levites: for Uriel, Asaiah, Joel, Shemaiah, Eliel, and Amminadab,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cYou are the heads of the fathers\u2019 households of the Levites. Sanctify yourselves, both you and your brothers, that you may bring the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel, up to the place that I have prepared for it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For because you didn\u2019t carry it at first, the LORD our God broke out in anger against us, because we didn\u2019t seek him according to the ordinance.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So the priests and the Levites sanctified themselves to bring up the ark of the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The children of the Levites bore God\u2019s ark on their shoulders with its poles, as Moses commanded according to the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"David spoke to the chief of the Levites to appoint their brothers as singers with instruments of music, stringed instruments, harps, and cymbals, sounding aloud and lifting up their voices with joy."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So the Levites appointed Heman the son of Joel; and of his brothers, Asaph the son of Berechiah; and of the sons of Merari their brothers, Ethan the son of Kushaiah;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and with them their brothers of the second rank: Zechariah, Ben, Jaaziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, Obed-Edom, and Jeiel, the doorkeepers."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"So the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, were given cymbals of bronze to sound aloud;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and Zechariah, Aziel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Unni, Eliab, Maaseiah, and Benaiah, with stringed instruments set to Alamoth;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and Mattithiah, Eliphelehu, Mikneiah, Obed-Edom, Jeiel, and Azaziah, with harps tuned to the eight-stringed lyre, to lead."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Chenaniah, chief of the Levites, was over the singing. He taught the singers, because he was skillful."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Berechiah and Elkanah were doorkeepers for the ark."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Shebaniah, Joshaphat, Nethanel, Amasai, Zechariah, Benaiah, and Eliezer, the priests, blew the trumpets before God\u2019s ark; and Obed-Edom and Jehiah were doorkeepers for the ark."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"So David, the elders of Israel, and the captains over thousands went to bring the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant up out of the house of Obed-Edom with joy."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When God helped the Levites who bore the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, they sacrificed seven bulls and seven rams."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, as were all the Levites who bore the ark, the singers, and Chenaniah the choir master with the singers; and David had an ephod of linen on him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Thus all Israel brought the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant up with shouting, with sound of the cornet, with trumpets, and with cymbals, sounding aloud with stringed instruments and harps."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"As the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant came to David\u2019s city, Michal the daughter of Saul looked out at the window, and saw king David dancing and playing; and she despised him in her heart."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"They brought in God\u2019s ark, and set it in the middle of the tent that David had pitched for it; and they offered burnt offerings and peace offerings before God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When David had finished offering the burnt offering and the peace offerings, he blessed the people in the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He gave to everyone of Israel, both man and woman, to everyone a loaf of bread, a portion of meat, and a cake of raisins."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"He appointed some of the Levites to minister before the LORD\u2019s ark, and to commemorate, to thank, and to praise the LORD, the God of Israel:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Asaph the chief, and second to him Zechariah, then Jeiel, Shemiramoth, Jehiel, Mattithiah, Eliab, Benaiah, Obed-Edom, and Jeiel, with stringed instruments and with harps; and Asaph with cymbals, sounding aloud;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"with Benaiah and Jahaziel the priests with trumpets continually, before the ark of the covenant of God."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then on that day David first ordained giving of thanks to the LORD by the hand of Asaph and his brothers."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh give thanks to the LORD."],[2,"Call on his name."],[2,"Make what he has done known among the peoples."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to him."],[2,"Sing praises to him."],[2,"Tell of all his marvelous works."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Glory in his holy name."],[2,"Let the heart of those who seek the LORD rejoice."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Seek the LORD and his strength."],[2,"Seek his face forever more."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember his marvelous works that he has done,"],[2,"his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"you offspring of Israel his servant,"],[2,"you children of Jacob, his chosen ones."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He is the LORD our God."],[2,"His judgments are in all the earth."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember his covenant forever,"],[2,"the word which he commanded to a thousand generations,"]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"the covenant which he made with Abraham,"],[2,"his oath to Isaac."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He confirmed it to Jacob for a statute,"],[2,"and to Israel for an everlasting covenant,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"saying, \u201cI will give you the land of Canaan,"],[2,"The lot of your inheritance,\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[2,"when you were but a few men in number,"],[2,"yes, very few, and foreigners in it."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"They went about from nation to nation,"],[2,"from one kingdom to another people."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He allowed no man to do them wrong."],[2,"Yes, he reproved kings for their sakes,"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t touch my anointed ones!"],[2,"Do my prophets no harm!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to the LORD, all the earth!"],[2,"Display his salvation from day to day."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Declare his glory among the nations,"],[2,"and his marvelous works among all the peoples."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"For great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised."],[2,"He also is to be feared above all gods."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"For all the gods of the peoples are idols,"],[2,"but the LORD made the heavens."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Honor and majesty are before him."],[2,"Strength and gladness are in his place."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Ascribe to the LORD, you families of the peoples,"],[2,"ascribe to the LORD glory and strength!"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his name."],[2,"Bring an offering, and come before him."],[2,"Worship the LORD in holy array."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Tremble before him, all the earth."],[2,"The world also is established that it can\u2019t be moved."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the heavens be glad,"],[2,"and let the earth rejoice!"],[2,"Let them say among the nations, \u201cThe LORD reigns!\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the sea roar, and its fullness!"],[2,"Let the field exult, and all that is in it!"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the trees of the forest will sing for joy before the LORD,"],[2,"for he comes to judge the earth."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"Say, \u201cSave us, God of our salvation!"],[2,"Gather us together and deliver us from the nations,"],[2,"to give thanks to your holy name,"],[2,"to triumph in your praise.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel,"],[2,"from everlasting even to everlasting."],[0,"All the people said, \u201cAmen,\u201d and praised the LORD."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"So he left Asaph and his brothers there before the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, to minister before the ark continually, as every day\u2019s work required;"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"and Obed-Edom with their sixty-eight relatives; Obed-Edom also the son of Jeduthun and Hosah to be doorkeepers;"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and Zadok the priest and his brothers the priests, before the LORD\u2019s tabernacle in the high place that was at Gibeon,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"to offer burnt offerings to the LORD on the altar of burnt offering continually morning and evening, even according to all that is written in the LORD\u2019s law, which he commanded to Israel;"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"and with them Heman and Jeduthun and the rest who were chosen, who were mentioned by name, to give thanks to the LORD, because his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"and with them Heman and Jeduthun with trumpets and cymbals for those that should sound aloud, and with instruments for the songs of God, and the sons of Jeduthun to be at the gate."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"All the people departed, each man to his house; and David returned to bless his house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When David was living in his house, David said to Nathan the prophet, \u201cBehold, I live in a cedar house, but the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant is in a tent.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Nathan said to David, \u201cDo all that is in your heart; for God is with you.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"That same night, the word of God came to Nathan, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cGo and tell David my servant, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cYou shall not build me a house to dwell in;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"for I have not lived in a house since the day that I brought up Israel to this day, but have gone from tent to tent, and from one tent to another."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In all places in which I have walked with all Israel, did I speak a word with any of the judges of Israel, whom I commanded to be shepherd of my people, saying, \u2018Why have you not built me a house of cedar?\u2019\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore, you shall tell my servant David, \u2018The LORD of Armies says, \u201cI took you from the sheep pen, from following the sheep, to be prince over my people Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I have been with you wherever you have gone, and have cut off all your enemies from before you. I will make you a name like the name of the great ones who are on the earth."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I will appoint a place for my people Israel, and will plant them, that they may dwell in their own place, and be moved no more. The children of wickedness will not waste them any more, as at the first,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and from the day that I commanded judges to be over my people Israel. I will subdue all your enemies. Moreover I tell you that the LORD will build you a house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"It will happen, when your days are fulfilled that you must go to be with your fathers, that I will set up your offspring after you, who will be of your sons; and I will establish his kingdom."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He will build me a house, and I will establish his throne forever."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will be his father, and he will be my son. I will not take my loving kindness away from him, as I took it from him who was before you;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but I will settle him in my house and in my kingdom forever. His throne will be established forever.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so Nathan spoke to David."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David the king went in and sat before the LORD; and he said, \u201cWho am I, LORD God, and what is my house, that you have brought me this far?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"This was a small thing in your eyes, O God, but you have spoken of your servant\u2019s house for a great while to come, and have respected me according to the standard of a man of high degree, LORD God."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"What can David say yet more to you concerning the honor which is done to your servant? For you know your servant."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"LORD, for your servant\u2019s sake, and according to your own heart, you have done all this greatness, to make known all these great things."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"LORD, there is no one like you, neither is there any God besides you, according to all that we have heard with our ears."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"What one nation on the earth is like your people Israel, whom God went to redeem to himself for a people, to make you a name by great and awesome things, in driving out nations from before your people whom you redeemed out of Egypt?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For you made your people Israel your own people forever; and you, LORD, became their God."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now, LORD, let the word that you have spoken concerning your servant, and concerning his house, be established forever, and do as you have spoken."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Let your name be established and magnified forever, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies is the God of Israel, even a God to Israel. The house of David your servant is established before you.\u2019"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For you, my God, have revealed to your servant that you will build him a house. Therefore your servant has found courage to pray before you."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Now, LORD, you are God, and have promised this good thing to your servant."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Now it has pleased you to bless the house of your servant, that it may continue forever before you; for you, LORD, have blessed, and it is blessed forever.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, David defeated the Philistines and subdued them, and took Gath and its towns out of the hand of the Philistines."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He defeated Moab; and the Moabites became servants to David and brought tribute."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"David defeated Hadadezer king of Zobah, toward Hamath, as he went to establish his dominion by the river Euphrates."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"David took from him one thousand chariots, seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen; and David hamstrung all the chariot horses, but reserved of them enough for one hundred chariots."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When the Syrians of Damascus came to help Hadadezer king of Zobah, David struck twenty-two thousand men of the Syrians."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then David put garrisons in Syria of Damascus; and the Syrians became servants to David and brought tribute. The LORD gave victory to David wherever he went."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"David took the shields of gold that were on the servants of Hadadezer, and brought them to Jerusalem."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"From Tibhath and from Cun, cities of Hadadezer, David took very much bronze, with which Solomon made the bronze sea, the pillars, and the vessels of bronze."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When Tou king of Hamath heard that David had struck all the army of Hadadezer king of Zobah,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"he sent Hadoram his son to King David to greet him and to bless him, because he had fought against Hadadezer and struck him (for Hadadezer had wars with Tou); and he had with him all kinds of vessels of gold and silver and bronze."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"King David also dedicated these to the LORD, with the silver and the gold that he carried away from all the nations: from Edom, from Moab, from the children of Ammon, from the Philistines, and from Amalek."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Abishai the son of Zeruiah struck eighteen thousand of the Edomites in the Valley of Salt."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He put garrisons in Edom; and all the Edomites became servants to David. The LORD gave victory to David wherever he went."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"David reigned over all Israel; and he executed justice and righteousness for all his people."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Joab the son of Zeruiah was over the army; Jehoshaphat the son of Ahilud was recorder;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Zadok the son of Ahitub and Abimelech the son of Abiathar were priests; Shavsha was scribe;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada was over the Cherethites and the Pelethites; and the sons of David were chief officials serving the king."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Nahash the king of the children of Ammon died, and his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cI will show kindness to Hanun the son of Nahash, because his father showed kindness to me.\u201d"],[0,"So David sent messengers to comfort him concerning his father. David\u2019s servants came into the land of the children of Ammon to Hanun to comfort him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But the princes of the children of Ammon said to Hanun, \u201cDo you think that David honors your father, in that he has sent comforters to you? Haven\u2019t his servants come to you to search, to overthrow, and to spy out the land?\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"So Hanun took David\u2019s servants, shaved them, and cut off their garments in the middle at their buttocks, and sent them away."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then some people went and told David how the men were treated. He sent to meet them; for the men were greatly humiliated. The king said, \u201cStay at Jericho until your beards have grown, and then return.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When the children of Ammon saw that they had made themselves odious to David, Hanun and the children of Ammon sent one thousand talents of silver to hire chariots and horsemen out of Mesopotamia, out of Aram-maacah, and out of Zobah."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds, so 1000 talents is about 30 metric tons"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So they hired for themselves thirty-two thousand chariots, and the king of Maacah with his people, who came and encamped near Medeba. The children of Ammon gathered themselves together from their cities, and came to battle."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When David heard of it, he sent Joab with all the army of the mighty men."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The children of Ammon came out, and put the battle in array at the gate of the city; and the kings who had come were by themselves in the field."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Joab saw that the battle was set against him before and behind, he chose some of all the choice men of Israel, and put them in array against the Syrians."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The rest of the people he committed into the hand of Abishai his brother; and they put themselves in array against the children of Ammon."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cIf the Syrians are too strong for me, then you are to help me; but if the children of Ammon are too strong for you, then I will help you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Be courageous, and let\u2019s be strong for our people and for the cities of our God. May the LORD do that which seems good to him.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So Joab and the people who were with him came near to the front of the Syrians to the battle; and they fled before him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When the children of Ammon saw that the Syrians had fled, they likewise fled before Abishai his brother, and entered into the city. Then Joab came to Jerusalem."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Syrians saw that they were defeated by Israel, they sent messengers and called out the Syrians who were beyond the River, with Shophach the captain of the army of Hadadezer leading them."]],f:["or, the Euphrates River"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"David was told that, so he gathered all Israel together, passed over the Jordan, came to them, and set the battle in array against them. So when David had put the battle in array against the Syrians, they fought with him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The Syrians fled before Israel; and David killed of the Syrian men seven thousand charioteers and forty thousand footmen, and also killed Shophach the captain of the army."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When the servants of Hadadezer saw that they were defeated by Israel, they made peace with David and served him. The Syrians would not help the children of Ammon any more."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At the time of the return of the year, at the time when kings go out, Joab led out the army and wasted the country of the children of Ammon, and came and besieged Rabbah. But David stayed at Jerusalem. Joab struck Rabbah, and overthrew it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David took the crown of their king from off his head, and found it to weigh a talent of gold, and there were precious stones in it. It was set on David\u2019s head, and he brought very much plunder out of the city."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He brought out the people who were in it, and had them cut with saws, with iron picks, and with axes. David did so to all the cities of the children of Ammon. Then David and all the people returned to Jerusalem."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, war arose at Gezer with the Philistines. Then Sibbecai the Hushathite killed Sippai, of the sons of the giant; and they were subdued."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Again there was war with the Philistines; and Elhanan the son of Jair killed Lahmi the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the staff of whose spear was like a weaver\u2019s beam."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"There was again war at Gath, where there was a man of great stature, who had twenty-four fingers and toes, six on each hand and six on each foot; and he also was born to the giant."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When he defied Israel, Jonathan the son of Shimea, David\u2019s brother, killed him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"These were born to the giant in Gath; and they fell by the hand of David and by the hand of his servants."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Satan stood up against Israel, and moved David to take a census of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David said to Joab and to the princes of the people, \u201cGo, count Israel from Beersheba even to Dan; and bring me word, that I may know how many there are.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Joab said, \u201cMay the LORD make his people a hundred times as many as they are. But, my lord the king, aren\u2019t they all my lord\u2019s servants? Why does my lord require this thing? Why will he be a cause of guilt to Israel?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Nevertheless the king\u2019s word prevailed against Joab. Therefore Joab departed and went throughout all Israel, then came to Jerusalem."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Joab gave the sum of the census of the people to David. All those of Israel were one million one hundred thousand men who drew a sword; and in Judah were four hundred seventy thousand men who drew a sword."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But he didn\u2019t count Levi and Benjamin among them, for the king\u2019s word was abominable to Joab."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"God was displeased with this thing; therefore he struck Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"David said to God, \u201cI have sinned greatly, in that I have done this thing. But now put away, I beg you, the iniquity of your servant, for I have done very foolishly.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Gad, David\u2019s seer, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cGo and speak to David, saying, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cI offer you three things. Choose one of them, that I may do it to you.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"So Gad came to David and said to him, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Take your choice:"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"either three years of famine; or three months to be consumed before your foes, while the sword of your enemies overtakes you; or else three days of the sword of the LORD, even pestilence in the land, and the LORD\u2019s angel destroying throughout all the borders of Israel. Now therefore consider what answer I shall return to him who sent me.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Gad, \u201cI am in distress. Let me fall, I pray, into the LORD\u2019s hand, for his mercies are very great. Don\u2019t let me fall into man\u2019s hand.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So the LORD sent a pestilence on Israel, and seventy thousand men of Israel fell."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"God sent an angel to Jerusalem to destroy it. As he was about to destroy, the LORD saw, and he relented of the disaster, and said to the destroying angel, \u201cIt is enough. Now withdraw your hand.\u201d the LORD\u2019s angel was standing by the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"David lifted up his eyes, and saw the LORD\u2019s angel standing between earth and the sky, having a drawn sword in his hand stretched out over Jerusalem."],[0,"Then David and the elders, clothed in sackcloth, fell on their faces."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"David said to God, \u201cIsn\u2019t it I who commanded the people to be counted? It is even I who have sinned and done very wickedly; but these sheep, what have they done? Please let your hand, O LORD my God, be against me and against my father\u2019s house; but not against your people, that they should be plagued.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s angel commanded Gad to tell David that David should go up and raise an altar to the LORD on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"David went up at the saying of Gad, which he spoke in the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Ornan turned back and saw the angel; and his four sons who were with him hid themselves. Now Ornan was threshing wheat."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"As David came to Ornan, Ornan looked and saw David, and went out of the threshing floor, and bowed himself to David with his face to the ground."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said to Ornan, \u201cSell me the place of this threshing floor, that I may build an altar to the LORD on it. You shall sell it to me for the full price, that the plague may be stopped from afflicting the people.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Ornan said to David, \u201cTake it for yourself, and let my lord the king do that which is good in his eyes. Behold, I give the oxen for burnt offerings, and the threshing instruments for wood, and the wheat for the meal offering. I give it all.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"King David said to Ornan, \u201cNo, but I will most certainly buy it for the full price. For I will not take that which is yours for the LORD, nor offer a burnt offering that costs me nothing.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"So David gave to Ornan six hundred shekels of gold by weight for the place."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.32 Troy ounces, so 600 shekels was about 6 kilograms or about 192 Troy ounces."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"David built an altar to the LORD there, and offered burnt offerings and peace offerings, and called on the LORD; and he answered him from the sky by fire on the altar of burnt offering."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD commanded the angel, and he put his sword back into its sheath."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time, when David saw that the LORD had answered him in the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite, then he sacrificed there."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For the LORD\u2019s tabernacle, which Moses made in the wilderness, and the altar of burnt offering, were at that time in the high place at Gibeon."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But David couldn\u2019t go before it to inquire of God, for he was afraid because of the sword of the LORD\u2019s angel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said, \u201cThis is the house of the LORD God, and this is the altar of burnt offering for Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"David gave orders to gather together the foreigners who were in the land of Israel; and he set masons to cut dressed stones to build God\u2019s house."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"David prepared iron in abundance for the nails for the doors of the gates and for the couplings, and bronze in abundance without weight,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and cedar trees without number, for the Sidonians and the people of Tyre brought cedar trees in abundance to David."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cSolomon my son is young and tender, and the house that is to be built for the LORD must be exceedingly magnificent, of fame and of glory throughout all countries. I will therefore make preparation for it.\u201d So David prepared abundantly before his death."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then he called for Solomon his son, and commanded him to build a house for the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"David said to Solomon his son, \u201cAs for me, it was in my heart to build a house to the name of the LORD my God."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying, \u2018You have shed blood abundantly and have made great wars. You shall not build a house to my name, because you have shed much blood on the earth in my sight."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Behold, a son shall be born to you, who shall be a man of peace. I will give him rest from all his enemies all around; for his name shall be Solomon, and I will give peace and quietness to Israel in his days."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He shall build a house for my name; and he will be my son, and I will be his father; and I will establish the throne of his kingdom over Israel forever.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now, my son, may the LORD be with you and prosper you, and build the house of the LORD your God, as he has spoken concerning you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"May the LORD give you discretion and understanding, and put you in charge of Israel, so that you may keep the law of the LORD your God."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then you will prosper, if you observe to do the statutes and the ordinances which the LORD gave Moses concerning Israel. Be strong and courageous. Don\u2019t be afraid and don\u2019t be dismayed."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now, behold, in my affliction I have prepared for the LORD\u2019s house one hundred thousand talents of gold, one million talents of silver, and bronze and iron without weight; for it is in abundance. I have also prepared timber and stone; and you may add to them."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 100,000 talents is about 3 metric tons","about 30,000 metric tons"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"There are also workmen with you in abundance\u2014cutters and workers of stone and timber, and all kinds of men who are skillful in every kind of work;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"of the gold, the silver, the bronze, and the iron, there is no number. Arise and be doing, and may the LORD be with you.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"David also commanded all the princes of Israel to help Solomon his son, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cIsn\u2019t the LORD your God with you? Hasn\u2019t he given you rest on every side? For he has delivered the inhabitants of the land into my hand; and the land is subdued before the LORD and before his people."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now set your heart and your soul to follow the LORD your God. Arise therefore, and build the sanctuary of the LORD God, to bring the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant and the holy vessels of God into the house that is to be built for the LORD\u2019s name.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now David was old and full of days; and he made Solomon his son king over Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He gathered together all the princes of Israel, with the priests and the Levites."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The Levites were counted from thirty years old and upward; and their number by their polls, man by man, was thirty-eight thousand."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"David said, \u201cOf these, twenty-four thousand were to oversee the work of the LORD\u2019s house, six thousand were officers and judges,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"four thousand were doorkeepers, and four thousand praised the LORD with the instruments which I made for giving praise.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"David divided them into divisions according to the sons of Levi: Gershon, Kohath, and Merari."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the Gershonites: Ladan and Shimei."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The sons of Ladan: Jehiel the chief, Zetham, and Joel, three."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The sons of Shimei: Shelomoth, Haziel, and Haran, three. These were the heads of the fathers\u2019 households of Ladan."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The sons of Shimei: Jahath, Zina, Jeush, and Beriah. These four were the sons of Shimei."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Jahath was the chief, and Zizah the second; but Jeush and Beriah didn\u2019t have many sons; therefore they became a fathers\u2019 house in one reckoning."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Kohath: Amram, Izhar, Hebron, and Uzziel, four."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The sons of Amram: Aaron and Moses; and Aaron was separated that he should sanctify the most holy things, he and his sons forever, to burn incense before the LORD, to minister to him, and to bless in his name forever."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But as for Moses the man of God, his sons were named among the tribe of Levi."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The sons of Moses: Gershom and Eliezer."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The sons of Gershom: Shebuel the chief."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The son of Eliezer was Rehabiah the chief; and Eliezer had no other sons, but the sons of Rehabiah were very many."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The son of Izhar: Shelomith the chief."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The sons of Hebron: Jeriah the chief, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The sons of Uzziel: Micah the chief, and Isshiah the second."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The sons of Mahli: Eleazar and Kish."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Eleazar died, and had no sons, but daughters only; and their relatives, the sons of Kish, took them as wives."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jeremoth, three."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"These were the sons of Levi after their fathers\u2019 houses, even the heads of the fathers\u2019 houses of those who were counted individually, in the number of names by their polls, who did the work for the service of the LORD\u2019s house, from twenty years old and upward."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For David said, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, has given rest to his people; and he dwells in Jerusalem forever."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Also the Levites will no longer need to carry the tabernacle and all its vessels for its service.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For by the last words of David the sons of Levi were counted, from twenty years old and upward."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For their duty was to wait on the sons of Aaron for the service of the LORD\u2019s house\u2014in the courts, in the rooms, and in the purifying of all holy things, even the work of the service of God\u2019s house;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"for the show bread also, and for the fine flour for a meal offering, whether of unleavened wafers, or of that which is baked in the pan, or of that which is soaked, and for all measurements of quantity and size;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and to stand every morning to thank and praise the LORD, and likewise in the evening;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and to offer all burnt offerings to the LORD on the Sabbaths, on the new moons, and on the set feasts, in number according to the ordinance concerning them, continually before the LORD;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and that they should keep the duty of the Tent of Meeting, the duty of the holy place, and the duty of the sons of Aaron their brothers for the service of the LORD\u2019s house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These were the divisions of the sons of Aaron. The sons of Aaron: Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But Nadab and Abihu died before their father, and had no children; therefore Eleazar and Ithamar served as priests."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"David, with Zadok of the sons of Eleazar and Ahimelech of the sons of Ithamar, divided them according to their ordering in their service."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"There were more chief men found of the sons of Eleazar than of the sons of Ithamar; and they were divided like this: of the sons of Eleazar there were sixteen, heads of fathers\u2019 houses; and of the sons of Ithamar, according to their fathers\u2019 houses, eight."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Thus they were divided impartially by drawing lots; for there were princes of the sanctuary and princes of God, both of the sons of Eleazar, and of the sons of Ithamar."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Shemaiah the son of Nethanel the scribe, who was of the Levites, wrote them in the presence of the king, the princes, Zadok the priest, Ahimelech the son of Abiathar, and the heads of the fathers\u2019 households of the priests and of the Levites; one fathers\u2019 house being taken for Eleazar, and one taken for Ithamar."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the first lot came out to Jehoiarib, the second to Jedaiah,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"the third to Harim, the fourth to Seorim,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"the fifth to Malchijah, the sixth to Mijamin,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"the seventh to Hakkoz, the eighth to Abijah,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"the ninth to Jeshua, the tenth to Shecaniah,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"the eleventh to Eliashib, the twelfth to Jakim,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"the thirteenth to Huppah, the fourteenth to Jeshebeab,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the fifteenth to Bilgah, the sixteenth to Immer,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"the seventeenth to Hezir, the eighteenth to Happizzez,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the nineteenth to Pethahiah, the twentieth to Jehezkel,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the twenty-first to Jachin, the twenty-second to Gamul,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"the twenty-third to Delaiah, and the twenty-fourth to Maaziah."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"This was their ordering in their service, to come into the LORD\u2019s house according to the ordinance given to them by Aaron their father, as the LORD, the God of Israel, had commanded him."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the rest of the sons of Levi: of the sons of Amram, Shubael; of the sons of Shubael, Jehdeiah."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Of Rehabiah: of the sons of Rehabiah, Isshiah the chief."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Of the Izharites, Shelomoth; of the sons of Shelomoth, Jahath."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The sons of Hebron: Jeriah, Amariah the second, Jahaziel the third, and Jekameam the fourth."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The sons of Uzziel: Micah; of the sons of Micah, Shamir."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The brother of Micah: Isshiah; of the sons of Isshiah, Zechariah."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The sons of Merari: Mahli and Mushi. The son of Jaaziah: Beno."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The sons of Merari by Jaaziah: Beno, Shoham, Zaccur, and Ibri."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Of Mahli: Eleazar, who had no sons."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Of Kish, the son of Kish: Jerahmeel."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The sons of Mushi: Mahli, Eder, and Jerimoth. These were the sons of the Levites after their fathers\u2019 houses."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"These likewise cast lots even as their brothers the sons of Aaron in the presence of David the king, Zadok, Ahimelech, and the heads of the fathers\u2019 households of the priests and of the Levites, the fathers\u2019 households of the chief even as those of his younger brother."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover, David and the captains of the army set apart for the service certain of the sons of Asaph, of Heman, and of Jeduthun, who were to prophesy with harps, with stringed instruments, and with cymbals. The number of those who did the work according to their service was:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"of the sons of Asaph: Zaccur, Joseph, Nethaniah, and Asharelah. The sons of Asaph were under the hand of Asaph, who prophesied at the order of the king."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Of Jeduthun, the sons of Jeduthun: Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Shimei, Hashabiah, and Mattithiah, six, under the hands of their father Jeduthun, who prophesied in giving thanks and praising the LORD with the harp."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Of Heman, the sons of Heman: Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, Romamti-Ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, and Mahazioth."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All these were the sons of Heman the king\u2019s seer in the words of God, to lift up the horn. God gave to Heman fourteen sons and three daughters."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"All these were under the hands of their father for song in the LORD\u2019s house, with cymbals, stringed instruments, and harps, for the service of God\u2019s house: Asaph, Jeduthun, and Heman being under the order of the king."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The number of them, with their brothers who were instructed in singing to the LORD, even all who were skillful, was two hundred eighty-eight."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They cast lots for their offices, all alike, the small as well as the great, the teacher as well as the student."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the first lot came out for Asaph to Joseph; the second to Gedaliah, he and his brothers and sons were twelve;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"the third to Zaccur, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"the fourth to Izri, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"the fifth to Nethaniah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"the sixth to Bukkiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the seventh to Jesharelah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"the eighth to Jeshaiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the ninth to Mattaniah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the tenth to Shimei, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"the eleventh to Azarel, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the twelfth to Hashabiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"for the thirteenth, Shubael, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"for the fourteenth, Mattithiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"for the fifteenth to Jeremoth, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"for the sixteenth to Hananiah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"for the seventeenth to Joshbekashah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"for the eighteenth to Hanani, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"for the nineteenth to Mallothi, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"for the twentieth to Eliathah, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"for the twenty-first to Hothir, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"for the twenty-second to Giddalti, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"for the twenty-third to Mahazioth, his sons and his brothers, twelve;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"for the twenty-fourth to Romamti-Ezer, his sons and his brothers, twelve."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For the divisions of the doorkeepers: of the Korahites, Meshelemiah the son of Kore, of the sons of Asaph."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Meshelemiah had sons: Zechariah the firstborn, Jediael the second, Zebadiah the third, Jathniel the fourth,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Elam the fifth, Jehohanan the sixth, and Eliehoenai the seventh."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Obed-Edom had sons: Shemaiah the firstborn, Jehozabad the second, Joah the third, Sacar the fourth, Nethanel the fifth,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ammiel the sixth, Issachar the seventh, and Peullethai the eighth; for God blessed him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Sons were also born to Shemaiah his son, who ruled over the house of their father; for they were mighty men of valor."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The sons of Shemaiah: Othni, Rephael, Obed, and Elzabad, whose relatives were valiant men, Elihu, and Semachiah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All these were of the sons of Obed-Edom with their sons and their brothers, able men in strength for the service: sixty-two of Obed-Edom."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Meshelemiah had sons and brothers, eighteen valiant men."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Also Hosah, of the children of Merari, had sons: Shimri the chief (for though he was not the firstborn, yet his father made him chief),"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Hilkiah the second, Tebaliah the third, and Zechariah the fourth. All the sons and brothers of Hosah were thirteen."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Of these were the divisions of the doorkeepers, even of the chief men, having offices like their brothers, to minister in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They cast lots, the small as well as the great, according to their fathers\u2019 houses, for every gate."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The lot eastward fell to Shelemiah. Then for Zechariah his son, a wise counselor, they cast lots; and his lot came out northward."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"To Obed-Edom southward; and to his sons the storehouse."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"To Shuppim and Hosah westward, by the gate of Shallecheth, at the causeway that goes up, watchman opposite watchman."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Eastward were six Levites, northward four a day, southward four a day, and for the storehouse two and two."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For Parbar westward, four at the causeway, and two at Parbar."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"These were the divisions of the doorkeepers; of the sons of the Korahites, and of the sons of Merari."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the Levites, Ahijah was over the treasures of God\u2019s house and over the treasures of the dedicated things."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The sons of Ladan, the sons of the Gershonites belonging to Ladan, the heads of the fathers\u2019 households belonging to Ladan the Gershonite: Jehieli."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The sons of Jehieli: Zetham, and Joel his brother, over the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Of the Amramites, of the Izharites, of the Hebronites, of the Uzzielites:"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Shebuel the son of Gershom, the son of Moses, was ruler over the treasuries."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"His brothers: of Eliezer, Rehabiah his son, and Jeshaiah his son, and Joram his son, and Zichri his son, and Shelomoth his son."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"This Shelomoth and his brothers were over all the treasuries of the dedicated things, which David the king, and the heads of the fathers\u2019 households, the captains over thousands and hundreds, and the captains of the army, had dedicated."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They dedicated some of the plunder won in battles to repair the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"All that Samuel the seer, Saul the son of Kish, Abner the son of Ner, and Joab the son of Zeruiah had dedicated, whoever had dedicated anything, it was under the hand of Shelomoth and of his brothers."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the Izharites, Chenaniah and his sons were appointed to the outward business over Israel, for officers and judges."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Of the Hebronites, Hashabiah and his brothers, one thousand seven hundred men of valor, had the oversight of Israel beyond the Jordan westward, for all the business of the LORD and for the service of the king."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Of the Hebronites, Jerijah was the chief of the Hebronites, according to their generations by fathers\u2019 households. They were sought for in the fortieth year of the reign of David, and mighty men of valor were found among them at Jazer of Gilead."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"His relatives, men of valor, were two thousand seven hundred, heads of fathers\u2019 households, whom King David made overseers over the Reubenites, the Gadites, and the half-tribe of the Manassites, for every matter pertaining to God and for the affairs of the king."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the children of Israel after their number, the heads of fathers\u2019 households and the captains of thousands and of hundreds, and their officers who served the king in any matter of the divisions which came in and went out month by month throughout all the months of the year\u2014of every division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Over the first division for the first month was Jashobeam the son of Zabdiel. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He was of the children of Perez, the chief of all the captains of the army for the first month."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Over the division of the second month was Dodai the Ahohite and his division, and Mikloth the ruler; and in his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The third captain of the army for the third month was Benaiah, the son of Jehoiada the chief priest. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"This is that Benaiah who was the mighty man of the thirty and over the thirty. Of his division was Ammizabad his son."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The fourth captain for the fourth month was Asahel the brother of Joab, and Zebadiah his son after him. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The fifth captain for the fifth month was Shamhuth the Izrahite. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The sixth captain for the sixth month was Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The seventh captain for the seventh month was Helez the Pelonite, of the children of Ephraim. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The eighth captain for the eighth month was Sibbecai the Hushathite, of the Zerahites. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The ninth captain for the ninth month was Abiezer the Anathothite, of the Benjamites. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The tenth captain for the tenth month was Maharai the Netophathite, of the Zerahites. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The eleventh captain for the eleventh month was Benaiah the Pirathonite, of the children of Ephraim. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The twelfth captain for the twelfth month was Heldai the Netophathite, of Othniel. In his division were twenty-four thousand."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Furthermore over the tribes of Israel: of the Reubenites, Eliezer the son of Zichri was the ruler; of the Simeonites, Shephatiah the son of Maacah;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"of Levi, Hashabiah the son of Kemuel; of Aaron, Zadok;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"of Judah, Elihu, one of the brothers of David; of Issachar, Omri the son of Michael;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"of Zebulun, Ishmaiah the son of Obadiah; of Naphtali, Jeremoth the son of Azriel;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"of the children of Ephraim, Hoshea the son of Azaziah; of the half-tribe of Manasseh, Joel the son of Pedaiah;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"of the half-tribe of Manasseh in Gilead, Iddo the son of Zechariah; of Benjamin, Jaasiel the son of Abner;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"of Dan, Azarel the son of Jeroham. These were the captains of the tribes of Israel."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But David didn\u2019t take the number of them from twenty years old and under, because the LORD had said he would increase Israel like the stars of the sky."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Joab the son of Zeruiah began to take a census, but didn\u2019t finish; and wrath came on Israel for this. The number wasn\u2019t put into the account in the chronicles of King David."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Over the king\u2019s treasures was Azmaveth the son of Adiel. Over the treasures in the fields, in the cities, in the villages, and in the towers was Jonathan the son of Uzziah;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Over those who did the work of the field for tillage of the ground was Ezri the son of Chelub."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Over the vineyards was Shimei the Ramathite. Over the increase of the vineyards for the wine cellars was Zabdi the Shiphmite."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Over the olive trees and the sycamore trees that were in the lowland was Baal Hanan the Gederite. Over the cellars of oil was Joash."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Over the herds that fed in Sharon was Shitrai the Sharonite. Over the herds that were in the valleys was Shaphat the son of Adlai."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Over the camels was Obil the Ishmaelite. Over the donkeys was Jehdeiah the Meronothite. Over the flocks was Jaziz the Hagrite."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"All these were the rulers of the property which was King David\u2019s."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Also Jonathan, David\u2019s uncle, was a counselor, a man of understanding, and a scribe. Jehiel the son of Hachmoni was with the king\u2019s sons."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Ahithophel was the king\u2019s counselor. Hushai the Archite was the king\u2019s friend."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"After Ahithophel was Jehoiada the son of Benaiah, and Abiathar. Joab was the captain of the king\u2019s army."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David assembled all the princes of Israel, the princes of the tribes, the captains of the companies who served the king by division, the captains of thousands, the captains of hundreds, and the rulers over all the substance and possessions of the king and of his sons, with the officers and the mighty men, even all the mighty men of valor, to Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then David the king stood up on his feet and said, \u201cHear me, my brothers and my people! As for me, it was in my heart to build a house of rest for the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant, and for the footstool of our God; and I had prepared for the building."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But God said to me, \u2018You shall not build a house for my name, because you are a man of war and have shed blood.\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"However the LORD, the God of Israel, chose me out of all the house of my father to be king over Israel forever. For he has chosen Judah to be prince; and in the house of Judah, the house of my father; and among the sons of my father he took pleasure in me to make me king over all Israel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Of all my sons (for the LORD has given me many sons), he has chosen Solomon my son to sit on the throne of the LORD\u2019s kingdom over Israel."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u2018Solomon, your son, shall build my house and my courts; for I have chosen him to be my son, and I will be his father."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I will establish his kingdom forever if he continues to do my commandments and my ordinances, as it is today.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now therefore, in the sight of all Israel, the LORD\u2019s assembly, and in the audience of our God, observe and seek out all the commandments of the LORD your God, that you may possess this good land, and leave it for an inheritance to your children after you forever."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"You, Solomon my son, know the God of your father, and serve him with a perfect heart and with a willing mind; for the LORD searches all hearts, and understands all the imaginations of the thoughts. If you seek him, he will be found by you; but if you forsake him, he will cast you off forever."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Take heed now, for the LORD has chosen you to build a house for the sanctuary. Be strong, and do it.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David gave to Solomon his son the plans for the porch of the temple, for its houses, for its treasuries, for its upper rooms, for its inner rooms, for the place of the mercy seat;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and the plans of all that he had by the Spirit, for the courts of the LORD\u2019s house, for all the surrounding rooms, for the treasuries of God\u2019s house, and for the treasuries of the dedicated things;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"also for the divisions of the priests and the Levites, for all the work of the service of the LORD\u2019s house, and for all the vessels of service in the LORD\u2019s house\u2014"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"of gold by weight for the gold for all vessels of every kind of service, for all the vessels of silver by weight, for all vessels of every kind of service;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"by weight also for the lamp stands of gold, and for its lamps, of gold, by weight for every lamp stand and for its lamps; and for the lamp stands of silver, by weight for every lamp stand and for its lamps, according to the use of every lamp stand;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and the gold by weight for the tables of show bread, for every table; and silver for the tables of silver;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and the forks, the basins, and the cups, of pure gold; and for the golden bowls by weight for every bowl; and for the silver bowls by weight for every bowl;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and for the altar of incense, refined gold by weight; and gold for the plans for the chariot, and the cherubim that spread out and cover the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"\u201cAll this\u201d, David said, \u201cI have been made to understand in writing from the LORD\u2019s hand, even all the works of this pattern.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"David said to Solomon his son, \u201cBe strong and courageous, and do it. Don\u2019t be afraid, nor be dismayed, for the LORD God, even my God, is with you. He will not fail you nor forsake you, until all the work for the service of the LORD\u2019s house is finished."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Behold, there are the divisions of the priests and the Levites for all the service of God\u2019s house. Every willing man who has skill for any kind of service shall be with you in all kinds of work. Also the captains and all the people will be entirely at your command.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"David the king said to all the assembly, \u201cSolomon my son, whom alone God has chosen, is yet young and tender, and the work is great; for the palace is not for man, but for the LORD God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now I have prepared with all my might for the house of my God the gold for the things of gold, the silver for the things of silver, the bronze for the things of bronze, iron for the things of iron, and wood for the things of wood, also onyx stones, stones to be set, stones for inlaid work of various colors, all kinds of precious stones, and marble stones in abundance."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In addition, because I have set my affection on the house of my God, since I have a treasure of my own of gold and silver, I give it to the house of my God, over and above all that I have prepared for the holy house:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"even three thousand talents of gold, of the gold of Ophir, and seven thousand talents of refined silver, with which to overlay the walls of the houses;"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 3000 talents is about 90 metric tons","about 210 metric tons"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"of gold for the things of gold, and of silver for the things of silver, and for all kinds of work to be made by the hands of artisans. Who then offers willingly to consecrate himself today to the LORD?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the princes of the fathers\u2019 households, and the princes of the tribes of Israel, and the captains of thousands and of hundreds, with the rulers over the king\u2019s work, offered willingly;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and they gave for the service of God\u2019s house of gold five thousand talents and ten thousand darics, of silver ten thousand talents, of bronze eighteen thousand talents, and of iron one hundred thousand talents."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 5000 talents is about 150 metric tons","a daric was a gold coin issued by a Persian king, weighing about 8.4 grams or about 0.27 troy ounces each."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"People with whom precious stones were found gave them to the treasure of the LORD\u2019s house, under the hand of Jehiel the Gershonite."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then the people rejoiced, because they offered willingly, because with a perfect heart they offered willingly to the LORD; and David the king also rejoiced with great joy."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore David blessed the LORD before all the assembly; and David said, \u201cYou are blessed, LORD, the God of Israel our father, forever and ever."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Yours, LORD, is the greatness, the power, the glory, the victory, and the majesty! For all that is in the heavens and on the earth is yours. Yours is the kingdom, LORD, and you are exalted as head above all."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Both riches and honor come from you, and you rule over all! In your hand is power and might! It is in your hand to make great, and to give strength to all!"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now therefore, our God, we thank you and praise your glorious name."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But who am I, and what is my people, that we should be able to offer so willingly as this? For all things come from you, and we have given you of your own."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For we are strangers before you and foreigners, as all our fathers were. Our days on the earth are as a shadow, and there is no remaining."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"LORD our God, all this store that we have prepared to build you a house for your holy name comes from your hand, and is all your own."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I know also, my God, that you try the heart and have pleasure in uprightness. As for me, in the uprightness of my heart I have willingly offered all these things. Now I have seen with joy your people, who are present here, offer willingly to you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"LORD, the God of Abraham, of Isaac, and of Israel, our fathers, keep this desire forever in the thoughts of the heart of your people, and prepare their heart for you;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and give to Solomon my son a perfect heart, to keep your commandments, your testimonies, and your statutes, and to do all these things, and to build the palace, for which I have made provision.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then David said to all the assembly, \u201cNow bless the LORD your God!\u201d"],[0,"All the assembly blessed the LORD, the God of their fathers, and bowed down their heads and prostrated themselves before the LORD and the king."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They sacrificed sacrifices to the LORD and offered burnt offerings to the LORD on the next day after that day, even one thousand bulls, one thousand rams, and one thousand lambs, with their drink offerings and sacrifices in abundance for all Israel,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and ate and drank before the LORD on that day with great gladness. They made Solomon the son of David king the second time, and anointed him before the LORD to be prince, and Zadok to be priest."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon sat on the throne of the LORD as king instead of David his father, and prospered; and all Israel obeyed him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"All the princes, the mighty men, and also all of the sons of King David submitted themselves to Solomon the king."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The LORD magnified Solomon exceedingly in the sight of all Israel, and gave to him such royal majesty as had not been on any king before him in Israel."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Now David the son of Jesse reigned over all Israel."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The time that he reigned over Israel was forty years; he reigned seven years in Hebron, and he reigned thirty-three years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He died at a good old age, full of days, riches, and honor; and Solomon his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Now the acts of David the king, first and last, behold, they are written in the history of Samuel the seer, and in the history of Nathan the prophet, and in the history of Gad the seer,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"with all his reign and his might, and the events that involved him, Israel, and all the kingdoms of the lands."]]}]]}},1284,[]);
__d(function(e,t,h,o,a,n,s){a.exports={book:"2Chr",name:"2 Chronicles",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon the son of David was firmly established in his kingdom, and the LORD his God was with him, and made him exceedingly great."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh).","The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon spoke to all Israel, to the captains of thousands and of hundreds, to the judges, and to every prince in all Israel, the heads of the fathers\u2019 households."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then Solomon, and all the assembly with him, went to the high place that was at Gibeon; for God\u2019s Tent of Meeting was there, which the LORD\u2019s servant Moses had made in the wilderness."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But David had brought God\u2019s ark up from Kiriath Jearim to the place that David had prepared for it; for he had pitched a tent for it at Jerusalem."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Moreover the bronze altar that Bezalel the son of Uri, the son of Hur, had made was there before the LORD\u2019s tabernacle; and Solomon and the assembly were seeking counsel there."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Solomon went up there to the bronze altar before the LORD, which was at the Tent of Meeting, and offered one thousand burnt offerings on it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"That night, God appeared to Solomon and said to him, \u201cAsk for what you want me to give you.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon said to God, \u201cYou have shown great loving kindness to David my father, and have made me king in his place."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now, LORD God, let your promise to David my father be established; for you have made me king over a people like the dust of the earth in multitude."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now give me wisdom and knowledge, that I may go out and come in before this people; for who can judge this great people of yours?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Solomon, \u201cBecause this was in your heart, and you have not asked riches, wealth, honor, or the life of those who hate you, nor yet have you asked for long life; but have asked for wisdom and knowledge for yourself, that you may judge my people, over whom I have made you king,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"therefore wisdom and knowledge is granted to you. I will give you riches, wealth, and honor, such as none of the kings have had who have been before you, and none after you will have.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"So Solomon came from the high place that was at Gibeon, from before the Tent of Meeting, to Jerusalem; and he reigned over Israel."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon gathered chariots and horsemen. He had one thousand four hundred chariots and twelve thousand horsemen that he placed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Jerusalem."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The king made silver and gold to be as common as stones in Jerusalem, and he made cedars to be as common as the sycamore trees that are in the lowland."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The horses which Solomon had were brought out of Egypt and from Kue. The king\u2019s merchants purchased them from Kue."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They imported from Egypt then exported a chariot for six hundred pieces of silver and a horse for one hundred fifty. They also exported them to the Hittite kings and the Syrian kings."]],f:["The pieces of silver were probably shekels, so 600 pieces would be about 13.2 pounds or 6 kilograms of silver, and 150 would be about 3.3 pounds or 1.5 kilograms of silver.","or, Aramean"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Solomon decided to build a house for the LORD\u2019s name, and a house for his kingdom."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Solomon counted out seventy thousand men to bear burdens, eighty thousand men who were stone cutters in the mountains, and three thousand six hundred to oversee them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon sent to Huram the king of Tyre, saying, \u201cAs you dealt with David my father, and sent him cedars to build him a house in which to dwell, so deal with me."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, I am about to build a house for the name of the LORD my God, to dedicate it to him, to burn before him incense of sweet spices, for the continual show bread, and for the burnt offerings morning and evening, on the Sabbaths, on the new moons, and on the set feasts of the LORD our God. This is an ordinance forever to Israel."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe house which I am building will be great, for our God is greater than all gods."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But who is able to build him a house, since heaven and the heaven of heavens can\u2019t contain him? Who am I then, that I should build him a house, except just to burn incense before him?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore send me a man skillful to work in gold, in silver, in bronze, in iron, and in purple, crimson, and blue, and who knows how to engrave engravings, to be with the skillful men who are with me in Judah and in Jerusalem, whom David my father provided."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSend me also cedar trees, cypress trees, and algum trees out of Lebanon, for I know that your servants know how to cut timber in Lebanon. Behold, my servants will be with your servants,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"even to prepare timber in abundance for me; for the house which I am about to build will be great and wonderful."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Behold, I will give to your servants, the cutters who cut timber, twenty thousand cors of beaten wheat, twenty thousand baths of barley, twenty thousand baths of wine, and twenty thousand baths of oil.\u201d"]],f:["1 cor is the same as a homer, or about 55.9 U. S. gallons (liquid) or 211 liters or 6 bushels, so 20,000 cors of wheat would weigh about 545 metric tons","1 bath is one tenth of a cor, or about 5.6 U. S. gallons or 21 liters or 2.4 pecks. 20,000 baths of barley would weigh about 262 metric tons."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Huram the king of Tyre answered in writing, which he sent to Solomon, \u201cBecause the LORD loves his people, he has made you king over them.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Huram continued, \u201cBlessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who made heaven and earth, who has given to David the king a wise son, endowed with discretion and understanding, who would build a house for the LORD and a house for his kingdom."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I have sent a skillful man, endowed with understanding, Huram-abi,"]],f:["or, Huram, my father"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the son of a woman of the daughters of Dan; and his father was a man of Tyre. He is skillful to work in gold, in silver, in bronze, in iron, in stone, in timber, in purple, in blue, in fine linen, and in crimson, also to engrave any kind of engraving and to devise any device, that there may be a place appointed to him with your skillful men, and with the skillful men of my lord David your father."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore, the wheat, the barley, the oil, and the wine which my lord has spoken of, let him send to his servants;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and we will cut wood out of Lebanon, as much as you need. We will bring it to you in rafts by sea to Joppa; then you shall carry it up to Jerusalem.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon counted all the foreigners who were in the land of Israel, after the census with which David his father had counted them; and they found one hundred fifty-three thousand six hundred."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He set seventy thousand of them to bear burdens, eighty thousand who were stone cutters in the mountains, and three thousand six hundred overseers to assign the people their work."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon began to build the LORD\u2019s house at Jerusalem on Mount Moriah, where the LORD appeared to David his father, which he prepared in the place that David had appointed, on the threshing floor of Ornan the Jebusite."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He began to build in the second day of the second month, in the fourth year of his reign."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now these are the foundations which Solomon laid for the building of God\u2019s house: the length by cubits after the first measure was sixty cubits, and the width twenty cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The porch that was in front, its length, across the width of the house, was twenty cubits, and the height one hundred twenty; and he overlaid it within with pure gold."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He made the larger room with a ceiling of cypress wood, which he overlaid with fine gold, and ornamented it with palm trees and chains."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He decorated the house with precious stones for beauty. The gold was gold from Parvaim."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He also overlaid the house, the beams, the thresholds, its walls, and its doors with gold, and engraved cherubim on the walls."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the most holy place. Its length, according to the width of the house, was twenty cubits, and its width twenty cubits; and he overlaid it with fine gold, amounting to six hundred talents."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 600 talents is about 18 metric tons"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The weight of the nails was fifty shekels of gold. He overlaid the upper rooms with gold."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.32 Troy ounces, so 50 shekels was about 0.5 kilograms or about 16 Troy ounces."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"In the most holy place he made two cherubim by carving, and they overlaid them with gold."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The wings of the cherubim were twenty cubits long: the wing of the one was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house; and the other wing was five cubits, reaching to the wing of the other cherub."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The wing of the other cherub was five cubits, reaching to the wall of the house; and the other wing was five cubits, joining to the wing of the other cherub."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The wings of these cherubim spread themselves out twenty cubits. They stood on their feet, and their faces were toward the house."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He made the veil of blue, purple, crimson, and fine linen, and ornamented it with cherubim."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Also he made before the house two pillars thirty-five cubits high, and the capital that was on the top of each of them was five cubits."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He made chains in the inner sanctuary, and put them on the tops of the pillars; and he made one hundred pomegranates, and put them on the chains."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He set up the pillars before the temple, one on the right hand and the other on the left; and called the name of that on the right hand Jachin, and the name of that on the left Boaz."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he made an altar of bronze, twenty cubits long, twenty cubits wide, and ten cubits high."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Also he made the molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim. It was round, five cubits high, and thirty cubits in circumference."]],f:["or, pool, or, reservoir"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Under it was the likeness of oxen, which encircled it, for ten cubits, encircling the sea. The oxen were in two rows, cast when it was cast."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"It stood on twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, three looking toward the west, three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east; and the sea was set on them above, and all their hindquarters were inward."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It was a handbreadth thick. Its brim was made like the brim of a cup, like the flower of a lily. It received and held three thousand baths."]],f:["A bath is about 5.6 U. S. gallons or 21.1 liters, so 3,000 baths is about 16,800 gallons or 63.3 kiloliters."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He also made ten basins, and put five on the right hand and five on the left, to wash in them. The things that belonged to the burnt offering were washed in them, but the sea was for the priests to wash in."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He made the ten lamp stands of gold according to the ordinance concerning them; and he set them in the temple, five on the right hand and five on the left."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He made also ten tables, and placed them in the temple, five on the right side and five on the left. He made one hundred basins of gold."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Furthermore he made the court of the priests, the great court, and doors for the court, and overlaid their doors with bronze."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He set the sea on the right side of the house eastward, toward the south."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Huram made the pots, the shovels, and the basins."],[0,"So Huram finished doing the work that he did for King Solomon in God\u2019s house:"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"the two pillars, the bowls, the two capitals which were on the top of the pillars, the two networks to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the top of the pillars,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and the four hundred pomegranates for the two networks\u2014two rows of pomegranates for each network, to cover the two bowls of the capitals that were on the pillars."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He also made the bases, and he made the basins on the bases\u2014"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"one sea, and the twelve oxen under it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Huram-abi also made the pots, the shovels, the forks, and all its vessels for King Solomon, for the LORD\u2019s house, of bright bronze."]],f:["\u201cabi\u201d means \u201chis father\u201d"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The king cast them in the plain of the Jordan, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zeredah."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Thus Solomon made all these vessels in great abundance, so that the weight of the bronze could not be determined."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon made all the vessels that were in God\u2019s house: the golden altar, the tables with the show bread on them,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and the lamp stands with their lamps to burn according to the ordinance before the inner sanctuary, of pure gold;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and the flowers, the lamps, and the tongs of gold that was purest gold;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and the snuffers, the basins, the spoons, and the fire pans of pure gold. As for the entry of the house, its inner doors for the most holy place and the doors of the main hall of the temple were of gold."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus all the work that Solomon did for the LORD\u2019s house was finished. Solomon brought in the things that David his father had dedicated, even the silver, the gold, and all the vessels, and put them in the treasuries of God\u2019s house."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon assembled the elders of Israel and all the heads of the tribes, the princes of the fathers\u2019 households of the children of Israel, to Jerusalem, to bring up the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant out of David\u2019s city, which is Zion."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So all the men of Israel assembled themselves to the king at the feast, which was in the seventh month."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"All the elders of Israel came. The Levites took up the ark."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They brought up the ark, the Tent of Meeting, and all the holy vessels that were in the Tent. The Levitical priests brought these up."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"King Solomon and all the congregation of Israel who were assembled to him were before the ark, sacrificing sheep and cattle that could not be counted or numbered for multitude."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The priests brought in the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant to its place, into the inner sanctuary of the house, to the most holy place, even under the wings of the cherubim."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the cherubim spread out their wings over the place of the ark, and the cherubim covered the ark and its poles above."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The poles were so long that the ends of the poles were seen from the ark in front of the inner sanctuary, but they were not seen outside; and it is there to this day."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"There was nothing in the ark except the two tablets which Moses put there at Horeb, when the LORD made a covenant with the children of Israel, when they came out of Egypt."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When the priests had come out of the holy place (for all the priests who were present had sanctified themselves, and didn\u2019t keep their divisions;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"also the Levites who were the singers, all of them, even Asaph, Heman, Jeduthun, and their sons and their brothers, arrayed in fine linen, with cymbals and stringed instruments and harps, stood at the east end of the altar, and with them one hundred twenty priests sounding with trumpets);"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"when the trumpeters and singers were as one, to make one sound to be heard in praising and thanking the LORD; and when they lifted up their voice with the trumpets and cymbals and instruments of music, and praised the LORD, saying,"],[1,"\u201cFor he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever!\u201d"],[0,"then the house was filled with a cloud, even the LORD\u2019s house,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"so that the priests could not stand to minister by reason of the cloud; for the LORD\u2019s glory filled God\u2019s house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon said, \u201cThe LORD has said that he would dwell in the thick darkness."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But I have built you a house and home, a place for you to dwell in forever.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The king turned his face, and blessed all the assembly of Israel; and all the assembly of Israel stood."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBlessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, who spoke with his mouth to David my father, and has with his hands fulfilled it, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u2018Since the day that I brought my people out of the land of Egypt, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Israel to build a house in, that my name might be there, and I chose no man to be prince over my people Israel;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but now I have chosen Jerusalem, that my name might be there; and I have chosen David to be over my people Israel.\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now it was in the heart of David my father to build a house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But the LORD said to David my father, \u2018Whereas it was in your heart to build a house for my name, you did well that it was in your heart;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"nevertheless you shall not build the house, but your son who will come out of your body, he shall build the house for my name.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD has performed his word that he spoke; for I have risen up in the place of David my father, and sit on the throne of Israel, as the LORD promised, and have built the house for the name of the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"There I have set the ark, in which is the LORD\u2019s covenant, which he made with the children of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He stood before the LORD\u2019s altar in the presence of all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"(for Solomon had made a bronze platform, five cubits long, five cubits wide, and three cubits high, and had set it in the middle of the court; and he stood on it, and knelt down on his knees before all the assembly of Israel, and spread out his hands toward heaven)."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cLORD, the God of Israel, there is no God like you in heaven or on earth\u2014you who keep covenant and loving kindness with your servants who walk before you with all their heart;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"who have kept with your servant David my father that which you promised him. Yes, you spoke with your mouth, and have fulfilled it with your hand, as it is today."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore, LORD, the God of Israel, keep with your servant David my father that which you have promised him, saying, \u2018There shall not fail you a man in my sight to sit on the throne of Israel, if only your children take heed to their way, to walk in my law as you have walked before me.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now therefore, LORD, the God of Israel, let your word be verified, which you spoke to your servant David."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut will God indeed dwell with men on the earth? Behold, heaven and the heaven of heavens can\u2019t contain you; how much less this house which I have built!"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Yet have respect for the prayer of your servant and to his supplication, LORD my God, to listen to the cry and to the prayer which your servant prays before you;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"that your eyes may be open toward this house day and night, even toward the place where you have said that you would put your name, to listen to the prayer which your servant will pray toward this place."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Listen to the petitions of your servant and of your people Israel, when they pray toward this place. Yes, hear from your dwelling place, even from heaven; and when you hear, forgive."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf a man sins against his neighbor, and an oath is laid on him to cause him to swear, and he comes and swears before your altar in this house,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"then hear from heaven, act, and judge your servants, bringing retribution to the wicked, to bring his way on his own head; and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf your people Israel are struck down before the enemy because they have sinned against you, and they turn again and confess your name, and pray and make supplication before you in this house,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"then hear from heaven, and forgive the sin of your people Israel, and bring them again to the land which you gave to them and to their fathers."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the sky is shut up and there is no rain because they have sinned against you, if they pray toward this place and confess your name, and turn from their sin when you afflict them,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"then hear in heaven, and forgive the sin of your servants, your people Israel, when you teach them the good way in which they should walk, and send rain on your land, which you have given to your people for an inheritance."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf there is famine in the land, if there is pestilence, if there is blight or mildew, locust or caterpillar; if their enemies besiege them in the land of their cities; whatever plague or whatever sickness there is\u2014"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"whatever prayer and supplication is made by any man, or by all your people Israel, who will each know his own plague and his own sorrow, and shall spread out his hands toward this house,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"then hear from heaven your dwelling place and forgive, and give to every man according to all his ways, whose heart you know (for you, even you only, know the hearts of the children of men),"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"that they may fear you, to walk in your ways as long as they live in the land which you gave to our fathers."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover, concerning the foreigner, who is not of your people Israel, when he comes from a far country for your great name\u2019s sake and your mighty hand and your outstretched arm, when they come and pray toward this house,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"then hear from heaven, even from your dwelling place, and do according to all that the foreigner calls to you for; that all the peoples of the earth may know your name and fear you, as do your people Israel, and that they may know that this house which I have built is called by your name."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf your people go out to battle against their enemies, by whatever way you send them, and they pray to you toward this city which you have chosen, and the house which I have built for your name;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"then hear from heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf they sin against you (for there is no man who doesn\u2019t sin), and you are angry with them and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captive to a land far off or near;"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"yet if they come to their senses in the land where they are carried captive, and turn again, and make supplication to you in the land of their captivity, saying, \u2018We have sinned, we have done perversely, and have dealt wickedly;\u2019"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"if they return to you with all their heart and with all their soul in the land of their captivity, where they have been taken captive, and pray toward their land which you gave to their fathers, and the city which you have chosen, and toward the house which I have built for your name;"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"then hear from heaven, even from your dwelling place, their prayer and their petitions, and maintain their cause, and forgive your people who have sinned against you."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, my God, let, I beg you, your eyes be open, and let your ears be attentive to the prayer that is made in this place."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore arise, LORD God, into your resting place, you, and the ark of your strength. Let your priests, LORD God, be clothed with salvation, and let your saints rejoice in goodness."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cLORD God, don\u2019t turn away the face of your anointed. Remember your loving kindnesses to David your servant.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Solomon had finished praying, fire came down from heaven and consumed the burnt offering and the sacrifices; and the LORD\u2019s glory filled the house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The priests could not enter into the LORD\u2019s house, because the LORD\u2019s glory filled the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All the children of Israel looked on, when the fire came down, and the LORD\u2019s glory was on the house. They bowed themselves with their faces to the ground on the pavement, worshiped, and gave thanks to the LORD, saying,"],[1,"\u201cFor he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever!\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king and all the people offered sacrifices before the LORD."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"King Solomon offered a sacrifice of twenty-two thousand head of cattle and a hundred twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the people dedicated God\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The priests stood, according to their positions; the Levites also with instruments of music of the LORD, which David the king had made to give thanks to the LORD, when David praised by their ministry, saying \u201cFor his loving kindness endures forever.\u201d The priests sounded trumpets before them; and all Israel stood."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Solomon made the middle of the court that was before the LORD\u2019s house holy; for there he offered the burnt offerings and the fat of the peace offerings, because the bronze altar which Solomon had made was not able to receive the burnt offering, the meal offering, and the fat."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So Solomon held the feast at that time for seven days, and all Israel with him, a very great assembly, from the entrance of Hamath to the brook of Egypt."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"On the eighth day, they held a solemn assembly; for they kept the dedication of the altar seven days, and the feast seven days."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"On the twenty-third day of the seventh month, he sent the people away to their tents, joyful and glad of heart for the goodness that the LORD had shown to David, to Solomon, and to Israel his people."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus Solomon finished the LORD\u2019s house and the king\u2019s house; and he successfully completed all that came into Solomon\u2019s heart to make in the LORD\u2019s house and in his own house."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD appeared to Solomon by night, and said to him, \u201cI have heard your prayer, and have chosen this place for myself for a house of sacrifice."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf I shut up the sky so that there is no rain, or if I command the locust to devour the land, or if I send pestilence among my people,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"if my people who are called by my name will humble themselves, pray, seek my face, and turn from their wicked ways, then I will hear from heaven, will forgive their sin, and will heal their land."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now my eyes will be open and my ears attentive to prayer that is made in this place."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For now I have chosen and made this house holy, that my name may be there forever; and my eyes and my heart will be there perpetually."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for you, if you will walk before me as David your father walked, and do according to all that I have commanded you, and will keep my statutes and my ordinances,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"then I will establish the throne of your kingdom, according as I covenanted with David your father, saying, \u2018There shall not fail you a man to be ruler in Israel.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But if you turn away and forsake my statutes and my commandments which I have set before you, and go and serve other gods and worship them,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"then I will pluck them up by the roots out of my land which I have given them; and this house, which I have made holy for my name, I will cast out of my sight, and I will make it a proverb and a byword among all peoples."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"This house, which is so high, everyone who passes by it will be astonished and say, \u2018Why has the LORD done this to this land and to this house?\u2019"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They shall answer, \u2018Because they abandoned the LORD, the God of their fathers, who brought them out of the land of Egypt, and took other gods, worshiped them, and served them. Therefore he has brought all this evil on them.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of twenty years, in which Solomon had built the LORD\u2019s house and his own house,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Solomon built the cities which Huram had given to Solomon, and caused the children of Israel to dwell there."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon went to Hamath Zobah, and prevailed against it."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He built Tadmor in the wilderness, and all the storage cities, which he built in Hamath."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Also he built Beth Horon the upper and Beth Horon the lower, fortified cities with walls, gates, and bars;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and Baalath, and all the storage cities that Solomon had, and all the cities for his chariots, the cities for his horsemen, and all that Solomon desired to build for his pleasure in Jerusalem, in Lebanon, and in all the land of his dominion."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"As for all the people who were left of the Hittites, the Amorites, the Perizzites, the Hivites, and the Jebusites, who were not of Israel\u2014"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"of their children who were left after them in the land, whom the children of Israel didn\u2019t consume\u2014of them Solomon conscripted forced labor to this day."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But of the children of Israel, Solomon made no servants for his work, but they were men of war, chief of his captains, and rulers of his chariots and of his horsemen."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"These were the chief officers of King Solomon, even two-hundred fifty, who ruled over the people."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Solomon brought up Pharaoh\u2019s daughter out of David\u2019s city to the house that he had built for her; for he said, \u201cMy wife shall not dwell in the house of David king of Israel, because the places where the LORD\u2019s ark has come are holy.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon offered burnt offerings to the LORD on the LORD\u2019s altar which he had built before the porch,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"even as the duty of every day required, offering according to the commandment of Moses on the Sabbaths, on the new moons, and on the set feasts, three times per year, during the feast of unleavened bread, during the feast of weeks, and during the feast of booths."]],f:["or, feast of tents (Sukkot)"]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He appointed, according to the ordinance of David his father, the divisions of the priests to their service, and the Levites to their offices, to praise and to minister before the priests, as the duty of every day required, the doorkeepers also by their divisions at every gate, for David the man of God had so commanded."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t depart from the commandment of the king to the priests and Levites concerning any matter or concerning the treasures."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Now all the work of Solomon was accomplished from the day of the foundation of the LORD\u2019s house until it was finished. So the LORD\u2019s house was completed."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Solomon went to Ezion Geber and to Eloth, on the seashore in the land of Edom."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Huram sent him ships and servants who had knowledge of the sea by the hands of his servants; and they came with the servants of Solomon to Ophir, and brought from there four hundred fifty talents of gold, and brought them to King Solomon."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 450 talents is about 13.5 metric tons"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon, she came to test Solomon with hard questions at Jerusalem, with a very great caravan, including camels that bore spices, gold in abundance, and precious stones. When she had come to Solomon, she talked with him about all that was in her heart."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Solomon answered all her questions. There wasn\u2019t anything hidden from Solomon which he didn\u2019t tell her."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When the queen of Sheba had seen the wisdom of Solomon, the house that he had built,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"the food of his table, the seating of his servants, the attendance of his ministers, their clothing, his cup bearers and their clothing, and his ascent by which he went up to the LORD\u2019s house, there was no more spirit in her."]],f:["or, she was breathless."]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to the king, \u201cIt was a true report that I heard in my own land of your acts and of your wisdom."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"However I didn\u2019t believe their words until I came, and my eyes had seen it; and behold half of the greatness of your wisdom wasn\u2019t told me. You exceed the fame that I heard!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Happy are your men, and happy are these your servants, who stand continually before you and hear your wisdom."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Blessed be the LORD your God, who delighted in you and set you on his throne to be king for the LORD your God, because your God loved Israel, to establish them forever. Therefore he made you king over them, to do justice and righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"She gave the king one hundred and twenty talents of gold, spices in great abundance, and precious stones. There was never before such spice as the queen of Sheba gave to King Solomon."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 120 talents is about 3.6 metric tons"]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The servants of Huram and the servants of Solomon, who brought gold from Ophir, also brought algum trees and precious stones."]],f:["possibly Indian sandalwood, which has nice grain and a pleasant scent and is good for woodworking"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The king used algum tree wood to make terraces for the LORD\u2019s house and for the king\u2019s house, and harps and stringed instruments for the singers. There were none like these seen before in the land of Judah."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"King Solomon gave to the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatever she asked, more than that which she had brought to the king. So she turned and went to her own land, she and her servants."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred sixty-six talents of gold,"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces, so 666 talents is about 20 metric tons"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"in addition to that which the traders and merchants brought. All the kings of Arabia and the governors of the country brought gold and silver to Solomon."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"King Solomon made two hundred large shields of beaten gold. Six hundred shekels of beaten gold went to one large shield."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.32 Troy ounces, so 600 shekels was about 6 kilograms or about 192 Troy ounces."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He made three hundred shields of beaten gold. Three hundred shekels of gold went to one shield. The king put them in the House of the Forest of Lebanon."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.32 Troy ounces, so 300 shekels was about 3 kilograms or about 96 Troy ounces."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with pure gold."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"There were six steps to the throne, with a footstool of gold, which were fastened to the throne, and armrests on either side by the place of the seat, and two lions standing beside the armrests."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other on the six steps. There was nothing like it made in any other kingdom."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"All King Solomon\u2019s drinking vessels were of gold, and all the vessels of the House of the Forest of Lebanon were of pure gold. Silver was not considered valuable in the days of Solomon."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For the king had ships that went to Tarshish with Huram\u2019s servants. Once every three years, the ships of Tarshish came bringing gold, silver, ivory, apes, and peacocks."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"So King Solomon exceeded all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"All the kings of the earth sought the presence of Solomon to hear his wisdom, which God had put in his heart."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They each brought tribute: vessels of silver, vessels of gold, clothing, armor, spices, horses, and mules every year."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Solomon had four thousand stalls for horses and chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen that he stationed in the chariot cities and with the king at Jerusalem."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He ruled over all the kings from the River even to the land of the Philistines, and to the border of Egypt."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The king made silver as common in Jerusalem as stones, and he made cedars to be as abundant as the sycamore trees that are in the lowland."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They brought horses for Solomon out of Egypt and out of all lands."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Solomon, first and last, aren\u2019t they written in the history of Nathan the prophet, and in the prophecy of Ahijah the Shilonite, and in the visions of Iddo the seer concerning Jeroboam the son of Nebat?"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Solomon reigned in Jerusalem over all Israel forty years."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Solomon slept with his fathers, and he was buried in his father David\u2019s city; and Rehoboam his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Rehoboam went to Shechem, for all Israel had come to Shechem to make him king."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When Jeroboam the son of Nebat heard of it (for he was in Egypt, where he had fled from the presence of King Solomon), Jeroboam returned out of Egypt."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They sent and called him; and Jeroboam and all Israel came, and they spoke to Rehoboam, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cYour father made our yoke grievous. Now therefore make the grievous service of your father and his heavy yoke which he put on us, lighter, and we will serve you.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cCome again to me after three days.\u201d"],[0,"So the people departed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"King Rehoboam took counsel with the old men, who had stood before Solomon his father while he yet lived, saying, \u201cWhat counsel do you give me about how to answer these people?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They spoke to him, saying, \u201cIf you are kind to these people, please them, and speak good words to them, then they will be your servants forever.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"But he abandoned the counsel of the old men which they had given him, and took counsel with the young men who had grown up with him, who stood before him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat counsel do you give, that we may give an answer to these people, who have spoken to me, saying, \u2018Make the yoke that your father put on us lighter\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The young men who had grown up with him spoke to him, saying, \u201cThus you shall tell the people who spoke to you, saying, \u2018Your father made our yoke heavy, but make it lighter on us;\u2019 thus you shall say to them, \u2018My little finger is thicker than my father\u2019s waist."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now whereas my father burdened you with a heavy yoke, I will add to your yoke. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jeroboam and all the people came to Rehoboam the third day, as the king asked, saying, \u201cCome to me again the third day.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The king answered them roughly; and King Rehoboam abandoned the counsel of the old men,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and spoke to them after the counsel of the young men, saying, \u201cMy father made your yoke heavy, but I will add to it. My father chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king didn\u2019t listen to the people; for it was brought about by God, that the LORD might establish his word, which he spoke by Ahijah the Shilonite to Jeroboam the son of Nebat."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When all Israel saw that the king didn\u2019t listen to them, the people answered the king, saying, \u201cWhat portion do we have in David? We don\u2019t have an inheritance in the son of Jesse! Every man to your tents, Israel! Now see to your own house, David.\u201d So all Israel departed to their tents."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But as for the children of Israel who lived in the cities of Judah, Rehoboam reigned over them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then King Rehoboam sent Hadoram, who was over the men subject to forced labor; and the children of Israel stoned him to death with stones. King Rehoboam hurried to get himself up to his chariot, to flee to Jerusalem."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"So Israel rebelled against David\u2019s house to this day."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Rehoboam had come to Jerusalem, he assembled the house of Judah and Benjamin, one hundred eighty thousand chosen men who were warriors, to fight against Israel, to bring the kingdom again to Rehoboam."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But the LORD\u2019s word came to Shemaiah the man of God, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Rehoboam the son of Solomon, king of Judah, and to all Israel in Judah and Benjamin, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u2018The LORD says, \u201cYou shall not go up, nor fight against your brothers! Every man return to his house; for this thing is of me.\u201d\u2019\u201d So they listened to the LORD\u2019s words, and returned from going against Jeroboam."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Rehoboam lived in Jerusalem, and built cities for defense in Judah."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He built Bethlehem, Etam, Tekoa,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Beth Zur, Soco, Adullam,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Gath, Mareshah, Ziph,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Adoraim, Lachish, Azekah,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Zorah, Aijalon, and Hebron, which are fortified cities in Judah and in Benjamin."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He fortified the strongholds and put captains in them with stores of food, oil and wine."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He put shields and spears in every city, and made them exceedingly strong. Judah and Benjamin belonged to him."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The priests and the Levites who were in all Israel stood with him out of all their territory."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For the Levites left their pasture lands and their possessions, and came to Judah and Jerusalem; for Jeroboam and his sons cast them off, that they should not execute the priest\u2019s office to the LORD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He himself appointed priests for the high places, for the male goat and calf idols which he had made."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"After them, out of all the tribes of Israel, those who set their hearts to seek the LORD, the God of Israel, came to Jerusalem to sacrifice to the LORD, the God of their fathers."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So they strengthened the kingdom of Judah and made Rehoboam the son of Solomon strong for three years, for they walked three years in the way of David and Solomon."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Rehoboam took a wife for himself, Mahalath the daughter of Jerimoth the son of David and of Abihail the daughter of Eliab the son of Jesse."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"She bore him sons: Jeush, Shemariah, and Zaham."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"After her, he took Maacah the granddaughter of Absalom; and she bore him Abijah, Attai, Ziza, and Shelomith."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Rehoboam loved Maacah the granddaughter of Absalom above all his wives and his concubines; for he took eighteen wives and sixty concubines, and became the father of twenty-eight sons and sixty daughters."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Rehoboam appointed Abijah the son of Maacah to be chief, the prince among his brothers, for he intended to make him king."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He dealt wisely, and dispersed some of his sons throughout all the lands of Judah and Benjamin, to every fortified city. He gave them food in abundance; and he sought many wives for them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the kingdom of Rehoboam was established and he was strong, he abandoned the LORD\u2019s law, and all Israel with him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In the fifth year of King Rehoboam, Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem, because they had trespassed against the LORD,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"with twelve hundred chariots and sixty thousand horsemen. The people were without number who came with him out of Egypt: the Lubim, the Sukkiim, and the Ethiopians."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He took the fortified cities which belonged to Judah, and came to Jerusalem."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now Shemaiah the prophet came to Rehoboam and to the princes of Judah, who were gathered together to Jerusalem because of Shishak, and said to them, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018You have forsaken me, therefore I have also left you in the hand of Shishak.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the princes of Israel and the king humbled themselves; and they said, \u201cThe LORD is righteous.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD saw that they humbled themselves, the LORD\u2019s word came to Shemaiah, saying, \u201cThey have humbled themselves. I will not destroy them, but I will grant them some deliverance, and my wrath won\u2019t be poured out on Jerusalem by the hand of Shishak."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Nevertheless they will be his servants, that they may know my service, and the service of the kingdoms of the countries.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"So Shishak king of Egypt came up against Jerusalem and took away the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house and the treasures of the king\u2019s house. He took it all away. He also took away the shields of gold which Solomon had made."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"King Rehoboam made shields of bronze in their place, and committed them to the hands of the captains of the guard, who kept the door of the king\u2019s house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"As often as the king entered into the LORD\u2019s house, the guard came and bore them, then brought them back into the guard room."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When he humbled himself, the LORD\u2019s wrath turned from him, so as not to destroy him altogether. Moreover, there were good things found in Judah."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"So King Rehoboam strengthened himself in Jerusalem and reigned; for Rehoboam was forty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Jerusalem, the city which the LORD had chosen out of all the tribes of Israel to put his name there. His mother\u2019s name was Naamah the Ammonitess."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil, because he didn\u2019t set his heart to seek the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the acts of Rehoboam, first and last, aren\u2019t they written in the histories of Shemaiah the prophet and of Iddo the seer, in the genealogies? There were wars between Rehoboam and Jeroboam continually."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Rehoboam slept with his fathers, and was buried in David\u2019s city; and Abijah his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the eighteenth year of King Jeroboam, Abijah began to reign over Judah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He reigned three years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Micaiah the daughter of Uriel of Gibeah. There was war between Abijah and Jeroboam."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Abijah joined battle with an army of valiant men of war, even four hundred thousand chosen men; and Jeroboam set the battle in array against him with eight hundred thousand chosen men, who were mighty men of valor."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Abijah stood up on Mount Zemaraim, which is in the hill country of Ephraim, and said, \u201cHear me, Jeroboam and all Israel:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ought you not to know that the LORD, the God of Israel, gave the kingdom over Israel to David forever, even to him and to his sons by a covenant of salt?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Yet Jeroboam the son of Nebat, the servant of Solomon the son of David, rose up, and rebelled against his lord."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Worthless men were gathered to him, wicked fellows who strengthened themselves against Rehoboam the son of Solomon, when Rehoboam was young and tender hearted, and could not withstand them."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow you intend to withstand the kingdom of the LORD in the hand of the sons of David. You are a great multitude, and the golden calves which Jeroboam made you for gods are with you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Haven\u2019t you driven out the priests of the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the Levites, and made priests for yourselves according to the ways of the peoples of other lands? Whoever comes to consecrate himself with a young bull and seven rams may be a priest of those who are no gods."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut as for us, the LORD is our God, and we have not forsaken him. We have priests serving the LORD, the sons of Aaron, and the Levites in their work."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They burn to the LORD every morning and every evening burnt offerings and sweet incense. They also set the show bread in order on the pure table, and care for the gold lamp stand with its lamps, to burn every evening; for we keep the instruction of the LORD our God, but you have forsaken him."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Behold, God is with us at our head, and his priests with the trumpets of alarm to sound an alarm against you. Children of Israel, don\u2019t fight against the LORD, the God of your fathers; for you will not prosper.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jeroboam caused an ambush to come about behind them; so they were before Judah, and the ambush was behind them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When Judah looked back, behold, the battle was before and behind them; and they cried to the LORD, and the priests sounded with the trumpets."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then the men of Judah gave a shout. As the men of Judah shouted, God struck Jeroboam and all Israel before Abijah and Judah."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The children of Israel fled before Judah, and God delivered them into their hand."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Abijah and his people killed them with a great slaughter, so five hundred thousand chosen men of Israel fell down slain."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Thus the children of Israel were brought under at that time, and the children of Judah prevailed, because they relied on the LORD, the God of their fathers."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Abijah pursued Jeroboam, and took cities from him: Bethel with its villages, Jeshanah with its villages, and Ephron with its villages."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Jeroboam didn\u2019t recover strength again in the days of Abijah. The LORD struck him, and he died."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But Abijah grew mighty and took for himself fourteen wives, and became the father of twenty-two sons and sixteen daughters."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The rest of the acts of Abijah, his ways, and his sayings are written in the commentary of the prophet Iddo."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"So Abijah slept with his fathers, and they buried him in David\u2019s city; and Asa his son reigned in his place. In his days, the land was quiet ten years."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Asa did that which was good and right in the LORD his God\u2019s eyes,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"for he took away the foreign altars and the high places, broke down the pillars, cut down the Asherah poles,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and commanded Judah to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, and to obey his law and command."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Also he took away out of all the cities of Judah the high places and the sun images; and the kingdom was quiet before him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He built fortified cities in Judah; for the land was quiet, and he had no war in those years, because the LORD had given him rest."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For he said to Judah, \u201cLet\u2019s build these cities and make walls around them, with towers, gates, and bars. The land is yet before us, because we have sought the LORD our God. We have sought him, and he has given us rest on every side.\u201d So they built and prospered."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Asa had an army of three hundred thousand out of Judah who bore bucklers and spears, and two hundred eighty thousand out of Benjamin who bore shields and drew bows. All these were mighty men of valor."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Zerah the Ethiopian came out against them with an army of a million troops and three hundred chariots, and he came to Mareshah."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Then Asa went out to meet him, and they set the battle in array in the valley of Zephathah at Mareshah."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Asa cried to the LORD his God, and said, \u201cLORD, there is no one besides you to help, between the mighty and him who has no strength. Help us, LORD our God; for we rely on you, and in your name we have come against this multitude. LORD, you are our God. Don\u2019t let man prevail against you.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So the LORD struck the Ethiopians before Asa and before Judah; and the Ethiopians fled."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Asa and the people who were with him pursued them to Gerar. So many of the Ethiopians fell that they could not recover themselves, for they were destroyed before the LORD and before his army. Judah\u2019s army carried away very much booty."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They struck all the cities around Gerar, for the fear of the LORD came on them. They plundered all the cities, for there was much plunder in them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They also struck the tents of those who had livestock, and carried away sheep and camels in abundance, then returned to Jerusalem."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The Spirit of God came on Azariah the son of Oded."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He went out to meet Asa, and said to him, \u201cHear me, Asa, and all Judah and Benjamin! The LORD is with you while you are with him; and if you seek him, he will be found by you; but if you forsake him, he will forsake you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now for a long time Israel was without the true God, without a teaching priest, and without law."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But when in their distress they turned to the LORD, the God of Israel, and sought him, he was found by them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"In those times there was no peace to him who went out, nor to him who came in; but great troubles were on all the inhabitants of the lands."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They were broken in pieces, nation against nation, and city against city; for God troubled them with all adversity."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But you be strong! Don\u2019t let your hands be slack, for your work will be rewarded.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"When Asa heard these words and the prophecy of Oded the prophet, he took courage, and put away the abominations out of all the land of Judah and Benjamin, and out of the cities which he had taken from the hill country of Ephraim; and he renewed the LORD\u2019s altar that was before the LORD\u2019s porch."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He gathered all Judah and Benjamin, and those who lived with them out of Ephraim, Manasseh, and Simeon; for they came to him out of Israel in abundance when they saw that the LORD his God was with him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So they gathered themselves together at Jerusalem in the third month, in the fifteenth year of Asa\u2019s reign."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They sacrificed to the LORD in that day, from the plunder which they had brought, seven hundred head of cattle and seven thousand sheep."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They entered into the covenant to seek the LORD, the God of their fathers, with all their heart and with all their soul;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and that whoever would not seek the LORD, the God of Israel, should be put to death, whether small or great, whether man or woman."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They swore to the LORD with a loud voice, with shouting, with trumpets, and with cornets."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"All Judah rejoiced at the oath, for they had sworn with all their heart and sought him with their whole desire; and he was found by them. Then the LORD gave them rest all around."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Also Maacah, the mother of Asa the king, he removed from being queen mother, because she had made an abominable image for an Asherah; so Asa cut down her image, ground it into dust, and burned it at the brook Kidron."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But the high places were not taken away out of Israel; nevertheless the heart of Asa was perfect all his days."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He brought the things that his father had dedicated and that he himself had dedicated, silver, gold, and vessels into God\u2019s house."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There was no more war to the thirty-fifth year of Asa\u2019s reign."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the thirty-sixth year of Asa\u2019s reign, Baasha king of Israel went up against Judah, and built Ramah, that he might not allow anyone to go out or come in to Asa king of Judah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Asa brought out silver and gold out of the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house and of the king\u2019s house, and sent to Ben Hadad king of Syria, who lived at Damascus, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cLet there be a treaty between me and you, as there was between my father and your father. Behold, I have sent you silver and gold. Go, break your treaty with Baasha king of Israel, that he may depart from me.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Ben Hadad listened to King Asa, and sent the captains of his armies against the cities of Israel; and they struck Ijon, Dan, Abel Maim, and all the storage cities of Naphtali."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When Baasha heard of it, he stopped building Ramah, and let his work cease."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then Asa the king took all Judah, and they carried away the stones and timber of Ramah, with which Baasha had built; and he built Geba and Mizpah with them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time Hanani the seer came to Asa king of Judah, and said to him, \u201cBecause you have relied on the king of Syria, and have not relied on the LORD your God, therefore the army of the king of Syria has escaped out of your hand."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Weren\u2019t the Ethiopians and the Lubim a huge army, with chariots and exceedingly many horsemen? Yet, because you relied on the LORD, he delivered them into your hand."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For the LORD\u2019s eyes run back and forth throughout the whole earth, to show himself strong in the behalf of them whose heart is perfect toward him. You have done foolishly in this; for from now on you will have wars.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Asa was angry with the seer, and put him in the prison; for he was in a rage with him because of this thing. Asa oppressed some of the people at the same time."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the acts of Asa, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"In the thirty-ninth year of his reign, Asa was diseased in his feet. His disease was exceedingly great; yet in his disease he didn\u2019t seek the LORD, but just the physicians."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Asa slept with his fathers, and died in the forty-first year of his reign."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They buried him in his own tomb, which he had dug out for himself in David\u2019s city, and laid him in the bed which was filled with sweet odors and various kinds of spices prepared by the perfumers\u2019 art; and they made a very great fire for him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat his son reigned in his place, and strengthened himself against Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He placed forces in all the fortified cities of Judah, and set garrisons in the land of Judah and in the cities of Ephraim, which Asa his father had taken."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD was with Jehoshaphat, because he walked in the first ways of his father David, and didn\u2019t seek the Baals,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"but sought the God of his father, and walked in his commandments, and not in the ways of Israel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD established the kingdom in his hand. All Judah brought tribute to Jehoshaphat, and he had riches and honor in abundance."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"His heart was lifted up in the ways of the LORD. Furthermore, he took away the high places and the Asherah poles out of Judah."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Also in the third year of his reign he sent his princes, even Ben Hail, Obadiah, Zechariah, Nethanel, and Micaiah, to teach in the cities of Judah;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and with them Levites, even Shemaiah, Nethaniah, Zebadiah, Asahel, Shemiramoth, Jehonathan, Adonijah, Tobijah, and Tobadonijah, the Levites; and with them Elishama and Jehoram, the priests."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They taught in Judah, having the book of the LORD\u2019s law with them. They went about throughout all the cities of Judah and taught among the people."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The fear of the LORD fell on all the kingdoms of the lands that were around Judah, so that they made no war against Jehoshaphat."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Some of the Philistines brought Jehoshaphat presents and silver for tribute. The Arabians also brought him flocks: seven thousand seven hundred rams and seven thousand seven hundred male goats."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat grew great exceedingly; and he built fortresses and store cities in Judah."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He had many works in the cities of Judah; and men of war, mighty men of valor, in Jerusalem."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"This was the numbering of them according to their fathers\u2019 houses: From Judah, the captains of thousands: Adnah the captain, and with him three hundred thousand mighty men of valor;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and next to him Jehohanan the captain, and with him two hundred eighty thousand;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and next to him Amasiah the son of Zichri, who willingly offered himself to the LORD, and with him two hundred thousand mighty men of valor."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"From Benjamin: Eliada, a mighty man of valor, and with him two hundred thousand armed with bow and shield;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and next to him Jehozabad, and with him one hundred eighty thousand ready and prepared for war."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"These were those who waited on the king, in addition to those whom the king put in the fortified cities throughout all Judah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jehoshaphat had riches and honor in abundance; and he allied himself with Ahab."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"After some years, he went down to Ahab to Samaria. Ahab killed sheep and cattle for him in abundance, and for the people who were with him, and moved him to go up with him to Ramoth Gilead."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Ahab king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat king of Judah, \u201cWill you go with me to Ramoth Gilead?\u201d"],[0,"He answered him, \u201cI am as you are, and my people as your people. We will be with you in the war.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, \u201cPlease inquire first for the LORD\u2019s word.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king of Israel gathered the prophets together, four hundred men, and said to them, \u201cShall we go to Ramoth Gilead to battle, or shall I forbear?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cGo up, for God will deliver it into the hand of the king.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jehoshaphat said, \u201cIsn\u2019t there here a prophet of the LORD besides, that we may inquire of him?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cThere is yet one man by whom we may inquire of the LORD; but I hate him, for he never prophesies good concerning me, but always evil. He is Micaiah the son of Imla.\u201d"],[0,"Jehoshaphat said, \u201cDon\u2019t let the king say so.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king of Israel called an officer, and said, \u201cGet Micaiah the son of Imla quickly.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah each sat on his throne, arrayed in their robes, and they were sitting in an open place at the entrance of the gate of Samaria; and all the prophets were prophesying before them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah made himself horns of iron and said, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018With these you shall push the Syrians, until they are consumed.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"All the prophets prophesied so, saying, \u201cGo up to Ramoth Gilead, and prosper; for the LORD will deliver it into the hand of the king.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The messenger who went to call Micaiah spoke to him, saying, \u201cBehold, the words of the prophets declare good to the king with one mouth. Let your word therefore, please be like one of theirs, and speak good.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cAs the LORD lives, I will say what my God says.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had come to the king, the king said to him, \u201cMicaiah, shall we go to Ramoth Gilead to battle, or shall I forbear?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cGo up, and prosper. They shall be delivered into your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to him, \u201cHow many times shall I adjure you that you speak to me nothing but the truth in the LORD\u2019s name?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI saw all Israel scattered on the mountains, as sheep that have no shepherd. The LORD said, \u2018These have no master. Let them each return to his house in peace.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cDidn\u2019t I tell you that he would not prophesy good concerning me, but evil?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cTherefore hear the LORD\u2019s word: I saw the LORD sitting on his throne, and all the army of heaven standing on his right hand and on his left."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u2018Who will entice Ahab king of Israel, that he may go up and fall at Ramoth Gilead?\u2019 One spoke saying in this way, and another saying in that way."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"A spirit came out, stood before the LORD, and said, \u2018I will entice him.\u2019"],[0,"\u201cThe LORD said to him, \u2018How?\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said, \u2018I will go, and will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets.\u2019"],[0,"\u201cHe said, \u2018You will entice him, and will prevail also. Go and do so.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore, behold, the LORD has put a lying spirit in the mouth of these your prophets; and the LORD has spoken evil concerning you.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah came near, and struck Micaiah on the cheek, and said, \u201cWhich way did the LORD\u2019s Spirit go from me to speak to you?\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cBehold, you shall see on that day, when you go into an inner room to hide yourself.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said, \u201cTake Micaiah, and carry him back to Amon the governor of the city, and to Joash the king\u2019s son;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018The king says, \u201cPut this fellow in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I return in peace.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Micaiah said, \u201cIf you return at all in peace, the LORD has not spoken by me.\u201d He said, \u201cListen, you people, all of you!\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah went up to Ramoth Gilead."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The king of Israel said to Jehoshaphat, \u201cI will disguise myself, and go into the battle; but you put on your robes.\u201d So the king of Israel disguised himself; and they went into the battle."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Now the king of Syria had commanded the captains of his chariots, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t fight with small nor great, except only with the king of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"When the captains of the chariots saw Jehoshaphat, they said, \u201cIt is the king of Israel!\u201d Therefore they turned around to fight against him. But Jehoshaphat cried out, and the LORD helped him; and God moved them to depart from him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"When the captains of the chariots saw that it was not the king of Israel, they turned back from pursuing him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"A certain man drew his bow at random, and struck the king of Israel between the joints of the armor. Therefore he said to the driver of the chariot, \u201cTurn around and carry me out of the battle, for I am severely wounded.\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The battle increased that day. However, the king of Israel propped himself up in his chariot against the Syrians until the evening; and at about sunset, he died."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat the king of Judah returned to his house in peace to Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jehu the son of Hanani the seer went out to meet him, and said to King Jehoshaphat, \u201cShould you help the wicked, and love those who hate the LORD? Because of this, wrath is on you from before the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Nevertheless there are good things found in you, in that you have put away the Asheroth out of the land, and have set your heart to seek God.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat lived at Jerusalem; and he went out again among the people from Beersheba to the hill country of Ephraim, and brought them back to the LORD, the God of their fathers."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He set judges in the land throughout all the fortified cities of Judah, city by city,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and said to the judges, \u201cConsider what you do, for you don\u2019t judge for man, but for the LORD; and he is with you in the judgment."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now therefore let the fear of the LORD be on you. Take heed and do it; for there is no iniquity with the LORD our God, nor respect of persons, nor taking of bribes.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover in Jerusalem Jehoshaphat appointed certain Levites, priests, and heads of the fathers\u2019 households of Israel to give judgment for the LORD and for controversies. They returned to Jerusalem."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He commanded them, saying, \u201cYou shall do this in the fear of the LORD, faithfully, and with a perfect heart."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Whenever any controversy comes to you from your brothers who dwell in their cities, between blood and blood, between law and commandment, statutes and ordinances, you must warn them, that they not be guilty toward the LORD, and so wrath come on you and on your brothers. Do this, and you will not be guilty."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Behold, Amariah the chief priest is over you in all matters of the LORD; and Zebadiah the son of Ishmael, the ruler of the house of Judah, in all the king\u2019s matters. Also the Levites shall be officers before you. Deal courageously, and may the LORD be with the good.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, the children of Moab, the children of Ammon, and with them some of the Meunites, came against Jehoshaphat to battle."]],f:["The LXX reads Meunites. Heb. reads Ammonites."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then some came who told Jehoshaphat, saying, \u201cA great multitude is coming against you from beyond the sea from Syria. Behold, they are in Hazazon Tamar\u201d (that is, En Gedi)."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat was alarmed, and set himself to seek the LORD. He proclaimed a fast throughout all Judah."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Judah gathered themselves together to seek help from the LORD. They came out of all the cities of Judah to seek the LORD."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat stood in the assembly of Judah and Jerusalem, in the LORD\u2019s house, before the new court;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and he said, \u201cLORD, the God of our fathers, aren\u2019t you God in heaven? Aren\u2019t you ruler over all the kingdoms of the nations? Power and might are in your hand, so that no one is able to withstand you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t you, our God, drive out the inhabitants of this land before your people Israel, and give it to the offspring of Abraham your friend forever?"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They lived in it, and have built you a sanctuary in it for your name, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u2018If evil comes on us\u2014the sword, judgment, pestilence, or famine\u2014we will stand before this house, and before you (for your name is in this house), and cry to you in our affliction, and you will hear and save.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now, behold, the children of Ammon and Moab and Mount Seir, whom you would not let Israel invade when they came out of the land of Egypt, but they turned away from them, and didn\u2019t destroy them;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"behold, how they reward us, to come to cast us out of your possession, which you have given us to inherit."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Our God, will you not judge them? For we have no might against this great company that comes against us. We don\u2019t know what to do, but our eyes are on you.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"All Judah stood before the LORD, with their little ones, their wives, and their children."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s Spirit came on Jahaziel the son of Zechariah, the son of Benaiah, the son of Jeiel, the son of Mattaniah, the Levite, of the sons of Asaph, in the middle of the assembly;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and he said, \u201cListen, all Judah, and you inhabitants of Jerusalem, and you, King Jehoshaphat. The LORD says to you, \u2018Don\u2019t be afraid, and don\u2019t be dismayed because of this great multitude; for the battle is not yours, but God\u2019s."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Tomorrow, go down against them. Behold, they are coming up by the ascent of Ziz. You will find them at the end of the valley, before the wilderness of Jeruel."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You will not need to fight this battle. Set yourselves, stand still, and see the salvation of the LORD with you, O Judah and Jerusalem. Don\u2019t be afraid, nor be dismayed. Go out against them tomorrow, for the LORD is with you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat bowed his head with his face to the ground; and all Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem fell down before the LORD, worshiping the LORD."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The Levites, of the children of the Kohathites and of the children of the Korahites, stood up to praise the LORD, the God of Israel, with an exceedingly loud voice."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"They rose early in the morning and went out into the wilderness of Tekoa. As they went out, Jehoshaphat stood and said, \u201cListen to me, Judah and you inhabitants of Jerusalem! Believe in the LORD your God, so you will be established! Believe his prophets, so you will prosper.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had taken counsel with the people, he appointed those who were to sing to the LORD and give praise in holy array as they go out before the army, and say, \u201cGive thanks to the LORD, for his loving kindness endures forever.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When they began to sing and to praise, the LORD set ambushers against the children of Ammon, Moab, and Mount Seir, who had come against Judah; and they were struck."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For the children of Ammon and Moab stood up against the inhabitants of Mount Seir to utterly kill and destroy them. When they had finished the inhabitants of Seir, everyone helped to destroy each other."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When Judah came to the place overlooking the wilderness, they looked at the multitude; and behold, they were dead bodies fallen to the earth, and there were none who escaped."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When Jehoshaphat and his people came to take their plunder, they found among them in abundance both riches and dead bodies with precious jewels, which they stripped off for themselves, more than they could carry away. They took plunder for three days, it was so much."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"On the fourth day, they assembled themselves in Beracah Valley, for there they blessed the LORD. Therefore the name of that place was called \u201cBeracah Valley\u201d to this day."]],f:["\u201cBeracah\u201d means \u201cblessing\u201d."]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Then they returned, every man of Judah and Jerusalem, with Jehoshaphat in front of them, to go again to Jerusalem with joy; for the LORD had made them to rejoice over their enemies."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They came to Jerusalem with stringed instruments, harps, and trumpets to the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The fear of God was on all the kingdoms of the countries when they heard that the LORD fought against the enemies of Israel."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"So the realm of Jehoshaphat was quiet, for his God gave him rest all around."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jehoshaphat reigned over Judah. He was thirty-five years old when he began to reign. He reigned twenty-five years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Azubah the daughter of Shilhi."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He walked in the way of Asa his father, and didn\u2019t turn away from it, doing that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"However the high places were not taken away, and the people had still not set their hearts on the God of their fathers."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jehoshaphat, first and last, behold, they are written in the history of Jehu the son of Hanani, which is included in the book of the kings of Israel."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Jehoshaphat king of Judah joined himself with Ahaziah king of Israel. The same did very wickedly."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He joined himself with him to make ships to go to Tarshish. They made the ships in Ezion Geber."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Then Eliezer the son of Dodavahu of Mareshah prophesied against Jehoshaphat, saying, \u201cBecause you have joined yourself with Ahaziah, the LORD has destroyed your works.\u201d The ships were wrecked, so that they were not able to go to Tarshish."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoshaphat slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in David\u2019s city; and Jehoram his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He had brothers, the sons of Jehoshaphat: Azariah, Jehiel, Zechariah, Azariah, Michael, and Shephatiah. All these were the sons of Jehoshaphat king of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Their father gave them great gifts of silver, of gold, and of precious things, with fortified cities in Judah; but he gave the kingdom to Jehoram, because he was the firstborn."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now when Jehoram had risen up over the kingdom of his father, and had strengthened himself, he killed all his brothers with the sword, and also some of the princes of Israel."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jehoram was thirty-two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eight years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He walked in the way of the kings of Israel, as did Ahab\u2019s house, for he had Ahab\u2019s daughter as his wife. He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"However the LORD would not destroy David\u2019s house, because of the covenant that he had made with David, and as he promised to give a lamp to him and to his children always."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"In his days Edom revolted from under the hand of Judah, and made a king over themselves."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Jehoram went there with his captains and all his chariots with him. He rose up by night and struck the Edomites who surrounded him, along with the captains of the chariots."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So Edom has been in revolt from under the hand of Judah to this day. Then Libnah revolted at the same time from under his hand, because he had forsaken the LORD, the God of his fathers."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover he made high places in the mountains of Judah, and made the inhabitants of Jerusalem play the prostitute, and led Judah astray."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"A letter came to him from Elijah the prophet, saying, \u201cthe LORD, the God of David your father, says, \u2018Because you have not walked in the ways of Jehoshaphat your father, nor in the ways of Asa king of Judah,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but have walked in the way of the kings of Israel, and have made Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem to play the prostitute like Ahab\u2019s house did, and also have slain your brothers of your father\u2019s house, who were better than yourself,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"behold, the LORD will strike your people with a great plague, including your children, your wives, and all your possessions;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and you will have great sickness with a disease of your bowels, until your bowels fall out by reason of the sickness, day by day.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD stirred up against Jehoram the spirit of the Philistines and of the Arabians who are beside the Ethiopians;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and they came up against Judah, broke into it, and carried away all the possessions that were found in the king\u2019s house, including his sons and his wives, so that there was no son left to him except Jehoahaz, the youngest of his sons."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"After all this the LORD struck him in his bowels with an incurable disease."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"In process of time, at the end of two years, his bowels fell out by reason of his sickness, and he died of severe diseases. His people made no burning for him, like the burning of his fathers."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He was thirty-two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem eight years. He departed with no one\u2019s regret. They buried him in David\u2019s city, but not in the tombs of the kings."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The inhabitants of Jerusalem made Ahaziah his youngest son king in his place, because the band of men who came with the Arabians to the camp had slain all the oldest. So Ahaziah the son of Jehoram king of Judah reigned."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Ahaziah was forty-two years old when he began to reign, and he reigned one year in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Athaliah the daughter of Omri."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He also walked in the ways of Ahab\u2019s house, because his mother was his counselor in acting wickedly."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, as did Ahab\u2019s house, for they were his counselors after the death of his father, to his destruction."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He also followed their counsel, and went with Jehoram the son of Ahab king of Israel to war against Hazael king of Syria at Ramoth Gilead; and the Syrians wounded Joram."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He returned to be healed in Jezreel of the wounds which they had given him at Ramah, when he fought against Hazael king of Syria. Azariah the son of Jehoram, king of Judah, went down to see Jehoram the son of Ahab in Jezreel, because he was sick."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the destruction of Ahaziah was of God, in that he went to Joram; for when he had come, he went out with Jehoram against Jehu the son of Nimshi, whom the LORD had anointed to cut off Ahab\u2019s house."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When Jehu was executing judgment on Ahab\u2019s house, he found the princes of Judah and the sons of the brothers of Ahaziah serving Ahaziah, and killed them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He sought Ahaziah, and they caught him (now he was hiding in Samaria), and they brought him to Jehu and killed him; and they buried him, for they said, \u201cHe is the son of Jehoshaphat, who sought the LORD with all his heart.\u201d The house of Ahaziah had no power to hold the kingdom."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Athaliah the mother of Ahaziah saw that her son was dead, she arose and destroyed all the royal offspring of the house of Judah."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But Jehoshabeath, the king\u2019s daughter, took Joash the son of Ahaziah, and stealthily rescued him from among the king\u2019s sons who were slain, and put him and his nurse in the bedroom. So Jehoshabeath, the daughter of King Jehoram, the wife of Jehoiada the priest (for she was the sister of Ahaziah), hid him from Athaliah, so that she didn\u2019t kill him."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He was with them hidden in God\u2019s house six years while Athaliah reigned over the land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the seventh year, Jehoiada strengthened himself, and took the captains of hundreds\u2014Azariah the son of Jeroham, Ishmael the son of Jehohanan, Azariah the son of Obed, Maaseiah the son of Adaiah, and Elishaphat the son of Zichri\u2014into a covenant with him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They went around in Judah and gathered the Levites out of all the cities of Judah, and the heads of fathers\u2019 households of Israel, and they came to Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All the assembly made a covenant with the king in God\u2019s house. Jehoiada said to them, \u201cBehold, the king\u2019s son must reign, as the LORD has spoken concerning the sons of David."]],f:["Hebrew He"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"This is the thing that you must do: a third part of you, who come in on the Sabbath, of the priests and of the Levites, shall be gatekeepers of the thresholds."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"A third part shall be at the king\u2019s house; and a third part at the gate of the foundation. All the people will be in the courts of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But let no one come into the LORD\u2019s house except the priests and those who minister of the Levites. They shall come in, for they are holy, but all the people shall follow the LORD\u2019s instructions."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The Levites shall surround the king, every man with his weapons in his hand. Whoever comes into the house, let him be slain. Be with the king when he comes in and when he goes out.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So the Levites and all Judah did according to all that Jehoiada the priest commanded. They each took his men, those who were to come in on the Sabbath, with those who were to go out on the Sabbath, for Jehoiada the priest didn\u2019t dismiss the shift."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Jehoiada the priest delivered to the captains of hundreds the spears, bucklers, and shields that had been king David\u2019s, which were in God\u2019s house."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He set all the people, every man with his weapon in his hand, from the right side of the house to the left side of the house, near the altar and the house, around the king."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then they brought out the king\u2019s son, put the crown on him, gave him the covenant, and made him king. Jehoiada and his sons anointed him, and they said, \u201cLong live the king!\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When Athaliah heard the noise of the people running and praising the king, she came to the people into the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then she looked, and behold, the king stood by his pillar at the entrance, with the captains and the trumpeters by the king. All the people of the land rejoiced and blew trumpets. The singers also played musical instruments, and led the singing of praise. Then Athaliah tore her clothes, and said, \u201cTreason! treason!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoiada the priest brought out the captains of hundreds who were set over the army, and said to them, \u201cBring her out between the ranks; and whoever follows her, let him be slain with the sword.\u201d For the priest said, \u201cDon\u2019t kill her in the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So they made way for her. She went to the entrance of the horse gate to the king\u2019s house; and they killed her there."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoiada made a covenant between himself, all the people, and the king, that they should be the LORD\u2019s people."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All the people went to the house of Baal, broke it down, broke his altars and his images in pieces, and killed Mattan the priest of Baal before the altars."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jehoiada appointed the officers of the LORD\u2019s house under the hand of the Levitical priests, whom David had distributed in the LORD\u2019s house, to offer the burnt offerings of the LORD, as it is written in the law of Moses, with rejoicing and with singing, as David had ordered."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He set the gatekeepers at the gates of the LORD\u2019s house, that no one who was unclean in anything should enter in."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He took the captains of hundreds, the nobles, the governors of the people, and all the people of the land, and brought the king down from the LORD\u2019s house. They came through the upper gate to the king\u2019s house, and set the king on the throne of the kingdom."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So all the people of the land rejoiced, and the city was quiet. They had slain Athaliah with the sword."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Joash was seven years old when he began to reign, and he reigned forty years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Zibiah, of Beersheba."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Joash did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes all the days of Jehoiada the priest."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jehoiada took for him two wives, and he became the father of sons and daughters."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Joash intended to restore the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He gathered together the priests and the Levites, and said to them, \u201cGo out to the cities of Judah, and gather money to repair the house of your God from all Israel from year to year. See that you expedite this matter.\u201d However the Levites didn\u2019t do it right away."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The king called for Jehoiada the chief, and said to him, \u201cWhy haven\u2019t you required of the Levites to bring in the tax of Moses the servant of the LORD, and of the assembly of Israel, out of Judah and out of Jerusalem, for the Tent of the Testimony?\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the sons of Athaliah, that wicked woman, had broken up God\u2019s house; and they also gave all the dedicated things of the LORD\u2019s house to the Baals."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king commanded, and they made a chest, and set it outside at the gate of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They made a proclamation through Judah and Jerusalem, to bring in for the LORD the tax that Moses the servant of God laid on Israel in the wilderness."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All the princes and all the people rejoiced, and brought in, and cast into the chest, until they had filled it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Whenever the chest was brought to the king\u2019s officers by the hand of the Levites, and when they saw that there was much money, the king\u2019s scribe and the chief priest\u2019s officer came and emptied the chest, and took it, and carried it to its place again. Thus they did day by day, and gathered money in abundance."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The king and Jehoiada gave it to those who did the work of the service of the LORD\u2019s house. They hired masons and carpenters to restore the LORD\u2019s house, and also those who worked iron and bronze to repair the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So the workmen worked, and the work of repairing went forward in their hands. They set up God\u2019s house as it was designed, and strengthened it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When they had finished, they brought the rest of the money before the king and Jehoiada, from which were made vessels for the LORD\u2019s house, even vessels with which to minister and to offer, including spoons and vessels of gold and silver. They offered burnt offerings in the LORD\u2019s house continually all the days of Jehoiada."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jehoiada grew old and was full of days, and he died. He was one hundred thirty years old when he died."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They buried him in David\u2019s city among the kings, because he had done good in Israel, and toward God and his house."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after the death of Jehoiada, the princes of Judah came and bowed down to the king. Then the king listened to them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They abandoned the house of the LORD, the God of their fathers, and served the Asherah poles and the idols, so wrath came on Judah and Jerusalem for this their guiltiness."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Yet he sent prophets to them to bring them again to the LORD, and they testified against them; but they would not listen."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The Spirit of God came on Zechariah the son of Jehoiada the priest; and he stood above the people, and said to them, \u201cGod says, \u2018Why do you disobey the LORD\u2019s commandments, so that you can\u2019t prosper? Because you have forsaken the LORD, he has also forsaken you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"They conspired against him, and stoned him with stones at the commandment of the king in the court of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Thus Joash the king didn\u2019t remember the kindness which Jehoiada his father had done to him, but killed his son. When he died, he said, \u201cMay the LORD look at it, and repay it.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of the year, the army of the Syrians came up against him. They came to Judah and Jerusalem, and destroyed all the princes of the people from among the people, and sent all their plunder to the king of Damascus."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For the army of the Syrians came with a small company of men; and the LORD delivered a very great army into their hand, because they had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers. So they executed judgment on Joash."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had departed from him (for they left him seriously wounded), his own servants conspired against him for the blood of the sons of Jehoiada the priest, and killed him on his bed, and he died. They buried him in David\u2019s city, but they didn\u2019t bury him in the tombs of the kings."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"These are those who conspired against him: Zabad the son of Shimeath the Ammonitess and Jehozabad the son of Shimrith the Moabitess."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Now concerning his sons, the greatness of the burdens laid on him, and the rebuilding of God\u2019s house, behold, they are written in the commentary of the book of the kings. Amaziah his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Amaziah was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Jehoaddan, of Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, but not with a perfect heart."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now when the kingdom was established to him, he killed his servants who had killed his father the king."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But he didn\u2019t put their children to death, but did according to that which is written in the law in the book of Moses, as the LORD commanded, saying, \u201cThe fathers shall not die for the children, neither shall the children die for the fathers; but every man shall die for his own sin.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Amaziah gathered Judah together and ordered them according to their fathers\u2019 houses, under captains of thousands and captains of hundreds, even all Judah and Benjamin. He counted them from twenty years old and upward, and found that there were three hundred thousand chosen men, able to go out to war, who could handle spear and shield."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He also hired one hundred thousand mighty men of valor out of Israel for one hundred talents of silver."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"A man of God came to him, saying, \u201cO king, don\u2019t let the army of Israel go with you, for the LORD is not with Israel, with all the children of Ephraim."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But if you will go, take action, and be strong for the battle. God will overthrow you before the enemy; for God has power to help, and to overthrow.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Amaziah said to the man of God, \u201cBut what shall we do for the hundred talents which I have given to the army of Israel?\u201d"],[0,"The man of God answered, \u201cThe LORD is able to give you much more than this.\u201d"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds"]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Amaziah separated them, the army that had come to him out of Ephraim, to go home again. Therefore their anger was greatly kindled against Judah, and they returned home in fierce anger."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Amaziah took courage, and led his people out and went to the Valley of Salt, and struck ten thousand of the children of Seir."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The children of Judah carried away ten thousand alive, and brought them to the top of the rock, and threw them down from the top of the rock, so that they all were broken in pieces."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But the men of the army whom Amaziah sent back, that they should not go with him to battle, fell on the cities of Judah from Samaria even to Beth Horon, and struck of them three thousand, and took much plunder."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after Amaziah had come from the slaughter of the Edomites, he brought the gods of the children of Seir, and set them up to be his gods, and bowed down himself before them and burned incense to them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD\u2019s anger burned against Amaziah, and he sent to him a prophet who said to him, \u201cWhy have you sought after the gods of the people, which have not delivered their own people out of your hand?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"As he talked with him, the king said to him, \u201cHave we made you one of the king\u2019s counselors? Stop! Why should you be struck down?\u201d"],[0,"Then the prophet stopped, and said, \u201cI know that God has determined to destroy you, because you have done this and have not listened to my counsel.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Amaziah king of Judah consulted his advisers, and sent to Joash, the son of Jehoahaz, the son of Jehu, king of Israel, saying, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s look one another in the face.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Joash king of Israel sent to Amaziah king of Judah, saying, \u201cThe thistle that was in Lebanon sent to the cedar that was in Lebanon, saying, \u2018Give your daughter to my son as his wife. Then a wild animal that was in Lebanon passed by and trampled down the thistle."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You say to yourself that you have struck Edom; and your heart lifts you up to boast. Now stay at home. Why should you meddle with trouble, that you should fall, even you and Judah with you?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"But Amaziah would not listen; for it was of God, that he might deliver them into the hand of their enemies, because they had sought after the gods of Edom."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So Joash king of Israel went up, and he and Amaziah king of Judah looked one another in the face at Beth Shemesh, which belongs to Judah."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Judah was defeated by Israel; so every man fled to his tent."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Joash king of Israel took Amaziah king of Judah, the son of Joash the son of Jehoahaz, at Beth Shemesh and brought him to Jerusalem, and broke down the wall of Jerusalem from the gate of Ephraim to the corner gate, four hundred cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters, so 400 cubits is about 200 yards or 184 meters."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He took all the gold and silver, and all the vessels that were found in God\u2019s house with Obed-Edom, and the treasures of the king\u2019s house, and the hostages, and returned to Samaria."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Amaziah the son of Joash, king of Judah, lived for fifteen years after the death of Joash, son of Jehoahaz, king of Israel."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Amaziah, first and last, behold, aren\u2019t they written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Now from the time that Amaziah turned away from following the LORD, they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem. He fled to Lachish, but they sent after him to Lachish and killed him there."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They brought him on horses and buried him with his fathers in the City of Judah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people of Judah took Uzziah, who was sixteen years old, and made him king in the place of his father Amaziah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He built Eloth and restored it to Judah. After that the king slept with his fathers."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Uzziah was sixteen years old when he began to reign; and he reigned fifty-two years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Jechiliah, of Jerusalem."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, according to all that his father Amaziah had done."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He set himself to seek God in the days of Zechariah, who had understanding in the vision of God; and as long as he sought the LORD, God made him prosper."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He went out and fought against the Philistines, and broke down the wall of Gath, the wall of Jabneh, and the wall of Ashdod; and he built cities in the country of Ashdod, and among the Philistines."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"God helped him against the Philistines, and against the Arabians who lived in Gur Baal, and the Meunim."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The Ammonites gave tribute to Uzziah. His name spread abroad even to the entrance of Egypt, for he grew exceedingly strong."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moreover Uzziah built towers in Jerusalem at the corner gate, at the valley gate, and at the turning of the wall, and fortified them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He built towers in the wilderness, and dug out many cisterns, for he had much livestock, both in the lowlands and in the plains. He had farmers and vineyard keepers in the mountains and in the fruitful fields, for he loved farming."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Moreover Uzziah had an army of fighting men who went out to war by bands, according to the number of their reckoning made by Jeiel the scribe and Maaseiah the officer, under the hand of Hananiah, one of the king\u2019s captains."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The whole number of the heads of fathers\u2019 households, even the mighty men of valor, was two thousand six hundred."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Under their hand was an army, three hundred seven thousand five hundred, who made war with mighty power, to help the king against the enemy."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Uzziah prepared for them, even for all the army, shields, spears, helmets, coats of mail, bows, and stones for slinging."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"In Jerusalem, he made devices, invented by skillful men, to be on the towers and on the battlements, with which to shoot arrows and great stones. His name spread far abroad, because he was marvelously helped until he was strong."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But when he was strong, his heart was lifted up, so that he did corruptly and he trespassed against the LORD his God, for he went into the LORD\u2019s temple to burn incense on the altar of incense."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Azariah the priest went in after him, and with him eighty priests of the LORD, who were valiant men."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They resisted Uzziah the king, and said to him, \u201cIt isn\u2019t for you, Uzziah, to burn incense to the LORD, but for the priests the sons of Aaron, who are consecrated to burn incense. Go out of the sanctuary, for you have trespassed. It will not be for your honor from the LORD God.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Uzziah was angry. He had a censer in his hand to burn incense, and while he was angry with the priests, the leprosy broke out on his forehead before the priests in the LORD\u2019s house, beside the altar of incense."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Azariah the chief priest and all the priests looked at him, and behold, he was leprous in his forehead; and they thrust him out quickly from there. Indeed, he himself also hurried to go out, because the LORD had struck him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Uzziah the king was a leper to the day of his death, and lived in a separate house, being a leper; for he was cut off from the LORD\u2019s house. Jotham his son was over the king\u2019s house, judging the people of the land."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Uzziah, first and last, Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, wrote."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So Uzziah slept with his fathers; and they buried him with his fathers in the field of burial which belonged to the kings, for they said, \u201cHe is a leper.\u201d Jotham his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jotham was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Jerushah the daughter of Zadok."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, according to all that his father Uzziah had done. However he didn\u2019t enter into the LORD\u2019s temple. The people still acted corruptly."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He built the upper gate of the LORD\u2019s house, and he built much on the wall of Ophel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Moreover he built cities in the hill country of Judah, and in the forests he built fortresses and towers."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He also fought with the king of the children of Ammon, and prevailed against them. The children of Ammon gave him the same year one hundred talents of silver, ten thousand cors of wheat, and ten thousand cors of barley. The children of Ammon also gave that much to him in the second year, and in the third."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds","1 cor is the same as a homer, or about 55.9 U. S. gallons (liquid) or 211 liters or 6 bushels. 10,000 cors of wheat would weigh about 1,640 metric tons.","10,000 cors of barley would weigh about 1,310 metric tons."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Jotham became mighty, because he ordered his ways before the LORD his God."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jotham, and all his wars and his ways, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Jotham slept with his fathers, and they buried him in David\u2019s city; and Ahaz his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Ahaz was twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned sixteen years in Jerusalem. He didn\u2019t do that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, like David his father,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"but he walked in the ways of the kings of Israel, and also made molten images for the Baals."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Moreover he burned incense in the valley of the son of Hinnom, and burned his children in the fire, according to the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He sacrificed and burned incense in the high places, and on the hills, and under every green tree."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD his God delivered him into the hand of the king of Syria. They struck him, and carried away from him a great multitude of captives, and brought them to Damascus. He was also delivered into the hand of the king of Israel, who struck him with a great slaughter."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For Pekah the son of Remaliah killed in Judah one hundred twenty thousand in one day, all of them valiant men, because they had forsaken the LORD, the God of their fathers."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Zichri, a mighty man of Ephraim, killed Maaseiah the king\u2019s son, Azrikam the ruler of the house, and Elkanah who was next to the king."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of Israel carried away captive of their brothers two hundred thousand women, sons, and daughters, and also took away much plunder from them, and brought the plunder to Samaria."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But a prophet of the LORD was there, whose name was Oded; and he went out to meet the army that came to Samaria, and said to them, \u201cBehold, because the LORD, the God of your fathers, was angry with Judah, he has delivered them into your hand, and you have slain them in a rage which has reached up to heaven."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now you intend to degrade the children of Judah and Jerusalem as male and female slaves for yourselves. Aren\u2019t there even with you trespasses of your own against the LORD your God?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now hear me therefore, and send back the captives that you have taken captive from your brothers, for the fierce wrath of the LORD is on you.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Then some of the heads of the children of Ephraim, Azariah the son of Johanan, Berechiah the son of Meshillemoth, Jehizkiah the son of Shallum, and Amasa the son of Hadlai, stood up against those who came from the war,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cYou must not bring in the captives here, for you intend that which will bring on us a trespass against the LORD, to add to our sins and to our guilt; for our guilt is great, and there is fierce wrath against Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"So the armed men left the captives and the plunder before the princes and all the assembly."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The men who have been mentioned by name rose up and took the captives, and with the plunder clothed all who were naked among them, dressed them, gave them sandals, gave them something to eat and to drink, anointed them, carried all the feeble of them on donkeys, and brought them to Jericho, the city of palm trees, to their brothers. Then they returned to Samaria."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time King Ahaz sent to the kings of Assyria to help him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For again the Edomites had come and struck Judah, and carried away captives."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The Philistines also had invaded the cities of the lowland and of the South of Judah, and had taken Beth Shemesh, Aijalon, Gederoth, Soco with its villages, Timnah with its villages, and also Gimzo and its villages; and they lived there."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the LORD brought Judah low because of Ahaz king of Israel, because he acted without restraint in Judah and trespassed severely against the LORD."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Tilgath-pilneser king of Assyria came to him and gave him trouble, but didn\u2019t strengthen him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For Ahaz took away a portion out of the LORD\u2019s house, and out of the house of the king and of the princes, and gave it to the king of Assyria; but it didn\u2019t help him."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"In the time of his distress, he trespassed yet more against the LORD, this same King Ahaz."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For he sacrificed to the gods of Damascus which had defeated him. He said, \u201cBecause the gods of the kings of Syria helped them, I will sacrifice to them, that they may help me.\u201d But they were the ruin of him and of all Israel."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Ahaz gathered together the vessels of God\u2019s house, cut the vessels of God\u2019s house in pieces, and shut up the doors of the LORD\u2019s house; and he made himself altars in every corner of Jerusalem."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In every city of Judah he made high places to burn incense to other gods, and provoked the LORD, the God of his fathers, to anger."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of his acts, and all his ways, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Ahaz slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the city, even in Jerusalem, because they didn\u2019t bring him into the tombs of the kings of Israel; and Hezekiah his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah began to reign when he was twenty-five years old, and he reigned twenty-nine years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Abijah, the daughter of Zechariah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, according to all that David his father had done."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In the first year of his reign, in the first month, he opened the doors of the LORD\u2019s house and repaired them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He brought in the priests and the Levites and gathered them together into the wide place on the east,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cListen to me, you Levites! Now sanctify yourselves, and sanctify the house of the LORD, the God of your fathers, and carry the filthiness out of the holy place."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For our fathers were unfaithful, and have done that which was evil in the LORD our God\u2019s sight, and have forsaken him, and have turned away their faces from the habitation of the LORD, and turned their backs."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Also they have shut up the doors of the porch, and put out the lamps, and have not burned incense nor offered burnt offerings in the holy place to the God of Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD\u2019s wrath was on Judah and Jerusalem, and he has delivered them to be tossed back and forth, to be an astonishment and a hissing, as you see with your eyes."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For behold, our fathers have fallen by the sword, and our sons and our daughters and our wives are in captivity for this."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now it is in my heart to make a covenant with the LORD, the God of Israel, that his fierce anger may turn away from us."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"My sons, don\u2019t be negligent now; for the LORD has chosen you to stand before him, to minister to him, and that you should be his ministers and burn incense.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Levites arose: Mahath, the son of Amasai, and Joel the son of Azariah, of the sons of the Kohathites; and of the sons of Merari, Kish the son of Abdi, and Azariah the son of Jehallelel; and of the Gershonites, Joah the son of Zimmah, and Eden the son of Joah;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and of the sons of Elizaphan, Shimri and Jeuel; and of the sons of Asaph, Zechariah and Mattaniah;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and of the sons of Heman, Jehuel and Shimei; and of the sons of Jeduthun, Shemaiah and Uzziel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They gathered their brothers, sanctified themselves, and went in, according to the commandment of the king by the LORD\u2019s words, to cleanse the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The priests went into the inner part of the LORD\u2019s house to cleanse it, and brought out all the uncleanness that they found in the LORD\u2019s temple into the court of the LORD\u2019s house. The Levites took it from there to carry it out to the brook Kidron."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now they began on the first day of the first month to sanctify, and on the eighth day of the month they came to the LORD\u2019s porch. They sanctified the LORD\u2019s house in eight days, and on the sixteenth day of the first month they finished."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then they went in to Hezekiah the king within the palace and said, \u201cWe have cleansed all the LORD\u2019s house, including the altar of burnt offering with all its vessels, and the table of show bread with all its vessels."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Moreover, we have prepared and sanctified all the vessels which King Ahaz threw away in his reign when he was unfaithful. Behold, they are before the LORD\u2019s altar.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hezekiah the king arose early, gathered the princes of the city, and went up to the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They brought seven bulls, seven rams, seven lambs, and seven male goats, for a sin offering for the kingdom, for the sanctuary, and for Judah. He commanded the priests the sons of Aaron to offer them on the LORD\u2019s altar."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"So they killed the bulls, and the priests received the blood and sprinkled it on the altar. They killed the rams and sprinkled the blood on the altar. They also killed the lambs and sprinkled the blood on the altar."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They brought near the male goats for the sin offering before the king and the assembly; and they laid their hands on them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then the priests killed them, and they made a sin offering with their blood on the altar, to make atonement for all Israel; for the king commanded that the burnt offering and the sin offering should be made for all Israel."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He set the Levites in the LORD\u2019s house with cymbals, with stringed instruments, and with harps, according to the commandment of David, of Gad the king\u2019s seer, and Nathan the prophet; for the commandment was from the LORD by his prophets."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The Levites stood with David\u2019s instruments, and the priests with the trumpets."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Hezekiah commanded them to offer the burnt offering on the altar. When the burnt offering began, the LORD\u2019s song also began, along with the trumpets and instruments of David king of Israel."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"All the assembly worshiped, the singers sang, and the trumpeters sounded. All this continued until the burnt offering was finished."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had finished offering, the king and all who were present with him bowed themselves and worshiped."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Moreover Hezekiah the king and the princes commanded the Levites to sing praises to the LORD with the words of David, and of Asaph the seer. They sang praises with gladness, and they bowed their heads and worshiped."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hezekiah answered, \u201cNow you have consecrated yourselves to the LORD. Come near and bring sacrifices and thank offerings into the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d The assembly brought in sacrifices and thank offerings, and as many as were of a willing heart brought burnt offerings."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The number of the burnt offerings which the assembly brought was seventy bulls, one hundred rams, and two hundred lambs. All these were for a burnt offering to the LORD."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The consecrated things were six hundred head of cattle and three thousand sheep."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But the priests were too few, so that they could not skin all the burnt offerings. Therefore their brothers the Levites helped them until the work was ended, and until the priests had sanctified themselves, for the Levites were more upright in heart to sanctify themselves than the priests."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Also the burnt offerings were in abundance, with the fat of the peace offerings and with the drink offerings for every burnt offering. So the service of the LORD\u2019s house was set in order."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Hezekiah and all the people rejoiced because of that which God had prepared for the people; for the thing was done suddenly."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah sent to all Israel and Judah, and wrote letters also to Ephraim and Manasseh, that they should come to the LORD\u2019s house at Jerusalem, to keep the Passover to the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For the king had taken counsel with his princes and all the assembly in Jerusalem to keep the Passover in the second month."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For they could not keep it at that time, because the priests had not sanctified themselves in sufficient number, and the people had not gathered themselves together to Jerusalem."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The thing was right in the eyes of the king and of all the assembly."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So they established a decree to make proclamation throughout all Israel, from Beersheba even to Dan, that they should come to keep the Passover to the LORD, the God of Israel, at Jerusalem, for they had not kept it in great numbers in the way it is written."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"So the couriers went with the letters from the king and his princes throughout all Israel and Judah, according to the commandment of the king, saying, \u201cYou children of Israel, turn again to the LORD, the God of Abraham, Isaac, and Israel, that he may return to the remnant of you that have escaped out of the hand of the kings of Assyria."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be like your fathers and like your brothers, who trespassed against the LORD, the God of their fathers, so that he gave them up to desolation, as you see."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now don\u2019t be stiff-necked, as your fathers were, but yield yourselves to the LORD, and enter into his sanctuary, which he has sanctified forever, and serve the LORD your God, that his fierce anger may turn away from you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For if you turn again to the LORD, your brothers and your children will find compassion with those who led them captive, and will come again into this land, because the LORD your God is gracious and merciful, and will not turn away his face from you if you return to him.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So the couriers passed from city to city through the country of Ephraim and Manasseh, even to Zebulun, but people ridiculed them and mocked them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Nevertheless some men of Asher, Manasseh, and Zebulun humbled themselves and came to Jerusalem."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Also the hand of God came on Judah to give them one heart, to do the commandment of the king and of the princes by the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Many people assembled at Jerusalem to keep the feast of unleavened bread in the second month, a very great assembly."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They arose and took away the altars that were in Jerusalem, and they took away all the altars for incense and threw them into the brook Kidron."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then they killed the Passover on the fourteenth day of the second month. The priests and the Levites were ashamed, and sanctified themselves, and brought burnt offerings into the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They stood in their place after their order, according to the law of Moses the man of God. The priests sprinkled the blood which they received of the hand of the Levites."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For there were many in the assembly who had not sanctified themselves; therefore the Levites were in charge of killing the Passovers for everyone who was not clean, to sanctify them to the LORD."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For a multitude of the people, even many of Ephraim, Manasseh, Issachar, and Zebulun, had not cleansed themselves, yet they ate the Passover other than the way it is written. For Hezekiah had prayed for them, saying, \u201cMay the good LORD pardon everyone"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"who sets his heart to seek God, the LORD, the God of his fathers, even if they aren\u2019t clean according to the purification of the sanctuary.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD listened to Hezekiah, and healed the people."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The children of Israel who were present at Jerusalem kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with great gladness. The Levites and the priests praised the LORD day by day, singing with loud instruments to the LORD."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Hezekiah spoke encouragingly to all the Levites who had good understanding in the service of the LORD. So they ate throughout the feast for the seven days, offering sacrifices of peace offerings and making confession to the LORD, the God of their fathers."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The whole assembly took counsel to keep another seven days, and they kept another seven days with gladness."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For Hezekiah king of Judah gave to the assembly for offerings one thousand bulls and seven thousand sheep; and the princes gave to the assembly a thousand bulls and ten thousand sheep; and a great number of priests sanctified themselves."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"All the assembly of Judah, with the priests and the Levites, and all the assembly who came out of Israel, and the foreigners who came out of the land of Israel and who lived in Judah, rejoiced."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"So there was great joy in Jerusalem; for since the time of Solomon the son of David king of Israel there was nothing like this in Jerusalem."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Then the Levitical priests arose and blessed the people. Their voice was heard, and their prayer came up to his holy habitation, even to heaven."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when all this was finished, all Israel who were present went out to the cities of Judah and broke the pillars in pieces, cut down the Asherah poles, and broke down the high places and the altars out of all Judah and Benjamin, also in Ephraim and Manasseh, until they had destroyed them all. Then all the children of Israel returned, every man to his possession, into their own cities."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah appointed the divisions of the priests and the Levites after their divisions, every man according to his service, both the priests and the Levites, for burnt offerings and for peace offerings, to minister, to give thanks, and to praise in the gates of the LORD\u2019s camp."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He also appointed the king\u2019s portion of his possessions for the burnt offerings: for the morning and evening burnt offerings, and the burnt offerings for the Sabbaths, for the new moons, and for the set feasts, as it is written in the LORD\u2019s law."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Moreover he commanded the people who lived in Jerusalem to give the portion of the priests and the Levites, that they might give themselves to the LORD\u2019s law."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"As soon as the commandment went out, the children of Israel gave in abundance the first fruits of grain, new wine, oil, honey, and of all the increase of the field; and they brought in the tithe of all things abundantly."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The children of Israel and Judah, who lived in the cities of Judah, also brought in the tithe of cattle and sheep, and the tithe of dedicated things which were consecrated to the LORD their God, and laid them in heaps."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"In the third month, they began to lay the foundation of the heaps, and finished them in the seventh month."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When Hezekiah and the princes came and saw the heaps, they blessed the LORD and his people Israel."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Hezekiah questioned the priests and the Levites about the heaps."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Azariah the chief priest, of the house of Zadok, answered him and said, \u201cSince people began to bring the offerings into the LORD\u2019s house, we have eaten and had enough, and have plenty left over, for the LORD has blessed his people; and that which is left is this great store.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hezekiah commanded them to prepare rooms in the LORD\u2019s house, and they prepared them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They brought in the offerings, the tithes, and the dedicated things faithfully. Conaniah the Levite was ruler over them, and Shimei his brother was second."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Jehiel, Azaziah, Nahath, Asahel, Jerimoth, Jozabad, Eliel, Ismachiah, Mahath, and Benaiah were overseers under the hand of Conaniah and Shimei his brother, by the appointment of Hezekiah the king and Azariah the ruler of God\u2019s house."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Kore the son of Imnah the Levite, the gatekeeper at the east gate, was over the free will offerings of God, to distribute the LORD\u2019s offerings and the most holy things."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Under him were Eden, Miniamin, Jeshua, Shemaiah, Amariah, and Shecaniah, in the cities of the priests, in their office of trust, to give to their brothers by divisions, to the great as well as to the small;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"in addition to those who were listed by genealogy of males, from three years old and upward, even everyone who entered into the LORD\u2019s house, as the duty of every day required, for their service in their offices according to their divisions;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and those who were listed by genealogy of the priests by their fathers\u2019 houses, and the Levites from twenty years old and upward, in their offices by their divisions;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and those who were listed by genealogy of all their little ones, their wives, their sons, and their daughters, through all the congregation; for in their office of trust they sanctified themselves in holiness."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Also for the sons of Aaron the priests, who were in the fields of the pasture lands of their cities, in every city, there were men who were mentioned by name to give portions to all the males among the priests and to all who were listed by genealogy among the Levites."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah did so throughout all Judah; and he did that which was good, right, and faithful before the LORD his God."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"In every work that he began in the service of God\u2019s house, in the law, and in the commandments, to seek his God, he did it with all his heart and prospered."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things and this faithfulness, Sennacherib king of Assyria came, entered into Judah, encamped against the fortified cities, and intended to win them for himself."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When Hezekiah saw that Sennacherib had come, and that he was planning to fight against Jerusalem,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"he took counsel with his princes and his mighty men to stop the waters of the springs which were outside of the city, and they helped him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then many people gathered together and they stopped all the springs and the brook that flowed through the middle of the land, saying, \u201cWhy should the kings of Assyria come, and find abundant water?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He took courage, built up all the wall that was broken down, and raised it up to the towers, with the other wall outside, and strengthened Millo in David\u2019s city, and made weapons and shields in abundance."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He set captains of war over the people, gathered them together to him in the wide place at the gate of the city, and spoke encouragingly to them, saying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u201cBe strong and courageous. Don\u2019t be afraid or dismayed because of the king of Assyria, nor for all the multitude who is with him; for there is a greater one with us than with him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"An arm of flesh is with him, but the LORD our God is with us to help us and to fight our battles.\u201d The people rested themselves on the words of Hezekiah king of Judah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Sennacherib king of Assyria sent his servants to Jerusalem, (now he was attacking Lachish, and all his forces were with him), to Hezekiah king of Judah, and to all Judah who were at Jerusalem, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Sennacherib king of Assyria says, \u201cIn whom do you trust, that you remain under siege in Jerusalem?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Doesn\u2019t Hezekiah persuade you to give you over to die by famine and by thirst, saying, \u2018The LORD our God will deliver us out of the hand of the king of Assyria\u2019?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Hasn\u2019t the same Hezekiah taken away his high places and his altars, and commanded Judah and Jerusalem, saying, \u2018You shall worship before one altar, and you shall burn incense on it\u2019?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know what I and my fathers have done to all the peoples of the lands? Were the gods of the nations of those lands in any way able to deliver their land out of my hand?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Who was there among all the gods of those nations which my fathers utterly destroyed that could deliver his people out of my hand, that your God should be able to deliver you out of my hand?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now therefore don\u2019t let Hezekiah deceive you nor persuade you in this way. Don\u2019t believe him, for no god of any nation or kingdom was able to deliver his people out of my hand, and out of the hand of my fathers. How much less will your God deliver you out of my hand?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"His servants spoke yet more against the LORD God and against his servant Hezekiah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He also wrote letters insulting the LORD, the God of Israel, and speaking against him, saying, \u201cAs the gods of the nations of the lands, which have not delivered their people out of my hand, so shall the God of Hezekiah not deliver his people out of my hand.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They called out with a loud voice in the Jews\u2019 language to the people of Jerusalem who were on the wall, to frighten them and to trouble them, that they might take the city."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They spoke of the God of Jerusalem as of the gods of the peoples of the earth, which are the work of men\u2019s hands."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah the king and Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, prayed because of this, and cried to heaven."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD sent an angel, who cut off all the mighty men of valor, the leaders, and captains in the camp of the king of Assyria. So he returned with shame of face to his own land. When he had come into the house of his god, those who came out of his own body killed him there with the sword."]],f:["i.e., his own sons"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Thus the LORD saved Hezekiah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem from the hand of Sennacherib the king of Assyria and from the hand of all others, and guided them on every side."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Many brought gifts to the LORD to Jerusalem, and precious things to Hezekiah king of Judah, so that he was exalted in the sight of all nations from then on."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days Hezekiah was terminally ill, and he prayed to the LORD; and he spoke to him, and gave him a sign."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But Hezekiah didn\u2019t reciprocate appropriate to the benefit done for him, because his heart was lifted up. Therefore there was wrath on him, Judah, and Jerusalem."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"However, Hezekiah humbled himself for the pride of his heart, both he and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so that the LORD\u2019s wrath didn\u2019t come on them in the days of Hezekiah."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah had exceedingly great riches and honor. He provided himself with treasuries for silver, for gold, for precious stones, for spices, for shields, and for all kinds of valuable vessels;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"also storehouses for the increase of grain, new wine, and oil; and stalls for all kinds of animals, and flocks in folds."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Moreover he provided for himself cities, and possessions of flocks and herds in abundance; for God had given him abundant possessions."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"This same Hezekiah also stopped the upper spring of the waters of Gihon, and brought them straight down on the west side of David\u2019s city. Hezekiah prospered in all his works."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"However, concerning the ambassadors of the princes of Babylon, who sent to him to inquire of the wonder that was done in the land, God left him to test him, that he might know all that was in his heart."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Hezekiah and his good deeds, behold, they are written in the vision of Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, in the book of the kings of Judah and Israel."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Hezekiah slept with his fathers, and they buried him in the ascent to the tombs of the sons of David. All Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem honored him at his death. Manasseh his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty-five years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, after the abominations of the nations whom the LORD cast out before the children of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For he built again the high places which Hezekiah his father had broken down; and he raised up altars for the Baals, made Asheroth, and worshiped all the army of the sky, and served them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He built altars in the LORD\u2019s house, of which the LORD said, \u201cMy name shall be in Jerusalem forever.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He built altars for all the army of the sky in the two courts of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He also made his children to pass through the fire in the valley of the son of Hinnom. He practiced sorcery, divination, and witchcraft, and dealt with those who had familiar spirits and with wizards. He did much evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, to provoke him to anger."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He set the engraved image of the idol, which he had made, in God\u2019s house, of which God said to David and to Solomon his son, \u201cIn this house, and in Jerusalem, which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel, I will put my name forever."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will not any more remove the foot of Israel from off the land which I have appointed for your fathers, if only they will observe to do all that I have commanded them, even all the law, the statutes, and the ordinances given by Moses.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Manasseh seduced Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so that they did more evil than did the nations whom the LORD destroyed before the children of Israel."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to Manasseh and to his people, but they didn\u2019t listen."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD brought on them the captains of the army of the king of Assyria, who took Manasseh in chains, bound him with fetters, and carried him to Babylon."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When he was in distress, he begged the LORD his God, and humbled himself greatly before the God of his fathers."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He prayed to him; and he was entreated by him, and heard his supplication, and brought him again to Jerusalem into his kingdom. Then Manasseh knew that the LORD was God."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after this, he built an outer wall to David\u2019s city on the west side of Gihon, in the valley, even to the entrance at the fish gate. He encircled Ophel with it, and raised it up to a very great height; and he put valiant captains in all the fortified cities of Judah."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He took away the foreign gods and the idol out of the LORD\u2019s house, and all the altars that he had built in the mountain of the LORD\u2019s house and in Jerusalem, and cast them out of the city."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He built up the LORD\u2019s altar, and offered sacrifices of peace offerings and of thanksgiving on it, and commanded Judah to serve the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Nevertheless the people still sacrificed in the high places, but only to the LORD their God."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Manasseh, and his prayer to his God, and the words of the seers who spoke to him in the name of the LORD, the God of Israel, behold, they are written among the acts of the kings of Israel."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"His prayer also, and how God listened to his request, and all his sin and his trespass, and the places in which he built high places and set up the Asherah poles and the engraved images before he humbled himself: behold, they are written in the history of Hozai."]],f:["or, the seers"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"So Manasseh slept with his fathers, and they buried him in his own house; and Amon his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Amon was twenty-two years old when he began to reign; and he reigned two years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, as did Manasseh his father; and Amon sacrificed to all the engraved images which Manasseh his father had made, and served them."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He didn\u2019t humble himself before the LORD, as Manasseh his father had humbled himself; but this same Amon trespassed more and more."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"His servants conspired against him, and put him to death in his own house."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But the people of the land killed all those who had conspired against King Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Josiah was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned thirty-one years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was right in the LORD\u2019s eyes, and walked in the ways of David his father, and didn\u2019t turn away to the right hand or to the left."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For in the eighth year of his reign, while he was yet young, he began to seek after the God of David his father; and in the twelfth year he began to purge Judah and Jerusalem from the high places, the Asherah poles, the engraved images, and the molten images."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They broke down the altars of the Baals in his presence; and he cut down the incense altars that were on high above them. He broke the Asherah poles, the engraved images, and the molten images in pieces, made dust of them, and scattered it on the graves of those who had sacrificed to them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He burned the bones of the priests on their altars, and purged Judah and Jerusalem."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He did this in the cities of Manasseh, Ephraim, and Simeon, even to Naphtali, around in their ruins."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He broke down the altars, beat the Asherah poles and the engraved images into powder, and cut down all the incense altars throughout all the land of Israel, then returned to Jerusalem."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the eighteenth year of his reign, when he had purged the land and the house, he sent Shaphan the son of Azaliah, Maaseiah the governor of the city, and Joah the son of Joahaz the recorder to repair the house of the LORD his God."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They came to Hilkiah the high priest and delivered the money that was brought into God\u2019s house, which the Levites, the keepers of the threshold, had gathered from the hands of Manasseh, Ephraim, of all the remnant of Israel, of all Judah and Benjamin, and of the inhabitants of Jerusalem."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They delivered it into the hands of the workmen who had the oversight of the LORD\u2019s house; and the workmen who labored in the LORD\u2019s house gave it to mend and repair the house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They gave it to the carpenters and to the builders to buy cut stone and timber for couplings, and to make beams for the houses which the kings of Judah had destroyed."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The men did the work faithfully. Their overseers were Jahath and Obadiah the Levites, of the sons of Merari; and Zechariah and Meshullam, of the sons of the Kohathites, to give direction; and others of the Levites, who were all skillful with musical instruments."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Also they were over the bearers of burdens, and directed all who did the work in every kind of service. Of the Levites, there were scribes, officials, and gatekeepers."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When they brought out the money that was brought into the LORD\u2019s house, Hilkiah the priest found the book of the LORD\u2019s law given by Moses."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Hilkiah answered Shaphan the scribe, \u201cI have found the book of the law in the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d So Hilkiah delivered the book to Shaphan."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Shaphan carried the book to the king, and moreover brought back word to the king, saying, \u201cAll that was committed to your servants, they are doing."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They have emptied out the money that was found in the LORD\u2019s house, and have delivered it into the hand of the overseers and into the hand of the workmen.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Shaphan the scribe told the king, saying, \u201cHilkiah the priest has delivered me a book.\u201d Shaphan read from it to the king."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"When the king had heard the words of the law, he tore his clothes."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The king commanded Hilkiah, Ahikam the son of Shaphan, Abdon the son of Micah, Shaphan the scribe, and Asaiah the king\u2019s servant, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cGo inquire of the LORD for me, and for those who are left in Israel and in Judah, concerning the words of the book that is found; for great is the LORD\u2019s wrath that is poured out on us, because our fathers have not kept the LORD\u2019s word, to do according to all that is written in this book.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hilkiah and those whom the king had commanded went to Huldah the prophetess, the wife of Shallum the son of Tokhath, the son of Hasrah, keeper of the wardrobe (now she lived in Jerusalem in the second quarter), and they spoke to her to that effect."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to them, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel says: \u2018Tell the man who sent you to me,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Behold, I will bring evil on this place and on its inhabitants, even all the curses that are written in the book which they have read before the king of Judah."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Because they have forsaken me, and have burned incense to other gods, that they might provoke me to anger with all the works of their hands, therefore my wrath is poured out on this place, and it will not be quenched.\u2019\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But to the king of Judah, who sent you to inquire of the LORD, you shall tell him this, \u2018The LORD, the God of Israel says: \u201cAbout the words which you have heard,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"because your heart was tender, and you humbled yourself before God when you heard his words against this place and against its inhabitants, and have humbled yourself before me, and have torn your clothes and wept before me, I also have heard you,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I will gather you to your fathers, and you will be gathered to your grave in peace. Your eyes won\u2019t see all the evil that I will bring on this place and on its inhabitants.\u201d\u2019\u201d"],[0,"They brought back this message to the king."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king sent and gathered together all the elders of Judah and Jerusalem."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The king went up to the LORD\u2019s house with all the men of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem\u2014the priests, the Levites, and all the people, both great and small\u2014and he read in their hearing all the words of the book of the covenant that was found in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The king stood in his place and made a covenant before the LORD, to walk after the LORD, and to keep his commandments, his testimonies, and his statutes with all his heart and with all his soul, to perform the words of the covenant that were written in this book."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He caused all who were found in Jerusalem and Benjamin to stand. The inhabitants of Jerusalem did according to the covenant of God, the God of their fathers."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Josiah took away all the abominations out of all the countries that belonged to the children of Israel, and made all who were found in Israel to serve, even to serve the LORD their God. All his days they didn\u2019t depart from following the LORD, the God of their fathers."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Josiah kept a Passover to the LORD in Jerusalem. They killed the Passover on the fourteenth day of the first month."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He set the priests in their offices and encouraged them in the service of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He said to the Levites who taught all Israel, who were holy to the LORD, \u201cPut the holy ark in the house which Solomon the son of David king of Israel built. It will no longer be a burden on your shoulders. Now serve the LORD your God and his people Israel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Prepare yourselves after your fathers\u2019 houses by your divisions, according to the writing of David king of Israel, and according to the writing of Solomon his son."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Stand in the holy place according to the divisions of the fathers\u2019 houses of your brothers the children of the people, and let there be for each a portion of a fathers\u2019 house of the Levites."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Kill the Passover lamb, sanctify yourselves, and prepare for your brothers, to do according to the LORD\u2019s word by Moses.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Josiah gave to the children of the people, of the flock, lambs and young goats, all of them for the Passover offerings, to all who were present, to the number of thirty thousand, and three thousand bulls. These were of the king\u2019s substance."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"His princes gave a free will offering to the people, to the priests, and to the Levites. Hilkiah, Zechariah, and Jehiel, the rulers of God\u2019s house, gave to the priests for the Passover offerings two thousand six hundred small livestock, and three hundred head of cattle."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Conaniah also, and Shemaiah and Nethanel, his brothers, and Hashabiah, Jeiel, and Jozabad, the chiefs of the Levites, gave to the Levites for the Passover offerings five thousand small livestock and five hundred head of cattle."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So the service was prepared, and the priests stood in their place, and the Levites by their divisions, according to the king\u2019s commandment."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They killed the Passover lambs, and the priests sprinkled the blood which they received from their hands, and the Levites skinned them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They removed the burnt offerings, that they might give them according to the divisions of the fathers\u2019 houses of the children of the people, to offer to the LORD, as it is written in the book of Moses. They did the same with the cattle."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They roasted the Passover with fire according to the ordinance. They boiled the holy offerings in pots, in cauldrons, and in pans, and carried them quickly to all the children of the people."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Afterward they prepared for themselves and for the priests, because the priests the sons of Aaron were busy with offering the burnt offerings and the fat until night. Therefore the Levites prepared for themselves and for the priests the sons of Aaron."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The singers, the sons of Asaph, were in their place, according to the commandment of David, Asaph, Heman, and Jeduthun the king\u2019s seer; and the gatekeepers were at every gate. They didn\u2019t need to depart from their service, because their brothers the Levites prepared for them."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So all the service of the LORD was prepared the same day, to keep the Passover, and to offer burnt offerings on the LORD\u2019s altar, according to the commandment of King Josiah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The children of Israel who were present kept the Passover at that time, and the feast of unleavened bread seven days."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"There was no Passover like that kept in Israel from the days of Samuel the prophet, nor did any of the kings of Israel keep such a Passover as Josiah kept\u2014with the priests, the Levites, and all Judah and Israel who were present, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"This Passover was kept in the eighteenth year of the reign of Josiah."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"After all this, when Josiah had prepared the temple, Neco king of Egypt went up to fight against Carchemish by the Euphrates, and Josiah went out against him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But he sent ambassadors to him, saying, \u201cWhat have I to do with you, you king of Judah? I come not against you today, but against the house with which I have war. God has commanded me to make haste. Beware that it is God who is with me, that he not destroy you.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Nevertheless Josiah would not turn his face from him, but disguised himself, that he might fight with him, and didn\u2019t listen to the words of Neco from the mouth of God, and came to fight in the valley of Megiddo."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The archers shot at King Josiah; and the king said to his servants, \u201cTake me away, because I am seriously wounded!\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"So his servants took him out of the chariot, and put him in the second chariot that he had, and brought him to Jerusalem; and he died, and was buried in the tombs of his fathers. All Judah and Jerusalem mourned for Josiah."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Jeremiah lamented for Josiah, and all the singing men and singing women spoke of Josiah in their lamentations to this day; and they made them an ordinance in Israel. Behold, they are written in the lamentations."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Josiah and his good deeds, according to that which is written in the LORD\u2019s law,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and his acts, first and last, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the people of the land took Jehoahaz the son of Josiah, and made him king in his father\u2019s place in Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Joahaz was twenty-three years old when he began to reign; and he reigned three months in Jerusalem."]],f:["Joahaz is a variant of Jehoahaz."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The king of Egypt removed him from office at Jerusalem, and fined the land one hundred talents of silver and a talent of gold."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The king of Egypt made Eliakim his brother king over Judah and Jerusalem, and changed his name to Jehoiakim. Neco took Joahaz his brother, and carried him to Egypt."]],f:["Joahaz is a variant of Jehoahaz."]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoiakim was twenty-five years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. He did that which was evil in the LORD his God\u2019s sight."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up against him, and bound him in fetters to carry him to Babylon."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Nebuchadnezzar also carried some of the vessels of the LORD\u2019s house to Babylon, and put them in his temple at Babylon."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now the rest of the acts of Jehoiakim, and his abominations which he did, and that which was found in him, behold, they are written in the book of the kings of Israel and Judah; and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his place."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jehoiachin was eight years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months and ten days in Jerusalem. He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"At the return of the year, King Nebuchadnezzar sent and brought him to Babylon, with the valuable vessels of the LORD\u2019s house, and made Zedekiah his brother king over Judah and Jerusalem."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD his God\u2019s sight. He didn\u2019t humble himself before Jeremiah the prophet speaking from the LORD\u2019s mouth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He also rebelled against King Nebuchadnezzar, who had made him swear by God; but he stiffened his neck, and hardened his heart against turning to the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Moreover all the chiefs of the priests and the people trespassed very greatly after all the abominations of the nations; and they polluted the LORD\u2019s house which he had made holy in Jerusalem."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD, the God of their fathers, sent to them by his messengers, rising up early and sending, because he had compassion on his people and on his dwelling place;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"but they mocked the messengers of God, despised his words, and scoffed at his prophets, until the LORD\u2019s wrath arose against his people, until there was no remedy."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore he brought on them the king of the Chaldeans, who killed their young men with the sword in the house of their sanctuary, and had no compassion on young man or virgin, old man or infirm. He gave them all into his hand."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All the vessels of God\u2019s house, great and small, and the treasures of the LORD\u2019s house, and the treasures of the king and of his princes, all these he brought to Babylon."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They burned God\u2019s house, broke down the wall of Jerusalem, burned all its palaces with fire, and destroyed all of its valuable vessels."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He carried those who had escaped from the sword away to Babylon, and they were servants to him and his sons until the reign of the kingdom of Persia,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"to fulfill the LORD\u2019s word by Jeremiah\u2019s mouth, until the land had enjoyed its Sabbaths. As long as it lay desolate, it kept Sabbath, to fulfill seventy years."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the LORD\u2019s word by the mouth of Jeremiah might be accomplished, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, so that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"\u201cCyrus king of Persia says, \u2018The LORD, the God of heaven, has given all the kingdoms of the earth to me; and he has commanded me to build him a house in Jerusalem, which is in Judah. Whoever there is among you of all his people, the LORD his God be with him, and let him go up.\u2019\u201d"]]}]]}},1285,[]);
__d(function(e,t,h,o,a,n,i){a.exports={book:"Ezra",name:"Ezra",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the first year of Cyrus king of Persia, that the LORD\u2019s word by Jeremiah\u2019s mouth might be accomplished, the LORD stirred up the spirit of Cyrus king of Persia, so that he made a proclamation throughout all his kingdom, and put it also in writing, saying,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cCyrus king of Persia says, \u2018The LORD, the God of heaven, has given me all the kingdoms of the earth; and he has commanded me to build him a house in Jerusalem, which is in Judah."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Whoever there is among you of all his people, may his God be with him, and let him go up to Jerusalem, which is in Judah, and build the house of the LORD, the God of Israel (he is God), which is in Jerusalem."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Whoever is left, in any place where he lives, let the men of his place help him with silver, with gold, with goods, and with animals, in addition to the free will offering for God\u2019s house which is in Jerusalem.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the heads of fathers\u2019 households of Judah and Benjamin, the priests and the Levites, all whose spirit God had stirred to go up, rose up to build the LORD\u2019s house which is in Jerusalem."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"All those who were around them strengthened their hands with vessels of silver, with gold, with goods, with animals, and with precious things, in addition to all that was willingly offered."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Also Cyrus the king brought out the vessels of the LORD\u2019s house, which Nebuchadnezzar had brought out of Jerusalem, and had put in the house of his gods;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"even those, Cyrus king of Persia brought out by the hand of Mithredath the treasurer, and counted them out to Sheshbazzar the prince of Judah."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"This is the number of them: thirty platters of gold, one thousand platters of silver, twenty-nine knives,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"thirty bowls of gold, four hundred ten silver bowls of a second kind, and one thousand other vessels."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"All the vessels of gold and of silver were five thousand four hundred. Sheshbazzar brought all these up when the captives were brought up from Babylon to Jerusalem."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the children of the province who went up out of the captivity of those who had been carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away to Babylon, and who returned to Jerusalem and Judah, everyone to his city;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"who came with Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Seraiah, Reelaiah, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispar, Bigvai, Rehum, and Baanah."],[0,"The number of the men of the people of Israel:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The children of Parosh, two thousand one hundred seventy-two."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The children of Shephatiah, three hundred seventy-two."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The children of Arah, seven hundred seventy-five."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The children of Pahathmoab, of the children of Jeshua and Joab, two thousand eight hundred twelve."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The children of Elam, one thousand two hundred fifty-four."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The children of Zattu, nine hundred forty-five."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The children of Zaccai, seven hundred sixty."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The children of Bani, six hundred forty-two."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The children of Bebai, six hundred twenty-three."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The children of Azgad, one thousand two hundred twenty-two."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The children of Adonikam, six hundred sixty-six."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The children of Bigvai, two thousand fifty-six."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The children of Adin, four hundred fifty-four."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The children of Ater, of Hezekiah, ninety-eight."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The children of Bezai, three hundred twenty-three."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The children of Jorah, one hundred twelve."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The children of Hashum, two hundred twenty-three."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The children of Gibbar, ninety-five."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The children of Bethlehem, one hundred twenty-three."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The men of Netophah, fifty-six."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The men of Anathoth, one hundred twenty-eight."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The children of Azmaveth, forty-two."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The children of Kiriath Arim, Chephirah, and Beeroth, seven hundred forty-three."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The children of Ramah and Geba, six hundred twenty-one."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The men of Michmas, one hundred twenty-two."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The men of Bethel and Ai, two hundred twenty-three."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The children of Nebo, fifty-two."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The children of Magbish, one hundred fifty-six."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The children of the other Elam, one thousand two hundred fifty-four."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The children of Harim, three hundred twenty."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The children of Lod, Hadid, and Ono, seven hundred twenty-five."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The children of Jericho, three hundred forty-five."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The children of Senaah, three thousand six hundred thirty."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The priests: the children of Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua, nine hundred seventy-three."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The children of Immer, one thousand fifty-two."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The children of Pashhur, one thousand two hundred forty-seven."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The children of Harim, one thousand seventeen."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"The Levites: the children of Jeshua and Kadmiel, of the children of Hodaviah, seventy-four."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The singers: the children of Asaph, one hundred twenty-eight."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"The children of the gatekeepers: the children of Shallum, the children of Ater, the children of Talmon, the children of Akkub, the children of Hatita, the children of Shobai, in all one hundred thirty-nine."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"The temple servants: the children of Ziha, the children of Hasupha, the children of Tabbaoth,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"the children of Keros, the children of Siaha, the children of Padon,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"the children of Lebanah, the children of Hagabah, the children of Akkub,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"the children of Hagab, the children of Shamlai, the children of Hanan,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"the children of Giddel, the children of Gahar, the children of Reaiah,"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"the children of Rezin, the children of Nekoda, the children of Gazzam,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"the children of Uzza, the children of Paseah, the children of Besai,"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"the children of Asnah, the children of Meunim, the children of Nephisim,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"the children of Bakbuk, the children of Hakupha, the children of Harhur,"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"the children of Bazluth, the children of Mehida, the children of Harsha,"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"the children of Barkos, the children of Sisera, the children of Temah,"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"the children of Neziah, the children of Hatipha."]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Solomon\u2019s servants: the children of Sotai, the children of Hassophereth, the children of Peruda,"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"the children of Jaalah, the children of Darkon, the children of Giddel,"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"the children of Shephatiah, the children of Hattil, the children of Pochereth Hazzebaim, the children of Ami."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"All the temple servants, and the children of Solomon\u2019s servants, were three hundred ninety-two."]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"These were those who went up from Tel Melah, Tel Harsha, Cherub, Addan, and Immer; but they could not show their fathers\u2019 houses and their offspring, whether they were of Israel:"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:60,l:[[0,"the children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda, six hundred fifty-two."]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"Of the children of the priests: the children of Habaiah, the children of Hakkoz, and the children of Barzillai, who took a wife of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite, and was called after their name."]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"These sought their place among those who were registered by genealogy, but they were not found; therefore they were deemed disqualified and removed from the priesthood."]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"The governor told them that they should not eat of the most holy things until a priest stood up to serve with Urim and with Thummim."]]},{v:64,p:1,l:[[0,"The whole assembly together was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,"]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"in addition to their male servants and their female servants, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred thirty-seven; and they had two hundred singing men and singing women."]]},{v:66,l:[[0,"Their horses were seven hundred thirty-six; their mules, two hundred forty-five;"]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"their camels, four hundred thirty-five; their donkeys, six thousand seven hundred twenty."]]},{v:68,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of the heads of fathers\u2019 households, when they came to the LORD\u2019s house which is in Jerusalem, offered willingly for God\u2019s house to set it up in its place."]]},{v:69,l:[[0,"They gave according to their ability into the treasury of the work sixty-one thousand darics of gold, five thousand minas of silver, and one hundred priests\u2019 garments."]],f:["a daric was a gold coin issued by a Persian king, weighing about 8.4 grams or about 0.27 troy ounces each.","A mina is about 600 grams or 1.3 U. S. pounds, so 5,000 minas is about 3 metric tons."]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[0,"So the priests and the Levites, with some of the people, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants, lived in their cities, and all Israel in their cities."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the seventh month had come, and the children of Israel were in the cities, the people gathered themselves together as one man to Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Jeshua the son of Jozadak stood up with his brothers the priests and Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel and his relatives, and built the altar of the God of Israel, to offer burnt offerings on it, as it is written in the law of Moses the man of God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In spite of their fear because of the peoples of the surrounding lands, they set the altar on its base; and they offered burnt offerings on it to the LORD, even burnt offerings morning and evening."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They kept the feast of booths, as it is written, and offered the daily burnt offerings by number, according to the ordinance, as the duty of every day required;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and afterward the continual burnt offering, the offerings of the new moons, of all the set feasts of the LORD that were consecrated, and of everyone who willingly offered a free will offering to the LORD."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"From the first day of the seventh month, they began to offer burnt offerings to the LORD; but the foundation of the LORD\u2019s temple was not yet laid."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They also gave money to the masons and to the carpenters. They also gave food, drink, and oil to the people of Sidon and Tyre to bring cedar trees from Lebanon to the sea, to Joppa, according to the grant that they had from Cyrus King of Persia."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the second year of their coming to God\u2019s house at Jerusalem, in the second month, Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, Jeshua the son of Jozadak, and the rest of their brothers the priests and the Levites, and all those who had come out of the captivity to Jerusalem, began the work and appointed the Levites, from twenty years old and upward, to have the oversight of the work of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Jeshua stood with his sons and his brothers, Kadmiel and his sons, the sons of Judah, together to have the oversight of the workmen in God\u2019s house: the sons of Henadad, with their sons and their brothers the Levites."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When the builders laid the foundation of the LORD\u2019s temple, they set the priests in their vestments with trumpets, with the Levites the sons of Asaph with cymbals, to praise the LORD, according to the directions of David king of Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They sang to one another in praising and giving thanks to the LORD, \u201cFor he is good, for his loving kindness endures forever toward Israel.\u201d All the people shouted with a great shout, when they praised the LORD, because the foundation of the LORD\u2019s house had been laid."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"But many of the priests and Levites and heads of fathers\u2019 households, the old men who had seen the first house, when the foundation of this house was laid before their eyes, wept with a loud voice. Many also shouted aloud for joy,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"so that the people could not discern the noise of the shout of joy from the noise of the weeping of the people; for the people shouted with a loud shout, and the noise was heard far away."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when the adversaries of Judah and Benjamin heard that the children of the captivity were building a temple to the LORD, the God of Israel,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"they came near to Zerubbabel, and to the heads of fathers\u2019 households, and said to them, \u201cLet us build with you, for we seek your God as you do; and we have been sacrificing to him since the days of Esar Haddon king of Assyria, who brought us up here.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"But Zerubbabel, Jeshua, and the rest of the heads of fathers\u2019 households of Israel said to them, \u201cYou have nothing to do with us in building a house to our God; but we ourselves together will build to the LORD, the God of Israel, as King Cyrus the king of Persia has commanded us.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the people of the land weakened the hands of the people of Judah, and troubled them in building."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They hired counselors against them to frustrate their purpose all the days of Cyrus king of Persia, even until the reign of Darius king of Persia."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In the reign of Ahasuerus, in the beginning of his reign, they wrote an accusation against the inhabitants of Judah and Jerusalem."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"In the days of Artaxerxes, Bishlam, Mithredath, Tabeel, and the rest of his companions wrote to Artaxerxes king of Persia; and the writing of the letter was written in Syrian and delivered in the Syrian language."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Rehum the chancellor and Shimshai the scribe wrote a letter against Jerusalem to Artaxerxes the king as follows."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Rehum the chancellor, Shimshai the scribe, and the rest of their companions, the Dinaites, and the Apharsathchites, the Tarpelites, the Apharsites, the Archevites, the Babylonians, the Shushanchites, the Dehaites, the Elamites,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and the rest of the nations whom the great and noble Osnappar brought over and settled in the city of Samaria, and in the rest of the country beyond the River, and so forth, wrote."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the copy of the letter that they sent:"],[0,"To King Artaxerxes, from your servants, the people beyond the River."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Be it known to the king that the Jews who came up from you have come to us to Jerusalem. They are building the rebellious and bad city, and have finished the walls and repaired the foundations."]]},{v:13,l:[[1,"Be it known now to the king that if this city is built and the walls finished, they will not pay tribute, custom, or toll, and in the end it will be hurtful to the kings."]]},{v:14,l:[[1,"Now because we eat the salt of the palace and it is not appropriate for us to see the king\u2019s dishonor, therefore we have sent and informed the king,"]]},{v:15,l:[[1,"that search may be made in the book of the records of your fathers. You will see in the book of the records, and know that this city is a rebellious city, and hurtful to kings and provinces, and that they have started rebellions within it in the past. That is why this city was destroyed."]]},{v:16,l:[[1,"We inform the king that if this city is built and the walls finished, then you will have no possession beyond the River."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king sent an answer to Rehum the chancellor, and to Shimshai the scribe, and to the rest of their companions who live in Samaria, and in the rest of the country beyond the River:"],[0,"Peace."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The letter which you sent to us has been plainly read before me."]]},{v:19,l:[[1,"I decreed, and search has been made, and it was found that this city has made insurrection against kings in the past, and that rebellion and revolts have been made in it."]]},{v:20,l:[[1,"There have also been mighty kings over Jerusalem who have ruled over all the country beyond the River; and tribute, custom, and toll was paid to them."]]},{v:21,l:[[1,"Make a decree now to cause these men to cease, and that this city not be built until a decree is made by me."]]},{v:22,l:[[1,"Be careful that you not be slack doing so. Why should damage grow to the hurt of the kings?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then when the copy of King Artaxerxes\u2019 letter was read before Rehum, Shimshai the scribe, and their companions, they went in haste to Jerusalem to the Jews, and made them to cease by force of arms."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then work stopped on God\u2019s house which is at Jerusalem. It stopped until the second year of the reign of Darius king of Persia."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the prophets, Haggai the prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo, prophesied to the Jews who were in Judah and Jerusalem. They prophesied to them in the name of the God of Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua the son of Jozadak rose up and began to build God\u2019s house which is at Jerusalem; and with them were the prophets of God, helping them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"At the same time Tattenai, the governor beyond the River, came to them, with Shetharbozenai and their companions, and asked them, \u201cWho gave you a decree to build this house and to finish this wall?\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They also asked for the names of the men who were making this building."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But the eye of their God was on the elders of the Jews, and they didn\u2019t make them cease until the matter should come to Darius, and an answer should be returned by letter concerning it."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The copy of the letter that Tattenai, the governor beyond the River, and Shetharbozenai, and his companions the Apharsachites who were beyond the River, sent to Darius the king follows."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They sent a letter to him, in which was written:"],[0,"To Darius the king, all peace."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Be it known to the king that we went into the province of Judah, to the house of the great God, which is being built with great stones and timber is laid in the walls. This work goes on with diligence and prospers in their hands."]]},{v:9,l:[[1,"Then we asked those elders, and said to them thus, \u201cWho gave you a decree to build this house, and to finish this wall?\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[1,"We asked them their names also, to inform you that we might write the names of the men who were at their head."]]},{v:11,l:[[1,"Thus they returned us answer, saying, \u201cWe are the servants of the God of heaven and earth and are building the house that was built these many years ago, which a great king of Israel built and finished."]]},{v:12,l:[[1,"But after our fathers had provoked the God of heaven to wrath, he gave them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, the Chaldean, who destroyed this house and carried the people away into Babylon."]]},{v:13,l:[[1,"But in the first year of Cyrus king of Babylon, Cyrus the king made a decree to build this house of God."]]},{v:14,l:[[1,"The gold and silver vessels of God\u2019s house, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple that was in Jerusalem and brought into the temple of Babylon, those Cyrus the king also took out of the temple of Babylon, and they were delivered to one whose name was Sheshbazzar, whom he had made governor."]]},{v:15,l:[[1,"He said to him, \u2018Take these vessels, go, put them in the temple that is in Jerusalem, and let God\u2019s house be built in its place.\u2019"]]},{v:16,l:[[1,"Then the same Sheshbazzar came and laid the foundations of God\u2019s house which is in Jerusalem. Since that time even until now it has been being built, and yet it is not completed."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Now therefore, if it seems good to the king, let a search be made in the king\u2019s treasure house, which is there at Babylon, whether it is so that a decree was made by Cyrus the king to build this house of God at Jerusalem; and let the king send his pleasure to us concerning this matter.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Darius the king made a decree, and the house of the archives, where the treasures were laid up in Babylon, was searched."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"A scroll was found at Achmetha, in the palace that is in the province of Media, and in it this was written for a record:"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"In the first year of Cyrus the king, Cyrus the king made a decree: Concerning God\u2019s house at Jerusalem, let the house be built, the place where they offer sacrifices, and let its foundations be strongly laid, with its height sixty cubits and its width sixty cubits;"]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:4,l:[[1,"with three courses of great stones and a course of new timber. Let the expenses be given out of the king\u2019s house."]]},{v:5,l:[[1,"Also let the gold and silver vessels of God\u2019s house, which Nebuchadnezzar took out of the temple which is at Jerusalem and brought to Babylon, be restored and brought again to the temple which is at Jerusalem, everything to its place. You shall put them in God\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Now therefore, Tattenai, governor beyond the River, Shetharbozenai, and your companions the Apharsachites, who are beyond the River, you must stay far from there."]]},{v:7,l:[[1,"Leave the work of this house of God alone; let the governor of the Jews and the elders of the Jews build this house of God in its place."]]},{v:8,l:[[1,"Moreover I make a decree regarding what you shall do for these elders of the Jews for the building of this house of God: that of the king\u2019s goods, even of the tribute beyond the River, expenses must be given with all diligence to these men, that they not be hindered."]]},{v:9,l:[[1,"That which they have need of, including young bulls, rams, and lambs, for burnt offerings to the God of heaven; also wheat, salt, wine, and oil, according to the word of the priests who are at Jerusalem, let it be given them day by day without fail,"]]},{v:10,l:[[1,"that they may offer sacrifices of pleasant aroma to the God of heaven, and pray for the life of the king and of his sons."]]},{v:11,l:[[1,"I have also made a decree that whoever alters this message, let a beam be pulled out from his house, and let him be lifted up and fastened on it; and let his house be made a dunghill for this."]]},{v:12,l:[[1,"May the God who has caused his name to dwell there overthrow all kings and peoples who stretch out their hand to alter this, to destroy this house of God which is at Jerusalem. I Darius have made a decree. Let it be done with all diligence."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Tattenai, the governor beyond the River, Shetharbozenai, and their companions did accordingly with all diligence, because Darius the king had sent a decree."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The elders of the Jews built and prospered, through the prophesying of Haggai the prophet and Zechariah the son of Iddo. They built and finished it, according to the commandment of the God of Israel, and according to the decree of Cyrus, Darius, and Artaxerxes king of Persia."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"This house was finished on the third day of the month Adar, which was in the sixth year of the reign of Darius the king."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Israel, the priests, the Levites, and the rest of the children of the captivity, kept the dedication of this house of God with joy."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They offered at the dedication of this house of God one hundred bulls, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs; and for a sin offering for all Israel, twelve male goats, according to the number of the tribes of Israel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They set the priests in their divisions and the Levites in their courses, for the service of God which is at Jerusalem, as it is written in the book of Moses."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of the captivity kept the Passover on the fourteenth day of the first month."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Because the priests and the Levites had purified themselves together, all of them were pure. They killed the Passover for all the children of the captivity, for their brothers the priests, and for themselves."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The children of Israel who had returned out of the captivity, and all who had separated themselves to them from the filthiness of the nations of the land to seek the LORD, the God of Israel, ate,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with joy; because the LORD had made them joyful, and had turned the heart of the king of Assyria to them, to strengthen their hands in the work of God, the God of Israel\u2019s house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after these things, in the reign of Artaxerxes king of Persia, Ezra the son of Seraiah, the son of Azariah, the son of Hilkiah,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"the son of Shallum, the son of Zadok, the son of Ahitub,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"the son of Amariah, the son of Azariah, the son of Meraioth,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"the son of Zerahiah, the son of Uzzi, the son of Bukki,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"the son of Abishua, the son of Phinehas, the son of Eleazar, the son of Aaron the chief priest\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"this Ezra went up from Babylon. He was a skilled scribe in the law of Moses, which the LORD, the God of Israel, had given; and the king granted him all his request, according to the LORD his God\u2019s hand on him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Some of the children of Israel, including some of the priests, the Levites, the singers, the gatekeepers, and the temple servants went up to Jerusalem in the seventh year of Artaxerxes the king."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He came to Jerusalem in the fifth month, which was in the seventh year of the king."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For on the first day of the first month he began to go up from Babylon; and on the first day of the fifth month he came to Jerusalem, according to the good hand of his God on him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For Ezra had set his heart to seek the LORD\u2019s law, and to do it, and to teach statutes and ordinances in Israel."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this is the copy of the letter that King Artaxerxes gave to Ezra the priest, the scribe, even the scribe of the words of the LORD\u2019s commandments, and of his statutes to Israel:"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Artaxerxes, king of kings,"],[0,"To Ezra the priest, the scribe of the law of the perfect God of heaven."],[1,"Now"]]},{v:13,l:[[1,"I make a decree that all those of the people of Israel and their priests and the Levites in my realm, who intend of their own free will to go to Jerusalem, go with you."]]},{v:14,l:[[1,"Because you are sent by the king and his seven counselors to inquire concerning Judah and Jerusalem, according to the law of your God which is in your hand,"]]},{v:15,l:[[1,"and to carry the silver and gold, which the king and his counselors have freely offered to the God of Israel, whose habitation is in Jerusalem,"]]},{v:16,l:[[1,"and all the silver and gold that you will find in all the province of Babylon, with the free will offering of the people and of the priests, offering willingly for the house of their God which is in Jerusalem."]]},{v:17,l:[[1,"Therefore you shall with all diligence buy with this money bulls, rams, and lambs with their meal offerings and their drink offerings, and shall offer them on the altar of the house of your God which is in Jerusalem."]]},{v:18,l:[[1,"Whatever seems good to you and to your brothers to do with the rest of the silver and the gold, do that according to the will of your God."]]},{v:19,l:[[1,"The vessels that are given to you for the service of the house of your God, deliver before the God of Jerusalem."]]},{v:20,l:[[1,"Whatever more will be needed for the house of your God, which you may have occasion to give, give it out of the king\u2019s treasure house."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"I, even I, Artaxerxes the king, make a decree to all the treasurers who are beyond the River, that whatever Ezra the priest, the scribe of the law of the God of heaven, requires of you, it shall be done with all diligence,"]]},{v:22,l:[[1,"up to one hundred talents of silver, and to one hundred cors of wheat, and to one hundred baths of wine, and to one hundred baths of oil, and salt without prescribing how much."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces","1 cor is the same as a homer, or about 55.9 U. S. gallons (liquid) or 211 liters or 6 bushels.","1 bath is one tenth of a cor, or about 5.6 U. S. gallons or 21 liters or 2.4 pecks. 100 baths would be about 2,100 liters."]},{v:23,l:[[1,"Whatever is commanded by the God of heaven, let it be done exactly for the house of the God of heaven; for why should there be wrath against the realm of the king and his sons?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Also we inform you that it shall not be lawful to impose tribute, custom, or toll on any of the priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, temple servants, or laborers of this house of God."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"You, Ezra, according to the wisdom of your God that is in your hand, appoint magistrates and judges who may judge all the people who are beyond the River, who all know the laws of your God; and teach him who doesn\u2019t know them."]]},{v:26,l:[[1,"Whoever will not do the law of your God and the law of the king, let judgment be executed on him with all diligence, whether it is to death, or to banishment, or to confiscation of goods, or to imprisonment."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Blessed be the LORD, the God of our fathers, who has put such a thing as this in the king\u2019s heart, to beautify the LORD\u2019s house which is in Jerusalem;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and has extended loving kindness to me before the king and his counselors, and before all the king\u2019s mighty princes. I was strengthened according to the LORD my God\u2019s hand on me, and I gathered together chief men out of Israel to go up with me."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the heads of their fathers\u2019 households, and this is the genealogy of those who went up with me from Babylon, in the reign of Artaxerxes the king:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Phinehas, Gershom."],[1,"Of the sons of Ithamar, Daniel."],[1,"Of the sons of David, Hattush."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Shecaniah, of the sons of Parosh, Zechariah; and with him were listed by genealogy of the males one hundred fifty."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Pahathmoab, Eliehoenai the son of Zerahiah; and with him two hundred males."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Shecaniah, the son of Jahaziel; and with him three hundred males."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Adin, Ebed the son of Jonathan; and with him fifty males."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Elam, Jeshaiah the son of Athaliah; and with him seventy males."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Shephatiah, Zebadiah the son of Michael; and with him eighty males."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Joab, Obadiah the son of Jehiel; and with him two hundred eighteen males."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Shelomith, the son of Josiphiah; and with him one hundred sixty males."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Bebai, Zechariah the son of Bebai; and with him twenty-eight males."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Azgad, Johanan the son of Hakkatan; and with him one hundred ten males."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Adonikam, who were the last, their names are: Eliphelet, Jeuel, and Shemaiah; and with them sixty males."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Bigvai, Uthai and Zabbud; and with them seventy males."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"I gathered them together to the river that runs to Ahava; and there we encamped three days. Then I looked around at the people and the priests, and found there were none of the sons of Levi."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then I sent for Eliezer, for Ariel, for Shemaiah, for Elnathan, for Jarib, for Elnathan, for Nathan, for Zechariah, and for Meshullam, chief men; also for Joiarib and for Elnathan, who were teachers."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I sent them out to Iddo the chief at the place Casiphia; and I told them what they should tell Iddo and his brothers the temple servants at the place Casiphia, that they should bring to us ministers for the house of our God."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"According to the good hand of our God on us they brought us a man of discretion, of the sons of Mahli, the son of Levi, the son of Israel, namely Sherebiah, with his sons and his brothers, eighteen;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and Hashabiah, and with him Jeshaiah of the sons of Merari, his brothers and their sons, twenty;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and of the temple servants, whom David and the princes had given for the service of the Levites, two hundred twenty temple servants. All of them were mentioned by name."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I proclaimed a fast there at the river Ahava, that we might humble ourselves before our God, to seek from him a straight way for us, for our little ones, and for all our possessions."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For I was ashamed to ask of the king a band of soldiers and horsemen to help us against the enemy on the way, because we had spoken to the king, saying, \u201cThe hand of our God is on all those who seek him, for good; but his power and his wrath is against all those who forsake him.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So we fasted and begged our God for this, and he granted our request."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I set apart twelve of the chiefs of the priests, even Sherebiah, Hashabiah, and ten of their brothers with them,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and weighed to them the silver, the gold, and the vessels, even the offering for the house of our God, which the king, his counselors, his princes, and all Israel there present, had offered."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I weighed into their hand six hundred fifty talents of silver, one hundred talents of silver vessels, one hundred talents of gold,"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:27,l:[[0,"twenty bowls of gold weighing one thousand darics, and two vessels of fine bright bronze, precious as gold."]],f:["a daric was a gold coin issued by a Persian king, weighing about 8.4 grams or about 0.27 troy ounces each."]},{v:28,l:[[0,"I said to them, \u201cYou are holy to the LORD, and the vessels are holy. The silver and the gold are a free will offering to the LORD, the God of your fathers."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Watch and keep them until you weigh them before the chiefs of the priests, the Levites, and the princes of the fathers\u2019 households of Israel at Jerusalem, in the rooms of the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"So the priests and the Levites received the weight of the silver, the gold, and the vessels, to bring them to Jerusalem to the house of our God."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then we departed from the river Ahava on the twelfth day of the first month, to go to Jerusalem. The hand of our God was on us, and he delivered us from the hand of the enemy and the bandits by the way."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"We came to Jerusalem, and stayed there three days."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"On the fourth day the silver and the gold and the vessels were weighed in the house of our God into the hand of Meremoth the son of Uriah the priest; and with him was Eleazar the son of Phinehas; and with them were Jozabad the son of Jeshua, and Noadiah the son of Binnui, the Levites."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Everything was counted and weighed; and all the weight was written at that time."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of the captivity, who had come out of exile, offered burnt offerings to the God of Israel: twelve bulls for all Israel, ninety-six rams, seventy-seven lambs, and twelve male goats for a sin offering. All this was a burnt offering to the LORD."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"They delivered the king\u2019s commissions to the king\u2019s local governors and to the governors beyond the River. So they supported the people and God\u2019s house."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when these things were done, the princes came near to me, saying, \u201cThe people of Israel, the priests, and the Levites have not separated themselves from the peoples of the lands, following their abominations, even those of the Canaanites, the Hittites, the Perizzites, the Jebusites, the Ammonites, the Moabites, the Egyptians, and the Amorites."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For they have taken of their daughters for themselves and for their sons, so that the holy offspring have mixed themselves with the peoples of the lands. Yes, the hand of the princes and rulers has been chief in this trespass.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"When I heard this thing, I tore my garment and my robe, and pulled the hair out of my head and of my beard, and sat down confounded."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then everyone who trembled at the words of the God of Israel were assembled to me because of the trespass of the exiles; and I sat confounded until the evening offering."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"At the evening offering I rose up from my humiliation, even with my garment and my robe torn; and I fell on my knees, and spread out my hands to the LORD my God;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and I said, \u201cMy God, I am ashamed and blush to lift up my face to you, my God, for our iniquities have increased over our head, and our guiltiness has grown up to the heavens."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Since the days of our fathers we have been exceedingly guilty to this day; and for our iniquities we, our kings, and our priests have been delivered into the hand of the kings of the lands, to the sword, to captivity, to plunder, and to confusion of face, as it is this day."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now for a little moment grace has been shown from the LORD our God, to leave us a remnant to escape, and to give us a stake in his holy place, that our God may lighten our eyes, and revive us a little in our bondage."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For we are bondservants; yet our God has not forsaken us in our bondage, but has extended loving kindness to us in the sight of the kings of Persia, to revive us, to set up the house of our God, and to repair its ruins, and to give us a wall in Judah and in Jerusalem."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, our God, what shall we say after this? For we have forsaken your commandments,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"which you have commanded by your servants the prophets, saying, \u2018The land to which you go to possess is an unclean land through the uncleanness of the peoples of the lands, through their abominations, which have filled it from one end to another with their filthiness."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now therefore don\u2019t give your daughters to their sons. Don\u2019t take their daughters to your sons, nor seek their peace or their prosperity forever, that you may be strong and eat the good of the land, and leave it for an inheritance to your children forever.\u2019"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAfter all that has come on us for our evil deeds and for our great guilt, since you, our God, have punished us less than our iniquities deserve, and have given us such a remnant,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"shall we again break your commandments, and join ourselves with the peoples that do these abominations? Wouldn\u2019t you be angry with us until you had consumed us, so that there would be no remnant, nor any to escape?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"LORD, the God of Israel, you are righteous; for we are left a remnant that has escaped, as it is today. Behold, we are before you in our guiltiness; for no one can stand before you because of this.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now while Ezra prayed and made confession, weeping and casting himself down before God\u2019s house, there was gathered together to him out of Israel a very great assembly of men and women and children; for the people wept very bitterly."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Shecaniah the son of Jehiel, one of the sons of Elam, answered Ezra, \u201cWe have trespassed against our God, and have married foreign women of the peoples of the land. Yet now there is hope for Israel concerning this thing."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now therefore let\u2019s make a covenant with our God to put away all the wives and those who are born of them, according to the counsel of my lord and of those who tremble at the commandment of our God. Let it be done according to the law."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Arise, for the matter belongs to you and we are with you. Be courageous, and do it.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Ezra arose, and made the chiefs of the priests, the Levites, and all Israel to swear that they would do according to this word. So they swore."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then Ezra rose up from before God\u2019s house, and went into the room of Jehohanan the son of Eliashib. When he came there, he didn\u2019t eat bread or drink water, for he mourned because of the trespass of the exiles."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They made a proclamation throughout Judah and Jerusalem to all the children of the captivity, that they should gather themselves together to Jerusalem;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and that whoever didn\u2019t come within three days, according to the counsel of the princes and the elders, all his possessions should be forfeited, and he himself separated from the assembly of the captivity."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the men of Judah and Benjamin gathered themselves together to Jerusalem within the three days. It was the ninth month, on the twentieth day of the month; and all the people sat in the wide place in front of God\u2019s house, trembling because of this matter, and because of the great rain."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Ezra the priest stood up and said to them, \u201cYou have trespassed, and have married foreign women, increasing the guilt of Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now therefore make confession to the LORD, the God of your fathers and do his pleasure. Separate yourselves from the peoples of the land and from the foreign women.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the assembly answered with a loud voice, \u201cWe must do as you have said concerning us."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But the people are many, and it is a time of much rain, and we are not able to stand outside. This is not a work of one day or two, for we have greatly transgressed in this matter."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now let our princes be appointed for all the assembly, and let all those who are in our cities who have married foreign women come at appointed times, and with them the elders of every city and its judges, until the fierce wrath of our God is turned from us, until this matter is resolved.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Only Jonathan the son of Asahel and Jahzeiah the son of Tikvah stood up against this; and Meshullam and Shabbethai the Levite helped them."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of the captivity did so. Ezra the priest, with certain heads of fathers\u2019 households, after their fathers\u2019 houses, and all of them by their names, were set apart; and they sat down in the first day of the tenth month to examine the matter."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They finished with all the men who had married foreign women by the first day of the first month."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Among the sons of the priests there were found who had married foreign women:"],[1,"of the sons of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and his brothers: Maaseiah, Eliezer, Jarib, and Gedaliah."]]},{v:19,l:[[1,"They gave their hand that they would put away their wives; and being guilty, they offered a ram of the flock for their guilt."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Immer: Hanani and Zebadiah."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Harim: Maaseiah, Elijah, Shemaiah, Jehiel, and Uzziah."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Pashhur: Elioenai, Maaseiah, Ishmael, Nethanel, Jozabad, and Elasah."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the Levites: Jozabad, Shimei, Kelaiah (also called Kelita), Pethahiah, Judah, and Eliezer."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the singers: Eliashib."],[1,"Of the gatekeepers: Shallum, Telem, and Uri."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Of Israel: Of the sons of Parosh: Ramiah, Izziah, Malchijah, Mijamin, Eleazar, Malchijah, and Benaiah."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Elam: Mattaniah, Zechariah, Jehiel, Abdi, Jeremoth, and Elijah."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Zattu: Elioenai, Eliashib, Mattaniah, Jeremoth, Zabad, and Aziza."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Bebai: Jehohanan, Hananiah, Zabbai, and Athlai."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Bani: Meshullam, Malluch, Adaiah, Jashub, Sheal, and Jeremoth."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Pahathmoab: Adna, Chelal, Benaiah, Maaseiah, Mattaniah, Bezalel, Binnui, and Manasseh."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Harim: Eliezer, Isshijah, Malchijah, Shemaiah, Shimeon,"]]},{v:32,l:[[1,"Benjamin, Malluch, and Shemariah."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Hashum: Mattenai, Mattattah, Zabad, Eliphelet, Jeremai, Manasseh, and Shimei."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Bani: Maadai, Amram, Uel,"]]},{v:35,l:[[1,"Benaiah, Bedeiah, Cheluhi,"]]},{v:36,l:[[1,"Vaniah, Meremoth, Eliashib,"]]},{v:37,l:[[1,"Mattaniah, Mattenai, Jaasu,"]]},{v:38,l:[[1,"Bani, Binnui, Shimei,"]]},{v:39,l:[[1,"Shelemiah, Nathan, Adaiah,"]]},{v:40,l:[[1,"Machnadebai, Shashai, Sharai,"]]},{v:41,l:[[1,"Azarel, Shelemiah, Shemariah,"]]},{v:42,l:[[1,"Shallum, Amariah, and Joseph."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the sons of Nebo: Jeiel, Mattithiah, Zabad, Zebina, Iddo, Joel, and Benaiah."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"All these had taken foreign wives. Some of them had wives by whom they had children."]]}]]}},1286,[]);
__d(function(e,t,h,o,a,n,i){a.exports={book:"Neh",name:"Nehemiah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The words of Nehemiah the son of Hacaliah."],[0,"Now in the month Chislev, in the twentieth year, as I was in Susa the palace,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Hanani, one of my brothers, came, he and certain men out of Judah; and I asked them about the Jews who had escaped, who were left of the captivity, and concerning Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They said to me, \u201cThe remnant who are left of the captivity there in the province are in great affliction and reproach. The wall of Jerusalem is also broken down, and its gates are burned with fire.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When I heard these words, I sat down and wept, and mourned several days; and I fasted and prayed before the God of heaven,"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cI beg you, LORD, the God of heaven, the great and awesome God who keeps covenant and loving kindness with those who love him and keep his commandments,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"let your ear now be attentive and your eyes open, that you may listen to the prayer of your servant which I pray before you at this time, day and night, for the children of Israel your servants, while I confess the sins of the children of Israel which we have sinned against you. Yes, I and my father\u2019s house have sinned."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"We have dealt very corruptly against you, and have not kept the commandments, nor the statutes, nor the ordinances, which you commanded your servant Moses."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cRemember, I beg you, the word that you commanded your servant Moses, saying, \u2018If you trespass, I will scatter you among the peoples;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but if you return to me, and keep my commandments and do them, though your outcasts were in the uttermost part of the heavens, yet I will gather them from there, and will bring them to the place that I have chosen, to cause my name to dwell there.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow these are your servants and your people, whom you have redeemed by your great power and by your strong hand."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Lord, I beg you, let your ear be attentive now to the prayer of your servant, and to the prayer of your servants who delight to fear your name; and please prosper your servant today, and grant him mercy in the sight of this man.\u201d"],[0,"Now I was cup bearer to the king."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the month Nisan, in the twentieth year of Artaxerxes the king, when wine was before him, I picked up the wine, and gave it to the king. Now I had not been sad before in his presence."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The king said to me, \u201cWhy is your face sad, since you are not sick? This is nothing else but sorrow of heart.\u201d"],[0,"Then I was very much afraid."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I said to the king, \u201cLet the king live forever! Why shouldn\u2019t my face be sad, when the city, the place of my fathers\u2019 tombs, lies waste, and its gates have been consumed with fire?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said to me, \u201cWhat is your request?\u201d"],[0,"So I prayed to the God of heaven."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I said to the king, \u201cIf it pleases the king, and if your servant has found favor in your sight, I ask that you would send me to Judah, to the city of my fathers\u2019 tombs, that I may build it.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to me (the queen was also sitting by him), \u201cHow long will your journey be? When will you return?\u201d"],[0,"So it pleased the king to send me, and I set a time for him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Moreover I said to the king, \u201cIf it pleases the king, let letters be given me to the governors beyond the River, that they may let me pass through until I come to Judah;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and a letter to Asaph the keeper of the king\u2019s forest, that he may give me timber to make beams for the gates of the citadel by the temple, for the wall of the city, and for the house that I will occupy.\u201d"],[0,"The king granted my requests, because of the good hand of my God on me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then I came to the governors beyond the River, and gave them the king\u2019s letters. Now the king had sent captains of the army and horsemen with me."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When Sanballat the Horonite and Tobiah the Ammonite servant heard of it, it grieved them exceedingly, because a man had come to seek the welfare of the children of Israel."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"So I came to Jerusalem, and was there three days."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I arose in the night, I and a few men with me. I didn\u2019t tell anyone what my God put into my heart to do for Jerusalem. There wasn\u2019t any animal with me except the animal that I rode on."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I went out by night by the valley gate toward the jackal\u2019s well, then to the dung gate; and I inspected the walls of Jerusalem, which were broken down, and its gates were consumed with fire."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Then I went on to the spring gate and to the king\u2019s pool, but there was no place for the animal that was under me to pass."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then I went up in the night by the brook and inspected the wall; and I turned back, and entered by the valley gate, and so returned."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The rulers didn\u2019t know where I went, or what I did. I had not as yet told it to the Jews, nor to the priests, nor to the nobles, nor to the rulers, nor to the rest who did the work."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said to them, \u201cYou see the bad situation that we are in, how Jerusalem lies waste, and its gates are burned with fire. Come, let\u2019s build up the wall of Jerusalem, that we won\u2019t be disgraced.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I told them about the hand of my God which was good on me, and also about the king\u2019s words that he had spoken to me."],[0,"They said, \u201cLet\u2019s rise up and build.\u201d So they strengthened their hands for the good work."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Sanballat the Horonite, Tobiah the Ammonite servant, and Geshem the Arabian, heard it, they ridiculed us and despised us, and said, \u201cWhat is this thing that you are doing? Will you rebel against the king?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I answered them, and said to them, \u201cThe God of heaven will prosper us. Therefore we, his servants, will arise and build; but you have no portion, nor right, nor memorial in Jerusalem.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eliashib the high priest rose up with his brothers the priests, and they built the sheep gate. They sanctified it, and set up its doors. They sanctified it even to the tower of Hammeah, to the tower of Hananel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Next to him the men of Jericho built. Next to them Zaccur the son of Imri built."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The sons of Hassenaah built the fish gate. They laid its beams, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Next to them, Meremoth the son of Uriah, the son of Hakkoz made repairs. Next to them, Meshullam the son of Berechiah, the son of Meshezabel made repairs. Next to them, Zadok the son of Baana made repairs."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Next to them, the Tekoites made repairs; but their nobles didn\u2019t put their necks to the Lord\u2019s work."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Joiada the son of Paseah and Meshullam the son of Besodeiah repaired the old gate. They laid its beams and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Next to them, Melatiah the Gibeonite and Jadon the Meronothite, the men of Gibeon and of Mizpah, repaired the residence of the governor beyond the River."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Next to him, Uzziel the son of Harhaiah, goldsmiths, made repairs. Next to him, Hananiah, one of the perfumers, made repairs, and they fortified Jerusalem even to the wide wall."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Next to them, Rephaiah the son of Hur, the ruler of half the district of Jerusalem, made repairs."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Next to them, Jedaiah the son of Harumaph made repairs across from his house. Next to him, Hattush the son of Hashabneiah made repairs."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Malchijah the son of Harim and Hasshub the son of Pahathmoab repaired another portion and the tower of the furnaces."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Next to him, Shallum the son of Hallohesh, the ruler of half the district of Jerusalem, he and his daughters made repairs."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Hanun and the inhabitants of Zanoah repaired the valley gate. They built it, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars, and one thousand cubits of the wall to the dung gate."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Malchijah the son of Rechab, the ruler of the district of Beth Haccherem, repaired the dung gate. He built it, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Shallun the son of Colhozeh, the ruler of the district of Mizpah, repaired the spring gate. He built it, covered it, and set up its doors, its bolts, and its bars; and he repaired the wall of the pool of Shelah by the king\u2019s garden, even to the stairs that go down from David\u2019s city."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"After him, Nehemiah the son of Azbuk, the ruler of half the district of Beth Zur, made repairs to the place opposite the tombs of David, and to the pool that was made, and to the house of the mighty men."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"After him, the Levites\u2014Rehum the son of Bani made repairs. Next to him, Hashabiah, the ruler of half the district of Keilah, made repairs for his district."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"After him, their brothers, Bavvai the son of Henadad, the ruler of half the district of Keilah made repairs."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Next to him, Ezer the son of Jeshua, the ruler of Mizpah, repaired another portion across from the ascent to the armory at the turning of the wall."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"After him, Baruch the son of Zabbai earnestly repaired another portion, from the turning of the wall to the door of the house of Eliashib the high priest."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"After him, Meremoth the son of Uriah the son of Hakkoz repaired another portion, from the door of the house of Eliashib even to the end of the house of Eliashib."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"After him, the priests, the men of the surrounding area made repairs."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"After them, Benjamin and Hasshub made repairs across from their house. After them, Azariah the son of Maaseiah the son of Ananiah made repairs beside his own house."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"After him, Binnui the son of Henadad repaired another portion, from the house of Azariah to the turning of the wall, and to the corner."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Palal the son of Uzai made repairs opposite the turning of the wall, and the tower that stands out from the upper house of the king, which is by the court of the guard. After him Pedaiah the son of Parosh made repairs."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"(Now the temple servants lived in Ophel, to the place opposite the water gate toward the east, and the tower that stands out.)"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"After him the Tekoites repaired another portion, opposite the great tower that stands out, and to the wall of Ophel."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Above the horse gate, the priests made repairs, everyone across from his own house."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"After them, Zadok the son of Immer made repairs across from his own house. After him, Shemaiah the son of Shecaniah, the keeper of the east gate, made repairs."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"After him, Hananiah the son of Shelemiah, and Hanun, the sixth son of Zalaph, repaired another portion. After him, Meshullam the son of Berechiah made repairs across from his room."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"After him, Malchijah, one of the goldsmiths to the house of the temple servants, and of the merchants, made repairs opposite the gate of Hammiphkad and to the ascent of the corner."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Between the ascent of the corner and the sheep gate, the goldsmiths and the merchants made repairs."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Sanballat heard that we were building the wall, he was angry, and was very indignant, and mocked the Jews."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He spoke before his brothers and the army of Samaria, and said, \u201cWhat are these feeble Jews doing? Will they fortify themselves? Will they sacrifice? Will they finish in a day? Will they revive the stones out of the heaps of rubbish, since they are burned?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Tobiah the Ammonite was by him, and he said, \u201cWhat they are building, if a fox climbed up it, he would break down their stone wall.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHear, our God, for we are despised. Turn back their reproach on their own head. Give them up for a plunder in a land of captivity."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t cover their iniquity. Don\u2019t let their sin be blotted out from before you; for they have insulted the builders.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"So we built the wall; and all the wall was joined together to half its height, for the people had a mind to work."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Sanballat, Tobiah, the Arabians, the Ammonites, and the Ashdodites heard that the repairing of the walls of Jerusalem went forward, and that the breaches began to be filled, they were very angry;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and they all conspired together to come and fight against Jerusalem, and to cause confusion among us."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But we made our prayer to our God, and set a watch against them day and night because of them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Judah said, \u201cThe strength of the bearers of burdens is fading and there is much rubble, so that we are not able to build the wall.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Our adversaries said, \u201cThey will not know or see, until we come in among them and kill them, and cause the work to cease.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Jews who lived by them came, they said to us ten times from all places, \u201cWherever you turn, they will attack us.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore I set guards in the lowest parts of the space behind the wall, in the open places. I set the people by family groups with their swords, their spears, and their bows."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I looked, and rose up, and said to the nobles, to the rulers, and to the rest of the people, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid of them! Remember the Lord, who is great and awesome, and fight for your brothers, your sons, your daughters, your wives, and your houses.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When our enemies heard that it was known to us, and God had brought their counsel to nothing, all of us returned to the wall, everyone to his work."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"From that time forth, half of my servants did the work, and half of them held the spears, the shields, the bows, and the coats of mail; and the rulers were behind all the house of Judah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Those who built the wall, and those who bore burdens loaded themselves; everyone with one of his hands did the work, and with the other held his weapon."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Among the builders, everyone wore his sword at his side, and so built. He who sounded the trumpet was by me."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I said to the nobles, and to the rulers and to the rest of the people, \u201cThe work is great and widely spread out, and we are separated on the wall, far from one another."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Wherever you hear the sound of the trumpet, rally there to us. Our God will fight for us.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"So we did the work. Half of the people held the spears from the rising of the morning until the stars appeared."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Likewise at the same time I said to the people, \u201cLet everyone with his servant lodge within Jerusalem, that in the night they may be a guard to us, and may labor in the day.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So neither I, nor my brothers, nor my servants, nor the men of the guard who followed me took off our clothes. Everyone took his weapon to the water."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then there arose a great cry of the people and of their wives against their brothers the Jews."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For there were some who said, \u201cWe, our sons and our daughters, are many. Let us get grain, that we may eat and live.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"There were also some who said, \u201cWe are mortgaging our fields, our vineyards, and our houses. Let us get grain, because of the famine.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"There were also some who said, \u201cWe have borrowed money for the king\u2019s tribute using our fields and our vineyards as collateral."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Yet now our flesh is as the flesh of our brothers, our children as their children. Behold, we bring our sons and our daughters into bondage to be servants, and some of our daughters have been brought into bondage. It is also not in our power to help it, because other men have our fields and our vineyards.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I was very angry when I heard their cry and these words."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then I consulted with myself, and contended with the nobles and the rulers, and said to them, \u201cYou exact usury, everyone of his brother.\u201d I held a great assembly against them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I said to them, \u201cWe, after our ability, have redeemed our brothers the Jews that were sold to the nations; and would you even sell your brothers, and should they be sold to us?\u201d Then they held their peace, and found not a word to say."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Also I said, \u201cThe thing that you do is not good. Shouldn\u2019t you walk in the fear of our God because of the reproach of the nations, our enemies?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I likewise, my brothers and my servants, lend them money and grain. Please let us stop this usury."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Please restore to them, even today, their fields, their vineyards, their olive groves, and their houses, also the hundredth part of the money, and of the grain, the new wine, and the oil, that you are charging them.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they said, \u201cWe will restore them, and will require nothing of them. We will do so, even as you say.\u201d"],[0,"Then I called the priests, and took an oath of them, that they would do according to this promise."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Also I shook out my lap, and said, \u201cSo may God shake out every man from his house, and from his labor, that doesn\u2019t perform this promise; even may he be shaken out and emptied like this.\u201d"],[0,"All the assembly said, \u201cAmen,\u201d and praised the LORD. The people did according to this promise."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover from the time that I was appointed to be their governor in the land of Judah, from the twentieth year even to the thirty-second year of Artaxerxes the king, that is, twelve years, I and my brothers have not eaten the bread of the governor."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But the former governors who were before me were supported by the people, and took bread and wine from them, plus forty shekels of silver; yes, even their servants ruled over the people, but I didn\u2019t do so, because of the fear of God."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Yes, I also continued in the work of this wall. We didn\u2019t buy any land. All my servants were gathered there to the work."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Moreover there were at my table, of the Jews and the rulers, one hundred fifty men, in addition to those who came to us from among the nations that were around us."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now that which was prepared for one day was one ox and six choice sheep. Also fowls were prepared for me, and once in ten days a store of all sorts of wine. Yet for all this, I didn\u2019t demand the governor\u2019s pay, because the bondage was heavy on this people."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Remember me, my God, for all the good that I have done for this people."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when it was reported to Sanballat, Tobiah, Geshem the Arabian, and to the rest of our enemies that I had built the wall, and that there was no breach left in it (though even to that time I had not set up the doors in the gates),"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Sanballat and Geshem sent to me, saying, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s meet together in the villages in the plain of Ono.\u201d But they intended to harm me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"I sent messengers to them, saying, \u201cI am doing a great work, so that I can\u2019t come down. Why should the work cease while I leave it and come down to you?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"They sent to me four times like this; and I answered them the same way."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then Sanballat sent his servant to me the same way the fifth time with an open letter in his hand,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"in which was written, \u201cIt is reported among the nations, and Gashmu says it, that you and the Jews intend to rebel. Because of that, you are building the wall. You would be their king, according to these words."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You have also appointed prophets to proclaim of you at Jerusalem, saying, \u2018There is a king in Judah!\u2019 Now it will be reported to the king according to these words. Come now therefore, and let\u2019s take counsel together.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I sent to him, saying, \u201cThere are no such things done as you say, but you imagine them out of your own heart.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For they all would have made us afraid, saying, \u201cTheir hands will be weakened from the work, that it not be done.\u201d But now, strengthen my hands."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"I went to the house of Shemaiah the son of Delaiah the son of Mehetabel, who was shut in at his home; and he said, \u201cLet us meet together in God\u2019s house, within the temple, and let\u2019s shut the doors of the temple; for they will come to kill you. Yes, in the night they will come to kill you.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"I said, \u201cShould a man like me flee? Who is there that, being such as I, would go into the temple to save his life? I will not go in.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I discerned, and behold, God had not sent him, but he pronounced this prophecy against me. Tobiah and Sanballat had hired him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He was hired so that I would be afraid, do so, and sin, and that they might have material for an evil report, that they might reproach me."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"\u201cRemember, my God, Tobiah and Sanballat according to these their works, and also the prophetess Noadiah and the rest of the prophets that would have put me in fear.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"So the wall was finished in the twenty-fifth day of Elul, in fifty-two days."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When all our enemies heard of it, all the nations that were around us were afraid, and they lost their confidence; for they perceived that this work was done by our God."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Moreover in those days the nobles of Judah sent many letters to Tobiah, and Tobiah\u2019s letters came to them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For there were many in Judah sworn to him because he was the son-in-law of Shecaniah the son of Arah; and his son Jehohanan had taken the daughter of Meshullam the son of Berechiah as wife."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Also they spoke of his good deeds before me, and reported my words to him. Tobiah sent letters to put me in fear."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when the wall was built and I had set up the doors, and the gatekeepers and the singers and the Levites were appointed,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I put my brother Hanani, and Hananiah the governor of the fortress, in charge of Jerusalem; for he was a faithful man and feared God above many."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t let the gates of Jerusalem be opened until the sun is hot; and while they stand guard, let them shut the doors, and you bar them; and appoint watches of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, everyone in his watch, with everyone near his house.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the city was wide and large; but the people were few therein, and the houses were not built."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"My God put into my heart to gather together the nobles, and the rulers, and the people, that they might be listed by genealogy. I found the book of the genealogy of those who came up at the first, and I found this written in it:"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the children of the province who went up out of the captivity of those who had been carried away, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away, and who returned to Jerusalem and to Judah, everyone to his city,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"who came with Zerubbabel, Jeshua, Nehemiah, Azariah, Raamiah, Nahamani, Mordecai, Bilshan, Mispereth, Bigvai, Nehum, and Baanah."],[0,"The number of the men of the people of Israel:"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Parosh: two thousand one hundred seventy-two."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Shephatiah: three hundred seventy-two."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Arah: six hundred fifty-two."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Pahathmoab, of the children of Jeshua and Joab: two thousand eight hundred eighteen."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Elam: one thousand two hundred fifty-four."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Zattu: eight hundred forty-five."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Zaccai: seven hundred sixty."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Binnui: six hundred forty-eight."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Bebai: six hundred twenty-eight."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Azgad: two thousand three hundred twenty-two."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Adonikam: six hundred sixty-seven."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Bigvai: two thousand sixty-seven."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Adin: six hundred fifty-five."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Ater: of Hezekiah, ninety-eight."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Hashum: three hundred twenty-eight."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Bezai: three hundred twenty-four."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Hariph: one hundred twelve."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Gibeon: ninety-five."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Bethlehem and Netophah: one hundred eighty-eight."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Anathoth: one hundred twenty-eight."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Beth Azmaveth: forty-two."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Kiriath Jearim, Chephirah, and Beeroth: seven hundred forty-three."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Ramah and Geba: six hundred twenty-one."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Michmas: one hundred twenty-two."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Bethel and Ai: one hundred twenty-three."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of the other Nebo: fifty-two."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of the other Elam: one thousand two hundred fifty-four."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Harim: three hundred twenty."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Jericho: three hundred forty-five."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Lod, Hadid, and Ono: seven hundred twenty-one."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Senaah: three thousand nine hundred thirty."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"The priests: The children of Jedaiah, of the house of Jeshua: nine hundred seventy-three."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Immer: one thousand fifty-two."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Pashhur: one thousand two hundred forty-seven."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Harim: one thousand seventeen."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"The Levites: the children of Jeshua, of Kadmiel, of the children of Hodevah: seventy-four."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"The singers: the children of Asaph: one hundred forty-eight."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"The gatekeepers: the children of Shallum, the children of Ater, the children of Talmon, the children of Akkub, the children of Hatita, the children of Shobai: one hundred thirty-eight."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"The temple servants: the children of Ziha, the children of Hasupha, the children of Tabbaoth,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"the children of Keros, the children of Sia, the children of Padon,"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"the children of Lebana, the children of Hagaba, the children of Salmai,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"the children of Hanan, the children of Giddel, the children of Gahar,"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"the children of Reaiah, the children of Rezin, the children of Nekoda,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"the children of Gazzam, the children of Uzza, the children of Paseah,"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"the children of Besai, the children of Meunim, the children of Nephushesim,"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"the children of Bakbuk, the children of Hakupha, the children of Harhur,"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"the children of Bazlith, the children of Mehida, the children of Harsha,"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"the children of Barkos, the children of Sisera, the children of Temah,"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"the children of Neziah, and the children of Hatipha."]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"The children of Solomon\u2019s servants: the children of Sotai, the children of Sophereth, the children of Perida,"]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"the children of Jaala, the children of Darkon, the children of Giddel,"]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"the children of Shephatiah, the children of Hattil, the children of Pochereth Hazzebaim, and the children of Amon."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"All the temple servants and the children of Solomon\u2019s servants were three hundred ninety-two."]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"These were those who went up from Tel Melah, Tel Harsha, Cherub, Addon, and Immer; but they could not show their fathers\u2019 houses, nor their offspring, whether they were of Israel:"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Delaiah, the children of Tobiah, the children of Nekoda: six hundred forty-two."]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[1,"Of the priests: the children of Hobaiah, the children of Hakkoz, the children of Barzillai, who took a wife of the daughters of Barzillai the Gileadite, and was called after their name."]]},{v:64,p:1,l:[[0,"These searched for their genealogical records, but couldn\u2019t find them. Therefore they were deemed disqualified and removed from the priesthood."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"The governor told them not to eat of the most holy things until a priest stood up to minister with Urim and Thummim."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[0,"The whole assembly together was forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,"]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"in addition to their male servants and their female servants, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred thirty-seven. They had two hundred forty-five singing men and singing women."]]},{v:68,l:[[0,"Their horses were seven hundred thirty-six; their mules, two hundred forty-five;"]]},{v:69,l:[[0,"their camels, four hundred thirty-five; their donkeys, six thousand seven hundred twenty."]]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[0,"Some from among the heads of fathers\u2019 households gave to the work. The governor gave to the treasury one thousand darics of gold, fifty basins, and five hundred thirty priests\u2019 garments."]],f:["a daric was a gold coin issued by a Persian king, weighing about 8.4 grams or about 0.27 troy ounces each."]},{v:71,l:[[0,"Some of the heads of fathers\u2019 households gave into the treasury of the work twenty thousand darics of gold, and two thousand two hundred minas of silver."]],f:["A mina is about 600 grams or 1.3 U. S. pounds, so 2,200 minas is about 1.3 metric tons."]},{v:72,l:[[0,"That which the rest of the people gave was twenty thousand darics of gold, plus two thousand minas of silver, and sixty-seven priests\u2019 garments."]]},{v:73,p:1,l:[[0,"So the priests, the Levites, the gatekeepers, the singers, some of the people, the temple servants, and all Israel lived in their cities."],[0,"When the seventh month had come, the children of Israel were in their cities."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people gathered themselves together as one man into the wide place that was in front of the water gate; and they spoke to Ezra the scribe to bring the book of the law of Moses, which the LORD had commanded to Israel."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Ezra the priest brought the law before the assembly, both men and women, and all who could hear with understanding, on the first day of the seventh month."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He read from it before the wide place that was in front of the water gate from early morning until midday, in the presence of the men and the women, and of those who could understand. The ears of all the people were attentive to the book of the law."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Ezra the scribe stood on a pulpit of wood, which they had made for the purpose; and beside him stood Mattithiah, Shema, Anaiah, Uriah, Hilkiah, and Maaseiah, on his right hand; and on his left hand, Pedaiah, Mishael, Malchijah, Hashum, Hashbaddanah, Zechariah, and Meshullam."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Ezra opened the book in the sight of all the people (for he was above all the people), and when he opened it, all the people stood up."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then Ezra blessed the LORD, the great God."],[0,"All the people answered, \u201cAmen, Amen,\u201d with the lifting up of their hands. They bowed their heads, and worshiped the LORD with their faces to the ground."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Also Jeshua, Bani, Sherebiah, Jamin, Akkub, Shabbethai, Hodiah, Maaseiah, Kelita, Azariah, Jozabad, Hanan, Pelaiah, and the Levites, caused the people to understand the law; and the people stayed in their place."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They read in the book, in the law of God, distinctly; and they gave the sense, so that they understood the reading."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Nehemiah, who was the governor, Ezra the priest and scribe, and the Levites who taught the people said to all the people, \u201cToday is holy to the LORD your God. Don\u2019t mourn, nor weep.\u201d For all the people wept when they heard the words of the law."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Then he said to them, \u201cGo your way. Eat the fat, drink the sweet, and send portions to him for whom nothing is prepared, for today is holy to our Lord. Don\u2019t be grieved, for the joy of the LORD is your strength.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"So the Levites calmed all the people, saying, \u201cHold your peace, for the day is holy. Don\u2019t be grieved.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people went their way to eat, to drink, to send portions, and to celebrate, because they had understood the words that were declared to them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"On the second day, the heads of fathers\u2019 households of all the people, the priests, and the Levites were gathered together to Ezra the scribe, to study the words of the law."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They found written in the law how the LORD had commanded by Moses that the children of Israel should dwell in booths in the feast of the seventh month;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and that they should publish and proclaim in all their cities and in Jerusalem, saying, \u201cGo out to the mountain, and get olive branches, branches of wild olive, myrtle branches, palm branches, and branches of thick trees, to make temporary shelters, as it is written.\u201d"]],f:["or, booths"]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So the people went out and brought them, and made themselves temporary shelters, everyone on the roof of his house, in their courts, in the courts of God\u2019s house, in the wide place of the water gate, and in the wide place of Ephraim\u2019s gate."]],f:["or, booths"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All the assembly of those who had come back out of the captivity made temporary shelters and lived in the temporary shelters, for since the days of Joshua the son of Nun to that day the children of Israel had not done so. There was very great gladness."]],f:["or, booths"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Also day by day, from the first day to the last day, he read in the book of the law of God. They kept the feast seven days; and on the eighth day was a solemn assembly, according to the ordinance."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the twenty-fourth day of this month the children of Israel were assembled with fasting, with sackcloth, and dirt on them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The offspring of Israel separated themselves from all foreigners and stood and confessed their sins and the iniquities of their fathers."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They stood up in their place, and read in the book of the law of the LORD their God a fourth part of the day; and a fourth part they confessed and worshiped the LORD their God."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then Jeshua, Bani, Kadmiel, Shebaniah, Bunni, Sherebiah, Bani, and Chenani of the Levites stood up on the stairs, and cried with a loud voice to the LORD their God."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Levites, Jeshua, and Kadmiel, Bani, Hashabneiah, Sherebiah, Hodiah, Shebaniah, and Pethahiah, said, \u201cStand up and bless the LORD your God from everlasting to everlasting! Blessed be your glorious name, which is exalted above all blessing and praise!"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You are the LORD, even you alone. You have made heaven, the heaven of heavens, with all their army, the earth and all things that are on it, the seas and all that is in them, and you preserve them all. The army of heaven worships you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You are the LORD, the God who chose Abram, brought him out of Ur of the Chaldees, gave him the name of Abraham,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"found his heart faithful before you, and made a covenant with him to give the land of the Canaanite, the Hittite, the Amorite, the Perizzite, the Jebusite, and the Girgashite, to give it to his offspring, and have performed your words, for you are righteous."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou saw the affliction of our fathers in Egypt, and heard their cry by the Red Sea,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and showed signs and wonders against Pharaoh, against all his servants, and against all the people of his land, for you knew that they dealt proudly against them, and made a name for yourself, as it is today."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You divided the sea before them, so that they went through the middle of the sea on the dry land; and you cast their pursuers into the depths, as a stone into the mighty waters."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Moreover, in a pillar of cloud you led them by day; and in a pillar of fire by night, to give them light in the way in which they should go."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou also came down on Mount Sinai, and spoke with them from heaven, and gave them right ordinances and true laws, good statutes and commandments,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and made known to them your holy Sabbath, and commanded them commandments, statutes, and a law, by Moses your servant,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and gave them bread from the sky for their hunger, and brought water out of the rock for them for their thirst, and commanded them that they should go in to possess the land which you had sworn to give them."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut they and our fathers behaved proudly, hardened their neck, didn\u2019t listen to your commandments,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and refused to obey. They weren\u2019t mindful of your wonders that you did among them, but hardened their neck, and in their rebellion appointed a captain to return to their bondage. But you are a God ready to pardon, gracious and merciful, slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness, and didn\u2019t forsake them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Yes, when they had made themselves a molded calf, and said, \u2018This is your God who brought you up out of Egypt,\u2019 and had committed awful blasphemies,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"yet you in your manifold mercies didn\u2019t forsake them in the wilderness. The pillar of cloud didn\u2019t depart from over them by day, to lead them in the way; neither did the pillar of fire by night, to show them light, and the way in which they should go."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You gave also your good Spirit to instruct them, and didn\u2019t withhold your manna from their mouth, and gave them water for their thirst."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYes, forty years you sustained them in the wilderness. They lacked nothing. Their clothes didn\u2019t grow old, and their feet didn\u2019t swell."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Moreover you gave them kingdoms and peoples, which you allotted according to their portions. So they possessed the land of Sihon, even the land of the king of Heshbon, and the land of Og king of Bashan."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You also multiplied their children as the stars of the sky, and brought them into the land concerning which you said to their fathers that they should go in to possess it."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo the children went in and possessed the land; and you subdued before them the inhabitants of the land, the Canaanites, and gave them into their hands, with their kings and the peoples of the land, that they might do with them as they pleased."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They took fortified cities and a rich land, and possessed houses full of all good things, cisterns dug out, vineyards, olive groves, and fruit trees in abundance. So they ate, were filled, became fat, and delighted themselves in your great goodness."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNevertheless they were disobedient and rebelled against you, cast your law behind their back, killed your prophets that testified against them to turn them again to you, and they committed awful blasphemies."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Therefore you delivered them into the hand of their adversaries, who distressed them. In the time of their trouble, when they cried to you, you heard from heaven; and according to your manifold mercies you gave them saviors who saved them out of the hands of their adversaries."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But after they had rest, they did evil again before you; therefore you left them in the hands of their enemies, so that they had the dominion over them; yet when they returned and cried to you, you heard from heaven; and many times you delivered them according to your mercies,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"and testified against them, that you might bring them again to your law. Yet they were arrogant, and didn\u2019t listen to your commandments, but sinned against your ordinances (which if a man does, he shall live in them), turned their backs, stiffened their neck, and would not hear."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Yet many years you put up with them, and testified against them by your Spirit through your prophets. Yet they would not listen. Therefore you gave them into the hand of the peoples of the lands."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNevertheless in your manifold mercies you didn\u2019t make a full end of them, nor forsake them; for you are a gracious and merciful God."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Now therefore, our God, the great, the mighty, and the awesome God, who keeps covenant and loving kindness, don\u2019t let all the travail seem little before you that has come on us, on our kings, on our princes, on our priests, on our prophets, on our fathers, and on all your people, since the time of the kings of Assyria to this day."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"However you are just in all that has come on us; for you have dealt truly, but we have done wickedly."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Also our kings, our princes, our priests, and our fathers have not kept your law, nor listened to your commandments and your testimonies with which you testified against them."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"For they have not served you in their kingdom, and in your great goodness that you gave them, and in the large and rich land which you gave before them. They didn\u2019t turn from their wicked works."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, we are servants today, and as for the land that you gave to our fathers to eat its fruit and its good, behold, we are servants in it."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"It yields much increase to the kings whom you have set over us because of our sins. Also they have power over our bodies and over our livestock, at their pleasure, and we are in great distress."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Yet for all this, we make a sure covenant, and write it; and our princes, our Levites, and our priests, seal it.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now those who sealed were: Nehemiah the governor, the son of Hacaliah, and Zedekiah,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Seraiah, Azariah, Jeremiah,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Pashhur, Amariah, Malchijah,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Hattush, Shebaniah, Malluch,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Harim, Meremoth, Obadiah,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Daniel, Ginnethon, Baruch,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Meshullam, Abijah, Mijamin,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Maaziah, Bilgai, and Shemaiah. These were the priests."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The Levites: Jeshua the son of Azaniah, Binnui of the sons of Henadad, Kadmiel;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and their brothers, Shebaniah, Hodiah, Kelita, Pelaiah, Hanan,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Mica, Rehob, Hashabiah,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Zaccur, Sherebiah, Shebaniah,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Hodiah, Bani, and Beninu."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The chiefs of the people: Parosh, Pahathmoab, Elam, Zattu, Bani,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Bunni, Azgad, Bebai,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Adonijah, Bigvai, Adin,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Ater, Hezekiah, Azzur,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Hodiah, Hashum, Bezai,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Hariph, Anathoth, Nobai,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Magpiash, Meshullam, Hezir,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Meshezabel, Zadok, Jaddua,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Pelatiah, Hanan, Anaiah,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Hoshea, Hananiah, Hasshub,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Hallohesh, Pilha, Shobek,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Rehum, Hashabnah, Maaseiah,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Ahiah, Hanan, Anan,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Malluch, Harim, and Baanah."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The rest of the people, the priests, the Levites, the gatekeepers, the singers, the temple servants, and all those who had separated themselves from the peoples of the lands to the law of God, their wives, their sons, and their daughters\u2014everyone who had knowledge and understanding\u2014"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"joined with their brothers, their nobles, and entered into a curse and into an oath, to walk in God\u2019s law, which was given by Moses the servant of God, and to observe and do all the commandments of the LORD our Lord, and his ordinances and his statutes;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and that we would not give our daughters to the peoples of the land, nor take their daughters for our sons;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and if the peoples of the land bring wares or any grain on the Sabbath day to sell, that we would not buy from them on the Sabbath, or on a holy day; and that we would forego the seventh year crops and the exaction of every debt."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Also we made ordinances for ourselves, to charge ourselves yearly with the third part of a shekel for the service of the house of our God:"]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:33,l:[[0,"for the show bread, for the continual meal offering, for the continual burnt offering, for the Sabbaths, for the new moons, for the set feasts, for the holy things, for the sin offerings to make atonement for Israel, and for all the work of the house of our God."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"We, the priests, the Levites, and the people, cast lots for the wood offering, to bring it into the house of our God, according to our fathers\u2019 houses, at times appointed year by year, to burn on the LORD our God\u2019s altar, as it is written in the law;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"and to bring the first fruits of our ground and the first fruits of all fruit of all kinds of trees, year by year, to the LORD\u2019s house;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"also the firstborn of our sons and of our livestock, as it is written in the law, and the firstborn of our herds and of our flocks, to bring to the house of our God, to the priests who minister in the house of our God;"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"and that we should bring the first fruits of our dough, our wave offerings, the fruit of all kinds of trees, and the new wine and the oil, to the priests, to the rooms of the house of our God; and the tithes of our ground to the Levites; for they, the Levites, take the tithes in all our farming villages."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The priest, the descendent of Aaron, shall be with the Levites when the Levites take tithes. The Levites shall bring up the tithe of the tithes to the house of our God, to the rooms, into the treasure house."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"For the children of Israel and the children of Levi shall bring the wave offering of the grain, of the new wine, and of the oil, to the rooms where the vessels of the sanctuary are, and the priests who minister, with the gatekeepers and the singers. We will not forsake the house of our God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The princes of the people lived in Jerusalem. The rest of the people also cast lots to bring one of ten to dwell in Jerusalem, the holy city, and nine parts in the other cities."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The people blessed all the men who willingly offered themselves to dwell in Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the chiefs of the province who lived in Jerusalem; but in the cities of Judah, everyone lived in his possession in their cities\u2014Israel, the priests, the Levites, the temple servants, and the children of Solomon\u2019s servants."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Some of the children of Judah and of the children of Benjamin lived in Jerusalem. Of the children of Judah: Athaiah the son of Uzziah, the son of Zechariah, the son of Amariah, the son of Shephatiah, the son of Mahalalel, of the children of Perez;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and Maaseiah the son of Baruch, the son of Colhozeh, the son of Hazaiah, the son of Adaiah, the son of Joiarib, the son of Zechariah, the son of the Shilonite."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"All the sons of Perez who lived in Jerusalem were four hundred sixty-eight valiant men."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the sons of Benjamin: Sallu the son of Meshullam, the son of Joed, the son of Pedaiah, the son of Kolaiah, the son of Maaseiah, the son of Ithiel, the son of Jeshaiah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"After him Gabbai and Sallai, nine hundred twenty-eight."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Joel the son of Zichri was their overseer; and Judah the son of Hassenuah was second over the city."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the priests: Jedaiah the son of Joiarib, Jachin,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Seraiah the son of Hilkiah, the son of Meshullam, the son of Zadok, the son of Meraioth, the son of Ahitub, the ruler of God\u2019s house,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and their brothers who did the work of the house, eight hundred twenty-two; and Adaiah the son of Jeroham, the son of Pelaliah, the son of Amzi, the son of Zechariah, the son of Pashhur, the son of Malchijah,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and his brothers, chiefs of fathers\u2019 households, two hundred forty-two; and Amashsai the son of Azarel, the son of Ahzai, the son of Meshillemoth, the son of Immer,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and their brothers, mighty men of valor, one hundred twenty-eight; and their overseer was Zabdiel, the son of Haggedolim."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the Levites: Shemaiah the son of Hasshub, the son of Azrikam, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Bunni;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and Shabbethai and Jozabad, of the chiefs of the Levites, who had the oversight of the outward business of God\u2019s house;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and Mattaniah the son of Mica, the son of Zabdi, the son of Asaph, who was the chief to begin the thanksgiving in prayer, and Bakbukiah, the second among his brothers; and Abda the son of Shammua, the son of Galal, the son of Jeduthun."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All the Levites in the holy city were two hundred eighty-four."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the gatekeepers, Akkub, Talmon, and their brothers, who kept watch at the gates, were one hundred seventy-two."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The residue of Israel, of the priests, and the Levites were in all the cities of Judah, everyone in his inheritance."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But the temple servants lived in Ophel; and Ziha and Gishpa were over the temple servants."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The overseer also of the Levites at Jerusalem was Uzzi the son of Bani, the son of Hashabiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Mica, of the sons of Asaph, the singers responsible for the service of God\u2019s house."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For there was a commandment from the king concerning them, and a settled provision for the singers, as every day required."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Pethahiah the son of Meshezabel, of the children of Zerah the son of Judah, was at the king\u2019s hand in all matters concerning the people."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"As for the villages with their fields, some of the children of Judah lived in Kiriath Arba and its towns, in Dibon and its towns, in Jekabzeel and its villages,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"in Jeshua, in Moladah, Beth Pelet,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"in Hazar Shual, in Beersheba and its towns,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"in Ziklag, in Meconah and in its towns,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"in En Rimmon, in Zorah, in Jarmuth,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Zanoah, Adullam, and their villages, Lachish and its fields, and Azekah and its towns. So they encamped from Beersheba to the valley of Hinnom."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The children of Benjamin also lived from Geba onward, at Michmash and Aija, and at Bethel and its towns,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"at Anathoth, Nob, Ananiah,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Hazor, Ramah, Gittaim,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Hadid, Zeboim, Neballat,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Lod, and Ono, the valley of craftsmen."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Of the Levites, certain divisions in Judah settled in Benjamin\u2019s territory."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the priests and the Levites who went up with Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, and Jeshua: Seraiah, Jeremiah, Ezra,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Amariah, Malluch, Hattush,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Shecaniah, Rehum, Meremoth,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Iddo, Ginnethoi, Abijah,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Mijamin, Maadiah, Bilgah,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Shemaiah, Joiarib, Jedaiah,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Sallu, Amok, Hilkiah, and Jedaiah. These were the chiefs of the priests and of their brothers in the days of Jeshua."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the Levites were Jeshua, Binnui, Kadmiel, Sherebiah, Judah, and Mattaniah, who was over the thanksgiving songs, he and his brothers."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Also Bakbukiah and Unno, their brothers, were close to them according to their offices."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Jeshua became the father of Joiakim, and Joiakim became the father of Eliashib, and Eliashib became the father of Joiada,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and Joiada became the father of Jonathan, and Jonathan became the father of Jaddua."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"In the days of Joiakim were priests, heads of fathers\u2019 households: of Seraiah, Meraiah; of Jeremiah, Hananiah;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"of Ezra, Meshullam; of Amariah, Jehohanan;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"of Malluchi, Jonathan; of Shebaniah, Joseph;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"of Harim, Adna; of Meraioth, Helkai;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"of Iddo, Zechariah; of Ginnethon, Meshullam;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"of Abijah, Zichri; of Miniamin, of Moadiah, Piltai;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"of Bilgah, Shammua; of Shemaiah, Jehonathan;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"of Joiarib, Mattenai; of Jedaiah, Uzzi;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"of Sallai, Kallai; of Amok, Eber;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"of Hilkiah, Hashabiah; of Jedaiah, Nethanel."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"As for the Levites, in the days of Eliashib, Joiada, Johanan, and Jaddua, there were recorded the heads of fathers\u2019 households; also the priests, in the reign of Darius the Persian."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The sons of Levi, heads of fathers\u2019 households, were written in the book of the chronicles, even until the days of Johanan the son of Eliashib."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The chiefs of the Levites: Hashabiah, Sherebiah, and Jeshua the son of Kadmiel, with their brothers close to them, to praise and give thanks according to the commandment of David the man of God, section next to section."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Mattaniah, Bakbukiah, Obadiah, Meshullam, Talmon, and Akkub were gatekeepers keeping the watch at the storehouses of the gates."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"These were in the days of Joiakim the son of Jeshua, the son of Jozadak, and in the days of Nehemiah the governor, and of Ezra the priest and scribe."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"At the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem, they sought the Levites out of all their places, to bring them to Jerusalem to keep the dedication with gladness, both with giving thanks and with singing, with cymbals, stringed instruments, and with harps."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The sons of the singers gathered themselves together, both out of the plain around Jerusalem and from the villages of the Netophathites;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"also from Beth Gilgal and out of the fields of Geba and Azmaveth, for the singers had built themselves villages around Jerusalem."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The priests and the Levites purified themselves; and they purified the people, the gates, and the wall."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I brought the princes of Judah up on the wall, and appointed two great companies who gave thanks and went in procession. One went on the right hand on the wall toward the dung gate;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and after them went Hoshaiah, with half of the princes of Judah,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"and Azariah, Ezra, and Meshullam,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Judah, Benjamin, Shemaiah, Jeremiah,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"and some of the priests\u2019 sons with trumpets: Zechariah the son of Jonathan, the son of Shemaiah, the son of Mattaniah, the son of Micaiah, the son of Zaccur, the son of Asaph;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"and his brothers, Shemaiah, Azarel, Milalai, Gilalai, Maai, Nethanel, Judah, and Hanani, with the musical instruments of David the man of God; and Ezra the scribe was before them."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"By the spring gate, and straight before them, they went up by the stairs of David\u2019s city, at the ascent of the wall, above David\u2019s house, even to the water gate eastward."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"The other company of those who gave thanks went to meet them, and I after them, with the half of the people on the wall above the tower of the furnaces, even to the wide wall,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and above the gate of Ephraim, and by the old gate, and by the fish gate, the tower of Hananel, and the tower of Hammeah, even to the sheep gate; and they stood still in the gate of the guard."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"So the two companies of those who gave thanks in God\u2019s house stood, and I and the half of the rulers with me;"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"and the priests, Eliakim, Maaseiah, Miniamin, Micaiah, Elioenai, Zechariah, and Hananiah, with trumpets;"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"and Maaseiah, Shemaiah, Eleazar, Uzzi, Jehohanan, Malchijah, Elam, and Ezer. The singers sang loud, with Jezrahiah their overseer."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"They offered great sacrifices that day, and rejoiced, for God had made them rejoice with great joy; and the women and the children also rejoiced, so that the joy of Jerusalem was heard even far away."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"On that day, men were appointed over the rooms for the treasures, for the wave offerings, for the first fruits, and for the tithes, to gather into them according to the fields of the cities the portions appointed by the law for the priests and Levites; for Judah rejoiced for the priests and for the Levites who served."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"They performed the duty of their God and the duty of the purification, and so did the singers and the gatekeepers, according to the commandment of David and of Solomon his son."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"For in the days of David and Asaph of old there was a chief of the singers, and songs of praise and thanksgiving to God."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"All Israel in the days of Zerubbabel and in the days of Nehemiah gave the portions of the singers and the gatekeepers, as every day required; and they set apart that which was for the Levites; and the Levites set apart that which was for the sons of Aaron."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"On that day they read in the book of Moses in the hearing of the people; and it was found written in it that an Ammonite and a Moabite should not enter into the assembly of God forever,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"because they didn\u2019t meet the children of Israel with bread and with water, but hired Balaam against them to curse them; however, our God turned the curse into a blessing."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It came to pass, when they had heard the law, that they separated all the mixed multitude from Israel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now before this, Eliashib the priest, who was appointed over the rooms of the house of our God, being allied to Tobiah,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"had prepared for him a great room, where previously they laid the meal offerings, the frankincense, the vessels, and the tithes of the grain, the new wine, and the oil, which were given by commandment to the Levites, the singers, and the gatekeepers; and the wave offerings for the priests."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But in all this, I was not at Jerusalem; for in the thirty-second year of Artaxerxes king of Babylon I went to the king; and after some days I asked leave of the king,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and I came to Jerusalem, and understood the evil that Eliashib had done for Tobiah, in preparing him a room in the courts of God\u2019s house."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"It grieved me severely. Therefore I threw all Tobiah\u2019s household stuff out of the room."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then I commanded, and they cleansed the rooms. I brought into them the vessels of God\u2019s house, with the meal offerings and the frankincense again."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"I perceived that the portions of the Levites had not been given them, so that the Levites and the singers, who did the work, had each fled to his field."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then I contended with the rulers, and said, \u201cWhy is God\u2019s house forsaken?\u201d I gathered them together, and set them in their place."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Then all Judah brought the tithe of the grain, the new wine, and the oil to the treasuries."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I made treasurers over the treasuries, Shelemiah the priest, and Zadok the scribe, and of the Levites, Pedaiah: and next to them was Hanan the son of Zaccur, the son of Mattaniah; for they were counted faithful, and their business was to distribute to their brothers."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Remember me, my God, concerning this, and don\u2019t wipe out my good deeds that I have done for the house of my God, and for its observances."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days I saw some men treading wine presses on the Sabbath in Judah, bringing in sheaves, and loading donkeys with wine, grapes, figs, and all kinds of burdens which they brought into Jerusalem on the Sabbath day; and I testified against them in the day in which they sold food."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Some men of Tyre also lived there, who brought in fish and all kinds of wares, and sold on the Sabbath to the children of Judah, and in Jerusalem."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then I contended with the nobles of Judah, and said to them, \u201cWhat evil thing is this that you do, and profane the Sabbath day?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t your fathers do this, and didn\u2019t our God bring all this evil on us and on this city? Yet you bring more wrath on Israel by profaning the Sabbath.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass that when the gates of Jerusalem began to be dark before the Sabbath, I commanded that the doors should be shut, and commanded that they should not be opened until after the Sabbath. I set some of my servants over the gates, so that no burden should be brought in on the Sabbath day."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"So the merchants and sellers of all kinds of wares camped outside of Jerusalem once or twice."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then I testified against them, and said to them, \u201cWhy do you stay around the wall? If you do so again, I will lay hands on you.\u201d From that time on, they didn\u2019t come on the Sabbath."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I commanded the Levites that they should purify themselves, and that they should come and keep the gates, to sanctify the Sabbath day. Remember me for this also, my God, and spare me according to the greatness of your loving kindness."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days I also saw the Jews who had married women of Ashdod, of Ammon, and of Moab;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and their children spoke half in the speech of Ashdod, and could not speak in the Jews\u2019 language, but according to the language of each people."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I contended with them, cursed them, struck certain of them, plucked off their hair, and made them swear by God, \u201cYou shall not give your daughters to their sons, nor take their daughters for your sons, or for yourselves."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t Solomon king of Israel sin by these things? Yet among many nations there was no king like him, and he was loved by his God, and God made him king over all Israel. Nevertheless foreign women caused even him to sin."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Shall we then listen to you to do all this great evil, to trespass against our God in marrying foreign women?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the sons of Joiada, the son of Eliashib the high priest, was son-in-law to Sanballat the Horonite; therefore I chased him from me."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Remember them, my God, because they have defiled the priesthood and the covenant of the priesthood and of the Levites."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus I cleansed them from all foreigners and appointed duties for the priests and for the Levites, everyone in his work;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and for the wood offering, at appointed times, and for the first fruits. Remember me, my God, for good."]]}]]}},1287,[]);
__d(function(e,t,h,a,n,o,i){n.exports={book:"Esth",name:"Esther",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the days of Ahasuerus (this is Ahasuerus who reigned from India even to Ethiopia, over one hundred twenty-seven provinces),"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"in those days, when the King Ahasuerus sat on the throne of his kingdom, which was in Susa the palace,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"in the third year of his reign, he made a feast for all his princes and his servants; the army of Persia and Media, the nobles and princes of the provinces being before him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He displayed the riches of his glorious kingdom and the honor of his excellent majesty many days, even one hundred eighty days."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When these days were fulfilled, the king made a seven day feast for all the people who were present in Susa the palace, both great and small, in the court of the garden of the king\u2019s palace."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"There were hangings of white and blue material, fastened with cords of fine linen and purple to silver rings and marble pillars. The couches were of gold and silver, on a pavement of red, white, yellow, and black marble."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They gave them drinks in golden vessels of various kinds, including royal wine in abundance, according to the bounty of the king."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"In accordance with the law, the drinking was not compulsory; for so the king had instructed all the officials of his house, that they should do according to every man\u2019s pleasure."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Also Vashti the queen made a feast for the women in the royal house which belonged to King Ahasuerus."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"On the seventh day, when the heart of the king was merry with wine, he commanded Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, and Abagtha, Zethar, and Carcass, the seven eunuchs who served in the presence of Ahasuerus the king,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"to bring Vashti the queen before the king wearing the royal crown, to show the people and the princes her beauty; for she was beautiful."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But the queen Vashti refused to come at the king\u2019s commandment by the eunuchs. Therefore the king was very angry, and his anger burned in him."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said to the wise men, who knew the times (for it was the king\u2019s custom to consult those who knew law and judgment;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and next to him were Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media, who saw the king\u2019s face, and sat first in the kingdom),"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cWhat shall we do to Queen Vashti according to law, because she has not done the bidding of the King Ahasuerus by the eunuchs?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Memucan answered before the king and the princes, \u201cVashti the queen has not done wrong to just the king, but also to all the princes, and to all the people who are in all the provinces of the King Ahasuerus."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For this deed of the queen will become known to all women, causing them to show contempt for their husbands when it is reported, \u2018King Ahasuerus commanded Vashti the queen to be brought in before him, but she didn\u2019t come.\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Today, the princesses of Persia and Media who have heard of the queen\u2019s deed will tell all the king\u2019s princes. This will cause much contempt and wrath."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf it pleases the king, let a royal commandment go from him, and let it be written among the laws of the Persians and the Medes, so that it cannot be altered, that Vashti may never again come before King Ahasuerus; and let the king give her royal estate to another who is better than she."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When the king\u2019s decree which he shall make is published throughout all his kingdom (for it is great), all the wives will give their husbands honor, both great and small.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"This advice pleased the king and the princes, and the king did according to the word of Memucan:"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"for he sent letters into all the king\u2019s provinces, into every province according to its writing, and to every people in their language, that every man should rule his own house, speaking in the language of his own people."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, when the wrath of King Ahasuerus was pacified, he remembered Vashti, and what she had done, and what was decreed against her."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then the king\u2019s servants who served him said, \u201cLet beautiful young virgins be sought for the king."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Let the king appoint officers in all the provinces of his kingdom, that they may gather together all the beautiful young virgins to the citadel of Susa, to the women\u2019s house, to the custody of Hegai the king\u2019s eunuch, keeper of the women. Let cosmetics be given them;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and let the maiden who pleases the king be queen instead of Vashti.\u201d The thing pleased the king, and he did so."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a certain Jew in the citadel of Susa whose name was Mordecai, the son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish, a Benjamite,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"who had been carried away from Jerusalem with the captives who had been carried away with Jeconiah king of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He brought up Hadassah, that is, Esther, his uncle\u2019s daughter; for she had neither father nor mother. The maiden was fair and beautiful; and when her father and mother were dead, Mordecai took her for his own daughter."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So, when the king\u2019s commandment and his decree was heard, and when many maidens were gathered together to the citadel of Susa, to the custody of Hegai, Esther was taken into the king\u2019s house, to the custody of Hegai, keeper of the women."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The maiden pleased him, and she obtained kindness from him. He quickly gave her cosmetics and her portions of food, and the seven choice maidens who were to be given her out of the king\u2019s house. He moved her and her maidens to the best place in the women\u2019s house."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Esther had not made known her people nor her relatives, because Mordecai had instructed her that she should not make it known."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Mordecai walked every day in front of the court of the women\u2019s house, to find out how Esther was doing, and what would become of her."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Each young woman\u2019s turn came to go in to King Ahasuerus after her purification for twelve months (for so were the days of their purification accomplished, six months with oil of myrrh, and six months with sweet fragrances and with preparations for beautifying women)."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The young woman then came to the king like this: whatever she desired was given her to go with her out of the women\u2019s house to the king\u2019s house."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"In the evening she went, and on the next day she returned into the second women\u2019s house, to the custody of Shaashgaz, the king\u2019s eunuch, who kept the concubines. She came in to the king no more, unless the king delighted in her, and she was called by name."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when the turn of Esther, the daughter of Abihail the uncle of Mordecai, who had taken her for his daughter, came to go in to the king, she required nothing but what Hegai the king\u2019s eunuch, the keeper of the women, advised. Esther obtained favor in the sight of all those who looked at her."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So Esther was taken to King Ahasuerus into his royal house in the tenth month, which is the month Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The king loved Esther more than all the women, and she obtained favor and kindness in his sight more than all the virgins; so that he set the royal crown on her head, and made her queen instead of Vashti."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king made a great feast for all his princes and his servants, even Esther\u2019s feast; and he proclaimed a holiday in the provinces, and gave gifts according to the king\u2019s bounty."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"When the virgins were gathered together the second time, Mordecai was sitting in the king\u2019s gate."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Esther had not yet made known her relatives nor her people, as Mordecai had commanded her; for Esther obeyed Mordecai, like she did when she was brought up by him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"In those days, while Mordecai was sitting in the king\u2019s gate, two of the king\u2019s eunuchs, Bigthan and Teresh, who were doorkeepers, were angry, and sought to lay hands on the King Ahasuerus."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"This thing became known to Mordecai, who informed Esther the queen; and Esther informed the king in Mordecai\u2019s name."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When this matter was investigated, and it was found to be so, they were both hanged on a gallows; and it was written in the book of the chronicles in the king\u2019s presence."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things King Ahasuerus promoted Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes who were with him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"All the king\u2019s servants who were in the king\u2019s gate bowed down and paid homage to Haman, for the king had so commanded concerning him. But Mordecai didn\u2019t bow down or pay him homage."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then the king\u2019s servants who were in the king\u2019s gate said to Mordecai, \u201cWhy do you disobey the king\u2019s commandment?\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now it came to pass, when they spoke daily to him, and he didn\u2019t listen to them, that they told Haman, to see whether Mordecai\u2019s reason would stand; for he had told them that he was a Jew."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When Haman saw that Mordecai didn\u2019t bow down nor pay him homage, Haman was full of wrath."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But he scorned the thought of laying hands on Mordecai alone, for they had made known to him Mordecai\u2019s people. Therefore Haman sought to destroy all the Jews who were throughout the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, even Mordecai\u2019s people."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"In the first month, which is the month Nisan, in the twelfth year of King Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that is, the lot, before Haman from day to day, and from month to month, and chose the twelfth month, which is the month Adar."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Haman said to King Ahasuerus, \u201cThere is a certain people scattered abroad and dispersed among the peoples in all the provinces of your kingdom, and their laws are different from other people\u2019s. They don\u2019t keep the king\u2019s laws. Therefore it is not for the king\u2019s profit to allow them to remain."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If it pleases the king, let it be written that they be destroyed; and I will pay ten thousand talents of silver into the hands of those who are in charge of the king\u2019s business, to bring it into the king\u2019s treasuries.\u201d"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds or 965 Troy ounces"]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The king took his ring from his hand, and gave it to Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, the Jews\u2019 enemy."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The king said to Haman, \u201cThe silver is given to you, the people also, to do with them as it seems good to you.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king\u2019s scribes were called in on the first month, on the thirteenth day of the month; and all that Haman commanded was written to the king\u2019s local governors, and to the governors who were over every province, and to the princes of every people, to every province according to its writing, and to every people in their language. It was written in the name of King Ahasuerus, and it was sealed with the king\u2019s ring."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Letters were sent by couriers into all the king\u2019s provinces, to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, both young and old, little children and women, in one day, even on the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, and to plunder their possessions."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"A copy of the letter, that the decree should be given out in every province, was published to all the peoples, that they should be ready against that day."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The couriers went out in haste by the king\u2019s commandment, and the decree was given out in the citadel of Susa. The king and Haman sat down to drink; but the city of Susa was perplexed."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Mordecai found out all that was done, Mordecai tore his clothes and put on sackcloth with ashes, and went out into the middle of the city, and wailed loudly and bitterly."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He came even before the king\u2019s gate, for no one is allowed inside the king\u2019s gate clothed with sackcloth."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In every province, wherever the king\u2019s commandment and his decree came, there was great mourning among the Jews, and fasting, and weeping, and wailing; and many lay in sackcloth and ashes."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Esther\u2019s maidens and her eunuchs came and told her this, and the queen was exceedingly grieved. She sent clothing to Mordecai, to replace his sackcloth, but he didn\u2019t receive it."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then Esther called for Hathach, one of the king\u2019s eunuchs, whom he had appointed to attend her, and commanded him to go to Mordecai, to find out what this was, and why it was."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Hathach went out to Mordecai, to the city square which was before the king\u2019s gate."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Mordecai told him of all that had happened to him, and the exact sum of the money that Haman had promised to pay to the king\u2019s treasuries for the destruction of the Jews."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He also gave him the copy of the writing of the decree that was given out in Susa to destroy them, to show it to Esther, and to declare it to her, and to urge her to go in to the king to make supplication to him, and to make request before him for her people."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Hathach came and told Esther the words of Mordecai."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Then Esther spoke to Hathach, and gave him a message to Mordecai:"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cAll the king\u2019s servants and the people of the king\u2019s provinces know that whoever, whether man or woman, comes to the king into the inner court without being called, there is one law for him, that he be put to death, except those to whom the king might hold out the golden scepter, that he may live. I have not been called to come in to the king these thirty days.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"They told Esther\u2019s words to Mordecai."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then Mordecai asked them to return this answer to Esther: \u201cDon\u2019t think to yourself that you will escape in the king\u2019s house any more than all the Jews."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For if you remain silent now, then relief and deliverance will come to the Jews from another place, but you and your father\u2019s house will perish. Who knows if you haven\u2019t come to the kingdom for such a time as this?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Esther asked them to answer Mordecai,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cGo, gather together all the Jews who are present in Susa, and fast for me, and neither eat nor drink three days, night or day. I and my maidens will also fast the same way. Then I will go in to the king, which is against the law; and if I perish, I perish.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So Mordecai went his way, and did according to all that Esther had commanded him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the third day, Esther put on her royal clothing and stood in the inner court of the king\u2019s house, next to the king\u2019s house. The king sat on his royal throne in the royal house, next to the entrance of the house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When the king saw Esther the queen standing in the court, she obtained favor in his sight; and the king held out to Esther the golden scepter that was in his hand. So Esther came near and touched the top of the scepter."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king asked her, \u201cWhat would you like, queen Esther? What is your request? It shall be given you even to the half of the kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Esther said, \u201cIf it seems good to the king, let the king and Haman come today to the banquet that I have prepared for him.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said, \u201cBring Haman quickly, so that it may be done as Esther has said.\u201d So the king and Haman came to the banquet that Esther had prepared."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said to Esther at the banquet of wine, \u201cWhat is your petition? It shall be granted you. What is your request? Even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Esther answered and said, \u201cMy petition and my request is this."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If I have found favor in the sight of the king, and if it pleases the king to grant my petition and to perform my request, let the king and Haman come to the banquet that I will prepare for them, and I will do tomorrow as the king has said.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Haman went out that day joyful and glad of heart, but when Haman saw Mordecai in the king\u2019s gate, that he didn\u2019t stand up nor move for him, he was filled with wrath against Mordecai."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Nevertheless Haman restrained himself, and went home. There, he sent and called for his friends and Zeresh his wife."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Haman recounted to them the glory of his riches, the multitude of his children, all the things in which the king had promoted him, and how he had advanced him above the princes and servants of the king."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Haman also said, \u201cYes, Esther the queen let no man come in with the king to the banquet that she had prepared but myself; and tomorrow I am also invited by her together with the king."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Yet all this avails me nothing, so long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king\u2019s gate.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zeresh his wife and all his friends said to him, \u201cLet a gallows be made fifty cubits high, and in the morning speak to the king about hanging Mordecai on it. Then go in merrily with the king to the banquet.\u201d This pleased Haman, so he had the gallows made."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"On that night, the king couldn\u2019t sleep. He commanded the book of records of the chronicles to be brought, and they were read to the king."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It was found written that Mordecai had told of Bigthana and Teresh, two of the king\u2019s eunuchs, who were doorkeepers, who had tried to lay hands on the King Ahasuerus."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cWhat honor and dignity has been given to Mordecai for this?\u201d"],[0,"Then the king\u2019s servants who attended him said, \u201cNothing has been done for him.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The king said, \u201cWho is in the court?\u201d Now Haman had come into the outer court of the king\u2019s house, to speak to the king about hanging Mordecai on the gallows that he had prepared for him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The king\u2019s servants said to him, \u201cBehold, Haman stands in the court.\u201d"],[0,"The king said, \u201cLet him come in.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Haman came in. The king said to him, \u201cWhat shall be done to the man whom the king delights to honor?\u201d"],[0,"Now Haman said in his heart, \u201cWho would the king delight to honor more than myself?\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Haman said to the king, \u201cFor the man whom the king delights to honor,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"let royal clothing be brought which the king uses to wear, and the horse that the king rides on, and on the head of which a royal crown is set."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Let the clothing and the horse be delivered to the hand of one of the king\u2019s most noble princes, that they may array the man whom the king delights to honor with them, and have him ride on horseback through the city square, and proclaim before him, \u2018Thus it shall be done to the man whom the king delights to honor!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king said to Haman, \u201cHurry and take the clothing and the horse, as you have said, and do this for Mordecai the Jew, who sits at the king\u2019s gate. Let nothing fail of all that you have spoken.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Haman took the clothing and the horse, and arrayed Mordecai, and had him ride through the city square, and proclaimed before him, \u201cThus it shall be done to the man whom the king delights to honor!\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Mordecai came back to the king\u2019s gate, but Haman hurried to his house, mourning and having his head covered."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Haman recounted to Zeresh his wife and all his friends everything that had happened to him. Then his wise men and Zeresh his wife said to him, \u201cIf Mordecai, before whom you have begun to fall, is of Jewish descent, you will not prevail against him, but you will surely fall before him.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"While they were yet talking with him, the king\u2019s eunuchs came, and hurried to bring Haman to the banquet that Esther had prepared."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"So the king and Haman came to banquet with Esther the queen."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The king said again to Esther on the second day at the banquet of wine, \u201cWhat is your petition, queen Esther? It shall be granted you. What is your request? Even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Esther the queen answered, \u201cIf I have found favor in your sight, O king, and if it pleases the king, let my life be given me at my petition, and my people at my request."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For we are sold, I and my people, to be destroyed, to be slain, and to perish. But if we had been sold for male and female slaves, I would have held my peace, although the adversary could not have compensated for the king\u2019s loss.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then King Ahasuerus said to Esther the queen, \u201cWho is he, and where is he who dared presume in his heart to do so?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Esther said, \u201cAn adversary and an enemy, even this wicked Haman!\u201d"],[0,"Then Haman was afraid before the king and the queen."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The king arose in his wrath from the banquet of wine and went into the palace garden. Haman stood up to make request for his life to Esther the queen, for he saw that there was evil determined against him by the king."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then the king returned out of the palace garden into the place of the banquet of wine; and Haman had fallen on the couch where Esther was. Then the king said, \u201cWill he even assault the queen in front of me in the house?\u201d As the word went out of the king\u2019s mouth, they covered Haman\u2019s face."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Harbonah, one of the eunuchs who were with the king, said, \u201cBehold, the gallows fifty cubits high, which Haman has made for Mordecai, who spoke good for the king, is standing at Haman\u2019s house.\u201d"],[0,"The king said, \u201cHang him on it!\u201d"]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So they hanged Haman on the gallows that he had prepared for Mordecai. Then the king\u2019s wrath was pacified."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"On that day, King Ahasuerus gave the house of Haman, the Jews\u2019 enemy, to Esther the queen. Mordecai came before the king; for Esther had told what he was to her."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The king took off his ring, which he had taken from Haman, and gave it to Mordecai. Esther set Mordecai over the house of Haman."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Esther spoke yet again before the king, and fell down at his feet and begged him with tears to put away the mischief of Haman the Agagite, and his plan that he had planned against the Jews."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then the king held out to Esther the golden scepter. So Esther arose, and stood before the king."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cIf it pleases the king, and if I have found favor in his sight, and the thing seems right to the king, and I am pleasing in his eyes, let it be written to reverse the letters devised by Haman, the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, which he wrote to destroy the Jews who are in all the king\u2019s provinces."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For how can I endure to see the evil that would come to my people? How can I endure to see the destruction of my relatives?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then King Ahasuerus said to Esther the queen and to Mordecai the Jew, \u201cSee, I have given Esther the house of Haman, and they have hanged him on the gallows because he laid his hand on the Jews."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Write also to the Jews as it pleases you, in the king\u2019s name, and seal it with the king\u2019s ring; for the writing which is written in the king\u2019s name, and sealed with the king\u2019s ring, may not be reversed by any man.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king\u2019s scribes were called at that time, in the third month, which is the month Sivan, on the twenty-third day of the month; and it was written according to all that Mordecai commanded to the Jews, and to the local governors, and the governors and princes of the provinces which are from India to Ethiopia, one hundred twenty-seven provinces, to every province according to its writing, and to every people in their language, and to the Jews in their writing, and in their language."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He wrote in the name of King Ahasuerus, and sealed it with the king\u2019s ring, and sent letters by courier on horseback, riding on royal horses that were bred from swift steeds."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In those letters, the king granted the Jews who were in every city to gather themselves together and to defend their lives\u2014to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish all the power of the people and province that would assault them, their little ones and women, and to plunder their possessions,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"on one day in all the provinces of King Ahasuerus, on the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"A copy of the letter, that the decree should be given out in every province, was published to all the peoples, that the Jews should be ready for that day to avenge themselves on their enemies."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So the couriers who rode on royal horses went out, hastened and pressed on by the king\u2019s commandment. The decree was given out in the citadel of Susa."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Mordecai went out of the presence of the king in royal clothing of blue and white, and with a great crown of gold, and with a robe of fine linen and purple; and the city of Susa shouted and was glad."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The Jews had light, gladness, joy, and honor."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"In every province and in every city, wherever the king\u2019s commandment and his decree came, the Jews had gladness, joy, a feast and a holiday. Many from among the peoples of the land became Jews, for the fear of the Jews had fallen on them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, on the thirteenth day of the month, when the king\u2019s commandment and his decree came near to be put in execution, on the day that the enemies of the Jews hoped to conquer them, (but it turned out that the opposite happened, that the Jews conquered those who hated them),"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"the Jews gathered themselves together in their cities throughout all the provinces of the King Ahasuerus, to lay hands on those who wanted to harm them. No one could withstand them, because the fear of them had fallen on all the people."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All the princes of the provinces, the local governors, the governors, and those who did the king\u2019s business helped the Jews, because the fear of Mordecai had fallen on them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For Mordecai was great in the king\u2019s house, and his fame went out throughout all the provinces, for the man Mordecai grew greater and greater."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The Jews struck all their enemies with the stroke of the sword, and with slaughter and destruction, and did what they wanted to those who hated them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In the citadel of Susa, the Jews killed and destroyed five hundred men."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They killed Parshandatha, Dalphon, Aspatha,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Poratha, Adalia, Aridatha,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Parmashta, Arisai, Aridai, and Vaizatha,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"the ten sons of Haman the son of Hammedatha, the Jews\u2019 enemy, but they didn\u2019t lay their hand on the plunder."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"On that day, the number of those who were slain in the citadel of Susa was brought before the king."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The king said to Esther the queen, \u201cThe Jews have slain and destroyed five hundred men in the citadel of Susa, including the ten sons of Haman; what then have they done in the rest of the king\u2019s provinces! Now what is your petition? It shall be granted you. What is your further request? It shall be done.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Esther said, \u201cIf it pleases the king, let it be granted to the Jews who are in Susa to do tomorrow also according to today\u2019s decree, and let Haman\u2019s ten sons be hanged on the gallows.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The king commanded this to be done. A decree was given out in Susa; and they hanged Haman\u2019s ten sons."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The Jews who were in Susa gathered themselves together on the fourteenth day also of the month Adar, and killed three hundred men in Susa; but they didn\u2019t lay their hand on the plunder."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The other Jews who were in the king\u2019s provinces gathered themselves together, defended their lives, had rest from their enemies, and killed seventy-five thousand of those who hated them; but they didn\u2019t lay their hand on the plunder."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"This was done on the thirteenth day of the month Adar; and on the fourteenth day of that month they rested and made it a day of feasting and gladness."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"But the Jews who were in Susa assembled together on the thirteenth and on the fourteenth days of the month; and on the fifteenth day of that month, they rested, and made it a day of feasting and gladness."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore the Jews of the villages, who live in the unwalled towns, make the fourteenth day of the month Adar a day of gladness and feasting, a holiday, and a day of sending presents of food to one another."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Mordecai wrote these things, and sent letters to all the Jews who were in all the provinces of the King Ahasuerus, both near and far,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"to enjoin them that they should keep the fourteenth and fifteenth days of the month Adar yearly,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"as the days in which the Jews had rest from their enemies, and the month which was turned to them from sorrow to gladness, and from mourning into a holiday; that they should make them days of feasting and gladness, and of sending presents of food to one another, and gifts to the needy."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The Jews accepted the custom that they had begun, as Mordecai had written to them,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"because Haman the son of Hammedatha, the Agagite, the enemy of all the Jews, had plotted against the Jews to destroy them, and had cast \u201cPur\u201d, that is the lot, to consume them and to destroy them;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"but when this became known to the king, he commanded by letters that his wicked plan, which he had planned against the Jews, should return on his own head, and that he and his sons should be hanged on the gallows."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore they called these days \u201cPurim\u201d, from the word \u201cPur.\u201d Therefore because of all the words of this letter, and of that which they had seen concerning this matter, and that which had come to them,"]],f:["Purim is the Hebrew plural for pur, which means lot."]},{v:27,l:[[0,"the Jews established and imposed on themselves, on their descendants, and on all those who joined themselves to them, so that it should not fail that they would keep these two days according to what was written and according to its appointed time every year;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and that these days should be remembered and kept throughout every generation, every family, every province, and every city; and that these days of Purim should not fail from among the Jews, nor their memory perish from their offspring."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Esther the queen, the daughter of Abihail, and Mordecai the Jew wrote with all authority to confirm this second letter of Purim."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He sent letters to all the Jews in the hundred twenty-seven provinces of the kingdom of Ahasuerus with words of peace and truth,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"to confirm these days of Purim in their appointed times, as Mordecai the Jew and Esther the queen had decreed, and as they had imposed upon themselves and their descendants in the matter of the fastings and their mourning."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The commandment of Esther confirmed these matters of Purim; and it was written in the book."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"King Ahasuerus laid a tribute on the land and on the islands of the sea."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t all the acts of his power and of his might, and the full account of the greatness of Mordecai, to which the king advanced him, written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Media and Persia?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For Mordecai the Jew was next to King Ahasuerus, and great among the Jews and accepted by the multitude of his brothers, seeking the good of his people and speaking peace to all his descendants."]]}]]}},1288,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,s,i){a.exports={book:"Job",name:"Job",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a man in the land of Uz, whose name was Job. That man was blameless and upright, and one who feared God, and turned away from evil."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"There were born to him seven sons and three daughters."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His possessions also were seven thousand sheep, three thousand camels, five hundred yoke of oxen, five hundred female donkeys, and a very great household; so that this man was the greatest of all the children of the east."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"His sons went and held a feast in the house of each one on his birthday; and they sent and called for their three sisters to eat and to drink with them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It was so, when the days of their feasting had run their course, that Job sent and sanctified them, and rose up early in the morning, and offered burnt offerings according to the number of them all. For Job said, \u201cIt may be that my sons have sinned, and renounced God in their hearts.\u201d Job did so continually."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the day when God\u2019s sons came to present themselves before the LORD, Satan also came among them."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Satan, \u201cWhere have you come from?\u201d"],[0,"Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, \u201cFrom going back and forth on the earth, and from walking up and down in it.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Satan, \u201cHave you considered my servant, Job? For there is no one like him on the earth, a blameless and an upright man, one who fears God, and turns away from evil.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Satan answered the LORD, and said, \u201cDoes Job fear God for nothing?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Haven\u2019t you made a hedge around him, and around his house, and around all that he has, on every side? You have blessed the work of his hands, and his substance is increased in the land."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But stretch out your hand now, and touch all that he has, and he will renounce you to your face.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Satan, \u201cBehold, all that he has is in your power. Only on himself don\u2019t stretch out your hand.\u201d"],[0,"So Satan went out from the presence of the LORD."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It fell on a day when his sons and his daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother\u2019s house,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"that a messenger came to Job, and said, \u201cThe oxen were plowing, and the donkeys feeding beside them,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and the Sabeans attacked, and took them away. Yes, they have killed the servants with the edge of the sword, and I alone have escaped to tell you.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still speaking, another also came and said, \u201cThe fire of God has fallen from the sky, and has burned up the sheep and the servants, and consumed them, and I alone have escaped to tell you.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still speaking, another also came and said, \u201cThe Chaldeans made three bands, and swept down on the camels, and have taken them away, yes, and killed the servants with the edge of the sword; and I alone have escaped to tell you.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still speaking, there came also another, and said, \u201cYour sons and your daughters were eating and drinking wine in their oldest brother\u2019s house,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and behold, there came a great wind from the wilderness, and struck the four corners of the house, and it fell on the young men, and they are dead. I alone have escaped to tell you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job arose, and tore his robe, and shaved his head, and fell down on the ground, and worshiped."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cNaked I came out of my mother\u2019s womb, and naked will I return there. The LORD gave, and the LORD has taken away. Blessed be the LORD\u2019s name.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"In all this, Job didn\u2019t sin, nor charge God with wrongdoing."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, on the day when God\u2019s sons came to present themselves before the LORD, Satan came also among them to present himself before the LORD."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Satan, \u201cWhere have you come from?\u201d"],[0,"Satan answered the LORD, and said, \u201cFrom going back and forth on the earth, and from walking up and down in it.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Satan, \u201cHave you considered my servant Job? For there is no one like him on the earth, a blameless and an upright man, one who fears God, and turns away from evil. He still maintains his integrity, although you incited me against him, to ruin him without cause.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Satan answered the LORD, and said, \u201cSkin for skin. Yes, all that a man has he will give for his life."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But stretch out your hand now, and touch his bone and his flesh, and he will renounce you to your face.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Satan, \u201cBehold, he is in your hand. Only spare his life.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"So Satan went out from the presence of the LORD, and struck Job with painful sores from the sole of his foot to his head."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He took for himself a potsherd to scrape himself with, and he sat among the ashes."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then his wife said to him, \u201cDo you still maintain your integrity? Renounce God, and die.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said to her, \u201cYou speak as one of the foolish women would speak. What? Shall we receive good at the hand of God, and shall we not receive evil?\u201d"],[0,"In all this Job didn\u2019t sin with his lips."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now when Job\u2019s three friends heard of all this evil that had come on him, they each came from his own place: Eliphaz the Temanite, Bildad the Shuhite, and Zophar the Naamathite; and they made an appointment together to come to sympathize with him and to comfort him."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When they lifted up their eyes from a distance, and didn\u2019t recognize him, they raised their voices, and wept; and they each tore his robe, and sprinkled dust on their heads toward the sky."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So they sat down with him on the ground seven days and seven nights, and no one spoke a word to him, for they saw that his grief was very great."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this Job opened his mouth, and cursed the day of his birth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Job answered:"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLet the day perish in which I was born,"],[2,"the night which said, \u2018There is a boy conceived.\u2019"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Let that day be darkness."],[2,"Don\u2019t let God from above seek for it,"],[2,"neither let the light shine on it."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let darkness and the shadow of death claim it for their own."],[2,"Let a cloud dwell on it."],[2,"Let all that makes the day black terrify it."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"As for that night, let thick darkness seize on it."],[2,"Let it not rejoice among the days of the year."],[2,"Let it not come into the number of the months."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, let that night be barren."],[2,"Let no joyful voice come therein."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them curse it who curse the day,"],[2,"who are ready to rouse up leviathan."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the stars of its twilight be dark."],[2,"Let it look for light, but have none,"],[2,"neither let it see the eyelids of the morning,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"because it didn\u2019t shut up the doors of my mother\u2019s womb,"],[2,"nor did it hide trouble from my eyes."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhy didn\u2019t I die from the womb?"],[2,"Why didn\u2019t I give up the spirit when my mother bore me?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Why did the knees receive me?"],[2,"Or why the breast, that I should nurse?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For now I should have lain down and been quiet."],[2,"I should have slept, then I would have been at rest,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"with kings and counselors of the earth,"],[2,"who built up waste places for themselves;"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"or with princes who had gold,"],[2,"who filled their houses with silver;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"or as a hidden untimely birth I had not been,"],[2,"as infants who never saw light."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"There the wicked cease from troubling."],[2,"There the weary are at rest."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"There the prisoners are at ease together."],[2,"They don\u2019t hear the voice of the taskmaster."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The small and the great are there."],[2,"The servant is free from his master."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhy is light given to him who is in misery,"],[2,"life to the bitter in soul,"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"who long for death, but it doesn\u2019t come;"],[2,"and dig for it more than for hidden treasures,"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"who rejoice exceedingly,"],[2,"and are glad, when they can find the grave?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Why is light given to a man whose way is hidden,"],[2,"whom God has hedged in?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"For my sighing comes before I eat."],[2,"My groanings are poured out like water."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"For the thing which I fear comes on me,"],[2,"that which I am afraid of comes to me."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"I am not at ease, neither am I quiet, neither do I have rest;"],[2,"but trouble comes.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf someone ventures to talk with you, will you be grieved?"],[2,"But who can withhold himself from speaking?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you have instructed many,"],[2,"you have strengthened the weak hands."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Your words have supported him who was falling,"],[2,"you have made the feeble knees firm."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"But now it has come to you, and you faint."],[2,"It touches you, and you are troubled."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t your piety your confidence?"],[2,"Isn\u2019t the integrity of your ways your hope?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cRemember, now, who ever perished, being innocent?"],[2,"Or where were the upright cut off?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"According to what I have seen, those who plow iniquity"],[2,"and sow trouble, reap the same."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"By the breath of God they perish."],[2,"By the blast of his anger are they consumed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The roaring of the lion,"],[2,"and the voice of the fierce lion,"],[2,"the teeth of the young lions, are broken."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The old lion perishes for lack of prey."],[2,"The cubs of the lioness are scattered abroad."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow a thing was secretly brought to me."],[2,"My ear received a whisper of it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"In thoughts from the visions of the night,"],[2,"when deep sleep falls on men,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"fear came on me, and trembling,"],[2,"which made all my bones shake."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Then a spirit passed before my face."],[2,"The hair of my flesh stood up."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"It stood still, but I couldn\u2019t discern its appearance."],[2,"A form was before my eyes."],[2,"Silence, then I heard a voice, saying,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018Shall mortal man be more just than God?"],[2,"Shall a man be more pure than his Maker?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he puts no trust in his servants."],[2,"He charges his angels with error."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"How much more those who dwell in houses of clay,"],[2,"whose foundation is in the dust,"],[2,"who are crushed before the moth!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Between morning and evening they are destroyed."],[2,"They perish forever without any regarding it."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t their tent cord plucked up within them?"],[2,"They die, and that without wisdom.\u2019"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCall now; is there any who will answer you?"],[2,"To which of the holy ones will you turn?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For resentment kills the foolish man,"],[2,"and jealousy kills the simple."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I have seen the foolish taking root,"],[2,"but suddenly I cursed his habitation."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"His children are far from safety."],[2,"They are crushed in the gate."],[2,"Neither is there any to deliver them,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"whose harvest the hungry eat up,"],[2,"and take it even out of the thorns."],[2,"The snare gapes for their substance."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For affliction doesn\u2019t come out of the dust,"],[2,"neither does trouble spring out of the ground;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"but man is born to trouble,"],[2,"as the sparks fly upward."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut as for me, I would seek God."],[2,"I would commit my cause to God,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"who does great things that can\u2019t be fathomed,"],[2,"marvelous things without number;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"who gives rain on the earth,"],[2,"and sends waters on the fields;"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"so that he sets up on high those who are low,"],[2,"those who mourn are exalted to safety."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"He frustrates the plans of the crafty,"],[2,"so that their hands can\u2019t perform their enterprise."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He takes the wise in their own craftiness;"],[2,"the counsel of the cunning is carried headlong."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They meet with darkness in the day time,"],[2,"and grope at noonday as in the night."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"But he saves from the sword of their mouth,"],[2,"even the needy from the hand of the mighty."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"So the poor has hope,"],[2,"and injustice shuts her mouth."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, happy is the man whom God corrects."],[2,"Therefore do not despise the chastening of the Almighty."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For he wounds and binds up."],[2,"He injures and his hands make whole."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He will deliver you in six troubles;"],[2,"yes, in seven no evil will touch you."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"In famine he will redeem you from death;"],[2,"in war, from the power of the sword."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"You will be hidden from the scourge of the tongue,"],[2,"neither will you be afraid of destruction when it comes."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"You will laugh at destruction and famine,"],[2,"neither will you be afraid of the animals of the earth."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"For you will be allied with the stones of the field."],[2,"The animals of the field will be at peace with you."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"You will know that your tent is in peace."],[2,"You will visit your fold, and will miss nothing."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"You will know also that your offspring will be great,"],[2,"your offspring as the grass of the earth."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"You will come to your grave in a full age,"],[2,"like a shock of grain comes in its season."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, we have researched it. It is so."],[2,"Hear it, and know it for your good.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOh that my anguish were weighed,"],[2,"and all my calamity laid in the balances!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For now it would be heavier than the sand of the seas,"],[2,"therefore my words have been rash."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the arrows of the Almighty are within me."],[2,"My spirit drinks up their poison."],[1,"The terrors of God set themselves in array against me."]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"Does the wild donkey bray when he has grass?"],[1,"Or does the ox low over his fodder?"]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"Can that which has no flavor be eaten without salt?"],[1,"Or is there any taste in the white of an egg?"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"My soul refuses to touch them."],[1,"They are as loathsome food to me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOh that I might have my request,"],[2,"that God would grant the thing that I long for,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"even that it would please God to crush me;"],[2,"that he would let loose his hand, and cut me off!"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Let it still be my consolation,"],[2,"yes, let me exult in pain that doesn\u2019t spare,"],[2,"that I have not denied the words of the Holy One."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"What is my strength, that I should wait?"],[2,"What is my end, that I should be patient?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Is my strength the strength of stones?"],[2,"Or is my flesh of bronze?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t it that I have no help in me,"],[2,"that wisdom is driven away from me?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTo him who is ready to faint, kindness should be shown from his friend;"],[2,"even to him who forsakes the fear of the Almighty."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"My brothers have dealt deceitfully as a brook,"],[2,"as the channel of brooks that pass away;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"which are black by reason of the ice,"],[2,"in which the snow hides itself."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"In the dry season, they vanish."],[2,"When it is hot, they are consumed out of their place."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The caravans that travel beside them turn away."],[2,"They go up into the waste, and perish."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The caravans of Tema looked."],[2,"The companies of Sheba waited for them."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"They were distressed because they were confident."],[2,"They came there, and were confounded."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For now you are nothing."],[2,"You see a terror, and are afraid."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Did I ever say, \u2018Give to me\u2019?"],[2,"or, \u2018Offer a present for me from your substance\u2019?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"or, \u2018Deliver me from the adversary\u2019s hand\u2019?"],[2,"or, \u2018Redeem me from the hand of the oppressors\u2019?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTeach me, and I will hold my peace."],[2,"Cause me to understand my error."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"How forcible are words of uprightness!"],[2,"But your reproof, what does it reprove?"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you intend to reprove words,"],[2,"since the speeches of one who is desperate are as wind?"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, you would even cast lots for the fatherless,"],[2,"and make merchandise of your friend."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Now therefore be pleased to look at me,"],[2,"for surely I will not lie to your face."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Please return."],[2,"Let there be no injustice."],[2,"Yes, return again."],[2,"My cause is righteous."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Is there injustice on my tongue?"],[2,"Can\u2019t my taste discern mischievous things?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIsn\u2019t a man forced to labor on earth?"],[2,"Aren\u2019t his days like the days of a hired hand?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"As a servant who earnestly desires the shadow,"],[2,"as a hireling who looks for his wages,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"so I am made to possess months of misery,"],[2,"wearisome nights are appointed to me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"When I lie down, I say,"],[2,"\u2018When will I arise, and the night be gone?\u2019"],[2,"I toss and turn until the dawning of the day."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My flesh is clothed with worms and clods of dust."],[2,"My skin closes up, and breaks out afresh."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My days are swifter than a weaver\u2019s shuttle,"],[2,"and are spent without hope."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh remember that my life is a breath."],[2,"My eye will no more see good."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The eye of him who sees me will see me no more."],[2,"Your eyes will be on me, but I will not be."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"As the cloud is consumed and vanishes away,"],[2,"so he who goes down to Sheol will come up no more."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He will return no more to his house,"],[2,"neither will his place know him any more."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore I will not keep silent."],[2,"I will speak in the anguish of my spirit."],[2,"I will complain in the bitterness of my soul."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Am I a sea, or a sea monster,"],[2,"that you put a guard over me?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"When I say, \u2018My bed will comfort me."],[2,"My couch will ease my complaint,\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"then you scare me with dreams"],[2,"and terrify me through visions,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"so that my soul chooses strangling,"],[2,"death rather than my bones."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I loathe my life."],[2,"I don\u2019t want to live forever."],[2,"Leave me alone, for my days are but a breath."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"What is man, that you should magnify him,"],[2,"that you should set your mind on him,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"that you should visit him every morning,"],[2,"and test him every moment?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"How long will you not look away from me,"],[2,"nor leave me alone until I swallow down my spittle?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"If I have sinned, what do I do to you, you watcher of men?"],[2,"Why have you set me as a mark for you,"],[2,"so that I am a burden to myself?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you not pardon my disobedience, and take away my iniquity?"],[2,"For now will I lie down in the dust."],[2,"You will seek me diligently, but I will not be.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow long will you speak these things?"],[2,"Shall the words of your mouth be a mighty wind?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Does God pervert justice?"],[2,"Or does the Almighty pervert righteousness?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"If your children have sinned against him,"],[2,"he has delivered them into the hand of their disobedience."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"If you want to seek God diligently,"],[2,"make your supplication to the Almighty."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"If you were pure and upright,"],[2,"surely now he would awaken for you,"],[1,"and make the habitation of your righteousness prosperous."]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"Though your beginning was small,"],[1,"yet your latter end would greatly increase."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cPlease inquire of past generations."],[2,"Find out about the learning of their fathers."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"(For we are but of yesterday, and know nothing,"],[2,"because our days on earth are a shadow.)"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall they not teach you, tell you,"],[2,"and utter words out of their heart?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan the papyrus grow up without mire?"],[2,"Can the rushes grow without water?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"While it is yet in its greenness, not cut down,"],[2,"it withers before any other reed."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"So are the paths of all who forget God."],[2,"The hope of the godless man will perish,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"whose confidence will break apart,"],[2,"whose trust is a spider\u2019s web."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He will lean on his house, but it will not stand."],[2,"He will cling to it, but it will not endure."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He is green before the sun."],[2,"His shoots go out along his garden."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"His roots are wrapped around the rock pile."],[2,"He sees the place of stones."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"If he is destroyed from his place,"],[2,"then it will deny him, saying, \u2018I have not seen you.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, this is the joy of his way."],[2,"Out of the earth, others will spring."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, God will not cast away a blameless man,"],[2,"neither will he uphold the evildoers."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He will still fill your mouth with laughter,"],[2,"your lips with shouting."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who hate you will be clothed with shame."],[2,"The tent of the wicked will be no more.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTruly I know that it is so,"],[2,"but how can man be just with God?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"If he is pleased to contend with him,"],[2,"he can\u2019t answer him one time in a thousand."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"God is wise in heart, and mighty in strength."],[2,"Who has hardened himself against him and prospered?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He removes the mountains, and they don\u2019t know it,"],[2,"when he overturns them in his anger."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He shakes the earth out of its place."],[2,"Its pillars tremble."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He commands the sun and it doesn\u2019t rise,"],[2,"and seals up the stars."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He alone stretches out the heavens,"],[2,"and treads on the waves of the sea."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes the Bear, Orion, and the Pleiades,"],[2,"and the rooms of the south."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He does great things past finding out;"],[2,"yes, marvelous things without number."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he goes by me, and I don\u2019t see him."],[2,"He passes on also, but I don\u2019t perceive him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he snatches away."],[2,"Who can hinder him?"],[2,"Who will ask him, \u2018What are you doing?\u2019"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGod will not withdraw his anger."],[2,"The helpers of Rahab stoop under him."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"How much less will I answer him,"],[2,"and choose my words to argue with him?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Though I were righteous, yet I wouldn\u2019t answer him."],[2,"I would make supplication to my judge."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"If I had called, and he had answered me,"],[2,"yet I wouldn\u2019t believe that he listened to my voice."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For he breaks me with a storm,"],[2,"and multiplies my wounds without cause."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not allow me to catch my breath,"],[2,"but fills me with bitterness."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"If it is a matter of strength, behold, he is mighty!"],[2,"If of justice, \u2018Who,\u2019 says he, \u2018will summon me?\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Though I am righteous, my own mouth will condemn me."],[2,"Though I am blameless, it will prove me perverse."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"I am blameless."],[2,"I don\u2019t respect myself."],[2,"I despise my life."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIt is all the same."],[2,"Therefore I say he destroys the blameless and the wicked."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"If the scourge kills suddenly,"],[2,"he will mock at the trial of the innocent."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth is given into the hand of the wicked."],[2,"He covers the faces of its judges."],[2,"If not he, then who is it?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow my days are swifter than a runner."],[2,"They flee away. They see no good."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"They have passed away as the swift ships,"],[2,"as the eagle that swoops on the prey."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"If I say, \u2018I will forget my complaint,"],[2,"I will put off my sad face, and cheer up,\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"I am afraid of all my sorrows."],[2,"I know that you will not hold me innocent."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"I will be condemned."],[2,"Why then do I labor in vain?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"If I wash myself with snow,"],[2,"and cleanse my hands with lye,"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"yet you will plunge me in the ditch."],[2,"My own clothes will abhor me."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"For he is not a man, as I am, that I should answer him,"],[2,"that we should come together in judgment."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no umpire between us,"],[2,"that might lay his hand on us both."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Let him take his rod away from me."],[2,"Let his terror not make me afraid;"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"then I would speak, and not fear him,"],[2,"for I am not so in myself."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMy soul is weary of my life."],[2,"I will give free course to my complaint."],[2,"I will speak in the bitterness of my soul."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will tell God, \u2018Do not condemn me."],[2,"Show me why you contend with me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Is it good to you that you should oppress,"],[2,"that you should despise the work of your hands,"],[2,"and smile on the counsel of the wicked?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you have eyes of flesh?"],[2,"Or do you see as man sees?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Are your days as the days of mortals,"],[2,"or your years as man\u2019s years,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"that you inquire after my iniquity,"],[2,"and search after my sin?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Although you know that I am not wicked,"],[2,"there is no one who can deliver out of your hand."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018Your hands have framed me and fashioned me altogether,"],[2,"yet you destroy me."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember, I beg you, that you have fashioned me as clay."],[2,"Will you bring me into dust again?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Haven\u2019t you poured me out like milk,"],[2,"and curdled me like cheese?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You have clothed me with skin and flesh,"],[2,"and knit me together with bones and sinews."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You have granted me life and loving kindness."],[2,"Your visitation has preserved my spirit."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet you hid these things in your heart."],[2,"I know that this is with you:"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"if I sin, then you mark me."],[2,"You will not acquit me from my iniquity."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"If I am wicked, woe to me."],[2,"If I am righteous, I still will not lift up my head,"],[2,"being filled with disgrace,"],[2,"and conscious of my affliction."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"If my head is held high, you hunt me like a lion."],[2,"Again you show yourself powerful to me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"You renew your witnesses against me,"],[2,"and increase your indignation on me."],[2,"Changes and warfare are with me."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018Why, then, have you brought me out of the womb?"],[2,"I wish I had given up the spirit, and no eye had seen me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I should have been as though I had not been."],[2,"I should have been carried from the womb to the grave."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Aren\u2019t my days few?"],[2,"Stop!"],[1,"Leave me alone, that I may find a little comfort,"]]},{v:21,l:[[2,"before I go where I will not return from,"],[2,"to the land of darkness and of the shadow of death;"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"the land dark as midnight,"],[2,"of the shadow of death,"],[2,"without any order,"],[2,"where the light is as midnight.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zophar, the Naamathite, answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cShouldn\u2019t the multitude of words be answered?"],[2,"Should a man full of talk be justified?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Should your boastings make men hold their peace?"],[2,"When you mock, will no man make you ashamed?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For you say, \u2018My doctrine is pure."],[2,"I am clean in your eyes.\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"But oh that God would speak,"],[2,"and open his lips against you,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"that he would show you the secrets of wisdom!"],[2,"For true wisdom has two sides."],[2,"Know therefore that God exacts of you less than your iniquity deserves."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan you fathom the mystery of God?"],[2,"Or can you probe the limits of the Almighty?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They are high as heaven. What can you do?"],[2,"They are deeper than Sheol. What can you know?"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Its measure is longer than the earth,"],[2,"and broader than the sea."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"If he passes by, or confines,"],[2,"or convenes a court, then who can oppose him?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For he knows false men."],[2,"He sees iniquity also, even though he doesn\u2019t consider it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"An empty-headed man becomes wise"],[2,"when a man is born as a wild donkey\u2019s colt."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf you set your heart aright,"],[2,"stretch out your hands toward him."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"If iniquity is in your hand, put it far away."],[2,"Don\u2019t let unrighteousness dwell in your tents."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely then you will lift up your face without spot."],[2,"Yes, you will be steadfast, and will not fear,"]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"for you will forget your misery."],[2,"You will remember it like waters that have passed away."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Life will be clearer than the noonday."],[2,"Though there is darkness, it will be as the morning."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"You will be secure, because there is hope."],[2,"Yes, you will search, and will take your rest in safety."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Also you will lie down, and no one will make you afraid."],[2,"Yes, many will court your favor."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"But the eyes of the wicked will fail."],[2,"They will have no way to flee."],[2,"Their hope will be the giving up of the spirit.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNo doubt, but you are the people,"],[2,"and wisdom will die with you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"But I have understanding as well as you;"],[2,"I am not inferior to you."],[2,"Yes, who doesn\u2019t know such things as these?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I am like one who is a joke to his neighbor,"],[2,"I, who called on God, and he answered."],[2,"The just, the blameless man is a joke."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"In the thought of him who is at ease there is contempt for misfortune."],[2,"It is ready for them whose foot slips."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The tents of robbers prosper."],[2,"Those who provoke God are secure,"],[2,"who carry their god in their hands."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut ask the animals now, and they will teach you;"],[2,"the birds of the sky, and they will tell you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Or speak to the earth, and it will teach you."],[2,"The fish of the sea will declare to you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Who doesn\u2019t know that in all these,"],[2,"the LORD\u2019s hand has done this,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"in whose hand is the life of every living thing,"],[2,"and the breath of all mankind?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Doesn\u2019t the ear try words,"],[2,"even as the palate tastes its food?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"With aged men is wisdom,"],[2,"in length of days understanding."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWith God is wisdom and might."],[2,"He has counsel and understanding."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he breaks down, and it can\u2019t be built again."],[2,"He imprisons a man, and there can be no release."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he withholds the waters, and they dry up."],[2,"Again, he sends them out, and they overturn the earth."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"With him is strength and wisdom."],[2,"The deceived and the deceiver are his."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He leads counselors away stripped."],[2,"He makes judges fools."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He loosens the bond of kings."],[2,"He binds their waist with a belt."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He leads priests away stripped,"],[2,"and overthrows the mighty."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He removes the speech of those who are trusted,"],[2,"and takes away the understanding of the elders."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He pours contempt on princes,"],[2,"and loosens the belt of the strong."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"He uncovers deep things out of darkness,"],[2,"and brings out to light the shadow of death."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"He increases the nations, and he destroys them."],[2,"He enlarges the nations, and he leads them captive."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"He takes away understanding from the chiefs of the people of the earth,"],[2,"and causes them to wander in a wilderness where there is no way."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"They grope in the dark without light."],[2,"He makes them stagger like a drunken man."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, my eye has seen all this."],[2,"My ear has heard and understood it."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"What you know, I know also."],[2,"I am not inferior to you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSurely I would speak to the Almighty."],[2,"I desire to reason with God."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"But you are forgers of lies."],[2,"You are all physicians of no value."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that you would be completely silent!"],[2,"Then you would be wise."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear now my reasoning."],[2,"Listen to the pleadings of my lips."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you speak unrighteously for God,"],[2,"and talk deceitfully for him?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you show partiality to him?"],[2,"Will you contend for God?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Is it good that he should search you out?"],[2,"Or as one deceives a man, will you deceive him?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He will surely reprove you"],[2,"if you secretly show partiality."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Won\u2019t his majesty make you afraid"],[2,"and his dread fall on you?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Your memorable sayings are proverbs of ashes."],[2,"Your defenses are defenses of clay."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBe silent!"],[2,"Leave me alone, that I may speak."],[2,"Let come on me what will."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Why should I take my flesh in my teeth,"],[2,"and put my life in my hand?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he will kill me."],[2,"I have no hope."],[2,"Nevertheless, I will maintain my ways before him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"This also will be my salvation,"],[2,"that a godless man will not come before him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen carefully to my speech."],[2,"Let my declaration be in your ears."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"See now, I have set my cause in order."],[2,"I know that I am righteous."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is he who will contend with me?"],[2,"For then I would hold my peace and give up the spirit."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOnly don\u2019t do two things to me,"],[2,"then I will not hide myself from your face:"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"withdraw your hand far from me,"],[2,"and don\u2019t let your terror make me afraid."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Then call, and I will answer,"],[2,"or let me speak, and you answer me."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"How many are my iniquities and sins?"],[2,"Make me know my disobedience and my sin."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you hide your face,"],[2,"and consider me your enemy?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you harass a driven leaf?"],[2,"Will you pursue the dry stubble?"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"For you write bitter things against me,"],[2,"and make me inherit the iniquities of my youth."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"You also put my feet in the stocks,"],[2,"and mark all my paths."],[2,"You set a bound to the soles of my feet,"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"though I am decaying like a rotten thing,"],[2,"like a garment that is moth-eaten."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMan, who is born of a woman,"],[2,"is of few days, and full of trouble."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He grows up like a flower, and is cut down."],[2,"He also flees like a shadow, and doesn\u2019t continue."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you open your eyes on such a one,"],[2,"and bring me into judgment with you?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can bring a clean thing out of an unclean?"],[2,"Not one."]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"Seeing his days are determined,"],[2,"the number of his months is with you,"],[2,"and you have appointed his bounds that he can\u2019t pass."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Look away from him, that he may rest,"],[2,"until he accomplishes, as a hireling, his day."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor there is hope for a tree if it is cut down,"],[2,"that it will sprout again,"],[2,"that the tender branch of it will not cease."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Though its root grows old in the earth,"],[2,"and its stock dies in the ground,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"yet through the scent of water it will bud,"],[2,"and sprout boughs like a plant."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But man dies, and is laid low."],[2,"Yes, man gives up the spirit, and where is he?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"As the waters fail from the sea,"],[2,"and the river wastes and dries up,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"so man lies down and doesn\u2019t rise."],[2,"Until the heavens are no more, they will not awake,"],[2,"nor be roused out of their sleep."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOh that you would hide me in Sheol,"],[2,"that you would keep me secret until your wrath is past,"],[2,"that you would appoint me a set time and remember me!"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"If a man dies, will he live again?"],[2,"I would wait all the days of my warfare,"],[2,"until my release should come."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You would call, and I would answer you."],[2,"You would have a desire for the work of your hands."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"But now you count my steps."],[2,"Don\u2019t you watch over my sin?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"My disobedience is sealed up in a bag."],[2,"You fasten up my iniquity."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut the mountain falling comes to nothing."],[2,"The rock is removed out of its place."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The waters wear the stones."],[2,"The torrents of it wash away the dust of the earth."],[2,"So you destroy the hope of man."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"You forever prevail against him, and he departs."],[2,"You change his face, and send him away."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"His sons come to honor, and he doesn\u2019t know it."],[2,"They are brought low, but he doesn\u2019t perceive it of them."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"But his flesh on him has pain,"],[2,"and his soul within him mourns.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cShould a wise man answer with vain knowledge,"],[2,"and fill himself with the east wind?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Should he reason with unprofitable talk,"],[2,"or with speeches with which he can do no good?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, you do away with fear,"],[2,"and hinder devotion before God."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For your iniquity teaches your mouth,"],[2,"and you choose the language of the crafty."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Your own mouth condemns you, and not I."],[2,"Yes, your own lips testify against you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAre you the first man who was born?"],[2,"Or were you brought out before the hills?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Have you heard the secret counsel of God?"],[2,"Do you limit wisdom to yourself?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"What do you know that we don\u2019t know?"],[2,"What do you understand which is not in us?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"With us are both the gray-headed and the very aged men,"],[2,"much older than your father."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Are the consolations of God too small for you,"],[2,"even the word that is gentle toward you?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Why does your heart carry you away?"],[2,"Why do your eyes flash,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"that you turn your spirit against God,"],[2,"and let such words go out of your mouth?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"What is man, that he should be clean?"],[2,"What is he who is born of a woman, that he should be righteous?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he puts no trust in his holy ones."],[2,"Yes, the heavens are not clean in his sight;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"how much less one who is abominable and corrupt,"],[2,"a man who drinks iniquity like water!"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will show you, listen to me;"],[2,"that which I have seen I will declare"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"(which wise men have told by their fathers,"],[2,"and have not hidden it;"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"to whom alone the land was given,"],[2,"and no stranger passed among them):"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"the wicked man writhes in pain all his days,"],[2,"even the number of years that are laid up for the oppressor."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"A sound of terrors is in his ears."],[2,"In prosperity the destroyer will come on him."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"He doesn\u2019t believe that he will return out of darkness."],[2,"He is waited for by the sword."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"He wanders abroad for bread, saying, \u2018Where is it?\u2019"],[2,"He knows that the day of darkness is ready at his hand."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Distress and anguish make him afraid."],[2,"They prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Because he has stretched out his hand against God,"],[2,"and behaves himself proudly against the Almighty,"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"he runs at him with a stiff neck,"],[2,"with the thick shields of his bucklers,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"because he has covered his face with his fatness,"],[2,"and gathered fat on his thighs."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"He has lived in desolate cities,"],[2,"in houses which no one inhabited,"],[2,"which were ready to become heaps."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not be rich, neither will his substance continue,"],[2,"neither will their possessions be extended on the earth."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not depart out of darkness."],[2,"The flame will dry up his branches."],[2,"He will go away by the breath of God\u2019s mouth."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Let him not trust in emptiness, deceiving himself,"],[2,"for emptiness will be his reward."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"It will be accomplished before his time."],[2,"His branch will not be green."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"He will shake off his unripe grape as the vine,"],[2,"and will cast off his flower as the olive tree."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"For the company of the godless will be barren,"],[2,"and fire will consume the tents of bribery."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"They conceive mischief and produce iniquity."],[2,"Their heart prepares deceit.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have heard many such things."],[2,"You are all miserable comforters!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall vain words have an end?"],[2,"Or what provokes you that you answer?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I also could speak as you do."],[2,"If your soul were in my soul\u2019s place,"],[2,"I could join words together against you,"],[2,"and shake my head at you,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"but I would strengthen you with my mouth."],[2,"The solace of my lips would relieve you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThough I speak, my grief is not subsided."],[2,"Though I forbear, what am I eased?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But now, God, you have surely worn me out."],[2,"You have made all my company desolate."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You have shriveled me up. This is a witness against me."],[2,"My leanness rises up against me."],[2,"It testifies to my face."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He has torn me in his wrath and persecuted me."],[2,"He has gnashed on me with his teeth."],[2,"My adversary sharpens his eyes on me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They have gaped on me with their mouth."],[2,"They have struck me on the cheek reproachfully."],[2,"They gather themselves together against me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"God delivers me to the ungodly,"],[2,"and casts me into the hands of the wicked."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I was at ease, and he broke me apart."],[2,"Yes, he has taken me by the neck, and dashed me to pieces."],[2,"He has also set me up for his target."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"His archers surround me."],[2,"He splits my kidneys apart, and does not spare."],[2,"He pours out my bile on the ground."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He breaks me with breach on breach."],[2,"He runs at me like a giant."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I have sewed sackcloth on my skin,"],[2,"and have thrust my horn in the dust."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"My face is red with weeping."],[2,"Deep darkness is on my eyelids,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"although there is no violence in my hands,"],[2,"and my prayer is pure."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEarth, don\u2019t cover my blood."],[2,"Let my cry have no place to rest."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Even now, behold, my witness is in heaven."],[2,"He who vouches for me is on high."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My friends scoff at me."],[2,"My eyes pour out tears to God,"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"that he would maintain the right of a man with God,"],[2,"of a son of man with his neighbor!"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For when a few years have come,"],[2,"I will go the way of no return."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMy spirit is consumed."],[2,"My days are extinct"],[2,"and the grave is ready for me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely there are mockers with me."],[2,"My eye dwells on their provocation."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow give a pledge. Be collateral for me with yourself."],[2,"Who is there who will strike hands with me?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have hidden their heart from understanding,"],[2,"therefore you will not exalt them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He who denounces his friends for plunder,"],[2,"even the eyes of his children will fail."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut he has made me a byword of the people."],[2,"They spit in my face."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"My eye also is dim by reason of sorrow."],[2,"All my members are as a shadow."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Upright men will be astonished at this."],[2,"The innocent will stir himself up against the godless."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet the righteous will hold to his way."],[2,"He who has clean hands will grow stronger and stronger."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for you all, come back."],[2,"I will not find a wise man among you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"My days are past."],[2,"My plans are broken off,"],[2,"as are the thoughts of my heart."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They change the night into day,"],[2,"saying \u2018The light is near\u2019 in the presence of darkness."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"If I look for Sheol as my house,"],[2,"if I have spread my couch in the darkness,"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"if I have said to corruption, \u2018You are my father,\u2019"],[2,"and to the worm, \u2018My mother,\u2019 and \u2018My sister,\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"where then is my hope?"],[2,"As for my hope, who will see it?"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall it go down with me to the gates of Sheol,"],[2,"or descend together into the dust?\u201d"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow long will you hunt for words?"],[2,"Consider, and afterwards we will speak."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Why are we counted as animals,"],[2,"which have become unclean in your sight?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You who tear yourself in your anger,"],[2,"will the earth be forsaken for you?"],[2,"Or will the rock be removed out of its place?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYes, the light of the wicked will be put out."],[2,"The spark of his fire won\u2019t shine."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The light will be dark in his tent."],[2,"His lamp above him will be put out."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The steps of his strength will be shortened."],[2,"His own counsel will cast him down."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For he is cast into a net by his own feet,"],[2,"and he wanders into its mesh."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"A snare will take him by the heel."],[2,"A trap will catch him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"A noose is hidden for him in the ground,"],[2,"a trap for him on the path."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Terrors will make him afraid on every side,"],[2,"and will chase him at his heels."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"His strength will be famished."],[2,"Calamity will be ready at his side."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The members of his body will be devoured."],[2,"The firstborn of death will devour his members."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He will be rooted out of the security of his tent."],[2,"He will be brought to the king of terrors."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"There will dwell in his tent that which is none of his."],[2,"Sulfur will be scattered on his habitation."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"His roots will be dried up beneath."],[2,"His branch will be cut off above."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"His memory will perish from the earth."],[2,"He will have no name in the street."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He will be driven from light into darkness,"],[2,"and chased out of the world."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He will have neither son nor grandson among his people,"],[2,"nor any remaining where he lived."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who come after will be astonished at his day,"],[2,"as those who went before were frightened."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely such are the dwellings of the unrighteous."],[2,"This is the place of him who doesn\u2019t know God.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow long will you torment me,"],[2,"and crush me with words?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You have reproached me ten times."],[2,"You aren\u2019t ashamed that you attack me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"If it is true that I have erred,"],[2,"my error remains with myself."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"If indeed you will magnify yourselves against me,"],[2,"and plead against me my reproach,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"know now that God has subverted me,"],[2,"and has surrounded me with his net."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I cry out of wrong, but I am not heard."],[2,"I cry for help, but there is no justice."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He has walled up my way so that I can\u2019t pass,"],[2,"and has set darkness in my paths."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He has stripped me of my glory,"],[2,"and taken the crown from my head."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He has broken me down on every side, and I am gone."],[2,"He has plucked my hope up like a tree."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He has also kindled his wrath against me."],[2,"He counts me among his adversaries."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"His troops come on together,"],[2,"build a siege ramp against me,"],[2,"and encamp around my tent."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHe has put my brothers far from me."],[2,"My acquaintances are wholly estranged from me."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"My relatives have gone away."],[2,"My familiar friends have forgotten me."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who dwell in my house and my maids consider me a stranger."],[2,"I am an alien in their sight."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I call to my servant, and he gives me no answer."],[2,"I beg him with my mouth."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"My breath is offensive to my wife."],[2,"I am loathsome to the children of my own mother."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Even young children despise me."],[2,"If I arise, they speak against me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"All my familiar friends abhor me."],[2,"They whom I loved have turned against me."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My bones stick to my skin and to my flesh."],[2,"I have escaped by the skin of my teeth."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHave pity on me. Have pity on me, you my friends,"],[2,"for the hand of God has touched me."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you persecute me as God,"],[2,"and are not satisfied with my flesh?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOh that my words were now written!"],[2,"Oh that they were inscribed in a book!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"That with an iron pen and lead"],[2,"they were engraved in the rock forever!"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, I know that my Redeemer lives."],[2,"In the end, he will stand upon the earth."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"After my skin is destroyed,"],[2,"then I will see God in my flesh,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"whom I, even I, will see on my side."],[2,"My eyes will see, and not as a stranger."],[1,"\u201cMy heart is consumed within me."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"If you say, \u2018How we will persecute him!\u2019"],[2,"because the root of the matter is found in me,"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"be afraid of the sword,"],[2,"for wrath brings the punishments of the sword,"],[2,"that you may know there is a judgment.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zophar the Naamathite answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore my thoughts answer me,"],[2,"even by reason of my haste that is in me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I have heard the reproof which puts me to shame."],[2,"The spirit of my understanding answers me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t you know this from old time,"],[2,"since man was placed on earth,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"that the triumphing of the wicked is short,"],[2,"the joy of the godless but for a moment?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Though his height mount up to the heavens,"],[2,"and his head reach to the clouds,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"yet he will perish forever like his own dung."],[2,"Those who have seen him will say, \u2018Where is he?\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He will fly away as a dream, and will not be found."],[2,"Yes, he will be chased away like a vision of the night."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The eye which saw him will see him no more,"],[2,"neither will his place see him any more."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"His children will seek the favor of the poor."],[2,"His hands will give back his wealth."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"His bones are full of his youth,"],[2,"but youth will lie down with him in the dust."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThough wickedness is sweet in his mouth,"],[2,"though he hide it under his tongue,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"though he spare it, and will not let it go,"],[2,"but keep it still within his mouth,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"yet his food in his bowels is turned."],[2,"It is cobra venom within him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He has swallowed down riches, and he will vomit them up again."],[2,"God will cast them out of his belly."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He will suck cobra venom."],[2,"The viper\u2019s tongue will kill him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not look at the rivers,"],[2,"the flowing streams of honey and butter."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He will restore that for which he labored, and will not swallow it down."],[2,"He will not rejoice according to the substance that he has gotten."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has oppressed and forsaken the poor."],[2,"He has violently taken away a house, and he will not build it up."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBecause he knew no quietness within him,"],[2,"he will not save anything of that in which he delights."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"There was nothing left that he didn\u2019t devour,"],[2,"therefore his prosperity will not endure."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"In the fullness of his sufficiency, distress will overtake him."],[2,"The hand of everyone who is in misery will come on him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"When he is about to fill his belly, God will cast the fierceness of his wrath on him."],[2,"It will rain on him while he is eating."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"He will flee from the iron weapon."],[2,"The bronze arrow will strike him through."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"He draws it out, and it comes out of his body."],[2,"Yes, the glittering point comes out of his liver."],[2,"Terrors are on him."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"All darkness is laid up for his treasures."],[2,"An unfanned fire will devour him."],[2,"It will consume that which is left in his tent."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The heavens will reveal his iniquity."],[2,"The earth will rise up against him."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"The increase of his house will depart."],[2,"They will rush away in the day of his wrath."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"This is the portion of a wicked man from God,"],[2,"the heritage appointed to him by God.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cListen diligently to my speech."],[2,"Let this be your consolation."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Allow me, and I also will speak."],[2,"After I have spoken, mock on."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"As for me, is my complaint to man?"],[2,"Why shouldn\u2019t I be impatient?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Look at me, and be astonished."],[2,"Lay your hand on your mouth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"When I remember, I am troubled."],[2,"Horror takes hold of my flesh."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhy do the wicked live,"],[2,"become old, yes, and grow mighty in power?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Their child is established with them in their sight,"],[2,"their offspring before their eyes."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Their houses are safe from fear,"],[2,"neither is the rod of God upon them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Their bulls breed without fail."],[2,"Their cows calve, and don\u2019t miscarry."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They send out their little ones like a flock."],[2,"Their children dance."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They sing to the tambourine and harp,"],[2,"and rejoice at the sound of the pipe."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They spend their days in prosperity."],[2,"In an instant they go down to Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They tell God, \u2018Depart from us,"],[2,"for we don\u2019t want to know about your ways."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"What is the Almighty, that we should serve him?"],[2,"What profit should we have, if we pray to him?\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, their prosperity is not in their hand."],[2,"The counsel of the wicked is far from me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow often is it that the lamp of the wicked is put out,"],[2,"that their calamity comes on them,"],[2,"that God distributes sorrows in his anger?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"How often is it that they are as stubble before the wind,"],[2,"as chaff that the storm carries away?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"You say, \u2018God lays up his iniquity for his children.\u2019"],[2,"Let him recompense it to himself, that he may know it."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Let his own eyes see his destruction."],[2,"Let him drink of the wrath of the Almighty."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For what does he care for his house after him,"],[2,"when the number of his months is cut off?"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cShall any teach God knowledge,"],[2,"since he judges those who are high?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"One dies in his full strength,"],[2,"being wholly at ease and quiet."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"His pails are full of milk."],[2,"The marrow of his bones is moistened."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Another dies in bitterness of soul,"],[2,"and never tastes of good."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"They lie down alike in the dust."],[2,"The worm covers them."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I know your thoughts,"],[2,"the plans with which you would wrong me."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"For you say, \u2018Where is the house of the prince?"],[2,"Where is the tent in which the wicked lived?\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Haven\u2019t you asked wayfaring men?"],[2,"Don\u2019t you know their evidences,"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"that the evil man is reserved to the day of calamity,"],[2,"that they are led out to the day of wrath?"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Who will declare his way to his face?"],[2,"Who will repay him what he has done?"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet he will be borne to the grave."],[2,"Men will keep watch over the tomb."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"The clods of the valley will be sweet to him."],[2,"All men will draw after him,"],[2,"as there were innumerable before him."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"So how can you comfort me with nonsense,"],[2,"because in your answers there remains only falsehood?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eliphaz the Temanite answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan a man be profitable to God?"],[2,"Surely he who is wise is profitable to himself."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Is it any pleasure to the Almighty that you are righteous?"],[2,"Or does it benefit him that you make your ways perfect?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Is it for your piety that he reproves you,"],[2,"that he enters with you into judgment?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t your wickedness great?"],[2,"Neither is there any end to your iniquities."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have taken pledges from your brother for nothing,"],[2,"and stripped the naked of their clothing."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You haven\u2019t given water to the weary to drink,"],[2,"and you have withheld bread from the hungry."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for the mighty man, he had the earth."],[2,"The honorable man, he lived in it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You have sent widows away empty,"],[2,"and the arms of the fatherless have been broken."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore snares are around you."],[2,"Sudden fear troubles you,"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"or darkness, so that you can not see,"],[2,"and floods of waters cover you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIsn\u2019t God in the heights of heaven?"],[2,"See the height of the stars, how high they are!"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You say, \u2018What does God know?"],[2,"Can he judge through the thick darkness?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Thick clouds are a covering to him, so that he doesn\u2019t see."],[2,"He walks on the vault of the sky.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you keep the old way,"],[2,"which wicked men have trodden,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"who were snatched away before their time,"],[2,"whose foundation was poured out as a stream,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"who said to God, \u2018Depart from us!\u2019"],[2,"and, \u2018What can the Almighty do for us?\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet he filled their houses with good things,"],[2,"but the counsel of the wicked is far from me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous see it, and are glad."],[2,"The innocent ridicule them,"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"saying, \u2018Surely those who rose up against us are cut off."],[2,"The fire has consumed their remnant.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAcquaint yourself with him now, and be at peace."],[2,"By it, good will come to you."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Please receive instruction from his mouth,"],[2,"and lay up his words in your heart."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"If you return to the Almighty, you will be built up,"],[2,"if you put away unrighteousness far from your tents."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Lay your treasure in the dust,"],[2,"the gold of Ophir among the stones of the brooks."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The Almighty will be your treasure,"],[2,"and precious silver to you."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"For then you will delight yourself in the Almighty,"],[2,"and will lift up your face to God."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"You will make your prayer to him, and he will hear you."],[2,"You will pay your vows."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"You will also decree a thing, and it will be established to you."],[2,"Light will shine on your ways."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"When they cast down, you will say, \u2018be lifted up.\u2019"],[2,"He will save the humble person."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"He will even deliver him who is not innocent."],[2,"Yes, he will be delivered through the cleanness of your hands.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEven today my complaint is rebellious."],[2,"His hand is heavy in spite of my groaning."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that I knew where I might find him!"],[2,"That I might come even to his seat!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I would set my cause in order before him,"],[2,"and fill my mouth with arguments."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I would know the words which he would answer me,"],[2,"and understand what he would tell me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Would he contend with me in the greatness of his power?"],[2,"No, but he would listen to me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"There the upright might reason with him,"],[2,"so I should be delivered forever from my judge."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf I go east, he is not there."],[2,"If I go west, I can\u2019t find him."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He works to the north, but I can\u2019t see him."],[2,"He turns south, but I can\u2019t catch a glimpse of him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But he knows the way that I take."],[2,"When he has tried me, I will come out like gold."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"My foot has held fast to his steps."],[2,"I have kept his way, and not turned away."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I haven\u2019t gone back from the commandment of his lips."],[2,"I have treasured up the words of his mouth more than my necessary food."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"But he stands alone, and who can oppose him?"],[2,"What his soul desires, even that he does."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For he performs that which is appointed for me."],[2,"Many such things are with him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I am terrified at his presence."],[2,"When I consider, I am afraid of him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For God has made my heart faint."],[2,"The Almighty has terrified me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Because I was not cut off before the darkness,"],[2,"neither did he cover the thick darkness from my face."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhy aren\u2019t times laid up by the Almighty?"],[2,"Why don\u2019t those who know him see his days?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"There are people who remove the landmarks."],[2,"They violently take away flocks, and feed them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They drive away the donkey of the fatherless,"],[2,"and they take the widow\u2019s ox for a pledge."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They turn the needy out of the way."],[2,"The poor of the earth all hide themselves."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, as wild donkeys in the desert,"],[2,"they go out to their work, seeking diligently for food."],[1,"The wilderness yields them bread for their children."]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"They cut their food in the field."],[1,"They glean the vineyard of the wicked."]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"They lie all night naked without clothing,"],[1,"and have no covering in the cold."]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"They are wet with the showers of the mountains,"],[1,"and embrace the rock for lack of a shelter."]]},{v:9,l:[[2,"There are those who pluck the fatherless from the breast,"],[1,"and take a pledge of the poor,"]]},{v:10,l:[[2,"so that they go around naked without clothing."],[2,"Being hungry, they carry the sheaves."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They make oil within the walls of these men."],[2,"They tread wine presses, and suffer thirst."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"From out of the populous city, men groan."],[2,"The soul of the wounded cries out,"],[2,"yet God doesn\u2019t regard the folly."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThese are of those who rebel against the light."],[2,"They don\u2019t know its ways,"],[2,"nor stay in its paths."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The murderer rises with the light."],[2,"He kills the poor and needy."],[2,"In the night he is like a thief."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The eye also of the adulterer waits for the twilight,"],[2,"saying, \u2018No eye will see me.\u2019"],[2,"He disguises his face."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"In the dark they dig through houses."],[2,"They shut themselves up in the daytime."],[2,"They don\u2019t know the light."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For the morning is to all of them like thick darkness,"],[2,"for they know the terrors of the thick darkness."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThey are foam on the surface of the waters."],[2,"Their portion is cursed on the earth."],[2,"They don\u2019t turn into the way of the vineyards."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Drought and heat consume the snow waters,"],[2,"so does Sheol those who have sinned."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The womb will forget him."],[2,"The worm will feed sweetly on him."],[2,"He will be no more remembered."],[2,"Unrighteousness will be broken as a tree."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He devours the barren who don\u2019t bear."],[2,"He shows no kindness to the widow."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet God preserves the mighty by his power."],[2,"He rises up who has no assurance of life."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"God gives them security, and they rest in it."],[2,"His eyes are on their ways."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"They are exalted; yet a little while, and they are gone."],[2,"Yes, they are brought low, they are taken out of the way as all others,"],[2,"and are cut off as the tops of the ears of grain."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"If it isn\u2019t so now, who will prove me a liar,"],[2,"and make my speech worth nothing?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Bildad the Shuhite answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDominion and fear are with him."],[2,"He makes peace in his high places."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Can his armies be counted?"],[2,"On whom does his light not arise?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"How then can man be just with God?"],[2,"Or how can he who is born of a woman be clean?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, even the moon has no brightness,"],[2,"and the stars are not pure in his sight;"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"How much less man, who is a worm,"],[2,"and the son of man, who is a worm!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow have you helped him who is without power!"],[2,"How have you saved the arm that has no strength!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"How have you counseled him who has no wisdom,"],[2,"and plentifully declared sound knowledge!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"To whom have you uttered words?"],[2,"Whose spirit came out of you?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe departed spirits tremble,"],[2,"those beneath the waters and all that live in them."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Sheol is naked before God,"],[2,"and Abaddon has no covering."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead.","Abaddon means Destroyer."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He stretches out the north over empty space,"],[2,"and hangs the earth on nothing."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He binds up the waters in his thick clouds,"],[2,"and the cloud is not burst under them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He encloses the face of his throne,"],[2,"and spreads his cloud on it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He has described a boundary on the surface of the waters,"],[2,"and to the confines of light and darkness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The pillars of heaven tremble"],[2,"and are astonished at his rebuke."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"He stirs up the sea with his power,"],[2,"and by his understanding he strikes through Rahab."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"By his Spirit the heavens are garnished."],[2,"His hand has pierced the swift serpent."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, these are but the outskirts of his ways."],[2,"How small a whisper do we hear of him!"],[2,"But the thunder of his power who can understand?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Job again took up his parable, and said,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAs God lives, who has taken away my right,"],[2,"the Almighty, who has made my soul bitter"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"(for the length of my life is still in me,"],[2,"and the spirit of God is in my nostrils);"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"surely my lips will not speak unrighteousness,"],[2,"neither will my tongue utter deceit."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Far be it from me that I should justify you."],[2,"Until I die I will not put away my integrity from me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I hold fast to my righteousness, and will not let it go."],[2,"My heart will not reproach me so long as I live."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLet my enemy be as the wicked."],[2,"Let him who rises up against me be as the unrighteous."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For what is the hope of the godless, when he is cut off,"],[2,"when God takes away his life?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Will God hear his cry when trouble comes on him?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Will he delight himself in the Almighty,"],[2,"and call on God at all times?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I will teach you about the hand of God."],[2,"I will not conceal that which is with the Almighty."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, all of you have seen it yourselves;"],[2,"why then have you become altogether vain?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThis is the portion of a wicked man with God,"],[2,"the heritage of oppressors, which they receive from the Almighty."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"If his children are multiplied, it is for the sword."],[2,"His offspring will not be satisfied with bread."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who remain of him will be buried in death."],[2,"His widows will make no lamentation."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Though he heap up silver as the dust,"],[2,"and prepare clothing as the clay;"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"he may prepare it, but the just will put it on,"],[2,"and the innocent will divide the silver."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He builds his house as the moth,"],[2,"as a booth which the watchman makes."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He lies down rich, but he will not do so again."],[2,"He opens his eyes, and he is not."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Terrors overtake him like waters."],[2,"A storm steals him away in the night."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The east wind carries him away, and he departs."],[2,"It sweeps him out of his place."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For it hurls at him, and does not spare,"],[2,"as he flees away from his hand."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Men will clap their hands at him,"],[2,"and will hiss him out of his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSurely there is a mine for silver,"],[2,"and a place for gold which they refine."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Iron is taken out of the earth,"],[2,"and copper is smelted out of the ore."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Man sets an end to darkness,"],[2,"and searches out, to the furthest bound,"],[2,"the stones of obscurity and of thick darkness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He breaks open a shaft away from where people live."],[2,"They are forgotten by the foot."],[2,"They hang far from men, they swing back and forth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"As for the earth, out of it comes bread."],[2,"Underneath it is turned up as it were by fire."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Sapphires come from its rocks."],[2,"It has dust of gold."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"That path no bird of prey knows,"],[2,"neither has the falcon\u2019s eye seen it."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The proud animals have not trodden it,"],[2,"nor has the fierce lion passed by there."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He puts his hand on the flinty rock,"],[2,"and he overturns the mountains by the roots."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He cuts out channels among the rocks."],[2,"His eye sees every precious thing."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He binds the streams that they don\u2019t trickle."],[2,"The thing that is hidden he brings out to light."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut where will wisdom be found?"],[2,"Where is the place of understanding?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Man doesn\u2019t know its price,"],[2,"and it isn\u2019t found in the land of the living."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The deep says, \u2018It isn\u2019t in me.\u2019"],[2,"The sea says, \u2018It isn\u2019t with me.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"It can\u2019t be gotten for gold,"],[2,"neither will silver be weighed for its price."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"It can\u2019t be valued with the gold of Ophir,"],[2,"with the precious onyx, or the sapphire."]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Gold and glass can\u2019t equal it,"],[2,"neither will it be exchanged for jewels of fine gold."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"No mention will be made of coral or of crystal."],[2,"Yes, the price of wisdom is above rubies."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The topaz of Ethiopia will not equal it."],[2,"It won\u2019t be valued with pure gold."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Where then does wisdom come from?"],[2,"Where is the place of understanding?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Seeing it is hidden from the eyes of all living,"],[2,"and kept close from the birds of the sky."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Destruction and Death say,"],[2,"\u2018We have heard a rumor of it with our ears.\u2019"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGod understands its way,"],[2,"and he knows its place."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"For he looks to the ends of the earth,"],[2,"and sees under the whole sky."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"He establishes the force of the wind."],[2,"Yes, he measures out the waters by measure."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"When he made a decree for the rain,"],[2,"and a way for the lightning of the thunder,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"then he saw it, and declared it."],[2,"He established it, yes, and searched it out."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"To man he said,"],[2,"\u2018Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom."],[2,"To depart from evil is understanding.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Job again took up his parable, and said,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOh that I were as in the months of old,"],[2,"as in the days when God watched over me;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"when his lamp shone on my head,"],[2,"and by his light I walked through darkness,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"as I was in my prime,"],[2,"when the friendship of God was in my tent,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"when the Almighty was yet with me,"],[2,"and my children were around me,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"when my steps were washed with butter,"],[2,"and the rock poured out streams of oil for me,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"when I went out to the city gate,"],[2,"when I prepared my seat in the street."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The young men saw me and hid themselves."],[2,"The aged rose up and stood."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The princes refrained from talking,"],[2,"and laid their hand on their mouth."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The voice of the nobles was hushed,"],[2,"and their tongue stuck to the roof of their mouth."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For when the ear heard me, then it blessed me,"],[2,"and when the eye saw me, it commended me,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"because I delivered the poor who cried,"],[2,"and the fatherless also, who had no one to help him,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"the blessing of him who was ready to perish came on me,"],[2,"and I caused the widow\u2019s heart to sing for joy."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I put on righteousness, and it clothed me."],[2,"My justice was as a robe and a diadem."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I was eyes to the blind,"],[2,"and feet to the lame."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I was a father to the needy."],[2,"I researched the cause of him whom I didn\u2019t know."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I broke the jaws of the unrighteous"],[2,"and plucked the prey out of his teeth."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I said, \u2018I will die in my own house,"],[2,"I will count my days as the sand."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"My root is spread out to the waters."],[2,"The dew lies all night on my branch."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My glory is fresh in me."],[2,"My bow is renewed in my hand.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMen listened to me, waited,"],[2,"and kept silence for my counsel."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"After my words they didn\u2019t speak again."],[2,"My speech fell on them."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"They waited for me as for the rain."],[2,"Their mouths drank as with the spring rain."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"I smiled on them when they had no confidence."],[2,"They didn\u2019t reject the light of my face."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"I chose out their way, and sat as chief."],[2,"I lived as a king in the army,"],[2,"as one who comforts the mourners."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut now those who are younger than I have me in derision,"],[2,"whose fathers I considered unworthy to put with my sheep dogs."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Of what use is the strength of their hands to me,"],[2,"men in whom ripe age has perished?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They are gaunt from lack and famine."],[2,"They gnaw the dry ground, in the gloom of waste and desolation."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They pluck salt herbs by the bushes."],[2,"The roots of the broom tree are their food."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They are driven out from among men."],[2,"They cry after them as after a thief,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"so that they live in frightful valleys,"],[2,"and in holes of the earth and of the rocks."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They bray among the bushes."],[2,"They are gathered together under the nettles."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They are children of fools, yes, children of wicked men."],[2,"They were flogged out of the land."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow I have become their song."],[2,"Yes, I am a byword to them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They abhor me, they stand aloof from me,"],[2,"and don\u2019t hesitate to spit in my face."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has untied his cord, and afflicted me;"],[2,"and they have thrown off restraint before me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"On my right hand rise the rabble."],[2,"They thrust aside my feet."],[2,"They cast their ways of destruction up against me."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They mar my path."],[2,"They promote my destruction"],[2,"without anyone\u2019s help."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"As through a wide breach they come."],[2,"They roll themselves in amid the ruin."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Terrors have turned on me."],[2,"They chase my honor as the wind."],[2,"My welfare has passed away as a cloud."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow my soul is poured out within me."],[2,"Days of affliction have taken hold of me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"In the night season my bones are pierced in me,"],[2,"and the pains that gnaw me take no rest."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"My garment is disfigured by great force."],[2,"It binds me about as the collar of my tunic."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He has cast me into the mire."],[2,"I have become like dust and ashes."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"I cry to you, and you do not answer me."],[2,"I stand up, and you gaze at me."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"You have turned to be cruel to me."],[2,"With the might of your hand you persecute me."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"You lift me up to the wind, and drive me with it."],[2,"You dissolve me in the storm."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"For I know that you will bring me to death,"],[2,"to the house appointed for all living."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHowever doesn\u2019t one stretch out a hand in his fall?"],[2,"Or in his calamity therefore cry for help?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Didn\u2019t I weep for him who was in trouble?"],[2,"Wasn\u2019t my soul grieved for the needy?"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"When I looked for good, then evil came."],[2,"When I waited for light, darkness came."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"My heart is troubled, and doesn\u2019t rest."],[2,"Days of affliction have come on me."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"I go mourning without the sun."],[2,"I stand up in the assembly, and cry for help."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"I am a brother to jackals,"],[2,"and a companion to ostriches."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"My skin grows black and peels from me."],[2,"My bones are burned with heat."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore my harp has turned to mourning,"],[2,"and my pipe into the voice of those who weep."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI made a covenant with my eyes;"],[2,"how then should I look lustfully at a young woman?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For what is the portion from God above,"],[2,"and the heritage from the Almighty on high?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Is it not calamity to the unrighteous,"],[2,"and disaster to the workers of iniquity?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Doesn\u2019t he see my ways,"],[2,"and count all my steps?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf I have walked with falsehood,"],[2,"and my foot has hurried to deceit"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"(let me be weighed in an even balance,"],[2,"that God may know my integrity);"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"if my step has turned out of the way,"],[2,"if my heart walked after my eyes,"],[2,"if any defilement has stuck to my hands,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"then let me sow, and let another eat."],[2,"Yes, let the produce of my field be rooted out."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf my heart has been enticed to a woman,"],[2,"and I have laid wait at my neighbor\u2019s door,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"then let my wife grind for another,"],[2,"and let others sleep with her."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For that would be a heinous crime."],[2,"Yes, it would be an iniquity to be punished by the judges,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"for it is a fire that consumes to destruction,"],[2,"and would root out all my increase."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf I have despised the cause of my male servant"],[2,"or of my female servant,"],[2,"when they contended with me,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"what then will I do when God rises up?"],[2,"When he visits, what will I answer him?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Didn\u2019t he who made me in the womb make him?"],[2,"Didn\u2019t one fashion us in the womb?"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf I have withheld the poor from their desire,"],[2,"or have caused the eyes of the widow to fail,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"or have eaten my morsel alone,"],[2,"and the fatherless has not eaten of it"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"(no, from my youth he grew up with me as with a father,"],[2,"I have guided her from my mother\u2019s womb);"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"if I have seen any perish for want of clothing,"],[2,"or that the needy had no covering;"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"if his heart hasn\u2019t blessed me,"],[2,"if he hasn\u2019t been warmed with my sheep\u2019s fleece;"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"if I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless,"],[2,"because I saw my help in the gate;"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"then let my shoulder fall from the shoulder blade,"],[2,"and my arm be broken from the bone."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"For calamity from God is a terror to me."],[2,"Because of his majesty, I can do nothing."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf I have made gold my hope,"],[2,"and have said to the fine gold, \u2018You are my confidence;\u2019"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"If I have rejoiced because my wealth was great,"],[2,"and because my hand had gotten much;"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"if I have seen the sun when it shined,"],[2,"or the moon moving in splendor,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"and my heart has been secretly enticed,"],[2,"and my hand threw a kiss from my mouth;"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"this also would be an iniquity to be punished by the judges,"],[2,"for I would have denied the God who is above."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf I have rejoiced at the destruction of him who hated me,"],[2,"or lifted up myself when evil found him"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"(I have certainly not allowed my mouth to sin"],[2,"by asking his life with a curse);"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"if the men of my tent have not said,"],[2,"\u2018Who can find one who has not been filled with his meat?\u2019"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"(the foreigner has not camped in the street,"],[2,"but I have opened my doors to the traveler);"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"if like Adam I have covered my transgressions,"],[2,"by hiding my iniquity in my heart,"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"because I feared the great multitude,"],[2,"and the contempt of families terrified me,"],[2,"so that I kept silence, and didn\u2019t go out of the door\u2014"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"oh that I had one to hear me!"],[2,"Behold, here is my signature! Let the Almighty answer me!"],[2,"Let the accuser write my indictment!"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely I would carry it on my shoulder,"],[2,"and I would bind it to me as a crown."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"I would declare to him the number of my steps."],[2,"I would go near to him like a prince."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"If my land cries out against me,"],[2,"and its furrows weep together;"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"if I have eaten its fruits without money,"],[2,"or have caused its owners to lose their life,"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"let briers grow instead of wheat,"],[2,"and stinkweed instead of barley.\u201d"],[0,"The words of Job are ended."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"So these three men ceased to answer Job, because he was righteous in his own eyes."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then the wrath of Elihu the son of Barachel, the Buzite, of the family of Ram, was kindled against Job. His wrath was kindled because he justified himself rather than God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Also his wrath was kindled against his three friends, because they had found no answer, and yet had condemned Job."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now Elihu had waited to speak to Job, because they were older than he."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When Elihu saw that there was no answer in the mouth of these three men, his wrath was kindled."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Elihu the son of Barachel the Buzite answered,"],[1,"\u201cI am young, and you are very old."],[2,"Therefore I held back, and didn\u2019t dare show you my opinion."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u2018Days should speak,"],[2,"and multitude of years should teach wisdom.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But there is a spirit in man,"],[2,"and the Spirit of the Almighty gives them understanding."]],f:["or, breath"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"It is not the great who are wise,"],[2,"nor the aged who understand justice."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I said, \u2018Listen to me;"],[2,"I also will show my opinion.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I waited for your words,"],[2,"and I listened for your reasoning,"],[2,"while you searched out what to say."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, I gave you my full attention,"],[2,"but there was no one who convinced Job,"],[2,"or who answered his words, among you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Beware lest you say, \u2018We have found wisdom."],[2,"God may refute him, not man;\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"for he has not directed his words against me;"],[2,"neither will I answer him with your speeches."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThey are amazed. They answer no more."],[2,"They don\u2019t have a word to say."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall I wait, because they don\u2019t speak,"],[2,"because they stand still, and answer no more?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I also will answer my part,"],[2,"and I also will show my opinion."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For I am full of words."],[2,"The spirit within me constrains me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, my breast is as wine which has no vent;"],[2,"like new wineskins it is ready to burst."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"I will speak, that I may be refreshed."],[2,"I will open my lips and answer."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Please don\u2019t let me respect any man\u2019s person,"],[2,"neither will I give flattering titles to any man."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For I don\u2019t know how to give flattering titles,"],[2,"or else my Maker would soon take me away."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHowever, Job, please hear my speech,"],[2,"and listen to all my words."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"See now, I have opened my mouth."],[2,"My tongue has spoken in my mouth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My words will utter the uprightness of my heart."],[2,"That which my lips know they will speak sincerely."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The Spirit of God has made me,"],[2,"and the breath of the Almighty gives me life."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"If you can, answer me."],[2,"Set your words in order before me, and stand up."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I am toward God even as you are."],[2,"I am also formed out of the clay."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, my terror will not make you afraid,"],[2,"neither will my pressure be heavy on you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSurely you have spoken in my hearing,"],[2,"I have heard the voice of your words, saying,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018I am clean, without disobedience."],[2,"I am innocent, neither is there iniquity in me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he finds occasions against me."],[2,"He counts me for his enemy."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He puts my feet in the stocks."],[2,"He marks all my paths.\u2019"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I will answer you. In this you are not just,"],[2,"for God is greater than man."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you strive against him,"],[2,"because he doesn\u2019t give account of any of his matters?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For God speaks once,"],[2,"yes twice, though man pays no attention."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"In a dream, in a vision of the night,"],[2,"when deep sleep falls on men,"],[2,"in slumbering on the bed,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"then he opens the ears of men,"],[2,"and seals their instruction,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"that he may withdraw man from his purpose,"],[2,"and hide pride from man."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He keeps back his soul from the pit,"],[2,"and his life from perishing by the sword."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHe is chastened also with pain on his bed,"],[2,"with continual strife in his bones,"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"so that his life abhors bread,"],[2,"and his soul dainty food."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"His flesh is so consumed away that it can\u2019t be seen."],[2,"His bones that were not seen stick out."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, his soul draws near to the pit,"],[2,"and his life to the destroyers."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf there is beside him an angel,"],[2,"an interpreter, one among a thousand,"],[2,"to show to man what is right for him,"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"then God is gracious to him, and says,"],[2,"\u2018Deliver him from going down to the pit,"],[2,"I have found a ransom.\u2019"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"His flesh will be fresher than a child\u2019s."],[2,"He returns to the days of his youth."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"He prays to God, and he is favorable to him,"],[2,"so that he sees his face with joy."],[2,"He restores to man his righteousness."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"He sings before men, and says,"],[2,"\u2018I have sinned, and perverted that which was right,"],[2,"and it didn\u2019t profit me."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"He has redeemed my soul from going into the pit."],[2,"My life will see the light.\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, God does all these things,"],[2,"twice, yes three times, with a man,"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"to bring back his soul from the pit,"],[2,"that he may be enlightened with the light of the living."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Mark well, Job, and listen to me."],[2,"Hold your peace, and I will speak."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"If you have anything to say, answer me."],[2,"Speak, for I desire to justify you."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"If not, listen to me."],[2,"Hold your peace, and I will teach you wisdom.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Elihu answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear my words, you wise men."],[2,"Give ear to me, you who have knowledge."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the ear tries words,"],[2,"as the palate tastes food."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Let us choose for us that which is right."],[2,"Let us know among ourselves what is good."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For Job has said, \u2018I am righteous,"],[2,"God has taken away my right."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Notwithstanding my right I am considered a liar."],[2,"My wound is incurable, though I am without disobedience.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"What man is like Job,"],[2,"who drinks scorn like water,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"who goes in company with the workers of iniquity,"],[2,"and walks with wicked men?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has said, \u2018It profits a man nothing"],[2,"that he should delight himself with God.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore listen to me, you men of understanding:"],[2,"far be it from God, that he should do wickedness,"],[2,"from the Almighty, that he should commit iniquity."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For the work of a man he will give to him,"],[2,"and cause every man to find according to his ways."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes surely, God will not do wickedly,"],[2,"neither will the Almighty pervert justice."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Who put him in charge of the earth?"],[2,"Or who has appointed him over the whole world?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"If he set his heart on himself,"],[2,"if he gathered to himself his spirit and his breath,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"all flesh would perish together,"],[2,"and man would turn again to dust."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf now you have understanding, hear this."],[2,"Listen to the voice of my words."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Should even one who hates justice govern?"],[2,"Will you condemn him who is righteous and mighty,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"who says to a king, \u2018Vile!\u2019"],[2,"or to nobles, \u2018Wicked!\u2019?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He doesn\u2019t respect the persons of princes,"],[2,"nor respect the rich more than the poor,"],[2,"for they all are the work of his hands."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"In a moment they die, even at midnight."],[2,"The people are shaken and pass away."],[2,"The mighty are taken away without a hand."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor his eyes are on the ways of a man."],[2,"He sees all his goings."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no darkness, nor thick gloom,"],[2,"where the workers of iniquity may hide themselves."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"For he doesn\u2019t need to consider a man further,"],[2,"that he should go before God in judgment."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"He breaks mighty men in pieces in ways past finding out,"],[2,"and sets others in their place."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore he takes knowledge of their works."],[2,"He overturns them in the night, so that they are destroyed."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"He strikes them as wicked men"],[2,"in the open sight of others;"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"because they turned away from following him,"],[2,"and wouldn\u2019t pay attention to any of his ways,"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"so that they caused the cry of the poor to come to him."],[2,"He heard the cry of the afflicted."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"When he gives quietness, who then can condemn?"],[2,"When he hides his face, who then can see him?"],[2,"He is over a nation or a man alike,"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"that the godless man may not reign,"],[2,"that there be no one to ensnare the people."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor has any said to God,"],[2,"\u2018I am guilty, but I will not offend any more."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Teach me that which I don\u2019t see."],[2,"If I have done iniquity, I will do it no more\u2019?"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall his recompense be as you desire, that you refuse it?"],[2,"For you must choose, and not I."],[2,"Therefore speak what you know."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Men of understanding will tell me,"],[2,"yes, every wise man who hears me:"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018Job speaks without knowledge."],[2,"His words are without wisdom.\u2019"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"I wish that Job were tried to the end,"],[2,"because of his answering like wicked men."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"For he adds rebellion to his sin."],[2,"He claps his hands among us,"],[2,"and multiplies his words against God.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Elihu answered,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDo you think this to be your right,"],[2,"or do you say, \u2018My righteousness is more than God\u2019s,\u2019"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"that you ask, \u2018What advantage will it be to you?"],[2,"What profit will I have, more than if I had sinned?\u2019"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will answer you,"],[2,"and your companions with you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Look to the skies, and see."],[2,"See the skies, which are higher than you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"If you have sinned, what effect do you have against him?"],[2,"If your transgressions are multiplied, what do you do to him?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"If you are righteous, what do you give him?"],[2,"Or what does he receive from your hand?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Your wickedness may hurt a man as you are,"],[2,"and your righteousness may profit a son of man."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBy reason of the multitude of oppressions they cry out."],[2,"They cry for help by reason of the arm of the mighty."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But no one says, \u2018Where is God my Maker,"],[2,"who gives songs in the night,"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"who teaches us more than the animals of the earth,"],[2,"and makes us wiser than the birds of the sky?\u2019"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"There they cry, but no one answers,"],[2,"because of the pride of evil men."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely God will not hear an empty cry,"],[2,"neither will the Almighty regard it."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"How much less when you say you don\u2019t see him."],[2,"The cause is before him, and you wait for him!"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"But now, because he has not visited in his anger,"],[2,"neither does he greatly regard arrogance,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"therefore Job opens his mouth with empty talk,"],[2,"and he multiplies words without knowledge.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Elihu also continued, and said,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBear with me a little, and I will show you;"],[2,"for I still have something to say on God\u2019s behalf."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I will get my knowledge from afar,"],[2,"and will ascribe righteousness to my Maker."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For truly my words are not false."],[2,"One who is perfect in knowledge is with you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, God is mighty, and doesn\u2019t despise anyone."],[2,"He is mighty in strength of understanding."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He doesn\u2019t preserve the life of the wicked,"],[2,"but gives justice to the afflicted."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He doesn\u2019t withdraw his eyes from the righteous,"],[2,"but with kings on the throne,"],[2,"he sets them forever, and they are exalted."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"If they are bound in fetters,"],[2,"and are taken in the cords of afflictions,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"then he shows them their work,"],[2,"and their transgressions, that they have behaved themselves proudly."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He also opens their ears to instruction,"],[2,"and commands that they return from iniquity."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"If they listen and serve him,"],[2,"they will spend their days in prosperity,"],[2,"and their years in pleasures."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"But if they don\u2019t listen, they will perish by the sword;"],[2,"they will die without knowledge."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut those who are godless in heart lay up anger."],[2,"They don\u2019t cry for help when he binds them."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They die in youth."],[2,"Their life perishes among the unclean."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He delivers the afflicted by their affliction,"],[2,"and opens their ear in oppression."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, he would have allured you out of distress,"],[2,"into a wide place, where there is no restriction."],[2,"That which is set on your table would be full of fatness."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut you are full of the judgment of the wicked."],[2,"Judgment and justice take hold of you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let riches entice you to wrath,"],[2,"neither let the great size of a bribe turn you aside."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Would your wealth sustain you in distress,"],[2,"or all the might of your strength?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t desire the night,"],[2,"when people are cut off in their place."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Take heed, don\u2019t regard iniquity;"],[2,"for you have chosen this rather than affliction."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, God is exalted in his power."],[2,"Who is a teacher like him?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has prescribed his way for him?"],[2,"Or who can say, \u2018You have committed unrighteousness\u2019?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cRemember that you magnify his work,"],[2,"about which men have sung."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"All men have looked on it."],[2,"Man sees it afar off."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, God is great, and we don\u2019t know him."],[2,"The number of his years is unsearchable."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"For he draws up the drops of water,"],[2,"which distill in rain from his vapor,"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"which the skies pour down"],[2,"and which drop on man abundantly."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Indeed, can anyone understand the spreading of the clouds"],[2,"and the thunderings of his pavilion?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he spreads his light around him."],[2,"He covers the bottom of the sea."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"For by these he judges the people."],[2,"He gives food in abundance."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"He covers his hands with the lightning,"],[2,"and commands it to strike the mark."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Its noise tells about him,"],[2,"and the livestock also, concerning the storm that comes up."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYes, at this my heart trembles,"],[2,"and is moved out of its place."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, oh, hear the noise of his voice,"],[2,"the sound that goes out of his mouth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He sends it out under the whole sky,"],[2,"and his lightning to the ends of the earth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"After it a voice roars."],[2,"He thunders with the voice of his majesty."],[2,"He doesn\u2019t hold back anything when his voice is heard."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"God thunders marvelously with his voice."],[2,"He does great things, which we can\u2019t comprehend."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For he says to the snow, \u2018Fall on the earth,\u2019"],[2,"likewise to the shower of rain,"],[2,"and to the showers of his mighty rain."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He seals up the hand of every man,"],[2,"that all men whom he has made may know it."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the animals take cover,"],[2,"and remain in their dens."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Out of its room comes the storm,"],[2,"and cold out of the north."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"By the breath of God, ice is given,"],[2,"and the width of the waters is frozen."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, he loads the thick cloud with moisture."],[2,"He spreads abroad the cloud of his lightning."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"It is turned around by his guidance,"],[2,"that they may do whatever he commands them"],[2,"on the surface of the habitable world,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"whether it is for correction, or for his land,"],[2,"or for loving kindness, that he causes it to come."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cListen to this, Job."],[2,"Stand still, and consider the wondrous works of God."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you know how God controls them,"],[2,"and causes the lightning of his cloud to shine?"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you know the workings of the clouds,"],[2,"the wondrous works of him who is perfect in knowledge?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"You whose clothing is warm"],[2,"when the earth is still by reason of the south wind?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Can you, with him, spread out the sky,"],[2,"which is strong as a cast metal mirror?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Teach us what we will tell him,"],[2,"for we can\u2019t make our case by reason of darkness."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Will it be told him that I would speak?"],[2,"Or should a man wish that he were swallowed up?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Now men don\u2019t see the light which is bright in the skies,"],[2,"but the wind passes, and clears them."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Out of the north comes golden splendor."],[2,"With God is awesome majesty."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"We can\u2019t reach the Almighty."],[2,"He is exalted in power."],[2,"In justice and great righteousness, he will not oppress."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore men revere him."],[2,"He doesn\u2019t regard any who are wise of heart.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWho is this who darkens counsel"],[2,"by words without knowledge?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Brace yourself like a man,"],[2,"for I will question you, then you answer me!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhere were you when I laid the foundations of the earth?"],[2,"Declare, if you have understanding."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Who determined its measures, if you know?"],[2,"Or who stretched the line on it?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"What were its foundations fastened on?"],[2,"Or who laid its cornerstone,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"when the morning stars sang together,"],[2,"and all the sons of God shouted for joy?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOr who shut up the sea with doors,"],[2,"when it broke out of the womb,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"when I made clouds its garment,"],[2,"and wrapped it in thick darkness,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"marked out for it my bound,"],[2,"set bars and doors,"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"and said, \u2018You may come here, but no further."],[2,"Your proud waves shall be stopped here\u2019?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHave you commanded the morning in your days,"],[2,"and caused the dawn to know its place,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"that it might take hold of the ends of the earth,"],[2,"and shake the wicked out of it?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"It is changed as clay under the seal,"],[2,"and presented as a garment."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"From the wicked, their light is withheld."],[2,"The high arm is broken."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHave you entered into the springs of the sea?"],[2,"Or have you walked in the recesses of the deep?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Have the gates of death been revealed to you?"],[2,"Or have you seen the gates of the shadow of death?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Have you comprehended the earth in its width?"],[2,"Declare, if you know it all."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhat is the way to the dwelling of light?"],[2,"As for darkness, where is its place,"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"that you should take it to its bound,"],[2,"that you should discern the paths to its house?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely you know, for you were born then,"],[2,"and the number of your days is great!"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Have you entered the storehouses of the snow,"],[2,"or have you seen the storehouses of the hail,"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"which I have reserved against the time of trouble,"],[2,"against the day of battle and war?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"By what way is the lightning distributed,"],[2,"or the east wind scattered on the earth?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has cut a channel for the flood water,"],[2,"or the path for the thunderstorm,"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"to cause it to rain on a land where there is no man,"],[2,"on the wilderness, in which there is no man,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"to satisfy the waste and desolate ground,"],[2,"to cause the tender grass to grow?"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Does the rain have a father?"],[2,"Or who fathers the drops of dew?"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Whose womb did the ice come out of?"],[2,"Who has given birth to the gray frost of the sky?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The waters become hard like stone,"],[2,"when the surface of the deep is frozen."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan you bind the cluster of the Pleiades,"],[2,"or loosen the cords of Orion?"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Can you lead the constellations out in their season?"],[2,"Or can you guide the Bear with her cubs?"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you know the laws of the heavens?"],[2,"Can you establish its dominion over the earth?"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan you lift up your voice to the clouds,"],[2,"that abundance of waters may cover you?"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"Can you send out lightnings, that they may go?"],[2,"Do they report to you, \u2018Here we are\u2019?"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has put wisdom in the inward parts?"],[2,"Or who has given understanding to the mind?"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can count the clouds by wisdom?"],[2,"Or who can pour out the containers of the sky,"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"when the dust runs into a mass,"],[2,"and the clods of earth stick together?"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan you hunt the prey for the lioness,"],[2,"or satisfy the appetite of the young lions,"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"when they crouch in their dens,"],[2,"and lie in wait in the thicket?"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"Who provides for the raven his prey,"],[2,"when his young ones cry to God,"],[2,"and wander for lack of food?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDo you know the time when the mountain goats give birth?"],[2,"Do you watch when the doe bears fawns?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Can you count the months that they fulfill?"],[2,"Or do you know the time when they give birth?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They bow themselves. They bear their young."],[2,"They end their labor pains."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Their young ones become strong."],[2,"They grow up in the open field."],[2,"They go out, and don\u2019t return again."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWho has set the wild donkey free?"],[2,"Or who has loosened the bonds of the swift donkey,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"whose home I have made the wilderness,"],[2,"and the salt land his dwelling place?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He scorns the tumult of the city,"],[2,"neither does he hear the shouting of the driver."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The range of the mountains is his pasture."],[2,"He searches after every green thing."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWill the wild ox be content to serve you?"],[2,"Or will he stay by your feeding trough?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Can you hold the wild ox in the furrow with his harness?"],[2,"Or will he till the valleys after you?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you trust him, because his strength is great?"],[2,"Or will you leave to him your labor?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you confide in him, that he will bring home your seed,"],[2,"and gather the grain of your threshing floor?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe wings of the ostrich wave proudly,"],[2,"but are they the feathers and plumage of love?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For she leaves her eggs on the earth,"],[2,"warms them in the dust,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"and forgets that the foot may crush them,"],[2,"or that the wild animal may trample them."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"She deals harshly with her young ones, as if they were not hers."],[2,"Though her labor is in vain, she is without fear,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"because God has deprived her of wisdom,"],[2,"neither has he imparted to her understanding."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"When she lifts up herself on high,"],[2,"she scorns the horse and his rider."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHave you given the horse might?"],[2,"Have you clothed his neck with a quivering mane?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Have you made him to leap as a locust?"],[2,"The glory of his snorting is awesome."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He paws in the valley, and rejoices in his strength."],[2,"He goes out to meet the armed men."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"He mocks at fear, and is not dismayed,"],[2,"neither does he turn back from the sword."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The quiver rattles against him,"],[2,"the flashing spear and the javelin."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"He eats up the ground with fierceness and rage,"],[2,"neither does he stand still at the sound of the trumpet."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"As often as the trumpet sounds he snorts, \u2018Aha!\u2019"],[2,"He smells the battle afar off,"],[2,"the thunder of the captains, and the shouting."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIs it by your wisdom that the hawk soars,"],[2,"and stretches her wings toward the south?"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Is it at your command that the eagle mounts up,"],[2,"and makes his nest on high?"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"On the cliff he dwells and makes his home,"],[2,"on the point of the cliff and the stronghold."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"From there he spies out the prey."],[2,"His eyes see it afar off."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"His young ones also suck up blood."],[2,"Where the slain are, there he is.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD answered Job,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cShall he who argues contend with the Almighty?"],[2,"He who argues with God, let him answer it.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered the LORD,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I am of small account. What will I answer you?"],[2,"I lay my hand on my mouth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I have spoken once, and I will not answer;"],[2,"Yes, twice, but I will proceed no further.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind:"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow brace yourself like a man."],[2,"I will question you, and you will answer me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you even annul my judgment?"],[2,"Will you condemn me, that you may be justified?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Or do you have an arm like God?"],[2,"Can you thunder with a voice like him?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow deck yourself with excellency and dignity."],[2,"Array yourself with honor and majesty."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Pour out the fury of your anger."],[2,"Look at everyone who is proud, and bring him low."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Look at everyone who is proud, and humble him."],[2,"Crush the wicked in their place."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Hide them in the dust together."],[2,"Bind their faces in the hidden place."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I will also admit to you"],[2,"that your own right hand can save you."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSee now behemoth, which I made as well as you."],[2,"He eats grass as an ox."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Look now, his strength is in his thighs."],[2,"His force is in the muscles of his belly."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He moves his tail like a cedar."],[2,"The sinews of his thighs are knit together."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"His bones are like tubes of bronze."],[2,"His limbs are like bars of iron."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He is the chief of the ways of God."],[2,"He who made him gives him his sword."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely the mountains produce food for him,"],[2,"where all the animals of the field play."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He lies under the lotus trees,"],[2,"in the covert of the reed, and the marsh."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The lotuses cover him with their shade."],[2,"The willows of the brook surround him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, if a river overflows, he doesn\u2019t tremble."],[2,"He is confident, though the Jordan swells even to his mouth."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall any take him when he is on the watch,"],[2,"or pierce through his nose with a snare?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan you draw out Leviathan with a fish hook,"],[2,"or press down his tongue with a cord?"]],f:["Leviathan is a name for a crocodile or similar creature."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Can you put a rope into his nose,"],[2,"or pierce his jaw through with a hook?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Will he make many petitions to you,"],[2,"or will he speak soft words to you?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Will he make a covenant with you,"],[2,"that you should take him for a servant forever?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you play with him as with a bird?"],[2,"Or will you bind him for your girls?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Will traders barter for him?"],[2,"Will they part him among the merchants?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Can you fill his skin with barbed irons,"],[2,"or his head with fish spears?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Lay your hand on him."],[2,"Remember the battle, and do so no more."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the hope of him is in vain."],[2,"Won\u2019t one be cast down even at the sight of him?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"None is so fierce that he dare stir him up."],[2,"Who then is he who can stand before me?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has first given to me, that I should repay him?"],[2,"Everything under the heavens is mine."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will not keep silence concerning his limbs,"],[2,"nor his mighty strength, nor his goodly frame."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can strip off his outer garment?"],[2,"Who will come within his jaws?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can open the doors of his face?"],[2,"Around his teeth is terror."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Strong scales are his pride,"],[2,"shut up together with a close seal."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"One is so near to another,"],[2,"that no air can come between them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"They are joined to one another."],[2,"They stick together, so that they can\u2019t be pulled apart."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"His sneezing flashes out light."],[2,"His eyes are like the eyelids of the morning."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Out of his mouth go burning torches."],[2,"Sparks of fire leap out."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Out of his nostrils a smoke goes,"],[2,"as of a boiling pot over a fire of reeds."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"His breath kindles coals."],[2,"A flame goes out of his mouth."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"There is strength in his neck."],[2,"Terror dances before him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The flakes of his flesh are joined together."],[2,"They are firm on him."],[2,"They can\u2019t be moved."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"His heart is as firm as a stone,"],[2,"yes, firm as the lower millstone."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"When he raises himself up, the mighty are afraid."],[2,"They retreat before his thrashing."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"If one attacks him with the sword, it can\u2019t prevail;"],[2,"nor the spear, the dart, nor the pointed shaft."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"He counts iron as straw,"],[2,"and bronze as rotten wood."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"The arrow can\u2019t make him flee."],[2,"Sling stones are like chaff to him."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Clubs are counted as stubble."],[2,"He laughs at the rushing of the javelin."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"His undersides are like sharp potsherds,"],[2,"leaving a trail in the mud like a threshing sledge."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes the deep to boil like a pot."],[2,"He makes the sea like a pot of ointment."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes a path shine after him."],[2,"One would think the deep had white hair."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"On earth there is not his equal,"],[2,"that is made without fear."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"He sees everything that is high."],[2,"He is king over all the sons of pride.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Job answered the LORD:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI know that you can do all things,"],[2,"and that no purpose of yours can be restrained."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You asked, \u2018Who is this who hides counsel without knowledge?\u2019"],[2,"therefore I have uttered that which I didn\u2019t understand,"],[2,"things too wonderful for me, which I didn\u2019t know."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You said, \u2018Listen, now, and I will speak;"],[2,"I will question you, and you will answer me.\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I had heard of you by the hearing of the ear,"],[2,"but now my eye sees you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I abhor myself,"],[2,"and repent in dust and ashes.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"It was so, that after the LORD had spoken these words to Job, the LORD said to Eliphaz the Temanite, \u201cMy wrath is kindled against you, and against your two friends; for you have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my servant Job has."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now therefore, take to yourselves seven bulls and seven rams, and go to my servant Job, and offer up for yourselves a burnt offering; and my servant Job shall pray for you, for I will accept him, that I not deal with you according to your folly. For you have not spoken of me the thing that is right, as my servant Job has.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"So Eliphaz the Temanite and Bildad the Shuhite and Zophar the Naamathite went and did what the LORD commanded them, and the LORD accepted Job."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD restored Job\u2019s prosperity when he prayed for his friends. The LORD gave Job twice as much as he had before."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then all his brothers, all his sisters, and all those who had been of his acquaintance before, came to him and ate bread with him in his house. They comforted him, and consoled him concerning all the evil that the LORD had brought on him. Everyone also gave him a piece of money, and everyone a ring of gold."]],f:["literally, kesitah, a unit of money, probably silver"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So the LORD blessed the latter end of Job more than his beginning. He had fourteen thousand sheep, six thousand camels, one thousand yoke of oxen, and a thousand female donkeys."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He had also seven sons and three daughters."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He called the name of the first, Jemimah; and the name of the second, Keziah; and the name of the third, Keren Happuch."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"In all the land were no women found so beautiful as the daughters of Job. Their father gave them an inheritance among their brothers."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"After this Job lived one hundred forty years, and saw his sons, and his sons\u2019 sons, to four generations."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So Job died, being old and full of days."]]}]]}},1289,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,h,a,s,r){a.exports={book:"Ps",name:"Psalms",chapters:[[{v:1,h:["BOOK 1"],p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man who doesn\u2019t walk in the counsel of the wicked,"],[2,"nor stand on the path of sinners,"],[2,"nor sit in the seat of scoffers;"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"but his delight is in the LORD\u2019s law."],[2,"On his law he meditates day and night."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He will be like a tree planted by the streams of water,"],[2,"that produces its fruit in its season,"],[2,"whose leaf also does not wither."],[2,"Whatever he does shall prosper."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked are not so,"],[2,"but are like the chaff which the wind drives away."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the wicked shall not stand in the judgment,"],[2,"nor sinners in the congregation of the righteous."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD knows the way of the righteous,"],[2,"but the way of the wicked shall perish."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do the nations rage,"],[2,"and the peoples plot a vain thing?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The kings of the earth take a stand,"],[2,"and the rulers take counsel together,"],[2,"against the LORD, and against his Anointed, saying,"]],f:["The word \u201cAnointed\u201d is the same as the word for \u201cMessiah\u201d or \u201cChrist\u201d"]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLet\u2019s break their bonds apart,"],[2,"and cast their cords from us.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He who sits in the heavens will laugh."],[2,"The Lord will have them in derision."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Then he will speak to them in his anger,"],[2,"and terrify them in his wrath:"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYet I have set my King on my holy hill of Zion.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"I will tell of the decree:"],[1,"The LORD said to me, \u201cYou are my son."],[2,"Today I have become your father."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Ask of me, and I will give the nations for your inheritance,"],[2,"the uttermost parts of the earth for your possession."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You shall break them with a rod of iron."],[2,"You shall dash them in pieces like a potter\u2019s vessel.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Now therefore be wise, you kings."],[2,"Be instructed, you judges of the earth."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Serve the LORD with fear,"],[2,"and rejoice with trembling."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Give sincere homage to the Son, lest he be angry, and you perish on the way,"],[2,"for his wrath will soon be kindled."],[2,"Blessed are all those who take refuge in him."]],f:["or, Kiss the son"]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David, when he fled from Absalom his son."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, how my adversaries have increased!"],[2,"Many are those who rise up against me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Many there are who say of my soul,"],[2,"\u201cThere is no help for him in God.\u201d Selah."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, LORD, are a shield around me,"],[2,"my glory, and the one who lifts up my head."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I cry to the LORD with my voice,"],[2,"and he answers me out of his holy hill. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I laid myself down and slept."],[2,"I awakened, for the LORD sustains me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I will not be afraid of tens of thousands of people"],[2,"who have set themselves against me on every side."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, LORD!"],[2,"Save me, my God!"],[1,"For you have struck all of my enemies on the cheek bone."],[2,"You have broken the teeth of the wicked."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Salvation belongs to the LORD."],[2,"May your blessing be on your people. Selah."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Answer me when I call, God of my righteousness."],[2,"Give me relief from my distress."],[2,"Have mercy on me, and hear my prayer."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You sons of men, how long shall my glory be turned into dishonor?"],[2,"Will you love vanity and seek after falsehood? Selah."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"But know that the LORD has set apart for himself him who is godly;"],[2,"The LORD will hear when I call to him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Stand in awe, and don\u2019t sin."],[2,"Search your own heart on your bed, and be still. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Offer the sacrifices of righteousness."],[2,"Put your trust in the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Many say, \u201cWho will show us any good?\u201d"],[2,"LORD, let the light of your face shine on us."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You have put gladness in my heart,"],[2,"more than when their grain and their new wine are increased."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"In peace I will both lay myself down and sleep,"],[2,"for you alone, LORD, make me live in safety."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician, with the flutes. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Give ear to my words, LORD."],[2,"Consider my meditation."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen to the voice of my cry, my King and my God,"],[2,"for I pray to you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, in the morning you will hear my voice."],[2,"In the morning I will lay my requests before you, and will watch expectantly."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are not a God who has pleasure in wickedness."],[2,"Evil can\u2019t live with you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The arrogant will not stand in your sight."],[2,"You hate all workers of iniquity."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You will destroy those who speak lies."],[2,"The LORD abhors the bloodthirsty and deceitful man."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, in the abundance of your loving kindness I will come into your house."],[2,"I will bow toward your holy temple in reverence of you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Lead me, LORD, in your righteousness because of my enemies."],[2,"Make your way straight before my face."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For there is no faithfulness in their mouth."],[2,"Their heart is destruction."],[2,"Their throat is an open tomb."],[2,"They flatter with their tongue."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Hold them guilty, God."],[2,"Let them fall by their own counsels."],[1,"Thrust them out in the multitude of their transgressions,"],[2,"for they have rebelled against you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"But let all those who take refuge in you rejoice."],[2,"Let them always shout for joy, because you defend them."],[1,"Let them also who love your name be joyful in you."]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"For you will bless the righteous."],[1,"LORD, you will surround him with favor as with a shield."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician; on stringed instruments, upon the eight-stringed lyre. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, don\u2019t rebuke me in your anger,"],[2,"neither discipline me in your wrath."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Have mercy on me, LORD, for I am faint."],[2,"LORD, heal me, for my bones are troubled."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul is also in great anguish."],[2,"But you, LORD\u2014how long?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Return, LORD. Deliver my soul,"],[2,"and save me for your loving kindness\u2019 sake."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For in death there is no memory of you."],[2,"In Sheol, who shall give you thanks?"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I am weary with my groaning."],[2,"Every night I flood my bed."],[2,"I drench my couch with my tears."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"My eye wastes away because of grief."],[2,"It grows old because of all my adversaries."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity,"],[2,"for the LORD has heard the voice of my weeping."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has heard my supplication."],[2,"The LORD accepts my prayer."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"May all my enemies be ashamed and dismayed."],[2,"They shall turn back, they shall be disgraced suddenly."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A meditation by David, which he sang to the LORD, concerning the words of Cush, the Benjamite."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, my God, I take refuge in you."],[2,"Save me from all those who pursue me, and deliver me,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"lest they tear apart my soul like a lion,"],[2,"ripping it in pieces, while there is no one to deliver."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, my God, if I have done this,"],[2,"if there is iniquity in my hands,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"if I have rewarded evil to him who was at peace with me"],[2,"(yes, I have plundered him who without cause was my adversary),"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"let the enemy pursue my soul, and overtake it;"],[1,"yes, let him tread my life down to the earth,"],[2,"and lay my glory in the dust. Selah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, LORD, in your anger."],[2,"Lift up yourself against the rage of my adversaries."],[1,"Awake for me. You have commanded judgment."]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"Let the congregation of the peoples surround you."],[2,"Rule over them on high."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD administers judgment to the peoples."],[2,"Judge me, LORD, according to my righteousness,"],[2,"and to my integrity that is in me."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end,"],[2,"but establish the righteous;"],[2,"their minds and hearts are searched by the righteous God."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"My shield is with God,"],[2,"who saves the upright in heart."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"God is a righteous judge,"],[2,"yes, a God who has indignation every day."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"If a man doesn\u2019t repent, he will sharpen his sword;"],[2,"he has bent and strung his bow."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He has also prepared for himself the instruments of death."],[2,"He makes ready his flaming arrows."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he travails with iniquity."],[2,"Yes, he has conceived mischief,"],[2,"and brought out falsehood."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He has dug a hole,"],[2,"and has fallen into the pit which he made."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The trouble he causes shall return to his own head."],[2,"His violence shall come down on the crown of his own head."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give thanks to the LORD according to his righteousness,"],[2,"and will sing praise to the name of the LORD Most High."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician; on an instrument of Gath. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, our Lord, how majestic is your name in all the earth!"],[2,"You have set your glory above the heavens!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"From the lips of babes and infants you have established strength,"],[2,"because of your adversaries, that you might silence the enemy and the avenger."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"When I consider your heavens, the work of your fingers,"],[2,"the moon and the stars, which you have ordained,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"what is man, that you think of him?"],[2,"What is the son of man, that you care for him?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have made him a little lower than the angels,"],[2,"and crowned him with glory and honor."]],f:["Hebrew: Elohim. The word Elohim, used here, usually means \u201cGod\u201d, but can also mean \u201cgods\u201d, \u201cprinces\u201d, or \u201cangels\u201d. The Septuagint reads \u201cangels\u201d here. See also the quote from the Septuagint in Hebrews 2:7."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You make him ruler over the works of your hands."],[2,"You have put all things under his feet:"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"All sheep and cattle,"],[2,"yes, and the animals of the field,"]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"the birds of the sky, the fish of the sea,"],[2,"and whatever passes through the paths of the seas."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, our Lord,"],[2,"how majestic is your name in all the earth!"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. Set to \u201cThe Death of the Son.\u201d A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will give thanks to the LORD with my whole heart."],[2,"I will tell of all your marvelous works."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will be glad and rejoice in you."],[2,"I will sing praise to your name, O Most High."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"When my enemies turn back,"],[2,"they stumble and perish in your presence."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have maintained my just cause."],[2,"You sit on the throne judging righteously."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You have rebuked the nations."],[2,"You have destroyed the wicked."],[2,"You have blotted out their name forever and ever."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The enemy is overtaken by endless ruin."],[2,"The very memory of the cities which you have overthrown has perished."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But the LORD reigns forever."],[2,"He has prepared his throne for judgment."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He will judge the world in righteousness."],[2,"He will administer judgment to the peoples in uprightness."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will also be a high tower for the oppressed;"],[2,"a high tower in times of trouble."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who know your name will put their trust in you,"],[2,"for you, LORD, have not forsaken those who seek you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing praises to the LORD, who dwells in Zion,"],[2,"and declare among the people what he has done."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For he who avenges blood remembers them."],[2,"He doesn\u2019t forget the cry of the afflicted."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Have mercy on me, LORD."],[2,"See my affliction by those who hate me,"],[1,"and lift me up from the gates of death,"]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"that I may show all of your praise."],[2,"I will rejoice in your salvation in the gates of the daughter of Zion."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The nations have sunk down in the pit that they made."],[2,"In the net which they hid, their own foot is taken."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has made himself known."],[2,"He has executed judgment."],[2,"The wicked is snared by the work of his own hands. Meditation. Selah."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked shall be turned back to Sheol,"],[2,"even all the nations that forget God."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For the needy shall not always be forgotten,"],[2,"nor the hope of the poor perish forever."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, LORD! Don\u2019t let man prevail."],[2,"Let the nations be judged in your sight."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Put them in fear, LORD."],[2,"Let the nations know that they are only men. Selah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you stand far off, LORD?"],[2,"Why do you hide yourself in times of trouble?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"In arrogance, the wicked hunt down the weak."],[2,"They are caught in the schemes that they devise."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the wicked boasts of his heart\u2019s cravings."],[2,"He blesses the greedy and condemns the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked, in the pride of his face,"],[2,"has no room in his thoughts for God."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"His ways are prosperous at all times."],[2,"He is arrogant, and your laws are far from his sight."],[1,"As for all his adversaries, he sneers at them."]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"He says in his heart, \u201cI shall not be shaken."],[2,"For generations I shall have no trouble.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"His mouth is full of cursing, deceit, and oppression."],[2,"Under his tongue is mischief and iniquity."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He lies in wait near the villages."],[2,"From ambushes, he murders the innocent."],[1,"His eyes are secretly set against the helpless."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He lurks in secret as a lion in his ambush."],[2,"He lies in wait to catch the helpless."],[2,"He catches the helpless when he draws him in his net."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The helpless are crushed."],[2,"They collapse."],[2,"They fall under his strength."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He says in his heart, \u201cGod has forgotten."],[2,"He hides his face."],[2,"He will never see it.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, LORD!"],[2,"God, lift up your hand!"],[2,"Don\u2019t forget the helpless."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Why does the wicked person condemn God,"],[2,"and say in his heart, \u201cGod won\u2019t call me into account\u201d?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"But you do see trouble and grief."],[2,"You consider it to take it into your hand."],[2,"You help the victim and the fatherless."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Break the arm of the wicked."],[2,"As for the evil man, seek out his wickedness until you find none."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is King forever and ever!"],[2,"The nations will perish out of his land."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you have heard the desire of the humble."],[2,"You will prepare their heart."],[2,"You will cause your ear to hear,"]]},{v:18,l:[[2,"to judge the fatherless and the oppressed,"],[2,"that man who is of the earth may terrify no more."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"In the LORD, I take refuge."],[2,"How can you say to my soul, \u201cFlee as a bird to your mountain\u201d?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, the wicked bend their bows."],[2,"They set their arrows on the strings,"],[2,"that they may shoot in darkness at the upright in heart."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"If the foundations are destroyed,"],[2,"what can the righteous do?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is in his holy temple."],[2,"The LORD is on his throne in heaven."],[1,"His eyes observe."],[2,"His eyes examine the children of men."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD examines the righteous,"],[2,"but his soul hates the wicked and him who loves violence."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"On the wicked he will rain blazing coals;"],[2,"fire, sulfur, and scorching wind shall be the portion of their cup."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD is righteous."],[2,"He loves righteousness."],[2,"The upright shall see his face."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician; upon an eight-stringed lyre. A Psalm of David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Help, LORD; for the godly man ceases."],[2,"For the faithful fail from among the children of men."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Everyone lies to his neighbor."],[2,"They speak with flattering lips, and with a double heart."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"May the LORD cut off all flattering lips,"],[2,"and the tongue that boasts,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"who have said, \u201cWith our tongue we will prevail."],[2,"Our lips are our own."],[2,"Who is lord over us?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBecause of the oppression of the weak and because of the groaning of the needy,"],[2,"I will now arise,\u201d says the LORD;"],[1,"\u201cI will set him in safety from those who malign him.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s words are flawless words,"],[2,"as silver refined in a clay furnace, purified seven times."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You will keep them, LORD."],[2,"You will preserve them from this generation forever."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked walk on every side,"],[2,"when what is vile is exalted among the sons of men."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"How long, LORD?"],[2,"Will you forget me forever?"],[2,"How long will you hide your face from me?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"How long shall I take counsel in my soul,"],[2,"having sorrow in my heart every day?"],[2,"How long shall my enemy triumph over me?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, and answer me, LORD, my God."],[2,"Give light to my eyes, lest I sleep in death;"]]},{v:4,l:[[2,"lest my enemy say, \u201cI have prevailed against him;\u201d"],[2,"lest my adversaries rejoice when I fall."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"But I trust in your loving kindness."],[2,"My heart rejoices in your salvation."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I will sing to the LORD,"],[2,"because he has been good to me."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The fool has said in his heart, \u201cThere is no God.\u201d"],[2,"They are corrupt."],[2,"They have done abominable deeds."],[2,"There is no one who does good."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD looked down from heaven on the children of men,"],[2,"to see if there were any who understood,"],[2,"who sought after God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They have all gone aside."],[2,"They have together become corrupt."],[2,"There is no one who does good, no, not one."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Have all the workers of iniquity no knowledge,"],[2,"who eat up my people as they eat bread,"],[2,"and don\u2019t call on the LORD?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"There they were in great fear,"],[2,"for God is in the generation of the righteous."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You frustrate the plan of the poor,"],[2,"because the LORD is his refuge."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that the salvation of Israel would come out of Zion!"],[2,"When the LORD restores the fortunes of his people,"],[2,"then Jacob shall rejoice, and Israel shall be glad."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, who shall dwell in your sanctuary?"],[2,"Who shall live on your holy hill?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He who walks blamelessly and does what is right,"],[2,"and speaks truth in his heart;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"he who doesn\u2019t slander with his tongue,"],[2,"nor does evil to his friend,"],[2,"nor casts slurs against his fellow man;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"in whose eyes a vile man is despised,"],[2,"but who honors those who fear the LORD;"],[2,"he who keeps an oath even when it hurts, and doesn\u2019t change;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"he who doesn\u2019t lend out his money for usury,"],[2,"nor take a bribe against the innocent."],[1,"He who does these things shall never be shaken."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Poem by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Preserve me, God, for I take refuge in you."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul, you have said to the LORD, \u201cYou are my Lord."],[2,"Apart from you I have no good thing.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"As for the saints who are on the earth,"],[2,"they are the excellent ones in whom is all my delight."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Their sorrows shall be multiplied who give gifts to another god."],[2,"Their drink offerings of blood I will not offer,"],[2,"nor take their names on my lips."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD assigned my portion and my cup."],[2,"You made my lot secure."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The lines have fallen to me in pleasant places."],[2,"Yes, I have a good inheritance."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bless the LORD, who has given me counsel."],[2,"Yes, my heart instructs me in the night seasons."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I have set the LORD always before me."],[2,"Because he is at my right hand, I shall not be moved."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore my heart is glad, and my tongue rejoices."],[2,"My body shall also dwell in safety."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For you will not leave my soul in Sheol,"],[2,"neither will you allow your holy one to see corruption."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You will show me the path of life."],[2,"In your presence is fullness of joy."],[1,"In your right hand there are pleasures forever more."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Prayer by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, LORD, my righteous plea."],[2,"Give ear to my prayer that doesn\u2019t go out of deceitful lips."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my sentence come out of your presence."],[2,"Let your eyes look on equity."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You have proved my heart."],[2,"You have visited me in the night."],[2,"You have tried me, and found nothing."],[2,"I have resolved that my mouth shall not disobey."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"As for the deeds of men, by the word of your lips,"],[2,"I have kept myself from the ways of the violent."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My steps have held fast to your paths."],[2,"My feet have not slipped."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I have called on you, for you will answer me, God."],[2,"Turn your ear to me."],[2,"Hear my speech."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Show your marvelous loving kindness,"],[2,"you who save those who take refuge by your right hand from their enemies."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Keep me as the apple of your eye."],[2,"Hide me under the shadow of your wings,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"from the wicked who oppress me,"],[2,"my deadly enemies, who surround me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They close up their callous hearts."],[2,"With their mouth they speak proudly."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They have now surrounded us in our steps."],[2,"They set their eyes to cast us down to the earth."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"He is like a lion that is greedy of his prey,"],[2,"as it were a young lion lurking in secret places."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, LORD, confront him."],[2,"Cast him down."],[1,"Deliver my soul from the wicked by your sword,"]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"from men by your hand, LORD,"],[2,"from men of the world, whose portion is in this life."],[1,"You fill the belly of your cherished ones."],[2,"Your sons have plenty,"],[2,"and they store up wealth for their children."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"As for me, I shall see your face in righteousness."],[2,"I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with seeing your form."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. By David the servant of the LORD, who spoke to the LORD the words of this song in the day that the LORD delivered him from the hand of all his enemies, and from the hand of Saul. He said,"],p:1,l:[[1,"I love you, LORD, my strength."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is my rock, my fortress, and my deliverer;"],[2,"my God, my rock, in whom I take refuge;"],[2,"my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I call on the LORD, who is worthy to be praised;"],[2,"and I am saved from my enemies."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The cords of death surrounded me."],[2,"The floods of ungodliness made me afraid."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The cords of Sheol were around me."],[2,"The snares of death came on me."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"In my distress I called on the LORD,"],[2,"and cried to my God."],[1,"He heard my voice out of his temple."],[2,"My cry before him came into his ears."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the earth shook and trembled."],[2,"The foundations also of the mountains quaked and were shaken,"],[2,"because he was angry."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Smoke went out of his nostrils."],[2,"Consuming fire came out of his mouth."],[2,"Coals were kindled by it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He bowed the heavens also, and came down."],[2,"Thick darkness was under his feet."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He rode on a cherub, and flew."],[2,"Yes, he soared on the wings of the wind."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He made darkness his hiding place, his pavilion around him,"],[2,"darkness of waters, thick clouds of the skies."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"At the brightness before him his thick clouds passed,"],[2,"hailstones and coals of fire."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD also thundered in the sky."],[2,"The Most High uttered his voice:"],[2,"hailstones and coals of fire."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent out his arrows, and scattered them."],[2,"He routed them with great lightning bolts."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the channels of waters appeared."],[2,"The foundations of the world were laid bare at your rebuke, LORD,"],[2,"at the blast of the breath of your nostrils."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent from on high."],[2,"He took me."],[2,"He drew me out of many waters."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He delivered me from my strong enemy,"],[2,"from those who hated me; for they were too mighty for me."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"They came on me in the day of my calamity,"],[2,"but the LORD was my support."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought me out also into a large place."],[2,"He delivered me, because he delighted in me."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness."],[2,"According to the cleanness of my hands, he has recompensed me."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For I have kept the ways of the LORD,"],[2,"and have not wickedly departed from my God."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For all his ordinances were before me."],[2,"I didn\u2019t put away his statutes from me."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I was also blameless with him."],[2,"I kept myself from my iniquity."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD has rewarded me according to my righteousness,"],[2,"according to the cleanness of my hands in his eyesight."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"With the merciful you will show yourself merciful."],[2,"With the perfect man, you will show yourself perfect."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"With the pure, you will show yourself pure."],[2,"With the crooked you will show yourself shrewd."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"For you will save the afflicted people,"],[2,"but the arrogant eyes you will bring down."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"For you will light my lamp, LORD."],[2,"My God will light up my darkness."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"For by you, I advance through a troop."],[2,"By my God, I leap over a wall."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"As for God, his way is perfect."],[2,"The LORD\u2019s word is tried."],[2,"He is a shield to all those who take refuge in him."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"For who is God, except the LORD?"],[2,"Who is a rock, besides our God,"]]},{v:32,l:[[2,"the God who arms me with strength, and makes my way perfect?"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes my feet like deer\u2019s feet,"],[2,"and sets me on my high places."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"He teaches my hands to war,"],[2,"so that my arms bend a bow of bronze."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"You have also given me the shield of your salvation."],[2,"Your right hand sustains me."],[2,"Your gentleness has made me great."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"You have enlarged my steps under me,"],[2,"My feet have not slipped."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"I will pursue my enemies, and overtake them."],[2,"I won\u2019t turn away until they are consumed."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"I will strike them through, so that they will not be able to rise."],[2,"They shall fall under my feet."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have armed me with strength to the battle."],[2,"You have subdued under me those who rose up against me."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"You have also made my enemies turn their backs to me,"],[2,"that I might cut off those who hate me."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"They cried, but there was no one to save;"],[2,"even to the LORD, but he didn\u2019t answer them."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I beat them small as the dust before the wind."],[2,"I cast them out as the mire of the streets."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"You have delivered me from the strivings of the people."],[2,"You have made me the head of the nations."],[1,"A people whom I have not known shall serve me."]]},{v:44,l:[[2,"As soon as they hear of me they shall obey me."],[2,"The foreigners shall submit themselves to me."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"The foreigners shall fade away,"],[2,"and shall come trembling out of their strongholds."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD lives! Blessed be my rock."],[2,"Exalted be the God of my salvation,"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"even the God who executes vengeance for me,"],[2,"and subdues peoples under me."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[1,"He rescues me from my enemies."],[2,"Yes, you lift me up above those who rise up against me."],[2,"You deliver me from the violent man."]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will give thanks to you, LORD, among the nations,"],[2,"and will sing praises to your name."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"He gives great deliverance to his king,"],[2,"and shows loving kindness to his anointed,"],[2,"to David and to his offspring, forever more."]],f:["or, seed"]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The heavens declare the glory of God."],[2,"The expanse shows his handiwork."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Day after day they pour out speech,"],[2,"and night after night they display knowledge."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no speech nor language"],[2,"where their voice is not heard."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Their voice has gone out through all the earth,"],[2,"their words to the end of the world."],[1,"In them he has set a tent for the sun,"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"which is as a bridegroom coming out of his room,"],[2,"like a strong man rejoicing to run his course."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"His going out is from the end of the heavens,"],[2,"his circuit to its ends."],[2,"There is nothing hidden from its heat."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s law is perfect, restoring the soul."],[2,"The LORD\u2019s covenant is sure, making wise the simple."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s precepts are right, rejoicing the heart."],[2,"The LORD\u2019s commandment is pure, enlightening the eyes."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD is clean, enduring forever."],[2,"The LORD\u2019s ordinances are true, and righteous altogether."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They are more to be desired than gold, yes, than much fine gold,"],[2,"sweeter also than honey and the extract of the honeycomb."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Moreover your servant is warned by them."],[2,"In keeping them there is great reward."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can discern his errors?"],[2,"Forgive me from hidden errors."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Keep back your servant also from presumptuous sins."],[2,"Let them not have dominion over me."],[1,"Then I will be upright."],[2,"I will be blameless and innocent of great transgression."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart"],[2,"be acceptable in your sight,"],[2,"LORD, my rock, and my redeemer."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"May the LORD answer you in the day of trouble."],[2,"May the name of the God of Jacob set you up on high,"]]},{v:2,l:[[2,"send you help from the sanctuary,"],[2,"grant you support from Zion,"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"remember all your offerings,"],[2,"and accept your burned sacrifice. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"May he grant you your heart\u2019s desire,"],[2,"and fulfill all your counsel."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"We will triumph in your salvation."],[2,"In the name of our God, we will set up our banners."],[2,"May the LORD grant all your requests."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Now I know that the LORD saves his anointed."],[2,"He will answer him from his holy heaven,"],[2,"with the saving strength of his right hand."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Some trust in chariots, and some in horses,"],[2,"but we trust in the name of the LORD our God."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They are bowed down and fallen,"],[2,"but we rise up, and stand upright."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Save, LORD!"],[2,"Let the King answer us when we call!"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The king rejoices in your strength, LORD!"],[2,"How greatly he rejoices in your salvation!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You have given him his heart\u2019s desire,"],[2,"and have not withheld the request of his lips. Selah."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For you meet him with the blessings of goodness."],[2,"You set a crown of fine gold on his head."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He asked life of you and you gave it to him,"],[2,"even length of days forever and ever."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"His glory is great in your salvation."],[2,"You lay honor and majesty on him."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For you make him most blessed forever."],[2,"You make him glad with joy in your presence."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For the king trusts in the LORD."],[2,"Through the loving kindness of the Most High, he shall not be moved."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Your hand will find out all of your enemies."],[2,"Your right hand will find out those who hate you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You will make them as a fiery furnace in the time of your anger."],[2,"The LORD will swallow them up in his wrath."],[2,"The fire shall devour them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You will destroy their descendants from the earth,"],[2,"their posterity from among the children of men."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For they intended evil against you."],[2,"They plotted evil against you which cannot succeed."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For you will make them turn their back,"],[2,"when you aim drawn bows at their face."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Be exalted, LORD, in your strength,"],[2,"so we will sing and praise your power."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician; set to \u201cThe Doe of the Morning.\u201d A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?"],[2,"Why are you so far from helping me, and from the words of my groaning?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My God, I cry in the daytime, but you don\u2019t answer;"],[2,"in the night season, and am not silent."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"But you are holy,"],[2,"you who inhabit the praises of Israel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Our fathers trusted in you."],[2,"They trusted, and you delivered them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They cried to you, and were delivered."],[2,"They trusted in you, and were not disappointed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"But I am a worm, and no man;"],[2,"a reproach of men, and despised by the people."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"All those who see me mock me."],[2,"They insult me with their lips. They shake their heads, saying,"]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"\u201cHe trusts in the LORD."],[2,"Let him deliver him."],[2,"Let him rescue him, since he delights in him.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"But you brought me out of the womb."],[2,"You made me trust while at my mother\u2019s breasts."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I was thrown on you from my mother\u2019s womb."],[2,"You are my God since my mother bore me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be far from me, for trouble is near."],[2,"For there is no one to help."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Many bulls have surrounded me."],[2,"Strong bulls of Bashan have encircled me."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They open their mouths wide against me,"],[2,"lions tearing prey and roaring."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I am poured out like water."],[2,"All my bones are out of joint."],[1,"My heart is like wax."],[2,"It is melted within me."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"My strength is dried up like a potsherd."],[2,"My tongue sticks to the roof of my mouth."],[1,"You have brought me into the dust of death."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For dogs have surrounded me."],[2,"A company of evildoers have enclosed me."],[2,"They have pierced my hands and feet."]],f:["So Dead Sea Scrolls. Masoretic Text reads, \u201cLike a lion, they pin my hands and feet.\u201d"]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I can count all of my bones."],[1,"They look and stare at me."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"They divide my garments among them."],[2,"They cast lots for my clothing."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"But don\u2019t be far off, LORD."],[2,"You are my help. Hurry to help me!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver my soul from the sword,"],[2,"my precious life from the power of the dog."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Save me from the lion\u2019s mouth!"],[2,"Yes, you have rescued me from the horns of the wild oxen."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"I will declare your name to my brothers."],[2,"Among the assembly, I will praise you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"You who fear the LORD, praise him!"],[2,"All you descendants of Jacob, glorify him!"],[2,"Stand in awe of him, all you descendants of Israel!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has not despised nor abhorred the affliction of the afflicted,"],[2,"neither has he hidden his face from him;"],[2,"but when he cried to him, he heard."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"My praise of you comes in the great assembly."],[2,"I will pay my vows before those who fear him."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The humble shall eat and be satisfied."],[2,"They shall praise the LORD who seek after him."],[2,"Let your hearts live forever."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"All the ends of the earth shall remember and turn to the LORD."],[2,"All the relatives of the nations shall worship before you."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"For the kingdom is the LORD\u2019s."],[2,"He is the ruler over the nations."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"All the rich ones of the earth shall eat and worship."],[2,"All those who go down to the dust shall bow before him,"],[2,"even he who can\u2019t keep his soul alive."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Posterity shall serve him."],[2,"Future generations shall be told about the Lord."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall come and shall declare his righteousness to a people that shall be born,"],[2,"for he has done it."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is my shepherd;"],[2,"I shall lack nothing."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes me lie down in green pastures."],[2,"He leads me beside still waters."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He restores my soul."],[2,"He guides me in the paths of righteousness for his name\u2019s sake."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,"],[2,"I will fear no evil, for you are with me."],[1,"Your rod and your staff,"],[2,"they comfort me."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You prepare a table before me"],[2,"in the presence of my enemies."],[1,"You anoint my head with oil."],[2,"My cup runs over."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely goodness and loving kindness shall follow me all the days of my life,"],[2,"and I will dwell in the LORD\u2019s house forever."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The earth is the LORD\u2019s, with its fullness;"],[2,"the world, and those who dwell in it."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has founded it on the seas,"],[2,"and established it on the floods."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Who may ascend to the LORD\u2019s hill?"],[2,"Who may stand in his holy place?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He who has clean hands and a pure heart;"],[2,"who has not lifted up his soul to falsehood,"],[2,"and has not sworn deceitfully."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He shall receive a blessing from the LORD,"],[2,"righteousness from the God of his salvation."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"This is the generation of those who seek Him,"],[2,"who seek your face\u2014even Jacob. Selah."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your heads, you gates!"],[2,"Be lifted up, you everlasting doors,"],[2,"and the King of glory will come in."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is the King of glory?"],[2,"The LORD strong and mighty,"],[2,"the LORD mighty in battle."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your heads, you gates;"],[2,"yes, lift them up, you everlasting doors,"],[2,"and the King of glory will come in."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is this King of glory?"],[2,"The LORD of Armies is the King of glory! Selah."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"To you, LORD, I lift up my soul."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My God, I have trusted in you."],[2,"Don\u2019t let me be shamed."],[2,"Don\u2019t let my enemies triumph over me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, no one who waits for you will be shamed."],[2,"They will be shamed who deal treacherously without cause."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Show me your ways, LORD."],[2,"Teach me your paths."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Guide me in your truth, and teach me,"],[2,"for you are the God of my salvation."],[2,"I wait for you all day long."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, remember your tender mercies and your loving kindness,"],[2,"for they are from old times."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t remember the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions."],[2,"Remember me according to your loving kindness,"],[2,"for your goodness\u2019 sake, LORD."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Good and upright is the LORD,"],[2,"therefore he will instruct sinners in the way."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He will guide the humble in justice."],[2,"He will teach the humble his way."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"All the paths of the LORD are loving kindness and truth"],[2,"to such as keep his covenant and his testimonies."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For your name\u2019s sake, LORD,"],[2,"pardon my iniquity, for it is great."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"What man is he who fears the LORD?"],[2,"He shall instruct him in the way that he shall choose."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"His soul will dwell at ease."],[2,"His offspring will inherit the land."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The friendship of the LORD is with those who fear him."],[2,"He will show them his covenant."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"My eyes are ever on the LORD,"],[2,"for he will pluck my feet out of the net."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn to me, and have mercy on me,"],[2,"for I am desolate and afflicted."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The troubles of my heart are enlarged."],[2,"Oh bring me out of my distresses."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Consider my affliction and my travail."],[2,"Forgive all my sins."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Consider my enemies, for they are many."],[2,"They hate me with cruel hatred."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh keep my soul, and deliver me."],[2,"Let me not be disappointed, for I take refuge in you."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Let integrity and uprightness preserve me,"],[2,"for I wait for you."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"God, redeem Israel"],[2,"out of all his troubles."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Judge me, LORD, for I have walked in my integrity."],[2,"I have trusted also in the LORD without wavering."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Examine me, LORD, and prove me."],[2,"Try my heart and my mind."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For your loving kindness is before my eyes."],[2,"I have walked in your truth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I have not sat with deceitful men,"],[2,"neither will I go in with hypocrites."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I hate the assembly of evildoers,"],[2,"and will not sit with the wicked."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I will wash my hands in innocence,"],[2,"so I will go about your altar, LORD,"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"that I may make the voice of thanksgiving to be heard"],[2,"and tell of all your wondrous deeds."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, I love the habitation of your house,"],[2,"the place where your glory dwells."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t gather my soul with sinners,"],[2,"nor my life with bloodthirsty men"]]},{v:10,l:[[2,"in whose hands is wickedness;"],[2,"their right hand is full of bribes."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, I will walk in my integrity."],[2,"Redeem me, and be merciful to me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"My foot stands in an even place."],[2,"In the congregations I will bless the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is my light and my salvation."],[2,"Whom shall I fear?"],[1,"The LORD is the strength of my life."],[2,"Of whom shall I be afraid?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"When evildoers came at me to eat up my flesh,"],[2,"even my adversaries and my foes, they stumbled and fell."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Though an army should encamp against me,"],[2,"my heart shall not fear."],[1,"Though war should rise against me,"],[2,"even then I will be confident."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"One thing I have asked of the LORD, that I will seek after:"],[2,"that I may dwell in the LORD\u2019s house all the days of my life,"],[2,"to see the LORD\u2019s beauty,"],[2,"and to inquire in his temple."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For in the day of trouble, he will keep me secretly in his pavilion."],[2,"In the secret place of his tabernacle, he will hide me."],[2,"He will lift me up on a rock."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Now my head will be lifted up above my enemies around me."],[1,"I will offer sacrifices of joy in his tent."],[2,"I will sing, yes, I will sing praises to the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, LORD, when I cry with my voice."],[2,"Have mercy also on me, and answer me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"When you said, \u201cSeek my face,\u201d"],[2,"my heart said to you, \u201cI will seek your face, LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t hide your face from me."],[2,"Don\u2019t put your servant away in anger."],[1,"You have been my help."],[2,"Don\u2019t abandon me,"],[2,"neither forsake me, God of my salvation."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"When my father and my mother forsake me,"],[2,"then the LORD will take me up."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Teach me your way, LORD."],[2,"Lead me in a straight path, because of my enemies."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t deliver me over to the desire of my adversaries,"],[2,"for false witnesses have risen up against me,"],[2,"such as breathe out cruelty."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I am still confident of this:"],[2,"I will see the goodness of the LORD in the land of the living."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Wait for the LORD."],[2,"Be strong, and let your heart take courage."],[1,"Yes, wait for the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"To you, LORD, I call."],[2,"My rock, don\u2019t be deaf to me,"],[2,"lest, if you are silent to me,"],[2,"I would become like those who go down into the pit."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear the voice of my petitions, when I cry to you,"],[2,"when I lift up my hands toward your Most Holy Place."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t draw me away with the wicked,"],[2,"with the workers of iniquity who speak peace with their neighbors,"],[2,"but mischief is in their hearts."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Give them according to their work, and according to the wickedness of their doings."],[2,"Give them according to the operation of their hands."],[2,"Bring back on them what they deserve."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Because they don\u2019t respect the works of the LORD,"],[2,"nor the operation of his hands,"],[2,"he will break them down and not build them up."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD,"],[2,"because he has heard the voice of my petitions."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is my strength and my shield."],[2,"My heart has trusted in him, and I am helped."],[1,"Therefore my heart greatly rejoices."],[2,"With my song I will thank him."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is their strength."],[2,"He is a stronghold of salvation to his anointed."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Save your people,"],[2,"and bless your inheritance."],[1,"Be their shepherd also,"],[2,"and bear them up forever."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Ascribe to the LORD, you sons of the mighty,"],[2,"ascribe to the LORD glory and strength."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his name."],[2,"Worship the LORD in holy array."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s voice is on the waters."],[2,"The God of glory thunders, even the LORD on many waters."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s voice is powerful."],[2,"The LORD\u2019s voice is full of majesty."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s voice breaks the cedars."],[2,"Yes, the LORD breaks in pieces the cedars of Lebanon."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes them also to skip like a calf;"],[2,"Lebanon and Sirion like a young, wild ox."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s voice strikes with flashes of lightning."]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"The LORD\u2019s voice shakes the wilderness."],[2,"The LORD shakes the wilderness of Kadesh."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s voice makes the deer calve,"],[2,"and strips the forests bare."],[2,"In his temple everything says, \u201cGlory!\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD sat enthroned at the Flood."],[2,"Yes, the LORD sits as King forever."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will give strength to his people."],[2,"The LORD will bless his people with peace."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm. A Song for the Dedication of the Temple. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will extol you, LORD, for you have raised me up,"],[2,"and have not made my foes to rejoice over me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD my God, I cried to you,"],[2,"and you have healed me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you have brought up my soul from Sheol."],[2,"You have kept me alive, that I should not go down to the pit."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing praise to the LORD, you saints of his."],[2,"Give thanks to his holy name."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For his anger is but for a moment."],[2,"His favor is for a lifetime."],[1,"Weeping may stay for the night,"],[2,"but joy comes in the morning."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"As for me, I said in my prosperity,"],[2,"\u201cI shall never be moved.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You, LORD, when you favored me, made my mountain stand strong;"],[2,"but when you hid your face, I was troubled."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I cried to you, LORD."],[2,"I made supplication to the Lord:"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhat profit is there in my destruction, if I go down to the pit?"],[2,"Shall the dust praise you?"],[2,"Shall it declare your truth?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, LORD, and have mercy on me."],[2,"LORD, be my helper.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You have turned my mourning into dancing for me."],[2,"You have removed my sackcloth, and clothed me with gladness,"]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"to the end that my heart may sing praise to you, and not be silent."],[1,"LORD my God, I will give thanks to you forever!"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"In you, LORD, I take refuge."],[2,"Let me never be disappointed."],[2,"Deliver me in your righteousness."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Bow down your ear to me."],[2,"Deliver me speedily."],[1,"Be to me a strong rock,"],[2,"a house of defense to save me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are my rock and my fortress,"],[2,"therefore for your name\u2019s sake lead me and guide me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Pluck me out of the net that they have laid secretly for me,"],[2,"for you are my stronghold."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Into your hand I commend my spirit."],[2,"You redeem me, LORD, God of truth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I hate those who regard lying vanities,"],[2,"but I trust in the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I will be glad and rejoice in your loving kindness,"],[2,"for you have seen my affliction."],[2,"You have known my soul in adversities."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You have not shut me up into the hand of the enemy."],[2,"You have set my feet in a large place."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Have mercy on me, LORD, for I am in distress."],[2,"My eye, my soul, and my body waste away with grief."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For my life is spent with sorrow,"],[2,"my years with sighing."],[1,"My strength fails because of my iniquity."],[2,"My bones are wasted away."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Because of all my adversaries I have become utterly contemptible to my neighbors,"],[2,"a horror to my acquaintances."],[2,"Those who saw me on the street fled from me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I am forgotten from their hearts like a dead man."],[2,"I am like broken pottery."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For I have heard the slander of many, terror on every side,"],[2,"while they conspire together against me,"],[2,"they plot to take away my life."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"But I trust in you, LORD."],[2,"I said, \u201cYou are my God.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"My times are in your hand."],[2,"Deliver me from the hand of my enemies, and from those who persecute me."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Make your face to shine on your servant."],[2,"Save me in your loving kindness."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Let me not be disappointed, LORD, for I have called on you."],[2,"Let the wicked be disappointed."],[2,"Let them be silent in Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the lying lips be mute,"],[2,"which speak against the righteous insolently, with pride and contempt."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh how great is your goodness,"],[2,"which you have laid up for those who fear you,"],[2,"which you have worked for those who take refuge in you,"],[2,"before the sons of men!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"In the shelter of your presence you will hide them from the plotting of man."],[2,"You will keep them secretly in a dwelling away from the strife of tongues."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise be to the LORD,"],[2,"for he has shown me his marvelous loving kindness in a strong city."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"As for me, I said in my haste, \u201cI am cut off from before your eyes.\u201d"],[2,"Nevertheless you heard the voice of my petitions when I cried to you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh love the LORD, all you his saints!"],[2,"The LORD preserves the faithful,"],[1,"and fully recompenses him who behaves arrogantly."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Be strong, and let your heart take courage,"],[2,"all you who hope in the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David. A contemplative psalm."],p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is he whose disobedience is forgiven,"],[2,"whose sin is covered."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man to whom the LORD doesn\u2019t impute iniquity,"],[2,"in whose spirit there is no deceit."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"When I kept silence, my bones wasted away through my groaning all day long."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For day and night your hand was heavy on me."],[2,"My strength was sapped in the heat of summer. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I acknowledged my sin to you."],[2,"I didn\u2019t hide my iniquity."],[1,"I said, I will confess my transgressions to the LORD,"],[2,"and you forgave the iniquity of my sin. Selah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For this, let everyone who is godly pray to you in a time when you may be found."],[2,"Surely when the great waters overflow, they shall not reach to him."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You are my hiding place."],[2,"You will preserve me from trouble."],[2,"You will surround me with songs of deliverance. Selah."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will instruct you and teach you in the way which you shall go."],[2,"I will counsel you with my eye on you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be like the horse, or like the mule, which have no understanding,"],[2,"who are controlled by bit and bridle, or else they will not come near to you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Many sorrows come to the wicked,"],[2,"but loving kindness shall surround him who trusts in the LORD."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Be glad in the LORD, and rejoice, you righteous!"],[2,"Shout for joy, all you who are upright in heart!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Rejoice in the LORD, you righteous!"],[2,"Praise is fitting for the upright."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Give thanks to the LORD with the lyre."],[2,"Sing praises to him with the harp of ten strings."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to him a new song."],[2,"Play skillfully with a shout of joy!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD\u2019s word is right."],[2,"All his work is done in faithfulness."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He loves righteousness and justice."],[2,"The earth is full of the loving kindness of the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"By the LORD\u2019s word, the heavens were made:"],[2,"all their army by the breath of his mouth."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He gathers the waters of the sea together as a heap."],[2,"He lays up the deeps in storehouses."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let all the earth fear the LORD."],[2,"Let all the inhabitants of the world stand in awe of him."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For he spoke, and it was done."],[2,"He commanded, and it stood firm."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD brings the counsel of the nations to nothing."],[2,"He makes the thoughts of the peoples to be of no effect."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The counsel of the LORD stands fast forever,"],[2,"the thoughts of his heart to all generations."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the nation whose God is the LORD,"],[2,"the people whom he has chosen for his own inheritance."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD looks from heaven."],[2,"He sees all the sons of men."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"From the place of his habitation he looks out on all the inhabitants of the earth,"]]},{v:15,l:[[2,"he who fashions all of their hearts;"],[2,"and he considers all of their works."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no king saved by the multitude of an army."],[2,"A mighty man is not delivered by great strength."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"A horse is a vain thing for safety,"],[2,"neither does he deliver any by his great power."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the LORD\u2019s eye is on those who fear him,"],[2,"on those who hope in his loving kindness,"]]},{v:19,l:[[2,"to deliver their soul from death,"],[2,"to keep them alive in famine."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Our soul has waited for the LORD."],[2,"He is our help and our shield."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For our heart rejoices in him,"],[2,"because we have trusted in his holy name."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your loving kindness be on us, LORD,"],[2,"since we have hoped in you."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David; when he pretended to be insane before Abimelech, who drove him away, and he departed."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will bless the LORD at all times."],[2,"His praise will always be in my mouth."]],f:["Psalm 34 is an acrostic poem, with each verse starting with a letter of the alphabet (ordered from Alef to Tav)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul shall boast in the LORD."],[2,"The humble shall hear of it and be glad."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh magnify the LORD with me."],[2,"Let\u2019s exalt his name together."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I sought the LORD, and he answered me,"],[2,"and delivered me from all my fears."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They looked to him, and were radiant."],[2,"Their faces shall never be covered with shame."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"This poor man cried, and the LORD heard him,"],[2,"and saved him out of all his troubles."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s angel encamps around those who fear him,"],[2,"and delivers them."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh taste and see that the LORD is good."],[2,"Blessed is the man who takes refuge in him."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh fear the LORD, you his saints,"],[2,"for there is no lack with those who fear him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The young lions do lack, and suffer hunger,"],[2,"but those who seek the LORD shall not lack any good thing."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Come, you children, listen to me."],[2,"I will teach you the fear of the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is someone who desires life,"],[2,"and loves many days, that he may see good?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Keep your tongue from evil,"],[2,"and your lips from speaking lies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Depart from evil, and do good."],[2,"Seek peace, and pursue it."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s eyes are toward the righteous."],[2,"His ears listen to their cry."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s face is against those who do evil,"],[2,"to cut off their memory from the earth."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous cry, and the LORD hears,"],[2,"and delivers them out of all their troubles."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is near to those who have a broken heart,"],[2,"and saves those who have a crushed spirit."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Many are the afflictions of the righteous,"],[2,"but the LORD delivers him out of them all."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He protects all of his bones."],[2,"Not one of them is broken."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Evil shall kill the wicked."],[2,"Those who hate the righteous shall be condemned."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD redeems the soul of his servants."],[2,"None of those who take refuge in him shall be condemned."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Contend, LORD, with those who contend with me."],[2,"Fight against those who fight against me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Take hold of shield and buckler,"],[2,"and stand up for my help."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Brandish the spear and block those who pursue me."],[2,"Tell my soul, \u201cI am your salvation.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Let those who seek after my soul be disappointed and brought to dishonor."],[2,"Let those who plot my ruin be turned back and confounded."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be as chaff before the wind,"],[2,"the LORD\u2019s angel driving them on."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Let their way be dark and slippery,"],[2,"the LORD\u2019s angel pursuing them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For without cause they have hidden their net in a pit for me."],[2,"Without cause they have dug a pit for my soul."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let destruction come on him unawares."],[2,"Let his net that he has hidden catch himself."],[2,"Let him fall into that destruction."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul shall be joyful in the LORD."],[2,"It shall rejoice in his salvation."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"All my bones shall say, \u201cLORD, who is like you,"],[2,"who delivers the poor from him who is too strong for him;"],[2,"yes, the poor and the needy from him who robs him?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Unrighteous witnesses rise up."],[2,"They ask me about things that I don\u2019t know about."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They reward me evil for good,"],[2,"to the bereaving of my soul."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth."],[2,"I afflicted my soul with fasting."],[2,"My prayer returned into my own bosom."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I behaved myself as though it had been my friend or my brother."],[2,"I bowed down mourning, as one who mourns his mother."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"But in my adversity, they rejoiced, and gathered themselves together."],[2,"The attackers gathered themselves together against me, and I didn\u2019t know it."],[2,"They tore at me, and didn\u2019t cease."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Like the profane mockers in feasts,"],[2,"they gnashed their teeth at me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, how long will you look on?"],[2,"Rescue my soul from their destruction,"],[2,"my precious life from the lions."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give you thanks in the great assembly."],[2,"I will praise you among many people."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let those who are my enemies wrongfully rejoice over me;"],[2,"neither let those who hate me without a cause wink their eyes."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"For they don\u2019t speak peace,"],[2,"but they devise deceitful words against those who are quiet in the land."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, they opened their mouth wide against me."],[2,"They said, \u201cAha! Aha! Our eye has seen it!\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"You have seen it, LORD. Don\u2019t keep silent."],[2,"Lord, don\u2019t be far from me."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Wake up! Rise up to defend me, my God!"],[2,"My Lord, contend for me!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Vindicate me, LORD my God, according to your righteousness."],[2,"Don\u2019t let them gloat over me."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let them say in their heart, \u201cAha! That\u2019s the way we want it!\u201d"],[2,"Don\u2019t let them say, \u201cWe have swallowed him up!\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be disappointed and confounded together who rejoice at my calamity."],[2,"Let them be clothed with shame and dishonor who magnify themselves against me."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Let those who favor my righteous cause shout for joy and be glad."],[2,"Yes, let them say continually, \u201cMay the LORD be magnified,"],[2,"who has pleasure in the prosperity of his servant!\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"My tongue shall talk about your righteousness and about your praise all day long."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. By David, the servant of the LORD."],p:1,l:[[1,"A revelation is within my heart about the disobedience of the wicked:"],[2,"There is no fear of God before his eyes."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For he flatters himself in his own eyes,"],[2,"too much to detect and hate his sin."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The words of his mouth are iniquity and deceit."],[2,"He has ceased to be wise and to do good."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He plots iniquity on his bed."],[2,"He sets himself in a way that is not good."],[2,"He doesn\u2019t abhor evil."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Your loving kindness, LORD, is in the heavens."],[2,"Your faithfulness reaches to the skies."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Your righteousness is like the mountains of God."],[2,"Your judgments are like a great deep."],[2,"LORD, you preserve man and animal."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"How precious is your loving kindness, God!"],[2,"The children of men take refuge under the shadow of your wings."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall be abundantly satisfied with the abundance of your house."],[2,"You will make them drink of the river of your pleasures."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For with you is the spring of life."],[2,"In your light we will see light."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh continue your loving kindness to those who know you,"],[2,"your righteousness to the upright in heart."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let the foot of pride come against me."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the hand of the wicked drive me away."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"There the workers of iniquity are fallen."],[2,"They are thrust down, and shall not be able to rise."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t fret because of evildoers,"],[2,"neither be envious against those who work unrighteousness."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For they shall soon be cut down like the grass,"],[2,"and wither like the green herb."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Trust in the LORD, and do good."],[2,"Dwell in the land, and enjoy safe pasture."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Also delight yourself in the LORD,"],[2,"and he will give you the desires of your heart."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Commit your way to the LORD."],[2,"Trust also in him, and he will do this:"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"he will make your righteousness shine out like light,"],[2,"and your justice as the noon day sun."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Rest in the LORD, and wait patiently for him."],[2,"Don\u2019t fret because of him who prospers in his way,"],[2,"because of the man who makes wicked plots happen."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Cease from anger, and forsake wrath."],[2,"Don\u2019t fret; it leads only to evildoing."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For evildoers shall be cut off,"],[2,"but those who wait for the LORD shall inherit the land."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For yet a little while, and the wicked will be no more."],[2,"Yes, though you look for his place, he isn\u2019t there."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"But the humble shall inherit the land,"],[2,"and shall delight themselves in the abundance of peace."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked plots against the just,"],[2,"and gnashes at him with his teeth."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord will laugh at him,"],[2,"for he sees that his day is coming."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked have drawn out the sword, and have bent their bow,"],[2,"to cast down the poor and needy,"],[2,"to kill those who are upright on the path."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Their sword shall enter into their own heart."],[2,"Their bows shall be broken."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is a little that the righteous has,"],[2,"than the abundance of many wicked."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For the arms of the wicked shall be broken,"],[2,"but the LORD upholds the righteous."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD knows the days of the perfect."],[2,"Their inheritance shall be forever."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall not be disappointed in the time of evil."],[2,"In the days of famine they shall be satisfied."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"But the wicked shall perish."],[2,"The enemies of the LORD shall be like the beauty of the fields."],[2,"They will vanish\u2014"],[2,"vanish like smoke."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked borrow, and don\u2019t pay back,"],[2,"but the righteous give generously."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For such as are blessed by him shall inherit the land."],[2,"Those who are cursed by him shall be cut off."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"A man\u2019s steps are established by the LORD."],[2,"He delights in his way."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Though he stumble, he shall not fall,"],[2,"for the LORD holds him up with his hand."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"I have been young, and now am old,"],[2,"yet I have not seen the righteous forsaken,"],[2,"nor his children begging for bread."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"All day long he deals graciously, and lends."],[2,"His offspring is blessed."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Depart from evil, and do good."],[2,"Live securely forever."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD loves justice,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t forsake his saints."],[2,"They are preserved forever,"],[2,"but the children of the wicked shall be cut off."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous shall inherit the land,"],[2,"and live in it forever."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The mouth of the righteous talks of wisdom."],[2,"His tongue speaks justice."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"The law of his God is in his heart."],[2,"None of his steps shall slide."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked watch the righteous,"],[2,"and seek to kill him."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will not leave him in his hand,"],[2,"nor condemn him when he is judged."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Wait for the LORD, and keep his way,"],[2,"and he will exalt you to inherit the land."],[2,"When the wicked are cut off, you shall see it."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"I have seen the wicked in great power,"],[2,"spreading himself like a green tree in its native soil."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"But he passed away, and behold, he was not."],[2,"Yes, I sought him, but he could not be found."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"Mark the perfect man, and see the upright,"],[2,"for there is a future for the man of peace."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"As for transgressors, they shall be destroyed together."],[2,"The future of the wicked shall be cut off."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"But the salvation of the righteous is from the LORD."],[2,"He is their stronghold in the time of trouble."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD helps them and rescues them."],[2,"He rescues them from the wicked and saves them,"],[2,"because they have taken refuge in him."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David, for a memorial."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, don\u2019t rebuke me in your wrath,"],[2,"neither chasten me in your hot displeasure."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For your arrows have pierced me,"],[2,"your hand presses hard on me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no soundness in my flesh because of your indignation,"],[2,"neither is there any health in my bones because of my sin."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For my iniquities have gone over my head."],[2,"As a heavy burden, they are too heavy for me."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My wounds are loathsome and corrupt"],[2,"because of my foolishness."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I am in pain and bowed down greatly."],[2,"I go mourning all day long."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For my waist is filled with burning."],[2,"There is no soundness in my flesh."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I am faint and severely bruised."],[2,"I have groaned by reason of the anguish of my heart."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, all my desire is before you."],[2,"My groaning is not hidden from you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"My heart throbs."],[2,"My strength fails me."],[2,"As for the light of my eyes, it has also left me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"My lovers and my friends stand aloof from my plague."],[2,"My kinsmen stand far away."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They also who seek after my life lay snares."],[2,"Those who seek my hurt speak mischievous things,"],[2,"and meditate deceits all day long."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"But I, as a deaf man, don\u2019t hear."],[2,"I am as a mute man who doesn\u2019t open his mouth."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, I am as a man who doesn\u2019t hear,"],[2,"in whose mouth are no reproofs."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"For I hope in you, LORD."],[2,"You will answer, Lord my God."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For I said, \u201cDon\u2019t let them gloat over me,"],[2,"or exalt themselves over me when my foot slips.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For I am ready to fall."],[2,"My pain is continually before me."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will declare my iniquity."],[2,"I will be sorry for my sin."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"But my enemies are vigorous and many."],[2,"Those who hate me without reason are numerous."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"They who give evil for good are also adversaries to me,"],[2,"because I follow what is good."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t forsake me, LORD."],[2,"My God, don\u2019t be far from me."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Hurry to help me,"],[2,"Lord, my salvation."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. For Jeduthun. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cI will watch my ways, so that I don\u2019t sin with my tongue."],[2,"I will keep my mouth with a bridle while the wicked is before me.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I was mute with silence."],[2,"I held my peace, even from good."],[2,"My sorrow was stirred."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My heart was hot within me."],[2,"While I meditated, the fire burned."],[1,"I spoke with my tongue:"]]},{v:4,l:[[2,"\u201cLORD, show me my end,"],[2,"what is the measure of my days."],[2,"Let me know how frail I am."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you have made my days hand widths."],[2,"My lifetime is as nothing before you."],[1,"Surely every man stands as a breath.\u201d Selah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSurely every man walks like a shadow."],[2,"Surely they busy themselves in vain."],[2,"He heaps up, and doesn\u2019t know who shall gather."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Now, Lord, what do I wait for?"],[2,"My hope is in you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me from all my transgressions."],[2,"Don\u2019t make me the reproach of the foolish."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I was mute."],[2,"I didn\u2019t open my mouth,"],[2,"because you did it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Remove your scourge away from me."],[2,"I am overcome by the blow of your hand."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"When you rebuke and correct man for iniquity,"],[2,"you consume his wealth like a moth."],[1,"Surely every man is but a breath.\u201d Selah."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear my prayer, LORD, and give ear to my cry."],[2,"Don\u2019t be silent at my tears."],[1,"For I am a stranger with you,"],[2,"a foreigner, as all my fathers were."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh spare me, that I may recover strength,"],[2,"before I go away and exist no more.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I waited patiently for the LORD."],[2,"He turned to me, and heard my cry."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought me up also out of a horrible pit,"],[2,"out of the miry clay."],[1,"He set my feet on a rock,"],[2,"and gave me a firm place to stand."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He has put a new song in my mouth, even praise to our God."],[2,"Many shall see it, and fear, and shall trust in the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man who makes the LORD his trust,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t respect the proud, nor such as turn away to lies."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Many, LORD, my God, are the wonderful works which you have done,"],[2,"and your thoughts which are toward us."],[1,"They can\u2019t be declared back to you."],[2,"If I would declare and speak of them, they are more than can be counted."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Sacrifice and offering you didn\u2019t desire."],[2,"You have opened my ears."],[2,"You have not required burnt offering and sin offering."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I said, \u201cBehold, I have come."],[2,"It is written about me in the book in the scroll."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I delight to do your will, my God."],[2,"Yes, your law is within my heart.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I have proclaimed glad news of righteousness in the great assembly."],[2,"Behold, I will not seal my lips, LORD, you know."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I have not hidden your righteousness within my heart."],[2,"I have declared your faithfulness and your salvation."],[2,"I have not concealed your loving kindness and your truth from the great assembly."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t withhold your tender mercies from me, LORD."],[2,"Let your loving kindness and your truth continually preserve me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For innumerable evils have surrounded me."],[2,"My iniquities have overtaken me, so that I am not able to look up."],[1,"They are more than the hairs of my head."],[2,"My heart has failed me."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Be pleased, LORD, to deliver me."],[2,"Hurry to help me, LORD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be disappointed and confounded together who seek after my soul to destroy it."],[2,"Let them be turned backward and brought to dishonor who delight in my hurt."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be desolate by reason of their shame that tell me, \u201cAha! Aha!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Let all those who seek you rejoice and be glad in you."],[2,"Let such as love your salvation say continually, \u201cLet the LORD be exalted!\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"But I am poor and needy."],[2,"May the Lord think about me."],[1,"You are my help and my deliverer."],[2,"Don\u2019t delay, my God."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is he who considers the poor."],[2,"The LORD will deliver him in the day of evil."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will preserve him, and keep him alive."],[2,"He shall be blessed on the earth,"],[2,"and he will not surrender him to the will of his enemies."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will sustain him on his sickbed,"],[2,"and restore him from his bed of illness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cLORD, have mercy on me!"],[2,"Heal me, for I have sinned against you.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My enemies speak evil against me:"],[2,"\u201cWhen will he die, and his name perish?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"If he comes to see me, he speaks falsehood."],[2,"His heart gathers iniquity to itself."],[2,"When he goes abroad, he tells it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"All who hate me whisper together against me."],[2,"They imagine the worst for me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAn evil disease\u201d, they say, \u201chas afflicted him."],[2,"Now that he lies he shall rise up no more.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, my own familiar friend, in whom I trusted,"],[2,"who ate bread with me,"],[2,"has lifted up his heel against me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, LORD, have mercy on me, and raise me up,"],[2,"that I may repay them."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"By this I know that you delight in me,"],[2,"because my enemy doesn\u2019t triumph over me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"As for me, you uphold me in my integrity,"],[2,"and set me in your presence forever."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel,"],[2,"from everlasting and to everlasting!"],[1,"Amen and amen."]]}],[{v:1,h:["BOOK 2","For the Chief Musician. A contemplation by the sons of Korah."],p:1,l:[[1,"As the deer pants for the water brooks,"],[2,"so my soul pants after you, God."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul thirsts for God, for the living God."],[2,"When shall I come and appear before God?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My tears have been my food day and night,"],[2,"while they continually ask me, \u201cWhere is your God?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"These things I remember, and pour out my soul within me,"],[2,"how I used to go with the crowd, and led them to God\u2019s house,"],[2,"with the voice of joy and praise, a multitude keeping a holy day."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Why are you in despair, my soul?"],[2,"Why are you disturbed within me?"],[1,"Hope in God!"],[2,"For I shall still praise him for the saving help of his presence."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My God, my soul is in despair within me."],[2,"Therefore I remember you from the land of the Jordan,"],[2,"the heights of Hermon, from the hill Mizar."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Deep calls to deep at the noise of your waterfalls."],[2,"All your waves and your billows have swept over me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will command his loving kindness in the daytime."],[2,"In the night his song shall be with me:"],[2,"a prayer to the God of my life."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will ask God, my rock, \u201cWhy have you forgotten me?"],[2,"Why do I go mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"As with a sword in my bones, my adversaries reproach me,"],[2,"while they continually ask me, \u201cWhere is your God?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Why are you in despair, my soul?"],[2,"Why are you disturbed within me?"],[1,"Hope in God! For I shall still praise him,"],[2,"the saving help of my countenance, and my God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Vindicate me, God, and plead my cause against an ungodly nation."],[2,"Oh, deliver me from deceitful and wicked men."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are the God of my strength. Why have you rejected me?"],[2,"Why do I go mourning because of the oppression of the enemy?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh, send out your light and your truth."],[2,"Let them lead me."],[2,"Let them bring me to your holy hill,"],[2,"to your tents."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I will go to the altar of God,"],[2,"to God, my exceeding joy."],[1,"I will praise you on the harp, God, my God."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Why are you in despair, my soul?"],[2,"Why are you disturbed within me?"],[1,"Hope in God!"],[2,"For I shall still praise him:"],[2,"my Savior, my helper, and my God."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. By the sons of Korah. A contemplative psalm."],p:1,l:[[1,"We have heard with our ears, God;"],[2,"our fathers have told us what work you did in their days,"],[2,"in the days of old."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You drove out the nations with your hand,"],[2,"but you planted them."],[1,"You afflicted the peoples,"],[2,"but you spread them abroad."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For they didn\u2019t get the land in possession by their own sword,"],[2,"neither did their own arm save them;"],[1,"but your right hand, your arm, and the light of your face,"],[2,"because you were favorable to them."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"God, you are my King."],[2,"Command victories for Jacob!"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Through you, we will push down our adversaries."],[2,"Through your name, we will tread down those who rise up against us."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will not trust in my bow,"],[2,"neither will my sword save me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But you have saved us from our adversaries,"],[2,"and have shamed those who hate us."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"In God we have made our boast all day long."],[2,"We will give thanks to your name forever. Selah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"But now you rejected us, and brought us to dishonor,"],[2,"and don\u2019t go out with our armies."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You make us turn back from the adversary."],[2,"Those who hate us take plunder for themselves."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You have made us like sheep for food,"],[2,"and have scattered us among the nations."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You sell your people for nothing,"],[2,"and have gained nothing from their sale."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You make us a reproach to our neighbors,"],[2,"a scoffing and a derision to those who are around us."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You make us a byword among the nations,"],[2,"a shaking of the head among the peoples."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"All day long my dishonor is before me,"],[2,"and shame covers my face,"]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"at the taunt of one who reproaches and verbally abuses,"],[2,"because of the enemy and the avenger."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"All this has come on us,"],[2,"yet we haven\u2019t forgotten you."],[2,"We haven\u2019t been false to your covenant."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Our heart has not turned back,"],[2,"neither have our steps strayed from your path,"]]},{v:19,l:[[2,"though you have crushed us in the haunt of jackals,"],[2,"and covered us with the shadow of death."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"If we have forgotten the name of our God,"],[2,"or spread out our hands to a strange god,"]]},{v:21,l:[[2,"won\u2019t God search this out?"],[2,"For he knows the secrets of the heart."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, for your sake we are killed all day long."],[2,"We are regarded as sheep for the slaughter."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Wake up!"],[2,"Why do you sleep, Lord?"],[1,"Arise!"],[2,"Don\u2019t reject us forever."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you hide your face,"],[2,"and forget our affliction and our oppression?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"For our soul is bowed down to the dust."],[2,"Our body clings to the earth."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Rise up to help us."],[2,"Redeem us for your loving kindness\u2019 sake."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. Set to \u201cThe Lilies.\u201d A contemplation by the sons of Korah. A wedding song."],p:1,l:[[1,"My heart overflows with a noble theme."],[2,"I recite my verses for the king."],[2,"My tongue is like the pen of a skillful writer."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You are the most excellent of the sons of men."],[2,"Grace has anointed your lips,"],[2,"therefore God has blessed you forever."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Strap your sword on your thigh, O mighty one,"],[2,"in your splendor and your majesty."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"In your majesty ride on victoriously on behalf of truth, humility, and righteousness."],[2,"Let your right hand display awesome deeds."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Your arrows are sharp."],[2,"The nations fall under you, with arrows in the heart of the king\u2019s enemies."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Your throne, God, is forever and ever."],[2,"A scepter of equity is the scepter of your kingdom."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You have loved righteousness, and hated wickedness."],[2,"Therefore God, your God, has anointed you with the oil of gladness above your fellows."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"All your garments smell like myrrh, aloes, and cassia."],[2,"Out of ivory palaces stringed instruments have made you glad."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Kings\u2019 daughters are among your honorable women."],[2,"At your right hand the queen stands in gold of Ophir."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen, daughter, consider, and turn your ear."],[2,"Forget your own people, and also your father\u2019s house."]]},{v:11,l:[[2,"So the king will desire your beauty,"],[2,"honor him, for he is your lord."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The daughter of Tyre comes with a gift."],[2,"The rich among the people entreat your favor."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The princess inside is all glorious."],[2,"Her clothing is interwoven with gold."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"She shall be led to the king in embroidered work."],[2,"The virgins, her companions who follow her, shall be brought to you."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"With gladness and rejoicing they shall be led."],[2,"They shall enter into the king\u2019s palace."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Your sons will take the place of your fathers."],[2,"You shall make them princes in all the earth."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make your name to be remembered in all generations."],[2,"Therefore the peoples shall give you thanks forever and ever."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. By the sons of Korah. According to Alamoth."],p:1,l:[[1,"God is our refuge and strength,"],[2,"a very present help in trouble."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore we won\u2019t be afraid, though the earth changes,"],[2,"though the mountains are shaken into the heart of the seas;"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"though its waters roar and are troubled,"],[2,"though the mountains tremble with their swelling. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"There is a river, the streams of which make the city of God glad,"],[2,"the holy place of the tents of the Most High."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"God is within her. She shall not be moved."],[2,"God will help her at dawn."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The nations raged. The kingdoms were moved."],[2,"He lifted his voice and the earth melted."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD of Armies is with us."],[2,"The God of Jacob is our refuge. Selah."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Come, see the LORD\u2019s works,"],[2,"what desolations he has made on the earth."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes wars cease to the end of the earth."],[2,"He breaks the bow, and shatters the spear."],[2,"He burns the chariots in the fire."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBe still, and know that I am God."],[2,"I will be exalted among the nations."],[2,"I will be exalted on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD of Armies is with us."],[2,"The God of Jacob is our refuge. Selah."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by the sons of Korah."],p:1,l:[[1,"Oh clap your hands, all you nations."],[2,"Shout to God with the voice of triumph!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD Most High is awesome."],[2,"He is a great King over all the earth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He subdues nations under us,"],[2,"and peoples under our feet."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He chooses our inheritance for us,"],[2,"the glory of Jacob whom he loved. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"God has gone up with a shout,"],[2,"the LORD with the sound of a trumpet."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing praises to God! Sing praises!"],[2,"Sing praises to our King! Sing praises!"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For God is the King of all the earth."],[2,"Sing praises with understanding."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"God reigns over the nations."],[2,"God sits on his holy throne."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The princes of the peoples are gathered together,"],[1,"the people of the God of Abraham."],[2,"For the shields of the earth belong to God."],[2,"He is greatly exalted!"]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song. A Psalm by the sons of Korah."],p:1,l:[[1,"Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised,"],[2,"in the city of our God, in his holy mountain."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Beautiful in elevation, the joy of the whole earth,"],[2,"is Mount Zion, on the north sides,"],[2,"the city of the great King."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"God has shown himself in her citadels as a refuge."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, the kings assembled themselves,"],[2,"they passed by together."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They saw it, then they were amazed."],[2,"They were dismayed."],[2,"They hurried away."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Trembling took hold of them there,"],[2,"pain, as of a woman in travail."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"With the east wind, you break the ships of Tarshish."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"As we have heard, so we have seen,"],[2,"in the city of the LORD of Armies, in the city of our God."],[1,"God will establish it forever. Selah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"We have thought about your loving kindness, God,"],[2,"in the middle of your temple."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"As is your name, God,"],[2,"so is your praise to the ends of the earth."],[2,"Your right hand is full of righteousness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Let Mount Zion be glad!"],[2,"Let the daughters of Judah rejoice because of your judgments."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Walk about Zion, and go around her."],[2,"Number its towers."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Notice her bulwarks."],[2,"Consider her palaces,"],[2,"that you may tell it to the next generation."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For this God is our God forever and ever."],[2,"He will be our guide even to death."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by the sons of Korah."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear this, all you peoples."],[2,"Listen, all you inhabitants of the world,"]]},{v:2,l:[[2,"both low and high,"],[2,"rich and poor together."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My mouth will speak words of wisdom."],[2,"My heart will utter understanding."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will incline my ear to a proverb."],[2,"I will solve my riddle on the harp."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Why should I fear in the days of evil,"],[2,"when iniquity at my heels surrounds me?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who trust in their wealth,"],[2,"and boast in the multitude of their riches\u2014"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"none of them can by any means redeem his brother,"],[2,"nor give God a ransom for him."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For the redemption of their life is costly,"],[2,"no payment is ever enough,"]]},{v:9,l:[[2,"that he should live on forever,"],[2,"that he should not see corruption."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For he sees that wise men die;"],[2,"likewise the fool and the senseless perish,"],[2,"and leave their wealth to others."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Their inward thought is that their houses will endure forever,"],[2,"and their dwelling places to all generations."],[2,"They name their lands after themselves."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"But man, despite his riches, doesn\u2019t endure."],[2,"He is like the animals that perish."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"This is the destiny of those who are foolish,"],[2,"and of those who approve their sayings. Selah."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They are appointed as a flock for Sheol."],[2,"Death shall be their shepherd."],[1,"The upright shall have dominion over them in the morning."],[2,"Their beauty shall decay in Sheol,"],[2,"far from their mansion."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead.","Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"But God will redeem my soul from the power of Sheol,"],[2,"for he will receive me. Selah."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be afraid when a man is made rich,"],[2,"when the glory of his house is increased;"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"for when he dies he will carry nothing away."],[2,"His glory won\u2019t descend after him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Though while he lived he blessed his soul\u2014"],[2,"and men praise you when you do well for yourself\u2014"]]},{v:19,l:[[2,"he shall go to the generation of his fathers."],[2,"They shall never see the light."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"A man who has riches without understanding,"],[2,"is like the animals that perish."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"The Mighty One, God, the LORD, speaks,"],[2,"and calls the earth from sunrise to sunset."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty,"],[2,"God shines out."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Our God comes, and does not keep silent."],[2,"A fire devours before him."],[2,"It is very stormy around him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He calls to the heavens above,"],[2,"to the earth, that he may judge his people:"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGather my saints together to me,"],[2,"those who have made a covenant with me by sacrifice.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The heavens shall declare his righteousness,"],[2,"for God himself is judge. Selah."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear, my people, and I will speak."],[2,"Israel, I will testify against you."],[1,"I am God, your God."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I don\u2019t rebuke you for your sacrifices."],[2,"Your burnt offerings are continually before me."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I have no need for a bull from your stall,"],[2,"nor male goats from your pens."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For every animal of the forest is mine,"],[2,"and the livestock on a thousand hills."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I know all the birds of the mountains."],[2,"The wild animals of the field are mine."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"If I were hungry, I would not tell you,"],[2,"for the world is mine, and all that is in it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Will I eat the meat of bulls,"],[2,"or drink the blood of goats?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Offer to God the sacrifice of thanksgiving."],[2,"Pay your vows to the Most High."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Call on me in the day of trouble."],[2,"I will deliver you, and you will honor me.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"But to the wicked God says,"],[2,"\u201cWhat right do you have to declare my statutes,"],[2,"that you have taken my covenant on your lips,"]]},{v:17,l:[[2,"since you hate instruction,"],[2,"and throw my words behind you?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"When you saw a thief, you consented with him,"],[2,"and have participated with adulterers."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou give your mouth to evil."],[2,"Your tongue frames deceit."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"You sit and speak against your brother."],[2,"You slander your own mother\u2019s son."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"You have done these things, and I kept silent."],[2,"You thought that I was just like you."],[2,"I will rebuke you, and accuse you in front of your eyes."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow consider this, you who forget God,"],[2,"lest I tear you into pieces, and there be no one to deliver."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever offers the sacrifice of thanksgiving glorifies me,"],[2,"and prepares his way so that I will show God\u2019s salvation to him.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David, when Nathan the prophet came to him, after he had gone in to Bathsheba."],p:1,l:[[1,"Have mercy on me, God, according to your loving kindness."],[2,"According to the multitude of your tender mercies, blot out my transgressions."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Wash me thoroughly from my iniquity."],[2,"Cleanse me from my sin."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For I know my transgressions."],[2,"My sin is constantly before me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Against you, and you only, I have sinned,"],[2,"and done that which is evil in your sight,"],[1,"so you may be proved right when you speak,"],[2,"and justified when you judge."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I was born in iniquity."],[2,"My mother conceived me in sin."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you desire truth in the inward parts."],[2,"You teach me wisdom in the inmost place."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Purify me with hyssop, and I will be clean."],[2,"Wash me, and I will be whiter than snow."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let me hear joy and gladness,"],[2,"that the bones which you have broken may rejoice."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Hide your face from my sins,"],[2,"and blot out all of my iniquities."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Create in me a clean heart, O God."],[2,"Renew a right spirit within me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t throw me from your presence,"],[2,"and don\u2019t take your Holy Spirit from me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Restore to me the joy of your salvation."],[2,"Uphold me with a willing spirit."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I will teach transgressors your ways."],[2,"Sinners will be converted to you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me from the guilt of bloodshed, O God, the God of my salvation."],[2,"My tongue will sing aloud of your righteousness."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, open my lips."],[2,"My mouth will declare your praise."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For you don\u2019t delight in sacrifice, or else I would give it."],[2,"You have no pleasure in burnt offering."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit."],[2,"O God, you will not despise a broken and contrite heart."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Do well in your good pleasure to Zion."],[2,"Build the walls of Jerusalem."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Then you will delight in the sacrifices of righteousness,"],[2,"in burnt offerings and in whole burnt offerings."],[1,"Then they will offer bulls on your altar."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A contemplation by David, when Doeg the Edomite came and told Saul, \u201cDavid has come to Ahimelech\u2019s house.\u201d"],p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you boast of mischief, mighty man?"],[2,"God\u2019s loving kindness endures continually."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Your tongue plots destruction,"],[2,"like a sharp razor, working deceitfully."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You love evil more than good,"],[2,"lying rather than speaking the truth. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You love all devouring words,"],[2,"you deceitful tongue."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"God will likewise destroy you forever."],[2,"He will take you up, and pluck you out of your tent,"],[2,"and root you out of the land of the living. Selah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous also will see it, and fear,"],[2,"and laugh at him, saying,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, this is the man who didn\u2019t make God his strength,"],[2,"but trusted in the abundance of his riches,"],[2,"and strengthened himself in his wickedness.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, I am like a green olive tree in God\u2019s house."],[2,"I trust in God\u2019s loving kindness forever and ever."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give you thanks forever, because you have done it."],[2,"I will hope in your name, for it is good,"],[2,"in the presence of your saints."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cMahalath.\u201d A contemplation by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The fool has said in his heart, \u201cThere is no God.\u201d"],[2,"They are corrupt, and have done abominable iniquity."],[2,"There is no one who does good."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"God looks down from heaven on the children of men,"],[2,"to see if there are any who understood,"],[2,"who seek after God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Every one of them has gone back."],[2,"They have become filthy together."],[2,"There is no one who does good, no, not one."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Have the workers of iniquity no knowledge,"],[2,"who eat up my people as they eat bread,"],[2,"and don\u2019t call on God?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"There they were in great fear, where no fear was,"],[2,"for God has scattered the bones of him who encamps against you."],[1,"You have put them to shame,"],[2,"because God has rejected them."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that the salvation of Israel would come out of Zion!"],[2,"When God brings back his people from captivity,"],[2,"then Jacob shall rejoice,"],[2,"and Israel shall be glad."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. On stringed instruments. A contemplation by David, when the Ziphites came and said to Saul, \u201cIsn\u2019t David hiding himself among us?\u201d"],p:1,l:[[1,"Save me, God, by your name."],[2,"Vindicate me in your might."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear my prayer, God."],[2,"Listen to the words of my mouth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For strangers have risen up against me."],[2,"Violent men have sought after my soul."],[2,"They haven\u2019t set God before them. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, God is my helper."],[2,"The Lord is the one who sustains my soul."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He will repay the evil to my enemies."],[2,"Destroy them in your truth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"With a free will offering, I will sacrifice to you."],[2,"I will give thanks to your name, LORD, for it is good."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has delivered me out of all trouble."],[2,"My eye has seen triumph over my enemies."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. On stringed instruments. A contemplation by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Listen to my prayer, God."],[2,"Don\u2019t hide yourself from my supplication."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Attend to me, and answer me."],[2,"I am restless in my complaint,"],[2,"and moan"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"because of the voice of the enemy,"],[2,"because of the oppression of the wicked."],[1,"For they bring suffering on me."],[2,"In anger they hold a grudge against me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"My heart is severely pained within me."],[2,"The terrors of death have fallen on me."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Fearfulness and trembling have come on me."],[2,"Horror has overwhelmed me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cOh that I had wings like a dove!"],[2,"Then I would fly away, and be at rest."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, then I would wander far off."],[2,"I would lodge in the wilderness.\u201d Selah."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI would hurry to a shelter from the stormy wind and storm.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Confuse them, Lord, and confound their language,"],[2,"for I have seen violence and strife in the city."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Day and night they prowl around on its walls."],[2,"Malice and abuse are also within her."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Destructive forces are within her."],[2,"Threats and lies don\u2019t depart from her streets."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For it was not an enemy who insulted me,"],[2,"then I could have endured it."],[1,"Neither was it he who hated me who raised himself up against me,"],[2,"then I would have hidden myself from him."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"But it was you, a man like me,"],[2,"my companion, and my familiar friend."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"We took sweet fellowship together."],[2,"We walked in God\u2019s house with company."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Let death come suddenly on them."],[2,"Let them go down alive into Sheol."],[2,"For wickedness is among them, in their dwelling."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"As for me, I will call on God."],[2,"The LORD will save me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Evening, morning, and at noon, I will cry out in distress."],[2,"He will hear my voice."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He has redeemed my soul in peace from the battle that was against me,"],[2,"although there are many who oppose me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"God, who is enthroned forever,"],[2,"will hear and answer them. Selah."],[1,"They never change"],[2,"and don\u2019t fear God."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He raises his hands against his friends."],[2,"He has violated his covenant."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"His mouth was smooth as butter,"],[2,"but his heart was war."],[1,"His words were softer than oil,"],[2,"yet they were drawn swords."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Cast your burden on the LORD and he will sustain you."],[2,"He will never allow the righteous to be moved."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, God, will bring them down into the pit of destruction."],[2,"Bloodthirsty and deceitful men shall not live out half their days,"],[2,"but I will trust in you."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cSilent Dove in Distant Lands.\u201d A poem by David, when the Philistines seized him in Gath."],p:1,l:[[1,"Be merciful to me, God, for man wants to swallow me up."],[2,"All day long, he attacks and oppresses me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My enemies want to swallow me up all day long,"],[2,"for they are many who fight proudly against me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"When I am afraid,"],[2,"I will put my trust in you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"In God, I praise his word."],[2,"In God, I put my trust."],[1,"I will not be afraid."],[2,"What can flesh do to me?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"All day long they twist my words."],[2,"All their thoughts are against me for evil."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They conspire and lurk,"],[2,"watching my steps."],[2,"They are eager to take my life."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall they escape by iniquity?"],[2,"In anger cast down the peoples, God."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You count my wanderings."],[2,"You put my tears into your container."],[2,"Aren\u2019t they in your book?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Then my enemies shall turn back in the day that I call."],[2,"I know this: that God is for me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"In God, I will praise his word."],[2,"In the LORD, I will praise his word."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I have put my trust in God."],[2,"I will not be afraid."],[2,"What can man do to me?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Your vows are on me, God."],[2,"I will give thank offerings to you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have delivered my soul from death,"],[2,"and prevented my feet from falling,"],[2,"that I may walk before God in the light of the living."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cDo Not Destroy.\u201d A poem by David, when he fled from Saul, in the cave."],p:1,l:[[1,"Be merciful to me, God, be merciful to me,"],[2,"for my soul takes refuge in you."],[1,"Yes, in the shadow of your wings, I will take refuge,"],[2,"until disaster has passed."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I cry out to God Most High,"],[1,"to God who accomplishes my requests for me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He will send from heaven, and save me,"],[2,"he rebukes the one who is pursuing me. Selah."],[1,"God will send out his loving kindness and his truth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul is among lions."],[2,"I lie among those who are set on fire,"],[2,"even the sons of men, whose teeth are spears and arrows,"],[2,"and their tongue a sharp sword."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Be exalted, God, above the heavens!"],[2,"Let your glory be above all the earth!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They have prepared a net for my steps."],[2,"My soul is bowed down."],[1,"They dig a pit before me."],[2,"They fall into the middle of it themselves. Selah."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"My heart is steadfast, God."],[2,"My heart is steadfast."],[2,"I will sing, yes, I will sing praises."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Wake up, my glory! Wake up, lute and harp!"],[2,"I will wake up the dawn."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give thanks to you, Lord, among the peoples."],[2,"I will sing praises to you among the nations."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For your great loving kindness reaches to the heavens,"],[2,"and your truth to the skies."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Be exalted, God, above the heavens."],[2,"Let your glory be over all the earth."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cDo Not Destroy.\u201d A poem by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Do you indeed speak righteousness, silent ones?"],[2,"Do you judge blamelessly, you sons of men?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"No, in your heart you plot injustice."],[2,"You measure out the violence of your hands on the earth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked go astray from the womb."],[2,"They are wayward as soon as they are born, speaking lies."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Their poison is like the poison of a snake,"],[2,"like a deaf cobra that stops its ear,"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"which doesn\u2019t listen to the voice of charmers,"],[2,"no matter how skillful the charmer may be."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Break their teeth, God, in their mouth."],[2,"Break out the great teeth of the young lions, LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them vanish like water that flows away."],[2,"When they draw the bow, let their arrows be made blunt."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be like a snail which melts and passes away,"],[2,"like the stillborn child, who has not seen the sun."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Before your pots can feel the heat of the thorns,"],[2,"he will sweep away the green and the burning alike."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous shall rejoice when he sees the vengeance."],[2,"He shall wash his feet in the blood of the wicked,"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"so that men shall say, \u201cMost certainly there is a reward for the righteous."],[2,"Most certainly there is a God who judges the earth.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cDo Not Destroy.\u201d A poem by David, when Saul sent, and they watched the house to kill him."],p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me from my enemies, my God."],[2,"Set me on high from those who rise up against me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me from the workers of iniquity."],[2,"Save me from the bloodthirsty men."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, they lie in wait for my soul."],[2,"The mighty gather themselves together against me,"],[2,"not for my disobedience, nor for my sin, LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I have done no wrong, yet they are ready to attack me."],[2,"Rise up, behold, and help me!"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You, LORD God of Armies, the God of Israel,"],[2,"rouse yourself to punish the nations."],[2,"Show no mercy to the wicked traitors. Selah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They return at evening, howling like dogs,"],[2,"and prowl around the city."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, they spew with their mouth."],[2,"Swords are in their lips,"],[2,"\u201cFor\u201d, they say, \u201cwho hears us?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, LORD, laugh at them."],[2,"You scoff at all the nations."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh, my Strength, I watch for you,"],[2,"for God is my high tower."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"My God will go before me with his loving kindness."],[2,"God will let me look at my enemies in triumph."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t kill them, or my people may forget."],[2,"Scatter them by your power, and bring them down, Lord our shield."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For the sin of their mouth, and the words of their lips,"],[2,"let them be caught in their pride,"],[2,"for the curses and lies which they utter."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Consume them in wrath."],[2,"Consume them, and they will be no more."],[1,"Let them know that God rules in Jacob,"],[2,"to the ends of the earth. Selah."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"At evening let them return."],[2,"Let them howl like a dog, and go around the city."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall wander up and down for food,"],[2,"and wait all night if they aren\u2019t satisfied."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"But I will sing of your strength."],[2,"Yes, I will sing aloud of your loving kindness in the morning."],[1,"For you have been my high tower,"],[2,"a refuge in the day of my distress."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"To you, my strength, I will sing praises."],[2,"For God is my high tower, the God of my mercy."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cThe Lily of the Covenant.\u201d A teaching poem by David, when he fought with Aram Naharaim and with Aram Zobah, and Joab returned, and killed twelve thousand of Edom in the Valley of Salt."],p:1,l:[[1,"God, you have rejected us."],[2,"You have broken us down."],[1,"You have been angry."],[2,"Restore us, again."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You have made the land tremble."],[2,"You have torn it."],[1,"Mend its fractures,"],[2,"for it quakes."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You have shown your people hard things."],[2,"You have made us drink the wine that makes us stagger."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You have given a banner to those who fear you,"],[2,"that it may be displayed because of the truth. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"So that your beloved may be delivered,"],[2,"save with your right hand, and answer us."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"God has spoken from his sanctuary:"],[2,"\u201cI will triumph."],[2,"I will divide Shechem,"],[2,"and measure out the valley of Succoth."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Gilead is mine, and Manasseh is mine."],[2,"Ephraim also is the defense of my head."],[2,"Judah is my scepter."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Moab is my wash basin."],[2,"I will throw my sandal on Edom."],[2,"I shout in triumph over Philistia.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Who will bring me into the strong city?"],[2,"Who has led me to Edom?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Haven\u2019t you, God, rejected us?"],[2,"You don\u2019t go out with our armies, God."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Give us help against the adversary,"],[2,"for the help of man is vain."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Through God we will do valiantly,"],[2,"for it is he who will tread down our adversaries."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. For a stringed instrument. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear my cry, God."],[2,"Listen to my prayer."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"From the end of the earth, I will call to you when my heart is overwhelmed."],[2,"Lead me to the rock that is higher than I."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have been a refuge for me,"],[2,"a strong tower from the enemy."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will dwell in your tent forever."],[2,"I will take refuge in the shelter of your wings. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For you, God, have heard my vows."],[2,"You have given me the heritage of those who fear your name."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You will prolong the king\u2019s life."],[2,"His years will be for generations."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He shall be enthroned in God\u2019s presence forever."],[2,"Appoint your loving kindness and truth, that they may preserve him."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"So I will sing praise to your name forever,"],[2,"that I may fulfill my vows daily."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To Jeduthun. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"My soul rests in God alone."],[2,"My salvation is from him."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He alone is my rock, my salvation, and my fortress."],[2,"I will never be greatly shaken."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"How long will you assault a man?"],[2,"Would all of you throw him down,"],[2,"like a leaning wall, like a tottering fence?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They fully intend to throw him down from his lofty place."],[2,"They delight in lies."],[2,"They bless with their mouth, but they curse inwardly. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul, wait in silence for God alone,"],[2,"for my expectation is from him."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He alone is my rock and my salvation, my fortress."],[2,"I will not be shaken."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"My salvation and my honor is with God."],[2,"The rock of my strength, and my refuge, is in God."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Trust in him at all times, you people."],[2,"Pour out your heart before him."],[2,"God is a refuge for us. Selah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely men of low degree are just a breath,"],[2,"and men of high degree are a lie."],[1,"In the balances they will go up."],[2,"They are together lighter than a breath."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t trust in oppression."],[2,"Don\u2019t become vain in robbery."],[1,"If riches increase,"],[2,"don\u2019t set your heart on them."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"God has spoken once;"],[2,"twice I have heard this,"],[2,"that power belongs to God."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Also to you, Lord, belongs loving kindness,"],[2,"for you reward every man according to his work."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David, when he was in the desert of Judah."],p:1,l:[[1,"God, you are my God."],[2,"I will earnestly seek you."],[1,"My soul thirsts for you."],[2,"My flesh longs for you,"],[2,"in a dry and weary land, where there is no water."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"So I have seen you in the sanctuary,"],[2,"watching your power and your glory."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Because your loving kindness is better than life,"],[2,"my lips shall praise you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"So I will bless you while I live."],[2,"I will lift up my hands in your name."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul shall be satisfied as with the richest food."],[2,"My mouth shall praise you with joyful lips,"]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"when I remember you on my bed,"],[2,"and think about you in the night watches."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have been my help."],[2,"I will rejoice in the shadow of your wings."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul stays close to you."],[2,"Your right hand holds me up."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"But those who seek my soul to destroy it"],[2,"shall go into the lower parts of the earth."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall be given over to the power of the sword."],[2,"They shall be jackal food."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"But the king shall rejoice in God."],[2,"Everyone who swears by him will praise him,"],[2,"for the mouth of those who speak lies shall be silenced."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear my voice, God, in my complaint."],[2,"Preserve my life from fear of the enemy."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hide me from the conspiracy of the wicked,"],[2,"from the noisy crowd of the ones doing evil;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"who sharpen their tongue like a sword,"],[2,"and aim their arrows, deadly words,"]]},{v:4,l:[[2,"to shoot innocent men from ambushes."],[2,"They shoot at him suddenly and fearlessly."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They encourage themselves in evil plans."],[2,"They talk about laying snares secretly."],[2,"They say, \u201cWho will see them?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They plot injustice, saying, \u201cWe have made a perfect plan!\u201d"],[2,"Surely man\u2019s mind and heart are cunning."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But God will shoot at them."],[2,"They will be suddenly struck down with an arrow."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Their own tongues shall ruin them."],[2,"All who see them will shake their heads."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"All mankind shall be afraid."],[2,"They shall declare the work of God,"],[2,"and shall wisely ponder what he has done."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous shall be glad in the LORD,"],[2,"and shall take refuge in him."],[2,"All the upright in heart shall praise him!"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David. A song."],p:1,l:[[1,"Praise waits for you, God, in Zion."],[2,"Vows shall be performed to you."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You who hear prayer,"],[2,"all men will come to you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Sins overwhelmed me,"],[2,"but you atoned for our transgressions."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the one whom you choose and cause to come near,"],[2,"that he may live in your courts."],[2,"We will be filled with the goodness of your house,"],[2,"your holy temple."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"By awesome deeds of righteousness, you answer us,"],[2,"God of our salvation."],[1,"You who are the hope of all the ends of the earth,"],[2,"of those who are far away on the sea."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"By your power, you form the mountains,"],[2,"having armed yourself with strength."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You still the roaring of the seas,"],[2,"the roaring of their waves,"],[2,"and the turmoil of the nations."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They also who dwell in faraway places are afraid at your wonders."],[2,"You call the morning\u2019s dawn and the evening with songs of joy."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You visit the earth, and water it."],[2,"You greatly enrich it."],[1,"The river of God is full of water."],[2,"You provide them grain, for so you have ordained it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You drench its furrows."],[2,"You level its ridges."],[2,"You soften it with showers."],[2,"You bless it with a crop."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You crown the year with your bounty."],[2,"Your carts overflow with abundance."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The wilderness grasslands overflow."],[2,"The hills are clothed with gladness."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The pastures are covered with flocks."],[2,"The valleys also are clothed with grain."],[1,"They shout for joy!"],[2,"They also sing."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A song. A Psalm."],p:1,l:[[1,"Make a joyful shout to God, all the earth!"]]},{v:2,l:[[2,"Sing to the glory of his name!"],[2,"Offer glory and praise!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Tell God, \u201cHow awesome are your deeds!"],[2,"Through the greatness of your power, your enemies submit themselves to you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"All the earth will worship you,"],[2,"and will sing to you;"],[2,"they will sing to your name.\u201d Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Come, and see God\u2019s deeds\u2014"],[2,"awesome work on behalf of the children of men."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He turned the sea into dry land."],[2,"They went through the river on foot."],[2,"There, we rejoiced in him."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He rules by his might forever."],[2,"His eyes watch the nations."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the rebellious rise up against him. Selah."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise our God, you peoples!"],[2,"Make the sound of his praise heard,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"who preserves our life among the living,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t allow our feet to be moved."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For you, God, have tested us."],[2,"You have refined us, as silver is refined."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You brought us into prison."],[2,"You laid a burden on our backs."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You allowed men to ride over our heads."],[2,"We went through fire and through water,"],[2,"but you brought us to the place of abundance."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I will come into your temple with burnt offerings."],[2,"I will pay my vows to you,"]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"which my lips promised,"],[2,"and my mouth spoke, when I was in distress."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will offer to you burnt offerings of fat animals,"],[2,"with the offering of rams,"],[2,"I will offer bulls with goats. Selah."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Come and hear, all you who fear God."],[2,"I will declare what he has done for my soul."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I cried to him with my mouth."],[2,"He was extolled with my tongue."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"If I cherished sin in my heart,"],[2,"the Lord wouldn\u2019t have listened."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"But most certainly, God has listened."],[2,"He has heard the voice of my prayer."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be God, who has not turned away my prayer,"],[2,"nor his loving kindness from me."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. With stringed instruments. A Psalm. A song."],p:1,l:[[1,"May God be merciful to us, bless us,"],[2,"and cause his face to shine on us. Selah."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"That your way may be known on earth,"],[2,"and your salvation among all nations,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"let the peoples praise you, God."],[2,"Let all the peoples praise you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh let the nations be glad and sing for joy,"],[2,"for you will judge the peoples with equity,"],[2,"and govern the nations on earth. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the peoples praise you, God."],[2,"Let all the peoples praise you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth has yielded its increase."],[2,"God, even our own God, will bless us."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"God will bless us."],[2,"All the ends of the earth shall fear him."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David. A song."],p:1,l:[[1,"Let God arise!"],[2,"Let his enemies be scattered!"],[2,"Let them who hate him also flee before him."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"As smoke is driven away,"],[2,"so drive them away."],[1,"As wax melts before the fire,"],[2,"so let the wicked perish at the presence of God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"But let the righteous be glad."],[2,"Let them rejoice before God."],[2,"Yes, let them rejoice with gladness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to God! Sing praises to his name!"],[2,"Extol him who rides on the clouds:"],[1,"to the LORD, his name!"],[2,"Rejoice before him!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"A father of the fatherless, and a defender of the widows,"],[2,"is God in his holy habitation."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"God sets the lonely in families."],[1,"He brings out the prisoners with singing,"],[2,"but the rebellious dwell in a sun-scorched land."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"God, when you went out before your people,"],[2,"when you marched through the wilderness... Selah."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth trembled."],[2,"The sky also poured down rain at the presence of the God of Sinai\u2014"],[2,"at the presence of God, the God of Israel."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You, God, sent a plentiful rain."],[2,"You confirmed your inheritance when it was weary."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Your congregation lived therein."],[2,"You, God, prepared your goodness for the poor."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord announced the word."],[2,"The ones who proclaim it are a great company."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cKings of armies flee! They flee!\u201d"],[2,"She who waits at home divides the plunder,"]]},{v:13,l:[[2,"while you sleep among the camp fires,"],[2,"the wings of a dove sheathed with silver,"],[2,"her feathers with shining gold."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"When the Almighty scattered kings in her,"],[2,"it snowed on Zalmon."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains of Bashan are majestic mountains."],[2,"The mountains of Bashan are rugged."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you look in envy, you rugged mountains,"],[2,"at the mountain where God chooses to reign?"],[2,"Yes, the LORD will dwell there forever."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The chariots of God are tens of thousands and thousands of thousands."],[2,"The Lord is among them, from Sinai, into the sanctuary."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"You have ascended on high."],[2,"You have led away captives."],[1,"You have received gifts among people,"],[2,"yes, among the rebellious also, that the LORD God might dwell there."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the Lord, who daily bears our burdens,"],[2,"even the God who is our salvation. Selah."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"God is to us a God of deliverance."],[2,"To GOD, the Lord, belongs escape from death."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"But God will strike through the head of his enemies,"],[2,"the hairy scalp of such a one as still continues in his guiltiness."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord said, \u201cI will bring you again from Bashan,"],[2,"I will bring you again from the depths of the sea,"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"that you may crush them, dipping your foot in blood,"],[2,"that the tongues of your dogs may have their portion from your enemies.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"They have seen your processions, God,"],[2,"even the processions of my God, my King, into the sanctuary."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The singers went before, the minstrels followed after,"],[2,"among the ladies playing with tambourines,"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBless God in the congregations,"],[2,"even the Lord in the assembly of Israel!\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"There is little Benjamin, their ruler,"],[2,"the princes of Judah, their council,"],[2,"the princes of Zebulun, and the princes of Naphtali."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Your God has commanded your strength."],[2,"Strengthen, God, that which you have done for us."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Because of your temple at Jerusalem,"],[2,"kings will bring presents to you."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Rebuke the wild animal of the reeds,"],[2,"the multitude of the bulls with the calves of the peoples."],[1,"Trample under foot the bars of silver."],[2,"Scatter the nations who delight in war."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Princes shall come out of Egypt."],[2,"Ethiopia shall hurry to stretch out her hands to God."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to God, you kingdoms of the earth!"],[2,"Sing praises to the Lord\u2014Selah\u2014"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who rides on the heaven of heavens, which are of old;"],[2,"behold, he utters his voice, a mighty voice."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Ascribe strength to God!"],[2,"His excellency is over Israel,"],[2,"his strength is in the skies."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"You are awesome, God, in your sanctuaries."],[2,"The God of Israel gives strength and power to his people."],[2,"Praise be to God!"]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cLilies.\u201d By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Save me, God,"],[2,"for the waters have come up to my neck!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I sink in deep mire, where there is no foothold."],[2,"I have come into deep waters, where the floods overflow me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I am weary with my crying."],[2,"My throat is dry."],[2,"My eyes fail looking for my God."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who hate me without a cause are more than the hairs of my head."],[2,"Those who want to cut me off, being my enemies wrongfully, are mighty."],[2,"I have to restore what I didn\u2019t take away."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"God, you know my foolishness."],[2,"My sins aren\u2019t hidden from you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let those who wait for you be shamed through me, Lord GOD of Armies."],[2,"Don\u2019t let those who seek you be brought to dishonor through me, God of Israel."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Because for your sake, I have borne reproach."],[2,"Shame has covered my face."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I have become a stranger to my brothers,"],[2,"an alien to my mother\u2019s children."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For the zeal of your house consumes me."],[2,"The reproaches of those who reproach you have fallen on me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"When I wept and I fasted,"],[2,"that was to my reproach."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"When I made sackcloth my clothing,"],[2,"I became a byword to them."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who sit in the gate talk about me."],[2,"I am the song of the drunkards."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, my prayer is to you, LORD, in an acceptable time."],[2,"God, in the abundance of your loving kindness, answer me in the truth of your salvation."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me out of the mire, and don\u2019t let me sink."],[2,"Let me be delivered from those who hate me, and out of the deep waters."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let the flood waters overwhelm me,"],[2,"neither let the deep swallow me up."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the pit shut its mouth on me."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Answer me, LORD, for your loving kindness is good."],[2,"According to the multitude of your tender mercies, turn to me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t hide your face from your servant,"],[2,"for I am in distress."],[2,"Answer me speedily!"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Draw near to my soul and redeem it."],[2,"Ransom me because of my enemies."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"You know my reproach, my shame, and my dishonor."],[2,"My adversaries are all before you."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Reproach has broken my heart, and I am full of heaviness."],[2,"I looked for some to take pity, but there was none;"],[2,"for comforters, but I found none."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"They also gave me poison for my food."],[2,"In my thirst, they gave me vinegar to drink."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Let their table before them become a snare."],[2,"May it become a retribution and a trap."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Let their eyes be darkened, so that they can\u2019t see."],[2,"Let their backs be continually bent."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Pour out your indignation on them."],[2,"Let the fierceness of your anger overtake them."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Let their habitation be desolate."],[2,"Let no one dwell in their tents."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"For they persecute him whom you have wounded."],[2,"They tell of the sorrow of those whom you have hurt."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Charge them with crime upon crime."],[2,"Don\u2019t let them come into your righteousness."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be blotted out of the book of life,"],[2,"and not be written with the righteous."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"But I am in pain and distress."],[2,"Let your salvation, God, protect me."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"I will praise the name of God with a song,"],[2,"and will magnify him with thanksgiving."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"It will please the LORD better than an ox,"],[2,"or a bull that has horns and hoofs."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"The humble have seen it, and are glad."],[2,"You who seek after God, let your heart live."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD hears the needy,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t despise his captive people."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Let heaven and earth praise him;"],[2,"the seas, and everything that moves therein!"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"For God will save Zion, and build the cities of Judah."],[2,"They shall settle there, and own it."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"The children also of his servants shall inherit it."],[2,"Those who love his name shall dwell therein."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. By David. A reminder."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hurry, God, to deliver me."],[2,"Come quickly to help me, LORD."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be disappointed and confounded who seek my soul."],[2,"Let those who desire my ruin be turned back in disgrace."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be turned because of their shame"],[2,"who say, \u201cAha! Aha!\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Let all those who seek you rejoice and be glad in you."],[2,"Let those who love your salvation continually say,"],[2,"\u201cLet God be exalted!\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"But I am poor and needy."],[2,"Come to me quickly, God."],[1,"You are my help and my deliverer."],[2,"LORD, don\u2019t delay."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"In you, LORD, I take refuge."],[2,"Never let me be disappointed."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me in your righteousness, and rescue me."],[2,"Turn your ear to me, and save me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Be to me a rock of refuge to which I may always go."],[2,"Give the command to save me,"],[2,"for you are my rock and my fortress."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Rescue me, my God, from the hand of the wicked,"],[2,"from the hand of the unrighteous and cruel man."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are my hope, Lord GOD,"],[2,"my confidence from my youth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I have relied on you from the womb."],[2,"You are he who took me out of my mother\u2019s womb."],[2,"I will always praise you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I am a marvel to many,"],[2,"but you are my strong refuge."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"My mouth shall be filled with your praise,"],[2,"with your honor all day long."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t reject me in my old age."],[2,"Don\u2019t forsake me when my strength fails."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For my enemies talk about me."],[2,"Those who watch for my soul conspire together,"]]},{v:11,l:[[2,"saying, \u201cGod has forsaken him."],[2,"Pursue and take him, for no one will rescue him.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"God, don\u2019t be far from me."],[2,"My God, hurry to help me."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my accusers be disappointed and consumed."],[2,"Let them be covered with disgrace and scorn who want to harm me."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"But I will always hope,"],[2,"and will add to all of your praise."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"My mouth will tell about your righteousness,"],[2,"and of your salvation all day,"],[2,"though I don\u2019t know its full measure."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I will come with the mighty acts of the Lord GOD."],[2,"I will make mention of your righteousness, even of yours alone."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"God, you have taught me from my youth."],[2,"Until now, I have declared your wondrous works."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, even when I am old and gray-haired, God, don\u2019t forsake me,"],[2,"until I have declared your strength to the next generation,"],[2,"your might to everyone who is to come."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"God, your righteousness also reaches to the heavens."],[2,"You have done great things."],[2,"God, who is like you?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"You, who have shown us many and bitter troubles,"],[2,"you will let me live."],[2,"You will bring us up again from the depths of the earth."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Increase my honor"],[2,"and comfort me again."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also praise you with the harp for your faithfulness, my God."],[2,"I sing praises to you with the lyre, Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"My lips shall shout for joy!"],[2,"My soul, which you have redeemed, sings praises to you!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"My tongue will also talk about your righteousness all day long,"],[2,"for they are disappointed, and they are confounded,"],[2,"who want to harm me."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By Solomon."],p:1,l:[[1,"God, give the king your justice;"],[2,"your righteousness to the royal son."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He will judge your people with righteousness,"],[2,"and your poor with justice."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains shall bring prosperity to the people."],[2,"The hills bring the fruit of righteousness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He will judge the poor of the people."],[2,"He will save the children of the needy,"],[2,"and will break the oppressor in pieces."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall fear you while the sun endures;"],[2,"and as long as the moon, throughout all generations."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He will come down like rain on the mown grass,"],[2,"as showers that water the earth."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"In his days, the righteous shall flourish,"],[2,"and abundance of peace, until the moon is no more."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He shall have dominion also from sea to sea,"],[2,"from the River to the ends of the earth."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who dwell in the wilderness shall bow before him."],[2,"His enemies shall lick the dust."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The kings of Tarshish and of the islands will bring tribute."],[2,"The kings of Sheba and Seba shall offer gifts."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, all kings shall fall down before him."],[2,"All nations shall serve him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For he will deliver the needy when he cries;"],[2,"the poor, who has no helper."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He will have pity on the poor and needy."],[2,"He will save the souls of the needy."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He will redeem their soul from oppression and violence."],[2,"Their blood will be precious in his sight."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He will live; and Sheba\u2019s gold will be given to him."],[2,"Men will pray for him continually."],[2,"They will bless him all day long."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Abundance of grain shall be throughout the land."],[2,"Its fruit sways like Lebanon."],[2,"Let it flourish, thriving like the grass of the field."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"His name endures forever."],[2,"His name continues as long as the sun."],[1,"Men shall be blessed by him."],[2,"All nations will call him blessed."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise be to the LORD God, the God of Israel,"],[2,"who alone does marvelous deeds."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be his glorious name forever!"],[2,"Let the whole earth be filled with his glory!"],[1,"Amen and amen."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"This ends the prayers by David, the son of Jesse."]]}],[{v:1,h:["BOOK 3","A Psalm by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"Surely God is good to Israel,"],[2,"to those who are pure in heart."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, my feet were almost gone."],[2,"My steps had nearly slipped."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For I was envious of the arrogant,"],[2,"when I saw the prosperity of the wicked."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For there are no struggles in their death,"],[2,"but their strength is firm."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They are free from burdens of men,"],[2,"neither are they plagued like other men."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore pride is like a chain around their neck."],[2,"Violence covers them like a garment."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Their eyes bulge with fat."],[2,"Their minds pass the limits of conceit."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They scoff and speak with malice."],[2,"In arrogance, they threaten oppression."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They have set their mouth in the heavens."],[2,"Their tongue walks through the earth."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore their people return to them,"],[2,"and they drink up waters of abundance."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They say, \u201cHow does God know?"],[2,"Is there knowledge in the Most High?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, these are the wicked."],[2,"Being always at ease, they increase in riches."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely I have cleansed my heart in vain,"],[2,"and washed my hands in innocence,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For all day long I have been plagued,"],[2,"and punished every morning."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"If I had said, \u201cI will speak thus\u201d,"],[2,"behold, I would have betrayed the generation of your children."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"When I tried to understand this,"],[2,"it was too painful for me\u2014"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"until I entered God\u2019s sanctuary,"],[2,"and considered their latter end."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely you set them in slippery places."],[2,"You throw them down to destruction."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"How they are suddenly destroyed!"],[2,"They are completely swept away with terrors."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"As a dream when one wakes up,"],[2,"so, Lord, when you awake, you will despise their fantasies."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For my soul was grieved."],[2,"I was embittered in my heart."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"I was so senseless and ignorant."],[2,"I was a brute beast before you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Nevertheless, I am continually with you."],[2,"You have held my right hand."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"You will guide me with your counsel,"],[2,"and afterward receive me to glory."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Whom do I have in heaven?"],[2,"There is no one on earth whom I desire besides you."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"My flesh and my heart fails,"],[2,"but God is the strength of my heart and my portion forever."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, those who are far from you shall perish."],[2,"You have destroyed all those who are unfaithful to you."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"But it is good for me to come close to God."],[2,"I have made the Lord GOD my refuge,"],[2,"that I may tell of all your works."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]}],[{v:1,h:["A contemplation by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"God, why have you rejected us forever?"],[2,"Why does your anger smolder against the sheep of your pasture?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember your congregation, which you purchased of old,"],[2,"which you have redeemed to be the tribe of your inheritance:"],[2,"Mount Zion, in which you have lived."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your feet to the perpetual ruins,"],[2,"all the evil that the enemy has done in the sanctuary."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Your adversaries have roared in the middle of your assembly."],[2,"They have set up their standards as signs."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They behaved like men wielding axes,"],[2,"cutting through a thicket of trees."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Now they break all its carved work down with hatchet and hammers."]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"They have burned your sanctuary to the ground."],[2,"They have profaned the dwelling place of your Name."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They said in their heart, \u201cWe will crush them completely.\u201d"],[2,"They have burned up all the places in the land where God was worshiped."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"We see no miraculous signs."],[2,"There is no longer any prophet,"],[2,"neither is there among us anyone who knows how long."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"How long, God, shall the adversary reproach?"],[2,"Shall the enemy blaspheme your name forever?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you draw back your hand, even your right hand?"],[2,"Take it from your chest and consume them!"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet God is my King of old,"],[2,"working salvation throughout the earth."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You divided the sea by your strength."],[2,"You broke the heads of the sea monsters in the waters."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You broke the heads of Leviathan in pieces."],[2,"You gave him as food to people and desert creatures."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You opened up spring and stream."],[2,"You dried up mighty rivers."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The day is yours, the night is also yours."],[2,"You have prepared the light and the sun."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"You have set all the boundaries of the earth."],[2,"You have made summer and winter."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember this, that the enemy has mocked you, LORD."],[2,"Foolish people have blasphemed your name."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t deliver the soul of your dove to wild beasts."],[2,"Don\u2019t forget the life of your poor forever."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Honor your covenant,"],[2,"for haunts of violence fill the dark places of the earth."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let the oppressed return ashamed."],[2,"Let the poor and needy praise your name."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, God! Plead your own cause."],[2,"Remember how the foolish man mocks you all day."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t forget the voice of your adversaries."],[2,"The tumult of those who rise up against you ascends continually."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cDo Not Destroy.\u201d A Psalm by Asaph. A song."],p:1,l:[[1,"We give thanks to you, God."],[2,"We give thanks, for your Name is near."],[2,"Men tell about your wondrous works."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"When I choose the appointed time,"],[2,"I will judge blamelessly."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth and all its inhabitants quake."],[2,"I firmly hold its pillars. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I said to the arrogant, \u201cDon\u2019t boast!\u201d"],[2,"I said to the wicked, \u201cDon\u2019t lift up the horn."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t lift up your horn on high."],[2,"Don\u2019t speak with a stiff neck.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For neither from the east, nor from the west,"],[2,"nor yet from the south, comes exaltation."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But God is the judge."],[2,"He puts down one, and lifts up another."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For in the LORD\u2019s hand there is a cup,"],[2,"full of foaming wine mixed with spices."],[1,"He pours it out."],[2,"Indeed the wicked of the earth drink and drink it to its very dregs."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"But I will declare this forever:"],[2,"I will sing praises to the God of Jacob."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cut off all the horns of the wicked,"],[2,"but the horns of the righteous shall be lifted up."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. On stringed instruments. A Psalm by Asaph. A song."],p:1,l:[[1,"In Judah, God is known."],[2,"His name is great in Israel."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"His tabernacle is also in Salem."],[2,"His dwelling place in Zion."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"There he broke the flaming arrows of the bow,"],[2,"the shield, and the sword, and the weapons of war. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Glorious are you, and excellent,"],[2,"more than mountains of game."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Valiant men lie plundered,"],[2,"they have slept their last sleep."],[2,"None of the men of war can lift their hands."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"At your rebuke, God of Jacob,"],[2,"both chariot and horse are cast into a dead sleep."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You, even you, are to be feared."],[2,"Who can stand in your sight when you are angry?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You pronounced judgment from heaven."],[2,"The earth feared, and was silent,"]]},{v:9,l:[[2,"when God arose to judgment,"],[2,"to save all the afflicted ones of the earth. Selah."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely the wrath of man praises you."],[2,"The survivors of your wrath are restrained."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Make vows to the LORD your God, and fulfill them!"],[2,"Let all of his neighbors bring presents to him who is to be feared."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"He will cut off the spirit of princes."],[2,"He is feared by the kings of the earth."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To Jeduthun. A Psalm by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"My cry goes to God!"],[2,"Indeed, I cry to God for help,"],[2,"and for him to listen to me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord."],[2,"My hand was stretched out in the night, and didn\u2019t get tired."],[2,"My soul refused to be comforted."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I remember God, and I groan."],[2,"I complain, and my spirit is overwhelmed. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You hold my eyelids open."],[2,"I am so troubled that I can\u2019t speak."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I have considered the days of old,"],[2,"the years of ancient times."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I remember my song in the night."],[2,"I consider in my own heart;"],[2,"my spirit diligently inquires:"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWill the Lord reject us forever?"],[2,"Will he be favorable no more?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Has his loving kindness vanished forever?"],[2,"Does his promise fail for generations?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Has God forgotten to be gracious?"],[2,"Has he, in anger, withheld his compassion?\u201d Selah."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I thought, \u201cI will appeal to this:"],[2,"the years of the right hand of the Most High.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I will remember the LORD\u2019s deeds;"],[2,"for I will remember your wonders of old."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also meditate on all your work,"],[2,"and consider your doings."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Your way, God, is in the sanctuary."],[2,"What god is great like God?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You are the God who does wonders."],[2,"You have made your strength known among the peoples."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You have redeemed your people with your arm,"],[2,"the sons of Jacob and Joseph. Selah."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The waters saw you, God."],[2,"The waters saw you, and they writhed."],[2,"The depths also convulsed."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The clouds poured out water."],[2,"The skies resounded with thunder."],[2,"Your arrows also flashed around."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The voice of your thunder was in the whirlwind."],[2,"The lightnings lit up the world."],[2,"The earth trembled and shook."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Your way was through the sea,"],[2,"your paths through the great waters."],[2,"Your footsteps were not known."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"You led your people like a flock,"],[2,"by the hand of Moses and Aaron."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A contemplation by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear my teaching, my people."],[2,"Turn your ears to the words of my mouth."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will open my mouth in a parable."],[2,"I will utter dark sayings of old,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"which we have heard and known,"],[2,"and our fathers have told us."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"We will not hide them from their children,"],[2,"telling to the generation to come the praises of the LORD,"],[2,"his strength, and his wondrous deeds that he has done."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For he established a covenant in Jacob,"],[2,"and appointed a teaching in Israel,"],[2,"which he commanded our fathers,"],[2,"that they should make them known to their children;"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"that the generation to come might know, even the children who should be born;"],[2,"who should arise and tell their children,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"that they might set their hope in God,"],[2,"and not forget God\u2019s deeds,"],[2,"but keep his commandments,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"and might not be as their fathers\u2014"],[2,"a stubborn and rebellious generation,"],[2,"a generation that didn\u2019t make their hearts loyal,"],[2,"whose spirit was not steadfast with God."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of Ephraim, being armed and carrying bows,"],[2,"turned back in the day of battle."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They didn\u2019t keep God\u2019s covenant,"],[2,"and refused to walk in his law."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They forgot his doings,"],[2,"his wondrous deeds that he had shown them."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"He did marvelous things in the sight of their fathers,"],[2,"in the land of Egypt, in the field of Zoan."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He split the sea, and caused them to pass through."],[2,"He made the waters stand as a heap."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"In the daytime he also led them with a cloud,"],[2,"and all night with a light of fire."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He split rocks in the wilderness,"],[2,"and gave them drink abundantly as out of the depths."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought streams also out of the rock,"],[2,"and caused waters to run down like rivers."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet they still went on to sin against him,"],[2,"to rebel against the Most High in the desert."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"They tempted God in their heart"],[2,"by asking food according to their desire."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, they spoke against God."],[2,"They said, \u201cCan God prepare a table in the wilderness?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he struck the rock, so that waters gushed out,"],[2,"and streams overflowed."],[1,"Can he give bread also?"],[2,"Will he provide meat for his people?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD heard, and was angry."],[2,"A fire was kindled against Jacob,"],[2,"anger also went up against Israel,"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"because they didn\u2019t believe in God,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t trust in his salvation."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet he commanded the skies above,"],[2,"and opened the doors of heaven."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"He rained down manna on them to eat,"],[2,"and gave them food from the sky."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Man ate the bread of angels."],[2,"He sent them food to the full."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"He caused the east wind to blow in the sky."],[2,"By his power he guided the south wind."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"He also rained meat on them as the dust,"],[2,"winged birds as the sand of the seas."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"He let them fall in the middle of their camp,"],[2,"around their habitations."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"So they ate, and were well filled."],[2,"He gave them their own desire."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"They didn\u2019t turn from their cravings."],[2,"Their food was yet in their mouths,"]]},{v:31,l:[[2,"when the anger of God went up against them,"],[2,"killed some of their strongest,"],[2,"and struck down the young men of Israel."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"For all this they still sinned,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t believe in his wondrous works."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore he consumed their days in vanity,"],[2,"and their years in terror."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"When he killed them, then they inquired after him."],[2,"They returned and sought God earnestly."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"They remembered that God was their rock,"],[2,"the Most High God, their redeemer."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"But they flattered him with their mouth,"],[2,"and lied to him with their tongue."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"For their heart was not right with him,"],[2,"neither were they faithful in his covenant."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"But he, being merciful, forgave iniquity, and didn\u2019t destroy them."],[2,"Yes, many times he turned his anger away,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t stir up all his wrath."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"He remembered that they were but flesh,"],[2,"a wind that passes away, and doesn\u2019t come again."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"How often they rebelled against him in the wilderness,"],[2,"and grieved him in the desert!"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"They turned again and tempted God,"],[2,"and provoked the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"They didn\u2019t remember his hand,"],[2,"nor the day when he redeemed them from the adversary;"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"how he set his signs in Egypt,"],[2,"his wonders in the field of Zoan,"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"he turned their rivers into blood,"],[2,"and their streams, so that they could not drink."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent among them swarms of flies, which devoured them;"],[2,"and frogs, which destroyed them."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"He also gave their increase to the caterpillar,"],[2,"and their labor to the locust."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"He destroyed their vines with hail,"],[2,"their sycamore fig trees with frost."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[1,"He also gave over their livestock to the hail,"],[2,"and their flocks to hot thunderbolts."]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[1,"He threw on them the fierceness of his anger,"],[2,"wrath, indignation, and trouble,"],[2,"and a band of angels of evil."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"He made a path for his anger."],[2,"He didn\u2019t spare their soul from death,"],[2,"but gave their life over to the pestilence,"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[1,"and struck all the firstborn in Egypt,"],[2,"the chief of their strength in the tents of Ham."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[1,"But he led out his own people like sheep,"],[2,"and guided them in the wilderness like a flock."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[1,"He led them safely, so that they weren\u2019t afraid,"],[2,"but the sea overwhelmed their enemies."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought them to the border of his sanctuary,"],[2,"to this mountain, which his right hand had taken."]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[1,"He also drove out the nations before them,"],[2,"allotted them for an inheritance by line,"],[2,"and made the tribes of Israel to dwell in their tents."]]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet they tempted and rebelled against the Most High God,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t keep his testimonies,"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[1,"but turned back, and dealt treacherously like their fathers."],[2,"They were twisted like a deceitful bow."]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[1,"For they provoked him to anger with their high places,"],[2,"and moved him to jealousy with their engraved images."]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[1,"When God heard this, he was angry,"],[2,"and greatly abhorred Israel,"]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[1,"so that he abandoned the tent of Shiloh,"],[2,"the tent which he placed among men,"]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[1,"and delivered his strength into captivity,"],[2,"his glory into the adversary\u2019s hand."]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[1,"He also gave his people over to the sword,"],[2,"and was angry with his inheritance."]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[1,"Fire devoured their young men."],[2,"Their virgins had no wedding song."]]},{v:64,p:1,l:[[1,"Their priests fell by the sword,"],[2,"and their widows couldn\u2019t weep."]]},{v:65,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the Lord awakened as one out of sleep,"],[2,"like a mighty man who shouts by reason of wine."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[1,"He struck his adversaries backward."],[2,"He put them to a perpetual reproach."]]},{v:67,p:1,l:[[1,"Moreover he rejected the tent of Joseph,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t choose the tribe of Ephraim,"]]},{v:68,p:1,l:[[1,"But chose the tribe of Judah,"],[2,"Mount Zion which he loved."]]},{v:69,p:1,l:[[1,"He built his sanctuary like the heights,"],[2,"like the earth which he has established forever."]]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[1,"He also chose David his servant,"],[2,"and took him from the sheepfolds;"]]},{v:71,p:1,l:[[1,"from following the ewes that have their young,"],[2,"he brought him to be the shepherd of Jacob, his people,"],[2,"and Israel, his inheritance."]]},{v:72,p:1,l:[[1,"So he was their shepherd according to the integrity of his heart,"],[2,"and guided them by the skillfulness of his hands."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"God, the nations have come into your inheritance."],[2,"They have defiled your holy temple."],[2,"They have laid Jerusalem in heaps."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"They have given the dead bodies of your servants to be food for the birds of the sky,"],[2,"the flesh of your saints to the animals of the earth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They have shed their blood like water around Jerusalem."],[2,"There was no one to bury them."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"We have become a reproach to our neighbors,"],[2,"a scoffing and derision to those who are around us."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"How long, LORD?"],[2,"Will you be angry forever?"],[2,"Will your jealousy burn like fire?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Pour out your wrath on the nations that don\u2019t know you,"],[2,"on the kingdoms that don\u2019t call on your name,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"for they have devoured Jacob,"],[2,"and destroyed his homeland."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t hold the iniquities of our forefathers against us."],[2,"Let your tender mercies speedily meet us,"],[2,"for we are in desperate need."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Help us, God of our salvation, for the glory of your name."],[2,"Deliver us, and forgive our sins, for your name\u2019s sake."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Why should the nations say, \u201cWhere is their God?\u201d"],[2,"Let it be known among the nations, before our eyes,"],[2,"that vengeance for your servants\u2019 blood is being poured out."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the sighing of the prisoner come before you."],[2,"According to the greatness of your power, preserve those who are sentenced to death."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Pay back to our neighbors seven times into their bosom"],[2,"their reproach with which they have reproached you, Lord."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"So we, your people and sheep of your pasture,"],[2,"will give you thanks forever."],[2,"We will praise you forever, to all generations."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cThe Lilies of the Covenant.\u201d A Psalm by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear us, Shepherd of Israel,"],[2,"you who lead Joseph like a flock,"],[2,"you who sit above the cherubim, shine out."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Before Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh, stir up your might!"],[2,"Come to save us!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn us again, God."],[2,"Cause your face to shine,"],[2,"and we will be saved."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD God of Armies,"],[2,"how long will you be angry against the prayer of your people?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You have fed them with the bread of tears,"],[2,"and given them tears to drink in large measure."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You make us a source of contention to our neighbors."],[2,"Our enemies laugh among themselves."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn us again, God of Armies."],[2,"Cause your face to shine,"],[2,"and we will be saved."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You brought a vine out of Egypt."],[2,"You drove out the nations, and planted it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You cleared the ground for it."],[2,"It took deep root, and filled the land."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains were covered with its shadow."],[2,"Its boughs were like God\u2019s cedars."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"It sent out its branches to the sea,"],[2,"its shoots to the River."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Why have you broken down its walls,"],[2,"so that all those who pass by the way pluck it?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The boar out of the wood ravages it."],[2,"The wild animals of the field feed on it."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn again, we beg you, God of Armies."],[2,"Look down from heaven, and see, and visit this vine,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"the stock which your right hand planted,"],[2,"the branch that you made strong for yourself."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"It\u2019s burned with fire."],[2,"It\u2019s cut down."],[2,"They perish at your rebuke."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your hand be on the man of your right hand,"],[2,"on the son of man whom you made strong for yourself."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"So we will not turn away from you."],[2,"Revive us, and we will call on your name."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn us again, LORD God of Armies."],[2,"Cause your face to shine, and we will be saved."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. On an instrument of Gath. By Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"Sing aloud to God, our strength!"],[2,"Make a joyful shout to the God of Jacob!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Raise a song, and bring here the tambourine,"],[2,"the pleasant lyre with the harp."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Blow the trumpet at the New Moon,"],[2,"at the full moon, on our feast day."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For it is a statute for Israel,"],[2,"an ordinance of the God of Jacob."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He appointed it in Joseph for a covenant,"],[2,"when he went out over the land of Egypt,"],[2,"I heard a language that I didn\u2019t know."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI removed his shoulder from the burden."],[2,"His hands were freed from the basket."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You called in trouble, and I delivered you."],[2,"I answered you in the secret place of thunder."],[2,"I tested you at the waters of Meribah.\u201d Selah."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear, my people, and I will testify to you,"],[2,"Israel, if you would listen to me!"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"There shall be no strange god in you,"],[2,"neither shall you worship any foreign god."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I am the LORD, your God,"],[2,"who brought you up out of the land of Egypt."],[2,"Open your mouth wide, and I will fill it."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"But my people didn\u2019t listen to my voice."],[2,"Israel desired none of me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"So I let them go after the stubbornness of their hearts,"],[2,"that they might walk in their own counsels."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that my people would listen to me,"],[2,"that Israel would walk in my ways!"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I would soon subdue their enemies,"],[2,"and turn my hand against their adversaries."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The haters of the LORD would cringe before him,"],[2,"and their punishment would last forever."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"But he would have also fed them with the finest of the wheat."],[2,"I will satisfy you with honey out of the rock.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"God presides in the great assembly."],[2,"He judges among the gods."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow long will you judge unjustly,"],[2,"and show partiality to the wicked?\u201d Selah."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDefend the weak, the poor, and the fatherless."],[2,"Maintain the rights of the poor and oppressed."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Rescue the weak and needy."],[2,"Deliver them out of the hand of the wicked.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They don\u2019t know, neither do they understand."],[2,"They walk back and forth in darkness."],[2,"All the foundations of the earth are shaken."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cYou are gods,"],[2,"all of you are sons of the Most High."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Nevertheless you shall die like men,"],[2,"and fall like one of the rulers.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, God, judge the earth,"],[2,"for you inherit all of the nations."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A song. A Psalm by Asaph."],p:1,l:[[1,"God, don\u2019t keep silent."],[2,"Don\u2019t keep silent,"],[2,"and don\u2019t be still, God."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, your enemies are stirred up."],[2,"Those who hate you have lifted up their heads."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They conspire with cunning against your people."],[2,"They plot against your cherished ones."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCome,\u201d they say, \u201clet\u2019s destroy them as a nation,"],[2,"that the name of Israel may be remembered no more.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For they have conspired together with one mind."],[2,"They form an alliance against you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites;"],[2,"Moab, and the Hagrites;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Gebal, Ammon, and Amalek;"],[2,"Philistia with the inhabitants of Tyre;"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Assyria also is joined with them."],[2,"They have helped the children of Lot. Selah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Do to them as you did to Midian,"],[2,"as to Sisera, as to Jabin, at the river Kishon;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"who perished at Endor,"],[2,"who became as dung for the earth."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Make their nobles like Oreb and Zeeb,"],[2,"yes, all their princes like Zebah and Zalmunna,"]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"who said, \u201cLet\u2019s take possession of God\u2019s pasture lands.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"My God, make them like tumbleweed,"],[2,"like chaff before the wind."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"As the fire that burns the forest,"],[2,"as the flame that sets the mountains on fire,"]]},{v:15,l:[[2,"so pursue them with your tempest,"],[2,"and terrify them with your storm."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Fill their faces with confusion,"],[2,"that they may seek your name, LORD."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be disappointed and dismayed forever."],[2,"Yes, let them be confounded and perish;"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"that they may know that you alone, whose name is the LORD,"],[2,"are the Most High over all the earth."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. On an instrument of Gath. A Psalm by the sons of Korah."],p:1,l:[[1,"How lovely are your dwellings,"],[2,"LORD of Armies!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul longs, and even faints for the courts of the LORD."],[2,"My heart and my flesh cry out for the living God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, the sparrow has found a home,"],[2,"and the swallow a nest for herself, where she may have her young,"],[2,"near your altars, LORD of Armies, my King, and my God."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those who dwell in your house."],[2,"They are always praising you. Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those whose strength is in you,"],[2,"who have set their hearts on a pilgrimage."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Passing through the valley of Weeping, they make it a place of springs."],[2,"Yes, the autumn rain covers it with blessings."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They go from strength to strength."],[2,"Every one of them appears before God in Zion."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, God of Armies, hear my prayer."],[2,"Listen, God of Jacob. Selah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, God our shield,"],[2,"look at the face of your anointed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For a day in your courts is better than a thousand."],[2,"I would rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God,"],[2,"than to dwell in the tents of wickedness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD God is a sun and a shield."],[2,"The LORD will give grace and glory."],[2,"He withholds no good thing from those who walk blamelessly."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD of Armies,"],[2,"blessed is the man who trusts in you."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by the sons of Korah."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you have been favorable to your land."],[2,"You have restored the fortunes of Jacob."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You have forgiven the iniquity of your people."],[2,"You have covered all their sin. Selah."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You have taken away all your wrath."],[2,"You have turned from the fierceness of your anger."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn us, God of our salvation,"],[2,"and cause your indignation toward us to cease."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you be angry with us forever?"],[2,"Will you draw out your anger to all generations?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Won\u2019t you revive us again,"],[2,"that your people may rejoice in you?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Show us your loving kindness, LORD."],[2,"Grant us your salvation."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will hear what God, the LORD, will speak,"],[2,"for he will speak peace to his people, his saints;"],[2,"but let them not turn again to folly."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely his salvation is near those who fear him,"],[2,"that glory may dwell in our land."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Mercy and truth meet together."],[2,"Righteousness and peace have kissed each other."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Truth springs out of the earth."],[2,"Righteousness has looked down from heaven."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, the LORD will give that which is good."],[2,"Our land will yield its increase."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Righteousness goes before him,"],[2,"and prepares the way for his steps."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Prayer by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, LORD, and answer me,"],[2,"for I am poor and needy."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Preserve my soul, for I am godly."],[2,"You, my God, save your servant who trusts in you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Be merciful to me, Lord,"],[2,"for I call to you all day long."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Bring joy to the soul of your servant,"],[2,"for to you, Lord, do I lift up my soul."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For you, Lord, are good, and ready to forgive,"],[2,"abundant in loving kindness to all those who call on you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, LORD, my prayer."],[2,"Listen to the voice of my petitions."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"In the day of my trouble I will call on you,"],[2,"for you will answer me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no one like you among the gods, Lord,"],[2,"nor any deeds like your deeds."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"All nations you have made will come and worship before you, Lord."],[2,"They shall glorify your name."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are great, and do wondrous things."],[2,"You are God alone."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Teach me your way, LORD."],[2,"I will walk in your truth."],[2,"Make my heart undivided to fear your name."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will praise you, Lord my God, with my whole heart."],[2,"I will glorify your name forever more."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For your loving kindness is great toward me."],[2,"You have delivered my soul from the lowest Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"God, the proud have risen up against me."],[2,"A company of violent men have sought after my soul,"],[2,"and they don\u2019t hold regard for you before them."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, Lord, are a merciful and gracious God,"],[2,"slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness and truth."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn to me, and have mercy on me!"],[2,"Give your strength to your servant."],[2,"Save the son of your servant."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Show me a sign of your goodness,"],[2,"that those who hate me may see it, and be shamed,"],[2,"because you, LORD, have helped me, and comforted me."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by the sons of Korah; a Song."],p:1,l:[[1,"His foundation is in the holy mountains."]]},{v:2,l:[[2,"The LORD loves the gates of Zion more than all the dwellings of Jacob."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Glorious things are spoken about you, city of God. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will record Rahab and Babylon among those who acknowledge me."],[2,"Behold, Philistia, Tyre, and also Ethiopia:"],[2,"\u201cThis one was born there.\u201d"]],f:["Rahab is a reference to Egypt."]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, of Zion it will be said, \u201cThis one and that one was born in her;\u201d"],[2,"the Most High himself will establish her."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will count, when he writes up the peoples,"],[2,"\u201cThis one was born there.\u201d Selah."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who sing as well as those who dance say,"],[2,"\u201cAll my springs are in you.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song. A Psalm by the sons of Korah. For the Chief Musician. To the tune of \u201cThe Suffering of Affliction.\u201d A contemplation by Heman, the Ezrahite."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, the God of my salvation,"],[2,"I have cried day and night before you."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my prayer enter into your presence."],[2,"Turn your ear to my cry."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For my soul is full of troubles."],[2,"My life draws near to Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I am counted among those who go down into the pit."],[2,"I am like a man who has no help,"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"set apart among the dead,"],[2,"like the slain who lie in the grave,"],[2,"whom you remember no more."],[2,"They are cut off from your hand."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You have laid me in the lowest pit,"],[2,"in the darkest depths."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Your wrath lies heavily on me."],[2,"You have afflicted me with all your waves. Selah."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You have taken my friends from me."],[2,"You have made me an abomination to them."],[2,"I am confined, and I can\u2019t escape."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"My eyes are dim from grief."],[2,"I have called on you daily, LORD."],[2,"I have spread out my hands to you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you show wonders to the dead?"],[2,"Do the departed spirits rise up and praise you? Selah."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Is your loving kindness declared in the grave?"],[2,"Or your faithfulness in Destruction?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Are your wonders made known in the dark?"],[2,"Or your righteousness in the land of forgetfulness?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"But to you, LORD, I have cried."],[2,"In the morning, my prayer comes before you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, why do you reject my soul?"],[2,"Why do you hide your face from me?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I am afflicted and ready to die from my youth up."],[2,"While I suffer your terrors, I am distracted."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Your fierce wrath has gone over me."],[2,"Your terrors have cut me off."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"They came around me like water all day long."],[2,"They completely engulfed me."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"You have put lover and friend far from me,"],[2,"and my friends into darkness."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A contemplation by Ethan, the Ezrahite."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will sing of the loving kindness of the LORD forever."],[2,"With my mouth, I will make known your faithfulness to all generations."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I indeed declare, \u201cLove stands firm forever."],[2,"You established the heavens."],[2,"Your faithfulness is in them.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have made a covenant with my chosen one,"],[2,"I have sworn to David, my servant,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018I will establish your offspring forever,"],[2,"and build up your throne to all generations.\u2019\u201d Selah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The heavens will praise your wonders, LORD,"],[2,"your faithfulness also in the assembly of the holy ones."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For who in the skies can be compared to the LORD?"],[2,"Who among the sons of the heavenly beings is like the LORD,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"a very awesome God in the council of the holy ones,"],[2,"to be feared above all those who are around him?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, God of Armies, who is a mighty one, like you?"],[2,"LORD, your faithfulness is around you."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah.","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You rule the pride of the sea."],[2,"When its waves rise up, you calm them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You have broken Rahab in pieces, like one of the slain."],[2,"You have scattered your enemies with your mighty arm."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The heavens are yours."],[2,"The earth also is yours,"],[2,"the world and its fullness."],[2,"You have founded them."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You have created the north and the south."],[2,"Tabor and Hermon rejoice in your name."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You have a mighty arm."],[2,"Your hand is strong, and your right hand is exalted."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Righteousness and justice are the foundation of your throne."],[2,"Loving kindness and truth go before your face."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are the people who learn to acclaim you."],[2,"They walk in the light of your presence, LORD."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"In your name they rejoice all day."],[2,"In your righteousness, they are exalted."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are the glory of their strength."],[2,"In your favor, our horn will be exalted."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For our shield belongs to the LORD,"],[2,"our king to the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Then you spoke in vision to your saints,"],[2,"and said, \u201cI have given strength to the warrior."],[2,"I have exalted a young man from the people."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"I have found David, my servant."],[2,"I have anointed him with my holy oil,"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"with whom my hand shall be established."],[2,"My arm will also strengthen him."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"No enemy will tax him."],[2,"No wicked man will oppress him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I will beat down his adversaries before him,"],[2,"and strike those who hate him."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"But my faithfulness and my loving kindness will be with him."],[2,"In my name, his horn will be exalted."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"I will set his hand also on the sea,"],[2,"and his right hand on the rivers."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"He will call to me, \u2018You are my Father,"],[2,"my God, and the rock of my salvation!\u2019"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also appoint him my firstborn,"],[2,"the highest of the kings of the earth."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"I will keep my loving kindness for him forever more."],[2,"My covenant will stand firm with him."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also make his offspring endure forever,"],[2,"and his throne as the days of heaven."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"If his children forsake my law,"],[2,"and don\u2019t walk in my ordinances;"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"if they break my statutes,"],[2,"and don\u2019t keep my commandments;"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"then I will punish their sin with the rod,"],[2,"and their iniquity with stripes."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"But I will not completely take my loving kindness from him,"],[2,"nor allow my faithfulness to fail."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"I will not break my covenant,"],[2,"nor alter what my lips have uttered."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"Once I have sworn by my holiness,"],[2,"I will not lie to David."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"His offspring will endure forever,"],[2,"his throne like the sun before me."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"It will be established forever like the moon,"],[2,"the faithful witness in the sky.\u201d Selah."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"But you have rejected and spurned."],[2,"You have been angry with your anointed."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"You have renounced the covenant of your servant."],[2,"You have defiled his crown in the dust."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"You have broken down all his hedges."],[2,"You have brought his strongholds to ruin."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"All who pass by the way rob him."],[1,"He has become a reproach to his neighbors."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"You have exalted the right hand of his adversaries."],[2,"You have made all of his enemies rejoice."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, you turn back the edge of his sword,"],[2,"and haven\u2019t supported him in battle."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"You have ended his splendor,"],[2,"and thrown his throne down to the ground."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"You have shortened the days of his youth."],[2,"You have covered him with shame. Selah."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"How long, LORD?"],[2,"Will you hide yourself forever?"],[2,"Will your wrath burn like fire?"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember how short my time is,"],[2,"for what vanity you have created all the children of men!"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[1,"What man is he who shall live and not see death,"],[2,"who shall deliver his soul from the power of Sheol? Selah."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, where are your former loving kindnesses,"],[2,"which you swore to David in your faithfulness?"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember, Lord, the reproach of your servants,"],[2,"how I bear in my heart the taunts of all the mighty peoples,"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[1,"With which your enemies have mocked, LORD,"],[2,"with which they have mocked the footsteps of your anointed one."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD forever more."],[1,"Amen, and Amen."]]}],[{v:1,h:["BOOK 4","A Prayer by Moses, the man of God."],p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, you have been our dwelling place for all generations."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[2,"Before the mountains were born,"],[2,"before you had formed the earth and the world,"],[2,"even from everlasting to everlasting, you are God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You turn man to destruction, saying,"],[2,"\u201cReturn, you children of men.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For a thousand years in your sight are just like yesterday when it is past,"],[2,"like a watch in the night."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You sweep them away as they sleep."],[2,"In the morning they sprout like new grass."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"In the morning it sprouts and springs up."],[2,"By evening, it is withered and dry."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For we are consumed in your anger."],[2,"We are troubled in your wrath."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You have set our iniquities before you,"],[2,"our secret sins in the light of your presence."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For all our days have passed away in your wrath."],[2,"We bring our years to an end as a sigh."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The days of our years are seventy,"],[2,"or even by reason of strength eighty years;"],[2,"yet their pride is but labor and sorrow,"],[2,"for it passes quickly, and we fly away."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Who knows the power of your anger,"],[2,"your wrath according to the fear that is due to you?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"So teach us to count our days,"],[2,"that we may gain a heart of wisdom."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Relent, LORD!"],[2,"How long?"],[2,"Have compassion on your servants!"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Satisfy us in the morning with your loving kindness,"],[2,"that we may rejoice and be glad all our days."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Make us glad for as many days as you have afflicted us,"],[2,"for as many years as we have seen evil."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your work appear to your servants,"],[2,"your glory to their children."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the favor of the Lord our God be on us."],[2,"Establish the work of our hands for us."],[2,"Yes, establish the work of our hands."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"He who dwells in the secret place of the Most High"],[2,"will rest in the shadow of the Almighty."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will say of the LORD, \u201cHe is my refuge and my fortress;"],[2,"my God, in whom I trust.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For he will deliver you from the snare of the fowler,"],[2,"and from the deadly pestilence."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He will cover you with his feathers."],[2,"Under his wings you will take refuge."],[2,"His faithfulness is your shield and rampart."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You shall not be afraid of the terror by night,"],[2,"nor of the arrow that flies by day,"]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"nor of the pestilence that walks in darkness,"],[2,"nor of the destruction that wastes at noonday."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"A thousand may fall at your side,"],[2,"and ten thousand at your right hand;"],[2,"but it will not come near you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You will only look with your eyes,"],[2,"and see the recompense of the wicked."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Because you have made the LORD your refuge,"],[2,"and the Most High your dwelling place,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"no evil shall happen to you,"],[2,"neither shall any plague come near your dwelling."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For he will put his angels in charge of you,"],[2,"to guard you in all your ways."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They will bear you up in their hands,"],[2,"so that you won\u2019t dash your foot against a stone."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You will tread on the lion and cobra."],[2,"You will trample the young lion and the serpent underfoot."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBecause he has set his love on me, therefore I will deliver him."],[2,"I will set him on high, because he has known my name."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He will call on me, and I will answer him."],[2,"I will be with him in trouble."],[2,"I will deliver him, and honor him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I will satisfy him with long life,"],[2,"and show him my salvation.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm. A song for the Sabbath day."],p:1,l:[[1,"It is a good thing to give thanks to the LORD,"],[2,"to sing praises to your name, Most High,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"to proclaim your loving kindness in the morning,"],[2,"and your faithfulness every night,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"with the ten-stringed lute, with the harp,"],[2,"and with the melody of the lyre."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For you, LORD, have made me glad through your work."],[2,"I will triumph in the works of your hands."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"How great are your works, LORD!"],[2,"Your thoughts are very deep."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"A senseless man doesn\u2019t know,"],[2,"neither does a fool understand this:"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"though the wicked spring up as the grass,"],[2,"and all the evildoers flourish,"],[2,"they will be destroyed forever."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, LORD, are on high forever more."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For behold, your enemies, LORD,"],[2,"for behold, your enemies shall perish."],[2,"All the evildoers will be scattered."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But you have exalted my horn like that of the wild ox."],[2,"I am anointed with fresh oil."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"My eye has also seen my enemies."],[2,"My ears have heard of the wicked enemies who rise up against me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous shall flourish like the palm tree."],[2,"He will grow like a cedar in Lebanon."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They are planted in the LORD\u2019s house."],[2,"They will flourish in our God\u2019s courts."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They will still produce fruit in old age."],[2,"They will be full of sap and green,"]]},{v:15,l:[[2,"to show that the LORD is upright."],[1,"He is my rock,"],[2,"and there is no unrighteousness in him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD reigns!"],[2,"He is clothed with majesty!"],[2,"The LORD is armed with strength."],[1,"The world also is established."],[2,"It can\u2019t be moved."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Your throne is established from long ago."],[2,"You are from everlasting."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The floods have lifted up, LORD,"],[2,"the floods have lifted up their voice."],[2,"The floods lift up their waves."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Above the voices of many waters,"],[2,"the mighty breakers of the sea,"],[2,"the LORD on high is mighty."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Your statutes stand firm."],[2,"Holiness adorns your house,"],[2,"LORD, forever more."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you God to whom vengeance belongs,"],[2,"you God to whom vengeance belongs, shine out."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Rise up, you judge of the earth."],[2,"Pay back the proud what they deserve."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, how long will the wicked,"],[2,"how long will the wicked triumph?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They pour out arrogant words."],[2,"All the evildoers boast."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They break your people in pieces, LORD,"],[2,"and afflict your heritage."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They kill the widow and the alien,"],[2,"and murder the fatherless."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They say, \u201cThe LORD will not see,"],[2,"neither will Jacob\u2019s God consider.\u201d"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Consider, you senseless among the people;"],[2,"you fools, when will you be wise?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He who implanted the ear, won\u2019t he hear?"],[2,"He who formed the eye, won\u2019t he see?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He who disciplines the nations, won\u2019t he punish?"],[2,"He who teaches man knows."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD knows the thoughts of man,"],[2,"that they are futile."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man whom you discipline, LORD,"],[2,"and teach out of your law,"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"that you may give him rest from the days of adversity,"],[2,"until the pit is dug for the wicked."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD won\u2019t reject his people,"],[2,"neither will he forsake his inheritance."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"For judgment will return to righteousness."],[2,"All the upright in heart shall follow it."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Who will rise up for me against the wicked?"],[2,"Who will stand up for me against the evildoers?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Unless the LORD had been my help,"],[2,"my soul would have soon lived in silence."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"When I said, \u201cMy foot is slipping!\u201d"],[2,"Your loving kindness, LORD, held me up."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"In the multitude of my thoughts within me,"],[2,"your comforts delight my soul."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall the throne of wickedness have fellowship with you,"],[2,"which brings about mischief by statute?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"They gather themselves together against the soul of the righteous,"],[2,"and condemn the innocent blood."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"But the LORD has been my high tower,"],[2,"my God, the rock of my refuge."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"He has brought on them their own iniquity,"],[2,"and will cut them off in their own wickedness."],[2,"The LORD, our God, will cut them off."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh come, let\u2019s sing to the LORD."],[2,"Let\u2019s shout aloud to the rock of our salvation!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let\u2019s come before his presence with thanksgiving."],[2,"Let\u2019s extol him with songs!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD is a great God,"],[2,"a great King above all gods."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"In his hand are the deep places of the earth."],[2,"The heights of the mountains are also his."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The sea is his, and he made it."],[2,"His hands formed the dry land."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh come, let\u2019s worship and bow down."],[2,"Let\u2019s kneel before the LORD, our Maker,"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"for he is our God."],[1,"We are the people of his pasture,"],[2,"and the sheep in his care."],[1,"Today, oh that you would hear his voice!"]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"Don\u2019t harden your heart, as at Meribah,"],[2,"as in the day of Massah in the wilderness,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"when your fathers tempted me,"],[2,"tested me, and saw my work."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Forty long years I was grieved with that generation,"],[2,"and said, \u201cThey are a people who err in their heart."],[2,"They have not known my ways.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I swore in my wrath,"],[2,"\u201cThey won\u2019t enter into my rest.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to the LORD a new song!"],[2,"Sing to the LORD, all the earth."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to the LORD!"],[2,"Bless his name!"],[2,"Proclaim his salvation from day to day!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Declare his glory among the nations,"],[2,"his marvelous works among all the peoples."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD is great, and greatly to be praised!"],[2,"He is to be feared above all gods."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For all the gods of the peoples are idols,"],[2,"but the LORD made the heavens."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Honor and majesty are before him."],[2,"Strength and beauty are in his sanctuary."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Ascribe to the LORD, you families of nations,"],[2,"ascribe to the LORD glory and strength."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his name."],[2,"Bring an offering, and come into his courts."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Worship the LORD in holy array."],[2,"Tremble before him, all the earth."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Say among the nations, \u201cThe LORD reigns.\u201d"],[2,"The world is also established."],[2,"It can\u2019t be moved."],[2,"He will judge the peoples with equity."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth rejoice."],[2,"Let the sea roar, and its fullness!"]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"Let the field and all that is in it exult!"],[2,"Then all the trees of the woods shall sing for joy"]]},{v:13,l:[[2,"before the LORD; for he comes,"],[2,"for he comes to judge the earth."],[1,"He will judge the world with righteousness,"],[2,"the peoples with his truth."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD reigns!"],[2,"Let the earth rejoice!"],[2,"Let the multitude of islands be glad!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Clouds and darkness are around him."],[2,"Righteousness and justice are the foundation of his throne."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A fire goes before him,"],[2,"and burns up his adversaries on every side."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"His lightning lights up the world."],[2,"The earth sees, and trembles."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains melt like wax at the presence of the LORD,"],[2,"at the presence of the Lord of the whole earth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The heavens declare his righteousness."],[2,"All the peoples have seen his glory."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Let all them be shamed who serve engraved images,"],[2,"who boast in their idols."],[2,"Worship him, all you gods!"]],f:["LXX reads \u201cangels\u201d instead of \u201cgods\u201d."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Zion heard and was glad."],[2,"The daughters of Judah rejoiced"],[2,"because of your judgments, LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For you, LORD, are most high above all the earth."],[2,"You are exalted far above all gods."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You who love the LORD, hate evil!"],[2,"He preserves the souls of his saints."],[2,"He delivers them out of the hand of the wicked."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Light is sown for the righteous,"],[2,"and gladness for the upright in heart."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Be glad in the LORD, you righteous people!"],[2,"Give thanks to his holy Name."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm."],p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to the LORD a new song,"],[2,"for he has done marvelous things!"],[2,"His right hand and his holy arm have worked salvation for him."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has made known his salvation."],[2,"He has openly shown his righteousness in the sight of the nations."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He has remembered his loving kindness and his faithfulness toward the house of Israel."],[2,"All the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Make a joyful noise to the LORD, all the earth!"],[2,"Burst out and sing for joy, yes, sing praises!"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing praises to the LORD with the harp,"],[2,"with the harp and the voice of melody."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"With trumpets and sound of the ram\u2019s horn,"],[2,"make a joyful noise before the King, the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the sea roar with its fullness;"],[2,"the world, and those who dwell therein."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the rivers clap their hands."],[2,"Let the mountains sing for joy together."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them sing before the LORD,"],[2,"for he comes to judge the earth."],[1,"He will judge the world with righteousness,"],[2,"and the peoples with equity."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD reigns! Let the peoples tremble."],[2,"He sits enthroned among the cherubim."],[2,"Let the earth be moved."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is great in Zion."],[2,"He is high above all the peoples."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise your great and awesome name."],[2,"He is Holy!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The King\u2019s strength also loves justice."],[2,"You establish equity."],[2,"You execute justice and righteousness in Jacob."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Exalt the LORD our God."],[2,"Worship at his footstool."],[2,"He is Holy!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Moses and Aaron were among his priests,"],[2,"Samuel was among those who call on his name."],[2,"They called on the LORD, and he answered them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He spoke to them in the pillar of cloud."],[2,"They kept his testimonies,"],[2,"the statute that he gave them."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You answered them, LORD our God."],[2,"You are a God who forgave them,"],[2,"although you took vengeance for their doings."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Exalt the LORD, our God."],[2,"Worship at his holy hill,"],[2,"for the LORD, our God, is holy!"]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm of thanksgiving."],p:1,l:[[1,"Shout for joy to the LORD, all you lands!"]]},{v:2,l:[[2,"Serve the LORD with gladness."],[2,"Come before his presence with singing."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Know that the LORD, he is God."],[2,"It is he who has made us, and we are his."],[2,"We are his people, and the sheep of his pasture."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Enter into his gates with thanksgiving,"],[2,"and into his courts with praise."],[2,"Give thanks to him, and bless his name."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD is good."],[2,"His loving kindness endures forever,"],[2,"his faithfulness to all generations."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will sing of loving kindness and justice."],[2,"To you, LORD, I will sing praises."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will be careful to live a blameless life."],[2,"When will you come to me?"],[2,"I will walk within my house with a blameless heart."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I will set no vile thing before my eyes."],[2,"I hate the deeds of faithless men."],[2,"They will not cling to me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"A perverse heart will be far from me."],[2,"I will have nothing to do with evil."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I will silence whoever secretly slanders his neighbor."],[2,"I won\u2019t tolerate one who is arrogant and conceited."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My eyes will be on the faithful of the land,"],[2,"that they may dwell with me."],[1,"He who walks in a perfect way,"],[2,"he will serve me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He who practices deceit won\u2019t dwell within my house."],[2,"He who speaks falsehood won\u2019t be established before my eyes."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Morning by morning, I will destroy all the wicked of the land,"],[2,"to cut off all the workers of iniquity from the LORD\u2019s city."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Prayer of the afflicted, when he is overwhelmed and pours out his complaint before the LORD."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear my prayer, LORD!"],[2,"Let my cry come to you."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t hide your face from me in the day of my distress."],[2,"Turn your ear to me."],[2,"Answer me quickly in the day when I call."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For my days consume away like smoke."],[2,"My bones are burned as a torch."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"My heart is blighted like grass, and withered,"],[2,"for I forget to eat my bread."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"By reason of the voice of my groaning,"],[2,"my bones stick to my skin."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I am like a pelican of the wilderness."],[2,"I have become as an owl of the waste places."]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"I watch, and have become like a sparrow that is alone on the housetop."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"My enemies reproach me all day."],[2,"Those who are mad at me use my name as a curse."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For I have eaten ashes like bread,"],[2,"and mixed my drink with tears,"]]},{v:10,l:[[2,"because of your indignation and your wrath;"],[2,"for you have taken me up and thrown me away."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"My days are like a long shadow."],[2,"I have withered like grass."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, LORD, will remain forever;"],[2,"your renown endures to all generations."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You will arise and have mercy on Zion,"],[2,"for it is time to have pity on her."],[2,"Yes, the set time has come."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For your servants take pleasure in her stones,"],[2,"and have pity on her dust."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"So the nations will fear the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"all the kings of the earth your glory."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD has built up Zion."],[2,"He has appeared in his glory."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He has responded to the prayer of the destitute,"],[2,"and has not despised their prayer."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"This will be written for the generation to come."],[2,"A people which will be created will praise the LORD,"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"for he has looked down from the height of his sanctuary."],[2,"From heaven, the LORD saw the earth,"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"to hear the groans of the prisoner,"],[2,"to free those who are condemned to death,"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"that men may declare the LORD\u2019s name in Zion,"],[2,"and his praise in Jerusalem,"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"when the peoples are gathered together,"],[2,"the kingdoms, to serve the LORD."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"He weakened my strength along the course."],[2,"He shortened my days."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cMy God, don\u2019t take me away in the middle of my days."],[2,"Your years are throughout all generations."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Of old, you laid the foundation of the earth."],[2,"The heavens are the work of your hands."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"They will perish, but you will endure."],[2,"Yes, all of them will wear out like a garment."],[2,"You will change them like a cloak, and they will be changed."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"But you are the same."],[2,"Your years will have no end."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of your servants will continue."],[2,"Their offspring will be established before you.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, my soul!"],[2,"All that is within me, praise his holy name!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, my soul,"],[2,"and don\u2019t forget all his benefits,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"who forgives all your sins,"],[2,"who heals all your diseases,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"who redeems your life from destruction,"],[2,"who crowns you with loving kindness and tender mercies,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"who satisfies your desire with good things,"],[2,"so that your youth is renewed like the eagle\u2019s."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD executes righteous acts,"],[2,"and justice for all who are oppressed."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He made known his ways to Moses,"],[2,"his deeds to the children of Israel."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is merciful and gracious,"],[2,"slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not always accuse;"],[2,"neither will he stay angry forever."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He has not dealt with us according to our sins,"],[2,"nor repaid us for our iniquities."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For as the heavens are high above the earth,"],[2,"so great is his loving kindness toward those who fear him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"As far as the east is from the west,"],[2,"so far has he removed our transgressions from us."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Like a father has compassion on his children,"],[2,"so the LORD has compassion on those who fear him."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For he knows how we are made."],[2,"He remembers that we are dust."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"As for man, his days are like grass."],[2,"As a flower of the field, so he flourishes."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For the wind passes over it, and it is gone."],[2,"Its place remembers it no more."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"But the LORD\u2019s loving kindness is from everlasting to everlasting with those who fear him,"],[2,"his righteousness to children\u2019s children,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"to those who keep his covenant,"],[2,"to those who remember to obey his precepts."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has established his throne in the heavens."],[2,"His kingdom rules over all."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, you angels of his,"],[2,"who are mighty in strength, who fulfill his word,"],[2,"obeying the voice of his word."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, all you armies of his,"],[2,"you servants of his, who do his pleasure."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, all you works of his,"],[2,"in all places of his dominion."],[2,"Praise the LORD, my soul!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Bless the LORD, my soul."],[2,"The LORD, my God, you are very great."],[2,"You are clothed with honor and majesty."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He covers himself with light as with a garment."],[2,"He stretches out the heavens like a curtain."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He lays the beams of his rooms in the waters."],[2,"He makes the clouds his chariot."],[2,"He walks on the wings of the wind."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes his messengers winds,"],[2,"and his servants flames of fire."]],f:["or, angels"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He laid the foundations of the earth,"],[2,"that it should not be moved forever."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You covered it with the deep as with a cloak."],[2,"The waters stood above the mountains."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"At your rebuke they fled."],[2,"At the voice of your thunder they hurried away."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains rose,"],[2,"the valleys sank down,"],[2,"to the place which you had assigned to them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You have set a boundary that they may not pass over,"],[2,"that they don\u2019t turn again to cover the earth."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He sends springs into the valleys."],[2,"They run among the mountains."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They give drink to every animal of the field."],[2,"The wild donkeys quench their thirst."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The birds of the sky nest by them."],[2,"They sing among the branches."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He waters the mountains from his rooms."],[2,"The earth is filled with the fruit of your works."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He causes the grass to grow for the livestock,"],[2,"and plants for man to cultivate,"],[2,"that he may produce food out of the earth:"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"wine that makes the heart of man glad,"],[2,"oil to make his face to shine,"],[2,"and bread that strengthens man\u2019s heart."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s trees are well watered,"],[2,"the cedars of Lebanon, which he has planted,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"where the birds make their nests."],[2,"The stork makes its home in the cypress trees."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The high mountains are for the wild goats."],[2,"The rocks are a refuge for the rock badgers."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He appointed the moon for seasons."],[2,"The sun knows when to set."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"You make darkness, and it is night,"],[2,"in which all the animals of the forest prowl."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The young lions roar after their prey,"],[2,"and seek their food from God."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The sun rises, and they steal away,"],[2,"and lie down in their dens."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Man goes out to his work,"],[2,"to his labor until the evening."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, how many are your works!"],[2,"In wisdom, you have made them all."],[2,"The earth is full of your riches."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"There is the sea, great and wide,"],[2,"in which are innumerable living things,"],[2,"both small and large animals."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"There the ships go,"],[2,"and leviathan, whom you formed to play there."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"These all wait for you,"],[2,"that you may give them their food in due season."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"You give to them; they gather."],[2,"You open your hand; they are satisfied with good."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"You hide your face; they are troubled."],[2,"You take away their breath; they die and return to the dust."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"You send out your Spirit and they are created."],[2,"You renew the face of the ground."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the LORD\u2019s glory endure forever."],[2,"Let the LORD rejoice in his works."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"He looks at the earth, and it trembles."],[2,"He touches the mountains, and they smoke."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"I will sing to the LORD as long as I live."],[2,"I will sing praise to my God while I have any being."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my meditation be sweet to him."],[2,"I will rejoice in the LORD."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"Let sinners be consumed out of the earth."],[2,"Let the wicked be no more."],[2,"Bless the LORD, my soul."],[2,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah.","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Give thanks to the LORD! Call on his name!"],[2,"Make his doings known among the peoples."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to him, sing praises to him!"],[2,"Tell of all his marvelous works."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Glory in his holy name."],[2,"Let the heart of those who seek the LORD rejoice."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Seek the LORD and his strength."],[2,"Seek his face forever more."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember his marvelous works that he has done:"],[2,"his wonders, and the judgments of his mouth,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"you offspring of Abraham, his servant,"],[2,"you children of Jacob, his chosen ones."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He is the LORD, our God."],[2,"His judgments are in all the earth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He has remembered his covenant forever,"],[2,"the word which he commanded to a thousand generations,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"the covenant which he made with Abraham,"],[2,"his oath to Isaac,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"and confirmed it to Jacob for a statute;"],[2,"to Israel for an everlasting covenant,"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"saying, \u201cTo you I will give the land of Canaan,"],[2,"the lot of your inheritance,\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"when they were but a few men in number,"],[2,"yes, very few, and foreigners in it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They went about from nation to nation,"],[2,"from one kingdom to another people."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He allowed no one to do them wrong."],[2,"Yes, he reproved kings for their sakes,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t touch my anointed ones!"],[2,"Do my prophets no harm!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He called for a famine on the land."],[2,"He destroyed the food supplies."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent a man before them."],[2,"Joseph was sold for a slave."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"They bruised his feet with shackles."],[2,"His neck was locked in irons,"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"until the time that his word happened,"],[2,"and the LORD\u2019s word proved him true."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The king sent and freed him,"],[2,"even the ruler of peoples, and let him go free."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He made him lord of his house,"],[2,"and ruler of all of his possessions,"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"to discipline his princes at his pleasure,"],[2,"and to teach his elders wisdom."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel also came into Egypt."],[2,"Jacob lived in the land of Ham."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"He increased his people greatly,"],[2,"and made them stronger than their adversaries."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"He turned their heart to hate his people,"],[2,"to conspire against his servants."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent Moses, his servant,"],[2,"and Aaron, whom he had chosen."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"They performed miracles among them,"],[2,"and wonders in the land of Ham."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent darkness, and made it dark."],[2,"They didn\u2019t rebel against his words."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"He turned their waters into blood,"],[2,"and killed their fish."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Their land swarmed with frogs,"],[2,"even in the rooms of their kings."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"He spoke, and swarms of flies came,"],[2,"and lice in all their borders."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"He gave them hail for rain,"],[2,"with lightning in their land."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"He struck their vines and also their fig trees,"],[2,"and shattered the trees of their country."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"He spoke, and the locusts came"],[2,"with the grasshoppers, without number."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"They ate up every plant in their land,"],[2,"and ate up the fruit of their ground."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"He struck also all the firstborn in their land,"],[2,"the first fruits of all their manhood."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought them out with silver and gold."],[2,"There was not one feeble person among his tribes."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"Egypt was glad when they departed,"],[2,"for the fear of them had fallen on them."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"He spread a cloud for a covering,"],[2,"fire to give light in the night."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"They asked, and he brought quails,"],[2,"and satisfied them with the bread of the sky."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"He opened the rock, and waters gushed out."],[2,"They ran as a river in the dry places."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"For he remembered his holy word,"],[2,"and Abraham, his servant."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought his people out with joy,"],[2,"his chosen with singing."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"He gave them the lands of the nations."],[2,"They took the labor of the peoples in possession,"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"that they might keep his statutes,"],[2,"and observe his laws."],[2,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD,"],[2,"or fully declare all his praise?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those who keep justice."],[2,"Blessed is one who does what is right at all times."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember me, LORD, with the favor that you show to your people."],[2,"Visit me with your salvation,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"that I may see the prosperity of your chosen,"],[2,"that I may rejoice in the gladness of your nation,"],[2,"that I may glory with your inheritance."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"We have sinned with our fathers."],[2,"We have committed iniquity."],[2,"We have done wickedly."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Our fathers didn\u2019t understand your wonders in Egypt."],[2,"They didn\u2019t remember the multitude of your loving kindnesses,"],[2,"but were rebellious at the sea, even at the Red Sea."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Nevertheless he saved them for his name\u2019s sake,"],[2,"that he might make his mighty power known."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He rebuked the Red Sea also, and it was dried up;"],[2,"so he led them through the depths, as through a desert."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He saved them from the hand of him who hated them,"],[2,"and redeemed them from the hand of the enemy."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The waters covered their adversaries."],[2,"There was not one of them left."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they believed his words."],[2,"They sang his praise."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They soon forgot his works."],[2,"They didn\u2019t wait for his counsel,"]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"but gave in to craving in the desert,"],[2,"and tested God in the wasteland."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He gave them their request,"],[2,"but sent leanness into their soul."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"They envied Moses also in the camp,"],[2,"and Aaron, the LORD\u2019s saint."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan,"],[2,"and covered the company of Abiram."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"A fire was kindled in their company."],[2,"The flame burned up the wicked."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"They made a calf in Horeb,"],[2,"and worshiped a molten image."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Thus they exchanged their glory"],[2,"for an image of a bull that eats grass."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"They forgot God, their Savior,"],[2,"who had done great things in Egypt,"]]},{v:22,l:[[2,"wondrous works in the land of Ham,"],[2,"and awesome things by the Red Sea."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore he said that he would destroy them,"],[2,"had Moses, his chosen, not stood before him in the breach,"],[2,"to turn away his wrath, so that he wouldn\u2019t destroy them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, they despised the pleasant land."],[2,"They didn\u2019t believe his word,"]]},{v:25,l:[[2,"but murmured in their tents,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t listen to the LORD\u2019s voice."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore he swore to them"],[2,"that he would overthrow them in the wilderness,"]]},{v:27,l:[[2,"that he would overthrow their offspring among the nations,"],[2,"and scatter them in the lands."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"They joined themselves also to Baal Peor,"],[2,"and ate the sacrifices of the dead."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Thus they provoked him to anger with their deeds."],[2,"The plague broke in on them."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Then Phinehas stood up and executed judgment,"],[2,"so the plague was stopped."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"That was credited to him for righteousness,"],[2,"for all generations to come."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"They angered him also at the waters of Meribah,"],[2,"so that Moses was troubled for their sakes;"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"because they were rebellious against his spirit,"],[2,"he spoke rashly with his lips."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"They didn\u2019t destroy the peoples,"],[2,"as the LORD commanded them,"]]},{v:35,l:[[2,"but mixed themselves with the nations,"],[2,"and learned their works."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"They served their idols,"],[2,"which became a snare to them."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, they sacrificed their sons and their daughters to demons."]]},{v:38,l:[[2,"They shed innocent blood,"],[2,"even the blood of their sons and of their daughters,"],[2,"whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan."],[2,"The land was polluted with blood."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"Thus they were defiled with their works,"],[2,"and prostituted themselves in their deeds."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD burned with anger against his people."],[2,"He abhorred his inheritance."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"He gave them into the hand of the nations."],[2,"Those who hated them ruled over them."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"Their enemies also oppressed them."],[2,"They were brought into subjection under their hand."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"He rescued them many times,"],[2,"but they were rebellious in their counsel,"],[2,"and were brought low in their iniquity."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"Nevertheless he regarded their distress,"],[2,"when he heard their cry."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"He remembered for them his covenant,"],[2,"and repented according to the multitude of his loving kindnesses."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"He made them also to be pitied"],[2,"by all those who carried them captive."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"Save us, LORD, our God,"],[2,"gather us from among the nations,"],[2,"to give thanks to your holy name,"],[2,"to triumph in your praise!"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel,"],[2,"from everlasting even to everlasting!"],[1,"Let all the people say, \u201cAmen.\u201d"],[2,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,h:["BOOK 5"],p:1,l:[[1,"Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the redeemed by the LORD say so,"],[2,"whom he has redeemed from the hand of the adversary,"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"and gathered out of the lands,"],[2,"from the east and from the west,"],[2,"from the north and from the south."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They wandered in the wilderness in a desert way."],[2,"They found no city to live in."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Hungry and thirsty,"],[2,"their soul fainted in them."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they cried to the LORD in their trouble,"],[2,"and he delivered them out of their distresses."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He led them also by a straight way,"],[2,"that they might go to a city to live in."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness,"],[2,"for his wonderful deeds to the children of men!"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For he satisfies the longing soul."],[2,"He fills the hungry soul with good."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Some sat in darkness and in the shadow of death,"],[2,"being bound in affliction and iron,"]]},{v:11,l:[[2,"because they rebelled against the words of God,"],[2,"and condemned the counsel of the Most High."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore he brought down their heart with labor."],[2,"They fell down, and there was no one to help."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they cried to the LORD in their trouble,"],[2,"and he saved them out of their distresses."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought them out of darkness and the shadow of death,"],[2,"and broke away their chains."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness,"],[2,"for his wonderful deeds to the children of men!"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has broken the gates of bronze,"],[2,"and cut through bars of iron."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Fools are afflicted because of their disobedience,"],[2,"and because of their iniquities."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Their soul abhors all kinds of food."],[2,"They draw near to the gates of death."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they cry to the LORD in their trouble,"],[2,"and he saves them out of their distresses."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He sends his word, and heals them,"],[2,"and delivers them from their graves."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness,"],[2,"for his wonderful deeds to the children of men!"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them offer the sacrifices of thanksgiving,"],[2,"and declare his deeds with singing."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who go down to the sea in ships,"],[2,"who do business in great waters,"]]},{v:24,l:[[2,"these see the LORD\u2019s deeds,"],[2,"and his wonders in the deep."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"For he commands, and raises the stormy wind,"],[2,"which lifts up its waves."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"They mount up to the sky; they go down again to the depths."],[2,"Their soul melts away because of trouble."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"They reel back and forth, and stagger like a drunken man,"],[2,"and are at their wits\u2019 end."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they cry to the LORD in their trouble,"],[2,"and he brings them out of their distress."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes the storm a calm,"],[2,"so that its waves are still."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they are glad because it is calm,"],[2,"so he brings them to their desired haven."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise the LORD for his loving kindness,"],[2,"for his wonderful deeds for the children of men!"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them exalt him also in the assembly of the people,"],[2,"and praise him in the seat of the elders."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"He turns rivers into a desert,"],[2,"water springs into a thirsty ground,"]]},{v:34,l:[[2,"and a fruitful land into a salt waste,"],[2,"for the wickedness of those who dwell in it."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"He turns a desert into a pool of water,"],[2,"and a dry land into water springs."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"There he makes the hungry live,"],[2,"that they may prepare a city to live in,"]]},{v:37,l:[[2,"sow fields, plant vineyards,"],[2,"and reap the fruits of increase."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"He blesses them also, so that they are multiplied greatly."],[2,"He doesn\u2019t allow their livestock to decrease."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"Again, they are diminished and bowed down"],[2,"through oppression, trouble, and sorrow."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"He pours contempt on princes,"],[2,"and causes them to wander in a trackless waste."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet he lifts the needy out of their affliction,"],[2,"and increases their families like a flock."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"The upright will see it, and be glad."],[2,"All the wicked will shut their mouths."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever is wise will pay attention to these things."],[2,"They will consider the loving kindnesses of the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"My heart is steadfast, God."],[2,"I will sing and I will make music with my soul."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Wake up, harp and lyre!"],[2,"I will wake up the dawn."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give thanks to you, LORD, among the nations."],[2,"I will sing praises to you among the peoples."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For your loving kindness is great above the heavens."],[2,"Your faithfulness reaches to the skies."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Be exalted, God, above the heavens!"],[2,"Let your glory be over all the earth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"That your beloved may be delivered,"],[2,"save with your right hand, and answer us."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"God has spoken from his sanctuary: \u201cIn triumph,"],[2,"I will divide Shechem, and measure out the valley of Succoth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Gilead is mine. Manasseh is mine."],[2,"Ephraim also is my helmet."],[2,"Judah is my scepter."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Moab is my wash pot."],[2,"I will toss my sandal on Edom."],[2,"I will shout over Philistia.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Who will bring me into the fortified city?"],[2,"Who will lead me to Edom?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Haven\u2019t you rejected us, God?"],[2,"You don\u2019t go out, God, with our armies."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Give us help against the enemy,"],[2,"for the help of man is vain."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Through God, we will do valiantly,"],[2,"for it is he who will tread down our enemies."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"God of my praise, don\u2019t remain silent,"]]},{v:2,l:[[2,"for they have opened the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of deceit against me."],[2,"They have spoken to me with a lying tongue."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They have also surrounded me with words of hatred,"],[2,"and fought against me without a cause."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"In return for my love, they are my adversaries;"],[2,"but I am in prayer."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They have rewarded me evil for good,"],[2,"and hatred for my love."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Set a wicked man over him."],[2,"Let an adversary stand at his right hand."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"When he is judged, let him come out guilty."],[2,"Let his prayer be turned into sin."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Let his days be few."],[2,"Let another take his office."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Let his children be fatherless,"],[2,"and his wife a widow."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Let his children be wandering beggars."],[2,"Let them be sought from their ruins."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the creditor seize all that he has."],[2,"Let strangers plunder the fruit of his labor."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Let there be no one to extend kindness to him,"],[2,"neither let there be anyone to have pity on his fatherless children."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Let his posterity be cut off."],[2,"In the generation following let their name be blotted out."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered by the LORD."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the sin of his mother be blotted out."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be before the LORD continually,"],[2,"that he may cut off their memory from the earth;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"because he didn\u2019t remember to show kindness,"],[2,"but persecuted the poor and needy man,"],[2,"the broken in heart, to kill them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, he loved cursing, and it came to him."],[2,"He didn\u2019t delight in blessing, and it was far from him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He clothed himself also with cursing as with his garment."],[2,"It came into his inward parts like water,"],[2,"like oil into his bones."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Let it be to him as the clothing with which he covers himself,"],[2,"for the belt that is always around him."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"This is the reward of my adversaries from the LORD,"],[2,"of those who speak evil against my soul."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"But deal with me, GOD the Lord, for your name\u2019s sake,"],[2,"because your loving kindness is good, deliver me;"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:22,l:[[2,"for I am poor and needy."],[2,"My heart is wounded within me."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I fade away like an evening shadow."],[2,"I am shaken off like a locust."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"My knees are weak through fasting."],[2,"My body is thin and lacks fat."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"I have also become a reproach to them."],[2,"When they see me, they shake their head."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Help me, LORD, my God."],[2,"Save me according to your loving kindness;"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"that they may know that this is your hand;"],[2,"that you, LORD, have done it."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"They may curse, but you bless."],[2,"When they arise, they will be shamed,"],[2,"but your servant shall rejoice."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my adversaries be clothed with dishonor."],[2,"Let them cover themselves with their own shame as with a robe."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give great thanks to the LORD with my mouth."],[2,"Yes, I will praise him among the multitude."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"For he will stand at the right hand of the needy,"],[2,"to save him from those who judge his soul."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD says to my Lord, \u201cSit at my right hand,"],[2,"until I make your enemies your footstool for your feet.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will send out the rod of your strength out of Zion."],[2,"Rule among your enemies."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Your people offer themselves willingly in the day of your power, in holy array."],[2,"Out of the womb of the morning, you have the dew of your youth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has sworn, and will not change his mind:"],[2,"\u201cYou are a priest forever in the order of Melchizedek.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord is at your right hand."],[2,"He will crush kings in the day of his wrath."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He will judge among the nations."],[2,"He will heap up dead bodies."],[2,"He will crush the ruler of the whole earth."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He will drink of the brook on the way;"],[2,"therefore he will lift up his head."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"I will give thanks to the LORD with my whole heart,"],[2,"in the council of the upright, and in the congregation."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah. Psalm 111 is an acrostic poem, with each verse after the initial \u201cPraise the LORD!\u201d starting with a letter of the alphabet (ordered from Alef to Tav).","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s works are great,"],[2,"pondered by all those who delight in them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"His work is honor and majesty."],[2,"His righteousness endures forever."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He has caused his wonderful works to be remembered."],[2,"The LORD is gracious and merciful."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He has given food to those who fear him."],[2,"He always remembers his covenant."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He has shown his people the power of his works,"],[2,"in giving them the heritage of the nations."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The works of his hands are truth and justice."],[2,"All his precepts are sure."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They are established forever and ever."],[2,"They are done in truth and uprightness."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He has sent redemption to his people."],[2,"He has ordained his covenant forever."],[2,"His name is holy and awesome!"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom."],[2,"All those who do his work have a good understanding."],[1,"His praise endures forever!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Blessed is the man who fears the LORD,"],[2,"who delights greatly in his commandments."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah. Psalm 112 is an acrostic poem, with each verse after the initial \u201cPraise the LORD!\u201d starting with a letter of the alphabet (ordered from Alef to Tav).","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"His offspring will be mighty in the land."],[2,"The generation of the upright will be blessed."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Wealth and riches are in his house."],[2,"His righteousness endures forever."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Light dawns in the darkness for the upright,"],[2,"gracious, merciful, and righteous."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"It is well with the man who deals graciously and lends."],[2,"He will maintain his cause in judgment."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For he will never be shaken."],[2,"The righteous will be remembered forever."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not be afraid of evil news."],[2,"His heart is steadfast, trusting in the LORD."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"His heart is established."],[2,"He will not be afraid in the end when he sees his adversaries."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He has dispersed, he has given to the poor."],[2,"His righteousness endures forever."],[2,"His horn will be exalted with honor."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked will see it, and be grieved."],[2,"He shall gnash with his teeth, and melt away."],[2,"The desire of the wicked will perish."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Praise, you servants of the LORD,"],[2,"praise the LORD\u2019s name."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u200e Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"from this time forward and forever more."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"From the rising of the sun to its going down,"],[2,"the LORD\u2019s name is to be praised."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is high above all nations,"],[2,"his glory above the heavens."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is like the LORD, our God,"],[2,"who has his seat on high,"]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"who stoops down to see in heaven and on the earth?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He raises up the poor out of the dust,"],[2,"and lifts up the needy from the ash heap,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"that he may set him with princes,"],[2,"even with the princes of his people."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He settles the barren woman in her home"],[2,"as a joyful mother of children."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"When Israel went out of Egypt,"],[2,"the house of Jacob from a people of foreign language,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Judah became his sanctuary,"],[2,"Israel his dominion."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The sea saw it, and fled."],[2,"The Jordan was driven back."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains skipped like rams,"],[2,"the little hills like lambs."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"What was it, you sea, that you fled?"],[2,"You Jordan, that you turned back?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You mountains, that you skipped like rams?"],[2,"You little hills, like lambs?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Tremble, you earth, at the presence of the Lord,"],[2,"at the presence of the God of Jacob,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"who turned the rock into a pool of water,"],[2,"the flint into a spring of waters."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Not to us, LORD, not to us,"],[2,"but to your name give glory,"],[2,"for your loving kindness, and for your truth\u2019s sake."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Why should the nations say,"],[2,"\u201cWhere is their God, now?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"But our God is in the heavens."],[2,"He does whatever he pleases."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Their idols are silver and gold,"],[2,"the work of men\u2019s hands."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They have mouths, but they don\u2019t speak."],[2,"They have eyes, but they don\u2019t see."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They have ears, but they don\u2019t hear."],[2,"They have noses, but they don\u2019t smell."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They have hands, but they don\u2019t feel."],[2,"They have feet, but they don\u2019t walk,"],[2,"neither do they speak through their throat."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who make them will be like them;"],[2,"yes, everyone who trusts in them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel, trust in the LORD!"],[2,"He is their help and their shield."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"House of Aaron, trust in the LORD!"],[2,"He is their help and their shield."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You who fear the LORD, trust in the LORD!"],[2,"He is their help and their shield."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD remembers us. He will bless us."],[2,"He will bless the house of Israel."],[2,"He will bless the house of Aaron."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He will bless those who fear the LORD,"],[2,"both small and great."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"May the LORD increase you more and more,"],[2,"you and your children."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are you by the LORD,"],[2,"who made heaven and earth."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The heavens are the LORD\u2019s heavens,"],[2,"but he has given the earth to the children of men."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The dead don\u2019t praise the LORD,"],[2,"nor any who go down into silence,"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"but we will bless the LORD,"],[2,"from this time forward and forever more."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"I love the LORD, because he listens to my voice,"],[2,"and my cries for mercy."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Because he has turned his ear to me,"],[2,"therefore I will call on him as long as I live."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The cords of death surrounded me,"],[2,"the pains of Sheol got a hold of me."],[2,"I found trouble and sorrow."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I called on the LORD\u2019s name:"],[2,"\u201cLORD, I beg you, deliver my soul.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is gracious and righteous."],[2,"Yes, our God is merciful."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD preserves the simple."],[2,"I was brought low, and he saved me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Return to your rest, my soul,"],[2,"for the LORD has dealt bountifully with you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have delivered my soul from death,"],[2,"my eyes from tears,"],[2,"and my feet from falling."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will walk before the LORD in the land of the living."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I believed, therefore I said,"],[2,"\u201cI was greatly afflicted.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I said in my haste,"],[2,"\u201cAll people are liars.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"What will I give to the LORD for all his benefits toward me?"]]},{v:13,l:[[2,"I will take the cup of salvation, and call on the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will pay my vows to the LORD,"],[2,"yes, in the presence of all his people."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Precious in the LORD\u2019s sight is the death of his saints."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, truly I am your servant."],[2,"I am your servant, the son of your servant girl."],[2,"You have freed me from my chains."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I will offer to you the sacrifice of thanksgiving,"],[2,"and will call on the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I will pay my vows to the LORD,"],[2,"yes, in the presence of all his people,"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"in the courts of the LORD\u2019s house,"],[2,"in the middle of you, Jerusalem."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, all you nations!"],[2,"Extol him, all you peoples!"]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For his loving kindness is great toward us."],[2,"The LORD\u2019s faithfulness endures forever."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let Israel now say"],[2,"that his loving kindness endures forever."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the house of Aaron now say"],[2,"that his loving kindness endures forever."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Now let those who fear the LORD say"],[2,"that his loving kindness endures forever."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Out of my distress, I called on the LORD."],[2,"The LORD answered me with freedom."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is on my side. I will not be afraid."],[2,"What can man do to me?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is on my side among those who help me."],[2,"Therefore I will look in triumph at those who hate me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"It is better to take refuge in the LORD,"],[2,"than to put confidence in man."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"It is better to take refuge in the LORD,"],[2,"than to put confidence in princes."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"All the nations surrounded me,"],[2,"but in the LORD\u2019s name I cut them off."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They surrounded me, yes, they surrounded me."],[2,"In the LORD\u2019s name I indeed cut them off."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They surrounded me like bees."],[2,"They are quenched like the burning thorns."],[2,"In the LORD\u2019s name I cut them off."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You pushed me back hard, to make me fall,"],[2,"but the LORD helped me."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is my strength and song."],[2,"He has become my salvation."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The voice of rejoicing and salvation is in the tents of the righteous."],[2,"\u201cThe right hand of the LORD does valiantly."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The right hand of the LORD is exalted!"],[2,"The right hand of the LORD does valiantly!\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I will not die, but live,"],[2,"and declare the LORD\u2019s works."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has punished me severely,"],[2,"but he has not given me over to death."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Open to me the gates of righteousness."],[2,"I will enter into them."],[2,"I will give thanks to the LORD."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"This is the gate of the LORD;"],[2,"the righteous will enter into it."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give thanks to you, for you have answered me,"],[2,"and have become my salvation."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The stone which the builders rejected"],[2,"has become the cornerstone."]],f:["Literally, head of the corner"]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"This is the LORD\u2019s doing."],[2,"It is marvelous in our eyes."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"This is the day that the LORD has made."],[2,"We will rejoice and be glad in it!"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Save us now, we beg you, LORD!"],[2,"LORD, we beg you, send prosperity now."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is he who comes in the LORD\u2019s name!"],[2,"We have blessed you out of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is God, and he has given us light."],[2,"Bind the sacrifice with cords, even to the horns of the altar."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"You are my God, and I will give thanks to you."],[2,"You are my God, I will exalt you."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]]}],[{v:1,h:["ALEPH"],p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those whose ways are blameless,"],[2,"who walk according to the LORD\u2019s law."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those who keep his statutes,"],[2,"who seek him with their whole heart."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, they do nothing wrong."],[2,"They walk in his ways."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You have commanded your precepts,"],[2,"that we should fully obey them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that my ways were steadfast"],[2,"to obey your statutes!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I wouldn\u2019t be disappointed,"],[2,"when I consider all of your commandments."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give thanks to you with uprightness of heart,"],[2,"when I learn your righteous judgments."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will observe your statutes."],[2,"Don\u2019t utterly forsake me."]]},{v:9,h:["BETH"],p:1,l:[[1,"How can a young man keep his way pure?"],[2,"By living according to your word."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"With my whole heart I have sought you."],[2,"Don\u2019t let me wander from your commandments."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I have hidden your word in my heart,"],[2,"that I might not sin against you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are you, LORD."],[2,"Teach me your statutes."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"With my lips,"],[2,"I have declared all the ordinances of your mouth."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I have rejoiced in the way of your testimonies,"],[2,"as much as in all riches."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will meditate on your precepts,"],[2,"and consider your ways."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I will delight myself in your statutes."],[2,"I will not forget your word."]]},{v:17,h:["GIMEL"],p:1,l:[[1,"Do good to your servant."],[2,"I will live and I will obey your word."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Open my eyes,"],[2,"that I may see wondrous things out of your law."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I am a stranger on the earth."],[2,"Don\u2019t hide your commandments from me."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul is consumed with longing for your ordinances at all times."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"You have rebuked the proud who are cursed,"],[2,"who wander from your commandments."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Take reproach and contempt away from me,"],[2,"for I have kept your statutes."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Though princes sit and slander me,"],[2,"your servant will meditate on your statutes."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Indeed your statutes are my delight,"],[2,"and my counselors."]]},{v:25,h:["DALETH"],p:1,l:[[1,"My soul is laid low in the dust."],[2,"Revive me according to your word!"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"I declared my ways, and you answered me."],[2,"Teach me your statutes."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Let me understand the teaching of your precepts!"],[2,"Then I will meditate on your wondrous works."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul is weary with sorrow;"],[2,"strengthen me according to your word."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Keep me from the way of deceit."],[2,"Grant me your law graciously!"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"I have chosen the way of truth."],[2,"I have set your ordinances before me."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"I cling to your statutes, LORD."],[2,"Don\u2019t let me be disappointed."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"I run in the path of your commandments,"],[2,"for you have set my heart free."]]},{v:33,h:["HE"],p:1,l:[[1,"Teach me, LORD, the way of your statutes."],[2,"I will keep them to the end."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Give me understanding, and I will keep your law."],[2,"Yes, I will obey it with my whole heart."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"Direct me in the path of your commandments,"],[2,"for I delight in them."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn my heart toward your statutes,"],[2,"not toward selfish gain."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn my eyes away from looking at worthless things."],[2,"Revive me in your ways."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"Fulfill your promise to your servant,"],[2,"that you may be feared."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"Take away my disgrace that I dread,"],[2,"for your ordinances are good."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I long for your precepts!"],[2,"Revive me in your righteousness."]]},{v:41,h:["VAV"],p:1,l:[[1,"Let your loving kindness also come to me, LORD,"],[2,"your salvation, according to your word."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"So I will have an answer for him who reproaches me,"],[2,"for I trust in your word."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t snatch the word of truth out of my mouth,"],[2,"for I put my hope in your ordinances."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"So I will obey your law continually,"],[2,"forever and ever."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"I will walk in liberty,"],[2,"for I have sought your precepts."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also speak of your statutes before kings,"],[2,"and will not be disappointed."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"I will delight myself in your commandments,"],[2,"because I love them."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[1,"I reach out my hands for your commandments, which I love."],[2,"I will meditate on your statutes."]]},{v:49,h:["ZAYIN"],p:1,l:[[1,"Remember your word to your servant,"],[2,"because you gave me hope."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"This is my comfort in my affliction,"],[2,"for your word has revived me."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[1,"The arrogant mock me excessively,"],[2,"but I don\u2019t swerve from your law."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[1,"I remember your ordinances of old, LORD,"],[2,"and have comforted myself."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[1,"Indignation has taken hold on me,"],[2,"because of the wicked who forsake your law."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[1,"Your statutes have been my songs"],[2,"in the house where I live."]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[1,"I have remembered your name, LORD, in the night,"],[2,"and I obey your law."]]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[1,"This is my way,"],[2,"that I keep your precepts."]]},{v:57,h:["HETH"],p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is my portion."],[2,"I promised to obey your words."]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[1,"I sought your favor with my whole heart."],[2,"Be merciful to me according to your word."]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[1,"I considered my ways,"],[2,"and turned my steps to your statutes."]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[1,"I will hurry, and not delay,"],[2,"to obey your commandments."]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[1,"The ropes of the wicked bind me,"],[2,"but I won\u2019t forget your law."]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[1,"At midnight I will rise to give thanks to you,"],[2,"because of your righteous ordinances."]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[1,"I am a friend of all those who fear you,"],[2,"of those who observe your precepts."]]},{v:64,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth is full of your loving kindness, LORD."],[2,"Teach me your statutes."]]},{v:65,h:["TETH"],p:1,l:[[1,"You have treated your servant well,"],[2,"according to your word, LORD."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[1,"Teach me good judgment and knowledge,"],[2,"for I believe in your commandments."]]},{v:67,p:1,l:[[1,"Before I was afflicted, I went astray;"],[2,"but now I observe your word."]]},{v:68,p:1,l:[[1,"You are good, and do good."],[2,"Teach me your statutes."]]},{v:69,p:1,l:[[1,"The proud have smeared a lie upon me."],[2,"With my whole heart, I will keep your precepts."]]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[1,"Their heart is as callous as the fat,"],[2,"but I delight in your law."]]},{v:71,p:1,l:[[1,"It is good for me that I have been afflicted,"],[2,"that I may learn your statutes."]]},{v:72,p:1,l:[[1,"The law of your mouth is better to me than thousands of pieces of gold and silver."]]},{v:73,h:["YODH"],p:1,l:[[1,"Your hands have made me and formed me."],[2,"Give me understanding, that I may learn your commandments."]]},{v:74,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who fear you will see me and be glad,"],[2,"because I have put my hope in your word."]]},{v:75,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, I know that your judgments are righteous,"],[2,"that in faithfulness you have afflicted me."]]},{v:76,p:1,l:[[1,"Please let your loving kindness be for my comfort,"],[2,"according to your word to your servant."]]},{v:77,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your tender mercies come to me, that I may live;"],[2,"for your law is my delight."]]},{v:78,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the proud be disappointed, for they have overthrown me wrongfully."],[2,"I will meditate on your precepts."]]},{v:79,p:1,l:[[1,"Let those who fear you turn to me."],[2,"They will know your statutes."]]},{v:80,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my heart be blameless toward your decrees,"],[2,"that I may not be disappointed."]]},{v:81,h:["KAPF"],p:1,l:[[1,"My soul faints for your salvation."],[2,"I hope in your word."]]},{v:82,p:1,l:[[1,"My eyes fail for your word."],[2,"I say, \u201cWhen will you comfort me?\u201d"]]},{v:83,p:1,l:[[1,"For I have become like a wineskin in the smoke."],[2,"I don\u2019t forget your statutes."]]},{v:84,p:1,l:[[1,"How many are the days of your servant?"],[2,"When will you execute judgment on those who persecute me?"]]},{v:85,p:1,l:[[1,"The proud have dug pits for me,"],[2,"contrary to your law."]]},{v:86,p:1,l:[[1,"All of your commandments are faithful."],[2,"They persecute me wrongfully."],[2,"Help me!"]]},{v:87,p:1,l:[[1,"They had almost wiped me from the earth,"],[2,"but I didn\u2019t forsake your precepts."]]},{v:88,p:1,l:[[1,"Preserve my life according to your loving kindness,"],[2,"so I will obey the statutes of your mouth."]]},{v:89,h:["LAMEDH"],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, your word is settled in heaven forever."]]},{v:90,p:1,l:[[1,"Your faithfulness is to all generations."],[2,"You have established the earth, and it remains."]]},{v:91,p:1,l:[[1,"Your laws remain to this day,"],[2,"for all things serve you."]]},{v:92,p:1,l:[[1,"Unless your law had been my delight,"],[2,"I would have perished in my affliction."]]},{v:93,p:1,l:[[1,"I will never forget your precepts,"],[2,"for with them, you have revived me."]]},{v:94,p:1,l:[[1,"I am yours."],[2,"Save me, for I have sought your precepts."]]},{v:95,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked have waited for me, to destroy me."],[2,"I will consider your statutes."]]},{v:96,p:1,l:[[1,"I have seen a limit to all perfection,"],[2,"but your commands are boundless."]]},{v:97,h:["MEM"],p:1,l:[[1,"How I love your law!"],[2,"It is my meditation all day."]]},{v:98,p:1,l:[[1,"Your commandments make me wiser than my enemies,"],[2,"for your commandments are always with me."]]},{v:99,p:1,l:[[1,"I have more understanding than all my teachers,"],[2,"for your testimonies are my meditation."]]},{v:100,p:1,l:[[1,"I understand more than the aged,"],[2,"because I have kept your precepts."]]},{v:101,p:1,l:[[1,"I have kept my feet from every evil way,"],[2,"that I might observe your word."]]},{v:102,p:1,l:[[1,"I have not turned away from your ordinances,"],[2,"for you have taught me."]]},{v:103,p:1,l:[[1,"How sweet are your promises to my taste,"],[2,"more than honey to my mouth!"]]},{v:104,p:1,l:[[1,"Through your precepts, I get understanding;"],[2,"therefore I hate every false way."]]},{v:105,h:["NUN"],p:1,l:[[1,"Your word is a lamp to my feet,"],[2,"and a light for my path."]]},{v:106,p:1,l:[[1,"I have sworn, and have confirmed it,"],[2,"that I will obey your righteous ordinances."]]},{v:107,p:1,l:[[1,"I am afflicted very much."],[2,"Revive me, LORD, according to your word."]]},{v:108,p:1,l:[[1,"Accept, I beg you, the willing offerings of my mouth."],[2,"LORD, teach me your ordinances."]]},{v:109,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul is continually in my hand,"],[2,"yet I won\u2019t forget your law."]]},{v:110,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked have laid a snare for me,"],[2,"yet I haven\u2019t gone astray from your precepts."]]},{v:111,p:1,l:[[1,"I have taken your testimonies as a heritage forever,"],[2,"for they are the joy of my heart."]]},{v:112,p:1,l:[[1,"I have set my heart to perform your statutes forever,"],[2,"even to the end."]]},{v:113,h:["SAMEKH"],p:1,l:[[1,"I hate double-minded men,"],[2,"but I love your law."]]},{v:114,p:1,l:[[1,"You are my hiding place and my shield."],[2,"I hope in your word."]]},{v:115,p:1,l:[[1,"Depart from me, you evildoers,"],[2,"that I may keep the commandments of my God."]]},{v:116,p:1,l:[[1,"Uphold me according to your word, that I may live."],[2,"Let me not be ashamed of my hope."]]},{v:117,p:1,l:[[1,"Hold me up, and I will be safe,"],[2,"and will have respect for your statutes continually."]]},{v:118,p:1,l:[[1,"You reject all those who stray from your statutes,"],[2,"for their deceit is in vain."]]},{v:119,p:1,l:[[1,"You put away all the wicked of the earth like dross."],[2,"Therefore I love your testimonies."]]},{v:120,p:1,l:[[1,"My flesh trembles for fear of you."],[2,"I am afraid of your judgments."]]},{v:121,h:["AYIN"],p:1,l:[[1,"I have done what is just and righteous."],[2,"Don\u2019t leave me to my oppressors."]]},{v:122,p:1,l:[[1,"Ensure your servant\u2019s well-being."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the proud oppress me."]]},{v:123,p:1,l:[[1,"My eyes fail looking for your salvation,"],[2,"for your righteous word."]]},{v:124,p:1,l:[[1,"Deal with your servant according to your loving kindness."],[2,"Teach me your statutes."]]},{v:125,p:1,l:[[1,"I am your servant. Give me understanding,"],[2,"that I may know your testimonies."]]},{v:126,p:1,l:[[1,"It is time to act, LORD,"],[2,"for they break your law."]]},{v:127,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I love your commandments more than gold,"],[2,"yes, more than pure gold."]]},{v:128,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I consider all of your precepts to be right."],[2,"I hate every false way."]]},{v:129,h:["PE"],p:1,l:[[1,"Your testimonies are wonderful,"],[2,"therefore my soul keeps them."]]},{v:130,p:1,l:[[1,"The entrance of your words gives light."],[2,"It gives understanding to the simple."]]},{v:131,p:1,l:[[1,"I opened my mouth wide and panted,"],[2,"for I longed for your commandments."]]},{v:132,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn to me, and have mercy on me,"],[2,"as you always do to those who love your name."]]},{v:133,p:1,l:[[1,"Establish my footsteps in your word."],[2,"Don\u2019t let any iniquity have dominion over me."]]},{v:134,p:1,l:[[1,"Redeem me from the oppression of man,"],[2,"so I will observe your precepts."]]},{v:135,p:1,l:[[1,"Make your face shine on your servant."],[2,"Teach me your statutes."]]},{v:136,p:1,l:[[1,"Streams of tears run down my eyes,"],[2,"because they don\u2019t observe your law."]]},{v:137,h:["TZADHE"],p:1,l:[[1,"You are righteous, LORD."],[2,"Your judgments are upright."]]},{v:138,p:1,l:[[1,"You have commanded your statutes in righteousness."],[2,"They are fully trustworthy."]]},{v:139,p:1,l:[[1,"My zeal wears me out,"],[2,"because my enemies ignore your words."]]},{v:140,p:1,l:[[1,"Your promises have been thoroughly tested,"],[2,"and your servant loves them."]]},{v:141,p:1,l:[[1,"I am small and despised."],[2,"I don\u2019t forget your precepts."]]},{v:142,p:1,l:[[1,"Your righteousness is an everlasting righteousness."],[2,"Your law is truth."]]},{v:143,p:1,l:[[1,"Trouble and anguish have taken hold of me."],[2,"Your commandments are my delight."]]},{v:144,p:1,l:[[1,"Your testimonies are righteous forever."],[2,"Give me understanding, that I may live."]]},{v:145,h:["QOPH"],p:1,l:[[1,"I have called with my whole heart."],[2,"Answer me, LORD!"],[2,"I will keep your statutes."]]},{v:146,p:1,l:[[1,"I have called to you. Save me!"],[2,"I will obey your statutes."]]},{v:147,p:1,l:[[1,"I rise before dawn and cry for help."],[2,"I put my hope in your words."]]},{v:148,p:1,l:[[1,"My eyes stay open through the night watches,"],[2,"that I might meditate on your word."]]},{v:149,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear my voice according to your loving kindness."],[2,"Revive me, LORD, according to your ordinances."]]},{v:150,p:1,l:[[1,"They draw near who follow after wickedness."],[2,"They are far from your law."]]},{v:151,p:1,l:[[1,"You are near, LORD."],[2,"All your commandments are truth."]]},{v:152,p:1,l:[[1,"Of old I have known from your testimonies,"],[2,"that you have founded them forever."]]},{v:153,h:["RESH"],p:1,l:[[1,"Consider my affliction, and deliver me,"],[2,"for I don\u2019t forget your law."]]},{v:154,p:1,l:[[1,"Plead my cause, and redeem me!"],[2,"Revive me according to your promise."]]},{v:155,p:1,l:[[1,"Salvation is far from the wicked,"],[2,"for they don\u2019t seek your statutes."]]},{v:156,p:1,l:[[1,"Great are your tender mercies, LORD."],[2,"Revive me according to your ordinances."]]},{v:157,p:1,l:[[1,"Many are my persecutors and my adversaries."],[2,"I haven\u2019t swerved from your testimonies."]]},{v:158,p:1,l:[[1,"I look at the faithless with loathing,"],[2,"because they don\u2019t observe your word."]]},{v:159,p:1,l:[[1,"Consider how I love your precepts."],[2,"Revive me, LORD, according to your loving kindness."]]},{v:160,p:1,l:[[1,"All of your words are truth."],[2,"Every one of your righteous ordinances endures forever."]]},{v:161,h:["SIN AND SHIN"],p:1,l:[[1,"Princes have persecuted me without a cause,"],[2,"but my heart stands in awe of your words."]]},{v:162,p:1,l:[[1,"I rejoice at your word,"],[2,"as one who finds great plunder."]]},{v:163,p:1,l:[[1,"I hate and abhor falsehood."],[2,"I love your law."]]},{v:164,p:1,l:[[1,"Seven times a day, I praise you,"],[2,"because of your righteous ordinances."]]},{v:165,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who love your law have great peace."],[2,"Nothing causes them to stumble."]]},{v:166,p:1,l:[[1,"I have hoped for your salvation, LORD."],[2,"I have done your commandments."]]},{v:167,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul has observed your testimonies."],[2,"I love them exceedingly."]]},{v:168,p:1,l:[[1,"I have obeyed your precepts and your testimonies,"],[2,"for all my ways are before you."]]},{v:169,h:["TAV"],p:1,l:[[1,"Let my cry come before you, LORD."],[2,"Give me understanding according to your word."]]},{v:170,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my supplication come before you."],[2,"Deliver me according to your word."]]},{v:171,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my lips utter praise,"],[2,"for you teach me your statutes."]]},{v:172,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my tongue sing of your word,"],[2,"for all your commandments are righteousness."]]},{v:173,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your hand be ready to help me,"],[2,"for I have chosen your precepts."]]},{v:174,p:1,l:[[1,"I have longed for your salvation, LORD."],[2,"Your law is my delight."]]},{v:175,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my soul live, that I may praise you."],[2,"Let your ordinances help me."]]},{v:176,p:1,l:[[1,"I have gone astray like a lost sheep."],[2,"Seek your servant, for I don\u2019t forget your commandments."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"In my distress, I cried to the LORD."],[2,"He answered me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver my soul, LORD, from lying lips,"],[2,"from a deceitful tongue."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"What will be given to you, and what will be done more to you,"],[2,"you deceitful tongue?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Sharp arrows of the mighty,"],[2,"with coals of juniper."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe is me, that I live in Meshech,"],[2,"that I dwell among the tents of Kedar!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul has had her dwelling too long"],[2,"with him who hates peace."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I am for peace,"],[2,"but when I speak, they are for war."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will lift up my eyes to the hills."],[2,"Where does my help come from?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"My help comes from the LORD,"],[2,"who made heaven and earth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not allow your foot to be moved."],[2,"He who keeps you will not slumber."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he who keeps Israel"],[2,"will neither slumber nor sleep."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is your keeper."],[2,"The LORD is your shade on your right hand."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The sun will not harm you by day,"],[2,"nor the moon by night."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will keep you from all evil."],[2,"He will keep your soul."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will keep your going out and your coming in,"],[2,"from this time forward, and forever more."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I was glad when they said to me,"],[2,"\u201cLet\u2019s go to the LORD\u2019s house!\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Our feet are standing within your gates, Jerusalem!"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"Jerusalem is built as a city that is compact together,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"where the tribes go up, even the LORD\u2019s tribes,"],[2,"according to an ordinance for Israel,"],[2,"to give thanks to the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For there are set thrones for judgment,"],[2,"the thrones of David\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Pray for the peace of Jerusalem."],[2,"Those who love you will prosper."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Peace be within your walls,"],[2,"and prosperity within your palaces."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For my brothers\u2019 and companions\u2019 sakes,"],[2,"I will now say, \u201cPeace be within you.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For the sake of the house of the LORD our God,"],[2,"I will seek your good."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"I lift up my eyes to you,"],[2,"you who sit in the heavens."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, as the eyes of servants look to the hand of their master,"],[2,"as the eyes of a maid to the hand of her mistress,"],[2,"so our eyes look to the LORD, our God,"],[2,"until he has mercy on us."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Have mercy on us, LORD, have mercy on us,"],[2,"for we have endured much contempt."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scoffing of those who are at ease,"],[2,"with the contempt of the proud."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"If it had not been the LORD who was on our side,"],[2,"let Israel now say,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"if it had not been the LORD who was on our side,"],[2,"when men rose up against us,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"then they would have swallowed us up alive,"],[2,"when their wrath was kindled against us,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"then the waters would have overwhelmed us,"],[2,"the stream would have gone over our soul."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the proud waters would have gone over our soul."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD,"],[2,"who has not given us as a prey to their teeth."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Our soul has escaped like a bird out of the fowler\u2019s snare."],[2,"The snare is broken, and we have escaped."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Our help is in the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"who made heaven and earth."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"Those who trust in the LORD are as Mount Zion,"],[2,"which can\u2019t be moved, but remains forever."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"As the mountains surround Jerusalem,"],[2,"so the LORD surrounds his people from this time forward and forever more."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the scepter of wickedness won\u2019t remain over the allotment of the righteous,"],[2,"so that the righteous won\u2019t use their hands to do evil."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Do good, LORD, to those who are good,"],[2,"to those who are upright in their hearts."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for those who turn away to their crooked ways,"],[2,"the LORD will lead them away with the workers of iniquity."],[1,"Peace be on Israel."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"When the LORD brought back those who returned to Zion,"],[2,"we were like those who dream."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Then our mouth was filled with laughter,"],[2,"and our tongue with singing."],[1,"Then they said among the nations,"],[2,"\u201cThe LORD has done great things for them.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has done great things for us,"],[2,"and we are glad."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Restore our fortunes again, LORD,"],[2,"like the streams in the Negev."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who sow in tears will reap in joy."]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"He who goes out weeping, carrying seed for sowing,"],[2,"will certainly come again with joy, carrying his sheaves."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents. By Solomon."],p:1,l:[[1,"Unless the LORD builds the house,"],[2,"they who build it labor in vain."],[1,"Unless the LORD watches over the city,"],[2,"the watchman guards it in vain."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"It is vain for you to rise up early,"],[2,"to stay up late,"],[2,"eating the bread of toil,"],[2,"for he gives sleep to his loved ones."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, children are a heritage of the LORD."],[2,"The fruit of the womb is his reward."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"As arrows in the hand of a mighty man,"],[2,"so are the children of youth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Happy is the man who has his quiver full of them."],[2,"They won\u2019t be disappointed when they speak with their enemies in the gate."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is everyone who fears the LORD,"],[2,"who walks in his ways."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For you will eat the labor of your hands."],[2,"You will be happy, and it will be well with you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Your wife will be as a fruitful vine in the innermost parts of your house,"],[2,"your children like olive shoots around your table."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, this is how the man who fears the LORD is blessed."]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"May the LORD bless you out of Zion,"],[2,"and may you see the good of Jerusalem all the days of your life."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, may you see your children\u2019s children."],[2,"Peace be upon Israel."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"Many times they have afflicted me from my youth up."],[2,"Let Israel now say:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"many times they have afflicted me from my youth up,"],[2,"yet they have not prevailed against me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The plowers plowed on my back."],[2,"They made their furrows long."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is righteous."],[2,"He has cut apart the cords of the wicked."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be disappointed and turned backward,"],[2,"all those who hate Zion."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be as the grass on the housetops,"],[2,"which withers before it grows up,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"with which the reaper doesn\u2019t fill his hand,"],[2,"nor he who binds sheaves, his bosom."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Neither do those who go by say,"],[2,"\u201cThe blessing of the LORD be on you."],[2,"We bless you in the LORD\u2019s name.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"Out of the depths I have cried to you, LORD."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, hear my voice."],[2,"Let your ears be attentive to the voice of my petitions."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"If you, LORD, kept a record of sins,"],[2,"Lord, who could stand?"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"But there is forgiveness with you,"],[2,"therefore you are feared."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I wait for the LORD."],[2,"My soul waits."],[2,"I hope in his word."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul longs for the Lord more than watchmen long for the morning,"],[2,"more than watchmen for the morning."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel, hope in the LORD,"],[2,"for there is loving kindness with the LORD."],[2,"Abundant redemption is with him."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He will redeem Israel from all their sins."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, my heart isn\u2019t arrogant, nor my eyes lofty;"],[2,"nor do I concern myself with great matters,"],[2,"or things too wonderful for me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely I have stilled and quieted my soul,"],[2,"like a weaned child with his mother,"],[2,"like a weaned child is my soul within me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel, hope in the LORD,"],[2,"from this time forward and forever more."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, remember David and all his affliction,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"how he swore to the LORD,"],[2,"and vowed to the Mighty One of Jacob:"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSurely I will not come into the structure of my house,"],[2,"nor go up into my bed;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will not give sleep to my eyes,"],[2,"or slumber to my eyelids,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"until I find out a place for the LORD,"],[2,"a dwelling for the Mighty One of Jacob.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, we heard of it in Ephrathah."],[2,"We found it in the field of Jaar."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWe will go into his dwelling place."],[2,"We will worship at his footstool.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, LORD, into your resting place,"],[2,"you, and the ark of your strength."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your priests be clothed with righteousness."],[2,"Let your saints shout for joy!"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For your servant David\u2019s sake,"],[2,"don\u2019t turn away the face of your anointed one."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has sworn to David in truth."],[2,"He will not turn from it:"],[2,"\u201cI will set the fruit of your body on your throne."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"If your children will keep my covenant,"],[2,"my testimony that I will teach them,"],[2,"their children also will sit on your throne forever more.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD has chosen Zion."],[2,"He has desired it for his habitation."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThis is my resting place forever."],[2,"I will live here, for I have desired it."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will abundantly bless her provision."],[2,"I will satisfy her poor with bread."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also clothe her priests with salvation."],[2,"Her saints will shout aloud for joy."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make the horn of David to bud there."],[2,"I have ordained a lamp for my anointed."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I will clothe his enemies with shame,"],[2,"but on himself, his crown will shine.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents. By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"See how good and how pleasant it is"],[2,"for brothers to live together in unity!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"It is like the precious oil on the head,"],[2,"that ran down on the beard,"],[2,"even Aaron\u2019s beard,"],[2,"that came down on the edge of his robes,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"like the dew of Hermon,"],[2,"that comes down on the hills of Zion;"],[2,"for there the LORD gives the blessing,"],[2,"even life forever more."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Song of Ascents."],p:1,l:[[1,"Look! Praise the LORD, all you servants of the LORD,"],[2,"who stand by night in the LORD\u2019s house!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your hands in the sanctuary."],[2,"Praise the LORD!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"May the LORD bless you from Zion,"],[2,"even he who made heaven and earth."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Praise the LORD\u2019s name!"],[2,"Praise him, you servants of the LORD,"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"you who stand in the LORD\u2019s house,"],[2,"in the courts of our God\u2019s house."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, for the LORD is good."],[2,"Sing praises to his name, for that is pleasant."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD has chosen Jacob for himself,"],[2,"Israel for his own possession."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For I know that the LORD is great,"],[2,"that our Lord is above all gods."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Whatever the LORD pleased, that he has done,"],[2,"in heaven and in earth, in the seas and in all deeps."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He causes the clouds to rise from the ends of the earth."],[2,"He makes lightnings with the rain."],[2,"He brings the wind out of his treasuries."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He struck the firstborn of Egypt,"],[2,"both of man and animal."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He sent signs and wonders into the middle of you, Egypt,"],[2,"on Pharaoh, and on all his servants."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He struck many nations,"],[2,"and killed mighty kings\u2014"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Sihon king of the Amorites,"],[2,"Og king of Bashan,"],[2,"and all the kingdoms of Canaan\u2014"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"and gave their land for a heritage,"],[2,"a heritage to Israel, his people."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Your name, LORD, endures forever;"],[2,"your renown, LORD, throughout all generations."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD will judge his people"],[2,"and have compassion on his servants."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The idols of the nations are silver and gold,"],[2,"the work of men\u2019s hands."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"They have mouths, but they can\u2019t speak."],[2,"They have eyes, but they can\u2019t see."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"They have ears, but they can\u2019t hear,"],[2,"neither is there any breath in their mouths."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who make them will be like them,"],[2,"yes, everyone who trusts in them."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"House of Israel, praise the LORD!"],[2,"House of Aaron, praise the LORD!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"House of Levi, praise the LORD!"],[2,"You who fear the LORD, praise the LORD!"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD from Zion,"],[2,"who dwells in Jerusalem."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Give thanks to the God of gods,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Give thanks to the Lord of lords,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who alone does great wonders,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who by understanding made the heavens,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who spread out the earth above the waters,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who made the great lights,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"the sun to rule by day,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"the moon and stars to rule by night,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who struck down the Egyptian firstborn,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"and brought out Israel from among them,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"with a strong hand, and with an outstretched arm,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who divided the Red Sea apart,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"and made Israel to pass through the middle of it,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"but overthrew Pharaoh and his army in the Red Sea,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who led his people through the wilderness,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"to him who struck great kings,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"and killed mighty kings,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Sihon king of the Amorites,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Og king of Bashan,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"and gave their land as an inheritance,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"even a heritage to Israel his servant,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"who remembered us in our low estate,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"and has delivered us from our adversaries,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever;"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"who gives food to every creature,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh give thanks to the God of heaven,"],[2,"for his loving kindness endures forever."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat down."],[2,"Yes, we wept, when we remembered Zion."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"On the willows in that land,"],[2,"we hung up our harps."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For there, those who led us captive asked us for songs."],[2,"Those who tormented us demanded songs of joy:"],[2,"\u201cSing us one of the songs of Zion!\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"How can we sing the LORD\u2019s song in a foreign land?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"If I forget you, Jerusalem,"],[2,"let my right hand forget its skill."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my tongue stick to the roof of my mouth if I don\u2019t remember you,"],[2,"if I don\u2019t prefer Jerusalem above my chief joy."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember, LORD, against the children of Edom in the day of Jerusalem,"],[2,"who said, \u201cRaze it!"],[2,"Raze it even to its foundation!\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Daughter of Babylon, doomed to destruction,"],[2,"he will be happy who repays you,"],[2,"as you have done to us."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Happy shall he be,"],[2,"who takes and dashes your little ones against the rock."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will give you thanks with my whole heart."],[2,"Before the gods, I will sing praises to you."]],f:["The word elohim, used here, usually means \u201cGod\u201d but can also mean \u201cgods\u201d, \u201cprinces\u201d, or \u201cangels\u201d."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bow down toward your holy temple,"],[2,"and give thanks to your Name for your loving kindness and for your truth;"],[2,"for you have exalted your Name and your Word above all."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"In the day that I called, you answered me."],[2,"You encouraged me with strength in my soul."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"All the kings of the earth will give you thanks, LORD,"],[2,"for they have heard the words of your mouth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, they will sing of the ways of the LORD,"],[2,"for the LORD\u2019s glory is great!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For though the LORD is high, yet he looks after the lowly;"],[2,"but he knows the proud from afar."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Though I walk in the middle of trouble, you will revive me."],[2,"You will stretch out your hand against the wrath of my enemies."],[2,"Your right hand will save me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will fulfill that which concerns me."],[2,"Your loving kindness, LORD, endures forever."],[2,"Don\u2019t forsake the works of your own hands."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you have searched me,"],[2,"and you know me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You know my sitting down and my rising up."],[2,"You perceive my thoughts from afar."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You search out my path and my lying down,"],[2,"and are acquainted with all my ways."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For there is not a word on my tongue,"],[2,"but behold, LORD, you know it altogether."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You hem me in behind and before."],[2,"You laid your hand on me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"This knowledge is beyond me."],[2,"It\u2019s lofty."],[2,"I can\u2019t attain it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Where could I go from your Spirit?"],[2,"Or where could I flee from your presence?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"If I ascend up into heaven, you are there."],[2,"If I make my bed in Sheol, behold, you are there!"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"If I take the wings of the dawn,"],[2,"and settle in the uttermost parts of the sea,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"even there your hand will lead me,"],[2,"and your right hand will hold me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"If I say, \u201cSurely the darkness will overwhelm me."],[2,"The light around me will be night,\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"even the darkness doesn\u2019t hide from you,"],[2,"but the night shines as the day."],[2,"The darkness is like light to you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For you formed my inmost being."],[2,"You knit me together in my mother\u2019s womb."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give thanks to you,"],[2,"for I am fearfully and wonderfully made."],[1,"Your works are wonderful."],[2,"My soul knows that very well."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"My frame wasn\u2019t hidden from you,"],[2,"when I was made in secret,"],[2,"woven together in the depths of the earth."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Your eyes saw my body."],[2,"In your book they were all written,"],[2,"the days that were ordained for me,"],[2,"when as yet there were none of them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"How precious to me are your thoughts, God!"],[2,"How vast is their sum!"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"If I would count them, they are more in number than the sand."],[2,"When I wake up, I am still with you."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"If only you, God, would kill the wicked."],[2,"Get away from me, you bloodthirsty men!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"For they speak against you wickedly."],[2,"Your enemies take your name in vain."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, don\u2019t I hate those who hate you?"],[2,"Am I not grieved with those who rise up against you?"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"I hate them with perfect hatred."],[2,"They have become my enemies."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Search me, God, and know my heart."],[2,"Try me, and know my thoughts."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"See if there is any wicked way in me,"],[2,"and lead me in the everlasting way."]]}],[{v:1,h:["For the Chief Musician. A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me, LORD, from evil men."],[2,"Preserve me from violent men:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"those who devise mischief in their hearts."],[2,"They continually gather themselves together for war."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They have sharpened their tongues like a serpent."],[2,"Viper\u2019s poison is under their lips. Selah."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, keep me from the hands of the wicked."],[2,"Preserve me from the violent men who have determined to trip my feet."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The proud have hidden a snare for me,"],[2,"they have spread the cords of a net by the path."],[2,"They have set traps for me. Selah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I said to the LORD, \u201cYou are my God.\u201d"],[2,"Listen to the cry of my petitions, LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, the Lord, the strength of my salvation,"],[2,"you have covered my head in the day of battle."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, don\u2019t grant the desires of the wicked."],[2,"Don\u2019t let their evil plans succeed, or they will become proud. Selah."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"As for the head of those who surround me,"],[2,"let the mischief of their own lips cover them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Let burning coals fall on them."],[2,"Let them be thrown into the fire,"],[2,"into miry pits, from where they never rise."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"An evil speaker won\u2019t be established on the earth."],[2,"Evil will hunt the violent man to overthrow him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I know that the LORD will maintain the cause of the afflicted,"],[2,"and justice for the needy."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely the righteous will give thanks to your name."],[2,"The upright will dwell in your presence."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, I have called on you."],[2,"Come to me quickly!"],[2,"Listen to my voice when I call to you."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let my prayer be set before you like incense;"],[2,"the lifting up of my hands like the evening sacrifice."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Set a watch, LORD, before my mouth."],[2,"Keep the door of my lips."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t incline my heart to any evil thing,"],[2,"to practice deeds of wickedness with men who work iniquity."],[2,"Don\u2019t let me eat of their delicacies."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the righteous strike me, it is kindness;"],[2,"let him reprove me, it is like oil on the head;"],[2,"don\u2019t let my head refuse it;"],[2,"Yet my prayer is always against evil deeds."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Their judges are thrown down by the sides of the rock."],[2,"They will hear my words, for they are well spoken."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAs when one plows and breaks up the earth,"],[2,"our bones are scattered at the mouth of Sheol.\u201d"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For my eyes are on you, LORD, the Lord."],[2,"I take refuge in you."],[2,"Don\u2019t leave my soul destitute."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Keep me from the snare which they have laid for me,"],[2,"from the traps of the workers of iniquity."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the wicked fall together into their own nets"],[2,"while I pass by."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A contemplation by David, when he was in the cave. A Prayer."],p:1,l:[[1,"I cry with my voice to the LORD."],[2,"With my voice, I ask the LORD for mercy."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I pour out my complaint before him."],[2,"I tell him my troubles."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"When my spirit was overwhelmed within me,"],[2,"you knew my route."],[1,"On the path in which I walk,"],[2,"they have hidden a snare for me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Look on my right, and see;"],[2,"for there is no one who is concerned for me."],[2,"Refuge has fled from me."],[2,"No one cares for my soul."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I cried to you, LORD."],[2,"I said, \u201cYou are my refuge,"],[2,"my portion in the land of the living.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen to my cry,"],[2,"for I am in desperate need."],[1,"Deliver me from my persecutors,"],[2,"for they are too strong for me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Bring my soul out of prison,"],[2,"that I may give thanks to your name."],[1,"The righteous will surround me,"],[2,"for you will be good to me."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A Psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Hear my prayer, LORD."],[2,"Listen to my petitions."],[2,"In your faithfulness and righteousness, relieve me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t enter into judgment with your servant,"],[2,"for in your sight no man living is righteous."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the enemy pursues my soul."],[2,"He has struck my life down to the ground."],[2,"He has made me live in dark places, as those who have been long dead."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore my spirit is overwhelmed within me."],[2,"My heart within me is desolate."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I remember the days of old."],[2,"I meditate on all your doings."],[2,"I contemplate the work of your hands."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I spread out my hands to you."],[2,"My soul thirsts for you, like a parched land. Selah."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Hurry to answer me, LORD."],[2,"My spirit fails."],[1,"Don\u2019t hide your face from me,"],[2,"so that I don\u2019t become like those who go down into the pit."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Cause me to hear your loving kindness in the morning,"],[2,"for I trust in you."],[1,"Cause me to know the way in which I should walk,"],[2,"for I lift up my soul to you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Deliver me, LORD, from my enemies."],[2,"I flee to you to hide me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Teach me to do your will,"],[2,"for you are my God."],[1,"Your Spirit is good."],[2,"Lead me in the land of uprightness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Revive me, LORD, for your name\u2019s sake."],[2,"In your righteousness, bring my soul out of trouble."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"In your loving kindness, cut off my enemies,"],[2,"and destroy all those who afflict my soul,"],[2,"for I am your servant."]]}],[{v:1,h:["By David."],p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed be the LORD, my rock,"],[2,"who trains my hands to war,"],[2,"and my fingers to battle\u2014"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"my loving kindness, my fortress,"],[2,"my high tower, my deliverer,"],[2,"my shield, and he in whom I take refuge,"],[2,"who subdues my people under me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, what is man, that you care for him?"],[2,"Or the son of man, that you think of him?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Man is like a breath."],[2,"His days are like a shadow that passes away."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Part your heavens, LORD, and come down."],[2,"Touch the mountains, and they will smoke."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Throw out lightning, and scatter them."],[2,"Send out your arrows, and rout them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Stretch out your hand from above,"],[2,"rescue me, and deliver me out of great waters,"],[2,"out of the hands of foreigners,"]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"whose mouths speak deceit,"],[2,"whose right hand is a right hand of falsehood."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will sing a new song to you, God."],[2,"On a ten-stringed lyre, I will sing praises to you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You are he who gives salvation to kings,"],[2,"who rescues David, his servant, from the deadly sword."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Rescue me, and deliver me out of the hands of foreigners,"],[2,"whose mouths speak deceit,"],[2,"whose right hand is a right hand of falsehood."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Then our sons will be like well-nurtured plants,"],[2,"our daughters like pillars carved to adorn a palace."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Our barns are full, filled with all kinds of provision."],[2,"Our sheep produce thousands and ten thousands in our fields."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Our oxen will pull heavy loads."],[2,"There is no breaking in, and no going away,"],[2,"and no outcry in our streets."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Happy are the people who are in such a situation."],[2,"Happy are the people whose God is the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,h:["A praise psalm by David."],p:1,l:[[1,"I will exalt you, my God, the King."],[2,"I will praise your name forever and ever."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Every day I will praise you."],[2,"I will extol your name forever and ever."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Great is the LORD, and greatly to be praised!"],[2,"His greatness is unsearchable."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"One generation will commend your works to another,"],[2,"and will declare your mighty acts."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I will meditate on the glorious majesty of your honor,"],[2,"on your wondrous works."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Men will speak of the might of your awesome acts."],[2,"I will declare your greatness."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They will utter the memory of your great goodness,"],[2,"and will sing of your righteousness."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is gracious, merciful,"],[2,"slow to anger, and of great loving kindness."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is good to all."],[2,"His tender mercies are over all his works."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"All your works will give thanks to you, LORD."],[2,"Your saints will extol you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They will speak of the glory of your kingdom,"],[2,"and talk about your power,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"to make known to the sons of men his mighty acts,"],[2,"the glory of the majesty of his kingdom."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Your kingdom is an everlasting kingdom."],[2,"Your dominion endures throughout all generations."],[1,"The LORD is faithful in all his words,"],[2,"and loving in all his deeds."]],f:["Some manuscripts omit these last two lines."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD upholds all who fall,"],[2,"and raises up all those who are bowed down."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The eyes of all wait for you."],[2,"You give them their food in due season."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"You open your hand,"],[2,"and satisfy the desire of every living thing."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is righteous in all his ways,"],[2,"and gracious in all his works."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is near to all those who call on him,"],[2,"to all who call on him in truth."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He will fulfill the desire of those who fear him."],[2,"He also will hear their cry, and will save them."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD preserves all those who love him,"],[2,"but he will destroy all the wicked."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"My mouth will speak the praise of the LORD."],[2,"Let all flesh bless his holy name forever and ever."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Praise the LORD, my soul."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"While I live, I will praise the LORD."],[2,"I will sing praises to my God as long as I exist."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t put your trust in princes,"],[2,"in a son of man in whom there is no help."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"His spirit departs, and he returns to the earth."],[2,"In that very day, his thoughts perish."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Happy is he who has the God of Jacob for his help,"],[2,"whose hope is in the LORD, his God,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"who made heaven and earth,"],[2,"the sea, and all that is in them;"],[2,"who keeps truth forever;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"who executes justice for the oppressed;"],[2,"who gives food to the hungry."],[1,"The LORD frees the prisoners."]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"The LORD opens the eyes of the blind."],[2,"The LORD raises up those who are bowed down."],[2,"The LORD loves the righteous."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD preserves the foreigners."],[2,"He upholds the fatherless and widow,"],[2,"but he turns the way of the wicked upside down."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will reign forever;"],[2,"your God, O Zion, to all generations."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD,"],[2,"for it is good to sing praises to our God;"],[2,"for it is pleasant and fitting to praise him."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD builds up Jerusalem."],[2,"He gathers together the outcasts of Israel."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He heals the broken in heart,"],[2,"and binds up their wounds."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He counts the number of the stars."],[2,"He calls them all by their names."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Great is our Lord, and mighty in power."],[2,"His understanding is infinite."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD upholds the humble."],[2,"He brings the wicked down to the ground."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to the LORD with thanksgiving."],[2,"Sing praises on the harp to our God,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"who covers the sky with clouds,"],[2,"who prepares rain for the earth,"],[2,"who makes grass grow on the mountains."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He provides food for the livestock,"],[2,"and for the young ravens when they call."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He doesn\u2019t delight in the strength of the horse."],[2,"He takes no pleasure in the legs of a man."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD takes pleasure in those who fear him,"],[2,"in those who hope in his loving kindness."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD, Jerusalem!"],[2,"Praise your God, Zion!"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has strengthened the bars of your gates."],[2,"He has blessed your children within you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He makes peace in your borders."],[2,"He fills you with the finest of the wheat."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He sends out his commandment to the earth."],[2,"His word runs very swiftly."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He gives snow like wool,"],[2,"and scatters frost like ashes."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He hurls down his hail like pebbles."],[2,"Who can stand before his cold?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He sends out his word, and melts them."],[2,"He causes his wind to blow, and the waters flow."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He shows his word to Jacob,"],[2,"his statutes and his ordinances to Israel."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He has not done this for just any nation."],[2,"They don\u2019t know his ordinances."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Praise the LORD from the heavens!"],[2,"Praise him in the heights!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise him, all his angels!"],[2,"Praise him, all his army!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise him, sun and moon!"],[2,"Praise him, all you shining stars!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise him, you heavens of heavens,"],[2,"you waters that are above the heavens."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"for he commanded, and they were created."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He has also established them forever and ever."],[2,"He has made a decree which will not pass away."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD from the earth,"],[2,"you great sea creatures, and all depths,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"lightning and hail, snow and clouds,"],[2,"stormy wind, fulfilling his word,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"mountains and all hills,"],[2,"fruit trees and all cedars,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"wild animals and all livestock,"],[2,"small creatures and flying birds,"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"kings of the earth and all peoples,"],[2,"princes and all judges of the earth,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"both young men and maidens,"],[2,"old men and children."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"for his name alone is exalted."],[2,"His glory is above the earth and the heavens."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He has lifted up the horn of his people,"],[2,"the praise of all his saints,"],[2,"even of the children of Israel, a people near to him."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Sing to the LORD a new song,"],[2,"his praise in the assembly of the saints."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let Israel rejoice in him who made them."],[2,"Let the children of Zion be joyful in their King."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them praise his name in the dance!"],[2,"Let them sing praises to him with tambourine and harp!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD takes pleasure in his people."],[2,"He crowns the humble with salvation."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the saints rejoice in honor."],[2,"Let them sing for joy on their beds."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"May the high praises of God be in their mouths,"],[2,"and a two-edged sword in their hand,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"to execute vengeance on the nations,"],[2,"and punishments on the peoples;"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"to bind their kings with chains,"],[2,"and their nobles with fetters of iron;"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"to execute on them the written judgment."],[2,"All his saints have this honor."],[1,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise the LORD!"],[2,"Praise God in his sanctuary!"],[2,"Praise him in his heavens for his acts of power!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise him for his mighty acts!"],[2,"Praise him according to his excellent greatness!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise him with the sounding of the trumpet!"],[2,"Praise him with harp and lyre!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise him with tambourine and dancing!"],[2,"Praise him with stringed instruments and flute!"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Praise him with loud cymbals!"],[2,"Praise him with resounding cymbals!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Let everything that has breath praise the LORD!"],[2,"Praise the LORD!"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]}]]}},1290,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,s,h,i,a){h.exports={book:"Prov",name:"Proverbs",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The proverbs of Solomon, the son of David, king of Israel:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"to know wisdom and instruction;"],[2,"to discern the words of understanding;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"to receive instruction in wise dealing,"],[2,"in righteousness, justice, and equity;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"to give prudence to the simple,"],[2,"knowledge and discretion to the young man\u2014"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"that the wise man may hear, and increase in learning;"],[2,"that the man of understanding may attain to sound counsel;"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"to understand a proverb and parables,"],[2,"the words and riddles of the wise."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge,"],[2,"but the foolish despise wisdom and instruction."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, listen to your father\u2019s instruction,"],[2,"and don\u2019t forsake your mother\u2019s teaching;"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"for they will be a garland to grace your head,"],[2,"and chains around your neck."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, if sinners entice you,"],[2,"don\u2019t consent."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"If they say, \u201cCome with us."],[2,"Let\u2019s lie in wait for blood."],[2,"Let\u2019s lurk secretly for the innocent without cause."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Let\u2019s swallow them up alive like Sheol,"],[2,"and whole, like those who go down into the pit."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"We\u2019ll find all valuable wealth."],[2,"We\u2019ll fill our houses with plunder."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You shall cast your lot among us."],[2,"We\u2019ll all have one purse\u201d\u2014"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"my son, don\u2019t walk on the path with them."],[2,"Keep your foot from their path,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"for their feet run to evil."],[2,"They hurry to shed blood."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For the net is spread in vain in the sight of any bird;"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"but these lay in wait for their own blood."],[2,"They lurk secretly for their own lives."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"So are the ways of everyone who is greedy for gain."],[2,"It takes away the life of its owners."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Wisdom calls aloud in the street."],[2,"She utters her voice in the public squares."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"She calls at the head of noisy places."],[2,"At the entrance of the city gates, she utters her words:"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow long, you simple ones, will you love simplicity?"],[2,"How long will mockers delight themselves in mockery,"],[2,"and fools hate knowledge?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn at my reproof."],[2,"Behold, I will pour out my spirit on you."],[2,"I will make known my words to you."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Because I have called, and you have refused;"],[2,"I have stretched out my hand, and no one has paid attention;"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"but you have ignored all my counsel,"],[2,"and wanted none of my reproof;"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"I also will laugh at your disaster."],[2,"I will mock when calamity overtakes you,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"when calamity overtakes you like a storm,"],[2,"when your disaster comes on like a whirlwind,"],[2,"when distress and anguish come on you."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they will call on me, but I will not answer."],[2,"They will seek me diligently, but they will not find me,"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"because they hated knowledge,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t choose the fear of the LORD."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"They wanted none of my counsel."],[2,"They despised all my reproof."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore they will eat of the fruit of their own way,"],[2,"and be filled with their own schemes."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"For the backsliding of the simple will kill them."],[2,"The careless ease of fools will destroy them."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"But whoever listens to me will dwell securely,"],[2,"and will be at ease, without fear of harm.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, if you will receive my words,"],[2,"and store up my commandments within you,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"so as to turn your ear to wisdom,"],[2,"and apply your heart to understanding;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"yes, if you call out for discernment,"],[2,"and lift up your voice for understanding;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"if you seek her as silver,"],[2,"and search for her as for hidden treasures;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"then you will understand the fear of the LORD,"],[2,"and find the knowledge of God."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD gives wisdom."],[2,"Out of his mouth comes knowledge and understanding."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He lays up sound wisdom for the upright."],[2,"He is a shield to those who walk in integrity,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"that he may guard the paths of justice,"],[2,"and preserve the way of his saints."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Then you will understand righteousness and justice,"],[2,"equity and every good path."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For wisdom will enter into your heart."],[2,"Knowledge will be pleasant to your soul."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Discretion will watch over you."],[2,"Understanding will keep you,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"to deliver you from the way of evil,"],[2,"from the men who speak perverse things,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"who forsake the paths of uprightness,"],[2,"to walk in the ways of darkness,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"who rejoice to do evil,"],[2,"and delight in the perverseness of evil,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"who are crooked in their ways,"],[2,"and wayward in their paths,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"to deliver you from the strange woman,"],[2,"even from the foreigner who flatters with her words,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"who forsakes the friend of her youth,"],[2,"and forgets the covenant of her God;"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"for her house leads down to death,"],[2,"her paths to the departed spirits."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"None who go to her return again,"],[2,"neither do they attain to the paths of life."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore walk in the way of good men,"],[2,"and keep the paths of the righteous."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For the upright will dwell in the land."],[2,"The perfect will remain in it."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"But the wicked will be cut off from the land."],[2,"The treacherous will be rooted out of it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, don\u2019t forget my teaching,"],[2,"but let your heart keep my commandments,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"for they will add to you length of days,"],[2,"years of life, and peace."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let kindness and truth forsake you."],[2,"Bind them around your neck."],[2,"Write them on the tablet of your heart."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"So you will find favor,"],[2,"and good understanding in the sight of God and man."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Trust in the LORD with all your heart,"],[2,"and don\u2019t lean on your own understanding."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"In all your ways acknowledge him,"],[2,"and he will make your paths straight."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be wise in your own eyes."],[2,"Fear the LORD, and depart from evil."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"It will be health to your body,"],[2,"and nourishment to your bones."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Honor the LORD with your substance,"],[2,"with the first fruits of all your increase;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"so your barns will be filled with plenty,"],[2,"and your vats will overflow with new wine."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, don\u2019t despise the LORD\u2019s discipline,"],[2,"neither be weary of his correction;"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"for whom the LORD loves, he corrects,"],[2,"even as a father reproves the son in whom he delights."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Happy is the man who finds wisdom,"],[2,"the man who gets understanding."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For her good profit is better than getting silver,"],[2,"and her return is better than fine gold."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"She is more precious than rubies."],[2,"None of the things you can desire are to be compared to her."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Length of days is in her right hand."],[2,"In her left hand are riches and honor."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Her ways are ways of pleasantness."],[2,"All her paths are peace."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"She is a tree of life to those who lay hold of her."],[2,"Happy is everyone who retains her."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"By wisdom the LORD founded the earth."],[2,"By understanding, he established the heavens."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"By his knowledge, the depths were broken up,"],[2,"and the skies drop down the dew."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, let them not depart from your eyes."],[2,"Keep sound wisdom and discretion,"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"so they will be life to your soul,"],[2,"and grace for your neck."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Then you shall walk in your way securely."],[2,"Your foot won\u2019t stumble."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"When you lie down, you will not be afraid."],[2,"Yes, you will lie down, and your sleep will be sweet."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be afraid of sudden fear,"],[2,"neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it comes;"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"for the LORD will be your confidence,"],[2,"and will keep your foot from being taken."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t withhold good from those to whom it is due,"],[2,"when it is in the power of your hand to do it."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t say to your neighbor, \u201cGo, and come again;"],[2,"tomorrow I will give it to you,\u201d"],[2,"when you have it by you."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t devise evil against your neighbor,"],[2,"since he dwells securely by you."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t strive with a man without cause,"],[2,"if he has done you no harm."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t envy the man of violence."],[2,"Choose none of his ways."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"For the perverse is an abomination to the LORD,"],[2,"but his friendship is with the upright."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s curse is in the house of the wicked,"],[2,"but he blesses the habitation of the righteous."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely he mocks the mockers,"],[2,"but he gives grace to the humble."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"The wise will inherit glory,"],[2,"but shame will be the promotion of fools."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen, sons, to a father\u2019s instruction."],[2,"Pay attention and know understanding;"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"for I give you sound learning."],[2,"Don\u2019t forsake my law."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For I was a son to my father,"],[2,"tender and an only child in the sight of my mother."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He taught me, and said to me:"],[2,"\u201cLet your heart retain my words."],[2,"Keep my commandments, and live."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Get wisdom."],[2,"Get understanding."],[2,"Don\u2019t forget, and don\u2019t deviate from the words of my mouth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t forsake her, and she will preserve you."],[2,"Love her, and she will keep you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Wisdom is supreme."],[2,"Get wisdom."],[2,"Yes, though it costs all your possessions, get understanding."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Esteem her, and she will exalt you."],[2,"She will bring you to honor when you embrace her."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"She will give to your head a garland of grace."],[2,"She will deliver a crown of splendor to you.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen, my son, and receive my sayings."],[2,"The years of your life will be many."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I have taught you in the way of wisdom."],[2,"I have led you in straight paths."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"When you go, your steps will not be hampered."],[2,"When you run, you will not stumble."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Take firm hold of instruction."],[2,"Don\u2019t let her go."],[2,"Keep her, for she is your life."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t enter into the path of the wicked."],[2,"Don\u2019t walk in the way of evil men."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Avoid it, and don\u2019t pass by it."],[2,"Turn from it, and pass on."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For they don\u2019t sleep unless they do evil."],[2,"Their sleep is taken away, unless they make someone fall."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For they eat the bread of wickedness"],[2,"and drink the wine of violence."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"But the path of the righteous is like the dawning light"],[2,"that shines more and more until the perfect day."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The way of the wicked is like darkness."],[2,"They don\u2019t know what they stumble over."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, attend to my words."],[2,"Turn your ear to my sayings."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them not depart from your eyes."],[2,"Keep them in the center of your heart."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For they are life to those who find them,"],[2,"and health to their whole body."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Keep your heart with all diligence,"],[2,"for out of it is the wellspring of life."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Put away from yourself a perverse mouth."],[2,"Put corrupt lips far from you."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your eyes look straight ahead."],[2,"Fix your gaze directly before you."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Make the path of your feet level."],[2,"Let all of your ways be established."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t turn to the right hand nor to the left."],[2,"Remove your foot from evil."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, pay attention to my wisdom."],[2,"Turn your ear to my understanding,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"that you may maintain discretion,"],[2,"that your lips may preserve knowledge."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the lips of an adulteress drip honey."],[2,"Her mouth is smoother than oil,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"but in the end she is as bitter as wormwood,"],[2,"and as sharp as a two-edged sword."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Her feet go down to death."],[2,"Her steps lead straight to Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"She gives no thought to the way of life."],[2,"Her ways are crooked, and she doesn\u2019t know it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Now therefore, my sons, listen to me."],[2,"Don\u2019t depart from the words of my mouth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Remove your way far from her."],[2,"Don\u2019t come near the door of her house,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"lest you give your honor to others,"],[2,"and your years to the cruel one;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"lest strangers feast on your wealth,"],[2,"and your labors enrich another man\u2019s house."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You will groan at your latter end,"],[2,"when your flesh and your body are consumed,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"and say, \u201cHow I have hated instruction,"],[2,"and my heart despised reproof."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I haven\u2019t obeyed the voice of my teachers,"],[2,"nor turned my ear to those who instructed me!"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I have come to the brink of utter ruin,"],[2,"among the gathered assembly.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Drink water out of your own cistern,"],[2,"running water out of your own well."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Should your springs overflow in the streets,"],[2,"streams of water in the public squares?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be for yourself alone,"],[2,"not for strangers with you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your spring be blessed."],[2,"Rejoice in the wife of your youth."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"A loving doe and a graceful deer\u2014"],[2,"let her breasts satisfy you at all times."],[2,"Be captivated always with her love."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"For why should you, my son, be captivated with an adulteress?"],[2,"Why embrace the bosom of another?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For the ways of man are before the LORD\u2019s eyes."],[2,"He examines all his paths."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The evil deeds of the wicked ensnare him."],[2,"The cords of his sin hold him firmly."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"He will die for lack of instruction."],[2,"In the greatness of his folly, he will go astray."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, if you have become collateral for your neighbor,"],[2,"if you have struck your hands in pledge for a stranger,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"you are trapped by the words of your mouth;"],[2,"you are ensnared with the words of your mouth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Do this now, my son, and deliver yourself,"],[2,"since you have come into the hand of your neighbor."],[1,"Go, humble yourself."],[2,"Press your plea with your neighbor."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Give no sleep to your eyes,"],[2,"nor slumber to your eyelids."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Free yourself, like a gazelle from the hand of the hunter,"],[2,"like a bird from the snare of the fowler."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Go to the ant, you sluggard."],[2,"Consider her ways, and be wise;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"which having no chief, overseer, or ruler,"]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"provides her bread in the summer,"],[2,"and gathers her food in the harvest."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"How long will you sleep, sluggard?"],[2,"When will you arise out of your sleep?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"A little sleep, a little slumber,"],[2,"a little folding of the hands to sleep\u2014"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"so your poverty will come as a robber,"],[2,"and your scarcity as an armed man."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"A worthless person, a man of iniquity,"],[2,"is he who walks with a perverse mouth,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"who winks with his eyes, who signals with his feet,"],[2,"who motions with his fingers,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"in whose heart is perverseness,"],[2,"who devises evil continually,"],[2,"who always sows discord."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore his calamity will come suddenly."],[2,"He will be broken suddenly, and that without remedy."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"There are six things which the LORD hates;"],[2,"yes, seven which are an abomination to him:"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"arrogant eyes, a lying tongue,"],[2,"hands that shed innocent blood,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"a heart that devises wicked schemes,"],[2,"feet that are swift in running to mischief,"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"a false witness who utters lies,"],[2,"and he who sows discord among brothers."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, keep your father\u2019s commandment,"],[2,"and don\u2019t forsake your mother\u2019s teaching."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Bind them continually on your heart."],[2,"Tie them around your neck."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"When you walk, it will lead you."],[2,"When you sleep, it will watch over you."],[2,"When you awake, it will talk with you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"For the commandment is a lamp,"],[2,"and the law is light."],[2,"Reproofs of instruction are the way of life,"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"to keep you from the immoral woman,"],[2,"from the flattery of the wayward wife\u2019s tongue."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t lust after her beauty in your heart,"],[2,"neither let her captivate you with her eyelids."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"For a prostitute reduces you to a piece of bread."],[2,"The adulteress hunts for your precious life."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Can a man scoop fire into his lap,"],[2,"and his clothes not be burned?"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Or can one walk on hot coals,"],[2,"and his feet not be scorched?"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"So is he who goes in to his neighbor\u2019s wife."],[2,"Whoever touches her will not be unpunished."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Men don\u2019t despise a thief"],[2,"if he steals to satisfy himself when he is hungry,"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"but if he is found, he shall restore seven times."],[2,"He shall give all the wealth of his house."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"He who commits adultery with a woman is void of understanding."],[2,"He who does it destroys his own soul."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"He will get wounds and dishonor."],[2,"His reproach will not be wiped away."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"For jealousy arouses the fury of the husband."],[2,"He won\u2019t spare in the day of vengeance."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"He won\u2019t regard any ransom,"],[2,"neither will he rest content, though you give many gifts."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, keep my words."],[2,"Lay up my commandments within you."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Keep my commandments and live!"],[2,"Guard my teaching as the apple of your eye."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Bind them on your fingers."],[2,"Write them on the tablet of your heart."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Tell wisdom, \u201cYou are my sister.\u201d"],[2,"Call understanding your relative,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"that they may keep you from the strange woman,"],[2,"from the foreigner who flatters with her words."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For at the window of my house,"],[2,"I looked out through my lattice."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I saw among the simple ones."],[2,"I discerned among the youths a young man void of understanding,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"passing through the street near her corner,"],[2,"he went the way to her house,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"in the twilight, in the evening of the day,"],[2,"in the middle of the night and in the darkness."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, there a woman met him with the attire of a prostitute,"],[2,"and with crafty intent."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"She is loud and defiant."],[2,"Her feet don\u2019t stay in her house."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Now she is in the streets, now in the squares,"],[2,"and lurking at every corner."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"So she caught him, and kissed him."],[2,"With an impudent face she said to him:"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSacrifices of peace offerings are with me."],[2,"Today I have paid my vows."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I came out to meet you,"],[2,"to diligently seek your face,"],[2,"and I have found you."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I have spread my couch with carpets of tapestry,"],[2,"with striped cloths of the yarn of Egypt."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Come, let\u2019s take our fill of loving until the morning."],[2,"Let\u2019s solace ourselves with loving."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"For my husband isn\u2019t at home."],[2,"He has gone on a long journey."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He has taken a bag of money with him."],[2,"He will come home at the full moon.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"With persuasive words, she led him astray."],[2,"With the flattering of her lips, she seduced him."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"He followed her immediately,"],[2,"as an ox goes to the slaughter,"],[2,"as a fool stepping into a noose."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Until an arrow strikes through his liver,"],[2,"as a bird hurries to the snare,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t know that it will cost his life."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Now therefore, sons, listen to me."],[2,"Pay attention to the words of my mouth."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let your heart turn to her ways."],[2,"Don\u2019t go astray in her paths,"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"for she has thrown down many wounded."],[2,"Yes, all her slain are a mighty army."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Her house is the way to Sheol,"],[2,"going down to the rooms of death."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Doesn\u2019t wisdom cry out?"],[2,"Doesn\u2019t understanding raise her voice?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"On the top of high places by the way,"],[2,"where the paths meet, she stands."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Beside the gates, at the entry of the city,"],[2,"at the entry doors, she cries aloud:"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI call to you men!"],[2,"I send my voice to the sons of mankind."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You simple, understand prudence!"],[2,"You fools, be of an understanding heart!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, for I will speak excellent things."],[2,"The opening of my lips is for right things."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For my mouth speaks truth."],[2,"Wickedness is an abomination to my lips."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"All the words of my mouth are in righteousness."],[2,"There is nothing crooked or perverse in them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They are all plain to him who understands,"],[2,"right to those who find knowledge."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Receive my instruction rather than silver,"],[2,"knowledge rather than choice gold."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For wisdom is better than rubies."],[2,"All the things that may be desired can\u2019t be compared to it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI, wisdom, have made prudence my dwelling."],[2,"Find out knowledge and discretion."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD is to hate evil."],[2,"I hate pride, arrogance, the evil way, and the perverse mouth."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Counsel and sound knowledge are mine."],[2,"I have understanding and power."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"By me kings reign,"],[2,"and princes decree justice."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"By me princes rule,"],[2,"nobles, and all the righteous rulers of the earth."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I love those who love me."],[2,"Those who seek me diligently will find me."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"With me are riches, honor,"],[2,"enduring wealth, and prosperity."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"My fruit is better than gold, yes, than fine gold,"],[2,"my yield than choice silver."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"I walk in the way of righteousness,"],[2,"in the middle of the paths of justice,"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"that I may give wealth to those who love me."],[2,"I fill their treasuries."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe LORD possessed me in the beginning of his work,"],[2,"before his deeds of old."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I was set up from everlasting, from the beginning,"],[2,"before the earth existed."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"When there were no depths, I was born,"],[2,"when there were no springs abounding with water."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Before the mountains were settled in place,"],[2,"before the hills, I was born;"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"while as yet he had not made the earth, nor the fields,"],[2,"nor the beginning of the dust of the world."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"When he established the heavens, I was there."],[2,"When he set a circle on the surface of the deep,"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"when he established the clouds above,"],[2,"when the springs of the deep became strong,"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"when he gave to the sea its boundary,"],[2,"that the waters should not violate his commandment,"],[2,"when he marked out the foundations of the earth,"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"then I was the craftsman by his side."],[2,"I was a delight day by day,"],[2,"always rejoicing before him,"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"rejoicing in his whole world."],[2,"My delight was with the sons of men."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow therefore, my sons, listen to me,"],[2,"for blessed are those who keep my ways."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear instruction, and be wise."],[2,"Don\u2019t refuse it."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man who hears me,"],[2,"watching daily at my gates,"],[2,"waiting at my door posts."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"For whoever finds me finds life,"],[2,"and will obtain favor from the LORD."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"But he who sins against me wrongs his own soul."],[2,"All those who hate me love death.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Wisdom has built her house."],[2,"She has carved out her seven pillars."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"She has prepared her meat."],[2,"She has mixed her wine."],[2,"She has also set her table."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"She has sent out her maidens."],[2,"She cries from the highest places of the city:"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhoever is simple, let him turn in here!\u201d"],[2,"As for him who is void of understanding, she says to him,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCome, eat some of my bread,"],[2,"Drink some of the wine which I have mixed!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Leave your simple ways, and live."],[2,"Walk in the way of understanding.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"One who corrects a mocker invites insult."],[2,"One who reproves a wicked man invites abuse."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t reprove a scoffer, lest he hate you."],[2,"Reprove a wise person, and he will love you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Instruct a wise person, and he will be still wiser."],[2,"Teach a righteous person, and he will increase in learning."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom."],[2,"The knowledge of the Holy One is understanding."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For by me your days will be multiplied."],[2,"The years of your life will be increased."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"If you are wise, you are wise for yourself."],[2,"If you mock, you alone will bear it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The foolish woman is loud,"],[2,"undisciplined, and knows nothing."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"She sits at the door of her house,"],[2,"on a seat in the high places of the city,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"to call to those who pass by,"],[2,"who go straight on their ways,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhoever is simple, let him turn in here.\u201d"],[2,"As for him who is void of understanding, she says to him,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cStolen water is sweet."],[2,"Food eaten in secret is pleasant.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"But he doesn\u2019t know that the departed spirits are there,"],[2,"that her guests are in the depths of Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The proverbs of Solomon."],[1,"A wise son makes a glad father;"],[2,"but a foolish son brings grief to his mother."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Treasures of wickedness profit nothing,"],[2,"but righteousness delivers from death."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will not allow the soul of the righteous to go hungry,"],[2,"but he thrusts away the desire of the wicked."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He becomes poor who works with a lazy hand,"],[2,"but the hand of the diligent brings wealth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He who gathers in summer is a wise son,"],[2,"but he who sleeps during the harvest is a son who causes shame."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessings are on the head of the righteous,"],[2,"but violence covers the mouth of the wicked."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The memory of the righteous is blessed,"],[2,"but the name of the wicked will rot."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The wise in heart accept commandments,"],[2,"but a chattering fool will fall."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He who walks blamelessly walks surely,"],[2,"but he who perverts his ways will be found out."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"One who winks with the eye causes sorrow,"],[2,"but a chattering fool will fall."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The mouth of the righteous is a spring of life,"],[2,"but violence covers the mouth of the wicked."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Hatred stirs up strife,"],[2,"but love covers all wrongs."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Wisdom is found on the lips of him who has discernment,"],[2,"but a rod is for the back of him who is void of understanding."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Wise men lay up knowledge,"],[2,"but the mouth of the foolish is near ruin."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The rich man\u2019s wealth is his strong city."],[2,"The destruction of the poor is their poverty."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The labor of the righteous leads to life."],[2,"The increase of the wicked leads to sin."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He is in the way of life who heeds correction,"],[2,"but he who forsakes reproof leads others astray."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"He who hides hatred has lying lips."],[2,"He who utters a slander is a fool."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"In the multitude of words there is no lack of disobedience,"],[2,"but he who restrains his lips does wisely."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The tongue of the righteous is like choice silver."],[2,"The heart of the wicked is of little worth."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The lips of the righteous feed many,"],[2,"but the foolish die for lack of understanding."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s blessing brings wealth,"],[2,"and he adds no trouble to it."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"It is a fool\u2019s pleasure to do wickedness,"],[2,"but wisdom is a man of understanding\u2019s pleasure."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"What the wicked fear will overtake them,"],[2,"but the desire of the righteous will be granted."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"When the whirlwind passes, the wicked is no more;"],[2,"but the righteous stand firm forever."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"As vinegar to the teeth, and as smoke to the eyes,"],[2,"so is the sluggard to those who send him."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD prolongs days,"],[2,"but the years of the wicked shall be shortened."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"The prospect of the righteous is joy,"],[2,"but the hope of the wicked will perish."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"The way of the LORD is a stronghold to the upright,"],[2,"but it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous will never be removed,"],[2,"but the wicked will not dwell in the land."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"The mouth of the righteous produces wisdom,"],[2,"but the perverse tongue will be cut off."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"The lips of the righteous know what is acceptable,"],[2,"but the mouth of the wicked is perverse."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"A false balance is an abomination to the LORD,"],[2,"but accurate weights are his delight."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"When pride comes, then comes shame,"],[2,"but with humility comes wisdom."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The integrity of the upright shall guide them,"],[2,"but the perverseness of the treacherous shall destroy them."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Riches don\u2019t profit in the day of wrath,"],[2,"but righteousness delivers from death."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteousness of the blameless will direct his way,"],[2,"but the wicked shall fall by his own wickedness."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteousness of the upright shall deliver them,"],[2,"but the unfaithful will be trapped by evil desires."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"When a wicked man dies, hope perishes,"],[2,"and expectation of power comes to nothing."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"A righteous person is delivered out of trouble,"],[2,"and the wicked takes his place."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"With his mouth the godless man destroys his neighbor,"],[2,"but the righteous will be delivered through knowledge."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"When it goes well with the righteous, the city rejoices."],[2,"When the wicked perish, there is shouting."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"By the blessing of the upright, the city is exalted,"],[2,"but it is overthrown by the mouth of the wicked."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"One who despises his neighbor is void of wisdom,"],[2,"but a man of understanding holds his peace."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"One who brings gossip betrays a confidence,"],[2,"but one who is of a trustworthy spirit is one who keeps a secret."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Where there is no wise guidance, the nation falls,"],[2,"but in the multitude of counselors there is victory."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is collateral for a stranger will suffer for it,"],[2,"but he who refuses pledges of collateral is secure."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"A gracious woman obtains honor,"],[2,"but violent men obtain riches."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The merciful man does good to his own soul,"],[2,"but he who is cruel troubles his own flesh."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Wicked people earn deceitful wages,"],[2,"but one who sows righteousness reaps a sure reward."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is truly righteous gets life."],[2,"He who pursues evil gets death."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who are perverse in heart are an abomination to the LORD,"],[2,"but those whose ways are blameless are his delight."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Most certainly, the evil man will not be unpunished,"],[2,"but the offspring of the righteous will be delivered."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Like a gold ring in a pig\u2019s snout,"],[2,"is a beautiful woman who lacks discretion."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The desire of the righteous is only good."],[2,"The expectation of the wicked is wrath."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"There is one who scatters, and increases yet more."],[2,"There is one who withholds more than is appropriate, but gains poverty."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The liberal soul shall be made fat."],[2,"He who waters shall be watered also himself."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"People curse someone who withholds grain,"],[2,"but blessing will be on the head of him who sells it."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"He who diligently seeks good seeks favor,"],[2,"but he who searches after evil, it shall come to him."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"He who trusts in his riches will fall,"],[2,"but the righteous shall flourish as the green leaf."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"He who troubles his own house shall inherit the wind."],[2,"The foolish shall be servant to the wise of heart."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The fruit of the righteous is a tree of life."],[2,"He who is wise wins souls."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the righteous shall be repaid on the earth,"],[2,"how much more the wicked and the sinner!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever loves correction loves knowledge,"],[2,"but he who hates reproof is stupid."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"A good man shall obtain favor from the LORD,"],[2,"but he will condemn a man of wicked plans."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A man shall not be established by wickedness,"],[2,"but the root of the righteous shall not be moved."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"A worthy woman is the crown of her husband,"],[2,"but a disgraceful wife is as rottenness in his bones."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The thoughts of the righteous are just,"],[2,"but the advice of the wicked is deceitful."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The words of the wicked are about lying in wait for blood,"],[2,"but the speech of the upright rescues them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked are overthrown, and are no more,"],[2,"but the house of the righteous shall stand."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"A man shall be commended according to his wisdom,"],[2,"but he who has a warped mind shall be despised."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is he who is little known, and has a servant,"],[2,"than he who honors himself and lacks bread."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"A righteous man respects the life of his animal,"],[2,"but the tender mercies of the wicked are cruel."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He who tills his land shall have plenty of bread,"],[2,"but he who chases fantasies is void of understanding."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked desires the plunder of evil men,"],[2,"but the root of the righteous flourishes."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"An evil man is trapped by sinfulness of lips,"],[2,"but the righteous shall come out of trouble."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"A man shall be satisfied with good by the fruit of his mouth."],[2,"The work of a man\u2019s hands shall be rewarded to him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The way of a fool is right in his own eyes,"],[2,"but he who is wise listens to counsel."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"A fool shows his annoyance the same day,"],[2,"but one who overlooks an insult is prudent."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is truthful testifies honestly,"],[2,"but a false witness lies."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"There is one who speaks rashly like the piercing of a sword,"],[2,"but the tongue of the wise heals."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Truth\u2019s lips will be established forever,"],[2,"but a lying tongue is only momentary."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Deceit is in the heart of those who plot evil,"],[2,"but joy comes to the promoters of peace."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"No mischief shall happen to the righteous,"],[2,"but the wicked shall be filled with evil."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Lying lips are an abomination to the LORD,"],[2,"but those who do the truth are his delight."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"A prudent man keeps his knowledge,"],[2,"but the hearts of fools proclaim foolishness."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The hands of the diligent ones shall rule,"],[2,"but laziness ends in slave labor."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Anxiety in a man\u2019s heart weighs it down,"],[2,"but a kind word makes it glad."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"A righteous person is cautious in friendship,"],[2,"but the way of the wicked leads them astray."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The slothful man doesn\u2019t roast his game,"],[2,"but the possessions of diligent men are prized."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"In the way of righteousness is life;"],[2,"in its path there is no death."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"A wise son listens to his father\u2019s instruction,"],[2,"but a scoffer doesn\u2019t listen to rebuke."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"By the fruit of his lips, a man enjoys good things,"],[2,"but the unfaithful crave violence."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He who guards his mouth guards his soul."],[2,"One who opens wide his lips comes to ruin."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The soul of the sluggard desires, and has nothing,"],[2,"but the desire of the diligent shall be fully satisfied."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"A righteous man hates lies,"],[2,"but a wicked man brings shame and disgrace."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Righteousness guards the way of integrity,"],[2,"but wickedness overthrows the sinner."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"There are some who pretend to be rich, yet have nothing."],[2,"There are some who pretend to be poor, yet have great wealth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The ransom of a man\u2019s life is his riches,"],[2,"but the poor hear no threats."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The light of the righteous shines brightly,"],[2,"but the lamp of the wicked is snuffed out."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Pride only breeds quarrels,"],[2,"but wisdom is with people who take advice."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Wealth gained dishonestly dwindles away,"],[2,"but he who gathers by hand makes it grow."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Hope deferred makes the heart sick,"],[2,"but when longing is fulfilled, it is a tree of life."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever despises instruction will pay for it,"],[2,"but he who respects a command will be rewarded."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The teaching of the wise is a spring of life,"],[2,"to turn from the snares of death."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Good understanding wins favor,"],[2,"but the way of the unfaithful is hard."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Every prudent man acts from knowledge,"],[2,"but a fool exposes folly."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"A wicked messenger falls into trouble,"],[2,"but a trustworthy envoy gains healing."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Poverty and shame come to him who refuses discipline,"],[2,"but he who heeds correction shall be honored."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Longing fulfilled is sweet to the soul,"],[2,"but fools detest turning from evil."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"One who walks with wise men grows wise,"],[2,"but a companion of fools suffers harm."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Misfortune pursues sinners,"],[2,"but prosperity rewards the righteous."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"A good man leaves an inheritance to his children\u2019s children,"],[2,"but the wealth of the sinner is stored for the righteous."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"An abundance of food is in poor people\u2019s fields,"],[2,"but injustice sweeps it away."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"One who spares the rod hates his son,"],[2,"but one who loves him is careful to discipline him."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous one eats to the satisfying of his soul,"],[2,"but the belly of the wicked goes hungry."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Every wise woman builds her house,"],[2,"but the foolish one tears it down with her own hands."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He who walks in his uprightness fears the LORD,"],[2,"but he who is perverse in his ways despises him."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The fool\u2019s talk brings a rod to his back,"],[2,"but the lips of the wise protect them."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Where no oxen are, the crib is clean,"],[2,"but much increase is by the strength of the ox."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"A truthful witness will not lie,"],[2,"but a false witness pours out lies."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"A scoffer seeks wisdom, and doesn\u2019t find it,"],[2,"but knowledge comes easily to a discerning person."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Stay away from a foolish man,"],[2,"for you won\u2019t find knowledge on his lips."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The wisdom of the prudent is to think about his way,"],[2,"but the folly of fools is deceit."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Fools mock at making atonement for sins,"],[2,"but among the upright there is good will."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart knows its own bitterness and joy;"],[2,"he will not share these with a stranger."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The house of the wicked will be overthrown,"],[2,"but the tent of the upright will flourish."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"There is a way which seems right to a man,"],[2,"but in the end it leads to death."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Even in laughter the heart may be sorrowful,"],[2,"and mirth may end in heaviness."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The unfaithful will be repaid for his own ways;"],[2,"likewise a good man will be rewarded for his ways."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"A simple man believes everything,"],[2,"but the prudent man carefully considers his ways."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"A wise man fears and shuns evil,"],[2,"but the fool is hot headed and reckless."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is quick to become angry will commit folly,"],[2,"and a crafty man is hated."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The simple inherit folly,"],[2,"but the prudent are crowned with knowledge."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The evil bow down before the good,"],[2,"and the wicked at the gates of the righteous."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The poor person is shunned even by his own neighbor,"],[2,"but the rich person has many friends."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He who despises his neighbor sins,"],[2,"but he who has pity on the poor is blessed."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t they go astray who plot evil?"],[2,"But love and faithfulness belong to those who plan good."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"In all hard work there is profit,"],[2,"but the talk of the lips leads only to poverty."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The crown of the wise is their riches,"],[2,"but the folly of fools crowns them with folly."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"A truthful witness saves souls,"],[2,"but a false witness is deceitful."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"In the fear of the LORD is a secure fortress,"],[2,"and he will be a refuge for his children."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life,"],[2,"turning people from the snares of death."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"In the multitude of people is the king\u2019s glory,"],[2,"but in the lack of people is the destruction of the prince."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is slow to anger has great understanding,"],[2,"but he who has a quick temper displays folly."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The life of the body is a heart at peace,"],[2,"but envy rots the bones."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"He who oppresses the poor shows contempt for his Maker,"],[2,"but he who is kind to the needy honors him."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked is brought down in his calamity,"],[2,"but in death, the righteous has a refuge."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Wisdom rests in the heart of one who has understanding,"],[2,"and is even made known in the inward part of fools."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Righteousness exalts a nation,"],[2,"but sin is a disgrace to any people."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"The king\u2019s favor is toward a servant who deals wisely,"],[2,"but his wrath is toward one who causes shame."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"A gentle answer turns away wrath,"],[2,"but a harsh word stirs up anger."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The tongue of the wise commends knowledge,"],[2,"but the mouths of fools gush out folly."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s eyes are everywhere,"],[2,"keeping watch on the evil and the good."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"A gentle tongue is a tree of life,"],[2,"but deceit in it crushes the spirit."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"A fool despises his father\u2019s correction,"],[2,"but he who heeds reproof shows prudence."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"In the house of the righteous is much treasure,"],[2,"but the income of the wicked brings trouble."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The lips of the wise spread knowledge;"],[2,"not so with the heart of fools."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The sacrifice made by the wicked is an abomination to the LORD,"],[2,"but the prayer of the upright is his delight."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The way of the wicked is an abomination to the LORD,"],[2,"but he loves him who follows after righteousness."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"There is stern discipline for one who forsakes the way."],[2,"Whoever hates reproof shall die."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Sheol and Abaddon are before the LORD\u2014"],[2,"how much more then the hearts of the children of men!"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"A scoffer doesn\u2019t love to be reproved;"],[2,"he will not go to the wise."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"A glad heart makes a cheerful face,"],[2,"but an aching heart breaks the spirit."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart of one who has understanding seeks knowledge,"],[2,"but the mouths of fools feed on folly."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"All the days of the afflicted are wretched,"],[2,"but one who has a cheerful heart enjoys a continual feast."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is little, with the fear of the LORD,"],[2,"than great treasure with trouble."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is a dinner of herbs, where love is,"],[2,"than a fattened calf with hatred."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"A wrathful man stirs up contention,"],[2,"but one who is slow to anger appeases strife."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The way of the sluggard is like a thorn patch,"],[2,"but the path of the upright is a highway."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"A wise son makes a father glad,"],[2,"but a foolish man despises his mother."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Folly is joy to one who is void of wisdom,"],[2,"but a man of understanding keeps his way straight."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Where there is no counsel, plans fail;"],[2,"but in a multitude of counselors they are established."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Joy comes to a man with the reply of his mouth."],[2,"How good is a word at the right time!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The path of life leads upward for the wise,"],[2,"to keep him from going downward to Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will uproot the house of the proud,"],[2,"but he will keep the widow\u2019s borders intact."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD detests the thoughts of the wicked,"],[2,"but the thoughts of the pure are pleasing."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is greedy for gain troubles his own house,"],[2,"but he who hates bribes will live."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart of the righteous weighs answers,"],[2,"but the mouth of the wicked gushes out evil."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is far from the wicked,"],[2,"but he hears the prayer of the righteous."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The light of the eyes rejoices the heart."],[2,"Good news gives health to the bones."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"The ear that listens to reproof lives,"],[2,"and will be at home among the wise."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"He who refuses correction despises his own soul,"],[2,"but he who listens to reproof gets understanding."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD teaches wisdom."],[2,"Before honor is humility."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The plans of the heart belong to man,"],[2,"but the answer of the tongue is from the LORD."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"All the ways of a man are clean in his own eyes,"],[2,"but the LORD weighs the motives."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Commit your deeds to the LORD,"],[2,"and your plans shall succeed."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has made everything for its own end\u2014"],[2,"yes, even the wicked for the day of evil."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Everyone who is proud in heart is an abomination to the LORD;"],[2,"they shall certainly not be unpunished."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"By mercy and truth iniquity is atoned for."],[2,"By the fear of the LORD men depart from evil."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"When a man\u2019s ways please the LORD,"],[2,"he makes even his enemies to be at peace with him."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is a little with righteousness,"],[2,"than great revenues with injustice."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"A man\u2019s heart plans his course,"],[2,"but the LORD directs his steps."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Inspired judgments are on the lips of the king."],[2,"He shall not betray his mouth."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Honest balances and scales are the LORD\u2019s;"],[2,"all the weights in the bag are his work."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"It is an abomination for kings to do wrong,"],[2,"for the throne is established by righteousness."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Righteous lips are the delight of kings."],[2,"They value one who speaks the truth."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The king\u2019s wrath is a messenger of death,"],[2,"but a wise man will pacify it."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"In the light of the king\u2019s face is life."],[2,"His favor is like a cloud of the spring rain."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"How much better it is to get wisdom than gold!"],[2,"Yes, to get understanding is to be chosen rather than silver."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The highway of the upright is to depart from evil."],[2,"He who keeps his way preserves his soul."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Pride goes before destruction,"],[2,"and an arrogant spirit before a fall."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"It is better to be of a lowly spirit with the poor,"],[2,"than to divide the plunder with the proud."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He who heeds the Word finds prosperity."],[2,"Whoever trusts in the LORD is blessed."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The wise in heart shall be called prudent."],[2,"Pleasantness of the lips promotes instruction."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Understanding is a fountain of life to one who has it,"],[2,"but the punishment of fools is their folly."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart of the wise instructs his mouth,"],[2,"and adds learning to his lips."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Pleasant words are a honeycomb,"],[2,"sweet to the soul, and health to the bones."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"There is a way which seems right to a man,"],[2,"but in the end it leads to death."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The appetite of the laboring man labors for him,"],[2,"for his mouth urges him on."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"A worthless man devises mischief."],[2,"His speech is like a scorching fire."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"A perverse man stirs up strife."],[2,"A whisperer separates close friends."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"A man of violence entices his neighbor,"],[2,"and leads him in a way that is not good."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"One who winks his eyes to plot perversities,"],[2,"one who compresses his lips, is bent on evil."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Gray hair is a crown of glory."],[2,"It is attained by a life of righteousness."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"One who is slow to anger is better than the mighty;"],[2,"one who rules his spirit, than he who takes a city."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"The lot is cast into the lap,"],[2,"but its every decision is from the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is a dry morsel with quietness,"],[2,"than a house full of feasting with strife."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"A servant who deals wisely will rule over a son who causes shame,"],[2,"and shall have a part in the inheritance among the brothers."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The refining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold,"],[2,"but the LORD tests the hearts."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"An evildoer heeds wicked lips."],[2,"A liar gives ear to a mischievous tongue."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever mocks the poor reproaches his Maker."],[2,"He who is glad at calamity shall not be unpunished."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Children\u2019s children are the crown of old men;"],[2,"the glory of children is their parents."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Excellent speech isn\u2019t fitting for a fool,"],[2,"much less do lying lips fit a prince."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"A bribe is a precious stone in the eyes of him who gives it;"],[2,"wherever he turns, he prospers."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He who covers an offense promotes love;"],[2,"but he who repeats a matter separates best friends."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"A rebuke enters deeper into one who has understanding"],[2,"than a hundred lashes into a fool."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"An evil man seeks only rebellion;"],[2,"therefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Let a bear robbed of her cubs meet a man,"],[2,"rather than a fool in his folly."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever rewards evil for good,"],[2,"evil shall not depart from his house."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The beginning of strife is like breaching a dam,"],[2,"therefore stop contention before quarreling breaks out."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He who justifies the wicked, and he who condemns the righteous,"],[2,"both of them alike are an abomination to the LORD."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Why is there money in the hand of a fool to buy wisdom,"],[2,"since he has no understanding?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"A friend loves at all times;"],[2,"and a brother is born for adversity."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"A man void of understanding strikes hands,"],[2,"and becomes collateral in the presence of his neighbor."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He who loves disobedience loves strife."],[2,"One who builds a high gate seeks destruction."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"One who has a perverse heart doesn\u2019t find prosperity,"],[2,"and one who has a deceitful tongue falls into trouble."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He who becomes the father of a fool grieves."],[2,"The father of a fool has no joy."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"A cheerful heart makes good medicine,"],[2,"but a crushed spirit dries up the bones."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"A wicked man receives a bribe in secret,"],[2,"to pervert the ways of justice."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Wisdom is before the face of one who has understanding,"],[2,"but the eyes of a fool wander to the ends of the earth."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"A foolish son brings grief to his father,"],[2,"and bitterness to her who bore him."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Also to punish the righteous is not good,"],[2,"nor to flog officials for their integrity."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"He who spares his words has knowledge."],[2,"He who is even tempered is a man of understanding."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Even a fool, when he keeps silent, is counted wise."],[2,"When he shuts his lips, he is thought to be discerning."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"A man who isolates himself pursues selfishness,"],[2,"and defies all sound judgment."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"A fool has no delight in understanding,"],[2,"but only in revealing his own opinion."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"When wickedness comes, contempt also comes,"],[2,"and with shame comes disgrace."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The words of a man\u2019s mouth are like deep waters."],[2,"The fountain of wisdom is like a flowing brook."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"To be partial to the faces of the wicked is not good,"],[2,"nor to deprive the innocent of justice."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"A fool\u2019s lips come into strife,"],[2,"and his mouth invites beatings."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"A fool\u2019s mouth is his destruction,"],[2,"and his lips are a snare to his soul."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The words of a gossip are like dainty morsels:"],[2,"they go down into a person\u2019s innermost parts."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"One who is slack in his work"],[2,"is brother to him who is a master of destruction."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s name is a strong tower:"],[2,"the righteous run to him, and are safe."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The rich man\u2019s wealth is his strong city,"],[2,"like an unscalable wall in his own imagination."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Before destruction the heart of man is proud,"],[2,"but before honor is humility."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He who answers before he hears,"],[2,"that is folly and shame to him."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"A man\u2019s spirit will sustain him in sickness,"],[2,"but a crushed spirit, who can bear?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart of the discerning gets knowledge."],[2,"The ear of the wise seeks knowledge."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"A man\u2019s gift makes room for him,"],[2,"and brings him before great men."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He who pleads his cause first seems right\u2014"],[2,"until another comes and questions him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The lot settles disputes,"],[2,"and keeps strong ones apart."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"A brother offended is more difficult than a fortified city."],[2,"Disputes are like the bars of a fortress."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"A man\u2019s stomach is filled with the fruit of his mouth."],[2,"With the harvest of his lips he is satisfied."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Death and life are in the power of the tongue;"],[2,"those who love it will eat its fruit."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever finds a wife finds a good thing,"],[2,"and obtains favor of the LORD."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The poor plead for mercy,"],[2,"but the rich answer harshly."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"A man of many companions may be ruined,"],[2,"but there is a friend who sticks closer than a brother."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is the poor who walks in his integrity"],[2,"than he who is perverse in his lips and is a fool."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"It isn\u2019t good to have zeal without knowledge,"],[2,"nor to be hasty with one\u2019s feet and miss the way."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The foolishness of man subverts his way;"],[2,"his heart rages against the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Wealth adds many friends,"],[2,"but the poor is separated from his friend."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"A false witness shall not be unpunished."],[2,"He who pours out lies shall not go free."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Many will entreat the favor of a ruler,"],[2,"and everyone is a friend to a man who gives gifts."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"All the relatives of the poor shun him;"],[2,"how much more do his friends avoid him!"],[2,"He pursues them with pleas, but they are gone."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He who gets wisdom loves his own soul."],[2,"He who keeps understanding shall find good."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"A false witness shall not be unpunished."],[2,"He who utters lies shall perish."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Delicate living is not appropriate for a fool,"],[2,"much less for a servant to have rule over princes."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The discretion of a man makes him slow to anger."],[2,"It is his glory to overlook an offense."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The king\u2019s wrath is like the roaring of a lion,"],[2,"but his favor is like dew on the grass."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"A foolish son is the calamity of his father."],[2,"A wife\u2019s quarrels are a continual dripping."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"House and riches are an inheritance from fathers,"],[2,"but a prudent wife is from the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Slothfulness casts into a deep sleep."],[2,"The idle soul shall suffer hunger."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He who keeps the commandment keeps his soul,"],[2,"but he who is contemptuous in his ways shall die."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He who has pity on the poor lends to the LORD;"],[2,"he will reward him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Discipline your son, for there is hope;"],[2,"don\u2019t be a willing party to his death."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"A hot-tempered man must pay the penalty,"],[2,"for if you rescue him, you must do it again."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen to counsel and receive instruction,"],[2,"that you may be wise in your latter end."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"There are many plans in a man\u2019s heart,"],[2,"but the LORD\u2019s counsel will prevail."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"That which makes a man to be desired is his kindness."],[2,"A poor man is better than a liar."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of the LORD leads to life, then contentment;"],[2,"he rests and will not be touched by trouble."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The sluggard buries his hand in the dish;"],[2,"he will not so much as bring it to his mouth again."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Flog a scoffer, and the simple will learn prudence;"],[2,"rebuke one who has understanding, and he will gain knowledge."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"He who robs his father and drives away his mother"],[2,"is a son who causes shame and brings reproach."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"If you stop listening to instruction, my son,"],[2,"you will stray from the words of knowledge."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"A corrupt witness mocks justice,"],[2,"and the mouth of the wicked gulps down iniquity."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Penalties are prepared for scoffers,"],[2,"and beatings for the backs of fools."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Wine is a mocker and beer is a brawler."],[2,"Whoever is led astray by them is not wise."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The terror of a king is like the roaring of a lion."],[2,"He who provokes him to anger forfeits his own life."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"It is an honor for a man to keep aloof from strife,"],[2,"but every fool will be quarreling."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The sluggard will not plow by reason of the winter;"],[2,"therefore he shall beg in harvest, and have nothing."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Counsel in the heart of man is like deep water,"],[2,"but a man of understanding will draw it out."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Many men claim to be men of unfailing love,"],[2,"but who can find a faithful man?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"A righteous man walks in integrity."],[2,"Blessed are his children after him."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"A king who sits on the throne of judgment"],[2,"scatters away all evil with his eyes."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can say, \u201cI have made my heart pure."],[2,"I am clean and without sin\u201d?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Differing weights and differing measures,"],[2,"both of them alike are an abomination to the LORD."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Even a child makes himself known by his doings,"],[2,"whether his work is pure, and whether it is right."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The hearing ear, and the seeing eye,"],[2,"the LORD has made even both of them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t love sleep, lest you come to poverty."],[2,"Open your eyes, and you shall be satisfied with bread."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIt\u2019s no good, it\u2019s no good,\u201d says the buyer;"],[2,"but when he is gone his way, then he boasts."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"There is gold and abundance of rubies,"],[2,"but the lips of knowledge are a rare jewel."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Take the garment of one who puts up collateral for a stranger;"],[2,"and hold him in pledge for a wayward woman."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Fraudulent food is sweet to a man,"],[2,"but afterwards his mouth is filled with gravel."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Plans are established by advice;"],[2,"by wise guidance you wage war!"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He who goes about as a tale-bearer reveals secrets;"],[2,"therefore don\u2019t keep company with him who opens wide his lips."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever curses his father or his mother,"],[2,"his lamp shall be put out in blackness of darkness."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"An inheritance quickly gained at the beginning"],[2,"won\u2019t be blessed in the end."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t say, \u201cI will pay back evil.\u201d"],[2,"Wait for the LORD, and he will save you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD detests differing weights,"],[2,"and dishonest scales are not pleasing."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"A man\u2019s steps are from the LORD;"],[2,"how then can man understand his way?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"It is a snare to a man to make a rash dedication,"],[2,"then later to consider his vows."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"A wise king winnows out the wicked,"],[2,"and drives the threshing wheel over them."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The spirit of man is the LORD\u2019s lamp,"],[2,"searching all his innermost parts."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Love and faithfulness keep the king safe."],[2,"His throne is sustained by love."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"The glory of young men is their strength."],[2,"The splendor of old men is their gray hair."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Wounding blows cleanse away evil,"],[2,"and beatings purge the innermost parts."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The king\u2019s heart is in the LORD\u2019s hand like the watercourses."],[2,"He turns it wherever he desires."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Every way of a man is right in his own eyes,"],[2,"but the LORD weighs the hearts."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"To do righteousness and justice"],[2,"is more acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"A high look and a proud heart,"],[2,"the lamp of the wicked, is sin."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The plans of the diligent surely lead to profit;"],[2,"and everyone who is hasty surely rushes to poverty."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Getting treasures by a lying tongue"],[2,"is a fleeting vapor for those who seek death."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The violence of the wicked will drive them away,"],[2,"because they refuse to do what is right."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The way of the guilty is devious,"],[2,"but the conduct of the innocent is upright."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop"],[2,"than to share a house with a contentious woman."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The soul of the wicked desires evil;"],[2,"his neighbor finds no mercy in his eyes."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"When the mocker is punished, the simple gains wisdom."],[2,"When the wise is instructed, he receives knowledge."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The Righteous One considers the house of the wicked,"],[2,"and brings the wicked to ruin."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever stops his ears at the cry of the poor,"],[2,"he will also cry out, but shall not be heard."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"A gift in secret pacifies anger,"],[2,"and a bribe in the cloak, strong wrath."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"It is joy to the righteous to do justice;"],[2,"but it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The man who wanders out of the way of understanding"],[2,"shall rest in the assembly of the departed spirits."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He who loves pleasure will be a poor man."],[2,"He who loves wine and oil won\u2019t be rich."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked is a ransom for the righteous,"],[2,"the treacherous for the upright."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"It is better to dwell in a desert land,"],[2,"than with a contentious and fretful woman."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"There is precious treasure and oil in the dwelling of the wise,"],[2,"but a foolish man swallows it up."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He who follows after righteousness and kindness"],[2,"finds life, righteousness, and honor."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"A wise man scales the city of the mighty,"],[2,"and brings down the strength of its confidence."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever guards his mouth and his tongue"],[2,"keeps his soul from troubles."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The proud and arrogant man\u2014\u201cScoffer\u201d is his name\u2014"],[2,"he works in the arrogance of pride."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The desire of the sluggard kills him,"],[2,"for his hands refuse to labor."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"There are those who covet greedily all day long;"],[2,"but the righteous give and don\u2019t withhold."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination\u2014"],[2,"how much more, when he brings it with a wicked mind!"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"A false witness will perish."],[2,"A man who listens speaks to eternity."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"A wicked man hardens his face;"],[2,"but as for the upright, he establishes his ways."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no wisdom nor understanding"],[2,"nor counsel against the LORD."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"The horse is prepared for the day of battle;"],[2,"but victory is with the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"A good name is more desirable than great riches,"],[2,"and loving favor is better than silver and gold."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The rich and the poor have this in common:"],[2,"The LORD is the maker of them all."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A prudent man sees danger and hides himself;"],[2,"but the simple pass on, and suffer for it."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The result of humility and the fear of the LORD"],[2,"is wealth, honor, and life."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Thorns and snares are in the path of the wicked;"],[2,"whoever guards his soul stays far from them."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Train up a child in the way he should go,"],[2,"and when he is old he will not depart from it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The rich rule over the poor."],[2,"The borrower is servant to the lender."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He who sows wickedness reaps trouble,"],[2,"and the rod of his fury will be destroyed."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He who has a generous eye will be blessed,"],[2,"for he shares his food with the poor."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Drive out the mocker, and strife will go out;"],[2,"yes, quarrels and insults will stop."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He who loves purity of heart and speaks gracefully"],[2,"is the king\u2019s friend."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s eyes watch over knowledge,"],[2,"but he frustrates the words of the unfaithful."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The sluggard says, \u201cThere is a lion outside!"],[2,"I will be killed in the streets!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The mouth of an adulteress is a deep pit."],[2,"He who is under the LORD\u2019s wrath will fall into it."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Folly is bound up in the heart of a child;"],[2,"the rod of discipline drives it far from him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever oppresses the poor for his own increase and whoever gives to the rich,"],[2,"both come to poverty."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn your ear, and listen to the words of the wise."],[2,"Apply your heart to my teaching."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For it is a pleasant thing if you keep them within you,"],[2,"if all of them are ready on your lips."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I teach you today, even you,"],[2,"so that your trust may be in the LORD."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Haven\u2019t I written to you thirty excellent things"],[2,"of counsel and knowledge,"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"To teach you truth, reliable words,"],[2,"to give sound answers to the ones who sent you?"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t exploit the poor because he is poor;"],[2,"and don\u2019t crush the needy in court;"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"for the LORD will plead their case,"],[2,"and plunder the life of those who plunder them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t befriend a hot-tempered man."],[2,"Don\u2019t associate with one who harbors anger,"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"lest you learn his ways"],[2,"and ensnare your soul."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t you be one of those who strike hands,"],[2,"of those who are collateral for debts."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"If you don\u2019t have means to pay,"],[2,"why should he take away your bed from under you?"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t move the ancient boundary stone"],[2,"which your fathers have set up."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you see a man skilled in his work?"],[2,"He will serve kings."],[2,"He won\u2019t serve obscure men."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"When you sit to eat with a ruler,"],[2,"consider diligently what is before you;"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"put a knife to your throat"],[2,"if you are a man given to appetite."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be desirous of his dainties,"],[2,"since they are deceitful food."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t weary yourself to be rich."],[2,"In your wisdom, show restraint."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you set your eyes on that which is not?"],[2,"For it certainly sprouts wings like an eagle and flies in the sky."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t eat the food of him who has a stingy eye,"],[2,"and don\u2019t crave his delicacies,"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"for as he thinks about the cost, so he is."],[2,"\u201cEat and drink!\u201d he says to you,"],[2,"but his heart is not with you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You will vomit up the morsel which you have eaten"],[2,"and waste your pleasant words."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t speak in the ears of a fool,"],[2,"for he will despise the wisdom of your words."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t move the ancient boundary stone."],[2,"Don\u2019t encroach on the fields of the fatherless,"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"for their Defender is strong."],[2,"He will plead their case against you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Apply your heart to instruction,"],[2,"and your ears to the words of knowledge."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t withhold correction from a child."],[2,"If you punish him with the rod, he will not die."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Punish him with the rod,"],[2,"and save his soul from Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, if your heart is wise,"],[2,"then my heart will be glad, even mine."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, my heart will rejoice"],[2,"when your lips speak what is right."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let your heart envy sinners,"],[2,"but rather fear the LORD all day long."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Indeed surely there is a future hope,"],[2,"and your hope will not be cut off."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen, my son, and be wise,"],[2,"and keep your heart on the right path!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be among ones drinking too much wine,"],[2,"or those who gorge themselves on meat;"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"for the drunkard and the glutton shall become poor;"],[2,"and drowsiness clothes them in rags."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen to your father who gave you life,"],[2,"and don\u2019t despise your mother when she is old."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Buy the truth, and don\u2019t sell it."],[2,"Get wisdom, discipline, and understanding."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The father of the righteous has great joy."],[2,"Whoever fathers a wise child delights in him."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your father and your mother be glad!"],[2,"Let her who bore you rejoice!"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, give me your heart;"],[2,"and let your eyes keep in my ways."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"For a prostitute is a deep pit;"],[2,"and a wayward wife is a narrow well."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, she lies in wait like a robber,"],[2,"and increases the unfaithful among men."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has woe?"],[2,"Who has sorrow?"],[2,"Who has strife?"],[2,"Who has complaints?"],[2,"Who has needless bruises?"],[2,"Who has bloodshot eyes?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who stay long at the wine;"],[2,"those who go to seek out mixed wine."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t look at the wine when it is red,"],[2,"when it sparkles in the cup,"],[2,"when it goes down smoothly."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"In the end, it bites like a snake,"],[2,"and poisons like a viper."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Your eyes will see strange things,"],[2,"and your mind will imagine confusing things."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, you will be as he who lies down in the middle of the sea,"],[2,"or as he who lies on top of the rigging:"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThey hit me, and I was not hurt!"],[2,"They beat me, and I don\u2019t feel it!"],[2,"When will I wake up? I can do it again."],[2,"I will look for more.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be envious of evil men,"],[2,"neither desire to be with them;"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"for their hearts plot violence"],[2,"and their lips talk about mischief."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Through wisdom a house is built;"],[2,"by understanding it is established;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"by knowledge the rooms are filled"],[2,"with all rare and beautiful treasure."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"A wise man has great power."],[2,"A knowledgeable man increases strength,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"for by wise guidance you wage your war,"],[2,"and victory is in many advisors."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Wisdom is too high for a fool."],[2,"He doesn\u2019t open his mouth in the gate."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"One who plots to do evil"],[2,"will be called a schemer."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The schemes of folly are sin."],[2,"The mocker is detested by men."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"If you falter in the time of trouble,"],[2,"your strength is small."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Rescue those who are being led away to death!"],[2,"Indeed, hold back those who are staggering to the slaughter!"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"If you say, \u201cBehold, we didn\u2019t know this,\u201d"],[2,"doesn\u2019t he who weighs the hearts consider it?"],[1,"He who keeps your soul, doesn\u2019t he know it?"],[2,"Shall he not give to every man according to his work?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, eat honey, for it is good,"],[2,"the droppings of the honeycomb, which are sweet to your taste;"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"so you shall know wisdom to be to your soul."],[2,"If you have found it, then there will be a reward:"],[2,"Your hope will not be cut off."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t lay in wait, wicked man, against the habitation of the righteous."],[2,"Don\u2019t destroy his resting place;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"for a righteous man falls seven times and rises up again,"],[2,"but the wicked are overthrown by calamity."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t rejoice when your enemy falls."],[2,"Don\u2019t let your heart be glad when he is overthrown,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"lest the LORD see it, and it displease him,"],[2,"and he turn away his wrath from him."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t fret yourself because of evildoers,"],[2,"neither be envious of the wicked;"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"for there will be no reward to the evil man."],[2,"The lamp of the wicked will be snuffed out."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"My son, fear the LORD and the king."],[2,"Don\u2019t join those who are rebellious,"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"for their calamity will rise suddenly."],[2,"Who knows what destruction may come from them both?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"These also are sayings of the wise:"],[1,"To show partiality in judgment is not good."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"He who says to the wicked, \u201cYou are righteous,\u201d"],[2,"peoples will curse him, and nations will abhor him\u2014"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"but it will go well with those who convict the guilty,"],[2,"and a rich blessing will come on them."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"An honest answer"],[2,"is like a kiss on the lips."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Prepare your work outside,"],[2,"and get your fields ready."],[2,"Afterwards, build your house."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be a witness against your neighbor without cause."],[2,"Don\u2019t deceive with your lips."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t say, \u201cI will do to him as he has done to me;"],[2,"I will repay the man according to his work.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"I went by the field of the sluggard,"],[2,"by the vineyard of the man void of understanding."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, it was all grown over with thorns."],[2,"Its surface was covered with nettles,"],[2,"and its stone wall was broken down."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I saw, and considered well."],[2,"I saw, and received instruction:"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"a little sleep, a little slumber,"],[2,"a little folding of the hands to sleep,"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"so your poverty will come as a robber"],[2,"and your want as an armed man."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"These also are proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"It is the glory of God to conceal a thing,"],[2,"but the glory of kings is to search out a matter."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"As the heavens for height, and the earth for depth,"],[2,"so the hearts of kings are unsearchable."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Take away the dross from the silver,"],[2,"and material comes out for the refiner."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Take away the wicked from the king\u2019s presence,"],[2,"and his throne will be established in righteousness."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t exalt yourself in the presence of the king,"],[2,"or claim a place among great men;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"for it is better that it be said to you, \u201cCome up here,\u201d"],[2,"than that you should be put lower in the presence of the prince,"],[2,"whom your eyes have seen."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be hasty in bringing charges to court."],[2,"What will you do in the end when your neighbor shames you?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Debate your case with your neighbor,"],[2,"and don\u2019t betray the confidence of another,"]]},{v:10,l:[[2,"lest one who hears it put you to shame,"],[2,"and your bad reputation never depart."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"A word fitly spoken"],[2,"is like apples of gold in settings of silver."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"As an earring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold,"],[2,"so is a wise reprover to an obedient ear."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"As the cold of snow in the time of harvest,"],[2,"so is a faithful messenger to those who send him;"],[2,"for he refreshes the soul of his masters."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"As clouds and wind without rain,"],[2,"so is he who boasts of gifts deceptively."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"By patience a ruler is persuaded."],[2,"A soft tongue breaks the bone."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Have you found honey?"],[2,"Eat as much as is sufficient for you,"],[2,"lest you eat too much, and vomit it."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your foot be seldom in your neighbor\u2019s house,"],[2,"lest he be weary of you, and hate you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"A man who gives false testimony against his neighbor"],[2,"is like a club, a sword, or a sharp arrow."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Confidence in someone unfaithful in time of trouble"],[2,"is like a bad tooth or a lame foot."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"As one who takes away a garment in cold weather,"],[2,"or vinegar on soda,"],[2,"so is one who sings songs to a heavy heart."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"If your enemy is hungry, give him food to eat."],[2,"If he is thirsty, give him water to drink;"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"for you will heap coals of fire on his head,"],[2,"and the LORD will reward you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"The north wind produces rain;"],[2,"so a backbiting tongue brings an angry face."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"It is better to dwell in the corner of the housetop"],[2,"than to share a house with a contentious woman."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Like cold water to a thirsty soul,"],[2,"so is good news from a far country."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Like a muddied spring and a polluted well,"],[2,"so is a righteous man who gives way before the wicked."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"It is not good to eat much honey,"],[2,"nor is it honorable to seek one\u2019s own honor."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Like a city that is broken down and without walls"],[2,"is a man whose spirit is without restraint."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Like snow in summer, and as rain in harvest,"],[2,"so honor is not fitting for a fool."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Like a fluttering sparrow,"],[2,"like a darting swallow,"],[2,"so the undeserved curse doesn\u2019t come to rest."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A whip is for the horse,"],[2,"a bridle for the donkey,"],[2,"and a rod for the back of fools!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t answer a fool according to his folly,"],[2,"lest you also be like him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Answer a fool according to his folly,"],[2,"lest he be wise in his own eyes."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"One who sends a message by the hand of a fool"],[2,"is cutting off feet and drinking violence."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Like the legs of the lame that hang loose,"],[2,"so is a parable in the mouth of fools."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"As one who binds a stone in a sling,"],[2,"so is he who gives honor to a fool."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Like a thorn bush that goes into the hand of a drunkard,"],[2,"so is a parable in the mouth of fools."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"As an archer who wounds all,"],[2,"so is he who hires a fool"],[2,"or he who hires those who pass by."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"As a dog that returns to his vomit,"],[2,"so is a fool who repeats his folly."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you see a man wise in his own eyes?"],[2,"There is more hope for a fool than for him."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The sluggard says, \u201cThere is a lion in the road!"],[2,"A fierce lion roams the streets!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"As the door turns on its hinges,"],[2,"so does the sluggard on his bed."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The sluggard buries his hand in the dish."],[2,"He is too lazy to bring it back to his mouth."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The sluggard is wiser in his own eyes"],[2,"than seven men who answer with discretion."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Like one who grabs a dog\u2019s ears"],[2,"is one who passes by and meddles in a quarrel not his own."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Like a madman who shoots torches, arrows, and death,"]]},{v:19,l:[[2,"is the man who deceives his neighbor and says, \u201cAm I not joking?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"For lack of wood a fire goes out."],[2,"Without gossip, a quarrel dies down."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"As coals are to hot embers,"],[2,"and wood to fire,"],[2,"so is a contentious man to kindling strife."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The words of a whisperer are as dainty morsels,"],[2,"they go down into the innermost parts."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Like silver dross on an earthen vessel"],[2,"are the lips of a fervent one with an evil heart."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"A malicious man disguises himself with his lips,"],[2,"but he harbors evil in his heart."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"When his speech is charming, don\u2019t believe him,"],[2,"for there are seven abominations in his heart."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"His malice may be concealed by deception,"],[2,"but his wickedness will be exposed in the assembly."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever digs a pit shall fall into it."],[2,"Whoever rolls a stone, it will come back on him."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"A lying tongue hates those it hurts;"],[2,"and a flattering mouth works ruin."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t boast about tomorrow;"],[2,"for you don\u2019t know what a day may bring."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Let another man praise you,"],[2,"and not your own mouth;"],[2,"a stranger, and not your own lips."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A stone is heavy,"],[2,"and sand is a burden;"],[2,"but a fool\u2019s provocation is heavier than both."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Wrath is cruel,"],[2,"and anger is overwhelming;"],[2,"but who is able to stand before jealousy?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is open rebuke"],[2,"than hidden love."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The wounds of a friend are faithful,"],[2,"although the kisses of an enemy are profuse."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"A full soul loathes a honeycomb;"],[2,"but to a hungry soul, every bitter thing is sweet."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"As a bird that wanders from her nest,"],[2,"so is a man who wanders from his home."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Perfume and incense bring joy to the heart;"],[2,"so does earnest counsel from a man\u2019s friend."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t forsake your friend and your father\u2019s friend."],[2,"Don\u2019t go to your brother\u2019s house in the day of your disaster."],[2,"A neighbor who is near is better than a distant brother."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Be wise, my son,"],[2,"and bring joy to my heart,"],[2,"then I can answer my tormentor."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"A prudent man sees danger and takes refuge;"],[2,"but the simple pass on, and suffer for it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Take his garment when he puts up collateral for a stranger."],[2,"Hold it for a wayward woman!"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He who blesses his neighbor with a loud voice early in the morning,"],[2,"it will be taken as a curse by him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"A continual dropping on a rainy day"],[2,"and a contentious wife are alike:"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"restraining her is like restraining the wind,"],[2,"or like grasping oil in his right hand."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Iron sharpens iron;"],[2,"so a man sharpens his friend\u2019s countenance."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever tends the fig tree shall eat its fruit."],[2,"He who looks after his master shall be honored."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Like water reflects a face,"],[2,"so a man\u2019s heart reflects the man."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied;"],[2,"and a man\u2019s eyes are never satisfied."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The crucible is for silver,"],[2,"and the furnace for gold;"],[2,"but man is refined by his praise."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Though you grind a fool in a mortar with a pestle along with grain,"],[2,"yet his foolishness will not be removed from him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Know well the state of your flocks,"],[2,"and pay attention to your herds,"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"for riches are not forever,"],[2,"nor does the crown endure to all generations."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The hay is removed, and the new growth appears,"],[2,"the grasses of the hills are gathered in."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The lambs are for your clothing,"],[2,"and the goats are the price of a field."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"There will be plenty of goats\u2019 milk for your food,"],[2,"for your family\u2019s food,"],[2,"and for the nourishment of your servant girls."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The wicked flee when no one pursues;"],[2,"but the righteous are as bold as a lion."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"In rebellion, a land has many rulers,"],[2,"but order is maintained by a man of understanding and knowledge."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A needy man who oppresses the poor"],[2,"is like a driving rain which leaves no crops."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who forsake the law praise the wicked;"],[2,"but those who keep the law contend with them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Evil men don\u2019t understand justice;"],[2,"but those who seek the LORD understand it fully."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Better is the poor who walks in his integrity"],[2,"than he who is perverse in his ways, and he is rich."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever keeps the law is a wise son;"],[2,"but he who is a companion of gluttons shames his father."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He who increases his wealth by excessive interest"],[2,"gathers it for one who has pity on the poor."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He who turns away his ear from hearing the law,"],[2,"even his prayer is an abomination."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever causes the upright to go astray in an evil way,"],[2,"he will fall into his own trap;"],[2,"but the blameless will inherit good."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The rich man is wise in his own eyes;"],[2,"but the poor who has understanding sees through him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"When the righteous triumph, there is great glory;"],[2,"but when the wicked rise, men hide themselves."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He who conceals his sins doesn\u2019t prosper,"],[2,"but whoever confesses and renounces them finds mercy."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man who always fears;"],[2,"but one who hardens his heart falls into trouble."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"As a roaring lion or a charging bear,"],[2,"so is a wicked ruler over helpless people."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"A tyrannical ruler lacks judgment."],[2,"One who hates ill-gotten gain will have long days."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"A man who is tormented by blood guilt will be a fugitive until death."],[2,"No one will support him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever walks blamelessly is kept safe;"],[2,"but one with perverse ways will fall suddenly."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"One who works his land will have an abundance of food;"],[2,"but one who chases fantasies will have his fill of poverty."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"A faithful man is rich with blessings;"],[2,"but one who is eager to be rich will not go unpunished."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"To show partiality is not good,"],[2,"yet a man will do wrong for a piece of bread."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"A stingy man hurries after riches,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t know that poverty waits for him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"One who rebukes a man will afterward find more favor"],[2,"than one who flatters with the tongue."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever robs his father or his mother and says, \u201cIt\u2019s not wrong,\u201d"],[2,"is a partner with a destroyer."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"One who is greedy stirs up strife;"],[2,"but one who trusts in the LORD will prosper."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"One who trusts in himself is a fool;"],[2,"but one who walks in wisdom is kept safe."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"One who gives to the poor has no lack;"],[2,"but one who closes his eyes will have many curses."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"When the wicked rise, men hide themselves;"],[2,"but when they perish, the righteous thrive."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is often rebuked and stiffens his neck"],[2,"will be destroyed suddenly, with no remedy."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"When the righteous thrive, the people rejoice;"],[2,"but when the wicked rule, the people groan."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever loves wisdom brings joy to his father;"],[2,"but a companion of prostitutes squanders his wealth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The king by justice makes the land stable,"],[2,"but he who takes bribes tears it down."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"A man who flatters his neighbor"],[2,"spreads a net for his feet."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"An evil man is snared by his sin,"],[2,"but the righteous can sing and be glad."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous care about justice for the poor."],[2,"The wicked aren\u2019t concerned about knowledge."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Mockers stir up a city,"],[2,"but wise men turn away anger."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"If a wise man goes to court with a foolish man,"],[2,"the fool rages or scoffs, and there is no peace."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The bloodthirsty hate a man of integrity;"],[2,"and they seek the life of the upright."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"A fool vents all of his anger,"],[2,"but a wise man brings himself under control."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"If a ruler listens to lies,"],[2,"all of his officials are wicked."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The poor man and the oppressor have this in common:"],[2,"The LORD gives sight to the eyes of both."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The king who fairly judges the poor,"],[2,"his throne shall be established forever."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The rod of correction gives wisdom,"],[2,"but a child left to himself causes shame to his mother."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"When the wicked increase, sin increases;"],[2,"but the righteous will see their downfall."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Correct your son, and he will give you peace;"],[2,"yes, he will bring delight to your soul."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Where there is no revelation, the people cast off restraint;"],[2,"but one who keeps the law is blessed."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"A servant can\u2019t be corrected by words."],[2,"Though he understands, yet he will not respond."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Do you see a man who is hasty in his words?"],[2,"There is more hope for a fool than for him."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He who pampers his servant from youth"],[2,"will have him become a son in the end."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"An angry man stirs up strife,"],[2,"and a wrathful man abounds in sin."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"A man\u2019s pride brings him low,"],[2,"but one of lowly spirit gains honor."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Whoever is an accomplice of a thief is an enemy of his own soul."],[2,"He takes an oath, but dares not testify."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The fear of man proves to be a snare,"],[2,"but whoever puts his trust in the LORD is kept safe."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Many seek the ruler\u2019s favor,"],[2,"but a man\u2019s justice comes from the LORD."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"A dishonest man detests the righteous,"],[2,"and the upright in their ways detest the wicked."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The words of Agur the son of Jakeh, the revelation:"],[1,"the man says to Ithiel,"],[2,"to Ithiel and Ucal:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSurely I am the most ignorant man,"],[2,"and don\u2019t have a man\u2019s understanding."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I have not learned wisdom,"],[2,"neither do I have the knowledge of the Holy One."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has ascended up into heaven, and descended?"],[2,"Who has gathered the wind in his fists?"],[2,"Who has bound the waters in his garment?"],[2,"Who has established all the ends of the earth?"],[2,"What is his name, and what is his son\u2019s name, if you know?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEvery word of God is flawless."],[2,"He is a shield to those who take refuge in him."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t you add to his words,"],[2,"lest he reprove you, and you be found a liar."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTwo things I have asked of you."],[2,"Don\u2019t deny me before I die."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Remove far from me falsehood and lies."],[2,"Give me neither poverty nor riches."],[2,"Feed me with the food that is needful for me,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"lest I be full, deny you, and say, \u2018Who is the LORD?\u2019"],[2,"or lest I be poor, and steal,"],[2,"and so dishonor the name of my God."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t slander a servant to his master,"],[2,"lest he curse you, and you be held guilty."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"There is a generation that curses their father,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t bless their mother."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"There is a generation that is pure in their own eyes,"],[2,"yet are not washed from their filthiness."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"There is a generation, oh how lofty are their eyes!"],[2,"Their eyelids are lifted up."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"There is a generation whose teeth are like swords,"],[2,"and their jaws like knives,"],[2,"to devour the poor from the earth, and the needy from among men."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe leech has two daughters:"],[2,"\u2018Give, give.\u2019"],[1,"\u201cThere are three things that are never satisfied;"],[2,"four that don\u2019t say, \u2018Enough!\u2019:"]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"Sheol,"],[2,"the barren womb,"],[2,"the earth that is not satisfied with water,"],[2,"and the fire that doesn\u2019t say, \u2018Enough!\u2019"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe eye that mocks at his father,"],[2,"and scorns obedience to his mother,"],[2,"the ravens of the valley shall pick it out,"],[2,"the young eagles shall eat it."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThere are three things which are too amazing for me,"],[2,"four which I don\u2019t understand:"]]},{v:19,l:[[2,"The way of an eagle in the air,"],[2,"the way of a serpent on a rock,"],[2,"the way of a ship in the middle of the sea,"],[2,"and the way of a man with a maiden."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSo is the way of an adulterous woman:"],[2,"She eats and wipes her mouth,"],[2,"and says, \u2018I have done nothing wrong.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor three things the earth trembles,"],[2,"and under four, it can\u2019t bear up:"]]},{v:22,l:[[2,"For a servant when he is king,"],[2,"a fool when he is filled with food,"]]},{v:23,l:[[2,"for an unloved woman when she is married,"],[2,"and a servant who is heir to her mistress."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThere are four things which are little on the earth,"],[2,"but they are exceedingly wise:"]]},{v:25,l:[[2,"The ants are not a strong people,"],[2,"yet they provide their food in the summer."]]},{v:26,l:[[2,"The hyraxes are but a feeble folk,"],[2,"yet make they their houses in the rocks."]]},{v:27,l:[[2,"The locusts have no king,"],[2,"yet they advance in ranks."]]},{v:28,l:[[2,"You can catch a lizard with your hands,"],[2,"yet it is in kings\u2019 palaces."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThere are three things which are stately in their march,"],[2,"four which are stately in going:"]]},{v:30,l:[[2,"The lion, which is mightiest among animals,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t turn away for any;"]]},{v:31,l:[[2,"the greyhound;"],[2,"the male goat;"],[2,"and the king against whom there is no rising up."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf you have done foolishly in lifting up yourself,"],[2,"or if you have thought evil,"],[1,"put your hand over your mouth."]]},{v:33,l:[[2,"For as the churning of milk produces butter,"],[2,"and the wringing of the nose produces blood,"],[2,"so the forcing of wrath produces strife.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The words of King Lemuel\u2014the revelation which his mother taught him:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOh, my son!"],[2,"Oh, son of my womb!"],[2,"Oh, son of my vows!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t give your strength to women,"],[2,"nor your ways to that which destroys kings."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"It is not for kings, Lemuel,"],[2,"it is not for kings to drink wine,"],[2,"nor for princes to say, \u2018Where is strong drink?\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"lest they drink, and forget the law,"],[2,"and pervert the justice due to anyone who is afflicted."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Give strong drink to him who is ready to perish,"],[2,"and wine to the bitter in soul."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Let him drink, and forget his poverty,"],[2,"and remember his misery no more."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Open your mouth for the mute,"],[2,"in the cause of all who are left desolate."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Open your mouth, judge righteously,"],[2,"and serve justice to the poor and needy.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Who can find a worthy woman?"],[2,"For her value is far above rubies."]],f:["Proverbs 31:10-31 form an acrostic, with each verse starting with each letter of the Hebrew alphabet, in order."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart of her husband trusts in her."],[2,"He shall have no lack of gain."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"She does him good, and not harm,"],[2,"all the days of her life."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"She seeks wool and flax,"],[2,"and works eagerly with her hands."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"She is like the merchant ships."],[2,"She brings her bread from afar."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"She rises also while it is yet night,"],[2,"gives food to her household,"],[2,"and portions for her servant girls."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"She considers a field, and buys it."],[2,"With the fruit of her hands, she plants a vineyard."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"She arms her waist with strength,"],[2,"and makes her arms strong."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"She perceives that her merchandise is profitable."],[2,"Her lamp doesn\u2019t go out by night."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"She lays her hands to the distaff,"],[2,"and her hands hold the spindle."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"She opens her arms to the poor;"],[2,"yes, she extends her hands to the needy."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"She is not afraid of the snow for her household,"],[2,"for all her household are clothed with scarlet."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"She makes for herself carpets of tapestry."],[2,"Her clothing is fine linen and purple."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Her husband is respected in the gates,"],[2,"when he sits among the elders of the land."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"She makes linen garments and sells them,"],[2,"and delivers sashes to the merchant."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Strength and dignity are her clothing."],[2,"She laughs at the time to come."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"She opens her mouth with wisdom."],[2,"Kind instruction is on her tongue."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"She looks well to the ways of her household,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t eat the bread of idleness."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Her children rise up and call her blessed."],[2,"Her husband also praises her:"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMany women do noble things,"],[2,"but you excel them all.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Charm is deceitful, and beauty is vain;"],[2,"but a woman who fears the LORD, she shall be praised."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Give her of the fruit of her hands!"],[2,"Let her works praise her in the gates!"]]}]]}},1291,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,s){h.exports={book:"Eccl",name:"Ecclesiastes",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The words of the Preacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cVanity of vanities,\u201d says the Preacher; \u201cVanity of vanities, all is vanity.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"What does man gain from all his labor in which he labors under the sun?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"One generation goes, and another generation comes; but the earth remains forever."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The sun also rises, and the sun goes down, and hurries to its place where it rises."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The wind goes toward the south, and turns around to the north. It turns around continually as it goes, and the wind returns again to its courses."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"All the rivers run into the sea, yet the sea is not full. To the place where the rivers flow, there they flow again."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All things are full of weariness beyond uttering. The eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"That which has been is that which shall be, and that which has been done is that which shall be done; and there is no new thing under the sun."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Is there a thing of which it may be said, \u201cBehold, this is new\u201d? It has been long ago, in the ages which were before us."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"There is no memory of the former; neither shall there be any memory of the latter that are to come, among those that shall come after."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I, the Preacher, was king over Israel in Jerusalem."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I applied my heart to seek and to search out by wisdom concerning all that is done under the sky. It is a heavy burden that God has given to the sons of men to be afflicted with."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and behold, all is vanity and a chasing after wind."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"That which is crooked can\u2019t be made straight; and that which is lacking can\u2019t be counted."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I said to myself, \u201cBehold, I have obtained for myself great wisdom above all who were before me in Jerusalem. Yes, my heart has had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I applied my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly. I perceived that this also was a chasing after wind."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For in much wisdom is much grief; and he who increases knowledge increases sorrow."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I said in my heart, \u201cCome now, I will test you with mirth; therefore enjoy pleasure;\u201d and behold, this also was vanity."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I said of laughter, \u201cIt is foolishness;\u201d and of mirth, \u201cWhat does it accomplish?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"I searched in my heart how to cheer my flesh with wine, my heart yet guiding me with wisdom, and how to lay hold of folly, until I might see what it was good for the sons of men that they should do under heaven all the days of their lives."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I made myself great works. I built myself houses. I planted myself vineyards."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I made myself gardens and parks, and I planted trees in them of all kinds of fruit."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I made myself pools of water, to water the forest where trees were grown."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I bought male servants and female servants, and had servants born in my house. I also had great possessions of herds and flocks, above all who were before me in Jerusalem."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I also gathered silver and gold for myself, and the treasure of kings and of the provinces. I got myself male and female singers, and the delights of the sons of men: musical instruments of all sorts."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So I was great, and increased more than all who were before me in Jerusalem. My wisdom also remained with me."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Whatever my eyes desired, I didn\u2019t keep from them. I didn\u2019t withhold my heart from any joy, for my heart rejoiced because of all my labor, and this was my portion from all my labor."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then I looked at all the works that my hands had worked, and at the labor that I had labored to do; and behold, all was vanity and a chasing after wind, and there was no profit under the sun."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I turned myself to consider wisdom, madness, and folly; for what can the king\u2019s successor do? Just that which has been done long ago."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then I saw that wisdom excels folly, as far as light excels darkness."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The wise man\u2019s eyes are in his head, and the fool walks in darkness\u2014and yet I perceived that one event happens to them all."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then I said in my heart, \u201cAs it happens to the fool, so will it happen even to me; and why was I then more wise?\u201d Then I said in my heart that this also is vanity."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For of the wise man, even as of the fool, there is no memory forever, since in the days to come all will have been long forgotten. Indeed, the wise man must die just like the fool!"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So I hated life, because the work that is worked under the sun was grievous to me; for all is vanity and a chasing after wind."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I hated all my labor in which I labored under the sun, because I must leave it to the man who comes after me."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Who knows whether he will be a wise man or a fool? Yet he will have rule over all of my labor in which I have labored, and in which I have shown myself wise under the sun. This also is vanity."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore I began to cause my heart to despair concerning all the labor in which I had labored under the sun."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For there is a man whose labor is with wisdom, with knowledge, and with skillfulness; yet he shall leave it for his portion to a man who has not labored for it. This also is vanity and a great evil."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For what does a man have of all his labor and of the striving of his heart, in which he labors under the sun?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For all his days are sorrows, and his travail is grief; yes, even in the night his heart takes no rest. This also is vanity."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"There is nothing better for a man than that he should eat and drink, and make his soul enjoy good in his labor. This also I saw, that it is from the hand of God."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For who can eat, or who can have enjoyment, more than I?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For to the man who pleases him, God gives wisdom, knowledge, and joy; but to the sinner he gives travail, to gather and to heap up, that he may give to him who pleases God. This also is vanity and a chasing after wind."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For everything there is a season, and a time for every purpose under heaven:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"a time to be born,"],[2,"and a time to die;"],[1,"a time to plant,"],[2,"and a time to pluck up that which is planted;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"a time to kill,"],[2,"and a time to heal;"],[1,"a time to break down,"],[2,"and a time to build up;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"a time to weep,"],[2,"and a time to laugh;"],[1,"a time to mourn,"],[2,"and a time to dance;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"a time to cast away stones,"],[2,"and a time to gather stones together;"],[1,"a time to embrace,"],[2,"and a time to refrain from embracing;"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"a time to seek,"],[2,"and a time to lose;"],[1,"a time to keep,"],[2,"and a time to cast away;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"a time to tear,"],[2,"and a time to sew;"],[1,"a time to keep silence,"],[2,"and a time to speak;"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"a time to love,"],[2,"and a time to hate;"],[1,"a time for war,"],[2,"and a time for peace."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"What profit has he who works in that in which he labors?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I have seen the burden which God has given to the sons of men to be afflicted with."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He has made everything beautiful in its time. He has also set eternity in their hearts, yet so that man can\u2019t find out the work that God has done from the beginning even to the end."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I know that there is nothing better for them than to rejoice, and to do good as long as they live."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Also that every man should eat and drink, and enjoy good in all his labor, is the gift of God."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I know that whatever God does, it shall be forever. Nothing can be added to it, nor anything taken from it; and God has done it, that men should fear before him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"That which is has been long ago, and that which is to be has been long ago. God seeks again that which is passed away."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover I saw under the sun, in the place of justice, that wickedness was there; and in the place of righteousness, that wickedness was there."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I said in my heart, \u201cGod will judge the righteous and the wicked; for there is a time there for every purpose and for every work.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I said in my heart, \u201cAs for the sons of men, God tests them, so that they may see that they themselves are like animals."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For that which happens to the sons of men happens to animals. Even one thing happens to them. As the one dies, so the other dies. Yes, they have all one breath; and man has no advantage over the animals, for all is vanity."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"All go to one place. All are from the dust, and all turn to dust again."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Who knows the spirit of man, whether it goes upward, and the spirit of the animal, whether it goes downward to the earth?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore I saw that there is nothing better than that a man should rejoice in his works, for that is his portion; for who can bring him to see what will be after him?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I returned and saw all the oppressions that are done under the sun: and behold, the tears of those who were oppressed, and they had no comforter; and on the side of their oppressors there was power; but they had no comforter."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore I praised the dead who have been long dead more than the living who are yet alive."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Yes, better than them both is him who has not yet been, who has not seen the evil work that is done under the sun."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then I saw all the labor and achievement that is the envy of a man\u2019s neighbor. This also is vanity and a striving after wind."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The fool folds his hands together and ruins himself."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Better is a handful, with quietness, than two handfuls with labor and chasing after wind."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I returned and saw vanity under the sun."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"There is one who is alone, and he has neither son nor brother. There is no end to all of his labor, neither are his eyes satisfied with wealth. \u201cFor whom then do I labor and deprive my soul of enjoyment?\u201d This also is vanity. Yes, it is a miserable business."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Two are better than one, because they have a good reward for their labor."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For if they fall, the one will lift up his fellow; but woe to him who is alone when he falls, and doesn\u2019t have another to lift him up."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Again, if two lie together, then they have warmth; but how can one keep warm alone?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If a man prevails against one who is alone, two shall withstand him; and a threefold cord is not quickly broken."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Better is a poor and wise youth than an old and foolish king who doesn\u2019t know how to receive admonition any more."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For out of prison he came out to be king; yes, even in his kingdom he was born poor."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I saw all the living who walk under the sun, that they were with the youth, the other, who succeeded him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"There was no end of all the people, even of all them over whom he was\u2014yet those who come after shall not rejoice in him. Surely this also is vanity and a chasing after wind."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Guard your steps when you go to God\u2019s house; for to draw near to listen is better than to give the sacrifice of fools, for they don\u2019t know that they do evil."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be rash with your mouth, and don\u2019t let your heart be hasty to utter anything before God; for God is in heaven, and you on earth. Therefore let your words be few."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For as a dream comes with a multitude of cares, so a fool\u2019s speech with a multitude of words."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When you vow a vow to God, don\u2019t defer to pay it; for he has no pleasure in fools. Pay that which you vow."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It is better that you should not vow, than that you should vow and not pay."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t allow your mouth to lead you into sin. Don\u2019t protest before the messenger that this was a mistake. Why should God be angry at your voice, and destroy the work of your hands?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For in the multitude of dreams there are vanities, as well as in many words; but you must fear God."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"If you see the oppression of the poor, and the violent taking away of justice and righteousness in a district, don\u2019t marvel at the matter, for one official is eyed by a higher one, and there are officials over them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moreover the profit of the earth is for all. The king profits from the field."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He who loves silver shall not be satisfied with silver, nor he who loves abundance, with increase. This also is vanity."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When goods increase, those who eat them are increased; and what advantage is there to its owner, except to feast on them with his eyes?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The sleep of a laboring man is sweet, whether he eats little or much; but the abundance of the rich will not allow him to sleep."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"There is a grievous evil which I have seen under the sun: wealth kept by its owner to his harm."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Those riches perish by misfortune, and if he has fathered a son, there is nothing in his hand."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"As he came out of his mother\u2019s womb, naked shall he go again as he came, and shall take nothing for his labor, which he may carry away in his hand."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"This also is a grievous evil, that in all points as he came, so shall he go. And what profit does he have who labors for the wind?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All his days he also eats in darkness, he is frustrated, and has sickness and wrath."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, that which I have seen to be good and proper is for one to eat and to drink, and to enjoy good in all his labor, in which he labors under the sun, all the days of his life which God has given him; for this is his portion."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Every man also to whom God has given riches and wealth, and has given him power to eat of it, and to take his portion, and to rejoice in his labor\u2014this is the gift of God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For he shall not often reflect on the days of his life, because God occupies him with the joy of his heart."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, and it is heavy on men:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"a man to whom God gives riches, wealth, and honor, so that he lacks nothing for his soul of all that he desires, yet God gives him no power to eat of it, but an alien eats it. This is vanity, and it is an evil disease."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"If a man fathers a hundred children, and lives many years, so that the days of his years are many, but his soul is not filled with good, and moreover he has no burial, I say that a stillborn child is better than he;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for it comes in vanity, and departs in darkness, and its name is covered with darkness."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Moreover it has not seen the sun nor known it. This has rest rather than the other."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Yes, though he live a thousand years twice told, and yet fails to enjoy good, don\u2019t all go to one place?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"All the labor of man is for his mouth, and yet the appetite is not filled."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For what advantage has the wise more than the fool? What has the poor man, that knows how to walk before the living?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Better is the sight of the eyes than the wandering of the desire. This also is vanity and a chasing after wind."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Whatever has been, its name was given long ago; and it is known what man is; neither can he contend with him who is mightier than he."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For there are many words that create vanity. What does that profit man?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For who knows what is good for man in life, all the days of his vain life which he spends like a shadow? For who can tell a man what will be after him under the sun?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A good name is better than fine perfume; and the day of death better than the day of one\u2019s birth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It is better to go to the house of mourning than to go to the house of feasting; for that is the end of all men, and the living should take this to heart."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Sorrow is better than laughter; for by the sadness of the face the heart is made good."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The heart of the wise is in the house of mourning; but the heart of fools is in the house of mirth."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It is better to hear the rebuke of the wise than for a man to hear the song of fools."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For as the crackling of thorns under a pot, so is the laughter of the fool. This also is vanity."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Surely extortion makes the wise man foolish; and a bribe destroys the understanding."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Better is the end of a thing than its beginning."],[0,"The patient in spirit is better than the proud in spirit."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be hasty in your spirit to be angry, for anger rests in the bosom of fools."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t say, \u201cWhy were the former days better than these?\u201d For you do not ask wisely about this."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Wisdom is as good as an inheritance. Yes, it is more excellent for those who see the sun."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For wisdom is a defense, even as money is a defense; but the excellency of knowledge is that wisdom preserves the life of him who has it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Consider the work of God, for who can make that straight which he has made crooked?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"In the day of prosperity be joyful, and in the day of adversity consider; yes, God has made the one side by side with the other, to the end that man should not find out anything after him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"All this I have seen in my days of vanity: there is a righteous man who perishes in his righteousness, and there is a wicked man who lives long in his evildoing."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be overly righteous, neither make yourself overly wise. Why should you destroy yourself?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be too wicked, neither be foolish. Why should you die before your time?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"It is good that you should take hold of this. Yes, also don\u2019t withdraw your hand from that; for he who fears God will come out of them all."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Wisdom is a strength to the wise man more than ten rulers who are in a city."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Surely there is not a righteous man on earth who does good and doesn\u2019t sin."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Also don\u2019t take heed to all words that are spoken, lest you hear your servant curse you;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"for often your own heart knows that you yourself have likewise cursed others."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"All this I have proved in wisdom. I said, \u201cI will be wise;\u201d but it was far from me."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"That which is, is far off and exceedingly deep. Who can find it out?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I turned around, and my heart sought to know and to search out, and to seek wisdom and the scheme of things, and to know that wickedness is stupidity, and that foolishness is madness."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"I find more bitter than death the woman whose heart is snares and traps, whose hands are chains. Whoever pleases God shall escape from her; but the sinner will be ensnared by her."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I have found this,\u201d says the Preacher, \u201cto one another, to find an explanation"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"which my soul still seeks, but I have not found. I have found one man among a thousand, but I have not found a woman among all those."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Behold, I have only found this: that God made mankind upright; but they search for many inventions.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Who is like the wise man? And who knows the interpretation of a thing? A man\u2019s wisdom makes his face shine, and the hardness of his face is changed."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"I say, \u201cKeep the king\u2019s command!\u201d because of the oath to God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be hasty to go out of his presence. Don\u2019t persist in an evil thing, for he does whatever pleases him,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for the king\u2019s word is supreme. Who can say to him, \u201cWhat are you doing?\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Whoever keeps the commandment shall not come to harm, and his wise heart will know the time and procedure."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For there is a time and procedure for every purpose, although the misery of man is heavy on him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For he doesn\u2019t know that which will be; for who can tell him how it will be?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"There is no man who has power over the spirit to contain the spirit; neither does he have power over the day of death. There is no discharge in war; neither shall wickedness deliver those who practice it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"All this I have seen, and applied my mind to every work that is done under the sun. There is a time in which one man has power over another to his hurt."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So I saw the wicked buried. Indeed they came also from holiness. They went and were forgotten in the city where they did this. This also is vanity."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Because sentence against an evil work is not executed speedily, therefore the heart of the sons of men is fully set in them to do evil."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Though a sinner commits crimes a hundred times, and lives long, yet surely I know that it will be better with those who fear God, who are reverent before him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But it shall not be well with the wicked, neither shall he lengthen days like a shadow, because he doesn\u2019t fear God."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"There is a vanity which is done on the earth, that there are righteous men to whom it happens according to the work of the wicked. Again, there are wicked men to whom it happens according to the work of the righteous. I said that this also is vanity."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then I commended mirth, because a man has no better thing under the sun than to eat, to drink, and to be joyful: for that will accompany him in his labor all the days of his life which God has given him under the sun."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When I applied my heart to know wisdom, and to see the business that is done on the earth (even though eyes see no sleep day or night),"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"then I saw all the work of God, that man can\u2019t find out the work that is done under the sun, because however much a man labors to seek it out, yet he won\u2019t find it. Yes even though a wise man thinks he can comprehend it, he won\u2019t be able to find it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For all this I laid to my heart, even to explore all this: that the righteous, and the wise, and their works, are in the hand of God; whether it is love or hatred, man doesn\u2019t know it; all is before them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"All things come alike to all. There is one event to the righteous and to the wicked; to the good, to the clean, to the unclean, to him who sacrifices, and to him who doesn\u2019t sacrifice. As is the good, so is the sinner; he who takes an oath, as he who fears an oath."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This is an evil in all that is done under the sun, that there is one event to all. Yes also, the heart of the sons of men is full of evil, and madness is in their heart while they live, and after that they go to the dead."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For to him who is joined with all the living there is hope; for a living dog is better than a dead lion."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For the living know that they will die, but the dead don\u2019t know anything, neither do they have any more a reward; for their memory is forgotten."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Also their love, their hatred, and their envy has perished long ago; neither do they any longer have a portion forever in anything that is done under the sun."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Go your way\u2014eat your bread with joy, and drink your wine with a merry heart; for God has already accepted your works."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Let your garments be always white, and don\u2019t let your head lack oil."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Live joyfully with the wife whom you love all the days of your life of vanity, which he has given you under the sun, all your days of vanity, for that is your portion in life, and in your labor in which you labor under the sun."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Whatever your hand finds to do, do it with your might; for there is no work, nor plan, nor knowledge, nor wisdom, in Sheol, where you are going."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"I returned and saw under the sun that the race is not to the swift, nor the battle to the strong, neither yet bread to the wise, nor yet riches to men of understanding, nor yet favor to men of skill; but time and chance happen to them all."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For man also doesn\u2019t know his time. As the fish that are taken in an evil net, and as the birds that are caught in the snare, even so are the sons of men snared in an evil time, when it falls suddenly on them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"I have also seen wisdom under the sun in this way, and it seemed great to me."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"There was a little city, and few men within it; and a great king came against it, besieged it, and built great bulwarks against it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now a poor wise man was found in it, and he by his wisdom delivered the city; yet no man remembered that same poor man."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cWisdom is better than strength.\u201d Nevertheless the poor man\u2019s wisdom is despised, and his words are not heard."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The words of the wise heard in quiet are better than the cry of him who rules among fools."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Wisdom is better than weapons of war; but one sinner destroys much good."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Dead flies cause the oil of the perfumer to produce an evil odor;"],[2,"so does a little folly outweigh wisdom and honor."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"A wise man\u2019s heart is at his right hand,"],[2,"but a fool\u2019s heart at his left."]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"Yes also when the fool walks by the way, his understanding fails him, and he says to everyone that he is a fool."]]},{v:4,l:[[2,"If the spirit of the ruler rises up against you, don\u2019t leave your place; for gentleness lays great offenses to rest."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, the sort of error which proceeds from the ruler."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in a low place."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I have seen servants on horses, and princes walking like servants on the earth."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He who digs a pit may fall into it; and whoever breaks through a wall may be bitten by a snake."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Whoever carves out stones may be injured by them. Whoever splits wood may be endangered by it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If the ax is blunt, and one doesn\u2019t sharpen the edge, then he must use more strength; but skill brings success."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"If the snake bites before it is charmed, then is there no profit for the charmer\u2019s tongue."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The words of a wise man\u2019s mouth are gracious; but a fool is swallowed by his own lips."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The beginning of the words of his mouth is foolishness; and the end of his talk is mischievous madness."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"A fool also multiplies words."],[0,"Man doesn\u2019t know what will be; and that which will be after him, who can tell him?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The labor of fools wearies every one of them; for he doesn\u2019t know how to go to the city."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to you, land, when your king is a child,"],[2,"and your princes eat in the morning!"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Happy are you, land, when your king is the son of nobles,"],[2,"and your princes eat in due season,"],[2,"for strength, and not for drunkenness!"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"By slothfulness the roof sinks in;"],[2,"and through idleness of the hands the house leaks."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"A feast is made for laughter,"],[2,"and wine makes the life glad;"],[2,"and money is the answer for all things."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t curse the king, no, not in your thoughts;"],[2,"and don\u2019t curse the rich in your bedroom,"],[2,"for a bird of the sky may carry your voice,"],[2,"and that which has wings may tell the matter."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Cast your bread on the waters;"],[2,"for you shall find it after many days."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Give a portion to seven, yes, even to eight;"],[2,"for you don\u2019t know what evil will be on the earth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"If the clouds are full of rain, they empty themselves on the earth;"],[2,"and if a tree falls toward the south, or toward the north,"],[2,"in the place where the tree falls, there shall it be."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He who observes the wind won\u2019t sow;"],[2,"and he who regards the clouds won\u2019t reap."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"As you don\u2019t know what is the way of the wind,"],[2,"nor how the bones grow in the womb of her who is with child;"],[2,"even so you don\u2019t know the work of God who does all."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"In the morning sow your seed,"],[2,"and in the evening don\u2019t withhold your hand;"],[2,"for you don\u2019t know which will prosper, whether this or that,"],[2,"or whether they both will be equally good."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Truly the light is sweet,"],[2,"and it is a pleasant thing for the eyes to see the sun."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, if a man lives many years, let him rejoice in them all;"],[2,"but let him remember the days of darkness, for they shall be many."],[2,"All that comes is vanity."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Rejoice, young man, in your youth,"],[2,"and let your heart cheer you in the days of your youth,"],[2,"and walk in the ways of your heart,"],[2,"and in the sight of your eyes;"],[2,"but know that for all these things God will bring you into judgment."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore remove sorrow from your heart,"],[2,"and put away evil from your flesh;"],[2,"for youth and the dawn of life are vanity."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Remember also your Creator in the days of your youth,"],[2,"before the evil days come, and the years draw near,"],[2,"when you will say, \u201cI have no pleasure in them;\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Before the sun, the light, the moon, and the stars are darkened,"],[2,"and the clouds return after the rain;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"in the day when the keepers of the house shall tremble,"],[2,"and the strong men shall bow themselves,"],[2,"and the grinders cease because they are few,"],[2,"and those who look out of the windows are darkened,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"and the doors shall be shut in the street;"],[2,"when the sound of the grinding is low,"],[2,"and one shall rise up at the voice of a bird,"],[2,"and all the daughters of music shall be brought low;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"yes, they shall be afraid of heights,"],[2,"and terrors will be on the way;"],[2,"and the almond tree shall blossom,"],[2,"and the grasshopper shall be a burden,"],[2,"and desire shall fail;"],[2,"because man goes to his everlasting home,"],[2,"and the mourners go about the streets;"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"before the silver cord is severed,"],[2,"or the golden bowl is broken,"],[2,"or the pitcher is broken at the spring,"],[2,"or the wheel broken at the cistern,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"and the dust returns to the earth as it was,"],[2,"and the spirit returns to God who gave it."]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"\u201cVanity of vanities,\u201d says the Preacher."],[2,"\u201cAll is vanity!\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Further, because the Preacher was wise, he still taught the people knowledge. Yes, he pondered, sought out, and set in order many proverbs."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The Preacher sought to find out acceptable words, and that which was written blamelessly, words of truth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The words of the wise are like goads; and like nails well fastened are words from the masters of assemblies, which are given from one shepherd."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Furthermore, my son, be admonished: of making many books there is no end; and much study is a weariness of the flesh."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the end of the matter. All has been heard. Fear God and keep his commandments; for this is the whole duty of man."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For God will bring every work into judgment, with every hidden thing, whether it is good, or whether it is evil."]]}]]}},1292,[]);
__d(function(e,o,a,t,s,i,h){s.exports={book:"Song",name:"Song of Solomon",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The Song of songs, which is Solomon\u2019s."]]},{v:2,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth;"],[2,"for your love is better than wine."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Your oils have a pleasing fragrance."],[2,"Your name is oil poured out,"],[2,"therefore the virgins love you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Take me away with you."],[2,"Let\u2019s hurry."],[2,"The king has brought me into his rooms."],[1,"We will be glad and rejoice in you."],[2,"We will praise your love more than wine!"],[1,"They are right to love you."]]},{v:5,h:["Friends","Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"I am dark, but lovely,"],[2,"you daughters of Jerusalem,"],[2,"like Kedar\u2019s tents,"],[2,"like Solomon\u2019s curtains."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t stare at me because I am dark,"],[2,"because the sun has scorched me."],[1,"My mother\u2019s sons were angry with me."],[2,"They made me keeper of the vineyards."],[2,"I haven\u2019t kept my own vineyard."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Tell me, you whom my soul loves,"],[2,"where you graze your flock,"],[2,"where you rest them at noon;"],[2,"for why should I be as one who is veiled"],[2,"beside the flocks of your companions?"]]},{v:8,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"If you don\u2019t know, most beautiful among women,"],[2,"follow the tracks of the sheep."],[2,"Graze your young goats beside the shepherds\u2019 tents."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I have compared you, my love,"],[2,"to a steed in Pharaoh\u2019s chariots."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Your cheeks are beautiful with earrings,"],[2,"your neck with strings of jewels."]]},{v:11,h:["Friends"],p:1,l:[[1,"We will make you earrings of gold,"],[2,"with studs of silver."]]},{v:12,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"While the king sat at his table,"],[2,"my perfume spread its fragrance."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved is to me a sachet of myrrh,"],[2,"that lies between my breasts."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved is to me a cluster of henna blossoms"],[2,"from the vineyards of En Gedi."]]},{v:15,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you are beautiful, my love."],[2,"Behold, you are beautiful."],[2,"Your eyes are like doves."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:16,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you are beautiful, my beloved, yes, pleasant;"],[2,"and our couch is verdant."]]},{v:17,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"The beams of our house are cedars."],[2,"Our rafters are firs."]]}],[{v:1,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"I am a rose of Sharon,"],[2,"a lily of the valleys."]]},{v:2,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"As a lily among thorns,"],[2,"so is my love among the daughters."]]},{v:3,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"As the apple tree among the trees of the wood,"],[2,"so is my beloved among the sons."],[1,"I sat down under his shadow with great delight,"],[2,"his fruit was sweet to my taste."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He brought me to the banquet hall."],[2,"His banner over me is love."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Strengthen me with raisins,"],[2,"refresh me with apples;"],[2,"for I am faint with love."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"His left hand is under my head."],[2,"His right hand embraces me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem,"],[2,"by the roes, or by the hinds of the field,"],[2,"that you not stir up, nor awaken love,"],[2,"until it so desires."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The voice of my beloved!"],[2,"Behold, he comes,"],[2,"leaping on the mountains,"],[2,"skipping on the hills."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved is like a roe or a young deer."],[2,"Behold, he stands behind our wall!"],[1,"He looks in at the windows."],[2,"He glances through the lattice."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved spoke, and said to me,"],[2,"\u201cRise up, my love, my beautiful one, and come away."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For behold, the winter is past."],[2,"The rain is over and gone."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The flowers appear on the earth."],[2,"The time of the singing has come,"],[2,"and the voice of the turtledove is heard in our land."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The fig tree ripens her green figs."],[2,"The vines are in blossom."],[2,"They give out their fragrance."],[1,"Arise, my love, my beautiful one,"],[2,"and come away.\u201d"]]},{v:14,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"My dove in the clefts of the rock,"],[2,"in the hiding places of the mountainside,"],[2,"let me see your face."],[2,"Let me hear your voice;"],[2,"for your voice is sweet and your face is lovely."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Catch for us the foxes,"],[2,"the little foxes that plunder the vineyards;"],[2,"for our vineyards are in blossom."]]},{v:16,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved is mine, and I am his."],[2,"He browses among the lilies."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Until the day is cool, and the shadows flee away,"],[2,"turn, my beloved,"],[2,"and be like a roe or a young deer on the mountains of Bether."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"By night on my bed,"],[2,"I sought him whom my soul loves."],[2,"I sought him, but I didn\u2019t find him."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will get up now, and go about the city;"],[2,"in the streets and in the squares I will seek him whom my soul loves."],[2,"I sought him, but I didn\u2019t find him."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The watchmen who go about the city found me;"],[2,"\u201cHave you seen him whom my soul loves?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I had scarcely passed from them,"],[2,"when I found him whom my soul loves."],[1,"I held him, and would not let him go,"],[2,"until I had brought him into my mother\u2019s house,"],[2,"into the room of her who conceived me."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem,"],[2,"by the roes, or by the hinds of the field,"],[2,"that you not stir up nor awaken love,"],[2,"until it so desires."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is this who comes up from the wilderness like pillars of smoke,"],[2,"perfumed with myrrh and frankincense,"],[2,"with all spices of the merchant?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, it is Solomon\u2019s carriage!"],[2,"Sixty mighty men are around it,"],[2,"of the mighty men of Israel."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They all handle the sword, and are expert in war."],[2,"Every man has his sword on his thigh,"],[2,"because of fear in the night."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"King Solomon made himself a carriage"],[2,"of the wood of Lebanon."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He made its pillars of silver,"],[2,"its bottom of gold, its seat of purple,"],[2,"the middle of it being paved with love,"],[2,"from the daughters of Jerusalem."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Go out, you daughters of Zion, and see King Solomon,"],[2,"with the crown with which his mother has crowned him,"],[2,"in the day of his weddings,"],[2,"in the day of the gladness of his heart."]]}],[{v:1,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, you are beautiful, my love."],[2,"Behold, you are beautiful."],[1,"Your eyes are like doves behind your veil."],[2,"Your hair is as a flock of goats,"],[2,"that descend from Mount Gilead."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Your teeth are like a newly shorn flock,"],[2,"which have come up from the washing,"],[2,"where every one of them has twins."],[2,"None is bereaved among them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Your lips are like scarlet thread."],[2,"Your mouth is lovely."],[2,"Your temples are like a piece of a pomegranate behind your veil."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Your neck is like David\u2019s tower built for an armory,"],[2,"on which a thousand shields hang,"],[2,"all the shields of the mighty men."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Your two breasts are like two fawns"],[2,"that are twins of a roe,"],[2,"which feed among the lilies."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Until the day is cool, and the shadows flee away,"],[2,"I will go to the mountain of myrrh,"],[2,"to the hill of frankincense."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You are all beautiful, my love."],[2,"There is no spot in you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Come with me from Lebanon, my bride,"],[2,"with me from Lebanon."],[2,"Look from the top of Amana,"],[2,"from the top of Senir and Hermon,"],[2,"from the lions\u2019 dens,"],[2,"from the mountains of the leopards."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You have ravished my heart, my sister, my bride."],[2,"You have ravished my heart with one of your eyes,"],[2,"with one chain of your neck."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"How beautiful is your love, my sister, my bride!"],[2,"How much better is your love than wine,"],[2,"the fragrance of your perfumes than all kinds of spices!"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Your lips, my bride, drip like the honeycomb."],[2,"Honey and milk are under your tongue."],[2,"The smell of your garments is like the smell of Lebanon."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"My sister, my bride, is a locked up garden;"],[2,"a locked up spring,"],[2,"a sealed fountain."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Your shoots are an orchard of pomegranates, with precious fruits,"],[2,"henna with spikenard plants,"]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"spikenard and saffron,"],[2,"calamus and cinnamon, with every kind of incense tree;"],[2,"myrrh and aloes, with all the best spices,"]]},{v:15,l:[[2,"a fountain of gardens,"],[2,"a well of living waters,"],[2,"flowing streams from Lebanon."]]},{v:16,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"Awake, north wind, and come, you south!"],[2,"Blow on my garden, that its spices may flow out."],[1,"Let my beloved come into his garden,"],[2,"and taste his precious fruits."]]}],[{v:1,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"I have come into my garden, my sister, my bride."],[2,"I have gathered my myrrh with my spice;"],[2,"I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey;"],[2,"I have drunk my wine with my milk."],[1,"Eat, friends!"],[2,"Drink, yes, drink abundantly, beloved."]]},{v:2,h:["Friends","Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"I was asleep, but my heart was awake."],[2,"It is the voice of my beloved who knocks:"],[2,"\u201cOpen to me, my sister, my love, my dove, my undefiled;"],[2,"for my head is filled with dew,"],[2,"and my hair with the dampness of the night.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I have taken off my robe. Indeed, must I put it on?"],[2,"I have washed my feet. Indeed, must I soil them?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved thrust his hand in through the latch opening."],[2,"My heart pounded for him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I rose up to open for my beloved."],[2,"My hands dripped with myrrh,"],[2,"my fingers with liquid myrrh,"],[2,"on the handles of the lock."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I opened to my beloved;"],[2,"but my beloved left, and had gone away."],[1,"My heart went out when he spoke."],[2,"I looked for him, but I didn\u2019t find him."],[2,"I called him, but he didn\u2019t answer."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The watchmen who go about the city found me."],[2,"They beat me."],[2,"They bruised me."],[2,"The keepers of the walls took my cloak away from me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem,"],[2,"If you find my beloved,"],[2,"that you tell him that I am faint with love."]]},{v:9,h:["Friends"],p:1,l:[[1,"How is your beloved better than another beloved,"],[2,"you fairest among women?"],[1,"How is your beloved better than another beloved,"],[1,"that you do so adjure us?"]]},{v:10,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved is white and ruddy."],[2,"The best among ten thousand."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"His head is like the purest gold."],[2,"His hair is bushy, black as a raven."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"His eyes are like doves beside the water brooks,"],[2,"washed with milk, mounted like jewels."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"His cheeks are like a bed of spices with towers of perfumes."],[2,"His lips are like lilies, dropping liquid myrrh."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"His hands are like rings of gold set with beryl."],[2,"His body is like ivory work overlaid with sapphires."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"His legs are like pillars of marble set on sockets of fine gold."],[2,"His appearance is like Lebanon, excellent as the cedars."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"His mouth is sweetness;"],[2,"yes, he is altogether lovely."],[1,"This is my beloved, and this is my friend,"],[2,"daughters of Jerusalem."]]}],[{v:1,h:["Friends"],p:1,l:[[1,"Where has your beloved gone, you fairest among women?"],[2,"Where has your beloved turned, that we may seek him with you?"]]},{v:2,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"My beloved has gone down to his garden,"],[2,"to the beds of spices,"],[2,"to pasture his flock in the gardens, and to gather lilies."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I am my beloved\u2019s, and my beloved is mine."],[2,"He browses among the lilies."]]},{v:4,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"You are beautiful, my love, as Tirzah,"],[2,"lovely as Jerusalem,"],[2,"awesome as an army with banners."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn away your eyes from me,"],[2,"for they have overcome me."],[1,"Your hair is like a flock of goats,"],[2,"that lie along the side of Gilead."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Your teeth are like a flock of ewes,"],[2,"which have come up from the washing,"],[2,"of which every one has twins;"],[2,"not one is bereaved among them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Your temples are like a piece of a pomegranate behind your veil."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"There are sixty queens, eighty concubines,"],[2,"and virgins without number."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"My dove, my perfect one, is unique."],[2,"She is her mother\u2019s only daughter."],[2,"She is the favorite one of her who bore her."],[1,"The daughters saw her, and called her blessed."],[2,"The queens and the concubines saw her, and they praised her."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is she who looks out as the morning,"],[2,"beautiful as the moon,"],[2,"clear as the sun,"],[2,"and awesome as an army with banners?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I went down into the nut tree grove,"],[2,"to see the green plants of the valley,"],[2,"to see whether the vine budded,"],[2,"and the pomegranates were in flower."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Without realizing it,"],[2,"my desire set me with my royal people\u2019s chariots."]]},{v:13,h:["Friends"],p:1,l:[[1,"Return, return, Shulammite!"],[2,"Return, return, that we may gaze at you."],[1,"Why do you desire to gaze at the Shulammite,"],[2,"as at the dance of Mahanaim?"]]}],[{v:1,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[0,"How beautiful are your feet in sandals, prince\u2019s daughter!"],[2,"Your rounded thighs are like jewels,"],[2,"the work of the hands of a skillful workman."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Your body is like a round goblet,"],[2,"no mixed wine is wanting."],[1,"Your waist is like a heap of wheat,"],[2,"set about with lilies."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Your two breasts are like two fawns,"],[2,"that are twins of a roe."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Your neck is like an ivory tower."],[2,"Your eyes are like the pools in Heshbon by the gate of Bathrabbim."],[2,"Your nose is like the tower of Lebanon which looks toward Damascus."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Your head on you is like Carmel."],[2,"The hair of your head like purple."],[2,"The king is held captive in its tresses."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"How beautiful and how pleasant you are,"],[2,"love, for delights!"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"This, your stature, is like a palm tree,"],[2,"your breasts like its fruit."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cI will climb up into the palm tree."],[2,"I will take hold of its fruit.\u201d"],[1,"Let your breasts be like clusters of the vine,"],[2,"the smell of your breath like apples."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Your mouth is like the best wine,"],[2,"that goes down smoothly for my beloved,"],[2,"gliding through the lips of those who are asleep."]]},{v:10,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"I am my beloved\u2019s."],[2,"His desire is toward me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Come, my beloved! Let\u2019s go out into the field."],[2,"Let\u2019s lodge in the villages."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Let\u2019s go early up to the vineyards."],[2,"Let\u2019s see whether the vine has budded,"],[2,"its blossom is open,"],[2,"and the pomegranates are in flower."],[2,"There I will give you my love."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The mandrakes produce fragrance."],[2,"At our doors are all kinds of precious fruits, new and old,"],[2,"which I have stored up for you, my beloved."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Oh that you were like my brother,"],[2,"who nursed from the breasts of my mother!"],[1,"If I found you outside, I would kiss you;"],[2,"yes, and no one would despise me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I would lead you, bringing you into the house of my mother,"],[2,"who would instruct me."],[1,"I would have you drink spiced wine,"],[2,"of the juice of my pomegranate."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"His left hand would be under my head."],[2,"His right hand would embrace me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I adjure you, daughters of Jerusalem,"],[2,"that you not stir up, nor awaken love,"],[2,"until it so desires."]]},{v:5,h:["Friends"],p:1,l:[[1,"Who is this who comes up from the wilderness,"],[2,"leaning on her beloved?"],[1,"Under the apple tree I awakened you."],[2,"There your mother conceived you."],[2,"There she was in labor and bore you."]]},{v:6,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"Set me as a seal on your heart,"],[2,"as a seal on your arm;"],[2,"for love is strong as death."],[2,"Jealousy is as cruel as Sheol."],[2,"Its flashes are flashes of fire,"],[2,"a very flame of the LORD."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead.","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Many waters can\u2019t quench love,"],[2,"neither can floods drown it."],[1,"If a man would give all the wealth of his house for love,"],[2,"he would be utterly scorned."]]},{v:8,h:["Brothers"],p:1,l:[[1,"We have a little sister."],[2,"She has no breasts."],[1,"What shall we do for our sister"],[2,"in the day when she is to be spoken for?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"If she is a wall,"],[2,"we will build on her a turret of silver."],[1,"If she is a door,"],[2,"we will enclose her with boards of cedar."]]},{v:10,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"I am a wall, and my breasts like towers,"],[2,"then I was in his eyes like one who found peace."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Solomon had a vineyard at Baal Hamon."],[2,"He leased out the vineyard to keepers."],[2,"Each was to bring a thousand shekels of silver for its fruit."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 1000 shekels is about 10 kilograms or about 22 pounds."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"My own vineyard is before me."],[2,"The thousand are for you, Solomon,"],[2,"two hundred for those who tend its fruit."]]},{v:13,h:["Lover"],p:1,l:[[1,"You who dwell in the gardens, with friends in attendance,"],[2,"let me hear your voice!"]]},{v:14,h:["Beloved"],p:1,l:[[1,"Come away, my beloved!"],[2,"Be like a gazelle or a young stag on the mountains of spices!"]]}]]}},1293,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,h,n,i){h.exports={book:"Isa",name:"Isaiah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The vision of Isaiah the son of Amoz, which he saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem, in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, heavens,"],[2,"and listen, earth; for the LORD has spoken:"],[1,"\u201cI have nourished and brought up children"],[2,"and they have rebelled against me."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The ox knows his owner,"],[2,"and the donkey his master\u2019s crib;"],[2,"but Israel doesn\u2019t know."],[2,"My people don\u2019t consider.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Ah sinful nation,"],[2,"a people loaded with iniquity,"],[2,"offspring of evildoers,"],[2,"children who deal corruptly!"],[1,"They have forsaken the LORD."],[2,"They have despised the Holy One of Israel."],[2,"They are estranged and backward."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Why should you be beaten more,"],[2,"that you revolt more and more?"],[1,"The whole head is sick,"],[2,"and the whole heart faint."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"From the sole of the foot even to the head there is no soundness in it,"],[2,"but wounds, welts, and open sores."],[2,"They haven\u2019t been closed, bandaged, or soothed with oil."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Your country is desolate."],[2,"Your cities are burned with fire."],[2,"Strangers devour your land in your presence"],[2,"and it is desolate,"],[2,"as overthrown by strangers."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The daughter of Zion is left like a shelter in a vineyard,"],[2,"like a hut in a field of melons,"],[2,"like a besieged city."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Unless the LORD of Armies had left to us a very small remnant,"],[2,"we would have been as Sodom."],[2,"We would have been like Gomorrah."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear the LORD\u2019s word, you rulers of Sodom!"],[2,"Listen to the law of our God, you people of Gomorrah!"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhat are the multitude of your sacrifices to me?\u201d, says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cI have had enough of the burnt offerings of rams"],[2,"and the fat of fed animals."],[2,"I don\u2019t delight in the blood of bulls,"],[2,"or of lambs,"],[2,"or of male goats."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"When you come to appear before me,"],[2,"who has required this at your hand, to trample my courts?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Bring no more vain offerings."],[2,"Incense is an abomination to me."],[2,"New moons, Sabbaths, and convocations\u2014"],[2,"I can\u2019t stand evil assemblies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul hates your New Moons and your appointed feasts."],[2,"They are a burden to me."],[2,"I am weary of bearing them."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"When you spread out your hands, I will hide my eyes from you."],[2,"Yes, when you make many prayers, I will not hear."],[2,"Your hands are full of blood."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Wash yourselves. Make yourself clean."],[2,"Put away the evil of your doings from before my eyes."],[2,"Cease to do evil."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Learn to do well."],[2,"Seek justice."],[2,"Relieve the oppressed."],[1,"Defend the fatherless."],[2,"Plead for the widow.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCome now, and let\u2019s reason together,\u201d says the LORD:"],[2,"\u201cThough your sins are as scarlet, they shall be as white as snow."],[2,"Though they are red like crimson, they shall be as wool."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"If you are willing and obedient,"],[2,"you will eat the good of the land;"]]},{v:20,l:[[2,"but if you refuse and rebel, you will be devoured with the sword;"],[2,"for the LORD\u2019s mouth has spoken it.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"How the faithful city has become a prostitute!"],[2,"She was full of justice."],[1,"Righteousness lodged in her,"],[2,"but now there are murderers."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Your silver has become dross,"],[2,"your wine mixed with water."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Your princes are rebellious and companions of thieves."],[2,"Everyone loves bribes and follows after rewards."],[2,"They don\u2019t defend the fatherless,"],[2,"neither does the cause of the widow come to them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the Lord, GOD of Armies,"],[2,"the Mighty One of Israel, says:"],[1,"\u201cAh, I will get relief from my adversaries,"],[2,"and avenge myself on my enemies."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"I will turn my hand on you,"],[2,"thoroughly purge away your dross,"],[2,"and will take away all your tin."]],f:["tin is a metal that is separated from silver during the refining and purification process."]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"I will restore your judges as at the first,"],[2,"and your counselors as at the beginning."],[1,"Afterward you shall be called \u2018The city of righteousness,"],[2,"a faithful town.\u2019"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Zion shall be redeemed with justice,"],[2,"and her converts with righteousness."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"But the destruction of transgressors and sinners shall be together,"],[2,"and those who forsake the LORD shall be consumed."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"For they shall be ashamed of the oaks which you have desired,"],[2,"and you shall be confounded for the gardens that you have chosen."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"For you shall be as an oak whose leaf fades,"],[2,"and as a garden that has no water."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"The strong will be like tinder,"],[2,"and his work like a spark."],[1,"They will both burn together,"],[2,"and no one will quench them.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is what Isaiah the son of Amoz saw concerning Judah and Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"It shall happen in the latter days, that the mountain of the LORD\u2019s house shall be established on the top of the mountains,"],[2,"and shall be raised above the hills;"],[2,"and all nations shall flow to it."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Many peoples shall go and say,"],[2,"\u201cCome, let\u2019s go up to the mountain of the LORD,"],[2,"to the house of the God of Jacob;"],[2,"and he will teach us of his ways,"],[2,"and we will walk in his paths.\u201d"],[1,"For the law shall go out of Zion,"],[2,"and the LORD\u2019s word from Jerusalem."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He will judge between the nations,"],[2,"and will decide concerning many peoples."],[2,"They shall beat their swords into plowshares,"],[2,"and their spears into pruning hooks."],[1,"Nation shall not lift up sword against nation,"],[2,"neither shall they learn war any more."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"House of Jacob, come, and let\u2019s walk in the light of the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have forsaken your people, the house of Jacob,"],[2,"because they are filled from the east,"],[2,"with those who practice divination like the Philistines,"],[2,"and they clasp hands with the children of foreigners."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Their land is full of silver and gold,"],[2,"neither is there any end of their treasures."],[1,"Their land also is full of horses,"],[2,"neither is there any end of their chariots."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Their land also is full of idols."],[2,"They worship the work of their own hands,"],[2,"that which their own fingers have made."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Man is brought low,"],[2,"and mankind is humbled;"],[2,"therefore don\u2019t forgive them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Enter into the rock,"],[2,"and hide in the dust,"],[1,"from before the terror of the LORD,"],[2,"and from the glory of his majesty."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The lofty looks of man will be brought low,"],[2,"the arrogance of men will be bowed down,"],[2,"and the LORD alone will be exalted in that day."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For there will be a day of the LORD of Armies for all that is proud and arrogant,"],[2,"and for all that is lifted up,"],[2,"and it shall be brought low\u2014"]]},{v:13,l:[[2,"for all the cedars of Lebanon, that are high and lifted up,"],[2,"for all the oaks of Bashan,"]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"for all the high mountains,"],[2,"for all the hills that are lifted up,"]]},{v:15,l:[[2,"for every lofty tower,"],[2,"for every fortified wall,"]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"for all the ships of Tarshish,"],[2,"and for all pleasant imagery."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The loftiness of man shall be bowed down,"],[2,"and the arrogance of men shall be brought low;"],[2,"and the LORD alone shall be exalted in that day."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"The idols shall utterly pass away."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Men shall go into the caves of the rocks,"],[2,"and into the holes of the earth,"],[2,"from before the terror of the LORD,"],[2,"and from the glory of his majesty,"],[2,"when he arises to shake the earth mightily."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"In that day, men shall cast away their idols of silver"],[2,"and their idols of gold,"],[2,"which have been made for themselves to worship,"],[2,"to the moles and to the bats,"]]},{v:21,l:[[2,"to go into the caverns of the rocks,"],[2,"and into the clefts of the ragged rocks,"],[2,"from before the terror of the LORD,"],[2,"and from the glory of his majesty,"],[2,"when he arises to shake the earth mightily."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Stop trusting in man, whose breath is in his nostrils;"],[2,"for of what account is he?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, the Lord, GOD of Armies, takes away from Jerusalem and from Judah supply and support,"],[2,"the whole supply of bread,"],[2,"and the whole supply of water;"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection.","When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[2,"the mighty man,"],[2,"the man of war,"],[2,"the judge,"],[2,"the prophet,"],[2,"the diviner,"],[2,"the elder,"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"the captain of fifty,"],[2,"the honorable man,"],[2,"the counselor,"],[2,"the skilled craftsman,"],[2,"and the clever enchanter."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give boys to be their princes,"],[2,"and children shall rule over them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The people will be oppressed,"],[2,"everyone by another,"],[2,"and everyone by his neighbor."],[1,"The child will behave himself proudly against the old man,"],[2,"and the wicked against the honorable."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Indeed a man shall take hold of his brother in the house of his father, saying,"],[2,"\u201cYou have clothing, you be our ruler,"],[2,"and let this ruin be under your hand.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"In that day he will cry out, saying, \u201cI will not be a healer;"],[2,"for in my house is neither bread nor clothing."],[2,"You shall not make me ruler of the people.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For Jerusalem is ruined, and Judah is fallen;"],[2,"because their tongue and their doings are against the LORD,"],[1,"to provoke the eyes of his glory."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The look of their faces testify against them."],[2,"They parade their sin like Sodom."],[2,"They don\u2019t hide it."],[2,"Woe to their soul!"],[2,"For they have brought disaster upon themselves."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Tell the righteous that it will be well with them,"],[2,"for they will eat the fruit of their deeds."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to the wicked!"],[2,"Disaster is upon them,"],[2,"for the deeds of their hands will be paid back to them."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"As for my people, children are their oppressors,"],[2,"and women rule over them."],[2,"My people, those who lead you cause you to err,"],[2,"and destroy the way of your paths."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD stands up to contend,"],[2,"and stands to judge the peoples."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will enter into judgment with the elders of his people"],[2,"and their leaders:"],[2,"\u201cIt is you who have eaten up the vineyard."],[2,"The plunder of the poor is in your houses."]]},{v:15,l:[[2,"What do you mean that you crush my people,"],[2,"and grind the face of the poor?\u201d says the Lord, GOD of Armies."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Moreover the LORD said, \u201cBecause the daughters of Zion are arrogant,"],[2,"and walk with outstretched necks and flirting eyes,"],[2,"walking daintily as they go,"],[2,"jingling ornaments on their feet;"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"therefore the Lord brings sores on the crown of the head of the women of Zion,"],[2,"and the LORD will make their scalps bald.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day the Lord will take away the beauty of their anklets, the headbands, the crescent necklaces,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the earrings, the bracelets, the veils,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"the headdresses, the ankle chains, the sashes, the perfume containers, the charms,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"the signet rings, the nose rings,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"the fine robes, the capes, the cloaks, the purses,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"the hand mirrors, the fine linen garments, the tiaras, and the shawls."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"It shall happen that instead of sweet spices, there shall be rottenness;"],[2,"instead of a belt, a rope;"],[2,"instead of well set hair, baldness;"],[2,"instead of a robe, a wearing of sackcloth;"],[2,"and branding instead of beauty."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Your men shall fall by the sword,"],[2,"and your mighty in the war."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Her gates shall lament and mourn."],[2,"She shall be desolate and sit on the ground."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Seven women shall take hold of one man in that day, saying, \u201cWe will eat our own bread, and wear our own clothing. Just let us be called by your name. Take away our reproach.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, the LORD\u2019s branch will be beautiful and glorious, and the fruit of the land will be the beauty and glory of the survivors of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It will happen that he who is left in Zion and he who remains in Jerusalem shall be called holy, even everyone who is written among the living in Jerusalem,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"when the Lord shall have washed away the filth of the daughters of Zion, and shall have purged the blood of Jerusalem from within it, by the spirit of justice and by the spirit of burning."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD will create over the whole habitation of Mount Zion and over her assemblies, a cloud and smoke by day, and the shining of a flaming fire by night, for over all the glory will be a canopy."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"There will be a pavilion for a shade in the daytime from the heat, and for a refuge and for a shelter from storm and from rain."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Let me sing for my well beloved a song of my beloved about his vineyard."],[2,"My beloved had a vineyard on a very fruitful hill."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He dug it up,"],[2,"gathered out its stones,"],[2,"planted it with the choicest vine,"],[2,"built a tower in the middle of it,"],[2,"and also cut out a wine press in it."],[1,"He looked for it to yield grapes,"],[2,"but it yielded wild grapes."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow, inhabitants of Jerusalem and men of Judah,"],[2,"please judge between me and my vineyard."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"What could have been done more to my vineyard, that I have not done in it?"],[2,"Why, when I looked for it to yield grapes, did it yield wild grapes?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Now I will tell you what I will do to my vineyard."],[2,"I will take away its hedge, and it will be eaten up."],[2,"I will break down its wall, and it will be trampled down."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I will lay it a wasteland."],[2,"It won\u2019t be pruned or hoed,"],[2,"but it will grow briers and thorns."],[2,"I will also command the clouds that they rain no rain on it.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For the vineyard of the LORD of Armies is the house of Israel,"],[2,"and the men of Judah his pleasant plant."],[2,"He looked for justice, but behold, oppression,"],[2,"for righteousness, but behold, a cry of distress."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who join house to house,"],[2,"who lay field to field, until there is no room,"],[2,"and you are made to dwell alone in the middle of the land!"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"In my ears, the LORD of Armies says: \u201cSurely many houses will be desolate,"],[2,"even great and beautiful, unoccupied."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For ten acres of vineyard shall yield one bath,"],[2,"and a homer of seed shall yield an ephah.\u201d"]],f:["literally, ten yokes, or the amount of land that ten yokes of oxen can plow in one day, which is about 10 acres or 4 hectares.","1 bath is about 22 liters or 5.8 U. S. gallons","1 homer is about 220 liters or 6 bushels","1 ephah is about 22 liters or 0.6 bushels or about 2 pecks\u2014only one tenth of what was sown."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who rise up early in the morning, that they may follow strong drink,"],[2,"who stay late into the night, until wine inflames them!"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The harp, lyre, tambourine, and flute, with wine, are at their feasts;"],[2,"but they don\u2019t respect the work of the LORD,"],[2,"neither have they considered the operation of his hands."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore my people go into captivity for lack of knowledge."],[2,"Their honorable men are famished,"],[2,"and their multitudes are parched with thirst."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore Sheol has enlarged its desire,"],[2,"and opened its mouth without measure;"],[2,"and their glory, their multitude, their pomp, and he who rejoices among them, descend into it."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"So man is brought low,"],[2,"mankind is humbled,"],[2,"and the eyes of the arrogant ones are humbled;"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"but the LORD of Armies is exalted in justice,"],[2,"and God the Holy One is sanctified in righteousness."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the lambs will graze as in their pasture,"],[2,"and strangers will eat the ruins of the rich."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who draw iniquity with cords of falsehood,"],[2,"and wickedness as with cart rope,"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"who say, \u201cLet him make haste, let him hasten his work, that we may see it;"],[2,"let the counsel of the Holy One of Israel draw near and come,"],[2,"that we may know it!\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who call evil good, and good evil;"],[2,"who put darkness for light,"],[2,"and light for darkness;"],[1,"who put bitter for sweet,"],[2,"and sweet for bitter!"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who are wise in their own eyes,"],[2,"and prudent in their own sight!"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who are mighty to drink wine,"],[2,"and champions at mixing strong drink;"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"who acquit the guilty for a bribe,"],[2,"but deny justice for the innocent!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore as the tongue of fire devours the stubble,"],[2,"and as the dry grass sinks down in the flame,"],[2,"so their root shall be as rottenness,"],[2,"and their blossom shall go up as dust,"],[1,"because they have rejected the law of the LORD of Armies,"],[2,"and despised the word of the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD\u2019s anger burns against his people,"],[2,"and he has stretched out his hand against them and has struck them."],[1,"The mountains tremble,"],[2,"and their dead bodies are as refuse in the middle of the streets."],[1,"For all this, his anger is not turned away,"],[2,"but his hand is still stretched out."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"He will lift up a banner to the nations from far away,"],[2,"and he will whistle for them from the end of the earth."],[2,"Behold, they will come speedily and swiftly."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"No one shall be weary nor stumble among them;"],[2,"no one shall slumber nor sleep,"],[2,"neither shall the belt of their waist be untied,"],[2,"nor the strap of their sandals be broken,"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"whose arrows are sharp,"],[2,"and all their bows bent."],[1,"Their horses\u2019 hoofs will be like flint,"],[2,"and their wheels like a whirlwind."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Their roaring will be like a lioness."],[2,"They will roar like young lions."],[1,"Yes, they shall roar,"],[2,"and seize their prey and carry it off,"],[2,"and there will be no one to deliver."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"They will roar against them in that day like the roaring of the sea."],[2,"If one looks to the land, behold, darkness and distress."],[2,"The light is darkened in its clouds."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the year that King Uzziah died, I saw the Lord sitting on a throne, high and lifted up; and his train filled the temple."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Above him stood the seraphim. Each one had six wings. With two he covered his face. With two he covered his feet. With two he flew."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"One called to another, and said,"],[1,"\u201cHoly, holy, holy, is the LORD of Armies!"],[2,"The whole earth is full of his glory!\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The foundations of the thresholds shook at the voice of him who called, and the house was filled with smoke."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cWoe is me! For I am undone, because I am a man of unclean lips and I live among a people of unclean lips, for my eyes have seen the King, the LORD of Armies!\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then one of the seraphim flew to me, having a live coal in his hand, which he had taken with the tongs from off the altar."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He touched my mouth with it, and said, \u201cBehold, this has touched your lips; and your iniquity is taken away, and your sin forgiven.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard the Lord\u2019s voice, saying, \u201cWhom shall I send, and who will go for us?\u201d"],[0,"Then I said, \u201cHere I am. Send me!\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGo, and tell this people,"],[1,"\u2018You hear indeed,"],[2,"but don\u2019t understand."],[1,"You see indeed,"],[2,"but don\u2019t perceive.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Make the heart of this people fat."],[2,"Make their ears heavy, and shut their eyes;"],[1,"lest they see with their eyes,"],[2,"hear with their ears,"],[2,"understand with their heart,"],[2,"and turn again, and be healed.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cLord, how long?\u201d"],[0,"He answered,"],[1,"\u201cUntil cities are waste without inhabitant,"],[2,"houses without man,"],[2,"the land becomes utterly waste,"]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"and the LORD has removed men far away,"],[2,"and the forsaken places are many within the land."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"If there is a tenth left in it,"],[2,"that also will in turn be consumed,"],[1,"as a terebinth, and as an oak whose stump remains when they are cut down,"],[2,"so the holy seed is its stump.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the days of Ahaz the son of Jotham, the son of Uzziah, king of Judah, Rezin the king of Syria and Pekah the son of Remaliah, king of Israel, went up to Jerusalem to war against it, but could not prevail against it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"David\u2019s house was told, \u201cSyria is allied with Ephraim.\u201d His heart trembled, and the heart of his people, as the trees of the forest tremble with the wind."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to Isaiah, \u201cGo out now to meet Ahaz, you, and Shearjashub your son, at the end of the conduit of the upper pool, on the highway of the fuller\u2019s field."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Tell him, \u2018Be careful, and keep calm. Don\u2019t be afraid, neither let your heart be faint because of these two tails of smoking torches, for the fierce anger of Rezin and Syria, and of the son of Remaliah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Because Syria, Ephraim, and the son of Remaliah, have plotted evil against you, saying,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cLet\u2019s go up against Judah, and tear it apart, and let\u2019s divide it among ourselves, and set up a king within it, even the son of Tabeel.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"This is what the Lord GOD says: \u201cIt shall not stand, neither shall it happen.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the head of Syria is Damascus, and the head of Damascus is Rezin. Within sixty-five years Ephraim shall be broken in pieces, so that it shall not be a people."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The head of Ephraim is Samaria, and the head of Samaria is Remaliah\u2019s son. If you will not believe, surely you shall not be established.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke again to Ahaz, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cAsk a sign of the LORD your God; ask it either in the depth, or in the height above.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"But Ahaz said, \u201cI won\u2019t ask. I won\u2019t tempt the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cListen now, house of David. Is it not enough for you to try the patience of men, that you will try the patience of my God also?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord himself will give you a sign. Behold, the virgin will conceive, and bear a son, and shall call his name Immanuel."]],f:["\u201cImmanuel\u201d means \u201cGod with us\u201d."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He shall eat butter and honey when he knows to refuse the evil and choose the good."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For before the child knows to refuse the evil and choose the good, the land whose two kings you abhor shall be forsaken."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The LORD will bring on you, on your people, and on your father\u2019s house days that have not come, from the day that Ephraim departed from Judah, even the king of Assyria."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that the LORD will whistle for the fly that is in the uttermost part of the rivers of Egypt, and for the bee that is in the land of Assyria."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They shall come, and shall all rest in the desolate valleys, in the clefts of the rocks, on all thorn hedges, and on all pastures."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day the Lord will shave with a razor that is hired in the parts beyond the River, even with the king of Assyria, the head and the hair of the feet; and it shall also consume the beard."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall happen in that day that a man shall keep alive a young cow, and two sheep."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"It shall happen, that because of the abundance of milk which they shall give he shall eat butter, for everyone will eat butter and honey that is left within the land."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that every place where there were a thousand vines worth a thousand silver shekels, will be for briers and thorns."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, so 1000 shekels is about 10 kilograms or 22 pounds."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"People will go there with arrows and with bow, because all the land will be briers and thorns."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"All the hills that were cultivated with the hoe, you shall not come there for fear of briers and thorns; but it shall be for the sending out of oxen, and for sheep to tread on.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cTake a large tablet, and write on it with a man\u2019s pen, \u2018For Maher Shalal Hash Baz\u2019;"]],f:["\u201cMaher Shalal Hash Baz\u201d means \u201cquick to the plunder, swift to the prey\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and I will take for myself faithful witnesses to testify: Uriah the priest, and Zechariah the son of Jeberechiah.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"I went to the prophetess, and she conceived, and bore a son. Then the LORD said to me, \u201cCall his name \u2018Maher Shalal Hash Baz.\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For before the child knows how to say, \u2018My father\u2019 and \u2018My mother,\u2019 the riches of Damascus and the plunder of Samaria will be carried away by the king of Assyria.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD spoke to me yet again, saying,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cBecause this people has refused the waters of Shiloah that go softly, and rejoice in Rezin and Remaliah\u2019s son;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"now therefore, behold, the Lord brings upon them the mighty flood waters of the River: the king of Assyria and all his glory. It will come up over all its channels, and go over all its banks."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"It will sweep onward into Judah. It will overflow and pass through. It will reach even to the neck. The stretching out of its wings will fill the width of your land, O Immanuel."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Make an uproar, you peoples, and be broken in pieces! Listen, all you from far countries: dress for battle, and be shattered! Dress for battle, and be shattered!"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Take counsel together, and it will be brought to nothing; speak the word, and it will not stand, for God is with us.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD spoke this to me with a strong hand, and instructed me not to walk in the way of this people, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t call a conspiracy all that this people call a conspiracy. Don\u2019t fear their threats or be terrorized."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies is who you must respect as holy. He is the one you must fear. He is the one you must dread."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He will be a sanctuary, but for both houses of Israel, he will be a stumbling stone and a rock that makes them fall. For the people of Jerusalem, he will be a trap and a snare."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Many will stumble over it, fall, be broken, be snared, and be captured.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Wrap up the covenant. Seal the law among my disciples."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I will wait for the LORD, who hides his face from the house of Jacob, and I will look for him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Behold, I and the children whom the LORD has given me are for signs and for wonders in Israel from the LORD of Armies, who dwells in Mount Zion."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"When they tell you, \u201cConsult with those who have familiar spirits and with the wizards, who chirp and who mutter,\u201d shouldn\u2019t a people consult with their God? Should they consult the dead on behalf of the living?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Turn to the law and to the covenant! If they don\u2019t speak according to this word, surely there is no morning for them."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They will pass through it, very distressed and hungry. It will happen that when they are hungry, they will worry, and curse their king and their God. They will turn their faces upward,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"then look to the earth and see distress, darkness, and the gloom of anguish. They will be driven into thick darkness."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But there shall be no more gloom for her who was in anguish. In the former time, he brought into contempt the land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali; but in the latter time he has made it glorious, by the way of the sea, beyond the Jordan, Galilee of the nations."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The people who walked in darkness have seen a great light."],[2,"The light has shined on those who lived in the land of the shadow of death."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You have multiplied the nation."],[2,"You have increased their joy."],[0,"They rejoice before you according to the joy in harvest, as men rejoice when they divide the plunder."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For the yoke of his burden, and the staff of his shoulder, the rod of his oppressor, you have broken as in the day of Midian."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For all the armor of the armed man in the noisy battle, and the garments rolled in blood, will be for burning, fuel for the fire."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For a child is born to us. A son is given to us; and the government will be on his shoulders. His name will be called Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God, Everlasting Father, Prince of Peace."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Of the increase of his government and of peace there shall be no end, on David\u2019s throne, and on his kingdom, to establish it, and to uphold it with justice and with righteousness from that time on, even forever. The zeal of the LORD of Armies will perform this."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord sent a word into Jacob,"],[2,"and it falls on Israel."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"All the people will know,"],[2,"including Ephraim and the inhabitants of Samaria, who say in pride and in arrogance of heart,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe bricks have fallen,"],[2,"but we will build with cut stone."],[1,"The sycamore fig trees have been cut down,"],[2,"but we will put cedars in their place.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD will set up on high against him the adversaries of Rezin,"],[2,"and will stir up his enemies,"]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"The Syrians in front,"],[2,"and the Philistines behind;"],[2,"and they will devour Israel with open mouth."],[1,"For all this, his anger is not turned away,"],[2,"but his hand is stretched out still."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet the people have not turned to him who struck them,"],[2,"neither have they sought the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD will cut off from Israel head and tail,"],[2,"palm branch and reed, in one day."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The elder and the honorable man is the head,"],[2,"and the prophet who teaches lies is the tail."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For those who lead this people lead them astray;"],[2,"and those who are led by them are destroyed."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the Lord will not rejoice over their young men,"],[2,"neither will he have compassion on their fatherless and widows;"],[1,"for everyone is profane and an evildoer,"],[2,"and every mouth speaks folly."],[1,"For all this his anger is not turned away,"],[2,"but his hand is stretched out still."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For wickedness burns like a fire."],[2,"It devours the briers and thorns;"],[2,"yes, it kindles in the thickets of the forest,"],[2,"and they roll upward in a column of smoke."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Through the LORD of Armies\u2019 wrath, the land is burned up;"],[2,"and the people are the fuel for the fire."],[2,"No one spares his brother."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"One will devour on the right hand, and be hungry;"],[2,"and he will eat on the left hand, and they will not be satisfied."],[1,"Everyone will eat the flesh of his own arm:"]]},{v:21,l:[[2,"Manasseh eating Ephraim and Ephraim eating Manasseh, and they together will be against Judah."],[1,"For all this his anger is not turned away,"],[2,"but his hand is stretched out still."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to those who decree unrighteous decrees, and to the writers who write oppressive decrees"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to deprive the needy of justice, and to rob the poor among my people of their rights, that widows may be their plunder, and that they may make the fatherless their prey!"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"What will you do in the day of visitation, and in the desolation which will come from afar? To whom will you flee for help? Where will you leave your wealth?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"They will only bow down under the prisoners,"],[2,"and will fall under the slain."],[1,"For all this his anger is not turned away,"],[2,"but his hand is stretched out still."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Alas Assyrian, the rod of my anger, the staff in whose hand is my indignation!"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I will send him against a profane nation, and against the people who anger me I will give him a command to take the plunder and to take the prey, and to tread them down like the mire of the streets."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"However, he doesn\u2019t mean so, neither does his heart think so; but it is in his heart to destroy, and to cut off not a few nations."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For he says, \u201cAren\u2019t all of my princes kings?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t Calno like Carchemish? Isn\u2019t Hamath like Arpad? Isn\u2019t Samaria like Damascus?\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As my hand has found the kingdoms of the idols, whose engraved images exceeded those of Jerusalem and of Samaria,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"shall I not, as I have done to Samaria and her idols, so do to Jerusalem and her idols?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore it will happen that when the Lord has performed his whole work on Mount Zion and on Jerusalem, I will punish the fruit of the willful proud heart of the king of Assyria, and the insolence of his arrogant looks."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For he has said, \u201cBy the strength of my hand I have done it, and by my wisdom, for I have understanding. I have removed the boundaries of the peoples, and have robbed their treasures. Like a valiant man I have brought down their rulers."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"My hand has found the riches of the peoples like a nest, and like one gathers eggs that are abandoned, I have gathered all the earth. There was no one who moved their wing, or that opened their mouth, or chirped.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Should an ax brag against him who chops with it? Should a saw exalt itself above him who saws with it? As if a rod should lift those who lift it up, or as if a staff should lift up someone who is not wood."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord, GOD of Armies, will send among his fat ones leanness; and under his glory a burning will be kindled like the burning of fire."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The light of Israel will be for a fire, and his Holy One for a flame; and it will burn and devour his thorns and his briers in one day."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He will consume the glory of his forest and of his fruitful field, both soul and body. It will be as when a standard bearer faints."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The remnant of the trees of his forest shall be few, so that a child could write their number."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"It will come to pass in that day that the remnant of Israel, and those who have escaped from the house of Jacob will no more again lean on him who struck them, but shall lean on the LORD, the Holy One of Israel, in truth."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"A remnant will return, even the remnant of Jacob, to the mighty God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For though your people, Israel, are like the sand of the sea, only a remnant of them will return. A destruction is determined, overflowing with righteousness."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For the Lord, GOD of Armies, will make a full end, and that determined, throughout all the earth."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord, GOD of Armies, says, \u201cMy people who dwell in Zion, don\u2019t be afraid of the Assyrian, though he strike you with the rod, and lift up his staff against you, as Egypt did."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For yet a very little while, and the indignation against you will be accomplished, and my anger will be directed to his destruction.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies will stir up a scourge against him, as in the slaughter of Midian at the rock of Oreb. His rod will be over the sea, and he will lift it up like he did against Egypt."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that his burden will depart from off your shoulder, and his yoke from off your neck, and the yoke shall be destroyed because of the anointing oil."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He has come to Aiath. He has passed through Migron. At Michmash he stores his baggage."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They have gone over the pass. They have taken up their lodging at Geba. Ramah trembles. Gibeah of Saul has fled."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Cry aloud with your voice, daughter of Gallim! Listen, Laishah! You poor Anathoth!"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Madmenah is a fugitive. The inhabitants of Gebim flee for safety."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"This very day he will halt at Nob. He shakes his hand at the mountain of the daughter of Zion, the hill of Jerusalem."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the Lord, GOD of Armies, will lop the boughs with terror. The tall will be cut down, and the lofty will be brought low."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He will cut down the thickets of the forest with iron, and Lebanon will fall by the Mighty One."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"A shoot will come out of the stock of Jesse,"],[2,"and a branch out of his roots will bear fruit."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s Spirit will rest on him:"],[2,"the spirit of wisdom and understanding,"],[2,"the spirit of counsel and might,"],[2,"the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of the LORD."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"His delight will be in the fear of the LORD."],[1,"He will not judge by the sight of his eyes,"],[2,"neither decide by the hearing of his ears;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"but he will judge the poor with righteousness,"],[2,"and decide with equity for the humble of the earth."],[1,"He will strike the earth with the rod of his mouth;"],[2,"and with the breath of his lips he will kill the wicked."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Righteousness will be the belt around his waist,"],[2,"and faithfulness the belt around his waist."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The wolf will live with the lamb,"],[2,"and the leopard will lie down with the young goat,"],[2,"the calf, the young lion, and the fattened calf together;"],[2,"and a little child will lead them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The cow and the bear will graze."],[2,"Their young ones will lie down together."],[2,"The lion will eat straw like the ox."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The nursing child will play near a cobra\u2019s hole,"],[2,"and the weaned child will put his hand on the viper\u2019s den."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They will not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain;"],[2,"for the earth will be full of the knowledge of the LORD,"],[2,"as the waters cover the sea."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that the nations will seek the root of Jesse, who stands as a banner of the peoples; and his resting place will be glorious."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that the Lord will set his hand again the second time to recover the remnant that is left of his people from Assyria, from Egypt, from Pathros, from Cush, from Elam, from Shinar, from Hamath, and from the islands of the sea."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He will set up a banner for the nations, and will assemble the outcasts of Israel, and gather together the dispersed of Judah from the four corners of the earth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The envy also of Ephraim will depart, and those who persecute Judah will be cut off. Ephraim won\u2019t envy Judah, and Judah won\u2019t persecute Ephraim."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They will fly down on the shoulders of the Philistines on the west. Together they will plunder the children of the east. They will extend their power over Edom and Moab, and the children of Ammon will obey them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The LORD will utterly destroy the tongue of the Egyptian sea; and with his scorching wind he will wave his hand over the River, and will split it into seven streams, and cause men to march over in sandals."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"There will be a highway for the remnant that is left of his people from Assyria, like there was for Israel in the day that he came up out of the land of Egypt."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day you will say, \u201cI will give thanks to you, the LORD; for though you were angry with me, your anger has turned away and you comfort me."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, God is my salvation. I will trust, and will not be afraid; for the LORD, the LORD, is my strength and song; and he has become my salvation.\u201d"]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore with joy you will draw water out of the wells of salvation."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"In that day you will say, \u201cGive thanks to the LORD! Call on his name! Declare his doings among the peoples! Proclaim that his name is exalted!"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Sing to the LORD, for he has done excellent things! Let this be known in all the earth!"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Cry aloud and shout, you inhabitant of Zion, for the Holy One of Israel is great among you!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of Babylon, which Isaiah the son of Amoz saw."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Set up a banner on the bare mountain! Lift up your voice to them! Wave your hand, that they may go into the gates of the nobles."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I have commanded my consecrated ones; yes, I have called my mighty men for my anger, even my proudly exulting ones."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The noise of a multitude is in the mountains, as of a great people; the noise of an uproar of the kingdoms of the nations gathered together! The LORD of Armies is mustering the army for the battle."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They come from a far country, from the uttermost part of heaven, even the LORD, and the weapons of his indignation, to destroy the whole land."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Wail, for the LORD\u2019s day is at hand! It will come as destruction from the Almighty."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore all hands will be feeble, and everyone\u2019s heart will melt."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They will be dismayed. Pangs and sorrows will seize them. They will be in pain like a woman in labor. They will look in amazement one at another. Their faces will be faces of flame."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Behold, the day of the LORD comes, cruel, with wrath and fierce anger; to make the land a desolation, and to destroy its sinners out of it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the stars of the sky and its constellations will not give their light. The sun will be darkened in its going out, and the moon will not cause its light to shine."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I will punish the world for their evil, and the wicked for their iniquity. I will cause the arrogance of the proud to cease, and will humble the arrogance of the terrible."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I will make people more rare than fine gold, even a person than the pure gold of Ophir."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore I will make the heavens tremble, and the earth will be shaken out of its place in the LORD of Armies\u2019 wrath, and in the day of his fierce anger."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"It will happen that like a hunted gazelle and like sheep that no one gathers, they will each turn to their own people, and will each flee to their own land."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Everyone who is found will be thrust through. Everyone who is captured will fall by the sword."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Their infants also will be dashed in pieces before their eyes. Their houses will be ransacked, and their wives raped."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them, who will not value silver, and as for gold, they will not delight in it."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Their bows will dash the young men in pieces; and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb. Their eyes will not spare children."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Babylon, the glory of kingdoms, the beauty of the Chaldeans\u2019 pride, will be like when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"It will never be inhabited, neither will it be lived in from generation to generation. The Arabian will not pitch a tent there, neither will shepherds make their flocks lie down there."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But wild animals of the desert will lie there, and their houses will be full of jackals. Ostriches will dwell there, and wild goats will frolic there."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Hyenas will cry in their fortresses, and jackals in the pleasant palaces. Her time is near to come, and her days will not be prolonged."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD will have compassion on Jacob, and will yet choose Israel, and set them in their own land. The foreigner will join himself with them, and they will unite with the house of Jacob."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The peoples will take them, and bring them to their place. The house of Israel will possess them in the LORD\u2019s land for servants and for handmaids. They will take as captives those whose captives they were; and they shall rule over their oppressors."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in the day that the LORD will give you rest from your sorrow, from your trouble, and from the hard service in which you were made to serve,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"that you will take up this parable against the king of Babylon, and say, \u201cHow the oppressor has ceased! The golden city has ceased!\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD has broken the staff of the wicked, the scepter of the rulers,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"who struck the peoples in wrath with a continual stroke, who ruled the nations in anger, with a persecution that no one restrained."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The whole earth is at rest, and is quiet. They break out in song."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Yes, the cypress trees rejoice with you, with the cedars of Lebanon, saying, \u201cSince you are humbled, no lumberjack has come up against us.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Sheol from beneath has moved for you to meet you at your coming. It stirs up the departed spirits for you, even all the rulers of the earth. It has raised up from their thrones all the kings of the nations."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They all will answer and ask you, \u201cHave you also become as weak as we are? Have you become like us?\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Your pomp is brought down to Sheol, with the sound of your stringed instruments. Maggots are spread out under you, and worms cover you."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"How you have fallen from heaven, shining one, son of the dawn! How you are cut down to the ground, who laid the nations low!"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You said in your heart, \u201cI will ascend into heaven! I will exalt my throne above the stars of God! I will sit on the mountain of assembly, in the far north!"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will ascend above the heights of the clouds! I will make myself like the Most High!\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Yet you shall be brought down to Sheol, to the depths of the pit."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Those who see you will stare at you. They will ponder you, saying, \u201cIs this the man who made the earth to tremble, who shook kingdoms,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"who made the world like a wilderness, and overthrew its cities, who didn\u2019t release his prisoners to their home?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"All the kings of the nations sleep in glory, everyone in his own house."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But you are cast away from your tomb like an abominable branch, clothed with the slain who are thrust through with the sword, who go down to the stones of the pit; like a dead body trodden under foot."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You will not join them in burial, because you have destroyed your land. You have killed your people. The offspring of evildoers will not be named forever."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Prepare for slaughter of his children because of the iniquity of their fathers, that they not rise up and possess the earth, and fill the surface of the world with cities."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"\u201cI will rise up against them,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cand cut off from Babylon name and remnant, and son and son\u2019s son,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"\u201cI will also make it a possession for the porcupine, and pools of water. I will sweep it with the broom of destruction,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies has sworn, saying, \u201cSurely, as I have thought, so shall it happen; and as I have purposed, so shall it stand:"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"that I will break the Assyrian in my land, and tread him under foot on my mountains. Then his yoke will leave them, and his burden leave their shoulders."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"This is the plan that is determined for the whole earth. This is the hand that is stretched out over all the nations."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies has planned, and who can stop it? His hand is stretched out, and who can turn it back?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"This burden was in the year that King Ahaz died."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t rejoice, O Philistia, all of you, because the rod that struck you is broken; for out of the serpent\u2019s root an adder will emerge, and his fruit will be a fiery flying serpent."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The firstborn of the poor will eat, and the needy will lie down in safety; and I will kill your root with famine, and your remnant will be killed."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Howl, gate! Cry, city! You are melted away, Philistia, all of you; for smoke comes out of the north, and there is no straggler in his ranks."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"What will they answer the messengers of the nation? That the LORD has founded Zion, and in her the afflicted of his people will take refuge."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of Moab."],[0,"For in a night, Ar of Moab is laid waste, and brought to nothing. For in a night Kir of Moab is laid waste, and brought to nothing."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They have gone up to Bayith, and to Dibon, to the high places, to weep. Moab wails over Nebo and over Medeba. Baldness is on all of their heads. Every beard is cut off."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In their streets, they clothe themselves in sackcloth. In their streets and on their housetops, everyone wails, weeping abundantly."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Heshbon cries out with Elealeh. Their voice is heard even to Jahaz. Therefore the armed men of Moab cry aloud. Their souls tremble within them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"My heart cries out for Moab! Her nobles flee to Zoar, to Eglath Shelishiyah; for they go up by the ascent of Luhith with weeping; for on the way to Horonaim, they raise up a cry of destruction."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the waters of Nimrim will be desolate; for the grass has withered away, the tender grass fails, there is no green thing."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore they will carry away the abundance they have gotten, and that which they have stored up, over the brook of the willows."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the cry has gone around the borders of Moab, its wailing to Eglaim, and its wailing to Beer Elim."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For the waters of Dimon are full of blood; for I will bring yet more on Dimon, a lion on those of Moab who escape, and on the remnant of the land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Send the lambs for the ruler of the land from Selah to the wilderness, to the mountain of the daughter of Zion."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For it will be that as wandering birds, as a scattered nest, so will the daughters of Moab be at the fords of the Arnon."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Give counsel! Execute justice! Make your shade like the night in the middle of the noonday! Hide the outcasts! Don\u2019t betray the fugitive!"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Let my outcasts dwell with you! As for Moab, be a hiding place for him from the face of the destroyer. For the extortionist is brought to nothing. Destruction ceases. The oppressors are consumed out of the land."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"A throne will be established in loving kindness. One will sit on it in truth, in the tent of David, judging, seeking justice, and swift to do righteousness."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"We have heard of the pride of Moab, that he is very proud; even of his arrogance, his pride, and his wrath. His boastings are nothing."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore Moab will wail for Moab. Everyone will wail. You will mourn for the raisin cakes of Kir Hareseth, utterly stricken."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the fields of Heshbon languish with the vine of Sibmah. The lords of the nations have broken down its choice branches, which reached even to Jazer, which wandered into the wilderness. Its shoots were spread abroad. They passed over the sea."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore I will weep with the weeping of Jazer for the vine of Sibmah. I will water you with my tears, Heshbon, and Elealeh: for on your summer fruits and on your harvest the battle shout has fallen."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Gladness is taken away, and joy out of the fruitful field; and in the vineyards there will be no singing, neither joyful noise. Nobody will tread out wine in the presses. I have made the shouting stop."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore my heart sounds like a harp for Moab, and my inward parts for Kir Heres."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It will happen that when Moab presents himself, when he wearies himself on the high place, and comes to his sanctuary to pray, that he will not prevail."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the word that the LORD spoke concerning Moab in time past."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But now the LORD has spoken, saying, \u201cWithin three years, as a worker bound by contract would count them, the glory of Moab shall be brought into contempt, with all his great multitude; and the remnant will be very small and feeble.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of Damascus."],[0,"\u201cBehold, Damascus is taken away from being a city, and it will be a ruinous heap."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The cities of Aroer are forsaken. They will be for flocks, which shall lie down, and no one shall make them afraid."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The fortress shall cease from Ephraim, and the kingdom from Damascus, and the remnant of Syria. They will be as the glory of the children of Israel,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt will happen in that day that the glory of Jacob will be made thin, and the fatness of his flesh will become lean."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It will be like when the harvester gathers the wheat, and his arm reaps the grain. Yes, it will be like when one gleans grain in the valley of Rephaim."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Yet gleanings will be left there, like the shaking of an olive tree, two or three olives in the top of the uppermost bough, four or five in the outermost branches of a fruitful tree,\u201d says the LORD, the God of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In that day, people will look to their Maker, and their eyes will have respect for the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They will not look to the altars, the work of their hands; neither shall they respect that which their fingers have made, either the Asherah poles or the incense altars."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"In that day, their strong cities will be like the forsaken places in the woods and on the mountain top, which were forsaken from before the children of Israel; and it will be a desolation."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For you have forgotten the God of your salvation, and have not remembered the rock of your strength. Therefore you plant pleasant plants, and set out foreign seedlings."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In the day of your planting, you hedge it in. In the morning, you make your seed blossom, but the harvest flees away in the day of grief and of desperate sorrow."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Ah, the uproar of many peoples who roar like the roaring of the seas; and the rushing of nations that rush like the rushing of mighty waters!"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The nations will rush like the rushing of many waters, but he will rebuke them, and they will flee far off, and will be chased like the chaff of the mountains before the wind, and like the whirling dust before the storm."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"At evening, behold, terror! Before the morning, they are no more. This is the portion of those who plunder us, and the lot of those who rob us."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Ah, the land of the rustling of wings, which is beyond the rivers of Ethiopia;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that sends ambassadors by the sea, even in vessels of papyrus on the waters, saying, \u201cGo, you swift messengers, to a nation tall and smooth, to a people awesome from their beginning onward, a nation that measures out and treads down, whose land the rivers divide!\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All you inhabitants of the world, and you dwellers on the earth, when a banner is lifted up on the mountains, look! When the trumpet is blown, listen!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD said to me, \u201cI will be still, and I will see in my dwelling place, like clear heat in sunshine, like a cloud of dew in the heat of harvest.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For before the harvest, when the blossom is over, and the flower becomes a ripening grape, he will cut off the sprigs with pruning hooks, and he will cut down and take away the spreading branches."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They will be left together for the ravenous birds of the mountains, and for the animals of the earth. The ravenous birds will eat them in the summer, and all the animals of the earth will eat them in the winter."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In that time, a present will be brought to the LORD of Armies from a people tall and smooth, even from a people awesome from their beginning onward, a nation that measures out and treads down, whose land the rivers divide, to the place of the name of the LORD of Armies, Mount Zion."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of Egypt."],[0,"\u201cBehold, the LORD rides on a swift cloud, and comes to Egypt. The idols of Egypt will tremble at his presence; and the heart of Egypt will melt within it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will stir up the Egyptians against the Egyptians, and they will fight everyone against his brother, and everyone against his neighbor; city against city, and kingdom against kingdom."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The spirit of the Egyptians will fail within them. I will destroy their counsel. They will seek the idols, the charmers, those who have familiar spirits, and the wizards."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will give over the Egyptians into the hand of a cruel lord. A fierce king will rule over them,\u201d says the Lord, GOD of Armies."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The waters will fail from the sea, and the river will be wasted and become dry."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The rivers will become foul. The streams of Egypt will be diminished and dried up. The reeds and flags will wither away."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The meadows by the Nile, by the brink of the Nile, and all the sown fields of the Nile, will become dry, be driven away, and be no more."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The fishermen will lament, and all those who fish in the Nile will mourn, and those who spread nets on the waters will languish."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Moreover those who work in combed flax, and those who weave white cloth, will be confounded."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The pillars will be broken in pieces. All those who work for hire will be grieved in soul."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The princes of Zoan are utterly foolish. The counsel of the wisest counselors of Pharaoh has become stupid. How do you say to Pharaoh, \u201cI am the son of the wise, the son of ancient kings\u201d?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Where then are your wise men? Let them tell you now; and let them know what the LORD of Armies has purposed concerning Egypt."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The princes of Zoan have become fools. The princes of Memphis are deceived. They have caused Egypt to go astray, those who are the cornerstone of her tribes."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The LORD has mixed a spirit of perverseness in the middle of her; and they have caused Egypt to go astray in all of its works, like a drunken man staggers in his vomit."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Neither shall there be any work for Egypt, which head or tail, palm branch or rush, may do."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"In that day the Egyptians will be like women. They will tremble and fear because of the shaking of the LORD of Armies\u2019s hand, which he shakes over them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The land of Judah will become a terror to Egypt. Everyone to whom mention is made of it will be afraid, because of the plans of the LORD of Armies, which he determines against it."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In that day, there will be five cities in the land of Egypt that speak the language of Canaan, and swear to the LORD of Armies. One will be called \u201cThe city of destruction.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, there will be an altar to the LORD in the middle of the land of Egypt, and a pillar to the LORD at its border."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"It will be for a sign and for a witness to the LORD of Armies in the land of Egypt; for they will cry to the LORD because of oppressors, and he will send them a savior and a defender, and he will deliver them."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD will be known to Egypt, and the Egyptians will know the LORD in that day. Yes, they will worship with sacrifice and offering, and will vow a vow to the LORD, and will perform it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The LORD will strike Egypt, striking and healing. They will return to the LORD, and he will be entreated by them, and will heal them."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day there will be a highway out of Egypt to Assyria, and the Assyrian shall come into Egypt, and the Egyptian into Assyria; and the Egyptians will worship with the Assyrians."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, Israel will be the third with Egypt and with Assyria, a blessing within the earth;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"because the LORD of Armies has blessed them, saying, \u201cBlessed be Egypt my people, Assyria the work of my hands, and Israel my inheritance.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the year that Tartan came to Ashdod, when Sargon the king of Assyria sent him, and he fought against Ashdod and took it;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"at that time the LORD spoke by Isaiah the son of Amoz, saying, \u201cGo, and loosen the sackcloth from off your waist, and take your sandals from off your feet.\u201d He did so, walking naked and barefoot."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cAs my servant Isaiah has walked naked and barefoot three years for a sign and a wonder concerning Egypt and concerning Ethiopia,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"so the king of Assyria will lead away the captives of Egypt and the exiles of Ethiopia, young and old, naked and barefoot, and with buttocks uncovered, to the shame of Egypt."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They will be dismayed and confounded, because of Ethiopia their expectation, and of Egypt their glory."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The inhabitants of this coast land will say in that day, \u2018Behold, this is our expectation, where we fled for help to be delivered from the king of Assyria. And we, how will we escape?\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of the wilderness of the sea."],[0,"As whirlwinds in the South sweep through, it comes from the wilderness, from an awesome land."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"A grievous vision is declared to me. The treacherous man deals treacherously, and the destroyer destroys. Go up, Elam; attack! I have stopped all of Media\u2019s sighing."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore my thighs are filled with anguish. Pains have seized me, like the pains of a woman in labor. I am in so much pain that I can\u2019t hear. I am so dismayed that I can\u2019t see."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"My heart flutters. Horror has frightened me. The twilight that I desired has been turned into trembling for me."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They prepare the table. They set the watch. They eat. They drink. Rise up, you princes, oil the shield!"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the Lord said to me, \u201cGo, set a watchman. Let him declare what he sees."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When he sees a troop, horsemen in pairs, a troop of donkeys, a troop of camels, he shall listen diligently with great attentiveness.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He cried like a lion: \u201cLord, I stand continually on the watchtower in the daytime, and every night I stay at my post."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Behold, here comes a troop of men, horsemen in pairs.\u201d He answered, \u201cFallen, fallen is Babylon; and all the engraved images of her gods are broken to the ground."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"You are my threshing, and the grain of my floor!\u201d That which I have heard from the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, I have declared to you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of Dumah."],[0,"One calls to me out of Seir, \u201cWatchman, what of the night? Watchman, what of the night?\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The watchman said, \u201cThe morning comes, and also the night. If you will inquire, inquire. Come back again.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden on Arabia."],[0,"You will lodge in the thickets in Arabia, you caravans of Dedanites."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They brought water to him who was thirsty. The inhabitants of the land of Tema met the fugitives with their bread."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For they fled away from the swords, from the drawn sword, from the bent bow, and from the heat of battle."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For the Lord said to me, \u201cWithin a year, as a worker bound by contract would count it, all the glory of Kedar will fail,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and the residue of the number of the archers, the mighty men of the children of Kedar, will be few; for the LORD, the God of Israel, has spoken it.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of the valley of vision."],[0,"What ails you now, that you have all gone up to the housetops?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You that are full of shouting, a tumultuous city, a joyous town, your slain are not slain with the sword, neither are they dead in battle."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All your rulers fled away together. They were bound by the archers. All who were found by you were bound together. They fled far away."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Therefore I said, \u201cLook away from me. I will weep bitterly. Don\u2019t labor to comfort me for the destruction of the daughter of my people."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"For it is a day of confusion, and of treading down, and of perplexity from the Lord, GOD of Armies, in the valley of vision, a breaking down of the walls, and a crying to the mountains.\u201d"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Elam carried his quiver, with chariots of men and horsemen; and Kir uncovered the shield."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Your choicest valleys were full of chariots, and the horsemen set themselves in array at the gate."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He took away the covering of Judah; and you looked in that day to the armor in the house of the forest."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You saw the breaches of David\u2019s city, that they were many; and you gathered together the waters of the lower pool."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You counted the houses of Jerusalem, and you broke down the houses to fortify the wall."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You also made a reservoir between the two walls for the water of the old pool. But you didn\u2019t look to him who had done this, neither did you have respect for him who planned it long ago."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, the Lord, GOD of Armies, called to weeping, to mourning, to baldness, and to dressing in sackcloth;"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and behold, there is joy and gladness, killing cattle and killing sheep, eating meat and drinking wine: \u201cLet\u2019s eat and drink, for tomorrow we will die.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies revealed himself in my ears, \u201cSurely this iniquity will not be forgiven you until you die,\u201d says the Lord, GOD of Armies."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord, GOD of Armies says, \u201cGo, get yourself to this treasurer, even to Shebna, who is over the house, and say,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u2018What are you doing here? Who has you here, that you have dug out a tomb here?\u2019 Cutting himself out a tomb on high, chiseling a habitation for himself in the rock!\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Behold, the LORD will overcome you and hurl you away violently. Yes, he will grasp you firmly."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He will surely wind you around and around, and throw you like a ball into a large country. There you will die, and there the chariots of your glory will be, you disgrace of your lord\u2019s house."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I will thrust you from your office. You will be pulled down from your station."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that I will call my servant Eliakim the son of Hilkiah,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and I will clothe him with your robe, and strengthen him with your belt. I will commit your government into his hand; and he will be a father to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and to the house of Judah."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will lay the key of David\u2019s house on his shoulder. He will open, and no one will shut. He will shut, and no one will open."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will fasten him like a nail in a sure place. He will be for a throne of glory to his father\u2019s house."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They will hang on him all the glory of his father\u2019s house, the offspring and the issue, every small vessel, from the cups even to all the pitchers."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"\u201cIn that day,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cthe nail that was fastened in a sure place will give way. It will be cut down and fall. The burden that was on it will be cut off, for the LORD has spoken it.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of Tyre."],[0,"Howl, you ships of Tarshish! For it is laid waste, so that there is no house, no entering in. From the land of Kittim it is revealed to them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Be still, you inhabitants of the coast, you whom the merchants of Sidon that pass over the sea have replenished."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"On great waters, the seed of the Shihor, the harvest of the Nile, was her revenue. She was the market of nations."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Be ashamed, Sidon; for the sea has spoken, the stronghold of the sea, saying, \u201cI have not travailed, nor given birth, neither have I nourished young men, nor brought up virgins.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When the report comes to Egypt, they will be in anguish at the report of Tyre."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Pass over to Tarshish! Wail, you inhabitants of the coast!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Is this your joyous city, whose antiquity is of ancient days, whose feet carried her far away to travel?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Who has planned this against Tyre, the giver of crowns, whose merchants are princes, whose traders are the honorable of the earth?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies has planned it, to stain the pride of all glory, to bring into contempt all the honorable of the earth."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Pass through your land like the Nile, daughter of Tarshish. There is no restraint any more."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He has stretched out his hand over the sea. He has shaken the kingdoms. The LORD has ordered the destruction of Canaan\u2019s strongholds."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYou shall rejoice no more, you oppressed virgin daughter of Sidon. Arise, pass over to Kittim. Even there you will have no rest.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the land of the Chaldeans. This people didn\u2019t exist. The Assyrians founded it for those who dwell in the wilderness. They set up their towers. They overthrew its palaces. They made it a ruin."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Howl, you ships of Tarshish, for your stronghold is laid waste!"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"It will come to pass in that day that Tyre will be forgotten seventy years, according to the days of one king. After the end of seventy years it will be to Tyre like in the song of the prostitute."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Take a harp; go about the city, you prostitute that has been forgotten. Make sweet melody. Sing many songs, that you may be remembered."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It will happen after the end of seventy years that the LORD will visit Tyre. She will return to her wages, and will play the prostitute with all the kingdoms of the world on the surface of the earth."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Her merchandise and her wages will be holiness to the LORD. It will not be treasured nor laid up; for her merchandise will be for those who dwell before the LORD, to eat sufficiently, and for durable clothing."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the LORD makes the earth empty, makes it waste, turns it upside down, and scatters its inhabitants."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It will be as with the people, so with the priest; as with the servant, so with his master; as with the maid, so with her mistress; as with the buyer, so with the seller; as with the creditor, so with the debtor; as with the taker of interest, so with the giver of interest."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The earth will be utterly emptied and utterly laid waste; for the LORD has spoken this word."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The earth mourns and fades away. The world languishes and fades away. The lofty people of the earth languish."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The earth also is polluted under its inhabitants, because they have transgressed the laws, violated the statutes, and broken the everlasting covenant."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore the curse has devoured the earth, and those who dwell therein are found guilty. Therefore the inhabitants of the earth are burned, and few men are left."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The new wine mourns. The vine languishes. All the merry-hearted sigh."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The mirth of tambourines ceases. The sound of those who rejoice ends. The joy of the harp ceases."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They will not drink wine with a song. Strong drink will be bitter to those who drink it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The confused city is broken down. Every house is shut up, that no man may come in."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"There is a crying in the streets because of the wine. All joy is darkened. The mirth of the land is gone."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The city is left in desolation, and the gate is struck with destruction."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For it will be so within the earth among the peoples, as the shaking of an olive tree, as the gleanings when the vintage is done."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"These shall lift up their voice. They will shout for the majesty of the LORD. They cry aloud from the sea."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Therefore glorify the LORD in the east, even the name of the LORD, the God of Israel, in the islands of the sea!"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"From the uttermost part of the earth have we heard songs. Glory to the righteous!"],[0,"But I said, \u201cI pine away! I pine away! woe is me!\u201d The treacherous have dealt treacherously. Yes, the treacherous have dealt very treacherously."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Fear, the pit, and the snare are on you who inhabit the earth."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"It will happen that he who flees from the noise of the fear will fall into the pit; and he who comes up out of the middle of the pit will be taken in the snare; for the windows on high are opened, and the foundations of the earth tremble."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The earth is utterly broken. The earth is torn apart. The earth is shaken violently."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The earth will stagger like a drunken man, and will sway back and forth like a hammock. Its disobedience will be heavy on it, and it will fall and not rise again."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that the LORD will punish the army of the high ones on high, and the kings of the earth on the earth."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They will be gathered together, as prisoners are gathered in the pit, and will be shut up in the prison; and after many days they will be visited."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then the moon will be confounded, and the sun ashamed; for the LORD of Armies will reign on Mount Zion and in Jerusalem; and glory will be before his elders."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD, you are my God. I will exalt you! I will praise your name, for you have done wonderful things, things planned long ago, in complete faithfulness and truth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For you have made a city into a heap, a fortified city into a ruin, a palace of strangers to be no city. It will never be built."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore a strong people will glorify you. A city of awesome nations will fear you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For you have been a stronghold to the poor, a stronghold to the needy in his distress, a refuge from the storm, a shade from the heat, when the blast of the dreaded ones is like a storm against the wall."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"As the heat in a dry place you will bring down the noise of strangers; as the heat by the shade of a cloud, the song of the dreaded ones will be brought low."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"In this mountain, the LORD of Armies will make all peoples a feast of choice meat, a feast of choice wines, of choice meat full of marrow, of well refined choice wines."]],f:["literally, fat things"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He will destroy in this mountain the surface of the covering that covers all peoples, and the veil that is spread over all nations."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He has swallowed up death forever! The Lord GOD will wipe away tears from off all faces. He will take the reproach of his people away from off all the earth, for the LORD has spoken it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"It shall be said in that day, \u201cBehold, this is our God! We have waited for him, and he will save us! This is the LORD! We have waited for him. We will be glad and rejoice in his salvation!\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the LORD\u2019s hand will rest in this mountain."],[0,"Moab will be trodden down in his place, even like straw is trodden down in the water of the dunghill."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He will spread out his hands in the middle of it, like one who swims spreads out hands to swim, but his pride will be humbled together with the craft of his hands."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He has brought the high fortress of your walls down, laid low, and brought to the ground, even to the dust."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, this song will be sung in the land of Judah:"],[1,"\u201cWe have a strong city."],[2,"God appoints salvation for walls and bulwarks."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Open the gates, that the righteous nation may enter:"],[2,"the one which keeps faith."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You will keep whoever\u2019s mind is steadfast in perfect peace,"],[2,"because he trusts in you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Trust in the LORD forever;"],[2,"for in the LORD, the LORD, is an everlasting Rock."]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah.","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For he has brought down those who dwell on high, the lofty city."],[2,"He lays it low."],[2,"He lays it low even to the ground."],[2,"He brings it even to the dust."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The foot shall tread it down,"],[2,"even the feet of the poor"],[2,"and the steps of the needy.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The way of the just is uprightness."],[2,"You who are upright make the path of the righteous level."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, in the way of your judgments, LORD, we have waited for you."],[2,"Your name and your renown are the desire of our soul."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"With my soul I have desired you in the night."],[2,"Yes, with my spirit within me I will seek you earnestly;"],[2,"for when your judgments are on the earth, the inhabitants of the world learn righteousness."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Let favor be shown to the wicked,"],[2,"yet he will not learn righteousness."],[1,"In the land of uprightness he will deal wrongfully,"],[2,"and will not see the LORD\u2019s majesty."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, your hand is lifted up, yet they don\u2019t see;"],[2,"but they will see your zeal for the people and be disappointed."],[2,"Yes, fire will consume your adversaries."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you will ordain peace for us,"],[2,"for you have also done all our work for us."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD our God, other lords besides you have had dominion over us,"],[2,"but we will only acknowledge your name."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The dead shall not live."],[2,"The departed spirits shall not rise."],[1,"Therefore you have visited and destroyed them,"],[2,"and caused all memory of them to perish."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You have increased the nation, O LORD."],[2,"You have increased the nation!"],[1,"You are glorified!"],[2,"You have enlarged all the borders of the land."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, in trouble they have visited you."],[2,"They poured out a prayer when your chastening was on them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Just as a woman with child, who draws near the time of her delivery,"],[2,"is in pain and cries out in her pangs,"],[2,"so we have been before you, LORD."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"We have been with child."],[2,"We have been in pain."],[1,"We gave birth, it seems, only to wind."],[2,"We have not worked any deliverance on the earth;"],[2,"neither have the inhabitants of the world fallen."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Your dead shall live."],[2,"Their dead bodies shall arise."],[1,"Awake and sing, you who dwell in the dust;"],[2,"for your dew is like the dew of herbs,"],[2,"and the earth will cast out the departed spirits."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Come, my people, enter into your rooms,"],[2,"and shut your doors behind you."],[1,"Hide yourself for a little moment,"],[2,"until the indignation is past."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, the LORD comes out of his place to punish the inhabitants of the earth for their iniquity."],[2,"The earth also will disclose her blood, and will no longer cover her slain."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, the LORD with his hard and great and strong sword will punish leviathan, the fleeing serpent, and leviathan, the twisted serpent; and he will kill the dragon that is in the sea."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, sing to her, \u201cA pleasant vineyard!"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I, the LORD, am its keeper. I will water it every moment. Lest anyone damage it, I will keep it night and day."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Wrath is not in me, but if I should find briers and thorns, I would do battle! I would march on them and I would burn them together."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Or else let him take hold of my strength, that he may make peace with me. Let him make peace with me.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"In days to come, Jacob will take root. Israel will blossom and bud. They will fill the surface of the world with fruit."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Has he struck them as he struck those who struck them? Or are they killed like those who killed them were killed?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"In measure, when you send them away, you contend with them. He has removed them with his rough blast in the day of the east wind."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore by this the iniquity of Jacob will be forgiven, and this is all the fruit of taking away his sin: that he makes all the stones of the altar as chalk stones that are beaten in pieces, so that the Asherah poles and the incense altars shall rise no more."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the fortified city is solitary, a habitation deserted and forsaken, like the wilderness. The calf will feed there, and there he will lie down, and consume its branches."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When its boughs are withered, they will be broken off. The women will come and set them on fire, for they are a people of no understanding. Therefore he who made them will not have compassion on them, and he who formed them will show them no favor."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that the LORD will thresh from the flowing stream of the Euphrates to the brook of Egypt; and you will be gathered one by one, children of Israel."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that a great trumpet will be blown; and those who were ready to perish in the land of Assyria, and those who were outcasts in the land of Egypt, shall come; and they will worship the LORD in the holy mountain at Jerusalem."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to the crown of pride of the drunkards of Ephraim, and to the fading flower of his glorious beauty, which is on the head of the fertile valley of those who are overcome with wine!"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, the Lord has one who is mighty and strong. Like a storm of hail, a destroying storm, and like a storm of mighty waters overflowing, he will cast them down to the earth with his hand."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The crown of pride of the drunkards of Ephraim will be trodden under foot."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The fading flower of his glorious beauty, which is on the head of the fertile valley, shall be like the first-ripe fig before the summer, which someone picks and eats as soon as he sees it."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"In that day, the LORD of Armies will become a crown of glory and a diadem of beauty to the residue of his people,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and a spirit of justice to him who sits in judgment, and strength to those who turn back the battle at the gate."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They also reel with wine, and stagger with strong drink. The priest and the prophet reel with strong drink. They are swallowed up by wine. They stagger with strong drink. They err in vision. They stumble in judgment."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For all tables are completely full of filthy vomit and filthiness."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Whom will he teach knowledge? To whom will he explain the message? Those who are weaned from the milk, and drawn from the breasts?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For it is precept on precept, precept on precept; line on line, line on line; here a little, there a little."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But he will speak to this nation with stammering lips and in another language,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"to whom he said, \u201cThis is the resting place. Give rest to the weary,\u201d and \u201cThis is the refreshing;\u201d yet they would not hear."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD\u2019s word will be to them precept on precept, precept on precept; line on line, line on line; here a little, there a little; that they may go, fall backward, be broken, be snared, and be taken."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore hear the LORD\u2019s word, you scoffers, that rule this people in Jerusalem:"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cBecause you have said, \u2018We have made a covenant with death, and we are in agreement with Sheol. When the overflowing scourge passes through, it won\u2019t come to us; for we have made lies our refuge, and we have hidden ourselves under falsehood.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says, \u201cBehold, I lay in Zion for a foundation a stone, a tried stone, a precious cornerstone of a sure foundation. He who believes shall not act hastily."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I will make justice the measuring line, and righteousness the plumb line. The hail will sweep away the refuge of lies, and the waters will overflow the hiding place."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Your covenant with death shall be annulled, and your agreement with Sheol shall not stand. When the overflowing scourge passes through, then you will be trampled down by it."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:19,l:[[0,"As often as it passes through, it will seize you; for morning by morning it will pass through, by day and by night; and it will be nothing but terror to understand the message.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For the bed is too short to stretch out on, and the blanket is too narrow to wrap oneself in."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For the LORD will rise up as on Mount Perazim. He will be angry as in the valley of Gibeon; that he may do his work, his unusual work, and bring to pass his act, his extraordinary act."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Now therefore don\u2019t be scoffers, lest your bonds be made strong; for I have heard a decree of destruction from the Lord, GOD of Armies, on the whole earth."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Give ear, and hear my voice! Listen, and hear my speech!"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Does he who plows to sow plow continually? Does he keep turning the soil and breaking the clods?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When he has leveled its surface, doesn\u2019t he plant the dill, and scatter the cumin seed, and put in the wheat in rows, the barley in the appointed place, and the spelt in its place?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For his God instructs him in right judgment and teaches him."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For the dill isn\u2019t threshed with a sharp instrument, neither is a cart wheel turned over the cumin; but the dill is beaten out with a stick, and the cumin with a rod."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Bread flour must be ground; so he will not always be threshing it. Although he drives the wheel of his threshing cart over it, his horses don\u2019t grind it."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"This also comes out from the LORD of Armies, who is wonderful in counsel, and excellent in wisdom."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to Ariel! Ariel, the city where David encamped! Add year to year; let the feasts come around;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"then I will distress Ariel, and there will be mourning and lamentation. She shall be to me as an altar hearth."]],f:["or, Ariel"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will encamp against you all around you, and will lay siege against you with posted troops. I will raise siege works against you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You will be brought down, and will speak out of the ground. Your speech will mumble out of the dust. Your voice will be as of one who has a familiar spirit, out of the ground, and your speech will whisper out of the dust."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But the multitude of your foes will be like fine dust, and the multitude of the ruthless ones like chaff that blows away. Yes, it will be in an instant, suddenly."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"She will be visited by the LORD of Armies with thunder, with earthquake, with great noise, with whirlwind and storm, and with the flame of a devouring fire."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The multitude of all the nations that fight against Ariel, even all who fight against her and her stronghold, and who distress her, will be like a dream, a vision of the night."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"It will be like when a hungry man dreams, and behold, he eats; but he awakes, and his hunger isn\u2019t satisfied; or like when a thirsty man dreams, and behold, he drinks; but he awakes, and behold, he is faint, and he is still thirsty. The multitude of all the nations that fight against Mount Zion will be like that."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Pause and wonder! Blind yourselves and be blind! They are drunken, but not with wine; they stagger, but not with strong drink."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the LORD has poured out on you a spirit of deep sleep, and has closed your eyes, the prophets; and he has covered your heads, the seers."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"All vision has become to you like the words of a book that is sealed, which men deliver to one who is educated, saying, \u201cRead this, please;\u201d and he says, \u201cI can\u2019t, for it is sealed;\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and the book is delivered to one who is not educated, saying, \u201cRead this, please;\u201d and he says, \u201cI can\u2019t read.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord said, \u201cBecause this people draws near with their mouth and honors me with their lips, but they have removed their heart far from me, and their fear of me is a commandment of men which has been taught;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"therefore, behold, I will proceed to do a marvelous work among this people, even a marvelous work and a wonder; and the wisdom of their wise men will perish, and the understanding of their prudent men will be hidden.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to those who deeply hide their counsel from the LORD, and whose deeds are in the dark, and who say, \u201cWho sees us?\u201d and \u201cWho knows us?\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You turn things upside down! Should the potter be thought to be like clay, that the thing made should say about him who made it, \u201cHe didn\u2019t make me;\u201d or the thing formed say of him who formed it, \u201cHe has no understanding\u201d?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t it yet a very little while, and Lebanon will be turned into a fruitful field, and the fruitful field will be regarded as a forest?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In that day, the deaf will hear the words of the book, and the eyes of the blind will see out of obscurity and out of darkness."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The humble also will increase their joy in the LORD, and the poor among men will rejoice in the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For the ruthless is brought to nothing, and the scoffer ceases, and all those who are alert to do evil are cut off\u2014"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"who cause a person to be indicted by a word, and lay a snare for one who reproves in the gate, and who deprive the innocent of justice with false testimony."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD, who redeemed Abraham, says concerning the house of Jacob: \u201cJacob shall no longer be ashamed, neither shall his face grow pale."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But when he sees his children, the work of my hands, in the middle of him, they will sanctify my name. Yes, they will sanctify the Holy One of Jacob, and will stand in awe of the God of Israel."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They also who err in spirit will come to understanding, and those who grumble will receive instruction.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to the rebellious children\u201d, says the LORD, \u201cwho take counsel, but not from me; and who make an alliance, but not with my Spirit, that they may add sin to sin;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"who set out to go down into Egypt without asking for my advice, to strengthen themselves in the strength of Pharaoh, and to take refuge in the shadow of Egypt!"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore the strength of Pharaoh will be your shame, and the refuge in the shadow of Egypt your confusion."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For their princes are at Zoan, and their ambassadors have come to Hanes."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They shall all be ashamed because of a people that can\u2019t profit them, that are not a help nor profit, but a shame, and also a reproach.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The burden of the animals of the South."],[0,"Through the land of trouble and anguish, of the lioness and the lion, the viper and fiery flying serpent, they carry their riches on the shoulders of young donkeys, and their treasures on the humps of camels, to an unprofitable people."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For Egypt helps in vain, and to no purpose; therefore I have called her Rahab who sits still."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now go, write it before them on a tablet, and inscribe it in a book, that it may be for the time to come forever and ever."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For it is a rebellious people, lying children, children who will not hear the LORD\u2019s law;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"who tell the seers, \u201cDon\u2019t see!\u201d and the prophets, \u201cDon\u2019t prophesy to us right things. Tell us pleasant things. Prophesy deceits."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Get out of the way. Turn away from the path. Cause the Holy One of Israel to cease from before us.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore the Holy One of Israel says, \u201cBecause you despise this word, and trust in oppression and perverseness, and rely on it,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"therefore this iniquity shall be to you like a breach ready to fall, swelling out in a high wall, whose breaking comes suddenly in an instant."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He will break it as a potter\u2019s vessel is broken, breaking it in pieces without sparing, so that there won\u2019t be found among the broken pieces a piece good enough to take fire from the hearth, or to dip up water out of the cistern.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"For thus said the Lord GOD, the Holy One of Israel, \u201cYou will be saved in returning and rest. Your strength will be in quietness and in confidence.\u201d You refused,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"but you said, \u201cNo, for we will flee on horses;\u201d therefore you will flee; and, \u201cWe will ride on the swift;\u201d therefore those who pursue you will be swift."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"One thousand will flee at the threat of one. At the threat of five, you will flee until you are left like a beacon on the top of a mountain, and like a banner on a hill."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD will wait, that he may be gracious to you; and therefore he will be exalted, that he may have mercy on you, for the LORD is a God of justice. Blessed are all those who wait for him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the people will dwell in Zion at Jerusalem. You will weep no more. He will surely be gracious to you at the voice of your cry. When he hears you, he will answer you."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Though the Lord may give you the bread of adversity and the water of affliction, yet your teachers won\u2019t be hidden any more, but your eyes will see your teachers;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and when you turn to the right hand, and when you turn to the left, your ears will hear a voice behind you, saying, \u201cThis is the way. Walk in it.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall defile the overlaying of your engraved images of silver, and the plating of your molten images of gold. You shall cast them away as an unclean thing. You shall tell it, \u201cGo away!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He will give the rain for your seed, with which you will sow the ground; and bread of the increase of the ground will be rich and plentiful. In that day, your livestock will feed in large pastures."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The oxen likewise and the young donkeys that till the ground will eat savory feed, which has been winnowed with the shovel and with the fork."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There will be brooks and streams of water on every lofty mountain and on every high hill in the day of the great slaughter, when the towers fall."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Moreover the light of the moon will be like the light of the sun, and the light of the sun will be seven times brighter, like the light of seven days, in the day that the LORD binds up the fracture of his people, and heals the wound they were struck with."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the LORD\u2019s name comes from far away, burning with his anger, and in thick rising smoke. His lips are full of indignation. His tongue is as a devouring fire."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"His breath is as an overflowing stream that reaches even to the neck, to sift the nations with the sieve of destruction. A bridle that leads to ruin will be in the jaws of the peoples."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You will have a song, as in the night when a holy feast is kept, and gladness of heart, as when one goes with a flute to come to the LORD\u2019s mountain, to Israel\u2019s Rock."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The LORD will cause his glorious voice to be heard, and will show the descent of his arm, with the indignation of his anger and the flame of a devouring fire, with a blast, storm, and hailstones."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For through the LORD\u2019s voice the Assyrian will be dismayed. He will strike him with his rod."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Every stroke of the rod of punishment, which the LORD will lay on him, will be with the sound of tambourines and harps. He will fight with them in battles, brandishing weapons."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"For his burning place has long been ready. Yes, it is prepared for the king. He has made its pyre deep and large with fire and much wood. The LORD\u2019s breath, like a stream of sulfur, kindles it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who go down to Egypt for help,"],[2,"and rely on horses,"],[2,"and trust in chariots because they are many,"],[2,"and in horsemen because they are very strong,"],[2,"but they don\u2019t look to the Holy One of Israel,"],[2,"and they don\u2019t seek the LORD!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet he also is wise, and will bring disaster,"],[2,"and will not call back his words, but will arise against the house of the evildoers,"],[2,"and against the help of those who work iniquity."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Now the Egyptians are men, and not God;"],[2,"and their horses flesh, and not spirit."],[1,"When the LORD stretches out his hand, both he who helps shall stumble,"],[2,"and he who is helped shall fall,"],[2,"and they all shall be consumed together."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD says to me,"],[1,"\u201cAs the lion and the young lion growling over his prey,"],[2,"if a multitude of shepherds is called together against him,"],[2,"will not be dismayed at their voice,"],[2,"nor abase himself for their noise,"],[2,"so the LORD of Armies will come down to fight on Mount Zion and on its heights."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"As birds hovering, so the LORD of Armies will protect Jerusalem."],[2,"He will protect and deliver it."],[2,"He will pass over and preserve it.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Return to him from whom you have deeply revolted, children of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[1,"For in that day everyone shall cast away his idols of silver and his idols of gold\u2014sin which your own hands have made for you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Assyrian will fall by the sword, not of man;"],[2,"and the sword, not of mankind, shall devour him."],[1,"He will flee from the sword,"],[2,"and his young men will become subject to forced labor."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"His rock will pass away by reason of terror,"],[2,"and his princes will be afraid of the banner,\u201d"],[1,"says the LORD, whose fire is in Zion,"],[2,"and his furnace in Jerusalem."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, a king shall reign in righteousness,"],[2,"and princes shall rule in justice."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"A man shall be as a hiding place from the wind,"],[2,"and a covert from the storm,"],[2,"as streams of water in a dry place,"],[2,"as the shade of a large rock in a weary land."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The eyes of those who see will not be dim,"],[2,"and the ears of those who hear will listen."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart of the rash will understand knowledge,"],[2,"and the tongue of the stammerers will be ready to speak plainly."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The fool will no longer be called noble,"],[2,"nor the scoundrel be highly respected."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For the fool will speak folly,"],[2,"and his heart will work iniquity,"],[2,"to practice profanity,"],[2,"and to utter error against the LORD,"],[2,"to make empty the soul of the hungry,"],[2,"and to cause the drink of the thirsty to fail."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The ways of the scoundrel are evil."],[2,"He devises wicked plans to destroy the humble with lying words,"],[2,"even when the needy speaks right."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But the noble devises noble things,"],[2,"and he will continue in noble things."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Rise up, you women who are at ease! Hear my voice!"],[2,"You careless daughters, give ear to my speech!"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For days beyond a year you will be troubled, you careless women;"],[2,"for the vintage will fail."],[2,"The harvest won\u2019t come."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Tremble, you women who are at ease!"],[2,"Be troubled, you careless ones!"],[2,"Strip yourselves, make yourselves naked,"],[2,"and put sackcloth on your waist."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Beat your breasts for the pleasant fields,"],[2,"for the fruitful vine."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Thorns and briers will come up on my people\u2019s land;"],[2,"yes, on all the houses of joy in the joyous city."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For the palace will be forsaken."],[2,"The populous city will be deserted."],[2,"The hill and the watchtower will be for dens forever,"],[2,"a delight for wild donkeys,"],[2,"a pasture of flocks,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"until the Spirit is poured on us from on high,"],[2,"and the wilderness becomes a fruitful field,"],[2,"and the fruitful field is considered a forest."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Then justice will dwell in the wilderness;"],[2,"and righteousness will remain in the fruitful field."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The work of righteousness will be peace,"],[2,"and the effect of righteousness, quietness and confidence forever."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"My people will live in a peaceful habitation,"],[2,"in safe dwellings,"],[2,"and in quiet resting places,"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"though hail flattens the forest,"],[2,"and the city is leveled completely."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are you who sow beside all waters,"],[2,"who send out the feet of the ox and the donkey."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to you who destroy, but you weren\u2019t destroyed,"],[2,"and who betray, but nobody betrayed you!"],[1,"When you have finished destroying, you will be destroyed;"],[2,"and when you have finished betrayal, you will be betrayed."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, be gracious to us. We have waited for you."],[2,"Be our strength every morning,"],[2,"our salvation also in the time of trouble."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"At the noise of the thunder, the peoples have fled."],[2,"When you lift yourself up, the nations are scattered."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Your plunder will be gathered as the caterpillar gathers."],[2,"Men will leap on it as locusts leap."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is exalted, for he dwells on high."],[2,"He has filled Zion with justice and righteousness."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"There will be stability in your times, abundance of salvation, wisdom, and knowledge."],[2,"The fear of the LORD is your treasure."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, their valiant ones cry outside;"],[2,"the ambassadors of peace weep bitterly."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The highways are desolate."],[2,"The traveling man ceases."],[2,"The covenant is broken."],[2,"He has despised the cities."],[2,"He doesn\u2019t respect man."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The land mourns and languishes."],[2,"Lebanon is confounded and withers away."],[2,"Sharon is like a desert, and Bashan and Carmel are stripped bare."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow I will arise,\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cNow I will lift myself up."],[2,"Now I will be exalted."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"You will conceive chaff."],[2,"You will give birth to stubble."],[2,"Your breath is a fire that will devour you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The peoples will be like the burning of lime,"],[2,"like thorns that are cut down and burned in the fire."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, you who are far off, what I have done;"],[2,"and, you who are near, acknowledge my might.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The sinners in Zion are afraid."],[2,"Trembling has seized the godless ones."],[1,"Who among us can live with the devouring fire?"],[2,"Who among us can live with everlasting burning?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He who walks righteously"],[2,"and speaks blamelessly,"],[2,"he who despises the gain of oppressions,"],[2,"who gestures with his hands, refusing to take a bribe,"],[2,"who stops his ears from hearing of bloodshed,"],[2,"and shuts his eyes from looking at evil\u2014"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"he will dwell on high."],[2,"His place of defense will be the fortress of rocks."],[2,"His bread will be supplied."],[2,"His waters will be sure."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Your eyes will see the king in his beauty."],[2,"They will see a distant land."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Your heart will meditate on the terror."],[2,"Where is he who counted?"],[2,"Where is he who weighed?"],[2,"Where is he who counted the towers?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"You will no longer see the fierce people,"],[2,"a people of a deep speech that you can\u2019t comprehend,"],[2,"with a strange language that you can\u2019t understand."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Look at Zion, the city of our appointed festivals."],[2,"Your eyes will see Jerusalem, a quiet habitation,"],[2,"a tent that won\u2019t be removed."],[1,"Its stakes will never be plucked up,"],[2,"nor will any of its cords be broken."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"But there the LORD will be with us in majesty,"],[2,"a place of wide rivers and streams,"],[2,"in which no galley with oars will go,"],[2,"neither will any gallant ship pass by there."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD is our judge."],[2,"The LORD is our lawgiver."],[2,"The LORD is our king."],[2,"He will save us."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Your rigging is untied."],[2,"They couldn\u2019t strengthen the foot of their mast."],[2,"They couldn\u2019t spread the sail."],[1,"Then the prey of a great plunder was divided."],[2,"The lame took the prey."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The inhabitant won\u2019t say, \u201cI am sick.\u201d"],[2,"The people who dwell therein will be forgiven their iniquity."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Come near, you nations, to hear!"],[2,"Listen, you peoples."],[2,"Let the earth and all it contains hear,"],[2,"the world, and everything that comes from it."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD is enraged against all the nations,"],[2,"and angry with all their armies."],[1,"He has utterly destroyed them."],[2,"He has given them over for slaughter."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Their slain will also be cast out,"],[2,"and the stench of their dead bodies will come up."],[2,"The mountains will melt in their blood."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"All of the army of the sky will be dissolved."],[2,"The sky will be rolled up like a scroll,"],[2,"and all its armies will fade away,"],[2,"as a leaf fades from off a vine or a fig tree."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For my sword has drunk its fill in the sky."],[2,"Behold, it will come down on Edom,"],[2,"and on the people of my curse, for judgment."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s sword is filled with blood."],[2,"It is covered with fat, with the blood of lambs and goats,"],[2,"with the fat of the kidneys of rams;"],[2,"for the LORD has a sacrifice in Bozrah,"],[2,"and a great slaughter in the land of Edom."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The wild oxen will come down with them,"],[2,"and the young bulls with the mighty bulls;"],[2,"and their land will be drunken with blood,"],[2,"and their dust made greasy with fat."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD has a day of vengeance,"],[2,"a year of recompense for the cause of Zion."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Its streams will be turned into pitch,"],[2,"its dust into sulfur,"],[2,"and its land will become burning pitch."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"It won\u2019t be quenched night or day."],[2,"Its smoke will go up forever."],[2,"From generation to generation, it will lie waste."],[2,"No one will pass through it forever and ever."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"But the pelican and the porcupine will possess it."],[2,"The owl and the raven will dwell in it."],[1,"He will stretch the line of confusion over it,"],[2,"and the plumb line of emptiness."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall call its nobles to the kingdom, but none shall be there;"],[2,"and all its princes shall be nothing."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Thorns will come up in its palaces,"],[2,"nettles and thistles in its fortresses;"],[2,"and it will be a habitation of jackals,"],[2,"a court for ostriches."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The wild animals of the desert will meet with the wolves,"],[2,"and the wild goat will cry to his fellow."],[1,"Yes, the night creature shall settle there,"],[2,"and shall find herself a place of rest."]],f:["literally, lilith, which could also be a night demon or night monster"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The arrow snake will make her nest there,"],[2,"and lay, hatch, and gather under her shade."],[2,"Yes, the kites will be gathered there, every one with her mate."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Search in the book of the LORD, and read:"],[2,"not one of these will be missing."],[2,"None will lack her mate."],[2,"For my mouth has commanded,"],[2,"and his Spirit has gathered them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He has cast the lot for them,"],[2,"and his hand has divided it to them with a measuring line."],[2,"They shall possess it forever."],[2,"From generation to generation they will dwell in it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The wilderness and the dry land will be glad."],[2,"The desert will rejoice and blossom like a rose."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"It will blossom abundantly,"],[2,"and rejoice even with joy and singing."],[2,"Lebanon\u2019s glory will be given to it,"],[2,"the excellence of Carmel and Sharon."],[2,"They will see the LORD\u2019s glory,"],[2,"the excellence of our God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Strengthen the weak hands,"],[2,"and make the feeble knees firm."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Tell those who have a fearful heart, \u201cBe strong!"],[2,"Don\u2019t be afraid!"],[1,"Behold, your God will come with vengeance, God\u2019s retribution."],[2,"He will come and save you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the eyes of the blind will be opened,"],[2,"and the ears of the deaf will be unstopped."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the lame man will leap like a deer,"],[2,"and the tongue of the mute will sing;"],[2,"for waters will break out in the wilderness,"],[2,"and streams in the desert."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The burning sand will become a pool,"],[2,"and the thirsty ground springs of water."],[2,"Grass with reeds and rushes will be in the habitation of jackals, where they lay."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"A highway will be there, a road,"],[2,"and it will be called \u201cThe Holy Way\u201d."],[1,"The unclean shall not pass over it,"],[2,"but it will be for those who walk in the Way."],[2,"Wicked fools shall not go there."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"No lion will be there,"],[2,"nor will any ravenous animal go up on it."],[2,"They will not be found there;"],[2,"but the redeemed will walk there."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the LORD\u2019s ransomed ones will return,"],[2,"and come with singing to Zion;"],[2,"and everlasting joy will be on their heads."],[1,"They will obtain gladness and joy,"],[2,"and sorrow and sighing will flee away.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the fourteenth year of King Hezekiah, Sennacherib king of Assyria attacked all of the fortified cities of Judah and captured them."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The king of Assyria sent Rabshakeh from Lachish to Jerusalem to King Hezekiah with a large army. He stood by the aqueduct from the upper pool in the fuller\u2019s field highway."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, the son of Asaph the recorder came out to him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Rabshakeh said to them, \u201cNow tell Hezekiah, \u2018The great king, the king of Assyria, says, \u201cWhat confidence is this in which you trust?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I say that your counsel and strength for the war are only vain words. Now in whom do you trust, that you have rebelled against me?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Behold, you trust in the staff of this bruised reed, even in Egypt, which if a man leans on it, it will go into his hand and pierce it. So is Pharaoh king of Egypt to all who trust in him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But if you tell me, \u2018We trust in the LORD our God,\u2019 isn\u2019t that he whose high places and whose altars Hezekiah has taken away, and has said to Judah and to Jerusalem, \u2018You shall worship before this altar\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now therefore, please make a pledge to my master the king of Assyria, and I will give you two thousand horses, if you are able on your part to set riders on them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"How then can you turn away the face of one captain of the least of my master\u2019s servants, and put your trust in Egypt for chariots and for horsemen?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Have I come up now without the LORD against this land to destroy it? The LORD said to me, \u201cGo up against this land, and destroy it.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eliakim, Shebna and Joah said to Rabshakeh, \u201cPlease speak to your servants in Aramaic, for we understand it. Don\u2019t speak to us in the Jews\u2019 language in the hearing of the people who are on the wall.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"But Rabshakeh said, \u201cHas my master sent me only to your master and to you, to speak these words, and not to the men who sit on the wall, who will eat their own dung and drink their own urine with you?\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then Rabshakeh stood, and called out with a loud voice in the Jews\u2019 language, and said, \u201cHear the words of the great king, the king of Assyria!"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The king says, \u2018Don\u2019t let Hezekiah deceive you; for he will not be able to deliver you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t let Hezekiah make you trust in the LORD, saying, \u201cThe LORD will surely deliver us. This city won\u2019t be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t listen to Hezekiah, for the king of Assyria says, \u2018Make your peace with me, and come out to me; and each of you eat from his vine, and each one from his fig tree, and each one of you drink the waters of his own cistern;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"until I come and take you away to a land like your own land, a land of grain and new wine, a land of bread and vineyards."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Beware lest Hezekiah persuade you, saying, \u201cThe LORD will deliver us.\u201d Have any of the gods of the nations delivered their lands from the hand of the king of Assyria?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Where are the gods of Hamath and Arpad? Where are the gods of Sepharvaim? Have they delivered Samaria from my hand?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Who are they among all the gods of these countries that have delivered their country out of my hand, that the LORD should deliver Jerusalem out of my hand?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"But they remained silent, and said nothing in reply, for the king\u2019s commandment was, \u201cDon\u2019t answer him.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Eliakim the son of Hilkiah, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and Joah, the son of Asaph the recorder, came to Hezekiah with their clothes torn, and told him the words of Rabshakeh."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When King Hezekiah heard it, he tore his clothes, covered himself with sackcloth, and went into the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He sent Eliakim, who was over the household, and Shebna the scribe, and the elders of the priests, covered with sackcloth, to Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cHezekiah says, \u2018Today is a day of trouble, and of rebuke, and of rejection; for the children have come to the birth, and there is no strength to give birth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"It may be the LORD your God will hear the words of Rabshakeh, whom the king of Assyria his master has sent to defy the living God, and will rebuke the words which the LORD your God has heard. Therefore lift up your prayer for the remnant that is left.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"So the servants of King Hezekiah came to Isaiah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah said to them, \u201cTell your master, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid of the words that you have heard, with which the servants of the king of Assyria have blasphemed me."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Behold, I will put a spirit in him and he will hear news, and will return to his own land. I will cause him to fall by the sword in his own land.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"So Rabshakeh returned, and found the king of Assyria warring against Libnah, for he heard that he had departed from Lachish."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He heard news concerning Tirhakah king of Ethiopia, \u201cHe has come out to fight against you.\u201d When he heard it, he sent messengers to Hezekiah, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cThus you shall speak to Hezekiah king of Judah, saying, \u2018Don\u2019t let your God in whom you trust deceive you, saying, \u201cJerusalem won\u2019t be given into the hand of the king of Assyria.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Behold, you have heard what the kings of Assyria have done to all lands, by destroying them utterly. Shall you be delivered?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Have the gods of the nations delivered them, which my fathers have destroyed, Gozan, Haran, Rezeph, and the children of Eden who were in Telassar?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Where is the king of Hamath, and the king of Arpad, and the king of the city of Sepharvaim, of Hena, and Ivvah?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Hezekiah received the letter from the hand of the messengers and read it. Then Hezekiah went up to the LORD\u2019s house, and spread it before the LORD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Hezekiah prayed to the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cLORD of Armies, the God of Israel, who is enthroned among the cherubim, you are the God, even you alone, of all the kingdoms of the earth. You have made heaven and earth."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Turn your ear, LORD, and hear. Open your eyes, LORD, and behold. Hear all of the words of Sennacherib, who has sent to defy the living God."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Truly, LORD, the kings of Assyria have destroyed all the countries and their land,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and have cast their gods into the fire; for they were no gods, but the work of men\u2019s hands, wood and stone; therefore they have destroyed them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now therefore, LORD our God, save us from his hand, that all the kingdoms of the earth may know that you are the LORD, even you only.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Isaiah the son of Amoz sent to Hezekiah, saying, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel says, \u2018Because you have prayed to me against Sennacherib king of Assyria,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"this is the word which the LORD has spoken concerning him: The virgin daughter of Zion has despised you and ridiculed you. The daughter of Jerusalem has shaken her head at you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Whom have you defied and blasphemed? Against whom have you exalted your voice and lifted up your eyes on high? Against the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"By your servants, you have defied the Lord, and have said, \u201cWith the multitude of my chariots I have come up to the height of the mountains, to the innermost parts of Lebanon. I will cut down its tall cedars and its choice cypress trees. I will enter into its farthest height, the forest of its fruitful field."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I have dug and drunk water, and with the sole of my feet I will dry up all the rivers of Egypt.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Have you not heard how I have done it long ago, and formed it in ancient times? Now I have brought it to pass, that it should be yours to destroy fortified cities, turning them into ruinous heaps."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Therefore their inhabitants had little power. They were dismayed and confounded. They were like the grass of the field, and like the green herb, like the grass on the housetops, and like a field before its crop has grown."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But I know your sitting down, your going out, your coming in, and your raging against me."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Because of your raging against me, and because your arrogance has come up into my ears, therefore I will put my hook in your nose and my bridle in your lips, and I will turn you back by the way by which you came."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This shall be the sign to you: You will eat this year that which grows of itself, and in the second year that which springs from it; and in the third year sow and reap and plant vineyards, and eat their fruit."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The remnant that is escaped of the house of Judah will again take root downward, and bear fruit upward."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For out of Jerusalem a remnant will go out, and survivors will escape from Mount Zion. The zeal of the LORD of Armies will perform this.\u2019"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the LORD says concerning the king of Assyria, \u2018He will not come to this city, nor shoot an arrow there, neither will he come before it with shield, nor cast up a mound against it."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He will return the way that he came, and he won\u2019t come to this city,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"\u2018For I will defend this city to save it, for my own sake, and for my servant David\u2019s sake.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s angel went out and struck one hundred and eighty-five thousand men in the camp of the Assyrians. When men arose early in the morning, behold, these were all dead bodies."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"So Sennacherib king of Assyria departed, went away, returned to Nineveh, and stayed there."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"As he was worshiping in the house of Nisroch his god, Adrammelech and Sharezer his sons struck him with the sword; and they escaped into the land of Ararat. Esar Haddon his son reigned in his place."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days Hezekiah was sick and near death. Isaiah the prophet, the son of Amoz, came to him, and said to him, \u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Set your house in order, for you will die, and not live.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["LORD or GOD in all caps is from the Hebrew \u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4 Yahweh except when otherwise noted as being from the short form \u05d9\u05d4 Yah."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hezekiah turned his face to the wall and prayed to the LORD,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cRemember now, LORD, I beg you, how I have walked before you in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is good in your sight.\u201d Then Hezekiah wept bitterly."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Isaiah, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cGo, and tell Hezekiah, \u2018The LORD, the God of David your father, says, \u201cI have heard your prayer. I have seen your tears. Behold, I will add fifteen years to your life."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I will deliver you and this city out of the hand of the king of Assyria, and I will defend this city."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"This shall be the sign to you from the LORD, that the LORD will do this thing that he has spoken."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, I will cause the shadow on the sundial, which has gone down on the sundial of Ahaz with the sun, to return backward ten steps.\u201d\u2019\u201d So the sun returned ten steps on the sundial on which it had gone down."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The writing of Hezekiah king of Judah, when he had been sick, and had recovered of his sickness:"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cIn the middle of my life I go into the gates of Sheol."],[2,"I am deprived of the residue of my years.\u201d"]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cI won\u2019t see the LORD,"],[2,"the LORD in the land of the living."],[2,"I will see man no more with the inhabitants of the world."]],f:["Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah","Hebrew: \u05d9\u05d4 Yah"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"My dwelling is removed,"],[2,"and is carried away from me like a shepherd\u2019s tent."],[1,"I have rolled up my life like a weaver."],[2,"He will cut me off from the loom."],[2,"From day even to night you will make an end of me."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I waited patiently until morning."],[2,"He breaks all my bones like a lion."],[2,"From day even to night you will make an end of me."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I chattered like a swallow or a crane."],[2,"I moaned like a dove."],[2,"My eyes weaken looking upward."],[2,"Lord, I am oppressed."],[2,"Be my security.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"What will I say?"],[2,"He has both spoken to me, and himself has done it."],[2,"I will walk carefully all my years because of the anguish of my soul."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, men live by these things;"],[2,"and my spirit finds life in all of them."],[2,"You restore me, and cause me to live."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, for peace I had great anguish,"],[2,"but you have in love for my soul delivered it from the pit of corruption;"],[2,"for you have cast all my sins behind your back."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For Sheol can\u2019t praise you."],[2,"Death can\u2019t celebrate you."],[1,"Those who go down into the pit can\u2019t hope for your truth."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The living, the living, he shall praise you, as I do today."],[2,"The father shall make known your truth to the children."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will save me."],[2,"Therefore we will sing my songs with stringed instruments all the days of our life in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Isaiah had said, \u201cLet them take a cake of figs, and lay it for a poultice on the boil, and he shall recover.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Hezekiah also had said, \u201cWhat is the sign that I will go up to the LORD\u2019s house?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time, Merodach-baladan the son of Baladan, king of Babylon, sent letters and a present to Hezekiah, for he heard that he had been sick, and had recovered."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Hezekiah was pleased with them, and showed them the house of his precious things, the silver, the gold, the spices, and the precious oil, and all the house of his armor, and all that was found in his treasures. There was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominion, that Hezekiah didn\u2019t show them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then Isaiah the prophet came to King Hezekiah, and asked him, \u201cWhat did these men say? From where did they come to you?\u201d"],[0,"Hezekiah said, \u201cThey have come from a country far from me, even from Babylon.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he asked, \u201cWhat have they seen in your house?\u201d"],[0,"Hezekiah answered, \u201cThey have seen all that is in my house. There is nothing among my treasures that I have not shown them.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Isaiah said to Hezekiah, \u201cHear the word of the LORD of Armies:"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u2018Behold, the days are coming when all that is in your house, and that which your fathers have stored up until today, will be carried to Babylon. Nothing will be left,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u2018They will take away your sons who will issue from you, whom you shall father, and they will be eunuchs in the king of Babylon\u2019s palace.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hezekiah said to Isaiah, \u201cThe LORD\u2019s word which you have spoken is good.\u201d He said moreover, \u201cFor there will be peace and truth in my days.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cComfort, comfort my people,\u201d says your God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak comfortably to Jerusalem, and call out to her that her warfare is accomplished, that her iniquity is pardoned, that she has received of the LORD\u2019s hand double for all her sins.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The voice of one who calls out,"],[2,"\u201cPrepare the way of the LORD in the wilderness!"],[2,"Make a level highway in the desert for our God."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Every valley shall be exalted,"],[2,"and every mountain and hill shall be made low."],[2,"The uneven shall be made level,"],[2,"and the rough places a plain."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s glory shall be revealed,"],[2,"and all flesh shall see it together;"],[2,"for the mouth of the LORD has spoken it.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The voice of one saying, \u201cCry out!\u201d"],[2,"One said, \u201cWhat shall I cry?\u201d"],[1,"\u201cAll flesh is like grass,"],[2,"and all its glory is like the flower of the field."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The grass withers,"],[2,"the flower fades,"],[2,"because the LORD\u2019s breath blows on it."],[2,"Surely the people are like grass."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The grass withers,"],[2,"the flower fades;"],[2,"but the word of our God stands forever.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You who tell good news to Zion, go up on a high mountain."],[2,"You who tell good news to Jerusalem, lift up your voice with strength!"],[2,"Lift it up! Don\u2019t be afraid!"],[2,"Say to the cities of Judah, \u201cBehold, your God!\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the Lord GOD will come as a mighty one,"],[2,"and his arm will rule for him."],[2,"Behold, his reward is with him,"],[2,"and his recompense before him."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He will feed his flock like a shepherd."],[2,"He will gather the lambs in his arm,"],[2,"and carry them in his bosom."],[2,"He will gently lead those who have their young."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has measured the waters in the hollow of his hand,"],[2,"and marked off the sky with his span,"],[2,"and calculated the dust of the earth in a measuring basket,"],[2,"and weighed the mountains in scales,"],[2,"and the hills in a balance?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has directed the LORD\u2019s Spirit,"],[2,"or has taught him as his counselor?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Who did he take counsel with,"],[2,"and who instructed him,"],[2,"and taught him in the path of justice,"],[2,"and taught him knowledge,"],[2,"and showed him the way of understanding?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the nations are like a drop in a bucket,"],[2,"and are regarded as a speck of dust on a balance."],[2,"Behold, he lifts up the islands like a very little thing."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Lebanon is not sufficient to burn,"],[2,"nor its animals sufficient for a burnt offering."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"All the nations are like nothing before him."],[2,"They are regarded by him as less than nothing, and vanity."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"To whom then will you liken God?"],[2,"Or what likeness will you compare to him?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"A workman has cast an image,"],[2,"and the goldsmith overlays it with gold,"],[2,"and casts silver chains for it."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is too impoverished for such an offering chooses a tree that will not rot."],[2,"He seeks a skillful workman to set up a carved image for him that will not be moved."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Haven\u2019t you known?"],[2,"Haven\u2019t you heard?"],[2,"Haven\u2019t you been told from the beginning?"],[2,"Haven\u2019t you understood from the foundations of the earth?"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"It is he who sits above the circle of the earth,"],[2,"and its inhabitants are like grasshoppers;"],[2,"who stretches out the heavens like a curtain,"],[2,"and spreads them out like a tent to dwell in,"]]},{v:23,l:[[2,"who brings princes to nothing,"],[2,"who makes the judges of the earth meaningless."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"They are planted scarcely."],[2,"They are sown scarcely."],[2,"Their stock has scarcely taken root in the ground."],[2,"He merely blows on them, and they wither,"],[2,"and the whirlwind takes them away as stubble."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTo whom then will you liken me?"],[2,"Who is my equal?\u201d says the Holy One."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your eyes on high,"],[2,"and see who has created these,"],[2,"who brings out their army by number."],[2,"He calls them all by name."],[2,"By the greatness of his might,"],[2,"and because he is strong in power,"],[2,"not one is lacking."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you say, Jacob,"],[2,"and speak, Israel,"],[2,"\u201cMy way is hidden from the LORD,"],[2,"and the justice due me is disregarded by my God\u201d?"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Haven\u2019t you known?"],[2,"Haven\u2019t you heard?"],[2,"The everlasting God, the LORD,"],[2,"the Creator of the ends of the earth, doesn\u2019t faint."],[2,"He isn\u2019t weary."],[2,"His understanding is unsearchable."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"He gives power to the weak."],[2,"He increases the strength of him who has no might."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Even the youths faint and get weary,"],[2,"and the young men utterly fall;"]]},{v:31,l:[[2,"but those who wait for the LORD will renew their strength."],[2,"They will mount up with wings like eagles."],[2,"They will run, and not be weary."],[2,"They will walk, and not faint."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cKeep silent before me, islands,"],[2,"and let the peoples renew their strength."],[1,"Let them come near,"],[2,"then let them speak."],[2,"Let\u2019s meet together for judgment."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has raised up one from the east?"],[2,"Who called him to his feet in righteousness?"],[2,"He hands over nations to him"],[2,"and makes him rule over kings."],[2,"He gives them like the dust to his sword,"],[2,"like the driven stubble to his bow."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He pursues them"],[2,"and passes by safely,"],[2,"even by a way that he had not gone with his feet."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has worked and done it,"],[2,"calling the generations from the beginning?"],[2,"I, the LORD, the first, and with the last, I am he.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The islands have seen, and fear."],[2,"The ends of the earth tremble."],[2,"They approach, and come."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Everyone helps his neighbor."],[2,"They say to their brothers, \u201cBe strong!\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"So the carpenter encourages the goldsmith."],[2,"He who smooths with the hammer encourages him who strikes the anvil,"],[2,"saying of the soldering, \u201cIt is good;\u201d"],[2,"and he fastens it with nails, that it might not totter."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut you, Israel, my servant,"],[2,"Jacob whom I have chosen,"],[2,"the offspring of Abraham my friend,"]]},{v:9,l:[[2,"you whom I have taken hold of from the ends of the earth,"],[2,"and called from its corners,"],[2,"and said to you, \u2018You are my servant. I have chosen you and have not cast you away.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t you be afraid, for I am with you."],[2,"Don\u2019t be dismayed, for I am your God."],[2,"I will strengthen you."],[2,"Yes, I will help you."],[2,"Yes, I will uphold you with the right hand of my righteousness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, all those who are incensed against you will be disappointed and confounded."],[2,"Those who strive with you will be like nothing, and shall perish."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You will seek them, and won\u2019t find them,"],[2,"even those who contend with you."],[2,"Those who war against you will be as nothing,"],[2,"as a nonexistent thing."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For I, the LORD your God, will hold your right hand,"],[2,"saying to you, \u2018Don\u2019t be afraid."],[2,"I will help you.\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be afraid, you worm Jacob,"],[2,"and you men of Israel."],[2,"I will help you,\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cYour Redeemer is the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I have made you into a new sharp threshing instrument with teeth."],[2,"You will thresh the mountains,"],[2,"and beat them small,"],[2,"and will make the hills like chaff."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"You will winnow them,"],[2,"and the wind will carry them away,"],[2,"and the whirlwind will scatter them."],[1,"You will rejoice in the LORD."],[2,"You will glory in the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The poor and needy seek water, and there is none."],[2,"Their tongue fails for thirst."],[1,"I, the LORD, will answer them."],[2,"I, the God of Israel, will not forsake them."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I will open rivers on the bare heights,"],[2,"and springs in the middle of the valleys."],[2,"I will make the wilderness a pool of water,"],[2,"and the dry land springs of water."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I will put cedar, acacia, myrtle, and oil trees in the wilderness."],[2,"I will set cypress trees, pine, and box trees together in the desert;"]]},{v:20,l:[[2,"that they may see, know, consider, and understand together,"],[2,"that the LORD\u2019s hand has done this,"],[2,"and the Holy One of Israel has created it."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Produce your cause,\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cBring out your strong reasons!\u201d says the King of Jacob."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLet them announce and declare to us what will happen!"],[2,"Declare the former things, what they are,"],[2,"that we may consider them, and know the latter end of them;"],[2,"or show us things to come."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Declare the things that are to come hereafter,"],[2,"that we may know that you are gods."],[1,"Yes, do good, or do evil,"],[2,"that we may be dismayed,"],[2,"and see it together."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you are nothing,"],[2,"and your work is nothing."],[2,"He who chooses you is an abomination."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have raised up one from the north, and he has come,"],[2,"from the rising of the sun, one who calls on my name,"],[2,"and he shall come on rulers as on mortar,"],[2,"and as the potter treads clay."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has declared it from the beginning, that we may know?"],[2,"and before, that we may say, \u2018He is right\u2019?"],[1,"Surely, there is no one who declares."],[2,"Surely, there is no one who shows."],[2,"Surely, there is no one who hears your words."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"I am the first to say to Zion, \u2018Behold, look at them;\u2019"],[2,"and I will give one who brings good news to Jerusalem."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"When I look, there is no man,"],[2,"even among them there is no counselor who, when I ask, can answer a word."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, all of their deeds are vanity and nothing."],[2,"Their molten images are wind and confusion."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, my servant, whom I uphold,"],[2,"my chosen, in whom my soul delights:"],[2,"I have put my Spirit on him."],[2,"He will bring justice to the nations."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not shout,"],[2,"nor raise his voice,"],[2,"nor cause it to be heard in the street."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He won\u2019t break a bruised reed."],[2,"He won\u2019t quench a dimly burning wick."],[2,"He will faithfully bring justice."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not fail nor be discouraged,"],[2,"until he has set justice on the earth,"],[2,"and the islands wait for his law.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"God the LORD,"],[2,"he who created the heavens and stretched them out,"],[2,"he who spread out the earth and that which comes out of it,"],[2,"he who gives breath to its people and spirit to those who walk in it, says:"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI, the LORD, have called you in righteousness."],[2,"I will hold your hand."],[2,"I will keep you,"],[2,"and make you a covenant for the people,"],[2,"as a light for the nations,"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"to open the blind eyes,"],[2,"to bring the prisoners out of the dungeon,"],[2,"and those who sit in darkness out of the prison."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI am the LORD."],[2,"That is my name."],[2,"I will not give my glory to another,"],[2,"nor my praise to engraved images."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the former things have happened"],[2,"and I declare new things."],[2,"I tell you about them before they come up.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to the LORD a new song,"],[2,"and his praise from the end of the earth,"],[2,"you who go down to the sea,"],[2,"and all that is therein,"],[2,"the islands and their inhabitants."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the wilderness and its cities raise their voices,"],[2,"with the villages that Kedar inhabits."],[2,"Let the inhabitants of Sela sing."],[2,"Let them shout from the top of the mountains!"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them give glory to the LORD,"],[2,"and declare his praise in the islands."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will go out like a mighty man."],[2,"He will stir up zeal like a man of war."],[2,"He will raise a war cry."],[2,"Yes, he will shout aloud."],[2,"He will triumph over his enemies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have been silent a long time."],[2,"I have been quiet and restrained myself."],[2,"Now I will cry out like a travailing woman. I will both gasp and pant."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will destroy mountains and hills,"],[2,"and dry up all their herbs."],[2,"I will make the rivers islands,"],[2,"and will dry up the pools."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring the blind by a way that they don\u2019t know."],[2,"I will lead them in paths that they don\u2019t know."],[2,"I will make darkness light before them,"],[2,"and crooked places straight."],[2,"I will do these things,"],[2,"and I will not forsake them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThose who trust in engraved images,"],[2,"who tell molten images,"],[2,"\u2018You are our gods,\u2019"],[2,"will be turned back."],[2,"They will be utterly disappointed."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear, you deaf,"],[2,"and look, you blind,"],[2,"that you may see."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is blind, but my servant?"],[2,"Or who is as deaf as my messenger whom I send?"],[1,"Who is as blind as he who is at peace,"],[2,"and as blind as the LORD\u2019s servant?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"You see many things, but don\u2019t observe."],[2,"His ears are open, but he doesn\u2019t listen."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"It pleased the LORD, for his righteousness\u2019 sake, to magnify the law"],[2,"and make it honorable."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"But this is a robbed and plundered people."],[2,"All of them are snared in holes,"],[2,"and they are hidden in prisons."],[1,"They have become captives, and no one delivers,"],[2,"and a plunder, and no one says, \u2018Restore them!\u2019"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is there among you who will give ear to this?"],[2,"Who will listen and hear for the time to come?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Who gave Jacob as plunder,"],[2,"and Israel to the robbers?"],[2,"Didn\u2019t the LORD, he against whom we have sinned?"],[2,"For they would not walk in his ways,"],[2,"and they disobeyed his law."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore he poured the fierceness of his anger on him,"],[2,"and the strength of battle."],[1,"It set him on fire all around, but he didn\u2019t know."],[2,"It burned him, but he didn\u2019t take it to heart.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"But now the LORD who created you, Jacob,"],[2,"and he who formed you, Israel, says:"],[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for I have redeemed you."],[2,"I have called you by your name."],[2,"You are mine."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"When you pass through the waters, I will be with you,"],[2,"and through the rivers, they will not overflow you."],[1,"When you walk through the fire, you will not be burned,"],[2,"and flame will not scorch you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For I am the LORD your God,"],[2,"the Holy One of Israel,"],[2,"your Savior."],[1,"I have given Egypt as your ransom,"],[2,"Ethiopia and Seba in your place."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Since you have been precious and honored in my sight,"],[2,"and I have loved you,"],[2,"therefore I will give people in your place,"],[2,"and nations instead of your life."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be afraid, for I am with you."],[2,"I will bring your offspring from the east,"],[2,"and gather you from the west."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I will tell the north, \u2018Give them up!\u2019"],[2,"and tell the south, \u2018Don\u2019t hold them back!"],[2,"Bring my sons from far away,"],[2,"and my daughters from the ends of the earth\u2014"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"everyone who is called by my name,"],[2,"and whom I have created for my glory,"],[2,"whom I have formed,"],[2,"yes, whom I have made.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Bring out the blind people who have eyes,"],[2,"and the deaf who have ears."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Let all the nations be gathered together,"],[2,"and let the peoples be assembled."],[1,"Who among them can declare this,"],[2,"and show us former things?"],[1,"Let them bring their witnesses, that they may be justified,"],[2,"or let them hear, and say, \u201cThat is true.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou are my witnesses,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cWith my servant whom I have chosen;"],[2,"that you may know and believe me,"],[2,"and understand that I am he."],[1,"Before me there was no God formed,"],[2,"neither will there be after me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I myself am the LORD."],[2,"Besides me, there is no savior."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I have declared, I have saved, and I have shown,"],[2,"and there was no strange god among you."],[1,"Therefore you are my witnesses\u201d,"],[2,"says the LORD, \u201cand I am God."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, since the day was, I am he."],[2,"There is no one who can deliver out of my hand."],[2,"I will work, and who can hinder it?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD, your Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel says: \u201cFor your sake, I have sent to Babylon, and I will bring all of them down as fugitives, even the Chaldeans, in the ships of their rejoicing."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I am the LORD, your Holy One, the Creator of Israel, your King.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD, who makes a way in the sea,"],[2,"and a path in the mighty waters,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"who brings out the chariot and horse,"],[2,"the army and the mighty man"],[2,"(they lie down together, they shall not rise;"],[2,"they are extinct, they are quenched like a wick) says:"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t remember the former things,"],[2,"and don\u2019t consider the things of old."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I will do a new thing."],[2,"It springs out now."],[2,"Don\u2019t you know it?"],[1,"I will even make a way in the wilderness,"],[2,"and rivers in the desert."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The animals of the field, the jackals and the ostriches, shall honor me,"],[2,"because I give water in the wilderness and rivers in the desert,"],[2,"to give drink to my people, my chosen,"]]},{v:21,l:[[2,"the people which I formed for myself,"],[2,"that they might declare my praise."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet you have not called on me, Jacob;"],[2,"but you have been weary of me, Israel."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"You have not brought me any of your sheep for burnt offerings,"],[2,"neither have you honored me with your sacrifices."],[1,"I have not burdened you with offerings,"],[2,"nor wearied you with frankincense."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"You have bought me no sweet cane with money,"],[2,"nor have you filled me with the fat of your sacrifices,"],[1,"but you have burdened me with your sins."],[2,"You have wearied me with your iniquities."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"I, even I, am he who blots out your transgressions for my own sake;"],[2,"and I will not remember your sins."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Put me in remembrance."],[2,"Let us plead together."],[1,"Declare your case,"],[2,"that you may be justified."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Your first father sinned,"],[2,"and your teachers have transgressed against me."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will profane the princes of the sanctuary;"],[2,"and I will make Jacob a curse,"],[2,"and Israel an insult.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet listen now, Jacob my servant,"],[2,"and Israel, whom I have chosen."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"This is what the LORD who made you,"],[2,"and formed you from the womb,"],[2,"who will help you says:"],[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, Jacob my servant;"],[2,"and you, Jeshurun, whom I have chosen."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will pour water on him who is thirsty,"],[2,"and streams on the dry ground."],[1,"I will pour my Spirit on your descendants,"],[2,"and my blessing on your offspring;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"and they will spring up among the grass,"],[2,"as willows by the watercourses."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"One will say, \u2018I am the LORD\u2019s.\u2019"],[2,"Another will be called by the name of Jacob;"],[2,"and another will write with his hand \u2018to the LORD,\u2019"],[2,"and honor the name of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"This is what the LORD, the King of Israel,"],[2,"and his Redeemer, the LORD of Armies, says:"],[1,"\u201cI am the first, and I am the last;"],[2,"and besides me there is no God."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is like me?"],[2,"Who will call,"],[2,"and will declare it,"],[2,"and set it in order for me,"],[2,"since I established the ancient people?"],[1,"Let them declare the things that are coming,"],[2,"and that will happen."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t fear,"],[2,"neither be afraid."],[1,"Haven\u2019t I declared it to you long ago,"],[2,"and shown it?"],[1,"You are my witnesses."],[2,"Is there a God besides me?"],[1,"Indeed, there is not."],[2,"I don\u2019t know any other Rock.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Everyone who makes a carved image is vain."],[2,"The things that they delight in will not profit."],[2,"Their own witnesses don\u2019t see, nor know, that they may be disappointed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has fashioned a god,"],[2,"or molds an image that is profitable for nothing?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, all his fellows will be disappointed;"],[2,"and the workmen are mere men."],[1,"Let them all be gathered together."],[2,"Let them stand up."],[2,"They will fear."],[2,"They will be put to shame together."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The blacksmith takes an ax,"],[2,"works in the coals,"],[2,"fashions it with hammers,"],[2,"and works it with his strong arm."],[1,"He is hungry,"],[2,"and his strength fails;"],[1,"he drinks no water,"],[2,"and is faint."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The carpenter stretches out a line."],[2,"He marks it out with a pencil."],[2,"He shapes it with planes."],[2,"He marks it out with compasses,"],[2,"and shapes it like the figure of a man,"],[2,"with the beauty of a man,"],[2,"to reside in a house."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He cuts down cedars for himself,"],[2,"and takes the cypress and the oak,"],[2,"and strengthens for himself one among the trees of the forest."],[1,"He plants a cypress tree,"],[2,"and the rain nourishes it."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Then it will be for a man to burn;"],[2,"and he takes some of it and warms himself."],[2,"Yes, he burns it and bakes bread."],[1,"Yes, he makes a god and worships it;"],[2,"he makes it a carved image, and falls down to it."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He burns part of it in the fire."],[2,"With part of it, he eats meat."],[2,"He roasts a roast and is satisfied."],[1,"Yes, he warms himself"],[2,"and says, \u201cAha! I am warm. I have seen the fire.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The rest of it he makes into a god,"],[2,"even his engraved image."],[1,"He bows down to it and worships,"],[2,"and prays to it, and says, \u201cDeliver me, for you are my god!\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"They don\u2019t know, neither do they consider,"],[2,"for he has shut their eyes, that they can\u2019t see,"],[2,"and their hearts, that they can\u2019t understand."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"No one thinks,"],[2,"neither is there knowledge nor understanding to say,"],[2,"\u201cI have burned part of it in the fire."],[2,"Yes, I have also baked bread on its coals."],[2,"I have roasted meat and eaten it."],[2,"Shall I make the rest of it into an abomination?"],[2,"Shall I bow down to a tree trunk?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He feeds on ashes."],[2,"A deceived heart has turned him aside;"],[2,"and he can\u2019t deliver his soul,"],[2,"nor say, \u201cIsn\u2019t there a lie in my right hand?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember these things, Jacob and Israel,"],[2,"for you are my servant."],[2,"I have formed you."],[2,"You are my servant."],[2,"Israel, you will not be forgotten by me."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"I have blotted out, as a thick cloud, your transgressions,"],[2,"and, as a cloud, your sins."],[2,"Return to me, for I have redeemed you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing, you heavens, for the LORD has done it!"],[2,"Shout, you lower parts of the earth!"],[2,"Break out into singing, you mountains, O forest, all of your trees,"],[2,"for the LORD has redeemed Jacob,"],[2,"and will glorify himself in Israel."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD, your Redeemer,"],[2,"and he who formed you from the womb says:"],[1,"\u201cI am the LORD, who makes all things;"],[2,"who alone stretches out the heavens;"],[2,"who spreads out the earth by myself;"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"who frustrates the signs of the liars,"],[2,"and makes diviners mad;"],[1,"who turns wise men backward,"],[2,"and makes their knowledge foolish;"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"who confirms the word of his servant,"],[2,"and performs the counsel of his messengers;"],[1,"who says of Jerusalem, \u2018She will be inhabited;\u2019"],[2,"and of the cities of Judah, \u2018They will be built,\u2019"],[2,"and \u2018I will raise up its waste places;\u2019"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"who says to the deep, \u2018Be dry,\u2019"],[2,"and \u2018I will dry up your rivers,\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"who says of Cyrus, \u2018He is my shepherd, and shall perform all my pleasure,\u2019"],[2,"even saying of Jerusalem, \u2018She will be built;\u2019"],[2,"and of the temple, \u2018Your foundation will be laid.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says to his anointed, to Cyrus, whose right hand I have held to subdue nations before him and strip kings of their armor, to open the doors before him, and the gates shall not be shut:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will go before you"],[2,"and make the rough places smooth."],[1,"I will break the doors of bronze in pieces"],[2,"and cut apart the bars of iron."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give you the treasures of darkness"],[2,"and hidden riches of secret places,"],[1,"that you may know that it is I, the LORD, who calls you by your name,"],[2,"even the God of Israel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For Jacob my servant\u2019s sake,"],[2,"and Israel my chosen,"],[1,"I have called you by your name."],[2,"I have given you a title,"],[2,"though you have not known me."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I am the LORD, and there is no one else."],[2,"Besides me, there is no God."],[1,"I will strengthen you,"],[2,"though you have not known me,"]],f:["or, equip"]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"that they may know from the rising of the sun,"],[2,"and from the west,"],[1,"that there is no one besides me."],[2,"I am the LORD, and there is no one else."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I form the light"],[2,"and create darkness."],[1,"I make peace"],[2,"and create calamity."],[1,"I am the LORD,"],[2,"who does all these things."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Rain, you heavens, from above,"],[2,"and let the skies pour down righteousness."],[1,"Let the earth open, that it may produce salvation,"],[2,"and let it cause righteousness to spring up with it."],[1,"I, the LORD, have created it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to him who strives with his Maker\u2014"],[2,"a clay pot among the clay pots of the earth!"],[1,"Shall the clay ask him who fashions it, \u2018What are you making?\u2019"],[2,"or your work, \u2018He has no hands\u2019?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to him who says to a father, \u2018What have you become the father of?\u2019"],[2,"or to a mother, \u2018What have you given birth to?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD, the Holy One of Israel"],[2,"and his Maker says:"],[1,"\u201cYou ask me about the things that are to come, concerning my sons,"],[2,"and you command me concerning the work of my hands!"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I have made the earth, and created man on it."],[2,"I, even my hands, have stretched out the heavens."],[2,"I have commanded all their army."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I have raised him up in righteousness,"],[2,"and I will make all his ways straight."],[1,"He shall build my city,"],[2,"and he shall let my exiles go free,"],[2,"not for price nor reward,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD says: \u201cThe labor of Egypt,"],[2,"and the merchandise of Ethiopia,"],[2,"and the Sabeans, men of stature, will come over to you,"],[2,"and they will be yours."],[1,"They will go after you."],[2,"They shall come over in chains."],[2,"They will bow down to you."],[1,"They will make supplication to you:"],[2,"\u2018Surely God is in you; and there is no one else."],[2,"There is no other god."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Most certainly you are a God who has hidden yourself,"],[2,"God of Israel, the Savior.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"They will be disappointed,"],[2,"yes, confounded, all of them."],[2,"Those who are makers of idols will go into confusion together."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel will be saved by the LORD with an everlasting salvation."],[2,"You will not be disappointed nor confounded to ages everlasting."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD who created the heavens,"],[2,"the God who formed the earth and made it,"],[2,"who established it and didn\u2019t create it a waste,"],[2,"who formed it to be inhabited says:"],[1,"\u201cI am the LORD."],[2,"There is no other."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I have not spoken in secret,"],[2,"in a place of the land of darkness."],[1,"I didn\u2019t say to the offspring of Jacob, \u2018Seek me in vain.\u2019"],[2,"I, the LORD, speak righteousness."],[2,"I declare things that are right."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAssemble yourselves and come."],[2,"Draw near together, you who have escaped from the nations."],[1,"Those have no knowledge who carry the wood of their engraved image,"],[2,"and pray to a god that can\u2019t save."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Declare and present it."],[2,"Yes, let them take counsel together."],[1,"Who has shown this from ancient time?"],[2,"Who has declared it of old?"],[2,"Haven\u2019t I, the LORD?"],[1,"There is no other God besides me, a just God and a Savior."],[2,"There is no one besides me."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLook to me, and be saved, all the ends of the earth;"],[2,"for I am God, and there is no other."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I have sworn by myself."],[2,"The word has gone out of my mouth in righteousness, and will not be revoked,"],[1,"that to me every knee shall bow,"],[2,"every tongue shall take an oath."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"They will say of me,"],[2,"\u2018There is righteousness and strength only in the LORD.\u2019\u201d"],[1,"Even to him will men come."],[2,"All those who raged against him will be disappointed."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"All the offspring of Israel will be justified in the LORD,"],[2,"and will rejoice!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Bel bows down."],[2,"Nebo stoops."],[1,"Their idols are carried by animals,"],[2,"and on the livestock."],[1,"The things that you carried around are heavy loads,"],[2,"a burden for the weary."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"They stoop and they bow down together."],[2,"They could not deliver the burden,"],[2,"but they have gone into captivity."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cListen to me, house of Jacob,"],[2,"and all the remnant of the house of Israel,"],[2,"that have been carried from their birth,"],[2,"that have been carried from the womb."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Even to old age I am he,"],[2,"and even to gray hairs I will carry you."],[1,"I have made, and I will bear."],[2,"Yes, I will carry, and will deliver."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTo whom will you compare me, and consider my equal,"],[2,"and compare me, as if we were the same?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Some pour out gold from the bag,"],[2,"and weigh silver in the balance."],[1,"They hire a goldsmith,"],[2,"and he makes it a god."],[1,"They fall down\u2014"],[2,"yes, they worship."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They bear it on their shoulder."],[2,"They carry it, and set it in its place, and it stands there."],[2,"It cannot move from its place."],[1,"Yes, one may cry to it, yet it can not answer."],[2,"It cannot save him out of his trouble."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cRemember this, and show yourselves men."],[2,"Bring it to mind again, you transgressors."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember the former things of old;"],[2,"for I am God, and there is no other."],[2,"I am God, and there is none like me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I declare the end from the beginning,"],[2,"and from ancient times things that are not yet done."],[1,"I say: My counsel will stand,"],[2,"and I will do all that I please."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I call a ravenous bird from the east,"],[2,"the man of my counsel from a far country."],[1,"Yes, I have spoken."],[2,"I will also bring it to pass."],[1,"I have planned."],[2,"I will also do it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen to me, you stubborn-hearted,"],[2,"who are far from righteousness!"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I bring my righteousness near."],[2,"It is not far off,"],[2,"and my salvation will not wait."],[1,"I will grant salvation to Zion,"],[2,"my glory to Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cCome down and sit in the dust, virgin daughter of Babylon."],[2,"Sit on the ground without a throne, daughter of the Chaldeans."],[2,"For you will no longer be called tender and delicate."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Take the millstones and grind flour."],[2,"Remove your veil, lift up your skirt, uncover your legs,"],[2,"and wade through the rivers."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Your nakedness will be uncovered."],[2,"Yes, your shame will be seen."],[1,"I will take vengeance,"],[2,"and will spare no one.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Our Redeemer, the LORD of Armies is his name,"],[2,"is the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSit in silence, and go into darkness,"],[2,"daughter of the Chaldeans."],[1,"For you shall no longer be called"],[2,"the mistress of kingdoms."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I was angry with my people."],[2,"I profaned my inheritance"],[2,"and gave them into your hand."],[1,"You showed them no mercy."],[2,"You laid a very heavy yoke on the aged."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You said, \u2018I will be a princess forever,\u2019"],[2,"so that you didn\u2019t lay these things to your heart,"],[2,"nor did you remember the results."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow therefore hear this, you who are given to pleasures,"],[2,"who sit securely,"],[1,"who say in your heart,"],[2,"\u2018I am, and there is no one else besides me."],[1,"I won\u2019t sit as a widow,"],[2,"neither will I know the loss of children.\u2019"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"But these two things will come to you in a moment in one day:"],[2,"the loss of children and widowhood."],[1,"They will come on you in their full measure,"],[2,"in the multitude of your sorceries,"],[2,"and the great abundance of your enchantments."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For you have trusted in your wickedness."],[2,"You have said, \u2018No one sees me.\u2019"],[1,"Your wisdom and your knowledge has perverted you."],[2,"You have said in your heart, \u2018I am, and there is no one else besides me.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore disaster will come on you."],[2,"You won\u2019t know when it dawns."],[1,"Mischief will fall on you."],[2,"You won\u2019t be able to put it away."],[1,"Desolation will come on you suddenly,"],[2,"which you don\u2019t understand."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cStand now with your enchantments"],[2,"and with the multitude of your sorceries,"],[2,"in which you have labored from your youth,"],[1,"as if you might profit,"],[2,"as if you might prevail."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You are wearied in the multitude of your counsels."],[2,"Now let the astrologers, the stargazers, and the monthly prognosticators stand up and save you from the things that will happen to you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, they are like stubble."],[2,"The fire will burn them."],[2,"They won\u2019t deliver themselves from the power of the flame."],[1,"It won\u2019t be a coal to warm at"],[2,"or a fire to sit by."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The things that you labored in will be like this:"],[2,"those who have trafficked with you from your youth will each wander in his own way."],[2,"There will be no one to save you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear this, house of Jacob,"],[2,"you who are called by the name of Israel,"],[2,"and have come out of the waters of Judah."],[1,"You swear by the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"and make mention of the God of Israel,"],[2,"but not in truth, nor in righteousness\u2014"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"for they call themselves citizens of the holy city,"],[2,"and rely on the God of Israel;"],[2,"the LORD of Armies is his name."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I have declared the former things from of old."],[2,"Yes, they went out of my mouth, and I revealed them."],[2,"I did them suddenly, and they happened."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Because I knew that you are obstinate,"],[2,"and your neck is an iron sinew,"],[2,"and your brow bronze;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"therefore I have declared it to you from of old;"],[2,"before it came to pass I showed it to you;"],[2,"lest you should say, \u2018My idol has done them."],[2,"My engraved image and my molten image has commanded them.\u2019"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You have heard it."],[2,"Now see all this."],[2,"And you, won\u2019t you declare it?"],[1,"\u201cI have shown you new things from this time,"],[2,"even hidden things, which you have not known."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They are created now, and not from of old."],[2,"Before today, you didn\u2019t hear them,"],[2,"lest you should say, \u2018Behold, I knew them.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, you didn\u2019t hear."],[2,"Yes, you didn\u2019t know."],[2,"Yes, from of old your ear was not opened,"],[1,"for I knew that you dealt very treacherously,"],[2,"and were called a transgressor from the womb."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For my name\u2019s sake, I will defer my anger,"],[2,"and for my praise, I hold it back for you"],[2,"so that I don\u2019t cut you off."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I have refined you,"],[2,"but not as silver."],[2,"I have chosen you in the furnace of affliction."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For my own sake,"],[2,"for my own sake, I will do it;"],[1,"for how would my name be profaned?"],[2,"I will not give my glory to another."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cListen to me, O Jacob,"],[2,"and Israel my called:"],[1,"I am he."],[2,"I am the first."],[2,"I am also the last."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, my hand has laid the foundation of the earth,"],[2,"and my right hand has spread out the heavens."],[2,"when I call to them, they stand up together."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAssemble yourselves, all of you, and hear!"],[2,"Who among them has declared these things?"],[1,"He whom the LORD loves will do what he likes to Babylon,"],[2,"and his arm will be against the Chaldeans."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I, even I, have spoken."],[2,"Yes, I have called him."],[1,"I have brought him"],[2,"and he shall make his way prosperous."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cCome near to me and hear this:"],[1,"\u201cFrom the beginning I have not spoken in secret;"],[2,"from the time that it happened, I was there.\u201d"],[1,"Now the Lord GOD has sent me"],[2,"with his Spirit."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD,"],[2,"your Redeemer,"],[2,"the Holy One of Israel, says:"],[1,"\u201cI am the LORD your God,"],[2,"who teaches you to profit,"],[2,"who leads you by the way that you should go."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that you had listened to my commandments!"],[2,"Then your peace would have been like a river"],[2,"and your righteousness like the waves of the sea."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Your offspring also would have been as the sand"],[2,"and the descendants of your body like its grains."],[2,"His name would not be cut off nor destroyed from before me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Leave Babylon!"],[2,"Flee from the Chaldeans!"],[1,"With the sound of joyful shouting announce this,"],[2,"tell it even to the end of the earth;"],[2,"say, \u201cThe LORD has redeemed his servant Jacob!\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"They didn\u2019t thirst when he led them through the deserts."],[2,"He caused the waters to flow out of the rock for them."],[2,"He also split the rock and the waters gushed out."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThere is no peace\u201d, says the LORD, \u201cfor the wicked.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen, islands, to me."],[2,"Listen, you peoples, from afar:"],[1,"the LORD has called me from the womb;"],[2,"from the inside of my mother, he has mentioned my name."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He has made my mouth like a sharp sword."],[2,"He has hidden me in the shadow of his hand."],[1,"He has made me a polished shaft."],[2,"He has kept me close in his quiver."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He said to me, \u201cYou are my servant,"],[2,"Israel, in whom I will be glorified.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"But I said, \u201cI have labored in vain."],[2,"I have spent my strength in vain for nothing;"],[1,"yet surely the justice due to me is with the LORD,"],[2,"and my reward with my God.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Now the LORD, he who formed me from the womb to be his servant,"],[2,"says to bring Jacob again to him,"],[2,"and to gather Israel to him,"],[2,"for I am honorable in the LORD\u2019s eyes,"],[2,"and my God has become my strength."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Indeed, he says, \u201cIt is too light a thing that you should be my servant to raise up the tribes of Jacob,"],[2,"and to restore the preserved of Israel."],[1,"I will also give you as a light to the nations,"],[2,"that you may be my salvation to the end of the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD, the Redeemer of Israel, and his Holy One,"],[2,"says to him whom man despises, to him whom the nation abhors, to a servant of rulers:"],[1,"\u201cKings shall see and rise up,"],[2,"princes, and they shall worship,"],[2,"because of the LORD who is faithful, even the Holy One of Israel, who has chosen you.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD says, \u201cI have answered you in an acceptable time."],[2,"I have helped you in a day of salvation."],[1,"I will preserve you and give you for a covenant of the people,"],[2,"to raise up the land, to make them inherit the desolate heritage,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"saying to those who are bound, \u2018Come out!\u2019;"],[2,"to those who are in darkness, \u2018Show yourselves!\u2019"],[1,"\u201cThey shall feed along the paths,"],[2,"and their pasture shall be on all treeless heights."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They shall not hunger nor thirst;"],[2,"neither shall the heat nor sun strike them,"],[2,"for he who has mercy on them will lead them."],[2,"He will guide them by springs of water."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make all my mountains a road,"],[2,"and my highways shall be exalted."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, these shall come from afar,"],[2,"and behold, these from the north and from the west,"],[2,"and these from the land of Sinim.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing, heavens, and be joyful, earth!"],[2,"Break out into singing, mountains!"],[1,"For the LORD has comforted his people,"],[2,"and will have compassion on his afflicted."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"But Zion said, \u201cThe LORD has forsaken me,"],[2,"and the Lord has forgotten me.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan a woman forget her nursing child,"],[2,"that she should not have compassion on the son of her womb?"],[1,"Yes, these may forget,"],[2,"yet I will not forget you!"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I have engraved you on the palms of my hands."],[2,"Your walls are continually before me."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Your children hurry."],[2,"Your destroyers and those who devastated you will leave you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your eyes all around, and see:"],[2,"all these gather themselves together, and come to you."],[1,"As I live,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cyou shall surely clothe yourself with them all as with an ornament,"],[2,"and dress yourself with them, like a bride."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor, as for your waste and your desolate places,"],[2,"and your land that has been destroyed,"],[1,"surely now that land will be too small for the inhabitants,"],[2,"and those who swallowed you up will be far away."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The children of your bereavement will say in your ears,"],[2,"\u2018This place is too small for me."],[2,"Give me a place to live in.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Then you will say in your heart, \u2018Who has conceived these for me, since I have been bereaved of my children"],[2,"and am alone, an exile, and wandering back and forth?"],[1,"Who has brought these up?"],[2,"Behold, I was left alone. Where were these?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord GOD says, \u201cBehold, I will lift up my hand to the nations,"],[2,"and lift up my banner to the peoples."],[1,"They shall bring your sons in their bosom,"],[2,"and your daughters shall be carried on their shoulders."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Kings shall be your foster fathers,"],[2,"and their queens your nursing mothers."],[1,"They will bow down to you with their faces to the earth,"],[2,"and lick the dust of your feet."],[1,"Then you will know that I am the LORD;"],[2,"and those who wait for me won\u2019t be disappointed.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall the plunder be taken from the mighty,"],[2,"or the lawful captives be delivered?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"But the LORD says, \u201cEven the captives of the mighty shall be taken away,"],[2,"and the plunder retrieved from the fierce,"],[1,"for I will contend with him who contends with you"],[2,"and I will save your children."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"I will feed those who oppress you with their own flesh;"],[2,"and they will be drunk on their own blood, as with sweet wine."],[1,"Then all flesh shall know that I, the LORD, am your Savior"],[2,"and your Redeemer, the Mighty One of Jacob.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD says, \u201cWhere is the bill of your mother\u2019s divorce, with which I have put her away?"],[2,"Or to which of my creditors have I sold you?"],[1,"Behold, you were sold for your iniquities,"],[2,"and your mother was put away for your transgressions."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Why, when I came, was there no one?"],[2,"When I called, why was there no one to answer?"],[1,"Is my hand shortened at all, that it can\u2019t redeem?"],[2,"Or have I no power to deliver?"],[1,"Behold, at my rebuke I dry up the sea."],[2,"I make the rivers a wilderness."],[2,"Their fish stink because there is no water, and die of thirst."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I clothe the heavens with blackness."],[2,"I make sackcloth their covering.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord GOD has given me the tongue of those who are taught,"],[2,"that I may know how to sustain with words him who is weary."],[1,"He awakens morning by morning,"],[2,"he awakens my ear to hear as those who are taught."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord GOD has opened my ear."],[2,"I was not rebellious."],[2,"I have not turned back."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I gave my back to those who beat me,"],[2,"and my cheeks to those who plucked off the hair."],[2,"I didn\u2019t hide my face from shame and spitting."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For the Lord GOD will help me."],[2,"Therefore I have not been confounded."],[1,"Therefore I have set my face like a flint,"],[2,"and I know that I won\u2019t be disappointed."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He who justifies me is near."],[2,"Who will bring charges against me?"],[1,"Let us stand up together."],[2,"Who is my adversary?"],[2,"Let him come near to me."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the Lord GOD will help me!"],[2,"Who is he who will condemn me?"],[1,"Behold, they will all grow old like a garment."],[2,"The moths will eat them up."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Who among you fears the LORD"],[2,"and obeys the voice of his servant?"],[1,"He who walks in darkness"],[2,"and has no light,"],[1,"let him trust in the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"and rely on his God."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, all you who kindle a fire,"],[2,"who adorn yourselves with torches around yourselves,"],[1,"walk in the flame of your fire,"],[2,"and among the torches that you have kindled."],[1,"You will have this from my hand:"],[2,"you will lie down in sorrow."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cListen to me, you who follow after righteousness,"],[2,"you who seek the LORD."],[1,"Look to the rock you were cut from,"],[2,"and to the quarry you were dug from."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Look to Abraham your father,"],[2,"and to Sarah who bore you;"],[1,"for when he was but one I called him,"],[2,"I blessed him,"],[2,"and made him many."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD has comforted Zion."],[2,"He has comforted all her waste places,"],[2,"and has made her wilderness like Eden,"],[2,"and her desert like the garden of the LORD."],[1,"Joy and gladness will be found in them,"],[2,"thanksgiving, and the voice of melody."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cListen to me, my people;"],[2,"and hear me, my nation,"],[1,"for a law will go out from me,"],[2,"and I will establish my justice for a light to the peoples."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My righteousness is near."],[2,"My salvation has gone out,"],[2,"and my arms will judge the peoples."],[1,"The islands will wait for me,"],[2,"and they will trust my arm."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your eyes to the heavens,"],[2,"and look at the earth beneath;"],[1,"for the heavens will vanish away like smoke,"],[2,"and the earth will wear out like a garment."],[1,"Its inhabitants will die in the same way,"],[2,"but my salvation will be forever,"],[2,"and my righteousness will not be abolished."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cListen to me, you who know righteousness,"],[2,"the people in whose heart is my law."],[1,"Don\u2019t fear the reproach of men,"],[2,"and don\u2019t be dismayed at their insults."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For the moth will eat them up like a garment,"],[2,"and the worm will eat them like wool;"],[1,"but my righteousness will be forever,"],[2,"and my salvation to all generations.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Awake, awake, put on strength, arm of the LORD!"],[2,"Awake, as in the days of old,"],[2,"the generations of ancient times."],[1,"Isn\u2019t it you who cut Rahab in pieces,"],[2,"who pierced the monster?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t it you who dried up the sea,"],[2,"the waters of the great deep;"],[2,"who made the depths of the sea a way for the redeemed to pass over?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Those ransomed by the LORD will return,"],[2,"and come with singing to Zion."],[2,"Everlasting joy shall be on their heads."],[1,"They will obtain gladness and joy."],[2,"Sorrow and sighing shall flee away."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI, even I, am he who comforts you."],[2,"Who are you, that you are afraid of man who shall die,"],[2,"and of the son of man who will be made as grass?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Have you forgotten the LORD your Maker,"],[2,"who stretched out the heavens,"],[2,"and laid the foundations of the earth?"],[1,"Do you live in fear continually all day because of the fury of the oppressor,"],[2,"when he prepares to destroy?"],[2,"Where is the fury of the oppressor?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The captive exile will speedily be freed."],[2,"He will not die and go down into the pit."],[2,"His bread won\u2019t fail."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"For I am the LORD your God, who stirs up the sea"],[2,"so that its waves roar."],[2,"the LORD of Armies is his name."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I have put my words in your mouth"],[2,"and have covered you in the shadow of my hand,"],[1,"that I may plant the heavens,"],[2,"and lay the foundations of the earth,"],[2,"and tell Zion, \u2018You are my people.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Awake, awake!"],[2,"Stand up, Jerusalem,"],[2,"you who have drunk from the LORD\u2019s hand the cup of his wrath."],[1,"You have drunken the bowl of the cup of staggering,"],[2,"and drained it."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no one to guide her among all the sons to whom she has given birth;"],[2,"and there is no one who takes her by the hand among all the sons whom she has brought up."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"These two things have happened to you\u2014"],[2,"who will grieve with you?\u2014"],[1,"desolation and destruction,"],[2,"and famine and the sword."],[2,"How can I comfort you?"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Your sons have fainted."],[2,"They lie at the head of all the streets,"],[2,"like an antelope in a net."],[1,"They are full of the LORD\u2019s wrath,"],[2,"the rebuke of your God."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore now hear this, you afflicted,"],[2,"and drunken, but not with wine:"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Your Lord GOD,"],[2,"your God who pleads the cause of his people, says,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I have taken out of your hand the cup of staggering,"],[2,"even the bowl of the cup of my wrath."],[2,"You will not drink it any more."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I will put it into the hand of those who afflict you,"],[2,"who have said to your soul, \u2018Bow down, that we may walk over you;\u2019"],[2,"and you have laid your back as the ground,"],[2,"like a street to those who walk over.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Awake, awake! Put on your strength, Zion."],[2,"Put on your beautiful garments, Jerusalem, the holy city,"],[2,"for from now on the uncircumcised and the unclean will no more come into you."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Shake yourself from the dust!"],[2,"Arise, sit up, Jerusalem!"],[2,"Release yourself from the bonds of your neck, captive daughter of Zion!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD says, \u201cYou were sold for nothing;"],[2,"and you will be redeemed without money.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"For the Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cMy people went down at the first into Egypt to live there;"],[2,"and the Assyrian has oppressed them without cause."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow therefore, what do I do here,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cseeing that my people are taken away for nothing?"],[1,"Those who rule over them mock,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cand my name is blasphemed continually all day long."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore my people shall know my name."],[2,"Therefore they shall know in that day that I am he who speaks."],[2,"Behold, it is I.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"How beautiful on the mountains are the feet of him who brings good news,"],[2,"who publishes peace,"],[2,"who brings good news,"],[2,"who proclaims salvation,"],[2,"who says to Zion, \u201cYour God reigns!\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Your watchmen lift up their voice."],[2,"Together they sing;"],[2,"for they shall see eye to eye when the LORD returns to Zion."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Break out into joy!"],[2,"Sing together, you waste places of Jerusalem;"],[2,"for the LORD has comforted his people."],[2,"He has redeemed Jerusalem."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has made his holy arm bare in the eyes of all the nations."],[2,"All the ends of the earth have seen the salvation of our God."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Depart! Depart! Go out from there! Touch no unclean thing!"],[2,"Go out from among her!"],[2,"Cleanse yourselves, you who carry the LORD\u2019s vessels."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For you shall not go out in haste,"],[2,"neither shall you go by flight;"],[1,"for the LORD will go before you,"],[2,"and the God of Israel will be your rear guard."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, my servant will deal wisely."],[2,"He will be exalted and lifted up,"],[2,"and will be very high."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Just as many were astonished at you\u2014"],[2,"his appearance was marred more than any man, and his form more than the sons of men\u2014"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"so he will cleanse many nations."],[2,"Kings will shut their mouths at him;"],[2,"for they will see that which had not been told them,"],[2,"and they will understand that which they had not heard."]],f:["or, sprinkle"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has believed our message?"],[2,"To whom has the LORD\u2019s arm been revealed?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For he grew up before him as a tender plant,"],[2,"and as a root out of dry ground."],[1,"He has no good looks or majesty."],[2,"When we see him, there is no beauty that we should desire him."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He was despised"],[2,"and rejected by men,"],[1,"a man of suffering"],[2,"and acquainted with disease."],[1,"He was despised as one from whom men hide their face;"],[2,"and we didn\u2019t respect him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely he has borne our sickness"],[2,"and carried our suffering;"],[1,"yet we considered him plagued,"],[2,"struck by God, and afflicted."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"But he was pierced for our transgressions."],[2,"He was crushed for our iniquities."],[1,"The punishment that brought our peace was on him;"],[2,"and by his wounds we are healed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"All we like sheep have gone astray."],[2,"Everyone has turned to his own way;"],[2,"and the LORD has laid on him the iniquity of us all."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He was oppressed,"],[2,"yet when he was afflicted he didn\u2019t open his mouth."],[1,"As a lamb that is led to the slaughter,"],[2,"and as a sheep that before its shearers is silent,"],[2,"so he didn\u2019t open his mouth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He was taken away by oppression and judgment."],[2,"As for his generation,"],[2,"who considered that he was cut off out of the land of the living"],[2,"and stricken for the disobedience of my people?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They made his grave with the wicked,"],[2,"and with a rich man in his death,"],[1,"although he had done no violence,"],[2,"nor was any deceit in his mouth."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet it pleased the LORD to bruise him."],[2,"He has caused him to suffer."],[1,"When you make his soul an offering for sin,"],[2,"he will see his offspring."],[1,"He will prolong his days"],[2,"and the LORD\u2019s pleasure will prosper in his hand."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"After the suffering of his soul,"],[2,"he will see the light and be satisfied."],[1,"My righteous servant will justify many by the knowledge of himself;"],[2,"and he will bear their iniquities."]],f:["So read the Dead Sea Scrolls and Septuagint. Masoretic Text omits \u201cthe light\u201d."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will give him a portion with the great."],[2,"He will divide the plunder with the strong,"],[1,"because he poured out his soul to death"],[2,"and was counted with the transgressors;"],[1,"yet he bore the sins of many"],[2,"and made intercession for the transgressors."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSing, barren, you who didn\u2019t give birth!"],[2,"Break out into singing, and cry aloud, you who didn\u2019t travail with child!"],[2,"For more are the children of the desolate than the children of the married wife,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEnlarge the place of your tent,"],[2,"and let them stretch out the curtains of your habitations;"],[2,"don\u2019t spare; lengthen your cords, and strengthen your stakes."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For you will spread out on the right hand and on the left;"],[2,"and your offspring will possess the nations"],[2,"and settle in desolate cities."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for you will not be ashamed."],[2,"Don\u2019t be confounded, for you will not be disappointed."],[1,"For you will forget the shame of your youth."],[2,"You will remember the reproach of your widowhood no more."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For your Maker is your husband; the LORD of Armies is his name."],[2,"The Holy One of Israel is your Redeemer."],[2,"He will be called the God of the whole earth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD has called you as a wife forsaken and grieved in spirit,"],[2,"even a wife of youth, when she is cast off,\u201d says your God."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor a small moment I have forsaken you,"],[2,"but I will gather you with great mercies."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"In overflowing wrath I hid my face from you for a moment,"],[2,"but with everlasting loving kindness I will have mercy on you,\u201d says the LORD your Redeemer."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor this is like the waters of Noah to me;"],[2,"for as I have sworn that the waters of Noah will no more go over the earth,"],[2,"so I have sworn that I will not be angry with you, nor rebuke you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For the mountains may depart,"],[2,"and the hills be removed,"],[1,"but my loving kindness will not depart from you,"],[2,"and my covenant of peace will not be removed,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD who has mercy on you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou afflicted, tossed with storms, and not comforted,"],[2,"behold, I will set your stones in beautiful colors,"],[2,"and lay your foundations with sapphires."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make your pinnacles of rubies,"],[2,"your gates of sparkling jewels,"],[2,"and all your walls of precious stones."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"All your children will be taught by the LORD,"],[2,"and your children\u2019s peace will be great."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You will be established in righteousness."],[2,"You will be far from oppression,"],[2,"for you will not be afraid,"],[2,"and far from terror,"],[2,"for it shall not come near you."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, they may gather together, but not by me."],[2,"Whoever gathers together against you will fall because of you."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I have created the blacksmith who fans the coals into flame,"],[2,"and forges a weapon for his work;"],[2,"and I have created the destroyer to destroy."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"No weapon that is formed against you will prevail;"],[2,"and you will condemn every tongue that rises against you in judgment."],[1,"This is the heritage of the LORD\u2019s servants,"],[2,"and their righteousness is of me,\u201d says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHey! Come, everyone who thirsts, to the waters!"],[2,"Come, he who has no money, buy, and eat!"],[2,"Yes, come, buy wine and milk without money and without price."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you spend money for that which is not bread,"],[2,"and your labor for that which doesn\u2019t satisfy?"],[1,"Listen diligently to me, and eat that which is good,"],[2,"and let your soul delight itself in richness."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn your ear, and come to me."],[2,"Hear, and your soul will live."],[2,"I will make an everlasting covenant with you, even the sure mercies of David."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I have given him for a witness to the peoples,"],[2,"a leader and commander to the peoples."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you shall call a nation that you don\u2019t know;"],[2,"and a nation that didn\u2019t know you shall run to you,"],[2,"because of the LORD your God,"],[2,"and for the Holy One of Israel;"],[2,"for he has glorified you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Seek the LORD while he may be found."],[2,"Call on him while he is near."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the wicked forsake his way,"],[2,"and the unrighteous man his thoughts."],[1,"Let him return to the LORD, and he will have mercy on him,"],[2,"to our God, for he will freely pardon."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor my thoughts are not your thoughts,"],[2,"and your ways are not my ways,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor as the heavens are higher than the earth,"],[2,"so are my ways higher than your ways,"],[2,"and my thoughts than your thoughts."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For as the rain comes down and the snow from the sky,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t return there, but waters the earth,"],[2,"and makes it grow and bud,"],[2,"and gives seed to the sower and bread to the eater;"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"so is my word that goes out of my mouth:"],[2,"it will not return to me void,"],[2,"but it will accomplish that which I please,"],[2,"and it will prosper in the thing I sent it to do."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For you shall go out with joy,"],[2,"and be led out with peace."],[1,"The mountains and the hills will break out before you into singing;"],[2,"and all the trees of the fields will clap their hands."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Instead of the thorn the cypress tree will come up;"],[2,"and instead of the brier the myrtle tree will come up."],[1,"It will make a name for the LORD,"],[2,"for an everlasting sign that will not be cut off.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cMaintain justice"],[2,"and do what is right,"],[1,"for my salvation is near"],[2,"and my righteousness will soon be revealed."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man who does this,"],[2,"and the son of man who holds it fast;"],[1,"who keeps the Sabbath without profaning it"],[2,"and keeps his hand from doing any evil.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Let no foreigner who has joined himself to the LORD speak, saying,"],[2,"\u201cThe LORD will surely separate me from his people.\u201d"],[2,"Do not let the eunuch say, \u201cBehold, I am a dry tree.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD says, \u201cTo the eunuchs who keep my Sabbaths,"],[2,"choose the things that please me,"],[2,"and hold fast to my covenant,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give them in my house and within my walls a memorial and a name better than of sons and of daughters."],[2,"I will give them an everlasting name that will not be cut off."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Also the foreigners who join themselves to the LORD"],[2,"to serve him,"],[1,"and to love the LORD\u2019s name,"],[2,"to be his servants,"],[1,"everyone who keeps the Sabbath from profaning it,"],[2,"and holds fast my covenant,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring these to my holy mountain,"],[2,"and make them joyful in my house of prayer."],[1,"Their burnt offerings and their sacrifices will be accepted on my altar;"],[2,"for my house will be called a house of prayer for all peoples.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord GOD, who gathers the outcasts of Israel, says,"],[2,"\u201cI will yet gather others to him,"],[2,"in addition to his own who are gathered.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"All you animals of the field,"],[2,"come to devour,"],[2,"all you animals in the forest."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"His watchmen are blind."],[2,"They are all without knowledge."],[1,"They are all mute dogs."],[2,"They can\u2019t bark\u2014"],[2,"dreaming, lying down, loving to slumber."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, the dogs are greedy."],[2,"They can never have enough."],[1,"They are shepherds who can\u2019t understand."],[2,"They have all turned to their own way,"],[2,"each one to his gain, from every quarter."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCome,\u201d they say, \u201cI will get wine,"],[2,"and we will fill ourselves with strong drink;"],[2,"and tomorrow will be as today,"],[2,"great beyond measure.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The righteous perish,"],[2,"and no one lays it to heart."],[1,"Merciful men are taken away,"],[2,"and no one considers that the righteous is taken away from the evil."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He enters into peace."],[2,"They rest in their beds,"],[2,"each one who walks in his uprightness."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut draw near here, you sons of a sorceress,"],[2,"you offspring of adulterers and prostitutes."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Whom do you mock?"],[2,"Against whom do you make a wide mouth"],[2,"and stick out your tongue?"],[1,"Aren\u2019t you children of disobedience"],[2,"and offspring of falsehood,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"you who inflame yourselves among the oaks,"],[2,"under every green tree;"],[1,"who kill the children in the valleys,"],[2,"under the clefts of the rocks?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Among the smooth stones of the valley is your portion."],[2,"They, they are your lot."],[1,"You have even poured a drink offering to them."],[2,"You have offered an offering."],[2,"Shall I be appeased for these things?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"On a high and lofty mountain you have set your bed."],[2,"You also went up there to offer sacrifice."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You have set up your memorial behind the doors and the posts,"],[2,"for you have exposed yourself to someone besides me,"],[2,"and have gone up."],[1,"You have enlarged your bed"],[2,"and made a covenant for yourself with them."],[2,"You loved what you saw on their bed."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You went to the king with oil,"],[2,"increased your perfumes,"],[2,"sent your ambassadors far off,"],[2,"and degraded yourself even to Sheol."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You were wearied with the length of your ways;"],[2,"yet you didn\u2019t say, \u2018It is in vain.\u2019"],[1,"You found a reviving of your strength;"],[2,"therefore you weren\u2019t faint."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhom have you dreaded and feared,"],[2,"so that you lie,"],[2,"and have not remembered me, nor laid it to your heart?"],[1,"Haven\u2019t I held my peace for a long time,"],[2,"and you don\u2019t fear me?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will declare your righteousness;"],[2,"and as for your works, they will not benefit you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"When you cry,"],[2,"let those whom you have gathered deliver you,"],[1,"but the wind will take them."],[2,"A breath will carry them all away,"],[1,"but he who takes refuge in me will possess the land,"],[2,"and will inherit my holy mountain.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"He will say, \u201cBuild up, build up, prepare the way!"],[2,"Remove the stumbling-block out of the way of my people.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"For the high and lofty One who inhabits eternity,"],[2,"whose name is Holy, says:"],[1,"\u201cI dwell in the high and holy place, with him also who is of a contrite and humble spirit,"],[2,"to revive the spirit of the humble,"],[2,"and to revive the heart of the contrite."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will not contend forever, neither will I always be angry;"],[2,"for the spirit would faint before me,"],[2,"and the souls whom I have made."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I was angry because of the iniquity of his covetousness and struck him."],[2,"I hid myself and was angry;"],[2,"and he went on backsliding in the way of his heart."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I have seen his ways, and will heal him."],[2,"I will lead him also,"],[2,"and restore comforts to him and to his mourners."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I create the fruit of the lips:"],[2,"Peace, peace, to him who is far off and to him who is near,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD; \u201cand I will heal them.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"But the wicked are like the troubled sea;"],[2,"for it can\u2019t rest and its waters cast up mire and mud."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThere is no peace\u201d, says my God,"],[2,"\u201cfor the wicked.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCry aloud! Don\u2019t spare!"],[2,"Lift up your voice like a trumpet!"],[1,"Declare to my people their disobedience,"],[2,"and to the house of Jacob their sins."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet they seek me daily,"],[2,"and delight to know my ways."],[1,"As a nation that did righteousness,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t forsake the ordinance of their God,"],[1,"they ask of me righteous judgments."],[2,"They delight to draw near to God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018Why have we fasted,\u2019 they say, \u2018and you don\u2019t see?"],[2,"Why have we afflicted our soul, and you don\u2019t notice?\u2019"],[1,"\u201cBehold, in the day of your fast you find pleasure,"],[2,"and oppress all your laborers."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, you fast for strife and contention,"],[2,"and to strike with the fist of wickedness."],[2,"You don\u2019t fast today so as to make your voice to be heard on high."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Is this the fast that I have chosen?"],[2,"A day for a man to humble his soul?"],[1,"Is it to bow down his head like a reed,"],[2,"and to spread sackcloth and ashes under himself?"],[1,"Will you call this a fast,"],[2,"and an acceptable day to the LORD?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIsn\u2019t this the fast that I have chosen:"],[2,"to release the bonds of wickedness,"],[2,"to undo the straps of the yoke,"],[2,"to let the oppressed go free,"],[2,"and that you break every yoke?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t it to distribute your bread to the hungry,"],[2,"and that you bring the poor who are cast out to your house?"],[1,"When you see the naked,"],[2,"that you cover him;"],[2,"and that you not hide yourself from your own flesh?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Then your light will break out as the morning,"],[2,"and your healing will appear quickly;"],[1,"then your righteousness shall go before you,"],[2,"and the LORD\u2019s glory will be your rear guard."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Then you will call, and the LORD will answer."],[2,"You will cry for help, and he will say, \u2018Here I am.\u2019"],[1,"\u201cIf you take away from among you the yoke,"],[2,"finger pointing,"],[2,"and speaking wickedly;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"and if you pour out your soul to the hungry,"],[2,"and satisfy the afflicted soul,"],[1,"then your light will rise in darkness,"],[2,"and your obscurity will be as the noonday;"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"and the LORD will guide you continually,"],[2,"satisfy your soul in dry places,"],[2,"and make your bones strong."],[1,"You will be like a watered garden,"],[2,"and like a spring of water"],[2,"whose waters don\u2019t fail."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who will be of you will build the old waste places."],[2,"You will raise up the foundations of many generations."],[1,"You will be called Repairer of the Breach,"],[2,"Restorer of Paths with Dwellings."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf you turn away your foot from the Sabbath,"],[2,"from doing your pleasure on my holy day,"],[1,"and call the Sabbath a delight,"],[2,"and the holy of the LORD honorable,"],[2,"and honor it,"],[2,"not doing your own ways,"],[2,"nor finding your own pleasure,"],[2,"nor speaking your own words,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"then you will delight yourself in the LORD,"],[2,"and I will make you to ride on the high places of the earth,"],[2,"and I will feed you with the heritage of Jacob your father;\u201d"],[2,"for the LORD\u2019s mouth has spoken it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the LORD\u2019s hand is not shortened, that it can\u2019t save;"],[2,"nor his ear dull, that it can\u2019t hear."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"But your iniquities have separated you and your God,"],[2,"and your sins have hidden his face from you,"],[2,"so that he will not hear."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For your hands are defiled with blood,"],[2,"and your fingers with iniquity."],[1,"Your lips have spoken lies."],[2,"Your tongue mutters wickedness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"No one sues in righteousness,"],[2,"and no one pleads in truth."],[1,"They trust in vanity"],[2,"and speak lies."],[1,"They conceive mischief"],[2,"and give birth to iniquity."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They hatch adders\u2019 eggs"],[2,"and weave the spider\u2019s web."],[1,"He who eats of their eggs dies;"],[2,"and that which is crushed breaks out into a viper."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Their webs won\u2019t become garments."],[2,"They won\u2019t cover themselves with their works."],[1,"Their works are works of iniquity,"],[2,"and acts of violence are in their hands."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Their feet run to evil,"],[2,"and they hurry to shed innocent blood."],[1,"Their thoughts are thoughts of iniquity."],[2,"Desolation and destruction are in their paths."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They don\u2019t know the way of peace;"],[2,"and there is no justice in their ways."],[1,"They have made crooked paths for themselves;"],[2,"whoever goes in them doesn\u2019t know peace."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore justice is far from us,"],[2,"and righteousness doesn\u2019t overtake us."],[1,"We look for light, but see darkness;"],[2,"for brightness, but we walk in obscurity."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"We grope for the wall like the blind."],[2,"Yes, we grope as those who have no eyes."],[1,"We stumble at noon as if it were twilight."],[2,"Among those who are strong, we are like dead men."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"We all roar like bears"],[2,"and moan sadly like doves."],[1,"We look for justice, but there is none,"],[2,"for salvation, but it is far off from us."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For our transgressions are multiplied before you,"],[2,"and our sins testify against us;"],[1,"for our transgressions are with us,"],[2,"and as for our iniquities, we know them:"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"transgressing and denying the LORD,"],[2,"and turning away from following our God,"],[2,"speaking oppression and revolt,"],[2,"conceiving and uttering from the heart words of falsehood."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Justice is turned away backward,"],[2,"and righteousness stands far away;"],[1,"for truth has fallen in the street,"],[2,"and uprightness can\u2019t enter."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, truth is lacking;"],[2,"and he who departs from evil makes himself a prey."],[1,"The LORD saw it,"],[2,"and it displeased him that there was no justice."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He saw that there was no man,"],[2,"and wondered that there was no intercessor."],[1,"Therefore his own arm brought salvation to him;"],[2,"and his righteousness sustained him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"He put on righteousness as a breastplate,"],[2,"and a helmet of salvation on his head."],[1,"He put on garments of vengeance for clothing,"],[2,"and was clad with zeal as a mantle."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"According to their deeds,"],[2,"he will repay as appropriate:"],[2,"wrath to his adversaries,"],[2,"recompense to his enemies."],[2,"He will repay the islands their due."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"So they will fear the LORD\u2019s name from the west,"],[2,"and his glory from the rising of the sun;"],[1,"for he will come as a rushing stream,"],[2,"which the LORD\u2019s breath drives."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cA Redeemer will come to Zion,"],[2,"and to those who turn from disobedience in Jacob,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for me, this is my covenant with them,\u201d says the LORD. \u201cMy Spirit who is on you, and my words which I have put in your mouth shall not depart out of your mouth, nor out of the mouth of your offspring, nor out of the mouth of your offspring\u2019s offspring,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cfrom now on and forever.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cArise, shine; for your light has come,"],[2,"and the LORD\u2019s glory has risen on you!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For behold, darkness will cover the earth,"],[2,"and thick darkness the peoples;"],[1,"but the LORD will arise on you,"],[2,"and his glory shall be seen on you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Nations will come to your light,"],[2,"and kings to the brightness of your rising."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLift up your eyes all around, and see:"],[2,"they all gather themselves together."],[2,"They come to you."],[1,"Your sons will come from far away,"],[2,"and your daughters will be carried in arms."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Then you shall see and be radiant,"],[2,"and your heart will thrill and be enlarged;"],[1,"because the abundance of the sea will be turned to you."],[2,"The wealth of the nations will come to you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"A multitude of camels will cover you,"],[2,"the dromedaries of Midian and Ephah."],[1,"All from Sheba will come."],[2,"They will bring gold and frankincense,"],[2,"and will proclaim the praises of the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"All the flocks of Kedar will be gathered together to you."],[2,"The rams of Nebaioth will serve you."],[1,"They will be accepted as offerings on my altar;"],[2,"and I will beautify my glorious house."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWho are these who fly as a cloud,"],[2,"and as the doves to their windows?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely the islands will wait for me,"],[2,"and the ships of Tarshish first,"],[1,"to bring your sons from far away,"],[2,"their silver and their gold with them,"],[1,"for the name of the LORD your God,"],[2,"and for the Holy One of Israel,"],[2,"because he has glorified you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cForeigners will build up your walls,"],[2,"and their kings will serve you;"],[1,"for in my wrath I struck you,"],[2,"but in my favor I have had mercy on you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Your gates also shall be open continually; they shall not be shut day nor night, that men may bring to you the wealth of the nations, and their kings led captive."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For that nation and kingdom that will not serve you shall perish; yes, those nations shall be utterly wasted."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe glory of Lebanon shall come to you, the cypress tree, the pine, and the box tree together, to beautify the place of my sanctuary; and I will make the place of my feet glorious."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The sons of those who afflicted you will come bowing to you;"],[2,"and all those who despised you will bow themselves down at the soles of your feet."],[1,"They will call you the LORD\u2019s City,"],[2,"the Zion of the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhereas you have been forsaken and hated,"],[2,"so that no one passed through you,"],[1,"I will make you an eternal excellency,"],[2,"a joy of many generations."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"You will also drink the milk of the nations,"],[2,"and will nurse from royal breasts."],[1,"Then you will know that I, the LORD, am your Savior,"],[2,"your Redeemer,"],[2,"the Mighty One of Jacob."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For bronze I will bring gold;"],[2,"for iron I will bring silver;"],[2,"for wood, bronze,"],[2,"and for stones, iron."],[1,"I will also make peace your governor,"],[2,"and righteousness your ruler."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Violence shall no more be heard in your land,"],[2,"nor desolation or destruction within your borders;"],[1,"but you will call your walls Salvation,"],[2,"and your gates Praise."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The sun will be no more your light by day,"],[2,"nor will the brightness of the moon give light to you,"],[1,"but the LORD will be your everlasting light,"],[2,"and your God will be your glory."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Your sun will not go down any more,"],[2,"nor will your moon withdraw itself;"],[1,"for the LORD will be your everlasting light,"],[2,"and the days of your mourning will end."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Then your people will all be righteous."],[2,"They will inherit the land forever,"],[2,"the branch of my planting,"],[2,"the work of my hands,"],[2,"that I may be glorified."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The little one will become a thousand,"],[2,"and the small one a strong nation."],[2,"I, the LORD, will do this quickly in its time.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord GOD\u2019s Spirit is on me,"],[2,"because the LORD has anointed me to preach good news to the humble."],[1,"He has sent me to bind up the broken hearted,"],[2,"to proclaim liberty to the captives"],[2,"and release to those who are bound,"]],f:["LXX and DSS add: recovery of sight to the blind"]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"to proclaim the year of the LORD\u2019s favor"],[2,"and the day of vengeance of our God,"],[2,"to comfort all who mourn,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"to provide for those who mourn in Zion,"],[2,"to give to them a garland for ashes,"],[2,"the oil of joy for mourning,"],[2,"the garment of praise for the spirit of heaviness,"],[1,"that they may be called trees of righteousness,"],[2,"the planting of the LORD,"],[2,"that he may be glorified."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They will rebuild the old ruins."],[2,"They will raise up the former devastated places."],[1,"They will repair the ruined cities"],[2,"that have been devastated for many generations."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Strangers will stand and feed your flocks."],[2,"Foreigners will work your fields and your vineyards."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"But you will be called the LORD\u2019s priests."],[2,"Men will call you the servants of our God."],[1,"You will eat the wealth of the nations."],[2,"You will boast in their glory."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Instead of your shame you will have double."],[2,"Instead of dishonor, they will rejoice in their portion."],[1,"Therefore in their land they will possess double."],[2,"Everlasting joy will be to them."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor I, the LORD, love justice."],[2,"I hate robbery and iniquity."],[1,"I will give them their reward in truth"],[2,"and I will make an everlasting covenant with them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Their offspring will be known among the nations,"],[2,"and their offspring among the peoples."],[1,"All who see them will acknowledge them,"],[2,"that they are the offspring which the LORD has blessed.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I will greatly rejoice in the LORD!"],[2,"My soul will be joyful in my God,"],[1,"for he has clothed me with the garments of salvation."],[2,"He has covered me with the robe of righteousness,"],[2,"as a bridegroom decks himself with a garland"],[2,"and as a bride adorns herself with her jewels."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For as the earth produces its bud,"],[2,"and as the garden causes the things that are sown in it to spring up,"],[2,"so the Lord GOD will cause righteousness and praise to spring up before all the nations."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"For Zion\u2019s sake I will not hold my peace,"],[2,"and for Jerusalem\u2019s sake I will not rest,"],[1,"until her righteousness shines out like the dawn,"],[2,"and her salvation like a burning lamp."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The nations will see your righteousness,"],[2,"and all kings your glory."],[1,"You will be called by a new name,"],[2,"which the LORD\u2019s mouth will name."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You will also be a crown of beauty in the LORD\u2019s hand,"],[2,"and a royal diadem in your God\u2019s hand."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You will not be called Forsaken any more,"],[2,"nor will your land be called Desolate any more;"],[1,"but you will be called Hephzibah,"],[2,"and your land Beulah;"],[1,"for the LORD delights in you,"],[2,"and your land will be married."]],f:["Hephzibah means \u201cI delight in her\u201d.","Beulah means \u201cmarried\u201d"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For as a young man marries a virgin,"],[2,"so your sons will marry you."],[1,"As a bridegroom rejoices over his bride,"],[2,"so your God will rejoice over you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I have set watchmen on your walls, Jerusalem."],[2,"They will never be silent day nor night."],[1,"You who call on the LORD, take no rest,"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"and give him no rest until he establishes,"],[2,"and until he makes Jerusalem a praise on the earth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has sworn by his right hand,"],[2,"and by the arm of his strength,"],[1,"\u201cSurely I will no more give your grain to be food for your enemies,"],[2,"and foreigners will not drink your new wine, for which you have labored,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"but those who have harvested it will eat it, and praise the LORD."],[2,"Those who have gathered it will drink it in the courts of my sanctuary.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Go through, go through the gates!"],[2,"Prepare the way of the people!"],[1,"Build up, build up the highway!"],[2,"Gather out the stones!"],[2,"Lift up a banner for the peoples."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the LORD has proclaimed to the end of the earth:"],[2,"\u201cSay to the daughter of Zion,"],[2,"\u2018Behold, your salvation comes!"],[1,"Behold, his reward is with him,"],[2,"and his recompense before him!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They will call them \u201cThe Holy People,"],[2,"The LORD\u2019s Redeemed\u201d."],[1,"You will be called \u201cSought Out,"],[2,"A City Not Forsaken\u201d."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is this who comes from Edom,"],[2,"with dyed garments from Bozrah?"],[1,"Who is this who is glorious in his clothing,"],[2,"marching in the greatness of his strength?"],[1,"\u201cIt is I who speak in righteousness,"],[2,"mighty to save.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Why is your clothing red,"],[2,"and your garments like him who treads in the wine vat?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have trodden the wine press alone."],[2,"Of the peoples, no one was with me."],[1,"Yes, I trod them in my anger"],[2,"and trampled them in my wrath."],[1,"Their lifeblood is sprinkled on my garments,"],[2,"and I have stained all my clothing."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For the day of vengeance was in my heart,"],[2,"and the year of my redeemed has come."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I looked, and there was no one to help;"],[2,"and I wondered that there was no one to uphold."],[1,"Therefore my own arm brought salvation to me."],[2,"My own wrath upheld me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I trod down the peoples in my anger"],[2,"and made them drunk in my wrath."],[2,"I poured their lifeblood out on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I will tell of the loving kindnesses of the LORD"],[2,"and the praises of the LORD,"],[2,"according to all that the LORD has given to us,"],[1,"and the great goodness toward the house of Israel,"],[2,"which he has given to them according to his mercies,"],[2,"and according to the multitude of his loving kindnesses."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For he said, \u201cSurely, they are my people,"],[2,"children who will not deal falsely;\u201d"],[2,"so he became their Savior."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"In all their affliction he was afflicted,"],[2,"and the angel of his presence saved them."],[1,"In his love and in his pity he redeemed them."],[2,"He bore them,"],[2,"and carried them all the days of old."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But they rebelled"],[2,"and grieved his Holy Spirit."],[1,"Therefore he turned and became their enemy,"],[2,"and he himself fought against them."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Then he remembered the days of old,"],[2,"Moses and his people, saying,"],[1,"\u201cWhere is he who brought them up out of the sea with the shepherds of his flock?"],[2,"Where is he who put his Holy Spirit among them?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Who caused his glorious arm to be at Moses\u2019 right hand?"],[2,"Who divided the waters before them, to make himself an everlasting name?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Who led them through the depths,"],[2,"like a horse in the wilderness,"],[2,"so that they didn\u2019t stumble?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"As the livestock that go down into the valley,"],[2,"the LORD\u2019s Spirit caused them to rest."],[2,"So you led your people to make yourself a glorious name."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Look down from heaven,"],[2,"and see from the habitation of your holiness and of your glory."],[1,"Where are your zeal and your mighty acts?"],[2,"The yearning of your heart and your compassion is restrained toward me."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For you are our Father,"],[2,"though Abraham doesn\u2019t know us,"],[2,"and Israel does not acknowledge us."],[1,"You, LORD, are our Father."],[2,"Our Redeemer from everlasting is your name."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"O LORD, why do you make us wander from your ways,"],[2,"and harden our heart from your fear?"],[1,"Return for your servants\u2019 sake,"],[2,"the tribes of your inheritance."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Your holy people possessed it but a little while."],[2,"Our adversaries have trodden down your sanctuary."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"We have become like those over whom you never ruled,"],[2,"like those who were not called by your name."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that you would tear the heavens,"],[2,"that you would come down,"],[2,"that the mountains might quake at your presence\u2014"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"as when fire kindles the brushwood,"],[2,"and the fire causes the water to boil."],[1,"Make your name known to your adversaries,"],[2,"that the nations may tremble at your presence!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"When you did awesome things which we didn\u2019t look for,"],[2,"you came down, and the mountains quaked at your presence."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For from of old men have not heard,"],[2,"nor perceived by the ear,"],[2,"nor has the eye seen a God besides you,"],[2,"who works for him who waits for him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You meet him who rejoices and does righteousness,"],[2,"those who remember you in your ways."],[1,"Behold, you were angry, and we sinned."],[2,"We have been in sin for a long time."],[2,"Shall we be saved?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For we have all become like one who is unclean,"],[2,"and all our righteousness is like a polluted garment."],[1,"We all fade like a leaf;"],[2,"and our iniquities, like the wind, take us away."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no one who calls on your name,"],[2,"who stirs himself up to take hold of you;"],[1,"for you have hidden your face from us,"],[2,"and have consumed us by means of our iniquities."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But now, LORD, you are our Father."],[2,"We are the clay and you our potter."],[2,"We all are the work of your hand."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be furious, LORD."],[2,"Don\u2019t remember iniquity forever."],[1,"Look and see, we beg you,"],[2,"we are all your people."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Your holy cities have become a wilderness."],[2,"Zion has become a wilderness,"],[2,"Jerusalem a desolation."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Our holy and our beautiful house where our fathers praised you"],[2,"is burned with fire."],[2,"All our pleasant places are laid waste."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you hold yourself back for these things, LORD?"],[2,"Will you keep silent and punish us very severely?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI am inquired of by those who didn\u2019t ask."],[2,"I am found by those who didn\u2019t seek me."],[2,"I said, \u2018See me, see me,\u2019 to a nation that was not called by my name."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I have spread out my hands all day to a rebellious people,"],[2,"who walk in a way that is not good,"],[2,"after their own thoughts;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"a people who provoke me to my face continually,"],[2,"sacrificing in gardens,"],[2,"and burning incense on bricks;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"who sit among the graves,"],[2,"and spend nights in secret places;"],[1,"who eat pig\u2019s meat,"],[2,"and broth of abominable things is in their vessels;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"who say, \u2018Stay by yourself,"],[2,"don\u2019t come near to me,"],[2,"for I am holier than you.\u2019"],[1,"These are smoke in my nose,"],[2,"a fire that burns all day."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, it is written before me:"],[2,"I will not keep silence,"],[2,"but will repay,"],[2,"yes, I will repay into their bosom"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"your own iniquities and the iniquities of your fathers together\u201d, says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cwho have burned incense on the mountains,"],[2,"and blasphemed me on the hills."],[2,"Therefore I will first measure their work into their bosom.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cAs the new wine is found in the cluster,"],[2,"and one says, \u2018Don\u2019t destroy it, for a blessing is in it:\u2019"],[1,"so I will do for my servants\u2019 sake,"],[2,"that I may not destroy them all."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring offspring out of Jacob,"],[2,"and out of Judah an inheritor of my mountains."],[1,"My chosen will inherit it,"],[2,"and my servants will dwell there."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Sharon will be a fold of flocks,"],[2,"and the valley of Achor a place for herds to lie down in,"],[2,"for my people who have sought me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut you who forsake the LORD,"],[2,"who forget my holy mountain,"],[2,"who prepare a table for Fortune,"],[2,"and who fill up mixed wine to Destiny;"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will destine you to the sword,"],[2,"and you will all bow down to the slaughter;"],[1,"because when I called, you didn\u2019t answer."],[2,"When I spoke, you didn\u2019t listen;"],[1,"but you did that which was evil in my eyes,"],[2,"and chose that in which I didn\u2019t delight.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, my servants will eat,"],[2,"but you will be hungry;"],[1,"behold, my servants will drink,"],[2,"but you will be thirsty."],[1,"Behold, my servants will rejoice,"],[2,"but you will be disappointed."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, my servants will sing for joy of heart,"],[2,"but you will cry for sorrow of heart,"],[2,"and will wail for anguish of spirit."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You will leave your name for a curse to my chosen,"],[2,"and the Lord GOD will kill you."],[1,"He will call his servants by another name,"]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"so that he who blesses himself on the earth will bless himself in the God of truth;"],[2,"and he who swears on the earth will swear by the God of truth;"],[1,"because the former troubles are forgotten,"],[2,"and because they are hidden from my eyes."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor, behold, I create new heavens and a new earth;"],[2,"and the former things will not be remembered,"],[2,"nor come into mind."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"But be glad and rejoice forever in that which I create;"],[2,"for, behold, I create Jerusalem to be a delight,"],[2,"and her people a joy."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I will rejoice in Jerusalem,"],[2,"and delight in my people;"],[1,"and the voice of weeping and the voice of crying"],[2,"will be heard in her no more."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNo more will there be an infant who only lives a few days,"],[2,"nor an old man who has not filled his days;"],[1,"for the child will die one hundred years old,"],[2,"and the sinner being one hundred years old will be accursed."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"They will build houses and inhabit them."],[2,"They will plant vineyards and eat their fruit."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"They will not build and another inhabit."],[2,"They will not plant and another eat;"],[1,"for the days of my people will be like the days of a tree,"],[2,"and my chosen will long enjoy the work of their hands."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"They will not labor in vain"],[2,"nor give birth for calamity;"],[1,"for they are the offspring of the LORD\u2019s blessed"],[2,"and their descendants with them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"It will happen that before they call, I will answer;"],[2,"and while they are yet speaking, I will hear."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The wolf and the lamb will feed together."],[2,"The lion will eat straw like the ox."],[2,"Dust will be the serpent\u2019s food."],[1,"They will not hurt nor destroy in all my holy mountain,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cHeaven is my throne, and the earth is my footstool."],[2,"What kind of house will you build to me?"],[2,"Where will I rest?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For my hand has made all these things,"],[2,"and so all these things came to be,\u201d says the LORD:"],[1,"\u201cbut I will look to this man,"],[2,"even to he who is poor and of a contrite spirit,"],[2,"and who trembles at my word."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He who kills an ox is as he who kills a man;"],[2,"he who sacrifices a lamb, as he who breaks a dog\u2019s neck;"],[2,"he who offers an offering, as he who offers pig\u2019s blood;"],[2,"he who burns frankincense, as he who blesses an idol."],[1,"Yes, they have chosen their own ways,"],[2,"and their soul delights in their abominations."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I also will choose their delusions,"],[2,"and will bring their fears on them,"],[1,"because when I called, no one answered;"],[2,"when I spoke, they didn\u2019t listen,"],[1,"but they did that which was evil in my eyes,"],[2,"and chose that in which I didn\u2019t delight.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear the LORD\u2019s word,"],[2,"you who tremble at his word:"],[1,"\u201cYour brothers who hate you,"],[2,"who cast you out for my name\u2019s sake, have said,"],[1,"\u2018Let the LORD be glorified,"],[2,"that we may see your joy;\u2019"],[2,"but it is those who shall be disappointed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"A voice of tumult from the city,"],[2,"a voice from the temple,"],[2,"a voice of the LORD that repays his enemies what they deserve."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBefore she travailed, she gave birth."],[2,"Before her pain came, she delivered a son."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Who has heard of such a thing?"],[2,"Who has seen such things?"],[1,"Shall a land be born in one day?"],[2,"Shall a nation be born at once?"],[1,"For as soon as Zion travailed,"],[2,"she gave birth to her children."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall I bring to the birth, and not cause to be delivered?\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cShall I who cause to give birth shut the womb?\u201d says your God."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cRejoice with Jerusalem, and be glad for her, all you who love her."],[2,"Rejoice for joy with her, all you who mourn over her;"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"that you may nurse and be satisfied at the comforting breasts;"],[2,"that you may drink deeply,"],[2,"and be delighted with the abundance of her glory.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD says, \u201cBehold, I will extend peace to her like a river,"],[2,"and the glory of the nations like an overflowing stream,"],[2,"and you will nurse."],[1,"You will be carried on her side,"],[2,"and will be dandled on her knees."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"As one whom his mother comforts,"],[2,"so I will comfort you."],[2,"You will be comforted in Jerusalem.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You will see it, and your heart shall rejoice,"],[2,"and your bones will flourish like the tender grass."],[1,"The LORD\u2019s hand will be known among his servants;"],[2,"and he will have indignation against his enemies."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, the LORD will come with fire,"],[2,"and his chariots will be like the whirlwind;"],[1,"to give his anger with fierceness,"],[2,"and his rebuke with flames of fire."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD will execute judgment by fire and by his sword on all flesh;"],[2,"and those slain by the LORD will be many."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThose who sanctify themselves and purify themselves to go to the gardens, following one in the middle, eating pig\u2019s meat, abominable things, and the mouse, they shall come to an end together,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor I know their works and their thoughts. The time comes that I will gather all nations and languages, and they will come, and will see my glory."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI will set a sign among them, and I will send those who escape of them to the nations, to Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, who draw the bow, to Tubal and Javan, to far-away islands, who have not heard my fame, nor have seen my glory; and they shall declare my glory among the nations."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They shall bring all your brothers out of all the nations for an offering to the LORD, on horses, in chariots, in litters, on mules, and on camels, to my holy mountain Jerusalem, says the LORD, as the children of Israel bring their offering in a clean vessel into the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Of them I will also select priests and Levites,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor as the new heavens and the new earth, which I will make, shall remain before me,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cso your offspring and your name shall remain."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"It shall happen that from one new moon to another, and from one Sabbath to another, all flesh will come to worship before me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cThey will go out, and look at the dead bodies of the men who have transgressed against me; for their worm will not die, nor will their fire be quenched, and they will be loathsome to all mankind.\u201d"]]}]]}},1294,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,i){h.exports={book:"Jer",name:"Jeremiah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The words of Jeremiah the son of Hilkiah, one of the priests who were in Anathoth in the land of Benjamin."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to him in the days of Josiah the son of Amon, king of Judah, in the thirteenth year of his reign."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It came also in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, to the end of the eleventh year of Zedekiah, the son of Josiah, king of Judah, to the carrying away of Jerusalem captive in the fifth month."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBefore I formed you in the womb, I knew you."],[2,"Before you were born, I sanctified you."],[2,"I have appointed you a prophet to the nations.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cAh, Lord GOD! Behold, I don\u2019t know how to speak; for I am a child.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d","\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But the LORD said to me, \u201cDon\u2019t say, \u2018I am a child;\u2019 for you must go to whomever I send you, and you must say whatever I command you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be afraid because of them, for I am with you to rescue you,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD stretched out his hand and touched my mouth. Then the LORD said to me, \u201cBehold, I have put my words in your mouth."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Behold, I have today set you over the nations and over the kingdoms, to uproot and to tear down, to destroy and to overthrow, to build and to plant.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying, \u201cJeremiah, what do you see?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cI see a branch of an almond tree.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to me, \u201cYou have seen well; for I watch over my word to perform it.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me the second time, saying, \u201cWhat do you see?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cI see a boiling cauldron; and it is tipping away from the north.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to me, \u201cOut of the north, evil will break out on all the inhabitants of the land."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For behold, I will call all the families of the kingdoms of the north,\u201d says the LORD."],[1,"\u201cThey will come, and they will each set his throne at the entrance of the gates of Jerusalem,"],[2,"and against all its walls all around, and against all the cities of Judah."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I will utter my judgments against them concerning all their wickedness,"],[2,"in that they have forsaken me,"],[2,"and have burned incense to other gods,"],[2,"and worshiped the works of their own hands."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou therefore put your belt on your waist, arise, and say to them all that I command you. Don\u2019t be dismayed at them, lest I dismay you before them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For behold, I have made you today a fortified city, an iron pillar, and bronze walls against the whole land\u2014against the kings of Judah, against its princes, against its priests, and against the people of the land."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They will fight against you, but they will not prevail against you; for I am with you\u201d, says the LORD, \u201cto rescue you.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cGo and proclaim in the ears of Jerusalem, saying, \u2018The LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cI remember for you the kindness of your youth,"],[2,"your love as a bride,"],[1,"how you went after me in the wilderness,"],[2,"in a land that was not sown."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel was holiness to the LORD,"],[2,"the first fruits of his increase."],[1,"All who devour him will be held guilty."],[2,"Evil will come on them,\u201d\u2019 says the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Hear the LORD\u2019s word, O house of Jacob, and all the families of the house of Israel!"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cWhat unrighteousness have your fathers found in me,"],[2,"that they have gone far from me,"],[1,"and have walked after worthless vanity,"],[2,"and have become worthless?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They didn\u2019t say, \u2018Where is the LORD who brought us up out of the land of Egypt,"],[2,"who led us through the wilderness,"],[2,"through a land of deserts and of pits,"],[2,"through a land of drought and of the shadow of death,"],[2,"through a land that no one passed through,"],[2,"and where no man lived?\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I brought you into a plentiful land"],[2,"to eat its fruit and its goodness;"],[1,"but when you entered, you defiled my land,"],[2,"and made my heritage an abomination."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The priests didn\u2019t say, \u2018Where is the LORD?\u2019"],[2,"and those who handle the law didn\u2019t know me."],[1,"The rulers also transgressed against me,"],[2,"and the prophets prophesied by Baal"],[2,"and followed things that do not profit."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore I will yet contend with you,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cand I will contend with your children\u2019s children."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For pass over to the islands of Kittim, and see."],[2,"Send to Kedar, and consider diligently,"],[2,"and see if there has been such a thing."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Has a nation changed its gods,"],[2,"which really are no gods?"],[2,"But my people have changed their glory for that which doesn\u2019t profit."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBe astonished, you heavens, at this"],[2,"and be horribly afraid."],[2,"Be very desolate,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor my people have committed two evils:"],[2,"they have forsaken me, the spring of living waters,"],[2,"and cut out cisterns for themselves: broken cisterns that can\u2019t hold water."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Is Israel a slave?"],[2,"Is he born into slavery?"],[2,"Why has he become a captive?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The young lions have roared at him and raised their voices."],[2,"They have made his land waste."],[2,"His cities are burned up, without inhabitant."]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"The children also of Memphis and Tahpanhes have broken the crown of your head."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHaven\u2019t you brought this on yourself,"],[2,"in that you have forsaken the LORD your God, when he led you by the way?"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Now what do you gain by going to Egypt, to drink the waters of the Shihor?"],[2,"Or why do you go on the way to Assyria, to drink the waters of the River?"]],f:["i.e., the Euphrates River"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYour own wickedness will correct you,"],[2,"and your backsliding will rebuke you."],[1,"Know therefore and see that it is an evil and bitter thing,"],[2,"that you have forsaken the LORD your God,"],[2,"and that my fear is not in you,\u201d says the Lord, GOD of Armies."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor long ago I broke off your yoke,"],[2,"and burst your bonds."],[1,"You said, \u2018I will not serve;\u2019"],[2,"for on every high hill and under every green tree you bowed yourself,"],[2,"playing the prostitute."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet I had planted you a noble vine,"],[2,"a pure and faithful seed."],[2,"How then have you turned into the degenerate branches of a foreign vine to me?"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"For though you wash yourself with lye,"],[2,"and use much soap,"],[2,"yet your iniquity is marked before me,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow can you say, \u2018I am not defiled."],[2,"I have not gone after the Baals\u2019?"],[1,"See your way in the valley."],[2,"Know what you have done."],[1,"You are a swift dromedary traversing her ways,"]]},{v:24,l:[[1,"a wild donkey used to the wilderness, that sniffs the wind in her craving."],[2,"When she is in heat, who can turn her away?"],[2,"All those who seek her will not weary themselves. In her month, they will find her."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cKeep your feet from being bare,"],[2,"and your throat from thirst."],[1,"But you said, \u2018It is in vain."],[2,"No, for I have loved strangers,"],[2,"and I will go after them.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"As the thief is ashamed when he is found,"],[2,"so the house of Israel is ashamed\u2014"],[2,"they, their kings, their princes, their priests, and their prophets,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"who tell wood, \u2018You are my father,\u2019"],[2,"and a stone, \u2018You have given birth to me,\u2019"],[1,"for they have turned their back to me,"],[2,"and not their face,"],[2,"but in the time of their trouble they will say, \u2018Arise, and save us!\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut where are your gods that you have made for yourselves?"],[2,"Let them arise, if they can save you in the time of your trouble,"],[2,"for you have as many gods as you have towns, O Judah."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhy will you contend with me?"],[2,"You all have transgressed against me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have struck your children in vain."],[2,"They received no correction."],[1,"Your own sword has devoured your prophets,"],[2,"like a destroying lion."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Generation, consider the LORD\u2019s word."],[2,"Have I been a wilderness to Israel?"],[2,"Or a land of thick darkness?"],[1,"Why do my people say, \u2018We have broken loose."],[2,"We will come to you no more\u2019?"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCan a virgin forget her ornaments,"],[2,"or a bride her attire?"],[2,"Yet my people have forgotten me for days without number."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"How well you prepare your way to seek love!"],[2,"Therefore you have even taught the wicked women your ways."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Also the blood of the souls of the innocent poor is found in your skirts."],[2,"You didn\u2019t find them breaking in,"],[2,"but it is because of all these things."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYet you said, \u2018I am innocent."],[2,"Surely his anger has turned away from me.\u2019"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I will judge you,"],[2,"because you say, \u2018I have not sinned.\u2019"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you go about so much to change your ways?"],[2,"You will be ashamed of Egypt also,"],[2,"as you were ashamed of Assyria."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"You will also leave that place with your hands on your head;"],[2,"for the LORD has rejected those in whom you trust,"],[2,"and you won\u2019t prosper with them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey say, \u2018If a man puts away his wife, and she goes from him, and becomes another man\u2019s, should he return to her again?\u2019 Wouldn\u2019t that land be greatly polluted? But you have played the prostitute with many lovers; yet return again to me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cLift up your eyes to the bare heights, and see! Where have you not been lain with? You have sat waiting for them by the road, as an Arabian in the wilderness. You have polluted the land with your prostitution and with your wickedness."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore the showers have been withheld and there has been no latter rain; yet you have had a prostitute\u2019s forehead and you refused to be ashamed."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Will you not from this time cry to me, \u2018My Father, you are the guide of my youth!\u2019?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Will he retain his anger forever? Will he keep it to the end?\u2019 Behold, you have spoken and have done evil things, and have had your way.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover, the LORD said to me in the days of Josiah the king, \u201cHave you seen that which backsliding Israel has done? She has gone up on every high mountain and under every green tree, and has played the prostitute there."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I said after she had done all these things, \u2018She will return to me;\u2019 but she didn\u2019t return, and her treacherous sister Judah saw it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I saw when, for this very cause, that backsliding Israel had committed adultery, I had put her away and given her a certificate of divorce, yet treacherous Judah, her sister, had no fear, but she also went and played the prostitute."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Because she took her prostitution lightly, the land was polluted, and she committed adultery with stones and with wood."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Yet for all this her treacherous sister, Judah, has not returned to me with her whole heart, but only in pretense,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cBacksliding Israel has shown herself more righteous than treacherous Judah."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Go, and proclaim these words toward the north, and say, \u2018Return, you backsliding Israel,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018I will not look in anger on you, for I am merciful,\u2019 says the LORD. \u2018I will not keep anger forever."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Only acknowledge your iniquity, that you have transgressed against the LORD your God, and have scattered your ways to the strangers under every green tree, and you have not obeyed my voice,\u2019\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"\u201cReturn, backsliding children,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cfor I am a husband to you. I will take one of you from a city, and two from a family, and I will bring you to Zion."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I will give you shepherds according to my heart, who will feed you with knowledge and understanding."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"It will come to pass, when you are multiplied and increased in the land in those days,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthey will no longer say, \u2018the ark of the LORD\u2019s covenant!\u2019 It will not come to mind. They won\u2019t remember it. They won\u2019t miss it, nor will another be made."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"At that time they will call Jerusalem \u2018The LORD\u2019s Throne;\u2019 and all the nations will be gathered to it, to the LORD\u2019s name, to Jerusalem. They will no longer walk after the stubbornness of their evil heart."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In those days the house of Judah will walk with the house of Israel, and they will come together out of the land of the north to the land that I gave for an inheritance to your fathers."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut I said, \u2018How I desire to put you among the children, and give you a pleasant land, a goodly heritage of the armies of the nations!\u2019 and I said, \u2018You shall call me \u201cMy Father\u201d, and shall not turn away from following me.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSurely as a wife treacherously departs from her husband, so you have dealt treacherously with me, house of Israel,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"A voice is heard on the bare heights, the weeping and the petitions of the children of Israel; because they have perverted their way, they have forgotten the LORD their God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Return, you backsliding children, and I will heal your backsliding."],[0,"\u201cBehold, we have come to you; for you are the LORD our God."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Truly help from the hills, the tumult on the mountains, is in vain. Truly the salvation of Israel is in the LORD our God."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But the shameful thing has devoured the labor of our fathers from our youth, their flocks and their herds, their sons and their daughters."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Let us lie down in our shame, and let our confusion cover us; for we have sinned against the LORD our God, we and our fathers, from our youth even to this day. We have not obeyed the LORD our God\u2019s voice.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf you will return, Israel,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cif you will return to me, and if you will put away your abominations out of my sight; then you will not be removed;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and you will swear, \u2018As the LORD lives,\u2019 in truth, in justice, and in righteousness. The nations will bless themselves in him, and they will glory in him.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says to the men of Judah and to Jerusalem, \u201cBreak up your fallow ground, and don\u2019t sow among thorns."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Circumcise yourselves to the LORD, and take away the foreskins of your heart, you men of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem; lest my wrath go out like fire, and burn so that no one can quench it, because of the evil of your doings."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Declare in Judah, and publish in Jerusalem; and say, \u2018Blow the trumpet in the land!\u2019 Cry aloud and say, \u2018Assemble yourselves! Let\u2019s go into the fortified cities!\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Set up a standard toward Zion. Flee for safety! Don\u2019t wait; for I will bring evil from the north, and a great destruction.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"A lion has gone up from his thicket, and a destroyer of nations. He is on his way. He has gone out from his place, to make your land desolate, that your cities be laid waste, without inhabitant."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For this, clothe yourself with sackcloth, lament and wail; for the fierce anger of the LORD hasn\u2019t turned back from us."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cIt will happen at that day,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat the heart of the king will perish, along with the heart of the princes. The priests will be astonished, and the prophets will wonder.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cAh, Lord GOD! Surely you have greatly deceived this people and Jerusalem, saying, \u2018You will have peace;\u2019 whereas the sword reaches to the heart.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time it will be said to this people and to Jerusalem, \u201cA hot wind blows from the bare heights in the wilderness toward the daughter of my people, not to winnow, nor to cleanse."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"A full wind from these will come for me. Now I will also utter judgments against them.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, he will come up as clouds, and his chariots will be as the whirlwind. His horses are swifter than eagles. Woe to us! For we are ruined."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Jerusalem, wash your heart from wickedness, that you may be saved. How long will your evil thoughts lodge within you?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For a voice declares from Dan, and publishes evil from the hills of Ephraim:"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cTell the nations, behold, publish against Jerusalem, \u2018Watchers come from a far country, and raise their voice against the cities of Judah."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"As keepers of a field, they are against her all around, because she has been rebellious against me,\u2019\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cYour way and your doings have brought these things to you. This is your wickedness, for it is bitter, for it reaches to your heart.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"My anguish, my anguish! I am pained at my very heart! My heart trembles within me. I can\u2019t hold my peace, because you have heard, O my soul, the sound of the trumpet, the alarm of war."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Destruction on destruction is decreed, for the whole land is laid waste. Suddenly my tents are destroyed, and my curtains gone in a moment."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"How long will I see the standard and hear the sound of the trumpet?"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor my people are foolish. They don\u2019t know me. They are foolish children, and they have no understanding. They are skillful in doing evil, but they don\u2019t know how to do good.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I saw the earth and, behold, it was waste and void, and the heavens, and they had no light."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I saw the mountains, and behold, they trembled, and all the hills moved back and forth."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I saw, and behold, there was no man, and all the birds of the sky had fled."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I saw, and behold, the fruitful field was a wilderness, and all its cities were broken down at the presence of the LORD, before his fierce anger."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For the LORD says, \u201cThe whole land will be a desolation; yet I will not make a full end."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For this the earth will mourn, and the heavens above be black, because I have spoken it. I have planned it, and I have not repented, neither will I turn back from it.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Every city flees for the noise of the horsemen and archers. They go into the thickets and climb up on the rocks. Every city is forsaken, and not a man dwells therein."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You, when you are made desolate, what will you do? Though you clothe yourself with scarlet, though you deck yourself with ornaments of gold, though you enlarge your eyes with makeup, you make yourself beautiful in vain. Your lovers despise you. They seek your life."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For I have heard a voice as of a woman in travail, the anguish as of her who gives birth to her first child, the voice of the daughter of Zion, who gasps for breath, who spreads her hands, saying, \u201cWoe is me now! For my soul faints before the murderers.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cRun back and forth through the streets of Jerusalem, and see now, and know, and seek in its wide places, if you can find a man, if there is anyone who does justly, who seeks truth, then I will pardon her."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Though they say, \u2018As the LORD lives,\u2019 surely they swear falsely.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"O LORD, don\u2019t your eyes look on truth? You have stricken them, but they were not grieved. You have consumed them, but they have refused to receive correction. They have made their faces harder than a rock. They have refused to return."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cSurely these are poor. They are foolish; for they don\u2019t know the LORD\u2019s way, nor the law of their God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I will go to the great men and will speak to them, for they know the way of the LORD, and the law of their God.\u201d But these with one accord have broken the yoke, and burst the bonds."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore a lion out of the forest will kill them. A wolf of the evenings will destroy them. A leopard will watch against their cities. Everyone who goes out there will be torn in pieces, because their transgressions are many and their backsliding has increased."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHow can I pardon you? Your children have forsaken me, and sworn by what are no gods. When I had fed them to the full, they committed adultery, and assembled themselves in troops at the prostitutes\u2019 houses."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They were as fed horses roaming at large. Everyone neighed after his neighbor\u2019s wife."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Shouldn\u2019t I punish them for these things?\u201d says the LORD. \u201cShouldn\u2019t my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cGo up on her walls, and destroy, but don\u2019t make a full end. Take away her branches, for they are not the LORD\u2019s."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the house of Israel and the house of Judah have dealt very treacherously against me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"They have denied the LORD, and said, \u201cIt is not he. Evil won\u2019t come on us. We won\u2019t see sword or famine."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The prophets will become wind, and the word is not in them. Thus it will be done to them.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD, the God of Armies says, \u201cBecause you speak this word, behold, I will make my words in your mouth fire, and this people wood, and it will devour them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Behold, I will bring a nation on you from far away, house of Israel,\u201d says the LORD. \u201cIt is a mighty nation. It is an ancient nation, a nation whose language you don\u2019t know and don\u2019t understand what they say."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Their quiver is an open tomb. They are all mighty men."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They will eat up your harvest and your bread, which your sons and your daughters should eat. They will eat up your flocks and your herds. They will eat up your vines and your fig trees. They will beat down your fortified cities in which you trust with the sword."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut even in those days,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cI will not make a full end of you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"It will happen when you say, \u2018Why has the LORD our God done all these things to us?\u2019 Then you shall say to them, \u2018Just as you have forsaken me and served foreign gods in your land, so you will serve strangers in a land that is not yours.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDeclare this in the house of Jacob, and publish it in Judah, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u2018Hear this now, foolish people without understanding, who have eyes, and don\u2019t see, who have ears, and don\u2019t hear:"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you fear me?\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018Won\u2019t you tremble at my presence, who have placed the sand for the bound of the sea by a perpetual decree, that it can\u2019t pass it? Though its waves toss themselves, yet they can\u2019t prevail. Though they roar, they still can\u2019t pass over it.\u2019"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut this people has a revolting and a rebellious heart. They have revolted and gone."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They don\u2019t say in their heart, \u2018Let\u2019s now fear the LORD our God, who gives rain, both the former and the latter, in its season, who preserves to us the appointed weeks of the harvest.\u2019"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYour iniquities have turned away these things, and your sins have withheld good from you."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For wicked men are found among my people. They watch, as fowlers lie in wait. They set a trap. They catch men."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"As a cage is full of birds, so are their houses full of deceit. Therefore they have become great, and grew rich."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They have grown fat. They shine; yes, they excel in deeds of wickedness. They don\u2019t plead the cause, the cause of the fatherless, that they may prosper; and they don\u2019t defend the rights of the needy."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cShouldn\u2019t I punish for these things?\u201d says the LORD. \u201cShouldn\u2019t my soul be avenged on such a nation as this?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAn astonishing and horrible thing has happened in the land."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The prophets prophesy falsely, and the priests rule by their own authority; and my people love to have it so. What will you do in the end of it?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFlee for safety, you children of Benjamin, out of the middle of Jerusalem! Blow the trumpet in Tekoa and raise up a signal on Beth Haccherem, for evil looks out from the north with a great destruction."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will cut off the beautiful and delicate one, the daughter of Zion."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Shepherds with their flocks will come to her. They will pitch their tents against her all around. They will feed everyone in his place.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cPrepare war against her! Arise! Let\u2019s go up at noon. Woe to us! For the day declines, for the shadows of the evening are stretched out."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Arise! Let\u2019s go up by night, and let\u2019s destroy her palaces.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies said, \u201cCut down trees, and cast up a mound against Jerusalem. This is the city to be visited. She is filled with oppression within herself."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"As a well produces its waters, so she produces her wickedness. Violence and destruction is heard in her. Sickness and wounds are continually before me."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Be instructed, Jerusalem, lest my soul be alienated from you, lest I make you a desolation, an uninhabited land.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says, \u201cThey will thoroughly glean the remnant of Israel like a vine. Turn again your hand as a grape gatherer into the baskets.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"To whom should I speak and testify, that they may hear? Behold, their ear is uncircumcised, and they can\u2019t listen. Behold, the LORD\u2019s word has become a reproach to them. They have no delight in it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore I am full of the LORD\u2019s wrath. I am weary with holding it in."],[1,"\u201cPour it out on the children in the street,"],[2,"and on the assembly of young men together;"],[1,"for even the husband with the wife will be taken,"],[2,"the aged with him who is full of days."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Their houses will be turned to others,"],[2,"their fields and their wives together;"],[1,"for I will stretch out my hand on the inhabitants of the land, says the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor from their least even to their greatest, everyone is given to covetousness."],[2,"From the prophet even to the priest, everyone deals falsely."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They have healed also the hurt of my people superficially,"],[2,"saying, \u2018Peace, peace!\u2019 when there is no peace."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Were they ashamed when they had committed abomination?"],[2,"No, they were not at all ashamed, neither could they blush."],[1,"Therefore they will fall among those who fall."],[2,"When I visit them, they will be cast down,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u201cStand in the ways and see, and ask for the old paths, \u2018Where is the good way?\u2019 and walk in it, and you will find rest for your souls. But they said, \u2018We will not walk in it.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I set watchmen over you, saying, \u2018Listen to the sound of the trumpet!\u2019 But they said, \u2018We will not listen!\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Therefore hear, you nations, and know, congregation, what is among them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Hear, earth! Behold, I will bring evil on this people, even the fruit of their thoughts, because they have not listened to my words; and as for my law, they have rejected it."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"To what purpose does frankincense from Sheba come to me, and the sweet cane from a far country? Your burnt offerings are not acceptable, and your sacrifices are not pleasing to me.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says, \u201cBehold, I will lay stumbling blocks before this people. The fathers and the sons together will stumble against them. The neighbor and his friend will perish.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u201cBehold, a people comes from the north country. A great nation will be stirred up from the uttermost parts of the earth."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They take hold of bow and spear. They are cruel, and have no mercy. Their voice roars like the sea, and they ride on horses, everyone set in array, as a man to the battle, against you, daughter of Zion.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"We have heard its report. Our hands become feeble. Anguish has taken hold of us, and pains as of a woman in labor."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t go out into the field or walk by the way; for the sword of the enemy and terror are on every side."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Daughter of my people, clothe yourself with sackcloth, and wallow in ashes! Mourn, as for an only son, most bitter lamentation, for the destroyer will suddenly come on us."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI have made you a tester of metals and a fortress among my people, that you may know and try their way."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They are all grievous rebels, going around to slander. They are bronze and iron. All of them deal corruptly."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The bellows blow fiercely. The lead is consumed in the fire. In vain they go on refining, for the wicked are not plucked away."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Men will call them rejected silver, because the LORD has rejected them.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cStand in the gate of the LORD\u2019s house, and proclaim this word there, and say, \u2018Hear the LORD\u2019s word, all you of Judah, who enter in at these gates to worship the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says, \u201cAmend your ways and your doings, and I will cause you to dwell in this place."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t trust in lying words, saying, \u2018The LORD\u2019s temple, the LORD\u2019s temple, the LORD\u2019s temple, are these.\u2019"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For if you thoroughly amend your ways and your doings, if you thoroughly execute justice between a man and his neighbor;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"if you don\u2019t oppress the foreigner, the fatherless, and the widow, and don\u2019t shed innocent blood in this place, and don\u2019t walk after other gods to your own hurt,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"then I will cause you to dwell in this place, in the land that I gave to your fathers, from of old even forever more."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, you trust in lying words that can\u2019t profit."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Will you steal, murder, commit adultery, swear falsely, burn incense to Baal, and walk after other gods that you have not known,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"then come and stand before me in this house, which is called by my name, and say, \u2018We are delivered,\u2019 that you may do all these abominations?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Has this house, which is called by my name, become a den of robbers in your eyes? Behold, I myself have seen it,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut go now to my place which was in Shiloh, where I caused my name to dwell at the first, and see what I did to it for the wickedness of my people Israel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now, because you have done all these works,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cand I spoke to you, rising up early and speaking, but you didn\u2019t hear; and I called you, but you didn\u2019t answer;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"therefore I will do to the house which is called by my name, in which you trust, and to the place which I gave to you and to your fathers, as I did to Shiloh."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I will cast you out of my sight, as I have cast out all your brothers, even the whole offspring of Ephraim."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore don\u2019t pray for this people. Don\u2019t lift up a cry or prayer for them or make intercession to me; for I will not hear you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you see what they do in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The children gather wood, and the fathers kindle the fire, and the women knead the dough, to make cakes to the queen of the sky, and to pour out drink offerings to other gods, that they may provoke me to anger."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Do they provoke me to anger?\u201d says the LORD. \u201cDon\u2019t they provoke themselves, to the confusion of their own faces?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, my anger and my wrath will be poured out on this place, on man, on animal, on the trees of the field, and on the fruit of the ground; and it will burn and will not be quenched.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says: \u201cAdd your burnt offerings to your sacrifices and eat meat."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For I didn\u2019t speak to your fathers or command them in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt concerning burnt offerings or sacrifices;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"but this thing I commanded them, saying, \u2018Listen to my voice, and I will be your God, and you shall be my people. Walk in all the way that I command you, that it may be well with you.\u2019"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But they didn\u2019t listen or turn their ear, but walked in their own counsels and in the stubbornness of their evil heart, and went backward, and not forward."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Since the day that your fathers came out of the land of Egypt to this day, I have sent to you all my servants the prophets, daily rising up early and sending them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Yet they didn\u2019t listen to me or incline their ear, but made their neck stiff. They did worse than their fathers."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall speak all these words to them, but they will not listen to you. You shall also call to them, but they will not answer you."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You shall tell them, \u2018This is the nation that has not listened to the LORD their God\u2019s voice, nor received instruction. Truth has perished, and is cut off from their mouth.\u2019"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Cut off your hair, and throw it away, and take up a lamentation on the bare heights; for the LORD has rejected and forsaken the generation of his wrath."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the children of Judah have done that which is evil in my sight,\u201d says the LORD. \u201cThey have set their abominations in the house which is called by my name, to defile it."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They have built the high places of Topheth, which is in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn their sons and their daughters in the fire, which I didn\u2019t command, nor did it come into my mind."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Therefore behold, the days come\u201d, says the LORD, \u201cthat it will no more be called \u2018Topheth\u2019 or \u2018The valley of the son of Hinnom\u2019, but \u2018The valley of Slaughter\u2019; for they will bury in Topheth until there is no place to bury."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The dead bodies of this people will be food for the birds of the sky, and for the animals of the earth. No one will frighten them away."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Then I will cause to cease from the cities of Judah and from the streets of Jerusalem the voice of mirth and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom and the voice of the bride; for the land will become a waste.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAt that time,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthey will bring the bones of the kings of Judah, the bones of his princes, the bones of the priests, the bones of the prophets, and the bones of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, out of their graves."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They will spread them before the sun, the moon, and all the army of the sky, which they have loved, which they have served, after which they have walked, which they have sought, and which they have worshiped. They will not be gathered or be buried. They will be like dung on the surface of the earth."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Death will be chosen rather than life by all the residue that remain of this evil family, that remain in all the places where I have driven them,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover you shall tell them, \u2018The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201c\u2018Do men fall, and not rise up again?"],[2,"Does one turn away, and not return?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Why then have the people of Jerusalem fallen back by a perpetual backsliding?"],[2,"They cling to deceit."],[2,"They refuse to return."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I listened and heard, but they didn\u2019t say what is right."],[2,"No one repents of his wickedness, saying, \u201cWhat have I done?\u201d"],[1,"Everyone turns to his course,"],[2,"as a horse that rushes headlong in the battle."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, the stork in the sky knows her appointed times."],[2,"The turtledove, the swallow, and the crane observe the time of their coming;"],[2,"but my people don\u2019t know the LORD\u2019s law."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018How do you say, \u201cWe are wise, and the LORD\u2019s law is with us\u201d?"],[2,"But, behold, the false pen of the scribes has made that a lie."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The wise men are disappointed."],[2,"They are dismayed and trapped."],[1,"Behold, they have rejected the LORD\u2019s word."],[2,"What kind of wisdom is in them?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will give their wives to others"],[2,"and their fields to those who will possess them."],[1,"For everyone from the least even to the greatest is given to covetousness;"],[2,"from the prophet even to the priest everyone deals falsely."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They have healed the hurt of the daughter of my people slightly, saying,"],[2,"\u201cPeace, peace,\u201d when there is no peace."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Were they ashamed when they had committed abomination?"],[2,"No, they were not at all ashamed."],[2,"They couldn\u2019t blush."],[1,"Therefore they will fall among those who fall."],[2,"In the time of their visitation they will be cast down, says the LORD."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018I will utterly consume them, says the LORD."],[2,"No grapes will be on the vine,"],[2,"no figs on the fig tree,"],[2,"and the leaf will fade."],[1,"The things that I have given them"],[2,"will pass away from them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhy do we sit still?"],[2,"Assemble yourselves!"],[2,"Let\u2019s enter into the fortified cities,"],[2,"and let\u2019s be silent there;"],[1,"for the LORD our God has put us to silence,"],[2,"and given us poisoned water to drink,"],[2,"because we have sinned against the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"We looked for peace, but no good came;"],[2,"and for a time of healing, and behold, dismay!"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The snorting of his horses is heard from Dan."],[2,"The whole land trembles at the sound of the neighing of his strong ones;"],[1,"for they have come, and have devoured the land and all that is in it,"],[2,"the city and those who dwell therein.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor, behold, I will send serpents,"],[2,"adders among you,"],[2,"which will not be charmed;"],[2,"and they will bite you,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that I could comfort myself against sorrow!"],[2,"My heart is faint within me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the voice of the cry of the daughter of my people from a land that is very far off:"],[2,"\u201cIsn\u2019t the LORD in Zion?"],[2,"Isn\u2019t her King in her?\u201d"],[1,"\u201cWhy have they provoked me to anger with their engraved images,"],[2,"and with foreign idols?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe harvest is past."],[2,"The summer has ended,"],[2,"and we are not saved.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For the hurt of the daughter of my people, I am hurt."],[2,"I mourn."],[2,"Dismay has taken hold of me."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Is there no balm in Gilead?"],[2,"Is there no physician there?"],[1,"Why then isn\u2019t the health of the daughter of my people recovered?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that my head were waters,"],[2,"and my eyes a spring of tears,"],[1,"that I might weep day and night"],[2,"for the slain of the daughter of my people!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Oh that I had in the wilderness"],[2,"a lodging place of wayfaring men,"],[1,"that I might leave my people"],[2,"and go from them!"],[1,"For they are all adulterers,"],[2,"an assembly of treacherous men."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThey bend their tongue,"],[2,"as their bow, for falsehood."],[1,"They have grown strong in the land,"],[2,"but not for truth;"],[1,"for they proceed from evil to evil,"],[2,"and they don\u2019t know me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEveryone beware of his neighbor,"],[2,"and don\u2019t trust in any brother;"],[1,"for every brother will utterly supplant,"],[2,"and every neighbor will go around like a slanderer."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Friends deceive each other,"],[2,"and will not speak the truth."],[1,"They have taught their tongue to speak lies."],[2,"They weary themselves committing iniquity."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Your habitation is in the middle of deceit."],[2,"Through deceit, they refuse to know me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD of Armies says,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I will melt them and test them;"],[2,"for how should I deal with the daughter of my people?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Their tongue is a deadly arrow."],[2,"It speaks deceit."],[1,"One speaks peaceably to his neighbor with his mouth,"],[2,"but in his heart, he waits to ambush him."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Shouldn\u2019t I punish them for these things?\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cShouldn\u2019t my soul be avenged on a nation such as this?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I will weep and wail for the mountains,"],[2,"and lament for the pastures of the wilderness,"],[1,"because they are burned up, so that no one passes through;"],[2,"Men can\u2019t hear the voice of the livestock."],[1,"Both the birds of the sky and the animals have fled."],[2,"They are gone."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will make Jerusalem heaps,"],[2,"a dwelling place of jackals."],[1,"I will make the cities of Judah a desolation,"],[2,"without inhabitant.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Who is wise enough to understand this? Who is he to whom the mouth of the LORD has spoken, that he may declare it? Why has the land perished and burned up like a wilderness, so that no one passes through?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u201cBecause they have forsaken my law which I set before them, and have not obeyed my voice or walked in my ways,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but have walked after the stubbornness of their own heart and after the Baals, which their fathers taught them.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says, \u201cBehold, I will feed them, even this people, with wormwood and give them poisoned water to drink."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I will scatter them also among the nations, whom neither they nor their fathers have known. I will send the sword after them, until I have consumed them.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says,"],[1,"\u201cConsider, and call for the mourning women, that they may come."],[2,"Send for the skillful women, that they may come."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them make haste"],[2,"and take up a wailing for us,"],[1,"that our eyes may run down with tears"],[2,"and our eyelids gush out with waters."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"For a voice of wailing is heard out of Zion,"],[2,"\u2018How we are ruined!"],[1,"We are greatly confounded"],[2,"because we have forsaken the land,"],[2,"because they have cast down our dwellings.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet hear the LORD\u2019s word, you women."],[2,"Let your ear receive the word of his mouth."],[1,"Teach your daughters wailing."],[2,"Everyone teach her neighbor a lamentation."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For death has come up into our windows."],[2,"It has entered into our palaces"],[1,"to cut off the children from outside,"],[2,"and the young men from the streets."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Speak, \u201cThe LORD says,"],[1,"\u201c\u2018The dead bodies of men will fall as dung on the open field,"],[2,"and as the handful after the harvester."],[2,"No one will gather them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t let the wise man glory in his wisdom."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the mighty man glory in his might."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the rich man glory in his riches."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"But let him who glories glory in this,"],[2,"that he has understanding, and knows me,"],[1,"that I am the LORD who exercises loving kindness, justice, and righteousness on the earth,"],[2,"for I delight in these things,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat I will punish all those who are circumcised only in their flesh:"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Egypt, Judah, Edom, the children of Ammon, Moab, and all who have the corners of their hair cut off, who dwell in the wilderness, for all the nations are uncircumcised, and all the house of Israel are uncircumcised in heart.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hear the word which the LORD speaks to you, house of Israel!"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t learn the way of the nations,"],[2,"and don\u2019t be dismayed at the signs of the sky;"],[2,"for the nations are dismayed at them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For the customs of the peoples are vanity;"],[2,"for one cuts a tree out of the forest,"],[2,"the work of the hands of the workman with the ax."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They deck it with silver and with gold."],[2,"They fasten it with nails and with hammers,"],[2,"so that it can\u2019t move."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They are like a palm tree, of turned work,"],[2,"and don\u2019t speak."],[1,"They must be carried,"],[2,"because they can\u2019t move."],[1,"Don\u2019t be afraid of them;"],[2,"for they can\u2019t do evil,"],[2,"neither is it in them to do good.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no one like you, LORD."],[2,"You are great,"],[2,"and your name is great in might."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Who shouldn\u2019t fear you,"],[2,"King of the nations?"],[2,"For it belongs to you."],[1,"Because among all the wise men of the nations,"],[2,"and in all their royal estate,"],[2,"there is no one like you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But they are together brutish and foolish,"],[2,"instructed by idols!"],[2,"It is just wood."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"There is silver beaten into plates, which is brought from Tarshish,"],[2,"and gold from Uphaz,"],[2,"the work of the engraver and of the hands of the goldsmith."],[1,"Their clothing is blue and purple."],[2,"They are all the work of skillful men."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But the LORD is the true God."],[2,"He is the living God,"],[2,"and an everlasting King."],[1,"At his wrath, the earth trembles."],[2,"The nations aren\u2019t able to withstand his indignation."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall say this to them: \u2018The gods that have not made the heavens and the earth will perish from the earth, and from under the heavens.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"God has made the earth by his power."],[2,"He has established the world by his wisdom,"],[2,"and by his understanding has he stretched out the heavens."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"When he utters his voice,"],[2,"the waters in the heavens roar,"],[2,"and he causes the vapors to ascend from the ends of the earth."],[1,"He makes lightnings for the rain,"],[2,"and brings the wind out of his treasuries."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Every man has become brutish and without knowledge."],[2,"Every goldsmith is disappointed by his engraved image;"],[1,"for his molten image is falsehood,"],[2,"and there is no breath in them."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"They are vanity, a work of delusion."],[2,"In the time of their visitation they will perish."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The portion of Jacob is not like these;"],[2,"for he is the maker of all things;"],[1,"and Israel is the tribe of his inheritance."],[2,"The LORD of Armies is his name."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Gather up your wares out of the land,"],[2,"you who live under siege."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD says,"],[2,"\u201cBehold, I will sling out the inhabitants of the land at this time,"],[2,"and will distress them, that they may feel it.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe is me because of my injury!"],[2,"My wound is serious;"],[1,"but I said,"],[2,"\u201cTruly this is my grief, and I must bear it.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My tent has been destroyed,"],[2,"and all my cords are broken."],[1,"My children have gone away from me, and they are no more."],[2,"There is no one to spread my tent any more,"],[2,"to set up my curtains."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"For the shepherds have become brutish,"],[2,"and have not inquired of the LORD."],[1,"Therefore they have not prospered,"],[2,"and all their flocks have scattered."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The voice of news, behold, it comes,"],[2,"and a great commotion out of the north country,"],[1,"to make the cities of Judah a desolation,"],[2,"a dwelling place of jackals."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, I know that the way of man is not in himself."],[2,"It is not in man who walks to direct his steps."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, correct me, but gently;"],[2,"not in your anger,"],[2,"lest you reduce me to nothing."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Pour out your wrath on the nations that don\u2019t know you,"],[2,"and on the families that don\u2019t call on your name;"],[1,"for they have devoured Jacob."],[2,"Yes, they have devoured him, consumed him,"],[2,"and have laid waste his habitation."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cHear the words of this covenant, and speak to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and say to them, the LORD, the God of Israel says: \u2018Cursed is the man who doesn\u2019t hear the words of this covenant,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"which I commanded your fathers in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, out of the iron furnace,\u2019 saying, \u2018Obey my voice and do them, according to all which I command you; so you shall be my people, and I will be your God;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"that I may establish the oath which I swore to your fathers, to give them a land flowing with milk and honey,\u2019 as it is today.\u201d"],[0,"Then I answered, and said, \u201cAmen, LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cProclaim all these words in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, saying, \u2018Hear the words of this covenant, and do them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For I earnestly protested to your fathers in the day that I brought them up out of the land of Egypt, even to this day, rising early and protesting, saying, \u201cObey my voice.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Yet they didn\u2019t obey, nor turn their ear, but everyone walked in the stubbornness of their evil heart. Therefore I brought on them all the words of this covenant, which I commanded them to do, but they didn\u2019t do them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cA conspiracy is found among the men of Judah, and among the inhabitants of Jerusalem."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They have turned back to the iniquities of their forefathers, who refused to hear my words. They have gone after other gods to serve them. The house of Israel and the house of Judah have broken my covenant which I made with their fathers."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says, \u2018Behold, I will bring evil on them which they will not be able to escape; and they will cry to me, but I will not listen to them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Then the cities of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem will go and cry to the gods to which they offer incense, but they will not save them at all in the time of their trouble."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For according to the number of your cities are your gods, Judah; and according to the number of the streets of Jerusalem you have set up altars to the shameful thing, even altars to burn incense to Baal.\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore don\u2019t pray for this people. Don\u2019t lift up cry or prayer for them; for I will not hear them in the time that they cry to me because of their trouble."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"What has my beloved to do in my house,"],[2,"since she has behaved lewdly with many,"],[2,"and the holy flesh has passed from you?"],[1,"When you do evil,"],[2,"then you rejoice.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD called your name, \u201cA green olive tree,"],[2,"beautiful with goodly fruit.\u201d"],[1,"With the noise of a great roar he has kindled fire on it,"],[2,"and its branches are broken."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies, who planted you, has pronounced evil against you, because of the evil of the house of Israel and of the house of Judah, which they have done to themselves in provoking me to anger by offering incense to Baal."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD gave me knowledge of it, and I knew it. Then you showed me their doings."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But I was like a gentle lamb that is led to the slaughter. I didn\u2019t know that they had devised plans against me, saying,"],[1,"\u201cLet\u2019s destroy the tree with its fruit,"],[2,"and let\u2019s cut him off from the land of the living,"],[2,"that his name may be no more remembered.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"But, LORD of Armies, who judges righteously,"],[2,"who tests the heart and the mind,"],[1,"I will see your vengeance on them;"],[2,"for to you I have revealed my cause."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the LORD says concerning the men of Anathoth, who seek your life, saying, \u2018You shall not prophesy in the LORD\u2019s name, that you not die by our hand\u2019\u2014"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"therefore the LORD of Armies says, \u2018Behold, I will punish them. The young men will die by the sword. Their sons and their daughters will die by famine."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"There will be no remnant to them, for I will bring evil on the men of Anathoth, even the year of their visitation.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"You are righteous, LORD,"],[2,"when I contend with you;"],[1,"yet I would like to plead a case with you."],[2,"Why does the way of the wicked prosper?"],[2,"Why are they all at ease who deal very treacherously?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You have planted them. Yes, they have taken root."],[2,"They grow. Yes, they produce fruit."],[1,"You are near in their mouth,"],[2,"and far from their heart."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, LORD, know me."],[2,"You see me, and test my heart toward you."],[1,"Pull them out like sheep for the slaughter,"],[2,"and prepare them for the day of slaughter."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"How long will the land mourn,"],[2,"and the herbs of the whole country wither?"],[1,"Because of the wickedness of those who dwell therein,"],[2,"the animals and birds are consumed;"],[1,"because they said,"],[2,"\u201cHe won\u2019t see our latter end.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf you have run with the footmen,"],[2,"and they have wearied you,"],[2,"then how can you contend with horses?"],[1,"Though in a land of peace you are secure,"],[2,"yet how will you do in the pride of the Jordan?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For even your brothers, and the house of your father,"],[2,"even they have dealt treacherously with you!"],[2,"Even they have cried aloud after you!"],[1,"Don\u2019t believe them,"],[2,"though they speak beautiful words to you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have forsaken my house."],[2,"I have cast off my heritage."],[2,"I have given the dearly beloved of my soul into the hand of her enemies."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"My heritage has become to me as a lion in the forest."],[2,"She has uttered her voice against me."],[2,"Therefore I have hated her."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Is my heritage to me as a speckled bird of prey?"],[2,"Are the birds of prey against her all around?"],[1,"Go, assemble all the animals of the field."],[2,"Bring them to devour."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Many shepherds have destroyed my vineyard."],[2,"They have trodden my portion under foot."],[2,"They have made my pleasant portion a desolate wilderness."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They have made it a desolation."],[2,"It mourns to me, being desolate."],[1,"The whole land is made desolate,"],[2,"because no one cares."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Destroyers have come on all the bare heights in the wilderness;"],[2,"for the sword of the LORD devours from the one end of the land even to the other end of the land."],[2,"No flesh has peace."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They have sown wheat,"],[2,"and have reaped thorns."],[1,"They have exhausted themselves,"],[2,"and profit nothing."],[1,"You will be ashamed of your fruits,"],[2,"because of the LORD\u2019s fierce anger.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u201cConcerning all my evil neighbors, who touch the inheritance which I have caused my people Israel to inherit: Behold, I will pluck them up from off their land, and will pluck up the house of Judah from among them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"It will happen that after I have plucked them up, I will return and have compassion on them. I will bring them again, every man to his heritage, and every man to his land."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"It will happen, if they will diligently learn the ways of my people, to swear by my name, \u2018As the LORD lives;\u2019 even as they taught my people to swear by Baal, then they will be built up in the middle of my people."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But if they will not hear, then I will pluck up that nation, plucking up and destroying it,\u201d says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cGo, and buy yourself a linen belt, and put it on your waist, and don\u2019t put it in water.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"So I bought a belt according to the LORD\u2019s word, and put it on my waist."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me the second time, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cTake the belt that you have bought, which is on your waist, and arise, go to the Euphrates, and hide it there in a cleft of the rock.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"So I went and hid it by the Euphrates, as the LORD commanded me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"After many days, the LORD said to me, \u201cArise, go to the Euphrates, and take the belt from there, which I commanded you to hide there.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I went to the Euphrates, and dug, and took the belt from the place where I had hidden it; and behold, the belt was ruined. It was profitable for nothing."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD says, \u2018In this way I will ruin the pride of Judah, and the great pride of Jerusalem."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"This evil people, who refuse to hear my words, who walk in the stubbornness of their heart, and have gone after other gods to serve them and to worship them, will even be as this belt, which is profitable for nothing."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For as the belt clings to the waist of a man, so I have caused the whole house of Israel and the whole house of Judah to cling to me,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018that they may be to me for a people, for a name, for praise, and for glory; but they would not hear.\u2019"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore you shall speak to them this word: \u2018The LORD, the God of Israel says, \u201cEvery container should be filled with wine.\u201d\u2019 They will tell you, \u2018Do we not certainly know that every container should be filled with wine?\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then tell them, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cBehold, I will fill all the inhabitants of this land, even the kings who sit on David\u2019s throne, the priests, the prophets, and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, with drunkenness."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will dash them one against another, even the fathers and the sons together,\u201d says the LORD: \u201cI will not pity, spare, or have compassion, that I should not destroy them.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, and give ear."],[2,"Don\u2019t be proud,"],[2,"for the LORD has spoken."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Give glory to the LORD your God,"],[2,"before he causes darkness,"],[2,"and before your feet stumble on the dark mountains,"],[1,"and while you look for light,"],[2,"he turns it into the shadow of death,"],[2,"and makes it deep darkness."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"But if you will not hear it,"],[2,"my soul will weep in secret for your pride."],[1,"My eye will weep bitterly,"],[2,"and run down with tears,"],[2,"because the LORD\u2019s flock has been taken captive."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Say to the king and to the queen mother,"],[2,"\u201cHumble yourselves."],[1,"Sit down, for your crowns have come down,"],[2,"even the crown of your glory."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The cities of the South are shut up,"],[2,"and there is no one to open them."],[1,"Judah is carried away captive: all of them."],[2,"They are wholly carried away captive."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Lift up your eyes,"],[2,"and see those who come from the north."],[1,"Where is the flock that was given to you,"],[2,"your beautiful flock?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"What will you say when he sets over you as head those whom you have yourself taught to be friends to you?"],[2,"Won\u2019t sorrows take hold of you, as of a woman in travail?"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"If you say in your heart,"],[2,"\u201cWhy have these things come on me?\u201d"],[1,"Your skirts are uncovered because of the greatness of your iniquity,"],[2,"and your heels suffer violence."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Can the Ethiopian change his skin,"],[2,"or the leopard his spots?"],[1,"Then may you also do good,"],[2,"who are accustomed to do evil."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore I will scatter them"],[2,"as the stubble that passes away"],[2,"by the wind of the wilderness."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"This is your lot,"],[2,"the portion measured to you from me,\u201d says the LORD,"],[1,"\u201cbecause you have forgotten me,"],[2,"and trusted in falsehood.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will also uncover your skirts on your face,"],[2,"and your shame will appear."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"I have seen your abominations, even your adulteries"],[2,"and your neighing, the lewdness of your prostitution,"],[2,"on the hills in the field."],[1,"Woe to you, Jerusalem!"],[2,"You will not be made clean."],[2,"How long will it yet be?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the LORD\u2019s word that came to Jeremiah concerning the drought:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cJudah mourns,"],[2,"and its gates languish."],[1,"They sit in black on the ground."],[2,"The cry of Jerusalem goes up."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Their nobles send their little ones to the waters."],[2,"They come to the cisterns,"],[2,"and find no water."],[1,"They return with their vessels empty."],[2,"They are disappointed and confounded,"],[2,"and cover their heads."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Because of the ground which is cracked,"],[2,"because no rain has been in the land,"],[1,"the plowmen are disappointed."],[2,"They cover their heads."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, the doe in the field also calves and forsakes her young,"],[2,"because there is no grass."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The wild donkeys stand on the bare heights."],[2,"They pant for air like jackals."],[1,"Their eyes fail,"],[2,"because there is no vegetation."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Though our iniquities testify against us,"],[2,"work for your name\u2019s sake, LORD;"],[1,"for our rebellions are many."],[2,"We have sinned against you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You hope of Israel,"],[2,"its Savior in the time of trouble,"],[1,"why should you be as a foreigner in the land,"],[2,"and as a wayfaring man who turns aside to stay for a night?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Why should you be like a scared man,"],[2,"as a mighty man who can\u2019t save?"],[1,"Yet you, LORD, are in the middle of us,"],[2,"and we are called by your name."],[2,"Don\u2019t leave us."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says to this people:"],[1,"\u201cEven so they have loved to wander."],[2,"They have not restrained their feet."],[1,"Therefore the LORD does not accept them."],[2,"Now he will remember their iniquity,"],[2,"and punish them for their sins.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cDon\u2019t pray for this people for their good."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When they fast, I will not hear their cry; and when they offer burnt offering and meal offering, I will not accept them; but I will consume them by the sword, by famine, and by pestilence.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cAh, Lord GOD! Behold, the prophets tell them, \u2018You will not see the sword, neither will you have famine; but I will give you assured peace in this place.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to me, \u201cThe prophets prophesy lies in my name. I didn\u2019t send them. I didn\u2019t command them. I didn\u2019t speak to them. They prophesy to you a lying vision, divination, and a thing of nothing, and the deceit of their own heart."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says concerning the prophets who prophesy in my name, but I didn\u2019t send them, yet they say, \u2018Sword and famine will not be in this land.\u2019 Those prophets will be consumed by sword and famine."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The people to whom they prophesy will be cast out in the streets of Jerusalem because of the famine and the sword. They will have no one to bury them\u2014them, their wives, their sons, or their daughters, for I will pour their wickedness on them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall say this word to them:"],[1,"\u201c\u2018Let my eyes run down with tears night and day,"],[2,"and let them not cease;"],[1,"for the virgin daughter of my people is broken with a great breach,"],[2,"with a very grievous wound."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"If I go out into the field,"],[2,"then behold, the slain with the sword!"],[1,"If I enter into the city,"],[2,"then behold, those who are sick with famine!"],[1,"For both the prophet and the priest go about in the land,"],[2,"and have no knowledge.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Have you utterly rejected Judah?"],[2,"Has your soul loathed Zion?"],[1,"Why have you struck us, and there is no healing for us?"],[2,"We looked for peace, but no good came;"],[2,"and for a time of healing, and behold, dismay!"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"We acknowledge, LORD, our wickedness,"],[2,"and the iniquity of our fathers;"],[2,"for we have sinned against you."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Do not abhor us, for your name\u2019s sake."],[2,"Do not disgrace the throne of your glory."],[2,"Remember, and don\u2019t break your covenant with us."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Are there any among the vanities of the nations that can cause rain?"],[2,"Or can the sky give showers?"],[2,"Aren\u2019t you he, the LORD our God?"],[1,"Therefore we will wait for you;"],[2,"for you have made all these things."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD said to me, \u201cThough Moses and Samuel stood before me, yet my mind would not turn toward this people. Cast them out of my sight, and let them go out!"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It will happen when they ask you, \u2018Where shall we go out?\u2019 then you shall tell them, \u2018The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cSuch as are for death, to death;"],[1,"such as are for the sword, to the sword;"],[1,"such as are for the famine, to the famine;"],[1,"and such as are for captivity, to captivity.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI will appoint over them four kinds,\u201d says the LORD: \u201cthe sword to kill, the dogs to tear, the birds of the sky, and the animals of the earth, to devour and to destroy."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will cause them to be tossed back and forth among all the kingdoms of the earth, because of Manasseh, the son of Hezekiah, king of Judah, for that which he did in Jerusalem."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For who will have pity on you, Jerusalem?"],[2,"Who will mourn you?"],[2,"Who will come to ask of your welfare?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You have rejected me,\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cYou have gone backward."],[1,"Therefore I have stretched out my hand against you"],[2,"and destroyed you."],[2,"I am weary of showing compassion."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I have winnowed them with a fan in the gates of the land."],[2,"I have bereaved them of children."],[1,"I have destroyed my people."],[2,"They didn\u2019t return from their ways."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Their widows are increased more than the sand of the seas."],[2,"I have brought on them against the mother of the young men a destroyer at noonday."],[2,"I have caused anguish and terrors to fall on her suddenly."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"She who has borne seven languishes."],[2,"She has given up the spirit."],[1,"Her sun has gone down while it was yet day."],[2,"She has been disappointed and confounded."],[2,"I will deliver their residue to the sword before their enemies,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe is me, my mother, that you have borne me, a man of strife,"],[2,"and a man of contention to the whole earth!"],[1,"I have not lent, neither have men lent to me;"],[2,"yet every one of them curses me."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said,"],[1,"\u201cMost certainly I will strengthen you for good."],[2,"Most certainly I will cause the enemy to make supplication to you in the time of evil"],[2,"and in the time of affliction."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Can one break iron,"],[2,"even iron from the north, and bronze?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give your substance and your treasures for a plunder without price,"],[2,"and that for all your sins,"],[2,"even in all your borders."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make them to pass with your enemies into a land which you don\u2019t know;"],[2,"for a fire is kindled in my anger,"],[2,"which will burn on you.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you know."],[2,"Remember me, visit me,"],[2,"and avenge me of my persecutors."],[1,"You are patient, so don\u2019t take me away."],[2,"Know that for your sake I have suffered reproach."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Your words were found,"],[2,"and I ate them."],[1,"Your words were to me a joy and the rejoicing of my heart,"],[2,"for I am called by your name, LORD, God of Armies."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I didn\u2019t sit in the assembly of those who make merry and rejoice."],[2,"I sat alone because of your hand,"],[2,"for you have filled me with indignation."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Why is my pain perpetual,"],[2,"and my wound incurable,"],[2,"which refuses to be healed?"],[1,"Will you indeed be to me as a deceitful brook,"],[2,"like waters that fail?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cIf you return, then I will bring you again,"],[2,"that you may stand before me;"],[1,"and if you take out the precious from the vile,"],[2,"you will be as my mouth."],[1,"They will return to you,"],[2,"but you will not return to them."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make you to this people a fortified bronze wall."],[2,"They will fight against you,"],[2,"but they will not prevail against you;"],[1,"for I am with you to save you"],[2,"and to deliver you,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will deliver you out of the hand of the wicked,"],[2,"and I will redeem you out of the hand of the terrible.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not take a wife, neither shall you have sons or daughters, in this place.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For the LORD says concerning the sons and concerning the daughters who are born in this place, and concerning their mothers who bore them, and concerning their fathers who became their father in this land:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cThey will die grievous deaths. They will not be lamented, neither will they be buried. They will be as dung on the surface of the ground. They will be consumed by the sword and by famine. Their dead bodies will be food for the birds of the sky and for the animals of the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says, \u201cDon\u2019t enter into the house of mourning. Don\u2019t go to lament. Don\u2019t bemoan them, for I have taken away my peace from this people,\u201d says the LORD, \u201ceven loving kindness and tender mercies."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Both great and small will die in this land. They will not be buried. Men won\u2019t lament for them, cut themselves, or make themselves bald for them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Men won\u2019t break bread for them in mourning, to comfort them for the dead. Men won\u2019t give them the cup of consolation to drink for their father or for their mother."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall not go into the house of feasting to sit with them, to eat and to drink.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says: \u201cBehold, I will cause to cease out of this place, before your eyes and in your days, the voice of mirth and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom and the voice of the bride."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"It will happen, when you tell this people all these words, and they ask you, \u2018Why has the LORD pronounced all this great evil against us?\u2019 or \u2018What is our iniquity?\u2019 or \u2018What is our sin that we have committed against the LORD our God?\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"then you shall tell them, \u2018Because your fathers have forsaken me,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018and have walked after other gods, have served them, have worshiped them, have forsaken me, and have not kept my law."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You have done evil more than your fathers, for behold, you each walk after the stubbornness of his evil heart, so that you don\u2019t listen to me."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore I will cast you out of this land into the land that you have not known, neither you nor your fathers. There you will serve other gods day and night, for I will show you no favor.\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore behold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat it will no more be said, \u2018As the LORD lives, who brought up the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt;\u2019"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but, \u2018As the LORD lives, who brought up the children of Israel from the land of the north, and from all the countries where he had driven them.\u2019 I will bring them again into their land that I gave to their fathers."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I will send for many fishermen,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cand they will fish them up. Afterward I will send for many hunters, and they will hunt them from every mountain, from every hill, and out of the clefts of the rocks."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For my eyes are on all their ways. They are not hidden from my face. Their iniquity isn\u2019t concealed from my eyes."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"First I will recompense their iniquity and their sin double, because they have polluted my land with the carcasses of their detestable things, and have filled my inheritance with their abominations.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, my strength, my stronghold,"],[2,"and my refuge in the day of affliction,"],[1,"the nations will come to you from the ends of the earth,"],[2,"and will say,"],[1,"\u201cOur fathers have inherited nothing but lies,"],[2,"vanity and things in which there is no profit."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Should a man make to himself gods"],[2,"which yet are no gods?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore behold, I will cause them to know,"],[2,"this once I will cause them to know my hand and my might."],[2,"Then they will know that my name is the LORD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe sin of Judah is written with a pen of iron,"],[2,"and with the point of a diamond."],[1,"It is engraved on the tablet of their heart,"],[2,"and on the horns of your altars."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Even their children remember their altars"],[2,"and their Asherah poles by the green trees on the high hills."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My mountain in the field,"],[2,"I will give your substance and all your treasures for a plunder,"],[2,"and your high places, because of sin, throughout all your borders."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"You, even of yourself, will discontinue from your heritage that I gave you."],[2,"I will cause you to serve your enemies in the land which you don\u2019t know,"],[2,"for you have kindled a fire in my anger which will burn forever.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cCursed is the man who trusts in man,"],[2,"relies on strength of flesh,"],[2,"and whose heart departs from the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For he will be like a bush in the desert,"],[2,"and will not see when good comes,"],[1,"but will inhabit the parched places in the wilderness,"],[2,"an uninhabited salt land."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBlessed is the man who trusts in the LORD,"],[2,"and whose confidence is in the LORD."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For he will be as a tree planted by the waters,"],[2,"who spreads out its roots by the river,"],[1,"and will not fear when heat comes,"],[2,"but its leaf will be green,"],[1,"and will not be concerned in the year of drought."],[2,"It won\u2019t cease from yielding fruit."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The heart is deceitful above all things"],[2,"and it is exceedingly corrupt."],[2,"Who can know it?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI, the LORD, search the mind."],[2,"I try the heart,"],[1,"even to give every man according to his ways,"],[2,"according to the fruit of his doings.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"As the partridge that sits on eggs which she has not laid,"],[2,"so is he who gets riches, and not by right."],[1,"In the middle of his days, they will leave him."],[2,"At his end, he will be a fool."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"A glorious throne, set on high from the beginning,"],[2,"is the place of our sanctuary."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, the hope of Israel,"],[2,"all who forsake you will be disappointed."],[1,"Those who depart from me will be written in the earth,"],[2,"because they have forsaken the LORD,"],[2,"the spring of living waters."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Heal me, O LORD, and I will be healed."],[2,"Save me, and I will be saved;"],[2,"for you are my praise."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, they ask me,"],[2,"\u201cWhere is the LORD\u2019s word?"],[2,"Let it be fulfilled now.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"As for me, I have not hurried from being a shepherd after you."],[2,"I haven\u2019t desired the woeful day. You know."],[2,"That which came out of my lips was before your face."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be a terror to me."],[2,"You are my refuge in the day of evil."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Let them be disappointed who persecute me,"],[2,"but don\u2019t let me be disappointed."],[1,"Let them be dismayed,"],[2,"but don\u2019t let me be dismayed."],[1,"Bring on them the day of evil,"],[2,"and destroy them with double destruction."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said this to me: \u201cGo and stand in the gate of the children of the people, through which the kings of Judah come in and by which they go out, and in all the gates of Jerusalem."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Tell them, \u2018Hear the LORD\u2019s word, you kings of Judah, all Judah, and all the inhabitants of Jerusalem, that enter in by these gates:"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u201cBe careful, and bear no burden on the Sabbath day, nor bring it in by the gates of Jerusalem."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t carry a burden out of your houses on the Sabbath day. Don\u2019t do any work, but make the Sabbath day holy, as I commanded your fathers."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But they didn\u2019t listen. They didn\u2019t turn their ear, but made their neck stiff, that they might not hear, and might not receive instruction."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"It will happen, if you diligently listen to me,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cto bring in no burden through the gates of this city on the Sabbath day, but to make the Sabbath day holy, to do no work therein;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"then there will enter in by the gates of this city kings and princes sitting on David\u2019s throne, riding in chariots and on horses, they and their princes, the men of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem; and this city will remain forever."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They will come from the cities of Judah, and from the places around Jerusalem, from the land of Benjamin, from the lowland, from the hill country, and from the South, bringing burnt offerings, sacrifices, meal offerings, and frankincense, and bringing sacrifices of thanksgiving to the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But if you will not listen to me to make the Sabbath day holy, and not to bear a burden and enter in at the gates of Jerusalem on the Sabbath day, then I will kindle a fire in its gates, and it will devour the palaces of Jerusalem. It will not be quenched.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word which came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cArise, and go down to the potter\u2019s house, and there I will cause you to hear my words.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I went down to the potter\u2019s house, and behold, he was making something on the wheels."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When the vessel that he made of the clay was marred in the hand of the potter, he made it again another vessel, as seemed good to the potter to make it."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cHouse of Israel, can\u2019t I do with you as this potter?\u201d says the LORD. \u201cBehold, as the clay in the potter\u2019s hand, so are you in my hand, house of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"At the instant I speak concerning a nation, and concerning a kingdom, to pluck up and to break down and to destroy it,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"if that nation, concerning which I have spoken, turns from their evil, I will repent of the evil that I thought to do to them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"At the instant I speak concerning a nation, and concerning a kingdom, to build and to plant it,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"if they do that which is evil in my sight, that they don\u2019t obey my voice, then I will repent of the good with which I said I would benefit them."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow therefore, speak to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, saying, \u2018The LORD says: \u201cBehold, I frame evil against you, and devise a plan against you. Everyone return from his evil way now, and amend your ways and your doings.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But they say, \u2018It is in vain; for we will walk after our own plans, and we will each follow the stubbornness of his evil heart.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cAsk now among the nations,"],[2,"\u2018Who has heard such things?\u2019"],[2,"The virgin of Israel has done a very horrible thing."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Will the snow of Lebanon fail from the rock of the field?"],[2,"Will the cold waters that flow down from afar be dried up?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"For my people have forgotten me."],[2,"They have burned incense to false gods."],[1,"They have been made to stumble in their ways"],[2,"in the ancient paths,"],[2,"to walk in byways, in a way not built up,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"to make their land an astonishment,"],[2,"and a perpetual hissing."],[1,"Everyone who passes by it will be astonished,"],[2,"and shake his head."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I will scatter them as with an east wind before the enemy."],[2,"I will show them the back, and not the face,"],[2,"in the day of their calamity."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they said, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s devise plans against Jeremiah; for the law won\u2019t perish from the priest, nor counsel from the wise, nor the word from the prophet. Come, and let\u2019s strike him with the tongue, and let\u2019s not give heed to any of his words.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Give heed to me, LORD,"],[2,"and listen to the voice of those who contend with me."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Should evil be recompensed for good?"],[2,"For they have dug a pit for my soul."],[1,"Remember how I stood before you to speak good for them,"],[2,"to turn away your wrath from them."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore deliver up their children to the famine,"],[2,"and give them over to the power of the sword."],[1,"Let their wives become childless and widows."],[2,"Let their men be killed"],[2,"and their young men struck by the sword in battle."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Let a cry be heard from their houses"],[2,"when you bring a troop suddenly on them;"],[1,"for they have dug a pit to take me"],[2,"and hidden snares for my feet."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet, LORD, you know all their counsel against me to kill me."],[2,"Don\u2019t forgive their iniquity."],[2,"Don\u2019t blot out their sin from your sight,"],[1,"Let them be overthrown before you."],[2,"Deal with them in the time of your anger."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus said the LORD, \u201cGo, and buy a potter\u2019s earthen container, and take some of the elders of the people and of the elders of the priests;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and go out to the valley of the son of Hinnom, which is by the entry of the gate Harsith, and proclaim there the words that I will tell you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Say, \u2018Hear the LORD\u2019s word, kings of Judah and inhabitants of Jerusalem: The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says, \u201cBehold, I will bring evil on this place, which whoever hears, his ears will tingle."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Because they have forsaken me, and have defiled this place, and have burned incense in it to other gods that they didn\u2019t know\u2014they, their fathers, and the kings of Judah\u2014and have filled this place with the blood of innocents,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and have built the high places of Baal to burn their children in the fire for burnt offerings to Baal, which I didn\u2019t command, nor speak, which didn\u2019t even enter into my mind."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore, behold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat this place will no more be called \u2018Topheth\u2019, nor \u2018The Valley of the son of Hinnom\u2019, but \u2018The valley of Slaughter\u2019."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cI will make the counsel of Judah and Jerusalem void in this place. I will cause them to fall by the sword before their enemies, and by the hand of those who seek their life. I will give their dead bodies to be food for the birds of the sky and for the animals of the earth."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will make this city an astonishment and a hissing. Everyone who passes by it will be astonished and hiss because of all its plagues."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I will cause them to eat the flesh of their sons and the flesh of their daughters. They will each eat the flesh of his friend in the siege and in the distress with which their enemies, and those who seek their life, will distress them.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen you shall break the container in the sight of the men who go with you,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and shall tell them, \u2018The LORD of Armies says: \u201cEven so I will break this people and this city as one breaks a potter\u2019s vessel, that can\u2019t be made whole again. They will bury in Topheth until there is no place to bury."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"This is what I will do to this place,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cand to its inhabitants, even making this city as Topheth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The houses of Jerusalem and the houses of the kings of Judah, which are defiled, will be as the place of Topheth, even all the houses on whose roofs they have burned incense to all the army of the sky and have poured out drink offerings to other gods.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah came from Topheth, where the LORD had sent him to prophesy, and he stood in the court of the LORD\u2019s house, and said to all the people:"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says, \u2018Behold, I will bring on this city and on all its towns all the evil that I have pronounced against it, because they have made their neck stiff, that they may not hear my words.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Pashhur, the son of Immer the priest, who was chief officer in the LORD\u2019s house, heard Jeremiah prophesying these things."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Pashhur struck Jeremiah the prophet and put him in the stocks that were in the upper gate of Benjamin, which was in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"On the next day, Pashhur released Jeremiah out of the stocks. Then Jeremiah said to him, \u201cThe LORD has not called your name Pashhur, but Magormissabib."]],f:["\u201cMagormissabib\u201d means \u201csurrounded by terror\u201d"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For the LORD says, \u2018Behold, I will make you a terror to yourself and to all your friends. They will fall by the sword of their enemies, and your eyes will see it. I will give all Judah into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he will carry them captive to Babylon, and will kill them with the sword."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Moreover I will give all the riches of this city, and all its gains, and all its precious things, yes, I will give all the treasures of the kings of Judah into the hand of their enemies. They will make them captives, take them, and carry them to Babylon."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You, Pashhur, and all who dwell in your house will go into captivity. You will come to Babylon, and there you will die, and there you will be buried, you, and all your friends, to whom you have prophesied falsely.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you have persuaded me, and I was persuaded."],[2,"You are stronger than I, and have prevailed."],[1,"I have become a laughingstock all day."],[2,"Everyone mocks me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For as often as I speak, I cry out;"],[2,"I cry, \u201cViolence and destruction!\u201d"],[1,"because the LORD\u2019s word has been made a reproach to me,"],[2,"and a derision, all day."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"If I say that I will not make mention of him,"],[2,"or speak any more in his name,"],[1,"then there is in my heart as it were a burning fire shut up in my bones."],[2,"I am weary with holding it in."],[2,"I can\u2019t."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For I have heard the defaming of many:"],[2,"\u201cTerror on every side!"],[2,"Denounce, and we will denounce him!\u201d"],[1,"say all my familiar friends,"],[2,"those who watch for my fall."],[1,"\u201cPerhaps he will be persuaded,"],[2,"and we will prevail against him,"],[2,"and we will take our revenge on him.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"But the LORD is with me as an awesome mighty one."],[2,"Therefore my persecutors will stumble,"],[2,"and they won\u2019t prevail."],[1,"They will be utterly disappointed"],[2,"because they have not dealt wisely,"],[2,"even with an everlasting dishonor which will never be forgotten."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"But the LORD of Armies, who tests the righteous,"],[2,"who sees the heart and the mind,"],[1,"let me see your vengeance on them,"],[2,"for I have revealed my cause to you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Sing to the LORD!"],[2,"Praise the LORD,"],[2,"for he has delivered the soul of the needy from the hand of evildoers."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Cursed is the day in which I was born."],[2,"Don\u2019t let the day in which my mother bore me be blessed."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Cursed is the man who brought news to my father, saying,"],[2,"\u201cA boy is born to you,\u201d making him very glad."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Let that man be as the cities which the LORD overthrew,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t repent."],[1,"Let him hear a cry in the morning,"],[2,"and shouting at noontime,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"because he didn\u2019t kill me from the womb."],[2,"So my mother would have been my grave,"],[2,"and her womb always great."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Why did I come out of the womb to see labor and sorrow,"],[2,"that my days should be consumed with shame?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word which came to Jeremiah from the LORD, when King Zedekiah sent to him Pashhur the son of Malchijah, and Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah, the priest, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cPlease inquire of the LORD for us; for Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon makes war against us. Perhaps the LORD will deal with us according to all his wondrous works, that he may withdraw from us.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah said to them, \u201cTell Zedekiah:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u2018The LORD, the God of Israel says, \u201cBehold, I will turn back the weapons of war that are in your hands, with which you fight against the king of Babylon, and against the Chaldeans who besiege you outside the walls; and I will gather them into the middle of this city."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I myself will fight against you with an outstretched hand and with a strong arm, even in anger, in wrath, and in great indignation."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I will strike the inhabitants of this city, both man and animal. They will die of a great pestilence."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Afterward,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cI will deliver Zedekiah king of Judah, his servants, and the people, even those who are left in this city from the pestilence, from the sword, and from the famine, into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of their enemies, and into the hand of those who seek their life. He will strike them with the edge of the sword. He will not spare them, have pity, or have mercy.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall say to this people, \u2018The LORD says: \u201cBehold, I set before you the way of life and the way of death."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He who remains in this city will die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence, but he who goes out and passes over to the Chaldeans who besiege you, he will live, and he will escape with his life."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For I have set my face on this city for evil, and not for good,\u201d says the LORD. \u201cIt will be given into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he will burn it with fire.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cConcerning the house of the king of Judah, hear the LORD\u2019s word:"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"House of David, the LORD says,"],[1,"\u2018Execute justice in the morning,"],[2,"and deliver him who is robbed out of the hand of the oppressor,"],[1,"lest my wrath go out like fire,"],[2,"and burn so that no one can quench it,"],[2,"because of the evil of your doings."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I am against you, O inhabitant of the valley,"],[2,"and of the rock of the plain,\u2019 says the LORD."],[1,"\u2018You that say, \u201cWho would come down against us?\u201d"],[2,"or, \u201cWho would enter into our homes?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will punish you according to the fruit of your doings,\u2019 says the LORD;"],[2,"\u2018and I will kindle a fire in her forest,"],[2,"and it will devour all that is around her.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cGo down to the house of the king of Judah, and speak this word there:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u2018Hear the LORD\u2019s word, king of Judah, who sits on David\u2019s throne\u2014you, your servants, and your people who enter in by these gates."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD says: \u201cExecute justice and righteousness, and deliver him who is robbed out of the hand of the oppressor. Do no wrong. Do no violence to the foreigner, the fatherless, or the widow. Don\u2019t shed innocent blood in this place."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For if you do this thing indeed, then kings sitting on David\u2019s throne will enter in by the gates of this house, riding in chariots and on horses\u2014they, their servants, and their people."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But if you will not hear these words, I swear by myself,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat this house will become a desolation.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says concerning the house of the king of Judah:"],[1,"\u201cYou are Gilead to me,"],[2,"the head of Lebanon."],[1,"Yet surely I will make you a wilderness,"],[2,"cities which are not inhabited."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I will prepare destroyers against you,"],[2,"everyone with his weapons,"],[1,"and they will cut down your choice cedars,"],[2,"and cast them into the fire."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMany nations will pass by this city, and they will each ask his neighbor, \u2018Why has the LORD done this to this great city?\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then they will answer, \u2018Because they abandoned the covenant of the LORD their God, worshiped other gods, and served them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t weep for the dead."],[2,"Don\u2019t bemoan him;"],[1,"but weep bitterly for him who goes away,"],[2,"for he will return no more,"],[2,"and not see his native country."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says touching Shallum the son of Josiah, king of Judah, who reigned instead of Josiah his father, and who went out of this place: \u201cHe won\u2019t return there any more."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But he will die in the place where they have led him captive. He will see this land no more.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWoe to him who builds his house by unrighteousness,"],[2,"and his rooms by injustice;"],[1,"who uses his neighbor\u2019s service without wages,"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t give him his hire;"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"who says, \u2018I will build myself a wide house and spacious rooms,\u2019"],[2,"and cuts out windows for himself,"],[1,"with a cedar ceiling,"],[2,"and painted with red."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cShould you reign because you strive to excel in cedar?"],[2,"Didn\u2019t your father eat and drink,"],[2,"and do justice and righteousness?"],[2,"Then it was well with him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He judged the cause of the poor and needy;"],[2,"so then it was well."],[1,"Wasn\u2019t this to know me?\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"But your eyes and your heart are only for your covetousness,"],[2,"for shedding innocent blood,"],[2,"for oppression, and for doing violence.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says concerning Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah:"],[1,"\u201cThey won\u2019t lament for him,"],[2,"saying, \u2018Ah my brother!\u2019 or, \u2018Ah sister!\u2019"],[1,"They won\u2019t lament for him,"],[2,"saying \u2018Ah lord!\u2019 or, \u2018Ah his glory!\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He will be buried with the burial of a donkey,"],[2,"drawn and cast out beyond the gates of Jerusalem.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGo up to Lebanon, and cry out."],[2,"Lift up your voice in Bashan,"],[1,"and cry from Abarim;"],[2,"for all your lovers have been destroyed."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"I spoke to you in your prosperity,"],[2,"but you said, \u2018I will not listen.\u2019"],[1,"This has been your way from your youth,"],[2,"that you didn\u2019t obey my voice."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The wind will feed all your shepherds,"],[2,"and your lovers will go into captivity."],[1,"Surely then you will be ashamed"],[2,"and confounded for all your wickedness."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Inhabitant of Lebanon,"],[2,"who makes your nest in the cedars,"],[1,"how greatly to be pitied you will be when pangs come on you,"],[2,"the pain as of a woman in travail!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs I live,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthough Coniah the son of Jehoiakim king of Judah were the signet on my right hand, I would still pluck you from there."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I would give you into the hand of those who seek your life, and into the hand of them of whom you are afraid, even into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of the Chaldeans."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I will cast you out with your mother who bore you into another country, where you were not born; and there you will die."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But to the land to which their soul longs to return, there they will not return.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Is this man Coniah a despised broken vessel?"],[2,"Is he a vessel in which no one delights?"],[1,"Why are they cast out, he and his offspring,"],[2,"and cast into a land which they don\u2019t know?"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"O earth, earth, earth,"],[2,"hear the LORD\u2019s word!"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD says,"],[2,"\u201cRecord this man as childless,"],[2,"a man who will not prosper in his days;"],[1,"for no more will a man of his offspring prosper,"],[2,"sitting on David\u2019s throne"],[2,"and ruling in Judah.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to the shepherds who destroy and scatter the sheep of my pasture!\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD, the God of Israel, says against the shepherds who feed my people: \u201cYou have scattered my flock, driven them away, and have not visited them. Behold, I will visit on you the evil of your doings,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cI will gather the remnant of my flock out of all the countries where I have driven them, and will bring them again to their folds; and they will be fruitful and multiply."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will set up shepherds over them who will feed them. They will no longer be afraid or dismayed, neither will any be lacking,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthat I will raise to David a righteous Branch;"],[1,"and he will reign as king and deal wisely,"],[2,"and will execute justice and righteousness in the land."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"In his days Judah will be saved,"],[2,"and Israel will dwell safely."],[1,"This is his name by which he will be called:"],[2,"The LORD our righteousness."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore, behold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat they will no more say, \u2018As the LORD lives, who brought up the children of Israel out of the land of Egypt;\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but, \u2018As the LORD lives, who brought up and who led the offspring of the house of Israel out of the north country, and from all the countries where I had driven them.\u2019 Then they will dwell in their own land.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Concerning the prophets:"],[1,"My heart within me is broken."],[2,"All my bones shake."],[1,"I am like a drunken man,"],[2,"and like a man whom wine has overcome,"],[1,"because of the LORD,"],[2,"and because of his holy words."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor the land is full of adulterers;"],[2,"for because of the curse the land mourns."],[1,"The pastures of the wilderness have dried up."],[2,"Their course is evil,"],[2,"and their might is not right;"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"for both prophet and priest are profane."],[2,"Yes, in my house I have found their wickedness,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore their way will be to them as slippery places in the darkness."],[2,"They will be driven on,"],[2,"and fall therein;"],[1,"for I will bring evil on them,"],[2,"even the year of their visitation,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have seen folly in the prophets of Samaria."],[2,"They prophesied by Baal,"],[2,"and caused my people Israel to err."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"In the prophets of Jerusalem I have also seen a horrible thing:"],[2,"they commit adultery and walk in lies."],[1,"They strengthen the hands of evildoers,"],[2,"so that no one returns from his wickedness."],[1,"They have all become to me as Sodom,"],[2,"and its inhabitants as Gomorrah.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD of Armies says concerning the prophets:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I will feed them with wormwood,"],[2,"and make them drink poisoned water;"],[2,"for from the prophets of Jerusalem ungodliness has gone out into all the land.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says,"],[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t listen to the words of the prophets who prophesy to you."],[2,"They teach you vanity."],[2,"They speak a vision of their own heart,"],[2,"and not out of the mouth of the LORD."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"They say continually to those who despise me,"],[2,"\u2018The LORD has said, \u201cYou will have peace;\u201d\u2019"],[1,"and to everyone who walks in the stubbornness of his own heart they say,"],[2,"\u2018No evil will come on you.\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"For who has stood in the council of the LORD,"],[2,"that he should perceive and hear his word?"],[2,"Who has listened to my word, and heard it?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the LORD\u2019s storm, his wrath, has gone out."],[2,"Yes, a whirling storm!"],[2,"It will burst on the head of the wicked."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s anger will not return until he has executed"],[2,"and performed the intents of his heart."],[2,"In the latter days, you will understand it perfectly."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"I didn\u2019t send these prophets, yet they ran."],[2,"I didn\u2019t speak to them, yet they prophesied."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"But if they had stood in my council,"],[2,"then they would have caused my people to hear my words,"],[1,"and would have turned them from their evil way,"],[2,"and from the evil of their doings."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAm I a God at hand,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cand not a God afar off?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Can anyone hide himself in secret places"],[2,"so that I can\u2019t see him?\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cDon\u2019t I fill heaven and earth?\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI have heard what the prophets have said, who prophesy lies in my name, saying, \u2018I had a dream! I had a dream!\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"How long will this be in the heart of the prophets who prophesy lies, even the prophets of the deceit of their own heart?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They intend to cause my people to forget my name by their dreams which they each tell his neighbor, as their fathers forgot my name because of Baal."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The prophet who has a dream, let him tell a dream; and he who has my word, let him speak my word faithfully. What is the straw to the wheat?\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"\u201cIsn\u2019t my word like fire?\u201d says the LORD; \u201cand like a hammer that breaks the rock in pieces?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore behold, I am against the prophets,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cwho each steal my words from his neighbor."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Behold, I am against the prophets,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cwho use their tongues, and say, \u2018He says.\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Behold, I am against those who prophesy lying dreams,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cwho tell them, and cause my people to err by their lies, and by their vain boasting; yet I didn\u2019t send them or command them. They don\u2019t profit this people at all,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen this people, or the prophet, or a priest, asks you, saying, \u2018What is the message from the LORD?\u2019 Then you shall tell them, \u2018\u201cWhat message? I will cast you off,\u201d says the LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"As for the prophet, the priest, and the people, who say, \u2018The message from the LORD,\u2019 I will even punish that man and his household."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"You will say everyone to his neighbor, and everyone to his brother, \u2018What has the LORD answered?\u2019 and, \u2018What has the LORD said?\u2019"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"You will mention the message from the LORD no more, for every man\u2019s own word has become his message; for you have perverted the words of the living God, of the LORD of Armies, our God."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You will say to the prophet, \u2018What has the LORD answered you?\u2019 and, \u2018What has the LORD spoken?\u2019"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Although you say, \u2018The message from the LORD,\u2019 therefore the LORD says: \u2018Because you say this word, \u201cThe message from the LORD,\u201d and I have sent to you, telling you not to say, \u201cThe message from the LORD,\u201d"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"therefore behold, I will utterly forget you, and I will cast you off with the city that I gave to you and to your fathers, away from my presence."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"I will bring an everlasting reproach on you, and a perpetual shame, which will not be forgotten.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD showed me, and behold, two baskets of figs were set before the LORD\u2019s temple, after Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon had carried away captive Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim, king of Judah, and the princes of Judah, with the craftsmen and smiths, from Jerusalem, and had brought them to Babylon."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"One basket had very good figs, like the figs that are first-ripe; and the other basket had very bad figs, which could not be eaten, they were so bad."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD asked me, \u201cWhat do you see, Jeremiah?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cFigs. The good figs are very good, and the bad are very bad, so bad that they can\u2019t be eaten.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel says: \u2018Like these good figs, so I will regard the captives of Judah, whom I have sent out of this place into the land of the Chaldeans, as good."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For I will set my eyes on them for good, and I will bring them again to this land. I will build them, and not pull them down. I will plant them, and not pluck them up."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I will give them a heart to know me, that I am the LORD. They will be my people, and I will be their God; for they will return to me with their whole heart."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018As the bad figs, which can\u2019t be eaten, they are so bad,\u2019 surely the LORD says, \u2018So I will give up Zedekiah the king of Judah, and his princes, and the remnant of Jerusalem who remain in this land, and those who dwell in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I will even give them up to be tossed back and forth among all the kingdoms of the earth for evil, to be a reproach and a proverb, a taunt and a curse, in all places where I will drive them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I will send the sword, the famine, and the pestilence among them, until they are consumed from off the land that I gave to them and to their fathers.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the people of Judah, in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah (this was the first year of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon),"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"which Jeremiah the prophet spoke to all the people of Judah, and to all the inhabitants of Jerusalem:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"From the thirteenth year of Josiah the son of Amon, king of Judah, even to this day, these twenty-three years, the LORD\u2019s word has come to me, and I have spoken to you, rising up early and speaking; but you have not listened."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD has sent to you all his servants the prophets, rising up early and sending them (but you have not listened or inclined your ear to hear),"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cReturn now everyone from his evil way, and from the evil of your doings, and dwell in the land that the LORD has given to you and to your fathers, from of old and even forever more."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t go after other gods to serve them or worship them, and don\u2019t provoke me to anger with the work of your hands; then I will do you no harm.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYet you have not listened to me,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat you may provoke me to anger with the work of your hands to your own hurt.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD of Armies says: \u201cBecause you have not heard my words,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"behold, I will send and take all the families of the north,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cand I will send to Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, my servant, and will bring them against this land, and against its inhabitants, and against all these nations around. I will utterly destroy them, and make them an astonishment, and a hissing, and perpetual desolations."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Moreover I will take from them the voice of mirth and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom and the voice of the bride, the sound of the millstones, and the light of the lamp."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"This whole land will be a desolation, and an astonishment; and these nations will serve the king of Babylon seventy years."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt will happen, when seventy years are accomplished, that I will punish the king of Babylon and that nation,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cfor their iniquity. I will make the land of the Chaldeans desolate forever."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will bring on that land all my words which I have pronounced against it, even all that is written in this book, which Jeremiah has prophesied against all the nations."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For many nations and great kings will make bondservants of them, even of them. I will recompense them according to their deeds, and according to the work of their hands.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD, the God of Israel, says to me: \u201cTake this cup of the wine of wrath from my hand, and cause all the nations to whom I send you to drink it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They will drink, and reel back and forth, and be insane, because of the sword that I will send among them.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I took the cup at the LORD\u2019s hand, and made all the nations to drink, to whom the LORD had sent me:"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jerusalem, and the cities of Judah, with its kings and its princes, to make them a desolation, an astonishment, a hissing, and a curse, as it is today;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Pharaoh king of Egypt, with his servants, his princes, and all his people;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and all the mixed people, and all the kings of the land of Uz, all the kings of the Philistines, Ashkelon, Gaza, Ekron, and the remnant of Ashdod;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Edom, Moab, and the children of Ammon;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and all the kings of Tyre, all the kings of Sidon, and the kings of the isle which is beyond the sea;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Dedan, Tema, Buz, and all who have the corners of their beard cut off;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and all the kings of Arabia, all the kings of the mixed people who dwell in the wilderness;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and all the kings of Zimri, all the kings of Elam, and all the kings of the Medes;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and all the kings of the north, far and near, one with another; and all the kingdoms of the world, which are on the surface of the earth. The king of Sheshach will drink after them."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall tell them, \u2018The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says: \u201cDrink, and be drunk, vomit, fall, and rise no more, because of the sword which I will send among you.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"It shall be, if they refuse to take the cup at your hand to drink, then you shall tell them, \u2018The LORD of Armies says: \u201cYou shall surely drink."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For, behold, I begin to work evil at the city which is called by my name; and should you be utterly unpunished? You will not be unpunished; for I will call for a sword on all the inhabitants of the earth, says the LORD of Armies.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore prophesy against them all these words, and tell them,"],[1,"\u201c\u2018The LORD will roar from on high,"],[2,"and utter his voice from his holy habitation."],[2,"He will mightily roar against his fold."],[1,"He will give a shout, as those who tread grapes,"],[2,"against all the inhabitants of the earth."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"A noise will come even to the end of the earth;"],[2,"for the LORD has a controversy with the nations."],[1,"He will enter into judgment with all flesh."],[2,"As for the wicked, he will give them to the sword,\u201d\u2019 says the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, evil will go out from nation to nation,"],[2,"and a great storm will be raised up from the uttermost parts of the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The slain of the LORD will be at that day from one end of the earth even to the other end of the earth. They won\u2019t be lamented. They won\u2019t be gathered or buried. They will be dung on the surface of the ground."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Wail, you shepherds, and cry."],[2,"Wallow in dust, you leader of the flock;"],[1,"for the days of your slaughter and of your dispersions have fully come,"],[2,"and you will fall like fine pottery."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"The shepherds will have no way to flee."],[2,"The leader of the flock will have no escape."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"A voice of the cry of the shepherds,"],[2,"and the wailing of the leader of the flock,"],[2,"for the LORD destroys their pasture."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"The peaceful folds are brought to silence"],[2,"because of the fierce anger of the LORD."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"He has left his covert, as the lion;"],[2,"for their land has become an astonishment because of the fierceness of the oppression,"],[2,"and because of his fierce anger."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, this word came from the LORD:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD says: \u2018Stand in the court of the LORD\u2019s house, and speak to all the cities of Judah which come to worship in the LORD\u2019s house, all the words that I command you to speak to them. Don\u2019t omit a word."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It may be they will listen, and every man turn from his evil way, that I may relent from the evil which I intend to do to them because of the evil of their doings.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall tell them, \u201cThe LORD says: \u2018If you will not listen to me, to walk in my law which I have set before you,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"to listen to the words of my servants the prophets whom I send to you, even rising up early and sending them\u2014but you have not listened\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"then I will make this house like Shiloh, and will make this city a curse to all the nations of the earth.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The priests and the prophets and all the people heard Jeremiah speaking these words in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When Jeremiah had finished speaking all that the LORD had commanded him to speak to all the people, the priests and the prophets and all the people seized him, saying, \u201cYou shall surely die!"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Why have you prophesied in the LORD\u2019s name, saying, \u2018This house will be like Shiloh, and this city will be desolate, without inhabitant\u2019?\u201d All the people were crowded around Jeremiah in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When the princes of Judah heard these things, they came up from the king\u2019s house to the LORD\u2019s house; and they sat in the entry of the new gate of the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then the priests and the prophets spoke to the princes and to all the people, saying, \u201cThis man is worthy of death, for he has prophesied against this city, as you have heard with your ears.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah spoke to all the princes and to all the people, saying, \u201cThe LORD sent me to prophesy against this house and against this city all the words that you have heard."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now therefore amend your ways and your doings, and obey the LORD your God\u2019s voice; then the LORD will relent from the evil that he has pronounced against you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But as for me, behold, I am in your hand. Do with me what is good and right in your eyes."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Only know for certain that if you put me to death, you will bring innocent blood on yourselves, on this city, and on its inhabitants; for in truth the LORD has sent me to you to speak all these words in your ears.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the princes and all the people said to the priests and to the prophets: \u201cThis man is not worthy of death; for he has spoken to us in the name of the LORD our God.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then certain of the elders of the land rose up, and spoke to all the assembly of the people, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cMicah the Morashtite prophesied in the days of Hezekiah king of Judah; and he spoke to all the people of Judah, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies says:"],[1,"\u201c\u2018Zion will be plowed as a field,"],[2,"and Jerusalem will become heaps,"],[2,"and the mountain of the house as the high places of a forest.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Did Hezekiah king of Judah and all Judah put him to death? Didn\u2019t he fear the LORD, and entreat the favor of the LORD, and the LORD relented of the disaster which he had pronounced against them? We would commit great evil against our own souls that way!\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"There was also a man who prophesied in the LORD\u2019s name, Uriah the son of Shemaiah of Kiriath Jearim; and he prophesied against this city and against this land according to all the words of Jeremiah."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When Jehoiakim the king, with all his mighty men and all the princes heard his words, the king sought to put him to death; but when Uriah heard it, he was afraid, and fled, and went into Egypt."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Then Jehoiakim the king sent Elnathan the son of Achbor and certain men with him into Egypt."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They fetched Uriah out of Egypt and brought him to Jehoiakim the king, who killed him with the sword and cast his dead body into the graves of the common people."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"But the hand of Ahikam the son of Shaphan was with Jeremiah, so that they didn\u2019t give him into the hand of the people to put him to death."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the beginning of the reign of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, this word came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"the LORD says to me: \u201cMake bonds and bars, and put them on your neck."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then send them to the king of Edom, to the king of Moab, to the king of the children of Ammon, to the king of Tyre, and to the king of Sidon, by the hand of the messengers who come to Jerusalem to Zedekiah king of Judah."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Give them a command to their masters, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says, \u201cYou shall tell your masters:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u2018I have made the earth, the men, and the animals that are on the surface of the earth by my great power and by my outstretched arm. I give it to whom it seems right to me."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now I have given all these lands into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, my servant. I have also given the animals of the field to him to serve him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"All the nations will serve him, his son, and his son\u2019s son, until the time of his own land comes. Then many nations and great kings will make him their bondservant."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201c\u2018It will happen that I will punish the nation and the kingdom which will not serve the same Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and that will not put their neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018with the sword, with famine, and with pestilence, until I have consumed them by his hand."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But as for you, don\u2019t listen to your prophets, to your diviners, to your dreams, to your soothsayers, or to your sorcerers, who speak to you, saying, \u201cYou shall not serve the king of Babylon;\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for they prophesy a lie to you, to remove you far from your land, so that I would drive you out, and you would perish."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But the nation that brings their neck under the yoke of the king of Babylon and serves him, that nation I will let remain in their own land,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018and they will till it and dwell in it.\u2019\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I spoke to Zedekiah king of Judah according to all these words, saying, \u201cBring your necks under the yoke of the king of Babylon, and serve him and his people, and live."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Why will you die, you and your people, by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence, as the LORD has spoken concerning the nation that will not serve the king of Babylon?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t listen to the words of the prophets who speak to you, saying, \u2018You shall not serve the king of Babylon;\u2019 for they prophesy a lie to you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For I have not sent them,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cbut they prophesy falsely in my name; that I may drive you out, and that you may perish, you, and the prophets who prophesy to you.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Also I spoke to the priests and to all this people, saying, the LORD says, \u201cDon\u2019t listen to the words of your prophets who prophesy to you, saying, \u2018Behold, the vessels of the LORD\u2019s house will now shortly be brought again from Babylon;\u2019 for they prophesy a lie to you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t listen to them. Serve the king of Babylon, and live. Why should this city become a desolation?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But if they are prophets, and if the LORD\u2019s word is with them, let them now make intercession to the LORD of Armies, that the vessels which are left in the LORD\u2019s house, in the house of the king of Judah, and at Jerusalem, don\u2019t go to Babylon."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies says concerning the pillars, concerning the sea, concerning the bases, and concerning the rest of the vessels that are left in this city,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon didn\u2019t take when he carried away captive Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim, king of Judah, from Jerusalem to Babylon, and all the nobles of Judah and Jerusalem\u2014"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"yes, the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says concerning the vessels that are left in the LORD\u2019s house, and in the house of the king of Judah, and at Jerusalem:"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"\u2018They will be carried to Babylon, and there they will be, until the day that I visit them,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018then I will bring them up, and restore them to this place.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"That same year, in the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the fourth year, in the fifth month, Hananiah the son of Azzur, the prophet, who was of Gibeon, spoke to me in the LORD\u2019s house, in the presence of the priests and of all the people, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says, \u2018I have broken the yoke of the king of Babylon."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Within two full years I will bring again into this place all the vessels of the LORD\u2019s house that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon took away from this place and carried to Babylon."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will bring again to this place Jeconiah the son of Jehoiakim, king of Judah, with all the captives of Judah, who went to Babylon,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018for I will break the yoke of the king of Babylon.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the prophet Jeremiah said to the prophet Hananiah in the presence of the priests, and in the presence of all the people who stood in the LORD\u2019s house,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"even the prophet Jeremiah said, \u201cAmen! May the LORD do so. May the LORD perform your words which you have prophesied, to bring again the vessels of the LORD\u2019s house, and all those who are captives, from Babylon to this place."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Nevertheless listen now to this word that I speak in your ears, and in the ears of all the people:"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The prophets who have been before me and before you of old prophesied against many countries, and against great kingdoms, of war, of evil, and of pestilence."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"As for the prophet who prophesies of peace, when the word of the prophet happens, then the prophet will be known, that the LORD has truly sent him.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Hananiah the prophet took the bar from off the prophet Jeremiah\u2019s neck, and broke it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Hananiah spoke in the presence of all the people, saying, \u201cThe LORD says: \u2018Even so I will break the yoke of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon from off the neck of all the nations within two full years.\u2019\u201d Then the prophet Jeremiah went his way."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah, after Hananiah the prophet had broken the bar from off the neck of the prophet Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cGo, and tell Hananiah, saying, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cYou have broken the bars of wood, but you have made in their place bars of iron.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says, \u201cI have put a yoke of iron on the neck of all these nations, that they may serve Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon; and they will serve him. I have also given him the animals of the field.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the prophet Jeremiah said to Hananiah the prophet, \u201cListen, Hananiah! The LORD has not sent you, but you make this people trust in a lie."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says, \u2018Behold, I will send you away from off the surface of the earth. This year you will die, because you have spoken rebellion against the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So Hananiah the prophet died the same year in the seventh month."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these are the words of the letter that Jeremiah the prophet sent from Jerusalem to the residue of the elders of the captivity, and to the priests, to the prophets, and to all the people whom Nebuchadnezzar had carried away captive from Jerusalem to Babylon,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"(after Jeconiah the king, the queen mother, the eunuchs, the princes of Judah and Jerusalem, the craftsmen, and the smiths had departed from Jerusalem),"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"by the hand of Elasah the son of Shaphan and Gemariah the son of Hilkiah, (whom Zedekiah king of Judah sent to Babylon to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon). It said:"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says to all the captives whom I have caused to be carried away captive from Jerusalem to Babylon:"]]},{v:5,l:[[1,"\u201cBuild houses and dwell in them. Plant gardens and eat their fruit."]]},{v:6,l:[[1,"Take wives and father sons and daughters. Take wives for your sons, and give your daughters to husbands, that they may bear sons and daughters. Multiply there, and don\u2019t be diminished."]]},{v:7,l:[[1,"Seek the peace of the city where I have caused you to be carried away captive, and pray to the LORD for it; for in its peace you will have peace.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[1,"For the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says: \u201cDon\u2019t let your prophets who are among you and your diviners deceive you. Don\u2019t listen to your dreams which you cause to be dreamed."]]},{v:9,l:[[1,"For they prophesy falsely to you in my name. I have not sent them,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:10,l:[[1,"For the LORD says, \u201cAfter seventy years are accomplished for Babylon, I will visit you and perform my good word toward you, in causing you to return to this place."]]},{v:11,l:[[1,"For I know the thoughts that I think toward you,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthoughts of peace, and not of evil, to give you hope and a future."]]},{v:12,l:[[1,"You shall call on me, and you shall go and pray to me, and I will listen to you."]]},{v:13,l:[[1,"You shall seek me and find me, when you search for me with all your heart."]]},{v:14,l:[[1,"I will be found by you,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cand I will turn again your captivity, and I will gather you from all the nations, and from all the places where I have driven you,\u201d says the LORD. \u201cI will bring you again to the place from where I caused you to be carried away captive.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Because you have said, \u201cThe LORD has raised us up prophets in Babylon,\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[1,"the LORD says concerning the king who sits on David\u2019s throne, and concerning all the people who dwell in this city, your brothers who haven\u2019t gone with you into captivity,"]]},{v:17,l:[[1,"the LORD of Armies says: \u201cBehold, I will send on them the sword, the famine, and the pestilence, and will make them like rotten figs that can\u2019t be eaten, they are so bad."]]},{v:18,l:[[1,"I will pursue after them with the sword, with the famine, and with the pestilence, and will deliver them to be tossed back and forth among all the kingdoms of the earth, to be an object of horror, an astonishment, a hissing, and a reproach among all the nations where I have driven them,"]]},{v:19,l:[[1,"because they have not listened to my words,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cwith which I sent to them my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending them; but you would not hear,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear therefore the LORD\u2019s word, all you captives whom I have sent away from Jerusalem to Babylon."]]},{v:21,l:[[1,"The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says concerning Ahab the son of Kolaiah, and concerning Zedekiah the son of Maaseiah, who prophesy a lie to you in my name: \u201cBehold, I will deliver them into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon; and he will kill them before your eyes."]]},{v:22,l:[[1,"A curse will be taken up about them by all the captives of Judah who are in Babylon, saying, \u2018The LORD make you like Zedekiah and like Ahab, whom the king of Babylon roasted in the fire;\u2019"]]},{v:23,l:[[1,"because they have done foolish things in Israel, and have committed adultery with their neighbors\u2019 wives, and have spoken words in my name falsely, which I didn\u2019t command them. I am he who knows, and am witness,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Concerning Shemaiah the Nehelamite you shall speak, saying,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says, \u2018Because you have sent letters in your own name to all the people who are at Jerusalem, and to Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah, the priest, and to all the priests, saying,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD has made you priest in the place of Jehoiada the priest, that there may be officers in the LORD\u2019s house, for every man who is crazy and makes himself a prophet, that you should put him in the stocks and in shackles."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Now therefore, why have you not rebuked Jeremiah of Anathoth, who makes himself a prophet to you,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"because he has sent to us in Babylon, saying, The captivity is long. Build houses, and dwell in them. Plant gardens, and eat their fruit?\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Zephaniah the priest read this letter in the hearing of Jeremiah the prophet."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"\u201cSend to all of the captives, saying, \u2018The LORD says concerning Shemaiah the Nehelamite: \u201cBecause Shemaiah has prophesied to you, and I didn\u2019t send him, and he has caused you to trust in a lie,\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"therefore the LORD says, \u201cBehold, I will punish Shemaiah the Nehelamite and his offspring. He will not have a man to dwell among this people. He won\u2019t see the good that I will do to my people,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cbecause he has spoken rebellion against the LORD.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018Write all the words that I have spoken to you in a book."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For, behold, the days come,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018that I will reverse the captivity of my people Israel and Judah,\u2019 says the LORD. \u2018I will cause them to return to the land that I gave to their fathers, and they will possess it.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the words that the LORD spoke concerning Israel and concerning Judah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For the LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cWe have heard a voice of trembling;"],[2,"a voice of fear, and not of peace."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Ask now, and see whether a man travails with child."],[2,"Why do I see every man with his hands on his waist, as a woman in travail,"],[2,"and all faces are turned pale?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Alas, for that day is great, so that none is like it!"],[2,"It is even the time of Jacob\u2019s trouble;"],[2,"but he will be saved out of it."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"It will come to pass in that day, says the LORD of Armies, that I will break his yoke from off your neck,"],[2,"and will burst your bonds."],[2,"Strangers will no more make them their bondservants;"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"but they will serve the LORD their God,"],[2,"and David their king,"],[2,"whom I will raise up to them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore don\u2019t be afraid, O Jacob my servant, says the LORD."],[2,"Don\u2019t be dismayed, Israel."],[1,"For, behold, I will save you from afar,"],[2,"and save your offspring from the land of their captivity."],[1,"Jacob will return,"],[2,"and will be quiet and at ease."],[2,"No one will make him afraid."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For I am with you, says the LORD, to save you;"],[2,"for I will make a full end of all the nations where I have scattered you,"],[2,"but I will not make a full end of you;"],[1,"but I will correct you in measure,"],[2,"and will in no way leave you unpunished.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cYour hurt is incurable."],[2,"Your wound is grievous."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no one to plead your cause,"],[2,"that you may be bound up."],[2,"You have no healing medicines."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"All your lovers have forgotten you."],[2,"They don\u2019t seek you."],[1,"For I have wounded you with the wound of an enemy,"],[2,"with the chastisement of a cruel one,"],[1,"for the greatness of your iniquity,"],[2,"because your sins were increased."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you cry over your injury?"],[2,"Your pain is incurable."],[1,"For the greatness of your iniquity,"],[2,"because your sins have increased,"],[2,"I have done these things to you."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore all those who devour you will be devoured."],[2,"All your adversaries, everyone of them, will go into captivity."],[1,"Those who plunder you will be plunder."],[2,"I will make all who prey on you become prey."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will restore health to you,"],[2,"and I will heal you of your wounds,\u201d says the LORD,"],[1,"\u201cbecause they have called you an outcast,"],[2,"saying, \u2018It is Zion, whom no man seeks after.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I will reverse the captivity of Jacob\u2019s tents,"],[2,"and have compassion on his dwelling places."],[1,"The city will be built on its own hill,"],[2,"and the palace will be inhabited in its own place."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Thanksgiving will proceed out of them"],[2,"with the voice of those who make merry."],[1,"I will multiply them,"],[2,"and they will not be few;"],[1,"I will also glorify them,"],[2,"and they will not be small."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Their children also will be as before,"],[2,"and their congregation will be established before me."],[2,"I will punish all who oppress them."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Their prince will be one of them,"],[2,"and their ruler will proceed from among them."],[1,"I will cause him to draw near,"],[2,"and he will approach me;"],[2,"for who is he who has had boldness to approach me?\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou shall be my people,"],[2,"and I will be your God."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the LORD\u2019s storm, his wrath, has gone out,"],[2,"a sweeping storm;"],[2,"it will burst on the head of the wicked."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The fierce anger of the LORD will not return until he has accomplished,"],[2,"and until he has performed the intentions of his heart."],[2,"In the latter days you will understand it.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAt that time,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cI will be the God of all the families of Israel, and they will be my people.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u201cThe people who survive the sword found favor in the wilderness; even Israel, when I went to cause him to rest.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD appeared of old to me, saying,"],[1,"\u201cYes, I have loved you with an everlasting love."],[2,"Therefore I have drawn you with loving kindness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will build you again,"],[2,"and you will be built, O virgin of Israel."],[1,"You will again be adorned with your tambourines,"],[2,"and will go out in the dances of those who make merry."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Again you will plant vineyards on the mountains of Samaria."],[2,"The planters will plant,"],[2,"and will enjoy its fruit."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For there will be a day that the watchmen on the hills of Ephraim cry,"],[2,"\u2018Arise! Let\u2019s go up to Zion to the LORD our God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says,"],[1,"\u201cSing with gladness for Jacob,"],[2,"and shout for the chief of the nations."],[1,"Publish, praise, and say,"],[2,"\u2018LORD, save your people,"],[2,"the remnant of Israel!\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I will bring them from the north country,"],[2,"and gather them from the uttermost parts of the earth,"],[1,"along with the blind and the lame,"],[2,"the woman with child and her who travails with child together."],[2,"They will return as a great company."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They will come with weeping."],[2,"I will lead them with petitions."],[1,"I will cause them to walk by rivers of waters,"],[2,"in a straight way in which they won\u2019t stumble;"],[1,"for I am a father to Israel."],[2,"Ephraim is my firstborn."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHear the LORD\u2019s word, you nations,"],[2,"and declare it in the distant islands. Say,"],[1,"\u2018He who scattered Israel will gather him,"],[2,"and keep him, as a shepherd does his flock.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD has ransomed Jacob,"],[2,"and redeemed him from the hand of him who was stronger than he."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They will come and sing in the height of Zion,"],[2,"and will flow to the goodness of the LORD,"],[1,"to the grain, to the new wine, to the oil,"],[2,"and to the young of the flock and of the herd."],[1,"Their soul will be as a watered garden."],[2,"They will not sorrow any more at all."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the virgin will rejoice in the dance,"],[2,"the young men and the old together;"],[1,"for I will turn their mourning into joy,"],[2,"and will comfort them, and make them rejoice from their sorrow."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will satiate the soul of the priests with fatness,"],[2,"and my people will be satisfied with my goodness,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cA voice is heard in Ramah,"],[2,"lamentation and bitter weeping,"],[1,"Rachel weeping for her children."],[2,"She refuses to be comforted for her children,"],[2,"because they are no more.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cRefrain your voice from weeping,"],[2,"and your eyes from tears,"],[2,"for your work will be rewarded,\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cThey will come again from the land of the enemy."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"There is hope for your latter end,\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cYour children will come again to their own territory."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have surely heard Ephraim grieving thus,"],[2,"\u2018You have chastised me,"],[2,"and I was chastised, as an untrained calf."],[1,"Turn me, and I will be turned,"],[2,"for you are the LORD my God."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely after that I was turned."],[2,"I repented."],[1,"After that I was instructed."],[2,"I struck my thigh."],[1,"I was ashamed, yes, even confounded,"],[2,"because I bore the reproach of my youth.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Is Ephraim my dear son?"],[2,"Is he a darling child?"],[1,"For as often as I speak against him,"],[2,"I still earnestly remember him."],[1,"Therefore my heart yearns for him."],[2,"I will surely have mercy on him,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSet up road signs."],[2,"Make guideposts."],[1,"Set your heart toward the highway,"],[2,"even the way by which you went."],[1,"Turn again, virgin of Israel."],[2,"Turn again to these your cities."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"How long will you go here and there,"],[2,"you backsliding daughter?"],[1,"For the LORD has created a new thing on the earth:"],[2,"a woman will encompass a man.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u201cYet again they will use this speech in the land of Judah and in its cities, when I reverse their captivity: \u2018The LORD bless you, habitation of righteousness, mountain of holiness.\u2019"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Judah and all its cities will dwell therein together, the farmers, and those who go about with flocks."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For I have satiated the weary soul, and I have replenished every sorrowful soul.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"On this I awakened, and saw; and my sleep was sweet to me."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat I will sow the house of Israel and the house of Judah with the seed of man and with the seed of animal."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"It will happen that, like as I have watched over them to pluck up and to break down and to overthrow and to destroy and to afflict, so I will watch over them to build and to plant,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"\u201cIn those days they will say no more,"],[1,"\u201c\u2018The fathers have eaten sour grapes,"],[2,"and the children\u2019s teeth are set on edge.\u2019"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"But everyone will die for his own iniquity. Every man who eats the sour grapes, his teeth will be set on edge."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel, and with the house of Judah,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers in the day that I took them by the hand to bring them out of the land of Egypt, which covenant of mine they broke, although I was a husband to them,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"\u201cBut this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel after those days,\u201d says the LORD:"],[1,"\u201cI will put my law in their inward parts,"],[2,"and I will write it in their heart."],[1,"I will be their God,"],[2,"and they shall be my people."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"They will no longer each teach his neighbor,"],[2,"and every man teach his brother, saying, \u2018Know the LORD;\u2019"],[1,"for they will all know me,"],[2,"from their least to their greatest,\u201d says the LORD,"],[1,"\u201cfor I will forgive their iniquity,"],[2,"and I will remember their sin no more.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD, who gives the sun for a light by day,"],[2,"and the ordinances of the moon and of the stars for a light by night,"],[1,"who stirs up the sea, so that its waves roar\u2014"],[2,"the LORD of Armies is his name, says:"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIf these ordinances depart from before me,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthen the offspring of Israel also will cease from being a nation before me forever.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD says: \u201cIf heaven above can be measured,"],[2,"and the foundations of the earth searched out beneath,"],[2,"then I will also cast off all the offspring of Israel for all that they have done,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat the city will be built to the LORD from the tower of Hananel to the gate of the corner."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The measuring line will go out further straight onward to the hill Gareb, and will turn toward Goah."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The whole valley of the dead bodies and of the ashes, and all the fields to the brook Kidron, to the corner of the horse gate toward the east, will be holy to the LORD. It will not be plucked up or thrown down any more forever.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the word that came to Jeremiah from the LORD in the tenth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, which was the eighteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now at that time the king of Babylon\u2019s army was besieging Jerusalem. Jeremiah the prophet was shut up in the court of the guard, which was in the king of Judah\u2019s house."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"For Zedekiah king of Judah had shut him up, saying, \u201cWhy do you prophesy, and say, \u2018The LORD says, \u201cBehold, I will give this city into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he will take it;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and Zedekiah king of Judah won\u2019t escape out of the hand of the Chaldeans, but will surely be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon, and will speak with him mouth to mouth, and his eyes will see his eyes;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and he will bring Zedekiah to Babylon, and he will be there until I visit him,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthough you fight with the Chaldeans, you will not prosper\u201d\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Jeremiah said, \u201cThe LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u2018Behold, Hanamel the son of Shallum your uncle will come to you, saying, \u201cBuy my field that is in Anathoth; for the right of redemption is yours to buy it.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo Hanamel my uncle\u2019s son came to me in the court of the guard according to the LORD\u2019s word, and said to me, \u2018Please buy my field that is in Anathoth, which is in the land of Benjamin; for the right of inheritance is yours, and the redemption is yours. Buy it for yourself.\u2019"],[0,"\u201cThen I knew that this was the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I bought the field that was in Anathoth of Hanamel my uncle\u2019s son, and weighed him the money, even seventeen shekels of silver."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I signed the deed, sealed it, called witnesses, and weighed the money in the balances to him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"So I took the deed of the purchase, both that which was sealed, containing the terms and conditions, and that which was open;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and I delivered the deed of the purchase to Baruch the son of Neriah, the son of Mahseiah, in the presence of Hanamel my uncle\u2019s son, and in the presence of the witnesses who signed the deed of the purchase, before all the Jews who sat in the court of the guard."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI commanded Baruch before them, saying,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Take these deeds, this deed of the purchase which is sealed, and this deed which is open, and put them in an earthen vessel, that they may last many days.\u2019"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says: \u2018Houses and fields and vineyards will yet again be bought in this land.\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after I had delivered the deed of the purchase to Baruch the son of Neriah, I prayed to the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAh Lord GOD! Behold, you have made the heavens and the earth by your great power and by your outstretched arm. There is nothing too hard for you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You show loving kindness to thousands, and repay the iniquity of the fathers into the bosom of their children after them. The great, the mighty God, the LORD of Armies is your name:"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"great in counsel, and mighty in work; whose eyes are open to all the ways of the children of men, to give everyone according to his ways, and according to the fruit of his doings;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"who performed signs and wonders in the land of Egypt, even to this day, both in Israel and among other men; and made yourself a name, as it is today;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and brought your people Israel out of the land of Egypt with signs, with wonders, with a strong hand, with an outstretched arm, and with great terror;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and gave them this land, which you swore to their fathers to give them, a land flowing with milk and honey."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They came in and possessed it, but they didn\u2019t obey your voice and didn\u2019t walk in your law. They have done nothing of all that you commanded them to do. Therefore you have caused all this evil to come upon them."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, siege ramps have been built against the city to take it. The city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans who fight against it, because of the sword, of the famine, and of the pestilence. What you have spoken has happened. Behold, you see it."]]},{v:25,l:[[1,"You have said to me, Lord GOD, \u2018Buy the field for money, and call witnesses;\u2019 whereas the city is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I am the LORD, the God of all flesh. Is there anything too hard for me?"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says: Behold, I will give this city into the hand of the Chaldeans, and into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and he will take it."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The Chaldeans, who fight against this city, will come and set this city on fire, and burn it with the houses on whose roofs they have offered incense to Baal, and poured out drink offerings to other gods, to provoke me to anger."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the children of Israel and the children of Judah have done only that which was evil in my sight from their youth; for the children of Israel have only provoked me to anger with the work of their hands, says the LORD."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For this city has been to me a provocation of my anger and of my wrath from the day that they built it even to this day, so that I should remove it from before my face,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"because of all the evil of the children of Israel and of the children of Judah, which they have done to provoke me to anger\u2014they, their kings, their princes, their priests, their prophets, the men of Judah, and the inhabitants of Jerusalem."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They have turned their backs to me, and not their faces. Although I taught them, rising up early and teaching them, yet they have not listened to receive instruction."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But they set their abominations in the house which is called by my name, to defile it."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"They built the high places of Baal, which are in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to cause their sons and their daughters to pass through fire to Molech, which I didn\u2019t command them. It didn\u2019t even come into my mind, that they should do this abomination, to cause Judah to sin.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Now therefore the LORD, the God of Israel, says concerning this city, about which you say, \u201cIt is given into the hand of the king of Babylon by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence:\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I will gather them out of all the countries where I have driven them in my anger, and in my wrath, and in great indignation; and I will bring them again to this place. I will cause them to dwell safely."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Then they will be my people, and I will be their God."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"I will give them one heart and one way, that they may fear me forever, for their good and the good of their children after them."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"I will make an everlasting covenant with them, that I will not turn away from following them, to do them good. I will put my fear in their hearts, that they may not depart from me."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Yes, I will rejoice over them to do them good, and I will plant them in this land assuredly with my whole heart and with my whole soul.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says: \u201cJust as I have brought all this great evil on this people, so I will bring on them all the good that I have promised them."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Fields will be bought in this land, about which you say, \u2018It is desolate, without man or animal. It is given into the hand of the Chaldeans.\u2019"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Men will buy fields for money, sign the deeds, seal them, and call witnesses, in the land of Benjamin, and in the places around Jerusalem, in the cities of Judah, in the cities of the hill country, in the cities of the lowland, and in the cities of the South; for I will cause their captivity to be reversed,\u201d says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah the second time, while he was still locked up in the court of the guard, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD who does it, the LORD who forms it to establish it\u2014the LORD is his name, says:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u2018Call to me, and I will answer you, and will show you great and difficult things, which you don\u2019t know.\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For the LORD, the God of Israel, says concerning the houses of this city and concerning the houses of the kings of Judah, which are broken down to make a defense against the mounds and against the sword:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u2018While men come to fight with the Chaldeans, and to fill them with the dead bodies of men, whom I have killed in my anger and in my wrath, and for all whose wickedness I have hidden my face from this city,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"behold, I will bring it health and healing, and I will cure them; and I will reveal to them abundance of peace and truth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I will restore the fortunes of Judah and Israel, and will build them as at the first."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will cleanse them from all their iniquity by which they have sinned against me. I will pardon all their iniquities by which they have sinned against me and by which they have transgressed against me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"This city will be to me for a name of joy, for praise, and for glory, before all the nations of the earth, which will hear all the good that I do to them, and will fear and tremble for all the good and for all the peace that I provide to it.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says: \u201cYet again there will be heard in this place, about which you say, \u2018It is waste, without man and without animal, even in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, that are desolate, without man and without inhabitant and without animal,\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"the voice of joy and the voice of gladness, the voice of the bridegroom and the voice of the bride, the voice of those who say, \u2018Give thanks to the LORD of Armies, for the LORD is good, for his loving kindness endures forever;\u2019 who bring thanksgiving into the LORD\u2019s house. For I will cause the captivity of the land to be reversed as at the first,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cYet again there will be in this place, which is waste, without man and without animal, and in all its cities, a habitation of shepherds causing their flocks to lie down."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"In the cities of the hill country, in the cities of the lowland, in the cities of the South, in the land of Benjamin, in the places around Jerusalem, and in the cities of Judah, the flocks will again pass under the hands of him who counts them,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat I will perform that good word which I have spoken concerning the house of Israel and concerning the house of Judah."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIn those days and at that time,"],[2,"I will cause a Branch of righteousness to grow up to David."],[2,"He will execute justice and righteousness in the land."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"In those days Judah will be saved,"],[2,"and Jerusalem will dwell safely."],[1,"This is the name by which she will be called:"],[2,"The LORD our righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says: \u201cDavid will never lack a man to sit on the throne of the house of Israel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The Levitical priests won\u2019t lack a man before me to offer burnt offerings, to burn meal offerings, and to do sacrifice continually.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD says: \u2018If you can break my covenant of the day and my covenant of the night, so that there will not be day and night in their time,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"then my covenant could also be broken with David my servant, that he won\u2019t have a son to reign on his throne; and with the Levitical priests, my ministers."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"As the army of the sky can\u2019t be counted, and the sand of the sea can\u2019t be measured, so I will multiply the offspring of David my servant and the Levites who minister to me.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t consider what this people has spoken, saying, \u2018Has the LORD cast off the two families which he chose?\u2019 Thus they despise my people, that they should be no more a nation before them.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The LORD says: \u201cIf my covenant of day and night fails, if I have not appointed the ordinances of heaven and earth,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"then I will also cast away the offspring of Jacob, and of David my servant, so that I will not take of his offspring to be rulers over the offspring of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob; for I will cause their captivity to be reversed and will have mercy on them.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word which came to Jeremiah from the LORD, when Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, with all his army, all the kingdoms of the earth that were under his dominion, and all the peoples, were fighting against Jerusalem and against all its cities, saying:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018Go, and speak to Zedekiah king of Judah, and tell him, the LORD says, \u201cBehold, I will give this city into the hand of the king of Babylon and he will burn it with fire."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You won\u2019t escape out of his hand, but will surely be taken and delivered into his hand. Your eyes will see the eyes of the king of Babylon, and he will speak with you mouth to mouth. You will go to Babylon.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYet hear the LORD\u2019s word, O Zedekiah king of Judah. The LORD says concerning you, \u2018You won\u2019t die by the sword."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You will die in peace; and with the burnings of your fathers, the former kings who were before you, so they will make a burning for you. They will lament you, saying, \u201cAh Lord!\u201d for I have spoken the word,\u2019 says the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah the prophet spoke all these words to Zedekiah king of Judah in Jerusalem,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"when the king of Babylon\u2019s army was fighting against Jerusalem and against all the cities of Judah that were left, against Lachish and against Azekah; for these alone remained of the cities of Judah as fortified cities."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The word came to Jeremiah from the LORD, after King Zedekiah had made a covenant with all the people who were at Jerusalem, to proclaim liberty to them,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"that every man should let his male servant, and every man his female servant, who is a Hebrew or a Hebrewess, go free, that no one should make bondservants of them, of a Jew his brother."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All the princes and all the people obeyed who had entered into the covenant, that everyone should let his male servant and everyone his female servant go free, that no one should make bondservants of them any more. They obeyed and let them go,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"but afterwards they turned, and caused the servants and the handmaids whom they had let go free to return, and brought them into subjection for servants and for handmaids."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says: \u2018I made a covenant with your fathers in the day that I brought them out of the land of Egypt, out of the house of bondage, saying:"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"At the end of seven years, every man of you shall release his brother who is a Hebrew, who has been sold to you, and has served you six years. You shall let him go free from you. But your fathers didn\u2019t listen to me, and didn\u2019t incline their ear."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You had now turned, and had done that which is right in my eyes, in every man proclaiming liberty to his neighbor. You had made a covenant before me in the house which is called by my name;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"but you turned and profaned my name, and every man caused his servant and every man his handmaid, whom you had let go free at their pleasure, to return. You brought them into subjection, to be to you for servants and for handmaids.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says: \u201cYou have not listened to me, to proclaim liberty, every man to his brother, and every man to his neighbor. Behold, I proclaim to you a liberty,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cto the sword, to the pestilence, and to the famine. I will make you be tossed back and forth among all the kingdoms of the earth."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I will give the men who have transgressed my covenant, who have not performed the words of the covenant which they made before me when they cut the calf in two and passed between its parts:"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the princes of Judah, the princes of Jerusalem, the eunuchs, the priests, and all the people of the land, who passed between the parts of the calf."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"I will even give them into the hand of their enemies and into the hand of those who seek their life. Their dead bodies will be food for the birds of the sky and for the animals of the earth."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI will give Zedekiah king of Judah and his princes into the hands of their enemies, into the hands of those who seek their life and into the hands of the king of Babylon\u2019s army, who has gone away from you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Behold, I will command,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cand cause them to return to this city. They will fight against it, take it, and burn it with fire. I will make the cities of Judah a desolation, without inhabitant.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word which came to Jeremiah from the LORD in the days of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cGo to the house of the Rechabites, and speak to them, and bring them into the LORD\u2019s house, into one of the rooms, and give them wine to drink.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I took Jaazaniah the son of Jeremiah, the son of Habazziniah, with his brothers, all his sons, and the whole house of the Rechabites;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and I brought them into the LORD\u2019s house, into the room of the sons of Hanan the son of Igdaliah, the man of God, which was by the room of the princes, which was above the room of Maaseiah the son of Shallum, the keeper of the threshold."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I set before the sons of the house of the Rechabites bowls full of wine, and cups; and I said to them, \u201cDrink wine!\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But they said, \u201cWe will drink no wine; for Jonadab the son of Rechab, our father, commanded us, saying, \u2018You shall drink no wine, neither you nor your children, forever."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall not build a house, sow seed, plant a vineyard, or have any; but all your days you shall dwell in tents, that you may live many days in the land in which you live as nomads.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"We have obeyed the voice of Jonadab the son of Rechab, our father, in all that he commanded us, to drink no wine all our days, we, our wives, our sons, or our daughters;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and not to build houses for ourselves to dwell in. We have no vineyard, field, or seed;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but we have lived in tents, and have obeyed, and done according to all that Jonadab our father commanded us."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But when Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came up into the land, we said, \u2018Come! Let\u2019s go to Jerusalem for fear of the army of the Chaldeans, and for fear of the army of the Syrians; so we will dwell at Jerusalem.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Go and tell the men of Judah and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, \u201cWill you not receive instruction to listen to my words?\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"\u201cThe words of Jonadab the son of Rechab that he commanded his sons, not to drink wine, are performed; and to this day they drink none, for they obey their father\u2019s commandment; but I have spoken to you, rising up early and speaking, and you have not listened to me."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I have sent also to you all my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending them, saying, \u2018Every one of you must return now from his evil way, amend your doings, and don\u2019t go after other gods to serve them. Then you will dwell in the land which I have given to you and to your fathers;\u2019 but you have not inclined your ear, nor listened to me."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The sons of Jonadab the son of Rechab have performed the commandment of their father which he commanded them, but this people has not listened to me.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the LORD, the God of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Behold, I will bring on Judah and on all the inhabitants of Jerusalem all the evil that I have pronounced against them, because I have spoken to them, but they have not heard; and I have called to them, but they have not answered.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Jeremiah said to the house of the Rechabites, \u201cThe LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Because you have obeyed the commandment of Jonadab your father, and kept all his precepts, and done according to all that he commanded you,\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"therefore the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Jonadab the son of Rechab will not lack a man to stand before me forever.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, this word came to Jeremiah from the LORD, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cTake a scroll of a book, and write in it all the words that I have spoken to you against Israel, against Judah, and against all the nations, from the day I spoke to you, from the days of Josiah even to this day."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It may be that the house of Judah will hear all the evil which I intend to do to them, that they may each return from his evil way; that I may forgive their iniquity and their sin.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah called Baruch the son of Neriah; and Baruch wrote from the mouth of Jeremiah all the LORD\u2019s words, which he had spoken to him, on a scroll of a book."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jeremiah commanded Baruch, saying, \u201cI am restricted. I can\u2019t go into the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore you go, and read from the scroll which you have written from my mouth, the LORD\u2019s words, in the ears of the people in the LORD\u2019s house on the fast day. Also you shall read them in the ears of all Judah who come out of their cities."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It may be they will present their supplication before the LORD, and will each return from his evil way; for the LORD has pronounced great anger and wrath against this people.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Baruch the son of Neriah did according to all that Jeremiah the prophet commanded him, reading in the book the LORD\u2019s words in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now in the fifth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, in the ninth month, all the people in Jerusalem and all the people who came from the cities of Judah to Jerusalem, proclaimed a fast before the LORD."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Then Baruch read the words of Jeremiah from the book in the LORD\u2019s house, in the room of Gemariah the son of Shaphan the scribe, in the upper court, at the entry of the new gate of the LORD\u2019s house, in the ears of all the people."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When Micaiah the son of Gemariah, the son of Shaphan, had heard out of the book all the LORD\u2019s words,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"he went down into the king\u2019s house, into the scribe\u2019s room; and behold, all the princes were sitting there, Elishama the scribe, Delaiah the son of Shemaiah, Elnathan the son of Achbor, Gemariah the son of Shaphan, Zedekiah the son of Hananiah, and all the princes."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then Micaiah declared to them all the words that he had heard, when Baruch read the book in the ears of the people."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore all the princes sent Jehudi the son of Nethaniah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Cushi, to Baruch, saying, \u201cTake in your hand the scroll in which you have read in the ears of the people, and come.\u201d"],[0,"So Baruch the son of Neriah took the scroll in his hand, and came to them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cSit down now, and read it in our hearing.\u201d"],[0,"So Baruch read it in their hearing."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when they had heard all the words, they turned in fear one toward another, and said to Baruch, \u201cWe will surely tell the king of all these words.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They asked Baruch, saying, \u201cTell us now, how did you write all these words at his mouth?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Baruch answered them, \u201cHe dictated all these words to me with his mouth, and I wrote them with ink in the book.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the princes said to Baruch, \u201cYou and Jeremiah go hide. Don\u2019t let anyone know where you are.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"They went in to the king into the court, but they had laid up the scroll in the room of Elishama the scribe. Then they told all the words in the hearing of the king."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So the king sent Jehudi to get the scroll, and he took it out of the room of Elishama the scribe. Jehudi read it in the hearing of the king, and in the hearing of all the princes who stood beside the king."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Now the king was sitting in the winter house in the ninth month, and there was a fire in the brazier burning before him."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When Jehudi had read three or four columns, the king cut it with the penknife, and cast it into the fire that was in the brazier, until all the scroll was consumed in the fire that was in the brazier."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The king and his servants who heard all these words were not afraid, and didn\u2019t tear their garments."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Moreover Elnathan and Delaiah and Gemariah had made intercession to the king that he would not burn the scroll; but he would not listen to them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The king commanded Jerahmeel the king\u2019s son, and Seraiah the son of Azriel, and Shelemiah the son of Abdeel, to arrest Baruch the scribe and Jeremiah the prophet; but the LORD hid them."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah, after the king had burned the scroll, and the words which Baruch wrote at the mouth of Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"\u201cTake again another scroll, and write in it all the former words that were in the first scroll, which Jehoiakim the king of Judah has burned."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Concerning Jehoiakim king of Judah you shall say, \u2018The LORD says: \u201cYou have burned this scroll, saying, \u2018Why have you written therein, saying, \u201cThe king of Babylon will certainly come and destroy this land, and will cause to cease from there man and animal\u201d?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says concerning Jehoiakim king of Judah: \u201cHe will have no one to sit on David\u2019s throne. His dead body will be cast out in the day to the heat, and in the night to the frost."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"I will punish him, his offspring, and his servants for their iniquity. I will bring on them, on the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and on the men of Judah, all the evil that I have pronounced against them, but they didn\u2019t listen.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah took another scroll, and gave it to Baruch the scribe, the son of Neriah, who wrote therein from the mouth of Jeremiah all the words of the book which Jehoiakim king of Judah had burned in the fire; and many similar words were added to them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Zedekiah the son of Josiah reigned as king instead of Coniah the son of Jehoiakim, whom Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon made king in the land of Judah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But neither he, nor his servants, nor the people of the land, listened to the LORD\u2019s words, which he spoke by the prophet Jeremiah."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Zedekiah the king sent Jehucal the son of Shelemiah and Zephaniah the son of Maaseiah, the priest, to the prophet Jeremiah, saying, \u201cPray now to the LORD our God for us.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jeremiah came in and went out among the people, for they had not put him into prison."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Pharaoh\u2019s army had come out of Egypt; and when the Chaldeans who were besieging Jerusalem heard news of them, they withdrew from Jerusalem."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to the prophet Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says, \u2018You shall tell the king of Judah, who sent you to me to inquire of me: \u201cBehold, Pharaoh\u2019s army, which has come out to help you, will return to Egypt into their own land."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The Chaldeans will come again, and fight against this city. They will take it and burn it with fire.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD says, \u2018Don\u2019t deceive yourselves, saying, \u201cThe Chaldeans will surely depart from us;\u201d for they will not depart."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For though you had struck the whole army of the Chaldeans who fight against you, and only wounded men remained among them, they would each rise up in his tent and burn this city with fire.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When the army of the Chaldeans had withdrawn from Jerusalem for fear of Pharaoh\u2019s army,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"then Jeremiah went out of Jerusalem to go into the land of Benjamin, to receive his portion there, in the middle of the people."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When he was in Benjamin\u2019s gate, a captain of the guard was there, whose name was Irijah, the son of Shelemiah, the son of Hananiah; and he seized Jeremiah the prophet, saying, \u201cYou are defecting to the Chaldeans!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah said, \u201cThat is false! I am not defecting to the Chaldeans.\u201d"],[0,"But he didn\u2019t listen to him; so Irijah seized Jeremiah, and brought him to the princes."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The princes were angry with Jeremiah, and struck him, and put him in prison in the house of Jonathan the scribe; for they had made that the prison."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jeremiah had come into the dungeon house and into the cells, and Jeremiah had remained there many days,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"then Zedekiah the king sent and had him brought out. The king asked him secretly in his house, \u201cIs there any word from the LORD?\u201d"],[0,"Jeremiah said, \u201cThere is.\u201d He also said, \u201cYou will be delivered into the hand of the king of Babylon.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Jeremiah said to King Zedekiah, \u201cHow have I sinned against you, against your servants, or against this people, that you have put me in prison?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now where are your prophets who prophesied to you, saying, \u2018The king of Babylon will not come against you, nor against this land\u2019?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now please hear, my lord the king: please let my supplication be presented before you, that you not cause me to return to the house of Jonathan the scribe, lest I die there.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zedekiah the king commanded, and they committed Jeremiah into the court of the guard. They gave him daily a loaf of bread out of the bakers\u2019 street, until all the bread in the city was gone. Thus Jeremiah remained in the court of the guard."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Shephatiah the son of Mattan, Gedaliah the son of Pashhur, Jucal the son of Shelemiah, and Pashhur the son of Malchijah heard the words that Jeremiah spoke to all the people, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD says, \u2018He who remains in this city will die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence, but he who goes out to the Chaldeans will live. He will escape with his life and he will live.\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u2018This city will surely be given into the hand of the army of the king of Babylon, and he will take it.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the princes said to the king, \u201cPlease let this man be put to death, because he weakens the hands of the men of war who remain in this city, and the hands of all the people, in speaking such words to them; for this man doesn\u2019t seek the welfare of this people, but harm.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Zedekiah the king said, \u201cBehold, he is in your hand; for the king can\u2019t do anything to oppose you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they took Jeremiah and threw him into the dungeon of Malchijah the king\u2019s son, that was in the court of the guard. They let down Jeremiah with cords. In the dungeon there was no water, but mire; and Jeremiah sank in the mire."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Ebedmelech the Ethiopian, a eunuch, who was in the king\u2019s house, heard that they had put Jeremiah in the dungeon (the king was then sitting in Benjamin\u2019s gate),"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Ebedmelech went out of the king\u2019s house, and spoke to the king, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cMy lord the king, these men have done evil in all that they have done to Jeremiah the prophet, whom they have cast into the dungeon. He is likely to die in the place where he is, because of the famine; for there is no more bread in the city.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king commanded Ebedmelech the Ethiopian, saying, \u201cTake from here thirty men with you, and take up Jeremiah the prophet out of the dungeon, before he dies.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"So Ebedmelech took the men with him, and went into the house of the king under the treasury, and took from there rags and worn-out garments, and let them down by cords into the dungeon to Jeremiah."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Ebedmelech the Ethiopian said to Jeremiah, \u201cNow put these rags and worn-out garments under your armpits under the cords.\u201d"],[0,"Jeremiah did so."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So they lifted Jeremiah up with the cords, and took him up out of the dungeon; and Jeremiah remained in the court of the guard."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zedekiah the king sent and took Jeremiah the prophet to himself into the third entry that is in the LORD\u2019s house. Then the king said to Jeremiah, \u201cI will ask you something. Hide nothing from me.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah said to Zedekiah, \u201cIf I declare it to you, will you not surely put me to death? If I give you counsel, you will not listen to me.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So Zedekiah the king swore secretly to Jeremiah, saying, \u201cAs the LORD lives, who made our souls, I will not put you to death, neither will I give you into the hand of these men who seek your life.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah said to Zedekiah, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018If you will go out to the king of Babylon\u2019s princes, then your soul will live, and this city will not be burned with fire. You will live, along with your house."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But if you will not go out to the king of Babylon\u2019s princes, then this city will be given into the hand of the Chaldeans, and they will burn it with fire, and you won\u2019t escape out of their hand.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Zedekiah the king said to Jeremiah, \u201cI am afraid of the Jews who have defected to the Chaldeans, lest they deliver me into their hand, and they mock me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jeremiah said, \u201cThey won\u2019t deliver you. Obey, I beg you, the LORD\u2019s voice, in that which I speak to you; so it will be well with you, and your soul will live."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But if you refuse to go out, this is the word that the LORD has shown me:"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"\u2018Behold, all the women who are left in the king of Judah\u2019s house will be brought out to the king of Babylon\u2019s princes, and those women will say,"],[1,"\u201cYour familiar friends have turned on you,"],[2,"and have prevailed over you."],[1,"Your feet are sunk in the mire,"],[2,"they have turned away from you.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"They will bring out all your wives and your children to the Chaldeans. You won\u2019t escape out of their hand, but will be taken by the hand of the king of Babylon. You will cause this city to be burned with fire.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zedekiah said to Jeremiah, \u201cLet no man know of these words, and you won\u2019t die."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But if the princes hear that I have talked with you, and they come to you, and tell you, \u2018Declare to us now what you have said to the king; don\u2019t hide it from us, and we will not put you to death; also tell us what the king said to you;\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"then you shall tell them, \u2018I presented my supplication before the king, that he would not cause me to return to Jonathan\u2019s house, to die there.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the princes came to Jeremiah, and asked him; and he told them according to all these words that the king had commanded. So they stopped speaking with him, for the matter was not perceived."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jeremiah stayed in the court of the guard until the day that Jerusalem was taken."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the ninth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the tenth month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon and all his army came against Jerusalem, and besieged it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In the eleventh year of Zedekiah, in the fourth month, the ninth day of the month, a breach was made in the city."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All the princes of the king of Babylon came in, and sat in the middle gate: Nergal Sharezer, Samgarnebo, Sarsechim the Rabsaris, Nergal Sharezer the Rabmag, with all the rest of the princes of the king of Babylon."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When Zedekiah the king of Judah and all the men of war saw them, then they fled and went out of the city by night, by the way of the king\u2019s garden, through the gate between the two walls; and he went out toward the Arabah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But the army of the Chaldeans pursued them, and overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho. When they had taken him, they brought him up to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon to Riblah in the land of Hamath; and he pronounced judgment on him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then the king of Babylon killed Zedekiah\u2019s sons in Riblah before his eyes. The king of Babylon also killed all the nobles of Judah."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Moreover he put out Zedekiah\u2019s eyes and bound him in fetters, to carry him to Babylon."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The Chaldeans burned the king\u2019s house and the people\u2019s houses with fire and broke down the walls of Jerusalem."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive into Babylon the rest of the people who remained in the city, the deserters also who fell away to him, and the rest of the people who remained."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard left of the poor of the people, who had nothing, in the land of Judah, and gave them vineyards and fields at the same time."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon commanded Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard concerning Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cTake him and take care of him. Do him no harm; but do to him even as he tells you.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"So Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard, Nebushazban, Rabsaris, and Nergal Sharezer, Rabmag, and all the chief officers of the king of Babylon"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"sent and took Jeremiah out of the court of the guard, and committed him to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, that he should bring him home. So he lived among the people."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah while he was shut up in the court of the guard, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cGo, and speak to Ebedmelech the Ethiopian, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u201cBehold, I will bring my words on this city for evil, and not for good; and they will be accomplished before you in that day."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But I will deliver you in that day,\u201d says the LORD; \u201cand you will not be given into the hand of the men of whom you are afraid."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For I will surely save you. You won\u2019t fall by the sword, but you will escape with your life, because you have put your trust in me,\u201d says the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word which came to Jeremiah from the LORD, after Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had let him go from Ramah, when he had taken him being bound in chains among all the captives of Jerusalem and Judah who were carried away captive to Babylon."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The captain of the guard took Jeremiah and said to him, \u201cThe LORD your God pronounced this evil on this place;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and the LORD has brought it, and done according as he spoke. Because you have sinned against the LORD, and have not obeyed his voice, therefore this thing has come on you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now, behold, I release you today from the chains which are on your hand. If it seems good to you to come with me into Babylon, come, and I will take care of you; but if it seems bad to you to come with me into Babylon, don\u2019t. Behold, all the land is before you. Where it seems good and right to you to go, go there.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now while he had not yet gone back, \u201cGo back then,\u201d he said, \u201cto Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan, whom the king of Babylon has made governor over the cities of Judah, and dwell with him among the people; or go wherever it seems right to you to go.\u201d"],[0,"So the captain of the guard gave him food and a present, and let him go."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah went to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam to Mizpah, and lived with him among the people who were left in the land."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when all the captains of the forces who were in the fields, even they and their men, heard that the king of Babylon had made Gedaliah the son of Ahikam governor in the land, and had committed to him men, women, children, and of the poorest of the land, of those who were not carried away captive to Babylon,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"then Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and Johanan and Jonathan the sons of Kareah, and Seraiah the son of Tanhumeth, and the sons of Ephai the Netophathite, and Jezaniah the son of the Maacathite, they and their men came to Gedaliah to Mizpah."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan swore to them and to their men, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid to serve the Chaldeans. Dwell in the land, and serve the king of Babylon, and it will be well with you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As for me, behold, I will dwell at Mizpah, to stand before the Chaldeans who will come to us; but you, gather wine and summer fruits and oil, and put them in your vessels, and dwell in your cities that you have taken.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Likewise when all the Jews who were in Moab, and among the children of Ammon, and in Edom, and who were in all the countries, heard that the king of Babylon had left a remnant of Judah, and that he had set over them Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"then all the Jews returned out of all places where they were driven, and came to the land of Judah, to Gedaliah, to Mizpah, and gathered very much wine and summer fruits."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces who were in the fields, came to Gedaliah to Mizpah,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cDo you know that Baalis the king of the children of Ammon has sent Ishmael the son of Nethaniah to take your life?\u201d"],[0,"But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam didn\u2019t believe them."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Johanan the son of Kareah spoke to Gedaliah in Mizpah secretly, saying, \u201cPlease let me go, and I will kill Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and no man will know it. Why should he take your life, that all the Jews who are gathered to you should be scattered, and the remnant of Judah perish?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But Gedaliah the son of Ahikam said to Johanan the son of Kareah, \u201cYou shall not do this thing, for you speak falsely of Ishmael.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the seventh month, Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, the son of Elishama, of the royal offspring and one of the chief officers of the king, and ten men with him, came to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam to Mizpah; and there they ate bread together in Mizpah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Ishmael the son of Nethaniah arose, and the ten men who were with him, and struck Gedaliah the son of Ahikam the son of Shaphan with the sword and killed him, whom the king of Babylon had made governor over the land."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Ishmael also killed all the Jews who were with Gedaliah at Mizpah, and the Chaldean men of war who were found there."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The second day after he had killed Gedaliah, and no man knew it,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"men came from Shechem, from Shiloh, and from Samaria, even eighty men, having their beards shaved and their clothes torn, and having cut themselves, with meal offerings and frankincense in their hand, to bring them to the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Ishmael the son of Nethaniah went out from Mizpah to meet them, weeping all along as he went, and as he met them, he said to them, \u201cCome to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It was so, when they came into the middle of the city, that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah killed them, and cast them into the middle of the pit, he, and the men who were with him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But ten men were found among those who said to Ishmael, \u201cDon\u2019t kill us; for we have stores hidden in the field, of wheat, and of barley, and of oil, and of honey.\u201d"],[0,"So he stopped, and didn\u2019t kill them among their brothers."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now the pit in which Ishmael cast all the dead bodies of the men whom he had killed, by the side of Gedaliah (this was that which Asa the king had made for fear of Baasha king of Israel), Ishmael the son of Nethaniah filled it with those who were killed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Ishmael carried away captive all of the people who were left in Mizpah, even the king\u2019s daughters, and all the people who remained in Mizpah, whom Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had committed to Gedaliah the son of Ahikam. Ishmael the son of Nethaniah carried them away captive, and departed to go over to the children of Ammon."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces who were with him, heard of all the evil that Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had done,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"then they took all the men, and went to fight with Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, and found him by the great waters that are in Gibeon."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now when all the people who were with Ishmael saw Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces who were with him, then they were glad."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So all the people who Ishmael had carried away captive from Mizpah turned about and came back, and went to Johanan the son of Kareah."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But Ishmael the son of Nethaniah escaped from Johanan with eight men, and went to the children of Ammon."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Johanan the son of Kareah and all the captains of the forces who were with him took all the remnant of the people whom he had recovered from Ishmael the son of Nethaniah, from Mizpah, after he had killed Gedaliah the son of Ahikam\u2014the men of war, with the women, the children, and the eunuchs, whom he had brought back from Gibeon."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They departed and lived in Geruth Chimham, which is by Bethlehem, to go to enter into Egypt"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"because of the Chaldeans; for they were afraid of them, because Ishmael the son of Nethaniah had killed Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, whom the king of Babylon made governor over the land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the captains of the forces, and Johanan the son of Kareah, and Jezaniah the son of Hoshaiah, and all the people from the least even to the greatest, came near,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and said to Jeremiah the prophet, \u201cPlease let our supplication be presented before you, and pray for us to the LORD your God, even for all this remnant, for we are left but a few of many, as your eyes see us,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"that the LORD your God may show us the way in which we should walk, and the things that we should do.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah the prophet said to them, \u201cI have heard you. Behold, I will pray to the LORD your God according to your words; and it will happen that whatever thing the LORD answers you, I will declare it to you. I will keep nothing back from you.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they said to Jeremiah, \u201cMay the LORD be a true and faithful witness among us, if we don\u2019t do according to all the word with which the LORD your God sends you to tell us."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Whether it is good, or whether it is bad, we will obey the voice of the LORD our God, to whom we send you; that it may be well with us, when we obey the voice of the LORD our God.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"After ten days, the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then he called Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces who were with him, and all the people from the least even to the greatest,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, to whom you sent me to present your supplication before him, says:"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u2018If you will still live in this land, then I will build you, and not pull you down, and I will plant you, and not pluck you up; for I grieve over the distress that I have brought on you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be afraid of the king of Babylon, of whom you are afraid. Don\u2019t be afraid of him,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018for I am with you to save you, and to deliver you from his hand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I will grant you mercy, that he may have mercy on you, and cause you to return to your own land."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But if you say, \u201cWe will not dwell in this land,\u201d so that you don\u2019t obey the LORD your God\u2019s voice,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cNo, but we will go into the land of Egypt, where we will see no war, nor hear the sound of the trumpet, nor have hunger of bread; and there we will dwell;\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"now therefore hear the LORD\u2019s word, O remnant of Judah! The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says, \u2018If you indeed set your faces to enter into Egypt, and go to live there,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"then it will happen that the sword, which you fear, will overtake you there in the land of Egypt; and the famine, about which you are afraid, will follow close behind you there in Egypt; and you will die there."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So will it be with all the men who set their faces to go into Egypt to live there. They will die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence. None of them will remain or escape from the evil that I will bring on them.\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018As my anger and my wrath has been poured out on the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so my wrath will be poured out on you, when you enter into Egypt; and you will be an object of horror, an astonishment, a curse, and a reproach; and you will see this place no more.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD has spoken concerning you, remnant of Judah, \u2018Don\u2019t go into Egypt!\u2019 Know certainly that I have testified to you today."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For you have dealt deceitfully against your own souls; for you sent me to the LORD your God, saying, \u2018Pray for us to the LORD our God; and according to all that the LORD our God says, so declare to us, and we will do it.\u2019"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I have declared it to you today; but you have not obeyed the LORD your God\u2019s voice in anything for which he has sent me to you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Now therefore know certainly that you will die by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence in the place where you desire to go to live.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jeremiah had finished speaking to all the people all the words of the LORD their God, with which the LORD their God had sent him to them, even all these words,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"then Azariah the son of Hoshaiah, Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the proud men spoke, saying to Jeremiah, \u201cYou speak falsely. The LORD our God has not sent you to say, \u2018You shall not go into Egypt to live there;\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"but Baruch the son of Neriah has turned you against us, to deliver us into the hand of the Chaldeans, that they may put us to death or carry us away captive to Babylon.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"So Johanan the son of Kareah, and all the captains of the forces, and all the people, didn\u2019t obey the LORD\u2019s voice, to dwell in the land of Judah."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But Johanan the son of Kareah and all the captains of the forces took all the remnant of Judah, who had returned from all the nations where they had been driven, to live in the land of Judah\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"the men, the women, the children, the king\u2019s daughters, and every person who Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard had left with Gedaliah the son of Ahikam, the son of Shaphan; and Jeremiah the prophet, and Baruch the son of Neriah."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They came into the land of Egypt, for they didn\u2019t obey the LORD\u2019s voice; and they came to Tahpanhes."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah in Tahpanhes, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cTake great stones in your hand and hide them in mortar in the brick work which is at the entry of Pharaoh\u2019s house in Tahpanhes, in the sight of the men of Judah."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Tell them, the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Behold, I will send and take Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon, my servant, and will set his throne on these stones that I have hidden; and he will spread his royal pavilion over them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He will come, and will strike the land of Egypt; such as are for death will be put to death, and such as are for captivity to captivity, and such as are for the sword to the sword."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I will kindle a fire in the houses of the gods of Egypt. He will burn them, and carry them away captive. He will array himself with the land of Egypt, as a shepherd puts on his garment; and he will go out from there in peace."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He will also break the pillars of Beth Shemesh that is in the land of Egypt; and he will burn the houses of the gods of Egypt with fire.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word that came to Jeremiah concerning all the Jews who lived in the land of Egypt, who lived at Migdol, and at Tahpanhes, and at Memphis, and in the country of Pathros, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018You have seen all the evil that I have brought on Jerusalem, and on all the cities of Judah. Behold, today they are a desolation, and no man dwells in them,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"because of their wickedness which they have committed to provoke me to anger, in that they went to burn incense, to serve other gods that they didn\u2019t know, neither they, nor you, nor your fathers."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"However I sent to you all my servants the prophets, rising up early and sending them, saying, \u201cOh, don\u2019t do this abominable thing that I hate.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But they didn\u2019t listen and didn\u2019t incline their ear. They didn\u2019t turn from their wickedness, to stop burning incense to other gods."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore my wrath and my anger was poured out, and was kindled in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem; and they are wasted and desolate, as it is today.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore now the LORD, the God of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Why do you commit great evil against your own souls, to cut off from yourselves man and woman, infant and nursing child out of the middle of Judah, to leave yourselves no one remaining,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"in that you provoke me to anger with the works of your hands, burning incense to other gods in the land of Egypt where you have gone to live, that you may be cut off, and that you may be a curse and a reproach among all the nations of the earth?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Have you forgotten the wickedness of your fathers, the wickedness of the kings of Judah, the wickedness of their wives, your own wickedness, and the wickedness of your wives which they committed in the land of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They are not humbled even to this day, neither have they feared, nor walked in my law, nor in my statutes, that I set before you and before your fathers.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u2018Behold, I will set my face against you for evil, even to cut off all Judah."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I will take the remnant of Judah that have set their faces to go into the land of Egypt to live there, and they will all be consumed. They will fall in the land of Egypt. They will be consumed by the sword and by the famine. They will die, from the least even to the greatest, by the sword and by the famine. They will be an object of horror, an astonishment, a curse, and a reproach."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For I will punish those who dwell in the land of Egypt, as I have punished Jerusalem, by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"so that none of the remnant of Judah, who have gone into the land of Egypt to live there, will escape or be left to return into the land of Judah, to which they have a desire to return to dwell there; for no one will return except those who will escape.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the men who knew that their wives burned incense to other gods, and all the women who stood by, a great assembly, even all the people who lived in the land of Egypt, in Pathros, answered Jeremiah, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for the word that you have spoken to us in the LORD\u2019s name, we will not listen to you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But we will certainly perform every word that has gone out of our mouth, to burn incense to the queen of the sky and to pour out drink offerings to her, as we have done, we and our fathers, our kings and our princes, in the cities of Judah and in the streets of Jerusalem; for then we had plenty of food, and were well, and saw no evil."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But since we stopped burning incense to the queen of the sky, and pouring out drink offerings to her, we have lacked all things, and have been consumed by the sword and by the famine.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The women said, \u201cWhen we burned incense to the queen of the sky and poured out drink offerings to her, did we make her cakes to worship her, and pour out drink offerings to her, without our husbands?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jeremiah said to all the people\u2014to the men and to the women, even to all the people who had given him an answer, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cThe incense that you burned in the cities of Judah, and in the streets of Jerusalem, you and your fathers, your kings and your princes, and the people of the land, didn\u2019t the LORD remember them, and didn\u2019t it come into his mind?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Thus the LORD could no longer bear it, because of the evil of your doings and because of the abominations which you have committed. Therefore your land has become a desolation, an astonishment, and a curse, without inhabitant, as it is today."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Because you have burned incense and because you have sinned against the LORD, and have not obeyed the LORD\u2019s voice, nor walked in his law, nor in his statutes, nor in his testimonies; therefore this evil has happened to you, as it is today.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover Jeremiah said to all the people, including all the women, \u201cHear the LORD\u2019s word, all Judah who are in the land of Egypt!"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says, \u2018You and your wives have both spoken with your mouths, and with your hands have fulfilled it, saying, \u201cWe will surely perform our vows that we have vowed, to burn incense to the queen of the sky, and to pour out drink offerings to her.\u201d"],[0,"\u201c\u2018Establish then your vows, and perform your vows.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore hear the LORD\u2019s word, all Judah who dwell in the land of Egypt: \u2018Behold, I have sworn by my great name,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018that my name will no more be named in the mouth of any man of Judah in all the land of Egypt, saying, \u201cAs the Lord GOD lives.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Behold, I watch over them for evil, and not for good; and all the men of Judah who are in the land of Egypt will be consumed by the sword and by the famine, until they are all gone."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Those who escape the sword will return out of the land of Egypt into the land of Judah few in number. All the remnant of Judah, who have gone into the land of Egypt to live there, will know whose word will stand, mine or theirs."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018This will be the sign to you,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018that I will punish you in this place, that you may know that my words will surely stand against you for evil.\u2019"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The LORD says, \u2018Behold, I will give Pharaoh Hophra king of Egypt into the hand of his enemies and into the hand of those who seek his life, just as I gave Zedekiah king of Judah into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, who was his enemy and sought his life.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The message that Jeremiah the prophet spoke to Baruch the son of Neriah, when he wrote these words in a book at the mouth of Jeremiah, in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD, the God of Israel, says to you, Baruch:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u2018You said, \u201cWoe is me now! For the LORD has added sorrow to my pain! I am weary with my groaning, and I find no rest.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall tell him, the LORD says: \u2018Behold, that which I have built, I will break down, and that which I have planted I will pluck up; and this in the whole land."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Do you seek great things for yourself? Don\u2019t seek them; for, behold, I will bring evil on all flesh,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018but I will let you escape with your life wherever you go.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word which came to Jeremiah the prophet concerning the nations."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Egypt: concerning the army of Pharaoh Necoh king of Egypt, which was by the river Euphrates in Carchemish, which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon struck in the fourth year of Jehoiakim the son of Josiah, king of Judah."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cPrepare the buckler and shield,"],[2,"and draw near to battle!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Harness the horses, and get up, you horsemen,"],[2,"and stand up with your helmets."],[1,"Polish the spears,"],[2,"put on the coats of mail."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Why have I seen it?"],[2,"They are dismayed and are turned backward."],[1,"Their mighty ones are beaten down,"],[2,"have fled in haste,"],[2,"and don\u2019t look back."],[1,"Terror is on every side,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t let the swift flee away,"],[2,"nor the mighty man escape."],[1,"In the north by the river Euphrates"],[2,"they have stumbled and fallen."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWho is this who rises up like the Nile,"],[2,"like rivers whose waters surge?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Egypt rises up like the Nile,"],[2,"like rivers whose waters surge."],[1,"He says, \u2018I will rise up. I will cover the earth."],[2,"I will destroy cities and its inhabitants.\u2019"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Go up, you horses!"],[2,"Rage, you chariots!"],[1,"Let the mighty men go out:"],[2,"Cush and Put, who handle the shield;"],[2,"and the Ludim, who handle and bend the bow."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"For that day is of the Lord, GOD of Armies,"],[2,"a day of vengeance,"],[2,"that he may avenge himself of his adversaries."],[1,"The sword will devour and be satiated,"],[2,"and will drink its fill of their blood;"],[2,"for the Lord, GOD of Armies, has a sacrifice in the north country by the river Euphrates."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Go up into Gilead, and take balm, virgin daughter of Egypt."],[2,"You use many medicines in vain."],[2,"There is no healing for you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The nations have heard of your shame,"],[2,"and the earth is full of your cry;"],[2,"for the mighty man has stumbled against the mighty,"],[2,"they both fall together.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The word that the LORD spoke to Jeremiah the prophet, how that Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon should come and strike the land of Egypt:"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDeclare in Egypt,"],[2,"publish in Migdol,"],[2,"and publish in Memphis and in Tahpanhes;"],[1,"say, \u2018Stand up, and prepare,"],[2,"for the sword has devoured around you.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Why are your strong ones swept away?"],[2,"They didn\u2019t stand, because the LORD pushed them."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He made many to stumble."],[2,"Yes, they fell on one another."],[1,"They said, \u2018Arise! Let\u2019s go again to our own people,"],[2,"and to the land of our birth,"],[2,"from the oppressing sword.\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"They cried there, \u2018Pharaoh king of Egypt is but a noise;"],[2,"he has let the appointed time pass by.\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAs I live,\u201d says the King,"],[2,"whose name is the LORD of Armies,"],[1,"\u201csurely like Tabor among the mountains,"],[2,"and like Carmel by the sea,"],[2,"so he will come."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"You daughter who dwells in Egypt,"],[2,"furnish yourself to go into captivity;"],[1,"for Memphis will become a desolation,"],[2,"and will be burned up,"],[2,"without inhabitant."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEgypt is a very beautiful heifer;"],[2,"but destruction out of the north has come."],[2,"It has come."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Also her hired men in the middle of her are like calves of the stall,"],[2,"for they also are turned back."],[2,"They have fled away together."],[1,"They didn\u2019t stand,"],[2,"for the day of their calamity has come on them,"],[2,"the time of their visitation."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Its sound will go like the serpent,"],[2,"for they will march with an army,"],[2,"and come against her with axes, as wood cutters."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"They will cut down her forest,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthough it can\u2019t be searched;"],[1,"because they are more than the locusts,"],[2,"and are innumerable."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The daughter of Egypt will be disappointed;"],[2,"she will be delivered into the hand of the people of the north.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says: \u201cBehold, I will punish Amon of No, and Pharaoh, and Egypt, with her gods and her kings, even Pharaoh, and those who trust in him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I will deliver them into the hand of those who seek their lives, and into the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, and into the hand of his servants. Afterwards it will be inhabited, as in the days of old,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut don\u2019t you be afraid, Jacob my servant."],[2,"Don\u2019t be dismayed, Israel;"],[1,"for, behold, I will save you from afar,"],[2,"and your offspring from the land of their captivity."],[1,"Jacob will return,"],[2,"and will be quiet and at ease."],[2,"No one will make him afraid."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be afraid, O Jacob my servant,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cfor I am with you;"],[2,"for I will make a full end of all the nations where I have driven you,"],[1,"but I will not make a full end of you,"],[2,"but I will correct you in measure,"],[2,"and will in no way leave you unpunished.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word that came to Jeremiah the prophet concerning the Philistines, before Pharaoh struck Gaza."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, waters rise up out of the north,"],[2,"and will become an overflowing stream,"],[1,"and will overflow the land and all that is therein,"],[2,"the city and those who dwell therein."],[1,"The men will cry,"],[2,"and all the inhabitants of the land will wail."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"At the noise of the stamping of the hoofs of his strong ones,"],[2,"at the rushing of his chariots,"],[2,"at the rumbling of his wheels,"],[1,"the fathers don\u2019t look back for their children"],[2,"because their hands are so feeble,"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"because of the day that comes to destroy all the Philistines,"],[2,"to cut off from Tyre and Sidon every helper who remains;"],[1,"for the LORD will destroy the Philistines,"],[2,"the remnant of the isle of Caphtor."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Baldness has come on Gaza;"],[2,"Ashkelon is brought to nothing."],[1,"You remnant of their valley,"],[2,"how long will you cut yourself?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018You sword of the LORD, how long will it be before you are quiet?"],[2,"Put yourself back into your scabbard;"],[2,"rest, and be still.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow can you be quiet,"],[2,"since the LORD has given you a command?"],[1,"Against Ashkelon, and against the seashore,"],[2,"there he has appointed it.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Moab. The LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says:"],[1,"\u201cWoe to Nebo!"],[2,"For it is laid waste."],[1,"Kiriathaim is disappointed."],[2,"It is taken."],[1,"Misgab is put to shame"],[2,"and broken down."]],f:["or, The stronghold"]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The praise of Moab is no more."],[2,"In Heshbon they have devised evil against her:"],[2,"\u2018Come! Let\u2019s cut her off from being a nation.\u2019"],[1,"You also, Madmen, will be brought to silence."],[2,"The sword will pursue you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The sound of a cry from Horonaim,"],[2,"desolation and great destruction!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Moab is destroyed."],[2,"Her little ones have caused a cry to be heard."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For they will go up by the ascent of Luhith with continual weeping."],[2,"For at the descent of Horonaim they have heard the distress of the cry of destruction."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Flee! Save your lives!"],[2,"Be like the juniper bush in the wilderness."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For, because you have trusted in your works and in your treasures,"],[2,"you also will be taken."],[1,"Chemosh will go out into captivity,"],[2,"his priests and his princes together."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The destroyer will come on every city,"],[2,"and no city will escape;"],[1,"the valley also will perish,"],[2,"and the plain will be destroyed, as the LORD has spoken."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Give wings to Moab,"],[2,"that she may fly and get herself away:"],[1,"and her cities will become a desolation,"],[2,"without anyone to dwell in them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCursed is he who does the work of the LORD negligently;"],[2,"and cursed is he who keeps back his sword from blood."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMoab has been at ease from his youth,"],[2,"and he has settled on his dregs,"],[1,"and has not been emptied from vessel to vessel,"],[2,"neither has he gone into captivity;"],[1,"therefore his taste remains in him,"],[2,"and his scent is not changed."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore behold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthat I will send to him those who pour off,"],[1,"and they will pour him off;"],[2,"and they will empty his vessels,"],[2,"and break their containers in pieces."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Moab will be ashamed of Chemosh,"],[2,"as the house of Israel was ashamed of Bethel, their confidence."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow do you say, \u2018We are mighty men,"],[2,"and valiant men for the war\u2019?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Moab is laid waste,"],[2,"and they have gone up into his cities,"],[2,"and his chosen young men have gone down to the slaughter,\u201d"],[2,"says the King, whose name is the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe calamity of Moab is near to come,"],[2,"and his affliction hurries fast."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"All you who are around him, bemoan him;"],[2,"and all you who know his name, say,"],[1,"\u2018How the strong staff is broken,"],[2,"the beautiful rod!\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou daughter who dwells in Dibon,"],[2,"come down from your glory,"],[2,"and sit in thirst;"],[1,"for the destroyer of Moab has come up against you."],[2,"He has destroyed your strongholds."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Inhabitant of Aroer, stand by the way and watch."],[2,"Ask him who flees, and her who escapes;"],[2,"say, \u2018What has been done?\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Moab is disappointed;"],[2,"for it is broken down."],[1,"Wail and cry!"],[2,"Tell it by the Arnon, that Moab is laid waste."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Judgment has come on the plain country\u2014"],[2,"on Holon, on Jahzah, on Mephaath,"]]},{v:22,l:[[2,"on Dibon, on Nebo, on Beth Diblathaim,"]]},{v:23,l:[[2,"on Kiriathaim, on Beth Gamul, on Beth Meon,"]]},{v:24,l:[[2,"on Kerioth, on Bozrah,"],[2,"and on all the cities of the land of Moab, far or near."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The horn of Moab is cut off,"],[2,"and his arm is broken,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMake him drunk,"],[2,"for he magnified himself against the LORD."],[1,"Moab will wallow in his vomit,"],[2,"and he also will be in derision."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"For wasn\u2019t Israel a derision to you?"],[2,"Was he found among thieves?"],[1,"For as often as you speak of him,"],[2,"you shake your head."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"You inhabitants of Moab, leave the cities, and dwell in the rock."],[2,"Be like the dove that makes her nest over the mouth of the abyss."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWe have heard of the pride of Moab."],[2,"He is very proud in his loftiness, his pride,"],[2,"his arrogance, and the arrogance of his heart."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"I know his wrath,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat it is nothing;"],[2,"his boastings have done nothing."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will wail for Moab."],[2,"Yes, I will cry out for all Moab."],[2,"They will mourn for the men of Kir Heres."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"With more than the weeping of Jazer"],[2,"I will weep for you, vine of Sibmah."],[1,"Your branches passed over the sea."],[2,"They reached even to the sea of Jazer."],[1,"The destroyer has fallen on your summer fruits"],[2,"and on your vintage."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Gladness and joy is taken away from the fruitful field"],[2,"and from the land of Moab."],[1,"I have caused wine to cease from the wine presses."],[2,"No one will tread with shouting."],[2,"The shouting will be no shouting."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"From the cry of Heshbon even to Elealeh,"],[2,"even to Jahaz they have uttered their voice,"],[2,"from Zoar even to Horonaim, to Eglath Shelishiyah;"],[2,"for the waters of Nimrim will also become desolate."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"Moreover I will cause to cease in Moab,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201chim who offers in the high place,"],[2,"and him who burns incense to his gods."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore my heart sounds for Moab like flutes,"],[2,"and my heart sounds like flutes for the men of Kir Heres."],[2,"Therefore the abundance that he has gotten has perished."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"For every head is bald,"],[2,"and every beard clipped."],[1,"There are cuttings on all the hands,"],[2,"and sackcloth on the waist."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"On all the housetops of Moab,"],[2,"and in its streets, there is lamentation everywhere;"],[2,"for I have broken Moab like a vessel in which no one delights,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow it is broken down!"],[2,"How they wail!"],[1,"How Moab has turned the back with shame!"],[2,"So will Moab become a derision"],[2,"and a terror to all who are around him.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD says: \u201cBehold, he will fly as an eagle,"],[2,"and will spread out his wings against Moab."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"Kerioth is taken,"],[2,"and the strongholds are seized."],[1,"The heart of the mighty men of Moab at that day"],[2,"will be as the heart of a woman in her pangs."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"Moab will be destroyed from being a people,"],[2,"because he has magnified himself against the LORD."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Terror, the pit, and the snare are on you,"],[2,"inhabitant of Moab,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHe who flees from the terror will fall into the pit;"],[2,"and he who gets up out of the pit will be taken in the snare,"],[1,"for I will bring on him, even on Moab,"],[2,"the year of their visitation,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThose who fled stand without strength under the shadow of Heshbon;"],[2,"for a fire has gone out of Heshbon,"],[2,"and a flame from the middle of Sihon,"],[1,"and has devoured the corner of Moab,"],[2,"and the crown of the head of the tumultuous ones."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to you, O Moab!"],[2,"The people of Chemosh are undone;"],[1,"for your sons are taken away captive,"],[2,"and your daughters into captivity."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYet I will reverse the captivity of Moab in the latter days,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD."],[0,"Thus far is the judgment of Moab."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Of the children of Ammon. The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cHas Israel no sons?"],[2,"Has he no heir?"],[1,"Why then does Malcam possess Gad,"],[2,"and his people dwell in its cities?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore behold, the days come,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD,"],[1,"\u201cthat I will cause an alarm of war to be heard against Rabbah of the children of Ammon,"],[2,"and it will become a desolate heap,"],[2,"and her daughters will be burned with fire;"],[1,"then Israel will possess those who possessed him,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWail, Heshbon, for Ai is laid waste!"],[2,"Cry, you daughters of Rabbah!"],[1,"Clothe yourself in sackcloth."],[2,"Lament, and run back and forth among the fences;"],[1,"for Malcam will go into captivity,"],[2,"his priests and his princes together."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you boast in the valleys,"],[2,"your flowing valley, backsliding daughter?"],[1,"You trusted in her treasures,"],[2,"saying, \u2018Who will come to me?\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I will bring a terror on you,\u201d"],[2,"says the Lord, GOD of Armies,"],[1,"\u201cfrom all who are around you."],[2,"All of you will be driven completely out,"],[2,"and there will be no one to gather together the fugitives."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut afterward I will reverse the captivity of the children of Ammon,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Edom, the LORD of Armies says:"],[1,"\u201cIs wisdom no more in Teman?"],[2,"Has counsel perished from the prudent?"],[2,"Has their wisdom vanished?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Flee! Turn back!"],[2,"Dwell in the depths, inhabitants of Dedan;"],[2,"for I will bring the calamity of Esau on him when I visit him."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"If grape gatherers came to you,"],[2,"would they not leave some gleaning grapes?"],[1,"If thieves came by night,"],[2,"wouldn\u2019t they steal until they had enough?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But I have made Esau bare,"],[2,"I have uncovered his secret places,"],[2,"and he will not be able to hide himself."],[1,"His offspring is destroyed,"],[2,"with his brothers and his neighbors;"],[2,"and he is no more."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Leave your fatherless children."],[2,"I will preserve them alive."],[2,"Let your widows trust in me.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says: \u201cBehold, they to whom it didn\u2019t pertain to drink of the cup will certainly drink; and are you he who will altogether go unpunished? You won\u2019t go unpunished, but you will surely drink."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For I have sworn by myself,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cthat Bozrah will become an astonishment, a reproach, a waste, and a curse. All its cities will be perpetual wastes.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I have heard news from the LORD,"],[2,"and an ambassador is sent among the nations,"],[1,"saying, \u201cGather yourselves together!"],[2,"Come against her!"],[2,"Rise up to the battle!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor, behold, I have made you small among the nations,"],[2,"and despised among men."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"As for your terror,"],[2,"the pride of your heart has deceived you,"],[1,"O you who dwell in the clefts of the rock,"],[2,"who hold the height of the hill,"],[1,"though you should make your nest as high as the eagle,"],[2,"I will bring you down from there,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEdom will become an astonishment."],[2,"Everyone who passes by it will be astonished,"],[2,"and will hiss at all its plagues."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"As in the overthrow of Sodom and Gomorrah and its neighbor cities,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cno man will dwell there,"],[2,"neither will any son of man live therein."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, he will come up like a lion from the pride of the Jordan against the strong habitation;"],[2,"for I will suddenly make them run away from it,"],[1,"and whoever is chosen,"],[2,"I will appoint him over it."],[1,"For who is like me?"],[2,"Who will appoint me a time?"],[2,"Who is the shepherd who will stand before me?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore hear the counsel of the LORD, that he has taken against Edom,"],[2,"and his purposes that he has purposed against the inhabitants of Teman:"],[1,"Surely they will drag them away,"],[2,"the little ones of the flock."],[2,"Surely he will make their habitation desolate over them."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth trembles at the noise of their fall;"],[2,"there is a cry, the noise which is heard in the Red Sea."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, he will come up and fly as the eagle,"],[2,"and spread out his wings against Bozrah."],[2,"The heart of the mighty men of Edom at that day will be as the heart of a woman in her pangs."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Of Damascus:"],[1,"\u201cHamath and Arpad are confounded,"],[2,"for they have heard evil news."],[2,"They have melted away."],[1,"There is sorrow on the sea."],[2,"It can\u2019t be quiet."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"Damascus has grown feeble,"],[2,"she turns herself to flee,"],[2,"and trembling has seized her."],[1,"Anguish and sorrows have taken hold of her,"],[2,"as of a woman in travail."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"How is the city of praise not forsaken,"],[2,"the city of my joy?"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore her young men will fall in her streets,"],[2,"and all the men of war will be brought to silence in that day,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will kindle a fire in the wall of Damascus,"],[2,"and it will devour the palaces of Ben Hadad.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Of Kedar, and of the kingdoms of Hazor, which Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon struck, The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cArise, go up to Kedar,"],[2,"and destroy the children of the east."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"They will take their tents and their flocks."],[2,"they will carry away for themselves their curtains,"],[2,"all their vessels, and their camels;"],[2,"and they will cry to them, \u2018Terror on every side!\u2019"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Flee!"],[2,"Wander far off!"],[1,"Dwell in the depths, you inhabitants of Hazor,\u201d says the LORD;"],[2,"\u201cfor Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon has taken counsel against you,"],[2,"and has conceived a purpose against you."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise! Go up to a nation that is at ease,"],[2,"that dwells without care,\u201d says the LORD;"],[2,"\u201cthat has neither gates nor bars,"],[2,"that dwells alone."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"Their camels will be a booty,"],[2,"and the multitude of their livestock a plunder."],[1,"I will scatter to all winds those who have the corners of their beards cut off;"],[2,"and I will bring their calamity from every side of them,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"Hazor will be a dwelling place of jackals,"],[2,"a desolation forever."],[1,"No man will dwell there,"],[2,"neither will any son of man live therein.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word that came to Jeremiah the prophet concerning Elam, in the beginning of the reign of Zedekiah king of Judah, saying,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies says:"],[1,"\u2018Behold, I will break the bow of Elam,"],[2,"the chief of their might."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring on Elam the four winds from the four quarters of the sky,"],[2,"and will scatter them toward all those winds."],[2,"There will be no nation where the outcasts of Elam will not come."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cause Elam to be dismayed before their enemies,"],[2,"and before those who seek their life."],[1,"I will bring evil on them, even my fierce anger,\u2019 says the LORD;"],[2,"\u2018and I will send the sword after them,"],[2,"until I have consumed them."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"I will set my throne in Elam,"],[2,"and will destroy from there king and princes,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018But it will happen in the latter days"],[2,"that I will reverse the captivity of Elam,\u2019 says the LORD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word that the LORD spoke concerning Babylon, concerning the land of the Chaldeans, by Jeremiah the prophet."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDeclare among the nations and publish,"],[2,"and set up a standard;"],[2,"publish, and don\u2019t conceal;"],[1,"say, \u2018Babylon has been taken,"],[2,"Bel is disappointed,"],[2,"Merodach is dismayed!"],[1,"Her images are disappointed."],[2,"Her idols are dismayed.\u2019"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For a nation comes up out of the north against her,"],[2,"which will make her land desolate,"],[2,"and no one will dwell in it."],[1,"They have fled."],[2,"They are gone,"],[2,"both man and animal."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIn those days, and in that time,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthe children of Israel will come,"],[2,"they and the children of Judah together;"],[1,"they will go on their way weeping,"],[2,"and will seek the LORD their God."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They will inquire concerning Zion with their faces turned toward it,"],[2,"saying, \u2018Come, and join yourselves to the LORD in an everlasting covenant"],[2,"that will not be forgotten.\u2019"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My people have been lost sheep."],[2,"Their shepherds have caused them to go astray."],[1,"They have turned them away on the mountains."],[2,"They have gone from mountain to hill."],[2,"They have forgotten their resting place."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"All who found them have devoured them."],[2,"Their adversaries said, \u2018We are not guilty,"],[1,"because they have sinned against the LORD,"],[2,"the habitation of righteousness,"],[2,"even the LORD, the hope of their fathers.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFlee out of the middle of Babylon!"],[2,"Go out of the land of the Chaldeans,"],[2,"and be as the male goats before the flocks."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, I will stir up"],[2,"and cause to come up against Babylon a company of great nations from the north country;"],[2,"and they will set themselves in array against her."],[1,"She will be taken from there."],[2,"Their arrows will be as of an expert mighty man."],[2,"None of them will return in vain."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Chaldea will be a prey."],[2,"All who prey on her will be satisfied,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBecause you are glad,"],[2,"because you rejoice,"],[1,"O you who plunder my heritage,"],[2,"because you are wanton as a heifer that treads out the grain,"],[2,"and neigh as strong horses,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"your mother will be utterly disappointed."],[2,"She who bore you will be confounded."],[1,"Behold, she will be the least of the nations,"],[2,"a wilderness, a dry land, and a desert."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Because of the LORD\u2019s wrath she won\u2019t be inhabited,"],[2,"but she will be wholly desolate."],[1,"Everyone who goes by Babylon will be astonished,"],[2,"and hiss at all her plagues."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Set yourselves in array against Babylon all around,"],[2,"all you who bend the bow;"],[2,"shoot at her."],[1,"Spare no arrows,"],[2,"for she has sinned against the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Shout against her all around."],[2,"She has submitted herself."],[2,"Her bulwarks have fallen."],[1,"Her walls have been thrown down,"],[2,"for it is the vengeance of the LORD."],[1,"Take vengeance on her."],[2,"As she has done, do to her."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Cut off the sower from Babylon,"],[2,"and him who handles the sickle in the time of harvest."],[1,"For fear of the oppressing sword,"],[2,"they will each return to their own people,"],[2,"and they will each flee to their own land."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIsrael is a hunted sheep."],[2,"The lions have driven him away."],[1,"First, the king of Assyria devoured him,"],[2,"and now at last Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon has broken his bones.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I will punish the king of Babylon and his land,"],[2,"as I have punished the king of Assyria."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring Israel again to his pasture,"],[2,"and he will feed on Carmel and Bashan."],[2,"His soul will be satisfied on the hills of Ephraim and in Gilead."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"In those days, and in that time,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthe iniquity of Israel will be sought for,"],[2,"and there will be none,"],[1,"also the sins of Judah,"],[2,"and they won\u2019t be found;"],[2,"for I will pardon them whom I leave as a remnant."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGo up against the land of Merathaim,"],[2,"even against it, and against the inhabitants of Pekod."],[1,"Kill and utterly destroy after them,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cand do according to all that I have commanded you."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"A sound of battle is in the land,"],[2,"and of great destruction."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"How the hammer of the whole earth is cut apart and broken!"],[2,"How Babylon has become a desolation among the nations!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"I have laid a snare for you,"],[2,"and you are also taken, Babylon,"],[2,"and you weren\u2019t aware."],[1,"You are found,"],[2,"and also caught,"],[2,"because you have fought against the LORD."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has opened his armory,"],[2,"and has brought out the weapons of his indignation;"],[2,"for the Lord, GOD of Armies, has a work to do in the land of the Chaldeans."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Come against her from the farthest border."],[2,"Open her storehouses."],[2,"Cast her up as heaps."],[1,"Destroy her utterly."],[2,"Let nothing of her be left."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Kill all her bulls."],[2,"Let them go down to the slaughter."],[1,"Woe to them! For their day has come,"],[2,"the time of their visitation."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Listen to those who flee and escape out of the land of Babylon,"],[2,"to declare in Zion the vengeance of the LORD our God,"],[2,"the vengeance of his temple."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cCall together the archers against Babylon,"],[2,"all those who bend the bow."],[1,"Encamp against her all around."],[2,"Let none of it escape."],[1,"Pay her back according to her work."],[2,"According to all that she has done, do to her;"],[1,"for she has been proud against the LORD,"],[2,"against the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore her young men will fall in her streets."],[2,"All her men of war will be brought to silence in that day,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I am against you, you proud one,\u201d says the Lord, GOD of Armies;"],[2,"\u201cfor your day has come,"],[2,"the time that I will visit you."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"The proud one will stumble and fall,"],[2,"and no one will raise him up."],[1,"I will kindle a fire in his cities,"],[2,"and it will devour all who are around him.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cThe children of Israel and the children of Judah are oppressed together."],[2,"All who took them captive hold them fast."],[2,"They refuse to let them go."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"Their Redeemer is strong."],[2,"The LORD of Armies is his name."],[1,"He will thoroughly plead their cause,"],[2,"that he may give rest to the earth,"],[2,"and disquiet the inhabitants of Babylon."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cA sword is on the Chaldeans,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cand on the inhabitants of Babylon,"],[2,"on her princes,"],[2,"and on her wise men."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"A sword is on the boasters,"],[2,"and they will become fools."],[1,"A sword is on her mighty men,"],[2,"and they will be dismayed."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"A sword is on their horses,"],[2,"on their chariots,"],[2,"and on all the mixed people who are in the middle of her;"],[2,"and they will become as women."],[1,"A sword is on her treasures,"],[2,"and they will be robbed."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"A drought is on her waters,"],[2,"and they will be dried up;"],[1,"for it is a land of engraved images,"],[2,"and they are mad over idols."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the wild animals of the desert"],[2,"with the wolves will dwell there."],[1,"The ostriches will dwell therein."],[2,"It will be inhabited no more forever,"],[2,"neither will it be lived in from generation to generation."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"As when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah and its neighbor cities,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cso no man will dwell there,"],[2,"neither will any son of man live therein."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, a people comes from the north."],[2,"A great nation and many kings will be stirred up from the uttermost parts of the earth."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"They take up bow and spear."],[2,"They are cruel, and have no mercy."],[2,"Their voice roars like the sea."],[1,"They ride on horses,"],[2,"everyone set in array,"],[2,"as a man to the battle,"],[2,"against you, daughter of Babylon."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"The king of Babylon has heard the news of them,"],[2,"and his hands become feeble."],[1,"Anguish has taken hold of him,"],[2,"pains as of a woman in labor."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the enemy will come up like a lion"],[2,"from the thickets of the Jordan against the strong habitation;"],[2,"for I will suddenly make them run away from it."],[1,"Whoever is chosen,"],[2,"I will appoint him over it,"],[2,"for who is like me?"],[1,"Who will appoint me a time?"],[2,"Who is the shepherd who can stand before me?\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore hear the counsel of the LORD"],[2,"that he has taken against Babylon;"],[1,"and his purposes"],[2,"that he has purposed against the land of the Chaldeans:"],[1,"Surely they will drag them away,"],[2,"even the little ones of the flock."],[2,"Surely he will make their habitation desolate over them."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth trembles at the noise of the taking of Babylon."],[2,"The cry is heard among the nations."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I will raise up against Babylon,"],[2,"and against those who dwell in Lebkamai, a destroying wind."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will send to Babylon strangers, who will winnow her."],[2,"They will empty her land;"],[2,"for in the day of trouble they will be against her all around."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Against him who bends, let the archer bend his bow,"],[2,"also against him who lifts himself up in his coat of mail."],[1,"Don\u2019t spare her young men!"],[2,"Utterly destroy all her army!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They will fall down slain in the land of the Chaldeans,"],[2,"and thrust through in her streets."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For Israel is not forsaken, nor Judah, by his God,"],[2,"by the LORD of Armies;"],[2,"though their land is full of guilt against the Holy One of Israel."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFlee out of the middle of Babylon!"],[2,"Everyone save his own life!"],[1,"Don\u2019t be cut off in her iniquity,"],[2,"for it is the time of the LORD\u2019s vengeance."],[2,"He will give to her a recompense."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Babylon has been a golden cup in the LORD\u2019s hand,"],[2,"who made all the earth drunk."],[1,"The nations have drunk of her wine;"],[2,"therefore the nations have gone mad."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Babylon has suddenly fallen and been destroyed!"],[2,"Wail for her!"],[1,"Take balm for her pain."],[2,"Perhaps she may be healed."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWe would have healed Babylon,"],[2,"but she is not healed."],[1,"Forsake her,"],[2,"and let\u2019s each go into his own country;"],[1,"for her judgment reaches to heaven,"],[2,"and is lifted up even to the skies."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018The LORD has produced our righteousness."],[2,"Come, and let\u2019s declare in Zion the work of the LORD our God.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMake the arrows sharp!"],[2,"Hold the shields firmly!"],[1,"The LORD has stirred up the spirit of the kings of the Medes,"],[2,"because his purpose is against Babylon, to destroy it;"],[1,"for it is the vengeance of the LORD,"],[2,"the vengeance of his temple."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Set up a standard against the walls of Babylon!"],[2,"Make the watch strong!"],[1,"Set the watchmen,"],[2,"and prepare the ambushes;"],[1,"for the LORD has both purposed and done"],[2,"that which he spoke concerning the inhabitants of Babylon."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You who dwell on many waters, abundant in treasures,"],[2,"your end has come, the measure of your covetousness."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD of Armies has sworn by himself, saying,"],[2,"\u2018Surely I will fill you with men,"],[2,"as with locusts,"],[2,"and they will lift up a shout against you.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHe has made the earth by his power."],[2,"He has established the world by his wisdom."],[2,"By his understanding he has stretched out the heavens."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"When he utters his voice,"],[2,"there is a roar of waters in the heavens,"],[2,"and he causes the vapors to ascend from the ends of the earth."],[1,"He makes lightning for the rain,"],[2,"and brings the wind out of his treasuries."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEvery man has become stupid and without knowledge."],[2,"Every goldsmith is disappointed by his image,"],[1,"for his molten images are falsehood,"],[2,"and there is no breath in them."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"They are vanity,"],[2,"a work of delusion."],[2,"In the time of their visitation, they will perish."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The portion of Jacob is not like these,"],[2,"for he formed all things,"],[2,"including the tribe of his inheritance."],[2,"The LORD of Armies is his name."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou are my battle ax and weapons of war."],[2,"With you I will break the nations into pieces."],[2,"With you I will destroy kingdoms."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"the horse and his rider."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"the chariot and him who rides therein."],[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"man and woman."],[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"the old man and the youth."],[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"the young man and the virgin."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"the shepherd and his flock."],[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"the farmer and his yoke."],[1,"With you I will break in pieces"],[2,"governors and deputies."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI will give to Babylon and to all the inhabitants of Chaldea all their evil that they have done in Zion in your sight,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, I am against you, destroying mountain,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cwhich destroys all the earth."],[1,"I will stretch out my hand on you,"],[2,"roll you down from the rocks,"],[2,"and will make you a burned mountain."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"They won\u2019t take a cornerstone from you,"],[2,"nor a stone for foundations;"],[2,"but you will be desolate forever,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSet up a standard in the land!"],[2,"Blow the trumpet among the nations!"],[1,"Prepare the nations against her!"],[2,"Call together against her the kingdoms of Ararat, Minni, and Ashkenaz!"],[1,"Appoint a marshal against her!"],[2,"Cause the horses to come up as the swarming locusts!"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Prepare against her the nations,"],[2,"the kings of the Medes, its governors, and all its deputies, and all the land of their dominion!"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"The land trembles and is in pain;"],[2,"for the purposes of the LORD against Babylon stand,"],[2,"to make the land of Babylon a desolation, without inhabitant."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"The mighty men of Babylon have stopped fighting,"],[2,"they remain in their strongholds."],[1,"Their might has failed."],[2,"They have become as women."],[1,"Her dwelling places are set on fire."],[2,"Her bars are broken."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"One runner will run to meet another,"],[2,"and one messenger to meet another,"],[2,"to show the king of Babylon that his city is taken on every quarter."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"So the passages are seized."],[2,"They have burned the reeds with fire."],[2,"The men of war are frightened.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel says:"],[1,"\u201cThe daughter of Babylon is like a threshing floor at the time when it is trodden."],[2,"Yet a little while, and the time of harvest comes for her.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon has devoured me."],[2,"He has crushed me."],[2,"He has made me an empty vessel."],[1,"He has, like a monster, swallowed me up."],[2,"He has filled his mouth with my delicacies."],[2,"He has cast me out."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"May the violence done to me and to my flesh be on Babylon!\u201d"],[2,"the inhabitant of Zion will say; and,"],[1,"\u201cMay my blood be on the inhabitants of Chaldea!\u201d"],[2,"will Jerusalem say."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I will plead your cause,"],[2,"and take vengeance for you."],[1,"I will dry up her sea,"],[2,"and make her fountain dry."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"Babylon will become heaps,"],[2,"a dwelling place for jackals,"],[2,"an astonishment, and a hissing,"],[2,"without inhabitant."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"They will roar together like young lions."],[2,"They will growl as lions\u2019 cubs."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[1,"When they are inflamed, I will make their feast,"],[2,"and I will make them drunk,"],[1,"that they may rejoice,"],[2,"and sleep a perpetual sleep,"],[2,"and not wake up,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will bring them down like lambs to the slaughter,"],[2,"like rams with male goats."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow Sheshach is taken!"],[2,"How the praise of the whole earth is seized!"],[2,"How Babylon has become a desolation among the nations!"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[1,"The sea has come up on Babylon."],[2,"She is covered with the multitude of its waves."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"Her cities have become a desolation,"],[2,"a dry land, and a desert,"],[2,"a land in which no man dwells."],[2,"No son of man passes by it."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"I will execute judgment on Bel in Babylon,"],[2,"and I will bring out of his mouth that which he has swallowed up."],[1,"The nations will not flow any more to him."],[2,"Yes, the wall of Babylon will fall."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cMy people, go away from the middle of her,"],[2,"and each of you save yourselves from the LORD\u2019s fierce anger."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t let your heart faint."],[2,"Don\u2019t fear for the news that will be heard in the land."],[1,"For news will come one year,"],[2,"and after that in another year news will come,"],[2,"and violence in the land,"],[2,"ruler against ruler."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore behold, the days come that I will execute judgment on the engraved images of Babylon;"],[2,"and her whole land will be confounded."],[2,"All her slain will fall in the middle of her."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the heavens and the earth,"],[2,"and all that is therein,"],[1,"will sing for joy over Babylon;"],[2,"for the destroyers will come to her from the north,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAs Babylon has caused the slain of Israel to fall,"],[2,"so the slain of all the land will fall at Babylon."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"You who have escaped the sword, go!"],[2,"Don\u2019t stand still!"],[1,"Remember the LORD from afar,"],[2,"and let Jerusalem come into your mind.\u201d"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWe are confounded"],[2,"because we have heard reproach."],[1,"Confusion has covered our faces,"],[2,"for strangers have come into the sanctuaries of the LORD\u2019s house.\u201d"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore behold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthat I will execute judgment on her engraved images;"],[2,"and through all her land the wounded will groan."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[1,"Though Babylon should mount up to the sky,"],[2,"and though she should fortify the height of her strength,"],[2,"yet destroyers will come to her from me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe sound of a cry comes from Babylon,"],[2,"and of great destruction from the land of the Chaldeans!"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[1,"For the LORD lays Babylon waste,"],[2,"and destroys out of her the great voice!"],[1,"Their waves roar like many waters."],[2,"The noise of their voice is uttered."]]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[1,"For the destroyer has come on her,"],[2,"even on Babylon."],[1,"Her mighty men are taken."],[2,"Their bows are broken in pieces,"],[1,"for the LORD is a God of retribution."],[2,"He will surely repay."]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make her princes, her wise men,"],[2,"her governors, her deputies, and her mighty men drunk."],[1,"They will sleep a perpetual sleep,"],[2,"and not wake up,\u201d"],[2,"says the King, whose name is the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says:"],[1,"\u201cThe wide walls of Babylon will be utterly overthrown."],[2,"Her high gates will be burned with fire."],[1,"The peoples will labor for vanity,"],[2,"and the nations for the fire;"],[2,"and they will be weary.\u201d"]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"The word which Jeremiah the prophet commanded Seraiah the son of Neriah, the son of Mahseiah, when he went with Zedekiah the king of Judah to Babylon in the fourth year of his reign. Now Seraiah was chief quartermaster."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"Jeremiah wrote in a book all the evil that should come on Babylon, even all these words that are written concerning Babylon."]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"Jeremiah said to Seraiah, \u201cWhen you come to Babylon, then see that you read all these words,"]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018LORD, you have spoken concerning this place, to cut it off, that no one will dwell in it, neither man nor animal, but that it will be desolate forever.\u2019"]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"It will be, when you have finished reading this book, that you shall bind a stone to it, and cast it into the middle of the Euphrates."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"Then you shall say, \u2018Thus will Babylon sink, and will not rise again because of the evil that I will bring on her; and they will be weary.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"Thus far are the words of Jeremiah."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Zedekiah was twenty-one years old when he began to reign. He reigned eleven years in Jerusalem. His mother\u2019s name was Hamutal the daughter of Jeremiah of Libnah."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He did that which was evil in the LORD\u2019s sight, according to all that Jehoiakim had done."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For through the LORD\u2019s anger this happened in Jerusalem and Judah, until he had cast them out from his presence."],[0,"Zedekiah rebelled against the king of Babylon."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"In the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came, he and all his army, against Jerusalem, and encamped against it; and they built forts against it round about."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So the city was besieged to the eleventh year of King Zedekiah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fourth month, in the ninth day of the month, the famine was severe in the city, so that there was no bread for the people of the land."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then a breach was made in the city, and all the men of war fled, and went out of the city by night by the way of the gate between the two walls, which was by the king\u2019s garden. Now the Chaldeans were against the city all around. The men of war went toward the Arabah,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but the army of the Chaldeans pursued the king, and overtook Zedekiah in the plains of Jericho; and all his army was scattered from him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then they took the king, and carried him up to the king of Babylon to Riblah in the land of Hamath; and he pronounced judgment on him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The king of Babylon killed the sons of Zedekiah before his eyes. He also killed all the princes of Judah in Riblah."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He put out the eyes of Zedekiah; and the king of Babylon bound him in fetters, and carried him to Babylon, and put him in prison until the day of his death."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the fifth month, in the tenth day of the month, which was the nineteenth year of King Nebuchadnezzar, king of Babylon, Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard, who stood before the king of Babylon, came into Jerusalem."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He burned the LORD\u2019s house, and the king\u2019s house; and all the houses of Jerusalem, even every great house, he burned with fire."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"All the army of the Chaldeans, who were with the captain of the guard, broke down all the walls of Jerusalem all around."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive of the poorest of the people, and the rest of the people who were left in the city, and those who fell away, who defected to the king of Babylon, and the rest of the multitude."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard left of the poorest of the land to be vineyard keepers and farmers."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The Chaldeans broke the pillars of bronze that were in the LORD\u2019s house and the bases and the bronze sea that were in the LORD\u2019s house in pieces, and carried all of their bronze to Babylon."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They also took away the pots, the shovels, the snuffers, the basins, the spoons, and all the vessels of bronze with which they ministered."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The captain of the guard took away the cups, the fire pans, the basins, the pots, the lamp stands, the spoons, and the bowls; that which was of gold, as gold, and that which was of silver, as silver."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"They took the two pillars, the one sea, and the twelve bronze bulls that were under the bases, which King Solomon had made for the LORD\u2019s house. The bronze of all these vessels was without weight."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"As for the pillars, the height of the one pillar was eighteen cubits; and a line of twelve cubits encircled it; and its thickness was four fingers. It was hollow."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:22,l:[[0,"A capital of bronze was on it; and the height of the one capital was five cubits, with network and pomegranates on the capital all around, all of bronze. The second pillar also had the same, with pomegranates."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:23,l:[[0,"There were ninety-six pomegranates on the sides; all the pomegranates were one hundred on the network all around."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The captain of the guard took Seraiah the chief priest, and Zephaniah the second priest, and the three keepers of the threshold,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and out of the city he took an officer who was set over the men of war; and seven men of those who saw the king\u2019s face, who were found in the city; and the scribe of the captain of the army, who mustered the people of the land; and sixty men of the people of the land, who were found in the middle of the city."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard took them, and brought them to the king of Babylon to Riblah."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The king of Babylon struck them, and put them to death at Riblah in the land of Hamath."],[0,"So Judah was carried away captive out of his land."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"This is the number of the people whom Nebuchadnezzar carried away captive:"],[0,"in the seventh year, three thousand twenty-three Jews;"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"in the eighteenth year of Nebuchadnezzar, he carried away captive from Jerusalem eight hundred thirty-two persons;"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"in the twenty-third year of Nebuchadnezzar, Nebuzaradan the captain of the guard carried away captive of the Jews seven hundred forty-five people."],[0,"All the people numbered four thousand six hundred."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"In the thirty-seventh year of the captivity of Jehoiachin king of Judah, in the twelfth month, in the twenty-fifth day of the month, Evilmerodach king of Babylon, in the first year of his reign, lifted up the head of Jehoiachin king of Judah, and released him from prison."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He spoke kindly to him, and set his throne above the throne of the kings who were with him in Babylon,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"and changed his prison garments. Jehoiachin ate bread before him continually all the days of his life."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For his allowance, there was a continual allowance given him by the king of Babylon, every day a portion until the day of his death, all the days of his life."]]}]]}},1295,[]);
__d(function(e,o,a,h,t,s,r){t.exports={book:"Lam",name:"Lamentations",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"How the city sits solitary,"],[2,"that was full of people!"],[1,"She has become as a widow,"],[2,"who was great among the nations!"],[1,"She who was a princess among the provinces"],[2,"has become a slave!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"She weeps bitterly in the night."],[2,"Her tears are on her cheeks."],[1,"Among all her lovers"],[2,"she has no one to comfort her."],[1,"All her friends have dealt treacherously with her."],[2,"They have become her enemies."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Judah has gone into captivity because of affliction"],[2,"and because of great servitude."],[1,"She dwells among the nations."],[2,"She finds no rest."],[2,"All her persecutors overtook her in her distress."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The roads to Zion mourn,"],[2,"because no one comes to the solemn assembly."],[1,"All her gates are desolate."],[2,"Her priests sigh."],[1,"Her virgins are afflicted,"],[2,"and she herself is in bitterness."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Her adversaries have become the head."],[2,"Her enemies prosper;"],[1,"for the LORD has afflicted her for the multitude of her transgressions."],[2,"Her young children have gone into captivity before the adversary."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"All majesty has departed from the daughter of Zion."],[2,"Her princes have become like deer that find no pasture."],[2,"They have gone without strength before the pursuer."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Jerusalem remembers in the days of her affliction and of her miseries"],[2,"all her pleasant things that were from the days of old;"],[1,"when her people fell into the hand of the adversary,"],[2,"and no one helped her."],[1,"The adversaries saw her."],[2,"They mocked at her desolations."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Jerusalem has grievously sinned."],[2,"Therefore she has become unclean."],[1,"All who honored her despise her,"],[2,"because they have seen her nakedness."],[2,"Yes, she sighs and turns backward."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Her filthiness was in her skirts."],[2,"She didn\u2019t remember her latter end."],[1,"Therefore she has come down astoundingly."],[2,"She has no comforter."],[1,"\u201cSee, LORD, my affliction;"],[2,"for the enemy has magnified himself.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The adversary has spread out his hand on all her pleasant things;"],[2,"for she has seen that the nations have entered into her sanctuary,"],[2,"concerning whom you commanded that they should not enter into your assembly."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"All her people sigh."],[2,"They seek bread."],[2,"They have given their pleasant things for food to refresh their soul."],[1,"\u201cLook, LORD, and see,"],[2,"for I have become despised.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIs it nothing to you, all you who pass by?"],[2,"Look, and see if there is any sorrow like my sorrow,"],[2,"which is brought on me,"],[2,"with which the LORD has afflicted me in the day of his fierce anger."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFrom on high has he sent fire into my bones,"],[2,"and it prevails against them."],[1,"He has spread a net for my feet."],[2,"He has turned me back."],[2,"He has made me desolate and I faint all day long."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe yoke of my transgressions is bound by his hand."],[2,"They are knit together."],[2,"They have come up on my neck."],[2,"He made my strength fail."],[1,"The Lord has delivered me into their hands,"],[2,"against whom I am not able to stand."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe Lord has set at nothing all my mighty men within me."],[2,"He has called a solemn assembly against me to crush my young men."],[2,"The Lord has trodden the virgin daughter of Judah as in a wine press."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor these things I weep."],[2,"My eye, my eye runs down with water,"],[2,"because the comforter who should refresh my soul is far from me."],[1,"My children are desolate,"],[2,"because the enemy has prevailed.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Zion spreads out her hands."],[2,"There is no one to comfort her."],[1,"The LORD has commanded concerning Jacob,"],[2,"that those who are around him should be his adversaries."],[2,"Jerusalem is among them as an unclean thing."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe LORD is righteous,"],[2,"for I have rebelled against his commandment."],[1,"Please hear all you peoples,"],[2,"and see my sorrow."],[2,"My virgins and my young men have gone into captivity."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI called for my lovers,"],[2,"but they deceived me."],[1,"My priests and my elders gave up the spirit in the city,"],[2,"while they sought food for themselves to refresh their souls."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLook, LORD; for I am in distress."],[2,"My heart is troubled."],[1,"My heart turns over within me,"],[2,"for I have grievously rebelled."],[1,"Abroad, the sword bereaves."],[2,"At home, it is like death."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThey have heard that I sigh."],[2,"There is no one to comfort me."],[1,"All my enemies have heard of my trouble."],[2,"They are glad that you have done it."],[1,"You will bring the day that you have proclaimed,"],[2,"and they will be like me."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLet all their wickedness come before you."],[2,"Do to them as you have done to me for all my transgressions."],[1,"For my sighs are many,"],[2,"and my heart is faint."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"How has the Lord covered the daughter of Zion with a cloud in his anger!"],[2,"He has cast the beauty of Israel down from heaven to the earth,"],[2,"and hasn\u2019t remembered his footstool in the day of his anger."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord has swallowed up all the dwellings of Jacob"],[2,"without pity."],[1,"He has thrown down in his wrath the strongholds of the daughter of Judah."],[2,"He has brought them down to the ground."],[2,"He has profaned the kingdom and its princes."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"He has cut off all the horn of Israel in fierce anger."],[2,"He has drawn back his right hand from before the enemy."],[1,"He has burned up Jacob like a flaming fire,"],[2,"which devours all around."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He has bent his bow like an enemy."],[2,"He has stood with his right hand as an adversary."],[1,"He has killed all that were pleasant to the eye."],[2,"In the tent of the daughter of Zion, he has poured out his wrath like fire."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord has become as an enemy."],[2,"He has swallowed up Israel."],[1,"He has swallowed up all her palaces."],[2,"He has destroyed his strongholds."],[2,"He has multiplied mourning and lamentation in the daughter of Judah."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He has violently taken away his tabernacle,"],[2,"as if it were a garden."],[1,"He has destroyed his place of assembly."],[2,"The LORD has caused solemn assembly and Sabbath to be forgotten in Zion."],[2,"In the indignation of his anger, he has despised the king and the priest."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord has cast off his altar."],[2,"He has abhorred his sanctuary."],[1,"He has given the walls of her palaces into the hand of the enemy."],[2,"They have made a noise in the LORD\u2019s house,"],[2,"as in the day of a solemn assembly."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has purposed to destroy the wall of the daughter of Zion."],[2,"He has stretched out the line."],[2,"He has not withdrawn his hand from destroying;"],[1,"He has made the rampart and wall lament."],[2,"They languish together."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Her gates have sunk into the ground."],[2,"He has destroyed and broken her bars."],[1,"Her king and her princes are among the nations where the law is not."],[2,"Yes, her prophets find no vision from the LORD."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The elders of the daughter of Zion sit on the ground."],[2,"They keep silence."],[1,"They have cast up dust on their heads."],[2,"They have clothed themselves with sackcloth."],[2,"The virgins of Jerusalem hang down their heads to the ground."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"My eyes fail with tears."],[2,"My heart is troubled."],[1,"My bile is poured on the earth,"],[2,"because of the destruction of the daughter of my people,"],[2,"because the young children and the infants swoon in the streets of the city."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They ask their mothers,"],[2,"\u201cWhere is grain and wine?\u201d"],[2,"when they swoon as the wounded in the streets of the city,"],[2,"when their soul is poured out into their mothers\u2019 bosom."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"What shall I testify to you?"],[2,"What shall I liken to you, daughter of Jerusalem?"],[1,"What shall I compare to you,"],[2,"that I may comfort you, virgin daughter of Zion?"],[1,"For your breach is as big as the sea."],[2,"Who can heal you?"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Your prophets have seen false and foolish visions for you."],[2,"They have not uncovered your iniquity,"],[2,"to reverse your captivity,"],[2,"but have seen for you false revelations and causes of banishment."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"All that pass by clap their hands at you."],[2,"They hiss and wag their head at the daughter of Jerusalem, saying,"],[1,"\u201cIs this the city that men called \u2018The perfection of beauty,"],[2,"the joy of the whole earth\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"All your enemies have opened their mouth wide against you."],[2,"They hiss and gnash their teeth."],[2,"They say, \u201cWe have swallowed her up."],[1,"Certainly this is the day that we looked for."],[2,"We have found it."],[2,"We have seen it.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has done that which he planned."],[2,"He has fulfilled his word that he commanded in the days of old."],[1,"He has thrown down,"],[2,"and has not pitied."],[1,"He has caused the enemy to rejoice over you."],[2,"He has exalted the horn of your adversaries."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Their heart cried to the Lord."],[2,"O wall of the daughter of Zion,"],[2,"let tears run down like a river day and night."],[1,"Give yourself no relief."],[2,"Don\u2019t let your eyes rest."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, cry out in the night,"],[2,"at the beginning of the watches!"],[1,"Pour out your heart like water before the face of the Lord."],[2,"Lift up your hands toward him for the life of your young children,"],[2,"who faint for hunger at the head of every street."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLook, LORD, and see to whom you have done thus!"],[2,"Should the women eat their offspring,"],[2,"the children that they held and bounced on their knees?"],[2,"Should the priest and the prophet be killed in the sanctuary of the Lord?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe youth and the old man lie on the ground in the streets."],[2,"My virgins and my young men have fallen by the sword."],[1,"You have killed them in the day of your anger."],[2,"You have slaughtered, and not pitied."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou have called, as in the day of a solemn assembly, my terrors on every side."],[2,"There was no one that escaped or remained in the day of the LORD\u2019s anger."],[2,"My enemy has consumed those whom I have cared for and brought up."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"I am the man who has seen affliction"],[2,"by the rod of his wrath."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"He has led me and caused me to walk in darkness,"],[2,"and not in light."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely he turns his hand against me"],[2,"again and again all day long."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He has made my flesh and my skin old."],[2,"He has broken my bones."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He has built against me,"],[2,"and surrounded me with bitterness and hardship."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He has made me dwell in dark places,"],[2,"as those who have been long dead."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He has walled me about, so that I can\u2019t go out."],[2,"He has made my chain heavy."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, when I cry, and call for help,"],[2,"he shuts out my prayer."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"He has walled up my ways with cut stone."],[2,"He has made my paths crooked."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"He is to me as a bear lying in wait,"],[2,"as a lion in hiding."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He has turned away my path,"],[2,"and pulled me in pieces."],[2,"He has made me desolate."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"He has bent his bow,"],[2,"and set me as a mark for the arrow."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He has caused the shafts of his quiver to enter into my kidneys."]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"I have become a derision to all my people,"],[2,"and their song all day long."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He has filled me with bitterness."],[2,"He has stuffed me with wormwood."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He has also broken my teeth with gravel."],[2,"He has covered me with ashes."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"You have removed my soul far away from peace."],[2,"I forgot prosperity."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u201cMy strength has perished,"],[2,"along with my expectation from the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember my affliction and my misery,"],[2,"the wormwood and the bitterness."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"My soul still remembers them,"],[2,"and is bowed down within me."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"This I recall to my mind;"],[2,"therefore I have hope."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"It is because of the LORD\u2019s loving kindnesses that we are not consumed,"],[2,"because his mercies don\u2019t fail."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"They are new every morning."],[2,"Great is your faithfulness."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe LORD is my portion,\u201d says my soul."],[2,"\u201cTherefore I will hope in him.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD is good to those who wait for him,"],[2,"to the soul who seeks him."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"It is good that a man should hope"],[2,"and quietly wait for the salvation of the LORD."]]},{v:27,l:[[2,"It is good for a man that he bear the yoke in his youth."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"Let him sit alone and keep silence,"],[2,"because he has laid it on him."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"Let him put his mouth in the dust,"],[2,"if it is so that there may be hope."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Let him give his cheek to him who strikes him."],[2,"Let him be filled full of reproach."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"For the Lord will not cast off forever."]]},{v:32,l:[[2,"For though he causes grief,"],[2,"yet he will have compassion according to the multitude of his loving kindnesses."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"For he does not afflict willingly,"],[2,"nor grieve the children of men."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"To crush under foot all the prisoners of the earth,"]]},{v:35,l:[[2,"to turn away the right of a man before the face of the Most High,"]]},{v:36,l:[[2,"to subvert a man in his cause, the Lord doesn\u2019t approve."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is he who says, and it comes to pass,"],[2,"when the Lord doesn\u2019t command it?"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"Doesn\u2019t evil and good come out of the mouth of the Most High?"]]},{v:39,l:[[2,"Why should a living man complain,"],[2,"a man for the punishment of his sins?"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"Let us search and try our ways,"],[2,"and turn again to the LORD."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"Let\u2019s lift up our heart with our hands to God in the heavens."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:42,l:[[2,"\u201cWe have transgressed and have rebelled."],[2,"You have not pardoned."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou have covered us with anger and pursued us."],[2,"You have killed."],[2,"You have not pitied."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"You have covered yourself with a cloud,"],[2,"so that no prayer can pass through."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[1,"You have made us an off-scouring and refuse"],[2,"in the middle of the peoples."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAll our enemies have opened their mouth wide against us."]]},{v:47,l:[[2,"Terror and the pit have come on us,"],[2,"devastation and destruction.\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[1,"My eye runs down with streams of water,"],[2,"for the destruction of the daughter of my people."]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[1,"My eye pours down"],[2,"and doesn\u2019t cease,"],[2,"without any intermission,"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"until the LORD looks down,"],[2,"and sees from heaven."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[1,"My eye affects my soul,"],[2,"because of all the daughters of my city."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[1,"They have chased me relentlessly like a bird,"],[2,"those who are my enemies without cause."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[1,"They have cut off my life in the dungeon,"],[2,"and have cast a stone on me."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[1,"Waters flowed over my head."],[2,"I said, \u201cI am cut off.\u201d"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[1,"I called on your name, LORD,"],[2,"out of the lowest dungeon."]]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[1,"You heard my voice:"],[2,"\u201cDon\u2019t hide your ear from my sighing,"],[2,"and my cry.\u201d"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[1,"You came near in the day that I called on you."],[2,"You said, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid.\u201d"]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[1,"Lord, you have pleaded the causes of my soul."],[2,"You have redeemed my life."]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, you have seen my wrong."],[2,"Judge my cause."]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[1,"You have seen all their vengeance"],[2,"and all their plans against me."]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[1,"You have heard their reproach, LORD,"],[2,"and all their plans against me,"]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[1,"the lips of those that rose up against me,"],[2,"and their plots against me all day long."]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[1,"You see their sitting down and their rising up."],[2,"I am their song."]]},{v:64,p:1,l:[[1,"You will pay them back, LORD,"],[2,"according to the work of their hands."]]},{v:65,p:1,l:[[1,"You will give them hardness of heart,"],[2,"your curse to them."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[1,"You will pursue them in anger,"],[2,"and destroy them from under the heavens of the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"How the gold has become dim!"],[2,"The most pure gold has changed!"],[1,"The stones of the sanctuary are poured out"],[2,"at the head of every street."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The precious sons of Zion,"],[2,"comparable to fine gold,"],[1,"how they are esteemed as earthen pitchers,"],[2,"the work of the hands of the potter!"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Even the jackals offer their breast."],[2,"They nurse their young ones."],[1,"But the daughter of my people has become cruel,"],[2,"like the ostriches in the wilderness."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The tongue of the nursing child clings to the roof of his mouth for thirst."],[2,"The young children ask for bread,"],[2,"and no one breaks it for them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who ate delicacies are desolate in the streets."],[2,"Those who were brought up in purple embrace dunghills."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For the iniquity of the daughter of my people is greater than the sin of Sodom,"],[2,"which was overthrown as in a moment."],[2,"No hands were laid on her."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Her nobles were purer than snow."],[2,"They were whiter than milk."],[1,"They were more ruddy in body than rubies."],[2,"Their polishing was like sapphire."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Their appearance is blacker than a coal."],[2,"They are not known in the streets."],[1,"Their skin clings to their bones."],[2,"It is withered."],[2,"It has become like wood."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who are killed with the sword are better than those who are killed with hunger;"],[2,"for these pine away, stricken through,"],[2,"for lack of the fruits of the field."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The hands of the pitiful women have boiled their own children."],[2,"They were their food in the destruction of the daughter of my people."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has accomplished his wrath."],[2,"He has poured out his fierce anger."],[1,"He has kindled a fire in Zion,"],[2,"which has devoured its foundations."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The kings of the earth didn\u2019t believe,"],[2,"neither did all the inhabitants of the world,"],[2,"that the adversary and the enemy would enter into the gates of Jerusalem."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"It is because of the sins of her prophets"],[2,"and the iniquities of her priests,"],[2,"that have shed the blood of the just in the middle of her."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They wander as blind men in the streets."],[2,"They are polluted with blood,"],[2,"So that men can\u2019t touch their garments."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGo away!\u201d they cried to them."],[2,"\u201cUnclean! Go away! Go away! Don\u2019t touch!"],[1,"When they fled away and wandered, men said among the nations,"],[2,"\u201cThey can\u2019t live here any more.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s anger has scattered them."],[2,"He will not pay attention to them any more."],[1,"They didn\u2019t respect the persons of the priests."],[2,"They didn\u2019t favor the elders."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Our eyes still fail,"],[2,"looking in vain for our help."],[2,"In our watching we have watched for a nation that could not save."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"They hunt our steps,"],[2,"so that we can\u2019t go in our streets."],[1,"Our end is near."],[2,"Our days are fulfilled,"],[2,"for our end has come."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Our pursuers were swifter than the eagles of the sky."],[2,"They chased us on the mountains."],[2,"They set an ambush for us in the wilderness."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The breath of our nostrils,"],[2,"the anointed of the LORD,"],[2,"was taken in their pits;"],[1,"of whom we said,"],[2,"under his shadow we will live among the nations."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Rejoice and be glad, daughter of Edom,"],[2,"who dwells in the land of Uz."],[1,"The cup will pass through to you also."],[2,"You will be drunken,"],[2,"and will make yourself naked."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"The punishment of your iniquity is accomplished, daughter of Zion."],[2,"He will no more carry you away into captivity."],[1,"He will visit your iniquity, daughter of Edom."],[2,"He will uncover your sins."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Remember, LORD, what has come on us."],[2,"Look, and see our reproach."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Our inheritance has been turned over to strangers,"],[2,"our houses to aliens."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"We are orphans and fatherless."],[2,"Our mothers are as widows."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"We must pay for water to drink."],[2,"Our wood is sold to us."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Our pursuers are on our necks."],[2,"We are weary, and have no rest."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"We have given our hands to the Egyptians,"],[2,"and to the Assyrians, to be satisfied with bread."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Our fathers sinned, and are no more."],[2,"We have borne their iniquities."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Servants rule over us."],[2,"There is no one to deliver us out of their hand."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"We get our bread at the peril of our lives,"],[2,"because of the sword in the wilderness."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Our skin is black like an oven,"],[2,"because of the burning heat of famine."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They ravished the women in Zion,"],[2,"the virgins in the cities of Judah."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Princes were hanged up by their hands."],[2,"The faces of elders were not honored."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The young men carry millstones."],[2,"The children stumbled under loads of wood."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The elders have ceased from the gate,"],[2,"and the young men from their music."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The joy of our heart has ceased."],[2,"Our dance is turned into mourning."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The crown has fallen from our head."],[2,"Woe to us, for we have sinned!"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For this our heart is faint."],[2,"For these things our eyes are dim:"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"for the mountain of Zion, which is desolate."],[2,"The foxes walk on it."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"You, LORD, remain forever."],[2,"Your throne is from generation to generation."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Why do you forget us forever,"],[2,"and forsake us for so long a time?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn us to yourself, LORD, and we will be turned."],[2,"Renew our days as of old."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"But you have utterly rejected us."],[2,"You are very angry against us."]]}]]}},1296,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,s){h.exports={book:"Ezek",name:"Ezekiel",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the thirtieth year, in the fourth month, in the fifth day of the month, as I was among the captives by the river Chebar, the heavens were opened, and I saw visions of God."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fifth of the month, which was the fifth year of King Jehoiachin\u2019s captivity,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"the LORD\u2019s word came to Ezekiel the priest, the son of Buzi, in the land of the Chaldeans by the river Chebar; and the LORD\u2019s hand was there on him."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I looked, and behold, a stormy wind came out of the north: a great cloud, with flashing lightning, and a brightness around it, and out of the middle of it as it were glowing metal, out of the middle of the fire."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Out of its center came the likeness of four living creatures. This was their appearance: They had the likeness of a man."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Everyone had four faces, and each one of them had four wings."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Their feet were straight feet. The sole of their feet was like the sole of a calf\u2019s foot; and they sparkled like burnished bronze."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They had the hands of a man under their wings on their four sides. The four of them had their faces and their wings like this:"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Their wings were joined to one another. They didn\u2019t turn when they went. Each one went straight forward."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"As for the likeness of their faces, they had the face of a man. The four of them had the face of a lion on the right side. The four of them had the face of an ox on the left side. The four of them also had the face of an eagle."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Such were their faces. Their wings were spread out above. Two wings of each one touched another, and two covered their bodies."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Each one went straight forward. Where the spirit was to go, they went. They didn\u2019t turn when they went."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"As for the likeness of the living creatures, their appearance was like burning coals of fire, like the appearance of torches. The fire went up and down among the living creatures. The fire was bright, and lightning went out of the fire."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The living creatures ran and returned as the appearance of a flash of lightning."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now as I saw the living creatures, behold, there was one wheel on the earth beside the living creatures, for each of the four faces of it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The appearance of the wheels and their work was like a beryl. The four of them had one likeness. Their appearance and their work was as it were a wheel within a wheel."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When they went, they went in their four directions. They didn\u2019t turn when they went."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"As for their rims, they were high and dreadful; and the four of them had their rims full of eyes all around."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"When the living creatures went, the wheels went beside them. When the living creatures were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Wherever the spirit was to go, they went. The spirit was to go there. The wheels were lifted up beside them; for the spirit of the living creature was in the wheels."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When those went, these went. When those stood, these stood. When those were lifted up from the earth, the wheels were lifted up beside them; for the spirit of the living creature was in the wheels."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Over the head of the living creature there was the likeness of an expanse, like an awesome crystal to look at, stretched out over their heads above."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Under the expanse, their wings were straight, one toward the other. Each one had two which covered on this side, and each one had two which covered their bodies on that side."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When they went, I heard the noise of their wings like the noise of great waters, like the voice of the Almighty, a noise of tumult like the noise of an army. When they stood, they let down their wings."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"There was a voice above the expanse that was over their heads. When they stood, they let down their wings."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Above the expanse that was over their heads was the likeness of a throne, as the appearance of a sapphire stone. On the likeness of the throne was a likeness as the appearance of a man on it above."]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:27,l:[[0,"I saw as it were glowing metal, as the appearance of fire within it all around, from the appearance of his waist and upward; and from the appearance of his waist and downward I saw as it were the appearance of fire, and there was brightness around him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"As the appearance of the rainbow that is in the cloud in the day of rain, so was the appearance of the brightness all around."],[0,"This was the appearance of the likeness of the LORD\u2019s glory. When I saw it, I fell on my face, and I heard a voice of one that spoke."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, stand on your feet, and I will speak with you.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Spirit entered into me when he spoke to me, and set me on my feet; and I heard him who spoke to me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, I send you to the children of Israel, to a nation of rebels who have rebelled against me. They and their fathers have transgressed against me even to this very day."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The children are impudent and stiff-hearted. I am sending you to them, and you shall tell them, \u2018This is what the Lord GOD says.\u2019"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They, whether they will hear, or whether they will refuse\u2014for they are a rebellious house\u2014yet they will know that there has been a prophet among them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You, son of man, don\u2019t be afraid of them, neither be afraid of their words, though briers and thorns are with you, and you dwell among scorpions. Don\u2019t be afraid of their words, nor be dismayed at their looks, though they are a rebellious house."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall speak my words to them, whether they will hear or whether they will refuse; for they are most rebellious."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But you, son of man, hear what I tell you. Don\u2019t be rebellious like that rebellious house. Open your mouth, and eat that which I give you.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When I looked, behold, a hand was stretched out to me; and behold, a scroll of a book was in it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He spread it before me. It was written within and without; and lamentations, mourning, and woe were written in it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, eat what you find. Eat this scroll, and go, speak to the house of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"So I opened my mouth, and he caused me to eat the scroll."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, eat this scroll that I give you and fill your belly and your bowels with it.\u201d"],[0,"Then I ate it. It was as sweet as honey in my mouth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, go to the house of Israel, and speak my words to them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For you are not sent to a people of a strange speech and of a hard language, but to the house of Israel\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"not to many peoples of a strange speech and of a hard language, whose words you can\u2019t understand. Surely, if I sent you to them, they would listen to you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But the house of Israel will not listen to you, for they will not listen to me; for all the house of Israel are obstinate and hard-hearted."]],f:["Literally, have a hard forehead"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, I have made your face hard against their faces, and your forehead hard against their foreheads."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I have made your forehead as a diamond, harder than flint. Don\u2019t be afraid of them, neither be dismayed at their looks, though they are a rebellious house.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover he said to me, \u201cSon of man, receive in your heart and hear with your ears all my words that I speak to you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Go to them of the captivity, to the children of your people, and speak to them, and tell them, \u2018This is what the Lord GOD says,\u2019 whether they will hear, or whether they will refuse.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Spirit lifted me up, and I heard behind me the voice of a great rushing, saying, \u201cBlessed be the LORD\u2019s glory from his place.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I heard the noise of the wings of the living creatures as they touched one another, and the noise of the wheels beside them, even the noise of a great rushing."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So the Spirit lifted me up, and took me away; and I went in bitterness, in the heat of my spirit; and the LORD\u2019s hand was strong on me."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then I came to them of the captivity at Tel Aviv who lived by the river Chebar, and to where they lived; and I sat there overwhelmed among them seven days."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of seven days, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, I have made you a watchman to the house of Israel. Therefore hear the word from my mouth, and warn them from me."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When I tell the wicked, \u2018You will surely die;\u2019 and you give him no warning, nor speak to warn the wicked from his wicked way, to save his life, that wicked man will die in his iniquity; but I will require his blood at your hand."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Yet if you warn the wicked, and he doesn\u2019t turn from his wickedness, nor from his wicked way, he will die in his iniquity; but you have delivered your soul.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAgain, when a righteous man turns from his righteousness and commits iniquity, and I lay a stumbling block before him, he will die. Because you have not given him warning, he will die in his sin, and his righteous deeds which he has done will not be remembered; but I will require his blood at your hand."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Nevertheless if you warn the righteous man, that the righteous not sin, and he does not sin, he will surely live, because he took warning; and you have delivered your soul.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s hand was there on me; and he said to me, \u201cArise, go out into the plain, and I will talk with you there.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I arose, and went out into the plain, and behold, the LORD\u2019s glory stood there, like the glory which I saw by the river Chebar. Then I fell on my face."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Spirit entered into me and set me on my feet. He spoke with me, and said to me, \u201cGo, shut yourself inside your house."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But you, son of man, behold, they will put ropes on you, and will bind you with them, and you will not go out among them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I will make your tongue stick to the roof of your mouth so that you will be mute and will not be able to correct them, for they are a rebellious house."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But when I speak with you, I will open your mouth, and you shall tell them, \u2018This is what the Lord GOD says.\u2019 He who hears, let him hear; and he who refuses, let him refuse; for they are a rebellious house.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou also, son of man, take a tile, and lay it before yourself, and portray on it a city, even Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Lay siege against it, build forts against it, and cast up a mound against it. Also set camps against it and plant battering rams against it all around."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Take for yourself an iron pan and set it for a wall of iron between you and the city. Then set your face toward it. It will be besieged, and you shall lay siege against it. This shall be a sign to the house of Israel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover lie on your left side, and lay the iniquity of the house of Israel on it. According to the number of the days that you shall lie on it, you shall bear their iniquity."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For I have appointed the years of their iniquity to be to you a number of days, even three hundred ninety days. So you shall bear the iniquity of the house of Israel."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAgain, when you have accomplished these, you shall lie on your right side, and shall bear the iniquity of the house of Judah. I have appointed forty days, each day for a year, to you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You shall set your face toward the siege of Jerusalem, with your arm uncovered; and you shall prophesy against it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, I put ropes on you, and you shall not turn yourself from one side to the other, until you have accomplished the days of your siege."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTake for yourself also wheat, barley, beans, lentils, millet, and spelt, and put them in one vessel. Make bread of it. According to the number of the days that you will lie on your side, even three hundred ninety days, you shall eat of it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Your food which you shall eat shall be by weight, twenty shekels a day. From time to time you shall eat it."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You shall drink water by measure, the sixth part of a hin. From time to time you shall drink."]],f:["A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons."]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You shall eat it as barley cakes, and you shall bake it in their sight with dung that comes out of man.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cEven thus will the children of Israel eat their bread unclean, among the nations where I will drive them.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cAh Lord GOD! Behold, my soul has not been polluted; for from my youth up even until now I have not eaten of that which dies of itself, or is torn of animals. No abominable meat has come into my mouth!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cBehold, I have given you cow\u2019s dung for man\u2019s dung, and you shall prepare your bread on it.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover he said to me, \u201cSon of man, behold, I will break the staff of bread in Jerusalem. They will eat bread by weight, and with fearfulness. They will drink water by measure, and in dismay;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"that they may lack bread and water, be dismayed one with another, and pine away in their iniquity."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, take a sharp sword. You shall take it as a barber\u2019s razor to yourself, and shall cause it to pass over your head and over your beard. Then take balances to weigh and divide the hair."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"A third part you shall burn in the fire in the middle of the city, when the days of the siege are fulfilled. You shall take a third part, and strike with the sword around it. A third part you shall scatter to the wind, and I will draw out a sword after them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall take a small number of these and bind them in the folds of your robe."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Of these again you shall take, and cast them into the middle of the fire, and burn them in the fire. From it a fire will come out into all the house of Israel."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Lord GOD says: \u2018This is Jerusalem. I have set her in the middle of the nations, and countries are around her."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"She has rebelled against my ordinances in doing wickedness more than the nations, and against my statutes more than the countries that are around her; for they have rejected my ordinances, and as for my statutes, they have not walked in them.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Because you are more turbulent than the nations that are around you, and have not walked in my statutes, neither have kept my ordinances, neither have followed the ordinances of the nations that are around you;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"therefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I, even I, am against you; and I will execute judgments among you in the sight of the nations."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I will do in you that which I have not done, and which I will not do anything like it any more, because of all your abominations."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore the fathers will eat the sons within you, and the sons will eat their fathers. I will execute judgments on you; and I will scatter the whole remnant of you to all the winds."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore as I live,\u2019 says the Lord GOD, \u2018surely, because you have defiled my sanctuary with all your detestable things, and with all your abominations, therefore I will also diminish you. My eye won\u2019t spare, and I will have no pity."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"A third part of you will die with the pestilence, and they will be consumed with famine within you. A third part will fall by the sword around you. A third part I will scatter to all the winds, and will draw out a sword after them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Thus my anger will be accomplished, and I will cause my wrath toward them to rest, and I will be comforted. They will know that I, the LORD, have spoken in my zeal, when I have accomplished my wrath on them."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Moreover I will make you a desolation and a reproach among the nations that are around you, in the sight of all that pass by."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So it will be a reproach and a taunt, an instruction and an astonishment, to the nations that are around you, when I execute judgments on you in anger and in wrath, and in wrathful rebukes\u2014I, the LORD, have spoken it\u2014"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"when I send on them the evil arrows of famine that are for destruction, which I will send to destroy you. I will increase the famine on you and will break your staff of bread."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I will send on you famine and evil animals, and they will bereave you. Pestilence and blood will pass through you. I will bring the sword on you. I, the LORD, have spoken it.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face toward the mountains of Israel, and prophesy to them,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018You mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD! The Lord GOD says to the mountains and to the hills, to the watercourses and to the valleys: \u201cBehold, I, even I, will bring a sword on you, and I will destroy your high places."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Your altars will become desolate, and your incense altars will be broken. I will cast down your slain men before your idols."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I will lay the dead bodies of the children of Israel before their idols. I will scatter your bones around your altars."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In all your dwelling places, the cities will be laid waste and the high places will be desolate, so that your altars may be laid waste and made desolate, and your idols may be broken and cease, and your incense altars may be cut down, and your works may be abolished."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The slain will fall among you, and you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cYet I will leave a remnant, in that you will have some that escape the sword among the nations, when you are scattered through the countries."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Those of you that escape will remember me among the nations where they are carried captive, how I have been broken with their lewd heart, which has departed from me, and with their eyes, which play the prostitute after their idols. Then they will loathe themselves in their own sight for the evils which they have committed in all their abominations."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They will know that I am the LORD. I have not said in vain that I would do this evil to them.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Lord GOD says: \u2018Strike with your hand, and stamp with your foot, and say, \u201cAlas!\u201d, because of all the evil abominations of the house of Israel; for they will fall by the sword, by the famine, and by the pestilence."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He who is far off will die of the pestilence. He who is near will fall by the sword. He who remains and is besieged will die by the famine. Thus I will accomplish my wrath on them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You will know that I am the LORD when their slain men are among their idols around their altars, on every high hill, on all the tops of the mountains, under every green tree, and under every thick oak\u2014the places where they offered pleasant aroma to all their idols."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will stretch out my hand on them and make the land desolate and waste, from the wilderness toward Diblah, throughout all their habitations. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, the Lord GOD says to the land of Israel, \u2018An end! The end has come on the four corners of the land."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now the end is on you, and I will send my anger on you, and will judge you according to your ways. I will bring on you all your abominations."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"My eye will not spare you, neither will I have pity; but I will bring your ways on you, and your abominations will be among you. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Lord GOD says: \u2018A disaster! A unique disaster! Behold, it comes."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"An end has come. The end has come! It awakes against you. Behold, it comes."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Your doom has come to you, inhabitant of the land! The time has come! The day is near, a day of tumult, and not of joyful shouting, on the mountains."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now I will shortly pour out my wrath on you, and accomplish my anger against you, and will judge you according to your ways. I will bring on you all your abominations."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"My eye won\u2019t spare, neither will I have pity. I will punish you according to your ways. Your abominations will be among you. Then you will know that I, the LORD, strike."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Behold, the day! Behold, it comes! Your doom has gone out. The rod has blossomed. Pride has budded."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Violence has risen up into a rod of wickedness. None of them will remain, nor of their multitude, nor of their wealth. There will be nothing of value among them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The time has come! The day draws near. Don\u2019t let the buyer rejoice, nor the seller mourn; for wrath is on all its multitude."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For the seller won\u2019t return to that which is sold, although they are still alive; for the vision concerns the whole multitude of it. None will return. None will strengthen himself in the iniquity of his life."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They have blown the trumpet, and have made all ready; but no one goes to the battle, for my wrath is on all its multitude."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The sword is outside, and the pestilence and the famine within. He who is in the field will die by the sword. He who is in the city will be devoured by famine and pestilence."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But of those who escape, they will escape and will be on the mountains like doves of the valleys, all of them moaning, everyone in his iniquity."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All hands will be feeble, and all knees will be weak as water."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They will also clothe themselves with sackcloth, and horror will cover them. Shame will be on all faces, and baldness on all their heads."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They will cast their silver in the streets, and their gold will be as an unclean thing. Their silver and their gold won\u2019t be able to deliver them in the day of the LORD\u2019s wrath. They won\u2019t satisfy their souls or fill their bellies; because it has been the stumbling block of their iniquity."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As for the beauty of his ornament, he set it in majesty; but they made the images of their abominations and their detestable things therein. Therefore I have made it to them as an unclean thing."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I will give it into the hands of the strangers for a prey, and to the wicked of the earth for a plunder; and they will profane it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will also turn my face from them, and they will profane my secret place. Robbers will enter into it, and profane it."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Make chains, for the land is full of bloody crimes, and the city is full of violence."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Therefore I will bring the worst of the nations, and they will possess their houses. I will also make the pride of the strong to cease. Their holy places will be profaned."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Destruction comes! They will seek peace, and there will be none."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Mischief will come on mischief, and rumor will be on rumor. They will seek a vision of the prophet; but the law will perish from the priest, and counsel from the elders."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The king will mourn, and the prince will be clothed with desolation. The hands of the people of the land will be troubled. I will do to them after their way, and according to their own judgments I will judge them. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the sixth year, in the sixth month, in the fifth day of the month, as I sat in my house, and the elders of Judah sat before me, the Lord GOD\u2019s hand fell on me there."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then I saw, and behold, a likeness as the appearance of fire\u2014from the appearance of his waist and downward, fire, and from his waist and upward, as the appearance of brightness, as it were glowing metal."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He stretched out the form of a hand, and took me by a lock of my head; and the Spirit lifted me up between earth and the sky, and brought me in the visions of God to Jerusalem, to the door of the gate of the inner court that looks toward the north, where there was the seat of the image of jealousy, which provokes to jealousy."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, the glory of the God of Israel was there, according to the appearance that I saw in the plain."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cSon of man, lift up your eyes now the way toward the north.\u201d"],[0,"So I lifted up my eyes the way toward the north, and saw, northward of the gate of the altar this image of jealousy in the entry."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, do you see what they do? Even the great abominations that the house of Israel commit here, that I should go far off from my sanctuary? But you will again see yet other great abominations.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He brought me to the door of the court; and when I looked, behold, a hole in the wall."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cSon of man, dig now in the wall.\u201d"],[0,"When I had dug in the wall, I saw a door."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cGo in, and see the wicked abominations that they do here.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So I went in and looked, and saw every form of creeping things, abominable animals, and all the idols of the house of Israel, portrayed around on the wall."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Seventy men of the elders of the house of Israel stood before them. In the middle of them Jaazaniah the son of Shaphan stood, every man with his censer in his hand; and the smell of the cloud of incense went up."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cSon of man, have you seen what the elders of the house of Israel do in the dark, every man in his rooms of imagery? For they say, \u2018The LORD doesn\u2019t see us. The LORD has forsaken the land.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He said also to me, \u201cYou will again see more of the great abominations which they do.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me to the door of the gate of the LORD\u2019s house which was toward the north; and I saw the women sit there weeping for Tammuz."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cHave you seen this, son of man? You will again see yet greater abominations than these.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He brought me into the inner court of the LORD\u2019s house; and I saw at the door of the LORD\u2019s temple, between the porch and the altar, there were about twenty-five men with their backs toward the LORD\u2019s temple and their faces toward the east. They were worshiping the sun toward the east."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cHave you seen this, son of man? Is it a light thing to the house of Judah that they commit the abominations which they commit here? For they have filled the land with violence, and have turned again to provoke me to anger. Behold, they put the branch to their nose."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Therefore I will also deal in wrath. My eye won\u2019t spare, neither will I have pity. Though they cry in my ears with a loud voice, yet I will not hear them.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he cried in my ears with a loud voice, saying, \u201cCause those who are in charge of the city to draw near, each man with his destroying weapon in his hand.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, six men came from the way of the upper gate, which lies toward the north, every man with his slaughter weapon in his hand. One man in the middle of them was clothed in linen, with a writer\u2019s inkhorn by his side. They went in, and stood beside the bronze altar."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The glory of the God of Israel went up from the cherub, whereupon it was, to the threshold of the house; and he called to the man clothed in linen, who had the writer\u2019s inkhorn by his side."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cGo through the middle of the city, through the middle of Jerusalem, and set a mark on the foreheads of the men that sigh and that cry over all the abominations that are done within it.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"To the others he said in my hearing, \u201cGo through the city after him, and strike. Don\u2019t let your eye spare, neither have pity."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Kill utterly the old man, the young man, the virgin, little children and women; but don\u2019t come near any man on whom is the mark. Begin at my sanctuary.\u201d"],[0,"Then they began at the old men who were before the house."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDefile the house, and fill the courts with the slain. Go out!\u201d"],[0,"They went out, and struck in the city."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"While they were killing, and I was left, I fell on my face, and cried, and said, \u201cAh Lord GOD! Will you destroy all the residue of Israel in your pouring out of your wrath on Jerusalem?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cThe iniquity of the house of Israel and Judah is exceedingly great, and the land is full of blood, and the city full of perversion; for they say, \u2018The LORD has forsaken the land, and the LORD doesn\u2019t see.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As for me also, my eye won\u2019t spare, neither will I have pity, but I will bring their way on their head.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the man clothed in linen, who had the inkhorn by his side, reported the matter, saying, \u201cI have done as you have commanded me.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I looked, and see, in the expanse that was over the head of the cherubim there appeared above them as it were a sapphire stone, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne."]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He spoke to the man clothed in linen, and said, \u201cGo in between the whirling wheels, even under the cherub, and fill both your hands with coals of fire from between the cherubim, and scatter them over the city.\u201d"],[0,"He went in as I watched."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Now the cherubim stood on the right side of the house when the man went in; and the cloud filled the inner court."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s glory mounted up from the cherub, and stood over the threshold of the house; and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was full of the brightness of the LORD\u2019s glory."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The sound of the wings of the cherubim was heard even to the outer court, as the voice of God Almighty when he speaks."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass, when he commanded the man clothed in linen, saying, \u201cTake fire from between the whirling wheels, from between the cherubim,\u201d that he went in and stood beside a wheel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The cherub stretched out his hand from between the cherubim to the fire that was between the cherubim, and took some of it, and put it into the hands of him who was clothed in linen, who took it and went out."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The form of a man\u2019s hand appeared here in the cherubim under their wings."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"I looked, and behold, there were four wheels beside the cherubim, one wheel beside one cherub, and another wheel beside another cherub. The appearance of the wheels was like a beryl stone."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As for their appearance, the four of them had one likeness, like a wheel within a wheel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When they went, they went in their four directions. They didn\u2019t turn as they went, but to the place where the head looked they followed it. They didn\u2019t turn as they went."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Their whole body, including their backs, their hands, their wings, and the wheels, were full of eyes all around, even the wheels that the four of them had."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"As for the wheels, they were called in my hearing, \u201cthe whirling wheels\u201d."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Every one of them had four faces. The first face was the face of the cherub. The second face was the face of a man. The third face was the face of a lion. The fourth was the face of an eagle."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The cherubim mounted up. This is the living creature that I saw by the river Chebar."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When the cherubim went, the wheels went beside them; and when the cherubim lifted up their wings to mount up from the earth, the wheels also didn\u2019t turn from beside them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When they stood, these stood. When they mounted up, these mounted up with them; for the spirit of the living creature was in them."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s glory went out from over the threshold of the house and stood over the cherubim."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The cherubim lifted up their wings and mounted up from the earth in my sight when they went out, with the wheels beside them. Then they stood at the door of the east gate of the LORD\u2019s house; and the glory of the God of Israel was over them above."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the living creature that I saw under the God of Israel by the river Chebar; and I knew that they were cherubim."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Every one had four faces, and every one four wings. The likeness of the hands of a man was under their wings."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"As for the likeness of their faces, they were the faces which I saw by the river Chebar, their appearances and themselves. They each went straight forward."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the Spirit lifted me up and brought me to the east gate of the LORD\u2019s house, which looks eastward. Behold, twenty-five men were at the door of the gate; and I saw among them Jaazaniah the son of Azzur, and Pelatiah the son of Benaiah, princes of the people."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, these are the men who devise iniquity, and who give wicked counsel in this city;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"who say, \u2018The time is not near to build houses. This is the cauldron, and we are the meat.\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Therefore prophesy against them. Prophesy, son of man.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s Spirit fell on me, and he said to me, \u201cSpeak, \u2018The LORD says: \u201cThus you have said, house of Israel; for I know the things that come into your mind."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You have multiplied your slain in this city, and you have filled its streets with the slain.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cYour slain whom you have laid in the middle of it, they are the meat, and this is the cauldron; but you will be brought out of the middle of it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You have feared the sword; and I will bring the sword on you,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cI will bring you out of the middle of it, and deliver you into the hands of strangers, and will execute judgments among you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You will fall by the sword. I will judge you in the border of Israel. Then you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"This will not be your cauldron, neither will you be the meat in the middle of it. I will judge you in the border of Israel."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You will know that I am the LORD, for you have not walked in my statutes. You have not executed my ordinances, but have done after the ordinances of the nations that are around you.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When I prophesied, Pelatiah the son of Benaiah died. Then I fell down on my face, and cried with a loud voice, and said, \u201cAh Lord GOD! Will you make a full end of the remnant of Israel?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, your brothers, even your brothers, the men of your relatives, and all the house of Israel, all of them, are the ones to whom the inhabitants of Jerusalem have said, \u2018Go far away from the LORD. This land has been given to us for a possession.\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore say, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cWhereas I have removed them far off among the nations, and whereas I have scattered them among the countries, yet I will be to them a sanctuary for a little while in the countries where they have come.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore say, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cI will gather you from the peoples, and assemble you out of the countries where you have been scattered, and I will give you the land of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018They will come there, and they will take away all its detestable things and all its abominations from there."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I will give them one heart, and I will put a new spirit within them. I will take the stony heart out of their flesh, and will give them a heart of flesh,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"that they may walk in my statutes, and keep my ordinances, and do them. They will be my people, and I will be their God."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But as for them whose heart walks after the heart of their detestable things and their abominations, I will bring their way on their own heads,\u2019 says the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the cherubim lifted up their wings, and the wheels were beside them. The glory of the God of Israel was over them above."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s glory went up from the middle of the city, and stood on the mountain which is on the east side of the city."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The Spirit lifted me up, and brought me in the vision by the Spirit of God into Chaldea, to the captives."],[0,"So the vision that I had seen went up from me."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Then I spoke to the captives all the things that the LORD had shown me."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word also came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, you dwell in the middle of the rebellious house, who have eyes to see, and don\u2019t see, who have ears to hear, and don\u2019t hear; for they are a rebellious house."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore, you son of man, prepare your baggage for moving, and move by day in their sight. You shall move from your place to another place in their sight. It may be they will consider, though they are a rebellious house."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You shall bring out your baggage by day in their sight, as baggage for moving. You shall go out yourself at evening in their sight, as when men go out into exile."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Dig through the wall in their sight, and carry your baggage out that way."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In their sight you shall bear it on your shoulder, and carry it out in the dark. You shall cover your face, so that you don\u2019t see the land, for I have set you for a sign to the house of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"I did so as I was commanded. I brought out my baggage by day, as baggage for moving, and in the evening I dug through the wall with my hand. I brought it out in the dark, and bore it on my shoulder in their sight."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"In the morning, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, hasn\u2019t the house of Israel, the rebellious house, said to you, \u2018What are you doing?\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSay to them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cThis burden concerns the prince in Jerusalem, and all the house of Israel among whom they are.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSay, \u2018I am your sign. As I have done, so will it be done to them. They will go into exile, into captivity."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The prince who is among them will bear his baggage on his shoulder in the dark, and will go out. They will dig through the wall to carry things out that way. He will cover his face, because he will not see the land with his eyes."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will also spread my net on him, and he will be taken in my snare. I will bring him to Babylon to the land of the Chaldeans; yet he will not see it, though he will die there."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will scatter toward every wind all who are around him to help him, and all his bands. I will draw out the sword after them."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018They will know that I am the LORD when I disperse them among the nations and scatter them through the countries."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But I will leave a few men of them from the sword, from the famine, and from the pestilence, that they may declare all their abominations among the nations where they come. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, eat your bread with quaking, and drink your water with trembling and with fearfulness."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Tell the people of the land, \u2018The Lord GOD says concerning the inhabitants of Jerusalem and the land of Israel: \u201cThey will eat their bread with fearfulness and drink their water in dismay, that her land may be desolate, and all that is therein, because of the violence of all those who dwell therein."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The cities that are inhabited will be laid waste, and the land will be a desolation. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, what is this proverb that you have in the land of Israel, saying, \u2018The days are prolonged, and every vision fails\u2019?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Tell them therefore, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cI will make this proverb to cease, and they will no more use it as a proverb in Israel;\u201d\u2019 but tell them, \u2018\u201cThe days are at hand, and the fulfillment of every vision."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For there will be no more any false vision nor flattering divination within the house of Israel."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For I am the LORD. I will speak, and the word that I speak will be performed. It will be no more deferred; for in your days, rebellious house, I will speak the word and will perform it,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Again the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, behold, they of the house of Israel say, \u2018The vision that he sees is for many days to come, and he prophesies of times that are far off.\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cNone of my words will be deferred any more, but the word which I speak will be performed,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, prophesy against the prophets of Israel who prophesy, and say to those who prophesy out of their own heart, \u2018Hear the LORD\u2019s word:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The Lord GOD says, \u201cWoe to the foolish prophets, who follow their own spirit, and have seen nothing!"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Israel, your prophets have been like foxes in the waste places."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You have not gone up into the gaps or built up the wall for the house of Israel, to stand in the battle in the LORD\u2019s day."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They have seen falsehood and lying divination, who say, \u2018The LORD says;\u2019 but the LORD has not sent them. They have made men to hope that the word would be confirmed."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Haven\u2019t you seen a false vision, and haven\u2019t you spoken a lying divination, in that you say, \u2018The LORD says;\u2019 but I have not spoken?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cBecause you have spoken falsehood and seen lies, therefore, behold, I am against you,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cMy hand will be against the prophets who see false visions and who utter lying divinations. They will not be in the council of my people, neither will they be written in the writing of the house of Israel, neither will they enter into the land of Israel. Then you will know that I am the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Because, even because they have seduced my people, saying, \u201cPeace;\u201d and there is no peace. When one builds up a wall, behold, they plaster it with whitewash."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Tell those who plaster it with whitewash that it will fall. There will be an overflowing shower; and you, great hailstones, will fall. A stormy wind will tear it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Behold, when the wall has fallen, won\u2019t it be said to you, \u201cWhere is the plaster with which you have plastered it?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cI will even tear it with a stormy wind in my wrath. There will be an overflowing shower in my anger, and great hailstones in wrath to consume it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So I will break down the wall that you have plastered with whitewash, and bring it down to the ground, so that its foundation will be uncovered. It will fall, and you will be consumed in the middle of it. Then you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Thus I will accomplish my wrath on the wall, and on those who have plastered it with whitewash. I will tell you, \u2018The wall is no more, nor those who plastered it\u2014"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"to wit, the prophets of Israel who prophesy concerning Jerusalem, and who see visions of peace for her, and there is no peace,\u2019\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"You, son of man, set your face against the daughters of your people, who prophesy out of their own heart; and prophesy against them,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and say, \u201cThe Lord GOD says: \u2018Woe to the women who sew magic bands on all elbows and make veils for the head of persons of every stature to hunt souls! Will you hunt the souls of my people and save souls alive for yourselves?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You have profaned me among my people for handfuls of barley and for pieces of bread, to kill the souls who should not die and to save the souls alive who should not live, by your lying to my people who listen to lies.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I am against your magic bands, with which you hunt the souls to make them fly, and I will tear them from your arms. I will let the souls fly free, even the souls whom you ensnare like birds."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I will also tear your veils and deliver my people out of your hand; and they will no longer be in your hand to be ensnared. Then you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Because with lies you have grieved the heart of the righteous, whom I have not made sad; and strengthened the hands of the wicked, that he should not return from his wicked way, and be saved alive."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall no more see false visions nor practice divination. I will deliver my people out of your hand. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then some of the elders of Israel came to me and sat before me."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, these men have taken their idols into their heart, and put the stumbling block of their iniquity before their face. Should I be inquired of at all by them?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Therefore speak to them and tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cEvery man of the house of Israel who takes his idols into his heart and puts the stumbling block of his iniquity before his face then comes to the prophet, I the LORD will answer him there according to the multitude of his idols,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"that I may take the house of Israel in their own heart, because they are all estranged from me through their idols.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore tell the house of Israel, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cReturn, and turn yourselves from your idols! Turn away your faces from all your abominations."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cFor everyone of the house of Israel, or of the strangers who live in Israel, who separates himself from me and takes his idols into his heart, and puts the stumbling block of his iniquity before his face, and comes to the prophet to inquire for himself of me, I the LORD will answer him by myself."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will set my face against that man and will make him an astonishment, for a sign and a proverb, and I will cut him off from among my people. Then you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIf the prophet is deceived and speaks a word, I, the LORD, have deceived that prophet, and I will stretch out my hand on him, and will destroy him from among my people Israel."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They will bear their iniquity. The iniquity of the prophet will be even as the iniquity of him who seeks him,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"that the house of Israel may no more go astray from me, neither defile themselves any more with all their transgressions; but that they may be my people, and I may be their God,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, when a land sins against me by committing a trespass, and I stretch out my hand on it, and break the staff of its bread and send famine on it, and cut off from it man and animal\u2014"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"though these three men, Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it, they would deliver only their own souls by their righteousness,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf I cause evil animals to pass through the land, and they ravage it and it is made desolate, so that no man may pass through because of the animals\u2014"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"though these three men were in it, as I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cthey would deliver neither sons nor daughters. They only would be delivered, but the land would be desolate."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOr if I bring a sword on that land, and say, \u2018Sword, go through the land, so that I cut off from it man and animal\u2019\u2014"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"though these three men were in it, as I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cthey would deliver neither sons nor daughters, but they only would be delivered themselves."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOr if I send a pestilence into that land, and pour out my wrath on it in blood, to cut off from it man and animal\u2014"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"though Noah, Daniel, and Job, were in it, as I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cthey would deliver neither son nor daughter; they would deliver only their own souls by their righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"For the Lord GOD says: \u201cHow much more when I send my four severe judgments on Jerusalem\u2014the sword, the famine, the evil animals, and the pestilence\u2014to cut off from it man and animal!"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Yet, behold, there will be left a remnant in it that will be carried out, both sons and daughters. Behold, they will come out to you, and you will see their way and their doings. Then you will be comforted concerning the evil that I have brought on Jerusalem, even concerning all that I have brought on it."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They will comfort you, when you see their way and their doings; then you will know that I have not done all that I have done in it without cause,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, what is the vine tree more than any tree, the vine branch which is among the trees of the forest?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Will wood be taken of it to make anything? Will men take a pin of it to hang any vessel on it?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, it is cast into the fire for fuel; the fire has devoured both its ends, and the middle of it is burned. Is it profitable for any work?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Behold, when it was whole, it was suitable for no work. How much less, when the fire has devoured it, and it has been burned, will it yet be suitable for any work?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cAs the vine wood among the trees of the forest, which I have given to the fire for fuel, so I will give the inhabitants of Jerusalem."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I will set my face against them. They will go out from the fire, but the fire will still devour them. Then you will know that I am the LORD, when I set my face against them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will make the land desolate, because they have acted unfaithfully,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Again the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, cause Jerusalem to know her abominations;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says to Jerusalem: \u201cYour origin and your birth is of the land of the Canaanite. An Amorite was your father, and your mother was a Hittite."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"As for your birth, in the day you were born your navel was not cut. You weren\u2019t washed in water to cleanse you. You weren\u2019t salted at all, nor wrapped in blankets at all."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"No eye pitied you, to do any of these things to you, to have compassion on you; but you were cast out in the open field, because you were abhorred in the day that you were born."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cWhen I passed by you, and saw you wallowing in your blood, I said to you, \u2018Though you are in your blood, live!\u2019 Yes, I said to you, \u2018Though you are in your blood, live!\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I caused you to multiply as that which grows in the field, and you increased and grew great, and you attained to excellent beauty. Your breasts were formed, and your hair grew; yet you were naked and bare."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cNow when I passed by you, and looked at you, behold, your time was the time of love; and I spread my garment over you and covered your nakedness. Yes, I pledged myself to you and entered into a covenant with you,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cand you became mine."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThen I washed you with water. Yes, I thoroughly washed away your blood from you, and I anointed you with oil."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I clothed you also with embroidered work and put leather sandals on you. I dressed you with fine linen and covered you with silk."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I decked you with ornaments, put bracelets on your hands, and put a chain on your neck."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I put a ring on your nose, earrings in your ears, and a beautiful crown on your head."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Thus you were decked with gold and silver. Your clothing was of fine linen, silk, and embroidered work. You ate fine flour, honey, and oil. You were exceedingly beautiful, and you prospered to royal estate."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Your renown went out among the nations for your beauty; for it was perfect, through my majesty which I had put on you,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut you trusted in your beauty, and played the prostitute because of your renown, and poured out your prostitution on everyone who passed by. It was his."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You took some of your garments, and made for yourselves high places decked with various colors, and played the prostitute on them. This shouldn\u2019t happen, neither shall it be."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You also took your beautiful jewels of my gold and of my silver, which I had given you, and made for yourself images of men, and played the prostitute with them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You took your embroidered garments, covered them, and set my oil and my incense before them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"My bread also which I gave you, fine flour, oil, and honey, with which I fed you, you even set it before them for a pleasant aroma; and so it was,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cMoreover you have taken your sons and your daughters, whom you have borne to me, and you have sacrificed these to them to be devoured. Was your prostitution a small matter,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"that you have slain my children and delivered them up, in causing them to pass through the fire to them?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"In all your abominations and your prostitution you have not remembered the days of your youth, when you were naked and bare, and were wallowing in your blood."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIt has happened after all your wickedness\u2014woe, woe to you!\u201d says the Lord GOD\u2014"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cthat you have built for yourselves a vaulted place, and have made yourselves a lofty place in every street."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You have built your lofty place at the head of every way, and have made your beauty an abomination, and have opened your feet to everyone who passed by, and multiplied your prostitution."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You have also committed sexual immorality with the Egyptians, your neighbors, great of flesh; and have multiplied your prostitution, to provoke me to anger."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"See therefore, I have stretched out my hand over you, and have diminished your portion, and delivered you to the will of those who hate you, the daughters of the Philistines, who are ashamed of your lewd way."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You have played the prostitute also with the Assyrians, because you were insatiable; yes, you have played the prostitute with them, and yet you weren\u2019t satisfied."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"You have moreover multiplied your prostitution to the land of merchants, to Chaldea; and yet you weren\u2019t satisfied with this."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cHow weak is your heart,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201csince you do all these things, the work of an impudent prostitute;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"in that you build your vaulted place at the head of every way, and make your lofty place in every street, and have not been as a prostitute, in that you scorn pay."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cAdulterous wife, who takes strangers instead of her husband!"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"People give gifts to all prostitutes; but you give your gifts to all your lovers, and bribe them, that they may come to you on every side for your prostitution."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"You are different from other women in your prostitution, in that no one follows you to play the prostitute; and whereas you give hire, and no hire is given to you, therefore you are different.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore, prostitute, hear the LORD\u2019s word:"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"\u2018The Lord GOD says, \u201cBecause your filthiness was poured out, and your nakedness uncovered through your prostitution with your lovers; and because of all the idols of your abominations, and for the blood of your children, that you gave to them;"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"therefore see, I will gather all your lovers, with whom you have taken pleasure, and all those whom you have loved, with all those whom you have hated. I will even gather them against you on every side, and will uncover your nakedness to them, that they may see all your nakedness."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"I will judge you as women who break wedlock and shed blood are judged; and I will bring on you the blood of wrath and jealousy."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"I will also give you into their hand, and they will throw down your vaulted place, and break down your lofty places. They will strip you of your clothes and take your beautiful jewels. They will leave you naked and bare."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"They will also bring up a company against you, and they will stone you with stones, and thrust you through with their swords."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"They will burn your houses with fire, and execute judgments on you in the sight of many women. I will cause you to cease from playing the prostitute, and you will also give no hire any more."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"So I will cause my wrath toward you to rest, and my jealousy will depart from you. I will be quiet, and will not be angry any more."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBecause you have not remembered the days of your youth, but have raged against me in all these things; therefore, behold, I also will bring your way on your head,\u201d says the Lord GOD: \u201cand you shall not commit this lewdness with all your abominations."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBehold, everyone who uses proverbs will use this proverb against you, saying, \u2018As is the mother, so is her daughter.\u2019"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"You are the daughter of your mother, who loathes her husband and her children; and you are the sister of your sisters, who loathed their husbands and their children. Your mother was a Hittite, and your father an Amorite."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Your elder sister is Samaria, who dwells at your left hand, she and her daughters; and your younger sister, who dwells at your right hand, is Sodom with her daughters."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Yet you have not walked in their ways, nor done their abominations; but soon you were more corrupt than they in all your ways."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"As I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cSodom your sister has not done, she nor her daughters, as you have done, you and your daughters."]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBehold, this was the iniquity of your sister Sodom: pride, fullness of bread, and prosperous ease was in her and in her daughters. She also didn\u2019t strengthen the hand of the poor and needy."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"They were arrogant and committed abomination before me. Therefore I took them away when I saw it."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Samaria hasn\u2019t committed half of your sins; but you have multiplied your abominations more than they, and have justified your sisters by all your abominations which you have done."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"You also bear your own shame yourself, in that you have given judgment for your sisters; through your sins that you have committed more abominable than they, they are more righteous than you. Yes, be also confounded, and bear your shame, in that you have justified your sisters."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cI will reverse their captivity, the captivity of Sodom and her daughters, and the captivity of Samaria and her daughters, and the captivity of your captives among them;"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"that you may bear your own shame, and may be ashamed because of all that you have done, in that you are a comfort to them."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"Your sisters, Sodom and her daughters, will return to their former estate; and Samaria and her daughters will return to their former estate; and you and your daughters will return to your former estate."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"For your sister Sodom was not mentioned by your mouth in the day of your pride,"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"before your wickedness was uncovered, as at the time of the reproach of the daughters of Syria, and of all who are around her, the daughters of the Philistines, who despise you all around."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"You have borne your lewdness and your abominations,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018For the Lord GOD says: \u201cI will also deal with you as you have done, who have despised the oath in breaking the covenant."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"Nevertheless I will remember my covenant with you in the days of your youth, and I will establish an everlasting covenant with you."]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"Then you will remember your ways and be ashamed when you receive your sisters, your elder sisters and your younger; and I will give them to you for daughters, but not by your covenant."]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"I will establish my covenant with you. Then you will know that I am the LORD;"]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"that you may remember, and be confounded, and never open your mouth any more because of your shame, when I have forgiven you all that you have done,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, tell a riddle, and speak a parable to the house of Israel;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cA great eagle with great wings and long feathers, full of feathers which had various colors, came to Lebanon and took the top of the cedar."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He cropped off the topmost of its young twigs, and carried it to a land of traffic. He planted it in a city of merchants."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cHe also took some of the seed of the land and planted it in fruitful soil. He placed it beside many waters. He set it as a willow tree."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"It grew and became a spreading vine of low stature, whose branches turned toward him, and its roots were under him. So it became a vine, produced branches, and shot out sprigs."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThere was also another great eagle with great wings and many feathers. Behold, this vine bent its roots toward him, and shot out its branches toward him, from the ground where it was planted, that he might water it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"It was planted in a good soil by many waters, that it might produce branches and that it might bear fruit, that it might be a good vine.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSay, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cWill it prosper? Won\u2019t he pull up its roots and cut off its fruit, that it may wither, that all its fresh springing leaves may wither? It can\u2019t be raised from its roots by a strong arm or many people."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Yes, behold, being planted, will it prosper? Won\u2019t it utterly wither when the east wind touches it? It will wither in the ground where it grew.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cSay now to the rebellious house, \u2018Don\u2019t you know what these things mean?\u2019 Tell them, \u2018Behold, the king of Babylon came to Jerusalem, and took its king, and its princes, and brought them to him to Babylon."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He took one of the royal offspring, and made a covenant with him. He also brought him under an oath, and took away the mighty of the land,"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"that the kingdom might be brought low, that it might not lift itself up, but that by keeping his covenant it might stand."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But he rebelled against him in sending his ambassadors into Egypt, that they might give him horses and many people. Will he prosper? Will he who does such things escape? Will he break the covenant, and still escape?"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018As I live,\u2019 says the Lord GOD, \u2018surely in the place where the king dwells who made him king, whose oath he despised, and whose covenant he broke, even with him in the middle of Babylon he will die."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Pharaoh with his mighty army and great company won\u2019t help him in the war, when they cast up mounds and build forts to cut off many persons."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For he has despised the oath by breaking the covenant; and behold, he had given his hand, and yet has done all these things. He won\u2019t escape."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018As I live, I will surely bring on his own head my oath that he has despised and my covenant that he has broken."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"I will spread my net on him, and he will be taken in my snare. I will bring him to Babylon, and will enter into judgment with him there for his trespass that he has trespassed against me."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"All his fugitives in all his bands will fall by the sword, and those who remain will be scattered toward every wind. Then you will know that I, the LORD, have spoken it.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Lord GOD says: \u2018I will also take some of the lofty top of the cedar, and will plant it. I will crop off from the topmost of its young twigs a tender one, and I will plant it on a high and lofty mountain."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will plant it in the mountain of the height of Israel; and it will produce boughs, and bear fruit, and be a good cedar. Birds of every kind will dwell in the shade of its branches."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"All the trees of the field will know that I, the LORD, have brought down the high tree, have exalted the low tree, have dried up the green tree, and have made the dry tree flourish."],[0,"\u201c\u2018I, the LORD, have spoken and have done it.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me again, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cWhat do you mean, that you use this proverb concerning the land of Israel, saying,"],[1,"\u2018The fathers have eaten sour grapes,"],[2,"and the children\u2019s teeth are set on edge\u2019?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cyou shall not use this proverb any more in Israel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, all souls are mine; as the soul of the father, so also the soul of the son is mine. The soul who sins, he shall die."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut if a man is just,"],[2,"and does that which is lawful and right,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"and has not eaten on the mountains,"],[2,"hasn\u2019t lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel,"],[1,"hasn\u2019t defiled his neighbor\u2019s wife,"],[2,"hasn\u2019t come near a woman in her impurity,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"and has not wronged any,"],[2,"but has restored to the debtor his pledge,"],[1,"has taken nothing by robbery,"],[2,"has given his bread to the hungry,"],[2,"and has covered the naked with a garment;"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"he who hasn\u2019t lent to them with interest,"],[2,"hasn\u2019t taken any increase from them,"],[1,"who has withdrawn his hand from iniquity,"],[2,"has executed true justice between man and man,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"has walked in my statutes,"],[2,"and has kept my ordinances,"],[2,"to deal truly;"],[1,"he is just,"],[2,"he shall surely live,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf he fathers a son who is a robber who sheds blood, and who does any one of these things,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"or who does not do any of those things"],[1,"but has eaten at the mountain shrines"],[2,"and defiled his neighbor\u2019s wife,"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"has wronged the poor and needy,"],[2,"has taken by robbery,"],[1,"has not restored the pledge,"],[2,"and has lifted up his eyes to the idols,"],[2,"has committed abomination,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"has lent with interest,"],[2,"and has taken increase from the poor,"],[0,"shall he then live? He shall not live. He has done all these abominations. He shall surely die. His blood will be on him."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, behold, if he fathers a son who sees all his father\u2019s sins which he has done, and fears, and doesn\u2019t do likewise,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"who hasn\u2019t eaten on the mountains,"],[2,"hasn\u2019t lifted up his eyes to the idols of the house of Israel,"],[2,"hasn\u2019t defiled his neighbor\u2019s wife,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"hasn\u2019t wronged any,"],[2,"hasn\u2019t taken anything to pledge,"],[1,"hasn\u2019t taken by robbery,"],[2,"but has given his bread to the hungry,"],[2,"and has covered the naked with a garment;"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"who has withdrawn his hand from the poor,"],[2,"who hasn\u2019t received interest or increase,"],[1,"has executed my ordinances,"],[2,"has walked in my statutes;"],[0,"he shall not die for the iniquity of his father. He shall surely live."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"As for his father, because he cruelly oppressed, robbed his brother, and did that which is not good among his people, behold, he will die in his iniquity."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYet you say, \u2018Why doesn\u2019t the son bear the iniquity of the father?\u2019 When the son has done that which is lawful and right, and has kept all my statutes, and has done them, he will surely live."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The soul who sins, he shall die. The son shall not bear the iniquity of the father, neither shall the father bear the iniquity of the son. The righteousness of the righteous shall be on him, and the wickedness of the wicked shall be on him."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut if the wicked turns from all his sins that he has committed, and keeps all my statutes, and does that which is lawful and right, he shall surely live. He shall not die."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"None of his transgressions that he has committed will be remembered against him. In his righteousness that he has done, he shall live."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Have I any pleasure in the death of the wicked?\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cand not rather that he should return from his way, and live?"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut when the righteous turns away from his righteousness, and commits iniquity, and does according to all the abominations that the wicked man does, should he live? None of his righteous deeds that he has done will be remembered. In his trespass that he has trespassed, and in his sin that he has sinned, in them he shall die."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYet you say, \u2018The way of the Lord is not equal.\u2019 Hear now, house of Israel: Is my way not equal? Aren\u2019t your ways unequal?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When the righteous man turns away from his righteousness, and commits iniquity, and dies in it, then he dies in his iniquity that he has done."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Again, when the wicked man turns away from his wickedness that he has committed, and does that which is lawful and right, he will save his soul alive."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Because he considers, and turns away from all his transgressions that he has committed, he shall surely live. He shall not die."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Yet the house of Israel says, \u2018The way of the Lord is not fair.\u2019 House of Israel, aren\u2019t my ways fair? Aren\u2019t your ways unfair?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore I will judge you, house of Israel, everyone according to his ways,\u201d says the Lord GOD. \u201cReturn, and turn yourselves from all your transgressions, so iniquity will not be your ruin."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Cast away from you all your transgressions in which you have transgressed; and make yourself a new heart and a new spirit. For why will you die, house of Israel?"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For I have no pleasure in the death of him who dies,\u201d says the Lord GOD. \u201cTherefore turn yourselves, and live!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover, take up a lamentation for the princes of Israel,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and say,"],[1,"\u2018What was your mother?"],[2,"A lioness."],[1,"She couched among lions,"],[2,"in the middle of the young lions she nourished her cubs."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"She brought up one of her cubs."],[2,"He became a young lion."],[1,"He learned to catch the prey."],[2,"He devoured men."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The nations also heard of him."],[2,"He was taken in their pit;"],[2,"and they brought him with hooks to the land of Egypt."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018Now when she saw that she had waited,"],[2,"and her hope was lost,"],[1,"then she took another of her cubs,"],[2,"and made him a young lion."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He went up and down among the lions."],[2,"He became a young lion."],[1,"He learned to catch the prey."],[2,"He devoured men."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He knew their palaces,"],[2,"and laid waste their cities."],[1,"The land was desolate with its fullness,"],[2,"because of the noise of his roaring."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the nations attacked him on every side from the provinces."],[2,"They spread their net over him."],[2,"He was taken in their pit."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They put him in a cage with hooks,"],[2,"and brought him to the king of Babylon."],[1,"They brought him into strongholds,"],[2,"so that his voice should no more be heard on the mountains of Israel."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018Your mother was like a vine in your blood, planted by the waters."],[2,"It was fruitful and full of branches by reason of many waters."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"It had strong branches for the scepters of those who ruled."],[2,"Their stature was exalted among the thick boughs."],[1,"They were seen in their height"],[2,"with the multitude of their branches."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"But it was plucked up in fury."],[2,"It was cast down to the ground,"],[1,"and the east wind dried up its fruit."],[2,"Its strong branches were broken off and withered."],[2,"The fire consumed them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Now it is planted in the wilderness,"],[2,"in a dry and thirsty land."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Fire has gone out of its branches."],[2,"It has devoured its fruit,"],[2,"so that there is in it no strong branch to be a scepter to rule.\u2019"],[0,"This is a lamentation, and shall be for a lamentation.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the seventh year, in the fifth month, the tenth day of the month, some of the elders of Israel came to inquire of the LORD, and sat before me."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, speak to the elders of Israel, and tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cIs it to inquire of me that you have come? As I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cI will not be inquired of by you.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWill you judge them, son of man? Will you judge them? Cause them to know the abominations of their fathers."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cIn the day when I chose Israel, and swore to the offspring of the house of Jacob, and made myself known to them in the land of Egypt, when I swore to them, saying, \u2018I am the LORD your God;\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"in that day I swore to them to bring them out of the land of Egypt into a land that I had searched out for them, flowing with milk and honey, which is the glory of all lands."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I said to them, \u2018Each of you throw away the abominations of his eyes. Don\u2019t defile yourselves with the idols of Egypt. I am the LORD your God.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut they rebelled against me and wouldn\u2019t listen to me. They didn\u2019t all throw away the abominations of their eyes. They also didn\u2019t forsake the idols of Egypt. Then I said I would pour out my wrath on them, to accomplish my anger against them in the middle of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But I worked for my name\u2019s sake, that it should not be profaned in the sight of the nations among which they were, in whose sight I made myself known to them in bringing them out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So I caused them to go out of the land of Egypt and brought them into the wilderness."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I gave them my statutes and showed them my ordinances, which if a man does, he will live in them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Moreover also I gave them my Sabbaths, to be a sign between me and them, that they might know that I am the LORD who sanctifies them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut the house of Israel rebelled against me in the wilderness. They didn\u2019t walk in my statutes and they rejected my ordinances, which if a man keeps, he shall live in them. They greatly profaned my Sabbaths. Then I said I would pour out my wrath on them in the wilderness, to consume them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But I worked for my name\u2019s sake, that it should not be profaned in the sight of the nations, in whose sight I brought them out."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Moreover also I swore to them in the wilderness that I would not bring them into the land which I had given them, flowing with milk and honey, which is the glory of all lands,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"because they rejected my ordinances, and didn\u2019t walk in my statutes, and profaned my Sabbaths; for their heart went after their idols."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Nevertheless my eye spared them, and I didn\u2019t destroy them. I didn\u2019t make a full end of them in the wilderness."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I said to their children in the wilderness, \u2018Don\u2019t walk in the statutes of your fathers. Don\u2019t observe their ordinances or defile yourselves with their idols."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I am the LORD your God. Walk in my statutes, keep my ordinances, and do them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Make my Sabbaths holy. They shall be a sign between me and you, that you may know that I am the LORD your God.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut the children rebelled against me. They didn\u2019t walk in my statutes, and didn\u2019t keep my ordinances to do them, which if a man does, he shall live in them. They profaned my Sabbaths. Then I said I would pour out my wrath on them, to accomplish my anger against them in the wilderness."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Nevertheless I withdrew my hand and worked for my name\u2019s sake, that it should not be profaned in the sight of the nations, in whose sight I brought them out."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Moreover I swore to them in the wilderness, that I would scatter them among the nations and disperse them through the countries,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"because they had not executed my ordinances, but had rejected my statutes, and had profaned my Sabbaths, and their eyes were after their fathers\u2019 idols."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Moreover also I gave them statutes that were not good, and ordinances in which they couldn\u2019t live."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I polluted them in their own gifts, in that they caused all that opens the womb to pass through the fire, that I might make them desolate, to the end that they might know that I am the LORD.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore, son of man, speak to the house of Israel, and tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cMoreover, in this your fathers have blasphemed me, in that they have committed a trespass against me."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For when I had brought them into the land which I swore to give to them, then they saw every high hill and every thick tree, and they offered there their sacrifices, and there they presented the provocation of their offering. There they also made their pleasant aroma, and there they poured out their drink offerings."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Then I said to them, \u2018What does the high place where you go mean?\u2019 So its name is called Bamah to this day.\u201d\u2019"]],f:["\u201cBamah\u201d means \u201cHigh Place\u201d."]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore tell the house of Israel, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cDo you pollute yourselves in the way of your fathers? Do you play the prostitute after their abominations?"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"When you offer your gifts, when you make your sons pass through the fire, do you pollute yourselves with all your idols to this day? Should I be inquired of by you, house of Israel? As I live, says the Lord GOD, I will not be inquired of by you!"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThat which comes into your mind will not be at all, in that you say, \u2018We will be as the nations, as the families of the countries, to serve wood and stone.\u2019"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"As I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201csurely with a mighty hand, with an outstretched arm, and with wrath poured out, I will be king over you."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"I will bring you out from the peoples, and will gather you out of the countries in which you are scattered with a mighty hand, with an outstretched arm, and with wrath poured out."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"I will bring you into the wilderness of the peoples, and there I will enter into judgment with you face to face."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Just as I entered into judgment with your fathers in the wilderness of the land of Egypt, so I will enter into judgment with you,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"\u201cI will cause you to pass under the rod, and I will bring you into the bond of the covenant."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"I will purge out from among you the rebels and those who disobey me. I will bring them out of the land where they live, but they shall not enter into the land of Israel. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018As for you, house of Israel, the Lord GOD says: \u201cGo, everyone serve his idols, and hereafter also, if you will not listen to me; but you shall no more profane my holy name with your gifts and with your idols."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"For in my holy mountain, in the mountain of the height of Israel,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cthere all the house of Israel, all of them, shall serve me in the land. There I will accept them, and there I will require your offerings and the first fruits of your offerings, with all your holy things."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"I will accept you as a pleasant aroma when I bring you out from the peoples and gather you out of the countries in which you have been scattered. I will be sanctified in you in the sight of the nations."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"You will know that I am the LORD when I bring you into the land of Israel, into the country which I swore to give to your fathers."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"There you will remember your ways, and all your deeds in which you have polluted yourselves. Then you will loathe yourselves in your own sight for all your evils that you have committed."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"You will know that I am the LORD, when I have dealt with you for my name\u2019s sake, not according to your evil ways, nor according to your corrupt doings, you house of Israel,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face toward the south, and preach toward the south, and prophesy against the forest of the field in the south."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Tell the forest of the south, \u2018Hear the LORD\u2019s word: The Lord GOD says, \u201cBehold, I will kindle a fire in you, and it will devour every green tree in you, and every dry tree. The burning flame will not be quenched, and all faces from the south to the north will be burned by it."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"All flesh will see that I, the LORD, have kindled it. It will not be quenched.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cAh Lord GOD! They say of me, \u2018Isn\u2019t he a speaker of parables?\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face toward Jerusalem, and preach toward the sanctuaries, and prophesy against the land of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Tell the land of Israel, \u2018The LORD says: \u201cBehold, I am against you, and will draw my sword out of its sheath, and will cut off from you the righteous and the wicked."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Seeing then that I will cut off from you the righteous and the wicked, therefore my sword will go out of its sheath against all flesh from the south to the north."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All flesh will know that I, the LORD, have drawn my sword out of its sheath. It will not return any more.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore sigh, you son of man. You shall sigh before their eyes with a broken heart and with bitterness."]],f:["literally, the breaking of your thighs"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It shall be, when they ask you, \u2018Why do you sigh?\u2019 that you shall say, \u2018Because of the news, for it comes! Every heart will melt, all hands will be feeble, every spirit will faint, and all knees will be weak as water. Behold, it comes, and it shall be done, says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, prophesy, and say, \u2018The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cA sword! A sword!"],[2,"It is sharpened,"],[2,"and also polished."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"It is sharpened that it may make a slaughter."],[2,"It is polished that it may be as lightning."],[1,"Should we then make mirth?"],[2,"The rod of my son condemns every tree."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"It is given to be polished,"],[2,"that it may be handled."],[1,"The sword is sharpened."],[2,"Yes, it is polished"],[2,"to give it into the hand of the killer.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Cry and wail, son of man;"],[2,"for it is on my people."],[2,"It is on all the princes of Israel."],[1,"They are delivered over to the sword with my people."],[2,"Therefore beat your thigh."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor there is a trial. What if even the rod that condemns will be no more?\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYou therefore, son of man, prophesy,"],[2,"and strike your hands together."],[1,"Let the sword be doubled the third time,"],[2,"the sword of the fatally wounded."],[1,"It is the sword of the great one who is fatally wounded,"],[2,"which enters into their rooms."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I have set the threatening sword against all their gates,"],[2,"that their heart may melt,"],[2,"and their stumblings be multiplied."],[1,"Ah! It is made as lightning."],[2,"It is pointed for slaughter."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Gather yourselves together."],[2,"Go to the right."],[1,"Set yourselves in array."],[2,"Go to the left,"],[2,"wherever your face is set."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also strike my hands together,"],[2,"and I will cause my wrath to rest."],[2,"I, the LORD, have spoken it.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me again, saying,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"\u201cAlso, you son of man, appoint two ways, that the sword of the king of Babylon may come. They both will come out of one land, and mark out a place. Mark it out at the head of the way to the city."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall appoint a way for the sword to come to Rabbah of the children of Ammon, and to Judah in Jerusalem the fortified."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For the king of Babylon stood at the parting of the way, at the head of the two ways, to use divination. He shook the arrows back and forth. He consulted the teraphim. He looked in the liver."]],f:["teraphim were household idols that may have been associated with inheritance rights to the household property."]},{v:22,l:[[0,"In his right hand was the lot for Jerusalem, to set battering rams, to open the mouth in the slaughter, to lift up the voice with shouting, to set battering rams against the gates, to cast up mounds, and to build forts."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"It will be to them as a false divination in their sight, who have sworn oaths to them; but he brings iniquity to memory, that they may be taken."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Because you have caused your iniquity to be remembered, in that your transgressions are uncovered, so that in all your doings your sins appear; because you have come to memory, you will be taken with the hand."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018You, deadly wounded wicked one, the prince of Israel, whose day has come, in the time of the iniquity of the end,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"the Lord GOD says: \u201cRemove the turban, and take off the crown. This will not be as it was. Exalt that which is low, and humble that which is high."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"I will overturn, overturn, overturn it. This also will be no more, until he comes whose right it is; and I will give it.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, prophesy and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says this concerning the children of Ammon, and concerning their reproach:"],[1,"\u201cA sword! A sword is drawn!"],[2,"It is polished for the slaughter,"],[1,"to cause it to devour,"],[2,"that it may be as lightning;"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"while they see for you false visions,"],[2,"while they divine lies to you,"],[1,"to lay you on the necks of the wicked who are deadly wounded,"],[2,"whose day has come in the time of the iniquity of the end."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"Cause it to return into its sheath."],[2,"In the place where you were created,"],[2,"in the land of your birth, I will judge you."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"I will pour out my indignation on you."],[2,"I will blow on you with the fire of my wrath."],[1,"I will deliver you into the hand of brutish men,"],[2,"skillful to destroy."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"You will be for fuel to the fire."],[2,"Your blood will be in the middle of the land."],[1,"You will be remembered no more;"],[2,"for I, the LORD, have spoken it.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, will you judge? Will you judge the bloody city? Then cause her to know all her abominations."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall say, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cA city that sheds blood within herself, that her time may come, and that makes idols against herself to defile her!"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You have become guilty in your blood that you have shed, and are defiled in your idols which you have made! You have caused your days to draw near, and have come to the end of your years. Therefore I have made you a reproach to the nations, and a mocking to all the countries."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Those who are near and those who are far from you will mock you, you infamous one, full of tumult."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBehold, the princes of Israel, everyone according to his power, have been in you to shed blood."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In you have they treated father and mother with contempt. Among you they have oppressed the foreigner. In you they have wronged the fatherless and the widow."]],f:["Literally, made light of father and mother."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You have despised my holy things, and have profaned my Sabbaths."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Slanderous men have been in you to shed blood. In you they have eaten on the mountains. They have committed lewdness among you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"In you have they uncovered their fathers\u2019 nakedness. In you have they humbled her who was unclean in her impurity."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"One has committed abomination with his neighbor\u2019s wife, and another has lewdly defiled his daughter-in-law. Another in you has humbled his sister, his father\u2019s daughter."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"In you have they taken bribes to shed blood. You have taken interest and increase, and you have greedily gained of your neighbors by oppression, and have forgotten me,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBehold, therefore I have struck my hand at your dishonest gain which you have made, and at the blood which has been shed within you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Can your heart endure, or can your hands be strong, in the days that I will deal with you? I, the LORD, have spoken it, and will do it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I will scatter you among the nations, and disperse you through the countries. I will purge your filthiness out of you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You will be profaned in yourself in the sight of the nations. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, the house of Israel has become dross to me. All of them are bronze, tin, iron, and lead in the middle of the furnace. They are the dross of silver."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Because you have all become dross, therefore, behold, I will gather you into the middle of Jerusalem."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As they gather silver, bronze, iron, lead, and tin into the middle of the furnace, to blow the fire on it, to melt it, so I will gather you in my anger and in my wrath, and I will lay you there and melt you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Yes, I will gather you, and blow on you with the fire of my wrath, and you will be melted in the middle of it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"As silver is melted in the middle of the furnace, so you will be melted in the middle of it; and you will know that I, the LORD, have poured out my wrath on you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, tell her, \u2018You are a land that is not cleansed nor rained on in the day of indignation.\u2019"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There is a conspiracy of her prophets within it, like a roaring lion ravening the prey. They have devoured souls. They take treasure and precious things. They have made many widows within it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Her priests have done violence to my law and have profaned my holy things. They have made no distinction between the holy and the common, neither have they caused men to discern between the unclean and the clean, and have hidden their eyes from my Sabbaths. So I am profaned among them."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Her princes within it are like wolves ravening the prey, to shed blood and to destroy souls, that they may get dishonest gain."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Her prophets have plastered for them with whitewash, seeing false visions, and divining lies to them, saying, \u2018The Lord GOD says,\u2019 when the LORD has not spoken."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The people of the land have used oppression and exercised robbery. Yes, they have troubled the poor and needy, and have oppressed the foreigner wrongfully."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI sought for a man among them who would build up the wall and stand in the gap before me for the land, that I would not destroy it; but I found no one."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Therefore I have poured out my indignation on them. I have consumed them with the fire of my wrath. I have brought their own way on their heads,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came again to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, there were two women, the daughters of one mother."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They played the prostitute in Egypt. They played the prostitute in their youth. Their breasts were fondled there, and their youthful nipples were caressed there."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Their names were Oholah the elder, and Oholibah her sister. They became mine, and they bore sons and daughters. As for their names, Samaria is Oholah, and Jerusalem Oholibah."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOholah played the prostitute when she was mine. She doted on her lovers, on the Assyrians her neighbors,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"who were clothed with blue\u2014governors and rulers, all of them desirable young men, horsemen riding on horses."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"She gave herself as a prostitute to them, all of them the choicest men of Assyria. She defiled herself with the idols of whomever she lusted after."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"She hasn\u2019t left her prostitution since leaving Egypt; for in her youth they lay with her. They caressed her youthful nipples and they poured out their prostitution on her."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore I delivered her into the hand of her lovers, into the hand of the Assyrians on whom she doted."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"These uncovered her nakedness. They took her sons and her daughters, and they killed her with the sword. She became a byword among women; for they executed judgments on her."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHer sister Oholibah saw this, yet she was more corrupt in her lusting than she, and in her prostitution which was more depraved than the prostitution of her sister."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"She lusted after the Assyrians, governors and rulers\u2014her neighbors, clothed most gorgeously, horsemen riding on horses, all of them desirable young men."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I saw that she was defiled. They both went the same way."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cShe increased her prostitution; for she saw men portrayed on the wall, the images of the Chaldeans portrayed with red,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"dressed with belts on their waists, with flowing turbans on their heads, all of them looking like princes, after the likeness of the Babylonians in Chaldea, the land of their birth."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"As soon as she saw them, she lusted after them and sent messengers to them into Chaldea."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The Babylonians came to her into the bed of love, and they defiled her with their prostitution. She was polluted with them, and her soul was alienated from them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"So she uncovered her prostitution and uncovered her nakedness. Then my soul was alienated from her, just like my soul was alienated from her sister."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Yet she multiplied her prostitution, remembering the days of her youth, in which she had played the prostitute in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"She lusted after their lovers, whose flesh is as the flesh of donkeys, and whose issue is like the issue of horses."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Thus you called to memory the lewdness of your youth, in the caressing of your nipples by the Egyptians because of your youthful breasts."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore, Oholibah, the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I will raise up your lovers against you, from whom your soul is alienated, and I will bring them against you on every side:"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"the Babylonians and all the Chaldeans, Pekod, Shoa, Koa, and all the Assyrians with them; all of them desirable young men, governors and rulers, princes and men of renown, all of them riding on horses."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They will come against you with weapons, chariots, and wagons, and with a company of peoples. They will set themselves against you with buckler, shield, and helmet all around. I will commit the judgment to them, and they will judge you according to their judgments."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I will set my jealousy against you, and they will deal with you in fury. They will take away your nose and your ears. Your remnant will fall by the sword. They will take your sons and your daughters; and the rest of you will be devoured by the fire."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They will also strip you of your clothes and take away your beautiful jewels."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Thus I will make your lewdness to cease from you, and remove your prostitution from the land of Egypt, so that you will not lift up your eyes to them, nor remember Egypt any more.\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I will deliver you into the hand of them whom you hate, into the hand of them from whom your soul is alienated."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They will deal with you in hatred, and will take away all your labor, and will leave you naked and bare. The nakedness of your prostitution will be uncovered, both your lewdness and your prostitution."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"These things will be done to you because you have played the prostitute after the nations, and because you are polluted with their idols."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"You have walked in the way of your sister; therefore I will give her cup into your hand.\u2019"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u2018You will drink of your sister\u2019s cup,"],[2,"which is deep and large."],[1,"You will be ridiculed and held in derision."],[2,"It contains much."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"You will be filled with drunkenness and sorrow,"],[2,"with the cup of astonishment and desolation,"],[2,"with the cup of your sister Samaria."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"You will even drink it and drain it out."],[2,"You will gnaw the broken pieces of it,"],[2,"and will tear your breasts;"],[0,"for I have spoken it,\u2019 says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Because you have forgotten me and cast me behind your back, therefore you also bear your lewdness and your prostitution.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said moreover to me: \u201cSon of man, will you judge Oholah and Oholibah? Then declare to them their abominations."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For they have committed adultery, and blood is in their hands. They have committed adultery with their idols. They have also caused their sons, whom they bore to me, to pass through the fire to them to be devoured."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Moreover this they have done to me: they have defiled my sanctuary in the same day, and have profaned my Sabbaths."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"For when they had slain their children to their idols, then they came the same day into my sanctuary to profane it; and behold, they have done this in the middle of my house."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFurthermore you sisters have sent for men who come from far away, to whom a messenger was sent, and behold, they came; for whom you washed yourself, painted your eyes, decorated yourself with ornaments,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"and sat on a stately bed, with a table prepared before it, whereupon you set my incense and my oil."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe voice of a multitude being at ease was with her. With men of the common sort were brought drunkards from the wilderness; and they put bracelets on their hands, and beautiful crowns on their heads."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Then I said of her who was old in adulteries, \u2018Now they will play the prostitute with her, and she with them.\u2019"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"They went in to her, as they go in to a prostitute. So they went in to Oholah and to Oholibah, the lewd women."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Righteous men will judge them with the judgment of adulteresses and with the judgment of women who shed blood, because they are adulteresses, and blood is in their hands."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the Lord GOD says: \u2018I will bring up a mob against them, and will give them to be tossed back and forth and robbed."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"The company will stone them with stones and dispatch them with their swords. They will kill their sons and their daughters, and burn up their houses with fire."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Thus I will cause lewdness to cease out of the land, that all women may be taught not to be lewd like you."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"They will recompense your lewdness on you, and you will bear the sins of your idols. Then you will know that I am the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, in the ninth year, in the tenth month, in the tenth day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, write the name of the day, this same day. The king of Babylon drew close to Jerusalem this same day."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Utter a parable to the rebellious house, and tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says,"],[1,"\u201cPut the cauldron on the fire."],[2,"Put it on,"],[2,"and also pour water into it."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Gather its pieces into it,"],[2,"even every good piece:"],[2,"the thigh and the shoulder."],[2,"Fill it with the choice bones."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Take the choice of the flock,"],[2,"and also a pile of wood for the bones under the cauldron."],[1,"Make it boil well."],[2,"Yes, let its bones be boiled within it.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore the Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cWoe to the bloody city,"],[2,"to the cauldron whose rust is in it,"],[2,"and whose rust hasn\u2019t gone out of it!"],[1,"Take out of it piece after piece"],[2,"without casting lots for it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018\u201cFor the blood she shed is in the middle of her."],[2,"She set it on the bare rock."],[1,"She didn\u2019t pour it on the ground,"],[2,"to cover it with dust."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"That it may cause wrath to come up to take vengeance,"],[2,"I have set her blood on the bare rock,"],[2,"that it should not be covered.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore the Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cWoe to the bloody city!"],[2,"I also will make the pile great."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Heap on the wood."],[2,"Make the fire hot."],[1,"Boil the meat well."],[2,"Make the broth thick,"],[2,"and let the bones be burned."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Then set it empty on its coals,"],[2,"that it may be hot,"],[1,"and its bronze may burn,"],[2,"and that its filthiness may be molten in it,"],[2,"that its rust may be consumed."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"She is weary with toil;"],[2,"yet her great rust,"],[2,"rust by fire, doesn\u2019t leave her."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIn your filthiness is lewdness. Because I have cleansed you and you weren\u2019t cleansed, you won\u2019t be cleansed from your filthiness any more, until I have caused my wrath toward you to rest."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cI, the LORD, have spoken it. It will happen, and I will do it. I won\u2019t go back. I won\u2019t spare. I won\u2019t repent. According to your ways and according to your doings, they will judge you,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Also the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, behold, I will take away from you the desire of your eyes with one stroke; yet you shall neither mourn nor weep, neither shall your tears run down."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Sigh, but not aloud. Make no mourning for the dead. Bind your headdress on you, and put your sandals on your feet. Don\u2019t cover your lips, and don\u2019t eat mourner\u2019s bread.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"So I spoke to the people in the morning, and at evening my wife died. So I did in the morning as I was commanded."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The people asked me, \u201cWon\u2019t you tell us what these things mean to us, that you act like this?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I said to them, \u201cThe LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u2018Speak to the house of Israel, \u201cThe Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I will profane my sanctuary, the pride of your power, the desire of your eyes, and that which your soul pities; and your sons and your daughters whom you have left behind will fall by the sword."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You will do as I have done. You won\u2019t cover your lips or eat mourner\u2019s bread."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Your turbans will be on your heads, and your sandals on your feet. You won\u2019t mourn or weep; but you will pine away in your iniquities, and moan one toward another."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Thus Ezekiel will be a sign to you; according to all that he has done, you will do. When this comes, then you will know that I am the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, shouldn\u2019t it be in the day when I take from them their strength, the joy of their glory, the desire of their eyes, and that whereupon they set their heart\u2014their sons and their daughters\u2014"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"that in that day he who escapes will come to you, to cause you to hear it with your ears?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"In that day your mouth will be opened to him who has escaped, and you will speak and be no more mute. So you will be a sign to them. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face toward the children of Ammon, and prophesy against them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Tell the children of Ammon, \u2018Hear the word of the Lord GOD! The Lord GOD says, \u201cBecause you said, \u2018Aha!\u2019 against my sanctuary when it was profaned, and against the land of Israel when it was made desolate, and against the house of Judah when they went into captivity,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"therefore, behold, I will deliver you to the children of the east for a possession. They will set their encampments in you and make their dwellings in you. They will eat your fruit and they will drink your milk."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I will make Rabbah a stable for camels and the children of Ammon a resting place for flocks. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the Lord GOD says: \u201cBecause you have clapped your hands, stamped with the feet, and rejoiced with all the contempt of your soul against the land of Israel,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"therefore, behold, I have stretched out my hand on you, and will deliver you for a plunder to the nations. I will cut you off from the peoples, and I will cause you to perish out of the countries. I will destroy you. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBecause Moab and Seir say, \u2018Behold, the house of Judah is like all the nations,\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"therefore, behold, I will open the side of Moab from the cities, from his cities which are on its frontiers, the glory of the country, Beth Jeshimoth, Baal Meon, and Kiriathaim,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"to the children of the east, to go against the children of Ammon; and I will give them for a possession, that the children of Ammon may not be remembered among the nations."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I will execute judgments on Moab. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBecause Edom has dealt against the house of Judah by taking vengeance, and has greatly offended, and taken revenge on them,\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"therefore the Lord GOD says, \u201cI will stretch out my hand on Edom, and will cut off man and animal from it; and I will make it desolate from Teman. They will fall by the sword even to Dedan."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will lay my vengeance on Edom by the hand of my people Israel. They will do in Edom according to my anger and according to my wrath. Then they will know my vengeance,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBecause the Philistines have taken revenge, and have taken vengeance with contempt of soul to destroy with perpetual hostility,\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"therefore the Lord GOD says, \u201cBehold, I will stretch out my hand on the Philistines, and I will cut off the Cherethites, and destroy the remnant of the sea coast."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I will execute great vengeance on them with wrathful rebukes. Then they will know that I am the LORD, when I lay my vengeance on them.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the eleventh year, in the first of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, because Tyre has said against Jerusalem, \u2018Aha! She is broken! She who was the gateway of the peoples has been returned to me. I will be replenished, now that she is laid waste;\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"therefore the Lord GOD says, \u2018Behold, I am against you, Tyre, and will cause many nations to come up against you, as the sea causes its waves to come up."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They will destroy the walls of Tyre, and break down her towers. I will also scrape her dust from her, and make her a bare rock."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"She will be a place for the spreading of nets in the middle of the sea; for I have spoken it,\u2019 says the Lord GOD. \u2018She will become plunder for the nations."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Her daughters who are in the field will be slain with the sword. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I will bring on Tyre Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, king of kings, from the north, with horses, with chariots, with horsemen, and an army with many people."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He will kill your daughters in the field with the sword. He will make forts against you, cast up a mound against you, and raise up the buckler against you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He will set his battering engines against your walls, and with his axes he will break down your towers."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"By reason of the abundance of his horses, their dust will cover you. Your walls will shake at the noise of the horsemen, of the wagons, and of the chariots, when he enters into your gates, as men enter into a city which is broken open."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He will tread down all your streets with the hoofs of his horses. He will kill your people with the sword. The pillars of your strength will go down to the ground."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They will make a plunder of your riches and make a prey of your merchandise. They will break down your walls and destroy your pleasant houses. They will lay your stones, your timber, and your dust in the middle of the waters."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will cause the noise of your songs to cease. The sound of your harps won\u2019t be heard any more."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will make you a bare rock. You will be a place for the spreading of nets. You will be built no more; for I the LORD have spoken it,\u2019 says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Lord GOD says to Tyre: \u2018Won\u2019t the islands shake at the sound of your fall, when the wounded groan, when the slaughter is made within you?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then all the princes of the sea will come down from their thrones, and lay aside their robes, and strip off their embroidered garments. They will clothe themselves with trembling. They will sit on the ground, and will tremble every moment, and be astonished at you."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They will take up a lamentation over you, and tell you,"],[1,"\u201cHow you are destroyed,"],[2,"who were inhabited by seafaring men,"],[1,"the renowned city,"],[2,"who was strong in the sea,"],[1,"she and her inhabitants,"],[2,"who caused their terror to be on all who lived there!\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Now the islands will tremble in the day of your fall."],[2,"Yes, the islands that are in the sea will be dismayed at your departure.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the Lord GOD says: \u2018When I make you a desolate city, like the cities that are not inhabited, when I bring up the deep on you, and the great waters cover you,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"then I will bring you down with those who descend into the pit, to the people of old time, and will make you dwell in the lower parts of the earth, in the places that are desolate of old, with those who go down to the pit, that you be not inhabited; and I will set glory in the land of the living."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I will make you a terror, and you will no more have any being. Though you are sought for, yet you will never be found again,\u2019 says the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came again to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, take up a lamentation over Tyre;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and tell Tyre, \u2018You who dwell at the entry of the sea, who are the merchant of the peoples to many islands, the Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cYou, Tyre, have said,"],[2,"\u2018I am perfect in beauty.\u2019"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Your borders are in the heart of the seas."],[2,"Your builders have perfected your beauty."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"They have made all your planks of cypress trees from Senir."],[2,"They have taken a cedar from Lebanon to make a mast for you."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They have made your oars of the oaks of Bashan."],[2,"They have made your benches of ivory inlaid in cypress wood from the islands of Kittim."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Your sail was of fine linen with embroidered work from Egypt,"],[2,"that it might be to you for a banner."],[2,"Blue and purple from the islands of Elishah was your awning."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The inhabitants of Sidon and Arvad were your rowers."],[2,"Your wise men, Tyre, were in you."],[2,"They were your pilots."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The old men of Gebal"],[2,"and its wise men were your repairers of ship seams in you."],[1,"All the ships of the sea with their mariners were in you"],[2,"to deal in your merchandise."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018\u201cPersia, Lud, and Put were in your army,"],[2,"your men of war."],[1,"They hung the shield and helmet in you."],[2,"They showed your beauty."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The men of Arvad with your army were on your walls all around,"],[2,"and valiant men were in your towers."],[1,"They hung their shields on your walls all around."],[2,"They have perfected your beauty."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cTarshish was your merchant by reason of the multitude of all kinds of riches. They traded for your wares with silver, iron, tin, and lead."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cJavan, Tubal, and Meshech were your traders. They traded the persons of men and vessels of bronze for your merchandise."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThey of the house of Togarmah traded for your wares with horses, war horses, and mules."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThe men of Dedan traded with you. Many islands were the market of your hand. They brought you horns of ivory and ebony in exchange."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cSyria was your merchant by reason of the multitude of your handiworks. They traded for your wares with emeralds, purple, embroidered work, fine linen, coral, and rubies."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cJudah and the land of Israel were your traders. They traded wheat of Minnith, confections, honey, oil, and balm for your merchandise."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cDamascus was your merchant for the multitude of your handiworks by reason of the multitude of all kinds of riches, with the wine of Helbon, and white wool."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cVedan and Javan traded with yarn for your wares; wrought iron, cassia, and calamus were among your merchandise."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cDedan was your merchant in precious saddle blankets for riding."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cArabia and all the princes of Kedar were your favorite dealers in lambs, rams, and goats. In these, they were your merchants."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThe traders of Sheba and Raamah were your traders. They traded for your wares with the best of all spices, all precious stones, and gold."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cHaran, Canneh, Eden, the traders of Sheba, Asshur and Chilmad, were your traders."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"These were your traders in choice wares, in wrappings of blue and embroidered work, and in cedar chests of rich clothing bound with cords, among your merchandise."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThe ships of Tarshish were your caravans for your merchandise."],[2,"You were replenished"],[2,"and made very glorious in the heart of the seas."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Your rowers have brought you into great waters."],[2,"The east wind has broken you in the heart of the seas."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"Your riches, your wares, your merchandise,"],[2,"your mariners, your pilots, your repairers of ship seams,"],[1,"the dealers in your merchandise,"],[2,"and all your men of war who are in you,"],[1,"with all your company which is among you,"],[2,"will fall into the heart of the seas in the day of your ruin."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"At the sound of the cry of your pilots,"],[2,"the pasture lands will shake."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"All who handle the oars,"],[2,"the mariners and all the pilots of the sea,"],[2,"will come down from their ships."],[1,"They will stand on the land,"]]},{v:30,l:[[2,"and will cause their voice to be heard over you,"],[2,"and will cry bitterly."],[1,"They will cast up dust on their heads."],[2,"They will wallow in the ashes."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"They will make themselves bald for you,"],[2,"and clothe themselves with sackcloth."],[1,"They will weep for you in bitterness of soul,"],[2,"with bitter mourning."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"In their wailing they will take up a lamentation for you,"],[2,"and lament over you, saying,"],[1,"\u2018Who is there like Tyre,"],[2,"like her who is brought to silence in the middle of the sea?\u2019"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"When your wares came from the seas,"],[2,"you filled many peoples."],[1,"You enriched the kings of the earth"],[2,"with the multitude of your riches and of your merchandise."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"In the time that you were broken by the seas,"],[2,"in the depths of the waters,"],[2,"your merchandise and all your company fell within you."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"All the inhabitants of the islands are astonished at you,"],[2,"and their kings are horribly afraid."],[2,"They are troubled in their face."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"The merchants among the peoples hiss at you."],[2,"You have come to a terrible end,"],[2,"and you will be no more.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came again to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, tell the prince of Tyre, \u2018The Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cBecause your heart is lifted up,"],[2,"and you have said, \u2018I am a god,"],[1,"I sit in the seat of God,"],[2,"in the middle of the seas;\u2019"],[1,"yet you are man,"],[2,"and no god,"],[2,"though you set your heart as the heart of a god\u2014"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"behold, you are wiser than Daniel."],[2,"There is no secret that is hidden from you."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"By your wisdom and by your understanding you have gotten yourself riches,"],[2,"and have gotten gold and silver into your treasuries."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"By your great wisdom"],[2,"and by your trading you have increased your riches,"],[2,"and your heart is lifted up because of your riches\u2014\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018therefore the Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cBecause you have set your heart as the heart of God,"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"therefore, behold, I will bring strangers on you,"],[2,"the terrible of the nations."],[1,"They will draw their swords against the beauty of your wisdom."],[2,"They will defile your brightness."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They will bring you down to the pit."],[2,"You will die the death of those who are slain"],[2,"in the heart of the seas."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Will you yet say before him who kills you, \u2018I am God\u2019?"],[2,"But you are man, and not God,"],[2,"in the hand of him who wounds you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"You will die the death of the uncircumcised"],[2,"by the hand of strangers;"],[2,"for I have spoken it,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, take up a lamentation over the king of Tyre, and tell him, \u2018The Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cYou were the seal of full measure,"],[2,"full of wisdom,"],[2,"and perfect in beauty."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You were in Eden,"],[2,"the garden of God."],[1,"Every precious stone adorned you:"],[2,"ruby, topaz, emerald,"],[2,"chrysolite, onyx, jasper,"],[2,"sapphire, turquoise, and beryl."],[1,"Gold work of tambourines"],[2,"and of pipes was in you."],[2,"They were prepared in the day that you were created."]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You were the anointed cherub who covers."],[2,"Then I set you up on the holy mountain of God."],[2,"You have walked up and down in the middle of the stones of fire."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You were perfect in your ways from the day that you were created,"],[2,"until unrighteousness was found in you."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"By the abundance of your commerce, your insides were filled with violence,"],[2,"and you have sinned."],[1,"Therefore I have cast you as profane out of God\u2019s mountain."],[2,"I have destroyed you, covering cherub,"],[2,"from the middle of the stones of fire."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Your heart was lifted up because of your beauty."],[2,"You have corrupted your wisdom by reason of your splendor."],[1,"I have cast you to the ground."],[2,"I have laid you before kings,"],[2,"that they may see you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"By the multitude of your iniquities,"],[2,"in the unrighteousness of your commerce,"],[2,"you have profaned your sanctuaries."],[1,"Therefore I have brought out a fire from the middle of you."],[2,"It has devoured you."],[1,"I have turned you to ashes on the earth"],[2,"in the sight of all those who see you."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"All those who know you among the peoples will be astonished at you."],[2,"You have become a terror,"],[2,"and you will exist no more.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face toward Sidon, and prophesy against it,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I am against you, Sidon."],[2,"I will be glorified among you."],[1,"Then they will know that I am the LORD,"],[2,"when I have executed judgments in her,"],[2,"and am sanctified in her."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will send pestilence into her,"],[2,"and blood into her streets."],[1,"The wounded will fall within her,"],[2,"with the sword on her on every side."],[2,"Then they will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThere will no longer be a pricking brier to the house of Israel, nor a hurting thorn of any that are around them that scorned them. Then they will know that I am the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cWhen I have gathered the house of Israel from the peoples among whom they are scattered, and am shown as holy among them in the sight of the nations, then they will dwell in their own land which I gave to my servant Jacob."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They will dwell in it securely. Yes, they will build houses, plant vineyards, and will dwell securely when I have executed judgments on all those around them who have treated them with contempt. Then they will know that I am the LORD their God.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the tenth year, in the tenth month, on the twelfth day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and prophesy against him and against all Egypt."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Speak and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I am against you, Pharaoh king of Egypt,"],[2,"the great monster that lies in the middle of his rivers,"],[1,"that has said, \u2018My river is my own,"],[2,"and I have made it for myself.\u2019"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will put hooks in your jaws,"],[2,"and I will make the fish of your rivers stick to your scales."],[1,"I will bring you up out of the middle of your rivers,"],[2,"with all the fish of your rivers which stick to your scales."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I\u2019ll cast you out into the wilderness,"],[2,"you and all the fish of your rivers."],[1,"You\u2019ll fall on the open field."],[2,"You won\u2019t be brought together or gathered."],[1,"I have given you for food to the animals of the earth"],[2,"and to the birds of the sky."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cAll the inhabitants of Egypt will know that I am the LORD, because they have been a staff of reed to the house of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When they took hold of you by your hand, you broke and tore all their shoulders. When they leaned on you, you broke and paralyzed all of their thighs.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I will bring a sword on you, and will cut off man and animal from you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The land of Egypt will be a desolation and a waste. Then they will know that I am the LORD."],[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBecause he has said, \u2018The river is mine, and I have made it,\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"therefore, behold, I am against you and against your rivers. I will make the land of Egypt an utter waste and desolation, from the tower of Seveneh even to the border of Ethiopia."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"No foot of man will pass through it, nor will any animal foot pass through it. It won\u2019t be inhabited for forty years."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I will make the land of Egypt a desolation in the middle of the countries that are desolate. Her cities among the cities that are laid waste will be a desolation forty years. I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018For the Lord GOD says: \u201cAt the end of forty years I will gather the Egyptians from the peoples where they were scattered."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will reverse the captivity of Egypt, and will cause them to return into the land of Pathros, into the land of their birth. There they will be a lowly kingdom."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"It will be the lowest of the kingdoms. It won\u2019t lift itself up above the nations any more. I will diminish them so that they will no longer rule over the nations."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"It will no longer be the confidence of the house of Israel, bringing iniquity to memory, when they turn to look after them. Then they will know that I am the Lord GOD.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass in the twenty-seventh year, in the first month, in the first day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon caused his army to serve a great service against Tyre. Every head was made bald, and every shoulder was worn; yet he had no wages, nor did his army, from Tyre, for the service that he had served against it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I will give the land of Egypt to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon. He will carry off her multitude, take her plunder, and take her prey. That will be the wages for his army."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"I have given him the land of Egypt as his payment for which he served, because they worked for me,\u2019 says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn that day I will cause a horn to sprout for the house of Israel, and I will open your mouth among them. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came again to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, prophesy, and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cWail, \u2018Alas for the day!\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"For the day is near,"],[2,"even the LORD\u2019s day is near."],[1,"It will be a day of clouds,"],[2,"a time of the nations."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"A sword will come on Egypt,"],[2,"and anguish will be in Ethiopia,"],[2,"when the slain fall in Egypt."],[1,"They take away her multitude,"],[2,"and her foundations are broken down."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cEthiopia, Put, Lud, all the mixed people, Cub, and the children of the land that is allied with them, will fall with them by the sword.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cThey also who uphold Egypt will fall."],[2,"The pride of her power will come down."],[1,"They will fall by the sword in it from the tower of Seveneh,\u201d"],[2,"says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThey will be desolate in the middle of the countries that are desolate."],[2,"Her cities will be among the cities that are wasted."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They will know that I am the LORD"],[2,"when I have set a fire in Egypt,"],[2,"and all her helpers are destroyed."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIn that day messengers will go out from before me in ships to make the careless Ethiopians afraid. There will be anguish on them, as in the day of Egypt; for, behold, it comes.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cI will also make the multitude of Egypt to cease,"],[2,"by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He and his people with him,"],[2,"the terrible of the nations,"],[1,"will be brought in to destroy the land."],[2,"They will draw their swords against Egypt,"],[2,"and fill the land with the slain."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make the rivers dry,"],[2,"and will sell the land into the hand of evil men."],[1,"I will make the land desolate,"],[2,"and all that is therein,"],[2,"by the hand of foreigners."],[2,"I, the LORD, have spoken it.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cI will also destroy the idols,"],[2,"and I will cause the images to cease from Memphis."],[1,"There will be no more a prince from the land of Egypt."],[2,"I will put a fear in the land of Egypt."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make Pathros desolate,"],[2,"and will set a fire in Zoan,"],[2,"and will execute judgments on No."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will pour my wrath on Sin,"],[2,"the stronghold of Egypt."],[2,"I will cut off the multitude of No."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I will set a fire in Egypt"],[2,"Sin will be in great anguish."],[1,"No will be broken up."],[2,"Memphis will have adversaries in the daytime."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The young men of Aven and of Pibeseth will fall by the sword."],[2,"They will go into captivity."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"At Tehaphnehes also the day will withdraw itself,"],[2,"when I break the yokes of Egypt there."],[1,"The pride of her power will cease in her."],[2,"As for her, a cloud will cover her,"],[2,"and her daughters will go into captivity."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Thus I will execute judgments on Egypt."],[2,"Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"In the eleventh year, in the first month, in the seventh day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, I have broken the arm of Pharaoh king of Egypt. Behold, it has not been bound up, to apply medicines, to put a bandage to bind it, that it may become strong to hold the sword."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I am against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and will break his arms, the strong arm, and that which was broken. I will cause the sword to fall out of his hand."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations, and will disperse them through the countries."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and put my sword in his hand; but I will break the arms of Pharaoh, and he will groan before the king of Babylon with the groaning of a mortally wounded man."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I will hold up the arms of the king of Babylon, but the arms of Pharaoh will fall down. Then they will know that I am the LORD when I put my sword into the hand of the king of Babylon, and he stretches it out on the land of Egypt."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I will scatter the Egyptians among the nations and disperse them through the countries. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the eleventh year, in the third month, in the first day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, tell Pharaoh king of Egypt and his multitude:"],[1,"\u2018Whom are you like in your greatness?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the Assyrian was a cedar in Lebanon"],[2,"with beautiful branches,"],[1,"and with a forest-like shade,"],[2,"of high stature;"],[2,"and its top was among the thick boughs."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The waters nourished it."],[2,"The deep made it to grow."],[1,"Its rivers ran all around its plantation."],[2,"It sent out its channels to all the trees of the field."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore its stature was exalted above all the trees of the field;"],[2,"and its boughs were multiplied."],[1,"Its branches became long by reason of many waters,"],[2,"when it spread them out."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"All the birds of the sky made their nests in its boughs."],[2,"Under its branches, all the animals of the field gave birth to their young."],[2,"All great nations lived under its shadow."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Thus it was beautiful in its greatness,"],[2,"in the length of its branches;"],[2,"for its root was by many waters."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The cedars in the garden of God could not hide it."],[2,"The cypress trees were not like its branches."],[1,"The pine trees were not like its branches;"],[2,"nor was any tree in the garden of God like it in its beauty."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I made it beautiful by the multitude of its branches,"],[2,"so that all the trees of Eden,"],[2,"that were in the garden of God, envied it.\u2019"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore thus said the Lord GOD: \u2018Because he is exalted in stature, and he has set his top among the thick branches, and his heart is lifted up in his height,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I will deliver him into the hand of the mighty one of the nations. He will surely deal with him. I have driven him out for his wickedness."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Foreigners, the tyrants of the nations, have cut him off and have left him. His branches have fallen on the mountains and in all the valleys, and his boughs are broken by all the watercourses of the land. All the peoples of the earth have gone down from his shadow and have left him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"All the birds of the sky will dwell on his ruin, and all the animals of the field will be on his branches,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"to the end that none of all the trees by the waters exalt themselves in their stature, and don\u2019t set their top among the thick boughs. Their mighty ones don\u2019t stand up on their height, even all who drink water; for they are all delivered to death, to the lower parts of the earth, among the children of men, with those who go down to the pit.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Lord GOD says: \u2018In the day when he went down to Sheol, I caused a mourning. I covered the deep for him, and I restrained its rivers. The great waters were stopped. I caused Lebanon to mourn for him, and all the trees of the field fainted for him."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I made the nations to shake at the sound of his fall, when I cast him down to Sheol with those who descend into the pit. All the trees of Eden, the choice and best of Lebanon, all that drink water, were comforted in the lower parts of the earth."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They also went down into Sheol with him to those who are slain by the sword; yes, those who were his arm, who lived under his shadow in the middle of the nations."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018To whom are you thus like in glory and in greatness among the trees of Eden? Yet you will be brought down with the trees of Eden to the lower parts of the earth. You will lie in the middle of the uncircumcised, with those who are slain by the sword."],[0,"\u201c\u2018This is Pharaoh and all his multitude,\u2019 says the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twelfth year, in the twelfth month, in the first day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, take up a lamentation over Pharaoh king of Egypt, and tell him,"],[1,"\u2018You were likened to a young lion of the nations;"],[2,"yet you are as a monster in the seas."],[1,"You broke out with your rivers,"],[2,"and troubled the waters with your feet,"],[2,"and fouled their rivers.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord GOD says:"],[2,"\u201cI will spread out my net on you with a company of many peoples."],[2,"They will bring you up in my net."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I will leave you on the land."],[2,"I will cast you out on the open field,"],[1,"and will cause all the birds of the sky to settle on you."],[2,"I will satisfy the animals of the whole earth with you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I will lay your flesh on the mountains,"],[2,"and fill the valleys with your height."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also water the land in which you swim with your blood,"],[2,"even to the mountains."],[2,"The watercourses will be full of you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"When I extinguish you, I will cover the heavens"],[2,"and make its stars dark."],[1,"I will cover the sun with a cloud,"],[2,"and the moon won\u2019t give its light."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will make all the bright lights of the sky dark over you,"],[2,"and set darkness on your land,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will also trouble the hearts of many peoples,"],[2,"when I bring your destruction among the nations,"],[2,"into the countries which you have not known."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, I will make many peoples amazed at you,"],[2,"and their kings will be horribly afraid for you,"],[1,"when I brandish my sword before them."],[2,"They will tremble at every moment,"],[1,"every man for his own life,"],[2,"in the day of your fall.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"For the Lord GOD says:"],[2,"\u201cThe sword of the king of Babylon will come on you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cause your multitude to fall by the swords of the mighty."],[2,"They are all the ruthless of the nations."],[1,"They will bring the pride of Egypt to nothing,"],[2,"and all its multitude will be destroyed."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I will destroy also all its animals from beside many waters."],[2,"The foot of man won\u2019t trouble them any more,"],[2,"nor will the hoofs of animals trouble them."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Then I will make their waters clear,"],[2,"and cause their rivers to run like oil,\u201d"],[2,"says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhen I make the land of Egypt desolate and waste,"],[2,"a land destitute of that of which it was full,"],[1,"when I strike all those who dwell therein,"],[2,"then they will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThis is the lamentation with which they will lament. The daughters of the nations will lament with this. They will lament with it over Egypt, and over all her multitude,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Also in the twelfth year, in the fifteenth day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, wail for the multitude of Egypt, and cast them down, even her and the daughters of the famous nations, to the lower parts of the earth, with those who go down into the pit."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Whom do you pass in beauty? Go down, and be laid with the uncircumcised."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They will fall among those who are slain by the sword. She is delivered to the sword. Draw her away with all her multitudes."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The strong among the mighty will speak to him out of the middle of Sheol with those who help him. They have gone down. The uncircumcised lie still, slain by the sword."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAsshur is there with all her company. Her graves are all around her. All of them are slain, fallen by the sword,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"whose graves are set in the uttermost parts of the pit, and her company is around her grave, all of them slain, fallen by the sword, who caused terror in the land of the living."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThere is Elam and all her multitude around her grave; all of them slain, fallen by the sword, who have gone down uncircumcised into the lower parts of the earth, who caused their terror in the land of the living, and have borne their shame with those who go down to the pit."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They have made Elam a bed among the slain with all her multitude. Her graves are around her, all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword; for their terror was caused in the land of the living, and they have borne their shame with those who go down to the pit. He is put among those who are slain."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThere is Meshech, Tubal, and all their multitude. Their graves are around them, all of them uncircumcised, slain by the sword; for they caused their terror in the land of the living."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They will not lie with the mighty who are fallen of the uncircumcised, who have gone down to Sheol with their weapons of war and have laid their swords under their heads. Their iniquities are on their bones; for they were the terror of the mighty in the land of the living."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut you will be broken among the uncircumcised, and will lie with those who are slain by the sword."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThere is Edom, her kings, and all her princes, who in their might are laid with those who are slain by the sword. They will lie with the uncircumcised, and with those who go down to the pit."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThere are the princes of the north, all of them, and all the Sidonians, who have gone down with the slain. They are put to shame in the terror which they caused by their might. They lie uncircumcised with those who are slain by the sword, and bear their shame with those who go down to the pit."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cPharaoh will see them and will be comforted over all his multitude, even Pharaoh and all his army, slain by the sword,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"\u201cFor I have put his terror in the land of the living. He will be laid among the uncircumcised, with those who are slain by the sword, even Pharaoh and all his multitude,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, speak to the children of your people, and tell them, \u2018When I bring the sword on a land, and the people of the land take a man from among them, and set him for their watchman,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"if, when he sees the sword come on the land, he blows the trumpet and warns the people,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"then whoever hears the sound of the trumpet and doesn\u2019t heed the warning, if the sword comes and takes him away, his blood will be on his own head."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He heard the sound of the trumpet and didn\u2019t take warning. His blood will be on him; whereas if he had heeded the warning, he would have delivered his soul."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But if the watchman sees the sword come and doesn\u2019t blow the trumpet, and the people aren\u2019t warned, and the sword comes and takes any person from among them, he is taken away in his iniquity, but his blood I will require at the watchman\u2019s hand.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo you, son of man, I have set you a watchman to the house of Israel. Therefore hear the word from my mouth, and give them warnings from me."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When I tell the wicked, \u2018O wicked man, you will surely die,\u2019 and you don\u2019t speak to warn the wicked from his way, that wicked man will die in his iniquity, but I will require his blood at your hand."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, if you warn the wicked of his way to turn from it, and he doesn\u2019t turn from his way; he will die in his iniquity, but you have delivered your soul."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, tell the house of Israel: \u2018You say this, \u201cOur transgressions and our sins are on us, and we pine away in them. How then can we live?\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Tell them, \u2018\u201cAs I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cI have no pleasure in the death of the wicked, but that the wicked turn from his way and live. Turn, turn from your evil ways! For why will you die, house of Israel?\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, tell the children of your people, \u2018The righteousness of the righteous will not deliver him in the day of his disobedience. And as for the wickedness of the wicked, he will not fall by it in the day that he turns from his wickedness; neither will he who is righteous be able to live by it in the day that he sins."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When I tell the righteous that he will surely live, if he trusts in his righteousness and commits iniquity, none of his righteous deeds will be remembered; but he will die in his iniquity that he has committed."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Again, when I say to the wicked, \u201cYou will surely die,\u201d if he turns from his sin and does that which is lawful and right,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"if the wicked restore the pledge, give again that which he had taken by robbery, walk in the statutes of life, committing no iniquity, he will surely live. He will not die."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"None of his sins that he has committed will be remembered against him. He has done that which is lawful and right. He will surely live."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Yet the children of your people say, \u201cThe way of the Lord is not fair;\u201d but as for them, their way is not fair."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When the righteous turns from his righteousness and commits iniquity, he will even die therein."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When the wicked turns from his wickedness and does that which is lawful and right, he will live by it."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Yet you say, \u201cThe way of the Lord is not fair.\u201d House of Israel, I will judge every one of you after his ways.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twelfth year of our captivity, in the tenth month, in the fifth day of the month, one who had escaped out of Jerusalem came to me, saying, \u201cThe city has been defeated!\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Now the LORD\u2019s hand had been on me in the evening, before he who had escaped came; and he had opened my mouth until he came to me in the morning; and my mouth was opened, and I was no longer mute."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, those who inhabit the waste places in the land of Israel speak, saying, \u2018Abraham was one, and he inherited the land; but we are many. The land is given us for inheritance.\u2019"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Therefore tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cYou eat with the blood, and lift up your eyes to your idols, and shed blood. So should you possess the land?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You stand on your sword, you work abomination, and every one of you defiles his neighbor\u2019s wife. So should you possess the land?\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cAs I live, surely those who are in the waste places will fall by the sword. I will give whoever is in the open field to the animals to be devoured, and those who are in the strongholds and in the caves will die of the pestilence."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"I will make the land a desolation and an astonishment. The pride of her power will cease. The mountains of Israel will be desolate, so that no one will pass through."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Then they will know that I am the LORD, when I have made the land a desolation and an astonishment because of all their abominations which they have committed.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for you, son of man, the children of your people talk about you by the walls and in the doors of the houses, and speak to one another, everyone to his brother, saying, \u2018Please come and hear what the word is that comes out from the LORD.\u2019"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They come to you as the people come, and they sit before you as my people, and they hear your words, but don\u2019t do them; for with their mouth they show much love, but their heart goes after their gain."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Behold, you are to them as a very lovely song of one who has a pleasant voice, and can play well on an instrument; for they hear your words, but they don\u2019t do them."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen this comes to pass\u2014behold, it comes\u2014then they will know that a prophet has been among them.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel. Prophesy, and tell them, even the shepherds, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cWoe to the shepherds of Israel who feed themselves! Shouldn\u2019t the shepherds feed the sheep?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You eat the fat. You clothe yourself with the wool. You kill the fatlings, but you don\u2019t feed the sheep."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You haven\u2019t strengthened the diseased. You haven\u2019t healed that which was sick. You haven\u2019t bound up that which was broken. You haven\u2019t brought back that which was driven away. You haven\u2019t sought that which was lost, but you have ruled over them with force and with rigor."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They were scattered, because there was no shepherd. They became food to all the animals of the field, and were scattered."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"My sheep wandered through all the mountains and on every high hill. Yes, my sheep were scattered on all the surface of the earth. There was no one who searched or sought.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018Therefore, you shepherds, hear the LORD\u2019s word:"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"\u201cAs I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201csurely because my sheep became a prey, and my sheep became food to all the animals of the field, because there was no shepherd, and my shepherds didn\u2019t search for my sheep, but the shepherds fed themselves, and didn\u2019t feed my sheep,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"therefore, you shepherds, hear the LORD\u2019s word!\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I am against the shepherds. I will require my sheep at their hand, and cause them to cease from feeding the sheep. The shepherds won\u2019t feed themselves any more. I will deliver my sheep from their mouth, that they may not be food for them.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018For the Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I myself, even I, will search for my sheep, and will seek them out."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"As a shepherd seeks out his flock in the day that he is among his sheep that are scattered abroad, so I will seek out my sheep. I will deliver them out of all places where they have been scattered in the cloudy and dark day."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I will bring them out from the peoples, and gather them from the countries, and will bring them into their own land. I will feed them on the mountains of Israel, by the watercourses, and in all the inhabited places of the country."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will feed them with good pasture, and their fold will be on the mountains of the height of Israel. There they will lie down in a good fold. They will feed on rich pasture on the mountains of Israel."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I myself will be the shepherd of my sheep, and I will cause them to lie down,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cI will seek that which was lost, and will bring back that which was driven away, and will bind up that which was broken, and will strengthen that which was sick; but I will destroy the fat and the strong. I will feed them in justice.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for you, O my flock, the Lord GOD says: \u2018Behold, I judge between sheep and sheep, the rams and the male goats."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Does it seem a small thing to you to have fed on the good pasture, but you must tread down with your feet the residue of your pasture? And to have drunk of the clear waters, but must you foul the residue with your feet?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"As for my sheep, they eat that which you have trodden with your feet, and they drink that which you have fouled with your feet.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the Lord GOD says to them: \u2018Behold, I, even I, will judge between the fat sheep and the lean sheep."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Because you thrust with side and with shoulder, and push all the diseased with your horns, until you have scattered them abroad,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"therefore I will save my flock, and they will no more be a prey. I will judge between sheep and sheep."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will set up one shepherd over them, and he will feed them, even my servant David. He will feed them, and he will be their shepherd."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I, the LORD, will be their God, and my servant David prince among them. I, the LORD, have spoken it."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018I will make with them a covenant of peace, and will cause evil animals to cease out of the land. They will dwell securely in the wilderness and sleep in the woods."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I will make them and the places around my hill a blessing. I will cause the shower to come down in its season. There will be showers of blessing."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The tree of the field will yield its fruit, and the earth will yield its increase, and they will be secure in their land. Then they will know that I am the LORD, when I have broken the bars of their yoke, and have delivered them out of the hand of those who made slaves of them."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They will no more be a prey to the nations, neither will the animals of the earth devour them; but they will dwell securely, and no one will make them afraid."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I will raise up to them a plantation for renown, and they will no more be consumed with famine in the land, and not bear the shame of the nations any more."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"They will know that I, the LORD, their God am with them, and that they, the house of Israel, are my people, says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"You my sheep, the sheep of my pasture, are men, and I am your God,\u2019 says the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face against Mount Seir, and prophesy against it,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and tell it, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I am against you, Mount Seir, and I will stretch out my hand against you. I will make you a desolation and an astonishment."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will lay your cities waste, and you will be desolate. Then you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBecause you have had a perpetual hostility, and have given over the children of Israel to the power of the sword in the time of their calamity, in the time of the iniquity of the end,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"therefore, as I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cI will prepare you for blood, and blood will pursue you. Since you have not hated blood, therefore blood will pursue you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Thus I will make Mount Seir an astonishment and a desolation. I will cut off from it him who passes through and him who returns."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will fill its mountains with its slain. The slain with the sword will fall in your hills and in your valleys and in all your watercourses."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I will make you a perpetual desolation, and your cities will not be inhabited. Then you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBecause you have said, \u2018These two nations and these two countries will be mine, and we will possess it,\u2019 although the LORD was there,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"therefore, as I live,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cI will do according to your anger, and according to your envy which you have shown out of your hatred against them; and I will make myself known among them when I judge you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You will know that I, the LORD, have heard all your insults which you have spoken against the mountains of Israel, saying, \u2018They have been laid desolate. They have been given to us to devour.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You have magnified yourselves against me with your mouth, and have multiplied your words against me. I have heard it.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The Lord GOD says: \u201cWhen the whole earth rejoices, I will make you desolate."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"As you rejoiced over the inheritance of the house of Israel because it was desolate, so I will do to you. You will be desolate, Mount Seir, and all Edom, even all of it. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"You, son of man, prophesy to the mountains of Israel, and say, \u201cYou mountains of Israel, hear the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Lord GOD says: \u2018Because the enemy has said against you, \u201cAha!\u201d and, \u201cThe ancient high places are ours in possession!\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"therefore prophesy, and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBecause, even because they have made you desolate, and swallowed you up on every side, that you might be a possession to the residue of the nations, and you are taken up in the lips of talkers, and the evil report of the people;\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"therefore, you mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord GOD: The Lord GOD says to the mountains and to the hills, to the watercourses and to the valleys, to the desolate wastes and to the cities that are forsaken, which have become a prey and derision to the residue of the nations that are all around;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cSurely in the fire of my jealousy I have spoken against the residue of the nations, and against all Edom, that have appointed my land to themselves for a possession with the joy of all their heart, with despite of soul, to cast it out for a prey.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore prophesy concerning the land of Israel, and tell the mountains, the hills, the watercourses and the valleys, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I have spoken in my jealousy and in my wrath, because you have borne the shame of the nations.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says: \u201cI have sworn, \u2018Surely the nations that are around you will bear their shame.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut you, mountains of Israel, you shall shoot out your branches and yield your fruit to my people Israel; for they are at hand to come."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For, behold, I am for you, and I will come to you, and you will be tilled and sown."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I will multiply men on you, all the house of Israel, even all of it. The cities will be inhabited and the waste places will be built."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I will multiply man and animal on you. They will increase and be fruitful. I will cause you to be inhabited as you were before, and you will do better than at your beginnings. Then you will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Yes, I will cause men to walk on you, even my people Israel. They will possess you, and you will be their inheritance, and you will never again bereave them of their children.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBecause they say to you, \u2018You are a devourer of men, and have been a bereaver of your nation;\u2019"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"therefore you shall devour men no more, and not bereave your nation any more,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cI won\u2019t let you hear the shame of the nations any more. You won\u2019t bear the reproach of the peoples any more, and you won\u2019t cause your nation to stumble any more,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, when the house of Israel lived in their own land, they defiled it by their ways and by their deeds. Their way before me was as the uncleanness of a woman in her impurity."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Therefore I poured out my wrath on them for the blood which they had poured out on the land, and because they had defiled it with their idols."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I scattered them among the nations, and they were dispersed through the countries. I judged them according to their way and according to their deeds."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When they came to the nations where they went, they profaned my holy name, in that men said of them, \u2018These are the LORD\u2019s people, and have left his land.\u2019"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But I had respect for my holy name, which the house of Israel had profaned among the nations where they went."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore tell the house of Israel, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cI don\u2019t do this for your sake, house of Israel, but for my holy name, which you have profaned among the nations where you went."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will sanctify my great name, which has been profaned among the nations, which you have profaned among them. Then the nations will know that I am the LORD,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cwhen I am proven holy in you before their eyes."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cFor I will take you from among the nations and gather you out of all the countries, and will bring you into your own land."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I will sprinkle clean water on you, and you will be clean. I will cleanse you from all your filthiness and from all your idols."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I will also give you a new heart, and I will put a new spirit within you. I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you a heart of flesh."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"I will put my Spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes. You will keep my ordinances and do them."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You will dwell in the land that I gave to your fathers. You will be my people, and I will be your God."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I will save you from all your uncleanness. I will call for the grain and will multiply it, and lay no famine on you."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"I will multiply the fruit of the tree and the increase of the field, that you may receive no more the reproach of famine among the nations."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThen you will remember your evil ways, and your deeds that were not good; and you will loathe yourselves in your own sight for your iniquities and for your abominations."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"I don\u2019t do this for your sake,\u201d says the Lord GOD. \u201cLet it be known to you. Be ashamed and confounded for your ways, house of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cIn the day that I cleanse you from all your iniquities, I will cause the cities to be inhabited and the waste places will be built."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The land that was desolate will be tilled instead of being a desolation in the sight of all who passed by."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"They will say, \u2018This land that was desolate has become like the garden of Eden. The waste, desolate, and ruined cities are fortified and inhabited.\u2019"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Then the nations that are left around you will know that I, the LORD, have built the ruined places and planted that which was desolate. I, the LORD, have spoken it, and I will do it.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cFor this, moreover, I will be inquired of by the house of Israel, to do it for them: I will increase them with men like a flock."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"As the flock for sacrifice, as the flock of Jerusalem in her appointed feasts, so the waste cities will be filled with flocks of men. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s hand was on me, and he brought me out in the LORD\u2019s Spirit, and set me down in the middle of the valley; and it was full of bones."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He caused me to pass by them all around; and behold, there were very many in the open valley, and behold, they were very dry."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, can these bones live?\u201d"],[0,"I answered, \u201cLord GOD, you know.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he said to me, \u201cProphesy over these bones, and tell them, \u2018You dry bones, hear the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The Lord GOD says to these bones: \u201cBehold, I will cause breath to enter into you, and you will live."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I will lay sinews on you, and will bring up flesh on you, and cover you with skin, and put breath in you, and you will live. Then you will know that I am the LORD.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"So I prophesied as I was commanded. As I prophesied, there was a noise, and behold, there was an earthquake. Then the bones came together, bone to its bone."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I saw, and, behold, there were sinews on them, and flesh came up, and skin covered them above; but there was no breath in them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cProphesy to the wind, prophesy, son of man, and tell the wind, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cCome from the four winds, breath, and breathe on these slain, that they may live.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"So I prophesied as he commanded me, and the breath came into them, and they lived, and stood up on their feet, an exceedingly great army."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cSon of man, these bones are the whole house of Israel. Behold, they say, \u2018Our bones are dried up, and our hope is lost. We are completely cut off.\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore prophesy, and tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I will open your graves, and cause you to come up out of your graves, my people; and I will bring you into the land of Israel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You will know that I am the LORD, when I have opened your graves and caused you to come up out of your graves, my people."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I will put my Spirit in you, and you will live. Then I will place you in your own land; and you will know that I, the LORD, have spoken it and performed it,\u201d says the LORD.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came again to me, saying,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, take one stick and write on it, \u2018For Judah, and for the children of Israel his companions.\u2019 Then take another stick, and write on it, \u2018For Joseph, the stick of Ephraim, and for all the house of Israel his companions.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then join them for yourself to one another into one stick, that they may become one in your hand."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the children of your people speak to you, saying, \u2018Won\u2019t you show us what you mean by these?\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"tell them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I will take the stick of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel his companions; and I will put them with it, with the stick of Judah, and make them one stick, and they will be one in my hand."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The sticks on which you write will be in your hand before their eyes.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Say to them, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I will take the children of Israel from among the nations where they have gone, and will gather them on every side, and bring them into their own land."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will make them one nation in the land, on the mountains of Israel. One king will be king to them all. They will no longer be two nations. They won\u2019t be divided into two kingdoms any more at all."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They won\u2019t defile themselves any more with their idols, nor with their detestable things, nor with any of their transgressions; but I will save them out of all their dwelling places in which they have sinned, and will cleanse them. So they will be my people, and I will be their God."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cMy servant David will be king over them. They all will have one shepherd. They will also walk in my ordinances and observe my statutes, and do them."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They will dwell in the land that I have given to Jacob my servant, in which your fathers lived. They will dwell therein, they, and their children, and their children\u2019s children, forever. David my servant will be their prince forever."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Moreover I will make a covenant of peace with them. It will be an everlasting covenant with them. I will place them, multiply them, and will set my sanctuary among them forever more."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"My tent also will be with them. I will be their God, and they will be my people."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The nations will know that I am the LORD who sanctifies Israel, when my sanctuary is among them forever more.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSon of man, set your face toward Gog, of the land of Magog, the prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal, and prophesy against him,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I am against you, Gog, prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will turn you around, and put hooks into your jaws, and I will bring you out, with all your army, horses and horsemen, all of them clothed in full armor, a great company with buckler and shield, all of them handling swords;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Persia, Cush, and Put with them, all of them with shield and helmet;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Gomer, and all his hordes; the house of Togarmah in the uttermost parts of the north, and all his hordes\u2014even many peoples with you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBe prepared, yes, prepare yourself, you, and all your companies who are assembled to you, and be a guard to them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"After many days you will be visited. In the latter years you will come into the land that is brought back from the sword, that is gathered out of many peoples, on the mountains of Israel, which have been a continual waste; but it is brought out of the peoples and they will dwell securely, all of them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You will ascend. You will come like a storm. You will be like a cloud to cover the land, you and all your hordes, and many peoples with you.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cIt will happen in that day that things will come into your mind, and you will devise an evil plan."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You will say, \u2018I will go up to the land of unwalled villages. I will go to those who are at rest, who dwell securely, all of them dwelling without walls, and having neither bars nor gates,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"to take the plunder and to take prey; to turn your hand against the waste places that are inhabited, and against the people who are gathered out of the nations, who have gotten livestock and goods, who dwell in the middle of the earth.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Sheba, Dedan, and the merchants of Tarshish, with all its young lions, will ask you, \u2018Have you come to take the plunder? Have you assembled your company to take the prey, to carry away silver and gold, to take away livestock and goods, to take great plunder?\u2019\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore, son of man, prophesy, and tell Gog, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cIn that day when my people Israel dwells securely, will you not know it?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You will come from your place out of the uttermost parts of the north, you, and many peoples with you, all of them riding on horses, a great company and a mighty army."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You will come up against my people Israel as a cloud to cover the land. It will happen in the latter days that I will bring you against my land, that the nations may know me when I am sanctified in you, Gog, before their eyes.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cAre you he of whom I spoke in old time by my servants the prophets of Israel, who prophesied in those days for years that I would bring you against them?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day, when Gog comes against the land of Israel,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cthat my wrath will come up into my nostrils."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For in my jealousy and in the fire of my wrath I have spoken. Surely in that day there will be a great shaking in the land of Israel,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"so that the fish of the sea, the birds of the sky, the animals of the field, all creeping things who creep on the earth, and all the men who are on the surface of the earth will shake at my presence. Then the mountains will be thrown down, the steep places will fall, and every wall will fall to the ground."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I will call for a sword against him to all my mountains,\u201d says the Lord GOD. \u201cEvery man\u2019s sword will be against his brother."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will enter into judgment with him with pestilence and with blood. I will rain on him, on his hordes, and on the many peoples who are with him, torrential rains with great hailstones, fire, and sulfur."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will magnify myself and sanctify myself, and I will make myself known in the eyes of many nations. Then they will know that I am the LORD.\u201d\u2019"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, prophesy against Gog, and say, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cBehold, I am against you, Gog, prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I will turn you around, will lead you on, and will cause you to come up from the uttermost parts of the north; and I will bring you onto the mountains of Israel."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will strike your bow out of your left hand, and will cause your arrows to fall out of your right hand."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You will fall on the mountains of Israel, you, and all your hordes, and the peoples who are with you. I will give you to the ravenous birds of every sort and to the animals of the field to be devoured."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You will fall on the open field, for I have spoken it,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cI will send a fire on Magog and on those who dwell securely in the islands. Then they will know that I am the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cI will make my holy name known among my people Israel. I won\u2019t allow my holy name to be profaned any more. Then the nations will know that I am the LORD, the Holy One in Israel."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, it comes, and it will be done,\u201d says the Lord GOD. \u201cThis is the day about which I have spoken."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThose who dwell in the cities of Israel will go out and will make fires of the weapons and burn them, both the shields and the bucklers, the bows and the arrows, and the war clubs and the spears, and they will make fires with them for seven years;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"so that they will take no wood out of the field, and not cut down any out of the forests; for they will make fires with the weapons. They will plunder those who plundered them, and rob those who robbed them,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIt will happen in that day, that I will give to Gog a place for burial in Israel, the valley of those who pass through on the east of the sea; and it will stop those who pass through. They will bury Gog and all his multitude there, and they will call it \u2018The valley of Hamon Gog\u2019."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThe house of Israel will be burying them for seven months, that they may cleanse the land."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Yes, all the people of the land will bury them; and they will become famous in the day that I will be glorified,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThey will set apart men of continual employment who will pass through the land. Those who pass through will go with those who bury those who remain on the surface of the land, to cleanse it. After the end of seven months they will search."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Those who search through the land will pass through; and when anyone sees a man\u2019s bone, then he will set up a sign by it, until the undertakers have buried it in the valley of Hamon Gog."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Hamonah will also be the name of a city. Thus they will cleanse the land.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, the Lord GOD says: \u2018Speak to the birds of every sort, and to every animal of the field, \u201cAssemble yourselves, and come; gather yourselves on every side to my sacrifice that I sacrifice for you, even a great sacrifice on the mountains of Israel, that you may eat meat and drink blood."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"You shall eat the flesh of the mighty, and drink the blood of the princes of the earth, of rams, of lambs, and of goats, of bulls, all of them fatlings of Bashan."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall eat fat until you are full, and drink blood until you are drunk, of my sacrifice which I have sacrificed for you."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall be filled at my table with horses and charioteers, with mighty men, and with all men of war,\u201d says the Lord GOD.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI will set my glory among the nations. Then all the nations will see my judgment that I have executed, and my hand that I have laid on them."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"So the house of Israel will know that I am the LORD their God, from that day and forward."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The nations will know that the house of Israel went into captivity for their iniquity, because they trespassed against me, and I hid my face from them; so I gave them into the hand of their adversaries, and they all fell by the sword."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I did to them according to their uncleanness and according to their transgressions. I hid my face from them."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore the Lord GOD says: \u2018Now I will reverse the captivity of Jacob and have mercy on the whole house of Israel. I will be jealous for my holy name."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They will forget their shame and all their trespasses by which they have trespassed against me, when they dwell securely in their land. No one will make them afraid"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"when I have brought them back from the peoples, gathered them out of their enemies\u2019 lands, and am shown holy among them in the sight of many nations."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They will know that I am the LORD their God, in that I caused them to go into captivity among the nations, and have gathered them to their own land. Then I will leave none of them captive any more."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I won\u2019t hide my face from them any more, for I have poured out my Spirit on the house of Israel,\u2019 says the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twenty-fifth year of our captivity, in the beginning of the year, in the tenth day of the month, in the fourteenth year after the city was struck, in the same day, the LORD\u2019s hand was on me, and he brought me there."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In the visions of God he brought me into the land of Israel, and set me down on a very high mountain, on which was something like the frame of a city to the south."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He brought me there; and, behold, there was a man whose appearance was like the appearance of bronze, with a line of flax in his hand and a measuring reed; and he stood in the gate."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The man said to me, \u201cSon of man, see with your eyes, and hear with your ears, and set your heart on all that I will show you; for you have been brought here so that I may show them to you. Declare all that you see to the house of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, there was a wall on the outside of the house all around, and in the man\u2019s hand a measuring reed six cubits long, of a cubit and a hand width each. So he measured the thickness of the building, one reed; and the height, one reed."]],f:["A normal cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters. A handbreadth is about 4.3 inches or 11 centimeters, so the long cubit described here would be about 22.3 inches or 57 centimeters long. Thus, a 6 long cubit measuring reed would have been about 3 yards 26.6 inches or about 3.42 meters long."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he came to the gate which looks toward the east, and went up its steps. He measured the threshold of the gate, one reed wide; and the other threshold, one reed wide."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Every lodge was one reed long and one reed wide. Between the lodges was five cubits. The threshold of the gate by the porch of the gate toward the house was one reed."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He measured also the porch of the gate toward the house, one reed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then he measured the porch of the gate, eight cubits; and its posts, two cubits; and the porch of the gate was toward the house."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The side rooms of the gate eastward were three on this side, and three on that side. The three of them were of one measure. The posts had one measure on this side and on that side."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He measured the width of the opening of the gate, ten cubits; and the length of the gate, thirteen cubits;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and a border before the lodges, one cubit on this side, and a border, one cubit on that side; and the side rooms, six cubits on this side, and six cubits on that side."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He measured the gate from the roof of the one side room to the roof of the other, a width of twenty-five cubits, door against door."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He also made posts, sixty cubits; and the court reached to the posts, around the gate."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"From the forefront of the gate at the entrance to the forefront of the inner porch of the gate were fifty cubits."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"There were closed windows to the side rooms, and to their posts within the gate all around, and likewise to the arches. Windows were around inward. Palm trees were on each post."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me into the outer court. Behold, there were rooms and a pavement made for the court all around. Thirty rooms were on the pavement."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The pavement was by the side of the gates, corresponding to the length of the gates, even the lower pavement."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Then he measured the width from the forefront of the lower gate to the forefront of the inner court outside, one hundred cubits, both on the east and on the north."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He measured the length and width of the gate of the outer court which faces toward the north."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The lodges of it were three on this side and three on that side. Its posts and its arches were the same as the measure of the first gate: its length was fifty cubits, and the width twenty-five cubits."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Its windows, its arches, and its palm trees were the same as the measure of the gate which faces toward the east. They went up to it by seven steps. Its arches were before them."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"There was a gate to the inner court facing the other gate, on the north and on the east. He measured one hundred cubits from gate to gate."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"He led me toward the south; and behold, there was a gate toward the south. He measured its posts and its arches according to these measurements."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There were windows in it and in its arches all around, like the other windows: the length was fifty cubits, and the width twenty-five cubits."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"There were seven steps to go up to it, and its arches were before them. It had palm trees, one on this side, and another on that side, on its posts."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"There was a gate to the inner court toward the south. He measured one hundred cubits from gate to gate toward the south."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me to the inner court by the south gate. He measured the south gate according to these measurements;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"with its lodges, its posts, and its arches, according to these measurements. There were windows in it and in its arches all around. It was fifty cubits long, and twenty-five cubits wide."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"There were arches all around, twenty-five cubits long and five cubits wide."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Its arches were toward the outer court. Palm trees were on its posts. The ascent to it had eight steps."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"He brought me into the inner court toward the east. He measured the gate according to these measurements;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"with its lodges, its posts, and its arches, according to these measurements. There were windows in it and in its arches all around. It was fifty cubits long, and twenty-five cubits wide."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Its arches were toward the outer court. Palm trees were on its posts on this side and on that side. The ascent to it had eight steps."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"He brought me to the north gate, and he measured it according to these measurements\u2014"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"its lodges, its posts, and its arches. There were windows in it all around. The length was fifty cubits and the width twenty-five cubits."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Its posts were toward the outer court. Palm trees were on its posts on this side and on that side. The ascent to it had eight steps."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"A room with its door was by the posts at the gates. They washed the burnt offering there."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"In the porch of the gate were two tables on this side and two tables on that side, on which to kill the burnt offering, the sin offering, and the trespass offering."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"On the one side outside, as one goes up to the entry of the gate toward the north, were two tables; and on the other side, which belonged to the porch of the gate, were two tables."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Four tables were on this side, and four tables on that side, by the side of the gate: eight tables, on which they killed the sacrifices."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"There were four cut stone tables for the burnt offering, a cubit and a half long, a cubit and a half wide, and one cubit high. They laid the instruments with which they killed the burnt offering and the sacrifice on them."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"The hooks, a hand width long, were fastened within all around. The meat of the offering was on the tables."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"Outside of the inner gate were rooms for the singers in the inner court, which was at the side of the north gate. They faced toward the south. One at the side of the east gate faced toward the north."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cThis room, which faces toward the south, is for the priests who perform the duty of the house."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"The room which faces toward the north is for the priests who perform the duty of the altar. These are the sons of Zadok, who from among the sons of Levi come near to the LORD to minister to him.\u201d"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"He measured the court, one hundred cubits long and one hundred cubits wide, square. The altar was before the house."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me to the porch of the house, and measured each post of the porch, five cubits on this side, and five cubits on that side. The width of the gate was three cubits on this side and three cubits on that side."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"The length of the porch was twenty cubits and the width eleven cubits, even by the steps by which they went up to it. There were pillars by the posts, one on this side, and another on that side."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He brought me to the nave and measured the posts, six cubits wide on the one side and six cubits wide on the other side, which was the width of the tent."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The width of the entrance was ten cubits, and the sides of the entrance were five cubits on the one side, and five cubits on the other side. He measured its length, forty cubits, and the width, twenty cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he went inward and measured each post of the entrance, two cubits; and the entrance, six cubits; and the width of the entrance, seven cubits."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He measured its length, twenty cubits, and the width, twenty cubits, before the nave. He said to me, \u201cThis is the most holy place.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he measured the wall of the house, six cubits; and the width of every side room, four cubits, all around the house on every side."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The side rooms were in three stories, one over another, and thirty in each story. They entered into the wall which belonged to the house for the side rooms all around, that they might be supported and not penetrate the wall of the house."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The side rooms were wider on the higher levels, because the walls were narrower at the higher levels. Therefore the width of the house increased upward; and so one went up from the lowest level to the highest through the middle level."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw also that the house had a raised base all around. The foundations of the side rooms were a full reed of six great cubits."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The thickness of the outer wall of the side rooms was five cubits. That which was left was the place of the side rooms that belonged to the house."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Between the rooms was a width of twenty cubits around the house on every side."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The doors of the side rooms were toward an open area that was left, one door toward the north, and another door toward the south. The width of the open area was five cubits all around."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The building that was before the separate place at the side toward the west was seventy cubits wide; and the wall of the building was five cubits thick all around, and its length ninety cubits."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"So he measured the temple, one hundred cubits long; and the separate place, and the building, with its walls, one hundred cubits long;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"also the width of the face of the temple, and of the separate place toward the east, one hundred cubits."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He measured the length of the building before the separate place which was at its back, and its galleries on the one side and on the other side, one hundred cubits from the inner temple, and the porches of the court,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"the thresholds, and the closed windows, and the galleries around on their three stories, opposite the threshold, with wood ceilings all around, and from the ground up to the windows, (now the windows were covered),"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"to the space above the door, even to the inner house, and outside, and by all the wall all around inside and outside, by measure."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"It was made with cherubim and palm trees. A palm tree was between cherub and cherub, and every cherub had two faces,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"so that there was the face of a man toward the palm tree on the one side, and the face of a young lion toward the palm tree on the other side. It was made like this through all the house all around."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Cherubim and palm trees were made from the ground to above the door. The wall of the temple was like this."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The door posts of the nave were squared. As for the face of the nave, its appearance was as the appearance of the temple."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The altar was of wood, three cubits high, and its length two cubits. Its corners, its base, and its walls were of wood. He said to me, \u201cThis is the table that is before the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The temple and the sanctuary had two doors."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The doors had two leaves each, two turning leaves: two for the one door, and two leaves for the other."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There were made on them, on the doors of the nave, cherubim and palm trees, like those made on the walls. There was a threshold of wood on the face of the porch outside."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"There were closed windows and palm trees on the one side and on the other side, on the sides of the porch. This is how the side rooms of the temple and the thresholds were arranged."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me out into the outer court, the way toward the north. Then he brought me into the room that was opposite the separate place, and which was opposite the building toward the north."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Facing the length of one hundred cubits was the north door, and the width was fifty cubits."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Opposite the twenty cubits which belonged to the inner court, and opposite the pavement which belonged to the outer court, was gallery against gallery in the three stories."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Before the rooms was a walk of ten cubits\u2019 width inward, a way of one cubit; and their doors were toward the north."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now the upper rooms were shorter; for the galleries took away from these more than from the lower and the middle in the building."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For they were in three stories, and they didn\u2019t have pillars as the pillars of the courts. Therefore the uppermost was set back more than the lowest and the middle from the ground."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The wall that was outside by the side of the rooms, toward the outer court before the rooms, was fifty cubits long."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the length of the rooms that were in the outer court was fifty cubits. Behold, those facing the temple were one hundred cubits."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"From under these rooms was the entry on the east side, as one goes into them from the outer court."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"In the thickness of the wall of the court toward the east, before the separate place, and before the building, there were rooms."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The way before them was like the appearance of the rooms which were toward the north. Their length and width were the same. All their exits had the same arrangement and doors."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Like the doors of the rooms that were toward the south was a door at the head of the way, even the way directly before the wall toward the east, as one enters into them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cThe north rooms and the south rooms, which are opposite the separate place, are the holy rooms, where the priests who are near to the LORD shall eat the most holy things. There they shall lay the most holy things, with the meal offering, the sin offering, and the trespass offering; for the place is holy."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When the priests enter in, then they shall not go out of the holy place into the outer court until they lay their garments in which they minister there; for they are holy. Then they shall put on other garments, and shall approach that which is for the people.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when he had finished measuring the inner house, he brought me out by the way of the gate which faces toward the east, and measured it all around."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He measured on the east side with the measuring reed five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed all around."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He measured on the north side five hundred reeds with the measuring reed all around."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He measured on the south side five hundred reeds with the measuring reed."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He turned about to the west side, and measured five hundred reeds with the measuring reed."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He measured it on the four sides. It had a wall around it, the length five hundred cubits, and the width five hundred cubits, to make a separation between that which was holy and that which was common."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Afterward he brought me to the gate, even the gate that looks toward the east."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, the glory of the God of Israel came from the way of the east. His voice was like the sound of many waters; and the earth was illuminated with his glory."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It was like the appearance of the vision which I saw, even according to the vision that I saw when I came to destroy the city; and the visions were like the vision that I saw by the river Chebar; and I fell on my face."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s glory came into the house by the way of the gate which faces toward the east."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The Spirit took me up and brought me into the inner court; and behold, the LORD\u2019s glory filled the house."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard one speaking to me out of the house, and a man stood by me."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, this is the place of my throne and the place of the soles of my feet, where I will dwell among the children of Israel forever. The house of Israel will no more defile my holy name, neither they nor their kings, by their prostitution and by the dead bodies of their kings in their high places;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"in their setting of their threshold by my threshold and their door post beside my door post. There was a wall between me and them; and they have defiled my holy name by their abominations which they have committed. Therefore I have consumed them in my anger."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now let them put away their prostitution, and the dead bodies of their kings far from me. Then I will dwell among them forever."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, son of man, show the house to the house of Israel, that they may be ashamed of their iniquities; and let them measure the pattern."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If they are ashamed of all that they have done, make known to them the form of the house, its fashion, its exits, its entrances, its structure, all its ordinances, all its forms, and all its laws; and write it in their sight, that they may keep the whole form of it, and all its ordinances, and do them."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the law of the house. On the top of the mountain the whole limit around it shall be most holy. Behold, this is the law of the house."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThese are the measurements of the altar by cubits (the cubit is a cubit and a hand width): the bottom shall be a cubit, and the width a cubit, and its border around its edge a span; and this shall be the base of the altar."]],f:["A normal cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters. A hand width is about 4.3 inches or 11 cm.","A span is the length from the tip of a man\u2019s thumb to the tip of his little finger when his hand is stretched out (about half a cubit, or 9 inches, or 22.8 cm.)"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"From the bottom on the ground to the lower ledge shall be two cubits, and the width one cubit; and from the lesser ledge to the greater ledge shall be four cubits, and the width a cubit."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The upper altar shall be four cubits; and from the altar hearth and upward there shall be four horns."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The altar hearth shall be twelve cubits long by twelve wide, square in its four sides."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The ledge shall be fourteen cubits long by fourteen wide in its four sides; and the border about it shall be half a cubit; and its bottom shall be a cubit around; and its steps shall look toward the east.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, the Lord GOD says: \u2018These are the ordinances of the altar in the day when they make it, to offer burnt offerings on it, and to sprinkle blood on it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You shall give to the Levitical priests who are of the offspring of Zadok, who are near to me, to minister to me,\u2019 says the Lord GOD, \u2018a young bull for a sin offering."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You shall take of its blood and put it on its four horns, and on the four corners of the ledge, and on the border all around. You shall cleanse it and make atonement for it that way."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You shall also take the bull of the sin offering, and it shall be burned in the appointed place of the house, outside of the sanctuary."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOn the second day you shall offer a male goat without defect for a sin offering; and they shall cleanse the altar, as they cleansed it with the bull."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When you have finished cleansing it, you shall offer a young bull without defect and a ram out of the flock without defect."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You shall bring them near to the LORD, and the priests shall cast salt on them, and they shall offer them up for a burnt offering to the LORD."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSeven days you shall prepare every day a goat for a sin offering. They shall also prepare a young bull and a ram out of the flock, without defect."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Seven days shall they make atonement for the altar and purify it. So shall they consecrate it."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When they have accomplished the days, it shall be that on the eighth day and onward, the priests shall make your burnt offerings on the altar and your peace offerings. Then I will accept you,\u2019 says the Lord GOD.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me back by the way of the outer gate of the sanctuary, which looks toward the east; and it was shut."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cThis gate shall be shut. It shall not be opened, no man shall enter in by it; for the LORD, the God of Israel, has entered in by it. Therefore it shall be shut."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"As for the prince, he shall sit in it as prince to eat bread before the LORD. He shall enter by the way of the porch of the gate, and shall go out the same way.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me by the way of the north gate before the house; and I looked, and behold, the LORD\u2019s glory filled the LORD\u2019s house; so I fell on my face."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cSon of man, mark well, and see with your eyes, and hear with your ears all that I tell you concerning all the ordinances of the LORD\u2019s house and all its laws; and mark well the entrance of the house, with every exit of the sanctuary."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You shall tell the rebellious, even the house of Israel, \u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cYou house of Israel, let that be enough of all your abominations,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"in that you have brought in foreigners, uncircumcised in heart and uncircumcised in flesh, to be in my sanctuary, to profane it, even my house, when you offer my bread, the fat and the blood; and they have broken my covenant, to add to all your abominations."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You have not performed the duty of my holy things; but you have set performers of my duty in my sanctuary for yourselves.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The Lord GOD says, \u201cNo foreigner, uncircumcised in heart and uncircumcised in flesh, shall enter into my sanctuary, of any foreigners who are among the children of Israel."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut the Levites who went far from me when Israel went astray, who went astray from me after their idols, they will bear their iniquity."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Yet they shall be ministers in my sanctuary, having oversight at the gates of the house, and ministering in the house. They shall kill the burnt offering and the sacrifice for the people, and they shall stand before them to minister to them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Because they ministered to them before their idols, and became a stumbling block of iniquity to the house of Israel, therefore I have lifted up my hand against them,\u201d says the Lord GOD, \u201cand they will bear their iniquity."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They shall not come near to me, to execute the office of priest to me, nor to come near to any of my holy things, to the things that are most holy; but they will bear their shame and their abominations which they have committed."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Yet I will make them performers of the duty of the house, for all its service and for all that will be done therein."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut the Levitical priests, the sons of Zadok, who performed the duty of my sanctuary when the children of Israel went astray from me, shall come near to me to minister to me. They shall stand before me to offer to me the fat and the blood,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cThey shall enter into my sanctuary, and they shall come near to my table, to minister to me, and they shall keep my instruction."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIt will be that when they enter in at the gates of the inner court, they shall be clothed with linen garments. No wool shall come on them while they minister in the gates of the inner court, and within."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They shall have linen turbans on their heads, and shall have linen trousers on their waists. They shall not clothe themselves with anything that makes them sweat."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When they go out into the outer court, even into the outer court to the people, they shall put off their garments in which they minister and lay them in the holy rooms. They shall put on other garments, that they not sanctify the people with their garments."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThey shall not shave their heads, or allow their locks to grow long. They shall only cut off the hair of their heads."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"None of the priests shall drink wine when they enter into the inner court."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They shall not take for their wives a widow, or her who is put away; but they shall take virgins of the offspring of the house of Israel, or a widow who is the widow of a priest."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They shall teach my people the difference between the holy and the common, and cause them to discern between the unclean and the clean."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIn a controversy they shall stand to judge. They shall judge it according to my ordinances. They shall keep my laws and my statutes in all my appointed feasts. They shall make my Sabbaths holy."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThey shall go in to no dead person to defile themselves; but for father, or for mother, or for son, or for daughter, for brother, or for sister who has had no husband, they may defile themselves."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"After he is cleansed, they shall reckon to him seven days."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"In the day that he goes into the sanctuary, into the inner court, to minister in the sanctuary, he shall offer his sin offering,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018They shall have an inheritance: I am their inheritance; and you shall give them no possession in Israel. I am their possession."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They shall eat the meal offering, and the sin offering, and the trespass offering; and every devoted thing in Israel shall be theirs."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The first of all the first fruits of every thing, and every offering of everything, of all your offerings, shall be for the priest. You shall also give to the priests the first of your dough, to cause a blessing to rest on your house."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The priests shall not eat of anything that dies of itself or is torn, whether it is bird or animal."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cMoreover, when you divide by lot the land for inheritance, you shall offer an offering to the LORD, a holy portion of the land. The length shall be the length of twenty-five thousand reeds, and the width shall be ten thousand. It shall be holy in all its border all around."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Of this there shall be a five hundred by five hundred square for the holy place, and fifty cubits for its pasture lands all around."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Of this measure you shall measure a length of twenty-five thousand, and a width of ten thousand. In it shall be the sanctuary, which is most holy."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"It is a holy portion of the land; it shall be for the priests, the ministers of the sanctuary, who come near to minister to the LORD. It shall be a place for their houses and a holy place for the sanctuary."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Twenty-five thousand cubits in length and ten thousand in width shall be for the Levites, the ministers of the house, as a possession for themselves, for twenty rooms."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cYou shall appoint the possession of the city five thousand cubits wide and twenty-five thousand long, side by side with the offering of the holy portion. It shall be for the whole house of Israel."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cWhat is for the prince shall be on the one side and on the other side of the holy allotment and of the possession of the city, in front of the holy allotment and in front of the possession of the city, on the west side westward, and on the east side eastward, and in length corresponding to one of the portions, from the west border to the east border."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"In the land it shall be to him for a possession in Israel. My princes shall no more oppress my people, but they shall give the land to the house of Israel according to their tribes.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cEnough, you princes of Israel! Remove violence and plunder, and execute justice and righteousness! Stop dispossessing my people!\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cYou shall have just balances, a just ephah, and a just bath."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The ephah and the bath shall be of one measure, that the bath may contain one tenth of a homer, and the ephah one tenth of a homer. Its measure shall be the same as the homer."]],f:["1 homer is about 220 liters or 6 bushels"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The shekel shall be twenty gerahs. Twenty shekels plus twenty-five shekels plus fifteen shekels shall be your mina."]],f:["A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces.","a gerah is about 0.5 grams or about 7.7 grains","A mina is about 600 grams or 1.3 U. S. pounds."]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cThis is the offering that you shall offer: the sixth part of an ephah from a homer of wheat, and you shall give the sixth part of an ephah from a homer of barley,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and the set portion of oil, of the bath of oil, one tenth of a bath out of the cor, which is ten baths, even a homer (for ten baths are a homer),"]],f:["1 cor is the same as 1 homer in volume, and is about 211 liters, 55.9 gallons, or 6 bushels. 1 bath is about 21.1 liters, 5.59 gallons, or 2.4 pecks."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and one lamb of the flock out of two hundred, from the well-watered pastures of Israel\u2014for a meal offering, for a burnt offering, and for peace offerings, to make atonement for them,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cAll the people of the land shall give to this offering for the prince in Israel."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It shall be the prince\u2019s part to give the burnt offerings, the meal offerings, and the drink offerings, in the feasts, and on the new moons, and on the Sabbaths, in all the appointed feasts of the house of Israel. He shall prepare the sin offering, the meal offering, the burnt offering, and the peace offerings, to make atonement for the house of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cIn the first month, on the first day of the month, you shall take a young bull without defect, and you shall cleanse the sanctuary."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The priest shall take of the blood of the sin offering and put it on the door posts of the house, and on the four corners of the ledge of the altar, and on the posts of the gate of the inner court."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"So you shall do on the seventh day of the month for everyone who errs, and for him who is simple. So you shall make atonement for the house."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIn the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month, you shall have the Passover, a feast of seven days; unleavened bread shall be eaten."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"On that day the prince shall prepare for himself and for all the people of the land a bull for a sin offering."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The seven days of the feast he shall prepare a burnt offering to the LORD, seven bulls and seven rams without defect daily the seven days; and a male goat daily for a sin offering."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He shall prepare a meal offering, an ephah for a bull, an ephah for a ram, and a hin of oil to an ephah."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons."]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIn the seventh month, on the fifteenth day of the month, during the feast, he shall do like that for seven days. He shall make the same provision for sin offering, the burnt offering, the meal offering, and the oil.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cThe gate of the inner court that looks toward the east shall be shut the six working days; but on the Sabbath day it shall be opened, and on the day of the new moon it shall be opened."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The prince shall enter by the way of the porch of the gate outside, and shall stand by the post of the gate; and the priests shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, and he shall worship at the threshold of the gate. Then he shall go out, but the gate shall not be shut until the evening."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The people of the land shall worship at the door of that gate before the LORD on the Sabbaths and on the new moons."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The burnt offering that the prince shall offer to the LORD shall be on the Sabbath day, six lambs without defect and a ram without defect;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and the meal offering shall be an ephah for the ram, and the meal offering for the lambs as he is able to give, and a hin of oil to an ephah."]],f:["A hin is about 6.5 liters or 1.7 gallons.","1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"On the day of the new moon it shall be a young bull without defect, six lambs, and a ram. They shall be without defect."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He shall prepare a meal offering: an ephah for the bull, and an ephah for the ram, and for the lambs according as he is able, and a hin of oil to an ephah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When the prince enters, he shall go in by the way of the porch of the gate, and he shall go out by its way."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cBut when the people of the land come before the LORD in the appointed feasts, he who enters by the way of the north gate to worship shall go out by the way of the south gate; and he who enters by the way of the south gate shall go out by the way of the north gate. He shall not return by the way of the gate by which he came in, but shall go out straight before him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The prince shall go in with them when they go in. When they go out, he shall go out."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cIn the feasts and in the appointed holidays, the meal offering shall be an ephah for a bull, and an ephah for a ram, and for the lambs as he is able to give, and a hin of oil to an ephah."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When the prince prepares a free will offering, a burnt offering or peace offerings as a free will offering to the LORD, one shall open for him the gate that looks toward the east; and he shall prepare his burnt offering and his peace offerings, as he does on the Sabbath day. Then he shall go out; and after his going out one shall shut the gate."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018\u201cYou shall prepare a lamb a year old without defect for a burnt offering to the LORD daily. Morning by morning you shall prepare it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall prepare a meal offering with it morning by morning, the sixth part of an ephah, and the third part of a hin of oil to moisten the fine flour; a meal offering to the LORD continually by a perpetual ordinance."]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Thus they shall prepare the lamb, the meal offering, and the oil, morning by morning, for a continual burnt offering.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018The Lord GOD says: \u201cIf the prince gives a gift to any of his sons, it is his inheritance. It shall belong to his sons. It is their possession by inheritance."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But if he gives of his inheritance a gift to one of his servants, it shall be his to the year of liberty; then it shall return to the prince; but as for his inheritance, it shall be for his sons."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Moreover the prince shall not take of the people\u2019s inheritance, to thrust them out of their possession. He shall give inheritance to his sons out of his own possession, that my people not each be scattered from his possession.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me through the entry, which was at the side of the gate, into the holy rooms for the priests, which looked toward the north. Behold, there was a place on the back part westward."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cThis is the place where the priests shall boil the trespass offering and the sin offering, and where they shall bake the meal offering, that they not bring them out into the outer court, to sanctify the people.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he brought me out into the outer court and caused me to pass by the four corners of the court; and behold, in every corner of the court there was a court."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"In the four corners of the court there were courts enclosed, forty cubits long and thirty wide. These four in the corners were the same size."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:23,l:[[0,"There was a wall around in them, around the four, and boiling places were made under the walls all around."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cThese are the boiling houses, where the ministers of the house shall boil the sacrifice of the people.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He brought me back to the door of the temple; and behold, waters flowed out from under the threshold of the temple eastward, for the front of the temple faced toward the east. The waters came down from underneath, from the right side of the temple, on the south of the altar."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then he brought me out by the way of the gate northward, and led me around by the way outside to the outer gate, by the way of the gate that looks toward the east. Behold, waters ran out on the right side."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"When the man went out eastward with the line in his hand, he measured one thousand cubits, and he caused me to pass through the waters, waters that were to the ankles."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Again he measured one thousand, and caused me to pass through the waters, waters that were to the knees. Again he measured one thousand, and caused me to pass through waters that were to the waist."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Afterward he measured one thousand; and it was a river that I could not pass through, for the waters had risen, waters to swim in, a river that could not be walked through."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cSon of man, have you seen this?\u201d"],[0,"Then he brought me and caused me to return to the bank of the river."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now when I had returned, behold, on the bank of the river were very many trees on the one side and on the other."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cThese waters flow out toward the eastern region and will go down into the Arabah. Then they will go toward the sea and flow into the sea which will be made to flow out; and the waters will be healed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It will happen that every living creature which swarms, in every place where the rivers come, will live. Then there will be a very great multitude of fish; for these waters have come there, and the waters of the sea will be healed, and everything will live wherever the river comes."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"It will happen that fishermen will stand by it. From En Gedi even to En Eglaim will be a place for the spreading of nets. Their fish will be after their kinds, as the fish of the great sea, exceedingly many."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But its swamps and marshes will not be healed. They will be given up to salt."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"By the river banks, on both sides, will grow every tree for food, whose leaf won\u2019t wither, neither will its fruit fail. It will produce new fruit every month, because its waters issue out of the sanctuary. Its fruit will be for food, and its leaf for healing.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord GOD says: \u201cThis shall be the border by which you shall divide the land for inheritance according to the twelve tribes of Israel. Joseph shall have two portions."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You shall inherit it, one as well as another; for I swore to give it to your fathers. This land will fall to you for inheritance."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis shall be the border of the land:"],[0,"\u201cOn the north side, from the great sea, by the way of Hethlon, to the entrance of Zedad;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Hamath, Berothah, Sibraim (which is between the border of Damascus and the border of Hamath), to Hazer Hatticon, which is by the border of Hauran."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The border from the sea shall be Hazar Enon at the border of Damascus; and on the north northward is the border of Hamath. This is the north side."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe east side, between Hauran, Damascus, Gilead, and the land of Israel, shall be the Jordan; from the north border to the east sea you shall measure. This is the east side."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe south side southward shall be from Tamar as far as the waters of Meriboth Kadesh, to the brook, to the great sea. This is the south side southward."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe west side shall be the great sea, from the south border as far as opposite the entrance of Hamath. This is the west side."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo you shall divide this land to yourselves according to the tribes of Israel."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You shall divide it by lot for an inheritance to you and to the aliens who live among you, who will father children among you. Then they shall be to you as the native-born among the children of Israel. They shall have inheritance with you among the tribes of Israel."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"In whatever tribe the stranger lives, there you shall give him his inheritance,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow these are the names of the tribes: From the north end, beside the way of Hethlon to the entrance of Hamath, Hazar Enan at the border of Damascus, northward beside Hamath (and they shall have their sides east and west), Dan, one portion."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Dan, from the east side to the west side, Asher, one portion."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Asher, from the east side even to the west side, Naphtali, one portion."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Naphtali, from the east side to the west side, Manasseh, one portion."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Manasseh, from the east side to the west side, Ephraim, one portion."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Ephraim, from the east side even to the west side, Reuben, one portion."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Reuben, from the east side to the west side, Judah, one portion."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Judah, from the east side to the west side, shall be the offering which you shall offer, twenty-five thousand reeds in width, and in length as one of the portions, from the east side to the west side; and the sanctuary shall be in the middle of it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe offering that you shall offer to the LORD shall be twenty-five thousand reeds in length, and ten thousand in width."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For these, even for the priests, shall be the holy offering: toward the north twenty-five thousand in length, and toward the west ten thousand in width, and toward the east ten thousand in width, and toward the south twenty-five thousand in length; and the sanctuary of the LORD shall be in the middle of it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"It shall be for the priests who are sanctified of the sons of Zadok, who have kept my instruction, who didn\u2019t go astray when the children of Israel went astray, as the Levites went astray."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It shall be to them an offering from the offering of the land, a most holy thing, by the border of the Levites."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAlongside the border of the priests, the Levites shall have twenty-five thousand cubits in length and ten thousand in width. All the length shall be twenty-five thousand, and the width ten thousand."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They shall sell none of it, nor exchange it, nor shall the first fruits of the land be alienated, for it is holy to the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe five thousand cubits that are left in the width, in front of the twenty-five thousand, shall be for common use, for the city, for dwelling and for pasture lands; and the city shall be in the middle of it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"These shall be its measurements: the north side four thousand and five hundred, and the south side four thousand and five hundred, and on the east side four thousand and five hundred, and the west side four thousand and five hundred."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The city shall have pasture lands: toward the north two hundred fifty, and toward the south two hundred fifty, and toward the east two hundred fifty, and toward the west two hundred fifty."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The remainder of the length, alongside the holy offering, shall be ten thousand eastward and ten thousand westward; and it shall be alongside the holy offering. Its increase shall be for food to those who labor in the city."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Those who labor in the city, out of all the tribes of Israel, shall cultivate it."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"All the offering shall be a square of twenty-five thousand by twenty-five thousand. You shall offer it as a holy offering, with the possession of the city."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe remainder shall be for the prince, on the one side and on the other of the holy offering and of the possession of the city; in front of the twenty-five thousand of the offering toward the east border, and westward in front of the twenty-five thousand toward the west border, alongside the portions, it shall be for the prince. The holy offering and the sanctuary of the house shall be in the middle of it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Moreover, from the possession of the Levites, and from the possession of the city, being in the middle of that which is the prince\u2019s, between the border of Judah and the border of Benjamin, shall be for the prince."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for the rest of the tribes: from the east side to the west side, Benjamin, one portion."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Benjamin, from the east side to the west side, Simeon, one portion."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Simeon, from the east side to the west side, Issachar, one portion."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Issachar, from the east side to the west side, Zebulun, one portion."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Zebulun, from the east side to the west side, Gad, one portion."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy the border of Gad, at the south side southward, the border shall be even from Tamar to the waters of Meribath Kadesh, to the brook, to the great sea."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the land which you shall divide by lot to the tribes of Israel for inheritance, and these are their several portions, says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThese are the exits of the city: On the north side four thousand five hundred reeds by measure;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and the gates of the city shall be named after the tribes of Israel, three gates northward: the gate of Reuben, one; the gate of Judah, one; the gate of Levi, one."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAt the east side four thousand five hundred reeds, and three gates: even the gate of Joseph, one; the gate of Benjamin, one; the gate of Dan, one."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAt the south side four thousand five hundred reeds by measure, and three gates: the gate of Simeon, one; the gate of Issachar, one; the gate of Zebulun, one."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAt the west side four thousand five hundred reeds, with their three gates: the gate of Gad, one; the gate of Asher, one; the gate of Naphtali, one."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt shall be eighteen thousand reeds in circumference; and the name of the city from that day shall be, \u2018The LORD is there.\u2019"]]}]]}},1297,[]);
__d(function(e,t,n,a,o,h,i){o.exports={book:"Dan",name:"Daniel",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the third year of the reign of Jehoiakim king of Judah, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon came to Jerusalem and besieged it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Lord gave Jehoiakim king of Judah into his hand, with some of the vessels of the house of God; and he carried them into the land of Shinar to the house of his god. He brought the vessels into the treasure house of his god."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d","The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The king spoke to Ashpenaz, the master of his eunuchs, that he should bring in some of the children of Israel, even of the royal offspring and of the nobles:"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"youths in whom was no defect, but well-favored, skillful in all wisdom, endowed with knowledge, understanding science, and who had the ability to stand in the king\u2019s palace; and that he should teach them the learning and the language of the Chaldeans."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The king appointed for them a daily portion of the king\u2019s delicacies and of the wine which he drank, and that they should be nourished three years, that at its end they should stand before the king."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now among these of the children of Judah were Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The prince of the eunuchs gave names to them: to Daniel he gave the name Belteshazzar; to Hananiah, Shadrach; to Mishael, Meshach; and to Azariah, Abednego."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"But Daniel purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself with the king\u2019s delicacies, nor with the wine which he drank. Therefore he requested of the prince of the eunuchs that he might not defile himself."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now God made Daniel find kindness and compassion in the sight of the prince of the eunuchs."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The prince of the eunuchs said to Daniel, \u201cI fear my lord the king, who has appointed your food and your drink. For why should he see your faces worse looking than the youths who are of your own age? Then you would endanger my head with the king.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Daniel said to the steward whom the prince of the eunuchs had appointed over Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah:"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cTest your servants, I beg you, ten days; and let them give us vegetables to eat and water to drink."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then let our faces be examined before you, and the face of the youths who eat of the king\u2019s delicacies; and as you see, deal with your servants.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So he listened to them in this matter, and tested them for ten days."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of ten days, their faces appeared fairer and they were fatter in flesh than all the youths who ate of the king\u2019s delicacies."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So the steward took away their delicacies and the wine that they were given to drink, and gave them vegetables."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now as for these four youths, God gave them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom; and Daniel had understanding in all visions and dreams."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"At the end of the days which the king had appointed for bringing them in, the prince of the eunuchs brought them in before Nebuchadnezzar."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The king talked with them; and among them all was found no one like Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah. Therefore they stood before the king."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"In every matter of wisdom and understanding concerning which the king inquired of them, he found them ten times better than all the magicians and enchanters who were in all his realm."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Daniel continued even to the first year of King Cyrus."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the second year of the reign of Nebuchadnezzar, Nebuchadnezzar dreamed dreams; and his spirit was troubled, and his sleep went from him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then the king commanded that the magicians, the enchanters, the sorcerers, and the Chaldeans be called to tell the king his dreams. So they came in and stood before the king."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The king said to them, \u201cI have dreamed a dream, and my spirit is troubled to know the dream.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Chaldeans spoke to the king in the Syrian language, \u201cO king, live forever! Tell your servants the dream, and we will show the interpretation.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The king answered the Chaldeans, \u201cThe thing has gone from me. If you don\u2019t make known to me the dream and its interpretation, you will be cut in pieces, and your houses will be made a dunghill."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But if you show the dream and its interpretation, you will receive from me gifts, rewards, and great honor. Therefore show me the dream and its interpretation.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered the second time and said, \u201cLet the king tell his servants the dream, and we will show the interpretation.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The king answered, \u201cI know of a certainty that you are trying to gain time, because you see the thing has gone from me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But if you don\u2019t make known to me the dream, there is but one law for you; for you have prepared lying and corrupt words to speak before me, until the situation changes. Therefore tell me the dream, and I will know that you can show me its interpretation.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The Chaldeans answered the king and said, \u201cThere is not a man on the earth who can show the king\u2019s matter, because no king, lord, or ruler has asked such a thing of any magician, enchanter, or Chaldean."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"It is a rare thing that the king requires, and there is no other who can show it before the king except the gods, whose dwelling is not with flesh.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Because of this, the king was angry and very furious, and commanded that all the wise men of Babylon be destroyed."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So the decree went out, and the wise men were to be slain. They sought Daniel and his companions to be slain."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Daniel returned answer with counsel and prudence to Arioch the captain of the king\u2019s guard, who had gone out to kill the wise men of Babylon."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He answered Arioch the king\u2019s captain, \u201cWhy is the decree so urgent from the king?\u201d Then Arioch made the thing known to Daniel."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Daniel went in, and desired of the king that he would appoint him a time, and he would show the king the interpretation."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Daniel went to his house and made the thing known to Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, his companions:"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"that they would desire mercies of the God of heaven concerning this secret, that Daniel and his companions would not perish with the rest of the wise men of Babylon."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Then the secret was revealed to Daniel in a vision of the night. Then Daniel blessed the God of heaven."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Daniel answered,"],[1,"\u201cBlessed be the name of God forever and ever;"],[2,"for wisdom and might are his."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"He changes the times and the seasons."],[2,"He removes kings and sets up kings."],[1,"He gives wisdom to the wise,"],[2,"and knowledge to those who have understanding."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"He reveals the deep and secret things."],[2,"He knows what is in the darkness,"],[2,"and the light dwells with him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I thank you and praise you,"],[2,"O God of my fathers,"],[1,"who have given me wisdom and might,"],[2,"and have now made known to me what we desired of you;"],[2,"for you have made known to us the king\u2019s matter.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Daniel went in to Arioch, whom the king had appointed to destroy the wise men of Babylon. He went and said this to him: \u201cDon\u2019t destroy the wise men of Babylon. Bring me in before the king, and I will show to the king the interpretation.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Arioch brought in Daniel before the king in haste, and said this to him: \u201cI have found a man of the children of the captivity of Judah who will make known to the king the interpretation.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The king answered Daniel, whose name was Belteshazzar, \u201cAre you able to make known to me the dream which I have seen, and its interpretation?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Daniel answered before the king, and said, \u201cThe secret which the king has demanded can\u2019t be shown to the king by wise men, enchanters, magicians, or soothsayers;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"but there is a God in heaven who reveals secrets, and he has made known to King Nebuchadnezzar what will be in the latter days. Your dream and the visions of your head on your bed are these:"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for you, O king, your thoughts came on your bed, what should happen hereafter; and he who reveals secrets has made known to you what will happen."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But as for me, this secret is not revealed to me for any wisdom that I have more than any living, but to the intent that the interpretation may be made known to the king, and that you may know the thoughts of your heart."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, O king, saw, and behold, a great image. This image, which was mighty, and whose brightness was excellent, stood before you; and its appearance was terrifying."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:32,l:[[0,"As for this image, its head was of fine gold, its chest and its arms of silver, its belly and its thighs of bronze,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"its legs of iron, its feet part of iron and part of clay."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"You saw until a stone was cut out without hands, which struck the image on its feet that were of iron and clay, and broke them in pieces."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Then the iron, the clay, the bronze, the silver, and the gold were broken in pieces together, and became like the chaff of the summer threshing floors. The wind carried them away, so that no place was found for them. The stone that struck the image became a great mountain and filled the whole earth."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the dream; and we will tell its interpretation before the king."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"You, O king, are king of kings, to whom the God of heaven has given the kingdom, the power, the strength, and the glory."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Wherever the children of men dwell, he has given the animals of the field and the birds of the sky into your hand, and has made you rule over them all. You are the head of gold."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAfter you, another kingdom will arise that is inferior to you; and another third kingdom of bronze, which will rule over all the earth."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The fourth kingdom will be strong as iron, because iron breaks in pieces and subdues all things; and as iron that crushes all these, it will break in pieces and crush."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Whereas you saw the feet and toes, part of potters\u2019 clay and part of iron, it will be a divided kingdom; but there will be in it of the strength of the iron, because you saw the iron mixed with miry clay."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"As the toes of the feet were part of iron, and part of clay, so the kingdom will be partly strong and partly brittle."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Whereas you saw the iron mixed with miry clay, they will mingle themselves with the seed of men; but they won\u2019t cling to one another, even as iron does not mix with clay."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn the days of those kings the God of heaven will set up a kingdom which will never be destroyed, nor will its sovereignty be left to another people; but it will break in pieces and consume all these kingdoms, and it will stand forever."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Because you saw that a stone was cut out of the mountain without hands, and that it broke in pieces the iron, the bronze, the clay, the silver, and the gold, the great God has made known to the king what will happen hereafter. The dream is certain, and its interpretation sure.\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"Then King Nebuchadnezzar fell on his face, worshiped Daniel, and commanded that they should offer an offering and sweet odors to him."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"The king answered to Daniel, and said, \u201cOf a truth your God is the God of gods, and the Lord of kings, and a revealer of secrets, since you have been able to reveal this secret.\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king made Daniel great and gave him many great gifts, and made him rule over the whole province of Babylon and to be chief governor over all the wise men of Babylon."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Daniel requested of the king, and he appointed Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego over the affairs of the province of Babylon, but Daniel was in the king\u2019s gate."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Nebuchadnezzar the king made an image of gold, whose height was sixty cubits and its width six cubits. He set it up in the plain of Dura, in the province of Babylon."]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then Nebuchadnezzar the king sent to gather together the local governors, the deputies, and the governors, the judges, the treasurers, the counselors, the sheriffs, and all the rulers of the provinces, to come to the dedication of the image which Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then the local governors, the deputies, and the governors, the judges, the treasurers, the counselors, the sheriffs, and all the rulers of the provinces were gathered together to the dedication of the image that Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up; and they stood before the image that Nebuchadnezzar had set up."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the herald cried aloud, \u201cTo you it is commanded, peoples, nations, and languages,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"that whenever you hear the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, pipe, and all kinds of music, you fall down and worship the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king has set up."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Whoever doesn\u2019t fall down and worship shall be cast into the middle of a burning fiery furnace the same hour.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore at that time, when all the peoples heard the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, pipe, and all kinds of music, all the peoples, the nations, and the languages fell down and worshiped the golden image that Nebuchadnezzar the king had set up."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore at that time certain Chaldeans came near and brought accusation against the Jews."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They answered Nebuchadnezzar the king, \u201cO king, live for ever!"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You, O king, have made a decree that every man who hears the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, pipe, and all kinds of music shall fall down and worship the golden image;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and whoever doesn\u2019t fall down and worship shall be cast into the middle of a burning fiery furnace."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"There are certain Jews whom you have appointed over the affairs of the province of Babylon: Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego. These men, O king, have not respected you. They don\u2019t serve your gods, and don\u2019t worship the golden image which you have set up.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Nebuchadnezzar in rage and fury commanded that Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego be brought. Then these men were brought before the king."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Nebuchadnezzar answered them, \u201cIs it true, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, that you don\u2019t serve my gods and you don\u2019t worship the golden image which I have set up?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now if you are ready whenever you hear the sound of the horn, flute, zither, lyre, harp, pipe, and all kinds of music to fall down and worship the image which I have made, good; but if you don\u2019t worship, you shall be cast the same hour into the middle of a burning fiery furnace. Who is that god who will deliver you out of my hands?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego answered the king, \u201cNebuchadnezzar, we have no need to answer you in this matter."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If it happens, our God whom we serve is able to deliver us from the burning fiery furnace; and he will deliver us out of your hand, O king."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But if not, let it be known to you, O king, that we will not serve your gods or worship the golden image which you have set up.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Nebuchadnezzar was full of fury, and the form of his appearance was changed against Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego. He spoke, and commanded that they should heat the furnace seven times more than it was usually heated."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He commanded certain mighty men who were in his army to bind Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, and to cast them into the burning fiery furnace."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then these men were bound in their pants, their tunics, and their mantles, and their other clothes, and were cast into the middle of the burning fiery furnace."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Therefore because the king\u2019s commandment was urgent and the furnace exceedingly hot, the flame of the fire killed those men who took up Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"These three men, Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, fell down bound into the middle of the burning fiery furnace."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Nebuchadnezzar the king was astonished and rose up in haste. He spoke and said to his counselors, \u201cDidn\u2019t we cast three men bound into the middle of the fire?\u201d"],[0,"They answered the king, \u201cTrue, O king.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cLook, I see four men loose, walking in the middle of the fire, and they are unharmed. The appearance of the fourth is like a son of the gods.\u201d"]],f:["Or, the Son of God."]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Nebuchadnezzar came near to the mouth of the burning fiery furnace. He spoke and said, \u201cShadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, you servants of the Most High God, come out, and come here!\u201d"],[0,"Then Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego came out of the middle of the fire."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The local governors, the deputies, and the governors, and the king\u2019s counselors, being gathered together, saw these men, that the fire had no power on their bodies. The hair of their head wasn\u2019t singed. Their pants weren\u2019t changed. The smell of fire wasn\u2019t even on them."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Nebuchadnezzar spoke and said, \u201cBlessed be the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego, who has sent his angel and delivered his servants who trusted in him, and have changed the king\u2019s word, and have yielded their bodies, that they might not serve nor worship any god except their own God."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Therefore I make a decree that every people, nation, and language which speak anything evil against the God of Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego shall be cut in pieces, and their houses shall be made a dunghill, because there is no other god who is able to deliver like this.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king promoted Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego in the province of Babylon."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Nebuchadnezzar the king,"],[1,"to all the peoples, nations, and languages, who dwell in all the earth:"],[1,"Peace be multiplied to you."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"It has seemed good to me to show the signs and wonders that the Most High God has worked toward me."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"How great are his signs!"],[2,"How mighty are his wonders!"],[1,"His kingdom is an everlasting kingdom."],[2,"His dominion is from generation to generation."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I, Nebuchadnezzar, was at rest in my house, and flourishing in my palace."]]},{v:5,l:[[1,"I saw a dream which made me afraid; and the thoughts on my bed and the visions of my head troubled me."]]},{v:6,l:[[1,"Therefore I made a decree to bring in all the wise men of Babylon before me, that they might make known to me the interpretation of the dream."]]},{v:7,l:[[1,"Then the magicians, the enchanters, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers came in; and I told them the dream, but they didn\u2019t make known to me its interpretation."]]},{v:8,l:[[1,"But at last, Daniel came in before me, whose name was Belteshazzar according to the name of my god, and in whom is the spirit of the holy gods. I told the dream before him, saying,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBelteshazzar, master of the magicians, because I know that the spirit of the holy gods is in you and no secret troubles you, tell me the visions of my dream that I have seen, and its interpretation."]]},{v:10,l:[[1,"These were the visions of my head on my bed: I saw, and behold, a tree in the middle of the earth; and its height was great."]]},{v:11,l:[[1,"The tree grew and was strong. Its height reached to the sky and its sight to the end of all the earth."]]},{v:12,l:[[1,"Its leaves were beautiful, and it had much fruit, and in it was food for all. The animals of the field had shade under it, and the birds of the sky lived in its branches, and all flesh was fed from it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI saw in the visions of my head on my bed, and behold, a holy watcher came down from the sky."]]},{v:14,l:[[1,"He cried aloud and said this: \u2018Cut down the tree, and cut off its branches! Shake off its leaves and scatter its fruit! Let the animals get away from under it and the birds from its branches."]]},{v:15,l:[[1,"Nevertheless leave the stump of its roots in the earth, even with a band of iron and bronze, in the tender grass of the field; and let it be wet with the dew of the sky. Let his portion be with the animals in the grass of the earth."]]},{v:16,l:[[1,"Let his heart be changed from man\u2019s, and let an animal\u2019s heart be given to him. Then let seven times pass over him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201c\u2018The sentence is by the decree of the watchers and the demand by the word of the holy ones, to the intent that the living may know that the Most High rules in the kingdom of men, and gives it to whomever he will, and sets up over it the lowest of men.\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThis dream I, King Nebuchadnezzar, have seen; and you, Belteshazzar, declare the interpretation, because all the wise men of my kingdom are not able to make known to me the interpretation; but you are able, for the spirit of the holy gods is in you.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Then Daniel, whose name was Belteshazzar, was stricken mute for a while, and his thoughts troubled him. The king answered, \u201cBelteshazzar, don\u2019t let the dream or the interpretation trouble you.\u201d"],[1,"Belteshazzar answered, \u201cMy lord, may the dream be for those who hate you, and its interpretation to your adversaries."]]},{v:20,l:[[1,"The tree that you saw, which grew and was strong, whose height reached to the sky and its sight to all the earth;"]]},{v:21,l:[[1,"whose leaves were beautiful and its fruit plentiful, and in it was food for all; under which the animals of the field lived, and on whose branches the birds of the sky had their habitation\u2014"]]},{v:22,l:[[1,"it is you, O king, that have grown and become strong; for your greatness has grown, and reaches to the sky, and your dominion to the end of the earth."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhereas the king saw a holy watcher coming down from the sky and saying, \u2018Cut down the tree, and destroy it; nevertheless leave the stump of its roots in the earth, even with a band of iron and bronze, in the tender grass of the field, and let it be wet with the dew of the sky. Let his portion be with the animals of the field, until seven times pass over him.\u2019"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThis is the interpretation, O king, and it is the decree of the Most High, which has come on my lord the king:"]]},{v:25,l:[[1,"You will be driven from men and your dwelling shall be with the animals of the field. You will be made to eat grass as oxen, and will be wet with the dew of the sky, and seven times shall pass over you, until you know that the Most High rules in the kingdom of men, and gives it to whomever he will."]]},{v:26,l:[[1,"Whereas it was commanded to leave the stump of the roots of the tree, your kingdom will be restored to you after you learn that Heaven rules."]]},{v:27,l:[[1,"Therefore, O king, let my counsel be acceptable to you, and break off your sins by righteousness, and your iniquities by showing mercy to the poor. Perhaps there may be a lengthening of your tranquility.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"All this came on the King Nebuchadnezzar."]]},{v:29,l:[[1,"At the end of twelve months he was walking in the royal palace of Babylon."]]},{v:30,l:[[1,"The king spoke and said, \u201cIs not this great Babylon, which I have built for the royal dwelling place by the might of my power and for the glory of my majesty?\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"While the word was in the king\u2019s mouth, a voice came from the sky, saying, \u201cO King Nebuchadnezzar, to you it is spoken: \u2018The kingdom has departed from you."]]},{v:32,l:[[1,"You shall be driven from men, and your dwelling shall be with the animals of the field. You shall be made to eat grass like oxen. Seven times shall pass over you, until you know that the Most High rules in the kingdom of men, and gives it to whomever he will.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"This was fulfilled the same hour on Nebuchadnezzar. He was driven from men and ate grass like oxen; and his body was wet with the dew of the sky until his hair had grown like eagles\u2019 feathers, and his nails like birds\u2019 claws."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"At the end of the days I, Nebuchadnezzar, lifted up my eyes to heaven, and my understanding returned to me; and I blessed the Most High, and I praised and honored him who lives forever,"],[1,"for his dominion is an everlasting dominion,"],[2,"and his kingdom from generation to generation."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"All the inhabitants of the earth are reputed as nothing;"],[2,"and he does according to his will in the army of heaven,"],[2,"and among the inhabitants of the earth;"],[1,"and no one can stop his hand,"],[2,"or ask him, \u201cWhat are you doing?\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"At the same time my understanding returned to me; and for the glory of my kingdom, my majesty and brightness returned to me. My counselors and my lords sought me; and I was established in my kingdom, and excellent greatness was added to me."]]},{v:37,l:[[1,"Now I, Nebuchadnezzar, praise and extol and honor the King of heaven; for all his works are truth, and his ways justice; and those who walk in pride he is able to abase."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Belshazzar the king made a great feast to a thousand of his lords, and drank wine before the thousand."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Belshazzar, while he tasted the wine, commanded that the golden and silver vessels which Nebuchadnezzar his father had taken out of the temple which was in Jerusalem be brought to him, that the king and his lords, his wives and his concubines, might drink from them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then they brought the golden vessels that were taken out of the temple of God\u2019s house which was at Jerusalem; and the king and his lords, his wives and his concubines, drank from them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They drank wine, and praised the gods of gold, and of silver, of bronze, of iron, of wood, and of stone."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"In the same hour, the fingers of a man\u2019s hand came out and wrote near the lamp stand on the plaster of the wall of the king\u2019s palace. The king saw the part of the hand that wrote."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then the king\u2019s face was changed in him, and his thoughts troubled him; and the joints of his thighs were loosened, and his knees struck one against another."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The king cried aloud to bring in the enchanters, the Chaldeans, and the soothsayers. The king spoke and said to the wise men of Babylon, \u201cWhoever reads this writing and shows me its interpretation shall be clothed with purple, and have a chain of gold about his neck, and shall be the third ruler in the kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the king\u2019s wise men came in; but they could not read the writing, and couldn\u2019t make known to the king the interpretation."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then King Belshazzar was greatly troubled, and his face was changed in him, and his lords were perplexed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The queen by reason of the words of the king and his lords came into the banquet house. The queen spoke and said, \u201cO king, live forever; don\u2019t let your thoughts trouble you, nor let your face be changed."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"There is a man in your kingdom in whom is the spirit of the holy gods; and in the days of your father, light and understanding and wisdom, like the wisdom of the gods, were found in him. The king, Nebuchadnezzar, your father\u2014yes, the king, your father\u2014made him master of the magicians, enchanters, Chaldeans, and soothsayers,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"because an excellent spirit, knowledge, understanding, interpreting of dreams, showing of dark sentences, and dissolving of doubts were found in the same Daniel, whom the king named Belteshazzar. Now let Daniel be called, and he will show the interpretation.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Daniel was brought in before the king. The king spoke and said to Daniel, \u201cAre you that Daniel of the children of the captivity of Judah, whom the king my father brought out of Judah?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I have heard of you, that the spirit of the gods is in you and that light, understanding, and excellent wisdom are found in you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now the wise men, the enchanters, have been brought in before me, that they should read this writing, and make known to me its interpretation; but they could not show the interpretation of the thing."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But I have heard of you, that you can give interpretations and dissolve doubts. Now if you can read the writing and make known to me its interpretation, you shall be clothed with purple, and have a chain of gold around your neck, and shall be the third ruler in the kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Daniel answered before the king, \u201cLet your gifts be to yourself, and give your rewards to another. Nevertheless, I will read the writing to the king, and make known to him the interpretation."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo you, king, the Most High God gave Nebuchadnezzar your father the kingdom, and greatness, and glory, and majesty."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Because of the greatness that he gave him, all the peoples, nations, and languages trembled and feared before him. He killed whom he wanted to, and he kept alive whom he wanted to. He raised up whom he wanted to, and he put down whom he wanted to."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But when his heart was lifted up, and his spirit was hardened so that he dealt proudly, he was deposed from his kingly throne, and they took his glory from him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He was driven from the sons of men, and his heart was made like the animals\u2019, and his dwelling was with the wild donkeys. He was fed with grass like oxen, and his body was wet with the dew of the sky, until he knew that the Most High God rules in the kingdom of men, and that he sets up over it whomever he will."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou, his son, Belshazzar, have not humbled your heart, though you knew all this,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"but have lifted up yourself against the Lord of heaven; and they have brought the vessels of his house before you, and you and your lords, your wives, and your concubines, have drunk wine from them. You have praised the gods of silver and gold, of bronze, iron, wood, and stone, which don\u2019t see, or hear, or know; and you have not glorified the God in whose hand your breath is, and whose are all your ways."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then the part of the hand was sent from before him, and this writing was inscribed."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the writing that was inscribed: \u2018MENE, MENE, TEKEL, UPHARSIN.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is the interpretation of the thing:"],[0,"MENE: God has counted your kingdom, and brought it to an end."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"TEKEL: you are weighed in the balances, and are found wanting."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"PERES: your kingdom is divided, and given to the Medes and Persians.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Belshazzar commanded, and they clothed Daniel with purple, and put a chain of gold about his neck, and made proclamation concerning him, that he should be the third ruler in the kingdom."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"In that night Belshazzar the Chaldean King was slain."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Darius the Mede received the kingdom, being about sixty-two years old."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It pleased Darius to set over the kingdom one hundred twenty local governors, who should be throughout the whole kingdom;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and over them three presidents, of whom Daniel was one, that these local governors might give account to them, and that the king should suffer no loss."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then this Daniel was distinguished above the presidents and the local governors, because an excellent spirit was in him; and the king thought to set him over the whole realm."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the presidents and the local governors sought to find occasion against Daniel as touching the kingdom; but they could find no occasion or fault, because he was faithful. There wasn\u2019t any error or fault found in him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then these men said, \u201cWe won\u2019t find any occasion against this Daniel, unless we find it against him concerning the law of his God.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then these presidents and local governors assembled together to the king, and said this to him, \u201cKing Darius, live forever!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"All the presidents of the kingdom, the deputies and the local governors, the counselors and the governors, have consulted together to establish a royal statute and to make a strong decree, that whoever asks a petition of any god or man for thirty days, except of you, O king, he shall be cast into the den of lions."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now, O king, establish the decree and sign the writing, that it not be changed, according to the law of the Medes and Persians, which doesn\u2019t alter.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore King Darius signed the writing and the decree."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When Daniel knew that the writing was signed, he went into his house (now his windows were open in his room toward Jerusalem) and he kneeled on his knees three times a day, and prayed, and gave thanks before his God, as he did before."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then these men assembled together, and found Daniel making petition and supplication before his God."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Then they came near, and spoke before the king concerning the king\u2019s decree: \u201cHaven\u2019t you signed a decree that every man who makes a petition to any god or man within thirty days, except to you, O king, shall be cast into the den of lions?\u201d"],[0,"The king answered, \u201cThis thing is true, according to the law of the Medes and Persians, which doesn\u2019t alter.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they answered and said before the king, \u201cThat Daniel, who is of the children of the captivity of Judah, doesn\u2019t respect you, O king, nor the decree that you have signed, but makes his petition three times a day.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Then the king, when he heard these words, was very displeased, and set his heart on Daniel to deliver him; and he labored until the going down of the sun to rescue him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then these men assembled together to the king, and said to the king, \u201cKnow, O king, that it is a law of the Medes and Persians, that no decree nor statute which the king establishes may be changed.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king commanded, and they brought Daniel and cast him into the den of lions. The king spoke and said to Daniel, \u201cYour God whom you serve continually, he will deliver you.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"A stone was brought, and laid on the mouth of the den; and the king sealed it with his own signet, and with the signet of his lords; that nothing might be changed concerning Daniel."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then the king went to his palace, and passed the night fasting. No musical instruments were brought before him; and his sleep fled from him."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king arose very early in the morning, and went in haste to the den of lions."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When he came near to Daniel in the den, he cried with a troubled voice. The king spoke and said to Daniel, \u201cDaniel, servant of the living God, is your God, whom you serve continually, able to deliver you from the lions?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Daniel said to the king, \u201cO king, live forever!"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"My God has sent his angel, and has shut the lions\u2019 mouths, and they have not hurt me, because innocence was found in me before him; and also before you, O king, I have done no harm.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the king was exceedingly glad, and commanded that they should take Daniel up out of the den. So Daniel was taken up out of the den, and no kind of harm was found on him, because he had trusted in his God."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The king commanded, and they brought those men who had accused Daniel, and they cast them into the den of lions\u2014them, their children, and their wives; and the lions mauled them, and broke all their bones in pieces before they came to the bottom of the den."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then King Darius wrote to all the peoples, nations, and languages who dwell in all the earth:"],[1,"\u201cPeace be multiplied to you."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI make a decree that in all the dominion of my kingdom men tremble and fear before the God of Daniel."],[1,"\u201cFor he is the living God,"],[2,"and steadfast forever."],[1,"His kingdom is that which will not be destroyed."],[2,"His dominion will be even to the end."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"He delivers and rescues."],[2,"He works signs and wonders in heaven and in earth,"],[2,"who has delivered Daniel from the power of the lions.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"So this Daniel prospered in the reign of Darius and in the reign of Cyrus the Persian."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the first year of Belshazzar king of Babylon, Daniel had a dream and visions of his head while on his bed. Then he wrote the dream and told the sum of the matters."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Daniel spoke and said, \u201cI saw in my vision by night, and, behold, the four winds of the sky broke out on the great sea."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Four great animals came up from the sea, different from one another."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe first was like a lion, and had eagle\u2019s wings. I watched until its wings were plucked, and it was lifted up from the earth and made to stand on two feet as a man. A man\u2019s heart was given to it."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, there was another animal, a second, like a bear. It was raised up on one side, and three ribs were in its mouth between its teeth. They said this to it: \u2018Arise! Devour much flesh!\u2019"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAfter this I saw, and behold, another, like a leopard, which had on its back four wings of a bird. The animal also had four heads; and dominion was given to it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAfter this I saw in the night visions, and, behold, there was a fourth animal, awesome, powerful, and exceedingly strong. It had great iron teeth. It devoured and broke in pieces, and stamped the residue with its feet. It was different from all the animals that were before it. It had ten horns."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI considered the horns, and behold, there came up among them another horn, a little one, before which three of the first horns were plucked up by the roots; and behold, in this horn were eyes like the eyes of a man, and a mouth speaking arrogantly."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI watched until thrones were placed,"],[2,"and one who was Ancient of Days sat."],[1,"His clothing was white as snow,"],[2,"and the hair of his head like pure wool."],[1,"His throne was fiery flames,"],[2,"and its wheels burning fire."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"A fiery stream issued and came out from before him."],[2,"Thousands of thousands ministered to him."],[2,"Ten thousand times ten thousand stood before him."],[1,"The judgment was set."],[2,"The books were opened."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI watched at that time because of the voice of the arrogant words which the horn spoke. I watched even until the animal was slain, and its body destroyed, and it was given to be burned with fire."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"As for the rest of the animals, their dominion was taken away; yet their lives were prolonged for a season and a time."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI saw in the night visions, and behold, there came with the clouds of the sky one like a son of man, and he came even to the Ancient of Days, and they brought him near before him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Dominion was given him, and glory, and a kingdom, that all the peoples, nations, and languages should serve him. His dominion is an everlasting dominion, which will not pass away, and his kingdom one that will not be destroyed."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for me, Daniel, my spirit was grieved within my body, and the visions of my head troubled me."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I came near to one of those who stood by, and asked him the truth concerning all this."],[0,"\u201cSo he told me, and made me know the interpretation of the things."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"\u2018These great animals, which are four, are four kings, who will arise out of the earth."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But the saints of the Most High will receive the kingdom, and possess the kingdom forever, even forever and ever.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen I desired to know the truth concerning the fourth animal, which was different from all of them, exceedingly terrible, whose teeth were of iron, and its nails of bronze; which devoured, broke in pieces, and stamped the residue with its feet;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and concerning the ten horns that were on its head and the other horn which came up, and before which three fell, even that horn that had eyes and a mouth that spoke arrogantly, whose look was more stout than its fellows."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I saw, and the same horn made war with the saints, and prevailed against them,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"until the Ancient of Days came, and judgment was given to the saints of the Most High, and the time came that the saints possessed the kingdom."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo he said, \u2018The fourth animal will be a fourth kingdom on earth, which will be different from all the kingdoms, and will devour the whole earth, and will tread it down and break it in pieces."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"As for the ten horns, ten kings will arise out of this kingdom. Another will arise after them; and he will be different from the former, and he will put down three kings."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He will speak words against the Most High, and will wear out the saints of the Most High. He will plan to change the times and the law; and they will be given into his hand until a time and times and half a time."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201c\u2018But the judgment will be set, and they will take away his dominion, to consume and to destroy it to the end."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The kingdom and the dominion, and the greatness of the kingdoms under the whole sky, will be given to the people of the saints of the Most High. His kingdom is an everlasting kingdom, and all dominions will serve and obey him.\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHere is the end of the matter. As for me, Daniel, my thoughts troubled me greatly, and my face was changed in me; but I kept the matter in my heart.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the third year of the reign of King Belshazzar, a vision appeared to me, even to me, Daniel, after that which appeared to me at the first."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I saw the vision. Now it was so, that when I saw, I was in the citadel of Susa, which is in the province of Elam. I saw in the vision, and I was by the river Ulai."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then I lifted up my eyes and saw, and behold, a ram which had two horns stood before the river. The two horns were high, but one was higher than the other, and the higher came up last."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I saw the ram pushing westward, northward, and southward. No animals could stand before him. There wasn\u2019t any who could deliver out of his hand, but he did according to his will, and magnified himself."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"As I was considering, behold, a male goat came from the west over the surface of the whole earth, and didn\u2019t touch the ground. The goat had a notable horn between his eyes."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He came to the ram that had the two horns, which I saw standing before the river, and ran on him in the fury of his power."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I saw him come close to the ram, and he was moved with anger against him, and struck the ram, and broke his two horns. There was no power in the ram to stand before him; but he cast him down to the ground and trampled on him. There was no one who could deliver the ram out of his hand."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The male goat magnified himself exceedingly. When he was strong, the great horn was broken; and instead of it there came up four notable horns toward the four winds of the sky."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Out of one of them came out a little horn which grew exceedingly great\u2014toward the south, and toward the east, and toward the glorious land."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"It grew great, even to the army of the sky; and it cast down some of the army and of the stars to the ground and trampled on them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Yes, it magnified itself, even to the prince of the army; and it took away from him the continual burnt offering, and the place of his sanctuary was cast down."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The army was given over to it together with the continual burnt offering through disobedience. It cast down truth to the ground, and it did its pleasure and prospered."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I heard a holy one speaking; and another holy one said to that certain one who spoke, \u201cHow long will the vision about the continual burnt offering, and the disobedience that makes desolate, to give both the sanctuary and the army to be trodden under foot be?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cTo two thousand and three hundred evenings and mornings. Then the sanctuary will be cleansed.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When I, even I Daniel, had seen the vision, I sought to understand it. Then behold, there stood before me someone with the appearance of a man."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I heard a man\u2019s voice between the banks of the Ulai, which called and said, \u201cGabriel, make this man understand the vision.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So he came near where I stood; and when he came, I was frightened, and fell on my face; but he said to me, \u201cUnderstand, son of man, for the vision belongs to the time of the end.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now as he was speaking with me, I fell into a deep sleep with my face toward the ground; but he touched me and set me upright."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBehold, I will make you know what will be in the latter time of the indignation, for it belongs to the appointed time of the end."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The ram which you saw, that had the two horns, they are the kings of Media and Persia."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The rough male goat is the king of Greece. The great horn that is between his eyes is the first king."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"As for that which was broken, in the place where four stood up, four kingdoms will stand up out of the nation, but not with his power."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn the latter time of their kingdom, when the transgressors have come to the full, a king of fierce face, and understanding riddles, will stand up."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"His power will be mighty, but not by his own power. He will destroy awesomely, and will prosper in what he does. He will destroy the mighty ones and the holy people."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Through his policy he will cause deceit to prosper in his hand. He will magnify himself in his heart, and he will destroy many in their security. He will also stand up against the prince of princes, but he will be broken without human hands."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe vision of the evenings and mornings which has been told is true; but seal up the vision, for it belongs to many days to come.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"I, Daniel, fainted, and was sick for some days. Then I rose up and did the king\u2019s business. I wondered at the vision, but no one understood it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the first year of Darius the son of Ahasuerus, of the offspring of the Medes, who was made king over the realm of the Chaldeans\u2014"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"in the first year of his reign I, Daniel, understood by the books the number of the years about which the LORD\u2019s word came to Jeremiah the prophet for the accomplishing of the desolations of Jerusalem, even seventy years."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I set my face to the Lord God, to seek by prayer and petitions, with fasting and sackcloth and ashes."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I prayed to the LORD my God, and made confession, and said,"],[1,"\u201cOh, Lord, the great and dreadful God, who keeps covenant and loving kindness with those who love him and keep his commandments,"]]},{v:5,l:[[1,"we have sinned, and have dealt perversely, and have done wickedly, and have rebelled, even turning aside from your precepts and from your ordinances."]]},{v:6,l:[[1,"We haven\u2019t listened to your servants the prophets, who spoke in your name to our kings, our princes, and our fathers, and to all the people of the land."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLord, righteousness belongs to you, but to us confusion of face, as it is today; to the men of Judah, and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, and to all Israel, who are near and who are far off, through all the countries where you have driven them, because of their trespass that they have trespassed against you."]]},{v:8,l:[[1,"Lord, to us belongs confusion of face, to our kings, to our princes, and to our fathers, because we have sinned against you."]]},{v:9,l:[[1,"To the Lord our God belong mercies and forgiveness, for we have rebelled against him."]]},{v:10,l:[[1,"We haven\u2019t obeyed the LORD our God\u2019s voice, to walk in his laws, which he set before us by his servants the prophets."]]},{v:11,l:[[1,"Yes, all Israel have transgressed your law, turning aside, and not obeying your voice."],[1,"\u201cTherefore the curse and the oath written in the law of Moses the servant of God has been poured out on us, for we have sinned against him."]]},{v:12,l:[[1,"He has confirmed his words, which he spoke against us and against our judges who judged us, by bringing on us a great evil; for under the whole sky, such has not been done as has been done to Jerusalem."]]},{v:13,l:[[1,"As it is written in the law of Moses, all this evil has come on us. Yet we have not entreated the favor of the LORD our God, that we should turn from our iniquities and have discernment in your truth."]]},{v:14,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD has watched over the evil, and brought it on us; for the LORD our God is righteous in all his works which he does, and we have not obeyed his voice."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow, Lord our God, who has brought your people out of the land of Egypt with a mighty hand, and have gotten yourself renown, as it is today, we have sinned. We have done wickedly."]]},{v:16,l:[[1,"Lord, according to all your righteousness, please let your anger and your wrath be turned away from your city Jerusalem, your holy mountain; because for our sins and for the iniquities of our fathers, Jerusalem and your people have become a reproach to all who are around us."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow therefore, our God, listen to the prayer of your servant and to his petitions, and cause your face to shine on your sanctuary that is desolate, for the Lord\u2019s sake."]]},{v:18,l:[[1,"My God, turn your ear and hear. Open your eyes and see our desolations, and the city which is called by your name; for we do not present our petitions before you for our righteousness, but for your great mercies\u2019 sake."]]},{v:19,l:[[1,"Lord, hear. Lord, forgive. Lord, listen and do. Don\u2019t defer, for your own sake, my God, because your city and your people are called by your name.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"While I was speaking, praying, and confessing my sin and the sin of my people Israel, and presenting my supplication before the LORD my God for the holy mountain of my God\u2014"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"yes, while I was speaking in prayer\u2014the man Gabriel, whom I had seen in the vision at the beginning, being caused to fly swiftly, touched me about the time of the evening offering."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He instructed me and talked with me, and said, \u201cDaniel, I have now come to give you wisdom and understanding."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"At the beginning of your petitions the commandment went out, and I have come to tell you, for you are greatly beloved. Therefore consider the matter and understand the vision."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSeventy weeks are decreed on your people and on your holy city, to finish disobedience, to make an end of sins, to make reconciliation for iniquity, to bring in everlasting righteousness, to seal up vision and prophecy, and to anoint the most holy."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cKnow therefore and discern that from the going out of the commandment to restore and build Jerusalem to the Anointed One, the prince, will be seven weeks and sixty-two weeks. It will be built again, with street and moat, even in troubled times."]],f:["\u201cAnointed One\u201d can also be translated \u201cMessiah\u201d (same as \u201cChrist\u201d)."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"After the sixty-two weeks the Anointed One will be cut off, and will have nothing. The people of the prince who come will destroy the city and the sanctuary. Its end will be with a flood, and war will be even to the end. Desolations are determined."]],f:["\u201cAnointed One\u201d can also be translated \u201cMessiah\u201d (same as \u201cChrist\u201d)."]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He will make a firm covenant with many for one week. In the middle of the week he will cause the sacrifice and the offering to cease. On the wing of abominations will come one who makes desolate; and even to the decreed full end, wrath will be poured out on the desolate.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the third year of Cyrus king of Persia a message was revealed to Daniel, whose name was called Belteshazzar; and the message was true, even a great warfare. He understood the message, and had understanding of the vision."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days I, Daniel, was mourning three whole weeks."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I ate no pleasant food. No meat or wine came into my mouth. I didn\u2019t anoint myself at all, until three whole weeks were fulfilled."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twenty-fourth day of the first month, as I was by the side of the great river, which is Hiddekel,"]],f:["or, Tigris River"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I lifted up my eyes and looked, and behold, there was a man clothed in linen, whose waist was adorned with pure gold of Uphaz."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"His body also was like beryl, and his face as the appearance of lightning, and his eyes as flaming torches. His arms and his feet were like burnished bronze. The voice of his words was like the voice of a multitude."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"I, Daniel, alone saw the vision, for the men who were with me didn\u2019t see the vision, but a great quaking fell on them, and they fled to hide themselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So I was left alone and saw this great vision. No strength remained in me; for my face grew deathly pale, and I retained no strength."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Yet I heard the voice of his words. When I heard the voice of his words, then I fell into a deep sleep on my face, with my face toward the ground."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, a hand touched me, which set me on my knees and on the palms of my hands."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cDaniel, you greatly beloved man, understand the words that I speak to you, and stand upright, for I have been sent to you, now.\u201d When he had spoken this word to me, I stood trembling."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, Daniel; for from the first day that you set your heart to understand, and to humble yourself before your God, your words were heard. I have come for your words\u2019 sake."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But the prince of the kingdom of Persia withstood me twenty-one days; but, behold, Michael, one of the chief princes, came to help me because I remained there with the kings of Persia."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now I have come to make you understand what will happen to your people in the latter days, for the vision is yet for many days.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had spoken these words to me, I set my face toward the ground and was mute."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Behold, one in the likeness of the sons of men touched my lips. Then I opened my mouth, and spoke and said to him who stood before me, \u201cMy lord, by reason of the vision my sorrows have overtaken me, and I retain no strength."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For how can the servant of this my lord talk with this my lord? For as for me, immediately there remained no strength in me. There was no breath left in me.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then one like the appearance of a man touched me again, and he strengthened me."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGreatly beloved man, don\u2019t be afraid. Peace be to you. Be strong. Yes, be strong.\u201d"],[0,"When he spoke to me, I was strengthened, and said, \u201cLet my lord speak, for you have strengthened me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cDo you know why I have come to you? Now I will return to fight with the prince of Persia. When I go out, behold, the prince of Greece will come."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But I will tell you that which is inscribed in the writing of truth. There is no one who holds with me against these but Michael your prince."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for me, in the first year of Darius the Mede, I stood up to confirm and strengthen him."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow I will show you the truth. Behold, three more kings will stand up in Persia. The fourth will be far richer than all of them. When he has grown strong through his riches, he will stir up all against the realm of Greece."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"A mighty king will stand up, who will rule with great dominion, and do according to his will."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When he stands up, his kingdom will be broken and will be divided toward the four winds of the sky, but not to his posterity, nor according to his dominion with which he ruled; for his kingdom will be plucked up, even for others besides these."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe king of the south will be strong. One of his princes will become stronger than him, and have dominion. His dominion will be a great dominion."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"At the end of years they will join themselves together; and the daughter of the king of the south will come to the king of the north to make an agreement, but she will not retain the strength of her arm. He will also not stand, nor will his arm; but she will be given up, with those who brought her, and he who became the father of her, and he who strengthened her in those times."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut out of a shoot from her roots one will stand up in his place, who will come to the army and will enter into the fortress of the king of the north, and will deal against them and will prevail."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He will also carry their gods with their molten images, and with their goodly vessels of silver and of gold, captive into Egypt. He will refrain some years from the king of the north."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He will come into the realm of the king of the south, but he will return into his own land."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"His sons will wage war, and will assemble a multitude of great forces which will come on, and overflow, and pass through. They will return and wage war, even to his fortress."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe king of the south will be moved with anger and will come out and fight with him, even with the king of the north. He will send out a great multitude, and the multitude will be given into his hand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The multitude will be carried off, and his heart will be exalted. He will cast down tens of thousands, but he won\u2019t prevail."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The king of the north will return, and will send out a multitude greater than the former. He will come on at the end of the times, even of years, with a great army and with abundant supplies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn those times many will stand up against the king of the south. Also the children of the violent among your people will lift themselves up to establish the vision, but they will fall."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So the king of the north will come and cast up a mound, and take a well-fortified city. The forces of the south won\u2019t stand, neither will his select troops, neither will there be any strength to stand."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But he who comes against him will do according to his own will, and no one will stand before him. He will stand in the glorious land, and destruction will be in his hand."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He will set his face to come with the strength of his whole kingdom, and with him equitable conditions. He will perform them. He will give him the daughter of women, to destroy the kingdom, but she will not stand, and won\u2019t be for him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"After this he will turn his face to the islands, and will take many, but a prince will cause the reproach offered by him to cease. Yes, moreover, he will cause his reproach to turn on him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Then he will turn his face toward the fortresses of his own land; but he will stumble and fall, and won\u2019t be found."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen one who will cause a tax collector to pass through the kingdom to maintain its glory will stand up in his place; but within a few days he shall be destroyed, not in anger, and not in battle."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn his place a contemptible person will stand up, to whom they had not given the honor of the kingdom; but he will come in a time of security, and will obtain the kingdom by flatteries."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The overwhelming forces will be overwhelmed from before him, and will be broken. Yes, also the prince of the covenant."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"After the treaty made with him he will work deceitfully; for he will come up and will become strong with few people."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"In a time of security he will come even on the fattest places of the province. He will do that which his fathers have not done, nor his fathers\u2019 fathers. He will scatter among them prey, plunder, and wealth. Yes, he will devise his plans against the strongholds, but only for a time."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe will stir up his power and his courage against the king of the south with a great army; and the king of the south will wage war in battle with an exceedingly great and mighty army, but he won\u2019t stand; for they will devise plans against him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Yes, those who eat of his delicacies will destroy him, and his army will be swept away. Many will fall down slain."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"As for both these kings, their hearts will be to do evil, and they will speak lies at one table; but it won\u2019t prosper, for the end will still be at the appointed time."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Then he will return into his land with great wealth. His heart will be against the holy covenant. He will take action, and return to his own land."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe will return at the appointed time and come into the south; but it won\u2019t be in the latter time as it was in the former."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For ships of Kittim will come against him. Therefore he will be grieved, and will return, and have indignation against the holy covenant, and will take action. He will even return, and have regard to those who forsake the holy covenant."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cForces from him will profane the sanctuary, even the fortress, and will take away the continual burnt offering. Then they will set up the abomination that makes desolate."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He will corrupt those who do wickedly against the covenant by flatteries; but the people who know their God will be strong and take action."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThose who are wise among the people will instruct many; yet they will fall by the sword and by flame, by captivity and by plunder, many days."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Now when they fall, they will be helped with a little help; but many will join themselves to them with flatteries."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Some of those who are wise will fall\u2014to refine them, and to purify, and to make them white, even to the time of the end, because it is yet for the time appointed."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe king will do according to his will. He will exalt himself and magnify himself above every god, and will speak marvelous things against the God of gods. He will prosper until the indignation is accomplished, for that which is determined will be done."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He won\u2019t regard the gods of his fathers, or the desire of women, or regard any god; for he will magnify himself above all."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But in their place, he will honor the god of fortresses. He will honor a god whom his fathers didn\u2019t know with gold, silver, and with precious stones and pleasant things."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"He will deal with the strongest fortresses by the help of a foreign god. He will increase with glory whoever acknowledges him. He will cause them to rule over many, and will divide the land for a price."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAt the time of the end the king of the south will contend with him; and the king of the north will come against him like a whirlwind, with chariots, with horsemen, and with many ships. He will enter into the countries, and will overflow and pass through."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He will enter also into the glorious land, and many countries will be overthrown; but these will be delivered out of his hand: Edom, Moab, and the chief of the children of Ammon."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"He will also stretch out his hand on the countries. The land of Egypt won\u2019t escape."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"But he will have power over the treasures of gold and of silver, and over all the precious things of Egypt. The Libyans and the Ethiopians will follow his steps."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"But news out of the east and out of the north will trouble him; and he will go out with great fury to destroy and utterly to sweep away many."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"He will plant the tents of his palace between the sea and the glorious holy mountain; yet he will come to his end, and no one will help him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAt that time Michael will stand up, the great prince who stands for the children of your people; and there will be a time of trouble, such as never was since there was a nation even to that same time. At that time your people will be delivered, everyone who is found written in the book."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Many of those who sleep in the dust of the earth will awake, some to everlasting life, and some to shame and everlasting contempt."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Those who are wise will shine as the brightness of the expanse. Those who turn many to righteousness will shine as the stars forever and ever."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But you, Daniel, shut up the words and seal the book, even to the time of the end. Many will run back and forth, and knowledge will be increased.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I, Daniel, looked, and behold, two others stood, one on the river bank on this side, and the other on the river bank on that side."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"One said to the man clothed in linen, who was above the waters of the river, \u201cHow long will it be to the end of these wonders?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard the man clothed in linen, who was above the waters of the river, when he held up his right hand and his left hand to heaven, and swore by him who lives forever that it will be for a time, times, and a half; and when they have finished breaking in pieces the power of the holy people, all these things will be finished."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard, but I didn\u2019t understand. Then I said, \u201cMy lord, what will be the outcome of these things?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGo your way, Daniel; for the words are shut up and sealed until the time of the end."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Many will purify themselves, and make themselves white, and be refined, but the wicked will do wickedly; and none of the wicked will understand, but those who are wise will understand."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFrom the time that the continual burnt offering is taken away and the abomination that makes desolate set up, there will be one thousand two hundred ninety days."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Blessed is he who waits, and comes to the one thousand three hundred thirty-five days."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut go your way until the end; for you will rest, and will stand in your inheritance at the end of the days.\u201d"]]}]]}},1298,[]);
__d(function(e,t,a,o,i,h,l){i.exports={book:"Hos",name:"Hosea",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word that came to Hosea the son of Beeri, in the days of Uzziah, Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash, king of Israel."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"When the LORD spoke at first by Hosea, the LORD said to Hosea, \u201cGo, take for yourself a wife of prostitution and children of unfaithfulness; for the land commits great adultery, forsaking the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"So he went and took Gomer the daughter of Diblaim; and she conceived, and bore him a son."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to him, \u201cCall his name Jezreel, for yet a little while, and I will avenge the blood of Jezreel on the house of Jehu, and will cause the kingdom of the house of Israel to cease."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that I will break the bow of Israel in the valley of Jezreel.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"She conceived again, and bore a daughter."],[0,"Then he said to him, \u201cCall her name Lo-Ruhamah, for I will no longer have mercy on the house of Israel, that I should in any way pardon them."]],f:["Lo-Ruhamah means \u201cnot loved\u201d."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But I will have mercy on the house of Judah, and will save them by the LORD their God, and will not save them by bow, sword, battle, horses, or horsemen.\u201d"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when she had weaned Lo-Ruhamah, she conceived, and bore a son."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cCall his name Lo-Ammi, for you are not my people, and I will not be yours."]],f:["Lo-Ammi means \u201cnot my people\u201d."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Yet the number of the children of Israel will be as the sand of the sea, which can\u2019t be measured or counted; and it will come to pass that, in the place where it was said to them, \u2018You are not my people,\u2019 they will be called \u2018sons of the living God.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The children of Judah and the children of Israel will be gathered together, and they will appoint themselves one head, and will go up from the land; for great will be the day of Jezreel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSay to your brothers, \u2018My people!\u2019"],[2,"and to your sisters, \u2018My loved one!\u2019"]],f:["\u2018Ammi\u2019 in Hebrew","\u2018Ruhamah\u2019 in Hebrew"]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Contend with your mother!"],[2,"Contend, for she is not my wife,"],[2,"neither am I her husband;"],[1,"and let her put away her prostitution from her face,"],[2,"and her adulteries from between her breasts;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"lest I strip her naked,"],[2,"and make her bare as in the day that she was born,"],[1,"and make her like a wilderness,"],[2,"and set her like a dry land,"],[2,"and kill her with thirst."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Indeed, on her children I will have no mercy,"],[2,"for they are children of unfaithfulness."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"For their mother has played the prostitute."],[2,"She who conceived them has done shamefully;"],[1,"for she said, \u2018I will go after my lovers,"],[2,"who give me my bread and my water,"],[2,"my wool and my flax,"],[2,"my oil and my drink.\u2019"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore behold, I will hedge up your way with thorns,"],[2,"and I will build a wall against her,"],[2,"that she can\u2019t find her way."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"She will follow after her lovers,"],[2,"but she won\u2019t overtake them;"],[1,"and she will seek them,"],[2,"but won\u2019t find them."],[1,"Then she will say, \u2018I will go and return to my first husband,"],[2,"for then it was better with me than now.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For she didn\u2019t know that I gave her the grain, the new wine, and the oil,"],[2,"and multiplied to her silver and gold, which they used for Baal."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will take back my grain in its time,"],[2,"and my new wine in its season,"],[2,"and will pluck away my wool and my flax which should have covered her nakedness."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Now I will uncover her lewdness in the sight of her lovers,"],[2,"and no one will deliver her out of my hand."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I will also cause all her celebrations to cease:"],[2,"her feasts, her new moons, her Sabbaths, and all her solemn assemblies."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will lay waste her vines and her fig trees,"],[2,"about which she has said, \u2018These are my wages that my lovers have given me,\u2019"],[2,"and I will make them a forest,"],[2,"and the animals of the field shall eat them."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I will visit on her the days of the Baals,"],[2,"to which she burned incense"],[1,"when she decked herself with her earrings and her jewels,"],[2,"and went after her lovers"],[2,"and forgot me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore behold, I will allure her,"],[2,"and bring her into the wilderness,"],[2,"and speak tenderly to her."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will give her vineyards from there,"],[2,"and the valley of Achor for a door of hope;"],[1,"and she will respond there"],[2,"as in the days of her youth,"],[2,"and as in the day when she came up out of the land of Egypt."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"It will be in that day,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthat you will call me \u2018my husband,\u2019"],[2,"and no longer call me \u2018my master.\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will take away the names of the Baals out of her mouth,"],[2,"and they will no longer be mentioned by name."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"In that day I will make a covenant for them with the animals of the field,"],[2,"and with the birds of the sky,"],[2,"and with the creeping things of the ground."],[1,"I will break the bow, the sword, and the battle out of the land,"],[2,"and will make them lie down safely."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I will betroth you to me forever."],[2,"Yes, I will betroth you to me in righteousness, in justice, in loving kindness, and in compassion."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"I will even betroth you to me in faithfulness;"],[2,"and you shall know the LORD."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"It will happen in that day, that I will respond,\u201d says the LORD."],[2,"\u201cI will respond to the heavens,"],[2,"and they will respond to the earth;"]]},{v:22,l:[[2,"and the earth will respond to the grain, and the new wine, and the oil;"],[2,"and they will respond to Jezreel."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"I will sow her to me in the earth;"],[2,"and I will have mercy on her who had not obtained mercy;"],[2,"and I will tell those who were not my people, \u2018You are my people;\u2019"],[2,"and they will say, \u2018You are My God!\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cGo again, love a woman loved by another, and an adulteress, even as the LORD loves the children of Israel, though they turn to other gods, and love cakes of raisins.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"So I bought her for myself for fifteen pieces of silver and a homer and a half of barley."]],f:["1 homer is about 220 liters or 6 bushels"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I said to her, \u201cYou shall stay with me many days. You shall not play the prostitute, and you shall not be with any other man. I will also be so toward you.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"For the children of Israel shall live many days without king, without prince, without sacrifice, without sacred stone, and without ephod or idols."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Afterward the children of Israel shall return and seek the LORD their God, and David their king, and shall come with trembling to the LORD and to his blessings in the last days."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hear the LORD\u2019s word, you children of Israel,"],[2,"for the LORD has a charge against the inhabitants of the land:"],[1,"\u201cIndeed there is no truth, nor goodness,"],[2,"nor knowledge of God in the land."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"There is cursing, lying, murder, stealing, and committing adultery;"],[2,"they break boundaries, and bloodshed causes bloodshed."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the land will mourn,"],[2,"and everyone who dwells in it will waste away,"],[1,"with all living things in her,"],[2,"even the animals of the field and the birds of the sky;"],[2,"yes, the fish of the sea also die."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYet let no man bring a charge, neither let any man accuse;"],[2,"for your people are like those who bring charges against a priest."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"You will stumble in the day,"],[2,"and the prophet will also stumble with you in the night;"],[2,"and I will destroy your mother."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge."],[2,"Because you have rejected knowledge, I will also reject you,"],[2,"that you may be no priest to me."],[1,"Because you have forgotten your God\u2019s law,"],[2,"I will also forget your children."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"As they were multiplied, so they sinned against me."],[2,"I will change their glory into shame."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"They feed on the sin of my people,"],[2,"and set their heart on their iniquity."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"It will be like people, like priest;"],[2,"and I will punish them for their ways,"],[2,"and will repay them for their deeds."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They will eat, and not have enough."],[2,"They will play the prostitute, and will not increase;"],[2,"because they have abandoned listening to the LORD."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Prostitution, wine, and new wine take away understanding."]]},{v:12,l:[[2,"My people consult with their wooden idol,"],[2,"and answer to a stick of wood."],[1,"Indeed the spirit of prostitution has led them astray,"],[2,"and they have been unfaithful to their God."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"They sacrifice on the tops of the mountains,"],[2,"and burn incense on the hills, under oaks, poplars, and terebinths,"],[2,"because its shade is good."],[1,"Therefore your daughters play the prostitute,"],[2,"and your brides commit adultery."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will not punish your daughters when they play the prostitute,"],[2,"nor your brides when they commit adultery;"],[1,"because the men consort with prostitutes,"],[2,"and they sacrifice with the shrine prostitutes;"],[2,"so the people without understanding will come to ruin."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThough you, Israel, play the prostitute,"],[2,"yet don\u2019t let Judah offend;"],[2,"and don\u2019t come to Gilgal,"],[2,"neither go up to Beth Aven,"],[2,"nor swear, \u2018As the LORD lives.\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For Israel has behaved extremely stubbornly, like a stubborn heifer."],[2,"Then how will the LORD feed them like a lamb in a meadow?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim is joined to idols."],[2,"Leave him alone!"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Their drink has become sour."],[2,"They play the prostitute continually."],[2,"Her rulers dearly love their shameful way."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The wind has wrapped her up in its wings;"],[2,"and they shall be disappointed because of their sacrifices."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cListen to this, you priests!"],[2,"Listen, house of Israel,"],[2,"and give ear, house of the king!"],[1,"For the judgment is against you;"],[2,"for you have been a snare at Mizpah,"],[2,"and a net spread on Tabor."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The rebels are deep in slaughter,"],[2,"but I discipline all of them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"I know Ephraim,"],[2,"and Israel is not hidden from me;"],[1,"for now, Ephraim, you have played the prostitute."],[2,"Israel is defiled."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Their deeds won\u2019t allow them to turn to their God,"],[2,"for the spirit of prostitution is within them,"],[2,"and they don\u2019t know the LORD."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The pride of Israel testifies to his face."],[2,"Therefore Israel and Ephraim will stumble in their iniquity."],[2,"Judah also will stumble with them."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They will go with their flocks and with their herds to seek the LORD,"],[2,"but they won\u2019t find him."],[2,"He has withdrawn himself from them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They are unfaithful to the LORD;"],[2,"for they have borne illegitimate children."],[2,"Now the new moon will devour them with their fields."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBlow the cornet in Gibeah,"],[2,"and the trumpet in Ramah!"],[2,"Sound a battle cry at Beth Aven, behind you, Benjamin!"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim will become a desolation in the day of rebuke."],[2,"Among the tribes of Israel, I have made known that which will surely be."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The princes of Judah are like those who remove a landmark."],[2,"I will pour out my wrath on them like water."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim is oppressed,"],[2,"he is crushed in judgment,"],[2,"because he is intent in his pursuit of idols."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I am to Ephraim like a moth,"],[2,"and to the house of Judah like rottenness."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhen Ephraim saw his sickness,"],[2,"and Judah his wound,"],[2,"then Ephraim went to Assyria,"],[2,"and sent to King Jareb:"],[1,"but he is not able to heal you,"],[2,"neither will he cure you of your wound."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will be to Ephraim like a lion,"],[2,"and like a young lion to the house of Judah."],[1,"I myself will tear in pieces and go away."],[2,"I will carry off, and there will be no one to deliver."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will go and return to my place,"],[2,"until they acknowledge their offense,"],[2,"and seek my face."],[2,"In their affliction they will seek me earnestly.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cCome! Let\u2019s return to the LORD;"],[2,"for he has torn us to pieces,"],[2,"and he will heal us;"],[1,"he has injured us,"],[2,"and he will bind up our wounds."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"After two days he will revive us."],[2,"On the third day he will raise us up,"],[2,"and we will live before him."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Let\u2019s acknowledge the LORD."],[2,"Let\u2019s press on to know the LORD."],[1,"As surely as the sun rises,"],[2,"the LORD will appear."],[1,"He will come to us like the rain,"],[2,"like the spring rain that waters the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEphraim, what shall I do to you?"],[2,"Judah, what shall I do to you?"],[2,"For your love is like a morning cloud,"],[2,"and like the dew that disappears early."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I have cut them to pieces with the prophets;"],[2,"I killed them with the words of my mouth."],[2,"Your judgments are like a flash of lightning."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For I desire mercy, and not sacrifice;"],[2,"and the knowledge of God more than burnt offerings."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But they, like Adam, have broken the covenant."],[2,"They were unfaithful to me there."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Gilead is a city of those who work iniquity;"],[2,"it is stained with blood."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"As gangs of robbers wait to ambush a man,"],[2,"so the company of priests murder on the path toward Shechem,"],[2,"committing shameful crimes."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"In the house of Israel I have seen a horrible thing."],[2,"There is prostitution in Ephraim."],[2,"Israel is defiled."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAlso, Judah, there is a harvest appointed for you,"],[2,"when I restore the fortunes of my people."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When I would heal Israel,"],[2,"then the iniquity of Ephraim is uncovered,"],[2,"also the wickedness of Samaria;"],[2,"for they commit falsehood,"],[2,"and the thief enters in,"],[2,"and the gang of robbers ravages outside."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"They don\u2019t consider in their hearts that I remember all their wickedness."],[2,"Now their own deeds have engulfed them."],[2,"They are before my face."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They make the king glad with their wickedness,"],[2,"and the princes with their lies."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They are all adulterers."],[2,"They are burning like an oven that the baker stops stirring,"],[2,"from the kneading of the dough, until it is leavened."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"On the day of our king, the princes made themselves sick with the heat of wine."],[2,"He joined his hand with mockers."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For they have prepared their heart like an oven,"],[2,"while they lie in wait."],[2,"Their anger smolders all night."],[2,"In the morning it burns as a flaming fire."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They are all hot as an oven,"],[2,"and devour their judges."],[1,"All their kings have fallen."],[2,"There is no one among them who calls to me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim mixes himself among the nations."],[2,"Ephraim is a pancake not turned over."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Strangers have devoured his strength,"],[2,"and he doesn\u2019t realize it."],[1,"Indeed, gray hairs are here and there on him,"],[2,"and he doesn\u2019t realize it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The pride of Israel testifies to his face;"],[2,"yet they haven\u2019t returned to the LORD their God,"],[2,"nor sought him, for all this."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cEphraim is like an easily deceived dove, without understanding."],[2,"They call to Egypt."],[2,"They go to Assyria."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"When they go, I will spread my net on them."],[2,"I will bring them down like the birds of the sky."],[2,"I will chastise them, as their congregation has heard."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to them!"],[2,"For they have wandered from me."],[1,"Destruction to them!"],[2,"For they have trespassed against me."],[1,"Though I would redeem them,"],[2,"yet they have spoken lies against me."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"They haven\u2019t cried to me with their heart,"],[2,"but they howl on their beds."],[1,"They assemble themselves for grain and new wine."],[2,"They turn away from me."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Though I have taught and strengthened their arms,"],[2,"yet they plot evil against me."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"They return, but not to the Most High."],[2,"They are like a faulty bow."],[2,"Their princes will fall by the sword for the rage of their tongue."],[2,"This will be their derision in the land of Egypt."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cPut the trumpet to your lips!"],[2,"Something like an eagle is over the LORD\u2019s house,"],[2,"because they have broken my covenant"],[2,"and rebelled against my law."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"They cry to me, \u2018My God, we, Israel, acknowledge you!\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"Israel has cast off that which is good."],[2,"The enemy will pursue him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They have set up kings, but not by me."],[2,"They have made princes, and I didn\u2019t approve."],[2,"Of their silver and their gold they have made themselves idols,"],[2,"that they may be cut off."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Let Samaria throw out his calf idol!"],[2,"My anger burns against them!"],[2,"How long will it be until they are capable of purity?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For this is even from Israel!"],[2,"The workman made it, and it is no God;"],[2,"indeed, the calf of Samaria shall be broken in pieces."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"For they sow the wind,"],[2,"and they will reap the whirlwind."],[1,"He has no standing grain."],[2,"The stalk will yield no head."],[2,"If it does yield, strangers will swallow it up."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel is swallowed up."],[2,"Now they are among the nations like a worthless thing."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For they have gone up to Assyria,"],[2,"like a wild donkey wandering alone."],[2,"Ephraim has hired lovers for himself."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"But although they sold themselves among the nations,"],[2,"I will now gather them;"],[2,"and they begin to waste away because of the oppression of the king of mighty ones."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Because Ephraim has multiplied altars for sinning,"],[2,"they became for him altars for sinning."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I wrote for him the many things of my law,"],[2,"but they were regarded as a strange thing."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"As for the sacrifices of my offerings,"],[2,"they sacrifice meat and eat it,"],[2,"but the LORD doesn\u2019t accept them."],[1,"Now he will remember their iniquity,"],[2,"and punish their sins."],[2,"They will return to Egypt."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For Israel has forgotten his Maker and built palaces;"],[2,"and Judah has multiplied fortified cities;"],[2,"but I will send a fire on his cities,"],[2,"and it will devour its fortresses.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t rejoice, Israel, to jubilation like the nations;"],[2,"for you were unfaithful to your God."],[2,"You love the wages of a prostitute at every grain threshing floor."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The threshing floor and the wine press won\u2019t feed them,"],[2,"and the new wine will fail her."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"They won\u2019t dwell in the LORD\u2019s land;"],[2,"but Ephraim will return to Egypt,"],[2,"and they will eat unclean food in Assyria."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They won\u2019t pour out wine offerings to the LORD,"],[2,"neither will they be pleasing to him."],[2,"Their sacrifices will be to them like the bread of mourners;"],[2,"all who eat of it will be polluted;"],[2,"for their bread will be for their appetite."],[2,"It will not come into the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"What will you do in the day of solemn assembly,"],[2,"and in the day of the feast of the LORD?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, when they flee destruction,"],[2,"Egypt will gather them up."],[2,"Memphis will bury them."],[2,"Nettles will possess their pleasant things of silver."],[2,"Thorns will be in their tents."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The days of visitation have come."],[2,"The days of reckoning have come."],[1,"Israel will consider the prophet to be a fool,"],[2,"and the man who is inspired to be insane,"],[2,"because of the abundance of your sins,"],[2,"and because your hostility is great."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"A prophet watches over Ephraim with my God."],[2,"A fowler\u2019s snare is on all of his paths,"],[2,"and hostility in the house of his God."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They have deeply corrupted themselves,"],[2,"as in the days of Gibeah."],[2,"He will remember their iniquity."],[2,"He will punish them for their sins."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I found Israel like grapes in the wilderness."],[2,"I saw your fathers as the first ripe in the fig tree at its first season;"],[2,"but they came to Baal Peor, and consecrated themselves to the shameful thing,"],[2,"and became abominable like that which they loved."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"As for Ephraim, their glory will fly away like a bird."],[2,"There will be no birth, no one with child, and no conception."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Though they bring up their children,"],[2,"yet I will bereave them, so that not a man shall be left."],[2,"Indeed, woe also to them when I depart from them!"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I have seen Ephraim, like Tyre, planted in a pleasant place;"],[2,"but Ephraim will bring out his children to the murderer."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Give them\u2014LORD what will you give?"],[2,"Give them a miscarrying womb and dry breasts."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAll their wickedness is in Gilgal;"],[2,"for there I hated them."],[2,"Because of the wickedness of their deeds, I will drive them out of my house!"],[2,"I will love them no more."],[2,"All their princes are rebels."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim is struck."],[2,"Their root has dried up."],[2,"They will bear no fruit."],[2,"Even though they give birth, yet I will kill the beloved ones of their womb.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"My God will cast them away, because they didn\u2019t listen to him;"],[2,"and they will be wanderers among the nations."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Israel is a luxuriant vine that produces his fruit."],[2,"According to the abundance of his fruit he has multiplied his altars."],[2,"As their land has prospered, they have adorned their sacred stones."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Their heart is divided."],[2,"Now they will be found guilty."],[2,"He will demolish their altars."],[2,"He will destroy their sacred stones."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely now they will say, \u201cWe have no king; for we don\u2019t fear the LORD;"],[2,"and the king, what can he do for us?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"They make promises, swearing falsely in making covenants."],[2,"Therefore judgment springs up like poisonous weeds in the furrows of the field."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The inhabitants of Samaria will be in terror for the calves of Beth Aven,"],[2,"for its people will mourn over it,"],[2,"along with its priests who rejoiced over it,"],[2,"for its glory, because it has departed from it."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"It also will be carried to Assyria for a present to a great king."],[2,"Ephraim will receive shame,"],[2,"and Israel will be ashamed of his own counsel."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Samaria and her king float away"],[2,"like a twig on the water."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The high places also of Aven, the sin of Israel, will be destroyed."],[2,"The thorn and the thistle will come up on their altars."],[2,"They will tell the mountains, \u201cCover us!\u201d and the hills, \u201cFall on us!\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIsrael, you have sinned from the days of Gibeah."],[2,"There they remained."],[2,"The battle against the children of iniquity doesn\u2019t overtake them in Gibeah."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"When it is my desire, I will chastise them;"],[2,"and the nations will be gathered against them"],[2,"when they are bound to their two transgressions."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim is a trained heifer that loves to thresh,"],[2,"so I will put a yoke on her beautiful neck."],[2,"I will set a rider on Ephraim."],[2,"Judah will plow."],[2,"Jacob will break his clods."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Sow to yourselves in righteousness,"],[2,"reap according to kindness."],[1,"Break up your fallow ground,"],[2,"for it is time to seek the LORD,"],[2,"until he comes and rains righteousness on you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You have plowed wickedness."],[2,"You have reaped iniquity."],[2,"You have eaten the fruit of lies,"],[2,"for you trusted in your way, in the multitude of your mighty men."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore a battle roar will arise among your people,"],[2,"and all your fortresses will be destroyed,"],[2,"as Shalman destroyed Beth Arbel in the day of battle."],[2,"The mother was dashed in pieces with her children."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"So Bethel will do to you because of your great wickedness."],[2,"At daybreak the king of Israel will be destroyed."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen Israel was a child, then I loved him,"],[2,"and called my son out of Egypt."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"They called to them, so they went from them."],[2,"They sacrificed to the Baals,"],[2,"and burned incense to engraved images."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet I taught Ephraim to walk."],[2,"I took them by their arms,"],[2,"but they didn\u2019t know that I healed them."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I drew them with cords of a man, with ties of love;"],[2,"and I was to them like those who lift up the yoke on their necks;"],[2,"and I bent down to him and I fed him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThey won\u2019t return into the land of Egypt;"],[2,"but the Assyrian will be their king,"],[2,"because they refused to repent."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"The sword will fall on their cities,"],[2,"and will destroy the bars of their gates,"],[2,"and will put an end to their plans."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"My people are determined to turn from me."],[2,"Though they call to the Most High,"],[2,"he certainly won\u2019t exalt them."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHow can I give you up, Ephraim?"],[2,"How can I hand you over, Israel?"],[2,"How can I make you like Admah?"],[2,"How can I make you like Zeboiim?"],[1,"My heart is turned within me,"],[2,"my compassion is aroused."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will not execute the fierceness of my anger."],[2,"I will not return to destroy Ephraim,"],[2,"for I am God, and not man\u2014the Holy One among you."],[2,"I will not come in wrath."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They will walk after the LORD,"],[2,"who will roar like a lion;"],[2,"for he will roar, and the children will come trembling from the west."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They will come trembling like a bird out of Egypt,"],[2,"and like a dove out of the land of Assyria;"],[1,"and I will settle them in their houses,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim surrounds me with falsehood,"],[2,"and the house of Israel with deceit."],[2,"Judah still strays from God,"],[2,"and is unfaithful to the Holy One."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Ephraim feeds on wind,"],[2,"and chases the east wind."],[2,"He continually multiplies lies and desolation."],[2,"They make a covenant with Assyria,"],[2,"and oil is carried into Egypt."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD also has a controversy with Judah,"],[2,"and will punish Jacob according to his ways;"],[2,"according to his deeds he will repay him."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"In the womb he took his brother by the heel,"],[2,"and in his manhood he contended with God."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Indeed, he struggled with the angel, and prevailed;"],[2,"he wept, and made supplication to him."],[2,"He found him at Bethel, and there he spoke with us\u2014"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"even the LORD, the God of Armies."],[2,"The LORD is his name of renown!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore turn to your God."],[2,"Keep kindness and justice,"],[2,"and wait continually for your God."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"A merchant has dishonest scales in his hand."],[2,"He loves to defraud."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim said, \u201cSurely I have become rich."],[2,"I have found myself wealth."],[2,"In all my wealth they won\u2019t find in me any iniquity that is sin.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut I am the LORD your God from the land of Egypt."],[2,"I will yet again make you dwell in tents,"],[2,"as in the days of the solemn feast."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I have also spoken to the prophets,"],[2,"and I have multiplied visions;"],[2,"and by the ministry of the prophets I have used parables."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"If Gilead is wicked,"],[2,"surely they are worthless."],[1,"In Gilgal they sacrifice bulls."],[2,"Indeed, their altars are like heaps in the furrows of the field."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Jacob fled into the country of Aram."],[2,"Israel served to get a wife."],[2,"For a wife he tended flocks and herds."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"By a prophet the LORD brought Israel up out of Egypt,"],[2,"and by a prophet he was preserved."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim has bitterly provoked anger."],[2,"Therefore his blood will be left on him,"],[2,"and his Lord will repay his contempt."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Ephraim spoke, there was trembling."],[2,"He exalted himself in Israel,"],[2,"but when he became guilty through Baal, he died."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Now they sin more and more,"],[2,"and have made themselves molten images of their silver,"],[2,"even idols according to their own understanding,"],[2,"all of them the work of the craftsmen."],[2,"They say of them, \u2018They offer human sacrifice and kiss the calves.\u2019"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore they will be like the morning mist,"],[2,"like the dew that passes away early,"],[2,"like the chaff that is driven with the whirlwind out of the threshing floor,"],[2,"and like the smoke out of the chimney."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYet I am the LORD your God from the land of Egypt;"],[2,"and you shall acknowledge no god but me,"],[2,"and besides me there is no savior."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I knew you in the wilderness,"],[2,"in the land of great drought."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"According to their pasture, so were they filled;"],[2,"they were filled, and their heart was exalted."],[2,"Therefore they have forgotten me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I am like a lion to them."],[2,"Like a leopard, I will lurk by the path."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will meet them like a bear that is bereaved of her cubs,"],[2,"and will tear the covering of their heart."],[2,"There I will devour them like a lioness."],[2,"The wild animal will tear them."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You are destroyed, Israel, because you are against me,"],[2,"against your helper."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Where is your king now, that he may save you in all your cities?"],[2,"And your judges, of whom you said, \u2018Give me a king and princes\u2019?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I have given you a king in my anger,"],[2,"and have taken him away in my wrath."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The guilt of Ephraim is stored up."],[2,"His sin is stored up."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"The sorrows of a travailing woman will come on him."],[2,"He is an unwise son,"],[2,"for when it is time, he doesn\u2019t come to the opening of the womb."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will ransom them from the power of Sheol."],[2,"I will redeem them from death!"],[2,"Death, where are your plagues?"],[2,"Sheol, where is your destruction?"],[1,"\u201cCompassion will be hidden from my eyes."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:15,l:[[2,"Though he is fruitful among his brothers, an east wind will come,"],[2,"the breath of the LORD coming up from the wilderness;"],[2,"and his spring will become dry,"],[2,"and his fountain will be dried up."],[2,"He will plunder the storehouse of treasure."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Samaria will bear her guilt,"],[2,"for she has rebelled against her God."],[2,"They will fall by the sword."],[2,"Their infants will be dashed in pieces,"],[2,"and their pregnant women will be ripped open.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Israel, return to the LORD your God;"],[2,"for you have fallen because of your sin."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Take words with you, and return to the LORD."],[2,"Tell him, \u201cForgive all our sins,"],[2,"and accept that which is good;"],[2,"so we offer bulls as we vowed of our lips."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Assyria can\u2019t save us."],[2,"We won\u2019t ride on horses;"],[2,"neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, \u2018Our gods!\u2019"],[2,"for in you the fatherless finds mercy.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will heal their waywardness."],[2,"I will love them freely;"],[2,"for my anger is turned away from them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I will be like the dew to Israel."],[2,"He will blossom like the lily,"],[2,"and send down his roots like Lebanon."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"His branches will spread,"],[2,"and his beauty will be like the olive tree,"],[2,"and his fragrance like Lebanon."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Men will dwell in his shade."],[2,"They will revive like the grain,"],[2,"and blossom like the vine."],[2,"Their fragrance will be like the wine of Lebanon."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim, what have I to do any more with idols?"],[2,"I answer, and will take care of him."],[2,"I am like a green cypress tree;"],[2,"from me your fruit is found.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is wise, that he may understand these things?"],[2,"Who is prudent, that he may know them?"],[2,"For the ways of the LORD are right,"],[2,"and the righteous walk in them,"],[2,"but the rebellious stumble in them."]]}]]}},1299,[]);
__d(function(e,a,t,o,n,h,r){n.exports={book:"Joel",name:"Joel",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word that came to Joel, the son of Pethuel."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear this, you elders,"],[2,"and listen, all you inhabitants of the land!"],[1,"Has this ever happened in your days,"],[2,"or in the days of your fathers?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Tell your children about it,"],[2,"and have your children tell their children,"],[2,"and their children, another generation."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"What the swarming locust has left, the great locust has eaten."],[2,"What the great locust has left, the grasshopper has eaten."],[2,"What the grasshopper has left, the caterpillar has eaten."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Wake up, you drunkards, and weep!"],[2,"Wail, all you drinkers of wine, because of the sweet wine,"],[2,"for it is cut off from your mouth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For a nation has come up on my land, strong, and without number."],[2,"His teeth are the teeth of a lion,"],[2,"and he has the fangs of a lioness."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"He has laid my vine waste,"],[2,"and stripped my fig tree."],[2,"He has stripped its bark, and thrown it away."],[2,"Its branches are made white."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Mourn like a virgin dressed in sackcloth"],[2,"for the husband of her youth!"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The meal offering and the drink offering are cut off from the LORD\u2019s house."],[2,"The priests, the LORD\u2019s ministers, mourn."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The field is laid waste."],[2,"The land mourns, for the grain is destroyed,"],[2,"The new wine has dried up,"],[2,"and the oil languishes."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Be confounded, you farmers!"],[2,"Wail, you vineyard keepers,"],[2,"for the wheat and for the barley;"],[2,"for the harvest of the field has perished."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"The vine has dried up, and the fig tree withered\u2014"],[2,"the pomegranate tree, the palm tree also, and the apple tree,"],[2,"even all of the trees of the field are withered;"],[2,"for joy has withered away from the sons of men."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Put on sackcloth and mourn, you priests!"],[2,"Wail, you ministers of the altar."],[1,"Come, lie all night in sackcloth, you ministers of my God,"],[2,"for the meal offering and the drink offering are withheld from your God\u2019s house."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Sanctify a fast."],[2,"Call a solemn assembly."],[2,"Gather the elders and all the inhabitants of the land to the house of the LORD, your God,"],[2,"and cry to the LORD."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Alas for the day!"],[2,"For the day of the LORD is at hand,"],[2,"and it will come as destruction from the Almighty."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Isn\u2019t the food cut off before our eyes,"],[2,"joy and gladness from the house of our God?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"The seeds rot under their clods."],[2,"The granaries are laid desolate."],[2,"The barns are broken down, for the grain has withered."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"How the animals groan!"],[2,"The herds of livestock are perplexed, because they have no pasture."],[2,"Yes, the flocks of sheep are made desolate."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, I cry to you,"],[2,"for the fire has devoured the pastures of the wilderness,"],[2,"and the flame has burned all the trees of the field."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, the animals of the field pant to you,"],[2,"for the water brooks have dried up,"],[2,"and the fire has devoured the pastures of the wilderness."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Blow the trumpet in Zion,"],[2,"and sound an alarm in my holy mountain!"],[1,"Let all the inhabitants of the land tremble,"],[2,"for the day of the LORD comes,"],[2,"for it is close at hand:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"A day of darkness and gloominess,"],[2,"a day of clouds and thick darkness."],[1,"As the dawn spreading on the mountains,"],[2,"a great and strong people;"],[2,"there has never been the like,"],[2,"neither will there be any more after them,"],[2,"even to the years of many generations."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A fire devours before them,"],[2,"and behind them, a flame burns."],[1,"The land is as the garden of Eden before them,"],[2,"and behind them, a desolate wilderness."],[1,"Yes, and no one has escaped them."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Their appearance is as the appearance of horses,"],[2,"and they run as horsemen."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Like the noise of chariots on the tops of the mountains, they leap,"],[2,"like the noise of a flame of fire that devours the stubble,"],[2,"like a strong people set in battle array."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"At their presence the peoples are in anguish."],[2,"All faces have grown pale."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They run like mighty men."],[2,"They climb the wall like warriors."],[2,"They each march in his line, and they don\u2019t swerve off course."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"One doesn\u2019t jostle another."],[2,"They each march in their own path."],[2,"They burst through the defenses"],[2,"and don\u2019t break ranks."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"They rush on the city."],[2,"They run on the wall."],[2,"They climb up into the houses."],[2,"They enter in at the windows like thieves."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The earth quakes before them."],[2,"The heavens tremble."],[2,"The sun and the moon are darkened,"],[2,"and the stars withdraw their shining."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD thunders his voice before his army,"],[2,"for his forces are very great;"],[2,"for he is strong who obeys his command;"],[2,"for the day of the LORD is great and very awesome,"],[2,"and who can endure it?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYet even now,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cturn to me with all your heart,"],[2,"and with fasting, and with weeping, and with mourning.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Tear your heart and not your garments,"],[2,"and turn to the LORD, your God;"],[2,"for he is gracious and merciful,"],[2,"slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness,"],[2,"and relents from sending calamity."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Who knows? He may turn and relent,"],[2,"and leave a blessing behind him,"],[2,"even a meal offering and a drink offering to the LORD, your God."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Blow the trumpet in Zion!"],[2,"Sanctify a fast."],[2,"Call a solemn assembly."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Gather the people."],[2,"Sanctify the assembly."],[2,"Assemble the elders."],[2,"Gather the children, and those who nurse from breasts."],[1,"Let the bridegroom go out of his room,"],[2,"and the bride out of her chamber."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"Let the priests, the ministers of the LORD, weep between the porch and the altar,"],[2,"and let them say, \u201cSpare your people, LORD,"],[2,"and don\u2019t give your heritage to reproach,"],[2,"that the nations should rule over them."],[1,"Why should they say among the peoples,"],[2,"\u2018Where is their God?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Then the LORD was jealous for his land,"],[2,"and had pity on his people."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD answered his people,"],[2,"\u201cBehold, I will send you grain, new wine, and oil,"],[2,"and you will be satisfied with them;"],[2,"and I will no more make you a reproach among the nations."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"But I will remove the northern army far away from you,"],[2,"and will drive it into a barren and desolate land,"],[2,"its front into the eastern sea,"],[2,"and its back into the western sea;"],[2,"and its stench will come up,"],[2,"and its bad smell will rise.\u201d"],[1,"Surely he has done great things."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Land, don\u2019t be afraid."],[2,"Be glad and rejoice, for the LORD has done great things."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t be afraid, you animals of the field;"],[2,"for the pastures of the wilderness spring up,"],[2,"for the tree bears its fruit."],[2,"The fig tree and the vine yield their strength."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBe glad then, you children of Zion,"],[2,"and rejoice in the LORD, your God;"],[2,"for he gives you the early rain in just measure,"],[2,"and he causes the rain to come down for you,"],[2,"the early rain and the latter rain, as before."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"The threshing floors will be full of wheat,"],[2,"and the vats will overflow with new wine and oil."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"I will restore to you the years that the swarming locust has eaten,"],[2,"the great locust, the grasshopper, and the caterpillar,"],[2,"my great army, which I sent among you."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"You will have plenty to eat and be satisfied,"],[2,"and will praise the name of the LORD, your God,"],[2,"who has dealt wondrously with you;"],[2,"and my people will never again be disappointed."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"You will know that I am among Israel,"],[2,"and that I am the LORD, your God, and there is no one else;"],[2,"and my people will never again be disappointed."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIt will happen afterward, that I will pour out my Spirit on all flesh;"],[2,"and your sons and your daughters will prophesy."],[2,"Your old men will dream dreams."],[2,"Your young men will see visions."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"And also on the servants and on the handmaids in those days,"],[2,"I will pour out my Spirit."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"I will show wonders in the heavens and on the earth:"],[2,"blood, fire, and pillars of smoke."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[1,"The sun will be turned into darkness,"],[2,"and the moon into blood,"],[2,"before the great and terrible day of the LORD comes."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"It will happen that whoever will call on the LORD\u2019s name shall be saved;"],[2,"for in Mount Zion and in Jerusalem there will be those who escape,"],[2,"as the LORD has said,"],[2,"and among the remnant, those whom the LORD calls."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor, behold, in those days,"],[2,"and in that time,"],[2,"when I restore the fortunes of Judah and Jerusalem,"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"I will gather all nations,"],[2,"and will bring them down into the valley of Jehoshaphat;"],[2,"and I will execute judgment on them there for my people,"],[2,"and for my heritage, Israel, whom they have scattered among the nations."],[2,"They have divided my land,"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"and have cast lots for my people,"],[2,"and have given a boy for a prostitute,"],[2,"and sold a girl for wine, that they may drink."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cYes, and what are you to me, Tyre and Sidon,"],[2,"and all the regions of Philistia?"],[1,"Will you repay me?"],[2,"And if you repay me,"],[2,"I will swiftly and speedily return your repayment on your own head."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Because you have taken my silver and my gold,"],[2,"and have carried my finest treasures into your temples,"]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"and have sold the children of Judah and the children of Jerusalem to the sons of the Greeks,"],[2,"that you may remove them far from their border."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I will stir them up out of the place where you have sold them,"],[2,"and will return your repayment on your own head;"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"and I will sell your sons and your daughters into the hands of the children of Judah,"],[2,"and they will sell them to the men of Sheba,"],[2,"to a faraway nation,"],[2,"for the LORD has spoken it.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Proclaim this among the nations:"],[2,"\u201cPrepare for war!"],[2,"Stir up the mighty men."],[1,"Let all the warriors draw near."],[2,"Let them come up."]]},{v:10,l:[[2,"Beat your plowshares into swords,"],[2,"and your pruning hooks into spears."],[2,"Let the weak say, \u2018I am strong.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Hurry and come, all you surrounding nations,"],[2,"and gather yourselves together.\u201d"],[1,"Cause your mighty ones to come down there, LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cLet the nations arouse themselves,"],[2,"and come up to the valley of Jehoshaphat;"],[2,"for there I will sit to judge all the surrounding nations."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Put in the sickle;"],[2,"for the harvest is ripe."],[2,"Come, tread, for the wine press is full,"],[2,"the vats overflow, for their wickedness is great.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Multitudes, multitudes in the valley of decision!"],[2,"For the day of the LORD is near in the valley of decision."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The sun and the moon are darkened,"],[2,"and the stars withdraw their shining."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will roar from Zion,"],[2,"and thunder from Jerusalem;"],[2,"and the heavens and the earth will shake;"],[2,"but the LORD will be a refuge to his people,"],[2,"and a stronghold to the children of Israel."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cSo you will know that I am the LORD, your God,"],[2,"dwelling in Zion, my holy mountain."],[1,"Then Jerusalem will be holy,"],[2,"and no strangers will pass through her any more."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"It will happen in that day,"],[2,"that the mountains will drop down sweet wine,"],[2,"the hills will flow with milk,"],[2,"all the brooks of Judah will flow with waters;"],[2,"and a fountain will flow out from the LORD\u2019s house,"],[2,"and will water the valley of Shittim."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"Egypt will be a desolation"],[2,"and Edom will be a desolate wilderness,"],[2,"for the violence done to the children of Judah,"],[2,"because they have shed innocent blood in their land."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"But Judah will be inhabited forever,"],[2,"and Jerusalem from generation to generation."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cleanse their blood"],[2,"that I have not cleansed,"],[2,"for the LORD dwells in Zion.\u201d"]]}]]}},1300,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,s,n){h.exports={book:"Amos",name:"Amos",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The words of Amos, who was among the herdsmen of Tekoa, which he saw concerning Israel in the days of Uzziah king of Judah and in the days of Jeroboam the son of Joash, king of Israel, two years before the earthquake."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said:"],[1,"\u201cThe LORD will roar from Zion,"],[2,"and utter his voice from Jerusalem;"],[1,"and the pastures of the shepherds will mourn,"],[2,"and the top of Carmel will wither.\u201d"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of Damascus, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment,"],[2,"because they have threshed Gilead with threshing instruments of iron;"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"but I will send a fire into the house of Hazael,"],[2,"and it will devour the palaces of Ben Hadad."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"I will break the bar of Damascus,"],[2,"and cut off the inhabitant from the valley of Aven,"],[2,"and him who holds the scepter from the house of Eden;"],[2,"and the people of Syria shall go into captivity to Kir,\u201d"],[0,"says the LORD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of Gaza, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment,"],[2,"because they carried away captive the whole community,"],[2,"to deliver them up to Edom;"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"but I will send a fire on the wall of Gaza,"],[2,"and it will devour its palaces."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cut off the inhabitant from Ashdod,"],[2,"and him who holds the scepter from Ashkelon;"],[1,"and I will turn my hand against Ekron;"],[2,"and the remnant of the Philistines will perish,\u201d"],[0,"says the Lord GOD."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of Tyre, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment;"],[2,"because they delivered up the whole community to Edom,"],[2,"and didn\u2019t remember the brotherly covenant;"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"but I will send a fire on the wall of Tyre,"],[2,"and it will devour its palaces.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of Edom, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment,"],[2,"because he pursued his brother with the sword"],[2,"and cast off all pity,"],[2,"and his anger raged continually,"],[2,"and he kept his wrath forever;"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"but I will send a fire on Teman,"],[2,"and it will devour the palaces of Bozrah.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of the children of Ammon, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment,"],[2,"because they have ripped open the pregnant women of Gilead,"],[2,"that they may enlarge their border."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"But I will kindle a fire in the wall of Rabbah,"],[2,"and it will devour its palaces,"],[2,"with shouting in the day of battle,"],[2,"with a storm in the day of the whirlwind;"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"and their king will go into captivity,"],[2,"he and his princes together,\u201d"],[0,"says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of Moab, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment,"],[2,"because he burned the bones of the king of Edom into lime;"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"but I will send a fire on Moab,"],[2,"and it will devour the palaces of Kerioth;"],[2,"and Moab will die with tumult, with shouting, and with the sound of the trumpet;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"and I will cut off the judge from among them,"],[2,"and will kill all its princes with him,\u201d"],[0,"says the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of Judah, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment,"],[2,"because they have rejected the LORD\u2019s law,"],[2,"and have not kept his statutes,"],[2,"and their lies have led them astray,"],[2,"after which their fathers walked;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"but I will send a fire on Judah,"],[2,"and it will devour the palaces of Jerusalem.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cFor three transgressions of Israel, yes, for four,"],[2,"I will not turn away its punishment,"],[2,"because they have sold the righteous for silver,"],[2,"and the needy for a pair of sandals;"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"They trample the heads of the poor into the dust of the earth"],[2,"and deny justice to the oppressed."],[1,"A man and his father use the same maiden, to profane my holy name."]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"They lay themselves down beside every altar on clothes taken in pledge."],[2,"In the house of their God they drink the wine of those who have been fined."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet I destroyed the Amorite before them,"],[2,"whose height was like the height of the cedars,"],[2,"and he was strong as the oaks;"],[2,"yet I destroyed his fruit from above,"],[2,"and his roots from beneath."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Also I brought you up out of the land of Egypt"],[2,"and led you forty years in the wilderness,"],[2,"to possess the land of the Amorite."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I raised up some of your sons for prophets,"],[2,"and some of your young men for Nazirites."],[1,"Isn\u2019t this true,"],[2,"you children of Israel?\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut you gave the Nazirites wine to drink,"],[2,"and commanded the prophets, saying, \u2018Don\u2019t prophesy!\u2019"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, I will crush you in your place,"],[2,"as a cart crushes that is full of grain."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Flight will perish from the swift."],[2,"The strong won\u2019t strengthen his force."],[2,"The mighty won\u2019t deliver himself."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"He who handles the bow won\u2019t stand."],[2,"He who is swift of foot won\u2019t escape."],[2,"He who rides the horse won\u2019t deliver himself."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"He who is courageous among the mighty"],[2,"will flee away naked on that day,\u201d"],[0,"says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Hear this word that the LORD has spoken against you, children of Israel, against the whole family which I brought up out of the land of Egypt, saying:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have chosen only you of all the families of the earth."],[2,"Therefore I will punish you for all of your sins.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Do two walk together,"],[2,"unless they have agreed?"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Will a lion roar in the thicket,"],[2,"when he has no prey?"],[1,"Does a young lion cry out of his den,"],[2,"if he has caught nothing?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Can a bird fall in a trap on the earth,"],[2,"where no snare is set for him?"],[1,"Does a snare spring up from the ground,"],[2,"when there is nothing to catch?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Does the trumpet alarm sound in a city,"],[2,"without the people being afraid?"],[1,"Does evil happen to a city,"],[2,"and the LORD hasn\u2019t done it?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Surely the Lord GOD will do nothing,"],[2,"unless he reveals his secret to his servants the prophets."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The lion has roared."],[2,"Who will not fear?"],[1,"The Lord GOD has spoken."],[2,"Who can but prophesy?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Proclaim in the palaces at Ashdod,"],[2,"and in the palaces in the land of Egypt,"],[1,"and say, \u201cAssemble yourselves on the mountains of Samaria,"],[2,"and see what unrest is in her,"],[2,"and what oppression is among them.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIndeed they don\u2019t know to do right,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cWho hoard plunder and loot in their palaces.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cAn adversary will overrun the land;"],[2,"and he will pull down your strongholds,"],[2,"and your fortresses will be plundered.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cAs the shepherd rescues out of the mouth of the lion two legs,"],[2,"or a piece of an ear,"],[2,"so shall the children of Israel be rescued who sit in Samaria on the corner of a couch,"],[2,"and on the silken cushions of a bed.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cListen, and testify against the house of Jacob,\u201d says the Lord GOD, the God of Armies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor in the day that I visit the transgressions of Israel on him,"],[2,"I will also visit the altars of Bethel;"],[2,"and the horns of the altar will be cut off,"],[2,"and fall to the ground."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will strike the winter house with the summer house;"],[2,"and the houses of ivory will perish,"],[2,"and the great houses will have an end,\u201d"],[0,"says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Listen to this word, you cows of Bashan, who are on the mountain of Samaria, who oppress the poor, who crush the needy, who tell their husbands, \u201cBring us drinks!\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The Lord GOD has sworn by his holiness,"],[2,"\u201cBehold, the days shall come on you that they will take you away with hooks,"],[2,"and the last of you with fish hooks."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"You will go out at the breaks in the wall,"],[2,"everyone straight before her;"],[2,"and you will cast yourselves into Harmon,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGo to Bethel, and sin;"],[2,"to Gilgal, and sin more."],[1,"Bring your sacrifices every morning,"],[2,"your tithes every three days,"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"offer a sacrifice of thanksgiving of that which is leavened,"],[2,"and proclaim free will offerings and brag about them;"],[2,"for this pleases you, you children of Israel,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI also have given you cleanness of teeth in all your cities,"],[2,"and lack of bread in every town;"],[2,"yet you haven\u2019t returned to me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI also have withheld the rain from you,"],[2,"when there were yet three months to the harvest;"],[2,"and I caused it to rain on one city,"],[2,"and caused it not to rain on another city."],[1,"One field was rained on,"],[2,"and the field where it didn\u2019t rain withered."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"So two or three cities staggered to one city to drink water,"],[2,"and were not satisfied;"],[2,"yet you haven\u2019t returned to me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI struck you with blight and mildew many times in your gardens and your vineyards,"],[2,"and the swarming locusts have devoured your fig trees and your olive trees;"],[2,"yet you haven\u2019t returned to me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI sent plagues among you like I did Egypt."],[2,"I have slain your young men with the sword,"],[2,"and have carried away your horses."],[1,"I filled your nostrils with the stench of your camp,"],[2,"yet you haven\u2019t returned to me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI have overthrown some of you,"],[2,"as when God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah,"],[2,"and you were like a burning stick plucked out of the fire;"],[2,"yet you haven\u2019t returned to me,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore I will do this to you, Israel;"],[2,"because I will do this to you,"],[2,"prepare to meet your God, Israel."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, he who forms the mountains, creates the wind, declares to man what is his thought,"],[2,"who makes the morning darkness, and treads on the high places of the earth:"],[2,"The LORD, the God of Armies, is his name.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Listen to this word which I take up for a lamentation over you, O house of Israel:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe virgin of Israel has fallen;"],[2,"She shall rise no more."],[1,"She is cast down on her land;"],[2,"there is no one to raise her up.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"For the Lord GOD says:"],[1,"\u201cThe city that went out a thousand shall have a hundred left,"],[2,"and that which went out one hundred shall have ten left to the house of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD says to the house of Israel:"],[1,"\u201cSeek me, and you will live;"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"but don\u2019t seek Bethel,"],[2,"nor enter into Gilgal,"],[2,"and don\u2019t pass to Beersheba;"],[1,"for Gilgal shall surely go into captivity,"],[2,"and Bethel shall come to nothing."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Seek the LORD, and you will live,"],[2,"lest he break out like fire in the house of Joseph,"],[2,"and it devour, and there be no one to quench it in Bethel."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You who turn justice to wormwood,"],[2,"and cast down righteousness to the earth!"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Seek him who made the Pleiades and Orion,"],[2,"and turns the shadow of death into the morning,"],[2,"and makes the day dark with night;"],[2,"who calls for the waters of the sea,"],[2,"and pours them out on the surface of the earth, the LORD is his name,"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"who brings sudden destruction on the strong,"],[2,"so that destruction comes on the fortress."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"They hate him who reproves in the gate,"],[2,"and they abhor him who speaks blamelessly."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore, because you trample on the poor and take taxes from him of wheat,"],[2,"you have built houses of cut stone, but you will not dwell in them."],[1,"You have planted pleasant vineyards,"],[2,"but you shall not drink their wine."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For I know how many are your offenses,"],[2,"and how great are your sins\u2014"],[2,"you who afflict the just,"],[2,"who take a bribe,"],[2,"and who turn away the needy in the courts."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore a prudent person keeps silent in such a time,"],[2,"for it is an evil time."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Seek good, and not evil,"],[2,"that you may live;"],[2,"and so the LORD, the God of Armies, will be with you,"],[2,"as you say."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"Hate evil, love good,"],[2,"and establish justice in the courts."],[2,"It may be that the LORD, the God of Armies, will be gracious to the remnant of Joseph.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD, the God of Armies, the Lord, says:"],[1,"\u201cWailing will be in all the wide ways."],[2,"They will say in all the streets, \u2018Alas! Alas!\u2019"],[2,"They will call the farmer to mourning,"],[2,"and those who are skillful in lamentation to wailing."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"In all vineyards there will be wailing,"],[2,"for I will pass through the middle of you,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWoe to you who desire the day of the LORD!"],[2,"Why do you long for the day of the LORD?"],[1,"It is darkness,"],[2,"and not light."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"As if a man fled from a lion,"],[2,"and a bear met him;"],[1,"or he went into the house and leaned his hand on the wall,"],[2,"and a snake bit him."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"Won\u2019t the day of the LORD be darkness, and not light?"],[2,"Even very dark, and no brightness in it?"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"I hate, I despise your feasts,"],[2,"and I can\u2019t stand your solemn assemblies."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, though you offer me your burnt offerings and meal offerings,"],[2,"I will not accept them;"],[2,"neither will I regard the peace offerings of your fat animals."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"Take away from me the noise of your songs!"],[2,"I will not listen to the music of your harps."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"But let justice roll on like rivers,"],[2,"and righteousness like a mighty stream."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDid you bring to me sacrifices and offerings in the wilderness forty years, house of Israel?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You also carried the tent of your king and the shrine of your images, the star of your god, which you made for yourselves."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Therefore I will cause you to go into captivity beyond Damascus,\u201d says the LORD, whose name is the God of Armies."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to those who are at ease in Zion,"],[2,"and to those who are secure on the mountain of Samaria,"],[2,"the notable men of the chief of the nations,"],[2,"to whom the house of Israel come!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Go to Calneh, and see."],[2,"From there go to Hamath the great."],[2,"Then go down to Gath of the Philistines."],[1,"Are they better than these kingdoms?"],[2,"Is their border greater than your border?"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Alas for you who put far away the evil day,"],[2,"and cause the seat of violence to come near,"]]},{v:4,l:[[2,"who lie on beds of ivory,"],[2,"and stretch themselves on their couches,"],[2,"and eat the lambs out of the flock,"],[2,"and the calves out of the middle of the stall,"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"who strum on the strings of a harp,"],[2,"who invent for themselves instruments of music, like David;"]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"who drink wine in bowls,"],[2,"and anoint themselves with the best oils,"],[2,"but they are not grieved for the affliction of Joseph."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore they will now go captive with the first who go captive."],[2,"The feasting and lounging will end."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe Lord GOD has sworn by himself,\u201d says the LORD, the God of Armies:"],[2,"\u201cI abhor the pride of Jacob,"],[2,"and detest his fortresses."],[2,"Therefore I will deliver up the city with all that is in it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"It will happen that if ten men remain in one house,"],[2,"they will die."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen a man\u2019s relative carries him, even he who burns him, to bring bodies out of the house, and asks him who is in the innermost parts of the house, \u2018Is there yet any with you?\u2019 And he says, \u2018No;\u2019 then he will say, \u2018Hush! Indeed we must not mention the LORD\u2019s name.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor, behold, the LORD commands, and the great house will be smashed to pieces,"],[2,"and the little house into bits."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Do horses run on the rocky crags?"],[2,"Does one plow there with oxen?"],[1,"But you have turned justice into poison,"],[2,"and the fruit of righteousness into bitterness,"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"you who rejoice in a thing of nothing, who say,"],[2,"\u2018Haven\u2019t we taken for ourselves horns by our own strength?\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"For, behold, I will raise up against you a nation, house of Israel,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD, the God of Armies;"],[2,"\u201cand they will afflict you from the entrance of Hamath to the brook of the Arabah.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus the Lord GOD showed me: behold, he formed locusts in the beginning of the shooting up of the latter growth; and behold, it was the latter growth after the king\u2019s harvest."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When they finished eating the grass of the land, then I said, \u201cLord GOD, forgive, I beg you! How could Jacob stand? For he is small.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD relented concerning this. \u201cIt shall not be,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus the Lord GOD showed me: behold, the Lord GOD called for judgment by fire; and it dried up the great deep, and would have devoured the land."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cLord GOD, stop, I beg you! How could Jacob stand? For he is small.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD relented concerning this. \u201cThis also shall not be,\u201d says the Lord GOD."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus he showed me: behold, the Lord stood beside a wall made by a plumb line, with a plumb line in his hand."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cAmos, what do you see?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cA plumb line.\u201d"],[0,"Then the Lord said, \u201cBehold, I will set a plumb line in the middle of my people Israel. I will not again pass by them any more."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The high places of Isaac will be desolate, the sanctuaries of Israel will be laid waste; and I will rise against the house of Jeroboam with the sword.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Amaziah the priest of Bethel sent to Jeroboam king of Israel, saying, \u201cAmos has conspired against you in the middle of the house of Israel. The land is not able to bear all his words."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For Amos says, \u2018Jeroboam will die by the sword, and Israel shall surely be led away captive out of his land.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Amaziah also said to Amos, \u201cYou seer, go, flee away into the land of Judah, and there eat bread, and prophesy there,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but don\u2019t prophesy again any more at Bethel; for it is the king\u2019s sanctuary, and it is a royal house!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Amos answered Amaziah, \u201cI was no prophet, neither was I a prophet\u2019s son, but I was a herdsman, and a farmer of sycamore figs;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and the LORD took me from following the flock, and the LORD said to me, \u2018Go, prophesy to my people Israel.\u2019"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Now therefore listen to the LORD\u2019s word: \u2018You say, Don\u2019t prophesy against Israel, and don\u2019t preach against the house of Isaac.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says: \u2018Your wife shall be a prostitute in the city, and your sons and your daughters shall fall by the sword, and your land shall be divided by line; and you yourself shall die in a land that is unclean, and Israel shall surely be led away captive out of his land.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus the Lord GOD showed me: behold, a basket of summer fruit."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cAmos, what do you see?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cA basket of summer fruit.\u201d"],[0,"Then the LORD said to me,"],[1,"\u201cThe end has come on my people Israel."],[2,"I will not again pass by them any more."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"The songs of the temple will be wailing in that day,\u201d says the Lord GOD."],[2,"\u201cThe dead bodies will be many. In every place they will throw them out with silence."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear this, you who desire to swallow up the needy,"],[2,"and cause the poor of the land to fail,"]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"saying, \u2018When will the new moon be gone, that we may sell grain?"],[2,"And the Sabbath, that we may market wheat,"],[2,"making the ephah small, and the shekel large,"],[2,"and dealing falsely with balances of deceit;"]],f:["1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel","a normal shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"that we may buy the poor for silver,"],[2,"and the needy for a pair of sandals,"],[2,"and sell the sweepings with the wheat?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD has sworn by the pride of Jacob,"],[2,"\u201cSurely I will never forget any of their works."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Won\u2019t the land tremble for this,"],[2,"and everyone mourn who dwells in it?"],[1,"Yes, it will rise up wholly like the River;"],[2,"and it will be stirred up and sink again, like the River of Egypt."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"It will happen in that day,\u201d says the Lord GOD,"],[2,"\u201cthat I will cause the sun to go down at noon,"],[2,"and I will darken the earth in the clear day."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I will turn your feasts into mourning,"],[2,"and all your songs into lamentation;"],[1,"and I will make you wear sackcloth on all your bodies,"],[2,"and baldness on every head."],[1,"I will make it like the mourning for an only son,"],[2,"and its end like a bitter day."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the days come,\u201d says the Lord GOD,"],[2,"\u201cthat I will send a famine in the land,"],[2,"not a famine of bread,"],[2,"nor a thirst for water,"],[2,"but of hearing the LORD\u2019s words."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They will wander from sea to sea,"],[2,"and from the north even to the east;"],[2,"they will run back and forth to seek the LORD\u2019s word,"],[2,"and will not find it."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"In that day the beautiful virgins"],[2,"and the young men will faint for thirst."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who swear by the sin of Samaria,"],[2,"and say, \u2018As your god, Dan, lives,\u2019"],[2,"and, \u2018As the way of Beersheba lives,\u2019"],[2,"they will fall, and never rise up again.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw the Lord standing beside the altar, and he said, \u201cStrike the tops of the pillars, that the thresholds may shake. Break them in pieces on the head of all of them. I will kill the last of them with the sword. Not one of them will flee away. Not one of them will escape."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Though they dig into Sheol, there my hand will take them; and though they climb up to heaven, there I will bring them down."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Though they hide themselves in the top of Carmel, I will search and take them out from there; and though they be hidden from my sight in the bottom of the sea, there I will command the serpent, and it will bite them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Though they go into captivity before their enemies, there I will command the sword, and it will kill them. I will set my eyes on them for evil, and not for good."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For the Lord, the GOD of Armies, is he who touches the land and it melts, and all who dwell in it will mourn; and it will rise up wholly like the River, and will sink again, like the River of Egypt."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"It is he who builds his rooms in the heavens, and has founded his vault on the earth; he who calls for the waters of the sea, and pours them out on the surface of the earth\u2014the LORD is his name."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Are you not like the children of the Ethiopians to me, children of Israel?\u201d says the LORD. \u201cHaven\u2019t I brought up Israel out of the land of Egypt, and the Philistines from Caphtor, and the Syrians from Kir?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Behold, the eyes of the Lord GOD are on the sinful kingdom, and I will destroy it from off the surface of the earth, except that I will not utterly destroy the house of Jacob,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cFor behold, I will command, and I will sift the house of Israel among all the nations as grain is sifted in a sieve, yet not the least kernel will fall on the earth."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All the sinners of my people will die by the sword, who say, \u2018Evil won\u2019t overtake nor meet us.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In that day I will raise up the tent of David who is fallen and close up its breaches, and I will raise up its ruins, and I will build it as in the days of old,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that they may possess the remnant of Edom and all the nations who are called by my name,\u201d says the LORD who does this."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, the days come,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthat the plowman shall overtake the reaper,"],[2,"and the one treading grapes him who sows seed;"],[2,"and sweet wine will drip from the mountains,"],[2,"and flow from the hills."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring my people Israel back from captivity,"],[2,"and they will rebuild the ruined cities, and inhabit them;"],[2,"and they will plant vineyards, and drink wine from them."],[1,"They shall also make gardens,"],[2,"and eat their fruit."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will plant them on their land,"],[2,"and they will no more be plucked up out of their land which I have given them,\u201d"],[2,"says the LORD your God."]]}]]}},1301,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,n,h,s){n.exports={book:"Obad",name:"Obadiah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The vision of Obadiah. This is what the Lord GOD says about Edom. We have heard news from the LORD, and an ambassador is sent among the nations, saying, \u201cArise, and let\u2019s rise up against her in battle."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d","When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, I have made you small among the nations. You are greatly despised."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The pride of your heart has deceived you, you who dwell in the clefts of the rock, whose habitation is high, who says in his heart, \u2018Who will bring me down to the ground?\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Though you mount on high as the eagle, and though your nest is set among the stars, I will bring you down from there,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cIf thieves came to you, if robbers by night\u2014oh, what disaster awaits you\u2014wouldn\u2019t they only steal until they had enough? If grape pickers came to you, wouldn\u2019t they leave some gleaning grapes?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"How Esau will be ransacked! How his hidden treasures are sought out!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"All the men of your alliance have brought you on your way, even to the border. The men who were at peace with you have deceived you, and prevailed against you. Friends who eat your bread lay a snare under you. There is no understanding in him.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWon\u2019t I in that day\u201d, says the LORD, \u201cdestroy the wise men out of Edom, and understanding out of the mountain of Esau?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Your mighty men, Teman, will be dismayed, to the end that everyone may be cut off from the mountain of Esau by slaughter."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the violence done to your brother Jacob, shame will cover you, and you will be cut off forever."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In the day that you stood on the other side, in the day that strangers carried away his substance and foreigners entered into his gates and cast lots for Jerusalem, even you were like one of them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But don\u2019t look down on your brother in the day of his disaster, and don\u2019t rejoice over the children of Judah in the day of their destruction. Don\u2019t speak proudly in the day of distress."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t enter into the gate of my people in the day of their calamity. Don\u2019t look down on their affliction in the day of their calamity, neither seize their wealth on the day of their calamity."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t stand in the crossroads to cut off those of his who escape. Don\u2019t deliver up those of his who remain in the day of distress."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For the day of the LORD is near all the nations! As you have done, it will be done to you. Your deeds will return upon your own head."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For as you have drunk on my holy mountain, so all the nations will drink continually. Yes, they will drink, swallow down, and will be as though they had not been."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But in Mount Zion, there will be those who escape, and it will be holy. The house of Jacob will possess their possessions."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The house of Jacob will be a fire, the house of Joseph a flame, and the house of Esau for stubble. They will burn among them and devour them. There will not be any remaining to the house of Esau.\u201d Indeed, the LORD has spoken."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Those of the South will possess the mountain of Esau, and those of the lowland, the Philistines. They will possess the field of Ephraim, and the field of Samaria. Benjamin will possess Gilead."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The captives of this army of the children of Israel, who are among the Canaanites, will possess even to Zarephath; and the captives of Jerusalem, who are in Sepharad, will possess the cities of the Negev."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Saviors will go up on Mount Zion to judge the mountains of Esau, and the kingdom will be the LORD\u2019s."]]}]]}},1302,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,i){h.exports={book:"Jonah",name:"Jonah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the LORD\u2019s word came to Jonah the son of Amittai, saying,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cArise, go to Nineveh, that great city, and preach against it, for their wickedness has come up before me.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jonah rose up to flee to Tarshish from the presence of the LORD. He went down to Joppa, and found a ship going to Tarshish; so he paid its fare, and went down into it, to go with them to Tarshish from the presence of the LORD."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But the LORD sent out a great wind on the sea, and there was a mighty storm on the sea, so that the ship was likely to break up."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then the mariners were afraid, and every man cried to his god. They threw the cargo that was in the ship into the sea to lighten the ship. But Jonah had gone down into the innermost parts of the ship and he was laying down, and was fast asleep."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So the ship master came to him, and said to him, \u201cWhat do you mean, sleeper? Arise, call on your God! Maybe your God will notice us, so that we won\u2019t perish.\u201d"]],f:["or, gods","or, gods"]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They all said to each other, \u201cCome! Let\u2019s cast lots, that we may know who is responsible for this evil that is on us.\u201d So they cast lots, and the lot fell on Jonah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then they asked him, \u201cTell us, please, for whose cause this evil is on us. What is your occupation? Where do you come from? What is your country? Of what people are you?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cI am a Hebrew, and I fear the LORD, the God of heaven, who has made the sea and the dry land.\u201d"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the men were exceedingly afraid, and said to him, \u201cWhat have you done?\u201d For the men knew that he was fleeing from the presence of the LORD, because he had told them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then they said to him, \u201cWhat shall we do to you, that the sea may be calm to us?\u201d For the sea grew more and more stormy."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cTake me up, and throw me into the sea. Then the sea will be calm for you; for I know that because of me this great storm is on you.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Nevertheless the men rowed hard to get them back to the land; but they could not, for the sea grew more and more stormy against them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore they cried to the LORD, and said, \u201cWe beg you, LORD, we beg you, don\u2019t let us die for this man\u2019s life, and don\u2019t lay on us innocent blood; for you, LORD, have done as it pleased you.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So they took up Jonah and threw him into the sea; and the sea ceased its raging."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then the men feared the LORD exceedingly; and they offered a sacrifice to the LORD and made vows."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD prepared a huge fish to swallow up Jonah, and Jonah was in the belly of the fish three days and three nights."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jonah prayed to the LORD, his God, out of the fish\u2019s belly."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said,"],[1,"\u201cI called because of my affliction to the LORD."],[2,"He answered me."],[1,"Out of the belly of Sheol I cried."],[2,"You heard my voice."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For you threw me into the depths,"],[2,"in the heart of the seas."],[1,"The flood was all around me."],[2,"All your waves and your billows passed over me."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"I said, \u2018I have been banished from your sight;"],[2,"yet I will look again toward your holy temple.\u2019"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"The waters surrounded me,"],[2,"even to the soul."],[1,"The deep was around me."],[2,"The weeds were wrapped around my head."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"I went down to the bottoms of the mountains."],[2,"The earth barred me in forever;"],[2,"yet you have brought my life up from the pit, LORD my God."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cWhen my soul fainted within me, I remembered the LORD."],[2,"My prayer came in to you, into your holy temple."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Those who regard vain idols forsake their own mercy."]]},{v:9,l:[[2,"But I will sacrifice to you with the voice of thanksgiving."],[2,"I will pay that which I have vowed."],[1,"Salvation belongs to the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD spoke to the fish, and it vomited out Jonah on the dry land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Jonah the second time, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cArise, go to Nineveh, that great city, and preach to it the message that I give you.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jonah arose, and went to Nineveh, according to the LORD\u2019s word. Now Nineveh was an exceedingly great city, three days\u2019 journey across."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Jonah began to enter into the city a day\u2019s journey, and he cried out, and said, \u201cIn forty days, Nineveh will be overthrown!\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The people of Nineveh believed God; and they proclaimed a fast and put on sackcloth, from their greatest even to their least."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The news reached the king of Nineveh, and he arose from his throne, took off his royal robe, covered himself with sackcloth, and sat in ashes."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He made a proclamation and published through Nineveh by the decree of the king and his nobles, saying, \u201cLet neither man nor animal, herd nor flock, taste anything; let them not feed, nor drink water;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but let them be covered with sackcloth, both man and animal, and let them cry mightily to God. Yes, let them turn everyone from his evil way and from the violence that is in his hands."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Who knows whether God will not turn and relent, and turn away from his fierce anger, so that we might not perish?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"God saw their works, that they turned from their evil way. God relented of the disaster which he said he would do to them, and he didn\u2019t do it."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But it displeased Jonah exceedingly, and he was angry."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He prayed to the LORD, and said, \u201cPlease, LORD, wasn\u2019t this what I said when I was still in my own country? Therefore I hurried to flee to Tarshish, for I knew that you are a gracious God and merciful, slow to anger, and abundant in loving kindness, and you relent of doing harm."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore now, LORD, take, I beg you, my life from me, for it is better for me to die than to live.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cIs it right for you to be angry?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jonah went out of the city and sat on the east side of the city, and there made himself a booth and sat under it in the shade, until he might see what would become of the city."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The LORD God prepared a vine and made it to come up over Jonah, that it might be a shade over his head to deliver him from his discomfort. So Jonah was exceedingly glad because of the vine."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But God prepared a worm at dawn the next day, and it chewed on the vine so that it withered."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When the sun arose, God prepared a sultry east wind; and the sun beat on Jonah\u2019s head, so that he was faint and requested for himself that he might die. He said, \u201cIt is better for me to die than to live.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"God said to Jonah, \u201cIs it right for you to be angry about the vine?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am right to be angry, even to death.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said, \u201cYou have been concerned for the vine, for which you have not labored, neither made it grow; which came up in a night and perished in a night."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Shouldn\u2019t I be concerned for Nineveh, that great city, in which are more than one hundred twenty thousand persons who can\u2019t discern between their right hand and their left hand, and also many animals?\u201d"]]}]]}},1303,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,h,i,l){h.exports={book:"Mic",name:"Micah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word that came to Micah of Morasheth in the days of Jotham, Ahaz, and Hezekiah, kings of Judah, which he saw concerning Samaria and Jerusalem."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, you peoples, all of you!"],[2,"Listen, O earth, and all that is therein."],[1,"Let the Lord GOD be witness against you,"],[2,"the Lord from his holy temple."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"For behold, the LORD comes out of his place,"],[2,"and will come down and tread on the high places of the earth."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains melt under him,"],[2,"and the valleys split apart like wax before the fire,"],[2,"like waters that are poured down a steep place."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAll this is for the disobedience of Jacob,"],[2,"and for the sins of the house of Israel."],[1,"What is the disobedience of Jacob?"],[2,"Isn\u2019t it Samaria?"],[1,"And what are the high places of Judah?"],[2,"Aren\u2019t they Jerusalem?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I will make Samaria like a rubble heap of the field,"],[2,"like places for planting vineyards;"],[1,"and I will pour down its stones into the valley,"],[2,"and I will uncover its foundations."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"All her idols will be beaten to pieces,"],[2,"all her temple gifts will be burned with fire,"],[2,"and I will destroy all her images;"],[1,"for of the hire of a prostitute has she gathered them,"],[2,"and to the hire of a prostitute shall they return.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"For this I will lament and wail."],[2,"I will go stripped and naked."],[2,"I will howl like the jackals"],[2,"and mourn like the ostriches."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"For her wounds are incurable;"],[2,"for it has come even to Judah."],[1,"It reaches to the gate of my people,"],[2,"even to Jerusalem."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t tell it in Gath."],[2,"Don\u2019t weep at all."],[2,"At Beth Ophrah I have rolled myself in the dust."]],f:["Beth Ophrah means literally \u201cHouse of Dust.\u201d"]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Pass on, inhabitant of Shaphir, in nakedness and shame."],[2,"The inhabitant of Zaanan won\u2019t come out."],[2,"The wailing of Beth Ezel will take from you his protection."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For the inhabitant of Maroth waits anxiously for good,"],[2,"because evil has come down from the LORD to the gate of Jerusalem."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Harness the chariot to the swift steed, inhabitant of Lachish."],[2,"She was the beginning of sin to the daughter of Zion;"],[2,"for the transgressions of Israel were found in you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore you will give a parting gift to Moresheth Gath."],[2,"The houses of Achzib will be a deceitful thing to the kings of Israel."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will yet bring a conqueror to you, inhabitants of Mareshah."],[2,"The glory of Israel will come to Adullam."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"Shave your heads,"],[2,"and cut off your hair for the children of your delight."],[1,"Enlarge your baldness like the vulture,"],[2,"for they have gone into captivity from you!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to those who devise iniquity"],[2,"and work evil on their beds!"],[1,"When the morning is light, they practice it,"],[2,"because it is in the power of their hand."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"They covet fields and seize them,"],[2,"and houses, then take them away."],[1,"They oppress a man and his house,"],[2,"even a man and his heritage."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore the LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I am planning against these people a disaster,"],[2,"from which you will not remove your necks,"],[2,"neither will you walk haughtily,"],[2,"for it is an evil time."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"In that day they will take up a parable against you,"],[2,"and lament with a doleful lamentation, saying,"],[2,"\u2018We are utterly ruined!"],[2,"My people\u2019s possession is divided up."],[2,"Indeed he takes it from me and assigns our fields to traitors!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore you will have no one who divides the land by lot in the LORD\u2019s assembly."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDon\u2019t prophesy!\u201d\u2014they prophesy\u2014"],[2,"\u201cDon\u2019t prophesy about these things."],[2,"Disgrace won\u2019t overtake us.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall it be said, O house of Jacob,"],[2,"\u201cIs the LORD\u2019s Spirit angry?"],[2,"Are these his doings?"],[2,"Don\u2019t my words do good to him who walks blamelessly?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But lately my people have risen up as an enemy."],[2,"You strip the robe and clothing from those who pass by without a care, returning from battle."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You drive the women of my people out from their pleasant houses;"],[2,"from their young children you take away my blessing forever."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise, and depart!"],[2,"For this is not your resting place,"],[2,"because of uncleanness that destroys,"],[2,"even with a grievous destruction."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"If a man walking in a spirit of falsehood lies, saying,"],[2,"\u201cI will prophesy to you of wine and of strong drink,\u201d"],[2,"he would be the prophet of this people."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will surely assemble all of you, Jacob."],[2,"I will surely gather the remnant of Israel."],[1,"I will put them together as the sheep of Bozrah,"],[2,"as a flock in the middle of their pasture."],[2,"They will swarm with people."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"He who breaks open the way goes up before them."],[2,"They break through the gate, and go out."],[2,"Their king passes on before them,"],[2,"with the LORD at their head."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I said,"],[1,"\u201cPlease listen, you heads of Jacob,"],[2,"and rulers of the house of Israel:"],[2,"Isn\u2019t it for you to know justice?"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"You who hate the good,"],[2,"and love the evil;"],[2,"who tear off their skin,"],[2,"and their flesh from off their bones;"]]},{v:3,l:[[2,"who also eat the flesh of my people,"],[2,"and peel their skin from off them,"],[2,"and break their bones,"],[2,"and chop them in pieces, as for the pot,"],[2,"and as meat within the cauldron."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Then they will cry to the LORD,"],[2,"but he will not answer them."],[1,"Yes, he will hide his face from them at that time,"],[2,"because they made their deeds evil.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says concerning the prophets who lead my people astray\u2014for those who feed their teeth, they proclaim, \u201cPeace!\u201d and whoever doesn\u2019t provide for their mouths, they prepare war against him:"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore night is over you, with no vision,"],[2,"and it is dark to you, that you may not divine;"],[2,"and the sun will go down on the prophets,"],[2,"and the day will be black over them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The seers shall be disappointed,"],[2,"and the diviners confounded."],[1,"Yes, they shall all cover their lips,"],[2,"for there is no answer from God.\u201d"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, I am full of power by the LORD\u2019s Spirit,"],[2,"and of judgment, and of might,"],[2,"to declare to Jacob his disobedience,"],[2,"and to Israel his sin."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Please listen to this, you heads of the house of Jacob,"],[2,"and rulers of the house of Israel,"],[2,"who abhor justice,"],[2,"and pervert all equity,"]]},{v:10,l:[[2,"who build up Zion with blood,"],[2,"and Jerusalem with iniquity."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Her leaders judge for bribes,"],[2,"and her priests teach for a price,"],[2,"and her prophets tell fortunes for money;"],[1,"yet they lean on the LORD, and say,"],[2,"\u201cIsn\u2019t the LORD among us?"],[2,"No disaster will come on us.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore Zion for your sake will be plowed like a field,"],[2,"and Jerusalem will become heaps of rubble,"],[2,"and the mountain of the temple like the high places of a forest."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"But in the latter days,"],[2,"it will happen that the mountain of the LORD\u2019s temple will be established on the top of the mountains,"],[2,"and it will be exalted above the hills;"],[2,"and peoples will stream to it."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Many nations will go and say,"],[2,"\u201cCome! Let\u2019s go up to the mountain of the LORD,"],[2,"and to the house of the God of Jacob;"],[2,"and he will teach us of his ways,"],[2,"and we will walk in his paths.\u201d"],[1,"For the law will go out of Zion,"],[2,"and the LORD\u2019s word from Jerusalem;"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"and he will judge between many peoples,"],[2,"and will decide concerning strong nations afar off."],[2,"They will beat their swords into plowshares,"],[2,"and their spears into pruning hooks."],[1,"Nation will not lift up sword against nation,"],[2,"neither will they learn war any more."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"But every man will sit under his vine and under his fig tree."],[2,"No one will make them afraid,"],[2,"for the mouth of the LORD of Armies has spoken."]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"Indeed all the nations may walk in the name of their gods,"],[2,"but we will walk in the name of the LORD our God forever and ever."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIn that day,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cI will assemble that which is lame,"],[2,"and I will gather that which is driven away,"],[2,"and that which I have afflicted;"]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"and I will make that which was lame a remnant,"],[2,"and that which was cast far off a strong nation:"],[2,"and the LORD will reign over them on Mount Zion from then on, even forever.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"You, tower of the flock, the hill of the daughter of Zion,"],[2,"to you it will come."],[1,"Yes, the former dominion will come,"],[2,"the kingdom of the daughter of Jerusalem."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Now why do you cry out aloud?"],[2,"Is there no king in you?"],[2,"Has your counselor perished,"],[2,"that pains have taken hold of you as of a woman in travail?"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Be in pain, and labor to give birth, daughter of Zion,"],[2,"like a woman in travail;"],[2,"for now you will go out of the city,"],[2,"and will dwell in the field,"],[2,"and will come even to Babylon."],[1,"There you will be rescued."],[2,"There the LORD will redeem you from the hand of your enemies."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Now many nations have assembled against you, that say,"],[2,"\u201cLet her be defiled,"],[2,"and let our eye gloat over Zion.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"But they don\u2019t know the thoughts of the LORD,"],[2,"neither do they understand his counsel;"],[2,"for he has gathered them like the sheaves to the threshing floor."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Arise and thresh, daughter of Zion,"],[2,"for I will make your horn iron,"],[2,"and I will make your hoofs bronze."],[1,"You will beat in pieces many peoples."],[1,"I will devote their gain to the LORD,"],[2,"and their substance to the Lord of the whole earth."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Now you shall gather yourself in troops,"],[2,"daughter of troops."],[1,"He has laid siege against us."],[2,"They will strike the judge of Israel with a rod on the cheek."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"But you, Bethlehem Ephrathah,"],[2,"being small among the clans of Judah,"],[2,"out of you one will come out to me who is to be ruler in Israel;"],[2,"whose goings out are from of old, from ancient times."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore he will abandon them until the time that she who is in labor gives birth."],[2,"Then the rest of his brothers will return to the children of Israel."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"He shall stand, and shall shepherd in the strength of the LORD,"],[2,"in the majesty of the name of the LORD his God."],[2,"They will live, for then he will be great to the ends of the earth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"He will be our peace when Assyria invades our land"],[2,"and when he marches through our fortresses,"],[2,"then we will raise against him seven shepherds,"],[2,"and eight leaders of men."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"They will rule the land of Assyria with the sword,"],[2,"and the land of Nimrod in its gates."],[1,"He will deliver us from the Assyrian,"],[2,"when he invades our land,"],[2,"and when he marches within our border."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"The remnant of Jacob will be among many peoples"],[2,"like dew from the LORD,"],[2,"like showers on the grass,"],[2,"that don\u2019t wait for man"],[2,"nor wait for the sons of men."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"The remnant of Jacob will be among the nations,"],[2,"among many peoples,"],[2,"like a lion among the animals of the forest,"],[2,"like a young lion among the flocks of sheep;"],[2,"who, if he goes through, treads down and tears in pieces,"],[2,"and there is no one to deliver."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your hand be lifted up above your adversaries,"],[2,"and let all of your enemies be cut off."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIt will happen in that day\u201d, says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201cthat I will cut off your horses from among you"],[2,"and will destroy your chariots."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cut off the cities of your land"],[2,"and will tear down all your strongholds."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will destroy witchcraft from your hand."],[2,"You shall have no soothsayers."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cut off your engraved images and your pillars from among you;"],[2,"and you shall no more worship the work of your hands."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"I will uproot your Asherah poles from among you;"],[2,"and I will destroy your cities."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"I will execute vengeance in anger"],[2,"and wrath on the nations that didn\u2019t listen.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Listen now to what the LORD says:"],[1,"\u201cArise, plead your case before the mountains,"],[2,"and let the hills hear what you have to say."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Hear, you mountains, the LORD\u2019s indictment,"],[2,"and you enduring foundations of the earth;"],[2,"for the LORD has a case against his people,"],[2,"and he will contend with Israel."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My people, what have I done to you?"],[2,"How have I burdened you?"],[2,"Answer me!"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"For I brought you up out of the land of Egypt,"],[2,"and redeemed you out of the house of bondage."],[2,"I sent before you Moses, Aaron, and Miriam."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"My people, remember now what Balak king of Moab devised,"],[2,"and what Balaam the son of Beor answered him from Shittim to Gilgal,"],[2,"that you may know the righteous acts of the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"How shall I come before the LORD,"],[2,"and bow myself before the exalted God?"],[1,"Shall I come before him with burnt offerings,"],[2,"with calves a year old?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Will the LORD be pleased with thousands of rams?"],[2,"With tens of thousands of rivers of oil?"],[1,"Shall I give my firstborn for my disobedience?"],[2,"The fruit of my body for the sin of my soul?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"He has shown you, O man, what is good."],[2,"What does the LORD require of you, but to act justly,"],[2,"to love mercy, and to walk humbly with your God?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD\u2019s voice calls to the city\u2014"],[2,"and wisdom fears your name\u2014"],[1,"\u201cListen to the rod,"],[2,"and he who appointed it."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Are there yet treasures of wickedness in the house of the wicked,"],[2,"and a short ephah that is accursed?"]],f:["An ephah is a measure of volume (about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel), and a short ephah is made smaller than a full ephah for the purpose of cheating customers."]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Shall I tolerate dishonest scales,"],[2,"and a bag of deceitful weights?"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Her rich men are full of violence,"],[2,"her inhabitants speak lies,"],[2,"and their tongue is deceitful in their speech."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I also have struck you with a grievous wound."],[2,"I have made you desolate because of your sins."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You shall eat, but not be satisfied."],[2,"Your hunger will be within you."],[2,"You will store up, but not save,"],[2,"and that which you save I will give up to the sword."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You will sow, but won\u2019t reap."],[2,"You will tread the olives, but won\u2019t anoint yourself with oil;"],[2,"and crush grapes, but won\u2019t drink the wine."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"For the statutes of Omri are kept,"],[2,"and all the works of Ahab\u2019s house."],[2,"You walk in their counsels,"],[2,"that I may make you a ruin,"],[2,"and your inhabitants a hissing."],[2,"You will bear the reproach of my people.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Misery is mine!"],[2,"Indeed, I am like one who gathers the summer fruits, as gleanings of the vineyard."],[2,"There is no cluster of grapes to eat."],[2,"My soul desires to eat the early fig."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"The godly man has perished out of the earth,"],[2,"and there is no one upright among men."],[2,"They all lie in wait for blood;"],[2,"every man hunts his brother with a net."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Their hands are on that which is evil to do it diligently."],[2,"The ruler and judge ask for a bribe."],[1,"The powerful man dictates the evil desire of his soul."],[2,"Thus they conspire together."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"The best of them is like a brier."],[2,"The most upright is worse than a thorn hedge."],[1,"The day of your watchmen,"],[2,"even your visitation, has come;"],[2,"now is the time of their confusion."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t trust in a neighbor."],[2,"Don\u2019t put confidence in a friend."],[2,"With the woman lying in your embrace,"],[2,"be careful of the words of your mouth!"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"For the son dishonors the father,"],[2,"the daughter rises up against her mother,"],[2,"the daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law;"],[2,"a man\u2019s enemies are the men of his own house."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"But as for me, I will look to the LORD."],[2,"I will wait for the God of my salvation."],[2,"My God will hear me."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t rejoice against me, my enemy."],[2,"When I fall, I will arise."],[2,"When I sit in darkness, the LORD will be a light to me."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bear the indignation of the LORD,"],[2,"because I have sinned against him,"],[2,"until he pleads my case and executes judgment for me."],[2,"He will bring me out to the light."],[2,"I will see his righteousness."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Then my enemy will see it,"],[2,"and shame will cover her who said to me,"],[2,"\u201cWhere is the LORD your God?\u201d"],[1,"My eyes will see her."],[2,"Now she will be trodden down like the mire of the streets."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"A day to build your walls!"],[2,"In that day, he will extend your boundary."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"In that day they will come to you from Assyria and the cities of Egypt,"],[2,"and from Egypt even to the River,"],[2,"and from sea to sea,"],[2,"and mountain to mountain."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Yet the land will be desolate because of those who dwell therein,"],[2,"for the fruit of their doings."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"Shepherd your people with your staff,"],[2,"the flock of your heritage,"],[2,"who dwell by themselves in a forest."],[1,"Let them feed in the middle of fertile pasture land,"],[2,"in Bashan and Gilead, as in the days of old."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAs in the days of your coming out of the land of Egypt,"],[2,"I will show them marvelous things.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The nations will see and be ashamed of all their might."],[2,"They will lay their hand on their mouth."],[2,"Their ears will be deaf."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"They will lick the dust like a serpent."],[2,"Like crawling things of the earth, they will come trembling out of their dens."],[2,"They will come with fear to the LORD our God,"],[2,"and will be afraid because of you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Who is a God like you, who pardons iniquity,"],[2,"and passes over the disobedience of the remnant of his heritage?"],[1,"He doesn\u2019t retain his anger forever,"],[2,"because he delights in loving kindness."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He will again have compassion on us."],[2,"He will tread our iniquities under foot."],[2,"You will cast all their sins into the depths of the sea."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"You will give truth to Jacob,"],[2,"and mercy to Abraham,"],[2,"as you have sworn to our fathers from the days of old."]]}]]}},1304,[]);
__d(function(e,o,a,t,s,h,r){s.exports={book:"Nah",name:"Nahum",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A revelation about Nineveh. The book of the vision of Nahum the Elkoshite."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD is a jealous God and avenges. The LORD avenges and is full of wrath. The LORD takes vengeance on his adversaries, and he maintains wrath against his enemies."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh).","The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The LORD is slow to anger, and great in power, and will by no means leave the guilty unpunished. The LORD has his way in the whirlwind and in the storm, and the clouds are the dust of his feet."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He rebukes the sea and makes it dry, and dries up all the rivers. Bashan and Carmel languish. The flower of Lebanon languishes."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The mountains quake before him, and the hills melt away. The earth trembles at his presence, yes, the world, and all who dwell in it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Who can stand before his indignation? Who can endure the fierceness of his anger? His wrath is poured out like fire, and the rocks are broken apart by him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The LORD is good, a stronghold in the day of trouble; and he knows those who take refuge in him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But with an overflowing flood, he will make a full end of her place, and will pursue his enemies into darkness."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"What do you plot against the LORD? He will make a full end. Affliction won\u2019t rise up the second time."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For entangled like thorns, and drunken as with their drink, they are consumed utterly like dry stubble."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"One has gone out of you who devises evil against the LORD, who counsels wickedness."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says: \u201cThough they are in full strength and likewise many, even so they will be cut down and pass away. Though I have afflicted you, I will afflict you no more."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now I will break his yoke from off you, and will burst your bonds apart.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD has commanded concerning you: \u201cNo more descendants will bear your name. Out of the house of your gods, I will cut off the engraved image and the molten image. I will make your grave, for you are vile.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, on the mountains the feet of him who brings good news, who publishes peace! Keep your feasts, Judah! Perform your vows, for the wicked one will no more pass through you. He is utterly cut off."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He who dashes in pieces has come up against you. Keep the fortress! Watch the way! Strengthen your waist! Fortify your power mightily!"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD restores the excellency of Jacob as the excellency of Israel, for the destroyers have destroyed them and ruined their vine branches."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The shield of his mighty men is made red. The valiant men are in scarlet. The chariots flash with steel in the day of his preparation, and the pine spears are brandished."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The chariots rage in the streets. They rush back and forth in the wide ways. Their appearance is like torches. They run like the lightnings."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He summons his picked troops. They stumble on their way. They dash to its wall, and the protective shield is put in place."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The gates of the rivers are opened, and the palace is dissolved."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It is decreed: she is uncovered, she is carried away; and her servants moan as with the voice of doves, beating on their breasts."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But Nineveh has been from of old like a pool of water, yet they flee away. \u201cStop! Stop!\u201d they cry, but no one looks back."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Take the plunder of silver. Take the plunder of gold, for there is no end of treasure, an abundance of every precious thing."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"She is empty, void, and waste. The heart melts, the knees knock together, their bodies and faces have grown pale."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Where is the den of the lions, and the feeding place of the young lions, where the lion and the lioness walked with the lion\u2019s cubs, and no one made them afraid?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The lion tore in pieces enough for his cubs, and strangled prey for his lionesses, and filled his caves with the kill and his dens with prey."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I am against you,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cand I will burn her chariots in the smoke, and the sword will devour your young lions; and I will cut off your prey from the earth, and the voice of your messengers will no longer be heard.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to the bloody city! It is all full of lies and robbery\u2014no end to the prey."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The noise of the whip, the noise of the rattling of wheels, prancing horses, and bounding chariots,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"the horseman charging, and the flashing sword, the glittering spear, and a multitude of slain, and a great heap of corpses, and there is no end of the bodies. They stumble on their bodies"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"because of the multitude of the prostitution of the alluring prostitute, the mistress of witchcraft, who sells nations through her prostitution, and families through her witchcraft."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I am against you,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cand I will lift your skirts over your face. I will show the nations your nakedness, and the kingdoms your shame."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I will throw abominable filth on you and make you vile, and will make you a spectacle."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It will happen that all those who look at you will flee from you, and say, \u2018Nineveh is laid waste! Who will mourn for her?\u2019 Where will I seek comforters for you?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Are you better than No-Amon, who was situated among the rivers, who had the waters around her, whose rampart was the sea, and her wall was of the sea?"]],f:["or, Thebes","or, Nile"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Cush and Egypt were her boundless strength. Put and Libya were her helpers."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Yet was she carried away. She went into captivity. Her young children also were dashed in pieces at the head of all the streets, and they cast lots for her honorable men, and all her great men were bound in chains."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"You also will be drunken. You will be hidden. You also will seek a stronghold because of the enemy."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"All your fortresses will be like fig trees with the first-ripe figs. If they are shaken, they fall into the mouth of the eater."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Behold, your troops among you are women. The gates of your land are set wide open to your enemies. The fire has devoured your bars."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Draw water for the siege. Strengthen your fortresses. Go into the clay, and tread the mortar. Make the brick kiln strong."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"There the fire will devour you. The sword will cut you off. It will devour you like the grasshopper. Multiply like grasshoppers. Multiply like the locust."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You have increased your merchants more than the stars of the skies. The grasshopper strips and flees away."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Your guards are like the locusts, and your officials like the swarms of locusts, which settle on the walls on a cold day, but when the sun appears, they flee away, and their place is not known where they are."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Your shepherds slumber, king of Assyria. Your nobles lie down. Your people are scattered on the mountains, and there is no one to gather them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"There is no healing your wound, for your injury is fatal. All who hear the report of you clap their hands over you, for who hasn\u2019t felt your endless cruelty?"]]}]]}},1305,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,h,i,n){h.exports={book:"Hab",name:"Habakkuk",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The revelation which Habakkuk the prophet saw."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"LORD, how long will I cry, and you will not hear? I cry out to you \u201cViolence!\u201d and will you not save?"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Why do you show me iniquity, and look at perversity? For destruction and violence are before me. There is strife, and contention rises up."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Therefore the law is paralyzed, and justice never prevails; for the wicked surround the righteous; therefore justice comes out perverted."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cLook among the nations, watch, and wonder marvelously; for I am working a work in your days which you will not believe though it is told you."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For, behold, I am raising up the Chaldeans, that bitter and hasty nation who march through the width of the earth, to possess dwelling places that are not theirs."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They are feared and dreaded. Their judgment and their dignity proceed from themselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Their horses also are swifter than leopards, and are more fierce than the evening wolves. Their horsemen press proudly on. Yes, their horsemen come from afar. They fly as an eagle that hurries to devour."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"All of them come for violence. Their hordes face forward. They gather prisoners like sand."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Yes, they scoff at kings, and princes are a derision to them. They laugh at every stronghold, for they build up an earthen ramp and take it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then they sweep by like the wind and go on. They are indeed guilty, whose strength is their god.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t you from everlasting, LORD my God, my Holy One? We will not die. LORD, you have appointed them for judgment. You, Rock, have established him to punish."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You who have purer eyes than to see evil, and who cannot look on perversity, why do you tolerate those who deal treacherously and keep silent when the wicked swallows up the man who is more righteous than he,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and make men like the fish of the sea, like the creeping things that have no ruler over them?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He takes up all of them with the hook. He catches them in his net and gathers them in his dragnet. Therefore he rejoices and is glad."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Therefore he sacrifices to his net and burns incense to his dragnet, because by them his life is luxurious and his food is good."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Will he therefore continually empty his net, and kill the nations without mercy?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I will stand at my watch and set myself on the ramparts, and will look out to see what he will say to me, and what I will answer concerning my complaint."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD answered me, \u201cWrite the vision, and make it plain on tablets, that he who runs may read it."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For the vision is yet for the appointed time, and it hurries toward the end, and won\u2019t prove false. Though it takes time, wait for it, because it will surely come. It won\u2019t delay."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, his soul is puffed up. It is not upright in him, but the righteous will live by his faith."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Yes, moreover, wine is treacherous: an arrogant man who doesn\u2019t stay at home, who enlarges his desire as Sheol; he is like death and can\u2019t be satisfied, but gathers to himself all nations and heaps to himself all peoples."]],f:["Sheol is the place of the dead."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Won\u2019t all these take up a parable against him, and a taunting proverb against him, and say, \u2018Woe to him who increases that which is not his, and who enriches himself by extortion! How long?\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Won\u2019t your debtors rise up suddenly, and wake up those who make you tremble, and you will be their victim?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Because you have plundered many nations, all the remnant of the peoples will plunder you because of men\u2019s blood, and for the violence done to the land, to the city and to all who dwell in it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to him who gets an evil gain for his house, that he may set his nest on high, that he may be delivered from the hand of evil!"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You have devised shame to your house by cutting off many peoples, and have sinned against your soul."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the stone will cry out of the wall, and the beam out of the woodwork will answer it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to him who builds a town with blood, and establishes a city by iniquity!"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Behold, isn\u2019t it from the LORD of Armies that the peoples labor for the fire, and the nations weary themselves for vanity?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For the earth will be filled with the knowledge of the LORD\u2019s glory, as the waters cover the sea."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to him who gives his neighbor drink, pouring your inflaming wine until they are drunk, so that you may gaze at their naked bodies!"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You are filled with shame, and not glory. You will also drink and be exposed! The cup of the LORD\u2019s right hand will come around to you, and disgrace will cover your glory."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For the violence done to Lebanon will overwhelm you, and the destruction of the animals will terrify you, because of men\u2019s blood and for the violence done to the land, to every city and to those who dwell in them."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhat value does the engraved image have, that its maker has engraved it; the molten image, even the teacher of lies, that he who fashions its form trusts in it, to make mute idols?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Woe to him who says to the wood, \u2018Awake!\u2019 or to the mute stone, \u2018Arise!\u2019 Shall this teach? Behold, it is overlaid with gold and silver, and there is no breath at all within it."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But the LORD is in his holy temple. Let all the earth be silent before him!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A prayer of Habakkuk, the prophet, set to victorious music."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"LORD, I have heard of your fame."],[2,"I stand in awe of your deeds, LORD."],[1,"Renew your work in the middle of the years."],[2,"In the middle of the years make it known."],[2,"In wrath, you remember mercy."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"God came from Teman,"],[2,"the Holy One from Mount Paran. Selah."],[1,"His glory covered the heavens,"],[2,"and his praise filled the earth."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"His splendor is like the sunrise."],[2,"Rays shine from his hand, where his power is hidden."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Plague went before him,"],[2,"and pestilence followed his feet."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"He stood, and shook the earth."],[2,"He looked, and made the nations tremble."],[2,"The ancient mountains were crumbled."],[2,"The age-old hills collapsed."],[2,"His ways are eternal."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I saw the tents of Cushan in affliction."],[2,"The dwellings of the land of Midian trembled."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Was the LORD displeased with the rivers?"],[2,"Was your anger against the rivers,"],[2,"or your wrath against the sea,"],[2,"that you rode on your horses,"],[2,"on your chariots of salvation?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You uncovered your bow."],[2,"You called for your sworn arrows. Selah."],[1,"You split the earth with rivers."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"The mountains saw you, and were afraid."],[2,"The storm of waters passed by."],[2,"The deep roared and lifted up its hands on high."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"The sun and moon stood still in the sky"],[2,"at the light of your arrows as they went,"],[2,"at the shining of your glittering spear."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You marched through the land in wrath."],[2,"You threshed the nations in anger."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"You went out for the salvation of your people,"],[2,"for the salvation of your anointed."],[1,"You crushed the head of the land of wickedness."],[2,"You stripped them head to foot. Selah."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"You pierced the heads of his warriors with their own spears."],[2,"They came as a whirlwind to scatter me,"],[2,"gloating as if to devour the wretched in secret."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"You trampled the sea with your horses,"],[2,"churning mighty waters."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"I heard, and my body trembled."],[2,"My lips quivered at the voice."],[1,"Rottenness enters into my bones, and I tremble in my place"],[2,"because I must wait quietly for the day of trouble,"],[2,"for the coming up of the people who invade us."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For even though the fig tree doesn\u2019t flourish,"],[2,"nor fruit be in the vines,"],[2,"the labor of the olive fails,"],[2,"the fields yield no food,"],[2,"the flocks are cut off from the fold,"],[2,"and there is no herd in the stalls,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"yet I will rejoice in the LORD."],[2,"I will be joyful in the God of my salvation!"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"GOD, the Lord, is my strength."],[2,"He makes my feet like deer\u2019s feet,"],[2,"and enables me to go in high places."],[0,"For the music director, on my stringed instruments."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]}]]}},1306,[]);
__d(function(e,t,a,o,h,i,l){h.exports={book:"Zeph",name:"Zephaniah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word which came to Zephaniah, the son of Cushi, the son of Gedaliah, the son of Amariah, the son of Hezekiah, in the days of Josiah, the son of Amon, king of Judah."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"I will utterly sweep away everything from the surface of the earth, says the LORD."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will sweep away man and animal. I will sweep away the birds of the sky, the fish of the sea, and the heaps of rubble with the wicked. I will cut off man from the surface of the earth, says the LORD."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will stretch out my hand against Judah and against all the inhabitants of Jerusalem. I will cut off the remnant of Baal from this place\u2014the name of the idolatrous and pagan priests,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"those who worship the army of the sky on the housetops, those who worship and swear by the LORD and also swear by Malcam,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"those who have turned back from following the LORD, and those who haven\u2019t sought the LORD nor inquired after him."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Be silent at the presence of the Lord GOD, for the day of the LORD is at hand. For the LORD has prepared a sacrifice. He has consecrated his guests."]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"It will happen in the day of the LORD\u2019s sacrifice that I will punish the princes, the king\u2019s sons, and all those who are clothed with foreign clothing."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"In that day, I will punish all those who leap over the threshold, who fill their master\u2019s house with violence and deceit."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day, says the LORD, there will be the noise of a cry from the fish gate, a wailing from the second quarter, and a great crashing from the hills."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Wail, you inhabitants of Maktesh, for all the people of Canaan are undone! All those who were loaded with silver are cut off."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"It will happen at that time, that I will search Jerusalem with lamps, and I will punish the men who are settled on their dregs, who say in their heart, \u201cThe LORD will not do good, neither will he do evil.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Their wealth will become a plunder, and their houses a desolation. Yes, they will build houses, but won\u2019t inhabit them. They will plant vineyards, but won\u2019t drink their wine."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The great day of the LORD is near. It is near and hurries greatly, the voice of the day of the LORD. The mighty man cries there bitterly."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"That day is a day of wrath, a day of distress and anguish, a day of trouble and ruin, a day of darkness and gloom, a day of clouds and blackness,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"a day of the trumpet and alarm against the fortified cities and against the high battlements."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I will bring such distress on men that they will walk like blind men because they have sinned against the LORD. Their blood will be poured out like dust and their flesh like dung."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Neither their silver nor their gold will be able to deliver them in the day of the LORD\u2019s wrath, but the whole land will be devoured by the fire of his jealousy; for he will make an end, yes, a terrible end, of all those who dwell in the land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Gather yourselves together, yes, gather together, you nation that has no shame,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"before the appointed time when the day passes as the chaff, before the fierce anger of the LORD comes on you, before the day of the LORD\u2019s anger comes on you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Seek the LORD, all you humble of the land, who have kept his ordinances. Seek righteousness. Seek humility. It may be that you will be hidden in the day of the LORD\u2019s anger."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For Gaza will be forsaken, and Ashkelon a desolation. They will drive out Ashdod at noonday, and Ekron will be rooted up."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Woe to the inhabitants of the sea coast, the nation of the Cherethites! The LORD\u2019s word is against you, Canaan, the land of the Philistines. I will destroy you until there is no inhabitant."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The sea coast will be pastures, with cottages for shepherds and folds for flocks."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The coast will be for the remnant of the house of Judah. They will find pasture. In the houses of Ashkelon, they will lie down in the evening, for the LORD, their God, will visit them and restore them."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I have heard the reproach of Moab and the insults of the children of Ammon, with which they have reproached my people and magnified themselves against their border."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore, as I live, says the LORD of Armies, the God of Israel, surely Moab will be as Sodom, and the children of Ammon as Gomorrah, a possession of nettles and salt pits, and a perpetual desolation. The remnant of my people will plunder them, and the survivors of my nation will inherit them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"This they will have for their pride, because they have reproached and magnified themselves against the people of the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The LORD will be awesome to them, for he will famish all the gods of the land. Men will worship him, everyone from his place, even all the shores of the nations."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"You Cushites also, you will be killed by my sword."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He will stretch out his hand against the north, destroy Assyria, and will make Nineveh a desolation, as dry as the wilderness."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Herds will lie down in the middle of her, all kinds of animals. Both the pelican and the porcupine will lodge in its capitals. Their calls will echo through the windows. Desolation will be in the thresholds, for he has laid bare the cedar beams."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"This is the joyous city that lived carelessly, that said in her heart, \u201cI am, and there is no one besides me.\u201d How she has become a desolation, a place for animals to lie down in! Everyone who passes by her will hiss and shake their fists."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Woe to her who is rebellious and polluted, the oppressing city!"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"She didn\u2019t obey the voice. She didn\u2019t receive correction. She didn\u2019t trust in the LORD. She didn\u2019t draw near to her God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Her princes within her are roaring lions. Her judges are evening wolves. They leave nothing until the next day."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Her prophets are arrogant and treacherous people. Her priests have profaned the sanctuary. They have done violence to the law."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The LORD, within her, is righteous. He will do no wrong. Every morning he brings his justice to light. He doesn\u2019t fail, but the unjust know no shame."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I have cut off nations. Their battlements are desolate. I have made their streets waste, so that no one passes by. Their cities are destroyed, so that there is no man, so that there is no inhabitant."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I said, \u201cJust fear me. Receive correction,\u201d so that her dwelling won\u2019t be cut off, according to all that I have appointed concerning her. But they rose early and corrupted all their doings."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore wait for me\u201d, says the LORD, \u201cuntil the day that I rise up to the prey, for my determination is to gather the nations, that I may assemble the kingdoms to pour on them my indignation, even all my fierce anger, for all the earth will be devoured with the fire of my jealousy."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"For then I will purify the lips of the peoples, that they may all call on the LORD\u2019s name, to serve him shoulder to shoulder."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"From beyond the rivers of Cush, my worshipers, even the daughter of my dispersed people, will bring my offering."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In that day you will not be disappointed for all your doings in which you have transgressed against me; for then I will take away out from among you your proudly exulting ones, and you will no more be arrogant in my holy mountain."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But I will leave among you an afflicted and poor people, and they will take refuge in the LORD\u2019s name."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The remnant of Israel will not do iniquity nor speak lies, neither will a deceitful tongue be found in their mouth, for they will feed and lie down, and no one will make them afraid.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Sing, daughter of Zion! Shout, Israel! Be glad and rejoice with all your heart, daughter of Jerusalem."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The LORD has taken away your judgments. He has thrown out your enemy. The King of Israel, the LORD, is among you. You will not be afraid of evil any more."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"In that day, it will be said to Jerusalem, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, Zion. Don\u2019t let your hands be weak.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The LORD, your God, is among you, a mighty one who will save. He will rejoice over you with joy. He will calm you in his love. He will rejoice over you with singing."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I will remove those who grieve about the appointed feasts from you. They are a burden and a reproach to you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Behold, at that time I will deal with all those who afflict you; and I will save those who are lame and gather those who were driven away. I will give them praise and honor, whose shame has been in all the earth."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:20,l:[[0,"At that time I will bring you in, and at that time I will gather you; for I will give you honor and praise among all the peoples of the earth when I restore your fortunes before your eyes, says the LORD."]]}]]}},1307,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,s,n){a.exports={book:"Hag",name:"Haggai",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the second year of Darius the king, in the sixth month, in the first day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came by Haggai the prophet, to Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest, saying,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is what the LORD of Armies says: These people say, \u2018The time hasn\u2019t yet come, the time for the LORD\u2019s house to be built.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s word came by Haggai the prophet, saying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cIs it a time for you yourselves to dwell in your paneled houses, while this house lies waste?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now therefore this is what the LORD of Armies says: \u2018Consider your ways."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You have sown much, and bring in little. You eat, but you don\u2019t have enough. You drink, but you aren\u2019t filled with drink. You clothe yourselves, but no one is warm; and he who earns wages earns wages to put them into a bag with holes in it.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is what the LORD of Armies says: \u2018Consider your ways."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Go up to the mountain, bring wood, and build the house. I will take pleasure in it, and I will be glorified,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cYou looked for much, and, behold, it came to little; and when you brought it home, I blew it away. Why?\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cBecause of my house that lies waste, while each of you is busy with his own house."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore for your sake the heavens withhold the dew, and the earth withholds its fruit."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I called for a drought on the land, on the mountains, on the grain, on the new wine, on the oil, on that which the ground produces, on men, on livestock, and on all the labor of the hands.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel and Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest, with all the remnant of the people, obeyed the LORD their God\u2019s voice, and the words of Haggai the prophet, as the LORD their God had sent him; and the people feared the LORD."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Haggai, the LORD\u2019s messenger, spoke the LORD\u2019s message to the people, saying, \u201cI am with you,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD stirred up the spirit of Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and the spirit of Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest, and the spirit of all the remnant of the people; and they came and worked on the house of the LORD of Armies, their God,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"in the twenty-fourth day of the month, in the sixth month, in the second year of Darius the king."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the seventh month, in the twenty-first day of the month, the LORD\u2019s word came by Haggai the prophet, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak now to Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and to Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest, and to the remnant of the people, saying,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u2018Who is left among you who saw this house in its former glory? How do you see it now? Isn\u2019t it in your eyes as nothing?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Yet now be strong, Zerubbabel,\u2019 says the LORD. \u2018Be strong, Joshua son of Jehozadak, the high priest. Be strong, all you people of the land,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018and work, for I am with you,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"This is the word that I covenanted with you when you came out of Egypt, and my Spirit lived among you. \u2018Don\u2019t be afraid.\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For this is what the LORD of Armies says: \u2018Yet once more, it is a little while, and I will shake the heavens, the earth, the sea, and the dry land;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and I will shake all nations. The treasure of all nations will come, and I will fill this house with glory, says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The silver is mine, and the gold is mine,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u2018The latter glory of this house will be greater than the former,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies; \u2018and in this place I will give peace,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"In the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, in the second year of Darius, the LORD\u2019s word came by Haggai the prophet, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies says: Ask now the priests concerning the law, saying,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u2018If someone carries holy meat in the fold of his garment, and with his fold touches bread, stew, wine, oil, or any food, will it become holy?\u2019\u201d"],[0,"The priests answered, \u201cNo.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Haggai said, \u201cIf one who is unclean by reason of a dead body touches any of these, will it be unclean?\u201d"],[0,"The priests answered, \u201cIt will be unclean.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Haggai answered, \u201c\u2018So is this people, and so is this nation before me,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018and so is every work of their hands. That which they offer there is unclean."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now, please consider from this day and backward, before a stone was laid on a stone in the LORD\u2019s temple."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Through all that time, when one came to a heap of twenty measures, there were only ten. When one came to the wine vat to draw out fifty, there were only twenty."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I struck you with blight, mildew, and hail in all the work of your hands; yet you didn\u2019t turn to me,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u2018Consider, please, from this day and backward, from the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, since the day that the foundation of the LORD\u2019s temple was laid, consider it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Is the seed yet in the barn? Yes, the vine, the fig tree, the pomegranate, and the olive tree haven\u2019t produced. From today I will bless you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came the second time to Haggai in the twenty-fourth day of the month, saying,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to Zerubbabel, governor of Judah, saying, \u2018I will shake the heavens and the earth."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I will overthrow the throne of kingdoms. I will destroy the strength of the kingdoms of the nations. I will overthrow the chariots and those who ride in them. The horses and their riders will come down, everyone by the sword of his brother."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"In that day, says the LORD of Armies, I will take you, Zerubbabel my servant, the son of Shealtiel,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018and will make you like a signet ring, for I have chosen you,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies.\u201d"]]}]]}},1308,[]);
__d(function(e,t,h,a,o,i,s){o.exports={book:"Zech",name:"Zechariah",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the eighth month, in the second year of Darius, the LORD\u2019s word came to the prophet Zechariah the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo, saying,"]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD was very displeased with your fathers."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore tell them, the LORD of Armies says: \u2018Return to me,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies, \u2018and I will return to you,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you be like your fathers, to whom the former prophets proclaimed, saying: The LORD of Armies says, \u2018Return now from your evil ways and from your evil doings;\u2019 but they didn\u2019t hear nor listen to me, says the LORD."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Your fathers, where are they? And the prophets, do they live forever?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But my words and my decrees, which I commanded my servants the prophets, didn\u2019t they overtake your fathers?"],[0,"\u201cThen they repented and said, \u2018Just as the LORD of Armies determined to do to us, according to our ways and according to our practices, so he has dealt with us.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"On the twenty-fourth day of the eleventh month, which is the month Shebat, in the second year of Darius, the LORD\u2019s word came to the prophet Zechariah the son of Berechiah, the son of Iddo, saying,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"\u201cI had a vision in the night, and behold, a man riding on a red horse, and he stood among the myrtle trees that were in a ravine; and behind him there were red, brown, and white horses."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then I asked, \u2018My lord, what are these?\u2019\u201d"],[0,"The angel who talked with me said to me, \u201cI will show you what these are.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The man who stood among the myrtle trees answered, \u201cThey are the ones the LORD has sent to go back and forth through the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"They reported to the LORD\u2019s angel who stood among the myrtle trees, and said, \u201cWe have walked back and forth through the earth, and behold, all the earth is at rest and in peace.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the LORD\u2019s angel replied, \u201cO LORD of Armies, how long will you not have mercy on Jerusalem and on the cities of Judah, against which you have had indignation these seventy years?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD answered the angel who talked with me with kind and comforting words."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So the angel who talked with me said to me, \u201cProclaim, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies says: \u201cI am jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion with a great jealousy."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I am very angry with the nations that are at ease; for I was but a little displeased, but they added to the calamity.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Therefore the LORD says: \u201cI have returned to Jerusalem with mercy. My house shall be built in it,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cand a line shall be stretched out over Jerusalem.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cProclaim further, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies says: \u201cMy cities will again overflow with prosperity, and the LORD will again comfort Zion, and will again choose Jerusalem.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"I lifted up my eyes and saw, and behold, four horns."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I asked the angel who talked with me, \u201cWhat are these?\u201d"],[0,"He answered me, \u201cThese are the horns which have scattered Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD showed me four craftsmen."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then I asked, \u201cWhat are these coming to do?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cThese are the horns which scattered Judah, so that no man lifted up his head; but these have come to terrify them, to cast down the horns of the nations that lifted up their horn against the land of Judah to scatter it.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I lifted up my eyes, and saw, and behold, a man with a measuring line in his hand."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then I asked, \u201cWhere are you going?\u201d"],[0,"He said to me, \u201cTo measure Jerusalem, to see what is its width and what is its length.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the angel who talked with me went out, and another angel went out to meet him,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cRun, speak to this young man, saying, \u2018Jerusalem will be inhabited as villages without walls, because of the multitude of men and livestock in it."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For I,\u2019 says the LORD, \u2018will be to her a wall of fire around it, and I will be the glory in the middle of her."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Come! Come! Flee from the land of the north,\u2019 says the LORD; \u2018for I have spread you abroad as the four winds of the sky,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u2018Come, Zion! Escape, you who dwell with the daughter of Babylon.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies says: \u2018For honor he has sent me to the nations which plundered you; for he who touches you touches the apple of his eye."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For, behold, I will shake my hand over them, and they will be a plunder to those who served them; and you will know that the LORD of Armies has sent me."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Sing and rejoice, daughter of Zion! For behold, I come and I will dwell within you,\u2019 says the LORD."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Many nations shall join themselves to the LORD in that day, and shall be my people; and I will dwell among you, and you shall know that the LORD of Armies has sent me to you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD will inherit Judah as his portion in the holy land, and will again choose Jerusalem."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Be silent, all flesh, before the LORD; for he has roused himself from his holy habitation!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He showed me Joshua the high priest standing before the LORD\u2019s angel, and Satan standing at his right hand to be his adversary."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD said to Satan, \u201cThe LORD rebuke you, Satan! Yes, the LORD who has chosen Jerusalem rebuke you! Isn\u2019t this a burning stick plucked out of the fire?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Joshua was clothed with filthy garments, and was standing before the angel."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He answered and spoke to those who stood before him, saying, \u201cTake the filthy garments off him.\u201d To him he said, \u201cBehold, I have caused your iniquity to pass from you, and I will clothe you with rich clothing.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"I said, \u201cLet them set a clean turban on his head.\u201d"],[0,"So they set a clean turban on his head, and clothed him; and the LORD\u2019s angel was standing by."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s angel solemnly assured Joshua, saying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u201cThe LORD of Armies says: \u2018If you will walk in my ways, and if you will follow my instructions, then you also shall judge my house, and shall also keep my courts, and I will give you a place of access among these who stand by."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Hear now, Joshua the high priest, you and your fellows who sit before you, for they are men who are a sign; for, behold, I will bring out my servant, the Branch."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For, behold, the stone that I have set before Joshua: on one stone are seven eyes; behold, I will engrave its inscription,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies, \u2018and I will remove the iniquity of that land in one day."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"In that day,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies, \u2018you will invite every man his neighbor under the vine and under the fig tree.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The angel who talked with me came again and wakened me, as a man who is wakened out of his sleep."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cWhat do you see?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cI have seen, and behold, a lamp stand all of gold, with its bowl on the top of it, and its seven lamps on it; there are seven pipes to each of the lamps which are on the top of it;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and two olive trees by it, one on the right side of the bowl, and the other on the left side of it.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I answered and spoke to the angel who talked with me, saying, \u201cWhat are these, my lord?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the angel who talked with me answered me, \u201cDon\u2019t you know what these are?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cNo, my lord.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he answered and spoke to me, saying, \u201cThis is the LORD\u2019s word to Zerubbabel, saying, \u2018Not by might, nor by power, but by my Spirit,\u2019 says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Who are you, great mountain? Before Zerubbabel you are a plain; and he will bring out the capstone with shouts of \u2018Grace, grace, to it!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover the LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cThe hands of Zerubbabel have laid the foundation of this house. His hands shall also finish it; and you will know that the LORD of Armies has sent me to you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Indeed, who despises the day of small things? For these seven shall rejoice, and shall see the plumb line in the hand of Zerubbabel. These are the LORD\u2019s eyes, which run back and forth through the whole earth.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I asked him, \u201cWhat are these two olive trees on the right side of the lamp stand and on the left side of it?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I asked him the second time, \u201cWhat are these two olive branches, which are beside the two golden spouts that pour the golden oil out of themselves?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered me, \u201cDon\u2019t you know what these are?\u201d"],[0,"I said, \u201cNo, my lord.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said, \u201cThese are the two anointed ones who stand by the Lord of the whole earth.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then again I lifted up my eyes and saw, and behold, a flying scroll."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cWhat do you see?\u201d"],[0,"I answered, \u201cI see a flying scroll; its length is twenty cubits, and its width ten cubits.\u201d"]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to me, \u201cThis is the curse that goes out over the surface of the whole land, for everyone who steals shall be cut off according to it on the one side; and everyone who swears falsely shall be cut off according to it on the other side."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I will cause it to go out,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cand it will enter into the house of the thief, and into the house of him who swears falsely by my name; and it will remain in the middle of his house, and will destroy it with its timber and its stones.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the angel who talked with me came forward and said to me, \u201cLift up now your eyes and see what this is that is appearing.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I said, \u201cWhat is it?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cThis is the ephah basket that is appearing.\u201d He said moreover, \u201cThis is their appearance in all the land\u2014"]],f:["An ephah is a measure of volume of about 22 liters, 5.8 U. S. gallons, or about 2/3 of a bushel."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and behold, a lead cover weighing one talent was lifted up\u2014and there was a woman sitting in the middle of the ephah basket.\u201d"]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds.","1 ephah is about 22 liters or about 2/3 of a bushel"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThis is Wickedness;\u201d and he threw her down into the middle of the ephah basket; and he threw the lead weight on its mouth."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I lifted up my eyes and saw, and behold, there were two women; and the wind was in their wings. Now they had wings like the wings of a stork, and they lifted up the ephah basket between earth and the sky."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Then I said to the angel who talked with me, \u201cWhere are these carrying the ephah basket?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cTo build her a house in the land of Shinar. When it is prepared, she will be set there in her own place.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Again I lifted up my eyes, and saw, and behold, four chariots came out from between two mountains; and the mountains were mountains of bronze."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In the first chariot were red horses. In the second chariot were black horses."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In the third chariot were white horses. In the fourth chariot were dappled horses, all of them powerful."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then I asked the angel who talked with me, \u201cWhat are these, my lord?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The angel answered me, \u201cThese are the four winds of the sky, which go out from standing before the Lord of all the earth."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The one with the black horses goes out toward the north country; and the white went out after them; and the dappled went out toward the south country.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The strong went out, and sought to go that they might walk back and forth through the earth. He said, \u201cGo around and through the earth!\u201d So they walked back and forth through the earth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he called to me, and spoke to me, saying, \u201cBehold, those who go toward the north country have quieted my spirit in the north country.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to me, saying,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cTake of them of the captivity, even of Heldai, of Tobijah, and of Jedaiah; and come the same day, and go into the house of Josiah the son of Zephaniah, where they have come from Babylon."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Yes, take silver and gold, and make crowns, and set them on the head of Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and speak to him, saying, \u2018The LORD of Armies says, \u201cBehold, the man whose name is the Branch! He will grow up out of his place; and he will build the LORD\u2019s temple."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He will build the LORD\u2019s temple. He will bear the glory, and will sit and rule on his throne. He will be a priest on his throne. The counsel of peace will be between them both."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The crowns shall be to Helem, to Tobijah, to Jedaiah, and to Hen the son of Zephaniah, for a memorial in the LORD\u2019s temple."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who are far off shall come and build in the LORD\u2019s temple; and you shall know that the LORD of Armies has sent me to you. This will happen, if you will diligently obey the LORD your God\u2019s voice.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the fourth year of King Darius, the LORD\u2019s word came to Zechariah in the fourth day of the ninth month, the month of Chislev."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The people of Bethel sent Sharezer and Regem Melech and their men to entreat the LORD\u2019s favor,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and to speak to the priests of the house of the LORD of Armies and to the prophets, saying, \u201cShould I weep in the fifth month, separating myself, as I have done these so many years?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the word of the LORD of Armies came to me, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cSpeak to all the people of the land and to the priests, saying, \u2018When you fasted and mourned in the fifth and in the seventh month for these seventy years, did you at all fast to me, really to me?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When you eat and when you drink, don\u2019t you eat for yourselves and drink for yourselves?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t these the words which the LORD proclaimed by the former prophets when Jerusalem was inhabited and in prosperity, and its cities around her, and the South and the lowland were inhabited?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD\u2019s word came to Zechariah, saying,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cThus has the LORD of Armies spoken, saying, \u2018Execute true judgment, and show kindness and compassion every man to his brother."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t oppress the widow, the fatherless, the foreigner, nor the poor; and let none of you devise evil against his brother in your heart.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But they refused to listen, and turned their backs, and stopped their ears, that they might not hear."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Yes, they made their hearts as hard as flint, lest they might hear the law and the words which the LORD of Armies had sent by his Spirit by the former prophets. Therefore great wrath came from the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It has come to pass that, as he called and they refused to listen, so they will call and I will not listen,\u201d said the LORD of Armies;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"\u201cbut I will scatter them with a whirlwind among all the nations which they have not known. Thus the land was desolate after them, so that no man passed through nor returned; for they made the pleasant land desolate.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The word of the LORD of Armies came to me."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cI am jealous for Zion with great jealousy, and I am jealous for her with great wrath.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD says: \u201cI have returned to Zion, and will dwell in the middle of Jerusalem. Jerusalem shall be called \u2018The City of Truth;\u2019 and the mountain of the LORD of Armies, \u2018The Holy Mountain.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cOld men and old women will again dwell in the streets of Jerusalem, every man with his staff in his hand because of their old age."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The streets of the city will be full of boys and girls playing in its streets.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cIf it is marvelous in the eyes of the remnant of this people in those days, should it also be marvelous in my eyes?\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cBehold, I will save my people from the east country and from the west country."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I will bring them, and they will dwell within Jerusalem. They will be my people, and I will be their God, in truth and in righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cLet your hands be strong, you who hear in these days these words from the mouth of the prophets who were in the day that the foundation of the house of the LORD of Armies was laid, even the temple, that it might be built."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For before those days there was no wages for man nor any wages for an animal, neither was there any peace to him who went out or came in, because of the adversary. For I set all men everyone against his neighbor."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But now I will not be to the remnant of this people as in the former days,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the seed of peace and the vine will yield its fruit, and the ground will give its increase, and the heavens will give their dew. I will cause the remnant of this people to inherit all these things."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It shall come to pass that, as you were a curse among the nations, house of Judah and house of Israel, so I will save you, and you shall be a blessing. Don\u2019t be afraid. Let your hands be strong.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"For the LORD of Armies says: \u201cAs I thought to do evil to you when your fathers provoked me to wrath,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cand I didn\u2019t repent,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"so again I have thought in these days to do good to Jerusalem and to the house of Judah. Don\u2019t be afraid."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"These are the things that you shall do: speak every man the truth with his neighbor. Execute the judgment of truth and peace in your gates,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and let none of you devise evil in your hearts against his neighbor, and love no false oath; for all these are things that I hate,\u201d says the LORD."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The word of the LORD of Armies came to me."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cThe fasts of the fourth, fifth, seventh, and tenth months shall be for the house of Judah joy, gladness, and cheerful feasts. Therefore love truth and peace.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cMany peoples and the inhabitants of many cities will yet come."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The inhabitants of one will go to another, saying, \u2018Let\u2019s go speedily to entreat the favor of the LORD, and to seek the LORD of Armies. I will go also.\u2019"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Yes, many peoples and strong nations will come to seek the LORD of Armies in Jerusalem and to entreat the favor of the LORD.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The LORD of Armies says: \u201cIn those days, ten men out of all the languages of the nations will take hold of the skirt of him who is a Jew, saying, \u2018We will go with you, for we have heard that God is with you.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A revelation."],[1,"The LORD\u2019s word is against the land of Hadrach,"],[2,"and will rest upon Damascus\u2014"],[1,"for the eye of man"],[2,"and of all the tribes of Israel is toward the LORD\u2014"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"and Hamath, also, which borders on it,"],[2,"Tyre and Sidon, because they are very wise."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Tyre built herself a stronghold,"],[2,"and heaped up silver like the dust,"],[2,"and fine gold like the mire of the streets."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Behold, the Lord will dispossess her,"],[2,"and he will strike her power in the sea;"],[2,"and she will be devoured with fire."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Ashkelon will see it, and fear;"],[2,"Gaza also, and will writhe in agony;"],[2,"as will Ekron, for her expectation will be disappointed;"],[2,"and the king will perish from Gaza,"],[2,"and Ashkelon will not be inhabited."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Foreigners will dwell in Ashdod,"],[2,"and I will cut off the pride of the Philistines."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"I will take away his blood out of his mouth,"],[2,"and his abominations from between his teeth;"],[1,"and he also will be a remnant for our God;"],[2,"and he will be as a chieftain in Judah,"],[2,"and Ekron as a Jebusite."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will encamp around my house against the army,"],[2,"that no one pass through or return;"],[2,"and no oppressor will pass through them any more:"],[2,"for now I have seen with my eyes."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Rejoice greatly, daughter of Zion!"],[2,"Shout, daughter of Jerusalem!"],[1,"Behold, your King comes to you!"],[2,"He is righteous, and having salvation;"],[2,"lowly, and riding on a donkey,"],[2,"even on a colt, the foal of a donkey."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I will cut off the chariot from Ephraim"],[2,"and the horse from Jerusalem."],[1,"The battle bow will be cut off;"],[2,"and he will speak peace to the nations."],[1,"His dominion will be from sea to sea,"],[2,"and from the River to the ends of the earth."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"As for you also,"],[2,"because of the blood of your covenant,"],[2,"I have set free your prisoners from the pit in which is no water."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Turn to the stronghold, you prisoners of hope!"],[2,"Even today I declare that I will restore double to you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"For indeed I bend Judah as a bow for me."],[2,"I have loaded the bow with Ephraim."],[1,"I will stir up your sons, Zion,"],[2,"against your sons, Greece,"],[2,"and will make you like the sword of a mighty man."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD will be seen over them."],[2,"His arrow will flash like lightning."],[1,"The Lord GOD will blow the trumpet,"],[2,"and will go with whirlwinds of the south."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD of Armies will defend them."],[2,"They will destroy and overcome with sling stones."],[1,"They will drink, and roar as through wine."],[2,"They will be filled like bowls,"],[2,"like the corners of the altar."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"The LORD their God will save them in that day as the flock of his people;"],[2,"for they are like the jewels of a crown,"],[2,"lifted on high over his land."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"For how great is his goodness,"],[2,"and how great is his beauty!"],[1,"Grain will make the young men flourish,"],[2,"and new wine the virgins."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Ask of the LORD rain in the spring time,"],[2,"the LORD who makes storm clouds,"],[2,"and he gives rain showers to everyone for the plants in the field."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"For the teraphim have spoken vanity,"],[2,"and the diviners have seen a lie;"],[2,"and they have told false dreams."],[1,"They comfort in vain."],[2,"Therefore they go their way like sheep."],[2,"They are oppressed, because there is no shepherd."]],f:["teraphim were household idols that may have been associated with inheritance rights to the household property."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"My anger is kindled against the shepherds,"],[2,"and I will punish the male goats,"],[2,"for the LORD of Armies has visited his flock, the house of Judah,"],[2,"and will make them as his majestic horse in the battle."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"From him will come the cornerstone,"],[2,"from him the tent peg,"],[2,"from him the battle bow,"],[2,"from him every ruler together."]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"They will be as mighty men,"],[2,"treading down muddy streets in the battle."],[1,"They will fight, because the LORD is with them."],[2,"The riders on horses will be confounded."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will strengthen the house of Judah,"],[2,"and I will save the house of Joseph."],[1,"I will bring them back,"],[2,"for I have mercy on them."],[1,"They will be as though I had not cast them off,"],[2,"for I am the LORD their God, and I will hear them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Ephraim will be like a mighty man,"],[2,"and their heart will rejoice as through wine."],[1,"Yes, their children will see it and rejoice."],[2,"Their heart will be glad in the LORD."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"I will signal for them and gather them,"],[2,"for I have redeemed them."],[2,"They will increase as they were before."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will sow them among the peoples."],[2,"They will remember me in far countries."],[2,"They will live with their children and will return."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring them again also out of the land of Egypt,"],[2,"and gather them out of Assyria."],[1,"I will bring them into the land of Gilead and Lebanon;"],[2,"and there won\u2019t be room enough for them."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"He will pass through the sea of affliction,"],[2,"and will strike the waves in the sea,"],[2,"and all the depths of the Nile will dry up;"],[2,"and the pride of Assyria will be brought down,"],[2,"and the scepter of Egypt will depart."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"I will strengthen them in the LORD."],[2,"They will walk up and down in his name,\u201d says the LORD."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[1,"Open your doors, Lebanon,"],[2,"that the fire may devour your cedars."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[1,"Wail, cypress tree, for the cedar has fallen,"],[2,"because the stately ones are destroyed."],[1,"Wail, you oaks of Bashan,"],[2,"for the strong forest has come down."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"A voice of the wailing of the shepherds!"],[2,"For their glory is destroyed\u2014a voice of the roaring of young lions!"],[2,"For the pride of the Jordan is ruined."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD my God says: \u201cFeed the flock of slaughter."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Their buyers slaughter them and go unpunished. Those who sell them say, \u2018Blessed be the LORD, for I am rich;\u2019 and their own shepherds don\u2019t pity them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For I will no more pity the inhabitants of the land,\u201d says the LORD; \u201cbut, behold, I will deliver every one of the men into his neighbor\u2019s hand and into the hand of his king. They will strike the land, and out of their hand I will not deliver them.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"So I fed the flock to be slaughtered, especially the oppressed of the flock. I took for myself two staffs. The one I called \u201cFavor\u201d and the other I called \u201cUnion\u201d, and I fed the flock."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I cut off the three shepherds in one month; for my soul was weary of them, and their soul also loathed me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then I said, \u201cI will not feed you. That which dies, let it die; and that which is to be cut off, let it be cut off; and let those who are left eat each other\u2019s flesh.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I took my staff Favor and cut it apart, that I might break my covenant that I had made with all the peoples."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"It was broken in that day; and thus the poor of the flock that listened to me knew that it was the LORD\u2019s word."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I said to them, \u201cIf you think it best, give me my wages; and if not, keep them.\u201d So they weighed for my wages thirty pieces of silver."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cThrow it to the potter\u2014the handsome price that I was valued at by them!\u201d I took the thirty pieces of silver and threw them to the potter in the LORD\u2019s house."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Then I cut apart my other staff, Union, that I might break the brotherhood between Judah and Israel."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD said to me, \u201cTake for yourself yet again the equipment of a foolish shepherd."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For, behold, I will raise up a shepherd in the land who will not visit those who are cut off, neither will seek those who are scattered, nor heal that which is broken, nor feed that which is sound; but he will eat the meat of the fat sheep, and will tear their hoofs in pieces."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Woe to the worthless shepherd who leaves the flock! The sword will strike his arm and his right eye. His arm will be completely withered, and his right eye will be totally blinded!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A revelation of the LORD\u2019s word concerning Israel: The LORD, who stretches out the heavens and lays the foundation of the earth, and forms the spirit of man within him says:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I will make Jerusalem a cup of reeling to all the surrounding peoples, and it will also be on Judah in the siege against Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that I will make Jerusalem a burdensome stone for all the peoples. All who burden themselves with it will be severely wounded, and all the nations of the earth will be gathered together against it."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"In that day,\u201d says the LORD, \u201cI will strike every horse with terror and his rider with madness. I will open my eyes on the house of Judah, and will strike every horse of the peoples with blindness."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The chieftains of Judah will say in their heart, \u2018The inhabitants of Jerusalem are my strength in the LORD of Armies their God.\u2019"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day I will make the chieftains of Judah like a pan of fire among wood, and like a flaming torch among sheaves. They will devour all the surrounding peoples on the right hand and on the left; and Jerusalem will yet again dwell in their own place, even in Jerusalem."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD also will save the tents of Judah first, that the glory of David\u2019s house and the glory of the inhabitants of Jerusalem not be magnified above Judah."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"In that day the LORD will defend the inhabitants of Jerusalem. He who is feeble among them at that day will be like David, and David\u2019s house will be like God, like the LORD\u2019s angel before them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day, that I will seek to destroy all the nations that come against Jerusalem."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"I will pour on David\u2019s house and on the inhabitants of Jerusalem the spirit of grace and of supplication. They will look to me whom they have pierced; and they shall mourn for him as one mourns for his only son, and will grieve bitterly for him as one grieves for his firstborn."]],f:["After \u201cme\u201d, the Hebrew has the two letters \u201cAleph Tav\u201d (the first and last letters of the Hebrew alphabet), not as a word, but as a grammatical marker."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In that day there will be a great mourning in Jerusalem, like the mourning of Hadadrimmon in the valley of Megiddo."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The land will mourn, every family apart; the family of David\u2019s house apart, and their wives apart; the family of the house of Nathan apart, and their wives apart;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"the family of the house of Levi apart, and their wives apart; the family of the Shimeites apart, and their wives apart;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"all the families who remain, every family apart, and their wives apart."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn that day there will be a fountain opened to David\u2019s house and to the inhabitants of Jerusalem, for sin and for uncleanness."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"It will come to pass in that day, says the LORD of Armies, that I will cut off the names of the idols out of the land, and they will be remembered no more. I will also cause the prophets and the spirit of impurity to pass out of the land."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"It will happen that when anyone still prophesies, then his father and his mother who bore him will tell him, \u2018You must die, because you speak lies in the LORD\u2019s name;\u2019 and his father and his mother who bore him will stab him when he prophesies."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that the prophets will each be ashamed of his vision when he prophesies; they won\u2019t wear a hairy mantle to deceive,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"but he will say, \u2018I am no prophet, I am a tiller of the ground; for I have been made a bondservant from my youth.\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"One will say to him, \u2018What are these wounds between your arms?\u2019 Then he will answer, \u2018Those with which I was wounded in the house of my friends.\u2019"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cAwake, sword, against my shepherd,"],[2,"and against the man who is close to me,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."],[1,"\u201cStrike the shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered;"],[2,"and I will turn my hand against the little ones."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"It shall happen that in all the land,\u201d says the LORD,"],[2,"\u201ctwo parts in it will be cut off and die;"],[2,"but the third will be left in it."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"I will bring the third part into the fire,"],[2,"and will refine them as silver is refined,"],[2,"and will test them like gold is tested."],[1,"They will call on my name, and I will hear them."],[2,"I will say, \u2018It is my people;\u2019"],[2,"and they will say, \u2018The LORD is my God.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, a day of the LORD comes, when your plunder will be divided within you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For I will gather all nations against Jerusalem to battle; and the city will be taken, the houses rifled, and the women ravished. Half of the city will go out into captivity, and the rest of the people will not be cut off from the city."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then the LORD will go out and fight against those nations, as when he fought in the day of battle."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"His feet will stand in that day on the Mount of Olives, which is before Jerusalem on the east; and the Mount of Olives will be split in two from east to west, making a very great valley. Half of the mountain will move toward the north, and half of it toward the south."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You shall flee by the valley of my mountains, for the valley of the mountains shall reach to Azel. Yes, you shall flee, just like you fled from before the earthquake in the days of Uzziah king of Judah. The LORD my God will come, and all the holy ones with you."]],f:["Septuagint reads \u201chim\u201d instead of \u201cyou\u201d."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that there will not be light, cold, or frost."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It will be a unique day which is known to the LORD\u2014not day, and not night; but it will come to pass that at evening time there will be light."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that living waters will go out from Jerusalem, half of them toward the eastern sea, and half of them toward the western sea. It will be so in summer and in winter."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The LORD will be King over all the earth. In that day the LORD will be one, and his name one."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"All the land will be made like the Arabah, from Geba to Rimmon south of Jerusalem; and she will be lifted up and will dwell in her place, from Benjamin\u2019s gate to the place of the first gate, to the corner gate, and from the tower of Hananel to the king\u2019s wine presses."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Men will dwell therein, and there will be no more curse; but Jerusalem will dwell safely."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"This will be the plague with which the LORD will strike all the peoples who have fought against Jerusalem: their flesh will consume away while they stand on their feet, and their eyes will consume away in their sockets, and their tongue will consume away in their mouth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It will happen in that day that a great panic from the LORD will be among them; and they will each seize the hand of his neighbor, and his hand will rise up against the hand of his neighbor."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Judah also will fight at Jerusalem; and the wealth of all the surrounding nations will be gathered together: gold, silver, and clothing, in great abundance."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"A plague like this will fall on the horse, on the mule, on the camel, on the donkey, and on all the animals that will be in those camps."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"It will happen that everyone who is left of all the nations that came against Jerusalem will go up from year to year to worship the King, the LORD of Armies, and to keep the feast of booths."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It will be that whoever of all the families of the earth doesn\u2019t go up to Jerusalem to worship the King, the LORD of Armies, on them there will be no rain."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"If the family of Egypt doesn\u2019t go up and doesn\u2019t come, neither will it rain on them. This will be the plague with which the LORD will strike the nations that don\u2019t go up to keep the feast of booths."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"This will be the punishment of Egypt and the punishment of all the nations that don\u2019t go up to keep the feast of booths."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"In that day there will be inscribed on the bells of the horses, \u201cHOLY TO THE LORD\u201d; and the pots in the LORD\u2019s house will be like the bowls before the altar."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Yes, every pot in Jerusalem and in Judah will be holy to the LORD of Armies; and all those who sacrifice will come and take of them, and cook in them. In that day there will no longer be a Canaanite in the house of the LORD of Armies."]],f:["or, merchant"]}]]}},1309,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,s,h,n){s.exports={book:"Mal",name:"Malachi",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A revelation, the LORD\u2019s word to Israel by Malachi."]],f:["When rendered in ALL CAPITAL LETTERS, \u201cLORD\u201d or \u201cGOD\u201d is the translation of God\u2019s Proper Name (Hebrew \u201c\u05d9\u05d4\u05d5\u05d4\u201d, usually pronounced Yahweh)."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI have loved you,\u201d says the LORD."],[0,"Yet you say, \u201cHow have you loved us?\u201d"],[0,"\u201cWasn\u2019t Esau Jacob\u2019s brother?\u201d says the LORD, \u201cYet I loved Jacob;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"but Esau I hated, and made his mountains a desolation, and gave his heritage to the jackals of the wilderness.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Whereas Edom says, \u201cWe are beaten down, but we will return and build the waste places,\u201d the LORD of Armies says, \u201cThey shall build, but I will throw down; and men will call them \u2018The Wicked Land,\u2019 even the people against whom the LORD shows wrath forever.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Your eyes will see, and you will say, \u201cThe LORD is great\u2014even beyond the border of Israel!\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cA son honors his father, and a servant his master. If I am a father, then where is my honor? And if I am a master, where is the respect due me?\u201d says the LORD of Armies to you priests who despise my name. \u201cYou say, \u2018How have we despised your name?\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You offer polluted bread on my altar. You say, \u2018How have we polluted you?\u2019 In that you say, \u2018The LORD\u2019s table is contemptible.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When you offer the blind for sacrifice, isn\u2019t that evil? And when you offer the lame and sick, isn\u2019t that evil? Present it now to your governor! Will he be pleased with you? Or will he accept your person?\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, please entreat the favor of God, that he may be gracious to us. With this, will he accept any of you?\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]],f:["The Hebrew word rendered \u201cGod\u201d is \u201c\u05d0\u05b1\u05dc\u05b9\u05d4\u05b4\u0591\u05d9\u05dd\u201d (Elohim)."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOh that there were one among you who would shut the doors, that you might not kindle fire on my altar in vain! I have no pleasure in you,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cneither will I accept an offering at your hand."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For from the rising of the sun even to its going down, my name is great among the nations, and in every place incense will be offered to my name, and a pure offering; for my name is great among the nations,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cBut you profane it when you say, \u2018The LORD\u2019s table is polluted, and its fruit, even its food, is contemptible.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You say also, \u2018Behold, what a weariness it is!\u2019 And you have sniffed at it\u201d, says the LORD of Armies; \u201cand you have brought that which was taken by violence, the lame, and the sick; thus you bring the offering. Should I accept this at your hand?\u201d says the LORD."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut the deceiver is cursed who has in his flock a male, and vows and sacrifices to the Lord a defective thing; for I am a great King,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cand my name is awesome among the nations.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cLord\u201d is \u201cAdonai.\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, you priests, this commandment is for you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"If you will not listen, and if you will not take it to heart, to give glory to my name,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cthen I will send the curse on you, and I will curse your blessings. Indeed, I have cursed them already, because you do not take it to heart."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Behold, I will rebuke your offspring, and will spread dung on your faces, even the dung of your feasts; and you will be taken away with it."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You will know that I have sent this commandment to you, that my covenant may be with Levi,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cMy covenant was with him of life and peace; and I gave them to him that he might be reverent toward me; and he was reverent toward me, and stood in awe of my name."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The law of truth was in his mouth, and unrighteousness was not found in his lips. He walked with me in peace and uprightness, and turned many away from iniquity."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the priest\u2019s lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the law at his mouth; for he is the messenger of the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But you have turned away from the path. You have caused many to stumble in the law. You have corrupted the covenant of Levi,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore I have also made you contemptible and wicked before all the people, according to the way you have not kept my ways, but have had respect for persons in the law."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t we all have one father? Hasn\u2019t one God created us? Why do we deal treacherously every man against his brother, profaning the covenant of our fathers?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Judah has dealt treacherously, and an abomination is committed in Israel and in Jerusalem; for Judah has profaned the holiness of the LORD which he loves, and has married the daughter of a foreign god."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The LORD will cut off the man who does this, him who wakes and him who answers, out of the tents of Jacob and him who offers an offering to the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis again you do: you cover the LORD\u2019s altar with tears, with weeping, and with sighing, because he doesn\u2019t regard the offering any more, neither receives it with good will at your hand."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Yet you say, \u2018Why?\u2019 Because the LORD has been witness between you and the wife of your youth, against whom you have dealt treacherously, though she is your companion and the wife of your covenant."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Did he not make you one, although he had the residue of the Spirit? Why one? He sought godly offspring. Therefore take heed to your spirit, and let no one deal treacherously against the wife of his youth."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"One who hates and divorces\u201d, says the LORD, the God of Israel, \u201ccovers his garment with violence!\u201d says the LORD of Armies. \u201cTherefore pay attention to your spirit, that you don\u2019t be unfaithful."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"You have wearied the LORD with your words. Yet you say, \u2018How have we wearied him?\u2019 In that you say, \u2018Everyone who does evil is good in the LORD\u2019s sight, and he delights in them;\u2019 or \u2018Where is the God of justice?\u2019"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I send my messenger, and he will prepare the way before me! The Lord, whom you seek, will suddenly come to his temple. Behold, the messenger of the covenant, whom you desire, is coming!\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cBut who can endure the day of his coming? And who will stand when he appears? For he is like a refiner\u2019s fire, and like launderers\u2019 soap;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and he will sit as a refiner and purifier of silver, and he will purify the sons of Levi, and refine them as gold and silver; and they shall offer to the LORD offerings in righteousness."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then the offering of Judah and Jerusalem will be pleasant to the LORD as in the days of old and as in ancient years."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"I will come near to you to judgment. I will be a swift witness against the sorcerers, against the adulterers, against the perjurers, and against those who oppress the hireling in his wages, the widow, and the fatherless, and who deprive the foreigner of justice, and don\u2019t fear me,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor I, the LORD, don\u2019t change; therefore you, sons of Jacob, are not consumed."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"From the days of your fathers you have turned away from my ordinances and have not kept them. Return to me, and I will return to you,\u201d says the LORD of Armies. \u201cBut you say, \u2018How shall we return?\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Will a man rob God? Yet you rob me! But you say, \u2018How have we robbed you?\u2019 In tithes and offerings."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"You are cursed with the curse; for you rob me, even this whole nation."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Bring the whole tithe into the storehouse, that there may be food in my house, and test me now in this,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cif I will not open you the windows of heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that there will not be enough room for."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I will rebuke the devourer for your sakes, and he shall not destroy the fruits of your ground; neither shall your vine cast its fruit before its time in the field,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cAll nations shall call you blessed, for you will be a delightful land,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYour words have been harsh against me,\u201d says the LORD. \u201cYet you say, \u2018What have we spoken against you?\u2019"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You have said, \u2018It is vain to serve God,\u2019 and \u2018What profit is it that we have followed his instructions and that we have walked mournfully before the LORD of Armies?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now we call the proud happy; yes, those who work wickedness are built up; yes, they tempt God, and escape.\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then those who feared the LORD spoke one with another; and the LORD listened and heard, and a book of memory was written before him for those who feared the LORD and who honored his name."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They shall be mine,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cmy own possession in the day that I make. I will spare them, as a man spares his own son who serves him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then you shall return and discern between the righteous and the wicked, between him who serves God and him who doesn\u2019t serve him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor behold, the day comes, burning like a furnace, when all the proud and all who work wickedness will be stubble. The day that comes will burn them up,\u201d says the LORD of Armies, \u201cso that it will leave them neither root nor branch."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But to you who fear my name shall the sun of righteousness arise with healing in its wings. You will go out and leap like calves of the stall."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You shall tread down the wicked; for they will be ashes under the soles of your feet in the day that I make,\u201d says the LORD of Armies."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cRemember the law of Moses my servant, which I commanded to him in Horeb for all Israel, even statutes and ordinances."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, I will send you Elijah the prophet before the great and terrible day of the LORD comes."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He will turn the hearts of the fathers to the children and the hearts of the children to their fathers, lest I come and strike the earth with a curse.\u201d"]]}]]}},1310,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,s,i){a.exports={book:"Matt",name:"Matthew",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The book of the genealogy of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham."]],f:["Messiah (Hebrew) and Christ (Greek) both mean \u201cAnointed One\u201d"]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Abraham became the father of Isaac. Isaac became the father of Jacob. Jacob became the father of Judah and his brothers."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Judah became the father of Perez and Zerah by Tamar. Perez became the father of Hezron. Hezron became the father of Ram."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Ram became the father of Amminadab. Amminadab became the father of Nahshon. Nahshon became the father of Salmon."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Salmon became the father of Boaz by Rahab. Boaz became the father of Obed by Ruth. Obed became the father of Jesse."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Jesse became the father of King David. David the king became the father of Solomon by her who had been Uriah\u2019s wife."]],f:["NU omits \u201cthe king\u201d."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Solomon became the father of Rehoboam. Rehoboam became the father of Abijah. Abijah became the father of Asa."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Asa became the father of Jehoshaphat. Jehoshaphat became the father of Joram. Joram became the father of Uzziah."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Uzziah became the father of Jotham. Jotham became the father of Ahaz. Ahaz became the father of Hezekiah."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Hezekiah became the father of Manasseh. Manasseh became the father of Amon. Amon became the father of Josiah."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Josiah became the father of Jechoniah and his brothers at the time of the exile to Babylon."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"After the exile to Babylon, Jechoniah became the father of Shealtiel. Shealtiel became the father of Zerubbabel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Zerubbabel became the father of Abiud. Abiud became the father of Eliakim. Eliakim became the father of Azor."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Azor became the father of Zadok. Zadok became the father of Achim. Achim became the father of Eliud."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Eliud became the father of Eleazar. Eleazar became the father of Matthan. Matthan became the father of Jacob."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Jacob became the father of Joseph, the husband of Mary, from whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ."]],f:["\u201cJesus\u201d means \u201cSalvation\u201d."]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations; from David to the exile to Babylon fourteen generations; and from the carrying away to Babylon to the Christ, fourteen generations."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the birth of Jesus Christ was like this: After his mother, Mary, was engaged to Joseph, before they came together, she was found pregnant by the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Joseph, her husband, being a righteous man, and not willing to make her a public example, intended to put her away secretly."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But when he thought about these things, behold, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream, saying, \u201cJoseph, son of David, don\u2019t be afraid to take to yourself Mary as your wife, for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Spirit."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"She shall give birth to a son. You shall name him Jesus, for it is he who shall save his people from their sins.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cJesus\u201d means \u201cSalvation\u201d."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Now all this has happened that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the Lord through the prophet, saying,"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, the virgin shall be with child,"],[2,"and shall give birth to a son."],[1,"They shall call his name Immanuel,\u201d"],[2,"which is, being interpreted, \u201cGod with us.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph arose from his sleep, and did as the angel of the Lord commanded him, and took his wife to himself;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and didn\u2019t know her sexually until she had given birth to her firstborn son. He named him Jesus."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judea in the days of King Herod, behold, wise men from the east came to Jerusalem, saying,"]],f:["The word for \u201cwise men\u201d (magoi) can also mean teachers, scientists, physicians, astrologers, seers, interpreters of dreams, or sorcerers."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cWhere is he who is born King of the Jews? For we saw his star in the east, and have come to worship him.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When King Herod heard it, he was troubled, and all Jerusalem with him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Gathering together all the chief priests and scribes of the people, he asked them where the Christ would be born."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cIn Bethlehem of Judea, for this is written through the prophet,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018You Bethlehem, land of Judah,"],[2,"are in no way least among the princes of Judah;"],[1,"for out of you shall come a governor"],[2,"who shall shepherd my people, Israel.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Herod secretly called the wise men, and learned from them exactly what time the star appeared."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He sent them to Bethlehem, and said, \u201cGo and search diligently for the young child. When you have found him, bring me word, so that I also may come and worship him.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"They, having heard the king, went their way; and behold, the star, which they saw in the east, went before them until it came and stood over where the young child was."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When they saw the star, they rejoiced with exceedingly great joy."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They came into the house and saw the young child with Mary, his mother, and they fell down and worshiped him. Opening their treasures, they offered to him gifts: gold, frankincense, and myrrh."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Being warned in a dream not to return to Herod, they went back to their own country another way."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when they had departed, behold, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in a dream, saying, \u201cArise and take the young child and his mother, and flee into Egypt, and stay there until I tell you, for Herod will seek the young child to destroy him.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose and took the young child and his mother by night and departed into Egypt,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and was there until the death of Herod, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the Lord through the prophet, saying, \u201cOut of Egypt I called my son.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Herod, when he saw that he was mocked by the wise men, was exceedingly angry, and sent out and killed all the male children who were in Bethlehem and in all the surrounding countryside, from two years old and under, according to the exact time which he had learned from the wise men."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then that which was spoken by Jeremiah the prophet was fulfilled, saying,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cA voice was heard in Ramah,"],[2,"lamentation, weeping and great mourning,"],[1,"Rachel weeping for her children;"],[2,"she wouldn\u2019t be comforted,"],[2,"because they are no more.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Herod was dead, behold, an angel of the Lord appeared in a dream to Joseph in Egypt, saying,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"\u201cArise and take the young child and his mother, and go into the land of Israel, for those who sought the young child\u2019s life are dead.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose and took the young child and his mother, and came into the land of Israel."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But when he heard that Archelaus was reigning over Judea in the place of his father, Herod, he was afraid to go there. Being warned in a dream, he withdrew into the region of Galilee,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and came and lived in a city called Nazareth; that it might be fulfilled which was spoken through the prophets that he will be called a Nazarene."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days, John the Baptizer came, preaching in the wilderness of Judea, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cRepent, for the Kingdom of Heaven is at hand!\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For this is he who was spoken of by Isaiah the prophet, saying,"],[1,"\u201cThe voice of one crying in the wilderness,"],[2,"make the way of the Lord ready!"],[2,"Make his paths straight!\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now John himself wore clothing made of camel\u2019s hair with a leather belt around his waist. His food was locusts and wild honey."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then people from Jerusalem, all of Judea, and all the region around the Jordan went out to him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They were baptized by him in the Jordan, confessing their sins."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But when he saw many of the Pharisees and Sadducees coming for his baptism, he said to them, \u201cYou offspring of vipers, who warned you to flee from the wrath to come?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore produce fruit worthy of repentance!"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t think to yourselves, \u2018We have Abraham for our father,\u2019 for I tell you that God is able to raise up children to Abraham from these stones."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Even now the ax lies at the root of the trees. Therefore every tree that doesn\u2019t produce good fruit is cut down, and cast into the fire."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI indeed baptize you in water for repentance, but he who comes after me is mightier than I, whose sandals I am not worthy to carry. He will baptize you in the Holy Spirit."]],f:["TR and NU add \u201cand with fire\u201d"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"His winnowing fork is in his hand, and he will thoroughly cleanse his threshing floor. He will gather his wheat into the barn, but the chaff he will burn up with unquenchable fire.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus came from Galilee to the Jordan to John, to be baptized by him."]],f:["i.e., the Jordan River"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But John would have hindered him, saying, \u201cI need to be baptized by you, and you come to me?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus, answering, said to him, \u201cAllow it now, for this is the fitting way for us to fulfill all righteousness.\u201d Then he allowed him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, when he was baptized, went up directly from the water: and behold, the heavens were opened to him. He saw the Spirit of God descending as a dove, and coming on him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Behold, a voice out of the heavens said, \u201cThis is my beloved Son, with whom I am well pleased.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus was led up by the Spirit into the wilderness to be tempted by the devil."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When he had fasted forty days and forty nights, he was hungry afterward."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The tempter came and said to him, \u201cIf you are the Son of God, command that these stones become bread.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered, \u201cIt is written, \u2018Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word that proceeds out of God\u2019s mouth.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the devil took him into the holy city. He set him on the pinnacle of the temple,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cIf you are the Son of God, throw yourself down, for it is written,"],[1,"\u2018He will command his angels concerning you,\u2019 and,"],[1,"\u2018On their hands they will bear you up,"],[2,"so that you don\u2019t dash your foot against a stone.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cAgain, it is written, \u2018You shall not test the Lord, your God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, the devil took him to an exceedingly high mountain, and showed him all the kingdoms of the world and their glory."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cI will give you all of these things, if you will fall down and worship me.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said to him, \u201cGet behind me, Satan! For it is written, \u2018You shall worship the Lord your God, and you shall serve him only.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["TR and NU read \u201cGo away\u201d instead of \u201cGet behind me\u201d"]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the devil left him, and behold, angels came and served him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Jesus heard that John was delivered up, he withdrew into Galilee."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Leaving Nazareth, he came and lived in Capernaum, which is by the sea, in the region of Zebulun and Naphtali,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"that it might be fulfilled which was spoken through Isaiah the prophet, saying,"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe land of Zebulun and the land of Naphtali,"],[2,"toward the sea, beyond the Jordan,"],[2,"Galilee of the Gentiles,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"the people who sat in darkness saw a great light;"],[2,"to those who sat in the region and shadow of death,"],[2,"to them light has dawned.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"From that time, Jesus began to preach, and to say, \u201cRepent! For the Kingdom of Heaven is at hand.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Walking by the sea of Galilee, he saw two brothers: Simon, who is called Peter, and Andrew, his brother, casting a net into the sea; for they were fishermen."]],f:["TR reads \u201cJesus\u201d instead of \u201che\u201d"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cCome after me, and I will make you fishers for men.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"They immediately left their nets and followed him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Going on from there, he saw two other brothers, James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother, in the boat with Zebedee their father, mending their nets. He called them."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They immediately left the boat and their father, and followed him."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus went about in all Galilee, teaching in their synagogues, preaching the Good News of the Kingdom, and healing every disease and every sickness among the people."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The report about him went out into all Syria. They brought to him all who were sick, afflicted with various diseases and torments, possessed with demons, epileptics, and paralytics; and he healed them."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Great multitudes from Galilee, Decapolis, Jerusalem, Judea, and from beyond the Jordan followed him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Seeing the multitudes, he went up onto the mountain. When he had sat down, his disciples came to him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He opened his mouth and taught them, saying,"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBlessed are the poor in spirit,"],[2,"for theirs is the Kingdom of Heaven."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those who mourn,"],[2,"for they shall be comforted."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are the gentle,"],[2,"for they shall inherit the earth."]],f:["or, land."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those who hunger and thirst for righteousness,"],[2,"for they shall be filled."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are the merciful,"],[2,"for they shall obtain mercy."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are the pure in heart,"],[2,"for they shall see God."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are the peacemakers,"],[2,"for they shall be called children of God."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are those who have been persecuted for righteousness\u2019 sake,"],[2,"for theirs is the Kingdom of Heaven."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBlessed are you when people reproach you, persecute you, and say all kinds of evil against you falsely, for my sake."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Rejoice, and be exceedingly glad, for great is your reward in heaven. For that is how they persecuted the prophets who were before you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou are the salt of the earth, but if the salt has lost its flavor, with what will it be salted? It is then good for nothing, but to be cast out and trodden under the feet of men."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou are the light of the world. A city located on a hill can\u2019t be hidden."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Neither do you light a lamp and put it under a measuring basket, but on a stand; and it shines to all who are in the house."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Even so, let your light shine before men, that they may see your good works and glorify your Father who is in heaven."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t think that I came to destroy the law or the prophets. I didn\u2019t come to destroy, but to fulfill."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For most certainly, I tell you, until heaven and earth pass away, not even one smallest letter or one tiny pen stroke shall in any way pass away from the law, until all things are accomplished."]],f:["literally, iota","or, serif"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore, whoever shall break one of these least commandments and teach others to do so, shall be called least in the Kingdom of Heaven; but whoever shall do and teach them shall be called great in the Kingdom of Heaven."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For I tell you that unless your righteousness exceeds that of the scribes and Pharisees, there is no way you will enter into the Kingdom of Heaven."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou have heard that it was said to the ancient ones, \u2018You shall not murder;\u2019 and \u2018Whoever murders will be in danger of the judgment.\u2019"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But I tell you that everyone who is angry with his brother without a cause will be in danger of the judgment. Whoever says to his brother, \u2018Raca!\u2019 will be in danger of the council. Whoever says, \u2018You fool!\u2019 will be in danger of the fire of Gehenna."]],f:["NU omits \u201cwithout a cause\u201d.","\u201cRaca\u201d is an Aramaic insult, related to the word for \u201cempty\u201d and conveying the idea of empty-headedness.","or, Hell"]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf therefore you are offering your gift at the altar, and there remember that your brother has anything against you,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"leave your gift there before the altar, and go your way. First be reconciled to your brother, and then come and offer your gift."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Agree with your adversary quickly while you are with him on the way; lest perhaps the prosecutor deliver you to the judge, and the judge deliver you to the officer, and you be cast into prison."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, you shall by no means get out of there until you have paid the last penny."]],f:["literally, kodrantes. A kodrantes was a small copper coin worth about 2 lepta (widow\u2019s mites)\u2014not enough to buy very much of anything."]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou have heard that it was said, \u2018You shall not commit adultery;\u2019"]],f:["TR adds \u201cto the ancients\u201d."]},{v:28,l:[[0,"but I tell you that everyone who gazes at a woman to lust after her has committed adultery with her already in his heart."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"If your right eye causes you to stumble, pluck it out and throw it away from you. For it is more profitable for you that one of your members should perish than for your whole body to be cast into Gehenna."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:30,l:[[0,"If your right hand causes you to stumble, cut it off, and throw it away from you. For it is more profitable for you that one of your members should perish, than for your whole body to be cast into Gehenna."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt was also said, \u2018Whoever shall put away his wife, let him give her a writing of divorce,\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"but I tell you that whoever puts away his wife, except for the cause of sexual immorality, makes her an adulteress; and whoever marries her when she is put away commits adultery."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAgain you have heard that it was said to the ancient ones, \u2018You shall not make false vows, but shall perform to the Lord your vows,\u2019"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"but I tell you, don\u2019t swear at all: neither by heaven, for it is the throne of God;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"nor by the earth, for it is the footstool of his feet; nor by Jerusalem, for it is the city of the great King."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Neither shall you swear by your head, for you can\u2019t make one hair white or black."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"But let your \u2018Yes\u2019 be \u2018Yes\u2019 and your \u2018No\u2019 be \u2018No.\u2019 Whatever is more than these is of the evil one."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou have heard that it was said, \u2018An eye for an eye, and a tooth for a tooth.\u2019"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But I tell you, don\u2019t resist him who is evil; but whoever strikes you on your right cheek, turn to him the other also."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"If anyone sues you to take away your coat, let him have your cloak also."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Whoever compels you to go one mile, go with him two."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Give to him who asks you, and don\u2019t turn away him who desires to borrow from you."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou have heard that it was said, \u2018You shall love your neighbor and hate your enemy.\u2019"]],f:["not in the Bible, but see Qumran Manual of Discipline Ix, 21-26"]},{v:44,l:[[0,"But I tell you, love your enemies, bless those who curse you, do good to those who hate you, and pray for those who mistreat you and persecute you,"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"that you may be children of your Father who is in heaven. For he makes his sun to rise on the evil and the good, and sends rain on the just and the unjust."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"For if you love those who love you, what reward do you have? Don\u2019t even the tax collectors do the same?"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"If you only greet your friends, what more do you do than others? Don\u2019t even the tax collectors do the same?"]],f:["NU reads \u201cGentiles\u201d instead of \u201ctax collectors\u201d."]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Therefore you shall be perfect, just as your Father in heaven is perfect."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBe careful that you don\u2019t do your charitable giving before men, to be seen by them, or else you have no reward from your Father who is in heaven."]],f:["NU reads \u201cacts of righteousness\u201d instead of \u201ccharitable giving\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore, when you do merciful deeds, don\u2019t sound a trumpet before yourself, as the hypocrites do in the synagogues and in the streets, that they may get glory from men. Most certainly I tell you, they have received their reward."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But when you do merciful deeds, don\u2019t let your left hand know what your right hand does,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"so that your merciful deeds may be in secret, then your Father who sees in secret will reward you openly."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen you pray, you shall not be as the hypocrites, for they love to stand and pray in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen by men. Most certainly, I tell you, they have received their reward."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But you, when you pray, enter into your inner room, and having shut your door, pray to your Father who is in secret; and your Father who sees in secret will reward you openly."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In praying, don\u2019t use vain repetitions as the Gentiles do; for they think that they will be heard for their much speaking."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t be like them, for your Father knows what things you need before you ask him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Pray like this:"],[1,"\u201c\u2018Our Father in heaven, may your name be kept holy."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Let your Kingdom come."],[2,"Let your will be done on earth as it is in heaven."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Give us today our daily bread."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"Forgive us our debts,"],[2,"as we also forgive our debtors."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"Bring us not into temptation,"],[2,"but deliver us from the evil one."],[1,"For yours is the Kingdom, the power, and the glory forever. Amen.\u2019"]],f:["NU omits \u201cFor yours is the Kingdom, the power, and the glory forever. Amen.\u201d"]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor if you forgive men their trespasses, your heavenly Father will also forgive you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But if you don\u2019t forgive men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMoreover when you fast, don\u2019t be like the hypocrites, with sad faces. For they disfigure their faces that they may be seen by men to be fasting. Most certainly I tell you, they have received their reward."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But you, when you fast, anoint your head and wash your face,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"so that you are not seen by men to be fasting, but by your Father who is in secret; and your Father, who sees in secret, will reward you."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t lay up treasures for yourselves on the earth, where moth and rust consume, and where thieves break through and steal;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but lay up for yourselves treasures in heaven, where neither moth nor rust consume, and where thieves don\u2019t break through and steal;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"for where your treasure is, there your heart will be also."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe lamp of the body is the eye. If therefore your eye is sound, your whole body will be full of light."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But if your eye is evil, your whole body will be full of darkness. If therefore the light that is in you is darkness, how great is the darkness!"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNo one can serve two masters, for either he will hate the one and love the other, or else he will be devoted to one and despise the other. You can\u2019t serve both God and Mammon."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Therefore I tell you, don\u2019t be anxious for your life: what you will eat, or what you will drink; nor yet for your body, what you will wear. Isn\u2019t life more than food, and the body more than clothing?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"See the birds of the sky, that they don\u2019t sow, neither do they reap, nor gather into barns. Your heavenly Father feeds them. Aren\u2019t you of much more value than they?"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhich of you by being anxious, can add one moment to his lifespan?"]],f:["literally, cubit"]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Why are you anxious about clothing? Consider the lilies of the field, how they grow. They don\u2019t toil, neither do they spin,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"yet I tell you that even Solomon in all his glory was not dressed like one of these."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But if God so clothes the grass of the field, which today exists and tomorrow is thrown into the oven, won\u2019t he much more clothe you, you of little faith?"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore don\u2019t be anxious, saying, \u2018What will we eat?\u2019, \u2018What will we drink?\u2019 or, \u2018With what will we be clothed?\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For the Gentiles seek after all these things; for your heavenly Father knows that you need all these things."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But seek first God\u2019s Kingdom and his righteousness; and all these things will be given to you as well."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t be anxious for tomorrow, for tomorrow will be anxious for itself. Each day\u2019s own evil is sufficient."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t judge, so that you won\u2019t be judged."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For with whatever judgment you judge, you will be judged; and with whatever measure you measure, it will be measured to you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Why do you see the speck that is in your brother\u2019s eye, but don\u2019t consider the beam that is in your own eye?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Or how will you tell your brother, \u2018Let me remove the speck from your eye,\u2019 and behold, the beam is in your own eye?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You hypocrite! First remove the beam out of your own eye, and then you can see clearly to remove the speck out of your brother\u2019s eye."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t give that which is holy to the dogs, neither throw your pearls before the pigs, lest perhaps they trample them under their feet, and turn and tear you to pieces."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAsk, and it will be given you. Seek, and you will find. Knock, and it will be opened for you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For everyone who asks receives. He who seeks finds. To him who knocks it will be opened."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Or who is there among you who, if his son asks him for bread, will give him a stone?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Or if he asks for a fish, who will give him a serpent?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If you then, being evil, know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your Father who is in heaven give good things to those who ask him!"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore, whatever you desire for men to do to you, you shall also do to them; for this is the law and the prophets."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cEnter in by the narrow gate; for the gate is wide and the way is broad that leads to destruction, and there are many who enter in by it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"How narrow is the gate and the way is restricted that leads to life! There are few who find it."]],f:["TR reads \u201cBecause\u201d instead of \u201cHow\u201d"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBeware of false prophets, who come to you in sheep\u2019s clothing, but inwardly are ravening wolves."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"By their fruits you will know them. Do you gather grapes from thorns or figs from thistles?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Even so, every good tree produces good fruit, but the corrupt tree produces evil fruit."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"A good tree can\u2019t produce evil fruit, neither can a corrupt tree produce good fruit."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Every tree that doesn\u2019t grow good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Therefore by their fruits you will know them."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNot everyone who says to me, \u2018Lord, Lord,\u2019 will enter into the Kingdom of Heaven, but he who does the will of my Father who is in heaven."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Many will tell me in that day, \u2018Lord, Lord, didn\u2019t we prophesy in your name, in your name cast out demons, and in your name do many mighty works?\u2019"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then I will tell them, \u2018I never knew you. Depart from me, you who work iniquity.\u2019"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cEveryone therefore who hears these words of mine and does them, I will liken him to a wise man who built his house on the rock."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The rain came down, the floods came, and the winds blew and beat on that house; and it didn\u2019t fall, for it was founded on the rock."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Everyone who hears these words of mine and doesn\u2019t do them will be like a foolish man who built his house on the sand."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The rain came down, the floods came, and the winds blew and beat on that house; and it fell\u2014and its fall was great.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had finished saying these things, the multitudes were astonished at his teaching,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"for he taught them with authority, and not like the scribes."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came down from the mountain, great multitudes followed him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, a leper came to him and worshiped him, saying, \u201cLord, if you want to, you can make me clean.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus stretched out his hand and touched him, saying, \u201cI want to. Be made clean.\u201d Immediately his leprosy was cleansed."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cSee that you tell nobody; but go, show yourself to the priest, and offer the gift that Moses commanded, as a testimony to them.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came into Capernaum, a centurion came to him, asking him for help,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cLord, my servant lies in the house paralyzed, grievously tormented.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cI will come and heal him.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The centurion answered, \u201cLord, I\u2019m not worthy for you to come under my roof. Just say the word, and my servant will be healed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For I am also a man under authority, having under myself soldiers. I tell this one, \u2018Go,\u2019 and he goes; and tell another, \u2018Come,\u2019 and he comes; and tell my servant, \u2018Do this,\u2019 and he does it.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus heard it, he marveled and said to those who followed, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, I haven\u2019t found so great a faith, not even in Israel."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I tell you that many will come from the east and the west, and will sit down with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob in the Kingdom of Heaven,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"but the children of the Kingdom will be thrown out into the outer darkness. There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Jesus said to the centurion, \u201cGo your way. Let it be done for you as you have believed.\u201d His servant was healed in that hour."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus came into Peter\u2019s house, he saw his wife\u2019s mother lying sick with a fever."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He touched her hand, and the fever left her. So she got up and served him."]],f:["TR reads \u201cthem\u201d instead of \u201chim\u201d"]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When evening came, they brought to him many possessed with demons. He cast out the spirits with a word, and healed all who were sick,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"that it might be fulfilled which was spoken through Isaiah the prophet, saying, \u201cHe took our infirmities and bore our diseases.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Jesus saw great multitudes around him, he gave the order to depart to the other side."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"A scribe came and said to him, \u201cTeacher, I will follow you wherever you go.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cThe foxes have holes and the birds of the sky have nests, but the Son of Man has nowhere to lay his head.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Another of his disciples said to him, \u201cLord, allow me first to go and bury my father.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to him, \u201cFollow me, and leave the dead to bury their own dead.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"When he got into a boat, his disciples followed him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Behold, a violent storm came up on the sea, so much that the boat was covered with the waves; but he was asleep."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The disciples came to him and woke him up, saying, \u201cSave us, Lord! We are dying!\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhy are you fearful, O you of little faith?\u201d Then he got up, rebuked the wind and the sea, and there was a great calm."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"The men marveled, saying, \u201cWhat kind of man is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came to the other side, into the country of the Gergesenes, two people possessed by demons met him there, coming out of the tombs, exceedingly fierce, so that nobody could pass that way."]],f:["NU reads \u201cGadarenes\u201d"]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Behold, they cried out, saying, \u201cWhat do we have to do with you, Jesus, Son of God? Have you come here to torment us before the time?\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Now there was a herd of many pigs feeding far away from them."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The demons begged him, saying, \u201cIf you cast us out, permit us to go away into the herd of pigs.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cGo!\u201d"],[0,"They came out and went into the herd of pigs; and behold, the whole herd of pigs rushed down the cliff into the sea and died in the water."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Those who fed them fled and went away into the city and told everything, including what happened to those who were possessed with demons."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Behold, all the city came out to meet Jesus. When they saw him, they begged that he would depart from their borders."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He entered into a boat and crossed over, and came into his own city."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, they brought to him a man who was paralyzed, lying on a bed. Jesus, seeing their faith, said to the paralytic, \u201cSon, cheer up! Your sins are forgiven you.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, some of the scribes said to themselves, \u201cThis man blasphemes.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, knowing their thoughts, said, \u201cWhy do you think evil in your hearts?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For which is easier, to say, \u2018Your sins are forgiven;\u2019 or to say, \u2018Get up, and walk\u2019?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins\u2014\u201d (then he said to the paralytic), \u201cGet up, and take up your mat, and go to your house.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose and departed to his house."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But when the multitudes saw it, they marveled and glorified God, who had given such authority to men."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"As Jesus passed by from there, he saw a man called Matthew sitting at the tax collection office. He said to him, \u201cFollow me.\u201d He got up and followed him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As he sat in the house, behold, many tax collectors and sinners came and sat down with Jesus and his disciples."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When the Pharisees saw it, they said to his disciples, \u201cWhy does your teacher eat with tax collectors and sinners?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus heard it, he said to them, \u201cThose who are healthy have no need for a physician, but those who are sick do."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But you go and learn what this means: \u2018I desire mercy, and not sacrifice,\u2019 for I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.\u201d"]],f:["NU omits \u201cto repentance\u201d."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then John\u2019s disciples came to him, saying, \u201cWhy do we and the Pharisees fast often, but your disciples don\u2019t fast?\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cCan the friends of the bridegroom mourn as long as the bridegroom is with them? But the days will come when the bridegroom will be taken away from them, and then they will fast."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"No one puts a piece of unshrunk cloth on an old garment; for the patch would tear away from the garment, and a worse hole is made."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Neither do people put new wine into old wineskins, or else the skins would burst, and the wine be spilled, and the skins ruined. No, they put new wine into fresh wineskins, and both are preserved.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"While he told these things to them, behold, a ruler came and worshiped him, saying, \u201cMy daughter has just died, but come and lay your hand on her, and she will live.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus got up and followed him, as did his disciples."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Behold, a woman who had a discharge of blood for twelve years came behind him, and touched the fringe of his garment;"]],f:["or, tassel"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"for she said within herself, \u201cIf I just touch his garment, I will be made well.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus, turning around and seeing her, said, \u201cDaughter, cheer up! Your faith has made you well.\u201d And the woman was made well from that hour."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus came into the ruler\u2019s house and saw the flute players and the crowd in noisy disorder,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"he said to them, \u201cMake room, because the girl isn\u2019t dead, but sleeping.\u201d"],[0,"They were ridiculing him."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But when the crowd was sent out, he entered in, took her by the hand, and the girl arose."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The report of this went out into all that land."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"As Jesus passed by from there, two blind men followed him, calling out and saying, \u201cHave mercy on us, son of David!\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"When he had come into the house, the blind men came to him. Jesus said to them, \u201cDo you believe that I am able to do this?\u201d"],[0,"They told him, \u201cYes, Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he touched their eyes, saying, \u201cAccording to your faith be it done to you.\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Then their eyes were opened. Jesus strictly commanded them, saying, \u201cSee that no one knows about this.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But they went out and spread abroad his fame in all that land."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"As they went out, behold, a mute man who was demon possessed was brought to him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"When the demon was cast out, the mute man spoke. The multitudes marveled, saying, \u201cNothing like this has ever been seen in Israel!\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"But the Pharisees said, \u201cBy the prince of the demons, he casts out demons.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus went about all the cities and the villages, teaching in their synagogues and preaching the Good News of the Kingdom, and healing every disease and every sickness among the people."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion for them because they were harassed and scattered, like sheep without a shepherd."]],f:["TR reads \u201cweary\u201d instead of \u201charassed\u201d"]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Then he said to his disciples, \u201cThe harvest indeed is plentiful, but the laborers are few."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Pray therefore that the Lord of the harvest will send out laborers into his harvest.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He called to himself his twelve disciples, and gave them authority over unclean spirits, to cast them out, and to heal every disease and every sickness."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now the names of the twelve apostles are these. The first, Simon, who is called Peter; Andrew, his brother; James the son of Zebedee; John, his brother;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Philip; Bartholomew; Thomas; Matthew the tax collector; James the son of Alphaeus; Lebbaeus, who was also called Thaddaeus;"]],f:["NU omits \u201cLebbaeus, who was also called\u201d"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Simon the Zealot; and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus sent these twelve out and commanded them, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t go among the Gentiles, and don\u2019t enter into any city of the Samaritans."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Rather, go to the lost sheep of the house of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"As you go, preach, saying, \u2018The Kingdom of Heaven is at hand!\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Heal the sick, cleanse the lepers, and cast out demons. Freely you received, so freely give."]],f:["TR adds \u201craise the dead,\u201d"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t take any gold, silver, or brass in your money belts."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Take no bag for your journey, neither two coats, nor sandals, nor staff: for the laborer is worthy of his food."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Into whatever city or village you enter, find out who in it is worthy, and stay there until you go on."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"As you enter into the household, greet it."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"If the household is worthy, let your peace come on it, but if it isn\u2019t worthy, let your peace return to you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Whoever doesn\u2019t receive you or hear your words, as you go out of that house or that city, shake the dust off your feet."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, it will be more tolerable for the land of Sodom and Gomorrah in the day of judgment than for that city."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I send you out as sheep among wolves. Therefore be wise as serpents and harmless as doves."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But beware of men, for they will deliver you up to councils, and in their synagogues they will scourge you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Yes, and you will be brought before governors and kings for my sake, for a testimony to them and to the nations."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But when they deliver you up, don\u2019t be anxious how or what you will say, for it will be given you in that hour what you will say."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For it is not you who speak, but the Spirit of your Father who speaks in you."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBrother will deliver up brother to death, and the father his child. Children will rise up against parents and cause them to be put to death."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You will be hated by all men for my name\u2019s sake, but he who endures to the end will be saved."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But when they persecute you in this city, flee into the next, for most certainly I tell you, you will not have gone through the cities of Israel until the Son of Man has come."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cA disciple is not above his teacher, nor a servant above his lord."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"It is enough for the disciple that he be like his teacher, and the servant like his lord. If they have called the master of the house Beelzebul, how much more those of his household!"]],f:["Literally, Lord of the Flies, or the devil"]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t be afraid of them, for there is nothing covered that will not be revealed, or hidden that will not be known."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"What I tell you in the darkness, speak in the light; and what you hear whispered in the ear, proclaim on the housetops."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be afraid of those who kill the body, but are not able to kill the soul. Rather, fear him who is able to destroy both soul and body in Gehenna."]],f:["or, Hell."]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAren\u2019t two sparrows sold for an assarion coin? Not one of them falls to the ground apart from your Father\u2019s will."]],f:["An assarion is a small coin worth one tenth of a drachma or a sixteenth of a denarius. An assarion is approximately the wages of one half hour of agricultural labor."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But the very hairs of your head are all numbered."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t be afraid. You are of more value than many sparrows."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Everyone therefore who confesses me before men, I will also confess him before my Father who is in heaven."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But whoever denies me before men, I will also deny him before my Father who is in heaven."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t think that I came to send peace on the earth. I didn\u2019t come to send peace, but a sword."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"For I came to set a man at odds against his father, and a daughter against her mother, and a daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"A man\u2019s foes will be those of his own household."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He who loves father or mother more than me is not worthy of me; and he who loves son or daughter more than me isn\u2019t worthy of me."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He who doesn\u2019t take his cross and follow after me isn\u2019t worthy of me."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"He who seeks his life will lose it; and he who loses his life for my sake will find it."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who receives you receives me, and he who receives me receives him who sent me."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He who receives a prophet in the name of a prophet will receive a prophet\u2019s reward. He who receives a righteous man in the name of a righteous man will receive a righteous man\u2019s reward."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Whoever gives one of these little ones just a cup of cold water to drink in the name of a disciple, most certainly I tell you, he will in no way lose his reward.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had finished directing his twelve disciples, he departed from there to teach and preach in their cities."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when John heard in the prison the works of Christ, he sent two of his disciples"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cAre you he who comes, or should we look for another?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cGo and tell John the things which you hear and see:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"the blind receive their sight, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised up, and the poor have good news preached to them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Blessed is he who finds no occasion for stumbling in me.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"As these went their way, Jesus began to say to the multitudes concerning John, \u201cWhat did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken by the wind?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But what did you go out to see? A man in soft clothing? Behold, those who wear soft clothing are in kings\u2019 houses."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But why did you go out? To see a prophet? Yes, I tell you, and much more than a prophet."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For this is he, of whom it is written, \u2018Behold, I send my messenger before your face, who will prepare your way before you.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, among those who are born of women there has not arisen anyone greater than John the Baptizer; yet he who is least in the Kingdom of Heaven is greater than he."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"From the days of John the Baptizer until now, the Kingdom of Heaven suffers violence, and the violent take it by force."]],f:["or, plunder it."]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For all the prophets and the law prophesied until John."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If you are willing to receive it, this is Elijah, who is to come."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He who has ears to hear, let him hear."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut to what shall I compare this generation? It is like children sitting in the marketplaces, who call to their companions"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018We played the flute for you, and you didn\u2019t dance. We mourned for you, and you didn\u2019t lament.\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For John came neither eating nor drinking, and they say, \u2018He has a demon.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The Son of Man came eating and drinking, and they say, \u2018Behold, a gluttonous man and a drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and sinners!\u2019 But wisdom is justified by her children.\u201d"]],f:["NU reads \u201cactions\u201d instead of \u201cchildren\u201d"]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he began to denounce the cities in which most of his mighty works had been done, because they didn\u2019t repent."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, Chorazin! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the mighty works had been done in Tyre and Sidon which were done in you, they would have repented long ago in sackcloth and ashes."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But I tell you, it will be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon on the day of judgment than for you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You, Capernaum, who are exalted to heaven, you will go down to Hades. For if the mighty works had been done in Sodom which were done in you, it would have remained until today."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But I tell you that it will be more tolerable for the land of Sodom on the day of judgment, than for you.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time, Jesus answered, \u201cI thank you, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that you hid these things from the wise and understanding, and revealed them to infants."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Yes, Father, for so it was well-pleasing in your sight."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"All things have been delivered to me by my Father. No one knows the Son, except the Father; neither does anyone know the Father, except the Son and he to whom the Son desires to reveal him."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cCome to me, all you who labor and are heavily burdened, and I will give you rest."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Take my yoke upon you and learn from me, for I am gentle and humble in heart; and you will find rest for your souls."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time, Jesus went on the Sabbath day through the grain fields. His disciples were hungry and began to pluck heads of grain and to eat."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But the Pharisees, when they saw it, said to him, \u201cBehold, your disciples do what is not lawful to do on the Sabbath.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said to them, \u201cHaven\u2019t you read what David did when he was hungry, and those who were with him:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"how he entered into God\u2019s house and ate the show bread, which was not lawful for him to eat, nor for those who were with him, but only for the priests?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Or have you not read in the law that on the Sabbath day the priests in the temple profane the Sabbath and are guiltless?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But I tell you that one greater than the temple is here."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But if you had known what this means, \u2018I desire mercy, and not sacrifice,\u2019 you wouldn\u2019t have condemned the guiltless."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He departed from there and went into their synagogue."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"And behold, there was a man with a withered hand. They asked him, \u201cIs it lawful to heal on the Sabbath day?\u201d so that they might accuse him."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat man is there among you who has one sheep, and if this one falls into a pit on the Sabbath day, won\u2019t he grab on to it and lift it out?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Of how much more value then is a man than a sheep! Therefore it is lawful to do good on the Sabbath day.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then he told the man, \u201cStretch out your hand.\u201d He stretched it out; and it was restored whole, just like the other."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But the Pharisees went out and conspired against him, how they might destroy him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, perceiving that, withdrew from there. Great multitudes followed him; and he healed them all,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and commanded them that they should not make him known,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"that it might be fulfilled which was spoken through Isaiah the prophet, saying,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBehold, my servant whom I have chosen,"],[2,"my beloved in whom my soul is well pleased."],[1,"I will put my Spirit on him."],[2,"He will proclaim justice to the nations."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"He will not strive, nor shout,"],[2,"neither will anyone hear his voice in the streets."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"He won\u2019t break a bruised reed."],[2,"He won\u2019t quench a smoking flax,"],[1,"until he leads justice to victory."]]},{v:21,l:[[2,"In his name, the nations will hope.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then one possessed by a demon, blind and mute, was brought to him; and he healed him, so that the blind and mute man both spoke and saw."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"All the multitudes were amazed, and said, \u201cCan this be the son of David?\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But when the Pharisees heard it, they said, \u201cThis man does not cast out demons except by Beelzebul, the prince of the demons.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Knowing their thoughts, Jesus said to them, \u201cEvery kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation, and every city or house divided against itself will not stand."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"If Satan casts out Satan, he is divided against himself. How then will his kingdom stand?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"If I by Beelzebul cast out demons, by whom do your children cast them out? Therefore they will be your judges."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But if I by the Spirit of God cast out demons, then God\u2019s Kingdom has come upon you."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Or how can one enter into the house of the strong man and plunder his goods, unless he first bind the strong man? Then he will plunder his house."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who is not with me is against me, and he who doesn\u2019t gather with me, scatters."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Therefore I tell you, every sin and blasphemy will be forgiven men, but the blasphemy against the Spirit will not be forgiven men."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Whoever speaks a word against the Son of Man, it will be forgiven him; but whoever speaks against the Holy Spirit, it will not be forgiven him, either in this age, or in that which is to come."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cEither make the tree good and its fruit good, or make the tree corrupt and its fruit corrupt; for the tree is known by its fruit."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"You offspring of vipers, how can you, being evil, speak good things? For out of the abundance of the heart, the mouth speaks."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The good man out of his good treasure brings out good things, and the evil man out of his evil treasure brings out evil things."]],f:["TR adds \u201cof the heart\u201d"]},{v:36,l:[[0,"I tell you that every idle word that men speak, they will give account of it in the day of judgment."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For by your words you will be justified, and by your words you will be condemned.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Then certain of the scribes and Pharisees answered, \u201cTeacher, we want to see a sign from you.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered them, \u201cAn evil and adulterous generation seeks after a sign, but no sign will be given to it but the sign of Jonah the prophet."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"For as Jonah was three days and three nights in the belly of the huge fish, so will the Son of Man be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The men of Nineveh will stand up in the judgment with this generation and will condemn it, for they repented at the preaching of Jonah; and behold, someone greater than Jonah is here."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"The Queen of the South will rise up in the judgment with this generation and will condemn it, for she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and behold, someone greater than Solomon is here."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen an unclean spirit has gone out of a man, he passes through waterless places seeking rest, and doesn\u2019t find it."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Then he says, \u2018I will return into my house from which I came;\u2019 and when he has come back, he finds it empty, swept, and put in order."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Then he goes and takes with himself seven other spirits more evil than he is, and they enter in and dwell there. The last state of that man becomes worse than the first. Even so will it be also to this evil generation.\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was yet speaking to the multitudes, behold, his mother and his brothers stood outside, seeking to speak to him."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"One said to him, \u201cBehold, your mother and your brothers stand outside, seeking to speak to you.\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered him who spoke to him, \u201cWho is my mother? Who are my brothers?\u201d"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"He stretched out his hand toward his disciples, and said, \u201cBehold, my mother and my brothers!"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"For whoever does the will of my Father who is in heaven, he is my brother, and sister, and mother.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"On that day Jesus went out of the house and sat by the seaside."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Great multitudes gathered to him, so that he entered into a boat and sat; and all the multitude stood on the beach."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He spoke to them many things in parables, saying, \u201cBehold, a farmer went out to sow."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"As he sowed, some seeds fell by the roadside, and the birds came and devoured them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Others fell on rocky ground, where they didn\u2019t have much soil, and immediately they sprang up, because they had no depth of earth."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When the sun had risen, they were scorched. Because they had no root, they withered away."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Others fell among thorns. The thorns grew up and choked them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Others fell on good soil and yielded fruit: some one hundred times as much, some sixty, and some thirty."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He who has ears to hear, let him hear.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples came, and said to him, \u201cWhy do you speak to them in parables?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cTo you it is given to know the mysteries of the Kingdom of Heaven, but it is not given to them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For whoever has, to him will be given, and he will have abundance; but whoever doesn\u2019t have, from him will be taken away even that which he has."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore I speak to them in parables, because seeing they don\u2019t see, and hearing, they don\u2019t hear, neither do they understand."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"In them the prophecy of Isaiah is fulfilled, which says,"],[1,"\u2018By hearing you will hear,"],[2,"and will in no way understand;"],[1,"Seeing you will see,"],[2,"and will in no way perceive;"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"for this people\u2019s heart has grown callous,"],[2,"their ears are dull of hearing,"],[2,"and they have closed their eyes;"],[1,"or else perhaps they might perceive with their eyes,"],[2,"hear with their ears,"],[2,"understand with their heart,"],[1,"and would turn again,"],[2,"and I would heal them.\u2019"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut blessed are your eyes, for they see; and your ears, for they hear."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For most certainly I tell you that many prophets and righteous men desired to see the things which you see, and didn\u2019t see them; and to hear the things which you hear, and didn\u2019t hear them."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHear, then, the parable of the farmer."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When anyone hears the word of the Kingdom and doesn\u2019t understand it, the evil one comes and snatches away that which has been sown in his heart. This is what was sown by the roadside."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"What was sown on the rocky places, this is he who hears the word and immediately with joy receives it;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"yet he has no root in himself, but endures for a while. When oppression or persecution arises because of the word, immediately he stumbles."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"What was sown among the thorns, this is he who hears the word, but the cares of this age and the deceitfulness of riches choke the word, and he becomes unfruitful."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"What was sown on the good ground, this is he who hears the word and understands it, who most certainly bears fruit and produces, some one hundred times as much, some sixty, and some thirty.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"He set another parable before them, saying, \u201cThe Kingdom of Heaven is like a man who sowed good seed in his field,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"but while people slept, his enemy came and sowed darnel weeds also among the wheat, and went away."]],f:["darnel is a weed grass (probably bearded darnel or lolium temulentum) that looks very much like wheat until it is mature, when the difference becomes very apparent."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But when the blade sprang up and produced grain, then the darnel weeds appeared also."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The servants of the householder came and said to him, \u2018Sir, didn\u2019t you sow good seed in your field? Where did these darnel weeds come from?\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said to them, \u2018An enemy has done this.\u2019"],[0,"\u201cThe servants asked him, \u2018Do you want us to go and gather them up?\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut he said, \u2018No, lest perhaps while you gather up the darnel weeds, you root up the wheat with them."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Let both grow together until the harvest, and in the harvest time I will tell the reapers, \u201cFirst, gather up the darnel weeds, and bind them in bundles to burn them; but gather the wheat into my barn.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"He set another parable before them, saying, \u201cThe Kingdom of Heaven is like a grain of mustard seed which a man took, and sowed in his field,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"which indeed is smaller than all seeds. But when it is grown, it is greater than the herbs and becomes a tree, so that the birds of the air come and lodge in its branches.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"He spoke another parable to them. \u201cThe Kingdom of Heaven is like yeast which a woman took and hid in three measures of meal, until it was all leavened.\u201d"]],f:["literally, three sata. Three sata is about 39 liters or a bit more than a bushel"]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus spoke all these things in parables to the multitudes; and without a parable, he didn\u2019t speak to them,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"that it might be fulfilled which was spoken through the prophet, saying,"],[1,"\u201cI will open my mouth in parables;"],[2,"I will utter things hidden from the foundation of the world.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus sent the multitudes away, and went into the house. His disciples came to him, saying, \u201cExplain to us the parable of the darnel weeds of the field.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cHe who sows the good seed is the Son of Man,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"the field is the world, the good seeds are the children of the Kingdom, and the darnel weeds are the children of the evil one."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The enemy who sowed them is the devil. The harvest is the end of the age, and the reapers are angels."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"As therefore the darnel weeds are gathered up and burned with fire; so will it be at the end of this age."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"The Son of Man will send out his angels, and they will gather out of his Kingdom all things that cause stumbling and those who do iniquity,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"and will cast them into the furnace of fire. There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Then the righteous will shine like the sun in the Kingdom of their Father. He who has ears to hear, let him hear."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAgain, the Kingdom of Heaven is like treasure hidden in the field, which a man found and hid. In his joy, he goes and sells all that he has and buys that field."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAgain, the Kingdom of Heaven is like a man who is a merchant seeking fine pearls,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"who having found one pearl of great price, he went and sold all that he had and bought it."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAgain, the Kingdom of Heaven is like a dragnet that was cast into the sea and gathered some fish of every kind,"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"which, when it was filled, fishermen drew up on the beach. They sat down and gathered the good into containers, but the bad they threw away."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"So it will be in the end of the world. The angels will come and separate the wicked from among the righteous,"]],f:["or, end of the age."]},{v:50,l:[[0,"and will cast them into the furnace of fire. There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.\u201d"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cHave you understood all these things?\u201d"],[0,"They answered him, \u201cYes, Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cTherefore every scribe who has been made a disciple in the Kingdom of Heaven is like a man who is a householder, who brings out of his treasure new and old things.\u201d"]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had finished these parables, he departed from there."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"Coming into his own country, he taught them in their synagogue, so that they were astonished and said, \u201cWhere did this man get this wisdom and these mighty works?"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t this the carpenter\u2019s son? Isn\u2019t his mother called Mary, and his brothers James, Joses, Simon, and Judas?"]],f:["or, Judah"]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t all of his sisters with us? Where then did this man get all of these things?\u201d"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"They were offended by him."],[0,"But Jesus said to them, \u201cA prophet is not without honor, except in his own country and in his own house.\u201d"]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"He didn\u2019t do many mighty works there because of their unbelief."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"At that time, Herod the tetrarch heard the report concerning Jesus,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and said to his servants, \u201cThis is John the Baptizer. He is risen from the dead. That is why these powers work in him.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For Herod had arrested John, bound him, and put him in prison for the sake of Herodias, his brother Philip\u2019s wife."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For John said to him, \u201cIt is not lawful for you to have her.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When he would have put him to death, he feared the multitude, because they counted him as a prophet."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But when Herod\u2019s birthday came, the daughter of Herodias danced among them and pleased Herod."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore he promised with an oath to give her whatever she should ask."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"She, being prompted by her mother, said, \u201cGive me here on a platter the head of John the Baptizer.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The king was grieved, but for the sake of his oaths and of those who sat at the table with him, he commanded it to be given,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and he sent and beheaded John in the prison."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"His head was brought on a platter and given to the young lady; and she brought it to her mother."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"His disciples came, took the body, and buried it. Then they went and told Jesus."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now when Jesus heard this, he withdrew from there in a boat to a deserted place apart. When the multitudes heard it, they followed him on foot from the cities."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus went out, and he saw a great multitude. He had compassion on them and healed their sick."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When evening had come, his disciples came to him, saying, \u201cThis place is deserted, and the hour is already late. Send the multitudes away, that they may go into the villages, and buy themselves food.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to them, \u201cThey don\u2019t need to go away. You give them something to eat.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"They told him, \u201cWe only have here five loaves and two fish.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBring them here to me.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He commanded the multitudes to sit down on the grass; and he took the five loaves and the two fish, and looking up to heaven, he blessed, broke and gave the loaves to the disciples; and the disciples gave to the multitudes."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They all ate and were filled. They took up twelve baskets full of that which remained left over from the broken pieces."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Those who ate were about five thousand men, in addition to women and children."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately Jesus made the disciples get into the boat and go ahead of him to the other side, while he sent the multitudes away."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"After he had sent the multitudes away, he went up into the mountain by himself to pray. When evening had come, he was there alone."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But the boat was now in the middle of the sea, distressed by the waves, for the wind was contrary."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In the fourth watch of the night, Jesus came to them, walking on the sea."]],f:["The night was equally divided into four watches, so the fourth watch is approximately 3:00 a.m. to sunrise."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When the disciples saw him walking on the sea, they were troubled, saying, \u201cIt\u2019s a ghost!\u201d and they cried out for fear."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But immediately Jesus spoke to them, saying, \u201cCheer up! It is I! Don\u2019t be afraid.\u201d"]],f:["or, I AM!"]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter answered him and said, \u201cLord, if it is you, command me to come to you on the waters.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cCome!\u201d"],[0,"Peter stepped down from the boat and walked on the waters to come to Jesus."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But when he saw that the wind was strong, he was afraid, and beginning to sink, he cried out, saying, \u201cLord, save me!\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately Jesus stretched out his hand, took hold of him, and said to him, \u201cYou of little faith, why did you doubt?\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"When they got up into the boat, the wind ceased."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Those who were in the boat came and worshiped him, saying, \u201cYou are truly the Son of God!\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had crossed over, they came to the land of Gennesaret."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"When the people of that place recognized him, they sent into all that surrounding region and brought to him all who were sick;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"and they begged him that they might just touch the fringe of his garment. As many as touched it were made whole."]],f:["or, tassel"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Pharisees and scribes came to Jesus from Jerusalem, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cWhy do your disciples disobey the tradition of the elders? For they don\u2019t wash their hands when they eat bread.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cWhy do you also disobey the commandment of God because of your tradition?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For God commanded, \u2018Honor your father and your mother,\u2019 and, \u2018He who speaks evil of father or mother, let him be put to death.\u2019"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But you say, \u2018Whoever may tell his father or his mother, \u201cWhatever help you might otherwise have gotten from me is a gift devoted to God,\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"he shall not honor his father or mother.\u2019 You have made the commandment of God void because of your tradition."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You hypocrites! Well did Isaiah prophesy of you, saying,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018These people draw near to me with their mouth,"],[2,"and honor me with their lips;"],[2,"but their heart is far from me."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"And they worship me in vain,"],[2,"teaching as doctrine rules made by men.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He summoned the multitude, and said to them, \u201cHear, and understand."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"That which enters into the mouth doesn\u2019t defile the man; but that which proceeds out of the mouth, this defiles the man.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the disciples came and said to him, \u201cDo you know that the Pharisees were offended when they heard this saying?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered, \u201cEvery plant which my heavenly Father didn\u2019t plant will be uprooted."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Leave them alone. They are blind guides of the blind. If the blind guide the blind, both will fall into a pit.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter answered him, \u201cExplain the parable to us.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So Jesus said, \u201cDo you also still not understand?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you understand that whatever goes into the mouth passes into the belly and then out of the body?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But the things which proceed out of the mouth come out of the heart, and they defile the man."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For out of the heart come evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, sexual sins, thefts, false testimony, and blasphemies."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"These are the things which defile the man; but to eat with unwashed hands doesn\u2019t defile the man.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus went out from there and withdrew into the region of Tyre and Sidon."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Behold, a Canaanite woman came out from those borders and cried, saying, \u201cHave mercy on me, Lord, you son of David! My daughter is severely possessed by a demon!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered her not a word."],[0,"His disciples came and begged him, saying, \u201cSend her away; for she cries after us.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered, \u201cI wasn\u2019t sent to anyone but the lost sheep of the house of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But she came and worshiped him, saying, \u201cLord, help me.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered, \u201cIt is not appropriate to take the children\u2019s bread and throw it to the dogs.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But she said, \u201cYes, Lord, but even the dogs eat the crumbs which fall from their masters\u2019 table.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus answered her, \u201cWoman, great is your faith! Be it done to you even as you desire.\u201d And her daughter was healed from that hour."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus departed from there and came near to the sea of Galilee; and he went up on the mountain and sat there."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Great multitudes came to him, having with them the lame, blind, mute, maimed, and many others, and they put them down at his feet. He healed them,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"so that the multitude wondered when they saw the mute speaking, the injured healed, the lame walking, and the blind seeing\u2014and they glorified the God of Israel."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus summoned his disciples and said, \u201cI have compassion on the multitude, because they have continued with me now three days and have nothing to eat. I don\u2019t want to send them away fasting, or they might faint on the way.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples said to him, \u201cWhere could we get so many loaves in a deserted place as to satisfy so great a multitude?\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cHow many loaves do you have?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cSeven, and a few small fish.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"He commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"and he took the seven loaves and the fish. He gave thanks and broke them, and gave to the disciples, and the disciples to the multitudes."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They all ate and were filled. They took up seven baskets full of the broken pieces that were left over."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Those who ate were four thousand men, in addition to women and children."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Then he sent away the multitudes, got into the boat, and came into the borders of Magdala."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The Pharisees and Sadducees came, and testing him, asked him to show them a sign from heaven."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But he answered them, \u201cWhen it is evening, you say, \u2018It will be fair weather, for the sky is red.\u2019"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In the morning, \u2018It will be foul weather today, for the sky is red and threatening.\u2019 Hypocrites! You know how to discern the appearance of the sky, but you can\u2019t discern the signs of the times!"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"An evil and adulterous generation seeks after a sign, and there will be no sign given to it, except the sign of the prophet Jonah.\u201d"],[0,"He left them and departed."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The disciples came to the other side and had forgotten to take bread."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cTake heed and beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They reasoned among themselves, saying, \u201cWe brought no bread.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, perceiving it, said, \u201cWhy do you reason among yourselves, you of little faith, because you have brought no bread?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you yet perceive or remember the five loaves for the five thousand, and how many baskets you took up,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"or the seven loaves for the four thousand, and how many baskets you took up?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"How is it that you don\u2019t perceive that I didn\u2019t speak to you concerning bread? But beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they understood that he didn\u2019t tell them to beware of the yeast of bread, but of the teaching of the Pharisees and Sadducees."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Jesus came into the parts of Caesarea Philippi, he asked his disciples, saying, \u201cWho do men say that I, the Son of Man, am?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cSome say John the Baptizer, some, Elijah, and others, Jeremiah or one of the prophets.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cBut who do you say that I am?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter answered, \u201cYou are the Christ, the Son of the living God.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cBlessed are you, Simon Bar Jonah, for flesh and blood has not revealed this to you, but my Father who is in heaven."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I also tell you that you are Peter, and on this rock I will build my assembly, and the gates of Hades will not prevail against it."]],f:["Peter\u2019s name, Petros in Greek, is the word for a specific rock or stone.","Greek, petra, a rock mass or bedrock.","or, Hell"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I will give to you the keys of the Kingdom of Heaven, and whatever you bind on earth will have been bound in heaven; and whatever you release on earth will have been released in heaven.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Then he commanded the disciples that they should tell no one that he was Jesus the Christ."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"From that time, Jesus began to show his disciples that he must go to Jerusalem and suffer many things from the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and be killed, and the third day be raised up."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter took him aside and began to rebuke him, saying, \u201cFar be it from you, Lord! This will never be done to you.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But he turned and said to Peter, \u201cGet behind me, Satan! You are a stumbling block to me, for you are not setting your mind on the things of God, but on the things of men.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said to his disciples, \u201cIf anyone desires to come after me, let him deny himself, take up his cross, and follow me."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For whoever desires to save his life will lose it, and whoever will lose his life for my sake will find it."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For what will it profit a man if he gains the whole world and forfeits his life? Or what will a man give in exchange for his life?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For the Son of Man will come in the glory of his Father with his angels, and then he will give to everyone according to his deeds."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, there are some standing here who will in no way taste of death until they see the Son of Man coming in his Kingdom.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After six days, Jesus took with him Peter, James, and John his brother, and brought them up into a high mountain by themselves."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He was changed before them. His face shone like the sun, and his garments became as white as the light."]],f:["or, transfigured"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Behold, Moses and Elijah appeared to them talking with him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter answered and said to Jesus, \u201cLord, it is good for us to be here. If you want, let\u2019s make three tents here: one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still speaking, behold, a bright cloud overshadowed them. Behold, a voice came out of the cloud, saying, \u201cThis is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased. Listen to him.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When the disciples heard it, they fell on their faces, and were very afraid."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Jesus came and touched them and said, \u201cGet up, and don\u2019t be afraid.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Lifting up their eyes, they saw no one, except Jesus alone."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"As they were coming down from the mountain, Jesus commanded them, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t tell anyone what you saw, until the Son of Man has risen from the dead.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"His disciples asked him, saying, \u201cThen why do the scribes say that Elijah must come first?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cElijah indeed comes first, and will restore all things;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"but I tell you that Elijah has come already, and they didn\u2019t recognize him, but did to him whatever they wanted to. Even so the Son of Man will also suffer by them.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then the disciples understood that he spoke to them of John the Baptizer."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When they came to the multitude, a man came to him, kneeling down to him and saying,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cLord, have mercy on my son, for he is epileptic and suffers grievously; for he often falls into the fire, and often into the water."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So I brought him to your disciples, and they could not cure him.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cFaithless and perverse generation! How long will I be with you? How long will I bear with you? Bring him here to me.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jesus rebuked the demon, and it went out of him, and the boy was cured from that hour."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the disciples came to Jesus privately, and said, \u201cWhy weren\u2019t we able to cast it out?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cBecause of your unbelief. For most certainly I tell you, if you have faith as a grain of mustard seed, you will tell this mountain, \u2018Move from here to there,\u2019 and it will move; and nothing will be impossible for you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But this kind doesn\u2019t go out except by prayer and fasting.\u201d"]],f:["NU omits verse 21."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"While they were staying in Galilee, Jesus said to them, \u201cThe Son of Man is about to be delivered up into the hands of men,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and they will kill him, and the third day he will be raised up.\u201d"],[0,"They were exceedingly sorry."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had come to Capernaum, those who collected the didrachma coins came to Peter, and said, \u201cDoesn\u2019t your teacher pay the didrachma?\u201d"]],f:["A didrachma is a Greek silver coin worth 2 drachmas, about as much as 2 Roman denarii, or about 2 days\u2019 wages. It was commonly used to pay the half-shekel temple tax, because 2 drachmas were worth one half shekel of silver. A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cYes.\u201d"],[0,"When he came into the house, Jesus anticipated him, saying, \u201cWhat do you think, Simon? From whom do the kings of the earth receive toll or tribute? From their children, or from strangers?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter said to him, \u201cFrom strangers.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cTherefore the children are exempt."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But, lest we cause them to stumble, go to the sea, cast a hook, and take up the first fish that comes up. When you have opened its mouth, you will find a stater coin. Take that, and give it to them for me and you.\u201d"]],f:["A stater is a silver coin equivalent to four Attic or two Alexandrian drachmas, or a Jewish shekel: just exactly enough to cover the half-shekel temple tax for two people. A shekel is about 10 grams or about 0.35 ounces, usually in the form of a silver coin."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In that hour the disciples came to Jesus, saying, \u201cWho then is greatest in the Kingdom of Heaven?\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus called a little child to himself, and set him in the middle of them"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, unless you turn and become as little children, you will in no way enter into the Kingdom of Heaven."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Whoever therefore humbles himself as this little child is the greatest in the Kingdom of Heaven."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Whoever receives one such little child in my name receives me,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but whoever causes one of these little ones who believe in me to stumble, it would be better for him if a huge millstone were hung around his neck and that he were sunk in the depths of the sea."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to the world because of occasions of stumbling! For it must be that the occasions come, but woe to that person through whom the occasion comes!"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If your hand or your foot causes you to stumble, cut it off and cast it from you. It is better for you to enter into life maimed or crippled, rather than having two hands or two feet to be cast into the eternal fire."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If your eye causes you to stumble, pluck it out and cast it from you. It is better for you to enter into life with one eye, rather than having two eyes to be cast into the Gehenna of fire."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"See that you don\u2019t despise one of these little ones, for I tell you that in heaven their angels always see the face of my Father who is in heaven."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the Son of Man came to save that which was lost."]],f:["NU omits verse 11."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhat do you think? If a man has one hundred sheep, and one of them goes astray, doesn\u2019t he leave the ninety-nine, go to the mountains, and seek that which has gone astray?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"If he finds it, most certainly I tell you, he rejoices over it more than over the ninety-nine which have not gone astray."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Even so it is not the will of your Father who is in heaven that one of these little ones should perish."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf your brother sins against you, go, show him his fault between you and him alone. If he listens to you, you have gained back your brother."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But if he doesn\u2019t listen, take one or two more with you, that at the mouth of two or three witnesses every word may be established."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If he refuses to listen to them, tell it to the assembly. If he refuses to hear the assembly also, let him be to you as a Gentile or a tax collector."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, whatever things you bind on earth will have been bound in heaven, and whatever things you release on earth will have been released in heaven."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Again, assuredly I tell you, that if two of you will agree on earth concerning anything that they will ask, it will be done for them by my Father who is in heaven."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For where two or three are gathered together in my name, there I am in the middle of them.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Peter came and said to him, \u201cLord, how often shall my brother sin against me, and I forgive him? Until seven times?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cI don\u2019t tell you until seven times, but, until seventy times seven."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Therefore the Kingdom of Heaven is like a certain king who wanted to settle accounts with his servants."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When he had begun to settle, one was brought to him who owed him ten thousand talents."]],f:["Ten thousand talents (about 300 metric tons of silver) represents an extremely large sum of money, equivalent to about 60,000,000 denarii, where one denarius was typical of one day\u2019s wages for agricultural labor."]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But because he couldn\u2019t pay, his lord commanded him to be sold, with his wife, his children, and all that he had, and payment to be made."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The servant therefore fell down and knelt before him, saying, \u2018Lord, have patience with me, and I will repay you all!\u2019"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The lord of that servant, being moved with compassion, released him and forgave him the debt."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut that servant went out and found one of his fellow servants who owed him one hundred denarii, and he grabbed him and took him by the throat, saying, \u2018Pay me what you owe!\u2019"]],f:["100 denarii was about one sixtieth of a talent, or about 500 grams (1.1 pounds) of silver."]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo his fellow servant fell down at his feet and begged him, saying, \u2018Have patience with me, and I will repay you!\u2019"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He would not, but went and cast him into prison until he should pay back that which was due."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"So when his fellow servants saw what was done, they were exceedingly sorry, and came and told their lord all that was done."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Then his lord called him in and said to him, \u2018You wicked servant! I forgave you all that debt because you begged me."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Shouldn\u2019t you also have had mercy on your fellow servant, even as I had mercy on you?\u2019"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"His lord was angry, and delivered him to the tormentors until he should pay all that was due to him."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"So my heavenly Father will also do to you, if you don\u2019t each forgive your brother from your hearts for his misdeeds.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had finished these words, he departed from Galilee and came into the borders of Judea beyond the Jordan."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Great multitudes followed him, and he healed them there."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharisees came to him, testing him and saying, \u201cIs it lawful for a man to divorce his wife for any reason?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cHaven\u2019t you read that he who made them from the beginning made them male and female,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and said, \u2018For this cause a man shall leave his father and mother, and shall be joined to his wife; and the two shall become one flesh\u2019?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So that they are no more two, but one flesh. What therefore God has joined together, don\u2019t let man tear apart.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cWhy then did Moses command us to give her a certificate of divorce and divorce her?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cMoses, because of the hardness of your hearts, allowed you to divorce your wives, but from the beginning it has not been so."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I tell you that whoever divorces his wife, except for sexual immorality, and marries another, commits adultery; and he who marries her when she is divorced commits adultery.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"His disciples said to him, \u201cIf this is the case of the man with his wife, it is not expedient to marry.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said to them, \u201cNot all men can receive this saying, but those to whom it is given."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For there are eunuchs who were born that way from their mother\u2019s womb, and there are eunuchs who were made eunuchs by men; and there are eunuchs who made themselves eunuchs for the Kingdom of Heaven\u2019s sake. He who is able to receive it, let him receive it.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then little children were brought to him that he should lay his hands on them and pray; and the disciples rebuked them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But Jesus said, \u201cAllow the little children, and don\u2019t forbid them to come to me; for the Kingdom of Heaven belongs to ones like these.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He laid his hands on them, and departed from there."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, one came to him and said, \u201cGood teacher, what good thing shall I do, that I may have eternal life?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cWhy do you call me good? No one is good but one, that is, God. But if you want to enter into life, keep the commandments.\u201d"]],f:["So MT and TR. NU reads \u201cWhy do you ask me about what is good?\u201d"]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cWhich ones?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said, \u201c\u2018You shall not murder.\u2019 \u2018You shall not commit adultery.\u2019 \u2018You shall not steal.\u2019 \u2018You shall not offer false testimony.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"\u2018Honor your father and your mother.\u2019 And, \u2018You shall love your neighbor as yourself.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The young man said to him, \u201cAll these things I have observed from my youth. What do I still lack?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cIf you want to be perfect, go, sell what you have, and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven; and come, follow me.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But when the young man heard this, he went away sad, for he was one who had great possessions."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to his disciples, \u201cMost certainly I say to you, a rich man will enter into the Kingdom of Heaven with difficulty."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Again I tell you, it is easier for a camel to go through a needle\u2019s eye than for a rich man to enter into God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"When the disciples heard it, they were exceedingly astonished, saying, \u201cWho then can be saved?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Looking at them, Jesus said, \u201cWith men this is impossible, but with God all things are possible.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Peter answered, \u201cBehold, we have left everything and followed you. What then will we have?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you that you who have followed me, in the regeneration when the Son of Man will sit on the throne of his glory, you also will sit on twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Everyone who has left houses, or brothers, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or lands, for my name\u2019s sake, will receive one hundred times, and will inherit eternal life."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But many will be last who are first, and first who are last."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor the Kingdom of Heaven is like a man who was the master of a household, who went out early in the morning to hire laborers for his vineyard."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When he had agreed with the laborers for a denarius a day, he sent them into his vineyard."]],f:["A denarius is a silver Roman coin worth 1/25th of a Roman aureus. This was a common wage for a day of farm labor."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He went out about the third hour, and saw others standing idle in the marketplace."]],f:["Time was measured from sunrise to sunset, so the third hour would be about 9:00 a.m."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u2018You also go into the vineyard, and whatever is right I will give you.\u2019 So they went their way."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Again he went out about the sixth and the ninth hour, and did likewise."]],f:["noon and 3:00 p.m."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"About the eleventh hour he went out and found others standing idle. He said to them, \u2018Why do you stand here all day idle?\u2019"]],f:["5:00 p.m."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey said to him, \u2018Because no one has hired us.\u2019"],[0,"\u201cHe said to them, \u2018You also go into the vineyard, and you will receive whatever is right.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen evening had come, the lord of the vineyard said to his manager, \u2018Call the laborers and pay them their wages, beginning from the last to the first.\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen those who were hired at about the eleventh hour came, they each received a denarius."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When the first came, they supposed that they would receive more; and they likewise each received a denarius."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When they received it, they murmured against the master of the household,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"saying, \u2018These last have spent one hour, and you have made them equal to us who have borne the burden of the day and the scorching heat!\u2019"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut he answered one of them, \u2018Friend, I am doing you no wrong. Didn\u2019t you agree with me for a denarius?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Take that which is yours, and go your way. It is my desire to give to this last just as much as to you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t it lawful for me to do what I want to with what I own? Or is your eye evil, because I am good?\u2019"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So the last will be first, and the first last. For many are called, but few are chosen.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"As Jesus was going up to Jerusalem, he took the twelve disciples aside, and on the way he said to them,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, we are going up to Jerusalem, and the Son of Man will be delivered to the chief priests and scribes, and they will condemn him to death,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and will hand him over to the Gentiles to mock, to scourge, and to crucify; and the third day he will be raised up.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the mother of the sons of Zebedee came to him with her sons, kneeling and asking a certain thing of him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cWhat do you want?\u201d"],[0,"She said to him, \u201cCommand that these, my two sons, may sit, one on your right hand and one on your left hand, in your Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus answered, \u201cYou don\u2019t know what you are asking. Are you able to drink the cup that I am about to drink, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cWe are able.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cYou will indeed drink my cup, and be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with; but to sit on my right hand and on my left hand is not mine to give, but it is for whom it has been prepared by my Father.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When the ten heard it, they were indignant with the two brothers."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus summoned them, and said, \u201cYou know that the rulers of the nations lord it over them, and their great ones exercise authority over them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"It shall not be so among you; but whoever desires to become great among you shall be your servant."]],f:["TR reads \u201clet him be\u201d instead of \u201cshall be\u201d"]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Whoever desires to be first among you shall be your bondservant,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"even as the Son of Man came not to be served, but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"As they went out from Jericho, a great multitude followed him."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Behold, two blind men sitting by the road, when they heard that Jesus was passing by, cried out, \u201cLord, have mercy on us, you son of David!\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The multitude rebuked them, telling them that they should be quiet, but they cried out even more, \u201cLord, have mercy on us, you son of David!\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus stood still and called them, and asked, \u201cWhat do you want me to do for you?\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"They told him, \u201cLord, that our eyes may be opened.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, being moved with compassion, touched their eyes; and immediately their eyes received their sight, and they followed him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When they came near to Jerusalem and came to Bethsphage, to the Mount of Olives, then Jesus sent two disciples,"]],f:["TR & NU read \u201cBethphage\u201d instead of \u201cBethsphage\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"saying to them, \u201cGo into the village that is opposite you, and immediately you will find a donkey tied, and a colt with her. Untie them and bring them to me."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If anyone says anything to you, you shall say, \u2018The Lord needs them,\u2019 and immediately he will send them.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"All this was done that it might be fulfilled which was spoken through the prophet, saying,"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTell the daughter of Zion,"],[2,"behold, your King comes to you,"],[2,"humble, and riding on a donkey,"],[2,"on a colt, the foal of a donkey.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples went and did just as Jesus commanded them,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and brought the donkey and the colt and laid their clothes on them; and he sat on them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"A very great multitude spread their clothes on the road. Others cut branches from the trees and spread them on the road."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The multitudes who went in front of him, and those who followed, kept shouting, \u201cHosanna to the son of David! Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord! Hosanna in the highest!\u201d"]],f:["\u201cHosanna\u201d means \u201csave us\u201d or \u201chelp us, we pray\u201d."]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had come into Jerusalem, all the city was stirred up, saying, \u201cWho is this?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The multitudes said, \u201cThis is the prophet, Jesus, from Nazareth of Galilee.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus entered into the temple of God and drove out all of those who sold and bought in the temple, and overthrew the money changers\u2019 tables and the seats of those who sold the doves."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cIt is written, \u2018My house shall be called a house of prayer,\u2019 but you have made it a den of robbers!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The lame and the blind came to him in the temple, and he healed them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But when the chief priests and the scribes saw the wonderful things that he did, and the children who were crying in the temple and saying, \u201cHosanna to the son of David!\u201d they were indignant,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cDo you hear what these are saying?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cYes. Did you never read, \u2018Out of the mouth of children and nursing babies, you have perfected praise\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He left them and went out of the city to Bethany, and camped there."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the morning, as he returned to the city, he was hungry."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Seeing a fig tree by the road, he came to it and found nothing on it but leaves. He said to it, \u201cLet there be no fruit from you forever!\u201d"],[0,"Immediately the fig tree withered away."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When the disciples saw it, they marveled, saying, \u201cHow did the fig tree immediately wither away?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, if you have faith and don\u2019t doubt, you will not only do what was done to the fig tree, but even if you told this mountain, \u2018Be taken up and cast into the sea,\u2019 it would be done."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"All things, whatever you ask in prayer, believing, you will receive.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had come into the temple, the chief priests and the elders of the people came to him as he was teaching, and said, \u201cBy what authority do you do these things? Who gave you this authority?\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cI also will ask you one question, which if you tell me, I likewise will tell you by what authority I do these things."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The baptism of John, where was it from? From heaven or from men?\u201d"],[0,"They reasoned with themselves, saying, \u201cIf we say, \u2018From heaven,\u2019 he will ask us, \u2018Why then did you not believe him?\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But if we say, \u2018From men,\u2019 we fear the multitude, for all hold John as a prophet.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They answered Jesus, and said, \u201cWe don\u2019t know.\u201d"],[0,"He also said to them, \u201cNeither will I tell you by what authority I do these things."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But what do you think? A man had two sons, and he came to the first, and said, \u2018Son, go work today in my vineyard.\u2019"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He answered, \u2018I will not,\u2019 but afterward he changed his mind, and went."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He came to the second, and said the same thing. He answered, \u2018I\u2019m going, sir,\u2019 but he didn\u2019t go."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Which of the two did the will of his father?\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cThe first.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you that the tax collectors and the prostitutes are entering into God\u2019s Kingdom before you."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For John came to you in the way of righteousness, and you didn\u2019t believe him; but the tax collectors and the prostitutes believed him. When you saw it, you didn\u2019t even repent afterward, that you might believe him."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHear another parable. There was a man who was a master of a household who planted a vineyard, set a hedge about it, dug a wine press in it, built a tower, leased it out to farmers, and went into another country."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"When the season for the fruit came near, he sent his servants to the farmers to receive his fruit."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The farmers took his servants, beat one, killed another, and stoned another."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Again, he sent other servants more than the first; and they treated them the same way."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"But afterward he sent to them his son, saying, \u2018They will respect my son.\u2019"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But the farmers, when they saw the son, said among themselves, \u2018This is the heir. Come, let\u2019s kill him and seize his inheritance.\u2019"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"So they took him and threw him out of the vineyard, then killed him."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"When therefore the lord of the vineyard comes, what will he do to those farmers?\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"They told him, \u201cHe will miserably destroy those miserable men, and will lease out the vineyard to other farmers who will give him the fruit in its season.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cDid you never read in the Scriptures,"],[1,"\u2018The stone which the builders rejected"],[2,"was made the head of the corner."],[1,"This was from the Lord."],[2,"It is marvelous in our eyes\u2019?"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore I tell you, God\u2019s Kingdom will be taken away from you and will be given to a nation producing its fruit."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"He who falls on this stone will be broken to pieces, but on whomever it will fall, it will scatter him as dust.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"When the chief priests and the Pharisees heard his parables, they perceived that he spoke about them."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"When they sought to seize him, they feared the multitudes, because they considered him to be a prophet."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered and spoke to them again in parables, saying,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cThe Kingdom of Heaven is like a certain king, who made a wedding feast for his son,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and sent out his servants to call those who were invited to the wedding feast, but they would not come."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Again he sent out other servants, saying, \u2018Tell those who are invited, \u201cBehold, I have prepared my dinner. My cattle and my fatlings are killed, and all things are ready. Come to the wedding feast!\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But they made light of it, and went their ways, one to his own farm, another to his merchandise;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and the rest grabbed his servants, treated them shamefully, and killed them."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When the king heard that, he was angry, and sent his armies, destroyed those murderers, and burned their city."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen he said to his servants, \u2018The wedding is ready, but those who were invited weren\u2019t worthy."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Go therefore to the intersections of the highways, and as many as you may find, invite to the wedding feast.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Those servants went out into the highways and gathered together as many as they found, both bad and good. The wedding was filled with guests."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut when the king came in to see the guests, he saw there a man who didn\u2019t have on wedding clothing,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and he said to him, \u2018Friend, how did you come in here not wearing wedding clothing?\u2019 He was speechless."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then the king said to the servants, \u2018Bind him hand and foot, take him away, and throw him into the outer darkness. That is where the weeping and grinding of teeth will be.\u2019"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For many are called, but few chosen.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Pharisees went and took counsel how they might entrap him in his talk."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They sent their disciples to him, along with the Herodians, saying, \u201cTeacher, we know that you are honest, and teach the way of God in truth, no matter whom you teach; for you aren\u2019t partial to anyone."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Tell us therefore, what do you think? Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar, or not?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus perceived their wickedness, and said, \u201cWhy do you test me, you hypocrites?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Show me the tax money.\u201d"],[0,"They brought to him a denarius."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He asked them, \u201cWhose is this image and inscription?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cCaesar\u2019s.\u201d"],[0,"Then he said to them, \u201cGive therefore to Caesar the things that are Caesar\u2019s, and to God the things that are God\u2019s.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"When they heard it, they marveled, and left him and went away."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"On that day Sadducees (those who say that there is no resurrection) came to him. They asked him,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cTeacher, Moses said, \u2018If a man dies, having no children, his brother shall marry his wife and raise up offspring for his brother.\u2019"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Now there were with us seven brothers. The first married and died, and having no offspring left his wife to his brother."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"In the same way, the second also, and the third, to the seventh."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"After them all, the woman died."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"In the resurrection therefore, whose wife will she be of the seven? For they all had her.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus answered them, \u201cYou are mistaken, not knowing the Scriptures, nor the power of God."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For in the resurrection they neither marry nor are given in marriage, but are like God\u2019s angels in heaven."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But concerning the resurrection of the dead, haven\u2019t you read that which was spoken to you by God, saying,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"\u2018I am the God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob\u2019? God is not the God of the dead, but of the living.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"When the multitudes heard it, they were astonished at his teaching."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"But the Pharisees, when they heard that he had silenced the Sadducees, gathered themselves together."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"One of them, a lawyer, asked him a question, testing him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"\u201cTeacher, which is the greatest commandment in the law?\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201c\u2018You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, with all your soul, and with all your mind.\u2019"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"This is the first and great commandment."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"A second likewise is this, \u2018You shall love your neighbor as yourself.\u2019"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The whole law and the prophets depend on these two commandments.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Now while the Pharisees were gathered together, Jesus asked them a question,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cWhat do you think of the Christ? Whose son is he?\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cOf David.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cHow then does David in the Spirit call him Lord, saying,"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018The Lord said to my Lord,"],[2,"sit on my right hand,"],[2,"until I make your enemies a footstool for your feet\u2019?"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf then David calls him Lord, how is he his son?\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"No one was able to answer him a word, neither did any man dare ask him any more questions from that day forward."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus spoke to the multitudes and to his disciples,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cThe scribes and the Pharisees sit on Moses\u2019 seat."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All things therefore whatever they tell you to observe, observe and do, but don\u2019t do their works; for they say, and don\u2019t do."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For they bind heavy burdens that are grievous to be borne, and lay them on men\u2019s shoulders; but they themselves will not lift a finger to help them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But they do all their works to be seen by men. They make their phylacteries broad and enlarge the fringes of their garments,"]],f:["phylacteries (tefillin in Hebrew) are small leather pouches that some Jewish men wear on their forehead and arm in prayer. They are used to carry a small scroll with some Scripture in it. See Deuteronomy 6:8.","or, tassels"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and love the place of honor at feasts, the best seats in the synagogues,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"the salutations in the marketplaces, and to be called \u2018Rabbi, Rabbi\u2019 by men."]],f:["NU omits the second \u201cRabbi\u201d."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But you are not to be called \u2018Rabbi\u2019, for one is your teacher, the Christ, and all of you are brothers."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Call no man on the earth your father, for one is your Father, he who is in heaven."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Neither be called masters, for one is your master, the Christ."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But he who is greatest among you will be your servant."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Whoever exalts himself will be humbled, and whoever humbles himself will be exalted."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you devour widows\u2019 houses, and as a pretense you make long prayers. Therefore you will receive greater condemnation."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! Because you shut up the Kingdom of Heaven against men; for you don\u2019t enter in yourselves, neither do you allow those who are entering in to enter."]],f:["Some Greek texts reverse the order of verses 13 and 14, and some omit verse 13, numbering verse 14 as 13. NU omits verse 14."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you travel around by sea and land to make one proselyte; and when he becomes one, you make him twice as much a son of Gehenna as yourselves."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, you blind guides, who say, \u2018Whoever swears by the temple, it is nothing; but whoever swears by the gold of the temple, he is obligated.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You blind fools! For which is greater, the gold or the temple that sanctifies the gold?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"And, \u2018Whoever swears by the altar, it is nothing; but whoever swears by the gift that is on it, he is obligated.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You blind fools! For which is greater, the gift, or the altar that sanctifies the gift?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He therefore who swears by the altar, swears by it and by everything on it."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He who swears by the temple, swears by it and by him who has been living in it."]],f:["NU reads \u201clives\u201d"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He who swears by heaven, swears by the throne of God and by him who sits on it."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you tithe mint, dill, and cumin, and have left undone the weightier matters of the law: justice, mercy, and faith. But you ought to have done these, and not to have left the other undone."]],f:["cumin is an aromatic seed from Cuminum cyminum, resembling caraway in flavor and appearance. It is used as a spice."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You blind guides, who strain out a gnat, and swallow a camel!"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you clean the outside of the cup and of the platter, but within they are full of extortion and unrighteousness."]],f:["TR reads \u201cself-indulgence\u201d instead of \u201cunrighteousness\u201d"]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You blind Pharisee, first clean the inside of the cup and of the platter, that its outside may become clean also."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you are like whitened tombs, which outwardly appear beautiful, but inwardly are full of dead men\u2019s bones and of all uncleanness."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Even so you also outwardly appear righteous to men, but inwardly you are full of hypocrisy and iniquity."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you build the tombs of the prophets and decorate the tombs of the righteous,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and say, \u2018If we had lived in the days of our fathers, we wouldn\u2019t have been partakers with them in the blood of the prophets.\u2019"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Therefore you testify to yourselves that you are children of those who killed the prophets."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Fill up, then, the measure of your fathers."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"You serpents, you offspring of vipers, how will you escape the judgment of Gehenna?"]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Therefore, behold, I send to you prophets, wise men, and scribes. Some of them you will kill and crucify; and some of them you will scourge in your synagogues and persecute from city to city,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"that on you may come all the righteous blood shed on the earth, from the blood of righteous Abel to the blood of Zachariah son of Barachiah, whom you killed between the sanctuary and the altar."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, all these things will come upon this generation."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cJerusalem, Jerusalem, who kills the prophets and stones those who are sent to her! How often I would have gathered your children together, even as a hen gathers her chicks under her wings, and you would not!"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Behold, your house is left to you desolate."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"For I tell you, you will not see me from now on, until you say, \u2018Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord!\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus went out from the temple, and was going on his way. His disciples came to him to show him the buildings of the temple."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But he answered them, \u201cYou see all of these things, don\u2019t you? Most certainly I tell you, there will not be left here one stone on another, that will not be thrown down.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"As he sat on the Mount of Olives, the disciples came to him privately, saying, \u201cTell us, when will these things be? What is the sign of your coming, and of the end of the age?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cBe careful that no one leads you astray."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For many will come in my name, saying, \u2018I am the Christ,\u2019 and will lead many astray."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You will hear of wars and rumors of wars. See that you aren\u2019t troubled, for all this must happen, but the end is not yet."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom; and there will be famines, plagues, and earthquakes in various places."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But all these things are the beginning of birth pains."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen they will deliver you up to oppression and will kill you. You will be hated by all of the nations for my name\u2019s sake."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Then many will stumble, and will deliver up one another, and will hate one another."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Many false prophets will arise and will lead many astray."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Because iniquity will be multiplied, the love of many will grow cold."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But he who endures to the end will be saved."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"This Good News of the Kingdom will be preached in the whole world for a testimony to all the nations, and then the end will come."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen, therefore, you see the abomination of desolation, which was spoken of through Daniel the prophet, standing in the holy place (let the reader understand),"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Let him who is on the housetop not go down to take out the things that are in his house."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Let him who is in the field not return back to get his clothes."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But woe to those who are with child and to nursing mothers in those days!"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Pray that your flight will not be in the winter nor on a Sabbath,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"for then there will be great suffering, such as has not been from the beginning of the world until now, no, nor ever will be."]],f:["or, oppression"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Unless those days had been shortened, no flesh would have been saved. But for the sake of the chosen ones, those days will be shortened."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen if any man tells you, \u2018Behold, here is the Christ!\u2019 or, \u2018There!\u2019 don\u2019t believe it."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For false christs and false prophets will arise, and they will show great signs and wonders, so as to lead astray, if possible, even the chosen ones."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I have told you beforehand."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf therefore they tell you, \u2018Behold, he is in the wilderness,\u2019 don\u2019t go out; or \u2018Behold, he is in the inner rooms,\u2019 don\u2019t believe it."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For as the lightning flashes from the east, and is seen even to the west, so will the coming of the Son of Man be."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For wherever the carcass is, that is where the vultures gather together."]],f:["or, eagles"]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut immediately after the suffering of those days, the sun will be darkened, the moon will not give its light, the stars will fall from the sky, and the powers of the heavens will be shaken;"]],f:["or, oppression"]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and then the sign of the Son of Man will appear in the sky. Then all the tribes of the earth will mourn, and they will see the Son of Man coming on the clouds of the sky with power and great glory."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He will send out his angels with a great sound of a trumpet, and they will gather together his chosen ones from the four winds, from one end of the sky to the other."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow from the fig tree learn this parable: When its branch has now become tender and produces its leaves, you know that the summer is near."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Even so you also, when you see all these things, know that he is near, even at the doors."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all these things are accomplished."]],f:["The word for \u201cgeneration\u201d (genea) can also be translated as \u201crace.\u201d"]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Heaven and earth will pass away, but my words will not pass away."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut no one knows of that day and hour, not even the angels of heaven, but my Father only."]],f:["NU adds \u201cnor the son\u201d"]},{v:37,l:[[0,"As the days of Noah were, so will the coming of the Son of Man be."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"For as in those days which were before the flood they were eating and drinking, marrying and giving in marriage, until the day that Noah entered into the ship,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and they didn\u2019t know until the flood came and took them all away, so will the coming of the Son of Man be."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Then two men will be in the field: one will be taken and one will be left."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Two women will be grinding at the mill: one will be taken and one will be left."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Watch therefore, for you don\u2019t know in what hour your Lord comes."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"But know this, that if the master of the house had known in what watch of the night the thief was coming, he would have watched, and would not have allowed his house to be broken into."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Therefore also be ready, for in an hour that you don\u2019t expect, the Son of Man will come."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWho then is the faithful and wise servant, whom his lord has set over his household, to give them their food in due season?"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Blessed is that servant whom his lord finds doing so when he comes."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you that he will set him over all that he has."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"But if that evil servant should say in his heart, \u2018My lord is delaying his coming,\u2019"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"and begins to beat his fellow servants, and eat and drink with the drunkards,"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"the lord of that servant will come in a day when he doesn\u2019t expect it and in an hour when he doesn\u2019t know it,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"and will cut him in pieces and appoint his portion with the hypocrites. That is where the weeping and grinding of teeth will be."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen the Kingdom of Heaven will be like ten virgins who took their lamps and went out to meet the bridegroom."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Five of them were foolish, and five were wise."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Those who were foolish, when they took their lamps, took no oil with them,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"but the wise took oil in their vessels with their lamps."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now while the bridegroom delayed, they all slumbered and slept."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But at midnight there was a cry, \u2018Behold! The bridegroom is coming! Come out to meet him!\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then all those virgins arose, and trimmed their lamps."]],f:["The end of the wick of an oil lamp needs to be cut off periodically to avoid having it become clogged with carbon deposits. The wick height is also adjusted so that the flame burns evenly and gives good light without producing a lot of smoke."]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The foolish said to the wise, \u2018Give us some of your oil, for our lamps are going out.\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But the wise answered, saying, \u2018What if there isn\u2019t enough for us and you? You go rather to those who sell, and buy for yourselves.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"While they went away to buy, the bridegroom came, and those who were ready went in with him to the wedding feast, and the door was shut."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Afterward the other virgins also came, saying, \u2018Lord, Lord, open to us.\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But he answered, \u2018Most certainly I tell you, I don\u2019t know you.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Watch therefore, for you don\u2019t know the day nor the hour in which the Son of Man is coming."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor it is like a man going into another country, who called his own servants and entrusted his goods to them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"To one he gave five talents, to another two, to another one, to each according to his own ability. Then he went on his journey."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds (usually used to weigh silver unless otherwise specified)"]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Immediately he who received the five talents went and traded with them, and made another five talents."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"In the same way, he also who got the two gained another two."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But he who received the one talent went away and dug in the earth and hid his lord\u2019s money."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow after a long time the lord of those servants came, and settled accounts with them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He who received the five talents came and brought another five talents, saying, \u2018Lord, you delivered to me five talents. Behold, I have gained another five talents in addition to them.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHis lord said to him, \u2018Well done, good and faithful servant. You have been faithful over a few things, I will set you over many things. Enter into the joy of your lord.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe also who got the two talents came and said, \u2018Lord, you delivered to me two talents. Behold, I have gained another two talents in addition to them.\u2019"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHis lord said to him, \u2018Well done, good and faithful servant. You have been faithful over a few things. I will set you over many things. Enter into the joy of your lord.\u2019"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe also who had received the one talent came and said, \u2018Lord, I knew you that you are a hard man, reaping where you didn\u2019t sow, and gathering where you didn\u2019t scatter."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I was afraid, and went away and hid your talent in the earth. Behold, you have what is yours.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut his lord answered him, \u2018You wicked and slothful servant. You knew that I reap where I didn\u2019t sow, and gather where I didn\u2019t scatter."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"You ought therefore to have deposited my money with the bankers, and at my coming I should have received back my own with interest."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Take away therefore the talent from him and give it to him who has the ten talents."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For to everyone who has will be given, and he will have abundance, but from him who doesn\u2019t have, even that which he has will be taken away."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Throw out the unprofitable servant into the outer darkness, where there will be weeping and gnashing of teeth.\u2019"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut when the Son of Man comes in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then he will sit on the throne of his glory."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Before him all the nations will be gathered, and he will separate them one from another, as a shepherd separates the sheep from the goats."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He will set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Then the King will tell those on his right hand, \u2018Come, blessed of my Father, inherit the Kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"for I was hungry and you gave me food to eat. I was thirsty and you gave me drink. I was a stranger and you took me in."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"I was naked and you clothed me. I was sick and you visited me. I was in prison and you came to me.\u2019"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen the righteous will answer him, saying, \u2018Lord, when did we see you hungry and feed you, or thirsty and give you a drink?"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"When did we see you as a stranger and take you in, or naked and clothe you?"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"When did we see you sick or in prison and come to you?\u2019"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe King will answer them, \u2018Most certainly I tell you, because you did it to one of the least of these my brothers, you did it to me.\u2019"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here may be also correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Then he will say also to those on the left hand, \u2018Depart from me, you cursed, into the eternal fire which is prepared for the devil and his angels;"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"for I was hungry, and you didn\u2019t give me food to eat; I was thirsty, and you gave me no drink;"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"I was a stranger, and you didn\u2019t take me in; naked, and you didn\u2019t clothe me; sick, and in prison, and you didn\u2019t visit me.\u2019"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen they will also answer, saying, \u2018Lord, when did we see you hungry, or thirsty, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and didn\u2019t help you?\u2019"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThen he will answer them, saying, \u2018Most certainly I tell you, because you didn\u2019t do it to one of the least of these, you didn\u2019t do it to me.\u2019"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"These will go away into eternal punishment, but the righteous into eternal life.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had finished all these words, he said to his disciples,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cYou know that after two days the Passover is coming, and the Son of Man will be delivered up to be crucified.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the chief priests, the scribes, and the elders of the people were gathered together in the court of the high priest, who was called Caiaphas."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They took counsel together that they might take Jesus by deceit and kill him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But they said, \u201cNot during the feast, lest a riot occur among the people.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Jesus was in Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"a woman came to him having an alabaster jar of very expensive ointment, and she poured it on his head as he sat at the table."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But when his disciples saw this, they were indignant, saying, \u201cWhy this waste?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For this ointment might have been sold for much and given to the poor.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"However, knowing this, Jesus said to them, \u201cWhy do you trouble the woman? She has done a good work for me."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For you always have the poor with you, but you don\u2019t always have me."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For in pouring this ointment on my body, she did it to prepare me for burial."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, wherever this Good News is preached in the whole world, what this woman has done will also be spoken of as a memorial of her.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Then one of the twelve, who was called Judas Iscariot, went to the chief priests"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cWhat are you willing to give me if I deliver him to you?\u201d So they weighed out for him thirty pieces of silver."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"From that time he sought opportunity to betray him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the first day of unleavened bread, the disciples came to Jesus, saying to him, \u201cWhere do you want us to prepare for you to eat the Passover?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGo into the city to a certain person, and tell him, \u2018The Teacher says, \u201cMy time is at hand. I will keep the Passover at your house with my disciples.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples did as Jesus commanded them, and they prepared the Passover."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when evening had come, he was reclining at the table with the twelve disciples."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"As they were eating, he said, \u201cMost certainly I tell you that one of you will betray me.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"They were exceedingly sorrowful, and each began to ask him, \u201cIt isn\u2019t me, is it, Lord?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cHe who dipped his hand with me in the dish will betray me."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The Son of Man goes even as it is written of him, but woe to that man through whom the Son of Man is betrayed! It would be better for that man if he had not been born.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Judas, who betrayed him, answered, \u201cIt isn\u2019t me, is it, Rabbi?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cYou said it.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"As they were eating, Jesus took bread, gave thanks for it, and broke it. He gave to the disciples and said, \u201cTake, eat; this is my body.\u201d"]],f:["TR reads \u201cblessed\u201d instead of \u201cgave thanks for\u201d"]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He took the cup, gave thanks, and gave to them, saying, \u201cAll of you drink it,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"for this is my blood of the new covenant, which is poured out for many for the remission of sins."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But I tell you that I will not drink of this fruit of the vine from now on, until that day when I drink it anew with you in my Father\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said to them, \u201cAll of you will be made to stumble because of me tonight, for it is written, \u2018I will strike the shepherd, and the sheep of the flock will be scattered.\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"But after I am raised up, I will go before you into Galilee.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter answered him, \u201cEven if all will be made to stumble because of you, I will never be made to stumble.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cMost certainly I tell you that tonight, before the rooster crows, you will deny me three times.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter said to him, \u201cEven if I must die with you, I will not deny you.\u201d All of the disciples also said likewise."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus came with them to a place called Gethsemane, and said to his disciples, \u201cSit here, while I go there and pray.\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He took with him Peter and the two sons of Zebedee, and began to be sorrowful and severely troubled."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said to them, \u201cMy soul is exceedingly sorrowful, even to death. Stay here and watch with me.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"He went forward a little, fell on his face, and prayed, saying, \u201cMy Father, if it is possible, let this cup pass away from me; nevertheless, not what I desire, but what you desire.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"He came to the disciples and found them sleeping, and said to Peter, \u201cWhat, couldn\u2019t you watch with me for one hour?"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Watch and pray, that you don\u2019t enter into temptation. The spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, a second time he went away and prayed, saying, \u201cMy Father, if this cup can\u2019t pass away from me unless I drink it, your desire be done.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"He came again and found them sleeping, for their eyes were heavy."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"He left them again, went away, and prayed a third time, saying the same words."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Then he came to his disciples and said to them, \u201cAre you still sleeping and resting? Behold, the hour is at hand, and the Son of Man is betrayed into the hands of sinners."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Arise, let\u2019s be going. Behold, he who betrays me is at hand.\u201d"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still speaking, behold, Judas, one of the twelve, came, and with him a great multitude with swords and clubs, from the chief priests and elders of the people."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Now he who betrayed him had given them a sign, saying, \u201cWhoever I kiss, he is the one. Seize him.\u201d"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Immediately he came to Jesus, and said, \u201cGreetings, Rabbi!\u201d and kissed him."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cFriend, why are you here?\u201d"],[0,"Then they came and laid hands on Jesus, and took him."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Behold, one of those who were with Jesus stretched out his hand and drew his sword, and struck the servant of the high priest, and cut off his ear."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said to him, \u201cPut your sword back into its place, for all those who take the sword will die by the sword."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"Or do you think that I couldn\u2019t ask my Father, and he would even now send me more than twelve legions of angels?"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"How then would the Scriptures be fulfilled that it must be so?\u201d"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"In that hour Jesus said to the multitudes, \u201cHave you come out as against a robber with swords and clubs to seize me? I sat daily in the temple teaching, and you didn\u2019t arrest me."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"But all this has happened that the Scriptures of the prophets might be fulfilled.\u201d"],[0,"Then all the disciples left him and fled."]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who had taken Jesus led him away to Caiaphas the high priest, where the scribes and the elders were gathered together."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"But Peter followed him from a distance to the court of the high priest, and entered in and sat with the officers, to see the end."]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the chief priests, the elders, and the whole council sought false testimony against Jesus, that they might put him to death,"]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"and they found none. Even though many false witnesses came forward, they found none. But at last two false witnesses came forward"]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cThis man said, \u2018I am able to destroy the temple of God, and to build it in three days.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[0,"The high priest stood up and said to him, \u201cHave you no answer? What is this that these testify against you?\u201d"]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"But Jesus stayed silent. The high priest answered him, \u201cI adjure you by the living God that you tell us whether you are the Christ, the Son of God.\u201d"]]},{v:64,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cYou have said so. Nevertheless, I tell you, after this you will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power, and coming on the clouds of the sky.\u201d"]]},{v:65,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the high priest tore his clothing, saying, \u201cHe has spoken blasphemy! Why do we need any more witnesses? Behold, now you have heard his blasphemy."]]},{v:66,l:[[0,"What do you think?\u201d"],[0,"They answered, \u201cHe is worthy of death!\u201d"]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"Then they spat in his face and beat him with their fists, and some slapped him,"]]},{v:68,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cProphesy to us, you Christ! Who hit you?\u201d"]]},{v:69,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Peter was sitting outside in the court, and a maid came to him, saying, \u201cYou were also with Jesus, the Galilean!\u201d"]]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[0,"But he denied it before them all, saying, \u201cI don\u2019t know what you are talking about.\u201d"]]},{v:71,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had gone out onto the porch, someone else saw him and said to those who were there, \u201cThis man also was with Jesus of Nazareth.\u201d"]]},{v:72,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he denied it with an oath, \u201cI don\u2019t know the man.\u201d"]]},{v:73,p:1,l:[[0,"After a little while those who stood by came and said to Peter, \u201cSurely you are also one of them, for your speech makes you known.\u201d"]]},{v:74,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he began to curse and to swear, \u201cI don\u2019t know the man!\u201d"],[0,"Immediately the rooster crowed."]]},{v:75,l:[[0,"Peter remembered the word which Jesus had said to him, \u201cBefore the rooster crows, you will deny me three times.\u201d Then he went out and wept bitterly."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when morning had come, all the chief priests and the elders of the people took counsel against Jesus to put him to death."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They bound him, led him away, and delivered him up to Pontius Pilate, the governor."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Judas, who betrayed him, when he saw that Jesus was condemned, felt remorse, and brought back the thirty pieces of silver to the chief priests and elders,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cI have sinned in that I betrayed innocent blood.\u201d"],[0,"But they said, \u201cWhat is that to us? You see to it.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He threw down the pieces of silver in the sanctuary and departed. Then he went away and hanged himself."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The chief priests took the pieces of silver and said, \u201cIt\u2019s not lawful to put them into the treasury, since it is the price of blood.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They took counsel, and bought the potter\u2019s field with them to bury strangers in."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore that field has been called \u201cThe Field of Blood\u201d to this day."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then that which was spoken through Jeremiah the prophet was fulfilled, saying,"],[1,"\u201cThey took the thirty pieces of silver,"],[2,"the price of him upon whom a price had been set,"],[2,"whom some of the children of Israel priced,"]],f:["some manuscripts omit \u201cJeremiah\u201d"]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"and they gave them for the potter\u2019s field,"],[2,"as the Lord commanded me.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jesus stood before the governor; and the governor asked him, saying, \u201cAre you the King of the Jews?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cSo you say.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When he was accused by the chief priests and elders, he answered nothing."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then Pilate said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t you hear how many things they testify against you?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He gave him no answer, not even one word, so that the governor marveled greatly."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now at the feast the governor was accustomed to release to the multitude one prisoner whom they desired."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They had then a notable prisoner called Barabbas."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When therefore they were gathered together, Pilate said to them, \u201cWhom do you want me to release to you? Barabbas, or Jesus who is called Christ?\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For he knew that because of envy they had delivered him up."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was sitting on the judgment seat, his wife sent to him, saying, \u201cHave nothing to do with that righteous man, for I have suffered many things today in a dream because of him.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the chief priests and the elders persuaded the multitudes to ask for Barabbas and destroy Jesus."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But the governor answered them, \u201cWhich of the two do you want me to release to you?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cBarabbas!\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate said to them, \u201cWhat then shall I do to Jesus who is called Christ?\u201d"],[0,"They all said to him, \u201cLet him be crucified!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But the governor said, \u201cWhy? What evil has he done?\u201d"],[0,"But they cried out exceedingly, saying, \u201cLet him be crucified!\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"So when Pilate saw that nothing was being gained, but rather that a disturbance was starting, he took water and washed his hands before the multitude, saying, \u201cI am innocent of the blood of this righteous person. You see to it.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"All the people answered, \u201cMay his blood be on us and on our children!\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he released Barabbas to them, but Jesus he flogged and delivered to be crucified."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the governor\u2019s soldiers took Jesus into the Praetorium, and gathered the whole garrison together against him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They stripped him and put a scarlet robe on him."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They braided a crown of thorns and put it on his head, and a reed in his right hand; and they kneeled down before him and mocked him, saying, \u201cHail, King of the Jews!\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"They spat on him, and took the reed and struck him on the head."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"When they had mocked him, they took the robe off him, and put his clothes on him, and led him away to crucify him."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"As they came out, they found a man of Cyrene, Simon by name, and they compelled him to go with them, that he might carry his cross."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"When they came to a place called \u201cGolgotha\u201d, that is to say, \u201cThe place of a skull,\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"they gave him sour wine to drink mixed with gall. When he had tasted it, he would not drink."]],f:["or, vinegar","Gall is a bitter-tasting, dark green oil from a wormwood plant that is alcoholic in its effect."]},{v:35,l:[[0,"When they had crucified him, they divided his clothing among them, casting lots,"]],f:["TR adds \u201cthat it might be fulfilled which was spoken by the prophet: \u2018They divided my garments among them, and for my clothing they cast lots;\u2019\u201d [see Psalms 22:18 and John 19:24]"]},{v:36,l:[[0,"and they sat and watched him there."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They set up over his head the accusation against him written, \u201cTHIS IS JESUS, THE KING OF THE JEWS.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Then there were two robbers crucified with him, one on his right hand and one on the left."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who passed by blasphemed him, wagging their heads"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"and saying, \u201cYou who destroy the temple and build it in three days, save yourself! If you are the Son of God, come down from the cross!\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Likewise the chief priests also mocking with the scribes, the Pharisees, and the elders, said,"]],f:["TR omits \u201cthe Pharisees\u201d"]},{v:42,l:[[0,"\u201cHe saved others, but he can\u2019t save himself. If he is the King of Israel, let him come down from the cross now, and we will believe in him."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He trusts in God. Let God deliver him now, if he wants him; for he said, \u2018I am the Son of God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"The robbers also who were crucified with him cast on him the same reproach."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Now from the sixth hour there was darkness over all the land until the ninth hour."]],f:["noon","3:00 p.m."]},{v:46,l:[[0,"About the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, \u201cEli, Eli, lima sabachthani?\u201d That is, \u201cMy God, my God, why have you forsaken me?\u201d"]],f:["TR reads \u201clama\u201d instead of \u201clima\u201d"]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of them who stood there, when they heard it, said, \u201cThis man is calling Elijah.\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately one of them ran and took a sponge, filled it with vinegar, put it on a reed, and gave him a drink."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"The rest said, \u201cLet him be. Let\u2019s see whether Elijah comes to save him.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus cried again with a loud voice, and yielded up his spirit."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, the veil of the temple was torn in two from the top to the bottom. The earth quaked and the rocks were split."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"The tombs were opened, and many bodies of the saints who had fallen asleep were raised;"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"and coming out of the tombs after his resurrection, they entered into the holy city and appeared to many."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the centurion and those who were with him watching Jesus, when they saw the earthquake and the things that were done, were terrified, saying, \u201cTruly this was the Son of God!\u201d"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"Many women were there watching from afar, who had followed Jesus from Galilee, serving him."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Among them were Mary Magdalene, Mary the mother of James and Joses, and the mother of the sons of Zebedee."]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"When evening had come, a rich man from Arimathaea named Joseph, who himself was also Jesus\u2019 disciple, came."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"This man went to Pilate and asked for Jesus\u2019 body. Then Pilate commanded the body to be given up."]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"Joseph took the body and wrapped it in a clean linen cloth"]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"and laid it in his own new tomb, which he had cut out in the rock. Then he rolled a large stone against the door of the tomb, and departed."]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"Mary Magdalene was there, and the other Mary, sitting opposite the tomb."]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the next day, which was the day after the Preparation Day, the chief priests and the Pharisees were gathered together to Pilate,"]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cSir, we remember what that deceiver said while he was still alive: \u2018After three days I will rise again.\u2019"]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"Command therefore that the tomb be made secure until the third day, lest perhaps his disciples come at night and steal him away, and tell the people, \u2018He is risen from the dead;\u2019 and the last deception will be worse than the first.\u201d"]]},{v:65,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate said to them, \u201cYou have a guard. Go, make it as secure as you can.\u201d"]]},{v:66,l:[[0,"So they went with the guard and made the tomb secure, sealing the stone."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after the Sabbath, as it began to dawn on the first day of the week, Mary Magdalene and the other Mary came to see the tomb."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, there was a great earthquake, for an angel of the Lord descended from the sky and came and rolled away the stone from the door and sat on it."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His appearance was like lightning, and his clothing white as snow."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For fear of him, the guards shook, and became like dead men."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The angel answered the women, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for I know that you seek Jesus, who has been crucified."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He is not here, for he has risen, just like he said. Come, see the place where the Lord was lying."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Go quickly and tell his disciples, \u2018He has risen from the dead, and behold, he goes before you into Galilee; there you will see him.\u2019 Behold, I have told you.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"They departed quickly from the tomb with fear and great joy, and ran to bring his disciples word."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"As they went to tell his disciples, behold, Jesus met them, saying, \u201cRejoice!\u201d"],[0,"They came and took hold of his feet, and worshiped him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid. Go tell my brothers that they should go into Galilee, and there they will see me.\u201d"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here may be also correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now while they were going, behold, some of the guards came into the city and told the chief priests all the things that had happened."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When they were assembled with the elders and had taken counsel, they gave a large amount of silver to the soldiers,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cSay that his disciples came by night and stole him away while we slept."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If this comes to the governor\u2019s ears, we will persuade him and make you free of worry.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So they took the money and did as they were told. This saying was spread abroad among the Jews, and continues until today."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But the eleven disciples went into Galilee, to the mountain where Jesus had sent them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When they saw him, they bowed down to him; but some doubted."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Jesus came to them and spoke to them, saying, \u201cAll authority has been given to me in heaven and on earth."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit,"]],f:["TR and NU add \u201ctherefore\u201d"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"teaching them to observe all things that I commanded you. Behold, I am with you always, even to the end of the age.\u201d Amen."]]}]]}},1311,[]);
__d(function(e,t,a,h,o,i,n){o.exports={book:"Mark",name:"Mark",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The beginning of the Good News of Jesus Christ, the Son of God."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"As it is written in the prophets,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I send my messenger before your face,"],[2,"who will prepare your way before you:"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"the voice of one crying in the wilderness,"],[2,"\u2018Make ready the way of the Lord!"],[2,"Make his paths straight!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"John came baptizing in the wilderness and preaching the baptism of repentance for forgiveness of sins."]],f:["or, immersing"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"All the country of Judea and all those of Jerusalem went out to him. They were baptized by him in the Jordan river, confessing their sins."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"John was clothed with camel\u2019s hair and a leather belt around his waist. He ate locusts and wild honey."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He preached, saying, \u201cAfter me comes he who is mightier than I, the strap of whose sandals I am not worthy to stoop down and loosen."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I baptized you in water, but he will baptize you in the Holy Spirit.\u201d"]],f:["The Greek word (en) translated here as \u201cin\u201d could also be translated as \u201cwith\u201d in some contexts."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days, Jesus came from Nazareth of Galilee, and was baptized by John in the Jordan."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Immediately coming up from the water, he saw the heavens parting and the Spirit descending on him like a dove."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"A voice came out of the sky, \u201cYou are my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately the Spirit drove him out into the wilderness."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He was there in the wilderness forty days, tempted by Satan. He was with the wild animals; and the angels were serving him."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after John was taken into custody, Jesus came into Galilee, preaching the Good News of God\u2019s Kingdom,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and saying, \u201cThe time is fulfilled, and God\u2019s Kingdom is at hand! Repent, and believe in the Good News.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Passing along by the sea of Galilee, he saw Simon and Andrew, the brother of Simon, casting a net into the sea, for they were fishermen."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cCome after me, and I will make you into fishers for men.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately they left their nets, and followed him."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Going on a little further from there, he saw James the son of Zebedee, and John his brother, who were also in the boat mending the nets."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Immediately he called them, and they left their father, Zebedee, in the boat with the hired servants, and went after him."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"They went into Capernaum, and immediately on the Sabbath day he entered into the synagogue and taught."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They were astonished at his teaching, for he taught them as having authority, and not as the scribes."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Immediately there was in their synagogue a man with an unclean spirit, and he cried out,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cHa! What do we have to do with you, Jesus, you Nazarene? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are: the Holy One of God!\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus rebuked him, saying, \u201cBe quiet, and come out of him!\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The unclean spirit, convulsing him and crying with a loud voice, came out of him."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They were all amazed, so that they questioned among themselves, saying, \u201cWhat is this? What can this new doctrine be? For with authority he commands even the unclean spirits, and they obey him!\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The report of him went out immediately into all the region of Galilee and its surrounding area."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately, when they had come out of the synagogue, they came into the house of Simon and Andrew, with James and John."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Now Simon\u2019s wife\u2019s mother lay sick with a fever, and immediately they told him about her."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He came and took her by the hand and raised her up. The fever left her immediately, and she served them."]],f:["NU omits \u201cimmediately\u201d."]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"At evening, when the sun had set, they brought to him all who were sick and those who were possessed by demons."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"All the city was gathered together at the door."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He healed many who were sick with various diseases and cast out many demons. He didn\u2019t allow the demons to speak, because they knew him."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Early in the morning, while it was still dark, he rose up and went out, and departed into a deserted place, and prayed there."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Simon and those who were with him searched for him."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They found him and told him, \u201cEveryone is looking for you.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cLet\u2019s go elsewhere into the next towns, that I may preach there also, because I came out for this reason.\u201d"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"He went into their synagogues throughout all Galilee, preaching and casting out demons."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"A leper came to him, begging him, kneeling down to him, and saying to him, \u201cIf you want to, you can make me clean.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Being moved with compassion, he stretched out his hand, and touched him, and said to him, \u201cI want to. Be made clean.\u201d"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"When he had said this, immediately the leprosy departed from him and he was made clean."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He strictly warned him and immediately sent him out,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cSee that you say nothing to anybody, but go show yourself to the priest and offer for your cleansing the things which Moses commanded, for a testimony to them.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"But he went out, and began to proclaim it much, and to spread about the matter, so that Jesus could no more openly enter into a city, but was outside in desert places. People came to him from everywhere."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When he entered again into Capernaum after some days, it was heard that he was at home."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Immediately many were gathered together, so that there was no more room, not even around the door; and he spoke the word to them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Four people came, carrying a paralytic to him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When they could not come near to him for the crowd, they removed the roof where he was. When they had broken it up, they let down the mat that the paralytic was lying on."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jesus, seeing their faith, said to the paralytic, \u201cSon, your sins are forgiven you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But there were some of the scribes sitting there and reasoning in their hearts,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u201cWhy does this man speak blasphemies like that? Who can forgive sins but God alone?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately Jesus, perceiving in his spirit that they so reasoned within themselves, said to them, \u201cWhy do you reason these things in your hearts?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Which is easier, to tell the paralytic, \u2018Your sins are forgiven;\u2019 or to say, \u2018Arise, and take up your bed, and walk\u2019?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins\u201d\u2014he said to the paralytic\u2014"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cI tell you, arise, take up your mat, and go to your house.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose, and immediately took up the mat and went out in front of them all, so that they were all amazed and glorified God, saying, \u201cWe never saw anything like this!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He went out again by the seaside. All the multitude came to him, and he taught them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"As he passed by, he saw Levi the son of Alphaeus sitting at the tax office. He said to him, \u201cFollow me.\u201d And he arose and followed him."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He was reclining at the table in his house, and many tax collectors and sinners sat down with Jesus and his disciples, for there were many, and they followed him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The scribes and the Pharisees, when they saw that he was eating with the sinners and tax collectors, said to his disciples, \u201cWhy is it that he eats and drinks with tax collectors and sinners?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus heard it, he said to them, \u201cThose who are healthy have no need for a physician, but those who are sick. I came not to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"John\u2019s disciples and the Pharisees were fasting, and they came and asked him, \u201cWhy do John\u2019s disciples and the disciples of the Pharisees fast, but your disciples don\u2019t fast?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cCan the groomsmen fast while the bridegroom is with them? As long as they have the bridegroom with them, they can\u2019t fast."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But the days will come when the bridegroom will be taken away from them, and then they will fast in that day."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"No one sews a piece of unshrunk cloth on an old garment, or else the patch shrinks and the new tears away from the old, and a worse hole is made."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"No one puts new wine into old wineskins; or else the new wine will burst the skins, and the wine pours out, and the skins will be destroyed; but they put new wine into fresh wineskins.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He was going on the Sabbath day through the grain fields; and his disciples began, as they went, to pluck the ears of grain."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The Pharisees said to him, \u201cBehold, why do they do that which is not lawful on the Sabbath day?\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDid you never read what David did when he had need and was hungry\u2014he, and those who were with him?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"How he entered into God\u2019s house at the time of Abiathar the high priest, and ate the show bread, which is not lawful to eat except for the priests, and gave also to those who were with him?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThe Sabbath was made for man, not man for the Sabbath."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Therefore the Son of Man is lord even of the Sabbath.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He entered again into the synagogue, and there was a man there whose hand was withered."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They watched him, whether he would heal him on the Sabbath day, that they might accuse him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He said to the man whose hand was withered, \u201cStand up.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cIs it lawful on the Sabbath day to do good or to do harm? To save a life or to kill?\u201d But they were silent."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When he had looked around at them with anger, being grieved at the hardening of their hearts, he said to the man, \u201cStretch out your hand.\u201d He stretched it out, and his hand was restored as healthy as the other."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The Pharisees went out, and immediately conspired with the Herodians against him, how they might destroy him."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus withdrew to the sea with his disciples; and a great multitude followed him from Galilee, from Judea,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"from Jerusalem, from Idumaea, beyond the Jordan, and those from around Tyre and Sidon. A great multitude, hearing what great things he did, came to him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He spoke to his disciples that a little boat should stay near him because of the crowd, so that they wouldn\u2019t press on him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For he had healed many, so that as many as had diseases pressed on him that they might touch him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The unclean spirits, whenever they saw him, fell down before him and cried, \u201cYou are the Son of God!\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He sternly warned them that they should not make him known."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He went up into the mountain and called to himself those whom he wanted, and they went to him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He appointed twelve, that they might be with him, and that he might send them out to preach"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and to have authority to heal sicknesses and to cast out demons:"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Simon (to whom he gave the name Peter);"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"James the son of Zebedee; and John, the brother of James, (whom he called Boanerges, which means, Sons of Thunder);"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Andrew; Philip; Bartholomew; Matthew; Thomas; James, the son of Alphaeus; Thaddaeus; Simon the Zealot;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and Judas Iscariot, who also betrayed him."],[0,"Then he came into a house."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The multitude came together again, so that they could not so much as eat bread."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When his friends heard it, they went out to seize him; for they said, \u201cHe is insane.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The scribes who came down from Jerusalem said, \u201cHe has Beelzebul,\u201d and, \u201cBy the prince of the demons he casts out the demons.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He summoned them and said to them in parables, \u201cHow can Satan cast out Satan?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"If a kingdom is divided against itself, that kingdom cannot stand."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"If a house is divided against itself, that house cannot stand."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"If Satan has risen up against himself, and is divided, he can\u2019t stand, but has an end."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But no one can enter into the house of the strong man to plunder unless he first binds the strong man; then he will plunder his house."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMost certainly I tell you, all sins of the descendants of man will be forgiven, including their blasphemies with which they may blaspheme;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"but whoever may blaspheme against the Holy Spirit never has forgiveness, but is subject to eternal condemnation.\u201d"]],f:["NU reads, guilty of an eternal sin."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"\u2014because they said, \u201cHe has an unclean spirit.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"His mother and his brothers came, and standing outside, they sent to him, calling him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"A multitude was sitting around him, and they told him, \u201cBehold, your mother, your brothers, and your sisters are outside looking for you.\u201d"]],f:["TR omits \u201cyour sisters\u201d"]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cWho are my mother and my brothers?\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Looking around at those who sat around him, he said, \u201cBehold, my mother and my brothers!"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"For whoever does the will of God is my brother, my sister, and mother.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he began to teach by the seaside. A great multitude was gathered to him, so that he entered into a boat in the sea and sat down. All the multitude were on the land by the sea."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He taught them many things in parables, and told them in his teaching,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cListen! Behold, the farmer went out to sow."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"As he sowed, some seed fell by the road, and the birds came and devoured it."]],f:["TR adds \u201cof the air\u201d"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Others fell on the rocky ground, where it had little soil, and immediately it sprang up, because it had no depth of soil."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When the sun had risen, it was scorched; and because it had no root, it withered away."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Others fell among the thorns, and the thorns grew up and choked it, and it yielded no fruit."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Others fell into the good ground and yielded fruit, growing up and increasing. Some produced thirty times, some sixty times, and some one hundred times as much.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhoever has ears to hear, let him hear.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When he was alone, those who were around him with the twelve asked him about the parables."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cTo you is given the mystery of God\u2019s Kingdom, but to those who are outside, all things are done in parables,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that \u2018seeing they may see and not perceive, and hearing they may hear and not understand, lest perhaps they should turn again, and their sins should be forgiven them.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t you understand this parable? How will you understand all of the parables?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The farmer sows the word."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The ones by the road are the ones where the word is sown; and when they have heard, immediately Satan comes and takes away the word which has been sown in them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"These in the same way are those who are sown on the rocky places, who, when they have heard the word, immediately receive it with joy."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They have no root in themselves, but are short-lived. When oppression or persecution arises because of the word, immediately they stumble."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Others are those who are sown among the thorns. These are those who have heard the word,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and the cares of this age, and the deceitfulness of riches, and the lusts of other things entering in choke the word, and it becomes unfruitful."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Those which were sown on the good ground are those who hear the word, accept it, and bear fruit, some thirty times, some sixty times, and some one hundred times.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cIs a lamp brought to be put under a basket or under a bed? Isn\u2019t it put on a stand?"]],f:["literally, a modion, a dry measuring basket containing about a peck (about 9 liters)"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For there is nothing hidden except that it should be made known, neither was anything made secret but that it should come to light."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If any man has ears to hear, let him hear.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cTake heed what you hear. With whatever measure you measure, it will be measured to you; and more will be given to you who hear."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For whoever has, to him more will be given; and he who doesn\u2019t have, even that which he has will be taken away from him.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cGod\u2019s Kingdom is as if a man should cast seed on the earth,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and should sleep and rise night and day, and the seed should spring up and grow, though he doesn\u2019t know how."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For the earth bears fruit by itself: first the blade, then the ear, then the full grain in the ear."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But when the fruit is ripe, immediately he puts in the sickle, because the harvest has come.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cHow will we liken God\u2019s Kingdom? Or with what parable will we illustrate it?"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"It\u2019s like a grain of mustard seed, which, when it is sown in the earth, though it is less than all the seeds that are on the earth,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"yet when it is sown, grows up and becomes greater than all the herbs, and puts out great branches, so that the birds of the sky can lodge under its shadow.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"With many such parables he spoke the word to them, as they were able to hear it."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Without a parable he didn\u2019t speak to them; but privately to his own disciples he explained everything."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"On that day, when evening had come, he said to them, \u201cLet\u2019s go over to the other side.\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Leaving the multitude, they took him with them, even as he was, in the boat. Other small boats were also with him."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"A big wind storm arose, and the waves beat into the boat, so much that the boat was already filled."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He himself was in the stern, asleep on the cushion; and they woke him up and asked him, \u201cTeacher, don\u2019t you care that we are dying?\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"He awoke and rebuked the wind, and said to the sea, \u201cPeace! Be still!\u201d The wind ceased and there was a great calm."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhy are you so afraid? How is it that you have no faith?\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"They were greatly afraid and said to one another, \u201cWho then is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"They came to the other side of the sea, into the country of the Gadarenes."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When he had come out of the boat, immediately a man with an unclean spirit met him out of the tombs."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He lived in the tombs. Nobody could bind him any more, not even with chains,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"because he had been often bound with fetters and chains, and the chains had been torn apart by him, and the fetters broken in pieces. Nobody had the strength to tame him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Always, night and day, in the tombs and in the mountains, he was crying out, and cutting himself with stones."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When he saw Jesus from afar, he ran and bowed down to him,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and crying out with a loud voice, he said, \u201cWhat have I to do with you, Jesus, you Son of the Most High God? I adjure you by God, don\u2019t torment me.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For he said to him, \u201cCome out of the man, you unclean spirit!\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He asked him, \u201cWhat is your name?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cMy name is Legion, for we are many.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He begged him much that he would not send them away out of the country."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now on the mountainside there was a great herd of pigs feeding."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"All the demons begged him, saying, \u201cSend us into the pigs, that we may enter into them.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"At once Jesus gave them permission. The unclean spirits came out and entered into the pigs. The herd of about two thousand rushed down the steep bank into the sea, and they were drowned in the sea."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Those who fed the pigs fled, and told it in the city and in the country."],[0,"The people came to see what it was that had happened."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They came to Jesus, and saw him who had been possessed by demons sitting, clothed, and in his right mind, even him who had the legion; and they were afraid."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Those who saw it declared to them what happened to him who was possessed by demons, and about the pigs."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They began to beg him to depart from their region."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"As he was entering into the boat, he who had been possessed by demons begged him that he might be with him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He didn\u2019t allow him, but said to him, \u201cGo to your house, to your friends, and tell them what great things the Lord has done for you and how he had mercy on you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He went his way, and began to proclaim in Decapolis how Jesus had done great things for him, and everyone marveled."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had crossed back over in the boat to the other side, a great multitude was gathered to him; and he was by the sea."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Behold, one of the rulers of the synagogue, Jairus by name, came; and seeing him, he fell at his feet"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and begged him much, saying, \u201cMy little daughter is at the point of death. Please come and lay your hands on her, that she may be made healthy, and live.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"He went with him, and a great multitude followed him, and they pressed upon him on all sides."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"A certain woman who had a discharge of blood for twelve years,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and had suffered many things by many physicians, and had spent all that she had, and was no better, but rather grew worse,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"having heard the things concerning Jesus, came up behind him in the crowd and touched his clothes."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For she said, \u201cIf I just touch his clothes, I will be made well.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Immediately the flow of her blood was dried up, and she felt in her body that she was healed of her affliction."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately Jesus, perceiving in himself that the power had gone out from him, turned around in the crowd and asked, \u201cWho touched my clothes?\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"His disciples said to him, \u201cYou see the multitude pressing against you, and you say, \u2018Who touched me?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"He looked around to see her who had done this thing."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But the woman, fearing and trembling, knowing what had been done to her, came and fell down before him, and told him all the truth."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cDaughter, your faith has made you well. Go in peace, and be cured of your disease.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still speaking, people came from the synagogue ruler\u2019s house, saying, \u201cYour daughter is dead. Why bother the Teacher any more?\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus, when he heard the message spoken, immediately said to the ruler of the synagogue, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, only believe.\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"He allowed no one to follow him except Peter, James, and John the brother of James."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He came to the synagogue ruler\u2019s house, and he saw an uproar, weeping, and great wailing."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"When he had entered in, he said to them, \u201cWhy do you make an uproar and weep? The child is not dead, but is asleep.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"They ridiculed him. But he, having put them all out, took the father of the child, her mother, and those who were with him, and went in where the child was lying."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Taking the child by the hand, he said to her, \u201cTalitha cumi!\u201d which means, being interpreted, \u201cGirl, I tell you, get up!\u201d"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Immediately the girl rose up and walked, for she was twelve years old. They were amazed with great amazement."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He strictly ordered them that no one should know this, and commanded that something should be given to her to eat."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He went out from there. He came into his own country, and his disciples followed him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When the Sabbath had come, he began to teach in the synagogue, and many hearing him were astonished, saying, \u201cWhere did this man get these things?\u201d and, \u201cWhat is the wisdom that is given to this man, that such mighty works come about by his hands?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Isn\u2019t this the carpenter, the son of Mary and brother of James, Joses, Judah, and Simon? Aren\u2019t his sisters here with us?\u201d So they were offended at him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cA prophet is not without honor, except in his own country, and among his own relatives, and in his own house.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He could do no mighty work there, except that he laid his hands on a few sick people and healed them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He marveled because of their unbelief."],[0,"He went around the villages teaching."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He called to himself the twelve, and began to send them out two by two; and he gave them authority over the unclean spirits."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He commanded them that they should take nothing for their journey, except a staff only: no bread, no wallet, no money in their purse,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but to wear sandals, and not put on two tunics."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWherever you enter into a house, stay there until you depart from there."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Whoever will not receive you nor hear you, as you depart from there, shake off the dust that is under your feet for a testimony against them. Assuredly, I tell you, it will be more tolerable for Sodom and Gomorrah in the day of judgment than for that city!\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"They went out and preached that people should repent."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They cast out many demons, and anointed many with oil who were sick and healed them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"King Herod heard this, for his name had become known, and he said, \u201cJohn the Baptizer has risen from the dead, and therefore these powers are at work in him.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But others said, \u201cHe is Elijah.\u201d Others said, \u201cHe is a prophet, or like one of the prophets.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But Herod, when he heard this, said, \u201cThis is John, whom I beheaded. He has risen from the dead.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For Herod himself had sent out and arrested John and bound him in prison for the sake of Herodias, his brother Philip\u2019s wife, for he had married her."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For John had said to Herod, \u201cIt is not lawful for you to have your brother\u2019s wife.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Herodias set herself against him and desired to kill him, but she couldn\u2019t,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"for Herod feared John, knowing that he was a righteous and holy man, and kept him safe. When he heard him, he did many things, and he heard him gladly."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Then a convenient day came when Herod on his birthday made a supper for his nobles, the high officers, and the chief men of Galilee."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When the daughter of Herodias herself came in and danced, she pleased Herod and those sitting with him. The king said to the young lady, \u201cAsk me whatever you want, and I will give it to you.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He swore to her, \u201cWhatever you ask of me, I will give you, up to half of my kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"She went out and said to her mother, \u201cWhat shall I ask?\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cThe head of John the Baptizer.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"She came in immediately with haste to the king and requested, \u201cI want you to give me right now the head of John the Baptizer on a platter.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"The king was exceedingly sorry, but for the sake of his oaths and of his dinner guests, he didn\u2019t wish to refuse her."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Immediately the king sent out a soldier of his guard and commanded to bring John\u2019s head; and he went and beheaded him in the prison,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and brought his head on a platter, and gave it to the young lady; and the young lady gave it to her mother."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When his disciples heard this, they came and took up his corpse and laid it in a tomb."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"The apostles gathered themselves together to Jesus, and they told him all things, whatever they had done, and whatever they had taught."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cCome away into a deserted place, and rest awhile.\u201d For there were many coming and going, and they had no leisure so much as to eat."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They went away in the boat to a deserted place by themselves."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They saw them going, and many recognized him and ran there on foot from all the cities. They arrived before them and came together to him."]],f:["TR reads \u201cThe multitudes\u201d instead of \u201cThey\u201d"]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Jesus came out, saw a great multitude, and he had compassion on them because they were like sheep without a shepherd; and he began to teach them many things."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"When it was late in the day, his disciples came to him and said, \u201cThis place is deserted, and it is late in the day."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Send them away, that they may go into the surrounding country and villages and buy themselves bread, for they have nothing to eat.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered them, \u201cYou give them something to eat.\u201d"],[0,"They asked him, \u201cShall we go and buy two hundred denarii worth of bread and give them something to eat?\u201d"]],f:["200 denarii was about 7 or 8 months wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cHow many loaves do you have? Go see.\u201d"],[0,"When they knew, they said, \u201cFive, and two fish.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"He commanded them that everyone should sit down in groups on the green grass."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"They sat down in ranks, by hundreds and by fifties."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He took the five loaves and the two fish; and looking up to heaven, he blessed and broke the loaves, and he gave to his disciples to set before them, and he divided the two fish among them all."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"They all ate and were filled."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"They took up twelve baskets full of broken pieces and also of the fish."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Those who ate the loaves were five thousand men."]],f:["TR adds \u201cabout\u201d"]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately he made his disciples get into the boat and go ahead to the other side, to Bethsaida, while he himself sent the multitude away."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"After he had taken leave of them, he went up the mountain to pray."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"When evening had come, the boat was in the middle of the sea, and he was alone on the land."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Seeing them distressed in rowing, for the wind was contrary to them, about the fourth watch of the night he came to them, walking on the sea; and he would have passed by them,"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"but they, when they saw him walking on the sea, supposed that it was a ghost, and cried out;"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"for they all saw him and were troubled. But he immediately spoke with them and said to them, \u201cCheer up! It is I! Don\u2019t be afraid.\u201d"]],f:["or, \u201cI AM!\u201d"]},{v:51,l:[[0,"He got into the boat with them; and the wind ceased, and they were very amazed among themselves, and marveled;"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"for they hadn\u2019t understood about the loaves, but their hearts were hardened."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had crossed over, they came to land at Gennesaret and moored to the shore."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"When they had come out of the boat, immediately the people recognized him,"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"and ran around that whole region, and began to bring those who were sick on their mats to where they heard he was."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Wherever he entered\u2014into villages, or into cities, or into the country\u2014they laid the sick in the marketplaces and begged him that they might just touch the fringe of his garment; and as many as touched him were made well."]],f:["or, tassel"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Pharisees and some of the scribes gathered together to him, having come from Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now when they saw some of his disciples eating bread with defiled, that is unwashed, hands, they found fault."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"(For the Pharisees and all the Jews don\u2019t eat unless they wash their hands and forearms, holding to the tradition of the elders."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They don\u2019t eat when they come from the marketplace unless they bathe themselves, and there are many other things which they have received to hold to: washings of cups, pitchers, bronze vessels, and couches.)"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The Pharisees and the scribes asked him, \u201cWhy don\u2019t your disciples walk according to the tradition of the elders, but eat their bread with unwashed hands?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cWell did Isaiah prophesy of you hypocrites, as it is written,"],[1,"\u2018This people honors me with their lips,"],[2,"but their heart is far from me."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"They worship me in vain,"],[2,"teaching as doctrines the commandments of men.\u2019"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor you set aside the commandment of God, and hold tightly to the tradition of men\u2014the washing of pitchers and cups, and you do many other such things.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cFull well do you reject the commandment of God, that you may keep your tradition."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For Moses said, \u2018Honor your father and your mother;\u2019 and, \u2018He who speaks evil of father or mother, let him be put to death.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But you say, \u2018If a man tells his father or his mother, \u201cWhatever profit you might have received from me is Corban,\u201d\u2019\u201d that is to say, given to God,"]],f:["Corban is a Hebrew word for an offering devoted to God."]},{v:12,l:[[0,"\u201cthen you no longer allow him to do anything for his father or his mother,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"making void the word of God by your tradition which you have handed down. You do many things like this.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He called all the multitude to himself and said to them, \u201cHear me, all of you, and understand."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"There is nothing from outside of the man that going into him can defile him; but the things which proceed out of the man are those that defile the man."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"If anyone has ears to hear, let him hear!\u201d"]],f:["NU omits verse 16."]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had entered into a house away from the multitude, his disciples asked him about the parable."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cAre you also without understanding? Don\u2019t you perceive that whatever goes into the man from outside can\u2019t defile him,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"because it doesn\u2019t go into his heart, but into his stomach, then into the latrine, making all foods clean?\u201d"]],f:["NU ends Jesus\u2019 direct quote and question after \u201clatrine\u201d, ending the verse with \u201cThus he declared all foods clean."]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThat which proceeds out of the man, that defiles the man."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For from within, out of the hearts of men, proceed evil thoughts, adulteries, sexual sins, murders, thefts,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"covetings, wickedness, deceit, lustful desires, an evil eye, blasphemy, pride, and foolishness."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"All these evil things come from within and defile the man.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"From there he arose and went away into the borders of Tyre and Sidon. He entered into a house and didn\u2019t want anyone to know it, but he couldn\u2019t escape notice."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For a woman whose little daughter had an unclean spirit, having heard of him, came and fell down at his feet."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Now the woman was a Greek, a Syrophoenician by race. She begged him that he would cast the demon out of her daughter."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to her, \u201cLet the children be filled first, for it is not appropriate to take the children\u2019s bread and throw it to the dogs.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"But she answered him, \u201cYes, Lord. Yet even the dogs under the table eat the children\u2019s crumbs.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cFor this saying, go your way. The demon has gone out of your daughter.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"She went away to her house, and found the child having been laid on the bed, with the demon gone out."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he departed from the borders of Tyre and Sidon, and came to the sea of Galilee through the middle of the region of Decapolis."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They brought to him one who was deaf and had an impediment in his speech. They begged him to lay his hand on him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He took him aside from the multitude privately and put his fingers into his ears; and he spat and touched his tongue."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Looking up to heaven, he sighed, and said to him, \u201cEphphatha!\u201d that is, \u201cBe opened!\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Immediately his ears were opened, and the impediment of his tongue was released, and he spoke clearly."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He commanded them that they should tell no one, but the more he commanded them, so much the more widely they proclaimed it."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They were astonished beyond measure, saying, \u201cHe has done all things well. He makes even the deaf hear and the mute speak!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In those days, when there was a very great multitude, and they had nothing to eat, Jesus called his disciples to himself and said to them,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cI have compassion on the multitude, because they have stayed with me now three days and have nothing to eat."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If I send them away fasting to their home, they will faint on the way, for some of them have come a long way.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"His disciples answered him, \u201cFrom where could one satisfy these people with bread here in a deserted place?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He asked them, \u201cHow many loaves do you have?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cSeven.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground, and he took the seven loaves. Having given thanks, he broke them and gave them to his disciples to serve, and they served the multitude."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They also had a few small fish. Having blessed them, he said to serve these also."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They ate and were filled. They took up seven baskets of broken pieces that were left over."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Those who had eaten were about four thousand. Then he sent them away."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately he entered into the boat with his disciples and came into the region of Dalmanutha."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The Pharisees came out and began to question him, seeking from him a sign from heaven and testing him."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He sighed deeply in his spirit and said, \u201cWhy does this generation seek a sign? Most certainly I tell you, no sign will be given to this generation.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201cgeneration\u201d here (genea) could also be translated \u201cpeople\u201d, \u201crace\u201d, or \u201cfamily\u201d."]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He left them, and again entering into the boat, departed to the other side."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They forgot to take bread; and they didn\u2019t have more than one loaf in the boat with them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He warned them, saying, \u201cTake heed: beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and the yeast of Herod.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"They reasoned with one another, saying, \u201cIt\u2019s because we have no bread.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, perceiving it, said to them, \u201cWhy do you reason that it\u2019s because you have no bread? Don\u2019t you perceive yet or understand? Is your heart still hardened?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Having eyes, don\u2019t you see? Having ears, don\u2019t you hear? Don\u2019t you remember?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When I broke the five loaves among the five thousand, how many baskets full of broken pieces did you take up?\u201d"],[0,"They told him, \u201cTwelve.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the seven loaves fed the four thousand, how many baskets full of broken pieces did you take up?\u201d"],[0,"They told him, \u201cSeven.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He asked them, \u201cDon\u2019t you understand yet?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He came to Bethsaida. They brought a blind man to him and begged him to touch him."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He took hold of the blind man by the hand, and brought him out of the village. When he had spat on his eyes, and laid his hands on him, he asked him if he saw anything."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"He looked up, and said, \u201cI see men, but I see them like walking trees.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Then again he laid his hands on his eyes. He looked intently, and was restored, and saw everyone clearly."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He sent him away to his house, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t enter into the village, nor tell anyone in the village.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus went out, with his disciples, into the villages of Caesarea Philippi. On the way he asked his disciples, \u201cWho do men say that I am?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They told him, \u201cJohn the Baptizer, and others say Elijah, but others, one of the prophets.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cBut who do you say that I am?\u201d"],[0,"Peter answered, \u201cYou are the Christ.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"He commanded them that they should tell no one about him."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"He began to teach them that the Son of Man must suffer many things, and be rejected by the elders, the chief priests, and the scribes, and be killed, and after three days rise again."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He spoke to them openly. Peter took him and began to rebuke him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But he, turning around and seeing his disciples, rebuked Peter, and said, \u201cGet behind me, Satan! For you have in mind not the things of God, but the things of men.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"He called the multitude to himself with his disciples and said to them, \u201cWhoever wants to come after me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross, and follow me."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"For whoever wants to save his life will lose it; and whoever will lose his life for my sake and the sake of the Good News will save it."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"For what does it profit a man to gain the whole world and forfeit his life?"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For what will a man give in exchange for his life?"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"For whoever will be ashamed of me and of my words in this adulterous and sinful generation, the Son of Man also will be ashamed of him when he comes in his Father\u2019s glory with the holy angels.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, there are some standing here who will in no way taste death until they see God\u2019s Kingdom come with power.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"After six days Jesus took with him Peter, James, and John, and brought them up onto a high mountain privately by themselves, and he was changed into another form in front of them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His clothing became glistening, exceedingly white, like snow, such as no launderer on earth can whiten them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Elijah and Moses appeared to them, and they were talking with Jesus."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter answered Jesus, \u201cRabbi, it is good for us to be here. Let\u2019s make three tents: one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For he didn\u2019t know what to say, for they were very afraid."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"A cloud came, overshadowing them, and a voice came out of the cloud, \u201cThis is my beloved Son. Listen to him.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Suddenly looking around, they saw no one with them any more, except Jesus only."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"As they were coming down from the mountain, he commanded them that they should tell no one what things they had seen, until after the Son of Man had risen from the dead."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They kept this saying to themselves, questioning what the \u201crising from the dead\u201d meant."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"They asked him, saying, \u201cWhy do the scribes say that Elijah must come first?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cElijah indeed comes first, and restores all things. How is it written about the Son of Man, that he should suffer many things and be despised?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But I tell you that Elijah has come, and they have also done to him whatever they wanted to, even as it is written about him.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Coming to the disciples, he saw a great multitude around them, and scribes questioning them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Immediately all the multitude, when they saw him, were greatly amazed, and running to him, greeted him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He asked the scribes, \u201cWhat are you asking them?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the multitude answered, \u201cTeacher, I brought to you my son, who has a mute spirit;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and wherever it seizes him, it throws him down; and he foams at the mouth, grinds his teeth, and becomes rigid. I asked your disciples to cast it out, and they weren\u2019t able.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered him, \u201cUnbelieving generation, how long shall I be with you? How long shall I bear with you? Bring him to me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"They brought him to him, and when he saw him, immediately the spirit convulsed him and he fell on the ground, wallowing and foaming at the mouth."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He asked his father, \u201cHow long has it been since this has been happening to him?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cFrom childhood."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Often it has cast him both into the fire and into the water to destroy him. But if you can do anything, have compassion on us and help us.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cIf you can believe, all things are possible to him who believes.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately the father of the child cried out with tears, \u201cI believe. Help my unbelief!\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus saw that a multitude came running together, he rebuked the unclean spirit, saying to him, \u201cYou mute and deaf spirit, I command you, come out of him, and never enter him again!\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"After crying out and convulsing him greatly, it came out of him. The boy became like one dead, so much that most of them said, \u201cHe is dead.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But Jesus took him by the hand and raised him up; and he arose."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had come into the house, his disciples asked him privately, \u201cWhy couldn\u2019t we cast it out?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThis kind can come out by nothing but by prayer and fasting.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"They went out from there and passed through Galilee. He didn\u2019t want anyone to know it,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"for he was teaching his disciples, and said to them, \u201cThe Son of Man is being handed over to the hands of men, and they will kill him; and when he is killed, on the third day he will rise again.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"But they didn\u2019t understand the saying, and were afraid to ask him."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"He came to Capernaum, and when he was in the house he asked them, \u201cWhat were you arguing among yourselves on the way?\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"But they were silent, for they had disputed with one another on the way about who was the greatest."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"He sat down and called the twelve; and he said to them, \u201cIf any man wants to be first, he shall be last of all, and servant of all.\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He took a little child and set him in the middle of them. Taking him in his arms, he said to them,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"\u201cWhoever receives one such little child in my name receives me; and whoever receives me, doesn\u2019t receive me, but him who sent me.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"John said to him, \u201cTeacher, we saw someone who doesn\u2019t follow us casting out demons in your name; and we forbade him, because he doesn\u2019t follow us.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said, \u201cDon\u2019t forbid him, for there is no one who will do a mighty work in my name and be able quickly to speak evil of me."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"For whoever is not against us is on our side."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"For whoever will give you a cup of water to drink in my name because you are Christ\u2019s, most certainly I tell you, he will in no way lose his reward."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhoever will cause one of these little ones who believe in me to stumble, it would be better for him if he were thrown into the sea with a millstone hung around his neck."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"If your hand causes you to stumble, cut it off. It is better for you to enter into life maimed, rather than having your two hands to go into Gehenna, into the unquenchable fire,"]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:44,l:[[0,"\u2018where their worm doesn\u2019t die, and the fire is not quenched.\u2019"]],f:["NU omits verse 44."]},{v:45,l:[[0,"If your foot causes you to stumble, cut it off. It is better for you to enter into life lame, rather than having your two feet to be cast into Gehenna, into the fire that will never be quenched\u2014"]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:46,l:[[0,"\u2018where their worm doesn\u2019t die, and the fire is not quenched.\u2019"]],f:["NU omits verse 46."]},{v:47,l:[[0,"If your eye causes you to stumble, throw it out. It is better for you to enter into God\u2019s Kingdom with one eye, rather than having two eyes to be cast into the Gehenna of fire,"]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:48,l:[[0,"\u2018where their worm doesn\u2019t die, and the fire is not quenched.\u2019"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"For everyone will be salted with fire, and every sacrifice will be seasoned with salt."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Salt is good, but if the salt has lost its saltiness, with what will you season it? Have salt in yourselves, and be at peace with one another.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose from there and came into the borders of Judea and beyond the Jordan. Multitudes came together to him again. As he usually did, he was again teaching them."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Pharisees came to him testing him, and asked him, \u201cIs it lawful for a man to divorce his wife?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cWhat did Moses command you?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cMoses allowed a certificate of divorce to be written, and to divorce her.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to them, \u201cFor your hardness of heart, he wrote you this commandment."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But from the beginning of the creation, God made them male and female."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For this cause a man will leave his father and mother, and will join to his wife,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and the two will become one flesh, so that they are no longer two, but one flesh."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"What therefore God has joined together, let no man separate.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"In the house, his disciples asked him again about the same matter."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhoever divorces his wife and marries another commits adultery against her."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If a woman herself divorces her husband and marries another, she commits adultery.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"They were bringing to him little children, that he should touch them, but the disciples rebuked those who were bringing them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But when Jesus saw it, he was moved with indignation and said to them, \u201cAllow the little children to come to me! Don\u2019t forbid them, for God\u2019s Kingdom belongs to such as these."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, whoever will not receive God\u2019s Kingdom like a little child, he will in no way enter into it.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He took them in his arms and blessed them, laying his hands on them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"As he was going out into the way, one ran to him, knelt before him, and asked him, \u201cGood Teacher, what shall I do that I may inherit eternal life?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cWhy do you call me good? No one is good except one\u2014God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You know the commandments: \u2018Do not murder,\u2019 \u2018Do not commit adultery,\u2019 \u2018Do not steal,\u2019 \u2018Do not give false testimony,\u2019 \u2018Do not defraud,\u2019 \u2018Honor your father and mother.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cTeacher, I have observed all these things from my youth.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus looking at him loved him, and said to him, \u201cOne thing you lack. Go, sell whatever you have and give to the poor, and you will have treasure in heaven; and come, follow me, taking up the cross.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But his face fell at that saying, and he went away sorrowful, for he was one who had great possessions."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus looked around and said to his disciples, \u201cHow difficult it is for those who have riches to enter into God\u2019s Kingdom!\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples were amazed at his words. But Jesus answered again, \u201cChildren, how hard it is for those who trust in riches to enter into God\u2019s Kingdom!"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"It is easier for a camel to go through a needle\u2019s eye than for a rich man to enter into God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"They were exceedingly astonished, saying to him, \u201cThen who can be saved?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, looking at them, said, \u201cWith men it is impossible, but not with God, for all things are possible with God.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter began to tell him, \u201cBehold, we have left all and have followed you.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, there is no one who has left house, or brothers, or sisters, or father, or mother, or wife, or children, or land, for my sake, and for the sake of the Good News,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"but he will receive one hundred times more now in this time: houses, brothers, sisters, mothers, children, and land, with persecutions; and in the age to come eternal life."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But many who are first will be last, and the last first.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"They were on the way, going up to Jerusalem; and Jesus was going in front of them, and they were amazed; and those who followed were afraid. He again took the twelve, and began to tell them the things that were going to happen to him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, we are going up to Jerusalem. The Son of Man will be delivered to the chief priests and the scribes. They will condemn him to death, and will deliver him to the Gentiles."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"They will mock him, spit on him, scourge him, and kill him. On the third day he will rise again.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"James and John, the sons of Zebedee, came near to him, saying, \u201cTeacher, we want you to do for us whatever we will ask.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat do you want me to do for you?\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cGrant to us that we may sit, one at your right hand and one at your left hand, in your glory.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to them, \u201cYou don\u2019t know what you are asking. Are you able to drink the cup that I drink, and to be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with?\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cWe are able.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cYou shall indeed drink the cup that I drink, and you shall be baptized with the baptism that I am baptized with;"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"but to sit at my right hand and at my left hand is not mine to give, but for whom it has been prepared.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"When the ten heard it, they began to be indignant toward James and John."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus summoned them and said to them, \u201cYou know that they who are recognized as rulers over the nations lord it over them, and their great ones exercise authority over them."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"But it shall not be so among you, but whoever wants to become great among you shall be your servant."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Whoever of you wants to become first among you shall be bondservant of all."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"For the Son of Man also came not to be served but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"They came to Jericho. As he went out from Jericho with his disciples and a great multitude, the son of Timaeus, Bartimaeus, a blind beggar, was sitting by the road."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"When he heard that it was Jesus the Nazarene, he began to cry out and say, \u201cJesus, you son of David, have mercy on me!\u201d"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Many rebuked him, that he should be quiet, but he cried out much more, \u201cYou son of David, have mercy on me!\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus stood still and said, \u201cCall him.\u201d"],[0,"They called the blind man, saying to him, \u201cCheer up! Get up. He is calling you!\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"He, casting away his cloak, sprang up, and came to Jesus."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus asked him, \u201cWhat do you want me to do for you?\u201d"],[0,"The blind man said to him, \u201cRabboni, that I may see again.\u201d"]],f:["Rabboni is a transliteration of the Aramaic word for \u201cgreat teacher.\u201d"]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cGo your way. Your faith has made you well.\u201d Immediately he received his sight and followed Jesus on the way."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When they came near to Jerusalem, to Bethsphage and Bethany, at the Mount of Olives, he sent two of his disciples"]],f:["TR & NU read \u201cBethphage\u201d instead of \u201cBethsphage\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cGo your way into the village that is opposite you. Immediately as you enter into it, you will find a young donkey tied, on which no one has sat. Untie him and bring him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If anyone asks you, \u2018Why are you doing this?\u2019 say, \u2018The Lord needs him;\u2019 and immediately he will send him back here.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"They went away, and found a young donkey tied at the door outside in the open street, and they untied him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Some of those who stood there asked them, \u201cWhat are you doing, untying the young donkey?\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They said to them just as Jesus had said, and they let them go."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They brought the young donkey to Jesus and threw their garments on it, and Jesus sat on it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Many spread their garments on the way, and others were cutting down branches from the trees and spreading them on the road."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Those who went in front and those who followed cried out, \u201cHosanna! Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord!"]],f:["\u201cHosanna\u201d means \u201csave us\u201d or \u201chelp us, we pray\u201d."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Blessed is the kingdom of our father David that is coming in the name of the Lord! Hosanna in the highest!\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus entered into the temple in Jerusalem. When he had looked around at everything, it being now evening, he went out to Bethany with the twelve."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The next day, when they had come out from Bethany, he was hungry."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Seeing a fig tree afar off having leaves, he came to see if perhaps he might find anything on it. When he came to it, he found nothing but leaves, for it was not the season for figs."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Jesus told it, \u201cMay no one ever eat fruit from you again!\u201d and his disciples heard it."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"They came to Jerusalem, and Jesus entered into the temple and began to throw out those who sold and those who bought in the temple, and overthrew the money changers\u2019 tables and the seats of those who sold the doves."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He would not allow anyone to carry a container through the temple."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He taught, saying to them, \u201cIsn\u2019t it written, \u2018My house will be called a house of prayer for all the nations\u2019? But you have made it a den of robbers!\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The chief priests and the scribes heard it, and sought how they might destroy him. For they feared him, because all the multitude was astonished at his teaching."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"When evening came, he went out of the city."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"As they passed by in the morning, they saw the fig tree withered away from the roots."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Peter, remembering, said to him, \u201cRabbi, look! The fig tree which you cursed has withered away.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cHave faith in God."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For most certainly I tell you, whoever may tell this mountain, \u2018Be taken up and cast into the sea,\u2019 and doesn\u2019t doubt in his heart, but believes that what he says is happening, he shall have whatever he says."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Therefore I tell you, all things whatever you pray and ask for, believe that you have received them, and you shall have them."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Whenever you stand praying, forgive, if you have anything against anyone; so that your Father, who is in heaven, may also forgive you your transgressions."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But if you do not forgive, neither will your Father in heaven forgive your transgressions.\u201d"]],f:["NU omits verse 26."]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"They came again to Jerusalem, and as he was walking in the temple, the chief priests, the scribes, and the elders came to him,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and they began saying to him, \u201cBy what authority do you do these things? Or who gave you this authority to do these things?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cI will ask you one question. Answer me, and I will tell you by what authority I do these things."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The baptism of John\u2014was it from heaven, or from men? Answer me.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"They reasoned with themselves, saying, \u201cIf we should say, \u2018From heaven;\u2019 he will say, \u2018Why then did you not believe him?\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"If we should say, \u2018From men\u2019\u201d\u2014they feared the people, for all held John to really be a prophet."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They answered Jesus, \u201cWe don\u2019t know.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cNeither will I tell you by what authority I do these things.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He began to speak to them in parables. \u201cA man planted a vineyard, put a hedge around it, dug a pit for the wine press, built a tower, rented it out to a farmer, and went into another country."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When it was time, he sent a servant to the farmer to get from the farmer his share of the fruit of the vineyard."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They took him, beat him, and sent him away empty."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Again, he sent another servant to them; and they threw stones at him, wounded him in the head, and sent him away shamefully treated."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Again he sent another, and they killed him, and many others, beating some, and killing some."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Therefore still having one, his beloved son, he sent him last to them, saying, \u2018They will respect my son.\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But those farmers said among themselves, \u2018This is the heir. Come, let\u2019s kill him, and the inheritance will be ours.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They took him, killed him, and cast him out of the vineyard."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"What therefore will the lord of the vineyard do? He will come and destroy the farmers, and will give the vineyard to others."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Haven\u2019t you even read this Scripture:"],[1,"\u2018The stone which the builders rejected"],[2,"was made the head of the corner."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"This was from the Lord."],[2,"It is marvelous in our eyes\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"They tried to seize him, but they feared the multitude; for they perceived that he spoke the parable against them. They left him and went away."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They sent some of the Pharisees and the Herodians to him, that they might trap him with words."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When they had come, they asked him, \u201cTeacher, we know that you are honest, and don\u2019t defer to anyone; for you aren\u2019t partial to anyone, but truly teach the way of God. Is it lawful to pay taxes to Caesar, or not?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Shall we give, or shall we not give?\u201d"],[0,"But he, knowing their hypocrisy, said to them, \u201cWhy do you test me? Bring me a denarius, that I may see it.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"They brought it."],[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhose is this image and inscription?\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cCaesar\u2019s.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cGive to Caesar the things that are Caesar\u2019s, and to God the things that are God\u2019s.\u201d"],[0,"They marveled greatly at him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Some Sadducees, who say that there is no resurrection, came to him. They asked him, saying,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"\u201cTeacher, Moses wrote to us, \u2018If a man\u2019s brother dies and leaves a wife behind him, and leaves no children, that his brother should take his wife and raise up offspring for his brother.\u2019"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"There were seven brothers. The first took a wife, and dying left no offspring."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The second took her, and died, leaving no children behind him. The third likewise;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and the seven took her and left no children. Last of all the woman also died."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"In the resurrection, when they rise, whose wife will she be of them? For the seven had her as a wife.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cIsn\u2019t this because you are mistaken, not knowing the Scriptures nor the power of God?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For when they will rise from the dead, they neither marry nor are given in marriage, but are like angels in heaven."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But about the dead, that they are raised, haven\u2019t you read in the book of Moses about the Bush, how God spoke to him, saying, \u2018I am the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob\u2019?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He is not the God of the dead, but of the living. You are therefore badly mistaken.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the scribes came and heard them questioning together, and knowing that he had answered them well, asked him, \u201cWhich commandment is the greatest of all?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cThe greatest is: \u2018Hear, Israel, the Lord our God, the Lord is one."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"You shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, with all your soul, with all your mind, and with all your strength.\u2019 This is the first commandment."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The second is like this: \u2018You shall love your neighbor as yourself.\u2019 There is no other commandment greater than these.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The scribe said to him, \u201cTruly, teacher, you have said well that he is one, and there is none other but he;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"and to love him with all the heart, with all the understanding, all the soul, and with all the strength, and to love his neighbor as himself, is more important than all whole burnt offerings and sacrifices.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus saw that he answered wisely, he said to him, \u201cYou are not far from God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"],[0,"No one dared ask him any question after that."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Jesus responded, as he taught in the temple, \u201cHow is it that the scribes say that the Christ is the son of David?"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"For David himself said in the Holy Spirit,"],[1,"\u2018The Lord said to my Lord,"],[2,"\u201cSit at my right hand,"],[2,"until I make your enemies the footstool of your feet.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore David himself calls him Lord, so how can he be his son?\u201d"],[0,"The common people heard him gladly."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"In his teaching he said to them, \u201cBeware of the scribes, who like to walk in long robes, and to get greetings in the marketplaces,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and to get the best seats in the synagogues and the best places at feasts,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"those who devour widows\u2019 houses, and for a pretense make long prayers. These will receive greater condemnation.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus sat down opposite the treasury and saw how the multitude cast money into the treasury. Many who were rich cast in much."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"A poor widow came and she cast in two small brass coins, which equal a quadrans coin."]],f:["literally, lepta (or widow\u2019s mites). Lepta are very small brass coins worth half a quadrans each, which is a quarter of the copper assarion. Lepta are worth less than 1% of an agricultural worker\u2019s daily wages.","A quadrans is a coin worth about 1/64 of a denarius. A denarius is about one day\u2019s wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He called his disciples to himself and said to them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, this poor widow gave more than all those who are giving into the treasury,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"for they all gave out of their abundance, but she, out of her poverty, gave all that she had to live on.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"As he went out of the temple, one of his disciples said to him, \u201cTeacher, see what kind of stones and what kind of buildings!\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cDo you see these great buildings? There will not be left here one stone on another, which will not be thrown down.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"As he sat on the Mount of Olives opposite the temple, Peter, James, John, and Andrew asked him privately,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cTell us, when will these things be? What is the sign that these things are all about to be fulfilled?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, answering, began to tell them, \u201cBe careful that no one leads you astray."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For many will come in my name, saying, \u2018I am he!\u2019 and will lead many astray."]],f:["or, \u201cI AM!\u201d"]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen you hear of wars and rumors of wars, don\u2019t be troubled. For those must happen, but the end is not yet."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For nation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom. There will be earthquakes in various places. There will be famines and troubles. These things are the beginning of birth pains."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut watch yourselves, for they will deliver you up to councils. You will be beaten in synagogues. You will stand before rulers and kings for my sake, for a testimony to them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The Good News must first be preached to all the nations."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When they lead you away and deliver you up, don\u2019t be anxious beforehand or premeditate what you will say, but say whatever will be given you in that hour. For it is not you who speak, but the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBrother will deliver up brother to death, and the father his child. Children will rise up against parents and cause them to be put to death."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You will be hated by all men for my name\u2019s sake, but he who endures to the end will be saved."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut when you see the abomination of desolation, spoken of by Daniel the prophet, standing where it ought not\u201d (let the reader understand), \u201cthen let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and let him who is on the housetop not go down, nor enter in, to take anything out of his house."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Let him who is in the field not return back to take his cloak."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But woe to those who are with child and to those who nurse babies in those days!"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Pray that your flight won\u2019t be in the winter."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For in those days there will be oppression, such as there has not been the like from the beginning of the creation which God created until now, and never will be."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Unless the Lord had shortened the days, no flesh would have been saved; but for the sake of the chosen ones, whom he picked out, he shortened the days."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then if anyone tells you, \u2018Look, here is the Christ!\u2019 or, \u2018Look, there!\u2019 don\u2019t believe it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For false christs and false prophets will arise and will show signs and wonders, that they may lead astray, if possible, even the chosen ones."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But you watch."],[0,"\u201cBehold, I have told you all things beforehand."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But in those days, after that oppression, the sun will be darkened, the moon will not give its light,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"the stars will be falling from the sky, and the powers that are in the heavens will be shaken."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Then they will see the Son of Man coming in clouds with great power and glory."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Then he will send out his angels, and will gather together his chosen ones from the four winds, from the ends of the earth to the ends of the sky."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow from the fig tree, learn this parable. When the branch has now become tender and produces its leaves, you know that the summer is near;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"even so you also, when you see these things coming to pass, know that it is near, at the doors."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Most certainly I say to you, this generation will not pass away until all these things happen."]],f:["The word translated \u201cgeneration\u201d (genea) could also be translated \u201crace\u201d, \u201cfamily\u201d, or \u201cpeople\u201d."]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Heaven and earth will pass away, but my words will not pass away."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut of that day or that hour no one knows\u2014not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but only the Father."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Watch, keep alert, and pray; for you don\u2019t know when the time is."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIt is like a man traveling to another country, having left his house and given authority to his servants, and to each one his work, and also commanded the doorkeeper to keep watch."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Watch therefore, for you don\u2019t know when the lord of the house is coming\u2014whether at evening, or at midnight, or when the rooster crows, or in the morning;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"lest, coming suddenly, he might find you sleeping."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"What I tell you, I tell all: Watch!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It was now two days before the Passover and the Feast of Unleavened Bread, and the chief priests and the scribes sought how they might seize him by deception and kill him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For they said, \u201cNot during the feast, because there might be a riot among the people.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was at Bethany, in the house of Simon the leper, as he sat at the table, a woman came having an alabaster jar of ointment of pure nard\u2014very costly. She broke the jar and poured it over his head."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But there were some who were indignant among themselves, saying, \u201cWhy has this ointment been wasted?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For this might have been sold for more than three hundred denarii and given to the poor.\u201d So they grumbled against her."]],f:["300 denarii was about a year\u2019s wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said, \u201cLeave her alone. Why do you trouble her? She has done a good work for me."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For you always have the poor with you, and whenever you want to, you can do them good; but you will not always have me."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"She has done what she could. She has anointed my body beforehand for the burying."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, wherever this Good News may be preached throughout the whole world, that which this woman has done will also be spoken of for a memorial of her.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Judas Iscariot, who was one of the twelve, went away to the chief priests, that he might deliver him to them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They, when they heard it, were glad, and promised to give him money. He sought how he might conveniently deliver him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"On the first day of unleavened bread, when they sacrificed the Passover, his disciples asked him, \u201cWhere do you want us to go and prepare that you may eat the Passover?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He sent two of his disciples and said to them, \u201cGo into the city, and there a man carrying a pitcher of water will meet you. Follow him,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and wherever he enters in, tell the master of the house, \u2018The Teacher says, \u201cWhere is the guest room, where I may eat the Passover with my disciples?\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He will himself show you a large upper room furnished and ready. Get ready for us there.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"His disciples went out, and came into the city, and found things as he had said to them, and they prepared the Passover."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When it was evening he came with the twelve."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"As they sat and were eating, Jesus said, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, one of you will betray me\u2014he who eats with me.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They began to be sorrowful, and to ask him one by one, \u201cSurely not I?\u201d And another said, \u201cSurely not I?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cIt is one of the twelve, he who dips with me in the dish."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For the Son of Man goes as it is written about him, but woe to that man by whom the Son of Man is betrayed! It would be better for that man if he had not been born.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"As they were eating, Jesus took bread, and when he had blessed it, he broke it and gave to them, and said, \u201cTake, eat. This is my body.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He took the cup, and when he had given thanks, he gave to them. They all drank of it."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThis is my blood of the new covenant, which is poured out for many."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, I will no more drink of the fruit of the vine until that day when I drink it anew in God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When they had sung a hymn, they went out to the Mount of Olives."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cAll of you will be made to stumble because of me tonight, for it is written, \u2018I will strike the shepherd, and the sheep will be scattered.\u2019"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"However, after I am raised up, I will go before you into Galilee.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter said to him, \u201cAlthough all will be offended, yet I will not.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cMost certainly I tell you that you today, even this night, before the rooster crows twice, you will deny me three times.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"But he spoke all the more, \u201cIf I must die with you, I will not deny you.\u201d They all said the same thing."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"They came to a place which was named Gethsemane. He said to his disciples, \u201cSit here while I pray.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He took with him Peter, James, and John, and began to be greatly troubled and distressed."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cMy soul is exceedingly sorrowful, even to death. Stay here and watch.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"He went forward a little, and fell on the ground, and prayed that if it were possible, the hour might pass away from him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cAbba, Father, all things are possible to you. Please remove this cup from me. However, not what I desire, but what you desire.\u201d"]],f:["Abba is a Greek spelling for the Aramaic word for \u201cFather\u201d or \u201cDaddy\u201d used in a familiar, respectful, and loving way."]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"He came and found them sleeping, and said to Peter, \u201cSimon, are you sleeping? Couldn\u2019t you watch one hour?"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Watch and pray, that you may not enter into temptation. The spirit indeed is willing, but the flesh is weak.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he went away and prayed, saying the same words."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Again he returned and found them sleeping, for their eyes were very heavy; and they didn\u2019t know what to answer him."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He came the third time and said to them, \u201cSleep on now, and take your rest. It is enough. The hour has come. Behold, the Son of Man is betrayed into the hands of sinners."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Arise! Let\u2019s get going. Behold, he who betrays me is at hand.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately, while he was still speaking, Judas, one of the twelve, came\u2014and with him a multitude with swords and clubs, from the chief priests, the scribes, and the elders."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Now he who betrayed him had given them a sign, saying, \u201cWhomever I will kiss, that is he. Seize him, and lead him away safely.\u201d"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"When he had come, immediately he came to him and said, \u201cRabbi! Rabbi!\u201d and kissed him."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"They laid their hands on him and seized him."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"But a certain one of those who stood by drew his sword and struck the servant of the high priest, and cut off his ear."]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cHave you come out, as against a robber, with swords and clubs to seize me?"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"I was daily with you in the temple teaching, and you didn\u2019t arrest me. But this is so that the Scriptures might be fulfilled.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"They all left him, and fled."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"A certain young man followed him, having a linen cloth thrown around himself over his naked body. The young men grabbed him,"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"but he left the linen cloth and fled from them naked."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"They led Jesus away to the high priest. All the chief priests, the elders, and the scribes came together with him."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter had followed him from a distance, until he came into the court of the high priest. He was sitting with the officers, and warming himself in the light of the fire."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"Now the chief priests and the whole council sought witnesses against Jesus to put him to death, and found none."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"For many gave false testimony against him, and their testimony didn\u2019t agree with each other."]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"Some stood up and gave false testimony against him, saying,"]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"\u201cWe heard him say, \u2018I will destroy this temple that is made with hands, and in three days I will build another made without hands.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"Even so, their testimony didn\u2019t agree."]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[0,"The high priest stood up in the middle, and asked Jesus, \u201cHave you no answer? What is it which these testify against you?\u201d"]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"But he stayed quiet, and answered nothing. Again the high priest asked him, \u201cAre you the Christ, the Son of the Blessed?\u201d"]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said, \u201cI am. You will see the Son of Man sitting at the right hand of Power, and coming with the clouds of the sky.\u201d"]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[0,"The high priest tore his clothes and said, \u201cWhat further need have we of witnesses?"]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"You have heard the blasphemy! What do you think?\u201d They all condemned him to be worthy of death."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"Some began to spit on him, and to cover his face, and to beat him with fists, and to tell him, \u201cProphesy!\u201d The officers struck him with the palms of their hands."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[0,"As Peter was in the courtyard below, one of the maids of the high priest came,"]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"and seeing Peter warming himself, she looked at him and said, \u201cYou were also with the Nazarene, Jesus!\u201d"]]},{v:68,p:1,l:[[0,"But he denied it, saying, \u201cI neither know nor understand what you are saying.\u201d He went out on the porch, and the rooster crowed."]]},{v:69,p:1,l:[[0,"The maid saw him and began again to tell those who stood by, \u201cThis is one of them.\u201d"]]},{v:70,l:[[0,"But he again denied it. After a little while again those who stood by said to Peter, \u201cYou truly are one of them, for you are a Galilean, and your speech shows it.\u201d"]]},{v:71,l:[[0,"But he began to curse and to swear, \u201cI don\u2019t know this man of whom you speak!\u201d"]]},{v:72,p:1,l:[[0,"The rooster crowed the second time. Peter remembered the words that Jesus said to him, \u201cBefore the rooster crows twice, you will deny me three times.\u201d When he thought about that, he wept."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately in the morning the chief priests, with the elders, scribes, and the whole council, held a consultation, bound Jesus, carried him away, and delivered him up to Pilate."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Pilate asked him, \u201cAre you the King of the Jews?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cSo you say.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The chief priests accused him of many things."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Pilate again asked him, \u201cHave you no answer? See how many things they testify against you!\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus made no further answer, so that Pilate marveled."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now at the feast he used to release to them one prisoner, whomever they asked of him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"There was one called Barabbas, bound with his fellow insurgents, men who in the insurrection had committed murder."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The multitude, crying aloud, began to ask him to do as he always did for them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Pilate answered them, saying, \u201cDo you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For he perceived that for envy the chief priests had delivered him up."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But the chief priests stirred up the multitude, that he should release Barabbas to them instead."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Pilate again asked them, \u201cWhat then should I do to him whom you call the King of the Jews?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"They cried out again, \u201cCrucify him!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate said to them, \u201cWhy, what evil has he done?\u201d"],[0,"But they cried out exceedingly, \u201cCrucify him!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate, wishing to please the multitude, released Barabbas to them, and handed over Jesus, when he had flogged him, to be crucified."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The soldiers led him away within the court, which is the Praetorium; and they called together the whole cohort."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They clothed him with purple; and weaving a crown of thorns, they put it on him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They began to salute him, \u201cHail, King of the Jews!\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They struck his head with a reed and spat on him, and bowing their knees, did homage to him."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When they had mocked him, they took the purple cloak off him, and put his own garments on him. They led him out to crucify him."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"They compelled one passing by, coming from the country, Simon of Cyrene, the father of Alexander and Rufus, to go with them that he might bear his cross."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"They brought him to the place called Golgotha, which is, being interpreted, \u201cThe place of a skull.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They offered him wine mixed with myrrh to drink, but he didn\u2019t take it."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Crucifying him, they parted his garments among them, casting lots on them, what each should take."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"It was the third hour when they crucified him."]],f:["9:00 a.m."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The superscription of his accusation was written over him: \u201cTHE KING OF THE JEWS.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"With him they crucified two robbers, one on his right hand, and one on his left."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"The Scripture was fulfilled which says, \u201cHe was counted with transgressors.\u201d"]],f:["NU omits verse 28."]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who passed by blasphemed him, wagging their heads and saying, \u201cHa! You who destroy the temple and build it in three days,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"save yourself, and come down from the cross!\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Likewise, also the chief priests mocking among themselves with the scribes said, \u201cHe saved others. He can\u2019t save himself."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Let the Christ, the King of Israel, now come down from the cross, that we may see and believe him.\u201d Those who were crucified with him also insulted him."]],f:["TR omits \u201chim\u201d"]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"When the sixth hour had come, there was darkness over the whole land until the ninth hour."]],f:["or, noon","3:00 p.m."]},{v:34,l:[[0,"At the ninth hour Jesus cried with a loud voice, saying, \u201cEloi, Eloi, lama sabachthani?\u201d which is, being interpreted, \u201cMy God, my God, why have you forsaken me?\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of those who stood by, when they heard it, said, \u201cBehold, he is calling Elijah.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"One ran, and filling a sponge full of vinegar, put it on a reed and gave it to him to drink, saying, \u201cLet him be. Let\u2019s see whether Elijah comes to take him down.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus cried out with a loud voice, and gave up the spirit."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"The veil of the temple was torn in two from the top to the bottom."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"When the centurion, who stood by opposite him, saw that he cried out like this and breathed his last, he said, \u201cTruly this man was the Son of God!\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"There were also women watching from afar, among whom were both Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of James the less and of Joses, and Salome;"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"who, when he was in Galilee, followed him and served him; and many other women who came up with him to Jerusalem."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"When evening had now come, because it was the Preparation Day, that is, the day before the Sabbath,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Joseph of Arimathaea, a prominent council member who also himself was looking for God\u2019s Kingdom, came. He boldly went in to Pilate, and asked for Jesus\u2019 body."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Pilate was surprised to hear that he was already dead; and summoning the centurion, he asked him whether he had been dead long."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"When he found out from the centurion, he granted the body to Joseph."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"He bought a linen cloth, and taking him down, wound him in the linen cloth and laid him in a tomb which had been cut out of a rock. He rolled a stone against the door of the tomb."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Mary Magdalene and Mary the mother of Joses, saw where he was laid."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When the Sabbath was past, Mary Magdalene, and Mary the mother of James, and Salome bought spices, that they might come and anoint him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Very early on the first day of the week, they came to the tomb when the sun had risen."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They were saying among themselves, \u201cWho will roll away the stone from the door of the tomb for us?\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for it was very big. Looking up, they saw that the stone was rolled back."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Entering into the tomb, they saw a young man sitting on the right side, dressed in a white robe; and they were amazed."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t be amazed. You seek Jesus, the Nazarene, who has been crucified. He has risen! He is not here. See the place where they laid him!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But go, tell his disciples and Peter, \u2018He goes before you into Galilee. There you will see him, as he said to you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"They went out, and fled from the tomb, for trembling and astonishment had come on them. They said nothing to anyone; for they were afraid."]],f:["TR adds \u201cquickly\u201d","One isolated manuscript omits verses 9-20 but adds this \u201cshort ending of Mark\u201d to the end of verse 8: They told all that had been commanded them briefly to those around Peter. After that, Jesus himself sent them out, from east to west, with the sacred and imperishable proclamation of eternal salvation."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when he had risen early on the first day of the week, he appeared first to Mary Magdalene, from whom he had cast out seven demons."]],f:["NU includes the text of verses 9-20, but mentions in a footnote that a few manuscripts omitted it. The translators of the World English Bible regard Mark 16:9-20 as reliable based on an overwhelming majority of textual evidence, including not only the authoritative Greek Majority Text New Testament, but also the TR and many of the manuscripts cited in the NU text."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"She went and told those who had been with him, as they mourned and wept."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When they heard that he was alive and had been seen by her, they disbelieved."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things he was revealed in another form to two of them as they walked, on their way into the country."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They went away and told it to the rest. They didn\u2019t believe them, either."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Afterward he was revealed to the eleven themselves as they sat at the table; and he rebuked them for their unbelief and hardness of heart, because they didn\u2019t believe those who had seen him after he had risen."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cGo into all the world and preach the Good News to the whole creation."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He who believes and is baptized will be saved; but he who disbelieves will be condemned."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"These signs will accompany those who believe: in my name they will cast out demons; they will speak with new languages;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"they will take up serpents; and if they drink any deadly thing, it will in no way hurt them; they will lay hands on the sick, and they will recover.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So then the Lord, after he had spoken to them, was received up into heaven and sat down at the right hand of God."]],f:["NU adds \u201cJesus\u201d"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They went out and preached everywhere, the Lord working with them and confirming the word by the signs that followed. Amen."]]}]]}},1312,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,n,i){a.exports={book:"Luke",name:"Luke",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Since many have undertaken to set in order a narrative concerning those matters which have been fulfilled among us,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"even as those who from the beginning were eyewitnesses and servants of the word delivered them to us,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"it seemed good to me also, having traced the course of all things accurately from the first, to write to you in order, most excellent Theophilus;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"that you might know the certainty concerning the things in which you were instructed."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"There was in the days of Herod, the king of Judea, a certain priest named Zacharias, of the priestly division of Abijah. He had a wife of the daughters of Aaron, and her name was Elizabeth."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They were both righteous before God, walking blamelessly in all the commandments and ordinances of the Lord."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But they had no child, because Elizabeth was barren, and they both were well advanced in years."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now while he executed the priest\u2019s office before God in the order of his division"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"according to the custom of the priest\u2019s office, his lot was to enter into the temple of the Lord and burn incense."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The whole multitude of the people were praying outside at the hour of incense."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"An angel of the Lord appeared to him, standing on the right side of the altar of incense."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Zacharias was troubled when he saw him, and fear fell upon him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But the angel said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, Zacharias, because your request has been heard. Your wife, Elizabeth, will bear you a son, and you shall call his name John."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You will have joy and gladness, and many will rejoice at his birth."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For he will be great in the sight of the Lord, and he will drink no wine nor strong drink. He will be filled with the Holy Spirit, even from his mother\u2019s womb."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He will turn many of the children of Israel to the Lord their God."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He will go before him in the spirit and power of Elijah, \u2018to turn the hearts of the fathers to the children,\u2019 and the disobedient to the wisdom of the just; to prepare a people prepared for the Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Zacharias said to the angel, \u201cHow can I be sure of this? For I am an old man, and my wife is well advanced in years.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The angel answered him, \u201cI am Gabriel, who stands in the presence of God. I was sent to speak to you and to bring you this good news."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Behold, you will be silent and not able to speak until the day that these things will happen, because you didn\u2019t believe my words, which will be fulfilled in their proper time.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The people were waiting for Zacharias, and they marveled that he delayed in the temple."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When he came out, he could not speak to them. They perceived that he had seen a vision in the temple. He continued making signs to them, and remained mute."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When the days of his service were fulfilled, he departed to his house."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"After these days Elizabeth his wife conceived, and she hid herself five months, saying,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"\u201cThus has the Lord done to me in the days in which he looked at me, to take away my reproach among men.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the sixth month, the angel Gabriel was sent from God to a city of Galilee named Nazareth,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"to a virgin pledged to be married to a man whose name was Joseph, of David\u2019s house. The virgin\u2019s name was Mary."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Having come in, the angel said to her, \u201cRejoice, you highly favored one! The Lord is with you. Blessed are you among women!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"But when she saw him, she was greatly troubled at the saying, and considered what kind of salutation this might be."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The angel said to her, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, Mary, for you have found favor with God."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Behold, you will conceive in your womb and give birth to a son, and shall name him \u2018Jesus.\u2019"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He will be great and will be called the Son of the Most High. The Lord God will give him the throne of his father David,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"and he will reign over the house of Jacob forever. There will be no end to his Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Mary said to the angel, \u201cHow can this be, seeing I am a virgin?\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"The angel answered her, \u201cThe Holy Spirit will come on you, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you. Therefore also the holy one who is born from you will be called the Son of God."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Behold, Elizabeth your relative also has conceived a son in her old age; and this is the sixth month with her who was called barren."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For nothing spoken by God is impossible.\u201d"]],f:["or, \u201cFor everything spoken by God is possible.\u201d"]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Mary said, \u201cBehold, the servant of the Lord; let it be done to me according to your word.\u201d"],[0,"Then the angel departed from her."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Mary arose in those days and went into the hill country with haste, into a city of Judah,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"and entered into the house of Zacharias and greeted Elizabeth."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"When Elizabeth heard Mary\u2019s greeting, the baby leaped in her womb; and Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"She called out with a loud voice and said, \u201cBlessed are you among women, and blessed is the fruit of your womb!"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Why am I so favored, that the mother of my Lord should come to me?"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"For behold, when the voice of your greeting came into my ears, the baby leaped in my womb for joy!"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Blessed is she who believed, for there will be a fulfillment of the things which have been spoken to her from the Lord!\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"Mary said,"],[1,"\u201cMy soul magnifies the Lord."]]},{v:47,l:[[2,"My spirit has rejoiced in God my Savior,"]]},{v:48,l:[[2,"for he has looked at the humble state of his servant."],[1,"For behold, from now on, all generations will call me blessed."]]},{v:49,l:[[2,"For he who is mighty has done great things for me."],[2,"Holy is his name."]]},{v:50,l:[[2,"His mercy is for generations and generations on those who fear him."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[1,"He has shown strength with his arm."],[2,"He has scattered the proud in the imagination of their hearts."]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[1,"He has put down princes from their thrones,"],[2,"and has exalted the lowly."]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[1,"He has filled the hungry with good things."],[2,"He has sent the rich away empty."]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[1,"He has given help to Israel, his servant, that he might remember mercy,"]]},{v:55,l:[[2,"as he spoke to our fathers,"],[2,"to Abraham and his offspring forever.\u201d"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[0,"Mary stayed with her about three months, and then returned to her house."]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the time that Elizabeth should give birth was fulfilled, and she gave birth to a son."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"Her neighbors and her relatives heard that the Lord had magnified his mercy toward her, and they rejoiced with her."]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"On the eighth day, they came to circumcise the child; and they would have called him Zacharias, after the name of his father."]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"His mother answered, \u201cNot so; but he will be called John.\u201d"]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to her, \u201cThere is no one among your relatives who is called by this name.\u201d"]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"They made signs to his father, what he would have him called."]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[0,"He asked for a writing tablet, and wrote, \u201cHis name is John.\u201d"],[0,"They all marveled."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"His mouth was opened immediately and his tongue freed, and he spoke, blessing God."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"Fear came on all who lived around them, and all these sayings were talked about throughout all the hill country of Judea."]]},{v:66,l:[[0,"All who heard them laid them up in their heart, saying, \u201cWhat then will this child be?\u201d The hand of the Lord was with him."]]},{v:67,p:1,l:[[0,"His father Zacharias was filled with the Holy Spirit, and prophesied, saying,"]]},{v:68,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBlessed be the Lord, the God of Israel,"],[2,"for he has visited and redeemed his people;"]]},{v:69,p:1,l:[[1,"and has raised up a horn of salvation for us in the house of his servant David"]]},{v:70,l:[[2,"(as he spoke by the mouth of his holy prophets who have been from of old),"]]},{v:71,l:[[2,"salvation from our enemies and from the hand of all who hate us;"]]},{v:72,p:1,l:[[1,"to show mercy toward our fathers,"],[2,"to remember his holy covenant,"]]},{v:73,p:1,l:[[1,"the oath which he swore to Abraham our father,"]]},{v:74,l:[[2,"to grant to us that we, being delivered out of the hand of our enemies,"],[2,"should serve him without fear,"]]},{v:75,l:[[2,"in holiness and righteousness before him all the days of our life."]]},{v:76,p:1,l:[[1,"And you, child, will be called a prophet of the Most High;"],[2,"for you will go before the face of the Lord to prepare his ways,"]]},{v:77,l:[[2,"to give knowledge of salvation to his people by the remission of their sins,"]]},{v:78,p:1,l:[[1,"because of the tender mercy of our God,"],[2,"by which the dawn from on high will visit us,"]]},{v:79,l:[[2,"to shine on those who sit in darkness and the shadow of death;"],[2,"to guide our feet into the way of peace.\u201d"]]},{v:80,p:1,l:[[0,"The child was growing and becoming strong in spirit, and was in the desert until the day of his public appearance to Israel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in those days, a decree went out from Caesar Augustus that all the world should be enrolled."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"This was the first enrollment made when Quirinius was governor of Syria."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All went to enroll themselves, everyone to his own city."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Joseph also went up from Galilee, out of the city of Nazareth, into Judea, to David\u2019s city, which is called Bethlehem, because he was of the house and family of David,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"to enroll himself with Mary, who was pledged to be married to him as wife, being pregnant."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"While they were there, the day had come for her to give birth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"She gave birth to her firstborn son. She wrapped him in bands of cloth and laid him in a feeding trough, because there was no room for them in the inn."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"There were shepherds in the same country staying in the field, and keeping watch by night over their flock."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Behold, an angel of the Lord stood by them, and the glory of the Lord shone around them, and they were terrified."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The angel said to them, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, for behold, I bring you good news of great joy which will be to all the people."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For there is born to you today, in David\u2019s city, a Savior, who is Christ the Lord."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:12,l:[[0,"This is the sign to you: you will find a baby wrapped in strips of cloth, lying in a feeding trough.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Suddenly, there was with the angel a multitude of the heavenly army praising God and saying,"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cGlory to God in the highest,"],[2,"on earth peace, good will toward men.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When the angels went away from them into the sky, the shepherds said to one another, \u201cLet\u2019s go to Bethlehem, now, and see this thing that has happened, which the Lord has made known to us.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They came with haste and found both Mary and Joseph, and the baby was lying in the feeding trough."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When they saw it, they publicized widely the saying which was spoken to them about this child."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"All who heard it wondered at the things which were spoken to them by the shepherds."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But Mary kept all these sayings, pondering them in her heart."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The shepherds returned, glorifying and praising God for all the things that they had heard and seen, just as it was told them."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When eight days were fulfilled for the circumcision of the child, his name was called Jesus, which was given by the angel before he was conceived in the womb."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"When the days of their purification according to the law of Moses were fulfilled, they brought him up to Jerusalem to present him to the Lord"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"(as it is written in the law of the Lord, \u201cEvery male who opens the womb shall be called holy to the Lord\u201d),"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and to offer a sacrifice according to that which is said in the law of the Lord, \u201cA pair of turtledoves, or two young pigeons.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, there was a man in Jerusalem whose name was Simeon. This man was righteous and devout, looking for the consolation of Israel, and the Holy Spirit was on him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"It had been revealed to him by the Holy Spirit that he should not see death before he had seen the Lord\u2019s Christ."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d (Greek) and \u201cMessiah\u201d (Hebrew) both mean \u201cAnointed One\u201d"]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He came in the Spirit into the temple. When the parents brought in the child, Jesus, that they might do concerning him according to the custom of the law,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"then he received him into his arms and blessed God, and said,"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cNow you are releasing your servant, Master,"],[2,"according to your word, in peace;"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[1,"for my eyes have seen your salvation,"]]},{v:31,l:[[2,"which you have prepared before the face of all peoples;"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[1,"a light for revelation to the nations,"],[2,"and the glory of your people Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Joseph and his mother were marveling at the things which were spoken concerning him."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Simeon blessed them, and said to Mary, his mother, \u201cBehold, this child is appointed for the falling and the rising of many in Israel, and for a sign which is spoken against."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Yes, a sword will pierce through your own soul, that the thoughts of many hearts may be revealed.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"There was one Anna, a prophetess, the daughter of Phanuel, of the tribe of Asher (she was of a great age, having lived with a husband seven years from her virginity,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"and she had been a widow for about eighty-four years), who didn\u2019t depart from the temple, worshiping with fastings and petitions night and day."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Coming up at that very hour, she gave thanks to the Lord, and spoke of him to all those who were looking for redemption in Jerusalem."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had accomplished all things that were according to the law of the Lord, they returned into Galilee, to their own city, Nazareth."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"The child was growing, and was becoming strong in spirit, being filled with wisdom, and the grace of God was upon him."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"His parents went every year to Jerusalem at the feast of the Passover."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"When he was twelve years old, they went up to Jerusalem according to the custom of the feast;"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"and when they had fulfilled the days, as they were returning, the boy Jesus stayed behind in Jerusalem. Joseph and his mother didn\u2019t know it,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"but supposing him to be in the company, they went a day\u2019s journey; and they looked for him among their relatives and acquaintances."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"When they didn\u2019t find him, they returned to Jerusalem, looking for him."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"After three days they found him in the temple, sitting in the middle of the teachers, both listening to them and asking them questions."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"All who heard him were amazed at his understanding and his answers."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"When they saw him, they were astonished; and his mother said to him, \u201cSon, why have you treated us this way? Behold, your father and I were anxiously looking for you.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhy were you looking for me? Didn\u2019t you know that I must be in my Father\u2019s house?\u201d"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t understand the saying which he spoke to them."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"And he went down with them and came to Nazareth. He was subject to them, and his mother kept all these sayings in her heart."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"And Jesus increased in wisdom and stature, and in favor with God and men."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the fifteenth year of the reign of Tiberius Caesar, Pontius Pilate being governor of Judea, and Herod being tetrarch of Galilee, and his brother Philip tetrarch of the region of Ituraea and Trachonitis, and Lysanias tetrarch of Abilene,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"during the high priesthood of Annas and Caiaphas, the word of God came to John, the son of Zacharias, in the wilderness."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He came into all the region around the Jordan, preaching the baptism of repentance for remission of sins."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"As it is written in the book of the words of Isaiah the prophet,"],[1,"\u201cThe voice of one crying in the wilderness,"],[2,"\u2018Make ready the way of the Lord."],[1,"Make his paths straight."]]},{v:5,l:[[2,"Every valley will be filled."],[1,"Every mountain and hill will be brought low."],[2,"The crooked will become straight,"],[2,"and the rough ways smooth."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"All flesh will see God\u2019s salvation.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He said therefore to the multitudes who went out to be baptized by him, \u201cYou offspring of vipers, who warned you to flee from the wrath to come?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore produce fruits worthy of repentance, and don\u2019t begin to say among yourselves, \u2018We have Abraham for our father;\u2019 for I tell you that God is able to raise up children to Abraham from these stones!"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Even now the ax also lies at the root of the trees. Every tree therefore that doesn\u2019t produce good fruit is cut down and thrown into the fire.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The multitudes asked him, \u201cWhat then must we do?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cHe who has two coats, let him give to him who has none. He who has food, let him do likewise.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Tax collectors also came to be baptized, and they said to him, \u201cTeacher, what must we do?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cCollect no more than that which is appointed to you.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Soldiers also asked him, saying, \u201cWhat about us? What must we do?\u201d"],[0,"He said to them, \u201cExtort from no one by violence, neither accuse anyone wrongfully. Be content with your wages.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"As the people were in expectation, and all men reasoned in their hearts concerning John, whether perhaps he was the Christ,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"John answered them all, \u201cI indeed baptize you with water, but he comes who is mightier than I, the strap of whose sandals I am not worthy to loosen. He will baptize you in the Holy Spirit and fire."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"His winnowing fan is in his hand, and he will thoroughly cleanse his threshing floor, and will gather the wheat into his barn; but he will burn up the chaff with unquenchable fire.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then with many other exhortations he preached good news to the people,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"but Herod the tetrarch, being reproved by him for Herodias, his brother\u2019s wife, and for all the evil things which Herod had done,"]],f:["a tetrarch is one of four governors of a province","TR reads \u201cbrother Philip\u2019s\u201d instead of \u201cbrother\u2019s\u201d"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"added this also to them all, that he shut up John in prison."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when all the people were baptized, Jesus also had been baptized and was praying. The sky was opened,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"and the Holy Spirit descended in a bodily form like a dove on him; and a voice came out of the sky, saying \u201cYou are my beloved Son. In you I am well pleased.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus himself, when he began to teach, was about thirty years old, being the son (as was supposed) of Joseph, the son of Heli,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"the son of Matthat, the son of Levi, the son of Melchi, the son of Jannai, the son of Joseph,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"the son of Mattathias, the son of Amos, the son of Nahum, the son of Esli, the son of Naggai,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"the son of Maath, the son of Mattathias, the son of Semein, the son of Joseph, the son of Judah,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"the son of Joanan, the son of Rhesa, the son of Zerubbabel, the son of Shealtiel, the son of Neri,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"the son of Melchi, the son of Addi, the son of Cosam, the son of Elmodam, the son of Er,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"the son of Jose, the son of Eliezer, the son of Jorim, the son of Matthat, the son of Levi,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"the son of Simeon, the son of Judah, the son of Joseph, the son of Jonan, the son of Eliakim,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"the son of Melea, the son of Menan, the son of Mattatha, the son of Nathan, the son of David,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"the son of Jesse, the son of Obed, the son of Boaz, the son of Salmon, the son of Nahshon,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"the son of Amminadab, the son of Aram, the son of Hezron, the son of Perez, the son of Judah,"]],f:["NU reads \u201cAdmin, the son of Arni\u201d instead of \u201cAram\u201d"]},{v:34,l:[[0,"the son of Jacob, the son of Isaac, the son of Abraham, the son of Terah, the son of Nahor,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"the son of Serug, the son of Reu, the son of Peleg, the son of Eber, the son of Shelah,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"the son of Cainan, the son of Arphaxad, the son of Shem, the son of Noah, the son of Lamech,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"the son of Methuselah, the son of Enoch, the son of Jared, the son of Mahalaleel, the son of Cainan,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"the son of Enos, the son of Seth, the son of Adam, the son of God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, full of the Holy Spirit, returned from the Jordan and was led by the Spirit into the wilderness"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"for forty days, being tempted by the devil. He ate nothing in those days. Afterward, when they were completed, he was hungry."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The devil said to him, \u201cIf you are the Son of God, command this stone to become bread.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, saying, \u201cIt is written, \u2018Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word of God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The devil, leading him up on a high mountain, showed him all the kingdoms of the world in a moment of time."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The devil said to him, \u201cI will give you all this authority and their glory, for it has been delivered to me, and I give it to whomever I want."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If you therefore will worship before me, it will all be yours.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cGet behind me, Satan! For it is written, \u2018You shall worship the Lord your God, and you shall serve him only.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He led him to Jerusalem and set him on the pinnacle of the temple, and said to him, \u201cIf you are the Son of God, cast yourself down from here,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for it is written,"],[1,"\u2018He will put his angels in charge of you, to guard you;\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"and,"],[1,"\u2018On their hands they will bear you up,"],[2,"lest perhaps you dash your foot against a stone.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answering, said to him, \u201cIt has been said, \u2018You shall not tempt the Lord your God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When the devil had completed every temptation, he departed from him until another time."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus returned in the power of the Spirit into Galilee, and news about him spread through all the surrounding area."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He taught in their synagogues, being glorified by all."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He came to Nazareth, where he had been brought up. He entered, as was his custom, into the synagogue on the Sabbath day, and stood up to read."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The book of the prophet Isaiah was handed to him. He opened the book, and found the place where it was written,"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThe Spirit of the Lord is on me,"],[2,"because he has anointed me to preach good news to the poor."],[1,"He has sent me to heal the broken hearted,"],[2,"to proclaim release to the captives,"],[2,"recovering of sight to the blind,"],[2,"to deliver those who are crushed,"]],f:["NU omits \u201cto heal the broken hearted\u201d"]},{v:19,l:[[2,"and to proclaim the acceptable year of the Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He closed the book, gave it back to the attendant, and sat down. The eyes of all in the synagogue were fastened on him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He began to tell them, \u201cToday, this Scripture has been fulfilled in your hearing.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"All testified about him and wondered at the gracious words which proceeded out of his mouth; and they said, \u201cIsn\u2019t this Joseph\u2019s son?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDoubtless you will tell me this proverb, \u2018Physician, heal yourself! Whatever we have heard done at Capernaum, do also here in your hometown.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, no prophet is acceptable in his hometown."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But truly I tell you, there were many widows in Israel in the days of Elijah, when the sky was shut up three years and six months, when a great famine came over all the land."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Elijah was sent to none of them, except to Zarephath, in the land of Sidon, to a woman who was a widow."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"There were many lepers in Israel in the time of Elisha the prophet, yet not one of them was cleansed, except Naaman, the Syrian.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They were all filled with wrath in the synagogue as they heard these things."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They rose up, threw him out of the city, and led him to the brow of the hill that their city was built on, that they might throw him off the cliff."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But he, passing through the middle of them, went his way."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"He came down to Capernaum, a city of Galilee. He was teaching them on the Sabbath day,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"and they were astonished at his teaching, for his word was with authority."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"In the synagogue there was a man who had a spirit of an unclean demon; and he cried out with a loud voice,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cAh! what have we to do with you, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are: the Holy One of God!\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus rebuked him, saying, \u201cBe silent and come out of him!\u201d When the demon had thrown him down in the middle of them, he came out of him, having done him no harm."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Amazement came on all and they spoke together, one with another, saying, \u201cWhat is this word? For with authority and power he commands the unclean spirits, and they come out!\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"News about him went out into every place of the surrounding region."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"He rose up from the synagogue and entered into Simon\u2019s house. Simon\u2019s mother-in-law was afflicted with a great fever, and they begged him to help her."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"He stood over her and rebuked the fever, and it left her. Immediately she rose up and served them."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"When the sun was setting, all those who had any sick with various diseases brought them to him; and he laid his hands on every one of them, and healed them."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Demons also came out of many, crying out and saying, \u201cYou are the Christ, the Son of God!\u201d Rebuking them, he didn\u2019t allow them to speak, because they knew that he was the Christ."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"When it was day, he departed and went into an uninhabited place and the multitudes looked for him, and came to him, and held on to him, so that he wouldn\u2019t go away from them."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"But he said to them, \u201cI must preach the good news of God\u2019s Kingdom to the other cities also. For this reason I have been sent.\u201d"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"He was preaching in the synagogues of Galilee."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now while the multitude pressed on him and heard the word of God, he was standing by the lake of Gennesaret."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He saw two boats standing by the lake, but the fishermen had gone out of them and were washing their nets."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He entered into one of the boats, which was Simon\u2019s, and asked him to put out a little from the land. He sat down and taught the multitudes from the boat."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had finished speaking, he said to Simon, \u201cPut out into the deep and let down your nets for a catch.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon answered him, \u201cMaster, we worked all night and caught nothing; but at your word I will let down the net.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When they had done this, they caught a great multitude of fish, and their net was breaking."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They beckoned to their partners in the other boat, that they should come and help them. They came and filled both boats, so that they began to sink."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But Simon Peter, when he saw it, fell down at Jesus\u2019 knees, saying, \u201cDepart from me, for I am a sinful man, Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For he was amazed, and all who were with him, at the catch of fish which they had caught;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and so also were James and John, sons of Zebedee, who were partners with Simon."],[0,"Jesus said to Simon, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid. From now on you will be catching people alive.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had brought their boats to land, they left everything, and followed him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was in one of the cities, behold, there was a man full of leprosy. When he saw Jesus, he fell on his face and begged him, saying, \u201cLord, if you want to, you can make me clean.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"He stretched out his hand and touched him, saying, \u201cI want to. Be made clean.\u201d"],[0,"Immediately the leprosy left him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He commanded him to tell no one, \u201cBut go your way and show yourself to the priest, and offer for your cleansing according to what Moses commanded, for a testimony to them.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"But the report concerning him spread much more, and great multitudes came together to hear and to be healed by him of their infirmities."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But he withdrew himself into the desert and prayed."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"On one of those days, he was teaching; and there were Pharisees and teachers of the law sitting by who had come out of every village of Galilee, Judea, and Jerusalem. The power of the Lord was with him to heal them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Behold, men brought a paralyzed man on a cot, and they sought to bring him in to lay before Jesus."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Not finding a way to bring him in because of the multitude, they went up to the housetop and let him down through the tiles with his cot into the middle before Jesus."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Seeing their faith, he said to him, \u201cMan, your sins are forgiven you.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The scribes and the Pharisees began to reason, saying, \u201cWho is this who speaks blasphemies? Who can forgive sins, but God alone?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus, perceiving their thoughts, answered them, \u201cWhy are you reasoning so in your hearts?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Which is easier to say, \u2018Your sins are forgiven you,\u2019 or to say, \u2018Arise and walk\u2019?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But that you may know that the Son of Man has authority on earth to forgive sins,\u201d he said to the paralyzed man, \u201cI tell you, arise, take up your cot, and go to your house.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately he rose up before them, and took up that which he was laying on, and departed to his house, glorifying God."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Amazement took hold on all, and they glorified God. They were filled with fear, saying, \u201cWe have seen strange things today.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things he went out and saw a tax collector named Levi sitting at the tax office, and said to him, \u201cFollow me!\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He left everything, and rose up and followed him."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Levi made a great feast for him in his house. There was a great crowd of tax collectors and others who were reclining with them."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Their scribes and the Pharisees murmured against his disciples, saying, \u201cWhy do you eat and drink with the tax collectors and sinners?\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cThose who are healthy have no need for a physician, but those who are sick do."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners, to repentance.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cWhy do John\u2019s disciples often fast and pray, likewise also the disciples of the Pharisees, but yours eat and drink?\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cCan you make the friends of the bridegroom fast while the bridegroom is with them?"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"But the days will come when the bridegroom will be taken away from them. Then they will fast in those days.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"He also told a parable to them. \u201cNo one puts a piece from a new garment on an old garment, or else he will tear the new, and also the piece from the new will not match the old."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"No one puts new wine into old wineskins, or else the new wine will burst the skins, and it will be spilled and the skins will be destroyed."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But new wine must be put into fresh wineskins, and both are preserved."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"No man having drunk old wine immediately desires new, for he says, \u2018The old is better.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the second Sabbath after the first, he was going through the grain fields. His disciples plucked the heads of grain and ate, rubbing them in their hands."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But some of the Pharisees said to them, \u201cWhy do you do that which is not lawful to do on the Sabbath day?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, answering them, said, \u201cHaven\u2019t you read what David did when he was hungry, he and those who were with him,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"how he entered into God\u2019s house, and took and ate the show bread, and gave also to those who were with him, which is not lawful to eat except for the priests alone?\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThe Son of Man is lord of the Sabbath.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"It also happened on another Sabbath that he entered into the synagogue and taught. There was a man there, and his right hand was withered."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The scribes and the Pharisees watched him, to see whether he would heal on the Sabbath, that they might find an accusation against him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But he knew their thoughts; and he said to the man who had the withered hand, \u201cRise up and stand in the middle.\u201d He arose and stood."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said to them, \u201cI will ask you something: Is it lawful on the Sabbath to do good, or to do harm? To save a life, or to kill?\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He looked around at them all, and said to the man, \u201cStretch out your hand.\u201d He did, and his hand was restored as sound as the other."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But they were filled with rage, and talked with one another about what they might do to Jesus."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"In these days, he went out to the mountain to pray, and he continued all night in prayer to God."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When it was day, he called his disciples, and from them he chose twelve, whom he also named apostles:"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Simon, whom he also named Peter; Andrew, his brother; James; John; Philip; Bartholomew;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Matthew; Thomas; James the son of Alphaeus; Simon who was called the Zealot;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Judas the son of James; and Judas Iscariot, who also became a traitor."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"He came down with them and stood on a level place, with a crowd of his disciples and a great number of the people from all Judea and Jerusalem and the sea coast of Tyre and Sidon, who came to hear him and to be healed of their diseases,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"as well as those who were troubled by unclean spirits; and they were being healed."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"All the multitude sought to touch him, for power came out of him and healed them all."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He lifted up his eyes to his disciples, and said:"],[1,"\u201cBlessed are you who are poor,"],[2,"for God\u2019s Kingdom is yours."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are you who hunger now,"],[2,"for you will be filled."],[1,"Blessed are you who weep now,"],[2,"for you will laugh."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed are you when men hate you, and when they exclude and mock you, and throw out your name as evil, for the Son of Man\u2019s sake."]]},{v:23,l:[[2,"Rejoice in that day and leap for joy, for behold, your reward is great in heaven, for their fathers did the same thing to the prophets."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBut woe to you who are rich!"],[2,"For you have received your consolation."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe to you, you who are full now,"],[2,"for you will be hungry."],[1,"Woe to you who laugh now,"],[2,"for you will mourn and weep."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Woe, when men speak well of you,"],[2,"for their fathers did the same thing to the false prophets."]],f:["TR adds \u201cto you\u201d","TR adds \u201call\u201d"]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut I tell you who hear: love your enemies, do good to those who hate you,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"bless those who curse you, and pray for those who mistreat you."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"To him who strikes you on the cheek, offer also the other; and from him who takes away your cloak, don\u2019t withhold your coat also."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Give to everyone who asks you, and don\u2019t ask him who takes away your goods to give them back again."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs you would like people to do to you, do exactly so to them."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf you love those who love you, what credit is that to you? For even sinners love those who love them."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"If you do good to those who do good to you, what credit is that to you? For even sinners do the same."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"If you lend to those from whom you hope to receive, what credit is that to you? Even sinners lend to sinners, to receive back as much."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"But love your enemies, and do good, and lend, expecting nothing back; and your reward will be great, and you will be children of the Most High; for he is kind toward the unthankful and evil."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTherefore be merciful,"],[2,"even as your Father is also merciful."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"Don\u2019t judge,"],[2,"and you won\u2019t be judged."],[1,"Don\u2019t condemn,"],[2,"and you won\u2019t be condemned."],[1,"Set free,"],[2,"and you will be set free."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cGive, and it will be given to you: good measure, pressed down, shaken together, and running over, will be given to you. For with the same measure you measure it will be measured back to you.\u201d"]],f:["literally, into your bosom."]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"He spoke a parable to them. \u201cCan the blind guide the blind? Won\u2019t they both fall into a pit?"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"A disciple is not above his teacher, but everyone when he is fully trained will be like his teacher."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Why do you see the speck of chaff that is in your brother\u2019s eye, but don\u2019t consider the beam that is in your own eye?"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Or how can you tell your brother, \u2018Brother, let me remove the speck of chaff that is in your eye,\u2019 when you yourself don\u2019t see the beam that is in your own eye? You hypocrite! First remove the beam from your own eye, and then you can see clearly to remove the speck of chaff that is in your brother\u2019s eye."]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor there is no good tree that produces rotten fruit, nor again a rotten tree that produces good fruit."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"For each tree is known by its own fruit. For people don\u2019t gather figs from thorns, nor do they gather grapes from a bramble bush."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"The good man out of the good treasure of his heart brings out that which is good, and the evil man out of the evil treasure of his heart brings out that which is evil, for out of the abundance of the heart, his mouth speaks."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhy do you call me, \u2018Lord, Lord,\u2019 and don\u2019t do the things which I say?"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Everyone who comes to me, and hears my words and does them, I will show you who he is like."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He is like a man building a house, who dug and went deep and laid a foundation on the rock. When a flood arose, the stream broke against that house, and could not shake it, because it was founded on the rock."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"But he who hears and doesn\u2019t do, is like a man who built a house on the earth without a foundation, against which the stream broke, and immediately it fell; and the ruin of that house was great.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After he had finished speaking in the hearing of the people, he entered into Capernaum."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"A certain centurion\u2019s servant, who was dear to him, was sick and at the point of death."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When he heard about Jesus, he sent to him elders of the Jews, asking him to come and save his servant."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When they came to Jesus, they begged him earnestly, saying, \u201cHe is worthy for you to do this for him,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"for he loves our nation, and he built our synagogue for us.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Jesus went with them. When he was now not far from the house, the centurion sent friends to him, saying to him, \u201cLord, don\u2019t trouble yourself, for I am not worthy for you to come under my roof."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore I didn\u2019t even think myself worthy to come to you; but say the word, and my servant will be healed."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For I also am a man placed under authority, having under myself soldiers. I tell this one, \u2018Go!\u2019 and he goes; and to another, \u2018Come!\u2019 and he comes; and to my servant, \u2018Do this,\u2019 and he does it.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus heard these things, he marveled at him, and turned and said to the multitude who followed him, \u201cI tell you, I have not found such great faith, no, not in Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Those who were sent, returning to the house, found that the servant who had been sick was well."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Soon afterwards, he went to a city called Nain. Many of his disciples, along with a great multitude, went with him."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now when he came near to the gate of the city, behold, one who was dead was carried out, the only born son of his mother, and she was a widow. Many people of the city were with her."]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03b7\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d."]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When the Lord saw her, he had compassion on her and said to her, \u201cDon\u2019t cry.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He came near and touched the coffin, and the bearers stood still. He said, \u201cYoung man, I tell you, arise!\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He who was dead sat up and began to speak. Then he gave him to his mother."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Fear took hold of all, and they glorified God, saying, \u201cA great prophet has arisen among us!\u201d and, \u201cGod has visited his people!\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"This report went out concerning him in the whole of Judea and in all the surrounding region."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples of John told him about all these things."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"John, calling to himself two of his disciples, sent them to Jesus, saying, \u201cAre you the one who is coming, or should we look for another?\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When the men had come to him, they said, \u201cJohn the Baptizer has sent us to you, saying, \u2018Are you he who comes, or should we look for another?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"In that hour he cured many of diseases and plagues and evil spirits; and to many who were blind he gave sight."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cGo and tell John the things which you have seen and heard: that the blind receive their sight, the lame walk, the lepers are cleansed, the deaf hear, the dead are raised up, and the poor have good news preached to them."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Blessed is he who finds no occasion for stumbling in me.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"When John\u2019s messengers had departed, he began to tell the multitudes about John, \u201cWhat did you go out into the wilderness to see? A reed shaken by the wind?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But what did you go out to see? A man clothed in soft clothing? Behold, those who are gorgeously dressed and live delicately are in kings\u2019 courts."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But what did you go out to see? A prophet? Yes, I tell you, and much more than a prophet."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"This is he of whom it is written,"],[1,"\u2018Behold, I send my messenger before your face,"],[2,"who will prepare your way before you.\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor I tell you, among those who are born of women there is not a greater prophet than John the Baptizer; yet he who is least in God\u2019s Kingdom is greater than he.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When all the people and the tax collectors heard this, they declared God to be just, having been baptized with John\u2019s baptism."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But the Pharisees and the lawyers rejected the counsel of God, not being baptized by him themselves."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo what then should I compare the people of this generation? What are they like?"]],f:["TR adds \u201cBut the Lord said,\u201d"]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They are like children who sit in the marketplace and call to one another, saying, \u2018We piped to you, and you didn\u2019t dance. We mourned, and you didn\u2019t weep.\u2019"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"For John the Baptizer came neither eating bread nor drinking wine, and you say, \u2018He has a demon.\u2019"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The Son of Man has come eating and drinking, and you say, \u2018Behold, a glutton and a drunkard, a friend of tax collectors and sinners!\u2019"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Wisdom is justified by all her children.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the Pharisees invited him to eat with him. He entered into the Pharisee\u2019s house and sat at the table."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Behold, a woman in the city who was a sinner, when she knew that he was reclining in the Pharisee\u2019s house, brought an alabaster jar of ointment."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Standing behind at his feet weeping, she began to wet his feet with her tears, and she wiped them with the hair of her head, kissed his feet, and anointed them with the ointment."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Now when the Pharisee who had invited him saw it, he said to himself, \u201cThis man, if he were a prophet, would have perceived who and what kind of woman this is who touches him, that she is a sinner.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cSimon, I have something to tell you.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cTeacher, say on.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cA certain lender had two debtors. The one owed five hundred denarii, and the other fifty."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"When they couldn\u2019t pay, he forgave them both. Which of them therefore will love him most?\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon answered, \u201cHe, I suppose, to whom he forgave the most.\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cYou have judged correctly.\u201d"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Turning to the woman, he said to Simon, \u201cDo you see this woman? I entered into your house, and you gave me no water for my feet, but she has wet my feet with her tears, and wiped them with the hair of her head."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"You gave me no kiss, but she, since the time I came in, has not ceased to kiss my feet."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"You didn\u2019t anoint my head with oil, but she has anointed my feet with ointment."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Therefore I tell you, her sins, which are many, are forgiven, for she loved much. But one to whom little is forgiven, loves little.\u201d"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cYour sins are forgiven.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who sat at the table with him began to say to themselves, \u201cWho is this who even forgives sins?\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to the woman, \u201cYour faith has saved you. Go in peace.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Soon afterwards, he went about through cities and villages, preaching and bringing the good news of God\u2019s Kingdom. With him were the twelve,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and certain women who had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities: Mary who was called Magdalene, from whom seven demons had gone out;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and Joanna, the wife of Chuzas, Herod\u2019s steward; Susanna; and many others who served them from their possessions."]],f:["TR reads \u201chim\u201d instead of \u201cthem\u201d"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When a great multitude came together and people from every city were coming to him, he spoke by a parable:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cThe farmer went out to sow his seed. As he sowed, some fell along the road, and it was trampled under foot, and the birds of the sky devoured it."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Some seed fell on the rock, and as soon as it grew, it withered away, because it had no moisture."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Some fell amid the thorns, and the thorns grew with it and choked it."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Some fell into the good ground and grew and produced one hundred times as much fruit.\u201d As he said these things, he called out, \u201cHe who has ears to hear, let him hear!\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Then his disciples asked him, \u201cWhat does this parable mean?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cTo you it is given to know the mysteries of God\u2019s Kingdom, but to the rest it is given in parables, that \u2018seeing they may not see, and hearing they may not understand.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow the parable is this: The seed is the word of God."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Those along the road are those who hear; then the devil comes and takes away the word from their heart, that they may not believe and be saved."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Those on the rock are they who, when they hear, receive the word with joy; but these have no root. They believe for a while, then fall away in time of temptation."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"What fell among the thorns, these are those who have heard, and as they go on their way they are choked with cares, riches, and pleasures of life; and they bring no fruit to maturity."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Those in the good ground, these are those who with an honest and good heart, having heard the word, hold it tightly, and produce fruit with perseverance."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNo one, when he has lit a lamp, covers it with a container or puts it under a bed; but puts it on a stand, that those who enter in may see the light."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For nothing is hidden that will not be revealed, nor anything secret that will not be known and come to light."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Be careful therefore how you hear. For whoever has, to him will be given; and whoever doesn\u2019t have, from him will be taken away even that which he thinks he has.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"His mother and brothers came to him, and they could not come near him for the crowd."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Some people told him, \u201cYour mother and your brothers stand outside, desiring to see you.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"But he answered them, \u201cMy mother and my brothers are these who hear the word of God and do it.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on one of those days, he entered into a boat, himself and his disciples, and he said to them, \u201cLet\u2019s go over to the other side of the lake.\u201d So they launched out."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But as they sailed, he fell asleep. A wind storm came down on the lake, and they were taking on dangerous amounts of water."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They came to him and awoke him, saying, \u201cMaster, Master, we are dying!\u201d He awoke and rebuked the wind and the raging of the water; then they ceased, and it was calm."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhere is your faith?\u201d Being afraid, they marveled, saying to one another, \u201cWho is this then, that he commands even the winds and the water, and they obey him?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they arrived at the country of the Gadarenes, which is opposite Galilee."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When Jesus stepped ashore, a certain man out of the city who had demons for a long time met him. He wore no clothes, and didn\u2019t live in a house, but in the tombs."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"When he saw Jesus, he cried out and fell down before him, and with a loud voice said, \u201cWhat do I have to do with you, Jesus, you Son of the Most High God? I beg you, don\u2019t torment me!\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For Jesus was commanding the unclean spirit to come out of the man. For the unclean spirit had often seized the man. He was kept under guard and bound with chains and fetters. Breaking the bonds apart, he was driven by the demon into the desert."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus asked him, \u201cWhat is your name?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cLegion,\u201d for many demons had entered into him."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"They begged him that he would not command them to go into the abyss."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was there a herd of many pigs feeding on the mountain, and they begged him that he would allow them to enter into those. Then he allowed them."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The demons came out of the man and entered into the pigs, and the herd rushed down the steep bank into the lake and were drowned."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"When those who fed them saw what had happened, they fled and told it in the city and in the country."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"People went out to see what had happened. They came to Jesus and found the man from whom the demons had gone out, sitting at Jesus\u2019 feet, clothed and in his right mind; and they were afraid."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Those who saw it told them how he who had been possessed by demons was healed."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"All the people of the surrounding country of the Gadarenes asked him to depart from them, for they were very much afraid. Then he entered into the boat and returned."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But the man from whom the demons had gone out begged him that he might go with him, but Jesus sent him away, saying,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"\u201cReturn to your house, and declare what great things God has done for you.\u201d He went his way, proclaiming throughout the whole city what great things Jesus had done for him."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus returned, the multitude welcomed him, for they were all waiting for him."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Behold, a man named Jairus came. He was a ruler of the synagogue. He fell down at Jesus\u2019 feet and begged him to come into his house,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"for he had an only born daughter, about twelve years of age, and she was dying. But as he went, the multitudes pressed against him."]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03b7\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d."]},{v:43,l:[[0,"A woman who had a flow of blood for twelve years, who had spent all her living on physicians and could not be healed by any,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"came behind him and touched the fringe of his cloak. Immediately the flow of her blood stopped."]],f:["or, tassel"]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said, \u201cWho touched me?\u201d"],[0,"When all denied it, Peter and those with him said, \u201cMaster, the multitudes press and jostle you, and you say, \u2018Who touched me?\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said, \u201cSomeone did touch me, for I perceived that power has gone out of me.\u201d"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"When the woman saw that she was not hidden, she came trembling; and falling down before him declared to him in the presence of all the people the reason why she had touched him, and how she was healed immediately."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He said to her, \u201cDaughter, cheer up. Your faith has made you well. Go in peace.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"While he still spoke, one from the ruler of the synagogue\u2019s house came, saying to him, \u201cYour daughter is dead. Don\u2019t trouble the Teacher.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus hearing it, answered him, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid. Only believe, and she will be healed.\u201d"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came to the house, he didn\u2019t allow anyone to enter in, except Peter, John, James, the father of the child, and her mother."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"All were weeping and mourning her, but he said, \u201cDon\u2019t weep. She isn\u2019t dead, but sleeping.\u201d"]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"They were ridiculing him, knowing that she was dead."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"But he put them all outside, and taking her by the hand, he called, saying, \u201cChild, arise!\u201d"]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"Her spirit returned, and she rose up immediately. He commanded that something be given to her to eat."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Her parents were amazed, but he commanded them to tell no one what had been done."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He called the twelve together and gave them power and authority over all demons, and to cure diseases."]],f:["TR reads \u201chis twelve disciples\u201d instead of \u201cthe twelve\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He sent them out to preach God\u2019s Kingdom and to heal the sick."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cTake nothing for your journey\u2014no staffs, nor wallet, nor bread, nor money. Don\u2019t have two tunics each."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Into whatever house you enter, stay there, and depart from there."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"As many as don\u2019t receive you, when you depart from that city, shake off even the dust from your feet for a testimony against them.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"They departed and went throughout the villages, preaching the Good News and healing everywhere."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Herod the tetrarch heard of all that was done by him; and he was very perplexed, because it was said by some that John had risen from the dead,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and by some that Elijah had appeared, and by others that one of the old prophets had risen again."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Herod said, \u201cI beheaded John, but who is this about whom I hear such things?\u201d He sought to see him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The apostles, when they had returned, told him what things they had done."],[0,"He took them and withdrew apart to a desert region of a city called Bethsaida."]],f:["NU omits \u201ca desert region of\u201d."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But the multitudes, perceiving it, followed him. He welcomed them, spoke to them of God\u2019s Kingdom, and he cured those who needed healing."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The day began to wear away; and the twelve came and said to him, \u201cSend the multitude away, that they may go into the surrounding villages and farms and lodge and get food, for we are here in a deserted place.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said to them, \u201cYou give them something to eat.\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cWe have no more than five loaves and two fish, unless we should go and buy food for all these people.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For they were about five thousand men."],[0,"He said to his disciples, \u201cMake them sit down in groups of about fifty each.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They did so, and made them all sit down."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He took the five loaves and the two fish, and looking up to the sky, he blessed them, broke them, and gave them to the disciples to set before the multitude."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They ate and were all filled. They gathered up twelve baskets of broken pieces that were left over."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"As he was praying alone, the disciples were near him, and he asked them, \u201cWho do the multitudes say that I am?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered, \u201c\u2018John the Baptizer,\u2019 but others say, \u2018Elijah,\u2019 and others, that one of the old prophets has risen again.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cBut who do you say that I am?\u201d"],[0,"Peter answered, \u201cThe Christ of God.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"But he warned them and commanded them to tell this to no one,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cThe Son of Man must suffer many things, and be rejected by the elders, chief priests, and scribes, and be killed, and the third day be raised up.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to all, \u201cIf anyone desires to come after me, let him deny himself, take up his cross, and follow me."]],f:["TR, NU add \u201cdaily\u201d"]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For whoever desires to save his life will lose it, but whoever will lose his life for my sake will save it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For what does it profit a man if he gains the whole world, and loses or forfeits his own self?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For whoever will be ashamed of me and of my words, of him will the Son of Man be ashamed when he comes in his glory, and the glory of the Father, and of the holy angels."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But I tell you the truth: There are some of those who stand here who will in no way taste of death until they see God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"About eight days after these sayings, he took with him Peter, John, and James, and went up onto the mountain to pray."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"As he was praying, the appearance of his face was altered, and his clothing became white and dazzling."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Behold, two men were talking with him, who were Moses and Elijah,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"who appeared in glory and spoke of his departure, which he was about to accomplish at Jerusalem."]],f:["literally, \u201cexodus\u201d"]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Peter and those who were with him were heavy with sleep, but when they were fully awake, they saw his glory, and the two men who stood with him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"As they were parting from him, Peter said to Jesus, \u201cMaster, it is good for us to be here. Let\u2019s make three tents: one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah,\u201d not knowing what he said."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"While he said these things, a cloud came and overshadowed them, and they were afraid as they entered into the cloud."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"A voice came out of the cloud, saying, \u201cThis is my beloved Son. Listen to him!\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"When the voice came, Jesus was found alone. They were silent, and told no one in those days any of the things which they had seen."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, when they had come down from the mountain, a great multitude met him."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Behold, a man from the crowd called out, saying, \u201cTeacher, I beg you to look at my son, for he is my only born child."]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03b7\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d."]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Behold, a spirit takes him, he suddenly cries out, and it convulses him so that he foams; and it hardly departs from him, bruising him severely."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"I begged your disciples to cast it out, and they couldn\u2019t.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cFaithless and perverse generation, how long shall I be with you and bear with you? Bring your son here.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still coming, the demon threw him down and convulsed him violently. But Jesus rebuked the unclean spirit, healed the boy, and gave him back to his father."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"They were all astonished at the majesty of God."],[0,"But while all were marveling at all the things which Jesus did, he said to his disciples,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"\u201cLet these words sink into your ears, for the Son of Man will be delivered up into the hands of men.\u201d"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"But they didn\u2019t understand this saying. It was concealed from them, that they should not perceive it, and they were afraid to ask him about this saying."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"An argument arose among them about which of them was the greatest."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Jesus, perceiving the reasoning of their hearts, took a little child, and set him by his side,"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cWhoever receives this little child in my name receives me. Whoever receives me receives him who sent me. For whoever is least among you all, this one will be great.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"John answered, \u201cMaster, we saw someone casting out demons in your name, and we forbade him, because he doesn\u2019t follow with us.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cDon\u2019t forbid him, for he who is not against us is for us.\u201d"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass, when the days were near that he should be taken up, he intently set his face to go to Jerusalem"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"and sent messengers before his face. They went and entered into a village of the Samaritans, so as to prepare for him."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t receive him, because he was traveling with his face set toward Jerusalem."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"When his disciples, James and John, saw this, they said, \u201cLord, do you want us to command fire to come down from the sky and destroy them, just as Elijah did?\u201d"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"But he turned and rebuked them, \u201cYou don\u2019t know of what kind of spirit you are."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"For the Son of Man didn\u2019t come to destroy men\u2019s lives, but to save them.\u201d"],[0,"They went to another village."]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"As they went on the way, a certain man said to him, \u201cI want to follow you wherever you go, Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cThe foxes have holes and the birds of the sky have nests, but the Son of Man has no place to lay his head.\u201d"]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to another, \u201cFollow me!\u201d"],[0,"But he said, \u201cLord, allow me first to go and bury my father.\u201d"]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to him, \u201cLeave the dead to bury their own dead, but you go and announce God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"Another also said, \u201cI want to follow you, Lord, but first allow me to say good-bye to those who are at my house.\u201d"]]},{v:62,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to him, \u201cNo one, having put his hand to the plow and looking back, is fit for God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after these things, the Lord also appointed seventy others, and sent them two by two ahead of him into every city and place where he was about to come."]],f:["literally, \u201cbefore his face\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then he said to them, \u201cThe harvest is indeed plentiful, but the laborers are few. Pray therefore to the Lord of the harvest, that he may send out laborers into his harvest."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Go your ways. Behold, I send you out as lambs among wolves."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Carry no purse, nor wallet, nor sandals. Greet no one on the way."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Into whatever house you enter, first say, \u2018Peace be to this house.\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"If a son of peace is there, your peace will rest on him; but if not, it will return to you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Remain in that same house, eating and drinking the things they give, for the laborer is worthy of his wages. Don\u2019t go from house to house."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Into whatever city you enter and they receive you, eat the things that are set before you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Heal the sick who are there and tell them, \u2018God\u2019s Kingdom has come near to you.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But into whatever city you enter and they don\u2019t receive you, go out into its streets and say,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u2018Even the dust from your city that clings to us, we wipe off against you. Nevertheless know this, that God\u2019s Kingdom has come near to you.\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I tell you, it will be more tolerable in that day for Sodom than for that city."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWoe to you, Chorazin! Woe to you, Bethsaida! For if the mighty works had been done in Tyre and Sidon which were done in you, they would have repented long ago, sitting in sackcloth and ashes."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But it will be more tolerable for Tyre and Sidon in the judgment than for you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You, Capernaum, who are exalted to heaven, will be brought down to Hades."]],f:["Hades is the lower realm of the dead, or Hell."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Whoever listens to you listens to me, and whoever rejects you rejects me. Whoever rejects me rejects him who sent me.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The seventy returned with joy, saying, \u201cLord, even the demons are subject to us in your name!\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cI saw Satan having fallen like lightning from heaven."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Behold, I give you authority to tread on serpents and scorpions, and over all the power of the enemy. Nothing will in any way hurt you."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, don\u2019t rejoice in this, that the spirits are subject to you, but rejoice that your names are written in heaven.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"In that same hour, Jesus rejoiced in the Holy Spirit, and said, \u201cI thank you, O Father, Lord of heaven and earth, that you have hidden these things from the wise and understanding, and revealed them to little children. Yes, Father, for so it was well-pleasing in your sight.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Turning to the disciples, he said, \u201cAll things have been delivered to me by my Father. No one knows who the Son is, except the Father, and who the Father is, except the Son, and he to whomever the Son desires to reveal him.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Turning to the disciples, he said privately, \u201cBlessed are the eyes which see the things that you see,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"for I tell you that many prophets and kings desired to see the things which you see, and didn\u2019t see them, and to hear the things which you hear, and didn\u2019t hear them.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, a certain lawyer stood up and tested him, saying, \u201cTeacher, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cWhat is written in the law? How do you read it?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cYou shall love the Lord your God with all your heart, with all your soul, with all your strength, and with all your mind; and your neighbor as yourself.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cYou have answered correctly. Do this, and you will live.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"But he, desiring to justify himself, asked Jesus, \u201cWho is my neighbor?\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cA certain man was going down from Jerusalem to Jericho, and he fell among robbers, who both stripped him and beat him, and departed, leaving him half dead."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"By chance a certain priest was going down that way. When he saw him, he passed by on the other side."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"In the same way a Levite also, when he came to the place and saw him, passed by on the other side."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But a certain Samaritan, as he traveled, came where he was. When he saw him, he was moved with compassion,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"came to him, and bound up his wounds, pouring on oil and wine. He set him on his own animal, brought him to an inn, and took care of him."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"On the next day, when he departed, he took out two denarii, gave them to the host, and said to him, \u2018Take care of him. Whatever you spend beyond that, I will repay you when I return.\u2019"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Now which of these three do you think seemed to be a neighbor to him who fell among the robbers?\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cHe who showed mercy on him.\u201d"],[0,"Then Jesus said to him, \u201cGo and do likewise.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"As they went on their way, he entered into a certain village, and a certain woman named Martha received him into her house."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"She had a sister called Mary, who also sat at Jesus\u2019 feet and heard his word."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"But Martha was distracted with much serving, and she came up to him, and said, \u201cLord, don\u2019t you care that my sister left me to serve alone? Ask her therefore to help me.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered her, \u201cMartha, Martha, you are anxious and troubled about many things,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"but one thing is needed. Mary has chosen the good part, which will not be taken away from her.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When he finished praying in a certain place, one of his disciples said to him, \u201cLord, teach us to pray, just as John also taught his disciples.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhen you pray, say,"],[1,"\u2018Our Father in heaven,"],[2,"may your name be kept holy."],[1,"May your Kingdom come."],[2,"May your will be done on earth, as it is in heaven."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[1,"Give us day by day our daily bread."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Forgive us our sins,"],[2,"for we ourselves also forgive everyone who is indebted to us."],[1,"Bring us not into temptation,"],[2,"but deliver us from the evil one.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhich of you, if you go to a friend at midnight and tell him, \u2018Friend, lend me three loaves of bread,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"for a friend of mine has come to me from a journey, and I have nothing to set before him,\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and he from within will answer and say, \u2018Don\u2019t bother me. The door is now shut, and my children are with me in bed. I can\u2019t get up and give it to you\u2019?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I tell you, although he will not rise and give it to him because he is his friend, yet because of his persistence, he will get up and give him as many as he needs."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI tell you, keep asking, and it will be given you. Keep seeking, and you will find. Keep knocking, and it will be opened to you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For everyone who asks receives. He who seeks finds. To him who knocks it will be opened."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhich of you fathers, if your son asks for bread, will give him a stone? Or if he asks for a fish, he won\u2019t give him a snake instead of a fish, will he?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Or if he asks for an egg, he won\u2019t give him a scorpion, will he?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"If you then, being evil, know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your heavenly Father give the Holy Spirit to those who ask him?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"He was casting out a demon, and it was mute. When the demon had gone out, the mute man spoke; and the multitudes marveled."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But some of them said, \u201cHe casts out demons by Beelzebul, the prince of the demons.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Others, testing him, sought from him a sign from heaven."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But he, knowing their thoughts, said to them, \u201cEvery kingdom divided against itself is brought to desolation. A house divided against itself falls."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"If Satan also is divided against himself, how will his kingdom stand? For you say that I cast out demons by Beelzebul."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But if I cast out demons by Beelzebul, by whom do your children cast them out? Therefore they will be your judges."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But if I by God\u2019s finger cast out demons, then God\u2019s Kingdom has come to you."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the strong man, fully armed, guards his own dwelling, his goods are safe."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But when someone stronger attacks him and overcomes him, he takes from him his whole armor in which he trusted, and divides his plunder."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who is not with me is against me. He who doesn\u2019t gather with me scatters."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The unclean spirit, when he has gone out of the man, passes through dry places, seeking rest; and finding none, he says, \u2018I will turn back to my house from which I came out.\u2019"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When he returns, he finds it swept and put in order."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Then he goes and takes seven other spirits more evil than himself, and they enter in and dwell there. The last state of that man becomes worse than the first.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"It came to pass, as he said these things, a certain woman out of the multitude lifted up her voice and said to him, \u201cBlessed is the womb that bore you, and the breasts which nursed you!\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said, \u201cOn the contrary, blessed are those who hear the word of God, and keep it.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When the multitudes were gathering together to him, he began to say, \u201cThis is an evil generation. It seeks after a sign. No sign will be given to it but the sign of Jonah the prophet."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For even as Jonah became a sign to the Ninevites, so the Son of Man will also be to this generation."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The Queen of the South will rise up in the judgment with the men of this generation and will condemn them, for she came from the ends of the earth to hear the wisdom of Solomon; and behold, one greater than Solomon is here."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The men of Nineveh will stand up in the judgment with this generation, and will condemn it, for they repented at the preaching of Jonah; and behold, one greater than Jonah is here."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNo one, when he has lit a lamp, puts it in a cellar or under a basket, but on a stand, that those who come in may see the light."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"The lamp of the body is the eye. Therefore when your eye is good, your whole body is also full of light; but when it is evil, your body also is full of darkness."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Therefore see whether the light that is in you isn\u2019t darkness."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"If therefore your whole body is full of light, having no part dark, it will be wholly full of light, as when the lamp with its bright shining gives you light.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Now as he spoke, a certain Pharisee asked him to dine with him. He went in and sat at the table."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"When the Pharisee saw it, he marveled that he had not first washed himself before dinner."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"The Lord said to him, \u201cNow you Pharisees cleanse the outside of the cup and of the platter, but your inward part is full of extortion and wickedness."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"You foolish ones, didn\u2019t he who made the outside make the inside also?"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"But give for gifts to the needy those things which are within, and behold, all things will be clean to you."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"But woe to you Pharisees! For you tithe mint and rue and every herb, but you bypass justice and God\u2019s love. You ought to have done these, and not to have left the other undone."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Woe to you Pharisees! For you love the best seats in the synagogues and the greetings in the marketplaces."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you are like hidden graves, and the men who walk over them don\u2019t know it.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the lawyers answered him, \u201cTeacher, in saying this you insult us also.\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWoe to you lawyers also! For you load men with burdens that are difficult to carry, and you yourselves won\u2019t even lift one finger to help carry those burdens."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Woe to you! For you build the tombs of the prophets, and your fathers killed them."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"So you testify and consent to the works of your fathers. For they killed them, and you build their tombs."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Therefore also the wisdom of God said, \u2018I will send to them prophets and apostles; and some of them they will kill and persecute,"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"that the blood of all the prophets, which was shed from the foundation of the world, may be required of this generation,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"from the blood of Abel to the blood of Zachariah, who perished between the altar and the sanctuary.\u2019 Yes, I tell you, it will be required of this generation."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"Woe to you lawyers! For you took away the key of knowledge. You didn\u2019t enter in yourselves, and those who were entering in, you hindered.\u201d"]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"As he said these things to them, the scribes and the Pharisees began to be terribly angry, and to draw many things out of him,"]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"lying in wait for him, and seeking to catch him in something he might say, that they might accuse him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Meanwhile, when a multitude of many thousands had gathered together, so much so that they trampled on each other, he began to tell his disciples first of all, \u201cBeware of the yeast of the Pharisees, which is hypocrisy."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But there is nothing covered up that will not be revealed, nor hidden that will not be known."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore whatever you have said in the darkness will be heard in the light. What you have spoken in the ear in the inner rooms will be proclaimed on the housetops."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI tell you, my friends, don\u2019t be afraid of those who kill the body, and after that have no more that they can do."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But I will warn you whom you should fear. Fear him who after he has killed, has power to cast into Gehenna. Yes, I tell you, fear him."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAren\u2019t five sparrows sold for two assaria coins? Not one of them is forgotten by God."]],f:["An assarion was a small copper coin worth about an hour\u2019s wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But the very hairs of your head are all counted. Therefore don\u2019t be afraid. You are of more value than many sparrows."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI tell you, everyone who confesses me before men, the Son of Man will also confess before the angels of God;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but he who denies me in the presence of men will be denied in the presence of God\u2019s angels."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Everyone who speaks a word against the Son of Man will be forgiven, but those who blaspheme against the Holy Spirit will not be forgiven."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When they bring you before the synagogues, the rulers, and the authorities, don\u2019t be anxious how or what you will answer or what you will say;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"for the Holy Spirit will teach you in that same hour what you must say.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the multitude said to him, \u201cTeacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said to him, \u201cMan, who made me a judge or an arbitrator over you?\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cBeware! Keep yourselves from covetousness, for a man\u2019s life doesn\u2019t consist of the abundance of the things which he possesses.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"He spoke a parable to them, saying, \u201cThe ground of a certain rich man produced abundantly."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He reasoned within himself, saying, \u2018What will I do, because I don\u2019t have room to store my crops?\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He said, \u2018This is what I will do. I will pull down my barns, build bigger ones, and there I will store all my grain and my goods."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I will tell my soul, \u201cSoul, you have many goods laid up for many years. Take your ease, eat, drink, and be merry.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut God said to him, \u2018You foolish one, tonight your soul is required of you. The things which you have prepared\u2014whose will they be?\u2019"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So is he who lays up treasure for himself, and is not rich toward God.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to his disciples, \u201cTherefore I tell you, don\u2019t be anxious for your life, what you will eat, nor yet for your body, what you will wear."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Life is more than food, and the body is more than clothing."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Consider the ravens: they don\u2019t sow, they don\u2019t reap, they have no warehouse or barn, and God feeds them. How much more valuable are you than birds!"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Which of you by being anxious can add a cubit to his height?"]],f:["A cubit is the length from the tip of the middle finger to the elbow on a man\u2019s arm, or about 18 inches or 46 centimeters."]},{v:26,l:[[0,"If then you aren\u2019t able to do even the least things, why are you anxious about the rest?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Consider the lilies, how they grow. They don\u2019t toil, neither do they spin; yet I tell you, even Solomon in all his glory was not arrayed like one of these."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But if this is how God clothes the grass in the field, which today exists and tomorrow is cast into the oven, how much more will he clothe you, O you of little faith?"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t seek what you will eat or what you will drink; neither be anxious."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For the nations of the world seek after all of these things, but your Father knows that you need these things."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But seek God\u2019s Kingdom, and all these things will be added to you."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, little flock, for it is your Father\u2019s good pleasure to give you the Kingdom."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Sell what you have and give gifts to the needy. Make for yourselves purses which don\u2019t grow old, a treasure in the heavens that doesn\u2019t fail, where no thief approaches and no moth destroys."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For where your treasure is, there will your heart be also."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cLet your waist be dressed and your lamps burning."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Be like men watching for their lord when he returns from the wedding feast, that when he comes and knocks, they may immediately open to him."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Blessed are those servants whom the lord will find watching when he comes. Most certainly I tell you that he will dress himself, make them recline, and will come and serve them."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"They will be blessed if he comes in the second or third watch and finds them so."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But know this, that if the master of the house had known in what hour the thief was coming, he would have watched and not allowed his house to be broken into."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Therefore be ready also, for the Son of Man is coming in an hour that you don\u2019t expect him.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter said to him, \u201cLord, are you telling this parable to us, or to everybody?\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord said, \u201cWho then is the faithful and wise steward, whom his lord will set over his household, to give them their portion of food at the right times?"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Blessed is that servant whom his lord will find doing so when he comes."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Truly I tell you that he will set him over all that he has."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"But if that servant says in his heart, \u2018My lord delays his coming,\u2019 and begins to beat the menservants and the maidservants, and to eat and drink and to be drunken,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"then the lord of that servant will come in a day when he isn\u2019t expecting him and in an hour that he doesn\u2019t know, and will cut him in two, and place his portion with the unfaithful."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"That servant who knew his lord\u2019s will, and didn\u2019t prepare nor do what he wanted, will be beaten with many stripes,"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"but he who didn\u2019t know, and did things worthy of stripes, will be beaten with few stripes. To whomever much is given, of him will much be required; and to whom much was entrusted, of him more will be asked."]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI came to throw fire on the earth. I wish it were already kindled."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"But I have a baptism to be baptized with, and how distressed I am until it is accomplished!"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Do you think that I have come to give peace on the earth? I tell you, no, but rather division."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"For from now on, there will be five in one house divided, three against two, and two against three."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"They will be divided, father against son, and son against father; mother against daughter, and daughter against her mother; mother-in-law against her daughter-in-law, and daughter-in-law against her mother-in-law.\u201d"]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to the multitudes also, \u201cWhen you see a cloud rising from the west, immediately you say, \u2018A shower is coming,\u2019 and so it happens."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"When a south wind blows, you say, \u2018There will be a scorching heat,\u2019 and it happens."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"You hypocrites! You know how to interpret the appearance of the earth and the sky, but how is it that you don\u2019t interpret this time?"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhy don\u2019t you judge for yourselves what is right?"]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"For when you are going with your adversary before the magistrate, try diligently on the way to be released from him, lest perhaps he drag you to the judge, and the judge deliver you to the officer, and the officer throw you into prison."]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"I tell you, you will by no means get out of there until you have paid the very last penny.\u201d"]],f:["literally, lepton. A lepton is a very small brass Jewish coin worth half a Roman quadrans each, which is worth a quarter of the copper assarion. Lepta are worth less than 1% of an agricultural worker\u2019s daily wages."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there were some present at the same time who told him about the Galileans whose blood Pilate had mixed with their sacrifices."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cDo you think that these Galileans were worse sinners than all the other Galileans, because they suffered such things?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I tell you, no, but unless you repent, you will all perish in the same way."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Or those eighteen on whom the tower in Siloam fell and killed them\u2014do you think that they were worse offenders than all the men who dwell in Jerusalem?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I tell you, no, but, unless you repent, you will all perish in the same way.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He spoke this parable. \u201cA certain man had a fig tree planted in his vineyard, and he came seeking fruit on it and found none."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He said to the vine dresser, \u2018Behold, these three years I have come looking for fruit on this fig tree, and found none. Cut it down! Why does it waste the soil?\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He answered, \u2018Lord, leave it alone this year also, until I dig around it and fertilize it."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If it bears fruit, fine; but if not, after that, you can cut it down.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He was teaching in one of the synagogues on the Sabbath day."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Behold, there was a woman who had a spirit of infirmity eighteen years. She was bent over and could in no way straighten herself up."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When Jesus saw her, he called her and said to her, \u201cWoman, you are freed from your infirmity.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He laid his hands on her, and immediately she stood up straight and glorified God."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The ruler of the synagogue, being indignant because Jesus had healed on the Sabbath, said to the multitude, \u201cThere are six days in which men ought to work. Therefore come on those days and be healed, and not on the Sabbath day!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Lord answered him, \u201cYou hypocrites! Doesn\u2019t each one of you free his ox or his donkey from the stall on the Sabbath and lead him away to water?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Ought not this woman, being a daughter of Abraham whom Satan had bound eighteen long years, be freed from this bondage on the Sabbath day?\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"As he said these things, all his adversaries were disappointed; and all the multitude rejoiced for all the glorious things that were done by him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWhat is God\u2019s Kingdom like? To what shall I compare it?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"It is like a grain of mustard seed which a man took and put in his own garden. It grew and became a large tree, and the birds of the sky live in its branches.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he said, \u201cTo what shall I compare God\u2019s Kingdom?"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"It is like yeast, which a woman took and hid in three measures of flour, until it was all leavened.\u201d"]],f:["literally, three sata. 3 sata is about 39 liters or a bit more than a bushel."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He went on his way through cities and villages, teaching, and traveling on to Jerusalem."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"One said to him, \u201cLord, are they few who are saved?\u201d"],[0,"He said to them,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"\u201cStrive to enter in by the narrow door, for many, I tell you, will seek to enter in and will not be able."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When once the master of the house has risen up and has shut the door, and you begin to stand outside and to knock at the door, saying, \u2018Lord, Lord, open to us!\u2019 then he will answer and tell you, \u2018I don\u2019t know you or where you come from.\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Then you will begin to say, \u2018We ate and drank in your presence, and you taught in our streets.\u2019"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He will say, \u2018I tell you, I don\u2019t know where you come from. Depart from me, all you workers of iniquity.\u2019"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"There will be weeping and gnashing of teeth when you see Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and all the prophets in God\u2019s Kingdom, and yourselves being thrown outside."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"They will come from the east, west, north, and south, and will sit down in God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Behold, there are some who are last who will be first, and there are some who are first who will be last.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"On that same day, some Pharisees came, saying to him, \u201cGet out of here and go away, for Herod wants to kill you.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cGo and tell that fox, \u2018Behold, I cast out demons and perform cures today and tomorrow, and the third day I complete my mission."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Nevertheless I must go on my way today and tomorrow and the next day, for it can\u2019t be that a prophet would perish outside of Jerusalem.\u2019"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cJerusalem, Jerusalem, you who kills the prophets and stones those who are sent to her! How often I wanted to gather your children together, like a hen gathers her own brood under her wings, and you refused!"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Behold, your house is left to you desolate. I tell you, you will not see me until you say, \u2018Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord!\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When he went into the house of one of the rulers of the Pharisees on a Sabbath to eat bread, they were watching him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Behold, a certain man who had dropsy was in front of him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jesus, answering, spoke to the lawyers and Pharisees, saying, \u201cIs it lawful to heal on the Sabbath?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But they were silent."],[0,"He took him, and healed him, and let him go."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cWhich of you, if your son or an ox fell into a well, wouldn\u2019t immediately pull him out on a Sabbath day?\u201d"]],f:["TR reads \u201cdonkey\u201d instead of \u201cson\u201d"]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"They couldn\u2019t answer him regarding these things."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He spoke a parable to those who were invited, when he noticed how they chose the best seats, and said to them,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen you are invited by anyone to a wedding feast, don\u2019t sit in the best seat, since perhaps someone more honorable than you might be invited by him,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and he who invited both of you would come and tell you, \u2018Make room for this person.\u2019 Then you would begin, with shame, to take the lowest place."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But when you are invited, go and sit in the lowest place, so that when he who invited you comes, he may tell you, \u2018Friend, move up higher.\u2019 Then you will be honored in the presence of all who sit at the table with you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, and whoever humbles himself will be exalted.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"He also said to the one who had invited him, \u201cWhen you make a dinner or a supper, don\u2019t call your friends, nor your brothers, nor your kinsmen, nor rich neighbors, or perhaps they might also return the favor, and pay you back."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But when you make a feast, ask the poor, the maimed, the lame, or the blind;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and you will be blessed, because they don\u2019t have the resources to repay you. For you will be repaid in the resurrection of the righteous.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"When one of those who sat at the table with him heard these things, he said to him, \u201cBlessed is he who will feast in God\u2019s Kingdom!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said to him, \u201cA certain man made a great supper, and he invited many people."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He sent out his servant at supper time to tell those who were invited, \u2018Come, for everything is ready now.\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They all as one began to make excuses."],[0,"\u201cThe first said to him, \u2018I have bought a field, and I must go and see it. Please have me excused.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAnother said, \u2018I have bought five yoke of oxen, and I must go try them out. Please have me excused.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAnother said, \u2018I have married a wife, and therefore I can\u2019t come.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThat servant came, and told his lord these things. Then the master of the house, being angry, said to his servant, \u2018Go out quickly into the streets and lanes of the city, and bring in the poor, maimed, blind, and lame.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe servant said, \u2018Lord, it is done as you commanded, and there is still room.\u2019"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe lord said to the servant, \u2018Go out into the highways and hedges, and compel them to come in, that my house may be filled."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For I tell you that none of those men who were invited will taste of my supper. For many are called, but few are chosen.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["RP MT includes the last sentence. TR, NU, and FH MT omit: For many are called, but few are chosen."]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Now great multitudes were going with him. He turned and said to them,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u201cIf anyone comes to me, and doesn\u2019t disregard his own father, mother, wife, children, brothers, and sisters, yes, and his own life also, he can\u2019t be my disciple."]],f:["or, hate"]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Whoever doesn\u2019t bear his own cross and come after me, can\u2019t be my disciple."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For which of you, desiring to build a tower, doesn\u2019t first sit down and count the cost, to see if he has enough to complete it?"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Or perhaps, when he has laid a foundation and isn\u2019t able to finish, everyone who sees begins to mock him,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"saying, \u2018This man began to build and wasn\u2019t able to finish.\u2019"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Or what king, as he goes to encounter another king in war, will not sit down first and consider whether he is able with ten thousand to meet him who comes against him with twenty thousand?"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Or else, while the other is yet a great way off, he sends an envoy and asks for conditions of peace."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"So therefore, whoever of you who doesn\u2019t renounce all that he has, he can\u2019t be my disciple."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSalt is good, but if the salt becomes flat and tasteless, with what do you season it?"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"It is fit neither for the soil nor for the manure pile. It is thrown out. He who has ears to hear, let him hear.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now all the tax collectors and sinners were coming close to him to hear him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The Pharisees and the scribes murmured, saying, \u201cThis man welcomes sinners, and eats with them.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He told them this parable:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"\u201cWhich of you men, if you had one hundred sheep and lost one of them, wouldn\u2019t leave the ninety-nine in the wilderness and go after the one that was lost, until he found it?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When he has found it, he carries it on his shoulders, rejoicing."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When he comes home, he calls together his friends and his neighbors, saying to them, \u2018Rejoice with me, for I have found my sheep which was lost!\u2019"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I tell you that even so there will be more joy in heaven over one sinner who repents, than over ninety-nine righteous people who need no repentance."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOr what woman, if she had ten drachma coins, if she lost one drachma coin, wouldn\u2019t light a lamp, sweep the house, and seek diligently until she found it?"]],f:["A drachma coin was worth about a days wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When she has found it, she calls together her friends and neighbors, saying, \u2018Rejoice with me, for I have found the drachma which I had lost!\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Even so, I tell you, there is joy in the presence of the angels of God over one sinner repenting.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cA certain man had two sons."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The younger of them said to his father, \u2018Father, give me my share of your property.\u2019 So he divided his livelihood between them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Not many days after, the younger son gathered all of this together and traveled into a far country. There he wasted his property with riotous living."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When he had spent all of it, there arose a severe famine in that country, and he began to be in need."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He went and joined himself to one of the citizens of that country, and he sent him into his fields to feed pigs."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He wanted to fill his belly with the pods that the pigs ate, but no one gave him any."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But when he came to himself, he said, \u2018How many hired servants of my father\u2019s have bread enough to spare, and I\u2019m dying with hunger!"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I will get up and go to my father, and will tell him, \u201cFather, I have sinned against heaven and in your sight."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I am no more worthy to be called your son. Make me as one of your hired servants.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe arose and came to his father. But while he was still far off, his father saw him and was moved with compassion, and ran, fell on his neck, and kissed him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The son said to him, \u2018Father, I have sinned against heaven and in your sight. I am no longer worthy to be called your son.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut the father said to his servants, \u2018Bring out the best robe and put it on him. Put a ring on his hand and sandals on his feet."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Bring the fattened calf, kill it, and let\u2019s eat and celebrate;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"for this, my son, was dead and is alive again. He was lost and is found.\u2019 Then they began to celebrate."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow his elder son was in the field. As he came near to the house, he heard music and dancing."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He called one of the servants to him and asked what was going on."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u2018Your brother has come, and your father has killed the fattened calf, because he has received him back safe and healthy.\u2019"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But he was angry and would not go in. Therefore his father came out and begged him."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But he answered his father, \u2018Behold, these many years I have served you, and I never disobeyed a commandment of yours, but you never gave me a goat, that I might celebrate with my friends."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But when this your son came, who has devoured your living with prostitutes, you killed the fattened calf for him.\u2019"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said to him, \u2018Son, you are always with me, and all that is mine is yours."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"But it was appropriate to celebrate and be glad, for this, your brother, was dead, and is alive again. He was lost, and is found.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He also said to his disciples, \u201cThere was a certain rich man who had a manager. An accusation was made to him that this man was wasting his possessions."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He called him, and said to him, \u2018What is this that I hear about you? Give an accounting of your management, for you can no longer be manager.\u2019"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe manager said within himself, \u2018What will I do, seeing that my lord is taking away the management position from me? I don\u2019t have strength to dig. I am ashamed to beg."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I know what I will do, so that when I am removed from management, they may receive me into their houses.\u2019"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Calling each one of his lord\u2019s debtors to him, he said to the first, \u2018How much do you owe to my lord?\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said, \u2018A hundred batos of oil.\u2019 He said to him, \u2018Take your bill, and sit down quickly and write fifty.\u2019"]],f:["100 batos is about 395 liters or 104 U. S. gallons."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then he said to another, \u2018How much do you owe?\u2019 He said, \u2018A hundred cors of wheat.\u2019 He said to him, \u2018Take your bill, and write eighty.\u2019"]],f:["100 cors = about 2,110 liters or 600 bushels."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHis lord commended the dishonest manager because he had done wisely, for the children of this world are, in their own generation, wiser than the children of the light."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I tell you, make for yourselves friends by means of unrighteous mammon, so that when you fail, they may receive you into the eternal tents."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He who is faithful in a very little is faithful also in much. He who is dishonest in a very little is also dishonest in much."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If therefore you have not been faithful in the unrighteous mammon, who will commit to your trust the true riches?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If you have not been faithful in that which is another\u2019s, who will give you that which is your own?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"No servant can serve two masters, for either he will hate the one and love the other; or else he will hold to one and despise the other. You aren\u2019t able to serve God and Mammon.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cMammon\u201d refers to riches or a false god of wealth."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The Pharisees, who were lovers of money, also heard all these things, and they scoffed at him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cYou are those who justify yourselves in the sight of men, but God knows your hearts. For that which is exalted among men is an abomination in the sight of God."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe law and the prophets were until John. From that time the Good News of God\u2019s Kingdom is preached, and everyone is forcing his way into it."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But it is easier for heaven and earth to pass away than for one tiny stroke of a pen in the law to fall."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cEveryone who divorces his wife and marries another commits adultery. He who marries one who is divorced from a husband commits adultery."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow there was a certain rich man, and he was clothed in purple and fine linen, living in luxury every day."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"A certain beggar, named Lazarus, was taken to his gate, full of sores,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and desiring to be fed with the crumbs that fell from the rich man\u2019s table. Yes, even the dogs came and licked his sores."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The beggar died, and he was carried away by the angels to Abraham\u2019s bosom. The rich man also died and was buried."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"In Hades, he lifted up his eyes, being in torment, and saw Abraham far off, and Lazarus at his bosom."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He cried and said, \u2018Father Abraham, have mercy on me, and send Lazarus, that he may dip the tip of his finger in water and cool my tongue! For I am in anguish in this flame.\u2019"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut Abraham said, \u2018Son, remember that you, in your lifetime, received your good things, and Lazarus, in the same way, bad things. But here he is now comforted and you are in anguish."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Besides all this, between us and you there is a great gulf fixed, that those who want to pass from here to you are not able, and that no one may cross over from there to us.\u2019"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said, \u2018I ask you therefore, father, that you would send him to my father\u2019s house\u2014"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"for I have five brothers\u2014that he may testify to them, so they won\u2019t also come into this place of torment.\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut Abraham said to him, \u2018They have Moses and the prophets. Let them listen to them.\u2019"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said, \u2018No, father Abraham, but if one goes to them from the dead, they will repent.\u2019"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said to him, \u2018If they don\u2019t listen to Moses and the prophets, neither will they be persuaded if one rises from the dead.\u2019\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to the disciples, \u201cIt is impossible that no occasions of stumbling should come, but woe to him through whom they come!"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It would be better for him if a millstone were hung around his neck, and he were thrown into the sea, rather than that he should cause one of these little ones to stumble."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Be careful. If your brother sins against you, rebuke him. If he repents, forgive him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If he sins against you seven times in the day, and seven times returns, saying, \u2018I repent,\u2019 you shall forgive him.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The apostles said to the Lord, \u201cIncrease our faith.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord said, \u201cIf you had faith like a grain of mustard seed, you would tell this sycamore tree, \u2018Be uprooted and be planted in the sea,\u2019 and it would obey you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But who is there among you, having a servant plowing or keeping sheep, that will say when he comes in from the field, \u2018Come immediately and sit down at the table\u2019?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Wouldn\u2019t he rather tell him, \u2018Prepare my supper, clothe yourself properly, and serve me while I eat and drink. Afterward you shall eat and drink\u2019?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Does he thank that servant because he did the things that were commanded? I think not."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Even so you also, when you have done all the things that are commanded you, say, \u2018We are unworthy servants. We have done our duty.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"As he was on his way to Jerusalem, he was passing along the borders of Samaria and Galilee."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"As he entered into a certain village, ten men who were lepers met him, who stood at a distance."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They lifted up their voices, saying, \u201cJesus, Master, have mercy on us!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When he saw them, he said to them, \u201cGo and show yourselves to the priests.\u201d As they went, they were cleansed."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"One of them, when he saw that he was healed, turned back, glorifying God with a loud voice."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He fell on his face at Jesus\u2019 feet, giving him thanks; and he was a Samaritan."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cWeren\u2019t the ten cleansed? But where are the nine?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Were there none found who returned to give glory to God, except this foreigner?\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Then he said to him, \u201cGet up, and go your way. Your faith has healed you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Being asked by the Pharisees when God\u2019s Kingdom would come, he answered them, \u201cGod\u2019s Kingdom doesn\u2019t come with observation;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"neither will they say, \u2018Look, here!\u2019 or, \u2018Look, there!\u2019 for behold, God\u2019s Kingdom is within you.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to the disciples, \u201cThe days will come when you will desire to see one of the days of the Son of Man, and you will not see it."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They will tell you, \u2018Look, here!\u2019 or \u2018Look, there!\u2019 Don\u2019t go away or follow after them,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"for as the lightning, when it flashes out of one part under the sky, shines to another part under the sky, so will the Son of Man be in his day."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But first, he must suffer many things and be rejected by this generation."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"As it was in the days of Noah, even so it will also be in the days of the Son of Man."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"They ate, they drank, they married, and they were given in marriage until the day that Noah entered into the ship, and the flood came and destroyed them all."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Likewise, even as it was in the days of Lot: they ate, they drank, they bought, they sold, they planted, they built;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"but in the day that Lot went out from Sodom, it rained fire and sulfur from the sky and destroyed them all."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"It will be the same way in the day that the Son of Man is revealed."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"In that day, he who will be on the housetop and his goods in the house, let him not go down to take them away. Let him who is in the field likewise not turn back."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Remember Lot\u2019s wife!"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Whoever seeks to save his life loses it, but whoever loses his life preserves it."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"I tell you, in that night there will be two people in one bed. One will be taken and the other will be left."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"There will be two grinding grain together. One will be taken and the other will be left.\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[],f:["Some Greek manuscripts add: \u201cTwo will be in the field: the one taken, and the other left.\u201d"]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"They, answering, asked him, \u201cWhere, Lord?\u201d"],[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhere the body is, there the vultures will also be gathered together.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He also spoke a parable to them that they must always pray and not give up,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cThere was a judge in a certain city who didn\u2019t fear God and didn\u2019t respect man."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"A widow was in that city, and she often came to him, saying, \u2018Defend me from my adversary!\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He wouldn\u2019t for a while; but afterward he said to himself, \u2018Though I neither fear God nor respect man,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"yet because this widow bothers me, I will defend her, or else she will wear me out by her continual coming.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord said, \u201cListen to what the unrighteous judge says."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Won\u2019t God avenge his chosen ones who are crying out to him day and night, and yet he exercises patience with them?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I tell you that he will avenge them quickly. Nevertheless, when the Son of Man comes, will he find faith on the earth?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He also spoke this parable to certain people who were convinced of their own righteousness, and who despised all others:"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"\u201cTwo men went up into the temple to pray; one was a Pharisee, and the other was a tax collector."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The Pharisee stood and prayed by himself like this: \u2018God, I thank you that I am not like the rest of men: extortionists, unrighteous, adulterers, or even like this tax collector."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I fast twice a week. I give tithes of all that I get.\u2019"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But the tax collector, standing far away, wouldn\u2019t even lift up his eyes to heaven, but beat his chest, saying, \u2018God, be merciful to me, a sinner!\u2019"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I tell you, this man went down to his house justified rather than the other; for everyone who exalts himself will be humbled, but he who humbles himself will be exalted.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"They were also bringing their babies to him, that he might touch them. But when the disciples saw it, they rebuked them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Jesus summoned them, saying, \u201cAllow the little children to come to me, and don\u2019t hinder them, for God\u2019s Kingdom belongs to such as these."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Most certainly, I tell you, whoever doesn\u2019t receive God\u2019s Kingdom like a little child, he will in no way enter into it.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"A certain ruler asked him, saying, \u201cGood Teacher, what shall I do to inherit eternal life?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus asked him, \u201cWhy do you call me good? No one is good, except one: God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You know the commandments: \u2018Don\u2019t commit adultery,\u2019 \u2018Don\u2019t murder,\u2019 \u2018Don\u2019t steal,\u2019 \u2018Don\u2019t give false testimony,\u2019 \u2018Honor your father and your mother.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI have observed all these things from my youth up.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus heard these things, he said to him, \u201cYou still lack one thing. Sell all that you have and distribute it to the poor. Then you will have treasure in heaven; then come, follow me.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But when he heard these things, he became very sad, for he was very rich."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, seeing that he became very sad, said, \u201cHow hard it is for those who have riches to enter into God\u2019s Kingdom!"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For it is easier for a camel to enter in through a needle\u2019s eye than for a rich man to enter into God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who heard it said, \u201cThen who can be saved?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said, \u201cThe things which are impossible with men are possible with God.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter said, \u201cLook, we have left everything and followed you.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, there is no one who has left house, or wife, or brothers, or parents, or children, for God\u2019s Kingdom\u2019s sake,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"who will not receive many times more in this time, and in the world to come, eternal life.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"He took the twelve aside and said to them, \u201cBehold, we are going up to Jerusalem, and all the things that are written through the prophets concerning the Son of Man will be completed."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For he will be delivered up to the Gentiles, will be mocked, treated shamefully, and spit on."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They will scourge and kill him. On the third day, he will rise again.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"They understood none of these things. This saying was hidden from them, and they didn\u2019t understand the things that were said."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"As he came near Jericho, a certain blind man sat by the road, begging."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Hearing a multitude going by, he asked what this meant."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They told him that Jesus of Nazareth was passing by."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He cried out, \u201cJesus, you son of David, have mercy on me!\u201d"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Those who led the way rebuked him, that he should be quiet; but he cried out all the more, \u201cYou son of David, have mercy on me!\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Standing still, Jesus commanded him to be brought to him. When he had come near, he asked him,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"\u201cWhat do you want me to do?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cLord, that I may see again.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cReceive your sight. Your faith has healed you.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately he received his sight and followed him, glorifying God. All the people, when they saw it, praised God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He entered and was passing through Jericho."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"There was a man named Zacchaeus. He was a chief tax collector, and he was rich."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He was trying to see who Jesus was, and couldn\u2019t because of the crowd, because he was short."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He ran on ahead and climbed up into a sycamore tree to see him, for he was going to pass that way."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When Jesus came to the place, he looked up and saw him, and said to him, \u201cZacchaeus, hurry and come down, for today I must stay at your house.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He hurried, came down, and received him joyfully."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When they saw it, they all murmured, saying, \u201cHe has gone in to lodge with a man who is a sinner.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Zacchaeus stood and said to the Lord, \u201cBehold, Lord, half of my goods I give to the poor. If I have wrongfully exacted anything of anyone, I restore four times as much.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cToday, salvation has come to this house, because he also is a son of Abraham."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the Son of Man came to seek and to save that which was lost.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"As they heard these things, he went on and told a parable, because he was near Jerusalem, and they supposed that God\u2019s Kingdom would be revealed immediately."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He said therefore, \u201cA certain nobleman went into a far country to receive for himself a kingdom and to return."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He called ten servants of his and gave them ten mina coins, and told them, \u2018Conduct business until I come.\u2019"]],f:["10 minas was more than 3 years\u2019 wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But his citizens hated him, and sent an envoy after him, saying, \u2018We don\u2019t want this man to reign over us.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen he had come back again, having received the kingdom, he commanded these servants, to whom he had given the money, to be called to him, that he might know what they had gained by conducting business."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The first came before him, saying, \u2018Lord, your mina has made ten more minas.\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said to him, \u2018Well done, you good servant! Because you were found faithful with very little, you shall have authority over ten cities.\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe second came, saying, \u2018Your mina, Lord, has made five minas.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo he said to him, \u2018And you are to be over five cities.\u2019"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Another came, saying, \u2018Lord, behold, your mina, which I kept laid away in a handkerchief,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"for I feared you, because you are an exacting man. You take up that which you didn\u2019t lay down, and reap that which you didn\u2019t sow.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said to him, \u2018Out of your own mouth I will judge you, you wicked servant! You knew that I am an exacting man, taking up that which I didn\u2019t lay down and reaping that which I didn\u2019t sow."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Then why didn\u2019t you deposit my money in the bank, and at my coming, I might have earned interest on it?\u2019"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He said to those who stood by, \u2018Take the mina away from him and give it to him who has the ten minas.\u2019"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThey said to him, \u2018Lord, he has ten minas!\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u2018For I tell you that to everyone who has, will more be given; but from him who doesn\u2019t have, even that which he has will be taken away from him."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But bring those enemies of mine who didn\u2019t want me to reign over them here, and kill them before me.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Having said these things, he went on ahead, going up to Jerusalem."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came near to Bethsphage and Bethany, at the mountain that is called Olivet, he sent two of his disciples,"]],f:["TR, NU read \u201cBethpage\u201d instead of \u201cBethsphage\u201d"]},{v:30,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cGo your way into the village on the other side, in which, as you enter, you will find a colt tied, which no man has ever sat upon. Untie it and bring it."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"If anyone asks you, \u2018Why are you untying it?\u2019 say to him: \u2018The Lord needs it.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who were sent went away and found things just as he had told them."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"As they were untying the colt, its owners said to them, \u201cWhy are you untying the colt?\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cThe Lord needs it.\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Then they brought it to Jesus. They threw their cloaks on the colt and sat Jesus on them."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"As he went, they spread their cloaks on the road."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"As he was now getting near, at the descent of the Mount of Olives, the whole multitude of the disciples began to rejoice and praise God with a loud voice for all the mighty works which they had seen,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cBlessed is the King who comes in the name of the Lord! Peace in heaven, and glory in the highest!\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of the Pharisees from the multitude said to him, \u201cTeacher, rebuke your disciples!\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cI tell you that if these were silent, the stones would cry out.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came near, he saw the city and wept over it,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cIf you, even you, had known today the things which belong to your peace! But now, they are hidden from your eyes."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"For the days will come on you when your enemies will throw up a barricade against you, surround you, hem you in on every side,"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"and will dash you and your children within you to the ground. They will not leave in you one stone on another, because you didn\u2019t know the time of your visitation.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"He entered into the temple and began to drive out those who bought and sold in it,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"saying to them, \u201cIt is written, \u2018My house is a house of prayer,\u2019 but you have made it a \u2018den of robbers\u2019!\u201d"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"He was teaching daily in the temple, but the chief priests, the scribes, and the leading men among the people sought to destroy him."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"They couldn\u2019t find what they might do, for all the people hung on to every word that he said."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"On one of those days, as he was teaching the people in the temple and preaching the Good News, the priests and scribes came to him with the elders."]],f:["TR adds \u201cchief\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cTell us: by what authority do you do these things? Or who is giving you this authority?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cI also will ask you one question. Tell me:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"the baptism of John, was it from heaven, or from men?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"They reasoned with themselves, saying, \u201cIf we say, \u2018From heaven,\u2019 he will say, \u2018Why didn\u2019t you believe him?\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But if we say, \u2018From men,\u2019 all the people will stone us, for they are persuaded that John was a prophet.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They answered that they didn\u2019t know where it was from."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cNeither will I tell you by what authority I do these things.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He began to tell the people this parable: \u201cA man planted a vineyard and rented it out to some farmers, and went into another country for a long time."]],f:["NU (in brackets) and TR add \u201ccertain\u201d"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"At the proper season, he sent a servant to the farmers to collect his share of the fruit of the vineyard. But the farmers beat him and sent him away empty."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He sent yet another servant, and they also beat him and treated him shamefully, and sent him away empty."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He sent yet a third, and they also wounded him and threw him out."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The lord of the vineyard said, \u2018What shall I do? I will send my beloved son. It may be that seeing him, they will respect him.\u2019"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut when the farmers saw him, they reasoned among themselves, saying, \u2018This is the heir. Come, let\u2019s kill him, that the inheritance may be ours.\u2019"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then they threw him out of the vineyard and killed him. What therefore will the lord of the vineyard do to them?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He will come and destroy these farmers, and will give the vineyard to others.\u201d"],[0,"When they heard that, they said, \u201cMay that never be!\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But he looked at them and said, \u201cThen what is this that is written,"],[1,"\u2018The stone which the builders rejected"],[2,"was made the chief cornerstone\u2019?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Everyone who falls on that stone will be broken to pieces,"],[2,"but it will crush whomever it falls on to dust.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The chief priests and the scribes sought to lay hands on him that very hour, but they feared the people\u2014for they knew he had spoken this parable against them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They watched him and sent out spies, who pretended to be righteous, that they might trap him in something he said, so as to deliver him up to the power and authority of the governor."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cTeacher, we know that you say and teach what is right, and aren\u2019t partial to anyone, but truly teach the way of God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Is it lawful for us to pay taxes to Caesar, or not?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But he perceived their craftiness, and said to them, \u201cWhy do you test me?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Show me a denarius. Whose image and inscription are on it?\u201d"],[0,"They answered, \u201cCaesar\u2019s.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThen give to Caesar the things that are Caesar\u2019s, and to God the things that are God\u2019s.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"They weren\u2019t able to trap him in his words before the people. They marveled at his answer and were silent."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Some of the Sadducees came to him, those who deny that there is a resurrection."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cTeacher, Moses wrote to us that if a man\u2019s brother dies having a wife, and he is childless, his brother should take the wife and raise up children for his brother."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"There were therefore seven brothers. The first took a wife, and died childless."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The second took her as wife, and he died childless."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The third took her, and likewise the seven all left no children, and died."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Afterward the woman also died."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Therefore in the resurrection whose wife of them will she be? For the seven had her as a wife.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cThe children of this age marry and are given in marriage."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"But those who are considered worthy to attain to that age and the resurrection from the dead neither marry nor are given in marriage."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"For they can\u2019t die any more, for they are like the angels and are children of God, being children of the resurrection."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"But that the dead are raised, even Moses showed at the bush, when he called the Lord \u2018The God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.\u2019"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Now he is not the God of the dead, but of the living, for all are alive to him.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of the scribes answered, \u201cTeacher, you speak well.\u201d"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t dare to ask him any more questions."]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhy do they say that the Christ is David\u2019s son?"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"David himself says in the book of Psalms,"],[1,"\u2018The Lord said to my Lord,"],[2,"\u201cSit at my right hand,"]]},{v:43,l:[[2,"until I make your enemies the footstool of your feet.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDavid therefore calls him Lord, so how is he his son?\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"In the hearing of all the people, he said to his disciples,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"\u201cBeware of those scribes who like to walk in long robes, and love greetings in the marketplaces, the best seats in the synagogues, and the best places at feasts;"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"who devour widows\u2019 houses, and for a pretense make long prayers. These will receive greater condemnation.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He looked up and saw the rich people who were putting their gifts into the treasury."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He saw a certain poor widow casting in two small brass coins."]],f:["literally, \u201ctwo lepta.\u201d 2 lepta was about 1% of a day\u2019s wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cTruly I tell you, this poor widow put in more than all of them,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for all these put in gifts for God from their abundance, but she, out of her poverty, put in all that she had to live on.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"As some were talking about the temple and how it was decorated with beautiful stones and gifts, he said,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"\u201cAs for these things which you see, the days will come in which there will not be left here one stone on another that will not be thrown down.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cTeacher, so when will these things be? What is the sign that these things are about to happen?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWatch out that you don\u2019t get led astray, for many will come in my name, saying, \u2018I am he,\u2019 and, \u2018The time is at hand.\u2019 Therefore don\u2019t follow them."]],f:["or, I AM"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When you hear of wars and disturbances, don\u2019t be terrified, for these things must happen first, but the end won\u2019t come immediately.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to them, \u201cNation will rise against nation, and kingdom against kingdom."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"There will be great earthquakes, famines, and plagues in various places. There will be terrors and great signs from heaven."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But before all these things, they will lay their hands on you and will persecute you, delivering you up to synagogues and prisons, bringing you before kings and governors for my name\u2019s sake."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"It will turn out as a testimony for you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Settle it therefore in your hearts not to meditate beforehand how to answer,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"for I will give you a mouth and wisdom which all your adversaries will not be able to withstand or to contradict."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You will be handed over even by parents, brothers, relatives, and friends. They will cause some of you to be put to death."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You will be hated by all men for my name\u2019s sake."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"And not a hair of your head will perish."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBy your endurance you will win your lives."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut when you see Jerusalem surrounded by armies, then know that its desolation is at hand."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then let those who are in Judea flee to the mountains. Let those who are in the middle of her depart. Let those who are in the country not enter therein."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For these are days of vengeance, that all things which are written may be fulfilled."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Woe to those who are pregnant and to those who nurse infants in those days! For there will be great distress in the land and wrath to this people."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They will fall by the edge of the sword, and will be led captive into all the nations. Jerusalem will be trampled down by the Gentiles until the times of the Gentiles are fulfilled."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThere will be signs in the sun, moon, and stars; and on the earth anxiety of nations, in perplexity for the roaring of the sea and the waves;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"men fainting for fear and for expectation of the things which are coming on the world, for the powers of the heavens will be shaken."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Then they will see the Son of Man coming in a cloud with power and great glory."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But when these things begin to happen, look up and lift up your heads, because your redemption is near.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He told them a parable. \u201cSee the fig tree and all the trees."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When they are already budding, you see it and know by your own selves that the summer is already near."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Even so you also, when you see these things happening, know that God\u2019s Kingdom is near."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, this generation will not pass away until all things are accomplished."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Heaven and earth will pass away, but my words will by no means pass away."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cSo be careful, or your hearts will be loaded down with carousing, drunkenness, and cares of this life, and that day will come on you suddenly."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"For it will come like a snare on all those who dwell on the surface of all the earth."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Therefore be watchful all the time, praying that you may be counted worthy to escape all these things that will happen, and to stand before the Son of Man.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Every day Jesus was teaching in the temple, and every night he would go out and spend the night on the mountain that is called Olivet."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"All the people came early in the morning to him in the temple to hear him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the feast of unleavened bread, which is called the Passover, was approaching."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The chief priests and the scribes sought how they might put him to death, for they feared the people."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Satan entered into Judas, who was also called Iscariot, who was counted with the twelve."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He went away and talked with the chief priests and captains about how he might deliver him to them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They were glad, and agreed to give him money."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He consented and sought an opportunity to deliver him to them in the absence of the multitude."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The day of unleavened bread came, on which the Passover must be sacrificed."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Jesus sent Peter and John, saying, \u201cGo and prepare the Passover for us, that we may eat.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cWhere do you want us to prepare?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cBehold, when you have entered into the city, a man carrying a pitcher of water will meet you. Follow him into the house which he enters."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Tell the master of the house, \u2018The Teacher says to you, \u201cWhere is the guest room, where I may eat the Passover with my disciples?\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He will show you a large, furnished upper room. Make preparations there.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"They went, found things as Jesus had told them, and they prepared the Passover."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When the hour had come, he sat down with the twelve apostles."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cI have earnestly desired to eat this Passover with you before I suffer,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"for I tell you, I will no longer by any means eat of it until it is fulfilled in God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He received a cup, and when he had given thanks, he said, \u201cTake this and share it among yourselves,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"for I tell you, I will not drink at all again from the fruit of the vine, until God\u2019s Kingdom comes.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He took bread, and when he had given thanks, he broke and gave it to them, saying, \u201cThis is my body which is given for you. Do this in memory of me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Likewise, he took the cup after supper, saying, \u201cThis cup is the new covenant in my blood, which is poured out for you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But behold, the hand of him who betrays me is with me on the table."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The Son of Man indeed goes as it has been determined, but woe to that man through whom he is betrayed!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"They began to question among themselves which of them it was who would do this thing."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"A dispute also arose among them, which of them was considered to be greatest."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThe kings of the nations lord it over them, and those who have authority over them are called \u2018benefactors.\u2019"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But not so with you. Rather, the one who is greater among you, let him become as the younger, and one who is governing, as one who serves."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For who is greater, one who sits at the table, or one who serves? Isn\u2019t it he who sits at the table? But I am among you as one who serves."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut you are those who have continued with me in my trials."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I confer on you a kingdom, even as my Father conferred on me,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"that you may eat and drink at my table in my Kingdom. You will sit on thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord said, \u201cSimon, Simon, behold, Satan asked to have all of you, that he might sift you as wheat,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"but I prayed for you, that your faith wouldn\u2019t fail. You, when once you have turned again, establish your brothers.\u201d"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here may be also correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cLord, I am ready to go with you both to prison and to death!\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI tell you, Peter, the rooster will by no means crow today until you deny that you know me three times.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhen I sent you out without purse, bag, and sandals, did you lack anything?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cNothing.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he said to them, \u201cBut now, whoever has a purse, let him take it, and likewise a bag. Whoever has none, let him sell his cloak, and buy a sword."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For I tell you that this which is written must still be fulfilled in me: \u2018He was counted with transgressors.\u2019 For that which concerns me is being fulfilled.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cLord, behold, here are two swords.\u201d"],[0,"He said to them, \u201cThat is enough.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"He came out and went, as his custom was, to the Mount of Olives. His disciples also followed him."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"When he was at the place, he said to them, \u201cPray that you don\u2019t enter into temptation.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"He was withdrawn from them about a stone\u2019s throw, and he knelt down and prayed,"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cFather, if you are willing, remove this cup from me. Nevertheless, not my will, but yours, be done.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"An angel from heaven appeared to him, strengthening him."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Being in agony, he prayed more earnestly. His sweat became like great drops of blood falling down on the ground."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"When he rose up from his prayer, he came to the disciples and found them sleeping because of grief,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cWhy do you sleep? Rise and pray that you may not enter into temptation.\u201d"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"While he was still speaking, a crowd appeared. He who was called Judas, one of the twelve, was leading them. He came near to Jesus to kiss him."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"But Jesus said to him, \u201cJudas, do you betray the Son of Man with a kiss?\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"When those who were around him saw what was about to happen, they said to him, \u201cLord, shall we strike with the sword?\u201d"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"A certain one of them struck the servant of the high priest, and cut off his right ear."]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus answered, \u201cLet me at least do this\u201d\u2014and he touched his ear and healed him."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"Jesus said to the chief priests, captains of the temple, and elders, who had come against him, \u201cHave you come out as against a robber, with swords and clubs?"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"When I was with you in the temple daily, you didn\u2019t stretch out your hands against me. But this is your hour, and the power of darkness.\u201d"]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"They seized him and led him away, and brought him into the high priest\u2019s house. But Peter followed from a distance."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"When they had kindled a fire in the middle of the courtyard and had sat down together, Peter sat among them."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"A certain servant girl saw him as he sat in the light, and looking intently at him, said, \u201cThis man also was with him.\u201d"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"He denied Jesus, saying, \u201cWoman, I don\u2019t know him.\u201d"]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[0,"After a little while someone else saw him and said, \u201cYou also are one of them!\u201d"],[0,"But Peter answered, \u201cMan, I am not!\u201d"]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"After about one hour passed, another confidently affirmed, saying, \u201cTruly this man also was with him, for he is a Galilean!\u201d"]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter said, \u201cMan, I don\u2019t know what you are talking about!\u201d Immediately, while he was still speaking, a rooster crowed."]]},{v:61,l:[[0,"The Lord turned and looked at Peter. Then Peter remembered the Lord\u2019s word, how he said to him, \u201cBefore the rooster crows you will deny me three times.\u201d"]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"He went out, and wept bitterly."]]},{v:63,p:1,l:[[0,"The men who held Jesus mocked him and beat him."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"Having blindfolded him, they struck him on the face and asked him, \u201cProphesy! Who is the one who struck you?\u201d"]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"They spoke many other things against him, insulting him."]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[0,"As soon as it was day, the assembly of the elders of the people were gathered together, both chief priests and scribes, and they led him away into their council, saying,"]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"\u201cIf you are the Christ, tell us.\u201d"],[0,"But he said to them, \u201cIf I tell you, you won\u2019t believe,"]]},{v:68,l:[[0,"and if I ask, you will in no way answer me or let me go."]]},{v:69,l:[[0,"From now on, the Son of Man will be seated at the right hand of the power of God.\u201d"]]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[0,"They all said, \u201cAre you then the Son of God?\u201d"],[0,"He said to them, \u201cYou say it, because I am.\u201d"]]},{v:71,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cWhy do we need any more witness? For we ourselves have heard from his own mouth!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The whole company of them rose up and brought him before Pilate."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They began to accuse him, saying, \u201cWe found this man perverting the nation, forbidding paying taxes to Caesar, and saying that he himself is Christ, a king.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate asked him, \u201cAre you the King of the Jews?\u201d"],[0,"He answered him, \u201cSo you say.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate said to the chief priests and the multitudes, \u201cI find no basis for a charge against this man.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But they insisted, saying, \u201cHe stirs up the people, teaching throughout all Judea, beginning from Galilee even to this place.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Pilate heard Galilee mentioned, he asked if the man was a Galilean."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When he found out that he was in Herod\u2019s jurisdiction, he sent him to Herod, who was also in Jerusalem during those days."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when Herod saw Jesus, he was exceedingly glad, for he had wanted to see him for a long time, because he had heard many things about him. He hoped to see some miracle done by him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He questioned him with many words, but he gave no answers."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The chief priests and the scribes stood, vehemently accusing him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Herod with his soldiers humiliated him and mocked him. Dressing him in luxurious clothing, they sent him back to Pilate."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Herod and Pilate became friends with each other that very day, for before that they were enemies with each other."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate called together the chief priests, the rulers, and the people,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cYou brought this man to me as one that perverts the people, and behold, having examined him before you, I found no basis for a charge against this man concerning those things of which you accuse him."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Neither has Herod, for I sent you to him, and see, nothing worthy of death has been done by him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I will therefore chastise him and release him.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now he had to release one prisoner to them at the feast."]],f:["NU omits verse 17."]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But they all cried out together, saying, \u201cAway with this man! Release to us Barabbas!\u201d\u2014"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"one who was thrown into prison for a certain revolt in the city, and for murder."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Pilate spoke to them again, wanting to release Jesus,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"but they shouted, saying, \u201cCrucify! Crucify him!\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them the third time, \u201cWhy? What evil has this man done? I have found no capital crime in him. I will therefore chastise him and release him.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But they were urgent with loud voices, asking that he might be crucified. Their voices and the voices of the chief priests prevailed."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Pilate decreed that what they asked for should be done."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He released him who had been thrown into prison for insurrection and murder, for whom they asked, but he delivered Jesus up to their will."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"When they led him away, they grabbed one Simon of Cyrene, coming from the country, and laid the cross on him to carry it after Jesus."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"A great multitude of the people followed him, including women who also mourned and lamented him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But Jesus, turning to them, said, \u201cDaughters of Jerusalem, don\u2019t weep for me, but weep for yourselves and for your children."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For behold, the days are coming in which they will say, \u2018Blessed are the barren, the wombs that never bore, and the breasts that never nursed.\u2019"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Then they will begin to tell the mountains, \u2018Fall on us!\u2019 and tell the hills, \u2018Cover us.\u2019"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For if they do these things in the green tree, what will be done in the dry?\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"There were also others, two criminals, led with him to be put to death."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"When they came to the place that is called \u201cThe Skull\u201d, they crucified him there with the criminals, one on the right and the other on the left."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said, \u201cFather, forgive them, for they don\u2019t know what they are doing.\u201d"],[0,"Dividing his garments among them, they cast lots."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The people stood watching. The rulers with them also scoffed at him, saying, \u201cHe saved others. Let him save himself, if this is the Christ of God, his chosen one!\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The soldiers also mocked him, coming to him and offering him vinegar,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"and saying, \u201cIf you are the King of the Jews, save yourself!\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"An inscription was also written over him in letters of Greek, Latin, and Hebrew: \u201cTHIS IS THE KING OF THE JEWS.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the criminals who was hanged insulted him, saying, \u201cIf you are the Christ, save yourself and us!\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"But the other answered, and rebuking him said, \u201cDon\u2019t you even fear God, seeing you are under the same condemnation?"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"And we indeed justly, for we receive the due reward for our deeds, but this man has done nothing wrong.\u201d"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"He said to Jesus, \u201cLord, remember me when you come into your Kingdom.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cAssuredly I tell you, today you will be with me in Paradise.\u201d"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"It was now about the sixth hour, and darkness came over the whole land until the ninth hour."]],f:["Time was counted from sunrise, so the sixth hour was about noon.","3:00 p.m."]},{v:45,l:[[0,"The sun was darkened, and the veil of the temple was torn in two."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Jesus, crying with a loud voice, said, \u201cFather, into your hands I commit my spirit!\u201d Having said this, he breathed his last."]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"When the centurion saw what was done, he glorified God, saying, \u201cCertainly this was a righteous man.\u201d"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"All the multitudes that came together to see this, when they saw the things that were done, returned home beating their chests."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"All his acquaintances and the women who followed with him from Galilee stood at a distance, watching these things."]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, there was a man named Joseph, who was a member of the council, a good and righteous man"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"(he had not consented to their counsel and deed), from Arimathaea, a city of the Jews, who was also waiting for God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"This man went to Pilate, and asked for Jesus\u2019 body."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"He took it down and wrapped it in a linen cloth, and laid him in a tomb that was cut in stone, where no one had ever been laid."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"It was the day of the Preparation, and the Sabbath was drawing near."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"The women who had come with him out of Galilee followed after, and saw the tomb and how his body was laid."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"They returned and prepared spices and ointments. On the Sabbath they rested according to the commandment."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But on the first day of the week, at early dawn, they and some others came to the tomb, bringing the spices which they had prepared."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They found the stone rolled away from the tomb."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They entered in, and didn\u2019t find the Lord Jesus\u2019 body."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"While they were greatly perplexed about this, behold, two men stood by them in dazzling clothing."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Becoming terrified, they bowed their faces down to the earth."],[0,"The men said to them, \u201cWhy do you seek the living among the dead?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He isn\u2019t here, but is risen. Remember what he told you when he was still in Galilee,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"saying that the Son of Man must be delivered up into the hands of sinful men and be crucified, and the third day rise again?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"They remembered his words,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"returned from the tomb, and told all these things to the eleven and to all the rest."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now they were Mary Magdalene, Joanna, and Mary the mother of James. The other women with them told these things to the apostles."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"These words seemed to them to be nonsense, and they didn\u2019t believe them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But Peter got up and ran to the tomb. Stooping and looking in, he saw the strips of linen lying by themselves, and he departed to his home, wondering what had happened."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, two of them were going that very day to a village named Emmaus, which was sixty stadia from Jerusalem."]],f:["60 stadia = about 11 kilometers or about 7 miles."]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They talked with each other about all of these things which had happened."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"While they talked and questioned together, Jesus himself came near, and went with them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But their eyes were kept from recognizing him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat are you talking about as you walk, and are sad?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"One of them, named Cleopas, answered him, \u201cAre you the only stranger in Jerusalem who doesn\u2019t know the things which have happened there in these days?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhat things?\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cThe things concerning Jesus the Nazarene, who was a prophet mighty in deed and word before God and all the people;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and how the chief priests and our rulers delivered him up to be condemned to death, and crucified him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But we were hoping that it was he who would redeem Israel. Yes, and besides all this, it is now the third day since these things happened."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Also, certain women of our company amazed us, having arrived early at the tomb;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and when they didn\u2019t find his body, they came saying that they had also seen a vision of angels, who said that he was alive."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Some of us went to the tomb and found it just like the women had said, but they didn\u2019t see him.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cFoolish people, and slow of heart to believe in all that the prophets have spoken!"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t the Christ have to suffer these things and to enter into his glory?\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Beginning from Moses and from all the prophets, he explained to them in all the Scriptures the things concerning himself."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They came near to the village where they were going, and he acted like he would go further."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"They urged him, saying, \u201cStay with us, for it is almost evening, and the day is almost over.\u201d"],[0,"He went in to stay with them."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When he had sat down at the table with them, he took the bread and gave thanks. Breaking it, he gave it to them."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Their eyes were opened and they recognized him; then he vanished out of their sight."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They said to one another, \u201cWeren\u2019t our hearts burning within us while he spoke to us along the way, and while he opened the Scriptures to us?\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They rose up that very hour, returned to Jerusalem, and found the eleven gathered together, and those who were with them,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cThe Lord is risen indeed, and has appeared to Simon!\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"They related the things that happened along the way, and how he was recognized by them in the breaking of the bread."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"As they said these things, Jesus himself stood among them, and said to them, \u201cPeace be to you.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"But they were terrified and filled with fear, and supposed that they had seen a spirit."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cWhy are you troubled? Why do doubts arise in your hearts?"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"See my hands and my feet, that it is truly me. Touch me and see, for a spirit doesn\u2019t have flesh and bones, as you see that I have.\u201d"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"When he had said this, he showed them his hands and his feet."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"While they still didn\u2019t believe for joy, and wondered, he said to them, \u201cDo you have anything here to eat?\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"They gave him a piece of a broiled fish and some honeycomb."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He took them, and ate in front of them."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThis is what I told you while I was still with you, that all things which are written in the law of Moses, the prophets, and the psalms concerning me must be fulfilled.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Then he opened their minds, that they might understand the Scriptures."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cThus it is written, and thus it was necessary for the Christ to suffer and to rise from the dead the third day,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"and that repentance and remission of sins should be preached in his name to all the nations, beginning at Jerusalem."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"You are witnesses of these things."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Behold, I send out the promise of my Father on you. But wait in the city of Jerusalem until you are clothed with power from on high.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"He led them out as far as Bethany, and he lifted up his hands and blessed them."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"While he blessed them, he withdrew from them and was carried up into heaven."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"They worshiped him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy,"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"and were continually in the temple, praising and blessing God. Amen."]]}]]}},1313,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,s,i){a.exports={book:"John",name:"John",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The same was in the beginning with God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"All things were made through him. Without him, nothing was made that has been made."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"In him was life, and the life was the light of men."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The light shines in the darkness, and the darkness hasn\u2019t overcome it."]],f:["The word translated \u201covercome\u201d (\u03ba\u03b1\u03c4\u03ad\u03bb\u03b1\u03b2\u03b5\u03bd) can also be translated \u201ccomprehended.\u201d It refers to getting a grip on an enemy to defeat him."]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"There came a man sent from God, whose name was John."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The same came as a witness, that he might testify about the light, that all might believe through him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He was not the light, but was sent that he might testify about the light."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The true light that enlightens everyone was coming into the world."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"He was in the world, and the world was made through him, and the world didn\u2019t recognize him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He came to his own, and those who were his own didn\u2019t receive him."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But as many as received him, to them he gave the right to become God\u2019s children, to those who believe in his name:"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"who were born, not of blood, nor of the will of the flesh, nor of the will of man, but of God."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The Word became flesh and lived among us. We saw his glory, such glory as of the only born Son of the Father, full of grace and truth."]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03bf\u03c5\u03c2\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"John testified about him. He cried out, saying, \u201cThis was he of whom I said, \u2018He who comes after me has surpassed me, for he was before me.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"From his fullness we all received grace upon grace."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For the law was given through Moses. Grace and truth were realized through Jesus Christ."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:18,l:[[0,"No one has seen God at any time. The only born Son, who is in the bosom of the Father, has declared him."]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03b7\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d.","NU reads \u201cGod\u201d"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"This is John\u2019s testimony, when the Jews sent priests and Levites from Jerusalem to ask him, \u201cWho are you?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He declared, and didn\u2019t deny, but he declared, \u201cI am not the Christ.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cWhat then? Are you Elijah?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am not.\u201d"],[0,"\u201cAre you the prophet?\u201d"],[0,"He answered, \u201cNo.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"They said therefore to him, \u201cWho are you? Give us an answer to take back to those who sent us. What do you say about yourself?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cI am the voice of one crying in the wilderness, \u2018Make straight the way of the Lord,\u2019 as Isaiah the prophet said.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"The ones who had been sent were from the Pharisees."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"They asked him, \u201cWhy then do you baptize if you are not the Christ, nor Elijah, nor the prophet?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"John answered them, \u201cI baptize in water, but among you stands one whom you don\u2019t know."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He is the one who comes after me, who is preferred before me, whose sandal strap I\u2019m not worthy to loosen.\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"These things were done in Bethany beyond the Jordan, where John was baptizing."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The next day, he saw Jesus coming to him, and said, \u201cBehold, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"This is he of whom I said, \u2018After me comes a man who is preferred before me, for he was before me.\u2019"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"I didn\u2019t know him, but for this reason I came baptizing in water, that he would be revealed to Israel.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"John testified, saying, \u201cI have seen the Spirit descending like a dove out of heaven, and it remained on him."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"I didn\u2019t recognize him, but he who sent me to baptize in water said to me, \u2018On whomever you will see the Spirit descending and remaining on him is he who baptizes in the Holy Spirit.\u2019"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"I have seen and have testified that this is the Son of God.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, the next day, John was standing with two of his disciples,"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"and he looked at Jesus as he walked, and said, \u201cBehold, the Lamb of God!\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The two disciples heard him speak, and they followed Jesus."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Jesus turned and saw them following, and said to them, \u201cWhat are you looking for?\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cRabbi\u201d (which is to say, being interpreted, Teacher), \u201cwhere are you staying?\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cCome and see.\u201d"],[0,"They came and saw where he was staying, and they stayed with him that day. It was about the tenth hour."]],f:["4:00 p.m."]},{v:40,l:[[0,"One of the two who heard John and followed him was Andrew, Simon Peter\u2019s brother."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He first found his own brother, Simon, and said to him, \u201cWe have found the Messiah!\u201d (which is, being interpreted, Christ)."]],f:["\u201cMessiah\u201d (Hebrew) and \u201cChrist\u201d (Greek) both mean \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:42,l:[[0,"He brought him to Jesus. Jesus looked at him and said, \u201cYou are Simon the son of Jonah. You shall be called Cephas\u201d (which is by interpretation, Peter)."]],f:["\u201cCephas\u201d (Aramaic) and \u201cPeter\u201d (Greek) both mean \u201cRock\u201d."]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, he was determined to go out into Galilee, and he found Philip. Jesus said to him, \u201cFollow me.\u201d"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Now Philip was from Bethsaida, the city of Andrew and Peter."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"Philip found Nathanael, and said to him, \u201cWe have found him of whom Moses in the law and also the prophets, wrote: Jesus of Nazareth, the son of Joseph.\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"Nathanael said to him, \u201cCan any good thing come out of Nazareth?\u201d"],[0,"Philip said to him, \u201cCome and see.\u201d"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus saw Nathanael coming to him, and said about him, \u201cBehold, an Israelite indeed, in whom is no deceit!\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"Nathanael said to him, \u201cHow do you know me?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cBefore Philip called you, when you were under the fig tree, I saw you.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"Nathanael answered him, \u201cRabbi, you are the Son of God! You are King of Israel!\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cBecause I told you, \u2018I saw you underneath the fig tree,\u2019 do you believe? You will see greater things than these!\u201d"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"He said to him, \u201cMost certainly, I tell you all, hereafter you will see heaven opened, and the angels of God ascending and descending on the Son of Man.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The third day, there was a wedding in Cana of Galilee. Jesus\u2019 mother was there."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Jesus also was invited, with his disciples, to the wedding."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When the wine ran out, Jesus\u2019 mother said to him, \u201cThey have no wine.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cWoman, what does that have to do with you and me? My hour has not yet come.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"His mother said to the servants, \u201cWhatever he says to you, do it.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there were six water pots of stone set there after the Jews\u2019 way of purifying, containing two or three metretes apiece."]],f:["2 to 3 metretes is about 20 to 30 U. S. Gallons, or 75 to 115 liters."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cFill the water pots with water.\u201d So they filled them up to the brim."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cNow draw some out, and take it to the ruler of the feast.\u201d So they took it."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When the ruler of the feast tasted the water now become wine, and didn\u2019t know where it came from (but the servants who had drawn the water knew), the ruler of the feast called the bridegroom"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cEveryone serves the good wine first, and when the guests have drunk freely, then that which is worse. You have kept the good wine until now!\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"This beginning of his signs Jesus did in Cana of Galilee, and revealed his glory; and his disciples believed in him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, he went down to Capernaum, he, and his mother, his brothers, and his disciples; and they stayed there a few days."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The Passover of the Jews was at hand, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He found in the temple those who sold oxen, sheep, and doves, and the changers of money sitting."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He made a whip of cords and drove all out of the temple, both the sheep and the oxen; and he poured out the changers\u2019 money and overthrew their tables."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"To those who sold the doves, he said, \u201cTake these things out of here! Don\u2019t make my Father\u2019s house a marketplace!\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"His disciples remembered that it was written, \u201cZeal for your house will eat me up.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore answered him, \u201cWhat sign do you show us, seeing that you do these things?\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cDestroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore said, \u201cIt took forty-six years to build this temple! Will you raise it up in three days?\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But he spoke of the temple of his body."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When therefore he was raised from the dead, his disciples remembered that he said this, and they believed the Scripture and the word which Jesus had said."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when he was in Jerusalem at the Passover, during the feast, many believed in his name, observing his signs which he did."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But Jesus didn\u2019t entrust himself to them, because he knew everyone,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"and because he didn\u2019t need for anyone to testify concerning man; for he himself knew what was in man."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was a man of the Pharisees named Nicodemus, a ruler of the Jews."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He came to Jesus by night and said to him, \u201cRabbi, we know that you are a teacher who has come from God, for no one can do these signs that you do, unless God is with him.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, unless one is born anew, he can\u2019t see God\u2019s Kingdom.\u201d"]],f:["The word translated \u201canew\u201d here and in John 3:7 (\u1f04\u03bd\u03c9\u03b8\u03b5\u03bd) also means \u201cagain\u201d and \u201cfrom above\u201d."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Nicodemus said to him, \u201cHow can a man be born when he is old? Can he enter a second time into his mother\u2019s womb and be born?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, unless one is born of water and Spirit, he can\u2019t enter into God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"That which is born of the flesh is flesh. That which is born of the Spirit is spirit."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t marvel that I said to you, \u2018You must all be born anew.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The wind blows where it wants to, and you hear its sound, but don\u2019t know where it comes from and where it is going. So is everyone who is born of the Spirit.\u201d"]],f:["The same Greek word (\u03c0\u03bd\u03b5\u1fe6\u03bc\u03b1) means wind, breath, and spirit."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Nicodemus answered him, \u201cHow can these things be?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cAre you the teacher of Israel, and don\u2019t understand these things?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, we speak that which we know and testify of that which we have seen, and you don\u2019t receive our witness."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If I told you earthly things and you don\u2019t believe, how will you believe if I tell you heavenly things?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"No one has ascended into heaven but he who descended out of heaven, the Son of Man, who is in heaven."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"As Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness, even so must the Son of Man be lifted up,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For God so loved the world, that he gave his only born Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life."]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03b7\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For God didn\u2019t send his Son into the world to judge the world, but that the world should be saved through him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He who believes in him is not judged. He who doesn\u2019t believe has been judged already, because he has not believed in the name of the only born Son of God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"This is the judgment, that the light has come into the world, and men loved the darkness rather than the light, for their works were evil."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For everyone who does evil hates the light and doesn\u2019t come to the light, lest his works would be exposed."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But he who does the truth comes to the light, that his works may be revealed, that they have been done in God.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Jesus came with his disciples into the land of Judea. He stayed there with them and baptized."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"John also was baptizing in Enon near Salim, because there was much water there. They came and were baptized;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"for John was not yet thrown into prison."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Therefore a dispute arose on the part of John\u2019s disciples with some Jews about purification."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They came to John and said to him, \u201cRabbi, he who was with you beyond the Jordan, to whom you have testified, behold, he baptizes, and everyone is coming to him.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"John answered, \u201cA man can receive nothing unless it has been given him from heaven."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You yourselves testify that I said, \u2018I am not the Christ,\u2019 but, \u2018I have been sent before him.\u2019"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He who has the bride is the bridegroom; but the friend of the bridegroom, who stands and hears him, rejoices greatly because of the bridegroom\u2019s voice. Therefore my joy is made full."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"He must increase, but I must decrease."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe who comes from above is above all. He who is from the earth belongs to the earth and speaks of the earth. He who comes from heaven is above all."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"What he has seen and heard, of that he testifies; and no one receives his witness."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"He who has received his witness has set his seal to this, that God is true."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For he whom God has sent speaks the words of God; for God gives the Spirit without measure."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"The Father loves the Son, and has given all things into his hand."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"One who believes in the Son has eternal life, but one who disobeys the Son won\u2019t see life, but the wrath of God remains on him.\u201d"]],f:["The same word can be translated \u201cdisobeys\u201d or \u201cdisbelieves\u201d in this context."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore when the Lord knew that the Pharisees had heard that Jesus was making and baptizing more disciples than John"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"(although Jesus himself didn\u2019t baptize, but his disciples),"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"he left Judea and departed into Galilee."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He needed to pass through Samaria."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So he came to a city of Samaria called Sychar, near the parcel of ground that Jacob gave to his son Joseph."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Jacob\u2019s well was there. Jesus therefore, being tired from his journey, sat down by the well. It was about the sixth hour."]],f:["noon"]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"A woman of Samaria came to draw water. Jesus said to her, \u201cGive me a drink.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For his disciples had gone away into the city to buy food."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The Samaritan woman therefore said to him, \u201cHow is it that you, being a Jew, ask for a drink from me, a Samaritan woman?\u201d (For Jews have no dealings with Samaritans.)"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered her, \u201cIf you knew the gift of God, and who it is who says to you, \u2018Give me a drink,\u2019 you would have asked him, and he would have given you living water.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said to him, \u201cSir, you have nothing to draw with, and the well is deep. So where do you get that living water?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Are you greater than our father Jacob, who gave us the well and drank from it himself, as did his children and his livestock?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered her, \u201cEveryone who drinks of this water will thirst again,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but whoever drinks of the water that I will give him will never thirst again; but the water that I will give him will become in him a well of water springing up to eternal life.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said to him, \u201cSir, give me this water, so that I don\u2019t get thirsty, neither come all the way here to draw.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cGo, call your husband, and come here.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman answered, \u201cI have no husband.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cYou said well, \u2018I have no husband,\u2019"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"for you have had five husbands; and he whom you now have is not your husband. This you have said truly.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said to him, \u201cSir, I perceive that you are a prophet."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Our fathers worshiped in this mountain, and you Jews say that in Jerusalem is the place where people ought to worship.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cWoman, believe me, the hour is coming when neither in this mountain nor in Jerusalem will you worship the Father."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You worship that which you don\u2019t know. We worship that which we know; for salvation is from the Jews."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But the hour comes, and now is, when the true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit and truth, for the Father seeks such to be his worshipers."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"God is spirit, and those who worship him must worship in spirit and truth.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The woman said to him, \u201cI know that Messiah is coming, he who is called Christ. When he has come, he will declare to us all things.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cMessiah\u201d (Hebrew) and \u201cChrist\u201d (Greek) both mean \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cI am he, the one who speaks to you.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Just then, his disciples came. They marveled that he was speaking with a woman; yet no one said, \u201cWhat are you looking for?\u201d or, \u201cWhy do you speak with her?\u201d"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"So the woman left her water pot, went away into the city, and said to the people,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"\u201cCome, see a man who told me everything that I have done. Can this be the Christ?\u201d"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"They went out of the city, and were coming to him."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"In the meanwhile, the disciples urged him, saying, \u201cRabbi, eat.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said to them, \u201cI have food to eat that you don\u2019t know about.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples therefore said to one another, \u201cHas anyone brought him something to eat?\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cMy food is to do the will of him who sent me and to accomplish his work."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you say, \u2018There are yet four months until the harvest\u2019? Behold, I tell you, lift up your eyes and look at the fields, that they are white for harvest already."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"He who reaps receives wages and gathers fruit to eternal life, that both he who sows and he who reaps may rejoice together."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For in this the saying is true, \u2018One sows, and another reaps.\u2019"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"I sent you to reap that for which you haven\u2019t labored. Others have labored, and you have entered into their labor.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"From that city many of the Samaritans believed in him because of the word of the woman, who testified, \u201cHe told me everything that I have done.\u201d"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"So when the Samaritans came to him, they begged him to stay with them. He stayed there two days."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Many more believed because of his word."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"They said to the woman, \u201cNow we believe, not because of your speaking; for we have heard for ourselves, and know that this is indeed the Christ, the Savior of the world.\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"After the two days he went out from there and went into Galilee."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"For Jesus himself testified that a prophet has no honor in his own country."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"So when he came into Galilee, the Galileans received him, having seen all the things that he did in Jerusalem at the feast, for they also went to the feast."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Jesus came therefore again to Cana of Galilee, where he made the water into wine. There was a certain nobleman whose son was sick at Capernaum."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"When he heard that Jesus had come out of Judea into Galilee, he went to him and begged him that he would come down and heal his son, for he was at the point of death."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to him, \u201cUnless you people see signs and wonders, you will in no way believe.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"The nobleman said to him, \u201cSir, come down before my child dies.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cGo your way. Your son lives.\u201d The man believed the word that Jesus spoke to him, and he went his way."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"As he was going down, his servants met him and reported, saying \u201cYour child lives!\u201d"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"So he inquired of them the hour when he began to get better. They said therefore to him, \u201cYesterday at the seventh hour, the fever left him.\u201d"]],f:["1:00 p.m."]},{v:53,l:[[0,"So the father knew that it was at that hour in which Jesus said to him, \u201cYour son lives.\u201d He believed, as did his whole house."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"This is again the second sign that Jesus did, having come out of Judea into Galilee."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, there was a feast of the Jews, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now in Jerusalem by the sheep gate, there is a pool, which is called in Hebrew, \u201cBethesda\u201d, having five porches."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In these lay a great multitude of those who were sick, blind, lame, or paralyzed, waiting for the moving of the water;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for an angel went down at certain times into the pool and stirred up the water. Whoever stepped in first after the stirring of the water was healed of whatever disease he had."]],f:["NU omits from \u201cwaiting\u201d in verse 3 to the end of verse 4."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"A certain man was there who had been sick for thirty-eight years."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When Jesus saw him lying there, and knew that he had been sick for a long time, he asked him, \u201cDo you want to be made well?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The sick man answered him, \u201cSir, I have no one to put me into the pool when the water is stirred up, but while I\u2019m coming, another steps down before me.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cArise, take up your mat, and walk.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately, the man was made well, and took up his mat and walked."],[0,"Now that day was a Sabbath."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So the Jews said to him who was cured, \u201cIt is the Sabbath. It is not lawful for you to carry the mat.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cHe who made me well said to me, \u2018Take up your mat and walk.\u2019 \u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they asked him, \u201cWho is the man who said to you, \u2018Take up your mat and walk\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But he who was healed didn\u2019t know who it was, for Jesus had withdrawn, a crowd being in the place."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Afterward Jesus found him in the temple and said to him, \u201cBehold, you are made well. Sin no more, so that nothing worse happens to you.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The man went away, and told the Jews that it was Jesus who had made him well."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For this cause the Jews persecuted Jesus and sought to kill him, because he did these things on the Sabbath."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But Jesus answered them, \u201cMy Father is still working, so I am working, too.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause therefore the Jews sought all the more to kill him, because he not only broke the Sabbath, but also called God his own Father, making himself equal with God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore answered them, \u201cMost certainly, I tell you, the Son can do nothing of himself, but what he sees the Father doing. For whatever things he does, these the Son also does likewise."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For the Father has affection for the Son, and shows him all things that he himself does. He will show him greater works than these, that you may marvel."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For as the Father raises the dead and gives them life, even so the Son also gives life to whom he desires."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For the Father judges no one, but he has given all judgment to the Son,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"that all may honor the Son, even as they honor the Father. He who doesn\u2019t honor the Son doesn\u2019t honor the Father who sent him."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMost certainly I tell you, he who hears my word and believes him who sent me has eternal life, and doesn\u2019t come into judgment, but has passed out of death into life."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, the hour comes, and now is, when the dead will hear the Son of God\u2019s voice; and those who hear will live."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For as the Father has life in himself, even so he gave to the Son also to have life in himself."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He also gave him authority to execute judgment, because he is a son of man."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t marvel at this, for the hour comes in which all who are in the tombs will hear his voice"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"and will come out; those who have done good, to the resurrection of life; and those who have done evil, to the resurrection of judgment."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"I can of myself do nothing. As I hear, I judge; and my judgment is righteous, because I don\u2019t seek my own will, but the will of my Father who sent me."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIf I testify about myself, my witness is not valid."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"It is another who testifies about me. I know that the testimony which he testifies about me is true."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"You have sent to John, and he has testified to the truth."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But the testimony which I receive is not from man. However, I say these things that you may be saved."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"He was the burning and shining lamp, and you were willing to rejoice for a while in his light."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"But the testimony which I have is greater than that of John; for the works which the Father gave me to accomplish, the very works that I do, testify about me, that the Father has sent me."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"The Father himself, who sent me, has testified about me. You have neither heard his voice at any time, nor seen his form."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"You don\u2019t have his word living in you, because you don\u2019t believe him whom he sent."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou search the Scriptures, because you think that in them you have eternal life; and these are they which testify about me."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Yet you will not come to me, that you may have life."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"I don\u2019t receive glory from men."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"But I know you, that you don\u2019t have God\u2019s love in yourselves."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"I have come in my Father\u2019s name, and you don\u2019t receive me. If another comes in his own name, you will receive him."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"How can you believe, who receive glory from one another, and you don\u2019t seek the glory that comes from the only God?"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t think that I will accuse you to the Father. There is one who accuses you, even Moses, on whom you have set your hope."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"For if you believed Moses, you would believe me; for he wrote about me."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"But if you don\u2019t believe his writings, how will you believe my words?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Jesus went away to the other side of the sea of Galilee, which is also called the Sea of Tiberias."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"A great multitude followed him, because they saw his signs which he did on those who were sick."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jesus went up into the mountain, and he sat there with his disciples."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now the Passover, the feast of the Jews, was at hand."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore, lifting up his eyes and seeing that a great multitude was coming to him, said to Philip, \u201cWhere are we to buy bread, that these may eat?\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said this to test him, for he himself knew what he would do."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Philip answered him, \u201cTwo hundred denarii worth of bread is not sufficient for them, that every one of them may receive a little.\u201d"]],f:["A denarius was a silver coin worth about a day\u2019s wages for an agricultural laborer, so 200 denarii would be between 6 and 7 month\u2019s pay."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"One of his disciples, Andrew, Simon Peter\u2019s brother, said to him,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"\u201cThere is a boy here who has five barley loaves and two fish, but what are these among so many?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said, \u201cHave the people sit down.\u201d Now there was much grass in that place. So the men sat down, in number about five thousand."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Jesus took the loaves, and having given thanks, he distributed to the disciples, and the disciples to those who were sitting down, likewise also of the fish as much as they desired."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"When they were filled, he said to his disciples, \u201cGather up the broken pieces which are left over, that nothing be lost.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"So they gathered them up, and filled twelve baskets with broken pieces from the five barley loaves, which were left over by those who had eaten."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When therefore the people saw the sign which Jesus did, they said, \u201cThis is truly the prophet who comes into the world.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore, perceiving that they were about to come and take him by force to make him king, withdrew again to the mountain by himself."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"When evening came, his disciples went down to the sea."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They entered into the boat, and were going over the sea to Capernaum. It was now dark, and Jesus had not come to them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The sea was tossed by a great wind blowing."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When therefore they had rowed about twenty-five or thirty stadia, they saw Jesus walking on the sea and drawing near to the boat; and they were afraid."]],f:["25 to 30 stadia is about 5 to 6 kilometers or about 3 to 4 miles"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But he said to them, \u201cIt is I. Don\u2019t be afraid.\u201d"]],f:["or, I AM"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They were willing therefore to receive him into the boat. Immediately the boat was at the land where they were going."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day, the multitude that stood on the other side of the sea saw that there was no other boat there, except the one in which his disciples had embarked, and that Jesus hadn\u2019t entered with his disciples into the boat, but his disciples had gone away alone."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"However, boats from Tiberias came near to the place where they ate the bread after the Lord had given thanks."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When the multitude therefore saw that Jesus wasn\u2019t there, nor his disciples, they themselves got into the boats and came to Capernaum, seeking Jesus."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When they found him on the other side of the sea, they asked him, \u201cRabbi, when did you come here?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, you seek me, not because you saw signs, but because you ate of the loaves and were filled."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t work for the food which perishes, but for the food which remains to eternal life, which the Son of Man will give to you. For God the Father has sealed him.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They said therefore to him, \u201cWhat must we do, that we may work the works of God?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cThis is the work of God, that you believe in him whom he has sent.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"They said therefore to him, \u201cWhat then do you do for a sign, that we may see and believe you? What work do you do?"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Our fathers ate the manna in the wilderness. As it is written, \u2018He gave them bread out of heaven to eat.\u2019\u201d"]],f:["Greek and Hebrew use the same word for \u201cheaven\u201d, \u201cthe heavens\u201d, \u201cthe sky\u201d, and \u201cthe air\u201d."]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them, \u201cMost certainly, I tell you, it wasn\u2019t Moses who gave you the bread out of heaven, but my Father gives you the true bread out of heaven."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"For the bread of God is that which comes down out of heaven and gives life to the world.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"They said therefore to him, \u201cLord, always give us this bread.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cI am the bread of life. Whoever comes to me will not be hungry, and whoever believes in me will never be thirsty."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"But I told you that you have seen me, and yet you don\u2019t believe."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"All those whom the Father gives me will come to me. He who comes to me I will in no way throw out."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"For I have come down from heaven, not to do my own will, but the will of him who sent me."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"This is the will of my Father who sent me, that of all he has given to me I should lose nothing, but should raise him up at the last day."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"This is the will of the one who sent me, that everyone who sees the Son and believes in him should have eternal life; and I will raise him up at the last day.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore murmured concerning him, because he said, \u201cI am the bread which came down out of heaven.\u201d"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cIsn\u2019t this Jesus, the son of Joseph, whose father and mother we know? How then does he say, \u2018I have come down out of heaven\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Jesus answered them, \u201cDon\u2019t murmur among yourselves."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"No one can come to me unless the Father who sent me draws him; and I will raise him up in the last day."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"It is written in the prophets, \u2018They will all be taught by God.\u2019 Therefore everyone who hears from the Father and has learned, comes to me."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Not that anyone has seen the Father, except he who is from God. He has seen the Father."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"Most certainly, I tell you, he who believes in me has eternal life."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"I am the bread of life."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"Your fathers ate the manna in the wilderness and they died."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"This is the bread which comes down out of heaven, that anyone may eat of it and not die."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"I am the living bread which came down out of heaven. If anyone eats of this bread, he will live forever. Yes, the bread which I will give for the life of the world is my flesh.\u201d"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore contended with one another, saying, \u201cHow can this man give us his flesh to eat?\u201d"]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, unless you eat the flesh of the Son of Man and drink his blood, you don\u2019t have life in yourselves."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"He who eats my flesh and drinks my blood has eternal life, and I will raise him up at the last day."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"For my flesh is food indeed, and my blood is drink indeed."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"He who eats my flesh and drinks my blood lives in me, and I in him."]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"As the living Father sent me, and I live because of the Father, so he who feeds on me will also live because of me."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"This is the bread which came down out of heaven\u2014not as our fathers ate the manna and died. He who eats this bread will live forever.\u201d"]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"He said these things in the synagogue, as he taught in Capernaum."]]},{v:60,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore many of his disciples, when they heard this, said, \u201cThis is a hard saying! Who can listen to it?\u201d"]]},{v:61,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus knowing in himself that his disciples murmured at this, said to them, \u201cDoes this cause you to stumble?"]]},{v:62,l:[[0,"Then what if you would see the Son of Man ascending to where he was before?"]]},{v:63,l:[[0,"It is the spirit who gives life. The flesh profits nothing. The words that I speak to you are spirit, and are life."]]},{v:64,l:[[0,"But there are some of you who don\u2019t believe.\u201d For Jesus knew from the beginning who they were who didn\u2019t believe, and who it was who would betray him."]]},{v:65,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cFor this cause I have said to you that no one can come to me, unless it is given to him by my Father.\u201d"]]},{v:66,p:1,l:[[0,"At this, many of his disciples went back and walked no more with him."]]},{v:67,l:[[0,"Jesus said therefore to the twelve, \u201cYou don\u2019t also want to go away, do you?\u201d"]]},{v:68,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter answered him, \u201cLord, to whom would we go? You have the words of eternal life."]]},{v:69,l:[[0,"We have come to believe and know that you are the Christ, the Son of the living God.\u201d"]]},{v:70,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cDidn\u2019t I choose you, the twelve, and one of you is a devil?\u201d"]]},{v:71,l:[[0,"Now he spoke of Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot, for it was he who would betray him, being one of the twelve."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Jesus was walking in Galilee, for he wouldn\u2019t walk in Judea, because the Jews sought to kill him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now the feast of the Jews, the Feast of Booths, was at hand."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His brothers therefore said to him, \u201cDepart from here and go into Judea, that your disciples also may see your works which you do."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For no one does anything in secret while he seeks to be known openly. If you do these things, reveal yourself to the world.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For even his brothers didn\u2019t believe in him."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them, \u201cMy time has not yet come, but your time is always ready."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The world can\u2019t hate you, but it hates me, because I testify about it, that its works are evil."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You go up to the feast. I am not yet going up to this feast, because my time is not yet fulfilled.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Having said these things to them, he stayed in Galilee."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But when his brothers had gone up to the feast, then he also went up, not publicly, but as it were in secret."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore sought him at the feast, and said, \u201cWhere is he?\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"There was much murmuring among the multitudes concerning him. Some said, \u201cHe is a good man.\u201d Others said, \u201cNot so, but he leads the multitude astray.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Yet no one spoke openly of him for fear of the Jews."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But when it was now the middle of the feast, Jesus went up into the temple and taught."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore marveled, saying, \u201cHow does this man know letters, having never been educated?\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore answered them, \u201cMy teaching is not mine, but his who sent me."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If anyone desires to do his will, he will know about the teaching, whether it is from God or if I am speaking from myself."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He who speaks from himself seeks his own glory, but he who seeks the glory of him who sent him is true, and no unrighteousness is in him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Didn\u2019t Moses give you the law, and yet none of you keeps the law? Why do you seek to kill me?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The multitude answered, \u201cYou have a demon! Who seeks to kill you?\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cI did one work and you all marvel because of it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Moses has given you circumcision (not that it is of Moses, but of the fathers), and on the Sabbath you circumcise a boy."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If a boy receives circumcision on the Sabbath, that the law of Moses may not be broken, are you angry with me because I made a man completely healthy on the Sabbath?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t judge according to appearance, but judge righteous judgment.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore some of them of Jerusalem said, \u201cIsn\u2019t this he whom they seek to kill?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Behold, he speaks openly, and they say nothing to him. Can it be that the rulers indeed know that this is truly the Christ?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"However, we know where this man comes from, but when the Christ comes, no one will know where he comes from.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore cried out in the temple, teaching and saying, \u201cYou both know me, and know where I am from. I have not come of myself, but he who sent me is true, whom you don\u2019t know."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I know him, because I am from him, and he sent me.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"They sought therefore to take him; but no one laid a hand on him, because his hour had not yet come."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But of the multitude, many believed in him. They said, \u201cWhen the Christ comes, he won\u2019t do more signs than those which this man has done, will he?\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The Pharisees heard the multitude murmuring these things concerning him, and the chief priests and the Pharisees sent officers to arrest him."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus said, \u201cI will be with you a little while longer, then I go to him who sent me."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"You will seek me and won\u2019t find me. You can\u2019t come where I am.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore said among themselves, \u201cWhere will this man go that we won\u2019t find him? Will he go to the Dispersion among the Greeks and teach the Greeks?"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"What is this word that he said, \u2018You will seek me, and won\u2019t find me;\u2019 and \u2018Where I am, you can\u2019t come\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the last and greatest day of the feast, Jesus stood and cried out, \u201cIf anyone is thirsty, let him come to me and drink!"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He who believes in me, as the Scripture has said, from within him will flow rivers of living water.\u201d"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But he said this about the Spirit, which those believing in him were to receive. For the Holy Spirit was not yet given, because Jesus wasn\u2019t yet glorified."]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Many of the multitude therefore, when they heard these words, said, \u201cThis is truly the prophet.\u201d"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Others said, \u201cThis is the Christ.\u201d But some said, \u201cWhat, does the Christ come out of Galilee?"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Hasn\u2019t the Scripture said that the Christ comes of the offspring of David, and from Bethlehem, the village where David was?\u201d"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:43,l:[[0,"So a division arose in the multitude because of him."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"Some of them would have arrested him, but no one laid hands on him."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"The officers therefore came to the chief priests and Pharisees; and they said to them, \u201cWhy didn\u2019t you bring him?\u201d"]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"The officers answered, \u201cNo man ever spoke like this man!\u201d"]]},{v:47,p:1,l:[[0,"The Pharisees therefore answered them, \u201cYou aren\u2019t also led astray, are you?"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"Have any of the rulers or any of the Pharisees believed in him?"]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"But this multitude that doesn\u2019t know the law is cursed.\u201d"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[0,"Nicodemus (he who came to him by night, being one of them) said to them,"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"\u201cDoes our law judge a man unless it first hears from him personally and knows what he does?\u201d"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered him, \u201cAre you also from Galilee? Search and see that no prophet has arisen out of Galilee.\u201d"]]},{v:53,p:1,l:[[0,"Everyone went to his own house,"]]}],[{v:1,l:[[0,"but Jesus went to the Mount of Olives."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Now very early in the morning, he came again into the temple, and all the people came to him. He sat down and taught them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The scribes and the Pharisees brought a woman taken in adultery. Having set her in the middle,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"they told him, \u201cTeacher, we found this woman in adultery, in the very act."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now in our law, Moses commanded us to stone such women. What then do you say about her?\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They said this testing him, that they might have something to accuse him of."],[0,"But Jesus stooped down and wrote on the ground with his finger."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But when they continued asking him, he looked up and said to them, \u201cHe who is without sin among you, let him throw the first stone at her.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Again he stooped down and wrote on the ground with his finger."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"They, when they heard it, being convicted by their conscience, went out one by one, beginning from the oldest, even to the last. Jesus was left alone with the woman where she was, in the middle."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Jesus, standing up, saw her and said, \u201cWoman, where are your accusers? Did no one condemn you?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"She said, \u201cNo one, Lord.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said, \u201cNeither do I condemn you. Go your way. From now on, sin no more.\u201d"]],f:["NU includes John 7:53\u2013John 8:11, but puts brackets around it to indicate that the textual critics had less confidence that this was original."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, therefore, Jesus spoke to them, saying, \u201cI am the light of the world. He who follows me will not walk in the darkness, but will have the light of life.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The Pharisees therefore said to him, \u201cYou testify about yourself. Your testimony is not valid.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cEven if I testify about myself, my testimony is true, for I know where I came from, and where I am going; but you don\u2019t know where I came from, or where I am going."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You judge according to the flesh. I judge no one."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Even if I do judge, my judgment is true, for I am not alone, but I am with the Father who sent me."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"It\u2019s also written in your law that the testimony of two people is valid."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I am one who testifies about myself, and the Father who sent me testifies about me.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They said therefore to him, \u201cWhere is your Father?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cYou know neither me nor my Father. If you knew me, you would know my Father also.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Jesus spoke these words in the treasury, as he taught in the temple. Yet no one arrested him, because his hour had not yet come."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Jesus said therefore again to them, \u201cI am going away, and you will seek me, and you will die in your sins. Where I go, you can\u2019t come.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore said, \u201cWill he kill himself, because he says, \u2018Where I am going, you can\u2019t come\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cYou are from beneath. I am from above. You are of this world. I am not of this world."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"I said therefore to you that you will die in your sins; for unless you believe that I am he, you will die in your sins.\u201d"]],f:["or, I AM"]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"They said therefore to him, \u201cWho are you?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cJust what I have been saying to you from the beginning."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I have many things to speak and to judge concerning you. However, he who sent me is true; and the things which I heard from him, these I say to the world.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t understand that he spoke to them about the Father."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them, \u201cWhen you have lifted up the Son of Man, then you will know that I am he, and I do nothing of myself, but as my Father taught me, I say these things."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He who sent me is with me. The Father hasn\u2019t left me alone, for I always do the things that are pleasing to him.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"As he spoke these things, many believed in him."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to those Jews who had believed him, \u201cIf you remain in my word, then you are truly my disciples."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"You will know the truth, and the truth will make you free.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered him, \u201cWe are Abraham\u2019s offspring, and have never been in bondage to anyone. How do you say, \u2018You will be made free\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cMost certainly I tell you, everyone who commits sin is the bondservant of sin."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"A bondservant doesn\u2019t live in the house forever. A son remains forever."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"If therefore the Son makes you free, you will be free indeed."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"I know that you are Abraham\u2019s offspring, yet you seek to kill me, because my word finds no place in you."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"I say the things which I have seen with my Father; and you also do the things which you have seen with your father.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered him, \u201cOur father is Abraham.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cIf you were Abraham\u2019s children, you would do the works of Abraham."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"But now you seek to kill me, a man who has told you the truth which I heard from God. Abraham didn\u2019t do this."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"You do the works of your father.\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cWe were not born of sexual immorality. We have one Father, God.\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Jesus said to them, \u201cIf God were your father, you would love me, for I came out and have come from God. For I haven\u2019t come of myself, but he sent me."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Why don\u2019t you understand my speech? Because you can\u2019t hear my word."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"You are of your father the devil, and you want to do the desires of your father. He was a murderer from the beginning, and doesn\u2019t stand in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaks a lie, he speaks on his own; for he is a liar, and the father of lies."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"But because I tell the truth, you don\u2019t believe me."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Which of you convicts me of sin? If I tell the truth, why do you not believe me?"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"He who is of God hears the words of God. For this cause you don\u2019t hear, because you are not of God.\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Jews answered him, \u201cDon\u2019t we say well that you are a Samaritan, and have a demon?\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cI don\u2019t have a demon, but I honor my Father and you dishonor me."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"But I don\u2019t seek my own glory. There is one who seeks and judges."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Most certainly, I tell you, if a person keeps my word, he will never see death.\u201d"]]},{v:52,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the Jews said to him, \u201cNow we know that you have a demon. Abraham died, as did the prophets; and you say, \u2018If a man keeps my word, he will never taste of death.\u2019"]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"Are you greater than our father Abraham, who died? The prophets died. Who do you make yourself out to be?\u201d"]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cIf I glorify myself, my glory is nothing. It is my Father who glorifies me, of whom you say that he is our God."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"You have not known him, but I know him. If I said, \u2018I don\u2019t know him,\u2019 I would be like you, a liar. But I know him and keep his word."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Your father Abraham rejoiced to see my day. He saw it and was glad.\u201d"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore said to him, \u201cYou are not yet fifty years old! Have you seen Abraham?\u201d"]]},{v:58,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cMost certainly, I tell you, before Abraham came into existence, I AM.\u201d"]]},{v:59,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore they took up stones to throw at him, but Jesus hid himself and went out of the temple, having gone through the middle of them, and so passed by."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"As he passed by, he saw a man blind from birth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"His disciples asked him, \u201cRabbi, who sinned, this man or his parents, that he was born blind?\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cThis man didn\u2019t sin, nor did his parents, but that the works of God might be revealed in him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I must work the works of him who sent me while it is day. The night is coming, when no one can work."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"While I am in the world, I am the light of the world.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When he had said this, he spat on the ground, made mud with the saliva, anointed the blind man\u2019s eyes with the mud,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u201cGo, wash in the pool of Siloam\u201d (which means \u201cSent\u201d). So he went away, washed, and came back seeing."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the neighbors and those who saw that he was blind before said, \u201cIsn\u2019t this he who sat and begged?\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Others were saying, \u201cIt is he.\u201d Still others were saying, \u201cHe looks like him.\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am he.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"They therefore were asking him, \u201cHow were your eyes opened?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cA man called Jesus made mud, anointed my eyes, and said to me, \u2018Go to the pool of Siloam and wash.\u2019 So I went away and washed, and I received sight.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they asked him, \u201cWhere is he?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"They brought him who had been blind to the Pharisees."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"It was a Sabbath when Jesus made the mud and opened his eyes."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Again therefore the Pharisees also asked him how he received his sight. He said to them, \u201cHe put mud on my eyes, I washed, and I see.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Some therefore of the Pharisees said, \u201cThis man is not from God, because he doesn\u2019t keep the Sabbath.\u201d"],[0,"Others said, \u201cHow can a man who is a sinner do such signs?\u201d So there was division among them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore they asked the blind man again, \u201cWhat do you say about him, because he opened your eyes?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cHe is a prophet.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore didn\u2019t believe concerning him, that he had been blind and had received his sight, until they called the parents of him who had received his sight,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and asked them, \u201cIs this your son, whom you say was born blind? How then does he now see?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"His parents answered them, \u201cWe know that this is our son, and that he was born blind;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"but how he now sees, we don\u2019t know; or who opened his eyes, we don\u2019t know. He is of age. Ask him. He will speak for himself.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"His parents said these things because they feared the Jews; for the Jews had already agreed that if any man would confess him as Christ, he would be put out of the synagogue."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Therefore his parents said, \u201cHe is of age. Ask him.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"So they called the man who was blind a second time, and said to him, \u201cGive glory to God. We know that this man is a sinner.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He therefore answered, \u201cI don\u2019t know if he is a sinner. One thing I do know: that though I was blind, now I see.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him again, \u201cWhat did he do to you? How did he open your eyes?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered them, \u201cI told you already, and you didn\u2019t listen. Why do you want to hear it again? You don\u2019t also want to become his disciples, do you?\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They insulted him and said, \u201cYou are his disciple, but we are disciples of Moses."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"We know that God has spoken to Moses. But as for this man, we don\u2019t know where he comes from.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"The man answered them, \u201cHow amazing! You don\u2019t know where he comes from, yet he opened my eyes."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"We know that God doesn\u2019t listen to sinners, but if anyone is a worshiper of God and does his will, he listens to him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Since the world began it has never been heard of that anyone opened the eyes of someone born blind."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"If this man were not from God, he could do nothing.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered him, \u201cYou were altogether born in sins, and do you teach us?\u201d Then they threw him out."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus heard that they had thrown him out, and finding him, he said, \u201cDo you believe in the Son of God?\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"He answered, \u201cWho is he, Lord, that I may believe in him?\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cYou have both seen him, and it is he who speaks with you.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cLord, I believe!\u201d and he worshiped him."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said, \u201cI came into this world for judgment, that those who don\u2019t see may see; and that those who see may become blind.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Those of the Pharisees who were with him heard these things, and said to him, \u201cAre we also blind?\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cIf you were blind, you would have no sin; but now you say, \u2018We see.\u2019 Therefore your sin remains."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMost certainly, I tell you, one who doesn\u2019t enter by the door into the sheep fold, but climbs up some other way, is a thief and a robber."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But one who enters in by the door is the shepherd of the sheep."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The gatekeeper opens the gate for him, and the sheep listen to his voice. He calls his own sheep by name and leads them out."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Whenever he brings out his own sheep, he goes before them; and the sheep follow him, for they know his voice."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They will by no means follow a stranger, but will flee from him; for they don\u2019t know the voice of strangers.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Jesus spoke this parable to them, but they didn\u2019t understand what he was telling them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them again, \u201cMost certainly, I tell you, I am the sheep\u2019s door."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All who came before me are thieves and robbers, but the sheep didn\u2019t listen to them."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I am the door. If anyone enters in by me, he will be saved, and will go in and go out and will find pasture."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The thief only comes to steal, kill, and destroy. I came that they may have life, and may have it abundantly."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI am the good shepherd. The good shepherd lays down his life for the sheep."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He who is a hired hand, and not a shepherd, who doesn\u2019t own the sheep, sees the wolf coming, leaves the sheep, and flees. The wolf snatches the sheep and scatters them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The hired hand flees because he is a hired hand and doesn\u2019t care for the sheep."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I am the good shepherd. I know my own, and I\u2019m known by my own;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"even as the Father knows me, and I know the Father. I lay down my life for the sheep."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I have other sheep which are not of this fold. I must bring them also, and they will hear my voice. They will become one flock with one shepherd."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Therefore the Father loves me, because I lay down my life, that I may take it again."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"No one takes it away from me, but I lay it down by myself. I have power to lay it down, and I have power to take it again. I received this commandment from my Father.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore a division arose again among the Jews because of these words."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Many of them said, \u201cHe has a demon and is insane! Why do you listen to him?\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Others said, \u201cThese are not the sayings of one possessed by a demon. It isn\u2019t possible for a demon to open the eyes of the blind, is it?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"It was the Feast of the Dedication at Jerusalem."]],f:["The \u201cFeast of the Dedication\u201d is the Greek name for \u201cHanukkah\u201d, a celebration of the rededication of the Temple."]},{v:23,l:[[0,"It was winter, and Jesus was walking in the temple, in Solomon\u2019s porch."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore came around him and said to him, \u201cHow long will you hold us in suspense? If you are the Christ, tell us plainly.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cI told you, and you don\u2019t believe. The works that I do in my Father\u2019s name, these testify about me."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But you don\u2019t believe, because you are not of my sheep, as I told you."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"My sheep hear my voice, and I know them, and they follow me."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"I give eternal life to them. They will never perish, and no one will snatch them out of my hand."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"My Father who has given them to me is greater than all. No one is able to snatch them out of my Father\u2019s hand."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"I and the Father are one.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Jews took up stones again to stone him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cI have shown you many good works from my Father. For which of those works do you stone me?\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews answered him, \u201cWe don\u2019t stone you for a good work, but for blasphemy, because you, being a man, make yourself God.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cIsn\u2019t it written in your law, \u2018I said, you are gods\u2019?"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"If he called them gods, to whom the word of God came (and the Scripture can\u2019t be broken),"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"do you say of him whom the Father sanctified and sent into the world, \u2018You blaspheme,\u2019 because I said, \u2018I am the Son of God\u2019?"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"If I don\u2019t do the works of my Father, don\u2019t believe me."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But if I do them, though you don\u2019t believe me, believe the works, that you may know and believe that the Father is in me, and I in the Father.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"They sought again to seize him, and he went out of their hand."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"He went away again beyond the Jordan into the place where John was baptizing at first, and he stayed there."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Many came to him. They said, \u201cJohn indeed did no sign, but everything that John said about this man is true.\u201d"]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Many believed in him there."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now a certain man was sick, Lazarus from Bethany, of the village of Mary and her sister, Martha."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"It was that Mary who had anointed the Lord with ointment and wiped his feet with her hair, whose brother Lazarus was sick."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The sisters therefore sent to him, saying, \u201cLord, behold, he for whom you have great affection is sick.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Jesus heard it, he said, \u201cThis sickness is not to death, but for the glory of God, that God\u2019s Son may be glorified by it.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now Jesus loved Martha, and her sister, and Lazarus."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When therefore he heard that he was sick, he stayed two days in the place where he was."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then after this he said to the disciples, \u201cLet\u2019s go into Judea again.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples asked him, \u201cRabbi, the Jews were just trying to stone you. Are you going there again?\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cAren\u2019t there twelve hours of daylight? If a man walks in the day, he doesn\u2019t stumble, because he sees the light of this world."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But if a man walks in the night, he stumbles, because the light isn\u2019t in him.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He said these things, and after that, he said to them, \u201cOur friend Lazarus has fallen asleep, but I am going so that I may awake him out of sleep.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples therefore said, \u201cLord, if he has fallen asleep, he will recover.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Jesus had spoken of his death, but they thought that he spoke of taking rest in sleep."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"So Jesus said to them plainly then, \u201cLazarus is dead."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I am glad for your sakes that I was not there, so that you may believe. Nevertheless, let\u2019s go to him.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Thomas therefore, who is called Didymus, said to his fellow disciples, \u201cLet\u2019s also go, that we may die with him.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cDidymus\u201d means \u201cTwin\u201d."]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"So when Jesus came, he found that he had been in the tomb four days already."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now Bethany was near Jerusalem, about fifteen stadia away."]],f:["15 stadia is about 2.8 kilometers or 1.7 miles"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Many of the Jews had joined the women around Martha and Mary, to console them concerning their brother."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Then when Martha heard that Jesus was coming, she went and met him, but Mary stayed in the house."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Therefore Martha said to Jesus, \u201cLord, if you would have been here, my brother wouldn\u2019t have died."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Even now I know that whatever you ask of God, God will give you.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cYour brother will rise again.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Martha said to him, \u201cI know that he will rise again in the resurrection at the last day.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cI am the resurrection and the life. He who believes in me will still live, even if he dies."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Whoever lives and believes in me will never die. Do you believe this?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"She said to him, \u201cYes, Lord. I have come to believe that you are the Christ, God\u2019s Son, he who comes into the world.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"When she had said this, she went away and called Mary, her sister, secretly, saying, \u201cThe Teacher is here and is calling you.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When she heard this, she arose quickly and went to him."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Now Jesus had not yet come into the village, but was in the place where Martha met him."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Then the Jews who were with her in the house and were consoling her, when they saw Mary, that she rose up quickly and went out, followed her, saying, \u201cShe is going to the tomb to weep there.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore when Mary came to where Jesus was and saw him, she fell down at his feet, saying to him, \u201cLord, if you would have been here, my brother wouldn\u2019t have died.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus therefore saw her weeping, and the Jews weeping who came with her, he groaned in the spirit and was troubled,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cWhere have you laid him?\u201d"],[0,"They told him, \u201cLord, come and see.\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus wept."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews therefore said, \u201cSee how much affection he had for him!\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Some of them said, \u201cCouldn\u2019t this man, who opened the eyes of him who was blind, have also kept this man from dying?\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore, again groaning in himself, came to the tomb. Now it was a cave, and a stone lay against it."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Jesus said, \u201cTake away the stone.\u201d"],[0,"Martha, the sister of him who was dead, said to him, \u201cLord, by this time there is a stench, for he has been dead four days.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cDidn\u2019t I tell you that if you believed, you would see God\u2019s glory?\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"So they took away the stone from the place where the dead man was lying. Jesus lifted up his eyes and said, \u201cFather, I thank you that you listened to me."]],f:["NU omits \u201cfrom the place where the dead man was lying.\u201d"]},{v:42,l:[[0,"I know that you always listen to me, but because of the multitude standing around I said this, that they may believe that you sent me.\u201d"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"When he had said this, he cried with a loud voice, \u201cLazarus, come out!\u201d"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"He who was dead came out, bound hand and foot with wrappings, and his face was wrapped around with a cloth."],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cFree him, and let him go.\u201d"]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore many of the Jews who came to Mary and saw what Jesus did believed in him."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"But some of them went away to the Pharisees and told them the things which Jesus had done."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"The chief priests therefore and the Pharisees gathered a council, and said, \u201cWhat are we doing? For this man does many signs."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"If we leave him alone like this, everyone will believe in him, and the Romans will come and take away both our place and our nation.\u201d"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[0,"But a certain one of them, Caiaphas, being high priest that year, said to them, \u201cYou know nothing at all,"]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"nor do you consider that it is advantageous for us that one man should die for the people, and that the whole nation not perish.\u201d"]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"Now he didn\u2019t say this of himself, but being high priest that year, he prophesied that Jesus would die for the nation,"]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"and not for the nation only, but that he might also gather together into one the children of God who are scattered abroad."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"So from that day forward they took counsel that they might put him to death."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore walked no more openly among the Jews, but departed from there into the country near the wilderness, to a city called Ephraim. He stayed there with his disciples."]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the Passover of the Jews was at hand. Many went up from the country to Jerusalem before the Passover, to purify themselves."]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"Then they sought for Jesus and spoke with one another as they stood in the temple, \u201cWhat do you think\u2014that he isn\u2019t coming to the feast at all?\u201d"]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"Now the chief priests and the Pharisees had commanded that if anyone knew where he was, he should report it, that they might seize him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then, six days before the Passover, Jesus came to Bethany, where Lazarus was, who had been dead, whom he raised from the dead."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"So they made him a supper there. Martha served, but Lazarus was one of those who sat at the table with him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore Mary took a pound of ointment of pure nard, very precious, and anointed Jesus\u2019 feet and wiped his feet with her hair. The house was filled with the fragrance of the ointment."]],f:["a Roman pound of 12 ounces, or about 340 grams"]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Judas Iscariot, Simon\u2019s son, one of his disciples, who would betray him, said,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cWhy wasn\u2019t this ointment sold for three hundred denarii and given to the poor?\u201d"]],f:["300 denarii was about a year\u2019s wages for an agricultural laborer."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now he said this, not because he cared for the poor, but because he was a thief, and having the money box, used to steal what was put into it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But Jesus said, \u201cLeave her alone. She has kept this for the day of my burial."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For you always have the poor with you, but you don\u2019t always have me.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"A large crowd therefore of the Jews learned that he was there; and they came, not for Jesus\u2019 sake only, but that they might see Lazarus also, whom he had raised from the dead."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But the chief priests conspired to put Lazarus to death also,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"because on account of him many of the Jews went away and believed in Jesus."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"On the next day a great multitude had come to the feast. When they heard that Jesus was coming to Jerusalem,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"they took the branches of the palm trees and went out to meet him, and cried out, \u201cHosanna! Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord, the King of Israel!\u201d"]],f:["\u201cHosanna\u201d means \u201csave us\u201d or \u201chelp us, we pray\u201d."]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus, having found a young donkey, sat on it. As it is written,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, daughter of Zion. Behold, your King comes, sitting on a donkey\u2019s colt.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"His disciples didn\u2019t understand these things at first, but when Jesus was glorified, then they remembered that these things were written about him, and that they had done these things to him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The multitude therefore that was with him when he called Lazarus out of the tomb and raised him from the dead was testifying about it."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For this cause also the multitude went and met him, because they heard that he had done this sign."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The Pharisees therefore said among themselves, \u201cSee how you accomplish nothing. Behold, the world has gone after him.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there were certain Greeks among those who went up to worship at the feast."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Therefore, these came to Philip, who was from Bethsaida of Galilee, and asked him, saying, \u201cSir, we want to see Jesus.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Philip came and told Andrew, and in turn, Andrew came with Philip, and they told Jesus."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cThe time has come for the Son of Man to be glorified."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, unless a grain of wheat falls into the earth and dies, it remains by itself alone. But if it dies, it bears much fruit."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He who loves his life will lose it. He who hates his life in this world will keep it to eternal life."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"If anyone serves me, let him follow me. Where I am, there my servant will also be. If anyone serves me, the Father will honor him."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow my soul is troubled. What shall I say? \u2018Father, save me from this time\u2019? But I came to this time for this cause."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Father, glorify your name!\u201d"],[0,"Then a voice came out of the sky, saying, \u201cI have both glorified it and will glorify it again.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the multitude who stood by and heard it said that it had thundered. Others said, \u201cAn angel has spoken to him.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cThis voice hasn\u2019t come for my sake, but for your sakes."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Now is the judgment of this world. Now the prince of this world will be cast out."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"And I, if I am lifted up from the earth, will draw all people to myself.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"But he said this, signifying by what kind of death he should die."]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"The multitude answered him, \u201cWe have heard out of the law that the Christ remains forever. How do you say, \u2018The Son of Man must be lifted up\u2019? Who is this Son of Man?\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them, \u201cYet a little while the light is with you. Walk while you have the light, that darkness doesn\u2019t overtake you. He who walks in the darkness doesn\u2019t know where he is going."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"While you have the light, believe in the light, that you may become children of light.\u201d Jesus said these things, and he departed and hid himself from them."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"But though he had done so many signs before them, yet they didn\u2019t believe in him,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"that the word of Isaiah the prophet might be fulfilled, which he spoke:"],[1,"\u201cLord, who has believed our report?"],[2,"To whom has the arm of the Lord been revealed?\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause they couldn\u2019t believe, for Isaiah said again:"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cHe has blinded their eyes and he hardened their heart,"],[2,"lest they should see with their eyes,"],[2,"and perceive with their heart,"],[2,"and would turn,"],[2,"and I would heal them.\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah said these things when he saw his glory, and spoke of him."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, even many of the rulers believed in him, but because of the Pharisees they didn\u2019t confess it, so that they wouldn\u2019t be put out of the synagogue,"]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"for they loved men\u2019s praise more than God\u2019s praise."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus cried out and said, \u201cWhoever believes in me, believes not in me, but in him who sent me."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"He who sees me sees him who sent me."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"I have come as a light into the world, that whoever believes in me may not remain in the darkness."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"If anyone listens to my sayings and doesn\u2019t believe, I don\u2019t judge him. For I came not to judge the world, but to save the world."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He who rejects me, and doesn\u2019t receive my sayings, has one who judges him. The word that I spoke will judge him in the last day."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"For I spoke not from myself, but the Father who sent me gave me a commandment, what I should say and what I should speak."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"I know that his commandment is eternal life. The things therefore which I speak, even as the Father has said to me, so I speak.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now before the feast of the Passover, Jesus, knowing that his time had come that he would depart from this world to the Father, having loved his own who were in the world, he loved them to the end."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"During supper, the devil having already put into the heart of Judas Iscariot, Simon\u2019s son, to betray him,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Jesus, knowing that the Father had given all things into his hands, and that he came from God and was going to God,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"arose from supper, and laid aside his outer garments. He took a towel and wrapped a towel around his waist."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Then he poured water into the basin, and began to wash the disciples\u2019 feet and to wipe them with the towel that was wrapped around him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then he came to Simon Peter. He said to him, \u201cLord, do you wash my feet?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cYou don\u2019t know what I am doing now, but you will understand later.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter said to him, \u201cYou will never wash my feet!\u201d"],[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cIf I don\u2019t wash you, you have no part with me.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter said to him, \u201cLord, not my feet only, but also my hands and my head!\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cSomeone who has bathed only needs to have his feet washed, but is completely clean. You are clean, but not all of you.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For he knew him who would betray him; therefore he said, \u201cYou are not all clean.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So when he had washed their feet, put his outer garment back on, and sat down again, he said to them, \u201cDo you know what I have done to you?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You call me, \u2018Teacher\u2019 and \u2018Lord.\u2019 You say so correctly, for so I am."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If I then, the Lord and the Teacher, have washed your feet, you also ought to wash one another\u2019s feet."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For I have given you an example, that you should also do as I have done to you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, a servant is not greater than his lord, neither is one who is sent greater than he who sent him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If you know these things, blessed are you if you do them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I don\u2019t speak concerning all of you. I know whom I have chosen; but that the Scripture may be fulfilled, \u2018He who eats bread with me has lifted up his heel against me.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"From now on, I tell you before it happens, that when it happens, you may believe that I am he."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, he who receives whomever I send, receives me; and he who receives me, receives him who sent me.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had said this, he was troubled in spirit, and testified, \u201cMost certainly I tell you that one of you will betray me.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The disciples looked at one another, perplexed about whom he spoke."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"One of his disciples, whom Jesus loved, was at the table, leaning against Jesus\u2019 chest."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Simon Peter therefore beckoned to him, and said to him, \u201cTell us who it is of whom he speaks.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"He, leaning back, as he was, on Jesus\u2019 chest, asked him, \u201cLord, who is it?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore answered, \u201cIt is he to whom I will give this piece of bread when I have dipped it.\u201d So when he had dipped the piece of bread, he gave it to Judas, the son of Simon Iscariot."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"After the piece of bread, then Satan entered into him."],[0,"Then Jesus said to him, \u201cWhat you do, do quickly.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Now nobody at the table knew why he said this to him."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For some thought, because Judas had the money box, that Jesus said to him, \u201cBuy what things we need for the feast,\u201d or that he should give something to the poor."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Therefore having received that morsel, he went out immediately. It was night."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had gone out, Jesus said, \u201cNow the Son of Man has been glorified, and God has been glorified in him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"If God has been glorified in him, God will also glorify him in himself, and he will glorify him immediately."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Little children, I will be with you a little while longer. You will seek me, and as I said to the Jews, \u2018Where I am going, you can\u2019t come,\u2019 so now I tell you."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"A new commandment I give to you, that you love one another. Just as I have loved you, you also love one another."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"By this everyone will know that you are my disciples, if you have love for one another.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter said to him, \u201cLord, where are you going?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cWhere I am going, you can\u2019t follow now, but you will follow afterwards.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter said to him, \u201cLord, why can\u2019t I follow you now? I will lay down my life for you.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cWill you lay down your life for me? Most certainly I tell you, the rooster won\u2019t crow until you have denied me three times."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t let your heart be troubled. Believe in God. Believe also in me."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"In my Father\u2019s house are many homes. If it weren\u2019t so, I would have told you. I am going to prepare a place for you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If I go and prepare a place for you, I will come again and will receive you to myself; that where I am, you may be there also."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You know where I go, and you know the way.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Thomas said to him, \u201cLord, we don\u2019t know where you are going. How can we know the way?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cI am the way, the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father, except through me."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If you had known me, you would have known my Father also. From now on, you know him and have seen him.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Philip said to him, \u201cLord, show us the Father, and that will be enough for us.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cHave I been with you such a long time, and do you not know me, Philip? He who has seen me has seen the Father. How do you say, \u2018Show us the Father\u2019?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you believe that I am in the Father, and the Father in me? The words that I tell you, I speak not from myself; but the Father who lives in me does his works."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Believe me that I am in the Father, and the Father in me; or else believe me for the very works\u2019 sake."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, he who believes in me, the works that I do, he will do also; and he will do greater works than these, because I am going to my Father."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Whatever you will ask in my name, I will do it, that the Father may be glorified in the Son."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If you will ask anything in my name, I will do it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If you love me, keep my commandments."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I will pray to the Father, and he will give you another Counselor, that he may be with you forever:"]],f:["Greek \u03c0\u03b1\u03c1\u03b1\u03ba\u03bb\u03b7\u03c4\u03bf\u03bd: Counselor, Helper, Intercessor, Advocate, and Comforter."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"the Spirit of truth, whom the world can\u2019t receive, for it doesn\u2019t see him and doesn\u2019t know him. You know him, for he lives with you and will be in you."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I will not leave you orphans. I will come to you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Yet a little while, and the world will see me no more; but you will see me. Because I live, you will live also."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"In that day you will know that I am in my Father, and you in me, and I in you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"One who has my commandments and keeps them, that person is one who loves me. One who loves me will be loved by my Father, and I will love him, and will reveal myself to him.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Judas (not Iscariot) said to him, \u201cLord, what has happened that you are about to reveal yourself to us, and not to the world?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cIf a man loves me, he will keep my word. My Father will love him, and we will come to him and make our home with him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He who doesn\u2019t love me doesn\u2019t keep my words. The word which you hear isn\u2019t mine, but the Father\u2019s who sent me."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI have said these things to you while still living with you."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But the Counselor, the Holy Spirit, whom the Father will send in my name, will teach you all things, and will remind you of all that I said to you."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Peace I leave with you. My peace I give to you; not as the world gives, I give to you. Don\u2019t let your heart be troubled, neither let it be fearful."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"You heard how I told you, \u2018I am going away, and I will come back to you.\u2019 If you loved me, you would have rejoiced because I said \u2018I am going to my Father;\u2019 for the Father is greater than I."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Now I have told you before it happens so that when it happens, you may believe."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"I will no more speak much with you, for the prince of the world comes, and he has nothing in me."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But that the world may know that I love the Father, and as the Father commanded me, even so I do. Arise, let\u2019s go from here."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI am the true vine, and my Father is the farmer."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Every branch in me that doesn\u2019t bear fruit, he takes away. Every branch that bears fruit, he prunes, that it may bear more fruit."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You are already pruned clean because of the word which I have spoken to you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Remain in me, and I in you. As the branch can\u2019t bear fruit by itself unless it remains in the vine, so neither can you, unless you remain in me."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I am the vine. You are the branches. He who remains in me and I in him bears much fruit, for apart from me you can do nothing."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"If a man doesn\u2019t remain in me, he is thrown out as a branch and is withered; and they gather them, throw them into the fire, and they are burned."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"If you remain in me, and my words remain in you, you will ask whatever you desire, and it will be done for you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn this my Father is glorified, that you bear much fruit; and so you will be my disciples."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Even as the Father has loved me, I also have loved you. Remain in my love."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If you keep my commandments, you will remain in my love, even as I have kept my Father\u2019s commandments and remain in his love."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I have spoken these things to you, that my joy may remain in you, and that your joy may be made full."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis is my commandment, that you love one another, even as I have loved you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Greater love has no one than this, that someone lay down his life for his friends."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"You are my friends if you do whatever I command you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"No longer do I call you servants, for the servant doesn\u2019t know what his lord does. But I have called you friends, for everything that I heard from my Father, I have made known to you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"You didn\u2019t choose me, but I chose you and appointed you, that you should go and bear fruit, and that your fruit should remain; that whatever you will ask of the Father in my name, he may give it to you."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI command these things to you, that you may love one another."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"If the world hates you, you know that it has hated me before it hated you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"If you were of the world, the world would love its own. But because you are not of the world, since I chose you out of the world, therefore the world hates you."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Remember the word that I said to you: \u2018A servant is not greater than his lord.\u2019 If they persecuted me, they will also persecute you. If they kept my word, they will also keep yours."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But they will do all these things to you for my name\u2019s sake, because they don\u2019t know him who sent me."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"If I had not come and spoken to them, they would not have had sin; but now they have no excuse for their sin."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He who hates me, hates my Father also."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"If I hadn\u2019t done among them the works which no one else did, they wouldn\u2019t have had sin. But now they have seen and also hated both me and my Father."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But this happened so that the word may be fulfilled which was written in their law, \u2018They hated me without a cause.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen the Counselor has come, whom I will send to you from the Father, the Spirit of truth, who proceeds from the Father, he will testify about me."]],f:["Greek Parakletos: Counselor, Helper, Advocate, Intercessor, and Comforter."]},{v:27,l:[[0,"You will also testify, because you have been with me from the beginning."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI have said these things to you so that you wouldn\u2019t be caused to stumble."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"They will put you out of the synagogues. Yes, the time is coming that whoever kills you will think that he offers service to God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They will do these things because they have not known the Father nor me."]],f:["TR adds \u201cto you\u201d"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But I have told you these things so that when the time comes, you may remember that I told you about them. I didn\u2019t tell you these things from the beginning, because I was with you."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But now I am going to him who sent me, and none of you asks me, \u2018Where are you going?\u2019"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But because I have told you these things, sorrow has filled your heart."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Nevertheless I tell you the truth: It is to your advantage that I go away; for if I don\u2019t go away, the Counselor won\u2019t come to you. But if I go, I will send him to you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"When he has come, he will convict the world about sin, about righteousness, and about judgment;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"about sin, because they don\u2019t believe in me;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"about righteousness, because I am going to my Father, and you won\u2019t see me any more;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"about judgment, because the prince of this world has been judged."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI still have many things to tell you, but you can\u2019t bear them now."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"However, when he, the Spirit of truth, has come, he will guide you into all truth, for he will not speak from himself; but whatever he hears, he will speak. He will declare to you things that are coming."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He will glorify me, for he will take from what is mine and will declare it to you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"All things that the Father has are mine; therefore I said that he takes of mine and will declare it to you."]],f:["TR reads \u201cwill take\u201d instead of \u201ctakes\u201d"]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cA little while, and you will not see me. Again a little while, and you will see me.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of his disciples therefore said to one another, \u201cWhat is this that he says to us, \u2018A little while, and you won\u2019t see me, and again a little while, and you will see me;\u2019 and, \u2018Because I go to the Father\u2019?\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They said therefore, \u201cWhat is this that he says, \u2018A little while\u2019? We don\u2019t know what he is saying.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Jesus perceived that they wanted to ask him, and he said to them, \u201cDo you inquire among yourselves concerning this, that I said, \u2018A little while, and you won\u2019t see me, and again a little while, and you will see me\u2019?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you that you will weep and lament, but the world will rejoice. You will be sorrowful, but your sorrow will be turned into joy."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"A woman, when she gives birth, has sorrow because her time has come. But when she has delivered the child, she doesn\u2019t remember the anguish any more, for the joy that a human being is born into the world."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Therefore you now have sorrow, but I will see you again, and your heart will rejoice, and no one will take your joy away from you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIn that day you will ask me no questions. Most certainly I tell you, whatever you may ask of the Father in my name, he will give it to you."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Until now, you have asked nothing in my name. Ask, and you will receive, that your joy may be made full."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI have spoken these things to you in figures of speech. But the time is coming when I will no more speak to you in figures of speech, but will tell you plainly about the Father."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"In that day you will ask in my name; and I don\u2019t say to you that I will pray to the Father for you,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"for the Father himself loves you, because you have loved me, and have believed that I came from God."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"I came from the Father and have come into the world. Again, I leave the world and go to the Father.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"His disciples said to him, \u201cBehold, now you are speaking plainly, and using no figures of speech."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Now we know that you know all things, and don\u2019t need for anyone to question you. By this we believe that you came from God.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered them, \u201cDo you now believe?"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Behold, the time is coming, yes, and has now come, that you will be scattered, everyone to his own place, and you will leave me alone. Yet I am not alone, because the Father is with me."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"I have told you these things, that in me you may have peace. In the world you have trouble; but cheer up! I have overcome the world.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said these things, then lifting up his eyes to heaven, he said, \u201cFather, the time has come. Glorify your Son, that your Son may also glorify you;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"even as you gave him authority over all flesh, so he will give eternal life to all whom you have given him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This is eternal life, that they should know you, the only true God, and him whom you sent, Jesus Christ."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I glorified you on the earth. I have accomplished the work which you have given me to do."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now, Father, glorify me with your own self with the glory which I had with you before the world existed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI revealed your name to the people whom you have given me out of the world. They were yours, and you have given them to me. They have kept your word."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Now they have known that all things whatever you have given me are from you,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"for the words which you have given me I have given to them; and they received them, and knew for sure that I came from you. They have believed that you sent me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I pray for them. I don\u2019t pray for the world, but for those whom you have given me, for they are yours."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"All things that are mine are yours, and yours are mine, and I am glorified in them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I am no more in the world, but these are in the world, and I am coming to you. Holy Father, keep them through your name which you have given me, that they may be one, even as we are."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"While I was with them in the world, I kept them in your name. I have kept those whom you have given me. None of them is lost except the son of destruction, that the Scripture might be fulfilled."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But now I come to you, and I say these things in the world, that they may have my joy made full in themselves."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I have given them your word. The world hated them because they are not of the world, even as I am not of the world."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I pray not that you would take them from the world, but that you would keep them from the evil one."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They are not of the world, even as I am not of the world."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Sanctify them in your truth. Your word is truth."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"As you sent me into the world, even so I have sent them into the world."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For their sakes I sanctify myself, that they themselves also may be sanctified in truth."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNot for these only do I pray, but for those also who will believe in me through their word,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"that they may all be one; even as you, Father, are in me, and I in you, that they also may be one in us; that the world may believe that you sent me."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The glory which you have given me, I have given to them, that they may be one, even as we are one,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I in them, and you in me, that they may be perfected into one, that the world may know that you sent me and loved them, even as you loved me."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Father, I desire that they also whom you have given me be with me where I am, that they may see my glory which you have given me, for you loved me before the foundation of the world."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Righteous Father, the world hasn\u2019t known you, but I knew you; and these knew that you sent me."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I made known to them your name, and will make it known; that the love with which you loved me may be in them, and I in them.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When Jesus had spoken these words, he went out with his disciples over the brook Kidron, where there was a garden, into which he and his disciples entered."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Now Judas, who betrayed him, also knew the place, for Jesus often met there with his disciples."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Judas then, having taken a detachment of soldiers and officers from the chief priests and the Pharisees, came there with lanterns, torches, and weapons."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore, knowing all the things that were happening to him, went out and said to them, \u201cWho are you looking for?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered him, \u201cJesus of Nazareth.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cI am he.\u201d"],[0,"Judas also, who betrayed him, was standing with them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When therefore he said to them, \u201cI am he,\u201d they went backward and fell to the ground."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Again therefore he asked them, \u201cWho are you looking for?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cJesus of Nazareth.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cI told you that I am he. If therefore you seek me, let these go their way,\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"that the word might be fulfilled which he spoke, \u201cOf those whom you have given me, I have lost none.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter therefore, having a sword, drew it, struck the high priest\u2019s servant, and cut off his right ear. The servant\u2019s name was Malchus."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to Peter, \u201cPut the sword into its sheath. The cup which the Father has given me, shall I not surely drink it?\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So the detachment, the commanding officer, and the officers of the Jews seized Jesus and bound him,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and led him to Annas first, for he was father-in-law to Caiaphas, who was high priest that year."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now it was Caiaphas who advised the Jews that it was expedient that one man should perish for the people."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter followed Jesus, as did another disciple. Now that disciple was known to the high priest, and entered in with Jesus into the court of the high priest;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"but Peter was standing at the door outside. So the other disciple, who was known to the high priest, went out and spoke to her who kept the door, and brought in Peter."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then the maid who kept the door said to Peter, \u201cAre you also one of this man\u2019s disciples?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cI am not.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the servants and the officers were standing there, having made a fire of coals, for it was cold. They were warming themselves. Peter was with them, standing and warming himself."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The high priest therefore asked Jesus about his disciples and about his teaching."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cI spoke openly to the world. I always taught in synagogues and in the temple, where the Jews always meet. I said nothing in secret."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Why do you ask me? Ask those who have heard me what I said to them. Behold, they know the things which I said.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had said this, one of the officers standing by slapped Jesus with his hand, saying, \u201cDo you answer the high priest like that?\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cIf I have spoken evil, testify of the evil; but if well, why do you beat me?\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Annas sent him bound to Caiaphas, the high priest."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Simon Peter was standing and warming himself. They said therefore to him, \u201cYou aren\u2019t also one of his disciples, are you?\u201d"],[0,"He denied it and said, \u201cI am not.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the servants of the high priest, being a relative of him whose ear Peter had cut off, said, \u201cDidn\u2019t I see you in the garden with him?\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter therefore denied it again, and immediately the rooster crowed."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"They led Jesus therefore from Caiaphas into the Praetorium. It was early, and they themselves didn\u2019t enter into the Praetorium, that they might not be defiled, but might eat the Passover."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Pilate therefore went out to them and said, \u201cWhat accusation do you bring against this man?\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"They answered him, \u201cIf this man weren\u2019t an evildoer, we wouldn\u2019t have delivered him up to you.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate therefore said to them, \u201cTake him yourselves, and judge him according to your law.\u201d"],[0,"Therefore the Jews said to him, \u201cIt is illegal for us to put anyone to death,\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"that the word of Jesus might be fulfilled, which he spoke, signifying by what kind of death he should die."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate therefore entered again into the Praetorium, called Jesus, and said to him, \u201cAre you the King of the Jews?\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered him, \u201cDo you say this by yourself, or did others tell you about me?\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate answered, \u201cI\u2019m not a Jew, am I? Your own nation and the chief priests delivered you to me. What have you done?\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cMy Kingdom is not of this world. If my Kingdom were of this world, then my servants would fight, that I wouldn\u2019t be delivered to the Jews. But now my Kingdom is not from here.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate therefore said to him, \u201cAre you a king then?\u201d"],[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cYou say that I am a king. For this reason I have been born, and for this reason I have come into the world, that I should testify to the truth. Everyone who is of the truth listens to my voice.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate said to him, \u201cWhat is truth?\u201d"],[0,"When he had said this, he went out again to the Jews, and said to them, \u201cI find no basis for a charge against him."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But you have a custom that I should release someone to you at the Passover. Therefore, do you want me to release to you the King of the Jews?\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they all shouted again, saying, \u201cNot this man, but Barabbas!\u201d Now Barabbas was a robber."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"So Pilate then took Jesus and flogged him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The soldiers twisted thorns into a crown and put it on his head, and dressed him in a purple garment."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They kept saying, \u201cHail, King of the Jews!\u201d and they kept slapping him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Pilate went out again, and said to them, \u201cBehold, I bring him out to you, that you may know that I find no basis for a charge against him.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore came out, wearing the crown of thorns and the purple garment. Pilate said to them, \u201cBehold, the man!\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When therefore the chief priests and the officers saw him, they shouted, saying, \u201cCrucify! Crucify!\u201d"],[0,"Pilate said to them, \u201cTake him yourselves and crucify him, for I find no basis for a charge against him.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews answered him, \u201cWe have a law, and by our law he ought to die, because he made himself the Son of God.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"When therefore Pilate heard this saying, he was more afraid."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He entered into the Praetorium again, and said to Jesus, \u201cWhere are you from?\u201d But Jesus gave him no answer."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Pilate therefore said to him, \u201cAren\u2019t you speaking to me? Don\u2019t you know that I have power to release you and have power to crucify you?\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus answered, \u201cYou would have no power at all against me, unless it were given to you from above. Therefore he who delivered me to you has greater sin.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"At this, Pilate was seeking to release him, but the Jews cried out, saying, \u201cIf you release this man, you aren\u2019t Caesar\u2019s friend! Everyone who makes himself a king speaks against Caesar!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When Pilate therefore heard these words, he brought Jesus out and sat down on the judgment seat at a place called \u201cThe Pavement\u201d, but in Hebrew, \u201cGabbatha.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now it was the Preparation Day of the Passover, at about the sixth hour. He said to the Jews, \u201cBehold, your King!\u201d"]],f:["\u201cthe sixth hour\u201d would have been 6:00 a.m. according to the Roman timekeeping system, or noon for the Jewish timekeeping system in use, then."]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"They cried out, \u201cAway with him! Away with him! Crucify him!\u201d"],[0,"Pilate said to them, \u201cShall I crucify your King?\u201d"],[0,"The chief priests answered, \u201cWe have no king but Caesar!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"So then he delivered him to them to be crucified. So they took Jesus and led him away."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He went out, bearing his cross, to the place called \u201cThe Place of a Skull\u201d, which is called in Hebrew, \u201cGolgotha\u201d,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"where they crucified him, and with him two others, on either side one, and Jesus in the middle."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Pilate wrote a title also, and put it on the cross. There was written, \u201cJESUS OF NAZARETH, THE KING OF THE JEWS.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Therefore many of the Jews read this title, for the place where Jesus was crucified was near the city; and it was written in Hebrew, in Latin, and in Greek."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The chief priests of the Jews therefore said to Pilate, \u201cDon\u2019t write, \u2018The King of the Jews,\u2019 but, \u2018he said, \u201cI am King of the Jews.\u201d\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Pilate answered, \u201cWhat I have written, I have written.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Then the soldiers, when they had crucified Jesus, took his garments and made four parts, to every soldier a part; and also the tunic. Now the tunic was without seam, woven from the top throughout."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then they said to one another, \u201cLet\u2019s not tear it, but cast lots for it to decide whose it will be,\u201d that the Scripture might be fulfilled, which says,"],[1,"\u201cThey parted my garments among them."],[2,"They cast lots for my clothing.\u201d"],[0,"Therefore the soldiers did these things."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But standing by Jesus\u2019 cross were his mother, his mother\u2019s sister, Mary the wife of Clopas, and Mary Magdalene."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Therefore when Jesus saw his mother, and the disciple whom he loved standing there, he said to his mother, \u201cWoman, behold, your son!\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Then he said to the disciple, \u201cBehold, your mother!\u201d From that hour, the disciple took her to his own home."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, Jesus, seeing that all things were now finished, that the Scripture might be fulfilled, said, \u201cI am thirsty!\u201d"]],f:["NU, TR read \u201cknowing\u201d instead of \u201cseeing\u201d"]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Now a vessel full of vinegar was set there; so they put a sponge full of the vinegar on hyssop, and held it at his mouth."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When Jesus therefore had received the vinegar, he said, \u201cIt is finished!\u201d Then he bowed his head and gave up his spirit."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore the Jews, because it was the Preparation Day, so that the bodies wouldn\u2019t remain on the cross on the Sabbath (for that Sabbath was a special one), asked of Pilate that their legs might be broken and that they might be taken away."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Therefore the soldiers came and broke the legs of the first and of the other who was crucified with him;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"but when they came to Jesus and saw that he was already dead, they didn\u2019t break his legs."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"However, one of the soldiers pierced his side with a spear, and immediately blood and water came out."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"He who has seen has testified, and his testimony is true. He knows that he tells the truth, that you may believe."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"For these things happened that the Scripture might be fulfilled, \u201cA bone of him will not be broken.\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Again another Scripture says, \u201cThey will look on him whom they pierced.\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Joseph of Arimathaea, being a disciple of Jesus, but secretly for fear of the Jews, asked of Pilate that he might take away Jesus\u2019 body. Pilate gave him permission. He came therefore and took away his body."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Nicodemus, who at first came to Jesus by night, also came bringing a mixture of myrrh and aloes, about a hundred Roman pounds."]],f:["100 Roman pounds of 12 ounces each, or about 72 pounds, or 33 Kilograms."]},{v:40,l:[[0,"So they took Jesus\u2019 body, and bound it in linen cloths with the spices, as the custom of the Jews is to bury."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"Now in the place where he was crucified there was a garden. In the garden was a new tomb in which no man had ever yet been laid."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"Then, because of the Jews\u2019 Preparation Day (for the tomb was near at hand), they laid Jesus there."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the first day of the week, Mary Magdalene went early, while it was still dark, to the tomb, and saw that the stone had been taken away from the tomb."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore she ran and came to Simon Peter and to the other disciple whom Jesus loved, and said to them, \u201cThey have taken away the Lord out of the tomb, and we don\u2019t know where they have laid him!\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Peter and the other disciple went out, and they went toward the tomb."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They both ran together. The other disciple outran Peter and came to the tomb first."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Stooping and looking in, he saw the linen cloths lying there; yet he didn\u2019t enter in."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then Simon Peter came, following him, and entered into the tomb. He saw the linen cloths lying,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and the cloth that had been on his head, not lying with the linen cloths, but rolled up in a place by itself."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"So then the other disciple who came first to the tomb also entered in, and he saw and believed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For as yet they didn\u2019t know the Scripture, that he must rise from the dead."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So the disciples went away again to their own homes."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But Mary was standing outside at the tomb weeping. So as she wept, she stooped and looked into the tomb,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and she saw two angels in white sitting, one at the head and one at the feet, where the body of Jesus had lain."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"They asked her, \u201cWoman, why are you weeping?\u201d"],[0,"She said to them, \u201cBecause they have taken away my Lord, and I don\u2019t know where they have laid him.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When she had said this, she turned around and saw Jesus standing, and didn\u2019t know that it was Jesus."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cWoman, why are you weeping? Who are you looking for?\u201d"],[0,"She, supposing him to be the gardener, said to him, \u201cSir, if you have carried him away, tell me where you have laid him, and I will take him away.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cMary.\u201d"],[0,"She turned and said to him, \u201cRabboni!\u201d which is to say, \u201cTeacher!\u201d"]],f:["Rabboni is a transliteration of the Aramaic word for \u201cgreat teacher.\u201d","or, Master"]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to her, \u201cDon\u2019t hold me, for I haven\u2019t yet ascended to my Father; but go to my brothers and tell them, \u2018I am ascending to my Father and your Father, to my God and your God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Mary Magdalene came and told the disciples that she had seen the Lord, and that he had said these things to her."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When therefore it was evening on that day, the first day of the week, and when the doors were locked where the disciples were assembled, for fear of the Jews, Jesus came and stood in the middle and said to them, \u201cPeace be to you.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had said this, he showed them his hands and his side. The disciples therefore were glad when they saw the Lord."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them again, \u201cPeace be to you. As the Father has sent me, even so I send you.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When he had said this, he breathed on them, and said to them, \u201cReceive the Holy Spirit!"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If you forgive anyone\u2019s sins, they have been forgiven them. If you retain anyone\u2019s sins, they have been retained.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"But Thomas, one of the twelve, called Didymus, wasn\u2019t with them when Jesus came."]],f:["or, Twin"]},{v:25,l:[[0,"The other disciples therefore said to him, \u201cWe have seen the Lord!\u201d"],[0,"But he said to them, \u201cUnless I see in his hands the print of the nails, put my finger into the print of the nails, and put my hand into his side, I will not believe.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"After eight days, again his disciples were inside and Thomas was with them. Jesus came, the doors being locked, and stood in the middle, and said, \u201cPeace be to you.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Then he said to Thomas, \u201cReach here your finger, and see my hands. Reach here your hand, and put it into my side. Don\u2019t be unbelieving, but believing.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Thomas answered him, \u201cMy Lord and my God!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cBecause you have seen me, you have believed. Blessed are those who have not seen and have believed.\u201d"]],f:["TR adds \u201cThomas,\u201d"]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore Jesus did many other signs in the presence of his disciples, which are not written in this book;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"but these are written that you may believe that Jesus is the Christ, the Son of God, and that believing you may have life in his name."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, Jesus revealed himself again to the disciples at the sea of Tiberias. He revealed himself this way."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Simon Peter, Thomas called Didymus, Nathanael of Cana in Galilee, and the sons of Zebedee, and two others of his disciples were together."]],f:["or, Twin"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Simon Peter said to them, \u201cI\u2019m going fishing.\u201d"],[0,"They told him, \u201cWe are also coming with you.\u201d They immediately went out and entered into the boat. That night, they caught nothing."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But when day had already come, Jesus stood on the beach; yet the disciples didn\u2019t know that it was Jesus."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Jesus therefore said to them, \u201cChildren, have you anything to eat?\u201d"],[0,"They answered him, \u201cNo.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cCast the net on the right side of the boat, and you will find some.\u201d"],[0,"They cast it therefore, and now they weren\u2019t able to draw it in for the multitude of fish."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"That disciple therefore whom Jesus loved said to Peter, \u201cIt\u2019s the Lord!\u201d"],[0,"So when Simon Peter heard that it was the Lord, he wrapped his coat around himself (for he was naked), and threw himself into the sea."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But the other disciples came in the little boat (for they were not far from the land, but about two hundred cubits away), dragging the net full of fish."]],f:["200 cubits is about 100 yards or about 91 meters"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So when they got out on the land, they saw a fire of coals there, with fish and bread laid on it."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cBring some of the fish which you have just caught.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter went up, and drew the net to land, full of one hundred fifty-three great fish. Even though there were so many, the net wasn\u2019t torn."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to them, \u201cCome and eat breakfast!\u201d"],[0,"None of the disciples dared inquire of him, \u201cWho are you?\u201d knowing that it was the Lord."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Jesus came and took the bread, gave it to them, and the fish likewise."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"This is now the third time that Jesus was revealed to his disciples after he had risen from the dead."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So when they had eaten their breakfast, Jesus said to Simon Peter, \u201cSimon, son of Jonah, do you love me more than these?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cYes, Lord; you know that I have affection for you.\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cFeed my lambs.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He said to him again a second time, \u201cSimon, son of Jonah, do you love me?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cYes, Lord; you know that I have affection for you.\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cTend my sheep.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He said to him the third time, \u201cSimon, son of Jonah, do you have affection for me?\u201d"],[0,"Peter was grieved because he asked him the third time, \u201cDo you have affection for me?\u201d He said to him, \u201cLord, you know everything. You know that I have affection for you.\u201d"],[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cFeed my sheep."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Most certainly I tell you, when you were young, you dressed yourself and walked where you wanted to. But when you are old, you will stretch out your hands, and another will dress you and carry you where you don\u2019t want to go.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Now he said this, signifying by what kind of death he would glorify God. When he had said this, he said to him, \u201cFollow me.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Peter, turning around, saw a disciple following. This was the disciple whom Jesus loved, the one who had also leaned on Jesus\u2019 chest at the supper and asked, \u201cLord, who is going to betray you?\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Peter, seeing him, said to Jesus, \u201cLord, what about this man?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Jesus said to him, \u201cIf I desire that he stay until I come, what is that to you? You follow me.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"This saying therefore went out among the brothers that this disciple wouldn\u2019t die. Yet Jesus didn\u2019t say to him that he wouldn\u2019t die, but, \u201cIf I desire that he stay until I come, what is that to you?\u201d"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here may be also correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the disciple who testifies about these things, and wrote these things. We know that his witness is true."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"There are also many other things which Jesus did, which if they would all be written, I suppose that even the world itself wouldn\u2019t have room for the books that would be written."]]}]]}},1314,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,n,s){h.exports={book:"Acts",name:"Acts",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The first book I wrote, Theophilus, concerned all that Jesus began both to do and to teach,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"until the day in which he was received up, after he had given commandment through the Holy Spirit to the apostles whom he had chosen."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"To these he also showed himself alive after he suffered, by many proofs, appearing to them over a period of forty days and speaking about God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Being assembled together with them, he commanded them, \u201cDon\u2019t depart from Jerusalem, but wait for the promise of the Father, which you heard from me."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For John indeed baptized in water, but you will be baptized in the Holy Spirit not many days from now.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, when they had come together, they asked him, \u201cLord, are you now restoring the kingdom to Israel?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cIt isn\u2019t for you to know times or seasons which the Father has set within his own authority."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit has come upon you. You will be witnesses to me in Jerusalem, in all Judea and Samaria, and to the uttermost parts of the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had said these things, as they were looking, he was taken up, and a cloud received him out of their sight."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"While they were looking steadfastly into the sky as he went, behold, two men stood by them in white clothing,"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"who also said, \u201cYou men of Galilee, why do you stand looking into the sky? This Jesus, who was received up from you into the sky, will come back in the same way as you saw him going into the sky.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then they returned to Jerusalem from the mountain called Olivet, which is near Jerusalem, a Sabbath day\u2019s journey away."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When they had come in, they went up into the upper room where they were staying, that is Peter, John, James, Andrew, Philip, Thomas, Bartholomew, Matthew, James the son of Alphaeus, Simon the Zealot, and Judas the son of James."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"All these with one accord continued steadfastly in prayer and supplication, along with the women and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with his brothers."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"In these days, Peter stood up in the middle of the disciples (and the number of names was about one hundred twenty), and said,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cBrothers, it was necessary that this Scripture should be fulfilled, which the Holy Spirit spoke before by the mouth of David concerning Judas, who was guide to those who took Jesus."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For he was counted with us, and received his portion in this ministry."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now this man obtained a field with the reward for his wickedness; and falling headlong, his body burst open and all his intestines gushed out."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"It became known to everyone who lived in Jerusalem that in their language that field was called \u2018Akeldama,\u2019 that is, \u2018The field of blood.\u2019"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For it is written in the book of Psalms,"],[1,"\u2018Let his habitation be made desolate."],[2,"Let no one dwell in it;\u2019"],[0,"and,"],[1,"\u2018Let another take his office.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOf the men therefore who have accompanied us all the time that the Lord Jesus went in and out among us,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"beginning from the baptism of John to the day that he was received up from us, of these one must become a witness with us of his resurrection.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"They put forward two: Joseph called Barsabbas, who was also called Justus, and Matthias."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"They prayed and said, \u201cYou, Lord, who know the hearts of all men, show which one of these two you have chosen"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"to take part in this ministry and apostleship from which Judas fell away, that he might go to his own place.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"They drew lots for them, and the lot fell on Matthias; and he was counted with the eleven apostles."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when the day of Pentecost had come, they were all with one accord in one place."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Suddenly there came from the sky a sound like the rushing of a mighty wind, and it filled all the house where they were sitting."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Tongues like fire appeared and were distributed to them, and one sat on each of them."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak with other languages, as the Spirit gave them the ability to speak."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there were dwelling in Jerusalem Jews, devout men, from every nation under the sky."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When this sound was heard, the multitude came together and were bewildered, because everyone heard them speaking in his own language."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They were all amazed and marveled, saying to one another, \u201cBehold, aren\u2019t all these who speak Galileans?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"How do we hear, everyone in our own native language?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Parthians, Medes, Elamites, and people from Mesopotamia, Judea, Cappadocia, Pontus, Asia,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Phrygia, Pamphylia, Egypt, the parts of Libya around Cyrene, visitors from Rome, both Jews and proselytes,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Cretans and Arabians\u2014we hear them speaking in our languages the mighty works of God!\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They were all amazed and were perplexed, saying to one another, \u201cWhat does this mean?\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Others, mocking, said, \u201cThey are filled with new wine.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter, standing up with the eleven, lifted up his voice and spoke out to them, \u201cYou men of Judea and all you who dwell at Jerusalem, let this be known to you, and listen to my words."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For these aren\u2019t drunken, as you suppose, seeing it is only the third hour of the day."]],f:["about 9:00 a.m."]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But this is what has been spoken through the prophet Joel:"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018It will be in the last days, says God,"],[2,"that I will pour out my Spirit on all flesh."],[1,"Your sons and your daughters will prophesy."],[2,"Your young men will see visions."],[2,"Your old men will dream dreams."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"Yes, and on my servants and on my handmaidens in those days,"],[2,"I will pour out my Spirit, and they will prophesy."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[1,"I will show wonders in the sky above,"],[2,"and signs on the earth beneath:"],[2,"blood, and fire, and billows of smoke."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[1,"The sun will be turned into darkness,"],[2,"and the moon into blood,"],[2,"before the great and glorious day of the Lord comes."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[1,"It will be that whoever will call on the name of the Lord will be saved.\u2019"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cMen of Israel, hear these words! Jesus of Nazareth, a man approved by God to you by mighty works and wonders and signs which God did by him among you, even as you yourselves know,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"him, being delivered up by the determined counsel and foreknowledge of God, you have taken by the hand of lawless men, crucified and killed;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"whom God raised up, having freed him from the agony of death, because it was not possible that he should be held by it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For David says concerning him,"],[1,"\u2018I saw the Lord always before my face,"],[2,"for he is on my right hand, that I should not be moved."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore my heart was glad, and my tongue rejoiced."],[2,"Moreover my flesh also will dwell in hope,"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"because you will not leave my soul in Hades,"],[2,"neither will you allow your Holy One to see decay."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"You made known to me the ways of life."],[2,"You will make me full of gladness with your presence.\u2019"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBrothers, I may tell you freely of the patriarch David, that he both died and was buried, and his tomb is with us to this day."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Therefore, being a prophet, and knowing that God had sworn with an oath to him that of the fruit of his body, according to the flesh, he would raise up the Christ to sit on his throne,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:31,l:[[0,"he foreseeing this, spoke about the resurrection of the Christ, that his soul wasn\u2019t left in Hades, and his flesh didn\u2019t see decay."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:32,l:[[0,"This Jesus God raised up, to which we all are witnesses."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Being therefore exalted by the right hand of God, and having received from the Father the promise of the Holy Spirit, he has poured out this which you now see and hear."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For David didn\u2019t ascend into the heavens, but he says himself,"],[1,"\u2018The Lord said to my Lord, \u201cSit by my right hand"]]},{v:35,l:[[2,"until I make your enemies a footstool for your feet.\u201d\u2019"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cLet all the house of Israel therefore know certainly that God has made him both Lord and Christ, this Jesus whom you crucified.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when they heard this, they were cut to the heart, and said to Peter and the rest of the apostles, \u201cBrothers, what shall we do?\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter said to them, \u201cRepent and be baptized, every one of you, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of sins, and you will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"For the promise is to you and to your children, and to all who are far off, even as many as the Lord our God will call to himself.\u201d"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"With many other words he testified and exhorted them, saying, \u201cSave yourselves from this crooked generation!\u201d"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[0,"Then those who gladly received his word were baptized. There were added that day about three thousand souls."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"They continued steadfastly in the apostles\u2019 teaching and fellowship, in the breaking of bread, and prayer."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Fear came on every soul, and many wonders and signs were done through the apostles."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"All who believed were together, and had all things in common."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"They sold their possessions and goods, and distributed them to all, according as anyone had need."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"Day by day, continuing steadfastly with one accord in the temple, and breaking bread at home, they took their food with gladness and singleness of heart,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"praising God and having favor with all the people. The Lord added to the assembly day by day those who were being saved."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter and John were going up into the temple at the hour of prayer, the ninth hour."]],f:["3:00 p.m."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"A certain man who was lame from his mother\u2019s womb was being carried, whom they laid daily at the door of the temple which is called Beautiful, to ask gifts for the needy of those who entered into the temple."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Seeing Peter and John about to go into the temple, he asked to receive gifts for the needy."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Peter, fastening his eyes on him, with John, said, \u201cLook at us.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He listened to them, expecting to receive something from them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But Peter said, \u201cI have no silver or gold, but what I have, that I give you. In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, get up and walk!\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He took him by the right hand and raised him up. Immediately his feet and his ankle bones received strength."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Leaping up, he stood and began to walk. He entered with them into the temple, walking, leaping, and praising God."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"All the people saw him walking and praising God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They recognized him, that it was he who used to sit begging for gifts for the needy at the Beautiful Gate of the temple. They were filled with wonder and amazement at what had happened to him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"As the lame man who was healed held on to Peter and John, all the people ran together to them in the porch that is called Solomon\u2019s, greatly wondering."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When Peter saw it, he responded to the people, \u201cYou men of Israel, why do you marvel at this man? Why do you fasten your eyes on us, as though by our own power or godliness we had made him walk?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified his Servant Jesus, whom you delivered up and denied in the presence of Pilate, when he had determined to release him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But you denied the Holy and Righteous One and asked for a murderer to be granted to you,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and killed the Prince of life, whom God raised from the dead, to which we are witnesses."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"By faith in his name, his name has made this man strong, whom you see and know. Yes, the faith which is through him has given him this perfect soundness in the presence of you all."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, brothers, I know that you did this in ignorance, as did also your rulers."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here may be also correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But the things which God announced by the mouth of all his prophets, that Christ should suffer, he thus fulfilled."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cRepent therefore, and turn again, that your sins may be blotted out, so that there may come times of refreshing from the presence of the Lord,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and that he may send Christ Jesus, who was ordained for you before,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"whom heaven must receive until the times of restoration of all things, which God spoke long ago by the mouth of his holy prophets."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For Moses indeed said to the fathers, \u2018The Lord God will raise up a prophet for you from among your brothers, like me. You shall listen to him in all things whatever he says to you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"It will be that every soul that will not listen to that prophet will be utterly destroyed from among the people.\u2019"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Yes, and all the prophets from Samuel and those who followed after, as many as have spoken, also told of these days."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"You are the children of the prophets, and of the covenant which God made with our fathers, saying to Abraham, \u2018All the families of the earth will be blessed through your offspring.\u2019"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:26,l:[[0,"God, having raised up his servant Jesus, sent him to you first to bless you, in turning away every one of you from your wickedness.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"As they spoke to the people, the priests and the captain of the temple and the Sadducees came to them,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"being upset because they taught the people and proclaimed in Jesus the resurrection from the dead."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They laid hands on them, and put them in custody until the next day, for it was now evening."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But many of those who heard the word believed, and the number of the men came to be about five thousand."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"In the morning, their rulers, elders, and scribes were gathered together in Jerusalem."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Annas the high priest was there, with Caiaphas, John, Alexander, and as many as were relatives of the high priest."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When they had stood Peter and John in the middle of them, they inquired, \u201cBy what power, or in what name, have you done this?\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Peter, filled with the Holy Spirit, said to them, \u201cYou rulers of the people and elders of Israel,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"if we are examined today concerning a good deed done to a crippled man, by what means this man has been healed,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"may it be known to you all, and to all the people of Israel, that in the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, whom you crucified, whom God raised from the dead, this man stands here before you whole in him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He is \u2018the stone which was regarded as worthless by you, the builders, which has become the head of the corner.\u2019"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"There is salvation in no one else, for there is no other name under heaven that is given among men, by which we must be saved!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when they saw the boldness of Peter and John, and had perceived that they were unlearned and ignorant men, they marveled. They recognized that they had been with Jesus."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Seeing the man who was healed standing with them, they could say nothing against it."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But when they had commanded them to go aside out of the council, they conferred among themselves,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cWhat shall we do to these men? Because indeed a notable miracle has been done through them, as can be plainly seen by all who dwell in Jerusalem, and we can\u2019t deny it."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But so that this spreads no further among the people, let\u2019s threaten them, that from now on they don\u2019t speak to anyone in this name.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They called them, and commanded them not to speak at all nor teach in the name of Jesus."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter and John answered them, \u201cWhether it is right in the sight of God to listen to you rather than to God, judge for yourselves,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"for we can\u2019t help telling the things which we saw and heard.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had further threatened them, they let them go, finding no way to punish them, because of the people; for everyone glorified God for that which was done."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For the man on whom this miracle of healing was performed was more than forty years old."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Being let go, they came to their own company and reported all that the chief priests and the elders had said to them."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When they heard it, they lifted up their voice to God with one accord and said, \u201cO Lord, you are God, who made the sky, the earth, the sea, and all that is in them;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"who by the mouth of your servant David, said,"],[1,"\u2018Why do the nations rage,"],[2,"and the peoples plot a vain thing?"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"The kings of the earth take a stand,"],[2,"and the rulers plot together,"],[2,"against the Lord, and against his Christ.\u2019"]],f:["Christ (Greek) and Messiah (Hebrew) both mean Anointed One."]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cFor truly, both Herod and Pontius Pilate, with the Gentiles and the people of Israel, were gathered together against your holy servant Jesus, whom you anointed,"]],f:["nu adds \u201cin this city,\u201d"]},{v:28,l:[[0,"to do whatever your hand and your counsel foreordained to happen."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Now, Lord, look at their threats, and grant to your servants to speak your word with all boldness,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"while you stretch out your hand to heal; and that signs and wonders may be done through the name of your holy Servant Jesus.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had prayed, the place was shaken where they were gathered together. They were all filled with the Holy Spirit, and they spoke the word of God with boldness."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"The multitude of those who believed were of one heart and soul. Not one of them claimed that anything of the things which he possessed was his own, but they had all things in common."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"With great power, the apostles gave their testimony of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus. Great grace was on them all."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For neither was there among them any who lacked, for as many as were owners of lands or houses sold them, and brought the proceeds of the things that were sold,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"and laid them at the apostles\u2019 feet; and distribution was made to each, according as anyone had need."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Joses, who by the apostles was also called Barnabas (which is, being interpreted, Son of Encouragement), a Levite, a man of Cyprus by race,"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"having a field, sold it and brought the money and laid it at the apostles\u2019 feet."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But a certain man named Ananias, with Sapphira his wife, sold a possession,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and kept back part of the price, his wife also being aware of it, then brought a certain part and laid it at the apostles\u2019 feet."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But Peter said, \u201cAnanias, why has Satan filled your heart to lie to the Holy Spirit and to keep back part of the price of the land?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"While you kept it, didn\u2019t it remain your own? After it was sold, wasn\u2019t it in your power? How is it that you have conceived this thing in your heart? You haven\u2019t lied to men, but to God.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Ananias, hearing these words, fell down and died. Great fear came on all who heard these things."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The young men arose and wrapped him up, and they carried him out and buried him."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"About three hours later, his wife, not knowing what had happened, came in."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Peter answered her, \u201cTell me whether you sold the land for so much.\u201d"],[0,"She said, \u201cYes, for so much.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter asked her, \u201cHow is it that you have agreed together to tempt the Spirit of the Lord? Behold, the feet of those who have buried your husband are at the door, and they will carry you out.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"She fell down immediately at his feet and died. The young men came in and found her dead, and they carried her out and buried her by her husband."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Great fear came on the whole assembly, and on all who heard these things."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"By the hands of the apostles many signs and wonders were done among the people. They were all with one accord in Solomon\u2019s porch."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"None of the rest dared to join them; however, the people honored them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"More believers were added to the Lord, multitudes of both men and women."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"They even carried out the sick into the streets and laid them on cots and mattresses, so that as Peter came by, at least his shadow might overshadow some of them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The multitude also came together from the cities around Jerusalem, bringing sick people and those who were tormented by unclean spirits; and they were all healed."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But the high priest rose up, and all those who were with him (which is the sect of the Sadducees), and they were filled with jealousy"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and laid hands on the apostles, then put them in public custody."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But an angel of the Lord opened the prison doors by night, and brought them out and said,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"\u201cGo stand and speak in the temple to the people all the words of this life.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When they heard this, they entered into the temple about daybreak and taught. But the high priest and those who were with him came and called the council together, with all the senate of the children of Israel, and sent to the prison to have them brought."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But the officers who came didn\u2019t find them in the prison. They returned and reported,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"\u201cWe found the prison shut and locked, and the guards standing before the doors, but when we opened them, we found no one inside!\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when the high priest, the captain of the temple, and the chief priests heard these words, they were very perplexed about them and what might become of this."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"One came and told them, \u201cBehold, the men whom you put in prison are in the temple, standing and teaching the people.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Then the captain went with the officers, and brought them without violence, for they were afraid that the people might stone them."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had brought them, they set them before the council. The high priest questioned them,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cDidn\u2019t we strictly command you not to teach in this name? Behold, you have filled Jerusalem with your teaching, and intend to bring this man\u2019s blood on us.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter and the apostles answered, \u201cWe must obey God rather than men."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom you killed, hanging him on a tree."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"God exalted him with his right hand to be a Prince and a Savior, to give repentance to Israel, and remission of sins."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"We are his witnesses of these things; and so also is the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those who obey him.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"But they, when they heard this, were cut to the heart, and were determined to kill them."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But one stood up in the council, a Pharisee named Gamaliel, a teacher of the law, honored by all the people, and commanded to put the apostles out for a little while."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cYou men of Israel, be careful concerning these men, what you are about to do."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"For before these days Theudas rose up, making himself out to be somebody; to whom a number of men, about four hundred, joined themselves. He was slain; and all, as many as obeyed him, were dispersed and came to nothing."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"After this man, Judas of Galilee rose up in the days of the enrollment, and drew away some people after him. He also perished, and all, as many as obeyed him, were scattered abroad."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Now I tell you, withdraw from these men and leave them alone. For if this counsel or this work is of men, it will be overthrown."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But if it is of God, you will not be able to overthrow it, and you would be found even to be fighting against God!\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"They agreed with him. Summoning the apostles, they beat them and commanded them not to speak in the name of Jesus, and let them go."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"They therefore departed from the presence of the council, rejoicing that they were counted worthy to suffer dishonor for Jesus\u2019 name."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"Every day, in the temple and at home, they never stopped teaching and preaching Jesus, the Christ."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in those days, when the number of the disciples was multiplying, a complaint arose from the Hellenists against the Hebrews, because their widows were neglected in the daily service."]],f:["The Hellenists used Greek language and culture, even though they were also of Hebrew descent."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The twelve summoned the multitude of the disciples and said, \u201cIt is not appropriate for us to forsake the word of God and serve tables."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore, select from among you, brothers, seven men of good report, full of the Holy Spirit and of wisdom, whom we may appoint over this business."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But we will continue steadfastly in prayer and in the ministry of the word.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"These words pleased the whole multitude. They chose Stephen, a man full of faith and of the Holy Spirit, Philip, Prochorus, Nicanor, Timon, Parmenas, and Nicolaus, a proselyte of Antioch,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"whom they set before the apostles. When they had prayed, they laid their hands on them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The word of God increased and the number of the disciples greatly multiplied in Jerusalem. A great company of the priests were obedient to the faith."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Stephen, full of faith and power, performed great wonders and signs among the people."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But some of those who were of the synagogue called \u201cThe Libertines\u201d, and of the Cyrenians, of the Alexandrians, and of those of Cilicia and Asia arose, disputing with Stephen."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They weren\u2019t able to withstand the wisdom and the Spirit by which he spoke."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Then they secretly induced men to say, \u201cWe have heard him speak blasphemous words against Moses and God.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They stirred up the people, the elders, and the scribes, and came against him and seized him, then brought him in to the council,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and set up false witnesses who said, \u201cThis man never stops speaking blasphemous words against this holy place and the law."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For we have heard him say that this Jesus of Nazareth will destroy this place, and will change the customs which Moses delivered to us.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"All who sat in the council, fastening their eyes on him, saw his face like it was the face of an angel."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The high priest said, \u201cAre these things so?\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cBrothers and fathers, listen. The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham when he was in Mesopotamia, before he lived in Haran,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and said to him, \u2018Get out of your land and away from your relatives, and come into a land which I will show you.\u2019"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then he came out of the land of the Chaldaeans and lived in Haran. From there, when his father was dead, God moved him into this land where you are now living."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He gave him no inheritance in it, no, not so much as to set his foot on. He promised that he would give it to him for a possession, and to his offspring after him, when he still had no child."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"God spoke in this way: that his offspring would live as aliens in a strange land, and that they would be enslaved and mistreated for four hundred years."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"\u2018I will judge the nation to which they will be in bondage,\u2019 said God, \u2018and after that they will come out and serve me in this place.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He gave him the covenant of circumcision. So Abraham became the father of Isaac, and circumcised him the eighth day. Isaac became the father of Jacob, and Jacob became the father of the twelve patriarchs."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe patriarchs, moved with jealousy against Joseph, sold him into Egypt. God was with him"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and delivered him out of all his afflictions, and gave him favor and wisdom before Pharaoh, king of Egypt. He made him governor over Egypt and all his house."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now a famine came over all the land of Egypt and Canaan, and great affliction. Our fathers found no food."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But when Jacob heard that there was grain in Egypt, he sent out our fathers the first time."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"On the second time Joseph was made known to his brothers, and Joseph\u2019s family was revealed to Pharaoh."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Joseph sent and summoned Jacob his father and all his relatives, seventy-five souls."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Jacob went down into Egypt and he died, himself and our fathers;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and they were brought back to Shechem and laid in the tomb that Abraham bought for a price in silver from the children of Hamor of Shechem."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBut as the time of the promise came close which God had sworn to Abraham, the people grew and multiplied in Egypt,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"until there arose a different king who didn\u2019t know Joseph."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The same took advantage of our race and mistreated our fathers, and forced them to abandon their babies, so that they wouldn\u2019t stay alive."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"At that time Moses was born, and was exceedingly handsome to God. He was nourished three months in his father\u2019s house."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"When he was abandoned, Pharaoh\u2019s daughter took him up and reared him as her own son."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Moses was instructed in all the wisdom of the Egyptians. He was mighty in his words and works."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But when he was forty years old, it came into his heart to visit his brothers, the children of Israel."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may be also correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Seeing one of them suffer wrong, he defended him and avenged him who was oppressed, striking the Egyptian."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He supposed that his brothers understood that God, by his hand, was giving them deliverance; but they didn\u2019t understand."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThe day following, he appeared to them as they fought, and urged them to be at peace again, saying, \u2018Sirs, you are brothers. Why do you wrong one another?\u2019"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But he who did his neighbor wrong pushed him away, saying, \u2018Who made you a ruler and a judge over us?"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Do you want to kill me as you killed the Egyptian yesterday?\u2019"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Moses fled at this saying, and became a stranger in the land of Midian, where he became the father of two sons."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen forty years were fulfilled, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in the wilderness of Mount Sinai, in a flame of fire in a bush."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"When Moses saw it, he wondered at the sight. As he came close to see, the voice of the Lord came to him,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"\u2018I am the God of your fathers: the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.\u2019 Moses trembled and dared not look."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"The Lord said to him, \u2018Take off your sandals, for the place where you stand is holy ground."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"I have surely seen the affliction of my people who are in Egypt, and have heard their groaning. I have come down to deliver them. Now come, I will send you into Egypt.\u2019"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis Moses whom they refused, saying, \u2018Who made you a ruler and a judge?\u2019\u2014God has sent him as both a ruler and a deliverer by the hand of the angel who appeared to him in the bush."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"This man led them out, having worked wonders and signs in Egypt, in the Red Sea, and in the wilderness for forty years."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"This is that Moses who said to the children of Israel, \u2018The Lord our God will raise up a prophet for you from among your brothers, like me.\u2019"]],f:["TR adds \u201cYou shall listen to him.\u201d"]},{v:38,l:[[0,"This is he who was in the assembly in the wilderness with the angel that spoke to him on Mount Sinai, and with our fathers, who received living revelations to give to us,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"to whom our fathers wouldn\u2019t be obedient, but rejected him and turned back in their hearts to Egypt,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"saying to Aaron, \u2018Make us gods that will go before us, for as for this Moses who led us out of the land of Egypt, we don\u2019t know what has become of him.\u2019"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"They made a calf in those days, and brought a sacrifice to the idol, and rejoiced in the works of their hands."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"But God turned away and gave them up to serve the army of the sky, as it is written in the book of the prophets,"],[1,"\u2018Did you offer to me slain animals and sacrifices"],[2,"forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel?"]],f:["This idiom could also be translated \u201chost of heaven\u201d, or \u201cangelic beings\u201d, or \u201cheavenly bodies.\u201d"]},{v:43,p:1,l:[[1,"You took up the tabernacle of Moloch,"],[2,"the star of your god Rephan,"],[1,"the figures which you made to worship,"],[2,"so I will carry you away beyond Babylon.\u2019"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOur fathers had the tabernacle of the testimony in the wilderness, even as he who spoke to Moses commanded him to make it according to the pattern that he had seen;"]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"which also our fathers, in their turn, brought in with Joshua when they entered into the possession of the nations whom God drove out before the face of our fathers to the days of David,"]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"who found favor in the sight of God, and asked to find a habitation for the God of Jacob."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"But Solomon built him a house."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"However, the Most High doesn\u2019t dwell in temples made with hands, as the prophet says,"]]},{v:49,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018heaven is my throne,"],[2,"and the earth a footstool for my feet."],[1,"What kind of house will you build me?\u2019 says the Lord."],[2,"\u2018Or what is the place of my rest?"]]},{v:50,p:1,l:[[1,"Didn\u2019t my hand make all these things?\u2019"]]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cYou stiff-necked and uncircumcised in heart and ears, you always resist the Holy Spirit! As your fathers did, so you do."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"Which of the prophets didn\u2019t your fathers persecute? They killed those who foretold the coming of the Righteous One, of whom you have now become betrayers and murderers."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"You received the law as it was ordained by angels, and didn\u2019t keep it!\u201d"]]},{v:54,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when they heard these things, they were cut to the heart, and they gnashed at him with their teeth."]]},{v:55,l:[[0,"But he, being full of the Holy Spirit, looked up steadfastly into heaven and saw the glory of God, and Jesus standing on the right hand of God,"]]},{v:56,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cBehold, I see the heavens opened and the Son of Man standing at the right hand of God!\u201d"]]},{v:57,p:1,l:[[0,"But they cried out with a loud voice and stopped their ears, then rushed at him with one accord."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"They threw him out of the city and stoned him. The witnesses placed their garments at the feet of a young man named Saul."]]},{v:59,l:[[0,"They stoned Stephen as he called out, saying, \u201cLord Jesus, receive my spirit!\u201d"]]},{v:60,l:[[0,"He kneeled down and cried with a loud voice, \u201cLord, don\u2019t hold this sin against them!\u201d When he had said this, he fell asleep."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Saul was consenting to his death. A great persecution arose against the assembly which was in Jerusalem in that day. They were all scattered abroad throughout the regions of Judea and Samaria, except for the apostles."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Devout men buried Stephen and lamented greatly over him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But Saul ravaged the assembly, entering into every house and dragged both men and women off to prison."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Therefore those who were scattered abroad went around preaching the word."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Philip went down to the city of Samaria and proclaimed to them the Christ."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The multitudes listened with one accord to the things that were spoken by Philip when they heard and saw the signs which he did."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For unclean spirits came out of many of those who had them. They came out, crying with a loud voice. Many who had been paralyzed and lame were healed."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"There was great joy in that city."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"But there was a certain man, Simon by name, who used to practice sorcery in the city and amazed the people of Samaria, making himself out to be some great one,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"to whom they all listened, from the least to the greatest, saying, \u201cThis man is that great power of God.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They listened to him because for a long time he had amazed them with his sorceries."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But when they believed Philip preaching good news concerning God\u2019s Kingdom and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Simon himself also believed. Being baptized, he continued with Philip. Seeing signs and great miracles occurring, he was amazed."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when the apostles who were at Jerusalem heard that Samaria had received the word of God, they sent Peter and John to them,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"who, when they had come down, prayed for them, that they might receive the Holy Spirit;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"for as yet he had fallen on none of them. They had only been baptized in the name of Christ Jesus."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Then they laid their hands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now when Simon saw that the Holy Spirit was given through the laying on of the apostles\u2019 hands, he offered them money,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cGive me also this power, that whomever I lay my hands on may receive the Holy Spirit.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But Peter said to him, \u201cMay your silver perish with you, because you thought you could obtain the gift of God with money!"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You have neither part nor lot in this matter, for your heart isn\u2019t right before God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Repent therefore of this, your wickedness, and ask God if perhaps the thought of your heart may be forgiven you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For I see that you are in the poison of bitterness and in the bondage of iniquity.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon answered, \u201cPray for me to the Lord, that none of the things which you have spoken happen to me.\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"They therefore, when they had testified and spoken the word of the Lord, returned to Jerusalem, and preached the Good News to many villages of the Samaritans."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then an angel of the Lord spoke to Philip, saying, \u201cArise, and go toward the south to the way that goes down from Jerusalem to Gaza. This is a desert.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"He arose and went; and behold, there was a man of Ethiopia, a eunuch of great authority under Candace, queen of the Ethiopians, who was over all her treasure, who had come to Jerusalem to worship."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He was returning and sitting in his chariot, and was reading the prophet Isaiah."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"The Spirit said to Philip, \u201cGo near, and join yourself to this chariot.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Philip ran to him, and heard him reading Isaiah the prophet, and said, \u201cDo you understand what you are reading?\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cHow can I, unless someone explains it to me?\u201d He begged Philip to come up and sit with him."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Now the passage of the Scripture which he was reading was this,"],[1,"\u201cHe was led as a sheep to the slaughter."],[2,"As a lamb before his shearer is silent,"],[2,"so he doesn\u2019t open his mouth."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[1,"In his humiliation, his judgment was taken away."],[2,"Who will declare His generation?"],[2,"For his life is taken from the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"The eunuch answered Philip, \u201cWho is the prophet talking about? About himself, or about someone else?\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Philip opened his mouth, and beginning from this Scripture, preached to him about Jesus."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"As they went on the way, they came to some water; and the eunuch said, \u201cBehold, here is water. What is keeping me from being baptized?\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[],f:["TR adds Philip said, \u201cIf you believe with all your heart, you may.\u201d He answered, \u201cI believe that Jesus Christ is the Son of God.\u201d"]},{v:38,l:[[0,"He commanded the chariot to stand still, and they both went down into the water, both Philip and the eunuch, and he baptized him."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"When they came up out of the water, the Spirit of the Lord caught Philip away, and the eunuch didn\u2019t see him any more, for he went on his way rejoicing."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"But Philip was found at Azotus. Passing through, he preached the Good News to all the cities until he came to Caesarea."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But Saul, still breathing threats and slaughter against the disciples of the Lord, went to the high priest"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and asked for letters from him to the synagogues of Damascus, that if he found any who were of the Way, whether men or women, he might bring them bound to Jerusalem."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"As he traveled, he got close to Damascus, and suddenly a light from the sky shone around him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He fell on the earth, and heard a voice saying to him, \u201cSaul, Saul, why do you persecute me?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cWho are you, Lord?\u201d"],[0,"The Lord said, \u201cI am Jesus, whom you are persecuting."]],f:["TR adds \u201cIt\u2019s hard for you to kick against the cattle prods.\u201d"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But rise up and enter into the city, then you will be told what you must do.\u201d"]],f:["TR omits \u201cBut\u201d"]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The men who traveled with him stood speechless, hearing the sound, but seeing no one."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Saul arose from the ground, and when his eyes were opened, he saw no one. They led him by the hand and brought him into Damascus."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He was without sight for three days, and neither ate nor drank."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was a certain disciple at Damascus named Ananias. The Lord said to him in a vision, \u201cAnanias!\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cBehold, it\u2019s me, Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord said to him, \u201cArise and go to the street which is called Straight, and inquire in the house of Judah for one named Saul, a man of Tarsus. For behold, he is praying,"]],f:["or, Judas"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and in a vision he has seen a man named Ananias coming in and laying his hands on him, that he might receive his sight.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But Ananias answered, \u201cLord, I have heard from many about this man, how much evil he did to your saints at Jerusalem."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Here he has authority from the chief priests to bind all who call on your name.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"But the Lord said to him, \u201cGo your way, for he is my chosen vessel to bear my name before the nations and kings, and the children of Israel."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For I will show him how many things he must suffer for my name\u2019s sake.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Ananias departed and entered into the house. Laying his hands on him, he said, \u201cBrother Saul, the Lord, who appeared to you on the road by which you came, has sent me that you may receive your sight and be filled with the Holy Spirit.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Immediately something like scales fell from his eyes, and he received his sight. He arose and was baptized."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He took food and was strengthened."],[0,"Saul stayed several days with the disciples who were at Damascus."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Immediately in the synagogues he proclaimed the Christ, that he is the Son of God."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"All who heard him were amazed, and said, \u201cIsn\u2019t this he who in Jerusalem made havoc of those who called on this name? And he had come here intending to bring them bound before the chief priests!\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But Saul increased more in strength, and confounded the Jews who lived at Damascus, proving that this is the Christ."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When many days were fulfilled, the Jews conspired together to kill him,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"but their plot became known to Saul. They watched the gates both day and night that they might kill him,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"but his disciples took him by night and let him down through the wall, lowering him in a basket."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"When Saul had come to Jerusalem, he tried to join himself to the disciples; but they were all afraid of him, not believing that he was a disciple."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But Barnabas took him and brought him to the apostles, and declared to them how he had seen the Lord on the way, and that he had spoken to him, and how at Damascus he had preached boldly in the name of Jesus."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He was with them entering into Jerusalem,"]],f:["TR and NU add \u201cand going out\u201d"]},{v:29,l:[[0,"preaching boldly in the name of the Lord Jesus. He spoke and disputed against the Hellenists, but they were seeking to kill him."]],f:["TR and NU omit \u201cJesus\u201d and reverse the order of verses 28 & 29.","The Hellenists were Hebrews who used Greek language and culture."]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When the brothers knew it, they brought him down to Caesarea and sent him off to Tarsus."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"So the assemblies throughout all Judea, Galilee, and Samaria had peace and were built up. They were multiplied, walking in the fear of the Lord and in the comfort of the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"As Peter went throughout all those parts, he came down also to the saints who lived at Lydda."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"There he found a certain man named Aeneas, who had been bedridden for eight years because he was paralyzed."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Peter said to him, \u201cAeneas, Jesus Christ heals you. Get up and make your bed!\u201d Immediately he arose."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"All who lived at Lydda and in Sharon saw him, and they turned to the Lord."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was at Joppa a certain disciple named Tabitha, which when translated means Dorcas. This woman was full of good works and acts of mercy which she did."]],f:["\u201cDorcas\u201d is Greek for \u201cGazelle.\u201d"]},{v:37,l:[[0,"In those days, she became sick and died. When they had washed her, they laid her in an upper room."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"As Lydda was near Joppa, the disciples, hearing that Peter was there, sent two men to him, imploring him not to delay in coming to them."]],f:["Reading from NU, TR; MT omits \u201ctwo men\u201d"]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Peter got up and went with them. When he had come, they brought him into the upper room. All the widows stood by him weeping, and showing the tunics and other garments which Dorcas had made while she was with them."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Peter sent them all out, and knelt down and prayed. Turning to the body, he said, \u201cTabitha, get up!\u201d She opened her eyes, and when she saw Peter, she sat up."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He gave her his hand and raised her up. Calling the saints and widows, he presented her alive."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"This became known throughout all Joppa, and many believed in the Lord."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"He stayed many days in Joppa with a tanner named Simon."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there was a certain man in Caesarea, Cornelius by name, a centurion of what was called the Italian Regiment,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"a devout man, and one who feared God with all his house, who gave gifts for the needy generously to the people, and always prayed to God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"At about the ninth hour of the day, he clearly saw in a vision an angel of God coming to him and saying to him, \u201cCornelius!\u201d"]],f:["3:00 p.m."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"He, fastening his eyes on him and being frightened, said, \u201cWhat is it, Lord?\u201d"],[0,"He said to him, \u201cYour prayers and your gifts to the needy have gone up for a memorial before God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now send men to Joppa, and get Simon, who is also called Peter."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He is staying with a tanner named Simon, whose house is by the seaside."]],f:["TR adds \u201cThis one will tell you what it is necessary for you to do.\u201d"]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When the angel who spoke to him had departed, Cornelius called two of his household servants and a devout soldier of those who waited on him continually."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Having explained everything to them, he sent them to Joppa."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Now on the next day as they were on their journey and got close to the city, Peter went up on the housetop to pray at about noon."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He became hungry and desired to eat, but while they were preparing, he fell into a trance."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He saw heaven opened and a certain container descending to him, like a great sheet let down by four corners on the earth,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"in which were all kinds of four-footed animals of the earth, wild animals, reptiles, and birds of the sky."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"A voice came to him, \u201cRise, Peter, kill and eat!\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter said, \u201cNot so, Lord; for I have never eaten anything that is common or unclean.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"A voice came to him again the second time, \u201cWhat God has cleansed, you must not call unclean.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"This was done three times, and immediately the thing was received up into heaven."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now while Peter was very perplexed in himself what the vision which he had seen might mean, behold, the men who were sent by Cornelius, having made inquiry for Simon\u2019s house, stood before the gate,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and called and asked whether Simon, who was also called Peter, was lodging there."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"While Peter was pondering the vision, the Spirit said to him, \u201cBehold, three men seek you."]],f:["Reading from TR and NU. MT omits \u201cthree\u201d"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But arise, get down, and go with them, doubting nothing; for I have sent them.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter went down to the men, and said, \u201cBehold, I am he whom you seek. Why have you come?\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cCornelius, a centurion, a righteous man and one who fears God, and well spoken of by all the nation of the Jews, was directed by a holy angel to invite you to his house, and to listen to what you say.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So he called them in and provided a place to stay."],[0,"On the next day Peter arose and went out with them, and some of the brothers from Joppa accompanied him."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"On the next day they entered into Caesarea. Cornelius was waiting for them, having called together his relatives and his near friends."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When Peter entered, Cornelius met him, fell down at his feet, and worshiped him."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But Peter raised him up, saying, \u201cStand up! I myself am also a man.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"As he talked with him, he went in and found many gathered together."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cYou yourselves know how it is an unlawful thing for a man who is a Jew to join himself or come to one of another nation, but God has shown me that I shouldn\u2019t call any man unholy or unclean."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Therefore I also came without complaint when I was sent for. I ask therefore, why did you send for me?\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Cornelius said, \u201cFour days ago, I was fasting until this hour; and at the ninth hour, I prayed in my house, and behold, a man stood before me in bright clothing"]],f:["3:00 p.m."]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and said, \u2018Cornelius, your prayer is heard, and your gifts to the needy are remembered in the sight of God."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Send therefore to Joppa and summon Simon, who is also called Peter. He is staying in the house of a tanner named Simon, by the seaside. When he comes, he will speak to you.\u2019"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Therefore I sent to you at once, and it was good of you to come. Now therefore we are all here present in the sight of God to hear all things that have been commanded you by God.\u201d"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter opened his mouth and said, \u201cTruly I perceive that God doesn\u2019t show favoritism;"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"but in every nation he who fears him and works righteousness is acceptable to him."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"The word which he sent to the children of Israel, preaching good news of peace by Jesus Christ\u2014he is Lord of all\u2014"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"you yourselves know what happened, which was proclaimed throughout all Judea, beginning from Galilee, after the baptism which John preached;"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"how God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with the Holy Spirit and with power, who went about doing good and healing all who were oppressed by the devil, for God was with him."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"We are witnesses of everything he did both in the country of the Jews and in Jerusalem; whom they also killed, hanging him on a tree."]],f:["TR omits \u201calso\u201d"]},{v:40,l:[[0,"God raised him up the third day and gave him to be revealed,"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"not to all the people, but to witnesses who were chosen before by God, to us, who ate and drank with him after he rose from the dead."]]},{v:42,l:[[0,"He commanded us to preach to the people and to testify that this is he who is appointed by God as the Judge of the living and the dead."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"All the prophets testify about him, that through his name everyone who believes in him will receive remission of sins.\u201d"]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"While Peter was still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell on all those who heard the word."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"They of the circumcision who believed were amazed, as many as came with Peter, because the gift of the Holy Spirit was also poured out on the Gentiles."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"For they heard them speaking in other languages and magnifying God."],[0,"Then Peter answered,"]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"\u201cCan anyone forbid these people from being baptized with water? They have received the Holy Spirit just like us.\u201d"]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"He commanded them to be baptized in the name of Jesus Christ. Then they asked him to stay some days."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now the apostles and the brothers who were in Judea heard that the Gentiles had also received the word of God."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When Peter had come up to Jerusalem, those who were of the circumcision contended with him,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cYou went in to uncircumcised men and ate with them!\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"But Peter began, and explained to them in order, saying,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cI was in the city of Joppa praying, and in a trance I saw a vision: a certain container descending, like it was a great sheet let down from heaven by four corners. It came as far as me."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When I had looked intently at it, I considered, and saw the four-footed animals of the earth, wild animals, creeping things, and birds of the sky."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I also heard a voice saying to me, \u2018Rise, Peter, kill and eat!\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But I said, \u2018Not so, Lord, for nothing unholy or unclean has ever entered into my mouth.\u2019"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But a voice answered me the second time out of heaven, \u2018What God has cleansed, don\u2019t you call unclean.\u2019"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"This was done three times, and all were drawn up again into heaven."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Behold, immediately three men stood before the house where I was, having been sent from Caesarea to me."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The Spirit told me to go with them without discriminating. These six brothers also accompanied me, and we entered into the man\u2019s house."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He told us how he had seen the angel standing in his house and saying to him, \u2018Send to Joppa and get Simon, who is called Peter,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"who will speak to you words by which you will be saved, you and all your house.\u2019"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"As I began to speak, the Holy Spirit fell on them, even as on us at the beginning."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I remembered the word of the Lord, how he said, \u2018John indeed baptized in water, but you will be baptized in the Holy Spirit.\u2019"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If then God gave to them the same gift as us when we believed in the Lord Jesus Christ, who was I, that I could withstand God?\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"When they heard these things, they held their peace and glorified God, saying, \u201cThen God has also granted to the Gentiles repentance to life!\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They therefore who were scattered abroad by the oppression that arose about Stephen traveled as far as Phoenicia, Cyprus, and Antioch, speaking the word to no one except to Jews only."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But there were some of them, men of Cyprus and Cyrene, who, when they had come to Antioch, spoke to the Hellenists, preaching the Lord Jesus."]],f:["A Hellenist is someone who keeps Greek customs and culture."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The hand of the Lord was with them, and a great number believed and turned to the Lord."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The report concerning them came to the ears of the assembly which was in Jerusalem. They sent out Barnabas to go as far as Antioch,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"who, when he had come, and had seen the grace of God, was glad. He exhorted them all, that with purpose of heart they should remain near to the Lord."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For he was a good man, and full of the Holy Spirit and of faith, and many people were added to the Lord."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Barnabas went out to Tarsus to look for Saul."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When he had found him, he brought him to Antioch. For a whole year they were gathered together with the assembly, and taught many people. The disciples were first called Christians in Antioch."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in these days, prophets came down from Jerusalem to Antioch."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"One of them named Agabus stood up and indicated by the Spirit that there should be a great famine all over the world, which also happened in the days of Claudius."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"As any of the disciples had plenty, each determined to send relief to the brothers who lived in Judea;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"which they also did, sending it to the elders by the hands of Barnabas and Saul."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now about that time, King Herod stretched out his hands to oppress some of the assembly."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He killed James, the brother of John, with the sword."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When he saw that it pleased the Jews, he proceeded to seize Peter also. This was during the days of unleavened bread."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When he had arrested him, he put him in prison and delivered him to four squads of four soldiers each to guard him, intending to bring him out to the people after the Passover."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Peter therefore was kept in the prison, but constant prayer was made by the assembly to God for him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The same night when Herod was about to bring him out, Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, bound with two chains. Guards in front of the door kept the prison."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"And behold, an angel of the Lord stood by him, and a light shone in the cell. He struck Peter on the side and woke him up, saying, \u201cStand up quickly!\u201d His chains fell off his hands."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The angel said to him, \u201cGet dressed and put on your sandals.\u201d He did so. He said to him, \u201cPut on your cloak and follow me.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"And he went out and followed him. He didn\u2019t know that what was being done by the angel was real, but thought he saw a vision."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When they were past the first and the second guard, they came to the iron gate that leads into the city, which opened to them by itself. They went out and went down one street, and immediately the angel departed from him."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When Peter had come to himself, he said, \u201cNow I truly know that the Lord has sent out his angel and delivered me out of the hand of Herod, and from everything the Jewish people were expecting.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Thinking about that, he came to the house of Mary, the mother of John who was called Mark, where many were gathered together and were praying."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"When Peter knocked at the door of the gate, a servant girl named Rhoda came to answer."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When she recognized Peter\u2019s voice, she didn\u2019t open the gate for joy, but ran in and reported that Peter was standing in front of the gate."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to her, \u201cYou are crazy!\u201d But she insisted that it was so. They said, \u201cIt is his angel.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But Peter continued knocking. When they had opened, they saw him and were amazed."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But he, beckoning to them with his hand to be silent, declared to them how the Lord had brought him out of the prison. He said, \u201cTell these things to James and to the brothers.\u201d Then he departed and went to another place."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now as soon as it was day, there was no small stir among the soldiers about what had become of Peter."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When Herod had sought for him and didn\u2019t find him, he examined the guards, then commanded that they should be put to death. He went down from Judea to Caesarea, and stayed there."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Herod was very angry with the people of Tyre and Sidon. They came with one accord to him and, having made Blastus, the king\u2019s personal aide, their friend, they asked for peace, because their country depended on the king\u2019s country for food."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"On an appointed day, Herod dressed himself in royal clothing, sat on the throne, and gave a speech to them."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The people shouted, \u201cThe voice of a god, and not of a man!\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Immediately an angel of the Lord struck him, because he didn\u2019t give God the glory. Then he was eaten by worms and died."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"But the word of God grew and multiplied."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Barnabas and Saul returned to Jerusalem when they had fulfilled their service, also taking with them John who was called Mark."]],f:["TR reads \u201cfrom\u201d instead of \u201cto\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the assembly that was at Antioch there were some prophets and teachers: Barnabas, Simeon who was called Niger, Lucius of Cyrene, Manaen the foster brother of Herod the tetrarch, and Saul."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"As they served the Lord and fasted, the Holy Spirit said, \u201cSeparate Barnabas and Saul for me, for the work to which I have called them.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then, when they had fasted and prayed and laid their hands on them, they sent them away."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"So, being sent out by the Holy Spirit, they went down to Seleucia. From there they sailed to Cyprus."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When they were at Salamis, they proclaimed God\u2019s word in the Jewish synagogues. They also had John as their attendant."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When they had gone through the island to Paphos, they found a certain sorcerer, a false prophet, a Jew whose name was Bar Jesus,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"who was with the proconsul, Sergius Paulus, a man of understanding. This man summoned Barnabas and Saul, and sought to hear the word of God."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But Elymas the sorcerer (for so is his name by interpretation) withstood them, seeking to turn the proconsul away from the faith."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But Saul, who is also called Paul, filled with the Holy Spirit, fastened his eyes on him"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and said, \u201cYou son of the devil, full of all deceit and all cunning, you enemy of all righteousness, will you not cease to pervert the right ways of the Lord?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now, behold, the hand of the Lord is on you, and you will be blind, not seeing the sun for a season!\u201d"],[0,"Immediately a mist and darkness fell on him. He went around seeking someone to lead him by the hand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Then the proconsul, when he saw what was done, believed, being astonished at the teaching of the Lord."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now Paul and his company set sail from Paphos and came to Perga in Pamphylia. John departed from them and returned to Jerusalem."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But they, passing on from Perga, came to Antioch of Pisidia. They went into the synagogue on the Sabbath day and sat down."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"After the reading of the law and the prophets, the rulers of the synagogue sent to them, saying, \u201cBrothers, if you have any word of exhortation for the people, speak.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul stood up, and gesturing with his hand said, \u201cMen of Israel, and you who fear God, listen."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The God of this people chose our fathers, and exalted the people when they stayed as aliens in the land of Egypt, and with an uplifted arm, he led them out of it."]],f:["TR, NU add \u201cIsrael\u201d"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For a period of about forty years he put up with them in the wilderness."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When he had destroyed seven nations in the land of Canaan, he gave them their land for an inheritance for about four hundred fifty years."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"After these things, he gave them judges until Samuel the prophet."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Afterward they asked for a king, and God gave to them Saul the son of Kish, a man of the tribe of Benjamin, for forty years."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"When he had removed him, he raised up David to be their king, to whom he also testified, \u2018I have found David the son of Jesse, a man after my heart, who will do all my will.\u2019"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"From this man\u2019s offspring, God has brought salvation to Israel according to his promise,"]],f:["TR, NU read \u201ca Savior, Jesus\u201d instead of \u201csalvation\u201d"]},{v:24,l:[[0,"before his coming, when John had first preached the baptism of repentance to Israel."]],f:["TR, NU read \u201cto all the people of Israel\u201d instead of \u201cto Israel\u201d"]},{v:25,l:[[0,"As John was fulfilling his course, he said, \u2018What do you suppose that I am? I am not he. But behold, one comes after me, the sandals of whose feet I am not worthy to untie.\u2019"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBrothers, children of the stock of Abraham, and those among you who fear God, the word of this salvation is sent out to you."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For those who dwell in Jerusalem, and their rulers, because they didn\u2019t know him, nor the voices of the prophets which are read every Sabbath, fulfilled them by condemning him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Though they found no cause for death, they still asked Pilate to have him killed."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"When they had fulfilled all things that were written about him, they took him down from the tree and laid him in a tomb."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But God raised him from the dead,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and he was seen for many days by those who came up with him from Galilee to Jerusalem, who are his witnesses to the people."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"We bring you good news of the promise made to the fathers,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"that God has fulfilled this to us, their children, in that he raised up Jesus. As it is also written in the second psalm,"],[1,"\u2018You are my Son."],[2,"Today I have become your father.\u2019"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cConcerning that he raised him up from the dead, now no more to return to corruption, he has spoken thus: \u2018I will give you the holy and sure blessings of David.\u2019"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Therefore he says also in another psalm, \u2018You will not allow your Holy One to see decay.\u2019"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"For David, after he had in his own generation served the counsel of God, fell asleep, was laid with his fathers, and saw decay."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"But he whom God raised up saw no decay."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Be it known to you therefore, brothers, that through this man is proclaimed to you remission of sins;"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and by him everyone who believes is justified from all things, from which you could not be justified by the law of Moses."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Beware therefore, lest that come on you which is spoken in the prophets:"]]},{v:41,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018Behold, you scoffers!"],[2,"Wonder and perish,"],[2,"for I work a work in your days,"],[2,"a work which you will in no way believe, if one declares it to you.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"So when the Jews went out of the synagogue, the Gentiles begged that these words might be preached to them the next Sabbath."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"Now when the synagogue broke up, many of the Jews and of the devout proselytes followed Paul and Barnabas; who, speaking to them, urged them to continue in the grace of God."]]},{v:44,p:1,l:[[0,"The next Sabbath, almost the whole city was gathered together to hear the word of God."]]},{v:45,l:[[0,"But when the Jews saw the multitudes, they were filled with jealousy, and contradicted the things which were spoken by Paul, and blasphemed."]]},{v:46,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul and Barnabas spoke out boldly, and said, \u201cIt was necessary that God\u2019s word should be spoken to you first. Since indeed you thrust it from yourselves, and judge yourselves unworthy of eternal life, behold, we turn to the Gentiles."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"For so has the Lord commanded us, saying,"],[1,"\u2018I have set you as a light for the Gentiles,"],[2,"that you should bring salvation to the uttermost parts of the earth.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:48,p:1,l:[[0,"As the Gentiles heard this, they were glad and glorified the word of God. As many as were appointed to eternal life believed."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"The Lord\u2019s word was spread abroad throughout all the region."]]},{v:50,l:[[0,"But the Jews stirred up the devout and prominent women and the chief men of the city, and stirred up a persecution against Paul and Barnabas, and threw them out of their borders."]]},{v:51,l:[[0,"But they shook off the dust of their feet against them, and came to Iconium."]]},{v:52,l:[[0,"The disciples were filled with joy and with the Holy Spirit."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In Iconium, they entered together into the synagogue of the Jews, and so spoke that a great multitude both of Jews and of Greeks believed."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But the disbelieving Jews stirred up and embittered the souls of the Gentiles against the brothers."]],f:["or, disobedient"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore they stayed there a long time, speaking boldly in the Lord, who testified to the word of his grace, granting signs and wonders to be done by their hands."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But the multitude of the city was divided. Part sided with the Jews and part with the apostles."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When some of both the Gentiles and the Jews, with their rulers, made a violent attempt to mistreat and stone them,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"they became aware of it and fled to the cities of Lycaonia, Lystra, Derbe, and the surrounding region."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"There they preached the Good News."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"At Lystra a certain man sat, impotent in his feet, a cripple from his mother\u2019s womb, who never had walked."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He was listening to Paul speaking, who, fastening eyes on him and seeing that he had faith to be made whole,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"said with a loud voice, \u201cStand upright on your feet!\u201d He leaped up and walked."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When the multitude saw what Paul had done, they lifted up their voice, saying in the language of Lycaonia, \u201cThe gods have come down to us in the likeness of men!\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They called Barnabas \u201cJupiter\u201d, and Paul \u201cMercury\u201d, because he was the chief speaker."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The priest of Jupiter, whose temple was in front of their city, brought oxen and garlands to the gates, and would have made a sacrifice along with the multitudes."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"But when the apostles, Barnabas and Paul, heard of it, they tore their clothes and sprang into the multitude, crying out,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"\u201cMen, why are you doing these things? We also are men of the same nature as you, and bring you good news, that you should turn from these vain things to the living God, who made the sky, the earth, the sea, and all that is in them;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"who in the generations gone by allowed all the nations to walk in their own ways."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Yet he didn\u2019t leave himself without witness, in that he did good and gave you rains from the sky and fruitful seasons, filling our hearts with food and gladness.\u201d"]],f:["TR reads \u201cus\u201d instead of \u201cyou\u201d"]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Even saying these things, they hardly stopped the multitudes from making a sacrifice to them."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But some Jews from Antioch and Iconium came there, and having persuaded the multitudes, they stoned Paul and dragged him out of the city, supposing that he was dead."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"But as the disciples stood around him, he rose up, and entered into the city. On the next day he went out with Barnabas to Derbe."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had preached the Good News to that city and had made many disciples, they returned to Lystra, Iconium, and Antioch,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"strengthening the souls of the disciples, exhorting them to continue in the faith, and that through many afflictions we must enter into God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When they had appointed elders for them in every assembly, and had prayed with fasting, they commended them to the Lord on whom they had believed."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"They passed through Pisidia and came to Pamphylia."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When they had spoken the word in Perga, they went down to Attalia."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"From there they sailed to Antioch, from where they had been committed to the grace of God for the work which they had fulfilled."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When they had arrived and had gathered the assembly together, they reported all the things that God had done with them, and that he had opened a door of faith to the nations."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They stayed there with the disciples for a long time."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Some men came down from Judea and taught the brothers, \u201cUnless you are circumcised after the custom of Moses, you can\u2019t be saved.\u201d"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore when Paul and Barnabas had no small discord and discussion with them, they appointed Paul, Barnabas, and some others of them to go up to Jerusalem to the apostles and elders about this question."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They, being sent on their way by the assembly, passed through both Phoenicia and Samaria, declaring the conversion of the Gentiles. They caused great joy to all the brothers."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When they had come to Jerusalem, they were received by the assembly and the apostles and the elders, and they reported everything that God had done with them."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But some of the sect of the Pharisees who believed rose up, saying, \u201cIt is necessary to circumcise them, and to command them to keep the law of Moses.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The apostles and the elders were gathered together to see about this matter."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When there had been much discussion, Peter rose up and said to them, \u201cBrothers, you know that a good while ago God made a choice among you that by my mouth the nations should hear the word of the Good News and believe."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"God, who knows the heart, testified about them, giving them the Holy Spirit, just like he did to us."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He made no distinction between us and them, cleansing their hearts by faith."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now therefore why do you tempt God, that you should put a yoke on the neck of the disciples which neither our fathers nor we were able to bear?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But we believe that we are saved through the grace of the Lord Jesus, just as they are.\u201d"]],f:["TR adds \u201cChrist\u201d"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"All the multitude kept silence, and they listened to Barnabas and Paul reporting what signs and wonders God had done among the nations through them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"After they were silent, James answered, \u201cBrothers, listen to me."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Simeon has reported how God first visited the nations to take out of them a people for his name."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"This agrees with the words of the prophets. As it is written,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u2018After these things I will return."],[1,"I will again build the tabernacle of David, which has fallen."],[1,"I will again build its ruins."],[1,"I will set it up"]]},{v:17,l:[[1,"that the rest of men may seek after the Lord:"],[1,"all the Gentiles who are called by my name,"],[1,"says the Lord, who does all these things.\u2019"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll of God\u2019s works are known to him from eternity."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore my judgment is that we don\u2019t trouble those from among the Gentiles who turn to God,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but that we write to them that they abstain from the pollution of idols, from sexual immorality, from what is strangled, and from blood."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For Moses from generations of old has in every city those who preach him, being read in the synagogues every Sabbath.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Then it seemed good to the apostles and the elders, with the whole assembly, to choose men out of their company, and send them to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas: Judas called Barsabbas, and Silas, chief men among the brothers."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They wrote these things by their hand:"],[0,"\u201cThe apostles, the elders, and the brothers, to the brothers who are of the Gentiles in Antioch, Syria, and Cilicia: greetings."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Because we have heard that some who went out from us have troubled you with words, unsettling your souls, saying, \u2018You must be circumcised and keep the law,\u2019 to whom we gave no commandment;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"it seemed good to us, having come to one accord, to choose out men and send them to you with our beloved Barnabas and Paul,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"men who have risked their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"We have sent therefore Judas and Silas, who themselves will also tell you the same things by word of mouth."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For it seemed good to the Holy Spirit, and to us, to lay no greater burden on you than these necessary things:"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"that you abstain from things sacrificed to idols, from blood, from things strangled, and from sexual immorality, from which if you keep yourselves, it will be well with you. Farewell.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"So, when they were sent off, they came to Antioch. Having gathered the multitude together, they delivered the letter."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"When they had read it, they rejoiced over the encouragement."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Judas and Silas, also being prophets themselves, encouraged the brothers with many words and strengthened them."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"After they had spent some time there, they were dismissed in peace from the brothers to the apostles."]]},{v:34,l:[],f:["Some manuscripts add: But it seemed good to Silas to stay there."]},{v:35,l:[[0,"But Paul and Barnabas stayed in Antioch, teaching and preaching the word of the Lord, with many others also."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"After some days Paul said to Barnabas, \u201cLet\u2019s return now and visit our brothers in every city in which we proclaimed the word of the Lord, to see how they are doing.\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"Barnabas planned to take John, who was called Mark, with them also."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But Paul didn\u2019t think that it was a good idea to take with them someone who had withdrawn from them in Pamphylia, and didn\u2019t go with them to do the work."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"Then the contention grew so sharp that they separated from each other. Barnabas took Mark with him and sailed away to Cyprus,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"but Paul chose Silas and went out, being commended by the brothers to the grace of God."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"He went through Syria and Cilicia, strengthening the assemblies."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He came to Derbe and Lystra; and behold, a certain disciple was there, named Timothy, the son of a Jewess who believed, but his father was a Greek."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The brothers who were at Lystra and Iconium gave a good testimony about him."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Paul wanted to have him go out with him, and he took and circumcised him because of the Jews who were in those parts, for they all knew that his father was a Greek."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"As they went on their way through the cities, they delivered the decrees to them to keep which had been ordained by the apostles and elders who were at Jerusalem."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So the assemblies were strengthened in the faith, and increased in number daily."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had gone through the region of Phrygia and Galatia, they were forbidden by the Holy Spirit to speak the word in Asia."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When they had come opposite Mysia, they tried to go into Bithynia, but the Spirit didn\u2019t allow them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Passing by Mysia, they came down to Troas."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"A vision appeared to Paul in the night. There was a man of Macedonia standing, begging him and saying, \u201cCome over into Macedonia and help us.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"When he had seen the vision, immediately we sought to go out to Macedonia, concluding that the Lord had called us to preach the Good News to them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Setting sail therefore from Troas, we made a straight course to Samothrace, and the day following to Neapolis;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"and from there to Philippi, which is a city of Macedonia, the foremost of the district, a Roman colony. We were staying some days in this city."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"On the Sabbath day we went outside of the city by a riverside, where we supposed there was a place of prayer, and we sat down and spoke to the women who had come together."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"A certain woman named Lydia, a seller of purple, of the city of Thyatira, one who worshiped God, heard us. The Lord opened her heart to listen to the things which were spoken by Paul."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When she and her household were baptized, she begged us, saying, \u201cIf you have judged me to be faithful to the Lord, come into my house and stay.\u201d So she persuaded us."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"As we were going to prayer, a certain girl having a spirit of divination met us, who brought her masters much gain by fortune telling."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Following Paul and us, she cried out, \u201cThese men are servants of the Most High God, who proclaim to us a way of salvation!\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"She was doing this for many days."],[0,"But Paul, becoming greatly annoyed, turned and said to the spirit, \u201cI command you in the name of Jesus Christ to come out of her!\u201d It came out that very hour."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But when her masters saw that the hope of their gain was gone, they seized Paul and Silas and dragged them into the marketplace before the rulers."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When they had brought them to the magistrates, they said, \u201cThese men, being Jews, are agitating our city"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and advocate customs which it is not lawful for us to accept or to observe, being Romans.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The multitude rose up together against them and the magistrates tore their clothes from them, then commanded them to be beaten with rods."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When they had laid many stripes on them, they threw them into prison, charging the jailer to keep them safely."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Having received such a command, he threw them into the inner prison and secured their feet in the stocks."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But about midnight Paul and Silas were praying and singing hymns to God, and the prisoners were listening to them."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Suddenly there was a great earthquake, so that the foundations of the prison were shaken; and immediately all the doors were opened, and everyone\u2019s bonds were loosened."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"The jailer, being roused out of sleep and seeing the prison doors open, drew his sword and was about to kill himself, supposing that the prisoners had escaped."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But Paul cried with a loud voice, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t harm yourself, for we are all here!\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"He called for lights, sprang in, fell down trembling before Paul and Silas,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"brought them out, and said, \u201cSirs, what must I do to be saved?\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"They said, \u201cBelieve in the Lord Jesus Christ, and you will be saved, you and your household.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"They spoke the word of the Lord to him, and to all who were in his house."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"He took them the same hour of the night and washed their stripes, and was immediately baptized, he and all his household."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"He brought them up into his house and set food before them, and rejoiced greatly with all his household, having believed in God."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"But when it was day, the magistrates sent the sergeants, saying, \u201cLet those men go.\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"The jailer reported these words to Paul, saying, \u201cThe magistrates have sent to let you go; now therefore come out and go in peace.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"But Paul said to them, \u201cThey have beaten us publicly without a trial, men who are Romans, and have cast us into prison! Do they now release us secretly? No, most certainly, but let them come themselves and bring us out!\u201d"]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[0,"The sergeants reported these words to the magistrates, and they were afraid when they heard that they were Romans,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"and they came and begged them. When they had brought them out, they asked them to depart from the city."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"They went out of the prison and entered into Lydia\u2019s house. When they had seen the brothers, they encouraged them, then departed."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when they had passed through Amphipolis and Apollonia, they came to Thessalonica, where there was a Jewish synagogue."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Paul, as was his custom, went in to them; and for three Sabbath days reasoned with them from the Scriptures,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"explaining and demonstrating that the Christ had to suffer and rise again from the dead, and saying, \u201cThis Jesus, whom I proclaim to you, is the Christ.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Some of them were persuaded and joined Paul and Silas: of the devout Greeks a great multitude, and not a few of the chief women."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But the unpersuaded Jews took along some wicked men from the marketplace and gathering a crowd, set the city in an uproar. Assaulting the house of Jason, they sought to bring them out to the people."]],f:["TR reads \u201cAnd the Jews who were unpersuaded, becoming envious and taking along\u201d instead of \u201cBut the unpersuaded Jews took along\u201d"]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When they didn\u2019t find them, they dragged Jason and certain brothers before the rulers of the city, crying, \u201cThese who have turned the world upside down have come here also,"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may be also correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"whom Jason has received. These all act contrary to the decrees of Caesar, saying that there is another king, Jesus!\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The multitude and the rulers of the city were troubled when they heard these things."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When they had taken security from Jason and the rest, they let them go."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The brothers immediately sent Paul and Silas away by night to Beroea. When they arrived, they went into the Jewish synagogue."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these were more noble than those in Thessalonica, in that they received the word with all readiness of mind, examining the Scriptures daily to see whether these things were so."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Many of them therefore believed; also of the prominent Greek women, and not a few men."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But when the Jews of Thessalonica had knowledge that the word of God was proclaimed by Paul at Beroea also, they came there likewise, agitating the multitudes."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Then the brothers immediately sent out Paul to go as far as to the sea, and Silas and Timothy still stayed there."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But those who escorted Paul brought him as far as Athens. Receiving a commandment to Silas and Timothy that they should come to him very quickly, they departed."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Now while Paul waited for them at Athens, his spirit was provoked within him as he saw the city full of idols."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So he reasoned in the synagogue with the Jews and the devout persons, and in the marketplace every day with those who met him."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Some of the Epicurean and Stoic philosophers also were conversing with him. Some said, \u201cWhat does this babbler want to say?\u201d"],[0,"Others said, \u201cHe seems to be advocating foreign deities,\u201d because he preached Jesus and the resurrection."]],f:["TR omits \u201calso\u201d"]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"They took hold of him and brought him to the Areopagus, saying, \u201cMay we know what this new teaching is, which you are speaking about?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For you bring certain strange things to our ears. We want to know therefore what these things mean.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Now all the Athenians and the strangers living there spent their time in nothing else, but either to tell or to hear some new thing."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul stood in the middle of the Areopagus and said, \u201cYou men of Athens, I perceive that you are very religious in all things."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For as I passed along and observed the objects of your worship, I also found an altar with this inscription: \u2018TO AN UNKNOWN GOD.\u2019 What therefore you worship in ignorance, I announce to you."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The God who made the world and all things in it, he, being Lord of heaven and earth, doesn\u2019t dwell in temples made with hands."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He isn\u2019t served by men\u2019s hands, as though he needed anything, seeing he himself gives to all life and breath and all things."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He made from one blood every nation of men to dwell on all the surface of the earth, having determined appointed seasons and the boundaries of their dwellings,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"that they should seek the Lord, if perhaps they might reach out for him and find him, though he is not far from each one of us."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"\u2018For in him we live, move, and have our being.\u2019 As some of your own poets have said, \u2018For we are also his offspring.\u2019"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Being then the offspring of God, we ought not to think that the Divine Nature is like gold, or silver, or stone, engraved by art and design of man."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"The times of ignorance therefore God overlooked. But now he commands that all people everywhere should repent,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"because he has appointed a day in which he will judge the world in righteousness by the man whom he has ordained; of which he has given assurance to all men, in that he has raised him from the dead.\u201d"]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when they heard of the resurrection of the dead, some mocked; but others said, \u201cWe want to hear you again concerning this.\u201d"]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Thus Paul went out from among them."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But certain men joined with him and believed, including Dionysius the Areopagite, and a woman named Damaris, and others with them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things Paul departed from Athens and came to Corinth."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He found a certain Jew named Aquila, a man of Pontus by race, who had recently come from Italy with his wife Priscilla, because Claudius had commanded all the Jews to depart from Rome. He came to them,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and because he practiced the same trade, he lived with them and worked, for by trade they were tent makers."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He reasoned in the synagogue every Sabbath and persuaded Jews and Greeks."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul was compelled by the Spirit, testifying to the Jews that Jesus was the Christ."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When they opposed him and blasphemed, he shook out his clothing and said to them, \u201cYour blood be on your own heads! I am clean. From now on, I will go to the Gentiles!\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He departed there and went into the house of a certain man named Justus, one who worshiped God, whose house was next door to the synagogue."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Crispus, the ruler of the synagogue, believed in the Lord with all his house. Many of the Corinthians, when they heard, believed and were baptized."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The Lord said to Paul in the night by a vision, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid, but speak and don\u2019t be silent;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for I am with you, and no one will attack you to harm you, for I have many people in this city.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He lived there a year and six months, teaching the word of God among them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But when Gallio was proconsul of Achaia, the Jews with one accord rose up against Paul and brought him before the judgment seat,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cThis man persuades men to worship God contrary to the law.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Paul was about to open his mouth, Gallio said to the Jews, \u201cIf indeed it were a matter of wrong or of wicked crime, you Jews, it would be reasonable that I should bear with you;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but if they are questions about words and names and your own law, look to it yourselves. For I don\u2019t want to be a judge of these matters.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So he drove them from the judgment seat."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Then all the Greeks seized Sosthenes, the ruler of the synagogue, and beat him before the judgment seat. Gallio didn\u2019t care about any of these things."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, having stayed after this many more days, took his leave of the brothers, and sailed from there for Syria, together with Priscilla and Aquila. He shaved his head in Cenchreae, for he had a vow."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"He came to Ephesus, and he left them there; but he himself entered into the synagogue and reasoned with the Jews."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When they asked him to stay with them a longer time, he declined;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"but taking his leave of them, he said, \u201cI must by all means keep this coming feast in Jerusalem, but I will return again to you if God wills.\u201d Then he set sail from Ephesus."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had landed at Caesarea, he went up and greeted the assembly, and went down to Antioch."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Having spent some time there, he departed and went through the region of Galatia and Phrygia, in order, establishing all the disciples."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Now a certain Jew named Apollos, an Alexandrian by race, an eloquent man, came to Ephesus. He was mighty in the Scriptures."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"This man had been instructed in the way of the Lord; and being fervent in spirit, he spoke and taught accurately the things concerning Jesus, although he knew only the baptism of John."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He began to speak boldly in the synagogue. But when Priscilla and Aquila heard him, they took him aside, and explained to him the way of God more accurately."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had determined to pass over into Achaia, the brothers encouraged him; and wrote to the disciples to receive him. When he had come, he greatly helped those who had believed through grace;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"for he powerfully refuted the Jews, publicly showing by the Scriptures that Jesus was the Christ."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"While Apollos was at Corinth, Paul, having passed through the upper country, came to Ephesus and found certain disciples."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He said to them, \u201cDid you receive the Holy Spirit when you believed?\u201d"],[0,"They said to him, \u201cNo, we haven\u2019t even heard that there is a Holy Spirit.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cInto what then were you baptized?\u201d"],[0,"They said, \u201cInto John\u2019s baptism.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul said, \u201cJohn indeed baptized with the baptism of repentance, saying to the people that they should believe in the one who would come after him, that is, in Christ Jesus.\u201d"]],f:["NU omits Christ."]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When they heard this, they were baptized in the name of the Lord Jesus."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"When Paul had laid his hands on them, the Holy Spirit came on them and they spoke with other languages and prophesied."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"They were about twelve men in all."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"He entered into the synagogue and spoke boldly for a period of three months, reasoning and persuading about the things concerning God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"But when some were hardened and disobedient, speaking evil of the Way before the multitude, he departed from them and separated the disciples, reasoning daily in the school of Tyrannus."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"This continued for two years, so that all those who lived in Asia heard the word of the Lord Jesus, both Jews and Greeks."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"God worked special miracles by the hands of Paul,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"so that even handkerchiefs or aprons were carried away from his body to the sick, and the diseases departed from them, and the evil spirits went out."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But some of the itinerant Jews, exorcists, took on themselves to invoke over those who had the evil spirits the name of the Lord Jesus, saying, \u201cWe adjure you by Jesus whom Paul preaches.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"There were seven sons of one Sceva, a Jewish chief priest, who did this."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The evil spirit answered, \u201cJesus I know, and Paul I know, but who are you?\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The man in whom the evil spirit was leaped on them, overpowered them, and prevailed against them, so that they fled out of that house naked and wounded."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"This became known to all, both Jews and Greeks, who lived at Ephesus. Fear fell on them all, and the name of the Lord Jesus was magnified."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Many also of those who had believed came, confessing and declaring their deeds."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Many of those who practiced magical arts brought their books together and burned them in the sight of all. They counted their price, and found it to be fifty thousand pieces of silver."]],f:["The 50,000 pieces of silver here probably referred to 50,000 drachmas. If so, the value of the burned books was equivalent to about 160 man-years of wages for agricultural laborers"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"So the word of the Lord was growing and becoming mighty."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Now after these things had ended, Paul determined in the Spirit, when he had passed through Macedonia and Achaia, to go to Jerusalem, saying, \u201cAfter I have been there, I must also see Rome.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Having sent into Macedonia two of those who served him, Timothy and Erastus, he himself stayed in Asia for a while."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"About that time there arose no small disturbance concerning the Way."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For a certain man named Demetrius, a silversmith who made silver shrines of Artemis, brought no little business to the craftsmen,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"whom he gathered together with the workmen of like occupation, and said, \u201cSirs, you know that by this business we have our wealth."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"You see and hear that not at Ephesus alone, but almost throughout all Asia, this Paul has persuaded and turned away many people, saying that they are no gods that are made with hands."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Not only is there danger that this our trade come into disrepute, but also that the temple of the great goddess Artemis will be counted as nothing and her majesty destroyed, whom all Asia and the world worships.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"When they heard this they were filled with anger, and cried out, saying, \u201cGreat is Artemis of the Ephesians!\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"The whole city was filled with confusion, and they rushed with one accord into the theater, having seized Gaius and Aristarchus, men of Macedonia, Paul\u2019s companions in travel."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When Paul wanted to enter in to the people, the disciples didn\u2019t allow him."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Certain also of the Asiarchs, being his friends, sent to him and begged him not to venture into the theater."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Some therefore cried one thing, and some another, for the assembly was in confusion. Most of them didn\u2019t know why they had come together."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"They brought Alexander out of the multitude, the Jews putting him forward. Alexander beckoned with his hand, and would have made a defense to the people."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But when they perceived that he was a Jew, all with one voice for a time of about two hours cried out, \u201cGreat is Artemis of the Ephesians!\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"When the town clerk had quieted the multitude, he said, \u201cYou men of Ephesus, what man is there who doesn\u2019t know that the city of the Ephesians is temple keeper of the great goddess Artemis, and of the image which fell down from Zeus?"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Seeing then that these things can\u2019t be denied, you ought to be quiet and to do nothing rash."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"For you have brought these men here, who are neither robbers of temples nor blasphemers of your goddess."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"If therefore Demetrius and the craftsmen who are with him have a matter against anyone, the courts are open and there are proconsuls. Let them press charges against one another."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"But if you seek anything about other matters, it will be settled in the regular assembly."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"For indeed we are in danger of being accused concerning today\u2019s riot, there being no cause. Concerning it, we wouldn\u2019t be able to give an account of this commotion.\u201d"]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"When he had thus spoken, he dismissed the assembly."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After the uproar had ceased, Paul sent for the disciples, took leave of them, and departed to go into Macedonia."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When he had gone through those parts and had encouraged them with many words, he came into Greece."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When he had spent three months there, and a plot was made against him by Jews as he was about to set sail for Syria, he determined to return through Macedonia."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"These accompanied him as far as Asia: Sopater of Beroea, Aristarchus and Secundus of the Thessalonians, Gaius of Derbe, Timothy, and Tychicus and Trophimus of Asia."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But these had gone ahead, and were waiting for us at Troas."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"We sailed away from Philippi after the days of Unleavened Bread, and came to them at Troas in five days, where we stayed seven days."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"On the first day of the week, when the disciples were gathered together to break bread, Paul talked with them, intending to depart on the next day; and continued his speech until midnight."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"There were many lights in the upper room where we were gathered together."]],f:["TR reads \u201cthey\u201d instead of \u201cwe\u201d"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"A certain young man named Eutychus sat in the window, weighed down with deep sleep. As Paul spoke still longer, being weighed down by his sleep, he fell down from the third floor and was taken up dead."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Paul went down and fell upon him, and embracing him said, \u201cDon\u2019t be troubled, for his life is in him.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had gone up, had broken bread and eaten, and had talked with them a long while, even until break of day, he departed."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"They brought the boy in alive, and were greatly comforted."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But we, going ahead to the ship, set sail for Assos, intending to take Paul aboard there; for he had so arranged, intending himself to go by land."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When he met us at Assos, we took him aboard and came to Mitylene."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Sailing from there, we came the following day opposite Chios. The next day we touched at Samos and stayed at Trogyllium, and the day after we came to Miletus."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For Paul had determined to sail past Ephesus, that he might not have to spend time in Asia; for he was hastening, if it were possible for him, to be in Jerusalem on the day of Pentecost."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"From Miletus he sent to Ephesus and called to himself the elders of the assembly."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When they had come to him, he said to them, \u201cYou yourselves know, from the first day that I set foot in Asia, how I was with you all the time,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"serving the Lord with all humility, with many tears, and with trials which happened to me by the plots of the Jews;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"how I didn\u2019t shrink from declaring to you anything that was profitable, teaching you publicly and from house to house,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"testifying both to Jews and to Greeks repentance toward God and faith toward our Lord Jesus."]],f:["TR adds \u201cChrist\u201d"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Now, behold, I go bound by the Spirit to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me there;"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"except that the Holy Spirit testifies in every city, saying that bonds and afflictions wait for me."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But these things don\u2019t count; nor do I hold my life dear to myself, so that I may finish my race with joy, and the ministry which I received from the Lord Jesus, to fully testify to the Good News of the grace of God."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cNow, behold, I know that you all, among whom I went about preaching God\u2019s Kingdom, will see my face no more."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Therefore I testify to you today that I am clean from the blood of all men,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"for I didn\u2019t shrink from declaring to you the whole counsel of God."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Take heed, therefore, to yourselves and to all the flock, in which the Holy Spirit has made you overseers, to shepherd the assembly of the Lord and God which he purchased with his own blood."]],f:["TR, NU omit \u201cthe Lord and\u201d"]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For I know that after my departure, vicious wolves will enter in among you, not sparing the flock."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Men will arise from among your own selves, speaking perverse things, to draw away the disciples after them."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Therefore watch, remembering that for a period of three years I didn\u2019t cease to admonish everyone night and day with tears."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Now, brothers, I entrust you to God and to the word of his grace, which is able to build up and to give you the inheritance among all those who are sanctified."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where the context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:33,l:[[0,"I coveted no one\u2019s silver, gold, or clothing."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"You yourselves know that these hands served my necessities, and those who were with me."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"In all things I gave you an example, that so laboring you ought to help the weak, and to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, that he himself said, \u2018It is more blessed to give than to receive.\u2019 \u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had spoken these things, he knelt down and prayed with them all."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They all wept freely, and fell on Paul\u2019s neck and kissed him,"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"sorrowing most of all because of the word which he had spoken, that they should see his face no more. Then they accompanied him to the ship."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When we had departed from them and had set sail, we came with a straight course to Cos, and the next day to Rhodes, and from there to Patara."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Having found a ship crossing over to Phoenicia, we went aboard and set sail."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When we had come in sight of Cyprus, leaving it on the left hand, we sailed to Syria and landed at Tyre, for the ship was there to unload her cargo."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Having found disciples, we stayed there seven days. These said to Paul through the Spirit that he should not go up to Jerusalem."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When those days were over, we departed and went on our journey. They all, with wives and children, brought us on our way until we were out of the city. Kneeling down on the beach, we prayed."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"After saying goodbye to each other, we went on board the ship, and they returned home again."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When we had finished the voyage from Tyre, we arrived at Ptolemais. We greeted the brothers and stayed with them one day."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"On the next day, we who were Paul\u2019s companions departed and came to Caesarea."],[0,"We entered into the house of Philip the evangelist, who was one of the seven, and stayed with him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Now this man had four virgin daughters who prophesied."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As we stayed there some days, a certain prophet named Agabus came down from Judea."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Coming to us and taking Paul\u2019s belt, he bound his own feet and hands, and said, \u201cThe Holy Spirit says: \u2018So the Jews at Jerusalem will bind the man who owns this belt, and will deliver him into the hands of the Gentiles.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When we heard these things, both we and the people of that place begged him not to go up to Jerusalem."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Then Paul answered, \u201cWhat are you doing, weeping and breaking my heart? For I am ready not only to be bound, but also to die at Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"When he would not be persuaded, we ceased, saying, \u201cThe Lord\u2019s will be done.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"After these days we took up our baggage and went up to Jerusalem."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Some of the disciples from Caesarea also went with us, bringing one Mnason of Cyprus, an early disciple, with whom we would stay."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"When we had come to Jerusalem, the brothers received us gladly."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The day following, Paul went in with us to James; and all the elders were present."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"When he had greeted them, he reported one by one the things which God had worked among the Gentiles through his ministry."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"They, when they heard it, glorified God. They said to him, \u201cYou see, brother, how many thousands there are among the Jews of those who have believed, and they are all zealous for the law."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They have been informed about you, that you teach all the Jews who are among the Gentiles to forsake Moses, telling them not to circumcise their children and not to walk after the customs."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"What then? The assembly must certainly meet, for they will hear that you have come."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Therefore do what we tell you. We have four men who have taken a vow."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Take them and purify yourself with them, and pay their expenses for them, that they may shave their heads. Then all will know that there is no truth in the things that they have been informed about you, but that you yourself also walk keeping the law."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But concerning the Gentiles who believe, we have written our decision that they should observe no such thing, except that they should keep themselves from food offered to idols, from blood, from strangled things, and from sexual immorality.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Paul took the men, and the next day purified himself and went with them into the temple, declaring the fulfillment of the days of purification, until the offering was offered for every one of them."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"When the seven days were almost completed, the Jews from Asia, when they saw him in the temple, stirred up all the multitude and laid hands on him,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"crying out, \u201cMen of Israel, help! This is the man who teaches all men everywhere against the people, and the law, and this place. Moreover, he also brought Greeks into the temple and has defiled this holy place!\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For they had seen Trophimus the Ephesian with him in the city, and they supposed that Paul had brought him into the temple."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"All the city was moved and the people ran together. They seized Paul and dragged him out of the temple. Immediately the doors were shut."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"As they were trying to kill him, news came up to the commanding officer of the regiment that all Jerusalem was in an uproar."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Immediately he took soldiers and centurions and ran down to them. They, when they saw the chief captain and the soldiers, stopped beating Paul."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Then the commanding officer came near, arrested him, commanded him to be bound with two chains, and inquired who he was and what he had done."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Some shouted one thing and some another, among the crowd. When he couldn\u2019t find out the truth because of the noise, he commanded him to be brought into the barracks."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"When he came to the stairs, he was carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the crowd;"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"for the multitude of the people followed after, crying out, \u201cAway with him!\u201d"]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"As Paul was about to be brought into the barracks, he asked the commanding officer, \u201cMay I speak to you?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cDo you know Greek?"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t you then the Egyptian who before these days stirred up to sedition and led out into the wilderness the four thousand men of the Assassins?\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"But Paul said, \u201cI am a Jew from Tarsus in Cilicia, a citizen of no insignificant city. I beg you, allow me to speak to the people.\u201d"]]},{v:40,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had given him permission, Paul, standing on the stairs, beckoned with his hand to the people. When there was a great silence, he spoke to them in the Hebrew language, saying,"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBrothers and fathers, listen to the defense which I now make to you.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"When they heard that he spoke to them in the Hebrew language, they were even more quiet."],[0,"He said,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cI am indeed a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia, but brought up in this city at the feet of Gamaliel, instructed according to the strict tradition of the law of our fathers, being zealous for God, even as you all are today."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I persecuted this Way to the death, binding and delivering into prisons both men and women,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"as also the high priest and all the council of the elders testify, from whom also I received letters to the brothers, and traveled to Damascus to bring them also who were there to Jerusalem in bonds to be punished."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAs I made my journey and came close to Damascus, about noon suddenly a great light shone around me from the sky."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I fell to the ground and heard a voice saying to me, \u2018Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me?\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I answered, \u2018Who are you, Lord?\u2019 He said to me, \u2018I am Jesus of Nazareth, whom you persecute.\u2019"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThose who were with me indeed saw the light and were afraid, but they didn\u2019t understand the voice of him who spoke to me."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I said, \u2018What shall I do, Lord?\u2019 The Lord said to me, \u2018Arise, and go into Damascus. There you will be told about all things which are appointed for you to do.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When I couldn\u2019t see for the glory of that light, being led by the hand of those who were with me, I came into Damascus."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cOne Ananias, a devout man according to the law, well reported of by all the Jews who lived in Damascus,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"came to me, and standing by me said to me, \u2018Brother Saul, receive your sight!\u2019 In that very hour I looked up at him."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He said, \u2018The God of our fathers has appointed you to know his will, and to see the Righteous One, and to hear a voice from his mouth."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For you will be a witness for him to all men of what you have seen and heard."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Now why do you wait? Arise, be baptized, and wash away your sins, calling on the name of the Lord.\u2019"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhen I had returned to Jerusalem and while I prayed in the temple, I fell into a trance"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and saw him saying to me, \u2018Hurry and get out of Jerusalem quickly, because they will not receive testimony concerning me from you.\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I said, \u2018Lord, they themselves know that I imprisoned and beat in every synagogue those who believed in you."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When the blood of Stephen, your witness, was shed, I also was standing by, consenting to his death, and guarding the cloaks of those who killed him.\u2019"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cHe said to me, \u2018Depart, for I will send you out far from here to the Gentiles.\u2019 \u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"They listened to him until he said that; then they lifted up their voice and said, \u201cRid the earth of this fellow, for he isn\u2019t fit to live!\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"As they cried out, threw off their cloaks, and threw dust into the air,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"the commanding officer commanded him to be brought into the barracks, ordering him to be examined by scourging, that he might know for what crime they shouted against him like that."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When they had tied him up with straps, Paul asked the centurion who stood by, \u201cIs it lawful for you to scourge a man who is a Roman, and not found guilty?\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"When the centurion heard it, he went to the commanding officer and told him, \u201cWatch what you are about to do, for this man is a Roman!\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"The commanding officer came and asked him, \u201cTell me, are you a Roman?\u201d"],[0,"He said, \u201cYes.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The commanding officer answered, \u201cI bought my citizenship for a great price.\u201d"],[0,"Paul said, \u201cBut I was born a Roman.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately those who were about to examine him departed from him, and the commanding officer also was afraid when he realized that he was a Roman, because he had bound him."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But on the next day, desiring to know the truth about why he was accused by the Jews, he freed him from the bonds and commanded the chief priests and all the council to come together, and brought Paul down and set him before them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, looking steadfastly at the council, said, \u201cBrothers, I have lived before God in all good conscience until today.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The high priest, Ananias, commanded those who stood by him to strike him on the mouth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Paul said to him, \u201cGod will strike you, you whitewashed wall! Do you sit to judge me according to the law, and command me to be struck contrary to the law?\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Those who stood by said, \u201cDo you malign God\u2019s high priest?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul said, \u201cI didn\u2019t know, brothers, that he was high priest. For it is written, \u2018You shall not speak evil of a ruler of your people.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Paul perceived that the one part were Sadducees and the other Pharisees, he cried out in the council, \u201cMen and brothers, I am a Pharisee, a son of Pharisees. Concerning the hope and resurrection of the dead I am being judged!\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had said this, an argument arose between the Pharisees and Sadducees, and the crowd was divided."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For the Sadducees say that there is no resurrection, nor angel, nor spirit; but the Pharisees confess all of these."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"A great clamor arose, and some of the scribes of the Pharisees\u2019 part stood up, and contended, saying, \u201cWe find no evil in this man. But if a spirit or angel has spoken to him, let\u2019s not fight against God!\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When a great argument arose, the commanding officer, fearing that Paul would be torn in pieces by them, commanded the soldiers to go down and take him by force from among them and bring him into the barracks."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"The following night, the Lord stood by him and said, \u201cCheer up, Paul, for as you have testified about me at Jerusalem, so you must testify also at Rome.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When it was day, some of the Jews banded together and bound themselves under a curse, saying that they would neither eat nor drink until they had killed Paul."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"There were more than forty people who had made this conspiracy."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"They came to the chief priests and the elders, and said, \u201cWe have bound ourselves under a great curse to taste nothing until we have killed Paul."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now therefore, you with the council inform the commanding officer that he should bring him down to you tomorrow, as though you were going to judge his case more exactly. We are ready to kill him before he comes near.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But Paul\u2019s sister\u2019s son heard they were lying in wait, and he came and entered into the barracks and told Paul."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Paul summoned one of the centurions and said, \u201cBring this young man to the commanding officer, for he has something to tell him.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"So he took him and brought him to the commanding officer and said, \u201cPaul, the prisoner, summoned me and asked me to bring this young man to you. He has something to tell you.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The commanding officer took him by the hand, and going aside, asked him privately, \u201cWhat is it that you have to tell me?\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"He said, \u201cThe Jews have agreed to ask you to bring Paul down to the council tomorrow, as though intending to inquire somewhat more accurately concerning him."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t yield to them, for more than forty men lie in wait for him, who have bound themselves under a curse to neither eat nor drink until they have killed him. Now they are ready, looking for the promise from you.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"So the commanding officer let the young man go, charging him, \u201cTell no one that you have revealed these things to me.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"He called to himself two of the centurions, and said, \u201cPrepare two hundred soldiers to go as far as Caesarea, with seventy horsemen and two hundred men armed with spears, at the third hour of the night.\u201d"]],f:["about 9:00 p.m."]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He asked them to provide mounts, that they might set Paul on one, and bring him safely to Felix the governor."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"He wrote a letter like this:"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cClaudius Lysias to the most excellent governor Felix: Greetings."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cThis man was seized by the Jews, and was about to be killed by them when I came with the soldiers and rescued him, having learned that he was a Roman."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Desiring to know the cause why they accused him, I brought him down to their council."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I found him to be accused about questions of their law, but not to be charged with anything worthy of death or of imprisonment."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"When I was told that the Jews lay in wait for the man, I sent him to you immediately, charging his accusers also to bring their accusations against him before you. Farewell.\u201d"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"So the soldiers, carrying out their orders, took Paul and brought him by night to Antipatris."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"But on the next day they left the horsemen to go with him, and returned to the barracks."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"When they came to Caesarea and delivered the letter to the governor, they also presented Paul to him."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"When the governor had read it, he asked what province he was from. When he understood that he was from Cilicia, he said,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"\u201cI will hear you fully when your accusers also arrive.\u201d He commanded that he be kept in Herod\u2019s palace."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After five days, the high priest, Ananias, came down with certain elders and an orator, one Tertullus. They informed the governor against Paul."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"When he was called, Tertullus began to accuse him, saying, \u201cSeeing that by you we enjoy much peace, and that prosperity is coming to this nation by your foresight,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"we accept it in all ways and in all places, most excellent Felix, with all thankfulness."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But that I don\u2019t delay you, I entreat you to bear with us and hear a few words."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For we have found this man to be a plague, an instigator of insurrections among all the Jews throughout the world, and a ringleader of the sect of the Nazarenes."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He even tried to profane the temple, and we arrested him."]],f:["TR adds \u201cWe wanted to judge him according to our law,\u201d"]},{v:7,l:[],f:["TR adds \u201cbut the commanding officer, Lysias, came by and with great violence took him out of our hands,\u201d"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"By examining him yourself you may ascertain all these things of which we accuse him.\u201d"]],f:["TR adds \u201ccommanding his accusers to come to you.\u201d"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The Jews also joined in the attack, affirming that these things were so."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"When the governor had beckoned to him to speak, Paul answered, \u201cBecause I know that you have been a judge of this nation for many years, I cheerfully make my defense,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"seeing that you can verify that it is not more than twelve days since I went up to worship at Jerusalem."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"In the temple they didn\u2019t find me disputing with anyone or stirring up a crowd, either in the synagogues or in the city."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Nor can they prove to you the things of which they now accuse me."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But this I confess to you, that according to the Way, which they call a sect, so I serve the God of our fathers, believing all things which are according to the law, and which are written in the prophets;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"having hope toward God, which these also themselves look for, that there will be a resurrection of the dead, both of the just and unjust."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"In this I also practice always having a conscience void of offense toward God and men."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now after some years, I came to bring gifts for the needy to my nation, and offerings;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"amid which certain Jews from Asia found me purified in the temple, not with a mob, nor with turmoil."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They ought to have been here before you and to make accusation if they had anything against me."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Or else let these men themselves say what injustice they found in me when I stood before the council,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"unless it is for this one thing that I cried standing among them, \u2018Concerning the resurrection of the dead I am being judged before you today!\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But Felix, having more exact knowledge concerning the Way, deferred them, saying, \u201cWhen Lysias, the commanding officer, comes down, I will decide your case.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"He ordered the centurion that Paul should be kept in custody and should have some privileges, and not to forbid any of his friends to serve him or to visit him."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"After some days, Felix came with Drusilla his wife, who was a Jewess, and sent for Paul and heard him concerning the faith in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"As he reasoned about righteousness, self-control, and the judgment to come, Felix was terrified, and answered, \u201cGo your way for this time, and when it is convenient for me, I will summon you.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Meanwhile, he also hoped that money would be given to him by Paul, that he might release him. Therefore also he sent for him more often and talked with him."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But when two years were fulfilled, Felix was succeeded by Porcius Festus, and desiring to gain favor with the Jews, Felix left Paul in bonds."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Festus therefore, having come into the province, after three days went up to Jerusalem from Caesarea."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then the high priest and the principal men of the Jews informed him against Paul, and they begged him,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"asking a favor against him, that he would summon him to Jerusalem, plotting to kill him on the way."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"However Festus answered that Paul should be kept in custody at Caesarea, and that he himself was about to depart shortly."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"\u201cLet them therefore\u201d, he said, \u201cthat are in power among you go down with me, and if there is anything wrong in the man, let them accuse him.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had stayed among them more than ten days, he went down to Caesarea, and on the next day he sat on the judgment seat, and commanded Paul to be brought."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When he had come, the Jews who had come down from Jerusalem stood around him, bringing against him many and grievous charges which they could not prove,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"while he said in his defense, \u201cNeither against the law of the Jews, nor against the temple, nor against Caesar, have I sinned at all.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"But Festus, desiring to gain favor with the Jews, answered Paul and said, \u201cAre you willing to go up to Jerusalem and be judged by me there concerning these things?\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But Paul said, \u201cI am standing before Caesar\u2019s judgment seat, where I ought to be tried. I have done no wrong to the Jews, as you also know very well."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For if I have done wrong and have committed anything worthy of death, I don\u2019t refuse to die; but if none of those things is true that they accuse me of, no one can give me up to them. I appeal to Caesar!\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Then Festus, when he had conferred with the council, answered, \u201cYou have appealed to Caesar. To Caesar you shall go.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when some days had passed, King Agrippa and Bernice arrived at Caesarea and greeted Festus."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"As he stayed there many days, Festus laid Paul\u2019s case before the king, saying, \u201cThere is a certain man left a prisoner by Felix;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"about whom, when I was at Jerusalem, the chief priests and the elders of the Jews informed me, asking for a sentence against him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I answered them that it is not the custom of the Romans to give up any man to destruction before the accused has met the accusers face to face and has had opportunity to make his defense concerning the matter laid against him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When therefore they had come together here, I didn\u2019t delay, but on the next day sat on the judgment seat and commanded the man to be brought."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"When the accusers stood up, they brought no charges against him of such things as I supposed;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"but had certain questions against him about their own religion and about one Jesus, who was dead, whom Paul affirmed to be alive."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Being perplexed how to inquire concerning these things, I asked whether he was willing to go to Jerusalem and there be judged concerning these matters."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But when Paul had appealed to be kept for the decision of the emperor, I commanded him to be kept until I could send him to Caesar.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Agrippa said to Festus, \u201cI also would like to hear the man myself.\u201d"],[0,"\u201cTomorrow,\u201d he said, \u201cyou shall hear him.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"So on the next day, when Agrippa and Bernice had come with great pomp, and they had entered into the place of hearing with the commanding officers and the principal men of the city, at the command of Festus, Paul was brought in."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Festus said, \u201cKing Agrippa, and all men who are here present with us, you see this man about whom all the multitude of the Jews petitioned me, both at Jerusalem and here, crying that he ought not to live any longer."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But when I found that he had committed nothing worthy of death, and as he himself appealed to the emperor, I determined to send him,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"of whom I have no certain thing to write to my lord. Therefore I have brought him out before you, and especially before you, King Agrippa, that, after examination I may have something to write."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For it seems to me unreasonable, in sending a prisoner, not to also specify the charges against him.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Agrippa said to Paul, \u201cYou may speak for yourself.\u201d"],[0,"Then Paul stretched out his hand, and made his defense."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cI think myself happy, King Agrippa, that I am to make my defense before you today concerning all the things the Jews accuse me of,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"especially because you are expert in all customs and questions which are among the Jews. Therefore I beg you to hear me patiently."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cIndeed, all the Jews know my way of life from my youth up, which was from the beginning among my own nation and at Jerusalem;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"having known me from the first, if they are willing to testify, that after the strictest sect of our religion I lived a Pharisee."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now I stand here to be judged for the hope of the promise made by God to our fathers,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"which our twelve tribes, earnestly serving night and day, hope to attain. Concerning this hope I am accused by the Jews, King Agrippa!"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Why is it judged incredible with you if God does raise the dead?"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI myself most certainly thought that I ought to do many things contrary to the name of Jesus of Nazareth."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I also did this in Jerusalem. I both shut up many of the saints in prisons, having received authority from the chief priests; and when they were put to death I gave my vote against them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Punishing them often in all the synagogues, I tried to make them blaspheme. Being exceedingly enraged against them, I persecuted them even to foreign cities."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWhereupon as I traveled to Damascus with the authority and commission from the chief priests,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"at noon, O king, I saw on the way a light from the sky, brighter than the sun, shining around me and those who traveled with me."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"When we had all fallen to the earth, I heard a voice saying to me in the Hebrew language, \u2018Saul, Saul, why are you persecuting me? It is hard for you to kick against the goads.\u2019"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI said, \u2018Who are you, Lord?\u2019"],[0,"\u201cHe said, \u2018I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But arise, and stand on your feet, for I have appeared to you for this purpose: to appoint you a servant and a witness both of the things which you have seen and of the things which I will reveal to you;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"delivering you from the people and from the Gentiles, to whom I send you,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"to open their eyes, that they may turn from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to God, that they may receive remission of sins and an inheritance among those who are sanctified by faith in me.\u2019"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTherefore, King Agrippa, I was not disobedient to the heavenly vision,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but declared first to them of Damascus, at Jerusalem, and throughout all the country of Judea, and also to the Gentiles, that they should repent and turn to God, doing works worthy of repentance."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For this reason the Jews seized me in the temple and tried to kill me."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Having therefore obtained the help that is from God, I stand to this day testifying both to small and great, saying nothing but what the prophets and Moses said would happen,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"how the Christ must suffer, and how, by the resurrection of the dead, he would be first to proclaim light both to these people and to the Gentiles.\u201d"]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"As he thus made his defense, Festus said with a loud voice, \u201cPaul, you are crazy! Your great learning is driving you insane!\u201d"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But he said, \u201cI am not crazy, most excellent Festus, but boldly declare words of truth and reasonableness."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For the king knows of these things, to whom also I speak freely. For I am persuaded that none of these things is hidden from him, for this has not been done in a corner."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know that you believe.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Agrippa said to Paul, \u201cWith a little persuasion are you trying to make me a Christian?\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul said, \u201cI pray to God, that whether with little or with much, not only you, but also all that hear me today, might become such as I am, except for these bonds.\u201d"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"The king rose up with the governor and Bernice, and those who sat with them."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"When they had withdrawn, they spoke to one another, saying, \u201cThis man does nothing worthy of death or of bonds.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Agrippa said to Festus, \u201cThis man might have been set free if he had not appealed to Caesar.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When it was determined that we should sail for Italy, they delivered Paul and certain other prisoners to a centurion named Julius, of the Augustan band."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Embarking in a ship of Adramyttium, which was about to sail to places on the coast of Asia, we put to sea, Aristarchus, a Macedonian of Thessalonica being with us."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"The next day, we touched at Sidon. Julius treated Paul kindly and gave him permission to go to his friends and refresh himself."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Putting to sea from there, we sailed under the lee of Cyprus, because the winds were contrary."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"When we had sailed across the sea which is off Cilicia and Pamphylia, we came to Myra, a city of Lycia."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"There the centurion found a ship of Alexandria sailing for Italy, and he put us on board."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"When we had sailed slowly many days, and had come with difficulty opposite Cnidus, the wind not allowing us further, we sailed under the lee of Crete, opposite Salmone."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"With difficulty sailing along it we came to a certain place called Fair Havens, near the city of Lasea."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When much time had passed and the voyage was now dangerous because the Fast had now already gone by, Paul admonished them"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and said to them, \u201cSirs, I perceive that the voyage will be with injury and much loss, not only of the cargo and the ship, but also of our lives.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But the centurion gave more heed to the master and to the owner of the ship than to those things which were spoken by Paul."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Because the haven was not suitable to winter in, the majority advised going to sea from there, if by any means they could reach Phoenix and winter there, which is a port of Crete, looking southwest and northwest."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When the south wind blew softly, supposing that they had obtained their purpose, they weighed anchor and sailed along Crete, close to shore."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But before long, a stormy wind beat down from shore, which is called Euroclydon."]],f:["Or, \u201ca northeaster\u201d."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"When the ship was caught and couldn\u2019t face the wind, we gave way to it and were driven along."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Running under the lee of a small island called Clauda, we were able, with difficulty, to secure the boat."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"After they had hoisted it up, they used cables to help reinforce the ship. Fearing that they would run aground on the Syrtis sand bars, they lowered the sea anchor, and so were driven along."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"As we labored exceedingly with the storm, the next day they began to throw things overboard."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"On the third day, they threw out the ship\u2019s tackle with their own hands."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When neither sun nor stars shone on us for many days, and no small storm pressed on us, all hope that we would be saved was now taken away."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had been long without food, Paul stood up in the middle of them and said, \u201cSirs, you should have listened to me, and not have set sail from Crete and have gotten this injury and loss."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Now I exhort you to cheer up, for there will be no loss of life among you, but only of the ship."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For there stood by me this night an angel, belonging to the God whose I am and whom I serve,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"saying, \u2018Don\u2019t be afraid, Paul. You must stand before Caesar. Behold, God has granted you all those who sail with you.\u2019"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Therefore, sirs, cheer up! For I believe God, that it will be just as it has been spoken to me."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But we must run aground on a certain island.\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"But when the fourteenth night had come, as we were driven back and forth in the Adriatic Sea, about midnight the sailors surmised that they were drawing near to some land."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"They took soundings and found twenty fathoms. After a little while, they took soundings again, and found fifteen fathoms."]],f:["20 fathoms = 120 feet = 36.6 meters","15 fathoms = 90 feet = 27.4 meters"]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Fearing that we would run aground on rocky ground, they let go four anchors from the stern, and wished for daylight."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"As the sailors were trying to flee out of the ship and had lowered the boat into the sea, pretending that they would lay out anchors from the bow,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Paul said to the centurion and to the soldiers, \u201cUnless these stay in the ship, you can\u2019t be saved.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Then the soldiers cut away the ropes of the boat and let it fall off."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"While the day was coming on, Paul begged them all to take some food, saying, \u201cToday is the fourteenth day that you wait and continue fasting, having taken nothing."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Therefore I beg you to take some food, for this is for your safety; for not a hair will perish from any of your heads.\u201d"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"When he had said this and had taken bread, he gave thanks to God in the presence of all; then he broke it and began to eat."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Then they all cheered up, and they also took food."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"In all, we were two hundred seventy-six souls on the ship."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"When they had eaten enough, they lightened the ship, throwing out the wheat into the sea."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"When it was day, they didn\u2019t recognize the land, but they noticed a certain bay with a beach, and they decided to try to drive the ship onto it."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Casting off the anchors, they left them in the sea, at the same time untying the rudder ropes. Hoisting up the foresail to the wind, they made for the beach."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"But coming to a place where two seas met, they ran the vessel aground. The bow struck and remained immovable, but the stern began to break up by the violence of the waves."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"The soldiers\u2019 counsel was to kill the prisoners, so that none of them would swim out and escape."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"But the centurion, desiring to save Paul, stopped them from their purpose, and commanded that those who could swim should throw themselves overboard first to go toward the land;"]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"and the rest should follow, some on planks and some on other things from the ship. So they all escaped safely to the land."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When we had escaped, then they learned that the island was called Malta."]],f:["NU reads \u201cwe\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The natives showed us uncommon kindness; for they kindled a fire and received us all, because of the present rain and because of the cold."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But when Paul had gathered a bundle of sticks and laid them on the fire, a viper came out because of the heat and fastened on his hand."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When the natives saw the creature hanging from his hand, they said to one another, \u201cNo doubt this man is a murderer, whom, though he has escaped from the sea, yet Justice has not allowed to live.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"However he shook off the creature into the fire, and wasn\u2019t harmed."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But they expected that he would have swollen or fallen down dead suddenly, but when they watched for a long time and saw nothing bad happen to him, they changed their minds and said that he was a god."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the neighborhood of that place were lands belonging to the chief man of the island, named Publius, who received us and courteously entertained us for three days."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The father of Publius lay sick of fever and dysentery. Paul entered in to him, prayed, and laying his hands on him, healed him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Then when this was done, the rest also who had diseases in the island came and were cured."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They also honored us with many honors; and when we sailed, they put on board the things that we needed."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"After three months, we set sail in a ship of Alexandria which had wintered in the island, whose figurehead was \u201cThe Twin Brothers.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Touching at Syracuse, we stayed there three days."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"From there we circled around and arrived at Rhegium. After one day, a south wind sprang up, and on the second day we came to Puteoli,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"where we found brothers, and were entreated to stay with them for seven days. So we came to Rome."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"From there the brothers, when they heard of us, came to meet us as far as The Market of Appius and The Three Taverns. When Paul saw them, he thanked God and took courage."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When we entered into Rome, the centurion delivered the prisoners to the captain of the guard, but Paul was allowed to stay by himself with the soldier who guarded him."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"After three days Paul called together those who were the leaders of the Jews. When they had come together, he said to them, \u201cI, brothers, though I had done nothing against the people or the customs of our fathers, still was delivered prisoner from Jerusalem into the hands of the Romans,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"who, when they had examined me, desired to set me free, because there was no cause of death in me."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But when the Jews spoke against it, I was constrained to appeal to Caesar, not that I had anything about which to accuse my nation."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For this cause therefore I asked to see you and to speak with you. For because of the hope of Israel I am bound with this chain.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"They said to him, \u201cWe neither received letters from Judea concerning you, nor did any of the brothers come here and report or speak any evil of you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But we desire to hear from you what you think. For, as concerning this sect, it is known to us that everywhere it is spoken against.\u201d"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"When they had appointed him a day, many people came to him at his lodging. He explained to them, testifying about God\u2019s Kingdom, and persuading them concerning Jesus, both from the law of Moses and from the prophets, from morning until evening."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Some believed the things which were spoken, and some disbelieved."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"When they didn\u2019t agree among themselves, they departed after Paul had spoken one message: \u201cThe Holy Spirit spoke rightly through Isaiah the prophet to our fathers,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"saying,"],[1,"\u2018Go to this people and say,"],[1,"in hearing, you will hear,"],[2,"but will in no way understand."],[1,"In seeing, you will see,"],[2,"but will in no way perceive."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"For this people\u2019s heart has grown callous."],[2,"Their ears are dull of hearing."],[2,"Their eyes they have closed."],[1,"Lest they should see with their eyes,"],[2,"hear with their ears,"],[2,"understand with their heart,"],[2,"and would turn again,"],[2,"then I would heal them.\u2019"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBe it known therefore to you that the salvation of God is sent to the nations, and they will listen.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"When he had said these words, the Jews departed, having a great dispute among themselves."]],f:["NU omits verse 29."]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul stayed two whole years in his own rented house and received all who were coming to him,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"preaching God\u2019s Kingdom and teaching the things concerning the Lord Jesus Christ with all boldness, without hindrance."]]}]]}},1315,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,h,i,s,a){i.exports={book:"Rom",name:"Romans",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, a servant of Jesus Christ, called to be an apostle, set apart for the Good News of God,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"which he promised before through his prophets in the holy Scriptures,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"concerning his Son, who was born of the offspring of David according to the flesh,"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"who was declared to be the Son of God with power according to the Spirit of holiness, by the resurrection from the dead, Jesus Christ our Lord,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"through whom we received grace and apostleship for obedience of faith among all the nations for his name\u2019s sake;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"among whom you are also called to belong to Jesus Christ;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"to all who are in Rome, beloved of God, called to be saints: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"First, I thank my God through Jesus Christ for all of you, that your faith is proclaimed throughout the whole world."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For God is my witness, whom I serve in my spirit in the Good News of his Son, how unceasingly I make mention of you always in my prayers,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"requesting, if by any means now at last I may be prospered by the will of God to come to you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For I long to see you, that I may impart to you some spiritual gift, to the end that you may be established;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that is, that I with you may be encouraged in you, each of us by the other\u2019s faith, both yours and mine."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I don\u2019t desire to have you unaware, brothers, that I often planned to come to you (and was hindered so far), that I might have some fruit among you also, even as among the rest of the Gentiles."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I am debtor both to Greeks and to foreigners, both to the wise and to the foolish."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So as much as is in me, I am eager to preach the Good News to you also who are in Rome."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"For I am not ashamed of the Good News of Christ, because it is the power of God for salvation for everyone who believes, for the Jew first, and also for the Greek."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For in it is revealed God\u2019s righteousness from faith to faith. As it is written, \u201cBut the righteous shall live by faith.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"For the wrath of God is revealed from heaven against all ungodliness and unrighteousness of men who suppress the truth in unrighteousness,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"because that which is known of God is revealed in them, for God revealed it to them."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For the invisible things of him since the creation of the world are clearly seen, being perceived through the things that are made, even his everlasting power and divinity, that they may be without excuse."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Because knowing God, they didn\u2019t glorify him as God, and didn\u2019t give thanks, but became vain in their reasoning, and their senseless heart was darkened."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Professing themselves to be wise, they became fools,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and traded the glory of the incorruptible God for the likeness of an image of corruptible man, and of birds, four-footed animals, and creeping things."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Therefore God also gave them up in the lusts of their hearts to uncleanness, that their bodies should be dishonored among themselves;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"who exchanged the truth of God for a lie, and worshiped and served the creature rather than the Creator, who is blessed forever. Amen."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"For this reason, God gave them up to vile passions. For their women changed the natural function into that which is against nature."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Likewise also the men, leaving the natural function of the woman, burned in their lust toward one another, men doing what is inappropriate with men, and receiving in themselves the due penalty of their error."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Even as they refused to have God in their knowledge, God gave them up to a reprobate mind, to do those things which are not fitting;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"being filled with all unrighteousness, sexual immorality, wickedness, covetousness, malice; full of envy, murder, strife, deceit, evil habits, secret slanderers,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"backbiters, hateful to God, insolent, arrogant, boastful, inventors of evil things, disobedient to parents,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"without understanding, covenant breakers, without natural affection, unforgiving, unmerciful;"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"who, knowing the ordinance of God, that those who practice such things are worthy of death, not only do the same, but also approve of those who practice them."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore you are without excuse, O man, whoever you are who judge. For in that which you judge another, you condemn yourself. For you who judge practice the same things."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"We know that the judgment of God is according to truth against those who practice such things."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Do you think this, O man who judges those who practice such things, and do the same, that you will escape the judgment of God?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Or do you despise the riches of his goodness, forbearance, and patience, not knowing that the goodness of God leads you to repentance?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But according to your hardness and unrepentant heart you are treasuring up for yourself wrath in the day of wrath, revelation, and of the righteous judgment of God,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"who \u201cwill pay back to everyone according to their works:\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"to those who by perseverance in well-doing seek for glory, honor, and incorruptibility, eternal life;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but to those who are self-seeking and don\u2019t obey the truth, but obey unrighteousness, will be wrath, indignation,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"oppression, and anguish on every soul of man who does evil, to the Jew first, and also to the Greek."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But glory, honor, and peace go to every man who does good, to the Jew first, and also to the Greek."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For there is no partiality with God."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For as many as have sinned without the law will also perish without the law. As many as have sinned under the law will be judged by the law."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For it isn\u2019t the hearers of the law who are righteous before God, but the doers of the law will be justified"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"(for when Gentiles who don\u2019t have the law do by nature the things of the law, these, not having the law, are a law to themselves,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"in that they show the work of the law written in their hearts, their conscience testifying with them, and their thoughts among themselves accusing or else excusing them)"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"in the day when God will judge the secrets of men, according to my Good News, by Jesus Christ."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Indeed you bear the name of a Jew, rest on the law, glory in God,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"know his will, and approve the things that are excellent, being instructed out of the law,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and are confident that you yourself are a guide of the blind, a light to those who are in darkness,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"a corrector of the foolish, a teacher of babies, having in the law the form of knowledge and of the truth."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You therefore who teach another, don\u2019t you teach yourself? You who preach that a man shouldn\u2019t steal, do you steal?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You who say a man shouldn\u2019t commit adultery, do you commit adultery? You who abhor idols, do you rob temples?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You who glory in the law, do you dishonor God by disobeying the law?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For \u201cthe name of God is blasphemed among the Gentiles because of you,\u201d just as it is written."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For circumcision indeed profits, if you are a doer of the law, but if you are a transgressor of the law, your circumcision has become uncircumcision."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"If therefore the uncircumcised keep the ordinances of the law, won\u2019t his uncircumcision be accounted as circumcision?"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Won\u2019t those who are physically uncircumcised, but fulfill the law, judge you, who with the letter and circumcision are a transgressor of the law?"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For he is not a Jew who is one outwardly, neither is that circumcision which is outward in the flesh;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"but he is a Jew who is one inwardly, and circumcision is that of the heart, in the spirit, not in the letter; whose praise is not from men, but from God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then what advantage does the Jew have? Or what is the profit of circumcision?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Much in every way! Because first of all, they were entrusted with the revelations of God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For what if some were without faith? Will their lack of faith nullify the faithfulness of God?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"May it never be! Yes, let God be found true, but every man a liar. As it is written,"],[1,"\u201cthat you might be justified in your words,"],[2,"and might prevail when you come into judgment.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But if our unrighteousness commends the righteousness of God, what will we say? Is God unrighteous who inflicts wrath? I speak like men do."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"May it never be! For then how will God judge the world?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For if the truth of God through my lie abounded to his glory, why am I also still judged as a sinner?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Why not (as we are slanderously reported, and as some affirm that we say), \u201cLet\u2019s do evil, that good may come?\u201d Those who say so are justly condemned."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"What then? Are we better than they? No, in no way. For we previously warned both Jews and Greeks that they are all under sin."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As it is written,"],[1,"\u201cThere is no one righteous;"],[2,"no, not one."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"There is no one who understands."],[2,"There is no one who seeks after God."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"They have all turned away."],[2,"They have together become unprofitable."],[1,"There is no one who does good,"],[2,"no, not so much as one.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTheir throat is an open tomb."],[2,"With their tongues they have used deceit.\u201d"],[1,"\u201cThe poison of vipers is under their lips.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[2,"\u201cTheir mouth is full of cursing and bitterness.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cTheir feet are swift to shed blood."]]},{v:16,l:[[2,"Destruction and misery are in their ways."]]},{v:17,l:[[2,"The way of peace, they haven\u2019t known.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThere is no fear of God before their eyes.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Now we know that whatever things the law says, it speaks to those who are under the law, that every mouth may be closed, and all the world may be brought under the judgment of God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Because by the works of the law, no flesh will be justified in his sight; for through the law comes the knowledge of sin."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"But now apart from the law, a righteousness of God has been revealed, being testified by the law and the prophets;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"even the righteousness of God through faith in Jesus Christ to all and on all those who believe. For there is no distinction,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"for all have sinned, and fall short of the glory of God;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"being justified freely by his grace through the redemption that is in Christ Jesus,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"whom God sent to be an atoning sacrifice through faith in his blood, for a demonstration of his righteousness through the passing over of prior sins, in God\u2019s forbearance;"]],f:["or, a propitiation"]},{v:26,l:[[0,"to demonstrate his righteousness at this present time, that he might himself be just and the justifier of him who has faith in Jesus."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Where then is the boasting? It is excluded. By what kind of law? Of works? No, but by a law of faith."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"We maintain therefore that a man is justified by faith apart from the works of the law."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Or is God the God of Jews only? Isn\u2019t he the God of Gentiles also? Yes, of Gentiles also,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"since indeed there is one God who will justify the circumcised by faith and the uncircumcised through faith."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Do we then nullify the law through faith? May it never be! No, we establish the law."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"What then will we say that Abraham, our forefather, has found according to the flesh?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For if Abraham was justified by works, he has something to boast about, but not toward God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For what does the Scripture say? \u201cAbraham believed God, and it was accounted to him for righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now to him who works, the reward is not counted as grace, but as something owed."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But to him who doesn\u2019t work, but believes in him who justifies the ungodly, his faith is accounted for righteousness."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Even as David also pronounces blessing on the man to whom God counts righteousness apart from works:"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cBlessed are they whose iniquities are forgiven,"],[2,"whose sins are covered."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"Blessed is the man whom the Lord will by no means charge with sin.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Is this blessing then pronounced only on the circumcised, or on the uncircumcised also? For we say that faith was accounted to Abraham for righteousness."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"How then was it counted? When he was in circumcision, or in uncircumcision? Not in circumcision, but in uncircumcision."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He received the sign of circumcision, a seal of the righteousness of the faith which he had while he was in uncircumcision, that he might be the father of all those who believe, though they might be in uncircumcision, that righteousness might also be accounted to them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He is the father of circumcision to those who not only are of the circumcision, but who also walk in the steps of that faith of our father Abraham, which he had in uncircumcision."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"For the promise to Abraham and to his offspring that he would be heir of the world wasn\u2019t through the law, but through the righteousness of faith."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For if those who are of the law are heirs, faith is made void, and the promise is made of no effect."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For the law produces wrath; for where there is no law, neither is there disobedience."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause it is of faith, that it may be according to grace, to the end that the promise may be sure to all the offspring, not to that only which is of the law, but to that also which is of the faith of Abraham, who is the father of us all."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"As it is written, \u201cI have made you a father of many nations.\u201d This is in the presence of him whom he believed: God, who gives life to the dead, and calls the things that are not, as though they were."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Against hope, Abraham in hope believed, to the end that he might become a father of many nations, according to that which had been spoken, \u201cSo will your offspring be.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Without being weakened in faith, he didn\u2019t consider his own body, already having been worn out, (he being about a hundred years old), and the deadness of Sarah\u2019s womb."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Yet, looking to the promise of God, he didn\u2019t waver through unbelief, but grew strong through faith, giving glory to God,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and being fully assured that what he had promised, he was also able to perform."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Therefore it also was \u201ccredited to him for righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now it was not written that it was accounted to him for his sake alone,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"but for our sake also, to whom it will be accounted, who believe in him who raised Jesus our Lord from the dead,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"who was delivered up for our trespasses, and was raised for our justification."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Being therefore justified by faith, we have peace with God through our Lord Jesus Christ;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"through whom we also have our access by faith into this grace in which we stand. We rejoice in hope of the glory of God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Not only this, but we also rejoice in our sufferings, knowing that suffering produces perseverance;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and perseverance, proven character; and proven character, hope;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and hope doesn\u2019t disappoint us, because God\u2019s love has been poured into our hearts through the Holy Spirit who was given to us."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"For while we were yet weak, at the right time Christ died for the ungodly."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For one will hardly die for a righteous man. Yet perhaps for a good person someone would even dare to die."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But God commends his own love toward us, in that while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Much more then, being now justified by his blood, we will be saved from God\u2019s wrath through him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For if while we were enemies, we were reconciled to God through the death of his Son, much more, being reconciled, we will be saved by his life."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Not only so, but we also rejoice in God through our Lord Jesus Christ, through whom we have now received the reconciliation."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore, as sin entered into the world through one man, and death through sin, so death passed to all men because all sinned."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For until the law, sin was in the world; but sin is not charged when there is no law."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Nevertheless death reigned from Adam until Moses, even over those whose sins weren\u2019t like Adam\u2019s disobedience, who is a foreshadowing of him who was to come."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"But the free gift isn\u2019t like the trespass. For if by the trespass of the one the many died, much more did the grace of God and the gift by the grace of the one man, Jesus Christ, abound to the many."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The gift is not as through one who sinned; for the judgment came by one to condemnation, but the free gift followed many trespasses to justification."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For if by the trespass of the one, death reigned through the one; so much more will those who receive the abundance of grace and of the gift of righteousness reign in life through the one, Jesus Christ."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"So then as through one trespass, all men were condemned; even so through one act of righteousness, all men were justified to life."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For as through the one man\u2019s disobedience many were made sinners, even so through the obedience of the one, many will be made righteous."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The law came in that the trespass might abound; but where sin abounded, grace abounded more exceedingly,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"that as sin reigned in death, even so grace might reign through righteousness to eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"What shall we say then? Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"May it never be! We who died to sin, how could we live in it any longer?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Or don\u2019t you know that all of us who were baptized into Christ Jesus were baptized into his death?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"We were buried therefore with him through baptism into death, that just as Christ was raised from the dead through the glory of the Father, so we also might walk in newness of life."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"For if we have become united with him in the likeness of his death, we will also be part of his resurrection;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"knowing this, that our old man was crucified with him, that the body of sin might be done away with, so that we would no longer be in bondage to sin."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For he who has died has been freed from sin."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But if we died with Christ, we believe that we will also live with him,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"knowing that Christ, being raised from the dead, dies no more. Death no longer has dominion over him!"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the death that he died, he died to sin one time; but the life that he lives, he lives to God."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Thus consider yourselves also to be dead to sin, but alive to God in Christ Jesus our Lord."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t let sin reign in your mortal body, that you should obey it in its lusts."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Also, do not present your members to sin as instruments of unrighteousness, but present yourselves to God as alive from the dead, and your members as instruments of righteousness to God."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For sin will not have dominion over you, for you are not under law, but under grace."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"What then? Shall we sin because we are not under law but under grace? May it never be!"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know that when you present yourselves as servants and obey someone, you are the servants of whomever you obey, whether of sin to death, or of obedience to righteousness?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But thanks be to God that, whereas you were bondservants of sin, you became obedient from the heart to that form of teaching to which you were delivered."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Being made free from sin, you became bondservants of righteousness."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"I speak in human terms because of the weakness of your flesh; for as you presented your members as servants to uncleanness and to wickedness upon wickedness, even so now present your members as servants to righteousness for sanctification."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For when you were servants of sin, you were free from righteousness."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"What fruit then did you have at that time in the things of which you are now ashamed? For the end of those things is death."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But now, being made free from sin and having become servants of God, you have your fruit of sanctification and the result of eternal life."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For the wages of sin is death, but the free gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Or don\u2019t you know, brothers (for I speak to men who know the law), that the law has dominion over a man for as long as he lives?"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For the woman that has a husband is bound by law to the husband while he lives, but if the husband dies, she is discharged from the law of the husband."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So then if, while the husband lives, she is joined to another man, she would be called an adulteress. But if the husband dies, she is free from the law, so that she is no adulteress, though she is joined to another man."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Therefore, my brothers, you also were made dead to the law through the body of Christ, that you would be joined to another, to him who was raised from the dead, that we might produce fruit to God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For when we were in the flesh, the sinful passions which were through the law worked in our members to bring out fruit to death."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But now we have been discharged from the law, having died to that in which we were held; so that we serve in newness of the spirit, and not in oldness of the letter."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"What shall we say then? Is the law sin? May it never be! However, I wouldn\u2019t have known sin except through the law. For I wouldn\u2019t have known coveting unless the law had said, \u201cYou shall not covet.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But sin, finding occasion through the commandment, produced in me all kinds of coveting. For apart from the law, sin is dead."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I was alive apart from the law once, but when the commandment came, sin revived and I died."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The commandment which was for life, this I found to be for death;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"for sin, finding occasion through the commandment, deceived me, and through it killed me."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore the law indeed is holy, and the commandment holy, righteous, and good."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Did then that which is good become death to me? May it never be! But sin, that it might be shown to be sin, was producing death in me through that which is good; that through the commandment sin might become exceedingly sinful."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For we know that the law is spiritual, but I am fleshly, sold under sin."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For I don\u2019t understand what I am doing. For I don\u2019t practice what I desire to do; but what I hate, that I do."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But if what I don\u2019t desire, that I do, I consent to the law that it is good."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So now it is no more I that do it, but sin which dwells in me."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For I know that in me, that is, in my flesh, dwells no good thing. For desire is present with me, but I don\u2019t find it doing that which is good."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the good which I desire, I don\u2019t do; but the evil which I don\u2019t desire, that I practice."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But if what I don\u2019t desire, that I do, it is no more I that do it, but sin which dwells in me."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I find then the law that, while I desire to do good, evil is present."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For I delight in God\u2019s law after the inward person,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"but I see a different law in my members, warring against the law of my mind, and bringing me into captivity under the law of sin which is in my members."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"What a wretched man I am! Who will deliver me out of the body of this death?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"I thank God through Jesus Christ, our Lord! So then with the mind, I myself serve God\u2019s law, but with the flesh, sin\u2019s law."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"There is therefore now no condemnation to those who are in Christ Jesus, who don\u2019t walk according to the flesh, but according to the Spirit."]],f:["NU omits \u201cwho don\u2019t walk according to the flesh, but according to the Spirit\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For the law of the Spirit of life in Christ Jesus made me free from the law of sin and of death."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For what the law couldn\u2019t do, in that it was weak through the flesh, God did, sending his own Son in the likeness of sinful flesh and for sin, he condemned sin in the flesh,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"that the ordinance of the law might be fulfilled in us who don\u2019t walk according to the flesh, but according to the Spirit."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For those who live according to the flesh set their minds on the things of the flesh, but those who live according to the Spirit, the things of the Spirit."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For the mind of the flesh is death, but the mind of the Spirit is life and peace;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"because the mind of the flesh is hostile toward God, for it is not subject to God\u2019s law, neither indeed can it be."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Those who are in the flesh can\u2019t please God."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"But you are not in the flesh but in the Spirit, if it is so that the Spirit of God dwells in you. But if any man doesn\u2019t have the Spirit of Christ, he is not his."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If Christ is in you, the body is dead because of sin, but the spirit is alive because of righteousness."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But if the Spirit of him who raised up Jesus from the dead dwells in you, he who raised up Christ Jesus from the dead will also give life to your mortal bodies through his Spirit who dwells in you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So then, brothers, we are debtors, not to the flesh, to live after the flesh."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For if you live after the flesh, you must die; but if by the Spirit you put to death the deeds of the body, you will live."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For as many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are children of God."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For you didn\u2019t receive the spirit of bondage again to fear, but you received the Spirit of adoption, by whom we cry, \u201cAbba! Father!\u201d"]],f:["Abba is an Aramaic word for \u201cFather\u201d or \u201cDaddy\u201d, which can be used affectionately and respectfully in prayer to our Father in heaven."]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The Spirit himself testifies with our spirit that we are children of God;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and if children, then heirs\u2014heirs of God and joint heirs with Christ, if indeed we suffer with him, that we may also be glorified with him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"For I consider that the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory which will be revealed toward us."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the creation waits with eager expectation for the children of God to be revealed."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For the creation was subjected to vanity, not of its own will, but because of him who subjected it, in hope"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"that the creation itself also will be delivered from the bondage of decay into the liberty of the glory of the children of God."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For we know that the whole creation groans and travails in pain together until now."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Not only so, but ourselves also, who have the first fruits of the Spirit, even we ourselves groan within ourselves, waiting for adoption, the redemption of our body."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For we were saved in hope, but hope that is seen is not hope. For who hopes for that which he sees?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But if we hope for that which we don\u2019t see, we wait for it with patience."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"In the same way, the Spirit also helps our weaknesses, for we don\u2019t know how to pray as we ought. But the Spirit himself makes intercession for us with groanings which can\u2019t be uttered."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He who searches the hearts knows what is on the Spirit\u2019s mind, because he makes intercession for the saints according to God."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"We know that all things work together for good for those who love God, for those who are called according to his purpose."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For whom he foreknew, he also predestined to be conformed to the image of his Son, that he might be the firstborn among many brothers."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Whom he predestined, those he also called. Whom he called, those he also justified. Whom he justified, those he also glorified."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"What then shall we say about these things? If God is for us, who can be against us?"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"He who didn\u2019t spare his own Son, but delivered him up for us all, how would he not also with him freely give us all things?"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Who could bring a charge against God\u2019s chosen ones? It is God who justifies."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Who is he who condemns? It is Christ who died, yes rather, who was raised from the dead, who is at the right hand of God, who also makes intercession for us."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"Who shall separate us from the love of Christ? Could oppression, or anguish, or persecution, or famine, or nakedness, or peril, or sword?"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Even as it is written,"],[1,"\u201cFor your sake we are killed all day long."],[2,"We were accounted as sheep for the slaughter.\u201d"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"No, in all these things we are more than conquerors through him who loved us."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"For I am persuaded that neither death, nor life, nor angels, nor principalities, nor things present, nor things to come, nor powers,"]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"nor height, nor depth, nor any other created thing will be able to separate us from God\u2019s love which is in Christ Jesus our Lord."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I tell the truth in Christ. I am not lying, my conscience testifying with me in the Holy Spirit"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that I have great sorrow and unceasing pain in my heart."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For I could wish that I myself were accursed from Christ for my brothers\u2019 sake, my relatives according to the flesh"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"who are Israelites; whose is the adoption, the glory, the covenants, the giving of the law, the service, and the promises;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"of whom are the fathers, and from whom is Christ as concerning the flesh, who is over all, God, blessed forever. Amen."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But it is not as though the word of God has come to nothing. For they are not all Israel that are of Israel."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Neither, because they are Abraham\u2019s offspring, are they all children. But, \u201cyour offspring will be accounted as from Isaac.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"That is, it is not the children of the flesh who are children of God, but the children of the promise are counted as heirs."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For this is a word of promise: \u201cAt the appointed time I will come, and Sarah will have a son.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Not only so, but Rebekah also conceived by one, by our father Isaac."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For being not yet born, neither having done anything good or bad, that the purpose of God according to election might stand, not of works, but of him who calls,"]],f:["NU puts the phrase \u201cnot of works, but of him who calls\u201d at the beginning of verse 12 instead of the end of verse 11."]},{v:12,l:[[0,"it was said to her, \u201cThe elder will serve the younger.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Even as it is written, \u201cJacob I loved, but Esau I hated.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"What shall we say then? Is there unrighteousness with God? May it never be!"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For he said to Moses, \u201cI will have mercy on whom I have mercy, and I will have compassion on whom I have compassion.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So then it is not of him who wills, nor of him who runs, but of God who has mercy."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For the Scripture says to Pharaoh, \u201cFor this very purpose I caused you to be raised up, that I might show in you my power, and that my name might be proclaimed in all the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"So then, he has mercy on whom he desires, and he hardens whom he desires."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"You will say then to me, \u201cWhy does he still find fault? For who withstands his will?\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But indeed, O man, who are you to reply against God? Will the thing formed ask him who formed it, \u201cWhy did you make me like this?\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Or hasn\u2019t the potter a right over the clay, from the same lump to make one part a vessel for honor, and another for dishonor?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"What if God, willing to show his wrath and to make his power known, endured with much patience vessels of wrath prepared for destruction,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and that he might make known the riches of his glory on vessels of mercy, which he prepared beforehand for glory\u2014"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"us, whom he also called, not from the Jews only, but also from the Gentiles?"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"As he says also in Hosea,"],[1,"\u201cI will call them \u2018my people,\u2019 which were not my people;"],[2,"and her \u2018beloved,\u2019 who was not beloved.\u201d"]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIt will be that in the place where it was said to them, \u2018You are not my people,\u2019"],[2,"there they will be called \u2018children of the living God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah cries concerning Israel,"],[1,"\u201cIf the number of the children of Israel are as the sand of the sea,"],[2,"it is the remnant who will be saved;"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[1,"for he will finish the work and cut it short in righteousness,"],[2,"because the Lord will make a short work upon the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"As Isaiah has said before,"],[1,"\u201cUnless the Lord of Armies had left us a seed,"],[2,"we would have become like Sodom,"],[2,"and would have been made like Gomorrah.\u201d"]],f:["Greek: Sabaoth (or Hebrew: Tze\u2019va\u2019ot)"]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"What shall we say then? That the Gentiles, who didn\u2019t follow after righteousness, attained to righteousness, even the righteousness which is of faith;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"but Israel, following after a law of righteousness, didn\u2019t arrive at the law of righteousness."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Why? Because they didn\u2019t seek it by faith, but as it were by works of the law. They stumbled over the stumbling stone,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"even as it is written,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I lay in Zion a stumbling stone and a rock of offense;"],[2,"and no one who believes in him will be disappointed.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, my heart\u2019s desire and my prayer to God is for Israel, that they may be saved."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For I testify about them that they have a zeal for God, but not according to knowledge."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For being ignorant of God\u2019s righteousness, and seeking to establish their own righteousness, they didn\u2019t subject themselves to the righteousness of God."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For Christ is the fulfillment of the law for righteousness to everyone who believes."]],f:["or, completion, or end"]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"For Moses writes about the righteousness of the law, \u201cThe one who does them will live by them.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But the righteousness which is of faith says this, \u201cDon\u2019t say in your heart, \u2018Who will ascend into heaven?\u2019 (that is, to bring Christ down);"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"or, \u2018Who will descend into the abyss?\u2019 (that is, to bring Christ up from the dead.)\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But what does it say? \u201cThe word is near you, in your mouth and in your heart;\u201d that is, the word of faith which we preach:"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"that if you will confess with your mouth that Jesus is Lord and believe in your heart that God raised him from the dead, you will be saved."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For with the heart one believes resulting in righteousness; and with the mouth confession is made resulting in salvation."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the Scripture says, \u201cWhoever believes in him will not be disappointed.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"For there is no distinction between Jew and Greek; for the same Lord is Lord of all, and is rich to all who call on him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For, \u201cWhoever will call on the name of the Lord will be saved.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"How then will they call on him in whom they have not believed? How will they believe in him whom they have not heard? How will they hear without a preacher?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"And how will they preach unless they are sent? As it is written:"],[1,"\u201cHow beautiful are the feet of those who preach the Good News of peace,"],[2,"who bring glad tidings of good things!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But they didn\u2019t all listen to the glad news. For Isaiah says, \u201cLord, who has believed our report?\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"So faith comes by hearing, and hearing by the word of God."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But I say, didn\u2019t they hear? Yes, most certainly,"],[1,"\u201cTheir sound went out into all the earth,"],[2,"their words to the ends of the world.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But I ask, didn\u2019t Israel know? First Moses says,"],[1,"\u201cI will provoke you to jealousy with that which is no nation."],[2,"I will make you angry with a nation void of understanding.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Isaiah is very bold and says,"],[1,"\u201cI was found by those who didn\u2019t seek me."],[2,"I was revealed to those who didn\u2019t ask for me.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"But about Israel he says, \u201cAll day long I stretched out my hands to a disobedient and contrary people.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I ask then, did God reject his people? May it never be! For I also am an Israelite, a descendant of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"God didn\u2019t reject his people, whom he foreknew. Or don\u2019t you know what the Scripture says about Elijah? How he pleads with God against Israel:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cLord, they have killed your prophets. They have broken down your altars. I am left alone, and they seek my life.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But how does God answer him? \u201cI have reserved for myself seven thousand men who have not bowed the knee to Baal.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Even so too at this present time also there is a remnant according to the election of grace."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"And if by grace, then it is no longer of works; otherwise grace is no longer grace. But if it is of works, it is no longer grace; otherwise work is no longer work."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"What then? That which Israel seeks for, that he didn\u2019t obtain, but the chosen ones obtained it, and the rest were hardened."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"According as it is written, \u201cGod gave them a spirit of stupor, eyes that they should not see, and ears that they should not hear, to this very day.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"David says,"],[1,"\u201cLet their table be made a snare, a trap,"],[2,"a stumbling block, and a retribution to them."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Let their eyes be darkened, that they may not see."],[2,"Always keep their backs bent.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"I ask then, did they stumble that they might fall? May it never be! But by their fall salvation has come to the Gentiles, to provoke them to jealousy."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now if their fall is the riches of the world, and their loss the riches of the Gentiles, how much more their fullness!"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"For I speak to you who are Gentiles. Since then as I am an apostle to Gentiles, I glorify my ministry,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"if by any means I may provoke to jealousy those who are my flesh, and may save some of them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For if the rejection of them is the reconciling of the world, what would their acceptance be, but life from the dead?"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"If the first fruit is holy, so is the lump. If the root is holy, so are the branches."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But if some of the branches were broken off, and you, being a wild olive, were grafted in among them and became partaker with them of the root and of the richness of the olive tree,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"don\u2019t boast over the branches. But if you boast, remember that it is not you who support the root, but the root supports you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"You will say then, \u201cBranches were broken off, that I might be grafted in.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"True; by their unbelief they were broken off, and you stand by your faith. Don\u2019t be conceited, but fear;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"for if God didn\u2019t spare the natural branches, neither will he spare you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"See then the goodness and severity of God. Toward those who fell, severity; but toward you, goodness, if you continue in his goodness; otherwise you also will be cut off."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"They also, if they don\u2019t continue in their unbelief, will be grafted in, for God is able to graft them in again."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For if you were cut out of that which is by nature a wild olive tree, and were grafted contrary to nature into a good olive tree, how much more will these, which are the natural branches, be grafted into their own olive tree?"]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"For I don\u2019t desire you to be ignorant, brothers, of this mystery, so that you won\u2019t be wise in your own conceits, that a partial hardening has happened to Israel, until the fullness of the Gentiles has come in,"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and so all Israel will be saved. Even as it is written,"],[1,"\u201cThere will come out of Zion the Deliverer,"],[2,"and he will turn away ungodliness from Jacob."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[1,"This is my covenant with them,"],[2,"when I will take away their sins.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Concerning the Good News, they are enemies for your sake. But concerning the election, they are beloved for the fathers\u2019 sake."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For the gifts and the calling of God are irrevocable."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For as you in time past were disobedient to God, but now have obtained mercy by their disobedience,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"even so these also have now been disobedient, that by the mercy shown to you they may also obtain mercy."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"For God has bound all to disobedience, that he might have mercy on all."]]},{v:33,p:1,l:[[0,"Oh the depth of the riches both of the wisdom and the knowledge of God! How unsearchable are his judgments, and his ways past tracing out!"]]},{v:34,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor who has known the mind of the Lord?"],[2,"Or who has been his counselor?\u201d"]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cOr who has first given to him,"],[2,"and it will be repaid to him again?\u201d"]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"For of him and through him and to him are all things. To him be the glory for ever! Amen."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore I urge you, brothers, by the mercies of God, to present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable to God, which is your spiritual service."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind, so that you may prove what is the good, well-pleasing, and perfect will of God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"For I say through the grace that was given me, to everyone who is among you, not to think of yourself more highly than you ought to think; but to think reasonably, as God has apportioned to each person a measure of faith."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For even as we have many members in one body, and all the members don\u2019t have the same function,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"so we, who are many, are one body in Christ, and individually members of one another,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"having gifts differing according to the grace that was given to us: if prophecy, let\u2019s prophesy according to the proportion of our faith;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"or service, let\u2019s give ourselves to service; or he who teaches, to his teaching;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"or he who exhorts, to his exhorting; he who gives, let him do it with generosity; he who rules, with diligence; he who shows mercy, with cheerfulness."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Let love be without hypocrisy. Abhor that which is evil. Cling to that which is good."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"In love of the brothers be tenderly affectionate to one another; in honor prefer one another,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"not lagging in diligence, fervent in spirit, serving the Lord,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"rejoicing in hope, enduring in troubles, continuing steadfastly in prayer,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"contributing to the needs of the saints, and given to hospitality."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Bless those who persecute you; bless, and don\u2019t curse."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Rejoice with those who rejoice. Weep with those who weep."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Be of the same mind one toward another. Don\u2019t set your mind on high things, but associate with the humble. Don\u2019t be wise in your own conceits."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Repay no one evil for evil. Respect what is honorable in the sight of all men."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"If it is possible, as much as it is up to you, be at peace with all men."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t seek revenge yourselves, beloved, but give place to God\u2019s wrath. For it is written, \u201cVengeance belongs to me; I will repay, says the Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Therefore"],[1,"\u201cIf your enemy is hungry, feed him."],[2,"If he is thirsty, give him a drink;"],[2,"for in doing so, you will heap coals of fire on his head.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Let every soul be in subjection to the higher authorities, for there is no authority except from God, and those who exist are ordained by God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Therefore he who resists the authority withstands the ordinance of God; and those who withstand will receive to themselves judgment."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For rulers are not a terror to the good work, but to the evil. Do you desire to have no fear of the authority? Do that which is good, and you will have praise from the authority,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for he is a servant of God to you for good. But if you do that which is evil, be afraid, for he doesn\u2019t bear the sword in vain; for he is a servant of God, an avenger for wrath to him who does evil."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Therefore you need to be in subjection, not only because of the wrath, but also for conscience\u2019 sake."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For this reason you also pay taxes, for they are servants of God\u2019s service, continually doing this very thing."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore give everyone what you owe: if you owe taxes, pay taxes; if customs, then customs; if respect, then respect; if honor, then honor."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Owe no one anything, except to love one another; for he who loves his neighbor has fulfilled the law."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For the commandments, \u201cYou shall not commit adultery,\u201d \u201cYou shall not murder,\u201d \u201cYou shall not steal,\u201d \u201cYou shall not covet,\u201d and whatever other commandments there are, are all summed up in this saying, namely, \u201cYou shall love your neighbor as yourself.\u201d"]],f:["TR adds \u201cYou shall not give false testimony,\u201d"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Love doesn\u2019t harm a neighbor. Love therefore is the fulfillment of the law."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Do this, knowing the time, that it is already time for you to awaken out of sleep, for salvation is now nearer to us than when we first believed."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The night is far gone, and the day is near. Let\u2019s therefore throw off the deeds of darkness, and let\u2019s put on the armor of light."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s walk properly, as in the day; not in reveling and drunkenness, not in sexual promiscuity and lustful acts, and not in strife and jealousy."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But put on the Lord Jesus Christ, and make no provision for the flesh, for its lusts."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now accept one who is weak in faith, but not for disputes over opinions."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"One man has faith to eat all things, but he who is weak eats only vegetables."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t let him who eats despise him who doesn\u2019t eat. Don\u2019t let him who doesn\u2019t eat judge him who eats, for God has accepted him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Who are you who judge another\u2019s servant? To his own lord he stands or falls. Yes, he will be made to stand, for God has power to make him stand."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"One man esteems one day as more important. Another esteems every day alike. Let each man be fully assured in his own mind."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He who observes the day, observes it to the Lord; and he who does not observe the day, to the Lord he does not observe it. He who eats, eats to the Lord, for he gives God thanks. He who doesn\u2019t eat, to the Lord he doesn\u2019t eat, and gives God thanks."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For none of us lives to himself, and none dies to himself."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For if we live, we live to the Lord. Or if we die, we die to the Lord. If therefore we live or die, we are the Lord\u2019s."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For to this end Christ died, rose, and lived again, that he might be Lord of both the dead and the living."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But you, why do you judge your brother? Or you again, why do you despise your brother? For we will all stand before the judgment seat of Christ."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For it is written,"],[1,"\u201c\u2018As I live,\u2019 says the Lord, \u2018to me every knee will bow."],[2,"Every tongue will confess to God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So then each one of us will give account of himself to God."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore let\u2019s not judge one another any more, but judge this rather, that no man put a stumbling block in his brother\u2019s way, or an occasion for falling."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I know and am persuaded in the Lord Jesus that nothing is unclean of itself; except that to him who considers anything to be unclean, to him it is unclean."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Yet if because of food your brother is grieved, you walk no longer in love. Don\u2019t destroy with your food him for whom Christ died."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Then don\u2019t let your good be slandered,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"for God\u2019s Kingdom is not eating and drinking, but righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For he who serves Christ in these things is acceptable to God and approved by men."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"So then, let\u2019s follow after things which make for peace, and things by which we may build one another up."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t overthrow God\u2019s work for food\u2019s sake. All things indeed are clean, however it is evil for that man who creates a stumbling block by eating."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"It is good to not eat meat, drink wine, nor do anything by which your brother stumbles, is offended, or is made weak."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Do you have faith? Have it to yourself before God. Happy is he who doesn\u2019t judge himself in that which he approves."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But he who doubts is condemned if he eats, because it isn\u2019t of faith; and whatever is not of faith is sin."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Now to him who is able to establish you according to my Good News and the preaching of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery which has been kept secret through long ages,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"but now is revealed, and by the Scriptures of the prophets, according to the commandment of the eternal God, is made known for obedience of faith to all the nations;"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"to the only wise God, through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory forever! Amen."]],f:["TR places verses 24-26 after Romans 16:24 as verses 25-27."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now we who are strong ought to bear the weaknesses of the weak, and not to please ourselves."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Let each one of us please his neighbor for that which is good, to be building him up."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For even Christ didn\u2019t please himself. But, as it is written, \u201cThe reproaches of those who reproached you fell on me.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For whatever things were written before were written for our learning, that through perseverance and through encouragement of the Scriptures we might have hope."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now the God of perseverance and of encouragement grant you to be of the same mind with one another according to Christ Jesus,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"that with one accord you may with one mouth glorify the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore accept one another, even as Christ also accepted you, to the glory of God."]],f:["TR reads \u201cus\u201d instead of \u201cyou\u201d"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now I say that Christ has been made a servant of the circumcision for the truth of God, that he might confirm the promises given to the fathers,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and that the Gentiles might glorify God for his mercy. As it is written,"],[1,"\u201cTherefore I will give praise to you among the Gentiles"],[2,"and sing to your name.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Again he says,"],[1,"\u201cRejoice, you Gentiles, with his people.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Again,"],[1,"\u201cPraise the Lord, all you Gentiles!"],[2,"Let all the peoples praise him.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, Isaiah says,"],[1,"\u201cThere will be the root of Jesse,"],[2,"he who arises to rule over the Gentiles;"],[2,"in him the Gentiles will hope.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now may the God of hope fill you with all joy and peace in believing, that you may abound in hope in the power of the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"I myself am also persuaded about you, my brothers, that you yourselves are full of goodness, filled with all knowledge, able also to admonish others."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But I write the more boldly to you in part as reminding you, because of the grace that was given to me by God,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"that I should be a servant of Christ Jesus to the Gentiles, serving as a priest of the Good News of God, that the offering up of the Gentiles might be made acceptable, sanctified by the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I have therefore my boasting in Christ Jesus in things pertaining to God."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For I will not dare to speak of any things except those which Christ worked through me for the obedience of the Gentiles, by word and deed,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"in the power of signs and wonders, in the power of God\u2019s Spirit; so that from Jerusalem and around as far as to Illyricum, I have fully preached the Good News of Christ;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"yes, making it my aim to preach the Good News, not where Christ was already named, that I might not build on another\u2019s foundation."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"But, as it is written,"],[1,"\u201cThey will see, to whom no news of him came."],[2,"They who haven\u2019t heard will understand.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore also I was hindered these many times from coming to you,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"but now, no longer having any place in these regions, and having these many years a longing to come to you,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"whenever I travel to Spain, I will come to you. For I hope to see you on my journey, and to be helped on my way there by you, if first I may enjoy your company for a while."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But now, I say, I am going to Jerusalem, serving the saints."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For it has been the good pleasure of Macedonia and Achaia to make a certain contribution for the poor among the saints who are at Jerusalem."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Yes, it has been their good pleasure, and they are their debtors. For if the Gentiles have been made partakers of their spiritual things, they owe it to them also to serve them in material things."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"When therefore I have accomplished this, and have sealed to them this fruit, I will go on by way of you to Spain."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"I know that when I come to you, I will come in the fullness of the blessing of the Good News of Christ."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I beg you, brothers, by our Lord Jesus Christ and by the love of the Spirit, that you strive together with me in your prayers to God for me,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"that I may be delivered from those who are disobedient in Judea, and that my service which I have for Jerusalem may be acceptable to the saints,"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"that I may come to you in joy through the will of God, and together with you, find rest."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Now the God of peace be with you all. Amen."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I commend to you Phoebe, our sister, who is a servant of the assembly that is at Cenchreae,"]],f:["or, deacon"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that you receive her in the Lord in a way worthy of the saints, and that you assist her in whatever matter she may need from you, for she herself also has been a helper of many, and of my own self."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Greet Prisca and Aquila, my fellow workers in Christ Jesus,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"who risked their own necks for my life, to whom not only I give thanks, but also all the assemblies of the Gentiles."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Greet the assembly that is in their house. Greet Epaenetus, my beloved, who is the first fruits of Achaia to Christ."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Greet Mary, who labored much for us."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Greet Andronicus and Junia, my relatives and my fellow prisoners, who are notable among the apostles, who were also in Christ before me."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Greet Amplias, my beloved in the Lord."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Greet Urbanus, our fellow worker in Christ, and Stachys, my beloved."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Greet Apelles, the approved in Christ. Greet those who are of the household of Aristobulus."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Greet Herodion, my kinsman. Greet them of the household of Narcissus, who are in the Lord."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Greet Tryphaena and Tryphosa, who labor in the Lord. Greet Persis, the beloved, who labored much in the Lord."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Greet Rufus, the chosen in the Lord, and his mother and mine."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Greet Asyncritus, Phlegon, Hermes, Patrobas, Hermas, and the brothers who are with them."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Greet Philologus and Julia, Nereus and his sister, and Olympas, and all the saints who are with them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Greet one another with a holy kiss. The assemblies of Christ greet you."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I beg you, brothers, look out for those who are causing the divisions and occasions of stumbling, contrary to the doctrine which you learned, and turn away from them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For those who are such don\u2019t serve our Lord Jesus Christ, but their own belly; and by their smooth and flattering speech they deceive the hearts of the innocent."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For your obedience has become known to all. I rejoice therefore over you. But I desire to have you wise in that which is good, but innocent in that which is evil."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"And the God of peace will quickly crush Satan under your feet."],[0,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Timothy, my fellow worker, greets you, as do Lucius, Jason, and Sosipater, my relatives."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I, Tertius, who write the letter, greet you in the Lord."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Gaius, my host and host of the whole assembly, greets you. Erastus, the treasurer of the city, greets you, as does Quartus, the brother."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all! Amen."]]},{v:25,l:[],f:["TR places Romans 14:24-26 at the end of Romans instead of at the end of chapter 14, and numbers these verses 16:25-27."]}]]}},1316,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,a,h,s,i){h.exports={book:"1Cor",name:"1 Corinthians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, called to be an apostle of Jesus Christ through the will of God, and our brother Sosthenes,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to the assembly of God which is at Corinth\u2014those who are sanctified in Christ Jesus, called saints, with all who call on the name of our Lord Jesus Christ in every place, both theirs and ours:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I always thank my God concerning you for the grace of God which was given you in Christ Jesus,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"that in everything you were enriched in him, in all speech and all knowledge\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"even as the testimony of Christ was confirmed in you\u2014"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"so that you come behind in no gift, waiting for the revelation of our Lord Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"who will also confirm you until the end, blameless in the day of our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"God is faithful, through whom you were called into the fellowship of his Son, Jesus Christ our Lord."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I beg you, brothers, through the name of our Lord, Jesus Christ, that you all speak the same thing, and that there be no divisions among you, but that you be perfected together in the same mind and in the same judgment."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For it has been reported to me concerning you, my brothers, by those who are from Chloe\u2019s household, that there are contentions among you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now I mean this, that each one of you says, \u201cI follow Paul,\u201d \u201cI follow Apollos,\u201d \u201cI follow Cephas,\u201d and, \u201cI follow Christ.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Is Christ divided? Was Paul crucified for you? Or were you baptized into the name of Paul?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I thank God that I baptized none of you except Crispus and Gaius,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"so that no one should say that I had baptized you into my own name."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"(I also baptized the household of Stephanas; besides them, I don\u2019t know whether I baptized any other.)"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For Christ sent me not to baptize, but to preach the Good News\u2014not in wisdom of words, so that the cross of Christ wouldn\u2019t be made void."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For the word of the cross is foolishness to those who are dying, but to us who are being saved it is the power of God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For it is written,"],[1,"\u201cI will destroy the wisdom of the wise."],[2,"I will bring the discernment of the discerning to nothing.\u201d"]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Where is the wise? Where is the scribe? Where is the debater of this age? Hasn\u2019t God made foolish the wisdom of this world?"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For seeing that in the wisdom of God, the world through its wisdom didn\u2019t know God, it was God\u2019s good pleasure through the foolishness of the preaching to save those who believe."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For Jews ask for signs, Greeks seek after wisdom,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"but we preach Christ crucified, a stumbling block to Jews and foolishness to Greeks,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"but to those who are called, both Jews and Greeks, Christ is the power of God and the wisdom of God;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"because the foolishness of God is wiser than men, and the weakness of God is stronger than men."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"For you see your calling, brothers, that not many are wise according to the flesh, not many mighty, and not many noble;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"but God chose the foolish things of the world that he might put to shame those who are wise. God chose the weak things of the world that he might put to shame the things that are strong."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"God chose the lowly things of the world, and the things that are despised, and the things that don\u2019t exist, that he might bring to nothing the things that exist,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"that no flesh should boast before God."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Because of him, you are in Christ Jesus, who was made to us wisdom from God, and righteousness and sanctification, and redemption,"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"that, as it is written, \u201cHe who boasts, let him boast in the Lord.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When I came to you, brothers, I didn\u2019t come with excellence of speech or of wisdom, proclaiming to you the testimony of God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For I determined not to know anything among you except Jesus Christ and him crucified."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I was with you in weakness, in fear, and in much trembling."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"My speech and my preaching were not in persuasive words of human wisdom, but in demonstration of the Spirit and of power,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"that your faith wouldn\u2019t stand in the wisdom of men, but in the power of God."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"We speak wisdom, however, among those who are full grown, yet a wisdom not of this world nor of the rulers of this world who are coming to nothing."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But we speak God\u2019s wisdom in a mystery, the wisdom that has been hidden, which God foreordained before the worlds for our glory,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"which none of the rulers of this world has known. For had they known it, they wouldn\u2019t have crucified the Lord of glory."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But as it is written,"],[1,"\u201cThings which an eye didn\u2019t see, and an ear didn\u2019t hear,"],[2,"which didn\u2019t enter into the heart of man,"],[2,"these God has prepared for those who love him.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But to us, God revealed them through the Spirit. For the Spirit searches all things, yes, the deep things of God."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For who among men knows the things of a man except the spirit of the man which is in him? Even so, no one knows the things of God except God\u2019s Spirit."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But we received not the spirit of the world, but the Spirit which is from God, that we might know the things that were freely given to us by God."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"We also speak these things, not in words which man\u2019s wisdom teaches but which the Holy Spirit teaches, comparing spiritual things with spiritual things."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now the natural man doesn\u2019t receive the things of God\u2019s Spirit, for they are foolishness to him; and he can\u2019t know them, because they are spiritually discerned."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But he who is spiritual discerns all things, and he himself is to be judged by no one."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"\u201cFor who has known the mind of the Lord that he should instruct him?\u201d But we have Christ\u2019s mind."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, I couldn\u2019t speak to you as to spiritual, but as to fleshly, as to babies in Christ."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I fed you with milk, not with solid food, for you weren\u2019t yet ready. Indeed, you aren\u2019t ready even now,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"for you are still fleshly. For insofar as there is jealousy, strife, and factions among you, aren\u2019t you fleshly, and don\u2019t you walk in the ways of men?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For when one says, \u201cI follow Paul,\u201d and another, \u201cI follow Apollos,\u201d aren\u2019t you fleshly?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Who then is Apollos, and who is Paul, but servants through whom you believed, and each as the Lord gave to him?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I planted. Apollos watered. But God gave the increase."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So then neither he who plants is anything, nor he who waters, but God who gives the increase."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now he who plants and he who waters are the same, but each will receive his own reward according to his own labor."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For we are God\u2019s fellow workers. You are God\u2019s farming, God\u2019s building."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"According to the grace of God which was given to me, as a wise master builder I laid a foundation, and another builds on it. But let each man be careful how he builds on it."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For no one can lay any other foundation than that which has been laid, which is Jesus Christ."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But if anyone builds on the foundation with gold, silver, costly stones, wood, hay, or straw,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"each man\u2019s work will be revealed. For the Day will declare it, because it is revealed in fire; and the fire itself will test what sort of work each man\u2019s work is."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If any man\u2019s work remains which he built on it, he will receive a reward."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If any man\u2019s work is burned, he will suffer loss, but he himself will be saved, but as through fire."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know that you are God\u2019s temple and that God\u2019s Spirit lives in you?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If anyone destroys God\u2019s temple, God will destroy him; for God\u2019s temple is holy, which you are."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Let no one deceive himself. If anyone thinks that he is wise among you in this world, let him become a fool that he may become wise."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the wisdom of this world is foolishness with God. For it is written, \u201cHe has taken the wise in their craftiness.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"And again, \u201cThe Lord knows the reasoning of the wise, that it is worthless.\u201d"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Therefore let no one boast in men. For all things are yours,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"whether Paul, or Apollos, or Cephas, or the world, or life, or death, or things present, or things to come. All are yours,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and you are Christ\u2019s, and Christ is God\u2019s."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"So let a man think of us as Christ\u2019s servants and stewards of God\u2019s mysteries."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Here, moreover, it is required of stewards that they be found faithful."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But with me it is a very small thing that I should be judged by you, or by a human court. Yes, I don\u2019t even judge my own self."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For I know nothing against myself. Yet I am not justified by this, but he who judges me is the Lord."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Therefore judge nothing before the time, until the Lord comes, who will both bring to light the hidden things of darkness and reveal the counsels of the hearts. Then each man will get his praise from God."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these things, brothers, I have in a figure transferred to myself and Apollos for your sakes, that in us you might learn not to think beyond the things which are written, that none of you be puffed up against one another."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For who makes you different? And what do you have that you didn\u2019t receive? But if you did receive it, why do you boast as if you had not received it?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"You are already filled. You have already become rich. You have come to reign without us. Yes, and I wish that you did reign, that we also might reign with you!"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For I think that God has displayed us, the apostles, last of all, like men sentenced to death. For we are made a spectacle to the world, both to angels and men."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"We are fools for Christ\u2019s sake, but you are wise in Christ. We are weak, but you are strong. You have honor, but we have dishonor."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Even to this present hour we hunger, thirst, are naked, are beaten, and have no certain dwelling place."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"We toil, working with our own hands. When people curse us, we bless. Being persecuted, we endure."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Being defamed, we entreat. We are made as the filth of the world, the dirt wiped off by all, even until now."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"I don\u2019t write these things to shame you, but to admonish you as my beloved children."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For though you have ten thousand tutors in Christ, you don\u2019t have many fathers. For in Christ Jesus, I became your father through the Good News."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I beg you therefore, be imitators of me."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Because of this I have sent Timothy to you, who is my beloved and faithful child in the Lord, who will remind you of my ways which are in Christ, even as I teach everywhere in every assembly."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now some are puffed up, as though I were not coming to you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But I will come to you shortly, if the Lord is willing. And I will know, not the word of those who are puffed up, but the power."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For God\u2019s Kingdom is not in word, but in power."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"What do you want? Shall I come to you with a rod, or in love and a spirit of gentleness?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It is actually reported that there is sexual immorality among you, and such sexual immorality as is not even named among the Gentiles, that one has his father\u2019s wife."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You are arrogant, and didn\u2019t mourn instead, that he who had done this deed might be removed from among you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For I most certainly, as being absent in body but present in spirit, have already, as though I were present, judged him who has done this thing."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"In the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, when you are gathered together with my spirit with the power of our Lord Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"you are to deliver such a one to Satan for the destruction of the flesh, that the spirit may be saved in the day of the Lord Jesus."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Your boasting is not good. Don\u2019t you know that a little yeast leavens the whole lump?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Purge out the old yeast, that you may be a new lump, even as you are unleavened. For indeed Christ, our Passover, has been sacrificed in our place."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore let\u2019s keep the feast, not with old yeast, neither with the yeast of malice and wickedness, but with the unleavened bread of sincerity and truth."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"I wrote to you in my letter to have no company with sexual sinners;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"yet not at all meaning with the sexual sinners of this world, or with the covetous and extortionists, or with idolaters, for then you would have to leave the world."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But as it is, I wrote to you not to associate with anyone who is called a brother who is a sexual sinner, or covetous, or an idolater, or a slanderer, or a drunkard, or an extortionist. Don\u2019t even eat with such a person."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For what do I have to do with also judging those who are outside? Don\u2019t you judge those who are within?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But those who are outside, God judges. \u201cPut away the wicked man from among yourselves.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Dare any of you, having a matter against his neighbor, go to law before the unrighteous, and not before the saints?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know that the saints will judge the world? And if the world is judged by you, are you unworthy to judge the smallest matters?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know that we will judge angels? How much more, things that pertain to this life?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If then you have to judge things pertaining to this life, do you set them to judge who are of no account in the assembly?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I say this to move you to shame. Isn\u2019t there even one wise man among you who would be able to decide between his brothers?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But brother goes to law with brother, and that before unbelievers!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore it is already altogether a defect in you that you have lawsuits one with another. Why not rather be wronged? Why not rather be defrauded?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"No, but you yourselves do wrong and defraud, and that against your brothers."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Or don\u2019t you know that the unrighteous will not inherit God\u2019s Kingdom? Don\u2019t be deceived. Neither the sexually immoral, nor idolaters, nor adulterers, nor male prostitutes, nor homosexuals,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"nor thieves, nor covetous, nor drunkards, nor slanderers, nor extortionists, will inherit God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Some of you were such, but you were washed. You were sanctified. You were justified in the name of the Lord Jesus, and in the Spirit of our God."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll things are lawful for me,\u201d but not all things are expedient. \u201cAll things are lawful for me,\u201d but I will not be brought under the power of anything."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"\u201cFoods for the belly, and the belly for foods,\u201d but God will bring to nothing both it and them. But the body is not for sexual immorality, but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Now God raised up the Lord, and will also raise us up by his power."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know that your bodies are members of Christ? Shall I then take the members of Christ and make them members of a prostitute? May it never be!"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Or don\u2019t you know that he who is joined to a prostitute is one body? For, \u201cThe two\u201d, he says, \u201cwill become one flesh.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But he who is joined to the Lord is one spirit."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Flee sexual immorality! \u201cEvery sin that a man does is outside the body,\u201d but he who commits sexual immorality sins against his own body."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Or don\u2019t you know that your body is a temple of the Holy Spirit who is in you, whom you have from God? You are not your own,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"for you were bought with a price. Therefore glorify God in your body and in your spirit, which are God\u2019s."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now concerning the things about which you wrote to me: it is good for a man not to touch a woman."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But, because of sexual immoralities, let each man have his own wife, and let each woman have her own husband."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Let the husband give his wife the affection owed her, and likewise also the wife her husband."]],f:["NU and TR have \u201cwhat is owed her\u201d instead of \u201cthe affection owed her\u201d."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The wife doesn\u2019t have authority over her own body, but the husband does. Likewise also the husband doesn\u2019t have authority over his own body, but the wife does."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t deprive one another, unless it is by consent for a season, that you may give yourselves to fasting and prayer, and may be together again, that Satan doesn\u2019t tempt you because of your lack of self-control."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But this I say by way of concession, not of commandment."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Yet I wish that all men were like me. However, each man has his own gift from God, one of this kind, and another of that kind."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But I say to the unmarried and to widows, it is good for them if they remain even as I am."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But if they don\u2019t have self-control, let them marry. For it\u2019s better to marry than to burn with passion."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But to the married I command\u2014not I, but the Lord\u2014that the wife not leave her husband"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"(but if she departs, let her remain unmarried, or else be reconciled to her husband), and that the husband not leave his wife."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"But to the rest I\u2014not the Lord\u2014say, if any brother has an unbelieving wife, and she is content to live with him, let him not leave her."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The woman who has an unbelieving husband, and he is content to live with her, let her not leave her husband."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For the unbelieving husband is sanctified in the wife, and the unbelieving wife is sanctified in the husband. Otherwise your children would be unclean, but now they are holy."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Yet if the unbeliever departs, let there be separation. The brother or the sister is not under bondage in such cases, but God has called us in peace."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For how do you know, wife, whether you will save your husband? Or how do you know, husband, whether you will save your wife?"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Only, as the Lord has distributed to each man, as God has called each, so let him walk. So I command in all the assemblies."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Was anyone called having been circumcised? Let him not become uncircumcised. Has anyone been called in uncircumcision? Let him not be circumcised."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Circumcision is nothing, and uncircumcision is nothing, but what matters is keeping God\u2019s commandments."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Let each man stay in that calling in which he was called."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Were you called being a bondservant? Don\u2019t let that bother you, but if you get an opportunity to become free, use it."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For he who was called in the Lord being a bondservant is the Lord\u2019s free man. Likewise he who was called being free is Christ\u2019s bondservant."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"You were bought with a price. Don\u2019t become bondservants of men."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Brothers, let each man, in whatever condition he was called, stay in that condition with God."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Now concerning virgins, I have no commandment from the Lord, but I give my judgment as one who has obtained mercy from the Lord to be trustworthy."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Therefore I think that because of the distress that is on us, it\u2019s good for a man to remain as he is."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Are you bound to a wife? Don\u2019t seek to be freed. Are you free from a wife? Don\u2019t seek a wife."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But if you marry, you have not sinned. If a virgin marries, she has not sinned. Yet such will have oppression in the flesh, and I want to spare you."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But I say this, brothers: the time is short. From now on, both those who have wives may be as though they had none;"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"and those who weep, as though they didn\u2019t weep; and those who rejoice, as though they didn\u2019t rejoice; and those who buy, as though they didn\u2019t possess;"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"and those who use the world, as not using it to the fullest. For the mode of this world passes away."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"But I desire to have you to be free from cares. He who is unmarried is concerned for the things of the Lord, how he may please the Lord;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"but he who is married is concerned about the things of the world, how he may please his wife."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"There is also a difference between a wife and a virgin. The unmarried woman cares about the things of the Lord, that she may be holy both in body and in spirit. But she who is married cares about the things of the world\u2014how she may please her husband."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"This I say for your own benefit, not that I may ensnare you, but for that which is appropriate, and that you may attend to the Lord without distraction."]]},{v:36,p:1,l:[[0,"But if any man thinks that he is behaving inappropriately toward his virgin, if she is past the flower of her age, and if need so requires, let him do what he desires. He doesn\u2019t sin. Let them marry."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"But he who stands steadfast in his heart, having no urgency, but has power over his own will, and has determined in his own heart to keep his own virgin, does well."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"So then both he who gives his own virgin in marriage does well, and he who doesn\u2019t give her in marriage does better."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"A wife is bound by law for as long as her husband lives; but if the husband is dead, she is free to be married to whomever she desires, only in the Lord."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"But she is happier if she stays as she is, in my judgment, and I think that I also have God\u2019s Spirit."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now concerning things sacrificed to idols: We know that we all have knowledge. Knowledge puffs up, but love builds up."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But if anyone thinks that he knows anything, he doesn\u2019t yet know as he ought to know."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But anyone who loves God is known by him."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore concerning the eating of things sacrificed to idols, we know that no idol is anything in the world, and that there is no other God but one."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For though there are things that are called \u201cgods\u201d, whether in the heavens or on earth\u2014as there are many \u201cgods\u201d and many \u201clords\u201d\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"yet to us there is one God, the Father, of whom are all things, and we for him; and one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom are all things, and we live through him."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"However, that knowledge isn\u2019t in all men. But some, with consciousness of an idol until now, eat as of a thing sacrificed to an idol, and their conscience, being weak, is defiled."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But food will not commend us to God. For neither, if we don\u2019t eat are we the worse, nor if we eat are we the better."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But be careful that by no means does this liberty of yours become a stumbling block to the weak."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For if a man sees you who have knowledge sitting in an idol\u2019s temple, won\u2019t his conscience, if he is weak, be emboldened to eat things sacrificed to idols?"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"And through your knowledge, he who is weak perishes, the brother for whose sake Christ died."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Thus, sinning against the brothers, and wounding their conscience when it is weak, you sin against Christ."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore, if food causes my brother to stumble, I will eat no meat forever more, that I don\u2019t cause my brother to stumble."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Am I not free? Am I not an apostle? Haven\u2019t I seen Jesus Christ, our Lord? Aren\u2019t you my work in the Lord?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"If to others I am not an apostle, yet at least I am to you; for you are the seal of my apostleship in the Lord."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"My defense to those who examine me is this:"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Have we no right to eat and to drink?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Have we no right to take along a wife who is a believer, even as the rest of the apostles, and the brothers of the Lord, and Cephas?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Or have only Barnabas and I no right to not work?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"What soldier ever serves at his own expense? Who plants a vineyard, and doesn\u2019t eat of its fruit? Or who feeds a flock, and doesn\u2019t drink from the flock\u2019s milk?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Do I speak these things according to the ways of men? Or doesn\u2019t the law also say the same thing?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For it is written in the law of Moses, \u201cYou shall not muzzle an ox while it treads out the grain.\u201d Is it for the oxen that God cares,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"or does he say it assuredly for our sake? Yes, it was written for our sake, because he who plows ought to plow in hope, and he who threshes in hope should partake of his hope."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If we sowed to you spiritual things, is it a great thing if we reap your fleshly things?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"If others partake of this right over you, don\u2019t we yet more?"],[0,"Nevertheless we didn\u2019t use this right, but we bear all things, that we may cause no hindrance to the Good News of Christ."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know that those who serve around sacred things eat from the things of the temple, and those who wait on the altar have their portion with the altar?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Even so the Lord ordained that those who proclaim the Good News should live from the Good News."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"But I have used none of these things, and I don\u2019t write these things that it may be done so in my case; for I would rather die, than that anyone should make my boasting void."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For if I preach the Good News, I have nothing to boast about, for necessity is laid on me; but woe is to me if I don\u2019t preach the Good News."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For if I do this of my own will, I have a reward. But if not of my own will, I have a stewardship entrusted to me."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"What then is my reward? That when I preach the Good News, I may present the Good News of Christ without charge, so as not to abuse my authority in the Good News."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"For though I was free from all, I brought myself under bondage to all, that I might gain the more."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"To the Jews I became as a Jew, that I might gain Jews; to those who are under the law, as under the law, that I might gain those who are under the law;"]],f:["NU adds: though I myself am not under the law"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"to those who are without law, as without law (not being without law toward God, but under law toward Christ), that I might win those who are without law."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"To the weak I became as weak, that I might gain the weak. I have become all things to all men, that I may by all means save some."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Now I do this for the sake of the Good News, that I may be a joint partaker of it."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you know that those who run in a race all run, but one receives the prize? Run like that, so that you may win."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Every man who strives in the games exercises self-control in all things. Now they do it to receive a corruptible crown, but we an incorruptible."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I therefore run like that, not aimlessly. I fight like that, not beating the air,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"but I beat my body and bring it into submission, lest by any means, after I have preached to others, I myself should be disqualified."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I would not have you ignorant, brothers, that our fathers were all under the cloud, and all passed through the sea;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and were all baptized into Moses in the cloud and in the sea;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and all ate the same spiritual food;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and all drank the same spiritual drink. For they drank of a spiritual rock that followed them, and the rock was Christ."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"However with most of them, God was not well pleased, for they were overthrown in the wilderness."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these things were our examples, to the intent we should not lust after evil things as they also lusted."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be idolaters, as some of them were. As it is written, \u201cThe people sat down to eat and drink, and rose up to play.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s not commit sexual immorality, as some of them committed, and in one day twenty-three thousand fell."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s not test Christ, as some of them tested, and perished by the serpents."]],f:["NU reads \u201cthe Lord\u201d instead of \u201cChrist\u201d."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t grumble, as some of them also grumbled, and perished by the destroyer."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now all these things happened to them by way of example, and they were written for our admonition, on whom the ends of the ages have come."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore let him who thinks he stands be careful that he doesn\u2019t fall."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"No temptation has taken you except what is common to man. God is faithful, who will not allow you to be tempted above what you are able, but will with the temptation also make the way of escape, that you may be able to endure it."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, my beloved, flee from idolatry."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I speak as to wise men. Judge what I say."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The cup of blessing which we bless, isn\u2019t it a sharing of the blood of Christ? The bread which we break, isn\u2019t it a sharing of the body of Christ?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Because there is one loaf of bread, we, who are many, are one body; for we all partake of the one loaf of bread."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Consider Israel according to the flesh. Don\u2019t those who eat the sacrifices participate in the altar?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"What am I saying then? That a thing sacrificed to idols is anything, or that an idol is anything?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But I say that the things which the Gentiles sacrifice, they sacrifice to demons and not to God, and I don\u2019t desire that you would have fellowship with demons."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"You can\u2019t both drink the cup of the Lord and the cup of demons. You can\u2019t both partake of the table of the Lord and of the table of demons."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Or do we provoke the Lord to jealousy? Are we stronger than he?"]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAll things are lawful for me,\u201d but not all things are profitable. \u201cAll things are lawful for me,\u201d but not all things build up."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Let no one seek his own, but each one his neighbor\u2019s good."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Whatever is sold in the butcher shop, eat, asking no question for the sake of conscience,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"for \u201cthe earth is the Lord\u2019s, and its fullness.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"But if one of those who don\u2019t believe invites you to a meal, and you are inclined to go, eat whatever is set before you, asking no questions for the sake of conscience."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But if anyone says to you, \u201cThis was offered to idols,\u201d don\u2019t eat it for the sake of the one who told you, and for the sake of conscience. For \u201cthe earth is the Lord\u2019s, with all its fullness.\u201d"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Conscience, I say, not your own, but the other\u2019s conscience. For why is my liberty judged by another conscience?"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"If I partake with thankfulness, why am I denounced for something I give thanks for?"]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"Whether therefore you eat or drink, or whatever you do, do all to the glory of God."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"Give no occasion for stumbling, whether to Jews, to Greeks, or to the assembly of God;"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"even as I also please all men in all things, not seeking my own profit, but the profit of the many, that they may be saved."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Be imitators of me, even as I also am of Christ."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I praise you, brothers, that you remember me in all things, and hold firm the traditions, even as I delivered them to you."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But I would have you know that the head of every man is Christ, and the head of the woman is man, and the head of Christ is God."]],f:["or, origin","or, origin","or, origin"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Every man praying or prophesying, having his head covered, dishonors his head."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But every woman praying or prophesying with her head uncovered dishonors her head. For it is one and the same thing as if she were shaved."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For if a woman is not covered, let her hair also be cut off. But if it is shameful for a woman to have her hair cut off or be shaved, let her be covered."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For a man indeed ought not to have his head covered, because he is the image and glory of God, but the woman is the glory of the man."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For man is not from woman, but woman from man;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"for man wasn\u2019t created for the woman, but woman for the man."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For this cause the woman ought to have authority over her own head, because of the angels."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, neither is the woman independent of the man, nor the man independent of the woman, in the Lord."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For as woman came from man, so a man also comes through a woman; but all things are from God."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Judge for yourselves. Is it appropriate that a woman pray to God unveiled?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Doesn\u2019t even nature itself teach you that if a man has long hair, it is a dishonor to him?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But if a woman has long hair, it is a glory to her, for her hair is given to her for a covering."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But if any man seems to be contentious, we have no such custom, neither do God\u2019s assemblies."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But in giving you this command I don\u2019t praise you, because you come together not for the better but for the worse."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For first of all, when you come together in the assembly, I hear that divisions exist among you, and I partly believe it."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For there also must be factions among you, that those who are approved may be revealed among you."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"When therefore you assemble yourselves together, it is not the Lord\u2019s supper that you eat."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For in your eating each one takes his own supper first. One is hungry, and another is drunken."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"What, don\u2019t you have houses to eat and to drink in? Or do you despise God\u2019s assembly and put them to shame who don\u2019t have enough? What shall I tell you? Shall I praise you? In this I don\u2019t praise you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"For I received from the Lord that which also I delivered to you, that the Lord Jesus on the night in which he was betrayed took bread."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"When he had given thanks, he broke it and said, \u201cTake, eat. This is my body, which is broken for you. Do this in memory of me.\u201d"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In the same way he also took the cup after supper, saying, \u201cThis cup is the new covenant in my blood. Do this, as often as you drink, in memory of me.\u201d"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For as often as you eat this bread and drink this cup, you proclaim the Lord\u2019s death until he comes."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore whoever eats this bread or drinks the Lord\u2019s cup in a way unworthy of the Lord will be guilty of the body and the blood of the Lord."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But let a man examine himself, and so let him eat of the bread and drink of the cup."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For he who eats and drinks in an unworthy way eats and drinks judgment to himself if he doesn\u2019t discern the Lord\u2019s body."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For this cause many among you are weak and sickly, and not a few sleep."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For if we discerned ourselves, we wouldn\u2019t be judged."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"But when we are judged, we are disciplined by the Lord, that we may not be condemned with the world."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Therefore, my brothers, when you come together to eat, wait for one another."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"But if anyone is hungry, let him eat at home, lest your coming together be for judgment. The rest I will set in order whenever I come."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now concerning spiritual things, brothers, I don\u2019t want you to be ignorant."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You know that when you were heathen, you were led away to those mute idols, however you might be led."]],f:["or Gentiles"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Therefore I make known to you that no man speaking by God\u2019s Spirit says, \u201cJesus is accursed.\u201d No one can say, \u201cJesus is Lord,\u201d but by the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now there are various kinds of gifts, but the same Spirit."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"There are various kinds of service, and the same Lord."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"There are various kinds of workings, but the same God who works all things in all."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But to each one is given the manifestation of the Spirit for the profit of all."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For to one is given through the Spirit the word of wisdom, and to another the word of knowledge according to the same Spirit,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"to another faith by the same Spirit, and to another gifts of healings by the same Spirit,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and to another workings of miracles, and to another prophecy, and to another discerning of spirits, to another different kinds of languages, and to another the interpretation of languages."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But the one and the same Spirit produces all of these, distributing to each one separately as he desires."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"For as the body is one and has many members, and all the members of the body, being many, are one body; so also is Christ."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, whether bond or free; and were all given to drink into one Spirit."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"For the body is not one member, but many."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If the foot would say, \u201cBecause I\u2019m not the hand, I\u2019m not part of the body,\u201d it is not therefore not part of the body."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"If the ear would say, \u201cBecause I\u2019m not the eye, I\u2019m not part of the body,\u201d it\u2019s not therefore not part of the body."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If the whole body were an eye, where would the hearing be? If the whole were hearing, where would the smelling be?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But now God has set the members, each one of them, in the body, just as he desired."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"If they were all one member, where would the body be?"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But now they are many members, but one body."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The eye can\u2019t tell the hand, \u201cI have no need for you,\u201d or again the head to the feet, \u201cI have no need for you.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"No, much rather, those members of the body which seem to be weaker are necessary."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Those parts of the body which we think to be less honorable, on those we bestow more abundant honor; and our unpresentable parts have more abundant modesty,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"while our presentable parts have no such need. But God composed the body together, giving more abundant honor to the inferior part,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"that there should be no division in the body, but that the members should have the same care for one another."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"When one member suffers, all the members suffer with it. When one member is honored, all the members rejoice with it."]]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Now you are the body of Christ, and members individually."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"God has set some in the assembly: first apostles, second prophets, third teachers, then miracle workers, then gifts of healings, helps, governments, and various kinds of languages."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Are all apostles? Are all prophets? Are all teachers? Are all miracle workers?"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Do all have gifts of healings? Do all speak with various languages? Do all interpret?"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"But earnestly desire the best gifts. Moreover, I show a most excellent way to you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"If I speak with the languages of men and of angels, but don\u2019t have love, I have become sounding brass or a clanging cymbal."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"If I have the gift of prophecy, and know all mysteries and all knowledge, and if I have all faith, so as to remove mountains, but don\u2019t have love, I am nothing."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"If I give away all my goods to feed the poor, and if I give my body to be burned, but don\u2019t have love, it profits me nothing."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Love is patient and is kind. Love doesn\u2019t envy. Love doesn\u2019t brag, is not proud,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"doesn\u2019t behave itself inappropriately, doesn\u2019t seek its own way, is not provoked, takes no account of evil;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"doesn\u2019t rejoice in unrighteousness, but rejoices with the truth;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"bears all things, believes all things, hopes all things, and endures all things."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Love never fails. But where there are prophecies, they will be done away with. Where there are various languages, they will cease. Where there is knowledge, it will be done away with."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For we know in part and we prophesy in part;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but when that which is complete has come, then that which is partial will be done away with."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"When I was a child, I spoke as a child, I felt as a child, I thought as a child. Now that I have become a man, I have put away childish things."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For now we see in a mirror, dimly, but then face to face. Now I know in part, but then I will know fully, even as I was also fully known."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But now faith, hope, and love remain\u2014these three. The greatest of these is love."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Follow after love and earnestly desire spiritual gifts, but especially that you may prophesy."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For he who speaks in another language speaks not to men, but to God, for no one understands, but in the Spirit he speaks mysteries."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But he who prophesies speaks to men for their edification, exhortation, and consolation."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He who speaks in another language edifies himself, but he who prophesies edifies the assembly."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now I desire to have you all speak with other languages, but even more that you would prophesy. For he is greater who prophesies than he who speaks with other languages, unless he interprets, that the assembly may be built up."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But now, brothers, if I come to you speaking with other languages, what would I profit you unless I speak to you either by way of revelation, or of knowledge, or of prophesying, or of teaching?"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Even lifeless things that make a sound, whether pipe or harp, if they didn\u2019t give a distinction in the sounds, how would it be known what is piped or harped?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For if the trumpet gave an uncertain sound, who would prepare himself for war?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So also you, unless you uttered by the tongue words easy to understand, how would it be known what is spoken? For you would be speaking into the air."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"There are, it may be, so many kinds of languages in the world, and none of them is without meaning."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If then I don\u2019t know the meaning of the language, I would be to him who speaks a foreigner, and he who speaks would be a foreigner to me."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So also you, since you are zealous for spiritual gifts, seek that you may abound to the building up of the assembly."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore let him who speaks in another language pray that he may interpret."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For if I pray in another language, my spirit prays, but my understanding is unfruitful."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"What should I do? I will pray with the spirit, and I will pray with the understanding also. I will sing with the spirit, and I will sing with the understanding also."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Otherwise, if you bless with the spirit, how will he who fills the place of the unlearned say the \u201cAmen\u201d at your giving of thanks, seeing he doesn\u2019t know what you say?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For you most certainly give thanks well, but the other person is not built up."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I thank my God, I speak with other languages more than you all."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"However, in the assembly I would rather speak five words with my understanding, that I might instruct others also, than ten thousand words in another language."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, don\u2019t be children in thoughts, yet in malice be babies, but in thoughts be mature."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"In the law it is written, \u201cBy men of strange languages and by the lips of strangers I will speak to this people. They won\u2019t even listen to me that way, says the Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Therefore other languages are for a sign, not to those who believe, but to the unbelieving; but prophesying is for a sign, not to the unbelieving, but to those who believe."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"If therefore the whole assembly is assembled together and all speak with other languages, and unlearned or unbelieving people come in, won\u2019t they say that you are crazy?"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But if all prophesy, and someone unbelieving or unlearned comes in, he is reproved by all, and he is judged by all."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"And thus the secrets of his heart are revealed. So he will fall down on his face and worship God, declaring that God is among you indeed."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"What is it then, brothers? When you come together, each one of you has a psalm, has a teaching, has a revelation, has another language, or has an interpretation. Let all things be done to build each other up."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"If any man speaks in another language, let there be two, or at the most three, and in turn; and let one interpret."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"But if there is no interpreter, let him keep silent in the assembly, and let him speak to himself and to God."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Let two or three of the prophets speak, and let the others discern."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"But if a revelation is made to another sitting by, let the first keep silent."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"For you all can prophesy one by one, that all may learn and all may be exhorted."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"The spirits of the prophets are subject to the prophets,"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"for God is not a God of confusion but of peace, as in all the assemblies of the saints."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Let the wives be quiet in the assemblies, for it has not been permitted for them to be talking except in submission, as the law also says,"]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"if they desire to learn anything. \u201cLet them ask their own husbands at home, for it is shameful for a wife to be talking in the assembly.\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"What!? Was it from you that the word of God went out? Or did it come to you alone?"]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[0,"If any man thinks himself to be a prophet or spiritual, let him recognize the things which I write to you, that they are the commandment of the Lord."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But if anyone is ignorant, let him be ignorant."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, brothers, desire earnestly to prophesy, and don\u2019t forbid speaking with other languages."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"Let all things be done decently and in order."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I declare to you, brothers, the Good News which I preached to you, which also you received, in which you also stand,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"by which also you are saved, if you hold firmly the word which I preached to you\u2014unless you believed in vain."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"For I delivered to you first of all that which I also received: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"that he was buried, that he was raised on the third day according to the Scriptures,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and that he appeared to Cephas, then to the twelve."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Then he appeared to over five hundred brothers at once, most of whom remain until now, but some have also fallen asleep."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then he appeared to James, then to all the apostles,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and last of all, as to the child born at the wrong time, he appeared to me also."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For I am the least of the apostles, who is not worthy to be called an apostle, because I persecuted the assembly of God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But by the grace of God I am what I am. His grace which was given to me was not futile, but I worked more than all of them; yet not I, but the grace of God which was with me."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Whether then it is I or they, so we preach, and so you believed."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now if Christ is preached, that he has been raised from the dead, how do some among you say that there is no resurrection of the dead?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But if there is no resurrection of the dead, neither has Christ been raised."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If Christ has not been raised, then our preaching is in vain and your faith also is in vain."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Yes, we are also found false witnesses of God, because we testified about God that he raised up Christ, whom he didn\u2019t raise up if it is true that the dead are not raised."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For if the dead aren\u2019t raised, neither has Christ been raised."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"If Christ has not been raised, your faith is vain; you are still in your sins."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Then they also who are fallen asleep in Christ have perished."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"If we have only hoped in Christ in this life, we are of all men most pitiable."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"But now Christ has been raised from the dead. He became the first fruit of those who are asleep."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For since death came by man, the resurrection of the dead also came by man."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For as in Adam all die, so also in Christ all will be made alive."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But each in his own order: Christ the first fruits, then those who are Christ\u2019s at his coming."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Then the end comes, when he will deliver up the Kingdom to God the Father, when he will have abolished all rule and all authority and power."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For he must reign until he has put all his enemies under his feet."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"The last enemy that will be abolished is death."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For, \u201cHe put all things in subjection under his feet.\u201d But when he says, \u201cAll things are put in subjection\u201d, it is evident that he is excepted who subjected all things to him."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"When all things have been subjected to him, then the Son will also himself be subjected to him who subjected all things to him, that God may be all in all."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"Or else what will they do who are baptized for the dead? If the dead aren\u2019t raised at all, why then are they baptized for the dead?"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Why do we also stand in jeopardy every hour?"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"I affirm, by the boasting in you which I have in Christ Jesus our Lord, I die daily."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"If I fought with animals at Ephesus for human purposes, what does it profit me? If the dead are not raised, then \u201clet\u2019s eat and drink, for tomorrow we die.\u201d"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be deceived! \u201cEvil companionships corrupt good morals.\u201d"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"Wake up righteously and don\u2019t sin, for some have no knowledge of God. I say this to your shame."]]},{v:35,p:1,l:[[0,"But someone will say, \u201cHow are the dead raised?\u201d and, \u201cWith what kind of body do they come?\u201d"]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"You foolish one, that which you yourself sow is not made alive unless it dies."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"That which you sow, you don\u2019t sow the body that will be, but a bare grain, maybe of wheat, or of some other kind."]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"But God gives it a body even as it pleased him, and to each seed a body of its own."]]},{v:39,l:[[0,"All flesh is not the same flesh, but there is one flesh of men, another flesh of animals, another of fish, and another of birds."]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"There are also celestial bodies and terrestrial bodies; but the glory of the celestial differs from that of the terrestrial."]]},{v:41,l:[[0,"There is one glory of the sun, another glory of the moon, and another glory of the stars; for one star differs from another star in glory."]]},{v:42,p:1,l:[[0,"So also is the resurrection of the dead. The body is sown perishable; it is raised imperishable."]]},{v:43,l:[[0,"It is sown in dishonor; it is raised in glory. It is sown in weakness; it is raised in power."]]},{v:44,l:[[0,"It is sown a natural body; it is raised a spiritual body. There is a natural body and there is also a spiritual body."]]},{v:45,p:1,l:[[0,"So also it is written, \u201cThe first man Adam became a living soul.\u201d The last Adam became a life-giving spirit."]]},{v:46,l:[[0,"However, that which is spiritual isn\u2019t first, but that which is natural, then that which is spiritual."]]},{v:47,l:[[0,"The first man is of the earth, made of dust. The second man is the Lord from heaven."]]},{v:48,l:[[0,"As is the one made of dust, such are those who are also made of dust; and as is the heavenly, such are they also that are heavenly."]]},{v:49,l:[[0,"As we have borne the image of those made of dust, let\u2019s also bear the image of the heavenly."]],f:["NU, TR read \u201cwe will\u201d instead of \u201clet\u2019s\u201d"]},{v:50,l:[[0,"Now I say this, brothers, that flesh and blood can\u2019t inherit God\u2019s Kingdom; neither does the perishable inherit imperishable."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:51,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, I tell you a mystery. We will not all sleep, but we will all be changed,"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:52,l:[[0,"in a moment, in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trumpet. For the trumpet will sound and the dead will be raised incorruptible, and we will be changed."]]},{v:53,l:[[0,"For this perishable body must become imperishable, and this mortal must put on immortality."]]},{v:54,l:[[0,"But when this perishable body will have become imperishable, and this mortal will have put on immortality, then what is written will happen: \u201cDeath is swallowed up in victory.\u201d"]]},{v:55,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cDeath, where is your sting?"],[2,"Hades, where is your victory?\u201d"]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:56,p:1,l:[[0,"The sting of death is sin, and the power of sin is the law."]]},{v:57,l:[[0,"But thanks be to God, who gives us the victory through our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:58,l:[[0,"Therefore, my beloved brothers, be steadfast, immovable, always abounding in the Lord\u2019s work, because you know that your labor is not in vain in the Lord."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now concerning the collection for the saints: as I commanded the assemblies of Galatia, you do likewise."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"On the first day of every week, let each one of you save as he may prosper, that no collections are made when I come."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"When I arrive, I will send whoever you approve with letters to carry your gracious gift to Jerusalem."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"If it is appropriate for me to go also, they will go with me."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"I will come to you when I have passed through Macedonia, for I am passing through Macedonia."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But with you it may be that I will stay with you, or even winter with you, that you may send me on my journey wherever I go."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For I do not wish to see you now in passing, but I hope to stay a while with you, if the Lord permits."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But I will stay at Ephesus until Pentecost,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"for a great and effective door has opened to me, and there are many adversaries."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now if Timothy comes, see that he is with you without fear, for he does the work of the Lord, as I also do."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore let no one despise him. But set him forward on his journey in peace, that he may come to me; for I expect him with the brothers."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now concerning Apollos the brother, I strongly urged him to come to you with the brothers, but it was not at all his desire to come now; but he will come when he has an opportunity."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Watch! Stand firm in the faith! Be courageous! Be strong!"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Let all that you do be done in love."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I beg you, brothers\u2014you know the house of Stephanas, that it is the first fruits of Achaia, and that they have set themselves to serve the saints\u2014"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"that you also be in subjection to such, and to everyone who helps in the work and labors."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"I rejoice at the coming of Stephanas, Fortunatus, and Achaicus; for that which was lacking on your part, they supplied."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For they refreshed my spirit and yours. Therefore acknowledge those who are like that."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"The assemblies of Asia greet you. Aquila and Priscilla greet you warmly in the Lord, together with the assembly that is in their house."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"All the brothers greet you. Greet one another with a holy kiss."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"This greeting is by me, Paul, with my own hand."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"If any man doesn\u2019t love the Lord Jesus Christ, let him be cursed. Come, Lord!"]],f:["Greek: anathema.","Aramaic: Maranatha!"]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with you."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"My love to all of you in Christ Jesus. Amen."]]}]]}},1317,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,s,n,i){s.exports={book:"2Cor",name:"2 Corinthians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus through the will of God, and Timothy our brother, to the assembly of God which is at Corinth, with all the saints who are in the whole of Achaia:"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of mercies and God of all comfort,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"who comforts us in all our affliction, that we may be able to comfort those who are in any affliction, through the comfort with which we ourselves are comforted by God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For as the sufferings of Christ abound to us, even so our comfort also abounds through Christ."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But if we are afflicted, it is for your comfort and salvation. If we are comforted, it is for your comfort, which produces in you the patient enduring of the same sufferings which we also suffer."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Our hope for you is steadfast, knowing that, since you are partakers of the sufferings, so you are also of the comfort."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"For we don\u2019t desire to have you uninformed, brothers, concerning our affliction which happened to us in Asia: that we were weighed down exceedingly, beyond our power, so much that we despaired even of life."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Yes, we ourselves have had the sentence of death within ourselves, that we should not trust in ourselves, but in God who raises the dead,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"who delivered us out of so great a death, and does deliver, on whom we have set our hope that he will also still deliver us,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"you also helping together on our behalf by your supplication; that, for the gift given to us by means of many, thanks may be given by many persons on your behalf."]],f:["+ MT: your; TR and NU: our"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"For our boasting is this: the testimony of our conscience that in holiness and sincerity of God, not in fleshly wisdom but in the grace of God, we behaved ourselves in the world, and more abundantly toward you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For we write no other things to you than what you read or even acknowledge, and I hope you will acknowledge to the end\u2014"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"as also you acknowledged us in part\u2014that we are your boasting, even as you also are ours, in the day of our Lord Jesus."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"In this confidence, I was determined to come first to you, that you might have a second benefit,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and by you to pass into Macedonia, and again from Macedonia to come to you, and to be sent forward by you on my journey to Judea."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When I therefore planned this, did I show fickleness? Or the things that I plan, do I plan according to the flesh, that with me there should be the \u201cYes, yes\u201d and the \u201cNo, no?\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But as God is faithful, our word toward you was not \u201cYes and no.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the Son of God, Jesus Christ, who was preached among you by us\u2014by me, Silvanus, and Timothy\u2014was not \u201cYes and no,\u201d but in him is \u201cYes.\u201d"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For however many are the promises of God, in him is the \u201cYes.\u201d Therefore also through him is the \u201cAmen\u201d, to the glory of God through us."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Now he who establishes us with you in Christ and anointed us is God,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"who also sealed us and gave us the down payment of the Spirit in our hearts."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But I call God for a witness to my soul, that to spare you, I didn\u2019t come to Corinth."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"We don\u2019t control your faith, but are fellow workers with you for your joy. For you stand firm in faith."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But I determined this for myself, that I would not come to you again in sorrow."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For if I make you grieve, then who will make me glad but he who is made to grieve by me?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"And I wrote this very thing to you, so that when I came, I wouldn\u2019t have sorrow from them of whom I ought to rejoice; having confidence in you all that my joy would be shared by all of you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For out of much affliction and anguish of heart I wrote to you with many tears, not that you should be made to grieve, but that you might know the love that I have so abundantly for you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But if any has caused sorrow, he has caused sorrow not to me, but in part (that I not press too heavily) to you all."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"This punishment which was inflicted by the many is sufficient for such a one;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"so that, on the contrary, you should rather forgive him and comfort him, lest by any means such a one should be swallowed up with his excessive sorrow."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore I beg you to confirm your love toward him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For to this end I also wrote, that I might know the proof of you, whether you are obedient in all things."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Now I also forgive whomever you forgive anything. For if indeed I have forgiven anything, I have forgiven that one for your sakes in the presence of Christ,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"that no advantage may be gained over us by Satan, for we are not ignorant of his schemes."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now when I came to Troas for the Good News of Christ, and when a door was opened to me in the Lord,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I had no relief for my spirit, because I didn\u2019t find Titus my brother, but taking my leave of them, I went out into Macedonia."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Now thanks be to God who always leads us in triumph in Christ, and reveals through us the sweet aroma of his knowledge in every place."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For we are a sweet aroma of Christ to God in those who are being saved and in those who perish:"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"to the one a stench from death to death, to the other a sweet aroma from life to life. Who is sufficient for these things?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For we are not as so many, peddling the word of God. But as of sincerity, but as of God, in the sight of God, we speak in Christ."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Are we beginning again to commend ourselves? Or do we need, as do some, letters of commendation to you or from you?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You are our letter, written in our hearts, known and read by all men,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"being revealed that you are a letter of Christ, served by us, written not with ink, but with the Spirit of the living God; not in tablets of stone, but in tablets that are hearts of flesh."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Such confidence we have through Christ toward God,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"not that we are sufficient of ourselves to account anything as from ourselves; but our sufficiency is from God,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"who also made us sufficient as servants of a new covenant, not of the letter but of the Spirit. For the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But if the service of death, written engraved on stones, came with glory, so that the children of Israel could not look steadfastly on the face of Moses for the glory of his face, which was passing away,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"won\u2019t service of the Spirit be with much more glory?"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For if the service of condemnation has glory, the service of righteousness exceeds much more in glory."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For most certainly that which has been made glorious has not been made glorious in this respect, by reason of the glory that surpasses."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For if that which passes away was with glory, much more that which remains is in glory."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Having therefore such a hope, we use great boldness of speech,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and not as Moses, who put a veil on his face so that the children of Israel wouldn\u2019t look steadfastly on the end of that which was passing away."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But their minds were hardened, for until this very day at the reading of the old covenant the same veil remains, because in Christ it passes away."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But to this day, when Moses is read, a veil lies on their heart."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But whenever someone turns to the Lord, the veil is taken away."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now the Lord is the Spirit; and where the Spirit of the Lord is, there is liberty."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But we all, with unveiled face seeing the glory of the Lord as in a mirror, are transformed into the same image from glory to glory, even as from the Lord, the Spirit."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, seeing we have this ministry, even as we obtained mercy, we don\u2019t faint."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"But we have renounced the hidden things of shame, not walking in craftiness nor handling the word of God deceitfully, but by the manifestation of the truth commending ourselves to every man\u2019s conscience in the sight of God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Even if our Good News is veiled, it is veiled in those who are dying,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"in whom the god of this world has blinded the minds of the unbelieving, that the light of the Good News of the glory of Christ, who is the image of God, should not dawn on them."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For we don\u2019t preach ourselves, but Christ Jesus as Lord, and ourselves as your servants for Jesus\u2019 sake,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"seeing it is God who said, \u201cLight will shine out of darkness,\u201d who has shone in our hearts to give the light of the knowledge of the glory of God in the face of Jesus Christ."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But we have this treasure in clay vessels, that the exceeding greatness of the power may be of God and not from ourselves."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"We are pressed on every side, yet not crushed; perplexed, yet not to despair;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"pursued, yet not forsaken; struck down, yet not destroyed;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"always carrying in the body the putting to death of the Lord Jesus, that the life of Jesus may also be revealed in our body."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For we who live are always delivered to death for Jesus\u2019 sake, that the life also of Jesus may be revealed in our mortal flesh."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So then death works in us, but life in you."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But having the same spirit of faith, according to that which is written, \u201cI believed, and therefore I spoke.\u201d We also believe, and therefore we also speak,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"knowing that he who raised the Lord Jesus will raise us also through Jesus, and will present us with you."]],f:["NU reads with instead of through."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For all things are for your sakes, that the grace, being multiplied through the many, may cause the thanksgiving to abound to the glory of God."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore we don\u2019t faint, but though our outward person is decaying, yet our inward person is renewed day by day."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For our light affliction, which is for the moment, works for us more and more exceedingly an eternal weight of glory,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"while we don\u2019t look at the things which are seen, but at the things which are not seen. For the things which are seen are temporal, but the things which are not seen are eternal."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For we know that if the earthly house of our tent is dissolved, we have a building from God, a house not made with hands, eternal, in the heavens."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For most certainly in this we groan, longing to be clothed with our habitation which is from heaven,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"if indeed being clothed, we will not be found naked."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For indeed we who are in this tent do groan, being burdened, not that we desire to be unclothed, but that we desire to be clothed, that what is mortal may be swallowed up by life."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now he who made us for this very thing is God, who also gave to us the down payment of the Spirit."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore we are always confident and know that while we are at home in the body, we are absent from the Lord;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"for we walk by faith, not by sight."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"We are courageous, I say, and are willing rather to be absent from the body and to be at home with the Lord."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore also we make it our aim, whether at home or absent, to be well pleasing to him."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For we must all be revealed before the judgment seat of Christ that each one may receive the things in the body according to what he has done, whether good or bad."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Knowing therefore the fear of the Lord, we persuade men, but we are revealed to God, and I hope that we are revealed also in your consciences."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For we are not commending ourselves to you again, but speak as giving you occasion of boasting on our behalf, that you may have something to answer those who boast in appearance and not in heart."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For if we are beside ourselves, it is for God. Or if we are of sober mind, it is for you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For the love of Christ compels us; because we judge thus: that one died for all, therefore all died."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He died for all, that those who live should no longer live to themselves, but to him who for their sakes died and rose again."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore we know no one according to the flesh from now on. Even though we have known Christ according to the flesh, yet now we know him so no more."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Therefore if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation. The old things have passed away. Behold, all things have become new."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But all things are of God, who reconciled us to himself through Jesus Christ, and gave to us the ministry of reconciliation;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"namely, that God was in Christ reconciling the world to himself, not reckoning to them their trespasses, and having committed to us the word of reconciliation."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"We are therefore ambassadors on behalf of Christ, as though God were entreating by us: we beg you on behalf of Christ, be reconciled to God."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For him who knew no sin he made to be sin on our behalf, so that in him we might become the righteousness of God."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Working together, we entreat also that you do not receive the grace of God in vain."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For he says,"],[1,"\u201cAt an acceptable time I listened to you."],[1,"In a day of salvation I helped you.\u201d"],[0,"Behold, now is the acceptable time. Behold, now is the day of salvation."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"We give no occasion of stumbling in anything, that our service may not be blamed,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"but in everything commending ourselves as servants of God: in great endurance, in afflictions, in hardships, in distresses,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"in beatings, in imprisonments, in riots, in labors, in watchings, in fastings,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"in pureness, in knowledge, in perseverance, in kindness, in the Holy Spirit, in sincere love,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"in the word of truth, in the power of God, by the armor of righteousness on the right hand and on the left,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"by glory and dishonor, by evil report and good report, as deceivers and yet true,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"as unknown and yet well known, as dying and behold\u2014we live, as punished and not killed,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"as sorrowful yet always rejoicing, as poor yet making many rich, as having nothing and yet possessing all things."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Our mouth is open to you, Corinthians. Our heart is enlarged."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"You are not restricted by us, but you are restricted by your own affections."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Now in return\u2014I speak as to my children\u2014you also open your hearts."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be unequally yoked with unbelievers, for what fellowship do righteousness and iniquity have? Or what fellowship does light have with darkness?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"What agreement does Christ have with Belial? Or what portion does a believer have with an unbeliever?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"What agreement does a temple of God have with idols? For you are a temple of the living God. Even as God said, \u201cI will dwell in them and walk in them. I will be their God and they will be my people.\u201d"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Therefore"],[1,"\u201c\u2018Come out from among them,"],[2,"and be separate,\u2019 says the Lord."],[1,"\u2018Touch no unclean thing."],[2,"I will receive you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[1,"I will be to you a Father."],[2,"You will be to me sons and daughters,\u2019"],[0,"says the Lord Almighty.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Having therefore these promises, beloved, let\u2019s cleanse ourselves from all defilement of flesh and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Open your hearts to us. We wronged no one. We corrupted no one. We took advantage of no one."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I say this not to condemn you, for I have said before that you are in our hearts to die together and live together."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Great is my boldness of speech toward you. Great is my boasting on your behalf. I am filled with comfort. I overflow with joy in all our affliction."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"For even when we had come into Macedonia, our flesh had no relief, but we were afflicted on every side. Fightings were outside. Fear was inside."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, he who comforts the lowly, God, comforted us by the coming of Titus,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and not by his coming only, but also by the comfort with which he was comforted in you while he told us of your longing, your mourning, and your zeal for me, so that I rejoiced still more."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"For though I grieved you with my letter, I do not regret it, though I did regret it. For I see that my letter made you grieve, though just for a while."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"I now rejoice, not that you were grieved, but that you were grieved to repentance. For you were grieved in a godly way, that you might suffer loss by us in nothing."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For godly sorrow produces repentance leading to salvation, which brings no regret. But the sorrow of the world produces death."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For behold, this same thing, that you were grieved in a godly way, what earnest care it worked in you. Yes, what defense, indignation, fear, longing, zeal, and vindication! In everything you demonstrated yourselves to be pure in the matter."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So although I wrote to you, I wrote not for his cause that did the wrong, nor for his cause that suffered the wrong, but that your earnest care for us might be revealed in you in the sight of God."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore we have been comforted. In our comfort we rejoiced the more exceedingly for the joy of Titus, because his spirit has been refreshed by you all."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For if in anything I have boasted to him on your behalf, I was not disappointed. But as we spoke all things to you in truth, so our glorying also which I made before Titus was found to be truth."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"His affection is more abundantly toward you, while he remembers all of your obedience, how with fear and trembling you received him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I rejoice that in everything I am confident concerning you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Moreover, brothers, we make known to you the grace of God which has been given in the assemblies of Macedonia,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"how in a severe ordeal of affliction, the abundance of their joy and their deep poverty abounded to the riches of their generosity."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For according to their power, I testify, yes and beyond their power, they gave of their own accord,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"begging us with much entreaty to receive this grace and the fellowship in the service to the saints."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"This was not as we had expected, but first they gave their own selves to the Lord, and to us through the will of God."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So we urged Titus, that as he had made a beginning before, so he would also complete in you this grace."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But as you abound in everything\u2014in faith, utterance, knowledge, all earnestness, and in your love to us\u2014see that you also abound in this grace."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"I speak not by way of commandment, but as proving through the earnestness of others the sincerity also of your love."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For you know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, that though he was rich, yet for your sakes he became poor, that you through his poverty might become rich."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I give advice in this: it is expedient for you who were the first to start a year ago, not only to do, but also to be willing."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But now complete the doing also, that as there was the readiness to be willing, so there may be the completion also out of your ability."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For if the readiness is there, it is acceptable according to what you have, not according to what you don\u2019t have."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For this is not that others may be eased and you distressed,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but for equality. Your abundance at this present time supplies their lack, that their abundance also may become a supply for your lack, that there may be equality."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"As it is written, \u201cHe who gathered much had nothing left over, and he who gathered little had no lack.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But thanks be to God, who puts the same earnest care for you into the heart of Titus."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For he indeed accepted our exhortation, but being himself very earnest, he went out to you of his own accord."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"We have sent together with him the brother whose praise in the Good News is known throughout all the assemblies."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Not only so, but he was also appointed by the assemblies to travel with us in this grace, which is served by us to the glory of the Lord himself, and to show our readiness."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"We are avoiding this, that any man should blame us concerning this abundance which is administered by us."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Having regard for honorable things, not only in the sight of the Lord, but also in the sight of men."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"We have sent with them our brother whom we have many times proved earnest in many things, but now much more earnest, by reason of the great confidence which he has in you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"As for Titus, he is my partner and fellow worker for you. As for our brothers, they are the apostles of the assemblies, the glory of Christ."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Therefore show the proof of your love to them before the assemblies, and of our boasting on your behalf."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It is indeed unnecessary for me to write to you concerning the service to the saints,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"for I know your readiness, of which I boast on your behalf to those of Macedonia, that Achaia has been prepared for the past year. Your zeal has stirred up very many of them."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But I have sent the brothers so that our boasting on your behalf may not be in vain in this respect, that, just as I said, you may be prepared,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"lest by any means, if anyone from Macedonia comes there with me and finds you unprepared, we (to say nothing of you) would be disappointed in this confident boasting."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I thought it necessary therefore to entreat the brothers that they would go before to you and arrange ahead of time the generous gift that you promised before, that the same might be ready as a matter of generosity, and not of greediness."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Remember this: he who sows sparingly will also reap sparingly. He who sows bountifully will also reap bountifully."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Let each man give according as he has determined in his heart, not grudgingly or under compulsion, for God loves a cheerful giver."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"And God is able to make all grace abound to you, that you, always having all sufficiency in everything, may abound to every good work."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"As it is written,"],[1,"\u201cHe has scattered abroad. He has given to the poor."],[2,"His righteousness remains forever.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Now may he who supplies seed to the sower and bread for food, supply and multiply your seed for sowing, and increase the fruits of your righteousness,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"you being enriched in everything for all generosity, which produces thanksgiving to God through us."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For this service of giving that you perform not only makes up for lack among the saints, but abounds also through much giving of thanks to God,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"seeing that through the proof given by this service, they glorify God for the obedience of your confession to the Good News of Christ and for the generosity of your contribution to them and to all,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"while they themselves also, with supplication on your behalf, yearn for you by reason of the exceeding grace of God in you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Now thanks be to God for his unspeakable gift!"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I Paul, myself, entreat you by the humility and gentleness of Christ, I who in your presence am lowly among you, but being absent am bold toward you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Yes, I beg you that I may not, when present, show courage with the confidence with which I intend to be bold against some, who consider us to be walking according to the flesh."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For though we walk in the flesh, we don\u2019t wage war according to the flesh;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"for the weapons of our warfare are not of the flesh, but mighty before God to the throwing down of strongholds,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"throwing down imaginations and every high thing that is exalted against the knowledge of God and bringing every thought into captivity to the obedience of Christ,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and being in readiness to avenge all disobedience when your obedience is made full."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Do you look at things only as they appear in front of your face? If anyone trusts in himself that he is Christ\u2019s, let him consider this again with himself, that even as he is Christ\u2019s, so we also are Christ\u2019s."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For even if I boast somewhat abundantly concerning our authority, which the Lord gave for building you up and not for casting you down, I will not be ashamed,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"that I may not seem as if I desire to terrify you by my letters."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For, \u201cHis letters\u201d, they say, \u201care weighty and strong, but his bodily presence is weak, and his speech is despised.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Let such a person consider this, that what we are in word by letters when we are absent, such are we also in deed when we are present."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"For we are not bold to number or compare ourselves with some of those who commend themselves. But they themselves, measuring themselves by themselves, and comparing themselves with themselves, are without understanding."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But we will not boast beyond proper limits, but within the boundaries with which God appointed to us, which reach even to you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For we don\u2019t stretch ourselves too much, as though we didn\u2019t reach to you. For we came even as far as to you with the Good News of Christ,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"not boasting beyond proper limits in other men\u2019s labors, but having hope that as your faith grows, we will be abundantly enlarged by you in our sphere of influence,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"so as to preach the Good News even to the parts beyond you, not to boast in what someone else has already done."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But \u201che who boasts, let him boast in the Lord.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For it isn\u2019t he who commends himself who is approved, but whom the Lord commends."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I wish that you would bear with me in a little foolishness, but indeed you do bear with me."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For I am jealous over you with a godly jealousy. For I promised you in marriage to one husband, that I might present you as a pure virgin to Christ."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But I am afraid that somehow, as the serpent deceived Eve in his craftiness, so your minds might be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Christ."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For if he who comes preaches another Jesus whom we didn\u2019t preach, or if you receive a different spirit which you didn\u2019t receive, or a different \u201cgood news\u201d which you didn\u2019t accept, you put up with that well enough."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For I reckon that I am not at all behind the very best apostles."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But though I am unskilled in speech, yet I am not unskilled in knowledge. No, in every way we have been revealed to you in all things."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Or did I commit a sin in humbling myself that you might be exalted, because I preached to you God\u2019s Good News free of charge?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I robbed other assemblies, taking wages from them that I might serve you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"When I was present with you and was in need, I wasn\u2019t a burden on anyone, for the brothers, when they came from Macedonia, supplied the measure of my need. In everything I kept myself from being burdensome to you, and I will continue to do so."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As the truth of Christ is in me, no one will stop me from this boasting in the regions of Achaia."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Why? Because I don\u2019t love you? God knows."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"But what I do, that I will continue to do, that I may cut off opportunity from those who desire an opportunity, that in which they boast, they may be recognized just like us."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For such men are false apostles, deceitful workers, masquerading as Christ\u2019s apostles."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"And no wonder, for even Satan masquerades as an angel of light."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"It is no great thing therefore if his servants also masquerade as servants of righteousness, whose end will be according to their works."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"I say again, let no one think me foolish. But if so, yet receive me as foolish, that I also may boast a little."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"That which I speak, I don\u2019t speak according to the Lord, but as in foolishness, in this confidence of boasting."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Seeing that many boast after the flesh, I will also boast."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For you bear with the foolish gladly, being wise."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For you bear with a man if he brings you into bondage, if he devours you, if he takes you captive, if he exalts himself, or if he strikes you on the face."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"To my shame, I speak as though we had been weak. Yet in whatever way anyone is bold (I speak in foolishness), I am bold also."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Are they Hebrews? So am I. Are they Israelites? So am I. Are they the offspring of Abraham? So am I."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Are they servants of Christ? (I speak as one beside himself.) I am more so: in labors more abundantly, in prisons more abundantly, in stripes above measure, and in deaths often."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Five times I received forty stripes minus one from the Jews."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Three times I was beaten with rods. Once I was stoned. Three times I suffered shipwreck. I have been a night and a day in the deep."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"I have been in travels often, perils of rivers, perils of robbers, perils from my countrymen, perils from the Gentiles, perils in the city, perils in the wilderness, perils in the sea, perils among false brothers;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"in labor and travail, in watchings often, in hunger and thirst, in fastings often, and in cold and nakedness."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Besides those things that are outside, there is that which presses on me daily: anxiety for all the assemblies."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Who is weak, and I am not weak? Who is caused to stumble, and I don\u2019t burn with indignation?"]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"If I must boast, I will boast of the things that concern my weakness."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"The God and Father of the Lord Jesus Christ, he who is blessed forever more, knows that I don\u2019t lie."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"In Damascus the governor under King Aretas guarded the Damascenes\u2019 city, desiring to arrest me."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"I was let down in a basket through a window by the wall, and escaped his hands."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"It is doubtless not profitable for me to boast, but I will come to visions and revelations of the Lord."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I know a man in Christ who was caught up into the third heaven fourteen years ago\u2014whether in the body, I don\u2019t know, or whether out of the body, I don\u2019t know; God knows."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I know such a man (whether in the body, or outside of the body, I don\u2019t know; God knows),"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"how he was caught up into Paradise and heard unspeakable words, which it is not lawful for a man to utter."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"On behalf of such a one I will boast, but on my own behalf I will not boast, except in my weaknesses."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For if I would desire to boast, I will not be foolish; for I will speak the truth. But I refrain, so that no man may think more of me than that which he sees in me or hears from me."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"By reason of the exceeding greatness of the revelations, that I should not be exalted excessively, a thorn in the flesh was given to me: a messenger of Satan to torment me, that I should not be exalted excessively."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Concerning this thing, I begged the Lord three times that it might depart from me."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He has said to me, \u201cMy grace is sufficient for you, for my power is made perfect in weakness.\u201d Most gladly therefore I will rather glory in my weaknesses, that the power of Christ may rest on me."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore I take pleasure in weaknesses, in injuries, in necessities, in persecutions, and in distresses, for Christ\u2019s sake. For when I am weak, then am I strong."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I have become foolish in boasting. You compelled me, for I ought to have been commended by you, for I am in no way inferior to the very best apostles, though I am nothing."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Truly the signs of an apostle were worked among you in all perseverance, in signs and wonders and mighty works."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For what is there in which you were made inferior to the rest of the assemblies, unless it is that I myself was not a burden to you? Forgive me this wrong!"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, this is the third time I am ready to come to you, and I will not be a burden to you; for I seek not your possessions, but you. For the children ought not to save up for the parents, but the parents for the children."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"I will most gladly spend and be spent for your souls. If I love you more abundantly, am I loved the less?"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Even so, I myself didn\u2019t burden you. But you might say that being crafty, I caught you with deception."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Did I take advantage of you by anyone of those whom I have sent to you?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I exhorted Titus, and I sent the brother with him. Did Titus take any advantage of you? Didn\u2019t we walk in the same spirit? Didn\u2019t we walk in the same steps?"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, do you think that we are excusing ourselves to you? In the sight of God we speak in Christ. But all things, beloved, are for your edifying."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For I am afraid that perhaps when I come, I might find you not the way I want to, and that I might be found by you as you don\u2019t desire, that perhaps there would be strife, jealousy, outbursts of anger, factions, slander, whisperings, proud thoughts, or riots,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"that again when I come my God would humble me before you, and I would mourn for many of those who have sinned before now, and not repented of the uncleanness, sexual immorality, and lustfulness which they committed."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the third time I am coming to you. \u201cAt the mouth of two or three witnesses shall every word be established.\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I have warned previously, and I warn again, as when I was present the second time, so now, being absent, I write to those who have sinned before now and to all the rest that if I come again, I will not spare,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"seeing that you seek a proof of Christ who speaks in me who is not weak, but is powerful in you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For he was crucified through weakness, yet he lives through the power of God. For we also are weak in him, but we will live with him through the power of God toward you."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Examine your own selves, whether you are in the faith. Test your own selves. Or don\u2019t you know about your own selves, that Jesus Christ is in you?\u2014unless indeed you are disqualified."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But I hope that you will know that we aren\u2019t disqualified."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I pray to God that you do no evil; not that we may appear approved, but that you may do that which is honorable, though we may seem to have failed."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For we can do nothing against the truth, but for the truth."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For we rejoice when we are weak and you are strong. We also pray for this: your becoming perfect."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For this cause I write these things while absent, that I may not deal sharply when present, according to the authority which the Lord gave me for building up and not for tearing down."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Finally, brothers, rejoice! Be perfected. Be comforted. Be of the same mind. Live in peace, and the God of love and peace will be with you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Greet one another with a holy kiss."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"All the saints greet you."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ, God\u2019s love, and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with you all. Amen."]]}]]}},1318,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,i,r){a.exports={book:"Gal",name:"Galatians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, an apostle\u2014not from men, nor through man, but through Jesus Christ, and God the Father, who raised him from the dead\u2014"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and all the brothers who are with me, to the assemblies of Galatia:"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace from God the Father and our Lord Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"who gave himself for our sins, that he might deliver us out of this present evil age, according to the will of our God and Father\u2014"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"to whom be the glory forever and ever. Amen."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I marvel that you are so quickly deserting him who called you in the grace of Christ to a different \u201cgood news\u201d,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"but there isn\u2019t another \u201cgood news.\u201d Only there are some who trouble you and want to pervert the Good News of Christ."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But even though we, or an angel from heaven, should preach to you any \u201cgood news\u201d other than that which we preached to you, let him be cursed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"As we have said before, so I now say again: if any man preaches to you any \u201cgood news\u201d other than that which you received, let him be cursed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"For am I now seeking the favor of men, or of God? Or am I striving to please men? For if I were still pleasing men, I wouldn\u2019t be a servant of Christ."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But I make known to you, brothers, concerning the Good News which was preached by me, that it is not according to man."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For I didn\u2019t receive it from man, nor was I taught it, but it came to me through revelation of Jesus Christ."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For you have heard of my way of living in time past in the Jews\u2019 religion, how that beyond measure I persecuted the assembly of God and ravaged it."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I advanced in the Jews\u2019 religion beyond many of my own age among my countrymen, being more exceedingly zealous for the traditions of my fathers."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But when it was the good pleasure of God, who separated me from my mother\u2019s womb and called me through his grace,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"to reveal his Son in me, that I might preach him among the Gentiles, I didn\u2019t immediately confer with flesh and blood,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"nor did I go up to Jerusalem to those who were apostles before me, but I went away into Arabia. Then I returned to Damascus."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Then after three years I went up to Jerusalem to visit Peter, and stayed with him fifteen days."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"But of the other apostles I saw no one except James, the Lord\u2019s brother."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now about the things which I write to you, behold, before God, I\u2019m not lying."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Then I came to the regions of Syria and Cilicia."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I was still unknown by face to the assemblies of Judea which were in Christ,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"but they only heard, \u201cHe who once persecuted us now preaches the faith that he once tried to destroy.\u201d"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"So they glorified God in me."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then after a period of fourteen years I went up again to Jerusalem with Barnabas, taking Titus also with me."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I went up by revelation, and I laid before them the Good News which I preach among the Gentiles, but privately before those who were respected, for fear that I might be running, or had run, in vain."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But not even Titus, who was with me, being a Greek, was compelled to be circumcised."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"This was because of the false brothers secretly brought in, who stole in to spy out our liberty which we have in Christ Jesus, that they might bring us into bondage,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"to whom we gave no place in the way of subjection, not for an hour, that the truth of the Good News might continue with you."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But from those who were reputed to be important\u2014whatever they were, it makes no difference to me; God doesn\u2019t show partiality to man\u2014they, I say, who were respected imparted nothing to me,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"but to the contrary, when they saw that I had been entrusted with the Good News for the uncircumcised, even as Peter with the Good News for the circumcised\u2014"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"for he who worked through Peter in the apostleship with the circumcised also worked through me with the Gentiles\u2014"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and when they perceived the grace that was given to me, James and Cephas and John, those who were reputed to be pillars, gave to Barnabas and me the right hand of fellowship, that we should go to the Gentiles, and they to the circumcision."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They only asked us to remember the poor\u2014which very thing I was also zealous to do."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But when Peter came to Antioch, I resisted him to his face, because he stood condemned."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For before some people came from James, he ate with the Gentiles. But when they came, he drew back and separated himself, fearing those who were of the circumcision."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"And the rest of the Jews joined him in his hypocrisy, so that even Barnabas was carried away with their hypocrisy."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But when I saw that they didn\u2019t walk uprightly according to the truth of the Good News, I said to Peter before them all, \u201cIf you, being a Jew, live as the Gentiles do, and not as the Jews do, why do you compel the Gentiles to live as the Jews do?"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cWe, being Jews by nature and not Gentile sinners,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"yet knowing that a man is not justified by the works of the law but through faith in Jesus Christ, even we believed in Christ Jesus, that we might be justified by faith in Christ and not by the works of the law, because no flesh will be justified by the works of the law."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But if while we sought to be justified in Christ, we ourselves also were found sinners, is Christ a servant of sin? Certainly not!"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For if I build up again those things which I destroyed, I prove myself a law-breaker."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For I through the law died to the law, that I might live to God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"I have been crucified with Christ, and it is no longer I who live, but Christ lives in me. That life which I now live in the flesh, I live by faith in the Son of God, who loved me and gave himself up for me."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I don\u2019t reject the grace of God. For if righteousness is through the law, then Christ died for nothing!\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Foolish Galatians, who has bewitched you not to obey the truth, before whose eyes Jesus Christ was openly portrayed among you as crucified?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I just want to learn this from you: Did you receive the Spirit by the works of the law, or by hearing of faith?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Are you so foolish? Having begun in the Spirit, are you now completed in the flesh?"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Did you suffer so many things in vain, if it is indeed in vain?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He therefore who supplies the Spirit to you and does miracles among you, does he do it by the works of the law, or by hearing of faith?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Even so, Abraham \u201cbelieved God, and it was counted to him for righteousness.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Know therefore that those who are of faith are children of Abraham."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The Scripture, foreseeing that God would justify the Gentiles by faith, preached the Good News beforehand to Abraham, saying, \u201cIn you all the nations will be blessed.\u201d"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"So then, those who are of faith are blessed with the faithful Abraham."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"For as many as are of the works of the law are under a curse. For it is written, \u201cCursed is everyone who doesn\u2019t continue in all things that are written in the book of the law, to do them.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Now that no man is justified by the law before God is evident, for, \u201cThe righteous will live by faith.\u201d"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The law is not of faith, but, \u201cThe man who does them will live by them.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Christ redeemed us from the curse of the law, having become a curse for us. For it is written, \u201cCursed is everyone who hangs on a tree,\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"that the blessing of Abraham might come on the Gentiles through Christ Jesus, that we might receive the promise of the Spirit through faith."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, speaking of human terms, though it is only a man\u2019s covenant, yet when it has been confirmed, no one makes it void or adds to it."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Now the promises were spoken to Abraham and to his offspring. He doesn\u2019t say, \u201cTo descendants\u201d, as of many, but as of one, \u201cTo your offspring\u201d, which is Christ."]],f:["or, seed","or, seeds"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now I say this: A covenant confirmed beforehand by God in Christ, the law, which came four hundred thirty years after, does not annul, so as to make the promise of no effect."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For if the inheritance is of the law, it is no more of promise; but God has granted it to Abraham by promise."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Then why is there the law? It was added because of transgressions, until the offspring should come to whom the promise has been made. It was ordained through angels by the hand of a mediator."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now a mediator is not between one, but God is one."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Is the law then against the promises of God? Certainly not! For if there had been a law given which could make alive, most certainly righteousness would have been of the law."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But the Scripture imprisoned all things under sin, that the promise by faith in Jesus Christ might be given to those who believe."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"But before faith came, we were kept in custody under the law, confined for the faith which should afterwards be revealed."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"So that the law has become our tutor to bring us to Christ, that we might be justified by faith."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But now that faith has come, we are no longer under a tutor."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For you are all children of God, through faith in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For as many of you as were baptized into Christ have put on Christ."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"There is neither Jew nor Greek, there is neither slave nor free man, there is neither male nor female; for you are all one in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"If you are Christ\u2019s, then you are Abraham\u2019s offspring and heirs according to promise."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But I say that so long as the heir is a child, he is no different from a bondservant, though he is lord of all,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"but is under guardians and stewards until the day appointed by the father."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"So we also, when we were children, were held in bondage under the elemental principles of the world."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But when the fullness of the time came, God sent out his Son, born to a woman, born under the law,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"that he might redeem those who were under the law, that we might receive the adoption as children."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"And because you are children, God sent out the Spirit of his Son into your hearts, crying, \u201cAbba, Father!\u201d"]],f:["Abba is a Greek spelling for the Aramaic word for \u201cFather\u201d or \u201cDaddy\u201d used in a familiar, respectful, and loving way."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"So you are no longer a bondservant, but a son; and if a son, then an heir of God through Christ."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"However at that time, not knowing God, you were in bondage to those who by nature are not gods."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But now that you have come to know God, or rather to be known by God, why do you turn back again to the weak and miserable elemental principles, to which you desire to be in bondage all over again?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You observe days, months, seasons, and years."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I am afraid for you, that I might have wasted my labor for you."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I beg you, brothers, become as I am, for I also have become as you are. You did me no wrong,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but you know that because of weakness in the flesh I preached the Good News to you the first time."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"That which was a temptation to you in my flesh, you didn\u2019t despise nor reject; but you received me as an angel of God, even as Christ Jesus."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"What was the blessing you enjoyed? For I testify to you that, if possible, you would have plucked out your eyes and given them to me."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So then, have I become your enemy by telling you the truth?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"They zealously seek you in no good way. No, they desire to alienate you, that you may seek them."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But it is always good to be zealous in a good cause, and not only when I am present with you."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"My little children, of whom I am again in travail until Christ is formed in you\u2014"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"but I could wish to be present with you now, and to change my tone, for I am perplexed about you."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Tell me, you that desire to be under the law, don\u2019t you listen to the law?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"For it is written that Abraham had two sons, one by the servant, and one by the free woman."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"However, the son by the servant was born according to the flesh, but the son by the free woman was born through promise."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"These things contain an allegory, for these are two covenants. One is from Mount Sinai, bearing children to bondage, which is Hagar."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For this Hagar is Mount Sinai in Arabia, and answers to the Jerusalem that exists now, for she is in bondage with her children."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"But the Jerusalem that is above is free, which is the mother of us all."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For it is written,"],[1,"\u201cRejoice, you barren who don\u2019t bear."],[2,"Break out and shout, you who don\u2019t travail."],[2,"For the desolate women have more children than her who has a husband.\u201d"]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Now we, brothers, as Isaac was, are children of promise."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"But as then, he who was born according to the flesh persecuted him who was born according to the Spirit, so also it is now."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"However, what does the Scripture say? \u201cThrow out the servant and her son, for the son of the servant will not inherit with the son of the free woman.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"So then, brothers, we are not children of a servant, but of the free woman."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Stand firm therefore in the liberty by which Christ has made us free, and don\u2019t be entangled again with a yoke of bondage."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, I, Paul, tell you that if you receive circumcision, Christ will profit you nothing."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Yes, I testify again to every man who receives circumcision that he is a debtor to do the whole law."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You are alienated from Christ, you who desire to be justified by the law. You have fallen away from grace."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For we through the Spirit, by faith wait for the hope of righteousness."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For in Christ Jesus neither circumcision nor uncircumcision amounts to anything, but faith working through love."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"You were running well! Who interfered with you that you should not obey the truth?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"This persuasion is not from him who calls you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"A little yeast grows through the whole lump."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I have confidence toward you in the Lord that you will think no other way. But he who troubles you will bear his judgment, whoever he is."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But I, brothers, if I still preach circumcision, why am I still persecuted? Then the stumbling block of the cross has been removed."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I wish that those who disturb you would cut themselves off."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"For you, brothers, were called for freedom. Only don\u2019t use your freedom as an opportunity for the flesh, but through love be servants to one another."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For the whole law is fulfilled in one word, in this: \u201cYou shall love your neighbor as yourself.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But if you bite and devour one another, be careful that you don\u2019t consume one another."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"But I say, walk by the Spirit, and you won\u2019t fulfill the lust of the flesh."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For the flesh lusts against the Spirit, and the Spirit against the flesh; and these are contrary to one another, that you may not do the things that you desire."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But if you are led by the Spirit, you are not under the law."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Now the deeds of the flesh are obvious, which are: adultery, sexual immorality, uncleanness, lustfulness,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"idolatry, sorcery, hatred, strife, jealousies, outbursts of anger, rivalries, divisions, heresies,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"envy, murders, drunkenness, orgies, and things like these; of which I forewarn you, even as I also forewarned you, that those who practice such things will not inherit God\u2019s Kingdom."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But the fruit of the Spirit is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faith,"]],f:["or, faithfulness"]},{v:23,l:[[0,"gentleness, and self-control. Against such things there is no law."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Those who belong to Christ have crucified the flesh with its passions and lusts."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"If we live by the Spirit, let\u2019s also walk by the Spirit."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s not become conceited, provoking one another, and envying one another."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, even if a man is caught in some fault, you who are spiritual must restore such a one in a spirit of gentleness, looking to yourself so that you also aren\u2019t tempted."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Bear one another\u2019s burdens, and so fulfill the law of Christ."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For if a man thinks himself to be something when he is nothing, he deceives himself."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But let each man examine his own work, and then he will have reason to boast in himself, and not in someone else."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For each man will bear his own burden."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But let him who is taught in the word share all good things with him who teaches."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be deceived. God is not mocked, for whatever a man sows, that he will also reap."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For he who sows to his own flesh will from the flesh reap corruption. But he who sows to the Spirit will from the Spirit reap eternal life."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s not be weary in doing good, for we will reap in due season if we don\u2019t give up."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"So then, as we have opportunity, let\u2019s do what is good toward all men, and especially toward those who are of the household of the faith."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"See with what large letters I write to you with my own hand."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"As many as desire to make a good impression in the flesh compel you to be circumcised, just so they may not be persecuted for the cross of Christ."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For even they who receive circumcision don\u2019t keep the law themselves, but they desire to have you circumcised, so that they may boast in your flesh."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But far be it from me to boast except in the cross of our Lord Jesus Christ, through which the world has been crucified to me, and I to the world."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For in Christ Jesus neither is circumcision anything, nor uncircumcision, but a new creation."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"As many as walk by this rule, peace and mercy be on them, and on God\u2019s Israel."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"From now on, let no one cause me any trouble, for I bear the marks of the Lord Jesus branded on my body."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit, brothers. Amen."]]}]]}},1319,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,i,a,n){i.exports={book:"Eph",name:"Ephesians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus through the will of God, to the saints who are at Ephesus, and the faithful in Christ Jesus:"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly places in Christ,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"even as he chose us in him before the foundation of the world, that we would be holy and without defect before him in love,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"having predestined us for adoption as children through Jesus Christ to himself, according to the good pleasure of his desire,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"to the praise of the glory of his grace, by which he freely gave us favor in the Beloved."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In him we have our redemption through his blood, the forgiveness of our trespasses, according to the riches of his grace"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"which he made to abound toward us in all wisdom and prudence,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"making known to us the mystery of his will, according to his good pleasure which he purposed in him"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"to an administration of the fullness of the times, to sum up all things in Christ, the things in the heavens and the things on the earth, in him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"We were also assigned an inheritance in him, having been foreordained according to the purpose of him who does all things after the counsel of his will,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"to the end that we should be to the praise of his glory, we who had before hoped in Christ."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"In him you also, having heard the word of the truth, the Good News of your salvation\u2014in whom, having also believed, you were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"who is a pledge of our inheritance, to the redemption of God\u2019s own possession, to the praise of his glory."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause I also, having heard of the faith in the Lord Jesus which is among you and the love which you have toward all the saints,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"don\u2019t cease to give thanks for you, making mention of you in my prayers,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give to you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in the knowledge of him,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"having the eyes of your hearts enlightened, that you may know what is the hope of his calling, and what are the riches of the glory of his inheritance in the saints,"]],f:["TR reads \u201cunderstanding\u201d instead of \u201chearts\u201d"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and what is the exceeding greatness of his power toward us who believe, according to that working of the strength of his might"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"which he worked in Christ when he raised him from the dead and made him to sit at his right hand in the heavenly places,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"far above all rule, authority, power, dominion, and every name that is named, not only in this age, but also in that which is to come."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He put all things in subjection under his feet, and gave him to be head over all things for the assembly,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"which is his body, the fullness of him who fills all in all."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"You were made alive when you were dead in transgressions and sins,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"in which you once walked according to the course of this world, according to the prince of the power of the air, the spirit who now works in the children of disobedience."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"We also all once lived among them in the lusts of our flesh, doing the desires of the flesh and of the mind, and were by nature children of wrath, even as the rest."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But God, being rich in mercy, for his great love with which he loved us,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"even when we were dead through our trespasses, made us alive together with Christ\u2014by grace you have been saved\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and raised us up with him, and made us to sit with him in the heavenly places in Christ Jesus,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"that in the ages to come he might show the exceeding riches of his grace in kindness toward us in Christ Jesus;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"for by grace you have been saved through faith, and that not of yourselves; it is the gift of God,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"not of works, that no one would boast."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God prepared before that we would walk in them."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore remember that once you, the Gentiles in the flesh, who are called \u201cuncircumcision\u201d by that which is called \u201ccircumcision\u201d (in the flesh, made by hands),"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that you were at that time separate from Christ, alienated from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers from the covenants of the promise, having no hope and without God in the world."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But now in Christ Jesus you who once were far off are made near in the blood of Christ."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For he is our peace, who made both one, and broke down the middle wall of separation,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"having abolished in his flesh the hostility, the law of commandments contained in ordinances, that he might create in himself one new man of the two, making peace,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and might reconcile them both in one body to God through the cross, having killed the hostility through it."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He came and preached peace to you who were far off and to those who were near."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For through him we both have our access in one Spirit to the Father."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"So then you are no longer strangers and foreigners, but you are fellow citizens with the saints and of the household of God,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"being built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, Christ Jesus himself being the chief cornerstone;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"in whom the whole building, fitted together, grows into a holy temple in the Lord;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"in whom you also are built together for a habitation of God in the Spirit."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause I, Paul, am the prisoner of Christ Jesus on behalf of you Gentiles,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"if it is so that you have heard of the administration of that grace of God which was given me toward you,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"how that by revelation the mystery was made known to me, as I wrote before in few words,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"by which, when you read, you can perceive my understanding in the mystery of Christ,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"which in other generations was not made known to the children of men, as it has now been revealed to his holy apostles and prophets in the Spirit,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"that the Gentiles are fellow heirs and fellow members of the body, and fellow partakers of his promise in Christ Jesus through the Good News,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"of which I was made a servant according to the gift of that grace of God which was given me according to the working of his power."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"To me, the very least of all saints, was this grace given, to preach to the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and to make all men see what is the administration of the mystery which for ages has been hidden in God, who created all things through Jesus Christ,"]],f:["TR reads \u201cfellowship\u201d instead of \u201cadministration\u201d"]},{v:10,l:[[0,"to the intent that now through the assembly the manifold wisdom of God might be made known to the principalities and the powers in the heavenly places,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"according to the eternal purpose which he accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"In him we have boldness and access in confidence through our faith in him."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore I ask that you may not lose heart at my troubles for you, which are your glory."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause, I bow my knees to the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"from whom every family in heaven and on earth is named,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"that he would grant you, according to the riches of his glory, that you may be strengthened with power through his Spirit in the inner person,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"that Christ may dwell in your hearts through faith, to the end that you, being rooted and grounded in love,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"may be strengthened to comprehend with all the saints what is the width and length and height and depth,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and to know Christ\u2019s love which surpasses knowledge, that you may be filled with all the fullness of God."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now to him who is able to do exceedingly abundantly above all that we ask or think, according to the power that works in us,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"to him be the glory in the assembly and in Christ Jesus to all generations, forever and ever. Amen."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I therefore, the prisoner in the Lord, beg you to walk worthily of the calling with which you were called,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"with all lowliness and humility, with patience, bearing with one another in love,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"being eager to keep the unity of the Spirit in the bond of peace."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"There is one body and one Spirit, even as you also were called in one hope of your calling,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"one Lord, one faith, one baptism,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"one God and Father of all, who is over all and through all and in us all."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But to each one of us, the grace was given according to the measure of the gift of Christ."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore he says,"],[1,"\u201cWhen he ascended on high,"],[2,"he led captivity captive,"],[2,"and gave gifts to people.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Now this, \u201cHe ascended\u201d, what is it but that he also first descended into the lower parts of the earth?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He who descended is the one who also ascended far above all the heavens, that he might fill all things."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"He gave some to be apostles; and some, prophets; and some, evangelists; and some, shepherds and teachers;"]],f:["or, pastors"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"for the perfecting of the saints, to the work of serving, to the building up of the body of Christ,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"until we all attain to the unity of the faith and of the knowledge of the Son of God, to a full grown man, to the measure of the stature of the fullness of Christ,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"that we may no longer be children, tossed back and forth and carried about with every wind of doctrine, by the trickery of men, in craftiness, after the wiles of error;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but speaking truth in love, we may grow up in all things into him who is the head, Christ,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"from whom all the body, being fitted and knit together through that which every joint supplies, according to the working in measure of each individual part, makes the body increase to the building up of itself in love."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"This I say therefore, and testify in the Lord, that you no longer walk as the rest of the Gentiles also walk, in the futility of their mind,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"being darkened in their understanding, alienated from the life of God because of the ignorance that is in them, because of the hardening of their hearts."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They, having become callous, gave themselves up to lust, to work all uncleanness with greediness."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But you didn\u2019t learn Christ that way,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"if indeed you heard him and were taught in him, even as truth is in Jesus:"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"that you put away, as concerning your former way of life, the old man that grows corrupt after the lusts of deceit,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and that you be renewed in the spirit of your mind,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"and put on the new man, who in the likeness of God has been created in righteousness and holiness of truth."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, putting away falsehood, speak truth each one with his neighbor, for we are members of one another."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"\u201cBe angry, and don\u2019t sin.\u201d Don\u2019t let the sun go down on your wrath,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"and don\u2019t give place to the devil."]],f:["or, opportunity"]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Let him who stole steal no more; but rather let him labor, producing with his hands something that is good, that he may have something to give to him who has need."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Let no corrupt speech proceed out of your mouth, but only what is good for building others up as the need may be, that it may give grace to those who hear."]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t grieve the Holy Spirit of God, in whom you were sealed for the day of redemption."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"Let all bitterness, wrath, anger, outcry, and slander be put away from you, with all malice."]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"And be kind to one another, tender hearted, forgiving each other, just as God also in Christ forgave you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Be therefore imitators of God, as beloved children."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Walk in love, even as Christ also loved us and gave himself up for us, an offering and a sacrifice to God for a sweet-smelling fragrance."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"But sexual immorality, and all uncleanness or covetousness, let it not even be mentioned among you, as becomes saints;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"nor filthiness, nor foolish talking, nor jesting, which are not appropriate, but rather giving of thanks."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Know this for sure, that no sexually immoral person, nor unclean person, nor covetous man (who is an idolater), has any inheritance in the Kingdom of Christ and God."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Let no one deceive you with empty words, for because of these things the wrath of God comes on the children of disobedience."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t be partakers with them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For you were once darkness, but are now light in the Lord. Walk as children of light,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"for the fruit of the Spirit is in all goodness and righteousness and truth,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"proving what is well pleasing to the Lord."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Have no fellowship with the unfruitful deeds of darkness, but rather even reprove them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For it is a shame even to speak of the things which are done by them in secret."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But all things, when they are reproved, are revealed by the light, for everything that reveals is light."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Therefore he says, \u201cAwake, you who sleep, and arise from the dead, and Christ will shine on you.\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore watch carefully how you walk, not as unwise, but as wise,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"redeeming the time, because the days are evil."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Therefore, don\u2019t be foolish, but understand what the will of the Lord is."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be drunken with wine, in which is dissipation, but be filled with the Spirit,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"speaking to one another in psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs; singing and making melody in your heart to the Lord;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"giving thanks always concerning all things in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ to God, even the Father;"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"subjecting yourselves to one another in the fear of Christ."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Wives, be subject to your own husbands, as to the Lord."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For the husband is the head of the wife, as Christ also is the head of the assembly, being himself the savior of the body."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But as the assembly is subject to Christ, so let the wives also be to their own husbands in everything."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Husbands, love your wives, even as Christ also loved the assembly and gave himself up for her,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"that he might sanctify her, having cleansed her by the washing of water with the word,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"that he might present the assembly to himself gloriously, not having spot or wrinkle or any such thing, but that she should be holy and without defect."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Even so husbands also ought to love their own wives as their own bodies. He who loves his own wife loves himself."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"For no man ever hated his own flesh, but nourishes and cherishes it, even as the Lord also does the assembly,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"because we are members of his body, of his flesh and bones."]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"\u201cFor this cause a man will leave his father and mother and will be joined to his wife. Then the two will become one flesh.\u201d"]]},{v:32,l:[[0,"This mystery is great, but I speak concerning Christ and the assembly."]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"Nevertheless each of you must also love his own wife even as himself; and let the wife see that she respects her husband."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Children, obey your parents in the Lord, for this is right."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"\u201cHonor your father and mother,\u201d which is the first commandment with a promise:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"\u201cthat it may be well with you, and you may live long on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"You fathers, don\u2019t provoke your children to wrath, but nurture them in the discipline and instruction of the Lord."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Servants, be obedient to those who according to the flesh are your masters, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as to Christ,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"not in the way of service only when eyes are on you, as men pleasers, but as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from the heart,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"with good will doing service as to the Lord and not to men,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"knowing that whatever good thing each one does, he will receive the same good again from the Lord, whether he is bound or free."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"You masters, do the same things to them, and give up threatening, knowing that he who is both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no partiality with him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Finally, be strong in the Lord and in the strength of his might."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Put on the whole armor of God, that you may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For our wrestling is not against flesh and blood, but against the principalities, against the powers, against the world\u2019s rulers of the darkness of this age, and against the spiritual forces of wickedness in the heavenly places."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Therefore put on the whole armor of God, that you may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Stand therefore, having the utility belt of truth buckled around your waist, and having put on the breastplate of righteousness,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and having fitted your feet with the preparation of the Good News of peace,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"above all, taking up the shield of faith, with which you will be able to quench all the fiery darts of the evil one."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God;"]],f:["from the Greek \u201c\u1fe5\u1fc6\u03bc\u03b1\u201d (rhema), which means \u201cspoken word\u201d"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"with all prayer and requests, praying at all times in the Spirit, and being watchful to this end in all perseverance and requests for all the saints."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Pray for me, that utterance may be given to me in opening my mouth, to make known with boldness the mystery of the Good News,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"for which I am an ambassador in chains; that in it I may speak boldly, as I ought to speak."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"But that you also may know my affairs, how I am doing, Tychicus, the beloved brother and faithful servant in the Lord, will make known to you all things."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"I have sent him to you for this very purpose, that you may know our state and that he may comfort your hearts."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Peace be to the brothers, and love with faith, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Grace be with all those who love our Lord Jesus Christ with incorruptible love. Amen."]]}]]}},1320,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,h,a,n,i){a.exports={book:"Phil",name:"Philippians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul and Timothy, servants of Jesus Christ, to all the saints in Christ Jesus who are at Philippi, with the overseers and servants:"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d.","or, superintendents, or bishops","Or, deacons"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"I thank my God whenever I remember you,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"always in every request of mine on behalf of you all, making my requests with joy,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"for your partnership in furtherance of the Good News from the first day until now;"]],f:["The word translated \u201cpartnership\u201d (\u03ba\u03bf\u03b9\u03bd\u03c9\u03bd\u03af\u1fb3) also means \u201cfellowship\u201d and \u201csharing\u201d."]},{v:6,l:[[0,"being confident of this very thing, that he who began a good work in you will complete it until the day of Jesus Christ."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It is even right for me to think this way on behalf of all of you, because I have you in my heart, because both in my bonds and in the defense and confirmation of the Good News, you all are partakers with me of grace."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For God is my witness, how I long after all of you in the tender mercies of Christ Jesus."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"This I pray, that your love may abound yet more and more in knowledge and all discernment,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"so that you may approve the things that are excellent, that you may be sincere and without offense to the day of Christ,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"being filled with the fruits of righteousness which are through Jesus Christ, to the glory and praise of God."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I desire to have you know, brothers, that the things which happened to me have turned out rather to the progress of the Good News,"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:13,l:[[0,"so that it became evident to the whole palace guard, and to all the rest, that my bonds are in Christ,"]],f:["or, praetorian"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"and that most of the brothers in the Lord, being confident through my bonds, are more abundantly bold to speak the word of God without fear."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Some indeed preach Christ even out of envy and strife, and some also out of good will."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The former insincerely preach Christ from selfish ambition, thinking that they add affliction to my chains;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"but the latter out of love, knowing that I am appointed for the defense of the Good News."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"What does it matter? Only that in every way, whether in pretense or in truth, Christ is proclaimed. I rejoice in this, yes, and will rejoice."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For I know that this will turn out to my salvation through your prayers and the supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"according to my earnest expectation and hope, that I will in no way be disappointed, but with all boldness, as always, now also Christ will be magnified in my body, whether by life or by death."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For to me to live is Christ, and to die is gain."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But if I live on in the flesh, this will bring fruit from my work; yet I don\u2019t know what I will choose."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But I am hard pressed between the two, having the desire to depart and be with Christ, which is far better."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"Yet to remain in the flesh is more needful for your sake."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Having this confidence, I know that I will remain, yes, and remain with you all for your progress and joy in the faith,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"that your boasting may abound in Christ Jesus in me through my presence with you again."]],f:["or, rejoicing"]},{v:27,p:1,l:[[0,"Only let your way of life be worthy of the Good News of Christ, that whether I come and see you or am absent, I may hear of your state, that you stand firm in one spirit, with one soul striving for the faith of the Good News;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and in nothing frightened by the adversaries, which is for them a proof of destruction, but to you of salvation, and that from God."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Because it has been granted to you on behalf of Christ, not only to believe in him, but also to suffer on his behalf,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"having the same conflict which you saw in me and now hear is in me."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"If therefore there is any exhortation in Christ, if any consolation of love, if any fellowship of the Spirit, if any tender mercies and compassion,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"make my joy full by being like-minded, having the same love, being of one accord, of one mind;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"doing nothing through rivalry or through conceit, but in humility, each counting others better than himself;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"each of you not just looking to his own things, but each of you also to the things of others."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Have this in your mind, which was also in Christ Jesus,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"who, existing in the form of God, didn\u2019t consider equality with God a thing to be grasped,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"but emptied himself, taking the form of a servant, being made in the likeness of men."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"And being found in human form, he humbled himself, becoming obedient to the point of death, yes, the death of the cross."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Therefore God also highly exalted him, and gave to him the name which is above every name,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"that at the name of Jesus every knee should bow, of those in heaven, those on earth, and those under the earth,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and that every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"So then, my beloved, even as you have always obeyed, not only in my presence, but now much more in my absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For it is God who works in you both to will and to work for his good pleasure."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Do all things without complaining and arguing,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"that you may become blameless and harmless, children of God without defect in the middle of a crooked and perverse generation, among whom you are seen as lights in the world,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"holding up the word of life, that I may have something to boast in the day of Christ that I didn\u2019t run in vain nor labor in vain."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Yes, and if I am poured out on the sacrifice and service of your faith, I am glad and rejoice with you all."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In the same way, you also should be glad and rejoice with me."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"But I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you soon, that I also may be cheered up when I know how you are doing."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For I have no one else like-minded, who will truly care about you."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For they all seek their own, not the things of Jesus Christ."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But you know that he has proved himself. As a child serves a father, so he served with me in furtherance of the Good News."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Therefore I hope to send him at once, as soon as I see how it will go with me."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But I trust in the Lord that I myself also will come shortly."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"But I thought it necessary to send to you Epaphroditus, my brother, fellow worker, fellow soldier, and your apostle and servant of my need,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"since he longed for you all, and was very troubled because you had heard that he was sick."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"For indeed he was sick nearly to death, but God had mercy on him, and not on him only, but on me also, that I might not have sorrow on sorrow."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"I have sent him therefore the more diligently, that when you see him again, you may rejoice, and that I may be the less sorrowful."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"Receive him therefore in the Lord with all joy, and hold such people in honor,"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"because for the work of Christ he came near to death, risking his life to supply that which was lacking in your service toward me."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Finally, my brothers, rejoice in the Lord! To write the same things to you, to me indeed is not tiresome, but for you it is safe."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Beware of the dogs; beware of the evil workers; beware of the false circumcision."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For we are the circumcision, who worship God in the Spirit, and rejoice in Christ Jesus, and have no confidence in the flesh;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"though I myself might have confidence even in the flesh. If any other man thinks that he has confidence in the flesh, I yet more:"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"circumcised the eighth day, of the stock of Israel, of the tribe of Benjamin, a Hebrew of Hebrews; concerning the law, a Pharisee;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"concerning zeal, persecuting the assembly; concerning the righteousness which is in the law, found blameless."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"However, I consider those things that were gain to me as a loss for Christ."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Yes most certainly, and I count all things to be a loss for the excellency of the knowledge of Christ Jesus, my Lord, for whom I suffered the loss of all things, and count them nothing but refuse, that I may gain Christ"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and be found in him, not having a righteousness of my own, that which is of the law, but that which is through faith in Christ, the righteousness which is from God by faith,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"that I may know him and the power of his resurrection, and the fellowship of his sufferings, becoming conformed to his death,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"if by any means I may attain to the resurrection from the dead."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Not that I have already obtained, or am already made perfect; but I press on, that I may take hold of that for which also I was taken hold of by Christ Jesus."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, I don\u2019t regard myself as yet having taken hold, but one thing I do: forgetting the things which are behind and stretching forward to the things which are before,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I press on toward the goal for the prize of the high calling of God in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Let us therefore, as many as are perfect, think this way. If in anything you think otherwise, God will also reveal that to you."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, to the extent that we have already attained, let\u2019s walk by the same rule. Let\u2019s be of the same mind."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, be imitators together of me, and note those who walk this way, even as you have us for an example."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For many walk, of whom I told you often, and now tell you even weeping, as the enemies of the cross of Christ,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"whose end is destruction, whose god is the belly, and whose glory is in their shame, who think about earthly things."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For our citizenship is in heaven, from where we also wait for a Savior, the Lord Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"who will change the body of our humiliation to be conformed to the body of his glory, according to the working by which he is able even to subject all things to himself."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, my brothers, beloved and longed for, my joy and crown, stand firm in the Lord in this way, my beloved."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"I exhort Euodia, and I exhort Syntyche, to think the same way in the Lord."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Yes, I beg you also, true partner, help these women, for they labored with me in the Good News with Clement also, and the rest of my fellow workers, whose names are in the book of life."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Rejoice in the Lord always! Again I will say, \u201cRejoice!\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Let your gentleness be known to all men. The Lord is at hand."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In nothing be anxious, but in everything, by prayer and petition with thanksgiving, let your requests be made known to God."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"And the peace of God, which surpasses all understanding, will guard your hearts and your thoughts in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Finally, brothers, whatever things are true, whatever things are honorable, whatever things are just, whatever things are pure, whatever things are lovely, whatever things are of good report: if there is any virtue and if there is anything worthy of praise, think about these things."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Do the things which you learned, received, heard, and saw in me, and the God of peace will be with you."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But I rejoice in the Lord greatly that now at length you have revived your thought for me; in which you did indeed take thought, but you lacked opportunity."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Not that I speak because of lack, for I have learned in whatever state I am, to be content in it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I know how to be humbled, and I also know how to abound. In any and all circumstances I have learned the secret both to be filled and to be hungry, both to abound and to be in need."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I can do all things through Christ who strengthens me."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"However you did well that you shared in my affliction."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"You yourselves also know, you Philippians, that in the beginning of the Good News, when I departed from Macedonia, no assembly shared with me in the matter of giving and receiving but you only."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For even in Thessalonica you sent once and again to my need."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Not that I seek for the gift, but I seek for the fruit that increases to your account."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But I have all things and abound. I am filled, having received from Epaphroditus the things that came from you, a sweet-smelling fragrance, an acceptable and well-pleasing sacrifice to God."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"My God will supply every need of yours according to his riches in glory in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Now to our God and Father be the glory forever and ever! Amen."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Greet every saint in Christ Jesus. The brothers who are with me greet you."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"All the saints greet you, especially those who are of Caesar\u2019s household."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen."]]}]]}},1321,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,i,h,a,n){h.exports={book:"Col",name:"Colossians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus through the will of God, and Timothy our brother,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to the saints and faithful brothers in Christ at Colossae: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"We give thanks to God the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, praying always for you,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"having heard of your faith in Christ Jesus and of the love which you have toward all the saints,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"because of the hope which is laid up for you in the heavens, of which you heard before in the word of the truth of the Good News"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"which has come to you, even as it is in all the world and is bearing fruit and growing, as it does in you also, since the day you heard and knew the grace of God in truth,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"even as you learned from Epaphras our beloved fellow servant, who is a faithful servant of Christ on your behalf,"]],f:["NU reads our"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"who also declared to us your love in the Spirit."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause, we also, since the day we heard this, don\u2019t cease praying and making requests for you, that you may be filled with the knowledge of his will in all spiritual wisdom and understanding,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"that you may walk worthily of the Lord, to please him in all respects, bearing fruit in every good work and increasing in the knowledge of God,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"strengthened with all power, according to the might of his glory, for all endurance and perseverance with joy,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"giving thanks to the Father, who made us fit to be partakers of the inheritance of the saints in light,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"who delivered us out of the power of darkness, and translated us into the Kingdom of the Son of his love,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"in whom we have our redemption, the forgiveness of our sins."]],f:["TR adds \u201cthrough his blood,\u201d"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He is the image of the invisible God, the firstborn of all creation."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For by him all things were created in the heavens and on the earth, visible things and invisible things, whether thrones or dominions or principalities or powers. All things have been created through him and for him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He is before all things, and in him all things are held together."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He is the head of the body, the assembly, who is the beginning, the firstborn from the dead, that in all things he might have the preeminence."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For all the fullness was pleased to dwell in him,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"and through him to reconcile all things to himself by him, whether things on the earth or things in the heavens, having made peace through the blood of his cross."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"You, being in past times alienated and enemies in your mind in your evil deeds,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"yet now he has reconciled in the body of his flesh through death, to present you holy and without defect and blameless before him,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"if it is so that you continue in the faith, grounded and steadfast, and not moved away from the hope of the Good News which you heard, which was proclaimed in all creation under heaven, of which I, Paul, was made a servant."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I rejoice in my sufferings for your sake, and fill up on my part that which is lacking of the afflictions of Christ in my flesh for his body\u2019s sake, which is the assembly,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"of which I was made a servant according to the stewardship of God which was given me toward you to fulfill the word of God,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"the mystery which has been hidden for ages and generations. But now it has been revealed to his saints,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"to whom God was pleased to make known what are the riches of the glory of this mystery among the Gentiles, which is Christ in you, the hope of glory."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"We proclaim him, admonishing every man and teaching every man in all wisdom, that we may present every man perfect in Christ Jesus;"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"for which I also labor, striving according to his working, which works in me mightily."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For I desire to have you know how greatly I struggle for you and for those at Laodicea, and for as many as have not seen my face in the flesh;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that their hearts may be comforted, they being knit together in love, and gaining all riches of the full assurance of understanding, that they may know the mystery of God, both of the Father and of Christ,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"in whom all the treasures of wisdom and knowledge are hidden."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Now I say this that no one may delude you with persuasiveness of speech."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For though I am absent in the flesh, yet I am with you in the spirit, rejoicing and seeing your order, and the steadfastness of your faith in Christ."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"As therefore you received Christ Jesus the Lord, walk in him,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"rooted and built up in him and established in the faith, even as you were taught, abounding in it in thanksgiving."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Be careful that you don\u2019t let anyone rob you through his philosophy and vain deceit, after the tradition of men, after the elemental spirits of the world, and not after Christ."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For in him all the fullness of the Deity dwells bodily,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and in him you are made full, who is the head of all principality and power."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"In him you were also circumcised with a circumcision not made with hands, in the putting off of the body of the sins of the flesh, in the circumcision of Christ,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"having been buried with him in baptism, in which you were also raised with him through faith in the working of God, who raised him from the dead."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"You were dead through your trespasses and the uncircumcision of your flesh. He made you alive together with him, having forgiven us all our trespasses,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"wiping out the handwriting in ordinances which was against us. He has taken it out of the way, nailing it to the cross."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Having stripped the principalities and the powers, he made a show of them openly, triumphing over them in it."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Let no one therefore judge you in eating or drinking, or with respect to a feast day or a new moon or a Sabbath day,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"which are a shadow of the things to come; but the body is Christ\u2019s."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Let no one rob you of your prize by self-abasement and worshiping of the angels, dwelling in the things which he has not seen, vainly puffed up by his fleshly mind,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"and not holding firmly to the Head, from whom all the body, being supplied and knit together through the joints and ligaments, grows with God\u2019s growth."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"If you died with Christ from the elemental spirits of the world, why, as though living in the world, do you subject yourselves to ordinances,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"\u201cDon\u2019t handle, nor taste, nor touch\u201d"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"(all of which perish with use), according to the precepts and doctrines of men?"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"These things indeed appear like wisdom in self-imposed worship, humility, and severity to the body, but aren\u2019t of any value against the indulgence of the flesh."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"If then you were raised together with Christ, seek the things that are above, where Christ is, seated on the right hand of God."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Set your mind on the things that are above, not on the things that are on the earth."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For you died, and your life is hidden with Christ in God."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When Christ, our life, is revealed, then you will also be revealed with him in glory."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Put to death therefore your members which are on the earth: sexual immorality, uncleanness, depraved passion, evil desire, and covetousness, which is idolatry."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For these things\u2019 sake the wrath of God comes on the children of disobedience."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"You also once walked in those, when you lived in them,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but now you must put them all away: anger, wrath, malice, slander, and shameful speaking out of your mouth."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t lie to one another, seeing that you have put off the old man with his doings,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and have put on the new man, who is being renewed in knowledge after the image of his Creator,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"where there can\u2019t be Greek and Jew, circumcision and uncircumcision, barbarian, Scythian, bondservant, or free person; but Christ is all, and in all."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Put on therefore, as God\u2019s chosen ones, holy and beloved, a heart of compassion, kindness, lowliness, humility, and perseverance;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"bearing with one another, and forgiving each other, if any man has a complaint against any; even as Christ forgave you, so you also do."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Above all these things, walk in love, which is the bond of perfection."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"And let the peace of God rule in your hearts, to which also you were called in one body, and be thankful."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Let the word of Christ dwell in you richly; in all wisdom teaching and admonishing one another with psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs, singing with grace in your heart to the Lord."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Whatever you do, in word or in deed, do all in the name of the Lord Jesus, giving thanks to God the Father through him."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Wives, be in subjection to your husbands, as is fitting in the Lord."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Husbands, love your wives, and don\u2019t be bitter against them."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Children, obey your parents in all things, for this pleases the Lord."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Fathers, don\u2019t provoke your children, so that they won\u2019t be discouraged."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Servants, obey in all things those who are your masters according to the flesh, not just when they are looking, as men pleasers, but in singleness of heart, fearing God."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"And whatever you do, work heartily, as for the Lord and not for men,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"knowing that from the Lord you will receive the reward of the inheritance; for you serve the Lord Christ."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But he who does wrong will receive again for the wrong that he has done, and there is no partiality."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Masters, give to your servants that which is just and equal, knowing that you also have a Master in heaven."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Continue steadfastly in prayer, watching in it with thanksgiving,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"praying together for us also, that God may open to us a door for the word, to speak the mystery of Christ, for which I am also in bonds,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"that I may reveal it as I ought to speak."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Walk in wisdom toward those who are outside, redeeming the time."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Let your speech always be with grace, seasoned with salt, that you may know how you ought to answer each one."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"All my affairs will be made known to you by Tychicus, the beloved brother, faithful servant, and fellow bondservant in the Lord."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"I am sending him to you for this very purpose, that he may know your circumstances and comfort your hearts,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"together with Onesimus, the faithful and beloved brother, who is one of you. They will make known to you everything that is going on here."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Aristarchus, my fellow prisoner, greets you, and Mark the cousin of Barnabas (concerning whom you received instructions, \u201cif he comes to you, receive him\u201d),"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and Jesus who is called Justus. These are my only fellow workers for God\u2019s Kingdom who are of the circumcision, men who have been a comfort to me."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Epaphras, who is one of you, a servant of Christ, salutes you, always striving for you in his prayers, that you may stand perfect and complete in all the will of God."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For I testify about him that he has great zeal for you, and for those in Laodicea, and for those in Hierapolis."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Luke the beloved physician and Demas greet you."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Greet the brothers who are in Laodicea, with Nymphas and the assembly that is in his house."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"When this letter has been read among you, cause it to be read also in the assembly of the Laodiceans, and that you also read the letter from Laodicea."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Tell Archippus, \u201cTake heed to the ministry which you have received in the Lord, that you fulfill it.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"I, Paul, write this greeting with my own hand. Remember my chains. Grace be with you. Amen."]]}]]}},1322,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,r,n,h){r.exports={book:"1Thess",name:"1 Thessalonians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, to the assembly of the Thessalonians in God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ: Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"We always give thanks to God for all of you, mentioning you in our prayers,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"remembering without ceasing your work of faith and labor of love and perseverance of hope in our Lord Jesus Christ, before our God and Father."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"We know, brothers loved by God, that you are chosen,"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and that our Good News came to you not in word only, but also in power, and in the Holy Spirit and with much assurance. You know what kind of men we showed ourselves to be among you for your sake."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You became imitators of us and of the Lord, having received the word in much affliction, with joy of the Holy Spirit,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"so that you became an example to all who believe in Macedonia and in Achaia."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For from you the word of the Lord has been declared, not only in Macedonia and Achaia, but also in every place your faith toward God has gone out, so that we need not say anything."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For they themselves report concerning us what kind of a reception we had from you, and how you turned to God from idols to serve a living and true God,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and to wait for his Son from heaven, whom he raised from the dead: Jesus, who delivers us from the wrath to come."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For you yourselves know, brothers, our visit to you wasn\u2019t in vain,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"but having suffered before and been shamefully treated, as you know, at Philippi, we grew bold in our God to tell you the Good News of God in much conflict."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For our exhortation is not of error, nor of uncleanness, nor in deception."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But even as we have been approved by God to be entrusted with the Good News, so we speak\u2014not as pleasing men, but God, who tests our hearts."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For neither were we at any time found using words of flattery, as you know, nor a cloak of covetousness (God is witness),"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"nor seeking glory from men (neither from you nor from others), when we might have claimed authority as apostles of Christ."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But we were gentle among you, like a nursing mother cherishes her own children."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Even so, affectionately longing for you, we were well pleased to impart to you not the Good News of God only, but also our own souls, because you had become very dear to us."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For you remember, brothers, our labor and travail; for working night and day, that we might not burden any of you, we preached to you the Good News of God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"You are witnesses with God how holy, righteously, and blamelessly we behaved ourselves toward you who believe."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"As you know, we exhorted, comforted, and implored every one of you, as a father does his own children,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"to the end that you should walk worthily of God, who calls you into his own Kingdom and glory."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause we also thank God without ceasing that when you received from us the word of the message of God, you accepted it not as the word of men, but as it is in truth, God\u2019s word, which also works in you who believe."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For you, brothers, became imitators of the assemblies of God which are in Judea in Christ Jesus; for you also suffered the same things from your own countrymen, even as they did from the Jews"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"who killed both the Lord Jesus and their own prophets, and drove us out, and don\u2019t please God, and are contrary to all men,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"forbidding us to speak to the Gentiles that they may be saved, to fill up their sins always. But wrath has come on them to the uttermost."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But we, brothers, being bereaved of you for a short season in presence, not in heart, tried even harder to see your face with great desire,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"because we wanted to come to you\u2014indeed, I, Paul, once and again\u2014but Satan hindered us."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For what is our hope, or joy, or crown of rejoicing? Isn\u2019t it even you, before our Lord Jesus at his coming?"]],f:["TR adds \u201cChrist\u201d"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For you are our glory and our joy."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore when we couldn\u2019t stand it any longer, we thought it good to be left behind at Athens alone,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and sent Timothy, our brother and God\u2019s servant in the Good News of Christ, to establish you and to comfort you concerning your faith,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"that no one would be moved by these afflictions. For you know that we are appointed to this task."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For most certainly, when we were with you, we told you beforehand that we are to suffer affliction, even as it happened, and you know."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For this cause I also, when I couldn\u2019t stand it any longer, sent that I might know your faith, for fear that by any means the tempter had tempted you, and our labor would have been in vain."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But Timothy has just now come to us from you, and brought us glad news of your faith and love, and that you have good memories of us always, longing to see us, even as we also long to see you."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For this cause, brothers, we were comforted over you in all our distress and affliction through your faith."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For now we live, if you stand fast in the Lord."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For what thanksgiving can we give again to God for you, for all the joy with which we rejoice for your sakes before our God,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"night and day praying exceedingly that we may see your face and may perfect that which is lacking in your faith?"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now may our God and Father himself, and our Lord Jesus Christ, direct our way to you."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"May the Lord make you to increase and abound in love toward one another and toward all men, even as we also do toward you,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"to the end he may establish your hearts blameless in holiness before our God and Father at the coming of our Lord Jesus with all his saints."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Finally then, brothers, we beg and exhort you in the Lord Jesus, that as you received from us how you ought to walk and to please God, that you abound more and more."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For you know what instructions we gave you through the Lord Jesus."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For this is the will of God: your sanctification, that you abstain from sexual immorality,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"that each one of you know how to control his own body in sanctification and honor,"]],f:["literally, possess his own vessel"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"not in the passion of lust, even as the Gentiles who don\u2019t know God,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"that no one should take advantage of and wrong a brother or sister in this matter; because the Lord is an avenger in all these things, as also we forewarned you and testified."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For God called us not for uncleanness, but in sanctification."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore he who rejects this doesn\u2019t reject man, but God, who has also given his Holy Spirit to you."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"But concerning brotherly love, you have no need that one write to you. For you yourselves are taught by God to love one another,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for indeed you do it toward all the brothers who are in all Macedonia. But we exhort you, brothers, that you abound more and more;"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and that you make it your ambition to lead a quiet life, and to do your own business, and to work with your own hands, even as we instructed you,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that you may walk properly toward those who are outside, and may have need of nothing."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But we don\u2019t want you to be ignorant, brothers, concerning those who have fallen asleep, so that you don\u2019t grieve like the rest, who have no hope."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For if we believe that Jesus died and rose again, even so God will bring with him those who have fallen asleep in Jesus."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For this we tell you by the word of the Lord, that we who are alive, who are left until the coming of the Lord, will in no way precede those who have fallen asleep."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For the Lord himself will descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel and with God\u2019s trumpet. The dead in Christ will rise first,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"then we who are alive, who are left, will be caught up together with them in the clouds to meet the Lord in the air. So we will be with the Lord forever."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Therefore comfort one another with these words."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But concerning the times and the seasons, brothers, you have no need that anything be written to you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For you yourselves know well that the day of the Lord comes like a thief in the night."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For when they are saying, \u201cPeace and safety,\u201d then sudden destruction will come on them, like birth pains on a pregnant woman. Then they will in no way escape."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But you, brothers, aren\u2019t in darkness, that the day should overtake you like a thief."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You are all children of light and children of the day. We don\u2019t belong to the night, nor to darkness,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"so then let\u2019s not sleep, as the rest do, but let\u2019s watch and be sober."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For those who sleep, sleep in the night; and those who are drunk are drunk in the night."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But since we belong to the day, let\u2019s be sober, putting on the breastplate of faith and love, and for a helmet, the hope of salvation."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For God didn\u2019t appoint us to wrath, but to the obtaining of salvation through our Lord Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"who died for us, that, whether we wake or sleep, we should live together with him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore exhort one another, and build each other up, even as you also do."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"But we beg you, brothers, to know those who labor among you, and are over you in the Lord and admonish you,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and to respect and honor them in love for their work\u2019s sake."],[0,"Be at peace among yourselves."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"We exhort you, brothers: Admonish the disorderly; encourage the faint-hearted; support the weak; be patient toward all."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"See that no one returns evil for evil to anyone, but always follow after that which is good for one another and for all."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Always rejoice."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Pray without ceasing."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"In everything give thanks, for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus toward you."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t quench the Spirit."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t despise prophecies."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Test all things, and hold firmly that which is good."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Abstain from every form of evil."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"May the God of peace himself sanctify you completely. May your whole spirit, soul, and body be preserved blameless at the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"He who calls you is faithful, who will also do it."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, pray for us."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"Greet all the brothers with a holy kiss."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"I solemnly command you by the Lord that this letter be read to all the holy brothers."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you. Amen."]]}]]}},1323,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,h,i,r){h.exports={book:"2Thess",name:"2 Thessalonians",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, Silvanus, and Timothy, to the assembly of the Thessalonians in God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"We are bound to always give thanks to God for you, brothers, even as it is appropriate, because your faith grows exceedingly, and the love of each and every one of you toward one another abounds,"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"so that we ourselves boast about you in the assemblies of God for your perseverance and faith in all your persecutions and in the afflictions which you endure."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"This is an obvious sign of the righteous judgment of God, to the end that you may be counted worthy of God\u2019s Kingdom, for which you also suffer."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For it is a righteous thing with God to repay affliction to those who afflict you,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and to give relief to you who are afflicted with us when the Lord Jesus is revealed from heaven with his mighty angels in flaming fire,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"punishing those who don\u2019t know God, and to those who don\u2019t obey the Good News of our Lord Jesus,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"who will pay the penalty: eternal destruction from the face of the Lord and from the glory of his might,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"when he comes in that day to be glorified in his saints and to be admired among all those who have believed, because our testimony to you was believed."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"To this end we also pray always for you that our God may count you worthy of your calling, and fulfill every desire of goodness and work of faith with power,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that the name of our Lord Jesus may be glorified in you, and you in him, according to the grace of our God and the Lord Jesus Christ."]],f:["TR adds \u201cChrist\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now, brothers, concerning the coming of our Lord Jesus Christ and our gathering together to him, we ask you"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"not to be quickly shaken in your mind or troubled, either by spirit or by word or by letter as if from us, saying that the day of Christ has already come."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Let no one deceive you in any way. For it will not be unless the rebellion comes first, and the man of sin is revealed, the son of destruction."]],f:["or, falling away, or, defection"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He opposes and exalts himself against all that is called God or that is worshiped, so that he sits as God in the temple of God, setting himself up as God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t you remember that when I was still with you, I told you these things?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Now you know what is restraining him, to the end that he may be revealed in his own season."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the mystery of lawlessness already works. Only there is one who restrains now, until he is taken out of the way."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Then the lawless one will be revealed, whom the Lord will kill with the breath of his mouth and destroy by the manifestation of his coming;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"even he whose coming is according to the working of Satan with all power and signs and lying wonders,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and with all deception of wickedness for those who are being lost, because they didn\u2019t receive the love of the truth, that they might be saved."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Because of this, God sends them a powerful delusion, that they should believe a lie,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that they all might be judged who didn\u2019t believe the truth, but had pleasure in unrighteousness."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But we are bound to always give thanks to God for you, brothers loved by the Lord, because God chose you from the beginning for salvation through sanctification of the Spirit and belief in the truth,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"to which he called you through our Good News, for the obtaining of the glory of our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So then, brothers, stand firm and hold the traditions which you were taught by us, whether by word or by letter."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Now our Lord Jesus Christ himself, and God our Father, who loved us and gave us eternal comfort and good hope through grace,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"comfort your hearts and establish you in every good work and word."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Finally, brothers, pray for us, that the word of the Lord may spread rapidly and be glorified, even as also with you,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"and that we may be delivered from unreasonable and evil men; for not all have faith."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But the Lord is faithful, who will establish you and guard you from the evil one."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"We have confidence in the Lord concerning you, that you both do and will do the things we command."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"May the Lord direct your hearts into God\u2019s love and into the perseverance of Christ."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now we command you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that you withdraw yourselves from every brother who walks in rebellion and not after the tradition which they received from us."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For you know how you ought to imitate us. For we didn\u2019t behave ourselves rebelliously among you,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"neither did we eat bread from anyone\u2019s hand without paying for it, but in labor and travail worked night and day, that we might not burden any of you."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"This was not because we don\u2019t have the right, but to make ourselves an example to you, that you should imitate us."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For even when we were with you, we commanded you this: \u201cIf anyone is not willing to work, don\u2019t let him eat.\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For we hear of some who walk among you in rebellion, who don\u2019t work at all, but are busybodies."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Now those who are that way, we command and exhort in the Lord Jesus Christ, that they work with quietness and eat their own bread."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But you, brothers, don\u2019t be weary in doing what is right."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If any man doesn\u2019t obey our word in this letter, note that man and have no company with him, to the end that he may be ashamed."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t count him as an enemy, but admonish him as a brother."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"Now may the Lord of peace himself give you peace at all times in all ways. The Lord be with you all."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"I, Paul, write this greeting with my own hand, which is the sign in every letter. This is how I write."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you all. Amen."]]}]]}},1324,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,n,a,i,h){a.exports={book:"1Tim",name:"1 Timothy",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ according to the commandment of God our Savior and the Lord Jesus Christ our hope,"]],f:["NU reads Christ Jesus and omits the Lord."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to Timothy, my true child in faith: Grace, mercy, and peace from God our Father and Christ Jesus our Lord."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"As I urged you when I was going into Macedonia, stay at Ephesus that you might command certain men not to teach a different doctrine,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and not to pay attention to myths and endless genealogies, which cause disputes rather than God\u2019s stewardship, which is in faith."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But the goal of this command is love from a pure heart, a good conscience, and sincere faith,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"from which things some, having missed the mark, have turned away to vain talking,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"desiring to be teachers of the law, though they understand neither what they say nor about what they strongly affirm."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"But we know that the law is good if a person uses it lawfully,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"as knowing this, that law is not made for a righteous person, but for the lawless and insubordinate, for the ungodly and sinners, for the unholy and profane, for murderers of fathers and murderers of mothers, for manslayers,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for the sexually immoral, for homosexuals, for slave-traders, for liars, for perjurers, and for any other thing contrary to the sound doctrine,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"according to the Good News of the glory of the blessed God, which was committed to my trust."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I thank him who enabled me, Christ Jesus our Lord, because he counted me faithful, appointing me to service,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"although I used to be a blasphemer, a persecutor, and insolent. However, I obtained mercy because I did it ignorantly in unbelief."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The grace of our Lord abounded exceedingly with faith and love which is in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The saying is faithful and worthy of all acceptance, that Christ Jesus came into the world to save sinners, of whom I am chief."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"However, for this cause I obtained mercy, that in me first, Jesus Christ might display all his patience for an example of those who were going to believe in him for eternal life."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Now to the King eternal, immortal, invisible, to God who alone is wise, be honor and glory forever and ever. Amen."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"I commit this instruction to you, my child Timothy, according to the prophecies which were given to you before, that by them you may wage the good warfare,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"holding faith and a good conscience, which some having thrust away made a shipwreck concerning the faith,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"of whom are Hymenaeus and Alexander, whom I delivered to Satan that they might be taught not to blaspheme."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I exhort therefore, first of all, that petitions, prayers, intercessions, and givings of thanks be made for all men,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"for kings and all who are in high places, that we may lead a tranquil and quiet life in all godliness and reverence."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For this is good and acceptable in the sight of God our Savior,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"who desires all people to be saved and come to full knowledge of the truth."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For there is one God and one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"who gave himself as a ransom for all, the testimony at the proper time,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"to which I was appointed a preacher and an apostle\u2014I am telling the truth in Christ, not lying\u2014a teacher of the Gentiles in faith and truth."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"I desire therefore that the men in every place pray, lifting up holy hands without anger and doubting."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"In the same way, that women also adorn themselves in decent clothing, with modesty and propriety, not with braided hair, gold, pearls, or expensive clothing,"]],f:["The word for \u201cnot\u201d is the negative particle \u201c\u03bc\u03b7\u201d which denies an expected idea, as opposed to the usual word for \u201cnot\u201d (\u03bf\u03c5) which denies a fact. Thus \u201c\u03bc\u03b7\u201d in this context is denying an expected idea (that women can be properly dressed without good works)."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but with good works, which is appropriate for women professing godliness."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Let a woman learn in quietness with full submission."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But I don\u2019t permit a woman to teach, nor to exercise authority over a man, but to be in quietness."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For Adam was formed first, then Eve."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Adam wasn\u2019t deceived, but the woman, being deceived, has fallen into disobedience;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but she will be saved through her childbearing, if they continue in faith, love, and holiness with sobriety."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is a faithful saying: someone who seeks to be an overseer desires a good work."]],f:["or, superintendent, or bishop"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The overseer therefore must be without reproach, the husband of one wife, temperate, sensible, modest, hospitable, good at teaching;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"not a drinker, not violent, not greedy for money, but gentle, not quarrelsome, not covetous;"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"one who rules his own house well, having children in subjection with all reverence;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"(for how could someone who doesn\u2019t know how to rule his own house take care of God\u2019s assembly?)"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"not a new convert, lest being puffed up he fall into the same condemnation as the devil."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Moreover he must have good testimony from those who are outside, to avoid falling into reproach and the snare of the devil."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Servants, in the same way, must be reverent, not double-tongued, not addicted to much wine, not greedy for money,"]],f:["or, Deacons."]},{v:9,l:[[0,"holding the mystery of the faith in a pure conscience."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Let them also first be tested; then let them serve if they are blameless."]],f:["or, serve as deacons"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Their wives in the same way must be reverent, not slanderers, temperate, and faithful in all things."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Let servants be husbands of one wife, ruling their children and their own houses well."]],f:["or, deacons"]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For those who have served well gain for themselves a good standing and great boldness in the faith which is in Christ Jesus."]],f:["or, served well as deacons"]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"These things I write to you, hoping to come to you shortly,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but if I wait long, that you may know how men ought to behave themselves in God\u2019s house, which is the assembly of the living God, the pillar and ground of the truth."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Without controversy, the mystery of godliness is great:"],[1,"God was revealed in the flesh,"],[1,"justified in the spirit,"],[1,"seen by angels,"],[1,"preached among the nations,"],[1,"believed on in the world,"],[1,"and received up in glory."]],f:["NU replaces \u201cGod\u201d with \u201cwho\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But the Spirit says expressly that in later times some will fall away from the faith, paying attention to seducing spirits and doctrines of demons,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"through the hypocrisy of men who speak lies, branded in their own conscience as with a hot iron,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"forbidding marriage and commanding to abstain from foods which God created to be received with thanksgiving by those who believe and know the truth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For every creature of God is good, and nothing is to be rejected if it is received with thanksgiving."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For it is sanctified through the word of God and prayer."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"If you instruct the brothers of these things, you will be a good servant of Christ Jesus, nourished in the words of the faith and of the good doctrine which you have followed."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But refuse profane and old wives\u2019 fables. Exercise yourself toward godliness."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For bodily exercise has some value, but godliness has value in all things, having the promise of the life which is now and of that which is to come."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"This saying is faithful and worthy of all acceptance."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For to this end we both labor and suffer reproach, because we have set our trust in the living God, who is the Savior of all men, especially of those who believe."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Command and teach these things."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Let no man despise your youth; but be an example to those who believe, in word, in your way of life, in love, in spirit, in faith, and in purity."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Until I come, pay attention to reading, to exhortation, and to teaching."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t neglect the gift that is in you, which was given to you by prophecy with the laying on of the hands of the elders."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Be diligent in these things. Give yourself wholly to them, that your progress may be revealed to all."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Pay attention to yourself and to your teaching. Continue in these things, for in doing this you will save both yourself and those who hear you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t rebuke an older man, but exhort him as a father; the younger men as brothers;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"the elder women as mothers; the younger as sisters, in all purity."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Honor widows who are widows indeed."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But if any widow has children or grandchildren, let them learn first to show piety toward their own family and to repay their parents, for this is acceptable in the sight of God."]],f:["TR adds \u201cgood and\u201d"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now she who is a widow indeed and desolate, has her hope set on God and continues in petitions and prayers night and day."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But she who gives herself to pleasure is dead while she lives."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Also command these things, that they may be without reproach."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But if anyone doesn\u2019t provide for his own, and especially his own household, he has denied the faith and is worse than an unbeliever."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Let no one be enrolled as a widow under sixty years old, having been the wife of one man,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"being approved by good works, if she has brought up children, if she has been hospitable to strangers, if she has washed the saints\u2019 feet, if she has relieved the afflicted, and if she has diligently followed every good work."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But refuse younger widows, for when they have grown wanton against Christ, they desire to marry,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"having condemnation, because they have rejected their first pledge."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Besides, they also learn to be idle, going about from house to house. Not only idle, but also gossips and busybodies, saying things which they ought not."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"I desire therefore that the younger widows marry, bear children, rule the household, and give no occasion to the adversary for insulting."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For already some have turned away after Satan."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"If any man or woman who believes has widows, let them relieve them, and don\u2019t let the assembly be burdened, that it might relieve those who are widows indeed."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Let the elders who rule well be counted worthy of double honor, especially those who labor in the word and in teaching."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For the Scripture says, \u201cYou shall not muzzle the ox when it treads out the grain.\u201d And, \u201cThe laborer is worthy of his wages.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t receive an accusation against an elder except at the word of two or three witnesses."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Those who sin, reprove in the sight of all, that the rest also may be in fear."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I command you in the sight of God, and the Lord Jesus Christ, and the chosen angels, that you observe these things without prejudice, doing nothing by partiality."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Lay hands hastily on no one. Don\u2019t be a participant in other people\u2019s sins. Keep yourself pure."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Be no longer a drinker of water only, but use a little wine for your stomach\u2019s sake and your frequent infirmities."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Some men\u2019s sins are evident, preceding them to judgment, and some also follow later."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In the same way also there are good works that are obvious, and those that are otherwise can\u2019t be hidden."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Let as many as are bondservants under the yoke count their own masters worthy of all honor, that the name of God and the doctrine not be blasphemed."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Those who have believing masters, let them not despise them because they are brothers, but rather let them serve them, because those who partake of the benefit are believing and beloved. Teach and exhort these things."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"If anyone teaches a different doctrine and doesn\u2019t consent to sound words, the words of our Lord Jesus Christ, and to the doctrine which is according to godliness,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"he is conceited, knowing nothing, but obsessed with arguments, disputes, and word battles, from which come envy, strife, insulting, evil suspicions,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"constant friction of people of corrupt minds and destitute of the truth, who suppose that godliness is a means of gain. Withdraw yourself from such."]],f:["NU omits \u201cWithdraw yourself from such.\u201d"]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"But godliness with contentment is great gain."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For we brought nothing into the world, and we certainly can\u2019t carry anything out."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But having food and clothing, we will be content with that."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But those who are determined to be rich fall into a temptation, a snare, and many foolish and harmful lusts, such as drown men in ruin and destruction."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For the love of money is a root of all kinds of evil. Some have been led astray from the faith in their greed, and have pierced themselves through with many sorrows."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But you, man of God, flee these things, and follow after righteousness, godliness, faith, love, perseverance, and gentleness."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Fight the good fight of faith. Take hold of the eternal life to which you were called, and you confessed the good confession in the sight of many witnesses."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I command you before God who gives life to all things, and before Christ Jesus who before Pontius Pilate testified the good confession,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"that you keep the commandment without spot, blameless until the appearing of our Lord Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"which at the right time he will show, who is the blessed and only Ruler, the King of kings and Lord of lords."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He alone has immortality, dwelling in unapproachable light, whom no man has seen nor can see, to whom be honor and eternal power. Amen."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Charge those who are rich in this present age that they not be arrogant, nor have their hope set on the uncertainty of riches, but on the living God, who richly provides us with everything to enjoy;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"that they do good, that they be rich in good works, that they be ready to distribute, willing to share;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"laying up in store for themselves a good foundation against the time to come, that they may lay hold of eternal life."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Timothy, guard that which is committed to you, turning away from the empty chatter and oppositions of what is falsely called knowledge,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"which some profess, and thus have wandered from the faith."],[0,"Grace be with you. Amen."]]}]]}},1325,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,h,a,s,r){a.exports={book:"2Tim",name:"2 Timothy",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, an apostle of Jesus Christ through the will of God, according to the promise of the life which is in Christ Jesus,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to Timothy, my beloved child: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and Christ Jesus our Lord."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"I thank God, whom I serve as my forefathers did, with a pure conscience. How unceasing is my memory of you in my petitions, night and day"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"longing to see you, remembering your tears, that I may be filled with joy;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"having been reminded of the sincere faith that is in you, which lived first in your grandmother Lois and your mother Eunice and, I am persuaded, in you also."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"For this cause, I remind you that you should stir up the gift of God which is in you through the laying on of my hands."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For God didn\u2019t give us a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and self-control."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t be ashamed of the testimony of our Lord, nor of me his prisoner; but endure hardship for the Good News according to the power of God,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"who saved us and called us with a holy calling, not according to our works, but according to his own purpose and grace, which was given to us in Christ Jesus before times eternal,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but has now been revealed by the appearing of our Savior, Christ Jesus, who abolished death, and brought life and immortality to light through the Good News."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For this I was appointed as a preacher, an apostle, and a teacher of the Gentiles."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For this cause I also suffer these things."],[0,"Yet I am not ashamed, for I know him whom I have believed, and I am persuaded that he is able to guard that which I have committed to him against that day."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Hold the pattern of sound words which you have heard from me, in faith and love which is in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"That good thing which was committed to you, guard through the Holy Spirit who dwells in us."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"This you know, that all who are in Asia turned away from me, of whom are Phygelus and Hermogenes."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"May the Lord grant mercy to the house of Onesiphorus, for he often refreshed me, and was not ashamed of my chain,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"but when he was in Rome, he sought me diligently and found me"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"(the Lord grant to him to find the Lord\u2019s mercy in that day); and in how many things he served at Ephesus, you know very well."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"You therefore, my child, be strengthened in the grace that is in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The things which you have heard from me among many witnesses, commit the same things to faithful men who will be able to teach others also."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You therefore must endure hardship as a good soldier of Christ Jesus."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"No soldier on duty entangles himself in the affairs of life, that he may please him who enrolled him as a soldier."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Also, if anyone competes in athletics, he isn\u2019t crowned unless he has competed by the rules."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The farmer who labors must be the first to get a share of the crops."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Consider what I say, and may the Lord give you understanding in all things."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Remember Jesus Christ, risen from the dead, of the offspring of David, according to my Good News,"]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:9,l:[[0,"in which I suffer hardship to the point of chains as a criminal. But God\u2019s word isn\u2019t chained."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore I endure all things for the chosen ones\u2019 sake, that they also may obtain the salvation which is in Christ Jesus with eternal glory."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"This saying is trustworthy:"],[1,"\u201cFor if we died with him,"],[2,"we will also live with him."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"If we endure,"],[2,"we will also reign with him."],[1,"If we deny him,"],[2,"he also will deny us."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[1,"If we are faithless,"],[2,"he remains faithful;"],[2,"for he can\u2019t deny himself.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Remind them of these things, charging them in the sight of the Lord that they don\u2019t argue about words to no profit, to the subverting of those who hear."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Give diligence to present yourself approved by God, a workman who doesn\u2019t need to be ashamed, properly handling the Word of Truth."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But shun empty chatter, for it will go further in ungodliness,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and those words will consume like gangrene, of whom is Hymenaeus and Philetus:"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"men who have erred concerning the truth, saying that the resurrection is already past, and overthrowing the faith of some."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"However, God\u2019s firm foundation stands, having this seal: \u201cThe Lord knows those who are his,\u201d and, \u201cLet every one who names the name of the Lord depart from unrighteousness.\u201d"]],f:["TR reads \u201cChrist\u201d instead of \u201cthe Lord\u201d"]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in a large house there are not only vessels of gold and of silver, but also of wood and of clay. Some are for honor and some for dishonor."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"If anyone therefore purges himself from these, he will be a vessel for honor, sanctified, and suitable for the master\u2019s use, prepared for every good work."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Flee from youthful lusts; but pursue righteousness, faith, love, and peace with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"But refuse foolish and ignorant questionings, knowing that they generate strife."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The Lord\u2019s servant must not quarrel, but be gentle toward all, able to teach, patient,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"in gentleness correcting those who oppose him. Perhaps God may give them repentance leading to a full knowledge of the truth,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and they may recover themselves out of the devil\u2019s snare, having been taken captive by him to do his will."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But know this: that in the last days, grievous times will come."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For men will be lovers of self, lovers of money, boastful, arrogant, blasphemers, disobedient to parents, unthankful, unholy,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"without natural affection, unforgiving, slanderers, without self-control, fierce, not lovers of good,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"traitors, headstrong, conceited, lovers of pleasure rather than lovers of God,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"holding a form of godliness but having denied its power. Turn away from these, also."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For some of these are people who creep into houses and take captive gullible women loaded down with sins, led away by various lusts,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"always learning and never able to come to the knowledge of the truth."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Even as Jannes and Jambres opposed Moses, so these also oppose the truth, men corrupted in mind, who concerning the faith are rejected."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But they will proceed no further. For their folly will be evident to all men, as theirs also came to be."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"But you followed my teaching, conduct, purpose, faith, patience, love, steadfastness,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"persecutions, and sufferings\u2014those things that happened to me at Antioch, Iconium, and Lystra. I endured those persecutions. The Lord delivered me out of them all."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Yes, and all who desire to live godly in Christ Jesus will suffer persecution."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But evil men and impostors will grow worse and worse, deceiving and being deceived."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But you remain in the things which you have learned and have been assured of, knowing from whom you have learned them."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"From infancy, you have known the holy Scriptures which are able to make you wise for salvation through faith which is in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Every Scripture is God-breathed and profitable for teaching, for reproof, for correction, and for instruction in righteousness,"]],f:["or, Every writing inspired by God is"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"that each person who belongs to God may be complete, thoroughly equipped for every good work."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I command you therefore before God and the Lord Jesus Christ, who will judge the living and the dead at his appearing and his Kingdom:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"preach the word; be urgent in season and out of season; reprove, rebuke, and exhort with all patience and teaching."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For the time will come when they will not listen to the sound doctrine, but having itching ears, will heap up for themselves teachers after their own lusts,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and will turn away their ears from the truth, and turn away to fables."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But you be sober in all things, suffer hardship, do the work of an evangelist, and fulfill your ministry."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"For I am already being offered, and the time of my departure has come."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"I have fought the good fight. I have finished the course. I have kept the faith."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"From now on, the crown of righteousness is stored up for me, which the Lord, the righteous judge, will give to me on that day; and not to me only, but also to all those who have loved his appearing."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Be diligent to come to me soon,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for Demas left me, having loved this present world, and went to Thessalonica; Crescens to Galatia; and Titus to Dalmatia."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Only Luke is with me. Take Mark and bring him with you, for he is useful to me for service."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But I sent Tychicus to Ephesus."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Bring the cloak that I left at Troas with Carpus when you come\u2014and the books, especially the parchments."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Alexander the coppersmith did much evil to me. The Lord will repay him according to his deeds."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Beware of him, for he greatly opposed our words."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"At my first defense, no one came to help me, but all left me. May it not be held against them."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But the Lord stood by me and strengthened me, that through me the message might be fully proclaimed, and that all the Gentiles might hear. So I was delivered out of the mouth of the lion."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"And the Lord will deliver me from every evil work and will preserve me for his heavenly Kingdom. To him be the glory forever and ever. Amen."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Greet Prisca and Aquila, and the house of Onesiphorus."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Erastus remained at Corinth, but I left Trophimus at Miletus sick."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Be diligent to come before winter. Eubulus salutes you, as do Pudens, Linus, Claudia, and all the brothers."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"The Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Grace be with you. Amen."]]}]]}},1326,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,n,i,a,s){i.exports={book:"Titus",name:"Titus",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, a servant of God and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God\u2019s chosen ones and the knowledge of the truth which is according to godliness,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"in hope of eternal life, which God, who can\u2019t lie, promised before time began;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"but in his own time revealed his word in the message with which I was entrusted according to the commandment of God our Savior,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"to Titus, my true child according to a common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ our Savior."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"I left you in Crete for this reason, that you would set in order the things that were lacking and appoint elders in every city, as I directed you\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"if anyone is blameless, the husband of one wife, having children who believe, who are not accused of loose or unruly behavior."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the overseer must be blameless, as God\u2019s steward, not self-pleasing, not easily angered, not given to wine, not violent, not greedy for dishonest gain;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but given to hospitality, a lover of good, sober minded, fair, holy, self-controlled,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"holding to the faithful word which is according to the teaching, that he may be able to exhort in the sound doctrine, and to convict those who contradict him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"For there are also many unruly men, vain talkers and deceivers, especially those of the circumcision,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"whose mouths must be stopped: men who overthrow whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for dishonest gain\u2019s sake."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"One of them, a prophet of their own, said, \u201cCretans are always liars, evil beasts, and idle gluttons.\u201d"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"This testimony is true. For this cause, reprove them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"not paying attention to Jewish fables and commandments of men who turn away from the truth."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"To the pure, all things are pure, but to those who are defiled and unbelieving, nothing is pure; but both their mind and their conscience are defiled."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They profess that they know God, but by their deeds they deny him, being abominable, disobedient, and unfit for any good work."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But say the things which fit sound doctrine,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that older men should be temperate, sensible, sober minded, sound in faith, in love, and in perseverance,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and that older women likewise be reverent in behavior, not slanderers nor enslaved to much wine, teachers of that which is good,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"that they may train the young wives to love their husbands, to love their children,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"to be sober minded, chaste, workers at home, kind, being in subjection to their own husbands, that God\u2019s word may not be blasphemed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Likewise, exhort the younger men to be sober minded."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"In all things show yourself an example of good works. In your teaching, show integrity, seriousness, incorruptibility,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and soundness of speech that can\u2019t be condemned, that he who opposes you may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say about us."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Exhort servants to be in subjection to their own masters and to be well-pleasing in all things, not contradicting,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"not stealing, but showing all good fidelity, that they may adorn the doctrine of God, our Savior, in all things."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the grace of God has appeared, bringing salvation to all men,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"instructing us to the intent that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we would live soberly, righteously, and godly in this present age;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"looking for the blessed hope and appearing of the glory of our great God and Savior, Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity and purify for himself a people for his own possession, zealous for good works."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Say these things and exhort and reprove with all authority. Let no one despise you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Remind them to be in subjection to rulers and to authorities, to be obedient, to be ready for every good work,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to speak evil of no one, not to be contentious, to be gentle, showing all humility toward all men."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For we were also once foolish, disobedient, deceived, serving various lusts and pleasures, living in malice and envy, hateful, and hating one another."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But when the kindness of God our Savior and his love toward mankind appeared,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"not by works of righteousness which we did ourselves, but according to his mercy, he saved us through the washing of regeneration and renewing by the Holy Spirit,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"whom he poured out on us richly through Jesus Christ our Savior;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"that being justified by his grace, we might be made heirs according to the hope of eternal life."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"This saying is faithful, and concerning these things I desire that you insist confidently, so that those who have believed God may be careful to maintain good works. These things are good and profitable to men;"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"but shun foolish questionings, genealogies, strife, and disputes about the law; for they are unprofitable and vain."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Avoid a factious man after a first and second warning,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"knowing that such a one is perverted and sinful, being self-condemned."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"When I send Artemas to you, or Tychicus, be diligent to come to me to Nicopolis, for I have determined to winter there."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Send Zenas the lawyer and Apollos on their journey speedily, that nothing may be lacking for them."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Let our people also learn to maintain good works to meet necessary needs, that they may not be unfruitful."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"All who are with me greet you. Greet those who love us in faith."],[0,"Grace be with you all. Amen."]]}]]}},1327,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,r,h,a,s){h.exports={book:"Phlm",name:"Philemon",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Paul, a prisoner of Christ Jesus, and Timothy our brother, to Philemon, our beloved fellow worker,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to the beloved Apphia, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the assembly in your house:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I thank my God always, making mention of you in my prayers,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"hearing of your love and of the faith which you have toward the Lord Jesus and toward all the saints,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"that the fellowship of your faith may become effective in the knowledge of every good thing which is in us in Christ Jesus."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For we have much joy and comfort in your love, because the hearts of the saints have been refreshed through you, brother."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore though I have all boldness in Christ to command you that which is appropriate,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"yet for love\u2019s sake I rather appeal to you, being such a one as Paul, the aged, but also a prisoner of Jesus Christ."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I appeal to you for my child Onesimus, whom I have become the father of in my chains,"]],f:["Onesimus means \u201cuseful\u201d."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"who once was useless to you, but now is useful to you and to me."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I am sending him back. Therefore receive him, that is, my own heart,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"whom I desired to keep with me, that on your behalf he might serve me in my chains for the Good News."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But I was willing to do nothing without your consent, that your goodness would not be as of necessity, but of free will."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For perhaps he was therefore separated from you for a while that you would have him forever,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"no longer as a slave, but more than a slave, a beloved brother\u2014especially to me, but how much rather to you, both in the flesh and in the Lord."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"If then you count me a partner, receive him as you would receive me."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But if he has wronged you at all or owes you anything, put that to my account."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I, Paul, write this with my own hand: I will repay it (not to mention to you that you owe to me even your own self besides)."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Yes, brother, let me have joy from you in the Lord. Refresh my heart in the Lord."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Having confidence in your obedience, I write to you, knowing that you will do even beyond what I say."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Also, prepare a guest room for me, for I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ Jesus, greets you,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"as do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with your spirit. Amen."]]}]]}},1328,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,i,s){a.exports={book:"Heb",name:"Hebrews",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"God, having in the past spoken to the fathers through the prophets at many times and in various ways,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"has at the end of these days spoken to us by his Son, whom he appointed heir of all things, through whom also he made the worlds."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"His Son is the radiance of his glory, the very image of his substance, and upholding all things by the word of his power, who, when he had by himself purified us of our sins, sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"having become as much better than the angels as the more excellent name he has inherited is better than theirs."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For to which of the angels did he say at any time,"],[1,"\u201cYou are my Son."],[2,"Today I have become your father?\u201d"],[0,"and again,"],[1,"\u201cI will be to him a Father,"],[2,"and he will be to me a Son?\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"When he again brings in the firstborn into the world he says, \u201cLet all the angels of God worship him.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Of the angels he says,"],[1,"\u201cHe makes his angels winds,"],[2,"and his servants a flame of fire.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"But of the Son he says,"],[1,"\u201cYour throne, O God, is forever and ever."],[2,"The scepter of uprightness is the scepter of your Kingdom."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"You have loved righteousness and hated iniquity;"],[2,"therefore God, your God, has anointed you with the oil of gladness above your fellows.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"And,"],[1,"\u201cYou, Lord, in the beginning, laid the foundation of the earth."],[2,"The heavens are the works of your hands."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They will perish, but you continue."],[2,"They all will grow old like a garment does."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"You will roll them up like a mantle,"],[2,"and they will be changed;"],[2,"but you are the same."],[2,"Your years won\u2019t fail.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"But which of the angels has he told at any time,"],[1,"\u201cSit at my right hand,"],[2,"until I make your enemies the footstool of your feet?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Aren\u2019t they all serving spirits, sent out to do service for the sake of those who will inherit salvation?"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore we ought to pay greater attention to the things that were heard, lest perhaps we drift away."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For if the word spoken through angels proved steadfast, and every transgression and disobedience received a just penalty,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"how will we escape if we neglect so great a salvation\u2014which at the first having been spoken through the Lord, was confirmed to us by those who heard,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"God also testifying with them, both by signs and wonders, by various works of power, and by gifts of the Holy Spirit, according to his own will?"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"For he didn\u2019t subject the world to come, of which we speak, to angels."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But one has somewhere testified, saying,"],[1,"\u201cWhat is man, that you think of him?"],[2,"Or the son of man, that you care for him?"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"You made him a little lower than the angels."],[2,"You crowned him with glory and honor."]],f:["TR adds \u201cand set him over the works of your hands\u201d"]},{v:8,l:[[2,"You have put all things in subjection under his feet.\u201d"],[0,"For in that he subjected all things to him, he left nothing that is not subject to him. But now we don\u2019t yet see all things subjected to him."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But we see him who has been made a little lower than the angels, Jesus, because of the suffering of death crowned with glory and honor, that by the grace of God he should taste of death for everyone."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"For it became him, for whom are all things and through whom are all things, in bringing many children to glory, to make the author of their salvation perfect through sufferings."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For both he who sanctifies and those who are sanctified are all from one, for which cause he is not ashamed to call them brothers,"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:12,l:[[0,"saying,"],[1,"\u201cI will declare your name to my brothers."],[2,"Among the congregation I will sing your praise.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Again, \u201cI will put my trust in him.\u201d Again, \u201cBehold, here I am with the children whom God has given me.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Since then the children have shared in flesh and blood, he also himself in the same way partook of the same, that through death he might bring to nothing him who had the power of death, that is, the devil,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and might deliver all of them who through fear of death were all their lifetime subject to bondage."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For most certainly, he doesn\u2019t give help to angels, but he gives help to the offspring of Abraham."]],f:["or, seed"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Therefore he was obligated in all things to be made like his brothers, that he might become a merciful and faithful high priest in things pertaining to God, to make atonement for the sins of the people."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For in that he himself has suffered being tempted, he is able to help those who are tempted."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, holy brothers, partakers of a heavenly calling, consider the Apostle and High Priest of our confession: Jesus,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"who was faithful to him who appointed him, as also Moses was in all his house."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For he has been counted worthy of more glory than Moses, because he who built the house has more honor than the house."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For every house is built by someone; but he who built all things is God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Moses indeed was faithful in all his house as a servant, for a testimony of those things which were afterward to be spoken,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but Christ is faithful as a Son over his house. We are his house, if we hold fast our confidence and the glorying of our hope firm to the end."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Therefore, even as the Holy Spirit says,"],[1,"\u201cToday if you will hear his voice,"]]},{v:8,l:[[2,"don\u2019t harden your hearts as in the rebellion,"],[2,"in the day of the trial in the wilderness,"]]},{v:9,l:[[2,"where your fathers tested me and tried me,"],[2,"and saw my deeds for forty years."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"Therefore I was displeased with that generation,"],[2,"and said, \u2018They always err in their heart,"],[2,"but they didn\u2019t know my ways.\u2019"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"As I swore in my wrath,"],[2,"\u2018They will not enter into my rest.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Beware, brothers, lest perhaps there might be in any one of you an evil heart of unbelief, in falling away from the living God;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"but exhort one another day by day, so long as it is called \u201ctoday\u201d, lest any one of you be hardened by the deceitfulness of sin."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For we have become partakers of Christ, if we hold the beginning of our confidence firm to the end,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"while it is said,"],[1,"\u201cToday if you will hear his voice,"],[2,"don\u2019t harden your hearts, as in the rebellion.\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"For who, when they heard, rebelled? Wasn\u2019t it all those who came out of Egypt led by Moses?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"With whom was he displeased forty years? Wasn\u2019t it with those who sinned, whose bodies fell in the wilderness?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"To whom did he swear that they wouldn\u2019t enter into his rest, but to those who were disobedient?"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"We see that they weren\u2019t able to enter in because of unbelief."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s fear therefore, lest perhaps anyone of you should seem to have come short of a promise of entering into his rest."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For indeed we have had good news preached to us, even as they also did, but the word they heard didn\u2019t profit them, because it wasn\u2019t mixed with faith by those who heard."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For we who have believed do enter into that rest, even as he has said, \u201cAs I swore in my wrath, they will not enter into my rest;\u201d although the works were finished from the foundation of the world."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For he has said this somewhere about the seventh day, \u201cGod rested on the seventh day from all his works;\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and in this place again, \u201cThey will not enter into my rest.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Seeing therefore it remains that some should enter into it, and they to whom the good news was preached before failed to enter in because of disobedience,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"he again defines a certain day, \u201ctoday\u201d, saying through David so long a time afterward (just as has been said),"],[1,"\u201cToday if you will hear his voice,"],[2,"don\u2019t harden your hearts.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"For if Joshua had given them rest, he would not have spoken afterward of another day."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"There remains therefore a Sabbath rest for the people of God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For he who has entered into his rest has himself also rested from his works, as God did from his."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s therefore give diligence to enter into that rest, lest anyone fall after the same example of disobedience."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For the word of God is living and active, and sharper than any two-edged sword, piercing even to the dividing of soul and spirit, of both joints and marrow, and is able to discern the thoughts and intentions of the heart."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"There is no creature that is hidden from his sight, but all things are naked and laid open before the eyes of him to whom we must give an account."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Having then a great high priest who has passed through the heavens, Jesus, the Son of God, let\u2019s hold tightly to our confession."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For we don\u2019t have a high priest who can\u2019t be touched with the feeling of our infirmities, but one who has been in all points tempted like we are, yet without sin."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s therefore draw near with boldness to the throne of grace, that we may receive mercy and may find grace for help in time of need."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For every high priest, being taken from among men, is appointed for men in things pertaining to God, that he may offer both gifts and sacrifices for sins."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The high priest can deal gently with those who are ignorant and going astray, because he himself is also surrounded with weakness."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Because of this, he must offer sacrifices for sins for the people, as well as for himself."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Nobody takes this honor on himself, but he is called by God, just like Aaron was."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So also Christ didn\u2019t glorify himself to be made a high priest, but it was he who said to him,"],[1,"\u201cYou are my Son."],[2,"Today I have become your father.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"As he says also in another place,"],[1,"\u201cYou are a priest forever,"],[2,"after the order of Melchizedek.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"He, in the days of his flesh, having offered up prayers and petitions with strong crying and tears to him who was able to save him from death, and having been heard for his godly fear,"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"though he was a Son, yet learned obedience by the things which he suffered."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Having been made perfect, he became to all of those who obey him the author of eternal salvation,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"named by God a high priest after the order of Melchizedek."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"About him we have many words to say, and hard to interpret, seeing you have become dull of hearing."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For although by this time you should be teachers, you again need to have someone teach you the rudiments of the first principles of the revelations of God. You have come to need milk, and not solid food."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For everyone who lives on milk is not experienced in the word of righteousness, for he is a baby."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But solid food is for those who are full grown, who by reason of use have their senses exercised to discern good and evil."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore leaving the teaching of the first principles of Christ, let\u2019s press on to perfection\u2014not laying again a foundation of repentance from dead works, of faith toward God,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"of the teaching of baptisms, of laying on of hands, of resurrection of the dead, and of eternal judgment."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This will we do, if God permits."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For concerning those who were once enlightened and tasted of the heavenly gift, and were made partakers of the Holy Spirit,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and tasted the good word of God and the powers of the age to come,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and then fell away, it is impossible to renew them again to repentance; seeing they crucify the Son of God for themselves again, and put him to open shame."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For the land which has drunk the rain that comes often on it and produces a crop suitable for them for whose sake it is also tilled, receives blessing from God;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but if it bears thorns and thistles, it is rejected and near being cursed, whose end is to be burned."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"But, beloved, we are persuaded of better things for you, and things that accompany salvation, even though we speak like this."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For God is not unrighteous, so as to forget your work and the labor of love which you showed toward his name, in that you served the saints, and still do serve them."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"We desire that each one of you may show the same diligence to the fullness of hope even to the end,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"that you won\u2019t be sluggish, but imitators of those who through faith and perseverance inherited the promises."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"For when God made a promise to Abraham, since he could swear by no one greater, he swore by himself,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cSurely blessing I will bless you, and multiplying I will multiply you.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Thus, having patiently endured, he obtained the promise."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For men indeed swear by a greater one, and in every dispute of theirs the oath is final for confirmation."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"In this way God, being determined to show more abundantly to the heirs of the promise the immutability of his counsel, interposed with an oath,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"that by two immutable things, in which it is impossible for God to lie, we may have a strong encouragement, who have fled for refuge to take hold of the hope set before us."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"This hope we have as an anchor of the soul, a hope both sure and steadfast and entering into that which is within the veil,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"where as a forerunner Jesus entered for us, having become a high priest forever after the order of Melchizedek."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For this Melchizedek, king of Salem, priest of God Most High, who met Abraham returning from the slaughter of the kings and blessed him,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"to whom also Abraham divided a tenth part of all (being first, by interpretation, \u201cking of righteousness\u201d, and then also \u201cking of Salem\u201d, which means \u201cking of peace\u201d,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"without father, without mother, without genealogy, having neither beginning of days nor end of life, but made like the Son of God), remains a priest continually."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Now consider how great this man was, to whom even Abraham the patriarch gave a tenth out of the best plunder."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They indeed of the sons of Levi who receive the priest\u2019s office have a commandment to take tithes from the people according to the law, that is, of their brothers, though these have come out of the body of Abraham,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"but he whose genealogy is not counted from them has accepted tithes from Abraham, and has blessed him who has the promises."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But without any dispute the lesser is blessed by the greater."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Here people who die receive tithes, but there one receives tithes of whom it is testified that he lives."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"We can say that through Abraham even Levi, who receives tithes, has paid tithes,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"for he was yet in the body of his father when Melchizedek met him."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Now if perfection was through the Levitical priesthood (for under it the people have received the law), what further need was there for another priest to arise after the order of Melchizedek, and not be called after the order of Aaron?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"For the priesthood being changed, there is of necessity a change made also in the law."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For he of whom these things are said belongs to another tribe, from which no one has officiated at the altar."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For it is evident that our Lord has sprung out of Judah, about which tribe Moses spoke nothing concerning priesthood."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"This is yet more abundantly evident, if after the likeness of Melchizedek there arises another priest,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"who has been made, not after the law of a fleshly commandment, but after the power of an endless life;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"for it is testified,"],[1,"\u201cYou are a priest forever,"],[2,"according to the order of Melchizedek.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"For there is an annulling of a foregoing commandment because of its weakness and uselessness"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"(for the law made nothing perfect), and a bringing in of a better hope, through which we draw near to God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Inasmuch as he was not made priest without the taking of an oath"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"(for they indeed have been made priests without an oath), but he with an oath by him that says of him,"],[1,"\u201cThe Lord swore and will not change his mind,"],[2,"\u2018You are a priest forever,"],[2,"according to the order of Melchizedek.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"By so much, Jesus has become the guarantee of a better covenant."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"Many, indeed, have been made priests, because they are hindered from continuing by death."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But he, because he lives forever, has his priesthood unchangeable."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Therefore he is also able to save to the uttermost those who draw near to God through him, seeing that he lives forever to make intercession for them."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"For such a high priest was fitting for us: holy, guiltless, undefiled, separated from sinners, and made higher than the heavens;"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"who doesn\u2019t need, like those high priests, to offer up sacrifices daily, first for his own sins, and then for the sins of the people. For he did this once for all, when he offered up himself."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"For the law appoints men as high priests who have weakness, but the word of the oath, which came after the law, appoints a Son forever who has been perfected."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now in the things which we are saying, the main point is this: we have such a high priest, who sat down on the right hand of the throne of the Majesty in the heavens,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"a servant of the sanctuary and of the true tabernacle which the Lord pitched, not man."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For every high priest is appointed to offer both gifts and sacrifices. Therefore it is necessary that this high priest also have something to offer."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For if he were on earth, he would not be a priest at all, seeing there are priests who offer the gifts according to the law,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"who serve a copy and shadow of the heavenly things, even as Moses was warned by God when he was about to make the tabernacle, for he said, \u201cSee, you shall make everything according to the pattern that was shown to you on the mountain.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But now he has obtained a more excellent ministry, by as much as he is also the mediator of a better covenant, which on better promises has been given as law."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"For if that first covenant had been faultless, then no place would have been sought for a second."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For finding fault with them, he said,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, the days are coming\u201d, says the Lord,"],[2,"\u201cthat I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah;"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[1,"not according to the covenant that I made with their fathers"],[2,"in the day that I took them by the hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt;"],[1,"for they didn\u2019t continue in my covenant,"],[2,"and I disregarded them,\u201d says the Lord."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cFor this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel"],[2,"after those days,\u201d says the Lord:"],[1,"\u201cI will put my laws into their mind;"],[2,"I will also write them on their heart."],[1,"I will be their God,"],[2,"and they will be my people."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"They will not teach every man his fellow citizen"],[2,"and every man his brother, saying, \u2018Know the Lord,\u2019"],[2,"for all will know me,"],[2,"from their least to their greatest."]],f:["TR reads \u201cneighbor\u201d instead of \u201cfellow citizen\u201d"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For I will be merciful to their unrighteousness."],[2,"I will remember their sins and lawless deeds no more.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"In that he says, \u201cA new covenant\u201d, he has made the first obsolete. But that which is becoming obsolete and grows aged is near to vanishing away."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now indeed even the first covenant had ordinances of divine service and an earthly sanctuary."]],f:["TR adds \u201ctabernacle\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For a tabernacle was prepared. In the first part were the lamp stand, the table, and the show bread, which is called the Holy Place."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"After the second veil was the tabernacle which is called the Holy of Holies,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"having a golden altar of incense and the ark of the covenant overlaid on all sides with gold, in which was a golden pot holding the manna, Aaron\u2019s rod that budded, and the tablets of the covenant;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and above it cherubim of glory overshadowing the mercy seat, of which things we can\u2019t speak now in detail."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"Now these things having been thus prepared, the priests go in continually into the first tabernacle, accomplishing the services,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"but into the second the high priest alone, once in the year, not without blood, which he offers for himself and for the errors of the people."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The Holy Spirit is indicating this, that the way into the Holy Place wasn\u2019t yet revealed while the first tabernacle was still standing."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"This is a symbol of the present age, where gifts and sacrifices are offered that are incapable, concerning the conscience, of making the worshiper perfect,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"being only (with foods and drinks and various washings) fleshly ordinances, imposed until a time of reformation."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"But Christ having come as a high priest of the coming good things, through the greater and more perfect tabernacle, not made with hands, that is to say, not of this creation,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"nor yet through the blood of goats and calves, but through his own blood, entered in once for all into the Holy Place, having obtained eternal redemption."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For if the blood of goats and bulls, and the ashes of a heifer sprinkling those who have been defiled, sanctify to the cleanness of the flesh,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"how much more will the blood of Christ, who through the eternal Spirit offered himself without defect to God, cleanse your conscience from dead works to serve the living God?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For this reason he is the mediator of a new covenant, since a death has occurred for the redemption of the transgressions that were under the first covenant, that those who have been called may receive the promise of the eternal inheritance."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For where a last will and testament is, there must of necessity be the death of him who made it."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For a will is in force where there has been death, for it is never in force while he who made it lives."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Therefore even the first covenant has not been dedicated without blood."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For when every commandment had been spoken by Moses to all the people according to the law, he took the blood of the calves and the goats, with water and scarlet wool and hyssop, and sprinkled both the book itself and all the people,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cThis is the blood of the covenant which God has commanded you.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"He sprinkled the tabernacle and all the vessels of the ministry in the same way with the blood."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"According to the law, nearly everything is cleansed with blood, and apart from shedding of blood there is no remission."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"It was necessary therefore that the copies of the things in the heavens should be cleansed with these, but the heavenly things themselves with better sacrifices than these."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For Christ hasn\u2019t entered into holy places made with hands, which are representations of the true, but into heaven itself, now to appear in the presence of God for us;"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"nor yet that he should offer himself often, as the high priest enters into the holy place year by year with blood not his own,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"or else he must have suffered often since the foundation of the world. But now once at the end of the ages, he has been revealed to put away sin by the sacrifice of himself."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Inasmuch as it is appointed for men to die once, and after this, judgment,"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"so Christ also, having been offered once to bear the sins of many, will appear a second time, not to deal with sin, but to save those who are eagerly waiting for him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"For the law, having a shadow of the good to come, not the very image of the things, can never with the same sacrifices year by year, which they offer continually, make perfect those who draw near."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Or else wouldn\u2019t they have ceased to be offered, because the worshipers, having been once cleansed, would have had no more consciousness of sins?"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"But in those sacrifices there is a yearly reminder of sins."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For it is impossible that the blood of bulls and goats should take away sins."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Therefore when he comes into the world, he says,"],[1,"\u201cYou didn\u2019t desire sacrifice and offering,"],[2,"but you prepared a body for me."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"You had no pleasure in whole burnt offerings and sacrifices for sin."]]},{v:7,l:[[2,"Then I said, \u2018Behold, I have come (in the scroll of the book it is written of me)"],[2,"to do your will, O God.\u2019\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Previously saying, \u201cSacrifices and offerings and whole burnt offerings and sacrifices for sin you didn\u2019t desire, neither had pleasure in them\u201d (those which are offered according to the law),"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"then he has said, \u201cBehold, I have come to do your will.\u201d He takes away the first, that he may establish the second,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"by which will we have been sanctified through the offering of the body of Jesus Christ once for all."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Every priest indeed stands day by day serving and offering often the same sacrifices, which can never take away sins,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"but he, when he had offered one sacrifice for sins forever, sat down on the right hand of God,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"from that time waiting until his enemies are made the footstool of his feet."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For by one offering he has perfected forever those who are being sanctified."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The Holy Spirit also testifies to us, for after saying,"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cThis is the covenant that I will make with them"],[2,"after those days,\u201d says the Lord,"],[1,"\u201cI will put my laws on their heart,"],[2,"I will also write them on their mind;\u201d"],[0,"then he says,"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cI will remember their sins and their iniquities no more.\u201d"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Now where remission of these is, there is no more offering for sin."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Having therefore, brothers, boldness to enter into the holy place by the blood of Jesus,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"by the way which he dedicated for us, a new and living way, through the veil, that is to say, his flesh,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"and having a great priest over God\u2019s house,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"let\u2019s draw near with a true heart in fullness of faith, having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience and having our body washed with pure water,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"let\u2019s hold fast the confession of our hope without wavering; for he who promised is faithful."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s consider how to provoke one another to love and good works,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"not forsaking our own assembling together, as the custom of some is, but exhorting one another, and so much the more as you see the Day approaching."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"For if we sin willfully after we have received the knowledge of the truth, there remains no more a sacrifice for sins,"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"but a certain fearful expectation of judgment, and a fierceness of fire which will devour the adversaries."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"A man who disregards Moses\u2019 law dies without compassion on the word of two or three witnesses."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"How much worse punishment do you think he will be judged worthy of who has trodden under foot the Son of God, and has counted the blood of the covenant with which he was sanctified an unholy thing, and has insulted the Spirit of grace?"]]},{v:30,l:[[0,"For we know him who said, \u201cVengeance belongs to me. I will repay,\u201d says the Lord. Again, \u201cThe Lord will judge his people.\u201d"]]},{v:31,l:[[0,"It is a fearful thing to fall into the hands of the living God."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"But remember the former days, in which, after you were enlightened, you endured a great struggle with sufferings:"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"partly, being exposed to both reproaches and oppressions, and partly, becoming partakers with those who were treated so."]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"For you both had compassion on me in my chains and joyfully accepted the plundering of your possessions, knowing that you have for yourselves a better possession and an enduring one in the heavens."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Therefore don\u2019t throw away your boldness, which has a great reward."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"For you need endurance so that, having done the will of God, you may receive the promise."]]},{v:37,p:1,l:[[1,"\u201cIn a very little while,"],[2,"he who comes will come and will not wait."]]},{v:38,p:1,l:[[1,"But the righteous one will live by faith."],[2,"If he shrinks back, my soul has no pleasure in him.\u201d"]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"But we are not of those who shrink back to destruction, but of those who have faith to the saving of the soul."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Now faith is assurance of things hoped for, proof of things not seen."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For by this, the elders obtained approval."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"By faith we understand that the universe has been framed by the word of God, so that what is seen has not been made out of things which are visible."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Abel offered to God a more excellent sacrifice than Cain, through which he had testimony given to him that he was righteous, God testifying with respect to his gifts; and through it he, being dead, still speaks."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Enoch was taken away, so that he wouldn\u2019t see death, and he was not found, because God translated him. For he has had testimony given to him that before his translation he had been well pleasing to God."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Without faith it is impossible to be well pleasing to him, for he who comes to God must believe that he exists, and that he is a rewarder of those who seek him."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Noah, being warned about things not yet seen, moved with godly fear, prepared a ship for the saving of his house, through which he condemned the world and became heir of the righteousness which is according to faith."]],f:["or, reverence"]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Abraham, when he was called, obeyed to go out to the place which he was to receive for an inheritance. He went out, not knowing where he went."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"By faith he lived as an alien in the land of promise, as in a land not his own, dwelling in tents with Isaac and Jacob, the heirs with him of the same promise."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For he was looking for the city which has foundations, whose builder and maker is God."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith even Sarah herself received power to conceive, and she bore a child when she was past age, since she counted him faithful who had promised."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore as many as the stars of the sky in multitude, and as innumerable as the sand which is by the sea shore, were fathered by one man, and him as good as dead."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"These all died in faith, not having received the promises, but having seen them and embraced them from afar, and having confessed that they were strangers and pilgrims on the earth."]],f:["TR adds \u201cand being convinced of\u201d"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For those who say such things make it clear that they are seeking a country of their own."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If indeed they had been thinking of that country from which they went out, they would have had enough time to return."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But now they desire a better country, that is, a heavenly one. Therefore God is not ashamed of them, to be called their God, for he has prepared a city for them."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith, Abraham, being tested, offered up Isaac. Yes, he who had gladly received the promises was offering up his only born son,"]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03b7\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d."]},{v:18,l:[[0,"to whom it was said, \u201cYour offspring will be accounted as from Isaac,\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"concluding that God is able to raise up even from the dead. Figuratively speaking, he also did receive him back from the dead."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Isaac blessed Jacob and Esau, even concerning things to come."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Jacob, when he was dying, blessed each of the sons of Joseph, and worshiped, leaning on the top of his staff."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Joseph, when his end was near, made mention of the departure of the children of Israel, and gave instructions concerning his bones."]]},{v:23,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Moses, when he was born, was hidden for three months by his parents, because they saw that he was a beautiful child; and they were not afraid of the king\u2019s commandment."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Moses, when he had grown up, refused to be called the son of Pharaoh\u2019s daughter,"]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"choosing rather to share ill treatment with God\u2019s people than to enjoy the pleasures of sin for a time,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"considering the reproach of Christ greater riches than the treasures of Egypt; for he looked to the reward."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"By faith he left Egypt, not fearing the wrath of the king; for he endured, as seeing him who is invisible."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"By faith he kept the Passover and the sprinkling of the blood, that the destroyer of the firstborn should not touch them."]]},{v:29,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith they passed through the Red Sea as on dry land. When the Egyptians tried to do so, they were swallowed up."]]},{v:30,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith the walls of Jericho fell down after they had been encircled for seven days."]]},{v:31,p:1,l:[[0,"By faith Rahab the prostitute didn\u2019t perish with those who were disobedient, having received the spies in peace."]]},{v:32,p:1,l:[[0,"What more shall I say? For the time would fail me if I told of Gideon, Barak, Samson, Jephthah, David, Samuel, and the prophets\u2014"]]},{v:33,l:[[0,"who through faith subdued kingdoms, worked out righteousness, obtained promises, stopped the mouths of lions,"]]},{v:34,l:[[0,"quenched the power of fire, escaped the edge of the sword, from weakness were made strong, grew mighty in war, and caused foreign armies to flee."]]},{v:35,l:[[0,"Women received their dead by resurrection. Others were tortured, not accepting their deliverance, that they might obtain a better resurrection."]]},{v:36,l:[[0,"Others were tried by mocking and scourging, yes, moreover by bonds and imprisonment."]]},{v:37,l:[[0,"They were stoned. They were sawn apart. They were tempted. They were slain with the sword. They went around in sheep skins and in goat skins; being destitute, afflicted, ill-treated\u2014"]]},{v:38,l:[[0,"of whom the world was not worthy\u2014wandering in deserts, mountains, caves, and the holes of the earth."]]},{v:39,p:1,l:[[0,"These all, having been commended for their faith, didn\u2019t receive the promise,"]]},{v:40,l:[[0,"God having provided some better thing concerning us, so that apart from us they should not be made perfect."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore let\u2019s also, seeing we are surrounded by so great a cloud of witnesses, lay aside every weight and the sin which so easily entangles us, and let\u2019s run with perseverance the race that is set before us,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"looking to Jesus, the author and perfecter of faith, who for the joy that was set before him endured the cross, despising its shame, and has sat down at the right hand of the throne of God."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"For consider him who has endured such contradiction of sinners against himself, that you don\u2019t grow weary, fainting in your souls."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You have not yet resisted to blood, striving against sin."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You have forgotten the exhortation which reasons with you as with children,"],[1,"\u201cMy son, don\u2019t take lightly the chastening of the Lord,"],[2,"nor faint when you are reproved by him;"]]},{v:6,l:[[2,"for whom the Lord loves, he disciplines,"],[2,"and chastises every son whom he receives.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"It is for discipline that you endure. God deals with you as with children, for what son is there whom his father doesn\u2019t discipline?"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But if you are without discipline, of which all have been made partakers, then you are illegitimate, and not children."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Furthermore, we had the fathers of our flesh to chasten us, and we paid them respect. Shall we not much rather be in subjection to the Father of spirits and live?"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For they indeed for a few days disciplined us as seemed good to them, but he for our profit, that we may be partakers of his holiness."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"All chastening seems for the present to be not joyous but grievous; yet afterward it yields the peaceful fruit of righteousness to those who have been trained by it."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore lift up the hands that hang down and the feeble knees,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and make straight paths for your feet, so what is lame may not be dislocated, but rather be healed."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Follow after peace with all men, and the sanctification without which no man will see the Lord,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"looking carefully lest there be any man who falls short of the grace of God, lest any root of bitterness springing up trouble you and many be defiled by it,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"lest there be any sexually immoral person or profane person, like Esau, who sold his birthright for one meal."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For you know that even when he afterward desired to inherit the blessing, he was rejected, for he found no place for a change of mind though he sought it diligently with tears."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"For you have not come to a mountain that might be touched and that burned with fire, and to blackness, darkness, storm,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"the sound of a trumpet, and the voice of words; which those who heard it begged that not one more word should be spoken to them,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"for they could not stand that which was commanded, \u201cIf even an animal touches the mountain, it shall be stoned\u201d."]],f:["TR adds \u201cor shot with an arrow\u201d"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"So fearful was the appearance that Moses said, \u201cI am terrified and trembling.\u201d"]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But you have come to Mount Zion and to the city of the living God, the heavenly Jerusalem, and to innumerable multitudes of angels,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"to the festal gathering and assembly of the firstborn who are enrolled in heaven, to God the Judge of all, to the spirits of just men made perfect,"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"to Jesus, the mediator of a new covenant, and to the blood of sprinkling that speaks better than that of Abel."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"See that you don\u2019t refuse him who speaks. For if they didn\u2019t escape when they refused him who warned on the earth, how much more will we not escape who turn away from him who warns from heaven,"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"whose voice shook the earth then, but now he has promised, saying, \u201cYet once more I will shake not only the earth, but also the heavens.\u201d"]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"This phrase, \u201cYet once more\u201d signifies the removing of those things that are shaken, as of things that have been made, that those things which are not shaken may remain."]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"Therefore, receiving a Kingdom that can\u2019t be shaken, let\u2019s have grace, through which we serve God acceptably, with reverence and awe,"]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"for our God is a consuming fire."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Let brotherly love continue."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t forget to show hospitality to strangers, for in doing so, some have entertained angels without knowing it."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Remember those who are in bonds, as bound with them, and those who are ill-treated, since you are also in the body."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Let marriage be held in honor among all, and let the bed be undefiled; but God will judge the sexually immoral and adulterers."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Be free from the love of money, content with such things as you have, for he has said, \u201cI will in no way leave you, neither will I in any way forsake you.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So that with good courage we say,"],[1,"\u201cThe Lord is my helper. I will not fear."],[2,"What can man do to me?\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Remember your leaders, men who spoke to you the word of God, and considering the results of their conduct, imitate their faith."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Jesus Christ is the same yesterday, today, and forever."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be carried away by various and strange teachings, for it is good that the heart be established by grace, not by foods, through which those who were so occupied were not benefited."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"We have an altar from which those who serve the holy tabernacle have no right to eat."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the bodies of those animals, whose blood is brought into the holy place by the high priest as an offering for sin, are burned outside of the camp."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore Jesus also, that he might sanctify the people through his own blood, suffered outside of the gate."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s therefore go out to him outside of the camp, bearing his reproach."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"For we don\u2019t have here an enduring city, but we seek that which is to come."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Through him, then, let\u2019s offer up a sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of lips which proclaim allegiance to his name."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But don\u2019t forget to be doing good and sharing, for with such sacrifices God is well pleased."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Obey your leaders and submit to them, for they watch on behalf of your souls, as those who will give account, that they may do this with joy and not with groaning, for that would be unprofitable for you."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Pray for us, for we are persuaded that we have a good conscience, desiring to live honorably in all things."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I strongly urge you to do this, that I may be restored to you sooner."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"Now may the God of peace, who brought again from the dead the great shepherd of the sheep with the blood of an eternal covenant, our Lord Jesus,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"make you complete in every good work to do his will, working in you that which is well pleasing in his sight, through Jesus Christ, to whom be the glory forever and ever. Amen."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But I exhort you, brothers, endure the word of exhortation, for I have written to you in few words."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Know that our brother Timothy has been freed, with whom, if he comes shortly, I will see you."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Greet all of your leaders and all the saints. The Italians greet you."]]},{v:25,p:1,l:[[0,"Grace be with you all. Amen."]]}]]}},1329,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,a,i,s,r){i.exports={book:"Jas",name:"James",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"James, a servant of God and of the Lord Jesus Christ, to the twelve tribes which are in the Dispersion: Greetings."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Count it all joy, my brothers, when you fall into various temptations,"]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"knowing that the testing of your faith produces endurance."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Let endurance have its perfect work, that you may be perfect and complete, lacking in nothing."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"But if any of you lacks wisdom, let him ask of God, who gives to all liberally and without reproach, and it will be given to him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But let him ask in faith, without any doubting, for he who doubts is like a wave of the sea, driven by the wind and tossed."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For that man shouldn\u2019t think that he will receive anything from the Lord."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He is a double-minded man, unstable in all his ways."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Let the brother in humble circumstances glory in his high position;"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"and the rich, in that he is made humble, because like the flower in the grass, he will pass away."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For the sun arises with the scorching wind and withers the grass; and the flower in it falls, and the beauty of its appearance perishes. So the rich man will also fade away in his pursuits."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Blessed is a person who endures temptation, for when he has been approved, he will receive the crown of life which the Lord promised to those who love him."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Let no man say when he is tempted, \u201cI am tempted by God,\u201d for God can\u2019t be tempted by evil, and he himself tempts no one."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But each one is tempted when he is drawn away by his own lust and enticed."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Then the lust, when it has conceived, bears sin. The sin, when it is full grown, produces death."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be deceived, my beloved brothers."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Every good gift and every perfect gift is from above, coming down from the Father of lights, with whom can be no variation nor turning shadow."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Of his own will he gave birth to us by the word of truth, that we should be a kind of first fruits of his creatures."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"So, then, my beloved brothers, let every man be swift to hear, slow to speak, and slow to anger;"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"for the anger of man doesn\u2019t produce the righteousness of God."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Therefore, putting away all filthiness and overflowing of wickedness, receive with humility the implanted word, which is able to save your souls."]],f:["or, preserve your life."]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"But be doers of the word, and not only hearers, deluding your own selves."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"For if anyone is a hearer of the word and not a doer, he is like a man looking at his natural face in a mirror;"]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"for he sees himself, and goes away, and immediately forgets what kind of man he was."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"But he who looks into the perfect law of freedom and continues, not being a hearer who forgets but a doer of the work, this man will be blessed in what he does."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"If anyone among you thinks himself to be religious while he doesn\u2019t bridle his tongue, but deceives his heart, this man\u2019s religion is worthless."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"Pure religion and undefiled before our God and Father is this: to visit the fatherless and widows in their affliction, and to keep oneself unstained by the world."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"My brothers, don\u2019t hold the faith of our glorious Lord Jesus Christ with partiality."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For if a man with a gold ring, in fine clothing, comes into your synagogue, and a poor man in filthy clothing also comes in,"]],f:["or, meeting"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and you pay special attention to him who wears the fine clothing and say, \u201cSit here in a good place;\u201d and you tell the poor man, \u201cStand there,\u201d or \u201cSit by my footstool\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"haven\u2019t you shown partiality among yourselves, and become judges with evil thoughts?"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Listen, my beloved brothers. Didn\u2019t God choose those who are poor in this world to be rich in faith and heirs of the Kingdom which he promised to those who love him?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But you have dishonored the poor man. Don\u2019t the rich oppress you and personally drag you before the courts?"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t they blaspheme the honorable name by which you are called?"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"However, if you fulfill the royal law according to the Scripture, \u201cYou shall love your neighbor as yourself,\u201d you do well."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But if you show partiality, you commit sin, being convicted by the law as transgressors."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For whoever keeps the whole law, and yet stumbles in one point, he has become guilty of all."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For he who said, \u201cDo not commit adultery,\u201d also said, \u201cDo not commit murder.\u201d Now if you do not commit adultery but do murder, you have become a transgressor of the law."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"So speak and so do as men who are to be judged by the law of freedom."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"For judgment is without mercy to him who has shown no mercy. Mercy triumphs over judgment."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"What good is it, my brothers, if a man says he has faith, but has no works? Can faith save him?"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"And if a brother or sister is naked and in lack of daily food,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"and one of you tells them, \u201cGo in peace. Be warmed and filled;\u201d yet you didn\u2019t give them the things the body needs, what good is it?"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Even so faith, if it has no works, is dead in itself."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Yes, a man will say, \u201cYou have faith, and I have works.\u201d Show me your faith without works, and I will show you my faith by my works."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"You believe that God is one. You do well. The demons also believe\u2014and shudder."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But do you want to know, vain man, that faith apart from works is dead?"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Wasn\u2019t Abraham our father justified by works, in that he offered up Isaac his son on the altar?"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"You see that faith worked with his works, and by works faith was perfected."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"So the Scripture was fulfilled which says, \u201cAbraham believed God, and it was accounted to him as righteousness,\u201d and he was called the friend of God."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"You see then that by works a man is justified, and not only by faith."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"In the same way, wasn\u2019t Rahab the prostitute also justified by works when she received the messengers and sent them out another way?"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"For as the body apart from the spirit is dead, even so faith apart from works is dead."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Let not many of you be teachers, my brothers, knowing that we will receive heavier judgment."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"For we all stumble in many things. Anyone who doesn\u2019t stumble in word is a perfect person, able to bridle the whole body also."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Indeed, we put bits into the horses\u2019 mouths so that they may obey us, and we guide their whole body."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, the ships also, though they are so big and are driven by fierce winds, are yet guided by a very small rudder, wherever the pilot desires."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:5,l:[[0,"So the tongue is also a little member, and boasts great things. See how a small fire can spread to a large forest!"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"And the tongue is a fire. The world of iniquity among our members is the tongue, which defiles the whole body, and sets on fire the course of nature, and is set on fire by Gehenna."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For every kind of animal, bird, creeping thing, and sea creature is tamed, and has been tamed by mankind;"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"but nobody can tame the tongue. It is a restless evil, full of deadly poison."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"With it we bless our God and Father, and with it we curse men who are made in the image of God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Out of the same mouth comes blessing and cursing. My brothers, these things ought not to be so."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Does a spring send out from the same opening fresh and bitter water?"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Can a fig tree, my brothers, yield olives, or a vine figs? Thus no spring yields both salt water and fresh water."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Who is wise and understanding among you? Let him show by his good conduct that his deeds are done in gentleness of wisdom."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But if you have bitter jealousy and selfish ambition in your heart, don\u2019t boast and don\u2019t lie against the truth."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"This wisdom is not that which comes down from above, but is earthly, sensual, and demonic."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For where jealousy and selfish ambition are, there is confusion and every evil deed."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But the wisdom that is from above is first pure, then peaceful, gentle, reasonable, full of mercy and good fruits, without partiality, and without hypocrisy."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Now the fruit of righteousness is sown in peace by those who make peace."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Where do wars and fightings among you come from? Don\u2019t they come from your pleasures that war in your members?"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"You lust, and don\u2019t have. You murder and covet, and can\u2019t obtain. You fight and make war. You don\u2019t have, because you don\u2019t ask."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You ask, and don\u2019t receive, because you ask with wrong motives, so that you may spend it on your pleasures."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You adulterers and adulteresses, don\u2019t you know that friendship with the world is hostility toward God? Whoever therefore wants to be a friend of the world makes himself an enemy of God."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Or do you think that the Scripture says in vain, \u201cThe Spirit who lives in us yearns jealously\u201d?"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But he gives more grace. Therefore it says, \u201cGod resists the proud, but gives grace to the humble.\u201d"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Be subject therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Draw near to God, and he will draw near to you. Cleanse your hands, you sinners. Purify your hearts, you double-minded."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Lament, mourn, and weep. Let your laughter be turned to mourning and your joy to gloom."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Humble yourselves in the sight of the Lord, and he will exalt you."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t speak against one another, brothers. He who speaks against a brother and judges his brother, speaks against the law and judges the law. But if you judge the law, you are not a doer of the law but a judge."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Only one is the lawgiver, who is able to save and to destroy. But who are you to judge another?"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Come now, you who say, \u201cToday or tomorrow let\u2019s go into this city and spend a year there, trade, and make a profit.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Yet you don\u2019t know what your life will be like tomorrow. For what is your life? For you are a vapor that appears for a little time and then vanishes away."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For you ought to say, \u201cIf the Lord wills, we will both live, and do this or that.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But now you glory in your boasting. All such boasting is evil."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"To him therefore who knows to do good and doesn\u2019t do it, to him it is sin."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Come now, you rich, weep and howl for your miseries that are coming on you."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Your riches are corrupted and your garments are moth-eaten."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Your gold and your silver are corroded, and their corrosion will be for a testimony against you and will eat your flesh like fire. You have laid up your treasure in the last days."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Behold, the wages of the laborers who mowed your fields, which you have kept back by fraud, cry out; and the cries of those who reaped have entered into the ears of the Lord of Armies."]],f:["Greek: Sabaoth (or Hebrew: Tze\u2019va\u2019ot)"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You have lived in luxury on the earth, and taken your pleasure. You have nourished your hearts as in a day of slaughter."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"You have condemned and you have murdered the righteous one. He doesn\u2019t resist you."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Be patient therefore, brothers, until the coming of the Lord. Behold, the farmer waits for the precious fruit of the earth, being patient over it, until it receives the early and late rain."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"You also be patient. Establish your hearts, for the coming of the Lord is at hand."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t grumble, brothers, against one another, so that you won\u2019t be judged. Behold, the judge stands at the door."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Take, brothers, for an example of suffering and of perseverance, the prophets who spoke in the name of the Lord."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Behold, we call them blessed who endured. You have heard of the perseverance of Job and have seen the Lord in the outcome, and how the Lord is full of compassion and mercy."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"But above all things, my brothers, don\u2019t swear\u2014not by heaven, or by the earth, or by any other oath; but let your \u201cyes\u201d be \u201cyes\u201d, and your \u201cno\u201d, \u201cno\u201d, so that you don\u2019t fall into hypocrisy."]],f:["TR reads \u201cunder judgment\u201d instead of \u201cinto hypocrisy\u201d"]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Is any among you suffering? Let him pray. Is any cheerful? Let him sing praises."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Is any among you sick? Let him call for the elders of the assembly, and let them pray over him, anointing him with oil in the name of the Lord;"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"and the prayer of faith will heal him who is sick, and the Lord will raise him up. If he has committed sins, he will be forgiven."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Confess your sins to one another and pray for one another, that you may be healed. The insistent prayer of a righteous person is powerfully effective."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Elijah was a man with a nature like ours, and he prayed earnestly that it might not rain, and it didn\u2019t rain on the earth for three years and six months."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"He prayed again, and the sky gave rain, and the earth produced its fruit."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, if any among you wanders from the truth and someone turns him back,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"let him know that he who turns a sinner from the error of his way will save a soul from death and will cover a multitude of sins."]]}]]}},1330,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,i,r,s,h){r.exports={book:"1Pet",name:"1 Peter",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Peter, an apostle of Jesus Christ, to the chosen ones who are living as foreigners in the Dispersion in Pontus, Galatia, Cappadocia, Asia, and Bithynia,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"according to the foreknowledge of God the Father, in sanctification of the Spirit, that you may obey Jesus Christ and be sprinkled with his blood: Grace to you and peace be multiplied."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who according to his great mercy caused us to be born again to a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"to an incorruptible and undefiled inheritance that doesn\u2019t fade away, reserved in Heaven for you,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"who by the power of God are guarded through faith for a salvation ready to be revealed in the last time."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In this you greatly rejoice, though now for a little while, if need be, you have been grieved in various trials,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"that the proof of your faith, which is more precious than gold that perishes, even though it is tested by fire, may be found to result in praise, glory, and honor at the revelation of Jesus Christ\u2014"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"whom, not having known, you love. In him, though now you don\u2019t see him, yet believing, you rejoice greatly with joy that is unspeakable and full of glory,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"receiving the result of your faith, the salvation of your souls."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"Concerning this salvation, the prophets sought and searched diligently. They prophesied of the grace that would come to you,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"searching for who or what kind of time the Spirit of Christ which was in them pointed to when he predicted the sufferings of Christ and the glories that would follow them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"To them it was revealed that they served not themselves, but you, in these things, which now have been announced to you through those who preached the Good News to you by the Holy Spirit sent out from heaven; which things angels desire to look into."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore prepare your minds for action. Be sober, and set your hope fully on the grace that will be brought to you at the revelation of Jesus Christ\u2014"]],f:["literally, \u201cgird up the waist of your mind\u201d or \u201cput on the belt of the waist of your mind\u201d"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"as children of obedience, not conforming yourselves according to your former lusts as in your ignorance,"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"but just as he who called you is holy, you yourselves also be holy in all of your behavior,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"because it is written, \u201cYou shall be holy, for I am holy.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"If you call on him as Father, who without respect of persons judges according to each man\u2019s work, pass the time of your living as foreigners here in reverent fear,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"knowing that you were redeemed, not with corruptible things like silver or gold, from the useless way of life handed down from your fathers,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"but with precious blood, as of a lamb without blemish or spot, the blood of Christ,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"who was foreknown indeed before the foundation of the world, but was revealed in this last age for your sake,"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"who through him are believers in God, who raised him from the dead and gave him glory, so that your faith and hope might be in God."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"Seeing you have purified your souls in your obedience to the truth through the Spirit in sincere brotherly affection, love one another from the heart fervently,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"having been born again, not of corruptible seed, but of incorruptible, through the word of God, which lives and remains forever."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"For,"],[1,"\u201cAll flesh is like grass,"],[2,"and all of man\u2019s glory like the flower in the grass."],[1,"The grass withers, and its flower falls;"]]},{v:25,l:[[2,"but the Lord\u2019s word endures forever.\u201d"],[0,"This is the word of Good News which was preached to you."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Putting away therefore all wickedness, all deceit, hypocrisies, envies, and all evil speaking,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"as newborn babies, long for the pure spiritual milk, that with it you may grow,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"if indeed you have tasted that the Lord is gracious."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Come to him, a living stone, rejected indeed by men, but chosen by God, precious."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You also as living stones are built up as a spiritual house, to be a holy priesthood, to offer up spiritual sacrifices, acceptable to God through Jesus Christ."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Because it is contained in Scripture,"],[1,"\u201cBehold, I lay in Zion a chief cornerstone, chosen and precious."],[2,"He who believes in him will not be disappointed.\u201d"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u05d4\u05b4\u05e0\u05b5\u05bc\u05d4\u201d or \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"For you who believe therefore is the honor, but for those who are disobedient,"],[1,"\u201cThe stone which the builders rejected"],[2,"has become the chief cornerstone,\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"and,"],[1,"\u201ca stumbling stone and a rock of offense.\u201d"],[0,"For they stumble at the word, being disobedient, to which also they were appointed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But you are a chosen race, a royal priesthood, a holy nation, a people for God\u2019s own possession, that you may proclaim the excellence of him who called you out of darkness into his marvelous light."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"In the past, you were not a people, but now are God\u2019s people, who had not obtained mercy, but now have obtained mercy."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, I beg you as foreigners and pilgrims to abstain from fleshly lusts which war against the soul,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"having good behavior among the nations, so in that of which they speak against you as evildoers, they may see your good works and glorify God in the day of visitation."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore subject yourselves to every ordinance of man for the Lord\u2019s sake: whether to the king, as supreme,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"or to governors, as sent by him for vengeance on evildoers and for praise to those who do well."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"For this is the will of God, that by well-doing you should put to silence the ignorance of foolish men."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Live as free people, yet not using your freedom for a cloak of wickedness, but as bondservants of God."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Honor all men. Love the brotherhood. Fear God. Honor the king."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Servants, be in subjection to your masters with all respect, not only to the good and gentle, but also to the wicked."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For it is commendable if someone endures pain, suffering unjustly, because of conscience toward God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"For what glory is it if, when you sin, you patiently endure beating? But if when you do well, you patiently endure suffering, this is commendable with God."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For you were called to this, because Christ also suffered for us, leaving you an example, that you should follow his steps,"]],f:["TR reads \u201cus\u201d instead of \u201cyou\u201d"]},{v:22,l:[[0,"who didn\u2019t sin, \u201cneither was deceit found in his mouth.\u201d"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"When he was cursed, he didn\u2019t curse back. When he suffered, he didn\u2019t threaten, but committed himself to him who judges righteously."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He himself bore our sins in his body on the tree, that we, having died to sins, might live to righteousness. You were healed by his wounds."]],f:["or, stripes"]},{v:25,l:[[0,"For you were going astray like sheep; but now you have returned to the Shepherd and Overseer of your souls."]],f:["\u201cOverseer\u201d is from the Greek \u1f10\u03c0\u03af\u03c3\u03ba\u03bf\u03c0\u03bf\u03bd, which can mean overseer, curator, guardian, or superintendent."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"In the same way, wives, be in subjection to your own husbands, so that, even if any don\u2019t obey the Word, they may be won by the behavior of their wives without a word,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"seeing your pure behavior in fear."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Let your beauty come not from the outward adorning of braiding your hair, and of wearing gold ornaments or of putting on fine clothing,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"but from the hidden person of the heart, in the incorruptible adornment of a gentle and quiet spirit, which is very precious in God\u2019s sight."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For this is how in the past the holy women who hoped in God also adorned themselves, being in subjection to their own husbands."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"So Sarah obeyed Abraham, calling him lord, whose children you now are if you do well and are not put in fear by any terror."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"You husbands, in the same way, live with your wives according to knowledge, giving honor to the woman as to the weaker vessel, as also being joint heirs of the grace of life, that your prayers may not be hindered."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Finally, all of you be like-minded, compassionate, loving as brothers, tenderhearted, courteous,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"not rendering evil for evil or insult for insult; but instead blessing, knowing that you were called to this, that you may inherit a blessing."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"For,"],[1,"\u201cHe who would love life"],[2,"and see good days,"],[1,"let him keep his tongue from evil"],[2,"and his lips from speaking deceit."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[1,"Let him turn away from evil and do good."],[2,"Let him seek peace and pursue it."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[1,"For the eyes of the Lord are on the righteous,"],[2,"and his ears open to their prayer;"],[2,"but the face of the Lord is against those who do evil.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Now who will harm you if you become imitators of that which is good?"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But even if you should suffer for righteousness\u2019 sake, you are blessed. \u201cDon\u2019t fear what they fear, neither be troubled.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But sanctify the Lord God in your hearts. Always be ready to give an answer to everyone who asks you a reason concerning the hope that is in you, with humility and fear,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"having a good conscience. Thus, while you are spoken against as evildoers, they may be disappointed who curse your good way of life in Christ."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For it is better, if it is God\u2019s will, that you suffer for doing what is right than for doing evil."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Because Christ also suffered for sins once, the righteous for the unrighteous, that he might bring you to God, being put to death in the flesh, but made alive in the Spirit,"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"in whom he also went and preached to the spirits in prison,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"who before were disobedient when God waited patiently in the days of Noah while the ship was being built. In it, few, that is, eight souls, were saved through water."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"This is a symbol of baptism, which now saves you\u2014not the putting away of the filth of the flesh, but the answer of a good conscience toward God\u2014through the resurrection of Jesus Christ,"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"who is at the right hand of God, having gone into heaven, angels and authorities and powers being made subject to him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, since Christ suffered for us in the flesh, arm yourselves also with the same mind; for he who has suffered in the flesh has ceased from sin,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that you no longer should live the rest of your time in the flesh for the lusts of men, but for the will of God."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For we have spent enough of our past time doing the desire of the Gentiles, and having walked in lewdness, lusts, drunken binges, orgies, carousings, and abominable idolatries."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They think it is strange that you don\u2019t run with them into the same excess of riot, speaking evil of you."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They will give account to him who is ready to judge the living and the dead."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For to this end the Good News was preached even to the dead, that they might be judged indeed as men in the flesh, but live as to God in the spirit."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"But the end of all things is near. Therefore be of sound mind, self-controlled, and sober in prayer."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"And above all things be earnest in your love among yourselves, for love covers a multitude of sins."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Be hospitable to one another without grumbling."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"As each has received a gift, employ it in serving one another, as good managers of the grace of God in its various forms."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"If anyone speaks, let it be as it were the very words of God. If anyone serves, let it be as of the strength which God supplies, that in all things God may be glorified through Jesus Christ, to whom belong the glory and the dominion forever and ever. Amen."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, don\u2019t be astonished at the fiery trial which has come upon you to test you, as though a strange thing happened to you."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But because you are partakers of Christ\u2019s sufferings, rejoice, that at the revelation of his glory you also may rejoice with exceeding joy."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"If you are insulted for the name of Christ, you are blessed, because the Spirit of glory and of God rests on you. On their part he is blasphemed, but on your part he is glorified."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"But let none of you suffer as a murderer, or a thief, or an evil doer, or a meddler in other men\u2019s matters."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"But if one of you suffers for being a Christian, let him not be ashamed; but let him glorify God in this matter."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For the time has come for judgment to begin with the household of God. If it begins first with us, what will happen to those who don\u2019t obey the Good News of God?"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"\u201cIf it is hard for the righteous to be saved, what will happen to the ungodly and the sinner?\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Therefore let them also who suffer according to the will of God in doing good entrust their souls to him, as to a faithful Creator."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore I exhort the elders among you, as a fellow elder and a witness of the sufferings of Christ, and who will also share in the glory that will be revealed:"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"shepherd the flock of God which is among you, exercising the oversight, not under compulsion, but voluntarily; not for dishonest gain, but willingly;"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"not as lording it over those entrusted to you, but making yourselves examples to the flock."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When the chief Shepherd is revealed, you will receive the crown of glory that doesn\u2019t fade away."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Likewise, you younger ones, be subject to the elder. Yes, all of you clothe yourselves with humility and subject yourselves to one another; for \u201cGod resists the proud, but gives grace to the humble.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Humble yourselves therefore under the mighty hand of God, that he may exalt you in due time,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"casting all your worries on him, because he cares for you."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Be sober and self-controlled. Be watchful. Your adversary, the devil, walks around like a roaring lion, seeking whom he may devour."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Withstand him steadfast in your faith, knowing that your brothers who are in the world are undergoing the same sufferings."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But may the God of all grace, who called you to his eternal glory by Christ Jesus, after you have suffered a little while, perfect, establish, strengthen, and settle you."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"To him be the glory and the power forever and ever. Amen."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Through Silvanus, our faithful brother, as I consider him, I have written to you briefly, exhorting and testifying that this is the true grace of God in which you stand."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"She who is in Babylon, chosen together with you, greets you. So does Mark, my son."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Greet one another with a kiss of love."],[0,"Peace be to all of you who are in Christ Jesus. Amen."]]}]]}},1331,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,n,s,i,r){s.exports={book:"2Pet",name:"2 Peter",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Simon Peter, a servant and apostle of Jesus Christ, to those who have obtained a like precious faith with us in the righteousness of our God and Savior, Jesus Christ:"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Grace to you and peace be multiplied in the knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"seeing that his divine power has granted to us all things that pertain to life and godliness, through the knowledge of him who called us by his own glory and virtue,"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"by which he has granted to us his precious and exceedingly great promises; that through these you may become partakers of the divine nature, having escaped from the corruption that is in the world by lust."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Yes, and for this very cause adding on your part all diligence, in your faith supply moral excellence; and in moral excellence, knowledge;"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and in knowledge, self-control; and in self-control, perseverance; and in perseverance, godliness;"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and in godliness, brotherly affection; and in brotherly affection, love."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"For if these things are yours and abound, they make you to not be idle or unfruitful in the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"For he who lacks these things is blind, seeing only what is near, having forgotten the cleansing from his old sins."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore, brothers, be more diligent to make your calling and election sure. For if you do these things, you will never stumble."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For thus you will be richly supplied with the entrance into the eternal Kingdom of our Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore I will not be negligent to remind you of these things, though you know them and are established in the present truth."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I think it right, as long as I am in this tent, to stir you up by reminding you,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"knowing that the putting off of my tent comes swiftly, even as our Lord Jesus Christ made clear to me."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Yes, I will make every effort that you may always be able to remember these things even after my departure."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"For we didn\u2019t follow cunningly devised fables when we made known to you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but we were eyewitnesses of his majesty."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For he received from God the Father honor and glory when the voice came to him from the Majestic Glory, \u201cThis is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased.\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"We heard this voice come out of heaven when we were with him on the holy mountain."]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"We have the more sure word of prophecy; and you do well that you heed it as to a lamp shining in a dark place, until the day dawns and the morning star arises in your hearts,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"knowing this first, that no prophecy of Scripture is of private interpretation."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For no prophecy ever came by the will of man, but holy men of God spoke, being moved by the Holy Spirit."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"But false prophets also arose among the people, as false teachers will also be among you, who will secretly bring in destructive heresies, denying even the Master who bought them, bringing on themselves swift destruction."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Many will follow their immoral ways, and as a result, the way of the truth will be maligned."]],f:["TR reads \u201cdestructive\u201d instead of \u201cimmoral\u201d"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"In covetousness they will exploit you with deceptive words: whose sentence now from of old doesn\u2019t linger, and their destruction will not slumber."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"For if God didn\u2019t spare angels when they sinned, but cast them down to Tartarus, and committed them to pits of darkness to be reserved for judgment;"]],f:["Tartarus is another name for Hell"]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and didn\u2019t spare the ancient world, but preserved Noah with seven others, a preacher of righteousness, when he brought a flood on the world of the ungodly,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and turning the cities of Sodom and Gomorrah into ashes, condemned them to destruction, having made them an example to those who would live in an ungodly way,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"and delivered righteous Lot, who was very distressed by the lustful life of the wicked"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"(for that righteous man dwelling among them was tormented in his righteous soul from day to day with seeing and hearing lawless deeds),"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"then the Lord knows how to deliver the godly out of temptation and to keep the unrighteous under punishment for the day of judgment,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"but chiefly those who walk after the flesh in the lust of defilement and despise authority. Daring, self-willed, they are not afraid to speak evil of dignitaries,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"whereas angels, though greater in might and power, don\u2019t bring a slanderous judgment against them before the Lord."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"But these, as unreasoning creatures, born natural animals to be taken and destroyed, speaking evil in matters about which they are ignorant, will in their destroying surely be destroyed,"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"receiving the wages of unrighteousness; people who count it pleasure to revel in the daytime, spots and defects, reveling in their deceit while they feast with you;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"having eyes full of adultery, and who can\u2019t cease from sin, enticing unsettled souls, having a heart trained in greed, accursed children!"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Forsaking the right way, they went astray, having followed the way of Balaam the son of Beor, who loved the wages of wrongdoing;"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"but he was rebuked for his own disobedience. A speechless donkey spoke with a man\u2019s voice and stopped the madness of the prophet."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"These are wells without water, clouds driven by a storm, for whom the blackness of darkness has been reserved forever."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"For, uttering great swelling words of emptiness, they entice in the lusts of the flesh, by licentiousness, those who are indeed escaping from those who live in error;"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"promising them liberty, while they themselves are bondservants of corruption; for a man is brought into bondage by whoever overcomes him."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"For if, after they have escaped the defilement of the world through the knowledge of the Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, they are again entangled in it and overcome, the last state has become worse for them than the first."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"For it would be better for them not to have known the way of righteousness, than after knowing it, to turn back from the holy commandment delivered to them."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"But it has happened to them according to the true proverb, \u201cThe dog turns to his own vomit again,\u201d and \u201cthe sow that has washed to wallowing in the mire.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is now, beloved, the second letter that I have written to you; and in both of them I stir up your sincere mind by reminding you"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"that you should remember the words which were spoken before by the holy prophets and the commandment of us, the apostles of the Lord and Savior,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"knowing this first, that in the last days mockers will come, walking after their own lusts"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"and saying, \u201cWhere is the promise of his coming? For, from the day that the fathers fell asleep, all things continue as they were from the beginning of the creation.\u201d"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"For they willfully forget that there were heavens from of old, and an earth formed out of water and amid water by the word of God,"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"by which means the world that existed then, being overflowed with water, perished."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But the heavens that exist now and the earth, by the same word have been stored up for fire, being reserved against the day of judgment and destruction of ungodly men."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"But don\u2019t forget this one thing, beloved, that one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The Lord is not slow concerning his promise, as some count slowness; but he is patient with us, not wishing that anyone should perish, but that all should come to repentance."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But the day of the Lord will come as a thief in the night, in which the heavens will pass away with a great noise, and the elements will be dissolved with fervent heat; and the earth and the works that are in it will be burned up."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Therefore, since all these things will be destroyed like this, what kind of people ought you to be in holy living and godliness,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"looking for and earnestly desiring the coming of the day of God, which will cause the burning heavens to be dissolved, and the elements will melt with fervent heat?"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"But, according to his promise, we look for new heavens and a new earth, in which righteousness dwells."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, beloved, seeing that you look for these things, be diligent to be found in peace, without defect and blameless in his sight."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Regard the patience of our Lord as salvation; even as our beloved brother Paul also, according to the wisdom given to him, wrote to you,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"as also in all of his letters, speaking in them of these things. In those, there are some things that are hard to understand, which the ignorant and unsettled twist, as they also do to the other Scriptures, to their own destruction."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"You therefore, beloved, knowing these things beforehand, beware, lest being carried away with the error of the wicked, you fall from your own steadfastness."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"But grow in the grace and knowledge of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ. To him be the glory both now and forever. Amen."]]}]]}},1332,[]);
__d(function(e,o,h,t,s,i,n){s.exports={book:"1John",name:"1 John",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"That which was from the beginning, that which we have heard, that which we have seen with our eyes, that which we saw, and our hands touched, concerning the Word of life"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"(and the life was revealed, and we have seen, and testify, and declare to you the life, the eternal life, which was with the Father, and was revealed to us);"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"that which we have seen and heard we declare to you, that you also may have fellowship with us. Yes, and our fellowship is with the Father and with his Son, Jesus Christ."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:4,l:[[0,"And we write these things to you, that our joy may be fulfilled."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the message which we have heard from him and announce to you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"If we say that we have fellowship with him and walk in the darkness, we lie and don\u2019t tell the truth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"But if we walk in the light as he is in the light, we have fellowship with one another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanses us from all sin."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"If we say that we have no sin, we deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and righteous to forgive us the sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If we say that we haven\u2019t sinned, we make him a liar, and his word is not in us."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"My little children, I write these things to you so that you may not sin. If anyone sins, we have a Counselor with the Father, Jesus Christ, the righteous."]],f:["Greek \u03c0\u03b1\u03c1\u03b1\u03ba\u03bb\u03b7\u03c4\u03bf\u03bd: Counselor, Helper, Intercessor, Advocate, and Comforter."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"And he is the atoning sacrifice for our sins, and not for ours only, but also for the whole world."]],f:["\u201catoning sacrifice\u201d is from the Greek \u201c\u03b9\u03bb\u03b1\u03c3\u03bc\u03bf\u03c2\u201d, an appeasing, propitiating, or the means of appeasement or propitiation\u2014the sacrifice that turns away God\u2019s wrath because of our sin."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"This is how we know that we know him: if we keep his commandments."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"One who says, \u201cI know him,\u201d and doesn\u2019t keep his commandments, is a liar, and the truth isn\u2019t in him."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"But God\u2019s love has most certainly been perfected in whoever keeps his word. This is how we know that we are in him:"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"he who says he remains in him ought himself also to walk just like he walked."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Brothers, I write no new commandment to you, but an old commandment which you had from the beginning. The old commandment is the word which you heard from the beginning."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Again, I write a new commandment to you, which is true in him and in you, because the darkness is passing away and the true light already shines."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He who says he is in the light and hates his brother is in the darkness even until now."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He who loves his brother remains in the light, and there is no occasion for stumbling in him."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"But he who hates his brother is in the darkness, and walks in the darkness, and doesn\u2019t know where he is going, because the darkness has blinded his eyes."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I write to you, little children, because your sins are forgiven you for his name\u2019s sake."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"I write to you, fathers, because you know him who is from the beginning."],[0,"I write to you, young men, because you have overcome the evil one."],[0,"I write to you, little children, because you know the Father."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"I have written to you, fathers, because you know him who is from the beginning."],[0,"I have written to you, young men, because you are strong, and the word of God remains in you, and you have overcome the evil one."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t love the world or the things that are in the world. If anyone loves the world, the Father\u2019s love isn\u2019t in him."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"For all that is in the world\u2014the lust of the flesh, the lust of the eyes, and the pride of life\u2014isn\u2019t the Father\u2019s, but is the world\u2019s."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The world is passing away with its lusts, but he who does God\u2019s will remains forever."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"Little children, these are the end times, and as you heard that the Antichrist is coming, even now many antichrists have arisen. By this we know that it is the final hour."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They went out from us, but they didn\u2019t belong to us; for if they had belonged to us, they would have continued with us. But they left, that they might be revealed that none of them belong to us."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"You have an anointing from the Holy One, and you all have knowledge."]],f:["Or, \u201cknow what is true\u201d, or, \u201cknow all things\u201d"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I have not written to you because you don\u2019t know the truth, but because you know it, and because no lie is of the truth."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Who is the liar but he who denies that Jesus is the Christ? This is the Antichrist, he who denies the Father and the Son."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"Whoever denies the Son doesn\u2019t have the Father. He who confesses the Son has the Father also."]],f:["MT omits: He who confesses the Son has the Father also."]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Therefore, as for you, let that remain in you which you heard from the beginning. If that which you heard from the beginning remains in you, you also will remain in the Son, and in the Father."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"This is the promise which he promised us, the eternal life."]]},{v:26,p:1,l:[[0,"These things I have written to you concerning those who would lead you astray."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"As for you, the anointing which you received from him remains in you, and you don\u2019t need for anyone to teach you. But as his anointing teaches you concerning all things, and is true, and is no lie, and even as it taught you, you will remain in him."]]},{v:28,p:1,l:[[0,"Now, little children, remain in him, that when he appears, we may have boldness and not be ashamed before him at his coming."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"If you know that he is righteous, you know that everyone who practices righteousness has been born of him."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"See how great a love the Father has given to us, that we should be called children of God! For this cause the world doesn\u2019t know us, because it didn\u2019t know him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Beloved, now we are children of God. It is not yet revealed what we will be; but we know that when he is revealed, we will be like him, for we will see him just as he is."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Everyone who has this hope set on him purifies himself, even as he is pure."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"Everyone who sins also commits lawlessness. Sin is lawlessness."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"You know that he was revealed to take away our sins, and no sin is in him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Whoever remains in him doesn\u2019t sin. Whoever sins hasn\u2019t seen him and doesn\u2019t know him."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Little children, let no one lead you astray. He who does righteousness is righteous, even as he is righteous."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He who sins is of the devil, for the devil has been sinning from the beginning. To this end the Son of God was revealed: that he might destroy the works of the devil."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Whoever is born of God doesn\u2019t commit sin, because his seed remains in him, and he can\u2019t sin, because he is born of God."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"In this the children of God are revealed, and the children of the devil. Whoever doesn\u2019t do righteousness is not of God, neither is he who doesn\u2019t love his brother."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"For this is the message which you heard from the beginning, that we should love one another\u2014"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"unlike Cain, who was of the evil one and killed his brother. Why did he kill him? Because his deeds were evil, and his brother\u2019s righteous."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be surprised, my brothers, if the world hates you."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"We know that we have passed out of death into life, because we love the brothers. He who doesn\u2019t love his brother remains in death."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Whoever hates his brother is a murderer, and you know that no murderer has eternal life remaining in him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"By this we know love, because he laid down his life for us. And we ought to lay down our lives for the brothers."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"But whoever has the world\u2019s goods and sees his brother in need, then closes his heart of compassion against him, how does God\u2019s love remain in him?"]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"My little children, let\u2019s not love in word only, or with the tongue only, but in deed and truth."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"And by this we know that we are of the truth and persuade our hearts before him,"]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"because if our heart condemns us, God is greater than our heart, and knows all things."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Beloved, if our hearts don\u2019t condemn us, we have boldness toward God;"]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"so whatever we ask, we receive from him, because we keep his commandments and do the things that are pleasing in his sight."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"This is his commandment, that we should believe in the name of his Son, Jesus Christ, and love one another, even as he commanded."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"He who keeps his commandments remains in him, and he in him. By this we know that he remains in us, by the Spirit which he gave us."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, don\u2019t believe every spirit, but test the spirits, whether they are of God, because many false prophets have gone out into the world."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"By this you know the Spirit of God: every spirit who confesses that Jesus Christ has come in the flesh is of God,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and every spirit who doesn\u2019t confess that Jesus Christ has come in the flesh is not of God; and this is the spirit of the Antichrist, of whom you have heard that it comes. Now it is in the world already."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"You are of God, little children, and have overcome them, because greater is he who is in you than he who is in the world."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They are of the world. Therefore they speak of the world, and the world hears them."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"We are of God. He who knows God listens to us. He who is not of God doesn\u2019t listen to us. By this we know the spirit of truth, and the spirit of error."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, let\u2019s love one another, for love is of God; and everyone who loves has been born of God and knows God."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"He who doesn\u2019t love doesn\u2019t know God, for God is love."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"By this God\u2019s love was revealed in us, that God has sent his only born Son into the world that we might live through him."]],f:["The phrase \u201conly born\u201d is from the Greek word \u201c\u03bc\u03bf\u03bd\u03bf\u03b3\u03b5\u03bd\u03b7\u201d, which is sometimes translated \u201conly begotten\u201d or \u201cone and only\u201d."]},{v:10,l:[[0,"In this is love, not that we loved God, but that he loved us, and sent his Son as the atoning sacrifice for our sins."]],f:["\u201catoning sacrifice\u201d is from the Greek \u201c\u03b9\u03bb\u03b1\u03c3\u03bc\u03bf\u03c2\u201d, an appeasing, propitiating, or the means of appeasement or propitiation\u2014the sacrifice that turns away God\u2019s wrath because of our sin."]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Beloved, if God loved us in this way, we also ought to love one another."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"No one has seen God at any time. If we love one another, God remains in us, and his love has been perfected in us."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"By this we know that we remain in him and he in us, because he has given us of his Spirit."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"We have seen and testify that the Father has sent the Son as the Savior of the world."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Whoever confesses that Jesus is the Son of God, God remains in him, and he in God."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"We know and have believed the love which God has for us. God is love, and he who remains in love remains in God, and God remains in him."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"In this, love has been made perfect among us, that we may have boldness in the day of judgment, because as he is, even so we are in this world."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"There is no fear in love; but perfect love casts out fear, because fear has punishment. He who fears is not made perfect in love."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"We love him, because he first loved us."]],f:["NU omits \u201chim\u201d."]},{v:20,l:[[0,"If a man says, \u201cI love God,\u201d and hates his brother, he is a liar; for he who doesn\u2019t love his brother whom he has seen, how can he love God whom he has not seen?"]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"This commandment we have from him, that he who loves God should also love his brother."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Whoever believes that Jesus is the Christ has been born of God. Whoever loves the Father also loves the child who is born of him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"By this we know that we love the children of God, when we love God and keep his commandments."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For this is loving God, that we keep his commandments. His commandments are not grievous."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For whatever is born of God overcomes the world. This is the victory that has overcome the world: your faith."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Who is he who overcomes the world, but he who believes that Jesus is the Son of God?"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"This is he who came by water and blood, Jesus Christ; not with the water only, but with the water and the blood. It is the Spirit who testifies, because the Spirit is the truth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"For there are three who testify:"]],f:["Only a few recent manuscripts add \u201cin heaven: the Father, the Word, and the Holy Spirit; and these three are one. And there are three that testify on earth:\u201d"]},{v:8,l:[[0,"the Spirit, the water, and the blood; and the three agree as one."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If we receive the witness of men, the witness of God is greater; for this is God\u2019s testimony which he has testified concerning his Son."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He who believes in the Son of God has the testimony in himself. He who doesn\u2019t believe God has made him a liar, because he has not believed in the testimony that God has given concerning his Son."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The testimony is this: that God gave to us eternal life, and this life is in his Son."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He who has the Son has the life. He who doesn\u2019t have God\u2019s Son doesn\u2019t have the life."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"These things I have written to you who believe in the name of the Son of God, that you may know that you have eternal life, and that you may continue to believe in the name of the Son of God."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the boldness which we have toward him, that if we ask anything according to his will, he listens to us."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"And if we know that he listens to us, whatever we ask, we know that we have the petitions which we have asked of him."]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"If anyone sees his brother sinning a sin not leading to death, he shall ask, and God will give him life for those who sin not leading to death. There is sin leading to death. I don\u2019t say that he should make a request concerning this."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"All unrighteousness is sin, and there is sin not leading to death."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"We know that whoever is born of God doesn\u2019t sin, but he who was born of God keeps himself, and the evil one doesn\u2019t touch him."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"We know that we are of God, and the whole world lies in the power of the evil one."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"We know that the Son of God has come and has given us an understanding, that we know him who is true; and we are in him who is true, in his Son Jesus Christ. This is the true God and eternal life."]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"Little children, keep yourselves from idols."]]}]]}},1333,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,n,a,i){n.exports={book:"2John",name:"2 John",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The elder, to the chosen lady and her children, whom I love in truth, and not I only, but also all those who know the truth,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"for the truth\u2019s sake, which remains in us, and it will be with us forever:"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Grace, mercy, and peace will be with us, from God the Father and from the Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and love."]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I rejoice greatly that I have found some of your children walking in truth, even as we have been commanded by the Father."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Now I beg you, dear lady, not as though I wrote to you a new commandment, but that which we had from the beginning, that we love one another."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"This is love, that we should walk according to his commandments. This is the commandment, even as you heard from the beginning, that you should walk in it."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"For many deceivers have gone out into the world, those who don\u2019t confess that Jesus Christ came in the flesh. This is the deceiver and the Antichrist."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Watch yourselves, that we don\u2019t lose the things which we have accomplished, but that we receive a full reward."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Whoever transgresses and doesn\u2019t remain in the teaching of Christ doesn\u2019t have God. He who remains in the teaching has both the Father and the Son."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If anyone comes to you and doesn\u2019t bring this teaching, don\u2019t receive him into your house, and don\u2019t welcome him,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"for he who welcomes him participates in his evil deeds."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Having many things to write to you, I don\u2019t want to do so with paper and ink, but I hope to come to you and to speak face to face, that our joy may be made full."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The children of your chosen sister greet you. Amen."]]}]]}},1334,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,s,a,r){s.exports={book:"3John",name:"3 John",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The elder to Gaius the beloved, whom I love in truth."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, I pray that you may prosper in all things and be healthy, even as your soul prospers."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For I rejoiced greatly when brothers came and testified about your truth, even as you walk in truth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I have no greater joy than this: to hear about my children walking in truth."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, you do a faithful work in whatever you accomplish for those who are brothers and strangers."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"They have testified about your love before the assembly. You will do well to send them forward on their journey in a way worthy of God,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"because for the sake of the Name they went out, taking nothing from the Gentiles."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"We therefore ought to receive such, that we may be fellow workers for the truth."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"I wrote to the assembly, but Diotrephes, who loves to be first among them, doesn\u2019t accept what we say."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Therefore, if I come, I will call attention to his deeds which he does, unjustly accusing us with wicked words. Not content with this, he doesn\u2019t receive the brothers himself, and those who would, he forbids and throws out of the assembly."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, don\u2019t imitate that which is evil, but that which is good. He who does good is of God. He who does evil hasn\u2019t seen God."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Demetrius has the testimony of all, and of the truth itself; yes, we also testify, and you know that our testimony is true."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"I had many things to write to you, but I am unwilling to write to you with ink and pen;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"but I hope to see you soon. Then we will speak face to face."],[0,"Peace be to you. The friends greet you. Greet the friends by name."]]}]]}},1335,[]);
__d(function(e,o,t,n,a,s,r){a.exports={book:"Jude",name:"Jude",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Jude, a servant of Jesus Christ, and brother of James, to those who are called, sanctified by God the Father, and kept for Jesus Christ:"]],f:["or, Judah","\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d."]},{v:2,l:[[0,"May mercy, peace, and love be multiplied to you."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Beloved, while I was very eager to write to you about our common salvation, I was constrained to write to you exhorting you to contend earnestly for the faith which was once for all delivered to the saints."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"For there are certain men who crept in secretly, even those who were long ago written about for this condemnation: ungodly men, turning the grace of our God into indecency, and denying our only Master, God, and Lord, Jesus Christ."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I desire to remind you, though you already know this, that the Lord, having saved a people out of the land of Egypt, afterward destroyed those who didn\u2019t believe."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Angels who didn\u2019t keep their first domain, but deserted their own dwelling place, he has kept in everlasting bonds under darkness for the judgment of the great day."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Even as Sodom and Gomorrah and the cities around them, having in the same way as these given themselves over to sexual immorality and gone after strange flesh, are shown as an example, suffering the punishment of eternal fire."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Yet in the same way, these also in their dreaming defile the flesh, despise authority, and slander celestial beings."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"But Michael, the archangel, when contending with the devil and arguing about the body of Moses, dared not bring against him an abusive condemnation, but said, \u201cMay the Lord rebuke you!\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"But these speak evil of whatever things they don\u2019t know. They are destroyed in these things that they understand naturally, like the creatures without reason."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"Woe to them! For they went in the way of Cain, and ran riotously in the error of Balaam for hire, and perished in Korah\u2019s rebellion."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"These are hidden rocky reefs in your love feasts when they feast with you, shepherds who without fear feed themselves; clouds without water, carried along by winds; autumn trees without fruit, twice dead, plucked up by the roots;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"wild waves of the sea, foaming out their own shame; wandering stars, for whom the blackness of darkness has been reserved forever."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"About these also Enoch, the seventh from Adam, prophesied, saying, \u201cBehold, the Lord came with ten thousands of his holy ones,"]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"to execute judgment on all, and to convict all the ungodly of all their works of ungodliness which they have done in an ungodly way, and of all the hard things which ungodly sinners have spoken against him.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"These are murmurers and complainers, walking after their lusts\u2014and their mouth speaks proud things\u2014showing respect of persons to gain advantage."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"But you, beloved, remember the words which have been spoken before by the apostles of our Lord Jesus Christ."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"They said to you, \u201cIn the last time there will be mockers, walking after their own ungodly lusts.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"These are those who cause divisions and are sensual, not having the Spirit."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"But you, beloved, keep building up yourselves on your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Spirit."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Keep yourselves in God\u2019s love, looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ to eternal life."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"On some have compassion, making a distinction,"]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"and some save, snatching them out of the fire with fear, hating even the clothing stained by the flesh."]]},{v:24,p:1,l:[[0,"Now to him who is able to keep them from stumbling, and to present you faultless before the presence of his glory in great joy,"]],f:["TR and NU read \u201cyou\u201d"]},{v:25,l:[[0,"to God our Savior, who alone is wise, be glory and majesty, dominion and power, both now and forever. Amen."]]}]]}},1336,[]);
__d(function(e,t,o,h,a,n,s){a.exports={book:"Rev",name:"Revelation",chapters:[[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"This is the Revelation of Jesus Christ, which God gave him to show to his servants the things which must happen soon, which he sent and made known by his angel to his servant, John,"]],f:["\u201cChrist\u201d means \u201cAnointed One\u201d.","or, messenger (here and wherever angel is mentioned)"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"who testified to God\u2019s word and of the testimony of Jesus Christ, about everything that he saw."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Blessed is he who reads and those who hear the words of the prophecy, and keep the things that are written in it, for the time is near."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"John, to the seven assemblies that are in Asia: Grace to you and peace from God, who is and who was and who is to come; and from the seven Spirits who are before his throne;"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"and from Jesus Christ, the faithful witness, the firstborn of the dead, and the ruler of the kings of the earth. To him who loves us, and washed us from our sins by his blood\u2014"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and he made us to be a Kingdom, priests to his God and Father\u2014to him be the glory and the dominion forever and ever. Amen."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"Behold, he is coming with the clouds, and every eye will see him, including those who pierced him. All the tribes of the earth will mourn over him. Even so, Amen."]],f:["\u201cBehold\u201d, from \u201c\u1f30\u03b4\u03bf\u1f7a\u201d, means look at, take notice, observe, see, or gaze at. It is often used as an interjection."]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI am the Alpha and the Omega,\u201d says the Lord God, \u201cwho is and who was and who is to come, the Almighty.\u201d"]],f:["TR adds \u201cthe Beginning and the End\u201d","TR omits \u201cGod\u201d"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"I John, your brother and partner with you in the oppression, Kingdom, and perseverance in Christ Jesus, was on the isle that is called Patmos because of God\u2019s Word and the testimony of Jesus Christ."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"I was in the Spirit on the Lord\u2019s day, and I heard behind me a loud voice, like a trumpet"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cWhat you see, write in a book and send to the seven assemblies: to Ephesus, Smyrna, Pergamum, Thyatira, Sardis, Philadelphia, and to Laodicea.\u201d"]],f:["TR adds \u201cI am the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last.\u201d","TR adds \u201cwhich are in Asia\u201d"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I turned to see the voice that spoke with me. Having turned, I saw seven golden lamp stands."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"And among the lamp stands was one like a son of man, clothed with a robe reaching down to his feet, and with a golden sash around his chest."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"His head and his hair were white as white wool, like snow. His eyes were like a flame of fire."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"His feet were like burnished brass, as if it had been refined in a furnace. His voice was like the voice of many waters."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He had seven stars in his right hand. Out of his mouth proceeded a sharp two-edged sword. His face was like the sun shining at its brightest."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"When I saw him, I fell at his feet like a dead man."],[0,"He laid his right hand on me, saying, \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid. I am the first and the last,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and the Living one. I was dead, and behold, I am alive forever and ever. Amen. I have the keys of Death and of Hades."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:19,l:[[0,"Write therefore the things which you have seen, and the things which are, and the things which will happen hereafter."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The mystery of the seven stars which you saw in my right hand, and the seven golden lamp stands is this: The seven stars are the angels of the seven assemblies. The seven lamp stands are seven assemblies."]],f:["or, messengers (here and wherever angels are mentioned)"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo the angel of the assembly in Ephesus write:"],[0,"\u201cHe who holds the seven stars in his right hand, he who walks among the seven golden lamp stands says these things:"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI know your works, and your toil and perseverance, and that you can\u2019t tolerate evil men, and have tested those who call themselves apostles, and they are not, and found them false."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"You have perseverance and have endured for my name\u2019s sake, and have not grown weary."]],f:["TR adds \u201chave labored and\u201d"]},{v:4,l:[[0,"But I have this against you, that you left your first love."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Remember therefore from where you have fallen, and repent and do the first works; or else I am coming to you swiftly, and will move your lamp stand out of its place, unless you repent."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"But this you have, that you hate the works of the Nicolaitans, which I also hate."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies. To him who overcomes I will give to eat from the tree of life, which is in the Paradise of my God."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo the angel of the assembly in Smyrna write:"],[0,"\u201cThe first and the last, who was dead, and has come to life says these things:"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI know your works, oppression, and your poverty (but you are rich), and the blasphemy of those who say they are Jews, and they are not, but are a synagogue of Satan."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Don\u2019t be afraid of the things which you are about to suffer. Behold, the devil is about to throw some of you into prison, that you may be tested; and you will have oppression for ten days. Be faithful to death, and I will give you the crown of life."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies. He who overcomes won\u2019t be harmed by the second death."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo the angel of the assembly in Pergamum write:"],[0,"\u201cHe who has the sharp two-edged sword says these things:"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI know your works and where you dwell, where Satan\u2019s throne is. You hold firmly to my name, and didn\u2019t deny my faith in the days of Antipas my witness, my faithful one, who was killed among you, where Satan dwells."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"But I have a few things against you, because you have there some who hold the teaching of Balaam, who taught Balak to throw a stumbling block before the children of Israel, to eat things sacrificed to idols, and to commit sexual immorality."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"So also you likewise have some who hold to the teaching of the Nicolaitans."]],f:["TR reads \u201cwhich I hate\u201d instead of \u201clikewise\u201d"]},{v:16,l:[[0,"Repent therefore, or else I am coming to you quickly and I will make war against them with the sword of my mouth."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies. To him who overcomes, to him I will give of the hidden manna, and I will give him a white stone, and on the stone a new name written which no one knows but he who receives it."]],f:["Manna is supernatural food, named after the Hebrew for \u201cWhat is it?\u201d. See Exodus 11:7-9."]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo the angel of the assembly in Thyatira write:"],[0,"\u201cThe Son of God, who has his eyes like a flame of fire, and his feet are like burnished brass, says these things:"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI know your works, your love, faith, service, patient endurance, and that your last works are more than the first."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"But I have this against you, that you tolerate your woman Jezebel, who calls herself a prophetess. She teaches and seduces my servants to commit sexual immorality and to eat things sacrificed to idols."]],f:["TR, NU read \u201cthat\u201d instead of \u201cyour\u201d"]},{v:21,l:[[0,"I gave her time to repent, but she refuses to repent of her sexual immorality."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"Behold, I will throw her and those who commit adultery with her into a bed of great oppression, unless they repent of her works."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"I will kill her children with Death, and all the assemblies will know that I am he who searches the minds and hearts. I will give to each one of you according to your deeds."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"But to you I say, to the rest who are in Thyatira\u2014as many as don\u2019t have this teaching, who don\u2019t know what some call \u2018the deep things of Satan\u2019\u2014to you I say, I am not putting any other burden on you."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Nevertheless, hold that which you have firmly until I come."]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"He who overcomes, and he who keeps my works to the end, to him I will give authority over the nations."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"He will rule them with a rod of iron, shattering them like clay pots, as I also have received of my Father;"]]},{v:28,l:[[0,"and I will give him the morning star."]]},{v:29,l:[[0,"He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cAnd to the angel of the assembly in Sardis write:"],[0,"\u201cHe who has the seven Spirits of God and the seven stars says these things:"],[0,"\u201cI know your works, that you have a reputation of being alive, but you are dead."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Wake up and strengthen the things that remain, which you were about to throw away, for I have found no works of yours perfected before my God."]],f:["NU & TR read \u201cwhich were about to die\u201d instead of \u201cwhich you were about to throw away\u201d."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Remember therefore how you have received and heard. Keep it and repent. If therefore you won\u2019t watch, I will come as a thief, and you won\u2019t know what hour I will come upon you."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Nevertheless you have a few names in Sardis that didn\u2019t defile their garments. They will walk with me in white, for they are worthy."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"He who overcomes will be arrayed in white garments, and I will in no way blot his name out of the book of life, and I will confess his name before my Father, and before his angels."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo the angel of the assembly in Philadelphia write:"],[0,"\u201cHe who is holy, he who is true, he who has the key of David, he who opens and no one can shut, and who shuts and no one opens, says these things:"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI know your works (behold, I have set before you an open door, which no one can shut), that you have a little power, and kept my word, and didn\u2019t deny my name."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"Behold, I make some of the synagogue of Satan, of those who say they are Jews, and they are not, but lie\u2014behold, I will make them to come and worship before your feet, and to know that I have loved you."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Because you kept my command to endure, I also will keep you from the hour of testing which is to come on the whole world, to test those who dwell on the earth."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"I am coming quickly! Hold firmly that which you have, so that no one takes your crown."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He who overcomes, I will make him a pillar in the temple of my God, and he will go out from there no more. I will write on him the name of my God and the name of the city of my God, the new Jerusalem, which comes down out of heaven from my God, and my own new name."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cTo the angel of the assembly in Laodicea write:"],[0,"\u201cThe Amen, the Faithful and True Witness, the Beginning of God\u2019s creation, says these things:"]],f:["or, Source, or Head"]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cI know your works, that you are neither cold nor hot. I wish you were cold or hot."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"So, because you are lukewarm, and neither hot nor cold, I will vomit you out of my mouth."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Because you say, \u2018I am rich, and have gotten riches, and have need of nothing,\u2019 and don\u2019t know that you are the wretched one, miserable, poor, blind, and naked;"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"I counsel you to buy from me gold refined by fire, that you may become rich; and white garments, that you may clothe yourself, and that the shame of your nakedness may not be revealed; and eye salve to anoint your eyes, that you may see."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"As many as I love, I reprove and chasten. Be zealous therefore, and repent."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Behold, I stand at the door and knock. If anyone hears my voice and opens the door, then I will come in to him and will dine with him, and he with me."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"He who overcomes, I will give to him to sit down with me on my throne, as I also overcame and sat down with my Father on his throne."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"He who has an ear, let him hear what the Spirit says to the assemblies.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things I looked and saw a door opened in heaven; and the first voice that I heard, like a trumpet speaking with me, was one saying, \u201cCome up here, and I will show you the things which must happen after this.\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"Immediately I was in the Spirit. Behold, there was a throne set in heaven, and one sitting on the throne"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"that looked like a jasper stone and a sardius. There was a rainbow around the throne, like an emerald to look at."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Around the throne were twenty-four thrones. On the thrones were twenty-four elders sitting, dressed in white garments, with crowns of gold on their heads."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"Out of the throne proceed lightnings, sounds, and thunders. There were seven lamps of fire burning before his throne, which are the seven Spirits of God."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Before the throne was something like a sea of glass, similar to crystal. In the middle of the throne, and around the throne were four living creatures full of eyes before and behind."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"The first creature was like a lion, the second creature like a calf, the third creature had a face like a man, and the fourth was like a flying eagle."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The four living creatures, each one of them having six wings, are full of eyes around and within. They have no rest day and night, saying, \u201cHoly, holy, holy is the Lord God, the Almighty, who was and who is and who is to come!\u201d"]],f:["Hodges/Farstad MT reads \u201choly\u201d 9 times instead of 3."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When the living creatures give glory, honor, and thanks to him who sits on the throne, to him who lives forever and ever,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"the twenty-four elders fall down before him who sits on the throne and worship him who lives forever and ever, and throw their crowns before the throne, saying,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"\u201cWorthy are you, our Lord and God, the Holy One, to receive the glory, the honor, and the power, for you created all things, and because of your desire they existed and were created!\u201d"]],f:["TR omits \u201cand God, the Holy One,\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw, in the right hand of him who sat on the throne, a book written inside and outside, sealed shut with seven seals."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I saw a mighty angel proclaiming with a loud voice, \u201cWho is worthy to open the book, and to break its seals?\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"No one in heaven above, or on the earth, or under the earth, was able to open the book or to look in it."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Then I wept much, because no one was found worthy to open the book or to look in it."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"One of the elders said to me, \u201cDon\u2019t weep. Behold, the Lion who is of the tribe of Judah, the Root of David, has overcome: he who opens the book and its seven seals.\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw in the middle of the throne and of the four living creatures, and in the middle of the elders, a Lamb standing, as though it had been slain, having seven horns and seven eyes, which are the seven Spirits of God, sent out into all the earth."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Then he came, and he took it out of the right hand of him who sat on the throne."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Now when he had taken the book, the four living creatures and the twenty-four elders fell down before the Lamb, each one having a harp, and golden bowls full of incense, which are the prayers of the saints."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They sang a new song, saying,"],[1,"\u201cYou are worthy to take the book"],[2,"and to open its seals,"],[1,"for you were killed,"],[2,"and bought us for God with your blood"],[2,"out of every tribe, language, people, and nation,"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[1,"and made us kings and priests to our God;"],[2,"and we will reign on the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"I looked, and I heard something like a voice of many angels around the throne, the living creatures, and the elders. The number of them was ten thousands of ten thousands, and thousands of thousands,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"saying with a loud voice, \u201cWorthy is the Lamb who has been killed to receive the power, wealth, wisdom, strength, honor, glory, and blessing!\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard every created thing which is in heaven, on the earth, under the earth, on the sea, and everything in them, saying, \u201cTo him who sits on the throne and to the Lamb be the blessing, the honor, the glory, and the dominion, forever and ever! Amen!\u201d"]],f:["TR omits \u201cAmen!\u201d"]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The four living creatures said, \u201cAmen!\u201d Then the elders fell down and worshiped."]],f:["TR adds \u201ctwenty-four\u201d","TR adds \u201cthe one living forever and ever\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw that the Lamb opened one of the seven seals, and I heard one of the four living creatures saying, as with a voice of thunder, \u201cCome and see!\u201d"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Then a white horse appeared, and he who sat on it had a bow. A crown was given to him, and he came out conquering, and to conquer."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"When he opened the second seal, I heard the second living creature saying, \u201cCome!\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"Another came out, a red horse. To him who sat on it was given power to take peace from the earth, and that they should kill one another. There was given to him a great sword."]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"When he opened the third seal, I heard the third living creature saying, \u201cCome and see!\u201d And behold, a black horse, and he who sat on it had a balance in his hand."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I heard a voice in the middle of the four living creatures saying, \u201cA choenix of wheat for a denarius, and three choenix of barley for a denarius! Don\u2019t damage the oil and the wine!\u201d"]],f:["A choenix is a dry volume measure that is a little more than a liter (a little more than a quart)."]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When he opened the fourth seal, I heard the fourth living creature saying, \u201cCome and see!\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"And behold, a pale horse, and the name of he who sat on it was Death. Hades followed with him. Authority over one fourth of the earth, to kill with the sword, with famine, with death, and by the wild animals of the earth was given to him."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"When he opened the fifth seal, I saw underneath the altar the souls of those who had been killed for the Word of God, and for the testimony of the Lamb which they had."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They cried with a loud voice, saying, \u201cHow long, Master, the holy and true, until you judge and avenge our blood on those who dwell on the earth?\u201d"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"A long white robe was given to each of them. They were told that they should rest yet for a while, until their fellow servants and their brothers, who would also be killed even as they were, should complete their course."]],f:["The word for \u201cbrothers\u201d here and where context allows may also be correctly translated \u201cbrothers and sisters\u201d or \u201csiblings.\u201d"]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw when he opened the sixth seal, and there was a great earthquake. The sun became black as sackcloth made of hair, and the whole moon became as blood."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The stars of the sky fell to the earth, like a fig tree dropping its unripe figs when it is shaken by a great wind."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The sky was removed like a scroll when it is rolled up. Every mountain and island was moved out of its place."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The kings of the earth, the princes, the commanding officers, the rich, the strong, and every slave and free person, hid themselves in the caves and in the rocks of the mountains."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They told the mountains and the rocks, \u201cFall on us, and hide us from the face of him who sits on the throne, and from the wrath of the Lamb,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"for the great day of his wrath has come, and who is able to stand?\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After this, I saw four angels standing at the four corners of the earth, holding the four winds of the earth, so that no wind would blow on the earth, or on the sea, or on any tree."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I saw another angel ascend from the sunrise, having the seal of the living God. He cried with a loud voice to the four angels to whom it was given to harm the earth and the sea,"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cDon\u2019t harm the earth, the sea, or the trees, until we have sealed the bondservants of our God on their foreheads!\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"I heard the number of those who were sealed, one hundred forty-four thousand, sealed out of every tribe of the children of Israel:"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[1,"of the tribe of Judah twelve thousand were sealed,"],[1,"of the tribe of Reuben twelve thousand,"],[1,"of the tribe of Gad twelve thousand,"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[1,"of the tribe of Asher twelve thousand,"],[1,"of the tribe of Naphtali twelve thousand,"],[1,"of the tribe of Manasseh twelve thousand,"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[1,"of the tribe of Simeon twelve thousand,"],[1,"of the tribe of Levi twelve thousand,"],[1,"of the tribe of Issachar twelve thousand,"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[1,"of the tribe of Zebulun twelve thousand,"],[1,"of the tribe of Joseph twelve thousand, and"],[1,"of the tribe of Benjamin twelve thousand were sealed."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things I looked, and behold, a great multitude which no man could count, out of every nation and of all tribes, peoples, and languages, standing before the throne and before the Lamb, dressed in white robes, with palm branches in their hands."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They cried with a loud voice, saying, \u201cSalvation be to our God, who sits on the throne, and to the Lamb!\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"All the angels were standing around the throne, the elders, and the four living creatures; and they fell on their faces before his throne, and worshiped God,"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"saying, \u201cAmen! Blessing, glory, wisdom, thanksgiving, honor, power, and might, be to our God forever and ever! Amen.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the elders answered, saying to me, \u201cThese who are arrayed in the white robes, who are they, and where did they come from?\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"I told him, \u201cMy lord, you know.\u201d"],[0,"He said to me, \u201cThese are those who came out of the great suffering. They washed their robes and made them white in the Lamb\u2019s blood."]],f:["or, oppression"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Therefore they are before the throne of God, and they serve him day and night in his temple. He who sits on the throne will spread his tabernacle over them."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"They will never be hungry or thirsty any more. The sun won\u2019t beat on them, nor any heat;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"for the Lamb who is in the middle of the throne shepherds them and leads them to springs of life-giving waters. And God will wipe away every tear from their eyes.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"When he opened the seventh seal, there was silence in heaven for about half an hour."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I saw the seven angels who stand before God, and seven trumpets were given to them."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Another angel came and stood over the altar, having a golden censer. Much incense was given to him, that he should add it to the prayers of all the saints on the golden altar which was before the throne."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The smoke of the incense, with the prayers of the saints, went up before God out of the angel\u2019s hand."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The angel took the censer, and he filled it with the fire of the altar, then threw it on the earth. Thunders, sounds, lightnings, and an earthquake followed."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"The seven angels who had the seven trumpets prepared themselves to sound."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The first sounded, and there followed hail and fire, mixed with blood, and they were thrown to the earth. One third of the earth was burned up, and one third of the trees were burned up, and all green grass was burned up."]],f:["TR omits \u201cOne third of the earth was burned up\u201d"]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The second angel sounded, and something like a great burning mountain was thrown into the sea. One third of the sea became blood,"]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"and one third of the living creatures which were in the sea died. One third of the ships were destroyed."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The third angel sounded, and a great star fell from the sky, burning like a torch, and it fell on one third of the rivers, and on the springs of water."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The name of the star is \u201cWormwood.\u201d One third of the waters became wormwood. Many people died from the waters, because they were made bitter."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The fourth angel sounded, and one third of the sun was struck, and one third of the moon, and one third of the stars, so that one third of them would be darkened; and the day wouldn\u2019t shine for one third of it, and the night in the same way."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I saw, and I heard an eagle, flying in mid heaven, saying with a loud voice, \u201cWoe! Woe! Woe to those who dwell on the earth, because of the other blasts of the trumpets of the three angels, who are yet to sound!\u201d"]],f:["TR reads \u201cangel\u201d instead of \u201ceagle\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"The fifth angel sounded, and I saw a star from the sky which had fallen to the earth. The key to the pit of the abyss was given to him."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He opened the pit of the abyss, and smoke went up out of the pit, like the smoke from a burning furnace. The sun and the air were darkened because of the smoke from the pit."]],f:["TR adds \u201cgreat\u201d"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"Then out of the smoke came locusts on the earth, and power was given to them, as the scorpions of the earth have power."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They were told that they should not hurt the grass of the earth, neither any green thing, neither any tree, but only those people who don\u2019t have God\u2019s seal on their foreheads."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"They were given power, not to kill them, but to torment them for five months. Their torment was like the torment of a scorpion when it strikes a person."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"In those days people will seek death, and will in no way find it. They will desire to die, and death will flee from them."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The shapes of the locusts were like horses prepared for war. On their heads were something like golden crowns, and their faces were like people\u2019s faces."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They had hair like women\u2019s hair, and their teeth were like those of lions."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They had breastplates like breastplates of iron. The sound of their wings was like the sound of many chariots and horses rushing to war."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They have tails like those of scorpions, with stingers. In their tails they have power to harm men for five months."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They have over them as king the angel of the abyss. His name in Hebrew is \u201cAbaddon\u201d, but in Greek, he has the name \u201cApollyon\u201d."]],f:["\u201cAbaddon\u201d is a Hebrew word that means \u201cruin\u201d, \u201cdestruction\u201d, or \u201cthe place of destruction\u201d","\u201cApollyon\u201d means \u201cDestroyer\u201d."]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The first woe is past. Behold, there are still two woes coming after this."]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"The sixth angel sounded. I heard a voice from the horns of the golden altar which is before God,"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"saying to the sixth angel who had the trumpet, \u201cFree the four angels who are bound at the great river Euphrates!\u201d"]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The four angels were freed who had been prepared for that hour and day and month and year, so that they might kill one third of mankind."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The number of the armies of the horsemen was two hundred million. I heard the number of them."]],f:["literally, \u201cten thousands of ten thousands\u201d"]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Thus I saw the horses in the vision and those who sat on them, having breastplates of fiery red, hyacinth blue, and sulfur yellow; and the horses\u2019 heads resembled lions\u2019 heads. Out of their mouths proceed fire, smoke, and sulfur."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"By these three plagues, one third of mankind was killed: by the fire, the smoke, and the sulfur, which proceeded out of their mouths."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"For the power of the horses is in their mouths and in their tails. For their tails are like serpents, and have heads; and with them they harm."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"The rest of mankind, who were not killed with these plagues, didn\u2019t repent of the works of their hands, that they wouldn\u2019t worship demons, and the idols of gold, and of silver, and of brass, and of stone, and of wood, which can\u2019t see, hear, or walk."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t repent of their murders, their sorceries, their sexual immorality, or their thefts."]],f:["The word for \u201csorceries\u201d (pharmakeia) also implies the use of potions, poisons, and drugs"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw a mighty angel coming down out of the sky, clothed with a cloud. A rainbow was on his head. His face was like the sun, and his feet like pillars of fire."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He had in his hand a little open book. He set his right foot on the sea, and his left on the land."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He cried with a loud voice, as a lion roars. When he cried, the seven thunders uttered their voices."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"When the seven thunders sounded, I was about to write; but I heard a voice from the sky saying, \u201cSeal up the things which the seven thunders said, and don\u2019t write them.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"The angel whom I saw standing on the sea and on the land lifted up his right hand to the sky"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"and swore by him who lives forever and ever, who created heaven and the things that are in it, the earth and the things that are in it, and the sea and the things that are in it, that there will no longer be delay,"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"but in the days of the voice of the seventh angel, when he is about to sound, then the mystery of God is finished, as he declared to his servants the prophets."]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The voice which I heard from heaven, again speaking with me, said, \u201cGo, take the book which is open in the hand of the angel who stands on the sea and on the land.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"I went to the angel, telling him to give me the little book."],[0,"He said to me, \u201cTake it and eat it. It will make your stomach bitter, but in your mouth it will be as sweet as honey.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"I took the little book out of the angel\u2019s hand, and ate it. It was as sweet as honey in my mouth. When I had eaten it, my stomach was made bitter."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They told me, \u201cYou must prophesy again over many peoples, nations, languages, and kings.\u201d"]],f:["TR reads \u201cHe\u201d instead of \u201cThey\u201d"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A reed like a rod was given to me. Someone said, \u201cRise and measure God\u2019s temple, and the altar, and those who worship in it."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"Leave out the court which is outside of the temple, and don\u2019t measure it, for it has been given to the nations. They will tread the holy city under foot for forty-two months."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I will give power to my two witnesses, and they will prophesy one thousand two hundred sixty days, clothed in sackcloth.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"These are the two olive trees and the two lamp stands, standing before the Lord of the earth."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"If anyone desires to harm them, fire proceeds out of their mouth and devours their enemies. If anyone desires to harm them, he must be killed in this way."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"These have the power to shut up the sky, that it may not rain during the days of their prophecy. They have power over the waters, to turn them into blood, and to strike the earth with every plague, as often as they desire."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"When they have finished their testimony, the beast that comes up out of the abyss will make war with them, and overcome them, and kill them."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Their dead bodies will be in the street of the great city, which spiritually is called Sodom and Egypt, where also their Lord was crucified."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"From among the peoples, tribes, languages, and nations, people will look at their dead bodies for three and a half days, and will not allow their dead bodies to be laid in a tomb."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"Those who dwell on the earth will rejoice over them, and they will be glad. They will give gifts to one another, because these two prophets tormented those who dwell on the earth."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"After the three and a half days, the breath of life from God entered into them, and they stood on their feet. Great fear fell on those who saw them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I heard a loud voice from heaven saying to them, \u201cCome up here!\u201d They went up into heaven in a cloud, and their enemies saw them."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"In that day there was a great earthquake, and a tenth of the city fell. Seven thousand people were killed in the earthquake, and the rest were terrified and gave glory to the God of heaven."]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"The second woe is past. Behold, the third woe comes quickly."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"The seventh angel sounded, and great voices in heaven followed, saying, \u201cThe kingdom of the world has become the Kingdom of our Lord and of his Christ. He will reign forever and ever!\u201d"]]},{v:16,p:1,l:[[0,"The twenty-four elders, who sit on their thrones before God\u2019s throne, fell on their faces and worshiped God,"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"saying: \u201cWe give you thanks, Lord God, the Almighty, the one who is and who was, because you have taken your great power and reigned."]],f:["TR adds \u201cand who is coming\u201d"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The nations were angry, and your wrath came, as did the time for the dead to be judged, and to give your bondservants the prophets, their reward, as well as to the saints and those who fear your name, to the small and the great, and to destroy those who destroy the earth.\u201d"]]},{v:19,p:1,l:[[0,"God\u2019s temple that is in heaven was opened, and the ark of the Lord\u2019s covenant was seen in his temple. Lightnings, sounds, thunders, an earthquake, and great hail followed."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"A great sign was seen in heaven: a woman clothed with the sun, and the moon under her feet, and on her head a crown of twelve stars."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"She was with child. She cried out in pain, laboring to give birth."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"Another sign was seen in heaven. Behold, a great red dragon, having seven heads and ten horns, and on his heads seven crowns."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"His tail drew one third of the stars of the sky, and threw them to the earth. The dragon stood before the woman who was about to give birth, so that when she gave birth he might devour her child."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"She gave birth to a son, a male child, who is to rule all the nations with a rod of iron. Her child was caught up to God and to his throne."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The woman fled into the wilderness, where she has a place prepared by God, that there they may nourish her one thousand two hundred sixty days."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"There was war in the sky. Michael and his angels made war on the dragon. The dragon and his angels made war."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"They didn\u2019t prevail. No place was found for them any more in heaven."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"The great dragon was thrown down, the old serpent, he who is called the devil and Satan, the deceiver of the whole world. He was thrown down to the earth, and his angels were thrown down with him."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard a loud voice in heaven, saying, \u201cNow the salvation, the power, and the Kingdom of our God, and the authority of his Christ has come; for the accuser of our brothers has been thrown down, who accuses them before our God day and night."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"They overcame him because of the Lamb\u2019s blood, and because of the word of their testimony. They didn\u2019t love their life, even to death."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"Therefore rejoice, heavens, and you who dwell in them. Woe to the earth and to the sea, because the devil has gone down to you, having great wrath, knowing that he has but a short time.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"When the dragon saw that he was thrown down to the earth, he persecuted the woman who gave birth to the male child."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Two wings of the great eagle were given to the woman, that she might fly into the wilderness to her place, so that she might be nourished for a time, times, and half a time, from the face of the serpent."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The serpent spewed water out of his mouth after the woman like a river, that he might cause her to be carried away by the stream."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The earth helped the woman, and the earth opened its mouth and swallowed up the river which the dragon spewed out of his mouth."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"The dragon grew angry with the woman, and went away to make war with the rest of her offspring, who keep God\u2019s commandments and hold Jesus\u2019 testimony."]],f:["or, seed"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"Then I stood on the sand of the sea. I saw a beast coming up out of the sea, having ten horns and seven heads. On his horns were ten crowns, and on his heads, blasphemous names."]],f:["NU reads he stood"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"The beast which I saw was like a leopard, and his feet were like those of a bear, and his mouth like the mouth of a lion. The dragon gave him his power, his throne, and great authority."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"One of his heads looked like it had been wounded fatally. His fatal wound was healed, and the whole earth marveled at the beast."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They worshiped the dragon because he gave his authority to the beast; and they worshiped the beast, saying, \u201cWho is like the beast? Who is able to make war with him?\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"A mouth speaking great things and blasphemy was given to him. Authority to make war for forty-two months was given to him."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He opened his mouth for blasphemy against God, to blaspheme his name, his dwelling, and those who dwell in heaven."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"It was given to him to make war with the saints and to overcome them. Authority over every tribe, people, language, and nation was given to him."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"All who dwell on the earth will worship him, everyone whose name has not been written from the foundation of the world in the book of life of the Lamb who has been killed."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"If anyone has an ear, let him hear."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"If anyone is to go into captivity, he will go into captivity. If anyone is to be killed with the sword, he must be killed. Here is the endurance and the faith of the saints."]],f:["TR reads \u201cIf anyone leads into captivity, into captivity he goes. If anyone will kill with the sword, he must be killed with a sword.\u201d instead of \u201cIf anyone is to go into captivity, he will go into captivity. If anyone is to be killed with the sword, he must be killed.\u201d"]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw another beast coming up out of the earth. He had two horns like a lamb and it spoke like a dragon."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"He exercises all the authority of the first beast in his presence. He makes the earth and those who dwell in it to worship the first beast, whose fatal wound was healed."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He performs great signs, even making fire come down out of the sky to the earth in the sight of people."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"He deceives my own people who dwell on the earth because of the signs he was granted to do in front of the beast, saying to those who dwell on the earth that they should make an image to the beast who had the sword wound and lived."]],f:["NU omits \u201cmy own\u201d"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"It was given to him to give breath to the image of the beast, that the image of the beast should both speak, and cause as many as wouldn\u2019t worship the image of the beast to be killed."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He causes all, the small and the great, the rich and the poor, and the free and the slave, to be given marks on their right hands or on their foreheads;"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"and that no one would be able to buy or to sell unless he has that mark, which is the name of the beast or the number of his name."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Here is wisdom. He who has understanding, let him calculate the number of the beast, for it is the number of a man. His number is six hundred sixty-six."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw, and behold, the Lamb standing on Mount Zion, and with him a number, one hundred forty-four thousand, having his name and the name of his Father written on their foreheads."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I heard a sound from heaven like the sound of many waters and like the sound of a great thunder. The sound which I heard was like that of harpists playing on their harps."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They sing a new song before the throne and before the four living creatures and the elders. No one could learn the song except the one hundred forty-four thousand, those who had been redeemed out of the earth."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"These are those who were not defiled with women, for they are virgins. These are those who follow the Lamb wherever he goes. These were redeemed by Jesus from among men, the first fruits to God and to the Lamb."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"In their mouth was found no lie, for they are blameless."]],f:["TR adds \u201cbefore the throne of God\u201d"]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw an angel flying in mid heaven, having an eternal Good News to proclaim to those who dwell on the earth\u2014to every nation, tribe, language, and people."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He said with a loud voice, \u201cFear the Lord, and give him glory, for the hour of his judgment has come. Worship him who made the heaven, the earth, the sea, and the springs of waters!\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Another, a second angel, followed, saying, \u201cBabylon the great has fallen, which has made all the nations to drink of the wine of the wrath of her sexual immorality.\u201d"]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Another angel, a third, followed them, saying with a great voice, \u201cIf anyone worships the beast and his image, and receives a mark on his forehead or on his hand,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"he also will drink of the wine of the wrath of God, which is prepared unmixed in the cup of his anger. He will be tormented with fire and sulfur in the presence of the holy angels and in the presence of the Lamb."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The smoke of their torment goes up forever and ever. They have no rest day and night, those who worship the beast and his image, and whoever receives the mark of his name."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"Here is the perseverance of the saints, those who keep the commandments of God and the faith of Jesus.\u201d"]]},{v:13,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard a voice from heaven saying, \u201cWrite, \u2018Blessed are the dead who die in the Lord from now on.\u2019\u201d"],[0,"\u201cYes,\u201d says the Spirit, \u201cthat they may rest from their labors, for their works follow with them.\u201d"]]},{v:14,p:1,l:[[0,"I looked, and saw a white cloud, and on the cloud one sitting like a son of man, having on his head a golden crown, and in his hand a sharp sickle."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Another angel came out of the temple, crying with a loud voice to him who sat on the cloud, \u201cSend your sickle and reap, for the hour to reap has come; for the harvest of the earth is ripe!\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He who sat on the cloud thrust his sickle on the earth, and the earth was reaped."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"Another angel came out of the temple which is in heaven. He also had a sharp sickle."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"Another angel came out from the altar, he who has power over fire, and he called with a great voice to him who had the sharp sickle, saying, \u201cSend your sharp sickle and gather the clusters of the vine of the earth, for the earth\u2019s grapes are fully ripe!\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The angel thrust his sickle into the earth, and gathered the vintage of the earth and threw it into the great wine press of the wrath of God."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The wine press was trodden outside of the city, and blood came out of the wine press, up to the bridles of the horses, as far as one thousand six hundred stadia."]],f:["1600 stadia = 296 kilometers or 184 miles"]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw another great and marvelous sign in the sky: seven angels having the seven last plagues, for in them God\u2019s wrath is finished."]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw something like a sea of glass mixed with fire, and those who overcame the beast, his image, and the number of his name, standing on the sea of glass, having harps of God."]],f:["TR adds \u201chis mark,\u201d"]},{v:3,l:[[0,"They sang the song of Moses, the servant of God, and the song of the Lamb, saying,"],[1,"\u201cGreat and marvelous are your works, Lord God, the Almighty!"],[2,"Righteous and true are your ways, you King of the nations."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[1,"Who wouldn\u2019t fear you, Lord,"],[2,"and glorify your name?"],[1,"For you only are holy."],[2,"For all the nations will come and worship before you."],[2,"For your righteous acts have been revealed.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things I looked, and the temple of the tabernacle of the testimony in heaven was opened."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"The seven angels who had the seven plagues came out, clothed with pure, bright linen, and wearing golden sashes around their chests."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the four living creatures gave to the seven angels seven golden bowls full of the wrath of God, who lives forever and ever."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The temple was filled with smoke from the glory of God and from his power. No one was able to enter into the temple until the seven plagues of the seven angels would be finished."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard a loud voice out of the temple, saying to the seven angels, \u201cGo and pour out the seven bowls of the wrath of God on the earth!\u201d"]]},{v:2,p:1,l:[[0,"The first went, and poured out his bowl into the earth, and it became a harmful and painful sore on the people who had the mark of the beast, and who worshiped his image."]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"The second angel poured out his bowl into the sea, and it became blood as of a dead man. Every living thing in the sea died."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"The third poured out his bowl into the rivers and springs of water, and they became blood."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"I heard the angel of the waters saying, \u201cYou are righteous, who are and who were, O Holy One, because you have judged these things."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"For they poured out the blood of saints and prophets, and you have given them blood to drink. They deserve this.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard the altar saying, \u201cYes, Lord God, the Almighty, true and righteous are your judgments.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"The fourth poured out his bowl on the sun, and it was given to him to scorch men with fire."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"People were scorched with great heat, and people blasphemed the name of God who has the power over these plagues. They didn\u2019t repent and give him glory."]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"The fifth poured out his bowl on the throne of the beast, and his kingdom was darkened. They gnawed their tongues because of the pain,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"and they blasphemed the God of heaven because of their pains and their sores. They still didn\u2019t repent of their works."]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"The sixth poured out his bowl on the great river, the Euphrates. Its water was dried up, that the way might be prepared for the kings that come from the sunrise."]],f:["or, east"]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I saw coming out of the mouth of the dragon, and out of the mouth of the beast, and out of the mouth of the false prophet, three unclean spirits, something like frogs;"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"for they are spirits of demons, performing signs, which go out to the kings of the whole inhabited earth, to gather them together for the war of that great day of God the Almighty."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I come like a thief. Blessed is he who watches, and keeps his clothes, so that he doesn\u2019t walk naked, and they see his shame.\u201d"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He gathered them together into the place which is called in Hebrew, \u201cHarmagedon\u201d."]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The seventh poured out his bowl into the air. A loud voice came out of the temple of heaven, from the throne, saying, \u201cIt is done!\u201d"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"There were lightnings, sounds, and thunders; and there was a great earthquake such as has not happened since there were men on the earth\u2014so great an earthquake and so mighty."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The great city was divided into three parts, and the cities of the nations fell. Babylon the great was remembered in the sight of God, to give to her the cup of the wine of the fierceness of his wrath."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"Every island fled away, and the mountains were not found."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"Great hailstones, about the weight of a talent, came down out of the sky on people. People blasphemed God because of the plague of the hail, for this plague was exceedingly severe."]],f:["A talent is about 30 kilograms or 66 pounds."]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the seven angels who had the seven bowls came and spoke with me, saying, \u201cCome here. I will show you the judgment of the great prostitute who sits on many waters,"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"with whom the kings of the earth committed sexual immorality. Those who dwell on the earth were made drunken with the wine of her sexual immorality.\u201d"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"He carried me away in the Spirit into a wilderness. I saw a woman sitting on a scarlet-colored beast, full of blasphemous names, having seven heads and ten horns."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The woman was dressed in purple and scarlet, and decked with gold and precious stones and pearls, having in her hand a golden cup full of abominations and the impurities of the sexual immorality of the earth."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"And on her forehead a name was written, \u201cMYSTERY, BABYLON THE GREAT, THE MOTHER OF THE PROSTITUTES AND OF THE ABOMINATIONS OF THE EARTH.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"I saw the woman drunken with the blood of the saints and with the blood of the martyrs of Jesus. When I saw her, I wondered with great amazement."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"The angel said to me, \u201cWhy do you wonder? I will tell you the mystery of the woman and of the beast that carries her, which has the seven heads and the ten horns."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"The beast that you saw was, and is not; and is about to come up out of the abyss and to go into destruction. Those who dwell on the earth and whose names have not been written in the book of life from the foundation of the world will marvel when they see that the beast was, and is not, and shall be present."]],f:["TR reads \u201cyet is\u201d instead of \u201cshall be present\u201d"]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"Here is the mind that has wisdom. The seven heads are seven mountains on which the woman sits."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"They are seven kings. Five have fallen, the one is, and the other has not yet come. When he comes, he must continue a little while."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The beast that was, and is not, is himself also an eighth, and is of the seven; and he goes to destruction."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"The ten horns that you saw are ten kings who have received no kingdom as yet, but they receive authority as kings with the beast for one hour."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"These have one mind, and they give their power and authority to the beast."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"These will war against the Lamb, and the Lamb will overcome them, for he is Lord of lords and King of kings; and those who are with him are called, chosen, and faithful.\u201d"]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cThe waters which you saw, where the prostitute sits, are peoples, multitudes, nations, and languages."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The ten horns which you saw, they and the beast will hate the prostitute, will make her desolate, will strip her naked, will eat her flesh, and will burn her utterly with fire."]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For God has put in their hearts to do what he has in mind, to be of one mind, and to give their kingdom to the beast, until the words of God should be accomplished."]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The woman whom you saw is the great city which reigns over the kings of the earth.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things, I saw another angel coming down out of the sky, having great authority. The earth was illuminated with his glory."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He cried with a mighty voice, saying, \u201cFallen, fallen is Babylon the great, and she has become a habitation of demons, a prison of every unclean spirit, and a prison of every unclean and hated bird!"]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"For all the nations have drunk of the wine of the wrath of her sexual immorality, the kings of the earth committed sexual immorality with her, and the merchants of the earth grew rich from the abundance of her luxury.\u201d"]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard another voice from heaven, saying, \u201cCome out of her, my people, that you have no participation in her sins, and that you don\u2019t receive of her plagues,"]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"for her sins have reached to the sky, and God has remembered her iniquities."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Return to her just as she returned, and repay her double as she did, and according to her works. In the cup which she mixed, mix to her double."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"However much she glorified herself and grew wanton, so much give her of torment and mourning. For she says in her heart, \u2018I sit a queen, and am no widow, and will in no way see mourning.\u2019"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"Therefore in one day her plagues will come: death, mourning, and famine; and she will be utterly burned with fire, for the Lord God who has judged her is strong."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"The kings of the earth who committed sexual immorality and lived wantonly with her will weep and wail over her, when they look at the smoke of her burning,"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"standing far away for the fear of her torment, saying, \u2018Woe, woe, the great city, Babylon, the strong city! For your judgment has come in one hour.\u2019"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"The merchants of the earth weep and mourn over her, for no one buys their merchandise any more:"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"merchandise of gold, silver, precious stones, pearls, fine linen, purple, silk, scarlet, all expensive wood, every vessel of ivory, every vessel made of most precious wood, and of brass, and iron, and marble;"]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"and cinnamon, incense, perfume, frankincense, wine, olive oil, fine flour, wheat, cattle, sheep, horses, chariots, and people\u2019s bodies and souls."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The fruits which your soul lusted after have been lost to you. All things that were dainty and sumptuous have perished from you, and you will find them no more at all."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"The merchants of these things, who were made rich by her, will stand far away for the fear of her torment, weeping and mourning,"]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"saying, \u2018Woe, woe, the great city, she who was dressed in fine linen, purple, and scarlet, and decked with gold and precious stones and pearls!"]]},{v:17,l:[[0,"For in an hour such great riches are made desolate.\u2019 Every ship master, and everyone who sails anywhere, and mariners, and as many as gain their living by sea, stood far away,"]]},{v:18,l:[[0,"and cried out as they looked at the smoke of her burning, saying, \u2018What is like the great city?\u2019"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"They cast dust on their heads, and cried, weeping and mourning, saying, \u2018Woe, woe, the great city, in which all who had their ships in the sea were made rich by reason of her great wealth!\u2019 For she is made desolate in one hour."]]},{v:20,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cRejoice over her, O heaven, you saints, apostles, and prophets, for God has judged your judgment on her.\u201d"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"A mighty angel took up a stone like a great millstone and cast it into the sea, saying, \u201cThus with violence will Babylon, the great city, be thrown down, and will be found no more at all."]]},{v:22,l:[[0,"The voice of harpists, minstrels, flute players, and trumpeters will be heard no more at all in you. No craftsman of whatever craft will be found any more at all in you. The sound of a mill will be heard no more at all in you."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The light of a lamp will shine no more at all in you. The voice of the bridegroom and of the bride will be heard no more at all in you, for your merchants were the princes of the earth; for with your sorcery all the nations were deceived."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"In her was found the blood of prophets and of saints, and of all who have been slain on the earth.\u201d"]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"After these things I heard something like a loud voice of a great multitude in heaven, saying, \u201cHallelujah! Salvation, power, and glory belong to our God;"]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"for his judgments are true and righteous. For he has judged the great prostitute who corrupted the earth with her sexual immorality, and he has avenged the blood of his servants at her hand.\u201d"]]},{v:3,p:1,l:[[0,"A second said, \u201cHallelujah! Her smoke goes up forever and ever.\u201d"]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"The twenty-four elders and the four living creatures fell down and worshiped God who sits on the throne, saying, \u201cAmen! Hallelujah!\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"A voice came from the throne, saying, \u201cGive praise to our God, all you his servants, you who fear him, the small and the great!\u201d"]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"I heard something like the voice of a great multitude, and like the voice of many waters, and like the voice of mighty thunders, saying, \u201cHallelujah! For the Lord our God, the Almighty, reigns!"]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"Let\u2019s rejoice and be exceedingly glad, and let\u2019s give the glory to him. For the wedding of the Lamb has come, and his wife has made herself ready.\u201d"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"It was given to her that she would array herself in bright, pure, fine linen, for the fine linen is the righteous acts of the saints."]]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cWrite, \u2018Blessed are those who are invited to the wedding supper of the Lamb.\u2019\u201d He said to me, \u201cThese are true words of God.\u201d"]]},{v:10,p:1,l:[[0,"I fell down before his feet to worship him. He said to me, \u201cLook! Don\u2019t do it! I am a fellow bondservant with you and with your brothers who hold the testimony of Jesus. Worship God, for the testimony of Jesus is the Spirit of Prophecy.\u201d"]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw heaven opened, and behold, a white horse, and he who sat on it is called Faithful and True. In righteousness he judges and makes war."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"His eyes are a flame of fire, and on his head are many crowns. He has names written and a name written which no one knows but he himself."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"He is clothed in a garment sprinkled with blood. His name is called \u201cThe Word of God.\u201d"]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The armies which are in heaven, clothed in white, pure, fine linen, followed him on white horses."]]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Out of his mouth proceeds a sharp, double-edged sword that with it he should strike the nations. He will rule them with an iron rod. He treads the wine press of the fierceness of the wrath of God, the Almighty."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"He has on his garment and on his thigh a name written, \u201cKING OF KINGS AND LORD OF LORDS.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw an angel standing in the sun. He cried with a loud voice, saying to all the birds that fly in the sky, \u201cCome! Be gathered together to the great supper of God,"]],f:["TR reads \u201csupper of the great God\u201d instead of \u201cgreat supper of God\u201d"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"that you may eat the flesh of kings, the flesh of captains, the flesh of mighty men, and the flesh of horses and of those who sit on them, and the flesh of all men, both free and slave, small and great.\u201d"]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"I saw the beast, the kings of the earth, and their armies, gathered together to make war against him who sat on the horse and against his army."]]},{v:20,l:[[0,"The beast was taken, and with him the false prophet who worked the signs in his sight, with which he deceived those who had received the mark of the beast and those who worshiped his image. These two were thrown alive into the lake of fire that burns with sulfur."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The rest were killed with the sword of him who sat on the horse, the sword which came out of his mouth. So all the birds were filled with their flesh."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw an angel coming down out of heaven, having the key of the abyss and a great chain in his hand."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"He seized the dragon, the old serpent, who is the devil and Satan, who deceives the whole inhabited earth, and bound him for a thousand years,"]],f:["TR and NU omit \u201cwho deceives the whole inhabited earth\u201d."]},{v:3,l:[[0,"and cast him into the abyss, and shut it and sealed it over him, that he should deceive the nations no more until the thousand years were finished. After this, he must be freed for a short time."]]},{v:4,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw thrones, and they sat on them, and judgment was given to them. I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded for the testimony of Jesus and for the word of God, and such as didn\u2019t worship the beast nor his image, and didn\u2019t receive the mark on their forehead and on their hand. They lived and reigned with Christ for a thousand years."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"The rest of the dead didn\u2019t live until the thousand years were finished. This is the first resurrection."]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"Blessed and holy is he who has part in the first resurrection. Over these, the second death has no power, but they will be priests of God and of Christ, and will reign with him one thousand years."]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"And after the thousand years, Satan will be released from his prison"]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"and he will come out to deceive the nations which are in the four corners of the earth, Gog and Magog, to gather them together to the war, whose number is as the sand of the sea."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"They went up over the width of the earth and surrounded the camp of the saints and the beloved city. Fire came down out of heaven from God and devoured them."]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"The devil who deceived them was thrown into the lake of fire and sulfur, where the beast and the false prophet are also. They will be tormented day and night forever and ever."]]},{v:11,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw a great white throne and him who sat on it, from whose face the earth and the sky fled away. There was found no place for them."]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"I saw the dead, the great and the small, standing before the throne, and they opened books. Another book was opened, which is the book of life. The dead were judged out of the things which were written in the books, according to their works."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"The sea gave up the dead who were in it. Death and Hades gave up the dead who were in them. They were judged, each one according to his works."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Death and Hades were thrown into the lake of fire. This is the second death, the lake of fire."]],f:["or, Hell"]},{v:15,l:[[0,"If anyone was not found written in the book of life, he was cast into the lake of fire."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw a new heaven and a new earth, for the first heaven and the first earth have passed away, and the sea is no more."]]},{v:2,l:[[0,"I saw the holy city, New Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God, prepared like a bride adorned for her husband."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"I heard a loud voice out of heaven saying, \u201cBehold, God\u2019s dwelling is with people; and he will dwell with them, and they will be his people, and God himself will be with them as their God."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"He will wipe away every tear from their eyes. Death will be no more; neither will there be mourning, nor crying, nor pain any more. The first things have passed away.\u201d"]]},{v:5,p:1,l:[[0,"He who sits on the throne said, \u201cBehold, I am making all things new.\u201d He said, \u201cWrite, for these words of God are faithful and true.\u201d"]]},{v:6,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cI am the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End. I will give freely to him who is thirsty from the spring of the water of life."]]},{v:7,l:[[0,"He who overcomes, I will give him these things. I will be his God, and he will be my son."]]},{v:8,l:[[0,"But for the cowardly, unbelieving, sinners, abominable, murderers, sexually immoral, sorcerers, idolaters, and all liars, their part is in the lake that burns with fire and sulfur, which is the second death.\u201d"]],f:["TR and NU omit \u201csinners\u201d","The word for \u201csorcerers\u201d here also includes users of potions and drugs."]},{v:9,p:1,l:[[0,"One of the seven angels who had the seven bowls which were loaded with the seven last plagues came, and he spoke with me, saying, \u201cCome here. I will show you the bride, the Lamb\u2019s wife.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He carried me away in the Spirit to a great and high mountain, and showed me the holy city, Jerusalem, coming down out of heaven from God,"]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"having the glory of God. Her light was like a most precious stone, like a jasper stone, clear as crystal;"]]},{v:12,l:[[0,"having a great and high wall with twelve gates, and at the gates twelve angels, and names written on them, which are the names of the twelve tribes of the children of Israel."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"On the east were three gates, and on the north three gates, and on the south three gates, and on the west three gates."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"The wall of the city had twelve foundations, and on them twelve names of the twelve Apostles of the Lamb."]]},{v:15,p:1,l:[[0,"He who spoke with me had for a measure a golden reed to measure the city, its gates, and its walls."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"The city is square. Its length is as great as its width. He measured the city with the reed: twelve thousand twelve stadia. Its length, width, and height are equal."]],f:["12,012 stadia = 2,221 kilometers or 1,380 miles. TR reads 12,000 stadia instead of 12,012 stadia."]},{v:17,l:[[0,"Its wall is one hundred forty-four cubits, by the measure of a man, that is, of an angel."]],f:["144 cubits is about 65.8 meters or 216 feet"]},{v:18,l:[[0,"The construction of its wall was jasper. The city was pure gold, like pure glass."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"The foundations of the city\u2019s wall were adorned with all kinds of precious stones. The first foundation was jasper, the second sapphire, the third chalcedony, the fourth emerald,"]],f:["or, lapis lazuli"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"the fifth sardonyx, the sixth sardius, the seventh chrysolite, the eighth beryl, the ninth topaz, the tenth chrysoprase, the eleventh jacinth, and the twelfth amethyst."]]},{v:21,l:[[0,"The twelve gates were twelve pearls. Each one of the gates was made of one pearl. The street of the city was pure gold, like transparent glass."]]},{v:22,p:1,l:[[0,"I saw no temple in it, for the Lord God the Almighty and the Lamb are its temple."]]},{v:23,l:[[0,"The city has no need for the sun or moon to shine, for the very glory of God illuminated it and its lamp is the Lamb."]]},{v:24,l:[[0,"The nations will walk in its light. The kings of the earth bring the glory and honor of the nations into it."]]},{v:25,l:[[0,"Its gates will in no way be shut by day (for there will be no night there),"]]},{v:26,l:[[0,"and they shall bring the glory and the honor of the nations into it so that they may enter."]]},{v:27,l:[[0,"There will in no way enter into it anything profane, or one who causes an abomination or a lie, but only those who are written in the Lamb\u2019s book of life."]]}],[{v:1,p:1,l:[[0,"He showed me a river of water of life, clear as crystal, proceeding out of the throne of God and of the Lamb,"]],f:["TR adds \u201cpure\u201d"]},{v:2,l:[[0,"in the middle of its street. On this side of the river and on that was the tree of life, bearing twelve kinds of fruits, yielding its fruit every month. The leaves of the tree were for the healing of the nations."]]},{v:3,l:[[0,"There will be no curse any more. The throne of God and of the Lamb will be in it, and his servants will serve him."]]},{v:4,l:[[0,"They will see his face, and his name will be on their foreheads."]]},{v:5,l:[[0,"There will be no night, and they need no lamp light or sun light; for the Lord God will illuminate them. They will reign forever and ever."]]},{v:6,p:1,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cThese words are faithful and true. The Lord God of the spirits of the prophets sent his angel to show to his bondservants the things which must happen soon.\u201d"]]},{v:7,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I am coming soon! Blessed is he who keeps the words of the prophecy of this book.\u201d"]]},{v:8,p:1,l:[[0,"Now I, John, am the one who heard and saw these things. When I heard and saw, I fell down to worship before the feet of the angel who had shown me these things."]]},{v:9,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cYou must not do that! I am a fellow bondservant with you and with your brothers, the prophets, and with those who keep the words of this book. Worship God.\u201d"]]},{v:10,l:[[0,"He said to me, \u201cDon\u2019t seal up the words of the prophecy of this book, for the time is at hand."]]},{v:11,l:[[0,"He who acts unjustly, let him act unjustly still. He who is filthy, let him be filthy still. He who is righteous, let him do righteousness still. He who is holy, let him be holy still.\u201d"]]},{v:12,p:1,l:[[0,"\u201cBehold, I am coming soon! My reward is with me, to repay to each man according to his work."]]},{v:13,l:[[0,"I am the Alpha and the Omega, the First and the Last, the Beginning and the End."]]},{v:14,l:[[0,"Blessed are those who do his commandments, that they may have the right to the tree of life, and may enter in by the gates into the city."]],f:["NU reads \u201cwash their robes\u201d instead of \u201cdo his commandments\u201d."]},{v:15,l:[[0,"Outside are the dogs, the sorcerers, the sexually immoral, the murderers, the idolaters, and everyone who loves and practices falsehood."]]},{v:16,l:[[0,"I, Jesus, have sent my angel to testify these things to you for the assemblies. I am the root and the offspring of David, the Bright and Morning Star.\u201d"]]},{v:17,p:1,l:[[0,"The Spirit and the bride say, \u201cCome!\u201d He who hears, let him say, \u201cCome!\u201d He who is thirsty, let him come. He who desires, let him take the water of life freely."]]},{v:18,p:1,l:[[0,"I testify to everyone who hears the words of the prophecy of this book: if anyone adds to them, God will add to him the plagues which are written in this book."]]},{v:19,l:[[0,"If anyone takes away from the words of the book of this prophecy, God will take away his part from the tree of life, and out of the holy city, which are written in this book."]],f:["TR reads \u201cBook\u201d instead of \u201ctree\u201d"]},{v:20,l:[[0,"He who testifies these things says, \u201cYes, I am coming soon.\u201d"],[0,"Amen! Yes, come, Lord Jesus!"]]},{v:21,p:1,l:[[0,"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ be with all the saints. Amen."]]}]]}},1337,[]);
